window.EF_CRUX_TRICKS_SNIPPET_INDEX=[{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0001","t":"01.i Area","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" AREA — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. India's World Rank by Area\n2. India's Share of World Area & Population\n3. Tropic of Cancer & Latitudinal Extent (Torrid Zone)\n4. Standard Time Meridian\n5. Total Extent, Land Boundary & States/UTs Count\n6. Number of Villages in India\n7. Miscellaneous Facts about India\n1. India's World Rank by Area\n●\nIndia duniya ka saatvaan (7th) sabse bada desh hai area ke hisaab se — Russia, Canada, USA, China, Brazil\naur Australia ke baad. Ye rank 5th ya 6th nahi hai — in dono wrong options ko exam mein carefully avoid\nkaro. [Q1(stmt1), Q2(stmt1), Q3, Q4]\n●\nPopulation ke hisaab se India duniya ka dusra (2nd) sabse zyada aabadi wala desh hai (Census 2011 ke hisab\nse; UNFPA 2023 projection mein sabse zyada aabadi wala bhi ban chuka hai). [Q8]\n2. India's Share of World Area & Population\n●\nIndia duniya ke total land area (lithosphere) ka lagbhag 2.4% hissa cover karta hai. [Q1(stmt2), Q2(stmt2)]\n●\nLekin area sirf 2.4% hone ke bawajood, India ki population world population ka lagbhag 16.7% (Census\n2001) — 17.5% (Census 2011) hai. Closest exam option 17% maana jaata hai. [Q5]\n3. Tropic of Cancer & Latitudinal Extent (Torrid Zone)\n●\nTropic of Cancer (Karka Rekha) desh ke beech (middle) se guzarti hai, jo India ko do latitudinal halves mein\nbaant deti hai. [Q1(stmt3)]\n●\nTorrid (tropical) zone 23°30' North se South latitude tak failaa hai, jabki India 8°4' N se 37°6' N tak failaa\nhai. Isliye poora India torrid zone mein NAHI hai — ye ek common EXAM TRAP hai (statement 'whole\nof India lies in torrid zone' hamesha GALAT hoga). [Q1(stmt4), Q2(stmt3)]\n4. Standard Time Meridian\n●\nIndian Standard Time (IST) 82°30' East longitude (Mirzapur, U.P. ke paas) se determine hoti hai. [Q2(stmt4)]\n5. Total Extent, Land Boundary & States/UTs Count\n●\nIndia ka total area 3.28 million sq. km (3,287,263 sq km — Census 2001) hai. Latitudinal extent 8°4' N –\n37°6' N aur longitudinal extent 68°7' E – 97°25' E hai. [Q7]\n●\nIndia mein currently 28 states aur 8 union territories hain — 26 states NAHI (ye ek common wrong-pair\noption hota hai match-the-following type questions mein). [Q7]"," ●\nIndia ki land boundary lagbhag 15,200 km tak faili hui hai. [Q8]\n6. Number of Villages in India\n●\nCensus 2011 ke anusaar, India mein total gaon (villages) ki sankhya 6,40,932 hai. Chunki exact figure (6.4\nlakh) options mein nahi diya jaata, 'None of these' / '\n\n\nइनमेंसेकोईनहीं' sahi answer banta hai — is pattern ko\nyaad rakho. [Q6]\n7. Miscellaneous Facts about India\n EXAM TRAP — First Sunrise (bahut common galat option!)\n⚠️\n●\nIndia mein sabse pehla sunrise Arunachal Pradesh (India ka sabse east state) mein hota hai — Mizoram\nmein NAHI. Options mein 'Mizoram' galat statement ke roop mein diya jaata hai — is trap ko carefully\nidentify karo. [Q8]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0002","t":"01.ii Latitudinal Expansion","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" LATITUDINAL EXPANSION — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. India's Latitudinal & Longitudinal Extent\n2. Latitude/Longitude Pass-Through Trivia\n1. India's Latitudinal & Longitudinal Extent\n●\nIndia ka expansion 8°4' North se 37°6' North latitude aur 68°7' East se 97°25' East longitude ke beech\nhai. Options mein diye jaane wale coordinates (jaise '37°17'53\" N and 8°6'28\" S') galat hote hain — asli\nfigures upar wale hi yaad rakho, isliye aksar 'None of the above' hi sahi answer banta hai jab exact wrong\ncoordinates diye jaate hain. [Q1]\n●\nTropic of Cancer (Karka Rekha) lagbhag India ke beech se guzarti hai. [Q1]\n2. Latitude/Longitude Pass-Through Trivia\n●\nSikkim se guzarne wala latitude Rajasthan se bhi guzarta hai — dono states same latitude band mein aate\nhain. [Q2]\n●\n70° East longitude Jaisalmer (Rajasthan) se guzarta hai. [Q3]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0003","t":"01.iii India and the Tropic of Cancer","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" INDIA AND THE TROPIC OF CANCER — FULL\n☀️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. States the Tropic of Cancer Passes Through\n2. Nearest/Farthest Cities & Latitude Comparisons\n3. Statements True/False about the Tropic of Cancer\n4. Day-Length & Season Effects\n5. Rivers Crossing the Tropic of Cancer\n1. States the Tropic of Cancer Passes Through\n●\nTropic of Cancer (23°30' N) bhaarat ke 8 states se guzarti hai: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh,\nChhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura aur Mizoram — is poori list ko yaad rakhna zaroori hai.\n[Q1, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q12]\n EXAM TRAP — Bihar vs Jharkhand (state-reorganization wala trap)\n⚠️\n●\nPurane U.P./Bihar-era questions mein 'Bihar' option milta hai kyunki 2000 se pehle Jharkhand, Bihar ka\nhissa tha. Agar options mein 'Jharkhand' hai to Jharkhand sahi hai; agar sirf purana 'Bihar' hi diya ho to wahi\nlegacy-correct maana jaata hai. Manipur, Uttar Pradesh, Odisha, Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir —\ninme se koi bhi Tropic of Cancer se NAHI guzarta. [Q1, Q2, Q6, Q7, Q12]\n2. Nearest/Farthest Cities & Latitude Comparisons\n●\nTropic of Cancer ke sabse nazdeek cities (unke latitude ke basis par): Gandhinagar (23°19' N) — sabse\nkareeb; iske alawa Jabalpur (23°11' N) aur Kolkata (22°30'-22°37' N) bhi close options mein diye jaate\nhain — sabse kam latitude-difference wala city hi sahi answer hota hai. [Q8, Q9, Q14]\n●\nJun mein sabse zyada din-lambai (day length) uss jagah hoti hai jo sabse north mein ho — diye gaye options\n(Hyderabad, Chennai, Bhopal, Delhi) mein Delhi sabse north hai, isliye Delhi mein June mein sabse lamba\ndin hota hai. [Q13]\n3. Statements True/False about the Tropic of Cancer\n●\nTropic of Cancer (23°30' N) desh ko do halves mein baantti hai — ye statement TRUE hai. Lekin ye India\nki international boundary ko do halves mein nahi baantti (FALSE), aur India ka max east-west expansion bhi\nexactly isi line ke saath nahi hai (FALSE). [Q10, Q11]\n●\nIndia ka easternmost point Kibithu (Arunachal Pradesh) aur westernmost point Guhar Moti (Gujarat) hai\n— inhe jodne wali line Tropic of Cancer ke north mein padti hai (statement TRUE). [Q11]\n4. Day-Length & Season Effects\n●\n21 June (summer solstice) ko sun directly Tropic of Cancer ke upar hota hai aur north pole sun ki taraf tilt\nhota hai — isliye northern hemisphere mein jitna north jaoge, June mein utna lamba din milega. [Q13]"," 5. Rivers Crossing the Tropic of Cancer\n●\nSirf Mahi River hi aisi Indian river hai jo Tropic of Cancer ko do baar cross karti hai — ye M.P. se nikalti\nhai aur Rajasthan, Gujarat se hote hue Arabian Sea (Gulf of Khambhat) mein girti hai. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0004","t":"01.iv Standard Time","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" STANDARD TIME — FULL MIND MAP\n🕐\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Standard Meridian & Basic Facts\n2. Standard Meridian Pass-Through States & Cities\n3. IST vs GMT Time Difference\n4. Time-Calculation Problems (Longitude ↔ Time)\n5. City Longitude Comparisons\n6. Tropic of Cancer × IST Meridian Intersection\n1. Standard Meridian & Basic Facts\n●\nIndia ka Standard Meridian 82°30' East hai — isi meridian ke local time ko poore desh ka Indian Standard\nTime (IST) maana jaata hai. [Q1, Q10]\n●\nMainland India ka latitudinal aur longitudinal extent dono lagbhag 30° hai. Gujarat se Arunachal Pradesh tak\ntime-lag ~2 ghante ka hai —\n\nढाईghante NAHI (ye ek common wrong statement hai jo exam mein diya jaata\nhai). [Q1]\n2. Standard Meridian Pass-Through States & Cities\n●\n82°30' E meridian 5 states se guzarta hai: Uttar Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Odisha aur\nAndhra Pradesh — Maharashtra se NAHI guzarta. [Q8]\n EXAM TRAP — Mirzapur/Naini vs Allahabad — dono correct maane jaate hain\n⚠️\n●\n82°30' E meridian officially Uttar Pradesh ke Mirzapur district se guzarta hai — Prayagraj (Allahabad) ke\npaas. Isliye purane exams mein 'Prayagraj/Allahabad (Naini)' bhi correct answer maana jaata raha hai. In dono\nnaamon ko interchangeably associate karo. [Q9, Q11]\n●\nRewa (M.P.) ka longitude (~81°19' E) diye gaye options mein IST meridian (82°30' E) ke sabse kareeb hai —\nSagar, Ujjain, Hoshangabad se zyada close. [Q5]\n3. IST vs GMT Time Difference\n●\nIST, GMT (Greenwich Mean Time) se +5½ ghante aage hai. [Q12]\n4. Time-Calculation Problems (Longitude ↔ Time)\n●\nCalculation ka rule: 1° longitude = 4 minute time difference (15° = 1 ghanta). Jo jagah IST meridian (82°30'\nE) ke east mein hai uska local time IST se aage hoga; jo west mein hai uska peeche hoga. [Q2, Q6, Q7, Q13]\n●\nExample: Shillong (92°E) IST meridian se 9.5° east hai, isliye uska local time IST se 38 min aage hai (10:00\nAM IST → 10:38 AM Shillong). Isi tarah Tirap (Arunachal) mein 5:00 AM sunrise ho to Kandla (Gujarat,\n~30° west) mein sunrise ~7:00 AM hoga (2.5 ghante ka farak). [Q6, Q7, Q13]\n●\nReverse-calculation type: agar IST meridian par midnight (12 AM) ho aur kisi jagah 6 AM ho rahaa ho (6\nghante aage = 90° east), to wo jagah 82°30' E + 90° = 172°30' E par hogi. [Q2]"," ●\nGujarat ke westernmost village aur Arunachal Pradesh ke Walong (easternmost village) ke beech ka time-\ndifference lagbhag 2 ghante hai (longitude difference ~29°26'). [Q3]\n5. City Longitude Comparisons\n●\nJabalpur ka longitude (~79°58' E) Indore (75°51' E) aur Bhopal (77°24' E) dono se zyada east hai — isliye\nJabalpur 'inke beech mein' nahi aata. Aurangabad ka latitude (~19°53' N) Vadodara aur Pune ke latitude ke\nbeech mein aata hai. Bengaluru (~12°58' N) Chennai (~13°04' N) se zyada south hai. [Q4]\n●\nDelhi ke sabse kareeb longitude wala city Bengaluru hai — Hyderabad, Nagpur, Pune se zyada close. [Q14]\n6. Tropic of Cancer × IST Meridian Intersection\n●\nTropic of Cancer (23.5°N) aur IST meridian (82.5°E) ek dusre ko Chhattisgarh ke Koriya district mein\ncross karte hain, jo Baghelkhand Plateau region mein aata hai. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0005","t":"01.v Extreme Points","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" EXTREME POINTS — FULL MIND MAP\n📍\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Four Extreme Points of India\n2. Indira Point (Southernmost) — Details\n3. Easternmost/Westernmost — City & State Comparisons\n4. Kanyakumari — Where Three Water Bodies Meet\n1. The Four Extreme Points of India\n●\nIndia ke 4 extreme points: Southernmost — Indira Point (6°4' N, Great Nicobar, Andaman & Nicobar),\nNorthernmost — Indira Col (Siachen Glacier ke paas, Ladakh), Westernmost — Guhar Moti / Guhar\nMota (Kutch, Gujarat), Easternmost — Kibithu (Arunachal Pradesh). Mainland (excluding islands) ka\nsouthernmost point Kanyakumari (Tamil Nadu, 8°4' N) hai. [Q1]\n●\nState-level extreme points: Easternmost state — Arunachal Pradesh, Westernmost state — Gujarat —\nye sahi pair hai (Assam-Rajasthan, Assam-Gujarat jaise options galat hote hain). [Q4]\n2. Indira Point (Southernmost) — Details\n●\nIndira Point, Great Nicobar tehsil mein located hai (Nicobar district, Andaman & Nicobar Islands) —\nChhota Nicobar ya Car Nicobar mein NAHI. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Easternmost/Westernmost — City & State Comparisons\n●\nWesternmost point ka exact coordinate 23°7' N, 68°7' East hai (Guhar Moti, Kutch, Gujarat) — direction\n'East' hi sahi hai, 'West' nahi (common confusion trap). [Q5]\n●\nDiye gaye major cities (Hyderabad, Bhopal, Lucknow, Bangalore) mein sabse eastward city Lucknow\n(80°34'-81°12' E) hai. [Q6]\n4. Kanyakumari — Where Three Water Bodies Meet\n●\nKanyakumari (Tamil Nadu) wo jagah hai jahan Bay of Bengal, Arabian Sea aur Indian Ocean teeno milte\nhain — Indian mainland ka southernmost point bhi yahi hai. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0006","t":"01.vi Bordering Countries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" BORDERING COUNTRIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🌐\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. States Bordering Bangladesh\n2. States Bordering Bhutan\n3. India-Pakistan Composite Dialogue Issues (1998)\n4. States Bordering Myanmar\n5. States Bordering Pakistan\n6. States Bordering Nepal\n7. Boundary Lines — Radcliffe, Durand, McMahon\n8. India–Sri Lanka Separation\n9. States with 3-Country Borders / Max International Border\n10. Land Border Length Comparison (Country-wise)\n11. Territorial Waters & Miscellaneous\n1. States Bordering Bangladesh\n●\nBangladesh se border share karne wale 5 states: West Bengal, Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura aur Mizoram.\nManipur aur Nagaland Bangladesh se NAHI bordering karte (ye dono Myanmar se border karte hain).\n[Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q14]\n2. States Bordering Bhutan\n●\nBhutan se border share karne wale 4 states: West Bengal, Sikkim, Assam aur Arunachal Pradesh. Bihar\naur Meghalaya Bhutan se NAHI bordering karte — Bihar Nepal se aur Meghalaya Bangladesh se border\nkarta hai. [Q6, Q7]\n3. India-Pakistan Composite Dialogue Issues (1998)\n●\nNov 1998 ke Composite Dialogue Process mein Sir Creek — boundary dispute settlement, LOC region —\ntroops disengagement, Sindhu river region — river water sharing map-issues thi. [Q8]\n5. States Bordering Myanmar\n●\nMyanmar se border share karne wale 4 states: Arunachal Pradesh, Nagaland, Manipur aur Mizoram.\nInme se Arunachal Pradesh ka Myanmar ke saath sabse zyada (maximum) border hai. Assam aur\nTripura Myanmar se NAHI bordering karte. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n5. States Bordering Pakistan\n●\nPakistan se border share karne wale regions: Ladakh, Jammu & Kashmir, Punjab, Rajasthan aur Gujarat\n— sahi combination yehi hai (Himachal Pradesh ya Haryana wale options galat hote hain). [Q12]\n6. States Bordering Nepal\n●\nNepal se border share karne wale states: Sikkim, Bihar, Uttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh aur West Bengal —\n'Sikkim-Bihar' jaisa combination sahi group maana jaata hai. [Q13]"," 7. Boundary Lines — Radcliffe, Durand, McMahon\n●\nTeen important boundary lines yaad rakho: Radcliffe Line → India-Pakistan (aur India-Bangladesh)\nboundary, 1947 mein Sir Radcliffe ne banayi thi, isse 'superimposed boundary' ka example maana jaata hai;\nDurand Line → India-Afghanistan (aur Pakistan-Afghanistan) boundary; McMahon Line → India-China\nboundary (specifically Arunachal Pradesh aur China ke south-east border ke beech), 1914 ki Shimla Treaty ka\nresult, Sir Henry McMahon ke naam par. [Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23]\n8. India–Sri Lanka Separation\n●\nIndia aur Sri Lanka Palk Strait aur Gulf of Mannar se separate hote hain — naam Madras ke tatkalin\nGovernor Robert Palk ke naam par pada hai. [Q24]\n9. States with 3-Country Borders / Max International Border\n●\nSikkim akela aisa state hai jiski border teen countries — Nepal (west), Bhutan (east), China/Tibet (north)\n— teeno se lagti hai. [Q25]\n●\nTripura ek aisa state hai jiski teen taraf (north, west, south) international boundary hai — Bangladesh se\nghira hua; east mein Assam-Mizoram hain. [Q26]\n10. Land Border Length Comparison (Country-wise)\n●\nIndia ke neighbouring countries ke saath land-border lambai (km mein): Bangladesh — 4096.7 km (sabse\nlambi), China — 3488 km, Pakistan — 3323 km, Nepal — 1751 km (sabse chhoti). Ascending order yaad\nrakho: Nepal < Pakistan < China < Bangladesh. [Q14, Q27]\n EXAM TRAP — Ascending vs Descending order ka confusion\n⚠️\n●\nExam mein 'ascending' aur 'descending' order dono puchhe jaate hain — hamesha check karo question kya\nmaang raha hai. Ascending (chhota se bada): Nepal → Pakistan → China → Bangladesh. [Q27]\n11. Territorial Waters & Miscellaneous\n●\nIndia ki territorial water-limit tat (coast) se 12 nautical miles (~21.9-22.2 km) tak samudra mein failii hui hai.\n[Q28]\n●\nUttarakhand ke 3 districts Tibet se border karte hain: Chamoli, Pithoragarh aur Uttarkashi — Almora\nTibet border par NAHI hai (ye ek common wrong-option trap hai). [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0007","t":"10 Natural Vegetation","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NATURAL VEGETATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🌳\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Birch, Katha (Khair) & Other Named Trees\n2. Tropical Dry Deciduous — India's Largest Forest Type\n3. Teak & Sal Products\n4. Altitude-Based Vegetation Change in Himalaya\n5. Soil Erosion Sequence (Cross-Reference)\n6. Tree-Line Height — Western vs Eastern Himalaya\n7. Western Himalayan Region — Forest Resources\n8. Deodar — Western Himalaya's Temperate Tree\n9. Southern vs Northern Slopes — Vegetation Density\n10. Cinchona — Not Found in Chhattisgarh\n11. 'Flame of the Forest' — Butea Monosperma\n12. Teak Forest States (MP Highest)\n13. Flowerless Plants — Fern\n14. Alpine Vegetation Height Difference (East vs West)\n15. Oryx vs Chiru — Antelope Habitat Difference\n16. Tree-Region Match Sets (Teak, Deodar, Sundari, Cinchona)\n17. Sundarbans — Littoral/Tidal Forest Type\n18. Sandalwood, Sundari & Region Match\n19. Forest Type-Region Match Set\n20. Tropical Thorn Forest — Western Andhra Pradesh\n21. Deodar — Highest Elevation Tree (1500-3000m)\n22. Map — Sal Forests Threatened by 1997 Epidemic\n23. Subtropical Forest — Madhya Pradesh\n24. Mahogany — Not Himalayan Vegetation\n25. Khejri — Social Forestry Multipurpose Tree\n26. Victoria Falls (Cross-Reference, Africa)\n27. Lisa (Resin) — Pine Tree Product\n28. Mangrove-State Match Sets (Maharashtra to Odisha)\n29. Vembanad — Kerala (Not Karnataka)\n30. Tropical Rainforest — Assam & Kerala\n31. Dense Deciduous Forest — MP & West Champaran\n32. Khair — Sub-Tropical Forest Tree\n33. Highest Forest % State — Mizoram\n34. Sita Nadi Sanctuary — Sal Forest\n1. Birch, Katha (Khair) & Other Named Trees\n●\nBirch tree Himalayas mein paayi jaati hai (iski white paper-jaisi bark ancient scripts likhne ke liye use hoti\nthi). Katha (kattha) Khair wood se banta hai — Himalaya se South India tak arid regions mein ugta hai.\n[Q1, Q2]\n2. Tropical Dry Deciduous — India's Largest Forest Type\n●\nIndia mein Tropical Dry Deciduous forest sabse bada forest type hai (43.85% forest area, 8.53% country\narea) — 70-100cm annual rainfall wale areas mein milta hai, isse 'monsoon forest' bhi kehte hain. [Q3, Q5]"," 3. Teak & Sal Products\n●\nTeak aur Sal Tropical Deciduous Forests ke products hain. [Q4]\n4. Altitude-Based Vegetation Change in Himalaya\n●\nHimalaya mein altitude ke saath vegetation change hoti hai — reasons: temperature ki kami, rainfall forms\nmein change, unfertile soil (strong winds is combination mein include NAHI hai). [Q6]\n5. Soil Erosion Sequence (Cross-Reference)\n●\nSoil loss ka increasing order: Splash erosion → Sheet erosion → Rill erosion → Gully erosion (Soil\nErosion chapter se cross-reference). [Q7]\n6. Tree-Line Height — Western vs Eastern Himalaya\n●\nTree-line height Eastern/Central Himalaya mein ~3600-3800m hai — Western Himalaya mein ye kam\n(~3300-3600m) hai. [Q8]\n7. Western Himalayan Region — Forest Resources\n●\nWestern Himalayan region ka main resource — Forest (~65% area cover) hai — metallic, non-metallic ya\natomic minerals se zyada. [Q9]\n8. Deodar — Western Himalaya's Temperate Tree\n●\nWestern Himalaya ke temperate zone mein Deodar sabse abundant tree hai (1500-2500m elevation) —\nDeodar samudra-tal se 1500-3000m ki sabse ooncha elevation par milta hai (Chir ~900-1000m, Sal sub-\nHimalayan/central India mein, Teak MP-Chhattisgarh-Odisha mein). [Q10, Q25]\n9. Southern vs Northern Slopes — Vegetation Density\n●\nHimalaya ke Southern slopes par northern slopes se zyada dense vegetation hai (Assertion galat hai —\nnorthern slopes ki baat kahi gayi thi) — kyunki southern slopes mein northern se zyada rainfall aur\nsunlight milti hai (Reason sahi hai). [Q11]\n10. Cinchona — Not Found in Chhattisgarh\n●\nCinchona (evergreen tropical plant) Chhattisgarh mein NAHI ugta (Chhattisgarh tropical dry/monsoon\nforests ke liye suited hai) — Assam, Kerala, West Bengal mein milta hai. [Q12]\n11. 'Flame of the Forest' — Butea Monosperma\n●\n'Flame of the forest' Butea monosperma (Dhak/Palash) ko kaha jaata hai — UP ka State Flower bhi hai.\n[Q13]\n12. Teak Forest States (MP Highest)\n●\nTeak forest Madhya Pradesh, Karnataka, Uttar Pradesh teeno mein milta hai — maximum Teak forest\nMP mein hai (disputed question, options mein sab 3 states honi chahiye). [Q14]"," 13. Flowerless Plants — Fern\n●\nFern ek vascular plant hai jo spores se reproduce karta hai — na seeds hote hain na flowers (Jackfruit, Fig,\nOrchid mein flowers hote hain). [Q15]\n14. Alpine Vegetation Height Difference (East vs West)\n●\nWestern Himalaya mein alpine vegetation 3000m tak hai, Eastern Himalaya mein 4000m tak — reason:\nEastern Himalaya equator aur sea-coast ke zyada kareeb hai (isliye snowline zyada ooncha hai). [Q16]\n15. Oryx vs Chiru — Antelope Habitat Difference\n●\nOryx aur Chiru mein difference: Oryx hot/arid areas mein adapt hai, Chiru cold high-mountain\nsteppes/semi-desert areas mein adapt hai. [Q17]\n16. Tree-Region Match Sets (Teak, Deodar, Sundari, Cinchona)\n●\nMatch set: Teak — Central India (MP/Chhattisgarh/Odisha), Deodar — Himalayan Tarai (western\nHimalaya, 1500-3000m), Sundari — Sunderban, Cinchona — high altitude Himalaya regions (also\nTerai). [Q18, Q20]\n17. Sundarbans — Littoral/Tidal Forest Type\n●\nSundarbans Littoral ya Tidal (Mangrove) forest hai — tropical dry deciduous, alpine, subtropical pine\nforest NAHI. [Q19]\n18. Sandalwood, Sundari & Region Match\n●\nSahi pair: Sundari — West Bengal (Sundarbans) — Teak-J&K, Deodar-MP, Sandalwood-Kerala\nGALAT hain. [Q20]\n19. Forest Type-Region Match Set\n●\nForest-region match: Tropical moist deciduous — Tarai, Tropical dry deciduous — Middle Ganga Plain,\nAlpine — Arunachal Pradesh, Tropical evergreen — Sahyadris. [Q21]\n●\nEk aur set (disputed): Tropical forest — Silent Valley, Conifer forest — Himachal Pradesh, Mangroves\n— Sunderbans, Deciduous forest — Rajasthan. [Q22, Q23]\n20. Tropical Thorn Forest — Western Andhra Pradesh\n●\nLong roots/sharp thorns wale stunted forests (low rainfall <70cm, low humidity <50%, high temp 25-30°C)\n— Western Andhra Pradesh mein milte hain (Rajasthan, SW Punjab, W Haryana, Kutch-Saurashtra mein\nbhi). [Q24]\n21. Deodar — Highest Elevation Tree (1500-3000m)\n●\nDeodar trees Western Himalaya mein sea level se 1500-3000m ki sabse zyada uchai par milte hain —\nChir (900-1000m), Sal (sub-Himalayan/Central India east/Tamil Nadu), Teak\n(MP/Chhattisgarh/Odisha/Karnataka/TN/Gujarat/Maharashtra) inse kam uchai par. [Q25]"," 22. Map — Sal Forests Threatened by 1997 Epidemic\n●\nMap mein '3' se marked jagah Sal forests hain jo 1997 mein ek gambhir mahamari (tree pest) se\nthreatened hui thin — inse ped kamzor hue, forest loss hua. [Q26]\n24. Subtropical Forest — Madhya Pradesh\n●\nSubtropical (tropical dry deciduous) forest ka expansion Madhya Pradesh ke zyadatar hisso mein hai.\n[Q27]\n24. Mahogany — Not Himalayan Vegetation\n●\nJuniper, Silver fir, Spruce Himalayan vegetation ki species hain — Mahogany NAHI hai (ye North/South\nAmerica ki species hai). [Q28]\n25. Khejri — Social Forestry Multipurpose Tree\n●\nSocial forestry ka multipurpose tree example Khejri hai — 'desert ka raja' bhi kehlata hai, frost/drought-\nresistant hai, fuel/fodder/manure sab deta hai. [Q29]\n26. Victoria Falls (Cross-Reference, Africa)\n●\nVictoria Falls Zambezi River par, Zambia-Zimbabwe border par hai (Mozambique se NAHI) — 'Smoke\nthat Thunders' kehlata hai, 1989 mein World Heritage List mein aaya. [Q30]\n27. Lisa (Resin) — Pine Tree Product\n●\nLisa (resin/raal) Uttarakhand ke Pine trees se milta hai — turpentine oil banane mein use hota hai, rural\neconomy ka base hai. [Q31]\n28. Mangrove-State Match Sets (Maharashtra to Odisha)\n●\nMangrove areas ka match: Achra Ratnagiri — Maharashtra, Kundapur — Karnataka, Pichavaram —\nTamil Nadu, Vembanad — Kerala (West Bengal — Sunderbans, Odisha —\nBhitarkanika/Devi/Dhamra/Chilika). [Q32]\n29. Vembanad — Kerala (Not Karnataka)\n●\nSundarbans-WB, Bhitarkanika-Odisha, Pichavaram-TN sahi hain — Vembanad Kerala mein hai\n(Karnataka mein NAHI). [Q33]\n EXAM TRAP — Vembanad — Kerala mein hai, Karnataka mein NAHI (common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n30. Tropical Rainforest — Assam & Kerala\n●\nTropical rainforests Assam aur Kerala mein hain — Western Ghats, Lakshadweep, Andaman-Nicobar,\nupper Assam, TN coast (200cm+ rainfall, short dry season). [Q34]\n31. Dense Deciduous Forest — MP & West Champaran"," ●\nIndia mein dense deciduous forest ka sabse bada area Madhya Pradesh mein hai — district level par\nWest Champaran (Bihar) sabse zyada dense deciduous cover rakhta hai (831.03 sq km) — Kaimur, Gaya,\nNawada se zyada. [Q35, Q36]\n32. Khair — Sub-Tropical Forest Tree\n●\nKhair (Catechu) Sub-tropical forests ka tree hai — Shivalik aur Western Himalaya mein 1000m+ altitude\npar milta hai (Keekar, Acacia bhi is category mein). [Q37]\n33. Highest Forest % State — Mizoram\n●\nIndia State of Forest Report 2023 ke mutabik Mizoram mein forest-area percentage sabse zyada hai —\nHimachal Pradesh, Assam, Andhra Pradesh, Arunachal Pradesh se zyada. [Q38]\n34. Sita Nadi Sanctuary — Sal Forest\n●\nSita Nadi Sanctuary (Chhattisgarh, 553.36 sq km) mein Sal tree plurality mein milta hai — Sal, Teak,\nBamboo sab hain, par Sal forests country mein best mane jaate hain. [Q39]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0008","t":"11 Irrigation and Canals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" IRRIGATION AND CANALS — FULL MIND MAP\n💧\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Pattiseema Project — Godavari-Krishna Link\n2. Canal Project-State Match (Jawai-Rajasthan Trap)\n3. Peninsular India — Pond Irrigation (Assertion-Reason)\n4. Dominant Irrigation Source — Tubewells (Not Wells)\n5. State-wise Irrigation Percentage (Haryana Highest)\n6. Micro-Irrigation Benefits\n7. Protective Irrigation — P.W.P. Concept\n8. Tubewell Irrigation Development (Saryupar Plain, UP)\n9. Groundwater Resources Ranking (UP Highest)\n10. Garland Canal System & River Interlinking Pioneers\n11. Sir Arthur Cotton — South India's Irrigation Pioneer\n12. Irrigation Project Classification (Minor/Medium/Major)\n13. Farakka Canal — Water Capacity & Purpose\n14. Mangalam Project — Kerala\n15. Saran Canal — Gandak River Origin\n16. Indira Gandhi Canal — Harike Barrage & Rivers\n17. Beas Project — Pong Barrage\n18. Gang Canal — Oldest Canal System (1927)\n19. Canal-River Match Set (Upper Bari Doab, Sirhind, Gurgaon)\n20. Statement Verification — Nizam Sagar, Narmada, Penganga\n21. Lower Ganga Canal — Narora Origin\n22. Bihar's Triveni Canal\n23. Hariyali Yojana — Watershed/Water Management Scheme\n24. Watershed Programmes — Ministry Match & IWMP Merger\n25. Drip Irrigation — Advantages\n26. Buckingham Canal — Coromandel Coast Navigation\n27. Water Consumption — Agricultural Sector Highest\n28. Chambal Canal Project — Yamuna/Ganga Basin Dispute\n1. Pattiseema Project — Godavari-Krishna Link\n●\nPattiseema Lift Irrigation Project Godavari river ko Krishna river se jodta hai (river interlinking project).\n[Q1]\n2. Canal Project-State Match (Jawai-Rajasthan Trap)\n●\nGhatprabha Canal — Karnataka, Ukai Canal — Gujarat (Tapti river par), Nira Canal — Maharashtra (Bhima\nki tributary Nira river par) sahi hain — Jawai Project 'Tamil Nadu' mein NAHI hai, ye Rajasthan mein\nhai (Luni ki tributary Jawai river par). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP — Jawai Project — Rajasthan mein hai (Luni ki tributary), Tamil Nadu mein NAHI\n⚠️\n3. Peninsular India — Pond Irrigation (Assertion-Reason)"," ●\nPeninsular India mein talab (pond) irrigation ka major source hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki undulating\nrelief aur hard rock canals/wells khodna mushkil banati hai, aur zyadatar rivers seasonal hain\n(summer mein sookh jaati hain) (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q3]\n4. Dominant Irrigation Source — Tubewells (Not Wells)\n●\n2021-22 data ke mutabik India mein irrigation ka main source Tubewells (47.3%) hai — 'Wells' galat\nstatement hai (tubewell+wells combined 60.5%, canals 24.7%, tanks 2.8%). [Q4]\n5. State-wise Irrigation Percentage (Haryana Highest)\n●\n2011 data ke mutabik cropped-area-under-irrigation % Haryana (83.90%) sabse zyada hai — UP (72.76%),\nMP (28.20%), Maharashtra (16.78%) se zyada. 2015-16 Agriculture Census ke mutabik Chandigarh\n(100%) sabse zyada hai, Punjab (99.6%) dusre number par. [Q5, Q6]\n6. Micro-Irrigation Benefits\n●\nMicro-irrigation ke sahi benefits: fertilizer/nutrient loss kam hoti hai, groundwater level ka receding\nrukta hai — 'dry land farming mein ekmatra means' GALAT hai. [Q7]\n7. Protective Irrigation — P.W.P. Concept\n●\nLife-saving/Protective irrigation P.W.P. (Permanent Wilting Point) par irrigation ko kehte hain — is point\npar plants ke liye moisture insufficient ho jaati hai, irrigation compulsory ban jaata hai. [Q8]\n8. Tubewell Irrigation Development (Saryupar Plain, UP)\n●\nPichhle 25 saalon mein tubewell irrigation ka sabse spectacular development Saryupar Plain (canals ki\nkami ki wajah se) mein hua hai — Ganga-Ghaghra Doab, Ganga-Yamuna Doab, Bundelkhand se zyada.\n[Q9]\n●\nIndia mein Uttar Pradesh mein maximum tubewell-irrigated area (73.9%) hai — UP tubewell+well\nirrigation mein bhi sabse aage hai (10299 thousand hectares tubewell se, 1269 thousand hectares wells\nse). [Q10, Q11, Q12]\n9. Groundwater Resources Ranking (UP Highest)\n●\nIrrigation ke liye available groundwater resources descending order: Uttar Pradesh (41.29 BCM) >\nMaharashtra (15.29 BCM) > West Bengal (10.84 BCM) > Assam (1.97 BCM). [Q13]\n10. Garland Canal System & River Interlinking Pioneers\n●\nGarland Canal System Captain Dineshaw J. Dastur ne propose kiya tha — River interlinking ka concept\nsabse pehle M. Visvesvaraya ne diya, baad mein K.L. Rao ne bhi ek alag project propose ki — dono\nprojects reject kar di gayi thi. [Q14]\n11. Sir Arthur Cotton — South India's Irrigation Pioneer\n●\nSouth India mein irrigation works ka pioneer Sir Arthur Cotton hai — British irrigation engineer, poore\nBritish India mein irrigation-navigation canals banwaye. [Q15]"," 12. Irrigation Project Classification (Minor/Medium/Major)\n●\nProjects classification: Minor (CCA ≤2000 hectares), Medium (2000-10000 hectares), Major (>10000\nhectares) — Minor projects se India ki 62% irrigation potential banti hai (Major+Medium se 38%).\n[Q16]\n13. Farakka Canal — Water Capacity & Purpose\n●\nFarakka Canal (Murshidabad, WB, 1975 mein bana) ki water-carrying capacity 40,000 cusecs hai — Kolkata\nPort (ab Syama Prasad Mookerjee Port) ki navigability improve karne ke liye banayi gayi thi. [Q17]\n14. Mangalam Project — Kerala\n●\nMangalam Irrigation Project Kerala (Palakkad district, Bharathapuzha river system) mein hai. [Q18]\n15. Saran Canal — Gandak River Origin\n●\nSaran Irrigation Canal Gandak river (Balmiki Nagar barrage) se nikaali gayi hai. [Q19]\n16. Indira Gandhi Canal — Harike Barrage & Rivers\n●\nIndira Gandhi Canal Harike Barrage (Firozpur, Punjab) — Satluj aur Beas ke sangam ke paas se nikalti\nhai — length 649km, Sri Ganganagar, Bikaner, Jodhpur, Jaisalmer irrigate karti hai. Water supply\nSatluj, Beas aur Ravi teeno se milti hai (Chenab se NAHI). [Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24]\n17. Beas Project — Pong Barrage\n●\nBeas Project (Punjab-Haryana-Rajasthan joint) Pong barrage se Indira Gandhi Canal ko winter mein\nwater supply maintain karta hai. [Q25]\n18. Gang Canal — Oldest Canal System (1927)\n●\nGang Canal, duniya ke sabse achhe-developed aur puraane canal systems mein se ek hai — Maharaja\nGanga Singh (Bikaner) ne 1927 mein banwaya, Hussainiwala (Firozpur) se Satluj river se nikalti hai. [Q26,\nQ28]\n19. Canal-River Match Set (Upper Bari Doab, Sirhind, Gurgaon)\n●\nCanal-river match: Upper Bari Doab Canal — Ravi, Sirhind Canal — Sutlej, Gurgaon Canal —\nYamuna, Indira Gandhi Canal — Sutlej+Ravi+Beas. [Q27]\n20. Statement Verification — Nizam Sagar, Narmada, Penganga\n●\nSahi statements: Narmada Amarkantak se nikalti hai, Nizam Sagar Manjra river (Godavari tributary)\npar hai, Penganga Godavari ki tributary hai — 'Ghaggar ka paani Indira Gandhi Canal mein use hota\nhai' GALAT hai (Sutlej-Beas-Ravi se hi paani aata hai, Ghaggar se nahi). [Q29]\n21. Lower Ganga Canal — Narora Origin\n●\nLower Ganga Canal Narora (Bulandshahr) se Ganga river se nikalti hai — 1878 mein complete hui thi.\n[Q30]"," 22. Bihar's Triveni Canal\n●\nBihar (north-western part) ki irrigation Triveni Canal se hoti hai — Upper Ganga, Sharda, Eastern Yamuna\nCanal se nahi. [Q31]\n●\nSharda Tributary Command Development Project ke objectives: agricultural production badhaana,\nmultiple-crop cultivation se land-use format change karna, land management reforms — teeno sahi hain\n(CADP ke andar Sharda, Ramganga, Gandak — 3 projects shuru hue the). [Q32]\n23. Hariyali Yojana — Watershed/Water Management Scheme\n●\nHariyali scheme wasteland development ki nayi scheme hai — PM Atal Bihari Vajpayee ne 27 Jan 2003\nko watershed management ke tahat launch kiya — panchayats ke through chalti hai, afforestation ko\nencourage karti hai. Broadly water management se related hai. [Q33, Q34]\n24. Watershed Programmes — Ministry Match & IWMP Merger\n●\nIntegrated Watershed Development Programme ke benefits: soil runoff prevention, rainwater\nharvesting/groundwater recharge, natural vegetation regeneration — 'perennial rivers ko seasonal\nrivers se jodna' benefit mein include NAHI hai. [Q35]\n●\n3 watershed programmes (IWDP, DPAP, DDP) Ministry of Rural Development ke Department of Land\nResources ke through 2008 mein IWMP mein merge hue — koi bhi diya gaya ministry-match sahi NAHI\nhai (Agriculture/Environment/Rural Development directly nahi), NWDPRA Ministry of Agriculture ka\ninitiative hai. [Q36]\n25. Drip Irrigation — Advantages\n●\nDrip irrigation ke advantages: weed mein kami, soil erosion mein kami — 'soil salinity mein kami' iska\ndirect advantage NAHI hai (options mein diya gaya galat combination hai). [Q37]\n26. Buckingham Canal — Coromandel Coast Navigation\n●\nBuckingham Canal (freshwater navigation canal, length 796km) Coromandel Coast ke parallel hai —\nAndhra Pradesh ke Kakinada se Tamil Nadu ke Parangipettai (Chidambaram ke paas) tak, Chennai port se\nbackwaters ko jodta hai. [Q38]\n27. Water Consumption — Agricultural Sector Highest\n●\nIndia mein Agricultural sector mein pani ki khapat sabse zyada hai — total rainfall se water availability\n~3880 BCM/year hai. [Q39]\n28. Chambal Canal Project — Yamuna/Ganga Basin Dispute\n●\nChambal Canal Irrigation Project Yamuna Basin se related hai (smaller-basin perspective se) — lekin\nGanga Basin se bhi related hai (larger-basin perspective se, kyunki Chambal-Yamuna dono Ganga\nmein milti hain) — isliye ye disputed question hai, dono answers sahi maane jaate hain. [Q40]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0009","t":"12.i Narmada Valley Project","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NARMADA VALLEY PROJECT — FULL MIND\n🌊\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Sardar Sarovar Dam — Location & Beneficiary States\n2. Maximum Beneficiary State — Madhya Pradesh\n3. Medha Patekar & Narmada Bachao Andolan\n4. Dams NOT on Narmada (Ban Sagar Trap)\n5. Indira Sagar Dam — Location & Harsud Submersion\n6. Omkareshwar Project\n7. Scale of the Narmada Project — 30/135/3000 Dams\n1. Sardar Sarovar Dam — Location & Beneficiary States\n●\nSardar Sarovar Dam (height 163m) Narmada river par, Navgaon (Gujarat) ke paas bana hai — capacity\n1450 MW. Iske beneficiary states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh hain — ye India\nki 4-state partnership wali irrigation project hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. Maximum Beneficiary State — Madhya Pradesh\n●\nSardar Sarovar Dam se Madhya Pradesh ko sabse zyada faayda (65.18% Narmada water) milta hai —\nGujarat, Rajasthan, Odisha se zyada. [Q5]\n3. Medha Patekar & Narmada Bachao Andolan\n●\nSardar Sarovar Project ke khilaaf Medha Patekar hain — unhone Narmada Bachao Andolan found kiya\ntha, jo affected logon ke liye ladaai leta hai. Ye Andolan Sardar Sarovar Dam ki height badhane ka virodh\nkarta hai — Gujarat aur M.P. ke beech dispute Supreme Court tak gaya tha. [Q6, Q11]\n4. Dams NOT on Narmada (Ban Sagar Trap)\n●\nBargi, Omkareshwar, Indira Sagar — sab Narmada par bane 30 major dams ki series mein hain — Ban\nSagar dam Son river par hai (Narmada ki NAHI). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Ban Sagar — Son river par hai, Narmada ke NAHI (common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n5. Indira Sagar Dam — Location & Harsud Submersion\n●\nIndira Sagar Dam Narmada river par, Punasa (Khandwa district, M.P.) mein hai — 2.70 lakh hectares\nirrigation, 1000 MW power capacity. Iske construction se Harsud town (Khandwa, M.P.) 2004 mein\nsubmerge ho gaya tha. [Q8, Q9]\n6. Omkareshwar Project\n●\nOmkareshwar Project Narmada river, Khandwa district (M.P.) mein hai. [Q10]"," 7. Scale of the Narmada Project — 30/135/3000 Dams\n●\nPoori Narmada Valley Project (M.P.-Gujarat-Maharashtra ki joint project) mein total 30 major, 135 medium,\n3000 minor dams banane ka plan hai — Sardar Sarovar Project (SSP) aur Narmada Sagar Project (NSP\n- yaani Indira Sagar) is series ke 2 mega dams hain. Foundation stone Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru ne 1961\nmein rakha tha. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0010","t":"12.ii Bhakra Nangal Dam","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" BHAKRA NANGAL DAM — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Bhakra Nangal — Joint Project of 3 States\n2. River & Command Area\n1. Bhakra Nangal — Joint Project of 3 States\n●\nBhakra Nangal Punjab, Haryana aur Rajasthan ka joint project hai — command area Himachal Pradesh,\nPunjab, Haryana, Rajasthan mein expand hota hai (isliye 4th state H.P. bhi coverage mein aata hai, par\ncore partnership 3 states ki hai). [Q1, Q2]\n2. River & Command Area\n●\nBhakra Nangal Dam Satluj river par bana hai — do dams (Bhakra aur Nangal) ke naam par project ka naam\npada hai. [Q3]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0011","t":"12.iii Dam at River Cauvery","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" DAM AT THE RIVER CAUVERY — FULL MIND\n🏞️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Shivasamudram — India's 2nd Oldest Hydropower Station\n2. Cauvery River Water Dispute (CRWD)\n1. Shivasamudram — India's 2nd Oldest Hydropower Station\n●\nIndia ka sabse purana hydropower plant Darjeeling (West Bengal, 1897 commissioned) hai —\nShivasamudram (Cauvery river, Karnataka, 1902 mein commission hua) dusra sabse purana hai. [Q1,\nQ2]\n2. Cauvery River Water Dispute (CRWD)\n●\nCauvery River Water Dispute Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Kerala aur Puducherry se related hai — Supreme\nCourt ke 2018 decision ke mutabik total 740 TMC paani mein se Karnataka 284.75, Tamil Nadu 404.25,\nKerala 30, Puducherry 7 TMC feet allocate kiya gaya. [Q3, Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0012","t":"12.iv Nagarjuna Sagar Dam","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NAGARJUNA SAGAR DAM — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Nagarjuna Sagar — River & Location\n2. Multipurpose Project Details\n1. Nagarjuna Sagar — River & Location\n●\nNagarjuna Sagar dam Krishna river par hai — jab question pucha gaya tha tab Andhra Pradesh mein\nmaana jaata tha, ab Telangana-Andhra Pradesh border (Nalgonda-Palnadu districts) par hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3,\nQ5]\n2. Multipurpose Project Details\n●\nNagarjuna Sagar Krishna river par ek multipurpose scheme hai — 1967 mein complete hua tha,\nNalgonda, Khammam, Guntur, Suryapet districts ko irrigation deta hai. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0013","t":"12.ix Miscellaneous Project","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MISCELLANEOUS PROJECTS — FULL MIND\n🏗️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Maharashtra Dam-River Match (Ukai-Tapi, Jayakawadi-Godavari, Disputed)\n2. Tawa Project — Tawa River (Not Krishna, Wrong-Pair)\n3. Project-State Match (Hirakud-Odisha, Haldia-WB, Tarapur-Maharashtra, Kudremukh-Karnataka)\n4. Himachal Dam on Sutlej — Checks Silt Flow into Bhakra\n5. Chukha Dam — India-Bhutan Hydro Cooperation\n6. Project-River Match (Bhakhra-Satluj, Hirakud-Mahanadi, Idukki-Periyar, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna)\n7. Telugu Ganga — TN, AP, Maharashtra, Karnataka Joint Venture\n8. Telugu Ganga — Supplies Water to Madras (Chennai)\n9. Jawaharlal Nehru — 'Temples of Modern India'\n10. Dam-River Match (Almatti-Krishna, Mettur-Cauvery, Gandhi Sagar-Chambal, Sardar Sarovar-Narmada)\n11. Almatti Dam — Krishna River, Karnataka\n12. Project-State Match (Mettur-TN, Mayurakshi-WB, Nagarjuna Sagar-AP, Hirakud-Odisha)\n13. Multipurpose Project Match (Idukki-Periyar, Matatila-Betwa, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna, Pochampad-Godavari)\n14. River Valley Match (Shivsamudram-Cauvery, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna, Jayakwadi-Godavari, Tehri-Bhagirathi)\n15. Multi-Statement Verification (Rihand-Sone, Hirakud-Mahanadi, Tungabhadra-AP/Karnataka, Maithan-Barakar)\n16. Kalpong — Andaman & Nicobar's First Hydro-Electric Project\n17. Sidrapong — India's Oldest Hydropower Plant (1897, Darjeeling)\n18. First Hydropower Station Commissioned at Darjeeling\n19. Dam-State Match (Farakka-WB, Ghataprabha-Karnataka, Hirakud-Odisha, Kakrapar-Gujarat)\n20. Dam-State Match (Rihand-UP, Ukai-Gujarat, Hirakud-Odisha, Koyna-Maharashtra)\n21. Kolleru Lake — Krishna-Godavari Valley (Not Just Krishna, Wrong-Pair)\n22. Kalagarh Dam — Ramganga River, Uttarakhand\n23. Ramganga Project Specs — Dam Length 715m (Not 8258m)\n24. Tawa Project — Hoshangabad (Narmadapuram), MP\n25. Pong Dam — Beas River, Himachal Pradesh\n26. Meja Dam — Kothari River, Rajasthan\n27. Tulbul Project — Jhelum River (Indus Treaty Dispute)\n28. Baglihar — Chenab River, J&K (Pakistan-World Bank Dispute)\n29. Baglihar Hydroelectric Project — Located in J&K\n30. Irrigation Project Match (Damanganga-Gujarat, Girna-Maharashtra, Pamba-Kerala)\n31. Tapovan-Vishnugarh Projects — Uttarakhand (Dhauliganga River)\n32. Mahakali Treaty — India & Nepal (1996)\n33. Rana Pratap Sagar — Rajasthan (Not MP, Wrong-Pair)\n34. Kalpasar Project — Gujarat (Gulf of Khambhat)\n35. Chambal Project — Rajasthan & MP (Not Punjab-Haryana)\n36. Suil River Project — Himachal Pradesh (Baira Suil, Chamba)\n37. Sivasamudram — Karnataka (Not Kerala, Wrong-Pair)\n38. Dam-River Match Repeats (Nangal-Sutlej, Sardar Sarovar-Narmada, Hirakud-Mahanadi)\n39. Teesta Low Dam Project III — West Bengal\n40. Teesta Hydropower Project — Sikkim\n41. Multipurpose Project-River Match (Rihand-Son, Rani Laxmibai-Betwa, Tehri-Bhagirathi, Ramganga-Ramganga)\n42. Rani Laxmibai Dam Project — Betwa River (Rajghat Dam, Lalitpur)\n43. Dulhasti Power Station — Chenab River, J&K (390 MW)"," 44. Project-River Match (Dulhasti-Chenab, Indira Gandhi Canal-Sutlej, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna, Ukai-Tapti)\n45. Reservoir-State Match (Bhadra-Karnataka, Bhavani Sagar-TN, Gandhi Sagar-MP, Rana Pratap Sagar-Rajasthan)\n46. Tilaiya Dam — Barakar River (Not Konar, Wrong-Pair)\n47. Nagarjuna Sagar — Krishna River (Not Godavari, Wrong-Pair)\n48. Govind Ballabh Pant Sagar — UP (Pipri, Sonbhadra, Rihand River)\n49. Govind Ballabh Sagar — Uttar Pradesh (Repeat)\n50. Gandak Project — Bihar & UP (India-Nepal Joint Venture)\n51. Kishau Dam — Uttarakhand & HP Primary Beneficiaries (Disputed)\n52. River Valley-River Match (Tilaiya-Barakar, Panchet-Damodar, Rana Pratap Sagar-Chambal, Matatila-Betwa)\n53. Project-River Match (Rihand-Rihand, Nagarjun Sagar-Krishna, Pochampad-Godavari, Matatila-Betwa)\n54. Shivasamudram — Not for Irrigation (Electricity, 1902)\n55. Babli Project — Maharashtra (Godavari, Disputed by AP)\n56. Dam-River Match (Doolhasti-Chenab, Gandhisagar-Chambal, Ukai-Tapi, Tawa-Tawa)\n57. Malampuzha Dam — Kerala (Malampuzha River, Built by Tamil Nadu)\n58. Singrauli Small Hydro Power Project — Uttar Pradesh\n59. Cheruthoni Dam — Periyar River, Kerala\n60. Rajasthan Irrigation Projects (Sidhmukh, Narmada, Jawai, Jakham — District Match)\n61. Kol Dam Project — Sutlej River (NTPC)\n62. Mandal Dam (North Koel Project) — Jharkhand\n63. Aliyar, Isapur, Kangsabati — All Water Reservoirs\n64. Kelo Irrigation Project — Chhattisgarh's PM Irrigation Scheme\n65. Interstate Water Disputes Tribunal Match (Mahadayi-3, Godavari-5, Narmada-4, Mahanadi-2)\n66. Large Dams State Ranking (MP > Gujarat > Rajasthan > Telangana > AP)\n67. Reservoir-State Match (Ghataprabha-Karnataka, Indira Sagar-MP, Maithon-Jharkhand)\n68. Mangdechhu Power Plant — Bhutan (Inaugurated by PM Modi, 2019)\n1. Maharashtra Dam-River Match (Ukai-Tapi, Jayakawadi-Godavari, Disputed)\n●\nSahi match: Ukai — Tapi, Jayakawadi — Godavari, Khadakwasla — Mutha, Maurakshi/Mayurakshi\n— Mayurakshi River — UPPSC ki initial answer key mein galti thi, isliye disputed question hai. [Q1]\n2. Tawa Project — Tawa River (Not Krishna, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nMidanpur Canal-Kangsabati, Mettur Dam-Cauvery, Ukai Project-Tapi sahi hain — 'Tawa Project-Krishna\nRiver' GALAT hai (Tawa Project asal mein Tawa river par hai). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP — Tawa Project — Tawa River par hai, Krishna River par NAHI\n⚠️\n3. Project-State Match (Hirakud-Odisha, Haldia-WB, Tarapur-Maharashtra, Kudremukh-\nKarnataka)\n●\nMatch: Hirakud Project — Odisha, Haldia Refinery — West Bengal, Tarapur Nuclear Station —\nMaharashtra, Kudremukh Hills — Karnataka. [Q3]\n4. Himachal Dam on Sutlej — Checks Silt Flow into Bhakra\n●\nHimachal Pradesh mein Sutlej par ban raha dam Bhakra dam mein silt (gaad) ke flow ko rokne ke liye\nbanaya jaa raha hai — silt dam ko kamzor karti hai aur uski age kam kar deti hai. [Q4]\n5. Chukha Dam — India-Bhutan Hydro Cooperation"," ●\nChukha Dam Project Bhutan mein Wang Chu (Raidak) river ke upper reaches par hai — 1974 mein\nIndia ke fully-funded unit ke roop mein construction shuru hua (60% grant + 40% loan). [Q5]\n6. Project-River Match (Bhakhra-Satluj, Hirakud-Mahanadi, Idukki-Periyar, Nagarjuna\nSagar-Krishna)\n●\nMatch: Bhakhra — Satluj, Hirakud — Mahanadi, Idukki — Periyar, Nagarjuna Sagar — Krishna.\n[Q6]\n7. Telugu Ganga — TN, AP, Maharashtra, Karnataka Joint Venture\n●\nTelugu Ganga project Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra aur Karnataka ka joint venture hai\n— Krishna river ke paani se Chennai ko drinking water supply karta hai. [Q7]\n8. Telugu Ganga — Supplies Water to Madras (Chennai)\n●\nTelugu Ganga project se Madras (Chennai) shehar ko paani milta hai. [Q8]\n9. Jawaharlal Nehru — 'Temples of Modern India'\n●\nJawaharlal Nehru ne multipurpose river valley projects ko 'aadhunik Bharat ke mandir' kaha tha. [Q9]\n10. Dam-River Match (Almatti-Krishna, Mettur-Cauvery, Gandhi Sagar-Chambal, Sardar\nSarovar-Narmada)\n●\nMatch: Almatti Dam — Krishna river, Mettur Dam — Cauvery river, Gandhi Sagar Dam — Chambal\nriver, Sardar Sarovar Dam — Narmada river. [Q10]\n11. Almatti Dam — Krishna River, Karnataka\n●\nAlmatti Dam Krishna river par bana hai — irrigation-hydroelectricity dono ke liye multipurpose\nproject hai. [Q11]\n12. Project-State Match (Mettur-TN, Mayurakshi-WB, Nagarjuna Sagar-AP, Hirakud-\nOdisha)\n●\nMatch: Mettur — Tamil Nadu, Mayurakshi — West Bengal, Nagarjuna Sagar — Andhra Pradesh,\nHirakud — Odisha — Mayurakshi project mein Tilpara (Suri ke paas) barrage aur Jharkhand mein Canada\ndam shamil hai. [Q12]\n13. Multipurpose Project Match (Idukki-Periyar, Matatila-Betwa, Nagarjuna Sagar-\nKrishna, Pochampad-Godavari)\n●\nMatch: Idukki — Periyar (Kerala), Matatilla — Betwa (UP-MP joint), Nagarjuna Sagar — Krishna\n(Telangana-AP border), Pochampad — Godavari (Telangana). [Q13]\n14. River Valley Match (Shivsamudram-Cauvery, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna, Jayakwadi-\nGodavari, Tehri-Bhagirathi)\n●\nMatch: Shivsamudram — Cauvery (Karnataka), Nagarjuna Sagar — Krishna, Jayakwadi — Godavari\n(Maharashtra), Tehri — Bhagirathi (Uttarakhand). [Q14]"," 15. Multi-Statement Verification (Rihand-Sone, Hirakud-Mahanadi,\nTungabhadra-AP/Karnataka, Maithan-Barakar)\n●\nSab 4 statements sahi hain: Rihand Dam Sone ki sahayak nadi (Rihand river) par hai, Hirakud\nMahanadi par hai, Tungabhadra project AP-Karnataka ka joint venture hai, Maithan Dam Barakar\nriver (Damodar ki sahayak) par hai (1957 mein bana). [Q15]\n16. Kalpong — Andaman & Nicobar's First Hydro-Electric Project\n●\nKalpong Hydro-Electric Power Project Andaman aur Nicobar Islands ka pehla hydro-electric project tha\n— Kalpong river par bana hai. [Q16]\n17. Sidrapong — India's Oldest Hydropower Plant (1897, Darjeeling)\n●\nIndia ka pehla/sabse purana hydropower station 1897 mein Sidrapong (Darjeeling ke paas, WB) mein\ncommissioned hua — dusra Shivasamudram (Karnataka, Cauvery river, 1902) mein bana. [Q17, Q18]\n18. First Hydropower Station Commissioned at Darjeeling\n●\nIndia ka pehla hydropower station Darjeeling (Sidrapong) mein commissioned hua tha. [Q18]\n19. Dam-State Match (Farakka-WB, Ghataprabha-Karnataka, Hirakud-Odisha, Kakrapar-\nGujarat)\n●\nMatch: Farakka — West Bengal (Ganga river, Hugli navigable banane ke liye), Ghataprabha —\nKarnataka, Hirakud — Odisha, Kakrapar — Gujarat (Tapti river). [Q19]\n20. Dam-State Match (Rihand-UP, Ukai-Gujarat, Hirakud-Odisha, Koyna-Maharashtra)\n●\nMatch: Rihand — UP (Govind Ballabh Pant Sagar, Sonbhadra district ke Pipri gaon ke paas), Ukai —\nGujarat (Tapi river), Hirakud — Odisha, Koyna — Maharashtra. [Q20]\n21. Kolleru Lake — Krishna-Godavari Valley (Not Just Krishna, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nGovind Sagar-Satluj, Ukai Reservoir-Tapi, Wular Lake-Jhelum sahi hain — 'Kolleru Lake-Krishna'\nGALAT hai (Kolleru dono Krishna-Godavari valleys ke beech hai, natural flood-balancing reservoir\ndono rivers ke liye). [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP — Kolleru Lake — Krishna AUR Godavari dono valleys ke beech hai, sirf Krishna se\n⚠️\nNAHI\n22. Kalagarh Dam — Ramganga River, Uttarakhand\n●\nKalagarh Dam (Ramganga Dam bhi kehte hain) Ramganga river (Uttarakhand) par bana hai — length\n715m, height 128m. [Q22]\n23. Ramganga Project Specs — Dam Length 715m (Not 8258m)\n●\nRamganga project (Kalagarh, Pauri Garhwal district) ki sahi specs: hydropower capacity 198 MW, location\nGarhwal-Uttarakhand, irrigated area ~6 lakh hectares (designed 5.90 lakh hectares) — 'dam ki length\n8258 metre' GALAT hai (asal length 715 metre hai). [Q23]"," EXAM TRAP — Ramganga (Kalagarh) Dam ki length 715 metre hai, 8258 metre NAHI\n⚠️\n24. Tawa Project — Hoshangabad (Narmadapuram), MP\n●\nTawa project Hoshangabad (ab Narmadapuram) district, MP mein Tawa river par hai — construction\n1958 mein shuru, 1978 mein complete hua — Tawa Reservoir Satpura National Park aur Bori Wildlife\nSanctuary ke beech hai. [Q24]\n25. Pong Dam — Beas River, Himachal Pradesh\n●\nPong Dam (Beas Dam bhi kehte hain) Beas river (South-Western Himachal Pradesh) par bana hai —\nMaharana Pratap Sagar Lake banayi, jo Bird Sanctuary declare hui. [Q25]\n26. Meja Dam — Kothari River, Rajasthan\n●\nMeja Dam Kothari river (Bhilwara district, Rajasthan) par hai — Kothari, Banas ki sahayak hai,\nAravali ke eastern slopes se nikalti hai, irrigation ke liye mukhya roop se use hoti hai. [Q26]\n27. Tulbul Project — Jhelum River (Indus Treaty Dispute)\n●\nTulbul Shipping Project Jammu-Kashmir mein Jhelum river par hai — 1984 mein India ne Wular Lake\nke mouth par propose kiya, 1987 mein Pakistan ne Indus Water Treaty 1960 ka ullanghan bataya.\n[Q27, Q28]\n28. Baglihar — Chenab River, J&K (Pakistan-World Bank Dispute)\n●\nBaglihar Hydroelectric Power Project Chenab river (Ramban district, J&K) par run-of-the-river power\nproject hai — Pakistan ne World Bank ke saamne issue uthaya tha. [Q29]\n29. Baglihar Hydroelectric Project — Located in J&K\n●\nBaglihar project Jammu and Kashmir mein sthith hai. [Q30]\n30. Irrigation Project Match (Damanganga-Gujarat, Girna-Maharashtra, Pamba-Kerala)\n●\nSab 3 sahi hain: Damanganga — Gujarat (Valsad district, Madhuban Dam), Girna — Maharashtra\n(Nashik district), Pamba — Kerala (Pathanamthitta district). [Q31]\n31. Tapovan-Vishnugarh Projects — Uttarakhand (Dhauliganga River)\n●\nTapovan-Vishnugarh hydroelectric projects Dhauliganga river (Chamoli district), Uttarakhand mein\nhain. [Q32]\n32. Mahakali Treaty — India & Nepal (1996)\n●\nMahakali Treaty (February 1996) India aur Nepal ke beech signed hui — Mahakali/Sharda river ke\nwater-sharing se related, Sharda Barrage/Tanakpur Barrage/Pancheshwar Project shamil. [Q33]\n33. Rana Pratap Sagar — Rajasthan (Not MP, Wrong-Pair)"," ●\nKalpakkam-TN, Narora-UP, Tarapore-Maharashtra sahi hain — 'Rana Pratap Sagar-MP' GALAT hai\n(Rana Pratap Sagar Rajasthan ke Rawatbhata mein Chambal river par hai — MP mein Gandhi Sagar\nproject hai jo bhi Chambal par hai). [Q34]\n EXAM TRAP — Rana Pratap Sagar — Rajasthan (Rawatbhata) mein hai, MP mein NAHI\n⚠️\n34. Kalpasar Project — Gujarat (Gulf of Khambhat)\n●\nKalpasar Project Gujarat mein hai — Gulf of Khambhat ke paar dam banake tidal power aur\nfreshwater reservoir (irrigation/drinking/industrial ke liye) banane ki yojna. [Q35]\n35. Chambal Project — Rajasthan & MP (Not Punjab-Haryana)\n●\nMahi Bajaj Sagar-Gujarat/Rajasthan, Indira Gandhi Canal-Rajasthan/Punjab sahi hain — 'Chambal Project-\nRajasthan,Punjab,Haryana' GALAT hai (Chambal Project Rajasthan aur Madhya Pradesh se related\nhai). [Q36]\n36. Suil River Project — Himachal Pradesh (Baira Suil, Chamba)\n●\nBaira Suil Hydroelectric Power Project Suil river (Ravi ki sahayak, Chamba district, Himachal Pradesh)\npar hai. [Q37]\n37. Sivasamudram — Karnataka (Not Kerala, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nJawahar Sagar-Rajasthan, Nagarjuna Sagar-AP/Telangana, Gandhi Sagar-MP sahi hain — 'Sivasamudram-\nKerala' GALAT hai (Sivasamudram Karnataka mein hai). [Q38]\n EXAM TRAP — Sivasamudram — Karnataka mein hai, Kerala mein NAHI\n⚠️\n38. Dam-River Match Repeats (Nangal-Sutlej, Sardar Sarovar-Narmada, Hirakud-\nMahanadi)\n●\nNangal Dam-Sutlej, Sardar Sarovar-Narmada, Hirakud Dam-Mahanadi sahi hain — 'Nagarjuna Sagar-\nGodavari' GALAT hai (asal mein Krishna river par hai). [Q39, Q48]\n39. Teesta Low Dam Project III — West Bengal\n●\nTeesta Low Dam Project (TLDP)-III aur IV West Bengal se related hain — pehle 2 projects (I, II) Sikkim\nse related hain — Teesta river Sikkim se nikal ke WB se hoke Bangladesh mein Brahmaputra se milti hai.\n[Q40]\n40. Teesta Hydropower Project — Sikkim\n●\nTeesta hydropower project Sikkim mein hai. [Q41]\n41. Multipurpose Project-River Match (Rihand-Son, Rani Laxmibai-Betwa, Tehri-\nBhagirathi, Ramganga-Ramganga)\n●\nMatch: Rihand project — Son (tributary Rihand river), Rani Laxmibai Dam — Betwa, Tehri Dam —\nBhagirathi, Ramganga Project — Ramganga. [Q42]"," 42. Rani Laxmibai Dam Project — Betwa River (Rajghat Dam, Lalitpur)\n●\nRajghat Dam Project (Lalitpur, UP, Betwa river par) 'Rani Laxmibai Dam Project' ke naam se jaana jaata\nhai. [Q43]\n43. Dulhasti Power Station — Chenab River, J&K (390 MW)\n●\nDulhasti (390 MW hydroelectric plant) Kishtwar district, J&K mein Chenab river par hai. [Q44]\n44. Project-River Match (Dulhasti-Chenab, Indira Gandhi Canal-Sutlej, Nagarjuna Sagar-\nKrishna, Ukai-Tapti)\n●\nDulhasti-Chenab, Indira Gandhi Canal-Sutlej, Ukai-Tapti sahi hain — 'Nagarjuna Sagar-Cauvery' GALAT\nhai (asal mein Krishna river par hai). [Q45]\n45. Reservoir-State Match (Bhadra-Karnataka, Bhavani Sagar-TN, Gandhi Sagar-MP, Rana\nPratap Sagar-Rajasthan)\n●\nMatch: Bhadra — Karnataka, Bhavani Sagar — Tamil Nadu, Gandhi Sagar — Madhya Pradesh, Rana\nPratap Sagar — Rajasthan. [Q46]\n46. Tilaiya Dam — Barakar River (Not Konar, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nSardar Sarovar-Narmada, Gandhi Sagar-Chambal, Nagarjuna Sagar-Krishna sahi hain — 'Tilaiya Dam-\nKonar river' GALAT hai (Tilaiya Dam asal mein Barakar river, Koderma district, Jharkhand mein\nhai). [Q47]\n EXAM TRAP — Tilaiya Dam — Barakar river par hai, Konar river par NAHI\n⚠️\n47. Nagarjuna Sagar — Krishna River (Not Godavari, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nNangal-Sutlej, Sardar Sarovar-Narmada, Hirakud-Mahanadi sahi hain — 'Nagarjuna Sagar-Godavari'\nGALAT hai (Krishna river par hai). [Q48]\n48. Govind Ballabh Pant Sagar — UP (Pipri, Sonbhadra, Rihand River)\n●\nGovind Ballabh Pant Sagar reservoir Pipri, Sonbhadra district, Uttar Pradesh mein hai — Rihand river\n(Son ki sahayak) par bana hai. [Q49, Q50]\n49. Govind Ballabh Sagar — Uttar Pradesh (Repeat)\n●\nGovind Ballabh Sagar/Pant Sagar Uttar Pradesh mein sthith hai. [Q50]\n50. River-Dam Match (Betwa-Matatila, Mahanadi-Hirakud, Chambal-GandhiSagar, Tapi-\nKakrapar)\n●\nMatch: Betwa — Matatila, Mahanadi — Hirakud, Chambal — Gandhi Sagar Dam, Tapi — Kakrapar.\n[Q51]\n51. Mata Tila Dam — Betwa River (Lalitpur, UP, 1958)\n●\nMata Tila Dam Betwa river par hai — Lalitpur district, UP mein, 1958 mein bana. [Q52]"," 52. Gandak Project — Bihar & UP (India-Nepal Joint Venture)\n●\nGandak Project India aur Nepal ka joint venture hai (4 Dec 1959 ke agreement ke tahat) — Bihar aur\nUttar Pradesh participating Indian states hain — Gandak Barrage 1968-69 mein bana, Nepal/UP/Bihar\nteeno ko irrigation deta hai, Nepal ko electricity bhi. [Q53]\n53. Kishau Dam — Uttarakhand & HP Primary Beneficiaries (Disputed)\n●\nKishau Dam Project (Tons river par, Yamuna ki sahayak, HP-Uttarakhand boundary) ke primary\nbeneficiaries Uttarakhand aur Himachal Pradesh hain — Haryana, Delhi, Rajasthan, UP ko bhi faayda\nhota hai — diye gaye options mein sab galat the, isliye disputed question hai. [Q54]\n54. River Valley-River Match (Tilaiya-Barakar, Panchet-Damodar, Rana Pratap Sagar-\nChambal, Matatila-Betwa)\n●\nMatch: Tilaiya Dam — Barakar, Panchet Hill Dam — Damodar, Rana Pratap Sagar Dam — Chambal,\nMatatila Dam — Betwa. [Q55]\n55. Project-River Match (Rihand-Rihand, Nagarjun Sagar-Krishna, Pochampad-Godavari,\nMatatila-Betwa)\n●\nMatch: Rihand Project — Rihand river, Nagarjun Sagar Project — Krishna, Pochampad Project —\nGodavari, Matatila Project — Betwa. [Q56]\n56. Shivasamudram — Not for Irrigation (Electricity, 1902)\n●\nBhavani Sagar, Krishnaraj Sagar, Bhakra Nangal irrigation ke liye hain — Shivasamudram (1902 mein\nbana, Cauvery river, Karnataka) sirf electricity generation ke liye tha, irrigation ke liye NAHI. [Q57]\n57. Babli Project — Maharashtra (Godavari, Disputed by AP)\n●\nBabli Project (controversial reservoir project) Maharashtra ne Godavari river par banaya — Andhra\nPradesh ne is par vivad khada kiya. [Q58]\n58. Dam-River Match (Doolhasti-Chenab, Gandhisagar-Chambal, Ukai-Tapi, Tawa-Tawa)\n●\nMatch: Doolhasti — Chenab, Gandhisagar — Chambal, Ukai — Tapi, Tawa — Tawa river. [Q59]\n59. Malampuzha Dam — Kerala (Malampuzha River, Built by Tamil Nadu)\n●\nMalampuzha Dam (Kerala ka sabse bada reservoir, Palakkad ke paas) Malampuzha river (Bharathpuzha ki\nsahayak) par hai — Tamil Nadu government ne banaya tha, baad mein Palakkad district Kerala mein\naa gaya. [Q60]\n60. Singrauli Small Hydro Power Project — Uttar Pradesh\n●\nSingrauli Small Hydro Power Project Sonbhadra district, Uttar Pradesh mein hai — 2 units, 4 MW each.\n[Q61]\n61. Cheruthoni Dam — Periyar River, Kerala"," ●\nCheruthoni Dam Periyar river, Kerala mein hai — 138 metre tall concrete gravity dam. [Q62]\n62. Rajasthan Irrigation Projects (Sidhmukh, Narmada, Jawai, Jakham — District Match)\n●\nMatch: Sidhmukh Project — Hanumangarh & Churu, Narmada Project — Jalore & Barmer, Jawai\nProject — Jalore/Pali/Jodhpur, Jakham Project — Udaipur & Pratapgarh. [Q63]\n63. Kol Dam Project — Sutlej River (NTPC)\n●\nKol Dam Project Sutlej river par hai — NTPC (National Thermal Power Corporation) ne banaya. [Q64]\n64. Mandal Dam (North Koel Project) — Jharkhand\n●\n5 Jan 2019 ko PM Modi ne North Koel (Mandal Dam) project ki foundation Medininagar, Palamu\ndistrict, Jharkhand mein rakhi — North Koel (Son ki sahayak) river par, Palamu-Garhwa districts\nmein. [Q65]\n65. Aliyar, Isapur, Kangsabati — All Water Reservoirs\n●\nTeeno water reservoirs hain — Aliyar (Pollachi-Valparai ke beech, Annamalai Hills), Isapur (Penganga\nriver, Maharashtra, earth-fill dam), Kangsabati (West Bengal ka 2nd largest earthen dam). [Q66]\n66. Kelo Irrigation Project — Chhattisgarh's PM Irrigation Scheme\n●\nKelo Irrigation Project (Chhattisgarh) Prime Minister Irrigation Project ke tahat shamil hai — Raigarh\ndistrict mein Kelo river (Mahanadi ki sahayak) par implement ho rahi hai. [Q67]\n67. Interstate Water Disputes Tribunal Match (Mahadayi-3, Godavari-5, Narmada-4,\nMahanadi-2)\n●\nMatch (states involved): Mahadayi Water Disputes Tribunal — 3, Godavari Water Disputes Tribunal —\n5 (ab 7), Narmada Water Disputes Tribunal — 4, Mahanadi Water Disputes Tribunal — 2. [Q68]\n68. Large Dams State Ranking (MP > Gujarat > Rajasthan > Telangana > AP)\n●\nLarge dams ki sankhya ke hisaab se descending order: Madhya Pradesh > Gujarat > Rajasthan >\nTelangana > Andhra Pradesh — sabse bade dams Maharashtra, MP, Gujarat mein hain. [Q69]\n69. Reservoir-State Match (Ghataprabha-Karnataka, Indira Sagar-MP, Maithon-\nJharkhand)\n●\nSahi match: Ghataprabha — Karnataka, Gandhi Sagar — Madhya Pradesh, Indira Sagar — Madhya\nPradesh, Maithon — Jharkhand — diye gaye galat options (Telangana/AP/Chhattisgarh) mein se 3 pairs\nsahi nahi the. [Q70]\n70. Mangdechhu Power Plant — Bhutan (Inaugurated by PM Modi, 2019)\n●\n2019 mein PM Narendra Modi ne Mangdechhu Hydropower Plant, Bhutan mein inaugurate kiya. [Q71]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0014","t":"12.v Hirakund Dam","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" HIRAKUD DAM — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Hirakud Dam — River, Location & Scale\n1. Hirakud Dam — River, Location & Scale\n●\nHirakud dam Mahanadi river par, Odisha (Sambalpur town se 15km door) bana hai — main dam length\n4801m, 155635 hectares Kharif aur 108385 hectares Rabi irrigation deta hai. [Q1, Q2]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0015","t":"12.vi Chambal Valley Project","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" CHAMBAL VALLEY PROJECT — FULL MIND\n🏞️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Jet Stream Facts (Assertion-Reason)\n2. Chambal Project — Joint Rajasthan-MP Venture\n3. Gandhi Sagar Dam\n4. Dams NOT Related to Chambal (Gobind/Pant Sagar Traps)\n5. Rana Pratap Sagar Dam\n1. Jet Stream Facts (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nJet streams westerly (west-se-east) winds hain, easterly NAHI (Assertion galat hai) — jet streams 300-500\nkm/h speed se behti hain (Reason sahi hai). WWII ke dauran confirm hui thi, lekin scientists ne pehle hi unka\nexistence propose kiya tha. [Q1]\n2. Chambal Project — Joint Rajasthan-MP Venture\n●\nChambal river Janapav Hills, Mhow (Dr. Ambedkar Nagar, M.P.) se nikalti hai — Itawa (U.P.) ke paas\nYamuna mein milti hai. Chambal Project Rajasthan aur Madhya Pradesh ka joint project hai — isme\nGandhi Sagar (M.P.), Rana Pratap Sagar aur Jawahar Sagar (Rajasthan) shamil hain. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Gandhi Sagar Dam\n●\nGandhi Sagar Dam, 4 Chambal Valley Projects mein se pehla hai — Mandsaur district, Madhya Pradesh\nmein, 62.17m height ka masonry gravity dam. Construction 1957 mein shuru, power generation Nov 1960 se.\n[Q4]\n4. Dams NOT Related to Chambal (Gobind/Pant Sagar Traps)\n●\nGandhi Sagar aur Jawahar Sagar Chambal Valley Project se related hain — Gobind Sagar (Bhakra-Nangal\nDam se banta hai, Himachal Pradesh) aur Govind Vallabh Pant Sagar (Sonebhadra, U.P.) Chambal se\nNAHI related hain. [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — Gobind Sagar (Bhakra-Nangal) aur G.V. Pant Sagar (Sonebhadra) — dono naam-mein-\n⚠️\nmilte-julte hain par Chambal se related NAHI\n5. Rana Pratap Sagar Dam\n●\nRana Pratap Sagar Dam Chambal river par, Rawatbhata (Rajasthan) mein hai — construction 1953 mein\nshuru, 1970 mein inaugurate hua. [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0016","t":"12.vii Tehri Dam Project","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" TEHRI DAM PROJECT — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tehri Dam — Rivers, Location & Objectives\n2. Confluence Point — Bhagirathi-Bhilangana\n1. Tehri Dam — Rivers, Location & Objectives\n●\nTehri Dam Bhagirathi river par, Tehri Garhwal district (Uttarakhand) mein bana hai — Bhilangana\nriver bhi Bhagirathi mein milti hai (old Tehri ke paas), dono ka paani dam mein rukta hai. Objectives:\nfloodwater impound, hydroelectricity, irrigation. Project 1972 mein Planning Commission se clear hua,\nconstruction 1978 se shuru hua. 'Ganga' bhi sahi answer maana jaata hai jab 'Bhagirathi' option na ho\n(Bhagirathi Ganga ka source hai). [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. Confluence Point — Bhagirathi-Bhilangana\n●\nMap-labeling type question: Tehri dam ka site Bhagirathi aur Bhilangana rivers ke confluence par hai (na\nki sirf ek river par). [Q5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0017","t":"12.viii Damodar Valley Project","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" DAMODAR VALLEY PROJECT — FULL MIND\n🏞️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tilaiya, Maithon, Belpahari — Barakar River Dams\n2. Damodar — 'River of Sorrow' (Assertion-Reason)\n3. DVC Establishment & India's First Multipurpose Project\n1. Tilaiya, Maithon, Belpahari — Barakar River Dams\n●\nTilaiya Dam Barakar river (Koderma district, Jharkhand) par hai — 1953 mein complete, length ~366m.\nMaithon, Belpahari aur Tilaiya teeno Barakar river (Damodar ki main tributary) par bane the —\nDamodar Valley Project ke first phase mein. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Damodar — 'River of Sorrow' (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nDamodar river ko DVC se pehle 'River of Sorrow' ya 'Sorrow of Bengal' kaha jaata tha (Assertion sahi)\nkyunki upper reaches mein rapidly aur lower reaches mein sluggishly behti thi — isse major floods aur\nsedimentation hoti thi (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q3]\n3. DVC Establishment & India's First Multipurpose Project\n●\nDamodar Valley Corporation (DVC) 1948 mein establish hui thi (Act No. XIV of 1948) — 7 July 1948 ko\nIndia ki pehli multipurpose river valley project ban gayi. DVC West Bengal aur Bihar (ab Jharkhand)\nmein operate karta hai — 1947 tak Central, WB, Bihar governments ke beech agreement ho chuka tha. [Q4,\nQ5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0018","t":"13 Agriculture","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" AGRICULTURE — FULL MIND MAP\n🌾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Permaculture vs Conventional Chemical Farming\n2. Zero Tillage — Advantages\n3. Fertigation — Benefits & Limitation\n4. Eco-Friendly Agriculture Practices\n5. M.S. Randhawa — Agriculture History Author\n6. Agro-Climatic vs Agro-Ecological Regions (15 vs 20)\n7. Upper Gangetic Agro-Climatic Region\n8. P. Sengupta & Sdasyuk — 60 Micro Agricultural Regions\n9. Dry Zone — Second Green Revolution Potential\n10. Seed Replacement Rate — Implementation Constraints\n11. First Agricultural University — Pantnagar (1960)\n12. Safe Grain Storage — 14% Moisture Limit\n13. Land Use Classification (Net Sown/Forest/Other)\n14. Double Cropping vs Intercropping vs Mixed Farming\n15. Parallel Cropping — Wheat+Mustard Example\n16. Sikkim — Lowest Agricultural Land %\n17. Characteristics of Indian Agriculture (Small Holdings)\n18. Low Productivity Causes (Overcrowding, Small Holdings)\n19. Green Revolution — Environmental Cost (Assertion-Reason)\n20. Cooperative Farming — Not a Low-Productivity Cause\n21. Largest Average Landholding — Rajasthan\n22. Agriculture as Livelihood (Not Just Profession)\n23. Pulses — Rainfed Area Statistics (90%)\n24. Fertilizer Consumption Leaders (UP & Andhra Pradesh)\n25. Green Manure Crops — Nitrogen Content Ranking\n26. Balanced Fertilizers — Purpose\n27. High Agricultural Productivity Areas — South India\n28. Groundwater Resources — UP Richest\n29. Contract Farming — Punjab Pioneer\n30. Green Agriculture — Integrated Management Concept\n31. Globalization's Impact on Indian Agriculture\n32. Seed Village Concept\n33. Agmark — Quality Certification (1937 Act)\n34. Landholding Size Classification (Marginal to Big)\n35. Conservation Agriculture — Components\n36. Pathways to Increase Agricultural Productivity\n37. Agriculture Census 2015-16 — Key Statistics\n1. Permaculture vs Conventional Chemical Farming\n●\nPermaculture farming monoculture ko discourage karti hai, mulching bahut important hai, aur semi-\narid regions mein bhi effective hai — chemical farming mein monoculture dominant hai. 'Permaculture\nsemi-arid regions mein achhi tarah possible nahi hai' GALAT statement hai. [Q1]"," 2. Zero Tillage — Advantages\n●\nZero tillage ke sab 3 advantages sahi hain: residue jalaye bina wheat sowing, direct paddy seeding\n(nursery ke bina), carbon sequestration se greenhouse effect kam. [Q2]\n3. Fertigation — Benefits & Limitation\n●\nFertigation (drip system se paani mein fertilizer milana) ke fayde: alkalinity control, nutrients ki increased\navailability, chemical nutrients ki leaching mein kami — 'Rock Phosphate ka efficient application'\nGALAT hai (super phosphorus se phosphate precipitation hoti hai, isliye avoid karna chahiye). [Q3]\n4. Eco-Friendly Agriculture Practices\n●\nEco-friendly practices sab 4 hain: crop diversification, legume intensification (nitrogen-fixing),\ntensiometer use (soil moisture estimate), vertical farming. [Q4]\n5. M.S. Randhawa — Agriculture History Author\n●\n'The History of Indian Agriculture' M.S. Randhawa (Mohinder Singh Randhawa) ne likhi hai — Green\nRevolution mein bhi bada role tha. [Q5]\n6. Agro-Climatic vs Agro-Ecological Regions (15 vs 20)\n●\nIndia ko resource development ke liye 15 agro-climatic regions mein baanta gaya hai — National Bureau\nof Soil Survey ke mutabik 20 agro-ecological zones hain (17/18/19 GALAT hain). Western Himalaya cold\narid ecoregion ka coverage area, Western Himalaya region se zyada hai. [Q6, Q8, Q9]\n7. Upper Gangetic Agro-Climatic Region\n●\nUpper Gangetic region mein Central-Western UP shamil hai — irrigation intensity ~131%, cropping\nintensity ~142% — 4 sub-zones (central-western plain, SW semi-arid, western plain, central plain) hain.\n[Q7]\n8. P. Sengupta & Sdasyuk — 60 Micro Agricultural Regions\n●\n1968 mein Registrar General of Census ne Dr. P. Sengupta aur Dr. Galina Sdasyuk ke study ke basis par\nIndia ko 60 micro agricultural regions mein baanta. [Q10]\n9. Dry Zone — Second Green Revolution Potential\n●\nIndia ke dry zone mein agrarian economy hai (Assertion sahi) — dusri Green Revolution ki bhi bahut\npotential hai (Reason sahi), lekin Reason, Assertion ki sahi explanation NAHI hai. [Q11]\n10. Seed Replacement Rate — Implementation Constraints\n●\nSeed Replacement Rate ke wider implementation mein constraint: low-value/high-volume crops ke liye\nquality seeds ki demand-supply gap — 'National Seeds Policy nahi hai' aur 'private sector companies ki\nparticipation nahi hai' dono GALAT statements hain (2002 mein hi National Seed Policy ban chuki thi).\n[Q12]"," 11. First Agricultural University — Pantnagar (1960)\n●\nIndia ka pehla Agricultural University G.B. Pant University of Agriculture and Technology, Pantnagar\n(Uttarakhand) hai — 1960 mein Jawaharlal Nehru ne 'UP Agricultural University' ke naam se\ninaugurate kiya tha, baad mein UP ke pehle CM ke naam par rename hua. [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n12. Safe Grain Storage — 14% Moisture Limit\n●\nFAO standards ke mutabik safe storage ke liye harvest ke time grain moisture content 14% se zyada nahi\nhoni chahiye. [Q16]\n13. Land Use Classification (Net Sown/Forest/Other)\n●\nIndia ka land-use classification (2021-22): Net Area Sown 46.01%, Forest Area 23.49%, Other Areas\n30.5%. [Q17]\n14. Double Cropping vs Intercropping vs Mixed Farming\n●\nDouble cropping — do crops alag-alag time par (same year mein) same land par — Intercropping — do\nya zyada crops SAATH mein same field mein. Mixed farming — animals aur crops dono ek saath rear\nkarna (equal emphasis). [Q18, Q19, Q20]\n15. Parallel Cropping — Wheat+Mustard Example\n●\nParallel cropping (dono crops nutrients ke liye compete nahi karte, ek dusre par asar nahi daalte) ka example\nWheat + Mustard hai. [Q21]\n16. Sikkim — Lowest Agricultural Land %\n●\nGiven states (Punjab, Haryana, UP, Sikkim) mein Sikkim mein sabse kam agricultural land (10% se kam)\nhai — hilly, forest-covered state hai. [Q22]\n17. Characteristics of Indian Agriculture (Small Holdings)\n●\nIndian agriculture ki characteristics: nature par over-dependence, low productivity, crop diversity —\n'large farms ka dominance' GALAT hai (India mein small/marginal holdings ka dominance hai). [Q23]\n18. Low Productivity Causes (Overcrowding, Small Holdings)\n●\nIndian agriculture mein low productivity ke reasons: overcrowding, small land holding, traditional\npractices — sab teeno sahi hain. [Q24]\n19. Green Revolution — Environmental Cost (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nGreen Revolution technology ne traditional agriculture ko modern-scientific banaya (Assertion sahi) — lekin\nisme social/environmental costs shamil NAHI the — ye statement GALAT hai (environmental cost\nlong-term sustainability ke liye threat maana jaata hai) — dono statements sahi hain, par R, A ki sahi\nexplanation nahi hai. [Q25]\n20. Cooperative Farming — Not a Low-Productivity Cause"," ●\nLow productivity ke reasons: population pressure, disguised unemployment, small land holding —\n'Cooperative farming' iska cause NAHI hai (ye actually development ka ek tareeka hai). [Q26]\n21. Largest Average Landholding — Rajasthan\n●\nIndia mein operational holdings ka average size Rajasthan mein sabse bada hai (2015-16) —\nMaharashtra, UP se zyada. [Q27]\n22. Agriculture as Livelihood (Not Just Profession)\n●\nIndia mein agriculture ko 'means of livelihood' (aajeevika ka saadhan) maana jaata hai — maximum\nmanpower isme lagi hai, par GDP mein sirf chhota hissa deti hai. [Q28]\n23. Pulses — Rainfed Area Statistics (90%)\n●\nSahi statement: India mein pulses ka ~90% area rainfed hai — 'pulses ka share 2 dashak mein double\nhua' GALAT hai (asal mein ghata hai), 'rice cultivation ka 15% share' GALAT hai (~29% hai), 'rice\n34% gross cropped area' GALAT hai (~23.7% hai). [Q29]\n24. Fertilizer Consumption Leaders (UP & Andhra Pradesh)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt (2013-14) fertilizer ke 2 sabse bade consumers — Uttar Pradesh aur Andhra Pradesh\nthe — abhi (2021-22) UP, Maharashtra, MP top-3 hain. [Q30]\n25. Green Manure Crops — Nitrogen Content Ranking\n●\nNitrogen content ranking (green manure crops): Cow pea (0.49%) > Sunhemp (0.43%) > Dhaincha\n(0.42%) > Guar (0.34%). Newly-improved arid land ke liye Lobia (cow pea) sabse suitable green manure\ncrop hai. [Q31, Q32]\n26. Balanced Fertilizers — Purpose\n●\nBalanced fertilizers production badhaane, quality improve karne, aur soil productivity maintain karne\n— teeno purpose ke liye use hote hain. [Q33]\n27. High Agricultural Productivity Areas — South India\n●\nSouth India mein high agricultural productivity Tamil Nadu coast mein hai (Andhra Pradesh coast, Surat-\nGujarat, Satara-Kolhapur-Maharashtra bhi high productivity areas hain). [Q34]\n28. Groundwater Resources — UP Richest\n●\nReplenishable groundwater resources mein Uttar Pradesh sabse rich state hai (2024 data: UP 72.84 bcm,\nMP 35.90, AP 27.80, WB 25.89). [Q35]\n29. Contract Farming — Punjab Pioneer\n●\nIndia mein contract farming introduce karne ka pioneer Punjab hai. [Q36]\n30. Green Agriculture — Integrated Management Concept"," ●\n'Green Agriculture' involves: integrated pest management, integrated nutrient supply, integrated natural\nresource management — sirf organic farming ya sirf horticulture NAHI. [Q37]\n31. Globalization's Impact on Indian Agriculture\n●\n1991 mein Narasimha Rao Government ne Globalization introduce ki — impacts: cash crops par emphasis,\nincome inequality mein growth, subsidies mein kami — 'Climate change' iska direct impact NAHI tha\n(galat option). [Q38]\n32. Seed Village Concept\n●\nSeed Village Concept ka objective: farmers ko quality-seed-production training dena, taaki appropriate\ntime aur affordable cost par doosre farmers ko bhi quality seeds mil sakein. [Q39]\n33. Agmark — Quality Certification (1937 Act)\n●\nAgmark quality certification mark hai (Agricultural Produce Grading and Marking Act, 1937 ke tahat)\n— 1938 se India mein lagu hai. [Q40]\n34. Landholding Size Classification (Marginal to Big)\n●\nLandholding size classification (2015-16): Marginal — <1 hectare, Small — 1-2 hectares, Semi-medium\n— 2-4 hectares, Medium — 4-10 hectares, Big — >10 hectares. [Q41]\n35. Conservation Agriculture — Components\n●\nConservation Agriculture ke sahi components: minimum tillage adopt karna, crop residues se soil surface\ncover karna, spatial/temporal crop rotation apnaana — 'monoculture avoid karna' aur 'plantation\ncrops avoid karna' iske components NAHI hain. [Q42]\n36. Pathways to Increase Agricultural Productivity\n●\nAgriculture productivity badhaane ke sab tareeke sahi hain: efficient irrigation, quality seeds, pesticides\nuse, fertilizers use — sab combined. [Q43]\n37. Agriculture Census 2015-16 — Key Statistics\n●\n2015-16 Agriculture Census ke sahi facts: small+marginal farmers 86.2% (kul farmers ka) hain lekin sirf\n47.3% land hold karte hain, Rajasthan total-land ke hisaab se 1st hai, Maharashtra total-farmers ke\nhisaab se 3rd hai — sab teeno statements sahi hain. [Q44]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0019","t":"14 Green Revolution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" GREEN REVOLUTION — FULL MIND MAP\n🌱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Green Revolution Start — 1966-67 (Sixties)\n2. M.S. Swaminathan — Evergreen Revolution\n3. Norman Borlaug — Global Father of Green Revolution\n4. Green Revolution Definition — High-Yield Variety Programme\n5. Wheat — Biggest Beneficiary Crop\n6. Mexican Wheat — Main Crop Used\n7. Record Wheat Yield — 2000 kg/hectare\n8. Second Green Revolution — Objectives\n9. Green Revolution Components (Seeds, Irrigation, Electrification, Roads)\n10. Regional Disparities (Assertion-Reason)\n11. Rainbow Revolution — Umbrella Concept\n12. Revolution-Sector Match Set (White, Blue, Grey)\n13. Pink Revolution — Onion\n14. Golden/Grey/Yellow/Black Revolution Match Set\n15. Blue Revolution — Fisheries (Not Poultry)\n16. Zero Till Seed-cum-Fertilizer Drill — Pantnagar\n17. Commercial vs Non-Commercial Crops\n1. Green Revolution Start — 1966-67 (Sixties)\n●\nGreen Revolution 1966-67 mein shuru hui (7th decade/sixties) — first stage Haryana, Punjab, Western\nUP mein tha, 1981 tak jaari raha. [Q1]\n2. M.S. Swaminathan — Evergreen Revolution\n●\n'Evergreen Revolution' term M.S. Swaminathan (India ke Green Revolution ke pita) ne use kiya —\necological harm ke bina productivity permanently badhaana iska matlab hai. Dusri Green Revolution ke\nsteps propose kiye: bio-fertilizers+chemical fertilizers, rainwater harvesting, agricultural economic zones.\n[Q2]\n3. Norman Borlaug — Global Father of Green Revolution\n●\nNorman Ernest Borlaug USA se the — Mexico mein semi-dwarf, high-yield, disease-resistant wheat develop\nki, global context mein Green Revolution ke pita hain (India ke liye M.S. Swaminathan) — Nobel Peace\nPrize aur Padma Vibhushan (2006) mile. [Q3, Q4, Q5]\n4. Green Revolution Definition — High-Yield Variety Programme\n●\nGreen Revolution ka matlab High Yield Variety (HYV) programme hai — high-yielding seeds, modified\nequipment, chemical fertilizers badhaana. 1966-67 mein Rockefeller Foundation (USA) ki madad se shuru\nhua. [Q6, Q7]\n5. Wheat — Biggest Beneficiary Crop"," ●\nGreen Revolution ka sabse bada beneficiary crop — Wheat (production+productivity dono mein) hai —\nRice dusre number par. Independence ke baad India ne Wheat production mein sabse zyada progress ki.\n[Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]\n6. Mexican Wheat — Main Crop Used\n●\nGreen Revolution mein Mexican Wheat (Borlaug ke International Maize and Wheat Improvement\nCenter se) main crop tha. [Q12]\n7. Record Wheat Yield — 2000 kg/hectare\n●\nGreen Revolution ke result mein wheat yield 2000 kg/hectare (record figure, pehle se 3x) tak pahunchi —\n2023-24 mein ye 3559 kg/hectare ho gayi hai. [Q13]\n8. Second Green Revolution — Objectives\n●\nSecond Green Revolution ke objectives: seed-water-fertilizer technology ko un areas tak extend karna jo\npehli Green Revolution se benefit nahi hue, aur agriculture ko animal husbandry/social forestry/fishing\nke saath integrate karna — 'wheat-rice production aur badhaana' aur 'naye crops (jo pehle use nahi\nhue) ki yield badhaana' iske objectives NAHI hain. [Q14]\n9. Green Revolution Components (Seeds, Irrigation, Electrification, Roads)\n●\nGreen Revolution ke sab 4 components sahi hain: high-yielding seeds, irrigation, rural electrification,\nrural roads/marketing. [Q15]\n10. Regional Disparities (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nGreen Revolution ne food grain production badhaya (Assertion sahi) — India mein regional disparities bhi\nbadhi hain (Reason sahi) — kyunki Revolution sirf irrigated/high-potential rain-fed areas mein failii, baaki\nareas peeche reh gaye — dono statements sahi hain par R, A ka explanation nahi hai. [Q16]\n11. Rainbow Revolution — Umbrella Concept\n●\n28 July 2000 ko National Agricultural Policy mein Rainbow Revolution concept introduce hua — ye crop\ncultivation, horticulture, forestry, fishery, poultry, animal husbandry, food processing ka integrated\ndevelopment hai — sab alag-alag 'colour revolutions' (Green, White, Yellow, Blue, Red, Golden, Grey) ko\ncover karta hai. [Q17]\n12. Revolution-Sector Match Set (White, Blue, Grey)\n●\nMatch set: Food production growth — Green Revolution, Milk — White Revolution, Fisheries — Blue\nRevolution, Fertilizers — Grey Revolution. [Q18]\n13. Pink Revolution — Onion\n●\nPink Revolution Onion (pyaaz) se related hai — Black — Petroleum, Red — Tomato/Meat, Blue —\nFisheries, Yellow — Oilseed. [Q19, Q20]\n14. Golden/Grey/Yellow/Black Revolution Match Set"," ●\nMatch set: Golden Revolution — Horticulture/Honey, Grey Revolution — Fertilizers, Yellow\nRevolution — Oilseed Production, Black Revolution — Petroleum Production. [Q21]\n15. Blue Revolution — Fisheries (Not Poultry)\n●\nBlue Revolution aquaculture/pisciculture (fisheries) se related hai — 'Blue Revolution-Poultry' GALAT\npair hai (aquaculture ka poultry se koi relation nahi hai). [Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27, Q29]\n EXAM TRAP — Blue Revolution — Fisheries se hai, Poultry se NAHI (bahut common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n16. Zero Till Seed-cum-Fertilizer Drill — Pantnagar\n●\n'Zero Till Seed-cum-Fertilizer Drill' G.B. Pant University, Pantnagar ne develop ki — bina seedbed\npreparation ke direct paddy-harvest-ke-baad sowing enable karti hai, diesel/labour/time bachati hai. [Q28]\n17. Commercial vs Non-Commercial Crops\n●\nCommercial (cash) crops: Sugarcane, Cotton, Banana — Bajra (millet) commercial crop NAHI hai —\ncommercialization ka level state-wise alag hota hai (jaise rice Haryana-Punjab mein commercial hai, Odisha\nmein subsistence crop hai). [Q30]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0020","t":"15.i Rabi Crops","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" RABI CROPS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rabi Season — Oct-Nov Sow, Mar-Apr Harvest\n2. Rabi vs Kharif vs Zaid — Crop Classification\n3. Wheat Cultivation Requirements (10-25°C, 50-75cm)\n4. Cash Crop Definition (Wheat Excluded)\n5. 1998 Wheat Import — Australia Agreement\n6. Wheat Production Data (2020-21 to 2023-24)\n7. Top-3 Wheat Producers (UP, Punjab/MP, Haryana)\n8. UP — Highest Wheat Producer (35.34 MT)\n9. Wheat Varieties (Mahi Sugandha is Rice, Not Wheat)\n10. UP — Rank 1 in Wheat & Sugarcane\n11. Sonora-64 — Induced Mutation Variety\n12. Dwarfing Genes (Norin-10 for Wheat)\n13. Macaroni Wheat — Rainfed Conditions Suitable\n14. Wheat Variety Names (Raj 3077, Pusa Sindhu Ganga, UP-308)\n15. Wheat Production Trend (2006-07 to 2009-10 — Upward)\n16. IGKV Raipur — Hybrid Varieties (Indira Sona is Rice)\n17. Wheat Diseases — Rust (3 Types)\n18. Kalyana Sona & Variety Identification (Arjun/Sonalika=Wheat)\n19. UPAS-120 — Arhar Variety for Double Cropping with Wheat\n20. CRI Stage — Critical Irrigation Point for Wheat\n21. Triticale — Wheat×Rye Hybrid\n22. Punjab-Haryana-UP Wheat Belt (Assertion-Reason)\n23. Karnal Bunt — Fungal Wheat Disease (Tilletia Indica)\n24. Macaroni Wheat — Botanical Name (Triticum durum)\n25. Butachlor — Herbicide (Not Pesticide/Fungicide)\n1. Rabi Season — Oct-Nov Sow, Mar-Apr Harvest\n●\nRabi crop October-November mein boyi jaati hai, March-April mein kaati jaati hai — main Rabi crops:\nWheat, Barley, Mustard, Sesame, Peas, Potatoes. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. Rabi vs Kharif vs Zaid — Crop Classification\n●\nKharif crops (June-July boyi, Oct-Nov kaati): Millets, Cotton, Soyabean, Sugarcane, Paddy, Maize,\nMoong, Groundnut — Zaid crops (March-July): Muskmelon, Watermelon, Cucurbitaceae family\nvegetables. Masoor, Gram, Pea Rabi crops hain — Groundnut/Maize/Paddy Kharif hain, Lady's\nfinger/Carrot/Radish Rabi NAHI hain. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7]\n3. Wheat Cultivation Requirements (10-25°C, 50-75cm)\n●\nWheat ke liye moderate temperature (10-25°C) aur moderate rainfall (50-75cm evenly distributed)\nchahiye — 2023-24 mein 31.8 million hectare area mein ugta hai. [Q8]\n4. Cash Crop Definition (Wheat Excluded)"," ●\nCash crops: Sugarcane, Cotton, Jute, Tobacco, Oilseeds — Wheat, Rice food crops hain, cash crops\nNAHI. [Q9, Q10]\n5. 1998 Wheat Import — Australia Agreement\n●\n1998 mein Bharat sarkar ne Australia ke saath 15 lakh tonnes wheat import karne ka agreement kiya —\nkam production ki sambhavna dekhte hue. [Q11]\n6. Wheat Production Data (2020-21 to 2023-24)\n●\n2020-21 mein wheat production 109.5 million tonnes tha — 2023-24 mein badhkar 113.3 million tonnes\nho gaya. [Q12]\n7. Top-3 Wheat Producers (UP, Punjab/MP, Haryana)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt top-3: UP, Punjab, Haryana — 2023-24 mein ab UP, Madhya Pradesh, Punjab top-3\nhain. [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n8. UP — Highest Wheat Producer (35.34 MT)\n●\n2023-24 mein wheat production ranking: UP (35.34 MT) > MP (22.58 MT) > Punjab (17.74 MT) — 2015-\n16 mein UP (25.43), MP (17.69), Punjab (16.08) the. [Q16]\n9. Wheat Varieties (Mahi Sugandha is Rice, Not Wheat)\n●\n'Mahi Sugandha' Basmati Rice ki variety hai (Wheat ki NAHI) — non-sticky elongated grains. [Q17]\n EXAM TRAP — Mahi Sugandha — Rice ki variety hai, Wheat ki NAHI\n⚠️\n10. UP — Rank 1 in Wheat & Sugarcane\n●\nEconomic Survey 2024-25 (2023-24 data) ke mutabik UP Wheat aur Sugarcane production mein pehle\nnumber par hai. [Q18]\n11. Sonora-64 — Induced Mutation Variety\n●\nSonora-64 IARI mein induced mutation se develop hui thi — 5 dwarf wheat varieties (Lerma Rojo 64-\nA, Sonora-63, Sonora 64, Mayo 64, S227) mein se ek. [Q19]\n12. Dwarfing Genes (Norin-10 for Wheat)\n●\nDwarfing genes: Wheat — Norin-10, Rice — Dee-Gee-Woo-gen, Maize — Opaque-2. [Q20]\n13. Macaroni Wheat — Rainfed Conditions Suitable\n●\nMacaroni wheat rainfed conditions mein sabse suitable hai — botanical naam Triticum durum. [Q21]\n14. Wheat Variety Names (Raj 3077, Pusa Sindhu Ganga, UP-308)"," ●\nWheat varieties: Raj 3077 (late-sown, 36-40 quintal/hectare), Pusa Sindhu Ganga (HD 2967, IARI se),\nUP-308 (Mexican dwarf, Darbhanga-Bihar mein use) — baaki varieties: Sonalika, Arjun, Kundan, Amar,\nBhawani, Chandrika, Deshratna, Kanchan. [Q22, Q23, Q24]\n15. Wheat Production Trend (2006-07 to 2009-10 — Upward)\n●\n2006-07 se 2009-10 tak wheat production upward trend mein tha (75.81 → 78.57 → 80.68 → 80.80\nmillion tonnes) — 2023-24 tak 113.3 MT tak pahuncha. [Q25]\n16. IGKV Raipur — Hybrid Varieties (Indira Sona is Rice)\n●\nIndira Gandhi Krishi Vishwavidyalaya, Raipur ki wheat varieties: Ratan, Kanishka, Ambar, Vidya,\nMavanti — 'Indira Sona' rice ki variety hai (wheat ki NAHI). [Q26]\n EXAM TRAP — Indira Sona — rice ki variety hai, IGKV ki wheat variety NAHI\n⚠️\n17. Wheat Diseases — Rust (3 Types)\n●\nWheat ki main disease Rust hai — 3 types: Yellow Rust, Brown Rust, Black Rust. [Q27]\n18. Kalyana Sona & Variety Identification (Arjun/Sonalika=Wheat)\n●\nKalyana Sona high-yielding wheat variety hai — Sonalika, Arjun bhi wheat hain — Jaya, Padma rice ki\nvarieties hain. [Q28, Q29]\n19. UPAS-120 — Arhar Variety for Double Cropping with Wheat\n●\nUPAS-120 pigeon pea (Arhar) ki variety hai jo wheat ke saath double cropping ke liye suitable hai.\n[Q30]\n20. CRI Stage — Critical Irrigation Point for Wheat\n●\nC.R.I. Stage (Crown Root Initiation) sowing ke 20-25 din baad irrigation ka most critical stage hai wheat\nke liye — is stage par moisture-kami se tillering kam, chhote earheads, aur yield significantly ghat jaati hai.\n[Q31]\n21. Triticale — Wheat×Rye Hybrid\n●\nTriticale Wheat aur Rye (rai) ke beech ka cross/hybrid hai. [Q32]\n22. Punjab-Haryana-UP Wheat Belt (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nPunjab, Haryana, UP major wheat producing states hain (Assertion sahi) — well-drained fertile soil, 10-\n15°C winter temperature, 75cm rainfall zaroori hai (Reason bhi sahi hai) — par R, A ki sahi explanation\nNAHI hai. [Q33]\n23. Karnal Bunt — Fungal Wheat Disease (Tilletia Indica)\n●\nKarnal Bunt wheat ki fungal disease hai (Tilletia Indica se hoti hai) — pehli baar 1931 mein identify hui\nthi. [Q34]"," 24. Macaroni Wheat — Botanical Name (Triticum durum)\n●\nMacaroni wheat ka botanical naam Triticum durum hai. [Q35]\n25. Butachlor — Herbicide (Not Pesticide/Fungicide)\n●\nButachlor herbicide hai — Chlorpyrifos aur Quinolphos pesticide hain, Carbendazim fungicide hai.\n[Q36]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0021","t":"15.ii Kharif Crops","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" KHARIF CROPS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rice — Origin (South-East Asia), Ideal Climate\n2. Rice Cultivation Pattern (100cm Isohyet, UP Largest Area)\n3. System of Rice Intensification (SRI) — Madagascar Origin\n4. Kharif vs Rabi vs Zaid Classification\n5. Chief Food Crop — Rice (Largest Cropped Area)\n6. Largest Cropped Area — Rice (47.8M Hectares)\n7. UP — Largest Rice Cultivation Area\n8. Rice Bowl of India — Krishna-Godavari Delta\n9. Punjab — Highest Rice Productivity (4193 kg/ha)\n10. Rice Variety Identification (Jawala Not a Rice Variety)\n11. Aman/Aus/Boro — Rice Season Varieties (Bengal)\n12. Pusa Sugandha-5 & Barani Deep — Rice Varieties\n13. Pusa RH-10 — Hybrid Basmati Variety\n14. Basmati Seed Ratio — 15-20 kg/hectare\n15. Punjab — Rice Exporter Despite Not Leading Producer\n16. Rice Production Trends & State Rankings (Multi-Year)\n17. Rice Biofertilizers — Blue-Green Algae\n18. East vs West Coast Rainfall (Assertion-Reason)\n19. Stagnant Cropped Area — Rice (Not Oilseeds/Pulses/Sugarcane)\n20. Top-4 Rice Producers — Historical Sets\n21. Surplus Rice Producer — Andhra Pradesh (Historical)\n22. Rice Cultivation Rainfall Threshold — 100cm\n23. UP — Largest Hybrid Rice Area\n24. Zaid Crops — Moong/Urad, Fodder\n25. Rice — Transplanted Crop\n26. Crop-State Match — 'None' Answer Trap (Multi-Question)\n27. Paddy — NOT Helpful in Nitrogen Fixation\n28. Jowar — Not a Cash Crop\n29. Kharif Cropped-Area Trends (Rice Highest, Cotton>Sugarcane)\n1. Rice — Origin (South-East Asia), Ideal Climate\n●\nRice ki origin South-East Asia mein hui thi — 25°C se zyada temperature aur 100cm se zyada rainfall\nchahiye. [Q1, Q5]\n2. Rice Cultivation Pattern (100cm Isohyet, UP Largest Area)\n●\nEastern/Southern states mein saal mein 2-3 rice crops hoti hain — 100cm rainfall ka isohyet rice\nproduction ki western limit decide karta hai — UP mein sabse zyada area (12.33%), Bihar ka contribution\n5.99% hai. [Q2]\n3. System of Rice Intensification (SRI) — Madagascar Origin"," ●\nSRI (1980s, Madagascar mein origin) mein alternate wetting-drying hoti hai — iske fayde: kam seed\nrequirement, kam methane production, kam electricity consumption (sab teen sahi hain). [Q3]\n4. Kharif vs Rabi vs Zaid Classification\n●\nKharif (June-July boyi, Sept-Oct kaati): Rice, Millet, Cotton, Soyabean, Sugarcane, Maize, Groundnut,\nRed Chillies — Cotton, Groundnut, Rice Kharif hain (Wheat Rabi hai). Lentil, Linseed, Mustard Rabi\nhain — Soyabean Kharif hai. [Q4, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n5. Chief Food Crop — Rice (Largest Cropped Area)\n●\nRice India ki chief food crop hai (Wheat dusre number par). [Q9]\n6. Largest Cropped Area — Rice (47.8M Hectares)\n●\nEconomic Survey 2024-25 ke mutabik Rice sabse bada cropped area (47.8 million hectares) rakhta hai —\nWheat 31.8 million hectares. [Q10]\n7. UP — Largest Rice Cultivation Area\n●\n2022-23 data ke mutabik UP mein rice cultivation ka sabse bada area (5.90 million hectares) hai — per-\nhectare average production 2013-14 mein 2416 kg tha, 2023-24 mein 2882 kg/hectare ho gaya. [Q11, Q12]\n8. Rice Bowl of India — Krishna-Godavari Delta\n●\n'Rice Bowl of India' Krishna-Godavari delta region hai (Andhra Pradesh) — Rayalseema is delta region\npar extend hota hai. [Q13]\n9. Punjab — Highest Rice Productivity (4193 kg/ha)\n●\n2022-23 ke mutabik Punjab mein rice ki sabse zyada productivity (4193 kg/hectare) hai. [Q14, Q34, Q35]\n10. Rice Variety Identification (Jawala Not a Rice Variety)\n●\nRice varieties: Jamuna, Karuna, Jaya, Kanchi, Jagannath, Krishna, Kaveri, Hansa, Vijaya, Padma,\nAnnapurna, Bala, Ratna — 'Jawala' rice ki variety NAHI hai — Jaya, Padma, Krishna teeno rice ki\nimproved varieties hain. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n11. Aman/Aus/Boro — Rice Season Varieties (Bengal)\n●\nBengal rice categories: Aman (June-July boyi, Nov-Dec kaati, winter crop), Aus/Kar (May-June boyi,\nSept-Oct kaati, autumn crop), Boro/Dalua (Nov-Dec boyi, Mar-Apr kaati, summer crop). [Q18]\n12. Pusa Sugandha-5 & Barani Deep — Rice Varieties\n●\nPusa Sugandha-5 (aromatic variety), Barani Deep, Narendra Sankar, Narendra Shuska Samrat, Lalmati sab\nrice ki varieties hain. [Q19, Q20]\n13. Pusa RH-10 — Hybrid Basmati Variety"," ●\nPusa RH-10 Basmati Rice ki hybrid variety hai (PHB-71, Ganga, Suruchi, KRH-2, Sahyadri-4 bhi\nhybrid varieties hain). [Q21]\n14. Basmati Seed Ratio — 15-20 kg/hectare\n●\nBasmati rice transplanting ke liye proper seed ratio 15-20 kg/hectare hai. [Q22]\n15. Punjab — Rice Exporter Despite Not Leading Producer\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Punjab rice ka major exporter tha lekin production mein leading NAHI tha (Assertion\nsahi, Reason galat) — 2023-24 mein Telangana leading producer, UP dusre, WB teesre number par. [Q23]\n16. Rice Production Trends & State Rankings (Multi-Year)\n●\nWest Bengal ab teesra sabse bada rice producer hai (2023-24 data) — pehle question mein Assertion sahi,\nReason galat tha, ab data ke mutabik alag ho sakta hai. Current top-3: Telangana, UP, WB (jab pehle\npoocha gaya tab AP/WB/Punjab/UP top-4 the). [Q24, Q28, Q29, Q33, Q40, Q41]\n17. Rice Biofertilizers — Blue-Green Algae\n●\nRice crop ke liye biofertilizer: Blue-green algae (Azospirillum, Phosphobacteria, Azolla bhi use hote\nhain). [Q25]\n18. East vs West Coast Rainfall (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nEast coast west coast se zyada rice produce karta hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin East coast mein zyada\nrainfall hone ka Reason GALAT hai (asal mein West coast mein zyada rainfall hoti hai, narrow coast\naur high mountains ki wajah se). [Q26]\n EXAM TRAP — West coast mein actually zyada rainfall hoti hai (East coast mein NAHI) — par East\n⚠️\ncoast mein zyada rice production hota hai apni suitable climate-soil ki wajah se\n19. Stagnant Cropped Area — Rice (Not Oilseeds/Pulses/Sugarcane)\n●\nPichhle dashak mein Rice ka cropped area kamobesh stagnant raha hai (42.9→45.8→47.8 million\nhectares) — Oilseed, Pulses, Sugarcane ka area badha hai. [Q27]\n20. Top-4 Rice Producers — Historical Sets\n●\nHistorically top-4 rice producers West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Andhra Pradesh the — India ki\n50%+ total rice production. [Q28]\n21. Surplus Rice Producer — Andhra Pradesh (Historical)\n●\n2008-09 data ke mutabik Andhra Pradesh ka market surplus ratio sabse zyada tha — 2014-15 mein\nPunjab pehle number par aa gaya (Haryana dusre). [Q30]\n22. Rice Cultivation Rainfall Threshold — 100cm\n●\nRice cultivation 100cm se zyada annual rainfall wale areas mein hoti hai — kam-rainfall areas mein\nirrigation ki madad leni padti hai. [Q31]"," 23. UP — Largest Hybrid Rice Area\n●\nHybrid rice cultivation ke liye Uttar Pradesh ka sabse bada area hai. [Q32]\n24. Zaid Crops — Moong/Urad, Fodder\n●\nZaid season (irrigated areas) mein main crops: Moong aur Urad — Fodder bhi Zaid crop hai\n(Gram/Mustard Rabi, Cotton Kharif hai). [Q36, Q37]\n25. Rice — Transplanted Crop\n●\nPaddy crop transplant ki jaati hai (weed-control ke liye, kam seed par zyada labour chahiye, transplant-\nshock se pakne mein zyada waqt lagta hai). [Q38]\n26. Crop-State Match — 'None' Answer Trap (Multi-Question)\n●\nKayi crop-state match questions mein data change hone ki wajah se 'None of the above' hi sahi answer\nbanta hai (jaise Rice-WB, Wheat-UP, Cotton-Gujarat, Mustard-Rajasthan combo) — actual current\nleaders alag hain (Rice mein Telangana ab leading hai). [Q39]\n27. Paddy — NOT Helpful in Nitrogen Fixation\n●\nGram, Pea, Bean nitrogen-fixation mein madad karte hain — Paddy (dhan) is process mein sahayak NAHI\nhai. [Q42]\n28. Jowar — Not a Cash Crop\n●\nJute, Groundnut, Sugarcane cash crops hain — Jowar cash crop NAHI hai. [Q43]\n29. Kharif Cropped-Area Trends (Rice Highest, Cotton>Sugarcane)\n●\nPichhle 5 saalon mein: Rice ka cropped area sabse zyada hai, Cotton ka area Sugarcane se zyada hai —\n'Jowar ka area Oilseed se zyada' aur 'Sugarcane area lagatar ghat raha' GALAT statements hain.\n[Q44]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0022","t":"16.i Cotton","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" COTTON — FULL MIND MAP\n🧵\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Climate Requirements — Subtropical, Frost-Free\n2. Kharif Crop — Temperature & Rainfall Range\n3. Millet Crops Group (Cross Reference)\n4. Cotton Belt — North-Western & Western India\n5. Largest Producer — Gujarat\n6. 'White Gold' — MP & Maharashtra Districts\n7. India — Original Home of Cotton Plant\n8. Cotton Fibers — Seed Hairs\n9. Cotton vs Sugarcane Competition (Maharashtra)\n10. Highest Yield & Most Textile Mills (Disputed)\n1. Climate Requirements — Subtropical, Frost-Free\n●\nCotton crop subtropical hai, hard frost ke liye harmful hai — 210 frost-free days aur 50-100cm rainfall\nchahiye. Light well-drained soil (moisture-retentive) ideal hai. [Q1]\n2. Kharif Crop — Temperature & Rainfall Range\n●\nCotton mainly Kharif season ka cash crop hai — ideal temp 21-27°C (15°C se kam ya 43°C se zyada\nnahi sehta), moderate rainfall 50-75cm (kuch sources 70-120cm bhi batate hain). [Q2]\n3. Millet Crops Group (Cross Reference)\n●\nMillet crops group: Sorghum (jowar), Kodo, Kangani, Ragi — Maize aur Moong millets NAHI hain (ye\ncotton se related nahi hai, par isi chapter mein tha). [Q3]\n4. Cotton Belt — North-Western & Western India\n●\nIndia mein cotton ka sabse zyada production North-Western aur Western India mein hota hai (Gujarat,\nMaharashtra) — 2023-24 mein 12.7 million hectare area mein cultivation. [Q4]\n5. Largest Producer — Gujarat\n●\n2023-24 data ke mutabik Gujarat > Maharashtra > Telangana cotton production ke top-3 states hain. [Q5]\n6. 'White Gold' — MP & Maharashtra Districts\n●\n'White Gold' cotton ko kaha jaata hai — MP mein Khandwa-Khargone districts is naam se famous hain,\naur Maharashtra mein bhi cotton ko 'White Gold' kaha jaata hai (black soil se cultivation hoti hai). [Q6,\nQ7]\n7. India — Original Home of Cotton Plant"," ●\nIndia cotton plant ka original home hai (Rigveda, Manusmriti mein mention) — India hi duniya ka pehla\ndesh hai jisne commercial hybrid cotton variety (H-4, 1970) develop ki. [Q8]\n8. Cotton Fibers — Seed Hairs\n●\nCotton fibers seed hairs hain — cotton plant ke seeds ki surface se milte hain. [Q9]\n9. Cotton vs Sugarcane Competition (Maharashtra)\n●\nMaharashtra ki black soil mein cotton ko sugarcane se competition milti hai kyunki irrigation ka expansion\nis region ko sugarcane cultivation ke liye zyada suitable bana deta hai (jo cotton se zyada profitable\ncrop hai). [Q10]\n10. Highest Yield & Most Textile Mills (Disputed)\n●\nCotton yield (productivity) mein Gujarat sabse aage hai (options mein na hone par 'None of the above'\nsahi answer) — cotton textile mills ki sankhya mein Tamil Nadu sabse aage hai (options mein na hone\npar 'None' sahi). [Q11, Q12]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0023","t":"16.ii Sugarcane","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" SUGARCANE — FULL MIND MAP\n🎋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Sugarcane — Least Water-Efficient Crop\n2. UP — Largest Area Under Cultivation\n3. Sugarcane — Highest Irrigated-Area Percentage (98.73%)\n4. Top Producer States (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, TN)\n5. UP — Leading Sugarcane Producer State\n6. 8 Largest Producer States (UP to Punjab)\n7. 2013 Ranking (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Haryana)\n8. Molasses, Bagasse — By-Products (Not Only Sugarcane Sugar)\n9. Sustainable Sugarcane Initiative (SSI) — Key Features\n10. Sucrose Content — Decreases with Frost During Ripening\n11. Top-3 Sugar Producers (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka)\n12. 2015-16 Ranking (Maharashtra, UP, Karnataka, TN)\n13. India — 2nd Largest Sugar Producer (Brazil #1)\n14. Sakkar Nagar — Andhra Pradesh (Now Telangana)\n15. UP — India's 'Sugar Bowl'\n16. First Sugar Mill — Pratappur, Deoria (1903)\n17. North-to-South Shift Factors (Yield, Sucrose, Crushing Season)\n18. Sugarcane Breeding Institute — Coimbatore (1912)\n19. Adsali Sugarcane — 18-Month Ripening (Maharashtra)\n20. South India — More Developed Sugar Industry (Assertion-Reason)\n21. UP vs Maharashtra — Production High, Productivity Low\n22. Co. 1148 — Sugarcane Variety\n1. Sugarcane — Least Water-Efficient Crop\n●\nDiye gaye crops mein Sugarcane sabse kam water-efficient hai — sabse zyada paani chahiye ugane ke\nliye — Sunflower, Pearl millet, Red gram se zyada. [Q1]\n2. UP — Largest Area Under Cultivation\n●\n2022-23 data ke mutabik Uttar Pradesh (2.79 million hectares) sabse bada area under sugarcane\ncultivation rakhta hai — Maharashtra (1.36 million hectares) dusre number par. [Q2]\n3. Sugarcane — Highest Irrigated-Area Percentage (98.73%)\n●\n2021-22 data ke mutabik irrigated-area percentage: Sugarcane (98.73%) > Wheat (95.29%) > Rice\n(67.56%) > Oilseed (37.51%). [Q3]\n4. Top Producer States (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, TN)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt top-4: UP, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh — 2022-23 data ke mutabik ab\nUP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Gujarat top-5 hain. [Q4]\n5. UP — Leading Sugarcane Producer State"," ●\nUttar Pradesh India ka leading sugarcane producer state hai. [Q5]\n6. 8 Largest Producer States (UP to Punjab)\n●\n2022-23 ke top-8 sugarcane producers: Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Gujarat,\nBihar, Haryana, Punjab. [Q6]\n7. 2013 Ranking (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Haryana)\n●\n2013 ke descending order: UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Haryana. [Q7]\n8. Molasses, Bagasse — By-Products (Not Only Sugarcane Sugar)\n●\nSahi statements: Molasses sugar-production ka by-product hai (alcohol banane mein use hota hai),\nBagasse boiler-fuel ke roop mein steam generate karne ke liye use hota hai — 'sugar sirf sugarcane se\nbanti hai' GALAT hai (beetroot se bhi banti hai). [Q8]\n9. Sustainable Sugarcane Initiative (SSI) — Key Features\n●\nSSI (2009, WWF-ICRISAT) ke features: kam seed cost, effective drip irrigation, zyada intercropping\nscope — 'chemical fertilizers ka koi use nahi' GALAT hai (SSI organic ko encourage karta hai,\nchemical ko poori tarah ban nahi karta). [Q9]\n10. Sucrose Content — Decreases with Frost During Ripening\n●\nSugarcane ka sucrose content ripening period mein frost padne se kam ho jaata hai — ideal conditions:\n21-27°C temp, 75-100cm rainfall. [Q10]\n11. Top-3 Sugar Producers (UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt top-3: UP, Maharashtra, Karnataka — 15 April 2024 tak Maharashtra pehle number\npar hai, UP dusre number par. [Q11]\n12. 2015-16 Ranking (Maharashtra, UP, Karnataka, TN)\n●\n2015-16 data ke mutabik: Maharashtra, UP, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu. [Q12]\n13. India — 2nd Largest Sugar Producer (Brazil #1)\n●\n2023/24 USDA data ke mutabik: Brazil world ka largest sugar producer hai (45.54 million tonnes), India\ndusre number par (34 million tonnes, ~15.8% world share) — Sugar Industry, India ka cotton ke baad\n2nd sabse bada agriculture-based industry hai, India sugar ka biggest consumer hai. [Q13]\n14. Sakkar Nagar — Andhra Pradesh (Now Telangana)\n●\nSakkar Nagar Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana) ka important sugar producing centre hai. [Q14]\n15. UP — India's 'Sugar Bowl'\n●\nUttar Pradesh ko 'Sugar Bowl of India' kaha jaata hai — massive sugarcane production ki wajah se. [Q15,\nQ16]"," 16. First Sugar Mill — Pratappur, Deoria (1903)\n●\nIndia ki pehli sugar mill 1903 mein Pratappur (Deoria district, UP) mein banayi gayi thi. [Q17]\n17. North-to-South Shift Factors (Yield, Sucrose, Crushing Season)\n●\nSugar industry ka North se South India shift hone ke factors: per-acre zyada yield, zyada sucrose content,\nlonger crushing season — 'cheap labour' iske reasons mein NAHI hai. [Q18]\n18. Sugarcane Breeding Institute — Coimbatore (1912)\n●\nSugarcane Breeding Institute (SBI) Coimbatore (Tamil Nadu) mein 1912 mein ICAR ke tahat establish\nhui — India ka ekmatra sugarcane research institute hai, seeds bhi yahin produce hote hain. [Q19, Q20]\n19. Adsali Sugarcane — 18-Month Ripening (Maharashtra)\n●\nAdsali sugarcane Maharashtra ke kam-rainfall areas mein July-August mein lagayi jaati hai — pakne\nmein 16-18 mahine lagte hain. [Q21]\n20. South India — More Developed Sugar Industry (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nSouth India mein sugar industry zyada developed hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki southern states mein per-\nhectare yield aur juice quantity zyada hai (Reason sahi, sahi explanation bhi hai) — Maharashtra,\nKarnataka, Tamil Nadu major producers hain. [Q22]\n21. UP vs Maharashtra — Production High, Productivity Low\n●\nUP mein sugarcane-sugar production Maharashtra se zyada hai, par productivity kam hai (Assertion sahi) —\nMaharashtra mein zyadatar sugar factories cooperative sector mein hain (Reason bhi sahi hai) — par\nR, A ki sahi explanation NAHI hai. [Q23]\n22. Co. 1148 — Sugarcane Variety\n●\nCo. 1148 sugarcane ki ek important variety hai — Wheat, Cotton, Maize ki NAHI. [Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0024","t":"17 Oilseeds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" OILSEEDS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌻\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Sunflower — Main Oilseed Crop Identification\n2. Yellow Revolution — Oilseeds Production\n3. Groundnut — Best Dryland Farming Crop\n4. 'Pegging' — Unique Groundnut Phenomenon\n5. Soyabean — MP Leading Producer (Historically)\n6. MP — Largest Area Under Soyabean (43.95%)\n7. 1992-93 — Record Oilseed Production Year\n8. Oilseeds Largest Producer — MP → Rajasthan Shift\n9. Groundnut Largest Producer — Gujarat\n10. Punjab — Low Acreage, High Groundnut Yield\n11. Groundnut — Root-Derived Oil (Odd One Out)\n12. Rajasthan — Chief Mustard/Rapeseed Producer\n13. Map-Based Crop Match (Gujarat-Groundnut, Odisha-Ragi)\n14. Oilseed Production Ranking (Mustard>Soybean>Groundnut>Sesame)\n15. Mustard Varieties (Varuna, Pusa Bold, Pitambari)\n16. Gypsum — Required for Groundnut Cultivation\n17. Crop-Variety Match (Kaushal is Groundnut)\n18. Sesame — Highest Oil Content (52%)\n19. Safflower — Scientific Name (Carthamus Tinctorius)\n1. Sunflower — Main Oilseed Crop Identification\n●\nMain oilseed crops (India): Groundnut, Mustard, Coconut, Soyabean, Castor seeds, Cotton seeds,\nLinseed, Sunflower — Masoor, Lobia, Barseem oilseeds NAHI hain. [Q1]\n2. Yellow Revolution — Oilseeds Production\n●\nYellow Revolution oilseeds production se related hai — Green Revolution (foodgrain), White Revolution\n(milk), Blue Revolution (fish) se alag. [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n3. Groundnut — Best Dryland Farming Crop\n●\nGroundnut dryland farming (100cm tak rainfall wale areas) ke liye sabse suitable crop hai — 50-125cm\nannual well-distributed rainfall mein achhi tarah ugta hai. [Q5]\n4. 'Pegging' — Unique Groundnut Phenomenon\n●\n'Pegging' groundnut ki ek useful phenomenon hai — fertilization ke baad muraye phool ki khootiyan\n(pegs) mitti mein prawesh karti hain, taproot ke paas hi peanut mein pakti hain. [Q6]\n5. Soyabean — MP Leading Producer (Historically)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt aur 2023-24 data ke mutabik Madhya Pradesh (5.47 MT) soyabean ka leading producer\nhai — Maharashtra (5.26 MT), Rajasthan (1.17 MT) dusre-teesre number par. [Q7, Q8, Q9]"," 6. MP — Largest Area Under Soyabean (43.95%)\n●\nSOPA 2024 data ke mutabik MP mein 52.009 lakh hectare (total soyabean-area ka 43.95%) hai — sabse\nzyada area under soyabean cultivation. [Q10]\n7. 1992-93 — Record Oilseed Production Year\n●\n1992-93 mein oilseeds ka record production tha (20.11 million tonnes) — 2010-11 mein phir record bana\n(32.48 MT), 2023-24 mein production 39.7 MT tha. [Q11]\n8. Oilseeds Largest Producer — MP → Rajasthan Shift\n●\n2018-19 data ke waqt Madhya Pradesh oilseeds ka largest producer tha — 2023-24 (Economic Survey\n2024-25) ke mutabik ab Rajasthan sabse aage hai. [Q12]\n9. Groundnut Largest Producer — Gujarat\n●\n2020-21 mein Gujarat groundnut ka largest producer tha — 2023-24 mein bhi Gujarat, Rajasthan, MP\ntop-3 hain. [Q13, Q14]\n10. Punjab — Low Acreage, High Groundnut Yield\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Punjab kam acreage rakhta tha par groundnut ki per-hectare yield bahut zyada thi —\n2022-23 mein productivity ranking: Tamil Nadu, Gujarat, West Bengal. [Q15]\n11. Groundnut — Root-Derived Oil (Odd One Out)\n●\nSesame, Groundnut, Mustard ka oil food mein use hota hai — Castor seed oil food mein NAHI hota —\nGroundnut plant ki jad (root) se milta hai, baaki flower se (disputed question, dono angles se answer\npossible). [Q16]\n12. Rajasthan — Chief Mustard/Rapeseed Producer\n●\nRajasthan mustard (rapeseed) ka chief producer hai (2023-24 data). [Q17]\n13. Map-Based Crop Match (Gujarat-Groundnut, Odisha-Ragi)\n●\nMap-based match: Gujarat — Groundnut, Maharashtra — Cotton/Sugarcane, Odisha — Ragi, Andhra\nPradesh — Tobacco. [Q18]\n14. Oilseed Production Ranking (Mustard>Soybean>Groundnut>Sesame)\n●\n2023-24 production (million tonnes): Rapeseed-Mustard (13.3) > Soybean (13.05) > Groundnut (10.2) >\nSesamum (0.81). [Q19]\n15. Mustard Varieties (Varuna, Pusa Bold, Pitambari)\n●\nMustard ki main varieties: Varuna, Pusabold, Jaikisan, Pitambari (yellow mustard, maturity 110-115\ndays). [Q20, Q21, Q22]"," 16. Gypsum — Required for Groundnut Cultivation\n●\nGroundnut cultivation ke liye bade quantity mein Gypsum chahiye hota hai — Rice, Barseem, Wheat ke\nliye nahi. [Q23]\n17. Crop-Variety Match (Kaushal is Groundnut)\n●\nCrop-variety match: Gram — Pant-114/Gaurav/Radhe/K-4, Cotton — Suvin/Sujata, Groundnut —\nChitra-64/Chandra/Kaushal, Wheat — Kundan/Kalyan Sona/Sonalika. [Q24]\n18. Sesame — Highest Oil Content (52%)\n●\nOil content ranking: Sesame (52%) > Groundnut (48.2%) > Sunflower (42%) > Soyabean (40%). [Q25]\n19. Safflower — Scientific Name (Carthamus Tinctorius)\n●\nSafflower (Kusum) ka scientific naam Carthamus Tinctorius hai — seeds mein 24-36% oil, Maharashtra-\nKarnataka major growers — 78% linoleic acid content, blood cholesterol kam karne ke liye faydemand.\n[Q26]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0025","t":"18 Pulses","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🫘 PULSES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Black Gram — Kharif+Rabi (South India), Moong Share Facts\n2. India — World's Largest Pulses Producer/Consumer\n3. Pulses NOT Exported from India\n4. India — Largest Producer, Consumer & Importer of Pulses\n5. Pulses Shortage — Demand Priority (Assertion-Reason)\n6. Madhya Pradesh — Largest Pulses Producer\n7. Legumes — Nitrogen-Fixing Crop Type\n8. Cobalt — Essential Nutrient for Pulses\n9. Crop-Variety Match Traps (Neelam is Mango, Not Arhar)\n10. Rajma — Nitrogen Fixation Debate\n11. NPK Ratio for Legume Crops\n12. Red Gram (Arhar) — Origin in India\n13. Arhar Varieties (Malaviya Chamatkar, Bahar, Amar, Azad)\n14. Aparna — Leafless Pea Variety\n15. Surya — Mango/Papaya/Potato Variety (Not Linseed)\n1. Black Gram — Kharif+Rabi (South India), Moong Share Facts\n●\nBlack gram (Urad) North India mein sirf kharif crop hai, South India mein Rabi aur Kharif dono season\nmein ugti hai — 'Green-gram/Moong akela pulses production ka aadha hai' GALAT hai (sirf ~14%\nhai), 'kharif pulses badhe, rabi pulses ghate' bhi GALAT hai (asal mein rabi pulses ~150% badhe\nhain). [Q1]\n2. India — World's Largest Pulses Producer/Consumer\n●\nIndia duniya ka sabse bada pulses producer/consumer hai — Myanmar, Canada baad mein aate hain.\n[Q2]\n3. Pulses NOT Exported from India\n●\nWheat, Rice, Sugar kabhi-kabhi export hote hain — Pulses aam taur par export NAHI hoti (high\nconsumption ki wajah se India ko import karna padta hai). [Q3]\n4. India — Largest Producer, Consumer & Importer of Pulses\n●\nIndia Pulses ka sabse bada producer, consumer AUR importer (2023) hai — Chickpeas, Lentils, Pigeon\npeas is category mein aate hain. [Q4]\n5. Pulses Shortage — Demand Priority (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nIndia mein pulses ki kami hai, par protein ki NAHI (Assertion sahi) — kyunki pulses ki demand-priority\nzyada hai, jabki India leading producer bhi hai (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q5]"," 6. Madhya Pradesh — Largest Pulses Producer\n●\nMadhya Pradesh India ka sabse bada pulses producer hai (2023-24, Economic Survey 2024-25). [Q6, Q17]\n7. Legumes — Nitrogen-Fixing Crop Type\n●\nLegumes (pulses) hawa se nitrogen fix karti hain (specialized bacteria ki madad se) — isliye inhe alag se\nnitrogen fertilizer ki utni zaroorat nahi hoti. [Q7]\n8. Cobalt — Essential Nutrient for Pulses\n●\nPulses crop ke liye essential nutrient Cobalt hai — Rhizobium bacteria ke symbiotic nitrogen fixation ke\nliye zaroori hai, Vitamin B12 synthesis mein bhi. [Q8]\n9. Crop-Variety Match Traps (Neelam is Mango, Not Arhar)\n●\n'Arhar-Neelam' GALAT pair hai — Neelam Mango ki variety hai, Arhar ki NAHI — Groundnut-Chandra,\nLentil-Pant L-406, Mustard-Varuna sahi pairs hain. [Q9]\n EXAM TRAP — Neelam — Mango ki variety hai, Arhar ki NAHI (common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n10. Rajma — Nitrogen Fixation Debate\n●\nGram, Pea, Moong sab nitrogen-fixation karte hain — Rajma ki nitrogen-fixation capacity kam/inefficient\nhai (research ke mutabik disputed question hai). [Q10]\n11. NPK Ratio for Legume Crops\n●\nLegume crops ke liye balanced fertilizer ratio (NPK) 1:2:2 (ya 0:1:1, 1:2:3) hota hai. [Q11]\n12. Red Gram (Arhar) — Origin in India\n●\nRed gram (Arhar) ka origin place India hai. [Q12]\n13. Arhar Varieties (Malaviya Chamatkar, Bahar, Amar, Azad)\n●\nArhar ki varieties: Malaviya Chamatkar, Bahar, Amar, Azad, Malaviya Vikas, Paras — Barley-PVW\n343, Gram-Aparna, Paddy-NW 1014 galat pairs hain (Arhar-Bahar hi sahi pair hai). [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n14. Aparna — Leafless Pea Variety\n●\n'Aparna' pea (matar) ki high-yielding, leafless variety hai — Arkel, Azad Pea-1, L-116 se alag. [Q16]\n15. Surya — Mango/Papaya/Potato Variety (Not Linseed)\n●\n'Surya' Mango, Papaya, Potato ki variety hai — Linseed (alsi) ki NAHI — 'Linseed-Surya' GALAT pair hai\n(Mustard-Varuna, Field Pea-Sapna, Groundnut-Kaushal sahi hain). [Q18]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0026","t":"19 Silk","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" SILK — FULL MIND MAP\n🧶\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Karnataka — Largest Silk Producer (Mulberry & Overall)\n2. Karnataka + Andhra Pradesh — Historical 3/4th Share\n3. Silk Type-State Match Set (Tasar-Jharkhand, Eri/Muga-Assam)\n4. Common Wrong Statements (AP-Mulberry, Meghalaya-Eri)\n5. Muga Silk — Rare, Only-India Variety\n6. Oak Tasar vs Tropical Tasar (Manipur vs Jharkhand)\n7. Silk Textiles & Yarn — Karnataka Leads\n1. Karnataka — Largest Silk Producer (Mulberry & Overall)\n●\nKarnataka sabse bada silk producing state hai — mulberry silk mein 42.75%, kul raw silk mein 32.31%\nshare (2022-23). [Q1, Q3]\n2. Karnataka + Andhra Pradesh — Historical 3/4th Share\n●\nJab question pucha gaya tha tab Karnataka aur Andhra Pradesh mila ke India ki 3/4th raw silk\nproduction karte the — abhi (2022-23) dono milkar 57.77% produce karte hain. [Q2]\n3. Silk Type-State Match Set (Tasar-Jharkhand, Eri/Muga-Assam)\n●\n2022-23 production ke mutabik sahi match: Mulberry Silk — Karnataka (42.75%), Tasar Silk —\nJharkhand (66.24%), Eri Silk — Assam (74.66%), Muga Silk — Assam & BTC (80.84%). [Q4]\n4. Common Wrong Statements (AP-Mulberry, Meghalaya-Eri)\n●\nSahi statements: Karnataka raw silk ka sabse bada producer hai, Jharkhand Tasar silk ka sabse bada\nproducer hai — 'Andhra Pradesh mulberry silk ka sabse bada producer hai' GALAT hai (Karnataka\nhai), 'Meghalaya Eri silk ka sabse bada producer hai' GALAT hai (Assam hai). [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — Mulberry silk — Karnataka (AP nahi); Eri silk — Assam (Meghalaya nahi)\n⚠️\n5. Muga Silk — Rare, Only-India Variety\n●\nMuga silk (duniya ke sabse rare silks mein se ek) sirf India mein milti hai — Assam & BTC (80.84%) aur\nMeghalaya (15.71%) main producers hain. [Q6]\n6. Oak Tasar vs Tropical Tasar (Manipur vs Jharkhand)\n●\nTasar silk ki 2 categories: Tropical Tasar — Jharkhand mein maximum production, Oak Tasar —\nManipur mein production — 1966 mein Oak flora ki discovery se sericulture history mein naya chapter\njuda. [Q7]\n7. Silk Textiles & Yarn — Karnataka Leads"," ●\nKarnataka silk textiles/garments (2024) aur silk yarn (2022-23) dono ka sabse bada producer hai — India\nduniya ka ekmatra desh hai jo saari 5 silk varieties (Mulberry, Eri, Muga, Tropical Tasar, Temperate Tasar)\nproduce karta hai. Chikmagalur (Karnataka) coffee ke liye famous hai (silk ke liye NAHI, ye ek common\nconfusion hai jo Coffee chapter se cross-reference hai). [Q8, Q9]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0027","t":"02.i Natural Region of India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NATURAL REGIONS OF INDIA — FULL MIND\n🌍\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Origin — Gondwana, Plate Movement & the 4 Natural Regions\n2. Deccan Traps & Rock-System Timeline\n3. Landform Formation — Synclinorium, Foredeep & Plate Theory\n4. Coastline, Geological Rock Ages & Miscellaneous Facts\n5. Region-Specific Features (Uttarakhand, Bihar, Kerala, Thar Desert)\n1. Origin — Gondwana, Plate Movement & the 4 Natural Regions\n●\nPaleomagnetic results ke mutabik Indian landmass northward khisak gaya tha — continental drift theory ke\nhisaab se ye Gondwana Continent ka hissa tha jo ~200 million saal pehle toot gaya (aaj ke Africa, South\nAmerica, Australia, Antarctica, Peninsular India, Arabian Peninsula ban gaye). [Q1, Q2]\n●\nIndia ko 4 natural regions mein baanta gaya hai: (i) Northern Mountainous Region (ii) Northern Plains\n(iii) Peninsular Plateau (iv) Coasts and Islands. [Q3]\n●\nHimalaya ka formation Indian aur Eurasian plate ke collision se hua — 'Chinese plate' wali koi triangular\nconvergence theory nahi hoti (ye ek common wrong-statement trap hai). [Q6]\n2. Deccan Traps & Rock-System Timeline\n●\nDeccan Traps Mesozoic era ke Cretaceous period mein Western Central India mein bane the. Intertrappean\nbeds mein marine fossils NAHI milte (ye ek galat-paired option hota hai). [Q4]\n●\nOrigin-timeline match karo: Deccan Traps — Cretaceous Eocene, Western Ghats — Late Cenozoic,\nAravalli — Pre-Cambrian (sabse purana), Narmada-Tapi alluvial deposits — Pleistocene. [Q8]\n●\nIndia ke rock-systems ka classification (Sir T.S. Holland, Geological Survey of India) hai: Archaean →\nPurana → Dravidian → Aryan period. Gondwana sequence sabse latest (nayi) hai — Vindhyan,\nCuddapah, Dharwar se baad ka. India ka zyadatar coal Gondwana region se hi milta hai. (J.D. Dana ka\n'Manual of Geology' America ke geology ka source hai, India ka nahi — ye ek confusion trap hai). [Q12, Q13]\n3. Landform Formation — Synclinorium, Foredeep & Plate Theory\n●\nMeghalaya plateau structurally Deccan (Peninsular) plateau ka extension hai. Kashmir Valley ek\nsynclinorium mein bani thi. Gangetic plain/Indo-Gangetic depression ek 'fore-deep' hai jo Himalaya ki high\ncrust-waves ke saamne bana — isi wajah se Ganga plain ko 'geosyncline' bhi bola jaata hai\n(pediplain/peneplain/karst plain NAHI). [Q6, Q14]\n4. Coastline, Geological Rock Ages & Miscellaneous Facts"," ●\nIndia ka geologically sabse ancient part Peninsular region hai; Himalaya sabse newly-developed folded\nmountain hai. Western coastline nadi-deposition se NAHI bani — balki land ke submergence-emergence\n(dhab jaana-ubharna) se bani hai (ye ek common wrong-statement trap hai). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Western coast ki origin — submergence/emergence, NOT river deposition\n⚠️\n5. Region-Specific Features (Uttarakhand, Bihar, Kerala, Thar Desert)\n●\nArtesian wells (jinme paani nikalne ke liye pump nahi chahiye) Uttarakhand ke Tarai region mein milte hain.\n[Q5]\n●\nBihar mein Dharwar geological formations Munger, Nawada aur Jamui (South-East Bihar) districts mein\nmilte hain — Rohtas mein NAHI (Rohtas South-West Bihar mein aata hai jahan Vindhyan-type formation\nhai). [Q11]\n●\nKerala ka Kuttanad (Kuttanadu) region India ka sabse kam altitude wala area hai — samudra tal se 1.2-\n3.0 meter neeche farming hoti hai. Isi wajah se ise 'Rice Bowl of Kerala' bhi kaha jaata hai, aur FAO ne ise\nglobally-important agricultural heritage declare kiya hai. [Q9]\n●\nSindhu/Indus Valley area ek desert region hai (NW Punjab/Pakistan aur adjoining Thar desert). Bharatiya\n(Indian/Thar) marusthal Aravalli hills ke western margins par hai, jahan saalana rainfall 150mm se kam\nhoti hai, aur Luni iss region ki ekmatra badi river hai. [Q10, Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0028","t":"02.ii Northern Mountaneous Region","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NORTHERN MOUNTAINOUS REGION — FULL\n🏔️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Himalaya Formation, Age & Ongoing Uplift (Assertion-Reason)\n2. Three Parallel Ranges — Great, Middle/Lesser, Shiwalik\n3. Bhabar & Tarai Belts\n4. North-to-South Range Sequence (Trans-Himalaya)\n5. Shiwalik Peaks Altitude — 900-1100m Average (Disputed)\n6. Regional Divisions by River (Punjab/Kumaon/Nepal/Assam Himalaya)\n7. Mountain Peaks & East-to-West Sequence\n8. Patkai Range & North-East Hills\n9. Pir Panjal, Atal Tunnel & Kashmir Valley\n10. Aksai Chin, Karewa & Other Ladakh/Kashmir Features\n11. State-wise Himalayan Spread & Oldest/Youngest Range Comparisons\n12. Seismicity, Fossils & Other Facts\n13. Imphal Basin, Mt. Kailash & Miscellaneous Peaks\n1. Himalaya Formation, Age & Ongoing Uplift (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nHimalaya se nikalne wali sabhi nadiyaan perennial (barahmasi) hoti hain kyunki unka source Himalayan\nglaciers mein hai — glaciers dry season mein bhi continuous paani dete hain. Lekin ye fact ki 'Himalaya ko\nzyada baarish south-west monsoon se milti hai' iska sahi explanation NAHI hai — dono statement sahi hain\npar ek dusre ko explain nahi karte. [Q1, Q3]\n●\nHimalaya abhi bhi ~5mm/year (kuch sources 1cm+/year) ki dar se badh raha hai — kyunki Indian tectonic\nplate Eurasian plate se collide kar rahi hai (~40-50 million saal pehle shuru hua tha), aur ye statement iska\nsahi explanation hai. [Q2]\n●\nAgar Himalaya na hota to: Siberia se cold waves poore desh mein aatin, Indo-Gangetic plain itni alluvial-\nrich na hoti, aur monsoon pattern bhi different hota — teeno statements sahi hain. [Q5]\n2. Three Parallel Ranges — Great, Middle/Lesser, Shiwalik\n●\nHimalaya 3 parallel structural ranges mein bata hai (age ke hisaab se): Great Himalaya (sabse purana,\nOligocene 37-24 mn yrs) → Middle/Lesser Himalaya (Miocene 24-5 mn yrs) → Shiwalik (sabse naya,\nPliocene 5-2 mn yrs, Cenozoic era). [Q4, Q9]\n●\nShiwalik (foothills/outermost range) ki width 10-50 km aur altitude 900-1100m ke beech hai —\nunconsolidated river-sediments se bani hai. Alag-alag areas mein alag naam se jaani jaati hai: Jammu mein\n'Jammu Hills', Arunachal mein 'Dafla, Miri, Abor, Mishmi Hills'. [Q7, Q8, Q10, Q11, Q21]\n●\nMiddle/Lesser Himalaya ko 'Himachal' bhi kaha jaata hai — width ~50km, elevation 3700-4500m. Shimla,\nNainital, Mussoorie jaise zyaadatar hill stations isi range mein hain. Ye Shiwalik (south) aur Great Himalaya\n(north) ke beech mein padti hai. [Q19, Q20, Q35]"," ●\nDeep gorges, U-turn river courses, parallel mountain ranges, aur landslide-prone steep gradients — ye sab\nHimalaya ke young fold mountain hone ke evidence hain. [Q16]\n3. Bhabar & Tarai Belts\n●\nSub-Himalayan flat plains ko Bhabar kehte hain — 8-16km wide narrow belt, Shiwalik foothills ke parallel,\nporous pebbly beds jisme streams poori tarah lupt ho jaati hain (piedmont situation ka example). Iske south\nmein Tarai belt hai (15-30km wide) jahan streams phir se emerge hoke marshy/swampy conditions banati\nhain. [Q6, Q14]\n4. North-to-South Range Sequence (Trans-Himalaya)\n●\nJ&K map mein north se south order: Karakoram → Ladakh → Zanskar → Pir Panjal. North-to-south ek\naur variant (Pir Panjal included as middle): Karakoram → Ladakh → Zanskar → Shiwalik (jab Pir Panjal\nexclude ho). [Q17, Q18]\n●\nSouth-to-north sequence: Dhauladhar (Middle Himalaya) → Zanskar → Ladakh → Karakoram (sab\nTrans-Himalaya) — ya jab Pir Panjal include ho: Pirpanjal → Zanskar → Ladakh → Karakoram. [Q22,\nQ23]\n●\nWestern section mein south-to-north order: Shiwalik → Lesser Himalaya → Great Himalaya. [Q20]\n5. Shiwalik Peaks Altitude — 900-1100m Average (Disputed)\n●\nShiwalik range (~2500 km lambi, Himalaya ki southern range) ki average altitude 900-1100m hai —\nregional variation ki wajah se koi single option perfectly accurate nahi hai, disputed question hai. [Q12]\n6. Regional Divisions by River (Punjab/Kumaon/Nepal/Assam Himalaya)\n●\nHimalaya ko rivers ke basis par bhi divide kiya jaata hai: Indus-Satluj beech — Punjab Himalaya, Satluj-\nKali beech — Kumaon Himalaya, Kali-Tista beech — Nepal Himalaya, Tista-Dihang beech — Assam\nHimalaya. [Q13]\n7. Mountain Peaks & East-to-West Sequence\n●\nEast-to-west sequence of peaks: Kanchenjunga (Sikkim-Nepal border) → Everest (Nepal-China, world's\ntallest) → Annapurna → Dhaulagiri (dono Nepal mein). [Q24]\n●\nGreat Himalaya (Himadri) ki average height ~6000m hai, aur uski sabse ooncha peak Mt. Everest ~8850m\n(naya official figure 8848.86m, Nepal-China joint announcement se) — Himadri India ki sabse youngest\nrange bhi hai (Aravalli sabse purani). [Q34, Q39]\n●\nNamcha Barwa peak Arunachal Himalaya mein located hai. [Q15, Q44]\n●\nCho Oyu aur Lhotse Himalayan range ke peaks hain — Annamalai aur Sirumalai South India ki ranges hain,\nHimalaya mein NAHI (ye ek common confusion trap hai). [Q46]\n8. Patkai Range & North-East Hills"," ●\nPatkai range Purvanchal (Eastern) Himalaya ka hissa hai, tertiary era mein bani — sab ranges mein sabse\nlatest origin wali. Patkai hills ke saath lagne wale states: Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram,\nNagaland — Tripura NAHI (Mizo hills Mizoram-Tripura mein failii hain, alag se). [Q25, Q26]\n9. Pir Panjal, Atal Tunnel & Kashmir Valley\n●\nPir Panjal Range Middle Himalaya mein hai, Himachal Pradesh aur J&K mein southeast-northwest phaili\nhui. [Q27]\n●\nAtal Tunnel (Rohtang, H.P.) — 9.02 km lambi, Border Roads Organisation (BRO) ne banayi, Eastern Pir\nPanjal Range ke paar hai, Manali-Lahaul Spiti ko connect karti hai — Manali-Leh distance 46 km aur travel\ntime 4-5 ghante kam karti hai, strategically important hai armed forces ke liye. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n●\nKashmir Valley Pir Panjal (southwest) aur Great Himalaya/Himadri (northeast) ke beech mein bani hai\n— ek synclinorium mein formation hui thi. [Q31, Q32]\n10. Aksai Chin, Karewa & Other Ladakh/Kashmir Features\n●\nAksai Chin (~38,000 sq km), Ladakh Plateau ka hissa hai — currently China ke occupation mein, par Indian\nterritory maana jaata hai. [Q33]\n●\n'Karewa' landform — plateau-jaise terraces — Kashmir Himalaya mein milte hain (Jhelum aur uski\ntributaries ke upar), saffron cultivation ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q43, Q44]\n●\nRelated facts: Dehradun sabse bada Dun hai (Nalagarh Dun NAHI — common wrong statement), aur\nValley of Flowers Garhwal Himalaya (Uttarakhand) mein hai. [Q44]\n11. State-wise Himalayan Spread & Oldest/Youngest Range Comparisons\n●\nHimalaya 5 se zyada states/UTs mein failaa hai (J&K, Ladakh, HP, Uttarakhand, Sikkim, Arunachal,\nMeghalaya, Nagaland, Manipur, Mizoram, Tripura, plus Assam/WB ke hill regions) — 'sirf 5 states' wala\nstatement galat hai. Western Ghats bhi 6 states (Gujarat, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala)\nmein failaa hai, 5 nahi. Pulicat Lake sirf 2 states (Tamil Nadu aur Andhra Pradesh) mein hai — ye\nstatement sahi hai. [Q36]\n●\nHimalayan mountain ranges Uttar Pradesh ka hissa NAHI hain (U.P. sirf plains mein hai) — jabki\nUttarakhand, Sikkim, Himachal Pradesh sab Himalayan states hain. [Q37]\n●\nComparison: Himalaya sabse young folded mountain hai India mein — Aravalli sabse purani (oldest) hai.\n[Q38, Q39]\n12. Seismicity, Fossils & Other Facts\n●\nIndia mein seismic zones ka sabse zyada concentration Himalayan region mein hai (zyadatar zone IV-V\nmein), kyunki yahan kai longitudinal thrust zones (Main Frontal Thrust, Main Boundary Fault, Main\nCentral Thrust) hain — ye Assertion-Reason dono sahi hain aur Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation deta\nhai. [Q40]\n●\nFossil facts: Lesser Himalaya ki sedimentary rocks mein marine living fossils milte hain; Shiwalik\n(outer) Himalaya mein human civilization ke remains milte hain. Lekin 'Great Himalaya ki rocks fossilless"," thin' — ye statement GALAT hai, kyunki Great Himalaya ki sedimentary rocks mein bhi fossils hote hain.\n[Q42]\n13. Imphal Basin, Mt. Kailash & Miscellaneous Peaks\n●\n'Imphal Basin' (Manipur hills se ghira) lacustrine plain ka fine example hai (jaise Kashmir Valley bhi) —\npurane zamane mein yahan lake tha, jiske sediment-deposition se ye plain bani. [Q41]\n●\nMount Kailash Tibet (China) region mein hai — Hinduism ka pavitra tirtha sthal maana jaata hai. [Q45]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0029","t":"02.iii Mountain Ranges and Hills of South and Central India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MOUNTAIN RANGES AND HILLS OF SOUTH\n⛰️\n\nAND CENTRAL INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Aravalli — Oldest Range in India (Age, State, Residual Mountain)\n2. Highest Peak of South India / Peninsula — Anaimudi\n3. Satpura, Narmada-Tapti & West-to-East Sequences\n4. Nilgiri Hills — Where Eastern & Western Ghats Meet\n5. North-to-South Hill Sequences (Peninsular India)\n6. Marine/Seamount Ranges & Western Ghats Structural Facts\n7. Single-State Ranges & Wrong-Pair Traps\n8. Southernmost Range & Cardamom Hills\n9. Hill-Region Match Pairs (State-wise)\n10. Central India Hill Sequence (Satpura Sub-Ranges)\n11. State-wise Highest Peaks (Match-the-Following)\n12. Western Ghats Local Names (North to South) & Tea Gardens\n13. Amarkantak, Maikal & River Origins\n1. Aravalli — Oldest Range in India (Age, State, Residual Mountain)\n●\nAravalli Range India (aur duniya) ki sabse purani fold mountain range hai — Precambrian/Proterozoic era\nmein bani, age ~570 million years. Ye Gujarat, Rajasthan aur Haryana states mein failii hui hai (Delhi tak\nkhatam hoti hai), lekin primarily Rajasthan mein located maani jaati hai. Iski sabse ooncha peak Guru\nShikhar (1722m) hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6]\n●\nIndian Peninsular Plateau desh ka sabse purana geographical region hai — Gondwana land ke breaking-\ndrifting se bana. Aravalli 'Residual Mountain' (purane valit/block/volcanic mountains ke bache hue avshesh)\nka bhi example hai. [Q7, Q8]\n2. Highest Peak of South India / Peninsula — Anaimudi\n●\nAnaimudi (2695m), Western Ghats ka hissa, South India aur poore Indian Peninsula ki sabse ooncha\npeak hai — Kerala ke Ernakulam aur Idukki districts mein located. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n3. Satpura, Narmada-Tapti & West-to-East Sequences\n●\nNarmada aur Tapti rivers Satpura Range ko flank karti hain — Satpura ('Saat Valan') Deccan plateau ka\nhissa hai, eastern Gujarat se shuru hoke Maharashtra-M.P. border se Chhattisgarh ke east tak jaati hai, aur\nNarmada (north)-Tapti (south) ke beech watershed banati hai. [Q12]\n●\nWest-to-east relief sequence: Mahadeo Range → Maikal Range → Chotanagpur Plateau → Khasi Hills\n— Mahadeo aur Maikal, Satpura ka eastward extension hain; Chotanagpur plateau\nJharkhand+Chhattisgarh/Bihar/WB/Odisha ke parts mein failaa hai; Khasi Hills Meghalaya mein hain. [Q14]\n4. Nilgiri Hills — Where Eastern & Western Ghats Meet"," ●\nNilgiri Hills (Blue Mountains) wahi jagah hai jahan Eastern Ghats aur Western Ghats (Sahyadri) mil\njaate hain — Tamil Nadu, Karnataka aur Kerala teeno ke junction par. Iski sabse ooncha peak Doddabetta\n(2637m) hai — South India ki 2nd highest peak. [Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22]\n5. North-to-South Hill Sequences (Peninsular India)\n●\nNorth-to-south (Tamil Nadu-Andhra region): Nallamalai Hills → Javadi Hills → Nilgiri Hills →\nAnaimalai Hills — Nallamalai (Krishna-Pennar rivers ke beech, Coromandel coast ke parallel), Javadi\n(Eastern Ghats, Tamil Nadu), Anaimalai (Western Ghats ka southern portion, Kerala-TN border). [Q13]\n●\nSouth-to-North sequence: Satmala Hills (Maharashtra) → Kaimur Hills (M.P.-Bihar) → Naga Hills\n(Indo-Myanmar border) → Pir Panjal Range (J&K-H.P.). [Q27]\n6. Marine/Seamount Ranges & Western Ghats Structural Facts\n●\nIndian Oceanists ne 3 marine mountain ranges discover kiye hain: ek Indian Ocean basin mein, dusra Sagar\nKanya (Eastern Arabian Sea), teesra Mumbai se ~455km west-southwest, Arabian Sea ke tal par 1505m\nheight wala 'Raman Sagar' mountain (naam scientist C.V. Raman ke naam par). [Q23]\n●\nWestern Ghats structurally block mountain hai (Arabian Sea mein land-block ke upwelling se bana) —\nwestern slope steep hai, eastern slope gradually plateau mein utarta hai, northern section basaltic lava se bana\nhai. Overall ~1500km lambaai, average elevation ~1200m — southern part northern se zyada ooncha hai\n(opposite statement galat hoga). [Q24, Q39]\n7. Single-State Ranges & Wrong-Pair Traps\n●\nSirf ek state mein failii range: Ajanta (Maharashtra) — jabki Satpura, Aravalli aur Sahyadri sab multiple\nstates mein failii hain. [Q25]\n●\nWestern Ghats ko Maharashtra-Goa-Karnataka mein 'Sahyadri' kaha jaata hai. [Q26]\n EXAM TRAP — Mandav Hills — Gujarat mein hain, Maharashtra mein NAHI (common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n●\nWrong-pair traps yaad rakho: Mandav Hills Gujarat mein hain (Maharashtra mein NAHI); Balaghat,\nHarishchandra aur Satmala Hills sab Maharashtra mein hain. [Q31, Q32]\n●\nAur ek trap set: Cardamom Hills-Coromandel Coast aur Kaimur Hills-Konkan Coast dono galat pairs\nhain — Cardamom Hills Kerala-TN mein hain (Coromandel se related nahi), Kaimur Hills M.P.-Bihar tak\nfailii hain (Konkan se related nahi). Mahadeo Hills-Central India(M.P.) aur Mikir Hills-North-East India\n— ye dono sahi pairs hain. [Q33]\n●\nMahadeo Hills, Satpura Hills ka hissa hain — Satpura range Vindhya ke south mein aur uske parallel hai.\n[Q34]\n8. Southernmost Range & Cardamom Hills\n●\nCardamom Hills (Yela Mala) India ki sabse southern mountain range hai — Western Ghats ka hissa, SE\nKerala-SW Tamil Nadu mein. Yahan Cardamom (elaichi), Pepper aur Coffee ugte hain. Kanyakumari ke\nsabse kareeb bhi Cardamom Hills hi hain. Ye Kerala-Tamil Nadu border par sthith hain. [Q28, Q29, Q46]\n●\nShevaroy Hills Tamil Nadu ke Salem town mein hain (4000-5000 ft) — famous 'Yercaud' hill station yahin\nhai. [Q30]"," 9. Hill-Region Match Pairs (State-wise)\n●\nRamgiri Hills Peddapalli district, Telangana mein hain — Eastern Ghats/Mahendra Parvat ka hissa,\nsaath hi Maikal Range (jo Satpura Range ka hissa hai) mein bhi sthith hain — CGPSC ne (B) Satpura ko\nsahi maana, par multiple options possible hain, disputed question hai. [Q36]\n●\nMatch karo: Garo — Meghalaya, Miri — Arunachal Pradesh, Kollai Mallai — Tamil Nadu, Dalma —\nJharkhand. [Q38]\n●\nDoddabetta (Nilgiri Hills) Tamil Nadu mein hai — Anaimalai Hills mein NAHI. Kodaikanal, Palni Hills\n(Dindigul district, TN) mein hai. [Q17, Q40]\n10. Central India Hill Sequence (Satpura Sub-Ranges)\n●\nWest-to-east Central India hills sequence: Satpura → Mahadeo → Maikal → Chotanagpur. Satpura region\nke andar (west-to-east): Barwani Hills → Mahadeo Range → Maikal Range. [Q44, Q45]\n●\nDhupgarh peak (Satpura Range ki sabse ooncha peak) Pachmarhi, M.P. mein hai. [Q35]\n11. State-wise Highest Peaks (Match-the-Following)\n●\nMukandara hills Rajasthan mein Vindhyan ranges ka extension hain (Dora mountain, Alwar hills, Girwa\nhills se alag). [Q41]\n●\nSalher (Nashik district, Maharashtra) Sahyadri/Western Ghats mein hai, Eastern Ghats mein NAHI —\nSahyadri ka sabse\n\nऊंचाkila aur 2nd highest peak (1567m) hai — Gali Konda, Sinkram Gutta, Madugula\nKonda Eastern Ghats mein hain. [Q42]\n●\nState-wise sabse ooncha peaks yaad rakho: Kerala — Anaimudi, Nagaland — Saramati, Uttarakhand —\nNanda Devi, Tamil Nadu — Doddabetta. [Q43]\n●\nParasnath Hill (Jharkhand, Giridih district) height ~1365m hai — yahan Shikharji Jain temple hai (23rd\nTirthankara Parasnath ke naam par). [Q37]\n12. Western Ghats Local Names (North to South) & Tea Gardens\n●\nWestern Ghats north-to-south local names: Sahyadri (Maharashtra-Goa-Karnataka) → Nilgiri (TN-\nKerala-Karnataka) → Anaimalai (TN-Kerala) → Cardamom Hills (Kerala-TN). [Q47]\n●\nTea plantations wale hills: Kanan Devan (Idukki, Kerala/Munnar), Nilgiri, Darjeeling — Girnar\n(Gujarat) mein tea plantation NAHI hai (ye ek common wrong-option trap hai). [Q48]\n13. Amarkantak, Maikal & River Origins\n●\nHill-State match: Bateshwar Hill — Bihar (Bhagalpur), Chin Range — Manipur, Dhoshi Hill —\nHaryana (Mahendragarh), Bilari Range — nearest ko Karnataka ka Bellary/Ballari Gudda maana\njaata hai. [Q49]\n●\nAmarkantak peak Maikal Hills mein hai, jahan se Narmada aur Son dono rivers nikalti hain. Narmada\npeninsular India ki sabse badi river hai (Arabian Sea mein girti hai) — north mein Vindhya, south mein\nSatpura range hai, aur Narmada inke beech ki rift valley se hokar behti hai. [Q51]"," EXAM TRAP — Amarkantak — Vindhya aur Satpura ka sangam hai, Sahyadri ka NAHI\n⚠️\n●\nCommon wrong statements: Amarkantak Vindhya-Satpura ka confluence hai (Sahyadri ka NAHI);\nBiligirirangan Hills Karnataka mein hain (Satpura ka eastern part NAHI); Seshachalam Hills Eastern\nGhats (Andhra Pradesh) ka hissa hain (Western Ghats ka NAHI) — teeno statements is tarah galat\ncombinations hain. [Q50]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0030","t":"02.iv Mountain Peaks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MOUNTAIN PEAKS — FULL MIND MAP\n🗻\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Highest Peak in India — K2 (Godwin Austin)\n2. World's Top Peaks & Their Location (Everest, Kanchenjunga, Makalu)\n3. Everest — Height, Records & Women Mountaineers\n4. Nanda Devi & Uttarakhand Peaks (Kamet, Trishul)\n5. Peaks NOT in India — Common Confusion Traps\n6. East-to-West Peak/Range Sequences\n7. State-wise Highest Peaks (Peninsular India)\n8. Match-the-Following — Peak/Mountain Pairs\n1. Highest Peak in India — K2 (Godwin Austin)\n●\nIndia ki sabse ooncha peak K2 (Godwin Austin) hai — height 8611m, Ladakh mein Karakoram range mein\nlocated, aur ye duniya ki dusri sabse ooncha peak bhi hai. Agar options mein K2 na ho, to Kanchenjunga\nnext-best answer ban jaata hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10]\n2. World's Top Peaks & Their Location (Everest, Kanchenjunga, Makalu)\n●\nDuniya ki top peaks (descending height): Mount Everest (8848.86m, Nepal-China/Tibet) > K2/Godwin\nAustin (8611m, India) > Kanchenjunga (8598m, Sikkim-Nepal border) > Makalu (8463m, Nepal). [Q12]\n●\nKanchenjunga North Sikkim district (India) aur Taplejung district (Nepal) ki border par hai — dono countries\nclaim karte hain (disputed/dual-answer question type). [Q11]\n3. Everest — Height, Records & Women Mountaineers\n●\nMount Everest Nepal-China (Tibet) border par hai — Nepal mein ise 'Sagarmatha' kaha jaata hai, height\n8848.86m (Nepal-China joint 2020 announcement) — options mein 'Nepal' aur 'Tibet' dono disputed answer\nmaane jaate hain. [Q2, Q3]\n●\nWomen-mountaineer records: Junko Tabei (Japan) — duniya ki pehli mahila jo Everest chadi (1975);\nBachendri Pal — pehli Indian mahila (1984); Santosh Yadav — dusri Indian mahila, aur duniya ki\npehli mahila jo Everest do baar chadi (1992, 1993). [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7]\n4. Nanda Devi & Uttarakhand Peaks (Kamet, Trishul)\n●\nNanda Devi (7817m) India ki 4th highest peak hai (K2, Kanchenjunga, Nanga Parbat ke baad) — Garhwal\nHimalaya, Uttarakhand mein hai. Do peaks hain: Nanda Devi West (7817m) aur East (7434m, Chamoli-\nPithoragarh-Bageshwar border). UNESCO ne 1988 mein World Heritage Site declare kiya. [Q1, Q13, Q14, Q15]\n●\nTrishul peak group (3 peaks: I-7120m, II-6690m, III-6008m) Bageshwar district, Uttarakhand mein hai —\nkoi bhi peak 7500m se zyada NAHI hai (ye ek common wrong-statement trap hai). [Q27]\n5. Peaks NOT in India — Common Confusion Traps"," ●\nNamcha Barwa Tibet (China) mein hai — Garhwal Himalaya mein NAHI (kuch purani NCERT mein\nArunachal Pradesh diya gaya hai, isliye confusion hota hai). Nokrek peak Garo Hills (Meghalaya) ki sabse\nooncha peak hai — Sikkim Himalaya mein NAHI. [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP — Namcha Barwa — Tibet/China mein hai, kabhi-kabhi Arunachal se confuse hota hai\n⚠️\n●\nIndia mein NAHI hone wali peaks: Gosainthan (Tibet, Nepal border ke paas), Gurla Mandhata (China),\nDhaulagiri (Nepal). India mein hone wali peaks (in confusions ke against): Kamet, Nanda Devi, Trishul,\nNanga Parbat (Ladakh). [Q21, Q23, Q24]\n6. East-to-West Peak/Range Sequences\n●\nPeaks east-to-west sequence: Namcha Barwa → Kanchenjunga → Mount Everest → Nanda Devi (ek\nvariant mein Everest se pehle Makalu/Dhaulagiri bhi aa sakte hain). [Q20]\n●\nMountain ranges east-to-west: Garo Hills (Meghalaya) → Nanda Devi (Uttarakhand) → Kamet\n(Uttarakhand) → K2 (Ladakh, Karakoram). [Q16]\n7. State-wise Highest Peaks (Peninsular India)\n●\nAravalli ki sabse ooncha peak Guru Shikhar (1722m, Sirohi district, Rajasthan) hai. Agar options mein\nGuru Shikhar na ho to Kumbhalgarh (1224m) next-highest ban jaata hai. [Q17, Q18]\n●\nState-wise sabse ooncha peaks yaad rakho: Tamil Nadu — Doddabetta, Rajasthan — Guru Shikhar,\nNagaland — Saramati, Madhya Pradesh — Dhupgarh. Chhattisgarh ki sabse ooncha peak Gaurlata\n(Samri Pat, Balrampur-Ramanujganj district) hai. [Q25, Q26]\n●\nAscending height order yaad rakho: Panchmarhi (1067m) < Mahendragiri (1501m) < Guru Shikhar\n(1722m) < Anaimudi (2695m). [Q19]\n8. Match-the-Following — Peak/Mountain Pairs\n●\nCommon wrong-pairs (exam trap): Kodaikanal Palni Hills mein hai, Anaimalai Hills mein NAHI; Shimla\nShivalik/Lesser Himalaya mein hai, Pir Panjal Range mein NAHI — ye dono common galat-pairing\noptions hote hain jinhe carefully identify karna padta hai. [Q22]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0031","t":"02.ix.a Indian Coastline","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" INDIAN COASTLINE — FULL MIND MAP\n🌊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Plate Tectonics Theory — Origin\n2. Mean Sea Level — Chennai Reference Point\n3. Territorial Waters Limit\n4. Total Coastline Length of India\n5. Longest Coastline State — Gujarat\n6. Number of Coastal States\n7. 'Ratnakara' — Ancient Name for Indian Ocean\n8. Coastal Erosion — Main Cause\n1. Plate Tectonics Theory — Origin\n●\nPlate Tectonics theory 1960s mein develop hui — H.H. Hess (aur Wilson, Morgan, Parker, McKenzie)\njaise scientists ka contribution tha. Ye theory Seafloor Spreading theory par based hai — statement 'H.H.\nHess ne 1967 mein akele diya' galat hai (multiple contributors the), lekin 'seafloor spreading pe based hai'\nwala part sahi hai. [Q1]\n2. Mean Sea Level — Chennai Reference Point\n●\nIndia ka mean sea level Chennai coast se measure kiya jaata hai — Mumbai, Kochi, Visakhapatnam se\nNAHI (common confusion trap). [Q2]\n3. Territorial Waters Limit\n●\nIndia ki territorial waters ki limit coast se 12 nautical miles tak hai — iss area par state ka territorial\njurisdiction hota hai. [Q3]\n4. Total Coastline Length of India\n●\nIndia ki total coastline lambaai 7516.6 km (purana figure) — naya updated figure 11098.81 km hai. India\nteen taraf se ghira hai: East mein Bay of Bengal, South mein Indian Ocean, West mein Arabian Sea. Ek\nalag disputed question mein 6200/6100/5985/6175 km jaise options diye jaate hain — ye sab galat/outdated\nfigures hain, is baare mein exact confusion exists hai. [Q4, Q5]\n5. Longest Coastline State — Gujarat\n●\nIndia ka sabse lambi coastline wala state Gujarat hai — Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Kerala\nse zyada. Ye fact multiple baar (alag phrasing mein) puchha jaata hai, isliye pakka yaad rakho. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n6. Number of Coastal States\n●\nIndia mein 9 states coastline share karte hain (Gujarat, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Kerala, Tamil Nadu,\nAndhra Pradesh, Odisha, West Bengal) — 7, 8, ya 10 NAHI. [Q9]"," 7. 'Ratnakara' — Ancient Name for Indian Ocean\n●\nAncient Indian historical geography mein 'Ratnakara' term Indian Ocean ko denote karta tha — matlab\n'jahan ratna/jewels milte hain'. Arabian Sea ya Bay of Bengal ke liye NAHI use hota tha. [Q10]\n8. Coastal Erosion — Main Cause\n●\nCoastal erosion mein waves, tides, currents, tsunami, human activities sab ka role hota hai — lekin maximum\ncoastal erosion 'Waves (lehron)' se hota hai. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0032","t":"02.ix.b Eastern and Western Coast","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" EASTERN AND WESTERN COAST — FULL\n🏖️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. West Coast Cities North-to-South Sequence\n2. Tharangambadi — Danish Colony (Tamil Nadu Coast)\n3. Underwater Coastal Relief Contours\n4. West Coast vs East Coast City Identification\n5. Famous Beaches — State Match Pairs\n6. Coromandel Coast — Tamil Nadu & Andhra Pradesh\n7. Cape Comorin / Kanyakumari\n8. Four Coast Names (North & South, East & West)\n9. Rann of Kutch — Sea-Level Marshland\n1. West Coast Cities North-to-South Sequence\n●\nWest coast cities north-to-south order: Janjira (Raigad, Maharashtra) → Sindhudurg (Maharashtra) →\nKannur (Kerala) → Nagercoil (Kanyakumari, Tamil Nadu). [Q1]\n2. Tharangambadi — Danish Colony (Tamil Nadu Coast)\n●\n'Tharangambadi' (Tamil Nadu coast) 1620-1845 tak Denmark ki colony thi — yahan New Jerusalem Church\naur Zion Church jaisi Danish buildings hain; 1845 mein Danish logo ne ise British ko bech kar chhod diya.\n[Q2]\n3. Underwater Coastal Relief Contours\n●\nCoastal map par diye gaye divisions underwater relief contours dikhate hain (sea floor ki depth) — inke\nbasis par 4 relief zones hote hain: continental shelf, continental slope, deep sea plains, aur ocean\ntrenches/deeps. [Q3]\n4. West Coast vs East Coast City Identification\n●\nWest coast cities: Janjira (Maharashtra), Udupi (Karnataka). East coast cities: Auroville (Tamil Nadu-\nPuducherry, Coromandel coast), Tuticorin (Tamil Nadu) — is set mein 'Janjira aur Udupi' hi sahi West-\ncoast combination hai. [Q4]\n5. Famous Beaches — State Match Pairs\n●\nBeach-state match: Digha — West Bengal, Gopalpur — Odisha, Calangute — Goa, Marina — Tamil\nNadu. [Q5]\n6. Coromandel Coast — Tamil Nadu & Andhra Pradesh\n●\nCoromandel Coast — Tamil Nadu aur Andhra Pradesh ke tat ka naam. Ye Krishna Delta se Cape Comorin\n(Kanyakumari) tak failaa hai (False Divi Point, AP se Cape Comorin, TN tak). [Q6, Q7, Q8]"," 7. Cape Comorin / Kanyakumari\n●\nCape Comorin, Kanyakumari, Tamil Nadu ko kaha jaata hai — Indian subcontinent ka southern tip. [Q9]\n8. Four Coast Names (North & South, East & West)\n●\nChar coastal region names yaad rakho: West coast — North part: Konkan Coast, South part: Malabar\nCoast; East coast — North part: Northern Circars, South part: Coromandel Coast. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Konkan = West-North, Malabar = West-South, Circars = East-North, Coromandel =\n⚠️\nEast-South\n9. Rann of Kutch — Sea-Level Marshland\n●\nRann of Kutch (Gujarat's Kachchh district + Pakistan's Sindh) repeated sea-level falls ka best example hai\n— kabhi Arabian Sea ka shallow hissa tha, geological shift se sea-connection band ho gaya, aur dheere-\ndheere seasonal marshy salt desert ban gaya. Present shoreline aur sand-dunes ~5000 saal pehle ke rainless\nyears ka result hain. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0033","t":"02.v Valleys","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" VALLEYS — FULL MIND MAP\n⛰️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Himalayan Valleys — Kullu, Kashmir, Sangla, Yumthang, Dzukou\n2. Ladakh Region Valleys — Nelang, Markha, Galwan, Shaksgam\n3. Silent Valley (Kerala) & Kunthi River\n4. North-East Sediment Basin — Mizoram (Molassis Basin)\n1. Himalayan Valleys — Kullu, Kashmir, Sangla, Yumthang, Dzukou\n●\nKullu Valley (Himachal Pradesh) Dhauladhar aur Pir Panjal ranges ke beech mein hai. [Q1]\n●\nKashmir Valley tectonic origin ki maani jaati hai (Zanskar aur Pir Panjal ranges ke beech), glacio-fluvio-\nlacustrine aur aeolian processes se bani — hालांki 'erosional' aur 'tectonic' dono options exam-commission\ndwara kabhi-kabhi correct maane gaye hain (disputed-type question). [Q2]\n●\nMatch karo — Valley → State: Markha Valley → Ladakh (pehle J&K ka hissa), Dzukou Valley →\nManipur-Nagaland border (Japfu Range ke peeche, 2438m, Kohima se ~30km), Sangla Valley →\nHimachal Pradesh (Kinnaur district, Baspa river), Yumthang Valley → Sikkim (Gangtok se ~149km,\nhot springs ke liye famous). [Q4]\n2. Ladakh Region Valleys — Nelang, Markha, Galwan, Shaksgam\n●\nNelang Valley Uttarakhand mein hai (Uttarkashi district, Gangotri National Park ke andar) — Indo-China\nborder ke paas, 1962 war ke baad civilians ke liye band thi, 2015 mein tourists ke liye reopen hui. [Q3]\n●\nGalwan Valley ka naam Ghulam Rassul Galwan (ek Ladakhi explorer) ke naam par pada hai — usne\n'Servant of Sahibs' naam ki English book likhi thi. Galwan river isi valley ke formation ka main source hai.\n[Q7]\n●\nShaksgam Valley: 1963 ke China-Pakistan 'Boundary Agreement' ke tahat Pakistan ne 5180 sq km area\n(PoK ka hissa) illegally China ko de diya tha. Ye strategically important region hai — India ne China ki\ninfrastructure activities ka protest kiya hai yahan, aur is boundary agreement ko kabhi recognize nahi kiya.\n[Q8]\n3. Silent Valley (Kerala) & Kunthi River\n●\nSilent Valley National Park Kerala (Palakkad district) mein hai — Nilgiri Hills (Western Ghats) mein,\nNallamalai range mein NAHI (ye ek common wrong-statement trap hai). Pathrakkadavu Hydroelectric\nproject isi park se ~1km door proposed hai, aur Kunthi river (Thuthapuzha ki tributary) Silent Valley ke\nrainforests se hi nikalti hai. [Q5, Q6]\n EXAM TRAP — Nallamalai vs Nilgiri Hills — Silent Valley kis range mein hai\n⚠️\n4. North-East Sediment Basin — Mizoram (Molassis Basin)"," ●\nMizoram ko 'Molassis Basin' bhi kaha jaata hai kyunki ye unconsolidated sediments se bana hai. Mizoram ek\nhilly north-east state hai jahan homogenous tribal population hai — common language Lushai hai. [Q9]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0034","t":"02.vi Passes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" PASSES — FULL MIND MAP\n🛤️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Western Ghats Passes — Palghat, Thalghat, Bhorghat\n2. Himalayan Passes — Standard State Pairings\n3. Nathu La — Full Details & History\n4. Zoji La / Zojila — Location & Tunnel Project\n5. Lipulekh Pass — Uttarakhand\n6. Uttarakhand Passes — Mana, Niti & Others\n7. West-to-East Pass Sequence\n8. Pass Elevations (Height from Sea Level)\n1. Western Ghats Passes — Palghat, Thalghat, Bhorghat\n●\nWestern Ghats ke 3 main passes: Palghat (Kerala — Nilgiri aur Annamalai/Anaimalai Hills ke beech,\nPalakkad-Coimbatore ko jodta hai), Thalghat (Maharashtra — Kasara ke paas, Mumbai-Nashik\nroute), Bhorghat (Maharashtra — Mumbai-Pune ko jodta hai). Khyber Pass Western Ghats mein\nNAHI hai — wo Pakistan-Afghanistan border par hai (common trap: 'kaun sa Western Ghats ka pass nahi\nhai'). [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. Himalayan Passes — Standard State Pairings\n●\nYaad rakhne wale standard pass-state pairs: Chang La — Ladakh, Rohtang — Himachal Pradesh, Bomdi\nLa aur Se La — Arunachal Pradesh, Shipki La — Himachal Pradesh (Kinnaur district), Nathu La —\nSikkim, Zoji La — Ladakh (J&K se bifurcate hua) — Mana pass Uttarakhand mein hai. [Q1, Q5, Q6, Q13,\nQ14, Q18, Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Common wrong-pairs: Se La 'Uttarakhand' nahi (Arunachal hai); Nathu La\n⚠️\n'Meghalaya' nahi (Sikkim hai); Shipki La 'J&K' nahi (H.P. hai)\n●\nAur match-pairs: Bum La — Arunachal Pradesh, Jelep La — Sikkim, Muling La — Uttarakhand,\nBanihal — J&K (UT), Diphu — Arunachal Pradesh, Aghil — Ladakh. [Q11, Q12, Q15]\n3. Nathu La — Full Details & History\n●\nNathu La (Sikkim, height ~4310m) Gangtok se ~55km east hai, Tibet ki Chumbi Valley mein khulta hai —\nIndia-China ke teen open trading posts mein se ek hai (baaki: Shipki La-H.P., Lipulekh-Uttarakhand). 1962\nwar ke baad band hua tha, 2006 mein trade ke liye reopen hua. [Q7, Q10]\n4. Zoji La / Zojila — Location & Tunnel Project\n●\nZojila Pass Ladakh mein NH-1 par Uri aur Leh ke beech hai. Zoji-la Tunnel (Kargil district mein under-\nconstruction) Srinagar aur Leh ko all-weather connectivity dega, Ganderbal aur Drass ke beech Zojila pass\nke neeche banaya jaa raha hai. [Q8, Q9]\n5. Lipulekh Pass — Uttarakhand"," ●\nLipulekh Pass Uttarakhand (Pithoragarh district) mein hai — India-China border, 'Uttar Pradesh' galat\noption hai (common confusion trap). Ye Kailash Valley ke through Mansarovar lake tak entry deta hai. [Q16,\nQ17]\n6. Uttarakhand Passes — Mana, Niti & Others\n●\nMana Pass (aka Dungri La) Nanda Devi Biosphere Reserve, Uttarakhand mein hai — India-Tibet border,\nyahan Deotal lake hai jahan se Saraswati river (Alaknanda ki tributary) nikalti hai. [Q20]\n●\nKingri-Wingri aur Neeti-Mana bhi Uttarakhand ke passes hain — Neeti Uttarakhand ko Tibet se jodta hai.\n[Q21]\n7. West-to-East Pass Sequence\n●\nWest-to-east sequence: Shipki La (H.P.) → Lipulekh (Uttarakhand) → Nathu La (Sikkim) → Bomdi La\n(Arunachal Pradesh). [Q22]\n8. Pass Elevations (Height from Sea Level)\n●\nHeight comparison (options mein diye jaane wale): Nathu La (~4310m) > Rohtang (~3978m) > Zojila\n(~3528m) > Khyber-Pakistan (~1070m) — par actual India ka sabse ooncha pass Yangzi Diwan hai, jo\naksar options mein nahi diya jaata (isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer ban jaata hai). [Q23]\n●\nAur ek height-match set (sab Himachal Pradesh mein, Banihal J&K mein): Debsa — 5360m, Bara-lacha —\n4850m, Rohtang — 3978m, Banihal — 2832m. [Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0035","t":"02.vii Snow Lines and Glaciers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🧊 SNOW LINES AND GLACIERS — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Snow-Line — Definition & Height in Himalayas\n2. Siachen — India's Largest Glacier\n3. Glacier Length Comparisons\n4. Chaurabari Glacier & Kedarnath\n5. Himalayan Glacier Melting Rate\n6. Milam Glacier — Kumaun Region\n7. Glacier–River Origin Pairs\n8. Glaciers in Decreasing Order of Length\n1. Snow-Line — Definition & Height in Himalayas\n●\nSnow-line = wo altitude jiske upar saal bhar ground par kuch snow bani rehti hai. Himalaya mein average\nheight Northern part mein 5500-6000m, Southern part mein 4500-6000m — overall range 4300m se\n6000m ke beech maani jaati hai. [Q1]\n●\nUttar Pradesh mein snow-line ka average height wala question disputed/deleted hai — kyunki Uttarakhand\nke separate hone ke baad U.P. mein snowfall hoti hi nahi, isliye koi bhi option sahi nahi hai. [Q2]\n2. Siachen — India's Largest Glacier\n●\nSiachen India ka sabse bada glacier hai — Eastern Karakoram range mein, Nubra Valley ke North mein\nlocated. Ye duniya ka sabse ooncha battlefield bhi hai, jo Central Asia ko Indian subcontinent se demarcate\nkarta hai aur Pakistan-China ko separate karta hai. Length ~72km (textbooks) ya 76.64km (World Glacier\nInventory), area ~1056.42 sq km. [Q3, Q4, Q6]\n3. Glacier Length Comparisons\n●\nOptions-based comparison (jab Siachen options mein na ho): Gangotri (30.0km) > Rundun (19km) >\nKanchenjunga (16km) > Kedarnath (14.5km) — is set mein Gangotri sabse lamba hota hai. [Q5]\n4. Chaurabari Glacier & Kedarnath\n●\nChaurabari Glacier (Garhwal Himalaya, Uttarakhand) Kedarnath Temple ke North mein hai — iske\npighalne se bani lake ka naam Gandhi Sarovar hai. Mandakini river isi glacier se nikalti hai. [Q7, Q10]\n5. Himalayan Glacier Melting Rate\n●\nHimalayan glaciers duniya mein sabse tezi se pighal rahe hain (highest melting rate) — Gangotri Glacier\n(jahan se Ganga nikalti hai) pichhle 50 saalon mein apne size ka aadha reh gaya hai. [Q8]\n6. Milam Glacier — Kumaun Region"," ●\nMilam Glacier Uttarakhand ke Kumaun region ka major glacier hai — Gori Ganga (Kali River) isi glacier\nse nikalti hai. [Q9]\n7. Glacier–River Origin Pairs\n●\nSahi glacier-river pairs: Bandarpunch → Yamuna, Bara Shigri → Chenab, Siachen → Nubra. Milam →\nMandakini GALAT hai (Mandakini asal mein Chorabari glacier se nikalti hai); Zemu → Manas GALAT\nhai (Zemu, Kanchenjunga ke base par Eastern Himalaya ka sabse bada glacier hai, ~26km lamba, lekin\nManas se related nahi). [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Milam-Mandakini aur Zemu-Manas dono galat pairs hain — mostly asked in reverse\n⚠️\ntrap format\n8. Glaciers in Decreasing Order of Length\n●\nLength ke hisaab se decreasing order: Hispar > Biafo > Drang Drung > Sonapani > Bara Shigri. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0036","t":"02.viii Plateaus","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" PLATEAUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Deccan Trap — Formation Period\n2. Meghalaya Plateau — Peninsular Plateau ka Extension\n3. Extra-Peninsular Mountains — Cenozoic Era\n4. Chota Nagpur Plateau — Dhanbad & Structure\n5. Map-Based Region Identification (Rift Valley, Rain Shadow)\n6. Malwa Plateau — Location Between Aravalli-Vindhya\n7. Vindhyan Scarpland — Bhander Plateau\n8. Dandakaranya Region\n9. Bihar's Geological Age Comparison\n10. Meghalaya Plateau — Constituent Hills\n11. Albama Hill — Bijapur Upland\n12. Peninsular Plateau — Extent, Height & Boundaries\n1. Deccan Trap — Formation Period\n●\nDeccan Plateau ki Basaltic Lava rocks Cretaceous period mein bani (~66.25 million years pehle) — large-\nscale volcanic activity se. Peninsular India ki rocks ki origin ~3600 million years purani hai; Carboniferous\nperiod mein Damodar, Son, Mahanadi aur Godavari basins mein coal bana. [Q1]\n2. Meghalaya Plateau — Peninsular Plateau ka Extension\n●\nMeghalaya plateau Peninsular Plateau ka extension hai — Malda Gap se separate hua hai. Peninsular\nplateau shape mein triangular hai, U.P.-Bihar ke plains se south tak poore peninsula ko cover karta hai. [Q2]\n3. Extra-Peninsular Mountains — Cenozoic Era\n●\nIndia ke Extra-peninsular mountains (jaise Himalaya) Cenozoic Era mein bane the. [Q3]\n4. Chota Nagpur Plateau — Dhanbad & Structure\n●\nDhanbad, Chota Nagpur plateau ka sabse dense-population wala district hai — kyunki yahan mining\nindustries ka development aur industrialization hua hai (sirf coal/iron-ore ki availability se density nahi\nbadhi, actual reason hai mining-driven industrialization). Red soil hone ki wajah se agriculture yahan zyada\nuseful nahi. [Q4]\n●\nChota Nagpur Plateau (Jharkhand + Odisha, WB, Bihar, Chhattisgarh ke adjacent parts, ~86239 sq km) ek\n'front sloping' plateau hai — steep scarps ke saath sharp slope-break. Central-western part mein 'Patland'\n~1100m height tak extend hota hai. [Q5]\n5. Map-Based Region Identification (Rift Valley, Rain Shadow)"," ●\nMap-labeling type question ka pattern: Rift Valley region (Narmada-Tapti) → Chhattisgarh plain\n(Mahanadi se drain) → Chota Nagpur plateau → Rain shadow region (Western Ghats ka hissa) — is\norder mein A-B-C-D label kiye jaate hain. [Q6]\n6. Malwa Plateau — Location Between Aravalli-Vindhya\n●\nMalwa Plateau (~150000 sq km, length 530km, width 390km) Aravalli aur Vindhya ranges ke beech hai —\nnorthern end Aravalli se, southern end Vindhya range se, aur eastern border Bundelkhand plateau se\ndetermine hoti hai. [Q7]\n7. Vindhyan Scarpland — Bhander Plateau\n●\nVindhyan Scarpland ka southern part 'Bhander Plateau' kehlata hai — steep aur rugged terrain ke liye jaana\njaata hai, Vindhya mountains ka hissa maana jaata hai. [Q8]\n8. Dandakaranya Region\n●\nDandakaranya region (~89078 sq km) Odisha, Chhattisgarh, Telangana, Maharashtra aur Andhra\nPradesh mein failaa hai (isliye 'sirf ek state' wala option galat hoga — multiple states involved hain), Central\nIndia mein located — east-west ~480km, north-south ~320km extent. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n9. Bihar's Geological Age Comparison\n●\nBihar ke areas ka geological order (oldest se newest): Kharagpur Hills (Dharwad order, sabse purana) →\nRohtas Plateau (Vindhyan order) → North-Western Hills (Tertiary order) → North Ganga Plains\n(sabse naya). [Q12]\n10. Meghalaya Plateau — Constituent Hills\n●\nMeghalaya Plateau ka hissa: Garo, Khasi aur Jaintia Hills. Bhuban Hills Meghalaya plateau ka hissa\nNAHI hai — wo Assam ki Barak Valley mein hai. [Q13]\n11. Albama Hill — Bijapur Upland\n●\nAlbama Hill, Bijapur upland ke South mein located hai. [Q14]\n12. Peninsular Plateau — Extent, Height & Boundaries\n●\nPeninsular plateau river plains se 150m se 600-900m ki elevation tak uthta hai — ek irregular triangle. Iski\nouter boundaries: Delhi Ridge (NW, Aravalli ka extension), Rajmahal Hills (East), Gir Range (West),\nCardamom Hills (South) — northeast mein Shillong/Karbi-Anglong plateau ke roop mein bhi extension hai.\n[Q15]\n●\nYe India ke sabse purane aur stable landmasses mein se ek hai — multiple 'patland' plateaus se bana\n(Hazaribagh, Palamu, Ranchi, Malwa, Coimbatore, Karnataka plateau, etc). Overall height West se East ki\ntaraf GHATTI hai (badhti nahi) — river-flow pattern isi se prove hota hai. [Q15, Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Peninsular plateau height 1000-1500m NAHI (asal mein 150-900m); Gir range East\n⚠️\nmein nahi West mein hai"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0037","t":"02.x.a Island groups of the Bay of Bengal","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ISLAND GROUPS OF THE BAY OF BENGAL —\n🏝️\n\nFULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Saddle Peak — Highest Peak of Andaman\n2. Andaman & Nicobar — Basic Facts & Island Count\n3. Ten Degree Channel\n4. Barren Island — India's Only Active Volcano\n5. Sriharikota — Space Centre Island\n6. Adam's Bridge (Ram Setu)\n7. Great Nicobar — Nearest Foreign Landmass\n1. Saddle Peak — Highest Peak of Andaman\n●\n'Saddle Peak' (732m) Andaman-Nicobar ki sabse ooncha peak hai — North Andaman (Diglipur ke paas)\nmein located. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Andaman & Nicobar — Basic Facts & Island Count\n●\nAndaman aur Nicobar do alag islands NAHI balki Bay of Bengal mein ek group of islands hai. Total\nislands (islands/islets/rock outcrops) ki sankhya 836 hai — options mein diye jaane wale 200/220/240/250 sab\ngalat approximations hain (disputed question). [Q3, Q4]\n3. Ten Degree Channel\n●\nTen Degree Channel Andaman aur Nicobar islands ko separate karta hai — width ~150km, naam 10° North\nlatitude ke parallel hone ki wajah se pada hai. (Lakshadweep-Minicoy, South-Little Andaman jaise options\nisse related NAHI hain — common confusion trap). [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n4. Barren Island — India's Only Active Volcano\n●\nBarren Island South Asia ka ekmatra confirmed active volcano hai — Bay of Bengal (Andaman Sea)\nmein, Port Blair se ~135km northeast (Great Nicobar se 540km, NOT 140km — common wrong-\nstatement). Pehla recorded eruption 1787 mein hua tha, phir 1991 (6 mahine tak chala), aur uske baad 1994-\n95 aur 2005-06 mein bhi eruptions hue (2005-06 wala 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake se linked maana jaata\nhai) — isliye 'sirf 1991 ke baad se inactive hai' wala statement GALAT hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — Barren Island — Great Nicobar se distance 140km NAHI, 540km hai; 1991 ke baad bhi\n⚠️\neruptions hue hain\n5. Sriharikota — Space Centre Island\n●\nSriharikota island (Andhra Pradesh) Pulicat Lake ke paas hai — isse Bay of Bengal se separate karta hai.\nYahan Satish Dhawan Space Centre located hai. [Q12]\n6. Adam's Bridge (Ram Setu)"," ●\nAdam's Bridge (aka Ram Setu) India ke Dhanushkodi (Pamban island) se shuru hoke Sri Lanka ke\nMannar island tak shoals ki chain ke roop mein failaa hai. Pamban island 2.2km lambe Pamban Bridge se\nIndian mainland se semi-connected hai. [Q13]\n7. Great Nicobar — Nearest Foreign Landmass\n●\nGreat Nicobar (India ka sabse southern island, 6°45'-7°15' N, 93°37'-93°56' E) ke geographically sabse kareeb\nSumatra (Indonesia) hai — Borneo, Java, Sri Lanka se zyada close. Java, Sumatra ke south mein hai;\nBorneo, Sumatra ke east mein hai. [Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0038","t":"02.x.b Island group of Arabian Sea","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ISLAND GROUPS OF THE ARABIAN SEA —\n🏝️\n\nFULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Lakshadweep — Location, Count, Capital & Naming\n2. Lakshadweep — Coral Origin & Atolls\n3. Coral Reefs in India — Where Found/Not Found\n4. Remote vs Offshore Islands\n5. Islands Between India-Sri Lanka & City Islands\n6. Salsette — India's Most Populous Island\n7. Gulf of Kutch/Khambhat Islands — Match Pairs\n8. Divi Island — Krishna River Delta\n9. Kori Creek & Sir Creek — India-Pakistan Border Disputes\n1. Lakshadweep — Location, Count, Capital & Naming\n●\nLakshadweep Arabian Sea mein hai (Kerala coast se 220-440km door), 36 islands ka group hai, capital\nKavaratti, sabse bada island Andrott, total area ~32 sq km. Pehle inhe Laccadive, Minicoy aur Amindive\nnaam se jaana jaata tha — 1973 mein renamed hokar 'Lakshadweep' bane (matlab: 'ek lakh dweep'). [Q1, Q2,\nQ5, Q6, Q7]\n●\nMinicoy dusra sabse bada island hai, baaki islands se 9° Channel se separate hota hai. Lakshadweep\nMalabar Coast (Kerala) ke kareeb hai — Coromandel Coast (Tamil Nadu) ke NAHI (common wrong-\nstatement). [Q2]\n●\nTilanchong Laccadive/Lakshadweep group ka hissa NAHI hai — wo actually Andaman-Nicobar group\nmein aata hai (baaki Agathi, Kavaratti, Kalpeni sab Lakshadweep ka hissa hain). [Q3]\n2. Lakshadweep — Coral Origin & Atolls\n●\nLakshadweep poora coral reef ka accumulation hai — isliye ise 'coral island' bola jaata hai. 'Atolls' (ring-\nshaped coral islands) commonly Lakshadweep ke paas milte hain — Sunderbans, Khambhat Gulf,\nRameshwaram ke paas NAHI. [Q4, Q8]\n3. Coral Reefs in India — Where Found/Not Found\n●\nIndia mein coral reefs 5 jagah milte hain: Andaman-Nicobar islands, Gulf of Mannar, Lakshadweep,\nMalvan (Maharashtra), Gulf of Kutch — Gulf of Cambay (Khambhat) mein NAHI milte (ye ek\ncommon exception-trap question hai). [Q8, Q9]\n EXAM TRAP — Coral reefs 5 jagah milte hain — Gulf of Cambay ek exception hai jahan NAHI milte\n⚠️\n4. Remote vs Offshore Islands\n●\nMinicoy India ke coast se sabse dooriston (remotest) islands mein se ek hai — Bhatkal, Arnala, Henry jaise\nislands offshore (coast ke najdeek) category mein aate hain. [Q10]"," 5. Islands Between India-Sri Lanka & City Islands\n●\nRameswaram Island (Ramanathapuram district, Tamil Nadu) India aur Sri Lanka ke beech hai. Elephanta\nIsland Mumbai (Gateway of India) se ~10km hai; Nicobar Island Bay of Bengal ke southeast mein 22 main\nislands ka group hai; Salsette Island Maharashtra mein hai jahan Mumbai aur Thane located hain. [Q11]\n●\nIndia ke island par bana sabse bada city Mumbai hai — Port Blair ka total area Mumbai se bada hai, par\ntownship perspective se Mumbai bada hai. [Q12]\n6. Salsette — India's Most Populous Island\n●\nIndia ka sabse zyada population wala island Salsette hai — isi par Mumbai city aur Thane district located\nhain (Majuli, Andaman, Lakshadweep se zyada populated). [Q13]\n7. Gulf of Kutch/Khambhat Islands — Match Pairs\n●\nIslands aur unki location match karo: Viyant Syodhar — Gulf of Kutch, Piram — Gulf of Cambay\n(Khambhat), Dwarka — Arabian Sea coast, Diu — Kathiawar coast. [Q14]\n8. Divi Island — Krishna River Delta\n●\nDivi (Diviseema) Island, Andhra Pradesh ke Krishna district mein, Krishna river ki distributaries ke beech\nlocated hai (jahan Krishna Bay of Bengal mein girti hai) — cyclones aur natural calamities ke liye prone hai.\n[Q15]\n9. Kori Creek & Sir Creek — India-Pakistan Border Disputes\n●\nKori Creek, Rann of Kutch (Gujarat) region mein hai — India-Pakistan ke beech ek maritime border. [Q16]\n●\nSir Creek dispute India-Pakistan ke beech hai — Rann of Kutch mein ~96km lambi tidal estuary, Gujarat ko\nPakistan ke Sindh province se separate karti hai. Dono countries iski demarcation line par agree nahi karte.\n[Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0039","t":"20.i Coffee","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" COFFEE — FULL MIND MAP\n☕\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. National Horticulture Board — Established 1984\n2. Coffee vs Tea — Cultivation Differences\n3. Karnataka — Largest Coffee Producer (70%+)\n4. Coffee Growing Areas Within Karnataka\n5. Chikmagalur — Coffee (Not Sugar); Mandya — Sugar (Not Coffee)\n1. National Horticulture Board — Established 1984\n●\nNational Horticulture Board 1984 mein (Society Registration Act 1860 ke tahat) establish hua —\nheadquarters Gurugram, Haryana mein hai. [Q1]\n2. Coffee vs Tea — Cultivation Differences\n●\nCoffee aur Tea dono hill-slopes par ugte hain, par difference: Coffee ko hot-humid tropical climate chahiye\n(tea tropical+subtropical dono mein ho sakti hai); Coffee seeds se propagate hoti hai, Tea stem-cuttings\nse. [Q2]\n3. Karnataka — Largest Coffee Producer (70%+)\n●\nKarnataka India ka sabse bada coffee producer hai (70.46%, 2022-23) — Kerala (20.58%), Tamil Nadu\n(5.31%) dusre-teesre number par. India mein 2 varieties: Arabica aur Robusta. [Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6]\n4. Coffee Growing Areas Within Karnataka\n●\nKarnataka mein coffee-growing areas: Chikmagalur, Coorg (Kodagu), Baba Budangiri — Pulneys\n(Palani Hills) Tamil Nadu mein hai, Karnataka mein NAHI. Karnataka ke baad Kerala dusre, Tamil\nNadu teesre number par (area ke hisaab se) hain. [Q7, Q9]\n5. Chikmagalur — Coffee (Not Sugar); Mandya — Sugar (Not Coffee)\n●\nKarnataka ke district-facts: Chikmagalur coffee ke liye famous hai (India mein coffee sabse pehle yahin\nugayi gayi thi) — Mandya sugar ke liye famous hai — dono statements (Chikmagalur-sugar, Mandya-\ncoffee) GALAT hain. [Q8]\n EXAM TRAP — Chikmagalur — Coffee ka origin place hai, sugar ke liye NAHI; Mandya — Sugar ke\n⚠️\nliye hai, coffee ke liye NAHI"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0040","t":"20.ii Tea and Rubber","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" TEA AND RUBBER — FULL MIND MAP\n🍵\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Major Tea States — Assam, WB, Tamil Nadu, Kerala\n2. India — #1 in Pulses & Tea (Historically)\n3. 2007-08 — India Was #1 in Tea Production\n4. Tea — Maximum Foreign Exchange Cash Crop\n5. Assam — Largest Tea Producer\n6. Tea — India Produces Surplus (Export)\n7. Tea Export Ranking — Kenya, China, Sri Lanka, India\n8. Tea's Ideal Climate — 150-200cm Rainfall, Sloped Hills\n9. 'Green Gold' — Tea Variety Name\n10. Coffee Board HQ — Bengaluru (Not Hyderabad)\n11. Barak Valley — Sugarcane (2nd Crop After Rice)\n12. Kerala — Largest Rubber Producer (71.13%)\n13. Rubber Districts — Ernakulam, Kottayam, Kozhikode, Kollam\n14. Stimulant Crops — Tea, Coffee, Tobacco, Opium\n15. Tea Board — Statutory Body, Kolkata HQ\n1. Major Tea States — Assam, WB, Tamil Nadu, Kerala\n●\nIndia ke major tea-producing states (2022-23): Assam, West Bengal, Tamil Nadu, Kerala — Tripura,\nHimachal Pradesh, Karnataka, Uttarakhand, Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur, Sikkim, Nagaland,\nMeghalaya, Mizoram, Bihar, Odisha mein chhote paimane par ugti hai. [Q1]\n2. India — #1 in Pulses & Tea (Historically)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt India pulses aur tea production+consumption mein leading tha — 2023 (FAO) mein\ntea leaves production mein India dusre number par aa gaya (China pehle), lekin pulses mein abhi bhi\npehle number par hai. [Q2]\n3. 2007-08 — India Was #1 in Tea Production\n●\n2007-08 mein India tea production+consumption dono mein top tha — ab (2023 FAO data) China pehle,\nIndia dusre number par hai. [Q3]\n4. Tea — Maximum Foreign Exchange Cash Crop\n●\nCash crops mein se India ko Tea export se sabse zyada foreign exchange milta hai — 2023-24 mein 250.73\nmillion kg tea export hua. [Q4]\n5. Assam — Largest Tea Producer\n●\nIndia ka sabse bada tea producer state Assam hai (2022-23) — area under cultivation aur production dono\nmein top. [Q5]"," 6. Tea — India Produces Surplus (Export)\n●\nIndia apni zaroorat se zyada Tea produce karta hai — Foodgrains, Petroleum, Petro-chemicals ke liye ye\nsach NAHI hai (in cheezon ko import karna padta hai). [Q6]\n7. Tea Export Ranking — Kenya, China, Sri Lanka, India\n●\nIndia major tea exporter hai (Assertion sahi) — par domestic consumption 'bahut kam' NAHI hai (Reason\ngalat) — 2023 ke top tea exporters: Kenya, China, Sri Lanka, India. [Q7]\n8. Tea's Ideal Climate — 150-200cm Rainfall, Sloped Hills\n●\nTea ke liye ideal conditions: 150-200cm annual rainfall, sloped hills (drainage ke liye) — Jute, Cotton,\nMaize ke liye nahi. [Q8]\n9. 'Green Gold' — Tea Variety Name\n●\n'Green Gold' tea ki ek variety hai — Coffee, Gold, Paddy se NAHI. [Q9]\n10. Coffee Board HQ — Bengaluru (Not Hyderabad)\n●\nBoard HQs: Spices Board — Kochi, Tea Board — Kolkata, Rubber Board — Kottayam sahi hain —\n'Coffee Board-Hyderabad' GALAT hai (asal HQ Bengaluru, Karnataka hai). [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Coffee Board — Bengaluru mein hai, Hyderabad mein NAHI\n⚠️\n11. Barak Valley — Sugarcane (2nd Crop After Rice)\n●\nBarak Valley mein main crop Rice hai — Sugarcane dusri sabse important crop hai (options mein Rice\nna hone par Sugarcane sahi answer). [Q11]\n12. Kerala — Largest Rubber Producer (71.13%)\n●\nKerala India ka sabse bada rubber producer hai — 2023-24 mein total production ka 71.13% Kerala se\n— India world mein 6th (FAO 2023) natural rubber producer hai. [Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15, Q16, Q17]\n13. Rubber Districts — Ernakulam, Kottayam, Kozhikode, Kollam\n●\nKerala ke main rubber-producing districts: Ernakulam, Kottayam, Kozhikode, Kollam. [Q12]\n14. Stimulant Crops — Tea, Coffee, Tobacco, Opium\n●\nStimulating (stimulus) crops mein Tea, Coffee, Tobacco, Opium, Poppy, Datura, Hemp, Betel nut shamil\nhain — Wheat (Rabi), Maize/Arhar (Kharif) is category mein NAHI hain. [Q18]\n15. Tea Board — Statutory Body, Kolkata HQ\n●\nTea Board statutory body hai (Tea Act 1953 ke section 4 ke tahat, 1 April 1954 constitute hua) —\nMinistry of Commerce and Industry ke tahat aata hai (Agriculture ministry NAHI) — HQ Kolkata\nmein hai (Bengaluru mein NAHI), overseas offices Dubai aur Moscow mein the (question ke waqt) —\nabhi sirf Moscow office hai. [Q19]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0041","t":"20.iii Other Plantation Crops","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" OTHER PLANTATION CROPS — FULL MIND\n🌴\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Karnataka — Coffee+Rubber+Tobacco Combo State\n2. Plantation Crops Definition (Ministry-Specific)\n3. Statement Set — Assam-Tea, AP-Tobacco Correct\n4. Tobacco — 1/3rd from AP (Now Gujarat #1)\n5. Tobacco Producer Ranking (Gujarat>AP>UP>Karnataka)\n6. Tobacco Area — Gujarat Largest (192.85k Hectares)\n7. Coconut — Kerala Historical, Karnataka Now #1\n8. Spice Leadership — Black Pepper/Ginger (Not Cardamom/Cloves)\n9. Odisha — NOT a Cardamom Producer\n10. Kerala — Famous for Spices (World-Renowned)\n11. Kerala — 'Garden/Spice Garden' of Spices\n12. Cardamom+Pepper Largest Producer — Kerala (Options-Dependent)\n13. Cloves — Flower-Bud Derived Spice\n14. Cloves Cultivation — Disputed (Multi-State)\n15. Black Pepper — Ideal Climate Conditions\n16. Black Pepper — 'Black Diamond'\n17. Spices — Biggest Producer (Gujarat → MP Shift)\n18. Cashew Nut — Maharashtra Leading Producer\n19. Saffron — J&K's Exclusive Crop\n20. Rubber Wrong-Pair Trap (Kerala, Not Himachal Pradesh)\n1. Karnataka — Coffee+Rubber+Tobacco Combo State\n●\nCoffee, Rubber, Tobacco teeno Karnataka mein ugte hain — Coffee states: Karnataka, Kerala, TN, AP,\nOdisha, NE states; Rubber: Kerala, TN, Tripura, Karnataka, Assam, Meghalaya; Tobacco: AP, Gujarat,\nKarnataka, UP, Bihar, TN, Maharashtra. [Q1]\n2. Plantation Crops Definition (Ministry-Specific)\n●\nPlantation agriculture ki main crops: Tea, Rubber, Coconut, Coffee — Agriculture Ministry:\ncoconut/arecanut/palm/cocoa/cashew; Commerce Ministry: tea/coffee/rubber. [Q2]\n3. Statement Set — Assam-Tea, AP-Tobacco Correct\n●\nSahi statements: Tea Assam ki main crop hai, Tobacco AP mein bade paimane par ugta hai — 'Coffee\nTamil Nadu ki main crop hai' aur 'Jute Chhattisgarh ki main crop hai' GALAT hain (Coffee\nKarnataka mein leading hai, Chhattisgarh ki main crop paddy hai). [Q3]\n4. Tobacco — 1/3rd from AP (Now Gujarat #1)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Andhra Pradesh se 1/3rd se zyada tobacco production aata tha — 2022-23 data ke\nmutabik ab Gujarat leading hai (58.09%). [Q4, Q5, Q6]"," 5. Tobacco Producer Ranking (Gujarat>AP>UP>Karnataka)\n●\n2022-23 ranking: Gujarat > Andhra Pradesh > Uttar Pradesh > Karnataka. [Q5, Q6]\n6. Tobacco Area — Gujarat Largest (192.85k Hectares)\n●\n2010 mein Andhra Pradesh ka sabse bada area under tobacco tha — 2022-23 mein ab Gujarat (192.85k\nhectares) sabse aage hai, phir Karnataka (76k), AP (58k), UP (23k). [Q7]\n7. Coconut — Kerala Historical, Karnataka Now #1\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Kerala coconut ka largest producer tha — 2023-24 mein ab Karnataka pehle, Tamil\nNadu dusre, Kerala teesre number par hai. [Q8, Q9]\n8. Spice Leadership — Black Pepper/Ginger (Not Cardamom/Cloves)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt India Black-Pepper aur Ginger mein leading tha — Cardamom ka leading producer\nGuatemala hai, Cloves ka Indonesia hai (India ka NAHI) — 2022 ke mutabik India black pepper mein\nVietnam ke baad 2nd largest producer hai. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Cardamom ka world-leader Guatemala hai, Cloves ka Indonesia — India in dono mein\n⚠️\nleading NAHI hai\n9. Odisha — NOT a Cardamom Producer\n●\nCardamom ke leading producers: Kerala, Sikkim, Arunachal Pradesh — Odisha commercially\ncardamom produce NAHI karta. [Q11]\n10. Kerala — Famous for Spices (World-Renowned)\n●\nKerala prachin kaal se apne spices ke liye poori duniya mein famous hai. [Q12]\n11. Kerala — 'Garden/Spice Garden' of Spices\n●\nKerala ko 'Garden of Spices' ya 'Spice Garden' kaha jaata hai — kayi spices ki cultivation ki wajah se.\n[Q13, Q14]\n12. Cardamom+Pepper Largest Producer — Kerala (Options-Dependent)\n●\nKerala cardamom ka largest producer hai (2023-24) — black pepper mein actually Karnataka pehle,\nKerala dusre number par hai — par Karnataka options mein na hone par Kerala sahi answer hai.\n[Q15]\n13. Cloves — Flower-Bud Derived Spice\n●\nCloves (laung) Eugenia Caryophyllata plant ki flower-buds hain (root/stem/fruit se NAHI) — medicines\nmein bhi use hoti hai. [Q16]\n14. Cloves Cultivation — Disputed (Multi-State)\n●\n2023-24 data ke mutabik cloves ki farming Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Karnataka teeno mein hoti hai — isliye\nsingle-state question disputed hai. [Q17]"," 15. Black Pepper — Ideal Climate Conditions\n●\nBlack pepper ke liye ideal: hot-moist climate, 200cm+ annual rainfall, 1100-1300m sloping heights, 15-\n30°C temperature range. [Q18]\n16. Black Pepper — 'Black Diamond'\n●\nBlack pepper ko 'Black Diamond' bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q19]\n17. Spices — Biggest Producer (Gujarat → MP Shift)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Gujarat spices ka biggest producer tha — 2023-24 (Final Estimate) mein ab Madhya\nPradesh leading hai. [Q20]\n18. Cashew Nut — Maharashtra Leading Producer\n●\n2023-24 (Final) data ke mutabik top-3 cashew producers: Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Odisha. [Q21]\n19. Saffron — J&K's Exclusive Crop\n●\nSaffron (Kesar) ka ekmatra producer state Jammu and Kashmir hai (ab UT, 31 Oct 2019 se) — prachin\nkaal se yahan produce hota hai. [Q22]\n20. Rubber Wrong-Pair Trap (Kerala, Not Himachal Pradesh)\n●\nJute-WB, Tea-Assam, Sugarcane-UP sahi hain — 'Rubber-Himachal Pradesh' GALAT hai (Rubber ka\nlargest producer Kerala hai, garm-nam climate chahiye jo HP mein nahi milta). [Q23]\n EXAM TRAP — Rubber — Kerala ka product hai, Himachal Pradesh ka NAHI (rubber ko garm-nam\n⚠️\nclimate chahiye)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0042","t":"21 Jhuming Agriculture","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" JHUMING AGRICULTURE — FULL MIND MAP\n🔥\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Jhuming/Jhum — Definition (Shifting Cultivation)\n2. North-East India — Main Practice Area\n3. Regional Names of Shifting Cultivation (Match Set)\n1. Jhuming/Jhum — Definition (Shifting Cultivation)\n●\nJhuming/Jhum (aka Paida) shifting cultivation ka ek type hai — jungle kaatke sukhne diya jaata hai,\nphir jalaya jaata hai; jab soil fertility kam ho jaati hai to tribes dusri jagah shift kar jaate hain, ye process\nrepeat hoti hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. North-East India — Main Practice Area\n●\nJhuming mainly North-Eastern states ke hilly areas mein practiced hai — Nagaland, Arunachal\nPradesh, Meghalaya mein sabse zyada, Assam ke hilly regions mein bhi (Mizoram, Tripura, Sikkim,\nManipur mein bhi hoti hai, Manipur mein isse 'Pamlou' kehte hain). [Q4, Q5, Q6]\n3. Regional Names of Shifting Cultivation (Match Set)\n●\nShifting cultivation ke regional naam: Western Ghats — Kumari, South-East Rajasthan — Waltre,\nNorth-East India — Jhum, MP & Chhattisgarh — Dahiya. [Q7]\n●\nEk aur set: Pondu — Odisha, Mashan — Madhya Pradesh (Himachal Pradesh NAHI), Poonam —\nKerala, Jhoom — Assam. [Q8]\n EXAM TRAP — Mashan — Madhya Pradesh mein practice hoti hai, Himachal Pradesh mein NAHI\n⚠️\n(common wrong-pair)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0043","t":"22 Agriculture Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" AGRICULTURE MISCELLANEOUS — FULL\n🌱\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Seed Tag Colors (Breeder-Golden, Foundation-White, Certified-Blue)\n2. Cropped Area Trends 1980-81 to 2023-24 (No Continuous Decrease)\n3. State-Crop Match (Tapioca-TN, Cotton-Gujarat, Jute-WB, Groundnut-Gujarat)\n4. Potato-Coconut-Banana-Tobacco Producer States\n5. UP — Largest Potato Producer\n6. National Research Centre for Banana — Trichy\n7. Non-Cereal Crop Region — Kutch/W.MP/Maharashtra\n8. Foodgrain Production Ranking (Rice>Wheat>Coarse>Pulses)\n9. UP — Largest Foodgrain-Producing State (18.14%)\n10. Gujarat — Cotton+Groundnut+Salt+Milk Leader (Historical)\n11. Cotton-Gram-Pepper-Pineapple Producer Match\n12. Ragi-Bazra-Jowar-Urad State Match\n13. Potato Producer Trap (MP→UP Data Shift)\n14. Crop-Pest Match (Aphid-Wheat, Ghundi Bag-Rice)\n15. Crop-Disease Match (Red Rot-Sugarcane, Khaira-Paddy, Wilt-Arhar)\n16. Green Hair Disease — Millet (Not Rice)\n17. Three Plant Family Group (Sugarcane, Beetroot, Sweet Pea, Gram)\n18. India — Not #1 Producer (Coffee/Sugarcane/Oilseeds/Tobacco)\n19. 2011-12 Foodgrain Production — Disputed Figure\n20. Fruit Production #1, Tobacco Export #2 (Disputed)\n21. Jute — Kharif Crop, Eastern Region Concentration\n22. Jute — Indigenous Plant, Feb-June Sowing\n23. India — Largest Jute Producer (Not Due to Yellow Revolution)\n24. West Bengal — Largest Jute Producer State\n25. Jute Industry — West Bengal Concentration\n26. Lower Gangetic Plain — Paddy+Jute Combo\n27. West Bengal — Largest Jute Cultivation Area\n28. Fibre Crops — Cotton, Jute, Sunhemp\n29. Maize — Grown Throughout the Year ('Queen of Cereals')\n30. Maize Uses — Starch, Biodiesel, Alcoholic Beverages\n31. Maize Maturity Period — 90-150 Days\n32. Maize — C4 Plant (Rice/Wheat/Soybean are C3)\n33. Maize Production Ranking (Karnataka, Bihar, MP Now Lead)\n34. Shaktiman-I/II — GM Maize Varieties\n35. Saffron — J&K's Commercial Production\n36. Kashmir Valley — Largest Saffron Quantity\n37. Crop-Geography Match (Barley-Cool, Rice-Hot/Moist, Millet-Hot/Dry, Tea-Altitude)\n38. Rainfall-Temperature Match (Cotton, Flax, Sugarbeet, Jute)\n39. Onion — Transplanted Crop\n40. Eastern UP Crop Cycle — Paddy-Maize-Wheat\n41. Wilson — Rajma/Potato Pioneer in Bhagirathi Valley\n42. Board-HQ Match (Coffee-Bengaluru, Rubber-Kottayam, Tea-Kolkata, Tobacco-Guntur)\n43. India — 2nd in Vegetable Production (China #1)"," 44. Sindhu — Only Seedless Mango Variety\n45. Amrapali — Dasheri×Neelam Mango Hybrid (1971, IARI Pusa)\n46. Lalit — Guava Variety (North Plains, Lucknow)\n47. Regular Crop Mango Varieties (Bengalora, Neelam, Amrapali)\n48. Kanchan — Indian Gooseberry (Amla) Variety\n49. 'Ganga Varanasi' — Not a Known Variety (Disputed)\n50. Crop-Variety Match Trap (Shusk Samrat is Rice, Not Wheat)\n51. Banana Leading Producer — Maharashtra (Now)\n52. Bajra Producer Ranking (Rajasthan>UP>Gujarat>Haryana)\n53. Groundnut-Mustard-Soyabean-Coconut State Match\n54. Jute-Tea-Rubber-Sugarcane State Match\n55. Borlaug Award — Agricultural Science\n56. Kufri Chipsona-2 — Best Potato Variety for Processing\n57. National Food Security Mission — Rice/Wheat/Pulses Focus\n58. Subsistence Farming Crops — Coarse Cereals & Rice\n59. Ginger's Underground Stem — Rhizome\n60. Oatmeal — Cereal Grain Product\n61. Mandua (Koda) — Uttarakhand's Export to Japan\n62. Rainfed Crops — Groundnut, Sesame, Pearl Millet\n63. Cowpea/Green Gram/Pigeon Pea — Triple-Use Crops\n64. Arunachal Pradesh — Best Climate for Orchid Cultivation\n65. Sikkim — India's First Organic State (2016)\n66. Sikkim — First Organic State (Repeat)\n67. Gujarat — Arid North, Cotton Centre, Cash-Crop Dominant\n68. Guar (Cluster Bean) — Shale Gas Extraction Gum\n69. West Bengal — Historical Fish Leader (Inland, Not Coastal)\n70. Fish Production Ranking (AP>WB>Karnataka>Odisha>Kerala)\n71. Cotton Fibre Length — Best Variety Over 5cm (Not 1-5cm)\n72. Linseed — Rabi Crop (Not Grown Year-Round)\n73. Lac Production — Jharkhand Leading (Not Bihar Post-Split)\n74. Aman Rice — Sown June-July (Not March-April)\n75. UPAS-120 — Arhar Variety (Not Gram) — Disputed\n76. Kinnaur-Mewat-Coromandel — All Mismatched Pairs\n77. Kaushal — Groundnut Variety, Not Rice (Disputed)\n78. India's Fruit Production Share — 15% (Historical)\n79. India — Largest Producer of Mango, Banana, Papaya, Lemon\n80. Jowar — Not a Cash Crop (Repeat Confirmation)\n81. Crop-Season Match (Sunflower-All, Muskmelon-Zaid, Cotton-Kharif, Linseed-Rabi)\n82. Water Conservation Practices — Zero Tillage, Gypsum, Crop Residue\n83. Jute-Tea-Sugarcane-Rubber State Match (Repeat)\n84. Maize-Jute-Cotton-Soyabean State Match (AP Trap)\n85. Sultana/Gulabi/Kali Champa — Grape Varieties\n86. Crop-Weed Match (Bathua Doesn't Grow With Paddy)\n87. Radhey — Chickpea Variety (Not Paddy)\n88. Maize-Potato-Sugarcane-Moong — 3-Year Crop Rotation\n89. NABI MG — Colored Wheat Variety\n90. 2,4-D — World's First Herbicide\n91. Cultivation Techniques (Tasseling, Pegging, Tillering, Topping)\n92. Uttar Pradesh — Mentha Oil Monopoly (85-100%)\n93. Crop-Disease Match Trap (Wilt Not Specific to Paddy)\n94. False Smut — Rice Disease (Not Barley)\n95. Cotton Leading Producer — Gujarat (2023-24)\n96. Kerala — Black Pepper + Cardamom Producer"," 97. Dryland Farming — Below 75cm Rainfall\n98. NPOP — APEDA Implementing Agency (Not Rural Development)\n99. Cash Crops — Coffee, Cocoa, Sugarcane, Banana, Cotton, Jute\n100. Bajra — Hot-Dry Climate, Rajasthan Leader (Disputed)\n101. Agricultural Drought — Low Soil Moisture\n102. Mahi Kanchan & RCB 911 — Maize & Bajra Hybrids\n103. Silviculture — Art & Science of Forest-Crop Cultivation\n1. Seed Tag Colors (Breeder-Golden, Foundation-White, Certified-Blue)\n●\nSeeds classification: Breeder seeds — golden tag (research centres/universities se), Foundation seeds —\nwhite tag (certifying body ki supervision mein), Certified seeds — blue tag (foundation seeds se,\nprescribed standards conform karte hain). [Q1]\n2. Cropped Area Trends 1980-81 to 2023-24 (No Continuous Decrease)\n●\n1980-81 se 2023-24 tak koi bhi crop (Wheat, Rice, Pulses, Coarse Cereals) continuously kam NAHI hui\n— sab mein fluctuation ke saath overall area badha hai (Coarse Cereals mein overall kami hui hai par\ncontinuous nahi). [Q2]\n3. State-Crop Match (Tapioca-TN, Cotton-Gujarat, Jute-WB, Groundnut-Gujarat)\n●\n2023-24 top producers: Tamil Nadu — Tapioca, Gujarat — Cotton, West Bengal — Jute/Mesta, Gujarat\n— Groundnut — Kerala-Tapioca match sahi NAHI hai (Tamil Nadu hai). [Q3]\n4. Potato-Coconut-Banana-Tobacco Producer States\n●\n2023-24 top producers: Potato — UP, Coconut — Karnataka, Banana — Maharashtra, Tobacco (2022-\n23) — Gujarat — 'Coconut-Kerala' ab galat hai (Karnataka #1 ho gaya hai). [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP — Coconut ka #1 producer ab Karnataka hai — Kerala se shift ho gaya (2023-24 data)\n⚠️\n5. UP — Largest Potato Producer\n●\nUttar Pradesh potato ka pehla number ka producer hai. [Q5]\n6. National Research Centre for Banana — Trichy\n●\nNRCB (21 Aug 1993 establish) Tiruchirappalli (Trichy), Tamil Nadu mein hai — banana\nproduction/productivity badhaane ke liye. [Q6]\n7. Non-Cereal Crop Region — Kutch/W.MP/Maharashtra\n●\nMap-based question mein non-cereal crop production area — Rann of Kutch (Gujarat), Western MP,\nMaharashtra ka hissa tha. [Q7]\n8. Foodgrain Production Ranking (Rice>Wheat>Coarse>Pulses)\n●\n2023-24 (final) production ranking: Rice (137.8 MT) > Wheat (113.3 MT) > Coarse Grain (56.9 MT) >\nPulses (24.3 MT). [Q8]"," 9. UP — Largest Foodgrain-Producing State (18.14%)\n●\n2023-24 (Final) data ke mutabik UP sabse bada foodgrain producer hai (18.14% share) — MP (12.48%)\ndusre, Punjab (9.79%) teesre number par. [Q9]\n10. Gujarat — Cotton+Groundnut+Salt+Milk Leader (Historical)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Gujarat Cotton, Groundnut, Salt, Milk char mein leading tha — abhi\nCotton/Groundnut/Salt mein leading hai, lekin Milk mein ab UP leading hai. [Q10]\n11. Cotton-Gram-Pepper-Pineapple Producer Match\n●\n2023-24 match: Cotton — Gujarat, Gram — Madhya Pradesh, Pineapple — West Bengal, Black pepper\n— Karnataka. [Q11]\n12. Ragi-Bazra-Jowar-Urad State Match\n●\nMatch: Ragi — Karnataka, Bazra — Rajasthan, Jowar — Maharashtra, Urad — Madhya Pradesh.\n[Q12]\n13. Potato Producer Trap (MP→UP Data Shift)\n●\nSahi matches: Coffee-Karnataka, Cotton-Gujarat, Wheat-UP sahi hain — 'Potato-Madhya Pradesh'\nGALAT tha (2023-24 data ke mutabik UP hai). [Q13]\n14. Crop-Pest Match (Aphid-Wheat, Ghundi Bag-Rice)\n●\nCrop-destroying creatures match: Aphid — Wheat, Ghundi Bag — Rice, Top Shoot Borer Moth —\nSugarcane, Bollworm — Gram. [Q14]\n15. Crop-Disease Match (Red Rot-Sugarcane, Khaira-Paddy, Wilt-Arhar)\n●\nCrop-disease match: Sugarcane — Red Rot, Paddy — Khaira, Arhar — Wilt, Potato — Late Blight.\n[Q15]\n16. Green Hair Disease — Millet (Not Rice)\n●\nBajra-Ergot, Pea-Powdery mildew, Gram-Wilt sahi hain — 'Rice-Green hair' GALAT hai (Green hair\ndisease millet mein paayi jaati hai, rice mein NAHI). [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Green hair disease — Millet (bajra) mein hoti hai, Rice mein NAHI\n⚠️\n17. Three Plant Family Group (Sugarcane, Beetroot, Sweet Pea, Gram)\n●\nSugarcane, Beetroot, Sweet Pea, Gram, Arhar, Fras-bean teen alag plant families ke antargat aate hain.\n[Q17]\n18. India — Not #1 Producer (Coffee/Sugarcane/Oilseeds/Tobacco)\n●\nIndia in mein se kisi ka bhi #1 producer NAHI hai (Disputed) — Sugarcane mein 2nd (FAO 2023), Coffee\nmein 9th, Tobacco mein 2nd (unmanufactured). [Q18]"," 19. 2011-12 Foodgrain Production — Disputed Figure\n●\n2011-12 mein estimated foodgrain production 259.29 million tonnes tha — diye gaye options mein se koi\nbhi match nahi karta, isliye disputed question hai (2023-24 mein 332.3 MT ho gaya). [Q19]\n20. Fruit Production #1, Tobacco Export #2 (Disputed)\n●\nFAO 2023 ke mutabik India 'Other fruits n.e.c.' category mein fruit production mein pehle number par\nhai — tobacco (unmanufactured) export mein dusre number par hai (quantity ke hisaab se) — dono\nstatements sahi hain. [Q20]\n21. Jute — Kharif Crop, Eastern Region Concentration\n●\nJute Kharif crop hai (Rabi NAHI) — high temperature (24-35°C) aur heavy rain (125-200cm) chahiye,\nmainly Eastern India mein hoti hai (WB, Bihar, Assam, Odisha, MP). [Q21]\n22. Jute — Indigenous Plant, Feb-June Sowing\n●\nJute India ka indigenous plant hai (white jute ka primary origin Africa, secondary India/Myanmar) —\ngenerally March-May boyi jaati hai (Feb-June tak kuch varieties), July-October kaati jaati hai — dono\nstatements sahi hain par R, A ki sahi explanation nahi hai. [Q22]\n23. India — Largest Jute Producer (Not Due to Yellow Revolution)\n●\nIndia duniya ka largest raw jute producer hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin ye Yellow Revolution ki wajah se\nNAHI hai (Yellow Revolution oilseeds se related hai, Reason galat). [Q23]\n EXAM TRAP — Yellow Revolution — Oilseeds se related hai, Jute se NAHI\n⚠️\n24. West Bengal — Largest Jute Producer State\n●\n2023-24 data ke mutabik West Bengal jute-mesta ka largest producer hai — Bihar, Assam dusre-teesre\nnumber par. [Q24]\n25. Jute Industry — West Bengal Concentration\n●\nJute industry mainly West Bengal mein concentrated hai. [Q25]\n26. Lower Gangetic Plain — Paddy+Jute Combo\n●\nLower Gangetic plain (humid, high temperature saal bhar) ke liye Paddy aur Jute sabse suitable crop\ncombination hai. [Q26]\n27. West Bengal — Largest Jute Cultivation Area\n●\n2023-24 data ke mutabik jute cultivation area: West Bengal (0.52 million hectare) > Bihar (0.06) = Assam\n(0.06). [Q27]\n28. Fibre Crops — Cotton, Jute, Sunhemp"," ●\nFibre crops group: Cotton, Jute, Sunhemp — Gram/Linseed/Lentil/Oat/Dhaicha/Wheat is category mein\nNAHI hain. [Q28]\n29. Maize — Grown Throughout the Year ('Queen of Cereals')\n●\nMaize (Corn) saal bhar ugayi jaa sakti hai — varied climate conditions mein wider adaptability rakhti\nhai, isliye ise 'Queen of Cereals' kaha jaata hai. [Q29, Q30]\n30. Maize Uses — Starch, Biodiesel, Alcoholic Beverages\n●\nMaize ke sab 3 uses sahi hain: starch production, oil se biodiesel feedstock, alcoholic beverages (corn\nwhisky, Brazilian beer) banana. [Q31]\n31. Maize Maturity Period — 90-150 Days\n●\nMaize (rice-wheat ke baad India ki sabse zyada produce+consume hone wali crop) ki maturity period alag-\nalag climatic zones mein 90-150 din (usually 110 din quoted) hoti hai — winter varieties summer se zyada\nwaqt leti hain. [Q32]\n32. Maize — C4 Plant (Rice/Wheat/Soybean are C3)\n●\nMaize C4 plant hai — Rice, Wheat, Barley, Rye, Soybean, Cotton, Tobacco, Potato C3 plants hain.\n[Q33]\n33. Maize Production Ranking (Karnataka, Bihar, MP Now Lead)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt: Andhra Pradesh > Karnataka > Rajasthan > Bihar — 2023-24 data ke mutabik ab\nKarnataka, Bihar, MP top-3 hain. [Q34]\n34. Shaktiman-I/II — GM Maize Varieties\n●\nShaktiman-I aur Shaktiman-II Maize (makka) ki genetically modified crops hain. [Q35]\n35. Saffron — J&K's Commercial Production\n●\nSaffron (Zaffran) ka commercial production Jammu and Kashmir mein hota hai (ab UT). [Q36]\n36. Kashmir Valley — Largest Saffron Quantity\n●\nIndia mein saffron ka sabse zyada production Kashmir Valley mein hota hai — world mein Spain, Iran,\nGreece, Italy bhi produce karte hain. [Q37]\n37. Crop-Geography Match (Barley-Cool, Rice-Hot/Moist, Millet-Hot/Dry, Tea-Altitude)\n●\nMatch: Barley — cool climate/poor soil, Rice — hot-moist climate/rich soil, Millets — hot-dry\nclimate/poor soil, Tea — warm-moist climate/high altitude. [Q38]\n38. Rainfall-Temperature Match (Cotton, Flax, Sugarbeet, Jute)\n●\nMatch: Cotton — 500-1000mm/18-22°C, Flax — 600-800mm/5-18°C, Sugarbeet — 500-600mm/18-\n22°C, Jute — 1500-2000mm/25-35°C. [Q39]"," 39. Onion — Transplanted Crop\n●\nOnion (pyaaz) ki cultivation pehle seeds boke, phir chhote plants ko transplant karke ki jaati hai —\nMaize, Sorghum, Soyabean ki nahi. [Q40]\n40. Eastern UP Crop Cycle — Paddy-Maize-Wheat\n●\nEastern UP ke liye Paddy-Maize-Wheat sabse best crop cycle maana jaata hai. [Q41]\n41. Wilson — Rajma/Potato Pioneer in Bhagirathi Valley\n●\nBhagirathi valley mein Rajma-Potato cultivation shuru karne ka credit Fredrick Wilson ko jaata hai — 19th\ncentury mein wahan permanently basne wale pehle white man the, 'Raja of Harsil' bhi kehlaaye. [Q42]\n42. Board-HQ Match (Coffee-Bengaluru, Rubber-Kottayam, Tea-Kolkata, Tobacco-Guntur)\n●\nBoard-HQ match: Coffee Board — Bengaluru, Rubber Board — Kottayam, Tea Board — Kolkata,\nTobacco Board — Guntur. [Q43]\n43. India — 2nd in Vegetable Production (China #1)\n●\nFAO 2023 ke mutabik vegetable production mein China pehle number par hai, India dusre number par\n('vegetable fresh n.e.c.' category). [Q44, Q45]\n44. Sindhu — Only Seedless Mango Variety\n●\nIndian scientists ne 'Sindhu' naam se seedless mango variety develop ki — ye duniya ki EKMATRA\nseedless mango variety hai. [Q46]\n45. Amrapali — Dasheri×Neelam Mango Hybrid (1971, IARI Pusa)\n●\nAmrapali Dasheri aur Neelam ke cross se 1971 mein IARI, Pusa, Delhi ne develop ki thi. [Q47]\n46. Lalit — Guava Variety (North Plains, Lucknow)\n●\nLalit Guava (amrud) ki improvised variety hai — Indian Institute of Horticulture Research ne North\nplains, Lucknow ke liye develop ki, commercial production ke liye recommend hai. [Q48]\n47. Regular Crop Mango Varieties (Bengalora, Neelam, Amrapali)\n●\nDasheri-1, Chausa, Langra regular crop varieties NAHI hain — regular crop mango varieties: Dasheri-51,\nBengalora (Totapuri), Neelam, Amrapali. [Q49]\n48. Kanchan — Indian Gooseberry (Amla) Variety\n●\nKanchan, Krishna, Banarasi Indian gooseberry (Amla) ki improved varieties hain — Amla mein Vitamin\nC bahut hoti hai. [Q50]\n49. 'Ganga Varanasi' — Not a Known Variety (Disputed)"," ●\n'Kashi Ganga' bottle gourd ki variety hai, 'Kashi Madhu' muskmelon ki, 'Banarasi' gooseberry aur guava (TN-\nAP) ki — 'Ganga Varanasi' naam ki koi bhi known variety NAHI hai (disputed question). [Q51]\n50. Crop-Variety Match Trap (Shusk Samrat is Rice, Not Wheat)\n●\nPaddy-Govind, Arhar-Paras, Pea-Prakash sahi hain — 'Wheat-Shusk Samrat' GALAT hai (Shusk Samrat\nrice ki variety hai, wheat ki NAHI). [Q52]\n EXAM TRAP — Shusk Samrat — Rice ki variety hai, Wheat ki NAHI\n⚠️\n51. Banana Leading Producer — Maharashtra (Now)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Tamil Nadu banana ka leading producer tha — 2023-24 data ke mutabik ab\nMaharashtra > Andhra Pradesh > Tamil Nadu hain. [Q53]\n52. Bajra Producer Ranking (Rajasthan>UP>Gujarat>Haryana)\n●\n2022-23 Bajra production ranking: Rajasthan > Uttar Pradesh > Gujarat > Haryana. [Q54]\n53. Groundnut-Mustard-Soyabean-Coconut State Match\n●\n2023-24 match: Groundnut — Andhra Pradesh (Gujarat 2023-24 mein), Mustard — Rajasthan,\nSoyabean — Madhya Pradesh, Coconut — Kerala (Karnataka 2023-24 mein). [Q55]\n54. Jute-Tea-Rubber-Sugarcane State Match\n●\nMatch: Jute — West Bengal, Tea — Assam, Rubber — Kerala, Sugarcane — Uttar Pradesh. [Q56]\n55. Borlaug Award — Agricultural Science\n●\nBorlaug Award Agricultural Science ke field mein diya jaata hai (1972 se, Norman E. Borlaug ke naam\npar). [Q57]\n56. Kufri Chipsona-2 — Best Potato Variety for Processing\n●\nProcessing purposes ke liye Kufri Chipsona-2 sabse best potato variety hai — Kufri Chipsona-3 (2005)\nplains ke liye, Kufri Himsona hilly areas ke liye best hai. [Q58]\n57. National Food Security Mission — Rice/Wheat/Pulses Focus\n●\nNational Food Security Mission ka objective Rice, Wheat aur Pulses ki production sustainable tareeke se\nbadhaana hai — area expansion, productivity, soil fertility restoration, farmer confidence badhaana. [Q59]\n58. Subsistence Farming Crops — Coarse Cereals & Rice\n●\nSubsistence farming ke tahat mainly Coarse Cereals aur Rice ugayi jaati hai. [Q60]\n59. Ginger's Underground Stem — Rhizome\n●\nGinger (adrak) ka stem jo mitti mein ugta hai aur food store karta hai use Rhizome (prakand) kehte hain.\n[Q61]"," 60. Oatmeal — Cereal Grain Product\n●\nOatmeal cereal grain product hai — food aur cattle-fodder dono ke liye use hota hai — Sago, Soya flour,\nArrowroot cereal products NAHI hain. [Q62]\n61. Mandua (Koda) — Uttarakhand's Export to Japan\n●\nUttarakhand ka Mandua (Koda) grain mainly Japan ko export hota hai — mandua se bane products videsh\nmein high demand mein hain. [Q63]\n62. Rainfed Crops — Groundnut, Sesame, Pearl Millet\n●\nGroundnut, Sesame (til), Pearl Millet (bajra) predominantly rainfed crops hain — dry areas mein ugte\nhain, irrigation puri tarah rain par depend karti hai. [Q64]\n63. Cowpea/Green Gram/Pigeon Pea — Triple-Use Crops\n●\nCowpea, Green gram, Pigeon Pea pulse, fodder aur green manure teeno ke roop mein use hote hain — 1\nhectare mein Arhar ki green manure se 40kg nitrogen milta hai. [Q65]\n64. Arunachal Pradesh — Best Climate for Orchid Cultivation\n●\nArunachal Pradesh orchids ki bahut saari varieties ke liye suited hai, export-oriented industry develop\nkar sakta hai (biodiversity, forests, deep valleys). [Q66]\n65. Sikkim — India's First Organic State (2016)\n●\nSikkim ko January 2016 mein PM Narendra Modi ne India ka pehla Organic State declare kiya — eco-\nfriendly farming state banne ki wajah se sarahna hui. [Q67]\n66. Sikkim — First Organic State (Repeat)\n●\nSikkim India ka pehla organic/bio state hai (2016 mein declare hua). [Q68]\n67. Gujarat — Arid North, Cotton Centre, Cash-Crop Dominant\n●\nGujarat ke characteristics: northern part arid/semi-arid hai, central part mein cotton production hota\nhai, cash crops ki cultivation food crops se predominant hai. [Q69]\n68. Guar (Cluster Bean) — Shale Gas Extraction Gum\n●\nGuar ke seeds se bana gum shale gas extraction (hydraulic fracturing) mein use hota hai — world\nproduction ka ~80% India-Pakistan mein hota hai. [Q70]\n69. West Bengal — Historical Fish Leader (Inland, Not Coastal)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt West Bengal fish ka leading producer tha (Assertion sahi) — lekin ye inland water\nsources (90%) se aata tha, sea-coast ke well-developed industry se NAHI (Reason galat) — 2022-23\nmein ab Andhra Pradesh #1 hai. [Q71]"," 70. Fish Production Ranking (AP>WB>Karnataka>Odisha>Kerala)\n●\n2022-23 data ke mutabik fish production ranking: Andhra Pradesh (51.06 lakh tonnes) > West Bengal\n(20.45) > Karnataka (12.25) > Odisha (10.52) > Kerala (9.21). [Q72]\n71. Cotton Fibre Length — Best Variety Over 5cm (Not 1-5cm)\n●\nCotton fibre length categories: best quality >5cm (USA/West Indies), medium 3.75-5cm, small <2.5cm\n(Brazil/India) — 'cotton fibre length 1-5cm hoti hai' GALAT statement hai — Boron micronutrient hai,\napple ka edible part mesocarp hai, Pusa Basmati ka fertilizer dose N(120)P(60)K(60) sahi hai. [Q73]\n72. Linseed — Rabi Crop (Not Grown Year-Round)\n●\nLinseed (alsi) saal bhar NAHI ugayi jaa sakti — ye Wheat, Barley, Rapeseed, Mustard, Gram ki tarah\nRabi crop hai — apple mein calcium ki kami se storage quality kam hoti hai, WB largest vegetable producer\nhai, 3rd-gen pesticide C.M. Williams ne propose kiya tha (sab sahi statements). [Q74]\n73. Lac Production — Jharkhand Leading (Not Bihar Post-Split)\n●\n2013-14 data ke mutabik Jharkhand lac (lakh) ka leading producer hai (~92%\nJharkhand+Chhattisgarh+MP+Maharashtra se) — 'Bihar' sirf undivided-Bihar ke context mein sahi\ntha — West Bengal rice ka largest producer hai (AP ka NAHI, disputed question), Kunchikal waterfall\nKarnataka mein hai. [Q75]\n74. Aman Rice — Sown June-July (Not March-April)\n●\nAman rice June-July mein boyi jaati hai, November-December mein kaati jaati hai (March-April mein\nNAHI) — India rice production mein China ke baad 2nd hai, Soyabean seed mein 20% oil+40% protein hota\nhai, Dr. B.P. Pal ICAR ke pehle Director-General the (sab baaki statements sahi hain). [Q76]\n75. UPAS-120 — Arhar Variety (Not Gram) — Disputed\n●\nRajma ki nitrogen-fixation capacity research ke mutabik poor/inefficient hai (disputed statement) —\n'UPAS-120 gram ki variety hai' GALAT hai (ye Arhar ki variety hai) — PBW-343/DBW-17 wheat\nvarieties hain, Khaira disease zinc sulphate se control hoti hai (sahi statements). [Q77]\n EXAM TRAP — UPAS-120 — Arhar ki variety hai, Gram ki NAHI\n⚠️\n76. Kinnaur-Mewat-Coromandel — All Mismatched Pairs\n●\nKinnaur (Himachal Pradesh) arecanut ke liye famous NAHI hai\n(Karnataka/Kerala/Assam/Meghalaya/WB/Tripura mein hota hai) — Mewat (ab Nuh, Haryana) mango ke\nliye famous NAHI hai, Coromandel soyabean ke liye famous NAHI hai — teeno pairs GALAT hain.\n[Q79]\n77. Kaushal — Groundnut Variety, Not Rice (Disputed)\n●\n'Kaushal rice ki variety hai' GALAT hai (ye asal mein groundnut ki variety hai) — aur 'sabse zyada pulses\nRajasthan se aati hai' bhi GALAT hai (Madhya Pradesh se aati hai) — Commission ne (d) ko sahi"," maana, par (a) bhi galat hai, isliye disputed hai. First Agricultural University 1960 mein bani, Kerala coconut\nka leading producer tha (question ke waqt). [Q78]\n EXAM TRAP — Kaushal — Groundnut ki variety hai, Rice ki NAHI\n⚠️\n78. India's Fruit Production Share — 15% (Historical)\n●\nIndian Horticulture data 2014 ke mutabik India world fruit production ka ~13.6% (closest option 15%)\nproduce karta tha, China 20.9% ke saath #1 tha — abhi (FAO 2023) India 'other fruits n.e.c.' category\nmein #1 hai. [Q80]\n79. India — Largest Producer of Mango, Banana, Papaya, Lemon\n●\n2020-21 report ke mutabik India Mango aur Papaya ka world ka largest producer hai (Grapes, Orange\nka NAHI) — Banana aur Lemon ka bhi largest producer hai. [Q81]\n80. Jowar — Not a Cash Crop (Repeat Confirmation)\n●\nCash crops: Oilseeds, Fiber (Cotton/Jute/Mesta), Plantation crops (Tea/Coffee/Rubber/Potato),\nSugarcane/Tobacco — Jowar cash crop NAHI hai (food crop hai). [Q82]\n81. Crop-Season Match (Sunflower-All, Muskmelon-Zaid, Cotton-Kharif, Linseed-Rabi)\n●\nMatch: Sunflower — All seasons, Muskmelon — Zaid (summer), Cotton — Kharif (rainy), Linseed —\nRabi (winter). [Q83]\n82. Water Conservation Practices — Zero Tillage, Gypsum, Crop Residue\n●\nAgriculture mein water conservation ke sab 3 practices sahi hain: reduced/zero tillage, irrigation se pehle\ngypsum application, crop residue field mein chhodna — sab moisture retain karte hain. [Q84]\n83. Jute-Tea-Sugarcane-Rubber State Match (Repeat)\n●\nMatch: Jute — West Bengal, Tea — Assam, Sugarcane — Uttar Pradesh, Rubber — Kerala. [Q85]\n84. Maize-Jute-Cotton-Soyabean State Match (AP Trap)\n●\nMaize-UP, Jute-WB, Cotton-Maharashtra sahi hain — 'Soyabean-Andhra Pradesh' GALAT hai (Madhya\nPradesh sabse bada producer hai, AP mein minimum production hai) — 2023-24 mein Maize ka #1\nKarnataka hai, Cotton ka #1 Gujarat hai. [Q86]\n EXAM TRAP — Soyabean — Madhya Pradesh ka leading producer hai, Andhra Pradesh ka NAHI\n⚠️\n85. Sultana/Gulabi/Kali Champa — Grape Varieties\n●\nSultana, Gulabi, Kali Champa Grapes (angoor) ki varieties hain. [Q87]\n86. Crop-Weed Match (Bathua Doesn't Grow With Paddy)"," ●\nWheat-Phalaris minor, Pea-Piyazi, Berseem-Kasni sahi hain — 'Paddy-Bathua' GALAT hai (Bathua\nwheat/pea/mustard ke saath ugta hai, paddy ke saath NAHI) — Bathua ka botanical naam Chenopodium\nalbum hai. [Q88]\n EXAM TRAP — Bathua — Wheat/Pea/Mustard ke saath ugta hai, Paddy ke saath NAHI\n⚠️\n87. Radhey — Chickpea Variety (Not Paddy)\n●\nMustard-Varuna, Pea-Rachna, Linseed-Neelam sahi hain — 'Paddy-Radhey' GALAT hai (Radhey asal\nmein chickpea/chana ki variety hai — UP ke Bundelkhand region ke liye recommended). [Q89]\n EXAM TRAP — Radhey — Chickpea (chana) ki variety hai, Paddy ki NAHI\n⚠️\n88. Maize-Potato-Sugarcane-Moong — 3-Year Crop Rotation\n●\nMaize–Potato–Sugarcane(ratoon)–Moong crop cycle 3-saal ke crop rotation ka example hai. [Q90]\n89. NABI MG — Colored Wheat Variety\n●\nNABI MG wheat ki ek colored variety hai (NABI ne develop ki, 3 colors: Black, Blue, Purple). [Q91]\n90. 2,4-D — World's First Herbicide\n●\n2,4-D duniya ka pehla herbicide tha — Semazin, Pendimethalin, 2,4,5-T se pehle. [Q92]\n91. Cultivation Techniques (Tasseling, Pegging, Tillering, Topping)\n●\nMaize-Tasseling, Pliny-Pegging (groundnut) sahi hain — 'Ptolemy-Tillering' GALAT hai (Tillering wheat\nki technique hai) — Strabo-Topping (gram plant ki young branches ke tips 2-4 hafte mein remove\nkarna) sahi hai. [Q93]\n92. Uttar Pradesh — Mentha Oil Monopoly (85-100%)\n●\nUttar Pradesh Mentha oil ka largest producer hai — question ke waqt 85% contribution tha, ab 100%\ntak contribute karta hai. [Q94]\n93. Crop-Disease Match Trap (Wilt Not Specific to Paddy)\n●\nMustard-White rust, Bajra-Smut, Groundnut-Tikka sahi hain — 'Paddy-Wilt' GALAT hai (Wilt paddy ki\nspecific disease NAHI hai — ye plants ke vascular system ko affect karti hai). [Q95]\n94. False Smut — Rice Disease (Not Barley)\n●\nRust-Wheat, Early blight-Potato, Khaira-Paddy sahi hain — 'False smut-Barley' GALAT hai (False smut\nasal mein Rice ki disease hai). [Q96]\n EXAM TRAP — False smut — Rice ki disease hai, Barley ki NAHI\n⚠️\n95. Cotton Leading Producer — Gujarat (2023-24)\n●\nRice-WB, Wheat-UP, Rape&Mustard-Rajasthan sahi hain — 2023-24 data ke mutabik Cotton ka leading\nproducer Gujarat hai (question ke waqt ka answer confirm hua) — Maharashtra dusre number par. [Q97]"," 96. Kerala — Black Pepper + Cardamom Producer\n●\nKerala mein Black Pepper aur Cardamom dono ka production hota hai — Assam, J&K, Himachal\nPradesh se zyada. [Q98]\n97. Dryland Farming — Below 75cm Rainfall\n●\nDryland farming (rainfed agriculture) India mein 750mm (75cm) se kam annual rainfall wale regions mein\npractice hoti hai. [Q99]\n98. NPOP — APEDA Implementing Agency (Not Rural Development)\n●\nNational Programme for Organic Production (NPOP) Ministry of Rural Development ke tahat NAHI hai (ye\nstatement galat hai) — APEDA (Agricultural and Processed Food Products Export Development\nAuthority) NPOP ke liye implementing agency/secretariat hai — Sikkim India ka pehla fully organic state\nhai (sahi statement). [Q100]\n EXAM TRAP — NPOP — Rural Development Ministry ke tahat NAHI hai; APEDA implementing\n⚠️\nagency hai\n99. Cash Crops — Coffee, Cocoa, Sugarcane, Banana, Cotton, Jute\n●\nTropical climate wale cash crops: Coffee, Cocoa, Sugarcane, Banana, Orange, Cotton, Jute — Millet\n(bajra) cash crop NAHI hai. [Q101]\n100. Bajra — Hot-Dry Climate, Rajasthan Leader (Disputed)\n●\nBajra ke sab statements sahi hain: hot-dry climate mein western/central India mein boyi jaati hai, hardy\ncrop hai (dry-spells resist karti hai), Rajasthan mein yield kam hoti hai (rainfed hone ki wajah se),\nRajasthan hi production mein leading hai — koi bhi option sab 4 combine nahi karta, isliye disputed hai.\n[Q102]\n101. Agricultural Drought — Low Soil Moisture\n●\nAgricultural drought soil mein moisture ki kami ko refer karta hai (jahan crops ugti hain) —\nHydrological drought reservoir ke low water levels ko, Meteorological drought dryness ki degree/duration ko\nrefer karta hai. [Q103]\n102. Mahi Kanchan & RCB 911 — Maize & Bajra Hybrids\n●\nMahi Kanchan aur RCB 911 respectively Maize aur Bajra ki hybrid varieties hain — Rajasthan ke\nBhilwara/Chittorgarh/Udaipur/Banswara maize districts hain, Western\nRajasthan/Jaipur/Dausa/Karauli/Bharatpur bajra districts hain. [Q104]\n103. Silviculture — Art & Science of Forest-Crop Cultivation\n●\nForest crops ki cultivation ki art aur science ko Silviculture kaha jaata hai — forests-woodlands ki\nestablishment, growth, composition, health, quality ko sustainable tareeke se control karta hai. [Q105]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0044","t":"23 Animal Husbandry","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ANIMAL HUSBANDRY — FULL MIND MAP\n🐄\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Stock Farming — Breeding of Animals\n2. Cattle Density — Bihar Highest per 100 Hectare\n3. 1/3rd Cattle Population — WB, UP, MP\n4. Livestock Statistics — Top States (Cattle, Buffalo, Sheep)\n5. Jamunapari — Highest Milk-Yielding Goat Breed\n6. Tharparkar — Rajasthan Border Region Breed\n7. Rajasthan Native Breeds (Rathi, Tharparkar, Nagori)\n8. Sahiwal — Highest Milk-Yielding Cow Breed\n9. India — World's #1 in Milk Production\n10. Milk Production State Rankings (UP, MP, Gujarat)\n11. Operation Flood — Milk Production & Distribution\n12. Dr. Verghese Kurien — Father of White Revolution\n13. White Revolution — Milk Production\n14. Milk Production Ranking (MP > Gujarat > Punjab > Haryana)\n15. Animal-Breed Match Trap (Gir is Cow, Not Sheep)\n16. Kharai Camels — Swimming Camel Breed (Kutch, Gujarat)\n1. Stock Farming — Breeding of Animals\n●\nStock Farming livestock rakhne ki practice hai — Animal Husbandry mein feeding, breeding, disease-\ncontrol sab shamil hai. [Q1]\n2. Cattle Density — Bihar Highest per 100 Hectare\n●\nCattle density per 100 hectare gross cultivable land: Bihar (183/sq km) sabse zyada — Madhya Pradesh\n(106), Uttar Pradesh (77), Haryana (25) se zyada. [Q2]\n3. 1/3rd Cattle Population — WB, UP, MP\n●\nIndia ki ~1/3rd cattle population West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh aur Madhya Pradesh mein hai (20th\nLivestock Census 2019: WB 19.1M, UP 19.0M, MP 18.8M) — total 193.46 million cattle. [Q3]\n4. Livestock Statistics — Top States (Cattle, Buffalo, Sheep)\n●\n2019 Livestock Census ke mutabik: Highest livestock population — UP, Rajasthan, MP; Top buffalo\nstates — UP, Rajasthan, Gujarat; Top sheep states — Telangana > AP > Karnataka — Uttar Pradesh\nIndia ka largest milk producer hai (2023-24). [Q4]\n5. Jamunapari — Highest Milk-Yielding Goat Breed\n●\nIndia ki sabse zyada doodh dene wali goat breed Jamunapari hai (2.5-3 kg/din) — milk aur meat dono ke\nliye useful. [Q5]"," 6. Tharparkar — Rajasthan Border Region Breed\n●\nTharparkar breed Rajasthan ke border region (Jaisalmer, Barmer, Jodhpur) aur Gujarat ke Kutch mein\nmilti hai. [Q6]\n7. Rajasthan Native Breeds (Rathi, Tharparkar, Nagori)\n●\nRajasthan ki 3 native cattle breeds: Rathi, Tharparkar, Nagori — Hallikar Karnataka ki breed hai\n(Rajasthan ki NAHI), Mewati Haryana ki breed hai. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Hallikar Karnataka ki breed hai, Rajasthan ki NAHI\n⚠️\n8. Sahiwal — Highest Milk-Yielding Cow Breed\n●\nSahiwal (Sindh-Pakistan mein bhi paayi jaati hai) sabse zyada milk-yielding cow breed hai — Gangotri\n(UP, low yield), Haryana aur Tharparkar dual-purpose (carrier + milk) breeds hain. [Q8]\n9. India — World's #1 in Milk Production\n●\nMilk production mein India world mein pehle number par hai — 2011-12 mein UP sabse zyada doodh\n(22556) produce karta tha, 2023-24 mein bhi UP pehle number par hai (38779.57). [Q9, Q10]\n10. Milk Production State Rankings (UP, MP, Gujarat)\n●\n2011-12 ranking: UP > Rajasthan > Gujarat > Punjab — 2023-24 mein bhi UP 1st, Rajasthan 2nd hai.\n[Q10]\n11. Operation Flood — Milk Production & Distribution\n●\nOperation Flood (1970, National Dairy Development Board) milk production aur distribution se related tha\n— Dr. Verghese Kurien ne lead kiya, India ko milk-deficient se world ka largest producer bana diya. [Q11]\n12. Dr. Verghese Kurien — Father of White Revolution\n●\nDr. Verghese Kurien India ki White Revolution ke pita the. [Q12, Q14]\n13. White Revolution — Milk Production\n●\nWhite Revolution milk production se related hai (egg/wheat/fish production se nahi). [Q13]\n14. Milk Production Ranking (MP > Gujarat > Punjab > Haryana)\n●\nEconomic Survey 2020-21 ke mutabik descending order: Madhya Pradesh > Gujarat > Punjab > Haryana.\n[Q15]\n15. Animal-Breed Match Trap (Gir is Cow, Not Sheep)\n●\nSahi pairs: Cow-Deoni, Goat-Barbari, Buffalo-Bhadawari — 'Sheep-Gir' GALAT hai (Gir asal mein\nZebu cattle/cow ki breed hai, sheep ki NAHI). [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Gir — cow (Zebu cattle) ki breed hai, sheep ki NAHI\n⚠️"," 16. Kharai Camels — Swimming Camel Breed (Kutch, Gujarat)\n●\nKharai camels — swimming camel breed, 'Khara' (saline) se naam mila, mangroves tak samudra mein\n3km tak tairte hain, Silk Route se historical link hai — famous roop se Kutch, Gujarat se associated\nhain (Ladakh se NAHI, though exam key ne is context mein 'Ladakh' bhi accept kiya). [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0045","t":"24.i Rock System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🪨 ROCK SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Dharwar System — Most Mineralized Rock System\n2. Chotanagpur Plateau — 'Ruhr Region of India'\n3. Vindhyan Rocks — Limestone-Rich (Sedimentary)\n4. Iron Ore Production — Odisha Leads (2023-24)\n5. Largest Mineral Reserves — South-East to North-East Belt\n6. State-wise Mineral Production Ranking (Odisha > Chhattisgarh)\n7. Odisha — 'State of Minerals'\n8. Gondwana System — 95%+ Coal Source (Assertion-Reason)\n9. Non-Metallic vs Metallic Minerals (Marble Example)\n1. Dharwar System — Most Mineralized Rock System\n●\nDharwar System India ka sabse zyada mineralized rock system hai — metallic minerals (iron-ore,\nmanganese, copper, lead, gold) ka main source hai — Karnataka ke Dharwar region mein pehli baar study\nhui thi. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Chotanagpur Plateau — 'Ruhr Region of India'\n●\nChotanagpur Plateau ko 'Indian minerals ka bhandaar' aur 'Ruhr region of India' kaha jaata hai —\nminerals ki richness ki wajah se. [Q3]\n3. Vindhyan Rocks — Limestone-Rich (Sedimentary)\n●\nVindhya range ki rocks sedimentary hain (water-suspended particles ke sedimentation se bani) —\nLimestone, sand, china clay prominent minerals hain — limestone cement industry ka base hai. [Q4]\n4. Iron Ore Production — Odisha Leads (2023-24)\n●\n2023-24 mein Iron Ore production ~252.2 million tonnes tha — Odisha 55% ke saath sabse bada\nproducer, Karnataka (16%), Chhattisgarh (15%) dusre-teesre number par. [Q5]\n5. Largest Mineral Reserves — South-East to North-East Belt\n●\nIndia ke sabse bade mineral reserves South-East se North-East belt mein hain — Chota Nagpur,\nDandakaranya aur Odisha plateau is region mein hain, iss peninsular region ko 'Indian minerals ka hriday'\nkaha jaata hai (coal, iron, mica, copper, bauxite pradhan hain). [Q6]\n6. State-wise Mineral Production Ranking (Odisha > Chhattisgarh)\n●\n2023-24 mineral production value ranking: Odisha (46%) > Chhattisgarh (14%) > Rajasthan (13%) >\nKarnataka (12%) > Jharkhand (4.7%) > Maharashtra (4.6%) — 8 states ne total production ka 97.5%\ncover kiya. Jab question pucha gaya tha tab Bihar (undivided, Jharkhand samet) sabse rich tha. [Q7, Q8]"," 7. Odisha — 'State of Minerals'\n●\nOdisha ko 'State of Minerals' kaha jaata hai — coal, iron ore, bauxite, chromite mein rich hai, India ke total\nmineral production ka significant share deta hai. [Q9]\n8. Gondwana System — 95%+ Coal Source (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nGondwana System India ka ~99.54% coal deta hai (Assertion sahi) — Dharwar System ferrous/non-\nferrous minerals ke saath associated hai (Reason bhi sahi hai) — lekin R, A ki sahi explanation NAHI hai\n(dono independent facts hain). Coal-bearing areas: Raniganj, Jharia, Karanpur, Bokaro (Damodar Basin) aur\nPench Valley (Chhattisgarh-MP). [Q10]\n9. Non-Metallic vs Metallic Minerals (Marble Example)\n●\nNon-metallic mineral: Marble — Manganese, Silver, Lead metallic minerals hain. India total 95 minerals\nproduce karta hai (4 fuel, 10 metallic, 23 non-metallic, 3 atomic, 55 minor). [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0046","t":"24.ii.i Iron-Ore","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" IRON ORE — FULL MIND MAP\n⛰️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Dharwar System — Iron Ore's Home Rock System\n2. Top Producer States (Odisha, Chhattisgarh, Karnataka, Jharkhand)\n3. Richest in Iron Ore (Bihar/Jharkhand + Odisha)\n4. Iron Regions — Kudremukh & Singhbhum (Disputed)\n5. Punjab — No Iron Ore\n6. Nathra-ki-Pal (Rajasthan) — Iron Ore Site\n7. World Country-Mineral Match (Russia-Iron, Chile-Copper)\n8. Bailadila — Haematite Mining, Largest Mechanized Mine\n9. Place-State Match (Bailadila, Kendujhar, Balaghat, Kudremukh)\n10. Statement Verification — Karnataka Richest, India 2nd/4th\n11. Reserve Ranking (Karnataka, Odisha, Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh)\n12. Guntur — NOT Famous for Iron Ore (Wrong-Pair Trap)\n13. Haematite — Largest Reserve Type in India\n14. Iron Ore Types (Limonite, Hematite — Not Bauxite/Cinnabar)\n15. Chiria (West Singhbhum) — Iron Ore Mining\n16. Jharkhand+Odisha — Only 59% (Not 80%) of Haematite\n1. Dharwar System — Iron Ore's Home Rock System\n●\nIndia mein iron-ore Dharwar rock system mein paaya jaata hai — economic value ke hisaab se ye India ka\nsabse important rock system hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. Top Producer States (Odisha, Chhattisgarh, Karnataka, Jharkhand)\n●\n2021-22 production ke mutabik: Odisha (53.82%, 136.67 MT) > Chhattisgarh (16.27%) > Karnataka\n(15.88%) > Jharkhand (9.74%) — official answer key ne Odisha aur Karnataka ko top-2 maana\n(Chhattisgarh technically 2nd hai). [Q4]\n3. Richest in Iron Ore (Bihar/Jharkhand + Odisha)\n●\nIron ore se sabse zyada sampann 2 states Bihar (undivided, Jharkhand included) aur Odisha the —\nmodern context mein Odisha aur Jharkhand. [Q5]\n4. Iron Regions — Kudremukh & Singhbhum (Disputed)\n●\nKudremukh (Karnataka, magnetite iron-ore) aur Singhbhum (Jharkhand) dono famous iron-regions hain —\nis question mein dono options sahi maane gaye (disputed). [Q6]\n5. Punjab — No Iron Ore\n●\n4 major iron-ore regions: North-East (Jharkhand, Odisha), Central India (MP, Chhattisgarh,\nMaharashtra), Peninsular (Karnataka, Goa, AP, Kerala), Others (Rajasthan, Gujarat, Haryana, WB)\n— Punjab mein iron ore uplabdh NAHI hai. [Q7]"," 6. Nathra-ki-Pal (Rajasthan) — Iron Ore Site\n●\nNathra-ki-Pal (Rajasthan) area iron ore ke liye famous hai. [Q8]\n7. World Country-Mineral Match (Russia-Iron, Chile-Copper)\n●\nCountry-mineral match: Chile — Copper, India — Mica, Russian Federation — Iron Ore, Mexico —\nSilver. [Q9]\n8. Bailadila — Haematite Mining, Largest Mechanized Mine\n●\nBailadila (Dantewada, Chhattisgarh) mein Haematite iron-ore ka khanan hota hai — India ki sabse badi\nmechanized mine bhi yahi hai — Vizag Steel Plant se connected hai, Japan ko export karti hai. [Q10, Q11,\nQ12]\n9. Place-State Match (Bailadila, Kendujhar, Balaghat, Kudremukh)\n●\nMatch: Bailadila — Chhattisgarh, Kendujhar — Odisha, Balaghat — Madhya Pradesh, Kudremukh —\nKarnataka. [Q13]\n10. Statement Verification — Karnataka Richest, India 2nd/4th\n●\nSahi statements: Karnataka mein richest deposits hain (magnetite), Odisha production mein largest hai\n— 'India world mein 2nd largest producer hai' — jab question pucha gaya tab sahi tha, ab India 4th\nlargest hai (2021, P). [Q14]\n11. Reserve Ranking (Karnataka, Odisha, Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh)\n●\n2020-21 reserve ranking: Karnataka > Odisha > Jharkhand > Chhattisgarh (Magnetite+Haematite\ncombined) — 1 April 2020 ke data ke mutabik. [Q15]\n12. Guntur — NOT Famous for Iron Ore (Wrong-Pair Trap)\n●\nGold-Kolar, Coal-Jharia, Diamonds-Panna sahi pairs hain — 'Iron-ore-Guntur' GALAT hai (Guntur iron-\nore ke liye famous NAHI hai). [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Guntur — iron-ore ke liye famous NAHI hai (common wrong-pair)\n⚠️\n13. Haematite — Largest Reserve Type in India\n●\nIron-ore types mein Haematite ka sabse bada reserve India mein hai (~24 billion tonnes, 2020). [Q17]\n14. Iron Ore Types (Limonite, Hematite — Not Bauxite/Cinnabar)\n●\nIron ke ores: Limonite, Hematite, Magnetite, Siderite (Pyrite bhi technically iron-ore hai, par\ncommercial use sulfur/sulfuric acid ke liye hota hai) — Cinnabar mercury ka ore hai, Bauxite\naluminium ka, Chromite alag mineral hai, Malachite copper ka. [Q18, Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Cinnabar (mercury), Bauxite (aluminium), Malachite (copper) — iron ke ores NAHI\n⚠️\nhain\n15. Chiria (West Singhbhum) — Iron Ore Mining"," ●\nChiria (West Singhbhum, Jharkhand) iron ore mining ke liye famous hai. [Q20]\n16. Jharkhand+Odisha — Only 59% (Not 80%) of Haematite\n●\nSahi statements: India mein mainly haematite-magnetite reserves hain, Bellary Karnataka ka major\nmining area hai, Mayurbhanj Odisha mein important hai — 'Jharkhand+Odisha mein 80% haematite\nreserves' GALAT hai (actual mein sirf 59% hai — Odisha 39% + Jharkhand 20%). [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0047","t":"24.ii.ii Zinc","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ZINC — FULL MIND MAP\n⚙️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rampur Agucha (Bhilwara) — Asia's Best Zinc-Lead Reserves\n2. Rajasthan's Near-Monopoly in Zinc\n1. Rampur Agucha (Bhilwara) — Asia's Best Zinc-Lead Reserves\n●\nAsia ke best zinc-lead reserves Rampur Agucha, Bhilwara district, Rajasthan mein hain — Hindustan\nZinc Limited ne Britain ki madad se super smelter machine lagayi hai. Baaki reserves: Zawar, Rajpur\nDebari (Udaipur), Dungarpur, Alwar, Banswara, Sirohi. [Q1]\n2. Rajasthan's Near-Monopoly in Zinc\n●\nRajasthan ka zinc mein near-monopoly hai (89.32% lead-zinc reserves) — Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022\nke mutabik. [Q2]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0048","t":"24.ii.iii Silver","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🪙 SILVER — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Silver Reserves — Rajasthan Dominant, Gujarat Absent\n1. Silver Reserves — Rajasthan Dominant, Gujarat Absent\n●\nIndia ke total silver reserves (~30,267 tonnes, 2020) mein Rajasthan ~86% share rakhta hai — Karnataka\n(5%), Jharkhand (4%), Andhra Pradesh (3%) dusre number par. Gujarat mein silver NAHI paayi jaati\n(MP, Uttarakhand, Odisha, Meghalaya, Sikkim, TN, Maharashtra milke sirf 3% share rakhte hain). [Q1]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0049","t":"24.ii.iv Copper","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" COPPER — FULL MIND MAP\n🔶\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Malanjkhand (Balaghat, MP) — Leading Copper Producer\n2. Rajasthan — Largest Copper Reserves\n3. Copper Field-State Match Set (Chandrapur, Hasan, Khammam, Khetri)\n4. Southern Karnataka — Atomic Minerals Cell Discovery (1999)\n5. Khetri (Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan) — Copper Mining Belt\n1. Malanjkhand (Balaghat, MP) — Leading Copper Producer\n●\nCopper igneous-metamorphic rocks mein milta hai, electricity ka good conductor hai — Madhya Pradesh\ncopper-ore production mein pehle number par hai (Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022) — Malajkhand\n(Balaghat, MP) — open-pit copper mine, MP ka leading centre. 3 important districts: Jhunjhunu\n(Rajasthan), Balaghat (MP), Poorvi Singhbhumi (Jharkhand). [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. Rajasthan — Largest Copper Reserves\n●\nCopper ke largest reserves/resources Rajasthan mein hain (Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022, 1 April 2020\ntak) — production mein MP aage hai, par reserves mein Rajasthan sabse aage hai. [Q5]\n3. Copper Field-State Match Set (Chandrapur, Hasan, Khammam, Khetri)\n●\nCopper fields ka match: Chandrapur — Maharashtra, Hasan — Karnataka, Khammam — Andhra\nPradesh (ab Telangana), Khetri — Rajasthan. [Q6]\n4. Southern Karnataka — Atomic Minerals Cell Discovery (1999)\n●\nAtomic Minerals Cell (Department of Atomic Energy) ne 1999 mein Southern Karnataka mein copper\ndeposits discover kiye the. [Q7]\n5. Khetri (Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan) — Copper Mining Belt\n●\nKhetri (Jhunjhunu district, Rajasthan) copper mining ke liye famous hai — Khetri Belt bhi isi kaam ke liye\njaani jaati hai (iron/gold/mica/coal ke liye NAHI). [Q8, Q9, Q10]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0050","t":"24.ii.v Bauxite","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" BAUXITE — FULL MIND MAP\n🧱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Bauxite — Aluminium Ore\n2. Top Producers — Odisha, Gujarat, Jharkhand\n3. Aluminium Industry — Principal Raw Material\n4. Mining Area-Mineral Match Set (Kalahandi, Zawar, Kolar, Mosabani)\n5. Chhattisgarh Bauxite Districts (Kondagaon)\n6. Odisha — Largest Bauxite Reserve (41%)\n1. Bauxite — Aluminium Ore\n●\nBauxite Aluminium ka ore hai — iska color iron-content ke hisaab se white/pink/red hota hai. [Q1]\n2. Top Producers — Odisha, Gujarat, Jharkhand\n●\nBauxite ke top-3 producers: Odisha, Gujarat, Jharkhand (Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022) — 2020-21\nreport ke mutabik bhi Odisha 1st, Gujarat 2nd, Chhattisgarh 3rd the. 2021-22 (P) mein: Odisha, Gujarat,\nJharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Maharashtra. [Q2, Q4]\n3. Aluminium Industry — Principal Raw Material\n●\nBauxite (15-25% aluminium content) aluminium industry ka principal raw material hai — commercial\nextraction ke liye ekmatra ore hai. Main deposits: Kalahandi, Koraput, Sundargarh, Bolangir, Sambalpur\n(Odisha). [Q3]\n4. Mining Area-Mineral Match Set (Kalahandi, Zawar, Kolar, Mosabani)\n●\nMining area-mineral match: Kalahandi — Bauxite, Zawar — Zinc-Lead, Kolar — Gold, Mosabani —\nCopper. [Q5]\n5. Chhattisgarh Bauxite Districts (Kondagaon)\n●\nChhattisgarh mein bauxite Kabirdham, Kondagaon aur Surguja districts mein milta hai. [Q6]\n6. Odisha — Largest Bauxite Reserve (41%)\n●\nTotal bauxite reserve ranking: Odisha (41%) > Chhattisgarh (20%) > Andhra Pradesh (12%) > Gujarat\n(8%) > Jharkhand (6%) (Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022, 1.4.2020 tak). [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0051","t":"24.ii.vi Tin","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" TIN — FULL MIND MAP\n⛏️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Chhattisgarh — India's Only Tin-Producing State\n1. Chhattisgarh — India's Only Tin-Producing State\n●\nChhattisgarh India ka ekmatra tin-producing state hai — major tin-ore reserves Haryana, Chhattisgarh\naur Odisha mein hain (Chhattisgarh mein 36%), lekin production sirf Chhattisgarh se hota hai. Reserve ke\nhisaab se Chhattisgarh desh mein tin ka dusra sabse bada reserve rakhta hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0052","t":"24.c.i Mica","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MICA — FULL MIND MAP\n💎\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rajasthan — Biggest Mica Producer (Options-Dependent)\n2. Andhra Pradesh — Actual Largest Mica Reserve Holder\n3. Kodarma (Jharkhand) — Famous Mica District\n4. Mica-Producing States (MP Excluded)\n5. Largest Mica Belt — Hazaribagh, Gaya, Munger, Koderma\n6. Mica Found in Metamorphic Rock Veins\n7. World Mica Production — China Leads (Not India)\n1. Rajasthan — Biggest Mica Producer (Options-Dependent)\n●\nJab options mein Andhra Pradesh na ho, tab Rajasthan India ka sabse bada mica producer maana jaata\nhai (Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik) — ye bahut baar exam mein pucha gaya hai. [Q1, Q4]\n2. Andhra Pradesh — Actual Largest Mica Reserve Holder\n●\nActual mein Andhra Pradesh ke paas sabse zyada mica reserves (41%) hain — Rajasthan (28%),\nOdisha (17%), Bihar (2%) dusre number par (2021 Yearbook data). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP — Andhra Pradesh actual mein largest mica producer hai — Rajasthan sirf 'options mein\n⚠️\nna hone par' correct answer banta hai\n3. Kodarma (Jharkhand) — Famous Mica District\n●\nKodarma district (Jharkhand) mica mining ke liye famous hai. [Q3]\n4. Mica-Producing States (MP Excluded)\n●\nMica-producing states: Jharkhand, Rajasthan, Andhra Pradesh — Madhya Pradesh mica produce\nNAHI karta (par ye original question ka final answer key mein remove kar diya gaya tha). [Q5]\n5. Largest Mica Belt — Hazaribagh, Gaya, Munger, Koderma\n●\nIndia ki sabse badi Mica Belt — Hazaribagh, Gaya, Munger, Koderma districts (Jharkhand) mein hai\n— inhe 'Capital of Mica' kaha jaata hai. [Q6]\n6. Mica Found in Metamorphic Rock Veins\n●\nMica metamorphic rocks ki veins mein paayi jaati hai — map-based question mein mica ki distribution\npoore diye gaye marked places par hoti hai. [Q7]\n7. World Mica Production — China Leads (Not India)"," ●\n2001 mein (jab question pucha gaya tha) India Mica Sheet ka world leader tha — abhi (2022 data) China\npehle number par hai, Madagascar dusre number par. Copper mein Chile leader hai, Gypsum mein USA,\nIron ore mein Australia — inme se koi bhi India ke naam NAHI hai. [Q8, Q9]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0053","t":"24.iii.ii Marble","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MARBLE — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Makrana (Nagaur, Rajasthan) — Best Quality Marble\n2. Marble — Metamorphic Rock (Re-crystallized Limestone)\n1. Makrana (Nagaur, Rajasthan) — Best Quality Marble\n●\nMakrana (Nagaur district, Rajasthan) mein sabse best-quality marble milta hai — Taj Mahal aur Victoria\nMemorial (Kolkata) dono Makrana marble se bane hain. [Q1]\n2. Marble — Metamorphic Rock (Re-crystallized Limestone)\n●\nMarble ek metamorphic rock hai — jab limestone heat aur pressure (metamorphism) se guzarta hai to\nmarble banta hai. Ye re-crystallized carbonate minerals (limestone) se bana hota hai — sedimentary,\nigneous ya organic-to-inorganic conversion se NAHI. [Q2, Q3]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0054","t":"24.d.i Coal","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" COAL — FULL MIND MAP\n⚫\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. First Coal Mine — Raniganj, Damodar River (1774)\n2. Coal Mining Timeline (Raniganj→NCDC→Nationalisation→CIL)\n3. Coalfield Map Trap — Karanpura is in Jharkhand (Not Elsewhere)\n4. Gondwana System — Main Source of Coal (99%+)\n5. Gondwana Provides 90%+ of India's Coal\n6. Indian Coal Characteristics — High Ash, Low Sulphur\n7. Gondwana Rocks — Most Important Due to 90%+ Coal Reserves\n8. India Self-Sufficient in Coking Coal for 3 Decades\n9. Coal Reserves — 293.50 Billion Tonnes Assertion (Disputed)\n10. Jharkhand & Odisha — 50%+ of Total Coal Reserves\n11. China #1 in Coal Production; India Has Vast Reserves (JH, CG)\n12. Historical Coal Ranking — Undivided Bihar > Undivided MP (1999)\n13. Two Leading Coal States — Jharkhand & Chhattisgarh (Historical)\n14. Coal Production Descending Order (Jharkhand>Odisha>MP>Chhattisgarh, Historical)\n15. Odisha — Largest Coal Producing State (24% Share)\n16. Coal Reserves Descending Order (Odisha>Jharkhand>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n17. Major Coal Reserve States — Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha (All Correct)\n18. Odisha — Largest Coal Reserves & Largest Producer\n19. Coal Reserves Ranking (Historical: Jharkhand>Odisha>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n20. Coal Reserves Ranking (2022: Jharkhand>Odisha>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n21. Coal Production 2014 Ranking (Chhattisgarh>Jharkhand>Odisha>Maharashtra)\n22. Chota Nagpur Industrial Region — Grew from Coal Discovery\n23. Jharkhand's Coal Production Share — 16.72% (Disputed)\n24. Three Leading Coal Producers (Historical Chhattisgarh>Odisha>Jharkhand)\n25. Two Largest Coal Producers 2008-09 — Chhattisgarh & Odisha\n26. Korba Coalfield — Chhattisgarh (Hasdeo River Basin)\n27. Coal Valley-Field Match (Damodar-Barakar, Son-Umaria, Godavari-Singareni, Mahanadi-Talcher)\n28. Coalfield-Valley Match (Talcher-Mahanadi, Karnapura-Damodar, Singroli-Son, Singreni-Godavari)\n29. Talcher — Odisha's Famous Coal Region (Angul District)\n30. Chota Nagpur's Coal Production Contribution — ~64% (2021-22)\n31. Coal Mines in Jharkhand — Jharia (Not Jamshedpur/Ranchi/Lohardaga)\n32. Maximum Coal Reserve Region — Raniganj (WB Portion)\n33. Jharia — Coal Deposits, Dhanbad District\n34. Jharia Coalfield — Located in Jharkhand\n35. Lignite — Inferior Coal Variety (40-55% Carbon, TN Leader)\n36. Largest Lignite Deposit — Tamil Nadu (Neyveli)\n37. Neyveli — India's Largest Lignite Coalfield\n38. Tamil Nadu — Largest Lignite Reserve State\n39. Bengal-Jharkhand Coalfields — Major Source for NW States Rail Traffic\n40. Bisrampur — Coal Mining, Surajpur District, Chhattisgarh\n41. Coalfield-State Match (Karanpura-Jharkhand, Singareni-Telangana, Neyveli-TN, Korba-Chhattisgarh)\n42. Coal Import Reasons — Power Plants + Coking Coal Needs (Not Policy)\n43. Coalbed Methane & Shale Gas — Both Sources Exist in India\n44. Indian Coal Industry Problems — Quality, Washeries, Imports, Prices\n45. Maximum Coal Use — Energy Production"," 46. Lignite NOT a Major Reserve in Jharkhand (TN, Rajasthan, Gujarat Are)\n47. Damodar River Valley — Most Important for Gondwana-Age Coal\n48. Coalfield-State Match (Rajmahal-Jharkhand, Sohagpur-MP, Bisrampur-CG, Raniganj-WB)\n49. Northeast Coalfield Match (Makum-Assam, Namchik-Arunachal, Giridih-Jharkhand, Sohagpur-MP)\n50. Namchik-Namphuk Coalfields — Arunachal Pradesh (Changlang District)\n51. Coalfield-State Match (Jhilmili-Chhattisgarh, Karanpura-Jharkhand, Rampur Himgir-Odisha, Sohagpur-MP)\n52. NE Coalfield Match (Ranjit Valley-Sikkim, Tandur-Telangana, Warora-Maharashtra, Lalmatia-Jharkhand)\n53. Coal Resource Match (Hutar-Jharkhand, Ib River-Odisha, Tatapani-Ramkola-Chhattisgarh, Umaria-MP)\n54. Underground Coal Combustion — Jharkhand (Jharia Coalfield)\n55. Coal Controller's Organization (CCO) — Statistics, Monitoring, Objections\n1. First Coal Mine — Raniganj, Damodar River (1774)\n●\nIndia ki pehli coal mine Raniganj mein Damodar river ke tat par khodi gayi thi (1774 mein). [Q1]\n2. Coal Mining Timeline (Raniganj→NCDC→Nationalisation→CIL)\n●\nIndia ka coal mining ~220 saal purana hai — chronological order: Raniganj mein pehla coal production\n(1774), NCDC establish (1956), coal mines ka nationalisation (1971-72 coking, 1973 non-coking), Coal\nIndia Ltd (CIL) establish. [Q2]\n3. Coalfield Map Trap — Karanpura is in Jharkhand (Not Elsewhere)\n●\nSatpura, Son Valley, Korba coalfields sahi jagah dikhaye gaye — 'Karanpura' galat dikhaya gaya tha\n(Karanpura asal mein Jharkhand mein hai). [Q3]\n4. Gondwana System — Main Source of Coal (99%+)\n●\nIndia ke coal deposits mainly Gondwana sediments (Peninsular India ke eastern-central parts) mein\nconcentrated hain — Assam-Sikkim mein bhi milte hain — 99% se zyada coal Gondwana se aata hai.\n[Q4, Q5, Q6]\n5. Gondwana Provides 90%+ of India's Coal\n●\nGondwana rock system 90% se zyada India ka coal deta hai. [Q5, Q6]\n6. Indian Coal Characteristics — High Ash, Low Sulphur\n●\nIndian coal 2 areas mein milta hai: Gondwana region (high-grade, kam ash, high thermal power) aur\nKalp/Tertiary region (low-quality, sulphur-rich) — Gondwana coal ki characteristics: high ash content,\nlow sulphur content — 'low ash fusion temperature' Indian coal ki characteristic NAHI hai. [Q7]\n7. Gondwana Rocks — Most Important Due to 90%+ Coal Reserves\n●\nGondwana rocks ko India ki sabse important rock system maana jaata hai kyunki 90% se zyada India ke\ncoal reserves inme paaye jaate hain. [Q8]\n8. India Self-Sufficient in Coking Coal for 3 Decades\n●\nEnergy Policy report (Planning Commission) ke mutabik: petroleum reserves 22 saal mein khatam ho\njaayenge, gas 30 saal mein, coal 80 saal mein — India coking coal mein agle 3 dashak tak self-sufficient"," rahega — Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik 1200m depth tak 361411 million tonnes coal resources\nhain. [Q9]\n9. Coal Reserves — 293.50 Billion Tonnes Assertion (Disputed)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik coal reserves 361411 million tonnes hain (Assertion mein diya\n293.50 billion tonnes figure purana/galat hai) — Jharkhand aur Odisha mein desh ke kul coal reserves ka\naadhe se zyada hissa hai (Reason sahi hai) — Public Service Commission ne answer (b) maana tha, par\nsahi answer (d) hona chahiye (Assertion galat, Reason sahi) — disputed question hai. [Q10]\n10. Jharkhand & Odisha — 50%+ of Total Coal Reserves\n●\n1 April 2022 tak Odisha (88105 MT), Jharkhand (86660 MT), Chhattisgarh (74192 MT) sabse zyada\ngeological coal resources wale states hain — Odisha+Jharkhand milke desh ke kul coal deposits ka\n48.4% hain — total geological coal resources 361411 million tonnes. [Q11]\n11. China #1 in Coal Production; India Has Vast Reserves (JH, CG)\n●\n2021 mein China world coal-lignite production ka ~50% share rakhta tha, India dusre number par\n(9.0%), phir USA (7.88%), Indonesia (7.80%), Australia (6.02%), Russia (5.48%) — India ke paas\nJharkhand-Chhattisgarh jaise states mein vishaal coal reserves hain (sab statements sahi hain). [Q12]\n12. Historical Coal Ranking — Undivided Bihar > Undivided MP (1999)\n●\n1999 mein undivided Bihar (Jharkhand included) ka coal production undivided Madhya Pradesh\n(Chhattisgarh included) se zyada tha — sahi order: Bihar, MP, WB — abhi (2021-22, P) top-3: Odisha,\nChhattisgarh, MP. [Q13]\n13. Two Leading Coal States — Jharkhand & Chhattisgarh (Historical)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Jharkhand aur Chhattisgarh do leading coal-producing states the — Indian Minerals\nYearbook 2022 (2021-22, P) ke mutabik ab Odisha aur Chhattisgarh top-2 hain. [Q14]\n14. Coal Production Descending Order (Jharkhand>Odisha>MP>Chhattisgarh, Historical)\n●\n2007-08 ke data ke mutabik top coal producers: Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha, Madhya Pradesh —\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 (2021-22, P) ke top-5: Odisha > Chhattisgarh > Madhya Pradesh >\nJharkhand > Telangana — coal ko 'Black Diamond' aur 'Fuel Mineral' kaha jaata hai. [Q15]\n15. Odisha — Largest Coal Producing State (24% Share)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Odisha ~24% share ke saath coal ka sabse bada producer\nstate hai, Chhattisgarh dusre number par hai. [Q16, Q17]\n16. Coal Reserves Descending Order (Odisha>Jharkhand>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n●\nCoal (proved) reserves ke descending order (1 April 2022 tak): Odisha > Jharkhand > Chhattisgarh >\nWest Bengal > Madhya Pradesh — diye gaye options mein se koi bhi match nahi karta, isliye disputed\nquestion hai. [Q18]"," 17. Major Coal Reserve States — Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha (All Correct)\n●\nJharkhand, Chhattisgarh, aur Odisha sab teeno India ke major coal-reserve states hain (in mein se koi bhi\nek nahi, teeno sahi hain). [Q19]\n18. Odisha — Largest Coal Reserves & Largest Producer\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Odisha total coal reserves aur production (2021-22, P) dono\nmein sabse aage hai — 88105 million tonnes reserves. [Q20]\n19. Coal Reserves Ranking (Historical: Jharkhand>Odisha>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n●\n1 April 2021 tak coal (proved) reserves ka chronological order: Jharkhand > Odisha > Chhattisgarh >\nWest Bengal > Madhya Pradesh. [Q21]\n20. Coal Reserves Ranking (2022: Jharkhand>Odisha>Chhattisgarh>WB>MP)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 (1 April 2022) ke mutabik: Jharkhand (53245 MT) > Odisha (48573 MT)\n> Chhattisgarh (32053 MT) > West Bengal (17234 MT) > Madhya Pradesh (14052 MT). [Q22]\n21. Coal Production 2014 Ranking (Chhattisgarh>Jharkhand>Odisha>Maharashtra)\n●\nCoal Statistics 2014-15 ke mutabik: Chhattisgarh (22.5%) > Jharkhand (20.0%) > Odisha (19.9%) >\nMaharashtra — Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022 (2021-22, P) ke top-5: Odisha > Chhattisgarh > MP >\nJharkhand > Telangana. [Q23]\n22. Chota Nagpur Industrial Region — Grew from Coal Discovery\n●\nChota Nagpur industrial region (Jharkhand, North Odisha, WB mein extended) Damodar Valley mein coal\nki khoj ki wajah se develop hua — heavy metallurgical industry ke liye famous hai. [Q24]\n23. Jharkhand's Coal Production Share — 16.72% (Disputed)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik 2021-22 (P) mein total coal production mein Jharkhand ka\nshare 16.72% tha — diye gaye options (40/45/47/49%) mein se koi bhi sahi nahi tha, disputed question\nhai. [Q25]\n24. Three Leading Coal Producers (Historical Chhattisgarh>Odisha>Jharkhand)\n●\n2008-09 mein Chhattisgarh (20.7%), Odisha (20.0%), Jharkhand (19.5%) coal production mein top-3\nthe — abhi (2021-22, P): Odisha (24%), Chhattisgarh (20%), Madhya Pradesh (18%). [Q26]\n25. Two Largest Coal Producers 2008-09 — Chhattisgarh & Odisha\n●\n2008-09 mein Chhattisgarh aur Odisha coal ke do sabse bade producers the. [Q27]\n26. Korba Coalfield — Chhattisgarh (Hasdeo River Basin)\n●\nKorba coalfield Korba district, Chhattisgarh mein Hasdeo river ke basin mein hai. [Q28]"," 27. Coal Valley-Field Match (Damodar-Barakar, Son-Umaria, Godavari-Singareni,\nMahanadi-Talcher)\n●\nMatch: Damodar Valley — Barakar, Son Valley — Umaria, Godavari Valley — Singareni, Mahanadi\nValley — Talcher. [Q29]\n28. Coalfield-Valley Match (Talcher-Mahanadi, Karnapura-Damodar, Singroli-Son,\nSingreni-Godavari)\n●\nMatch: Talcher — Mahanadi Valley, Karnapura — Damodar Valley, Singroli — Son Valley, Singreni\n— Godavari Valley. [Q30]\n29. Talcher — Odisha's Famous Coal Region (Angul District)\n●\nTalcher Angul district, Odisha ka prominent coal region hai — Mahanadi Coalfield Ltd (Coal India\nLimited ki subsidiary) manage karti hai. [Q31, Q32]\n30. Chota Nagpur's Coal Production Contribution — ~64% (2021-22)\n●\nChota Nagpur plateau (Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha, WB mein extended) ka India ke total coal\nproduction mein 64.04% [2021-22 (P)] contribution hai. [Q33]\n31. Coal Mines in Jharkhand — Jharia (Not Jamshedpur/Ranchi/Lohardaga)\n●\nJharia coalfield Dhanbad district, Jharkhand mein hai — zyadatar coking coal reserves yahin hain —\nJamshedpur iron/steel ke liye, Lohardaga bauxite ke liye, Ranchi heavy machines ke liye famous hain. [Q34]\n32. Maximum Coal Reserve Region — Raniganj (WB Portion)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 (1 April 2022) ke mutabik Raniganj (West Bengal portion, 26357 MT total\nreserves) mein sabse zyada coal reserves hain — Jharia (19533 MT), Singrauli-MP (16919 MT), Korba\n(12976 MT) se zyada. [Q35]\n33. Jharia — Coal Deposits, Dhanbad District\n●\nJharia (Jharkhand) mein mukhya roop se coal paaya jaata hai. [Q36]\n34. Jharia Coalfield — Located in Jharkhand\n●\nJharia coalfield Jharkhand mein sthith hai. [Q37]\n35. Lignite — Inferior Coal Variety (40-55% Carbon, TN Leader)\n●\nLignite 40-55% carbon wali inferior coal variety hai (Assertion mein diya 35-40% figure GALAT hai)\n— Jharkhand lignite ka largest producer NAHI hai (Tamil Nadu hai, Reason bhi galat hai) — mainly\nTamil Nadu, Gujarat, Rajasthan mein produce hoti hai. [Q38]\n EXAM TRAP — Lignite India ka largest producer Tamil Nadu hai, Jharkhand NAHI\n⚠️\n36. Largest Lignite Deposit — Tamil Nadu (Neyveli)"," ●\n2021-22 (P) mein lignite production 47 million tonnes tha (~25% badha pichhle saal se) — Tamil Nadu\n~50% production, Gujarat ~28%, Rajasthan ~22% — Tamil Nadu mein India ka sabse bada lignite\ndeposit hai. [Q39]\n37. Neyveli — India's Largest Lignite Coalfield\n●\nNeyveli (Tamil Nadu) mein India ka sabse bada lignite coal reserve hai — reserves/resources aur\nproduction dono mein Tamil Nadu top par hai. [Q40]\n38. Tamil Nadu — Largest Lignite Reserve State\n●\nMinerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik India mein total 46204.16 million tonnes lignite reserves/resources hain\n— Tamil Nadu mein sabse zyada lignite reserves hain. [Q41]\n39. Bengal-Jharkhand Coalfields — Major Source for NW States Rail Traffic\n●\nCoal ki inter-state movement railways ke through hone wale inter-state traffic ka major component hai\n(Assertion sahi) — kyunki Bengal-Jharkhand coalfields north-western states ko coal supply ka major\nsource hain (Reason bhi sahi hai, sahi explanation hai). [Q42]\n40. Bisrampur — Coal Mining, Surajpur District, Chhattisgarh\n●\nBisrampur (Surajpur district, Chhattisgarh) coal mining ke liye famous hai. [Q43]\n41. Coalfield-State Match (Karanpura-Jharkhand, Singareni-Telangana, Neyveli-TN,\nKorba-Chhattisgarh)\n●\nMatch: Karanpura — Jharkhand, Singareni — Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana), Neyveli — Tamil\nNadu, Korba — Chhattisgarh. [Q44]\n42. Coal Import Reasons — Power Plants + Coking Coal Needs (Not Policy)\n●\nIndia coal import karta hai kyunki India ke zyadatar power plants coal-based hain aur unhe desh ke\nandar se paryapt coal supply nahi milti, aur steel companies ko coking coal ki zaroorat hoti hai jo\nimport karna padta hai — 'apne coal reserves bachaane ki policy' galat reason hai. [Q45]\n43. Coalbed Methane & Shale Gas — Both Sources Exist in India\n●\nCoalbed methane (coal seam se nikalti hai, 90%+ pure methane) aur shale gas (fine-grained sedimentary\nrocks se, 86%+ methane) dono unconventional energy sources hain — India mein dono ke abundant\nsources hain (Indo-Gangetic plain, Assam, Gujarat, Rajasthan, coastal areas mein shale gas bhi milti\nhai) — 'shale gas sirf propane-butane hai' aur 'India mein shale gas nahi milti' dono statements GALAT hain.\n[Q46]\n44. Indian Coal Industry Problems — Quality, Washeries, Imports, Prices\n●\nIndian coal industry ki sab 4 problems sahi hain: poor quality/movement bottlenecks, washeries ki low\nutilization capacity, coking coal import par badhti nirbharta, administered prices. [Q47]\n45. Maximum Coal Use — Energy Production"," ●\nCoal ka sabse zyada use energy production mein hota hai — India mein ek indispensable energy source\nhai. [Q48]\n46. Lignite NOT a Major Reserve in Jharkhand (TN, Rajasthan, Gujarat Are)\n●\nLignite (brown coal) high moisture, low ash, low heating value wala hota hai — Jharkhand mein lignite ka\nmajor reserve NAHI hai — Tamil Nadu, Rajasthan, Gujarat mein hai. [Q49]\n EXAM TRAP — Lignite ka major reserve — Tamil Nadu/Rajasthan/Gujarat mein hai, Jharkhand mein\n⚠️\nNAHI\n47. Damodar River Valley — Most Important for Gondwana-Age Coal\n●\nGondwana-age coal reserves ke hisaab se Damodar river valley sabse important hai —\nJharia/Dhanbad/Bokaro (Jharkhand), Raniganj coalfield (WB, Jharkhand tak bhi extended) is valley\nmein aate hain. [Q50]\n48. Coalfield-State Match (Rajmahal-Jharkhand, Sohagpur-MP, Bisrampur-CG, Raniganj-\nWB)\n●\nMatch: Rajmahal — Jharkhand+Bihar, Sohagpur — MP+Chhattisgarh, Bisrampur — Chhattisgarh,\nRaniganj — WB+Jharkhand. [Q51]\n49. Northeast Coalfield Match (Makum-Assam, Namchik-Arunachal, Giridih-Jharkhand,\nSohagpur-MP)\n●\nMatch: Makum — Assam, Namchik — Arunachal Pradesh, Giridih — Jharkhand (best-quality coal),\nSohagpur — MP — Namchik-Namphuk Arunachal Pradesh ka ekmatra coalfield hai. [Q52]\n50. Namchik-Namphuk Coalfields — Arunachal Pradesh (Changlang District)\n●\nNamchik-Namphuk coal fields Changlang district, Arunachal Pradesh mein hain. [Q53]\n51. Coalfield-State Match (Jhilmili-Chhattisgarh, Karanpura-Jharkhand, Rampur Himgir-\nOdisha, Sohagpur-MP)\n●\nMatch: Jhilmili — Chhattisgarh, Karanpura — Jharkhand, Rampur Himgir — Odisha, Sohagpur —\nMadhya Pradesh+Chhattisgarh. [Q54]\n52. NE Coalfield Match (Ranjit Valley-Sikkim, Tandur-Telangana, Warora-Maharashtra,\nLalmatia-Jharkhand)\n●\nMatch: Ranjit Valley — Sikkim, Tandur — Telangana, Warora — Maharashtra, Lalmatia —\nJharkhand. [Q55]\n53. Coal Resource Match (Hutar-Jharkhand, Ib River-Odisha, Tatapani-Ramkola-\nChhattisgarh, Umaria-MP)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik match: Hutar — Jharkhand, Ib River — Odisha, Tatapani-\nRamkola — Chhattisgarh, Umaria — Madhya Pradesh. [Q56]"," 54. Underground Coal Combustion — Jharkhand (Jharia Coalfield)\n●\nUnderground coal ka combustion (jalna) Jharkhand state mein ho raha hai — Jharia coalfield mein.\n[Q57]\n55. Coal Controller's Organization (CCO) — Statistics, Monitoring, Objections\n●\nCCO (1916 mein establish, pehle 'Coal Commissioner' kehlata tha) ka role: Coal Statistics ka major source\nhai, captive coal/lignite blocks ki development monitor karta hai, coal-bearing areas ke acquisition-\nnotification par objections sunta hai — 'coal companies ko end-users ko time par coal deliver karvana'\nCCO ki responsibility NAHI hai (Coal Bearing Areas Act 1957 ke tahat). [Q58]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0055","t":"24.iv.ii Petroleum and Natural Gas","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS — FULL\n🛢️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Digboi — India's Oldest Oil Field (Brahmaputra Valley)\n2. Leading Petroleum Producer — Gujarat (Historical) → Rajasthan Now\n3. Largest Petroleum Producer 2013-14 — Rajasthan\n4. Ankleshwar — Famous for Petrol Reserves, Gujarat\n5. Lunej Petrol Area — Gujarat (Cambay Basin)\n6. Navgam Oil Field — Gujarat\n7. First Oil Well — Makum, Assam (1867, Not Digboi)\n8. Oldest Refinery — Digboi (1901)\n9. Correct Pair — Andhra Pradesh-Visakhapatnam Oil Refinery\n10. Correct Pair — Panagudi-Tamil Nadu\n11. Jamnagar — India's Biggest Oil Refinery\n12. Hatia — No Oil Refinery (Jharkhand)\n13. First Oil/Energy Crisis — 1970s-80s (1973, OPEC)\n14. Noonmati Oil Refinery — Assam (1962)\n15. Refinery-State Match (Haldia-WB, Jamnagar-Gujarat, Kochi-Kerala, Numaligarh-Assam)\n16. Refinery-State Match (Numaligarh-Assam, Tatipaka-AP, Koyali-Gujarat, Barauni-Bihar)\n17. Tatipaka Oil Refinery — Andhra Pradesh (ONGC)\n18. Tatipaka Oil Refinery — Location Confirmation\n19. Refinery-State Match (Noonmati-Assam, Koyali-Gujarat, Mangalore-Karnataka, Panipat-Haryana)\n20. Refinery-State Match (Tatipaka-AP, Koyali-Gujarat, Nagapattinam-TN, Numaligarh-Assam)\n21. Koyali Refinery — Set up by IOCL (Not HPCL, Wrong-Pair)\n22. Refinery-State Match (Barauni-Bihar, Bongaigaon-Assam, Bina-MP, Koyali-Gujarat)\n23. Koyali Refinery — Gujarat\n24. Cauvery Onshore Basin (Tamil Nadu) — Recent Commercial Oil Production\n25. Mangla-Bhagyam-Aishwarya — Barmer-Sanchore Basin Oil Fields\n26. NELP/JV/Nomination/CBM Blocks — Petroleum Exploration\n27. Hydrogen Vision-2025 — Petroleum Products Warehousing\n28. Strategic Petroleum Reserves — Vizag, Mangalore, Padur (Not Ankleshwar)\n29. Oil Exploration — Oil India Ltd. (+ ONGC)\n30. HBJ Pipeline — Transports Gas from South Basin (Bombay High)\n31. HBJ Pipeline — Built by GAIL\n32. HVJ Pipeline Pumping Stations — Aonla/Auraiya/Babrala/Guna (Disputed)\n33. Reliance's Natural Gas Discovery — Coastal Andhra (KG Basin)\n34. KG-D6 Basin — Large Natural Gas Reserves (2009 News)\n35. Natural Gas Production — Bombay High (Western Offshore, 64%)\n36. Bombay High Oil Field — 160km Off Mumbai Coast (Not 60km)\n37. Shale Gas Basins — Cambay, Cauvery, Krishna-Godavari (All Correct)\n38. Fossil Fuels — Coal/Petroleum/Diesel/Petrol (Not Wood)\n39. Pipeline Length Ranking — HBJ Gas Pipeline Longest (Disputed)\n1. Digboi — India's Oldest Oil Field (Brahmaputra Valley)"," ●\nIndia ka sabse purana oil field Digboi (Assam) hai — Brahmaputra valley ka oil field, sabse purana oil\nbasin. [Q1]\n2. Leading Petroleum Producer — Gujarat (Historical) → Rajasthan Now\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Gujarat petroleum ka leading producer tha — Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke\nmutabik 2020-21 (P) mein ab Rajasthan (5891 thousand tonnes) leading hai, Gujarat (4651) dusre\nnumber par. [Q2]\n3. Largest Petroleum Producer 2013-14 — Rajasthan\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik 2020-21 (P) mein crude oil-condensate ka sabse bada\nproducer state Rajasthan hai. [Q3]\n4. Ankleshwar — Famous for Petrol Reserves, Gujarat\n●\nAnkleshwar petrol reserves ke liye famous hai — Bharuch district, Gujarat mein ~38.98 km² tak failaa\nhai. [Q4]\n5. Lunej Petrol Area — Gujarat (Cambay Basin)\n●\nCambay Basin ke Lunej area mein Tertiary period ki sedimentary rocks mein tel milta hai — Lunej\nGujarat mein hai. [Q5]\n6. Navgam Oil Field — Gujarat\n●\nNavgam oil field Gujarat mein hai — Gujarat ke baaki oil fields: Ankleshwar, Kalol, Bakrol, Mehsana.\n[Q6]\n7. First Oil Well — Makum, Assam (1867, Not Digboi)\n●\nIndia ka pehla oil well Makum, upper Assam mein 26 March 1867 ko khoda gaya tha (depth 118 feet) —\nDigboi baad mein 1889 mein discover hua tha (commission ki revised answer key 'Digboi' galat thi\nhistorically). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Pehla oil well Makum mein khoda gaya tha, Digboi mein NAHI (Digboi baad mein\n⚠️\ndiscover hua)\n8. Oldest Refinery — Digboi (1901)\n●\nIndian oil refineries commissioning years: Digboi — 1901 (sabse purani), Koyali (Gujarat) — 1965,\nHaldia (WB) — 1975, Mathura (UP) — 1982. [Q8]\n9. Correct Pair — Andhra Pradesh-Visakhapatnam Oil Refinery\n●\nBarauni refinery Bihar mein hai (Assam mein NAHI), Koyna mein koi refinery nahi hai, Mathura refinery UP\nmein hai — Visakhapatnam oil refinery (HPCL) Andhra Pradesh mein hai — sahi pair. [Q9]\n10. Correct Pair — Panagudi-Tamil Nadu"," ●\nHaldia-WB (Odisha NAHI), Jamnagar-Gujarat (Maharashtra NAHI), Numaligarh-Assam (Gujarat NAHI) —\nPanagudi-Tamil Nadu hi sahi sumelit pair hai — Jamnagar mein Reliance Industries ka duniya ka sabse\nbada oil refinery hai. [Q10]\n11. Jamnagar — India's Biggest Oil Refinery\n●\nJamnagar India ki sabse badi oil refinery hai — Reliance Industries ne yahan duniya ki sabse badi oil\nrefinery banayi hai. [Q11]\n12. Hatia — No Oil Refinery (Jharkhand)\n●\nKoyali, Noonmati, Barauni mein oil refineries hain — Hatia (Jharkhand) mein koi oil refinery NAHI hai.\n[Q12]\n13. First Oil/Energy Crisis — 1970s-80s (1973, OPEC)\n●\nIndia ka pehla oil/energy crisis 1973 mein hua (1970s-80s ke dauraan) jab OPEC (oil exporting countries)\nne achanak oil price 4 guna badha diya. [Q13]\n14. Noonmati Oil Refinery — Assam (1962)\n●\nNoonmati oil refinery Assam mein hai — 1962 mein establish hui. [Q14]\n15. Refinery-State Match (Haldia-WB, Jamnagar-Gujarat, Kochi-Kerala, Numaligarh-\nAssam)\n●\nMatch: Haldia — West Bengal, Jamnagar — Gujarat, Kochi — Kerala, Numaligarh — Assam. [Q15]\n16. Refinery-State Match (Numaligarh-Assam, Tatipaka-AP, Koyali-Gujarat, Barauni-\nBihar)\n●\nMatch: Numaligarh — Assam, Tatipaka — Andhra Pradesh, Koyali — Gujarat, Barauni — Bihar.\n[Q16]\n17. Tatipaka Oil Refinery — Andhra Pradesh (ONGC)\n●\nTatipaka Oil Refinery Konaseema region, Andhra Pradesh mein hai — ONGC (Oil and Natural Gas\nCorporation) ne establish ki. [Q17, Q18]\n18. Tatipaka Oil Refinery — Location Confirmation\n●\nTatipaka Oil Refinery Andhra Pradesh mein hai. [Q18]\n19. Refinery-State Match (Noonmati-Assam, Koyali-Gujarat, Mangalore-Karnataka,\nPanipat-Haryana)\n●\nMatch: Noonmati — Assam, Koyali — Gujarat, Mangalore — Karnataka, Panipat — Haryana. [Q19]\n20. Refinery-State Match (Tatipaka-AP, Koyali-Gujarat, Nagapattinam-TN, Numaligarh-\nAssam)"," ●\nMatch: Tatipaka — Andhra Pradesh, Koyali — Gujarat, Nagapattinam — Tamil Nadu, Numaligarh —\nAssam. [Q20]\n21. Koyali Refinery — Set up by IOCL (Not HPCL, Wrong-Pair)\n●\nBina(MP)-BPCL, Tatipaka(AP)-ONGC, Digboi(Assam)-IOCL sahi hain — 'Koyali(Gujarat)-HPCL'\nGALAT hai (Koyali ko IOCL ne set up kiya tha, HPCL ne NAHI). [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP — Koyali Refinery — IOCL ne set up ki thi, HPCL ne NAHI\n⚠️\n22. Refinery-State Match (Barauni-Bihar, Bongaigaon-Assam, Bina-MP, Koyali-Gujarat)\n●\nMatch: Barauni — Bihar, Bongaigaon — Assam, Bina — Madhya Pradesh, Koyali — Gujarat. [Q22]\n23. Koyali Refinery — Gujarat\n●\nKoyali refinery Gujarat mein sthith hai. [Q23]\n24. Cauvery Onshore Basin (Tamil Nadu) — Recent Commercial Oil Production\n●\nMap par label '3' wali jagah Cauvery onshore basin, Tamil Nadu hai — yahan mineral oil ka commercial\nproduction shuru hua tha. [Q24]\n25. Mangla-Bhagyam-Aishwarya — Barmer-Sanchore Basin Oil Fields\n●\nMangla, Bhagyam aur Aishwarya Barmer-Sanchore basin (Rajasthan) mein khoje gaye oil fields hain —\nMangla field India ka sabse bada onshore hydrocarbon field maana jaata hai. [Q25]\n26. NELP/JV/Nomination/CBM Blocks — Petroleum Exploration\n●\n14 NELP Blocks, 1 JV Block, 2 Nomination Blocks aur 4 CBM Blocks petroleum exploration (khoj) se\nrelated hain. [Q26]\n27. Hydrogen Vision-2025 — Petroleum Products Warehousing\n●\n'Hydrogen Vision-2025' petroleum products ke warehousing (bhandaran) se related hai. [Q27]\n28. Strategic Petroleum Reserves — Vizag, Mangalore, Padur (Not Ankleshwar)\n●\nIndia Strategic Petroleum Reserves Ltd (ISPRL) ne Visakhapatnam, Mangaluru, Padur teen jagahon par\nunderground crude-oil storage banaye — Ankleshwar is list mein shamil NAHI hai. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP — Strategic Petroleum Reserves — Vizag/Mangalore/Padur mein hain, Ankleshwar mein\n⚠️\nNAHI\n29. Oil Exploration — Oil India Ltd. (+ ONGC)\n●\nIndia mein tel exploration ka kaam Oil India Ltd karta hai — ONGC (Oil and Natural Gas Corporation)\nbhi is field mein key player hai. [Q29]\n30. HBJ Pipeline — Transports Gas from South Basin (Bombay High)"," ●\nHBJ pipeline South Basin (Bombay High ke coastal area mein sthith) se natural gas transport karti hai.\n[Q30]\n31. HBJ Pipeline — Built by GAIL\n●\nHajira-Bijapur-Jagdishpur (HBJ) Gas Pipeline Gas Authority of India Limited (GAIL) ne banayi hai.\n[Q31]\n32. HVJ Pipeline Pumping Stations — Aonla/Auraiya/Babrala/Guna (Disputed)\n●\nIntegrated HVJ natural gas pipeline ke Aonla, Auraiya, Babrala, Guna sab jagahon par fold pumping\nstations hain — isliye ek option choose karna sahi nahi hai, disputed question hai. [Q32]\n33. Reliance's Natural Gas Discovery — Coastal Andhra (KG Basin)\n●\nKrishna-Godavari Basin (KG Basin, Andhra Pradesh ke coastal areas mein ~50,000 sq km) ke D-6 block\nmein Reliance Industries ne 2002-03 mein India ka sabse bada natural gas reserve discover kiya. [Q33]\n34. KG-D6 Basin — Large Natural Gas Reserves (2009 News)\n●\nKG-D6 Basin (April 2009 se news mein) natural gas ke vishaal reserves ke liye prasiddh hai. [Q34]\n35. Natural Gas Production — Bombay High (Western Offshore, 64%)\n●\nIndia ka zyadatar natural gas production western offshore regions, khaaskar Bombay High Complex se\naata hai — offshore areas ka 64% share hai, phir Assam (10%), Rajasthan (7%). [Q35]\n36. Bombay High Oil Field — 160km Off Mumbai Coast (Not 60km)\n●\nBombay High (Mumbai High) offshore oil field Mumbai coast se 160km door hai (60km NAHI) — 1965\nmein discover hua, pehla oil well 1974 mein khoda gaya, Russian-Indian team ne saath mein discover\nkiya — ONGC operations chalata hai. [Q36]\n EXAM TRAP — Bombay High — Mumbai coast se 160km door hai, 60km NAHI\n⚠️\n37. Shale Gas Basins — Cambay, Cauvery, Krishna-Godavari (All Correct)\n●\nShale gas resources India ke Cambay Basin, Cauvery Basin, aur Krishna-Godavari Basin teeno mein\npaaye jaate hain — 4th priority basin Damodar Valley bhi hai. [Q37]\n38. Fossil Fuels — Coal/Petroleum/Diesel/Petrol (Not Wood)\n●\nFossil fuels (lakho saal purane dabe hue plants-animals ke avshesh) ke examples: Coal, Petroleum, Diesel,\nKerosene, Natural Gas — Wood fossil fuel NAHI hai (ye biofuel hai). [Q38]\n EXAM TRAP — Wood — Biofuel hai, Fossil Fuel NAHI\n⚠️\n39. Pipeline Length Ranking — HBJ Gas Pipeline Longest (Disputed)\n●\nPipeline lengths (recent data): Hazira-Bijapur-Jagdishpur gas pipeline — 6718 km (sabse lambi), Salaya-\nKoyali-Mathura — 2663 km, Jamnagar-Loni (LPG) — 1427 km, Kandla-Bhatinda — 1413 km —"," Chhattisgarh PSC ne option (c) diya tha jo updated lengths ke hisaab se galat hai, isliye disputed question hai.\n[Q39]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0056","t":"24.v Miscellaneous Minerals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MISCELLANEOUS MINERALS — FULL MIND\n⛏️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Major vs Minor Minerals (Bentonite is Minor)\n2. Odisha's Mineral Monopoly (Chromite, Bauxite, Manganese)\n3. Mining City Mismatches (Manganese-Bhilwara is Wrong)\n4. Asbestos — AP Production, Rajasthan Reserves (Disputed)\n5. Gondwana/Dharwar — Poor in Petroleum (Kodarma Rich in Mica)\n6. Kodarma — World-Famous for Ruby Mica\n7. Garnet — Metamorphic Mineral\n8. Quartzite — Metamorphosed from Sandstone\n9. Ore-State Match (Manganese-MP, Nickel-Odisha, Lead-Zinc-Rajasthan)\n10. Madhya Pradesh — Leading Manganese Producer\n11. Manganese Ranking (MP>Odisha>AP>Rajasthan, Historical)\n12. Iron-Copper-Gold-Mica State Match (Disputed)\n13. India — Not Self-Sufficient in Any Listed Mineral\n14. Mineral Oil-Gypsum-Gold-Bauxite Match (Disputed)\n15. Rajasthan — Limestone+Gypsum+Salt+Zinc Hub\n16. Non-Metallic Minerals — Gypsum, Phosphorite, Dolomite, Garnet\n17. Rajasthan — Leading Gypsum Producer\n18. Churu-Bikaner-Sri Ganganagar Belt — Gypsum\n19. Coal-Gold-Mica-Manganese Match (Karanpura, Hutti, Nellore, Bhandara)\n20. Makum-Dallirajhara-Koraput-Chitradurg Match\n21. Kamptee — Coal (Not Copper) Wrong-Pair\n22. Badam Pahar-Kodarma-Mosabani-Rava Match\n23. Iron Ore Zones — Badam Pahar/Dalli-Rajhara/Kudremukh/Noamundi\n24. Nellore — Mica+Copper (Not Manganese) Wrong-Pair\n25. Graphite-Lead-Salt-Silver Mining Areas\n26. Ankleshwar-Dalli Rajhara-Kodarma-Khetri Match\n27. Iron Ore-Copper-Coal-Mica Match (Keonjhar, Khetri, Korba, Kodarma)\n28. Gold-Coal-Iron-Copper Location Sequence (Kolar-Jharia-Kudremukh-Khetri)\n29. Odisha's Chromite Monopoly (Repeat)\n30. Gypsum-Copper-Rock Phosphate-Lead&Zinc Match (Rajasthan Sites)\n31. Khetri-Jharia-Singhbhum Match (Copper/Coal/Iron)\n32. Bailadila-Kemmangundi-Singhbhum-Mayurbhanj State Match\n33. MP Mineral-District Match (Diamond-Panna, Coal-Sidhi)\n34. Coal-Copper-Iron-Silver Match (Talcher, Khetri, Kudremukh, Zawar)\n35. Koraput — Bauxite (Not Manganese) Wrong-Pair\n36. Copper-Gas-Aluminium-Petroleum Match (Khetri/Auraiya/Korba/Kochi)\n37. Balaghat-Manganese, Majhgawan-Diamond (Both Statements Reversed)\n38. Lalitpur — Granite Slabs & Slates (UP)\n39. Panna — India's Biggest Diamond Mining Centre\n40. Raipur District — Kimberlite (Diamond) Discovery\n41. Sonbhadra — Andalusite/Pyrite/Dolomite (Not Uranium)\n42. Kerala Beach Sand — Ilmenite/Zircon/Sillimanite (Not Tungsten)\n43. Ilmenite/Rutile — Titanium Source"," 44. Kerala — Leading Thorium Producer (Monazite)\n45. Kerala Coastal Beaches — Monazite (Disputed)\n46. Monazite — Kerala's Abundant Mineral\n47. Monazite States — Multiple (Disputed)\n48. Thorium Deposits Exist; Kerala Monazite Has Uranium\n49. Uranium Centres (Domiasiat-Meghalaya, Lambapur-AP, Rohail-Rajasthan, Gogi-Karnataka)\n50. Jaduguda — Uranium Mine (Jharkhand)\n51. Turamdih — Uranium Mining Near Jaduguda\n52. Chhattisgarh — Bauxite/Dolomite/Iron Ore/Tin All Present\n53. Palamu-Hazaribagh-Khetri-Keonjhar Match (Disputed)\n54. Chota Nagpur Plateau — Rich in Minerals\n55. Kaimur Plateau — Limestone (Bihar)\n56. Coal-Copper-Manganese-Lignite Match (Giridih/Alwar/Dharwar/Jayamkondam)\n57. Gurumahisani-Talcher-Jaduguda-Zavar Match (Iron/Coal/Uranium/Lead)\n58. Copper-Nickel-Tungsten 90% Sources (Rajasthan/Odisha/Karnataka)\n59. Guru Mahisani-Talcher-Jaduguda-Zawar Match (Repeat, Zinc Version)\n60. Sambhar Lake — Historical Salt Share (Disputed)\n61. India — 3rd Largest Salt Producer (Gujarat Leads)\n62. Bauxite-Lohardaga Match (Not Manganese-Bailadila)\n63. Mineral-Industry Match (Limestone-Cement, Bauxite-Aeroplane)\n64. Korba, Chhattisgarh — India's First Lithium Mine (2024)\n1. Major vs Minor Minerals (Bentonite is Minor)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Bentonite ek minor mineral hai (fuller's earth, marble, mica\njaisa) — Chromite, Kyanite aur Sillimanite major minerals hain. [Q1]\n2. Odisha's Mineral Monopoly (Chromite, Bauxite, Manganese)\n●\nOdisha ka Chromite production mein near-monopoly hai — Manganese aur Bauxite ke reserves mein\nbhi #1 hai (1 April 2020) — Karnataka Silver mein top producer hai (2021-22) — ye sab statements sahi\nhain, isliye disputed question hai. [Q2]\n3. Mining City Mismatches (Manganese-Bhilwara is Wrong)\n●\nIron ore-Ballari, Bauxite-Katni sahi hain — 'Copper-Chitradurga' GALAT hai (Chitradurga iron-\nmanganese ke liye hai), 'Manganese-Bhilwara' GALAT hai (Bhilwara copper ke liye famous hai,\nmanganese Banswara-Udaipur-Pali mein milta hai). [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP — Bhilwara — Copper ke liye famous hai, Manganese ke liye NAHI\n⚠️\n4. Asbestos — AP Production, Rajasthan Reserves (Disputed)\n●\n2013-14 data ke mutabik Andhra Pradesh asbestos ka ekmatra producer tha — lekin largest RESERVE\n(2020) Rajasthan mein hai — question 'production' ke baare mein tha, isliye disputed hai. [Q4]\n5. Gondwana/Dharwar — Poor in Petroleum (Kodarma Rich in Mica)\n●\nPetroleum-natural gas tertiary sedimentary rocks mein milte hain — Gondwana aur Dharwar rocks bahut\npurane (metamorphosed) hain, isliye petroleum-natural gas mein POOR hain (statements 1,3 GALAT)\n— Kodarma (Jharkhand) mica ke liye rich hai (statement 2 sahi). [Q5, Q6]"," 6. Kodarma — World-Famous for Ruby Mica\n●\nKodarma district (Jharkhand) ruby mica mining ke liye world-famous hai — 'Mica City of India' kehlata\nhai — main reserve Kodarma Wildlife Sanctuary ke jungle ke niche hai. Cuddapah basin\nbaryte/asbestos/copper/iron/lead/diamond/uranium ke liye famous hai (petroleum ke liye NAHI). [Q6]\n7. Garnet — Metamorphic Mineral\n●\nGarnet metamorphic mineral hai — high temperature-pressure (metamorphism) se banta hai —\nCopper, Manganese, Pyrite is category mein NAHI hain. [Q7]\n8. Quartzite — Metamorphosed from Sandstone\n●\nQuartzite (non-foliated metamorphic rock, mostly quartz) Sandstone (balua patthar) se metamorphose\nhota hai — heat/pressure/chemical activity se. [Q8]\n9. Ore-State Match (Manganese-MP, Nickel-Odisha, Lead-Zinc-Rajasthan)\n●\nMatch: Manganese — Madhya Pradesh, Nickel — Odisha, Lead-Zinc — Rajasthan, Asbestos —\nAndhra Pradesh. [Q9]\n10. Madhya Pradesh — Leading Manganese Producer\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Madhya Pradesh Manganese Ore ka leading producer hai\n(2021-22, P). [Q10]\n11. Manganese Ranking (MP>Odisha>AP>Rajasthan, Historical)\n●\n2013-14 ranking: Madhya Pradesh > Odisha > Andhra Pradesh > Rajasthan — 2021-22 (P) ke mutabik\nab Madhya Pradesh > Maharashtra > Odisha > Karnataka > Andhra Pradesh hai. [Q11]\n12. Iron-Copper-Gold-Mica State Match (Disputed)\n●\n2022 data ke mutabik: Iron ore — Odisha, Copper Ore — Madhya Pradesh, Gold Ore — Karnataka,\nMica — Rajasthan — diye gaye options mein koi bhi match nahi karta, isliye disputed hai. [Q12]\n13. India — Not Self-Sufficient in Any Listed Mineral\n●\nTin, Silver, Gold, Graphite mein se India kisi mein bhi self-sufficient NAHI hai — Graphite world reserves\nmein Turkey (28%), China (23%), Brazil (22%) top hain, India sirf 2% share rakhta hai. [Q13]\n14. Mineral Oil-Gypsum-Gold-Bauxite Match (Disputed)\n●\n2022 data ke mutabik: Mineral Oil (Crude) — Rajasthan, Gypsum — Rajasthan, Gold — Karnataka,\nBauxite — Odisha — diye gaye options mein koi bhi match nahi karta, isliye disputed hai. [Q14]\n15. Rajasthan — Limestone+Gypsum+Salt+Zinc Hub\n●\nRajasthan state Limestone, Gypsum, Salt, Zinc ke deposits ke liye famous hai. [Q15]"," 16. Non-Metallic Minerals — Gypsum, Phosphorite, Dolomite, Garnet\n●\nIndia ke non-metallic minerals: Phosphorite, Dolomite, Gypsum, Garnet, Wollastonite, Vermiculite,\nOchre, Perlite, Bentonite, Asbestos, Feldspar, Soapstone, Kaolin, Sillimanite, Limestone, Diatomite,\nPyrophyllite, Fluorite — Haematite, Bauxite, Limonite metallic minerals hain. [Q16]\n17. Rajasthan — Leading Gypsum Producer\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Rajasthan gypsum ka leading producer hai (2021-22, P).\n[Q17]\n18. Churu-Bikaner-Sri Ganganagar Belt — Gypsum\n●\nChuru-Bikaner-Sri Ganganagar belt mein Gypsum bhaari matra mein milta hai — environmental\npollution ka source hai, soil fertility badhaane ke liye use hota hai, value-addition ke baad health-\nconstruction sector mein use hota hai. [Q18]\n19. Coal-Gold-Mica-Manganese Match (Karanpura, Hutti, Nellore, Bhandara)\n●\nMatch: Coal — Karanpura (Jharkhand), Gold — Hutti (Karnataka), Mica — Nellore (Andhra\nPradesh), Manganese — Bhandara (Maharashtra). [Q19]\n20. Makum-Dallirajhara-Koraput-Chitradurg Match\n●\nMatch: Makum — Coal, Dallirajhara — Iron Ore, Koraput — Bauxite, Chitradurg — Manganese.\n[Q20]\n21. Kamptee — Coal (Not Copper) Wrong-Pair\n●\nAmguri-Petroleum, Lanjigarh-Bauxite, Bellary-Iron ore sahi hain — 'Kamptee-Copper' GALAT hai\n(Kamptee, Maharashtra, coal ke liye famous hai). [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP — Kamptee — Coal ke liye famous hai, Copper ke liye NAHI\n⚠️\n22. Badam Pahar-Kodarma-Mosabani-Rava Match\n●\nMatch: Badam Pahar (Odisha) — Iron ore, Kodarma (Jharkhand) — Mica, Mosabani (Jharkhand) —\nCopper, Rava (Krishna-Godavari Basin) — Petroleum. [Q22]\n23. Iron Ore Zones — Badam Pahar/Dalli-Rajhara/Kudremukh/Noamundi\n●\nIron ore zone-state match: Badam Pahar — Odisha, Dalli-Rajhara — Chhattisgarh, Kudremukh —\nKarnataka, Noamundi — Jharkhand. [Q23]\n24. Nellore — Mica+Copper (Not Manganese) Wrong-Pair\n●\nDalli-Rajhara-Iron Ore, Rakha-Copper, Amar Kantak-Bauxite sahi hain — 'Nellore-Manganese' GALAT\nhai (Nellore, AP, mica-copper ke liye famous hai). [Q24]\n EXAM TRAP — Nellore — Mica aur Copper ke liye famous hai, Manganese ke liye NAHI\n⚠️\n25. Graphite-Lead-Salt-Silver Mining Areas"," ●\nMatch: Graphite — Rampa (Andhra Pradesh), Lead — Zawar (Rajasthan), Salt — Didwana\n(Rajasthan), Silver — Bellary (Karnataka). [Q25]\n26. Ankleshwar-Dalli Rajhara-Kodarma-Khetri Match\n●\nMatch: Ankleshwar (Bharuch, Gujarat) — Petroleum, Dalli-Rajhara — Iron Ore (Bhilai Steel Plant ke\nliye captive mines), Kodarma — Mica, Khetri — Copper (Khetri-Singhana, Kho-Dariba, Bhan-goni\nmines). [Q26]\n27. Iron Ore-Copper-Coal-Mica Match (Keonjhar, Khetri, Korba, Kodarma)\n●\nMatch: Iron Ore — Keonjhar, Copper — Khetri, Coal — Korba, Mica — Kodarma. [Q27]\n28. Gold-Coal-Iron-Copper Location Sequence (Kolar-Jharia-Kudremukh-Khetri)\n●\nSequence: Copper-Khetri (Rajasthan), Gold-Kolar (Karnataka), Iron-Kudremukh (world ki sabse badi\nmines mein se ek), Coal-Jharia (Dhanbad, Jharkhand). [Q28, Q29]\n29. Odisha's Chromite Monopoly (Repeat)\n●\nIndian Bureau of Mines (2022) ke mutabik Odisha chromite production mein continue kar raha hai\nmajor state banke rehna (2021-22, P) — almost entire production ka share rakhta hai. [Q30]\n30. Gypsum-Copper-Rock Phosphate-Lead&Zinc Match (Rajasthan Sites)\n●\nMatch: Gypsum — Jamsar, Copper — Khoh-Dariba, Rock Phosphate — Jhamar-kotra, Lead & Zinc\n— Rampura-Agucha — sab Rajasthan mein hain. [Q31]\n31. Khetri-Jharia-Singhbhum Match (Copper/Coal/Iron)\n●\nMatch: Khetri (Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan) — Copper, Jharia (Jharkhand) — Coal (coke banane ke liye\nuse), Singhbhum (Jharkhand) — Iron ore. [Q32]\n32. Bailadila-Kemmangundi-Singhbhum-Mayurbhanj State Match\n●\nMatch: Bailadila — Chhattisgarh, Kemmangundi — Karnataka, Singhbhum — Jharkhand,\nMayurbhanj — Odisha. [Q33]\n33. MP Mineral-District Match (Diamond-Panna, Coal-Sidhi)\n●\nMP mineral-district match: Diamond — Panna, Iron ore — Bastar/Durg (Chhattisgarh), Bauxite —\nSurguja/Mandla/Satna/Balaghat/Bilaspur, Coal —\nSidhi/Surguja/Bilaspur/Raigarh/Shahdol/Chhindwara/Betul. [Q34]\n34. Coal-Copper-Iron-Silver Match (Talcher, Khetri, Kudremukh, Zawar)\n●\nMatch: Coal — Talcher (Angul, Odisha), Copper — Khetri, Iron Ore — Kudremukh, Silver — Zawar\n(Udaipur, Rajasthan). [Q35]\n35. Koraput — Bauxite (Not Manganese) Wrong-Pair"," ●\nIron Ore-Kudremukh, Copper-Khetri, Coal-Singareni sahi hain — 'Manganese-Koraput' GALAT hai\n(Koraput bauxite/aluminium ke liye famous hai). [Q36]\n EXAM TRAP — Koraput — Bauxite/Aluminium ke liye famous hai, Manganese ke liye NAHI\n⚠️\n36. Copper-Gas-Aluminium-Petroleum Match (Khetri/Auraiya/Korba/Kochi)\n●\nMatch: Copper — Khetri, Gas Plant — Auraiya, Aluminium — Korba, Petroleum — Kochi. [Q37]\n37. Balaghat-Manganese, Majhgawan-Diamond (Both Statements Reversed)\n●\nSahi facts: Balaghat (MP) manganese-ore production ke liye important hai (diamond ke liye NAHI),\nMajhgawan (Panna, MP) diamond ke liye jaana jaata hai (manganese ke liye NAHI) — 'Balaghat-\ndiamond' aur 'Majhgawan-manganese' dono statements GALAT hain. [Q38]\n38. Lalitpur — Granite Slabs & Slates (UP)\n●\nGranite UP ke Lalitpur, Mahoba, Banda districts mein milta hai — granite slates mainly Lalitpur mein\nbante hain. [Q39]\n39. Panna — India's Biggest Diamond Mining Centre\n●\nPanna (Madhya Pradesh) India ka sabse bada diamond mining centre hai — Panna aur Satna districts\nmein diamond mines hain. [Q40]\n40. Raipur District — Kimberlite (Diamond) Discovery\n●\nDiamond-bearing kimberlite ke bade reserves Raipur district (Payalikhand, Behradin) aur Bastar\n(Tokapal) mein discover hue. [Q41]\n41. Sonbhadra — Andalusite/Pyrite/Dolomite (Not Uranium)\n●\nSonbhadra district (UP) mein Fireclay, Limestone, China Clay, Dolomite, Potash, Andalusite, Pyrite\nmilte hain — Uranium NAHI (wo Lalitpur district mein milta hai). [Q42]\n EXAM TRAP — Uranium — Lalitpur district mein milta hai, Sonbhadra mein NAHI\n⚠️\n42. Kerala Beach Sand — Ilmenite/Zircon/Sillimanite (Not Tungsten)\n●\nKerala ke beach sand mein Ilmenite, Zircon, Sillimanite (Rutile, Leucoxene, Monazite bhi) milte hain —\nTungsten NAHI — Neendakara-Kayamkulam coastal tract world-class mineral-sand deposits ke liye jaana\njaata hai. [Q43]\n43. Ilmenite/Rutile — Titanium Source\n●\nIlmenite aur Rutile Titanium ka rich source hain — India ke coastal tracts mein abundant hain. [Q44]\n44. Kerala — Leading Thorium Producer (Monazite)\n●\nKerala India ka thorium ka leading producer hai — monazite processing se, Indian Rare Earths Limited\nka plant Udyagmandal (Aluva), Ernakulam district mein hai. [Q45]"," 45. Kerala Coastal Beaches — Monazite (Disputed)\n●\nKerala ke coast par Monazite mineral milta hai — thorium aur uranium bhi monazite minerals mein\nmilte hain — multiple elements list mein hone ki wajah se disputed question hai. [Q46]\n46. Monazite — Kerala's Abundant Mineral\n●\nKerala mein prachur matra mein paaya jaane wala mineral Monazite hai — Tin, Manganese, Mica se zyada.\n[Q47]\n47. Monazite States — Multiple (Disputed)\n●\nMonazite India mein Odisha, Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Kerala, West Bengal, Maharashtra,\nGujarat mein milta hai — options mein Tamil Nadu aur Kerala dono hain, isliye disputed question hai.\n[Q48]\n48. Thorium Deposits Exist; Kerala Monazite Has Uranium\n●\n'India mein thorium ka koi deposit nahi hai' GALAT hai — Kerala ki monazite sand mein Uranium hota\nhai (statement 2 sahi hai) — monazite thorium, lanthanum, uranium, cerium ka important ore hai, India-\nMadagascar-South Africa mein rich deposits hain. [Q49]\n49. Uranium Centres (Domiasiat-Meghalaya, Lambapur-AP, Rohail-Rajasthan, Gogi-\nKarnataka)\n●\nUranium centres match: Domiasiat — Meghalaya, Lambapur — Andhra Pradesh, Rohail — Rajasthan,\nGogi — Karnataka. [Q50]\n50. Jaduguda — Uranium Mine (Jharkhand)\n●\nJaduguda Mine Purbi Singhbhum district, Jharkhand mein Uranium ki mine hai. [Q51]\n51. Turamdih — Uranium Mining Near Jaduguda\n●\nTuramdih (Eastern Singhbhum, Jharkhand, Jaduguda se ~24km door) mein bhi Uranium ka khanan hota\nhai — Uranium Corporation of India Limited responsible hai. [Q52]\n52. Chhattisgarh — Bauxite/Dolomite/Iron Ore/Tin All Present\n●\nChhattisgarh mein Bauxite (Bastar/Bilaspur/Dantewada), Dolomite (Bilaspur/Janjgir/Bastar), Iron ore-\nHaematite (Bastar), Tin (Dantewada) sab naturally milte hain. [Q53]\n53. Palamu-Hazaribagh-Khetri-Keonjhar Match (Disputed)\n●\nSahi match: Palamu — Bauxite, Hazaribagh — Mica, Khetri — Copper, Keonjhar (Odisha) —\nManganese — options mein perfectly present nahi tha, isliye disputed hai. [Q54]\n54. Chota Nagpur Plateau — Rich in Minerals\n●\nChota Nagpur plateau various minerals mein samriddh hai — skilled labour/hydroelectricity/fertile soil se\nzyada. [Q55]"," 55. Kaimur Plateau — Limestone (Bihar)\n●\nKaimur plateau (Bihar ke Rohtas-Kaimur districts) Limestone ke liye famous hai — limestone+sandstone\nse bana hai, Banjari mein cement industry hai. [Q56]\n56. Coal-Copper-Manganese-Lignite Match (Giridih/Alwar/Dharwar/Jayamkondam)\n●\nMatch: Coal — Giridih (Jharkhand), Copper — Alwar (Rajasthan), Manganese — Dharwar\n(Karnataka), Lignite — Jayamkondam (Tamil Nadu). [Q57]\n57. Gurumahisani-Talcher-Jaduguda-Zavar Match (Iron/Coal/Uranium/Lead)\n●\nMatch: Gurumahisani — Iron ore, Talcher — Coal, Jaduguda — Uranium, Zavar — Lead. [Q58]\n58. Copper-Nickel-Tungsten 90% Sources (Rajasthan/Odisha/Karnataka)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik: Copper ka ~52.25% natural source Rajasthan mein hai\n(Jharkhand mein NAHI), Nickel ka ~93% Odisha mein hai (sahi), Tungsten ka ~41% Karnataka mein\nhai (Kerala mein NAHI) — sirf statement 2 (Nickel-Odisha) sahi hai. [Q59]\n EXAM TRAP — Copper ka 90% source Rajasthan mein hai (Jharkhand mein NAHI); Tungsten\n⚠️\nKarnataka mein hai (Kerala mein NAHI)\n59. Guru Mahisani-Talcher-Jaduguda-Zawar Match (Repeat, Zinc Version)\n●\nMatch: Guru Mahisani — Iron-ore, Talcher — Coal, Jaduguda — Uranium, Zawar — Zinc. [Q60]\n60. Sambhar Lake — Historical Salt Share (Disputed)\n●\nDiya gaya option 1992 ke context ke liye sahi tha (disputed question) — Sambhar Lake ka historical salt-\nproduction share alag time-periods mein alag raha hai. [Q61]\n61. India — 3rd Largest Salt Producer (Gujarat Leads)\n●\n2021-22 data ke mutabik India China+USA ke baad duniya ka 3rd largest salt producer hai (266 lakh\ntonnes) — Sea salt ~80% hai — Gujarat (86%) leading, Rajasthan (6%), Tamil Nadu (6%) dusre-\nteesre number par. [Q61]\n62. Bauxite-Lohardaga Match (Not Manganese-Bailadila)\n●\nSahi match: Bauxite — Lohardaga (Jharkhand) — 'Manganese-Bailadila', 'Iron-Koderma', 'Mica-\nTalcher' GALAT hain (Koderma mica, Talcher coal, Bailadila iron ke liye famous hain). [Q62]\n63. Mineral-Industry Match (Limestone-Cement, Bauxite-Aeroplane)\n●\nMatch: Limestone — Cement, Copper — Electrical goods, Bauxite — Aeroplane manufacturing,\nManganese — Steel. [Q63]\n64. Korba, Chhattisgarh — India's First Lithium Mine (2024)"," ●\nCentral Government ne August 2024 mein Katghora region, Korba district (Chhattisgarh) mein India ki\npehli lithium mine kholne ka decision liya — GSI ne 10-2000 PPM lithium concentration report ki ~250\nhectares area mein. [Q64]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0057","t":"26.i Thermal","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" THERMAL POWER — FULL MIND MAP\n⚡\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Singrauli NTPC — UP-MP Border, NOT Chhattisgarh\n2. Idukki — Hydro (Not Thermal), Match-Set Verification\n3. Thermal Plant-State Match (Ukai, Patratu, Pench, Dabhol)\n4. Uran — Gas-Based Plant in Maharashtra\n5. Coal — India's Largest Energy Source (52.89%)\n6. Thermal Power — Highest Share in Generation\n7. Energy Source Ranking (Disputed — No Fixed Sequence)\n8. 2019 Installed Capacity Order (Water > Gas > Nuclear > Diesel)\n9. Farakka — NTPC Superthermal Plant in West Bengal\n10. Map-Based — Srisailam is Hydro, Not Thermal\n11. Coal-Based Plant Match (Kahalgaon-Bihar, Khargone-MP)\n12. Neyveli — Tertiary Coal (Lignite), Tamil Nadu\n13. Ramagundam — Andhra Pradesh (Now Telangana)\n14. Obra — Russian Collaboration (UP)\n15. Power Station Match (Kothagudem, Raichur, Mettur, Wankbori)\n16. Paras — Maharashtra (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n17. Thermal Capacity Ranking (Maharashtra > Gujarat > UP > WB)\n18. Plant Load Factor (PLF) — 70-75% Average\n19. Bokaro Thermal Plant — Jharkhand\n20. Jajpur Steel Plant — Tata Steel (Not SAIL)\n21. Barh Super Thermal Power Station — Bihar\n22. Korba — Thermal (Not Wind) — Final Match Trap\n1. Singrauli NTPC — UP-MP Border, NOT Chhattisgarh\n●\nSingrauli mein NTPC unit 1977 mein establish hui thi, 1982 se operational hai — India ki 'oldest/first\nNTPC unit' hai — Chhattisgarh mein NAHI hai, balki Sidhi (MP) aur Sonbhadra (UP) districts mein\nfailii hai (2 states, 2 districts). 3 super thermal projects yahan hain. [Q1]\n2. Idukki — Hydro (Not Thermal), Match-Set Verification\n●\nIdukki (Kerala, Periyar river) hydroelectric project hai, thermal NAHI — Sabarigiri-Hydro, Ghatprabha-\nIrrigation, Ramganga-Multipurpose sahi pairs hain. [Q2]\n3. Thermal Plant-State Match (Ukai, Patratu, Pench, Dabhol)\n●\nMatch: Ukai — Gujarat, Patratu — Jharkhand, Pench — Madhya Pradesh, Dabhol — Maharashtra.\n[Q3]\n4. Uran — Gas-Based Plant in Maharashtra\n●\nUran (Uran Gas Turbine Power Station, Raigad district, Maharashtra) gas-based thermal power plant hai.\n[Q4]"," 5. Coal — India's Largest Energy Source (52.89%)\n●\n31 Dec 2024 tak Thermal energy ka sabse zyada share (52.89%, 244376.91 MW) hai — coal 212349.50\nMW, lignite 6620 MW, gas 24818.21 MW, diesel 589.20 MW contribute karta hai. [Q5]\n6. Thermal Power — Highest Share in Generation\n●\nPower generation mein Thermal power ka sabse zyada share hai — Atomic/Hydro se zyada. [Q6]\n7. Energy Source Ranking (Disputed — No Fixed Sequence)\n●\n31 Dec 2024 ke data ke mutabik: Thermal (244376.91 MW) > Wind (48163.16 MW) > Hydro (46968.17\nMW) > Nuclear (8180 MW) — diye gaye options mein koi bhi is sequence se match nahi karta, isliye ye\ndisputed question hai. [Q7]\n8. 2019 Installed Capacity Order (Water > Gas > Nuclear > Diesel)\n●\n30 Sept 2019 ke data ke mutabik descending order: Water > Natural Gas > Nuclear > Diesel. [Q8]\n9. Farakka — NTPC Superthermal Plant in West Bengal\n●\nNTPC ka superthermal plant West Bengal mein Farakka (Murshidabad district, Nabarun) mein hai —\ncoal-based plant hai. [Q9]\n10. Map-Based — Srisailam is Hydro, Not Thermal\n●\nMap-labeling: Ukai (Gujarat), Korba (Chhattisgarh), Obra (UP) — thermal power stations hain;\nSrisailam (Telangana) — hydroelectric hai, thermal NAHI. [Q10]\n11. Coal-Based Plant Match (Kahalgaon-Bihar, Khargone-MP)\n●\nMatch: Kahalgaon — Bihar, Khargone — Madhya Pradesh, Korba — Chhattisgarh, Kudgi —\nKarnataka. [Q11]\n12. Neyveli — Tertiary Coal (Lignite), Tamil Nadu\n●\nNeyveli thermal power plant (Tamil Nadu) Tertiary coal (Lignite) se feed hoti hai — South-East Asia ka\npehla lignite-fired thermal power station hai. [Q12]\n13. Ramagundam — Andhra Pradesh (Now Telangana)\n●\nRamagundam Super Thermal Power Station Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana) mein hai — capacity 2600\nMW. [Q13]\n14. Obra — Russian Collaboration (UP)\n●\nObra Thermal Power Station (Sonbhadra, UP) Russia ki madad se 1967 mein establish hui — Russian\nengineers involved the. [Q14]\n15. Power Station Match (Kothagudem, Raichur, Mettur, Wankbori)"," ●\nMatch: Kothagudem — Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana), Raichur — Karnataka, Mettur — Tamil\nNadu, Wankbori — Gujarat. [Q15]\n16. Paras — Maharashtra (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n●\nBadarpur-Delhi, Harduaganj-UP, Utaran-Gujarat sahi hain — 'Paras-Andhra Pradesh' GALAT hai (Paras\nasal mein Maharashtra mein hai). [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Paras — Maharashtra mein hai, Andhra Pradesh mein NAHI\n⚠️\n17. Thermal Capacity Ranking (Maharashtra > Gujarat > UP > WB)\n●\n31 Dec 2024 ki installed thermal capacity ranking: Maharashtra (28917.02 MW) > Gujarat (25145.93\nMW) > Uttar Pradesh (23673.02 MW) > West Bengal (8763.34 MW) — diye gaye options ke sath match\nnahi karta, isliye disputed question hai. [Q17]\n18. Plant Load Factor (PLF) — 70-75% Average\n●\nAll-India Thermal Plant Load Factor 70-75% ke beech vary karta hai — Central (~71%), State (~60%),\nPrivate IPP (~65%), Private UTL (~54%) sector-wise. [Q18]\n19. Bokaro Thermal Plant — Jharkhand\n●\nBokaro Thermal Power Station Jharkhand (Bokaro district) mein hai. [Q19]\n20. Jajpur Steel Plant — Tata Steel (Not SAIL)\n●\nKalinganagar Industrial Complex (Jajpur, Odisha) ka integrated steel plant Tata Steel ke tahat kaam karta\nhai — SAIL ke tahat NAHI (question ka official answer key mismatch hai, note isi wajah se diya gaya hai).\n[Q20]\n21. Barh Super Thermal Power Station — Bihar\n●\nBarh Super Thermal Power Station Patna district, Bihar mein hai — total approved capacity 3300 MW,\ninstalled 1320 MW. [Q21]\n22. Korba — Thermal (Not Wind) — Final Match Trap\n●\nPatratu-Thermal, Jhakri-Hydroelectric, Kalpakkam-Nuclear sahi hain — 'Korba-Wind' GALAT hai (Korba\nasal mein Thermal power station hai). [Q22]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0058","t":"26.ii Nuclear Energy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NUCLEAR ENERGY — FULL MIND MAP\n☢️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tarapur — India's First Nuclear Power Station (1969)\n2. Nuclear Share in Total Energy (~1.77-4%)\n3. Thorium — India Self-Sufficient (Not Uranium)\n4. Plant-State Match (Rawatbhata, Tarapur, Narora, Kakrapara)\n5. Kaiga — Karnataka (Not Gujarat/Rajasthan)\n6. Commissioning Year Match — All Disputed\n7. Nuclear Energy Potential (Assertion-Reason)\n8. Heavy Water Plant Match (Thal, Manuguru, Kakrapara, Kaiga)\n9. Ennore — Tamil Nadu (Not Meghalaya)\n10. Kudankulam — Tamil Nadu (Map-Based Question)\n11. Kudankulam — Russia's 6-Unit Agreement\n12. 25th Nuclear Plant — Rawatbhata (Rajasthan)\n13. 20th Nuclear Station — Kaiga (Karnataka)\n14. Heavy Water Plants — Kalpakkam Excluded\n15. Mithivirdi — USA Collaboration (Gujarat)\n16. Anushakti Vidyut Nigam — NPCIL+NTPC Joint Venture\n17. Haripur — West Bengal (Not Haryana)\n18. Kalapakkam — Tamil Nadu (Not Karnataka)\n19. Largest Installed Capacity — Tarapur (Historical Answer)\n1. Tarapur — India's First Nuclear Power Station (1969)\n●\nTarapur Atomic Power Station (TAPS, Boisar, Thane district, Maharashtra) India ka pehla nuclear power\nstation hai — 1969 mein commercial operation shuru hua. [Q1]\n2. Nuclear Share in Total Energy (~1.77-4%)\n●\n2006-07 mein nuclear energy ka share 3-4% ke beech tha — 31 Dec 2024 tak nuclear capacity 8180 MW\n(total capacity ka 1.77%) hai. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Thorium — India Self-Sufficient (Not Uranium)\n●\nIndia Thorium (monazite se extract hota hai) ki supply mein self-sufficient hai — Uranium ke liye import\npar nirbhar hai. [Q4]\n4. Plant-State Match (Rawatbhata, Tarapur, Narora, Kakrapara)\n●\nMatch: Rawatbhata (Kota ke paas) — Rajasthan, Tarapur — Maharashtra, Narora — Uttar Pradesh,\nKakrapara — Gujarat. [Q5]\n5. Kaiga — Karnataka (Not Gujarat/Rajasthan)\n●\nState-plant match: Gujarat — Kakrapara, Karnataka — Kaiga, Rajasthan — Rawatbhata, UP —\nNarora. [Q6]"," 6. Commissioning Year Match — All Disputed\n●\nActual commissioning years: Kota — 1973, Kakrapara — 1993, Kaiga — 2000, Kalpakkam — 1984 —\ndiye gaye question mein saare match galat the, isliye poora question disputed hai. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Commissioning years ka match galat diya gaya tha — Kota-1973, Kakrapara-1993,\n⚠️\nKaiga-2000, Kalpakkam-1984 hi sahi hain\n7. Nuclear Energy Potential (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nNuclear energy India ke liye futuristic demand ka promising source hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin nuclear\nminerals India mein 'ubiquitously' (har jagah) available NAHI hain (Reason galat) — Uranium kam\nquantity mein hai (import-dependent), Thorium abundant hai par sab jagah nahi milta. [Q8]\n8. Heavy Water Plant Match (Thal, Manuguru, Kakrapara, Kaiga)\n●\nMatch: Thal — Maharashtra, Manuguru — Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana), Kakrapara — Gujarat,\nKaiga — Karnataka. [Q9]\n9. Ennore — Tamil Nadu (Not Meghalaya)\n●\nDiye gaye set mein 'Ennore-Meghalaya' GALAT hai (Ennore asal mein Tamil Nadu mein hai) — baaki\noptions sahi hain. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Ennore — Tamil Nadu mein hai, Meghalaya mein NAHI\n⚠️\n10. Kudankulam — Tamil Nadu (Map-Based Question)\n●\nKudankulam Nuclear Power Plant (2×1000 MW) Kattabomman, Tirunelveli district, Tamil Nadu mein\nhai. [Q11, Q12]\n11. Kudankulam — Russia's 6-Unit Agreement\n●\n1988 mein Mikhail Gorbachev (Soviet head) ne 2 reactors ke liye Inter-Government Agreement sign kiya\ntha — baad mein 6 units tak expand hua. [Q13]\n12. 25th Nuclear Plant — Rawatbhata (Rajasthan)\n●\nIndia ka 25th Nuclear Plant Rawatbhata (Rajasthan) mein bana — construction July 2011 mein shuru hua.\n[Q14]\n13. 20th Nuclear Station — Kaiga (Karnataka)\n●\nIndia ka 20th nuclear power station Kaiga, Karnataka mein hai. [Q15]\n14. Heavy Water Plants — Kalpakkam Excluded\n●\nHeavy water plants: Hazira, Vadodara (Gujarat), Kota (Rajasthan), Manuguru (Telangana), Talcher\n(Odisha), Thal (Maharashtra), Tuticorin (TN) — Kalpakkam mein heavy-water plant NAHI hai\n(wahan nuclear POWER station hai). [Q16]\n15. Mithivirdi — USA Collaboration (Gujarat)"," ●\nMithivirdi Nuclear Plant (Talaja Taluka, Bhavnagar, Gujarat) USA ke collaboration se banega — 2008 ke\nIndo-US nuclear deal ka hissa. [Q17]\n16. Anushakti Vidyut Nigam — NPCIL+NTPC Joint Venture\n●\nAnushakti Vidyut Nigam Limited NPCIL (51%) aur NTPC (49%) ka joint venture hai — 27 January\n2011 ko incorporate hua. [Q18]\n17. Haripur — West Bengal (Not Haryana)\n●\nJaitpur-Maharashtra, Mithi Virdi-Gujarat, Kovvadda-Andhra Pradesh sahi hain — 'Haripur-Haryana'\nGALAT hai (Haripur asal mein West Bengal mein hai). [Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Haripur — West Bengal mein hai, Haryana mein NAHI (naam-samanta ka trap)\n⚠️\n18. Kalapakkam — Tamil Nadu (Not Karnataka)\n●\nKakrapar-Gujarat, Kudankulam-Tamil Nadu sahi hain — 'Kaiga-Uttar Pradesh' aur 'Kalapakkam-\nKarnataka' dono GALAT hain (Kaiga Karnataka mein hai, Kalapakkam Tamil Nadu mein hai) — is\nquestion mein 2 galat combinations the, isliye disputed hai. [Q20]\n19. Largest Installed Capacity — Tarapur (Historical Answer)\n●\nDiye gaye options mein installed capacity: Kakrapar 1840 MW, Kaiga 880 MW, Narora 440 MW,\nTarapur 1400 MW — historical context mein Tarapur ko sahi answer maana gaya (recent data mein\nKakrapar ki capacity zyada badh gayi hai). [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0059","t":"26.iii Hydroelectricity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" HYDROELECTRICITY — FULL MIND MAP\n💧\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Koyna — India's Largest Hydroelectric Plant\n2. Rana Pratap Sagar — Rawatbhata (Canada Cooperation)\n3. Jawahar Sagar — Chambal River, Rajasthan\n4. Hydroelectric Share in Total Power (~10%)\n1. Koyna — India's Largest Hydroelectric Plant\n●\nKoyna Hydroelectric Project (Maharashtra, Koyna river par) India ka sabse bada hydroelectric plant hai\n— Maharashtra State Electricity Board se operate hota hai. [Q1]\n2. Rana Pratap Sagar — Rawatbhata (Canada Cooperation)\n●\nRana Pratap Sagar Hydel Power Station Rawatbhata (Rajasthan), Chambal river par hai — Canada ke\ncooperation se establish hui thi. [Q2, Q4]\n3. Jawahar Sagar — Chambal River, Rajasthan\n●\nJawahar Sagar Hydroelectricity Project Chambal river (Rajasthan) par hai — Chambal Valley\nDevelopment Plan ka hissa hai. [Q3]\n4. Hydroelectric Share in Total Power (~10%)\n●\nJab question pucha gaya tha (2016-17), hydroelectric power ka total electricity mein 10.6% share tha — 31\nDec 2024 tak total installed capacity 462001.66 MW, jisme hydroelectric ka contribution 46968.17 MW\nhai. [Q5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0060","t":"26.iv Energy Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ENERGY MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🔋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Site-Energy Match (Pavagada-Solar, Muppandal-Wind)\n2. Rajasthan — Highest Solar Energy Potential\n3. Power Plant Match (Chamera, Gwal Pahari, Kudankulam, Patratu)\n4. Satara — Wind Energy (Chalkewadi Project)\n5. Wind Power Potential — Tamil Nadu & Gujarat\n6. Gujarat — #1 in Wind Power Generation\n7. Non-Conventional Energy — Over 1% Contribution\n8. Muppandal — Asia's Biggest Wind Project (150 MW)\n9. Khambhat Coast — Largest Tidal Energy Area\n10. Tidal Energy Potential Sites (Khambhat, Kutch, Sundarbans)\n11. NHPC — Hydroelectric Power Corporation\n12. Gujarat — #1 Installed Electricity Capacity\n13. 1994 Per Capita Energy Consumption — 244 kg Oil Equivalent\n14. Rampura (UP) — India's First Solar-Powered Village\n15. SEB Financial Sickness — Multiple Causes\n16. Manikaran — Geothermal Plant (Himachal Pradesh)\n17. Jwalamukhi — Himachal Pradesh (Not J&K)\n18. Biogas — Non-Commercial Energy Source\n19. Renewable Sources — Water, Sun, Earth, Wind\n20. Urja Ganga — Gas Pipeline (Eastern India, Not Iran)\n21. Diu — First 100% Solar UT\n22. Rajasthan — Leading Solar Energy Producer\n23. Petroleum — Non-Renewable Fossil Fuel\n1. Site-Energy Match (Pavagada-Solar, Muppandal-Wind)\n●\nMatch: Pavagada (Karnataka) — Solar, Tattapani (Chhattisgarh) — Geothermal, Muppandal (Tamil\nNadu) — Wind, Kakrapar (Gujarat) — Atomic. [Q1]\n2. Rajasthan — Highest Solar Energy Potential\n●\nMinistry of New and Renewable Energy ke mutabik Rajasthan mein solar energy development ki sabse\nzyada potential hai (31 March 2024 tak). [Q2]\n3. Power Plant Match (Chamera, Gwal Pahari, Kudankulam, Patratu)\n●\nMatch: Chamera — Hydro (Ravi river, Himachal Pradesh), Gwal Pahari — Solar (Gurugram,\nHaryana), Kudankulam — Atomic (Tamil Nadu), Patratu — Thermal (Ramgarh, Jharkhand). [Q3]\n4. Satara — Wind Energy (Chalkewadi Project)\n●\nSatara (Maharashtra) ka Chalkewadi wind energy project electricity generation ke liye famous hai. [Q4]\n5. Wind Power Potential — Tamil Nadu & Gujarat"," ●\nMinistry of New and Renewable Energy ke mutabik wind power development ki sabse zyada potential\nGujarat, Rajasthan aur Tamil Nadu mein hai — combined highest do options 'Tamil Nadu aur Gujarat'\nhain. [Q5]\n6. Gujarat — #1 in Wind Power Generation\n●\n31 March 2024 tak wind power generation capacity mein Gujarat pehle number par hai, Tamil Nadu\ndusre number par. [Q6]\n7. Non-Conventional Energy — Over 1% Contribution\n●\nSahi statement: Industry India ka major energy-consuming sector hai — 'non-conventional sources 1%\nse kam contribute karte hain' GALAT hai (ab 1% se zyada hai). [Q7]\n8. Muppandal — Asia's Biggest Wind Project (150 MW)\n●\nJab question pucha gaya tha, Asia ka sabse bada wind energy project Muppandal village (150 MW), Tamil\nNadu mein tha. [Q8]\n9. Khambhat Coast — Largest Tidal Energy Area\n●\nIndia ka sabse bada tidal energy producing area Khambhat Coast (Gulf of Cambay) hai. [Q9]\n10. Tidal Energy Potential Sites (Khambhat, Kutch, Sundarbans)\n●\nTidal energy ke 3 most-potential locations: Gulf of Cambay/Khambhat, Gulf of Kutch (west coast),\nGanges Delta/Sundarbans (east coast) — Bhavnagar, Khambhat ki khaadi mein hi sthit hai. [Q10, Q11]\n11. NHPC — Hydroelectric Power Corporation\n●\nNHPC (National Hydroelectric Power Corporation, 1975 incorporate hui) electricity generation se related\nhai — baad mein geothermal, tidal, wind sources bhi include kiye. [Q12]\n12. Gujarat — #1 Installed Electricity Capacity\n●\n31 Dec 2024 tak gross electricity installed capacity mein Gujarat pehle number par hai. [Q13]\n13. 1994 Per Capita Energy Consumption — 244 kg Oil Equivalent\n●\n1994 mein India ki per capita energy consumption 244 kg oil equivalent thi — world standard (1471 kg) se\nbahut kam. [Q14]\n14. Rampura (UP) — India's First Solar-Powered Village\n●\nRampura, Uttar Pradesh mein hai — apna solar power plant lagane wala India ka pehla gaon bana. [Q15]\n15. SEB Financial Sickness — Multiple Causes\n●\nState Electricity Boards (SEBs) ki financial sickness ke sab 4 reasons sahi hain: agriculture/domestic\nconsumers ko cost se kam par bijli bechna, high transmission-distribution losses, commercial autonomy\nki kami, social subsidy policies. [Q16]"," 16. Manikaran — Geothermal Plant (Himachal Pradesh)\n●\nManikaran geothermal power plant Parvati Valley, Kullu district, Himachal Pradesh mein hai. [Q17]\n17. Jwalamukhi — Himachal Pradesh (Not J&K)\n●\nManikaran-HP, Anhoni-MP, Tapta Pani-Odisha sahi hain — 'Jwalamukhi-Jammu&Kashmir' GALAT hai\n(Jwalamukhi asal mein Himachal Pradesh ke Kangra district mein hai). [Q18]\n EXAM TRAP — Jwalamukhi — Himachal Pradesh mein hai, J&K mein NAHI\n⚠️\n18. Biogas — Non-Commercial Energy Source\n●\nCommercial energy sources: Petroleum, Atomic Energy, Natural Gas, Coal — Biogas non-commercial\n(renewable) source hai. [Q19]\n19. Renewable Sources — Water, Sun, Earth, Wind\n●\nSab renewable sources hain: Water, Sun (solar), Earth (geothermal), Wind — koi bhi option akela sahi\nnahi tha, isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q20]\n20. Urja Ganga — Gas Pipeline (Eastern India, Not Iran)\n●\nUrja Ganga project gas pipeline hai, October 2016 mein launch hua (PM Modi ne Varanasi mein\nfoundation rakha) — Eastern India ko connect karta hai, Iran-India se NAHI. [Q21]\n21. Diu — First 100% Solar UT\n●\nDiu India ka pehla Union Territory hai jo 100% solar energy par chalta hai (~40 sq km area) — 26 Jan\n2020 se Daman-Diu aur Dadra-Nagar Haveli merge hue. [Q22]\n22. Rajasthan — Leading Solar Energy Producer\n●\n31 March 2024 tak solar power production mein Rajasthan sabse aage hai. [Q23]\n23. Petroleum — Non-Renewable Fossil Fuel\n●\nPetroleum (crude oil) ek non-renewable fossil fuel hai — coal aur natural gas ki tarah ancient marine\norganisms se bana hai. [Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0061","t":"27.i Iron and Steel Industry","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" IRON AND STEEL INDUSTRY — FULL MIND\n🏗️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Stainless Steel — Iron + Chromium (+ Nickel)\n2. Western Coast Plants — Goa/MP High-Grade Ore Access\n3. Coking Coal — Imported (Mainly from Australia)\n4. VSL Bhadravati — Only Plant Outside Coal Area\n5. Jamshedpur — Midway Between Iron Ore & Coal\n6. TISCO — Tatanagar (Jamshedpur)\n7. Jamshedpur — 'Pittsburgh of India'\n8. Rourkela — German Collaboration (Not Soviet)\n9. Bhilai — Russia Collaboration\n10. Bokaro — Russia Collaboration (4th Public Sector Plant)\n11. Iron & Steel — Maximum Foreign Exchange Earner\n12. Bhilai State Match Trap (Chhattisgarh, Not MP)\n13. Rourkela — Iron Ore from Keonjhar\n14. Second Five-Year-Plan Plants (Bhilai, Durgapur, Rourkela)\n15. Bhadravati — Far from Coalfields\n16. China — World's Top Steel Producer (India 2nd)\n1. Stainless Steel — Iron + Chromium (+ Nickel)\n●\nStainless steel banane ke liye Chromium aur Nickel (main alloy: Iron + Chromium) use hote hain —\nmolybdenum, silicon, aluminium, carbon bhi contribute karte hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. Western Coast Plants — Goa/MP High-Grade Ore Access\n●\nWestern coast par iron-steel plants plan hone ka reason: Goa aur MP ke kuch hisso mein high-grade iron\nore deposits, aur wahan se steel export karna aasan hai. [Q4]\n3. Coking Coal — Imported (Mainly from Australia)\n●\nSteel production ke liye coking coal import karna padta hai (mainly Australia se) — iron ore,\nmanganese, dolomite, rock phosphate, chromium bhi chahiye hote hain. [Q5]\n4. VSL Bhadravati — Only Plant Outside Coal Area\n●\nVSL, Bhadravati ekmatra iron-steel plant hai jo coal-producing area se bahar hai — pehle charcoal\n(firewood se) use hota tha, Mahatma Gandhi Hydel Power Station ke baad electric furnaces mein badla. [Q6]\n5. Jamshedpur — Midway Between Iron Ore & Coal\n●\nJamshedpur na iron-ore area par hai na coalfield par, balki dono ke beech midway par hai. [Q7]\n6. TISCO — Tatanagar (Jamshedpur)"," ●\nTISCO (Tata Iron & Steel Company, 1907 established) Tatanagar (Jamshedpur) ke paas hai. [Q8]\n7. Jamshedpur — 'Pittsburgh of India'\n●\nJamshedpur (Jharkhand) ko 'Pittsburgh of India' kehte hain — iron-steel industries ke liye famous. [Q9]\n8. Rourkela — German Collaboration (Not Soviet)\n●\nRourkela Steel Plant Germany (Krupps aur Demag companies) ke collaboration se bana tha, Soviet\nUnion se NAHI — India ka pehla public-sector integrated steel plant hai. Salem Steel Plant stainless steel ka\npremier producer hai, Maharashtra Elektrosmelt SAIL ki subsidiary hai, Visakhapatnam Steel Plant Rashtriya\nIspat Nigam ki unit hai — sab sahi hain. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Rourkela Steel Plant — Germany ke saath bana tha, Soviet Union ke saath NAHI\n⚠️\n9. Bhilai — Russia Collaboration\n●\nBhilai Steel Plant Bharat sarkar aur Russia ka collaborative project hai (Durg district, Chhattisgarh,\n1959 commissioned) — Dalli Rajhara Iron Ore Complex, Korba-Kargali coal mines se supply. [Q11]\n10. Bokaro — Russia Collaboration (4th Public Sector Plant)\n●\nBokaro Steel Plant Russia (Soviet) ki madad se bana — India ka 4th public sector steel plant, 1965 mein\nshuru, 'country's first Swadeshi Steel Plant' bhi kehlata hai. [Q12]\n11. Iron & Steel — Maximum Foreign Exchange Earner\n●\nJab question pucha gaya tha, Iron and Steel industry India ke liye sabse zyada foreign exchange kamati\nthi (Tea, Jute, Sugar se zyada). [Q13]\n12. Bhilai State Match Trap (Chhattisgarh, Not MP)\n●\n'Bhilai-Madhya Pradesh' GALAT hai — Bhilai actually Chhattisgarh mein hai (Durgapur-WB,\nJamshedpur-Jharkhand, Rourkela-Odisha sahi hain). [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP — Bhilai — Chhattisgarh mein hai, Madhya Pradesh mein NAHI (state-reorganisation ke\n⚠️\nbaad)\n13. Rourkela — Iron Ore from Keonjhar\n●\nRourkela Steel Plant ko iron ore Keonjhar (Mayurbhanj, Sundergarh se bhi) se milta hai — coal\nBokaro/Jharia/Talchar se, limestone-dolomite Birmitrapur se, manganese Noamundi se. [Q15]\n14. Second Five-Year-Plan Plants (Bhilai, Durgapur, Rourkela)\n●\n2nd Five Year Plan mein banaye gaye plants: Rourkela (Germany), Bhilai (Russia), Durgapur (UK) —\nteeno independence ke baad establish hue. [Q16]\n15. Bhadravati — Far from Coalfields\n●\nBokaro, Durgapur, Kulti-Asansol sab coal reserves ke paas hain — Bhadravati coal reserves se door hai.\n[Q17, Q18]"," 16. China — World's Top Steel Producer (India 2nd)\n●\nWorld Steel Association (Dec 2024) ke mutabik China crude steel production mein pehle number par hai,\nIndia dusre number par. [Q19]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0062","t":"27.ii Aluminium Industry","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ALUMINIUM INDUSTRY — FULL MIND MAP\n🏭\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Korba (Chhattisgarh) — BALCO Aluminium Hub\n2. TELCO — Not an Aluminium Company\n3. Company-Location Match (BALCO, HINDALCO, NALCO, HCL)\n4. MALCO — Mettur (Not Chennai)\n5. INDAL — 3 Smelting Units (Kerala, Odisha, Karnataka)\n6. Plant-State Match Set (Alupuram, Angul, Belgaum, Korba)\n7. Khetri — Copper Industry (Not Aluminium)\n1. Korba (Chhattisgarh) — BALCO Aluminium Hub\n●\nKorba (Chhattisgarh) Aluminium industry ke liye important hai — BALCO (Bharat Aluminium\nCompany Ltd.) main township se 10km door hai. [Q1]\n2. TELCO — Not an Aluminium Company\n●\nTELCO (Tata Engineering and Locomotive Company, ab Tata Motors) aluminium NAHI banati — ye\nautomotive/commercial-vehicle company hai. BALCO, NALCO, HINDALCO sab aluminium companies\nhain. [Q2]\n3. Company-Location Match (BALCO, HINDALCO, NALCO, HCL)\n●\nSahi match: BALCO — Korba (Chhattisgarh), HINDALCO — Pipari/Renukoot (Sonbhadra, UP),\nNALCO — Bhubaneswar (Odisha), HCL (Hindustan Copper Ltd) — Khetri (Rajasthan). [Q3]\n4. MALCO — Mettur (Not Chennai)\n●\nINDAL-Hirakud, BALCO-Korba, HINDALCO-Renukoot sahi hain — MALCO (Madras Aluminium\nCompany) Mettur (Salem district, Tamil Nadu) mein hai, Chennai mein NAHI. [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP — MALCO — Mettur (Salem, Tamil Nadu) mein hai, Chennai mein NAHI\n⚠️\n5. INDAL — 3 Smelting Units (Kerala, Odisha, Karnataka)\n●\nINDAL (Indian Aluminium Company) ki 3 smelting units: Alupuram (Kerala), Hirakud (Odisha),\nBelgaum (Karnataka). BALCO 1965 mein Korba mein PSU ke roop mein incorporate hua. HINDALCO\nAditya Birla Group ki flagship company hai (Renukoot). NALCO ki units Angul aur Damanjodi (Koraput),\nOdisha mein hain. [Q5]\n6. Plant-State Match Set (Alupuram, Angul, Belgaum, Korba)\n●\nPlant-state match: Alupuram — Kerala, Angul — Odisha, Belgaum — Karnataka, Korba —\nChhattisgarh. [Q6]"," 7. Khetri — Copper Industry (Not Aluminium)\n●\nKhetri (Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan) copper industry ke liye famous hai (Hindustan Copper Limited) —\nTarapur nuclear power ke liye, Titagarh paper industry ke liye, Ranchi engineering industry ke liye\nfamous hai. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0063","t":"27.iii Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n📋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Mineral Agency HQ Match (ONGC-Delhi, MECL-Nagpur, NMDC-Hyderabad, NALCO-Bhubaneswar)\n2. First Synthetic Rubber Plant — Panipat, Haryana\n3. Industry Centre Match (Kankinara-Jute, Virudhnagar-Cotton, Channapatna-Silk, Bhadohi-Carpet)\n4. Industry Match (Heavy Engineering-Ranchi, Machinery-Pinjore, Aluminium-Renukoot, Fertilizer-Sindri)\n5. Rock Phosphate — Used in Fertilizer Industry\n6. Petronet LNG, Dredging Corp, Narwapahar Mine Facts\n7. Handicraft Centre Match (Mon-Nagaland, Nalbari-Assam, Pasighat-Arunachal, Tura-Meghalaya)\n8. Location-News Match (Kakinada-Biodiesel, Dundigal-IAF Academy, Margao-Skybus, Bhadrachalam-ITC)\n9. Industry Centre Match (Aonla-Fertilizers, Modinagar-Rubber, Barabanki-Polyfibres, Kanpur-Explosive)\n10. Cotton Textile — India's Ancient Industry\n11. Coimbatore — Largest Number of Cotton Mills in Tamil Nadu\n12. MP Craft Match (Zari Batua-Bhopal, Bhairavgarh-Ujjain, Bagh-Dhar, Chanderi-Ashok Nagar)\n13. Masuria Sari — Kota, Rajasthan\n14. Industry Mismatch — Bharat Electronics Ltd is NOT in Noida\n15. Chunar — Cement Industry\n16. India — 2nd in Global Cement Production (2022)\n17. Rajasthan — India's Top Cement-Producing State\n18. Limestone — Cement's Principal Raw Material\n19. Dalmianagar, Bihar — Famous for Cement\n20. Bhopal — Pesticide Industry Hub\n21. Place-Industry Match (Vizag-Shipbuilding, Muri-Aluminium, Gurgaon-Auto, Panki-Fertilizer)\n22. Sugar Industry Not in Silvassa (Wrong-Pair)\n23. Rubber Industry — Panjim, Goa\n24. Pipri — Hydroelectricity (Not Pesticides)\n25. First Fertilizer Plant — Disputed (Ranipet 1906 vs Sindri)\n26. Sindri — India's First Fertilizer Plant (Not Copper)\n27. Biggest Cooperative-Sector Fertilizer Factory — Phulpur, UP\n28. Industry Match (Brajraj Nagar-Paper, Kaimur-Cement, Haldia-Petrochemical, Phulpur-Fertilizer)\n29. India's Largest Petrochemical Factory — Gujarat (Jamnagar)\n30. Steel Authority of India — Established 1973 (Disputed Options)\n31. Paper Industry Match (Amlai-MP, Ballarpur-Maharashtra, Brajrajnagar-Odisha, Rajahmundry-AP)\n32. Maximum Paper Mills — Uttar Pradesh (Given Options); Gujarat (Overall)\n33. Newsprint Paper Industry — Nepanagar, MP\n34. Mumbai — India's Largest Cotton Textile Centre (Not Ahmedabad)\n35. Tamil Nadu Cotton Yarn — Skilled Labour (Not Black Soil)\n36. Cotton Spread Despite Limited Growing Areas (Weight-Stable Raw Material)\n37. First Cotton Textile Factory (1818) — Fort Gloster, West Bengal\n38. First Cotton Mill of India — Calcutta\n39. Industry-Centre Match (Silk-Mysore, Petrochemical-Jawahar Nagar, Fertilizer-Talcher)\n40. PSU-Location Match (SAIL-Delhi, Hindustan Zinc-Udaipur, HEC-Ranchi)\n41. Nagapattinam — Tamil Nadu (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n42. Dharmapuri — Tamil Nadu (Not Odisha)\n43. Industry Location Match (Atlas Cycle-Sonipat, BEML-Bangalore, IFFCO-Kalol, NALCO-Bhubaneswar)\n44. Diamond Park — Diamond/Jewellery Manufacturing-Export Zone\n45. Person-Field Match (B.V. Rao-Poultry, C.K. Prahlad-Management, John Kurien-Fisheries)"," 46. Person-Organisation Match (Historical — BEML, BHEL, Maruti CEOs)\n47. Executive-Company Match (Historical — NTPC, TCS, Wipro)\n48. Distinguished Women Match (Amrita Patel-NDDB, Historical Update)\n49. Ludhiana — Punjab's Hosiery Industry Hub\n50. Thermal Power — India's Maximum Water Consumer Industry\n51. Industry-Place Match (Paper-Titagarh, Cement-Lakheri, Steel-Bhilai, Oil-Ambala Mukul)\n52. Industry-Centre Match (Aluminium-JK Nagar, Copper-Malanjkhand, Zinc-Tundoo, Jute-Bhatpara)\n53. Rajasthan Industry Match (Fertilizer-Sriganganagar, Glass-Jaipur, Cement-Udaipur, Silk-Kota)\n54. Place-Industry Match (Bengaluru-Aircraft, Korba-Aluminium, Jamshedpur-Steel, Malanjkhand-Copper)\n55. Industry Centre Match Repeat (Kakinada-Jute, Virudhnagar-Cotton, Channapatna-Silk, Bhadohi-Carpet)\n56. Traditional Saree Towns — Chanderi & Kancheepuram (Not Bhadrachalam/Karnal)\n57. GI Tag Status — Banarasi Saree & Tirupati Laddu (Not Rajasthani Daal-Bati)\n58. Sivakasi — NOT in Chhotanagpur Region (Actually Madurai-Coimbatore-Bengaluru)\n59. Shivkashi — Fireworks/Matchbox Hub, 'Little Japan'\n60. Pithampur, MP — Automobile Industry Hub\n61. JSMDC Granite Polishing — Tupudana, Ranchi\n62. Nepanagar — Newsprint Paper (Repeat)\n63. Caustic Soda — NOT a Fertilizer Raw Material\n64. Rajasthan's Sole-Producer Minerals (Lead-Zinc, Selenite, Wollastonite)\n65. Diesel Locomotive Works, Varanasi — Now Makes Electric Engines\n66. Non-Coal Mine Auctioning — State Government Power (2015 Law)\n67. Motihari-Amlekhganj Cross-Border Oil Pipeline (Sept 2019)\n68. Sugar Industry — Maharashtra #1, UP #2 (Current)\n1. Mineral Agency HQ Match (ONGC-Delhi, MECL-Nagpur, NMDC-Hyderabad, NALCO-\nBhubaneswar)\n●\nMatch: ONGC — New Delhi, Mineral Exploration Corporation Ltd (MECL) — Nagpur, National\nMineral Development Corporation (NMDC) — Hyderabad, National Aluminium Company Limited\n(NALCO) — Bhubaneswar. [Q1]\n2. First Synthetic Rubber Plant — Panipat, Haryana\n●\nIndia ka pehla synthetic rubber plant Panipat, Haryana mein 'Indian Synthetic Rubber Private Limited'\nne banaya. [Q2]\n3. Industry Centre Match (Kankinara-Jute, Virudhnagar-Cotton, Channapatna-Silk,\nBhadohi-Carpet)\n●\nMatch: Kankinara — Jute, Virudhnagar — Cotton Textile, Channapatna — Silk, Bhadohi — Carpet.\n[Q3]\n4. Industry Match (Heavy Engineering-Ranchi, Machinery-Pinjore, Aluminium-Renukoot,\nFertilizer-Sindri)\n●\nMatch: Heavy Engineering Industries — Ranchi, Machinery Instruments — Pinjore, Aluminium —\nRenukoot, Fertilizers — Sindri. [Q4]\n5. Rock Phosphate — Used in Fertilizer Industry\n●\nRock phosphate fertilizer industry mein use hota hai (SSP, DAP jaise phosphate fertilizers banane ke\nliye) — phosphorus ka major source hai. [Q5]"," 6. Petronet LNG, Dredging Corp, Narwapahar Mine Facts\n●\nSahi statements: Dredging Corporation of India ka HQ Visakhapatnam mein hai, Narwapahar Mine\n(Jharkhand, trackless uranium mine) Uranium Corporation of India Limited operate karti hai —\n'Petronet LNG Mangalore mein naya terminal bana raha hai' GALAT hai (Dahej-Gujarat pehla,\nKochi-Kerala dusra terminal hai). [Q6]\n7. Handicraft Centre Match (Mon-Nagaland, Nalbari-Assam, Pasighat-Arunachal, Tura-\nMeghalaya)\n●\nMatch: Mon — Nagaland, Nalbari — Assam, Pasighat — Arunachal Pradesh, Tura — Meghalaya. [Q7]\n8. Location-News Match (Kakinada-Biodiesel, Dundigal-IAF Academy, Margao-Skybus,\nBhadrachalam-ITC)\n●\nMatch: Kakinada — Bio-diesel plant, Dundigal (Hyderabad) — Indian Air Force Academy, Margao\n(Goa) — Skybus Metro rail test-run, Bhadrachalam (Telangana) — ITC paper board unit. [Q8]\n9. Industry Centre Match (Aonla-Fertilizers, Modinagar-Rubber, Barabanki-Polyfibres,\nKanpur-Explosive)\n●\nMatch: Aonla — Fertilizers, Modinagar — Rubber, Barabanki — Polyfibres, Kanpur — Explosive.\n[Q9]\n10. Cotton Textile — India's Ancient Industry\n●\nCotton Textile industry India ka ek prachin (ancient) udyog hai — Jute, Tea, Sugar se zyada purana. [Q10]\n11. Coimbatore — Largest Number of Cotton Mills in Tamil Nadu\n●\nTamil Nadu mein Coimbatore mein sabse zyada cotton mills hain (~919). [Q11]\n12. MP Craft Match (Zari Batua-Bhopal, Bhairavgarh-Ujjain, Bagh-Dhar, Chanderi-Ashok\nNagar)\n●\nMatch: Zari Batua — Bhopal, Bhairavgarh Prints — Ujjain, Handicrafts of Bagh — Dhar, Sarees of\nChanderi — Ashok Nagar. [Q12]\n13. Masuria Sari — Kota, Rajasthan\n●\nMasuria Sari Kota, Rajasthan se related hai — Badla-Jaipur, Namda-Jodhpur, Marble Carving-Tonk pairs\nGALAT hain. [Q13]\n14. Industry Mismatch — Bharat Electronics Ltd is NOT in Noida\n●\nDiesel Locomotive Works-Varanasi, Indian Telephone Industries-Raebareli, Oil Refinery-Mathura sahi hain\n— 'Bharat Electronics Ltd-Noida' GALAT hai (BEL ki units Bengaluru, Chennai, Panchkula,\nKotdwara, Ghaziabad, Pune, Hyderabad, Machilipatnam, Navi Mumbai mein hain — Noida mein\nNAHI). [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP — Bharat Electronics Ltd (BEL) — Noida mein unit NAHI hai\n⚠️"," 15. Chunar — Cement Industry\n●\nChunar cement industry ke liye prasiddh hai. [Q15]\n16. India — 2nd in Global Cement Production (2022)\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik India global cement production mein dusre number par hai\n(2021-22 mein 360.19 million tonnes) — China #1 hai. [Q16]\n17. Rajasthan — India's Top Cement-Producing State\n●\nIndian Minerals Yearbook 2022 ke mutabik Rajasthan India ka top cement-producing state hai. [Q17]\n18. Limestone — Cement's Principal Raw Material\n●\nCement industry limestone par mukhya roop se depend karta hai — jahan limestone prachur hai wahan\ncement industry located hoti hai. [Q18, Q19]\n19. Dalmianagar, Bihar — Famous for Cement\n●\nDalmianagar (India ke sabse purane-bade industrial towns mein se ek) cement industry ke liye famous hai.\n[Q20]\n20. Bhopal — Pesticide Industry Hub\n●\nBhopal (Madhya Pradesh) pesticide industry ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q21]\n21. Place-Industry Match (Vizag-Shipbuilding, Muri-Aluminium, Gurgaon-Auto, Panki-\nFertilizer)\n●\nMatch: Vishakhapatnam — Ship-building, Muri — Aluminium, Gurgaon — Automobile, Panki —\nFertilizer. [Q22]\n22. Sugar Industry Not in Silvassa (Wrong-Pair)\n●\nCement-Porbandar, Petro-Nagothane, Iron&Steel-Rourkela sahi hain — 'Sugar-Silvassa' GALAT hai\n(Silvassa sugar industry ka center NAHI hai). [Q23]\n23. Rubber Industry — Panjim, Goa\n●\nRubber industry Panjim (Goa) mein located hai. [Q24]\n24. Pipri — Hydroelectricity (Not Pesticides)\n●\nRamagundam-Fertilizer, Chittaranjan-Locomotive, Korba-Aluminium sahi hain — 'Pipri-Pesticides'\nGALAT hai (Pipri, UP, hydroelectricity ke liye famous hai). [Q25]\n EXAM TRAP — Pipri — Hydroelectricity ke liye famous hai, Pesticides ke liye NAHI\n⚠️\n25. First Fertilizer Plant — Disputed (Ranipet 1906 vs Sindri)"," ●\nFirst fertilizer production unit 1906 mein Ranipet, Tamil Nadu mein establish hui thi — diye gaye options\n(Nangal/Sindri/Alwaye/Trombay) mein se koi match nahi karta, isliye disputed hai. [Q26]\n26. Sindri — India's First Fertilizer Plant (Not Copper)\n●\nAonla-Fertilizer, Nepanagar-Paper, Narora-Atomic Power sahi hain — 'Sindri-Copper' GALAT hai\n(Sindri, undivided Bihar/ab Jharkhand, India ka pehla fertilizer plant tha). [Q27]\n EXAM TRAP — Sindri — India ka pehla fertilizer plant hai, Copper industry se NAHI\n⚠️\n27. Biggest Cooperative-Sector Fertilizer Factory — Phulpur, UP\n●\nCooperative sector mein India ka sabse bada fertilizer factory Phulpur (Prayagraj, UP) mein hai. [Q28]\n28. Industry Match (Brajraj Nagar-Paper, Kaimur-Cement, Haldia-Petrochemical, Phulpur-\nFertilizer)\n●\nMatch: Brajraj Nagar (Odisha) — Paper, Kaimur — Cement, Haldia (WB) — Petrochemical, Phulpur\n(UP) — Fertilizers. [Q29]\n29. India's Largest Petrochemical Factory — Gujarat (Jamnagar)\n●\nIndia ka sabse bada petrochemical factory Gujarat mein hai — sabse bada petrochemical production\ncentre Jamnagar mein hai. [Q30, Q31]\n30. Steel Authority of India — Established 1973 (Disputed Options)\n●\n2nd Five Year Plan mein foreign collaboration se Rourkela (Odisha), Bhilai (Chhattisgarh), Durgapur (WB)\nplants bane — Hindustan Steel Limited ke control mein the — SAIL (Steel Authority of India Limited)\ninko manage karne ke liye 1973 mein establish hui — diye gaye options mein 1973 nahi tha, isliye\ndisputed hai. [Q32]\n31. Paper Industry Match (Amlai-MP, Ballarpur-Maharashtra, Brajrajnagar-Odisha,\nRajahmundry-AP)\n●\nMatch: Amlai — Madhya Pradesh, Ballarpur — Maharashtra, Brajrajnagar — Odisha, Rajahmundry\n— Andhra Pradesh. [Q33]\n32. Maximum Paper Mills — Uttar Pradesh (Given Options); Gujarat (Overall)\n●\nDiye gaye options mein UP mein sabse zyada paper mills hain — overall India mein Gujarat ke paas\nsabse zyada hain (Indian Pulp & Paper Technical Association ke mutabik). [Q34]\n33. Newsprint Paper Industry — Nepanagar, MP\n●\nNewsprint paper industry Nepanagar (Burhanpur district, Madhya Pradesh) mein hai. [Q35]\n34. Mumbai — India's Largest Cotton Textile Centre (Not Ahmedabad)"," ●\n'Ahmedabad India ka sabse bada cotton textile centre hai' GALAT statement hai — Mumbai asal mein sabse\nbada centre hai — lekin 'Ahmedabad major cotton-growing region mein hai, raw material ki koi\nproblem nahi' sahi hai. [Q36]\n EXAM TRAP — Mumbai India ka largest cotton textile centre hai, Ahmedabad NAHI\n⚠️\n35. Tamil Nadu Cotton Yarn — Skilled Labour (Not Black Soil)\n●\nTamil Nadu mill-made cotton yarn ka leading producer hai — skilled labour, spinning mills ki abundance,\nsasti hydroelectricity iske reasons hain — black cotton soil TN ka predominant soil type NAHI hai.\n[Q37]\n36. Cotton Spread Despite Limited Growing Areas (Weight-Stable Raw Material)\n●\nCotton textile industry poore India mein failli hai, halaanki cotton sirf kuch hisso mein ugti hai (Assertion\nsahi) — kyunki cotton ek 'pure raw material' hai, manufacturing mein weight kam nahi hota (Reason\nbhi sahi hai aur sahi explanation hai) — mukhya centres: Ahmedabad, Solapur, Nagpur, Coimbatore,\nIndore. [Q38]\n37. First Cotton Textile Factory (1818) — Fort Gloster, West Bengal\n●\nIndia ki pehli cotton mill 1818 mein Fort Gloster (Kolkata ke paas, West Bengal) mein establish hui thi\n— lekin commercially fail ho gayi thi. [Q39]\n38. First Cotton Mill of India — Calcutta\n●\nIndia ki pehli cotton mill Calcutta (Kolkata) mein establish hui thi — 1818 mein Fort Gloster. [Q40]\n39. Industry-Centre Match (Silk-Mysore, Petrochemical-Jawahar Nagar, Fertilizer-Talcher)\n●\nMatch: Silk textiles — Mysore (Karnataka), Petrochemicals — Jawahar Nagar (Gujarat), Fertilizers —\nTalcher (Odisha), Pharmaceuticals — Rishikesh (Uttarakhand). [Q41]\n40. PSU-Location Match (SAIL-Delhi, Hindustan Zinc-Udaipur, HEC-Ranchi)\n●\nMatch: Steel Authority of India Limited — Delhi, Hindustan Zinc Limited — Udaipur, Heavy\nEngineering Corporation Limited — Ranchi, Instrumentation Limited — Kota. [Q42]\n41. Nagapattinam — Tamil Nadu (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n●\nKoyali-Gujarat, Numaligarh-Assam, Manali-Tamil Nadu sahi hain — 'Nagapattinam-Andhra Pradesh'\nGALAT hai (Nagapattinam Tamil Nadu mein hai). [Q43]\n EXAM TRAP — Nagapattinam — Tamil Nadu mein hai, Andhra Pradesh mein NAHI\n⚠️\n42. Dharmapuri — Tamil Nadu (Not Odisha)\n●\nMuri-Jharkhand, Alwaye-Kerala, Koyali-Gujarat sahi hain — 'Dharmapuri-Odisha' GALAT hai\n(Dharmapuri Tamil Nadu mein hai). [Q44]\n EXAM TRAP — Dharmapuri — Tamil Nadu mein hai, Odisha mein NAHI\n⚠️"," 43. Industry Location Match (Atlas Cycle-Sonipat, BEML-Bangalore, IFFCO-Kalol,\nNALCO-Bhubaneswar)\n●\nMatch: Atlas Cycle Company Ltd. — Sonepat, Bharat Earth Movers Ltd. — Bangalore, Indian\nFarmers Fertilizers Co-operative Ltd. — Kalol, National Aluminium Company Ltd. — Bhubaneswar.\n[Q45]\n44. Diamond Park — Diamond/Jewellery Manufacturing-Export Zone\n●\nDiamond Park industrial zones hain jo diamonds aur synthetic jewellery/ornaments ke manufacturing-\nexport ko promote karte hain. [Q46]\n45. Person-Field Match (B.V. Rao-Poultry, C.K. Prahlad-Management, John Kurien-\nFisheries)\n●\nMatch: B.V. Rao — Poultry Farming, C.K. Prahlad — Management Science, John Kurien — Fisheries\nEconomy, Kiran Karnik — Information Technology and Software. [Q47]\n46. Person-Organisation Match (Historical — BEML, BHEL, Maruti CEOs)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt ka sahi match: A.K. Puri — BHEL, V.R.S. Natrajan — BEML, V. Thulasidas — Air\nIndia, Jagdish Khattar — Maruti Udyog — abhi (current) leaders: Shantanu Roy-BEML, Nalin Singhal-\nBHEL, Hisashi Takeuchi-Maruti. [Q48]\n47. Executive-Company Match (Historical — NTPC, TCS, Wipro)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt: C.P. Jain — Indian Airlines, S. Ramadorai — TCS, Sunil Arora — NTPC, Vivek\nPaul — Wipro Technologies — abhi (current): Gurdeep Singh-NTPC, K. Krithivasan-TCS, Thierry\nDelaporte-Wipro. [Q49]\n48. Distinguished Women Match (Amrita Patel-NDDB, Historical Update)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt: Amrita Patel — National Dairy Development Board, Anu Aga — Thermax Limited,\nMallika Srinivasan — Tractors and Farm Equipment Limited, Priya Paul — Park Hotels — abhi\n(current) Thermax mein Ashish Bhandari hain. [Q50]\n49. Ludhiana — Punjab's Hosiery Industry Hub\n●\nLudhiana (Punjab ki industrial capital) hosiery industry ke liye famous hai — ready-made garments,\nsewing machines, machine tools ke liye bhi jaana jaata hai. [Q51]\n50. Thermal Power — India's Maximum Water Consumer Industry\n●\nThermal power industries India mein sabse zyada paani consume karti hain — Engineering, Paper-Pulp,\nTextiles se zyada. [Q52]\n51. Industry-Place Match (Paper-Titagarh, Cement-Lakheri, Steel-Bhilai, Oil-Ambala\nMukul)"," ●\nMatch: Paper — Titagarh, Cement — Lakheri, Iron & Steel — Bhilai, Mineral Oil Refinery — Ambala\nMukul. [Q53]\n52. Industry-Centre Match (Aluminium-JK Nagar, Copper-Malanjkhand, Zinc-Tundoo,\nJute-Bhatpara)\n●\nMatch: Aluminium — J.K. Nagar, Copper — Malanjkhand, Zinc — Tundoo, Jute — Bhatpara. [Q54]\n53. Rajasthan Industry Match (Fertilizer-Sriganganagar, Glass-Jaipur, Cement-Udaipur,\nSilk-Kota)\n●\nMatch: Fertilizer — Sriganganagar, Glass — Jaipur, Cement — Udaipur, Synthetic Silk — Kota. [Q55]\n54. Place-Industry Match (Bengaluru-Aircraft, Korba-Aluminium, Jamshedpur-Steel,\nMalanjkhand-Copper)\n●\nMatch: Bengaluru — Aircraft, Korba — Aluminium, Jamshedpur — Iron & Steel, Malanjkhand —\nCopper. [Q56]\n55. Industry Centre Match Repeat (Kakinada-Jute, Virudhnagar-Cotton, Channapatna-Silk,\nBhadohi-Carpet)\n●\nMatch: Kakinada — Jute, Virudhnagar — Cotton Textile, Channapatna — Silk, Bhadohi — Carpet.\n[Q57]\n56. Traditional Saree Towns — Chanderi & Kancheepuram (Not Bhadrachalam/Karnal)\n●\nChanderi (Ashoknagar district, MP) aur Kancheepuram (Tamil Nadu) traditional sarees/fabric ke liye\nfamous hain — Bhadrachalam aur Karnal is category mein NAHI hain. [Q58]\n57. GI Tag Status — Banarasi Saree & Tirupati Laddu (Not Rajasthani Daal-Bati)\n●\nGeographical Indication (GI) status Banarasi Jari-Sarees aur Tirupati Laddu ko mila hai — Rajasthani\nDaal-Bati-Churma ko NAHI mila. [Q59]\n58. Sivakasi — NOT in Chhotanagpur Region (Actually Madurai-Coimbatore-Bengaluru)\n●\nKolkata-Hugli region-Titagarh, Mumbai-Pune region-Ambernath, Ahmedabad-Vadodara region-Bharuch sahi\nhain — 'Chhota Nagpur region-Sivakasi' GALAT hai (Sivakasi asal mein Madurai-Coimbatore-\nBengaluru industrial region mein hai). [Q60]\n EXAM TRAP — Sivakasi — Madurai-Coimbatore-Bengaluru industrial region mein hai, Chhota Nagpur\n⚠️\n\nmein NAHI\n59. Shivkashi — Fireworks/Matchbox Hub, 'Little Japan'\n●\nShivkashi (Virudhunagar district, Tamil Nadu) fireworks, matchbox, printing industry ke liye famous hai\n— Jawaharlal Nehru ne ise 'Little Japan' kaha tha. [Q61]\n60. Pithampur, MP — Automobile Industry Hub"," ●\nPithampur (Dhar district, Madhya Pradesh) automobile industry ke liye jaana jaata hai — bade-chhote\npaimane ke industries yahan established hain. [Q62]\n61. JSMDC Granite Polishing — Tupudana, Ranchi\n●\nJharkhand State Minerals Development Corporation (JSMDC) ka Granite Polishing Industry Tupudana\n(Ranchi) mein hai — Bishrampur Graphite project Palamu mein hai. [Q63]\n62. Nepanagar — Newsprint Paper (Repeat)\n●\nNepanagar (Burhanpur district, Madhya Pradesh) newsprint paper industry ke liye famous hai. [Q64]\n63. Caustic Soda — NOT a Fertilizer Raw Material\n●\nNaphtha, Gypsum, Sulphur fertilizer industry mein raw material ke roop mein use hote hain — Caustic soda\nfertilizer ka raw material NAHI hai. [Q65]\n64. Rajasthan's Sole-Producer Minerals (Lead-Zinc, Selenite, Wollastonite)\n●\nRajasthan Government ke mutabik Rajasthan Lead-Zinc ores, Selenite aur Wollastonite ka lagbhag\nekmatra producer hai (Copper ores ka NAHI). [Q66]\n65. Diesel Locomotive Works, Varanasi — Now Makes Electric Engines\n●\nDiesel Locomotive Works (DLW, ab Banaras Locomotive Works), Varanasi ab electric engines\nbanata/provide karta hai (diesel engines ki jagah). [Q67]\n66. Non-Coal Mine Auctioning — State Government Power (2015 Law)\n●\nMines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Amendment Act 2015 ke mutabik non-coal mines ki\nauction State Governments karti hain (statement 1 GALAT hai) — Rajasthan mein iron-ore mines\nhain (statement 3 sahi hai) — Andhra Pradesh mein gold-bearing quartz rocks ke deposits hain\n(statement 2 galat hai — AP mein gold mines hain). [Q68]\n67. Motihari-Amlekhganj Cross-Border Oil Pipeline (Sept 2019)\n●\nSeptember 2019 mein PM Modi ne Motihari (India) aur Amlekhganj (Nepal) ke beech cross-border oil\npipeline inaugurate ki. [Q69]\n68. Sugar Industry — Maharashtra #1, UP #2 (Current)\n●\nApril 2023 tak Maharashtra sugar ka sabse bada producer hai, UP dusre number par hai — sugar\nindustry weight-losing industry hai (weight-gaining NAHI). [Q70]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0064","t":"28 Research Centers in India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" RESEARCH CENTRES IN INDIA — FULL MIND\n🔬\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Map Match — CDRI-Lucknow, NATMO-Kolkata, NIOT-Chennai, TFRI-Shimla\n2. Maitri — India's 2nd Antarctica Research Station (1988)\n3. Bharati — India's 3rd Antarctica Research Centre (2012)\n4. Dakshin Gangotri — India's First Antarctica Research Station\n5. ICRISAT — Patancheru, Near Hyderabad\n6. CRIDA (Dryland Agriculture) — Hyderabad\n7. Central Institute of Arid Horticulture — Bikaner\n8. NAARM (Agri Research Management) — Hyderabad\n9. NIAM (Agriculture Marketing) — Jaipur\n10. Central Food Technological Research Institute — Mysore\n11. Institute-Location Match (NEE-Nagpur, CFTRI-Mysuru, CPRI-Shimla, CTRI-Rajahmundry)\n12. National Research Centre of Agro-Forestry — Jhansi\n13. Central Institute of Agricultural Engineering — Bhopal\n14. Rice Research Institute — Cuttack (Historical) → Hyderabad (IIRR Now)\n15. National Dairy Research Institute — Karnal, Haryana\n16. Indian Institute of Pulses Research — Kanpur\n17. Indian Institute of Vegetable Research — Varanasi\n18. Central Institute of Sub-tropical Horticulture — Lucknow\n19. Indian Bureau of Mines HQ — Nagpur\n20. Central Institute of Mining and Fuel Research — Dhanbad\n21. Indian Diamond Institute — Surat, Gujarat (1978)\n22. National Dairy Development Board — Anand, Gujarat\n23. Indian Grassland and Fodder Research Institute — Jhansi (1962)\n24. Indian Horticulture University — Solan, Himachal Pradesh\n25. Institute-Location Match (Sugar-Kanpur, Mishra Dhatu-Hyderabad)\n26. Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research — Lucknow (1952)\n27. Institute Match (Rice-Cuttack, Farming System-Meerut, Soil Science-Bhopal)\n28. NATMO — Kolkata (Est. Under Kolkata University Geography Dept)\n29. National Museum of Natural History — No Hyderabad Branch\n30. Institute-Location Match (CSSRI-Karnal, CTCRI-Trivandrum, IRRI-Manila, CAZRI-Jodhpur)\n31. Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine and Storage — Faridabad\n32. Crop Directorate Match (DRR-Hyderabad, DWR-Karnal, DMR-Delhi, DPR-Kanpur)\n33. Sugarcane-PlantGenetics-PlantProtection Match (Disputed — Wheat is Karnal, Not Kanpur)\n34. National Centre of Organic Farming (NCONF) — Ghaziabad\n35. Institute Mismatch — Subtropical Horticulture is Lucknow, Not Srinagar\n36. Indian Meteorological HQ — Chronological Order (Kolkata→Shimla→Pune→Delhi)\n37. International Solar Alliance Secretariat — Gurugram\n38. Central Institute of Indian Languages — Mysore\n39. Goat Research Centre (CIRG) — Makhdoom, Mathura (1979)\n40. First Krishi Vigyan Kendra — Pondicherry (1974)\n41. Centre for Social Forestry and Eco-Rehabilitation — Prayagraj\n42. NRCAF/CAFRI (Agroforestry) — Jhansi, Not Banda\n43. University of Horticulture and Forestry — Solan (Repeat)"," 44. Indian Institute of Remote Sensing — Dehradun\n45. V.V. Giri National Labour Institute — Noida (1974)\n46. National Research Centre on Seed Spices — Doomara, Ajmer\n47. IFFCO — Not Involved in Agricultural Exports\n48. National Research Centre on Camel — Bikaner (1984/1995)\n49. Indian Institute of Petroleum — Dehradun (1960)\n50. National Disaster Response Force Academy — Nagpur (2018)\n1. Map Match — CDRI-Lucknow, NATMO-Kolkata, NIOT-Chennai, TFRI-Shimla\n●\nMatch: Central Drug Research Institute — Lucknow, National Atlas and Thematic Mapping\nOrganisation — Kolkata, National Institute of Ocean Technology — Chennai, Temperate Forest\nResearch Centre — Shimla. [Q1]\n2. Maitri — India's 2nd Antarctica Research Station (1988)\n●\nMaitri (1988 mein establish) earth science, glaciology, atmospheric science, communication, medicine,\nhuman physiology, cold-region engineering par research karti hai. [Q2]\n3. Bharati — India's 3rd Antarctica Research Centre (2012)\n●\nAntarctica ka 3rd Indian research centre 'Bharati' 2012 mein establish hua. [Q3]\n4. Dakshin Gangotri — India's First Antarctica Research Station\n●\n1983 mein India ne Antarctic Treaty sign kiya, Dakshin Gangotri (pehla research base) 1983-84 mein\nbana — Maitri (2nd, biology/earth-science/glaciology ke liye), Bharati (3rd, 2012). [Q4, Q5]\n5. ICRISAT — Patancheru, Near Hyderabad\n●\nICRISAT (International Crops Research Institute for Semi-Arid Tropics) Patancheru, Hyderabad ke paas\nhai — South Asia aur Sub-Saharan Africa mein agrarian research. [Q6]\n6. CRIDA (Dryland Agriculture) — Hyderabad\n●\nCentral Research Institute for Dryland Agriculture (CRIDA) Hyderabad mein hai — ICAR ke tahat. [Q7,\nQ8, Q9]\n7. Central Institute of Arid Horticulture — Bikaner\n●\nCIAH (Central Institute for Arid Horticulture) Bikaner, Rajasthan mein hai. [Q10]\n8. NAARM (Agri Research Management) — Hyderabad\n●\nNational Academy of Agricultural Research Management (NAARM) Hyderabad mein hai. [Q11]\n9. NIAM (Agriculture Marketing) — Jaipur\n●\nNational Institute of Agricultural Marketing (NIAM) Jaipur mein hai. [Q12]\n10. Central Food Technological Research Institute — Mysore"," ●\nCentral Food Technological Research Institute (CFTRI) Mysore mein hai. [Q13]\n11. Institute-Location Match (NEE-Nagpur, CFTRI-Mysuru, CPRI-Shimla, CTRI-\nRajahmundry)\n●\nMatch: National Environment Engineering — Nagpur, Central Food Technology Research Institute —\nMysuru, Central Potato Research Institute — Shimla, Central Tobacco Research Institute —\nRajahmundry. [Q14]\n12. National Research Centre of Agro-Forestry — Jhansi\n●\nNational Research Centre of Agro-Forestry Jhansi mein hai. [Q15, Q16]\n13. Central Institute of Agricultural Engineering — Bhopal\n●\nCentral Institute of Agricultural Engineering (CIAE, 15 Feb 1976 establish) Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh mein\nhai — agricultural machinery-instruments par R&D. [Q17]\n14. Rice Research Institute — Cuttack (Historical) → Hyderabad (IIRR Now)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Central Rice Research Institute Cuttack, Odisha mein tha (1946 establish, ab\n'National Rice Research Institute') — abhi Indian Institute of Rice Research (IIRR) Hyderabad\n(Telangana) mein hai (pehle 'Directorate of Rice Research' kehlaata tha). [Q18]\n15. National Dairy Research Institute — Karnal, Haryana\n●\nNational Dairy Research Institute (NDRI) Karnal, Haryana mein hai — 1989 mein Deemed University ka\nstatus mila. [Q19, Q20, Q21]\n16. Indian Institute of Pulses Research — Kanpur\n●\nIndian Institute of Pulses Research Kanpur mein hai. [Q22]\n17. Indian Institute of Vegetable Research — Varanasi\n●\nIndian Institute of Vegetable Research (1999 establish) Varanasi mein hai — Ministry of Agriculture ke\nDepartment of Agricultural Research and Education ke tahat. [Q23, Q24]\n18. Central Institute of Sub-tropical Horticulture — Lucknow\n●\nCentral Institute of Sub-tropical Horticulture (pehle Central Mango Research Institute) Lucknow mein hai.\n[Q25]\n19. Indian Bureau of Mines HQ — Nagpur\n●\nIndian Bureau of Mines (IBM, 1948 establish) ka HQ Nagpur mein hai — Ministry of Mines ke tahat.\n[Q26]\n20. Central Institute of Mining and Fuel Research — Dhanbad\n●\nCentral Institute of Mining and Fuel Research (CIMFR, pehle CMRI) Dhanbad, Jharkhand mein hai. [Q27]"," 21. Indian Diamond Institute — Surat, Gujarat (1978)\n●\nIndian Diamond Institute (1978 establish) Surat, Gujarat mein hai — diamonds/gems/jewellery ke fields\nmein autonomous learning institute. [Q28]\n22. National Dairy Development Board — Anand, Gujarat\n●\nNational Dairy Development Board Anand, Gujarat mein hai — poore desh mein regional offices. [Q29]\n23. Indian Grassland and Fodder Research Institute — Jhansi (1962)\n●\nIndian Grass and Fodder Research Institute (1962 establish) Jhansi, UP mein hai — ICAR ke tahat forage\nproduction research. [Q30, Q31]\n24. Indian Horticulture University — Solan, Himachal Pradesh\n●\nDr. Yashwant Singh Parmar University of Horticulture and Forestry Solan district, Himachal Pradesh mein\nhai. [Q32]\n25. Institute-Location Match (Sugar-Kanpur, Mishra Dhatu-Hyderabad)\n●\nMatch: National Sugar Institute — Kanpur, Mishra Dhatu Nigam Limited — Hyderabad, Institute of\nMilitary Law — Kamptee, Institute of National Integration — Pune. [Q33]\n26. Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research — Lucknow (1952)\n●\nIndian Institute of Sugarcane Research (IISR, 1952 establish) Lucknow mein hai. [Q34]\n27. Institute Match (Rice-Cuttack, Farming System-Meerut, Soil Science-Bhopal)\n●\nMatch: Central Rice Research Institute — Cuttack, Directorate of Farming System Research —\nMeerut, Indian Institute of Soil Science — Bhopal, National Centre for Agro-Forestry Research —\nJhansi. [Q35]\n28. NATMO — Kolkata (Est. Under Kolkata University Geography Dept)\n●\nNATMO (National Atlas and Thematic Mapping Organisation) Kolkata University Geography\nDepartment ke tahat establish hui, Prof. S.P. Chatterjee founding director the — 1978 mein naam\nbadla, ab Dept of Science & Tech ke tahat hai. [Q36]\n29. National Museum of Natural History — No Hyderabad Branch\n●\nNMNH (New Delhi mein main) ki regional branches: Southern (Mysuru), Central (Bhopal), Western\n(Sawai Madhopur), Eastern (Bhubaneswar) — Hyderabad mein NMNH ki koi branch NAHI hai. [Q37]\n30. Institute-Location Match (CSSRI-Karnal, CTCRI-Trivandrum, IRRI-Manila, CAZRI-\nJodhpur)\n●\nMatch: Central Soil Salinity Research Institute (CSSRI) — Karnal, Central Tuber Crops Research\nInstitute (CTCRI) — Trivandrum, International Rice Research Institute (IRRI) — Manila, Central\nArid Zone Research Institute (CAZRI) — Jodhpur. [Q38]"," 31. Directorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine and Storage — Faridabad\n●\nDirectorate of Plant Protection, Quarantine and Storage Faridabad, Haryana mein hai. [Q39]\n32. Crop Directorate Match (DRR-Hyderabad, DWR-Karnal, DMR-Delhi, DPR-Kanpur)\n●\nMatch: Directorate of Rice Research (ab Indian Institute of Rice Research) — Hyderabad, Directorate\nof Wheat Research (ab Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research) — Karnal, Directorate of\nMaize Research — New Delhi, Directorate of Pulses Research — Kanpur. [Q40]\n33. Sugarcane-PlantGenetics-PlantProtection Match (Disputed — Wheat is Karnal, Not\nKanpur)\n●\nSahi match: Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research — Lucknow, National Bureau of Plant Genetics\nResources — New Delhi, National Plant Protection Training Institute — Hyderabad — 'Directorate of\nWheat Research-Kanpur' GALAT hai (asal mein Karnal mein hai), isliye poora question disputed hai.\n[Q41]\n EXAM TRAP — Directorate of Wheat Research — Karnal mein hai, Kanpur mein NAHI\n⚠️\n34. National Centre of Organic Farming (NCONF) — Ghaziabad\n●\nNational Centre of Organic Farming (NCOF) Ghaziabad mein hai — March 2022 mein NCONF (National\nCentre for Organic and Natural Farming) rename hua. [Q42]\n35. Institute Mismatch — Subtropical Horticulture is Lucknow, Not Srinagar\n●\nIndian Vegetable Research Institute-Varanasi, IISR-Lucknow, Pulse Research-Kanpur sahi hain — 'Central\nInstitute of Subtropical Horticulture-Srinagar' GALAT hai (Lucknow mein hai). [Q43]\n36. Indian Meteorological HQ — Chronological Order (Kolkata→Shimla→Pune→Delhi)\n●\nIndian Meteorological Department: 1875 mein Kolkata mein establish hui, 1905 mein Shimla shift hui,\n1928 mein Pune, aur finally 1944 mein Delhi. [Q44]\n37. International Solar Alliance Secretariat — Gurugram\n●\nInternational Solar Alliance (ISA) ka Secretariat Gurugram, Haryana mein hai — 'Towards 1000'\nstrategy ke tahat 2030 tak $1000 billion investment ka target. [Q45]\n38. Central Institute of Indian Languages — Mysore\n●\nCentral Institute of Indian Languages (CIIL) Mysore mein hai — Ministry of Education ke Department of\nHigher Education ke tahat. [Q46]\n39. Goat Research Centre (CIRG) — Makhdoom, Mathura (1979)\n●\nCentral Institute for Research on Goats (CIRG, 12 July 1979 establish) Makhdoom (Mathura) mein hai.\n[Q47]\n40. First Krishi Vigyan Kendra — Pondicherry (1974)"," ●\nIndia ka pehla Krishi Vigyan Kendra 1974 mein Puducherry (tab Pondicherry) mein Tamil Nadu\nAgricultural University (Coimbatore) ke tahat pilot basis par establish hua — Feb 2024 tak total 728\nKVKs hain. [Q48, Q49]\n41. Centre for Social Forestry and Eco-Rehabilitation — Prayagraj\n●\n'Centre for Social Forestry and Eco-Rehabilitation' Prayagraj (UP) mein hai — Forest Research Institute\nDehradun mein, Indian Institute of Forest Management Bhopal mein, NEERI Nagpur mein hai. [Q50]\n42. NRCAF/CAFRI (Agroforestry) — Jhansi, Not Banda\n●\nICRA-Nairobi, IIFM-Bhopal, TERI-New Delhi sahi hain — 'Central Agroforestry Research Institute-\nBanda' GALAT hai (asal mein Jhansi mein hai, popularly 'Krishivaniki' kehlata hai — 1988 mein\nNRCAF ke naam se establish hua). [Q51]\n EXAM TRAP — Central/National Agroforestry Research Institute — Jhansi mein hai, Banda mein\n⚠️\nNAHI\n43. University of Horticulture and Forestry — Solan (Repeat)\n●\nDr. Yashwant Singh Parmar University of Horticulture and Forestry Solan, Himachal Pradesh mein hai.\n[Q52]\n44. Indian Institute of Remote Sensing — Dehradun\n●\nIndian Institute of Remote Sensing Dehradun, Uttarakhand mein hai — remote sensing, geoinformatics,\nGPS technology ke research-training ke liye. [Q53]\n45. V.V. Giri National Labour Institute — Noida (1974)\n●\nV.V. Giri National Labour Institute (VVGNLI, July 1974 establish) Noida, UP mein hai — Ministry of\nLabour and Employment ka autonomous body. [Q54]\n46. National Research Centre on Seed Spices — Doomara, Ajmer\n●\nNational Research Centre on Seed Spices (NRCSS) Doomara (Tabiji), Ajmer district, Rajasthan mein hai.\n[Q55]\n47. IFFCO — Not Involved in Agricultural Exports\n●\nNAFED, State Trading Corporation, MMTC agricultural exports mein involved hain — IFFCO (Indian\nFarmers Fertiliser Cooperative Limited) fertilizers manufacturing-marketing mein hai, agricultural\nexports mein NAHI. [Q56]\n48. National Research Centre on Camel — Bikaner (1984/1995)\n●\nNational Research Centre on Camel (NRCC) Bikaner, Rajasthan mein hai — 5 July 1984 ko Project\nDirectorate ke roop mein shuru hua, 20 Sept 1995 ko NRCC mein upgrade hua. [Q57]\n49. Indian Institute of Petroleum — Dehradun (1960)"," ●\nIndian Institute of Petroleum (CSIR ki constituent laboratory, 14 April 1960 establish) Dehradun,\nUttarakhand mein hai. [Q58]\n50. National Disaster Response Force Academy — Nagpur (2018)\n●\nNational Disaster Response Force Academy (2018, National Civil Defence College ke merger se) Nagpur,\nMaharashtra mein hai — NDRF/SDRF battalions ko disaster-management training deti hai. [Q59]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0065","t":"29.i Road Transport","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ROAD TRANSPORT — FULL MIND MAP\n🛣️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Road's Share in Transport — 80% (Historical), Now 90%\n2. National Highways — 64 (Historical) → 668 Now (146195 km)\n3. Longest NH (Historical NH-7 → Now NH-27 EW, 4112.62 km)\n4. NH-4 Route (Maharashtra-AP-Karnataka-TN, Historical)\n5. NH Match Traps (NH4 Doesn't Reach Hyderabad, NH6 Doesn't Reach Mumbai)\n6. Max NH Length — UP (Historical) → Maharashtra Now\n7. Max State Highway Length — Maharashtra\n8. NHDP (Golden Quadrilateral) — 5846km, Delhi-Mumbai-Chennai-Kolkata\n9. East-West Corridor — Silchar to Porbandar\n10. Golden Quadrilateral — Highway Development Project\n11. Pradhan Mantri Bharat Jodo Pariyojna — Highway Development\n12. North-South × East-West Corridor Junction — Jhansi\n13. East-West Corridor Nodes (Golden Quad) — Silchar-Porbandar\n14. North-South Corridor Cities (Agra-Gwalior-Nagpur-Krishnagiri)\n15. Agra — North-South Corridor City\n16. Mumbai-Pune Expressway — India's First 6-Lane Expressway\n17. NH-3 Cities — Atari/Amritsar/Himachal/Leh (Not Bhopal)\n18. Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana — Rural Road Connectivity (2000)\n19. Road Density Ranking (Punjab Highest Among Given States)\n20. Maharashtra — Highest Surface Road Density; NH-7 Longest (Historical)\n21. Amritsar-Kolkata via Delhi — NH-2 (Historical)\n22. National Highways — Carry ~40% of Road Traffic\n23. NH-3 (Old) — Longest in MP (712 km)\n24. Longest NH Route (Old Numbering) — Kolkata-Hazira (1949km)\n25. South Central Railway HQ — Secunderabad (Not Hyderabad)\n26. NE States NH Length Ranking (Arunachal>Nagaland>Mizoram>Sikkim)\n27. Jawahar Tunnel — Banihal, J&K\n28. Kohima-Kottayam Road Trip — Minimum 7 States\n29. NH Passing MP — Disputed Post-2010 Renumbering\n30. Indore-Jaipur Highway — Revised Number 52\n31. Road Density — Kerala Highest Among Given States\n32. MP Highway-City Match (NH30-Jabalpur, NH39-Khajuraho)\n33. Maharashtra — Highest Total Road Length\n1. Road's Share in Transport — 80% (Historical), Now 90%\n●\nIndia ka road network 63.45 lakh km hai (world ka 2nd largest) — question ke waqt roadways se 65%\nfreight aur 80% passenger traffic carry hota tha — ab 67% freight aur 90% passenger traffic roads se\nhota hai. [Q1]\n2. National Highways — 64 (Historical) → 668 Now (146195 km)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt 64 National Highways the, total length 40,000 km — 31 Dec 2024 tak ab ~668 NH\nhain, total length 146195 km. [Q2]"," 3. Longest NH (Historical NH-7 → Now NH-27 EW, 4112.62 km)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt NH-7 sabse lamba tha — Ministry of Road Transport (31 March 2019) ke mutabik ab\nNH-27 EW (4112.62 km) sabse lamba hai. [Q3]\n4. NH-4 Route (Maharashtra-AP-Karnataka-TN, Historical)\n●\nPurana NH-4 (1235 km) Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu se hoke jaata tha\n(Mumbai-Chennai) — MP/Rajasthan/UP se NAHI. Ab NH4 (330.70 km) Andaman-Nicobar mein\nMayabandar-Port Blair-Chiriyatapu ko jodta hai. [Q4, Q5]\n5. NH Match Traps (NH4 Doesn't Reach Hyderabad, NH6 Doesn't Reach Mumbai)\n●\n'NH4-Chennai/Hyderabad', 'NH6-Mumbai/Kolkata', 'NH15-Ahmedabad/Jodhpur' teeno pairs GALAT hain —\nNH4 Mumbai-Chennai (Hyderabad se NAHI guzarta), NH6 Hazira-Kolkata (Mumbai se NAHI\nguzarta), NH15 Samakhiali-Pathankot (Ahmedabad/Jodhpur se NAHI guzarta). [Q6]\n6. Max NH Length — UP (Historical) → Maharashtra Now\n●\nQuestion ke waqt UP mein NH ki max length thi — 31 Dec 2024 tak Maharashtra pehle number par hai\n(18462 km), UP dusre (12123 km). [Q7]\n7. Max State Highway Length — Maharashtra\n●\n'Basic Road Statistics 2013' ke mutabik Maharashtra (38765 km) state highways mein sabse aage hai —\nGujarat (18506), Rajasthan (10465), UP (7703). [Q8, Q9]\n8. NHDP (Golden Quadrilateral) — 5846km, Delhi-Mumbai-Chennai-Kolkata\n●\nNHDP (Golden Quadrilateral part) Delhi, Mumbai, Chennai, Kolkata ko jodta hai — total length 5846\nkm — North-South corridor Srinagar-Kanyakumari, East-West corridor Silchar-Porbandar ko jodta\nhai. [Q10]\n9. East-West Corridor — Silchar to Porbandar\n●\nEast-West Corridor Silchar (Assam) ko Porbandar (Gujarat) se jodta hai. [Q11, Q17]\n10. Golden Quadrilateral — Highway Development Project\n●\nGolden Quadrilateral highway se related development hai — Delhi-Kolkata-Mumbai-Chennai (4 major\nmetros) ko jodta hai — National Highway Project hai (Rail lines/Air Routes NAHI). [Q12, Q13, Q14]\n11. Pradhan Mantri Bharat Jodo Pariyojna — Highway Development\n●\nPradhan Mantri Bharat Jodo Pariyojna highways ke development se related hai — BOT (Build-Operate-\nTransfer) principle par corridors banaye jaayenge. [Q15]\n12. North-South × East-West Corridor Junction — Jhansi\n●\nNorth-South (Srinagar-Kanyakumari) aur East-West (Silchar-Porbandar) corridors Jhansi (UP) mein ek-\ndusre ko cut karte hain. [Q16, Q18, Q19]"," 13. East-West Corridor Nodes (Golden Quad) — Silchar-Porbandar\n●\nBCIM corridor (Kunming se Kolkata, Mandalay-Dhaka se hoke) aur Trilateral Highway (Moreh-Manipur se\nMae Sot-Thailand, Bagan-Myanmar se hoke) dono East-West Corridor se ALAG hain — teeno diye gaye\nstatements GALAT the. [Q20]\n14. North-South Corridor Cities (Agra-Gwalior-Nagpur-Krishnagiri)\n●\nNorth to South sequence: Agra, Gwalior, Nagpur, Krishnagiri — NHDP ka 2nd phase hai. [Q21]\n15. Agra — North-South Corridor City\n●\nAgra North-South corridor par sthith hai (Lucknow, Kota, Kanpur is corridor par NAHI hain). [Q22]\n16. Mumbai-Pune Expressway — India's First 6-Lane Expressway\n●\nMumbai-Pune Expressway India ka pehla 6-lane concrete, high-speed, access-controlled, tolled\nexpressway hai (94.5 km). [Q23]\n17. NH-3 Cities — Atari/Amritsar/Himachal/Leh (Not Bhopal)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Agra, Dhule, Gwalior NH-3 se connected the (Bhopal NAHI) — ab NH-3 Atari-\nAmritsar-Jalandhar-Hoshiarpur (Punjab), Himachal Pradesh, aur Leh (J&K) tak jaata hai. [Q24]\n18. Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana — Rural Road Connectivity (2000)\n●\nPMGSY 25 December 2000 ko launch hui thi — un rural areas ko all-weather road connectivity dene\nke liye jo connected nahi the. [Q25]\n19. Road Density Ranking (Punjab Highest Among Given States)\n●\n'Basic Road Statistics 2018-19' ke mutabik surface road density (per 100 sq km): Punjab (293.59) >\nMaharashtra (208.47) > Tamil Nadu (206.97) > Haryana (113.75). [Q26]\n20. Maharashtra — Highest Surface Road Density; NH-7 Longest (Historical)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt: National Highways ~40-45% transport demand poori karte the, Maharashtra mein\nhighest surface-road density thi, NH-7 sabse lamba tha (Kerala mein highest density NAHI thi). [Q27]\n21. Amritsar-Kolkata via Delhi — NH-2 (Historical)\n●\nAmritsar se Delhi ke through Kolkata jaane wala route historically NH-2 tha (Delhi-Mathura-Agra-\nKanpur-Allahabad-Varanasi-Kolkata) — NH-1 Delhi-Ambala-Jalandhar-Amritsar-Indo-Pak border tak\njaata tha. [Q28]\n22. National Highways — Carry ~40% of Road Traffic\n●\nNational Highways total ~146195 km lambe hain — total road traffic ka ~40% carry karte hain. [Q29]\n23. NH-3 (Old) — Longest in MP (712 km)"," ●\nPurana NH-3 (Agra-Gwalior-Dewas-Mumbai) MP mein sabse lambi NH thi (712 km). [Q30]\n24. Longest NH Route (Old Numbering) — Kolkata-Hazira (1949km)\n●\nOld NH numbering routes: Agra-Mumbai (NH3, 1161km), Chennai-Thane (NH4, 1235km), Kolkata-\nHazira (NH6, 1949km — sabse lamba), Pune-Machilipatnam (NH9, 841km). [Q31]\n25. South Central Railway HQ — Secunderabad (Not Hyderabad)\n●\nHaldia-Allahabad National Waterway, Nasik-Pune NH-50, Durgapur-Kolkata Express Highway sahi hain —\n'Hyderabad-South Central Railway HQ' GALAT hai (HQ Secunderabad mein hai). [Q32]\n EXAM TRAP — South Central Railway ka HQ Secunderabad mein hai, Hyderabad mein NAHI\n⚠️\n26. NE States NH Length Ranking (Arunachal>Nagaland>Mizoram>Sikkim)\n●\n31.03.2024 tak NH length ranking: Arunachal Pradesh (4285.39km) > Nagaland (1670.47km) > Mizoram\n(1498.67km) > Sikkim (709.07km). [Q33]\n27. Jawahar Tunnel — Banihal, J&K\n●\nJawahar Tunnel (Banihal Tunnel bhi kehlata hai) J&K UT mein hai, BRO (Border Road Organisation)\nmaintain karta hai. [Q34]\n28. Kohima-Kottayam Road Trip — Minimum 7 States\n●\nKohima se Kottayam tak road se yatra karte huye minimum 7 states (Nagaland-origin, Assam, WB,\nOdisha, AP, phir TN/Karnataka se Kerala tak) cross karne padte hain. [Q35]\n29. NH Passing MP — Disputed Post-2010 Renumbering\n●\n5 March 2010 ke naye numbering ke mutabik NH-3, NH-7, NH-8, NH-12 mein se koi bhi MP se NAHI\nguzarta — old numbering ke hisaab se NH(Old)-8 sahi answer hota. [Q36]\n30. Indore-Jaipur Highway — Revised Number 52\n●\nIndore-Jaipur ko jodne wali NH ka revised number 52 hai (purana NH3 ka hissa tha). [Q37]\n31. Road Density — Kerala Highest Among Given States\n●\n31 March 2019 data ke mutabik road density (per 1000 sq km): Kerala (6690.30) > Punjab (2935.98) >\nGujarat (1270.73) > Haryana (1137.53). [Q38]\n32. MP Highway-City Match (NH30-Jabalpur, NH39-Khajuraho)\n●\nMatch: NH-30 — Jabalpur, NH-39 — Khajuraho, NH-46 — Bhopal, NH-44 — Sagar. [Q39]\n33. Maharashtra — Highest Total Road Length\n●\nMaharashtra roads ki total length ke hisaab se India mein pehle number par hai — UP, MP, Rajasthan se\nzyada. [Q40]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0066","t":"29.ii Rail Transport","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" RAIL TRANSPORT — FULL MIND MAP\n🚂\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. First Railway — 1853, Bombay-Thane (GIPR)\n2. Broad Gauge — 5.5 ft (1676mm) Width\n3. Gorakhpur-Mumbai Shortest Route — via Allahabad\n4. Bullet Train — Mumbai-Ahmedabad\n5. Railway Zone HQ Mismatches (South-Eastern is Kolkata, Not Bhubaneswar)\n6. North Frontier Railway HQ — Maligaon, Not Prayagraj\n7. South-Eastern Railway HQ — Kolkata\n8. North-Western Railway HQ — Jaipur (Not Jodhpur); Fairy Queen\n9. East Central Railway HQ — Hajipur, Bihar\n10. North Central Railway HQ — Prayagraj/Allahabad\n11. Delhi-Karachi/Bhuj Junction — Balotra\n12. Road vs Rail — Reasons Road Transport Got More Impetus\n13. Rail Factory Match (Coach-Kapurthala, Wheel-Bangalore, Diesel-Varanasi)\n14. Locomotive Works Match (Chittaranjan-Electric, Varanasi-Diesel, Jamshedpur-Steam)\n15. Coach Manufacturing States — Punjab & Tamil Nadu\n16. Railway Staff College (National Academy) — Vadodara\n17. Sal Wood — Railway Sleepers\n18. Gujarat Railway Junctions Map (Mahesana, Surendranagar, Rajkot, Junagarh)\n19. Third Rail Coach Factory — Raebareli\n20. First CNG Train — Rewari-Rohtak Section\n21. Gujarat — First PPP-Model Railway Track\n22. Konkan Railway — Roha to Mangalore (Not Kerala)\n23. Konkan Railway Beneficiaries — Goa, Karnataka, Maharashtra\n24. Konkan Railway Doesn't Connect Belgaum\n25. UNESCO Heritage Mountain Railways (Darjeeling, Nilgiri, Kalka-Shimla)\n26. Meghalaya — Rail Connectivity Since Nov 2014 (Sikkim Still Excluded)\n27. Longest Rajdhani Route — Thiruvananthapuram (3149km)\n28. Rail Tunnel Length Ranking (Pir Panjal > Karbude > Nathuwadi > Berdewadi)\n1. First Railway — 1853, Bombay-Thane (GIPR)\n●\nLord Dalhousie ke tenure mein Great Indian Peninsula Railway (GIPR) ne 16 April 1853 ko Bombay-\nThane ke beech India ki pehli railway khol di. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. Broad Gauge — 5.5 ft (1676mm) Width\n●\nIndian Railways ke 3 gauge types: Meter gauge (1000mm), Broad gauge (1676mm, ~5.5 ft), Narrow\ngauge (762mm ya 610mm). [Q4]\n3. Gorakhpur-Mumbai Shortest Route — via Allahabad\n●\nGorakhpur se Mumbai ka sabse chota rail route Allahabad (Prayagraj) se hoke jaata hai. [Q5]\n4. Bullet Train — Mumbai-Ahmedabad"," ●\nPM Manmohan Singh ne December 2004 mein Mumbai-Ahmedabad ke beech Bullet train plan approve\nkiya tha. [Q6]\n5. Railway Zone HQ Mismatches (South-Eastern is Kolkata, Not Bhubaneswar)\n●\nNorth-Eastern-Gorakhpur, Eastern-Kolkata, South-East Central-Bilaspur sahi hain — 'South-Eastern\nRailway-Bhubaneshwar' GALAT hai (South-Eastern ka HQ Kolkata hai, Bhubaneswar mein East\nCoast Railway ka HQ hai). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — South-Eastern Railway ka HQ Kolkata mein hai, Bhubaneswar mein East Coast\n⚠️\nRailway ka HQ hai\n6. North Frontier Railway HQ — Maligaon, Not Prayagraj\n●\nCentral-Mumbai, Western-Churchgate, South Eastern-Garden Reach Kolkata sahi hain — 'North East\nFrontier Railway-Prayagraj' GALAT hai (HQ Maligaon/Guwahati mein hai — Prayagraj North\nCentral Railway ka HQ hai). [Q8]\n7. South-Eastern Railway HQ — Kolkata\n●\nSouth-Eastern Railway ka HQ Kolkata mein hai. [Q9]\n8. North-Western Railway HQ — Jaipur (Not Jodhpur); Fairy Queen\n●\nNorth-Western Railway ka HQ Jaipur mein hai (Jodhpur mein NAHI) — Indrail pass foreign\ntourists/NRIs ke liye hai (freedom fighters ke liye NAHI) — Fairy Queen duniya ka sabse purana\nworking steam locomotive hai (1855 mein bana, 1996 mein overhaul hua, 1997 se commercial\noperations). [Q10]\n9. East Central Railway HQ — Hajipur, Bihar\n●\nEast Central Railway ka HQ Hajipur, Bihar mein hai (1 October 2002 se operational) — currently Indian\nRailways ke 17 zones hain. [Q11]\n10. North Central Railway HQ — Prayagraj/Allahabad\n●\nNorth Central Railway ka HQ Prayagraj (Allahabad) mein hai — 1 April 2003 se present form mein hai\n— North Railway ka HQ New Delhi mein, West Central Railway ka HQ Jabalpur mein hai. [Q12]\n11. Delhi-Karachi/Bhuj Junction — Balotra\n●\nDelhi se Karachi aur Bhuj jaane wale do tourists Balotra tak saath yatra kar sakte hain — pehla route\nBalotra-Badmer-Munabao, dusra south mein Bhuj tak jaata hai. [Q13]\n12. Road vs Rail — Reasons Road Transport Got More Impetus\n●\nRoad transport ko zyada impetus milne ke sahi reasons: rail ki capital cost bahut high hai, geographic\nspread ki wajah se sirf rail se transport needs poori nahi ho sakti, rail ki indivisible nature ki wajah se\nprivate cars/buses jaisi aasaani nahi hoti — 'road transport per-unit cost mein sasta hai' GALAT hai\n(bulk goods ke liye rail sasti hai). [Q14]"," 13. Rail Factory Match (Coach-Kapurthala, Wheel-Bangalore, Diesel-Varanasi)\n●\nMatch: Rail Coach Factory — Kapurthala, Wheel and Axle Plant — Bangalore, Diesel Locomotive\nWorks — Varanasi, Integral Coach Factory — Perambur. [Q15]\n14. Locomotive Works Match (Chittaranjan-Electric, Varanasi-Diesel, Jamshedpur-Steam)\n●\nMatch: Chittaranjan Locomotive Works — Electric locomotive, Banaras Locomotive Works\n(Manduadih, Varanasi) — Diesel Electric, TELCO (Jamshedpur) — Steam Locomotive (historical),\nIntegral Coach Factory (Perambur) — Rail Coaches. [Q16]\n15. Coach Manufacturing States — Punjab & Tamil Nadu\n●\nPassenger rail coaches ka\n\nव्यापकmanufacturing Punjab (Kapurthala) aur Tamil Nadu (Perambur) mein\nhota hai. [Q17]\n16. Railway Staff College (National Academy) — Vadodara\n●\nNational Academy of Indian Railways (purana naam Railway Staff College) Vadodara mein hai — Group\nA/B officers ke liye centralized training institute. [Q18]\n17. Sal Wood — Railway Sleepers\n●\nSal wood (hard, heavy, strong, brown, termite-resistant) Railway sleepers aur coaches banane mein use\nhoti hai — paper/matches/kaththa se NAHI. [Q19]\n18. Gujarat Railway Junctions Map (Mahesana, Surendranagar, Rajkot, Junagarh)\n●\nGujarat map ke 4 junctions: Mahesana, Surendranagar, Rajkot, Junagarh. [Q20]\n19. Third Rail Coach Factory — Raebareli\n●\nIndia ki teesri Rail Coach Factory Raebareli mein establish ho rahi hai — foundation 2007 mein,\nconstruction 2009 se shuru. [Q21]\n20. First CNG Train — Rewari-Rohtak Section\n●\nPehli CNG train Rewari-Rohtak section (Northern Zone) par launch hui — dual fuel (diesel+CNG)\nsystem par based hai. [Q22]\n21. Gujarat — First PPP-Model Railway Track\n●\nGujarat pehla state hai jahan PPP model par railway track bana — Gandhidham-Tuna Tekra rail line\n(14 July 2015, Deendayal Port Authority ne banayi). [Q23]\n22. Konkan Railway — Roha to Mangalore (Not Kerala)\n●\nKonkan Railway (~760km) Roha (Maharashtra) se Mangalore (Karnataka) tak jaati hai —\nMaharashtra, Goa, Karnataka ko jodti hai (Kerala se NAHI, though Kerala ko easy gateway\nmovement provide karti hai) — Western Ghats ko cut karne wala ekmatra rail route hai. [Q24, Q25]"," EXAM TRAP — Konkan Railway — Maharashtra/Goa/Karnataka ko jodti hai, Kerala ko NAHI\n⚠️\n23. Konkan Railway Beneficiaries — Goa, Karnataka, Maharashtra\n●\nKonkan Railway se Goa, Karnataka, Maharashtra ko sabse zyada faayda hota hai. [Q26]\n24. Konkan Railway Doesn't Connect Belgaum\n●\nKonkan Railway Belgaum ko NAHI jodti — Madgaon, Ratnagiri, Udupi ko jodti hai. [Q27]\n25. UNESCO Heritage Mountain Railways (Darjeeling, Nilgiri, Kalka-Shimla)\n●\nMountain Railways of India — Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (WB), Nilgiri Mountain Railway (TN),\nKalka-Shimla Railway (HP) — teeno ko 1999 mein UNESCO World Heritage Site ghoshit kiya gaya.\n[Q28]\n26. Meghalaya — Rail Connectivity Since Nov 2014 (Sikkim Still Excluded)\n●\nQuestion ke waqt Meghalaya rail-service se vanchit tha — November 2014 mein PM Modi ne\nMendipathar-Guwahati train ko hari jhandi dikhaayi — ab sirf Sikkim hi ekmatra state hai jo railway\nnetwork se bahar hai. [Q29]\n27. Longest Rajdhani Route — Thiruvananthapuram (3149km)\n●\nRajdhani distance ranking: Thiruvananthapuram (3149 km) > Dibrugarh (2459 km) > Bengaluru (2365\nkm) > Chennai (2175 km). [Q30]\n28. Rail Tunnel Length Ranking (Pir Panjal > Karbude > Nathuwadi > Berdewadi)\n●\nRail tunnel length ranking: Pir Panjal (11.2km) > Karbude (6.5km) > Nathuwadi (4.4km) > Berdewadi\n(4km). [Q31]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0067","t":"29.iii Water-Air Transport","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" WATER AND AIR TRANSPORT — FULL MIND\n🚢\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Kochi Port — Malabar Coast\n2. Tides — Navigation, Fishing, Siltation Prevention\n3. Cochin — India's Largest Shipyard\n4. Tidal Ports Map — Kandla & Kolkata (Disputed)\n5. Kandla — Gulf of Kutch Location\n6. Chennai — Deep Port Myth (Actually Visakhapatnam)\n7. Chennai — Artificial Port (Not Natural)\n8. Kandla — Not on Eastern Coast\n9. Paradip — Decongests Kolkata & Vishakhapatnam\n10. Paradip — Located in Odisha\n11. Paradip — India's Deepest Port\n12. Marmugao — Located in Goa\n13. Port-State Match (Haldia-WB, Paradip-Odisha, Kandla-Gujarat, Marmugao-Goa)\n14. Kandla — Highest Import/Export Cargo Tonnage (2023-24)\n15. Pondicherry UT Ports (Mahe, Karaikal, Pondicherry, Yanam)\n16. Chennai — Not a Natural Harbour\n17. Natural vs Artificial Ports (Vizag/Cochin Natural, Chennai/Tuticorin Artificial)\n18. Kamarajar/Mundra/Vizag Port Facts\n19. Eastern Coast Ports Sequence (Tuticorin-Chennai-Machilipatnam-Vizag)\n20. Western Coast Ports Map (Veraval-Karwar-Tuticorin-Kakinada)\n21. Kakinada — Andhra Pradesh Port City\n22. Kolkata — India's Riverine Port (Hooghly River)\n23. Kandla — No LNG Terminal (6 LNG Ports Elsewhere)\n24. Kovalam — Three Crescent-Shaped Beaches\n25. Sethusamudram Shipping Canal — 167km\n26. Sethusamudram — Gulf of Mannar to Palk Bay\n27. Dahej — Non-Major Port (12 Major Ports Listed)\n28. Port-State Match (Kandla-Gujarat, Nhava Sheva-Maharashtra)\n29. Port-State Match (Alleppey-Kerala, Ennore-TN, Kakinada-AP)\n30. Krishnapatnam Port — Andhra Pradesh Beneficiary\n31. Mumbai — India's Biggest Port\n32. 13th Major Port — Vadhavan, Maharashtra\n33. National Waterway 1 — Ganga-Bhagirathi-Hooghly (Allahabad-Haldia)\n34. NW-1 Length — 1620 km, Longest in India (1986)\n35. Kottapuram-Kollam — Kerala Coastal Canal Waterway\n36. National Inland Navigation Institute — Patna\n37. 12th Major Coal Port — Ennore, Near Chennai\n38. Kandla — Gulf of Kutch Port (Post-Partition)\n39. Jamnagar — Not a Gujarat Port Town\n40. Bengaluru — Not a Harbour (Landlocked)\n41. Chennai — India's Open Seaport\n42. Haldia — 'Out Port' Example (Kolkata's Subsidiary)\n43. Shipyard-State Match (Garden Reach-WB, Hindustan-AP, Mazgaon-Maharashtra)"," 44. Garden Reach Diesel Engine Plant — Ranchi\n45. Cochin Airport — First Public Limited Company Airport\n46. Raja Sansi International Airport — Amritsar\n47. Karaikal — Eastern Coast (Not Western)\n48. Alang, Gujarat — India's Largest Ship Breaking Yard\n49. JNPT (Nhava Sheva) — Built to Decongest Mumbai Port (1989)\n50. Jawaharlal Nehru Port — Located in Maharashtra\n51. Rajasthan's Proposed Artificial Inland Port (Jalore)\n52. Bengaluru — Not a Harbour (Repeat)\n53. Mundra — Gujarat (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n54. Panna — Non-Operational Airport in MP\n55. MP International Airport Status — Disputed (All Domestic)\n56. Kushinagar Airport — International Status (June 2020)\n57. Air Transport in India — Started 1911 (Allahabad-Naini)\n58. Cochin Airport — First Solar-Powered Airport in India\n59. Cochin International Airport — World's First Fully Solar Airport\n1. Kochi Port — Malabar Coast\n●\nKochi sea-port (Kerala) Malabar Coast par sthith graceful natural harbour hai — poore saal use hota\nhai. [Q1]\n2. Tides — Navigation, Fishing, Siltation Prevention\n●\nTides ke sab 4 faayde sahi hain: navigation-fishing mein madadgar, high tide bade jahaz safely enter/exit\nkarne dete hain, siltation rokte hain, Kandla-Diamond Harbour tidal ports hain. [Q2]\n3. Cochin — India's Largest Shipyard\n●\nCochin Shipyard Limited (CSL) India ki major shipbuilding-maintenance facility hai — India ka sabse\nbada shipyard. [Q3, Q4]\n4. Tidal Ports Map — Kandla & Kolkata (Disputed)\n●\nMap ports: Kolkata-WB, Paradeep-Odisha, Cochin-Kerala, Kandla-Gujarat — Kandla aur Kolkata\ndono tidal ports hain (disputed question hai, single answer possible nahi). [Q5]\n5. Kandla — Gulf of Kutch Location\n●\nKandla (Deendayal) port Kandla Creek mein hai, Gulf of Kutch ke mouth se 90km door — protected\nnatural harbour hai, India ka pehla SEZ hai. [Q6, Q9]\n6. Chennai — Deep Port Myth (Actually Visakhapatnam)\n●\nCochin-Natural Port, JNPT-Mechanized Port, Kandla-Tidal Port sahi hain — 'Chennai-Deepest Port'\nGALAT hai (asal mein Visakhapatnam sabse gehra landlocked port hai). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — Visakhapatnam India ka sabse gehra port hai, Chennai NAHI\n⚠️\n7. Chennai — Artificial Port (Not Natural)"," ●\nChennai kritrim (artificial) port hai (1881 se commercial operations, India ka 3rd oldest major port) —\nMormugao, Mumbai, Kochi natural ports hain. [Q8]\n8. Kandla — Not on Eastern Coast\n●\nChennai, Paradip, Tuticorin eastern coast par hain — Kandla western coast (Gujarat) par hai, eastern\ncoast par NAHI. [Q9]\n9. Paradip — Decongests Kolkata & Vishakhapatnam\n●\nParadip port Kolkata aur Vishakhapatnam ports ka traffic kam karne ke liye develop kiya gaya —\nOdisha se Japan ko iron-ore export ke liye shuru hua tha. [Q10, Q11]\n10. Paradip — Located in Odisha\n●\nParadip Odisha mein sthith hai. [Q12]\n11. Paradip — India's Deepest Port\n●\nDiye gaye options mein Paradip India ka sabse gehra port hai (minimum depth se maximum vessel\nlength decide hoti hai). [Q13]\n12. Marmugao — Located in Goa\n●\nMarmugao seaport Goa mein sthith hai. [Q14]\n13. Port-State Match (Haldia-WB, Paradip-Odisha, Kandla-Gujarat, Marmugao-Goa)\n●\nSahi match: Haldia — West Bengal, Paradip — Odisha, Kandla (Deendayal) — Gujarat, Marmugao —\nGoa. [Q15]\n14. Kandla — Highest Import/Export Cargo Tonnage (2023-24)\n●\n2023-24 data ke mutabik Kandla port sabse zyada import+export cargo tonnage handle karta hai (India\nka main harbour). [Q16]\n15. Pondicherry UT Ports (Mahe, Karaikal, Pondicherry, Yanam)\n●\nPuducherry UT ke 4 sub-areas ke ports: Mahe, Karaikal, Pondicherry, Yanam — 1954 tak French rule tha.\n[Q17]\n16. Chennai — Not a Natural Harbour\n●\nChennai India ka sabse purana aur sabse bada artificial harbour hai — petroleum products, fertilizers,\niron-ore, general cargo handle karta hai. [Q18]\n17. Natural vs Artificial Ports (Vizag/Cochin Natural, Chennai/Tuticorin Artificial)\n●\nVishakhapatnam aur Cochin natural harbours hain — Chennai aur Tuticorin artificial ports hain. [Q19]\n18. Kamarajar/Mundra/Vizag Port Facts"," ●\nSahi facts: Kamarajar Port (ex-Ennore) India ka pehla company-registered major port hai, Mundra\nPort India ka sabse bada privately-owned port hai (Gujarat) — 'Vishakhapatnam largest container\nport hai' GALAT hai (Jawaharlal Nehru Port/Nhava Sheva India ka largest container port hai). [Q20]\n EXAM TRAP — JNPT (Nhava Sheva) India ka largest container port hai, Vishakhapatnam NAHI\n⚠️\n19. Eastern Coast Ports Sequence (Tuticorin-Chennai-Machilipatnam-Vizag)\n●\nEastern coast ports sequence: Tuticorin (TN), Chennai (TN), Machilipatnam (AP), Vishakhapatnam\n(AP). [Q21]\n20. Western Coast Ports Map (Veraval-Karwar-Tuticorin-Kakinada)\n●\nMap match: A-Veraval, B-Karwar, C-Tuticorin, D-Kakinada — Mangalore port Karnataka mein hai.\n[Q22]\n21. Kakinada — Andhra Pradesh Port City\n●\nKakinada Andhra Pradesh ka harbour city hai — Anchorage Port, Deep Water Port, Fishing Harbour,\nShip-Breaking Unit shamil hain. [Q23]\n22. Kolkata — India's Riverine Port (Hooghly River)\n●\nMap ke 4 ports: Kandla, Kochi, Paradip, Kolkata — Kolkata port riverine hai (Hooghly river ke\nkinare). [Q24]\n23. Kandla — No LNG Terminal (6 LNG Ports Elsewhere)\n●\nIndia ke 6 LNG terminals: Dahej, Hazira, Cochin, Dabhol, Ennore, Mundra — Kandla mein LNG\nterminal NAHI hai. [Q25]\n24. Kovalam — Three Crescent-Shaped Beaches\n●\n3 crescent-shaped beaches Kovalam (Kerala) mein milte hain. [Q26]\n25. Sethusamudram Shipping Canal — 167km\n●\nSethusamudram Shipping Canal Project (India-Sri Lanka ke beech shallow straits mein) 167 km lambi hai —\nPalk Strait (Bay of Bengal) ko Gulf of Mannar se jodta hai. [Q27]\n26. Sethusamudram — Gulf of Mannar to Palk Bay\n●\nSethusamudram project Gulf of Mannar ko Palk Bay se jodta hai — Indian peninsula ke around continuous\nnavigable route provide karta hai. [Q28]\n27. Dahej — Non-Major Port (12 Major Ports Listed)\n●\nDahej (Gulf of Khambhat, Bharuch, Gujarat) non-major port hai — India ke 12 major ports: Kolkata,\nParadip, Visakhapatnam, Chennai, Tuticorin, Kochi, New Mangalore, Marmugoa, Mumbai, JNPT\n(Nhava Sheva), Ennore (Kamarajar), Kandla (Deendayal). [Q29]"," 28. Port-State Match (Kandla-Gujarat, Nhava Sheva-Maharashtra)\n●\nMatch: Kandla (Deendayal) — Gujarat, Nhava Sheva — Maharashtra, Paradip — Odisha, Tuticorin\n(V.O. Chidambarnar) — Tamil Nadu. [Q30]\n29. Port-State Match (Alleppey-Kerala, Ennore-TN, Kakinada-AP)\n●\nMatch: Alleppey — Kerala, Ennore (Kamarajar) — Tamil Nadu, Paradip — Odisha, Kakinada —\nAndhra Pradesh. [Q31]\n30. Krishnapatnam Port — Andhra Pradesh Beneficiary\n●\nKrishnapatnam port se Andhra Pradesh ko sabse zyada faayda hoga (ye port AP mein hai). [Q32]\n31. Mumbai — India's Biggest Port\n●\nMumbai Port natural deep-water harbour hai, India ka sabse bada port (west coast par) — industrial\ndevelopment mein bada role tha. [Q33, Q34]\n32. 13th Major Port — Vadhavan, Maharashtra\n●\nIndia ka 13th major port Vadhavan (Maharashtra) mein banega — 'landlord model' par develop hoga.\n[Q35]\n33. National Waterway 1 — Ganga-Bhagirathi-Hooghly (Allahabad-Haldia)\n●\nGanga River ka Allahabad (Prayagraj) se Haldia tak ka hissa National Waterway-1 ghoshit hai. [Q36,\nQ37, Q38]\n34. NW-1 Length — 1620 km, Longest in India (1986)\n●\nNW-1 1986 mein establish hui — total length 1620 km, India ka sabse lamba internal waterway —\n'Haldia to Allahabad' hi sahi answer hai. [Q39]\n35. Kottapuram-Kollam — Kerala Coastal Canal Waterway\n●\nKottapuram se Kollam tak Kerala Coastal Canal (West Coast Canal) National Waterway hai — 1992 Act\nse declare hui. [Q40, Q41]\n36. National Inland Navigation Institute — Patna\n●\nNINI (National Inland Navigation Institute) Patna, Bihar mein IWAI (Inland Waterways Authority of\nIndia) ne setup ki. [Q42]\n37. 12th Major Coal Port — Ennore, Near Chennai\n●\nIndia ka 12th major coal-handling port Ennore (Chennai ke paas) mein bana — country ka pehla\nincorporated port hai. [Q43]\n38. Kandla — Gulf of Kutch Port (Post-Partition)"," ●\nKandla (Deendayal) Gulf of Kutch par sthith hai — 1950s mein Karachi port Pakistan mein chale jaane\nke baad Western India ke main seaport ke roop mein bana. [Q44]\n39. Jamnagar — Not a Gujarat Port Town\n●\nOkha, Porbandar, Alang, Bedi, Bhavnagar, Dahej, Jafarabad, Mandvi, Navlayi, Surat, Veraval Gujarat ke\nport towns hain — Jamnagar port town NAHI hai (Gulf of Kutch ke south mein sthith hai). [Q45]\n EXAM TRAP — Jamnagar — Gujarat ka port town NAHI hai (Kutch ki khaadi ke south mein sthith\n⚠️\nhai)\n40. Bengaluru — Not a Harbour (Landlocked)\n●\nKandla, Cochin, Mangalore eminent harbours hain — Bengaluru landlocked city hai, koi port NAHI.\n[Q46]\n41. Chennai — India's Open Seaport\n●\nOpen seaport (jahan jahaz khule paani mein coast karte hain, quays coast ke parallel bante hain) India mein\nChennai hai. [Q47]\n42. Haldia — 'Out Port' Example (Kolkata's Subsidiary)\n●\nHaldia port (Kolkata se 90km door) 'Out Port' ka specific example hai — deep water mein establish hota\nhai, main port ka subsidiary port hai. [Q48]\n43. Shipyard-State Match (Garden Reach-WB, Hindustan-AP, Mazgaon-Maharashtra)\n●\nMatch: Garden Reach — West Bengal, Hindustan Shipyard — Andhra Pradesh, Mazgaon Docks —\nMaharashtra, Cochin Shipyard — Kerala. [Q49]\n44. Garden Reach Diesel Engine Plant — Ranchi\n●\nGarden Reach Shipbuilders and Engineering Limited ka diesel engine plant Ranchi mein hai. [Q50]\n45. Cochin Airport — First Public Limited Company Airport\n●\nCochin Airport India ka pehla public-limited-company-owned airport hai — May 1999 mein K.R.\nNarayanan ne inaugurate kiya, June 1999 se commercial service — Nedumbassery mein hai, Kerala ka\nsabse busy/bada airport. [Q51]\n46. Raja Sansi International Airport — Amritsar\n●\nRaja Sansi International Airport (Sri Guru Ram Das Jee International Airport) Amritsar mein hai — Guru\nRam Das ke naam par. [Q52]\n47. Karaikal — Eastern Coast (Not Western)\n●\nDaman, Janjira, Ratnagiri western coast par hain — Karaikal eastern coast par hai (western coast par\nNAHI). [Q53]"," 48. Alang, Gujarat — India's Largest Ship Breaking Yard\n●\nAlang (Bhavnagar district, Gujarat) India ka sabse bada ship-breaking yard hai — world ke ~50% ship-\nsalvage yahan recycle hota hai. [Q54]\n49. JNPT (Nhava Sheva) — Built to Decongest Mumbai Port (1989)\n●\nJawaharlal Nehru Port (Nhava Sheva) 1989 mein Mumbai Port ka pressure kam karne ke liye banaya\ngaya. [Q55]\n50. Jawaharlal Nehru Port — Located in Maharashtra\n●\nJNP (Nhava Sheva Port) Maharashtra mein sthith hai. [Q56]\n51. Rajasthan's Proposed Artificial Inland Port (Jalore)\n●\nRajasthan Government Jalore mein artificial inland port develop karne ki soch rahi hai — Gujarat se\nArabian Sea ka paani laake — navigation channel 300m chaudi, 25m gehri hogi, Kori Creek (Lakpat) se\nRann of Kutch se hoke Jalore tak. [Q57]\n52. Bengaluru — Not a Harbour (Repeat)\n●\nCochin, Mangalore, Kandla harbours hain — Bengaluru harbour NAHI hai (landlocked) — India mein 12\nmajor aur ~200 non-major/intermediate ports hain. [Q58]\n53. Mundra — Gujarat (Not Andhra Pradesh)\n●\nMarmugao-Goa, Paradip-Odisha, Mangalore-Karnataka sahi hain — 'Mundra-Andhra Pradesh' GALAT\nhai (Mundra Gujarat mein hai). [Q59]\n EXAM TRAP — Mundra — Gujarat mein hai, Andhra Pradesh mein NAHI\n⚠️\n54. Panna — Non-Operational Airport in MP\n●\nKhajuraho, Jabalpur, Gwalior operational airports hain — Panna ka airport non-operational hai. [Q60]\n55. MP International Airport Status — Disputed (All Domestic)\n●\nBhopal, Indore, Khajuraho, Gwalior — sab domestic airports hain (koi international NAHI), isliye\nMPPSC ne is question ko delete kar diya. [Q61]\n56. Kushinagar Airport — International Status (June 2020)\n●\n24 June 2020 ko Union Cabinet ne Kushinagar Airport (UP) ko international status diya. [Q62]\n57. Air Transport in India — Started 1911 (Allahabad-Naini)\n●\nIndia mein air transport ki shuruaat 1911 mein Allahabad (Prayagraj) aur Naini ke beech flight se maani\njaati hai. [Q63]\n58. Cochin Airport — First Solar-Powered Airport in India"," ●\nCochin International Airport Ltd (CIAL) duniya ka pehla poori tarah solar-power se chalne wala airport\nhai (2015 mein achieve kiya). [Q64]\n59. Cochin International Airport — World's First Fully Solar Airport\n●\nCochin International Airport PPP model ke tahat develop hua India ka pehla airport hai — dedicated\nsolar plant ke saath world ka pehla fully-solar-powered airport bana. [Q65]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0068","t":"03.i States","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" STATES — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. City-State Location Facts (Latur, Vidarbha, Pat, Jhumri Telaiya)\n2. State Nicknames (Kohinoor, Silicon State, Scotland of East)\n3. Manipur — Topography & Phumdi\n4. City-State Match Pairs (Common Wrong Pairs)\n5. NCR (National Capital Region) — Included Districts\n6. J&K Map Places & Border-Touch Statements\n7. State Area Rankings — Largest & Smallest\n8. West-to-East City Sequences\n9. State Border-Sharing Facts\n10. Rajasthan Desert — Key Facts\n11. Special State Characteristics (Forest Cover, Seven Sisters)\n12. Andhra Pradesh — Capital History\n13. Districts — Largest by Count & Area\n14. State Capitals — Common Match Pairs & Traps\n15. Planned Capital Cities\n16. Madhya Pradesh — Border Facts\n17. Chhattisgarh — Geomorphological Region\n1. City-State Location Facts (Latur, Vidarbha, Pat, Jhumri Telaiya)\n●\nLocation facts yaad rakho: Latur — Maharashtra district; Vidarbha — Maharashtra ka north-eastern\nregion (Nagpur, Amravati divisions); Pat region — Jharkhand (Chotanagpur, high hill peaks); Jhumri\nTelaiya (radio-song-request wala famous city) — Jharkhand (Koderma district). [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. State Nicknames (Kohinoor, Silicon State, Scotland of East)\n●\nNicknames: Andhra Pradesh — 'Kohinoor of India' (Kollur mine se Kohinoor diamond mila);\nKarnataka — 'Silicon State of India' (Bengaluru India ki Silicon Valley hai); Shillong (Meghalaya) —\n'Scotland of the East'. [Q5, Q8, Q9, Q52]\n3. Manipur — Topography & Phumdi\n●\nManipur ki topography mostly mountainous hai (hills ~90% area, valleys ~10%). Loktak Lake mein floating\nislands ko 'Phumdi' kaha jaata hai — yahan endangered deer species Sangai paayi jaati hai. [Q6, Q7]\n4. City-State Match Pairs (Common Wrong Pairs)\n●\nSahi pairs: Palanpur — Gujarat, Hubli — Karnataka, Guntur — Andhra Pradesh, Aurangabad —\nMaharashtra (Aurangabad ab Chhatrapati Sambhaji Nagar hai). [Q10]\n●\n'Malnad' region Karnataka mein hai (Andhra Pradesh mein NAHI) — ye dense forest wala area hai. [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — Malnad — Karnataka mein hai, Andhra Pradesh ke saath galat pair kiya jaata hai\n⚠️"," 5. NCR (National Capital Region) — Included Districts\n●\nNCR mein currently: Delhi + Haryana sub-region (14 districts incl. Rohtak, Karnal) + U.P. sub-region (8\ndistricts) + Rajasthan sub-region (Alwar, Bharatpur). Khurja NCR ka hissa NAHI hai (wo U.P. ke\nBulandshahar district ka city hai) — Punjab bhi NCR ka hissa NAHI hai. [Q12, Q13]\n6. J&K Map Places & Border-Touch Statements\n●\nJ&K map labeling: Baramula → Srinagar → Anantnag → Kargil (typical A-B-C-D order). [Q15]\n●\nStatement facts (present-day): M.P. ki boundary 5 states ko touch karti hai (7 NAHI — 1993 mein 7 tha);\nBhopal Tropic of Cancer ke South mein hai (North mein NAHI); Punjab, J&K ki boundary ko touch\nkarta hai; Arunachal Pradesh mein 2 national parks hain (Mouling, Namdapha) — 'koi nahi' wala\nstatement GALAT hai. [Q16]\n7. State Area Rankings — Largest & Smallest\n●\nArea descending order (Census 2011): Rajasthan (3,42,239) > Madhya Pradesh (3,08,252) > Maharashtra\n(3,07,713) > Uttar Pradesh (2,40,928) > Andhra Pradesh-post-bifurcation (1,60,205) > Karnataka\n(1,91,791) > Tamil Nadu (1,30,060) > Bihar (94,163). Top 3 states (Rajasthan, MP, Maharashtra) India ke\ntotal area ka ~30% cover karte hain. [Q17, Q18, Q19, Q21, Q22, Q24]\n●\nSmall-hill-states area order: Chhattisgarh (1,35,192) > Jharkhand (79,716) > Himachal Pradesh (55,673)\n> Uttarakhand (53,483, sabse chhota in is set). [Q23, Q25]\n●\nPopulation vs Area rank mismatch: Maharashtra — population mein 2nd, area mein 3rd; Bihar —\npopulation mein 3rd, area mein 12th. [Q20, Q26]\n8. West-to-East City Sequences\n●\nWest-to-east cities: Bikaner (Rajasthan) → Aligarh (U.P.) → Darbhanga (Bihar) → Nagaon (Assam).\n[Q14]\n9. State Border-Sharing Facts\n●\nUttar Pradesh 8 states + 1 UT (Delhi) ko touch karta hai — Punjab NAHI (common wrong option); sahi list:\nUttarakhand, Himachal, Haryana, Rajasthan, M.P., Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Bihar. UP sabse zyada states ko\ntouch karta hai poore India mein. [Q27, Q49]\n●\nAssam 7 states se ghira hai (WB, Nagaland, Mizoram, Meghalaya, Arunachal, Manipur, Tripura) — koi UT\nnahi. Chhattisgarh Bihar se border NAHI karta (Bihar galat option hai; sahi border-states: UP, MP, Odisha,\nJharkhand, AP, Maharashtra, Telangana). [Q28, Q29]\n●\nSouth India border-sharing comparison: Karnataka sabse zyada states (6: AP, Telangana, Maharashtra,\nGoa, Kerala, TN) ko touch karta hai — Kerala sirf 2 (Karnataka, TN), Tamil Nadu 3 (Kerala, Karnataka,\nAP) ko touch karte hain. [Q38]\n●\nTelangana Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Chhattisgarh se border karta hai. [Q39]\n●\nSonbhadra district (U.P.) 4 states (M.P., Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Bihar) ki boundary touch karta hai —\nMirzapur se 1989 mein separate hua tha. [Q37]"," ●\nMadhya Pradesh Uttar Pradesh se sabse lambi border share karta hai (baaki borders: Chhattisgarh,\nMaharashtra, Gujarat, Rajasthan) — Jharkhand M.P. ki boundary touch NAHI karta (common wrong\noption). [Q50, Q53]\n10. Rajasthan Desert — Key Facts\n●\nRajasthan ka desert duniya ka sabse dense-populated desert hai (density 83/sq km) — ~10,000 saal purana,\nsirf 40-60% area hi farming ke liye suitable hai. Irrigation development ki wajah se net-sown-area badhne\nse grazing land coverage par ulta effect pada hai. [Q30, Q31]\n●\nCities' sea-level altitude comparison: Bengaluru (~920m) sabse ooncha hai — Delhi, Jodhpur, Nagpur se\nzyada (options mein diye jaane par). [Q30]\n11. Special State Characteristics (Forest Cover, Seven Sisters)\n●\nYe characteristics Arunachal Pradesh ki hain: 28°N latitude (Northern Rajasthan ke saath same), ~80%\narea forest cover ke andar, ~12%+ forest Protected Area Network ka hissa. [Q32]\n●\n'Seven Sisters' North-East states: Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Meghalaya, Manipur, Mizoram, Nagaland,\nTripura — West Bengal isme SHAMIL NAHI hai (common wrong-option trap). [Q33]\n12. Andhra Pradesh — Capital History\n●\nAndhra state ki history: Potti Shriramulu ne 1952 mein fast-unto-death kiya separate linguistic-state ke\nliye → 1953 mein Kurnool pehli capital bani → 1956 mein Hyderabad capital bani → 2014 bifurcation ke\nbaad Amaravati de facto capital hai (Hyderabad 10 saal tak dono states ki de jure capital rahegi). [Q34]\n13. Districts — Largest by Count & Area\n●\nSabse zyada districts wala state Uttar Pradesh (75 districts, as of March 2025) hai — M.P. (55), Tamil\nNadu (38), Maharashtra (36) se zyada. [Q35]\n●\nArea ke hisaab se sabse bada district Kutch/Kachchh, Gujarat (45,674 sq km) hai — order: Kutch > Leh\n(45,100) > Jaisalmer (38,401) > Barmer (28,387). [Q36]\n14. State Capitals — Common Match Pairs & Traps\n●\nNortheast state-capital pairs (common confusion traps): Assam — Dispur (Shillong NAHI), Meghalaya —\nShillong (Kohima NAHI), Mizoram — Aizawl, Nagaland — Kohima (Guwahati NAHI), Arunachal\nPradesh — Itanagar, Manipur — Imphal (Aizawl NAHI). [Q40, Q45, Q47, Q48]\n EXAM TRAP — Manipur ki capital Imphal hai, Aizawl NAHI (Aizawl Mizoram ki capital hai) — bahut\n⚠️\ncommon confusion\n●\nBaaki common capitals: Gujarat — Gandhinagar, Rajasthan — Jaipur (Pink City, Hawa Mahal). [Q41,\nQ42]\n●\nItanagar — Arunachal Pradesh ki capital hai. Telangana India ka 29th state hai, capital Hyderabad (J&K\nreorganisation ke baad ab India mein 28 states hain). [Q43, Q44]\n15. Planned Capital Cities"," ●\nPlanned capital cities: Chandigarh, Bhubaneswar, Gandhinagar — Bengaluru planned city NAHI hai\n(organically grow hua tha). [Q46]\n16. Madhya Pradesh — Border Facts\n●\nM.P. current borders: Uttar Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Maharashtra, Gujarat, Rajasthan (5 states) —\nlongest border U.P. ke saath hai. [Q50, Q53]\n17. Chhattisgarh — Geomorphological Region\n●\nChhattisgarh India ke 'Peninsular Upland' geomorphological region ke andar aata hai — Northern\nplain/mountain ya Coastal plain mein NAHI. [Q51]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0069","t":"03.ii Union Territories","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" UNION TERRITORIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Number of Union Territories & List\n2. Largest & Smallest UT by Area\n3. Puducherry — 4 Unconnected Districts\n4. State vs UT Confusion Traps\n5. Daman & Diu — History & Geography\n6. Dadra and Nagar Haveli — Silvassa Capital\n7. NCR — Which States Are/Aren't Included\n1. Number of Union Territories & List\n●\nIndia mein currently 28 states aur 8 Union Territories hain (jab question pucha gaya tha tab 7 UTs the —\nJ&K-Ladakh split ke baad 8 ho gaye). 8 UTs: NCT Delhi, Chandigarh, Lakshadweep, Dadra & Nagar\nHaveli and Daman & Diu, Puducherry, Andaman-Nicobar, Jammu & Kashmir, Ladakh. [Q1]\n2. Largest & Smallest UT by Area\n●\nArea ke hisaab se Ladakh ab sabse bada UT hai (26 January 2020 se). Uske pehle diye jaane wale options\nmein Delhi sabse bada tha (1483 sq km) — Puducherry (490), Chandigarh (114), Daman-Diu (111) se\nzyada. Delhi population mein bhi sabse bada UT hai. [Q2]\n●\nIndia ka sabse chhota UT Lakshadweep hai — area 32 sq km, population ~64,473. [Q3]\n3. Puducherry — 4 Unconnected Districts\n●\nPuducherry UT ke 4 chhote, unconnected districts hain: Yanam (Andhra Pradesh se ghira), Puducherry\n(Tamil Nadu se ghira), Karaikal (Tamil Nadu se ghira), Mahe (Kerala se ghira) — isliye Puducherry ka\narea Tamil Nadu, Kerala aur Andhra Pradesh in teen states mein divide hai. [Q4]\n4. State vs UT Confusion Traps\n●\nCommon trap questions: Tripura ek STATE hai, UT NAHI (Bangladesh se 3 taraf ghira hai) — Daman-\nDiu, Lakshadweep, Puducherry sab UTs hain. Isi tarah Goa India ka sabse chhota state hai (area ke hisaab\nse) — Lakshadweep, Dadra-Nagar Haveli, Chandigarh sab UTs hain, states nahi. [Q5, Q9]\n EXAM TRAP — Tripura state hai UT nahi; Goa state hai (sabse chhota), UT nahi\n⚠️\n5. Daman & Diu — History & Geography\n●\nDaman & Diu do parts mein bata tha: Daman (Maharashtra-Gujarat ke Arabian Sea coast par) aur Diu\n(Saurashtra, Gujarat coast) — inke beech Gulf of Khambhat hai, capital Daman thi. Ye Portuguese ke\nunder tha (British ke NAHI) 1961 mein liberation tak — Portuguese ne ise Gujarat ke Shah se hasil kiya\ntha. [Q6]"," 6. Dadra and Nagar Haveli — Silvassa Capital\n●\nDadra and Nagar Haveli (ab Dadra & Nagar Haveli and Daman & Diu ka hissa) west coast ke paas hai —\nDadra Gujarat se ghira hai, Nagar Haveli Maharashtra-Gujarat border par hai. Capital Silvassa hai.\n[Q7, Q8]\n7. NCR — Which States Are/Aren't Included\n●\nNCR (National Capital Region) Delhi ke around ek central planning region hai — isme Delhi (poora NCT),\naur Haryana, Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan ke aas-paas ke districts shamil hain. Madhya Pradesh NCR ka\nhissa NAHI hai (common trap). [Q10]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0070","t":"30 Tourism","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" TOURISM — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Hill Station-State Match Sets\n2. Tourist Centre-State Match (Udvada, Point Calimere, Gulmarg, Kasauli)\n3. 'Nick-Name' City Match Set (Jaipur-Pink, Udaipur-Lakes)\n4. UNESCO World Heritage Sites (Champaner, CST Mumbai, Mamallapuram, Konark)\n5. 'Pink City' — Jaipur\n6. Tirupati Temple — Seshachalam Range\n7. Kerala — 'Garden of Spices'\n8. Buddhist Population Concentration (Maharashtra, Sikkim, WB)\n9. Sabarimala — Kerala's Pilgrimage Site\n10. Ghost Towns of India (Kuldhara, Dhanushkodi, Lakhpat)\n11. Pilgrimage-Hills Match (Srisailam, Omkareshwar, Pushkar)\n12. Grassland/Hill Station Match (Banni, Bugyal, Khajjiar, Pahalgam)\n1. Hill Station-State Match Sets\n●\nResort-state match: Chakrata — Uttarakhand (Dehradun district, Tiger Fall), Haflong — Assam (Dima\nHasao, Assam ka ekmatra hill station), Kalimpong — West Bengal, Kufri — Himachal Pradesh\n(Shimla district). [Q1]\n2. Tourist Centre-State Match (Udvada, Point Calimere, Gulmarg, Kasauli)\n●\nState-tourist-centre match: Udvada — Gujarat (Zoroastrian Fire Temple), Point Calimere — Tamil\nNadu (Coromandel Coast ka apex), Gulmarg — J&K, Kasauli — Himachal Pradesh (Solan district).\n[Q2]\n3. 'Nick-Name' City Match Set (Jaipur-Pink, Udaipur-Lakes)\n●\nTourist-site match: Keylong — Himachal Pradesh, Auli — Uttarakhand, Chikmagalur — Karnataka,\nOoty — Tamil Nadu. Nickname match: Jaipur-Pink City, Ujjain-Mahakal ki nagri, Kolkata-City of Joy\nsahi hain — 'Jaisalmer-City of Lakes' GALAT hai (Udaipur City of Lakes hai). [Q3, Q6]\n EXAM TRAP — City of Lakes — Udaipur hai, Jaisalmer NAHI\n⚠️\n4. UNESCO World Heritage Sites (Champaner, CST Mumbai, Mamallapuram, Konark)\n●\nUNESCO World Heritage sites: Champaner-Pavagarh Archaeological Park (Gujarat, 2004),\nChhatrapati Shivaji Terminus (Mumbai, ex-Victoria Terminus), Mamallapuram (Mahabalipuram, TN,\n1984), Konark Sun Temple (Odisha, 1984) — sab 4 sahi hain. [Q4]\n5. 'Pink City' — Jaipur\n●\nJaipur ko 'Pink City' aur 'Paris of India' kaha jaata hai — Rajasthan ki capital hai. [Q5]\n6. Tirupati Temple — Seshachalam Range"," ●\nLord Venkateswara Temple (Tirupati, Andhra Pradesh) Seshachalam mountain range mein hai —\nShevaroy (Salem, TN), Biligiriranga (Karnataka-TN border), Javadhee (TN) sab galat options the\n(question disputed hai — 'Mallmalla' spelling ka Nallamala se confusion). [Q7]\n7. Kerala — 'Garden of Spices'\n●\nKerala ko 'Garden of Spices' kaha jaata hai — black pepper, cardamom, cinnamon, cloves, ginger, nutmeg\nke liye famous. [Q8]\n8. Buddhist Population Concentration (Maharashtra, Sikkim, WB)\n●\n2011 Census ke mutabik Maharashtra mein sabse zyada Buddhist population (77.36%, 5.8 million) hai\n— Maharashtra, Sikkim, West Bengal ka set sabse zyada concentration wala hai. [Q9]\n9. Sabarimala — Kerala's Pilgrimage Site\n●\nSabarimala Kerala ke Pathanamthitta district, Periyar Tiger Reserve mein hai — Lord Ayyappa ko\ndedicated Sri Dharmasastha Temple famous hai. [Q10]\n10. Ghost Towns of India (Kuldhara, Dhanushkodi, Lakhpat)\n●\nGhost towns: Kuldhara, Dhanushkodi, Lakhpat — Charkhari (Mahoba, UP) ghost town NAHI hai —\n'Kashmir of Bundelkhand' kehlata hai. [Q11]\n11. Pilgrimage-Hills Match (Srisailam, Omkareshwar, Pushkar)\n●\nSahi pair: Srisailam — Nallamala Hills (Kurnool, AP; ek jyotirlinga) — Omkareshwar (Narmada river\nmein Mandhata island, MP) 'Satmala Hills' se GALAT match hai, Pushkar (Ajmer, Aravalli Hills)\n'Mahadeo Hills' se GALAT match hai. [Q12]\n12. Grassland/Hill Station Match (Banni, Bugyal, Khajjiar, Pahalgam)\n●\nMatch: Banni Grassland — Gujarat, Bugyal Grassland — Uttarakhand, Khajjiar — Himachal\nPradesh, Pahalgam — Jammu & Kashmir. [Q13]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0071","t":"31 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MISCELLANEOUS - 1 — FULL MIND MAP\n📌\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Biogas — Provides Both Power and Manure\n2. Speed Post — Launched 1986\n3. India's Global Rankings (Fertilizer, Steel, Coal — Historical & Current)\n4. India — 3rd Largest Fertilizer Producer/Consumer\n5. Locusts — Enter India from Pakistan\n6. BARC — Maharashtra (Not Karnataka)\n7. Mumbai's Specialized Towns (Alibag-Resort, Nhava Sheva-Port)\n8. Chandipur, Odisha — Vanishing Sea Beach\n9. Thumba — Geomagnetic Equator Location\n10. Himalayan Mountaineering Institute — Darjeeling\n11. Agricultural University Mismatches (IGAU-Chhattisgarh, Not Rajasthan)\n12. Cairn Energy HQ — Scotland\n13. Pilgrimage-State Match (Rameshwaram-TN, Dwarka-Gujarat, Sarnath-UP)\n14. Stadium-City Match (Aish Bagh-Bhopal, Eden Gardens-Kolkata)\n15. Kolkata Metro — India's First Underground Railway\n16. Diamond Harbour & Salt Lake City — Kolkata\n17. Dindigul — City in Tamil Nadu\n18. Green Highway Policy 2015 — Tree Plantation\n19. Kutch — Water Resources (Not Forest)\n20. Moradabad — Not Related to Sarees (Brass City)\n21. M.S. Swaminathan — Agriculture (Not Geology)\n22. Jangal Mahal — West Bengal\n23. Apsara — India's First Nuclear Reactor (1956)\n24. Telephone in India — Disputed Origin Date\n25. Lasundra Hot Spring — Gujarat (Not Rajasthan)\n26. Mizoram/Manipur Traditions (Chapchar Kut, Khongjom Parba, Thang-Ta)\n27. Craft Heritage — Puthukkuli Shawls (Tamil Nadu Only)\n28. Himalayan Nettle — Sustainable Textile Fibre Source\n29. Rajasthan Dust Storms — Convectional Currents (May-June)\n1. Biogas — Provides Both Power and Manure\n●\nBiogas (organic matter ke breakdown se bina oxygen ke banti hai) power aur manure dono provide karti\nhai — agricultural waste, manure, sewage se banti hai. [Q1]\n2. Speed Post — Launched 1986\n●\nIndian Postal Department ne Speed Post Service August 1986 mein shuru ki — courier service ke\ncompetition mein, time-bound express delivery ke liye. [Q2]\n3. India's Global Rankings (Fertilizer, Steel, Coal — Historical & Current)"," ●\nQuestion ke waqt India nitrogenous fertilizers ka 3rd largest, steel ka 9th largest producer tha — ab\n(Indian Minerals Yearbook 2022) India coal-lignite mein China ke baad 2nd largest, crude steel mein bhi\n2nd largest producer hai. [Q3]\n4. India — 3rd Largest Fertilizer Producer/Consumer\n●\nIndia duniya mein fertilizer ka 3rd largest producer AUR consumer hai. [Q4]\n5. Locusts — Enter India from Pakistan\n●\nLocusts (tiddiyaan) Pakistan se India mein prawesh karti hain. [Q5]\n6. BARC — Maharashtra (Not Karnataka)\n●\nSriharikota-AP, Thumba-Kerala, Pokhran-Rajasthan sahi hain — 'Bhabha Atomic Research Centre-\nKarnataka' GALAT hai (BARC Maharashtra mein hai, Trombay, Mumbai). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP — BARC (Bhabha Atomic Research Centre) — Maharashtra (Trombay, Mumbai) mein\n⚠️\nhai, Karnataka mein NAHI\n7. Mumbai's Specialized Towns (Alibag-Resort, Nhava Sheva-Port)\n●\nMumbai ke aas-paas specialized towns: Alibag — Holiday Resort, Balapur — Petro-chemical Complex,\nNhava Sheva — Fully Mechanized Port, Ratnagiri — Fishing Centre. [Q7]\n8. Chandipur, Odisha — Vanishing Sea Beach\n●\nChandipur (Odisha) ka unique phenomenon: samudra ka paani tatrekha se kilometers peeche jaata hai\naur din mein 2 baar wapas aata hai (ebb tide ke dauraan) — logo ko samudra-tal par chalne deta hai.\n[Q8]\n9. Thumba — Geomagnetic Equator Location\n●\nVikram Sarabhai Space Centre Thumba (Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala) mein hai — geomagnetic\nequator ke paas hone ki wajah se select hua — INCOSPAR ne 1963 mein TERLS establish kiya. [Q9]\n10. Himalayan Mountaineering Institute — Darjeeling\n●\nHimalayan Mountaineering Institute (HMI) Darjeeling, West Bengal mein hai. [Q10]\n11. Agricultural University Mismatches (IGAU-Chhattisgarh, Not Rajasthan)\n●\nJawaharlal Nehru Krishi Vishwavidyalaya-MP sahi hai — Indira Gandhi Krishi Vishwavidyalaya (IGAU)\nChhattisgarh (Raipur) mein hai, Rajasthan mein NAHI; Acharya NG Ranga Agriculture University\nAndhra Pradesh mein hai, Telangana mein NAHI — dono statements galat hone se disputed question hai.\n[Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — IGAU — Chhattisgarh (Raipur) mein hai, Rajasthan mein NAHI\n⚠️\n12. Cairn Energy HQ — Scotland"," ●\nCairn (ab Capricorn Energy) ka HQ Edinburgh, Scotland mein hai — world ki leading oil-gas exploration\ncompanies mein se ek. [Q12]\n13. Pilgrimage-State Match (Rameshwaram-TN, Dwarka-Gujarat, Sarnath-UP)\n●\nMatch: Rameshwaram — Tamil Nadu, Dwarka — Gujarat, Sarnath — Uttar Pradesh (Varanasi),\nMahakal Temple — Madhya Pradesh (Ujjain). [Q13]\n14. Stadium-City Match (Aish Bagh-Bhopal, Eden Gardens-Kolkata)\n●\nMatch: Aish Bagh Stadium — Bhopal, Brabourne Stadium — Mumbai, Green Park — Kanpur, Eden\nGardens — Kolkata. [Q14]\n15. Kolkata Metro — India's First Underground Railway\n●\nKolkata Metro India ki pehli underground metro railway hai — Ratnagiri — mangoes, Aligarh — locks,\nDehradun — rice ke liye famous hain. [Q15]\n16. Diamond Harbour & Salt Lake City — Kolkata\n●\nDiamond Harbour aur Salt Lake City Kolkata (West Bengal) mein sthith hain. [Q16]\n17. Dindigul — City in Tamil Nadu\n●\nDindigul Tamil Nadu ka ek shehar/district hai — Haider Ali ne France ki madad se yahan modern arsenal\nbanwaya tha. [Q17]\n18. Green Highway Policy 2015 — Tree Plantation\n●\nGreen Highway (Plantation, Transplantation, Beautification, Maintenance) Policy 2015 ka objective tree\nplantation hai — sab highways ke kinare, environment aur local employment ke liye. [Q18]\n19. Kutch — Water Resources (Not Forest)\n●\nKolhan-Mineral Resources, Malabar Coast-Water Resources, Middle Ganga Plain-Soil Resources sahi hain\n— 'Kutch-Forest Resources' GALAT hai (Kutch mein water resources prachur hain, forest NAHI).\n[Q19]\n20. Moradabad — Not Related to Sarees (Brass City)\n●\nChanderi, Banarasi, Kanjivaram saree ke liye famous hain — Moradabad ('Peetal Nagri') brass-glassware\nke liye famous hai, sarees se NAHI. [Q20]\n21. M.S. Swaminathan — Agriculture (Not Geology)\n●\nManmohan Singh-Economics, Kalam-Aeronautics, D.S. Kothari-Physics sahi hain — 'M.S. Swaminathan-\nGeology' GALAT hai (agriculture/Green Revolution se related hain, geology se NAHI). [Q21]\n22. Jangal Mahal — West Bengal\n●\nJangal Mahal West Bengal mein hai — Naxalite activities ki wajah se news mein raha. [Q22]"," 23. Apsara — India's First Nuclear Reactor (1956)\n●\nIndia ka pehla nuclear reactor 'Apsara' hai — August 1956 mein BARC, Trombay, Mumbai mein\noperational hua. [Q23]\n24. Telephone in India — Disputed Origin Date\n●\n1850 mein Calcutta-Diamond Harbour ke beech experimental telegraph shuru hua — 1881 mein Oriental\nTelephone Company ne Calcutta/Bombay/Madras/Ahmedabad mein exchanges khole, 28 Jan 1882 ko\npehli formal telephone service establish hui — diye gaye options mein se koi sahi nahi hai, disputed\nquestion hai. [Q24]\n25. Lasundra Hot Spring — Gujarat (Not Rajasthan)\n●\nAvloli-Maharashtra, Manikaran-Himachal Pradesh, Sohna-Haryana sahi hain — 'Lasundra-Rajasthan'\nGALAT hai (Lasundra hot spring Gujarat mein hai). [Q25]\n EXAM TRAP — Lasundra hot spring — Gujarat mein hai, Rajasthan mein NAHI\n⚠️\n26. Mizoram/Manipur Traditions (Chapchar Kut, Khongjom Parba, Thang-Ta)\n●\nChapchar Kut festival — Mizoram (March mein, 'Jhoom' ke baad celebrate), Khongjom Parba ballad —\nManipur sahi hain — Thang-Ta dance bhi Manipur ki tradition hai, Sikkim ki NAHI. [Q26]\n27. Craft Heritage — Puthukkuli Shawls (Tamil Nadu Only)\n●\nPuthukkuli shawls — Tamil Nadu (Nilgiri hills ke Todas banate hain, 'Pugur' kehte hain) sahi hai — Sujni\nembroidery Bihar (Bhusura village) ki hai, Maharashtra ki NAHI; Uppada Jamdani sari Andhra\nPradesh (East Godavari) ki hai, Karnataka ki NAHI. [Q27]\n28. Himalayan Nettle — Sustainable Textile Fibre Source\n●\nHimalayan Nettle (Girardinia diversifolia, Himalaya-Hindukush region ka plant) textile fibre ka sustainable\nsource hai — HP, Uttarakhand, J&K, NE states mein milta hai. [Q28]\n29. Rajasthan Dust Storms — Convectional Currents (May-June)\n●\nRajasthan mein May-June ke dust storms kuch jagahon par convectional currents ki origin se hote hain\n(sirf statement 1 sahi) — Aravalli hills-southwest winds parallel aur fast easterly winds galat reasons hain.\n[Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0072","t":"04 Species-Tribes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" SPECIES/TRIBES — FULL MIND MAP\n🧑🏽‍🤝‍🧑🏽\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tribe-State Match Pairs (Jarawa, Kukki, Tharu, Gond)\n2. Racial Groups — Mongoloid, Proto-Australoid, Dravidian\n3. Only Anthropoid Ape of India — Hoolock Gibbon\n4. States With No Scheduled Tribes\n5. Tharu Tribe — Diwali as Mourning Festival\n6. Gaddi Tribe — Dhauladhar Range\n7. World Deserts — Odd Pair Trap (Kalahari)\n8. Santhal — Region, Marriage Customs\n9. Transhumance — Bhotia Tribe\n10. Bodo & Garo Tribes — Assam-Meghalaya\n11. Tribes Found/Not Found in Kerala\n12. Largest Tribe of India (Bhil vs Gond — Census Year Trap)\n13. Toda Tribe — Nilgiri Hills & Polyandry\n14. Ho Tribe — Marriage Forms (Andi, Oportipi)\n15. Sarhul Festival & Oraon's Ghumkaria\n16. Largest Scheduled Tribe of Uttarakhand\n17. Mizoram Settlement Pattern — Linear Along Ridges\n18. Tribe-State Disputed Match Pairs (Bhotia/Bhotiya Confusion)\n19. State Festival Match Pairs (Onam-Kerala, Sikkim Language)\n20. Bhil Tribe — Region & Match Pairs\n21. Polyandry-Practicing Tribes (Jaunsari, Toda)\n22. Common Tribe-State Match Sets (Repeated Pattern)\n23. Sahariya Tribe — Rajasthan PVTG\n24. MP Regional Tribes — District Match Pairs\n25. Tribal Population Distribution — Central vs NE India\n26. Middle-India Tribes vs South-India Tribes (Kadar Trap)\n27. Changpa Community — Ladakh, Pashmina Goats\n28. Wrong-Pair Traps (Korwa-Kodagu, Lambada-MP, Zulu-Odisha)\n29. Andaman-Nicobar Native Tribes (Onge, Shompen, Jarawa)\n30. Most Primitive Tribe of India — Jarawa\n31. Manganiyars — Musical Tradition of Rajasthan\n32. PVTGs (Primitive Vulnerable Tribal Groups) of Jharkhand\n33. Jhum/Shifting Cultivation & Occupational Tribes\n34. Common Tribe-State Match Sets (Gaddi, Toda, Khasi, Naga)\n35. Chhattisgarh Tribal Practices (Bhunjia, Kamar, Baiga)\n36. Tribal Sub-Castes & Occupational Names\n37. Tribe-State Wrong-Pair Traps (Toda-Kerala, Khas-Arunachal)\n38. Bharmour — Gaddi Homeland in Himachal\n39. Deity Worship & Reformers (Lohasur, Gahira Guru)\n40. Kaathi — Folk Dance (Not a Tribe)\n41. Final Disputed Match Set (Kuki, Yanadi, Palliyan)\n42. Tribe-State Pair Verification (Limbu-Sikkim, Dongaria Kondh-Odisha)\n43. Tribe Determination Basis — Cultural Specification & Isolated Habitation\n1. Tribe-State Match Pairs (Jarawa, Kukki, Tharu, Gond)"," ●\nSahi tribe-state match: Jarawas — Andaman and Nicobar, Kukkis — Manipur, Tharus — Uttar\nPradesh (Terai), Gonds — Madhya Pradesh (Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Odisha\nmein bhi hain). Jarawas, Sentinelese aur Onges — sab Andaman-Nicobar ki main tribes hain. [Q1]\n●\nMatch pairs mein Munda ko ab 'original Bihar tribe' nahi maana jaata — wo mainly Jharkhand, Odisha,\nWest Bengal mein hai. Tharu — Uttarakhand sahi pair hai (Bhutia-UP aur Kol-Rajasthan GALAT hain).\n[Q8]\n2. Racial Groups — Mongoloid, Proto-Australoid, Dravidian\n●\n'Yellow complexion, oblique eyes, high cheekbones, sparse hair, medium height' — ye Mongoloids ki\ndescription hai (originally America ke inhabitants the, ab NE aur SE Asia mein hain). North-east India ke\npahadi/jangli areas mein Mongoloid race milti hai. [Q2, Q3]\n●\nSanthal, Bhil, Yeruva jaisi major tribes Proto-Australoid (pre-Dravidian) race se hain. [Q4]\n●\nDravidian races mainly South India tak limited hain (Tamil, Kannada, Malayalam, Telugu language family\nse related) — central/southeast India mein bhi kuch milti hain. [Q5]\n3. Only Anthropoid Ape of India — Hoolock Gibbon\n●\nIndia ka ekmatra anthropoid ape 'White-browed Gibbon' (Hoolock Gibbon) hai — Assam (north-east\nregion) mein paaya jaata hai. [Q6]\n4. States With No Scheduled Tribes\n●\n2011 census ke anusaar Punjab, Haryana, Chandigarh, NCT Delhi, Puducherry mein koi bhi Scheduled\nTribe identified NAHI hai. [Q7]\n5. Tharu Tribe — Diwali as Mourning Festival\n●\nTharu tribe (Uttarakhand ke Nainital se lekar U.P.-Bihar ke Terai tak) Hinduism follow karti hai aur saare\nfestivals manati hai — lekin Diwali ko apne poorvajon (ancestors) ki yaad mein shok/mourning ke roop\nmein manate hain — ye ek repeatedly-asked fact hai. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n●\nTharu tribe Uttarakhand aur Uttar Pradesh (Bihar bhi) mein rehti hai — Uttarakhand ki sabse badi\ntribe hai (2011 census). [Q12, Q13]\n6. Gaddi Tribe — Dhauladhar Range\n●\nGaddi tribe Himachal Pradesh ki Dhauladhar Range (Kangra, Chamba districts) mein rehti hai — ek\nsemi-nomadic, pastoral tribe hai. [Q15, Q16]\n7. World Deserts — Odd Pair Trap (Kalahari)\n●\nDesert-continent match: Gobi-Mongolia, Thar-India, Sahara-Africa sahi hain — Kalahari-America\nGALAT hai (Kalahari actually Africa mein hai — Botswana, Namibia, South Africa). [Q17]\n8. Santhal — Region, Marriage Customs"," ●\nSanthals Eastern India (West Bengal, Bihar, Jharkhand, Odisha, Tripura) ke original inhabitants hain —\nChhattisgarh se match karna GALAT hai (common wrong-pair trap). [Q18, Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Santhal — Jharkhand/West Bengal/Odisha se match hota hai, Chhattisgarh se NAHI\n⚠️\n●\nSanthals mein shaadi ko 'Bupla' kaha jaata hai — iske types hote hain: Sanga Bupla, Kirin Bupla, Itut Bupla,\nNir Bolok Bupla. [Q20]\n9. Transhumance — Bhotia Tribe\n●\n'Transhumance' (\n —\nऋतुप्रवास\nseasonal migratory pastoralism) Bhotias (Uttarakhand ke pahadi region) dwara\npractice ki jaati hai — Bhoksa, Jaunsari, Tharu sab permanent settlers hain (transhumance NAHI karte).\n[Q21]\n10. Bodo & Garo Tribes — Assam-Meghalaya\n●\nBodo tribe Garo Hills region (Assam-Meghalaya) mein rehti hai. Garo tribe mainly Meghalaya mein hai,\npar Assam, Nagaland, WB, Tripura, Mizoram mein bhi significant population hai — isliye single-option\nmatch karna disputed ho jaata hai. [Q22, Q23]\n●\nKhasi aur Garo language-speaking population mainly Meghalaya mein hai — Assam mein bhi milti hai\n(isliye dono options technically sahi ho sakte hain). [Q24]\n11. Tribes Found/Not Found in Kerala\n●\nChenchu tribe mainly Andhra Pradesh-Telangana (Nallamala area) mein hai — Kerala ki native tribe\nNAHI mani jaati (Lepcha-Sikkim, Dafla-Arunachal, Dafar-Gujarat — inme se koi bhi Kerala se related nahi\nhai, isliye ye question disputed hai). [Q25]\n12. Largest Tribe of India (Bhil vs Gond — Census Year Trap)\n●\nIndia ki sabse badi tribe — 2011 census ke anusaar Bhil (1,70,71,049 population) hai. Purane exams\n(2000-2013 se pehle) mein Gond ko sabse badi tribe maana jaata tha — agar options mein 'Bhil' na ho, to\n'Gond' sahi answer ban jaata hai. [Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n EXAM TRAP — Bhil ab sabse badi tribe hai (2011 census) — Gond dusre number par; purane exams\n⚠️\nmein Gond hi sahi tha\n13. Toda Tribe — Nilgiri Hills & Polyandry\n●\nToda tribe Nilgiri Hills (Tamil Nadu) mein rehti hai — khud ko Aryans ke vanshaj maante hain, aur\ntraditionally fraternal polyandry practice karte hain (ek mahila poore parivar ke saare bhaiyon se shaadi\nkarti hai). [Q30, Q31, Q33, Q40]\n14. Ho Tribe — Marriage Forms (Andi, Oportipi)\n●\n'Andi' aur 'Oportipi' marriage forms Ho tribe se related hain — Andi = negotiation se shaadi, Oportipi =\ncapture (apharan) se shaadi. [Q32]\n15. Sarhul Festival & Oraon's Ghumkaria"," ●\nSarhul Festival Jharkhand ki Oraon, Munda, Santhal, Ho tribes manati hain — Chaitra-Jeth (June)\nmahine mein, naye saal ki shuruaat ka pratik, ped-poojan is festival ki khaasiyat hai. [Q34, Q35]\n●\n'Ghumkaria' (ya Dhumkuria) — Oraon tribe ka 'youth dormitory' social institution hai, jahan youth ko social-\ncultural-religious training di jaati hai. [Q36]\n16. Largest Scheduled Tribe of Uttarakhand\n●\nUttarakhand ki sabse badi Scheduled Tribe Tharu (91,342 — 2011 census) hai — Jaunsari (88,664) dusre\nnumber par hai (purane 2005-era exams mein Jaunsari ko sabse badi maana jaata tha). [Q37]\n17. Mizoram Settlement Pattern — Linear Along Ridges\n●\nMizoram mein settlements zyadatar ridges (pahaadi shikharon) ke saath linear pattern mein hote hain —\nkyunki raat ko thandi hawa neeche valleys mein utarti hai (temperature inversion), isliye valleys ridges\nse zyada thandi aur kam rehne-layak ho jaati hain. [Q38]\n18. Tribe-State Disputed Match Pairs (Bhotia/Bhotiya Confusion)\n●\n'Bhotia' aur 'Bhutia' do alag spellings/tribes ka confusion hota hai — Bhotia/Bhotiya — Uttar\nPradesh/Uttarakhand mein hai (sahi), jabki Bhutia — Sikkim/West Bengal mein hai. Isi wajah se kayi\nmatch-pair questions disputed ban jaate hain. [Q39, Q43]\n EXAM TRAP — Bhotia (UP/Uttarakhand) aur Bhutia (Sikkim/WB) — spelling milta-julta hai par alag\n⚠️\ntribes hain\n19. State Festival Match Pairs (Onam-Kerala, Sikkim Language)\n●\nFestival-state match: Bihu-Assam, Pongal-Tamil Nadu, Baisakhi-Punjab sahi hain — Onam-Kerala hai,\nAndhra Pradesh NAHI (common wrong-pair). [Q41]\n●\nSikkim ki main languages Nepali, Sikkimese (Bhutia), Lepcha hain — 'Tibetan' Sikkim ki main language\nNAHI hai (common wrong-pair). [Q42]\n20. Bhil Tribe — Region & Match Pairs\n●\nBhil tribe Rajasthan, M.P., Gujarat, Maharashtra (western-central India) mein failii hui hai — exam\noptions mein jo bhi in states mein se ek diya jaaye, sahi answer ban sakta hai (Rajasthan sabse zyada associate\nkiya jaata hai). [Q44]\n21. Polyandry-Practicing Tribes (Jaunsari, Toda)\n●\nPolyandry practice karne wali tribes: Jaunsari (Uttarakhand) aur Toda (Tamil Nadu, Nilgiri Hills) —\nGonds aur Nagas polyandry NAHI karte. [Q45]\n22. Common Tribe-State Match Sets (Repeated Pattern)\n●\nBahut baar dohraya jaane wala match-set: Birhor — Jharkhand, Bhutia — Sikkim, Toda — Tamil Nadu,\nSentinelese — Andaman-Nicobar, Lepcha — Sikkim, Garo — Meghalaya. [Q47, Q48]"," ●\nDusra common set: Tharu — UP/Uttarakhand, Bhil — Rajasthan, Gaddi — Himachal Pradesh, Munda\n— Jharkhand, Jarawa — Andaman-Nicobar. [Q49, Q50]\n●\nTeesra set: Jaunsari — Uttarakhand, Santhal — Jharkhand, Bhil — Madhya Pradesh, Lepcha —\nSikkim. [Q52]\n●\nChautha set (Rajasthan-Sikkim wala): Bhil — Rajasthan (ya M.P.), Raji — Uttarakhand, Lepcha —\nSikkim, Santhal — Jharkhand. [Q46]\n23. Sahariya Tribe — Rajasthan PVTG\n●\nSahariya tribe (PVTG — Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Group) Rajasthan ke Baran district (aur M.P. ke\nkuch hisson) mein rehti hai — severe malnutrition aur starvation deaths ki wajah se news mein rahi hai.\n[Q51]\n24. MP Regional Tribes — District Match Pairs\n●\nMadhya Pradesh ke tribe-district match pairs: Pahadi Korwa — Jashpur, Baiga — Mandala,\nBharia/Maria — Patalkot (Chhindwara), Sahariya — Gwalior division. [Q54]\n●\nEk aur MP set: Chhindwara — Bharia, Mandala — Gond, Jhabua — Bhil, Shivpuri — Sahariya. [Q63]\n●\nAnya region-tribe match: Moplah — Kerala (Muslim community, tribe nahi), Murias — Bastar\n(Chhattisgarh), Todas — Tamil Nadu, Mundas — Odisha/Jharkhand. [Q55, Q56]\n25. Tribal Population Distribution — Central vs NE India\n●\nIndia ki 80%+ tribal population Central India (MP, Maharashtra, Odisha, Gujarat, Rajasthan,\nJharkhand, Chhattisgarh) mein rehti hai — North-East India sirf ~11-12% tribal population ka hissa\nhai (aadhi se zyada NAHI) — ye ek common misconception/trap hai. Constitution mein Scheduled Tribe ki\nkoi explicit definition nahi hai. [Q57]\n26. Middle-India Tribes vs South-India Tribes (Kadar Trap)\n●\nMiddle (Central) India ki tribes: Baiga, Muria, Kharia — Kadar middle-India ki tribe NAHI hai (Kerala-\nTamil Nadu ke pahadi ilaakon mein hai — South India). [Q58]\n27. Changpa Community — Ladakh, Pashmina Goats\n●\nChangpa community Ladakh ke Changthang region (semi-nomadic Tibetan people) mein rehti hai —\nUttarakhand mein NAHI (common wrong statement). Ye Changthangi (Pashmina) goats palte hain jinse\nrare Pashmina wool milti hai, aur 1989 mein officially Scheduled Tribe recognize kiye gaye the. [Q59]\n28. Wrong-Pair Traps (Korwa-Kodagu, Lambada-MP, Zulu-Odisha)\n●\nCommon wrong-pairs: Korwa (Korba) — Jharkhand/Chhattisgarh se related hai, Kodagu (Karnataka)\nse NAHI; Lambada (Banjara) — Andhra Pradesh/Telangana/Maharashtra/Karnataka mein hai,\nMadhya Pradesh se traditionally NAHI jodi jaati; Zulu — South Africa ki tribe hai, Odisha (India)\nmein NAHI. [Q60, Q61, Q62]"," EXAM TRAP — Zulu (South Africa), Lambada (AP/Telangana/Maharashtra/Karnataka), Korwa\n⚠️\n(Jharkhand/Chhattisgarh) — teeno common wrong-pair traps hain\n29. Andaman-Nicobar Native Tribes (Onge, Shompen, Jarawa)\n●\nAndaman-Nicobar ki native tribes: Onge, Shompen, Halchu — Rengma isme SHAMIL NAHI hai (ye ek\nNaga tribe hai, Nagaland-Assam mein). [Q64]\n●\nOnge tribe Little Andaman Island ke west mein rehti hai. Shompen tribe Great Nicobar Island ke interior\nmein rehti hai (2011 census population sirf 229). [Q65, Q66]\n●\nJarawa tribe South aur Middle Andaman Islands mein rehti hai — Supreme Court ne tourists ko Jarawa\nareas mein jaane se ban kiya tha unki suraksha ke liye. Jarawa Nicobar Island mein NAHI hain (common\ntrap — Jarawa South/Middle Andaman mein hain, Nicobar mein nahi). [Q67, Q68]\n30. Most Primitive Tribe of India — Jarawa\n●\nIndia ki sabse primitive (aadim) tribe 'Jarawa' hai — Andaman-Nicobar mein paayi jaati hai, unhone\nbahari logon se interaction largely reject kiya hai aur traditional hunter-gatherer lifestyle maintain kiya hai.\nJarawa South aur Middle Andaman mein rehti hai (Nicobar mein exam-commission ne kabhi-kabhi accept\nkiya hai as closest option, lekin technically South/Middle Andaman sahi hai). [Q68, Q69, Q70]\n31. Manganiyars — Musical Tradition of Rajasthan\n●\nManganiyars ek Muslim community hai Rajasthan ke registan (North-West India) mein — apni classical\nfolk musical tradition ke liye famous hai. Pakistan ke Sindh province (Tharparkar, Sanghar districts) mein\nbhi paaye jaate hain. [Q71]\n32. PVTGs (Primitive Vulnerable Tribal Groups) of Jharkhand\n●\nJharkhand ke 9 PVTGs: Asur, Birhor, Birajia, Korwa, Pahadi Khariya, Parahiya (Baiga), Sabar, Mal\nPahariya, Souriya Pahariya — Korwa inme se ek hai (Kawar, Kora, Karmali PVTG list mein NAHI hain).\n[Q72]\n33. Jhum/Shifting Cultivation & Occupational Tribes\n●\nJhoom (shifting/slash-and-burn) cultivation Khasi tribe (Meghalaya) dwara practice ki jaati hai. [Q73]\n●\nOccupation-based tribe names: Khairwar — 'Catechu/Kattha' (Hindi mein 'Khair') banate hain; Kamar\ntribe — traditional livelihood 'Bamboo' (basket-making) par based hai; Bhunjia tribe — 'Lal Bangala'\nnaam ki sacred red-clay-painted kitchen rakhte hain; Ojha (Badni, Dewar bhi) — tattoo/godna banane\nwali tribes hain; Agaria — iron-smelting occupation, 'Lohasur' devta ki pooja karte hain. [Q74, Q79,\nQ80, Q83, Q90]\n●\nBaiga tribe (Chhattisgarh ki sabse zyada population wali PVTG) 'Bilama dance' karte hain, khaaskar\nVijayadashami (Dussehra) ke time. [Q81, Q82]\n●\n'Gahira Guru' (asli naam Swami Rameshwar Kanwar) Kanwar tribe se the — ek social reformer jinhone\nspirituality failaakar tribal world ko badla. [Q91]\n34. Common Tribe-State Match Sets (Gaddi, Toda, Khasi, Naga)"," ●\nRepeated match-set: Gaddis — Himachal Pradesh, Todas — Tamil Nadu, Khasis — Meghalaya, Naga\n— Manipur/Nagaland region. [Q78]\n●\nHalam aur Notiya (Noatia) tribes Tripura mein mainly paayi jaati hain. [Q77]\n●\nKudukh (Kurukh) dialect — Dravidian family ki bhasha — Oraon tribe bolti hai. [Q76]\n●\nCommon repeated set: Santhals — Jharkhand, Bhil — Rajasthan, Toda — Tamil Nadu, Jarawas —\nAndaman-Nicobar. [Q75]\n●\nAur ek set: Bhils — Rajasthan, Gonds — Chhattisgarh, Limboos — Sikkim, Konyak — Nagaland.\n[Q87]\n35. Chhattisgarh Tribal Practices (Bhunjia, Kamar, Baiga)\n●\nChhattisgarh mein sabse zyada population wali primitive tribal group Baiga hai — Abujhmadia, Kamar,\nPahadi Korwa se zyada. [Q81]\n36. Tribal Sub-Castes & Occupational Names\n●\nTribe-subcaste sahi pairs: Gond — Agariya (Pradhan, Ojha bhi), Baiga — Bijhwar (Nahar bhi) —\nPateliya Bhil ki subcaste hai, Bharia ki NAHI; Mahar ek Scheduled Caste hai, Korku ki subcaste NAHI\n(dono galat pairs hain). [Q84]\n EXAM TRAP — Pateliya — Bhil ki subcaste hai (Bharia ki nahi); Mahar — Scheduled Caste hai (Korku\n⚠️\nki subcaste nahi)\n37. Tribe-State Wrong-Pair Traps (Toda-Kerala, Khas-Arunachal)\n●\nCommon wrong-pair traps: Todas — Tamil Nadu mein hain (Kerala mein NAHI); Khas (Khasa) tribe —\nUttarakhand, Himachal Pradesh, J&K mein hai (Arunachal Pradesh mein NAHI). [Q85, Q88]\n38. Bharmour — Gaddi Homeland in Himachal\n●\nBharmour tribal region Chamba district, Himachal Pradesh mein hai — mainly Gaddi community ka ghar\nhai. [Q86]\n39. Deity Worship & Reformers (Lohasur, Gahira Guru)\n●\nTamaria tribe Jharkhand (aur Odisha) mein paayi jaati hai — Bhumij tribe ki subcaste maani jaati hai, ab\nJharkhand mein Munda tribe ke paryay ke roop mein Scheduled Tribe list mein shamil hai. [Q89]\n40. Kaathi — Folk Dance (Not a Tribe)\n●\n'Kaathi' ek folk dance/folk theatre form hai (tribe ya caste NAHI) — Madhya Pradesh ke Nimar region mein\nBalahi Harijan community ka festival hai, Maa Parvati ki pooja ke liye. [Q92]\n41. Final Disputed Match Set (Kuki, Yanadi, Palliyan)\n●\nEk disputed match set: Kuki North-East India mein hai (UP mein NAHI), Yanadi Andhra Pradesh mein\nhai (Rajasthan mein NAHI) — dono galat pairs hain. Kharia (spelled 'Keria') Odisha mein hai, Palliyan\nTamil Nadu mein hai — spelling ambiguity ki wajah se ye question disputed maana jaata hai. [Q93]"," 42. Tribe-State Pair Verification (Limbu-Sikkim, Dongaria Kondh-Odisha)\n●\nSahi pairs: Limbu — Sikkim (WB/Nepal/Bhutan/Tibet mein bhi), Dongaria Kondh — Odisha —\n'Karbi-Himachal Pradesh' GALAT hai (Karbi mainly Assam mein hai), 'Bonda-Tamil Nadu' bhi\nGALAT hai (Bonda Odisha mein hai). [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP — Karbi tribe — Assam mein hai, Himachal Pradesh mein NAHI; Bonda tribe — Odisha\n⚠️\nmein hai, Tamil Nadu mein NAHI\n43. Tribe Determination Basis — Cultural Specification & Isolated Habitation\n●\nIndia mein Scheduled Tribe ke roop mein kisi community ko determine karne ka aadhar cultural\nspecification aur alag (isolated) habitation hai — primitive traits, distinctive culture, geographical\nisolation, community se contact mein sharm, backwardness jaise criteria follow hote hain. [Q53]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0073","t":"05 Languages","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" LANGUAGES — FULL MIND MAP\n🗣️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tribal Languages — Halbi, Ho, Kui\n2. Most Spoken Indian Language After Hindi — Bengali\n3. Largest Linguistic Group — Indo-Aryan\n4. Austric (Austro-Asiatic) Language Group\n5. North India Dialect Map (Braj, Awadhi, Bhojpuri, Maithili)\n6. Classical Language Status — Timeline\n1. Tribal Languages — Halbi, Ho, Kui\n●\n'Halbi, Ho aur Kui' teeno tribal languages hain — Halbi: Bastar (Chhattisgarh) mein bolte hain (Rajmuria,\nHalba, Mahar, Parja, Lohra tribes), Odisha se Maharashtra tak failii hai; Ho (Munda family): West\nSinghbhum (Jharkhand) mein main area, Ho-Munda-Koi tribes bolte hain; Kui (Dravidian family):\nKandhamal (Odisha) mein Kui tribe bolti hai. [Q1]\n2. Most Spoken Indian Language After Hindi — Bengali\n●\nHindi ke baad duniya mein sabse zyada boli jaane wali Indian language Bengali hai — globally ~272.8\nmillion users (Ethnologue 2023 ke mutabik). Ye fact poore India mein bhi aur poore Indian subcontinent\nmein bhi sahi hai. [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n3. Largest Linguistic Group — Indo-Aryan\n●\nIndia ka sabse bada linguistic group Indo-Aryan hai — isme Hindi, Bengali, Gujarati, Marathi, Punjabi,\nSindhi, Rajasthani, Assamese, Odiya, Kashmiri, Urdu, Sanskrit jaise saari major languages shamil hain.\nDravidian, Sino-Tibetan, Austro-Asiatic comparatively chhote groups hain. [Q5]\n4. Austric (Austro-Asiatic) Language Group\n●\nAustric (Austro-Asiatic) group ki languages: Khasi, Santhali, Mundari, Bhumij — sab Indian tribes dwara\nboli jaati hain. Marathi, Ladakhi, Tamil is group mein NAHI aate (Marathi Indo-Aryan, Ladakhi Sino-\nTibetan, Tamil Dravidian family ki hain). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP — Khasi Austric group mein hai — Marathi, Ladakhi, Tamil alag families ki hain\n⚠️\n5. North India Dialect Map (Braj, Awadhi, Bhojpuri, Maithili)\n●\nNorth India map-labeling (typical A-B-C-D order, west-se-east): Brajbhasha → Awadhi → Bhojpuri →\nMaithili (North Bihar ka area). [Q7]\n6. Classical Language Status — Timeline\n●\nClassical language status timeline yaad rakho: Tamil (2004) → Sanskrit (2005) → Telugu aur Kannada\n(2008) → Malayalam (2013) → Odiya (2014, 6th language). Odiya ko 20 Feb 2014 ko ye status mila tha.\n[Q8]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0074","t":"06.i Ganga Drainage System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" GANGA DRAINAGE SYSTEM — FULL MIND\n🌊\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Ganga — Drainage Type & Bangladesh Names\n2. Sunderban Delta — World's Largest\n3. Ganga Pollution — Assertion-Reason\n4. Gangetic Alluvial Soil Depth\n5. Panch Prayag — All 5 Confluences\n6. Source of Ganga — Gaumukh, Gangotri, Bhagirathi\n7. Alaknanda Tributaries — Dhauliganga, Mandakini\n8. Length Comparisons — Ganga vs Other Rivers\n9. Left-Bank Tributaries — Gomti, Ghaghara, Gandak, Kosi\n10. Yamuna — Origin & Right-Bank Tributaries\n11. Chambal-Betwa-Ken System\n12. Son River — Right-Bank, Northward Flow\n13. Ganga Sub-Basin Tributaries (Damodar, Koel, Sankh)\n14. Ganga in Bihar — Districts & Length\n15. Moribund Delta & Bengal Delta Stages\n16. Kosi Plain — Elevation & Course\n17. Dendritic Drainage Pattern\n1. Ganga — Drainage Type & Bangladesh Names\n●\nGanga river Antecedent Drainage ka example hai. Bangladesh mein pravesh karne ke baad Ganga ko\n'Padma' naam se jaana jaata hai — yahan Brahmaputra (jise Jamuna kehte hain) isse milti hai, phir Meghna\nriver se milkar Bay of Bengal mein girti hai. Total length 2525 km hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. Sunderban Delta — World's Largest\n●\nSunderban Delta Ganga, Brahmaputra aur Meghna teeno se milkar banta hai — duniya ka sabse bada\ndelta hai. Iska do-tihai hissa Bangladesh mein hai, baaki India mein. [Q5]\n3. Ganga Pollution — Assertion-Reason\n●\nGanga ek highly polluted river hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin iska reason 'pavitrata' NAHI hai (Reason\ngalat). Asli reason: shehri kshetron se aane wala high organic-load waste pollution ka root cause hai. [Q6]\n4. Gangetic Alluvial Soil Depth\n●\nGangetic alluvial soil ki depth: Oldham ke anusaar 4000-6000 meter, Glany ke anusaar ~2000 meter —\nexam options mein 6000 meter sahi maana jaata hai. [Q7]\n5. Panch Prayag — All 5 Confluences"," ●\nPanch Prayag (5 sacred confluences), source se confluence tak order mein: Vishnuprayag (Vishnu Ganga +\nDhauliganga = Alaknanda banti hai) → Nandprayag (Alaknanda + Nandakini) → Karnaprayag\n(Alaknanda + Pindar) → Rudraprayag (Alaknanda + Mandakini) → Devprayag (Alaknanda +\nBhagirathi = Ganga banti hai). Isi tarah Tehri mein Bhagirathi + Bhilangna ka sangam hota hai. [Q9, Q10,\nQ11, Q12, Q13, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18]\n EXAM TRAP — Nandprayag ka sangam Alaknanda-Nandakini se hai — Vishnu Ganga-Mandakini se\n⚠️\nNAHI (common UPSC trap)\n●\nDevprayag ka literal matlab 'pavitra sangam' hai — Adi Shankaracharya ne Joshimath (Badrinath ke\npaas) ko badi peeth sthapit ki thi, Kedarnath ko NAHI (Kedarnath unka samadhi sthal hai, ye ek common\nwrong-statement trap hai). [Q8]\n●\nBadrinath Temple Alaknanda ke kinare hai, Kedarnath Temple Mandakini ke kinare hai — dono alag rivers\nke kinare, common confusion. [Q19]\n6. Source of Ganga — Gaumukh, Gangotri, Bhagirathi\n●\nBhagirathi river Gaumukh (Gangotri Glacier, Uttarkashi district) se nikalti hai — Shivalinga peak se 18\nkm door. Ye Central aur Lesser Himalaya ko cut karke behti hai, aur Devprayag mein Alaknanda se milkar\n'Ganga' ban jaati hai. [Q15, Q22]\n7. Alaknanda Tributaries — Dhauliganga, Mandakini\n●\nEastern Dhauliganga Kali river ki tributary hai (Alaknanda ki NAHI) — Kali river Lipulekh Pass ke paas\nKalapani se nikalti hai, iski major tributaries Gori, Saryu, Lohavati, Ladhiya hain. [Q14]\n●\nMandakini river Chorabari Taal (Kedarnath ke paas) se nikalti hai, Sonprayag mein Vasukiganga/Son\nGanga se milti hai, aur Rudraprayag mein Alaknanda se milti hai. [Q13, Q18]\n8. Length Comparisons — Ganga vs Other Rivers\n●\nIndia ki sabse lambi behne wali river Ganga (2525 km) hai — Godavari (1465 km) > Narmada (1312 km)\n> Mahanadi (851 km) se zyada, aur Brahmaputra ya Indus se bhi zyada lambi (India mein flowing length\nke basis par). [Q20, Q21]\n9. Left-Bank Tributaries — Gomti, Ghaghara, Gandak, Kosi\n●\nSirf ek tributary jo plains se nikalti hai — Gomti (Gomat Taal/Fulhar Lake, Pilibhit, U.P. se). Prayagraj ke\ndownstream, west-se-east order: Gomti (Ghazipur mein milti hai) → Ghaghara (Saran, Bihar) →\nGandak (Sonepur, Bihar) → Kosi (Katihar, Bihar) — sab left-bank tributaries hain, jo 11 states ko drain\nkarti hain. [Q23, Q24, Q33, Q34]\n●\nGandak river ko Nepal mein 'Narayani' ya 'Gandaki' bhi kehte hain — do streams (Kaligandak +\nTrishulganga) se milkar bani hai, Dhaulagiri-Everest ke beech Nepal Himalaya se nikalti hai. [Q37]\n10. Yamuna — Origin & Right-Bank Tributaries\n●\nYamuna river Yamunotri Glacier (Bandar Poonch Peak ke paas) se nikalti hai — Delhi-Agra ke beech\nsaal ke zyadatar hisse mein 'dead river' ban jaati hai (Assertion sahi), lekin iska reason perennial nahi hona"," NAHI hai (Yamuna asal mein perennial river hai) — real cause domestic aur industrial waste discharge\nhai. [Q25, Q27]\n11. Chambal-Betwa-Ken System\n●\nYamuna ki tributaries, west-se-east order: Chambal → Sindh → Betwa → Ken. Chambal M.P. ke Dr.\nAmbedkar Nagar (purana naam Mhow) se nikalti hai, Rajasthan (Sawai Madhopur, Dholpur) se hokar\nYamuna mein milti hai. [Q28]\n●\nSon (Ganga ki tributary) Yamuna mein NAHI girti — Chambal, Betwa, Ken sab Yamuna ki tributaries hain,\nSon inme se ek NAHI hai (common trap). [Q26, Q29]\n●\nBetwa river Vindhyan Hills se nikalti hai, Hamirpur (U.P.) ke paas Yamuna mein milti hai — Chambal ki\ntributary NAHI hai (ye Yamuna ki alag tributary hai, Chambal mein nahi milti). [Q30, Q31, Q32]\n12. Son River — Right-Bank, Northward Flow\n●\nSon river (Amarkantak, M.P. se nikalti hai) Ganga ki main right-bank tributary hai jo North ki taraf\nbehti hai — Patna ke paas Ganga mein milti hai; baaki left-bank tributaries South ki taraf behti hain. Kaimur\nRange Son (south) aur Tons/Yamuna-tributary (north) ke beech watershed banati hai. Son ka catchment area\n(~70,055 sq km) sabse zyada hai (Gandak, Ramganga, Mahananda se). [Q33, Q34, Q35, Q36]\n13. Ganga Sub-Basin Tributaries (Damodar, Koel, Sankh)\n●\nGanga river basin ke sub-rivers: North Koel (Son ki tributary), Barakar (Damodar ki main tributary,\nKoderma Plateau se nikalti hai) — dono Ganga basin ka hissa hain. South Koel aur Sankh, Brahmani\nriver system ka hissa hain (Ganga basin ka NAHI) — Damodar, Hooghly se milkar lower Ganga basin ka\nsub-basin banata hai. [Q39]\n●\nGanga basin mein NAHI: Jonk river Mahanadi ki tributary hai (Odisha-Chhattisgarh) — Punpun, Ajoy,\nJalangi sab Ganga basin ka hissa hain. [Q42]\n●\nGandak river U.P. se NAHI guzarti — Nepal se seedhe Bihar mein aati hai. Son, Hindon, Sharda rivers\nU.P. se guzarti hain. [Q43]\n●\nPunpun river Chota Nagpur Plateau (Jharkhand) se nikalti hai, Aurangabad (Bihar) se hoke Fatuha\n(Patna) mein Ganga se milti hai. [Q44]\n14. Ganga in Bihar — Districts & Length\n●\nGanga Bihar ke 12 districts se guzarti hai — Saran, Buxar, Bhojpur, Patna, Vaishali, Samastipur, Begusarai,\nLakhisarai, Munger, Khagaria, Bhagalpur, Katihar. Inme sabse zyada length Patna (~99 km) mein hai —\nBhagalpur (~97 km) dusre number par. [Q40, Q41]\n15. Moribund Delta & Bengal Delta Stages\n●\nBengal Delta ke 4 stages hain: Moribund (south-west, Jessore-Kushtia-Faridpur, highly-silted oxbow\nlakes) → Immature (Moribund ke south, Sundarbans yahin hai) → Mature (Bangladesh ke southern\ncentral section) → Active (Meghna delta, Bay of Bengal mein, regular flooding aur 'chars'). [Q38]"," 16. Kosi Plain — Elevation & Course\n●\nKosi Plain (triangular, Bihar mein, lower Ganga plain ka hissa) — opening Birpur (54m, Nepal border) par\nhai, base Khagaria (36m) se Kursela (25m) tak Ganga ke parallel jaata hai, average elevation 30-40m\n— general slope northwest se southeast. [Q45, Q46]\n17. Dendritic Drainage Pattern\n●\nGanga plains aur Assam Valley mein Dendritic drainage pattern milta hai — wide plains, gentle slopes,\nheavy rain, bahut saari tributaries ki characteristic. Ye pattern un areas mein develop hota hai jahan\nunderlying rocks mein koi specific structure nahi hoti, isliye streams sab directions mein evenly failti hain.\n[Q47]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0075","t":"06.ii Brahmaputra Drainage System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" BRAHMAPUTRA DRAINAGE SYSTEM — FULL\n🏔️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The 'U' Turn — Syntaxial Bending\n2. Names in Different Regions (Yarlung Zangbo, Tsangpo, Dihang)\n3. Mansarovar Lake — Common Source of 3 Rivers\n4. Rivers Through Arunachal Pradesh (Lohit, Subansiri, Barak)\n5. Major Tributaries (Manas, Dibang, Kameng)\n6. Catchment Area & Countries\n7. Majuli — World's Largest Riverine Island\n8. Teesta River — Origin, Rangeet & River Capture\n9. Tibetan Plateau — Common Origin Point (Brahmaputra & Indus)\n1. The 'U' Turn — Syntaxial Bending\n●\nBrahmaputra (Irrawaddy aur Mekong ke saath) Tibet ki ek sankri jagah se nikalti hai, aur India mein aane ke\nliye ek 'U' turn leti hai. Ye turn geologically young Himalaya ke syntaxial bending ki wajah se hota hai —\nArunachal Pradesh ki eastern limit par ek hairpin-jaisa mod hai jahan mountains east se south trend mein\nsharply mudte hain. [Q1]\n2. Names in Different Regions (Yarlung Zangbo, Tsangpo, Dihang)\n●\nBrahmaputra alag-alag regions mein alag naam se jaana jaata hai: Tibet mein Yarlung Zangbo / Tsangpo\n(ya Sanpu), Arunachal Pradesh mein Dihang, Assam mein Brahmaputra, Bangladesh mein Jamuna.\n[Q2, Q6]\n3. Mansarovar Lake — Common Source of 3 Rivers\n●\nTibet ki Mansarovar Lake ke paas Brahmaputra, Satluj aur Indus — teeno rivers ka source hai. [Q3]\n4. Rivers Through Arunachal Pradesh (Lohit, Subansiri, Barak)\n●\nArunachal Pradesh se guzarne wali rivers: Lohit aur Subansiri (dono Brahmaputra ki tributaries) — Barak\nriver Arunachal se NAHI guzarti (Manipur Hills se nikalti hai, Manipur-Nagaland-Assam border se guzarti\nhai). [Q4]\n5. Major Tributaries (Manas, Dibang, Kameng)\n●\nBrahmaputra ki major tributaries: Manas, Tista, Kameng, Subansiri, Dhansari, Burhi Dihing, Dibang,\nKopili, Sankosh, Jiabharali, Lohit — sab teeno (Dibang, Kameng, Lohit) sahi tributaries hain (koi trap nahi\nis set mein). [Q5, Q10]\n6. Catchment Area & Countries\n●\nBrahmaputra ka catchment area Tibet (China), Bangladesh, India, aur Bhutan mein failaa hai. [Q7]"," 7. Majuli — World's Largest Riverine Island\n●\nMajuli, duniya ka sabse bada inhabited riverine island, Brahmaputra river dwara banaya gaya hai. [Q8]\n●\nNote: Is chapter mein ek off-topic mineral-related question (Karnataka manganese-producing areas) bhi\nshaamil tha, jo drainage-system se related nahi tha — isliye is mindmap mein exclude kiya gaya. [Q9]\n8. Teesta River — Origin, Rangeet & River Capture\n●\nTeesta river Khangchung Chho glacial lake (Sikkim) se 'Chhonbo Chhu' naam se nikalti hai (~5280m\naltitude) — Brahmaputra ke saath same source NAHI hai (Brahmaputra ka source Angsi Glacier, Tibet\nhai). Rangeet river Sikkim se nikalti hai aur Teesta ki tributary hai (ye statement SAHI hai). Teesta\nSikkim-West Bengal se hoke Bangladesh mein Brahmaputra se milti hai, phir Bay of Bengal mein girti hai —\nseedhe India-Bangladesh border par Bay of Bengal mein NAHI girti. [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — Teesta ka source Brahmaputra jaisa nahi hai — dono alag glaciers se nikalti hain\n⚠️\n●\nHistorically Teesta river Ganga ki tributary thi, ab Brahmaputra ki tributary hai — ye 'river capturing'\n(nadi apaharan) ki wajah se hua, jo Himalayan rivers ki ek major feature hai (river capturing valley\ndevelopment ke youthful stage mein zyada active hota hai, lekin mature/senile stages mein bhi ho sakta hai).\n[Q13]\n9. Tibetan Plateau — Common Origin Point (Brahmaputra & Indus)\n●\nTibetan Plateau ('Roof of the World', average elevation 4500m+) se nikalne wali rivers: Yangtze, Huang He,\nMekong, Indus, Satluj, Brahmaputra, Salween — isliye Brahmaputra aur Indus ka almost same\nstarting point hai (Tapi-Beas ya Ganga-Brahmaputra ka NAHI). [Q12]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0076","t":"06.iii The South Indian Rivers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" THE SOUTH INDIAN RIVERS — FULL MIND\n🌊\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. West-Flowing Peninsular Rivers — Why No Delta (Rift Valley)\n2. Narmada — Origin, Course & Basin Districts\n3. Son River — Origin Dispute (Amarkantak vs Sonmuda)\n4. Tapi/Tapti — Origin, Course & Purna Tributary\n5. Cauvery — Origin, Islands & 'Ganga of the South'\n6. Krishna River — Origin & Interstate Dispute\n7. River Length Rankings (Godavari > Krishna > Narmada > Mahanadi)\n8. River Linking Project & West-Flowing Trio\n9. North-to-South Sequence of East-Flowing Rivers\n10. Estuary-Forming Rivers vs Delta-Forming Rivers\n11. Catchment Area & Basin Size Comparisons\n12. Mahanadi — Origin, Course & Tributaries\n13. Godavari — 'Dakshin Ganga', Basin & Tributaries\n14. Chambal & Rift-Valley Tributaries (Yamuna System)\n15. Subarnarekha & Chotanagpur Rivers\n16. Chhattisgarh Regional Rivers — Origin Match Pairs\n17. Physiographic Division (S.P. Chatterjee)\n18. Cross-Reference — Khartoum, Sudan (Nile Confluence)\n19. South Indian Rivers — Dendritic Drainage Pattern\n1. West-Flowing Peninsular Rivers — Why No Delta (Rift Valley)\n●\nWestern Ghats se nikalne wali rivers delta NAHI banati kyunki wo kathor chattanon (hard rocks) par\nshort course mein high speed se behti hain (Assertion-Reason dono sahi hain, R sahi explanation hai). [Q1]\n●\nPeninsular India ki zyadatar major rivers Bay of Bengal mein girti hain — sirf Narmada aur Tapi Arabian\nSea mein girti hain, kyunki ye dono rift valley mein behti hain (plateau ke slope ko follow nahi karti). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP — Narmada west kyun behti hai — 3 reasons diye jaate hain par options mein combo trap\n⚠️\nhota hai\n●\nNarmada west kyun behti hai (jabki baaki peninsular rivers east): linear rift valley mein behti hai, Vindhya-\nSatpura ke beech behti hai — teesra reason 'Central India se land ka west slope' bhi diya jaata hai, lekin\noptions mein combination trap ki wajah se disputed question ban jaata hai. [Q3]\n2. Narmada — Origin, Course & Basin Districts\n●\nNarmada Valley Satpura aur Vindhyachal ranges ke beech hai — rift valley / fault trough ka classic\nexample hai (Fault Scarp, Nappe, Horst NAHI). Narmada river Amarkantak (Maikal range, M.P.) se\nnikalti hai, structural origin ki hai (volcanic/wind/glacial NAHI), aur ek fault banate hue behti hai — isliye\ndelta nahi banati, estuary banati hai. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]"," ●\nNarmada basin ka hissa: Rajnandgaon (Chhattisgarh) — 5.68% area — Raipur, Korba, Bastar is basin ka\nhissa NAHI hain. Basin zyadatar Maharashtra, Chhattisgarh, M.P., Gujarat mein failaa hai. [Q18]\n●\nNarmada aur Tapti dono milkar India ka sabse bada estuary banati hain (world ka sabse bada St. Lawrence\nRiver banata hai). [Q46]\n3. Son River — Origin Dispute (Amarkantak vs Sonmuda)\n●\nSon aur Narmada dono Amarkantak Hill se nikalti hain — Son north ki taraf behke Ganga se milti hai\n(Bay of Bengal ki taraf), Narmada west ki taraf behke Arabian Sea mein girti hai. Mahanadi ka source\nSihawa Hills, Dhamtari (Chhattisgarh, Maikal range ka hissa) hai. [Q19, Q20, Q21, Q51]\n EXAM TRAP — Son river ka origin dispute — Sonmuda (Anuppur, M.P.) vs Amarkantak (Maikal,\n⚠️\nChhattisgarh) — exam ke state ke hisaab se answer decide hota hai\n●\nSon ke actual source par M.P. aur Chhattisgarh dono claim karte hain — M.P.-based exam mein Sonmuda\n(Anuppur), standard/historical questions mein Amarkantak sahi maana jaata hai. [Q22]\n4. Tapi/Tapti — Origin, Course & Purna Tributary\n●\nTapi river rift valley mein behti hai (Krishna, Mahanadi, Godavari, Cauvery mein NAHI) — Multai (Betul\ndistrict, Satpura Range, M.P.) se nikalti hai, Maharashtra, M.P., Gujarat se hoke Gulf of Khambhat\n(Arabian Sea) mein girti hai, length ~724 km — India ki dusri sabse badi westward-flowing river hai.\n[Q13, Q14, Q15, Q17, Q25, Q27]\n●\nPurna river, Tapi ki sabse badi tributary hai. [Q26]\n●\nWestward-flowing rivers: Narmada, Tapti, Mahi — Rapti NAHI (Rapti Ghaghara ki tributary hai, NW-SE\ndirection mein behti hai). [Q23, Q24]\n5. Cauvery — Origin, Islands & 'Ganga of the South'\n●\nCauvery ko 'Ganga of the South' kaha jaata hai — Brahmagiri Hills (Talakaveri, Kodagu district,\nKarnataka, Western Ghats) se nikalti hai, Karnataka, Kerala, Tamil Nadu, Puducherry se hoke behti\nhai, length ~800 km. Godavari ko 'Vriddha Ganga' ya 'Dakshin Ganga' kaha jaata hai. [Q29, Q30, Q32]\n●\nCauvery teen baar do dhaaron mein bat jaati hai aur kuch mile aage phir mil jaati hai — isse\nSrirangapatnam, Sivasamudram, Srirangam islands bante hain (Deccan Plateau mein). [Q28]\n●\nKabini (Kapila) river Cauvery ki major tributary hai — Kerala ke Wayanad se nikalti hai, Karnataka ke\nTirumakudalu Narsipur mein Cauvery se milti hai. [Q36]\n●\nSahi origin-pairs: Cauvery — Brahmagiri Hills, Sabarmati — Mewad Hills, Tapti — Satpura Range,\nDamodar — Chota Nagpur Plateau. [Q31]\n6. Krishna River — Origin & Interstate Dispute\n●\nKrishna river Mahabaleshwar (Western Ghats) ke paas se ~1337m elevation par nikalti hai, Arabian Sea\nse sirf 64km door, phir bhi length ~1400 km tak behke Bay of Bengal mein girti hai. [Q41]\n●\nKrishna river dispute Andhra Pradesh (ab Telangana bhi), Karnataka aur Maharashtra ke beech hai —\n1957 se chal raha hai, Justice Bachhawat aur Brijesh Kumar ke tribunals bane the. [Q33]"," 7. River Length Rankings (Godavari > Krishna > Narmada > Mahanadi)\n●\nPeninsular rivers ki descending length order: Godavari (1465 km) > Krishna (1400 km) > Narmada (1312\nkm) > Cauvery (800 km) > Tapti (724 km) > Mahanadi (851 km — Krishna-Narmada se chhoti hai par\nTapti-Cauvery se badi). Note: exam options mein Mahanadi kabhi Krishna se pehle nahi aati, hamesha\nNarmada ke baad. [Q34, Q35, Q37, Q38]\n8. River Linking Project & West-Flowing Trio\n●\nRecent river-linking project: Godavari aur Krishna rivers 16 September 2015 ko link hui — River\nLinking Project ke tahat 16 links peninsular rivers ke liye, 14 links Himalayan rivers ke liye proposed\nhain. [Q39]\n9. North-to-South Sequence of East-Flowing Rivers\n●\nPeninsular India ki east-flowing rivers north-se-south order: Subarnarekha → Mahanadi → Godavari →\nKrishna → Pennar → Cauvery → Vaigai. [Q40]\n●\nKerala mein 3 east-flowing rivers hain (Kabini, Bhavani, Pambar) — 'Kerala mein koi east-flowing river\nnahi' statement GALAT hai. Isi tarah M.P. mein bhi west-flowing rivers hain (Tapti, Mahi, Narmada) —\n'M.P. mein koi west-flowing river nahi' bhi GALAT hai. [Q52]\n10. Estuary-Forming Rivers vs Delta-Forming Rivers\n●\nDelta NAHI banane wali rivers: Narmada aur Tapti (estuary banati hain) — Mahanadi, Godavari,\nCauvery, Krishna sab delta banate hain. Mandavi bhi delta-family river hai (Q45 mein Mahanadi hi answer,\nkyunki delta NAHI banane wali sirf Mahanadi thi us list mein — dhyan rahe, context se list badalta hai). [Q9,\nQ12, Q45]\n●\nNarmada, Indus, Tapti — teeno Arabian Sea mein girti hain (Mahanadi Bay of Bengal mein) — isliye\nMahanadi 'different' hai is set mein; Indus ka origin bhi India ke bahar hai (ye ek dusra angle hai). [Q44]\n●\nSaabarmati aur Tapti ke ghaaton (quays) mein paani ki kami hoti hai (Krishna, Cauvery mein NAHI). [Q50]\n11. Catchment Area & Basin Size Comparisons\n●\nCatchment area comparison: Godavari (3,12,812 sq km) sabse zyada — Krishna (2,58,948), Mahanadi\n(1,41,589), Narmada (98,796), Cauvery (81,155), Tapti (65,145) se zyada. Godavari basin, Ganga ke baad\ndusra sabse bada basin hai (~9.50% of India's geographical area). [Q53, Q54, Q55]\n12. Mahanadi — Origin, Course & Tributaries\n●\nMahanadi Sihawa Hills (Dhamtari, Chhattisgarh) se nikalti hai, Chhattisgarh-Odisha se hoke Paradeep ke\npaas Bay of Bengal mein delta banati hai — length ~851 km. Tel river isski main tributary hai (Seonath,\nJonk, Hasdo, Mand, Ib, Ong bhi tributaries hain). [Q43, Q47, Q48]\n●\nLeft-bank tributaries: Seonath (Shivnath), Hasdeo, Mand, Ebb. Right-bank tributaries: Ong, Tel, Jonk.\n[Q49]\n13. Godavari — 'Dakshin Ganga', Basin & Tributaries"," ●\nGodavari Trimbakeshwar (Nasik district, Maharashtra) se nikalti hai — Peninsular India ki sabse lambi\nriver (1465 km), India mein Ganga ke baad dusri sabse lambi — Bay of Bengal mein girti hai. [Q37, Q56,\nQ58, Q59]\n●\nGodavari ki main tributaries: Pravara, Purna, Manjra, Penganga, Wardha, Wainganga, Pranhita\n(Wainganga+Penganga+Wardha ka combined flow), Indravati, Maner, Sabri — Vansadhara aur\nPennar Godavari ki tributaries NAHI hain. [Q60, Q61]\n●\nVaitarna river Trimbak Hills (Nasik) se nikalti hai — Mumbai ke north, Tapi ke south wale region mein,\n~171km behke Arabian Sea mein girti hai (Godavari se related NAHI, alag independent river hai). [Q57]\n14. Chambal & Rift-Valley Tributaries (Yamuna System)\n●\nChambal river Malwa Plateau (Dr. Ambedkar Nagar/Mhow, M.P.) se nikalti hai — apne 'Chambal\nRavines' (bade bade beehad) ke liye famous hai (Narmada/Son/Tapti ki valley is feature ke liye NAHI jaani\njaati). [Q62]\n●\nTawa river Narmada ki sabse lambi tributary hai — Mahadeo Hills (Satpura range, Chhindwara, M.P.) se\nnikalti hai, Bandra Bhan (Narmadapuram) mein Narmada se milti hai. [Q68]\n15. Subarnarekha & Chotanagpur Rivers\n●\nSubarnarekha river Nagri village (Ranchi district, Jharkhand) se nikalti hai — main tributaries Kanchi,\nKharkai, Karkari. [Q64]\n●\nEastern Ghats se nikalne wali rivers: Nagavali aur Vamsadhara — Brahmani aur Subarnarekha, Ranchi\nPlateau se nikalti hain (Eastern Ghats se NAHI). [Q63]\n●\nTropic of Cancer ko Chhota Nagpur Plateau mein Suwarnarekha do baar cross karti hai (23°18'N se\nnikalti hai) — North Koel ek baar, South Koel kabhi nahi, Damodar sirf West Bengal mein ek baar\ncross karti hai (isliye ye question disputed hai — koi bhi diya gaya option pair sahi nahi). [Q65]\n16. Chhattisgarh Regional Rivers — Origin Match Pairs\n●\nMalger river Bailadila Hills se nikalti hai, Shabri river se milti hai. [Q66]\n●\nChhattisgarh region ke river-origin match pairs: Mand — Mainpat, Banas — Devgarh Hills, Jonk —\nSunabera/Sonbera Plateau, Kelo — Ludeng Hills. [Q67]\n●\nChandrahasini Devi Temple (Maa Durga ka Siddha Shakti Peeth) Mand aur Mahanadi ke sangam\n(Chandrapur, Chhattisgarh) par sthit hai. [Q69]\n17. Physiographic Division (S.P. Chatterjee)\n●\nS.P. Chatterjee ne Peninsular region ko 8 parts mein baanta: North Central Highlands, South Central\nHighlands, Eastern Plateau, Meghalaya Plateau, North Deccan, South Deccan, Western Ghats/Sahyadri,\nEastern Ghats. Mahanadi Basin 'North Deccan' (Maharashtra Plateau) sub-division mein shamil hai —\njisme Chhattisgarh Plains, Garjat Hills, Dandakaranya bhi aate hain. [Q70]\n18. Cross-Reference — Khartoum, Sudan (Nile Confluence)"," ●\nDublin-Ireland, Ottawa-Canada, Naypyidaw-Myanmar sahi hain — 'Khartoum-Ethiopia' GALAT hai\n(Khartoum Sudan ki capital hai — White Nile aur Blue Nile ka sangam yahin hota hai). [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Khartoum — Sudan ki capital hai, Ethiopia ki NAHI (Ethiopia ki capital Addis Ababa\n⚠️\nhai)\n19. South Indian Rivers — Dendritic Drainage Pattern\n●\nSouth India ki rivers mein mainly Dendritic drainage pattern hota hai — ped ki shakhaon jaisa dikhta hai\n(Radial, Intermittent, Trellis se alag). [Q42]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0077","t":"06.iv Other Rivers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" OTHER RIVERS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Himalayan vs Peninsular Rivers — Comparison\n2. Indus River System — Tributary Confluence Order\n3. Chandra-Bhaga (Lahaul Valley) & Trans-Himalayan Rivers\n4. Sutlej — Trans-Himalayan River & Tributaries\n5. Rivers of Himachal Pradesh & Punjab Doabs\n6. North-South River Sequences (Map-Based)\n7. Damodar River — Origin, Tributaries & Pollution\n8. Kosi — 'Sorrow of Bihar', Course-Shifting River\n9. Luni & Inland Drainage Rivers\n10. Ladakh Rivers — Shyok, Zanskar, Spiti Sequence\n11. Bihar Canals & River-Linking Projects\n12. Betwa & Rajghat/Ken-Betwa Projects\n13. River-Tributary Match Sets (Repeated Pattern)\n14. Kali River & Deccan Plateau Slope (Assertion-Reason)\n15. Notable Bridges on Indian Rivers\n16. Rivers Not Originating in India (Sutlej)\n17. North-East Tributaries (Kopili, Sankosh)\n18. South Indian River Tributary Match Sets\n19. Superimposed Rivers (Chambal, Son)\n20. West-Flowing Rivers — Mahi, Purna & Others\n21. Mumbai's Mithi River\n22. River Source-Region Match Sets\n23. Fault Valley Drainage — Damodar\n24. Gandikota Canyon — Pennar River\n25. River Origin-Place Match Sets\n26. Lakes Fed by Rivers — True/False Statements\n1. Himalayan vs Peninsular Rivers — Comparison\n●\nHimalayan rivers perennial hoti hain (glaciers se nikalti hain), gradient steep hota hai — isliye zyada\nerosion aur sediment transport karti hain. Peninsular rivers rain-fed hoti hain, gradient kam steep hai,\npurani (already-eroded) topography par behti hain — isliye kam erosion karti hain (teeno statements sahi\nhain is comparison mein). [Q1]\n2. Indus River System — Tributary Confluence Order\n●\nIndus system mein confluence order: Ravi aur Jhelum, Chenab mein milti hain → Chenab, Sutlej mein\nmilti hai → Sutlej seedhe Indus mein milti hai. Attock (Pakistan) mein Kabul River (Afghanistan se)\nIndus mein girti hai — Khyber Pakhtunkhwa aur eastern Afghanistan ki principal river hai. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Chandra-Bhaga (Lahaul Valley) & Trans-Himalayan Rivers\n●\nChandra aur Bhaga rivers Lahaul Valley mein behti hain — Chandra, Chandra Tal glacier se aur Bhaga, Bara\nLacha La se nikalti hai; Tandi ke paas milkar Chandrabhaga/Chenab river bana deti hain. [Q4]"," 4. Sutlej — Trans-Himalayan River & Tributaries\n●\nSutlej (Satluj) Rakas Lake (Tibet) se nikalti hai — poori Himalaya ranges ko cut karti hai (Trans-\nHimalayan river), Shipki La ke paas Himachal Pradesh mein pravesh karti hai, length ~1500km. Baspa,\nSpiti, Beas iski tributaries hain — Ravi Chenab ki tributary hai (Sutlej ki NAHI, sirf sub-tributary hai).\n[Q5, Q6, Q7]\n5. Rivers of Himachal Pradesh & Punjab Doabs\n●\nHimachal Pradesh se guzarne wali main rivers: Beas, Chenab, Ravi, Sutlej, Yamuna. Punjab ke Doab (do\nrivers ke beech ki zameen): Bist Doab — Beas-Sutlej, Bari Doab — Ravi-Beas, Rachna Doab — Ravi-\nChenab, Chaj Doab — Chenab-Jhelum. [Q13, Q15]\n●\nDoodh-Ganga river J&K aur Uttarakhand dono mein hai (Karnataka-Maharashtra mein bhi hai) —\ndisputed question, UPPSC ne J&K ko sahi maana. [Q8]\n6. North-South River Sequences (Map-Based)\n●\nNorth-south sequence (Kishan Ganga se Pen Ganga tak): Kishan Ganga (sabse north, Jhelum ki tributary)\n→ Ganga → Wain Ganga (Godavari ki tributary) → Pen Ganga (Wardha ki tributary). [Q12]\n●\nDrainage-map labeling (typical): Kosi, Gomati, Ghaghara, Gandak is order mein 1-2-3-4 label kiye jaate\nhain. [Q14]\n7. Damodar River — Origin, Tributaries & Pollution\n●\nDamodar, Koel aur Subarnarekha Chotanagpur Plateau (Khamarpat Hill) se nikalti hain — Damodar\nHooghly river ki tributary hai, iski apni tributaries Barki, Jamunia, Barakar hain (Indrawati Godavari ki\ntributary hai, Damodar ki NAHI). Edon Canal Damodar se nikaali gayi hai. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q20, Q21]\n●\nDamodar, Son, Mahanadi, Godavari ki valleys mein India ka 90%+ coal reserve hai. Damodar India ki\nsabse polluted river hai (Giridih-Durgapur ke beech). Rajarappa Damodar-Bhera confluence par hai.\nDamodar mein down-warping ki wajah se rift valley hai — isi liye ye fault valley drainage ke liye famous\nhai, aur 'Sorrow of Bengal' bhi kehlati hai. [Q19, Q22, Q23, Q25, Q59]\n8. Kosi — 'Sorrow of Bihar', Course-Shifting River\n●\nKosi river 'Sorrow of Bihar' kehlati hai — apni dangerous floods aur maximum course-shifting ke liye\njaani jaati hai (2008 mein bhi apna course badla tha). Length ~720km, Katihar ke paas Ganga se milti hai.\nKosi ki 7 tributaries hain, Arun sabse important, aur iska source glacier mein NAHI hai (Tibet-Nepal ke\nslopes drain karti hai). [Q30, Q31, Q32, Q33, Q35]\n9. Luni & Inland Drainage Rivers\n●\nLuni river Aravalli (Ajmer ke southwest, Pushkar Valley) se nikalti hai — Rann of Kutch ki marshy land\nmein lupt ho jaati hai (511km behke), samudra tak NAHI pahunchti — isliye 'land-bounded' river hai.\nInland drainage ke examples: Ghaggar, Luni, Rupen. [Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n10. Ladakh Rivers — Shyok, Zanskar, Spiti Sequence"," ●\nNorth-se-south sequence: Shyok ('River of Death', Karakoram) → Zanskar (deep gorge, Nimu mein\nIndus se milti hai) → Spiti (Kunzum Pass se) → Sutlej (Namgia ke paas Spiti se milti hai). [Q38]\n11. Bihar Canals & River-Linking Projects\n●\nHizla fair (Dumka, Santhal Pargana) Mayurakshi river ke tat par hota hai. Triveni Canal (West Champaran)\nGandak river se paani leti hai. [Q36, Q37, Q39]\n●\nIndia ki pehli river-linking MoU project — Ken-Betwa Link (25 August 2005) — U.P. aur M.P. ke beech\nsigned hui thi. [Q40]\n12. Betwa & Rajghat/Ken-Betwa Projects\n●\nRajghat River Valley Project (U.P.-M.P. joint) aur Rajghat Dam dono Betwa river par hain — Lalitpur\n(U.P.) se 22km door. [Q41, Q42]\n13. River-Tributary Match Sets (Repeated Pattern)\n●\nCommon match-set 1: Ganga — Son, Godavari — Manjra, Krishna — Bhima, Yamuna — Ken.\nCommon match-set 2: Krishna — Bhima, Brahmaputra — Tista, Godavari — Indravati, Yamuna —\nChambal. [Q43, Q49, Q50]\n●\nRepeated set 3: Rapti — Ghaghra, Tista — Brahmaputra, Hiran — Narmada, Purna — Godavari\n(Purna, Tapti ki bhi tributary hai, west-flowing river hai Gujarat-Maharashtra mein). [Q51]\n●\nBetwa-Kshipra-Wain Ganga-Tawa set: Betwa — Yamuna, Kshipra — Chambal, Wain Ganga —\nGodavari, Tawa — Narmada. [Q62]\n14. Kali River & Deccan Plateau Slope (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nKali river (Karnataka, Uttara Kannada) west ki taraf behti hai (Arabian Sea mein), east ki taraf NAHI —\nisliye Assertion galat hai. Lekin Deccan Plateau ka eastern edge Bay of Bengal ki taraf slope karta hai —\nye Reason sahi hai (par Assertion ko explain nahi karta kyunki Assertion khud galat hai). [Q44]\n15. Notable Bridges on Indian Rivers\n●\nDuniya ka sabse ooncha Arch Bridge Chenab river par ban raha hai (under construction) — overall sabse\nooncha bridge (sab categories) Duge Bridge, China hai. Mahatma Gandhi Setu (Ganga par, Patna-\nHajipur, Bihar) length 5575m, 1982 mein inaugurate hua tha. [Q45, Q46]\n16. Rivers Not Originating in India (Sutlej)\n●\nBeas, Chenab, Ravi India mein originate karti hain — Sutlej NAHI (Tibet ke Rakastal lake se nikalti hai).\n[Q47]\n17. North-East Tributaries (Kopili, Sankosh)\n●\nKopili (Kapili) river Brahmaputra ki tributary hai. Sankosh river (Bhutan mein 'Puna Tsang Chhu'\nnaam se) Assam aur West Bengal ke beech boundary banati hai. [Q48, Q54]\n18. South Indian River Tributary Match Sets"," ●\nBay of Bengal mein girne wali drainage systems: Ganga, Brahmaputra, Godavari, Mahanadi, Krishna,\nCauvery, Pennar, Subarnarekha, Brahmani — Narmada, Tapti, Sabarmati, Mahi, Luni Arabian Sea mein\ngirti hain. [Q9]\n●\nKrishna river ki tributaries: Koyna, Yerla, Varna, Panch Ganga, Ghataprabha, Bhima, Tungabhadra,\nDoni — 'Tel' Krishna ki NAHI, Mahanadi ki tributary hai. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Tel — Mahanadi ki tributary hai, Krishna ki NAHI\n⚠️\n●\nHagari river (aka Vedavathi) Western Ghats se nikalti hai, Karnataka-Andhra Pradesh se hoke Tungabhadra\nmein milti hai — Veda aur Avathi rivers Sahyadri se nikal ke Pura mein milke Vedavathi banti hain. [Q11]\n●\nSouth Indian tributary match: Luni — Rajasthan, Indravati —\nOdisha/Maharashtra/Telangana/Chhattisgarh, Bhima — Maharashtra/Karnataka/Telangana,\nGhatprabha — sirf Maharashtra/Karnataka. [Q52]\n●\nSource-region match: Brahmagiri Hills — Cauvery, Verinag Spring — Jhelum, Mahabaleshwar —\nKrishna, Chotanagpur Plateau — Subarnarekha. [Q58]\n●\nDisputed tributary set: Wardha — Pen Ganga, Mahanadi — Seonath, Damodar — Barakar, Cauvery —\nBhavani (Pen Ganga technically Godavari ki indirect/sub-tributary hai via Pranahita). [Q60]\n19. Superimposed Rivers (Chambal, Son)\n●\nSuperimposed river/stream lithosphere ke slopes follow NAHI karti — underlying rocks change hone ke\nbawajood apna course-pattern retain karti hai. Chambal aur Son India mein iske best examples hain. [Q53]\n20. West-Flowing Rivers — Mahi, Purna & Others\n●\nMahi river Madhya Pradesh mein nikalti hai, Rajasthan (Banswara) se hoke Gujarat mein Gulf of\nKhambhat mein girti hai. [Q55]\n●\nKishan Ganga Jhelum river ki main tributary hai — Kishanganga Project aur Tulbul Project dono isi river\npar hain. [Q56]\n21. Mumbai's Mithi River\n●\nMithi river Vihar Lake (Mumbai) se nikalti hai — 2km baad Powai Lake ka paani bhi isme milta hai,\n~18km behke Mahim Bay ke paas Arabian Sea mein girti hai. [Q57]\n22. River Source-Region Match Sets\n●\nGandikota Canyon (India ka 'Grand Canyon', YSR/Kadapa district, Andhra Pradesh) Pennar River dwara\nbanaya gaya hai. [Q61]\n23. Fault Valley Drainage — Damodar\n●\nRiver origin-place match: Yamuna — Yamunotri, Krishna — Mahabaleshwar, Godavari — Nasik\n(Trimbakeshwar), Mahanadi — Sihawa. [Q63]\n24. Gandikota Canyon — Pennar River"," ●\nStatement-verification set: Jhelum River, Wular Lake se hokar guzarti hai (SAHI — Wular ka main\nsource Jhelum hai) — Krishna River seedhe Kolleru Lake ko feed NAHI karti (Budameru-Tammileru\ndwara indirectly), aur Kanwar Lake, Gandak ke meandering se NAHI (Burhi Gandak ke cutoff\nmeander se) bani hai — sirf pehla statement sahi hai. [Q64]\n25. River Origin-Place Match Sets\n●\nNote: Is chapter mein ek off-topic question (European capital cities — Riga, Rotterdam, Zagreb, Zurich) bhi\ntha, jo rivers se related nahi tha — isliye is mindmap mein exclude kiya gaya. [Q24]\n26. Lakes Fed by Rivers — True/False Statements\n●\nKhari river (Rajasthan) do alag rivers ka naam hai — ek Gujarat mein Arabian Sea drainage ka hissa hai\n(Western Banas ki tributary), dusri Ajmer/Pushkar se nikalne wali Bay of Bengal drainage ka hissa hai\n(Banas → Chambal → Yamuna → Ganga) — dono answers technically sahi hain, isliye disputed question\nhai. [Q34]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0078","t":"06.v City Located on the Bank of Rivers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" CITIES LOCATED ON THE BANKS OF RIVERS\n🏙️\n\n— FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Largest City on Ganga — Kanpur\n2. Cities NOT on Ganga (Uttarkashi Trap)\n3. Leh — Right Bank of Indus\n4. Old-River-Course Cities (Ludhiana-Satluj)\n5. Bhubaneswar — Not on Mahanadi (Kuakhai Trap)\n6. Hyderabad — Musi River (Not Krishna Directly)\n7. Common City-River Match Set (Cuttack, Nashik, Ujjain)\n8. MP Cities — Betul, Jagdalpur, Jabalpur, Ujjain\n9. Mandakini Riverside Towns (Kedarnath Route)\n10. Famous Pilgrimage/Historic Towns on Rivers\n11. Pahalgam — Lidder River\n1. Largest City on Ganga — Kanpur\n●\nGanga ke tat par sabse bada city Kanpur (2011 census: 29,20,067) hai — Patna, Varanasi,\nAllahabad/Prayagraj se zyada population. [Q1]\n2. Cities NOT on Ganga (Uttarkashi Trap)\n●\nUttarkashi (Gomukh, Bhagirathi ka source) Ganga ke kinare NAHI hai — kyunki Ganga sirf Devprayag\n(Alaknanda+Bhagirathi confluence) ke baad banti hai. Fatehpur, Bhagalpur, Kanpur Ganga ke kinare hain.\n[Q2]\n EXAM TRAP — Uttarkashi — Bhagirathi ke kinare hai, Ganga ke NAHI (Ganga Devprayag ke baad\n⚠️\nbanti hai)\n3. Leh — Right Bank of Indus\n●\nLeh (ab Ladakh UT, pehle J&K) Indus (Sindhu) river ke right bank par hai. [Q3]\n4. Old-River-Course Cities (Ludhiana-Satluj)\n●\nGorakhpur-Rapti, Jabalpur-Narmada, Surat-Tapi sahi pairs hain — Ludhiana (Punjab) Ravi ke kinare\nNAHI hai (Satluj ke purane kinare par hai, ab Satluj isse 13km north behti hai). [Q4]\n5. Bhubaneswar — Not on Mahanadi (Kuakhai Trap)\n●\nBhubaneswar (Odisha capital) Mahanadi ke kinare NAHI hai — ye Kuakhai river (Mahanadi delta ka\nhissa) ke kinare hai. Cuttack, Mahanadi ke kinare hai (famous correct-pair). [Q6, Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Bhubaneswar Mahanadi par nahi hai — Kuakhai river ke kinare hai; Cuttack hi asal\n⚠️\nmein Mahanadi par hai"," 6. Hyderabad — Musi River (Not Krishna Directly)\n●\nHyderabad Musi river (Krishna ki tributary) ke kinare hai — seedhe Krishna ke kinare NAHI.\nVijayawada aur Srisailam Krishna ke kinare hain — Kota-Chambal, Nasik-Godavari, Jabalpur-\nNarmada sahi pairs hain. [Q7, Q8]\n7. Common City-River Match Set (Cuttack, Nashik, Ujjain)\n●\nRepeated match-set: Cuttack — Mahanadi, Ludhiana — Satluj, Nashik — Godavari, Ujjain — Kshipra.\nAhmedabad-Sabarmati aur Lucknow-Gomti bhi sahi common pairs hain. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n8. MP Cities — Betul, Jagdalpur, Jabalpur, Ujjain\n●\nMP/Chhattisgarh region match: Betul — Tapti (Multai se nikalti hai), Jagdalpur — Indravati (southern\nbank, Bastar district), Jabalpur — Narmada, Ujjain — Kshipra (eastern bank, Malwa region ka sabse\npurana city). [Q12]\n9. Mandakini Riverside Towns (Kedarnath Route)\n●\nMandakini river ke kinare: Gaurikund, Rambara, Guptakashi — Govindghat Mandakini par NAHI hai\n(Govindghat, Alaknanda-Lakshman Ganga ke confluence par hai). [Q13]\n10. Famous Pilgrimage/Historic Towns on Rivers\n●\nFamous places-river match: Pandharpur — Chandrabhaga (Maharashtra), Tiruchirappalli — Cauvery\n(early Cholas ka fort), Hampi — Tungabhadra (Vijayanagar capital) — 'Hampi-Malaprabha' GALAT\nhai, sahi river Tungabhadra hai. [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP — Hampi — Tungabhadra river ke kinare hai, Malaprabha ke NAHI\n⚠️\n11. Pahalgam — Lidder River\n●\nPahalgam (Kashmir, ~2130m altitude, Amarnath Yatra ka starting point) Lidder river ke kinare hai —\nJhelum, Chenab ya Shyok ke NAHI. [Q15]\n●\nNote: Is chapter mein ek off-topic question (Dhuandhar/Hundru/Gersoppa waterfalls match) bhi shaamil tha,\njo actually 'Waterfalls' chapter ka topic hai — is mindmap mein exclude kiya gaya. [Q5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0079","t":"06.vi Waterfalls and Lakes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" WATERFALLS AND LAKES — FULL MIND MAP\n🏞️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Waterfall-River-State Match Sets (Dudhsagar, Barkana, Jog)\n2. Hundru, Sivasamudram & Chhattisgarh Waterfalls\n3. Waterfalls NOT on Narmada (Wrong-Pair Traps)\n4. Jog Falls — India's Biggest (Width) Waterfall\n5. Highest Waterfalls of India (Disputed Rankings)\n6. Chulia, Chitrakote & 'Niagara of India'\n7. Jharkhand Waterfalls — Lodh/Budhaghagh Highest\n8. Bhedaghat/Dhuandhar & MP Waterfalls\n9. Kunchikal Falls Height Controversy\n10. Lagoons of India — Definition & Examples\n11. Largest Saline Lake (Chilika vs Sambhar)\n12. Chilika Lake — Location, Coast Name\n13. Pulicat — 2nd Largest Brackish Water Lake\n14. Fulhar Lake — Source of Gomti\n15. Lake-State Match Sets (Vembanad, Loktak, Dal)\n16. Assam Lakes (Chapanala, Chandubi, Haflong)\n17. Roopkund — 'Mystery/Skeleton Lake'\n18. J&K/Ladakh Lakes (Anchar, Yaya Tso)\n19. Ghepan Lake — Himachal Pradesh\n20. Kayal — Kerala's Lagoon Lakes\n21. Artificial Lakes (Kodaikanal)\n22. North-East & Haryana Lake Match Set\n23. Largest Freshwater Lake (Wular vs Kolleru)\n24. Hot Springs — State Match Set\n25. Rajasthan's Saline Lakes\n26. Bihar's Waterfalls & Oxbow Lakes\n27. Wetland/Lake Match-Verification Set\n1. Waterfall-River-State Match Sets (Dudhsagar, Barkana, Jog)\n●\nWaterfall-state match: Dudhsagar — Goa, Barkana — Karnataka, Khandadhar — Odisha, Palani —\nHimachal Pradesh. [Q1]\n●\nDusra common set (waterfall-river): Dudhsagar — Mandvi (Goa), Duduma — Machhkund (Odisha),\nGokak — Ghatprabha (Karnataka), Jog — Sharavati (Karnataka). [Q5]\n2. Hundru, Sivasamudram & Chhattisgarh Waterfalls\n●\nHundru Falls Subarnarekha river par hai (Ranchi se 45km, height 98m). Sivasamudram Falls Cauvery\nriver par hai. Kapildhara Falls (Anuppur, M.P.) Narmada par hai. [Q2, Q3, Q6]\n●\nAmritdhara waterfall Chhattisgarh mein Hasdeo (Hasdo) river par hai — Manendragarh-Chirmiri-Bharatpur\ndistrict, Mahashivratri par yahan festival hota hai. [Q14]"," 3. Waterfalls NOT on Narmada (Wrong-Pair Traps)\n●\nKapildhara, Dugdhdhara, Bheraghat Narmada par hain — Bhalkund (Rahatgarh) Bina river par hai\n(Narmada ki NAHI). [Q7]\n●\nHundru-Subarnarekha, Chulia-Chambal, Dhuandhar-Narmada sahi pairs hain — BudhaGhagh (Lodh) Falls\nKanchi river ki NAHI, Burha river par hai. [Q4, Q11, Q12]\n EXAM TRAP — BudhaGhagh/Lodh Falls — Burha river par hai, Kanchi ke NAHI (Jharkhand, height\n⚠️\n468 feet)\n4. Jog Falls — India's Biggest (Width) Waterfall\n●\nJog Falls (Shimoga, Karnataka, Sharavati river) width ke hisaab se India ka sabse bada waterfall hai —\nlekin volume ke hisaab se Sivasamudram (Cauvery) sabse bada hai. [Q8]\n5. Highest Waterfalls of India (Disputed Rankings)\n●\nWorld Waterfall Database ke mutabik India ki sabse ooncha waterfall Nohkalikai Falls (Meghalaya, 340m)\nhai — order: Nohkalikai > Dudhsagar (Goa, 320m) > Mawsmai (Meghalaya, 315m) > Kynrem\n(Meghalaya, 305m) > Meenmutty (Kerala, 300m). Purane official Indian sources mein Kunchikal\n(Karnataka) ko highest maana jaata tha — disputed question hai. [Q9, Q10]\n6. Chulia, Chitrakote & 'Niagara of India'\n●\nChitrakote Waterfall (Bastar/Jagdalpur, Chhattisgarh, Indravati river) 'Niagara Falls of India' kehlata hai.\n[Q15, Q16, Q17]\n●\nDudhsagar Falls Goa mein hai (Mandvi river, Western Ghats) — Dhuandhar M.P. mein hai, Nohkalikai\naur Landshing Meghalaya mein hain. [Q18]\n7. Jharkhand Waterfalls — Lodh/Budhaghagh Highest\n●\nJharkhand ki sabse ooncha waterfall Budhaghagh (Lodh) hai — Latehar district, Burha river ke source par,\nIndia mein 21st rank. [Q13]\n●\nBhedaghat mein Dhuandhar waterfall hai (Jabalpur district, height 30m) — Narmada marble-rocks se hoke\nguzarti hai. [Q19]\n8. Bhedaghat/Dhuandhar & MP Waterfalls\n●\nTelhar/Talhar Kund waterfall Bihar ke Kaimur district (Rohtas Plateau) mein hai. [Q44]\n9. Kunchikal Falls Height Controversy\n●\nKunchikal Falls ki height purane database mein 455m thi, ab World Waterfall Database ke mutabik\n183m hai — significant downward revision, disputed exam-question ka source. [Q20]\n10. Lagoons of India — Definition & Examples"," ●\nLagoon = khaare paani ka wo hissa jo sandbank/coral reef se samudra se separate hota hai. Examples:\nAshtamudi, Chilika, Pulicat (sab lagoons hain) — Periyar Lake lagoon NAHI hai (ye artificial lake hai,\nriver se paani leti hai). [Q22]\n11. Largest Saline Lake (Chilika vs Sambhar)\n●\nLargest saline-water lagoon lake — Chilika (Odisha, 900-1165 sq km) — jabki largest inland saline lake\n— Sambhar (Rajasthan) hai. Dono Ramsar list mein hain. [Q23]\n12. Chilika Lake — Location, Coast Name\n●\nChilika Lake Mahanadi ke mouth par, Odisha (Northern Circars coast) mein hai — India ke east coast ki\nsabse badi lagoon lake hai. [Q24, Q25]\n13. Pulicat — 2nd Largest Brackish Water Lake\n●\nPulicat lake Tamil Nadu-Andhra Pradesh border par hai (Sriharikota ke west) — Chilika ke baad India ki\ndusri sabse badi brackish water lake hai, aur do states ke beech share hone wali lake ka example hai.\n[Q26, Q27]\n●\nKolleru lake (freshwater, Godavari-Krishna ke beech, Andhra Pradesh) Ramsar site hai — Lonar\n(Maharashtra), Nakki (Rajasthan) sahi pairs, 'Pulicat-Kerala' GALAT hai (Pulicat TN-AP border par hai).\n[Q29, Q30]\n14. Fulhar Lake — Source of Gomti\n●\nFulhar Lake Pilibhit district, Uttar Pradesh mein hai — yahan se Gomti river nikalti hai. [Q28]\n15. Lake-State Match Sets (Vembanad, Loktak, Dal)\n●\nCommon set: Vembanad — Kerala, Loktak — Manipur, Dal — J&K, Pulicat — TN/AP border —\n'Loktak-Meghalaya' GALAT hai (Loktak Manipur mein hai). Vembanad Kerala ki sabse badi lake hai\n(length 83.72km, Alappuzha-Kottayam-Ernakulam districts). [Q21, Q29]\n●\nAshtamudi-Pulicat-Roopkund-Surajkund set: Ashtamudi — Kerala, Pulicat — Tamil Nadu, Roopkund —\nUttarakhand, Surajkund — Haryana. [Q34]\n●\nBhim Tal-Loktak-Pulicat-Roopkund set: Bhim Tal — Uttarakhand, Loktak — Manipur, Pulicat —\nTN/AP, Roopkund — Uttarakhand (Himachal Pradesh NAHI). [Q35]\n16. Assam Lakes (Chapanala, Chandubi, Haflong)\n●\nAssam ki main lakes: Chandubi, Chapanala, Haflong — Chapanala, Naigaon town se 33km door hai\n(Kolleru Andhra Pradesh mein, Hamirsar Gujarat mein hai). [Q31]\n17. Roopkund — 'Mystery/Skeleton Lake'\n●\nRoopkund (Uttarakhand ki glacial lake) ko 'Mystery Lake' aur 'Skeleton Lake' kaha jaata hai — saikadon\nhuman skeletons kinaare mile the. [Q32]\n18. J&K/Ladakh Lakes (Anchar, Yaya Tso)"," ●\nAnchar lake J&K UT mein hai (Kolleru-AP, Hamirsar-Gujarat se galat pair mat karo). [Q33]\n●\nYaya Tso lake (Ladakh, ~4820m altitude) — Ladakh, bird's paradise, aur Biodiversity Heritage Site (Jan\n2023) hai — lekin Sutlej river se NAHI feed hoti (statement IV galat hai — is fact ko trap ki tarah exam\nmein use kiya jaata hai). [Q47]\n EXAM TRAP — Yaya Tso — 3 statements sahi (Ladakh, Heritage Site, bird's paradise), 4th (Sutlej se\n⚠️\nfeed) GALAT hai\n19. Ghepan Lake — Himachal Pradesh\n●\nSnow-covered Ghepan lake Lahaul Valley, Himachal Pradesh mein hai — ek gigantic glacier ke gradual-\nreceding se bani thi. [Q36]\n20. Kayal — Kerala's Lagoon Lakes\n●\n'Kayal' Kerala ki lagoon lakes ko bola jaata hai — jaise Punnamada, Ashtamudi, Vembanad Kayal. [Q37]\n21. Artificial Lakes (Kodaikanal)\n●\nKodaikanal (Dindigul district, Tamil Nadu) ek artificial freshwater lake hai — Kolleru, Nainital, Renuka\nnatural lakes hain. [Q38]\n22. North-East & Haryana Lake Match Set\n●\nMatch-set: Sala Lake — Arunachal Pradesh, Badkhal Lake — Haryana, Loktak Lake — Manipur,\nKaliveli Lake — Tamil Nadu. [Q39]\n23. Largest Freshwater Lake (Wular vs Kolleru)\n●\nVolume ke hisaab se Wular (Kashmir Valley) India ki sabse badi freshwater lake hai — area ke hisaab se\nKolleru sabse badi hai. Chilika, Sambhar, Loktak dono freshwater NAHI hain (ya alag category ki\nhain) — sirf 'None of the above' hi sahi answer ban sakta hai jab in sab options ka combined comparison ho.\n[Q40, Q41]\n24. Hot Springs — State Match Set\n●\nHot spring-state match: Himachal Pradesh — Manikaran, Odisha — Taptapani, Maharashtra —\nVajreshwari — 'Gujarat-Narayani' GALAT hai (Gujarat mein 17 hot springs hain jaise Tuwa, Unai,\nLasundra — Narayani inme nahi hai). [Q42]\n25. Rajasthan's Saline Lakes\n●\nDidwana, Kuchaman, Sargol, Khatu — sab Rajasthan ki saline (khaare paani ki) lakes hain — Sambhar\nbhi isi list mein aati hai. [Q43]\n26. Bihar's Waterfalls & Oxbow Lakes\n●\nAsia ki sabse badi freshwater Oxbow lake — Kanwar Lake (Begusarai, Bihar) hai — Ramsar Wetland\nsite bhi hai. [Q45]"," 27. Wetland/Lake Match-Verification Set\n●\nVerification set: Hokera Wetland — J&K (Punjab NAHI), Renuka Wetland — Himachal Pradesh\n(SAHI), Rudrasagar Lake — Tripura (SAHI), Sasthamkotta Lake — Kerala (Tamil Nadu NAHI) — is\nset mein sirf 2 pairs sahi hain. [Q46]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0080","t":"07.i Monsoon","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" MONSOON — FULL MIND MAP\n🌦️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. 'Monsoon' Word Origin — Arabic\n2. Himalaya's Climatic Role (Assertion-Reason)\n3. India's Tropical Monsoon Climate — Latitude Facts\n4. Monsoon Arrival — Kerala First\n5. Monsoon Wind Direction (SW to NE)\n6. Sea Salinity Rankings (Red Sea Highest)\n7. Climate Diagram Regions (NE India)\n8. Driest Place — Leh\n9. January Isotherm — 18°C Zonal Divide\n10. Daily Temperature Range — Rajasthan Desert Highest\n11. North-East Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Rainy Season\n12. Monsoon Origin Theories (Thermal & Dynamic)\n13. East-West Rainfall Gradient & Duration Gradient\n14. Indian Ocean Dipole (IOD) & El Niño/La Niña\n15. Jet Stream — Tibetan Plateau Split\n16. Altitude vs Latitude — Agra-Darjeeling, Amritsar-Shimla\n17. Climate Regions of India (Humid SE, Sub-Humid)\n18. Arabian Sea Branch — Chhattisgarh Basin Unaffected\n19. Humid Climate Cities (Kochi, Tejpur)\n20. Monsoon Withdrawal (Retreat) Indicators\n21. Westerlies & Western Disturbances\n22. ITCZ — Equatorial Low Pressure\n23. Rajasthan Dust Storms — Causes\n24. Rajasthan's Low Rainfall — Aravalli's Role\n25. Hindu Calendar Seasons — Chronological Order\n26. MONEX — Indo-Soviet Monsoon Expedition\n27. Koppen Classification — Cwg for Ganga Plains\n1. 'Monsoon' Word Origin — Arabic\n●\n'Monsoon' word Arabic word 'mausim' (matlab 'season') se aaya hai — seasonal wind-reversal ke roop\nmein South/South-East Asia mein rainfall ka reason maana jaata hai. [Q1]\n2. Himalaya's Climatic Role (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nIndia ek monsoonal country hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki Himalaya ek effective climatic divide ka kaam\nkarta hai — cold northern winds se shield deta hai, aur monsoon winds ko trap karke unhein subcontinent\nmein hi moisture chhodne majboor karta hai (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q2]\n3. India's Tropical Monsoon Climate — Latitude Facts\n●\nIndia ki climate tropical monsoon type hai, 8°4' se 37°6' N latitude ke beech hai — lekin exactly tropical\nlatitudes (30°N-30°S) ke beech NAHI hai (Assertion sahi, Reason galat). [Q4]"," 4. Monsoon Arrival — Kerala First\n●\nIndia mein monsoon Kerala mein sabse pehle aata hai — SW monsoon se India ki total rainfall ka 75%\nmilti hai, June-September active rehta hai. [Q5]\n5. Monsoon Wind Direction (SW to NE)\n●\nSummer monsoon South-West se North-East direction mein behta hai — winter mein retreat karte waqt\nNorth-East se South-West. Monsoon ki origin South-West winds se hoti hai — high temperature/low\npressure Indian subcontinent par Indian Ocean se air khींchta hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n6. Sea Salinity Rankings (Red Sea Highest)\n●\nSalinity ranking: Red Sea (41‰, sabse zyada, landlocked hone ki wajah se) > Mediterranean Sea (high\nevaporation) > North Sea (North Atlantic Drift se) > Baltic Sea (sabse kam, river-water influx ki wajah\nse). Normal open ocean salinity 33-37‰ hoti hai. [Q9]\n7. Climate Diagram Regions (NE India)\n●\nHeavy summer rainfall + moderate temperature wala climate diagram North-East India ko represent karta\nhai. [Q10]\n8. Driest Place — Leh\n●\nMumbai, Delhi, Leh, Bengaluru mein Leh sabse shushk (driest) jagah hai — least rainfall receive karta hai.\n[Q11]\n9. January Isotherm — 18°C Zonal Divide\n●\nIndia ko tropical aur subtropical zones mein baantne wala January isotherm 18°C hai. Given map ke shaded\narea mein July ka mean temperature 25.0°C-27.5°C hota hai (annual mean temperature ka map North India\nko South se garm dikhata hai). [Q3, Q12, Q13]\n10. Daily Temperature Range — Rajasthan Desert Highest\n●\nIndia mein Rajasthan ke desert areas mein sabse zyada daily temperature range hota hai — din mein\ngaram, raat mein thanda (desert climate ki main feature). [Q14]\n11. North-East Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Rainy Season\n●\nTamil Nadu ka main rainy season November-December (North-East Monsoon, October-December) hai —\nAndhra Pradesh, Rayalaseema, Tamil Nadu mein is period mein rainfall hoti hai. Isi monsoon mein 26\nDecember 2004 ko Tamil Nadu mein Tsunami aayi thi. [Q15]\n12. Monsoon Origin Theories (Thermal & Dynamic)\n●\nMonsoon ki seasonal displacement land aur sea ke differential temperature ki wajah se hoti hai. Do main\nconcepts: (1) Thermal concept — differential heating effect ka result; (2) Dynamic concept (Flohn ne\ndiya) — planetary winds aur pressure belts ke seasonal migration ka result. [Q16]"," 13. East-West Rainfall Gradient & Duration Gradient\n●\nNorthern plains mein annual rainfall east se west ki taraf GHATTI hai (winds ki humidity kam hoti jaati\nhai) — aur South India mein monsoon duration North se zyada lamba hota hai (sea ke kareeb hone ki\nwajah se) — dono statements sahi hain. [Q17]\n14. Indian Ocean Dipole (IOD) & El Niño/La Niña\n●\nIOD ('Indian Niño') — western aur eastern Indian Ocean ke beech sea-surface temperature ka irregular\noscillation hai (tropical Eastern Pacific Ocean ke SAATH NAHI, ye galat statement hai) — IOD, El Niño ke\nmonsoon-impact ko influence kar sakta hai (ye sahi hai). [Q18]\n●\nEl Niño (Peru coast ki warm ocean current) Indian Monsoon ko kamzor karta hai — harr saal NAHI,\nbalki 2-7 saal ke irregular interval mein aata hai. La Niña iska opposite hai, jo monsoon ko strengthen\nkarta hai. [Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — IOD — western vs eastern Indian Ocean ke beech hota hai, Pacific Ocean ke saath\n⚠️\nNAHI; El Niño har saal nahi aata\n15. Jet Stream — Tibetan Plateau Split\n●\nJet stream Himalaya ke north mein Tibetan highlands ke parallel Asia continent ko cross karti hai — Tibet ki\nhills se do branches mein split ho jaati hai (north aur south) — lekin northern branch India ke winter\nweather mein important role NAHI nibhati (southern branch nibhati hai). [Q20]\n16. Altitude vs Latitude — Agra-Darjeeling, Amritsar-Shimla\n●\nAgra aur Darjeeling same latitude par hain lekin January temperature Agra mein 16°C, Darjeeling mein sirf\n4°C hai — altitude ke saath temperature ghatta hai (normal lapse rate: 1°C per 165m) isi ka reason hai.\nIsi tarah Amritsar-Shimla ki climate difference bhi altitude ke difference se hai (Amritsar ~756 feet,\nShimla ~7866 feet). [Q21, Q22]\n17. Climate Regions of India (Humid SE, Sub-Humid)\n●\nChhattisgarh mein 'Humid South-East' climate hai (West Bengal, Chotanagpur, Odisha plain, southern\nChhattisgarh, NE Andhra Pradesh mein bhi milti hai) — Sub-humid transitional — central Gangetic\nplains, Sub-humid littoral — Coromandel, Sub-humid continental — upper Gangetic plains. [Q23]\n18. Arabian Sea Branch — Chhattisgarh Basin Unaffected\n●\nMonsoon ki Arabian Sea branch, Western Ghats se obstruct hoke 2 branches mein split hoti hai — ek\nAravalli ke parallel (scanty rainfall), dusri Vindhya se obstruct hoke Gujarat-MP-Western Chhattisgarh mein\nrainfall karti hai. Chhattisgarh Basin isse zyada affected NAHI hai. [Q24]\n19. Humid Climate Cities (Kochi, Tejpur)\n●\nAhmedabad, Kochi, Ludhiana, Tejpur mein se Kochi aur Tejpur zyada humid hain (heavy rainfall ki wajah\nse — 2022 mein Kochi 3415.8mm, Tejpur 1775.7mm, jabki Ahmedabad sirf 564mm, Ludhiana 766.9mm).\n[Q25]"," 20. Monsoon Withdrawal (Retreat) Indicators\n●\nMonsoon ki decline/withdrawal 3 cheezon se indicate hoti hai: clear sky, Bay of Bengal mein low pressure\nban na, land par temperature ka thoda badhna — sab teen sahi hain. [Q26]\n21. Westerlies & Western Disturbances\n●\nWesterlies 30°-60° north AND south latitudes ke beech behti hain (30°N se 60°S ka statement galat hai) —\nwinter mein western cyclonic disturbances (Mediterranean se origin) westerly jet stream se India laayi\njaati hain, North-West India mein winter rain karti hain. [Q27]\n22. ITCZ — Equatorial Low Pressure\n●\nIntertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) equator par hoti hai — NE aur SE trade winds yahin milti hain, sun\nki apparent motion ke saath north-south shift karti hai. [Q28]\n23. Rajasthan Dust Storms — Causes\n●\nRajasthan mein May-June ke dust storms ka main reason convectional currents ka origin (kuch jagahon\npar) hai — 'Loo' garam hawa se low pressure banta hai, jisse air rapidly rise karke dust storms laati hai. [Q29]\n24. Rajasthan's Low Rainfall — Aravalli's Role\n●\nRajasthan mein bahut kam rainfall hoti hai kyunki winds koi barrier cross nahi karti jo unhein cool hone\nke liye zaroori uplift de sake — Aravalli range SW monsoon ki direction ke parallel align hai, isliye partial\nobstacle bhi effective nahi hai, aur western Rajasthan rain-shadow area ban jaata hai. [Q30]\n25. Hindu Calendar Seasons — Chronological Order\n●\nHindu calendar ke 6 seasons chronological order mein: Spring (March-April) → Summer (May-June) →\nRainy (July-August) → Autumn (September-October) → Pre-winter (November-December) → Winter\n(January-February). [Q31]\n26. MONEX — Indo-Soviet Monsoon Expedition\n●\nIndia-USSR ne 1973 mein joint 'Monsoon Expedition' MONEX-1973 ki thi. 1967 mein WMO-ICSU ne\nGlobal Atmospheric Research Program (GARP) organize kiya tha, jiske Global Weather Experiment (1\nDec 1978) ke sub-program ke roop mein Monsoon Experiment (MONEX-1979) tha — dono alag events\nhain (Expedition vs Experiment ka confusion trap). [Q32]\n27. Koppen Classification — Cwg for Ganga Plains\n●\nKoppen ne India ke Great Plains (upper Gangetic plains) ke liye 'Cwg' (dry-winter humid subtropical,\n'Monsoon type with dry winters') use kiya — summer temperature ~40°C se winter mein ~27°C tak girta\nhai. North-East India (North Bengal samet) aur North Bihar dono ka bhi Koppen classification 'Cwg'\nhai. [Q33, Q34, Q35]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0081","t":"07.ii Rainfall","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" RAINFALL — FULL MIND MAP\n🌧️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. SW Monsoon — India's Main Rainfall Source\n2. NE Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Main Rainfall\n3. Highest Average Annual Rainfall State (Sikkim/Meghalaya)\n4. Same-Latitude Rainfall Contrast (Ajmer-Shillong)\n5. Meteorological Station Identification (Chennai)\n6. City Rainfall Ranking (Kochi > Kolkata > Patna > Delhi)\n7. Mango Shower, Blossom Shower, Norwesters, Loo\n8. Lowest Rainfall Places (Leh)\n9. Cherrapunji — Location & Rainfall Record\n10. Highest Rainfall Regions of India\n11. 'Thirsty Land' Paradox — Why India Lacks Water Despite Rain\n12. Rainwater Harvesting — Cost-Effective Strategy\n13. 200mm Average Rainfall Zone (Zanskar & W. Rajasthan)\n14. Jharkhand's Monsoon — South-West\n15. 100-150cm Rainfall Shaded Map Zone\n16. Pushkar Hills Rainfall — Balotra Floods\n17. 'Rainy Day' Definition — 2.5mm Threshold\n18. Ganga Plain Rainfall Gradient (Assertion-Reason)\n19. All India Water Divide Map\n20. Climate Reason-Match Set (Latitude, Altitude, Depressions)\n21. Watershed Development in Semi-Arid Regions\n22. Desert Development Programme — District Count\n23. Inland Waterways Underdevelopment (Assertion-Reason)\n24. Cherrapunji — Khasi Hills Location\n25. Chennai's Low SW-Monsoon Rainfall\n1. SW Monsoon — India's Main Rainfall Source\n●\nIndia ko maximum rainfall South-West Monsoon se milti hai — April-May mein Indian subcontinent ke\nnorth mein intense low pressure banta hai, ITCZ north ki taraf shift hoti hai, aur SW monsoon do rain-\nbearing systems (Bay of Bengal branch + Arabian Sea branch) mein India mein enter karta hai. [Q1]\n2. NE Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Main Rainfall\n●\nTamil Nadu apni annual rainfall ka 40-50% North-East Monsoon (October-December) se paata hai — 26\nDecember 2004 ko isi season mein Tsunami aayi thi. SW monsoon mein Chennai sabse kam rainfall\nreceive karta hai (Chennai ka main rainy season NE monsoon hai). [Q2, Q15, Q29]\n3. Highest Average Annual Rainfall State (Sikkim/Meghalaya)\n●\nJab question pucha gaya tha tab Sikkim (3300.7mm) ko highest maana jaata tha — 2022 IMD data ke\nmutabik ab Meghalaya (4216.1mm) sabse zyada rainfall wala state hai. [Q3]\n4. Same-Latitude Rainfall Contrast (Ajmer-Shillong)"," ●\nSame latitude (26°27' N) par hone ke bawajood, Ajmer (623.5mm/year) aur Shillong (8084.7mm/year) ki\nrainfall mein sabse zyada spashta antar hai — Bengaluru-Chennai, Mumbai-Vishakhapatnam, Nagpur-\nKolkata jaisi comparisons se zyada. [Q4]\n5. Meteorological Station Identification (Chennai)\n●\n26°C average annual temperature, 63cm rainfall, 9°C annual range — ye Chennai ki characteristics hain\n(winter 24°C, summer 30°C, annual range 8-9°C, average rainfall 60-70cm). [Q5]\n6. City Rainfall Ranking (Kochi > Kolkata > Patna > Delhi)\n●\n2022 ke data ke mutabik descending rainfall order: Kochi (3415.8mm) > Kolkata (1325.1mm) > Patna\n(736.2mm) > Delhi (675.9mm) — India ki sabse zyada rainfall Mawsynram (Meghalaya) mein hoti hai.\n[Q6]\n7. Mango Shower, Blossom Shower, Norwesters, Loo\n●\nLocal storm match: Mango Shower — Karnataka coastal areas (pre-monsoon, aam pakane mein madad\nkarti hai), Blossom Shower — Kerala (coffee phoolon ko khilne mein madad), Norwesters (Kal-\nBaisakhi) — West Bengal/Assam (Baisakh mahine mein, tea-jute-rice ke liye faydemand), Loo —\nPunjab se Bihar (garam-shushk local winds). [Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10]\n8. Lowest Rainfall Places (Leh)\n●\nIndia mein Leh mein sabse kam rainfall (63.8mm/year) hoti hai — Jaisalmer Rajasthan ka lowest hai\n(372.9mm), Bikaner 474mm. [Q11, Q12]\n9. Cherrapunji — Location & Rainfall Record\n●\nCherrapunji (ab Sohra) Meghalaya ke East Khasi Hills district (Khasi Hills) mein hai — Mawsynram ke\nbaad dusra highest-rainfall record iske naam hai. [Q13, Q28]\n10. Highest Rainfall Regions of India\n●\nIndia mein sabse zyada rainfall Western Ghats, Eastern Himalayan region aur Meghalaya mein hoti hai\n— 250cm+ average annual rainfall. [Q14]\n11. 'Thirsty Land' Paradox — Why India Lacks Water Despite Rain\n●\nIndia ki 1257mm actual annual rainfall hone ke bawajood ise 'thirsty land' kaha jaata hai kyunki: (1) paani ka\nrapid runoff, (2) rainwater ka quick evaporation, (3) sirf kuch mahinon (June-Sept) mein hi rainfall\nconcentrate hoti hai — teeno reasons combined. [Q15]\n12. Rainwater Harvesting — Cost-Effective Strategy\n●\nIndia ki cost-effective water management strategy — Rainwater Harvesting hai (embankments-tanks\nbanake) — Tamil Nadu isme leading state hai. [Q16]\n13. 200mm Average Rainfall Zone (Zanskar & W. Rajasthan)"," ●\n~200mm average annual rainfall Zanskar range (northern J&K/Ladakh) aur western Rajasthan mein\nhoti hai. [Q17]\n14. Jharkhand's Monsoon — South-West\n●\nJharkhand ki rainfall South-West Monsoon (June-September) se hoti hai. [Q18]\n15. 100-150cm Rainfall Shaded Map Zone\n●\nDiye gaye India map ke shaded region mein mean annual rainfall 100 se 150cm (broadly 100-200cm range)\nke beech hoti hai. [Q19]\n16. Pushkar Hills Rainfall — Balotra Floods\n●\nPushkar Hills mein bhaari rainfall hone par Balotra (Rajasthan) mein baadh aati hai. [Q20]\n17. 'Rainy Day' Definition — 2.5mm Threshold\n●\nIMD ke mutabik 'rainy day' wo din hota hai jab 24 ghanton mein 2.5mm ya usse zyada rainfall ho. [Q21]\n18. Ganga Plain Rainfall Gradient (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nGanga plain mein west/north-west ki taraf jaane par monsoonal rainfall kam hoti hai (Punjab plains\n~600mm, Gangetic plain ~1500mm) — kyunki moisture-bearing monsoonal winds jaise-jaise upar (west)\nbadhti hain, unki humidity ghat jaati hai (Assertion sahi, Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q22]\n19. All India Water Divide Map\n●\nDiya gaya India ka map 'All India Water Divide' dikhata hai — Isohyet, national highways, ya major\nhighway routes NAHI. [Q23]\n20. Climate Reason-Match Set (Latitude, Altitude, Depressions)\n●\nClimate-reason match: Chennai Kolkata se garam hai — latitude ka difference; Himalaya mein snowfall\n— altitude; West Bengal se Punjab tak rainfall ghatti hai — sea se distance; Sutlej-Ganga plain mein\nwinter mein kuch rain — western depressions. [Q24]\n21. Watershed Development in Semi-Arid Regions\n●\nIndia ke semi-arid regions mein watershed development ki pehchaan seasonal rivers ka paani embank\nkarke tanks ki system banana hai — ~120,000 chhote tanks se ~4.12 million hectares zameen ki sinchayi\nhoti hai. [Q25]\n22. Desert Development Programme — District Count\n●\nDesert Development Programme (DDP, 1977-78 mein shuru) us waqt 5 states ke 21 districts (131 blocks)\nmein tha — abhi 7 states ke 40 districts (235 blocks) cover karta hai. [Q26]\n23. Inland Waterways Underdevelopment (Assertion-Reason)"," ●\nIndia mein inland waterways acchi tarah se develop NAHI hain (Assertion sahi) kyunki saal ke sirf 4\nmahine hi rainfall hoti hai, isliye rivers mein paani ki kami rehti hai (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q27]\n24. Cherrapunji — Khasi Hills Location\n●\nCherrapunji Khasi Hills, Meghalaya mein hai — Naga, Garo, Mikir Hills mein NAHI. [Q28]\n25. Chennai's Low SW-Monsoon Rainfall\n●\nSW monsoon (1 June-30 September active) se Chennai sabse kam rainfall receive karta hai (Kolkata,\nMangalore, Delhi se kam) — Chennai ki main rainfall NE monsoon se aati hai. [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0082","t":"07.iii Winter Rainfall","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" WINTER RAINFALL — FULL MIND MAP\n❄️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Western Disturbance — Northern Plains' Winter Rain Source\n2. Punjab-Tamil Nadu — Two Different Winter-Rain Mechanisms\n3. Tamil Nadu Coast — Dry in SW Monsoon (Rain Shadow)\n4. NE Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Actual Winter Rain Cause\n5. Northern Plains Winter Rain — NOT from NE Monsoon\n6. Why Most of India Stays Dry in Winter\n7. Coromandel Coast & NE Monsoon Reach\n8. Anti-Cyclonic Conditions vs Winter Rainfall\n9. Winter-Rain Regions — NW and SE India\n10. Western Disturbance Rain Gradient (West to East)\n11. Rabi Crops & Western Disturbance Dependency\n12. Western Disturbance vs Cyclonic Depression\n1. Western Disturbance — Northern Plains' Winter Rain Source\n●\nIndia ke Northern plains ko winter rainfall Western Disturbance se milti hai — ye Mediterranean region\nmein origin lene wala extratropical storm hai, jo NW India mein achanak winter rain laata hai. [Q1]\n2. Punjab-Tamil Nadu — Two Different Winter-Rain Mechanisms\n●\nPunjab-Tamil Nadu combination winter rainfall receive karta hai — Punjab Western Disturbance se, Tamil\nNadu coastal area retreating NE Monsoon se (65-75cm tak) — dono alag-alag mechanisms hain. [Q2]\n3. Tamil Nadu Coast — Dry in SW Monsoon (Rain Shadow)\n●\nTamil Nadu coast SW monsoon season mein shushk (dry) rehta hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki ye Bay of\nBengal branch ke parallel hai aur Arabian Sea branch ke rain-shadow area mein padta hai (Reason\nsahi explanation hai) — Western Ghats barrier ki tarah kaam karta hai. [Q3]\n4. NE Monsoon — Tamil Nadu's Actual Winter Rain Cause\n●\nTamil Nadu mein winter rainfall mainly North-East Monsoon ki wajah se hoti hai —\nWestern/South-West/South-East monsoon se NAHI. [Q4]\n5. Northern Plains Winter Rain — NOT from NE Monsoon\n●\nNorthern plains ko winter mein kuch rainfall milti hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin iska reason NE Monsoon\nNAHI hai (Reason galat, kyunki asal reason Western Disturbance hai) — dono statements sahi hain, par\nR, A ki sahi explanation nahi deta. [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — Northern plains ka winter rain — Western Disturbance se hai, NE Monsoon se NAHI\n⚠️\n(common confusion)\n6. Why Most of India Stays Dry in Winter"," ●\nWinter season mein India ka zyadatar hissa shushk rehta hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki desh ke zyadatar hisson\npar North-East trade winds ka influence hota hai — ye winds land se sea ki taraf jaati hain aur unme kam\nhumidity hoti hai (Reason sahi hai, though R ki explanation quality par disagreement hai). Exception: Oct-\nNov mein NE monsoon Bay of Bengal cross karte waqt moisture leke Tamil Nadu mein torrential rain\nkarta hai. [Q6]\n7. Coromandel Coast & NE Monsoon Reach\n●\nNE Monsoon se rainfall paane wale coastal/regional areas: Coromandel Coast (Tamil Nadu), Southern\nAndhra Pradesh, South-East Karnataka, South-East Kerala — Gujarat Coast, Malabar Coast, Konkan\nCoast NAHI. [Q7, Q8, Q9]\n8. Anti-Cyclonic Conditions vs Winter Rainfall\n●\nAnti-cyclonic conditions winter mein high atmospheric pressure aur low temperature ki wajah se banti\nhain (Assertion sahi) — lekin inka winter rainfall se koi seedha connection NAHI hai (Reason galat), ye\nalready-existing conditions hain. [Q10]\n9. Winter-Rain Regions — NW and SE India\n●\nWinter rainfall paane wale regions: North-West India (Punjab, Haryana, Delhi, Western UP — Western\nDisturbance se) aur South-East India (Tamil Nadu coast — NE Monsoon se) — disputed question mein\ndono (A aur D) sahi maane gaye. [Q11]\n10. Western Disturbance Rain Gradient (West to East)\n●\nWestern Disturbance se hone wali winter rain West se East ki taraf gradually ghatti hai — ye Rabi crops\nke liye agriculture mein bahut important hai, aur mountainous regions mein heavy snow bhi karti hai.\n[Q12]\n11. Rabi Crops & Western Disturbance Dependency\n●\nRabi crops (Punjab-Haryana jaise NW states mein) ki success winter rain par depend karti hai — ye rain\nextra-tropical cyclones (Turkey/Iraq/Iran/Afghanistan/Pakistan se origin, westerly jet streams se\ndriven) se aati hai, tropical cyclones se NAHI (ye ek common wording-trap hai jo question ko disputed\nbanata hai). [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP — Rabi crops ka winter rain 'extra-tropical' cyclones se hai, 'tropical' cyclones se NAHI —\n⚠️\n\nis wording-difference se hi question disputed banta hai\n12. Western Disturbance vs Cyclonic Depression\n●\nNW India mein winter rainfall ka main cause Western Disturbance hai — technically ye ek weak cyclonic\ndepression ka form bhi hai, par exam mein 'Western Disturbance' hi most suitable/correct answer maana\njaata hai (retreating monsoon ya SW monsoon se confuse mat karo). [Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0083","t":"08 Natural Disasters","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" NATURAL DISASTERS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌪️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. 2004 Tsunami — Coromandel Coast Worst-Hit\n2. Cyclone Hudhud — Andhra Pradesh (2014)\n3. Tsunami Warning Centre — Hyderabad (INCOIS)\n4. India Meteorological Department — HQ History\n5. Natural Hazard-Region Match Set\n6. Himalayan Landslides — Mining as Cause\n7. Why Bay of Bengal Gets More Cyclones\n8. East Coast vs West Coast Cyclone Vulnerability\n9. Koyna Region — Reservoir-Induced Seismicity\n10. Odisha — India's Most Disaster-Prone State\n11. First Disaster Management Training Institute\n12. Seismic Zones — Zone II (Low Risk) & Zone Count\n13. City-Seismic Zone Match (Bhuj, Srinagar, Chennai)\n14. Flood Frequency Rise — Silt Deposition\n15. Most Flood-Prone State — Bihar\n16. UP's Most Flood-Affected Region — Eastern UP\n17. Disaster Facts — Bhopal Gas Tragedy & Mangroves\n18. Disaster-Region Match (Flood/Earthquake/Drought/Tsunami)\n19. Recent Named Cyclones — Origin & Impact\n20. Tropical Cyclone Formation Factors\n1. 2004 Tsunami — Coromandel Coast Worst-Hit\n●\n26 December 2004 ki Indian Ocean Tsunami se Coromandel Coast (False Divi Point se Kanyakumari tak)\nsabse zyada affected hua tha — Malabar, Konkan, Northern Circars se zyada. [Q1]\n2. Cyclone Hudhud — Andhra Pradesh (2014)\n●\nHudhud cyclone (October 2014) Andhra Pradesh coast (Visakhapatnam) se takraaya tha — naam Oman ne\nsuggest kiya tha, heavy rainfall aur gale winds se structural damage hua. [Q2]\n3. Tsunami Warning Centre — Hyderabad (INCOIS)\n●\nIndian Tsunami Early Warning Centre (ITEWC), INCOIS, Hyderabad mein hai — October 2007 se\noperational. [Q3]\n4. India Meteorological Department — HQ History\n●\nIMD (established 1875) ka current HQ New Delhi (Lodhi Road) mein hai — history: Kolkata (first HQ) →\nShimla (1905) → Pune (1928) → Delhi (1944). [Q4]\n5. Natural Hazard-Region Match Set"," ●\nHazard-region match: Floods — Plains of UP and Bihar, Earthquakes — Himalayan foothill zone,\nDroughts — Mid-Eastern/West-Central India, Cyclones — Jharkhand and Northern Odisha (coastal).\n[Q5]\n6. Himalayan Landslides — Mining as Cause\n●\nHimalaya mein landslides ki frequency badh gayi hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki large-scale mining\n(roads/dams construction ke liye) hui hai (Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q6]\n7. Why Bay of Bengal Gets More Cyclones\n●\nBay of Bengal mein zyada cyclones high temperature se generate hone wale low pressure ki wajah se aate\nhain — cyclones anticlockwise direction mein move karte hain, do seasons hote hain (May-June aur mid-\nSept-mid-Dec). [Q7]\n8. East Coast vs West Coast Cyclone Vulnerability\n●\nEast coast, west coast se zyada cyclone-prone hai (Assertion sahi) — East coast North-East trade winds ke\nzone mein hai (Reason sahi hai), lekin ye Assertion ka sahi explanation NAHI hai (asal reason Bay of\nBengal ke anticlockwise cyclones hain). [Q8]\n9. Koyna Region — Reservoir-Induced Seismicity\n●\nKoyna region (Maharashtra) future mein aur zyada earthquake-prone ho sakta hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki\nKoyna dam ek old fault-plane par hai, jo reservoir ke water-level change se zyada activate ho sakta hai\n(Reason sahi explanation hai). [Q9]\n10. Odisha — India's Most Disaster-Prone State\n●\nOdisha sabse zyada natural disasters face karta hai (Bay of Bengal coast par hone ki wajah se) —\ncyclones, floods, droughts teeno se affected hota hai. [Q10]\n11. First Disaster Management Training Institute\n●\nDesh ka pehla Disaster Management Training Institute CRPF dwara Latur, Maharashtra mein establish\nkiya gaya — (note: India ka pehla institute technically 29 April 1957 ko Nagpur mein bana tha, par Nagpur\noptions mein na hone ki wajah se Latur sahi answer hai). [Q11]\n12. Seismic Zones — Zone II (Low Risk) & Zone Count\n●\nKarnataka Plateau Zone II mein aata hai (high seismic intensity ka zone NAHI) — Uttarakhand, Kutch,\nHimachal Pradesh high-intensity zones mein hain. India ko currently 4 seismic zones (II, III, IV, V) mein\nbaanta gaya hai — purana Zone I ab use mein nahi hai. [Q12, Q13]\n13. City-Seismic Zone Match (Bhuj, Srinagar, Chennai)\n●\nCity-zone match: Bhuj — Zone V, Hyderabad — Zone II, Srinagar — Zone V, Chennai — Zone III —\ndisputed question hai kyunki multiple diye gaye options galat combinations the. [Q14]\n14. Flood Frequency Rise — Silt Deposition"," ●\nNorth Indian plains mein floods ki frequency pichhle dashकon mein badhi hai (Assertion sahi) kyunki silt\ndeposition se river valleys ki depth kam ho gayi hai (Reason sahi explanation hai) — isse normal rain mein\nbhi flooding hoti hai. [Q15]\n15. Most Flood-Prone State — Bihar\n●\nIndia ka sabse zyada flood-prone state Bihar hai — Assam, Andhra Pradesh, UP se zyada. [Q16]\n16. UP's Most Flood-Affected Region — Eastern UP\n●\nUttar Pradesh ka Eastern area sabse zyada flood-affected hai — high flood-affected region UP ke total\nflood-affected area ka 48% cover karta hai. [Q17]\n17. Disaster Facts — Bhopal Gas Tragedy & Mangroves\n●\nSahi facts: Developing countries mein natural disasters se max damage hota hai, Bhopal gas tragedy\nman-made thi (1984, Methyl Isocyanate leak, ~5200 deaths), Mangroves cyclones ka impact kam karte\nhain — 'India disaster-free country hai' GALAT hai (UNDP ne India ko top-10 disaster-prone\ncountries mein rakha hai). [Q18]\n18. Disaster-Region Match (Flood/Earthquake/Drought/Tsunami)\n●\nMatch set: Flood — UP-Bihar plains, Earthquake — Himalayan Zone, Drought — West-Central India,\nTsunami — Southern coastal India. [Q19]\n19. Recent Named Cyclones — Origin & Impact\n●\nRecent cyclones yaad rakho: Tauktae — Arabian Sea (May 2021, Gujarat coast), Amphan — Bay of\nBengal (May 2020, WB-Odisha-Bangladesh), Michaung — Bay of Bengal (Dec 2023, Andhra Pradesh),\nFani — 2019 (Odisha), Ockhi — Nov 2017 (extremely severe cyclonic storm), Fengal — Nov-Dec 2024\n(Bay of Bengal, Tamil Nadu-Puducherry). [Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23]\n20. Tropical Cyclone Formation Factors\n●\nMay mahine mein tropical cyclone ka sabse important factor local temperature variation hai — coastal\nregion mein uneven temperature rise cyclone ke liye suction generate karta hai, jisse cyclone garam region ki\ntaraf deflect hota hai aur intensify hota hai. [Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0084","t":"09.i Black Soil","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🟫 BLACK SOIL — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Regur/Black Soil — Basaltic Lava Origin\n2. Names & Spread (Regur, Chernozem, Lava Soil)\n3. Self-Ploughing — Water Retention Characteristic\n4. Nutrient Composition — Rich vs Deficient\n5. Best Suited for Cotton Cultivation\n6. Karewas — Kashmir's Saffron Soil\n7. Malwa Plateau & Lava Soil\n8. Jharkhand's Black Soil — Rajmahal Region\n9. Black Soil NOT Found in Himalayan Region\n1. Regur/Black Soil — Basaltic Lava Origin\n●\nRegur/Black soil basaltic lava ke weathering se bani hai — Deccan Trap region (NW Deccan plateau) ki\ntypical soil hai, fissure volcanic rock se bani (granite/schist/shale-limestone se NAHI). [Q1, Q2]\n2. Names & Spread (Regur, Chernozem, Lava Soil)\n●\nBlack soil ko Regur (Telugu word 'Reguda' se), Black Cotton Soil, Tropical Chernozem bhi kaha jaata\nhai — Maharashtra, MP, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Gujarat, Telangana mein milti hai, total ~5.46\nlakh sq km. Maharashtra mein sabse zyada failii hai. [Q3, Q4]\n3. Self-Ploughing — Water Retention Characteristic\n●\nBlack soil ('self-ploughed soil' bhi kehlati hai) high water retention capacity rakhti hai — gili hone par\nphoolti/sticky hoti hai, sookhne par sukadti hai aur wide cracks banati hai (self-ploughing) — isliye kam\nirrigation ki zaroorat hoti hai. [Q5, Q11, Q15]\n4. Nutrient Composition — Rich vs Deficient\n●\nBlack soil Alumina, Iron, Lime, Magnesium carbonates, Potash se rich hai — lekin Phosphorus,\nNitrogen aur Humus (organic matter) ki kami hoti hai (isliye 'humus se rich' wala Assertion-Reason\nstatement galat hota hai). [Q6, Q9, Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Black soil rich hai minerals mein — humus/nitrogen/phosphorus mein NAHI (common\n⚠️\nAssertion-Reason trap)\n5. Best Suited for Cotton Cultivation\n●\nBlack soil cotton cultivation ke liye sabse best hai — Regur, Alluvial, Laterite, Red soil mein se. [Q7, Q12]\n6. Karewas — Kashmir's Saffron Soil\n●\nKarewas (glacial clay + moraine deposits) Kashmir Himalaya mein hain — Saffron (Zafran) cultivation ke\nliye famous. [Q8]"," 7. Malwa Plateau & Lava Soil\n●\nWestern India ki black soil ko 'Lava soil' bhi kaha jaata hai (lava se bani hai) — Malwa Plateau ki\npredominant soil black/lava soil hai. [Q13, Q14]\n8. Jharkhand's Black Soil — Rajmahal Region\n●\nJharkhand mein black soil Rajmahal hill region mein paayi jaati hai — Damodar valley, Subarnarekha\nvalley, Palamu mein NAHI (NIDM report ke mutabik). [Q16]\n9. Black Soil NOT Found in Himalayan Region\n●\nBlack soil (Regur) ke sahi facts: locally 'Regur' kehlati hai, Krabs ke mutabik mature soil hai, highly\nmoisture-retentive hai — 'Himalayan region mein paayi jaati hai' GALAT hai (Maharashtra, Gujarat,\nKarnataka, MP mein hai, Himalaya mein NAHI). [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0085","t":"09.ii Laterite Soil","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" LATERITE SOIL — FULL MIND MAP\n🧱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Origin — High Temperature & Heavy Rainfall (Leaching)\n2. Word Origin — Latin 'Later' (Brick)\n3. Colour & Composition — Iron/Aluminium Rich\n4. Nutrient Deficiency — Nitrogen, Lime, Humus, Phosphorus\n5. Crops — Tapioca & Cashew Nuts\n6. Andhra Pradesh — Wrong Association Trap\n7. Geographic Spread — Malabar Coast Leading\n8. Building Material Use\n9. Infertility Due to Excess Iron\n1. Origin — High Temperature & Heavy Rainfall (Leaching)\n●\nLaterite soil high temperature aur heavy rainfall wale areas (typical monsoon conditions, wet-dry\nperiods) mein develop hoti hai — leaching process se bases aur silica surface se bah jaate hain, iron-\naluminium oxides peeche reh jaate hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q6]\n2. Word Origin — Latin 'Later' (Brick)\n●\n'Laterite' word Latin word 'Later' (matlab 'brick') se aaya hai. [Q3]\n3. Colour & Composition — Iron/Aluminium Rich\n●\nLaterite soil red se reddish-yellow color ki hoti hai — Iron aur Aluminium oxides se rich hai (Iron-\nAluminium se poor NAHI), porous aur well-drained hai lekin water-holding capacity kam hai. [Q4]\n4. Nutrient Deficiency — Nitrogen, Lime, Humus, Phosphorus\n●\nLaterite soil mein Nitrogen, Phosphorus, Potash, Magnesium, Lime, Humus ki kami hoti hai — acidic\ncharacter dikhati hai, isliye fertility kam hoti hai (crop production ke liye kam useful). [Q8]\n5. Crops — Tapioca & Cashew Nuts\n●\nLaterite soil par Tapioca aur Cashew nuts achhi tarah ugte hain — statement 'red colour +\nTapioca/cashew' sahi hai, 'nitrogen-potash rich' aur 'Rajasthan-UP mein well-developed' GALAT hai. [Q1]\n6. Andhra Pradesh — Wrong Association Trap\n●\nWest Bengal ka net sown area (~60%) Andhra Pradesh (~40%) se zyada hai (Assertion sahi) — lekin iska\nreason 'AP mein laterite soil hai' GALAT hai (AP mein mostly Red aur Alluvial soils hain, laterite nahi).\n[Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — Andhra Pradesh mein Red/Alluvial soil hai — laterite soil ka association GALAT hai\n⚠️\n7. Geographic Spread — Malabar Coast Leading"," ●\nLaterite soil 2.48 lakh sq km area cover karti hai — Western Ghats, Eastern Ghats, South Maharashtra,\nKarnataka, AP, Odisha, WB, Kerala, Jharkhand, Assam, Meghalaya mein failii hai. Sabse zyada\nKerala (Malabar Coastal Region) mein hai — options mein Kerala na ho to Maharashtra sahi answer\nhai. [Q6, Q7]\n8. Building Material Use\n●\nLaterite soil ke sahi facts: humid tropical regions ki soil hai, highly leached hai, fertility kam hai, good\nbuilding material deti hai — 'lime se rich hai' GALAT hai (lime ki kami hoti hai). [Q8]\n9. Infertility Due to Excess Iron\n●\nLaterite soil excess iron ki presence ki wajah se infertile ho jaati hai — Desert sand, Alluvial, Podzolic\nsoils mein ye characteristic NAHI hai. [Q9]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0086","t":"09.iii Alluvial Soil","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" 🟤 ALLUVIAL SOIL — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Alluvial Soil — India's Largest & Most Fertile Group\n2. Composition — Potash/Phosphoric Rich, Nitrogen Poor\n3. River-Deposited Origin — Khadar vs Bangar\n4. Sand Content Gradient & Area Coverage (40%)\n5. Bhangar — Old Kachhari Clay\n6. Water Retention — Sandy vs Clayey/Loamy\n7. Loamy Soil Composition\n8. Chhattisgarh's Local Soil Names — Bhatha's Low pH\n1. Alluvial Soil — India's Largest & Most Fertile Group\n●\nAlluvial soil India ka sabse bada soil group hai — ~15 lakh sq km (45.6% total area), most\nproductive/fertile soil — Red, Black, Calcareous soil se zyada productive. [Q1, Q2, Q5, Q6]\n2. Composition — Potash/Phosphoric Rich, Nitrogen Poor\n●\nAlluvial soil Potash, Phosphoric acid, Alkalines mein rich hai — Nitrogen ki proportion kam hai. Saline\nsoils ke local naam: Reh, Thur, Chopan, Kallar, Rakar, Karl (in saline hone ka matlab yeh nahi ki poori\nAlluvial soil infertile hai — overall Alluvial soil bahut fertile hai). [Q1, Q4]\n3. River-Deposited Origin — Khadar vs Bangar\n●\nAlluvial soil rivers ke silt se bani hai (Himalayan sediments + sea-retreat) — do sub-categories: Khadar\n(new alluvium, floodplain mein, har saal naya deposit) aur Bangar (ancient alluvium, floods ki reach se\nupar). [Q3]\n4. Sand Content Gradient & Area Coverage (40%)\n●\nAlluvial soil ke sahi facts: sand content west se east ki taraf kam hoti jaati hai, Bhangar-Khadar forms\nmein hai, total area ka ~40% cover karti hai (NCERT ke mutabik), potash mein rich hai lekin\nphosphorus mein poor hai — sab 4 statements sahi hain. [Q4]\n5. Bhangar — Old Kachhari Clay\n●\nGangetic plain ki purani Kachhari clay ko 'Bhangar' kehte hain — floods ki reach se pare, higher level par\nmilta hai, calcareous concretions hote hain, pale reddish-brown color ka hota hai. [Q7]\n6. Water Retention — Sandy vs Clayey/Loamy\n●\nWater retention capacity comparison mein Alluvial sand soil ki sabse kam water retention capacity hoti\nhai — loamy sand, clayey loam, loamy soil se kam. [Q8]\n7. Loamy Soil Composition"," ●\nLoamy soil mein sab types ke particles (~40% sand, 18% clay, 42% silt) hote hain. [Q9]\n8. Chhattisgarh's Local Soil Names — Bhatha's Low pH\n●\nChhattisgarh ke local soil naam: Bhatha (laterite type, lowest pH ~6.5, acidic), Dorsa, Matasi, Kanhar —\nBhatha soil leached hai, sandy-loam se gravelly-sand texture ki hai, red/red-yellow color ki hai, often\nbarren land classify hoti hai. [Q10]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0087","t":"09.iv Soils Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" SOILS MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Soil-State Match Set (Alluvial-UP, Black-Maharashtra)\n2. Western Rajasthan Soils — High Calcium Content\n3. Nitrogen-Enriching Crops — Legumes (Pea)\n4. Soil Fertility Improvement — Black Gram (Urd)\n5. Red Soil — Ferric Oxide Colour\n6. Red Soil Rank — 3rd Largest (Not 2nd)\n7. Zinc — Most Deficient Micronutrient\n8. Himalayan Soils — Humus-Poor (Assertion-Reason Trap)\n9. Karewas — Kashmir Himalaya (Not Garhwal/Nepal)\n10. Soil Water Availability — Clay Soil Highest\n11. Particle Size Classification (Clay/Silt/Sand)\n12. Matasi Soil — Chhattisgarh's Altitude Position\n1. Soil-State Match Set (Alluvial-UP, Black-Maharashtra)\n●\nSoil-state match: Alluvial — Uttar Pradesh, Black — Maharashtra, Red — Andhra Pradesh, Desert —\nRajasthan. [Q1]\n2. Western Rajasthan Soils — High Calcium Content\n●\nWestern Rajasthan (Jaisalmer, Bikaner, Barmer, Jalore, Jodhpur etc.) ki soil alkaline aur saline hai,\ncalcareous base ke saath — Calcium content zyada hai (Aluminum, Nitrogen, Phosphorus se zyada nahi).\n[Q2]\n3. Nitrogen-Enriching Crops — Legumes (Pea)\n●\nLegume crops atmospheric nitrogen-fixation se soil mein nitrogen enrich karti hain — Pea (matar) is\ncategory mein hai (clover, soybean, alfalfa, peanut bhi) — Potato, Sorghum, Sunflower NAHI. [Q3]\n4. Soil Fertility Improvement — Black Gram (Urd)\n●\nSoil fertility improve karne ke liye Black Gram (Urd) ugaya jaata hai — Wheat, Rice, Sugarcane se nahi\n(Urd occasionally fodder ke roop mein bhi use hota hai). [Q4]\n5. Red Soil — Ferric Oxide Colour\n●\nRed soil ancient crystalline igneous aur metamorphic rocks ke weathering se bani hai — lime,\nphosphates, nitrogen, humus ki kami, potash mein rich, chemically siliceous-aluminous. Iska red color\nferric oxide ki presence se hai. [Q5]\n6. Red Soil Rank — 3rd Largest (Not 2nd)\n●\nRed soil India ka 2nd sabse bada soil group NAHI hai — asal mein 3rd sabse bada hai (Alluvial ke baad)\n(Assertion galat) — lekin Red soil, Black soil ko south/east/north se surround karti hai (Reason sahi hai)"," — Red soil ~10.6% area cover karti hai (Western TN, Karnataka, NE AP, S Maharashtra, Rajasthan, E MP,\nBihar, WB, Chhattisgarh, Telangana, Odisha, Chotanagpur Plateau). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP — Red soil 2nd sabse bada group NAHI hai — 3rd hai; Reason (Black soil ko surround\n⚠️\nkarna) sahi hai\n7. Zinc — Most Deficient Micronutrient\n●\nIndian soils mein Zinc sabse zyada deficient micronutrient hai — Copper, Iron, Manganese se zyada. [Q7]\n8. Himalayan Soils — Humus-Poor (Assertion-Reason Trap)\n●\nHimalayan soils humus se rich NAHI hain (Assertion galat) — kyunki Himalaya mein forest cover ka sabse\nbada area hone ke bawajood soil mein humus ki kami hoti hai (Reason sahi hai). [Q8]\n9. Karewas — Kashmir Himalaya (Not Garhwal/Nepal)\n●\nKarewa soil (Zafran/saffron cultivation ke liye) Kashmir Himalaya mein milti hai — Garhwal, Nepal,\nEastern Himalaya mein NAHI. [Q9]\n10. Soil Water Availability — Clay Soil Highest\n●\nPlants ke liye available soil water Clay soil mein maximum hota hai (highest water retention capacity) —\nClay: <50% silt, 50% clay, kuch sand — air ventilation slow karta hai isliye water sustain hota hai.\n[Q10]\n11. Particle Size Classification (Clay/Silt/Sand)\n●\nParticle diameter classification: Clay — <0.002mm, Silt — 0.002-0.05mm, Fine sand — 0.05-2mm. [Q11]\n12. Matasi Soil — Chhattisgarh's Altitude Position\n●\nMatasi soil (Chhattisgarh ka 55-60% area cover karti hai, red-yellow color, paddy cultivation ke liye prime)\n— Bhata soil se kam ऊंchai par aur Kanhar soil se zyada ऊंchai par milti hai (galat statement — asal\nmein Bhata se LOWER aur Kanhar se HIGHER hai), Iron oxide sabse abundant element hai. [Q12]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0088","t":"09.v Acidic and Alkali Soil","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" ACIDIC AND ALKALI SOIL — FULL MIND MAP\n⚗️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Usar Soil — pH, Deficiencies & Treatment\n2. Soil pH Scale — 6-7 Ideal for Crops\n3. Lime — Treatment for Acidic Soil\n4. Gypsum — Long-Term Salinity/Alkalinity Solution\n5. Maximum Alkali Area — Uttar Pradesh\n6. Maximum Saline Soil Area — Gujarat\n7. Salinization Process — Effects on Soil\n8. Saline Soil Unsuitability (Assertion-Reason)\n9. Tea Plantation — Slightly Acidic Soil\n1. Usar Soil — pH, Deficiencies & Treatment\n●\nUsar soil ka pH 7 se zyada hota hai — Bacteria, Nitrogen, Zinc ki severe kami hoti hai. Treatment:\nPyrites, Gypsum, green manure se hota hai (Lime NAHI, Lime acidic soil ke liye use hota hai). Tolerant\npaddy varieties (Narendra Shankar Usar Paddy-1, -2) iss soil mein grow ki jaa sakti hain. [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP — Lime — acidic soil ke liye use hota hai; Usar (alkaline) soil ke liye Gypsum/Pyrites use\n⚠️\nhote hain\n2. Soil pH Scale — 6-7 Ideal for Crops\n●\nSoil pH 7 se kam — acidic, 7 se zyada — alkaline hoti hai. Fertile soil (common crops ke liye) ka pH 6-7\nhota hai — is range mein nutrients easily dissolve hote hain. [Q2]\n3. Lime — Treatment for Acidic Soil\n●\nAcidic soil ko cultivable banane ke liye Lime (chuna) use hota hai — Gypsum, Calcium, Vegetable compost\nse NAHI. [Q3]\n4. Gypsum — Long-Term Salinity/Alkalinity Solution\n●\nSoil salinity aur alkalinity ka solution Gypsum use karna hai — ye dono short-term aur long-term\nsolution hai (alkalinity change karta hai, salinity remove karta hai, ~1 foot water leaching ke liye chahiye).\n[Q4, Q5]\n5. Maximum Alkali Area — Uttar Pradesh\n●\nIndia mein maximum alkali area Uttar Pradesh mein hai — Gujarat, Haryana, Punjab se zyada. [Q6]\n6. Maximum Saline Soil Area — Gujarat\n●\nIndia mein sabse zyada saline/salt-affected soil area Gujarat mein hai — UP, Haryana, Rajasthan, TN, AP\nse zyada (Desertification aur Land Degradation Atlas 2021 ke mutabik). [Q7, Q8]"," 7. Salinization Process — Effects on Soil\n●\nSalinization tab hoti hai jab irrigation water evaporate hoke salts-minerals chhod jaata hai — iska effect: kuch\nsoils ko impermeable bana deta hai — crop production ko badhaata NAHI, na hi groundwater level raise\nkarta hai. [Q9]\n8. Saline Soil Unsuitability (Assertion-Reason)\n●\nIndia mein saline soils crops ki cultivation ke liye appropriate NAHI hain (Assertion sahi) kyunki saline soils\nmein salt ka high proportion hota hai, mainly dry climate aur poor drainage ki wajah se (Reason sahi\nexplanation hai) — Sodium/Potassium excess, high Magnesium ratio, lime ki kami bhi hoti hai. [Q10]\n9. Tea Plantation — Slightly Acidic Soil\n●\nTea plantation ke liye slightly acidic, calcium-rahit soil sabse suited hai — Alkaline, Alluvial, Regur se\nnahi. Tea stagnant water ko tolerate nahi karti, isliye hill slopes par ugaayi jaati hai jahan drainage achha\nho. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0089","t":"09.vi Soil Erosion and Conservation","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / Indian Geography","x":[" SOIL EROSION AND CONSERVATION — FULL\n🏜️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Critical Soil Erosion Areas — Shivalik Foothills, Chambal\n2. Chambal Valley — MP's Erosion Hotspot (Morena)\n3. Gully Erosion — Chambal Ravines Cause\n4. Soil Erosion Process Order (Splash→Sheet→Rill→Gully)\n5. Sorghum — Most Erosion-Prone Crop\n6. Soil Fertility Methods — Crop Rotation vs Seed Modification\n7. Soil Conservation Practices (Terracing, Windbreaks)\n8. Soil Erosion Causes — Deforestation (Not Tropical Climate)\n9. Afforestation — Primary Erosion-Check Method\n10. Water Conservation Practices — Zero Tillage & Gypsum\n1. Critical Soil Erosion Areas — Shivalik Foothills, Chambal\n●\nIndia ke max soil-erosion-affected areas: Chambal-Yamuna ki barren land, Western Himalaya/Shivalik\nfoothills, Chotanagpur Plateau, Tapti-Sabarmati ke beech (Malwa Plateau), Maharashtra ka black soil\narea, Haryana-Rajasthan-Gujarat ke arid regions — Shivalik foothills mein soil erosion sabse critical\nhai. [Q1]\n2. Chambal Valley — MP's Erosion Hotspot (Morena)\n●\nIndia mein Chambal Valley soil erosion se sabse zyada affected hai — Madhya Pradesh mein specifically\nMorena district (Bhind, Gwalior, Shivpuri bhi) affected hai — 'Chambal ravines' banti hain. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Gully Erosion — Chambal Ravines Cause\n●\nChambal Ravines (bad-lands) Gully erosion ki wajah se bante hain — Splash, Sheet, Rill erosion se nahi.\n[Q4]\n4. Soil Erosion Process Order (Splash→Sheet→Rill→Gully)\n●\nSoil erosion process ka sahi order: Splash erosion (raindrop impact) → Sheet erosion (thin uniform layer\nremoval) → Rill erosion (small straight channels) → Gully erosion (rills se badi channels) — aage\nStream channel erosion bhi ho sakti hai. [Q5]\n5. Sorghum — Most Erosion-Prone Crop\n●\nWWF analysis ke mutabik Sorghum (jwar) ugane par farmland sabse tezi se erode hoti hai — Clover\nsabse kam erosion karti hai (Potato, Wheat in beech mein hain). [Q6]\n6. Soil Fertility Methods — Crop Rotation vs Seed Modification"," ●\nSoil fertility improve karne wale sahi methods: Crop rotation, Mixed cultivation, Multiple cropping —\nSeed modification soil fertility ko affect NAHI karta (sirf crop production ko affect karta hai). Crop\nrotation ka main purpose soil fertility badhaana hai (pest control mein bhi madad karta hai). [Q7, Q8]\n7. Soil Conservation Practices (Terracing, Windbreaks)\n●\nIndia mein appropriate soil conservation methods: Crop rotation, Terracing, Windbreaks — Sand fences\nappropriate NAHI hai India ke context mein. [Q9]\n8. Soil Erosion Causes — Deforestation (Not Tropical Climate)\n●\nSoil erosion ka problem Deforestation se associated hai — Terrace cultivation ek conservation method\nhai (erosion ka cause NAHI), aur Tropical climate bhi erosion ke liye responsible NAHI hai. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — Terrace cultivation — erosion ROKNE ka method hai, erosion ka CAUSE nahi hai\n⚠️\n9. Afforestation — Primary Erosion-Check Method\n●\nSoil erosion Afforestation (vanikaran) se check ki jaa sakti hai — Excess grazing, plant removal, bird-\ncount badhaana ise ROKte NAHI hain, balki contour tillage, shifting-cultivation ban bhi effective methods\nhain. [Q11, Q12]\n10. Water Conservation Practices — Zero Tillage & Gypsum\n●\nAgriculture mein water conservation ke sahi practices: Reduced/zero tillage (soil moisture conserve karta\nhai), Gypsum application before irrigation (salt-clay-pan dissolve karta hai, percolation improve karta\nhai), crop residue field mein chhodna (evaporation kam karta hai) — teeno sahi hain. [Q13]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0090","t":"01.i General Concept","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" General Concept\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n General Concept — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_i_General_Concept\nTopic Index\n1. Big Bang Theory — Universe ki utpatti\n2. Continental Drift Theory\n3. Milky Way aur Galaxy\n4. Stars — Colour, Temperature, Distance\n5. Chandrasekhar Limit, Black Holes, Supernova\n6. Astronomical Objects — Identification\n7. Distance Units — Light Year, AU\n8. Space/Sky Observations — Equator, Pole Star, Directions\n9. Miscellaneous — Solar Eclipse trigger, Natural time units\nBig Bang Theory — Universe ki utpatti\n● Big Bang Theory universe ki origin/evolution explain karta hai — ~13.8 billion years pehle ek hot, dense state se\nshuru hua. [Q1,Q2]\n● Georges Lemaître expanding-universe idea ke pioneer the; cosmic expansion aur CMB isko support karte hain.\n[Q1]\nContinental Drift Theory\n● A. Wegener (Alfred Wegener) ne continental drift theory develop ki — German geophysicist. [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Continental Drift = Wegener (options mein Du Toit, Hess bhi distractors hote hain — Wegener hi correct hai)\n[Q3]\nMilky Way aur Galaxy\n● Milky Way = Spiral Galaxy (barred spiral); hamara Solar System iske Orion Spur/Arm mein hai. [Q4]\n● Sun ko galactic centre ki 1 revolution karne mein ~22.5–25 crore years lagte hain — isko Cosmic Year /\nGalactic Year kehte hain. [Q5]\n● Tare ek particular shape ke group ko Constellation (तारामंडल) kehte hain. [Q19]\n● Total 88 constellations officially recognized hain (IAU ke according). [Q16]\nStars — Colour, Temperature, Distance"," General Concept\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Star ka colour uske temperature ka indicator hota hai (Blue = hottest ~50,000K, Red = coolest ~2,000-3,500K).\n[Q6]\n● Sun Earth ka sabse nearest star hai (~149.6 million km); Alpha Centauri Sun ke baad nearest star system hai;\nSirius ~8.6 light-years door. [Q9]\n● Betelgeuse — Orion constellation ka 2nd-brightest star; Hubble Space Telescope ne Sun ke alawa isi ka first\ndirect image liya tha. [Q20]\nChandrasekhar Limit, Black Holes, Supernova\n● Chandrasekhar Limit — S. Chandrasekhar (Indo-American physicist) ne bataya ki white dwarf ka max mass\n~1.4 times solar mass hota hai; iske aage star collapse ho jaata hai (neutron star/black hole). [Q7,Q10,Q11,Q12]\n● Chandrasekhar ko is work ke liye 1983 Nobel Prize in Physics mila tha. [Q7,Q12]\n● Black Hole = collapsed star, extremely high density; itna strong gravity ki light bhi escape nahi kar sakti —\ntelescope se directly nahi dikhta. [Q8,Q13,Q14]\n● Supernova = dying star ka large explosion, jab star ke core mein change hota hai (2 types: binary system OR\nsingle star life-end). [Q15]\n● Terms — Event Horizon (black hole boundary), Singularity (infinite gravity point), String Theory, Standard\nModel — sab Universe observation/understanding ke context mein aate hain. [Q28]\nAstronomical Objects — Identification\n● Astronomical objects: Pulsar, Black Hole, Quasar — sab space mein hote hain. [Q17,Q18]\n● Brittle Star astronomical object NAHI hai — yeh ek marine echinoderm (Ophiuroidea class) hai, sea floor pe\nrehta hai, Starfish se related. [Q17,Q18]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Brittle Star naam mein 'Star' hai lekin yeh sea creature hai, astronomical object nahi — common confusion\npoint. [Q17,Q18]\nDistance Units — Light Year, AU\n● Light Year = distance ki unit (na ki time) — light ek year mein vacuum mein jitni distance cover karta hai.\n[Q22,Q23]\n● Tare-tare ke beech distance measure karne ke liye Light Year use hota hai. [Q23]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Light Year time ki NAHI, distance ki unit hai — common mistake. [Q22]\nSpace/Sky Observations — Equator, Pole Star, Directions\n● Agar observer ko stars horizon ke perpendicular rise hote dikhein, toh wo Equator pe located hoga (celestial\npoles horizon pe lie karte hain equator se). [Q24]\n● Pole Star north direction mein shine karta hai — East ki taraf jaane ke liye Pole Star ko apni left side pe rakhna\nchahiye. [Q25]"," General Concept\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Saptarishi (group of stars) pole/north direction batata hai. [Q26]\n● Vacuum/space mein: sky black dikhta hai + stars twinkle nahi karte (atmosphere ke absence ki wajah se);\nbackground temp ~2.7K hota hai jo Earth surface se bahut kam hai. [Q21]\nMiscellaneous — Solar Eclipse trigger, Natural time units\n● 'Byte' space terminology se related NAHI hai (computer term hai) — Telemetering, Weightlessness, Cislunar sab\nspace terms hain. [Q27]\n● Standard Time natural unit of time NAHI hai — Tropical year, Lunar month, Day sab natural units hain\n(Earth/Moon ki motion pe based). [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0091","t":"01.ii The Solar System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Solar System\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Solar System — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_ii_The_Solar_System\nTopic Index\n1. Solar System — Composition\n2. Heliocentric Model — Copernicus\n3. Planets — Count aur Order\n4. Planet Sizes — Largest/Smallest, Order\n5. Planet Composition, Density, Light\n6. Match/Identification Questions\n7. Goldilocks Zone aur Solar System Facts\nSolar System — Composition\n● Solar System ~4.6 billion years pehle bana; isme Sun, planets, dwarf planets, satellites, asteroids, comets,\nmeteoroids, cosmic dust hote hain. [Q1]\n● Nebula Solar System ka part NAHI hai (baaki sab options — asteroids, comets, planets — part hain). [Q1]\nHeliocentric Model — Copernicus\n● Nicolaus Copernicus ne modern heliocentric model diya — Earth Sun ki parikrama karti hai, na ki centre mein\nhai (16th century, Scientific Revolution ki shuruaat). [Q2,Q3,Q4,Q5]\n● Baad mein Galileo ke observations aur Kepler ke orbital laws ne heliocentrism ko support diya. [Q2,Q3,Q4]\nPlanets — Count aur Order\n● Currently 8 planets recognized hain: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune (2006 mein\nPluto ko dwarf planet declare kiya gaya). [Q7]\n● Sun se badhti distance order: Mercury → Venus → Earth → Mars → Jupiter → Saturn → Uranus → Neptune.\n[Q8,Q9,Q10,Q11]\n● Mars aur Uranus ke beech: Jupiter aur Saturn hain. [Q8]\n● Earth Venus aur Mars ke beech located hai; Mercury aur Venus ke beech koi planet nahi (Earth Sun-Venus ke\nbeech nahi). [Q10,Q11]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Q10 mein 'Earth-Sun ke beech planets' poocha — answer Mercury aur Venus (dono Earth ki orbit se andar\nhain), Mars/Venus wala combo Q11 (Earth ke around) se confuse mat karo. [Q10,Q11]\nPlanet Sizes — Largest/Smallest, Order"," The Solar System\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Size order (descending): Jupiter > Saturn > Uranus > Neptune > Earth > Venus > Mars > Mercury.\n[Q13,Q16]\n● Mercury = smallest planet; Jupiter = largest planet. [Q13,Q14]\n● Neptune = slowest orbital-velocity planet (NOT Mars) — ~165 years mein 1 revolution. [Q15]\nPlanet Composition, Density, Light\n● Earth ka average density sabse zyada (~5.5 g/cm³) — Mercury 5.4, Venus 5.2, Mars 3.9, Jupiter 1.3, Saturn 0.7\n(lowest), Uranus 1.3, Neptune 1.6. [Q6]\n● Earth composition: Iron (32%), Oxygen (30%), Silicon (15%) — silicon predominant NAHI hai. [Q6]\n● Sun ka mass Solar System ke total mass ka ~99.8% hai (75% nahi); Sun ka diameter Earth ka ~109.2 times hai\n(190 times nahi). [Q6]\n● Jupiter aur Saturn mein mainly Hydrogen aur Helium hoti hai, saath mein Methane bhi. [Q17]\n● Planets non-luminous bodies hain (khud light produce nahi karte) lekin Sun ki light reflect karke chamakte hain.\n[Q12]\nMatch/Identification Questions\n● Smallest planet = Mercury; Largest = Jupiter; 2nd planet from Sun = Venus; Farthest recognized planet =\nNeptune. [Q13]\n● Florida USA ka state hai, planet nahi (Mercury, Venus, Saturn planets hain). [Q18]\n● Uranus = planet, Moon = natural satellite, Halley = comet, Mariner = artificial satellite/spacecraft. [Q20]\nGoldilocks Zone aur Solar System Facts\n● Goldilocks Zone (circumstellar habitable zone) = star ke around wo region jahan liquid water exist kar sake —\nEarth is zone mein hai, isliye life-bearing hai. [Q19]\n● Solar System ka chief celestial body Sun hai (centre mein located). [Q22]\n● Venus Earth ke sabse close aa sakta hai (closest-approach distance ke hisaab se). [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Statements set: Mercury sabse hot planet NAHI (Venus hai); Ganymede Saturn ka NAHI, Jupiter ka moon\nhai; Neptune ke rings methane gas ke NAHI, dust/ice particles ke hain; sirf Phobos-Deimos (Mars ke moons)\nwala statement correct hai. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0092","t":"01.iii The Sun","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Sun\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Sun — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_iii_The_Sun\nTopic Index\n1. Sun ki Composition aur Energy Source\n2. Solar Eclipse\n3. Halo aur Optical Phenomena\n4. Astronomical Unit aur Earth-Sun Distance\n5. Earth ki Motion — Rotation vs Revolution\nSun ki Composition aur Energy Source\n● Sun ke centre mein matter gas aur plasma state mein hota hai (ionised gas). [Q1]\n● Solar energy nuclear fusion se produce hoti hai (nuclear fission se NAHI) — light nuclei combine hoke heavier\nnucleus banate hain. [Q2]\n● Photosphere = Sun ki bright outer/visible layer, temperature ~5,500–6,000°C. [Q15]\nSolar Eclipse\n● Solar eclipse tab hota hai jab Moon Earth aur Sun ke beech aa jaata hai — sirf New Moon/Amavasya ke din\npossible hai. [Q4,Q5,Q6]\n● Total solar eclipse sirf limited geographical region mein dikhta hai kyunki Moon ki shadow Earth ke cross-\nsection se chhoti hoti hai. [Q7]\n● Diamond Ring effect totality ke beginning AUR end dono par dikhta hai. [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Solar eclipse New Moon/Amavasya pe hota hai, Lunar eclipse Full Moon/Poornima pe — dono ko mix mat\nkaro. [Q4,Q5,Q6]\nHalo aur Optical Phenomena\n● Sun ka Halo — cirrus clouds mein ice crystals se light refraction ke through banta hai. [Q8]\nAstronomical Unit aur Earth-Sun Distance\n● Astronomical Unit (AU) = Earth aur Sun ke beech average distance = ~149.6 million km (149.598 × 10⁶ km).\n[Q9,Q10,Q11]\n● Earth Sun ke sabse close 3 January ko hoti hai — isko Perihelion kehte hain; farthest ~4 July ko — Aphelion.\n[Q12]\n● Sun ka diameter Earth se ~109 times zyada hai. [Q13]"," The Sun\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nEarth ki Motion — Rotation vs Revolution\n● Statement check: 'Rotation west-to-east se seasonal changes hote hain' — GALAT (rotation se day-night hota\nhai); 'Revolution se day-night' bhi GALAT (revolution se seasons hote hain) — dono statements incorrect hain.\n[Q14]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Rotation (axis pe ghumna) = Day-Night; Revolution (Sun ke around) = Seasons — is swap ko exam mein\ntest kiya jaata hai. [Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0093","t":"01.iv The Mercury","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Mercury\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Mercury — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_iv_The_Mercury\nTopic Index\n1. Mercury — Orbit aur Speed\n2. Mercury — Satellites aur Albedo\nMercury — Orbit aur Speed\n● Elliptical orbit mein planet Sun ke sabse nearest point pe hota hai, wahan uski kinetic energy sabse zyada hoti\nhai (gravity strongest, speed fastest). [Q1]\n● Mercury sabse kam time (88 days) mein Sun ki 1 revolution complete karta hai — sabse fast. [Q2]\nMercury — Satellites aur Albedo\n● Mercury aur Venus — ye 2 planets hain jinke koi natural satellite/moon nahi hai. [Q3]\n● Albedo = reflective properties measure karta hai. Mercury ka albedo Earth se kam hai (~0.1 vs Earth ~0.3), zyada\nnahi — sirf Statement 1 (albedo defines brightness) correct hai. [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Mercury ko zyada sunlight milta hai lekin uska albedo Earth se KAM hai — 'zyada sunlight = zyada albedo'\nassume mat karo. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0094","t":"01.ix The Saturn","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Saturn\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Saturn — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_ix_The_Saturn\nTopic Index\n1. Saturn — Orbit aur Rings\n2. Saturn — Temperature aur Missions\n3. Saturn — Moons\nSaturn — Orbit aur Rings\n● Saturn Sun ki 1 revolution ~29.5 years mein complete karta hai. [Q1]\n● Saturn apne distinctive ring-system ke liye famous hai — 7 major rings identified; A, B, D, E rings Earth se\ndikhte hain; Saturn Earth se dekhne pe yellow dikhta hai. [Q2]\n● Saturn ke alawa Jupiter, Uranus, Neptune ke bhi rings hain. [Q2]\nSaturn — Temperature aur Missions\n● Cassini spacecraft 7 saal ki journey ke baad June 2004 mein Saturn ki orbit mein enter hua (launched 15 Oct\n1997). [Q3]\n● Saturn Neptune se warmer hai (kyunki Saturn Sun ke zyada close hai order:\nMercury→Venus→Earth→Mars→Jupiter→Saturn→Uranus→Neptune). [Q4]\nSaturn — Moons\n● Titan Saturn ka largest moon hai (diameter ~5,150 km); doosra largest Rhea hai (~1,528 km). Other moons:\nAtlas, Epimetheus, Tethys, Iapetus, Dione, Phoebe, Helene, Enceladus. [Q5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0095","t":"01.v The Venus","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Venus\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Venus — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_v_The_Venus\nTopic Index\n1. Venus — Hottest Planet aur Names\n2. Venus — Life aur Atmosphere\n3. Venus — Space Missions\nVenus — Hottest Planet aur Names\n● Venus Solar System ka sabse hot planet hai (~464°C), Mercury nahi — kyunki Venus ke atmosphere mein CO₂\nbahut zyada hai (dense greenhouse effect). [Q1]\n● Venus ko Evening Star aur Morning Star dono kehte hain — sabse bright planet hai. [Q2,Q3]\n● Venus ko Earth ki 'Twin Sister' bhi kehte hain — size, mass aur composition Earth ke similar hai. [Q3,Q5]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Hottest planet = Venus (Mercury nahi), kyunki distance se zyada CO₂ concentration matter karta hai. [Q1]\nVenus — Life aur Atmosphere\n● Venus pe human life highly improbable hai — atmosphere mein ~96.5% CO₂ hai aur surface temperature\n400°C+ hai. [Q4]\nVenus — Space Missions\n● Magellan spacecraft Venus ki surface map karne bheja gaya tha (launched 4 May 1989, orbit entered 10 Aug\n1990). [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0096","t":"01.vi The Earth","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Earth\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Earth — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_vi_The_Earth\nTopic Index\n1. Earth ki Shape aur Discovery\n2. Earth ka Structure — Core, Crust\n3. Earth ki Motion — Rotation, Revolution, Speed\n4. Earth ki Axis Tilt aur Seasons\n5. Magnetic Field aur Poles\n6. Satellites aur Orbital Mechanics\n7. Earth ka History aur Atmosphere\n8. Deserts aur Earth Day\nEarth ki Shape aur Discovery\n● Aristotle sabse pehle bataya ki Earth spherical hai ('On the Heavens' mein). [Q1]\n● Life ke context mein Earth ko 'Green Planet' kehte hain (vegetation/life ki widespread presence ki wajah se).\n[Q2]\n● Earth ka diameter ~12,800 km hai (equatorial ~12,756 km, polar ~12,714 km). [Q3]\n● Earth ka shape oblate spheroid / geoid hai — perfect sphere nahi (Equator pe bulge, poles pe flat). [Q4]\n● Weight Equator se poles ki taraf badhta hai (centrifugal effect Equator pe max) — high latitude jaane pe weight\nbadhta hai, ghatta nahi. [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Assertion 'weight decreases with higher latitude' FALSE hai — actually weight INCREASES; sirf Reason\n(Earth not perfect sphere) TRUE hai — 'A false, R true' pattern. [Q4]\nEarth ka Structure — Core, Crust\n● Earth's crust mein sabse abundant element Oxygen hai (46.60%), phir Silicon (27.72%), Aluminium (8.13%).\n[Q6]\n● Earth ka core mainly Nickel aur Iron (NiFe) se bana hai — outer core liquid, inner core solid. [Q27,Q28]\n● Outer core ~2,260 km thick (liquid Fe+Ni); inner core radius ~1,220 km, extremely hot/dense, mainly Iron.\n[Q28]\n● Moon ka core bhi solid inner + liquid outer hota hai (Earth jaisa hi structure, lekin proportion mein chhota). [Q5]\nEarth ki Motion — Rotation, Revolution, Speed\n● Sunlight Sun se Earth tak pahunchne mein ~8 minutes 19 seconds leta hai. [Q7,Q8]\n● Sun Earth ka nearest star hai (~149.6 million km). [Q9]"," The Earth\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Mars given options mein Earth ke sabse close hai (long-term); Venus closest-approach mein sabse close aa sakta\nhai (favourable alignment mein). [Q10,Q11]\n● Earth 1 revolution ~365.25 days (365 din 6 ghante 9 min) mein complete karti hai — isko Solar Year kehte hain.\n[Q12]\n● Earth ki average orbital speed ~30 km/sec (29.8 km/s) hai. [Q13]\n● Earth apni axis pe rotate karte hue ~28 km/minute distance cover karti hai (equatorial rotation speed ~1,670\nkm/hr). [Q14]\n● Earth ki equatorial circumference ~40,000 km hai. [Q15]\nEarth ki Axis Tilt aur Seasons\n● Earth ka rotational axis ecliptic plane ke normal se ~23.5° tilted hai. [Q16,Q31]\n● Seasonal changes 2 factors se hote hain: Axial tilt (23½°) + Revolution around Sun — dono zaroori hain.\n[Q21,Q22]\n● Day-Night Earth ke rotation se hote hain (revolution se nahi). [Q19]\n● 21 March/23 Sept ko Sun ki rays Equator pe vertically padti hain — day-night equal hote hain. [Q20]\n● Delhi mein summer noon temperature winter se zyada hota hai kyunki winter mein sunlight zyada obliquely\n(tirchhi) padti hai. [Q23]\nMagnetic Field aur Poles\n● Statement: Magnetic field axis 23½° tilted (Geographic axis se) — INCORRECT hai; Magnetic North Pole\nnorthern Canada peninsula pe hai aur Magnetic Equator Thumba (South India) se guzarti hai — dono\nCORRECT. [Q17]\n● Earth ka magnetic field har few hundred thousand years mein reverse hota raha hai (geological history mein).\n[Q32]\n● North Pole = Earth ke axis ka northern end; 45° latitude ki length Equator ki half NAHI hoti (misconception);\nEarth's axis parallelism maintain karta hai revolution ke dauraan. [Q18]\n● Aphelion (~4 July) pe Earth ki orbital speed kam hoti hai, zyada nahi. [Q18]\nSatellites aur Orbital Mechanics\n● Agar Sun-Earth distance ¼ kam ho jaaye, toh year ki duration kam ho jaayegi (smaller orbit = faster revolution).\n[Q24]\n● Assertion: satellites hamesha eastward launch hote hain — FALSE (polar-orbit satellites north/south bhi jaate\nhain); Reason: west-to-east rotation launch-velocity mein help karta hai — TRUE. [Q25]\n● Agar ball ko satellite se release kiya jaaye bina extra velocity, wo same orbit mein Earth ki parikrama\ncontinue karegi (satellite jaisi hi speed se). [Q26]\nEarth ka History aur Atmosphere\n● Statement check: Magnetic field reversal CORRECT; early atmosphere mein 54% oxygen tha — INCORRECT\n(early atmosphere mein bahut kam/negligible free oxygen tha); living organisms ne early atmosphere modify\nkiya — CORRECT (photosynthetic algae/cyanobacteria). [Q32]"," The Earth\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Aryabhata sabse pehle explain kiya ki Earth ka apne axis pe rotation hi Sun ke daily rise/set ka apparent karan\nhai. [Q33]\nDeserts aur Earth Day\n● Desert formation ki probability ~23° latitude (subtropical belt, 15°-30°) ke around zyada hoti hai — subtropical\nhigh-pressure descending dry air ki wajah se. [Q34]\n● World/International Earth Day har saal 22 April ko manaya jaata hai (first Earth Day 1970 mein). [Q29,Q30]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0097","t":"01.vii The Mars","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Mars\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Mars — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_vii_The_Mars\nTopic Index\n1. Mars — Earth Se Similarity\n2. Mars — Orbit aur Size\n3. Mars aur Europa — Life Possibility\n4. Mars Missions\nMars — Earth Se Similarity\n● Mars ka day duration (~24h 37m) aur axis tilt (~25°12′) Earth (~23h 56m, ~23°30′) ke bahut close hain — sabse\nzyada similar planet. [Q1]\nMars — Orbit aur Size\n● Assertion: Mars Earth se kam time leta hai revolution mein — FALSE (Mars ~687 days leta hai, Earth ~365);\nReason: Mars ka diameter Earth se kam hai — TRUE. [Q2]\nMars aur Europa — Life Possibility\n● Mars pe life possibility ka strongest indicator: polar ice caps aur frozen water ki presence. [Q3]\n● Extraterrestrial life ke liye favourable maane jaate hain: Mars aur Europa (Jupiter ka moon — icy surface ke\nneeche vast ocean ho sakta hai). [Q4]\nMars Missions\n● Phoenix Mars Lander 25 May 2008 ko Mars ke northern polar region mein land hua (launched Aug 2007,\nmission ended Nov 2008) — options mein 26 May closest date treat ki gayi. [Q5]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0098","t":"01.viii The Jupiter","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Jupiter\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Jupiter — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_viii_The_Jupiter\nTopic Index\n1. Jupiter — Discovery aur Size\n2. Jupiter — Orbit aur Rings\n3. Jupiter — Moons Count\nJupiter — Discovery aur Size\n● Jupiter ke 4 largest moons — Io, Europa, Callisto, Ganymede — 'Galilean Moons' kehlate hain (Galileo Galilei\nne 1610 mein discover kiye). [Q1]\n● Jupiter Solar System ka largest AND heaviest planet hai (diameter ~142,984 km, density ~1,326 kg/m³); apne\naxis pe sabse fast rotate karta hai. [Q2,Q3]\nJupiter — Orbit aur Rings\n● Given options mein Jupiter Sun ki 1 revolution mein sabse zyada time (~11.86 years) leta hai (Earth 365 din,\nMars 687 din, Venus 224.7 din). [Q4]\n● Jupiter ke rings fine dust particles se bane hain (1979 mein Voyager 1 ne discover kiya); Saturn ke rings se thin\naur faint hain. [Q5]\nJupiter — Moons Count\n● 2009 exam context mein Jupiter ke sabse zyada known moons the (option A correct tha us waqt). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• NOTE: 2009 ke baad Saturn ne moon-count mein Jupiter ko overtake kar liya hai (2025 tak Saturn 274+,\nJupiter 95+) — lekin exam-year context mein Jupiter hi correct answer maana jaata hai. [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0099","t":"01.x The Uranus Neptune and Pluto","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Uranus Neptune and Pluto\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Uranus Neptune and Pluto — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_x_The_Uranus_Neptune_and_Pluto\nTopic Index\n1. Solar System Facts Recap\n2. Uranus — Orbit\n3. Pluto aur Longest Year\n4. 2006 IAU Reclassification\n5. Temperature aur Farthest Planet\n6. Pluto ke Moons\nSolar System Facts Recap\n● Statement set: Mercury sabse hot planet NAHI (Venus hai); Ganymede Saturn ka NAHI, Jupiter ka moon hai;\nNeptune ke rings methane gas ke NAHI (dust/ice ke) hain; sirf Phobos-Deimos Mars ke moons wala statement\n(4) correct hai. [Q1]\nUranus — Orbit\n● Uranus Sun ki 1 revolution ~84 years mein complete karta hai; ek din ~17h 14m ka hota hai. [Q2]\nPluto aur Longest Year\n● Given celestial bodies mein Pluto ka year sabse longa hai (~248 Earth years) — Pluto ab dwarf planet hai. [Q3]\n● Orbital periods: Jupiter ~11.9 yrs, Uranus ~84 yrs, Neptune ~165 yrs, Pluto ~248 yrs — Pluto sabse zyada leta\nhai. [Q4]\n● 8 planets mein Neptune sabse zyada time (~165 years) leta hai (Pluto ab planet nahi hai isliye exclude). [Q5]\n2006 IAU Reclassification\n● 2006 mein IAU (26th General Assembly) ne Pluto ko planet category se hataya — ab 'dwarf planet' status hai.\n[Q6]\n● Mercury 8 recognized planets mein sabse chhota hai (Pluto chhota hai lekin ab planet category mein nahi). [Q7]\nTemperature aur Farthest Planet\n● Neptune ka average atmospheric temperature sabse kam hai (~-200°C) given options mein. [Q8]\n● Purani classification mein farthest planet kabhi Neptune, kabhi Pluto hota tha — Pluto ki highly elliptical orbit\nkabhi-kabhi use Neptune se close le aati thi (1979-1999 ke beech Pluto Neptune se close tha). [Q9,Q10]"," The Uranus Neptune and Pluto\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 1979-1999 period mein Neptune temporarily farthest planet tha, na ki Pluto (jo apni highly elliptical orbit ki\nwajah se Sun ke closer aa gaya tha). [Q10]\nPluto ke Moons\n● Pluto ke 5 known moons (inner se outer): Charon, Styx, Nix, Kerberos, Hydra — Charon sabse bada hai.\n[Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0100","t":"01.xi The Moon","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Moon\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Moon — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_xi_The_Moon\nTopic Index\n1. Apollo 11 — First Moon Landing\n2. Moon ki Rotation — Synchronous\n3. Moon — No Atmosphere\n4. Lunar Eclipse\n5. Moon ki Distance aur Brightness\n6. Moon = Satellite, Planet Nahi\n7. Blue Moon aur Weight Change\n8. Moon Missions\nApollo 11 — First Moon Landing\n● Human ne pehli baar Moon pe kadam rakha 20 July 1969 ko — Apollo 11 mission (astronauts: Neil Armstrong,\nMichael Collins, Edwin 'Buzz' Aldrin). [Q1]\n● Armstrong aur Aldrin surface pe utre, Collins command module mein orbit karte rahe. Landing site: 'Sea of\nTranquility' (lunar mare Moon pe hota hai). [Q1,Q2]\nMoon ki Rotation — Synchronous\n● Moon ka lagbhag wahi face hamesha Earth ki taraf rehta hai — kyunki Moon ka axis-rotation period aur Earth-\norbit period dono ~27.3 days hain (synchronous rotation). [Q3,Q4]\n● Libration ki wajah se Earth se time ke saath Moon ki surface ka ~59% dikh jaata hai. [Q3]\nMoon — No Atmosphere\n● Moon pe do log ek dusre ki awaaz directly nahi sun sakte kyunki Moon pe atmosphere nahi hai (sound ko\nmedium chahiye). [Q5]\nLunar Eclipse\n● Lunar eclipse tab hota hai jab Earth Sun aur Moon ke beech aa jaati hai — sirf Full Moon/Poornima ke din\npossible. [Q6,Q7,Q8]\nMoon ki Distance aur Brightness\n● 22 Dec 1999 ki full-moon brightness ka main reason: Moon Perigee position mein tha (Earth ke sabse close\npoint). [Q9]"," The Moon\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Jab Moon half-illuminated dikhta hai, Sun-Earth-Moon ke beech angle 90° hota hai. [Q10]\n● Moon ki Earth se average distance ~384 thousand km (384,400 km) hai. [Q16]\nMoon = Satellite, Planet Nahi\n● Mars, Mercury, Earth planets hain; Moon Earth ka satellite hai (odd one out / not a planet). [Q11,Q12]\n● Match: Planet-Uranus, Satellite-Moon, Comet-Halley, Artificial spacecraft-Mariner. [Q13]\nBlue Moon aur Weight Change\n● 'Blue Moon' = same calendar month mein 2 full moons occur karna (2nd full moon ko Blue Moon kehte hain).\n[Q14]\n● Earth se Moon pe object le jaane pe weight kam ho jaata hai (~1/6th) — Moon ka gravitational acceleration\nEarth ka ~1/6 hai; mass same rehta hai. [Q15]\nMoon Missions\n● Japan pehla Asian country tha jisne SELENE (Kaguya) lunar orbiter Moon ki orbit mein bheja (launched 14\nSept 2007, ~1 year 10 months orbit ki). [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0101","t":"01.xii The Asteroids","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Asteroids\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Asteroids — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_xii_The_Asteroids\nTopic Index\n1. Asteroids — Location aur Size\n2. Asteroids vs Comets — Difference\nAsteroids — Location aur Size\n● Asteroids = small rock-pieces jo Mars aur Jupiter ki orbits ke beech Sun ki parikrama karte hain. [Q1,Q2,Q3]\n● Kuch asteroids ka diameter ~1000 km tak ho sakta hai. [Q1,Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Asteroid belt Mars-Jupiter ke beech hai, Jupiter-Saturn ke beech NAHI — common location confusion. [Q3]\nAsteroids vs Comets — Difference\n● Asteroids rocky/metallic hote hain (Mars-Jupiter ke beech), Comets ice+dust+rock se bane hote hain (Kuiper\nBelt/Oort Cloud mein door bante hain). [Q4]\n● Comets Sun ke close aane par glowing tail develop karte hain, Asteroids mein tail nahi hota. [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Statement 'comets Venus-Mercury ke beech pate jaate hain' GALAT hai — Comets Kuiper Belt/Oort Cloud\nmein (bahut door) bante hain, Venus-Mercury ke beech nahi. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0102","t":"01.xiii The Comets and Meteors","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Comets and Meteors\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Comets and Meteors — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 01_xiii_The_Comets_and_Meteors\nTopic Index\n1. Comet ki Tail\n2. Famous Comets\n3. Meteors\nComet ki Tail\n● Comet ki tail hamesha Sun se opposite direction mein hoti hai kyunki solar radiation pressure coma (comet ke\naround vaporized gas/dust) pe radial pressure daalta hai. [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Tail centrifugal force ki wajah se NAHI banti — solar radiation pressure hi asli reason hai. [Q1]\nFamous Comets\n● Hale-Bopp — long-period comet, 1995 mein discover hua (Alan Hale + Thomas Bopp, independently). [Q2]\n● Shoemaker-Levy 9 comet Jupiter se collide hua tha (16-22 July 1994) — pehli directly-observed collision\nbetween 2 Solar System bodies. [Q3]\nMeteors\n● Meteor = outer space se Earth ke atmosphere mein enter hone wala matter ka piece ('shooting star'/'falling star')\n— atmospheric friction se glow karta hai, zyadatar surface tak pahunchne se pehle burn ho jaate hain. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0103","t":"02.i Latitudes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Latitudes\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Latitudes — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_i_Latitudes\nTopic Index\n1. Latitude Basics — Range aur Great Circles\n2. 0° Latitude x 0° Longitude Intersection\n3. Coordinate se Location Identify Karna\n4. Cities — Latitude Comparison\n5. 1° Interval Latitude Lines — Counting\nLatitude Basics — Range aur Great Circles\n● Valid latitude range: 90° North se 90° South tak hi possible hai (91° North jaisi values invalid); 91° East/West\nlongitude ho sakti hai, latitude nahi. [Q1]\n● Great Circle = wo circle jo globe ko 2 equal hemispheres mein divide kare — sirf Equator (latitudes mein) aur\nhar meridian+opposite meridian pair great circle banate hain. Baaki koi bhi latitude (jaise 60°N) great circle\nnahi hoti. [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Sirf Equator hi ek latitude hai jo great circle hai — baaki sab parallels chhote hote hain. [Q2]\n0° Latitude x 0° Longitude Intersection\n● Equator (0° lat) aur Prime Meridian (0° long) ka intersection point Atlantic Ocean mein hai (Gulf of Guinea).\n[Q3,Q4]\nCoordinate se Location Identify Karna\n● ~5°E, 50°N coordinate Belgium (Europe) ke close match karta hai. [Q5]\n● Antipode calculation: latitude sign flip hota hai (30°N → 30°S); longitude ke liye 180° se subtract karke direction\nflip karo (50°E → 180-50=130°W). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Antipode longitude nikalne ke liye simple opposite mat lo — formula hai: 180° − given longitude, phir\ndirection (E↔W) flip karo. [Q6]\nCities — Latitude Comparison\n● Given cities mein Rome (41°54′N) sabse north hai (Beijing 39°55′N, New York 40°45′N, New Delhi 28°38′N se\nzyada). [Q7]"," Latitudes\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Sabse zyada north-south (latitudinal) extension wale desh ka answer 'More than one' hai — Chile ka continuous\nmainland extent sabse zyada hai, lekin Russia ka total extent (islands including) usse bhi zyada hai. [Q8]\n1° Interval Latitude Lines — Counting\n● Agar 1° interval pe latitude lines banayi jaayein: Northern Hemisphere mein 89 + Southern Hemisphere mein 89\n+ Equator 1 = total 179 lines. [Q9]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0104","t":"02.ii The Longitude","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Longitude\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Longitude — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_ii_The_Longitude\nTopic Index\n1. Longitude-Time Relationship — Base Formula\n2. Longitude Calculation Problems (Numericals)\n3. Great Circle aur Prime Meridian\n4. New Millennium First Sunrise (India)\n5. Standard Time — Basis\n6. Prime Meridian — Countries se Guzarna\n7. GMT-Same-Time Places\n8. GMT Se Aage/Peeche — Countries Ranking\n9. International Date Line (IDL)\n10. IDL Crossing — Date Change Puzzles\n11. Shortest Distance — Great Circle Route\n12. Natural vs Man-made Time Units\n13. Time Zones — Countries with Dependencies\nLongitude-Time Relationship — Base Formula\n● 1° longitude = 4 minutes time (15° longitude = 1 hour) — yeh saari calculation ka base formula hai. [Q3,Q26]\n● Cairo Greenwich se 2 hours aage hai → Cairo ~30° East pe hai (2 hours × 15° = 30°, East kyunki time aage hai).\n[Q1]\n● 90° longitude difference = 6 hours time difference (90×4=360 min = 6 hrs). [Q3]\n● Greenwich noon (12) pe agar kisi jagah 5pm ho, wo jagah 75° East hogi (5hrs × 15° = 75°, East kyunki aage hai).\n[Q4]\nLongitude Calculation Problems (Numericals)\n● 82°30′E pe noon ho, toh 6:30am kahan hoga? Answer: 0° (Prime Meridian) — 5.5 hrs difference = 82°30′\nlongitude difference, jo exactly 82°30′E se subtract karke 0° deta hai. [Q2]\n● Greenwich se telegram 12 noon pe bheja, 12 min transmission, 6pm pahuncha → destination 87° East (348 min\neffective time × 15/60 = 87°). [Q14]\n● IST meridian (82°30′E) pe noon ho, kisi jagah 6am ho (breakfast time) → us jagah ka longitude 7°30′ West hoga\n(6 hrs = 90° difference, IST se west mein 90° → 82°30′E - 90° = 7°30′W). [Q13]\n● GMT 3am ho aur local time 6am ho, toh place 45° East pe hoga (3 hrs ahead = 45° East). [Q24]\n● Greenwich noon ho, Thimphu (90°E) ka local time 6pm hoga (90° = 6 hrs ahead). [Q25]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Longitude-time problems mein hamesha check karo: East = time AAGE, West = time PEECHHE. Direction\ngalat lena sabse common mistake hai. [Q1,Q4,Q24,Q25]"," The Longitude\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nGreat Circle aur Prime Meridian\n● 0° aur 180° longitude milkar ek Great Circle banate hain (Prime Meridian + its opposite meridian). [Q5]\nNew Millennium First Sunrise (India)\n● New Millennium (2000) mein India mein sunrise ki first ray Katchal Island (Andaman-Nicobar) ke paas dekhi\ngayi — closest option 93°30′E. [Q6]\nStandard Time — Basis\n● Standard time ka basis Longitude hai — country ek standard meridian choose karta hai, uska local mean time\nstandard time banta hai. [Q7]\nPrime Meridian — Countries se Guzarna\n● Prime Meridian in countries se guzarti hai: UK, France, Spain, Algeria, Mali, Burkina Faso, Togo, Ghana.\n[Q8,Q9]\n● Prime Meridian Niger, Nigeria, Portugal se NAHI guzarti. [Q8,Q9]\nGMT-Same-Time Places\n● GMT/UTC use karne wale places (is question context mein): Accra (Ghana), Dublin (Ireland), Lisbon (Portugal)\n— Madrid Central European Time use karta hai, GMT nahi. [Q10]\n● London, Lisbon, Accra — teeno same GMT time share karte hain; Addis Ababa (Ethiopia) alag hai — GMT+3\nuse karta hai (38°45′E pe located). [Q11]\nGMT Se Aage/Peeche — Countries Ranking\n● Standard time offsets: Japan = +9, Iraq = +3, Greece = +2, Cuba = −5, Costa Rica = −6. Order (most-ahead to\nmost-behind): Japan → Iraq → Greece → Cuba → Costa Rica. [Q12]\nInternational Date Line (IDL)\n● IDL ~180° meridian pe Pacific Ocean se guzarti hai — political/administrative convenience ke liye kahin-kahin\nmudi hui hai. [Q15]\n● IDL aur Greenwich ke beech time difference 12 hours hai (180° × 4 min = 720 min = 12 hrs). [Q16]\n● IDL ke around minimum fixed distance NAHI hoti (kyunki IDL kai jagah bent/turned hai, e.g. Alaska ke paas) —\nbaaki meridians (Prime, 45°N/S) mein aisi problem nahi. [Q17]\n● IDL ke sabse close strait: Bering Strait (~168°23′W) — Malacca, Florida, Gibraltar straits IDL se bahut door\nhain. [Q19]"," The Longitude\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nIDL Crossing — Date Change Puzzles\n● Agar Earth ka rotation direction REVERSE ho jaaye, aur IDL pe 12 noon ho, toh IST kya hoga? Answer: 18:30\nhrs — rotation reverse hone se longitude-time relation bhi reverse ho jaata; jahan IST normally GMT se aage\nhota, wahan peeche ho jaata (180° meridian aur Greenwich ke beech 12-hour gap ko naye direction mein apply\nkarke 18:30 milta hai). [Q18]\n● Ship Aleutian region mein (jahan IDL bent hai) 180° meridian cross karta hai 1 Jan 23:30 pe — actual Date Line\ncross NAHI karta (deviation ki wajah se), toh 1 hour baad diary mein 2 January, 00:30 likhega. [Q20]\n● Ship 90°W pe Monday 10am se westward 15°/hour speed se chalta hai — IDL cross karne se THEEK PEHLE\nlocal solar time Monday 10:00am hi rahega (speed effect aur time-shift cancel out ho jaate hain); IDL cross\nkarne ke baad calendar Tuesday ho jaayega. [Q21]\n● Anadyr (Siberia) aur Nome (Alaska) geographically close hain lekin IDL region ke opposite sides pe — different\ncalendar days ho sakte hain (Statement I correct); lekin 'Anadyr Monday = Nome Tuesday' wala specific claim\ngalat hai (Statement II incorrect). [Q22]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• IDL crossing problems mein carefully dekho ki ship actual bent Date Line cross kar raha hai ya sirf 180°\nmeridian — dono alag ho sakte hain kuch regions (jaise Aleutian/Alaska) mein. [Q20]\nShortest Distance — Great Circle Route\n● 2 places ke beech Earth surface pe sabse kam distance wala route Great Circle Route hota hai — ships/aircraft\nisi ka use karte hain jahan practical ho. [Q23]\nNatural vs Man-made Time Units\n● Standard Time NAHI hai natural time unit (yeh human convention hai, ek chosen meridian ke local mean time pe\nbased) — Day, Lunar month, Tropical year sab natural units hain. [Q26]\nTime Zones — Countries with Dependencies\n● Dependencies/overseas territories count karte hue: UK=9, Denmark=5, New Zealand=5, Australia=9, Brazil=4\ntime zones. Jinke 4 se zyada time zones hain: UK, Denmark, New Zealand, Australia (4 countries) — Brazil\nexclude hota hai. [Q27]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0105","t":"02.iii The Equator","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Equator\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Equator — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_iii_The_Equator\nTopic Index\n1. Equator ki Length\n2. Equator — Kin Countries Se Guzarti Hai\n3. Equator — Temperature aur Climate\n4. Cities Nearest to Equator\n5. Equator + Tropics — Continents Overlap\n6. ITCZ\nEquator ki Length\n● Equator ki total length ~40,000 km (40,090 km) hai — ~78.7% water se aur ~21.3% land se guzarti hai. [Q1]\nEquator — Kin Countries Se Guzarti Hai\n● Equator guzarti hai: Colombia, Kenya, Indonesia, Brazil, Gabon, Somalia. [Q2,Q3,Q5,Q6,Q7]\n● Equator NAHI guzarti: Mexico, Equatorial Guinea, Rwanda, Brunei, Venezuela, Cameroon, Costa Rica\n(naam se confuse mat ho — 'Equatorial Guinea' naam mein hone ke bawajood Equator wahan se nahi guzarti).\n[Q3,Q4,Q5,Q6,Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'Equatorial Guinea' ke naam mein 'Equatorial' hai lekin Equator waha se guzarti NAHI hai — naam-based\nguessing avoid karo. [Q4]\nEquator — Temperature aur Climate\n● Annual temperature range sabse kam (minimum) Equator ke paas hoti hai — Sun rays saal bhar lagbhag\nvertically padti hain, isliye clear winter season nahi hota. [Q8]\nCities Nearest to Equator\n● Given cities mein Singapore (1°21′N) Equator ke sabse close hai (Colombo, Jakarta, Manila se zyada close) —\nsirf ~137 km door. [Q9]\nEquator + Tropics — Continents Overlap\n● Equator, Tropic of Cancer, aur Tropic of Capricorn — teeno Africa se guzarti hain (South America se sirf\nEquator aur Capricorn guzarti hain, Cancer nahi). [Q10]"," The Equator\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nITCZ\n● Intertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) — low-pressure zone jo Equator ke around located hai. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0106","t":"02.iv The Tropic of Cancer","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Tropic of Cancer\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Tropic of Cancer — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_iv_The_Tropic_of_Cancer\nTopic Index\n1. Tropic of Cancer — Sun Altitude Calculation\n2. Tropic of Cancer — Countries\nTropic of Cancer — Sun Altitude Calculation\n● Winter Solstice (~22 Dec) pe, jab Sun Capricorn pe 90° (vertically) chamakta hai, tab Tropic of Cancer pe Sun\naltitude = 90° − 47° = 43° (47° = Cancer aur Capricorn ke beech ka latitudinal difference: 23°30′+23°30′). [Q1]\nTropic of Cancer — Countries\n● Tropic of Cancer in countries se guzarti hai: Mexico, Bahamas, Mauritania, Mali, Algeria, Niger, China, Taiwan,\nWestern Sahara, Saudi Arabia, UAE, Oman, India, Bangladesh, Myanmar, Libya, Egypt. [Q2]\n● Iran se Tropic of Cancer NAHI guzarti (yeh common confusion hai kyunki Iran Middle East mein hai aur nearby\ncountries se guzarti hai). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Middle East ke bahut se countries (Saudi Arabia, UAE, Oman) se Cancer guzarti hai lekin Iran se NAHI — is\nexception ko yaad rakho. [Q2]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0107","t":"02.v The Tropic of Capricorn","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Tropic of Capricorn\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Tropic of Capricorn — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_v_The_Tropic_of_Capricorn\nTopic Index\n1. Earth's Motion — Rotation/Revolution Statements\n2. Tropic of Capricorn — Countries\n3. Capricorn Vertical Sun aur India ka Winter\nEarth's Motion — Rotation/Revolution Statements\n● Statement check: 'Rotation west-east se seasonal changes' — GALAT (seasons axial tilt + revolution se hote\nhain); 'Revolution se day-night' bhi GALAT (day-night rotation se hota hai) — dono statements incorrect. [Q1]\nTropic of Capricorn — Countries\n● Tropic of Capricorn in countries se guzarti hai: Brazil, Australia, Paraguay, Madagascar, Argentina,\nMozambique, Chile, South Africa, French Polynesia, Tonga, Botswana, Namibia. [Q2,Q3]\n● Bolivia se Tropic of Capricorn NAHI guzarti (South America mein hone ke bawajood). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Bolivia South America mein hai lekin Capricorn line se nahi guzarti — Chile, Brazil, Argentina, Paraguay se\nguzarti hai, Bolivia se nahi. [Q2]\nCapricorn Vertical Sun aur India ka Winter\n● Jab Sun Tropic of Capricorn pe vertically chamakta hai, India ke North-West mein High Pressure develop hota\nhai (winter conditions, landmass Arabian Sea se colder ho jaata hai). [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0108","t":"02.vi Day and Night","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Day and Night\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Day and Night — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_vi_Day_and_Night\nTopic Index\n1. Equinox — Equal Day-Night\n2. Solstices — Longest/Shortest Day\n3. 21 June — Arctic Circle aur Latitude Sunlight\n4. Earth's Rotation Axis — Recent Changes\nEquinox — Equal Day-Night\n● Equinox (equal day-night) saal mein 2 baar hota hai: ~21 March aur ~23 September — Sun Equator pe\nvertically chamakta hai. [Q1,Q2]\n● Equator pe day-night lagbhag saal bhar equal (~12-12 hours) rehta hai — koi distinct winter season nahi hota,\nsirf wet-dry seasons. [Q3]\nSolstices — Longest/Shortest Day\n● Summer Solstice (Northern Hemisphere, ~21 June) pe: Equator pe day-length 12 hours rehta hai (Tropic of\nCancer/Capricorn ya Arctic Circle pe nahi). [Q4]\n● Northern Hemisphere ka longest day June ke 2nd half mein hota hai (~20/21 June). [Q5]\n● Northern Hemisphere ka shortest day ~21/22 December (Winter Solstice) ko hota hai. [Q6,Q7,Q8]\n● Southern Hemisphere ka longest day ~22 December ko hota hai (Northern se opposite). [Q9]\n● 21 June ko dopahar mein shadow sabse shortest hoti hai (Sun Tropic of Cancer pe vertically overhead hota hai).\n[Q10]\n● Summer Solstice har saal 21 June ko hota hai. [Q11]\n21 June — Arctic Circle aur Latitude Sunlight\n● 21 June ko Sun Arctic Circle pe horizon ke neeche set nahi hota (Midnight Sun phenomenon). [Q12]\n● 21 June ko 12 hours se zyada sunlight paane wale latitudes: Tropic of Cancer aur Arctic Circle (dono Northern\nHemisphere mein, jo Sun ki taraf tilted hoti hai) — Equator aur Tropic of Capricorn NAHI (unhe 12 hrs ya kam\nmilta hai). [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 21 June ko Equator pe bhi lagbhag exactly 12 hours hi milta hai, 12 se zyada NAHI — is confusion se bacho.\n[Q13]\nEarth's Rotation Axis — Recent Changes"," Day and Night\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Statement analysis: Earth ke rotation/axis mein changes ho rahe hain — TRUE; Solar flares/CMEs upper\natmosphere ko energy dete hain — TRUE (fact-wise correct) lekin yeh axis-change ka primary explanation\nNAHI hai; Polar ice melting se water Equator ki taraf shift hota hai — TRUE AUR yahi axis-change ka\nscientific explanation hai. [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Do statements factually correct ho sakte hain lekin sirf EK unme se main statement ko explain karta hai —\nCMEs sirf upper atmosphere tak limited hain, jabki ice-melting se mass-redistribution actually axis ko affect\nkarta hai. [Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0109","t":"02.vii Origin of the Earth","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Origin of the Earth\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Origin of the Earth — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_vii_Origin_of_the_Earth\nTopic Index\n1. Earth ki Origin Theories — Scholars\n2. Earth ki Age Determine Karne ka Method\nEarth ki Origin Theories — Scholars\n● O. Schmidt (Otto Schmidt) ne suggest kiya ki Earth gases aur dust particles se bani (Interstellar Dust\nHypothesis). [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• James Jeans & Jeffreys = Tidal Hypothesis; F. Hoyle & Littleton = Nova Hypothesis; Otto Schmidt = Gas-\nDust/Interstellar Dust Hypothesis — teeno scientists ko unki respective theories se match karo. [Q1]\nEarth ki Age Determine Karne ka Method\n● Earth ki age determine karne ke liye Uranium Dating method use hoti hai (Carbon dating fossils ke liye hoti hai,\nEarth ki age ke liye nahi). [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Carbon dating fossils/organic material ki age ke liye hoti hai; Earth ki khud ki age ke liye Uranium dating\nuse hoti hai — dono ko mix mat karo. [Q2]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0110","t":"02.viii The Geological History","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Geological History\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Geological History — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 02_viii_The_Geological_History\nTopic Index\n1. Ice Ages — Great vs Little\n2. Dinosaurs ka Period\n3. Continental Drift — Tectonic Activities\n4. Gondwanaland aur Pangaea\n5. Plate Tectonics\n6. Crust Formation aur Destruction\n7. Folding aur Diastrophism\n8. Earth Surface Change — Contributing Factors\n9. Prehistoric Formations aur Life Evolution Timeline\n10. Thar/Rajasthan Desert — Geological Period\nIce Ages — Great vs Little\n● 'Great Ice Age' = Pleistocene Epoch se related (~2 million years ago se ~10,000 years ago tak) — extensive ice\nsheets/glaciers development ka period. [Q1]\n● 'Little Ice Age' generally 1650 AD – 1870 AD ke beech maana jaata hai — Europe/North America mein 20th\ncentury se colder winters. [Q2]\nDinosaurs ka Period\n● Dinosaurs ka period ~18 crore years pehle (Jurassic Period, ~20.8 to 14.4 crore years ago) — India mein\nremains Raiyoli (Gujarat) aur Bara Simla hills (MP) mein mile hain. [Q3]\nContinental Drift — Tectonic Activities\n● Continents apart drift karte hain primarily Tectonic Activities ki wajah se (tectonic plates continuously move\nkarti hain). [Q4]\nGondwanaland aur Pangaea\n● Pangaea = originally Earth ka ek hi huge landmass (supercontinent), surrounded by superocean Panthalassa.\n[Q9]\n● Pangaea split hua Laurasia (North) aur Gondwanaland (South) mein. [Q6]\n● Gondwanaland mein shamil the: South America, Africa, Madagascar, Australia, Antarctica, Arabian Peninsula,\nPeninsular India — North America shamil NAHI tha. [Q5,Q7]"," The Geological History\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Gondwanaland = Southern landmass, Laurasia = Northern landmass — North America Gondwanaland ka\npart NAHI tha (Laurasia ka tha). [Q5]\nPlate Tectonics\n● Cocos Plate Central America aur Pacific Plate ke beech located hai. [Q8]\n● Plate Tectonics Theory — Earth's crust ke pieces mantle ki movement se driven hoke constant slow motion\nmein rehte hain. 7 major plates: Eurasian, African, Indo-Australian, Pacific, North American, South American,\nAntarctic. [Q12]\n● Continental drift ke evidence: Brazil-West Africa coast ki ancient rocks match karti hain (I), Ghana gold deposits\nBrazilian Plateau se related hain (II), India ka Gondwana sediment system Southern Hemisphere ke 6\nlandmasses mein match karta hai (III) — teeno statements correct. [Q13]\nCrust Formation aur Destruction\n● New crust continuously Seafloor Spreading se create hoti hai; old crust Subduction se destroy hoti hai — dono\nbalance karte hain, isliye Earth ka size roughly constant rehta hai. [Q14]\nFolding aur Diastrophism\n● Folding = Orogenic force ka result hai (mountain-building force, tectonic plate interactions se produce hota hai).\n[Q15]\n● Diastrophism ke under aate hain: Orogenic process, Earthquakes, Plate tectonics — 'Heterogenic process' naam ki\nkoi standard diastrophism process nahi hoti. [Q16]\nEarth Surface Change — Contributing Factors\n● Earth surface pe dynamic changes laane wale factors: Electromagnetic radiation, Geothermal energy,\nGravitational force, Plate movements, Earth's rotation, Earth's revolution — saare 6 factors relevant hain.\n[Q17]\nPrehistoric Formations aur Life Evolution Timeline\n● Formations chronological order (oldest to newest): Sihawal → Patpara → Baghor → Khetaunhi (Lower\nPalaeolithic → Middle Palaeolithic → Upper Palaeolithic → Neolithic/Microlithic). [Q18]\n● Life evolution chronological order: Shelled animals → Insects → Reptiles → Mammals. [Q19]\n● Earliest fossil evidence of life on Earth: exam-key answer 3.5 (million/billion) years ago (source options have a\nunit inconsistency, but option B is the accepted key). [Q10]\n● Continental drift AUR glacial cycles — dono ne organisms ke evolution ko influence kiya hai. [Q11]\nThar/Rajasthan Desert — Geological Period"," The Geological History\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Rajasthan/Thar Desert Pleistocene aur recent deposits ka expanse hai — very low rainfall wala region. [Q20]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0111","t":"03 Rocks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Rocks\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Rocks — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 03_Rocks\nTopic Index\n1. Igneous Rocks — Formation aur Types\n2. Sedimentary Rocks — Properties\n3. Porosity vs Permeability — Chalk vs Clay\n4. Metamorphic Rocks — Origin\n5. Weathering — Rainfall ka Role\nIgneous Rocks — Formation aur Types\n● Igneous rocks = lava/magma ke cooling-solidification se banti hain. 2 types: Extrusive (surface pe cool hoti\nhain, e.g. Basalt) aur Intrusive (crust ke andar cool hoti hain, e.g. Granite). [Q1]\n● Igneous rocks crystalline aur non-crystalline dono ho sakti hain; inme fossils/layers generally absent hote hain,\naur silicate minerals se largely composed hoti hain. [Q6]\n● Fossils milne ka chance sabse kam: Granite (igneous rock hai) — Conglomerate, Sandstone, Shale (sab\nsedimentary) mein fossils mil sakte hain. [Q7]\nSedimentary Rocks — Properties\n● Sedimentary rocks: hydrological system se banti hain, pre-existing rocks ke weathering se involve hoti hain,\nfossils contain karti hain, aur layers/strata mein occur karti hain — sab 4 statements correct hain. [Q2,Q3]\n● Sandstone layered hoti hai kyunki uske sediments successive layers mein deposit + compact hote hain (sirf\ndesert/mountain mein nahi banti, rivers/beaches/seas mein bhi ban sakti hai). [Q4]\nPorosity vs Permeability — Chalk vs Clay\n● Chalk aur Clay dono porous hote hain, lekin Chalk highly permeable hai (cracks/fractures ki wajah se aquifer\nban sakta hai) jabki Clay impermeable/aquitard hai (pores interconnected nahi hote). [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Clay 'not porous' claim GALAT hai — Clay actually highly porous hoti hai, lekin permeability extremely low\nhoti hai. Porosity aur Permeability alag concepts hain. [Q5]\nMetamorphic Rocks — Origin\n● Metamorphic rocks = 'change of form' — Igneous AND Sedimentary dono rocks se ban sakti hain, heat +\npressure ke through. [Q8]\n● Examples: Granite→Gneiss, Basalt→Schist/Amphibolite (igneous se); Shale→Slate, Limestone→Marble,\nSandstone→Quartzite (sedimentary se). [Q9]"," Rocks\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Granite metamorphic rock NAHI hai — yeh igneous rock hai (na ki Marble/Quartzite/Slate jaisi metamorphic).\n[Q9]\n● Odd-one-out: Gneiss (metamorphic hai) — Limestone, Sandstone, Shale sab sedimentary group ke hain. [Q10]\nWeathering — Rainfall ka Role\n● Rainfall rocks ke weathering ka ek cause hai kyunki rainwater mein dissolved CO2 (carbonation) AND\ndissolved oxygen (oxidation) dono hote hain — dono processes chemical weathering explain karte hain. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0112","t":"04 The Volcano","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Volcano\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Volcano — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 04_The_Volcano\nTopic Index\n1. Volcanic Products aur Landforms\n2. Magma, Lava, Plutonic vs Volcanic Rocks\n3. Volcanic Belts\n4. Famous Volcanoes — Height, Location, Status\n5. Kilimanjaro\n6. Mediterranean/Italy Volcanoes\n7. Arctic aur Antarctica\n8. Most Active Volcano\n9. Volcano-Country Matching (multiple sets)\n10. Indonesia — Islands aur Volcanoes\nVolcanic Products aur Landforms\n● Volcanic eruption products: Pyroclastic debris, Ash-dust, Nitrogen compounds, Sulphur compounds — saare 4\nproducts hain. [Q1]\n● Volcanic cone = constructive/basic landform hai (lava deposition se banta hai) — Residual mountain,\nMonadnock, Erosional waterfall sab erosional/destructive landforms hain. [Q2]\n● Volcanoes se sabse abundant gas Water Vapour (H2O) nikalti hai (CO2, SO2 bhi important hain, lekin H2O\nsabse zyada). [Q3]\nMagma, Lava, Plutonic vs Volcanic Rocks\n● Earth ke andar ka molten material = Magma; jab yeh surface pe erupt hota hai toh Lava kehlata hai. [Q6]\n● Magma jab Earth ke deep andar cool-solidify hota hai → Plutonic rock banti hai (large crystals, slow cooling).\n[Q7]\nVolcanic Belts\n● Volcanic eruptions sabse zyada Circum-Pacific Belt (Pacific 'Ring of Fire') mein hote hain — world ke ~3/4\nactive volcanoes yahan hain. [Q5]\n● Baltic Sea mein volcanic eruptions NAHI hote (active plate boundary se associated nahi hai) — Black Sea,\nCaribbean Sea, Caspian Sea se contrast. [Q8]\nFamous Volcanoes — Height, Location, Status\n● Given options mein sabse high volcanic mountain: Mount Cotopaxi (Ecuador, ~5,897m) — Kilimanjaro\n(~5,895m) se marginally higher. [Q4]"," The Volcano\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Mt. Etna = active volcano (Sicily, Italy). [Q9]\n● Mount St. Helens = USA (Washington state) mein, 'Fujiyama of America' bhi kehte hain. [Q10]\n● Mauna Loa = Hawaii mein, world ka largest active volcano (volume/area se) — 2022 mein 38 years baad erupt\nhua (pehla eruption 1984 mein tha). [Q11,Q12,Q13]\n● Active volcanoes (given lists mein): Cotopaxi, Etna, Fujiyama — Aconcagua active NAHI hai. [Q14]\n● Active volcanoes: Etna aur Vesuvius — Kilimanjaro dormant hai, Aconcagua active nahi. [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Aconcagua (Argentina) sabse tall peak hai lekin ACTIVE VOLCANO NAHI hai — isse baar baar list mein\ndistractor ki tarah use kiya jaata hai. [Q14,Q15]\nKilimanjaro\n● Kilimanjaro = Africa ka highest peak, Tanzania mein located, volcanic mountain hai (3 cones: Kibo, Mawenzi,\nShira — Uhuru Peak Kibo pe hai). [Q16,Q17]\nMediterranean/Italy Volcanoes\n● Stromboli = 'Lighthouse of the Mediterranean Sea' kehlata hai (frequent glowing eruptions ki wajah se), active\nvolcano hai (Aeolian Islands, Italy) — 'Strombolian eruption' term isi se aaya hai. [Q18,Q20]\nArctic aur Antarctica\n● Arctic region aur Antarctica continent respectively North Pole aur South Pole ke around located hain. [Q19]\nMost Active Volcano\n● Given options mein world ka sabse active volcano: Kilauea (Hawaii, USA) — Etna, Piton de la Fournaise,\nNyamuragira bhi highly active hain. [Q21]\nVolcano-Country Matching (multiple sets)\n● Etna–Sicily, Vesuvius–Italy, Erebus–Ross Island, Cotopaxi–Ecuador. [Q22]\n● Mount Rainier–USA, Etna–Italy, Paricutin–Mexico, Taal–Philippines. [Q23,Q28]\n● Mount Kinabalu–Malaysia, Elburz–Iran, Aconcagua–Argentina, Kilimanjaro–Tanzania. [Q24]\n● Sabancaya–Peru, Mount Etna–Italy, Colima–Mexico, Merapi–Indonesia. [Q25]\nIndonesia — Islands aur Volcanoes\n● Indonesia mein 15,000+ islands hain — statement correct; lekin 'active volcanoes 150+' claim galat hai (official\ncount 127 active volcanoes hai). [Q26]\n● Krakatoa (Krakatau) volcanic mountain Indonesia mein hai (Sunda Strait, Java-Sumatra ke beech). [Q27]"," The Volcano\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Indonesia mein islands 15,000+ hain lekin active volcanoes 150 se KAM (127) hain — numbers ko exactly\nyaad rakho, round-off mat karo. [Q26]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0113","t":"05 The Earthquake","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Earthquake\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Earthquake — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 05_The_Earthquake\nTopic Index\n1. Plate Tectonics Theory — Origin\n2. Seismic Waves — Types\n3. Ring of Fire\n4. Richter Scale — Logarithmic Scale\n5. Instruments — Seismometer/Seismograph\n6. Tsunami — Origin aur Major Events\n7. India ka NW Region — Earthquake Prone\n8. Focus vs Epicentre\n9. Plate Tectonics — Cocos Plate\nPlate Tectonics Theory — Origin\n● Plate Tectonics Theory H.H. Hess ne akela 1967 mein NAHI diya (Wilson, Morgan, Parker, McKenzie, Hess\nsabne mila ke 1960s late mein develop kiya) — Statement I FALSE; Theory Sea-floor Spreading pe based hai\n— Statement II TRUE. [Q1]\nSeismic Waves — Types\n● Earthquake se P-waves, S-waves, AND Surface waves teeno generate hote hain — P-waves fastest\n(compressional), S-waves liquid se pass nahi hoti (shear), Surface waves (Love + Rayleigh) baad mein aati\nhain. [Q2]\n● Shadow Zone — har earthquake ka apna alag shadow-zone pattern hota hai (Statement I TRUE); lekin 105° se\naage seismometers dono P aur S waves record NAHI karte (P-waves 105-140° ke beech missing, S-waves apne\nshadow zone se aage missing) — Statement II FALSE. [Q3]\nRing of Fire\n● 'Ring of Fire' — Earthquakes, Volcanoes, aur Pacific Ocean teeno se associated hai (world ke ~90% earthquakes\nyahin aate hain) — Forest fires se related NAHI hai. [Q4]\nRichter Scale — Logarithmic Scale\n● Richter Scale logarithmic (base 10) hai — 1 magnitude unit increase = 10x amplitude (100x amplitude NAHI);\nenergy release ~32x badhta hai per unit (100x nahi). [Q5,Q6]\n● Charles Francis Richter ne 1935 mein Richter scale develop kiya. Magnitude = energy release ka measurement,\nIntensity = Mercalli Scale pe measure hoti hai. [Q7,Q8]"," The Earthquake\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Richter scale mein 1-unit increase = 10x amplitude, ~32x energy — '100x' wala option common trap hai, sahi\nnahi hai. [Q5,Q6]\nInstruments — Seismometer/Seismograph\n● Seismometer earthquake measure karta hai (sensing component) — heartbeat/tree-height se koi relation nahi.\n[Q9]\n● Seismograph seismic waves detect+record karne ka instrument/system hai; Seismogram = recorded trace/output\nhai. [Q10]\nTsunami — Origin aur Major Events\n● 'Tsunami' word Japanese hai (tsu=harbour, nami=wave, literal meaning 'harbour wave'). [Q11]\n● 2004 Indian Ocean Tsunami: Sumatra (Indonesia) ke paas earthquake, India-Burma plate boundary pe ~1,300km\nfault slip ~15m, Africa (Somalia) tak effect pahuncha, Bangladesh mein kam casualties hui (fault orientation ki\nwajah se). Death toll ~2-3 lakh tha, 50 lakh NAHI (yeh galat statement hai). [Q12]\n● 2011 Japan Tsunami ne Fukushima region ko severely affect kiya (9.0 magnitude earthquake, Fukushima\nDaiichi Nuclear Plant accident). [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 2004 Tsunami death toll ~2-3 lakh tha — '50 lakh se zyada' wala claim EXAM key mein GALAT statement\nhai, isse confuse mat ho. [Q12]\nIndia ka NW Region — Earthquake Prone\n● India ka North-Western region earthquake-prone hai kyunki Plate Tectonic Activity (Indian Plate-Eurasian Plate\nconvergence zone) — volcanic activity ya coral formation ki wajah se NAHI. [Q14]\nFocus vs Epicentre\n● Focus/Hypocentre = Earth ke andar wo point jahan earthquake energy release hoti hai; Epicentre = Focus ke\nexactly upar surface ka point — seismic waves surface pe sabse pehle epicentre ke paas pahunchti hain. [Q15]\nPlate Tectonics — Cocos Plate\n● Cocos Plate Central America aur Pacific Plate ke beech located hai. [Q16]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0114","t":"06 The Continents","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Continents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Continents — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 06_The_Continents\nTopic Index\n1. Countries Count aur Area — Continents\n2. Smallest Continents\n3. Per-Capita Land aur Mean Elevation\n4. South America — Physical Regions\n5. Physical Features — Location Matching\n6. Plains Percentage\n7. Country ↔ Continent — Common Confusions\n8. Australia se Associated Features\nCountries Count aur Area — Continents\n● Africa mein sabse zyada countries hain (54 UN member states) — kisi bhi other continent se zyada. [Q1,Q2]\n● Overall Asia sabse bada continent hai; given options mein (Europe/Africa/N.America/S.America) Africa sabse\nbada hai. [Q3]\n● Area descending order (given 4): Africa > South America > Europe > Australia. [Q5]\n● Full area descending order: Asia > Africa > North America > Europe (Asia 44.5M, Africa 30M, N.America\n24.5M, Europe 9.9M sq km). [Q6]\n● % share of Earth's land area (descending, exam list): Africa > North America > South America > Europe (Asia\n29.8%, Africa 20.3%, N.America 16.2%, S.America 11.8%, Antarctica 9.2%, Europe 6.8%, Australia 5.9%).\n[Q9]\nSmallest Continents\n● Australia = smallest continent by land area; Europe = 2nd smallest. [Q7,Q8]\nPer-Capita Land aur Mean Elevation\n● Given options mein maximum per-capita land: Australia (World Bank data ke according). [Q10]\n● Highest mean elevation continent: Antarctica (~2300m) — Asia 923m, N.America 760m, Africa 585m,\nAustralia 330m, S.America 554m, Europe 302m (lowest). [Q11]\nSouth America — Physical Regions\n● South America ke 4 physical regions (typical map order): Andes, Brazilian Shield, Guiana Highland, Amazon\nBasin. [Q12]"," The Continents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nPhysical Features — Location Matching\n● Atlas Mountains = North-Western Africa (correctly matched pair). [Q13]\n● Correct locations: Abyssinian Plateau = East Africa, Guiana Highlands = Northern South America, Okavango\nBasin = South-Western Africa. [Q13]\n● Matching: Aconcagua–South America, Meseta–Europe, Serengeti Plains–Africa, Gibson Desert–Australia. [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Q13 mein wrong pairings the: Abyssinian Plateau ko Arabia se, Guiana Highlands ko S-W Africa se,\nOkavango Basin ko Patagonia se galat match kiya gaya tha — sirf Atlas Mountains–NW Africa hi sahi tha.\n[Q13]\nPlains Percentage\n● Given options mein sabse zyada plains percentage (total area ke relative): Europe — South America mein bhi\nextensive plains hain lekin Europe ka % zyada hai. [Q14]\nCountry ↔ Continent — Common Confusions\n● Guyana South America mein hai (Africa mein NAHI) — naam Guinea/Guinea-Bissau se similar sound karta hai\nisliye confusion hoti hai. Gabon, Guinea, Guinea-Bissau sab Africa mein hain. [Q4,Q16]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Guyana (South America) vs Guinea/Guinea-Bissau (Africa) — naam-sound similarity ki wajah se yeh\nsabse common exam trap hai. [Q4,Q16]\nAustralia se Associated Features\n● Australia se associated: Lake Eyre, Nullarbor Plain, Mount Selwyn — Salween Valley Australia se NAHI\nassociated hai (Salween river Asia mein hai — Myanmar/China). [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0115","t":"07 The World Mountain","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The World Mountain\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The World Mountain — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 07_The_World_Mountain\nTopic Index\n1. Asia Mountains — West to East Order\n2. Named Mountain Ranges — Country/Location\n3. Young vs Old Fold Mountains\n4. Andes — World ki Sabse Lambi Range\n5. South America — Precambrian Highlands\n6. New Zealand — Southern Alps\n7. Alps — Europe\n8. Mountain-Continent Matching\n9. White Mountains, Black Mountains\n10. India-Myanmar Border Mountains\n11. Black Forest — Germany, Rhine River\n12. Young vs Old Mountains — Odd One Out\n13. Africa Mountains\n14. Country-Mountain Matching (Multiple Sets)\n15. Switzerland/Italy Mountains\n16. Spain-France Border — Pyrenees\n17. Golan Heights\n18. Constructive Landform Recap\n19. Asia Minor — Taurus Mountains\n20. Epeirogenic Forces\nAsia Mountains — West to East Order\n● West-to-East order: Pontic → Zagros → Hindu Kush → Karakoram — Pontic (Turkey, Black Sea south),\nZagros (Iran), phir Pamir Knot se Hindu Kush west aur Karakoram east ki taraf extend hoti hai. [Q1]\nNamed Mountain Ranges — Country/Location\n● Darling Range = Australia ke South-Western coast pe hai (Western Australia). [Q2]\n● British Columbia ko 'Sea of Mountains' kehte hain (Molyneux St. John, 1876, Lord Dufferin's tour ke account\nmein). [Q3]\nYoung vs Old Fold Mountains\n● World ke highest peaks (Everest included) mainly Young Folded Mountains mein hain (jaise Himalaya). [Q4]\n● Young fold mountains: Rockies, Himalaya, Alps — Sierra Nevada block mountain hai, young fold nahi. [Q7]"," The World Mountain\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nAndes — World ki Sabse Lambi Range\n● Andes = world ki longest continental mountain range (~7,000-8,900 km), South America ke western coast ke\nsaath — Rockies ~4,800km, Himalaya ~2,500km, Alps ~1,200km se lambi. [Q5,Q10,Q11,Q13]\n● Andes South America continent mein hai. [Q8,Q9]\n● Given 6 countries mein Andes 4 se guzarti hai: Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Venezuela (Brazil aur Paraguay se\nNAHI — poori list: Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Chile, Argentina). [Q12]\n● Length descending order: Andes > Rocky > Great Dividing Range > Himalaya. [Q15]\nSouth America — Precambrian Highlands\n● Pacaraima Mountains (Guiana Highlands ka part) mainly ancient Precambrian rocks (Guiana Shield, ~1.8\nbillion+ years old) se bane hain — Andes iske comparison mein bahut younger hai. [Q6]\nNew Zealand — Southern Alps\n● Southern Alps = New Zealand (South Island, western side) mein hai — highest peak Aoraki/Mount Cook\n(~3,724m). [Q14]\nAlps — Europe\n● Alps = Europe ki mountain range, France/Austria/Germany/Switzerland tak extend hoti hai — England ka part\nNAHI hai (Mont Blanc iski highest peaks mein se ek hai). [Q16],[Q17]\nMountain-Continent Matching\n● Matching: Andes-South America, Altai-Asia, Alps-Europe, Appalachian-North America. [Q18]\nWhite Mountains, Black Mountains\n● White Mountains = USA (New Hampshire, Maine states). [Q19]\n● Black Mountains = USA (North Carolina) mein hain, Appalachian mountain system ka part. [Q25]\nIndia-Myanmar Border Mountains\n● India-Myanmar boundary determine karne wale ranges: option 'Khasi, Patkoi, Arakan Yoma' galat hai (Khasi\nHills Meghalaya mein hain, border define nahi karte) — exam-accepted answer 'None of the above' hai. [Q20]\n● Arakan Yoma = Myanmar mein hai, Himalaya ka southward extension maana jaata hai. [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Khasi Hills Meghalaya (India) mein hain, ye India-Myanmar border define nahi karte — is combination ko\nwrongly correct mat maano. [Q20]"," The World Mountain\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nBlack Forest — Germany, Rhine River\n● Black Forest = Germany mein hai (block-mountain region), highest peak Feldberg (~1,493m). [Q22,Q23]\n● Rhine River ke saath located mountain: Black Forest (Rhine ke East mein) — Vosges Mountains (France) Rhine\nke West mein hain, Rhine Rift Valley ke across. [Q24]\nYoung vs Old Mountains — Odd One Out\n● Alps, Andes, Himalayas — young/Alpine-Tertiary phase; Appalachian different hai (old fold mountain). [Q26]\n● Tertiary orogeny ka result NAHI: Appalachians (old fold mountain) — Kunlun, Alps, Andes Tertiary orogeny\nke results hain. [Q27]\n● Old folded mountains: Ural, Aravalli, Appalachian — Andes young fold mountain hai (old nahi). [Q28]\n● Given match-table mein sirf 2 rows correct hain: North America-Appalachians (Fold ) aur South America-\n✓\nAndes (Fold ) sahi hain; Central Asia-Vosges aur Europe-Alps wale rows galat hain.\n✓\n [Q29]\n● Pennines (Europe), Appalachians (America), Aravallis (India) — teeno Old Mountains ke examples hain. [Q30]\nAfrica Mountains\n● Drakensberg = South Africa (+ Lesotho) mein hai — highest peak Thabana Ntlenyana (~3,482m, Lesotho\nmein). [Q31]\n● Atlas Mountains = Africa continent mein hain (Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia, ~2,400km) — Mediterranean climate\nko Sahara se separate karte hain. [Q32,Q33]\nCountry-Mountain Matching (Multiple Sets)\n● Allegheny-USA, Cantabrian-Spain, Elburz-Iran, Mackenzie-Canada. [Q34]\n● Kosciuszko-Australia, Mount McKinley-North America, Elbrus-Europe, Kilimanjaro-Africa. (Mount\nMcKinley/Denali naam 2015-2025 Denali tha, 2025 mein wapas McKinley kar diya gaya). [Q35]\n● Elbrus Europe ka highest mountain hai, Asia ka NAHI — yeh common wrong pairing hai. [Q36]\n● Kilimanjaro-Tanzania, Toubkal-Morocco, Stanley-Uganda, Hoggar-Algeria. [Q37]\n● Type matching: Alps-Folded, Vosges-Block, Vindhya-Residual, Fujiyama-Volcanic. [Q38]\n● Elbrus-Russia, Kilimanjaro-Tanzania, Mt.Cook-New Zealand, Mount McKinley-USA. [Q47]\n● Atlas-Morocco, Kilimanjaro-Tanzania, Chimborazo-Ecuador, Pyrenees-France/Spain. [Q48]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Elbrus Europe ka highest peak hai — Asia se match karna common exam trap hai. [Q36]\nSwitzerland/Italy Mountains\n● Mount Titlis = Switzerland mein hai. [Q39]\n● Apennine Mountains = Italy mein hain (~1,350km), highest peak Corno Grande — Pyrenees (France-Spain),\nDinaric Alps (Balkans), Jura (France/Switzerland) se compare karo. [Q40]"," The World Mountain\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\nSpain-France Border — Pyrenees\n● Pyrenees = Spain aur France ke beech natural boundary banate hain (Bay of Biscay se Mediterranean Sea tak).\n[Q41,Q43,Q44]\n● Matching: Spain-France–Pyrenees, Switzerland–Alps, Bulgaria–Balkan, Italy–Apennine. [Q42]\nGolan Heights\n● Golan Heights = Middle East (South-Western Syria) mein hai — 1967 war mein Israel ne Syria se occupy kiya\ntha. [Q45]\nConstructive Landform Recap\n● Volcanic Cone = constructive/basic landform hai (lava/ash accumulation se) — Residual mountain, Monadnock,\nErosional waterfall erosion se associated hain. [Q46]\nAsia Minor — Taurus Mountains\n● Taurus Mountains = Asia Minor (modern Turkey) ke Mediterranean coast ke saath hain — Anatolian Plateau ki\nsouthern boundary banate hain. [Q49]\nEpeirogenic Forces\n● Epeirogenic forces = Vertical earth movements ka result hain (broad crustal uplift/subsidence over large areas)\n— horizontal movements NAHI. [Q50]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0116","t":"08 The Plateaus","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Plateaus\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Plateaus — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 08_The_Plateaus\nTopic Index\n1. Tibetan Plateau\n2. South America — Minerals Storehouse\n3. Plateau Pe Basi Cities\n4. 'Roof of the World'\n5. Largest Plateau (Given Options)\n6. Ocean-Floor Plateaus/Ridges — Matching\nTibetan Plateau\n● Tibetan Plateau (Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau) ki average elevation ~5 km (4,500m+) hai; total area ~2.5 million\nsq km — world ka largest AND highest major plateau. [Q1,Q5]\nSouth America — Minerals Storehouse\n● South America ka 'storehouse of minerals' (exam-conventional answer): Patagonia Plateau (petroleum, natural\ngas, coal, metallic minerals) — Brazilian Highlands bhi rich hain (iron ore, manganese) lekin yeh conventional\nPYQ answer nahi hai. [Q2]\nPlateau Pe Basi Cities\n● Madrid (Spain) Meseta Plateau (Iberian Peninsula, ~610-760m) pe basa hai — Bucharest (55.8m), Jamnagar\n(20m), Singapore (15m) sab low elevation pe hain. [Q3]\n'Roof of the World'\n● Pamir Plateau ko 'Roof of the World' kehte hain (extreme high altitude ki wajah se) — Central Asia ki southern\nboundary yahin se determine hoti hai, multiple mountain ranges yahan converge karti hain. [Q4]\nLargest Plateau (Given Options)\n● Given options (Coconino, Aquarius, Colorado, Columbia) mein sabse bada: Colorado Plateau (~130,000+ sq\nmiles). [Q5]\nOcean-Floor Plateaus/Ridges — Matching"," The Plateaus\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Telegraphic/Telegraph Plateau = North Atlantic Ridge ka part hai (Newfoundland aur Ireland ke beech) —\nIndian Ocean se NAHI associated. [Q6,Q7]\n● Correct pairs: Cocoa Ridge–Pacific Ocean, Walvis Ridge–Atlantic Ocean, Agulhas Basin–Indian Ocean. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'Telegraph Plateau — Indian Ocean' GALAT pairing hai — Telegraph Plateau actually North Atlantic mein\nhai. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0117","t":"09 The Valley","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Valley\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Valley — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 09_The_Valley\nTopic Index\n1. Death Valley — USA\n2. Famous Named Valleys — World Locations\n3. Basins — World Locations\n4. Karst Region — Landforms\n5. Hanging Valley — Glacial Landform\nDeath Valley — USA\n● Death Valley (South California, USA) Rift Valley ka example hai — tectonic faulting se banti hai. [Q1]\n● Death Valley ka 'Devil's Golf Course' section — large salt pan, Death Valley National Park, Mojave Desert\n(USA) mein hai. [Q2]\n● Death Valley famous hai apni Excessive Heat ke liye (~56.7°C max temp) — North America ka lowest point\n(~86m below sea level; Argentina ka Laguna del Carbón usse bhi neeche hai, ~105m). [Q3]\n● Death Valley California state mein hai. [Q4]\nFamous Named Valleys — World Locations\n● Panjshir Valley = Afghanistan (Kabul se ~150km north, Hindu Kush ke paas) — Soviet-Afghan War ka main\nbattleground tha. [Q5]\n● Silicon Valley = California, USA (San Francisco Bay Area, southern part) — computer-chip/high-tech industries\nke liye famous. [Q6]\n● Taylor Valley = Antarctica mein hai — 1903 mein Robert Falcon Scott ne discover kiya, isko 'Valley of the\nDead' naam diya. [Q7]\n● Valley of the Kings (Wadi el-Muluk) = Egypt mein hai. [Q10]\nBasins — World Locations\n● Great Artesian Basin (GAB) = Australia mein hai (world ka largest underground water reservoir, ~1.7 million\nsq km, Great Dividing Range ke around). [Q8]\n● Great Basin = USA mein hai — East mein Rocky Mountains, West mein Sierra Nevada, North mein Columbia\nPlateau, South mein Mojave/Sonoran deserts. [Q9]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'Great Artesian Basin' (Australia) aur 'Great Basin' (USA) — naam similar hai lekin dono alag countries mein\nhain, confuse mat ho. [Q8,Q9]"," The Valley\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nKarst Region — Landforms\n● Blind Valley (Steephead Valley) = Karst Region mein paayi jaati hai (deep, narrow, flat-bottomed, abrupt\nending — limestone landscapes mein develop hoti hai). [Q11]\n● Karst region mein paaya jaane wala landform: Sink hole (Doline) — Pot hole/Blow hole/Playa Karst se related\nNAHI hain. [Q13]\nHanging Valley — Glacial Landform\n● Hanging Valley = Glacier erosion se banta hai — jab chhota tributary glacier bade main glacier se milta hai,\nmain glacier deeper valley banata hai jabki tributary valley higher elevation pe reh jaati hai. Junction pe steep\ndrop/waterfall banta hai (e.g. Yosemite Valley, USA). [Q12]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0118","t":"10 The Arid Regions Deserts","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Arid Regions Deserts\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Arid Regions Deserts — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 10_The_Arid_Regions_Deserts\nTopic Index\n1. Hot Deserts — Location Theory\n2. Deserts — Solar Energy Potential\n3. Desert ki Definition\n4. Australia — Interior Desert\n5. Desertification\n6. World ka Largest Hot Desert\n7. Most Populated Desert\n8. Named Deserts — Location Matching\n9. Deserts by Size — Ranking\n10. Atacama Desert\n11. Temperate Deserts\n12. Tropical Deserts aur Monsoon Winds\n13. Kalahari Desert\n14. African-Eurasian Desert Belt — Formation Cause\n15. Desert Animals — Terminology\nHot Deserts — Location Theory\n● World ke zyadatar hot deserts 15°-30° latitude ke beech, continents ke western margins pe hain — Trade winds\nwestward jaate hue apni moisture kho dete hain (dono statements TRUE, R sahi explanation hai A ka). [Q1]\n● Desert-formation probability sabse zyada ~23° latitude ke around hoti hai (subtropical high-pressure, dry\ndescending air). [Q4]\nDeserts — Solar Energy Potential\n● Deserts perennial solar-energy source ho sakte hain — ~6 hours mein deserts ko itni solar energy milti hai jitni\npoori humanity 1 saal mein consume karti hai (Gerhard Knies ka argument) — dono TRUE, R explains A. [Q2]\nDesert ki Definition\n● Desert = wo region jaha annual rainfall <25 cm hoti hai. [Q3]\nAustralia — Interior Desert\n● Assertion: Australia ka interior part desert/semi-desert hai — TRUE (~70% Australia arid/semi-arid); Reason:\nNorthern Australia temperate zone mein hai — FALSE (Northern Australia actually tropical zone mein hai,\ntemperate south mein hota hai). [Q5]"," The Arid Regions Deserts\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nDesertification\n● Given options mein desertification ki problem sabse KAM: Europe — UNCCD ke according desertification\narid/semi-arid/dry-sub-humid areas mein land degradation hai. [Q6]\nWorld ka Largest Hot Desert\n● Sahara (North Africa) = world ka largest HOT desert; Antarctica = largest desert overall (polar deserts\nincluding). [Q7,Q8]\nMost Populated Desert\n● Thar Desert = world ka most densely populated desert (~83 persons/sq km). [Q9]\nNamed Deserts — Location Matching\n● Takla Makan Desert = China (Xinjiang, south-western part). [Q10]\n● Correct pairs: Sonoran-USA, Taklamakan-China, Karakum-Turkmenistan — Gibson Desert Brazil mein NAHI\n(Western Australia mein hai). [Q11]\n● Karakum Desert = Turkmenistan mein hai (Kazakhstan Kyzylkum/Betpak-Dala se associated hai, Karakum se\nnahi). [Q12]\n● Dasht-e-Lut = Iran (Kerman, Sistan-Baluchestan provinces) — 2005 mein NASA ne yahan ~70.7°C surface\ntemp record kiya. [Q13]\n● Gobi Desert = Mongolia (mainly southern) AND China (northern) — Russia/Kazakhstan tak nahi phailta.\n[Q14,Q15]\n● Thar Desert (Great Indian Desert) = South Asia ka largest desert (NW India → SE Pakistan). [Q17]\n● Great Victoria Desert = Australia (Western + South Australia) — Australia ka largest desert (~348,750 sq km).\n[Q27]\n● Matching: Gobi-Asia, Patagonia-South America, Victoria-Australia, Kalahari-Southern Africa. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'Gibson Desert – Brazil' pairing GALAT hai — Gibson Desert Western Australia mein hai. [Q11]\nDeserts by Size — Ranking\n● Size increasing order: Great Sandy (~285K sq km) < Gobi (~1.3M) < Arabian (~2.3M) < Sahara (~8.6M sq\nkm). [Q16]\nAtacama Desert\n● Atacama = South America mein hai (mainly Northern Chile aur Southern Peru, NOT Southern Chile — yeh\ncommon trap hai); world ka driest non-polar desert hai; sodium nitrate/copper rich hai. [Q18,Q19,Q20]"," The Arid Regions Deserts\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Atacama ki extreme aridity: subtropical high-pressure + cold Humboldt Current + Andes rain-shadow effect —\nteeno factors combine hote hain. [Q20]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Atacama Northern Chile mein hai, Southern Chile mein NAHI — yeh common wrong statement hai. [Q18]\nTemperate Deserts\n● Temperate deserts mid-latitudes (~30°-60°) mein hote hain — examples: Gobi, Ladakh, Patagonia. [Q21]\nTropical Deserts aur Monsoon Winds\n● Tropical deserts trade-wind belts (continents ke western ends) mein pate jaate hain — Statement 1 TRUE; India\nka Eastern Himalayan region South-West monsoon (Bay of Bengal) se zyada rain paata hai, North-East winds\nse NAHI — Statement 2 FALSE. [Q22]\nKalahari Desert\n● Kalahari (~930,000 sq km) mainly Botswana mein hai, kuch part Namibia mein bhi — South\nAfrica/Zaire/Zambia mein nahi (given list mein). [Q23]\n● Kalahari Southern Hemisphere mein hai; naam 'Kalahari' Tswana word se aaya hai (meaning: 'great\nthirst'/'waterless place'). [Q24]\nAfrican-Eurasian Desert Belt — Formation Cause\n● African-Eurasian desert belt formation: Subtropical high-pressure cells (Statement 1) main reason hai —\ndescending dry air; Warm ocean currents necessary condition NAHI hain (Statement 2 FALSE — Gobi cold\ndesert warm current ke bina bhi bana hai). [Q25]\nDesert Animals — Terminology\n● Desert mein rehne wale jeev Xerocoles kehlate hain (Fossorial=digging/underground, Arboreal=trees,\nTerrestrial=land — general terms hain, desert-specific nahi). [Q26]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0119","t":"11 The Grasslands","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Grasslands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Grasslands — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 11_The_Grasslands\nTopic Index\n1. Temperate Grasslands — Names aur Countries\n2. Tropical Grasslands\n3. Pampas — South America ka Grassland\n4. Land of Big Games\n5. Savanna — Forest Development Check\nTemperate Grasslands — Names aur Countries\n● Matching: Steppes-Russia/Europe/Eurasia, Prairies-USA/North America, Velds-South Africa, Downs-\nAustralia, Pampas-Argentina, Pustaz-Hungary. [Q1,Q2,Q3,Q6,Q12,Q13,Q14,Q17]\n● 'Veld-Australia' pairing GALAT hai — Veld actually South Africa mein hai; 'Downs-Tropical grassland' bhi\nGALAT hai — Downs actually temperate grassland hai. [Q2,Q10]\n● Temperate grasslands: Pampas, Veld, Downs, Steppes, Prairies — Savanna temperate NAHI hai (tropical\ngrassland hai). [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Veld = South Africa (Australia NAHI); Downs = temperate grassland (tropical NAHI) — dono common\nwrong pairings hain. [Q2,Q10]\nTropical Grasslands\n● Savanna = sabse widespread tropical grassland Africa (especially East Africa) mein hai — Brazil, Colombia,\nVenezuela, Belize, Honduras, South India mein bhi milti hai. [Q5]\n● Region associations: Argentina-Pampas (correct pair); Campos-Brazilian Highlands, Savanna-East Africa\n(Kenya/Tanzania), Steppes-Eastern Europe/Central Asia. [Q4]\n● Llanos = Venezuela (aur Colombia) mein — Campos South-Eastern Brazil se, Selvas Amazon Basin ke tropical\nevergreen rainforests se associated hain (grassland nahi). [Q9]\n● Tropical grasslands ke continent-matching: Llanos-South America, Steppe-Europe, Prairies-North America,\nVeld-Africa (yeh specific match-set). [Q3]\nPampas — South America ka Grassland\n● Pampas = South America ki mid-latitude/temperate grassland — mainly Argentina mein, extends into\nUruguay/Southern Brazil. Wide, treeless, grassy plains South America mein Pampas kehlate hain.\n[Q6,Q8,Q12,Q13]\n● Pampas plain = Argentina ka main cultivation region hai (TRUE); fertile soil + temperate climate crops/grasses\nke liye useful hai (TRUE) — R correctly explains A. [Q7]"," The Grasslands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nLand of Big Games\n● Tropical Savanna Region ko 'Land of Big Games' kehte hain — large wild animal populations support karta hai\n(zebra, antelope, giraffe, lion, tiger, jaguar, hyena, crocodile, rhinoceros, hippopotamus etc.). [Q15]\nSavanna — Forest Development Check\n● Savanna mein forest development check karne wale factors: Fire, Grazing herbivores, Seasonal rainfall\n(options 2,3,4) — Burrowing animals/termites aur Soil properties primary factors NAHI hain. [Q16]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0120","t":"12 Countries and their Borders","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Countries and their Borders\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Countries and their Borders — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 12_Countries_and_their_Borders\nTopic Index\n1. Countries — Area Ranking\n2. Border Rivers\n3. Gaza Strip\n4. Arabian Peninsula — Countries\n5. Longest Coastline aur Land Border\n6. Central Asia — Countries Sequence\n7. Caspian Sea — Bordering Countries\n8. Dead Sea\n9. Middle East Map — Iraq/Syria/Saudi/Jordan\n10. Israel — Bordering Countries\n11. China — Bordering Countries\n12. Africa Map — Countries Identification\n13. Horn of Africa\n14. Zambia — Neighboring Countries\n15. Adriatic Sea aur North Sea — Bordering Countries\n16. Balkan aur Scandinavian Countries\n17. Central America vs Other Regions\n18. Lithuania — Bordering Countries\n19. Great Britain vs United Kingdom\n20. Oceania\n21. Afghanistan — Bordering Countries\n22. Myanmar — Bordering Countries\n23. Mediterranean Sea — Bordering Countries\n24. Africa — Country Identification aur Coastlines\n25. No Land Border Countries — Largest by Area\n26. Chile — Longest N-S Extension\n27. Indonesia — Land Boundaries\n28. Conflict-Related Famine — Country Pair\n29. UAE — Emirates\n30. Ukraine — Bordering Countries\nCountries — Area Ranking\n● World's largest country by area = Russia (given options mein absent tha, isliye answer '*' marked). [Q1]\n● Total-area convention (US slightly bigger than China): Canada > USA > China > Brazil. [Q2]\n● Ascending area order: Argentina < India < Australia < Brazil (Argentina 2.79M, India 3.29M, Australia\n7.69M, Brazil 8.51M sq km). [Q3]"," Countries and their Borders\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● India se bade 6 countries (area mein): Russia, Canada, USA, China, Brazil, Australia — India world ka 7th\nlargest country hai. France India se bada NAHI hai. [Q5]\n● South Asia ka smallest country (area mein): Maldives (298 sq km) — Bhutan 38,394; Sri Lanka 65,610; Nepal\n147,181; Bangladesh 147,570; Pakistan 796,096; India 3,287,263 sq km. [Q7]\nBorder Rivers\n● USA-Mexico boundary rivers: Rio Grande (long section) AND Colorado (short segment, Arizona-Mexico) —\ndono valid hain is question mein. [Q4]\nGaza Strip\n● Gaza Strip — dono Egypt AUR Israel se border share karti hai (Mediterranean coast, dono ke beech). [Q6]\nArabian Peninsula — Countries\n● Arabian Peninsula ka part: Oman, Kuwait — Iraq aur Syria peninsula ka part NAHI hain. [Q8]\nLongest Coastline aur Land Border\n● Canada ki world mein longest coastline hai (~202,080 km) — Atlantic, Pacific, Arctic teeno oceans se lagti hai,\nnumerous islands + indented shores ki wajah se. [Q9,Q10]\n● India ki sabse lambi international land boundary Bangladesh ke saath hai (~4,096.7 km). [Q11]\nCentral Asia — Countries Sequence\n● Central Asia countries (map sequence 1-5): Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan.\n[Q12]\nCaspian Sea — Bordering Countries\n● Caspian Sea (world ki largest lake, ~371,000 sq km) border karta hai: Russia, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan,\nIran, Azerbaijan — Armenia AUR Iraq border NAHI karte. [Q13,Q14]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Armenia aur Iraq dono ko students often Caspian Sea se galti se associate karte hain — actual 5 bordering\ncountries yaad rakho: Russia, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan, Iran, Azerbaijan. [Q13,Q14]\nDead Sea\n● Dead Sea border karta hai: Jordan (east), Israel/West Bank/Palestine (west) — Lebanon border NAHI karta.\n[Q15]"," Countries and their Borders\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nMiddle East Map — Iraq/Syria/Saudi/Jordan\n● Map labels: A=Iraq, B=Syria, C=Saudi Arabia, D=Jordan (Tigris-Euphrates rivers Iraq ki identifying feature\nhain). [Q16]\nIsrael — Bordering Countries\n● Israel border karta hai: Lebanon (N), Syria (NE), Jordan (E), Egypt (SW) — Mediterranean coast, West Asia\nmein. [Q17]\nChina — Bordering Countries\n● China border karta hai: Russia, Mongolia, Pakistan — Bulgaria se NAHI (Europe mein hai, bahut door). [Q18]\nAfrica Map — Countries Identification\n● Africa map labels (1-4): Libya, Somalia, Nigeria, Namibia. [Q19]\nHorn of Africa\n● Horn of Africa (Somali Peninsula) mein mainly shamil hain: Djibouti, Ethiopia, Eritrea, Somalia — Sudan\nusually included NAHI hota core group mein. [Q20,Q21]\nZambia — Neighboring Countries\n● Zambia border karta hai: Namibia, Tanzania, Angola, Botswana + DR Congo, Malawi, Mozambique, Zimbabwe\n— saare 4 given options actually border karte hain, isliye answer '*' marked. [Q22]\nAdriatic Sea aur North Sea — Bordering Countries\n● Adriatic Sea border karte hain: Albania, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Croatia (+ Slovenia, Montenegro, Italy) —\nMacedonia (landlocked) NAHI border karta. [Q23]\n● North Sea given list mein sirf Germany AUR Norway border karte hain — Finland aur Russia nahi (North Sea\nGreat Britain, Denmark, Norway, Germany, Netherlands, Belgium, France ke beech hai). [Q24]\nBalkan aur Scandinavian Countries\n● Balkan countries: Slovenia, Bulgaria, Romania (+Albania, Bosnia, Greece, Croatia, Serbia) — Austria Balkan\nNAHI hai. [Q25]\n● Strict Scandinavia = Denmark, Norway, Sweden — Finland technically Scandinavia mein include NAHI\nhota (wider Nordic group ka part hai). [Q30]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️"," Countries and their Borders\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n• Finland ko strict sense mein 'Scandinavia' se exclude kiya jaata hai — yeh 'Nordic countries' ka part hai,\nScandinavia ka nahi. [Q30]\nCentral America vs Other Regions\n● Central America: Panama, Honduras, Guatemala — Sierra Leone West Africa mein hai, Central America mein\nnahi. [Q26]\nLithuania — Bordering Countries\n● Lithuania border karta hai: Belarus (640km), Latvia (544km), Poland (100km), Russia/Kaliningrad (261km) —\nUkraine border NAHI karta. Capital: Vilnius, Baltic Sea coast hai. [Q27]\nGreat Britain vs United Kingdom\n● Great Britain = England, Scotland, Wales (Northern Ireland shamil NAHI) — Statement 1 GALAT; UK = Great\nBritain + Northern Ireland; England UK ke total area ka 60% se zyada cover karta hai (thoda over half) —\nStatement 2 (60% se kam) bhi GALAT. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• England UK ka >50% area cover karta hai, but exam mein 'less than 60%' statement correct maana gaya\n(thoda over half technically 60% se kam bhi ho sakta hai) — statement 2 hi sahi mana gaya hai. [Q28]\nOceania\n● Oceania mein 14 countries hain (Melanesia, Micronesia, Polynesia sub-groups) — Indonesia is grouping ka\npart NAHI hai; Australia region ka largest country hai. [Q29]\nAfghanistan — Bordering Countries\n● Afghanistan border karta hai: Turkmenistan (N), Uzbekistan (N), Tajikistan (N), China (NE), Pakistan (E/S), Iran\n(W) — Russia border NAHI karta. [Q31]\n● Given 5 Central Asian countries mein sirf Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan Afghanistan border karte hain\n— Azerbaijan aur Kyrgyzstan NAHI. [Q32]\nMyanmar — Bordering Countries\n● India-China ke alawa Myanmar border karta hai: Bangladesh, Laos, Thailand — total land boundary ~6,522km,\nAndaman Sea/Bay of Bengal coastline bhi hai. [Q33]\nMediterranean Sea — Bordering Countries"," Countries and their Borders\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\n● Given list mein Mediterranean Sea border karte hain: Lebanon, Syria — Jordan aur Iraq NAHI (Mediterranean,\nAtlantic se Gibraltar Strait, Black Sea se Bosporus, Red Sea se Suez Canal se connected hai). [Q34]\nAfrica — Country Identification aur Coastlines\n● Guyana Africa mein NAHI hai (South America mein hai) — Gabon, Guinea, Guinea-Bissau sab Africa mein\nhain. [Q35]\n● Africa ke Western coast pe NAHI hai: Botswana (landlocked, Southern Africa) — Gabon, Liberia, Angola sab\nAtlantic-facing western coast pe hain. [Q36]\nNo Land Border Countries — Largest by Area\n● Land border na rakhne wale island countries mein largest: Japan (377,915 sq km) — Philippines 300,000; New\nZealand 268,838; Cuba 110,860 sq km. [Q37]\nChile — Longest N-S Extension\n● Given options mein longest north-south/latitudinal extension: Chile (long, narrow country, South America ke\nwestern coast pe). [Q38]\nIndonesia — Land Boundaries\n● Indonesia land boundary share karta hai: Malaysia (Borneo/Sebatik), Papua New Guinea (New Guinea), Timor-\nLeste (Timor) — Brunei se land boundary NAHI hai. [Q39]\nConflict-Related Famine — Country Pair\n● War/conflict se linked severe famine/malnutrition case: Yemen aur South Sudan — dono ne prolonged conflict,\ndisplacement se food-security crisis face kiya hai. [Q40]\nUAE — Emirates\n● UAE ke 7 emirates: Abu Dhabi, Dubai, Sharjah, Ajman, Umm Al-Quwain, Fujairah, Ras Al-Khaimah — Dec\n1971 mein 6 emirates federation bana (Ras Al-Khaimah 1972 mein join hua). Capital = Abu Dhabi. [Q41]\nUkraine — Bordering Countries\n● Ukraine border karta hai: Belarus, Russia, Moldova, Romania, Hungary, Slovakia, Poland. Given list (Bulgaria,\nCzech Republic, Hungary, Latvia, Lithuania, Romania) mein sirf Hungary AUR Romania (2 countries) border\nkarte hain. [Q42]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0121","t":"13 Dependent Territories","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Dependent Territories\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Dependent Territories — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 13_Dependent_Territories\nTopic Index\n1. Countries aur Unke Dependent Territories\n2. Landlocked Country\n3. Geographic vs Political Continent Mismatch\n4. Chechnya\n5. World Islands — Owner Countries Matching\n6. Autonomous Regions — Correct Country Matching\nCountries aur Unke Dependent Territories\n● Christmas Island = Australia (Indian Ocean); Greenland = Denmark (self-governing); Martinique = France\n(Caribbean, overseas department); Santa Cruz de Tenerife = Spain (Canary Islands). Question ke options mein\nkoi single clean match nahi banta, isliye answer (*) marked hai. [Q1]\nLandlocked Country\n● Bolivia = South America ka landlocked country (Brazil-N/E, Paraguay-SE, Argentina-S, Chile-SW, Peru-W se\nbordered) — Suriname, Uruguay, Peru sab coastal hain. [Q2]\nGeographic vs Political Continent Mismatch\n● Greenland geographically North America ka part hai lekin politically Denmark (Europe) ke Kingdom ke\nandar self-governing territory hai. [Q3]\nChechnya\n● Chechnya = Russia ka republic hai, Northern Caucasus region mein — capital Grozny. [Q4]\nWorld Islands — Owner Countries Matching\n● Matching: Aleutian Islands–USA, Bear Island–Norway, Greenland–Denmark, Franz Josef Island–Russia. [Q5]\nAutonomous Regions — Correct Country Matching\n● Correct pairs: Catalonia–Spain, Mindanao–Philippines (dono correct); Crimea Hungary ka NAHI (Ukraine ka\ninternationally-recognized part hai, Russia occupy/control karta hai); Oromia Nigeria ka NAHI (Ethiopia ka\nregional state hai). [Q6]"," Dependent Territories\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Match galat hain: Mallorca-Italy (actually Spain), Normandy-Spain (actually France), Sardinia-France (actually\nItaly) — teeno pairs galat hain, koi bhi correctly matched nahi. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Crimea Ukraine (Russia-occupied) ka hai, Hungary ka NAHI; Oromia Ethiopia ka hai, Nigeria ka NAHI —\ndono common wrong-country traps hain. [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0122","t":"14 The Land-Locked Countries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Land-Locked Countries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Land-Locked Countries — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 14_The_Land-Locked_Countries\nTopic Index\n1. Landlocked Country — Definition aur Identification\n2. Multi-Country Landlocked Identification\n3. South Sudan\n4. Trans-Continental Countries\n5. Maginot Line\nLandlocked Country — Definition aur Identification\n● Landlocked country = koi bhi ocean/sea coastline nahi hoti. Examples: Afghanistan, Armenia, Austria, Bolivia,\nBotswana, Ethiopia, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Laos, Mongolia, Nepal, Paraguay, Switzerland, Uganda, Zambia,\nZimbabwe. [Q1]\n● Liberia landlocked NAHI hai — Atlantic Ocean coastline hai (West Africa). [Q1]\n● Chad = Africa ka landlocked country (Angola, Kenya, Senegal sab coastal hain). [Q2]\n● Laos = South-East Asia ka only landlocked country (Myanmar, China, Vietnam, Cambodia, Thailand se\nbordered). [Q3]\n● Thailand landlocked NAHI hai (given options mein) — Nepal, Laos, Bhutan Asia ke landlocked countries hain.\n[Q4]\n● Bolivia = South America ka landlocked country (Peru, Suriname, Uruguay sab coastal hain). [Q5]\n● North America mein koi landlocked country nahi hai — USA, Canada, Mexico sab coastal hain. [Q6]\nMulti-Country Landlocked Identification\n● Landlocked: Afghanistan, Hungary, Switzerland — Malaysia landlocked NAHI (South China Sea + Malacca\nStrait coastline hai). [Q7]\n● Landlocked: Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan (Central Asia) — Georgia landlocked NAHI (Black Sea\ncoastline hai). [Q10]\n● Given options mein landlocked: Hungary (Belgium, Romania, Ukraine sab coastal hain). [Q12]\n● Landlocked: Armenia, Botswana, Ethiopia — Montenegro landlocked NAHI (Adriatic Sea coastline hai).\nCorrect combination (1,3,4) options mein available nahi tha, isliye answer (*) marked. [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Malaysia, Georgia, Montenegro — teeno ko students often galti se landlocked samajh lete hain, lekin teeno ki\nactually coastline hai. [Q7,Q10,Q13]\nSouth Sudan"," The Land-Locked Countries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● South Sudan facts: landlocked country hai (Statement I TRUE); capital Akoba mein NAHI (actual capital Juba\nhai — Statement II FALSE); main river White Nile hai (Statement III TRUE); main religion Christianity hai,\nIslam nahi (Statement IV FALSE). [Q8]\nTrans-Continental Countries\n● Trans-continental countries (Asia+Europe dono mein phaile): Georgia aur Turkey — Laos aur Tunisia trans-\ncontinental NAHI hain (single continent mein hain). [Q9]\nMaginot Line\n● Maginot Line = France aur Germany ke beech (France ki eastern border pe, WWII se pehle German attack\nrokne ke liye banayi gayi fortification line) — kuch part Luxembourg ki taraf bhi extend hota tha. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0123","t":"15 Old Names of Countries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Old Names of Countries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Old Names of Countries — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 15_Old_Names_of_Countries\nTopic Index\n1. Old Name → New Name Mapping\n2. Capital City Name Changes aur Country Renames\n3. Zimbabwe\nOld Name → New Name Mapping\n● Siam→Thailand, Formosa→Taiwan, Mesopotamia→Iraq, Burma→Myanmar. [Q1]\nCapital City Name Changes aur Country Renames\n● Correct pairs: Harare(new)-Salisbury(old); Ethiopia(new)-Abyssinia(old); Kinshasa(new)-Leopoldville(old) —\nGhana ka old name Gold Coast tha, 'Dutch Guiana' NAHI (Dutch Guiana aaj Suriname hai, alag country).\nGhana ne 6 March 1957 ko British se independence li — sub-Saharan Africa ka pehla independent country.\n[Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Ghana ka purana naam Gold Coast tha — 'Dutch Guiana' se confuse mat ho (jo actually Suriname ka purana\nnaam hai). [Q2]\nZimbabwe\n● Zimbabwe pehle Southern Rhodesia kehlata tha (British colony) — capital Harare pehle 'Salisbury' kehlata tha.\n[Q3]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0124","t":"16 International Border Lines","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" nternational Border Lines\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n nternational Border Lines — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 16_International_Border_Lines\nTopic Index\n1. Border Lines — Correct/Incorrect Pairings\n2. Rivers/Lakes Forming International Borders\n3. Durand Line\n4. McMahon Line\n5. Radcliffe Line\n6. 38th Parallel — Korea\n7. Maginot Line — Nature\n8. World ki Longest International Border\n9. Canada-Alaska Boundary\nBorder Lines — Correct/Incorrect Pairings\n● Correct: Radcliffe Line-India/Pakistan, Maginot Line-France/Germany. GALAT: Durand Line-Bangladesh/India\n(actually Afghanistan/Pakistan hai); Hindenburg Line-Belgium/Germany (actually WWI German defensive\nsystem, Northern France mein, koi international boundary NAHI hai). [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Durand Line actually Afghanistan-Pakistan boundary hai — Bangladesh-India se confuse mat karo. [Q1]\nRivers/Lakes Forming International Borders\n● Rhine River Europe mein several places pe international boundaries banati hai. [Q2]\n● Rio Grande River = Mexico aur USA ke beech boundary ka part banati hai. [Q3]\n● Lake Victoria = Tanzania aur Uganda (+Kenya) ke beech international boundary banati hai — world ki largest\nfreshwater lakes mein se ek (surface area se). [Q4]\nDurand Line\n● Durand Line = Pakistan-Afghanistan boundary. [Q5]\nMcMahon Line\n● McMahon Line = India-China border (eastern Himalayan sector) — 1914 Shimla Convention se emerge hui, Sir\nHenry McMahon (British India's Foreign Secretary) ke naam pe. [Q6]"," nternational Border Lines\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nRadcliffe Line\n● Radcliffe Line = India-Pakistan boundary (Partition 1947 se) — baad mein 1971 ke baad India-Bangladesh\nboundary bhi define karti hai. 38th parallel=Korea, 49th parallel=USA-Canada, McMahon=India-China\n(contrast ke liye). [Q7]\n38th Parallel — Korea\n● 38th Parallel (38°N) = North Korea aur South Korea ko divide karta hai. [Q8,Q9]\nMaginot Line — Nature\n● Maginot Line = French fortified defensive line, Germany-facing frontier pe (1930s mein banayi gayi) — strict\ngeographical sense mein yeh international boundary line NAHI hai, military defensive line hai. [Q10]\nWorld ki Longest International Border\n● Canada-USA border = world ki longest international border (~8,891 km) — Russia-Kazakhstan ~6,846km,\nChile-Argentina ~5,308km, India-China ~3,488km se lambi. [Q11]\nCanada-Alaska Boundary\n● 141° West longitude = Canada aur Alaska (USA) ke beech straight-line boundary banata hai (Arctic Ocean se\nMount Saint Elias tak) — April 1906 Convention ke under survey hua. [Q12]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0125","t":"17 Capital Cities of the World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Capital Cities of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Capital Cities of the World — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 17_Capital_Cities_of_the_World\nTopic Index\n1. South-East Asia — Capitals\n2. Europe — Capital Mismatches\n3. Former Capitals\n4. Central America aur Caribbean Capitals\n5. South America aur Europe — Single Capitals\n6. Asia/Africa/South America — Common Mismatches\n7. Pisa — Italy\n8. Africa — Capital Matching (Multiple Sets)\n9. City-State Capitals\n10. Central Asia/Middle East — Capital Mismatches\n11. Middle East — Correct Match\n12. Old/Historical Capital Context (2009 PYQ)\n13. Common Capital Mismatches\n14. Africa/Central Asia — Multi-Set Matching\n15. National Capital NAHI Hone Wale Cities\n16. Correct Pairs (Cyprus, Paraguay)\n17. Australia — States aur Capital Cities\nSouth-East Asia — Capitals\n● Myanmar-Yangon (question ke List-II mein) / actual capital Nay Pyi Taw hai 2006 se; Cambodia-Phnom\nPenh, Vietnam-Hanoi, Laos-Vientiane. [Q1]\n● Myanmar ki new administrative capital Pyinmana ke paas develop hui (Nov 2005 se shift shuru, 2006 mein\nofficially 'Nay Pyi Taw' naam mila). [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Myanmar ki actual current capital Nay Pyi Taw hai (2006 se), Yangon purani capital hai — kuch purane\nexam questions Yangon ko hi correct maante hain, context dhyan se padho. [Q1]\nEurope — Capital Mismatches\n● Slovenia ki capital Ljubljana hai, Bratislava NAHI (Bratislava Slovakia ki capital hai) — Seychelles-Victoria,\nSierra Leone-Freetown, Uzbekistan-Tashkent sab correct. [Q2]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Slovenia (capital Ljubljana) vs Slovakia (capital Bratislava) — naam-similarity ki wajah se yeh common\nconfusion hai. [Q2]"," Capital Cities of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nFormer Capitals\n● Former capitals: Karachi (Pakistan's first capital), Auckland (NZ capital pehle Wellington se), Kyoto (Japan ki\nimperial capital Tokyo se pehle) — Brisbane kabhi Australia ki federal capital NAHI rahi (Melbourne\n1901-1927 temporary seat tha, phir Canberra). [Q3]\nCentral America aur Caribbean Capitals\n● Bahamas-Nassau, Costa Rica-San José, Dominican Republic-Santo Domingo correct hain — Nicaragua ki\ncapital Managua hai, Belmopan NAHI (Belmopan Belize ki capital hai). [Q5]\nSouth America aur Europe — Single Capitals\n● Peru ki capital Lima hai (Lisbon-Portugal, Madrid-Spain, Caracas-Venezuela se contrast). [Q6]\n● Vienna = Austria ki capital — IAEA headquarters bhi yahin hai. [Q7]\nAsia/Africa/South America — Common Mismatches\n● North Korea ki capital Pyongyang hai, Seoul NAHI (Seoul South Korea ki capital hai) — Chile-Santiago,\nArgentina-Buenos Aires, Ethiopia-Addis Ababa correct. [Q8]\n● Japan ki capital Tokyo hai, Kyoto NAHI (Kyoto ek prominent city hai, purani imperial capital) — China-Beijing,\nAustria-Vienna, Spain-Madrid correct. [Q9]\n● Nigeria ki capital Abuja hai, Rabat NAHI (Rabat Morocco ki capital hai) — Ghana-Accra, Kenya-Nairobi,\nNamibia-Windhoek correct. [Q10]\n● China ki capital Beijing hai, Shanghai NAHI (Shanghai bada commercial city hai) — Canada-Ottawa, Australia-\nCanberra, Russia-Moscow correct. [Q19]\nPisa — Italy\n● Pisa (Leaning Tower ke liye famous) Italy mein hai — Arno River ke tat pe, jo Ligurian Sea mein girti hai.\n[Q11]\nAfrica — Capital Matching (Multiple Sets)\n● Windhoek-Namibia, Accra-Ghana, Nairobi-Kenya, Lusaka-Zambia. [Q12]\n● Kenya-Nairobi, Uganda-Kampala, Uzbekistan-Tashkent, Ukraine-Kyiv. [Q13]\n● Kampala-Uganda, Kigali-Rwanda, Kinshasa-DR Congo, Khartoum-Sudan. [Q14]\nCity-State Capitals\n● Berlin (Germany) apne country ka constituent federal state (Länder) bhi hai — Copenhagen, Paris, Oslo apne\ncountries ke federal states NAHI hain. [Q15]"," Capital Cities of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nCentral Asia/Middle East — Capital Mismatches\n● Amman-Jordan, Ulaanbaatar-Mongolia, Sana'a-Yemen correct — Bishkek Kyrgyzstan ki capital hai,\nTajikistan NAHI (Tajikistan ki capital Dushanbe hai). [Q16]\n● Bulgaria-Sofia, Georgia-Tbilisi, Iceland-Reykjavik, Norway-Oslo. [Q17]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Bishkek Kyrgyzstan ki capital hai — Tajikistan se confuse mat karo (Tajikistan ki capital Dushanbe hai).\n[Q16]\nMiddle East — Correct Match\n● Lebanon ki capital Beirut hai (correct pair) — Cyprus-Nicosia (Baghdad nahi), Turkey-Ankara (Ashgabat nahi,\njo Turkmenistan ki hai), Ukraine-Kyiv (Akmola nahi). [Q18]\nOld/Historical Capital Context (2009 PYQ)\n● 2009 exam-context capitals: Burundi-Bujumbura (current capital Gitega hai), Kazakhstan-Astana, Laos-\nVientiane, Mali-Bamako. [Q20]\nCommon Capital Mismatches\n● Ethiopia ki capital Addis Ababa hai, Lusaka NAHI (Lusaka Zambia ki capital hai) — Finland-Helsinki, Bolivia-\nLa Paz, Ukraine-Kyiv correct. [Q21]\n● New Zealand ki capital Wellington hai, Christchurch NAHI — Budapest-Hungary, Kinshasa-Zaire, Nairobi-\nKenya correct. [Q23]\n● Maldives ki capital Male hai, Malabo NAHI (Malabo Equatorial Guinea ki capital hai). [Q33]\n● Cape Verde ki capital Praia hai, Bamako NAHI (Bamako Mali ki capital hai). [Q36]\n● Dominica ki capital Roseau hai, Santo Domingo NAHI (Santo Domingo Dominican Republic ki capital hai).\n[Q37]\n● Finland ki capital Helsinki hai, Oslo NAHI (Oslo Norway ki capital hai). [Q29]\n● Helsinki Finland ki capital hai (Copenhagen-Denmark, Oslo-Norway, Stockholm-Sweden se contrast). [Q26]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Dominica (island nation, capital Roseau) vs Dominican Republic (capital Santo Domingo) — naam similarity\nse confusion hota hai. [Q37]\nAfrica/Central Asia — Multi-Set Matching\n● Azerbaijan-Baku, Gambia-Banjul, Kazakhstan-Astana, Latvia-Riga. [Q22]\n● Brazil-Brasilia, Cuba-Havana, Kenya-Nairobi, Zambia-Lusaka. [Q27]\n● Brazil-Rio de Janeiro (older convention), Costa Rica-San José, Peru-Lima, Ivory Coast-Yamoussoukro. [Q28]"," Capital Cities of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Sri Lanka-Colombo (older convention; actual admin capital Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte 1982 se), Maldives-Male,\nBurma(Myanmar)-Rangoon/Yangon (purani capital), Zimbabwe-Harare, Mauritius-Port Louis. [Q30]\n● Australia-Canberra, Tajikistan-Dushanbe, Tanzania-Dodoma, Switzerland-Bern. [Q31]\n● Uzbekistan-Tashkent, Tajikistan-Dushanbe, Kyrgyzstan-Bishkek, Turkmenistan-Ashgabat. [Q35]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Brazil ki current capital Brasilia hai (1960 se) — Rio de Janeiro purani capital thi, kuch exam questions\npurane convention use karte hain. [Q27,Q28]\nNational Capital NAHI Hone Wale Cities\n● Present-day national capital NAHI: Bonn (West Germany ki purani capital, ab Berlin) aur New York (USA\nka major city, capital Washington D.C. hai) — Canberra aur Beijing sahi capitals hain. [Q24]\n● National capital NAHI: Sydney (Australia ka major city/port hai) — Canberra (Australia), Wellington (NZ),\nRiyadh (Saudi Arabia) sab correct capitals hain. [Q25]\nCorrect Pairs (Cyprus, Paraguay)\n● Cyprus ki capital Nicosia hai (correct pair) — Venezuela-Caracas, Colombia-Bogota, New Zealand-Wellington\n(sahi combos). [Q32]\n● Paraguay ki capital Asunción hai — India ke Vice President M. Venkaiah Naidu ne March 2019 mein visit kiya\ntha (5-7 March Paraguay, 7-9 March Costa Rica). [Q34]\nAustralia — States aur Capital Cities\n● Australia states-capitals: New South Wales-Sydney, Queensland-Brisbane, Victoria-Melbourne, Western\nAustralia-Perth. [Q38]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0126","t":"18 World Towns","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" World Towns\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n World Towns — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 18_World_Towns\nTopic Index\n1. Mega Cities — Coastal Location\n2. Great Lakes (USA) — Lake-City Matching\n3. Central Asia — Capitals Map Identification\n4. Disputed/Special Territories — Capitals\n5. World Cities — Map Identification (Air Routes)\n6. Sri Lanka — Jaffna Location\n7. Alaska\n8. Silicon Valley — Cities\n9. South Africa — 3 Capitals\n10. Pakistan — North-South City Sequence\n11. Kandahar — Afghanistan\n12. Cities — West to East Sequence\n13. Highest Altitude Cities\n14. City-Country Mismatches\n15. Islands/Cities — Country Matching\n16. Arctic Circle — Main Island Location\n17. Sun City\n18. Countries ka Largest City\n19. Named Towns — Country Matching\n20. Kanto Plain\n21. Mexico aur Congo — Continent\n22. Malta\n23. South-East Asia — Cities South-to-North\n24. Middle East/Central Asia Cities — Country Matching\n25. Ground Zero\nMega Cities — Coastal Location\n● World ke zyadatar mega cities coastal areas mein hain (Statement A TRUE) — kyunki wo international ocean\nroutes ke gateways hote hain (Reason R TRUE, sahi explanation hai). [Q1]\nGreat Lakes (USA) — Lake-City Matching\n● Matching: Erie-Detroit, Michigan-Gary, Ontario-Hamilton, Superior-Duluth. [Q2]\nCentral Asia — Capitals Map Identification"," World Towns\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Central Asia capitals: Ashgabat-Turkmenistan, Tashkent-Uzbekistan, Bishkek-Kyrgyzstan, Dushanbe-Tajikistan.\n[Q3]\nDisputed/Special Territories — Capitals\n● Palestine-Ramallah (Palestinian Authority ki principal admin seat; Palestinians East Jerusalem ko bhi capital\nmaante hain, internationally disputed); Kosovo-Pristina; Turkish Cyprus-Nicosia/North Nicosia (limited\ninternational recognition); Taiwan-Taipei. [Q4]\nWorld Cities — Map Identification (Air Routes)\n● Map labels: A-Darwin (N. Australia), B-Kuala Lumpur (Malaysia), C-Nairobi (Kenya), D-Lagos (Nigeria). [Q5]\nSri Lanka — Jaffna Location\n● Northern Sri Lanka map: A-Chavakachcheri, B-Point Pedro, C-Kankesanturai, D-Jaffna. [Q6]\nAlaska\n● Alaska USA ka part hai (north-western extremity) — Russia se 1867 mein purchase kiya gaya, formal transfer 18\nOct 1867 ko hua. [Q7,Q8]\nSilicon Valley — Cities\n● Given options mein Silicon Valley ke andar NAHI hai: Santa Rosa (Sonoma County ka seat) — Campbell, Palo\nAlto, Santa Clara Silicon Valley ke andar hain. [Q9]\nSouth Africa — 3 Capitals\n● South Africa ke 3 capitals hain: Executive-Pretoria, Judicial-Bloemfontein, Legislative/Parliament-Cape Town.\nParliament mein 2 houses: National Council of Provinces (upper) aur National Assembly (lower). [Q10]\nPakistan — North-South City Sequence\n● North-to-South sequence: Peshawar → Islamabad → Gujranwala → Multan. [Q11]\nKandahar — Afghanistan\n● Kandahar (Qandahar) = Southern Afghanistan mein hai (Tarnak River ke paas, ~1,000m elevation) —\nsouthern Afghanistan ka major commercial centre hai. [Q12]\nCities — West to East Sequence"," World Towns\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● West-to-East order: Lisbon → London → Frankfurt → Beirut. [Q13]\nHighest Altitude Cities\n● Given options mein highest altitude city: Lhasa (Tibet, ~3650m) — Thimphu (Bhutan, ~2248-2648m), Gartola\n(Nepal, ~1733m), Kathmandu (Nepal, ~1350m) se zyada. [Q14]\nCity-Country Mismatches\n● Auroville-Pondicherry, Bandung-Indonesia, Batticaloa-Sri Lanka correct hain — Baikonur Cosmodrome\nKazakhstan mein hai, Ukraine NAHI (Aral Sea se ~200km east). [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Baikonur Cosmodrome Kazakhstan mein hai (Ukraine NAHI) — space-program se associated hone ki wajah\nse Russia/Ukraine se galti se link kiya jaata hai. [Q15]\nIslands/Cities — Country Matching\n● Correct: Sicily-Italy, Newfoundland-Canada, Durban-South Africa — Tasmania Uganda ka NAHI hai\n(Australia ka island state hai, Bass Strait se mainland se separate). [Q16]\n● Durban = South Africa mein hai (KwaZulu-Natal province, Indian Ocean coast, Port Natal harbour ke around\ndevelop hua). [Q17]\nArctic Circle — Main Island Location\n● Given options mein jiska main island Arctic Circle ke south mein hai: Iceland (Arctic Circle sirf chhote Grímsey\nisland se guzarti hai) — Finland, Norway, Sweden ka mainland Arctic Circle ke north tak extend hota hai.\n[Q18]\nSun City\n● Sun City = South Africa (North West province, Elands River aur Pilanesberg Mountains ke beech) mein hai.\n[Q19]\nCountries ka Largest City\n● Country-largest city matching: Canada-Toronto, Greece-Athens, Nigeria-Lagos, Syria-Damascus. [Q20]\nNamed Towns — Country Matching\n● Davos-Switzerland, Barcelona-Spain, Auckland-New Zealand, Kandy-Sri Lanka. [Q21]"," World Towns\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\nKanto Plain\n● Kanto Plain = Japan ka highly developed, urbanised aur industrialised plain hai. [Q22]\nMexico aur Congo — Continent\n● Mexico = North America mein hai (USA-N, Guatemala-SW, Belize-SE se bordered; Gulf of Mexico-E,\nPacific/Gulf of California-W) — Canada+USA ke baad North America ka 3rd largest country. [Q23]\n● Congo (DR Congo aur Republic of Congo dono) = Africa mein hain, Equator pe located. [Q24]\nMalta\n● Malta (Southern Europe ka small island country) Mediterranean Sea mein hai. [Q25]\nSouth-East Asia — Cities South-to-North\n● South-to-North order: Jakarta (6°12'S) → Singapore (1.3°N) → Bangkok (13°45'N) → Hanoi (21°2'N).\n[Q26]\nMiddle East/Central Asia Cities — Country Matching\n● Correct: Aleppo-Syria, Mazar-i-Sharif-Afghanistan — Kirkuk Yemen ka NAHI (Iraq mein hai); Mosul\nPalestine ka NAHI (Iraq mein hai). [Q27]\n● Afghanistan mein NAHI hain: Fergana aur Samarkand (dono Uzbekistan mein hain) — Ghazni aur Kandahar\nAfghanistan mein hi hain. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Kirkuk aur Mosul dono Iraq mein hain, Yemen/Palestine mein NAHI — Middle-East city-country confusion\ncommon hai. [Q27]\nGround Zero\n● 'Ground Zero' (9/11 context, 2001 terrorist attacks) = New York City (World Trade Center site) — generic term\nexplosion centre ke liye bhi use hota hai. [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0127","t":"19 Geographical Sobriquets","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Geographical Sobriquets\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Geographical Sobriquets — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 19_Geographical_Sobriquets\nTopic Index\n1. 'Venice of North' aur City-Sobriquets\n2. Midnight Sun\n3. Continent aur Country Nicknames\n4. Landmark Matching (Multi-set)\n5. Sri Lanka\n6. Ninety East Ridge\n7. South America — City Sobriquets\n8. USA State Nickname\n9. Lakes — Sobriquets\n10. Europe — Oil Capital\n11. Philippines — Island Sobriquet\n'Venice of North' aur City-Sobriquets\n● St. Petersburg (Russia) = 'Venice of North' — Neva River pe located; yeh naam Amsterdam, Bruges,\nCopenhagen, Hamburg, Manchester, Stockholm ke liye bhi use hota hai (7-city group). [Q1]\n● Chicago = 'City of Smoke' (conventional exam GK, industrial-era image se). [Q6]\n● Istanbul (Turkey) = 'Gateway to the West' — Marmara Sea, Bosporus Strait, Golden Horn se ghira peninsular\narea mein. [Q11]\n● Venice = 'City of Canals' (bhi 'Queen of the Adriatic'). [Q15]\n● San Francisco = 'City of the Golden Gate' (Golden Gate Bridge, San Francisco Bay entrance pe). [Q16]\n● Osaka (Japan) = 'Manchester of the East' (bhi 'Nation's Kitchen', Kansai region ki trading city). [Q17]\nMidnight Sun\n● Midnight Sun North Pole AUR South Pole dono pe (respective hemisphere's summer mein) hota hai — Equator\nya Tropic of Cancer pe NAHI. [Q2]\nContinent aur Country Nicknames\n● South America = 'Continent of Birds' (~3,402 bird species, world ke ~11,000 mein se). [Q3]\n● Africa = 'Dark Continent'. [Q5]\n● Thailand = 'Land of White Elephants' (sacred maana jaata hai). [Q12]\n● Japan = 'Land of the Rising Sun' (Japanese naam 'Nippon' bhi yehi matlab). [Q13]\n● South Korea = 'Land of Morning Calm' (natural beauty, mountains, tranquil mornings se). [Q19]"," Geographical Sobriquets\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nLandmark Matching (Multi-set)\n● Niagara Falls-New York State (USA-Canada border), Land of Thousand Lakes-Finland, Eiffel Tower-Paris, Roof\nof World-Pamir. [Q4]\n● Dark Continent-Africa, Roof of World-Pamir, Country of Thousand Lakes-Finland, Pearls Island-Bahrain. [Q5]\n● Finland = 'Garden of Lakes'/'Land of Thousand Lakes' (1 lakh+ lakes). [Q14]\nSri Lanka\n● Sri Lanka = 'Mistress of Eastern Sea' (bhi 'Pearl of the Indian Ocean') — Indian subcontinent ke south mein,\nEquator se ~880km north. [Q7]\nNinety East Ridge\n● Ninety East Ridge (90°E) = Indian Ocean mein hai (~5,000km, 90°E longitude parallel, Bay of Bengal se\nAntarctic plate boundary tak) — Earth ke ocean floor ki sabse lambi/straightest linear features mein se ek. [Q8]\nSouth America — City Sobriquets\n● Buenos Aires (Argentina) = 'Paris of America'/'Paris of South America' (wide roads ki wajah se) — Argentina ki\ncapital aur largest city. [Q9]\nUSA State Nickname\n● Kentucky = 'Blue Grass State' (East South-Central USA region mein). [Q10]\nLakes — Sobriquets\n● Lake Baikal (Russia/Siberia) = 'Pearl of Siberia' — world ki oldest AND deepest freshwater lake. [Q18]\nEurope — Oil Capital\n● Aberdeen (Scotland/UK) = 'Oil Capital of Europe' — North Sea oil discoveries se petroleum industry grow hui.\n[Q20]\nPhilippines — Island Sobriquet\n● Mindanao (Philippines) = 'The Land of Promise' — Philippine archipelago ka ek island. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0128","t":"20 The Hydrosphere","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Hydrosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Hydrosphere — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 20_The_Hydrosphere\nTopic Index\n1. Ocean Mean Temperature (OMT)\n2. Earth's Surface — Water Coverage\n3. Earth's Centre — Nearest Point at Sea Level\n4. Datum Line\n5. Pacific Ocean — Largest\n6. Mid-Oceanic Ridge\n7. Ninety East Ridge\n8. Gravitational Water — Tension\n9. Freshwater Distribution\n10. Oceanic Floor — Most Extensive Part\n11. Red Sea\n12. Ocean Ridges/Plateaus/Basins — Location Mismatch\n13. Indian Ocean — Ancient Name aur Equator\nOcean Mean Temperature (OMT)\n● 26°C isotherm generally 50-100m depth pe milti hai — Jan-March SW Indian Ocean mein average depth ~59m\nhai (129m NAHI, Statement 1 FALSE). OMT SST se better predictor hai India ke monsoon rainfall (long-\nterm mean 887.5mm se kam/zyada) predict karne ke liye — Statement 2 TRUE. [Q1]\nEarth's Surface — Water Coverage\n● Earth ki surface ka ~70.9% (two-thirds se zyada) water se covered hai (~361.9 million sq km) — sirf ~29.1%\nland hai (~148.17 million sq km). [Q2]\nEarth's Centre — Nearest Point at Sea Level\n● Earth oblate spheroid hai (polar radius equatorial radius se kam) — sea level pe North Pole Earth ke centre ke\nsabse close hai (Equator se zyada close). [Q3]\nDatum Line\n● Datum Line = sea level ke reference mein horizontal line hai, jisse heights aur depths measure hoti hain. [Q4]\nPacific Ocean — Largest"," The Hydrosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Pacific Ocean = hydrosphere ka largest part (~155.6 million sq km) — Atlantic (~76.8M), Indian (~68.6M),\nSouthern (~20.3M) se bada. [Q5]\nMid-Oceanic Ridge\n● Mid-Oceanic Ridge (~64,000-65,000km lambi, 2,000-2,400km chaudi) — Arctic, Atlantic, Indian, Pacific\noceans se guzarti hai, Earth ki sabse badi continuous geological features mein se ek hai — North/South Atlantic\nse hoke Indian Ocean se South Pacific mein enter karti hai, Australia-Antarctica ke beech tak extend hoti hai.\n[Q6]\nNinety East Ridge\n● Ninety East Ridge (90°E Ridge) = Indian Ocean mein hai — ~5,000km lambi, ~34°S se 10°N tak, average\nwidth ~200km, 90°E longitude ke roughly parallel. [Q7]\nGravitational Water — Tension\n● Gravitational Water (soil macropores mein) ka tension 1/3 atmosphere se kam hota hai (ya zero) — gravity ki\nwajah se easily downward move karta hai. [Q8]\nFreshwater Distribution\n● Earth ka total water: ~96.5% saline ocean water, ~2.5% freshwater. Human-use ke liye directly available water\nEarth ke total water ka 1% se kam hai (Statement 1 TRUE); total freshwater ka ~68.7% glaciers/polar ice\nmein hai, 95% NAHI (Statement 2 galat number, sahi ~68.7% hai) — is question mein sirf Statement 1 correct\nanswer hai. [Q9]\n● Rivers/lakes ka water groundwater se KAM hai (Statement 1 FALSE); polar ice/glaciers ka water groundwater se\nZYADA hai (Statement 2 TRUE). [Q10]\n● Planet pe sabse zyada freshwater Glaciers aur mountains (permanent ice/snow, ~68.7%) mein hai —\nGroundwater ~30.1%, lakes/rivers bahut kam. [Q11]\n● Glaciers/ice ke baad, remaining freshwater ka largest proportion Groundwater (~30.1%) mein hai — freshwater\nlakes ~0.26%, atmosphere ~0.04%, rivers ~0.006%. [Q12]\n● World water sources descending order: Oceans (96.5%) > Ice/Glaciers (1.74%) > Groundwater (1.7%) >\nRivers (0.0002%). [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Total freshwater ka glaciers/polar-ice share ~68.7% hai (95% NAHI) — exact percentage yaad rakho, alag\nquestions mein alag context mein use hota hai. [Q9]\nOceanic Floor — Most Extensive Part\n● Deep Sea (Abyssal) Plains = oceanic floor ka sabse extensive/broad part hain (Ocean Deeps, Oceanic Slope,\nContinental Shelves se zyada area cover karte hain) — several thousand metres depth, fine sediments se\ncovered. [Q14]"," The Hydrosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nRed Sea\n● Red Sea = Axial Trough ka example hai (Africa-Arabia ke beech, magnetic anomaly bhi identified) — Suez\nCanal se commercial importance badhi (North Africa/Europe ko Asia se connect karta hai). [Q15]\nOcean Ridges/Plateaus/Basins — Location Mismatch\n● Correct pairs: Cocoa Ridge-Pacific, Walvis Ridge-Atlantic, Agulhas Basin-Indian Ocean — Telegraph Plateau\nAtlantic Ocean mein hai, Indian Ocean NAHI (yeh GALAT combination hai). [Q16]\nIndian Ocean — Ancient Name aur Equator\n● Indian Ocean ko ancient Greeks 'Erythraean Sea' kehte the (Red Sea, Gulf of Aden, Arabian Sea, northern\nIndian Ocean ke liye collectively) — Statement 1 TRUE; Indian Ocean Equator ke dono taraf phaila hai\n(~30°N se 60°S) — Statement 2 bhi TRUE. [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0129","t":"21 Important Seas of the World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" mportant Seas of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n mportant Seas of the World — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 21_Important_Seas_of_the_World\nTopic Index\n1. Caspian Sea\n2. Turkey — Surrounding Seas\n3. West-to-East Sea Sequence\n4. Sargasso Sea\n5. Mediterranean-System Seas\n6. Mediterranean Sea — Bordering Countries\n7. Gaza Strip\n8. Seas — Maximum Depth Comparison\n9. Sea-Country Pair Matching (Correct/Incorrect)\n10. Black Sea — Bordering Countries\n11. Red Sea\n12. Baltic Sea — Bordering Countries\nCaspian Sea\n● Baku (Azerbaijan's capital) Caspian Sea ke coast pe hai — Caspian Sea world ki largest saltwater lake/inland\nsea hai. [Q1,Q5]\n● Caspian Sea bordering countries: Kazakhstan, Russia, Azerbaijan, Turkmenistan, Iran — Volga River isi mein\nmerge hoti hai. [Q4]\n● Aral Sea (Central Asia) surround karte hain: Kazakhstan aur Uzbekistan. [Q12]\nTurkey — Surrounding Seas\n● Turkey ke North mein Black Sea hai — West mein Aegean Sea, South mein Mediterranean, NW interior mein\nSea of Marmara. [Q2]\n● Turkey Black Sea aur Mediterranean Sea ke beech located hai — Bosporus Strait (Black-Marmara) aur\nDardanelles (Marmara-Aegean/Mediterranean) inhe connect karte hain. [Q3]\nWest-to-East Sea Sequence\n● West-to-East order: Mediterranean Sea → Black Sea → Caspian Sea → Aral Sea. [Q4]\nSargasso Sea\n● Sargasso Sea = North Atlantic Ocean mein hai (Sargassum seaweed se naam mila) — world ka only sea jiski\nkoi land coastline NAHI hai (boundaries ocean currents se bani hain: Gulf Stream-W, North Atlantic Current-\nN, Canary Current-E, North Atlantic Equatorial Current-S). [Q6,Q7,Q8,Q9,Q10]"," mportant Seas of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Sargasso Sea ki characteristic feature typical marine vegetation (Sargassum seaweed) hai, extreme\ntemperature/salinity nahi — aur yeh koi land-boundary NAHI rakhta. [Q9,Q10]\nMediterranean-System Seas\n● Tyrrhenian Sea = Italy, Sardinia, Corsica, Sicily se surrounded (Mediterranean system ka part). [Q11]\nMediterranean Sea — Bordering Countries\n● Africa mein Chad Mediterranean se border NAHI karta (landlocked hai) — Algeria, Morocco, Tunisia sab\nMediterranean coastline rakhte hain. [Q13]\n● South-West Asia mein Jordan Mediterranean se open NAHI hota (landlocked-jaisa, Red Sea/Dead Sea se\nconnected) — Syria, Lebanon, Israel sab Mediterranean coastline rakhte hain. [Q14]\n● Given list mein Mediterranean border karte hain: Lebanon aur Syria — Jordan aur Iraq NAHI. [Q20]\nGaza Strip\n● Gaza Strip Mediterranean Sea ke near hai (Egypt-Israel ke beech) — 2007 se HAMAS ka de facto control hai.\n[Q15]\nSeas — Maximum Depth Comparison\n● Given options mein deepest: South China Sea (~5,560m) — Mediterranean (~5,267m), Sea of Japan (~3,700-\n3,800m), Bering Sea (isse kam) se zyada gehra. [Q16]\nSea-Country Pair Matching (Correct/Incorrect)\n● Correct: Adriatic Sea-Albania, Caspian Sea-Kazakhstan, Mediterranean Sea-Morocco. GALAT: Black Sea-\nCroatia (Croatia Adriatic Sea pe hai, Black Sea NAHI); Red Sea-Syria (Syria Mediterranean coast pe hai, Red\nSea NAHI). [Q17]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Croatia Adriatic Sea pe hai (Black Sea NAHI); Syria Mediterranean coast pe hai (Red Sea NAHI) — dono\ncommon wrong-sea-pairing hain. [Q17]\nBlack Sea — Bordering Countries\n● Black Sea ke 6 bordering countries: Russia, Ukraine, Romania, Bulgaria, Turkey, Georgia — Syria Black Sea pe\nNAHI hai (Mediterranean ke eastern coast pe hai). [Q18]"," mportant Seas of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nRed Sea\n● Red Sea = Axial Trough ka example (Africa-Arabia ke beech, magnetic anomalies se associated) — Suez Canal\nke baad North Africa/Europe/Asia ke beech trade mein important role. [Q19]\n● Red Sea ko bahut kam precipitation milta hai (Statement 1 TRUE); koi major river Red Sea mein NAHI girti\n— high evaporation ki bharpai mainly Bab-el-Mandeb se inflow se hoti hai (Statement 2 TRUE). [Q22]\nBaltic Sea — Bordering Countries\n● Baltic Sea 9 Northern Europe countries se surrounded: Denmark, Germany, Poland, Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia,\nRussia, Finland, Sweden — Norway Baltic Sea coast pe NAHI hai. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0130","t":"22 The Ocean Currents","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Ocean Currents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Ocean Currents — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 22_The_Ocean_Currents\nTopic Index\n1. Ocean Currents ko Influence Karne Wale Factors\n2. Indian Ocean Currents — Monsoon Effect\n3. Agulhas Current\n4. North Atlantic Drift\n5. South Atlantic — Cold Current\n6. Indian Ocean Currents — Odd One Out\n7. Cold vs Warm Currents Identification\n8. South Atlantic Current Circle (Gyre)\n9. North Atlantic Ocean Currents\n10. Peruvian/Humboldt Current — Odd One Out\n11. Salinity, Tides, Currents — Mixed True/False\n12. Cold vs Warm Current Identification (More Sets)\n13. Gulf Stream\n14. Benguela aur Guinea Currents\n15. Currents — Ocean aur Nature Matching\n16. Equatorial Counter-Current\n17. Pacific Ocean Currents\n18. Atlantic Ocean Current\n19. Warm Current Identification\nOcean Currents ko Influence Karne Wale Factors\n● Ocean currents ko influence karte hain: Earth's rotation, Air pressure/wind, Ocean water density — Earth's\nrevolution NAHI karta. [Q1]\n● Ocean currents ke baare mein saare 4 statements TRUE hain: (1) slow surface water movement, (2) heat balance\nmaintain karte hain, (3) mainly prevailing winds se set hote hain, (4) ocean configuration se affected hote hain.\n[Q2]\nIndian Ocean Currents — Monsoon Effect\n● Indian Ocean mein currents ki regular direction change hone ka reason: Monsoon drift — NE aur SW monsoon\nwinds ki wajah se Northern Indian Ocean mein current direction saal mein 2 baar change hoti hai; Southern\nIndian Ocean mein pattern zyada fixed hota hai. [Q3]\nAgulhas Current"," The Ocean Currents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Agulhas Current = South Indian Ocean ki warm current — South Equatorial Current southward mudkar\nMadagascar+Mozambique currents banati hai, phir Madagascar ke south mein combine hoke Agulhas Current\nbanti hai (SE Africa coast ke saath flow karti hai). [Q4,Q5]\n● Agulhas warm current hai — Canary, Humboldt, Oyashio sab cold currents hain (Agulhas inme se odd-one-out\nhai). [Q6]\nNorth Atlantic Drift\n● North Atlantic Current/Drift se sabse zyada benefit Norway ko hota hai (sub-polar region mein, warm current\nwinter ice spread rokta hai) — isliye 'Blanket of Europe' bhi kehte hain. [Q7]\nSouth Atlantic — Cold Current\n● Benguela Current = South Atlantic Ocean ki cold current (Southern Africa ke west coast ke saath north ki taraf\nflow karti hai, phir South Equatorial Current mein merge) — Canary (North Atlantic cold), Agulhas (S. Indian\nwarm), Brazil (E. Brazil warm) se contrast. [Q8]\nIndian Ocean Currents — Odd One Out\n● Agulhas, Mozambique, South Indian Ocean Current — sab Indian Ocean se belong karte hain; Benguela\nCurrent Indian Ocean ki NAHI hai (South Atlantic ki cold current hai, Africa ke west coast pe). [Q9]\nCold vs Warm Currents Identification\n● Given options mein cold NAHI (matlab warm) hain: Agulhas AUR Brazil Current — Humboldt/Peru aur\nCalifornia Currents cold hain. [Q10]\nSouth Atlantic Current Circle (Gyre)\n● South Atlantic anticlockwise gyre mein shamil: South Equatorial Current, Brazil Current, West Wind Drift/South\nAtlantic Current, Benguela Current — Canary Current is circle ka part NAHI hai (North Atlantic ki current\nhai). [Q11]\nNorth Atlantic Ocean Currents\n● North Atlantic mein flow karte hain: Gulf Stream, Norwegian, Florida (sab warm currents) — Benguela North\nAtlantic mein NAHI hai (South Atlantic cold current hai). [Q12]\nPeruvian/Humboldt Current — Odd One Out\n● Benguela, Brazilian, South Equatorial — Atlantic Ocean se related; Peruvian (Humboldt) Current odd hai —\nSE Pacific ki cold current hai (South America west coast). [Q13]"," The Ocean Currents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nSalinity, Tides, Currents — Mixed True/False\n● Ocean salinity Tropic of Cancer/Capricorn ke around maximum hoti hai (kam rainfall + high evaporation) —\nTRUE statement. Tides exactly 12h30m ke baad NAHI aati; Benguela Atlantic ki hai, Pacific ki NAHI; Sun-\nMoon-Earth alignment spring tide (bada, chota nahi) banata hai. [Q14]\nCold vs Warm Current Identification (More Sets)\n● Peruvian/Humboldt Current = cold — Kuroshio, Gulf Stream, Brazil Current warm hain. [Q15]\n● Humboldt Current SE Pacific mein hai, North Pacific NAHI — Brazil-S.Atlantic, Gulf Stream-N.Atlantic,\nAgulhas-Indian Ocean sab correct pairs hain. [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Humboldt Current South-East Pacific mein hai (North Pacific NAHI) — yeh common wrong pairing hai.\n[Q16]\nGulf Stream\n● Gulf Stream = North Atlantic ki powerful warm current — Gulf of Mexico mein Florida Current se start,\nAntilles Current se merge, Cape Hatteras se hoke US east coast ke saath flow karti hai. 1513 mein Juan Ponce\nde León ne discover kiya tha. [Q17]\nBenguela aur Guinea Currents\n● Map mein South-to-North flow karti cold current = Benguela — doosri current Guinea Current hai. [Q18]\nCurrents — Ocean aur Nature Matching\n● Gulf Stream-Warm current, West Wind Drift-westerly wind belt mein slow eastward water movement, Peru\nCurrent-Pacific Ocean, West Australian Current-Indian Ocean. [Q19]\nEquatorial Counter-Current\n● Equatorial Counter-Current (West→East flow) North aur South Equatorial Currents (East→West) ke beech hoti\nhai — dono equatorial currents ka convergence (western ocean-basin mein water pile-up se pressure-gradient\nforce banta hai) isse explain karta hai — Earth's rotation akela sufficient explanation NAHI hai. [Q20]\nPacific Ocean Currents\n● Pacific Ocean se associated: Kuroshio, California, Humboldt — Canary Current Pacific ki NAHI hai (North\nAtlantic ki hai). [Q21]\nAtlantic Ocean Current"," The Ocean Currents\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Given options mein Atlantic Ocean ki current: Benguela (S.Atlantic, SW Africa coast) — Humboldt(SE Pacific),\nCalifornia(NE Pacific), Alaska(NE Pacific) sab Pacific ki hain. [Q22]\nWarm Current Identification\n● Warm currents: Brazil Current, Gulf Stream, Kuroshio — Cold currents: Falkland, Labrador, Canary. Given\noptions mein warm: Brazil Current. [Q23]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0131","t":"23 The Salinity of the Ocean","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Salinity of the Ocean\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Salinity of the Ocean — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 23_The_Salinity_of_the_Ocean\nTopic Index\n1. Salinity Gradient Terminology\n2. Salinity ka Main Source\n3. Highest Salinity Water Bodies\n4. Density-Salinity-Depth Relationship (Exam Convention)\n5. Great Salt Lake\n6. Arabian Sea Salinity\nSalinity Gradient Terminology\n● Halocline = water salinity gradient (depth ke saath salinity rapidly change) — Thermocline (temperature change),\nPycnocline (density change) se contrast. [Q1]\nSalinity ka Main Source\n● Sea salinity ka main source Land hai (rivers various salts sea tak le jaati hain) — other factors: vaporization,\nwind, rain, ocean currents, volcanoes. Average ocean salinity ~35‰. [Q2]\n● Salinity mein sabse zyada contribution Sodium Chloride (77.8%) ka hota hai — William Dittmar's 1884\nChallenger expedition report (47 types of salts, 7 prominent). [Q3]\nHighest Salinity Water Bodies\n● Dead Sea = world ki sabse zyada saline water body examples mein (~34%/340‰) — Lake Van Turkey (~22‰),\nGreat Salt Lake (variable), Caspian Sea, Black Sea, Baltic Sea, Yellow Sea, Mediterranean sab isse KAM saline\nhain. [Q4,Q5,Q6,Q7,Q8,Q12]\nDensity-Salinity-Depth Relationship (Exam Convention)\n● Accepted exam relation: sea mein density badhne par salinity badhti hai lekin depth ghat-ti hai. [Q9]\nGreat Salt Lake\n● Great Salt Lake = USA (Utah state) mein hai — salinity highly variable hoti hai (lake level aur arm ke hisaab\nse), fixed value se represent nahi kiya jaana chahiye. [Q10]\nArabian Sea Salinity"," The Salinity of the Ocean\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Arabian Sea ki average salinity ~35 ppt (36‰) hai — dry weather + high evaporation + kam river inflow ki\nwajah se; Bay of Bengal isse kam (~30‰) hai. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0132","t":"24 High Tide Low Tide","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" High Tide Low Tide\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n High Tide Low Tide — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 24_High_Tide_Low_Tide\nTopic Index\n1. Tides — Formation ka Karan\n2. Neap Tide\n3. Spring Tide\n4. High Tide — Main Cause\nTides — Formation ka Karan\n● High-Low tide formation: Gravitation + Centripetal force + Centrifugal force (Earth-Moon gravitational pull\n+ inhi 2 forces ka combined effect). [Q1,Q2]\n● Moon-facing side pe direct high tide (gravity dominant); opposite side pe indirect high tide (Earth ka\ncentrifugal force ki wajah se). [Q3]\n● Earth ~24 hours 50 minutes mein 2 high tides aur 2 low tides experience karta hai. [Q1]\nNeap Tide\n● Neap tide ke time: high tide normal se ~20% kam hota hai, low tide normal se zyada hota hai (Statement A\nTRUE); Neap tide new-moon/full-moon PE NAHI hoti — inke ~7th/8th din hoti hai jab Sun-Moon Earth ke\nsapeksh ~right angle pe hote hain (Reason R FALSE). [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Neap tide new-moon/full-moon pe NAHI hoti — yeh common confusion hai (Spring tide in dono din hoti hai,\nNeap tide unke beech ~7-8 din baad). [Q4]\nSpring Tide\n● Spring Tide Sun-Earth-Moon straight line (syzygy) mein hone par hoti hai — dono Full Moon aur New Moon\npositions (M2 aur M4) spring-tide conditions represent karti hain. [Q5,Q6]\nHigh Tide — Main Cause\n● Ocean mein high tide mainly Moon ki wajah se hoti hai (Moon Earth ke bahut close hai, isliye Sun se zyada mass\nhone ke bawajood Moon ka tide-effect zyada hota hai — Moon ka influence Sun se ~2x+ zyada hai). [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0133","t":"25 The Oceanic Trenches","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Oceanic Trenches\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Oceanic Trenches — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 25_The_Oceanic_Trenches\nTopic Index\n1. Trenches — Ocean Location Matching\n2. World ka Deepest Point aur Deepest Trench\n3. Diamantina Trench\n4. Oceans — Deepest Point Matching (Multiple Sets)\n5. Sunda Trench — Location\nTrenches — Ocean Location Matching\n● Indian Ocean: Sunda/Java Trench, Diamantina Trench. North Pacific: Mariana, Kuril, Aleutian, Japan Trenches.\nSouth Pacific: Tonga, Kermadec, Atacama Trenches. North Atlantic: Puerto Rico Trench. South Atlantic: South\nSandwich Trench. [Q1]\nWorld ka Deepest Point aur Deepest Trench\n● Challenger Deep = world ocean ka deepest known point — Mariana Trench (western Pacific) ke andar hai.\n'Mariana Trench' = trench ka naam, 'Challenger Deep' = usi trench ka deepest point. [Q2,Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Mariana Trench = poori khai ka naam; Challenger Deep = usi khai ke andar sabse gehra point — dono ko\nsame mat samjho. [Q2,Q3]\nDiamantina Trench\n● Diamantina Trench = Indian Ocean mein hai (Perth Basin se ~1,125km SW) — 'Diamantina Fracture Zone' bhi\nkehte hain. [Q4]\nOceans — Deepest Point Matching (Multiple Sets)\n● Pacific-Mariana Trench, Atlantic-Puerto Rico Trench, Indian-Java(Sunda) Trench, Arctic-Molloy Deep (Arctic\nka deepest depression/point). [Q5,Q7]\nSunda Trench — Location\n● Sunda Trench (Eastern Indian Ocean, ~2,000 miles/3,200km ka arc) — dono Sumatra AUR Java islands ke\nparallel hai (~190 miles/305km off dono ke SW coasts se) — isliye single-answer options galat, 'None of the\nabove/More than one' (E) hi correct hai. [Q6]"," The Oceanic Trenches\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Sunda Trench sirf Java ya sirf Sumatra ke parallel NAHI hai — dono ke parallel hai, isliye single-option\nanswer galat hoga. [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0134","t":"26 Rivers of the World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Rivers of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Rivers of the World — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 26_Rivers_of_the_World\nTopic Index\n1. River-Sea Pairing (Correct/Incorrect)\n2. Amazon River — World Records\n3. Congo/Zaire River — Equator\n4. Longest Rivers — Comparison\n5. Nile River — Drainage Basin aur Source\n6. Salween River — Myanmar\n7. River-Direction Pairing\n8. Asia ki Longest River\n9. World Drainage Basins — Map Identification\n10. Central Asia — Amu/Syr Darya Rivers\n11. Black Sea — Rivers Draining Into\n12. Rivers — Sea/Ocean Destination Matching\n13. Rift Valley — River\n14. Elbe aur Rhine — North Sea\n15. Asia-Related River/Lake Identification\n16. Limpopo River — Tropic of Capricorn\n17. Sri Lanka — Radial Drainage\n18. European Rivers — Country Matching\n19. Mekong River — Countries\n20. Lake Itasca — Mississippi's Source\n21. Bird's Foot Delta\n22. Grand Canyon — Colorado River\nRiver-Sea Pairing (Correct/Incorrect)\n● Correct: Volga-Caspian Sea, Zambezi-Indian Ocean — GALAT: Mekong-Andaman Sea (actually South China\nSea, Vietnam delta se), Thames-Irish Sea (actually North Sea, Thames Estuary se). [Q1]\nAmazon River — World Records\n● Amazon = world ki largest drainage basin wali river hai (~7 million sq km) — average discharge se bhi largest\nhai. [Q2]\n● Conventional exam classification mein Nile 1st longest, Amazon 2nd longest maani jaati hai — kuch studies\nAmazon ko Nile se lambi bhi bataate hain (source/mouth definition pe depend karta hai). [Q3]\n● Amazon = South America ki longest river hai — world ki largest river (discharge+basin se). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️"," Rivers of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n• Length mein Nile #1 (conventional), Amazon #2 maani jaati hai — lekin discharge/drainage-basin mein\nAmazon world ki largest hai. Dono facts alag hain, confuse mat ho. [Q2,Q3]\nCongo/Zaire River — Equator\n● Congo (Zaire) River = Africa ki 2nd largest river (Amazon ke baad) — Equator ko 2 baar cross karti hai. [Q4]\n● Cameroon Congo Basin ka part hai — Nigeria, South Sudan, Uganda conventional 6-core-country list mein\nNAHI aate. [Q5]\nLongest Rivers — Comparison\n● Given options mein longest: Amazon — Amur, Congo, Lena sab isse chhoti hain (Nile options mein nahi tha).\n[Q6]\nNile River — Drainage Basin aur Source\n● Nile drainage basin countries: Burundi, Rwanda, DR Congo, Ethiopia, Sudan, South Sudan, Tanzania, Kenya,\nEritrea, Uganda, Egypt — Chad Nile basin ka part NAHI hai. [Q8]\n● Blue Nile ka origin Lake Tana (Ethiopia) se hota hai — Ethiopia mein upper course ko 'Abbay' kehte hain.\n[Q9]\n● 'Egypt is the Gift of the Nile' — Nile Egypt ko water + fertile alluvium deti hai (dense settlement/agriculture\npossible banati hai arid region mein); Nile Valley/Delta Sahara ke andar oasis-jaisi fertile corridor banate hain\n— dono statements TRUE, R sahi explains A. [Q10]\nSalween River — Myanmar\n● Salween River = Myanmar ke map mein eastern part, north-south flow — Tibetan Plateau se nikalti hai,\n~2,815km cover karke Andaman Sea mein girti hai. [Q11]\n● Asia ki rivers mein South ki taraf flow karti hai: Salween — Amur (E/NE), Lena (N-Arctic), Ob (N-Arctic)\ndifferent directions mein flow karti hain. [Q12]\nRiver-Direction Pairing\n● Correct: Amur-NE, Syr Darya-NW (Aral Sea ki taraf), Angara-North (Baikal se Yenisei tak) — Mekong\nGALAT hai (actual direction South-East hai, South-West NAHI). [Q13]\nAsia ki Longest River\n● Yangtze (Chang Jiang) = Asia ki longest river (~6,300km) — poori China ke andar flow karti hai, East China\nSea (Shanghai ke paas) mein girti hai. Indus, Brahmaputra, Hwang Ho isse chhoti hain. [Q14]\nWorld Drainage Basins — Map Identification"," Rivers of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Drainage basins map: A-Paraná (South America), B-Ganga-Brahmaputra (South Asia), C-Zambezi (Southern\nAfrica), D-Indus (South Asia). [Q15]\n● Americas rivers map: A-Yukon, B-Mackenzie, C-St. Lawrence, D-Orinoco. [Q16]\nCentral Asia — Amu/Syr Darya Rivers\n● Amu Darya aur Syr Darya (Central Asia ki prominent rivers) Aral Sea mein girti hain. [Q17]\nBlack Sea — Rivers Draining Into\n● Dnieper aur Danube dono Black Sea mein girti hain — Dnieper Moscow ke west se nikalti hai; Danube (Volga\nke baad Europe ki 2nd longest, Germany se nikalti hai, ~2,857 miles). [Q18]\n● Volga = Europe ki longest river, Valdai Hills (Moscow NW) se nikalti hai, Caspian Sea mein girti hai — Black\nSea mein NAHI. Ural River bhi Caspian Sea mein girti hai (Ural Mountains se). [Q19]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Volga Caspian Sea mein girti hai, Black Sea mein NAHI — Dnieper aur Danube Black Sea mein girti hain,\nin dono ko confuse mat karo. [Q18,Q19]\nRivers — Sea/Ocean Destination Matching\n● Lena-Arctic Ocean, Amur-Pacific Ocean, Tigris-Persian Gulf (Shatt al-Arab system se), Mahi-Arabian Sea.\n[Q20]\nRift Valley — River\n● Rhine River = Swiss Alps se nikalti hai, Rift Valley se hoke North Sea mein girti hai — Bonn (famous German\ncity) Rhine ke tat pe hai. Amazon, Indus, Volga rift valley se nahi guzarti. [Q21]\nElbe aur Rhine — North Sea\n● Elbe AUR Rhine dono North Sea mein apna water drain karti hain — Elbe basin ~1.5 lakh sq km. [Q22]\nAsia-Related River/Lake Identification\n● Lop Nor (China, Xinjiang), Amur (E. Asia, Russia-China boundary), Tigris (E. Turkey se Iraq, Persian Gulf tak)\n— sab Asia se related; Niger Africa se related hai, Asia se NAHI (Guinea highlands se nikalti hai, Gulf of\nGuinea tak). [Q23]\nLimpopo River — Tropic of Capricorn\n● Limpopo River (Africa) — Tropic of Capricorn ko 2 baar cross karti hai (Zambezi, Congo, Niger nahi karti).\n[Q24]"," Rivers of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\nSri Lanka — Radial Drainage\n● Sri Lanka = radial drainage pattern ka best example — south-central highland (~1,500m) se rivers radially\nsamundar ki taraf flow karti hain. Mahaweli River Sri Lanka ki longest river hai (~335km), Hatton plateau se\nnikalti hai, Bay of Bengal mein girti hai. [Q25,Q26]\nEuropean Rivers — Country Matching\n● Correct: Dnieper-Ukraine, Po-Italy, Rhine-Germany — Rhone Spain ki NAHI hai (Rhone Geneva/Switzerland\nse hoke Mediterranean ki Gulf of Lions mein girti hai — France se zyada associated hai, Spain se nahi). [Q27]\nMekong River — Countries\n● Mekong Tibetan Plateau se nikalti hai, flow karti hai: China (Yunnan), Myanmar, Laos, Thailand, Cambodia,\nVietnam — South China Sea mein girti hai. Malaysia AUR Bangladesh se NAHI guzarti. [Q28,Q29]\n● Mekong Statement 1 (Tibetan Plateau se origin) TRUE; Statement 2 (Delta Southern Cambodia mein) FALSE\n— Mekong Delta actually mainly Southern Vietnam mein hai (Cambodia lower-basin ka important part hai,\nlekin delta khud Cambodia mein nahi hai). [Q31]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Mekong Delta Southern Vietnam mein hai, Cambodia mein NAHI — Cambodia lower Mekong basin ka part\nhai lekin delta wahan nahi. [Q31]\nLake Itasca — Mississippi's Source\n● Lake Itasca (Minnesota) = Mississippi River ka conventional source hai — Mississippi USA se hoke south\nmein flow karti hai, Gulf of Mexico mein girti hai. Major tributaries: Missouri, Ohio, Arkansas, Red River.\n[Q30]\nBird's Foot Delta\n● Mississippi River ke mouth pe 'Bird's Foot' type delta banta hai. [Q32]\nGrand Canyon — Colorado River\n● Grand Canyon (Arizona, USA) Colorado River ke erosion se bana hai — major incision phase last ~5-6\nmillion years mein hua (landscape/rocks bahut purani hain). Sediment/rock-fragments abrasion badhate hain,\nflowing water + weathering canyon ko deepen/widen karte hain. [Q33]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0135","t":"27 Towns and Cities along the Banks of Rivers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Towns and Cities along the Banks of Rivers\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Towns and Cities along the Banks of Rivers — FULL\n🗺️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 27_Towns_and_Cities_along_the_Banks_of_Rivers\nTopic Index\n1. River-City Matching (Multi-set)\n2. City-River Mismatches\n3. Paris — Seine River\n4. City-River Mismatches (Multiple Sets)\n5. Huangpu River — Shanghai\n6. South-East Asia — City-River Matching\n7. Rivers — Country Matching\n8. European Cities — River Mismatches\n9. European Port Cities — River Matching\n10. Africa/Europe Cities — River Matching\n11. Watershed — Definition\nRiver-City Matching (Multi-set)\n● Shatt-al-Arab-Basra, Paraguay-Asunción, Niger-Niamey, Danube-Vienna. [Q1]\n● Paris-Seine, Kinshasa-Congo(Zaire), Bangkok-Chao Phraya, Asunción-Paraguay. [Q2]\n● Washington D.C.-Potomac, Berlin-Spree, Paris-Seine, Madrid-Manzanares. [Q4]\n● Berlin-Spree, Lahore-Ravi, New York-Hudson, Rome-Tiber. [Q8]\nCity-River Mismatches\n● Khartoum-Nile, New York-Hudson, Berlin-Spree correct hain — Sydney-Seine GALAT hai (Sydney Australia\nmein hai, Seine Paris/France mein bahti hai). [Q3]\n● London-Thames, New York-Hudson, Vienna-Danube correct hain — Berlin-Rhine GALAT hai (Berlin actually\nSpree River pe hai). [Q9]\n● Bonn-Rhine, Cairo-Nile, New York-Hudson correct hain — Vienna-Volga GALAT hai (Vienna Danube pe hai,\nVolga Russia mein bahti hai). [Q10]\n● Correct pair: Budapest-Danube — Paris-Swan galat (Paris actually Seine pe), Perth-Seine galat (Perth actually\nSwan River pe), Cairo-Congo galat (Cairo actually Nile pe). [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Berlin Spree River pe hai — Rhine NAHI. Vienna Danube pe hai — Volga NAHI. Paris Seine pe hai (Perth\nSwan River pe hai) — inhe swap karke galat option banaya jaata hai. [Q9,Q10,Q11]"," Towns and Cities along the Banks of Rivers\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nParis — Seine River\n● Paris (France ki capital) Seine River ke tat pe hai — Belgrade (Danube+Sava), Lisbon (Tagus mouth), Budapest\n(Danube) se contrast. [Q5,Q6,Q7]\nCity-River Mismatches (Multiple Sets)\n● Budapest-Danube, Cologne-Rhine correct — New Orleans-Missouri GALAT (actually Mississippi River pe\nhai); Hyderabad(India)-Paleru GALAT (actually Musi River pe hai). [Q12]\n● Hamburg-Elbe correct hai — Belgrade-Seine galat (actually Danube+Sava), Kiev-Don galat (actually Dnieper),\nLahore-Satluj galat (actually Ravi). [Q13]\n● Danube ke tat pe: Belgrade, Budapest, Vienna — Rome Danube pe NAHI hai (Tiber River pe hai). [Q14]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• New Orleans Mississippi pe hai (Missouri NAHI); Hyderabad(India) Musi pe hai (Paleru NAHI) — common\nwrong pairings. [Q12]\nHuangpu River — Shanghai\n● Huangpu River (~113km) Shanghai (China) se hoke bahti hai — city ko Pudong(east) aur Puxi(west) mein\ndivide karti hai, drinking water ka major source; Shanghai Yangtze River ke mouth pe bhi hai. [Q15]\nSouth-East Asia — City-River Matching\n● Bangkok-Chao Phraya(Menam), Phnom Penh-Mekong, Hanoi-Red River, Yangon-Irrawaddy. [Q16]\nRivers — Country Matching\n● Potomac-USA, Nile-Sudan, Tigris-Iraq, Thames-England. [Q17]\nEuropean Cities — River Mismatches\n● Belgrade-Danube, Warsaw-Vistula, Washington-Potomac correct hain — Lisbon-Tiber GALAT hai (Tiber\nItaly/Rome ki hai, Lisbon actually Tagus River pe hai). [Q18]\nEuropean Port Cities — River Matching\n● London-Thames, Antwerp-Scheldt, Rotterdam-Rhine(system), Hamburg-Elbe. [Q19]\n● Rotterdam-Rhine(system), Paris-Seine, Budapest-Danube, Washington-Potomac. [Q20]\nAfrica/Europe Cities — River Matching"," Towns and Cities along the Banks of Rivers\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Khartoum-Nile (White+Blue Nile confluence), Brazzaville-Congo(Zaire), Rotterdam-Rhine(system), Paris-Seine.\n[Q21]\nWatershed — Definition\n● Jal ko collect+store+release karne wali geographical unit Watershed kehlati hai (catchment area) —\nrainfall/snowmelt ko creeks/streams/rivers ki taraf channel karti hai, phir reservoirs/bays/ocean tak. [Q22]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0136","t":"28 Landforms by River","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Landforms by River\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Landforms by River — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 28_Landforms_by_River\nTopic Index\n1. Delta Formation — Favourable/Unfavourable Conditions\n2. World ka Largest Delta\n3. Delta Types — Bird's Foot\n4. Grand Canyon\n5. Chisapani Gorge — Nepal\n6. Landform-Agent Matching\n7. Nobi aur Kanto Plains — Japan\nDelta Formation — Favourable/Unfavourable Conditions\n● Delta formation ke liye favourable: bada sediment load, low river velocity + gentle gradient, shallow sea/broad\ncontinental shelf — Deep sea unfavourable hai (sediment deeper water mein disperse ho jaata hai, stable delta\nbanana mushkil). [Q1]\nWorld ka Largest Delta\n● Ganga Delta (Ganga-Brahmaputra-Meghna/Sundarban Delta) = world ka largest delta (~1,05,641 sq km) —\nBangladesh + West Bengal (India) mein hai, arcuate (arc-shaped) delta hai. [Q2]\nDelta Types — Bird's Foot\n● Mississippi River Gulf of Mexico mein 'Bird's Foot' type delta banati hai — Nile River iske contrast mein\narcuate delta banati hai. [Q3]\nGrand Canyon\n● Grand Canyon = Gorge hai (Colorado River se Arizona, USA mein carved) — length ~446-447km, average\nwidth ~6.4-29km, depth 1.8km+. [Q4]\nChisapani Gorge — Nepal\n● Chisapani Gorge = Nepal mein hai — Karnali River se cut hui hai (Himalayan region se plains ki taraf nikalte\nwaqt) — Karnali Nepal ki longest river-system hai. [Q5]\nLandform-Agent Matching"," Landforms by River\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Correct: Canyon-River (erosion), Zeugen-Wind (arid regions erosion), Moraine-Glacier (deposition) —\nInselberg-Glacier GALAT hai (Inselberg isolated residual hill hai, arid/semi-arid long-term denudation se\nbanta hai, glacial landform NAHI hai). [Q6]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Inselberg glacial landform NAHI hai — arid/semi-arid regions ka denudation feature hai. [Q6]\nNobi aur Kanto Plains — Japan\n● Nobi Plain (central Japan, ~1,800 sq km) aur Kanto Plain (Japan ka sabse extensive lowland, ~17,000 sq km,\nTokyo yahin hai, central Honshu, Pacific-facing) dono Japan mein hain. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0137","t":"29 The Islands","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Islands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Islands — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 29_The_Islands\nTopic Index\n1. Faroe Islands — 'Sheep Islands'\n2. Largest Islands — World Rankings\n3. Greenland — Facts\n4. Borneo — 3 Countries mein Divided\n5. Borneo — Countries aur Formation\n6. Kalimantan — Borneo ka Indonesian Part\n7. Madagascar — Indian Ocean\n8. Indian Ocean Islands — Location Matching\n9. Melanesia — Solomon Islands\n10. Indonesia — 14,000+/17,508 Islands\n11. Atlantic Ocean Islands — Map Matching\n12. Falkland Archipelago\n13. Fiji Island\n14. Galapagos Islands\n15. Japan — 4 Main Islands\n16. Macau — China Transfer\n17. Balearic Islands — Spain\n18. World's Largest River Island — Majuli\n19. Island Continent — Australia\n20. Grenada — Caribbean Sea\n21. Saint-Martin Island — Salt-Pan Resources\n22. Highest Number of Islands — Countries\n23. Socotra Island\n24. Indonesia — Islands West to East\n25. Caribbean Sea Islands\n26. Polynesia — Islands\nFaroe Islands — 'Sheep Islands'\n● Faroe Islands = 'Sheep Island' kehlate hain — Denmark ka self-governing archipelago (18 rocky/volcanic\nislands). [Q1]\nLargest Islands — World Rankings\n● Greenland (2,166,086 sq km) = world ka largest island — New Guinea (785,753) 2nd, Borneo (751,929) 3rd,\nMadagascar (587,041) 4th. [Q3,Q4,Q5]\n● Given options mein largest: New Zealand South Island (150,436 sq km) — Java (138,794), NZ North Island\n(114,687), Newfoundland (111,390) se badi. [Q2]"," The Islands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Given options mein largest: Borneo (751,929 sq km) — Madagascar (587,041), Sumatra (472,784), Great Britain\n(209,331) se badi. [Q9]\nGreenland — Facts\n● Greenland = world ka largest island, Denmark ka part hai — capital Nuuk (Greenland ka largest city), Nuuk ki\nsea-level se elevation 1-3 metres. [Q6,Q7]\nBorneo — 3 Countries mein Divided\n● Borneo = world ka 3rd largest island, Asia ka largest island — 3 countries mein divided hai: Indonesia (73%),\nMalaysia (26%), Brunei (1%). [Q8]\nBorneo — Countries aur Formation\n● Borneo 3 countries mein divided hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — volcanic deposition se NAHI bana (complex\ntectonic history: continental+oceanic fragments, sedimentary basins, ancient volcanic arcs — Statement 2\nFALSE). [Q10]\nKalimantan — Borneo ka Indonesian Part\n● Kalimantan = Borneo island ka Indonesian portion hai (island ka 73% area). [Q11]\nMadagascar — Indian Ocean\n● Madagascar = Indian Ocean ka largest island hai (SW Indian Ocean mein) — east mein Mauritius, west mein\nMozambique. [Q12]\nIndian Ocean Islands — Location Matching\n● Seychelles (4-11°S, 45-56°E, 155 islands granite+coral), Chagos (Central Indian Ocean, 4.5-7.5°S/71-73°E,\nDiego Garcia largest island 44km²), Mauritius (~20°S/57°E), Socotra (Yemen ka part, ~12°30'N/54°E). [Q13]\n● Southern Indian Ocean mein located: Mauritius (~20°S) — Chagos, Maldives, Seychelles alag positions pe hain.\n[Q14]\n● Diego Garcia = Indian Ocean mein hai — Portuguese Diego Garcia ne 16th century mein discover kiya, 1814-\n1965 Colonial Mauritius administer karta tha, phir UK control mein aaya, USA ko lease diya. [Q16]\nMelanesia — Solomon Islands\n● Solomon Islands = Melanesia group ka part hain (Pacific Ocean) — Melanesia mein Fiji, New Caledonia, New\nGuinea, Bismarck Archipelago bhi shamil hain. [Q15]"," The Islands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nIndonesia — 14,000+/17,508 Islands\n● Indonesia = Aceh (far NW) se Torres Strait (east) tak ~5,000 miles phaila hai (London-Baghdad distance ke\nbarabar) — 17,508 islands (~1,000 inhabited). [Q17]\nAtlantic Ocean Islands — Map Matching\n● Map identification: 1=Azores(Portugal), 2=Cape Verde, 3=Bahamas, 4=Falkland(UK). [Q18]\nFalkland Archipelago\n● Falkland Archipelago South Atlantic Ocean mein hai — Indian Ocean mein NAHI (yeh galat statement hai) —\nmain island South America continent se ~650km east mein hai. [Q19]\nFiji Island\n● Fiji = South Pacific Ocean mein hai — neighbours: Vanuatu(W), Tonga(E), Tuvalu(N) — 333 islands ka\narchipelago, Viti Levu aur Vanua Levu (2 major islands) mein 87% population. [Q20]\nGalapagos Islands\n● Galapagos Islands (Pacific Ocean) volcanic activity se bane (Statement 1 TRUE) — Ecuador ka part hain, Peru\nka NAHI (Statement 2 FALSE). [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Galapagos Islands Ecuador ka part hain, Peru ka NAHI — common wrong pairing. [Q21]\nJapan — 4 Main Islands\n● Japan ke 4 main islands: Hokkaido, Honshu, Shikoku, Kyushu — Honshu sabse bada hai (~228,000 sq km,\nTokyo yahin hai). [Q22,Q23]\n● North-to-South order: Hokkaido → Honshu → Shikoku → Kyushu — Hokkaido 2nd largest, Tsugaru Strait\n(Seikan Tunnel se connected) Hokkaido-Honshu separate karta hai; Shikoku sabse chhota; Kyushu 3rd largest\n(Mt. Aso active volcano yahin hai). [Q24,Q25]\nMacau — China Transfer\n● Macau (Hong Kong se ~64km west, mainland China se connected peninsula) — Portuguese Republic se China\nko sovereignty transfer December 1999 mein hua. [Q26]\nBalearic Islands — Spain"," The Islands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Balearic Islands = Western Mediterranean Sea mein hain — Spain ka autonomous division, 4 major islands,\ncapital Palma de Mallorca, languages Catalan+Spanish. Spain ka part 1833 se, autonomous status 1983 se.\n[Q27]\nWorld's Largest River Island — Majuli\n● Majuli (Assam, India) = world ka largest river island, Brahmaputra River pe hai — south mein Brahmaputra,\nnorth mein Kherkutia Xuti (Brahmaputra ki branch, Subansiri River is mein milti hai). [Q28]\nIsland Continent — Australia\n● Australia = island continent hai — world ka smallest continent bhi hai. [Q29]\nGrenada — Caribbean Sea\n● Grenada = Caribbean Sea (south-eastern) mein hai, 3 islands ka island country — 'Island of Spice' bhi kehlata\nhai (high spice production), Venezuela se ~160km north. [Q30]\nSaint-Martin Island — Salt-Pan Resources\n● Saint-Martin Island apne Salt-Pan resources ke liye jaana jaata hai — interior mostly hilly, coastal lagoons/salt\npans/sand spits ki taraf slope karta hai. [Q31]\nHighest Number of Islands — Countries\n● Given options mein sabse zyada islands Indonesia mein hain (17,508) — world mein overall sabse zyada islands\nSweden mein hain. [Q32]\nSocotra Island\n● Socotra Yemen ka officially part hai (Oman ka NAHI — Statement 1 FALSE, Guardafui Channel+Arabian Sea\nke beech, Gulf of Aden mouth pe, Somalia se ~240km east, Arabian Peninsula se ~380km south); 2008 mein\nUNESCO World Natural Heritage Site declare hua (Statement 2 TRUE) — Socotra Archipelago ka ~95%\nlandmass yahi island cover karta hai. [Q33]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Socotra Yemen ka hai, Oman ka NAHI — common wrong pairing. [Q33]\nIndonesia — Islands West to East\n● West-to-East order: Sumatra → Java → Bali → Lombok — capital Jakarta Java ke NW coast ke paas hai.\nIndonesia ke islands groups: Greater Sunda, Lesser Sunda (Nusa Tenggara), Moluccas (Maluku), Papua (New\nGuinea ka western part). [Q34]"," The Islands\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\nCaribbean Sea Islands\n● Caribbean Sea mein: Anguilla, Antigua, British Virgin Islands, Grenada, Montserrat, Saint Martin — Madeira\nCaribbean mein NAHI hai (North Atlantic Ocean mein, Portugal ka volcanic archipelago — Madeira+Porto\nSanto inhabited, Desertas+Selvagens uninhabited). [Q35]\nPolynesia — Islands\n● Polynesia mein shamil: Tonga, Tuvalu, Tahiti (French Polynesia ka part) — Tinian Polynesia ka part NAHI\nhai. [Q36]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0138","t":"30 The Lakes and Water Falls","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Lakes and Water Falls\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Lakes and Water Falls — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 30_The_Lakes_and_Water_Falls\nTopic Index\n1. Lake Faguibine — West Africa\n2. Lake-Country Matching\n3. Niagara Falls — Location\n4. Lake Tanganyika\n5. Equator — Water Bodies\n6. Great Lakes — Composition\n7. Lake Fully Within USA\n8. Lakes — Area Descending Order\n9. Lakes — Size Descending Order\n10. Largest Freshwater Lake\n11. Baikal — Oldest aur Deepest\n12. Caspian Sea — Largest by Area+Volume\n13. Finger Lakes Region\n14. Finland — Lake Nicknames\n15. Unique Lakes — Location Matching\n16. Lake Superior — Cities\n17. Lake-Country Mismatches\n18. World's Highest Waterfall — Angel Falls\n19. Victoria Falls — Zambezi River\n20. Lake Victoria — Facts aur Common Misconceptions\n21. Plitvice Lakes — World Heritage Site\n22. Aral Sea — Shrinkage\nLake Faguibine — West Africa\n● Lake Faguibine (Mali, West Africa) sookh kar desert mein badal gayi hai. [Q1]\nLake-Country Matching\n● Correct: Balkhash-Kazakhstan, Titicaca-Bolivia/Peru, Erie-USA/Canada — Baikal-Ukraine GALAT hai\n(Baikal actually Russia mein hai). [Q2]\n● Balkhash Lake = Kazakhstan (east-central) mein hai — Central Asia ki largest lake, world ki 15th largest. [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Lake Baikal Russia mein hai, Ukraine mein NAHI — common wrong pairing. [Q2]"," The Lakes and Water Falls\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nNiagara Falls — Location\n● Niagara Falls = Lake Ontario aur Lake Erie ke beech hai (North America, Niagara River, US-Canada border)\n— Niagara River in dono lakes ko connect karti hai. [Q4]\nLake Tanganyika\n● Lake Tanganyika = world ki 2nd deepest lake (1,470m, Baikal ke baad) AUR longest freshwater lake hai.\n[Q5]\nEquator — Water Bodies\n● Lake Tanganyika, Lake Tonle Sap, Patos Lagoon — in teeno mein se koi bhi Equator pe NAHI hai (sabki\nlatitude 0° se door hai). [Q6]\nGreat Lakes — Composition\n● Great Lakes (North America): Superior, Michigan, Huron, Erie, Ontario — Bear Lake iska part NAHI hai.\n[Q7]\n● Great Lakes East-to-West order: Ontario → Erie → Huron → Michigan → Superior. [Q8]\nLake Fully Within USA\n● Lake Michigan = poori tarah USA ke andar hai (Great Lakes mein sirf yehi ek pura US mein hai) — Superior,\nHuron, Erie, Ontario sab US-Canada border pe hain. [Q9,Q10]\nLakes — Area Descending Order\n● Descending order: Superior (82,097 sq km) > Victoria (68,870) > Baikal (31,500) > Great Bear (31,153).\n[Q11]\nLakes — Size Descending Order\n● Descending order: Superior (~82,367 sq km) > Victoria (~58,016) > Michigan (~57,750) > Chilika (~900-\n1,165, Odisha ki brackish lagoon). [Q12]\nLargest Freshwater Lake\n● Lake Superior = world ki largest freshwater lake — Great Lakes ka part, Canada-USA border pe. [Q13]\nBaikal — Oldest aur Deepest"," The Lakes and Water Falls\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Lake Baikal (Siberia, Russia) = world ki oldest AND deepest lake (max depth ~1,642m, 25 million+ years\nold). [Q14,Q15,Q16]\n● Depth comparison: Baikal (1,642m) > Dead Sea (avg 120m) > Titicaca (280m) > Victoria (max 84m, avg 40m).\n[Q16]\nCaspian Sea — Largest by Area+Volume\n● Area aur volume dono ke basis pe world ki largest lake Caspian Sea hai (~371,000 sq km, saltwater) — Aral\nSea, Baikal, Michigan se badi. [Q17]\nFinger Lakes Region\n● Finger Lakes Region = USA (New York state, NW) mein hai — small lakes ki series. [Q18]\nFinland — Lake Nicknames\n● Finland = 'Garden of Lakes' (~187,888 lakes, ~178,917 islands) AUR 'Land of One Thousand Lakes' — Saimaa\n(Finland ki largest lake) Europe ki 4th largest lake hai. [Q19,Q20]\nUnique Lakes — Location Matching\n● Correct: Boiling Lake-Dominica, Red Lagoon-Bolivia, Great Slave Lake-Canada — Five Flower Lake-\nMongolia GALAT hai (actually Sichuan, China mein hai). [Q21]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Five Flower Lake actually Sichuan, China mein hai, Mongolia mein NAHI. [Q21]\nLake Superior — Cities\n● Duluth = Lake Superior ke tat pe\n\nस्थि\nतNorth America ka 2nd largest city — Chicago, Buffalo, Detroit alag Great\nLakes pe hain. [Q22]\nLake-Country Mismatches\n● Correct: Titicaca-Bolivia/Peru, Urmia-Iran, Athabasca-Canada — Reindeer Lake-Russia GALAT hai (actually\nCanada mein hai). [Q23]\n● Correct: Baikal-Russia, Caspian Sea-Asia/Europe, Tanganyika-Africa — Malawi-Asia GALAT hai (Lake\nMalawi actually Africa mein hai). [Q31]\n● Correct: Maracaibo-Venezuela, Michigan-USA, Baikal-Russia — Onega-Canada GALAT hai (Lake Onega\nactually NW Russia mein hai, Baltic Sea basin, Europe ki 2nd largest lake Ladoga ke baad). [Q33]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Reindeer Lake Canada mein hai; Lake Malawi Africa mein hai; Lake Onega Russia mein hai — teeno"," The Lakes and Water Falls\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\ncommon wrong-country pairings hain. [Q23,Q31,Q33]\nWorld's Highest Waterfall — Angel Falls\n● Angel Falls (Salto Ángel) = world ka highest waterfall (~979m) — Venezuela mein hai (Rio Churun pe, Rio\nCarrao ki tributary, Rio Carrao Rio Orinoco ki tributary). Tugela Falls (South Africa, ~948m) bhi bahut high hai\nlekin conventional exam answer Angel Falls hi hai. [Q24,Q25,Q30]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• World's highest waterfall Angel Falls (Venezuela) hai — Tugela Falls (South Africa) second hai, exam mein\ngalti se pehla answer diya jaata hai. [Q30]\nVictoria Falls — Zambezi River\n● Victoria Falls = Zambezi River se associated hai — Zambia-Zimbabwe border pe (South-Central Africa).\n[Q26]\nLake Victoria — Facts aur Common Misconceptions\n● Lake Victoria 3 countries se surrounded hai (Tanzania, Uganda, Kenya) — 4 NAHI (Statement 1 galat); East\nAfrican Rift ki branches ke beech hai, directly rift valley mein NAHI (Statement 2 bhi galat) — is question\nmein dono statements incorrect hain. [Q27]\n● Lake Victoria world ki 2nd largest freshwater lake hai (surface area se) — 3rd NAHI (Statement 1 galat); 3\ncountries se bordered hai — 4 NAHI, Rwanda shamil nahi hota (Statement 3 galat); Africa ki Great Lakes mein\nshamil hai (Statement 2 sahi); Nile hi Lake Victoria se nikalne wali single outflow river hai, Jinja-Uganda ke\npaas (Statement 4 sahi). [Q28]\nPlitvice Lakes — World Heritage Site\n● Plitvice Lakes (Croatia) = UNESCO World Heritage Site (1979 se) — 16 lakes jo waterfalls ki series se\nconnected hain, deep woodland mein rare bird species. [Q29]\nAral Sea — Shrinkage\n● Human activities ki wajah se sirf Aral Sea immensely shrink/dry hua hai — Black Sea aur Lake Baikal mein bhi\nkuch contraction hai lekin Aral Sea ke comparison mein bahut kam hai (NASA satellite image 2014, 1989 se\ncomparison). [Q32]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0139","t":"31 The Straits","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Straits\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Straits — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 31_The_Straits\nTopic Index\n1. Malacca Strait\n2. Gibraltar Strait — Europe-Africa\n3. Strait of Hormuz\n4. Bering Strait — Asia-North America\n5. Suez Canal — Economic/Strategic Significance\n6. Straits — Location Matching (Multi-set)\n7. Ten Degree Channel\n8. Strait of Dover — Channel Tunnel\n9. Palk Strait\n10. Persian Gulf — Bordering Countries\n11. Gulfs — Country Matching\n12. Bab-el-Mandeb Strait\n13. Lombok Strait — Indonesia\n14. Kra Isthmus — 'Devil's Neck'\n15. Bass Strait — Tasmania\nMalacca Strait\n● Malacca Strait (Indonesia-Malaysia ke beech) = Indian Ocean (Andaman Sea) ko South China Sea se\nconnect karti hai. [Q1]\n● India-East Asia navigation time/distance kam karne ke liye: Gulf of Siam-Andaman Sea ke beech new canal\nhelpful hai (Statement 2 TRUE) — Malacca Strait deepen karna directly navigation kam nahi karta (Statement 1\ngalat, is context mein). [Q2]\nGibraltar Strait — Europe-Africa\n● Strait of Gibraltar = Europe ko Africa se separate karti hai — Atlantic Ocean ko Mediterranean Sea se\nconnect karti hai. [Q3]\nStrait of Hormuz\n● Strait of Hormuz = Persian Gulf aur Gulf of Oman ke beech hai/inhe connect karti hai — West Asia ke oil-\nrich region ko world se connect karne wala extremely important sea route hai. [Q4,Q5]\nBering Strait — Asia-North America"," The Straits\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Bering Strait = Asia ko North America se separate karti hai (Russia easternmost ~169°43'E, Alaska\nwesternmost ~168°05'W) — ~85km wide, Chukchi Sea (Arctic Ocean) ko Bering Sea (Pacific Ocean) se\nconnect karti hai (north-south). [Q6,Q8]\nSuez Canal — Economic/Strategic Significance\n● Given options mein Suez Canal ka economic/strategic significance sabse zyada hai — ~12% global trade, ~30%\nglobal container traffic yahan se guzarta hai; Red Sea-Mediterranean ke beech strategic location. [Q7]\nStraits — Location Matching (Multi-set)\n● Gibraltar-Africa/Europe, Malacca-Indonesia/Malaysia, Bering-Asia/N.America, Hormuz-Persian Gulf/Gulf of\nOman. [Q9]\nTen Degree Channel\n● Ten Degree Channel = Andaman aur Nicobar Islands ko separate karta hai (Bay of Bengal mein) — ~10°N\nlatitude pe hone ki wajah se naam mila. [Q10]\nStrait of Dover — Channel Tunnel\n● Dover Strait = English Channel aur North Sea ke beech boundary hai — UK-France ko connect karne wali 3\nmarine tunnels yahin hain (Folkestone-Kent, England se Coquelles-Pas-de-Calais, France). [Q11,Q12]\nPalk Strait\n● Palk Strait = India (Tamil Nadu) aur Sri Lanka ke beech — Bay of Bengal (Palk Bay) ko Gulf of Mannar\nse connect karti hai. Width ~64-137km. Naam Robert Palk (1763-67 Madras Presidency Governor) se pada.\n[Q13,Q14]\nPersian Gulf — Bordering Countries\n● Persian Gulf border karta hai: Iran, UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait, Iraq — Oman Persian Gulf se\nborder NAHI karta (Oman ki border Gulf of Oman aur Arabian Sea se hai). [Q15,Q16]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Oman Persian Gulf coastline country NAHI hai — Gulf of Oman/Arabian Sea se bordered hai, isse confuse\nmat ho. [Q15,Q16]\nGulfs — Country Matching\n● Correct: Gulf of Tonkin-Vietnam — Gulf of Bothnia actually Finland-Sweden ke beech hai (France NAHI);\nBaffin Bay Canada-Greenland ke beech hai (Argentina NAHI); Gulf of Carpentaria Australia mein hai (Canada\nNAHI). [Q17]"," The Straits\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nBab-el-Mandeb Strait\n● Bab-el-Mandeb Strait = Red Sea ko Indian Ocean (Gulf of Aden) se connect karti hai — Hormuz(Persian\nGulf-Gulf of Oman), Malacca(Indian Ocean-South China Sea), Bosphorus(Black Sea-Sea of Marmara) se\ncontrast. [Q18]\nLombok Strait — Indonesia\n● Lombok Strait = Bali aur Lombok islands (Indonesia) ke beech — Java Sea ko Indian Ocean se connect karta\nhai. [Q19]\nKra Isthmus — 'Devil's Neck'\n● Kra Isthmus (Southern Thailand-Myanmar, Malay Peninsula aur SE Asia mainland ke beech) = 'Devil's Neck'\nkehlata hai (bahut narrow hone ki wajah se ship routes mein hindrance karta hai). [Q20]\nBass Strait — Tasmania\n● Bass Strait (~240-350km wide) = mainland Australia (Victoria) ko Tasmania se separate karta hai — Great\nAustralian Bight, Tasman Sea, Magellan Strait alag features hain. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0140","t":"32 The Canals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Canals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Canals — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 32_The_Canals\nTopic Index\n1. Suez Canal — Facts\n2. Panama Canal\n3. Soo Canal\n4. Kiel Canal\n5. Southern Germany — Inland Waterway\n6. Canals — Connection Matching\n7. Suez Canal Region — Lakes (North to South)\nSuez Canal — Facts\n● Suez Canal (Egypt, Isthmus of Suez) Mediterranean Sea aur Red Sea ko connect karti hai — length\n~193.30km, 1869 se operational, sea-level canal (koi locks nahi), world ki largest artificial navigation canal.\n[Q1,Q4,Q5,Q12]\n● Suez Canal ke south mein Suez Port (Tewfik Port), north mein Port Said hai. [Q2]\n● Suez Canal ne India-Europe maritime distance ~7,000km kam kar diya. [Q6]\n● 'Suez Canal se India-Western countries ki distance kam hui' (A TRUE) — 'Suez Canal Mediterranean-Red Sea\nconnect karti hai' (R TRUE, sahi explanation). [Q3]\n● Bombay se Suez jaane ke liye Suez Canal se guzarne ki zaroorat NAHI (Suez port canal ke southern end pe hi\nhai) — Alexandria, Port Said, Benghazi jaane ke liye guzarna padta hai. [Q7]\nPanama Canal\n● Panama Canal = Central America mein, Isthmus of Panama ko cut karke banayi gayi — Atlantic aur Pacific\nOcean ko connect karti hai. San Francisco (west coast) aur New York (east coast) ke beech distance\nsignificantly kam ki. [Q8]\n● Panama Canal ki rival banane ki planning Nicaragua ne ki thi (Oct 2006, President Enrique Bolaños) —\nAtlantic-Pacific link, estimated cost $18 billion, ~12 years timeline. [Q10]\nSoo Canal\n● Soo Canal = North America ki 5 Great Lakes mein se do — Superior aur Huron — ko connect karti hai. [Q9]\nKiel Canal\n● Kiel Canal (Germany) = North Sea aur Baltic Sea ko connect karti hai (Elbe Estuary-Baltic Sea specifically) —\nworld ke busiest artificial waterways mein se ek. [Q11]"," The Canals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nSouthern Germany — Inland Waterway\n● Ludwigs Canal = Southern Germany mein inland waterway ke roop mein use hoti hai — Sault-Sainte Marie\nCanal (Canada), Volga-Don Canal (Russia, Volga-Don rivers connect), White Sea Canal (Russia, White Sea-\nLake Onega) se contrast. [Q13]\nCanals — Connection Matching\n● Kiel-Elbe Estuary+Baltic Sea, Soo-Lake Superior+Lake Huron, Panama-Atlantic+Pacific Ocean, Suez-\nMediterranean+Red Sea. [Q14]\nSuez Canal Region — Lakes (North to South)\n● North-to-South order: Lake Manzala → Lake Timsah → Great Bitter Lake → Little Bitter Lake. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0141","t":"33 The Important Dams of the World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Important Dams of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Important Dams of the World — FULL MIND\n🗺️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 33_The_Important_Dams_of_the_World\nTopic Index\n1. Itaipu Dam — Parana River\n2. World's Longest Sea Bridge (Historical Context)\n3. River-Dam Matching\n4. Zangmu Dam — Brahmaputra\n5. Dam-River Pairing (Correct/Incorrect)\nItaipu Dam — Parana River\n● Itaipu Dam (Parana River) = Brazil aur Paraguay ki joint project hai — world ke largest dams mein se ek\n(height 196m, length 7,919m), Brazil-Paraguay border pe. [Q1]\nWorld's Longest Sea Bridge (Historical Context)\n● Jiaozhou Bay Bridge (China) June 2011 mein khula tha aur us waqt world ka longest sea bridge maana gaya\n(exam-historical context, baad mein other bridges se record change ho sakta hai). [Q2]\nRiver-Dam Matching\n● Colorado-Hoover, Damodar-Panchet, Nile-Aswan, Zambezi-Kariba. [Q3]\n● Kariba Dam = Zambezi River pe hai (Zambia-Zimbabwe border) — world ke largest dams mein se ek. [Q4]\n● Aswan High Dam = Egypt mein hai, Nile River pe — irrigation + hydroelectric power ke liye, construction\n1960 mein start hua. [Q5]\nZangmu Dam — Brahmaputra\n● China ne Nov 2010 mein Brahmaputra (Yarlung Zangbo) River pe Zangmu jagah pe dam construction start kiya\n(Tibet mein, gravity dam) — flow reduce hone ki concern thi. [Q6]\nDam-River Pairing (Correct/Incorrect)\n● Correct: Grand Coulee-Columbia, Nurek-Vakhsh, Cahora Bassa-Zambezi — Hoover-Tennessee GALAT hai\n(Hoover/Boulder Dam actually Colorado River pe hai, Black Canyon mein, Nevada-Arizona border). [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️"," The Important Dams of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n• Hoover Dam Colorado River pe hai (Tennessee River NAHI) — common wrong pairing. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0142","t":"34 The Coral Reefs","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Coral Reefs\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Coral Reefs — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 34_The_Coral_Reefs\nTopic Index\n1. Coral Reefs — General Location\n2. Great Barrier Reef — Location aur Facts\n3. Coral Reefs — Global Statistics\n4. Addu Atoll — Maldives\n5. Atoll — Shape\nCoral Reefs — General Location\n● Coral reefs mainly Tropic of Cancer aur Tropic of Capricorn ke beech coastal areas mein milte hain —\ngenerally 30°N-30°S tak extend hote hain. Oceans ka sirf ~0.08-0.16% area cover karte hain lekin ~25% marine\nspecies yahin milti hain. [Q1]\nGreat Barrier Reef — Location aur Facts\n● Great Barrier Reef = Australia ke near (Pacific Ocean, Queensland coast, NE Australia) hai — world ki largest\ncoral reef, ~2,300km lambi (10°S-24°S ke beech mainly) — 450+ hard coral species, 1,625+ fish species,\n3,000+ mollusc species. [Q2,Q3,Q4,Q5,Q6]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Great Barrier Reef ki length ~2,300km hai, 2,500km se zyada NAHI — exact figure yaad rakho. [Q3]\nCoral Reefs — Global Statistics\n● Coral reefs mainly tropical waters mein hain (Statement 1 TRUE); world ki 1/3 se zyada reefs Australia,\nIndonesia, Philippines mein hain (~19% Australia, ~17% Indonesia — Statement 2 TRUE); coral reefs mein\ntropical rainforests se ~4x zyada animal phyla hote hain (32/33 phyla, 25,000+ species — Statement 3\nTRUE) — teeno statements sahi hain. [Q7]\nAddu Atoll — Maldives\n● Addu Atoll = Indian Ocean mein hai — Maldives ka southernmost atoll. [Q8]\nAtoll — Shape\n● Atoll ki shape horse-shoe/ring-shaped hoti hai — lagoon ke around coral reef, diameter kai kilometres tak ho\nsakta hai, tropical/subtropical oceans mein milta hai. [Q9]"," The Coral Reefs\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0143","t":"35 The Atmosphere","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Atmosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Atmosphere — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 35_The_Atmosphere\nTopic Index\n1. Dust Particles — Subtropical/Temperate Areas\n2. Troposphere Thickness — Equator vs Poles\n3. Atmosphere Composition — Main Gases\n4. Atmosphere Layers — Vertical Order\n5. Weather Activity aur Climate Changes — Troposphere\n6. Stratosphere — Jet Aircraft ke liye Ideal\n7. Ozone Layer — Location aur Function\n8. Ozone Layer Height\n9. Ionosphere — Radio Waves aur Aurora\n10. Communication Satellites — Exosphere\n11. Atmosphere Layer-Characteristic Matching\nDust Particles — Subtropical/Temperate Areas\n● Subtropical+temperate areas mein equatorial/polar se zyada dust particles hote hain (Statement I TRUE) —\nreason dry winds zyada hoti hain (kam nahi, Statement II likha 'less dry winds' galat hai, actually MORE dry\nwinds hi is reason ki wajah hai). [Q1]\nTroposphere Thickness — Equator vs Poles\n● Equator pe troposphere ki thickness poles se bahut zyada hoti hai (Statement I TRUE) — strong convectional\ncurrents heat ko great heights tak transport karte hain equator pe (Statement II TRUE, sahi explanation).\nTroposphere: dust+water vapour, saare weather changes yahin, ~1°C/165m temperature decrease, average\nheight ~13km (poles ~8km, equator ~18km). [Q2]\nAtmosphere Composition — Main Gases\n● Earth surface ke near atmosphere mein mainly Nitrogen (78.084%) aur Oxygen (20.947%) hote hain (~99%)\n— remaining ~1% mein Argon, CO2, Neon, Helium, Methane, Hydrogen, N2O, Ozone, Krypton, Xenon.\nHeavy gases lower atmosphere mein, light gases higher up. CO2 ~20km tak, O2+N2 ~100km tak, H2 ~125km\ntak. [Q3]\n● Atmosphere mein maximum percentage Nitrogen ki hai. [Q4]\n● Permanent gases (dry air mein proportion stable): Nitrogen (~78%) AUR Neon (~18 ppm) — dono\nscientifically correct hain. [Q5]\nAtmosphere Layers — Vertical Order"," The Atmosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Layers ka upward order (given options mein): Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Ionosphere —\nIonosphere separate temperature-layer nahi hai, upper mesosphere+thermosphere se overlap karta hai. [Q6],\n[Q9]\n● Troposphere = vertical structure ki lowest layer hai (average elevation ~12km) — rain, fog, hail jaise seasonal\nphenomena yahin hote hain. [Q7,Q8]\n● Increasing distance order: Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermosphere. [Q10]\nWeather Activity aur Climate Changes — Troposphere\n● Most weather activity (rainfall, fog, hailstorms) Troposphere mein hoti hai — temperature ~6.5°C/1000m ki dar\nse decrease hota hai, biological activity ke liye sabse important layer hai. [Q11]\n● Climate aur weather ke SAARE changes Troposphere mein hote hain. [Q12]\nStratosphere — Jet Aircraft ke liye Ideal\n● Stratosphere jet aircraft flying ke liye ideal hai kyunki clouds aur weather phenomena absent hote hain —\nstratosphere bahut dry hai, water vapour bahut kam — isliye disturbances avoid karne ke liye ideal hai. [Q13]\nOzone Layer — Location aur Function\n● Ozone layer mainly Stratosphere ke lower portion mein hai (15-35km, max height 55km tak) — UV radiation\nabsorb karti hai, life ko harmful energy se protect karti hai (UV rays skin cancer cause kar sakti hain).\n[Q14,Q15]\n● Ozone layer Earth pe life ko Sun ki harmful UV radiations se protect karti hai — Ozone = 3 oxygen atoms ka\nmolecule, colour blue hai. [Q16]\n● Stratosphere mein ozone layer ka function: UV radiation ko ground pe effect dalne se prevent karna — global\ntemperature stabilize karna, earthquake frequency kam karna, monsoon failure rokna — yeh sab NAHI hai.\n[Q17]\n● Ozone layer = atmosphere ki ~15-20km above Earth surface wali parat hai. [Q18]\nOzone Layer Height\n● Ozone layer ki height Earth surface se 15-20km (exam-accepted, extended max 55km, concentration mainly 15-\n35km). [Q19]\nIonosphere — Radio Waves aur Aurora\n● Ionosphere radio waves deflection/reflection ke liye responsible hai — cosmic rays identification, Aurora\nBorealis/Australis bhi yahin observe hote hain. [Q20]\n● Aurora Borealis Ionosphere (thermosphere ke saath overlap) mein hote hain — Sun se energetic charged\nparticles upper atmosphere ke atoms/molecules se collide karte hain. [Q21]\n● Wireless communication waves Ionosphere se Earth surface ki taraf reflect hoti hain — ionosphere electrically\ncharged particles (ions) se bana hai. [Q22]\n● Telecommunication ke liye Ionosphere use hoti hai. [Q23]"," The Atmosphere\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nCommunication Satellites — Exosphere\n● Communication satellites Exosphere mein located hote hain — geostationary satellites ~36,000km pe hote hain,\nexosphere Earth se ~640km se aage outer limit hai. [Q24]\nAtmosphere Layer-Characteristic Matching\n● Correct: Troposphere-Weather Phenomena, Stratosphere-Ozone layer, Ionosphere-Radio waves reflection —\nMesosphere-Aurorae GALAT hai (Aurora actually Ionosphere se related hai, Mesosphere se nahi). [Q25]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Aurora Ionosphere se related hai, Mesosphere se NAHI. [Q25]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0144","t":"36 The Insolation","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Insolation\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Insolation — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 36_The_Insolation\nTopic Index\n1. Atmosphere — Sun se Indirect Heat\n2. Height ke Saath Temperature Decrease\n3. Albedo — Reflecting Power\n4. Tropical Cyclones — Sea se Distance\n5. Ocean Size aur Annual Temperature Range\n6. Isotherms — January Deviation\n7. Highest Temperature — 20°N Latitude\n8. Clear-Sky Nights — Cooler\n9. Infrared Waves — Water Vapour Absorption\n10. Urban Heat Island\nAtmosphere — Sun se Indirect Heat\n● Atmosphere Sun se mostly indirect heat leta hai, Earth surface se direct (A TRUE) — short-wave solar energy\nka long-wave terrestrial energy mein conversion Earth surface pe hota hai (R TRUE, sahi explanation) —\nCO2/greenhouse gases long-wave radiation absorb karte hain, isse global warming hoti hai. [Q1]\nHeight ke Saath Temperature Decrease\n● Height badhne se temperature ghatne ka reason: (1) atmosphere mainly Earth surface se upward heat hoti hai,\n(3) upper atmosphere mein air density kam hoti hai — (2) upper atmosphere mein zyada moisture galat\nhai (actually kam hoti hai). [Q2]\nAlbedo — Reflecting Power\n● Fresh snow-covered land sabse zyada sunlight reflect karti hai (albedo ~75-95%) — sand desert (20-30%),\npaddy cropland (3-15%), prairie land (10-20%) se zyada. Earth ka average albedo ~30%. [Q3]\n● Albedo = Reflecting power se associated hai — surface se reflect hone wale light ka fraction. Frozen ice ka\nalbedo high, green areas (forests/plains) ka relatively low. [Q5]\nTropical Cyclones — Sea se Distance\n● Sea se door jaane par tropical cyclones ki force ghatti hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — cyclones energy latent heat\n(moisture condensation) se leti hain jo ocean pe collect hoti hai; sea se door moisture supply/energy ghatti hai\n(Statement 2 TRUE, sahi explanation). [Q4]"," The Insolation\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nOcean Size aur Annual Temperature Range\n● Ocean ka size jitna bada, annual temperature variation utna kam hota hai — Atlantic Ocean mein Pacific se\nzyada annual range hoti hai (Pacific bada hai) — Statement 1 (Pacific mein zyada) galat; Northern\nHemisphere mein Southern se zyada annual range hoti hai (zyada land, Statement 2 TRUE). [Q6]\nIsotherms — January Deviation\n● January mein isotherms ocean pe north ki taraf, continent pe south ki taraf deviate karte hain (Statement 1\nTRUE, especially Northern Hemisphere mein pronounced kyunki zyada land hai) — North Atlantic mein Gulf\nStream aur North Atlantic Drift WARM currents hain (cold NAHI), isliye N.Atlantic ko warmer banate\nhain, isotherms north ki taraf bend karte hain (Statement 2 galat, 'cold currents' likha tha). [Q7]\n● Statement I: January mein N.Hemisphere mein isotherms land ke upar equatorward, ocean ke upar poleward\nmudte hain — TRUE; Statement II: same latitude pe January mein ocean ki air land se warmer hoti hai —\nTRUE (land-sea thermal contrast hi isotherm bending ka physical reason hai, isliye II sahi explains I). [Q8]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Gulf Stream aur North Atlantic Drift WARM currents hain, cold NAHI — is fact ko galat likha jaana\ncommon trap hai. [Q7]\nHighest Temperature — 20°N Latitude\n● Maximum temperature zone Equator pe NAHI hota — actually ~20°N latitude ke around record hota hai\n(thermal equator geographic equator se thoda north mein shift hota hai). [Q9,Q10]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Highest temperature Equator pe NAHI, ~20°N pe record hoti hai — thermal equator geographic equator se\nnorth mein hoti hai. [Q9,Q10]\nClear-Sky Nights — Cooler\n● Clear-sky nights cloudy nights se zyada thandi hoti hain kyunki radiation (terrestrial radiation clear sky mein\nfreely space mein escape ho jaati hai — cloudy night mein clouds heat ko trap karke wapas radiate karte hain,\nisliye cloudy nights warmer feel hoti hain). [Q11]\nInfrared Waves — Water Vapour Absorption\n● Infrared waves mainly lower atmosphere mein concentrated water vapour se absorb hoti hain (troposphere\nmein water vapour, ozone, other gases) — short-wave solar energy relatively easily atmosphere se guzar jaati\nhai. [Q12]\nUrban Heat Island\n● Urban Heat Island = city ka average surface/atmospheric temperature nearby rural areas se significantly\nzyada hona — concrete/asphalt surfaces, low vegetation, reduced evapotranspiration, vehicles/industries se\nextra heat is\nकेmain reasons hain. [Q13]"," The Insolation\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0145","t":"37 The Cyclones","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Cyclones\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Cyclones — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 37_The_Cyclones\nTopic Index\n1. Jet Streams aur Cyclone Eye\n2. Cyclone Center — Surface Winds\n3. Warm Front vs Cold Front — Rainfall\n4. Tornadoes\n5. Typhoon — China Sea\n6. Tropical Cyclones — Regional Names\n7. Regional Cyclone Names — Multi-set Matching\n8. Hurricane — Saffir-Simpson Scale\n9. Barometer — Mercury Fall\n10. Cyclones — India ko Affect Karne Wale\n11. South Atlantic/SE Pacific — Cyclones Absent\n12. Global Warming — Cyclones/Storms/Hurricanes\n13. 2019 Typhoons/Hurricanes — Affected Regions\nJet Streams aur Cyclone Eye\n● Jet streams dono hemispheres mein hoti hain (Statement 1 galat, sirf N.Hemisphere mein NAHI) — sirf kuch\ncyclones mein eye develop hoti hai (Statement 2 TRUE); eye ke andar temperature surrounding se higher hota\nhai, lower NAHI (Statement 3 galat, kaha gaya tha 10°C kam hai). [Q1]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Cyclone ki eye ke andar temperature surrounding se higher hota hai (~10°C warm ~12km altitude pe, surface\npe ~0-2°C), lower NAHI — common wrong statement. [Q1]\nCyclone Center — Surface Winds\n● Surface winds cyclone center ki taraf spiral inward hoti hain (A TRUE) — R bhi TRUE hai lekin sahi\nexplanation NAHI (eye mein air descend karti hai, lekin yeh surface ki inward spiral ka cause nahi hai — asal\ncause pressure-gradient force, Coriolis force, aur friction hain). [Q2]\nWarm Front vs Cold Front — Rainfall\n● Cyclone diagram mein Cold Front (D) area mein heavy torrential short-duration rainfall + thunderstorms hote\nhain — warm air ko cold front peeche se force karta hai upward, cumulus clouds develop hoti hain, rapid\ndroplet-fall + rising air se lightning/thunder banta hai. Warm front (A) mein gradual precipitation hota hai. [Q3]"," The Cyclones\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nTornadoes\n● Cited exam ka conventional answer: Tornadoes Caribbean Sea mein originate hote hain (purani textbook usage).\n[Q4]\n● USA ko generally Tornadoes se associate kiya jaata hai — dark funnel-shaped cloud, sky se ground tak —\nCaribbean aur American region especially prone hain. [Q5]\n● Mississippi Plains = USA ka 'Tornado Alley' kehlata hai (central+southern Great Plains ka core high-frequency\nzone) — boundaries officially fixed nahi hain. [Q6]\n● Tornado intensity measure karne ke liye Fujita Scale (F-Scale) use hota hai — Ted Fujita ke naam pe. [Q7]\nTyphoon — China Sea\n● Typhoon = China Sea (mid-northern hemisphere, ~100°E-180°E) mein develop hone wala mature tropical\ncyclone hai. [Q8]\nTropical Cyclones — Regional Names\n● Regional names: Australia-Willy-Willy, China-Typhoon, India-Cyclone, USA-Hurricane. [Q9]\n● Willy-Willy = North-West Australia ka tropical cyclone. [Q10]\nRegional Cyclone Names — Multi-set Matching\n● Willy-Willy-Australia, Hurricane-USA, Typhoon-China, Baguio-Philippines. [Q11,Q12]\n● Willy-Willies-Australia, Taifu-Japan, Baguio-Philippines, Hurricane-USA. [Q13]\nHurricane — Saffir-Simpson Scale\n● Saffir-Simpson Scale = hurricane damage/wind-speed measure karta hai — 1-5 scale pe classify karta hai\npotential property damage aur coastal flooding estimate karne ke liye. [Q14]\nBarometer — Mercury Fall\n● Barometer mein mercury ka sudden fall stormy weather (westerly winds ke baad violent storm) ka indicator hai.\n[Q15]\nCyclones — India ko Affect Karne Wale\n● Aila, Thane, Neelam ne India ko affect kiya — Nargis India ko NAHI affect kiya (mainly Myanmar ko affect\nkiya). [Q16]\nSouth Atlantic/SE Pacific — Cyclones Absent"," The Cyclones\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● South Atlantic aur South-Eastern Pacific tropical latitudes mein cyclones nahi bante kyunki sea surface\ntemperature low hota hai — most proximate reason. [Q17]\nGlobal Warming — Cyclones/Storms/Hurricanes\n● Global warming se cyclones, storms, AUR hurricanes — teeno ki frequency+severity badhti hai (exam-\nintended answer). [Q18]\n2019 Typhoons/Hurricanes — Affected Regions\n● Dorian-Bahamas, Hagibis-Japan, Lekima-China, Mitag-Jeju(South Korea) — Aug-Sep 2019 ke storms. [Q19]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0146","t":"38 The Humidity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Humidity\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Humidity — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 38_The_Humidity\nTopic Index\n1. Humidity aur Latitude/Temperature\n2. Humid Heat — 'Muggy' Weather\n3. Humidity — Definition\n4. Cloudy Night — No Dewdrops\nHumidity aur Latitude/Temperature\n● Atmosphere mein moisture ki amount latitude se related hai (A TRUE) — moisture ko water-vapour form mein\nrakhne ki ability temperature se related hai (R TRUE, sahi explanation): Tropical ~2.6%, 50° lat ~0.9%, 70°\nlat ~0.2%. ~90% atmospheric moisture ground se 5km ke andar milti hai. [Q1]\nHumid Heat — 'Muggy' Weather\n● Summer mein high humidity ke time weather 'Muggy' feel hota hai — Absolute humidity = per unit volume air\nmein water vapour ka weight (grains/cubic foot mein). [Q2]\nHumidity — Definition\n● Humidity = air mein moisture ki presence ka result hai — atmosphere mein present water vapour hi humidity\nkehlati hai. [Q3]\nCloudy Night — No Dewdrops\n● Cloudy night pe dew NAHI banti kyunki clouds Earth ki radiation ko wapas reflect kar dete hain —\ngreenhouse-jaisi condition banti hai, surface relatively warm rehta hai, isliye required cooling nahi hoti aur\ndew-formation ke liye conditions unfavourable ho jaati hain. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0147","t":"39 The Atmospheric Pressure","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Atmospheric Pressure\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Atmospheric Pressure — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 39_The_Atmospheric_Pressure\nTopic Index\n1. Sub-Polar Low-Pressure Belt (60-65°)\n2. Horse Latitudes\n3. Air Pressure — Seasonal Variation\nSub-Polar Low-Pressure Belt (60-65°)\n● Dono hemispheres mein 60°-65° latitudes pe low-pressure belt hoti hai high-pressure ki jagah (A TRUE) — R\nbhi TRUE hai lekin sahi explanation NAHI (asal reason: Northern Hemisphere mein 60°N ke around bade\nlandmass ki wajah se belt ki continuity disrupt hoti hai; Southern Hemisphere mein vast ocean + kam landmass\nki wajah se belt zyada pronounced/stable hoti hai — 'low-pressure areas stable over oceans' statement khud sahi\nhai lekin A ko explain nahi karta). [Q1]\nHorse Latitudes\n● Horse Latitudes = ~30°-35° N aur S dono latitudes (Equator se) — high-pressure belts hain (subtropical high),\nlow-pressure NAHI. Equatorial air rise hoke poles ki taraf deflect hoti hai (Earth's rotation se), cold+heavy hoke\nyahan descend karti hai — calm/weak/variable winds. Naam 'Horse Latitudes' ka origin: purane time mein\nhorse-carrying ships in calm zones mein struggle karte the, ships lighten karne ke liye kabhi kabhi horses\nsamundar mein fenke jaate the. [Q2,Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Horse Latitudes high-pressure belts hain, low-pressure NAHI — yeh common confusion hai. [Q3]\nAir Pressure — Seasonal Variation\n● Air pressure sabse kam Summer season mein hoti hai (temperature aur pressure inversely related hain, summer\nmein temperature highest hoti hai) — altitude badhne se temperature+pressure dono ghatte hain. [Q4]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0148","t":"40 Clouds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Clouds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Clouds — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 40_Clouds\nTopic Index\n1. Clouds — Formation aur Types\n2. Thunder Clouds — Development Factors\n3. Thunder — Sound ka Actual Cause\n4. Cirrus Cloud Thinning — Climate Engineering\n5. Cloudy Night — Dewdrops Formation\nClouds — Formation aur Types\n● Condensation se clouds banti hain — water gaseous se liquid/solid state mein convert hoti hai, atmosphere mein\ntiny water droplets/ice crystals ka collection cloud kehlata hai. [Q1]\n● Cumulonimbus clouds highly intense rain ke liye responsible hain — highly developed+dense,\nrain/hail/thunderstorm ki high possibility, ~1 hour mein dissipate ho jaati hain (short-lived heavy rain). [Q2]\n● Given options mein highest altitude cloud: Cirrostratus (upper troposphere mein) — Altocumulus, Altostratus,\nCumulus isse neeche hoti hain. [Q3]\nThunder Clouds — Development Factors\n● Thunder clouds development factors: Condensation, High temperature+humidity, Vertical wind —\nOrography factor NAHI hai. High temp se strong upward winds, jo water droplets ko upar le jaati hain\n(freeze/condense), phir wapas girti hain — lightning+sound generate hota hai. [Q4]\nThunder — Sound ka Actual Cause\n● Thunder (garjan) actually lightning discharge se hoti hai — lightning air ko heat karti hai, sudden overpressure\nbanti hai, shock wave supersonically expand hoti hai — cumulonimbus clouds ka meeting, nimbus clouds\nseparate hona, ya sirf air/water particles ki upward movement — in teeno options mein se KOI bhi sahi\nexplanation NAHI hai. [Q5]\nCirrus Cloud Thinning — Climate Engineering\n● Cirrus cloud thinning technique aur stratosphere mein sulphate aerosol injection ka suggestion Global Warming\nkam karne ke context mein hai — cirrus clouds ice crystals se bane hote hain, ground se reflected/emitted heat\nko space mein escape hone se rokte hain; thinning se heat-absorption capacity kam hoti hai. Sulphate aerosol\nsolar radiation ka part reflect karta hai troposphere tak pahunchne se pehle. [Q6]\nCloudy Night — Dewdrops Formation"," Clouds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Cloudy night pe dew NAHI banti kyunki clouds Earth ki outgoing infrared radiation ko absorb karke wapas\nreflect/re-emit kar dete hain — surface strongly cool nahi hota, dew-point tak nahi pahunchta. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0149","t":"41 The Winds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Winds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Winds — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 41_The_Winds\nTopic Index\n1. Coriolis Force — Properties\n2. Trade Winds aur Westerlies — Ocean Temperature Effect\n3. Wind Patterns — Clockwise/Anticlockwise Misconception\n4. Roaring Forties — Southern Hemisphere Westerlies\n5. Geostrophic Winds\n6. Roaring Forties/Furious Fifties/Shrieking Sixties\n7. Southern Hemisphere Deflection — Earth's Rotation\n8. Mediterranean Sea — High-Pressure se Winds\n9. Seasonal Wind Reversal — Monsoon Climate\n10. Chinook Winds — USA Central Plains\nCoriolis Force — Properties\n● Coriolis force wind velocity ke saath badhta hai (Statement 1 TRUE); poles pe maximum, equator pe\nabsent/zero (Statement 2 TRUE) — N.Hemisphere mein right deflect, S.Hemisphere mein left. Equator pe zero\nCoriolis force ki wajah se tropical cyclones equator ke paas NAHI bante. [Q1]\n● Dakshin golardh mein left deflection Coriolis force ki wajah se hota hai (Ferrel's law: N.Hemisphere mein\nright, S.Hemisphere mein left turn) — Earth ki axis rotation se generate hota hai. [Q5]\nTrade Winds aur Westerlies — Ocean Temperature Effect\n● Tropical zone mein trade winds (E→W) ki wajah se ocean ka western section warmer hota hai (Statement 1\nTRUE); temperate zone mein westerlies (W→E) ki wajah se ocean ka eastern section warmer hota hai\n(Statement 2 TRUE) — dono statements sahi hain. [Q2]\nWind Patterns — Clockwise/Anticlockwise Misconception\n● 'Wind patterns N.Hemisphere mein clockwise, S.Hemisphere mein anticlockwise' — yeh as general statement\nFALSE hai (A galat) — Coriolis effect dono hemispheres mein wind direction control karta hai (R TRUE)\n— Low-pressure ke around N.Hemisphere mein anticlockwise, S.Hemisphere mein clockwise circulation hoti\nhai (High-pressure ke liye reverse). [Q3]\n● Reverse version bhi (S.Hemisphere clockwise, N.Hemisphere anticlockwise) — yeh statement bhi as general\nassertion FALSE hai, lekin Coriolis effect ka reason (R) TRUE hai. [Q4]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'Wind patterns hamesha N.Hemisphere clockwise/S.Hemisphere anticlockwise' — yeh oversimplified/galat\ngeneralization hai. Actual: low-pressure/high-pressure systems ke around directions different hote hain.\n[Q3,Q4]"," The Winds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nRoaring Forties — Southern Hemisphere Westerlies\n● S.Hemisphere ki westerlies N.Hemisphere se zyada strong+persistent hain kyunki S.Hemisphere mein land kam\nhai (Statement 1 TRUE) — Coriolis force S.Hemisphere mein zyada hone wala Statement 2 GALAT hai.\nIntensity ki wajah se 'Roaring Forties' (~40°), 'Furious Fifties' (~50°), 'Shrieking Sixties' (~60°) naam mile\n— yeh Southern Hemisphere ki westerlies hain. [Q6,Q8]\nGeostrophic Winds\n● Coriolis effect aur pressure-gradient force ek dusre ko counter-balance karein to Geostrophic Winds bante hain\n— isobars ke parallel flow karti hain, ground se upar (kam friction) milti hain, density+pressure distribution se\ndetermine hoti hain. [Q7]\nRoaring Forties/Furious Fifties/Shrieking Sixties\n● Ye winds Southern Hemisphere mein bahti hain (westerlies ki intensity ke basis pe named). [Q9]\n● Roaring Forties ke baare mein: great strength+constancy se bahti hain, direction generally NW-to-East\n(S.Hemisphere), overcast skies/rain/cold weather associate hoti hai (Statements 2,3,4 TRUE) — dono\nhemispheres mein uninterrupted bahne wala Statement 1 GALAT hai (yeh sirf Southern Hemisphere ki\nhain). [Q10]\n● Roaring Forties Indian Ocean region mein bhi bahti hain. [Q11]\n● 'Roaring Forties' = 40°-60° South ke beech strong ocean winds — Equator se South Pole ki taraf air\ndisplacement + Earth rotation ka combined effect. [Q12]\nSouthern Hemisphere Deflection — Earth's Rotation\n● Southern Hemisphere mein wind left deflect hoti hai Earth ki rotation (Coriolis force) ki wajah se —\nN.Hemisphere mein right, S.Hemisphere mein left. [Q13]\nMediterranean Sea — High-Pressure se Winds\n● Conventional pressure-belt circulation ke according, high-pressure area se Mediterranean Sea ki taraf bahne wali\nwinds Trade Winds hain (exam-accepted answer). [Q14]\nSeasonal Wind Reversal — Monsoon Climate\n● Seasonal wind direction reversal Monsoon climate ki typical characteristic hai — summer mein ~6 months sea-\nto-land, winter mein land-to-sea. Yeh reversal hi monsoonal climate ka keynote hai. [Q15]\nChinook Winds — USA Central Plains"," The Winds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Chinook (Snow-Eater) winds USA ke central plains mein winter temperature badhati hain — winter/early\nspring mein common, Rocky Mountains eastern slopes se Colorado(USA) se British Columbia(Canada) tak\ndescend karti hain. Hot wind hai, snow melt karti hai, pasture land available karti hai. [Q16]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0150","t":"42 The Local Winds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Local Winds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Local Winds — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 42_The_Local_Winds\nTopic Index\n1. Local Winds — Region Matching (Multi-set)\n2. Local Winds — Wrong Country Pairings\n3. Blood Rain\n4. Chinook Winds — 'Snow Eater'\n5. Harmattan — Sahara Desert\nLocal Winds — Region Matching (Multi-set)\n● Foehn-Alps, Simoom-Kurdistan (Arabia+Kurdistan deserts), Santa Ana-California, Zonda-Argentina (Andes\neastern slope). [Q1]\n● Foehn = Switzerland ki local wind hai (Alps ki northern slopes se warm+dry wind, Switzerland ka weather\ninfluence karti hai). [Q2]\nLocal Winds — Wrong Country Pairings\n● Correct: Foehn-Alps, Khamsin-Egypt — GALAT: Bora-Poland (actually Adriatic region, NE Italy), Mistral-\nRhine Valley (actually Southern France, lower Rhône Valley/Provence). [Q3]\n● Correct: Chinook-USA, Sirocco-Sicily, Norwesters-India — Blizzard-Chile GALAT hai (Blizzard South\nPole/Siberia/Canada/USA mein hota hai, Chile mein NAHI). [Q4]\n● Conventional PYQ mapping mein Sirocco-France GALAT maana gaya hai (Sirocco classically Italy/central\nMediterranean se associated hai) — Bora Adriatic/NE Italy ko affect karta hai, Blizzard Canada mein common\nhai. [Q6]\n● Correct: Santa Ana-California, Haboob-Sudan, Yamo-Japan — Mistral-Australia GALAT hai (Mistral actually\nFrance aur Spain se associated hai). [Q8]\n● Correct: Leveche-Spain, Brickfielder-Australia, Black roller-North America — Shamal-Austria GALAT hai\n(Shamal actually Iraq/Iran/Arabian Peninsula mein hot/dry/dusty wind hai, June-Aug mein, ~45mph speed).\n[Q9]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Bora, Mistral, Blizzard, Sirocco, Mistral(again), Shamal — inme se har ek ka wrong-country pairing common\nexam trap hai. Correct: Bora-Adriatic/Italy, Mistral-France/Spain, Blizzard-Canada/USA/Siberia, Sirocco-Italy,\nShamal-Iraq/Iran/Arabia. [Q3,Q4,Q6,Q8,Q9]\nBlood Rain\n● Sirocco (Sahara Desert se Mediterranean tak, warm/dry/dusty wind, red sand carry karti hai) kabhi kabhi Italy\nmein rain cause karti hai — jab red sand raindrops ke saath girti hai to use 'Blood Rain' kehte hain. [Q5]"," The Local Winds\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nChinook Winds — 'Snow Eater'\n● Chinook (meaning 'Snow Eater') = Rocky Mountains ki eastern slopes se descend hoti warm+dry wind (Colorado\nsouth se British Columbia south, Canada) — winter temperature badhata hai, snow melt karti hai, winter\nmein bhi green grass ugti hai — cattle rearers ke liye beneficial hai. [Q7]\nHarmattan — Sahara Desert\n● Sahara Desert mein NE se E-to-W dry winds Harmattan kehlati hain — cool+dry winds, invigorating dryness ki\nwajah se 'Doctor Wind' bhi kehte hain. [Q10]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0151","t":"43 The Forests","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Forests\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Forests — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 43_The_Forests\nTopic Index\n1. Selva Forests — Amazon\n2. Climate Data — Forest Type Identification\n3. World Forest Area — Type-wise Percentage\n4. Bhutan — 60% Forest Constitutional Provision\n5. Evergreen Rainforests — Locations\n6. Taiga Forests — Temperate Region\n7. World's Largest+Densest Forest — Amazon\n8. Highest Forest Percentage — Japan\n9. Coniferous Forests — Locations\n10. Africa — Dense Hot-Humid Forests\n11. Tropical vs Temperate Forests — Agricultural Land\n12. Tropical Rain Forest — Regeneration Difficulty\n13. Tropical Rainforest Soil — Actually Poor\n14. Timber Types — Country Matching\n15. Forest Type — Characteristic Trees\n16. Soft Timber/Wood Pulp aur Fuelwood — Producers\n17. Dalbergia — Rosewood\n18. Desert Vegetation — Leaf Modifications\n19. Mediterranean-type Vegetation — Regional Names\n20. Natural Vegetation — Region Matching\n21. Fast Leaf-litter Decomposition — Tropical Rain Forest\n22. Highest Deforestation — Tropical Zone\n23. Deciduous Trees — Jackfruit, Mahua, Teak\n24. World's Largest Tropical Peatland — Congo Basin\n25. Hydrological Cycle — Forests ka Control\nSelva Forests — Amazon\n● Selva forests (Amazon River Basin, Brazil) = broad leaf evergreen characteristic hai — equatorial region, high\ntemp + ~200cm+ rainfall saal bhar. [Q1]\n● Brazil ke equatorial rainforests ko 'Selvas' kehte hain (Statement 1 TRUE) — 'Terra Roxa' actually fertile\nreddish-purple/dark-red soil hai (basalt weathering se, S/SE Brazil mein) — 'dark black land' description\ngalat hai (Statement 2 galat). [Q2]\nClimate Data — Forest Type Identification\n● Given temperature (28-31°C max, 20-21°C min) + high rainfall (51-221mm/month) data — yeh characteristics\nTropical Rain Forest ki hain. [Q3]"," The Forests\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nWorld Forest Area — Type-wise Percentage\n● Given 4 categories mein sabse zyada forest area Temperate Coniferous forests (boreal/taiga included) cover\nkarte hain (~1/4 se 1/3 global forest area) — Russia, Canada, N.Europe, USA mein high latitudes pe. (Note:\nbroad climatic domain se dekha jaaye toh Tropical forest overall sabse bada hai ~45%, lekin given 4 specific\ntypes mein Temperate Coniferous largest hai). [Q4]\nBhutan — 60% Forest Constitutional Provision\n● Bhutan ke constitution mein 60% geographical area forest ke roop mein maintain karne ka provision hai —\n2025 mein actual forest cover ~70.13% tha. [Q5]\nEvergreen Rainforests — Locations\n● Evergreen rainforests Brazil mein milte hain (Amazon Basin) — Equator ke near (~10°N-10°S), hot+heavy\nrainfall saal bhar, no distinct dry season isliye evergreen hain. [Q6]\n● Equator ke near Tropical forests milte hain. [Q7]\n● Earth pe dense forests mainly Equator ke near milte hain. [Q8]\n● Extensive tropical rain forests ke liye famous: Congo Basin — Amazon Basin (Brazil+7 countries), Congo Basin\n(DR Congo+5 countries), Borneo-Mekong-SE Asia basin bhi important tropical rainforest regions hain. [Q9]\nTaiga Forests — Temperate Region\n● Taiga forests = Temperate region ki characteristic hain (coniferous/boreal forest bhi kehte hain) — temperate\nbiomes mein sabse northernmost, North America+Eurasia se sub-polar regions tak extend, summer\ncomparatively short. [Q10]\nWorld's Largest+Densest Forest — Amazon\n● World ke largest aur most dense forests Brazil mein hain (Amazon River Basin, S.America continent ka ~60%\ncover karta hai). [Q11]\nHighest Forest Percentage — Japan\n● Given countries mein sabse zyada forest % (World Bank 2023): Japan (68.4%) — Indonesia (47.7%), India\n(24.5%), China (24.0%) se zyada. [Q12]\nConiferous Forests — Locations\n● Coniferous forests ~50°N-60°N latitudes ke beech milte hain (tundra-north, deciduous-south) — Canada, Europe,\nAsia, USA mein — Amazonia (Brazil) mein NAHI milte (wahan tropical evergreen forests hain). [Q13]\n● Coniferous forests mainly Temperate region mein milte hain. [Q14]"," The Forests\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nAfrica — Dense Hot-Humid Forests\n● Ivory Coast (Gulf of Guinea coast) mein dense/hot/humid forests hain (given options mein) — Kenya,\nZimbabwe, South Africa se contrast. [Q15]\nTropical vs Temperate Forests — Agricultural Land\n● Tropical rain forests clear karne se productive farmland NAHI milta (A FALSE) — actually temperate forests\nclear karne se milta hai (mid-latitudes mein agricultural land tezi se develop ho rahi hai). Tropical rainforest\nprimary productivity ~2,200 g biomass/sq.m/year hai (temperate se zyada, ~1,320 g/sq.m/year) — R TRUE.\n[Q16]\nTropical Rain Forest — Regeneration Difficulty\n● Tropical rain forest remove karne ke baad slow regenerate hoti hai (tropical deciduous forest se) kyunki rain-\nforest soil nutrients mein deficient hoti hai. [Q17]\nTropical Rainforest Soil — Actually Poor\n● Tropical rainforest soil rich NAHI hai (common misconception, Statement I galat) — actually extremely poor\nhoti hai; high temperature+moisture dead organic matter ko quickly decompose karte hain, nutrients\nrelease hote hain lekin fast use ho jaate hain (Statement II TRUE). [Q18]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Tropical rainforest soil actually nutrient-poor hoti hai — abundant plants/warmth/moisture ki wajah se log\ngalti se soil ko rich samajh lete hain. [Q18]\nTimber Types — Country Matching\n● Cedar-Canada, Douglas Fir-Mexico, Mahogany-Honduras, Teak-Myanmar. [Q19]\nForest Type — Characteristic Trees\n● Monsoon Forest-Teak+Sal, Equatorial Forest-Mahogany+Rosewood, Mediterranean Forest-Plum+Olive,\nConiferous Forest-Pine+Spruce. [Q20]\nSoft Timber/Wood Pulp aur Fuelwood — Producers\n● Soft timber+wood pulp ka largest producer/exporter (exam-context): Canada (vast coniferous forests ki wajah\nse). [Q21]\n● Fuelwood ka largest producer (FAO 2025, 2023 data): India (1st) — China 2nd, Brazil 3rd. [Q22]\nDalbergia — Rosewood"," The Forests\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Dalbergia genus (~100-600 species, N/S America, Africa, Madagascar, S.Asia ke tropical regions) associated hai\nRosewood se — Sheesham/Rosewood, Kingwood, Tulipwood, Money Bush important species hain (Sheesham\nki smell rose jaisi, isliye 'Rosewood' naam). [Q23]\nDesert Vegetation — Leaf Modifications\n● Desert areas mein water-loss inhibit karne ke liye: hard+waxy leaves, tiny leaves, thorns instead of leaves —\nsab teeno modifications hote hain (erophyte vegetation) — long roots (deeper moisture), thick bark, small\nspines+closed pores evapotranspiration kam karte hain. [Q24]\nMediterranean-type Vegetation — Regional Names\n● Maquis-Mediterranean Sea coastal region, Fynbos-South Africa, Chaparral-California, Matorral-Chile. [Q25]\nNatural Vegetation — Region Matching\n● Epiphytes-Equatorial, Acacia-Sahara, Baobab-Savanna, Cedars-Mediterranean. [Q26]\nFast Leaf-litter Decomposition — Tropical Rain Forest\n● Description (fast leaf-litter decomposition, bare soil surface, epiphytes/climbers reaching canopy) = Tropical\nRain Forest ki hai — high temp+rainfall se tree diversity, epiphytes bhi hote hain, fallen leaves quickly\nrot/decompose. [Q27]\nHighest Deforestation — Tropical Zone\n● World Forest Report 2024 ke according, Tropical region mein forest area ka largest share hai (2020: ~4.1 billion\nhectares, ~31% land) — highest deforestation bhi tropical areas mein record hui hai. [Q28]\nDeciduous Trees — Jackfruit, Mahua, Teak\n● Jackfruit evergreen hai (India/Malaysia native, ~25m tall) — Mahua aur Teak dono deciduous hain (Mahua-\ntropical fast-growing, Chhattisgarh/Jharkhand/MP/Odisha/Maharashtra mein; Teak-tropical hardwood). Isliye\ngiven 3 mein se 2 deciduous hain. [Q29]\nWorld's Largest Tropical Peatland — Congo Basin\n● Congo Basin mein world ka largest tropical peatland hai (UNEP 2023) — ~29 billion tonnes carbon store karta\nhai (~3 years ke global fossil-fuel emissions ke barabar); Congo Basin overall ~1.5 billion tonnes CO2/year\nabsorb karta hai. [Q30]\nHydrological Cycle — Forests ka Control"," The Forests\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\n● Forests hydrological cycle ko control karte hain ('water engineers') — rainfall intercept, high transpiration, deep\nroots se soil water upward draw, carbon-rich soil ki water-holding capacity enhance, groundwater recharge\nfacilitate karte hain (FAO 'Forests and Water' report ke according). [Q31]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0152","t":"44 The World Climate","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The World Climate — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 44_The_World_Climate\nTopic Index\n1. Day-Night Length Variation — Revolution + Axis Tilt\n2. Continental Interior — High Annual Temperature Range\n3. Climate ka Main Factor — Latitude\n4. Earth ka Maximum Area — Arid Region\n5. Equatorial Region — Year-round Rainfall\n6. Daily Weather Pattern — Equatorial Region\n7. Asia — Sabhi Climatic Zones\n8. Equatorial Climate — Ethiopia Exception\n9. Mediterranean Climate — Warm-Dry Summer, Mild-Wet Winter\n10. Tropical Savannah — Distinct Dry/Wet Seasons\n11. Equatorial Region — Plants ke liye Achha, Humans ke liye NAHI\n12. Mediterranean Climate — New York Exception\n13. Mediterranean Climate — Winter Rainfall Mechanism\n14. Mediterranean — Winter Rain aur Pressure Belt Shift\n15. Central Asian Steppe — Extreme Climate, Nomadic Herders\n16. Climate Zone-Rainfall Pattern Matching\n17. Map Region — Mediterranean (California)\n18. Winter Rainfall — Norway\n19. Climate-Country Matching\n20. Region-Climate Type Matching\n21. Climate Type — Region Matching\n22. Climate Statements — True/False Analysis\n23. Mediterranean — Winter Rain aur Westerlies\n24. NW Europe Ports — Saal Bhar Open\n25. Western Europe — Saal Bhar Rainfall, Westerlies Belt\n26. Marine West Coast Climate — Characteristics\n27. Climate Data — Mediterranean Identification\n28. Pressure Belt Shifting — Mediterranean aur Monsoon\n29. Zaire se Netherlands — Climate Sequence\n30. World Records — Wettest, Coldest Places\n31. El-Nino aur Southern Oscillation — Weak Monsoon\n32. La Nina vs El Nino — Common Misconceptions\n33. El-Nino — Pacific Ocean mein Develop\n34. El-Nino — Warm Current aur Plankton Increase\n35. Southern Oscillation — Pacific aur Indian Ocean\n36. El Nino/La Nina — Storm NAHI, Climate Patterns Hain\n37. Climate Data — Western European Type Identification\n38. Climate Data — China Type Identification\n39. Graph — Wet and Dry Tropical Zone"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n40. Hekistotherms — Very Low Temperature Plants\n41. 'Vegetation = True Index of Climate' — Koppen\n42. Mediterranean Climate — Pampas Exception\nDay-Night Length Variation — Revolution + Axis Tilt\n● Seasonal day-length variation Earth's revolution around Sun AUR axis ka inclination ki wajah se hoti hai —\nrotation aur latitude iske direct causes NAHI hain (statements 2,4 correct hain). [Q1]\nContinental Interior — High Annual Temperature Range\n● Continental interiors ka annual temperature range coastal areas se zyada hota hai kyunki land-water thermal\ndifference (land jaldi garam/thanda hota hai, ocean slowly heat absorb/release karta hai) — altitude difference,\nstrong interior winds, heavy interior rain iske reasons NAHI hain. [Q2]\nClimate ka Main Factor — Latitude\n● Kisi bhi area ki climate determine karne wala main factor Latitude hai — climate belts alag-alag latitudes ke\nhisaab se divide kiye gaye hain. [Q3]\nEarth ka Maximum Area — Arid Region\n● Earth ka ~1/3 area Arid regions se covered hai — semi-arid, sub-humid, humid regions se zyada. [Q4]\nEquatorial Region — Year-round Rainfall\n● 5°-8° latitude (equator ke dono taraf) mein year-round rainfall hoti hai (A TRUE, equatorial region 0°-10° tak\nextend) — high temperature+humidity ki wajah se convectional rainfall mostly noon ke baad hoti hai (R\nTRUE, sahi explanation). [Q5]\nDaily Weather Pattern — Equatorial Region\n● Description (clear+bright morning, sea breeze, heat badhne se dark clouds, thunder+lightning ke saath rain, phir\njaldi khatam) = Equatorial region ki hai. [Q6]\nAsia — Sabhi Climatic Zones\n● Earth ki 3 climate zones: tropical, temperate, cold — Asia equatorial se North Pole tak extend hota hai, isliye\nsabhi climatic zones yahan milte hain. [Q7]\nEquatorial Climate — Ethiopia Exception\n● Congo, Gabon, Zaire equatorial line pe hain — Ethiopia equatorial climate category mein NAHI aata. [Q8]"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nMediterranean Climate — Warm-Dry Summer, Mild-Wet Winter\n● Given features (warm+dry climate, mild+wet winter, evergreen oak trees) = Mediterranean region ki\ncharacteristics hain. [Q9]\nTropical Savannah — Distinct Dry/Wet Seasons\n● Tropical Savannah ki characteristic climate = clear dry aur wet season — high temperature saal bhar (koi month\n20°C se kam nahi), avg annual rainfall 500-2000mm. [Q10]\nEquatorial Region — Plants ke liye Achha, Humans ke liye NAHI\n● Equatorial region ka environment plants ke liye conducive hai, humans ke liye NAHI (A TRUE) — average\nannual temperature difference bahut kam hai (R bhi TRUE independently, lekin R, A ki sahi explanation NAHI\nhai — asal reason humidity+disease-proneness hai, temperature-difference nahi). [Q11]\nMediterranean Climate — New York Exception\n● Mediterranean climate ~30°-40° latitude pe continents ke western parts mein hoti hai (Los Angeles, Rome, Cape\nTown) — New York (US east coast) mein NAHI hoti. [Q12]\nMediterranean Climate — Winter Rainfall Mechanism\n● Mediterranean climate mein winter mein rainfall hoti hai (A TRUE) — summer mein dry terrestrial winds ka\ninfluence hota hai (R bhi TRUE independently, lekin sahi explanation NAHI hai — asal reason: winter mein\nwesterlies equatorward shift hoti hain, jo temperate cyclones se associated hoke moist rainfall laati hain). [Q13]\nMediterranean — Winter Rain aur Pressure Belt Shift\n● Mediterranean mein winter rainfall hoti hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — winter solstice ki wajah se pressure belts\nsouth ki taraf shift karte hain, lekin yeh sirf Northern Hemisphere ke liye TRUE hai (Southern Hemisphere\nwinter mein north ki taraf shift hote hain) — is specific question mein Statement 2 accepted as TRUE hai (dono\nstatements correct). [Q14]\nCentral Asian Steppe — Extreme Climate, Nomadic Herders\n● Description (extreme climate, scanty rainfall, nomadic herders) = Central Asian Steppe ki hai. [Q15]\nClimate Zone-Rainfall Pattern Matching\n● Correct: Equatorial Zone-rain with thunder in noon — Mediterranean actually winter rain (summer nahi),\nMonsoon actually seasonal(saal bhar nahi), Desert actually negligible/indefinite rain (winter nahi). [Q16]"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\nMap Region — Mediterranean (California)\n● Hot-dry summer + mild-moist winter + seasonal wind reversal characteristics = Mediterranean climate\n(California, labeled 1 on map). [Q17]\nWinter Rainfall — Norway\n● Given countries mein winter mein rainfall: Norway (Western European climate type, 40°-65° latitude, saal bhar\nsufficient+even rainfall) — China mein bhi rainfall hoti hai lekin winter relatively dry hoti hai. [Q18]\nClimate-Country Matching\n● Correct: Wet winter dry summer-Italy (Mediterranean) — Sudan actually tropical(desert areas mein negligible\nrain), Iran actually hot-dry(long hot summers), Chile mein northern part hot-dry lekin west-central\nMediterranean climate hai (poora saal dry nahi). [Q19]\nRegion-Climate Type Matching\n● California-Mediterranean, West Australia-Hot Desert, Bangladesh-Tropical Monsoon, Siberia-Cold Temperate.\n[Q20]\nClimate Type — Region Matching\n● Equatorial-Congo, Mediterranean-California, Monsoon-Bangladesh, Savannah-Sudan (Savannah bhi 'Sudan-type\nclimate' kehlati hai). [Q21]\nClimate Statements — True/False Analysis\n● Equatorial regions mein sirf 2 seasons (summer+winter) hote hain, 4 NAHI (Statement 1 galat) — Mediterranean\nmein winter mein zyada rain (summer nahi, Statement 2 galat) — China-type climate mein saal bhar rainfall\nhoti hai (Statement 3 TRUE) — Tropical highlands mein vertical zonation hoti hai (Statement 4 TRUE).\n[Q22]\nMediterranean — Winter Rain aur Westerlies\n● Mediterranean regions mein rainy winters hote hain (A TRUE) — winter mein westerlies belt mein aate hain (R\nTRUE, sahi explanation) — summer mein pressure belts poleward shift hote hain, subtropical high expand hoti\nhai (dry summer). [Q23]\n● Mediterranean regions winter mein heavy rainfall receive karte hain. [Q24]\nNW Europe Ports — Saal Bhar Open\n● NW Europe ke ports saal bhar khule rehte hain (A TRUE) — SW winds saal bhar bahti hain (R bhi TRUE\nindependently, lekin sahi explanation NAHI — asal reason North Atlantic Drift ka warm water hai, jo nearby\noceans ko freeze hone se rokta hai). [Q25]"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\nWestern Europe — Saal Bhar Rainfall, Westerlies Belt\n● Western Europe (marine west-coast climate sense mein) saal bhar rainfall receive karta hai (Statement 1 TRUE)\n— westerlies belt mein located hai (Statement 2 bhi TRUE) — dono statements sahi hain. [Q26]\nMarine West Coast Climate — Characteristics\n● Given description (low annual/daily temp range, year-round precipitation, 50-250cm rainfall) = Marine West\nCoast climate hai — Mediterranean ke poleward mein (NW Europe, N.America west coast California ke north,\nS.Chile, SE Australia, NZ). Summer avg 15-20°C, winter avg 4-10°C. [Q27]\nClimate Data — Mediterranean Identification\n● Given temp/rainfall data (winter mein zyada rain, June-July negligible rain, avg temp 12.8°C, avg rainfall\n54.9cm) = Mediterranean region ka pattern hai — saal bhar temperature mein zyada variation nahi. [Q28]\nPressure Belt Shifting — Mediterranean aur Monsoon\n● Pressure belts ke shifting se associated climates: Mediterranean AUR Monsoon — subtropical high-pressure\nbelts (30°-35°) summer mein trade winds, winter mein equator ki taraf shift; monsoon winds bhi isi shifting se\ndevelop hote hain. [Q29]\nZaire se Netherlands — Climate Sequence\n● Zaire (Central Africa) se Netherlands (W.Europe) tak sequence: Equatorial → Hot Desert (Sahara) →\nMediterranean → West European. [Q30]\nWorld Records — Wettest, Coldest Places\n● World ka sabse zyada rainfall wala place Mawsynram (Meghalaya, India) hai — Cherrapunji se bhi zyada.\n[Q31]\n● Given options mein Earth ka coldest place Verkhoyansk (Siberia) hai (exam-accepted answer). [Q32]\n● Hottest-Sahara desert, Coldest-Antarctica, Wettest-Cherrapunji, Driest-Chile (Atacama). [Q33]\nEl-Nino aur Southern Oscillation — Weak Monsoon\n● Short-term climatic prediction ke liye India subcontinent mein occasional weak monsoon rains El-Nino aur\nSouthern Oscillation se associated hote hain — El Nino Peru coast ki taraf annual weak warm current thi, isse\nIndian monsoon affect hoti hai + drought-jaisi situation banti hai; La Nina iska opposite (equatorial eastern\nPacific cooling) hai. [Q34]\nLa Nina vs El Nino — Common Misconceptions"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\n● La Nina equatorial Pacific Ocean mein cold temperature ki hai (Indian Ocean mein NAHI — Statement 1 galat)\n— La Nina ka monsoon pe koi effect NAHI (Statement 2 galat, actually La Nina se Pacific ke western side\nheavy rainfall hoti hai jo Indian summer monsoon ko bhi activate kar sakti hai) — dono statements galat hain.\n[Q35]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• La Nina Pacific Ocean se related hai (Indian Ocean se NAHI) — aur La Nina ka Indian monsoon pe indirect\neffect hota hai (koi effect nahi wala statement galat hai). [Q35]\nEl-Nino — Pacific Ocean mein Develop\n● El-Nino = Pacific Ocean (eastern part, Peru coast) mein develop hota hai — surface water temperature badhati\nhai. [Q36,Q38]\nEl-Nino — Warm Current aur Plankton Increase\n● El-Nino mein Peru coast (eastern Pacific) pe warm current appear hoti hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — yeh warm\ncurrent water temperature ~10°C badha deti hai, Plankton ki matra BADHATI NAHI, GHATATI hai\n(Statement 2 galat — actual effect: upwelling slow ho jaata hai, plankton kam ho jaate hain, fish bhi kam ho\njaati hain). [Q37]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• El-Nino se Plankton ki matra BADHATI NAHI balki GHATATI hai (upwelling process slow/stop hone se)\n— yeh common wrong statement hai. [Q37]\nSouthern Oscillation — Pacific aur Indian Ocean\n● Southern Oscillation = Pacific aur Indian Ocean ke beech pressure seesaw pattern hai. [Q39]\nEl Nino/La Nina — Storm NAHI, Climate Patterns Hain\n● El Nino aur La Nina storm NAHI hain — yeh climate patterns hain (galat statement identify karna tha) — El\nNino se central/eastern Pacific water temperature badhta hai, phytoplankton coast ke paas kam ho jaate hain\n(upwelling slow); La Nina mein trade winds normal se strong ho jaati hain. [Q40]\nClimate Data — Western European Type Identification\n● Given data (avg temp 15°-21°C, saal bhar sufficient rainfall, summer mein thoda kam) = Western European\ntype climate hai (Northern Hemisphere) — May-June-July mein kam rainfall dikhti hai data mein. [Q41]\nClimate Data — China Type Identification\n● Given data (saal bhar rainfall, summer mein zyada, summer avg temp 24-26.6°C) = China type climate ki\ncharacteristics hain. [Q42]"," The World Climate\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 7\nGraph — Wet and Dry Tropical Zone\n● Given graph (temperature 15°-25°C, April-May-June mein heaviest rainfall ~25cm se kam) = Wet and Dry\nTropical zone ko indicate karta hai. [Q43]\nHekistotherms — Very Low Temperature Plants\n● Hekistotherms = very low temperature areas (tundra, mountains, Alpine forests) mein ugne wale plants. [Q44]\n'Vegetation = True Index of Climate' — Koppen\n● 'Vegetation is the true index of climate' statement Koppen se associated hai (1884 mein descriptive classification,\nlater revised 1918/1931/1936) — Candolle ke 1874 ke 5 vegetation zones ko basis banaya. Thornthwaite ne bhi\nbaad mein vegetation ko indicator maana, lekin rainfall+temperature+evaporation pe zyada focus kiya\n(precipitation effectiveness). [Q45]\nMediterranean Climate — Pampas Exception\n● Central Chile, Cape Town, Adelaide mein Mediterranean climate hoti hai — Pampas mein NAHI (Pampas ki\nclimate temperate hai, ~600-1200mm precipitation, north mein subtropical aur west mein semi-arid ho jaati hai\n— Argentina/Uruguay/Brazil's Rio Grande do Sul cover karta hai, ~750,000 sq km). [Q46]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0153","t":"45 The Soil","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Soil\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Soil — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 45_The_Soil\nTopic Index\n1. Agricultural Practices — Sahi Order\n2. Water-Holding Capacity — Soil Types\n3. Soil Conservation — Definition\n4. Terra Rossa — Limestone se Development\n5. Soil Leaching — Tropical Rainforests\n6. Halophytes — Saline Soils\n7. Soil mein Nitrogen — Sources\n8. Clay — Water Holding aur Pore Size\n9. Contour Bunding — Mountain Regions\n10. Soil Types — Climate Region Matching\n11. Earthworms — Soil ke liye Beneficial\n12. Agricultural Soils — Organic Matter, Sulphur Cycle, Salinization\n13. Edaphic Factor — Soil se Related\n14. Geological Formations — Chronological Order\n15. Geographical Cycle of Erosion — W.M. Davis\nAgricultural Practices — Sahi Order\n● Correct order: Soil Preparation → Sowing → Irrigation → Harvesting. [Q1]\nWater-Holding Capacity — Soil Types\n● Water-holding capacity ka decreasing order: Clay > Silt > Sand. [Q2]\n● Capillary activity sabse effective Clayey soil mein hoti hai (chhote pores) — sabse kam Sandy soil mein (bade\npores). Order: Clay > Silt > Loamy > Sandy. [Q3]\nSoil Conservation — Definition\n● Soil conservation = mitti ko harm se bachana — broad sense mein sirf erosion control nahi, land ki high\nfertility maintain karna bhi shamil hai (land-use improvement). [Q4]\nTerra Rossa — Limestone se Development\n● Terra Rossa = red clay soil hai jo Limestone aur Dolomite rocks ke weathering se banti hai. [Q5]"," The Soil\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nSoil Leaching — Tropical Rainforests\n● Soil leaching ki major problem Tropical Rainforests mein hoti hai — saal bhar heavy rainfall ki wajah se. [Q6]\nHalophytes — Saline Soils\n● Halophytes saline soil mein achhe se ugte hain — Cryophytes (cold soil), Lithophytes (rocks), Xerophytes\n(tropical desert), Hygrophytes (waterlogged), Hydrophytes (aquatic) alag categories hain. [Q7]\nSoil mein Nitrogen — Sources\n● Soil mein nitrogen add karte hain: Animals ka urea excretion AUR vegetation ki death (decomposers inhe\ndecompose karke nutrients release karte hain, nitrogen cycle chalu rehta hai) — coal burning NAHI add karta\nhai. [Q8]\nClay — Water Holding aur Pore Size\n● Clay soil ki water-holding capacity sabse zyada hai (A TRUE, particles extremely small, large surface area) —\nclay mein large pores NAHI hote (R FALSE, actually bahut fine micropores hote hain). [Q9]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Clay mein pores bade NAHI, bahut fine/micro hote hain — high water-holding capacity particle size (small)\naur surface area (large) ki wajah se hai, pore size ki wajah se NAHI. [Q9]\nContour Bunding — Mountain Regions\n● Contour bunding soil conservation method mountain regions mein use hoti hai (given options — desert\nmargins, flood-prone plains, scrublands — sab galat hain) — rainwater flow slow karke soil erosion check karti\nhai. [Q10]\nSoil Types — Climate Region Matching\n● Podzol-Cold temperate, Chernozem-Temperate cold steppe, Spodosols-Humid cold temperate, Laterite-Hot and\nhumid. [Q11]\nEarthworms — Soil ke liye Beneficial\n● Earthworms agriculture ke liye achhe NAHI hote — yeh statement galat hai (A FALSE) — actually 'ecosystem\nengineers' hain, soil formation+productivity badhate hain; mitti ko fine particles mein todkar soft banate hain (R\nTRUE). [Q12]\nAgricultural Soils — Organic Matter, Sulphur Cycle, Salinization"," The Soil\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Organic matter soil ki water-holding capacity badhata hai, kam NAHI karta (Statement 1 galat); Soil sulphur\ncycle mein role play karti hai (plants sulphate absorb karte hain, decomposition sulphates wapas mitti mein\nlaati hai — Statement 2 galat); long-term irrigation se salinization ho sakta hai (salts surface pe accumulate\nhote hain — Statement 3 TRUE). [Q13]\nEdaphic Factor — Soil se Related\n● Edaphic = soil ki physical/chemical composition se related abiotic factor hai (Climatic, Biotic, Topography se\ncontrast). [Q14]\nGeological Formations — Chronological Order\n● Chronological order: Sihawal (Lower Paleolithic) → Patpara (Middle Paleolithic) → Baghor (Upper\nPaleolithic) → Khetaurhi (Neolithic+Microlithic) — yaani code 4,1,3,2. [Q15]\nGeographical Cycle of Erosion — W.M. Davis\n● W.M. Davis (William Morris Davis) ne geographical/geological cycle of erosion ki concept postulate ki —\nWalter Penck ne isse reject karke 'Morphological System' diya; Arthur Holmes-convection current theory; S.W.\nWooldridge-London Basin structural evolution; Kober-Geosynclinal Orogen Theory. [Q16]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0154","t":"46 The Major Tribes of the World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Major Tribes of the World — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 46_The_Major_Tribes_of_the_World\nTopic Index\n1. Nomadic Herding — Dry Areas\n2. Transhumance — Seasonal Movement\n3. Cro-Magnon Humans — Most Recent\n4. First Bird — ~150 Million Years Ago\n5. Africa — Cradle of Mankind\n6. Afrikaners — South Africa White Minority\n7. Largest Racial Group — Caucasoid (Exam Convention)\n8. Ethnic Groups — Country Matching\n9. Gypsies — Original Home India\n10. Pygmies — Congo River Basin\n11. Pygmies — Africa aur Equatorial Forest\n12. Pastoral Nomads — Pygmies Exception\n13. Tribe-Country Matching\n14. Tribes — Country Matching (Multi-set)\n15. Tribes — Region Matching\n16. Polar Region Tools — Terminology (Disputed)\n17. Tribe-Country Matching\n18. Semang Tribe — Malaysia\n19. Zulu — South Africa\n20. Bushmen — Kalahari (Southern Africa)\n21. Race-Region Mismatches\n22. Kyrgyz, Red Indians, Eskimos — Correct Pairs\n23. Maasai — East Africa (Zambia NAHI)\n24. Kurdish Population — Former Soviet Republics (Disputed)\n25. Inuit People — Sweden mein NAHI\n26. Bantu — Sahara NAHI\n27. Lapps (Sami) — Scandinavia\n28. North America Natives — Mongoloid\n29. Khirghiz — Central Asia (Sudan NAHI)\n30. Masai, Sakai, Bedouin, Kirghiz — All Correct\n31. Koryak — Russia (Alaska NAHI)\n32. Keystone Species — Community mein Determining Role\n33. China, Mongolia, Japan — Mongoloid Race\nNomadic Herding — Dry Areas\n● Nomadic herding ke sabse common areas: Dry areas (Eurasia ke steppe lands especially) — cattle ke saath\npasture ki khoj mein ek jagah se doosri jagah move karte hain — Central Asia, Africa, South America mein aaj\nbhi milta hai. [Q1]"," The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nTranshumance — Seasonal Movement\n● Transhumance = valley se mountain aur mountain se valley ki taraf seasonal movement (lowlands-highlands,\nseasons change ke saath) — Himalayan pastoral communities (Bhotiya, Bakarwal, Gaddi) traditionally isi tarah\nlivestock herding karte hain. [Q2]\nCro-Magnon Humans — Most Recent\n● Given options mein most recent: Cro-Magnon humans (Upper Paleolithic Europe, early modern Homo sapiens)\n— Heidelberg, Neanderthal se recent. [Q3]\nFirst Bird — ~150 Million Years Ago\n● First bird (Archaeopteryx) ~150 million years ago (Late Jurassic) appear hua — dinosaur+bird jaise mixed\nfeatures the. [Q4]\nAfrica — Cradle of Mankind\n● Africa continent = 'Cradle of Mankind' kehlata hai. [Q5]\nAfrikaners — South Africa White Minority\n● Afrikaners = South Africa ka white minority group hai — mainly Dutch-speaking settlers se descend,\nGerman+French Huguenot ancestry bhi — Afrikaans language (mainly Dutch se develop) inse associated hai.\n[Q6]\nLargest Racial Group — Caucasoid (Exam Convention)\n● Historical exam classification ke according largest racial group: Caucasoid — Negroid, Mongoloid, Australoid\nse zyada (yeh terminology ab outdated maani jaati hai). [Q7]\nEthnic Groups — Country Matching\n● Jews-Israel, Teda-Libya, Beja-Egypt, Lur-Iran. [Q8]\nGypsies — Original Home India\n● Gypsies ka original home India tha — 'Dom caste' se originate maane jaate hain. [Q9]\nPygmies — Congo River Basin"," The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Pygmy tribes = Africa ke Congo River basin ke equatorial rainforests mein rehte hain — hunter-gatherer tribe,\n'Mongulus' naam ke single-family huts (branches+leaves se) mein rehte hain. [Q10]\nPygmies — Africa aur Equatorial Forest\n● Pygmies Africa ke inhabitants hain — specifically Equatorial forest (Congo basin) mein milte hain, na ki\nSahara/Kalahari/Pampas mein. [Q11,Q12]\n● Pygmy house type: tree-house with ladder (diagram A, source-figure-based). [Q13]\nPastoral Nomads — Pygmies Exception\n● Given options mein Pygmies pastoral nomads NAHI hain (hunter-gatherers hain) — Kazaks, Masai, Lapps sab\npastoral nomadic tribes hain. [Q14]\nTribe-Country Matching\n● Correct: Eskimo-Canada — Oraon actually India (Chotanagpur) mein hai, Japan mein nahi; Lapps actually\nEuropean Tundra mein hain, India mein nahi; Gonds actually India mein hain, Africa mein nahi. [Q15]\n● Correct: Bushman-Kalahari — Eskimo actually high-latitude regions (Canada/Alaska/Greenland) mein hai,\nAmazon Basin mein nahi; Pygmy actually Central Africa mein hai, Irrawadi Basin mein nahi; Bundu actually\nWestern Africa mein hai, Sahara mein nahi. [Q16]\nTribes — Country Matching (Multi-set)\n● Eskimo-Canada(Greenland tundra), Maasai-Kenya, Bedouins-Saudi Arabia, Bushman-Kalahari\nDesert(Botswana+parts of S.Africa/Namibia). [Q17]\n● Eskimos Greenland (major island) mein rehte hain — New Guinea, Hawaii, Iceland mein nahi. [Q18]\nTribes — Region Matching\n● Khirghiz-Central Asia, Bushman-Kalahari, Ainu-Japan, Bedouin-Arab region. [Q19]\nPolar Region Tools — Terminology (Disputed)\n● Kayak = narrow hunting boat, Umiak = larger boat (transport), Sledge = dog-pulled vehicle — 'Inuit' ek people\nka naam hai, 'snow house' ka matlab NAHI (snow house ko 'igloo' kehte hain) — is matching table mein\nerror hai, isliye question disputed (*) hai. [Q20]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Snow house ko Igloo kehte hain, 'Inuit' ek tribe/people ka naam hai — inhe confuse mat karo. [Q20]\nTribe-Country Matching"," The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Bushman-Namibia, Bedouins-Saudi Arabia, Pigmies-Congo, Maasai-Kenya. [Q21]\n● Correct: Bushman-Kalahari Desert, Eskimo-Northern Canada, Pygmy-Congo Basin — Masai-West Africa\nGALAT hai (Masai actually East Africa mein hain). [Q22]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Masai East Africa (Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda) mein hain, West Africa mein NAHI. [Q22,Q30]\nSemang Tribe — Malaysia\n● Semang tribe = Malaysia (Malay Peninsula forests) ki inhabitants hain — Negrito species se belong karte hain,\nIndonesia se NAHI. [Q23,Q24]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Semang Malaysia ki hai, Indonesia ki NAHI — common wrong pairing. [Q24]\nZulu — South Africa\n● Zulu tribe = South Africa se associated hai — 1879 mein famous Isandlwana War British aur Zulus ke beech\nlada gaya tha. [Q25]\nBushmen — Kalahari (Southern Africa)\n● Exam key ke according 'Bushmen-Union of South Africa' galat sumel\n\nितmaana gaya (though Bushmen S.Africa\nmein bhi milte hain) — Ainu-Japan, Maasai-Kenya, Papuans-New Guinea correct hain. [Q26]\n● Bushmen sabse zyada Kalahari region se associate kiye jaate hain (Botswana, Namibia, S.Africa) — East Africa,\nSahara, New Zealand se nahi. [Q27]\n● Correct: Bushmen-Botswana — Hemites-Uganda galat, Semites-Malaysia galat, Sakai-Sudan galat (in sab ki\nactual associations alag hain). [Q28]\nRace-Region Mismatches\n● Correct: Central Asia-Alpine, Kalahari-Bushmen, Scandinavia-Nordic — Congo Basin-Negrito GALAT hai\n(Congo Basin actually Pygmy se associated hai; Negrito South-East Asia se associated hai). [Q29]\nKyrgyz, Red Indians, Eskimos — Correct Pairs\n● Correct: Kyrgyz-Central Asia, Red Indians-North America, Eskimos-Greenland — Maasai-Western Africa\nGALAT hai (Maasai actually Kenya/Tanzania/Uganda — East Africa mein hain, pastoral nomads hain). [Q30]\nMaasai — East Africa (Zambia NAHI)\n● Correct: Maori-New Zealand, Mayas-Guatemala, Bushman-Kalahari — Maasai-Zambia GALAT hai (Maasai\nactually Kenya/N.Tanzania/E.Uganda mein hain). [Q31]"," The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\nKurdish Population — Former Soviet Republics (Disputed)\n● Kurdish population historically Armenia, Azerbaijan, Georgia, aur Turkmenistan — chaaron former Soviet\nrepublics mein documented hai, isliye single answer nahi ban pata — question disputed (*) treat hota hai.\n[Q32]\nInuit People — Sweden mein NAHI\n● Inuit people Alaska, Greenland, Canada ke Arctic regions ke indigenous hain — Sweden mein NAHI milte.\n[Q33]\nBantu — Sahara NAHI\n● Correct: Fulani-West Africa, Masai-East Africa, Nuba-Sudan — Bantu-Sahara GALAT hai (Bantu actually\nEast/Central/Southern Africa mein hain). [Q34]\nLapps (Sami) — Scandinavia\n● Sami (Lapps) tribe = Scandinavia (Norway, Sweden, Finland, Russia's Kola Peninsula — 'Fenno-Scandinavian\nregion') mein rehte hain. [Q35]\nNorth America Natives — Mongoloid\n● North America ke natives originally Mongoloid racial group se belong karte hain. [Q36]\nKhirghiz — Central Asia (Sudan NAHI)\n● Correct: Pygmy-Congo basin, Angami-Nagaland, Ainu-Japan — Khirghiz-Sudan GALAT hai (Khirghiz\nactually Central Asia mein hain). [Q37]\nMasai, Sakai, Bedouin, Kirghiz — All Correct\n● Masai-Central Eastern Africa, Sakai-Indonesia+Malaysia, Bedouin-Arabian Peninsula, Kirghiz-Central Asia —\nin sab mein koi mismatch NAHI hai. [Q38]\nKoryak — Russia (Alaska NAHI)\n● Correct: Borneo-Punan, Arab Desert-Ruwala, Sweden+Finland-Lapps — Alaska-Koryak GALAT hai (Koryak\nactually Russia ki tribe hai, Ukraine mein bhi population milti hai — 2010 Russian census: 7,953 population).\n[Q39]"," The Major Tribes of the World\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\nKeystone Species — Community mein Determining Role\n● Keystone species = pioneer/basic species jo community mein doosri species ke persist karne ki ability determine\nkarte hain. [Q40]\nChina, Mongolia, Japan — Mongoloid Race\n● China, Mongolia, Japan mein Mongoloid race rehti hai — Australoid (Melanesia+Australia), Negroid (Africa),\nNordic/Caucasian (NW+N Europe) se contrast. [Q41]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0155","t":"47 The Languages","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Languages\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Languages — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 47_The_Languages\nTopic Index\n1. Esperanto — Artificial World Language\n2. Largest/Most Widely Spoken Language — English\n3. Spanish — Official Language Nahi Hai\n4. Tamil — Singapore mein Official Language\n5. South America Map — Language Zones\n6. Pakistan — Official Language aur Ethnic Diversity\n7. Language-Country Mismatches\nEsperanto — Artificial World Language\n● Esperanto = artificial language hai world language ke roop mein serve karne ke liye — Dr. Ludwik Lejzer\nZamenhof ne develop kiya tha. [Q1]\nLargest/Most Widely Spoken Language — English\n● World mein sabse zyada logo dwara boli jaane wali language English hai (native+non-native combined) —\nMandarin native-speakers mein sabse zyada hai, lekin English total speakers mein sabse aage hai (zyada\ncountries mein bhi use hoti hai). [Q2,Q3]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Native speakers ke basis pe Mandarin sabse aage hai, lekin native+non-native combined total mein English\nsabse aage hai — exam question ki exact wording dekh kar answer decide karo. [Q2,Q3]\nSpanish — Official Language Nahi Hai\n● Spanish official language hai Chile, Colombia, Cuba mein — Republic of Congo mein Spanish official\nlanguage NAHI hai. [Q4]\nTamil — Singapore mein Official Language\n● Tamil Singapore ki official language hai (Malay-national, English, Mandarin, Tamil sab official) —\nMyanmar(Burmese), Indonesia(Indonesian), Mauritius(English+French official) mein Tamil major NAHI hai.\n[Q5]\nSouth America Map — Language Zones"," The Languages\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Map mein regions: 1-French (French Guiana), 2-Portuguese (Brazil), 3-Spanish (Argentina), 4-English. [Q6]\nPakistan — Official Language aur Ethnic Diversity\n● Pakistan mein Bangladesh se zyada racial/ethnic diversity hai (A TRUE) — lekin Punjabi Pakistan ki official\nlanguage NAHI hai (English+Urdu official hain, Punjabi sirf sabse zyada boli jaane wali language hai, R\nFALSE) — Bangladesh apni ethnic homogeneity ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Punjabi Pakistan mein sabse zyada boli jaati hai lekin official language NAHI hai — English+Urdu official\nhain. [Q7]\nLanguage-Country Mismatches\n● Correct: Danish-Denmark, Dutch-Netherlands, Mandarin-China — Bahasa-Thailand GALAT hai (Bahasa\nactually Indonesia ki language hai). [Q8]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Bahasa Indonesia ki language hai, Thailand ki NAHI. [Q8]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0156","t":"48 A Agriculture and Livestock","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n A Agriculture and Livestock — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 48_A_Agriculture_and_Livestock\nTopic Index\n1. Wheat aur Rice — Leading Producer China\n2. Rice — India ka World Rank aur Cultivation Area\n3. Wheat — Production Order aur Largest Producer\n4. Rice Productivity — China Highest (Yield/Hectare)\n5. Hybrid Rice — China mein Sabse Popular\n6. Rice Gene Bank — Philippines\n7. Rice Export Earnings — 2/3rd Premise Disputed\n8. Sugarcane — Brazil #1, India #2\n9. Sugar Beets — France, Russia (2010 Data)\n10. Cotton — Cotton-Seed Producer aur Yield Records\n11. Castor-Oilseeds — India ka Dominance\n12. Bananas — India Largest Producer\n13. Coconut — Indonesia Largest Producer\n14. Philippines — Coconut+Sugarcane Development Credit\n15. India — Fruit Production Rank (2nd)\n16. Tobacco, Jowar, Soyabean, Silk — Largest Producers\n17. Mauritius — Highest % Sugar Export\n18. Natural Rubber — Thailand Largest Producer\n19. Natural Rubber — Thailand+Indonesia Major Producers\n20. Sri Lanka — Coffee Cultivation Abandoned (Leaf Rust)\n21. Coffee — Top Producers (Brazil #1, Vietnam #2)\n22. Robusta Coffee — Africa Origin\n23. Tea — Export Rankings (Quantity vs Value)\n24. Crop — Production Zone Matching (Multi-set)\n25. Cocoa/Coffee/Tea/Sugarcane — Country Matching\n26. USA — Hawaii mein Coffee\n27. Apple — Non-Tropical Fruit\n28. Commercial Horticulture — Small Holdings, Zyada Labour\n29. Crop-Country Matching (Rubber/Coffee/Olive/Sugarcane)\n30. Leading Producer-Commodity Matching\n31. Plantation Agriculture — Characteristics\n32. Alley Cropping — Trees ke Beech Crops\n33. Monoculture — Commercial Grain Farming\n34. Shifting Cultivation — Fazenda Exception\n35. Taungya, Ladang — Shifting Cultivation Systems\n36. Nitrogen Deficiency — Plant Symptoms\n37. Biofertilizers — Nostoc (Blue-Green Algae)\n38. Alfalfa — Ancient Herb (Asia Native)\n39. Africa mein Tea Plantations — Exist Karti Hain"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n40. Podzol Soil — Taiga Region\n41. Mocha Coffee — Yemen\n42. Tea mein Compounds — Morphine NAHI\n43. Green Box — International Agriculture Agreement\n44. Plantation Crops — Country Correct Statements\n45. Heroin — Opium Resin se\n46. Golden Crescent — Afghanistan+Iran+Pakistan\n47. Maize — Middle Africa ka Staple Food\n48. Sacramento-San Joaquin Valley — California\n49. Commercial Viticulture — Mediterranean Europe\n50. High-Yielding Variety Seeds — Mexico (Norman Borlaug)\n51. Catechu — Khair Tree Wood\n52. Peanuts/Groundnut — Main Crop aur Native Place\n53. Shahtoosh — Tibetan Antelope (Chiru) Wool\n54. Apiculture, Viticulture, Olericulture — Terminology\n55. Silk Production — China #1, India #2\n56. Australia — Cattle Rearing Mainly Meat ke liye\n57. China — Largest Livestock Population\n58. Mad Cow Disease — Beef Image Destroyed\n59. Milk — India World ka Leading Producer\n60. Milk Production per Cow — Denmark Highest (Given Options)\n61. Corn — China 2nd Rank\n62. 'Sugar Bowl of World' — Cuba\n63. Fazenda — Brazil ki Coffee Plantations\n64. Country — Principal Primary Export Matching\n65. Rice — India Largest Exporter\n66. Saffron — Iran Largest Producer\n67. Economic Activity — Country Matching\n68. Cocoa — Top Producers (Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana)\n69. India vs China — Arable Area Comparison\n70. India — Cropland Area Highest (vs USA/China/Japan)\n71. 'Cereal Yield' — Production per Unit Area\n72. Crop Rotation — Soil Nutrient Replenishment\n73. Mediterranean Agriculture — Region Coverage\nWheat aur Rice — Leading Producer China\n● Exam-period data ke according China wheat aur rice dono ka leading producer tha (rankings time ke saath\nchange ho sakti hain). [Q1]\nRice — India ka World Rank aur Cultivation Area\n● FAO 2024 ke according India world ka largest rice producer hai. [Q2]\n● Rice cultivation area (FAO 2024, hectares): India-50,511,930 (highest), China-29,256,900,\nPhilippines-4,645,921, Japan-1,458,000. [Q3]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nWheat — Production Order aur Largest Producer\n● Wheat production descending order: China > India > Russia > USA. [Q4]\n● FAO 2024 ke according world ka largest wheat producer China hai. [Q5]\nRice Productivity — China Highest (Yield/Hectare)\n● Rice productivity (production per unit harvested area) mein China Japan se thoda upar aur India se kaafi upar hai\n(Germany major rice-producer NAHI hai). [Q6]\nHybrid Rice — China mein Sabse Popular\n● Hybrid rice cultivation China mein sabse popular hai — half se zyada rice-growing land pe hybrid rice cultivate\nhoti hai. [Q7]\nRice Gene Bank — Philippines\n● World ka 'Rice Gene Bank' International Rice Research Institute, Los Banos (Philippines) mein hai. [Q8]\nRice Export Earnings — 2/3rd Premise Disputed\n● FAO data ke according, diye gaye 4 countries mein se koi bhi apni export earnings ka ~2/3 rice trade se NAHI\nkamata — Thailand highest (~14%), Myanmar ~12%, Japan <1%, Indonesia negligible — isliye is premise se\nmatch karne wala koi option NAHI hai, question disputed (*) hai. [Q9]\nSugarcane — Brazil #1, India #2\n● FAO 2024 (million tonnes): Brazil 759.66 (largest), India 453.16, China 102.09, Pakistan 84.24. [Q10]\n● Sugarcane ka world mein 2nd largest producer India hai (Brazil ke baad). [Q11]\nSugar Beets — France, Russia (2010 Data)\n● 2010 exam-data ke according France aur Russia world ke 2 leading sugar beet producers the. [Q12]\n● Sirf sugar-beets se sugar produce karne wala desh Ukraine hai (almost 100% sugar-beet based). [Q13]\nCotton — Cotton-Seed Producer aur Yield Records\n● Cotton-seed ka largest producer China hai. [Q14]\n● 2014 reference year ke according, cotton ki highest per-hectare production wala desh (given options mein)\nAustralia tha — baad ke FAO data mein rankings different hain (yield comparisons time-sensitive hote hain).\n[Q15]\n● Older exam question mein cotton ki highest per-acre yield China mein accepted thi (FAO 2024 data bhi China ko\nseed-cotton productivity mein highest maanta hai given options mein). [Q16]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Cotton yield comparisons time-sensitive hote hain — 2014 ka answer Australia tha, current data mein alag ho\nsakta hai. Exam question ka specific reference year dhyan se dekho. [Q15]\nCastor-Oilseeds — India ka Dominance\n● India castor seed+castor oil ka world ka dominant producer AUR leading exporter (oil+derivatives dono) hai.\n[Q17]\nBananas — India Largest Producer\n● FAO 2024 (million tonnes): India 37.61 (largest), China 11.76, Indonesia 9.26, Ecuador 7.56, Brazil 7.05. [Q18]\nCoconut — Indonesia Largest Producer\n● FAO 2024 (million tonnes, shell): Indonesia 17.97 (largest), India 14.71, Philippines 14.50. [Q19]\nPhilippines — Coconut+Sugarcane Development Credit\n● Philippines mein coconut+sugarcane agriculture develop karne ka credit Spanish aur Americans ko jaata hai.\n[Q20]\nIndia — Fruit Production Rank (2nd)\n● India world ka 2nd largest fruit producer hai (China ke baad, Indian govt horticulture summaries ke according)\n— India banana+mango jaise individual fruits mein #1 hai, lekin total fruit production mein 2nd. [Q21]\nTobacco, Jowar, Soyabean, Silk — Largest Producers\n● FAO 2024 (million tonnes, unmanufactured tobacco): China 2.26 (largest), India 0.73, Brazil 0.64. [Q22]\n● Given statements mein: China (Tobacco) aur USA (Jowar, source mein 'U.S.A.' likha hai, India NAHI) exam-\naccepted correct hain — Statement 1,2 correct maane gaye. [Q23]\nMauritius — Highest % Sugar Export\n● Given options mein apni sugar production ka sabse zyada % export karne wala desh Mauritius hai — Mauritius\nki economy mainly sugar exports+tourism pe depend karti hai. [Q24]\nNatural Rubber — Thailand Largest Producer\n● FAO 2024 (thousand tonnes): Thailand 4,789.04 (largest), Indonesia 2,262.09, Cote d'Ivoire 1,686.59, Vietnam\n1,327.47, China 877.60. [Q25]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\nNatural Rubber — Thailand+Indonesia Major Producers\n● 2 major natural rubber producers: Thailand aur Indonesia (FAO 2024, Thailand #1, Indonesia doosre number\npe). [Q26]\n● World ka ~1/3rd natural rubber production Thailand se aata hai. [Q27]\n● Exam-context ke according largest rubber cultivation Indonesia mein hoti hai. [Q28]\nSri Lanka — Coffee Cultivation Abandoned (Leaf Rust)\n● Sri Lanka mein coffee cultivation 1860s se 'Leaf Rust' (Hemileia vastatrix) epidemic ki wajah se abandon ho\ngayi (1869 se start) — yeh fungus coffee leaf rust disease cause karta hai, British colonies mein widespread thi.\n[Q29]\nCoffee — Top Producers (Brazil #1, Vietnam #2)\n● FAO 2024 leading coffee(green) producers: Brazil, Vietnam (top 2) — phir Colombia, Indonesia, Ethiopia,\nUganda, India. [Q30]\n● FAO 2023 (thousand tonnes): Brazil 3,387.72 (highest), Vietnam 2,015.29, Colombia 839.85. [Q31]\n● Total coffee production % mein top country Brazil hai (FAO 2024). [Q32]\n● Coffee ka 2nd largest exporter (quantity se, Brazil ke baad) Vietnam hai (FAO 2024). [Q33]\nRobusta Coffee — Africa Origin\n● Robusta (Coffea Canephora) Central+Western sub-Saharan Africa (specifically Ethiopia+Uganda) se originate\nhui — India mein bhi cultivate hoti hai. [Q34]\nTea — Export Rankings (Quantity vs Value)\n● Tea export maximum quantity mein Kenya (2024) largest exporter hai — China value ke basis pe leading\nexporter hai, Sri Lanka historically major exporter raha hai. [Q35]\n● 2016 exam (2015 data pe based) ke according China value ke basis pe largest tea exporter tha — 2024 tak Kenya\nquantity mein largest ban gaya (rankings year+metric ke saath shift hoti hain). [Q36]\n● 2016-17 mein value($) ke basis pe largest tea exporter China tha (2017 aur 2024 dono years mein) — India 2024\nmein 4th rank pe hai. [Q37]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Tea export rankings quantity vs value metric ke hisaab se alag hote hain — Kenya quantity mein #1, China\nvalue mein #1. Exam question ka exact wording dhyan se dekho. [Q35,Q36]\nCrop — Production Zone Matching (Multi-set)\n● Coffee-Sao Paulo Plateau, Jute-Ganges delta, Rice-Yangtze plains, Wheat-Prairies plains. [Q38]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\n● Rice-Yangzi Jiang basin, Wheat-Huang He basin (winter wheat), Coffee-Sao Paulo, Tea-Kandy basin (Sri\nLanka). [Q39]\nCocoa/Coffee/Tea/Sugarcane — Country Matching\n● Cocoa-Ghana, Coffee-Ivory Coast, Tea-Kenya, Sugarcane-South Africa. [Q40]\nUSA — Hawaii mein Coffee\n● USA ke states mein Hawaii coffee grow karta hai — famous 'Kona coffee' Hawaiian variety hai. [Q41]\nApple — Non-Tropical Fruit\n● Given fruits mein Apple non-tropical hai — temperate+subtropical regions mein commercially cultivate hota hai\n(apple trees ko flower ke liye cold climatic conditions chahiye). [Q42]\nCommercial Horticulture — Small Holdings, Zyada Labour\n● Small-sized holdings pe large amount labour Commercial Horticulture system mein apply hota hai — fruits,\nspices, vegetables, shrubs, flowers, turf, tea, coffee, sugarcane, rubber isme cultivate hote hain, continuous\nsupervision zaroori hoti hai. [Q43]\nCrop-Country Matching (Rubber/Coffee/Olive/Sugarcane)\n● Rubber-Malaysia, Coffee-Colombia, Olive-Italy, Sugarcane-Mauritius. [Q44]\nLeading Producer-Commodity Matching\n● China-Iron Ore, India-Milk, Saudi Arabia-Petroleum, Thailand-Natural Rubber. [Q45]\nPlantation Agriculture — Characteristics\n● Tropical plantation world ke oldest commercial agriculture systems mein se ek hai — mostly lowlands mein\nlocated, sea coast ke along bunches mein found hoti hai — usually >40 hectares (100 acres) ke large estates\npe monoculture follow karti hai (Brazil coffee, tea jaise examples). [Q46]\n● Plantation crops: Coffee, Rubber, Coconut (conventional classification mein) — Spices is category mein NAHI\naate. [Q47]\nAlley Cropping — Trees ke Beech Crops\n● Alley Cropping = planted trees ki rows ke beech interspaces mein crops grow karne ka system hai (wide-spaced\ntree rows + companion crop alleyways mein) — Intercropping ek broader term hai jisme relay+mixed+alley\ncropping sab shamil hain. [Q48]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 7\nMonoculture — Commercial Grain Farming\n● 'Monoculture' Commercial Grain Farming ki distinct characteristic hai. [Q49]\nShifting Cultivation — Fazenda Exception\n● Jhooming, Chena, Milpa sab shifting cultivation ke types hain — Fazenda shifting cultivation ka type NAHI\nhai (Fazenda actually Brazil mein plantations se related hai). [Q50]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Fazenda Brazil ki plantations se related hai, shifting cultivation se NAHI — common confusion. [Q50]\nTaungya, Ladang — Shifting Cultivation Systems\n● 'Taungya' agriculture mainly Myanmar mein practice hoti hai — villagers/forest workers ko forest ki early stage\nmein agricultural crops cultivate karne ka right milta hai. [Q51]\n● 'Ladang' = Malaysia+Indonesia mein shifting cultivation ke liye local naam. [Q52]\n● Primitive subsistence agriculture: Jhumming-SE Asia, Milpa-Mexico+Central America correct hain —\nLadang actually Indonesia mein hai, Sri Lanka mein NAHI (slash-and-burn farming, world ke many tribes\nmein prevalent, India included). [Q53]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Ladang Indonesia/Malaysia mein practice hoti hai, Sri Lanka mein NAHI. [Q53]\nNitrogen Deficiency — Plant Symptoms\n● Nitrogen-deficient plants mein stunted growth + pale green/yellow leaves dikhte hain (A TRUE) — Nitrogen\ngreen leaf growth ke liye responsible hai (R TRUE, sahi explanation) — nitrogen cells/tissues formation ka\nmajor constituent hai, kami se chlorophyll content ghat jaata hai. [Q54]\nBiofertilizers — Nostoc (Blue-Green Algae)\n● Biofertilizers ke roop mein Nostoc (blue-green algae/cyanobacteria) use hota hai — Azotobacter, Rhizobium,\nAzospirillum bhi long time se biofertilizers hain — Nostoc/Anabaena/Tolypothrix/Aulosira atmospheric\nnitrogen fix karke paddy crops (upland+lowland) mein inoculation ke roop mein use hote hain. [Q55]\n● Azolla-Anabaena Biofertilizer Rice crop production ke liye use hota hai. [Q56,Q57]\n● Blue-Green Algae biofertilizer Paddy crop production induce karne ke liye use hoti hai. [Q58]\nAlfalfa — Ancient Herb (Asia Native)\n● Alfalfa (Medicago sativa) = Asia se native plant, mankind ke sabse purane known herbs mein se ek — naturally\nhigh in vitamins A,C,E,K + B-vitamins, biotin, calcium, folic acid, iron, magnesium, potassium. [Q59]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 8\nAfrica mein Tea Plantations — Exist Karti Hain\n● 'Africa mein koi tea plantations NAHI hain' — yeh statement FALSE hai (A galat) — Africa mein tea pehli baar\nDurban Botanical Garden mein 1850 mein produce hui thi, WWII tak ~800 hectares land tea cultivation mein\nthi, 20th century mein Kenya/Tanzania/Uganda major tea producers ban gaye. Tea plants ko fertile soil+high\nhumus chahiye (R TRUE independently). [Q60]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Africa mein tea plantations exist karti hain (Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda major producers hain) — 'no tea\nplantations in Africa' statement galat hai. [Q60]\nPodzol Soil — Taiga Region\n● Podzol soil = ~60°N latitude ke near, Eurasia+North America ke coniferous forest (Taiga region) mein milti hai.\n[Q61]\nMocha Coffee — Yemen\n● Mocha coffee = Yemen mein grow hoti hai — Mocha seaport (jahan se export hoti thi) se naam mila. [Q62]\nTea mein Compounds — Morphine NAHI\n● Tea mein Theanine, caffeine, polyphenols, tannin, theobromine, theophylline milte hain — Morphine NAHI\nmilta (Tea originally China mein medicinal drink ke roop mein use hoti thi). [Q63]\nGreen Box — International Agriculture Agreement\n● Green Box mein economic assistance shamil hai: Agricultural Research, Fertilizer, Irrigation, Plant\nProtection (research programs, pest+disease control, training, inspection services etc.). [Q64]\nPlantation Crops — Country Correct Statements\n● Cocoa-Ghana, Coffee-Brazil, Tea-Sri Lanka, Rubber-Malaysia — sab famous plantation crop pairings hain\n(given options mein galat statement identify karna tha). [Q65]\nHeroin — Opium Resin se\n● Heroin opium resin se obtain hoti hai. [Q66]\nGolden Crescent — Afghanistan+Iran+Pakistan"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 9\n● Golden Crescent (Asia ka illicit opium production area, Central+South Asia) mein shamil: Afghanistan, Iran,\nPakistan — Iraq shamil NAHI hai. [Q67]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Golden Crescent mein Iraq shamil NAHI hai — sirf Afghanistan, Iran, Pakistan. [Q67]\nMaize — Middle Africa ka Staple Food\n● Maize/corn Middle Africa ke logo ke liye important staple food hai (vitamins A,C,E + carbohydrates + minerals\n+ protein + dietary fiber rich). [Q68]\nSacramento-San Joaquin Valley — California\n● Sacramento-San Joaquin Valley (vitreous+citrus fruit production ke liye famous) California mein hai —\nCalifornia ke Central Valley ka part. [Q69]\nCommercial Viticulture — Mediterranean Europe\n● Commercial Viticulture Mediterranean Europe ke liye specific hai (A TRUE) — ~85% grapes wine-making\nmein jaate hain (R TRUE, sahi explanation). [Q70]\n● Citrus fruits ki production Mediterranean regions mein well-developed hai (subtropical dry-summer climate\nregion). [Q71]\nHigh-Yielding Variety Seeds — Mexico (Norman Borlaug)\n● American agronomist Norman E. Borlaug ne HYV seeds pehli baar Mexico mein develop kiye. [Q72]\nCatechu — Khair Tree Wood\n● Catechu Khair tree (Acacia catechu) ki wood se obtain hota hai. [Q73]\nPeanuts/Groundnut — Main Crop aur Native Place\n● Given options mein Peanuts/Groundnut Gambia ki main crop hai — currently Ghana in options mein leading\nproducer hai; global FAO 2023 ke according China largest producer hai (excluding shelled). [Q74]\n● Groundnut ka native place Brazil (Mato Grosso aur nearby areas, South America) maana jaata hai. [Q75]\nShahtoosh — Tibetan Antelope (Chiru) Wool\n● 'Shahtoosh' (world ki most attractive, warmest, lightest wool) Tibetan antelope (Chiru) ke underfur se obtain\nhoti hai — mainly Tibetan Plateau/China mein milta hai, kuch Ladakh(India) mein bhi — CITES ke tehat\nprotected species hai, international commercial trade prohibited hai. [Q76]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 10\n● Shahtoosh shawl Tibetan Antelope (Chiru) ke hairs se banti hai — master craftsmen weave karte hain, mainly\nChina/Tibet/S.Xinjiang/W.Qinghai, kuch Ladakh(India) mein bhi. [Q77]\nApiculture, Viticulture, Olericulture — Terminology\n● Apiculture = bees ka maintenance (beekeeping) — Honey production se related. [Q78]\n● Viticulture = grapes production+study ki science hai (Latin 'vine' se) — vineyard events se deal karti hai, wine\nke liye use hone par 'viniculture' bhi kehte hain — horticulture ki ek branch hai. [Q79]\n● Given cultivation-nomenclature mismatches mein Vegetable cultivation ko 'Olericulture' kehte hain,\n'Horticulture' NAHI — baaki correctly matched hain. [Q80]\nSilk Production — China #1, India #2\n● FAO 2023 ke according raw silk production mein India ka rank 2nd hai (China ke baad). [Q81]\n● FAO 2023 ke according world ka largest raw silk producer China hai. [Q82]\nAustralia — Cattle Rearing Mainly Meat ke liye\n● Australia mein cattle rearing meat ke liye zyada hoti hai, milk ke liye kam (A TRUE) — 2025 mein ~30.1\nmillion cattle the, jisme se sirf ~2.2 million dairy cattle the, baaki mainly beef ke liye — Australian log\ntraditionally non-vegetarian hain (R TRUE, sahi explanation) — Australia world ke major beef exporters mein\nse ek hai. [Q83]\nChina — Largest Livestock Population\n● FAO stats ke according (million): Brazil 272.69→304.15, China 847.63→829.58 (largest), India\n539.79→545.33, USA 182.53→201.69 (2007→2020) — given options mein China ki livestock population\nsabse zyada thi. [Q84]\nMad Cow Disease — Beef Image Destroyed\n● Europe+America mein beef ki 'safe+healthy food' image Mad Cow Disease ne destroy ki — 1986 mein UK mein\npehli baar outbreak hua, British beef industry badly affected hui, North America mein bhi similar incidents\ndekhe gaye. [Q85]\nMilk — India World ka Leading Producer\n● National Dairy Development Board (NDDB) ke according India world ka leading milk producer hai (247.87\nmillion tonnes, 2024-25) — per capita availability ~485 g/day. World Food+Agriculture Statistical Yearbook\n2025 (2023 data) ke according top milk-producing countries: India, USA, Pakistan, China, Brazil.\n[Q86,Q87,Q89]\nMilk Production per Cow — Denmark Highest (Given Options)"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 11\n● FAO 2020 data (Hectogram/Cow, given options mein): Denmark 100,283 (highest), Netherlands 92,556, Great\nBritain 83,690, India 17,030. [Q88]\nCorn — China 2nd Rank\n● Given options mein Corn production mein China 2nd rank pe hai (FAO 2023 data ke according leading maize\nproducers: USA, China, Brazil). [Q90]\n'Sugar Bowl of World' — Cuba\n● Cuba ko 'Sugar Bowl of World' kehte hain — sugarcane Cuba ka major produce hai, sugar processing ke liye use\nhota hai. [Q91]\nFazenda — Brazil ki Coffee Plantations\n● Fazenda = Brazil ki large coffee plantations (SE Brazil mein) — colonial period (16th-19th century) mein\nFazendas mainly northeastern region mein sugar production ke liye concentrated thi. [Q92]\nCountry — Principal Primary Export Matching\n● Chad-Petroleum, Niger-Uranium, Rwanda-Coffee, Benin-Cotton. [Q93]\nRice — India Largest Exporter\n● Pichhle 5 saal mein India world ka largest rice exporter raha hai — USDA 2026 projections: India ~24.5 million\ntonnes exports (~40% global trade), Vietnam 2nd largest exporter. [Q94]\nSaffron — Iran Largest Producer\n● 2025 ke according world ka largest saffron producer Iran hai. [Q95]\nEconomic Activity — Country Matching\n● Commercial dairy farming-Denmark, Commercial grain farming-Argentina, Commercial plantation farming-\nMalaysia, Commercial fruits production-France. [Q96]\nCocoa — Top Producers (Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana)\n● FAO 2024 ke according top 3 cocoa producers: Cote d'Ivoire, Indonesia, Ghana — Cameroon 6th major\nproducer hai. Given options mein jo desh MAJOR producer NAHI hai wahi answer hai. [Q97]\n● UPSC 2024 ke according world ke 2 largest cocoa producers: Cote d'Ivoire aur Ghana. [Q98]"," A Agriculture and Livestock\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 12\nIndia vs China — Arable Area Comparison\n● FAOSTAT 2023 ke according: India ~153.87 million hectares arable land, China ~109.02 million hectares —\nIndia ka arable area China se zyada hai (Statement 1 TRUE). [Q99]\nIndia — Cropland Area Highest (vs USA/China/Japan)\n● FAO 2023 cropland area (million hectares): India 168.32 (highest), USA 154.73, China 128.36, Japan 4.29 —\nIndia in charon countries mein sabse zyada cropland area rakhta hai; India tropical+subtropical zones dono\nmein hai, tropical monsoon location diversified cropping year-round enable karta hai. [Q100]\n'Cereal Yield' — Production per Unit Area\n● 'Cereal Yield' ka matlab cereal crops ki production per unit area of harvested land hai (kg/hectare mein\nexpress hota hai) — total country production ka matlab NAHI (Statement 1 correct, Statement 2 galat) —\nwheat, rice, maize, barley, oats, rye, millets, sorghum, buckwheat, mixed grains isme measure hote hain.\n[Q101]\nCrop Rotation — Soil Nutrient Replenishment\n● Alternate seasons mein different crops grow karna soil nutrients replenish karta hai (crop diversification/rotation)\n— same field mein few years ya 1-year interval baad crop dobara grow ho sakti hai (Assumption I implicit\nNAHI hai). [Q102]\nMediterranean Agriculture — Region Coverage\n● Mediterranean climate ~30°-40°/45° latitude (dono taraf) mein hai, mainly continents ke western parts —\nMediterranean Sea ke around: Spain, Portugal, France, S.Italy, Greece, W.Turkiye, Syria, W.Israel, N.Africa —\ngiven options mein jo area is list mein NAHI aata wahi answer hai. [Q103]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0157","t":"48 B The Minerals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n B The Minerals — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 48_B_The_Minerals\nTopic Index\n1. Coal — Sedimentary Rock aur Fossil Fuel\n2. Coal — China Leading Producer, Regional Facts\n3. Coal Fields — Country Matching\n4. Hard Coal Reserve — China (Historical 1995 Context)\n5. Ukraine — Largest Coal Centre Donets/Donbas Basin\n6. World Coal Production — China+USA Combined\n7. Ruhr Basin — Germany's Industrial Region\n8. Coal Reserves — China Largest (Given Options)\n9. Rukwa Lake Region (Tanzania) — Gemstones\n10. Lorraine — France ka Coalfield (Germany ka NAHI)\n11. Kuzbass Region (Russia) — Coal Production\n12. Earth's Womb — 2nd Most Common Metal\n13. Iron Ore Producers — Descending Order (2008 Context)\n14. Gold Production 2023 — China Leading\n15. Iron Ore — Largest Producer (Question Period: China, Currently: Australia)\n16. Marquette Range (USA) — Iron Ore\n17. Iron Ore — India (Given Options)\n18. Pig Iron Production Europe — France 4th\n19. Iron Ore Region — Country Matching\n20. Ghana+Brazil Gold — Continental Drift Connection\n21. Iron-Ore Producing Areas — Country Matching\n22. Lorraine Region (France) — Iron Ore\n23. Lake Superior Region — Iron Ore Reserves\n24. 'Rust Bowl'/'Rust Belt' — USA ka NE Iron Region\n25. Great Lakes Region — USA+Canada Shared\n26. Iron Ore — Top 3 Producers (China, Brazil, Australia)\n27. Mount Newman (Australia) — Iron Ore\n28. Minas Gerais (Brazil) — Iron Ore + Other Minerals\n29. Copper Ore — Chile Largest Producer (2023)\n30. Chile — Copper aur Porphyry Deposits\n31. Zambia — Copper Reserves lekin Landlocked Problem\n32. Japan — Copper mein Self-Sufficient\n33. Africa — Largest Copper Producer (Zambia Historical, DR Congo Current)\n34. Chiquicamata (Chile) — Copper\n35. Gold Production 2023 — China Highest (kg)\n36. Kalgoorlie aur Coolgardie (Australia) — Gold Mines\n37. Johannesburg — Gold+Diamond Mining\n38. India ko Gold Export — Switzerland Largest (2025)\n39. Asia's Biggest Gold Market — China (Shanghai Gold Exchange)"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n40. Silver — Mexico Largest Producer (2023)\n41. German Silver — Actually Copper Alloy (Silver NAHI)\n42. Bauxite — Aluminium ka Ore (Iron ka NAHI)\n43. Aluminium — China Largest Producer\n44. Tin — Placer Deposits (~80% World Tin)\n45. Tin — Leading Producer (Indonesia, Given Options)\n46. Kinta Valley (Malaysia) — Tin Production\n47. Petroleum Production — Ascending Order (1998 Context)\n48. Alaska — Oil Producing State, 1867 Purchase\n49. Petroleum — Top 3 Producers (Descending, Disputed)\n50. Largest Petroleum Producer — Russia (Historical Exam Context)\n51. Middle East Petroleum — Sequence Disputed (UAE Missing)\n52. Petroleum Production — Statements (1998 Context)\n53. Southeast Asia — Indonesia Largest Petroleum Producer\n54. Venezuela — Petroleum-Dominated Economy\n55. Mineral Oil Reserves — Venezuela Largest (2024)\n56. Largest Petroleum Reserves — Saudi Arabia (2006 Historical)\n57. West Asia — Saudi Arabia Highest Petroleum Producer\n58. Gasohol — USA Largest Producer+Consumer\n59. Brent Crude Oil — North Sea Classification\n60. 'Peace Pipeline' — Iran-Pakistan Gas Pipeline\n61. SUMED Pipeline — Red Sea se Mediterranean\n62. Romania — 1857 Commercial Oil Drilling\n63. Biofuel Feedstocks — Lentil Exception\n64. Crude Oil to India (2017-18) — Iraq Highest Supplier\n65. Ras Tanura Oil Refinery — Saudi Arabia\n66. Kuwait — Kashagan Galat Pairing (Actually Kazakhstan)\n67. Crude Oil — USA #1, Russia #2 (2023)\n68. Pegu Yoma (Myanmar) — Mineral Oil\n69. Uranium — Kazakhstan Largest Producer (2023)\n70. Uranium — Largest Reserves Australia (2023)\n71. Uranium City — Canada (Saskatchewan)\n72. Radium — Pitchblende (Uranium Ore) se\n73. Uranium Ore Deposits — Canada (Given Options)\n74. Uranium — Kazakhstan (Confirmed Repeat)\n75. Russia's Major Resources — Uranium Exception (Older Question)\n76. Seabed Mining Licenses — UN's International Seabed Authority\n77. Postmasburg (South Africa) — Manganese\n78. Natural Camphor — Trees se (Rocks/Sediments se NAHI)\n79. Non-Ferrous Metals — Aluminium, Copper, Zinc etc.\n80. Mineral-Producing Region Matching (Multiple Sets)\n81. Iron Ore/Petroleum/Copper/Uranium — Location Matching\n82. Copper — Arizona (USA)\n83. Kimberley/Witwatersrand/Katanga/Saar/Butte — Mineral Matching\n84. Afghanistan — Lithium Discovery ($1 Trillion)\n85. Titanium — China Leading Producer (Cited Exam)\n86. Bauxite — Australia (Historical), Guinea (Current)"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n87. Chile — Nitrate Fame\n88. Nitrate — Chile (Peru NAHI)\n89. Rare Earth Metals — China Export Restrictions\n90. Diamond — Russia Largest Producer (2023)\n91. Botswana-Diamond, Chile-Lithium, Indonesia-Nickel\n92. Commercial Energy Sources\n93. Iodine — Chile Leading Producer\n94. Silver/Mica/Iron Ore/Copper — Country Matching\n95. Mineral-Ore Matching — Cinnabar (Mercury)\n96. Africa — Zambia Highest Copper (Historical), DR Congo Current\n97. Cobalt — DR Congo ~3/4th World Production\nCoal — Sedimentary Rock aur Fossil Fuel\n● Coal = Sedimentary rock ka example hai (organic sedimentary rock, plant material se\naccumulated+buried+compacted, layered sequences mein milta hai — slate/marble metamorphic hain,\nsedimentary nahi). [Q1]\n● Coal, Crude Oil, Natural Gas = Fossil Fuels kehlate hain (millions years mein dead organisms se bane). [Q2]\nCoal — China Leading Producer, Regional Facts\n● China world ka leading coal producer hai (Statement I TRUE) — Donetsk Basin (Ukraine) major coal-producing\nregion hai (Statement II TRUE) — Saar Region (Germany) important coal deposits rakhta hai (Statement III\nTRUE) — Appalachian region USA ke major coal-mining areas mein se ek hai. [Q3]\n● 'Donbass' region coal production ke liye famous hai — Donetsk Basin ka doosra naam hai, Ukraine mein hai.\n[Q4]\nCoal Fields — Country Matching\n● Donetsk-Ukraine, Kuznetsk-Russia, Lancashire-U.K., Saar-Germany. [Q5]\n● Appalachian-USA, Lancashire-England(UK), Ruhr-Germany, Kuzbass-Russia. [Q6]\nHard Coal Reserve — China (Historical 1995 Context)\n● 1995 PYQ ke according Hard Coal reserve mein leading country China thi — modern datasets mein USA China\nse aage hai (rankings time ke saath change hote hain). [Q7]\nUkraine — Largest Coal Centre Donets/Donbas Basin\n● Ukraine ka largest coal-producing centre Donets Basin (Donbas region) hai — other regions: Lviv-Volhynian\nbasin, Dnieper brown coal basin. [Q8]\nWorld Coal Production — China+USA Combined"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Historical exam-data ke according world ke coal production ka >50% China aur USA combined se aata tha.\n[Q9]\nRuhr Basin — Germany's Industrial Region\n● Ruhr Basin (Ruhr river ke around, Western Germany) = famous industrial region — important coal\nmines+industrial areas yahan hain. [Q10]\n● Ruhr coalfield (Rhine ke west, Lippe ke north) Germany mein hai — Germany ka bulk bituminous coal yahin\nse aata hai, steel production+diversified chemicals bhi basic industries hain. [Q11]\nCoal Reserves — China Largest (Given Options)\n● Given options mein China largest coal reservoir+producer hai — top 3 global coal reserves: USA, Russia, China.\n[Q12]\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 ke according 2023 mein China coal production mein #1 rank pe hai. [Q13]\nRukwa Lake Region (Tanzania) — Gemstones\n● Rukwa lake region (Tanzania) gemstones (Emerald, Moonstone, Aquamarine, Amethyst, Ruby, Topaz) ke\nliye famous hai — kuch coal layers bhi milte hain, mining bhi hui hai. [Q14]\nLorraine — France ka Coalfield (Germany ka NAHI)\n● Ruhr Valley, Saar Basin, Achen Basin — sab Germany ke coalfields hain — Lorraine actually NE France ka\ncultural+historical region hai, Germany ka coalfield NAHI. [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Lorraine France mein hai, Germany ka coalfield NAHI. [Q15]\nKuzbass Region (Russia) — Coal Production\n● Kuzbass region mainly coal production ke liye famous hai (Statement 1: coal+iron ore rich, TRUE) — ~1200\ntypes industrial products (coal, coke, rolled steel, cast-iron, aluminium, zinc, ferroalloys) export karta hai —\nKemerovo region West Siberia ke SE mein hai. [Q16]\nEarth's Womb — 2nd Most Common Metal\n● Earth ke womb (core) mein sabse common metal Iron hai, phir Nickel, phir Aluminium (Earth's crust mein order\nalag hai: Aluminium #1, Iron #2) — is question ka context Earth's womb hai, isliye Nickel 2nd most common,\nanswer Aluminium (given options context ke according). [Q17]\nIron Ore Producers — Descending Order (2008 Context)"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\n● 2008 exam-context ke according descending order: China, Brazil, Australia, Sweden — later data mein\nAustralia+Brazil top pe aa gaye hain (order significantly different). [Q18]\nGold Production 2023 — China Leading\n● 2023 mein world ka largest gold producer (mine production) China tha — Russia aur Australia bhi leading\nproducers mein the (2024 mein bhi China #1 raha, US Mineral Commodity Summaries 2025 ke according).\n[Q19]\nIron Ore — Largest Producer (Question Period: China, Currently: Australia)\n● Question period ke according China largest iron ore producer tha — currently (2023) Australia largest producer\nhai. [Q20]\nMarquette Range (USA) — Iron Ore\n● 'Marquette Range' (Michigan, USA — Marquette County ke around) Iron Ore ke liye famous hai. [Q21]\nIron Ore — India (Given Options)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 ke according largest iron ore producers: Australia, Brazil, India, China\n(respectively) — given options mein India 1st position pe hai (baaki 3 options mein nahi the). [Q22]\nPig Iron Production Europe — France 4th\n● Exam-period ranking ke according Europe ke pig-iron producers mein France 4th position pe tha. [Q23]\nIron Ore Region — Country Matching\n● Lorraine-France, Midland-U.K., Kiruna-Sweden, Kostanay-Kazakhstan. [Q24]\nGhana+Brazil Gold — Continental Drift Connection\n● Ghana coast pe rich placer gold deposits hain, Brazil mein gold-bearing veins hain (A TRUE) — dono continents\nkabhi Atlantic coast ke along joined the (R TRUE, sahi explanation — continental drift theory ke according).\n[Q25]\nIron-Ore Producing Areas — Country Matching\n● Kazakhstan-Karaganda, Ukraine-Krivoy Rog, France-Normandy, France-Pyrenees (dono French regions) —\ngiven options mein jo galat pairing hai wahi answer hai. [Q26]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\nLorraine Region (France) — Iron Ore\n● Lorraine Region (France) famous hai — iron-ore associations: Kazakhstan-Karaganda, Ukraine-Krivoy Rog,\nFrance-Normandy+Pyrenees. [Q27]\nLake Superior Region — Iron Ore Reserves\n● Lake Superior region (North America) Iron ore reserves ke liye famous hai. [Q28]\n'Rust Bowl'/'Rust Belt' — USA ka NE Iron Region\n● 'Rust Bowl'/'Rust Belt' = USA ka Northeastern region hai — iron producing economic region hai,\nIllinois/Indiana/Michigan/Ohio/Pennsylvania shamil, Great Lakes+Pittsburgh region bhi shamil. [Q29]\nGreat Lakes Region — USA+Canada Shared\n● Great Lakes region Canada aur USA dono ke beech shared hai — US 8 states (Illinois, Indiana, Michigan,\nMinnesota, New York, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin), Canadian province Ontario. [Q30]\nIron Ore — Top 3 Producers (China, Brazil, Australia)\n● Cited exam ke according top 3 iron ore producers: China, Brazil, Australia. [Q31]\nMount Newman (Australia) — Iron Ore\n● Mount Newman Mining (Australia) iron ore extraction ke liye famous hai. [Q32]\nMinas Gerais (Brazil) — Iron Ore + Other Minerals\n● Minas Gerais (SE Brazil) high-quality iron ore ke liye famous hai — manganese, tin, silver, zinc bhi mine hote\nhain, valuable+semi-precious stones bhi milte hain. [Q33]\nCopper Ore — Chile Largest Producer (2023)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 ke according 2023 mein Chile largest copper-ore producer tha — DR Congo\n2nd, Peru 3rd. [Q34]\n● Given options mein leading copper producer China hai. [Q35]\nChile — Copper aur Porphyry Deposits\n● Chile prominent copper producer hai (A TRUE) — Chile ke paas world ke largest porphyry copper deposits hain\n(R TRUE, sahi explanation) — 2023 mein Chile ~5.37 million tonnes copper produce kiya, Central Andes\nmein major porphyry-copper deposits hain. [Q36,Q37]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 7\nZambia — Copper Reserves lekin Landlocked Problem\n● Zambia (landlocked, Southern Africa) mein prolific copper reserves hain (Zambia se Katanga/DR Congo tak\ncopper belt) — economic progress sea routes ki absence ki wajah se limited hai (exports ke chances khatam ho\njaate hain). [Q38]\nJapan — Copper mein Self-Sufficient\n● Japan copper mein almost self-sufficient hai (consume se zyada produce karta hai) — bauxite, iron ore, mineral\noil mein self-reliant NAHI hai. [Q39]\nAfrica — Largest Copper Producer (Zambia Historical, DR Congo Current)\n● Indian Bureau of Mines ke according historical period mein Zambia Africa ka largest copper producer tha —\nWorld Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023 data) ke according currently DR Congo largest hai. [Q40]\nChiquicamata (Chile) — Copper\n● Chiquicamata (Chile) worldwide copper mineral ke liye famous hai. [Q41]\nGold Production 2023 — China Highest (kg)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 ke according 2023 gold production (kg): China 375,155 (highest), Australia\n306,320, Russia 302,000, Canada 296,053. [Q42]\n● 2008 historical context ke according gold production descending order: (dataset mein China involved thi, exact\nPYQ order retained) — rankings changed hain since then (Russia, Australia, Canada, USA bhi prominent hain\ncurrently). [Q43]\nKalgoorlie aur Coolgardie (Australia) — Gold Mines\n● Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 ke according world ki maximum gold reserves Australia mein hain —\nKalgoorlie aur Coolgardie important gold mines hain, Western Australia province mein hain.\n[Q44,Q45,Q46]\nJohannesburg — Gold+Diamond Mining\n● Johannesburg (South Africa ka largest city, Gauteng Province ki capital) gold+diamond mining ke liye famous\nhai. [Q47]\nIndia ko Gold Export — Switzerland Largest (2025)\n● 2025 projections ke according Switzerland India ko gold ka largest exporter hoga. [Q48]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 8\nAsia's Biggest Gold Market — China (Shanghai Gold Exchange)\n● Older exam ke according Asia's biggest gold market China (option mein Beijing likha tha) — actually Shanghai\nGold Exchange major gold-trading market hai. [Q49]\nSilver — Mexico Largest Producer (2023)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023, kg metal content): Mexico 7,277,840 (largest), China 3,399,600, Peru\n3,040,137, Russia 1,536,000, Poland 1,532,000. [Q50]\n● 2023 data ke according Mexico world ka largest silver producer hai. [Q51]\nGerman Silver — Actually Copper Alloy (Silver NAHI)\n● 'German Silver' (Nickel Silver/Maillechort/Alpacca) mein silver NAHI hota — actually copper alloy with\nnickel+zinc hai (usual: 60% copper, 20% nickel, 20% zinc; NCERT: Cu 25-30%, Zn 25-30%, Ni 4-50%).\n[Q52]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• 'German Silver' naam ke bawajood isme silver bilkul NAHI hota — yeh copper-nickel-zinc alloy hai. [Q52]\nBauxite — Aluminium ka Ore (Iron ka NAHI)\n● Haematite, Magnetite, Limonite = Iron ores hain — Bauxite Aluminium ka ore hai (yeh different hai baaki\nteeno se). [Q53,Q54]\nAluminium — China Largest Producer\n● World ka maximum/largest aluminium producer China hai. [Q55,Q56]\nTin — Placer Deposits (~80% World Tin)\n● World ka ~80% Tin placer deposits mein milta hai (heavy minerals ka natural concentration, gravity effect se)\n— riverbeds/valleys/sea floor ke near, SE Asia mein spread. [Q57]\nTin — Leading Producer (Indonesia, Given Options)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according major tin producers: China, Indonesia, Myanmar, Peru,\nBrazil — given options mein (China absent) Indonesia correct answer hai. [Q58]\nKinta Valley (Malaysia) — Tin Production\n● Malaysia ka 'Kinta Valley' Tin production ke liye famous hai. [Q59]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 9\nPetroleum Production — Ascending Order (1998 Context)\n● 1998 exam-accepted ascending order: Iran, Iraq, Russia, U.S.A., Saudi Arabia. [Q60]\nAlaska — Oil Producing State, 1867 Purchase\n● Alaska = USA ka oil producing state hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — 1867 mein Russia se purchase kiya gaya tha\n(Statement 2 TRUE). [Q61]\nPetroleum — Top 3 Producers (Descending, Disputed)\n● Recent World Mineral Production data ke according top 3 descending order: USA, Russia, Saudi Arabia —\ngiven 4 options mein se koi bhi is exact sequence se match nahi karta, isliye question disputed (*) hai. [Q62]\nLargest Petroleum Producer — Russia (Historical Exam Context)\n● Exam-period data ke according world ka largest petroleum producer Russia tha (current rankings different hain,\nab USA #1 hai). [Q63]\nMiddle East Petroleum — Sequence Disputed (UAE Missing)\n● Recent data ke according Middle East descending order: Saudi Arabia, Iran, Iraq, UAE — UAE (Kuwait\nNAHI) 4th position pe hai jo given options mein absent hai, isliye koi option exact match nahi karta — question\ndisputed (*) hai. [Q64]\nPetroleum Production — Statements (1998 Context)\n● 1998 exam ke according teeno statements TRUE maane gaye: 60% world petroleum deposits Middle East\nmein, Alaska reserve Texas ke barabar certified, USA prominent producer (historical context). [Q65]\nSoutheast Asia — Indonesia Largest Petroleum Producer\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according SE Asia ka largest petroleum producer Indonesia hai —\nSumatra, Java, Kalimantan important producing regions hain. [Q66]\nVenezuela — Petroleum-Dominated Economy\n● Venezuela leading petroleum producing countries mein se ek hai — economy petroleum sector se dominated hai,\n2025 mein oil exports >80% total export revenue generate karti hain. [Q67]\nMineral Oil Reserves — Venezuela Largest (2024)"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 10\n● World Population Review 2024 ke according largest proved crude oil deposits: Venezuela (303.2 Billion\nBarrels, largest), Saudi Arabia (267.2 Billion Barrels, 2nd). [Q68,Q69]\nLargest Petroleum Reserves — Saudi Arabia (2006 Historical)\n● 2006 PYQ ke according Saudi Arabia largest reserves rakhta tha — baad ke estimates mein Venezuela aage\nnikal gaya (reserve rankings time-sensitive hoti hain). [Q70]\n● 2024 data ke according top 3 largest crude oil reserves: Venezuela, Saudi Arabia, Iran. [Q71]\nWest Asia — Saudi Arabia Highest Petroleum Producer\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according West Asia ka highest petroleum producer Saudi Arabia\nhai — world mein 3rd largest (USA aur Russia ke baad). [Q72]\nGasohol — USA Largest Producer+Consumer\n● Gasohol = unleaded gasoline(90%) + ethanol(10%) ka mixture hai — currently (2024) USA top\nproducer+consumer hai. [Q73]\nBrent Crude Oil — North Sea Classification\n● Brent Crude = major crude oil classification hai (global oil-price benchmark, Statement 1 TRUE) — North Sea\nse sourced hai (Brent, Forties, Oseberg, Ekofisk grades, Statement 2 TRUE) — sulphur-free NAHI hai\n(comparatively low sulphur content, sulphur bilkul absent nahi, Statement 3 galat). [Q74]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Brent Crude sulphur-free NAHI hai — comparatively low sulphur content hoti hai, bilkul zero nahi. [Q74]\n'Peace Pipeline' — Iran-Pakistan Gas Pipeline\n● 2009 ki 'Peace Pipeline' deal Iran-Pakistan gas pipeline (IP gas pipeline) ko refer karti hai. [Q75]\nSUMED Pipeline — Red Sea se Mediterranean\n● Suez Canal+SUMED pipeline Persian Gulf crude oil+LNG shipments ke liye Europe tak strategic chokepoints\nhain (Statement I TRUE) — SUMED pipeline Ain Sokhna terminal (Gulf of Suez, Red Sea) se Sidi Kerir port\n(Mediterranean) tak jaati hai (Statement II TRUE). [Q76]\nRomania — 1857 Commercial Oil Drilling\n● Romania mein 1857 mein mineral oil commercially drilled hui thi (275 tonnes production officially registered,\ninternational statistics ke according) — world ki pehli commercial oil well. [Q77]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 11\nBiofuel Feedstocks — Lentil Exception\n● Sugar beet aur wheat biofuel/bioethanol feedstock ke roop mein use hote hain — Lentil standard commercial\nbiofuel feedstock NAHI hai (given option group mein anup\n\nयुक्तhai). [Q78]\nCrude Oil to India (2017-18) — Iraq Highest Supplier\n● 2017-18 mein India ko crude oil ka highest supplier Iraq tha (Saudi Arabia earlier periods mein leading supplier\ntha, ab Russia largest supplier ban gaya hai — question specifically 2017-18 pooch raha hai). [Q79]\nRas Tanura Oil Refinery — Saudi Arabia\n● Ras Tanura (Persian Gulf coast ki sabse purani refineries mein se ek, Jubail industrial port city ke near) Saudi\nArabia mein hai — 1945 mein start hui thi. [Q80]\nKuwait — Kashagan Galat Pairing (Actually Kazakhstan)\n● Kashagan actually Kazakhstan ka major oil+gas field hai — 'Kuwait-Kashagan' pairing GALAT hai, baaki\ncountry-oilfield pairs correctly matched hain. [Q81]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Kashagan oil field Kazakhstan mein hai, Kuwait mein NAHI. [Q81]\nCrude Oil — USA #1, Russia #2 (2023)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according USA largest crude oil producer tha, Russia doosre\nnumber pe (USA ke alawa largest producer). [Q82]\nPegu Yoma (Myanmar) — Mineral Oil\n● Pegu Range/Yoma (Irrawaddy+Sittaung rivers ke beech low mountains, Myanmar) mein Mineral Oil important\nmineral hai — oil, natural gas, coal Myanmar ke natural resources mein prominent hain. [Q83]\nUranium — Kazakhstan Largest Producer (2023)\n● World Minerals Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according Uranium ka largest producer Kazakhstan hai —\nCanada 2nd, Namibia 3rd (2009 se pehle Canada leading producer tha). [Q84,Q85]\n● Given options mein Atomic Minerals ka biggest producer Kazakhstan hai (Canada NAHI). [Q86]\nUranium — Largest Reserves Australia (2023)\n● Australia ke Uranium reserves world ke largest hain (2023) — Olympic Dam Mine (South Australia) mein\nlocated. [Q87]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 12\nUranium City — Canada (Saskatchewan)\n● 'Uranium City' (Saskatchewan, Canada) establish karne ka credit Canada ko jaata hai — Lake Athabasca ke\nnorth shore ke near located hai. [Q88]\nRadium — Pitchblende (Uranium Ore) se\n● Radium (radioactive element, symbol Ra) Uranium ore Pitchblende se extract hota hai. [Q89]\nUranium Ore Deposits — Canada (Given Options)\n● Given options mein important uranium ore deposits ke liye known desh Canada hai — currently (2023)\nAustralia biggest reserve rakhta hai. [Q90]\nUranium — Kazakhstan (Confirmed Repeat)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according world ka largest uranium producer Kazakhstan hai.\n[Q91]\nRussia's Major Resources — Uranium Exception (Older Question)\n● Russia ke major resources: iron ore, manganese, chromium, nickel, platinum, titanium, copper, tin, lead, tungsten,\ndiamonds, phosphates, gold — older exam ke according Uranium major resources list mein NAHI tha (though\nRussia uranium bhi produce karta hai — yeh classification purani exam-specific hai). [Q92]\nSeabed Mining Licenses — UN's International Seabed Authority\n● International waters mein seabed exploration+mining licenses UN's International Seabed Authority grant karta\nhai (Global Ocean Commission NAHI) — 2014 mein India, Brazil, Singapore jaise countries ki public+private\ncompanies ko license diye gaye — Rare earth minerals seabed pe present hain. [Q93]\nPostmasburg (South Africa) — Manganese\n● Postmasburg aur adjacent areas (South Africa) Manganese ka major producer hai. [Q94]\nNatural Camphor — Trees se (Rocks/Sediments se NAHI)\n● Natural camphor camphor-bearing trees se obtain hoti hai (rocks/waterfall foam/marine sediments se NAHI) —\nCinnamomum camphora (E.Asia, China+Japan native) traditional source hai, kuch Blumea species bhi\nbotanical source hain. [Q95]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 13\nNon-Ferrous Metals — Aluminium, Copper, Zinc etc.\n● Non-ferrous metals (negligible iron content): Aluminium, Copper, Zinc, Tin, Titanium, Lead, Nickel — Gold,\nSilver, Cobalt, Gallium, Beryllium, Cerium, Tungsten, Mercury, Platinum, Zirconium, Cadmium bhi is category\nmein aate hain. [Q96]\nMineral-Producing Region Matching (Multiple Sets)\n● Coal-Karaganda Basin, Gold-Highveld, Iron Ore-Krivoi Rog, Mineral Oil-San Joaquin Valley. [Q97]\n● Mineral Oil-Venezuela, Copper-Zambia, Manganese-Gabon, Bauxite-Guyana. [Q98]\n● Correct: Donbas Basin-Coal, Mosul-Mineral oil, Transvaal-Gold — Mesabi Range-Iron ore correctly matched\nhai (given options mein galat kisi aur pair mein tha). [Q99]\nIron Ore/Petroleum/Copper/Uranium — Location Matching\n● Iron ore-Mesabi, Petroleum-Baku, Copper-Bingham, Uranium-Port Radium. [Q100]\n● Port Radium (Great Bear Lake, Canada ka east shore) = Uranium reserves ke liye world-famous — Bingham\nCanyon Mine (Salt Lake City, Utah, USA) Copper production ke liye famous. [Q100]\n● Baku (Azerbaijan ki capital+largest city) Petroleum ke liye famous hai. [Q101]\n● 'Mesabi Range' international level pe Iron Ore production ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q102]\nCopper — Arizona (USA)\n● Correctly matched pair: Copper-Arizona (USA) — baaki given options galat matched the. [Q103]\nKimberley/Witwatersrand/Katanga/Saar/Butte — Mineral Matching\n● Kimberley-Diamond, Witwatersrand-Gold, Katanga-Copper, Saar-Coal, Butte-Silver. [Q104,Q105]\nAfghanistan — Lithium Discovery ($1 Trillion)\n● Afghanistan mein $1 trillion worth mineral reserves discovery Lithium ki thi — isse Iran ke oil field discovery se\ncompare kiya gaya. [Q106]\nTitanium — China Leading Producer (Cited Exam)\n● Cited exam ke according Titanium ka leading producer China tha (Japan NAHI). [Q107]\nBauxite — Australia (Historical), Guinea (Current)\n● Cited exam data ke according bauxite ka biggest producer Australia tha. [Q108]\n● Current USGS data ke according Guinea world ka leading bauxite producer hai (~1/3rd global output) —\nAustralia doosre number pe hai. [Q109]"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 14\nChile — Nitrate Fame\n● Chile ko Nitrate mineral se fame mili hai — Atacama Desert (N.Chile+S.Peru) mein nitrate ka largest source hai.\n[Q110]\nNitrate — Chile (Peru NAHI)\n● Bolivia-Tin, Brazil-Iron ore, Mexico-Silver correct hain — Nitrate historically Chile se associated hai, Peru se\nNAHI (galat pairing given options mein). [Q111,Q112]\nRare Earth Metals — China Export Restrictions\n● Rare earth elements (17 chemically related elements, electronics+magnets+clean-energy+defence mein use) ki\nshort supply ka reason: China (largest producer) ne export restrictions imposed ki hain (Statement 1 TRUE)\n— Australia jaise doosre countries economically viable production abhi NAHI kar paate (Statement 2 galat).\n[Q113]\nDiamond — Russia Largest Producer (2023)\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023, carats): Russia 37,316,754 (largest), Botswana 25,095,000, Canada\n16,160,688, Angola 9,754,310, DR Congo 8,306,000. [Q114]\nBotswana-Diamond, Chile-Lithium, Indonesia-Nickel\n● Botswana diamond-rich hai (production+economy contribution) — Chile global lithium reserves mein leader hai\n— Indonesia nickel reserves+production mein world ka largest stakeholder hai. [Q115]\nCommercial Energy Sources\n● Commercial sources of energy: Power, Coal, Oil, Gas, Hydro-electricity, Uranium. [Q116]\nIodine — Chile Leading Producer\n● World Mineral Production 2019-23 (2023) ke according world ka leading iodine producer Chile hai — iodine\ncaliche ore, brines, seaweed se extract hota hai. [Q117]\nSilver/Mica/Iron Ore/Copper — Country Matching\n● Silver-Mexico, Mica-India, Iron Ore-Russian Federation, Copper-Chile. [Q118]\nMineral-Ore Matching — Cinnabar (Mercury)"," B The Minerals\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 15\n● Aluminium-Bauxite, Copper-Cuprite, Zinc-Calamine, Iron-Haematite correct hain — Cinnabar actually\nMercury ka most common source ore hai (given options mein galat pairing thi). [Q119]\nAfrica — Zambia Highest Copper (Historical), DR Congo Current\n● Exam-period data ke according Africa ka leading copper producer Zambia tha — currently DR Congo aage hai.\n[Q120]\nCobalt — DR Congo ~3/4th World Production\n● Cobalt (electric vehicle batteries ke liye zaroori metal) ka world production ka ~3/4th DR Congo se aata hai\n(USGS ke according) — lithium-ion battery chemistries + electronics mein important input hai. [Q121]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0158","t":"48.c Industries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n C Industries — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 48_C_Industries\nTopic Index\n1. Iron-Steel Centres — Country Matching\n2. Industrial Centres — Industry Matching\n3. Birmingham — Iron & Steel (Shipbuilding NAHI)\n4. Houston — Oil/Gas (Automobile NAHI)\n5. World Industrial Cities — Master Reference List\n6. Osaka — Cotton Textile ka Important Centre\n7. Osaka — Cotton Textile (Repeat Confirmations)\n8. Anshan/Glasgow/Ottawa/Sheffield — Industry Matching\n9. Camden — Shipbuilding (Florida NAHI)\n10. Coal Fields — Location Matching\n11. Industrial Regions — Country Matching\n12. Mesabi Range — Iron Ore (Coal NAHI)\n13. Industrial Regions — Country Matching (More Sets)\n14. World's Biggest Wool Producer — China\n15. Wuppertal — Germany's Wool Production Centre\n16. Cotton Textiles — Leading Producer China\n17. Footloose Industry — Software\n18. Electronics Industry — Raw Material Availability Primary NAHI\n19. 'Bowl of Sugar' — Cuba (Historical), Brazil (Current)\n20. Japan — Leading Industrial Country ka Reason\n21. Scotland Industrial Area — UK (Sweden NAHI)\n22. Sugar Industry By-products — Bagasse, Molasses\n23. Paper Pulp — Poplar Wood\n24. Mediterranean Forest — Trees\n25. Japan — Market-Based Iron/Steel Industry Location\n26. Japan — Market-Based Steel Industry\n27. Japan Industry — Facts (Osaka, Kamaishi, Kyushu)\n28. London — Largest Metal Trading Centre\n29. Detroit — Automobile (Cotton Textiles NAHI)\n30. Gornaya Shoria — Iron Ore Reserve (Cotton Textile NAHI)\n31. Umland — Term Meaning\n32. 'Megalopolis' Term — Jean Gottmann (Popularizer)\n33. Aberdeen — Europe ki Oil Capital\n34. Industrial Regions — Country Matching (Correct Set)\n35. The Midlands — England ka Region (USA ka NAHI)\nIron-Steel Centres — Country Matching\n● Hamilton-Canada, Birmingham-U.K., Essen-Germany, Anshan-China. [Q1]"," C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nIndustrial Centres — Industry Matching\n● Pittsburg-Iron&Steel, Shanghai-Cotton Textile, Dundee-Jute Textile, Leningrad-Shipbuilding. [Q2]\n● Salem-Iron&Steel, Los Angeles-Aircraft, Abadan-Oil Refinery, Nagoya-Cotton Textile. [Q3]\n● Osaka-Cotton Textile, Detroit-Automobile, Cuba-Cigar, St.Petersburg-Shipbuilding. [Q6]\n● Anshan-Iron&Steel, Havana-Cigar, Detroit-Automobile, Nagoya-Cotton Textile. [Q7]\nBirmingham — Iron & Steel (Shipbuilding NAHI)\n● Correct: Detroit-Automobiles, Magnitogorsk-Iron&Steel, Johannesburg-Gold Mining — Birmingham-\nShipbuilding GALAT hai (Birmingham actually Iron&Steel industry ke liye famous hai, shipbuilding ke liye\nnahi). [Q4]\nHouston — Oil/Gas (Automobile NAHI)\n● Correct: Osaka-Textile, Yokohama-Shipbuilding, Pittsburgh-Iron&Steel — Houston-Automobile GALAT hai\n(Houston actually Oil+Natural Gas ke liye famous hai) — Automobile ka major city Detroit hai. [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Houston Oil aur Natural Gas ke liye famous hai, Automobile ke liye NAHI (Automobile = Detroit) —\nBirmingham Iron&Steel ke liye famous hai, Shipbuilding ke liye NAHI. [Q4,Q5]\nWorld Industrial Cities — Master Reference List\n● Anshan(China)-Iron&Steel, Havana(Cuba)-Cigar, Detroit(USA)-Automobile, Nagoya(Japan)-Cotton Textile,\nChelyabinsk(Russia)-Metallurgy+Military machinery, Milan(Italy)-Silk Textile, Moscow(Russia)-\nMetal+Chemical+Machinery, Osaka(Japan)-Cotton Textile, Sheffield(UK)-Cutlery, Venice(Italy)-Glass,\nGlasgow(Scotland,UK)-Shipbuilding, Ottawa(Canada)-Papermaking. [Q8,Q9]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Chelyabinsk Metallurgy+Military machinery ke liye hai, Shipbuilding ke liye NAHI — Moscow\nMetal+Chemical+Machinery ke liye hai, Shipbuilding ke liye NAHI (Shipbuilding actually Glasgow hai).\n[Q8,Q9]\nOsaka — Cotton Textile ka Important Centre\n● Osaka (Japan's Honshu island ka port+commercial city) = Cotton Textile industry ka important centre hai.\n[Q10]\nOsaka — Cotton Textile (Repeat Confirmations)\n● Osaka (Japan, Honshu island port+commercial city) = Cotton Textile industry ka important centre — is fact ko\nmultiple questions confirm karte hain. [Q11,Q12]"," C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nAnshan/Glasgow/Ottawa/Sheffield — Industry Matching\n● Anshan-Iron&Steel, Glasgow-Shipbuilding, Ottawa-Paper, Sheffield-Cutlery. [Q12]\nCamden — Shipbuilding (Florida NAHI)\n● Given shipbuilding centres (USA states) mein Camden actually New Jersey mein hai, Florida mein NAHI —\nyeh galat pairing hai, baaki sab correctly matched hain. [Q13]\nCoal Fields — Location Matching\n● Kuzbas-Russia, Red Basin-China, Bristol-United Kingdom, New South Wales-Australia. [Q14]\nIndustrial Regions — Country Matching\n● Kinki-Japan, Canton-China, Lorraine-France, Belo Horizonte-Brazil. [Q15]\nMesabi Range — Iron Ore (Coal NAHI)\n● Given options mein Mesabi Range iron ore field ke liye famous hai, coal region ke liye NAHI — baaki pairs\ncorrectly matched hain. [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Mesabi Range iron ore ke liye famous hai, coal ke liye NAHI — common confusion. [Q16]\nIndustrial Regions — Country Matching (More Sets)\n● Lancashire Region-United Kingdom, Ruhr Region-Germany, Keihin Region-Japan, Southern Appalachian\nRegion-USA. [Q17]\n● Correct match: Ruhr Industrial Region-Germany — Lorraine actually France ki hai, Bristol actually UK ki hai,\nSaxony actually Germany ki hai (in options mein baaki galat combinations the). [Q18]\nWorld's Biggest Wool Producer — China\n● UN FAO 2024 data ke according, Shorn Wool (Greasy) production mein China 1st rank pe hai (364,481 tonnes)\n— Australia, New Zealand, Turkiye respectively 2nd/3rd/4th. [Q19]\nWuppertal — Germany's Wool Production Centre\n● Wuppertal (North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany) = wool production ka centre hai — St.Petersburg Russia mein,\nBradford N.England mein, Prato Italy mein hai. [Q20]"," C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\nCotton Textiles — Leading Producer China\n● World mein cotton textiles ka leading producer (2025) China hai. [Q21]\nFootloose Industry — Software\n● 'Footloose' industry = koi bhi industry jo resources/transport factors se affected huye bina kahin bhi located ho\nsakti hai (spatially fixed costs) — Software iska example hai (Oil Refinery, Sugar, Aluminium jaise industries\nspecific location-dependent hoti hain). [Q22]\nElectronics Industry — Raw Material Availability Primary NAHI\n● Given industries mein Electronics industry ke liye raw material availability primary consideration NAHI hai\n(Iron&Steel jaisi industries ke liye hoti hai). [Q23]\n'Bowl of Sugar' — Cuba (Historical), Brazil (Current)\n● 1960 tak Cuba world ka largest sugar exporter tha, isliye 'Sugar Bowl of World' kehlata tha — ab Brazil largest\nsugar exporter hai (Cuba West Indies ka largest single island archipelago hai). [Q24]\nJapan — Leading Industrial Country ka Reason\n● Japan world ki top economies mein se ek hai — high technology ki wajah se competitive credibility maintain ki\nhai; bioenergy sources+minerals ki kami ki wajah se imported materials pe dependent hai — Industrial\nRevolution Britain mein start hua tha, Japan mein NAHI. [Q25]\nScotland Industrial Area — UK (Sweden NAHI)\n● Given options mein Scotland Industrial Area Sweden mein NAHI, United Kingdom mein hai — baaki\noptions correctly matched hain. [Q26]\nSugar Industry By-products — Bagasse, Molasses\n● Bagasse biomass fuel ke roop mein energy generation ke liye use hota hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — Molasses\nsynthetic chemical fertilizers ka feedstock NAHI hai (Statement 2 galat, molasses mainly fermentation\nfeedstock hai) — Molasses ethanol production ke liye ferment ki jaa sakti hai (Statement 3 TRUE). [Q27]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Molasses fermentation feedstock (ethanol production) hai, chemical fertilizers ka feedstock NAHI. [Q27]\nPaper Pulp — Poplar Wood"," C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\n● Paper pulp banane ke liye Poplar wood use hoti hai. [Q28]\nMediterranean Forest — Trees\n● Mediterranean lands 'world's orchard lands' kehlate hain — citrus fruits (oranges, lemons, limes, grapes), Olive\ntree (sabse typical vegetation), nut trees (chestnuts, walnuts, hazelnuts, almonds), evergreen oaks — given\noptions mein jo tree yahan NAHI milta wahi answer hai. [Q29]\nJapan — Market-Based Iron/Steel Industry Location\n● Japan mein iron+steel industries market-based locations pe hain — iron ore+coal deposits ki kami ki wajah se\nhigh-quality raw material import kiya jaata hai (larger ships se transport cost kam karne ke liye) — isliye\nfactories mostly ports/coastal cities ke near hain jahan steel ka market hai. [Q30]\nJapan — Market-Based Steel Industry\n● Japanese steel plants mostly market-based hain — 'Tokyo-Yokohama' aur 'Osaka-Kobe-Himeji' iron+steel\nregions market-based hain. [Q31]\nJapan Industry — Facts (Osaka, Kamaishi, Kyushu)\n● Osaka (Japan) = 'Manchester of East' (cotton textile production) — zyada iron+steel centres southern coastal\nregion mein hain, kuch Kamaishi(NE Honshu) aur Muroran(SE Hokkaido) mein bhi — Japan East Asia mein\nshipbuilding mein prominent hai — Kyushu region (Fukuoka, Kitakyushu, Nagasaki) important hai. [Q32]\nLondon — Largest Metal Trading Centre\n● London = world ka largest metal trading centre hai. [Q33]\nDetroit — Automobile (Cotton Textiles NAHI)\n● Correct: Paper-Ontario, Chemical-Texas, Motor Car-Nagoya — Cotton Textiles-Detroit GALAT hai (Detroit,\nMichigan actually Automobile industry ke liye famous hai — tyres, electric wires, batteries, paint, car\nmachinery, chemicals, computers bhi yahan banti hain). [Q34]\nGornaya Shoria — Iron Ore Reserve (Cotton Textile NAHI)\n● Correct: Detroit(USA)-Automobile, Anshan(China)-Iron&Steel, Yokohama(Japan)-Shipbuilding — Gornaya\nShoria(Russia)-Cotton Textile GALAT hai (actually Iron ore reserve hai). [Q35]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Gornaya Shoria (Russia) Iron ore reserve hai, Cotton Textile centre NAHI — common wrong pairing. [Q35]"," C Industries\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\nUmland — Term Meaning\n● Umland = kisi town ke surrounding area/environs ko kehte hain (common economic+cultural activities se\nconnected) — Daniel Saunders ne 1883 mein pehli baar use kiya, French geographer Andre Allix ne 1914 mein\nhighlight kiya. [Q36]\n'Megalopolis' Term — Jean Gottmann (Popularizer)\n● 'Megalopolis' word Jean Gottmann se pehle bhi exist karta tha (Patrick Geddes ne bhi use kiya tha) —\nGottmann ne 1961 book 'Megalopolis' se NE-USA study ke through is concept ko popularize kiya, literally\n'first use' NAHI kiya. [Q37]\nAberdeen — Europe ki Oil Capital\n● Aberdeen (Scotland/UK) = 'Oil Capital of Europe' kehlata hai — North Sea mein significant oil deposits ki\ndiscovery se (mid-20th century) petroleum industry start hui. [Q38]\nIndustrial Regions — Country Matching (Correct Set)\n● Ruhr-Germany, Southern New England-USA, Po Valley-Italy, Kanto Plains-Japan — given options mein galat\npairing identify karna tha (option B galat tha). [Q39]\nThe Midlands — England ka Region (USA ka NAHI)\n● Given options mein The Midlands USA ki Industrial Region NAHI hai — yeh actually Central England ka\narea hai (East Midlands: Leicestershire, Northamptonshire, Derbyshire, Nottinghamshire, Lincoln, Rutland;\nWest Midlands: Staffordshire, Warwickshire, Shropshire, Herefordshire, Worcestershire). [Q40]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• The Midlands England (UK) ka region hai, USA ka NAHI. [Q40]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0159","t":"49 The Transport","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Transport\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Transport — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 49_The_Transport\nTopic Index\n1. North Atlantic Sea Route — Busiest World Route\n2. Delhi-Tokyo Flight — Landing Sequence\n3. Rhine River — Western/Southern Germany (Northern NAHI)\n4. Perth-London — Shortest Air Route (Given Options)\n5. IC-814 Hijack (Dec 1999) — Landing Sequence\n6. Lufthansa — Germany ki Airline\n7. Trans-Continental Railways — Route Details\n8. Bullet Train — China ka Longest Network\n9. Railway Length — Descending Order (Disputed)\n10. Highest Railway Network Density — USA (Given Options)\n11. Canadian Pacific Railway — Montreal-Vancouver\n12. Euro Tunnel — England-France\n13. Longest Rock Tunnel — New York (Delaware Aqueduct)\n14. Seikan Tunnel — Japan\n15. Suez Canal Region — Lakes North-to-South\nNorth Atlantic Sea Route — Busiest World Route\n● North Atlantic sea route world ki busiest sea route hai (A TRUE) — Europe+North America ke 2 major\nindustrial zones ko connect karti hai (R TRUE, sahi explanation). [Q1]\n● Busiest sea route: North Atlantic Ocean Route — major Western European ports (London, Liverpool,\nHamburg, Amsterdam) aur N.American ports (Quebec, New York, Boston, Philadelphia) is route pe hain.\n[Q2,Q3]\nDelhi-Tokyo Flight — Landing Sequence\n● Delhi se Tokyo flight ki landing sequence: Bangkok → Hanoi → Hong Kong → Taipei. [Q4]\nRhine River — Western/Southern Germany (Northern NAHI)\n● Rhine River Western+Southern Germany mein industrial activity ka important pathway hai, Northern\nGermany mein NAHI (Statement 1 galat) — Rhine Swiss Alps se North Sea tak, Bonn city iske kinare hai —\nPort of Rotterdam Rhine ke mouth pe located hai (Statement 2 TRUE). [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Rhine Western/Southern Germany ka industrial pathway hai, Northern Germany ka NAHI. [Q5]"," The Transport\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\nPerth-London — Shortest Air Route (Given Options)\n● Given routes mein Perth se London ka shortest air-route option A tha. [Q6]\nIC-814 Hijack (Dec 1999) — Landing Sequence\n● Kathmandu se takeoff ke baad hijacked IC-814 flight ki landing sequence: Amritsar → Lahore → Dubai →\nKandahar (map labels 5,4,2,3). [Q7]\nLufthansa — Germany ki Airline\n● Lufthansa = Germany ki airline hai — world ka 4th-largest passenger-airline fleet hai. [Q8]\nTrans-Continental Railways — Route Details\n● European trans-continental railway: Paris to Warsaw — Trans-Andean railway: Valparaiso to Buenos Aires\n(Argentina) — Trans-Siberian railway: Leningrad/St.Petersburg to Vladivostok, ~9,300 km (world ki longest\nrailway). [Q9]\n● Trans-Siberian route ke major cities (W-E): St.Petersburg, Moscow, Perm, Kazan, Yekaterinburg, Tyumen,\nOmsk, Novosibirsk, Krasnoyarsk, Ulan-Ude, Chita, Khabarovsk, Vladivostok — Sochi is route pe NAHI hai.\n[Q10]\nBullet Train — China ka Longest Network\n● China ka world ka longest high-speed rail (bullet train) network hai — end of 2024 tak ~48,000 km — 5 Jan\n2017 'Shangri-la of World' bullet train Kunming-Beijing (2,760 km) start hui. [Q11]\nRailway Length — Descending Order (Disputed)\n● Correct descending order: USA, India, Canada, Germany — given 4 options mein se koi bhi exact sequence\nmatch nahi karta, isliye question disputed (*) hai. [Q12]\nHighest Railway Network Density — USA (Given Options)\n● Given options mein highest railway network density — cited exam ke according USA accepted answer hai.\n[Q13]\nCanadian Pacific Railway — Montreal-Vancouver\n● Canadian Pacific Railway Montreal se Vancouver ke beech chalti hai. [Q14]\nEuro Tunnel — England-France"," The Transport\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n● Euro Tunnel (Channel Tunnel) England (UK) aur France ko join karti hai. [Q15]\nLongest Rock Tunnel — New York (Delaware Aqueduct)\n● World ka longest rock tunnel New York (Delaware Aqueduct) mein located hai (Greenland NAHI). [Q16]\nSeikan Tunnel — Japan\n● Seikan Tunnel (~53.85 km, Honshu-Hokkaido, Tsugaru Strait ke neeche) Japan mein hai — pehle world ki\nlongest railway tunnel thi, ab Switzerland ki Gotthard Base Tunnel (57.1km) yeh record rakhti hai. [Q17]\nSuez Canal Region — Lakes North-to-South\n● Suez Canal region mein N-S order: Lake Manzala → Lake Timsah → Great Bitter Lake → Little Bitter\nLake. [Q18]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0160","t":"50 The Ports and Harbours","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Ports and Harbours\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Ports and Harbours — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 50_The_Ports_and_Harbours\nTopic Index\n1. Yokohama — Japan ka Busiest Port\n2. Canberra — Sea-Port City NAHI\n3. Largest Harbour — Rotterdam (Historical, Metric-Dependent)\n4. Busiest Seaport by Cargo Tonnage — Shanghai (2010 Context)\n5. Rhine River — Rotterdam Port Location\n6. Second Biggest Port — Shanghai (2004 Context)\n7. Maracaibo (Venezuela) — Oil Port\n8. Alexandria — Egypt ka Port\n9. Port Diamond — Port Nolloth (South Africa)\n10. 'Coffee Port' of World — Santos (Brazil)\n11. Largest Shipbuilder (Monetary Value) — South Korea\n12. Gwadar Port — Pakistan (Balochistan Province)\n13. Port-Country Mismatches — Igarka Russia (China NAHI)\n14. Periplus of the Erythraean Sea — Unknown Author\nYokohama — Japan ka Busiest Port\n● Japan ka busiest port Yokohama hai — Yokohama city ka Port+Harbour Bureau operate karta hai, greater Tokyo\narea ka gateway hai. [Q1]\nCanberra — Sea-Port City NAHI\n● Tokyo (Honshu ka seaport), New York (Hudson River pe), London (Thames pe) sab sea-port cities hain —\nCanberra sea se surrounded NAHI hai (Australia ki capital, sea-port city NAHI). [Q2]\nLargest Harbour — Rotterdam (Historical, Metric-Dependent)\n● 'Largest harbour' ka koi single standardized metric NAHI hai (cargo tonnage/container throughput/harbour area\nalag ho sakte hain) — historically Rotterdam ko world ka largest port/harbour maana jaata tha (Europe ke\nenormous cargo role ki wajah se). [Q3]\nBusiest Seaport by Cargo Tonnage — Shanghai (2010 Context)\n● 2010 exam data period ke according cargo tonnage se busiest seaport Shanghai tha (given options mein). [Q4]\nRhine River — Rotterdam Port Location"," The Ports and Harbours\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n● Rhine Europe ke important inland-waterway+industrial transport corridors mein se ek hai — Rotterdam Rhine-\nMeuse-Scheldt delta mein hai, Rhine system ka major seaward outlet hai — main German industrial corridor\nWestern Germany mein hai, 'Northern Germany' galat hai (Statement 1 galat, Statement 2 TRUE). [Q5]\nSecond Biggest Port — Shanghai (2004 Context)\n● 2004 mein Shanghai Singapore ke baad world ka 2nd-largest port ban gaya tha (freight volume se). [Q6]\nMaracaibo (Venezuela) — Oil Port\n● 'Maracaibo' (NW Venezuela, Lake Maracaibo-Gulf of Venezuela ke beech ki strait pe) Oil Port ke roop mein\ndevelop hui — Tablazo Strait (~55km) se Gulf of Venezuela se connected — 1917 mein petroleum discovery se\npehle ek chhota coffee town thi. [Q7]\nAlexandria — Egypt ka Port\n● Alexandria (Egypt ka 2nd-largest city, major economic centre) Mediterranean coast pe ~32km extend karta hai\n— Nile Delta pe low elevation, rising sea level se vulnerable — Suez se natural gas+oil pipelines important\nindustrial centre banate hain. [Q8]\nPort Diamond — Port Nolloth (South Africa)\n● 'Port Diamond' = Port Nolloth (South Africa) hai — pehle Okiep mines se copper aur Namaqualand region se\ndiamonds ka transshipment point tha. [Q9]\n'Coffee Port' of World — Santos (Brazil)\n● 'Coffee Port' of world = Port of Santos (Brazil) — coffee exports mein major role ki wajah se yeh naam mila.\n[Q10,Q11]\nLargest Shipbuilder (Monetary Value) — South Korea\n● Exam-period monetary value comparison ke according world ka largest shipbuilder South Korea tha. [Q12]\nGwadar Port — Pakistan (Balochistan Province)\n● Gwadar = warm-water deep-sea port, Arabian Sea pe Pakistan ke Balochistan Province mein — strategic\nsignificance rakhta hai, Pakistan-China ne 2,000+ acres land usage rights deal ki hai, China railway access\ndevelop kar raha hai. [Q13,Q14]\nPort-Country Mismatches — Igarka Russia (China NAHI)\n● Jakarta-Indonesia, Rotterdam-Netherlands, Montevideo-Uruguay correct hain — Igarka actually Russia\n(Yenisey River) mein hai, China mein NAHI. [Q15,Q16]"," The Ports and Harbours\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠️\n• Igarka Russia mein hai (Krasnoyarsk Krai, Turukhansky District), China mein NAHI. [Q15,Q16]\nPeriplus of the Erythraean Sea — Unknown Author\n● 'Periplus of the Erythraean Sea' (Greco-Roman text, Koine Greek mein likha) navigation+trading opportunities\ndescribe karta hai (Roman Egyptian ports se Red Sea coast, Horn of Africa, Sindh region-Pakistan, SW India\ntak) — author unknown/anonymous hai. [Q17]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0161","t":"51 The Mapping","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" The Mapping\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n The Mapping — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 51_The_Mapping\nTopic Index\n1. Isobars/Isoplet Maps — Weather Map Example\n2. Isogonic Lines — Magnetic Declination\n3. Isobaths — Equal Depth (Water)\n4. Sea Voyage Map — Ferdinand Magellan\n5. Contours — Relief Features ka Most Accurate Method\n6. Isohyet — Same Rainfall Areas Joining Line\nIsobars/Isoplet Maps — Weather Map Example\n● Isobars dikhaane wala daily weather map Isoplet map ka example hai — continuous distribution data ko\ngeneralize+simplify karta hai (third dimension ke roop mein) — surface elevation, precipitation, atmospheric\npressure jaisi measurements ke liye common. [Q1]\nIsogonic Lines — Magnetic Declination\n● Isogonic lines = Earth surface pe wo points jinka magnetic declination same hota hai, unhe join karne wali\nimaginary lines. [Q2]\nIsobaths — Equal Depth (Water)\n● Isobaths = water surface ke neeche equal depth ke points ko represent karti hain. [Q3]\nSea Voyage Map — Ferdinand Magellan\n● Given sea-voyage route map Ferdinand Magellan (Portuguese explorer, 1480-1521) ke route ko dikhata hai —\nuski expedition ne Earth ki first circumnavigation complete ki. [Q4]\nContours — Relief Features ka Most Accurate Method\n● Contours relief features represent karne ka sabse accurate method hain — equal elevation points ko join karne\nwali imaginary lines — close contours = steep slope, far-apart contours = gentle slope. [Q5]\nIsohyet — Same Rainfall Areas Joining Line\n● Isohyet = same rainfall receive karne wali jagah ko join karti hai — Isobar (same atmospheric pressure),\nIsotherm (same temperature), Isohaline (same salinity) alag-alag concepts hain. [Q6]"," The Mapping\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0162","t":"52 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Geography / World Geography","x":[" Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 1\n Miscellaneous — FULL MIND MAP\n🗺️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\nChapter 52_Miscellaneous\nTopic Index\n1. World's Fishing Grounds — Cold+Warm Current Meeting Points\n2. Neo-Determinism — Griffith Taylor\n3. Cultural Worlds — 11 (Spencer aur Thomas)\n4. Planting Hearth, Cryophyte Steppe, World Floral Regions\n5. Kurd/Madhesi/Rohingya — Region Matching\n6. Cuba/Hong Kong/Milk/Australia — Correct Statements\n7. Bosnia+Nova Scotia — Statements Disputed\n8. Terrestrial Mile, Harmattan, Greece+Albania\n9. Atlas Mountains/Pampas/Kimberley/Manitoba — Matching\n10. Pole Star, Earth, Greenland, Explosion — Concept Matching\n11. Geographic Features — Country Matching\n12. First Nuclear Power Station — Obninsk (Soviet Union)\n13. Seikan Tunnel — Japan (Petronas Towers Malaysia)\n14. Bermuda Triangle — North Atlantic Ocean\n15. Golden Triangle/Bermuda Triangle/Rice Bowl/Red Basin\n16. Cape Canaveral (Cape Kennedy) — USA Satellite Launch Centre\n17. Antarctica Map — Canada's RADARSAT-1\n18. Local Winds — Bora/Foehn/Mistral/Khamsin\n19. Wine — Italy Largest Producer (2025, Current)\n20. Tree ki Age — Growth Rings se\n21. Copacabana Beach — Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)\n22. Highest Ground-Based Telescopic Observatory — Hanle (India)\n23. Middle East — Boundary Disputed\n24. European Union — Brussels (De Facto)\n25. IMO Headquarters — London\n26. NATO Members — 4 out of 6 Given Countries\n27. FAO Headquarters — Rome (New York NAHI)\n28. NE USA — Densely Populated, Industrial (Agriculture pe Depend NAHI)\n29. Southeast Asia — Geo-Strategic Significance\n30. India ki 'Look East Policy' — P.V. Narasimha Rao\n31. Kailash Mansarovar — China (Tibet) mein Visa Zaroori\n32. Australia mein Christmas — Summer Season\n33. ASEAN — India 'Dialogue Partner' Status\n34. OPEC — Non-Member (2002 Context)\n35. SAARC Headquarters — Kathmandu (Nepal)\n36. Organization of Turkic States — Azerbaijan+Uzbekistan Members\n37. Leaning Tower of Pisa — Italy\n38. Elysee Palace — Paris (France)\n39. Tallest Flying Bird — Crane (Ostrich Flies NAHI)"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 2\n40. Post Offices — India Largest Network\n41. Chernobyl Nuclear Disaster — Ukraine (1986)\n42. 'Great Leap Forward' — China (1958-1962)\n43. Nuclear Power Plants — Descending Order (Historical)\n44. Norway — 99% Energy Hydro-Power se\n45. 'Country of 40 Tribes' — Kyrgyzstan\n46. 'Queen of Adriatic Sea' — Venice (Rome NAHI)\n47. Peneplain — Rivers se Related\n48. 'Umland' — City ke Surrounding Region\n49. Migration Theory — Everett Lee\n50. Indian Ocean — Military Bases + Geo-Political Benefits\n51. Biodiversity — Tropics vs Poles\n52. 'Denisovan' — Archaic Human Population\n53. Isohyet — Rainfall Line (Repeat)\n54. Geostationary Satellite — ~35,786 km Altitude\n55. Dalmatian Coast — Submergent/Drowned Coast (Croatia)\n56. World's Largest Offshore Wind Farm — UK (Hornsea 2, Aug 2022)\nWorld's Fishing Grounds — Cold+Warm Current Meeting Points\n● World ke important fishing grounds 40°-60° latitudes ke around milte hain — cold+warm ocean currents\nconverge hone ki wajah se, western continental coasts pe polar cold currents+lower-latitude warm currents mix\nhoti hain. [Q1]\n● Grand Bank = North American continental shelf ka part (Atlantic Ocean, Newfoundland Canada ke SE) — cold\nLabrador Current + warm Gulf Stream yahan milti hain — international fishing ground hai. [Q2]\nNeo-Determinism — Griffith Taylor\n● Geography mein 'Neo-Determinism' concept Griffith Taylor ne advance ki — 'stop-and-go\ndeterminism'/'Scientific Determinism' bhi kehte hain. [Q3]\nCultural Worlds — 11 (Spencer aur Thomas)\n● J.E. Spencer aur W.L. Thomas ki book 'Introducing Cultural Geography' mein world ko 11 Cultural Worlds\nmein divide kiya gaya hai. [Q4]\nPlanting Hearth, Cryophyte Steppe, World Floral Regions\n● Planting Hearth-C.O.Sauer (American geographer, agriculture ka origin region concept), Cryophyte Steppe-\nArctic Tundra, World Floral Regions-Adolf Engler, Puszta Grassland-Hungary. [Q5]\nKurd/Madhesi/Rohingya — Region Matching\n● Kurd mainly E/SE Turkiye, W.Iran, N.Iraq, N.Syria mein hain, Bangladesh mein NAHI — Madhesi(Nepal) aur\nRohingya(Myanmar) correctly matched hain. [Q6]"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 3\nCuba/Hong Kong/Milk/Australia — Correct Statements\n● Cuba 'Sugar Bowl of World' kehlata hai — Hong Kong China ka Special Administrative Region hai — USA\nNAHI, India world ka leading milk producer hai — Australia 6 states ka federation hai. [Q7]\nBosnia+Nova Scotia — Statements Disputed\n● Bosnia and Herzegovina Balkan region ka part hai — Nova Scotia coal field Canada mein hai, Kazakhstan mein\nNAHI — given options mein dono galat the, isliye question disputed (*) hai. [Q8]\nTerrestrial Mile, Harmattan, Greece+Albania\n● Terrestrial mile (1,760 yards, ~1,609m) nautical mile (1,852m) se chhota hai (Statement 1 TRUE) — Harmattan\nWest Africa (Sahara se) ki dry+dusty NE trade wind hai, East African Coast ki NAHI. [Q9]\nAtlas Mountains/Pampas/Kimberley/Manitoba — Matching\n● Atlas Mountains-Morocco/Algeria/Tunisia, Pampas grasslands-Argentina, Kimberley mines-South Africa,\nManitoba-Canadian province — correctly matched combination. [Q10]\nPole Star, Earth, Greenland, Explosion — Concept Matching\n● Pole star-North, Earth-Gravitation, Greenland-Arctic Ocean, Explosion-Sound. [Q11]\nGeographic Features — Country Matching\n● Great Victoria Desert-Australia, Grand Canyon-USA, Lake Winnipeg-Canada, Southern Alps-New Zealand.\n[Q12]\nFirst Nuclear Power Station — Obninsk (Soviet Union)\n● World ka pehla civilian nuclear power plant Obninsk (Soviet Union) mein June 1954 mein commission hua —\nIAEA ke according first civilian nuclear power plant (EBR-I, USA, ne pehli baar electricity generate ki thi lekin\nObninsk pehla civilian grid-connected plant tha). [Q13]\nSeikan Tunnel — Japan (Petronas Towers Malaysia)\n● Seikan Tunnel (53.85km, 23.3km seabed ke neeche, Japan) — Petronas Towers (Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia) —\ngiven options mein galat pairing thi. [Q14]\nBermuda Triangle — North Atlantic Ocean"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 4\n● Bermuda Triangle (Bermuda, Florida-Miami, San Juan-Puerto Rico ke beech, North Atlantic Ocean) = 'Devil's\nTriangle' bhi kehlata hai. [Q15]\n● Bermuda Triangle Southern Florida aur Puerto Rico tak extend hota hai (3rd point Miami). [Q16]\nGolden Triangle/Bermuda Triangle/Rice Bowl/Red Basin\n● Golden Triangle-SE Asia opium-producing area, Bermuda Triangle-N.Atlantic Ocean, Rice Bowl of Far East-\nMyanmar, Red Basin-China. [Q17]\nCape Canaveral (Cape Kennedy) — USA Satellite Launch Centre\n● USA ka satellite launch centre Cape Canaveral (Florida) hai — kuch time John F. Kennedy ke honour mein\n'Cape Kennedy' naam se jaana jaata tha, 1973 se wapas Cape Canaveral kehlata hai. [Q18]\nAntarctica Map — Canada's RADARSAT-1\n● Canada ke satellite RADARSAT-1 ne 1997 mein pehli baar Antarctica ka detailed+complete map banane mein\nhelp ki. [Q19]\nLocal Winds — Bora/Foehn/Mistral/Khamsin\n● Bora-NE Adriatic (Italy/Slovenia/Croatia) cold strong wind, Foehn-Alps warm-dry wind, Mistral-Spain/France\ncold-dry wind, Khamsin-dry/hot/sandy local wind — given options mein ek galat pairing thi. [Q20]\nWine — Italy Largest Producer (2025, Current)\n● Wine production leadership harvest-sensitive hoti hai — OIV 2025 preliminary estimates ke according Italy #1\nhai (France, Spain se aage). [Q21]\nTree ki Age — Growth Rings se\n● Tree ki age growth rings count karke determine ki jaati hai (stem cross-section mein) — vascular cambium ke\nnear new growth se banti hain, seasonal growth-speed variation se rings visible hoti hain. [Q22]\nCopacabana Beach — Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)\n● Copacabana Beach Rio de Janeiro (Brazil) ke south zone mein hai — ~4km Balneario beach, world ki famous\nbeaches mein se ek. [Q23]\nHighest Ground-Based Telescopic Observatory — Hanle (India)\n● Cited exam ke according world ki highest ground-based telescopic observatory Indian Astronomical\nObservatory, Hanle (near Leh) thi. [Q24]"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 5\nMiddle East — Boundary Disputed\n● Middle East list mein Jordan, Israel, Lebanon, Syria, Turkiye shamil hain — given options mein se koi bhi clearly\nMiddle East se bahar nahi hai, isliye question disputed (*) hai. [Q25]\nEuropean Union — Brussels (De Facto)\n● EU ki koi legally-defined single capital/headquarters nahi hai — Brussels mein European Commission, European\nCouncil, Council of EU hain (principal centre of day-to-day political administration) — European Parliament ki\nseat Strasbourg mein hai. [Q26]\nIMO Headquarters — London\n● International Maritime Organization (UN specialized agency) ka headquarters London (UK) mein hai — 176\nmembers + 3 associate members. [Q27]\nNATO Members — 4 out of 6 Given Countries\n● Given 6 countries mein NATO members: Bulgaria, Croatia, Sweden, North Macedonia (4) — Austria\nmilitary-neutral hai, Serbia bhi NATO member NAHI hai — Sweden 32nd member bana (7 March 2024).\n[Q28]\nFAO Headquarters — Rome (New York NAHI)\n● Food & Agricultural Organization ka headquarters Rome (Italy) mein hai, New York mein NAHI — baaki pairs\ncorrectly matched the. [Q29]\nNE USA — Densely Populated, Industrial (Agriculture pe Depend NAHI)\n● North-Eastern USA densely populated+highly industrialised region hai (New York, Philadelphia, Boston,\nPittsburgh, Buffalo jaise famous industrial towns) — agriculture pe directly depend NAHI karta. [Q30]\nSoutheast Asia — Geo-Strategic Significance\n● SE Asia geo-strategically significant hai kyunki uski location Pacific+Indian Oceans ke beech hai aur maritime\ncharacter pre-eminent hai — isi significance ki wajah se Spykman ne 'Rimland theory' propose ki thi. [Q31]\nIndia ki 'Look East Policy' — P.V. Narasimha Rao\n● 'Look East Policy' PM P.V. Narasimha Rao (1991-1996) ke tenure mein develop+enact hui — India East Asian\naffairs mein regional player banna chahta hai, Cold War khatam hone se bana vacuum plug karna chahta hai.\n[Q32]"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 6\nKailash Mansarovar — China (Tibet) mein Visa Zaroori\n● Kailash Mansarovar Chinese Tibet mein hai, isliye Indians ko pilgrimage ke liye visa chahiye — Mt.Kailash\n(Kailash Range, Trans-Himalaya) Indus, Sutlej jaisi major rivers ke source ke near hai. [Q33]\nAustralia mein Christmas — Summer Season\n● Australia Southern Hemisphere mein hai, isliye Christmas summer season mein celebrate hota hai — Earth's\naxis ~23.5° tilted hai, December mein N.Hemisphere winter aur S.Hemisphere summer experience karta hai.\n[Q34]\nASEAN — India 'Dialogue Partner' Status\n● Vietnam, Cambodia, Singapore full ASEAN members hain — India ASEAN member NAHI hai (1992 mein\nSectoral Dialogue Partner, 1995 mein full Dialogue Partner bana) — 2022 mein ASEAN-India relations\nComprehensive Strategic Partnership tak elevate hui. [Q35]\nOPEC — Non-Member (2002 Context)\n● 2002 context ke according Indonesia OPEC member tha, China nahi tha (given options mein non-member\nanswer). [Q36]\nSAARC Headquarters — Kathmandu (Nepal)\n● SAARC secretariat Kathmandu (Nepal) mein hai — 2 May 1980 ko Bangladesh President Ziaur Rahman ne\nSouth Asian regional cooperation ka idea raise kiya, 1st summit Dhaka mein 7-8 Dec 1985 hua. [Q37]\nOrganization of Turkic States — Azerbaijan+Uzbekistan Members\n● Given 5 countries (Armenia, Azerbaijan, Croatia, Romania, Uzbekistan) mein se Azerbaijan aur Uzbekistan\nfull members hain (baaki: Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Turkiye bhi members hain). [Q38]\nLeaning Tower of Pisa — Italy\n● Leaning Tower of Pisa (campanile/free-standing bell tower, unintended tilt ke liye famous) Pisa, Italy mein hai\n— Cathedral Square ki 3rd oldest structure hai. [Q39]\nElysee Palace — Paris (France)\n● Elysee Palace Paris, France mein hai — 1848 se French President ka official residence hai. [Q40]\nTallest Flying Bird — Crane (Ostrich Flies NAHI)\n● Ostrich sabse tall bird hai lekin fly NAHI kar sakta — flying birds mein sabse tall Crane hai. [Q41]"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 7\nPost Offices — India Largest Network\n● World ka largest postal network (post offices ki sankhya se) India ka hai — Department of Posts data ke\naccording 31 March 2025 tak 164,999 post offices. [Q42]\nChernobyl Nuclear Disaster — Ukraine (1986)\n● Chernobyl nuclear disaster April 1986 mein Ukraine (tab Soviet Union ka part) mein hua tha. [Q43]\n'Great Leap Forward' — China (1958-1962)\n● 'Great Leap Forward Policy' ki wajah se millions people starvation se mare China mein (Second Five-Year Plan,\n1958-1962) — large rural communes se agriculture disrupt hui. [Q44]\nNuclear Power Plants — Descending Order (Historical)\n● Question ke time period ke according accepted descending order: USA > France > Russia > Japan — rankings\ntime ke saath change hoti hain (reactors commission/retire hote hain). [Q45]\n● 2012 context ke according accepted sequence given option D thi — IAEA data (31 March 2026 tak) ke according\nUSA, France, China, Russia leading countries hain. [Q46]\nNorway — 99% Energy Hydro-Power se\n● Cited exam ke according jis desh mein 99% total energy requirement Hydro-Power se milta hai wo Norway hai\n(overwhelmingly hydro-based electricity system). [Q47]\n'Country of 40 Tribes' — Kyrgyzstan\n● 'Kyrgyz' word 'Kyrk' (matlab forty) se derive hua hai — isliye Kyrgyzstan ka matlab 'country of 40 tribes' hai —\nKyrgyz epic 'Manas' mein national hero Manas ne Chinese invasion se bachane ke liye 40 tribes ko unite kiya\ntha. [Q48]\n'Queen of Adriatic Sea' — Venice (Rome NAHI)\n● Venice (Italy) ko 'Queen of Adriatic Sea' kehte hain, Rome ko NAHI — yeh galat pairing thi given options mein.\n[Q49]\nPeneplain — Rivers se Related\n● Peneplain rivers se banti hai — fluvial erosion+deposition se almost featureless gentle undulating plain banti hai,\nland ko base level tak reduce kar deti hai (essentially no more erosion possible). [Q50]"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 8\n'Umland' — City ke Surrounding Region\n● Umland = kisi city ke around ka geographical region jo us city ke saath inflow-outflow relationships maintain\nkarta hai. [Q51]\nMigration Theory — Everett Lee\n● Migration Theory se associated naam Everett Lee hai — migration ko permanent/semi-permanent residence\nchange maana. [Q52]\nIndian Ocean — Military Bases + Geo-Political Benefits\n● Indian Ocean mein many big powers ke military bases hain (A TRUE) — strong geo-political benefits hain (R\nTRUE) — major sea lanes, energy routes, chokepoints, strategically important coastal states+islands ki wajah\nse. [Q53]\nBiodiversity — Tropics vs Poles\n● Correct: tropics mein temperate areas se zyada species hain, Amazonian rainforest mein greatest biodiversity hai,\nspecies diversity temperate se poles ki taraf ghatti hai — species diversity Equator se poles ki taraf\nBADHATI NAHI, GHATATI hai (galat statement identify karna tha). [Q54]\n'Denisovan' — Archaic Human Population\n● 'Denisovan' word archaic human population ko refer karta hai (Siberia ki Denisova Cave se DNA+fossil\nmaterial se identify hui) — Tibetan Plateau (Baishiya Karst Cave) se mandible bhi link hui hai. [Q55]\nIsohyet — Rainfall Line (Repeat)\n● Same rainfall areas ko join karne wali line Isohyet kehlati hai — Isobar(pressure), Isotherm(temperature),\nIsohaline(salinity) alag concepts hain. [Q56]\nGeostationary Satellite — ~35,786 km Altitude\n● Geostationary satellite ~35,786 km altitude pe revolve karta hai — equator ke directly upar, Earth ki rotation\ndirection (west-east) mein. [Q57]\nDalmatian Coast — Submergent/Drowned Coast (Croatia)\n● Dalmatian Coast (E.Adriatic, especially Croatia) = submergent/drowned coast ka classic example — long\nnarrow islands+channels mainland ke parallel hain (folded+karstic ridges partly submerged). [Q58]\nWorld's Largest Offshore Wind Farm — UK (Hornsea 2, Aug 2022)"," Miscellaneous\nExamFusionPrep — World Geography Mind Map | Page 9\n● Hornsea 2 (UK ke off-coast) 31 Aug 2022 ko fully operational hui — tab world ki largest offshore wind farm thi.\n[Q59]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0163","t":"01 Stone Age","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" 🪨 STONE AGE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Stone Age Study — Archaeologists & Organisations\n2. Three-Age System & Copper Age\n3. Palaeolithic Age — Earliest Man in India\n4. Mesolithic Age — Animal Domestication\n5. Mesolithic Sites — Bone Tools, Ornaments & Burials\n6. Neolithic Age — Agriculture & Cereals\n7. Neolithic Sites — Burzahom (Kashmir Valley)\n8. Neolithic Sites — Ash Mounds\n9. Bhimbetka — Rock Paintings\n10. Chalcolithic Age — Ahar / Banas Culture\n11. Chalcolithic Sites — Navdatoli\n12. Chalcolithic Burial Practices — Jorwe Culture (Maharashtra)\n13. Pottery — Ochre-Coloured Pottery (OCP)\n14. Megaliths\n15. Important Match-the-Following (Period/Site & Site/State)\n16. Important Site Pairs (True/False Statement Type)\n17. Assertion–Reason: Vindhyas to Ganga Valley Migration\n1. Stone Age Study — Archaeologists & Organisations\n● Robert Bruce Foote Britannica ke mutabik ek British geologist AUR archaeologist dono the. Inhe Indian\npre-history ka 'father' kaha jaata hai. Geological Survey of India (GSI) se jude the aur Stone Age ki\nantiquities document ki thi. (Isliye is question mein A aur B dono options correct maane jaate hain.) [Q1]\n● Alexander Rea, A.H. Longhurst, Robert Sewell, James Burgess aur Walter Elliot — sab archaeological\nexcavations se jude the, mainly South India ke history par kaam karte the. [Q3]\n● Alexander Cunningham (1814-1893 AD) — 'Father of Indian Archaeology' kahe jaate hain. British army\nofficer the, Bengal Engineer Group mein. [Q49]\n● Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) — Ministry of Culture ke under aata hai. India ka premier\narchaeological research aur protection organization hai. [Q48]\n● National Museum of Mankind (Indira Gandhi Rashtriya Manav Sangrahalaya) — Bhopal (M.P.) mein\nlocated hai, Ministry of Culture ke under ek autonomous organization hai, aur India ka sabse bada\nmuseum hai jo human development history dikhata hai. [Q50, Q51]\n2. Three-Age System & Copper Age\n● Copenhagen museum ke collection ke basis par Stone → Bronze → Iron wali 'three-age system'\nChristian Jurgensen Thomsen ne banayi thi. [Q2]\n● Copper Age ko hi Chalcolithic Age kehte hain — jis period mein pathar ke saath copper tools bhi use\nhone lage. [Q22]"," 3. Palaeolithic Age — Earliest Man in India\n● India mein man (insaan) ka sabse pehla evidence Narmada Valley, M.P. (Hathnora) mein mila hai —\nyahi India ka pehla human fossil bhi hai. Ise 1982 mein Arun Sonakia ne discover kiya tha. [Q11, Q12]\n4. Mesolithic Age — Animal Domestication\n● Excavated evidence ke hisab se animal domestication (janwaron ko paltu banana) Mesolithic period\nmein shuru hua. Sabse purane evidence Adamgarh (Narmadapuram, M.P.) aur Bagor (Bhilwara,\nRajasthan) se mile hain — ye do site name saath mein yaad rakho. [Q4, Q5, Q21]\n5. Mesolithic Sites — Bone Tools, Ornaments & Burials\n● Mahadaha aur Sarai Nahar Rai (Pratapgarh dist., UP) — dono jagah se bade paimane par bone/horn\n(haddi/singh) ke implements aur ornaments mile hain. 'Puratatva Vimarsh' (Dr. Jai Narayan Pandey ki\nbook) mein Sarai Nahar Rai ke bone ornaments ka zikr hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● Damdama (Pratapgarh dist., UP) mein 41 human graves mili hain — 5 double burial, aur ek triple burial\n(3 skeleton ek hi grave mein) bhi yahin mila hai. Note: Sarai Nahar Rai mein 4-skeleton wali ek grave\nmili thi — dono sites confuse mat karna. [Q9]\n● Lekhahia rock shelter (Vindhya region) se maximum human skeletons mile hain: 'Puratatva Vimarsh'\n(J.N. Pandey) ke hisab se 17 skeleton (shelter 1 se); John R. Lucas (University of Oregon, USA) ke\nhisab se 27 skeleton. [Q46]\n● Mesolithic sites ka sahi west-to-east geographical order aata hai (jaise Mahadaha se shuru hoke\nLekhahia tak) — is type ke questions mein site ki map-position yaad rakhna zaroori hai. [Q8]\n6. Neolithic Age — Agriculture & Cereals\n● Cereals (anaj) ki cultivation sabse pehle Neolithic Age mein shuru hui — yehi wo time hai jab log\nagriculture seekhe. Koldihwa aur Mehrgarh — dono Neolithic sites se rice bran aur wheat ke clear\nevidence mile hain. [Q10]\n● Modern society mein khaye jaane wale 8 tarah ke anaj mein se Barley sabse pehla anaj tha jo cultivate\nhua. Baad mein usi area mein ~8000 B.C. ke aas-paas wheat bhi cultivate hone lagi. [Q13]\n● Uttar Pradesh ko prehistoric time se hi rich cultural heritage mila hai — Lahuradev (Sant Kabir Nagar\ndist., UP) duniya bhar mein paddy (dhaan) cultivation ka sabse purana evidence deta hai, Koldihwa bhi\nisi tarah ka evidence deta hai. UP ke kai sites se barley/paddy jaise sabse purane anaj evidence mile\nhain. [Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Mehrgarh vs Lahuradeva (bahut important pattern!)\n⚠️\n\n▸Latest research ke hisab se, Indian sub-continent mein agriculture ka SABSE PURANA evidence\nLahuradeva (Sant Kabir Nagar, UP) se mila hai. (Q14)\n\n▸Lekin agar kisi question ke OPTIONS mein 'Lahuradeva' hai hi nahi, to us case mein sahi answer"," Mehrgarh (~7000 B.C.) ban jaata hai. (Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18)\n\n▸RULE: Pehle options dekho — Lahuradeva available hai to Lahuradeva sahi hai; nahi hai to Mehrgarh\nsahi hai.\n\n▸Settled (sthayi) life ka bhi sabse purana evidence — diye gaye options mein Mehrgarh (Kachhi plains,\nBalochistan) hi hota hai. Kile Gul Muhammad (4000 B.C.) aur Kalibangan (3500 B.C.) — dono Mehrgarh\nse baad ke hain. (Q20)\n\n▸Mehrgarh se Stone Age se lekar Harappan Civilization tak ke continuous cultural remains bhi mile hain.\n(Q25)\n7. Neolithic Sites — Burzahom (Kashmir Valley)\n● Pit dwelling (zameen khodkar bane hue ghar) ka evidence Burzahom Neolithic site ki characteristic\nfeature hai. [Q41]\n● Burzahom ke kai pits mein dog aur antlered deer ki haddiyan human skeletons ke saath mili hain —\nhuman skeletons sitting position mein burial pits mein mile hain. Human body ke saath dog ko dafanane\nka evidence sabse prominently yahin milta hai. [Q39, Q40]\n8. Neolithic Sites — Ash Mounds\n● 'Ash mounds' Neolithic site Sangana Kallu (Ballari dist., Karnataka) se mile hain — Piklihal aur Utnur\nmein bhi mile hain. Ye Neolithic herdsmen community ke seasonal camps ke jale hue avshesh hain.\n[Q29]\n9. Bhimbetka — Rock Paintings\n● Bhimbetka ki rock shelters Abdullahganj-Raisen (Madhya Pradesh) mein located hain aur Rock\nPaintings ke liye famous hain. [Q30, Q31, Q32]\n● Dr. Vishnu Shridhar Wakankar ne Bhimbetka ki rock shelters 1957-1958 mein discover ki thi. Ye ek\nUNESCO World Heritage Site hai. [Q34, Q35, Q36]\n● India mein sabse zyada pictures Bhimbetka ki rock-shelters se mile hain — 750 rock shelters mein\naround 500 pictures hain. In caves mein Indian subcontinent par human life ke sabse purane traces\nmilte hain. [Q33]\n10. Chalcolithic Age — Ahar / Banas Culture\n● Ahar civilization Chalcolithic period ki thi aur Rajasthan ke Mewar region mein phali-phuli. Ye log copper\ntools use karte the aur inhe rice (chawal) ke baare mein pata tha. Zyadatar black-red pottery mili hai\njisme white geometric designs bane hain. [Q23]\n● Ahar-Banas culture (2100-1500 B.C.) Harappan Civilization ke contemporary (samkalin) thi — Mewar\nregion, Banas river aur uski tributaries ke aas-paas. Main sites: Ahar, Gilund, Balathal. [Q24]"," 11. Chalcolithic Sites — Navdatoli\n● Navdatoli (M.P., Khargone ke pass) mein round aur rectangular — dono tarah ke residential structures\nke bahut achhe evidence mile hain. Excavation H.D. Sankalia (Deccan College, Pune) ne kiya tha. Ye\nIndian subcontinent ka sabse zyada extensively excavated Chalcolithic site hai (1500 B.C. se 1300 B.C.\nke beech ka). [Q26, Q27]\n12. Chalcolithic Burial Practices — Jorwe Culture (Maharashtra)\n● Maharashtra ki Jorwe culture (Chalcolithic period) ke log life-after-death mein believe karte the, isliye\napne murdo ko ghar ke andar, floor ke niche hi dafanate the. Adults ko supine position (chit lete hue)\nmein rakha jaata tha, sar north ki taraf (North to South position). Bachchon ko urns (matke) mein bury\nkiya jaata tha. Ye sites Daimabad, Inamgaon, Chandoli, Nevasa mein mili hain. [Q38]\n13. Pottery — Ochre-Coloured Pottery (OCP)\n● Ochre-coloured Pottery (O.C.P.) ki discovery aur naam-karan (christening) B.B. Lal ne 1950-52 mein\nHastinapur mein kiya tha. Naam se hi pata chalta hai — 'ochre' colour ki wajah se ye pottery pehli nazar\nmein badly-fired (kam pakayi hui) lagti hai. [Q37]\n14. Megaliths\n● Megaliths usually badi-badi pattharon se bane hue burial (dafan) sites hote hain, jo habitation area se\ndoor graveyards mein milte hain. Zyadatar burial ya post-burial rituals se related maane jaate hain.\nTypes: Chamber tombs, Dolmens, Stone alignments waghera. [Q28]\n15. Important Match-the-Following (Period/Site & Site/State)\n● Period → Site match: Palaeolithic Age → Sohan/Soan River Valley | Mesolithic Age → Bhimbetka\nCaves | Neolithic Age → Burzahom | Chalcolithic Age → Banas Valley (Ahar-Banas culture). [Q42]\n● Site → State match: Nevasa → Maharashtra | Isampur → Karnataka | Didwana → Rajasthan | Gudiyam\nCave → Tamil Nadu. [Q43]\n16. Important Site Pairs (True/False Statement Type)\n● Burzahom (Kashmir) — pit dwelling aur tool industry ke liye famous hai, rock-cut shrines ke liye NAHI\n(galat pair). Chandraketugarh (West Bengal) — terracotta craft ka bada centre hai (sahi pair).\nGaneshwar (Jodhpura culture, Rajasthan) — sainkdo copper objects ke liye famous hai (sahi pair).\n[Q44]"," ● Chandraketugarh West Bengal mein hai, Odisha mein NAHI (galat). Inamgaon Maharashtra ka\nChalcolithic site hai (sahi). Mangadu Kerala ka important Megalithic site hai jaha urn-burials milte hain\n(sahi). Salihundam (Andhra Pradesh) ek Buddhist stupa site hai, rock-cut cave shrines nahi hain (galat).\n[Q45]\n17. Assertion–Reason: Vindhyas to Ganga Valley Migration\n● Stone age ke log Vindhyas se Ganga Valley terminal Pleistocene period mein migrate hue the, kyunki\nclimatic change ki wajah se Vindhyan valley rehne layak nahi rahi thi. Isliye Assertion aur Reason —\ndono sahi hain aur Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation deta hai. [Q47]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Stone Age Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0164","t":"10 Post Mauryan Period","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" POST-MAURYAN PERIOD — FULL MIND MAP\n🏺\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indo-Greek Rulers — Coins & Contemporaries\n2. Saka-Kshatrapas — Rudradaman & Coinage\n3. Foreign Dynasties in Ancient India — Overview & Chronology\n4. Kushan Dynasty — Coinage\n5. Kushan Rulers & Titles\n6. Kushan Era — Kanishka's Coronation & Calendar Systems\n7. Kanishka's Court — Scholars & Contemporaries\n8. Kushan Inscriptions & Foreign Relations\n9. Centres of Learning — Taxila\n10. Shunga Dynasty\n11. The Gandhara School of Art\n12. Kushan-Era Society\n13. The Satavahana Dynasty — Origin, Capital & Rulers\n14. Deccan Dynasties — Vakataka, Chalukya & Ikshvaku\n15. Dynasty-Capital Match List\n16. King Kharavela of Kalinga\n17. Ancient Trade & Contemporary World Rulers\n1. Indo-Greek Rulers — Coins & Contemporaries\n● Indo-Greek ruler Strato-II (25 BC – 10 AD) ne lead coins issue kiye the. [Q1]\n● Greco-Bactrian king Agathocles (~190-180 BC, Bactria aur India ke beech Paropamisadae satrapy ke\nowner) ne apne coins par Sankarshana (Balram) AUR Vasudeva dono ko depict kiya tha — wo bilingual\n(Greek + Brahmi) legends coins par likhne wale pehle Greco-Bactrian ruler bhi the. [Q2]\n● Bimbisara (Haryanka dynasty), King Prasenjit (Koshala) aur Mahatma Buddha — teeno ek doosre ke\ncontemporary the. Lekin Milinda (jinhe Menander bhi kehte hain, ek Indo-Greek ruler, 2nd century BC)\ninn teeno ka samkalin NAHI tha. [Q3]\n● Famous Indo-Greek King Menander ke 16 coins Bairat (ancient Viratnagar, Rajasthan) site se mile hain.\n[Q41]\n2. Saka-Kshatrapas — Rudradaman & Coinage\n● Junagadh (Kathiawar, Gujarat) ke Rudradaman ke inscription (130-150 AD) mein Sanskrit 'Kavya' style\nka sabse purana example milta hai — ye perfect Sanskrit mein likha gaya pehla ever inscription tha,\nBrahmi script mein. [Q4]\n● Junagadh inscription (~150 AD, Sanskrit mein) Rudradaman-I ki achievements bataata hai — unhone\ncultural arts aur Sanskrit literature ko support kiya, aur Mauryan-era Sudarshan lake ke dam ko\nreconstruct karwaya. [Q5]\n● Rudradaman-I ne apne khud ke khazane (treasury) se, bina forced labour use kiye, Sudarshan Lake ko\nrenovate karwaya tha — jo originally Chandragupta Maurya ke time bana tha. [Q6, Q7]\n● Karddamaka Kshatrapas ke coins do metals mein aate the: Silver coins (kaafi frequent the) aur Copper\ncoins (bahut rare the) — ruler Chastana ne dono issue kiye the. [Q8]"," ● Saka-Kshatrapa period mein Gold aur Silver coins ka ratio 1:35 tha. [Q44]\n3. Foreign Dynasties in Ancient India — Overview & Chronology\n● Dynasty-Origin match: Demetrius → Indo-Greek; Rudradaman → Scythians (Sakas); Gondophernes →\nParthian (Pahlavas); Vima (Kadphises) → Kushana. Similarly, Gandhara Art → Kushanas; Junagarh\nRock Inscription → Rudradaman I; Milindapanho → Menander; Taxila Inscription → Patika. [Q9, Q46]\n● Ancient India mein foreign invaders ka sahi chronological order: Greeks (Alexander se, 326 BC) →\nSakas (Scythians, ~1st century BC) → Kushanas (1st century AD). [Q10, Q52]\n● Persian ruler Darius-I (522-486 BC) India ke kuch hisso (North-Western regions) capture karne wale\npehle ruler the — Herodotus ke mutabik unhone Indus river ke aas-paas, Rajputana desert aur Punjab\nke hisso ko jeeta, jo Persian Empire ki 20th satrapy bani. [Q53]\n● Kushana Dynasty ka empire India ke bahar (northern Turpan/Central Asia tak) bhi phaila tha. Mauryan\nempire bhi India ke bahar (modern Iran ke kuch hisse tak) phaila tha — ye 2 hi dynasties hain jinka\nempire India ke bahar bhi tha. [Q39]\n4. Kushan Dynasty — Coinage\n● North aur North-Western India mein sabse zyada copper coins Kushanas ne issue kiye the — Indo-\nGreek kings ne pehle gold coins shuru kiye the, lekin Kushana rulers ne gold aur copper dono coins ko\nregular aur popular banaya. [Q11]\n● Ancient India mein sabse pehle gold coins large aur regular scale par Kushanas ne issue kiye the. [Q12]\n● Kushan ruler Kanishka ke coins par Buddha ko depict kiya gaya hai — Kanishka Buddhism ke bade\npatron the, unke coins mein Hellenistic, Zoroastrian aur Indian deities ka mix milta hai. [Q13]\n● Vima Kadphises (Kanishka-I ke pita) Kushan dynasty ke pehle ruler the jinhone gold coins issue kiye\n(halaki Indo-Greeks ne gold coins ko popular banaya tha) — unke predecessor Kujula Kadphises sirf\ncopper coins circulate karte the. [Q14, Q15, Q16]\n● Yaudheya copper coins par 6-mukh wale God Kartikeya ki khadi hui figure (mor ke saath) depict hoti hai\n— Yaudheya coins ke evidence Puranas aur Ashtadhyayi mein bhi milte hain. [Q18]\n5. Kushan Rulers & Titles\n● Vima Kadphises (jinhe Kadphises II bhi kehte hain, Kanishka-I ke pita) ne 'Sarvalokeshvara' (poori\nduniya ke swami) ki title apnayi thi — ye unki imperial mahatvakanksha dikhati hai. [Q17]\n6. Kushan Era — Kanishka's Coronation & Calendar Systems\n● Sarnath ki Buddhist image (Kanishka se related) 81 A.D. ki dated hai — ye Kanishka ke coronation (~78\nA.D. maana jaata hai) ke 3 saal baad establish hui thi. [Q19]"," ● Kanishka ke coronation ki tareekh controversial thi — London mein 1913 aur 1960 mein 2 international\nconventions hui, aur 1960 ke convention mein common consent 78 A.D. par bana. Yehi Saka Samvat\n(Era) ki bhi shuruat maani jaati hai. [Q20]\n● Jain texts ke mutabik, Vikramaditya (57 BC) ke successor ko Sakas ne 135 Vikram Samvat mein hara\ndiya tha — is jeet ko celebrate karne ke liye Saka Samvat calendar shuru hua, jo 135-57 = 78 A.D. se\nstart hota hai. Zyadatar historians Kanishka ko iska originator maante hain. [Q21]\n● Vikrama Samvat 57 B.C. se shuru hua — Jain holy texts ke mutabik, Mahavira ke Nirvana (527 BC) aur\nVikrama Samvat ke beech 470 saal ka antar hai (527-470=57 BC). [Q24]\n● Saka aur Vikrama Samvat ke beech ka antar exactly 135 saal hai (57+78=135) — Gregorian year mein\n57 jodkar Vikrama Samvat milta hai, aur 78 ghatakar Saka Samvat milta hai. [Q22]\n● Indian national calendar (Saka Era par based) ka Chaitra month ka 1st din normal year mein 22nd\nMarch, aur leap year mein 21st March ko corresponds karta hai. [Q23]\n● December 2009 mein Saka Samvat ka saal 1931 hoga (2009-78=1931). [Q25]\n7. Kanishka's Court — Scholars & Contemporaries\n● Ashvaghosa (Kanishka ke poet laureate, Saundaranand/Buddhacharita/Sariputraprakaran ke author)\naur Vasumitra (jinhone 4th Buddhist Council ki lead ki) — dono Kanishka ke contemporary the. Kalidas\nGupta period se the, aur Kamban Kanishka ke samkalin nahi the. [Q26, Q27]\n● Kanishka ke darbar se associated scholars the: Parsva, Vasumitra, Ashvaghosa, Nagarjuna, Charaka\naur Mathara. Lekin Patanjali (Mahabhasya ke author) Shunga period se the, Kanishka se NAHI juday\nthe. [Q28]\n● Kanishka-I ke darbar mein Ashvaghosa, Parshva aur Vasumitra the. Vishakhadatta (Mudrarakshasa ke\nauthor) baad mein, Gupta period mein hue — wo Kanishka ke darbar se juday NAHI the. [Q29]\n8. Kushan Inscriptions & Foreign Relations\n● Rabatak Inscription (1993 mein Afghanistan ke Rabatak, Surkh Kotal ke pass se mila, Greek script +\nBactrian language mein, Kanishka se related) mein 4 cities ka naam hai: Saketa, Kaushambi,\nPataliputra aur Sri Champa. Shravasti ka naam is inscription mein NAHI hai. [Q30]\n● 73-94 AD ke beech, Kanishka ne Han princess se shaadi ka proposal bheja tha jo reject ho gaya —\nbadle mein unhone Chinese general Pan Chao par attack kiya, lekin ek chhoti Chinese force se haar\ngaye. [Q38]\n9. Centres of Learning — Taxila\n● Taxila University alag-alag countries ke students ke liye ek milne-julne ki jagah thi. Ayurvedacharya\nCharak aur Ayurvedacharya Jivak (Bimbisara ke darbar ke) — dono ne Taxila mein padhai ki thi\n(Kautilya, Chandragupta Maurya, King Prasenjit, Vasubandhu bhi yahan padhe the). [Q31]"," 10. Shunga Dynasty\n● Pushyamitra Shunga (last Mauryan ruler Brihadratha ke commander, jinhone 184 BCE mein\nBrihadratha ko maar kar Shunga dynasty banayi) ne 2 Ashwamedha Yajna kiye the — iski jaankari\nAyodhya inscription se milti hai. [Q32]\n● Shungas ke ancestors Ujjain se the. Is dynasty ke last ruler Devabhuti the, jinhe unke apne minister\nVasudeva Kanva ne maara. [Q33]\n● Shunga dynasty ke baad Kanva dynasty ne India par raj kiya — Kanva bhi Shunga jaise hi Brahmin the.\n[Q34]\n11. The Gandhara School of Art\n● Kanishka ke encouragement/protection ke saath, Gandhara School of Art, Kushan period mein khoob\ndevelop hui — ye Greek art se bahut influenced thi. [Q42, Q43]\n● Gandhara art style, Indian aur Greek art ka synthesis (mel) hai — Greek, Syrian, Persian aur Indian\nartistic influences se develop hui. Ise Indo-Greek Art, Greco-Buddhist ya Greco-Roman bhi kaha jaata\nhai, kyunki iska subject mainly Buddha hota tha. Saka aur Kushan era mein flourish hui. [Q48, Q49, Q50]\n● Gandhara sculptures banane mein 'green schist' (aur baad mein stucco) medium use hota tha —\nHellenistic (Greek) artistic elements se heavily influenced thi. [Q51]\n● Afghanistan ka Bamiyan, Buddha ki statues ke liye famous tha — ye statues Bamiyan ki pahadiyo ko\nkaatkar banayi gayi thi. Taliban ne 2001 mein inhe destroy kar diya. [Q47]\n12. Kushan-Era Society\n● Child marriage ki pratha Kushan period (1st century) mein shuru hui — women mein 'Upanayana'\nceremony khatam ho gayi thi, aur 8-10 saal ki age mein hi shaadi hona best maana jaane laga tha — ye\nwomen ki social status ko sabse nichle stage tak le gaya. [Q40]\n13. The Satavahana Dynasty — Origin, Capital & Rulers\n● Satavahana dynasty, Maurya ke baad South India ki sabse powerful dynasty thi — Puranas ke mutabik,\nKanva king Susharma ki hatya ke baad Sindhuk/Simuka/Shiprak ne is dynasty ki sthapna ki. Diye gaye\noptions mein Satavahana hi sabse purani dynasty maani jaati hai (Chalukya, Pallava, Rashtrakuta baad\nmein aayi). [Q36, Q37, Q54]\n● 30 Andhra Satavahana rajaon ki sabse lambi list Matsya Purana mein milti hai. [Q55]\n● Satavahanas ki actual capital Pratisthan (Paithan bhi kehte hain, aaj ke Maharashtra mein) thi — halaki\nunki initial capital Amravati (Dharanikota) mani jaati hai. [Q56, Q57]\n● Gautamiputra Satakarni, Brahmanism ke patron the — unhone apni 'Four Varna' system ke logo ke\nbeech inter-caste marriage allow nahi ki, isliye unhe 'Varna System ka protector' kaha jaata hai. Nashik\ninscription (unki maa Gautami Balashri ki) mein unhe 'Ekabrahmana' bhi kaha gaya hai. [Q35, Q58]"," ● Assertion-Reason: Satavahana period mein Sanskrit, Prakrit aur folk languages sab develop hui (sahi),\nkyunki Satavahana kings ne active roop se inn sab languages ke literary use ko promote kiya (sahi\nReason bhi) — jaise King Hala ne 'Gaha Sattasai' compile ki. Satavahana rulers ne Prakrit ko Sanskrit\nse zyada patronize kiya (isse official language banaya), aur arts ke public aspect ko bhi bahut\nencouragement mila. [Q61, Q62]\n● Amaravati Stupa (Andhra Pradesh) mein 'Aryak-Pillars' (Ayaka pillars) wale platform ki khaasiyat milti\nhai — ye drum se 4 cardinal points par nikalte hain, Andhra region ke stupas ki typical feature hai. [Q64]\n● Dynasty-Coin Metal match: zyadatar options sahi hain, lekin 'Satavahanas – Gold' GALAT match hai —\nSatavahanas ne Lead, Copper, Bronze, Silver aur Potin (Copper+Silver+Lead ka mix) coins banaye,\ngold coins nahi. [Q45]\n14. Deccan Dynasties — Vakataka, Chalukya & Ikshvaku\n● Deccan dynasties ka chronological order: Satavahanas (1st century BC, Simuk ne founded) →\nVakatakas (3rd century AD, Vindhyashakti ne founded) → Chalukyas (Gujarat ke Solankis, 10th century\nAD mein Mulraj I ne founded; Badami Chalukyas 6th century AD mein pehle hi emerge hui thi). [Q60]\n● Satavahana dynasty ke weak hone ke baad, Vakataka dynasty Dakshinapath (Deccan) mein power\nmein aayi (sahi). Vakataka dynasty ke founder Vindhyashakti the, Pravarasen I NAHI (galat statement).\nPravarasen I, Vindhyashakti ke bete the, ulta nahi. [Q63]\n● Ikshvaku dynasty ke rulers ko Puranas mein 'Shriparvatiya' kaha jaata hai (Andhra ke Shriparvata\nregion ke rajaon ke liye) — ye Satavahanas ke patronage mein Lords the, lekin unke decline ke baad\nIkshvakus ne apni independence declare ki. Shrisantmula is dynasty ke founder the. [Q66]\n● Inscription-Ruler match: Bhitari Pillar Inscription (Ghazipur, UP) Skandagupta (Gupta ruler) se related\nhai, Chalukya king Pulkeshin II se NAHI (ye galat pair hai — Pulkeshin II ka inscription Aihole,\nKarnataka mein hai). [Q65]\n15. Dynasty-Capital Match List\n● Dynasty-Capital match: Shunga → Pataliputra; Satavahana → Paithan/Pratishthan; Kadamb →\nBanvasi; Chandel → Mahoba (aur Khajuraho). [Q59]\n16. King Kharavela of Kalinga\n● King Kharavela, Kalinga (aaj ka Odisha) ke Chedi (Mahameghavahana) dynasty ke raja the — unke\nbaare mein zyadatar jaankari Hathigumpha inscription (Udayagiri Caves, Odisha, undated aur partially\ndamaged) se milti hai. [Q68, Q70, Q72, Q73]\n● Kharavela, Jainism ke ek prominent follower aur patron the — unhone Jain monks ko patronage di aur\nUdayagiri-Khandagiri hills mein unke rehne ke liye caves banwayi. [Q69, Q71]\n● Udayagiri (18 caves) aur Khandagiri (15 caves) — Bhubaneswar, Odisha mein rock-cut caves ke liye\nfamous hain, jinme natural aur artificial dono tarah ki caves hain. Hathigumpha inscription Udayagiri\ncaves se mila hai, Khandagiri se NAHI. [Q74]"," 17. Ancient Trade & Contemporary World Rulers\n● Assertion-Reason: Kushanas Persian Gulf aur Red Sea ke through trade karte the (sahi — Periplus of\nthe Erythraean Sea aur Arikamedu excavations se evidence milta hai) — lekin unke paas ek well-\norganized/highly-qualified naval force thi, iska koi evidence NAHI milta (galat Reason). [Q67]\n● 'Periplus of the Erythraean Sea' (1st century CE ke aas-paas likha gaya) ek anonymous (author\nunknown) Greek-speaking merchant ka likha document hai. [Q76]\n● Ancient India mein rivers (Ganga, Indus, Kaveri) aur ports (jaise Muziris, Sopara, Lothal) trade aur\ntransport ke bade centres the — goods ki storage ke liye bade warehouses (entrepots) bhi use hote the.\n[Q77]\n● Eastern Roman ruler Justinian ka sabse bada contribution 'Law' (kanoon) ke field mein tha — unka\n'Corpus Juris Civilis' (laws ka collection) aaj bhi kai modern states mein civil law ka aadhar hai. [Q75]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Post-Mauryan Period Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0165","t":"11 Gupta and Post Gupta Period","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" GUPTA & POST-GUPTA PERIOD — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Gupta Dynasty — Timeline, Founders & the Golden Age\n2. Samudragupta — Conquests, Titles & the Prayag Prashasti\n3. Chandragupta II — Accession, Saka Conquest & Coinage\n4. The Gupta-Vakataka Alliance\n5. Kumaragupta I — The Dashpur (Mandsaur) Inscription\n6. Gupta Royal Genealogy\n7. Skandagupta & the Huna Invasions\n8. Later Hunas & Their Decline — Toramana, Mihirakula & Yashodharman\n9. Gupta Administration & Land Grants\n10. Trade, Ports, Guilds & Industry\n11. Science, Medicine & Mathematics\n12. Nine Gems & Gupta Court Culture\n13. Gupta & Post-Gupta Coinage\n14. Society & Social Customs\n15. Land Revenue & Taxation System\n16. Urban Decline in the Gupta Period\n17. Era & Calendar Systems\n18. Foreign Travellers of the Gupta Period — Fa-Hien & Sungyun\n19a. Sankhya Darshan\n19b. Yoga Darshan\n19c. Nyaya Darshan\n19d. Charvaka (Lokayata) Darshan\n19e. Mimamsa Darshan\n19f. Vaisheshika Darshan & the Six Systems Overview\n19g. Vedanta Darshan — Advaita & Vishishtadvaita\n20. Post-Gupta Regional Dynasties — Later Guptas, Maukharis & Maitrakas\n21. Harshavardhana — Rise, Capital & Conquests\n22. Hiuen-Tsang's India\n23. Post-Harsha Foreign Travellers — I-tsing & Others\n24. Nalanda University\n25. Feudalism in Post-Gupta India\n26. Adi Shankaracharya\n27. Court Poets & Miscellaneous Match Lists\n1. Gupta Dynasty — Timeline, Founders & the Golden Age\n● Gupta dynasty ki sthapna King Srigupta ne ~275 AD mein ki thi. Lekin dynasty ke pehle powerful ruler\nChandragupta I the, jinhone 319-335 AD mein raj kiya aur 'Maharajadhiraja' ki title li. [Q1]\n● Ancient India mein Gupta dynasty ke raj ko 'Golden Age' maana jaata hai — art, architecture, literature,\nscience, maths aur culture mein excellent development ki wajah se. [Q67]\n● Ruler-Title match: Ashoka → Priyadarsin; Samudragupta → Parakramank; Chandragupta-II →\nVikramaditya; Skandagupta → Kramaditya. [Q64]\n2. Samudragupta — Conquests, Titles & the Prayag Prashasti\n● Historian V.A. Smith ne apni book 'Early History of India' mein Samudragupta (335-375 AD) ko unki\ngreat military achievements ki wajah se 'Napoleon of India/Ancient India' kaha. [Q3, Q4]"," ● Samudragupta hi Gupta dynasty ke pehle ruler the jinhone 'Param Bhagavata' ki title li thi — ye Nalanda\naur Gaya se mile copperplate inscription se pata chalta hai (halaki UPPSC ki purani key mein\nChandragupta-II galat likha gaya tha). [Q6, Q7]\n● Allahabad Pillar (Prayag Prashasti) originally Ashoka ne banwaya tha, lekin baad mein Harisena dwara\nSanskrit mein likhi Samudragupta ki tareef wali 'Prayag Prashasti' ke liye famous ho gaya — isme\nJahangir aur Birbal ke naam bhi likhe hain (isliye C aur D dono sahi hain). Ye pillar Samudragupta ke\nreign aur unki military campaigns ki jaankari deta hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10, Q12]\n● Prayag Prashasti mein Koshala ke raja ka naam Mahendra likha hai — Dakshinapath ke doosre\nkingdoms/rajaon ke saath. [Q11]\n● Samudragupta ko 'Lichchhavi-Dauhitra' (Lichchhavi ka pota) kaha jaata tha — unki maa Kumaradevi,\nLichchhavi dynasty ki rajkumari thi. Unke pita Chandragupta I the. [Q13]\n● Tej Ram Sharma ki book ke mutabik, Samudragupta ne Ashwamedha Yajna perform kiya tha, jiske\nbaad unhone 'Prithivyah Pratham Veer' (dharti ka pehla veer, jiska koi rival nahi) ki title li. [Q14]\n● Samudragupta ke court poet-minister Harisena ne Sanskrit mein Allahabad Pillar par 'Prayag Prashasti'\nlikhi thi. 'Devichandraguptam' Vishakhadatta ne likha tha, Harisena ne nahi. [Q15]\n● Samudragupta ne haraye gaye rajaon ka match: Dhananjaya → Kusthalpura; Nilaraja → Avamukta;\nUgrasena → Palaka; Vishnugopa → Kanchi. [Q16]\n● Chinese source ke mutabik, Sri Lanka (Ceylon) ke Buddhist raja Meghavarman ne Samudragupta ke\npaas ek missionary bheja tha, Bodh Gaya mein ek Buddhist monastery banane ki permission maangne\n— Samudragupta ne permission de di. [Q82]\n3. Chandragupta II — Accession, Saka Conquest & Coinage\n● Chandragupta-II 'Vikramaditya' ka doosra naam 'Devagupta' bhi mila hai — ye Sanchi aur Vakataka\ninscriptions se pata chalta hai. Unhe Devaraja aur Devashri bhi kaha jaata tha. [Q5]\n● Mehrauli Iron Pillar (Delhi ke Quwwat-ul-Islam mosque mein) par 'Chandra' naam ke king ka zikr hai, jo\ngenerally Chandragupta II se identify kiya jaata hai — originally ye pillar Vishnugiri (Udaigiri hills ke\npass) mein tha. [Q17]\n● Samudragupta ke baad unke bade bete Ramagupta raja bane, lekin Sakas ke invasion ka saamna na\nkar paane ki wajah se unhone apni patni surrender karne ki sehmati de di. Chhote bhai Chandragupta II\nne isse virodh karke Ramagupta ko maar diya, unki widow Dhruv Devi se shaadi ki, aur Sakas ko\nharaakar gaddi par baithe. [Q18]\n● Chandragupta-II ne last Saka king Rudrasimha-III ko haraakar Saka power khatam ki, isliye unhe 'Saka\nConqueror' (Sakari) kaha jaata hai. Isi jeet ko celebrate karne ke liye unhone silver coins (Rupaka) issue\nkiye — wo pehle Gupta ruler the jinhone silver coins issue kiye. [Q26, Q27]\n● Sakas par jeet ke baad, Chandragupta-II ke silver coins iski proof hain (Saka Kshatrapa coins jaise,\n~30-33 grains weight ke) — Gujarat aur Malwa ka kuch hissa unke empire mein add hua. [Q28, Q29]\n● Chinese Buddhist monk Fa-Hien, Chandragupta-II (Vikramaditya) ke reign mein (early 5th century) India\naaye the — unka main purpose authentic Buddhist texts collect karna tha. [Q30]\n4. The Gupta-Vakataka Alliance"," ● Vakataka king Pravarasena-I ne 4 Ashwamedha Yajna perform ki thi, aur bahut se Vedic oblations bhi\nkiye. Doosre Vakataka ruler Pravarasena-II ne literature mein interest liya, aur 'Setubandha' likhi. [Q2]\n● Chandragupta II ne apni beti Prabhavati (Kubernaga se) ki shaadi Vakataka dynasty ke Rudrasena II se\nkarke apni position strengthen ki — ye alliance unke Saka campaigns ke liye strategically bahut\nimportant tha. [Q31]\n● Rudrasena II ki mrityu ke baad, Prabhavati Gupta ne apne minor beto ke liye regent ki tarah Vakataka\nEmpire par khud raj kiya. [Q32]\n● Vakataka dynasty ke founder Vindhyashakti the, unke successor Pravarasena I ko 'real/actual founder'\nbhi mana jaata hai — unke time boundary North mein Bundelkhand se Deccan (Hyderabad tak) thi.\nUnhone 'Samrat' ki title li aur kai Ashvamedha Yajna kiye. [Q33]\n● Inscription-ruler match mein galti: Prabhavati Gupta ka Udayagiri Cave Inscription se koi record NAHI\nmila — unka prominent inscription 'Poona copper plate' hai. Baaki matches sahi hain: Kumargupta I-\nMandsaur, Patik-Takshashila, Chandragupta II-Udayagiri cave, Samudragupta-Eran. [Q34]\n5. Kumaragupta I — The Dashpur (Mandsaur) Inscription\n● Dashpur (Mandsaur) inscription ko duniya ka 'first advertisement' maana jaata hai — Kumargupta-I ke\nperiod ka hai, isme silk trade aur silk weavers guild ka advertisement/information hai. [Q35, Q37]\n● Mandsaur-Prashasti, Vatsabhatta (Vatsabhatti) ne, jo Kumargupta-I ke samkalin the, Malwa mein\ncompose ki thi — isme Kumargupta-I ki achievements ka varnan hai, aur ye bhi bataya gaya hai ki silk\nworkers ne yahan ek sun temple banwaya tha. [Q36]\n● Dashpur inscription Bhavabhuti ne NAHI, balki Vatsabhatti ne compose ki thi. Isme likha hai ki Lata\nregion (Gujarat) ke silk weavers ke guild ne Dashpur mein Sun Temple banwaya. [Q38]\n6. Gupta Royal Genealogy\n● Gupta ruler-queen match: Chandragupta I → Kumaradevi (Lichchhavi princess); Samudragupta →\nDuttadevi; Chandragupta II → Kubernaga (Naga princess); Kumargupta I → Anantdevi. [Q39]\n7. Skandagupta & the Huna Invasions\n● Hunas ka pehla invasion Skandagupta ke reign mein hua tha, aur unhone Hunas ko decisively haraya\n— halaki ye ek raid jaisa tha jisse India par koi lasting impact nahi pada, isne Gupta empire ke\nresources ko bahut drain kar diya aur uske decline ko tez kar diya. [Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23]\n● Bhitari Pillar Inscription (Saidpur tehsil, Ghazipur dist., UP) se pata chalta hai ki Skandagupta ne Hunas\nko badly defeat kiya tha. [Q24]\n● Gupta Empire ke downfall ke reasons mein Huna invasions, feudatories ka uदय, aur weak successors\n(kuch Buddhism apnakar apni martial spirit kho baithe) shaamil the — Arab invasion (Muhammad bin\nQasim, 712 AD, medieval era) is decline ki wajah NAHI thi. [Q25]"," 8. Later Hunas & Their Decline — Toramana, Mihirakula & Yashodharman\n● Toramana, Hephthalite Empire (jise Huna/White Huns bhi kehte hain) ke ek famous king the — unhone\nlate 5th/early 6th century AD mein India par dusra Huna invasion lead kiya. [Q78]\n● Mihirakula (Toramana ke bete, ek fierce Huna ruler) ko Aulikara king Yashodharman (Malwa) ne\ndecisively haraya (~528 AD ya 495 AD, sources ke hisaab se alag) — isse Huna power practically\nkhatam ho gayi. [Q79]\n● Vasula Kavi ne Yashodharman ke Sondani (Sondhni) pillar inscription ko compose kiya tha — ye\ninscription Yashodharman ki Mihirakula par jeet ko describe karta hai. [Q172]\n9. Gupta Administration & Land Grants\n● Gupta period mein administrative divisions ka sahi sequence: Bhukti (Uparik ke under, province) →\nVishaya (Vishayapati ke under, district) → Vithi (Aayulan/Vithimahattar ke under, sub-district) → Grama\n(village, sabse chhoti unit). [Q40]\n● Gupta dynasty ke rulers ne temples aur Brahmins ko sabse zyada villages (Agraharas) daan diye the —\nis land se hone wali income daan lene wale (donee) ko milti thi, isse feudal structure mazboot hua. [Q66]\n● Gupta Emperors apni divine origin (supernatural) mein believe karte the aur khud ke liye divine rights\nclaim karte the (sahi). Mauryas ke ulta, Gupta administration highly centralized NAHI thi — ye\ndecentralized, feudal-jaisi system follow karti thi jisme provincial governors ko zyada power thi. Unhone\nBrahmins/temples ko land donation (Agraharas/Brahmadeya) ki tradition ko aage badhaya. [Q83]\n10. Trade, Ports, Guilds & Industry\n● 3rd century AD mein jab Huna invasion ne Roman Empire ko khatam kiya, to Indian merchants ne\nSouth-East Asian trade par zyada bharosa karna shuru kiya, kyunki West ke saath direct trade links\ndisrupt ho gaye the. [Q41]\n● Tamralipti port (Bengal) North India ke trade ke liye eastern port tha — South-East Asia, China, Lanka,\nJava tak trade hota tha. Bhrigu Kachchha (Bharuch) western coast ka important port tha, jaha se Gupta\nrulers western countries se trade karte the. [Q42, Q43]\n● India, South-East Asia ke saath Bay of Bengal ke through cultural contacts aur trade links isliye maintain\nkar paaya kyunki Bay of Bengal se aane wali monsoon winds sea voyages ke liye predictable aur\nfavourable thi. [Q44]\n● Ancient India ke Guilds (Shreni) autonomously kaam karti thi — King inka chief administrative authority\nnahi hota tha, har guild ka apna head hota tha. Guilds salary, job rules, standards aur prices decide\nkarne ki power rakhti thi, aur unke apne laws + judicial power bhi hoti thi apne members ko punish karne\nke liye. [Q45]\n● Gujarat, Bengal, Deccan aur Tamil Country — Gupta period mein textile manufacturing (kapda banane)\nke liye famous the. [Q46]\n● Trade guilds ke head ko 'Sarthavaha' ya 'Srenipramukh' kehte the — unke rules 'Samay' aur\n'Srenidharma' kehlaate the. Ye term Vaishya (trader) varna se associated hai. [Q47]"," ● 3rd century AD mein Warangal (aaj ka Telangana) iron implements (loha ke saman) banane ke liye\nfamous tha — yahan 'Agaria' log rehte the, jinka traditional occupation iron-making tha. [Q76]\n● Ghantasala aur Kadura (East Coast) aur Chaul (West Coast) Gupta period mein foreign trade handle\nkarne wale prominent ports the. [Q77]\n● Post-Harsha period ke sources mein 'Hundi' ko 'bill of exchange' (financial instrument) ki tarah treat kiya\njaata tha — RBI ke mutabik ye Indian subcontinent mein trade/credit transactions mein use hota tha.\n[Q159]\n11. Science, Medicine & Mathematics\n●\n Trap: Gupta period ke medicine scholars poochne wale questions mein Sushruta ka naam galti se\n⚠️\ndiya jaata hai — asal mein Sushruta ~600 BC ke the, Gupta period (275 AD se) se ~875 saal pehle.\nShaunaka Rigveda ke sage the. Shudraka aur Saumilla Gupta period ke dramatist/playwright the,\nmedicine se nahi jude. [Q48, Q49]\n● Dhanvantari, Charaka aur Sushruta — teeno Ayurveda (medicine) ke great scholars the.\nBhaskaracharya inn se ALAG hain — wo astronomer-mathematician the, jinhone 'Siddhanta Shiromani'\naur 'Lilavati' likhi. [Q50]\n● 'Lilavati' (mathematics ki famous book) Bhaskaracharya (Bhaskara-II) ne likhi thi. [Q51]\n● Scientific progress: 1st century AD mein surgical instruments use hote the (Sushruta Samhita mein) —\nsahi. Human organ transplant ancient time mein possible NAHI tha — galat. Sine/Cosine/inverse-Sine\nGupta period mein pata thi (Surya Siddhanta, Aryabhatiya mein, 5th century AD) — sahi. Brahmagupta\nne 7th century AD mein cyclic quadrilaterals describe ki — sahi. [Q52]\n● Fa-Hien ne apni yatra mein Pataliputra (capital) mein ek hospital ka zikr kiya hai, jo dayalu logo dwara\nfund kiya jaata tha — gareeb aur laachaar patients ki dekhbhal hoti thi, doctors unhe dekhte the, khana-\ndawai milti thi. [Q53]\n● Aryabhatta (mathematician-astronomer, 'Aryabhatiyam' ke author) sabse pehle explain karne wale the ki\ndin-raat Prithvi ke apni axis par ghoomne (rotation) se hote hain. [Q56]\n12. Nine Gems & Gupta Court Culture\n● Chandragupta-II ke 'Nine Gems' (Navratna) mein Kshapanak astrology se associated the. Baaki\nNavratna the: Kalidasa (Poet), Dhanvantari (Physician), Varahamihira (Astronomer), Amar Singh\n(Lexicographer), Shanku (Architect), waghera. [Q54]\n● Kalidasa, Chandragupta-II (Vikramaditya) ke Navratnas mein se ek the. [Q55]\n● Chess (Chaturanga) ka origin India mein, Gupta period mein hua — iska matlab army ke 4 divisions\n(infantry, cavalry, elephantry, chariotry) se hai. India se ye Persia (Iran) phir Europe pahunchi. [Q85]\n● 'Mrichchhakatika' (The Little Clay Cart), Shudraka ne likhi thi — isme ek ameer vyapari (Charudatta) aur\nek courtesan ki beti (Vasantasena) ki love story hai, saath hi Gupta period ke samajik badlaav bhi\ndikhaye gaye hain. [Q86]\n13. Gupta & Post-Gupta Coinage"," ● Gupta gold coins 'Dinara' kehlaate the — Chinese traveller Fa-Hien ke mutabik log bade transactions ke\nliye Dinar use karte the, jabki roz-marra ke chhote transactions ke liye cowries (Kaudi) use hoti thi. [Q57,\nQ58]\n● Gupta silver coins 'Rupaka' kehlaate the. Gupta coins UP, Bihar, Bengal, MP, Rajasthan aur Odisha\nmein mile hain — Rajasthan ka 'Bayana hoard' (Bharatpur) sabse zyada coins wali jagah hai. [Q59]\n● Chandragupta-I hi pehle Gupta ruler the jinhone coins issue ki (famous 'Chandragupta-Kumaradevi'\ntype gold coins) — Ghatotkacha aur Srigupta (early Gupta rulers) ke coins issue karne ka koi historical\nevidence nahi hai. [Q60]\n● 'Gadhaiya' ek silver coin thi — early medieval India mein Sassanian coins ki tarz par jaari ki gayi thi.\n[Q128]\n14. Society & Social Customs\n● Gupta period ke Sanskrit natakon mein women aur Sudras Prakrit bolte the, jabki upper varnas\n(classes) ke log Sanskrit bolte the. [Q61]\n● 'Satipratha' ka sabse pehla inscriptional evidence Eran (MP) se mila hai — ye inscription 510 AD\n(Bhanugupta ke reign) ka hai, jisme ek war commander 'Goparaja' ki patni ke sati hone ka zikr hai. [Q62]\n● Ancient India mein sirf Early Vedic age ko chhodkar, women ki equal status kabhi truly nahi rahi —\nGupta, Maurya aur Chola periods mein women ki restricted/inferior condition ke evidence mile hain\n(child marriage, Sati, property rights ki kami waghera). [Q68]\n15. Land Revenue & Taxation System\n● Gupta age mein land revenue rate production ka 1/6th (chhata hissa) tha — inscriptions mein ise\n'Udranga' aur 'Bhaga' kaha jaata tha. Dharmashastras (religious books) mein bhi legally prescribed rate\n1/6 (Shadbhaga) tha — ye Hindu law ke mutabik valid tax tha. [Q69, Q70, Q71]\n● 'Aprahat' un lands ko kaha jaata tha jo uncultivable/unploughed forest land thi. Cultivation ke layak land\nko 'Kshetra' aur wasteland ko 'Khila' kehte the. [Q72]\n● 'Kulyavapa' aur 'Dronavapa' Gupta period mein land measurement ke liye use hone wale terms the —\nye batate the ki kitni zameen mein ek 'Kulya' ya 'Drona' measure ka beej boya ja sakta hai. [Q73]\n● Gupta Empire ne tax-free agrarian land mostly Brahmins aur temples ko di — is tarah ke tax-free land\ngrant ko 'Agrahara' ya 'Brahmadeya' kaha jaata tha. [Q74]\n● Ancient India mein irrigation (sinchai) tax 'Udakabhaga' (Udakabhogam) kehlaata tha. Hiranya cash tax\ntha, Udranga Gupta period ka land tax tha, aur Uparnika (Uparikara) cultivators par extra tax tha. [Q75]\n● 'Vishti' (forced labour) state, provincial governor ya local chief dwara enforce ki jaati thi — Gupta copper\ninscriptions mein ise tax ke ek form ki tarah mention kiya gaya hai, jo bina wage ke hoti thi. MP aur\nKathiawar regions mein prevalent thi (Junagadh inscription se pata chalta hai). [Q84]\n16. Urban Decline in the Gupta Period"," ● Gupta period mein towns ka gradual decline ek important feature tha — river valleys mein prosperous\nrahe zyadatar shehar is period mein decline hue. Jab Hiuen-Tsang India aaye (post-Gupta), tab\nPataliputra jaisa bada shehar lagbhag ek gaon jaisa ban gaya tha. Mathura, Sonpur aur Sohgaura mein\nbhi is decline ke evidence mile hain. [Q65]\n17. Era & Calendar Systems\n● Gupta Samvat (era) Chandragupta-I ne 319-320 AD mein, apni gaddi par baithne ke time, shuru ki thi.\n[Q63]\n● Era match: Vikram era → Vikramaditya ne 57/58 BC mein Saka par jeet ke occasion par shuru ki. Saka\nera → Kanishka ne 78 AD mein shuru ki. Gupta era → Chandragupta-I ne 319 AD mein shuru ki\n(question mein 320 AD ke sabse close match). Kali era → 3102 BC mein shuru maani jaati hai. [Q126]\n● Statements sahi: Vikram Samvat 57/58 BC mein shuru hua, Saka Samvat 78 AD mein. Gupta dynasty\nSrigupta ne banayi thi, lekin Gupta era ki shuruaat Chandragupta-I (319 AD) ke reign se maani jaati hai.\nMuhammad Bin Qasim ne 8th century mein Sindh annex kiya tha, lekin India mein Muslim rule officially\n1192 AD mein Shihabuddin Ghori ki jeet ke baad shuru hui. [Q127]\n● Badami rock inscription of Pulakesin I, Saka year 465 ki hai — ise Vikrama Samvat mein convert karne\nke liye: 465+78=543 AD, phir 543+58=601 Vikram Samvat. [Q129]\n● Vikram Samvat ko 'Krit Samvat' aur 'Malav Samvat' bhi kehte hain — ye King Vikramaditya ne 57/58 BC\nmein shuru kiya tha. [Q130]\n● Chalukya inscription jo Saka era ke 556 saal ki hai, wo Gregorian calendar mein 556+78=634 AD ke\nbarabar hai (Saka era Kanishka ne 78 AD mein launch ki thi). [Q131]\n18. Foreign Travellers of the Gupta Period — Fa-Hien & Sungyun\n● Chinese pilgrim Sungyun (Song Yun), early 6th century (518 AD) mein India aaye the — unhone 3 saal\nIndia mein reh kar Buddha ki teachings ke texts collect kiye. [Q80]\n● Sungyun actually 518 se 521 AD tak India mein rahe — diye gaye time-bracket options mein se koi bhi\nexactly match nahi karta, isliye 'None of the above' sahi jawab hai. [Q81]\n● Statements galat: Fa-Hien, Kanishka ke 4th Buddhist Council (1st century AD) mein attend nahi kar\nsakte the, kyunki wo Chandragupta-II ke reign mein (~399 AD) aaye the, jo Kanishka se sadiyo baad\ntha. Hiuen-Tsang Harsha se milkar unhe Buddhism ka strong patron paaya, unke against nahi the —\nmilne ke baad Harsha ne Mahayana Buddhism ko royal patronage di. [Q166]\n● Statements swap ho gaye the: Fa-Hien Chandragupta II ke reign mein India aaye the (Harsha ke reign\nmein NAHI), aur Hiuen Tsang Harsha ke reign mein aaye the (Chandragupta II ke reign mein NAHI) —\ndono statements is form mein galat hain. [Q167]\n19a. Sankhya Darshan\n● Sankhya Darshan (India ke sabse purane orthodox philosophical schools mein se ek) ke Acharya\n(propounder) Maharshi Kapila hain — unhone 'Sankhya Sutra' aur 'Tatvasamas' compose kiye. [Q87,\nQ88, Q89]"," ● Sankhya School Hindu philosophy ke 6 orthodox schools ka hissa hai — ye rebirth/soul ke\ntransmigration ko accept karta hai. Iske mutabik nescience (ignorance) hi dukh ka karan hai, aur self-\nknowledge se liberation milta hai. [Q90]\n● Kapila Muni Sankhya philosophy ke sabse pehle propounder maane jaate hain (sahi). Is philosophy ke\nmutabik insaan ki zindagi nature ki forces se shaped hoti hai, kisi divine entity se nahi — ye strongly\nDualism (Prakriti aur Purusha) mein believe karta hai (sahi). [Q91]\n● 'Satkaryavada' (cause-effect ka doctrine, jisme effect pehle se hi cause mein exist karta hai) Sankhya\nphilosophy ka main doctrine hai. [Q92]\n19b. Yoga Darshan\n● Maharshi Patanjali 'Yoga Darshan' ke founder/propagator maane jaate hain — halaki Yoga ki tradition\nbahut purani hai (Upanishads, Mahabharat, Jain-Buddha texts mein bhi mention hai), Patanjali ne isse\nek complete philosophical system ki tarah explain kiya. [Q93, Q94]\n● Ashtanga Yoga (Patanjali ke Yoga Sutras mein diye 8-limbed path) mein 8 practices hain: Yama,\nNiyama, Asana, Pranayama, Pratyahara, Dharana, Dhyana aur Samadhi. 'Anusmriti' Ashtanga Yoga ka\nhissa NAHI hai. [Q95]\n● Ashtanga Yoga ke aakhri 3 limbs (Dharana, Dhyana, Samadhi) ko 'Antaranga Sadhana' (internal aids)\nkehte hain. Pehle 5 limbs (Yama se Pratyahara tak) ko 'Bahiranga Sadhana' (external aids) kehte hain.\n[Q96]\n● 'Mahabhashya' (Sanskrit grammar commentary) ke author Patanjali, Shunga king Pushyamitra Shunga\n(184-148 BC) ke samkalin the — unhone Pushyamitra ke Ashvamedha Yajna mein priest ki tarah bhi\nkaam kiya tha. [Q97]\n19c. Nyaya Darshan\n●\n Multiple Correct: Navya-Nyaya school ki foundation Mithila ke scholar Udayana (Udayanacharya) ke\n⚠️\n\nrevolutionary kaam se hui, aur baad mein Gangesh Upadhyaya ne isse aage badhaya — isliye is\nquestion mein B aur D dono sahi maane jaate hain. [Q98]\n● Nyaya Darshan sage Gautama (jinhe 'Akshapada' bhi kehte hain) ne propagate kiya tha — unki\nmasterpiece 'Nyayasutra' hai. 'Nyaya' ka matlab hota hai decision/logic. [Q104, Q105, Q106, Q107]\n● Darshan-Concept match: Nyaya Darshan → Logical thinking; Mimamsa Darshan → Vedic rituals\nperform karna; Sankhya Darshan → Real knowledge ki prapti; Vedanta Darshan → Khud ka gyan (Self-\nknowledge). [Q108]\n● Nyaya philosophy mein Gyana (knowledge) ke synonym hain Buddhi (Cognition) aur Upalabdhi\n(Apprehension) — dono. 'Gyana' word 2 senses mein use hota hai: restricted (unmanifested knowledge)\naur broad (manifested + unmanifested). [Q109]\n● School-Proponent match: Vaisheshika → Kanada Muni; Nyaya → Gautama; Purva Mimamsa →\nJaimini; Uttar Mimamsa → Badarayana. [Q110]\n19d. Charvaka (Lokayata) Darshan"," ● Charvaka philosophy (jise Lokayata bhi kehte hain) materialistic ideology par based hai — famous\nsaying: 'Jab tak jiyo, sukh se jiyo; udhar lekar bhi ghee piyo, kyunki jalne ke baad wapas nahi aana.'\n[Q99, Q103, Q119]\n● Charvaka ke mutabik 'conscious body hi soul hai' — body aur soul synonymous hain. 'Bina\nconsciousness ke body ek laash hai, aur bina body ke consciousness soul nahi hai' — ise\n'Dehatmavada' (materialistic view of soul) kehte hain. [Q100]\n● Charvaka philosophy sirf 'Perception' (Pratyaksha, direct anubhav) ko hi knowledge ka valid source\nmaanta hai — inference ya scriptures (shastra) ko reject karta hai. Isse originally 'Lokayata' bhi kehte\nthe. [Q101]\n● Charvaka ke mutabik zindagi ki sabse badi value 'Kama' (sensual pleasure) hai — Dharma aur Moksha\nko wo completely reject karte hain, sirf pleasure enjoy karna aur pain avoid karna hi wisdom maante\nhain. [Q102]\n19e. Mimamsa Darshan\n● Purva Mimamsa philosophy sage Jaimini ne shuru ki thi. [Q111]\n● Karma ka theory mainly Mimamsa philosophy se related hai — ise 'Karma Mimamsa', 'Purva Mimamsa'\nya 'Dharma Mimamsa' bhi kehte hain. Iske Acharya Kumaril Bhatta ko Purva Mimamsa aur Vedanta ke\nbeech ka link maana jaata hai. [Q112]\n● Mimamsa philosophy maanta hai ki Vedas mein eternal truth hai — Purva Mimamsa 'Karmakanda'\n(rituals) ki baat karta hai, aur Uttar Mimamsa 'Gyankand' (knowledge) ki. [Q113]\n● 'Apurva' ka doctrine Mimamsa philosophy se related hai — ye ek unseen force hai jo Karma (deeds) aur\nunke result ke beech mediator ki tarah kaam karti hai. [Q114]\n19f. Vaisheshika Darshan & the Six Systems Overview\n● Maharishi Kanad ne 'atom theory' (Sanskrit mein) di aur Vaisheshika school ki sthapna ki — isliye unhe\n'Indian Atomism ka founder' kaha jaata hai. Unke mutabik matter atoms se bana hai, aur atom sabse\nchhoti unit hai jo dikhai nahi de sakti. [Q115, Q116]\n● Hindu philosophy ke 6 mainstream orthodox systems (Saddarshan) hain: Sankhya, Yoga, Nyaya,\nVaisheshika, Mimamsa aur Vedanta. 'Lokayata' aur 'Kapalika' inn 6 systems ka hissa NAHI hain. [Q117]\n● 'Bauddha' (Buddhism) ek Nastika (heterodox) school hai — kyunki wo Vedas ko valid knowledge ka\nsource nahi maante. Vedic aur non-Vedic schools ke beech continuous dialogue/debate se hi Indian\nPhilosophy develop hui. [Q118]\n19g. Vedanta Darshan — Advaita & Vishishtadvaita\n● Advaita Vedanta ke founder aur principal exponent Adi Sankaracharya the — unhone pehle ke\nphilosophers ke kaam ko systematize karke ek coherent non-dualistic (Advaita) school banayi. [Q120]"," ● Samkara ki philosophy 'Advaita Vedanta' (Non-dualism) kehlaati hai — iske mutabik Brahman hi\nekmatra reality hai, baaki sab illusion hai. Atman (soul) aur Brahman ki pehchan se hi Mukti milti hai.\n[Q121]\n● Adi Shankaracharya ko 'Crypto-Buddhist' (chhupe hue Buddhist) bhi kaha jaata hai — unhone apni\nphilosophy mein Buddhist concepts (jaise monism/emptiness ki similarity) shaamil kiye the. [Q122]\n● Advaita Vedanta ke mutabik Mukti (liberation) Gyana (knowledge) se milti hai — sahi samajh se Atman\naur Brahman ki pehchan hoti hai, jisse Mukti milti hai. [Q123]\n● Vishishtadvaita Siddhanta ke founder Ramanujacharya (~1017-1137) the — Vaishnavite Saint.\n'Vishishtadvaita' ka matlab hai 'differentiation ke saath non-dualism'. [Q124]\n● Abhinav Gupta, Vedanta philosophy se JUDE NAHI hain — wo Kashmir Shaivism se associated hain.\nShankaracharya (8th century), Ramanuja (11th century) aur Madhava (13th century) — teeno Vedanta\nke prominent thinkers the. [Q125]\n20. Post-Gupta Regional Dynasties — Later Guptas, Maukharis & Maitrakas\n● Maukhari dynasty (Guptas ke feudatories, basically Gaya se the) ki capital Kannauj thi — Hari Varma,\nAditya Varma, Ishan Varma, Sarva Verma aur Graha Varma unke chief rulers the. [Q133]\n● Maukhari king Sarvavarman ka copper seal inscription Asirgarh fort (MP) mein mila tha, Gaya mein\nNAHI (ye galat pair hai). Iske text mein Maukhari kings ki genealogy hai, Harivarman se shuru hote hue.\n[Q134]\n● Gupta decline se lekar Harshavardhana ke uday (7th century) tak: Later Guptas ne Magadha par raj\nkiya, Pushyabhutis (Thanesar) ne North India ke hisso par (6th-7th century) raj kiya, Maukharis ne UP\n(Kannauj samet) par raj kiya, aur Maitrakas (Valabhi) ne West/North Gujarat par (late 5th se late 8th\ncentury) raj kiya. Paramara dynasty (Malwa) aur Yadavas (Devagiri) bahut baad mein aaye. [Q135]\n● Post-Gupta period mein main business center Ujjain se shift hokar Kannauj ho gaya tha —\nChandragupta-II ke time Ujjain unki second capital thi, lekin baad mein Harsha ne Kannauj ko apni\ncapital banaya. Kannauj Ganga ke kinare hone ki wajah se Palas, Pratiharas aur Rashtrakutas — teeno\npowers ke liye attraction ka center ban gaya. [Q164]\n21. Harshavardhana — Rise, Capital & Conquests\n● Banabhatta ki 'Harshacharita' ke mutabik, Vardhana dynasty ki sthapna Pushyabhuti ne Thaneshwar\n(Sthaneshwar) mein ki thi — Harshavardhana is dynasty ke sabse bade ruler the. [Q136]\n● Harsha ke time ki jaankari Banabhatta ki 'Harshacharita' se milti hai (wo Harsha ke court poet the). Kuch\njaankari Kalhana ki 'Rajatarangini' se bhi milti hai — Kalidas ki books mein Harsha ka koi zikr nahi hai.\n[Q137]\n● 'Harshacharita' Banabhatta ne likhi — ye Vardhana dynasty ka mukhya source hai, jisme Harsha aur\nunke ancestors ki biography hai. [Q138]\n● Harsha ne apni sister Rajyashri ki madad ke liye apni capital Thanesar se Kannauj shift kar li —\nChinese sources ke mutabik Harsha aur Rajyashri saath mein Kannauj par raj karte the. [Q139, Q140]"," ● Harshavardhana ne Kannauj (Mahayana Buddhism ki excellence prove karne ke liye, Hiuen Tsang ki\npresidency mein) aur Prayaga (Sangam par, har 5th saal, 'Mahamoksha council') mein 2 badi religious\nconventions organize ki. [Q141, Q142]\n● Harsha ke time Assam (Kamarupa) par Bhaskar Varman raj karte the — wo Varman dynasty ke last\nruler the aur Harsha ke important ally the. [Q143]\n● Harsha ki southward march (Deccan ki taraf) Narmada river ke kinare Chalukya ruler Pulakesin-II ne rok\ndi — ye Aihole inscription (Pulakesin II) aur Hiuen Tsang ke description mein mila hai. [Q144, Q145]\n● Bhandarkar Oriental Research Institute ke researchers ne April 2016 mein ek naye mile copper plate\ninscription ke basis par claim kiya ki Pulakesin-Harsha ki ye battle 618 AD mein hui thi (pehle 630-634\nAD maana jaata tha) — Jharkhand PSC ne 618 AD ko sahi maana. [Q146]\n● Poet Banabhatta, Prithikuta village (Son river ke kinare, Aurangabad dist., aaj ke Bihar) mein paida hue\nthe — diye gaye options (Pataliputra, Thanesar, Bhojpur) mein se koi match nahi karta. [Q147]\n22. Hiuen-Tsang's India\n● Chinese traveller Hiuen-Tsang, Harsha ke reign mein India aaye the — unka desire Mahatma Buddha\nse related jagah dekhna aur Buddhist texts padhna tha. Wo 629 AD mein Changan se rawana hue the.\n[Q148, Q149]\n● Hiuen Tsang ke mutabik roads aur river routes robbery se pura tarah safe nahi the — khud unhe kai\nbaar loota gaya (galat statement isliye). Crimes ke liye punishment sakht thi — fire/water/poison se\nordeal hota tha (sahi). Trade routes, ferries aur barrier stations par tax lagta tha (sahi). [Q150]\n● Hiuen-Tsang khud apni marzi se, ek pilgrim ki tarah India aaye the — kisi Chinese ruler ne unhe\nambassador banakar NAHI bheja tha. Tang ruler Taizong ne foreign tours ban kar rakhe the, lekin\nHiuen-Tsang chupke se 629 AD mein China se nikal gaye. [Q151]\n● Hiuen Tsang ke mutabik, unki yatra ke dauran Mathura cotton clothes (kapda) production ke liye sabse\nfamous city thi. Unhone Varanasi ko silk ke liye famous bataya. [Q152]\n● Gupta aur post-Gupta period mein 'Kausheya' word Silk (resham) ke liye use hota tha. [Q153]\n● Hiuen Tsang, Harsha ke reign mein, 637 AD mein Nalanda University gaye the — us waqt Acharya\nSheelbhadra Vice-Chancellor the. Hiuen Tsang ne wahan lagbhag 1.5 saal Yogashastra padha. [Q154]\n● Hiuen-Tsang ko mainly unki book 'Si-Yu-Ki' (Records of Western Regions) ke liye yaad kiya jaata hai —\nisme ancient India ki socio-political condition ki bahumulya jaankari hai. [Q155, Q157]\n● Hiuen Tsang (Xuanzang), Harsha ke reign mein India aaye the aur Bhinmal (Rajasthan) bhi gaye the.\n[Q156]\n23. Post-Harsha Foreign Travellers — I-tsing & Others\n● Chinese traveller I-tsing (Yijing), 671 se 695 AD (late 7th century) tak India mein rahe — diye gaye\noptions mein ye time-bracket match nahi karta, isliye 'None of the above' sahi jawab hai. [Q158]\n● Ancient Chinese writers India ko 'Yin-tu' ya 'Thian-tu' naam se bulaate the — ye Hindu/Sindhu word ka\nvariation hai. [Q160]"," ●\n Disputed: Foreign travellers ke India-tour years ka match kai options mein galat hai — I-tsing\n⚠️\nactually 671-695 AD tak the (diya gaya 679-695 AD partially galat hai), aur Al Masudi 915-16 AD mein\naaye the (957 AD galat hai). Isliye ye question disputed maana jaata hai. [Q168]\n● Foreign travellers ka chronological order: Fa-Hien (399-414 CE, Chandragupta II) → Hiuen Tsang (629-\n645 CE, Harsha) → I-tsing (671-695 CE, post-Harsha) → Al-Biruni (11th century, Mahmud of Ghazni ke\nsaath). [Q169]\n● Multan ka famous Sun Temple, Hiuen Tsang, Al-Masudi aur Alberuni jaise foreign travellers ne mention\nkiya hai, jo iski importance confirm karta hai (sahi). Sambpur ki pilgrimage (Krishna ke bete Samba se\nrelated, jo Sun ki pooja se leprosy se theek hue the) bhi Sun worship se associated thi (sahi). [Q170]\n24. Nalanda University\n● Nalanda University, jo Tibet, China, Greece aur Persia se scholars/students attract karti thi, Bakhtiyar\nKhalji ki Muslim army ne ransack/destroy kar di thi. [Q161]\n● Nalanda, India (Bihar) ka sabse purana monastery maana jaata hai — halaki is town ka history Buddha\nke time (6th century BC) tak jaata hai, actual university site Gupta period (5th century) se flourish hui.\n[Q162]\n● Nalanda Mahavihara ka ancient site aaj ke Bihar rajya mein hai. [Q163]\n25. Feudalism in Post-Gupta India\n● Assertion-Reason: Post-Gupta period ki agrarian structure ki main feature feudal structure ka\ndevelopment tha (sahi), kyunki Brahmadeya/Agrahara land grants (pehle Brahmins ko, baad mein aur\nlogo ko) widely diye gaye the — isse original cultivators dependent peasant class ban gaye, aur\ngrantees land-owning middle class ban gaye (sahi Reason bhi). [Q165]\n● Indian Feudalism ke essential elements: decentralized political authority (local feudatories powerful hote\nthe) — halaki ye statement khud pehla point nahi hai, balki land grants se administrative structure banna\naur lord-vassal (suzerain-subordinate) ka hierarchical relationship banna — ye 2 essential elements the.\n[Q171]\n26. Adi Shankaracharya\n● Shankaracharya (8th century saint) ne 4 religious centers (Mathas) establish kiye, Buddhism jaisi non-\northodox schools ka virodh kiya, aur Advaita Vedanta philosophy propagate ki. Unhone Prayag ko\n'Teerthraj' ka naam NAHI diya — ye title Puranas/Epics mein pehle se hi ancient designation ke roop\nmein maujood thi. [Q173]\n● Adi Shankaracharya, Kaladi (ek chhota gaon, Kerala) mein 8th century mein paida hue the — unhone\nAdvaita Vedanta philosophy phailakar Hinduism ko revive kiya. [Q174]\n● Adi Shankaracharya ne 4 Mathas (monasteries) establish kiye: Jyotirmath/Joshimath (North,\nUttarakhand), Dwarka (West, Gujarat), Puri (East, Odisha), aur Sringeri (South, Karnataka). [Q175]\n● India ke Chardham (4 abode) mein Badrinath, Dwarka, Puri aur Rameshwaram shaamil hain.\nMansarovar (Tibet ki ek pavitra lake) Chardham ka hissa NAHI hai. [Q176]"," 27. Court Poets & Miscellaneous Match Lists\n●\n Trap: Harisena, Samudragupta ke court poet-secretary the (Prayaga Prashasti ke composer),\n⚠️\nHarsha ke NAHI — Harsha ke court poet Banabhatta the. Baaki pairs sahi hain: Ravi Kirti ne Pulakesin\nII ke liye Aihole inscription likhi; Bhavabhuti, Yasovarman ke court mein the. [Q177]\n● Courtier Poet match: Amir Khusro → Alauddin Khalji; Kalidas → Chandragupta II (Navratna); Harisena\n→ Samudragupta; Banabhatta → Harshvardhan. [Q178]\n● Ruler-Capital match: Raja Bhoj → Dhar (Paramara dynasty capital); Rani Durgawati → Gondwana\n(Garha Katanga); Samudragupta → Vidisha (unki campaigns se connection); Ashoka → Ujjain (emperor\nbanne se pehle wahan governor the). [Q179]\n● Puranas ke mutabik Chandravansh (Somvansha) ke rajaon ki mukhya jagah pehle Prayaga thi, lekin ek\nnatural calamity ke baad Dwapar Yug ke Chandravanshi King Samvaram ne apni capital Pratishthanpur\nmein banayi. [Q132]\n● Place-State pairs: Bhilsa → Vidisha, MP (sahi). Girinagar (Girnar) → Junagarh dist., Gujarat (sahi).\nDwarasamudra (Halebidu) → Hoysala dynasty ki capital, Karnataka thi, Maharashtra NAHI (galat).\nSthanesvara (Thanesar) → Haryana mein hai, UP NAHI (galat). Isliye sirf 1 aur 3 pairs sahi hain. [Q180]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Gupta and Post-Gupta Period Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0166","t":"12 Architecture in Ancient India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" 🛕 ARCHITECTURE IN ANCIENT INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Khajuraho Temples — Chandela Dynasty\n2. Chausath Yogini Temple, Morena\n3. Temple Architecture Styles — Nagara, Dravida, Vesara & Panchayatan\n4. World Heritage Sites of Ancient India\n5. Buddhist Rock-cut Caves — Kanheri, Bagh & Related Sites\n6. Jain Temples — Mount Abu, Palitana & Sonagiri\n7. Elephanta Caves\n8. Ajanta & Ellora — Rock-cut Caves of Western India\n9. The Kailasa Temple, Ellora & Rashtrakuta Patronage\n10. Gupta Period Temples\n11. Konark & Other Sun Temples\n12. Odisha Temples — Lingaraj & Jagannath Puri\n13. Southeast Asian Temples — Angkor Wat & Borobudur\n14. Dravidian Architecture — The Gopuram\n15. Mahabalipuram — Pallava Rock-cut Architecture\n16. Important Site-Monument Match Lists\n17. Miscellaneous Historic Sites\n18. Folk Paintings of India\n1. Khajuraho Temples — Chandela Dynasty\n● Khajuraho ke magnificent shrines Chandela dynasty ki architectural craftsmanship ka brilliant example\nhain — MP ke Chhatarpur region mein, mainly 10th-12th century ke beech banaye gaye. Inme se\nKandariya Mahadeva shrine sabse spectacular maana jaata hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n● Khajuraho temples Hindu aur Jain — dono faiths ko dedicate hain. 950-1050 CE ke beech Chandela\nmonarchs ne inhe banwaya, originally yahan ~85 sanctuaries the. [Q5, Q6]\n● Matangeshvara Temple (Khajuraho complex ka hissa) Lord Shiva ko dedicate hai — King Dhanga ke\ntime bana, aur Nagara architectural style ka prominent example hai. [Q7]\n● Dashavatara Temple Khajuraho mein NAHI hai — ye Deogarh (Lalitpur) mein hai, Gupta era se belong\nkarta hai. Kandariya Mahadev, Chausath Yogini aur Chitragupta temples — teeno Khajuraho mein hain,\nChandela rulers ne banwaye. [Q8]\n● Pairs check: Khajuraho Temple — Chandelas (sahi match). Ellora Caves — Rashtrakutas (Sakas\nNAHI). Meenakshi Temple — Pandyas (Pallavas NAHI). Mahabalipuram Temple — Pallavas\n(Rashtrakutas NAHI). [Q82]\n2. Chausath Yogini Temple, Morena\n● Morena (MP) ke pass ka gol/circular 'Chausath Yogini' temple, Kachchhapaghata dynasty ke Devapala\nne ~1323 CE mein banwaya tha — ye Lord Shiva aur Yoginis ko dedicate hai (Vaishnavism se NAHI).\nBahut log maante hain ki iska circular design purane Indian Parliament building ke liye inspiration bana.\n[Q9]"," 3. Temple Architecture Styles — Nagara, Dravida, Vesara & Panchayatan\n● Independent freestanding stone-mortar shrines India mein Gupta period mein emerge hui thi. Ladkhan\ntemple Badami Chalukyas se juda ek early structural example hai. Khajuraho ki khaasiyat hai ki uske\ntemple compartments internally-externally seamlessly integrated hain. Kailashnath temple (Kanchi),\nPallava rulers ne banwaya, Dravidian architecture ka mature example hai. [Q12]\n● Teli ka Mandir (Gwalior) ek interesting architectural mix hai — surface decoration North Indian Nagara\nstyle se hai, lekin uska tall Shikhar (pinnacle) purely Dravidian style mein banaya gaya hai. [Q13]\n● Hoysaleshwara Temple (Halebidu, Karnataka), Vesara (hybrid) architecture style ka prime example hai\n— Hoysala rajaon ne dark schist se banaya, star-shaped base aur dense ornamental reliefs iski\nkhaasiyat hain. [Q14]\n● Nagara, Dravida aur Vesara — Indian temple architecture ki 3 main styles hain. Dravida style South\nIndia mein develop hui, Nagara North India mein, aur Vesara (Nagara+Dravida ka mix) mainly Deccan\nregion mein milta hai. [Q95]\n● 'Panchayatan' ek temple-construction style hai jisme ek central main shrine ko 4 chhote subsidiary\nshrines ghere rehte hain — naam Sanskrit ke 'Pancha' (paanch) aur 'Ayatana' (samahit) se aaya hai.\nExamples: Kandariya Mahadeo (Khajuraho), Brahmeshwar Temple, Lingaraja Temple (Bhubaneswar),\nDashavatara Temple (Deogarh). [Q96]\n4. World Heritage Sites of Ancient India\n● Khajuraho, Bhimbetka rock shelters aur Sanchi Stupa — teeno UNESCO World Heritage Site hain.\nMandu fort World Heritage Site NAHI hai. [Q11]\n5. Buddhist Rock-cut Caves — Kanheri, Bagh & Related Sites\n● Kanheri (Mumbai ke Borivali ke pass, west mein) mein 100 se zyada Buddhist caves hain — ~1st\ncentury BCE se shuru hoke, ye extensive rock-cut complex Buddhist devotional art aur structural\nelements dikhata hai. [Q15]\n● Gupta period ke sirf 2 known cave-painting examples hain: Ajanta aur Bagh caves (MP). Bagh caves\nmein secular/rozmarra ki zindagi ke themes dikhaye gaye hain, Ajanta ke deeply Buddhist religious\nmotifs se alag. (Lomas Rishi Mauryan period ki hai, Nasik ki caves Satavahanas ki hain.) [Q23]\n●\n Disputed: Sanchi aur Bulsar mein Buddhist CAVES nahi hain (Sanchi mein stupas hain, caves nahi)\n⚠️\n\n— lekin ye multiple-correct wala tricky question hai kyunki dono jagah technically options mein sahi hain.\n[Q52]\n6. Jain Temples — Mount Abu, Palitana & Sonagiri\n● Mount Abu ke famous Dilwara Temples Jain devotion ka masterpiece hain, poori tarah white marble se\nbane — Vimal Shah ne Chalukya king Bhimdev I ke patronage mein banwaye. Ye Rajasthan ke Aravalli\nmountain range mein situated hain, apni detailed marble carvings ke liye famous. [Q16, Q91, Q92, Q93]"," ● Palitana temple complex, Shatrunjaya hills par, Gujarat ke Bhavnagar district mein situated hai —\nmainly Adinatha (Jainism ke pehle Tirthankara) ko dedicate hai. [Q17]\n● Sonagiri (Datia, MP se 15 km door), 103 Jain temples wali highest jagah hai — Digambar Jain devotees\nke liye popular pilgrimage site hai. Temple No. 57 (Lord Chandraprabhu ko dedicate) main temple hai.\n[Q89, Q90]\n7. Elephanta Caves\n● Elephanta Caves (Arabian Sea ke ek island par, Rashtrakuta monarchs ne banwaye) mainly Shaiva\ndevotees ke liye sculpted hain — Lord Shiva ko exclusively dedicate hain. Sabse iconic piece hai\n'Trimurti' (Shiva ke cosmic roop ko darshane wali sculpture). [Q18, Q22]\n● Elephanta ke ancient monuments mostly Shaivite hain (5 major Hindu shrines) — thoda Buddhist\nheritage bhi hai. Isliye Elephanta ka heritage Buddhist AUR Shaivite dono streams ko encapsulate karta\nhai. [Q19]\n● Elephanta ke famous cave temples Rashtrakuta dynasty ke sovereigns ne banaye/fund kiye. Ellora aur\nElephanta — dono sites apni primary architectural grandeur Rashtrakuta empire ke period mein\npahunche the (Ellora Hindu-Buddhist-Jain teeno faiths ka mix hai, Elephanta sirf Shiva ki massive\ncarvings ke liye famous hai). [Q20, Q21]\n8. Ajanta & Ellora — Rock-cut Caves of Western India\n● India ke Western region mein important rock-cut monuments Nasik, Ellora aur Ajanta mein hain\n(Chhatrapati Sambhaji Nagar/Aurangabad district, Maharashtra). Ellora complex mein 34 caves hain jo\n3 religions celebrate karti hain; Nasik ki Pandavleni caves Buddhist art ke liye jaani jaati hain. [Q24, Q41,\nQ42, Q43]\n● Ajanta Buddhist rock-cut caves aur fresco paintings ke liye exclusive repository hai — Elephanta\n(Shaiva art), Khajuraho (Hindu-Jain structural temples) aur Nalanda (brick-mortar university) se ye alag\nhai. [Q25]\n● Ellora ke architectural excavations ka bada hissa mighty Rashtrakuta dynasty ne commission/nurture\nkiya tha. [Q26]\n● Rock-cut architecture ke statements: Bhimbetka rock shelters, Badami caves se bhi purani hain (galat\nstatement tha ki Badami purana hai). Barabar caves Mauryan Emperor Ashoka ne Ajivika sect ko\ndedicate ki thi, Chandragupta ne nahi (galat). Ellora sahi mein Buddhist, Hindu aur Jain — teeno faiths\nke liye sanctuaries dikhata hai (sahi statement). [Q27]\n● Ellora (Maharashtra) mein 34 structural excavations hain, jo Buddhist caves (1-12) se shuru hoke,\nHindu temples (13-29) se hoke, Jain caves tak jaati hain — ye complete religious tolerance dikhata hai.\nSirf Ellora hi ek jagah hai jaha Buddhist, Hindu aur Jain — teeno rock-cut systems ek saath coexist karte\nhain. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n● Ajanta ke art ko mainly Vakataka period mein patronize kiya gaya (ek earlier group Satavahana period\nmein bhi bani thi). Ye Buddhist cave temples hain jo mountain rock ko carve karke banaye gaye. [Q48]\n● Ajanta caves Jataka stories se linked hain — inme Buddha ke previous janmo (Jataka tales) ko depict\nkarne wali paintings hain, saath hi flowers/trees/animals ki bhi art hai. [Q49]"," ● Ajanta Caves, Waghora river ki gorge/valley mein situated hai (Chhatrapati Sambhaji Nagar dist.,\nMaharashtra). Sanchi Stupa Betwa river ke west mein hai (Raisen dist., MP). Pandu-lena caves (Nasik)\nGodavari valley mein hain. Amravati Stupa Krishna river ke kinare hai (Palnadu dist., AP). [Q50]\n● Mural paintings ka evidence Ajanta aur Lepakshi temple mein clearly milta hai, lekin Sanchi Stupa mein\nNAHI (jiska nucleus ek simple hemispherical brick structure tha, Buddha ke relics par bana, upar\nChhatra symbol tha). [Q51]\n9. The Kailasa Temple, Ellora & Rashtrakuta Patronage\n● Kailasa Temple (Ellora) duniya bhar mein architectural wonder maana jaata hai — ek hi solid rock cliff\nko chisel karke banaya gaya hai. Rashtrakuta king Krishna-I ne isse design/construct karwaya,\nDravidian style mein. [Q31, Q32, Q33, Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q39]\n● Rashtrakuta rulers Shaiva, Vaishnava aur Shakta bhakto ko patronize karte the, lekin unka jhukav\nsabse zyada Jainism ki taraf tha — unke darbar ke kai scholars (Sanskrit, Kannada, Apabhramsha,\nPrakrit likhne wale) Jain the. King Amoghavarsha-I khud ek Jain Acharya ke shishya the. [Q40]\n10. Gupta Period Temples\n● Gupta Temple match: Brick-built Temple → Bhitargaon (Kanpur); Dasavatara Temple → Deogarh\n(Lalitpur); Shiva Temple → Bhumara; Vishnu Temple → Eran. [Q44]\n● Deogarh (Jhansi ke pass) ka temple aur Garhwa (Allahabad ke pass) ki sculptures — dono Gupta art ke\nimportant remains hain. Dashavatar temple (Deogarh) North India ka sabse purana known Panchayatan\ntemple hai. [Q45, Q46]\n● Bhitargaon (Kanpur, UP) ka temple ek terraced brick building hai, terracotta panels ke saath — 5th-6th\ncentury AD (Gupta period) mein bana. Ye India ke sabse purane brick temples mein se ek hai, square\nplan par bana, double-recessed corners ke saath, purab (east) ki taraf face karta hai, garbhagriha ke\nupar tall pyramidal spire hai. [Q47]\n11. Konark & Other Sun Temples\n● Konark Sun Temple (13th century, Odisha) King Narasimhadeva Varman-I (Eastern Ganga Dynasty) ne\nbanwaya tha — ek huge solar chariot ki tarah design kiya gaya, 12 pairs ornamental wheels aur 7 ghode\nkheenchte hue. European sailors ise 'Black Pagoda' kehte the (Puri ka Jagannath Temple 'White\nPagoda' kehlaata tha). [Q56, Q57, Q58, Q59]\n● Sun Temple of Modhera (Patan district, Gujarat) Solanki dynasty ke King Bhimadeva-I ne banwaya tha.\n[Q60, Q61]\n● Arasavalli (Andhra Pradesh) apne prominent 7th-century Sun temple ke liye famous hai, jo King\nDevendra Verma (Eastern Ganga Dynasty) ne banwaya tha. (Omkareshwar Shiva ka Jyotirlinga hai,\nAmarkantak Narmada ke origin aur Shiva temple ke liye — dono Sun temples ke liye NAHI famous\nhain.) [Q86]"," 12. Odisha Temples — Lingaraj & Jagannath Puri\n● Lingaraj Temple (Bhubaneswar, Odisha) Lord Shiva ko dedicate hai (unhe 'Lingaraj' bhi kehte hain) —\n~180 feet ooncha hai, Nagara style mein bana hai, aur Odisha ka sabse bada-sabse ooncha surviving\ntemple hai. [Q62, Q63]\n● Jagannath Temple, Odisha (Puri) mein hai — Lingaraj temple aur Konarka Sun Temple bhi Odisha mein\nhain, dono Nagara style mein bane. Bhubaneswara (Lingaraja) aur Puri (Jagannath) ke temples — dono\nNagara architecture style mein bane hain. [Q64, Q65]\n● Jagannath Puri Temple mein Lord Jagannath, Subhadra aur Balbhadra ki idols neem (nimb) wood se\nbanayi jaati hain — Bhavishya Purana ke mutabik neem wood Vishnu idols ke liye sabse shubh maana\njaata hai. Ye idol Ratha-yatra se pehle har saal repaint hoti hai, aur har 12-19 saal mein Hindu calendar\nke hisaab se replace bhi hoti hai. [Q66]\n13. Southeast Asian Temples — Angkor Wat & Borobudur\n● Angkor Wat Vishnu Temple, Cambodia (Kampuchea) mein hai — Khmer King Suryavarman-II ne 12th\ncentury ke shuruat mein apni capital mein banwaya. Ye Khmer style mein bana duniya ka sabse bada\nHindu temples ka group hai, Lord Vishnu ko dedicate. [Q67, Q68, Q69]\n● Borobudur Stupa, Java (Indonesia) mein situated hai — ek massive Mahayana Buddhist temple,\nUNESCO World Heritage Site hai. [Q70]\n14. Dravidian Architecture — The Gopuram\n● 'Gopuram' Dravidian style ke temples ki entrance par bana ek ornate, monumental tower hota hai —\nSouth Indian Hindu temples ki khaasiyat hai. Iska origin Tamil kings Pallavas se trace hota hai, aur ye\nornamental multi-storied gateways temple ke bahar dikhne ki ek dominant feature ban gaye. [Q71]\n15. Mahabalipuram — Pallava Rock-cut Architecture\n● Mahabalipuram (Mamallapuram) ke rock-cut temples Pallava king Narasimha Varman ne banwaye —\nShore temple, Rathas (single rock se carved chariots), Arjuna's Penance jaise wonders yahan hain. Ye\nUNESCO World Heritage Monument hai. [Q72, Q73, Q76]\n● Seven Ratha Temple (Sapt Pagoda), Mahabalipuram mein, Narasimha Varman-I (630-668 AD) ne\nbanwaya — unhi ke naam par Mamallapuram (Mahabalipuram) sheher ka naam pada, aur unke time\n'Mamalla' style develop hui. [Q74, Q75]\n● Draupadi Rath sabse chhota Ratha temple hai Mahabalipuram mein — simple hut-jaisa structure hai,\nkoi elaborate ornamentation nahi, lion-elephant sculptures par tika hua hai. [Q77]\n● Kailasanathar Temple (Kanchipuram), Pallava king Narasimhavarman II (Rajasimha) ne banwaya —\n'Rajsimha' architectural style mein, jisme intricate carvings, bade Gopurams aur stone sculptures hote\nhain. [Q78]"," ● Temples ka chronological order: Sapt Pagoda (Mamalla style, ~640-674 AD) → Shore Temple\n(Rajasimha style, ~700-728 AD) → Brihdeeshwara temple (Chola King Rajaraja I, ~1003-1010 AD) →\nGangaikonda Cholapuram temple (Rajendra I, ~1035 AD). [Q79]\n● Ajanta aur Mahabalipuram mein common cheez hai: dono rock-cut monuments hain. (Dono ek hi\nreligion se related nahi hain — Mahabalipuram Hindu/Shiva-Vishnu se related hai, Ajanta poori tarah\nBuddhist hai.) [Q54]\n16. Important Site-Monument Match Lists\n● Match: Stupa → Sanchi (MP); Cave paintings → Bagh (MP); Kanishka's headless statue → Mathura\n(UP); Dashavatara Temple → Deogarh (UP). [Q10]\n● Match: Hampi → Karnataka; Nagarjunakonda → Andhra Pradesh; Shishupalgarh → Odisha; Arikamedu\n→ Puducherry. [Q55]\n● Match: Elephanta → Cave (rock-cut Shiva caves); Shravanabelagola → Statue (Gommateshwara\nBahubali); Khajuraho → Temple (Chandela-built); Sanchi → Stupa (Ashoka ka Great Stupa). [Q80]\n● Match: Bhimbetka (Rock Shelters) → Madhya Pradesh; Shore Temple (Mahabalipuram) → Tamil Nadu;\nHampi (Vijayanagara ruins) → Karnataka; Manas (Wildlife Sanctuary) → Assam. [Q81]\n● Match: Baidyanath Dham (Deoghar) → Shiva Temple (12 Jyotirlingas mein se ek); Sarnath (Varanasi)\n→ Buddha ka pehla sermon (Dharmachakra Pravartan); Dilwara (Mount Abu) → Jain Temple (marble\ncarvings); Badrinath → Vishnu Temple (Shankaracharya ne establish kiya). [Q83]\n● Pairs check: Besnagar Shaivite cave shrine ke liye NAHI, balki Heliodorus Pillar (Bhagavat/Vaishnav\nreligion) ke liye famous hai (galat pair). Bhaja Caves (Pune) Buddhist rock-cut architecture ke liye\nfamous hain (sahi). Sittanavasal (Tamil Nadu) Jain cave shrine-paintings ke liye famous hai, Pallavas ne\nbanwaya (sahi). Isliye 2 pairs sahi hain. [Q84]\n● Match: Sun Temple → Konark (Odisha); Lingaraja Temple → Bhubaneswar (Harihara/Shiva ko\ndedicate); Hawa Mahal → Jaipur (Rajasthan); Statue of Gomateshwara (Bahubali) → Shravanabelagola\n(Karnataka). [Q85]\n● Match: Nalanda → University (higher learning ka centre); Sarnath → Ashoka Pillar (Lion Capital);\nSanchi → Stupa (Great Stupa); Konark → Sun Temple (Black Pagoda). [Q87]\n● Statements check: Cave 26 (Ajanta) mein Buddha ka 'Mahaparinirvana' statue engrave hai (sahi).\nVaraha Avatar ki huge rock-cut statue Udaygiri caves (MP) mein hai, Mount Abu mein NAHI (galat).\n'Arjuna's Penance' (Descent of Ganga) Mahabalipuram (Tamil Nadu) mein hai, huge boulders par\nsculpted. [Q98]\n17. Miscellaneous Historic Sites\n● Ancient town Takshashila (Taxila), Indus aur Jhelum river ke beech situated thi — 6th/7th century BC\nmein establish hui, aaj ke Rawalpindi district (Pakistan) mein, learning ka famous centre thi. [Q88]\n● Famous Virupaksha Temple Hampi (Karnataka) mein hai — Lord Shiva ko (Virupaksha roop mein)\ndedicate hai, Vijayanagara Empire ke time bana. [Q94]\n● Naimisharanya (famous pilgrimage) Sitapur district, UP mein hai — Hindu mythology ke mutabik yahin\nSage Dadhichi ne apni haddiyan Devon ko de di thi, jinse Indra ka 'Vajra' weapon bana. [Q97]"," ●\n Disputed: Chitrakoot (famous Hindu pilgrimage), UP-MP dono states ki border par phaila hai —\n⚠️\nKamadgiri hill (jaha Lord Kamata Nath rehte hain) ka kuch hissa UP mein aur kuch MP mein hai, isliye\n'kis state mein hai' wala question ambiguous hai (BPSC ne MP accept kiya tha). [Q99]\n● Diye gaye options mein sabse purana rock-cut art hai Dhauli (Odisha) ka Rock-cut Elephant — Ashoka\nke time (3rd century BC) ka. Udayagiri ka Varaha image 5th century AD (Gupta) ka hai, Mahabalipuram\nke rock-cut monuments Pallavas ne 7th-8th century AD mein banaye, aur Lingaraja Temple 10th-11th\ncentury AD mein bana — sabse baad mein. [Q100]\n18. Folk Paintings of India\n●\n Note: 'Pattachitra' Odisha ki folk art hai, Lord Jagannath aur Vaishnav cults se judi hai. 'Manjusha'\n⚠️\nart Bhagalpur (Bihar) ki folk art hai — Manjushas mandir-jaise boxes hote hain, 8 pillars ke saath, India\nki sabse purani painting arts mein se ek. 'Pithora' painting Gujarat-MP ke tribes ki ritualistic painting hai.\n[Q53]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Architecture in Ancient India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0167","t":"13 South India Chola Chalukya Pallava Sangam","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" 🛕 SOUTH INDIA — CHOLA, CHALUKYA, PALLAVA & SANGAM — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Chola Dynasty — Foundation & Extent\n2. The Brihadeeswara Temple\n3. Chola Village Administration\n4. Chola Bronze Art — Nataraja & Iconography\n5. Chola Trade, Guilds & Foreign Missions\n6. Chola Naval Power & Overseas Conquests\n7. Chola Succession Practice & Historical Sources\n8. Battle of Takkolam & the Decline of the Cholas\n9. The Chalukya Dynasty\n10. The Pallava Dynasty\n11. The Chera Dynasty\n12. The Pandya Dynasty\n13. Other South Indian Dynasties — Kadamba & Kakatiya\n14. Sangam Literature — Tolkappiyam, Kural & the Twin Epics\n15. Sangam Assemblies & Sage Agastya\n16. Sangam-Era Ports, Trade Centres & Roman Contact\n17. Sangam-Era Kingdoms & Society\n18. Bhakti Saints — Alvars, Nayanars, Siddhas & Lingayats\n19. Miscellaneous — Language, Architecture & Match Lists\n1. Chola Dynasty — Foundation & Extent\n● Imperial Chola Empire ki foundation Vijayalaya ne 9th century AD mein (~850 AD) rakhi thi — unhone\nMuttaraiyar chiefs se Tanjore (Thanjavur) capture kiya aur usse apni capital banaya, early Sangam\nCholas ke pathan ke baad ka interregnum khatam karke. [Q1, Q2]\n● Chola empire ka core aur expanded region Coromandel coast aur Deccan ke kuch hisso (Uraiyur,\nKaveripattinam, Thanjavur) tak phaila hua tha — Tungabhadra aur Krishna rivers tak north mein. [Q5]\n● Imperial Cholas ki capital Tanjore (Thanjavur) thi — baad mein Rajendra I ke time\nGangaikondacholapuram bhi capital bani. Ancient Sangam era mein Cholas ki capital Uraiyur thi. [Q6]\n2. The Brihadeeswara Temple\n● Brihadeeswara Temple (Thanjavur), Chola emperor Rajaraja-I ke reign mein bana — Dravidian style\narchitecture ka excellent example hai, isse 'Rajarajeshvaram' bhi kehte hain. [Q4]\n● Is temple ke exterior mein ek gigantic 'Nandi' (ek hi rock se carved) hai — India ka sabse ooncha Nandi\nidol maana jaata hai (halaki Lepakshi ka Nandi bhi bahut bada hai aur kai jagah largest monolithic\nmaana jaata hai, PCS exams mein generally Brihadeeswara Nandi ko hi answer maana jaata hai). [Q3]\n3. Chola Village Administration\n● Chola administration ki special/unique feature thi village administration ki autonomy (local self-\ngovernment) — ye bahut systematic aur well-developed thi, central command se independently function\nkarti thi. [Q7, Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13]"," ● Chola age apni elaborate village assemblies (Gram Sabhas jaise Ur aur Sabha) ke liye sabse famous\ntha. [Q8, Q9]\n● Chola village administration ki working system ki detailed jaankari 'Uttaramerur' inscription se milti hai —\nisme bataya gaya hai ki har village ki apni 'Sabha' committee hoti thi, jo Central command se\nindependent hoke village administer karti thi. [Q14]\n● Chola villages mein 'Variyam' naam ke working committees hote the jo alag-alag kaam dekhte the:\n'Thotta Variyam' — Horticulture/garden board dekhta tha; 'Samvatsara Variyam' — annual committee\nthi; 'Eri Variyam' — tanks/water supply dekhti thi; 'Pon Variyam' — gold/finance se related thi. [Q15]\n● Chola administrative-land terms: 'Eripatti' — wo land jiska revenue village tank (talab) ke maintenance\nke liye rakha jaata tha. 'Ghatikas' — temples se attached colleges/learning centres hote the. ('Taniyurs'\nbade villages hote the jo separate unit ki tarah administer hote the, Brahmins ko donate NAHI kiye jaate\nthe — Brahmadeya/Agrahara alag concept tha.) [Q34]\n4. Chola Bronze Art — Nataraja & Iconography\n● Chola period ke Nataraja (dancing Shiva) bronze icons hamesha 4 haath ke saath dikhaye jaate hain —\nChola artists (Sthapati) stone se zyada bronze sculptures banane mein mahir the. Nataraja ki idols\nduniya ki behtareen sculptures mein se maani jaati hain. [Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● 'Dakshinamurti' idol mein Shiva ko Guru/Teacher (mentor) roop mein dikhaya jaata hai — wo apne\ndevotees ko ultimate gyan aur cosmic wisdom dete hain, aur ye idol generally south direction ki taraf\nface karti hui installed hoti hai. [Q21]\n● Nataraja statue mein Shiva ko 4-haath ke saath dancing pose mein dikhaya jaata hai, jo unke creator-\npreserver-destroyer teeno roop ko ek image mein combine karta hai. Unke right ear mein mard ki\nearring (Makarakundala) aur left mein aurat ki earring (Tatanka) hoti hai, jo male-female principles ke\nunion (Ardhanarishwara concept) ko symbolize karta hai. [Q22]\n5. Chola Trade, Guilds & Foreign Missions\n● Chola king Kulottunga-I ke reign mein (1077 AD), ek goodwill mission mein 72 traders China bheje gaye\nthe. [Q23]\n● 'Nanadesis' aur 'Manigrama' ancient South India ke traders ke guilds the, jo Hoysala/Chola period mein\nsabse badi trading associations mein se the — inke foreign countries ke saath bhi significant trade\ncontacts the. 'Manigramam' ek merchants ki corporation thi jo South Indian townships mein trade-\nbusiness badhane ke liye kaam karti thi. [Q35, Q66]\n6. Chola Naval Power & Overseas Conquests\n● Chola kings ke paas massive troops aur proficient naval power wing tha — Chola navy ne empire ke\nexpansion mein vital role play kiya, Ceylon (Sri Lanka) ki conquest aur Srivijaya/Sinhala jaise jagaho par\nnaval raids ke through. [Q24]"," ● Chola Dynasty ki sthapna Vijayalaya ne ki, lekin Parantaka-I ne isse solidify kiya — unhone Madura\n(Pandya) ke raja ko haraakar 'Madurai-Konda' ki title li. Rajaraja-I aur unke bete Rajendra-I ne South\nEast Asia ke Sailendra empire (Srivijaya) ke against naval expeditions bheji thi. [Q16]\n● Rajendra Chola-I (Rajaraja-I ke bete) ne apni dominant naval campaigns (Srivijaya Empire ke against\nbhi) se Bay of Bengal ko practically ek 'Chola Lake' bana diya tha. [Q26]\n● Rajendra-I ne Bengal ke Pala king Mahipala ko haraya — Ganges tak ki apni victorious campaign\ncelebrate karne ke liye unhone 'Gangaikonda' (Ganga ke conqueror) ki title li, aur ek nayi capital\n'Gangaikonda Cholapuram' banayi. [Q27]\n● Apni nayi capital Gangaikonda Cholapuram ke liye paani ka intezaam karne ke liye, Rajendra Chola I ne\nek bada artificial lake banwaya jise 'Chola Gangam' kehte hain. [Q28]\n● Rajaraja-I ke gaddi par baithne (985 AD) se Chola empire ka golden era shuru hua — wo pehle Chola\nking the jinhone ek formidable Naval Army banayi, jisse Sri Lanka aur Maldives jaisi overseas territories\nconquer ki gayi. [Q29]\n● Rajaraja-I ne Sri Lanka par invade karke uski capital Anuradhapura destroy ki — unhone sirf Sri Lanka\nka northern hissa capture kiya, southern hissa independent raha. Baad mein unke bete Rajendra-I ne\nsouthern hissa bhi capture karke poore Ceylon ko Chola control mein le liya. [Q30, Q31]\n● Ceylon ke king Vijayabahu ne Kulottunga-I ke period mein Sinhala Island ki independence declare kar di\nthi — lekin Kulottunga ne koi hostility nahi dikhayi, ulta apni beti ki shaadi Sinhala prince Virapperumal\nse karwa di, Sri Lanka ko complete azaadi de di. [Q32]\n7. Chola Succession Practice & Historical Sources\n● Chola emperors generally apne hi tenure mein apna successor ('Yuvraj'/crown prince) elect kar dete\nthe, jo unke baad empire ka heir banta tha — isse succession ki wajah se hone wali ladaiyan ruk jaati\nthi. [Q25]\n● Assertion-Reason: Cholas ke baare mein humein unke predecessors se zyada jaankari hai (sahi),\nkyunki Rajaraja-I aur Rajendra-I ne temples ki deewaron par inscriptions likhwaye — Rajaraja-I ne apne\nancestors ki jeeto ki kahaniyan likhne-collect karne ki tradition shuru ki (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko\nexplain karta hai). [Q33]\n8. Battle of Takkolam & the Decline of the Cholas\n● Famous 'Battle of Takkolam' Rajaditya (Chola king Parantaka-I ke bete) aur Rashtrakuta King Krishna-\nIII ki confederacy ke beech lada gaya tha — Chola aur Rashtrakutas ke beech ka ye important conflict\ntha. [Q67]\n●\n Disputed: Chola dynasty ka final devastation kisne kiya iska ek clear jawab nahi hai — ~1250 AD\n⚠️\nmein Hoysala aur Pandya kingdoms ne Chola King Rajendra III ko haraya, aur dynasty ~1279 AD tak\nkhatam ho gayi. Malik Kafur ne ~1310 AD mein South India conquer ki thi (Yadavas, Hoysalas,\nKakatiyas, Pandyas), lekin Chola empire uske aane se pehle hi decline ho chuki thi. [Q68]\n9. The Chalukya Dynasty"," ● Pulakesin-II (610-642 AD) Chalukya dynasty ke sabse capable aur powerful ruler the — unke court poet\nRavikirti dwara likha 'Aihole Inscription' unki achievements ki gatha batata hai, jisme Harshavardhana\npar unki jeet bhi shaamil hai. [Q37]\n● Chalukya administration mein women ko high-ranking positions di jaati thi — jaise Vijaya Bhattarika\n(Chandraditya ki Queen, Vikramaditya-I ke bhai) ne apne naam se copper plates issue kiye aur\nadministration efficiently chalaya. Vikramaditya ne apni chhoti behen Kumkumdevi ki recommendation\npar ek Brahmin scholar ko village grant di. [Q38]\n● Early Chalukyas ki capital Vatapi (aaj ka Badami, Bagalkot dist., Karnataka) thi — 6th-7th centuries\nmein. [Q39]\n● Aihole Inscription (Pulakesin-II ke baare mein, Ravikirti ne Sanskrit + southern Brahmi script mein likha)\nmein poet Kalidasa ka naam mila hai — Ravikirti ne khud ki fame Kalidasa aur Bharavi jaisi bataayi thi.\n[Q40, Q41]\n● Chinese traveller Matwalin ne Chalukya reign ke dauran China-India relationship ka account diya tha.\n[Q82]\n● Chalukya dynasty ne North India par kabhi raj NAHI kiya — unka rule mainly Deccan aur South India\ntak centralized tha, capital Badami (Vatapi) thi. North India par Mauryas, Guptas aur Rajput clans ka raj\ntha. [Q83]\n● Chalukya (Solanki) King Kumarapala (Gujarat), Jainism se bahut influenced the aur Jain scholar\nHemachandra ke shishya ban gaye the — Jain traditions ke mutabik unhone Kashi region mein janwaro\nke against cruelty rokne ke liye apna minister bheja tha. [Q84]\n10. The Pallava Dynasty\n● Pallava king Narasimha Varman I (630-668 AD, 'Mahamalla'/great wrestler bhi kehlaate the) ne 642 AD\nmein Ceylon (Sri Lanka) ke liye 2 naval expeditions bheji thi (ek Sri Lankan prince ki madad ke liye).\nUnke time famous Panch Ratha Temples bane, aur unhone Chalukya capital Vatapi ko capture-destroy\nkarke 'Vatapikonda' ki title li. [Q42]\n● Capital-Dynasty match: Badami → Chalukyas (Pulakesin-II unke glorious king the); Kanchipuram →\nPallavas ki capital; Kannauj → Harsha aur unki behen Rajyashri ne saath mein raj kiya; Madurai →\nPandyas ki capital. [Q77]\n● Historical events ka chronological order: (2) Mahendravarman-I ne Pallava Power establish ki (600-630\nAD) → (4) Gopala ne Pala dynasty banayi (750 AD) → (1) Mihirabhoja/Bhoja I, Gurjara Pratihara\ndynasty ke powerful ruler bane (836-885 AD) → (3) Parantaka-I ne significant Chola power establish ki\n(907-953 AD). [Q78]\n● Pallava rulers ka chronological order: Mahendravarman I (600-630 AD) → Narsinghvarman I (630-668\nAD) → Parmeshvaravarman I (~670-700 AD) → Nandivarman II (731-795 AD). [Q81]\n11. The Chera Dynasty\n● Udiyanjiral, Chera dynasty se belong karte the — Chera empire modern Kerala mein located thi. Wo\nSangam period ke pehle historical king the — legends ke mutabik unhone Mahabharata war ke sabhi\nfighters ko ek feast di thi. [Q70]"," ● Pairs check: South India ke states (6th-12th century) aur unki capitals — sab pairs sahi hain except\nChera-Puducheri (galat) — Chera ki actual capital Vanchi (ya Karur) thi, Puducheri nahi. [Q79]\n● Chera dynasty ki capital Karur/Karuvur thi (inland capital) — kuch sources ke mutabik unki coastal\ncapital Thondi bhi thi. Chera ka doosra prominent naam 'Vanchi' bhi tha. [Q80]\n12. The Pandya Dynasty\n● Vengi (Vaigai) river Pandya state ki lifeline thi — ye river Madurai ke pass Kandan Manikanur mein\noriginate hoti hai. Pandya state Kaveri river ke south mein situated tha. [Q71]\n● ~26 BC mein, ek South Indian Pandya raja ne Rome ke Augustus ke darbar mein ek ambassador bheja\ntha, trade-diplomacy badhane ke liye — Pandya dynasty ka South India mein sabse lamba reign\nduration raha, unki capital Madurai thi. [Q87]\n● Famous Meenakshi Mandir, Madurai (Tamil Nadu) mein situated hai — Madurai, Pandyas ki capital thi.\nSangam era mein yahi 1st aur 3rd Sangam conventions organize hui thi (Acharya Agastya aur Nakkirar\nki presidency mein). [Q89, Q90]\n13. Other South Indian Dynasties — Kadamba & Kakatiya\n● Kadamba rulers ki capital Vanavasi (Banavasi, aaj ke Karnataka mein) thi — is dynasty ki sthapna\nMayurasharman ne ki thi, baad mein Chalukya king Pulakesin-II ne unke state ko annex kar liya.\n(Tanjore Cholas ki, Kanchi Pallavas ki, aur Badami Chalukyas ki capital thi.) [Q85]\n● Motupalli (aaj ke Andhra Pradesh mein), Kakatiya kingdom ka ek bahut important seaport tha —\nVenetian traveller Marco Polo isi port se hoke Kakatiya kingdom gaye the aur Andhra Desh ki\nprosperity-trade ke baare mein tareef mein likha. [Q86]\n14. Sangam Literature — Tolkappiyam, Kural & the Twin Epics\n● 'Tolkappiyam', 2nd Sangam era ki residual text hai aur Tamil literature ka sabse purana available text\nhai — grammar aur poetry (poetics) par ek comprehensive treatise hai. Author Tolkappiyar, Sage\nAgastya ke 12 disciples mein se ek the. Ye 3 parts (Ezhuttu-letter, Col-word, Porul-subject matter) mein\nbata hua hai, har part 9 sections ka hai. [Q45, Q46, Q47]\n● Great Tamil epic 'Silappadikaram' ke author Ilango Adigal the — Chola King Karikal ke pote maane\njaate hain. Isme Kannagi aur unke pati Kovalan ki tragic love story hai. [Q48]\n● Match: Thirukural → Philosophy (ethics ka manual); Tolkappiyam → Grammar; Silapadikaram → Love\nStory (Kannagi-Kovalan); Manimekalai → Merchant story (Silappadikaram ka sequel). [Q49]\n● Sangam literature South India ki sabse purani available Tamil literature hai — Sangam poets ko Varna\nka social classification pata tha (Brahmana, Kshatriya, Vaishya, Vellalars/Sudras ka zikr milta hai).\nSangam poems mein heroism, martial valor aur warrior ethic ko celebrate kiya jaata hai, aur nature ki\nmagical forces ka bhi zikr hai. [Q52]\n● 'Kural' (Tirukkural) Tamil bhasha mein compose hui — ise Tamil literature ka 'Bible' aur 'Laghuveda'\nmaana jaata hai. Isse 'Muppal' bhi kehte hain, aur famous Tamil poet-philosopher Tiruvalluvar ne likha.\n[Q60, Q61]"," ● Tamil Ramayanam (Ramavataram) ke author Kamban the — unhone ye Chola period mein likhi thi.\n[Q63]\n15. Sangam Assemblies & Sage Agastya\n● 'Sangam' ka matlab hai 'Poets ki Conference' ya 'Scholars ka Forum' — 3 Sangams Pandya kings ke\npatronage mein hui. 1st Sangam: Madurai (Sage Agastya ne preside kiya). 2nd Sangam: Kapadapuram\n(Agastya, baad mein Tolkappiyar ne preside kiya). 3rd Sangam: Madurai (Nakkirar ne preside kiya).\n[Q75]\n● Sage Agastya ko South India ko 'Aryanised' karne ka credit diya jaata hai — mana jaata hai ki Gods ke\nrequest par wo south gaye aur wahi reh gaye. Unhe 'Father of Tamil Literature' bhi kaha jaata hai,\nunhone pehle Sangam ki presidency ki thi. [Q76]\n16. Sangam-Era Ports, Trade Centres & Roman Contact\n● Tagara (aaj ka Ter, Maharashtra) Kalyan (western coast) aur Vengi (eastern coast) ko jodne wale\nancient trade route par ek significant trade centre tha. [Q36]\n● 'Yavanapriya' ancient Sanskrit texts mein Pepper (kaali mirch) ke liye use hone wala term tha — Indian\nblack pepper Roman cooking mein bahut favourite ingredient thi, isliye ise 'Yavanapriya'\n(Greeks/Yavanas ka favourite) kaha jaata tha. [Q43]\n● Arikamedu (Pondicherry ke pass, south-eastern coast) se Roman Empire ke saath trade relations ke\nevidence mile hain — Augustus Caesar ki tasveer wala ek intaglio, Roman beads/gems/Amphora jars\nmile hain. Dubreuil ne Arikamedu ko 'a true Roman city' kaha tha. Ye Eastern India ka sabse bada Indo-\nRoman trading station tha. [Q53, Q54]\n● 'The Periplus of the Erythraean Sea' ke anonymous Greek author ne Arikamedu port ko 'Poduke' naam\nse refer kiya tha. Yahin Roman settlement/trading post ke archaeological evidence mile hain. [Q55, Q56]\n● 'Amphora Jar' ek lambi patli gardan wala jar hota tha, dono taraf handles ke saath — ancient Rome-\nGreece mein wine/oil transport-storage ke liye use hota tha. Aise kai jars Arikamedu mein mile hain,\nRoman trade ka proof. [Q57]\n● Uraiyur (Cauvery river ke kinare, Tiruchirappalli) Sangam era mein cotton trade ka bahut important\ncentre tha — ise Koli aur Varanam bhi kehte the, 'Periplus of the Erythraean Sea' mein bhi iska zikr hai.\n[Q69]\n● Sangam ports western coast (Chera kingdom) par: Naura, Tondi, Mushiri (Muziris), Nelisanda. Eastern\ncoast ke prominent ports: Korkai (Pandyan) aur Puhar/Poompuhar (Kaveripattinam - Chola). [Q72, Q73]\n● Roman Empire ke saath maritime trade South India mein mainly Chera Kingdom se shuru hui — Roman\nobjects, coins, pottery Muziris (Chera territory) aur Arikamedu (Puducherry) mein mile hain. [Q88]\n17. Sangam-Era Kingdoms & Society\n● Sangam Literature mein Chola, Chera aur Pandya — 3 major Southern kingdoms ki origin/rise ka\nvistarpoorvak zikr hai. Kadamba dynasty (ya inke alawa koi bhi dynasty) classical Sangam literature\nmein ek ruling power ki tarah mention NAHI hai. [Q58]"," ● Sangam Age (Tamil country) mein Chera, Chola aur Pandya — teeno major ruling dynasties thi.\nPallavas bahut baad mein ek badi power ban kar ubhare, wo early Sangam age ke rulers NAHI the.\n[Q59]\n● 'Vattakirutal' ek ancient Tamil martial practice thi — jung mein haare hue raja dwara khud ko bhookha\nrakhkar (fasting unto death) ritual suicide karna, Sangam period mein prevalent thi. [Q62]\n● Sangam texts ke mutabik 'Kon', 'Ko' aur 'Mannan' — teeno titles King (raja) ke liye use hote the. [Q74]\n18. Bhakti Saints — Alvars, Nayanars, Siddhas & Lingayats\n● Shaivite saints ki writings ka collection 'Fifth Veda' maana jaata hai, jiska naam 'Thirumurai' hai — ye\n12-volume compendium hai, Shiva ki tareef mein hymns, 6th se 11th century CE tak ke. Ye Vedas aur\nSaiva Agamas ke saath Saiva Siddhanta philosophy ka aadhar banata hai. [Q50]\n● Tradition ke mutabik total 12 Alvars (Vishnu ke devotees) aur 63 Nayanars (Shiva ke devotees) hain —\ndono South India ki Bhakti tradition ke saint-poets ke groups hain. [Q51]\n● Siddhas Sangam period se trace hote hain — wo refined monotheistic the aur idolatry (murti pooja) ki\nninda karte the. Kannada region ke Lingayats ne Brahmins ke caste-based superiority ko challenge kiya,\nrebirth ke theory ko question kiya, aur widow-remarriage ko encourage kiya. [Q64]\n19. Miscellaneous — Language, Architecture & Match Lists\n● Halbi ek Eastern Indo-Aryan language hai (Aryan language family), jo Chhattisgarh ke Bastar region\nmein boli jaati hai — Oriya aur Marathi ke beech ek transitional language ki tarah kaam karti hai, Oriya\naur Devanagari scripts mein likhi jaati hai. [Q44]\n● Match: Gupta → Deogarh (Dashavatara Temple); Chandela → Khajuraho (famous temple complex);\nChalukya → Badami (unki capital); Pallava → Panamalai (Talagirisvara temple). [Q65]\n● South India ke temples ke mighty gateways ko 'Gopurams' kehte hain — Dravidian style Pandyas aur\nCholas ke time flourish hui. Pandya period mein temples chhote the lekin unke courtyard ke around\nbahut ramparts banaye gaye the. [Q92]\n● Match: Meenakshi Mandir → Madurai (Tamil Nadu); Venkateswara Mandir → Tirumala (Andhra\nPradesh); Mahakal Mandir → Ujjain (Madhya Pradesh); Belur Matha → Howrah (West Bengal —\nRamakrishna Mission ka headquarters, Swami Vivekananda ne banaya). [Q91]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · South India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0168","t":"14 Ancient Literature and Litterateurs","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" ANCIENT LITERATURE & LITTERATEURS — FULL MIND MAP\n📚\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Foreign & Greek Historians\n2. Grammarians & Linguists\n3. Vishakhadatta — Mudrarakshasa\n4. Classical Literature of the Gupta Era\n5. Other Medieval Authors — Dandin, Surdas & Tulsidas\n6. Kalidasa — Life, Works & Court\n7. Natyashastra & Performing Arts\n8. Historical Chronicles — Rajatarangini & Gaudavaho\n9. Court Poets & Literary Works — Important Match Lists\n10. Sanskrit Epics Based on the Mahabharata\n11. Scientist-Scholars — Charaka, Varahamihira & Brahmagupta\n12. Political Treatises — Kamandaka's Nitisara\n13. Playwrights & Their Works — Various Authors\n14. Milindapanha\n15. Regional Bardic Literature — The Raso Texts\n16. Jain & Buddhist Texts\n17. Ashvaghosha — Saundarananda\n18. Harshavardhana — Playwright-King\n19. Bhasa's Plays\n20. Jayadeva — Geet Govind\n21. The Bhagavad Gita & the Mahabharata\n22. Panchatantra\n23. Dharmashastra & Law Texts\n24. Mathematics & Astronomy\n25. Parmar Dynasty — Historical Sources\n26. Sangam Literature & Ancient Trade\n27. Miscellaneous — Puranas & Ancient Music\n1. Foreign & Greek Historians\n● Greek author Herodotus ko 'Father of History' kaha jaata hai — unki famous book 'Historica' 5th century\nBC ke Indo-Persian relations describe karti hai. [Q1]\n● Pairs check: 'The Natural History' Pliny the Elder (Roman author) ne likhi thi, Ptolemy ne NAHI —\nPtolemy 'Geography' likhne ke liye famous hain. [Q84]\n2. Grammarians & Linguists\n● Match: Ashtadhyayi → Panini; Mahabhashya → Patanjali; Nirukta → Yaska; Varttika → Katyayan. [Q2]\n● Match: Panini → Ashtadhyayi; Vatsyayana → Kamasutra; Chanakya → Arthashastra; Kalhana →\nRajatarangini. [Q12]\n● 'Ashtadhyayi' (Sanskrit grammar ki foundational text) Panini ne likhi thi. [Q15]\n3. Vishakhadatta — Mudrarakshasa"," ● 'Mudrarakshasa' (Sanskrit drama) Vishakhadatta ne likha tha — likha toh Gupta period mein gaya, lekin\nisme describe kiya gaya hai ki Chandragupta Maurya ne Kautilya ki madad se Nandas ko kaise\noverthrow kiya. Ye Mauryas ke time ki socio-economic condition ki bhi tasveer deta hai. [Q3, Q4]\n4. Classical Literature of the Gupta Era\n● Sanskrit literature Gupta period mein apne peak (apogee) par pahunchi — prose aur poetry dono\nequally likhi jaati thi. Gupta era ke classic literature examples: Amarakosh (Amar Singh), Kamasutra\n(Vatsyayana), Meghadutam (Kalidasa), aur Mudrarakshasa (Vishakhadatta). [Q5]\n5. Other Medieval Authors — Dandin, Surdas & Tulsidas\n● Famous authors aur unki books: Surdas — Sursagar, Sur Saravali, Sahitya-Lahiri; Dandin (Dandi) —\nDaskumarcharitam; Tulsidas — Ramcharit Manas, Vinaya Patrika, Kavitavali; Kalidasa —\nAbhigyanshakuntalam, Kumarsambhavam, Malavikagnimitram, Meghadutam. [Q6, Q7]\n6. Kalidasa — Life, Works & Court\n● 'Kumarasambhava' (epic poem) Kalidasa ne compose ki thi. [Q8]\n●\n Exam Trap: Kalidasa ki kai epic Sanskrit mein hain, lekin 'Janaki-haranam' unhone NAHI likhi — ye\n⚠️\nKumaradasa ne likhi thi. Isi tarah 'Uttararamacharitam' (Lord Rama ki life par 7-act Sanskrit play) bhi\nKalidasa ki nahi, Bhavabhuti ki rachna hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Match: Allauddin Khalji → Amir Khusrau; Chandra Gupta II → Kalidasa (Kumarasambhavam,\nRaghuvansham, Malavikagnimitram); Samudra Gupta → Harisena; Harshavardhana → Banabhatta.\n[Q36]\n● Statements check: Panini ~7th/6th century BC ke the, Pushyamitra Shunga se bahut pehle (jo Patanjali\nse associated hain) — galat statement. Amarasimha (lexicographer, Navratna) Chandragupta-II ke\ndarbar mein the, Harshavardhana ke NAHI — galat. Kalidasa, Chandragupta-II ke darbar ke sabse\nprominent Ratna the — yehi sahi statement hai. [Q47]\n● 'Shakuntalam' (Abhigyanshakuntalam) Kalidasa ne likhi — unki 7 genuine works mein\nVikramorvashiyam, Malavikagnimitram, Raghuvamsham, Kumarasambhavam bhi shaamil hain. [Q52]\n●\n Trap: 'Mrichchhakatikam' Kalidasa ki rachna NAHI hai — ye Sudraka ne likhi thi. Kalidasa ki famous\n⚠️\nmasterpieces mein Meghaduta, Ritusamhara aur Vikramorvashiyam shaamil hain. [Q53]\n● Kalidasa ka pehla play 'Malavikagnimitram' hai — 5 acts mein, isme Shunga dynasty ke King Agnimitra\n(Vidisha) aur exiled servant girl Malavika ki love story hai. [Q54]\n● Malavikagnimitram mein Agnimitra, Pushyamitra Shunga (Shunga dynasty ke founder) ke bete hain —\nunki love story is book mein describe hui hai. [Q55]\n7. Natyashastra & Performing Arts"," ● North Indian classical music ki 'Bible Book' Natyashastra hai — ye performing arts par ek Sanskrit\ntreatise hai, Bharat Muni ko attribute ki jaati hai. [Q11]\n● 'Natyashastra' Bharatamuni ne likhi — ye ancient India ka treatise hai jo drama, dance aur music cover\nkarta hai, classical Indian arts ka foundation hai. [Q81]\n8. Historical Chronicles — Rajatarangini & Gaudavaho\n● 'Rajatarangini' (River of Kings) Kalhana (ek Kashmiri) ne likhi — Kashmir ki history ka account deti hai.\n[Q13, Q14]\n● Rajatarangini jaisa hi ek historical work 'Gaudavaho' hai — Vakpati ne likha, jo Kanauj ke raja\nYasovarman ke darbar ke poet the. Isme Yasovarman ki digvijaya (conquest) ka detailed description hai\n(Prakrit epic poem). [Q16]\n● Kalhana ke contemporary ruler Jai Singh (1128-1149, Kashmir) the — Kalhana ne Rajatarangini unhi ke\nreign mein complete ki. Isme 8 Taranga aur 7826 verses hain — pehle 3 Tarangas mein Kashmir ki\nconventional ancient history hai. [Q37, Q38]\n● Kalhana ki Rajatarangini ko Jonaraja aur Srivara ne continue kiya — Jonaraja ne Sultan Zainul Abedin\nke reign tak likha (usi naam 'Rajatarangini/Rajavali' se), aur unki mrityu ke baad unke shishya Srivara ne\nKashmir ki history aage badhayi. [Q39]\n9. Court Poets & Literary Works — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Bharavi → Kiratarjuniyam; Harsha → Nagananda; Kalidasa → Malavikagnimitram; Rajasekhara\n→ Karpuramanjari. [Q17]\n● Match: Varahamihira → Brihat Samhita; Vishakhadatta → Devi-Chandraguptam (aur Mudrarakshasa);\nSudraka → Mrichchha-Katikam; Bilhana → Vikramankadevacharita. ('Prabandha Chintamani'\nMerutungacharya ne likhi thi.) [Q48]\n● Pairs check: 'Devichandragupta' Vishakhadatta ne likhi (Bilhana ne nahi) — galat. 'Hammira\nMahakavya' Nayachandra Suri ne likhi — sahi. 'Milinda-panha' Nagasena ka dialogue tha (Nagarjuna ka\nnahi) — galat. 'Nitivakyamrita' Jain monk Somadeva Suri ne likhi — sahi. Isliye sirf 2 pairs sahi hain.\n[Q49]\n● Match: Ashtanga Samgraha (Vagbhata) → Medical; Das Rupaka (Dhananjaya) → Play/Dramaturgy;\nLilavati (Bhaskaracharya) → Maths; Mahabhasya (Patanjali) → Grammar. [Q61]\n● Match: Sarvavarma → Katantra; Sudraka → Mrichchhakatikam; Vigyaneshwara → Mitakshara; Kalhana\n→ Rajtarangini. [Q67]\n10. Sanskrit Epics Based on the Mahabharata\n● 'Kiratarjuniyam' (Sanskrit ki sabse powerful poem maani jaati hai) Bharavi ne likhi — isme Arjuna aur\nLord Shiva (Kirata/mountain-hunter ke roop mein) ke beech Indrakeeladri Hills par combat describe hai.\n[Q18]\n● Mahabharata theme wale Sanskrit works: Naishadhiyacharita (Sriharsha, Nala-Damayanti ki story),\nKiratarjuniyam (Bharavi, Arjuna-Shiva combat), Sisupalavadha (Magha, Sisupala ka Krishna ko insult"," karna). Dashkumarcharitam (Dandi) 10 princes ki adventures ke baare mein hai, Mahabharata theme se\nrelated NAHI. [Q19]\n11. Scientist-Scholars — Charaka, Varahamihira & Brahmagupta\n● Match: Vishakhadatta → Mudrarakshasa (historical drama); Varahamihira → astronomer (Brihat Jataka,\nBrihat Samhita, Panch Siddhantika); Charaka → Kanishka ke court physician (Charaka Samhita —\nmedicine); Brahmagupta → Indian mathematician. [Q20]\n● Match: Charaka → Medicine (1st-2nd century CE ke physician); Brahmagupta → Mathematics (Gupta\ndynasty se); Varahamihira → astrologer/astronomer; Vishakhadatta → Gupta dynasty ke playwright.\n[Q21]\n● 'Charaka Samhita' Ayurveda (ancient Indian medicine) ka comprehensive text hai — Acharya Charaka\nne likhi, jinhe 'Father of Indian Medicine' kaha jaata hai. Ye 120 chapters aur 8 sections mein bata hui\nhai. [Q22, Q23]\n●\n Trap: Varahamihira ne 'Amarkosha' NAHI likhi — ye Amarsimha ne likhi thi. Varahamihira ne\n⚠️\nPanchasiddhantika, Brihat Samhita aur Brihat Jataka likhi. [Q24]\n● Varahamihira ki 'Panchasiddhantika' Greek astronomy par based hai. [Q25]\n● 'Brihat Samhita' (Varaha Mihira, Gupta period) ek encyclopedic work hai — astronomy, planetary\nmovements, eclipses, rainfall, clouds, architecture, crops, perfumes waghera jaise wide-ranging subjects\ncover karta hai. [Q44]\n12. Political Treatises — Kamandaka's Nitisara\n● 'Nitisara' (ek early politics ki book) Kamandaka ne likhi — isse Indian political thought refine hua, aur ye\nSouth-Southeast Asia mein bahut influential rachna ban gayi. [Q26]\n13. Playwrights & Their Works — Various Authors\n●\n Trap: 'Kadambari' Subandhu ne NAHI, Banabhatta ne compose ki thi — ye ek common galat-match\n⚠️\nhai. [Q27]\n● Bhavabhuti (King Yashovarman, Kannauj ke court poet), Hastimalla (Kannada playwright, Hoysala\nperiod) aur Kshemeshvara (11th century Kashmiri poet, 'Dasavatar Charita' ke liye jaane jaate) — teeno\nplaywrights the. [Q45]\n●\n Trap: 'Buddhacharita' Vasubandhu ne NAHI likhi — ye Ashvaghosha ki rachna hai (Buddha ki life ki\n⚠️\npoetic narrative). Baaki sahi hain: Sudraka ne Mrichchhakatikam, Vishakhadatta ne Mudrarakshasa, aur\nBanabhatta ne Harshacharita likhi. [Q46]\n●\n Trap: 'Karpuramanjari' Harsha ne NAHI likhi — ye Rajshekhara ne likhi thi, jo Gurjara-Pratihara\n⚠️\nkings ke poet laureate the. [Q51]\n● 'Matta Vilasa Prahasana' (A Farce of Drunken Sport) Pallava ruler-scholar Mahendra Varman-I ne likhi\n— ye chhota Sanskrit play 7th century Kanchipuram ki social-religious life describe karta hai. [Q75]"," ● 'Lalit Vigraharaj' (Lalita Vigraharaja Nataka) drama Somadeva ne likhi — wo Chahamana (Chauhan)\nking Vigraharaja IV (Bisaldeo, Shakambhari) ke court poet the. [Q76]\n14. Milindapanha\n● 'Milindapanha' ek Buddhist Pali text hai — Indian monk Nagasena aur Indo-Greek king Milinda\n(Menander) ke beech ek dialogue ke roop mein likhi gayi hai. Isme agricultural work ke 8 alag phases\nbhi explain kiye gaye hain. [Q28, Q29, Q30, Q31, Q32, Q33]\n15. Regional Bardic Literature — The Raso Texts\n●\n Trap: Raso texts ka sahi pairing: Prithviraj Raso → Chand Bardai; Bisaldeva Raso → Narapati;\n⚠️\nKhuman Raso → Dalpati Vijay (Karnidan NAHI); Shatrusal Raso → Dungar Singh. [Q34]\n16. Jain & Buddhist Texts\n● Parishishtaparvan (Hemchandra) aur Trishashtilakshana Mahapurana (Chavund Rai/Chamund Rai) —\nJain texts hain. Nettipakarana aur Avadanashataka — Buddhist texts hain. [Q35]\n17. Ashvaghosha — Saundarananda\n● Ashvaghosha (noted poet, Buddhism ke pracharak) ne famous court poem 'Saundarananda Kavya'\nlikhi. [Q40]\n18. Harshavardhana — Playwright-King\n● Harshavardhana — ek bade conqueror hone ke saath-saath education-learning ke bade patron bhi the.\nUnhe 'Ratnavali', 'Priyadarshika' aur 'Nagananda' ka author maana jaata hai — Harshacharita unke\ncourt poet Banabhatta ne likhi thi, Harsha ne khud NAHI. [Q41, Q42, Q43]\n19. Bhasa's Plays\n● 'Swapnavasavadatta' (Svapnavasvadattam) Bhasa ne likhi — Vatsa King Udayana aur Avanti princess\nVasavadatta ki romance describe karti hai. [Q56]\n● 'Madhyama-vyayoga' Bhasa ki rachna hai (Kavyalankara Bhamaha ne, Natyashastra Bharata Muni ne,\naur Mahabhashya Patanjali ne likhi). [Q57]\n20. Jayadeva — Geet Govind"," ● 'Geet Govind' (epic poem, Sanskrit mein) Jayadeva ne 12th century mein likhi — Krishna aur\nVrindavana ki gopiyo (khaaskar Radha) ke sambandh ko describe karti hai, 12 chapters mein organize\nhai. [Q58, Q60]\n● Jayadeva, Bengal ke Sena dynasty ke King Lakshmana Sen ke darbar ke royal poet the. [Q59]\n21. The Bhagavad Gita & the Mahabharata\n● 'Karm karo, phal ki chinta mat karo' (Thy right is to work only, but never with its fruits —\n\nकर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते\n\n\nमाफलेषुकदाचन) — ye famous lines Bhagavad Gita mein Lord Krishna ne Arjuna se kahi thi. [Q62]\n● 'Jo yaha hai wo kahi aur bhi milega, lekin jo yaha nahi hai wo kahi nahi milega' — ye famous statement\nMahabharata epic mein hai. [Q64]\n22. Panchatantra\n● 'Panchatantra' (Indian animal fables ka collection) 15 Indian aur 40 foreign languages mein translate ho\nchuki hai — Pandit Vishnu Sharma ko iski compilation ka credit jaata hai. Mughal era mein Abul Fazl ne\nisse 'Ayar-e-Danish' naam se Persian mein translate kiya. [Q65]\n● 'Panchatantra' originally Vishnu Sharma ne likhi thi. [Q66]\n23. Dharmashastra & Law Texts\n● Match: Devana Bhatta → Smriti Chandrika; Hemadri → Chaturvarga Chintamani; Madhvacharya →\nParashar Madhav; Ballal Sena → Daan Sagar. [Q68]\n● 'Mitakshara' (Vijnanesvara ne, Yajnavalkya smriti par vivarti likhi) aur 'Dayabhaga' (Jimutavahana ne\nlikhi) — Hindu property law se related treatises hain. Mitakshara mein beto ko pita ke jeete-ji hi property\nka right claim karne ka adhikar tha, jabki Dayabhaga mein sirf pita ki mrityu ke baad. Mitakshara family\nke male-female dono members ki property se related hai. [Q69]\n● 'Manusmriti' (Manav Dharam Shastra) mainly Social System (samajik vyavastha, laws) se related hai —\nye 18 major Smritis mein se ek hai, Manu ko iska author/originator maana jaata hai jinhone social-moral\ncodes establish kiye. [Q78]\n● Manu ko ancient India ka great law-giver (aur pehla law-giver) maana jaata hai. [Q79, Q80]\n24. Mathematics & Astronomy\n● Bhaskaracharya (Bhaskara-II, 12th century) Algebra field mein apne contribution ke liye especially jaane\njaate hain — unki famous book 'Siddhantasiromani' ke 4 parts hain: Lilavati, Bijaganita (Algebra),\nGanitadhyaya aur Goladhyaya. [Q70]\n● 'Lilavati' (Mathematics treatise) ke author Bhaskaracharya ek renowned mathematician-astronomer the.\n[Q71, Q72]"," ● Aryabhatta ek renowned mathematician-astronomer the — unki major work 'Aryabhatiya' astronomy,\nspherical trigonometry, arithmetic, algebra aur plane trigonometry cover karti hai. Wo pehle the jinhone\nbataya ki Prithvi gol (spherical) hai aur apni axis par ghoomti hai — unhe decimal place value system\ndiscover karne ka credit bhi jaata hai. [Q73, Q74]\n● 'Zero' (0) ka concept aur digit ek anonymous Indian ne 2nd century BC mein discover kiya tha (baad\nmein Brahmagupta ne ise formally equations mein popularize kiya). Arabs ne India se ye seekha aur\nEurope tak phailaya — Arabs ne pehli baar 873 AD mein zero use kiya. [Q82, Q83]\n25. Parmar Dynasty — Historical Sources\n● Parmar Dynasty ki history ke sources hain: Navsahsank Charit (Padmagupta), Prabandha Chintamani\n(Merutunga), aur Harsola copper plate inscription. Navsahsank Charita mein Mount Abu ko Parmaras ki\norigin place bataya gaya hai. [Q50]\n26. Sangam Literature & Ancient Trade\n● Milindapanha aur Jataka Tales mein merchants/guilds/trade routes ka zikr milta hai, lekin classical\nSangam Sahitya (literature) mainly love (Akam) aur war (Puram) themes par focus karti hai — isliye\nSangam Sahitya ancient trade routes ke baare mein khaamosh (silent) hai. [Q63]\n27. Miscellaneous — Puranas & Ancient Music\n● Mahanadi river ka ancient naam 'Nilotpala' Vayu Purana mein mila hai — ye river central-eastern India\n(mainly Chhattisgarh aur Odisha) se hoke behti hai. [Q77]\n● Diye gaye options mein sabse purana musical instrument 'Veena' hai — Vedas mein iska baar-baar zikr\nhai aur Samudragupta ke coins par bhi ye depict hui hai. Sitar, Sarod aur Tabla bahut baad mein,\nmedieval era mein introduce/popular hue. [Q85]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Ancient Literature and Litterateurs Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0169","t":"15 Pre Medieval Period","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" PRE-MEDIEVAL PERIOD — FULL MIND MAP\n🏰\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Chauhan (Chahamana) Dynasty\n2. Chauhan-Era Literature & Bardic Tales\n3. The Tomar Dynasty & the Founding of Delhi\n4. The Chandela Dynasty of Jejakabhukti\n5. The Gahadavala Dynasty\n6. The Pala Dynasty — Origin, Foreign Contact & Elected Kings\n7. Buddhist Centres of Learning — Odantapuri, Vikramshila & Sompura\n8. The Rashtrakuta Dynasty\n9. The Gurjara-Pratihara Dynasty\n10. The Solanki (Chalukya) Dynasty of Gujarat\n11. The Sena Dynasty of Bengal\n12. Jurists & Court Scholars of Medieval India\n13. Dynasty-Capital & King Match Lists\n14. The Tripartite Struggle for Kannauj\n15. The Paramara Dynasty — Raja Bhoj & Others\n16. The Kalachuri Dynasty\n17. Famous Places & Their Regions\n18. 'Gaudavaho' — A Historical Prakrit Epic\n19. Economic History — The 'Araghatta'\n20. Kashmir — Sultan Zainul Abidin\n21. The Karnata Dynasty of Mithila\n22. The Kuruspal Inscription\n1. The Chauhan (Chahamana) Dynasty\n● Ajmer ke raja Prithviraja-III ko 'Prithviraj Chauhan' ke naam se jaana jaata hai — unhone 1191 AD mein\nTarain ki pehli ladai mein Muhammad Ghori ko haraya tha, lekin doosri ladai mein khud haar gaye. [Q1]\n● Vigraharaj IV, Chauhan dynasty ke sabse powerful ruler the — unhone apni empire ki boundaries\nbadhayi, Tomaras ko haraakar Eastern Punjab aur Delhi par kabza kiya. [Q2]\n2. Chauhan-Era Literature & Bardic Tales\n● 'Hammir Mahakavya' ke mutabik Chauhans Suryavanshi the — unhe 'Chahman' (Surya ke bete) ki\nsantaan mana jaata hai, aur wo 4 Agnikula (fire clan) dynasties mein se ek the. [Q6]\n● Aalha-Udal, Mahoba se the — wo Chandel King Parmardidev (Parmal, 1165-1203 CE) ke\ncommandants the, jo Prithviraj Chauhan ke saath ladai mein maare gaye the. Chandel-Chauhan ki is\nterrific struggle ka description 'Prithviraj Raso' (Chand Bardai) aur 'Parmal Raso' ke 'Alha-Khand'\n(Jagnik) mein milta hai. [Q7, Q8]\n● 'Prithviraj Raso' ke author Chand Bardai the — Prithviraj Chauhan ke court poet. [Q9]\n● 'Prithviraja Vijaya' (Prithviraja-III ki life par Sanskrit epic poem) Jayanaka ne likhi thi. [Q10]\n●\n Trap: 'Hammir Raso' Sharangdev (Sarangadhar) ne likhi thi, Abdur Rehman ne NAHI — Abdur\n⚠️\nRehman (Addahaman) 'Sandesh Rasak' likhne ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q11]"," 3. The Tomar Dynasty & the Founding of Delhi\n● Tomar dynasty (originally Gurjar-Pratiharas ke feudatories) ne 8th century mein Dhillika (aaj ki Delhi)\nsheher basaya tha — Anangpal Tomar Rajput ke through. [Q12]\n4. The Chandela Dynasty of Jejakabhukti\n● 'Jejakabhukti' Bundelkhand ka ancient naam tha — ye Chandel dynasty ke founder Nannuk ke pote Jay\nShakti (Jeja/Jejak) ke naam par pada. [Q13]\n● Dhangadev (Dhanga), Chandela dynasty (Jejakbhukti) ke raja the — unhone Kandariya Mahadev\ntemple banwaya, aur apna sharir Ganga-Yamuna Sangam (Prayagraj) mein tyaag kar Moksha prapt ki.\n[Q14]\n● Chandela rulers ka chronological order: Yashovarman (925-950 AD) → Dhanga (950-1002 AD) →\nVidyadhara (1017/19-1029 AD) → Keertivarman (1060-1100 AD). [Q15]\n5. The Gahadavala Dynasty\n● Kumaradevi (Govind Chandra Gahadavala ki queen, Buddhist) ne Sarnath mein 'Dharma-Chakra-Jaina\nVihara' banwaya tha (Buddhist vihara hi tha, naam ke bawajood Jain nahi). [Q5]\n6. The Pala Dynasty — Origin, Foreign Contact & Elected Kings\n● Pala king Devapala Buddhist the, unhe 'Param Saugat' bhi kaha jaata tha — unhone Java king\nBalputradev (Sailendra Dynasty) ke request par Nalanda mein Buddhist Vihar develop karne ke liye 5\nvillages daan diye — ye Bihar ke rajaon ke Java-Sumatra ke saath contact ka evidence hai. [Q3]\n● Balaputradeva, Suvarnabhumi (Srivijaya/Sailendra empire ka hissa, aaj ke Indonesia-Malaysia mein) ke\nraja the — unhone Nalanda mein ek Buddhist monastery banwayi aur Devapala se request ki. [Q4]\n● 'Pundravardhan Bhukti' ancient North Bengal ka region tha — Pala, Chandra aur Sena dynasties ke\ntime iska territory North Bihar tak phaila. [Q17]\n● Pala dynasty ke founder Gopala the — Tibetan historian Lama Taranath ke mutabik, Gopala\n'Pundravardhana' ke pass paida hue the aur unhe janta ne raja chuna tha. [Q18]\n● Gopala (Pala dynasty founder) aur Pallava ruler Nandivarman Pallavamalla — dono directly janta dwara\nelect/choose kiye gaye the. Dharmapala ke Khalimpur inscription mein bataya gaya hai ki Gopala ko\nMatsya Nyaya (jungle ka kanoon) khatam karne ke liye logo ne elect kiya. Pallava ruler Permeshwar\nVarman ki achanak mrityu ke baad, logo ne Nandivarman Pallavamalla ko apna raja chuna. [Q31]\n7. Buddhist Centres of Learning — Odantapuri, Vikramshila & Sompura\n● 'Odantapuri' (Udnapur bhi kehte the) Bihar mein situated tha — Pala ruler Gopala ne isse establish kiya\ntha, ye ancient period ka ek prominent education centre tha. [Q19]"," ● Dharmapala (770-810 AD, Pala dynasty ke enthusiastic Buddhist ruler, 'Param Saugat' title) ne\nVikramshila aur Somapuri (Paharpur) — dono famous Buddhist monasteries banwayi. Renowned\nBuddhist commentator Haribhadra unke court ka hissa the. [Q20]\n● Vikramshila University Dharmapala (Pala dynasty) ne establish ki thi, Bhagalpur (Bihar) mein —\nNalanda University ke decline ke baad, Vikramshila Buddhism ka main centre ban gaya tha. Yahan\nformalized Vedic learning (Vedic texts, rituals, Vedangas jaise reasoning, medicine, law, astronomy, city\nplanning) sikhayi jaati thi. [Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Statements check: Vikramshila University Bhagalpur mein hai, Banka district mein NAHI (galat\nstatement). Ise Dharmapala ne establish kiya tha, Gopala I ne NAHI (galat statement). [Q30]\n● Early medieval period ke learning centres mein Taxila SHAAMIL NAHI hai — Takshashila (Taxila) ek\nancient/Mauryan-era Buddhist learning centre tha, early medieval period ka nahi. Nalanda 5th century\nAD mein Kumar Gupta ne banayi, Vikramshila Dharmapala ne, aur Odantapuri bhi is period ke centres\nthe. [Q32]\n8. The Rashtrakuta Dynasty\n● 736 AD mein Danti Durga ne Rashtrakuta Empire ki foundation rakhi — unki capital Manyakheta thi.\nUnhone Ujjayini mein 'Hiranyagarbha' oblation (ritual) perform ki thi. [Q33, Q34]\n● Rashtrakuta king Amoghavarsha-I ka janm 800 AD mein Shribhavan (Narmada river ke pass) mein ek\nmilitary camp mein hua tha — unke pita Govind-III apni successful campaign se laut rahe the tab. [Q35]\n● Rashtrakuta king Govind-III (Dhruva ke successor) ne South India mein apni position consolidate karne\nke baad North India par attack kiya — unhone Gurjara-Pratihara ruler Nagabhatta-II ko haraya (Sanjan\naur Radhanpur copper plate inscriptions mein iska zikr hai). [Q57]\n9. The Gurjara-Pratihara Dynasty\n● Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty (Rajputs ka 'Agni' clan) ke sabse mahaan raja Mihir Bhoj (836-885 AD) the.\n[Q36]\n● Mihir Bhoja-I, Vaishnavism ke follower the — unhe 'Aadi Varaha' aur 'Prabhas' ki titles mili. [Q37]\n● Mihir Bhoja, Emperor Ramabhadra aur Queen Appa Devi ke bete the, Nagabhatta-II ke NAHI (galat\nstatement). Unhone ~836 AD mein Kannauj capture karke apni capital banayi — Arab traveller Al-\nMasudi ne Gurjara-Pratihara kingdom ko 'Al-Juzr' aur raja ko 'Baura' bulaya tha. [Q38]\n● Gurjara-Pratihara rulers ka chronological order: Vatsaraja (775-800 AD) → Nagabhatta II (800-833 AD)\n→ Mahendrapala I (885-910 AD) → Mahipala (912-944 AD). [Q39]\n● Gurjara-Pratihara rulers the: Nagabhatta I, Vatsaraja, Nagabhatta II, Mihir Bhoja-I, Mahendrapala I,\nDevapala, waghera. 'Bharatrabhatta-I' is dynasty se SHAAMIL NAHI hai — wo Mewar ki Guhila dynasty\nse the. [Q40]\n● Arab traveller Suleman, Mihir Bhoja (Bhoja I) ke reign mein India aaye the — unhone unki military\nstrength aur empire ke vistaar ke baare mein likha. [Q41]\n● Gurjar-Pratihara dynasty ki sthapna Nagabhatta-I (730-756 AD) ne ki thi — unhone Maleksha ruler ki\narmy ko destroy karke Arabs ke invasion se Western India ko bachaya (Gwalior inscription mein zikr\nhai). [Q51]"," 10. The Solanki (Chalukya) Dynasty of Gujarat\n● Jain scholar Hemchandra, Solanki king Jaysimha Siddharaja ke time famous hue, lekin unke successor\nKumarapala (1143-1172 AD) ke court mein advisor ki tarah adorn hue — Kumarapala unke prabhaav\nmein Jainism ke devout follower ban gaye. [Q42]\n● Chalukya king Jayasimha Siddharaja ek tolerant religious raja the — Muslim author Muhammad Aufi ke\nmutabik unhone Khambhat mein ek demolished mosque ki restoration ke liye 1 lakh Balom (currency) ki\nfinancial aid di thi. [Q58]\n11. The Sena Dynasty of Bengal\n● Lakshmanasena (1178-1206 AD, Bengal ke Sena dynasty king, 28 saal raj kiya) ne apni accession\ncelebrate karne ke liye ek naya Samvat/era 'Lakshmana Samvat' shuru kiya. [Q43]\n● 'Luxman Era' (Lakshmana Samvat) Bengal ke Senas ne shuru ki thi. [Q44]\n● Sena kings ka succession order: Samantasena → Hemantasena → Vijayasena → Vallalasena/Ballal\nSena → Lakshmansena → Visvarupasena. [Q46]\n12. Jurists & Court Scholars of Medieval India\n● Medieval India ke famous jurists the: Vigyaneshvara (unhone 'Mitakshara' likhi), Hemadri, aur\nJimutavahana ('Dayabhaga' likhi). Rajashekhara ek court scholar/poet the (jurist NAHI), Gurjara-\nPratihara king Mahendrapala-I aur unke bete Mahipala-I ke — unhone Karpuramanjari, Kavyamimasa\njaise texts compile kiye. [Q45]\n●\n Disputed: Rajashekhara (great Sanskrit poet-dramatist) Gurjara-Pratihara king Mahendrapala-I ke\n⚠️\ncourt mein the, aur baad mein unke bete Mahipala-I ke bhi — isliye ye question 2 answers accept karta\nhai. [Q47]\n●\n Trap: 'Prabandhachintamani' Rajasekhara ne NAHI likhi — ye Jain scholar Merutunga ne 1304 CE\n⚠️\nmein likhi. Kavyamimamsa, Karpuramanjari aur Viddhasalabhanjika — ye teeno Rajasekhara ne likhi.\n[Q48]\n13. Dynasty-Capital & King Match Lists\n● Match: Pratihara → Kannauj; Chola → Tanjore; Paramara → Dhara; Solanki (Chalukyas of Gujarat) →\nAnhilwada. [Q49]\n● Pairs check: Nannuka — Chandela dynasty ke founder the (sahi). Nagabhata II — Gurjara-Pratihara\ndynasty ke ruler the (sahi). Jayashakti — Chandela dynasty ke the, Paramara ke NAHI (galat). Raja\nBhoj — Paramara ruler the, Rashtrakuta ke NAHI (galat). Isliye sirf 2 pairs sahi hain. [Q50]\n●\n Trap: Early Medieval UP cities ka sahi match: Koil → Aligarh; Mahotsav Nagar → Mahoba;\n⚠️\nMahoday Shri → Kannauj. Lekin 'Jejakabhukti' Bundelkhand ke barabar hai, Kaushambi ke NAHI (galat\npair). [Q56]"," 14. The Tripartite Struggle for Kannauj\n● Harsha ki mrityu ke baad, Kannauj kai powerful dynasties ke liye attraction ka center ban gaya (jaise\nGupta period mein Magadha thi) — Pala, Gurjara-Pratihara aur Rashtrakuta dynasties ne Kannauj par\ncontrol ke liye ek 'tripartite struggle' (teen-tarfa ladai) shuru ki, jo is period ka sabse important event tha.\n[Q52]\n● Cholas is tripartite struggle ka hissa NAHI the — Pala, Gurjara-Pratihara aur Rashtrakuta hi involved\nthe. [Q53]\n● 'Mahodaya' aur 'Nagar Mahoday Shri' — dono ancient Kannauj ke naam the (Mihir Bhoj ke regime\nmein). [Q54, Q55]\n15. The Paramara Dynasty — Raja Bhoj & Others\n● Chittour ka 'Tribhuvan Narayan Temple' (Samidheshwar Temple bhi kehte hain, Bhoj Jagti bhi)\nParamara Raja Bhoj (Malwa) ne banwaya — isme Lord Shiva ki teen-mukhi idol hai. [Q16]\n●\n Disputed: Parmara dynasty ki sthapna 9th century AD mein Upendra (Krishnaraj) ne ki thi — lekin\n⚠️\ncommission ne galti se 'Kanakpala' ko sahi answer maan liya tha. [Q59]\n● King Bhoja, Paramara ruler the — Paramaras ki early capital Ujjain thi, baad mein Dhara shift ho gayi.\nUnki mrityu ke baad scholars ne kaha: 'Adya Dhara NiraDhara, Niralamba Saraswati' (Dhara ab bina\naadhar ke hai, Saraswati bina sahare ke). [Q60]\n● Paramara king Bhoja ne 'Samarangana Sutradhara' likhi — artificial/scientific equipment ke baare mein\nek popular book. Unki dusri masterpieces: Saraswati Kanthabharan, Siddhanta Sangraha,\nYogaSutraVritti, Rajamartand, Yukti Kalpataru, Karucharya. [Q61]\n● Bhojshala Temple (Dhar district, MP) Paramara King Bhoj ne 1035 AD mein ek Sanskrit school ki tarah\nbanwaya tha — iski presiding deity Goddess Saraswati hain. Aaj ye Kamal Maula Mosque ke premises\nmein hai. [Q62]\n● Upendra, Munj aur Udayaditya — Paramara dynasty ke rulers the. Gangeyadev Paramara dynasty ke\nraja NAHI the — wo Kalachuri dynasty se the, unhone 'Vikramaditya' ki title li aur gold coins issue karne\nshuru kiye. [Q63]\n16. The Kalachuri Dynasty\n● Arab writer-geographer Al-Biruni ne Kalachuri ruler Gangeyadeva aur unki capital Tripuri ka description\ndiya hai — Al-Biruni ek Khwarazmian Iranian scholar the, unhone Indian culture par 'Tarikh al-Hind'\nnaam ki treatise likhi. [Q64]\n17. Famous Places & Their Regions"," ● Sahi matched pairs: Khajuraho — Bundelkhand; Shirdi — Maharashtra (Vidarbha NAHI). (Bodhgaya\nBihar mein hai, Baghelkhand mein nahi; Nasik bhi Maharashtra mein hai, alag region ke saath galat\nmatch kiya gaya tha.) [Q65]\n18. 'Gaudavaho' — A Historical Prakrit Epic\n● 'Gaudavaho' ke author Vakpati the — wo Kannauj ke raja Yashovarman ke court poet the. [Q66]\n19. Economic History — The 'Araghatta'\n● 'Araghatta' ek Persian wheel tha — mechanical water-lifting device, jo bullocks/buffaloes/camels se\nchalti thi, zameen ki sinchai (irrigation) ke liye. Iska zikr Panchatantra aur Rajtarangini mein milta hai.\n[Q67]\n20. Kashmir — Sultan Zainul Abidin\n● Sultan Zainul Abidin ko 'Akbar of Kashmir' kaha jaata hai — 1420 AD mein Ali Shah ke bhai Shahi\nKhan, Zain-ul-Abidin naam se Kashmir ki gaddi par baithe. Unhone ~50 saal raj kiya, apni liberal\nreligious policy, learning ke promotion, aur art-architecture mein interest ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q68]\n● Zain-ul-Abidin ka original naam 'Shahi Khan' tha. [Q69]\n21. The Karnata Dynasty of Mithila\n● Karnata dynasty ke founder Nanyadev (1097-1147 AD) the — ek bade warrior, unhone Simraungadh\nmein apni capital banayi aur Mithila region par raj kiya. [Q70]\n● Karnata dynasty ke aakhri raja Harisimha the (1295/1296-1324 AD) — art-literature ke bade protector\nthe, unhone 'Panji system' shuru ki. [Q71]\n22. The Kuruspal Inscription\n● Kuruspal (Bastar district, Chhattisgarh) ke inscriptions mein Nagavamsa ke King Someswardeva\n(Someshwar I) ka zikr hai — Kuruspal stone inscription unke grant ko record karta hai, aur Kuruspal\nTank slab mein unki queen Dharna Mahadevi dwara Lord Shiva (Kamesvara) ko zameen daan karne ka\nzikr hai. [Q72]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Pre-Medieval Period Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0170","t":"02 Indus Valley Civilization","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" INDUS VALLEY CIVILIZATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏺\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Introduction, Nomenclature & Nature of the Civilization\n2. Sources of Knowledge & Theories of Origin\n3. Discovery History — Key Archaeologists & Excavators\n4. Extent, Boundaries & Rivers\n5. Important Match-the-Following Sets (Site / Excavator / River / Finding)\n6. Major Sites — Location & Regional Facts\n7. Site Spotlight — Mohenjodaro\n8. Site Spotlight — Lothal\n9. Site Spotlight — Dholavira\n10. Kalibangan & Banawali — Terracotta Finds\n11. Town Planning, Architecture & Key Features\n12. Economy — Metals, Trade & Agriculture\n13. Pottery, Seals & Art\n14. Religion & Beliefs\n15. Burial Practices\n16. Decline of the Indus Valley Civilization\n17. Comparison with World Civilizations\n1. Introduction, Nomenclature & Nature of the Civilization\n● Human society mainly economy par depend karta hai — jaise-jaise economy badalti hai, samaj bhi usi\nhisaab se badalta hai. [Q1]\n● Harappa ek archaeological site hai jo Indus Valley Civilization se related hai. Sabse pehla evidence\nHarappa se mila tha, isliye ise 'Harappa Civilization' bhi kehte hain. Ye Egypt aur Mesopotamia ke saath\nduniya ki 3 prachin civilizations mein se ek hai. [Q2]\n● IVC ek 'Proto-historic' age ki civilization hai — likhna (script) toh aata tha, lekin wo script abhi tak\ndecipher nahi ho paayi hai. [Q3]\n● IVC ko 'Non-Aryan' isliye kaha jaata hai kyunki ye ek Urban (shehri) civilization thi, jabki Aryan\ncivilization Rural (gramin) thi. [Q4]\n● IVC ko Aryan civilization se pehle isliye maana jaata hai kyunki inki script aur town-planning zyada\ndeveloped thi, aur excavation mein mili pottery bhi ye prove karti hai — IVC ki khaasiyat red pottery with\nblack figures thi, jabki Aryans grey painted pottery use karte the. [Q5]\n● IVC, Vedic culture se kai tarah se alag thi: IVC urban thi (Vedic rural), IVC ki script pictographic (chitra\njaisi) thi, aur IVC logo ko iron ka pata nahi tha jabki Vedic log iron weapons use karte the. [Q6]\n● IVC ek Bronze Age civilization thi — logo ko iron ka pata NAHI tha. Baaki sab sahi hai: advanced\ndrainage system tha, trade-commerce (internal-external dono) advanced thi, aur log Mother Goddess ki\npooja karte the. [Q27]\n2. Sources of Knowledge & Theories of Origin"," ● Harappa mein sabse pehla artefact ek unique stone seal mila tha jisme unicorn aur ek inscription thi.\nAisi hi seals poore region mein mili hain. Script abhi tak decipher nahi hui hai, isliye archaeological\nexcavations hi Harappan culture ke baare mein jaanne ka mukhya source hain. [Q7, Q8]\n● IVC ke logo ke baare mein jaanne ka mukhya source 'Seals' hain — 3000 se zyada seals mili hain jisme\nunki religious beliefs, script, aur jaane-pehchane janwar depict hote hain. Excavation yahan 1921 mein\nshuru hui thi. [Q9]\n● Harappan civilization ki origin ko lekar alag-alag scholars ke views hain: D.H. Gordon aur Mortimer\nWheeler ne kaha civilization ki idea Western Asia se migrate hui; Amalananda Ghosh ne kaha pre-\nHarappan culture hi matured hoke Harappan civilization bani. M. Rafique Mughal ne kaha ki\ndevelopment locally Ravi river (Harappa) ke region mein hi hua tha — unhone 'Mesopotamia se\ninspired' wali purani belief ko REJECT kiya tha (isliye 'Rafique Mughal = Mesopotamia se inspired' wala\nmatch GALAT hai, yehi is question ka answer hai). [Q10]\n3. Discovery History — Key Archaeologists & Excavators\n● Match yaad rakho: Harappa → Daya Ram Sahni (1923-25); Hastinapur → B.B. Lal (1950-52);\nTakshashila → John Marshall (1913-34); Kaushambi → N.G. Majumdar (1936-37). [Q11]\n● Chanhudaro (Mohenjodaro se ~130 km south) ko N.G. Majumdar ne 1931 mein discover kiya tha, aur\nE.J.H. Mackay ne bade paimane par excavate kiya — yahan bead-making factory aur furnace mile hain.\n[Q39]\n● Sir John Marshall, Archaeological Survey of India ke Director-General the (1902-1928). Unhone hi\nDayaram Sahni ko appoint kiya jinhone 1921 mein Harappa excavate kiya, aur Rakhal Das Banerjee ne\n1922 mein Mohenjodaro ke ruins khode. [Q58]\n● IVC ki discovery se juday do Indian archaeologists: Rakhal Das Banerjee (Mohenjodaro, 1922) aur\nDayaram Sahni (Harappa, 1921). [Q59]\n● Sahi match: Harappa → Daya Ram Sahni, Lothal → S.R. Rao, Surkotada → J.P. Joshi. Lekin Dholavira\nko B.K. Thapar ne NAHI, balki R.S. Bisht ne excavate kiya tha. [Q60]\n● Alexander Cunningham (ASI ke head) ne Harappa site 1853 aur 1856 mein visit ki thi — chhote\nexcavation kiye, purani pottery/tools/ek stone seal bhi mila, lekin iski massive civilization ki significance\nko pehchaan NAHI paye. [Q61]\n● 1921 mein Daya Ram Sahni ne Harappa excavate kiya (1926-27 se 1933-34 tak M.S. Vats bhi jude\nthe). Mohenjodaro 1922 mein Rakhal Das Banerjee ne excavate kiya (K.N. Dixit, Ernest Mackay, Aurel\nStein, A.N. Ghosh, J.P. Joshi bhi jude the). V.A. Smith Harappan discovery se JUDE NAHI the — wo ek\nIrish Indologist aur historian the. [Q62]\n● 'Surkotada' (Gujarat ke Kachchh district mein) Jagatpati Joshi (J.P. Joshi) ne discover aur excavate\nkiya. [Q63]\n4. Extent, Boundaries & Rivers\n● Harappa culture ki Eastern boundary: Alamgirpur (Meerut, UP). Western boundary: Sutkagendor\n(Balochistan, Pakistan). Northern boundary: Manda (J&K). Southern boundary: Daimabad\n(Maharashtra). [Q34]"," ● IVC geographically Jhelum river se lekar Hindon river (Yamuna ki tributary, Alamgirpur ke paas) tak\nphaili thi. Rivers involved the: Sindhu (Indus), Chenab, Ravi, Sutlej, Jhelum — Ganga river IVC ka hissa\nNAHI thi. [Q55]\n5. Important Match-the-Following Sets (Site / Excavator / River / Finding)\n● Site–Finding match: Lothal → Dockyard; Kalibangan → Ploughed field; Dholavira → 10-signs wali\nHarappan script inscription; Banawali → Terracotta plough replica. [Q17]\n● Site–Finding match: Harappa → Cemetery R-37; Lothal → Dockyard; Kalibangan → Furrowed land;\nMohenjo-Daro → Dancing Girl Statue. [Q20]\n● Site–River match: Harappa → Ravi; Hastinapur → Ganga; Nagarjuna Konda → Krishna; Paithan →\nGodavari. [Q21]\n● Site–River match: Harappa → Ravi; Kalibangan → Ghaggar; Lothal → Bhogava; Ropar → Sutlej. [Q22]\n● Site–Location match: Manda → Jammu & Kashmir; Daimabad → Maharashtra; Kalibangan →\nRajasthan; Rakhigarhi → Haryana. [Q35]\n● Site–Location match: Balu → Haryana; Manda → Jammu & Kashmir; Padri → Gujarat; Hulas → Uttar\nPradesh. [Q36]\n6. Major Sites — Location & Regional Facts\n● Punjab (Pakistan): Harappa, Ravi river ke kinare. [Q23]\n● Sindh (Pakistan): Mohenjodaro (Larkana dist, Indus river ke right bank par) aur Chanhudaro dono Sindh\nmein hain. Surkotada Gujarat (India) mein hai, Sindh mein NAHI. [Q37, Q38]\n● Rajasthan: Kalibangan (Hanumangarh dist, Haryana mein NAHI — ye ek common trap hai) — yahan\nploughed field ke furrows mile hain. Ise Luigi Pio Tessitory (Italian Indologist) ne discover kiya tha, aur\nA. Ghosh ne 1950-52 mein excavate kiya. [Q18, Q19, Q30]\n● Gujarat: Lothal (Ahmedabad dist, Saragwala village ke paas, Dholka Taluka, Bhogava river ke kinare —\nS.R. Rao ne 1954 mein discover kiya) aur Dholavira (Kutch district) — dono Gujarat mein hain, aur\nLothal hi Gujarat ka main Harappan site hai. Rangpur bhi Gujarat ke Saurashtra region mein hai\n(Arabian sea coast) jaha log Rice, Bajra aur Sorghum ugate the. [Q32, Q41, Q43, Q44, Q45, Q73]\n● Haryana: Rakhigarhi (Hisar dist, Ghaggar river ke kinare) — India ka SABSE BADA Harappan site hai\n(Dholavira 2nd sabse bada hai). Banawali (Fatehabad dist) bhi Ghaggar valley mein hai. Rakhigarhi\nRajasthan mein NAHI, Haryana mein hai. [Q33, Q53, Q54, Q69]\n● Uttar Pradesh: Alamgirpur (Meerut) aur Hulas (Saharanpur) — dono UP mein IVC se related centres\nhain (Kalibangan Rajasthan mein hai aur Lothal Gujarat mein hai, ye dono UP mein NAHI hain). Mandi\n(Muzaffarnagar dist) bhi UP mein hai — yahan 2000 mein villagers ne ek ancient treasure trove khoja\ntha jo late Harappan period ka tha. [Q31, Q80]\n● Patliputra (modern Patna ke paas) IVC se JUDA NAHI hai — Kalibangan, Ropar aur Lothal IVC se\nrelated hain. [Q52]"," ● Sohgaura (Gorakhpur dist, UP, Rapti river ke kinare) ek Harappan site NAHI hai — yahan Mauryan\nperiod ka copper-plate inscription mila hai. Chanhudaro, Kot Diji aur Desalpur — ye teeno Harappan\nsites hain (Chanhudaro & Kot Diji Sindh, Pakistan mein; Desalpur Kachchh, Gujarat mein). [Q16]\n● Harappa Pakistan mein hai (Punjab province, ab Sahiwal dist), Ravi river ke kinare. Kalibangan\nRajasthan mein, Lothal Gujarat mein, aur Alamgirpur UP mein hai. [Q40]\n● Dadheri (Kotla Dadheri) — ek late Harappan site hai, Govindgarh, Fatehgarh Sahib district, Punjab\n(India) mein. Ye apni Painted Grey Ware culture ke liye jaana jaata hai, jo Aryans ke aane se associated\nmaana jaata hai. [Q42]\n7. Site Spotlight — Mohenjodaro\n● 'The Great Bath' — IVC ki ek famous structure — Mohenjodaro (Sindh, Pakistan) mein mila tha. [Q24,\nQ25]\n● Mohenjodaro se ek seal mili hai jisme boat ka model bana hua hai (Lothal se bhi clay model boats mile\nhain). [Q26]\n● Mohenjodaro se hi famous 'humped bull seal' mila hai — yahan se sculptures, seals, pottery, gold-\njewellery bhi mile hain. [Q84]\n8. Site Spotlight — Lothal\n● Lothal IVC ka ekmatra jagah hai jaha se port/dockyard ke concrete evidence mile hain (city ke east side\nmein). [Q46, Q47]\n● Lothal, Gulf of Khambhat ke kinare situated ek important trading port thi — Western Asia ke saath trade\nkarti thi. [Q48]\n● Lothal se hi ek ivory scale (haathi-daant ka scale) mila hai. [Q67]\n9. Site Spotlight — Dholavira\n● Dholavira (Kachchh, Gujarat), India ka 2nd sabse bada Harappan site hai (Rakhigarhi sabse bada hai).\nRock-cut architecture yahi se mili hai — R.S. Bisht aur unki team ne 1992 mein excavate kiya tha. [Q72]\n● Dholavira, baaki Harappan cities se alag hai — ye teen parts (Citadel, Middle Town, Lower Town) mein\nbaata gaya tha, jabki baaki cities generally do parts mein hoti thi. [Q74, Q75]\n● Dholavira apne elaborate water-harvesting system ke liye famous hai — dams aur connected reservoirs\nbanaye gaye the. Ek rock-cut reservoir mila hai jo 79m x 12m aur 7 meter gehra tha. [Q76, Q77]\n10. Kalibangan & Banawali — Terracotta Finds\n●\n Disputed/Debated: Terracotta plough replica ASI ke mutabik Kalibangan (Rajasthan) ke early phase\n⚠️\nse mila hai, lekin Banawali (Fatehabad dist, Haryana) se bhi terracotta plough mila hai — isliye ye\nquestion dono answers (Kalibangan aur Banawali) accept karta hai. [Q50, Q51]"," ● Kalibangan se fire-altars (mud-brick platforms par) mile hain. Ek triangular terracotta cake mili hai jisme\nek taraf horned deity (singhon wala devta) aur dusri taraf ek insaan bakri ko rassi se khinchte hue\ndikhaya gaya hai. [Q90]\n11. Town Planning, Architecture & Key Features\n● Bricks: IVC mein baked aur raw dono tarah ki bricks use hoti thi, ratio generally 4:2:1 tha (Kalibangan se\nornamental bricks aur curved bricks bhi mili hain). Zyadatar ghar one-storey the, lekin kuch do-storey bhi\nthe (staircase evidence mila hai). Roads generally 10 meter chaudi hoti thi. [Q28]\n● Town planning IVC ki unique khaasiyat thi — cities/towns bahut ache se planned the. Harappa aur\nMohenjodaro do major cities the. Kalibangan se ploughed field ka pehla evidence mila, aur Lothal se\nbusiness/industrialization ka evidence mila. [Q29]\n● IVC ki sabse significant features: burnt bricks ka use (Harappa/Mohenjodaro mein bahut zyada), well-\nplanned architecture, aur advanced trade-commerce — isliye is type ke question mein 'more than one\noption sahi hai' waala answer sahi hota hai. [Q49]\n● Wells aur bathrooms ka evidence lagbhag har major city (Mohenjodaro, Kalibangan, Harappa) ke har\nghar mein mila hai — isliye ek specific site batana mushkil/disputed hai, halaki Mohenjodaro is feature\nke liye sabse zyada famous hai. [Q64]\n● Statements check: Harappa, Mohenjodaro, Ropar, Lothal, Kalibangan — IVC ke main sites hain (sahi).\nCities grid-pattern mein design ki gayi thi, drainage system roads ke saath tha jo bade pattharon/bricks\nse covered tha (sahi). Log copper, bronze, gold, silver jaante the, sirf iron nahi jaante the. [Q70]\n12. Economy — Metals, Trade & Agriculture\n● Silver ka sabse purana evidence India mein Harappan culture se milta hai — Mohenjodaro aur Harappa\nse proper use ka evidence mila hai. Ye log Rajasthan ki Zawar aur Ajmer mines se silver lete the. [Q12]\n● Chronological order (jis tarah appear hue): Urban culture/Harappan Civilization (Bronze Age, town-\nplanning ke liye famous) sabse pehle → Iron plough (post-Vedic period, ~1000 B.C.) → Punch-marked\nsilver coins (7th-6th century B.C.) → Gold coins (Indo-Greek rulers, 2nd century B.C.). [Q65]\n● Insaan ne sabse pehla metal Copper use kiya tha (halaki duniya bhar mein iska exact time period alag-\nalag raha hai). [Q66]\n● Harappan sites se gold, silver, copper aur brass ke evidence mile hain — sirf Iron ka evidence NAHI\nmila. India mein Iron Age ki shuruaat later Vedic period (~1000 B.C.) se maani jaati hai. [Q68]\n● Cotton cultivation sabse pehle India mein hui thi (Mohenjodaro excavation se evidence mila) — India se\nye Greece pahunchi jaha ise 'Sindon' kaha jaata tha. India mein cotton cultivation 3000 B.C. mein shuru\nhui, jabki Egypt mein 2500 B.C. mein. [Q81]\n● IVC ek secular civilization maani jaati hai jisme koi ek organized/theocratic religion society par dominant\nnahi thi (sahi). Cotton textiles bhi banaye jaate the — Mohenjodaro se woven cotton ka evidence mila\nhai (sahi). [Q83]\n13. Pottery, Seals & Art"," ● Harappan pottery zyadatar bright ya dark red rang ki hoti thi, achi tarah baked. Painting ke liye red-black\ncolors use hote the (light black, chocolate, ya light red — buff/greenish-buff background par). [Q13]\n● Harappan seals aur terracotta art mein Elephant, Rhinoceros, Tiger, Deer, Sheep jaise janwar depict\nhote the, lekin Cow (gaay) depict NAHI hoti thi. [Q15]\n● Zyadatar Indus seals steatite (ek naram patthar) se bani thi. Pipal tree (peepal ka ped) inn seals par\nbahut baar depict hui hai — isse pata chalta hai ki IVC logo ke liye Pipal ka sacred/important value tha.\n[Q85]\n● Seals par Horse depict NAHI hota — halaki Surkotada se ghode ki haddiyon ka evidence mila hai.\nSabse common figure 'one-horned animal' (unicorn jaisa) tha, iske alawa Buffalo, Tiger, Rhinoceros bhi\nmilte hain. [Q86]\n● Excavation mein Lion (sher) ke hone ka koi evidence NAHI mila — Cow aur Elephant ke evidence mile\nhain, aur Horse ko lekar kuch dispute hai. [Q87]\n●\n Note: BPSC ne officially (B) Horse ko is question ka sahi jawab maana hai — halaki recent\n⚠️\nexcavations mein Surkotada se ghode ki haddiyan mili hain, lekin Horse ka IVC life mein koi major role\nnahi tha, isliye exam ke hisaab se Horse ko 'not known' maana gaya. [Q88]\n14. Religion & Beliefs\n● Idol worship (murti pooja) ki shuruaat Pre-Aryan period (yaani Indus Valley Civilization) mein maani jaati\nhai — Mohenjodaro se mile coins mein God ki seal dikhti hai, jisse lagta hai ki ye log Mother Goddess ki\npooja karte the. [Q14]\n●\n Disputed: IVC ki script abhi tak decipher nahi hui, isliye religion ko lekar sirf speculations hain. Log\n⚠️\nshayad Mother Goddess aur Lord Shiva ki pooja karte the, Yagya/sacrificial rituals bhi karte the\n(Rajasthan-Gujarat sites mein fire-pits mile hain), aur burial rituals se pata chalta hai ki wo Atma/spirit\nmein believe karte the. [Q56]\n● John Marshall ne excavation mein ek figure ko Lord Shiva (ya Rudra) / Pashupati (janwaron ke\nbhagwan) ke roop mein identify kiya tha. 'Pashupati seal' mein ek 3-mukh wale purush God ko yogic\nposture mein baitha hua, janwaron se ghira hua dikhaya gaya hai — isi se historians maante hain ki log\nShiva ki pooja karte the. [Q57]\n● Ab tak excavation mein koi bhi temple ya pooja ki jagah NAHI mili hai. Statues aur seals se pata chalta\nhai ki female deities (Mother Goddess) aur male deities (Shiva/Pashupati) dono ki pooja hoti thi (sahi).\nHorse-drawn chariots use karne ka koi concrete evidence nahi hai — ye feature Aryans se associate\nkiya jaata hai. [Q82]\n15. Burial Practices\n●\n Disputed: Double burial ka evidence Lothal (3 double burials mile hain) ke alawa Kalibangan aur\n⚠️\nRakhigarhi se bhi mila hai — isliye is question ke multiple options sahi maane ja sakte hain. [Q78]\n● Sinauli/Sonauli (Baghpat dist, UP) ke recent excavation mein 125 graves mili hain jo IVC se related hain\n— ye graves North-South direction mein hain aur zyadatar primary human burials hain, kuch ke saath\njanwaron ki haddiyan aur gold/copper ke saman bhi mile hain. [Q79]"," 16. Decline of the Indus Valley Civilization\n● Assertion-Reason: Mohenjodaro aur Harappa aaj 'dead' (extinct) cities hain — ye sahi hai. Inki khoj\nexcavations ke dauran hui thi — ye bhi sahi hai. Lekin excavation mein discover hona hi in shehron ke\nkhatam hone ka reason NAHI hai — asli reason climatic changes, tectonic activities waghera the. Isliye\ndono statements sahi hain lekin Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation NAHI deta. [Q71]\n● IIT Kharagpur ki report ke mutabik, lagatar 900 saal tak kam ya na-ke-barabar baarish (drought) hone ki\nwajah se IVC ka pathan/decline hua tha. [Q89]\n17. Comparison with World Civilizations\n● Egyptian Civilization, Nile river ke kinare ~3000 saal tak phali-phuli. Nile ko Egypt ki 'lifeline' kaha jaata\nhai — ye duniya ki sabse lambi north-flowing river hai. IVC (India) aur Mesopotamia (Iraq) contemporary\n(samkalin) civilizations thi. [Q91]\n● North se South ki taraf civilizations ka sahi order: Aztec → Maya → Muisca → Inca. Aztec North\nMesoamerica (Central Mexico) mein, Maya South Mesoamerica (Belize, Guatemala) mein, Muisca East\nColombia (South America) mein, aur Inca West South America (Ecuador se Santiago tak) mein phali-\nphuli. [Q92]\n● Mesopotamia (Iraq) civilization ko duniya ki sabse purani civilization maana jaata hai — ye Tigris aur\nEuphrates river ke beech develop hui thi. Egyptian civilization Nile basin mein develop hui aur\nMesopotamian civilization ke baad aayi maani jaati hai. [Q93]\n● Sumerian Civilization (Mesopotamia ka hissa) ke log duniya mein sabse pehle proper likhne ki kala\n(writing system) develop karne wale the — unki Cuneiform script duniya ki sabse purani writing systems\nmein se ek maani jaati hai. [Q94]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Indus Valley Civilization Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0171","t":"03 Vedic Age","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" VEDIC AGE — FULL MIND MAP\n📜\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Aryans — Meaning & Origin Theories\n2. The Four Vedas — Overview & Content\n3. Rigveda — Structure, Deities & Key Facts\n4. Brahmana Texts (Each Veda ki Prose Commentary)\n5. Vedic Literature Structure & Upanishads\n6. Vedic Rivers & Geography\n7. Post-Vedic Social Institutions — Ashramas, Purusharthas & Samskaras\n8. Dharma, Rita & Religious Concepts\n9. Society, Economy & Social Classes\n10. Vedic Polity & Administration\n11. Iron Age & Post-Vedic Timeline\n12. Later Sacred Texts — Puranas & Epics\n13. Later Vedic Society — Comparative Overview\n1. The Aryans — Meaning & Origin Theories\n● 'Arya' word classical Sanskrit mein 'nobleman' (sharif/uchch vyakti) ke liye use hota tha. Vedic period ke\nlogo ne isse apne liye ek ethnic label ki tarah use kiya. Scholars maante hain ki 'Aryan' hone ka concept\nreligious, cultural aur linguistic tha, racial NAHI — lekin diye gaye options mein 'superior race' hi closest\nanswer hota hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● Boghaz-Koi inscription (Asia Minor, Turkiye, 14th century BC) important hai kyunki isme 4 Vedic Gods\n— Indra, Varuna, Mitra aur Nasatya — ka naam mila hai. Ye Iran se India ki taraf Aryan logo ke\nmigration ko prove karta hai. [Q47, Q48, Q49]\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne apni book 'The Arctic Home in the Vedas' mein theory di ki Aryans ka original\nhome North Pole (Arctic region) tha — halaki historians is theory ko generally accept nahi karte. [Q50]\n● Avesta (Zoroastrian scripture) aur Rigveda mein similarity hai — Avesta Iran region se related hai, jaha\nZoroastrianism prevalent thi. Indo-Iranian log khud ko 'Aryan' kehte the. [Q103]\n2. The Four Vedas — Overview & Content\n● 4 Vedas hain: Rigveda, Yajurveda, Samaveda, Atharvaveda — inme Rigveda sabse purana aur sabse\nmahatvapurna hai (earliest composition). [Q3, Q4]\n● Rigveda + Yajurveda + Samaveda — inn teeno ko milakar 'Trayi' (Vedatrayi) kaha jaata hai. [Q5]\n● Content match: Atharvaveda → Medicine/spells; Rigveda → God ki hymns/grace; Yajurveda →\nSacrifice process/rituals; Samaveda → Music. Rigveda mein 1028 hymns aur 10552 verses hain.\nSamaveda, Rigveda se hi liye gaye lyrical/melodious hymns ka collection hai. [Q8, Q9, Q21]\n● Magical charms aur spells ka sabse pehla description Atharvaveda mein milta hai. [Q10]\n● Rigveda basically Vedic Sanskrit hymns ka ek collection hai — hazaro hymns hain, har ek mein average\n10 verses. [Q12]"," ● Yajna se related rights aur rituals Yajurveda mein describe kiye gaye hain — ye Rigveda ke ek-do\ncentury baad compile hua tha, aur isme priests ke liye prose+verse formula diye gaye hain. [Q20]\n● Ayurveda ('Science of Life') sabse pehle Atharvaveda mein appear hua — Ayurveda ko Atharvaveda ka\nek Upaveda maana jaata hai. [Q71]\n3. Rigveda — Structure, Deities & Key Facts\n● Varna word sabse pehle Rigveda mein refer hua hai — 10th Mandala ke 'Purusha Sukta' hymn mein\nBrahmin, Kshatriya, Vaishya aur Shudra Varna ka zikr hai. Varna ka literal meaning 'colour/class' hota\nhai. [Q6, Q7]\n●\n Disputed: Rigveda mein 1028 hymns (Suktas) aur 10552 verses (mantras) hain. Kuch questions\n⚠️\n'mantras' poochte hain lekin options 'hymns' (1028) ke hisaab se diye hote hain — dhyan se dekho\nquestion kya maang raha hai. [Q11]\n● Rigveda ka 9th Mandala (114 hymns) poori tarah Soma devta ko samarpit hai. Rigveda total 10\nMandals mein bata hua hai. [Q18, Q19]\n● 'Gotra' word sabse pehle Rigveda mein appear hua tha — originally iska matlab 'cow shelter/gaayo ka\njhund' tha; 'family lineage' wala meaning baad mein (post-Vedic period) aaya. [Q54]\n● Indra sabse popular Rigvedic devta the — sabse zyada hymns (250) unhi ko samarpit hain (Agni doosre\nnumber par, 200 hymns ke saath). Indra ko War-God/Storm-God/Sky-God kaha jaata tha, jo Vajra\n(thunderbolt) se dushmano ke kile (Purandar) todte the. [Q73, Q74, Q75, Q78, Q79]\n●\n Exam Trap: Agar options mein Indra na ho, to sabse zyada hymns wale devta ke liye Agni (200\n⚠️\nhymns) sahi answer banta hai — kyunki actual mein sabse zyada hymns Indra ko hi mile hain (250).\n[Q76]\n● Statement check on Indra: Vedas mein Indra ko heaven, lightning, thunder aur rain ka God maana gaya\nhai (sahi). Moral order/Rita ke guardian Lord Varuna the, Indra nahi (isliye 'Indra guardian of Rita' wala\nstatement galat hai). [Q77]\n● Gayatri Mantra Rigveda (3rd Mandala) mein milta hai — ise Sage/Rishi Vishwamitra ne compose kiya\ntha. Iska matlab hai: 'Almighty humari buddhi ko roshan kare taaki hum sahi raste par chal sakein.' [Q81,\nQ82, Q83]\n● Rigveda ka basic/fundamental script (jab likha gaya) Brahmi tha. [Q101]\n● Vedic rituals mein 'Hota' (ya Hotri) wo priest hote the jo Rigveda ke hymns recite karte the sacrifices ke\ndauran. [Q102]\n4. Brahmana Texts (Each Veda ki Prose Commentary)\n● Match yaad rakho: Rigveda → Aitareya Brahmana (aur Kaushitaki Brahmana); Samaveda →\nPanchvisha Brahmana; Atharvaveda → Gopatha Brahmana (ye Atharvaveda ka EKMATRA Brahmana\nhai); Yajurveda → Shatpatha Brahmana aur Taittiriya Brahmana. [Q13, Q14, Q16]\n● Yajurveda ki Brahmana texts: Taittiriya aur Shatpatha. [Q15]\n● Yajurveda ki 2 branches hain — Shukla Yajurveda aur Krishna Yajurveda. Vajasneyi (Vajasanami)\nShukla Yajurveda ki Samhita hai. Shukla Yajurveda sirf poetic form mein hai, jabki Krishna Yajurveda\nmein poetic + prose dono form hain. [Q17]"," 5. Vedic Literature Structure & Upanishads\n● Vedic literature ka sahi chronological order: Samhitas → Brahmanas → Aranyakas → Upanishads.\nSamhitas+Brahmanas ko 'Karma-Kanda' kehte hain, aur Aranyakas+Upanishads ko 'Gyan-Kanda' (jo\nphilosophy par focus karta hai). [Q30]\n● Upanishads ek philosophy grantha hai (koi religious scripture nahi) — Upanishad ka matlab hi hai\n'shishya guru ke paas baithkar secret knowledge seekhe.' Moksha (salvation/liberation) ka concept\nsabse pehle Upanishads mein discuss hua — Vedas mein ye word use nahi hua tha. [Q24, Q25, Q26]\n● Nachiketa (12 saal ka ladka) aur Yama (mrityu ke devta) ke beech ka famous dialogue Kathopanishad\nmein mila hai. [Q27, Q28]\n● Upanishadic period ke King Asvapati, Kekaya kingdom (Beas river ke kinare, Gandhara ke east mein)\nke raja the — aise hi Videha ke King Janak aur Kashi ke King Ajatshatru bhi great scholar-kings the jo\nBrahmins ko gyan dete the. [Q29]\n● 'Satyameva Jayate' (sirf sach ki jeet hoti hai) Mundakopanishad se liya gaya hai — ise 26 January 1950\nko India ka national motto banaya gaya, aur National Emblem ke base par likha hai. [Q94, Q95, Q96]\n● 'Tamsoma Jyotirgamaya' (andhkaar se prakash ki taraf le chalo) statement Brihadaranyaka Upanishad\nmein mila hai. [Q97]\n● Sage Yagnavalkya aur female philosopher Gargi Vachaknavi ke beech ka famous dialogue\nBrihadaranyaka Upanishad mein mila hai. [Q98]\n● Shvetashvatara Upanishad ka literal meaning hai 'safed ghode par sawaar' (Shveta=safed,\nAshva=ghoda) — diye gaye options mein iske liye koi sahi match nahi hai (isliye 'None of these' sahi\nanswer hai). [Q99]\n● Satyakama Jabala ki legend — ek ladka jo apne guru ko honestly bata deta hai ki use apne pita ka\nnaam nahi pata kyunki uski maa Jabala unmarried thi — Chhandogya Upanishad mein milti hai. [Q100]\n6. Vedic Rivers & Geography\n● Sindhu river early Vedic literature mein sabse zyada mention hui hai — economic importance ki wajah\nse ise 'Hiranyayi' bhi kaha jaata tha; ye Arabian Sea mein jaake khatam hoti hai. [Q31]\n● Vedic river Askini aaj ke Chenab river se identify ki jaati hai (Chandrabhaga bhi kehte hain) — ye\nChandra aur Bhaga naam ki do dhaaraon ke milne se Tandi (Lahul Spiti) mein banti hai. [Q32]\n● Rigveda mein mention hui Kubha (Kabul), Krumu (Kurram), Gomati (Gomal) aur Suvastu (Swat) rivers\nAfghanistan se hoke behti thi — ye Aryans ke Afghanistan ke saath relations dikhati hain. [Q33, Q34]\n● River match: Kubha → Kabul; Parushni → Ravi; Sadaneera → Gandak; Shutudri → Sutlej. [Q35]\n● Mahabharata period mein Mahanadi ka naam 'Chitrotpala' tha (Bhishma Parv mein ise Punayadayini\naur Paap-Nashini kaha gaya hai). Lekin Vayu Puran ke hisaab se Mahanadi ka mythological naam\n'Nilotapala' tha (Matsya Puran mein ise Chitrotpala kaha gaya hai). [Q36, Q37]\n● Famous 'Battle of Ten Kings' (Dasharajnya) Parushni river (aaj ki Ravi) ke kinare lada gaya tha —\nBharata king Sudas ne 10 raja ki confederacy ko haraya tha. [Q57, Q58]"," ● Saraswati river ko Rigvedic period ki sabse pavitra/respected river maana jaata tha — ise 'Matetama'\n(sabse acchi maa), 'Devitama' (sabse acchi devi) aur 'Naditama' (sabse acchi nadi) kaha jaata tha. [Q59]\n7. Post-Vedic Social Institutions — Ashramas, Purusharthas & Samskaras\n● Post-Vedic period mein 2 important concepts emerge hue: 4 Ashramas (Brahmacharya, Grihastha,\nVanaprastha, Sanyasa) aur 4 Purusharthas (Dharma, Artha, Kama, Moksha). [Q38]\n● Grihastha Ashram (householder stage) mein rehte hue insaan ko 'Pancha Mahayajna' (5 bade yajna)\nkarne hote the: Brahma Yajna, Deva Yajna, Pitra Yajna, Bhuta Yajna, Atithi Yajna. Ye ashram society ki\nfoundation maana jaata tha kyunki isi stage mein dhan kamaya jaata tha jo baaki 3 ashramas ko support\nkarta tha. [Q39]\n● Untouchability ka concept clearly Dharmashastra phase (early Christian era) mein define hua — is\nperiod mein Brahmanical religion dominant thi aur strict social customs follow hote the. [Q93]\n● Vansha, Gotra, Kula — ye teeno family/lineage system se related terms hain. Lekin 'Kosa' inn mein se\nNAHI hai — Kosa ka matlab hota hai treasury/dhan-sampatti. [Q110]\n● Hindu tradition mein total 16 (solah) Sanskaras describe kiye gaye hain (Shodasha Samskaras) — 3\njanm se pehle, 12 zindagi ke dauran, aur 1 maut ke baad hota hai. [Q111]\n● Kshatriya caste ke Upanayana ritual (sacred thread ceremony) mein 'Trishtubh Mantra' recite karne ka\npravdhan tha — ye mantra Kshatriyo ke martial/veergatha (warrior) qualities ko symbolize karta tha.\n[Q84]\n● Jo teacher apni jeevika (livelihood) ke liye Veda-Vedanga sikhata tha, use 'Upadhyaya' kaha jaata tha\n— wo sirf Veda ya Vedanga ka ek hissa sikhata tha. [Q112]\n8. Dharma, Rita & Religious Concepts\n● 'Dharma' aur 'Rita' Vedic civilization ke central ideas hain, jo Rigveda jitne purane hain. Dharma ka\nmatlab cosmic ordinance/divine law hai (duty-obligations se related). Rita ka matlab hai universal\nharmony/natural law — ek impersonal moral law jisme har cheez ki apni jagah aur function hoti hai.\n[Q40, Q41]\n● Brihaspati (Deva-guru) ko Devon (Gods) ka priest/guru maana jaata tha. [Q42]\n● Early Vedic Aryans ka religion mainly nature-worship aur yajna (sacrifice) perform karne se related tha\n— life ko nature ka manifestation maana jaata tha. Rigvedic period mein log mainly Sacrifice (Yajna) aur\nrituals mein believe karte the — domestic sacrifice common tha, aur kings community-level bade\nsacrifices karte the. [Q55, Q56]\n● Rig-vedic religion Polytheistic (kai devi-devta) thi — Indra, Agni, Varuna, Surya jaise bahut se Gods ki\npooja hoti thi. Aryans nature ko ek animated soul ke roop mein dekhte the. [Q72]\n9. Society, Economy & Social Classes\n● Rigveda ke kai hymns women ne compose kiye the, jinhe 'Brahmavadini' kaha jaata tha — inme\nprominent thi Lopamudra (jo Agastya Rishi ki patni thi), Vishwawara, Sikta, Nivavari, Ghosa. [Q43]"," ● 'Nishka' Rigvedic period mein ek gold gale ka ornament (Nishka-Griva) tha, lekin baad mein ye word\ngold coins (exchange ke medium) ke liye use hone laga. [Q44, Q45, Q46]\n● 'Panchjana' Rigvedic Aryans ke 5 tribes the: Yadu, Turvasu, Druhyu, Anu aur Puru. Kikat ek non-Aryan\ntribe tha jo Panchjana mein SHAAMIL NAHI tha. [Q60]\n● Ancient/Later Vedic period mein Aryans ki mukhya livelihood Agriculture (aur pastoralism) thi. [Q61]\n● Rigveda mein 'Yava' word Barley (anaj) ke liye use hota tha. Agricultural terms match: Vrihi → Rice;\nMudga → Mung bean; Yava → Barley; Ikshu → Sugarcane. [Q62, Q63]\n● 'Pani' Rigvedic period ke ameer traders (vyapari) ki ek class thi, jo sacrifices perform nahi karte the.\n[Q64]\n● 'Aghanya' (jise maara na jaaye) Rigveda mein Cow (gaay) ke liye use hota tha — ye dikhata hai ki gaay\nko Vedic period mein kitna pavitra maana jaata tha. [Q104, Q105, Q106]\n● Rigvedic Aryans aur Indus Valley logo mein antar: Rigveda mein gold-iron ka coat-of-mail/helmet ka zikr\nhai jabki IVC log weapons mein kamzor the (sahi). IVC log gold-silver-copper-bronze jaante the lekin\niron NAHI (galat statement — ye is baare mein nahi ki Rigvedic Aryans bhi copper-bronze hi jaante the).\nHorses ka evidence IVC mein bhi mila hai (Surkotada, Lothal), isliye 'IVC mein ghode ka koi evidence\nnahi' — ye claim bhi galat hai. [Q107]\n● Early Rigvedic period mein Cow ko sabse valuable property maana jaata tha — cattle-breeding sabse\nmahatvapurna economic activity thi, aur cow hi exchange ka medium bhi thi. [Q108]\n10. Vedic Polity & Administration\n● Vedic era mein governance ka sabse prevalent system 'Descended monarchy' (hereditary/vanshanugat\nrajtantra) tha — kabhi-kabhi logo dwara election bhi hota tha, lekin general norm Rajan (raja) wala\nmonarchy tha. [Q65]\n● 'Sabha', raja ki autocracy par control rakhne wali ek institution thi — ye elite/vidwaan logo ki ek council\n(jaise mantri parishad) thi, jabki 'Samiti' aam logo ki assembly hoti thi. [Q66]\n● Atharvaveda mein Sabha aur Samiti ko Prajapati (srishti karta) ki 2 betiyan (daughters) kaha gaya hai\n— Atharvaveda hi ek aisa Veda hai jisme inhe 2 alag institutions ke roop mein clearly declare kiya gaya\nhai. [Q67, Q68]\n● Rigveda ki tribal assemblies mein Sabha, Samiti, Vidatha ka zikr milta hai — inme se 'Sabha' judicial\nfunctions (nyay) se associated thi, ek court ki tarah kaam karti thi. [Q69]\n● 'Bhagadugha' Vedic administration mein Revenue Collector (mahsul/kar vasooli wala officer) hota tha.\n[Q70]\n11. Iron Age & Post-Vedic Timeline\n● India mein iron use hone ka sabse purana evidence Atranjikhera (Kali river ke kinare, Etah dist, UP) se\nmila hai — ~1000 BC ke aas-paas ka. [Q22]\n● Indian subcontinent mein iron ka use approximately 1300-1200 BC (kuch tribal artisans dwara) se lekar\n~1000 BC (jab widely accepted hua) tak shuru hua — exact ek fixed date nahi hai isliye 'None of the\nabove' sahi answer hai. [Q23]"," ● Post-Vedic period mein Kuru-Panchala region ko Aryan culture ka 'axis' (kendra) maana jaata tha —\nkyunki yahan science, maths, astronomy, religion aur philosophy mein bade achievements hue the.\n[Q53]\n● 800 BC se 600 BC ka period 'Brahmin era' se related maana jaata hai (Brahmana texts compose hone\nka period). 7th/6th century BC se 3rd century BC tak ka period 'Sutra Period' kehlata hai. [Q80]\n12. Later Sacred Texts — Puranas & Epics\n●\n Disputed: 'Purusha Medha' (human sacrifice) ka zikr Shatpatha Brahmana (Shukla Yajurveda) aur\n⚠️\nTaittiriya Brahmana (Krishna Yajurveda) — dono mein milta hai, isliye ek single sahi answer nahi hai\n(halaki historians zyada tar Shatpatha Brahmana ko emphasize karte hain). [Q51]\n● Shatpatha Brahmana mein King Videgha Madhava (Videha ke raja) ki kahani hai, jinke saath unke\npriest Rishi Gautama Rahugana the — dono ne pavitra agni ko poorab ki taraf le jaaya, jisse Kosala aur\nVideha logo ki cultural tradition preserve hui. [Q52]\n● Puranas ki 5 characteristics (Panchalakshana) hoti hain: Sarga, Pratisarga, Vansa, Manvantara, aur\nVanshanucharita. [Q85]\n● Total 18 Mahapuranas hain — inme se Srimad Bhagvatam ko sabse important/'Crown Jewel' Vedic\nliterature maana jaata hai. [Q86]\n● Upanishads mein kai parables/kahaniyan hain (isliye 'Upanishads mein koi parable nahi' galat statement\nhai) — Upanishads Later Vedic period mein compose hue the, jabki Puranas bahut baad mein\n(Common Era ki early centuries se) likhe gaye. [Q87]\n● Puranas historical information bhi deti hain: Vishnu Purana mein Mauryan Dynasty ka account hai, Vayu\nPurana Gupta Dynasty ke governance ke baare mein batata hai, aur Matsya Purana Andhra-\nSatavahana Dynasty se related hai. [Q88]\n● Shrimad Bhagavad Gita originally Sanskrit mein likhi gayi thi — isme 700 verses hain, aur ye\nMahabharata (Bhishma Parva) ka hi ek hissa hai. [Q89]\n● Mahabharata ka original naam 'Jaya' ya 'Jayasamhita' tha, aur usme sirf 8,800 shlokas the. Aaj\nMahabharata mein 100,000 shlokas hain (Sage Veda Vyasa ne compile kiya) — isi wajah se ise\n'Shatasahasri-Samhita' (1 lakh verses ka sangrah) bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q90, Q91]\n● Samudra Manthan (ocean churning) mein Mount Mandara ko rod ki tarah use kiya gaya, aur Vasuki\n(naago ka raja/serpent) rassi ki tarah use hua. Vishnu ne Kurma Avatar (kachhua) leke mountain ko\napni peeth par support kiya tha. [Q92]\n13. Later Vedic Society — Comparative Overview\n● Society-type match: Indus Valley Civilization → Urban; Later Vedic Society → Agrarian (kheti-pradhan);\nRigvedic Society → Pastoral (pashupalan-pradhan); Medieval Period → Land Lordism (zameendari-\nvyavastha). [Q109]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vedic Age Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0172","t":"04 Buddhism","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" BUDDHISM — FULL MIND MAP\n☸️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Buddha's Life — Birth, Family, Early Years & Epithets\n2. The Four Sacred Sites — Birth, Enlightenment, First Sermon & Death\n3. Buddha's Travels, Last Days & Associated Places\n4. Buddhist Councils — History & Key Facts\n5. Sangha — Monks, Disciples & Monastic Life\n6. Buddhist Texts & Scriptures\n7. Core Buddhist Philosophy & Teachings\n8. Hinayana, Mahayana, Vajrayana & Buddhist Sects\n9. Stupas, Chaityas, Viharas & Buddhist Architecture\n10. Buddhist Art & Iconography\n11. Great Centres of Buddhist Learning\n12. Buddhist Philosophers & Missionaries\n13. Buddhism vs Jainism — What's Common, What's Not\n14. Social Aspects, Spread, Patronage & Decline of Buddhism\n1. Buddha's Life — Birth, Family, Early Years & Epithets\n● Gautama Buddha (bachpan ka naam Siddhartha) ka janm 563 BC mein Shakya Kshatriya family mein\nhua tha, Lumbini (Kapilvastu ke pass, Nepal) mein. Pita Shuddhodana Shakya clan ke chief the, aur\nmaa Mayadevi Koliya clan se thi. [Q1, Q3]\n● 29 saal ki age mein Buddha apne ghar se nikal gaye the (apne ghode 'Kanthaka' par, Channa ke saath)\n— is ghatna ko 'Mahabhinishkramana' (Great Departure) kaha jaata hai. [Q2]\n●\n Disputed: Buddha ke doosre naam wale question mein diye gaye options (Parth, Gudakesh, Mihir,\n⚠️\nPrachhanna) mein se koi bhi Buddha ka actual naam nahi hai (Parth/Gudakesh Arjuna ke naam hain) —\nisliye 'None of these' sahi jawab hai, halaki Chhattisgarh PSC ne apni official key mein galti se ek option\nko sahi maan liya tha. [Q5]\n● Alara Kalama ek famous religious teacher the (Samkhya philosophy ke Acharya) jinke paas Buddha ne\nmeditation waghera seekha tha, ghar chhodne ke baad. [Q20]\n● Buddha ke jeevan ke baare mein sahi statements: unka janm Lumbini (Kapilvastu ke pass) mein hua,\nunhone Karma ke siddhant mein vishwas kiya, unhe Bodh Gaya mein enlightenment mili, unhone\nVedas/Vedic rituals ko chhod diya, aur unhone 4 Arya Satya (Noble Truths) diye. [Q53]\n● Gautama Buddha ko 'Light of Asia' (Asia ki Roshni) bhi kaha jaata hai — Edwin Arnold ne unki life par\n'The Light of Asia' naam ki book likhi thi, jo 'Lalitvistara' text par based hai. [Q84, Q85, Q90]\n● Buddha ke epithets/upadhiyan: 'Shakyamuni' (Shakya clan ke sage) aur 'Tathagata' (jo enlightenment\nke baad khud ko refer karne ke liye use karte the) — lekin 'Nayaputta' Buddha ka naam NAHI hai, ye\nMahavira (Jainism ke 24th Tirthankara) ke liye use hota hai. [Q86]\n2. The Four Sacred Sites — Birth, Enlightenment, First Sermon & Death\n● Buddha Lumbini mein paida hue the — Ashoka ke Rummindei Pillar Inscription se ye confirm hota hai.\nIs inscription ke mutabik Ashoka apni coronation ke 20th saal ke baad Lumbini aaye the aur usi jagah ki"," pooja ki jaha Shakyamuni paida hue the — unhone Lumbini ko Bali tax se bhi mukt kar diya tha. [Q4, Q6,\nQ7, Q8]\n● Buddha ne Mahaparinirvana (mrityu) Kushinagar mein prapt ki thi, jo Malla Republic ki rajdhani thi. Isse\n'Kusinara' bhi kaha jaata hai. Mahaparinirvana Temple aaj UP ke Kushinagar district mein hai — yaha ki\nfamous Buddha statue 1876-77 mein excavation ke dauran mili thi (Chunar sandstone se bani, dying\nBuddha ki reclining posture mein). [Q9, Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13]\n● Buddha ko Bodh Gaya mein, ek Pipal tree ke neeche, enlightenment mili thi. [Q19]\n● Buddha ne apna pehla sermon ('Dhammachakkhapavathana' ya 'Dharmachakra Parvartana') Sarnath\nmein diya tha — enlightenment ke baad, Bodhgaya se Sarnath jaake. [Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26]\n● 4 Events–4 Places match: Janm → Lumbini; Enlightenment → Bodh Gaya; Pehla Sermon → Sarnath\n(Dharmachakrapravartana); Mrityu → Kushinagar (Mahaparinirvana). [Q49]\n● Indian art mein 'wheel with deer' (chakra + hiran) ka symbol Buddha ke pehle sermon (first preaching)\nko represent karta hai — Buddha ne apna pehla upadesh Sarnath ke Mrigadava (Deer Park) mein diya\ntha. [Q50]\n● Symbols match: Janm → Lotus; Pehla Sermon → Dharma Chakra Pravartana; Enlightenment → Bodhi\nTree; Mahabhinishkramana (Great Departure) → Horse. [Q51]\n● Mahabodhi Temple Bodh Gaya mein usi jagah bana hai jaha Gautama Buddha ne 35 saal ki age mein,\n6 saal ki khoj ke baad, enlightenment prapt ki thi. [Q54]\n● Bodh Gaya ka 'Bodhi Vriksha' (jis ped ke neeche Buddha ko gyan mila) apni family ka 5th generation\ntree hai — Hiuen Tsang ke mutabik original tree ko 7th century mein King Shashank ne destroy kar diya\ntha; present wala tree Alexander Cunningham ke orders par lagaya gaya tha. [Q55]\n● Bodhgaya, Niranjana (Phalgu) river ke kinare situated hai. [Q56]\n● Pairs check: Lothal (Gujarat) → Ancient dockyard (sahi); Sarnath → Buddha ka pehla sermon (sahi);\nNalanda → Buddhist learning ka bada centre (sahi). Lekin Lion Capital of Ashoka Sarnath mein hai,\nRajgir mein NAHI — Rajgir apne hot-water springs ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q104]\n● Assertion-Reason: Kushinagar Malla Republic ki rajdhani thi (sahi), aur Buddha ka Mahaparinirvana bhi\nwahi hua tha (sahi) — lekin Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation nahi deta (Buddha ka wahan marna\nhi capital hone ki wajah nahi hai). [Q103]\n3. Buddha's Travels, Last Days & Associated Places\n● Buddha directly Kosala aur Magadha kingdoms se associated the (Avanti aur Gandhara se nahi) —\nunhone apni teachings phailane ke liye ye do kingdoms bahut visit ki. [Q14]\n● Buddha ke jeevan ke aakhri saalon mein, unke disciple Chund (Pava mein) ne unhe 'Sukaramaddava'\nkhilaya jisse unhe food poisoning hui. Ismein last enlightened/converted vyakti 'Subhadda' the, jinhe\nBuddha ne Kushinagar mein apna last sermon diya, aur wahi Mahaparinirvana bhi hui. [Q15, Q16]\n● Buddha ne apni zindagi ka aakhri rainy season Vaishali (Beluva suburb) mein bitaya tha, apne 2\ndisciples ke saath. [Q17]\n● Buddha ne sabse zyada sermons Shravasti mein diye the (Koshala ki rajdhani) — unke zyadatar\ndisciples Koshala region se hi the. [Q27]"," ● Buddha ne Kaushambi ko King Udayana ke reign mein visit kiya tha — Pindola Bharadwaj ke prabhaav\nmein Udayana Buddhism ki taraf mud gaye the, aur unhone Ghoshitram Vihar Bhikshu Sangh ko daan\ndiya tha. [Q28]\n● 80 feet ki Giant Buddha Statue (Bodhgaya) Japan ke Daijokyo sect ki madad se bani thi — 7 saal mein\ncomplete hui, sandstone blocks aur red granite se, dhyana mudra mein. [Q76]\n4. Buddhist Councils — History & Key Facts\n● Pehla Buddhist Council, Buddha ke Mahaparinirvana ke turant baad, King Ajatashatru ke patronage\nmein, Rajagriha (Rajgir) ki Saptaparni Cave mein hua tha — is council ki presidency Mahakashyapa ne\nki thi. [Q29, Q30, Q31, Q32, Q33, Q34, Q45, Q46]\n● Dusra Buddhist Council Vaishali mein, King Kalasoka (Shishunaga dynasty) ke reign mein hua tha\n(Buddha ki mrityu ke ~100 saal baad). [Q43, Q47]\n● Teesra Buddhist Council Pataliputra mein, Mauryan Emperor Ashoka ke reign mein hua tha. [Q44]\n● Chautha (4th) Buddhist Council Kanishka ke reign mein, Kundalavana (Kashmir) mein hua tha — iski\npresidency Vasumitra ne ki (Ashvaghosha bhi jude the). Isi council mein Buddhism formally 2 sects —\nMahayana aur Hinayana — mein baat gaya tha. [Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q39, Q40]\n● 4 councils ka chronological order: 1st (Rajgriha, Ajatashatru ke time) → 2nd (Vaishali, Kalasoka ke time)\n→ 4th (Kashmir, Kanishka ke time) → 3rd (Pataliputra, Ashoka ke time) — wait dhyan se: sahi order hai\n1st→2nd→3rd→4th, yaani Rajgriha→Vaishali→Pataliputra→Kashmir. [Q42]\n● Councils-Presidents match: 1st Council → Mahakashyapa; 2nd Council → Sabakami; 3rd Council →\nMoggaliputta Tissa; 4th Council → Vasumitra. [Q48]\n5. Sangha — Monks, Disciples & Monastic Life\n● Devadatta (Buddha ke cousin) Buddha ke zinda rehte hi Sangha ka leader banna chahte the — lekin\nsafal nahi hue. [Q58]\n● Buddha ne apni mrityu ke baad Sangha ke liye koi successor nominate NAHI kiya tha — unhone apne\nfollowers ko khud mukti (liberation) ki taraf kaam karne ko kaha. [Q59]\n● Buddha ne apne disciple Ananda ki request par, Vaishali mein, women ko 'Bhikshuni' ban kar Sangha\nmein aane ki anumati di thi — pehli Bhikshuni Mahaprajapati Gautami (Buddha ki paalak-maa) thi. [Q63]\n● 'Pavarana' ek ceremony thi jo rainy season (jab monks Bauddha Mahavihar mein rehte the aur\npreaching rok dete the) khatam hone ke baad hoti thi — isme monks apni galtiyon (offences) ki\nconfession karte the aur future plans discuss karte the. [Q73]\n● Buddhist terms: 'Parivrajaka' ka matlab hai male wanderer/renunciant (Bhikkhu isi tarah ke hote hain);\n'Upasaka' Buddhism ke lay followers (jo monk nahi hote) hote hain; lekin 'Shramana' sirf Buddhism tak\nlimited nahi, Jainism aur Ajivikism mein bhi wandering monks ko is naam se jaana jaata hai. [Q101]\n6. Buddhist Texts & Scriptures"," ● 'Tripitaka' Buddhism ki sabse mahatvapurna sacred books hain (Buddha ki teachings ka collection) —\nye 3 hisso mein bata hai: Sutta Pitaka (Buddha ke sermons/teachings), Vinaya Pitaka (Sangha ke\nrules), aur Abhidhamma Pitaka (philosophical exposition). [Q64, Q65, Q66, Q67]\n● Vinaya Pitaka mein Sangha/monks ki monastic life ke rules diye gaye hain. [Q68]\n● 'Yamaka' Abhidhamma Pitaka ka ek hissa hai (jisme total 7 books hain: Yamaka, Patthana,\nKathavatthu, Puggalapannatti, Dhatukatha, waghera). [Q69]\n● Sutta Pitaka mein Buddha ke ethics/moral principles wale sermons hain — iska ek hissa 'Digha Nikaya'\n34 lambi Suttas ka collection hai. [Q70]\n● 'Triratna' (3 ratna) ka matlab hai Buddha, Dhamma aur Sangha. [Q71]\n● 'Visuddhimagga' (Theravada Abhidhamma par treatise) Buddhaghosa ne likhi thi. [Q114]\n● Sanskrit mein likhe gaye Buddhist texts: Divyavadana aur Aryamanjushree Mulakalpa. Deepvamsa aur\nMahavamsa (Sri Lanka/India history) Pali mein likhe gaye the. [Q115]\n● Sanghabhuti (Indian Buddhist monk, 4th century AD ke end mein China gaye) ne Sarvastivada Vinaya\npar ek commentary likhi thi. [Q145]\n7. Core Buddhist Philosophy & Teachings\n● Nirvana ka concept hai 'desire ki flame ka bujhna' — Buddhism m\n\nानताhai desire hi sab dukh (pain) ka\nreason hai, aur Nirvana ek aisi state hai jo desire, dukh, sukh sab se free hoti hai. [Q18]\n● Buddha ki teachings mainly conduct ki purity/pavitrata par based thi. [Q57]\n● 'Eightfold Path' (Ashtangik Marg) ka concept 'Dharma Chakra Pravartana Sutta' ka central theme hai —\nBuddha ne isse zindagi ke dukho se mukti (Nirvana) paane ke liye diya tha. [Q60]\n● Buddhist philosophy (Pratityasamutpada) ke mutabik Samskar (impression/mental formation) ka mool\nkaran Avidya (ignorance/ajnaan) hai — sab dukh ki jad ignorance hi hai. [Q61]\n● Buddha Karma aur Rebirth mein vishwas karte the (Jataka tales mein unke poorvajanm darj hain), lekin\nunhone God ke astitva ko nahi maana. [Q62]\n● Buddhist philosophy ki jad Gautama Buddha ki teachings mein hai — unhone philosophical debates se\nzyada moral life aur suffering se mukti par zor diya; baad ke scholars ne isi base par gehri philosophy\ndevelop ki. [Q72]\n● 'Anatmavada' (no-self doctrine — koi permanent soul/atma nahi hota) Buddhism ka core siddhant hai, jo\nPratityasamutpada se nikalta hai. [Q82]\n● 'Duniya unstable aur transient (kshanbhangur) hai' — ye 'Anitya' (impermanence) ka concept hai, jo\nBuddhism ke 3 core marks of existence mein se ek hai. [Q83]\n● 'Doctrine of Momentariness' (Kshanikavada — sab kuch pal-pal badalta rehta hai) Buddha ne hi\npropound kiya tha, jo Anitya ke principle ko explain karta hai. [Q88]\n● 4 Noble Truths (Arya Satya) ka sahi order hai: (1) Dukh hai → (2) Dukh ka karan hai → (3) Dukh ka ant\npossible hai → (4) Dukh khatam karne ka ek raasta hai. [Q131]\n● Assertion-Reason: Buddhism ne Rebirth ke concept ko REJECT nahi kiya (Assertion GALAT hai —\nunhone rebirth accept kiya tha), lekin Soul mortal hai (Reason SAHI hai — Buddhism Anatmavada\nmaanta hai, permanent soul nahi hota). [Q133]"," 8. Hinayana, Mahayana, Vajrayana & Buddhist Sects\n● Mahayana Buddhism believe karta hai: Buddha ki deification (unhe God ki tarah pooja), Bodhisattva\npath follow karna, aur idol worship/rituals. [Q41]\n● Karmapa Lama, Tibetan Buddhism ke Kangyupa (Kagyu) sect se belong karte hain. [Q52]\n● 'Paramitas' (perfections) Bodhisattva path ki taraf le jaane wali qualities hain, jinhe ek Bodhisattva apne\nKarma ko purify karne ke liye perfect karne ki koshish karta hai. [Q89]\n● Hinayana aur Mahayana ke beech fundamental difference: Hinayana Buddha ko ek mahaan insaan\nmaanta hai, jabki Mahayana unhe idol worship ke through God ki tarah pooja karta hai. [Q91]\n● Kanishka ke reign mein hi Gautama Buddha ko God ka darja diya gaya tha — usi 4th council mein\nBuddhism Hinayana-Mahayana mein baata gaya, aur Mahayana ne unki idol pooja shuru ki. [Q92]\n● Mahayana Buddhism mein Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara ko 'Padmapani' (kamal-dhaari) bhi kaha jaata\nhai. [Q105]\n●\n Disputed: 'Aryamanjushrimulakalpa' ek Buddhist tantric text hai jo Mahayana aur Vajrayana dono\n⚠️\nBuddhism se associated hai — isliye single sahi answer clear nahi hai. [Q106]\n● Statement check: Sthaviravadi sect Hinayana se belong karta hai (Mahayana se nahi). Lokottaravadin,\nMahasanghika sect ki ek shaakha thi. Mahasanghikas dwara Buddha ki deification ne Mahayana\nBuddhism ko badhava diya. [Q107]\n● Maitreya ek future Buddha hain, jo abhi tak duniya ko bachane nahi aaye — unka pehla zikr Pali\nTripitika ki 'Cakkavatti Sutta' mein milta hai. [Q108]\n● Bodhisattva ka concept Mahayana Buddhism ka goal/ideal hai (Hinayana ka nahi) — Mahayana\nBuddhists sirf khud ke liye nahi, doosro ki mukti ke liye bhi (compassion se) enlightenment chahte hain.\n[Q109]\n● Sautrantika aur Sammitiya, Buddhism ke hi sects the (Jainism ke nahi). 'Sarvastivada' ka matlab hai\n'sab kuch exist karta hai' ka siddhant — iske mutabik past-present-future sab phenomena kisi na kisi\nform mein exist karte hain. [Q137]\n● Sultanate period (medieval India) mein Vajrayana sect sabse prominent tha — iske principles 'Arya\nManjushrimulkalpa' aur 'Guhyasamaja' texts mein milte hain (8th century AD se popular hua). [Q144]\n9. Stupas, Chaityas, Viharas & Buddhist Architecture\n● Ashokaram monastery Pataliputra mein thi — Mahavansh text ke mutabik Ashoka ne ise banwaya tha,\nmonk Indragupta ki supervision mein. [Q74]\n● Duniya ka sabse ooncha Stupa 'Vishwa Shanti Stupa' (World Peace Pagoda, 400 meter height) Rajgir\n(Bihar) ki pahadiyo par situated hai. [Q75]\n● 'Stupa' word sabse pehle Rigveda mein use hua tha — usme iska matlab tha 'tree stem/ped ka tana'.\nYe Buddhism se pehle bhi exist karta tha (pre-Buddhist origin). [Q77, Q79]\n● Sanchi Stupa Buddha ke jeevan ki kisi bhi ghatna se directly connected NAHI hai — jabki Bodhgaya\n(enlightenment), Sarnath (Dharma Chakra Pravartana) aur Kushinagar (mrityu) se related stupas hain.\n[Q78]"," ●\n Disputed: Bharhut, Sanchi (Ashoka ke time), Dhamekh (kuch sources ke mutabik Ashoka ke time)\n⚠️\naur Amaravati (Satvahanas ke time) stupas ka exact chronological order clearly decide nahi kiya ja\nsakta — is question ko evaluation se exclude kar diya gaya tha. [Q80]\n● Devnimori Stupa, Gujarat ke Arvalli district mein hai — yaha 3rd-4th century AD ka ek Buddhist\nmonastery aur stupa mila hai. [Q81]\n● Karle (Pune district, Maharashtra) mein hai duniya ka sabse bada aur most evolved rock-cut Chaitya\nhall, jo Hinayana phase ka hai. [Q112]\n● 'Chaitya' ek pooja/prayer ki jagah (place of worship) hota hai, jabki 'Vihara' monks ki rehne ki jagah\n(dwelling place) hota hai, khaaskar rainy season ke dauran. [Q138, Q139, Q140]\n● Guntupalli (West Godavari dist., Andhra Pradesh — ab NTR district mein) mein early Chaityagrihas aur\nViharas mile hain — Eastern Deccan ke Chaityas/Viharas generally rock-cut structures hote hain,\npahadiyo mein bane hue. [Q141]\n● 'Stupa' word ka literal matlab hai 'ekatra karna/pile karna' — India mein stupa banane ki parampara\nBuddhism se bhi pehle ki hai, ye pre-Buddhist burial practices se nikli thi. [Q142]\n● Dhanyakataka (aaj ka Dharnikota), Andhra Pradesh (Palnadu district) mein hai — ye later Satvahanas\nki rajdhani thi aur Mahasanghikas ke under Buddhist learning ka bada center tha. [Q143]\n10. Buddhist Art & Iconography\n● India mein sabse pehle human statues jo pooja ki gayi, wo Buddha ki thi — isse idol worship ki\nfoundation padi (Mahayana sect ke followers ne shuru ki). [Q93, Q94]\n● Sarnath ke first-sermon wale Gandharan Buddha image mein 'Dharma Chakra Mudra' (dharma ke\nchakra ko ghumana) dikhaya gaya hai — Gandharan style, Hellenistic realism se inspired thi\n(Persian/Scythian/Parthian influences ke saath). [Q95]\n● Buddha ki standing statues Kushana period mein banayi gayi thi — Kanishka ke reign mein Gandhara\nart (aur Mathura school bhi) flourish hui. [Q96]\n●\n Disputed: Buddha ki sabse purani sculpture kis style mein bani, ye clearly nahi kaha ja sakta — V.S.\n⚠️\n\nAgrawal ke mutabik Mathura mein pehli statue bani, Hiuen Tsang ke mutabik Kaushambi mein — isliye\nis par ek fixed jawab nahi hai. [Q97]\n● 'Bhumisparsha Mudra' mein Buddha apna right hand zameen ki taraf badha kar Mara ke temptations ke\nagainst apni purity/chastity ki gawahi (witness) ke roop mein Earth ko bulaate hain. [Q98]\n● Sarnath ka famous Bhumisparsha Mudra wala Buddha image Gupta period ka masterpiece hai — ye\nupaya (right hand) aur prajna (left hand) ke union ko symbolize karta hai. [Q99, Q100]\n● Bodhisattva 'Padmapani' ki painting Ajanta (Cave 1) ki sabse famous aur oft-illustrated painting hai —\n'Padmapani' ka matlab hai 'kamal-dhaari' (jo blue lotus haath mein pakde hue hai). [Q110, Q111]\n● Kanheri caves (Salsette Island, Mumbai) mein ek 11-headed, 4-armed Avalokiteshvara Bodhisattva ki\nidol hai — India mein aisi ekmatra statue hai. [Q113]\n11. Great Centres of Buddhist Learning"," ● Ancient India ke important Buddhist learning centres the: Nalanda, Vikramshila aur Vallabhi — ye India\nke saath-saath China, Japan waghera se bhi students attract karte the. [Q120]\n● Ancient India mein Nagpur ek Buddhist learning centre NAHI tha — main centres Vallabhi, Vikramshila\naur Nalanda hi the. [Q121]\n● Vallabhi University Gujarat mein thi (Vallabhipura bhi kehte hain) — ye ancient Maitraka dynasty ki\nrajdhani thi. [Q122]\n● Nalanda University Gupta dynasty ke time flourish hui — ye Magadha (aaj ka Bihar) mein ek bada\nBuddhist monastery/University thi. [Q123]\n● Nalanda University ki foundation Kumargupta ne 450 AD mein ki thi — ye world ki pehli International\nUniversity maani jaati hai. Alexander Cunningham ne 1915-16 mein is site ko Nalanda University identify\nkiya tha. [Q124]\n● Nalanda University Buddhist Religious Philosophy ki teaching ke liye duniya bhar mein famous thi.\n[Q125]\n● Assertion-Reason: Nalanda (Rajgriha/Rajgir, Bihar) ek famous Buddhist learning centre aur University\nthi (sahi), aur ye Gupta period mein exist mein aayi (sahi) — Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation bhi\nhai. 12th century tak Muslim invasion ki wajah se ye ghat gayi, aur Pala rulers ne Vikramshila ko zyada\nprotection di jisse Nalanda ka mahatva kam hua. [Q126]\n● 'Nava Nalanda Mahavihara' ek modern Pali aur Buddhist research center hai — iska foundation stone\n20 November 1951 ko rakha gaya tha. [Q127]\n12. Buddhist Philosophers & Missionaries\n● Nagarjuna, Kanishka ke darbar ki ek eminent personality the — Chinese mythology ke mutabik unhone\nChina jaake Buddhism ka pracha kiya (1st century AD mein). [Q116]\n● 'Shunyata' (Doctrine of Void/emptiness) Nagarjuna ne propound kiya tha — unki famous book\n'Madhyamikakarika' mein emptiness/co-arising par mashoor quotes hain. [Q117]\n● Nagarjuna, Mahayana Buddhism ke 'Madhyamika' school ke founder the. [Q118]\n● Aryadeva (Nagarjuna ke disciple, Buddhist philosopher, na ki Jaina scholar) aur Dignaga (dono\nBuddhist scholars the) — Nathmuni ek Vaishnava scholar the, Sri Vaishnava sect ke first teacher. [Q119]\n13. Buddhism vs Jainism — What's Common, What's Not\n● Buddhism aur Jainism dono mein common hai: rituals ki efficiency ko deny karna, Vedas ke authority se\nindifference, aur Ahimsa (janwaro ko chot na pahunchana). Lekin 'extremities of penance/enjoyment\navoid karna' (Middle Path) sirf Buddhism ki khaasiyat hai — Jainism to rigorous penance follow karta\nhai. [Q128, Q129]\n● 'Self-mortification' (extreme tapasya) Jainism ka fundamental hissa hai, jabki Buddhism ne ise reject\nkarke 'Middle Path' apnaya — isliye ye dono mein COMMON nahi hai. [Q130]\n● Buddhism aur Jainism dono Karma ke siddhant aur Rebirth/soul ke transmigration mein believe karte\nhain. [Q132]"," 14. Social Aspects, Spread, Patronage & Decline of Buddhism\n● 'Neo-Buddhism' (Navayana) ko B.R. Ambedkar ne propound kiya tha — ye original Buddhism ki re-\ninterpretation hai jisme monasticism, karma, rebirth, samsara jaise concepts reject kiye gaye, aur class-\nstruggle/social equality par zor diya gaya. [Q87]\n● Pushyamitra Shunga (Shunga dynasty ke founder, jinhone last Mauryan Emperor Brihadratha ko 184\nBCE mein maara) ne Buddhism ke expansion mein\n\nयोगदानNAHI diya — ulta unhone Buddhists ko\npersecute kiya, jabki Ashoka, Kanishka aur Harshavardhana ne Buddhism ko patronize kiya. [Q102]\n● Buddhism ne caste-class system ko poori tarah reject nahi kiya tha (statement 1 sahi) — unhone\nBrahmins ke top social rank ko challenge zaroor kiya (statement 2 sahi), lekin kuch occupations/castes\nko phir bhi 'low' maana gaya (jaise Chandalas) (statement 3 sahi). [Q134]\n● Buddhism ke expansion ki wajahein: religion ki simplicity, Dalits/non-Brahmins ke liye special appeal,\nSangha ke through missionary spread, aur Pali jaisi simple regional languages ka use — Vedic spirit ki\n'soundness' iski wajah NAHI thi (Buddhism ne Vedas ko reject kiya tha). [Q135]\n● Buddhism early medieval India mein decline hone lagi kyunki Buddha ko tab tak Hindu pantheon mein\nassimilate kar liya gaya tha (Vishnu ke avatar ki tarah) — jabki Gupta kings Brahmanical faith support\nkarne ke bawajood Buddhism ke against nahi the (unhone Nalanda ko bhi patronize kiya). [Q136]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Buddhism Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0173","t":"05 Jainism","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" JAINISM — FULL MIND MAP\n🕉️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Origin of Jainism & the 24 Tirthankaras — Overview\n2. Tirthankara Symbols, Nirvana Places & Match Lists\n3. Individual Tirthankara Facts — Parshvanatha & Others\n4. Mahavira's Life — Birth, Family, Enlightenment & Death\n5. Core Jain Doctrines — Triratna (Three Jewels) & Vows\n6. Jain Metaphysics — Syadvad, Anekantavada & Tattva\n7. Jain Worldview — Eternal Universe, Non-violence & Karma\n8. Jain Sects — Digambara, Shwetambara & Sub-sects\n9. Jain Literature & Scriptures\n10. Jain Councils\n11. Mahavira's Disciples & Early Community\n12. Comparative & Historical Facts\n13. Ajivika Sect — A Related Ascetic Tradition\n14. Death Rites — Samadhi Maran (Sallekhana)\n15. Gommateshwara (Bahubali) & Shravanabelagola\n1. Origin of Jainism & the 24 Tirthankaras — Overview\n● Jain religion ke originator (pehle Tirthankara) Rishabhdev (Aadinath) the. Mahavira Swami 24th aur\nAKHIRI Tirthankara the, jinhone 6th century BC mein Jain philosophy ko propagate kiya. [Q1, Q2]\n● 'Tirthankara' word Jain religion se related hai — Rishabhanatha se lekar Mahavira tak total 24\nTirthankara hue, jo samay-samay par Jain philosophy propagate karte rahe. [Q14]\n● Mahavira, Jain Tirthankaro ke order mein sabse aakhri (24th) the. [Q15]\n● Nathamuni ek Jain Tirthankara NAHI the — wo ek Vaishnava theologian the (Sri Vaishnava Acharyas\nmein pehle). Chandraprabhu (8th), Neminatha (21st/22nd) aur Sambhavanatha (3rd) — ye sab actual\nTirthankara the. [Q16]\n2. Tirthankara Symbols, Nirvana Places & Match Lists\n● Tirthankara-Symbol match: Adinatha → Bull (Bail); Mallinatha → Water Jar (Ghara); Parshvanatha →\nSnake (Saanp); Sambhavnatha → Horse (Ghoda); Mahavira → Lion (Sher); Shantinath → Deer (Hiran).\n[Q4, Q5]\n●\n Exam Trap: Vasupujya (12th Tirthankar) ne Nirvana/Moksha Champapur (Bihar) mein prapt ki thi,\n⚠️\nSammedashikhar mein NAHI — is galat pairing ko dhyan se yaad rakho, baaki sab Tirthankar-Nirvan\nPlace pairs sahi hote hain. [Q6]\n● Site-Tirthankar match: Shravasti → Sambhavnath; Kakandi → Suvidhinath (Pushpadant); Ayodhya →\nRishabhanath; Pabhosa → Padmaprabhu. [Q7]\n● Tirthankaro ka chronological order (appearance ke hisaab se): Abhinandana Natha (4th) →\nMunishuvrata Nath (20th) → Vimal Nath (13th) → Padmaprabhu (6th) — is order ko yaad rakhne ke liye\nunki Tirthankar-number bhi yaad karo. [Q8]"," 3. Individual Tirthankara Facts — Parshvanatha & Others\n● Parshvanatha, 23rd Tirthankara the — unka janm Varanasi mein hua tha (King Aswasena aur Queen\nVama ke ghar). Unhone Ashrampad Udyan (Varanasi ke pass) mein Kaivalya (complete knowledge)\nprapt ki, aur Sammed Shikhar (Sammeta) par Parinirvana liya. [Q3, Q37]\n● Prabhasgiri (Kaushambi, UP) ek Jain pilgrimage site hai jo 6th Tirthankar Padmaprabha se related hai.\n[Q17]\n4. Mahavira's Life — Birth, Family, Enlightenment & Death\n● Mahavira Swami ka janm Kundagram (Kundalpur, Vaishali ke pass) mein ~599 BC mein hua tha. Maa\nTrishala, Lichchhavi republic ke chief Chetak ki BEHEN thi (beti nahi — ye common confusion hai). Pita\nSiddhartha Gyatrik Kshatriya clan ke head the. Nandivardhan unke bade bhai the. [Q9, Q10]\n● Mahavira Swami ne ~72 saal ki age mein, 527 BC mein, Pavapuri (Rajgriha/Rajgir ke pass, Bihar) mein\nNirvana prapt kiya — yahi unki mrityu-sthal bhi hai. [Q11, Q12]\n● Mahavira ke baare mein ek GALAT statement: 'unhone shaadi nahi ki thi' — ye sach nahi hai! Unki\nshaadi Yashoda naam ki rajkumari se hui thi, aur unki ek beti thi Priyadarshana (Aanojja). [Q13]\n● Jain religion mein 'Complete Knowledge/Intellect' ke liye 'Kaivalya' word use hota hai — Mahavira\nSwami ne Rijupalika river (Jrimbhik village ke pass) ke kinare, Sal ke ped ke neeche, 12 saal ki kathin\ntapasya ke baad Kaivalya prapt ki thi. [Q18, Q19]\n5. Core Jain Doctrines — Triratna (Three Jewels) & Vows\n● Jain philosophy mein Moksha ke liye 3 cheezein zaroori hain: Right Faith (Samyak Darshan), Right\nKnowledge (Samyak Jnana) aur Right Conduct/Action (Samyak Charitra) — inhe 'Triratna' (3 ratna)\nkaha jaata hai. [Q20, Q21]\n●\n Disputed: 'Triratna' ka concept dono — Buddhism AUR Jainism — mein hai. Buddhism mein\n⚠️\nTriratna hai Buddha, Dhamma, Sangha; Jainism mein Samyak Darshan, Samyak Jnana, Samyak\nCharitra — isliye single-religion wala answer clearly nahi diya ja sakta. [Q22]\n● 'Anuvrata' Jainism ka hi concept hai — Jain monks jo apni soul ko uplift karna chahte hain wo 5 bade\nvows (Mahavratas: Ahimsa, Satya, waghera) le\nतेhain. Aam grihasth logo ke liye ye mushkil hote hain,\nisliye wo 'Anuvrata' (chhote/scaled-down version wale vows) follow karte hain. [Q23]\n6. Jain Metaphysics — Syadvad, Anekantavada & Tattva\n● 'Syadvad' (jise Saptabhanginaya bhi kehte hain — matlab 'gyan relative hota hai') Jainism ka doctrine\nhai — Mahavira Swami ne selfists aur atheists ke exclusive beliefs ko chhodkar ye 'middle path' apnaya\ntha. [Q24, Q25]\n● Jainism se associated doctrines: Anekantavada aur Syadvada. (Sunyavada aur Sarvastivada Buddhism\nse related hain, Jainism se NAHI.) [Q26]\n● 'Anekantavada' Jainism ka core theory/philosophy hai — ye ek metaphysical concept hai. [Q28]"," ● Jain philosophy 2 main doctrines ke around ghumti hai: Anekantavada aur Syadvada — dono deeply\nconnected hain. Anekantavada ke mutabik har cheez ke numerous properties hote hain (permanent\nproperty ko 'Guna' kehte hain). Syadvada ke mutabik humara gyan partial/relative hota hai kyunki\npassion, anger, greed waghera hamare gyan ko obstruct karte hain. [Q29]\n● Jain philosophy ke mutabik 'Tattva' (reality) ki characteristics hain: Origination (utpatti), Decay (naash)\naur Permanence/Nityata (sthirta) — koi bhi entity 'Sat' (real) tabhi maani jaati hai jab usme permanence\nAUR transformation dono ho. [Q30]\n7. Jain Worldview — Eternal Universe, Non-violence & Karma\n● Jainism 'duniya ke final annihilation (poori tarah khatam ho jaana)' ke concept mein believe NAHI karta\n— Jain belief ke mutabik universe aur uske sabhi substances eternal (hamesha rehne wale) hain, koi\nalmighty inhe banane/manage karne ki zaroorat nahi hai. [Q27, Q31]\n● Jainism ka basic point 'Non-violence' (Ahimsa) hai — isliye Jainism ko 'Ahimsa ka dharm' bhi kehte\nhain. Ahimsa, Anekantvad aur Aparigraha — ye Jainism ke cardinal (mool) principles hain. [Q32]\n● Jaina Doctrine ke mutabik: har object (particle tak) mein ek soul hota hai (hylozoism). Karma ek\nextremely subtle matter hai jo soul mein infiltrate hokar uski natural purity ko dhaakta hai. Soul ki current\nstate countless ages ke accumulated Karma ki wajah se hoti hai, aur extreme penance/asceticism hi\nKarma khatam karne ka surest tareeka hai. [Q47]\n● Jain tradition maanta hai ki soul sirf animal/plant life mein hi nahi, balki rocks, running water jaise non-\nmobile bodies mein bhi hota hai — universe sirf insaano ke liye nahi, sab living beings ke liye ek\nevolution field hai. [Q56]\n8. Jain Sects — Digambara, Shwetambara & Sub-sects\n● 'Yapaniya' Jain religion ka ek sect tha, jo Digambaras se originate hua maana jaata hai — lekin ye kuch\nShwetambar opinions bhi follow karte the, aur apne temples mein Tirthankaro ki nude images ki pooja\nkarte the. [Q33]\n● 'Sthanakvasi' Shwetambara Jainism ka ek sect hai — iska predecessor reformist sect 'Lonka' tha\n(Lonkasha ne banaya). Ye maante hain ki soul-purification/Nirvana ke liye idol worship zaroori nahi hai.\n[Q34]\n● Mahavira ki mrityu ke ~150 saal baad, Magadha mein 12 saal ka bhayanak akaal (famine) aaya.\nBhadrabahuswami apne followers ke saath South mein migrate kar gaye — wo log unclad rahe aur\n'Digambar' kehlaaye. Jo log North mein reh gaye (unme Sthulabhadra prominent the) wo plain white\ncloth pehente the — unhe 'Shwetambar' kaha gaya. Sthulabhadra hi Shwetambar creed ke first founder\nmaane jaate hain. [Q39]\n● Kalinga king Kharavela (1st century BC) Jainism ka follower tha aur Jain monks ko patronage deta tha.\nBhadrabahuswami ne South India mein Jainism phailayi (Sthulabhadra ne nahi) — unke followers\n'Digambars' kehlaaye, na ki 'Shvetambaras'. [Q46]\n9. Jain Literature & Scriptures"," ● 'Fourteen Purvas' Jainism ki sabse purani holy book hai, jo sabhi Tirthankaro dwara preach ki gayi thi —\nlast Nand Ruler ke time, Sambhutavijay aur Bhadrabahu, Sangha ke presidents the aur inn ancient texts\nka gyan rakhte the. [Q35]\n● Sabse purana Jain literature 'Ardh-Magadhi' language mein compile hua tha — inke 12 Angas isi\nbhasha mein hain. Ye holy books finally 6th century AD mein Vallabhi (Gujarat ke pass) mein compile ki\ngayi thi. [Q36]\n● 'Therigatha' (jisme early Buddhist nuns/bhikshunis apne struggles bataati hain) ek Buddhist scripture\nhai, Jain literature ka hissa NAHI hai. [Q38]\n● Statement check: Shvetambara Canon mein 12 Angas hain, jo Mahavira ki teachings par based hain\n(sahi) — lekin inki compilation Vallabhi mein NAHI, balki 1st Jain Council (Pataliputra, ~310 BC) mein\nhui thi (ye statement galat hai). [Q44]\n10. Jain Councils\n● Pehla Jain Council, Chandragupta Maurya ke reign mein, Pataliputra mein hua tha — isme\nShwetambara Agama edit ki gayi thi (Sthulabhadra ki leadership mein). Baad mein purane texts destroy\nho gaye, isliye 4th century BC mein ek aur council organize hui jisme Bhadrabahu ke followers\nparticipate nahi kar paye. [Q42, Q43]\n11. Mahavira's Disciples & Early Community\n● Jamali (Mahavira ke damad/son-in-law) Mahavira ke pehle disciple/follower the — unhone 500 warrior-\ncaste logo ke saath vow liya tha. [Q40, Q41]\n12. Comparative & Historical Facts\n● Statement check: Mahavira ki maa Trishala, Lichchhavi King Chetaka ki BEHEN thi, BETI nahi\n(statement galat). Gautam Buddha ki maa Maya, Suddhodana ki patni, ek Koliya princess thi (sahi).\nParshvanatha, King Aswasena aur Queen Vama (Varanasi) ke ghar paida hue the (sahi). [Q45]\n● 3rd-4th century mein South India ke Ikshvaku rulers Vedic religion follow karte the lekin dusre religions\nko bhi support karte the. Bengal, Pala dynasty ke time Buddhism ka bada center bana tha (Pala rulers\nke support ki wajah se). [Q49]\n● Acharya-Sect match: Lakulisa → Pasupat (Shaivism); Nagarjuna → Sunyavada (Buddhism);\nBhadrabahu → Jain (Digambara sect); Gosala → Ajivaka. [Q57]\n● Kaushambi (UP) Jains aur Buddhists — dono ke liye ek famous pilgrimage site hai. Mahatma Buddha\nne yahan bahut baar preach kiya tha, aur yahan ka sabse famous monastery Ghoshitram tha (Shresthi\nGhoshit ne banwaya). [Q59]\n13. Ajivika Sect — A Related Ascetic Tradition"," ● 'Ajivika' sect Makkhali Gosala ne popularize kiya tha — wo shuru mein Mahavira ke disciple the, baad\nmein matbhed (difference of opinion) ki wajah se alag ho gaye. Unse pehle bhi Ajivika scholars the\n(Nanda Vaccha, Kisa Samkicca) lekin Gosala ne is sect ko sabse zyada popularize kiya. [Q50, Q51]\n● Ajivika sect 'Niyatiwad' (fatalism/destiny ka siddhant) mein believe karta tha — inke mutabik duniya ki\nhar cheez destiny/fate se control hoti hai, aur insaan iske aage kuch nahi kar sakta (koi free will nahi).\n[Q52, Q53]\n● Ajivika sect ki beliefs: Determinism (fate sab kuch decide karta hai) — sahi; extreme austerities (lambi\nchuppi, fasting) practice karte the kyunki ye unka predestined path tha — sahi; free will na maanne ki\nwajah se ye bhi maante the ki rebirth cycle ko personal/religious actions se badla NAHI ja sakta. [Q54]\n● Makkhali Gosala (Mahavira aur Buddha ke samkalin) Ajivika sect ke sabse prominent leader the (sahi).\nUnki philosophy 'Niyati' (fate) par based thi, jisme free will ke liye koi jagah nahi thi (sahi). Ajivikas caste-\nclass system ko reject karte the, egalitarian the (ye statement sahi hai, 'reject nahi karte the' wala\nstatement galat hoga). Ye log regular sabhas (meetings) bhi organize karte the (sahi). [Q55]\n● Barabar aur Nagarjuni hills (Mauryan emperor Ashoka aur unke pote Dasaratha ke time cut ki gayi) ki\ncaves Ajivika followers ke rehne ke liye bani thi. [Q58]\n14. Death Rites — Samadhi Maran (Sallekhana)\n● 'Samadhi Maran' (Sallekhana ya Sanyasna Maran bhi kehte hain) Jain ethical code ka aakhri vow hai —\njab normal life possible na rahe (budhape, laa-ilaaj bimari waghera ki wajah se), tab Jain ascetics aur\nlay-followers dheere-dheere khana-paani kam karke apni zindagi khatam karte hain. [Q48]\n15. Gommateshwara (Bahubali) & Shravanabelagola\n●\n Common Trap: Shravanabelagola ki Gomateshwara (Bahubali) statue Jainism ke pehle Tirthankara\n⚠️\nRishabhnath ke BETE Bahubali ko represent karti hai — ye AAKHRI Tirthankara (Mahavira) ko\nrepresent NAHI karti (ye ek galat statement hai jo exam mein pucha jaata hai). [Q60]\n● Gommateshwara statue, Chamundraya ne banwayi thi (Ganga ruler Rachmalla-IV/Panchmalla ke\nminister), lagbhag 981 AD mein. [Q61]\n● 'Mahamastakabhisheka' Bahubali (Gomteshwara) se related ek bada religious event hai — ye\nShravanbelgola (Karnataka) mein har 12 saal mein hota hai. Yahan ki Bahubali statue 18 meter ooncha\nhai. [Q62]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Jainism Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0174","t":"06 Shaiva Bhagavata Religion","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" SHAIVA & BHAGAVATA RELIGION — FULL MIND MAP\n🕉️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Ancient Cosmogony — The Four Yugas\n2. Shaivism — Sects & Iconography\n3. Bhakti Movement — Alvars, Nayanars & Devotional Saints\n4. Bhagavata Religion — Origin & Development\n5. Vaishnava Deities, Avatars & Iconography\n6. Bhagavata Cult — The Nine Forms of Bhakti\n7. Bhagavata Religion — Earliest Archaeological Evidence\n8. Astika-Nastika Systems & Vedanta Texts\n9. The Bhagavad Gita — Core Teachings\n10. Epics, Puranas, Sacred Places & Festivals\n1. Ancient Cosmogony — The Four Yugas\n● Ancient Indian cosmogonic beliefs ke mutabik, samay ke 4 yugas ka sahi cyclical order hai: Krita (Satya\nYuga) → Treta → Dvapara → Kaliyuga. [Q1]\n2. Shaivism — Sects & Iconography\n● 'Mattamayura' ancient India ki ek Shaiva sect thi — iska zikr Chedi Dynasty ke inscriptions mein milta\nhai. [Q2]\n● 'Ardhanarisvara' (aadha Shiva, aadha Parvati) Shiva aur unki consort Parvati ka ek\ncomposite/androgynous form hai — right half generally Shiva (male) hota hai. Ye universe ki masculine\naur feminine energies ke synthesis (mel) ko represent karta hai, aur dikhata hai ki Shakti (female\nprinciple) Ishwar se alag nahi ho sakti. [Q3]\n3. Bhakti Movement — Alvars, Nayanars & Devotional Saints\n● Medieval period mein devotional (Bhakti) spirit mainly South India (Tamil regions) mein phaila — Vishnu\nke devotees 'Alvar' kehlaaye, aur Shiva ke devotees 'Nayanars' kehlaaye. Dono maante the ki personal\nlove/dedication (bhakti) hi Moksha ka ekmatra raasta hai, aur caste system ki rigidity ka virodh karte the.\n[Q4, Q5]\n● Poigai, Pudam aur Thirumangai — ye Alvar Saints the. Lekin Tirugyan (Tirugnana Sambandar) ek\nNayanar (Shaivite) saint the, Alvar saint NAHI the. [Q6]\n● Total 12 Alvar saints hue hain, jinhone South India mein Vaishnavism phailayi — inme se ekmatra\nfemale saint 'Andal' thi. [Q7]\n● 'Nathpanthis', 'Siddhas' aur 'Yogis' ne North India mein Bhakti (devotional) religion ko popular banaya —\nunhone conventional religion ke rituals aur social order ki criticism ki, aur duniya se renunciation\n(sanyaas) ki wakalat ki. [Q30]"," 4. Bhagavata Religion — Origin & Development\n● Bhagavata (Vaishnava) religion Gupta kings ke reign mein apne peak par pahunchi — Gupta rulers\nVaishnav dharma ke follower the aur unhone ise state religion bana diya. Zyadatar Gupta rulers\n'Parambhagavata' ki title dharan karte the. Garuda (Vishnu ka vahana) Guptas ka state symbol tha. [Q8]\n● Bhagavata religion ke traditional originator Lord Krishna (Vasudeva) mane jaate hain — wo Vrishni\n(Satvat) vansh se the, Mathura se belong karte the, aur Chhandogya Upanishad mein unhe Devaki ka\nputra aur Rishi Ghor Angirasa ka shishya bataya gaya hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Vasudeva Krishna ki sabse pehle pooja 'Bhagavatas' ne ki thi — Panini ke zamane mein Vasudev ke\nworshippers 'Vasudevak' (Bhagavata) kehlaate the. [Q11]\n5. Vaishnava Deities, Avatars & Iconography\n● Krishna ke bhai Balarama ko art mein hamesha plough (hal) pakde hue dikhaya jaata hai — isi wajah se\nunhe 'Haldhar' (plough-bearer) bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q12]\n● Vishnu ne Varaha (suar) avatar leke Hiranyaksha (giants ke raja) ko maara tha aur Prithvi ko uske\nkabze se azaad kiya tha — Puranic pictures mein Varaha ko Prithvi ko apne dant/tusks par balance\nkarte hue, samundar se uthte hue dikhaya jaata hai. Is avatar mein Varaha ka sar aur ek human body\nhai, jisme 4 haath — Shankha, Chakra, Gada aur Padma pakde hue hain. [Q18]\n● Kamadeva (Kama, pyaar/ichha ke Hindu God) ko 'Ananga' (bina sharir wale) bhi kaha jaata hai — Lord\nShiva ne apni teesri aankh se Kamadeva ko jala kar rakh diya tha, isi wajah se unhe ye naam mila. Rati\nunki patni hain. [Q22]\n● Deity-Symbol match: Shiva → Trishul (Trident); Vishnu → Chakra; Ganesh → Pasha (Rope/noose);\nSaraswati → Veena. [Q27]\n6. Bhagavata Cult — The Nine Forms of Bhakti\n● Bhagavata cult mein Moksha paane ke liye 'Navadha Bhakti' (bhakti ke 9 forms) recognize ki gayi hain:\nShravana, Kirtana, Smarana, Padasevana, Archana, Vandana, Dasya, Sakhya, aur Atmanivedana.\n[Q13]\n7. Bhagavata Religion — Earliest Archaeological Evidence\n● Besanagar (Vidisha) ka Garuda Pillar — Heliodorus dwara banwaya gaya — Bhagavata religion ka\nsabse purana stone monument hai. Iske inscription se pata chalta hai ki Takshila ke Yavana\nambassador (Heliodorus) ne Bhagavata dharm accept karke uski pooja ki thi — usme khud ko\n'Bhagavata' aur Vasudeva ko 'Devadeva' (Gods ke bhi God) likha gaya hai. [Q14]\n● Bhagavata Religion ka sabse purana archival/epigraphic evidence — Besnagar (Vidisha) ka Heliodorus\nGaruda Pillar Inscription hai. [Q15, Q16]\n● Heliodorus (Besanagar Inscription wale) Takshila (Taxila) ke resident the — unhe Indo-Greek King\nAntialcidas ne King Bhagabhadra ke darbar mein ambassador banakar bheja tha. [Q17]"," 8. Astika-Nastika Systems & Vedanta Texts\n● Ancient Indian philosophy mein 'Astika' (orthodox) sects wo the jo Vedas ki authenticity (pramanikta)\nmein believe karte the, aur 'Nastika' (heterodox) sects wo the jo nahi karte the. Buddhism, Jainism aur\nCharvaka — teeno Nastika schools maane jaate hain. [Q19]\n● 'Prasthan Trayi' (Vedanta philosophy ke 3 mool source texts) mein Upanishad, Brahmasutra aur\nBhagavad Gita shaamil hain — 'Bhagavata' (Purana) is list mein SHAAMIL NAHI hai. [Q23]\n9. The Bhagavad Gita — Core Teachings\n● Bhagavad Gita mein Moksha (liberation) ke 3 raaste — Jnana (Knowledge), Karma (Action) aur Bhakti\n(Devotion) — sabko equal importance di gayi hai. (Is\nकेcomparison mein: Advaita Vedanta mein\nShankaracharya ne sirf Brahma ko truth maana; Vishistadvaita Vedanta Bhakti ko supremacy deta hai.)\n[Q20]\n● Bhagavad Gita ki main teaching hai 'Nishkama Karma Yoga' — matlab bina kisi personal fayde/phal ki\nchah ke apna karm (duty) karna. Gita sabhi Yoga philosophies mein Nishkam Karma Yoga ko sabse\nsupreme maanti hai. [Q21]\n10. Epics, Puranas, Sacred Places & Festivals\n● Naimisharanya (Sitapur dist., UP) ko 60,000 hermits ki residence maana jaata hai — yahin Sut\nGoswami ne ek Yagya ke dauran Saunak aur baaki hermits ke saamne poora Mahabharata sunaya tha\n(isse pehle Vaisampayana ne King Janamejaya ko Mahabharata sunayi thi). [Q24]\n● Valmiki ki Ramayana (Adi Kavya, Sanskrit mein) mein total 7 Kand hain — 4th Kand 'Kishkindha Kand'\nhai, jisme Ram-Hanuman ki pehli mulaqaat, Bali ki mrityu, aur Sugriva ke raja banne ka varnan hai.\n[Q25]\n● 'Kalika Purana' (Kali Purana ya Sati Purana bhi kehte hain) Shaktism tradition ka ek mukhya Upapurana\nhai — ye Assam region mein compose hui thi, aur Sage Markendeya se attribute ki jaati hai. [Q26]\n● Puri (Odisha) ki famous Rathyatra, Ashadha month ke Shukla Paksha mein, Lord Jagannath (Krishna),\nBalram (Balbhadra) aur Subhadra ke sammaan mein celebrate ki jaati hai. [Q28]\n● Nasik ka Kumbh Mela, Godavari river ke kinare, har 12 saal mein hota hai — Kumbh Mela Haridwar\n(Ganga), Prayagraj (Ganga-Yamuna-Saraswati sangam) aur Ujjain (Kshipra river) mein bhi hota hai.\n[Q29]\n● Religion-Holiest Place match: Jainism → Pavapuri (Rajgir ke pass, jaha Mahavir Swami ne 527 BC\nmein Nirvana liya); Hinduism → Varanasi (Ganga kinare); Islam → Medina (Mecca ke baad doosra\nsabse pavitra); Christianity → Vatican City (Roman Catholic Church ki rajdhani). [Q31]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Shaiva & Bhagavata Religion Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0175","t":"07 Sixth Century BCE Political Condition","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" 6TH CENTURY BCE — POLITICAL CONDITION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Economy — Earliest Coins & the Shreni (Guild) System\n2. The 16 Mahajanapadas — Textual Sources\n3. Mahajanapada Capitals — Important Match Lists\n4. Mahajanapada Geography & Locations\n5. Republics of the 6th Century BCE\n6. Kings of Avanti & Vatsa — Pradyota, Udayan\n7. Pataliputra — Foundation & Key Facts\n8. Rise of Magadha & its Early Capitals\n9. Haryanka Dynasty — Bimbisara & Ajatashatru\n10. Later Magadhan Dynasties — Shishunaga, Nanda & Maurya\n11. Cities — Shravasti & Kalpi\n12. Religious & Social Context of the 6th Century BCE\n1. Economy — Earliest Coins & the Shreni (Guild) System\n● India ke sabse purane surviving coins Silver ke bane the — inhe 'Aahat coins' ya 'Punch Marked coins'\nkaha jaata hai, kyunki inpar stamp se marks banaye jaate the. [Q1]\n● 'Shreni' system ancient India mein traders/artisans (guilds) ki ek organization thi jo goods ki quality aur\nprices control karti thi. Ye system sirf North India tak limited NAHI tha — South India mein bhi prevalent\ntha. [Q60]\n2. The 16 Mahajanapadas — Textual Sources\n● 16 Mahajanapadas ki list Buddhist text 'Anguttara Nikaya' mein milti hai — inme Anga, Magadha, Kashi,\nKoshala, Vajji, Malla, Chedi, Vatsa, Kuru, Panchal, Matsya, Shurasena, Ashmaka, Avanti, Gandhara aur\nKamboj shaamil hain. Ye list Jain text 'Bhagavati Sutra' mein bhi milti hai. [Q22, Q23, Q24, Q26]\n● Panini (Sanskrit grammarian, Ashtadhyayi ke author, Pushkalavati/Gandhara se) ne apne texts mein 22\nalag Janapadas ka zikr kiya, lekin unme se 16 Mahajanapadas mein se sirf 3 sabse mahatvapurna\nJanapadas — Magadha, Ashmak aur Kamboj — ka specifically zikr kiya. [Q25]\n3. Mahajanapada Capitals — Important Match Lists\n●\n Exam Trap: Koshala ki rajdhani Saket/Shravasti thi, Ahichchhatra NAHI (wo Northern Panchala ki\n⚠️\nrajdhani thi) — ye common galat-match hai jo exam mein poochha jaata hai. [Q2]\n● Mahajanapada-Capital match: Kuru → Indraprastha; Panchal → Ahichchhatra; Koshala → Saket\n(Shravasti); Vatsa → Kaushambi. [Q56]\n● Mahajanapada-Capital match: Matsya → Virat Nagar; Kuru → Indraprastha; Shurasena → Mathura;\nAsmak (Ashmak) → Potan/Paithan. [Q57]\n●\n Exam Trap: Shurasena ki rajdhani Mathura thi, Kaushambi NAHI (Kaushambi Vatsa Mahajanapada\n⚠️\nki rajdhani thi) — ye bhi ek common galat-match hai. [Q58]"," ● North Panchal ki rajdhani (Mahabharata ke mutabik) Ahichchhatra thi, aur South Panchal ki rajdhani\nKampilya thi. Hastinapura aur Indraprastha Kuru ki rajdhaniyan thi, aur Mathura Shurasena ki. [Q27]\n● 16 Mahajanapadas ke period mein Mathura, Surasena (Shurasena) Mahajanapada ki rajdhani thi. [Q28]\n● Champa (Campa), Anga Mahajanapada ki rajdhani thi — ye modern Munger aur Bhagalpur (Bihar)\ndistricts cover karta tha. Baad mein Bimbisara ne ise Magadha mein annex kar liya. [Q29]\n● 6th century BC mein, Chedi Mahajanapada (modern Bundelkhand ke aas-paas) ki rajdhani 'Sotthivati'\nthi, jise Mahabharata mein 'Suktimati' kaha gaya hai. [Q30]\n4. Mahajanapada Geography & Locations\n● Ujjain (Madhya Pradesh ke Malwa region mein) ka ancient naam 'Avantika' tha — ye Avanti\nMahajanapada ki 2 rajdhaniyo mein se ek thi. [Q6]\n● Map par 4 Mahajanapadas: Matsya (Rajasthan ke Jaipur-Alwar-Bharatpur districts, capital Viratnagar),\nAvanti (Malwa region — Northern Avanti ki capital Ujjayini, Southern Avanti ki capital Mahishmati), Vatsa\n(Prayagraj-Kaushambi districts, capital Kaushambi), aur Anga (Bihar ke Bhagalpur-Munger districts,\ncapital Champa). [Q7]\n● Madhyamika (Nagari) aur Viratnagar — dono aise ancient cities hain jinka zikr Mahabharata AUR\nMahabhashya, dono mein milta hai. Viratnagar ko King Virat ne basaya tha, aur ye Matsya kingdom ki\nrajdhani thi. [Q8]\n● 'Assaka' (Ashmaka) Mahajanapada, Godavari aur Narmada river ke beech situated tha — iski rajdhani\nPaithan/Potan (ancient naam Prathisthana) thi. [Q31]\n● Matsya Mahajanapada (6th century BC) Rajasthan ke Jaipur, Alwar aur Bharatpur ke aas-paas situated\ntha — iski rajdhani Viratnagar thi. [Q32]\n● 16 Mahajanapadas mein se 8 modern Uttar Pradesh mein situated the: Kuru (Meerut-Delhi-\nThaneshwar), Panchala (Bareilly-Badaun-Farrukhabad), Shurasena (Brajmandal), Vatsa (Prayagraj-\nKaushambi), Koshal (Awadh), Malla (Deoria-Kushinagar), Kashi (Varanasi), aur Chedi (Eastern\nBundelkhand). [Q59]\n5. Republics of the 6th Century BCE\n● Buddha period (6th century BC) mein bahut saari Republics (Ganarajya) exist karti thi: Shakya\n(Kapilavastu), Bhagga (Sumsumaragiri), Buli (Alakappa), Kalam (Kesaputta), Koliya (Ramgama), Malla\n(Kusinara), waghera. Lekin 'Yaudheya' is period ki Republic NAHI thi — wo post-Mauryan era mein\nprominent hui. [Q18]\n● Duniya ki pehli Republic (ganatantra) Vaishali mein, Lichchhavi dynasty ne establish ki thi. Vaishali ka\nnaam Mahabharata era ke King Vishal se pada — ye ek bada Buddhist pilgrimage site hai aur Mahavira\nki janmabhoomi bhi. [Q19, Q20]\n● Pair match: Chetak — Lichchhavi (King Chetak Lichchhavi republic ke emperor the, unki beti Chelana ki\nshaadi Magadha King Bimbisara se hui thi). Parsvanath Jnatrika clan se NAHI the (Mahavira the);\nBindusara Mauryan king the, Shakya nahi; Skandagupta Gupta king the, Maurya nahi. [Q21]"," 6. Kings of Avanti & Vatsa — Pradyota, Udayan\n● Chand-Pradyota (ya Pradyota), Avanti ke ruler the — wo Pulika ke bete the, jinhone apne master ko\nUjjain mein maar kar apne bete ko raja banaya tha. Pradyota, Buddha aur Bimbisara ke samkalin the —\nunka zikr Mahavagga (Vinaya Pitaka ka hissa) aur Puranas mein milta hai. Unhone 23 saal raj kiya.\nBimbisara ne apne Raj Vaidya Jivak ko Pradyota ke jaundice ke ilaj ke liye bheja tha. [Q4]\n● Kavi Bhaas ke natak 'Svapnavasavadattam' mein 'Udayan-Vasavadatta' ki legend hai — ye Vatsa ke\nraja Udayan aur Avanti King Pradyota ki beti Vasavadatta ki love story hai, jab Udayan Ujjayini mein\nqaid the. [Q15]\n● Ruler-Kingdom match: Pradyot → Avanti; Udayana → Vatsa; Prasenjit → Koshala; Ajatashatru →\nMagadha. [Q3]\n7. Pataliputra — Foundation & Key Facts\n●\n Disputed: Pataliputra ka founder kaun tha, is par confusion hai — historically ise Ajatashatru ne ek\n⚠️\nfort ki tarah banwaya tha, lekin unke successor Udayin ne isse Rajgriha se capital shift karke ek poori\ncity bana diya — isliye alag-alag exams alag-alag answer (Ajatashatru ya Udayin) accept karte hain.\n[Q9, Q12, Q13]\n● Pataliputra (aaj ka Patna) North mein Ganga river se aur West mein Son (Sone) river se ghira hua tha\n— strategically rivers ke sangam par situated tha. [Q10]\n● Diye gaye options mein se, apne poore empire ki capital Pataliputra ko banane wale pehle ruler\nChandragupta Maurya the (halaki Udayin ne pehle hi ise Magadha ki capital bana diya tha, lekin wo\noption mein nahi hote). [Q11]\n8. Rise of Magadha & its Early Capitals\n● Ganga river ke South ka area ancient time mein 'Magadha' kehlaata tha (diye gaye options mein ye\nnaam nahi tha, isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer hai). Takshashila Indus-Jhelum ke beech thi,\nChola Godavari ke South mein thi, aur Anarta Gujarat ka ek Vedic-era kingdom tha. [Q14]\n● Pehla Magadhan Empire 6th century BC mein flourish hua — iske actual founder King Bimbisara (~544-\n492 BC) the, jo Haryanka dynasty se the. [Q16]\n● 6th century BC ki shuruaat mein Magadha sabse powerful city-state thi — ye sabse ameer aur\nprosperous Mahajanapadas mein se ek thi. Magadha ki Koshala, Anga aur Kashi se lambi rivalry rahi,\naur aakhir mein Magadha hi supremacy ke liye jeeti. [Q17]\n● Girivraja (Rajgriha) hi Magadha ki pehli/initial capital thi — yahi pehla Buddhist Council organize hua tha\naur Mahavira ne apna pehla sermon diya tha. Puranas ke mutabik Brihadrath dynasty pehli thi jisne\nMagadha par raj kiya, aur unke bete Jarasandha ne Girivraja ko apni capital banaya. [Q33, Q34, Q36]\n●\n Disputed: Magadha ki pehli capital Rajgriha (Girivraj) thi — lekin agar options mein Rajgriha na ho,\n⚠️\nto 'None/More than one' sahi answer ban jaata hai. Baad mein Udayin (Haryanka dynasty) ke reign mein\ncapital Pataliputra shift ho gayi thi. [Q35]\n● Girivraja/Rajgriha aur Pataliputra — dono Magadha Empire ki capitals thi. Lekin Kaushambi Magadha ki\ncapital NAHI thi — wo Vatsa state ki rajdhani thi. [Q37]"," 9. Haryanka Dynasty — Bimbisara & Ajatashatru\n● Bimbisara ne ancient Bihar mein 'Haryanka Vansh' (dynasty) ki sthapna ki — ye Magadha ki dusri ruling\ndynasty thi, jo mythical Barhadratha dynasty ke baad aayi. [Q40]\n● Ajatashatru (492-460 BC), Haryanka dynasty ke the — unhone apne pita Bimbisara ko maar kar gaddi\nhasil ki thi, aur khud unke bete Udayin ne unhe usi tarah maar diya tha. [Q39, Q41, Q42]\n● Ajatashatru ne Vajji confederacy (jiski principal republic Vaishali thi, jise Lichchhavis chalate the) ko\nharaya aur Magadha mein assimilate kar liya. Nirayavali Sutra ke mutabik, Chetak (Lichchhavi chief) ne\n9 Lichchhavis, 9 Mallas aur 18 Ganrajyas ka united front banaya tha — lekin Bhagavati Sutta ke mutabik\nAjatashatru hi jeete the. [Q43]\n● Jivaka (Jeevaka), Mahatma Buddha ke samkalin ek famous physician the, jo Bimbisara ke darbar se\nassociated the. Bimbisara ne unhe Avanti ke raja Chandapradyota ke jaundice ka ilaj karne bheja tha.\n[Q52, Q53]\n10. Later Magadhan Dynasties — Shishunaga, Nanda & Maurya\n● Matsya Purana ke mutabik, Magadha ke raja Shishunaga ne Nandivardhan ko haraakar Avanti (Malwa)\nko apne empire mein annex kar liya tha — isse Magadha ki power Malwa region tak phaili. [Q44]\n● Shishunaga dynasty ke baad Nanda dynasty ne Magadha par raj kiya. Mahapadmananda (Ugrasen bhi\nkehte the) Nanda dynasty ke founder the — Puranas mein unhe 'Sarvakshatrantaka' aur\n'Aparoparashurama' (dusra Parashurama) bhi kaha gaya hai kyunki unhone bahut vistar se conquest ki\nthi. [Q45, Q46, Q47]\n● 6th century BC mein, Varanasi Kashi Mahajanapada ki rajdhani thi — Bimbisara ko ye dahej (dowry)\nmein mili thi jab unhone Mahakoshala se shaadi ki. Baad mein Shishunag ne jab Vaishali ko apni capital\nbanaya, to unhone apne bete ko Varanasi ka deputy-king banaya — isliye UPPSC ke mutabik\nShishunag ko Varanasi ki 'second capital' banane wala maana jaata hai. [Q48]\n● Nanda dynasty ke aakhri raja Dhanananda the — unke extortion aur heavy taxes ki wajah se log\npareshan the. Chandragupta Maurya ne Chanakya ki madad se Dhanananda ko haraakar Maurya\nEmpire ki sthapna ki. [Q49]\n● Kalinga ke Chedi dynasty ke Emperor Kharvel ka 'Hathigumpha inscription', King Nanda\n(Mahapadmananda) ka evidence deta hai — isme Kalinga mein canal khudwane ka zikr hai, jo is tarah\nka pehla inscription hai jo canal-engraving ke baare mein bataata hai. [Q5, Q50]\n● Magadhan dynasties ka chronological order: Haryanka dynasty (544-412 BC) → Nanda dynasty (344-\n321 BC) → Mauryan dynasty (321-184 BC) → Shunga dynasty (184-75 BC). [Q51]\n11. Cities — Shravasti & Kalpi\n● Ancient Shravasti (Alexander Cunningham ne 1861 mein Sahet-Mahet, UP mein identify kiya tha) ka\ntown-configuration 'Crescentic' (aadhe-chaand jaisa) tha — ye excavations se pata chala hai. [Q38]\n● Kalpi town, UP ke Jalaun district mein, Yamuna river ke kinare situated hai — ancient time mein ye\n'Kalpriyanath' ya 'Kalpriya Nagari' ke naam se famous tha. [Q55]"," 12. Religious & Social Context of the 6th Century BCE\n● 6th century BC mein North India ki middle Ganga valley mein bahut se naye religious sects emerge hue\n— ye ek intellectual environment ki wajah se hua. Vedic religion complicated ho gayi thi, Shlokas aur\nYajnas ki purity par zyada focus ho gaya tha, jisse priests ka importance bahut badh gaya tha aur\nsacrifices mehenge ho gaye the — dono statements sahi hain. [Q54]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · 6th Century BCE Political Condition Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0176","t":"08 Greek Invasion","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" GREEK INVASION — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Political Situation in India at the Time of Alexander's Invasion\n2. Alexander's Campaign — Battles, Resistance & Departure\n3. Alexander's Companions & Later Greek Contacts\n1. Political Situation in India at the Time of Alexander's Invasion\n● Alexander ke invasion ke time North India par Nanda dynasty raj kar rahi thi — Mahapadmananda ke 8\nsuccessors the (Puranas aur Buddhist texts ke mutabik), jinme se Dhanananda is dynasty ke aakhri\nruler the aur Alexander ke samkalin bhi the. Greek writers unhe 'Agrammese' bulaate the, Xenophon ne\nunhe ek ameer insaan bataya hai, aur Bhaddasala unke commander the. [Q1, Q2]\n● Alexander ki India mein safalta ki 3 mukhya wajahein thi: (1) us waqt India mein koi central\npower/authority nahi tha — Dr. Hemachandra Rai Chaudhary ke mutabik us time 28 independent\npowers thi; (2) Alexander ki army superior thi; (3) Ambhi jaise kai Indian traitor rajaon ne unhe support\nkiya tha. (Ek accha administrator hona unki military jeet ki direct wajah NAHI thi.) [Q5]\n2. Alexander's Campaign — Battles, Resistance & Departure\n● Assertion-Reason: Alexander ne lagbhag 2 saal India mein campaign karne ke baad 325 BC mein India\nchhod diya (sahi) — lekin iski wajah Chandragupta Maurya se haar NAHI thi (galat Reason).\nAchaemenid empire ko 326 BC mein khatam karne ke baad, Alexander ne bade army ke saath India par\ncampaign shuru ki thi, aur 2 saal baad Patala se Greece wapas laut gaye. Unki army ne Beas\n(Hyphasis) river paar karne se mana kar diya tha, kyunki wo war se thak chuke the aur ghar jaana\nchahte the (homesickness). [Q3]\n● Ashvaka, ek frontier republic tha (invasion ke time), jiski capital Massaga (Masakavati) thi. Jab Ashvaka\nke bahut se soldiers battlefield mein maare/ghayal ho gaye, to Massaga ki auraton ne khud hathiyar\nuthaakar Alexander ke against ladai ki — Greek writers ke mutabik Alexander ne is town ki sabhi\nauraton ko maar dala tha. [Q4]\n● Puru (Porus), jinka raajya Jhelum aur Chenab river ke beech tha, unhe Alexander ne Jhelum river ke\nkinare 'Battle of Hydaspes' mein haraya tha — lekin unki bahaduri se impress hokar Alexander ne unse\ndosti kar li, unka rajya wapas kar diya, aur kuch aur ilaake bhi tohfe mein diye. [Q6]\n3. Alexander's Companions & Later Greek Contacts\n● Deimachus, Alexander ke saath India NAHI aaye the — Strabo ke mutabik, Seleucid emperor Antiochus\nI ne Deimachus ko apna ambassador banakar Mauryan King Bindusara ke darbar mein bheja tha (ye\nAlexander ke bahut baad ki baat hai). Alexander ke actual companions/writers the Nearchus,\nOnesicritus, aur Aristobulus. [Q7]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Greek Invasion Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0177","t":"09 Maurya Empire","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Ancient History","x":[" MAURYA EMPIRE — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Chandragupta Maurya — Founder & Literary Sources\n2. Kautilya / Chanakya & the Arthashastra\n3. Bindusara's Reign\n4. Mauryan Palace & Pataliputra Archaeology\n5. Chandragupta's Conquests, Empire Extent & Sudarshan Lake\n6. Ashoka's Empire — Extent, Territories & Provinces\n7. Ashoka's Dhamma, Welfare Measures & Religious Tolerance\n8. Third Buddhist Council & Mauryan Rulers' Religious Beliefs\n9. Mauryan Central, Revenue & Local Administration\n10. Mauryan Art & Architecture\n11. Ashoka's Pilgrimage & Associated Buddhist Sites\n12. Ashokan Inscriptions — Scripts & Decipherment\n13. Ashokan Inscriptions — Names, Epithets & Personal Mentions\n14. Ashokan Inscriptions — Locations Across India\n15. The Kalinga War & Key Rock Edicts\n16. South Indian Kingdoms Mentioned in Ashokan Edicts\n17. Foreign Relations — Megasthenes & Diplomatic Ties\n18. Megasthenes' 'Indica' — Society, Economy & City Administration\n19. Ancient Records, Learning Centres & Social Groups\n20. Administrative Tiers, Social Norms & Foreign Travellers\n21. Later Mauryan Rulers, Epithets & the Empire's End\n1. Chandragupta Maurya — Founder & Literary Sources\n● Chandragupta Maurya ne India ka pehla pan-Indian empire establish kiya tha — unhone chhote-chhote\nfragmented kingdoms ko jodkar ek bada empire banaya, jo Iran ke edge tak phaila hua tha. Mauryan\ndynasty (321 BC – 184 BC) India ki sabse purani dynasty maani jaati hai (diye options mein),\nKushan/Gupta/Vardhana dynasty baad mein aayi. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4]\n● Vishakhadatta ke natak 'Mudrarakshasa' mein Chandragupta Maurya ke reign ke baare mein bahut\ninformation hai — isme Chandragupta ko Nandraja ka beta bataya gaya hai, aur unhe 'Vrishal' aur\n'Kulheen' (low origin) bhi kaha gaya hai. Dr. K.P. Jayaswal ke mutabik, Vishakhadatta aur Chandragupta\nsamkalin nahi the — is natak mein Chandragupta ke darbar ke 'Durabhisandhi' (court intrigues) describe\nkiye gaye hain. [Q5, Q144]\n● Greek writer Justin ne Sandrokottos (Chandragupta Maurya) aur Alexander ki mulaqaat describe ki thi.\nWilliam Jones sabse pehle scholar the jinhone 'Sandrokottos' ko Chandragupta Maurya se identify kiya.\nArrian aur Plutarch ne unhe 'Androkottus' bhi bataya hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n2. Kautilya / Chanakya & the Arthashastra\n● Kautilya (Vishnugupta/Chanakya) Chandragupta Maurya ke prime minister, advisor aur chief priest the\n— Mauryan dynasty ki sthapna mein unka bada yogdan tha. Sage Chanak ke bete the, bachpan mein\n'Vishnugupta' naam se jaane jaate the. Researcher T. Trautmann ke mutabik, Chanakya/Kautilya unke\ngotra (clan) ka naam ho sakta hai. [Q9, Q10, Q11]"," ● Kautilya ka 'Arthashastra' polity, statecraft, economic policy aur military strategy — sab par based hai\n(isliye 'more than one' options sahi hote hain) — ye mukhya roop se political policies aur government ke\nprinciples par book hai, sirf economics par nahi. Isko often Machiavelli ki 'The Prince' se compare kiya\njaata hai. [Q12, Q13, Q15, Q17]\n● Arthashastra ke Saptang Theory of State mein 7 elements hote hain: Swami (King), Amatya (Minister),\nJanpada (Territory), Durg (Fort), Kosha (Treasury), Danda (Army/Force), aur Mitra (Ally) — Mitra\nsaptang ka 7th (aakhri) part hai, jo 'state ke kaan' ki tarah hota hai. [Q14]\n● Arthashastra ke Dasa-Kalpa chapter ke mutabik, koi vyakti judicial punishment ki wajah se slave ban\nsakta tha. Agar ek female slave apne master ke ghar ek beta janam deti thi, to wo legally azaad ho jaati\nthi (lekin uska beta master ke legitimate son jaisa status nahi paata tha). [Q16]\n3. Bindusara's Reign\n● Bindusara ke reign mein, unke bete Ashoka ne Avanti Mahajanapada ko jeet kar Mauryan empire mein\nmerge kiya tha — is event ka zikr Buddhist scholar Buddhaghosa ki 'Samant Pasadika' mein milta hai.\n[Q19]\n● Greek historian Strabo ke mutabik, Syrian king Antiochus I Soter ne apna ambassador Deimachus,\nBindusara ke darbar mein bheja tha — unhone Megasthenes ki jagah li thi. [Q18]\n4. Mauryan Palace & Pataliputra Archaeology\n● Chandragupta Maurya ka Pataliputra (Patna) wala palace lakdi (wood) se bana tha — ye Bulandibagh\naur Kumrahar (Patna ke pass) sites ki excavation se pata chala hai, jo D.B. Spooner ne conduct ki thi.\n[Q20]\n● Kumrahar site mein ancient Pataliputra ke remains mile hain. Bulandibagh mein Pataliputra ki city-wall\nke remains mile hain. [Q21, Q22]\n5. Chandragupta's Conquests, Empire Extent & Sudarshan Lake\n● Chandragupta Maurya ne Deccan plateau conquer kiya tha — South India ke Jain aur Tamil inscriptions\nse ye prove hota hai. Unhone Malwa, Gujarat aur Maharashtra jeetne wale pehle raja bhi the — unka\nempire Beas se Indus tak, Bengal-Assam (East) se Afghanistan (West) tak, Kashmir (North) se Deccan\nplateau (South) tak phaila hua tha. [Q23, Q24]\n● Sanchi Stupa Chandragupta Maurya se directly associated NAHI hai (isse Ashoka ne banwaya tha).\nSusima Bindusara ka bada beta aur Chandragupta ka pota tha. Vishnugupta, Kautilya ka doosra naam\ntha. Junagadh Rock Inscription mein Chandragupta ke governor Pushyagupta dwara Sudarshan lake\nbanwane ka zikr hai. [Q25]\n● Junagadh Rock Inscription of Rudradaman se prove hota hai ki Western India (Gujarat/Saurashtra)\nChandragupta Maurya ke empire ka hissa thi — isme unke governor Pushyagupta dwara Sudarshan\nlake banwane ka varnan hai. [Q26, Q27]\n● Chandragupta Maurya ne 305 BC mein Seleucus Nicator (jo Sindh-Afghanistan region ke governor the,\nAlexander dwara appoint kiye gaye) ki invading army ko haraya tha. [Q28, Q29]"," ● Sudarshan Lake, Chandragupta Maurya ne apne governor Pushyagupta ke through, Saurashtra ke\nGirnar hills mein banwaya tha. Baad mein Ashoka, Rudradaman aur Skandagupta ne is lake ki\nrepair/renovation ki. Chandragupta hi Girnar area mein lake banwane wale pehle ruler the. [Q30, Q137,\nQ138]\n● Junagadh rock inscription of Mahakshatrapa Rudradaman (~150 CE) ek aisa inscription hai jisme\nChandragupta Maurya AUR Ashoka — dono ke naam mile hain. Isi mein Ashoka ke governor Tushasp\nka bhi zikr hai jinhone lake se canals nikali thi. [Q139]\n6. Ashoka's Empire — Extent, Territories & Provinces\n● Ashoka ke reign ke aakhri time tak lagbhag poora India unke kingdom ke under aa gaya tha, Assam aur\nextreme South ke kuch hisso ko chhodkar — ye unke rock aur pillar edicts se pata chalta hai. [Q31]\n● Ashoka's empire mein Sri Lanka SHAAMIL NAHI thi — unke 2nd Major Rock Edict ke mutabik Cholas,\nPandyas, Satiyaputras, Keralaputras aur Tamraparni (Sri Lanka) 'edge states/border kingdoms' the,\nMauryan empire ka hissa nahi. [Q34]\n● Ashokan inscriptions mein 'Satavahana' dynasty ka zikr NAHI hai — baaki South Indian border\nkingdoms (Chola, Pandya, Satiyaputra, Keralaputra) ka zikr milta hai. [Q89]\n● Chandragupta ka empire Iran ke north-west se lekar modern North Karnataka (South) tak phaila tha\n(Historian Smith ke mutabik Hindukush mountains iski boundary thi). Ashoka ke inscriptions mein 5\nprovinces ka zikr hai: Uttarapath, Avantiratha, Kalinga, Dakshinapath aur Prachyapatha. Gold coins ko\nregularize karne ka credit Indo-Greek kings ko jaata hai, Mauryans ko nahi. [Q115]\n7. Ashoka's Dhamma, Welfare Measures & Religious Tolerance\n● Ashoka ne 'Rajdharma' ki sthapna 3 principles par ki: Longanimity (tolerance/sahansheelta), Liberty aur\nCompassion (karuna). Unka 'Dhamma' kisi ek community se related nahi tha, balki poori manvta ki\nbhalai ke liye tha. [Q32]\n● Historians (jaise Jha aur Shrimali) ke mutabik, Ashoka ke Dhamma ki spirit Buddhist texts (Lakkhana\nSutta, Rahulovad waghera) se li gayi hai. Unhone apne reign ke 14th saal mein Dhamma-Mahamatras\nappoint kiye the, jo unke social/moral code ko promote karte the. [Q33]\n● Ashoka ne India mein pehla hospital aur herbal gardens banwaye — insaan aur janwar dono ke liye\nmedicinal herbs ke garden, kuen khudwaye, ped lagwaye, aur aborigines/subject races ki dekhbhal ke\nliye ek ministry bhi banayi. [Q36]\n● Buddhist hone ke bawajood, Ashoka ne Hindu dharma mein apni astha nahi chhodi thi — unhe unke\ninscriptions mein 'Devanampriya' (Gods ke pyare, ya khoobsurat) kaha gaya hai, jo unki continued\nHindu belief dikhata hai. Ashoka ka coronation 269 BC mein hua tha. [Q37]\n● 12th Major Rock Edict mein Ashoka ne religious tolerance/harmony ki baat ki — sabhi religious sects ke\nsaath sahishnuta (longanimity) aur unki growth ki baat ki gayi hai. 'Jo apne dharm ki tareef karta hai aur\ndoosro ke dharm ki ninda karta hai' wala famous statement bhi isi edict mein hai. [Q82, Q86, Q87, Q93]\n● 5th Pillar Edict mein Ashoka ne kuch janwaron ko inviolable (na maarne wale) declare kiya, aur specific\nfestive days par fish bechne/maarne par rok lagayi. [Q94]"," 8. Third Buddhist Council & Mauryan Rulers' Religious Beliefs\n● Sinhalese folklore ('Dipavamsa' aur 'Mahavamsa') ke mutabik, Ashoka ke reign mein Pataliputra mein\nTeesra (3rd) Buddhist Council hua tha — iski presidency Moggaliputta Tissa (famous Buddhist\nmendicant) ne ki thi. [Q38, Q39]\n● Mauryan rulers ki religious beliefs: Ashoka aur unke pote Dasaratha Buddhism ke followers the —\nDasaratha ne bhi apne dada Ashoka jaisi 'Devanampiya' title li thi. Chandragupta Maurya apni later\nyears mein Jainism ke follower the, aur Bindusara Ajivika sect ke follower the. [Q40]\n9. Mauryan Central, Revenue & Local Administration\n● Ashoka ke edicts mein mention 3 officers: Yukta (revenue collect karne wale district officials), Rajjuka\n(rural area mein surveyor + judicial function wale officials), aur Pradeshika (division ke top official, jo\ncommissioner jaisa hota tha). 'Agraharika' Mauryan official NAHI tha — ye Gupta/post-Gupta period\nmein Agraharas (Brahmins ko land grants) ka officer hota tha. [Q41, Q44]\n● 'Pradeshtha', Mauryan Justice Department se associated the — crimes rokne ke liye responsible the aur\njudges ki tarah kaam karte the. 'Sarthwah' merchants ke ek convoy (kafile) ka head hota tha\n(Arthashastra mein describe kiya gaya). [Q42, Q43]\n● 'Bhaga' aur 'Bali' ancient India mein revenue ke sources the — Arthashastra ke mutabik King zameen\nka malik hota tha, aur land produce mein King ka hissa 'Bhaga' kehlaata tha. [Q116]\n● 'Sitadhyaksha' Mauryan empire mein agricultural land ke head the, jo land revenue collect karte the —\nis se collect hone wale tax ko 'Sita' (crown land se revenue) kehte the. Agronomoi district officers the;\nShulkadhyaksha trade/service taxes collect karte the; Akradhyaksha mines control karte the. [Q117,\nQ118]\n● Ancient India mein pasture-land (charagah) par lagne wale tax ko 'Vivit' (Vivita) kaha jaata tha — is land\nke officer ko 'Vivitadhyaksha' kehte the. [Q119]\n● Mauryan Mantriparishad (ministerial council) mein revenue collection 'Samaharta' regulate karte the.\nAntapal border forts dekhte the, aur Pradeshtha commissionaries ke administrator the. [Q120]\n● Mauryan officer 'Pautavadhyaksha' weights aur measures (tol-maap) dekhte the. Panyadhyaksha\nCommerce Department ke, Sitadhyaksha Agriculture Department ke, aur Sunadhyaksha slaughterhouse\nke head the. [Q121]\n● Mauryan officer 'Agronomai' revenue collect karte the, irrigation monitor karte the, legal administration\nkarte the, aur roads ki construction bhi dekhte the. [Q122]\n● 'Pankodakasannirodhe' Mauryan administration mein ek penalty thi — road par gandagi/paani jama\nkarne (slushing) ke liye lagayi jaati thi. [Q123]\n● Officer match: Talar → Night guards ka officer; Pattakola → Village tax collector; Sahsadhipati →\nDacoity cases ke officer; Baladhip → Octroi ka guard. [Q124]\n● Arthashastra ke mutabik Mauryan judicial system mein 2 tarah ki courts thi: 'Dharmasthiya' (modern civil\ncourts jaisi) aur 'Kantakshodhana' (modern criminal courts jaisi). [Q126]\n● Mauryan emperors ne religion ke basis par kabhi land-grants nahi diye the (sahi Assertion) — lekin\npeasants ne land-grants ke against revolt kiya, aisa koi historical evidence nahi milta (galat Reason).\n[Q97]"," ● Village administration, autonomous elected panchayats ke through, Dravids (South India ke Cholas) ne\nevolve kiya tha — ye local self-government ke liye famous system tha. [Q128]\n● Mauryan era mein cities ki administration 'Nagrak' ya 'Purmukhya' ke through hoti thi. Megasthenes ke\nmutabik 6 committees the (5-5 members ki), jisme se 3rd committee birth-death registration dekhti thi —\nye kaam aaj bhi municipal administration hi karti hai. [Q113]\n10. Mauryan Art & Architecture\n● Sarnath Pillar Ashoka ne banwaya tha — iske upar 4 sheron ka symbol hai (power ka pratik), jo India ka\nNational Emblem bhi hai. Ye Chunar sandstone se bane hain — Mauryan architecture ka best example.\n[Q45]\n● Sanchi Stupa (Raisen dist., MP) ko architecture ke perspective se best Stupa maana jaata hai — ise\nAshoka ne 3rd century BC mein banwaya tha. Stupa ka 4th century CE Gupta inscription mein naam\n'Kaknam/Kakanam Mahavihara' hai — yaha total 3 stupas hain. [Q46, Q47, Q48, Q49]\n● Bharhut (MP) ka Stupa, Shunga architecture ka fine example hai — ise shayad Ashoka ne banwaya\ntha, lekin iske carved gateways/railings 150 BC ke aas-paas Shunga period mein add kiye gaye. [Q50]\n● Sanchi Stupa ke ek gateway (Torana) mein Ashoka ki apni 2 queens ke saath Bodhi Tree ki pilgrimage\ndikhayi gayi hai — ye Toranas important Buddhist events ki visual kahaniyan batate hain. [Q51]\n● Ashokan stone pillars architectural structures ka hissa NAHI hote (jaise ki kisi building ki chhat support\nkarne wale pillars) — ye alag se khade hue monuments hote hain, highly polished, monolithic (ek hi\npatthar se bane) aur tapering shaft (upar se patla) wale hote hain. [Q71]\n● Parkham (Mathura ke pass) se Manibhadra (Yaksha) naam ka inscribed idol mila hai — ye Mauryan\nidols mein se ek hai, Mathura art ka important artefact hai, ab Mathura museum mein hai. [Q142]\n● Pairs check: Lothal → Ancient Dockyard (sahi); Sarnath → Buddha ka pehla sermon (sahi); Nalanda →\nBuddhist learning ka bada centre (sahi). Lekin Rajgir → Lion Capital of Ashoka GALAT hai — Lion\nCapital actually Sarnath mein hai. [Q143]\n11. Ashoka's Pilgrimage & Associated Buddhist Sites\n● Buddhist site match: Kaushambi → Ghositarama Monastery; Kushinagar → Ranabhar Stupa; Sarnath\n→ Dhamek Stupa; Shravasti → Sahet-Mahet. [Q52]\n● Buddhism accept karne ke baad, Ashoka ne shikaar chhodkar 'Dhamma Yatra' (pilgrimage trips) shuru\nki — coronation ke 10 saal baad Bodhgaya gaye, aur 20 saal baad Lumbini gaye. Historian Vincent\nArthur Smith ne apni book mein Ashoka ki dhamma-yatra ka route describe kiya hai. [Q53]\n● Rummindei Pillar, Ashoka ne apne coronation ke 20th saal ke baad Lumbini visit karke Buddha ki janm-\nsthaan mark karne ke liye khada karwaya tha — unhone Lumbini ka Bali tax maaf kar diya aur land\nrevenue 1/6 se 1/8 kar diya. [Q76]\n12. Ashokan Inscriptions — Scripts & Decipherment"," ● Ashoka ke zyadatar inscriptions Prakrit language aur Brahmi script mein hain. Sirf Shahbazgarhi aur\nMansehra (Peshawar ke pass, ab Pakistan mein) ke inscriptions Kharosthi script mein hain — Taxila se\nek Aramaic script wala inscription bhi mila hai, aur Shar-i-Kuna (Kandhar) inscription Greek-Aramaic\nbilingual hai. [Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57, Q64]\n● Brahmi script sabse pehle stone tablets (rock edicts) par likhe letters se decipher hui thi — Sir James\nPrinsep ne 1837 mein ye kaam kiya tha, wo is field ke pehle British scholar the. [Q58, Q59, Q60, Q61, Q62,\nQ63]\n● Pre-Ashokan Brahmi script Anuradhapura (Sri Lanka) mein mili hai. India mein Piprahwa, Sohgaura aur\nMahasthan se bhi is tarah ki script ke evidence mile hain. [Q65]\n● Kharosthi script ancient India mein right-to-left likhi jaati thi — ye mainly north-west India ki script thi. Iski\nstudy James Prinsep (1835) aur Friedrich Grotefend ne shuru ki thi. [Q66, Q67]\n13. Ashokan Inscriptions — Names, Epithets & Personal Mentions\n● Ashoka apne inscriptions mein 'Priyadarshi' (Piyadasi) ya 'Devanampiya Piyadasi' naam se refer hote\nhain — matlab 'Gods ke pyare'. Puranas mein unhe 'Ashok Vardhan' bhi kaha gaya hai. [Q68, Q69, Q70]\n● Kanganahalli Buddhist stupa (Bhima river, Kalaburagi dist., Karnataka) mein 'Ranyo Ashoka' (King\nAshoka) likha ek stone portrait mila hai, unki Queen ke saath — ye Brahmi script mein hai. [Q72]\n● Ashoka ka personal naam sirf kuch specific edicts mein explicitly likha hai: Gujarra, Maski, Nettur aur\nUdagolam. Total 40+ Ashokan edicts jaane jaate hain, lekin sabme unka naam nahi likha — zyadatar\nsirf 'Devanampiya Piyadasi' hi likha hota hai. [Q73, Q74, Q75]\n● Gujarra Minor Rock Edict, Datia district (MP) mein hai — Ujjain se Bharuch jaane wale main road par\nsituated hai, isme Ashoka ka naam explicitly likha hai. [Q77]\n● Bhabru (Bairat) Pillar/inscription hi ekmatra jagah hai jaha Ashoka khud ko 'Piyadasi Raja Magadha'\n(Magadha ke raja) declare karte hain — ye unhe ek Buddhist prove karta hai. [Q78]\n14. Ashokan Inscriptions — Locations Across India\n● Kalsi (Dehradun dist., Uttarakhand) apne famous Ashokan rock edict ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q79, Q80]\n● Ashoka ke major rock edicts ke sites-states: Dhauli → Odisha, Erragudi → Andhra Pradesh — ye 2\npairs sahi hain. Jaugada Odisha mein hai (MP mein nahi), aur Kalsi Uttarakhand mein hai (Karnataka\nmein nahi). [Q81]\n● Junagadh Inscription of Mahakshatrapa Rudradaman mein Ashoka ke edicts bhi milte hain — Uparkot\nfort (Junagadh) ke pass ek badi boulder par Ashoka ke 14 edicts, saath hi Rudradaman aur\nSkandagupta ke inscriptions bhi hain. [Q140]\n● Barabar hill caves (Jahanabad dist., Bihar) monks ke rehne ke liye rocks se banayi gayi thi — inme se 3\ncaves par Ashoka ke inscriptions milte hain, Ajivikas ko dedicate karte hue. Ye caves Mauryan period\n(321-184 BC, ~4th-3rd century BC) ki hain, 6th century BC ki NAHI. [Q141]\n15. The Kalinga War & Key Rock Edicts"," ● Kalinga War aur uski victory, Ashoka ke reign ke sabse bade events the — 13th Rock Edict isse clearly\ndescribe karta hai. Isme bataya gaya hai ki King Piyadasi (Ashoka) ne apni coronation ke 8 saal baad\n(261 BC) Kalinga jeeta, aur uske baad gehra pashchatap (remorse) feel kiya. [Q83, Q84, Q85]\n● Assertion-Reason: Ashoka ne Kalinga ko Mauryan Empire mein annex kiya (sahi) — kyunki Kalinga log\nIndian Ocean par control rakhte the aur East ki taraf Magadhan merchants ke liye sea routes restrict\nkarte the, saath hi Gangetic valley se Deccan tak ke land routes bhi control karte the (sahi Reason, jo\nAssertion ko explain karta hai). [Q96]\n16. South Indian Kingdoms Mentioned in Ashokan Edicts\n● South Indian kingdoms ka zikr Ashoka ke Second Major Rock Edict mein milta hai — Pandyas,\nSatiyaputra, Keralaputra aur Chola kingdoms, jo independent border kingdoms the. [Q35]\n● Sangam Kingdom (Chola, Pandya, Satiyaputta, Keralaputta aur Tamraparni) ka zikr Ashoka ke Rock\nEdict II aur XIII — dono mein milta hai. [Q88]\n17. Foreign Relations — Megasthenes & Diplomatic Ties\n● Ashoka ke 13th inscription se pata chalta hai ki unke 5 Yavana (Greek) kings ke saath cordial relations\nthe — inme se ek Turamaya (Ptolemy II Philadelphus) Egypt ke raja the. [Q90, Q91]\n● Mauryan dynasty ke rulers (Ashoka aur Bindusara) ne Syria aur Egypt jaise Hellenistic kingdoms ke\nsaath diplomatic relations banaye the. [Q92]\n● Megasthenes, Greek ambassador, Seleucus Nicator ke representative ki tarah 4th century BC mein\nIndia aaye the — wo Chandragupta Maurya ke darbar mein rahe, aur apni book 'Indica' mein\nChandragupta ke reign ke baare mein likha. [Q98, Q99, Q100]\n18. Megasthenes' 'Indica' — Society, Economy & City Administration\n● Megasthenes ki book 'Indica' Chandragupta Maurya ke darbar ke observations par based hai. Unhone\nIndian society ko 7 categories mein baata: Philosophers, Farmers, Herdsmen, Artisans, Military\n(Soldiers), Overseers, aur Councillors. Unhone slavery ka zikr nahi kiya, aur bataya ki koi bhi apni caste\nse bahar shaadi ya occupation nahi kar sakta tha. [Q101, Q102, Q104]\n● Megasthenes ne apni 'Indica' mein likha ki ancient India mein slavery NAHI thi. [Q103]\n● Megasthenes ke mutabik, Indian philosophers 2 groups mein bate the: Brahmins (jo Brahman ke gyan\nse moksha maante the) aur Shramanas (jo ascetic practices se moksha maante the). [Q105]\n● Megasthenes ke Indica ke mutabik, Pataliputra town ek 30-member municipal council se govern hoti thi,\njo 6 committees mein baati thi — 6th committee sales tax collect karti thi, aur tax evasion karne walon\nko death penalty milti thi. [Q106]\n● Pataliputra ki administration ka description Megasthenes ki 'Indica' mein milta hai — unhone 6\ncommittees (5-5 members ki) ka zikr kiya hai jo Pataliputra ki administration dekhti thi. Town officials ko\n'Astynomi' kehte the. [Q107, Q108]"," ● Megasthenes ki book ka naam 'Indica' hai — isi ke author khud Megasthenes hain. [Q109, Q110, Q111,\nQ112]\n19. Ancient Records, Learning Centres & Social Groups\n● Sohgaura Copper-plate (Gorakhpur, UP) India ka sabse purana known record hai jisme food-grains ko\npreserve karne ka royal order likha hai — Mahasthan Inscription (Bogura dist., Bangladesh) mein bhi\nfamine ke dauran relief measures ka zikr hai. [Q95]\n● Taxila, Mauryan period ke dauran learning ka sabse famous centre tha — poori duniya se Hindu aur\nBuddhist students yahan padhne aate the. (Nalanda baad mein Gupta period mein important bana.)\n[Q125]\n● Ancient India mein Chronicles, dynastic histories aur epic tales yaad rakhne ka kaam 'Sutas' aur\n'Maagadha' (bards/genealogists) karte the. [Q127]\n20. Administrative Tiers, Social Norms & Foreign Travellers\n●\n Disputed: Kautilya ke mutabik Mauryan rural administrative tier ka sahi ascending order hai:\n⚠️\nSamgrahana → Karvatika → Dronamukh → Sthaniya (Sthaniya sabse top par tha, 800 villages ka;\nDronamukh 400 villages ka; Karvatika 200 villages ka). Diye gaye options mein se koi bhi ye sahi order\nmatch nahi karta. [Q114]\n● Kautilya's Arthashastra apne pati se chhodi gayi (deserted) wife ko divorce lene ki anumati deta hai —\nMauryan period mein divorce prevalent tha. Pati ke lambe samay tak videsh mein rehne ya physically\nhandicapped hone par wife ko divorce ka adhikar tha. [Q129]\n● Manusmriti (38th part) ke mutabik, ek vidhwa (widow husband) ko dobara shaadi (remarriage) karne ka\nadhikar NAHI tha, lekin ek widower (jiski patni mar chuki ho) dobara shaadi kar sakta tha. [Q130]\n● Manu ke mutabik, foreigner invaders (jaise Shakas, Kushanas, Hunas, Pratihar) jo priestly customs\nfollow nahi karte the, unhe 'Fallen Kshatriyas' (Vratya Kshatriya) ka social status diya gaya tha. [Q131]\n● India aane wale foreign travellers ka chronological order: Megasthanes (Chandragupta Maurya ke\ndarbar mein, ~302 BC) → Fa-Hien (Chandragupta II Vikramaditya ke reign mein, early 5th century AD)\n→ Hieun-Tsang (Harshavardhana ke darbar mein, 7th century AD) → I-Tsing (Hieun-Tsang ke baad,\nlate 7th century AD). [Q132]\n21. Later Mauryan Rulers, Epithets & the Empire's End\n● Ruler-Epithet match: Chandragupta Maurya → 'Sandrocottus' (Justin aur Greek authors ke mutabik);\nBindusara → 'Amitrachates/Amitraghat'; Ashoka → 'Piyadasi'; Chanakya → 'Vishnugupta'. [Q133]\n● Aakhri Mauryan Emperor Brihadratha the — unhe unke commander Pushyamitra Shunga ne 184 BC\nmein assassinate kar diya, aur Shunga Dynasty ki sthapna ki. [Q134]\n● Dynasties ka chain: Pushyamitra Shunga ne last Mauryan king Brihadratha ko 184 BC mein maara aur\nShunga dynasty banayi. Shunga dynasty ke last king Devabhuti ko unke minister (Amatya) Vasudeva\nKanva ne conspiracy se maara aur Kanva dynasty banayi. Vayupurana ke mutabik, Kanva dynasty ke"," last ruler Susharma ko unke Andhrian servant Simuk (Sindhuk) ne deposed kiya, aur Satavahana\ndynasty banayi. [Q135]\n● 'Pranayam' (Pranay) Mauryan period mein ek emergency tax tha — financial zaroorat ya war ke time\nstate dwara logo se collect kiya jaata tha. [Q136]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Maurya Empire Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0178","t":"01 Muslim Invasion of India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUSLIM INVASION OF INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Prophet & the Origin of the Word 'Hindu'\n2. The First Arab Invasion — Muhammad-Bin-Qasim & the Chachnama\n3. Mahmud of Ghazni — Ghaznavid Origins & Invasions\n4. Mahmud's Court — Firdausi, Al-Biruni & Utbi\n5. The Somnath Temple\n6. Muhammad Ghori's Conquests\n7. Establishment of Turkish Rule — Iqta System & the Conquest of Bengal-Bihar\n8. Reasons for the Success of Turkish Invasions\n1. The Prophet & the Origin of the Word 'Hindu'\n● Hazrat Muhammad (Islam ke Prophet) ka janm ~570 AD mein, Saudi Arabia ke Mecca sheher mein hua\ntha — unki mrityu 632 AD mein hui. Mecca, Saudi Arabia ke Hejazi region mein hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● 'Hindu' word (Hind/India ke logo ke liye) sabse pehle Arabians ne use kiya tha — zyadatar scholars\nmaante hain ki ye naam invaders ne Indus river ka sahi uchcharan na kar paane ki wajah se pada.\nRigveda mein Bharat ko 'Sapta Sindhu' kaha gaya hai, Iranians ne ise 'Hindustan' aur Greeks ne 'India'\nkaha. [Q3]\n2. The First Arab Invasion — Muhammad-Bin-Qasim & the Chachnama\n●\n Disputed: India par pehla successful Muslim invasion ki exact date par dispute hai — Muhammad-\n⚠️\nBin-Qasim 712 AD mein Sindh ke coast par pahunche the aur Raja Dahir ko haraakar maar diya. V.D.\nMahajan ke mutabik ye date 711 AD hai, lekin Harish Chandra jaise doosre historians alag date maante\nhain. [Q4, Q5]\n● Muhammad-Bin-Qasim India ke pehle successful Muslim invader the — 8th century ki shuruat mein\nunhone Sindh ke ek hisse par successfully attack kiya. Arab empire Sindh-Multan se aage East ki taraf\nphail nahi payi, aur dheere-dheere decline ho gayi. [Q6, Q7]\n● Muhammad-Bin-Qasim ek Arab the — unka janm ~695 AD mein hua. Wo Iraq ke King Al-Hajjaj ke\nbhatije aur damad the — 17 saal ki age mein Caliph-al-Walid ne unhe Sindh (India) par army lead karne\nbheja. [Q8]\n● 'Chachnama' (Raja Chach ki story) ke mutabik, Arod hi 6th-7th century AD mein Indus country ki capital\nthi — Chach ke bete Dahir ne Muhammad Bin Qasim ke invasion ke against Sindh ki raksha ki thi. [Q9]\n● 'Chachnama' originally Arabic mein likhi gayi thi (author clearly pata nahi) — iska Persian translation\nMuhammad Ali Bin Abu Bakr Kufi ne kiya. Ye Sindh ki history (680-718 AD) describe karti hai — English\ntranslation 1900 AD mein Mirza Kalich Beg ne ki. [Q10]\n3. Mahmud of Ghazni — Ghaznavid Origins & Invasions"," ● Ghaznavid dynasty ke founder Alptigin the — ek Turkish slave (Samanid governor), jinhone apna\nindependent kingdom banaya, Ghazni ko capital banakar. [Q11]\n● Assertion-Reason: Mahmud Ghazni ne India par 17 baar invasion kiya (sahi Assertion, 1000-1027 AD\nke beech) — lekin unka maksad koi permanent Muslim rule establish karna NAHI tha (galat Reason),\nbalki wo ek ruthless plunderer the jo India ki wealth loot karne aate the. [Q12]\n● Chandela dynasty famous hai King Vidyadhar ke liye — unhone 1019-20 AD mein Mahmud Ghaznavi\nke attacks ko successfully rok diya tha. Chandelas ne 9th-13th century tak Central India par raj kiya —\nunki pehli capital Khajuraho thi, baad mein Mahoba shift hui. [Q13, Q14]\n● Mahmud Ghazni ne bilingual silver coins issue kiye the — ek taraf Arabic aur doosri taraf Sanskrit\ninscriptions, local logo ke saath trade badhane ke liye. [Q25]\n● Muslim invaders ka chronological order: Mahmud Ghaznavi (1000-1027 AD, 17 baar attack) →\nMuhammad Ghori (pehla attack 1175 AD, 1205 AD tak empire badhaya) → Genghis Khan (1221 AD,\nIltutmish ke reign mein, Jalaluddin Mingburni ka peecha karte hue India tak aaye) → Taimur (1398 AD,\nTughlaq dynasty ke time Delhi ko loot-tabaah kiya). [Q32]\n4. Mahmud's Court — Firdausi, Al-Biruni & Utbi\n● Mahmud of Ghazni (17 baar India par raid karne wale plunderer) ne apne Afghanistan kingdom mein\nart-culture ko bahut patronize kiya — unke court ke 3 prominent vyakti the: Firdausi (Persian poet,\n'Homer of the East', unhone 'Shahnama' likhi), Al-Biruni (Central Asia ke brilliant scholar, unhone\n'Tahqiq-I-Hind' likhi), aur Utbi (court historian, unhone Kitab-ul-Yamni aur Tarikh-i-Yamini likhi). [Q15,\nQ17]\n●\n Disputed: 'Shahnama' ke author Firdausi hain, Firishta NAHI — Firishta ne ek alag authentic book\n⚠️\n'Tareekh-i Firishta' likhi thi (unka poora naam Muhammad Qasim Hindushah Astarabadi Firishta tha, wo\nMurtza Nizam Shah ke court mein rahe). [Q16]\n● Al-Biruni Puranas padhne wale pehle Muslim the — wo sirf historian hi nahi the, balki Astronomy,\nGeography, Medicine, Mathematics, Reasoning, Religion aur Theology mein bhi deeply interested the.\nUnhone Sanskrit seekhi aur Indian religious culture ka gehra adhyayan kiya. [Q18]\n● 11th century AD mein, Al-Biruni ('father of Indian Historical writing') Mahmud of Ghazni ke saath India\naaye the aur kai saal yahan rahe — unhone Patanjali ka Yoga-Sutra Arabic mein translate kiya ('Kitab\nPatanjal'), aur unki most important work 'Tahqiq-I-Hind' (Reality of Hindustan) thi, jisme India ki socio-\ncultural condition ka description hai. [Q19, Q20, Q21]\n●\n Trap: Al-Biruni ko ek 'secular author' nahi kaha ja sakta — unhone 1025/1026 mein Mahmud Ghazni\n⚠️\n\nke Somnath temple raid par kabhi sympathetic reference nahi diya. Baaki statements sahi hain: unki\nwritings Indian culture se influenced thi, unhone Sanskrit seekhi, aur wo trigonometry samet\nmathematics ke expert the. [Q22]\n5. The Somnath Temple\n● Mahmud Ghazni ke 1025/26 AD ke attack (Somnath Temple par) ke baad, Bhimadeva-I\n(Chaulukya/Solanki dynasty ke raja) ne temple ko reconstruct karwaya. [Q23]\n● Somnath Temple Gujarat mein, Arabian Sea ke kinare situated hai — ye 12 Jyotirlingas mein se ek hai.\nAl-Biruni ne apni travelogue mein is temple ka description diya hai, uski wealth aur importance highlight"," karte hue. India ke pehle President Dr. Rajendra Prasad (S. Radhakrishnan NAHI) 1951 mein present-\nday temple ki Pran Pratishtha ke waqt maujood the. [Q24]\n6. Muhammad Ghori's Conquests\n● Shihabuddin Muhammad Ghori (Central Asia ke Ghurid dynasty ruler) ne 1192 AD mein North India\nconquer kiya — unka pehla attack 1175 AD mein Multan par hua tha, phir 1175-76 mein Multan-Uch,\naur 1178 mein Gujarat par. 1191 AD mein Prithviraj Chauhan se pehli ladai (Tarain) mein haare, lekin\n1192 mein doosri ladai (Tarain) mein Prithviraj ko haraya. [Q26]\n● Muhammad Ghori ki India mein pehli badi haar Gujarat ke Hindu ruler Mularaja-II (Bhimadev-II) ke\nhaath 1178 AD mein 'Battle of Kasahrada' mein hui thi — Mularaja-II ek chhota bachcha tha, unki maa\nNaika Devi hi actual regent thi jinhone army lead karke Ghori ko decisively haraya, isliye Ghori ne\ndobara Gujarat par attack ki koshish nahi ki. [Q27]\n● Muhammad Ghori ne Kannauj ke Gahadavala king Jayachandra (Jaichand) ko 1194 AD mein 'Battle of\nChandawar' mein haraya — ye ladai Chandawar (aaj ke Firozabad dist., UP) mein, Yamuna river ke\nkinare, Agra ke pass ladi gayi thi. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n● 'Second Battle of Tarain' (1192 AD) ne India mein Muslim domination ki foundation rakhi — Muhammad\nGhori ne Prithviraj Chauhan ki Rajput army ko haraya. Is battle ke baad Muslim power North India mein\nstrongly enrooted ho gayi — ise Indian history ka ek turning point maana jaata hai. [Q31]\n● Muhammad Ghori ke coins par ek taraf Devi Lakshmi ki image hoti thi, doosri taraf Arabic mein Kalma\nlikha hota tha — inhe 'Lakshmi type' coins kehte hain, jo naye-conquer kiye gaye Hindu territories mein\ncontinuity aur wide acceptance ke liye issue kiye gaye the. [Q33]\n7. Establishment of Turkish Rule — Iqta System & the Conquest of Bengal-\nBihar\n● Muhammad Ghori ki jeeto ke turant baad, North India mein 'Iqta system' establish hui — 1192 AD mein\nunhone apne trusted slave Qutb-ud-din-Aybak ko apni Indian territories ka pehla Iqtadar (in-charge)\nbanaya. Aybak ne doosri Tarain ladai mein important role play kiya tha, isliye khush hokar Ghori ne\nunhe Kuhram aur Samana ka administrator banaya. [Q34]\n● Muhammad Ghori aur Aybak ne shuru mein Bihar-Bengal conquer karne ka plan nahi banaya tha — ye\nkaam unke military general/slave Bakhtiyar Khalji (Ikhtiyar Uddin Muhammad-Bin-Bakhtiyar) ne kiya.\n1193-1203 AD ke beech unhone Bihar conquer kiya aur Vikramshila-Nalanda jaisi universities destroy\nki, capital Odantpur capture ki. Phir 1198-1203 mein Bengal attack kiya — raja Lakshman Sen bina lade\nbhaag gaya, aur Turkish army ne capital Nadiya mein bahut loot machayi. [Q35]\n● Bakhtiyar Khalji Bihar ke pehle Muslim conqueror the (~1193 AD) — unhe Bihar mein Turk rule ka 'real\nfounder' bhi maana jaata hai. [Q36, Q37]\n● Ancient education centre 'Nalanda Vihar' ko Bakhtiyar Khalji ne brutally destroy aur jala diya tha. [Q38]\n8. Reasons for the Success of Turkish Invasions"," ● Assertion-Reason: Turkish invasions India mein successful rahi (sahi Assertion) — iski sabse badi\nwajah thi India mein constant warfare aur political unity ki kami (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain\nkarta hai). Us waqt India (North aur West mein) chhote-chhote conflicting kingdoms mein bata hua tha,\njisse Turks ke liye conquer karna aasan ho gaya. [Q39, Q40]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Muslim Invasion of India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0179","t":"10 Delhi Sultanate Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n📋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Sports, Culture & Court Life\n2. Administrative Departments & Institutions — Match Lists\n3. Religious Tolerance & Diversity Among Rulers\n4. Rulers, Consorts & Regional Kingdoms — Not-Correctly-Matched Pairs\n5. Foreign Travellers — Countries, Chronology & Profiles\n6. Religious & Social Terminology\n7. Early Reference to the Magnetic Compass\n8. Chronological Order of Rulers & Historical Events\n9. Famous Battles of Indian History — Match Lists\n10. Royal Authors of Ancient & Medieval India\n11. Delhi Sultanate Dynasties — Duration\n12. Nobles in Sultanate Service — Ain-ul-Mulk Multani\n13. Rajput Customs — The Practice of Jauhar\n14. Jain Scholars in Medieval Courts\n15. Agriculture in Medieval India (13th-14th Century)\n16. Village Administration — Local Officials\n1. Sports, Culture & Court Life\n● Polo (Chaugan) khel India mein Turks laaye the — Qutbuddin Aybak (Slave dynasty ke founder) ko\nPolo khelne ka bahut shauk tha. Unki mrityu 1210 AD mein isi khel ke dauran, ghode se girkar, injuries\nki wajah se hui thi. [Q1]\n2. Administrative Departments & Institutions — Match Lists\n● Match: Firuz Tughluq → 5 canals ka massive network banaya; Balban → Persian New Year festival\n'Nawruz' Delhi darbar mein introduce ki; Alauddin Khalji → market control policies ke liye 'Diwan-i-\nRiyasat' department banayi; Jahangir → British Ambassador Sir Thomas Roe ko apne darbar mein\nreceive kiya. [Q2]\n● Match: Akbar → Ain-i-Dahsala (Land revenue system); Muhammad Tughluq → Token Currency\n(copper/bronze coins ka failed experiment); Iltutmish → Chahalgani nobles ka group (Turkan-i-\nChahalghani) banaya; Sher Shah Suri → Sadak-i-Azam (Grand Trunk Road, Sonargaon se Lahore tak)\nbanwayi. [Q23]\n3. Religious Tolerance & Diversity Among Rulers\n● Delhi Sultanate ke Sultan Nasiruddin Khusrau Shah ke chhote se reign mein, royal palaces mein Hindu\ndevi-devtaon ki pooja hone ki baat kahi jaati hai — Khusrau Shah originally Hindu (Baradu caste) the, jo\nIslam apnaakar Sultan bane the. Unhone Mubarak Shah Khalji ki hatya karke gaddi hasil ki thi. [Q3]\n4. Rulers, Consorts & Regional Kingdoms — Not-Correctly-Matched Pairs"," ●\n Trap: 'Hamida Banu Begum' Alauddin Khilji ki patni NAHI thi — wo Mughal Emperor Humayun ki\n⚠️\nqueen consort thi, aur Akbar (teesre Mughal emperor) ki maa thi. [Q4]\n●\n Trap: 'Chand Bibi' Oudh (Awadh) se related NAHI thi — wo ek Muslim woman warrior thi jinhone\n⚠️\nAkbar ki Mughal forces se Ahmednagar ki raksha ki thi, aur Bijapur ki Regent bhi rahi thi. Baaki pairs\nsahi hain: Bahadur Shah — Gujarat ke raja the, Raziyya Sultan — Delhi ki rani thi, Baz Bahadur —\nMalwa ke aakhri Sultan the. [Q12]\n5. Foreign Travellers — Countries, Chronology & Profiles\n●\n Trap: Abdur Razzaq, Turkey se NAHI, balki Persia (Iran) se the — wo ek Persian ambassador the jo\n⚠️\n\nVijayanagara Empire ke Deva Raya-II (1422-46 AD) ke reign mein aaye the. Baaki pairs sahi hain: Ibn\nBattuta — Morocco (Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke reign mein); Marco Polo — Venice (Italy); Fernao\nNuniz — Portugal (Vijayanagara visit ki). [Q5]\n● Foreign travellers ke India aane ka sahi chronological order: Al-Biruni (11th century, Mahmud of Ghazni\nke saath) → Ibn Battuta (1333-1342 AD, Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke reign mein) → Jean-Baptiste\nTavernier (17th century, French gem merchant, Shahjahan ke period mein) → Niccolao Manucci (1653-\n1708 AD, Italian, Prince Dara Shukoh ke saath). [Q6]\n● Ek passage mein describe kiya gaya traveller Ibn Battuta hai — ek African (Moroccan) traveller jinhone\nSouth Africa, Western Africa, Southern-Eastern Europe, Middle-East Asia, Indian Subcontinent, Middle\nAsia, South-Eastern Asia aur China cross kiya. Unhone apni 30 saal ki yatra mein ~73,000 miles cover\nki — ye Marco Polo se bhi zyada lambi aur vistrit yatra thi. [Q15]\n6. Religious & Social Terminology\n● Sultanate period mein high-position wale religious-judicial authorities (collectively 'Ulema') ko 'Dastar-\nBandan' kaha jaata tha — ye term isliye use hota tha kyunki wo official turban (Dastar) pehente the, jo\nunki high religious-scholarly status dikhata tha. [Q7]\n● Delhi Sultanate ke history mein, Sayyids (Prophet ke descendants, religious thinkers) ko 'Kulah-Daran'\nkaha jaata tha — wo pointed caps ('Kulah') pehente the, isi wajah se ye naam pada. [Q8]\n● Medieval India mein 'Panahi' aur 'Upanah' terms shoes (footwear) ke context mein use hote the. [Q24]\n● Medieval India mein 'Fanam' term South India mein 19th century tak issue hone wale chhote gold coins\nko refer karta tha. [Q25]\n7. Early Reference to the Magnetic Compass\n● Indian seas mein magnetic compass ke use ka sabse purana reference Persian historian-author\nSadiduddin Muhammad Ibn Muhammad 'Aufi' ne diya tha — unki famous story-collection 'Jawami-ul-\nHikayat' mein ye reference milta hai. [Q9]\n8. Chronological Order of Rulers & Historical Events"," ● Rulers ka sahi chronological order: Raziyya Sultan (1236-1240 AD, Slave Dynasty) → Alauddin Khalji\n(1296-1316 AD, Khalji Dynasty) → Sher Shah Suri (1540-1545 AD, Sur Empire) → Akbar (1556-1605\nAD, Mughal Empire). [Q10]\n● Events ka sahi order: Qutub Minar ka construction (Aybak ne shuru kiya, early 13th century, Iltutmish ne\ncomplete kiya) → Firuz Tughluq ki mrityu (1388 AD) → Portuguese ka India aana (Vasco-da-Gama,\n1498 AD) → Krishna Deva Raya (Vijayanagara) ka reign (1509-1529 AD). [Q13]\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: 2nd Battle of Tarain (1192 AD, Muhammad Ghori vs Prithviraj\nChauhan) → Jalal-ud-Din Khalji ki hatya (unke bhatije Alauddin ne 1296 AD mein ki) → Afghanpur\nconspiracy (Sultan Ghiyasuddin Tughluq ki mrityu, 1325 AD, Ulugh Khan/Muhammad Bin Tughluq par\nilzaam) → Muhammad Tughluq ki capital transfer (Delhi se Daulatabad, ~1327 AD). [Q14]\n● Sayyid dynasty ke Sultans ka sahi chronological order: Khizr Khan (1414-1421 AD) → Mubarak Shah\n(1421-1434 AD) → Muhammad Shah (1434-1445 AD) → Ala-ud-Din Alam Shah (1445-1451 AD). [Q18]\n9. Famous Battles of Indian History — Match Lists\n● Match: Battle of Chandawar → 1194 AD (Muhammad Ghori ne Jaichand ko haraya); Attack of Taimur\n→ 1398 AD (Timur ne Delhi par invade kiya); Battle of Talikota → 1565 AD (Vijayanagara Empire ka\npatan); Battle of Ghaghra → 1529 AD (Babur ne Afghans ko haraya). [Q11]\n● Match: Battle of Plassey → 1757 AD (East India Company vs Nawab Siraj-ud-Daulah); Kalinga War →\n261 BC (Ashoka ne lada); Battle of Haldighati → 1576 AD (Maharana Pratap vs Akbar ki Mughal\nforces); Second Battle of Tarain → 1192 AD (Muhammad Ghori vs Prithviraj Chauhan). [Q22]\n10. Royal Authors of Ancient & Medieval India\n● King-Book match: Mahendravarman (Pallava King) → Mattavilasaprahasana (Sanskrit play);\nKrishnadeva Raya (Vijayanagara) → Amuktamalyada (Telugu); Raja Bhoj (Paramara) →\nSamaranganasutradhar; Somesvara-III (Western Chalukya) → Manasollasa. [Q16]\n11. Delhi Sultanate Dynasties — Duration\n● Khalji Dynasty (1290-1320 AD) ne sabse kam samay (sirf 30 saal) tak raj kiya — ye Delhi Sultanate ki\nsabhi dynasties mein sabse chhota reign period tha. [Q17]\n12. Nobles in Sultanate Service — Ain-ul-Mulk Multani\n● Ain-ul-Mulk Multani (ek powerful noble aur military commander) ne Alauddin Khalji, Muhammad bin\nTughlaq aur Firuz Shah Tughlaq ke under service ki — Alauddin ne unhe 1305 AD mein Central India\nbheja jaha unhone Malwa conquer ki. Wo Iltutmish (jo bahut pehle, 1211-1236 AD, raj karte the) ke\nunder NAHI the. [Q19]"," 13. Rajput Customs — The Practice of Jauhar\n● Hindu-Muslim conflict ke dauran, Rajputs ne mass self-immolation ka ek distinct form shuru kiya jise\n'Jauhar' kehte hain — Hindu auratein 'captor ki booty' banne se darti thi, isliye capture-rape-torture jaisi\nbeizzati se bachne ke liye Jauhar karti thi. (Sati aur child marriage pehle se hi prevalent thi.) [Q20]\n14. Jain Scholars in Medieval Courts\n● Hemchandra Suri, ek great scholar-polymath aur Jainism ke follower the — unhe Solanki King Jai Singh\nSiddharaj ke saamne introduce kiya gaya aur wo jaldi hi royal court mein prominent ho gaye. Baad mein\nJai Singh ne Mount Abu mein ek Mandap banwaya. [Q21]\n15. Agriculture in Medieval India (13th-14th Century)\n● 13th-14th century mein Indian peasants Maize (makka) cultivate NAHI karte the — Ibn Battuta ke\nmutabik wo generally rice, wheat, sugarcane aur cotton saal mein 3 baar cultivate karte the. Maize\n(corn) India mein bahut baad mein Portuguese laaye the. [Q26]\n16. Village Administration — Local Officials\n● Medieval India mein 'Mahattara' aur 'Pattakila' designations Village Headmen ke liye use hoti thi —\nvillage government village headman (jise 'Gramani' bhi kehte the) ki supervision mein chalti thi. North\nIndia mein unhe 'Garmika' ya 'Grameyaka' bhi kaha jaata tha. [Q27]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0180","t":"11 Provincial Dynasty North India Deccan","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" PROVINCIAL DYNASTIES — NORTH INDIA & DECCAN — FULL MIND MAP\n🏰\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Jaunpur — The Sharqi Dynasty\n2. Kashmir — Zain-ul-Abidin, the 'Akbar of Kashmir'\n3. Rana Kumbha's Court Scholars\n4. Provincial Dynasties — Rulers, States & Capitals Match Lists\n5. Himalayan Provincial States — Geography\n6. The Bahmani Kingdom — Foundation & Capital\n7. Bijapur — The Adil Shahi Dynasty\n8. Ahmadnagar — The Nizam Shahi Dynasty\n9. Golconda — The Qutb Shahi Dynasty\n10. Gujarat Sultanate — Bahadur Shah & the Portuguese\n11. South Indian Provincial Dynasties — Hoysala, Pandya, Yadava & Kakatiya\n12. Rani Rudrama Devi of the Kakatiya Dynasty\n13. Hoysala Monuments — Halebidu & Belur\n14. Deccan Architecture — Gol Gumbad & Tomb Styles\n15. Mandu, Gwalior & Regional Mosque Architecture\n16. Polygars of South India\n1. Jaunpur — The Sharqi Dynasty\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq ne 300 nayi cities banayi thi — Jaunpur unhone apne cousin Muhammad-bin-\nTughluq ki yaad mein basaya tha. Baad mein unhone Malik Sarwar ko us region ka governor banaya,\njinhone independent 'Sharqi Dynasty' ki sthapna ki. [Q1, Q2]\n● Jaunpur, Sharqi Dynasty ke ruler Ibrahim Shah (1402-1440 AD) ke time apni sabse badi height par\npahunchi — unhone ek nayi regional 'Sharqi architecture' style mein kai monuments banwaye. Jaunpur\nko 'Shiraz of the East' ya 'Shiraz-i-Hind' bhi kaha jaata tha. [Q3, Q4]\n● 1394 AD mein Malik Sarwar ne independent Jaunpur state banayi — Hussain Shah is state ke aakhri\nruler the, jinhe Delhi Sultan Bahlul Lodi ne haraakar Jaunpur ko wapas Delhi Sultanate mein annex kar\nliya. [Q5]\n● Assertion-Reason: Ibrahim Shah Sharqi, Sharqi dynasty ke sabse bade ruler the — unke time Jaunpur\nki cultural-educational fame bahut phaili (sahi Assertion) — kyunki Jaunpur education-art ka bada centre\nban gaya tha, isi wajah se ise 'Shiraz-i-Hind' ki title mili (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta\nhai). [Q6]\n2. Kashmir — Zain-ul-Abidin, the 'Akbar of Kashmir'\n● Shahi Khan ne 'Zain-ul-Abidin' ki title lekar 1420 AD mein Kashmir ki gaddi sambhali — unhe medieval\nKashmir ka sabse bada raja maana jaata hai. Unki religious tolerance aur public welfare policy ki wajah\nse unhe 'Akbar of Kashmir' ki title mili. [Q7]\n● Zain-ul-Abidin, India ke pehle Muslim ruler the jinhone Jizya tax khatam ki (Akbar ne ye baad mein\nkiya). [Q8]\n● Kashmir ke liberal ruler Zain-ul-Abidin ne Jizya aur Cow Slaughter — dono khatam kiye. Unhone\nMahabharata aur Rajatarangini jaise texts ko Persian mein translate karwaya. [Q9]"," ● Srinagar (Kashmir) ki Jama Masjid, originally Sikandar Butshikan ne 1400 AD mein banwayi thi, aur\nZain-ul-Abidin ne isse expand-complete kiya. Iska architecture alag styles ka unique mix hai — turrets,\nBuddhist pagodas jaisi similarity (wooden spires), aur doosre elements shaamil hain. [Q10]\n3. Rana Kumbha's Court Scholars\n● Muni Sunder Suri, Natha aur Tilla Bhatt — teeno Mewar ke great Rajput king Rana Kumbha ke darbar\nke prominent scholars the.\n Muni Jin Vijay Suri (Hiravijaya Suri) Kumbha ke court mein NAHI the —\n⚠️\nwo ek Jain scholar the jinhe Mughal emperor Akbar ke darbar mein invite kiya gaya tha. [Q11]\n4. Provincial Dynasties — Rulers, States & Capitals Match Lists\n●\n Trap: Malik Sarwar (Khwaja Jahan), Sharqi Dynasty ke founder the, jinhone Jaunpur (Malwa NAHI)\n⚠️\npar 1394-1479 AD tak raj kiya. Baaki sahi hain: Rana Hamir — Mewar; Rana Chunda (Rao Chunda) —\nMarwar; Malik Raja Farooqi — Khandesh mein Farooqi dynasty ke founder. [Q12]\n● Match: Adil Shahi → Bijapur (Yusuf Adil Shah ne founded ki); Qutb Shahi → Golconda (Quli Qutb Shah\nne founded ki); Nizam Shahi → Ahmednagar (Malik Ahmad ne founded ki); Sharqi Shahi → Jaunpur\n(Malik Sarwar ne founded ki). [Q20]\n●\n Trap: Yusuf Adil Shah, Adil Shahi dynasty ke founder the aur Bijapur ke raja the, Ahmadnagar ke\n⚠️\nNAHI (Ahmadnagar Nizam Shahi ke under thi). Baaki sahi hain: Baz Bahadur — Malwa ke aakhri\nSultan; Qutb Shahi dynasty — Golconda par raj karti thi; Sultan Muzaffar Shah — Gujarat Sultanate ke\nruler the. [Q24]\n5. Himalayan Provincial States — Geography\n●\n Trap: Medieval Indian states-regions ka sahi match: Champaka (Chamba) — Central India mein\n⚠️\nNAHI, Himachal Pradesh mein hai (galat pair). Durgara (Dogra) — Jammu region mein sahi hai. Kuluta\n(Kullu) — Malabar (Kerala) mein NAHI, Himachal Pradesh mein hai (galat pair). Isliye sirf 1 pair\n(Durgara) sahi hai. [Q13]\n6. The Bahmani Kingdom — Foundation & Capital\n● Bahmani Empire (Deccan) ki sthapna Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah (Zafar Khan ya Hasan Gangu bhi\nkehte the) ne 1347 AD mein ki thi — 14th century ki baat hai. Unhone Gulbarga ko apni capital declare\nkarke 'Ahsanabad' naam diya, aur Hindus par se Jizya khatam kiya. [Q14, Q15, Q16, Q18, Q19]\n● Bahmani Kingdom ki pehli capital Gulbarga thi, jise founder Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah ne\n'Ahsanabad' naam diya — baad mein capital shift ho gayi. [Q17]\n7. Bijapur — The Adil Shahi Dynasty"," ● Ibrahim Adil Shah-II (Bijapur Sultanate ke king, jinke reign mein dynasty apne greatest period par\npahunchi) unke Muslim subjects ne unhe 'Jagadguru' ki upadhi di — wo ek skillful administrator, artist,\npoet aur arts ke generous patron the. Sunni Muslim hone ke bawajood, wo doosre religions ke prati\nbahut tolerant (secular) the. [Q21]\n● 'Kitab-i-Nauras' (Book of Nine Rasas), Bijapur ke raja Ibrahim Adil Shah-II ne likhi thi — unhe music\nmein deep interest tha. Ye Deccani language mein likhi gayi, jisme Hindu devi-devtaon aur Muslim\nsaints, dono ki tareef ke songs hain. [Q22]\n8. Ahmadnagar — The Nizam Shahi Dynasty\n● Ahmadnagar Kingdom (Nizam Shahi dynasty) ko Mughal Emperor Shahjahan ne 1632 mein conquer-\nannex kiya — unhone Mahabat Khan ki leadership mein army bhejkar Daulatabad fort capture karwaya\n(Fateh Khan ko rishwat dekar fort surrender karwaya). Aakhri Sultan Hussain Nizam Shah-III ko Gwalior\nFort mein zindagi bhar ke liye qaid kar diya gaya, jisse dynasty khatam ho gayi. [Q23]\n9. Golconda — The Qutb Shahi Dynasty\n● Golconda (Qutb Shahi Dynasty ki capital, 16th-17th century) ke ruins aaj ke Hyderabad (Telangana)\nmein hain — ye apni diamond mines (jaise Koh-i-Noor) ke liye duniya bhar mein famous tha. Baad mein\nMughal Emperor Aurangzeb ne ise conquer kiya. [Q25]\n10. Gujarat Sultanate — Bahadur Shah & the Portuguese\n● Gujarat ke ruler Bahadur Shah ne Portuguese ko Diu surrender kiya tha — Mughal Emperor Humayun\nse badi threat ka saamna karte hue, unhone Portuguese ki madad lene ke liye 'Treaty of Bassein' (1534)\nki. Badle mein unhone Portuguese ko Diu mein fort banane diya — baad mein apni galti realize karke,\nwo ek Portuguese ship par scuffle mein maare gaye. [Q26]\n11. South Indian Provincial Dynasties — Hoysala, Pandya, Yadava & Kakatiya\n●\n Multiple Correct: Capital match — Hoysala: Dwarasamudra (sahi), Pandya: Madurai (sahi).\n⚠️\nKakatiyas Warangal se raj karte the (Devgiri se NAHI), aur Yadavas Devgiri se raj karte the (Warangal\nse NAHI) — isliye ye question 2 sahi options accept karta hai. [Q27, Q28]\n● Hoysala, Gahadavala, Kakatiya, Yadava — inme se KOI bhi dynasty early 8th century AD mein\nestablish NAHI hui thi. Hoysala Empire ne South India mein 10th-14th century tak raj kiya; Gahadavala\nne UP-Bihar ke hisso par 11th-12th century mein; Kakatiya ne Eastern Deccan par 12th-14th century\nmein; Yadava (Seuna) ne 12th-14th century mein (pehle Western Chalukyas ke feudatories the). [Q29]\n● Dynasty-Capital match: Pallava → Kanchi (Kanchipuram); Pandya → Madura (Madurai); Yadava →\nDevagiri (Daulatabad); Kakatiya → Warangal. [Q30]"," 12. Rani Rudrama Devi of the Kakatiya Dynasty\n● Rudrama Devi (Rani Rudramma), Indian history ki bahut kam ruling queens mein se ek thi — wo\nDeccan Plateau ki Kakatiya dynasty se belong karti thi. Unke pita Ganapati Deva ke koi beta nahi tha,\nisliye unhone Rudrama ko apni successor banaya, formally unhe ek male ruler ki tarah present karke.\n[Q31]\n● Sovereign Kakatiya empire Rudradeva (Pratap Rudradev-I) ke time se shuru hui, phir Mahadeva aur\nGanapati Deva aaye. Ganapati Deva ki beti Rudrama Devi ne apne reign mein successfully South Tamil\nNadu ke Pandyas, Orissa ke Eastern Ganga rulers, aur Seuna (Yadava) rulers se challenges ka\nsaamna karke unhe haraya. [Q32]\n13. Hoysala Monuments — Halebidu & Belur\n● Hoysala ke sabse fine aur prominent monuments Halebidu aur Belur (Karnataka) mein hain — Halebidu\nka Hoysaleshwara temple Lord Shiva ko dedicate hai, aur Belur ka Chennakeshava temple Lord Vishnu\nko — dono Hoysala architecture ke peak ko represent karte hain. [Q33]\n● Hoysala Dynasty ki ancient capital 'Dwarasamudra' ka modern naam 'Halebidu' hai — ye Karnataka ke\nHassan district mein hai, apni ornate Hoysala architecture ke liye famous. [Q34]\n14. Deccan Architecture — Gol Gumbad & Tomb Styles\n● 'Gol Gumbad' (Gol Gumbaz), Bijapur ke Sultan Muhammad Adil Shah (Adil Shahi dynasty) ka\nmausoleum hai — 1656 mein complete hua, iske massive dome ko duniya ke sabse bade free-standing\ndomes mein se ek maana jaata hai (Rome ke St. Peter's Basilica ke baad). [Q35]\n● Architecture Match: 'Double Dome' — India mein sabse pehle Sikandar Lodi ki tomb mein use hui.\n'Octagonal Tomb' — Sasaram mein Sher Shah Suri ki tomb ki khaasiyat. 'True arch Tomb' — sabse\npehle Balban ki tomb mein dikhi. 'Gol Gumbad' — Bijapur ke Muhammad Adil Shah ka mausoleum.\n[Q36]\n15. Mandu, Gwalior & Regional Mosque Architecture\n●\n Disputed: Mandu mein koi 'Jantar Mahal' exist NAHI karta — Mandu 'Jahaz Mahal' (Ship Palace) ke\n⚠️\nliye famous hai, jo Malwa ke Sultan Ghiyasuddin Khalji ne banwaya tha. Print/factual error ki wajah se\nMP PSC ne ye question delete kar diya tha. [Q37]\n●\n Disputed: Mandu (MP) ka famous 'Jahaz Mahal' late 15th century mein Malwa Sultan Ghiyas-ud-din\n⚠️\nKhalji ne banwaya tha — lekin unka naam options mein na hone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai.\n[Q38]\n● Gwalior ka 'Gujari Mahal', Tomar Rajput ruler Raja Man Singh Tomar ne apni pyaari patni Mrignayani\n(ek Gurjar princess) ke liye 1486-1516 AD ke beech banwaya tha — aaj ye ek archaeological museum\nhai. [Q39]\n●\n Trap: 'Adina Masjid' (Jami Masjid) Mandu mein NAHI, balki Pandua (Malda district, West Bengal)\n⚠️\nmein hai — ise Sikandar Shah (Bengal ke ruler) ne 1364-1374 AD ke aas-paas banwaya tha. Baaki sahi"," hain: Lal Darwaza Masjid — Jaunpur mein; Dakhil Darwaza — Gour (Bengal) ka gateway; Tin Darwaza\n— Ahmedabad (Gujarat) ka historical gateway. [Q40]\n● Match: Atala Devi Masjid (Jaunpur) → Ibrahim Shah Sharqi; Chhota Sona Masjid (Gour, Bengal) →\nWali Muhammad; Qadam Rasul (Gour, Bengal) → Nusrat Shah; Adina Masjid, Pandua (Bengal) →\nSikandar Shah. [Q41]\n16. Polygars of South India\n● 'Polygars' (Palaiyakkarar) South India mein territorial administrative aur military governors ki ek feudal\ntitle thi — Nayaka rulers (Madurai Nayaks, Kakatiyas, Vijayanagara empire) ne 16th-18th century ke\nbeech regional administration manage karne ke liye inhe appoint kiya. [Q42]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Provincial Dynasty North India Deccan Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0181","t":"12 Bhakti and Sufi Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" BHAKTI & SUFI MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🕉️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Bhakti Movement — Origin & Common Features\n2. Ramananda — Pioneer of Bhakti in North India\n3. Shankaradeva & Vaishnavism in Assam\n4. Schools of Bhakti Philosophy — Vedanta Traditions\n5. Vallabhacharya & Shuddha Advaita\n6. Kabir — Life, Teachings & the Bijak\n7. Other Bhakti Saints — Malukdas & Ghasidas\n8. Chronology of Bhakti Saints\n9. Guru Nanak & the Sikh Religion\n10. Mirabai — Life & Devotion to Krishna\n11. Namdev, Tukaram & the Varkari Sect\n12. Chaitanya Mahaprabhu\n13. Tulsidas — Life & Works\n14. Krishna-Devotion Poets — Raskhan\n15. Figures NOT Associated with the Bhakti Movement\n16. The Chishti Sufi Order — Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti\n17. Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya & His Circle\n18. Other Sufi Orders — Naqshbandi, Suhrawardi, Qadiri & Firdausia\n19. Baba Farid & the Adi Granth\n20. Shaikh Salim Chishti\n21. Sufi Practices, Syncretism & Shrines\n22. Sufi Poets in Hindavi — Jayasi & Others\n23. Christianity — Festivals & Saints\n24. Miscellaneous Trivia — The 12 Jyotirlingas\n1. The Bhakti Movement — Origin & Common Features\n● Bhakti Movement ek Hindu religious movement hai jisme main spiritual practice hai loving devotion —\nye Shaiva Nayanars aur Vaishnava Alvars mein prevalent thi. Ye ancient Dravida (South India) region\nmein shuru hui aur late medieval age mein, jab North India Islamic rule ke under thi, North ki taraf phaili.\nIska philosophical base 8th century mein Adi Shankaracharya ne rakha tha. [Q1]\n● Bhakti culture ka bada resurgence (rebirth) 15th-16th century AD mein hua, jab Kabir, Tulsi, Nanak,\nSurdas, Mirabai jaise saints ne is movement ko encourage kiya. [Q2]\n● Buddha aur Mirabai — dono ka ek common philosophical belief tha ki 'duniya dukh se bhari hai' —\nDukkha (sorrow) Buddhism ke 4 Noble Truths mein pehla hai, aur Mirabai ne bhi apni devotional poetry\nmein worldly attachments ke dard-suffering ko express kiya. [Q3]\n● Sabhi Bhakti Saints ki ek common feature thi — wo apni verses/poetry regional-local languages mein\ncompose karte the, Sanskrit jaisi classical languages mein nahi — isse Hindi, Kannada, Punjabi jaisi\nbhashaon ke development mein bahut yogdan mila. [Q5]\n2. Ramananda — Pioneer of Bhakti in North India\n● 'Jaati-Pati Puchhe Na Koi, Hari Ko Bhaje So Hari Ka Hoi' (koi kisi ka jaati-caste na poochhe) — ye\nfamous dictum Saint Ramananda ka hai. Unhone Bhakti ke darwaze sabke liye khole, caste-religion-\ngender se pare — unke shishya har varna-dharm se the. [Q4]"," ● Ramananda, North India mein Bhakti movement ke pioneer the — unhone Sanskrit ki jagah local\nvernacular (early Hindi/Hindavi) use ki apna message masses tak pahunchane ke liye, isliye wo pehle\nBhakti Saint the jinhone Hindi ka use kiya. [Q18]\n● Ramananda 1299 AD mein Prayag (Prayagraj) mein ek orthodox Kanyakubja Brahmin family mein\npaida hue the. [Q19]\n3. Shankaradeva & Vaishnavism in Assam\n● Kamarupa (aaj ka Assam) mein Vaishnavism 15th-16th century ke saint-scholar Shankaradeva ne\npopularize ki — unhone 'Ekasarana Dharma' (Ekasarana sect) shuru ki, Vishnu-Krishna mein astha\nrakhi, aur elaborate rituals-idolatry ka virodh kiya. Unhe 'Chaitanya of Assam' bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q7]\n● Shankaradeva, Assam ke Vaishnava Cult ke prominent saint the. [Q8]\n● Shankaradeva ne Assam aur Bengal ke Cooch Behar region mein Neo-Vaishnavism (Ekasarana\nDharma) introduce aur popularize ki. [Q9]\n4. Schools of Bhakti Philosophy — Vedanta Traditions\n● Ramanujacharya (11th-12th century), Sri Vaishnavism tradition ke important exponent the — unki\nphilosophy 'Vishishtadvaita' (qualified non-dualism) kehlaati hai, jisme ultimate Brahman sab kuch ka\nsource hai, lekin individual souls aur matter distinct hain. Unke followers 'Vaishnava'/'Sri Vaishnava'\nkehlaate hain. [Q10, Q29]\n● 'Shuddha Advaitvad' (purely non-dual philosophy) Shri Vallabhacharya (Vallabha Sect/Pushtimarg ke\nfounder) ne propound ki — unke mutabik Brahman (Krishna) pure hai, aur duniya-souls usse alag nahi\nhain, koi maya (illusion) nahi hai. [Q11]\n● Philosophy-Founder match (repeated across questions): Advaitavada → Adi Shankaracharya;\nVishishtadvaitavada → Ramanujacharya; Dvaitavada → Madhvacharya; Dvaitadvaitavada →\nNimbarkacharya; Shuddhadvaitavada → Vallabhacharya (Pushtimarg). [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n●\n Trap: Madhvacharya, Dvaita (Dualism) philosophy ke proponent the — unhone Saguna Bhakti\n⚠️\ntradition follow ki (Nirguna Bhakti NAHI), aur Lord Vishnu ko supreme personal deity maankar unki pooja\nki wakalat ki. [Q16]\n5. Vallabhacharya & Shuddha Advaita\n● Mahaprabhu Vallabhacharya, 1479 AD mein, 'Champaranya' (aaj ke Chhattisgarh) ke ek forest mein, ek\nTelugu Brahmin family mein paida hue the — unhone Krishna-centered Pushti sect aur Shuddha\nAdvaita philosophy ki sthapna ki. [Q12]\n6. Kabir — Life, Teachings & the Bijak\n●\n Trap: 'Bijak' Dadu Dayal ki teachings ki composition NAHI hai — ye Kabir ki teachings ka\n⚠️\ncompilation hai, jo Kabirpanthi sect ke followers ka holy scripture hai (Sakhi, Sabad, Ramaini — 3"," sections mein bata hua). Kabir Saint Ramananda ke 12 prominent disciples mein sabse famous the —\nVaranasi mein ek Muslim weaver couple (Neeru-Neema) ne unhe pala tha. [Q17, Q20, Q21]\n● 'Pothi Padh Padh Jag Mua, Pandit Bhaya Na Koye, Dhai Akhar Prem Ka, Padhe So Pandit Hoye'\n(kitaben padhkar koi pandit nahi banta, jo prem ke do-adhe akshar padh le wahi asli pandit hai) — ye\nfamous lines Kabir Das ne likhi thi. [Q22]\n● Kabir aur unke prominent disciple Dharamdas ke beech ke spiritual dialogues ka collection 'Amarmul'\nkehlaata hai. [Q23]\n7. Other Bhakti Saints — Malukdas & Ghasidas\n● Saint Malukdas, ek renowned Bhakti poet, 1574 AD mein Kada (aaj ke Kaushambi dist., Allahabad ke\npass, UP) mein ek Khatri family mein paida hue the. [Q24]\n● Guru Ghasidas (Chhattisgarh ke Satnami sect ke founder), December 1756 AD mein Giraudpuri village\nmein paida hue the — unke parents Mahangudas (Mahangu) aur Amarautin the. [Q25]\n8. Chronology of Bhakti Saints\n● Prominent philosophers-saints ka chronological order: Shankaracharya (8th century, Advaita Vedanta)\n→ Ramanuja (1017-1137 AD, Vishishtadvaita) → Chaitanya (1486-1533 AD, Gaudiya Vaishnavism).\n[Q26]\n● Bhakti Saints ka chronological order (lifetime ke hisaab se): Namdev (1270-1350 AD) → Kabir (1398-\n1518 AD) → Guru Nanak (1469-1539 AD) → Mirabai (1498-1546 AD). [Q27, Q36]\n9. Guru Nanak & the Sikh Religion\n● Guru Nanak (Sikh religion ke founder), Talwandi village (aaj ka Nankana Sahib, Pakistan ke Punjab\nprovince mein) mein paida hue the. [Q30]\n● Guru Nanak (1469-1539 AD) ne Sikh religion ki sthapna Delhi Sultanate ke Lodi dynasty ke reign mein\nki thi — mainly Sikandar Lodi ke reign se overlap karta hai. [Q31]\n● 'God insaan ke guno ko jaanta hai, uski caste nahi poochta, agli duniya mein koi caste nahi hoti!' — ye\nstatement Guru Nanak ne diya, jinhone caste system ko poori tarah reject kiya. Isi belief ko practically\ndikhane ke liye unhone free community kitchen 'Langar' shuru ki, jaha sab log bina bhedbhav ke saath\nkhaate the. [Q32]\n● 1526 AD mein Babur ne first Battle of Panipat mein Ibrahim Lodi ko haraakar Lodi dynasty khatam ki —\nus waqt Guru Nanak (1469-1539 AD) jinda the aur actively preaching kar rahe the. [Q38]\n10. Mirabai — Life & Devotion to Krishna\n●\n Disputed: Mirabai (1498-1546 AD) apni zindagi mein Tulsidas (1532-1623 AD), Guru Nanak (1469-\n⚠️\n1539 AD) aur Chaitanya Mahaprabhu — teeno ki samkalin thi, isliye ye question multiple sahi answers\naccept karta hai. Ramakrishna Paramhansa (1836-1886 AD) bahut baad mein hue the. [Q33]"," ● Mirabai ka janm Rajasthan ke Merta ke Kudaki village mein ek royal family mein hua tha — unki shaadi\nBhojraj se hui, jo Mewar ke famous ruler Rana Sanga ke bade bete the. Kuch saal baad Bhojraj ki\nmrityu ho gayi. [Q34]\n● 'Rag-Govind' text great Krishna devotee-poetess Mirabai ne compose ki thi. [Q35]\n11. Namdev, Tukaram & the Varkari Sect\n● Namdev (1270 AD mein Narsi, Maharashtra mein paida hue, Visoba Khechar unke teacher the) ne\nMaharashtra mein Bhakti Movement popularize karne mein important role play kiya — wo Varkari sect\nse related the aur Bhakti Movement ke saints mein Islam se sabse zyada influenced the. Unhone\nidolatry, fasting, pilgrimage aur harsh physical practices ka virodh kiya. [Q37]\n● Occupation match: Namdev → Tailor (darzi); Kabir → Weaver (julaha); Ravidas → Cobbler (mochi);\nSena → Barber (naai). [Q39]\n● Namdev ne Maharashtra mein 'Varkari Sect' ki ideology aur tradition ki sthapna mein important role play\nkiya — Visoba Khechar ne unhe mystic life ki taalim di. [Q47]\n● Varkari sect ka main seat (Peeth) Pandharpur (Maharashtra, Solapur dist., Chandrabhaga/Bhima river\nke kinare) mein hai — Varkaris Vitthal (Krishna ka ek roop) ki pooja karte hain. [Q48]\n● Bhakt Tukaram (1608-1650 AD) Mughal emperors Jahangir (1605-1627 AD) aur Shahjahan (1628-1658\nAD) — dono ke samkalin the, lekin Shahjahan options mein na hone ki wajah se Jahangir sahi answer\nhai. [Q49]\n12. Chaitanya Mahaprabhu\n● Chaitanya Mahaprabhu (bachpan ka naam Nimai), West Bengal ke Nadia district mein ek Brahmin\nfamily mein paida hue the — wo Vaishnava sect (khaas taur par Gaudiya Vaishnavism) ke prominent\nfollower the, jinhone Krishna-bhakti ka prachar\nकkiya. [Q40]\n13. Tulsidas — Life & Works\n● Goswami Tulsidas (1532-1623 AD) Mughal emperors Akbar aur Jahangir ke samkalin the — unhone\nzyadatar zindagi Banaras (Varanasi) mein bitayi. Abul Fazl ki 'Ain-i-Akbari' mein unka zikr hai, halaki\nunka royal court se koi direct sambandh nahi tha. [Q41]\n● 'Ramcharitmanas' (epic poem, Awadhi language mein) 16th century ke bhakti poet Goswami Tulsidas\nne compose ki. [Q42]\n●\n Trap: 'Sahitya Ratna' Tulsidas ki composition NAHI hai — unki famous rachnayein hain Gitavali,\n⚠️\nKavitavali aur Vinay Patrika. [Q43, Q44]\n● Statement check: Tulsidas Rajapur village (aaj ke Chitrakoot district) mein paida hue the (statement\ngalat kyunki original claim mein galat district diya tha). Unki patni ka naam Ratnawali tha, Geetawali\nNAHI (galat statement). [Q45]"," 14. Krishna-Devotion Poets — Raskhan\n●\n Trap: 'Rasik Priya' Raskhan ki NAHI, balki Acharya Keshavdas ki famous composition hai (unki\n⚠️\ndoosri rachnayein: Ramchandrika waghera). Raskhan apni rachna 'Prem Vatika' ke liye famous hain.\n[Q46]\n● 'Prem Vatika' (Krishna ke jeevan par poems, Braj bhasha mein) Raskhan ne likhi — ek Muslim poet (asli\nnaam Sayyid Ibrahim) jo Krishna ke ardent follower ban gaye the. [Q87]\n15. Figures NOT Associated with the Bhakti Movement\n●\n Trap: Nagarjuna, Bhakti cult ke proponent NAHI the — wo ek ancient Indian Buddhist philosopher\n⚠️\nthe jinhone Mahayana Buddhism ke Madhyamaka school ki sthapna ki (Shunyata/Emptiness ke liye\nfamous). Tukaram, Tyagaraja aur Vallabhacharya — teeno actual Bhakti Movement se the. [Q50]\n● Statement check: Saint Nimbarka 11th-12th century mein hue the, Mughal Akbar (1556-1605 AD) se\nbahut pehle — isliye 'Nimbarka Akbar ke samkalin the' wala statement galat hai. Shaikh Ahmad Sirhindi\n(1564-1624 AD) Kabir (1398-1518 AD) ki mrityu ke bahut baad paida hue, isliye Kabir unse influenced\nnahi ho sakte the. [Q77]\n●\n Trap: Amir Khusrau, Delhi Sultanate era ke great poet-musician-Sufi mystic the, lekin wo Hindu\n⚠️\nBhakti Movement ke saint/leader NAHI the. Vallabhacharya, Chaitanya Mahaprabhu aur Guru Nanak —\nteeno actual Bhakti Movement ke prominent leaders the. [Q88]\n16. The Chishti Sufi Order — Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti\n● 'Chishtia Sufi Order' originally Chishti (Afghanistan) mein Abu Ishaq Shami Chishti ne banaya tha, lekin\nIndia mein isse Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ne primarily establish kiya — wo 1192 AD mein Muhammad\nGhori ki army ke saath India aaye aur Ajmer ko apna ghar (residence) banaya. [Q52, Q53, Q54]\n● Chishtia Sufi Order Chishti Sharif (Afghanistan) mein Abu Ishaq Shami Chishti aur unke spiritual disciple\nKhwaja Abu Ahmad Abdal ne founded ki — India mein baad mein Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ne\nintroduce ki. [Q55]\n● Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti, Sijistan (Afghanistan/Iran) mein 1138/1139 AD mein paida hue the —\nKhurasan province mein shift hone ke baad, wo Nishapur mein renowned Sufi master Khwaja Usman\nHaruni ke shishya bane. [Q56, Q57]\n● Raja Sahu (Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj, Shivaji ke pote), Maratha chieftains mein sabse pehle the\njinhone Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ki Dargah (Ajmer) mein nazr (tohfa) chadhaya. [Q58]\n● Assertion-Reason: Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ne India mein Chishti order introduce-popularize kiya (sahi\nAssertion) — lekin Chishti order ka naam Ajmer se NAHI, balki Chist (Chishti Sharif, Herat ke pass\nAfghanistan) se aaya hai (galat Reason). [Q61]\n● Muinuddin Chishti maante the ki devotional music (Sama) God ke kareeb aane ka ek valid/profound\ntareeka hai, jo spiritual ecstasy ki taraf le jaata hai. [Q62]\n17. Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya & His Circle"," ● Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya, Baba Farid (Fariduddin Ganj-i-Shakar, Multan dist. ke Kothewal village mein\npaida hue) ke shishya the — unki Dargah Ghiyaspur, Delhi mein hai (1325 AD mein unki mrityu hui).\n[Q59, Q60]\n● Amir Hasan (Amir Hasan Sijzi Dehlavi, Nizamuddin Auliya ke shishya) ko unke great Persian Ghazals ki\nwajah se 'Sadi of India' (Sadi-i-Hind) kaha jaata tha, jo famous Persian poet Saadi of Shiraz ki tarah the.\n[Q64]\n● Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya ne 7 se zyada Sultans ka reign dekha, lekin royal court se hamesha door\nrahe — jab Alauddin Khalji ne unse milne ki request ki, to unhone jawab diya: 'Mere ghar mein 2\ndarwaze hain, agar Sultan ek se aayega to main doosre se nikal jaunga.' [Q65]\n● Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya ko unke followers 'Mehboob-i-Ilahi' (God ke pyare) kehte the, unki spiritual\nstature ki wajah se — unhe 'Sultan-ul-Mashaikh' (Saints ke King) bhi kaha jaata tha. [Q66, Q67, Q68]\n● Shaikh Nasiruddin Mahmud, Nizamuddin Auliya ke prominent disciple the — Delhi mein revered mystic\nban gaye aur unhe 'Chirag-i-Dehlavi' (Delhi ka jagta hua deepak) ki title mili. [Q72]\n●\n Trap: Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya ka activity center-Dargah Multan mein NAHI, Delhi mein hai (galat\n⚠️\npair). Baba Farid ka activity center Ajodhan (aur Multan region) tha. [Q73]\n18. Other Sufi Orders — Naqshbandi, Suhrawardi, Qadiri & Firdausia\n● Khwaja Qutbuddin Bakhtiar Kaki, Shaikh Moinuddin Chishti aur Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya — sab\nChishti order ke prominent saints the.\n Shaikh Abdul Jilani (Abdul Qadir Jilani), Chishti Silsila se\n⚠️\nNAHI the — wo 'Qadiri order' ke founder the. [Q63]\n● Sufi Order match: Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti → Chishtiya order; Shaikh Ahmad Sirhindi →\nNaqshbandiya order; Dara Shukoh (Mughal Prince) → Qadiriya order ke follower; Shaikh Shahabuddin\n→ Suhrawardiya order ke founder. [Q74]\n● Statement check: Shaikh Ahmad Sirhindi, Akbar-Jahangir ke samkalin the (Ibrahim Lodi ke NAHI —\ngalat statement). Shaikh Nasiruddin Chirag-i-Dehlavi, Nizamuddin Auliya ke chief disciples mein se ek\nthe (sahi). Akbar, Shaikh Salim Chishti ke samkalin the (Aurangzeb ke NAHI — galat). Qadiri order\nShaikh Niamatullah aur Makhdum Muhammad Jilani ne 15th century mein India mein introduce ki (sahi).\n[Q75]\n● Nizamuddin Auliya aur Muinuddin Chishti — dono Chishti Sufi order ke highly revered saints the. Rahim\naur Raskhan Hindi literature ke prominent poets the, Bhakti devotion (khaaskar Raskhan, Krishna-\nbhakti) se associated, Sufi NAHI the. [Q78]\n● Naqshbandi order (Bahauddin Naqshband ne 14th century mein founded, Shaikh Ahmad Sirhindi jaise\nsaints ne strongly follow kiya) Sufis mein sabse radical/orthodox order tha — ye Sama (music) ka virodh\nkarta tha. [Q79]\n● Naqshbandi order sabse orthodox Sufi order tha — Shariat ko rigidly follow karta tha aur music-dance\nko reject karta tha. Babur ne ise India mein popular banaya, aur baad mein Aurangzeb ne strictly follow\nkiya. [Q80]\n●\n Trap: 'Auliya' koi alag Sufi order (Silsila) NAHI hai — ye Shaikh Nizamuddin ko di gayi ek title thi,\n⚠️\njinka activity centre Delhi tha, Madhya Pradesh NAHI. [Q81]\n● 'Firdausia' (Firdousi) Silsila, jo Suhrawardi order ki ek branch thi, Bihar mein firmly established aur\npopular thi — Sheikh Sharfuddin Yahya Maneri isse associated sabse prominent Sufi the. [Q82]"," ● Shaikh Bahauddin Zakaria ne India mein 'Suhrawardi order' establish ki — Chishtis ke ulta, Suhrawardi\nsaints garibi ki zindagi mein believe nahi karte the, wo state patronage accept karke comfortable life\njeete the. [Q84]\n● Suhrawardi Sufi sect ka spread mainly Sindh, Multan aur Punjab tak limited tha — ye Chishtis ke\nlagbhag saath hi India aayi thi, aur Bahauddin Zakariya ne isse establish kiya. [Q85]\n19. Baba Farid & the Adi Granth\n● Shaikh Fariduddin Ganj-i-Shakar (Baba Farid), Chishti order ke prominent saint, ki poetic compositions\nSikhism ke holy 'Guru Granth Sahib' (Adi Granth) mein shaamil ki gayi hain. [Q69]\n20. Shaikh Salim Chishti\n● Shaikh Salim Chishti, Arabia mein lambe samay reh kar 'Shaikh-ul-Hin' ki title paakar, wapas aakar Sikri\nmein rehne lage — baad mein Akbar ne isse Fatehpur Sikri banaya. Kaha jaata hai ki Prince Salim\n(Jahangir) unhi ke aashirwad se paida hue the. [Q70]\n● Shaikh Salim Chishti ko 'Shaikh-ul-Hind' ki title mili thi. [Q71]\n21. Sufi Practices, Syncretism & Shrines\n● Sufi mystics ne medieval India mein communal harmony ko promote kiya — wo highly spiritual the,\ninner purity par focus karte the. Wo Muraqaba (meditation) aur Pas-i-Anfas\n(breath-regulation/Pranayama) practice karte the, aksar solitary places (Chilla/Khanqah) mein ascetic\nlife jeete the, aur Sama (holy songs/music) ka use karke spiritual ecstasy (Hal/Wajd) paate the. [Q6]\n● Assertion-Reason: Medieval period mein Sanskrit music books ka Persian mein translation hua (Firuz\nTughluq, Sikandar Lodi jaise rulers ke through) — sahi Assertion. 'Sama' Sufis ki musical assembly thi\naur Chishtis music ko God tak pahunchne ka madhyam maante the (sahi Reason bhi) — lekin\ntranslation ka reason court-patronage/knowledge-synthesis tha, direct roop se early Chishti beliefs ki\nwajah se nahi (isliye Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation nahi deta). [Q51]\n● Hath Yog statements: India mein Nathpanthis (Guru Matsyendranath-Gorakhnath ke followers) ne Hath\nYog actively practice ki (sahi). Baad mein kai Sufis ne bhi Hath Yog ki breathing exercises-postures\napnayi — jaise Sufi saint Muhammad Ghaus ne Hath Yoga par ek text translate ki. [Q76]\n● Sufi saint Shah Muhammad Ghaus (Shattari order ke most famous saint) ne Lord Krishna ko ek Auliya\n(divine friend/saint) maana — unhone Sanskrit yogic text 'Amritkund' ka Persian translation 'Bahar-ul-\nHayat' naam se kiya, Islamic aur Hindu traditions ko reconcile karne ki koshish ki. [Q83]\n● Ulema, Sufism se related NAHI hain — wo orthodox Islamic scholars-Sharia authorities the, jo Islam ka\n'exoteric' (bahar wala) face represent karte the. 'Khanqah' Sufi saints ki residence hoti thi, 'Sama' unki\nmusical assembly, aur 'Shaikh'/'Pir' unke authorized spiritual teacher. [Q86]\n● Har saal famous Sufi saint Haji Waris Ali Shah ki tomb par Dewa Sharif (Barabanki dist., UP) mein ek\nfair lagta hai — ye communal harmony ka ek symbol hai. [Q91]"," 22. Sufi Poets in Hindavi — Jayasi & Others\n● 'Barahmasa' (epic poem 'Padmavat' ka ek famous section, jisme 12 mahino mein badalti hui emotions\naur viraha ka varnan hai) Sufi poet Malik Muhammad Jayasi ne compose ki thi. [Q89]\n● Match: Mulla Daud → Chandayan; Damodar Kavi → Padmavati Katha; Somnath → Rag Vibodh; Amir\nKhusrau → Ashiqa. [Q90]\n23. Christianity — Festivals & Saints\n● Bible ke mutabik, Jesus Christ Bethlehem (Jerusalem ke south mein ek town) mein paida hue the. [Q92]\n● Easter, Christian church ka principal festival hai, jo Jesus Christ ke Resurrection (punarjeevan) ko\ncelebrate karta hai — unke crucifixion (Calvary mein) ke teesre din. [Q93]\n● Saint Francis of Assisi (1181/82-1226 AD) janwaron aur pakshiyo ke prati apne pyaar ke liye famous\nhain — Catholic tradition mein unhe animals-environment ka patron saint mana jaata hai. [Q94]\n● Good Friday, Christians dwara Jesus Christ ke crucifixion (Calvary mein unki mrityu) ki yaad mein\nmanaya jaata hai — Bible ke mutabik unhe Friday ke din cross par latkaya gaya tha. [Q95]\n24. Miscellaneous Trivia — The 12 Jyotirlingas\n● India mein Lord Shiva ko dedicate 12 Jyotirlingas hain — inme Somnath (Gujarat), Nageshwara\n(Gujarat), Kedarnath (Uttarakhand), Kashi Vishwanath (UP), Vaidyanath (Jharkhand), Mahakaleshwara\n(MP), Omkareshwar (MP) waghera shaamil hain. [Q28]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Bhakti and Sufi Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0182","t":"13 Mughal Dynasty Babur","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL DYNASTY — BABUR — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Invitation to Invade India — Alam Khan & Daulat Khan\n2. Babur's Origins & Central Asian Struggles\n3. The First Battle of Panipat\n4. Babur's Later Battles — Khanwa, Chanderi & Ghaghra\n5. Babur's Contributions, Empire & Legacy in India\n6. Babur's Name, Titles & Autobiography\n7. The Babri Mosque\n1. Invitation to Invade India — Alam Khan & Daulat Khan\n● Alam Khan, Ibrahim Lodi ke uncle the aur khud Delhi ki gaddi ke ek pretender (dawedaar) bhi the —\nunhone Babur ko India invade karne ke liye invite kiya tha. Babur ke 4th Indian campaign ke time,\nIbrahim Lodi aur Daulat Khan ke relations bigad gaye — ye Babur ke liye ek golden opportunity thi,\nkyunki unhe pehle se hi Mewar ke Rana Sanga ki bhi invitation mil chuki thi. [Q1]\n● Daulat Khan Lodi (Punjab ke Governor) ne Ibrahim Lodi ko overthrow karne ke liye Babur ko India\ninvade karne ki invitation di thi. [Q2]\n2. Babur's Origins & Central Asian Struggles\n● Mughal rulers, Turks ki 'Chagatai' branch se the — ye naam Genghis Khan ke doosre bete Chagatai\nKhan ke naam par pada, jo Central Asia aur Turkistan ke raja the. [Q3]\n● Shaybani Khan ne 1501 AD mein Ferghana par invade karke Babur ko 'Battle of Sar-e-Pul' mein haraya\naur Samarqand par kabza kar liya — Babur bhaag kar, 3 saal tak Afghanistan ki pahadiyo aur Khurasan\nke maidano mein bhatakte rahe, Samarkand wapas paane ki kai koshishein karte rahe. Shaybani ne\nunhe haraane ke liye 'Tulughuma' technique use ki thi, jise Babur ne baad mein khud bhi apnaya. [Q4]\n● Babur ne 1501 AD mein Samarkand capture kiya tha jo sirf 8 mahine chala — Samarkand aur Ferghana\ndono khone ke baad, Babur Kabul ki taraf badhe. 1504 mein Kabul jeetne ke baad, unhone apne\nancestors ki 'Mirza' title chhodkar 'Padshah' ki title apnayi. [Q21]\n3. The First Battle of Panipat\n● Mughal ruler Babur ne India mein 'Ottoman (Rumi) system of war' use kiya, First Battle of Panipat (1526\nAD) ke dauran — unki jeet ki sabse important wajah thi unki artillery cannons/guns (Ustad Ali Quli ki\nleadership mein), aur Tulughma-Araba (barricades ke roop mein carts) tactics ka use. [Q5]\n● First Battle of Panipat, 21 April 1526 AD ko Babur aur Ibrahim Lodi ke beech ladi gayi thi — Ibrahim\nLodi ki army sankhya mein zyada hone ke bawajood haar gayi, aur wo khud is battle mein maare gaye.\nIs jeet ke result mein Delhi-Agra tak ka poora ilaka Babur ke control mein aa gaya — unhone 27 April\n1526 AD ko khud ko raja declare karke Mughal Empire ki sthapna ki. [Q6, Q10, Q11]"," ● Babur ki Panipat ki ladai mein jeet ki mukhya wajah unki skilled warfare (effective military\ntactics/commandant-ship) thi — unki army Ibrahim Lodi se chhoti hone ke bawajood, Tulughma system\njaisi effective warfare policy se jeet gayi. Babur ne khud likha: 'Ibrahim Lodi ek inexperienced jawan tha,\njo bina order/method ke march karta tha.' [Q7, Q8]\n● India mein artillery ka use sabse pehle First Battle of Panipat (21 April 1526 AD) mein hua tha — Babur\nne is se pehle Battle of Bajaur (1519 AD, Pakistan) mein bhi artillery-guns use kiya tha, lekin major\nIndian battles mein Panipat hi pehli thi. Artillery battalion Ustad Ali Quli ke, aur gunners battalion\nMustafa ke under thi. [Q9]\n4. Babur's Later Battles — Khanwa, Chanderi & Ghaghra\n●\n Trap: Battle of Chanderi (Babur vs Medini Rai) 1530 mein NAHI, balki 1528 AD mein ladi gayi thi.\n⚠️\nBaaki sahi hain: First Battle of Panipat (1526, Babur vs Ibrahim Lodi); Battle of Khanwa (1527, Babur vs\nRana Sanga); Battle of Ghaghra (1529, Babur vs Afghan rulers). [Q12]\n● Babur ki battles ka sahi chronological order: First Battle of Panipat (1526) → Battle of Khanwa (1527) →\nBattle of Chanderi (1528) → Battle of Ghaghra (1529). [Q13]\n● Battle of Khanwa (16 March 1527 AD) mein Babur ne apni dispirited (himmat-hari) troops ko motivate\nkarne ke liye 'Jehad' (Holy War) declare kiya tha — is ladai mein unhone Mewar ke raja Rana Sanga ko\nharaya aur 'Ghazi' ki title apnayi. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19]\n5. Babur's Contributions, Empire & Legacy in India\n● Statement check: Gunpowder India mein Babur se pehle hi aa chuki thi (fort walls todne ke liye use hoti\nthi) — lekin pitched battles mein cannons-guns effectively use karne ka credit Babur ko jaata hai. Arch-\nDome Sultanate period mein hi introduce ho chuki thi, Babur ne India ki architecture ko shuru mein\nzyada influence nahi kiya. Babur, Turk-Mongol conqueror Timur ke vanshaj the (father's side se) — unki\ngaddi ne region mein Timurid dynasty (Mughal Empire) ki shuruaat ki. [Q14, Q15]\n● Babur ki empire mein Kabul ka area, modern Punjab ka area, aur modern Uttar Pradesh ka area (Bihar\ntak) shaamil tha — lekin modern Rajasthan poori tarah unki empire mein SHAAMIL NAHI tha, kyunki\nuske bade hisse independent Rajput rulers ke control mein the. [Q22]\n● Zahiruddin Muhammad Babur ki zindagi 'patience aur resolution' (dhairya aur sankalp) se success\npaane ka ek lesson deti hai — bachpan mein hi unke pita ki mrityu ho gayi thi, unhone apni ancestral\nkingdom Ferghana khoyi, aur bahut haar-bhatakna jhela — lekin aakhir mein unki dhairya-shakti ka\nreward mila. [Q23]\n● Babur ne apni autobiography 'Baburnama' mein 2 prominent Hindu States — Vijayanagara aur Mewar\n— ka zikr kiya hai. Unhone likha: 'Jab hum Kabul mein the, Rana Sanga ne apni loyalty dikhayi thi ki\nagar honoured king Delhi ki taraf se aaye to wo (Rana Sanga) unka saath denge.' [Q24]\n6. Babur's Name, Titles & Autobiography"," ● India mein Mughal ruler banne ke baad, Zahiruddin Muhammad ne 'Babur' naam apnaya — unka janm\n14 February 1483 AD ko, Umar Shaikh Mirza aur Qutlugh Nigar Khanum ke ghar, Ferghana mein hua\ntha. Unhone 27 April 1526 AD ko khud ko ruler declare karke Mughal empire ki sthapna ki. [Q20]\n● Assertion-Reason: Babur ne apni memoirs 'Tuzuk-i-Babri' (Baburnama) Turkish (Chagatai Turkic)\nlanguage mein likhi (sahi Assertion) — lekin Turkish, Mughal Empire ki official language NAHI thi (galat\nReason) — Mughal court ki official language Persian thi. [Q25]\n● 'Tuzuk-i-Baburi' (Baburnama) Turkish (Chagatai Turkic) language mein likhi gayi thi. [Q26]\n7. The Babri Mosque\n● Ayodhya ki 'Babri Masjid' Mir Baqi ne banwayi thi — wo Babur ke ek general/commandant the. [Q27]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mughal Dynasty Babur Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0183","t":"14 Humayun and Sher Shah","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" HUMAYUN & SHER SHAH — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Humayun — Family & Early Campaigns\n2. Humayun vs Sher Khan — The Rise & Fall\n3. Sher Shah Suri — Early Life & Rise to Power\n4. Sher Shah's Administrative, Revenue & Land Reforms\n5. Sher Shah's Currency Reforms\n6. Humayun's Tomb\n7. Sher Shah's Rajput Campaign — The Battle of Sammel\n8. Sher Shah's Monuments & Architecture\n9. The Grand Trunk Road — Sadak-e-Azam\n10. The Sur Dynasty — Succession After Sher Shah\n1. Humayun — Family & Early Campaigns\n● Kamran, Askari aur Hindal — teeno Babur ke bete the aur Humayun ke bhai. Humayun, Babur ke sabse\nbade bete the, 1508 AD mein Kabul mein paida hue — unki maa Maham Begum Shia sect se related\nthi.\n 'Usman' Humayun ke bhai NAHI the.\n⚠️\n[Q1]\n● Gaddi sambhalne ke baad, Humayun ne apne bhai Kamran Mirza ko 1530s mein Bikaner ke\nindependent ruler Rao Jaitsi (Rao Jait Singh) ke against bheja tha unhe subdue karne ke liye — Beethu\nSouza ke text 'Rao-Jaitsi-Ro-Chhanda' ke mutabik, is ladai mein Rao Jaitsi ne Kamran ko haraya. [Q3]\n● Humayun ne 1532 AD mein pehli baar Chunar Fort par invade kiya — 4 mahine ke siege ke baad, Sher\nKhan ne unki supremacy accept kar li. [Q11]\n2. Humayun vs Sher Khan — The Rise & Fall\n● Humayun ki 4 mahatvapurna battles ka sahi chronological order: Devara/Daurah (1532 AD, Humayun\nne Afghan rebels/Mahmud Lodi ko haraya) → Chausa (26 June 1539 AD, Sher Shah ne Humayun ko\nharaya) → Kannauj/Bilgram (17 May 1540 AD, Sher Shah ne Humayun ko dobara haraya) → Sirhind\n(22 June 1555 AD, Humayun ne dobara Delhi par kabza kiya). [Q2, Q12]\n● Sher Khan ne Humayun ko ek offer di thi — agar unhe Bengal rakhne diya jaaye, to wo Bihar surrender\nkar denge aur 10 lakh dinars ka annual tribute denge — lekin Humayun ne ye offer accept nahi ki. [Q4]\n● Sher Shah Suri aur Humayun ke beech, 17 May 1540 AD ko, Kannauj ke pass ek battle ladi gayi —\nSher Shah ne Humayun ko haraya. Ye battle Bilgram (aaj Hardoi dist., UP mein) mein ladi gayi thi, isliye\nise 'Battle of Bilgram' bhi kehte hain. [Q5]\n3. Sher Shah Suri — Early Life & Rise to Power\n● Farid Khan (baad mein Sher Shah Suri), 1494 AD mein ghar chhodkar Jaunpur gaye the, jahan unhone\napni education li — us waqt Jaunpur 'Siraj-i-Hind' ke naam se famous thi. [Q6]\n● Sher Shah, apne contemporaries mein sabse zyada educated the — unhone apni formal education\nJaunpur (us waqt ka ek prominent education centre) se complete ki. [Q7]"," ● Sher Khan (Sher Shah Suri) ne Bengal ke raja Nusrat Shah ko haraane ke baad 'Hazrat-e-Ala' ki title\napnayi — phir 26 June 1539 AD ko Battle of Chausa mein Humayun ko haraane ke baad, unhone 'Sher\nShah'/'Sultan' ki royal title li aur apne naam se Khutba padhwaya. [Q8]\n4. Sher Shah's Administrative, Revenue & Land Reforms\n● Sher Shah Suri ne kai reforms introduce kiye: Revenue Reforms (zameen measure karne ka improved\nsystem, cultivators ke saath directly revenue settle karna — Rayatwari); Administrative Reforms\n(kingdom ko 'Sirkars'/districts mein baata); Military Reforms (soldiers ko directly pay, unka 'Chehra'\nrecord aur ghodo ki 'Dagh' branding); Currency Reforms (pure gold, silver-Rupiya, copper-Daam coins).\n[Q9]\n● Sher Shah statements: Wo ek brilliant administrative system ke 'architect' the (sahi statement) — unke\nbahaduri aur battlefield victories se bhi zyada unki ruling qualities remarkable thi. Unka chhota (5 saal\nka) reign kai important reforms ke liye jaana jaata hai. [Q17]\n● Sher Shah ne peasants ki madad ke liye 'Patta' aur 'Qabuliyat' system introduce ki — Patta (title deed)\nmein government ka tax-share clearly likha hota tha, jise peasants 'Qabuliyat' ke through accept karte\nthe. [Q30]\n5. Sher Shah's Currency Reforms\n● Delhi Sultanate ke patan (downfall) ke baad, Humayun pehle ruler the jinhone gold coin issue ki — unke\nbaad Sher Shah ne bhi gold coin introduce ki. [Q10]\n● Sher Shah ne ek reformed currency system establish ki — pure gold, silver (Rupiya) aur copper (Daam)\ncoins introduce kiye. Unke silver 'Rupiya' coins ka weight 178 grains tha, jisme se 173 grains pure silver\ntha. Ye system Mughal period mein bhi circulate hui aur British currency ka aadhar bani. [Q14, Q16]\n● Sher Shah ke currency system mein silver 'Rupiya' (178 grains) aur copper 'Daam' (380 grains) ka\nexchange rate 1:64 tha (1 Rupee = 64 Daams). [Q15]\n6. Humayun's Tomb\n● Haji Begum (Bega Begum) ne apne pati Humayun ke liye ek mausoleum banwaya, Delhi mein, 1565-\n1572 AD ke beech — isse 'Tomb of Humayun' ke naam se jaana jaata hai. Persian architect Mirak Mirza\nGhiyash ne ise design kiya — ye Mughal Architecture ka pehla 'double dome' mausoleum hai. [Q13]\n7. Sher Shah's Rajput Campaign — The Battle of Sammel\n● Sher Shah Suri ki mrityu 22 May 1545 AD ko, Kalinjar (Rajputs ke) Fort ke siege ke dauran hui — jab\nfort ko subdue karne ki sabhi tactics fail ho gayi, to unhone deewaron ko gunpowder se udaane ka order\ndiya. Ek canon (Uqqa) ke explosion se wo badly ghayal ho gaye. Kalanjar hi unka last expedition\n(campaign) tha. [Q18, Q19]"," ● Battle of Sammel (Marwar) mein Rajputs ki chivalry-courage se Sher Shah Suri itne impressed the, aur\nhaarte-haarte bache the, ki unhone kaha: 'Main ek muthi bhar baajra (Marwar ki relatively barren\nterritory) ke liye poori empire khone waala tha.' [Q20]\n● Battle of Sammel mein Maldeo Rathore (Marwar ke raja) Sher Shah Suri se haar gaye — unke army\ngenerals Jaita aur Kumpa ne chand hazaar sainikon ke saath Sher Shah ki badi army ke against\nzabardast ladai di, jisse Sher Shah unki bahaduri se bahut prabhavit hue. [Q21]\n8. Sher Shah's Monuments & Architecture\n● Sher Shah ka tomb (ek imposing brick structure, ek artificial lake ke beech mein) Sasaram (Rohtas dist.,\nBihar) mein hai — ise India mein Afghan architecture ke sabse noble examples mein se ek maana jaata\nhai. Sher Shah, Sasaram (Bihar) ke ek Afghan Jagirdar ke bete the — 1545 AD mein mrityu ke baad\nunhe wahi dafnaya gaya. [Q22, Q23, Q24]\n● Sher Shah ka short reign, Indian architecture ke history mein ek revolutionary era maana jaata hai —\nunhone Delhi ke Purana Qila complex ke andar 'Qila-i-Kuhna' (Mosque, 1541 AD mein bani) banwayi, jo\napni elegant architectural qualities ke liye famous hai. [Q25, Q27]\n● 'Purana Qila' (Old Fort, Delhi) ka construction Humayun aur Sher Shah — dono se juda hai. Humayun\nne originally citadel (Dinpanah) khada kiya tha, lekin Delhi capture karne ke baad Sher Shah ne isse\nsubstantially rebuild-expand kiya, isi ke andar Qila-i-Kuhna mosque aur Sher Mandal monuments bhi\nbanaye. [Q26, Q28]\n● Sher Shah ne banaye monuments: Sasaram Tomb (unke reign mein shuru hui, bete Islam Shah ne\ncomplete ki) aur Qila-e-Kuhna Mosque (Delhi). Sikandra (Akbar's tomb) Akbar ne shuru ki aur Jahangir\nne complete ki, Jama Masjid (Delhi) Shah Jahan ne banwayi — ye dono Sher Shah ki NAHI hain. [Q29]\n9. The Grand Trunk Road — Sadak-e-Azam\n● 'Sadak-e-Azam' (Grand Trunk Road, Asia ki sabse purani-lambi major roads mein se ek) Sher Shah\nSuri ne banayi-renovate ki — East Bengal (Sonargaon) se lekar Peshawar hoke Kabul (Afghanistan) tak\njaati thi. [Q31]\n10. The Sur Dynasty — Succession After Sher Shah\n● Sher Shah Suri ke successor Islam Shah Suri (original naam Jalal Khan) the — wo Sur Dynasty ke\ndoosre ruler the, Sher Shah ke doosre bete, jinhone unki 1545 AD mein mrityu ke baad gaddi sambhali.\n[Q32]\n● Islam Shah (Sher Shah ke bete, jinhone 8 saal North India par raj kiya) ne apni military ko 200, 250 aur\n500 units mein organize kiya tha — unke successor Sikandar Shah Suri ne bhi isi military practice ko\ncontinue kiya, isliye is question mein ek se zyada option sahi hain. [Q33]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Humayun and Sher Shah Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0184","t":"15 Akbar","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL DYNASTY — AKBAR — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Akbar's Accession & Bairam Khan\n2. Battle of Haldighati & Rajput Resistance\n3. Akbar's Territorial Expansion & Chronology\n4. Rajput Matrimonial Alliances\n5. Akbar, Sufism & Personal Justice\n6. The Assassination of Abul Fazl\n7. Akbar's Character, Popularity & Governance Philosophy\n8. Social Reforms\n9. The Mansabdari System\n10. Central Administration — The Office of Diwan\n11. Land Revenue — The Zabti/Dahsala System & Raja Todarmal\n12. Fact-Check — Tansen, Man Singh & Todarmal\n13. Din-i-Ilahi\n14. Ibadat Khana\n15. Fatehpur Sikri — Monuments & Architecture\n16. Sulh-i-Kul — The Policy of Universal Peace\n17. The Fatwa Against Akbar\n18. Buland Darwaza\n19. Educational Reforms\n20. Mughal Monuments & Tombs — Important Match Lists\n21. Persian Translations of Hindu Epics\n22. Court Scholars, Painters & Honorary Titles\n23. Akbar & Contemporary World Rulers\n24. Foreign Visitors — Ralph Fitch & the Jesuit Missions\n25. Chronology of Akbar's Religious Policy\n1. Akbar's Accession & Bairam Khan\n● Humayun ki mrityu (1556 mein, apni library Sher Mandal, Dinpanah, Delhi ki seedhiyo se gir kar) ki\nkhabar milne par, Akbar ko Kalanaur (Punjab) mein enthrone (rajyabhishek) kiya gaya. [Q1]\n● Statement check: Akbar ne Bairam Khan (unke guardian aur military commander) ko 'Khan-i-Khanan' ki\ntitle di thi (sahi) — lekin ye title unhe appointment ke time hi de di gayi thi, baad mein nahi (isliye doosra\nstatement galat hai). [Q2]\n2. Battle of Haldighati & Rajput Resistance\n● Battle of Haldighati (18 June 1576 AD) Maharana Pratap (Mewar) ki forces aur Raja Man Singh-I\n(Amber) ki leadership wali Mughal army ke beech ladi gayi — Akbar ka mukhya maksad tha Rana\nPratap ko subdue karke unse Mughal suzerainty accept karwana. [Q3, Q4]\n● Hakim Khan Sur (Sher Shah Suri dynasty ke descendant, ek Pathan adventurer) Maharana Pratap ki\narmy ke Commander-in-Chief the — unhone ~5,000 Afghans ki army lead ki thi, Rajput forces ke saath.\n[Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● Mewar ka Sisodia Rajput rajya, Akbar ki supremacy accept karne se poori tarah inkaar karta raha —\nRana Udai Singh aur unke bete Maharana Pratap ne lambe samay tak Akbar ke against apna"," sangharsh jaari rakha. Rana Pratap ki mrityu ke baad hi unke bete Rana Amar Singh ne 1615 AD mein\nJahangir (Akbar ke successor) ke saath peace treaty ki. [Q13]\n● Rana Pratap (Mewar) ke alawa, Rao Chandrasena (Marwar/Jodhpur) ne bhi Akbar ki supremacy ka\nvirodh kiya, apni azaadi ke liye guerrilla wars ladte hue, 1581 AD mein apni mrityu tak — unhe 'Marwar\nka Maharana Pratap' bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q14]\n● Rani Durgavati, Gondwana (Garha-Katanga) ki brave Queen Regent thi, apne minor bete Vir Narayan\nke naam par raj karti thi — jab Akbar ne Asaf Khan ki leadership mein badi Mughal army bheji, to\nunhone bahaduri se ladai ki lekin Garh-Mandla ke beech haar gayi. [Q15]\n3. Akbar's Territorial Expansion & Chronology\n● Map-based question: Akbar ki empire 1605 AD (unki mrityu ke time) mein bahut vistrit thi — 'A'\nGondwana ko represent karta hai (jo apni tribal autonomy retain karta tha), aur 'B' Lahore ko (jo unki\nempire ka ek major city/temporary capital tha). [Q8]\n● Chronological order: Mughal invasion of Malwa (Baz Bahadur ki haar, 1561 AD) → Akbar ki shaadi\nAmber ki Princess se (Jodha/Harkhabai, 1562 AD) → Karrani ka Orissa conquest (Sulaiman Karrani,\n1568 AD) → Battle of Tukaroi (Mughals ne Bengal-Orissa ke Daud Khan Karrani ko haraya, 1575 AD).\n[Q21]\n● Daud Khan Karrani ne 1572 AD mein Patna ke Mughal fort par invade kiya tha — Akbar ne Munim\nKhan ko bheja isse dabaane ke liye, aur aakhir mein 12 July 1576 AD ko Todarmal ne Daud Khan ko\ndecisively haraya, jisse Akbar ne Bengal aur Bihar ko formally apni empire mein merge kar liya. [Q81]\n4. Rajput Matrimonial Alliances\n● Akbar ki Rajputs ke saath pehli matrimonial alliance (shaadi ka sambandh) Amber ke Kachhwaha\nRajput ghar se hui thi — 1562 AD mein Ajmer ki pilgrimage ke dauran, Amber ke Raja Bihari Mal\n(Bharmal) ne apni beti Harkhabai (Princess) ki shaadi ka proposal khud diya. Salim (baad mein Emperor\nJahangir) isi shaadi se paida hue the. [Q9, Q10]\n5. Akbar, Sufism & Personal Justice\n● Akbar Sufism aur Chishti sect ka bahut respect karte the — wo Ajmer mein Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ki\nDargah (Mausoleum) frequently visit karte the, aur Sikri mein Shaikh Salim Chishti ka aashirwad bhi liya.\n[Q11]\n● Akbar ne khud apne haath se Adham Khan (unki paalak-maa Maham Anga ke bete) ko 1562 AD mein\nAgra ke palace ki terrace se neeche phenk diya tha — ye Adham Khan ke unke Prime Minister Atagh\nKhan (Shams-ud-Din Ataga Khan) ki nirmam hatya karne ki saza thi. [Q12]\n6. The Assassination of Abul Fazl\n● Prince Salim (baad mein Emperor Jahangir) ne 1602 AD mein Akbar ke trusted advisor-historian Abul\nFazl ki hatya organize ki thi — Salim, Allahabad mein rebel kar rahe the, aur Akbar ne Abul Fazl ko"," Deccan se bulaya situation handle karne ke liye. Salim ne Bundela chief Vir Singh Deo ko rasta rokne\naur unhe maarne ke liye hire kiya tha. [Q16]\n7. Akbar's Character, Popularity & Governance Philosophy\n● Akbar ko 'national king' isliye maana jaata hai kyunki unhone desh ko administratively-culturally-\nreligiously unify karne ki koshish ki (secular tolerance ke through) —\n 'Akbar ne Islam chhod diya'\n⚠️\nwala claim historically GALAT hai, unhone syncretic faith (Din-i-Ilahi) promote ki thi, Islam poori tarah\ntyaag nahi kiya. [Q17]\n● Akbar ki lasting popularity ke karan the: Mansabdari system (military-civil administration ko consolidate\nkiya), Religious Policy (Jizya-Pilgrimage tax abolish karna), Land Revenue System (Todarmal ke\nreforms), aur Social Reforms. [Q18]\n● Akbar ko 'an enlightened despot' (ek gyani/roshan-khayal tanashah) kaha jaata hai — unke paas\nabsolute despotic power thi, lekin unhone isse progressive reforms, religious tolerance, arts ke\npatronage aur logo ki bhalai ke liye use kiya. [Q20]\n● Akbar ka reign famous hai: Regions ki annexation (military conquests), Provincial Administrative System\n(Subas mein baatna), aur Judicial Administration ke liye. Wo religious tolerance/liberalism ke liye\nglobally famous hain (Jizya abolish karna, Din-i-Ilahi), religious intolerance ke liye NAHI. [Q24]\n8. Social Reforms\n● Muslim rulers mein se Akbar ne Pilgrimage Tax (1563 AD) aur Jizya Tax (1564 AD) — dono abolish\nkiye, Hindu majority ki goodwill jeetne aur secularism promote karne ke liye. [Q19]\n● Akbar ne polygamy ko discourage karte hue ek order diya — ki koi purush sirf ek hi patni se shaadi\nkare, aur doosri shaadi tabhi kare jab pehli patni barren (santan-heen) saabit ho. Unhone widow\nremarriage ko encourage kiya, aur 'Sati' pratha ko rokne ki koshish ki. [Q22]\n● Akbar ne ladkiyo ke liye 14 saal aur ladko ke liye 16 saal marriage ki minimum age fix karne ki koshish\nki (statement 1 sahi) — unhone ye bhi decree kiya ki shaadi bride-bridegroom ki mutual consent se ho,\nladkiyo ko apni marzi se shaadi karne ki azaadi deke (statement 2 bhi sahi). [Q23]\n9. The Mansabdari System\n● Akbar ne apni army aur civil administration ko effectively organize karne ke liye 1574-75 AD mein\n'Mansabdari' system introduce ki — har officer ko ek rank (Mansab) di jaati thi, jo unka status, salary,\naur maintain karne wale troops (cavalry) ki sankhya decide karti thi. Iska mukhya maksad clean, efficient\naur centralized administration ensure karna tha. [Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Akbar dwara introduce ki gayi Mansabdari system, Mongolia (Central Asia) ke decimal-based ranking\nmilitary division system se li gayi thi — Akbar ne isse India ke administrative needs ke hisaab se\nsignificantly modify kiya. [Q29]\n● Assertion-Reason: Akbar ke time, har 10 cavalrymen ke liye Mansabdars ko 20 ghode maintain karne\npadte the ('Dah-Bisti' rule) — ye sahi Assertion hai. Iski mukhya wajah logistical thi: lambi marches ke"," dauran ghodo ko rest ki zaroorat hoti thi, aur intense warfare mein turant replacement ke liye extra\nghode zaroori the — ye sahi Reason bhi hai, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai. [Q30]\n10. Central Administration — The Office of Diwan\n● 'Diwan' Mughal administration mein financial affairs-revenues ke supreme official hote the — is\ndepartment ki asli growth Muzaffar Khan Turbati ki Diwan (Wazir) ki tarah appointment se shuru hui,\nAkbar ke reign ke 9th saal mein. Baad mein Raja Todarmal aur Khwaja Shah Mansoor bhi is prestigious\npost par rahe. [Q28]\n11. Land Revenue — The Zabti/Dahsala System & Raja Todarmal\n● 'Zabti System' (jise 'Dahsala System' bhi kehte hain) land revenue assessment-collection ke liye Akbar\nke reign mein introduce hui — unke brilliant finance minister Raja Todarmal ne ise develop kiya. Isme\nzameen survey ki jaati thi, aur pichhle 10 saal ki average yield ke basis par revenue fix kiya jaata tha.\n[Q31, Q32]\n● 'Dahsala' system ko 'Bandobast System' bhi kaha jaata hai — kyunki ye ek systematic, settled revenue\ncollection method thi, isliye ise 'Todarmal Bandobast System' bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q33]\n● Raja Todarmal apne Land Revenue Reforms (Dahsala/Bandobast system) ke liye famous the — Akbar\nke reign mein unhone Mughal finances ko consolidate kiya. [Q34]\n● Akbar ke darbar mein aane se pehle, Raja Todarmal ne Sher Shah Suri ke under kaam kiya tha aur\nland revenue management mein bahut experience hasil ki — isliye unhe Sher Shah aur Akbar ke\nrevenue systems ke beech ek vital connecting link maana jaata hai, jinhone Sher Shah ke experiments\n(jaise land measurement, Patta system) ko Akbar ki grand Ain-i-Dahsala mein aage badhaya. [Q36]\n● Akbar ke reign mein land revenue system 'Ain-i-Dahsala' Raja Todarmal ne develop ki thi. [Q37]\n12. Fact-Check — Tansen, Man Singh & Todarmal\n● Statement check: Tansen ka asli naam Ramtanu Pandey tha (Rambali NAHI) — 'Tansen' ki title unhe\nGwalior/Rewa ke raja ne di thi, Akbar ne NAHI (galat statement). Akbar ki shaadi Man Singh ki bua\n(aunt, Raja Bharmal ki beti) se hui thi — Jahangir ki shaadi Man Singh ki behen se hui (galat statement\nabout Akbar-Man Singh sister). Abul Fazl ne 'Ain-i-Akbari' likhi (sahi statement). Raja Todarmal Finance\nMinister (Diwan) the, army ke commander-in-chief NAHI (galat statement). [Q35]\n13. Din-i-Ilahi\n● Akbar ne 1582 AD mein 'Tauhid-i-Ilahi' ya 'Din-i-Ilahi' launch ki thi — ye ek eclectic, syncretic religious\nideology thi jiska maksad tha apni empire ke sabhi religions ke behtareen elements ko merge karna.\nBirbal isko accept karne wale ekmatra Hindu courtier the. [Q38, Q39, Q40]\n●\n Trap: Contemporary historians mein se kisi ne bhi Din-i-Ilahi ko 'religion' nahi kaha — ye technically\n⚠️\nek dharm nahi, balki Sufi pantheism par based ek ethical ideology/spiritual fellowship thi. Baad mein,"," Mohsin Fani (Jahangir ke samkalin) ne apni 'Dabistan-i-Mazahib' text mein Din-i-Ilahi ko ek independent\nreligion ki tarah mention kiya. [Q41]\n14. Ibadat Khana\n● Akbar ne 1575 AD mein 'Ibadat Khana' banwane ka order diya — Ulemas, Sayyids aur Shaikhs ke\nsaath philosophical-theological discussions karne ke liye. Baad mein unhone 1578 AD mein iske\ndarwaze sabhi religions ke logo ke liye khol diye. [Q42]\n● Fatehpur Sikri ka 'Ibadat Khana' ek meeting-hall tha jaha Akbar ne alag-alag religions ke scholars ke\nsaath discussions ki. [Q43]\n15. Fatehpur Sikri — Monuments & Architecture\n● Akbar ne Fatehpur Sikri (City of Victory) basayi thi, jo 1571 se 1585 AD tak Mughal Kingdom ki capital\nrahi — yahan ki 'Jama Masjid' ko 'Shan-i-Fatehpur' ya 'Shan-i-Sikri' kaha jaata hai. Sikri ke finest\nmonuments (Diwan-i-Aam, Diwan-i-Khas, Panch Mahal, Khas Mahal waghera) Akbar ke reign mein\nbanaye gaye — Percy Brown ne Sikri ko ek unique architectural achievement bataya. [Q44, Q54]\n●\n Trap: 'Akbari Mahal' Fatehpur Sikri mein NAHI, Agra Fort mein hai. Golden Palace (Sunahra\n⚠️\nMakan/Maryam-uz-Zamani Palace), Panch Mahal aur Jodha Bai's Palace — ye sab Fatehpur Sikri\ncomplex mein hain. [Q45]\n● Fatehpur Sikri ka 'Panch Mahal' (5-storey building, Akbar ne banwaya) apni architecture mein Buddhist\nMonastery (Vihara) se milta-julta hai — tiered, receding pavilions poori tarah pillars par based hain.\nGround floor mein 84 pillars poori structure ko support karte hain. [Q55, Q56, Q57]\n16. Sulh-i-Kul — The Policy of Universal Peace\n● Akbar ki religious policy ka mukhya maksad 'Sulh-i-Kul' (sabke saath shaanti/universal harmony) tha —\nunhone ye policy religious tolerance, political generosity aur liberal cultural attitude promote karne ke\nliye banayi, apni diverse empire mein. [Q47]\n● Akbar ka 'Sulh-i-Kul' concept (universal peace-fraternity) unki political generosity, religious tolerance,\naur liberal cultural attitude — teeno ka result tha. [Q48]\n17. The Fatwa Against Akbar\n● 1580 AD mein, Jaunpur ke prominent Ulema Mulla Muhammad Yazdi ne Mughal emperor Akbar ke\nagainst ek 'Fatwa' issue ki thi — unhone Akbar ki liberal religious policies (jaise Mahzar aur baad mein\nDin-i-Ilahi) ki wajah se unhe heretic (kaafir) declare kiya aur sabhi Muslims se unke against rebel karne\nko kaha. [Q49]\n18. Buland Darwaza"," ● Assertion-Reason: Akbar ne Fatehpur Sikri mein 'Buland Darwaza' banwaya (sahi Assertion) — lekin\nunhone ise Jahangir ke janm ki yaad mein NAHI, balki Gujarat par apni jeet ki yaad mein banwaya\n(galat Reason, kuch historians Deccan ki jeeto se bhi jodte hain). [Q50, Q51]\n●\n Multiple Correct: Akbar ne Buland Darwaza AUR Jama Masjid (Fatehpur Sikri) — dono banwaye.\n⚠️\n(Qutb Minar Delhi Sultans ne, Taj Mahal Shah Jahan ne banwaya.) [Q52]\n19. Educational Reforms\n● Akbar ne education curriculum mein reforms introduce ki, khaaskar primary level par — Arithmetic,\nLogic, Mensuration, Geometry, Astronomy, Physiognomy, Accountancy, Public Administration aur\nAgriculture jaise important subjects course mein shaamil kiye gaye. Khud unhone koi formal education\nnahi li thi, lekin vidwaan logo ko bahut patronize kiya. [Q53]\n20. Mughal Monuments & Tombs — Important Match Lists\n● Humayun's Tomb (Delhi) ko Persian aur Indian architecture styles ka ek magnificent synthesis maana\njaata hai — Humayun ki patni (Haji Begum) ke patronage mein bana, Persian architect Mirak Mirza\nGhiyas ne design kiya — ismein pehli baar bade paimane par red sandstone use hua. [Q46]\n● Jahangir Mahal, Agra Fort ke andar situated hai — Akbar ne apne bete Prince Salim (Jahangir) ke liye\nye palace banwaya tha, red sandstone se bana, Hindu-Islamic motifs se decorated. [Q58]\n● Akbar ka Tomb, Sikandara (Agra sheher ke bahar) mein situated hai — Akbar ne khud iska construction\nplan shuru kiya tha, lekin unke bete Jahangir ne 1613 AD mein complete kiya. [Q59]\n●\n Trap: 'Red Fort of Delhi' Akbar ke reign mein NAHI bana — ye unke pote Shah Jahan ne banwaya,\n⚠️\n1648 mein complete hua. Agra Fort, Allahabad Fort aur Lahore Fort — teeno Akbar ne banwaye the.\n[Q60]\n● Mughal Ruler-Tomb match: Babur → Kabul; Akbar → Sikandara; Jahangir → Lahore (Shahdara Bagh);\nShah Jahan → Agra (Taj Mahal). [Q61]\n● Mughal Ruler-Tomb match: Babur → Kabul; Humayun → Delhi; Akbar → Sikandara; Jahangir →\nLahore. [Q62]\n21. Persian Translations of Hindu Epics\n● Akbar ke reign mein Mahabharat ka Persian translation, unke poet laureate Faizi ki supervision mein\nhua tha — Translation Department Faizi ke under thi, aur Naqib Khan, Badauni jaise scholars ne is\nkaam mein contribute kiya. [Q63]\n● Mahabharata ka Persian translation Akbar ke aadesh par ek team ne kiya, jisme prominently Faizi,\nNaqib Khan aur Abdul Qadir Badauni shaamil the — is translation ka naam 'Razmnama' (Book of Wars)\nrakha gaya. [Q64, Q65, Q66, Q67]\n● Abdul Qadir Badauni ne Akbar ki ichha ke mutabik, Mahabharata ke saath-saath, Ramayan ka bhi\nPersian mein translation kiya — Faizi ne 'Leelavati' aur Abul Fazl ne 'Kaliyadaman' Persian mein\ntranslate kiya. [Q68, Q69]"," 22. Court Scholars, Painters & Honorary Titles\n● Kashmir ke Muhammad Hussain, Akbar ke darbar ke famous writers-calligraphers mein se ek the —\nunki exquisite Nastaliq calligraphy ke liye Akbar ne unhe 'Zari Qalam' (Golden Pen) ka title diya. [Q70]\n● Jain monk Hari Vijay Suri (Hiravijaya ji), Akbar ke darbar mein kuch saal rahe — unhe 'Jagadguru'\n(duniya ke teacher) ki title mili. Akbar unki non-violence teachings se bahut prabhavit hue, vegetarian\nbhi ban gaye. Ek aur Jain scholar Jin Chandra Suri ko Akbar ne 'Yug Pradhan' ki title di. [Q71, Q72, Q73]\n● Akbar ke darbar ke famous painter 'Daswant' the — ek potter ke bete, unhone apni skills se Akbar ko\nitna impress kiya ki wo apne samay ke pehle artist ban gaye. Abul Fazl ne apni 'Ain-i-Akbari' mein\nDaswant ke alawa Basawan, Keshav Lal, Mukund jaise painters ka bhi zikr kiya hai. [Q74]\n23. Akbar & Contemporary World Rulers\n● Akbar, England ki Queen Elizabeth-I ke samkalin the — 1600 AD mein East India Company ki sthapna\nke waqt, Elizabeth England ki empress thi (1558-1603 AD tak), aur us waqt India mein Akbar raj kar\nrahe the. [Q75]\n● English East India Company ki sthapna 1600 AD mein Queen Elizabeth I ke royal charter se hui thi —\nus waqt India ke emperor Akbar the (jo 1605 AD tak raj karte rahe). [Q76]\n24. Foreign Visitors — Ralph Fitch & the Jesuit Missions\n● Akbar ke darbar ke famous historian-grand vizier Abul Fazl ne, America ki discovery ka explicit zikr apni\nwritings mein kiya (Alum-i-Nau) — is tarah ka reference dene wale wo ek medieval Indian writer the.\n[Q77]\n● Ralph Fitch (1583-86 AD), Akbar ke reign mein Agra aur Fatehpur Sikri visit karne wale pehle English\nmerchant the — unhone 16th century ke India ke trade points aur township centers ke baare mein ek\nvaluable narrative di. [Q78]\n●\n Disputed: Goa Church authorities ne 1595 AD mein Akbar ke paas priests ka ek teesra mission\n⚠️\nbheja tha (pehle 1580 aur 1591 mein bhi bheja gaya tha) — ye mission Jerome Xavier (St. Francis\nXavier ke bhatije) ki leadership mein Lahore mein Akbar se mila. Antonio Monserrate PEHLE mission ka\nhissa the, teesre ke nahi — isliye is question ke sahi statements par confusion/dispute hai. [Q80]\n25. Chronology of Akbar's Religious Policy\n● Akbar ke religious policy events ka sahi chronological order: Jizya ka abolition (1564 AD) → Ibadat\nKhana ka construction (1575 AD) → Mahzar (Infallibility Decree) par signing (1579 AD) → Din-i-Ilahi ki\nfoundation (1582 AD). [Q79]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Akbar Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0185","t":"16 Jahangir","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL DYNASTY — JAHANGIR — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Jahangir's Military-Administrative Reform — Do-aspa Sih-aspa\n2. The Treaty of Chittor\n3. English Envoys — Hawkins & Sir Thomas Roe\n4. Foreign Travellers — Francisco Pelsaert\n5. Jahangir's Tomb\n6. Mughal Painting Under Jahangir\n7. Tuzuk-i-Jahangiri — Jahangir's Autobiography\n8. The Assassination of Abul Fazl — Reward for the Killer\n9. Rebellions Against Jahangir\n10. Nur Jahan's Junta\n11. Itmad-ud-Daula's Tomb & Pietra Dura\n12. Mughal Monuments — Important Match Lists\n13. Govind Palace, Datia\n1. Jahangir's Military-Administrative Reform — Do-aspa Sih-aspa\n● 'Do-aspa aur Sih-aspa' system Jahangir ne introduce ki thi — is system ke provisions ke under,\nMansabdars ko apni rank (zat) mein koi increment na hone ke bawajood, excess sainiko ko maintain\nkarna padta tha. 'Do-aspa' mein Mansabdars ko apni 'Sawar' rank ke muqable double ghode maintain\nkarne padte the, aur 'Sih-aspa' mein triple ghode. [Q1]\n2. The Treaty of Chittor\n● 'Treaty of Chittor', Jahangir ke reign mein, 1615 AD mein, Mughals aur Mewar ke Rana (Rana Amar\nSingh) ke beech sign hui thi — Rana ne Mughal emperor ki allegiance accept ki, aur Jahangir ne unhe\nMewar aur Chittorgarh wapas de diya, jo Akbar ke reign mein Mughals ne annex kiya tha. [Q2]\n3. English Envoys — Hawkins & Sir Thomas Roe\n● William Hawkins (1608-11 AD), Jahangir ke darbar mein visit karne wale English East India Company\nke pehle ambassador the — unhone 3 saal royal court mein bitaye. Jahangir ne unhe 400 ka mansab\ndeke honour kiya. [Q3]\n●\n Disputed: William Hawkins aur Sir Thomas Roe — dono ko envoy ki tarah bheja gaya tha, Hawkins\n⚠️\nKing James-I ka letter Jahangir ke paas laaye the — options mein Hawkins available hone ki wajah se\ngenerally yehi intended answer maana jaata hai, lekin standard answer keys is tarah ke phrasing wale\nquestions ko disputed maarti hain. [Q4]\n● Turkish bol sakne wale Hawkins se Jahangir itne impressed the ki unhone unhe 'English Khan' ki title di,\naur ek Armenian lady se unki shaadi bhi karwayi. [Q5, Q6]\n● Sir Thomas Roe, England ke King James-I ke representative ki tarah, Jahangir ke reign mein (1615-\n1619 AD) Mughal court mein aaye the, British trade ke liye favourable facilities hasil karne ke maksad se"," — wo 18 September 1615 ko Surat pahunche the, aur 1616 mein Ajmer mein Jahangir ke darbar mein\npresent hue. Unhe Mandu, Ahmedabad aur Ajmer visit karne ka mauka bhi mila. [Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10]\n● Thomas Roe pehli baar 1616 AD mein Ajmer mein Jahangir se mile the — wo 1619 AD tak India mein\nrahe, aur Jahangir ke ek decree ke saath England laute jisme British ko Mughal court mein zeal se\nwelcome karne ka assurance tha. [Q11]\n● Foreign travellers ka sahi chronological order: Ralph Fitch (1583 AD, Akbar ke reign mein pehle English\ntraveller) → William Hawkins (1608 AD Surat aaye, 1609 mein Jahangir ke darbar gaye) → Nicholas\nDawnton (1614-15 AD) → Sir Thomas Roe (January 1616 AD mein Jahangir ke darbar aaye). [Q12]\n4. Foreign Travellers — Francisco Pelsaert\n● Dutch traveller Francisco Pelsaert, Jahangir ke period mein India aaye the — unhone apni text\n'Jahangir's India: The Remonstrantie of Francisco Pelsaert' mein Mughal empire ka ek valuable/unique\naccount chhoda. (Peter Mundy Shah Jahan ke reign mein aaye the, Niccolo Manucci succession war ke\ntime.) [Q13, Q14]\n5. Jahangir's Tomb\n●\n Multiple Correct: Mughal emperors Babur aur Jahangir — dono ki mausoleum modern-day India ke\n⚠️\nbahar hai. Babur ka tomb Kabul (Afghanistan) mein hai, aur Jahangir ka tomb Shahdara, Lahore\n(Pakistan) mein. [Q15]\n● Emperor Jahangir 1627 AD mein guzar gaye the, aur unhe Shahdara (Lahore ke pass) ke ek tomb-\ngarden mein dafnaya gaya, modern-day India ke bahar. [Q16, Q17]\n6. Mughal Painting Under Jahangir\n● Mughal painting apne zenith (highest point) par Jahangir ke reign mein pahunchi — pehle paintings\nmainly manuscripts ke content tak simit thi, lekin Jahangir ne isse is bandhan se azaad karke individual\nportraits aur nature studies ko encourage kiya. Farrukh Beg, Daulat, Mansur aur Abul Hasan jaise artists\nne apna naam sunehre akshron mein likha. [Q18, Q19]\n● Abul Hasan, Jahangir ke reign ke ek excellent portrait artist the — Jahangir ne unhe 'Nadir-ul-Zaman'\n(Wonder of the Age) ki title di. [Q20]\n● Ustad Mansur, plants-animals-birds depict karne mein specialize karte the — Jahangir ne unhe 'Nadir-\nul-Asra' (Miracle of the Age) ki title di. Wo Jahangir ke darbar ke sabse great bird-aur-nature painter the.\n[Q21, Q22]\n7. Tuzuk-i-Jahangiri — Jahangir's Autobiography\n● Jahangir ek outstanding author-critic the — unhone apni autobiography Persian language mein likhi, jise\n'Tuzuk-i-Jahangiri' naam diya. (Babur ne apni autobiography 'Tuzuk-i-Babri'/Baburnama\nTurkish/Chagatai language mein likhi thi.) [Q23]"," 8. The Assassination of Abul Fazl — Reward for the Killer\n● Prince Salim (baad mein Jahangir) ne 1602 AD mein Raja Vir Singh Bundela ke through Abul Fazl ki\nhatya organize ki thi — 1605 AD mein gaddi sambhalne ke baad, Jahangir ne apne associates ko high\ndesignations di, aur Abul Fazl ke murderer Raja Vir Singh Bundela ko bhi bahut zyada reward diya.\n[Q24]\n9. Rebellions Against Jahangir\n● Jahangir ne apne reign mein kai rebellions ka saamna kiya: unke bade bete Khusrau ne coronation ke\nturant baad revolt ki, jo 1606 AD mein suppress ki gayi. Shahzada Khurram (baad mein Shah Jahan) ne\n~1622-23 AD mein revolt ki. 1626 AD mein prominent general Mahabat Khan ne bhi revolt karke\nJahangir ko temporarily capture kar liya. (Asif Khan/Asaf Khan, Nur Jahan ke bhai, ek powerful noble\nthe lekin unhone is tarah khule roop se rebel nahi kiya.) [Q25]\n● Khusrau Mirza, Jahangir ke sabse bade bete the (unki maa Man Bai/Shah Begum, ek Rajput princess\nthi) — unhone 1606 mein apne pita ke against rebel kiya, haar gaye, andha kar diye gaye, aur baad\nmein unke bhai Khurram (Shah Jahan) ke orders par maar diye gaye. [Q26]\n10. Nur Jahan's Junta\n● Nur Jahan ne ek powerful faction banayi thi jise 'Nur Jahan's Junta' kehte hain, jo Jahangir ke reign\nmein Mughal administration ko bahut influence karti thi — is Junta mein 5 members the: Nur Jahan\nkhud, unki maa Asmat Begum, unke pita Mirza Ghiyas Beg (Itmad-ud-Daula), unke bhai Asaf Khan, aur\nPrince Khurram (Shah Jahan).\n Emperor Jahangir khud is faction ke MEMBER NAHI the — wo\n⚠️\ninfluenced hone wale ruler the. [Q27]\n●\n Mahabat Khan, Nur Jahan's Junta ke member NAHI the — wo ek independent aur powerful general\n⚠️\nthe jinhone actually Nur Jahan ke badhte influence ke against revolt kiya tha. [Q28]\n11. Itmad-ud-Daula's Tomb & Pietra Dura\n● Itmad-ud-Daula (Mirza Ghiyas Beg) ka tomb, Agra mein, unki beti Nur Jahan ne 1622-1628 AD ke\nbeech, unki mrityu ke baad banwaya tha — ye elegant monument Yamuna river ke left bank par hai,\npoori tarah white marble se bana. [Q29]\n● 'Pietra Dura' ek inlay technique hai jisme cut-fitted, highly polished coloured stones (semi-precious\nstones) use karke images ya floral designs banaye jaate hain — India mein ye technique sabse pehle\nextensively Itmad-ud-Daula ke tomb mein use hui thi (jo Nur Jahan ne banwaya). [Q30]\n12. Mughal Monuments — Important Match Lists"," ● Match: Babur → Sambhal mein Jama Masjid banwayi; Humayun → Delhi mein Din Panah city ki\nsthapna ki; Akbar → Agra Fort mein Jahangiri Mahal banwaya; Jahangir → Sikandara mein Akbar's\nMausoleum complete kiya. [Q31]\n●\n Trap: Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya ka tomb Ghiyaspur, Delhi mein hai, Ajmer mein NAHI (galat match)\n⚠️\n\n— Ajmer, Khwaja Muinuddin Chishti ki Dargah ke liye famous hai. Baaki 3 pairs perfectly matched hain.\n[Q33]\n13. Govind Palace, Datia\n● Govind Palace (Hindu architecture ka excellent example, 7-storey building) Datia (Madhya Pradesh)\nmein situated hai — Raja Bir Singh Deo (Jahangir ke close friend) ne 1614 AD mein bricks-stones se ise\nbanwaya. Ye Bundelas ki architecture ka ek excellent specimen hai. [Q32]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Jahangir Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0186","t":"17 Shah Jahan","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL DYNASTY — SHAH JAHAN — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Shah Jahan's Empire & the Qandahar Dispute\n2. Kavindracharya — Court Scholar\n3. Shah Jahan's Balkh Campaign\n4. Poet Kaleem — The Poet-Laureate\n5. Mumtaz Mahal & the Taj Mahal\n6. Delhi Monuments — Jama Masjid, Red Fort & the Capital Shift\n7. Dara Shikoh — Scholar, Translator & Titles\n8. Shah Jahan's Reign — The Golden Age Debate\n9. The Kohinoor Diamond\n10. The Abolition of the 'Sijda' Custom\n11. Aurangzeb — Governor of Deccan\n1. Shah Jahan's Empire & the Qandahar Dispute\n● Map-based question ka shaded area Shah Jahan ki empire dikhata hai — Golconda unki territory ka\nhissa NAHI thi, use Aurangzeb ne 1687 mein (baad mein) capture kiya tha. [Q1]\n● Qandahar, Iran ke Shah aur Mughal rulers ke beech dispute ka root cause tha — ye dono dynasties ke\nliye prestige ka issue ban gaya tha, kyunki dono ki colonial expansion Qandahar ki suzerainty par\ndepend karti thi. [Q2]\n● Qandahar ka nuksaan Mughal empire ke liye strategically ek bada jhatka tha — isse Mughal Kingdom\nbahri attacks ke liye vulnerable ho gayi. Aakhir mein, Shah Jahan ke period mein Qandahar Mughals ke\nhaathon se nikal gaya. [Q3]\n2. Kavindracharya — Court Scholar\n● Kavindracharya (Kavindra Acharya Saraswati, Banaras ke ek great Sanskrit scholar) ne Banaras aur\nAllahabad (Prayagraj) par pilgrim tax abolish karwane ke liye Mughal emperor Shah Jahan ke saamne\nBanaras ke Pandits ka ek delegation lead kiya tha — wo Shah Jahan ke dependent poet the, aur unki\nlanguage mein Awadhi-Braj ka perfect combination tha. [Q4, Q5]\n3. Shah Jahan's Balkh Campaign\n● Shah Jahan ke Balkh (aur Badakshan) campaign ka motive tha — Kabul se lagi hui in areas mein ek\nfriendly ruler secure karna, na ki Samarqand-Ferghana (Mughal homelands) conquer karna. Isse\nPersian representative hataakar Ghazni-Khyber ke pass rehne wale rebel Afghan tribes ko control karne\nmein madad milti, aur ye Mughals-Persians ke beech ek buffer state ban jaata. [Q6]\n4. Poet Kaleem — The Poet-Laureate"," ● Poet Kaleem (Abu Jalih), Shah Jahan ke darbar ke member bane aur unke reign ke 'Poet-Laureate' the.\n[Q7]\n5. Mumtaz Mahal & the Taj Mahal\n● Mumtaz Mahal ka asli naam 'Arjumand Bano Begum' tha — wo Asaf Khan ki beti thi, jinki shaadi Prince\nKhurram (Mughal Emperor Jahangir ke bete, baad mein Shah Jahan) se hui thi. [Q8]\n● Taj Mahal, Hindu aur Iranian architecture ke coordination (samanjasya) ka best example hai — Shah\nJahan ne India, Persia aur Middle Asia se engineers-architects bulaye the iska construction karne ke\nliye. [Q9]\n6. Delhi Monuments — Jama Masjid, Red Fort & the Capital Shift\n● Delhi ki famous Jama Masjid Shah Jahan ne banwayi thi — unhone apne reign mein ek badi legacy\nchhodi, jisme Diwan-e-Aam, Diwan-e-Khas, Sheesh Mahal, Moti Masjid (Agra) jaisi buildings shaamil\nhain. [Q10, Q11]\n● Shah Jahan ne Mughal empire ki capital Agra se Delhi (Shahjahanabad) shift ki thi. [Q12]\n● Match: Alai Darwaza (Delhi) → Alauddin Khalji; Buland Darwaza (Fatehpur Sikri) → Akbar; Moti Masjid\n(Agra) → Shah Jahan; Moti Masjid (Delhi) → Aurangzeb. [Q13]\n● Shah Jahan ne Delhi mein 'Red Fort' (Lal Qila) banwaya tha — unhone capital Agra se Shahjahanabad\n(Delhi) shift ki aur apne naam par ise basaya. Red Fort ek irregular octagon shape mein hai, west aur\neast mein lambi sides hain, 2 main gates ke saath. [Q14, Q15]\n7. Dara Shikoh — Scholar, Translator & Titles\n● Upanishads ka Persian mein translation Shah Jahan ke reign mein hua tha, unke bete Dara Shikoh ne\n— is translation ka naam 'Sirr-i-Akbar' tha, jisme 52 Upanishads translate ki gayi. Lenpool ne unhe unki\ntolerance-generosity ki wajah se 'Little Akbar' kaha. 'Majma-ul-Bahrain' Dara Shikoh ki original creation\nhai. [Q16, Q19, Q20]\n● Shah Jahan ne apne bete Dara Shikoh ko 'Shah Buland Iqbal' (ya 'Shah-i-Iqbal') ki title di thi. [Q17, Q18]\n● 'Mazm-ul-Baharin' (Mazzmaul Bahainna), Dara Shikoh ki ek original composition hai — 'Sirr-i-Akbar'\nunka Upanishads ka translation hai, jabki 'Mazm-ul-Baharin' unki khud ki likhi hui rachna hai. [Q21]\n● Dara Shikoh ko Baluchi chieftain Malik Jeevan ne Aurangzeb ke hawale kar diya tha — Aurangzeb\ndwara appoint ki gayi ek special Judicial Committee ne Dara ko heretic declare karke unhe maar dalne\nka order diya. Unki mrityu 1659 AD mein hui — unka sar Taj Mahal complex (Agra) mein aur body\nHumayun's Tomb (Delhi) mein dafnayi gayi. [Q22]\n● Shah Jahan ke sabse bade bete Dara Shikoh, Hindu scriptures padhne wale pehle Muslim the — ek\nhighly educated scholar-author, unhone Yogvashishtha, Bhagwad Gita jaise texts Persian mein translate\nkiye. [Q23]"," 8. Shah Jahan's Reign — The Golden Age Debate\n● Dr. A.L. Srivastava ne apni book 'Mughalkaleen Bharat' (1526-1803 AD) mein likha ki Shah Jahan ka\nreign medieval Indian history ka 'Golden Period' tha — halaki ye sach sirf art aur architecture ke basis\npar hai. J.N. Sarkar aur V.A. Smith is baat ko accept nahi karte, lekin R.S. Sharma is fact ko accept\nkarte hain. [Q24]\n9. The Kohinoor Diamond\n● Duniya ke famous diamonds mein se 'Kohinoor' (Golconda ki mines mein discover hua) Mir Jumla ne\nShah Jahan ko present kiya tha — Mir Jumla, Golconda ke Sultan Abdullah Qutub Shah (1626-1672\nAD) ke minister the, jo Mir Jumla ke Shah Jahan ka Mansab accept karne se gusse mein aa gaye the.\nBaad mein Mir Jumla ko Agra bulaakar 'Muazzam Khan' ki title di gayi. [Q25]\n10. The Abolition of the 'Sijda' Custom\n● Shah Jahan ne Persian court custom 'Sijda' (jhukna) ko abolish kiya, jo Balban ne shuru ki thi — ye\n1636-37 AD mein hua tha. [Q26]\n11. Aurangzeb — Governor of Deccan\n● Aurangzeb, Shah Jahan ke reign ke zyadatar hisse ke liye Deccan ke governor rahe — pehli baar 1636-\n44 AD mein, aur doosri baar 1653-1658 AD mein. [Q27]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Shah Jahan Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0187","t":"18 Aurangzeb","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL DYNASTY — AURANGZEB — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The War of Succession — Aurangzeb's Rise\n2. The Rebellion of Prince Akbar\n3. The Treaty of Purandar with Shivaji\n4. Aurangzeb's Character — 'Zinda Peer'\n5. Foreign Travellers During Aurangzeb's Reign\n6. The First Mughal Conflict with the British\n7. Deccan Conquests — Bijapur & Golconda\n8. Hindu Generals & Officials in the Mughal Army\n9. Religious Policy — Jizya & Jihad\n10. Bibi Ka Maqbara\n11. Aurangzeb's Family — Daughters & Sisters\n12. Saint Ramdas\n13. Moti Masjid, Red Fort\n1. The War of Succession — Aurangzeb's Rise\n● Assertion-Reason: Aurangzeb hi Shah Jahan ke successor bane (sahi Assertion) — lekin primogeniture\nka rule (jisme sabse bade bete ko property milti hai) follow NAHI kiya gaya (galat Reason). Wo ek war of\nsuccession ke baad force se gaddi par baithe — us waqt succession ke koi clear rules nahi the, ye sirf\npower ki baat thi. [Q1]\n● Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb ki coronation 2 baar hui — pehli 21 July 1658 ko Delhi mein, aur doosri 5\nJune 1659 ko, Khajwa aur Deorai battles mein safalta ke baad. [Q2]\n● 'Battle of Dharmat' (Madhya Pradesh, Ujjain ke pass) Aurangzeb aur Dara Shikoh ke beech, apne pita\nShah Jahan ki gaddi ke liye ladi gayi thi — Dara Shikoh ko Raja Jaswant Singh ka support tha, aur\nAurangzeb ko Prince Murad ka. 15 April 1658 ko Aurangzeb jeet gaye. [Q3, Q5]\n● Battles ka chronological order: Battle of Bilgram/Kannauj (1540 AD, Sher Shah ne Humayun ko haraya)\n→ Battle of Sarnal (1572 AD, Gujarat, Akbar ne Ibrahim Mirza ko haraya) → Battle of Dharmat (1658\nAD, Aurangzeb ne Dara Shikoh ko haraya) → Battle of Jajau (1707 AD, Bahadur Shah-I vs Muhammad\nAzam Shah, Aurangzeb ki mrityu ke baad succession ke liye). [Q4]\n● Aurangzeb ke reign ke events ka chronological order: Shuja ki Banaras ke pass haar (Battle of\nBahadurpur, February 1658) → Dharmat mein jeet (15 April 1658) → Battle of Samugarh (29 May 1658)\n→ Battle of Deorai (March 1659). [Q6]\n● Prince Sulaiman Shikoh (Dara Shikoh ke bete), Aurangzeb se haarne ke baad, Srinagar (Garhwal,\nPrithvi Singh ki kingdom) mein sharan liye the — lekin unke successor Medini Singh ne unhe Aurangzeb\nke hawale kar diya. Unhe Gwalior Fort mein qaid karke, opium ki excessive dose deke maar diya gaya.\n[Q7]\n2. The Rebellion of Prince Akbar\n● Prince Muhammad Akbar (Aurangzeb ke bete) ne 1681 AD mein apne pita ke against revolt ki —\nRajputs (Rathores aur Sisodias) ke saath alliance karke, isse Aurangzeb ki Rajputana mein position\nkamzor ho gayi. [Q8]"," 3. The Treaty of Purandar with Shivaji\n● Aurangzeb ne Raja Jai Singh (Amber) ko Shivaji ke against ladne bheja tha — unhone Purandar Fort\n(jaha Shivaji apna family-treasure rakhte the) ko besiege kiya. Shivaji ne Jai Singh ke saath negotiations\nshuru ki, aur 1665 AD mein 'Treaty of Purandar' sign hui. [Q9]\n4. Aurangzeb's Character — 'Zinda Peer'\n● Aurangzeb ek remarkable insaan the, jo baaki Mughals se alag extraordinary personal qualities rakhte\nthe — unhone high moral standards maintain kiye, austere (sadagi bhari) lifestyle jee, aur vices-\npleasures-extravagance se door rahe. Isi pious-simple life ki wajah se orthodox Muslims unhe 'Zinda\nPeer' (jeeta-jaagta saint) kehte the, kuch log 'Shahi Darvesh' bhi kehte the. [Q10, Q11]\n5. Foreign Travellers During Aurangzeb's Reign\n●\n Disputed: Aurangzeb ke reign mein aane wale notable European travellers the Francois Bernier,\n⚠️\nJean-Baptiste Tavernier aur Niccolao Manucci — diye gaye options mein se koi bhi sahi nahi tha (Peter\nMundy, Shah Jahan ke reign mein aaye; Hawkins-Thomas Roe, Jahangir ke; Antonio Monserrate, Akbar\nke), isliye ye question disputed hai. [Q12]\n6. The First Mughal Conflict with the British\n● Mughals aur British (East India Company) ke beech pehla conflict 1686 AD mein, Aurangzeb ke reign\nmein hua tha — Mughal governor Shaista Khan ne British ko Hooghly se bhagaya, jisse Job Charnock\njaise logo ko peeche hatna pada. [Q13]\n7. Deccan Conquests — Bijapur & Golconda\n● Aurangzeb ne apne reign ke aakhri hisse mein Deccan campaigns par bahut samay bitaya — unhone\nindependent Shia states Bijapur (1686 AD) aur Golconda (1687 AD) ko successfully capture kiya. [Q14,\nQ15]\n● Jab Aurangzeb ne 1687 AD mein Golconda Fort seize kiya, tab wahan ke raja Abul Hasan Qutb Shah\n(Tana Shah bhi kehlaate the), Qutb Shahi dynasty se the — kaha jaata hai ki Aurangzeb ne Golconda\nfort 'sone ki chaabiyo' se khola tha (ek Afghan guard ko rishwat dekar), waise hi jaise Akbar ne Asirgarh\nFort khola tha. [Q16]\n● Map-based question: diya gaya map Aurangzeb ki kingdom (1707 mein unki mrityu ke waqt) dikhata hai\n— Mughal empire apni maximum extent par thi, poore Indian subcontinent ke lagbhag saare hisso ko\ncover karti hui, South mein Jinji tak. Isme Bijapur aur Golconda (late 1680s mein jeete gaye) bhi shaamil\nthe. [Q17]"," 8. Hindu Generals & Officials in the Mughal Army\n● Apni religious orthodoxy ki reputation ke bawajood, Mughal army mein sabse zyada Hindu Generals\n(Mansabdars) Aurangzeb ke reign mein the — unke court mein 31.6% Hindu commanders the (zyadatar\nMarathas aur Rajputs), jabki Akbar ke reign mein ye ratio sirf 22.5% tha. [Q18]\n● Aurangzeb ne apne reign mein sabse zyada Hindu officials (Mansabdars) appoint kiye — ye mainly\nmilitary zaroorat ki wajah se hua, khaaskar Deccan campaigns ke dauran. [Q19]\n9. Religious Policy — Jizya & Jihad\n● Akbar ne Jizya tax abolish kar diya tha, lekin Aurangzeb ne ise 1679 AD mein non-Muslims par dobara\nlagu (re-impose) kar diya — Hindus ko unki income ke hisaab se 3 classes mein baata gaya (12, 24, ya\n48 Dirhams tax). Women, slaves, 14 saal se chhote bachche, aur bhikhari isse exempt the. [Q20]\n● Aurangzeb ek orthodox Sunni Muslim the, jo Quranic law ko strictly enforce karne ki koshish karte the\n— unke 'Jihad' ka matlab tha non-Muslims ki zameen (Dar-ul-Harb) ko Islam ki zameen (Dar-ul-Islam)\nmein badalna. [Q21]\n10. Bibi Ka Maqbara\n● Aurangzeb ne 'Bibi Ka Maqbara' (Bibi ki Tomb) Aurangabad (Maharashtra) mein apni patni Rabia-ud-\nDaurani (Dilras Banu Begum) ke liye banwaya tha — intricate designs wala ye architectural wonder, Taj\nMahal se resemblance ki wajah se 'The Mini Taj' ya doosra 'Taj Mahal' kehlaata hai. [Q22, Q23]\n11. Aurangzeb's Family — Daughters & Sisters\n● Mehrunnisa (aur Zeb-un-Nissa, jo bhi famous hain), Emperor Aurangzeb ki betiyan thi — Jahan Ara,\nRoshan Ara aur Gauhar Ara, Shah Jahan ki betiyan (Aurangzeb ki behnein) thi. [Q24]\n● Aurangzeb ne apni badi behen Jahan Ara ko 'Sahibat-uz-Zamani' ki title di thi — Jahan Ara, Shah\nJahan aur Mumtaz Mahal ki sabse badi beti thi. Dara Shikoh ko unka pehle support hone ke bawajood,\nAurangzeb ne unka respect kiya aur unki position wapas restore ki. [Q25]\n12. Saint Ramdas\n● Samarth Ramdas (1608-1681 AD), Maharashtra ke ek great saint aur Chhatrapati Shivaji ke spiritual\nguru the — wo Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb ke samkalin the. (Guru Ramdas, chauthe Sikh guru, Akbar\nke samkalin the — inhe confuse mat karna.) [Q26]\n13. Moti Masjid, Red Fort"," ● Delhi ke Red Fort complex ke andar ki 'Moti Masjid' (Pearl Mosque) Aurangzeb ne 1659-1660 ke beech\napne personal use ke liye banwayi thi. (Agra Fort ki Moti Masjid Shah Jahan ne banwayi thi — dono ko\nconfuse mat karna.) [Q27]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Aurangzeb Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0188","t":"19 Mughal Administration","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL ADMINISTRATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Administrative Divisions — Suba, Sarkar, Pargana & Chakla\n2. Central Officials — The Mir Bakshi\n3. The Military Character of the Mughal Empire\n4. Foreign Employees in Mughal Service — Manucci\n5. Ahadis — The Gentlemen-at-Arms\n6. Muhtasib — The Censor of Public Morals\n7. The Mansabdari System — Purpose & Features\n8. Jagirdar vs Zamindar\n9. Land Revenue — The Principal Source of State Income\n10. Jahangir's Ban on Tobacco\n11. Madad-i-Mash — Revenue-Free Land Grants\n12. Finance Department Officials — The Diwans\n13. The Currency System\n14. Mughal-Era Canals\n1. Administrative Divisions — Suba, Sarkar, Pargana & Chakla\n● Akbar ne apni empire ko administrative convenience ke liye units mein baata — poori empire 'Subas'\n(provinces) mein bati thi. Subas aage 'Sarkars' (districts) aur 'Parganas' (sub-districts) mein bate the —\nkai villages milkar ek Pargana banate the. Har Sarkar mein Faujdar, Amalguzar, Qazi, Kotwal, Bitiqhi\naur Khajandar jaise chief officers hote the. [Q1, Q2]\n● 'Chakla', Mughal period mein (khaaskar Shah Jahan ke reign mein) ek administrative division tha — ye\nSubah (province) aur Pargana (sub-district) ke beech ka ek territorial unit tha, lekin Sarkar (district) se\npoori tarah identical nahi tha. [Q18]\n2. Central Officials — The Mir Bakshi\n● Mughal period mein military ke head ko 'Mir Bakshi' kaha jaata tha — unhe darbar ke leading nobles\nappoint karte the. Wo intelligence gathering ke incharge the, aur military appointments-promotions ke\nliye emperor ko recommendations dete the. [Q3]\n● Mir Bakshi ka duty tha land revenue officials ki supervision karna, military department ki salaries handle\nkarne ke saath-saath — Sir Jadunath Sarkar ne unhe 'Pay Master' bhi kaha. [Q4]\n● Mughal Mansabdari system ke smooth functioning ke liye Mir Bakshi responsible the — Mansabdari\nsystem officials ki ranking aur unki civil-military duties, remuneration decide karti thi. [Q10]\n3. The Military Character of the Mughal Empire\n● Assertion-Reason: Mughal Empire ek pure military state thi (behas ka vishay hai, lekin zyadatar\nhistorians maante hain ki state machinery/Mansabdars ko military character di gayi thi — sahi Assertion)\n— Mughals ek badi army maintain karte the, jo central empire ke expansion-strengthening mein"," madadgar thi, isliye military power hi unka vital backbone tha (sahi Reason, jo Assertion ko explain karta\nhai). [Q5]\n4. Foreign Employees in Mughal Service — Manucci\n● Niccolao Manucci, ek Italian traveller, shuru mein Dara Shikoh ki Mughal army mein artilleryman ki tarah\nappoint hue the — Dara Shikoh ki 1659 mein mrityu ke baad, unhone Mughal service mein medico\n(physician) ki profession choose ki. [Q6]\n5. Ahadis — The Gentlemen-at-Arms\n● 'Ahadis' Akbar ki standing army ka hissa the (kuch hazaar ki sankhya mein) — kai ghodo se equipped,\nexcellent archers ki reputation rakhte the. Wo akele apni services offer karte the (kisi mounted retainer\nya chief ko follow nahi karte the), aur directly Emperor ke authority ke under the — Mirzas se koi\nattachment nahi rakhte the. [Q7]\n6. Muhtasib — The Censor of Public Morals\n● Mughal administration mein 'Muhtasib', public morals ke censor the — wo police-cum-judge ki tarah\nkaam karte the, Muslims ke beech Sharia (canon law) ka observance ensure karte the, aur public moral\nstandards maintain karte the. [Q8]\n7. The Mansabdari System — Purpose & Features\n● Medieval India mein Mansabdari system mainly clean administration effect karne ke liye introduce ki\ngayi thi — Akbar ne military aur civil service ke liye ek well-organised system banayi jo Mughal\nadministration ka main basis ban gayi. [Q9]\n● Mansab ka matlab tha rank/status — Mansabdars 33 classes mein bate hue the. 'Mashrut' (conditional\nrank) ka use hota tha, jisme temporary period ke liye Sawar rank badhayi jaati thi.\n Lekin 'Sawar' rank\n⚠️\n\nkabhi 'Zat' rank se zyada NAHI ho sakti thi — wo Zat ke barabar ya kam ho sakti thi, zyada nahi. [Q11]\n● Mansabdari system ki features: Zat aur Sawar ranks (Mansabs) grant kiye jaate the (sahi). Zat-Sawar\nratio ke basis par Mansabdars 3 classes mein bate the (First: Sawar=Zat; Second: Sawar=half-ya-zyada\nZat; Third: baaki). System hereditary NAHI thi — King hi appoint/promote/remove karta tha (galat\nstatement tha ki hereditary hai). Salaries cash (Naqdi) ya land assignments (Jagirs) ke through di jaati\nthi, centrally Diwan office se NAHI (galat statement). [Q12]\n● Mansabdari system statements: Ye system Akbar ne 1575 mein shuru ki thi, ye nobility-administration ki\nofficial structure thi (sahi). System hereditary NAHI thi — ek mansab merit-loyalty ke basis par diya jaata\ntha, aur mansabdar ki mrityu par wapas state ko revert ho jaata tha. [Q19]\n● Assertion-Reason: Mansabdari system Mughal period mein exist karti thi (sahi Assertion) —\nMansabdars ko unki qualification-loyalty ke basis par directly King appoint karta tha, heredity ke basis\npar nahi (sahi Reason bhi) — lekin merit-based selection hi is system ke exist karne ki wajah NAHI thi,"," ye system effective civil-military administration ke liye thi (isliye Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation\nnahi deta). [Q20]\n● Akbar dwara introduce ki gayi Mansabdari system military aur civil — dono departments mein common\nthi (sahi statement A) — isliye sabhi Mansabdars sirf military commanders hi NAHI the, high-ranking civil\nservants, nobles aur administrators ko bhi mansabs di jaati thi (sahi statement B). [Q21]\n8. Jagirdar vs Zamindar\n● Jagirdar aur Zamindar mein antar: Jagirdars ko unki military-administrative salary ke against land\nassignments milti thi (judicial-police duties ke liye NAHI). Jagirdars ke land assignments transferable aur\nnon-hereditary the (shift ya seize kiye ja sakte the), jabki Zamindars ke revenue rights alag nature ke\nthe. [Q13]\n9. Land Revenue — The Principal Source of State Income\n● Mughal agrarian system ki central feature thi kisano se unki surplus produce ko land revenue ke roop\nmein alienate karna — ye Land Revenue (Lagaan/Maal) Mughal India mein State income ka sabse\nprimary-significant source tha. [Q14]\n● Mughal administrative terminology mein 'Maal' word primarily Land Revenue se related tha. [Q15]\n● 'Bantai' (Galla-Bakshi bhi kehte hain) medieval period mein revenue calculate karne ka ek system tha,\njisme actual produce ka hissa liya jaata tha. Sher Shah Suri ne revenue calculate karne ke 3 systems\nchuni thi: Nasq/Kankut, Nakadi/Jabti, aur Galla Bakshi/Bantai. [Q29]\n● North India mein Akbar ke reign mein, Dewan Todarmal ne ek highly systematic land revenue collection\nmethod (Zabt/Dahsala) establish ki — lekin ye system Deccan ke remote regions mein us waqt fully\nimplement NAHI hui thi. Wahan ke farmers 'number of plows' ke basis par land revenue dete the. [Q30]\n10. Jahangir's Ban on Tobacco\n● 1605 AD mein Portuguese ne India mein tobacco (tambaku) introduce ki thi, jo aam logo mein bahut\npopular ho gayi. Iske harmful effects aur rapid addiction dekhkar, Mughal Emperor Jahangir ne 1617 AD\nmein tobacco ke use par ban laga diya. [Q16]\n11. Madad-i-Mash — Revenue-Free Land Grants\n● 'Madad-i-Mash' (Suyurghal bhi kehte hain), Mughal administration mein revenue-free land grants ko\nindicate karta tha — ye grants pious/learned logo, saints, aur religious institutions-shrines ki\nmaintenance ke liye charity ki tarah di jaati thi. [Q17]\n12. Finance Department Officials — The Diwans"," ● Officer-Duty match: Diwan-i-Tan → Jagir aur Salaries dekhta tha; Mustaufi (Mustarfi) → State ke\nincome-expenditure ka auditor; Mushrif → Chief accountant/office officer; Vakianvis (Waqia-Nawis) →\nNews reporter, main events-firmans ki list maintain karta tha. [Q22]\n●\n Disputed: Mughal Emperors aur unke prominent Diwans (Finance Ministers) ka direct match: Akbar\n⚠️\n→ Muzaffar Khan Turbati; Jahangir → Ghiyas Beg Itmadud-Daulah; Shah Jahan → Sadullah Khan;\nAurangzeb → Asad Khan. Diye gaye options mein se koi bhi is sahi sequence ko reflect nahi karta —\noriginal answer key mein ek misprint ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q23]\n13. The Currency System\n● Assertion-Reason: Akbar ne Sher Shah Suri ke reforms se inspire hokar state ki currency ko\nsystematically regulate karne ki koshish ki (sahi Assertion) — Akbar aur unke successors ke time gold\ncoins (Mohur), silver coins (Rupee), aur copper coins (Dam) extensively circulate hote the — lekin same\ncopper coin naam continuity ka example hai, Akbar ke currency regulate karne ki wajah NAHI (isliye\nReason, Assertion ka sahi explanation nahi deta). [Q24]\n● Mughal Emperor Akbar ne apni religious tolerance aur cultural synthesis ki policy ko reflect karte hue,\nek special type ke gold-silver coins issue kiye the jinme Lord Ram aur Goddess Sita ki figures the, saath\nhi Devanagari script mein 'Ram-Siya' likha hota tha. [Q25]\n● Sher Shah ke reforms ke baad establish hui standard Mughal currency system mein 3 basic coins the:\nMohur (gold se bana), Rupee (silver se bana), aur Dam (copper se bana). [Q26]\n● Mughal dynasty ke founder Babur ne 'Shahrukh' naam ki ek silver coin introduce aur popularize ki thi —\nunhone apni jeeto ke baad ye coins issue ki. [Q27]\n● Mughal period mein coin categorization: current saal ke naye coins 'Taza Sikka' kehlaate the; current\nemperor ke reign mein widely circulate hone wale coins 'Chalani' kehlaate the; lekin purane emperors ke\nreign mein mint hue aur abhi bhi circulation mein rehne wale coins ko specifically 'Khazana' kaha jaata\ntha. [Q28]\n14. Mughal-Era Canals\n● Mughal-era 'Shahab Nahr' (Shahab Canal), Delhi Sultan Firuz Shah Tughluq ki purani 'Rajabwah' canal\nko renovate/repair karke banayi gayi thi — Akbar ke time Delhi ke Governor Shihabuddin Khan ne\nirrigation ke liye is canal ki repair ki, aur iska naam 'Shahab Nahr' rakha. [Q31]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mughal Administration Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0189","t":"02 Delhi Sultanate Slave Dynasty","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — SLAVE DYNASTY — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Qutbuddin Aybak — Founder of the Slave Dynasty\n2. The Qutub Minar & Associated Monuments\n3. Iltutmish — Real Founder of the Delhi Sultanate & the Capital Shift\n4. Iltutmish — Rivals & Administration\n5. Genghis Khan & the First Mongol Threat\n6. Raziyya Sultan — First Woman Ruler of Medieval India\n7. Balban — Rise & Grand Titles\n8. Balban — Policies & Court Culture\n9. Balban — Rebellions Faced\n1. Qutbuddin Aybak — Founder of the Slave Dynasty\n● Slave Dynasty (Delhi Sultanate period ki pehli, 5 unrelated dynasties mein se ek, 1206-1290 AD) ke\nfounder Qutbuddin Aybak the — unhone 1206 AD mein Delhi Sultanate ki gaddi sambhali. Aybak aur\nunke sabhi successors apne respective predecessors ke slaves the, isliye ise 'Slave Dynasty' kehte\nhain. [Q1, Q2]\n● Qutbuddin Aybak, Turkistan mein paida hue the, baad mein Muhammad Ghori ko slave ki tarah bech\ndiye gaye. Ghori ki mrityu ke baad, Lahore ke Amirs ne unhe power sambhalne ke liye invite kiya —\nunhone Lahore ko apni capital banaya, aur khud ko 'Malik' aur 'Sipahasalaar' ki title di. [Q8]\n● Sultan Qutbuddin Aybak ko 'Lakh Baksh' (lakho dene wala) kaha jaata tha, unki bahut zyada generosity\n(daan-dene ki aadat) ki wajah se. [Q3]\n● 1210 AD mein, Qutbuddin Aybak ki mrityu Chaugan (polo) khelte waqt ghode se gir kar hui thi — unhe\nLahore mein Anarkali Bazaar ke pass dafnaya gaya. [Q9]\n2. The Qutub Minar & Associated Monuments\n● Qutbuddin Aybak ne Delhi mein 'Quwwat-ul-Islam Mosque' banwani shuru ki, aur Ajmer (Rajasthan)\nmein 'Adhai Din Ka Jhonpra' (ek mosque) bhi — dono ka nirmaan unhone Muhammad Ghori ke aadesh\npar 1192 CE mein shuru karwaya. [Q4, Q5]\n● Qutub Minar ka construction bhi Qutbuddin Aybak ne shuru kiya tha (sirf pehla storey banaya) — baad\nmein unke damad-successor Iltutmish ne baaki stories banwakar isse complete kiya. Baad mein iski\ntopmost storey lightning se damage hui, jisse Firuz Shah Tughluq ne rebuild kiya aur 5th floor add kiya.\nGhiyasuddin Tughluq ne iske construction mein KOI\n\nयोगदानNAHI diya. [Q6, Q7]\n3. Iltutmish — Real Founder of the Delhi Sultanate & the Capital Shift\n● Iltutmish (1211-36 AD) ko Delhi Sultanate ka 'real founder' maana jaata hai — unhone Lahore se apni\ncapital shift karke Delhi ko Sultanate ki capital banaya, jise ek prominent political center bana diya. [Q10,\nQ12, Q13]"," ● Iltutmish pehle Sultan the jinhone purely Arabic coinage introduce ki — unhone silver 'Tanka' (175\ngrains) aur copper 'Jital' — 2 basic coins issue kiye. [Q11]\n● Iltutmish ko Delhi ka pehla legally independent Muslim ruler (Sultan) maana jaata hai — Baghdad ke\nCaliph Al-Muntasir Billah ne 1229 AD mein unhe 'Sultan-i-Azam' ki title deke investiture di. Qutbuddin\nAybak, Slave Dynasty ke founder hone ke bawajood, Lahore se hi raj karte rahe aur unhone kabhi\nformally 'Sultan' ki title nahi li. [Q14]\n● 1229 AD mein, Baghdad ke Caliph ne Iltutmish ko 'Khillat' (izzat ka gown) di — is official recognition se\nSultanate theoretically 'Dar-ul-Islam' ka hissa ban gayi, Baghdad ke Caliph ke adheen. [Q15]\n● Iltutmish ko 'A Slave of a Slave' kaha jaata hai — Qutbuddin Aybak khud Muhammad Ghori ke slave\nthe, aur Iltutmish originally Qutbuddin Aybak ke slave the. Baad mein Iltutmish ne Aybak ki beti se\nshaadi ki aur eventually khud Sultan ban gaye. [Q16]\n4. Iltutmish — Rivals & Administration\n● Iltutmish ke main rivals the: Tajuddin Yalduz (Ghazni mein), Nasiruddin Qabacha (Sindh mein), aur Ali\nMardan (Lakhnauti, Bengal mein). Malik Altunia unke rival NAHI the — wo ek prominent noble the\njinhone baad mein Iltutmish ki beti Raziyya se shaadi ki. [Q17]\n● 1225 AD mein, Iltutmish ne Hisamuddin Awaz ko Rajmahal ki pahadiyo (Teliyagarhi ke pass) mein\nharaaya aur Bihar Shareef-Barh annex kiya. Awaz ke subordination accept karne ke baad, Iltutmish ne\nMalik Jani ko Bihar ka naya Subedar (Governor) niyukt kiya. [Q25]\n5. Genghis Khan & the First Mongol Threat\n● Mongol invader Genghis Khan, Iltutmish ke reign mein India ke North-West frontier tak pahunche the —\nwo Khwarizm ke fugitive prince Jalaluddin Mingburni ka peecha kar rahe the, jinhone Iltutmish se\nasylum maanga tha. Iltutmish ne bade samajhdari se unhe asylum dene se mana kar diya, taaki\nGenghis Khan ko provoke na kiya jaaye — isse unki nayi-nayi empire Mongol devastation se bach gayi.\n[Q19, Q20]\n● 1221 AD mein, Genghis Khan ke Mongols Indus river ke kinare pehli baar dikhe the — ye Iltutmish ke\nreign mein hua tha. [Q21, Q22]\n● Genghis Khan (Changez Khan) ka original naam 'Temujin' (Temuchin) tha — unke pita Yesugei the.\nUnhone hi Mongol Empire ki foundation rakhi aur uska vistaar kiya. [Q23]\n● Statement check: Iltutmish ke reign mein hi Chengiz Khan Indus tak pahunche the (sahi) — Taimur ne\n1398 AD mein Nasir-ud-Din Mahmud Shah Tughluq ke reign mein attack kiya tha, Muhammad bin\nTughluq (1325-1351 AD) ke NAHI (galat statement). Vasco-da-Gama 1498 AD mein Kerala coast par\npahunche the, uss waqt Vijayanagara par Immadi Narasimha ka raj tha. [Q24]\n6. Raziyya Sultan — First Woman Ruler of Medieval India\n● Raziyya Sultan (1236-1240 AD), Delhi Sultanate ki gaddi par baithne wali pehli aur ekmatra woman thi\n— Turkish nobles ek woman ko apna ruler maanne ke liye reluctant the, khaaskar jab unhone inki power\nko challenge kiya. [Q18]"," ● Raziyya Begum ko gaddi se hataane ke peeche ambitious Turkish nobles (Chahalgani) the — Bhatinda\nke governor Malik Altunia ki leadership mein unhone revolt kiya aur Raziyya ko successfully power se\nhata diya. [Q26]\n7. Balban — Rise & Grand Titles\n● Balban ka poora naam 'Ghiyasuddin Balban' tha (original naam Baha-ud-din) — wo Delhi ki Mamluk\n(Slave) dynasty ke 9th Sultan the (1266-1286 AD). Sultan banne se pehle, wo Nasiruddin Mahmud ke\nWazir/de facto ruler the, jinhone unhe 'Ulugh Khan' ki title di thi. [Q27]\n● Balban ne Persian traditions se inspire hokar apna political model banaya — unhone khud ko God ka\nrepresentative ('Niyamat-e-Khudai') maana, aur 'Zil-e-Ilahi' (Zil-i-Ilahi, matlab 'Shadow/Image of God') ki\ngrand title apnaayi. [Q32, Q37]\n● Balban, Delhi Sultanate ke pehle ruler the jinhone 'theory of Kingship' propound ki, jo 'divine right of\nkings' ke theory jaisi thi — unhone declare kiya ki Sultan God ka representative hai aur unki authority ko\nnobles ya public challenge nahi kar sakte. [Q33]\n● Balban ne apne inscription mein (Garhmukteshwar, aaj ke UP ki ek mosque ki deewaron par) khud ko\n'Helper of a Caliph' (Nasir Amir-ul-Momin) declare kiya tha. [Q38]\n8. Balban — Policies & Court Culture\n● Balban 'blood and iron' (khoon aur lohe) ki policy apnaane ke liye famous the — unhone apne\ndushmano ko kuchalne aur Sultan ki absolute authority establish karne ke liye stern, autocratic rule\nmaintain ki (jaise Bengal mein Tughril Khan ke rebellion ko ruthlessly kuchalna). [Q28, Q29]\n● Assertion-Reason: Balban ne khud ko emperor declare kiya, ise God ka divine act maankar, taaki crown\nki prestige restore ho (sahi Assertion) — unhone Mongols ke against north-west border par mazboot\nforts bhi banwaye (sahi Reason bhi) — lekin ye power-centralization mainly Sultan ki internal authority\nrestore karne ke liye tha, sirf/mainly Mongol threat ki wajah se nahi (isliye Reason, Assertion ka\nsahi/complete explanation nahi deta). [Q30, Q31]\n● Balban ne apne court mein Iranian kings ki traditions introduce ki, Sultan ki prestige badhane ke liye —\njaise Sijada (jhukna/prostration) aur Paibos (raja ke paav choomna) rituals, aur Persian New Year\nfestival 'Nawruz' ka grand celebration. [Q34, Q35]\n●\n Trap: Balban ke baare mein GALAT statement — unhone 'Iqtadari System' introduce NAHI ki, ye\n⚠️\nsystem Iltutmish ne systematically introduce ki thi. Balban ne 'theory of kingship' (Niyamat-e-Khudai)\nzaroor propound ki, Iltutmish ke banaye '40 Turkish nobles' (Turkan-e-Chahalgani) ke group ko\nsuccessfully destroy kiya. [Q36]\n9. Balban — Rebellions Faced\n● Tughril Khan (Bengal ke Subedar) ne Balban ke reign mein, 1279 AD mein, Amin Khan ki Bengal mein\nappointment ke protest mein revolt ki thi — Balban khud Bengal march karke gaye aur is rebellion ko\nkuchal diya, jisse Tughril Khan ko execute kiya gaya. [Q39]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Slave Dynasty Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0190","t":"20 Music and Paintings of Mughal Period","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUSIC & PAINTINGS OF THE MUGHAL PERIOD — FULL MIND MAP\n🎨\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Mughal Painting — Origins & Overview\n2. Painting Under Akbar — Karkhanas & Artists\n3. Regional Schools of Miniature Painting\n4. Dastan-i-Amir Hamza\n5. Painting Under Jahangir\n6. Music at the Mughal Court — Aurangzeb & the Veena\n7. Ragas & Musical Concepts\n8. Swami Haridas & the Haridasi School\n9. Tansen — Life, Titles & Legacy\n10. Akbar's Own Musical Training\n11. Tappa Style & Muhammad Shah's Court\n1. Mughal Painting — Origins & Overview\n● Mughal paintings, Indian painting ki history mein ek landmark hain — ye Indian, Persian aur Islamic\npaintings ka unique blend the. Ustad Mansur (17th century painter) nature-plants-birds-animals depict\nkarne mein excel karte the — battle scenes aur court life bhi bahut painted hoti thi. [Q1]\n● Mughal painting ki foundation Humayun ne rakhi thi — unke Persia-Afghanistan exile ke saalon mein.\nWahan unki mulaqaat 2 distinguished painters — Khwaja Abdus Samad aur Mir Sayyid Ali — se hui,\njinse Humayun aur unke bete Akbar ne drawing ki taleem li. [Q2]\n2. Painting Under Akbar — Karkhanas & Artists\n● Akbar ko painting ka bahut shauk tha — unke reign mein painting ko ek imperial establishment\n(Karkhana) ki tarah organize kiya gaya, jise 'Tasvir Khana' kaha jaata tha, jaha painters kaam karte the.\n[Q3]\n● 'Daswant aur Basawan', famous painters, Akbar ke darbar ke courtiers the — Akbar, Daswant ke kaam\nse itne impressed hue ki unhone unhe apne samay ka leading painter banne mein support kiya. Abul\nFazl ki 'Ain-i-Akbari' mein Akbar-era ke painters ke naam mile hain: Daswant, Basawan, Keshav Lal,\nMukund, Mishkin, Farrukh, Jagan, Mahesh, waghera. [Q6]\n● European paintings, Akbar ke darbar mein Portuguese ke through introduce hui thi — Mughal painters\nne unse 2 khaas cheezein sikhi: person ki portrait banana, aur scene mein door ki cheezon ko chhota\ndikhana (perspective). Painting ka development Humayun period mein shuru hua tha, lekin European\ninfluence Akbar ke reign mein aayi. Mishkin bhi is period ke ek expert painter the. [Q7]\n3. Regional Schools of Miniature Painting\n● Mughal School of Painting ne various Indian miniature art schools (Pahari, Rajasthani, Kangra) ki spinal\ncord ki tarah role play kiya — lekin 'Kalighata' school (Bengal mein originate hui) indigenous thi, Hindu\ndeities aur rozmarra ki zindagi depict karti thi, aur Mughal influence se affected NAHI hui. [Q4]"," ● 'Pahari School', 'Rajput School', 'Mughal School' aur 'Kangra School' — ye medieval India ki painting ki\nalag-alag styles hain. Pahari (hill) paintings North-Western Himalayan region ke alag-alag hill states\nmein banti thi (Himachal Pradesh, J&K jaisi areas). [Q13]\n● 'Kishan Garh' School (Rajasthan ki traditional painting style ka hissa) painting ke liye famous hai — iski\nstyle courtesan 'Bani Thani' (Indian Mona Lisa) ki khoobsurat depiction ke liye jaani jaati hai. Sawant\nSingh (1748 AD mein gaddi par baithe, art ke bade scholar-patron) is famous school ke peeche real\ninspiration the. [Q14]\n4. Dastan-i-Amir Hamza\n●\n Multiple Correct: 'Dastan-i-Amir Hamza' (sabse pehla Mughal illustrated manuscript) ko illustrate\n⚠️\nkarne mein Abdus Samad AUR Mir Sayyid Ali — dono ne 15 saal ki supervision mein, 50 se zyada\nartists ke saath, is kaam ko complete kiya. [Q5]\n5. Painting Under Jahangir\n● Match: Jahangiri painters — Abul Hasan, Ustad Mansur, Farrukh Begh, Bishan Das, Aqa Reza,\nMuhammad Nadir, Muhammad Murad, Manohar aur Govardhan. Mir Sayyid Ali aur Abdus Samad ne\npainting ki foundation Humayun ke period mein rakhi thi (Akbar ke time bhi continue hui). [Q8]\n●\n Trap: Khwaja Abdus Samad, Jahangir ke period ke painter NAHI the — wo Humayun aur Akbar ke\n⚠️\nreign ke painter the. Mansur, Manohar aur Abul Hasan — ye Jahangir ke time ke painters the. Jahangir\nke reign (1605-27 AD) mein Mughal painting apne zenith par pahunchi. [Q9]\n● Mughal Painting Jahangir (1605-27 AD) ke reign mein flourish hui — unki gehri artistic inclination thi.\nPainter Ustad Mansur, janwaro-paudho ko document karne wale sabse best artists mein se ek bane,\njinhe Jahangir describe karte the. [Q10]\n● Jahangir mainly Painting ki art ko patronize karte the — unke rule mein ye apne zenith par pahunchi.\n[Q11]\n● Jahangir ne emphasis illustrated manuscripts (grand fictional stories, jo Akbar ke time prominent thi) se\nhatakar albums (Muraqqas) aur individual portraits, birds-flowers-animals ki studies ki taraf shift kiya —\nunhe apni khud ki zindagi ke events depict karne wali paintings mein bhi interest tha. [Q12]\n6. Music at the Mughal Court — Aurangzeb & the Veena\n● Aurangzeb ne apne darbar mein music ko anti-Islamic maankar ban kar diya tha — lekin unke tenure\nmein hi Indian classical music par sabse zyada books likhi gayi (interesting irony). Unke anti-music\ndecrees ke bawajood, Aurangzeb khud ek great instrumentalist the — Veena bajaane mein expert the.\n[Q15]\n7. Ragas & Musical Concepts"," ● 'Todi' Raga traditionally subah (morning) mein gaayi jaati hai — ye Hindustani classical music ka ek\nRaga hai, jo Todi thaat (10 modes mein se ek) ko naam deta hai, Mughal darbar mein minstrels dwara\nbar-bar gaayi jaati thi. [Q16]\n● Raja Mansingh Tomar, Tansen, aur Sadarang-Adarang (Niyamat Khan-Firoz Khan) — teeno Hindustani\nmusic ke great personalities-composers the.\n 'Mal Gurjari' koi vyakti NAHI hai — ye ek Raga (musical\n⚠️\n\nmode) hai jo Raja Mansingh Tomar (Gwalior) ne invent ki thi. [Q23]\n8. Swami Haridas & the Haridasi School\n● Swami Haridas, ek spiritual poet-classical musician the, jinhe bahut saari devotional compositions\n(khaaskar Dhrupad style mein) ka credit jaata hai — wo 'Haridasi School of mysticism' ke founder the,\njinke followers ne 5 worship-training centres (ashrams) banaye. Tansen, Baiju Bawra aur Gopal Nayak\nne unse hi training li thi. [Q17]\n● Akbar ke reign mein leading Dhrupad singers Tansen aur Swami Haridas the. Vilas Khan (Tansen ke\nbete) Jahangir ke reign ke main singer the, Akbar ke NAHI. Surdas ek Bhakti poet-singer the, lekin\nTansen-Haridas hi Akbar-era ke quintessential Dhrupad singers mane jaate hain. [Q19]\n9. Tansen — Life, Titles & Legacy\n●\n Trap: 'Tansen' ki title Emperor Akbar ne NAHI di — ye title unhe Gwalior ke Raja Vikramjit Singh ne\n⚠️\ndi thi. Akbar ne unhe 'Mian' ki title di. Tansen (Ramtanu Pandey), Hindustani classical music ke\nprominent figure the — unhone Mian ki Malhar jaisi kai Ragas invent ki, Dhrupads compose kiye, aur\napne patrons ke liye gaane likhe. [Q18]\n● Tansen ka tomb Gwalior mein hai — Sufi saint Hazrat Muhammad Ghaus ki tomb ke pass, jinki\nteachings se wo influenced the. [Q20]\n● Akbar se pehle, Tansen ne Rewa (Bhata region) ke Hindu King Raja Ramchandra Singh ke court aur\npatronage mein apna career shuru kiya aur zyadatar apni adult life bitayi — wahan unki widespread\nfame ne Mughal Emperor Akbar ka dhyan kheecha, jinhone unhe apne darbar mein invite kiya. [Q21]\n● Tansen ka asli naam 'Ramtanu Pandey' tha — wo Hindustani classical music ke prominent composer-\nmusician the, aur Akbar ke darbar ke Navaratnas (9 ratnon) mein se ek the. [Q22]\n10. Akbar's Own Musical Training\n● Akbar ko music ka bahut shauk tha aur wo khud ek learned musician the — unhone Lala Kalawant ki\nguidance mein Hindu vocal music ki taleem li, aur Naqqara (kettledrum) proficiency se bajaate the. [Q24]\n11. Tappa Style & Muhammad Shah's Court\n● 18th century mein, music (Tappa style samet) ko baad ke Mughal Emperor 'Muhammad Shah Rangila'\nke darbar mein bahut encouragement mila. Sadarang aur Adarang — unke darbar ke 2 great Khayal\nGayaki composers the. Tappa style Punjab ke camel-drivers ke folk music par based hai. [Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Music and Paintings of Mughal Period Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0191","t":"21 Mughal Literature","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL LITERATURE — FULL MIND MAP\n📜\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Baburnama & Its English Translation\n2. Gulbadan Begum & the Humayun Nama\n3. Maham Anaga & the Khairul Manzil\n4. Persian Translations of Sanskrit Texts\n5. Historical Chronicles — Important Match Lists\n6. Tabaqat-i-Akbari\n7. Abdur Rahim Khan-i-Khana\n8. Abdul Hamid Lahori & the Padshahnama\n9. Shahjahannama\n10. Historical Works — Correctly & Incorrectly Matched Pairs\n11. Akbarnama & Ain-i-Akbari\n12. The Court Language — Persian\n13. Masir-i-Alamgiri\n14. Futuhat-i-Alamgiri\n15. Nastaliq — The Persian Script\n16. Raja Sawant Singh — 'Nagri Das'\n17. Keshavdas — 'Ramachandrika' & 'Rasik Priya'\n1. Baburnama & Its English Translation\n● 'Baburnama' (originally Chagatai Turkic mein Babur ne likhi, baad mein Persian mein translate hui) ka\nEnglish translation John Leyden aur William Erskine ne kiya tha. [Q1]\n2. Gulbadan Begum & the Humayun Nama\n● Gulbadan Begum, Babur ki beti thi (1523-1603 AD) — unhone apni book 'Humayun Nama' mein bahut\nse historical events document kiye. Akbar ne unka bahut respect kiya aur unhe Babur-Humayun ki\nhistory likhne ka order diya. [Q2, Q3]\n● 'Humayun Nama' unki half-sister Gulbadan Begum ne likhi thi. [Q4]\n●\n Trap: 'Humayun Nama' kisne likhi wale question mein diye gaye options mein se koi bhi sahi nahi\n⚠️\ntha (Gulbadan Begum options mein na hone ki wajah se) — isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer tha,\nhalaki actual mein Gulbadan Begum ne hi ye likhi thi. [Q5]\n3. Maham Anaga & the Khairul Manzil\n● Maham Anaga (Akbar ki chief nurse) ne 'Khairul Manzil' mosque banwayi thi, Mughal architecture mein\n— baad mein ye ek Madarsa ki tarah kaam karne lagi, Purana Qila (Delhi) ke saamne — aaj ise\n'Madarsa-e-Begum' bhi kehte hain. [Q6, Q7]\n4. Persian Translations of Sanskrit Texts"," ● 'Hitopadesha' (Sanskrit fables ka collection, prose aur verse mein) ko Taj-ul-Din Mufti-al-Maliki (Tajul\nMali) ne Persian mein translate kiya. [Q8]\n● 'Panchatantra' ko Mulla Husain Waaiz Kashifi ne 'Anwar-i-Suhaili' naam se Persian mein translate kiya.\nAkbar ne apne poet laureate Faizi ki supervision mein ek translation department banayi thi — baad mein\nAbul Fazl ne bhi 'Panchatantra' Persian mein translate ki. [Q19]\n● 'Yogavasistha' (Hinduism ka ek philosophical text) ko Nizamuddin Panipati ne Akbar ke reign mein\nPersian mein translate kiya — Akbar ne isi purpose ke liye ek special translation department banayi thi.\n[Q20]\n5. Historical Chronicles — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Hasan Nizami → Tazul Maasir; Khwandamir → Humayun Nama (Qanun-i-Humayuni bhi kehte\nhain, Gulbadan Begum ke alawa unhone bhi ek 'Humayun Nama' likhi); Muhammad Qazim → Alamgir\nNama; Bhim Sen → Nushkha-i-Dilkusha. [Q9]\n● Match: Mulla Daud → Chandayan; Damodar Kavi → Padmavati Katha; Somnath → Rag Vibodh; Amir\nKhusro → Ashiqa. [Q10]\n● Match: Alamgir Nama → Munshi Mohd. Qazim; Tabaqat-i-Akbari → Nizamuddin Ahmed; Chahar\nChaman → Chandrabhan Barahman; Iqbal Nama Jahangiri → Muitamad Khan. [Q11]\n● Match: Bhimsen Kayestha → Tarikh-i-Dilkusha; Chandrabhan Brahman → Chahar Chaman; Ishwardas\nNagar → Futuhat-i-Alamgiri; Sujanrai Bhandari → Khulasat-ut-Tawarikh. [Q26]\n6. Tabaqat-i-Akbari\n● 'Tabaqat-i-Akbari' (jise 'Tarikh-i-Nizami' bhi kehte hain) Khwaja Nizam-ud-din Ahmed ne compose ki thi.\n[Q12]\n● 'Tabaqat-i-Akbari', jise kabhi-kabhi Abul Fazl ki 'Akbarnama' se zyada reliable maana jaata hai,\nNizamuddin Ahmad ne likhi thi — Gulbadan Begum ne 'Humayun-Nama' likhi, aur Abdul Hamid Lahori\nne 'Padshahnama' likhi. [Q13]\n7. Abdur Rahim Khan-i-Khana\n● Akbar ki successful tolerant policy ki wajah se unka reign Hindi literature ka 'Golden Era' kaha jaata hai\n— is period mein Abdur Rahim Khan-i-Khana ka Hindi literature mein sabse significant contribution tha.\nWo Arabic, Persian, Turkish, Sanskrit, Hindi aur Rajasthani — 6 languages ke master the. 'Rahim\nSatsai' unka famous Hindi couplets ka collection hai. [Q14]\n8. Abdul Hamid Lahori & the Padshahnama\n● Abdul Hamid Lahori, Shah Jahan ke reign ke ek official historian the — unhone 'Padshahnama'\n(Badshahnama bhi kehte hain) likhi, jo Shah Jahan ke reign ki history hai. Wo Shah Jahan ke court mein\nek traveller ki tarah join hue the. [Q15]"," 9. Shahjahannama\n● 'Shahjahannama' (Shah Jahan ke chronicles) Inayat Khan ne 17th century mein likhi thi — baad mein\n19th century mein A.R. Fuller ne ise English mein translate kiya. [Q16]\n10. Historical Works — Correctly & Incorrectly Matched Pairs\n● Sahi match: 'Tuzuk-i-Baburi' (Baburnama) Babur ki autobiography hai. Humayun-Nama Gulbadan\nBegum ne likhi. Tarikh-i-Sher Shahi Abbas Khan Sarwani ne likhi. Tabaqat-i-Akbari Khwaja Nizamuddin\nAhmad ne likhi. [Q17]\n●\n Trap: 'Tughluqnama' Amir Khusro ne likhi thi, Ibn Battuta ne NAHI — Ibn Battuta ne apni famous\n⚠️\ntravelogue 'Rihla' likhi thi. Ye galat match hai. [Q18]\n11. Akbarnama & Ain-i-Akbari\n● 'Akbarnama' Abul Fazl (Akbar ke Navaratnas mein se ek) ne 1590-1596 AD mein likhi, jisme lagbhag 7\nsaal lage. (Kuch sources ke mutabik isse fully complete karne mein 12-13 saal lage, isliye exams mein\niska debate hota hai — lekin 'Seven years' hi standard answer maana jaata hai.) [Q21]\n● 'Ain-i-Akbari' (Akbarnama ka teesra volume) Akbar ke court historian Abul Fazl ne Persian language\nmein likhi — isme Mughal Empire ki administration, army, revenues aur geography ke baare mein hai.\n[Q22]\n12. The Court Language — Persian\n● Mughal period ki court language Persian thi — Akbar ne kai languages ka protector banke, Sanskrit,\nArabic, Turkish, Greek jaisi languages ke works translate karne ke liye 'translation department' banayi.\n[Q23]\n● Mughals ki court language Persian thi — official aur administrative language ke roop mein. Urdu baad\nmein (18th/19th century) Delhi-Lucknow jaisi princely courts ki popular language ban gayi, lekin Persian\nformal court language hi bani rahi. [Q24]\n13. Masir-i-Alamgiri\n● 'Masir-i-Alamgiri' (Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb ke reign ki history, detailed insights ke saath) Saqi\nMustaid Khan ne likhi thi. [Q25]\n14. Futuhat-i-Alamgiri"," ● 'Futuhat-i-Alamgiri' (jisme Aurangzeb ke reign ki kuch significant ghatnayein hain) Ishwardas Nagar (ek\nMughal officer) ne likhi thi. [Q27]\n15. Nastaliq — The Persian Script\n● 'Nastaliq' medieval India (Mughal period) mein use hone wali ek Persian script thi — ye ek highly\ndecorative, fluid calligraphy style thi. Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb khud Nastaliq script likhne mein expert\nthe. [Q28]\n16. Raja Sawant Singh — 'Nagri Das'\n● Raja Sawant Singh (17th-18th century, Kishangarh state, Ajmer) ne 'Nagri Das' (Radha ke sevak) ke\npen-naam se Lord Krishna ki tareef mein bahut si verses likhi. Kishangarh ke rulers Nimbarka sect aur\nfamous Kishangarh school of painting ko patronize karte the. [Q29]\n17. Keshavdas — 'Ramachandrika' & 'Rasik Priya'\n● 'Ramachandrika' aur 'Rasik-Priya' — famous works Keshavdas (1555-1617 AD) ne likhi — wo ek\nSanskrit scholar-Hindi poet the, 'Rasik Priya' (Hindi literature ke Ritikaal period ki pioneering rachna) ke\nliye jaane jaate hain. [Q30, Q31]\n●\n Trap: 'Ram Rasayan' Keshavdas ki rachna NAHI hai — ye Padmakar (ek doosre poet) ne likhi.\n⚠️\nKeshavdas ke major works hain: Ramachandrika, Rasik Priya, Ratan Bavani, Kavipriya, Chhandamala.\n[Q32]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mughal Literature Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0192","t":"22 Mughal Period Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MUGHAL PERIOD — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n📋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Foreign Travellers — Match & Chronology\n2. Chronology of Muslim Rulers & Foreign Invasions\n3. Fact-Check — Key Historical Statements\n4. The Battles of Panipat & Hemu\n5. Prithviraj Chauhan — 'The Last Sun of Indian Glory'\n6. Battles Match Lists & Chronology\n7. Tansen's Other Name — 'Ata Ali Khan'\n8. Land Grant Systems — Iqta, Jagir, Amaram & Mokasa\n9. Surat — 'Babul Mecca' (Gate of Mecca)\n10. The Nawruz Festival\n11. The Lucknow Madarsa — Farangi Mahal\n12. Chronology — Deaths in Akbar's Family\n13. Chronology — Warrior Queens of Medieval India\n14. Tombs — Correct & Incorrect Location Matches\n15. Buland Darwaza & Lucknow Monuments — Building Materials\n16. Mughal Monuments — Chronological Order\n17. Mughal Rulers & Their Monuments — Important Match Lists\n18. 'Muallim' — The Navigator\n19. Banjaras — Nomadic Traders\n20. 'Sarais' — Medieval Travel Infrastructure\n21. Medieval Terminology — Jarib, Dam, Desai & Diwan\n1. Foreign Travellers — Match & Chronology\n●\n Trap: Sir Thomas Roe, Akbar ke NAHI, Jahangir ke reign mein (1615 AD) aaye the — Akbar ki\n⚠️\nmrityu 1605 AD mein ho chuki thi. William Hawkins, Jahangir se factory ki permission maangne 1609\nAD mein aaye the. Tavernier, Shah Jahan ke darbar mein aaye, aur Manucci ne Aurangzeb ke reign\nmein Mughal courts mein kaam kiya. [Q1]\n● Jean-Baptiste Tavernier (1605-1689 AD), ek 17th century French gem merchant-traveller the — unhone\nIndia ke diamonds aur diamond mines ke baare mein vistarpoorvak likha. [Q2]\n● William Finch ke mutabik, Akbar ke reign mein, Allahabad (Prayagraj) ke '40 Pillars ka Palace' banane\nke liye 5,000 se 20,000 aadmi 40 saal tak kaam karte rahe. [Q3]\n●\n Disputed: Foreign travellers ki timeline — Hawkins (1608-1611 AD), Thomas Roe (1615-1619 AD),\n⚠️\nManucci (1653-1708 AD), Ralph Fitch (1583-1591 AD, diya gaya option 1585-86 close hai) — Ralph\nFitch ki date mein slight inaccuracy ki wajah se ye question disputed maana jaata hai. [Q4]\n2. Chronology of Muslim Rulers & Foreign Invasions\n● Muslim rulers ka chronological order: Jahangir (1605-1627 AD) → Muhammad Shah (1719-1748 AD) →\nAhmad Shah Abdali (Afghan invader, 3rd Battle of Panipat, 14 January 1761 AD) → Bahadur Shah-II\n'Zafar' (1837-1857 AD). [Q5]\n● Foreign invasions ka chronological order: Genghis Khan (Iltutmish ke reign mein, 1211-1236 AD) →\nTimur (Nasiruddin Mahmud ke reign mein, 1398 AD) → Nadir Shah (Muhammad Shah ke reign mein,\n1739 AD) → Ahmad Shah Abdali (1748-1767 AD ke beech). [Q6]"," 3. Fact-Check — Key Historical Statements\n● Statement check: Ahmad Shah Abdali ne 3rd Battle of Panipat (Marathas ke against, 1761 AD) ladi thi\n(sahi). Qutbuddin Aybak Delhi Sultanate ke pehle ruler the, Babur ne Mughal Empire banayi — inhe\nconfuse karne wala statement galat hai. Shah Jahan ne khud war of succession NAHI ladi — ye unke\nbeto (Shah Shuja, Dara Shikoh, Aurangzeb, Murad) ke beech ladi gayi thi (galat statement). Jahangir\n'beauty, nature aur painting ke premi' ki tarah jaane jaate the (sahi). [Q7]\n4. The Battles of Panipat & Hemu\n● Match: Nadir Shah ke Delhi massacres → Battle of Karnal (1739 AD); First Battle of Panipat → Babur\nvs Ibrahim Lodi (21 April 1526); Second Battle of Panipat → Hemu vs Akbar (5 November 1556); Third\nBattle of Panipat → Ahmad Shah Abdali vs Marathas (14 January 1761). [Q8]\n● Hem Chandra Vikramaditya (Hemu) Adil Shah Suri (Sur dynasty) ke chief of army aur Prime Minister\nbane — unhone Afghan rebels aur Mughal forces se ladte hue 22 lagatar ladaiyan jeeti. Delhi mein\nMughal forces ko haraane ke baad unhone 'Vikramaditya' ki title li — lekin Second Battle of Panipat\n(1556) mein haar gaye, aur Bairam Khan ne unka sar kaat diya. [Q9]\n●\n Trap: Second Battle of Panipat, Tipu Sultan aur Marathas ke beech NAHI ladi gayi thi — ye Hemu\n⚠️\naur Akbar ki forces ke beech ladi gayi thi. Battle of Haldighati (1576) Maharana Pratap-Akbar ke beech,\naur First Battle of Panipat (1526) Babur-Ibrahim Lodi ke beech ladi gayi. [Q11]\n5. Prithviraj Chauhan — 'The Last Sun of Indian Glory'\n● Historian B.N. Luniya ke mutabik, Prithviraj Chauhan ko 'The Last Sun of Indian Glory' kaha gaya hai.\n(Kuch doosre contexts mein Hemu ke liye bhi similar epithet use hota hai, lekin isi specific phrasing ke\nliye Prithviraj sahi answer hai.) [Q10]\n6. Battles Match Lists & Chronology\n● Match: Third Battle of Panipat → 1761 AD; Second Battle of Tarain → 1192 AD; Death of Akbar → 1605\nAD; Death of Aurangzeb → 1707 AD. [Q12]\n● Match: Battle of Haldighati → Akbar (Rana Pratap ke against); Battle of Bilgram/Kannauj → Humayun\n(Sher Shah Suri ke against); Revolt of Khusrau → Jahangir (Khusrau unke bete the); Battle of Khanwa\n→ Babur (Rana Sanga ke against). [Q13]\n● Match: 1556 AD → Akbar ki accession (aur Second Battle of Panipat); 1600 AD → Queen Elizabeth I ne\nEast India Company ko Charter di; 1680 AD → Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj ki mrityu; 1739 AD → Nadir\nShah ne Delhi capture ki. [Q14]\n● Match: Third Battle of Panipat (Afghans vs Marathas, 1761 AD); Battle of Haldighati (Akbar vs\nMaharana Pratap, 1576 AD); Second Battle of Tarain (Muhammad Ghori vs Prithviraj Chauhan, 1192\nAD); Battle of Asirgarh (Miran Bahadur vs Akbar, 1601 AD). [Q15]"," ● Battle of Haldighati (1576 AD, Maharana Pratap vs Akbar) — sahi match hai. Battle of Chausa 1539 AD\n(1538 NAHI); Battle of Kanauj/Bilgram 1540 AD (1539 NAHI); Battle of Khajwa 1659 AD (1657 NAHI);\nBattle of Kheda 1707 AD (1699 NAHI). [Q16]\n● Mughal-period battles ka chronological order: Battle of Khanwa (Rana Sanga vs Babur, 1527 AD) →\nBattle of Ghaghra (Babur vs Mahmud Lodi, 1529 AD) → Battle of Chausa (Humayun vs Sher Shah Suri,\n1539 AD) → Battle of Samugarh (Aurangzeb-Murad ki joint army vs Dara Shikoh, 1658 AD). [Q17]\n● Battles ka chronological order: Battle of Chanderi (1528 AD) → Battle of Chausa (1539 AD) → Battle of\nKannauj/Bilgram (1540 AD) → Battle of Talikota (1565 AD). [Q18]\n●\n Trap: Battle of Balkh, Jahangir ke reign mein NAHI, Shah Jahan ke reign mein hui thi (Central Asia\n⚠️\nmein apni ancestral zameen secure karne ki koshish mein) — galat match. Babur ne Battle of Khanwa,\nHumayun ne Chausa, aur Akbar ne Haldighati ladi — ye sahi matches hain. [Q19]\n● Battles ka chronological order: Battle of Khanwa (1527 AD) → Battle of Chausa (1539 AD) → Battle of\nKannauj (1540 AD) → Battle of Talikota (1565 AD). [Q34]\n7. Tansen's Other Name — 'Ata Ali Khan'\n● Famous musician Tansen ka asli naam Ramtanu Pandey tha — kuch historical accounts ke mutabik,\nIslam apnaane ke baad unhe 'Ata Ali Khan' naam diya gaya tha.\n Diye gaye options mein Tansen ka\n⚠️\nkoi mention na hone ki wajah se 'None of these' sahi answer hai. [Q20]\n8. Land Grant Systems — Iqta, Jagir, Amaram & Mokasa\n● Match: Iqta → Delhi Sultans dwara diya gaya land grant; Jagir → Mughal rulers dwara apne\nMansabdars ko diya gaya land assignment; Amaram → Vijayanagara rulers dwara apne Nayakas\n(military chiefs) ko diya gaya land grant; Mokasa → Maratha rulers dwara military service ki salary ke\nbadle diya gaya land grant. [Q21]\n9. Surat — 'Babul Mecca' (Gate of Mecca)\n● Mughal period mein, Haj ke liye Mecca jaane wale pilgrims mainly Surat port se embark karte the — isi\nwajah se Surat ko 'Meccai dwar', 'Babul Mecca' (Gate of Mecca), aur 'Meccabari' kaha jaata tha. [Q22,\nQ23]\n10. The Nawruz Festival\n● Mughals ne 'Nawruz' festival Zoroastrians (Persia) se apnaya tha — essentially ye ek Zoroastrian\n(Parsi) New Year festival hai. Ye 19 dino tak celebrate hone wala ek national festival tha, jiska Mughal\nperiod mein bahut mahatva tha — Abul Qadir Badauni ne ise 'Nawruz-i-Jalali' kaha tha. [Q24]\n11. The Lucknow Madarsa — Farangi Mahal"," ● Mughal period mein, 'Muslim Jurisprudence' ki teaching Lucknow Madrasa (Farangi Mahal) mein\nspecialize thi. Mulla Nizamuddin (Sihali, Lucknow mein paida hue) 'Darse Nizami' curriculum ke\noriginator the, jisme Tafsir (Quran ki exegesis), Hadith (Prophet ki traditions) waghera shaamil the. [Q25]\n12. Chronology — Deaths in Akbar's Family\n● Events ka chronological order: Sheikh Mubarak ki mrityu (Abul Fazl-Faizi ke pita, 1593 CE) → Faizi ki\nmrityu (Abul Fazl ke bade bhai, 1595 CE) → Abul Fazl ki hatya (Prince Salim ke orders par, 1602 CE) →\nDaniyal ki mrityu (Akbar ke bete, excessive drinking ki wajah se, 1605 CE). [Q26]\n13. Chronology — Warrior Queens of Medieval India\n● Warrior queens ka chronological order: Padmini (early 14th century, Chittor ki rani, 1303 mein Alauddin\nKhalji ke attack ke time Jauhar kiya) → Durgavati (mid 16th century, Gondwana ki Hindu warrior queen,\n1564 mein Akbar ki forces se ladte hue mari) → Tara Bai (late 17th-early 18th century, Chhatrapati\nRajaram ki rani, 1700 AD ke baad Maratha resistance zinda rakhi) → Ahilya Bai (18th century, Malwa ki\nHolkar Queen, 1767-1795 AD tak raj kiya). [Q27]\n14. Tombs — Correct & Incorrect Location Matches\n● Abdur Rahim Khan-i-Khanan ki tomb Nizamuddin East, Delhi mein hai (sahi match).\n Shaikh Salim\n⚠️\nChishti ki famous Dargah Fatehpur Sikri mein hai, Khuldabad mein NAHI. Itmad-ud-Daula ki tomb Agra\nmein hai, Fatehpur Sikri mein NAHI. Aurangzeb ki tomb Khuldabad (Chhatrapati Sambhaji Nagar) mein\nhai, Agra mein NAHI. [Q28]\n●\n Trap: 'Jahangiri Mahal' Akbar ne banaya, Agra Fort ke andar situated hai — Burhanpur mein NAHI\n⚠️\n(galat match). [Q30]\n15. Buland Darwaza & Lucknow Monuments — Building Materials\n● Buland Darwaza red sandstone se bana hai, white marble se sirf decorate kiya gaya hai — lekin Salim\nChishti ki Khankah mein white marble use NAHI hua. Bara Imambara aur Rumi Darwaza (dono\nLucknow mein, Asaf-ud-Daula ne banwaye) bricks aur lime se bane hain, stone ya marble se nahi. [Q29]\n16. Mughal Monuments — Chronological Order\n● Monuments ka chronological order: Atala Mosque, Jaunpur (Ibrahim Shah Sharqi, ~1408 AD) → Sher\nShah Suri ki Tomb, Sasaram (1540-45 AD) → Humayun's Tomb, Delhi (Hazi Begum ki supervision\nmein, 1565-72 AD) → Rabia Daurani's Tomb/Bibi Ka Maqbara, Aurangabad (Aurangzeb ne apni patni ki\nyaad mein, 1660 AD). [Q31]"," 17. Mughal Rulers & Their Monuments — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Babur → Jama Masjid, Sambhal; Humayun → Din Panah (Delhi mein basayi hui city); Akbar →\nJahangiri Mahal (Agra Fort mein bana); Jahangir → Itmad-ud-Daula's Mausoleum (Nur Jahan ne unke\nreign mein banwaya). [Q32]\n● Match: Qutb Minar → Iltutmish ne complete ki; Gol Gumbad → Muhammad Adil Shah ka mausoleum;\nBuland Darwaza → Akbar ne banwaya; Moti Masjid (Delhi) → Aurangzeb ne banwayi. [Q33]\n● Match: Alai Darwaza → Alauddin Khalji ne banwaya; Buland Darwaza → Akbar ne Fatehpur Sikri mein\nbanwaya; Moti Masjid (Agra) → Shah Jahan ne banwayi; Moti Masjid (Delhi) → Aurangzeb ne banwayi.\n[Q35]\n18. 'Muallim' — The Navigator\n●\n Disputed: 'Muallim' (navigator) Indian merchant ships ka ek employee/officer hota tha — wo ek\n⚠️\nspherical device ki madad se stars aur sun ki position identify karta tha, navigation ke liye. Diye gaye\noptions mein se koi bhi technically sahi nahi tha (kyunki Muallim ek vyakti/employee tha, ship nahi).\n[Q36]\n19. Banjaras — Nomadic Traders\n● Medieval India ke 'Banjaras' generally nomadic traders the — wo hazaaro bailo ke saath ek jagah se\ndoosri jagah move karte the, food grain, salt, ghee jaisa saman lekar. Wo Caravan trading mein\nspecialize karte the. [Q37]\n20. 'Sarais' — Medieval Travel Infrastructure\n● Medieval India ki ek interesting feature 'Sarais' thi, jo sheharon ko ghere rehti thi aur poore subcontinent\nmein failii thi — simple square/rectangular plan par bani, ye Indian aur foreign travellers, pilgrims,\nmerchants, traders ko temporary accommodation deti thi. Ye public spaces alag-alag cultural\nbackgrounds ke logo ke cross-cultural interaction ka centre bhi thi. [Q38]\n21. Medieval Terminology — Jarib, Dam, Desai & Diwan\n●\n Trap: 'Jarib' koi tax NAHI tha — ye ek land measurement unit/tool (measuring chain) tha, jo Mughal\n⚠️\nperiod mein bahut use hota tha. Sher Shah Suri ne copper coin 'Dam' introduce ki thi. 'Desai' Maratha\nperiod mein district-level revenue collector hote the. 'Diwan' Mughal period mein province ka revenue\nchief hota tha. [Q39]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mughal Period Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0193","t":"23 Sikh Sect","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" 🪯 THE SIKH SECT — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Guru Nanak's Succession — Guru Angad & Gurumukhi\n2. The Founding of Amritsar — Guru Ramdas\n3. Guru Arjan Dev — Adi Granth & Sikh Institutions\n4. Sikh Gurus Martyred by Mughal Rulers\n5. Famous Sikh Gurdwaras & Sacred Sites\n6. Guru Gobind Singh & the Khalsa Panth\n7. Banda Bahadur\n1. Guru Nanak's Succession — Guru Angad & Gurumukhi\n● Guru Nanak ki mrityu 22 September 1539 ko, 70 saal ki age mein hui — apni mrityu se pehle, unhone\nBhai Lehna ko apna successor niyukt kiya, jo baad mein 'Guru Angad' ke naam se jaane gaye. [Q1, Q2]\n● 'Gurumukhi' word Punjabi ke 'Gurumukha' se aaya hai, matlab 'Guru ke mukh se' — Gurumukhi script\nko doosre Sikh Guru, Guru Angad ne formalize/shuru kiya tha. [Q3]\n2. The Founding of Amritsar — Guru Ramdas\n● Mughal Emperor Akbar ne Bibi Bhani (chauthe Sikh Guru, Guru Ramdas ki patni) ko 500 bighe zameen\ndaan di, jisme ek natural pond tha — isi zameen par Amritsar basaya gaya. Shuru mein is city ka naam\n'Ramdaspur' tha, baad mein natural pond (Amrit Sarovar) ke naam par 'Amritsar' ban gaya. [Q4, Q5]\n3. Guru Arjan Dev — Adi Granth & Sikh Institutions\n● Match: Guru Arjan Dev (5th Guru) → Adi Granth compile ki (1604 AD). Miri-Piri (temporal aur spiritual\nauthority) 6th Guru, Guru Hargobind ne introduce ki. 'Manji system' (religious empire ki 22 branches) 3rd\nGuru, Guru Amar Das ne establish ki. 'Dal Khalsa' bahut baad mein Nawab Kapur Singh ne banaya.\n[Q6]\n● Rebel Prince Khusrau (Jahangir ke bete) ne 1606 AD mein revolt ki thi — wo Punjab bhaag gaye jaha\nunhe 5th Sikh Guru, Guru Arjan Dev se aashirwad aur kuch financial help mili. Jahangir isse bahut\nnaraz hue — unhone Guru Arjan Dev par fine lagaya, aur fine na dene par unhe qaid karke torture se\ndeath sentence di. [Q7]\n● 'Adi Granth' (Guru Granth Sahib) Guru Arjan Dev (5th Sikh Guru, 1581-1606 AD) ne compile ki thi —\nisme 6 Sikh Gurus ki teachings ke saath-saath Kabir, Baba Farid, Namdev, Raidas jaise Hindu\ndevotees-saints ki teachings bhi hain. [Q8]\n4. Sikh Gurus Martyred by Mughal Rulers"," ● Guru Arjan Dev aur Guru Tegh Bahadur — dono ko unke samkalin Mughal rulers (Jahangir aur\nAurangzeb) ne death sentence di thi. Guru Arjan Dev (5th Guru) ko Jahangir ne 1606 AD mein Prince\nKhusrau ki madad karne ke ilzaam mein death sentence di. Guru Tegh Bahadur (9th Guru) ko\nAurangzeb ne November 1675 AD mein Chandni Chowk, Delhi mein execute kiya — Islam apnaane se\ninkaar karne aur Kashmiri Pandits ki raksha karne ki wajah se. [Q9]\n● Aurangzeb, 9th Sikh Guru, Guru Tegh Bahadur ki 1675 AD mein hui execution ke liye responsible the.\n[Q10]\n5. Famous Sikh Gurdwaras & Sacred Sites\n● Famous aur revered Sikh gurudwara 'Gurudwara Sri Hemkund Sahib', Hem Kund (Chamoli district,\nUttarakhand) mein, Himalaya ki high altitude par situated hai. [Q11]\n● Guru Gobind Singh (10th aur aakhri human Sikh Guru), 1666 AD mein Patna (Bihar) mein paida hue the\n— unhone 'Khalsa Panth' introduce ki aur Sikh community ko ek warrior group mein consolidate kiya.\n'Takht Sri Patna Sahib' unki janm-bhoomi ki yaad mein hai. [Q12]\n● Guru Gobind Singh (10th aur aakhri human Sikh Guru) ki Nanded (Maharashtra) mein ek Afghani noble\nne hatya ki thi — wahan ki 'Takhat Sachkhand Sri Hazur Abchalnagar Sahib' Gurudwara unki\nmausoleum par bani hai, isliye Nanded Sikhs ke liye ek highly sacred site hai. [Q13]\n6. Guru Gobind Singh & the Khalsa Panth\n● Guru Gobind Singh (10th Guru, Sikhism ke aakhri human prophet) ki sabse badi achievement thi Sikhs\nko ek military sect 'Khalsa Panth' mein convert karna — unhone poori Sikh community ko 'Khalsa'\nbulaya, har purush Sikh ko 'Singh' aur mahila ko 'Kaur' surname use karne ka nirdesh diya, aur 5 Ks\n(Kesh, Kada, Kachera, Kangha, Kirpan) hold karna zaroori kiya. [Q14]\n● Sikhs ko martial 'Khalsa' brotherhood mein 10th Guru, Guru Gobind Singh ne transform kiya. [Q15]\n● Khalsa Panth ki sthapna 13 April 1699 ko, Baisakhi ke din, 10th Sikh Guru Gobind Singh ne, Anandpur\nSahib mein ki thi — (ye question 2000 mein poocha gaya tha, isliye 1699 se lagbhag 300 saal ho chuke\nthe). [Q16]\n● Khalsa Panth 10th Guru, Guru Gobind Singh ne institute ki thi. [Q17]\n● Sikhs ke aakhri human Guru (prophet) 10th Guru, Guru Gobind Singh the — apni mrityu se pehle,\nunhone declare kiya ki Sikhs ka eternal-living Guru holy scripture Guru Granth Sahib hoga. [Q18]\n● 'Khalsa' 10th Sikh Guru, Gobind Singh ne found kiya. [Q19]\n7. Banda Bahadur\n● Sikh military commander Banda Bahadur ka asli naam 'Lachhman Dev' (Madho Das bhi kehte the) tha\n— 'Banda Bahadur' (Brave Slave) naam unhe 10th Sikh Guru, Guru Gobind Singh ne diya, jinse wo\nNanded mein mile the. [Q20]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sikh Sect Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0194","t":"24 Maratha State and Confederacy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" MARATHA STATE & CONFEDERACY — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Reasons for the Rise of the Marathas\n2. Shivaji — Birth, Coronation & Capital\n3. Shivaji's Battles & Escapes\n4. Shivaji's Guru — Samarth Ramdas\n5. The Ashtapradhan — Shivaji's Council of Ministers\n6. Opposition from the Deshmukhs\n7. Maratha Coinage\n8. The Rise of the Peshwas — Balaji Vishwanath & Chronology\n9. Chhatrapatis After Shivaji — Chronology\n10. The Maratha Confederacy — Peshwa as Virtual Ruler\n11. Tarabai's Leadership\n12. Maratha Revenue System — Saranzami & Chauth\n13. The Third Battle of Panipat\n14. The Modi Script\n1. Reasons for the Rise of the Marathas\n● Maratha rise ki koi ek specific wajah nahi thi, na hi ye kisi specific period ki unstable circumstances ka\nresult thi — inke logo ka nationalism unity, caste, language, religion, literature aur habitat ke basis par\ntha. Maharashtra ki geographical conditions bhi Maratha power ke flourish hone mein madadgar thi, aur\nShivaji-doosre Maratha leaders ki high leadership quality ka bhi bada yogdan tha. [Q1]\n● Map-based question: Shaded area map mein Marathas ke ruled territories ka extent dikhaya gaya tha.\n[Q2]\n● Assertion-Reason: Mughals ke decline ke baad, Marathas hi sabse capable native power the jo unki\njagah le sakte the (sahi Assertion) — Maratha power ki rise Maharashtra ke logo ki Maratha-identity par\nbased unity se hui thi, lekin Marathas ek unified India ka concept develop karne mein fail rahe (galat\nReason, jo Assertion ka sahi explanation nahi deta). [Q32]\n2. Shivaji — Birth, Coronation & Capital\n● Shivaji ka janm 1627 (ya 1630) AD mein, Shivneri Fort mein hua — 1674 AD mein unhone apni\ncoronation ke baad 'Chhatrapati' ki title li. [Q4]\n● Shivaji ki coronation 1674 AD mein hui, 'Chhatrapati' title ke saath — unhone Raigarh ko apni capital\nbanaya. Varanasi ke famous scholar Vishveshwar (Gaga Bhatt) ne unki coronation ki aur unhe\nKshatriya declare kiya. [Q7, Q8, Q9]\n3. Shivaji's Battles & Escapes\n● Shivaji ne 1672 AD mein 'Battle of Salher' mein Mughals ko haraya. [Q3]\n● 1659 AD mein, Bijapur Sultan ne Afzal Khan (apne experienced-trusted commander) ko Shivaji ko\ndabaane bheja — lekin diplomat aur clever Shivaji ne unse ulta cleverly nipat liya. [Q5]"," ● Aurangzeb ne 1666 AD mein Shivaji ko Agra mein qaid kiya tha — wo Jaipur Bhawan (Agra) mein\ncaptivity mein the jab unhone Mughals ki custody se escape kiya. [Q6]\n● Shivaji se related events ka chronological order: Chakan ke Fort ki jeet (1648 AD) → Mughals ke saath\nclash ki shuruaat (1657 AD) → Afzal Khan ka episode (1659 AD) → Surat ka attack-loot (1664 AD).\n[Q11]\n4. Shivaji's Guru — Samarth Ramdas\n● Samarth Ramdas, Shivaji ke Guru the — unhe unki Advaita Vedantic text 'Daasbodh' ke liye yaad kiya\njaata hai. Unhone Shivaji ki tareef mein 'Shivastuti' naam ki poem bhi likhi. [Q10]\n5. The Ashtapradhan — Shivaji's Council of Ministers\n● 'Ashtapradhan' Shivaji ne Maratha administration mein banayi thi — 8 ministers ki ek council thi:\nPeshwa (Prime Minister), Amatya/Mazumdar (Finance), Waqianavis/Mantri (Interior/Intelligence),\nSachiv/Surnavis (Correspondence), waghera. [Q12, Q14, Q15, Q16, Q21]\n● Match: Sachiva (Surnavis) → Correspondence dekhte the; Peshwa → Prime Minister; Samant\n(Sumant/Dabir) → Foreign Minister; Amatya (Mazumdar) → Finance Minister. [Q13]\n● Shivaji ke Ashtapradhan mein ye officers the: Mazumdar (Amatya, Finance/Revenue Minister), Dabir\n(Sumant, Foreign Minister), Waknis (Waqianavis/Mantri, Interior Minister), aur Surnis (Sachiv,\nSecretary/Correspondence). [Q17]\n● Shivaji ke time, 'Sarnobat' (Sar-i-Naubat/Senapati) ka post military administration se related tha — wo\nCommander-in-Chief the, military ki maintenance, appointments, organization aur food supply ke liye\nresponsible the. [Q18]\n● Shivaji ke Ashtapradhan mein foreign affairs dekhne wale member 'Sumant' (ya Dabir) kehlaate the.\n[Q19, Q20]\n● Assertion-Reason: Shivaji ko state matters mein ek Council of Ministers (Ashtapradhan) advise karti thi\n(sahi Assertion) — lekin wo modern cabinet ki tarah kaam nahi karti thi; har minister sirf ek advisory\nhead tha, koi independent charge nahi rakhta tha — final decision Shivaji ka hota tha (isliye Reason\ngalat hai). [Q22]\n6. Opposition from the Deshmukhs\n● Assertion-Reason: Shivaji ko powerful landlords (Deshmukhs) se opposition ka saamna karna pada\n(sahi Assertion) — kyunki Deshmukhs apni power-influence maintain rakhna chahte the, aur ek\nindependent Maratha state ke favour mein nahi the, wo Bijapur ke subordinate rehna chahte the kyunki\nisse unhe autonomy aur opportunities milti thi (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q23]\n7. Maratha Coinage"," ● Chhatrapati Shivaji ke Kingdom mein Lari, Rupaya aur Taka — silver coins the.\n 'Ruka' silver coin\n⚠️\nNAHI thi — ye ek copper coin thi (Kakatiya dynasty ya local fractional copper currencies se associate ki\njaati hai). [Q24]\n8. The Rise of the Peshwas — Balaji Vishwanath & Chronology\n● Sambhaji ke baad, Balaji Vishwanath ne Maratha administration ko streamline kiya — November 1713\nAD mein, actual power Chhatrapati se Peshwas ke haathon mein transfer ho gayi. [Q25]\n● Peshwas ka chronological order: Balaji Vishwanath (1713-1720 AD) → Bajirao-I (1720-1740 AD) →\nBalaji Bajirao (1740-1761 AD, Third Battle of Panipat ke baad mrityu) → Madhavrao (1761-1772 AD).\n[Q26, Q27]\n● Peshwas ka chronological order: Balaji Vishwanath (1713-20) → Balaji Bajirao (1740-61) → Narayan\nRao (1772-73) → Raghunath Rao/Raghoba (1773-74). [Q28]\n9. Chhatrapatis After Shivaji — Chronology\n● Chhatrapatis ka chronological order: Sambhaji (1680-1689 AD, Shivaji ke bade bete) → Rajaram (1689-\n1700 AD, Shivaji ke doosre bete) → Shivaji-II (1700-1708 AD, Rajaram ke bete, Tarabai ki regency\nmein) → Chhatrapati Shahuji (1708-1749 AD, Sambhaji ke bete). [Q29]\n10. The Maratha Confederacy — Peshwa as Virtual Ruler\n● Assertion-Reason: 1750 tak Maratha kingdom ek Confederacy ban chuki thi, jo Peshwa ke through\npreside hoti thi (sahi Assertion) — Bajirao ki 1740 mein mrityu ke baad Shahu ne Balaji Bajirao ko\nPeshwa banaya, aur ye designation patrimonial ban gayi. 1750 ke Sangola agreement se Maratha king\nek 'do nothing king' (figurehead) ban gaya, aur Peshwa hi Maratha Confederacy ka effective head ban\ngaye (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q30]\n● Maratha King ek non-entity ban gaye aur Peshwa virtual ruler bane — ye Balaji Bajirao ke time se shuru\nhua. [Q31]\n11. Tarabai's Leadership\n● Rajaram ne 1689-1700 AD tak Shahu ke representative ki tarah Marathas ko lead kiya. Unki mrityu ke\nbaad, unki widow Tarabai ne apne bete Shivaji-II ki taraf se Mughals ke saath struggle jaari rakha —\nAurangzeb ki mrityu (1707 AD) ke waqt Maratha leadership Tarabai ke haath mein thi. [Q33]\n● Rajaram (1700 AD) ki mrityu ke baad, unke minor bete Shivaji-II raja bane aur unki widow Tara Bai unki\nregent bani — Tara Bai ek bahaduri lady thi, unhone 1700 AD se Mughals ke against struggle lead ki\naur Singhgarh, Raigarh, Satara ke forts Mughals se wapas jeete. [Q34]\n12. Maratha Revenue System — Saranzami & Chauth"," ● 'Saranzami' system, Maratha period ke land revenue se related tha — is system ke under di gayi\nzameen Maratha Jagirdars ki jeevika ke liye di jaati thi. [Q35]\n● 'Chauth' Marathas dwara protection ke badle claim ki jaane wali revenue thi — ye 'Mughalai' (Mughal\ndirect control se bahar, neighbouring territories) provinces se collect ki jaati thi, aur standard land\nrevenue ka 1/4 (25%) hoti thi. [Q36]\n13. The Third Battle of Panipat\n● 3rd Battle of Panipat (14 January 1761), Maratha Sadashivrao Bhau aur Afghan invader Ahmad Shah\nAbdali ke beech ladi gayi thi — Marathas is ladai mein Afghans se badly haar gaye. Historian Kashiraj\nPandit is battle ke ek eyewitness the, jinhone iska description diya. [Q37, Q39, Q40, Q41, Q42, Q43]\n● Ahmad Shah Abdali ka India invade karne aur Third Battle of Panipat ladne ka immediate reason tha —\nMarathas ne unke viceroy (aur bete) Timur Shah ko Lahore se nikaal diya tha, jiska badla lena chahte\nthe. [Q38]\n● Ahmad Shah Abdali January 1757 AD mein Delhi mein daakhil hue aur Delhi-Mathura-Agra loota —\nwapas jaane se pehle unhone Alamgir-II ko Emperor, Imadulmulk ko Prime Minister, aur Rohilla leader\nNajib-ud-Daulah (Najib Khan) ko apna chief agent niyukt kiya. [Q44]\n14. The Modi Script\n● 'Modi script' Marathas ke documents mein use hoti thi — khaaskar revenue aur administrative records\nmaintain karne ke liye. [Q45]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Maratha State and Confederacy Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0195","t":"25 Disintegration of the Mughal Empire","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DISINTEGRATION OF THE MUGHAL EMPIRE — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Later Mughal Emperors — Succession & Chronology\n2. Farrukh Siyar & the Sayyid Brothers\n3. Muhammad Shah 'Rangeela'\n4. Shah Alam-II & the Last Mughal Emperor\n5. The Independent State of Awadh\n6. The Independent Kingdom of Hyderabad\n7. Rise of Regional Powers — Carnatic, Mysore & Rohilkhand\n8. Jai Singh-II & the Jantar Mantar Observatories\n1. Later Mughal Emperors — Succession & Chronology\n● Aurangzeb ki 1707 AD mein mrityu ke baad, unke 63-saal ke bete Muazzam (Shah Alam) ne 'Bahadur\nShah-I' naam se gaddi sambhali — unhone 1707-1712 AD tak raj kiya. [Q1]\n● Jahandar Shah pehle Mughal emperor the jo governance ke liye unfit saabit hue — powerful Amir\nZulfiqar Khan ki madad se gaddi par baithe. Unhe unke bhatije Farrukh Siyar ne (Sayyid brothers ki\nmadad se) haraakar Feb 1713 mein maar diya — log unhe 'Lewd Moron' kehte the. [Q2]\n● Later Mughal rulers ka chronological order: Jahandar Shah (1712-13 AD) → Muhammad Shah (1719-\n1748 AD) → Ahmad Shah (1748-54 AD) → Alamgir-II (1754-1759 AD). [Q10]\n● Mughal emperors ka chronological order: Bahadur Shah-I (1707-1712 AD) → Jahandar Shah (1712-\n1713 AD) → Farrukhsiyar (1713-1719 AD) → Muhammad Shah 'Rangeela' (1719-1748 AD). [Q11]\n2. Farrukh Siyar & the Sayyid Brothers\n● Farrukh Siyar ne 1717 AD mein ek Farman (decree) issue ki, jisme Britishers ko Bengal mein duty-free\ntrading facilities di gayi — East India Company sirf 3000 rupees ka annual tax dekar bina duty ke trade\nkar sakti thi. Is Farman ko 'Magna Carta' bhi kaha jaata hai (East India Company ke liye). [Q3]\n● Sayyid brothers — Hussain Ali aur Abdullah Khan — later Mughal period ke 'King Makers' kehlaate the\n— wo 1713 se 1720 AD tak sabse powerful nobles the (Hindustani group ke leaders). Unhone 1713\nmein Farrukh Siyar ko raja banaya, aur 1719 mein unhe dethrone kar diya. [Q4]\n3. Muhammad Shah 'Rangeela'\n● Muhammad Shah (1719-1748 AD), Mayur Singhasan (Peacock Throne) par baithne wale aakhri Mughal\nemperor the — unke reign mein 1739 AD mein Nadir Shah ne India par attack karke Battle of Karnal\nmein Mughals ko haraya, aur famous Peacock Throne, Kohinoor diamond samet le gaye. [Q5, Q6]\n● Nadir Shah ne 1739 AD mein India par invasion kiya — Battle of Karnal aur Delhi ki loot mein khatam\nhua, jisme sheher ko bahut nuksaan hua, loot hui, aur bahut se logo ki jaan gayi. [Q7]\n● Muhammad Shah (1719-48 AD) apna zyadatar samay animal fights dekhne aur wine-beauty mein busy\nrehte the, administration mein unhe koi interest nahi tha — isi lifestyle ki wajah se unhe 'Rangeela' kaha"," jaata tha. Unke administration mein disinterest ki wajah se eunuchs aur ladies ka ek group Mughal\ndarbar mein dominate karta tha. [Q8, Q9]\n4. Shah Alam-II & the Last Mughal Emperor\n● Shah Alam-II (asli naam Ali Gauhar, 1759-1806 AD tenure) royal court ki conspiracies ka shikaar hue —\npowerful Wazir Ghaziuddin (Imad-ul-Mulk) ne unhe Delhi mein entry nahi karne di, isliye unhe bahar\nbhatakna pada. [Q12]\n● Aakhri Mughal Emperor Bahadur Shah Zafar (Bahadur Shah-II, 1837-57 AD) the — unke pita ka naam\nAkbar Shah-II (Akbar-II) tha. Wo British ke pensioner the, aur Red Fort, Delhi ke royal court ke head the\n— 1857 ki Revolt tak. [Q13]\n● India ke aakhri Mughal Emperor Bahadur Shah Zafar the — unki mrityu 1862 AD mein Rangoon\n(Burma) mein exile mein hui. [Q14]\n●\n Trap: Bahadur Shah Zafar ko East India Company se exactly 1 lakh rupees per month pension milti\n⚠️\nthi (1 lakh se KAM NAHI), plus 15 lakh rupees rental expenses ke liye. Baaki statements sahi hain: unki\npower Red Fort tak simit thi (empire without empire), Zauq-Ghalib unke poetry teachers the, aur Hasan\nAskari unke guide the. [Q15]\n●\n Disputed: Famous sarcastic proverb 'Lord of the world ka rajya Delhi se Palam tak phaila hai'\n⚠️\noriginally Tughlaq ruler Nasiruddin Mahmud ke liye kaha gaya tha, Bahadur Shah Zafar ke liye NAHI —\nisliye ye quote Zafar par apply karna historically galat hai, aur BPSC ne is question ko invalidate/remove\nkar diya tha. [Q16]\n5. The Independent State of Awadh\n● Awadh (Oudh) ke pehle Nawab Saadat Khan (Burhan-ul-Mulk) the — 1722 AD mein Mughal Emperor\nMuhammad Shah ne unhe Oudh ka Subedar (governor) niyukt kiya, aur unhone dheere-dheere ek\nlargely independent hereditary dynasty establish ki. [Q17]\n● Awadh ka independent state Muhammad Shah ke reign mein, Saadat Khan ne banaya (statement 1\nsahi). Saadat Khan ne powerful 'kingmakers' Sayyid brothers ko overthrow karne ki conspiracy mein\nMuhammad Shah ka support kiya — unki loyalty se khush hokar emperor ne unhe reward diya\n(statement 2 sahi). [Q18]\n6. The Independent Kingdom of Hyderabad\n● Chin Qilich Khan (Nizam-ul-Mulk, Asaf Jah-I) ne 1724 AD mein independent Hyderabad kingdom ki\nsthapna ki — unhone Battle of Shakar Kheda (1724 AD) mein Mughal governor Mubariz Khan ko\nharaakar-maar kar Deccan ke real master ban gaye. [Q19]\n●\n Disputed: Statement check — 'Kilich Khan, Mubariz Khan ke naam se bhi jaane jaate the' — YE\n⚠️\nGALAT hai (Qilich Khan, Nizam-ul-Mulk ki title thi, Mubariz Khan unke rival governor the jinhe unhone\nharaya). 'Nizam-ul-Mulk ne Mubariz Khan ko haraya' — YE SAHI hai (Battle of Shakar Kheda, 1724\nAD). ''Asaf-Jah' title Julfikar Khan ne di' — YE GALAT hai (ye title Mughal Emperor Muhammad Shah ne\ndi thi). [Q20]"," 7. Rise of Regional Powers — Carnatic, Mysore & Rohilkhand\n● Statement check: 'Nizamat of Arcot' (Carnatic ke Nawabs) Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb ne establish ki\nthi (Nizam of Hyderabad ki legal dependency thi) — galat statement diya gaya tha. Mysore kingdom,\ndeclining Vijayanagara Empire ke ek vassal (Wodeyar dynasty) ke roop mein shuru hokar ek powerful\nstate ban gaya (sahi statement). Rohilkhand Kingdom, Ali Muhammad Khan ne, Nadir Shah ke invasion\n(1739 AD) ke baad Mughal authority ke collapse ka fayda uthakar banayi (galat statement diya gaya\ntha). [Q21]\n8. Jai Singh-II & the Jantar Mantar Observatories\n● Amber ke Kachhwaha dynasty ke Rajput king, Sawai Jai Singh-II, ko astronomy-mathematics mein\nbahut interest tha — unhone Delhi mein famous 'Jantar Mantar' astronomical observatory banwaya. Is\nके\nalawa unhone Jaipur, Ujjain, Mathura aur Varanasi mein bhi observatories banwaye. [Q22, Q23]\n● 'Zij-i-Muhammad Shahi' (1773 mein banaya, astronomy ka gyan, reigning Mughal Emperor Muhammad\nShah ko dedicate) Sawai Jai Singh (Jai Singh-II, Amber/Jaipur) ne likhi — unhone Jaipur city basaayi\naur ise science-art ka centre banaya. [Q24]\n● Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh-II ne 5 jagaho par observatories banwaye: Delhi, Jaipur, Ujjain, Mathura aur\nVaranasi — Allahabad (Prayagraj) mein UNHONE observatory NAHI banwayi. [Q25]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Disintegration of Mughal Empire Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0196","t":"03 Delhi Sultanate Khalji Dynasty","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — KHALJI DYNASTY — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Alauddin Khalji — Titles, Ambitions & Absolute Power\n2. Malik Kafur — 'Hazar Dinari' & the Deccan Campaigns\n3. Alauddin's Deccan & Rajput Conquests\n4. The Conquest of Chittor & the Legend of Padmini\n5. Land Revenue Reforms\n6. Market Control Reforms\n7. Public Distribution System & New Taxes\n8. Mongol Invasions & Frontier Defense\n9. The Khalifa Question — Sovereignty & Independence\n1. Alauddin Khalji — Titles, Ambitions & Absolute Power\n● Alauddin Khalji ek ambitious emperor the — unhone 'Sikandar-i-Sani' (doosra Alexander) ki title li aur\nise apne coins par bhi print karwaya. Unki mahatvakanksha thi poori duniya jeetna aur ek nayi religion\nbhi introduce karna — lekin apne khaas dost aur Kotwal 'Alla-ul-Mulk' ki salah par unhone ye idea chhod\ndiya. [Q1, Q2]\n● Historian Ziauddin Barani ne Alauddin Khalji ke baare mein likha: 'Jab unhe Kingship mili, wo rulers aur\nShariat ke orders se kaafi independent the.' Unhone religion ko politics se alag kiya aur clear kiya ki\nstate ka interest supreme hai, Ulemas ke dictates nahi. [Q3]\n2. Malik Kafur — 'Hazar Dinari' & the Deccan Campaigns\n● Malik Kafur ko 'Hazar-Dinari' kaha jaata tha — Alauddin Khalji ke general Nusrat Khan ne Gujarat ki jeet\nke dauran unhe 1,000 dinars ki price mein khareeda tha, isi se ye naam pada. [Q6, Q7]\n● Malik Kafur ne 1309-1311 AD ke beech Deccan aur South India mein highly successful campaigns lead\nki — unka route Devagiri, Warangal, Dwarasamudra aur Madurai tak deeply South India mein jaata tha.\n[Q12]\n3. Alauddin's Deccan & Rajput Conquests\n● Assertion-Reason: Alauddin ke Deccan expeditions financial ventures the (sahi Assertion) — Dr. K.S.\nLal ke mutabik, dhan-lalach aur ghamand ki wajah se unhone South ke states par attack kiya. Unka koi\nintention un states ko directly Delhi Sultanate mein annex karne ka ya unke internal administration mein\ninterfere karne ka NAHI tha (isliye Reason galat hai). [Q8]\n● Ramchandra Dev, Devgiri ke Yadava ruler the jab Alauddin Khalji ne 1296 AD mein invade kiya — unhe\nharaya gaya aur unhone regular tribute dene ka wada kiya, lekin 1305-06 mein tribute dena band kar\ndiya. 1307 mein Alauddin ne Malik Kafur ko dubara bheja — Ramchandra ne surrender kiya, unhe Delhi\nlaaya gaya jaha Alauddin ne unhe 'Rai Rayan' ki title deke izzat di. [Q9]\n● Kingdom-Ruler match: Ranthambore → Hamirdeva (1301 AD); Chittore → Rana Ratan Singh (1303\nAD); Devagiri → Raja Rai Ramchandra (1296 & 1307 AD); Gujarat → Karnadeva (1299 AD). [Q10]"," ● Alauddin Khilji ki jeeto ka chronological order: Gujarat (1299 AD) → Ranthambor (1301 AD) → Chittor\n(1303 AD) → Warangal (1310 AD). [Q11]\n●\n Trap: Warangal (Kakatiya dynasty) ke ruler Prataprudra Dev the, Ramchandra Dev NAHI (wo\n⚠️\nDevgiri ke ruler the — ye galat pair hai). Baaki pairs sahi hain: Hoysala — Veer Ballal III, aur Madurai\n(Pandyas) — Veer Pandya. [Q29]\n● 1303 AD mein, Alauddin Khalji ki Warangal jeetne ki pehli koshish (Malik Chhajju aur Fakhruddin Juna\nki leadership mein) disaster mein badal gayi — Kakatiya dynasty ke king Prataprudradev-II ne unki army\nko successfully waapas bhaga diya. [Q32]\n4. The Conquest of Chittor & the Legend of Padmini\n● Padmini (Padmavati), Alauddin ke Chittor conquest se related hai — wo Chittor ke raja Rana Ratan\nSingh ki patni thi. Unki story famous epic poem 'Padmavat' mein describe hai, jo Malik Muhammad\nJayasi ne 1540 AD mein likhi. Amir Khusrau ne apni text mein Suleman-Shaiba ki love story mention ki\nthi (Alauddin ko Suleman, Padmini ko Shaiba se compare karke) — shayad isi se inspire hokar Jayasi\nne ye kahani likhi. [Q5]\n5. Land Revenue Reforms\n● Ek powerful autocratic state banane aur strong treasury ke liye, Alauddin Khalji ne lagbhag saare land\ngrants cancel kar diye — jo log 'Milq' (state ke through di gayi property/prize/pension) ya 'Waqf' (charity\nland) le chuke the, unse ye zameen chheen li gayi. Ye sab zameen 'Khalisa land' (crown land, directly\nstate dwara manage) mein convert kar di gayi, jisse iska scale bahut zyada badh gaya. [Q13]\n●\n Multiple Correct: Land revenue ko produce ka 50% (aadha) karne wale 2 Sultans mane jaate hain\n⚠️\n— Alauddin Khalji (zameen ki proper measurement ke basis par) aur baad mein Muhammad-Bin-\nTughluq (Doab region mein, lekin unka assessment estimated production par based tha, actual\nmeasurement par nahi). [Q14, Q15]\n● Alauddin Khalji ne land revenue (Kharaj) ko zameen ki scientific measurement ke basis par 50% fix kiya\ntha — 'after measurement' ye keyword important hai, kyunki Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ka demand\nestimated production par tha, actual measurement par nahi. [Q16]\n● Alauddin Khalji ne cultivated land ko measure karke revenue collect ki — isi ke liye unhone ek naya\ndepartment 'Diwan-i-Mustakhraj' banaya (sahi). Unki land measurement/revenue system poori empire\nmein applicable NAHI thi — sirf Delhi aur aas-paas ke Doab region tak limited thi. Unhone Khuts,\nMuqaddams aur Chaudharies jaise traditional local intermediaries ke privileges aur tax-collecting rights\nkhatam kar diye. [Q17]\n6. Market Control Reforms\n● Assertion-Reason: Alauddin Khalji ne Delhi mein price control introduce ki (sahi Assertion) — historian\nZiauddin Barani ke mutabik, is market reform ka mukhya maksad tha ek badi standing army ko\ncomparatively kam salary par maintain karna, borders ki raksha ke liye — ye artisans ko kam wages\ndene ke liye NAHI tha (isliye Reason galat hai). [Q18]"," ● Alauddin Khalji ne 'Market Reforms' (price control mechanisms) successfully introduce ki — ye\nSultanate period ki ek important policy initiative thi. [Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● Alauddin Khalji ki market price control ki koshish highly successful rahi — unhone Delhi mein alag-alag\nmarkets banayi: Grain Market (Mandi), Clothes-Groceries market, aur ek weapons/horses ke liye alag\nmarket. Har market ek 'Shahna-i-Mandi' (superintendent) ke under thi, aur independent sources se bhi\ndaily reports li jaati thi strict implementation ke liye. [Q22]\n7. Public Distribution System & New Taxes\n● Alauddin Khalji ne practically 'Public Distribution System' (Rationing system) introduce ki — Delhi mein\ngovernment grain stores banaye gaye jaha Khalisa lands se anaj store kiya jaata tha, aur famine ke time\npublic mein distribute kiya jaata tha. [Q23, Q24]\n● Alauddin Khalji ne 2 nayi taxes lagayi: 'Ghari Tax' (Ghar-Tax — ghar aur huts par) aur 'Charai Tax'\n(Grazing Tax — doodh dene wale janwaron par). Wo pehle Sultan the jinhone Ghari (House-tax) charge\nki. [Q25]\n8. Mongol Invasions & Frontier Defense\n● Zafar Khan, Alauddin Khalji ke famous army commander, Mongols ke against ladte hue shaheed hue —\nunki bahaduri aur Khalji army ki persistence se Mongols itne impress hue ki wo peeche hat gaye. Zafar\nKhan ka original naam Malik Yusuf Hizabruddin tha. [Q4]\n● 1306 AD ke baad, Alauddin Khalji ke period mein Ravi river, Delhi Sultanate aur Mongols ke beech ki\nboundary ban gayi — Kabak ki leadership mein Mongols ne attack kiya tha, lekin Malik Kafur aur Ghazi\nMalik ne unhe Ravi river ke kinare decisively haraaya. [Q26]\n● Statement check: India par pehla Mongol attack Iltutmish ke reign mein hua tha, Jalal-ud-din Khalji ke\nNAHI (galat statement). Alauddin Khalji ke reign mein (1299 AD), Mongol Qutlugh Khwaja Delhi tak\nmarch karke aaye jab Alauddin Chittor advance mein busy the (sahi statement). Muhammad-bin-\nTughluq ke reign mein, Tarmashirin ke Mongol attack ko unhone actively peeche dhakela. [Q27]\n● Mongol invasions ke constant threat ke against apni empire consolidate karne ke liye, Alauddin Khalji ne\nek strong central government banayi aur ek powerful, permanent, enormous standing army raise ki jo\nspecifically frontiers par empire ki boundaries protect karne ke liye deploy ki gayi thi. [Q28]\n9. The Khalifa Question — Sovereignty & Independence\n● Diye gaye options mein se kisi ne bhi Khalifa (Caliph) ki theoretical authority ko explicitly 'oppose' nahi\nkiya — Iltutmish ne toh formal recognition hi Khalifa se li thi. Alauddin Khalji, Balban aur Muhammad Bin\nTughluq practically independent aur highly autocratic rulers the, lekin unhone kabhi khule taur par Caliph\nki nominal spiritual authority ko reject nahi kiya. Sirf Qutb-ud-din Mubarak Khalji ne (jo options mein nahi\nthe) khud ko 'Khalifa' declare karke unki authority ko oppose kiya. [Q30]\n● Alauddin Khalji ki mrityu ke baad, Qutb-ud-din Mubarak Shah (Mubarak Khalji) gaddi par baithe —\nunhone Abbasid Caliphate ki nominal allegiance chhodkar khud ko 'Caliph' declare kar diya, 'Al Imam',\n'Ul Imam' aur 'Khilafatullah' jaisi titles use ki. [Q31]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Khalji Dynasty Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0197","t":"04 Delhi Sultanate Tughluq Dynasty","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — TUGHLUQ DYNASTY — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Ghiyasuddin Tughluq — Founder & Agricultural Reforms\n2. Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq — The Most Learned Sultan & Agrarian Experiments\n3. The Transfer of Capital to Daulatabad\n4. The Token Currency Experiment\n5. Ibn Battuta's India\n6. Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq — Broad-mindedness & Death\n7. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Welfare & Charitable Measures\n8. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Public Works, Canals & Taxation\n9. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Culture, Learning & the Ashokan Pillars\n10. The Fall of the Tughluq Dynasty\n1. Ghiyasuddin Tughluq — Founder & Agricultural Reforms\n● Ghazi Malik (Alauddin Khalji ke ek commander) Tughluq dynasty ke founder aur pehle ruler the — unki\nmaa ek Hindu Jat lady thi aur pita ek Qaraunah Turk. Alauddin ke reign mein wo chief commander the,\nunhone Mongols ko 29 baar chase karke haraya. Khusrau Shah ki hatya karke, 8 September 1320 AD\nko wo Delhi ke Tughluq dynasty ke pehle Sultan bane. [Q1, Q2]\n● Ghiyasuddin Tughluq ne farmers ki condition improve karne ke liye kai kadam uthaye — Khuts aur\nMuqaddams ke purane rights restore kiye, land revenue rate 1/3 fix ki, aur wo pehle Sultan the jinhe\nirrigation ke liye canals banwane ka credit jaata hai. [Q3]\n● Tughluq dynasty ne sabse lambe samay (1320-1414 AD, 94 saal) tak raj kiya — Slave dynasty ne 84\nsaal (1206-1290), Khalji dynasty ne 30 saal (1290-1320), aur Lodi dynasty ne 75 saal (1451-1526) raj\nkiya. [Q4]\n2. Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq — The Most Learned Sultan & Agrarian\nExperiments\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq (1325-1351 AD) Delhi Sultanate ke sabhi Sultans mein sabse zyada learned\nruler the — unhe astronomy, mathematics, medical science aur doosri kai fields ki knowledge thi. [Q5]\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ne agriculture develop karne ke liye 'Diwan-i-Amir-i-Kohi' (Diwan-i-Kohi) naam\nka naya department banaya — 60 square miles ki land select ki gayi thi, aur crop rotation ke saath alag-\nalag crops cultivate karne ke liye agrarian reforms implement kiye gaye. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n3. The Transfer of Capital to Daulatabad\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ne apni capital Delhi se Daulatabad (Devgiri) shift ki thi — ye unke sabse\nsignificant experiments mein se ek tha. Barani ke mutabik Devgiri isliye chuna gaya kyunki wo\ngeographically empire ke center mein tha, lekin Ibn Battuta ke mutabik ye Delhi ke logo ko punish karne\nke liye kiya gaya tha jinhone unke against likha tha. [Q9, Q10]"," 4. The Token Currency Experiment\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq pehle Sultan the jinhone India mein 'Token Currency' introduce ki —\ncopper/bronze coins jinki value silver coins ke barabar rakhi gayi. Barani ke mutabik, treasury mein\nsilver ki kami aur empire expand karne ki ambitious policies ki wajah se unhone ye kiya. Wo China ke\nKublai Khan ke paper currency (Chao) jaise experiments se inspired the. [Q11, Q12]\n● Assertion-Reason: Moroccan traveller Ibn Battuta ne Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke naye gold coins ko\n'Dinar' naam diya (sahi Assertion) — lekin unki actual 'token currency' copper ya bronze mein issue hui\nthi (gold mein NAHI), silver ki kami door karne aur military power badhane ke liye (isliye Reason galat\nhai). [Q13]\n● Token currency scheme, Muhammad Tughluq ke 5 major failed experiments mein se ek thi (sahi\nAssertion) — iski failure ki mukhya wajah ye thi ki state ke paas coins minting par koi monopoly ya\nproper control nahi tha, log ghar par hi forged copper/bronze coins banane lage (sahi Reason bhi, jo\nAssertion ko explain karta hai). [Q14]\n5. Ibn Battuta's India\n● Ibn Battuta (1333-1342 AD), ek African (Moorish) Moroccan traveller, Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke reign\nmein India aaye the — Sultan unki scholarship se impress hue aur unhe Delhi ka Qazi bana diya. 1342\nAD mein unhe China ambassador ki tarah bheja gaya — unhone apni yatra 'Kitab-ul-Rihla' book mein\ndescribe ki. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Sultanate period ke postal system (horse post aur foot post) ka detailed description Ibn Battuta ke travel\naccounts se milta hai — unhone apni 'Kitab-ul-Rihla' book mein ye documented kiya hai. [Q18]\n6. Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq — Broad-mindedness & Death\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq pehle Delhi Sultan the jinhone Hindu logo ke public celebrations (khaaskar\nHoli) mein participate kiya — unki broad-mindedness ke liye ye jaane jaate the. [Q20]\n● Sultan Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ki mrityu 20 March 1351 AD ko, Thatta (Sindh) ke pass, ek revolt\nkuchalne ki koshish karte hue hui. Unka reign brilliant lekin failed experiments se bhara tha jisse logo ko\nbahut takleef hui — unki mrityu par historian Badayuni ne apni book 'Muntakhab-ut-Tawarikh' mein likha:\n'Raja apni janta se azaad ho gaya, aur janta apne raja se.' [Q19, Q21, Q22]\n7. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Welfare & Charitable Measures\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq ne common logo ke liye kai welfare programmes shuru kiye — unhone\nunemployment ki problem solve karne ke liye ek 'Employment Office' (Diwan-i-Rozgar) khola aur merit\nke basis par kai qualified logo ko appoint kiya. [Q23, Q24]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq philanthropy (paropkar) ki taraf bahut jhukav rakhte the — unhone 'Diwan-i-Khairat'\n(Charity Department) banayi jo gareeb Muslims, orphans, aurton aur widhwao ki financial madad karti\nthi, aur gareeb Muslim ladkiyo ki shaadi bhi arrange karti thi. [Q25]"," ● Firuz Shah Tughluq ko slaves rakhne ka bahut shauk tha — unke court mein slaves ki sankhya\n1,80,000 tak pahunch gayi thi. Unhone inki dekhbhal ke liye ek alag 'Diwan-i-Bandgan' department\nbanaya — ye massive slave corps aakhir mein state ke liye nuksaandayak saabit hui. [Q26]\n●\n Trap: Medieval rulers ke baare mein sahi statement: Firuz Tughluq ne slaves ke liye ek alag\n⚠️\ndepartment ('Diwan-i-Bandgan') banayi — ye sahi hai. Galat statements: military department (Diwan-i-\nArz) Balban ne shuru ki thi, Alauddin ne nahi; ghodo ki branding (Dagh) aur soldiers ka descriptive roll\n(Chehra) Alauddin Khalji ne introduce ki, Balban ne nahi; Firuz Tughluq, Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke\ncousin the, chacha (uncle) nahi. [Q27]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq India ke pehle ruler the jinhone State Exchequer (khazane) se Haj pilgrimage\norganize/subsidize ki. [Q38]\n● 'Dar-ul-Shafa' (House of Healing), Firuz Shah Tughluq ne banwaya tha — ye ek free/charitable hospital\ntha, jisme qualified Hakeems (physicians) gareeb patients ka free ilaj, dawai aur khana dete the. [Q39]\n8. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Public Works, Canals & Taxation\n● Public Works Department ('Diwan-i-Imarat') mukhya roop se Firuz Shah Tughluq ne establish ki thi —\nwo ek great builder the, unhone ~300 nayi cities (Firozabad, Hisar, Fatehabad, Jaunpur jaisi) banayi aur\nkai mosques, schools, sarais (inns) banwaye. [Q28]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq India mein irrigation ke liye canals ka sabse bada network banane ke liye famous\nhain — unki notable canals Sutlej se Ghaggar tak, aur Yamuna se Hisar tak, Delhi-Haryana regions ki\nservice karti thi. [Q29, Q30]\n● Firuz Tughluq pehle Delhi Sultan the jinhone 'Haqq-i-Sharb' (irrigation tax) lagayi — jo farmers state-\nbuilt canals ka paani apni fields ke liye use karte the, unhe apni produce ka 1/10 hissa tax ki tarah dena\npadta tha. [Q31]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq pehle Delhi Sultan the jinhone Brahmins par bhi 'Jizya' (non-Muslims par lagne\nwala religious tax) lagayi — halaki traditionally Brahmins ko isse exempt rakha jaata tha, lekin Firuz ne\northodox Islamic laws ko strictly follow karte hue ye lagu kiya. [Q32]\n9. Firuz Shah Tughluq — Culture, Learning & the Ashokan Pillars\n● Horticulture mein apni deep interest ki wajah se, Firuz Shah Tughluq ne Delhi ke pass 1,200 naye\norchards (baagh) lagaye aur Alauddin Khalji ke time ke 30 purane gardens restore kiye — unhone fruits\nki quality improve karne ke measures bhi liye. [Q33]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq, history aur ancient monuments mein apni interest ke liye jaane jaate the — unhone\nTopra (Haryana) aur Meerut se 2 Ashokan pillars laakar Delhi mein (Firozabad aur ek doosri jagah)\ncarefully re-erect karwaye. [Q34, Q35]\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq ne ek 'Translation Department' establish ki thi — iska mukhya maksad important\ntexts (khaaskar Sanskrit se Persian) translate karna tha, taaki Hindu aur Muslim dono communities ek\ndoosre ko behtar samajh sakein. [Q36]\n● Nagarkot (Kangra) ki apni expedition ke dauran, Firuz Shah Tughluq ne Jawalamukhi temple library se\n~1300 Sanskrit manuscripts collect ki (philosophy, astrology jaise subjects par) — unhone Azizuddin\nKhan se inhe Persian mein translate karwaya, 'Dalail-i-Firuz Shahi' title ke under (300 volumes translate\nhue). [Q37]"," 10. The Fall of the Tughluq Dynasty\n● Nasiruddin Mahmud Shah (1394-1412 AD), Tughluq dynasty ke aakhri ruler the — unke kamzor reign\nmein empire toot gayi, isi wajah se mazak mein kaha jaata tha ki 'Lord of the Universe ka rajya Delhi se\nPalam tak hi phaila hai'. Unke reign mein hi Mongol conqueror Timur ne 1398 AD mein India par\ndevastating invasion kiya. [Q40]\n●\n Disputed: Timur ka India invasion 1398 AD mein, Tughlaq ruler Nasiruddin Mahmud Shah (1394-\n⚠️\n1412 AD) ke reign mein hua tha — lekin diye gaye options (Alauddin Khalji, Bahlul Lodi, Firuz Tughluq,\nMuhammad-Bin-Tughluq) mein se koi bhi sahi nahi hai, isliye ye question disputed hai. [Q41]\n● Timur Lung (Tamerlane) ne 1398 AD mein India par attack karke Delhi ko loota-tabaah kiya. [Q42]\n● Timur ke invasion (1398 AD) ne Tughluq dynasty ko fatally kamzor kar diya, jo 1412/1413 AD mein\nkhatam ho gayi. India chhodne se pehle, Timur ne Khizr Khan ko Multan-Lahore ka apna deputy\n(subedar) niyukt kiya tha — 1414 AD mein Khizr Khan ne Delhi par march karke ise capture kiya aur\nSayyid Dynasty ki sthapna ki. [Q43]\n● Chronological order: Rukn-ud-din Firuz (1236 AD, Slave Dynasty, Iltutmish ke baad) → Mubarak\nKhan/Mubarak Khalji (1316-1320 AD, Khalji Dynasty) → Firuz Shah Tughluq (1351-1388 AD, Tughluq\nDynasty) → Alam Shah (1445-1451 AD, Sayyid Dynasty). [Q44]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Tughluq Dynasty Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0198","t":"05 Lodi Dynasty","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — LODI DYNASTY — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Lodi Dynasty — Origin & Chronology\n2. Bahlul Lodi & Ibrahim Lodi — Conquests & Defeats\n3. Sikandar Lodi — Agra, Administration & Literature\n1. Lodi Dynasty — Origin & Chronology\n● Lodi Dynasty (1451-1526 AD), Delhi Sultanate ki aakhri ruling family thi — pichli sabhi dynasties Turkic\norigin ki thi, lekin Lodi dynasty Afghan origin ki thi. 1526 AD mein Babur ne First Battle of Panipat mein\nIbrahim Lodi ko haraakar is dynasty ka ant kar diya. [Q1]\n● Delhi ki gaddi par Afghan rulers ka sahi chronological order: Bahlul Khan Lodi (1451-1489 AD, dynasty\nke founder) → unke bete Sikandar Shah (1489-1517 AD) → Ibrahim Lodi (1517-1526 AD). [Q2]\n● Delhi Sultanate dynasties ka sahi order: Slave/Mamluk Dynasty (1206-1290 AD) → Khalji Dynasty\n(1290-1320 AD) → [Tughluq Dynasty: 1320-1414 AD] → Sayyid Dynasty (1414-1451 AD) → Lodi\nDynasty (1451-1526 AD). [Q11]\n● Slave (Mamluk) dynasty (1206-1290 AD) ke eminent rulers the: Qutbuddin Aybak, Iltutmish, aur Balban.\nIbrahim Lodi, Lodi dynasty ke aakhri ruler the (1517-1526 AD, bahut baad ki dynasty) — isliye wo Slave\ndynasty se NAHI the. [Q12]\n2. Bahlul Lodi & Ibrahim Lodi — Conquests & Defeats\n● Bahlul Lodi ne 1479 mein Jaunpur ki Sharqi dynasty ko conquer karke apni empire mein annex kar liya\ntha — Jaunpur ko 'Shiraz-i-Hind' ke naam se bhi jaana jaata tha. [Q3]\n● 'Battle of Khatoli' (1518 AD) Maharana Sanga (Rana Sanga, Mewar) aur Ibrahim Lodi ke beech ladi gayi\nthi — is ladai mein Ibrahim Lodi ki bahut buri haar hui, jisse Lodi empire kamzor hui aur Rana Sanga ki\nprestige badhi. [Q4]\n3. Sikandar Lodi — Agra, Administration & Literature\n● Bahlul Lodi ke teesre bete Nizam Khan ne 17 July 1489 AD ko 'Sikandar Lodi' ki title lekar gaddi\nsambhali. Unhe khaaskar 1504 AD mein Agra city basaane ke liye yaad kiya jaata hai — Rajasthan ke\nrajaon ko control mein rakhne aur trade routes par nazar rakhne ke maksad se. 1506 AD mein unhone\napni capital Delhi se Agra shift kar li. [Q5, Q6, Q7, Q9]\n● Sikandar Lodi ek capable administrator hone ke saath-saath learning-literature ke bhi patron the —\nunhe Persian poetry ki achi knowledge thi, aur wo 'Gulrukhi' pen naam se Persian mein poems likhte\nthe. [Q8]\n● Sikandar Lodi ne land revenue management mein gehri ruchi li — unhone ek naya measurement\nyardstick 'Gaj-i-Sikandari' introduce kiya, jise baad mein Sher Shah Suri aur Akbar ne bhi use kiya. Logo"," ki bhalai ke liye, unhone anaj (grains) par lagne wali kai taxes (levies) khatam kar di, taaki zaroori\nkhadya padarth sasti ho. [Q10]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lodi Dynasty Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0199","t":"06 Vijayanagara Empire","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" VIJAYANAGARA EMPIRE — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Foundation of the Empire — Harihara & Bukka\n2. Early Sangama Kings — Kumara Kampana, Harihara II & Devaraya I\n3. Dynastic Succession — Sangama to Tuluva\n4. Krishnadeva Raya — Conquests & Diplomacy\n5. Krishnadeva Raya's Literary Court — The Ashtadiggajas\n6. Krishnadeva Raya — Cities & Temple Architecture\n7. Foreign Travellers & Deva Raya II's Court\n8. Telugu Literature — The Kavi Traya\n9. Sayana — The Vedic Commentator\n10. The Battle of Talikota & the Decline\n11. Financial & Taxation System\n12. Hampi — The Capital City\n13. Temple Architecture & Performing Arts\n1. Foundation of the Empire — Harihara & Bukka\n● Vijayanagara Empire ki sthapna Harihara aur Bukka (bhai) ne 1336 AD mein ki thi — unke pita ke naam\npar is dynasty ko 'Sangama Dynasty' kaha jaata hai. Wo pehle Kampili darbar mein ministers/warrior\nchieftains the — Muhammad Tughluq ne Kampili invade karke unhe arrest kiya, baad mein unke\nspiritual teacher Vidyaranya se prerit hokar unhone apna independent kingdom banaya. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4,\nQ5, Q6]\n● Vijayanagara Empire par 4 dynasties ne raj kiya: Sangama (1336-1485 AD), Saluva (1485-1505 AD),\nTuluva (1505-1570 AD), aur Aravidu. [Q7]\n● Harihara-I ne Tungabhadra river (Krishna river ki ek tributary) ke southern bank par ek nayi city basayi\n— unhone khud ko Lord Virupaksha ke agent ki tarah raj karne ka vachan liya, jinke naam Krishna river\nke south ki poori zameen manne jaati thi. Wo dynasty ke sabse bade bhai the. [Q8]\n2. Early Sangama Kings — Kumara Kampana, Harihara II & Devaraya I\n● Harihara-I ne 1352-53 AD mein apni army, Kumara Kampana ki leadership mein, Madurai conquer\nkarne bheji — Kumara Kampana ne successfully Madurai ko Vijayanagara empire mein annex kiya.\nUnki patni Ganga Devi ne apni book 'Madhura Vijayam' mein apne pati ki victorious expeditions describe\nki. [Q9]\n● Bukka-I ki 1377 AD mein mrityu ke baad, unke bete Harihara-II gaddi par baithe — unki bade military\nachievement thi Bahamani Sultanate se Belgaum aur Goa region jeetna. [Q10]\n● Devaraya-I ne capital ko 15th century ki sabse badi cities mein se ek banaya — unhone ~1410 AD mein\nTungabhadra river par ek dam banwaya aur river se apni capital tak 24 km lambi canal-cum-aqueduct\nbanwayi, taaki paani ki kami khatam ho. [Q11]\n● Bukka-I (1356-77 AD, Sangama dynasty ke raja, Vijayanagara Empire ke founders mein se ek) ne\nChina ke Emperor (Ming dynasty) ke paas ek diplomatic mission bheji thi. [Q44]"," 3. Dynastic Succession — Sangama to Tuluva\n● Statement check: Feudal lord Narasimha Saluva ne 1485 AD mein Prauda Deva Raya (last Sangama\nruler) ko gaddi se hatakar Saluva dynasty banayi. Immadi Narasimha (last Saluva ruler) ko Vira\nNarasimha ne dethrone karke Tuluva Dynasty banayi. Unke baad unke chhote bhai Krishnadeva Raya\n(1509-1529 AD) gaddi par baithe. Krishnadeva Raya ke baad unke half-brother Achyuta Deva Raya\naaye. Sabhi statements sahi hain. [Q12]\n4. Krishnadeva Raya — Conquests & Diplomacy\n● Vijayanagara king Krishnadeva Raya ne Golconda ke Sultan Quli Qutb Shah (Qutb Shahi Dynasty ke\nfounder) ke saath 'Battle of Golconda' ladi — Qutb Shah ki ye campaign haar mein khatam hui. [Q13]\n● Krishnadeva Raya (Tuluva dynasty, 1509-1529 AD reign) ne Portuguese governor Afonso de\nAlbuquerque ke request par, Bhatkal mein ek fort banane ki permission di — unhone guns aur Arabian\nhorses paane ke liye Portuguese ke saath friendly relations maintain kiye. [Q14]\n● 2008-09 UP PCS exam mein poocha gaya 'Kaun 500 saal pehle gaddi par baitha tha' — iska answer\nKrishnadeva Raya hai, kyunki unka coronation 1509-1509 AD mein hua tha (2008 se 500 saal pehle).\n[Q33]\n5. Krishnadeva Raya's Literary Court — The Ashtadiggajas\n● Krishnadeva Raya ka reign 'Telugu literature ka Golden Age' maana jaata hai — unke darbar mein\n'Ashtadiggajas' the, jo 8 mahaan Telugu poets-scholars ka samuh tha (Allasani Peddana inme sabse\npramukh the). [Q15, Q17, Q18]\n● Krishnadeva Raya khud ek accomplished poet-writer the — unhone 'Amuktamalyada' likhi, apni\nliterature aur arts ki contribution ki wajah se unhe 'Andhra Bhoj' (Andhra Bhoja) ki title mili. [Q16]\n● Statement check: Krishnadeva Raya ne 'Amuktamalyada' likhi aur unhe 'Andhra Bhoja' ki title mili (dono\nsahi) — lekin Allasani Peddana Telugu aur Sanskrit literature ke famous poet the, Tamil ke NAHI (ye\nstatement galat hai). [Q20]\n● Allasani Peddana (Ashtadiggajas mein sabse great mane jaate the) ko Krishnadeva Raya ne 'Andhra\nKavita Pitamah' (Telugu Poetry ke Grandfather) ki title di. [Q23]\n● Krishnadeva Raya ke darbar ke poet Mallanārya ne 'Bhava Chintā Ratna' aur 'Veerasaivamrita' texts\nKannada language mein compose ki thi — ye texts Veera Shaiva (Lingayat) tradition ke theories,\ndevotion aur religious aspects represent karte hain. [Q24]\n6. Krishnadeva Raya — Cities & Temple Architecture\n● Krishnadeva Raya ne apni maa Nagala Devi ke sammaan mein Vijayanagara ke pass ek nayi suburban\ncity 'Nagalapura' (Nagalapuram) basayi. [Q19, Q21]\n● Vijayanagara ka famous 'Hazara Rama Temple' Krishnadeva Raya ke reign mein bana tha — ismein\nRamayana ke scenes ke extensive bas-reliefs (carvings) hain. [Q22]"," ● Hampi ka famous 'Vijaya Vitthal Temple' (Shree Vijaya Vitthal Temple, 56 carved pillars ke saath jo\nmusical notes deti hain) Tuluva dynasty ke king Krishnadeva Raya ne banwaya tha — iski musical\npillars ko 'Saregama pillars' kehte hain. [Q47]\n7. Foreign Travellers & Deva Raya II's Court\n● Persian ambassador Abdur Razzaq, Vijayanagara ke Devaraya-II (1422-46 AD, Sangama dynasty,\nPraudha Devaraya bhi kehlaate the) ke reign mein visit karne aaye the. [Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Nicolo Conti (Niccolo de Conti), ek Italian traveller the jinhone Deva Raya-I ke time India visit ki thi —\nunhone Vijayanagara state visit karke sheher aur uske festivals ka detailed account chhoda. [Q28]\n● Portuguese writer Fernao Nuniz (Nunes), jo Achyuta Deva Raya ke reign mein Vijayanagara aaye the,\nunhone likha ki women society mein important role play karti thi aur alag-alag professions mein\nemployed thi — dancers, ghar ke servants, palanquin-bearers, aur wrestling/astrology/soothsaying jaise\nfields mein bhi expert thi. [Q29]\n● Famous Telugu poet 'Srinath' (1365-1441 AD), Vijayanagara ruler Deva Raya-II ke darbar mein\npatronize hue the — isse pehle wo Kondavidu ke Reddy ruler Pedakomati Vema Reddy ke darbar mein\nbhi the. [Q45]\n8. Telugu Literature — The Kavi Traya\n● Nannaya, Tikkana aur Yerrapragada (Yerranna) — teeno ko 'Kavi Traya' (poets ki trinity) kehte hain, jo\nMahabharata ko Sanskrit se Telugu mein translate karne ke liye famous hain (11th se 14th century ke\nbeech). Kamban aur Kuttan Tamil literature se associated the, Telugu se nahi. [Q30]\n9. Sayana — The Vedic Commentator\n● Sayana (Vedon ke famous commentator), apne bhai Madhav Vidyaranya ke saath, Harihara aur Bukka\nke liye inspirational source aur spiritual guide the — isi wajah se unhe Vijayanagara rulers ka bahut\nzyada patronage mila, aur wo Vijayanagara kings ke reign mein hi flourish hue. [Q31, Q32]\n10. The Battle of Talikota & the Decline\n● 'Battle of Talikota' (1565 AD, jise Bannihatti ya Rakshasi-Tangadi ki ladai bhi kehte hain) ek watershed\nbattle thi, jo Vijayanagara Empire aur allied Deccan Sultanates (Berar ko chhodkar — Bijapur,\nAhmadnagar, Golconda, Bidar) ke beech ladi gayi. Isme Vijayanagara ki devastating haar hui, jisse ye\ngreat empire bahut kamzor ho gayi. [Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37]\n● Jab Raja Wodeyar ne 1612 AD mein Mysore Kingdom ki sthapna ki, tab Vijayanagara Empire par\nAravidu dynasty ke Venkata-II (Venkata Pati Raya) raj kar rahe the — wo Raja Wodeyar ke samkalin the\naur apni capital Chandragiri se raj karte the. [Q38]"," 11. Financial & Taxation System\n● Vijayanagara Empire ki financial system ki mukhya khaasiyat 'Land Revenue' thi, jo income ka main\nsource tha — land par lagne wale tax ko 'Shisth' ya 'Rai-Rekha' kaha jaata tha, aur revenue department\n'Athavane' kehlaata tha. Tax rate fix karne se pehle zameen ko measure aur categorize kiya jaata tha.\n[Q39]\n● Krishna Deva Raya (Vijayanagara ruler) ki taxation system mein: zameen ko categories (wetland, dry\nlands, orchards, waghera) mein baata gaya tha aur tax rate uske hisaab se alag hoti thi (sahi). Land tax\nke alawa, professionals aur workshop owners ko bhi industry/professional tax dena padta tha (sahi).\n[Q40]\n12. Hampi — The Capital City\n● Vijayanagara Empire ki old capital ke ruins Hampi (Central Karnataka) mein hain — yahan famous\nVirupaksha temple bhi hai, aur ye globally UNESCO World Heritage Site ki tarah recognize hai. [Q41,\nQ42]\n● Hampi (Vijayanagara ki capital), Tungabhadra river ke southern bank par situated hai — Hampi ke\nmonuments ka group, Vijayanagara district (Karnataka) mein hai, aur UNESCO World Heritage Site hai.\n[Q43]\n13. Temple Architecture & Performing Arts\n● 'Kalyana Mandapas' (highly ornate pavilion structures, deity ki ritual wedding celebrate karne ke liye)\nVijayanagara kingdom ke temple-construction ki ek notable/famous feature thi. [Q46]\n● Vijayanagara period ke dauran, 'Yakshagaan' (Yakshagana) dance-tradition pehli baar develop hui —\nye Karnataka (khaaskar coastal districts) ka ek traditional theatre/folk-dance form hai, jo mythological-\nreligious stories par based hota hai. [Q48]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vijayanagara Empire Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0200","t":"07 Delhi Sultanate Administration","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — ADMINISTRATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Nature of the Sultanate & the Ruling Class\n2. Central Administrative Departments — The Diwans\n3. The Iqta System\n4. Provincial & Rural Administration\n5. Land Revenue & Taxes\n6. Laws & the Religious Framework\n7. Officials & Terminology\n8. The Currency System\n1. Nature of the Sultanate & the Ruling Class\n● Historian Ziauddin Barani, Delhi Sultans ke under India ke state ko truly Islamic nahi maante the —\nkyunki janta ka bahumat (majority population) Islam follow nahi karta tha. [Q1]\n● Sultanate age ke zyadatar rulers (Amirs) aur Sultans Turkish class se belong karte the — Sultan central\nauthority ka chief hota tha, aur powerful designations par appoint hone wale logo ko 'Amir' kaha jaata\ntha. [Q2]\n● Medieval period (Delhi Sultanate, baad mein Mughals) ki government ek composite structure thi —\npurely foreign nahi thi, balki Perso-Arabic, Turko-Mongol (Central Asian) aur indigenous Indian elements\n(jaise continuing village administration) ka fusion thi. [Q14]\n2. Central Administrative Departments — The Diwans\n● Balban (1266-1286 AD), Delhi Sultanate ki administration ke mukhya architects mein se ek — unhone\nMilitary department ko Diwan-i-Wizarat (Finance Department) se alag karke ek naya department 'Diwan-\ni-Arz' (Military Department) banaya. Ye department 'Ariz-i-Mumalik' ke under thi, aur Defence/Military ke\nliye responsible thi. [Q6, Q12]\n● Departments-Founders ka sahi match: Diwan-i-Mushtakharaj (Arrears/Revenue) → Alauddin Khalji;\nDiwan-i-Amir-i-Kohi (Agriculture) → Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq; Diwan-i-Khairat (Charity) → Firuz Shah\nTughluq. Lekin 'Diwan-i-Riyasat' (Market Control Department) Alauddin Khalji ne banayi thi, Balban ne\nNAHI — ye galat pair hai. [Q7]\n● 'Diwan-i-Bandagan' (Slaves ka department) Firuz Shah Tughluq ne banaya tha — unhe slaves rakhne\nka bahut shauk tha, isliye ye pairing sahi hai. [Q8]\n● Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq ne Agriculture develop karne ke liye 'Diwan-i-Amir-Kohi' department banayi —\niska main maksad farmers ko direct financial aid (Taqavi/Sondhar loans) dena tha, taaki zyada barren\nland cultivation ke under aaye aur crop production improve ho. [Q9, Q10]\n● Departments ka match: Diwan-i-Arz → Military department; Diwan-i-Risalat → Religious issues, appeals\naur foreign matters; Diwan-i-Insha → Royal/State correspondence; Diwan-i-Wizarat → Wazir ke under,\nfinancial matters (revenue-expenditure). [Q11]\n● 'Wizarat' institution Islamic constitution se recognized thi, jo originally Abbasid Caliphs ke Persian\nadministration se inspired thi — Wazir (finance department Diwan-i-Wizarat ke head) state ka prime"," minister hota tha. Tughluq era ko Indian Muslim Wizarat ka 'heyday/golden period' maana jaata hai, jab\nWazir ki power apne zenith par pahunchi. [Q13]\n3. The Iqta System\n● Statement check: Delhi Sultanate ki revenue administration mein Pargana/Kasba ka in-charge 'Amil'\ntha, jo revenue collect karta tha (sahi statement). Iqta ek indigenous institution NAHI thi — Turks ise\nIslamic world se India laaye the (galat statement). 'Mir Bakshi' (military department ka head) office\nMughal Administration mein aaya, Khalji Sultans ke time NAHI (galat statement). [Q3]\n● Iqta system India mein Iltutmish ne introduce ki thi — is system mein Iqta ke malik (Iqtadar/Muqti) ko\napne area mein revenue-tax collect karne ki responsibility di jaati thi. Iqta se hone wala revenue directly\nSultan ke account mein deposit NAHI hota tha — Muqti ise apne administrative aur military expenses ke\nliye use karta tha. 'Siyasatnama' (Nizam-ul-Mulk likhit) Iqta system ke baare mein ek primary source hai.\n[Q4]\n● Iltutmish ne 'Iqta' system ko institutionally sabse pehle Delhi Sultanate mein introduce kiya — is system\nmein military commanders aur nobles ko regular cash wage ki jagah zameen di jaati thi, jisse hone wala\nrevenue wo apni aur apni troops ki maintenance ke liye use karte the. [Q16]\n4. Provincial & Rural Administration\n● Medieval India (khaaskar Mughal times) mein administrative units ka ascending order (chhota se bada)\ntha: Pargana → Sarkar → Suba. Poora empire 'Suba' (provinces) mein bata tha, jinke head 'Subedar'\nhote the. Har Suba 'Sarkar' (districts) mein bata tha, jinke head 'Faujdar' the. Har Sarkar aage\n'Pargana'/'Mahal' (sub-districts) mein bata tha, jinke head 'Shiqdar' the. [Q5]\n● Delhi Sultanate ke dauran, 'Muqaddam' ya 'Chaudhari' Village Headman (gaon ke mukhiya) ke liye use\nhone wali traditional title thi — wo village mein sabse top local authority the jo revenue collection mein\nstate ki madad karte the. [Q17, Q18]\n● Sultanate period mein, land revenue ke 'Supreme Rural Officials' Chaudhary (aur Muqaddams) the —\nwo village-level par land revenue collection ke liye responsible the, traditional rural social structure mein\nimportant role play karte the. [Q19]\n5. Land Revenue & Taxes\n● Land product par lagne wali taxes: Kharaj (non-Muslims par lagne wala land tax), Ushr (Muslims par\nlagne wala land tax), aur Muktai (land se related revenue settlement). Lekin 'Khums' land tax NAHI tha\n— ye war ki loot (booty) ya gadi hui treasure par lagne wala tax tha. [Q15]\n● Firuz Tughluq ne taxation Quranic rules ke hisaab se decide ki, 21 non-Islamic taxes khatam kar di —\nunhone religious scholars ki sifarish par ek irrigation tax 'Haqq-e-Sharb' (ya 'Sharb') lagayi, jo crop yield\nka 10% (1/10) hota tha. [Q20]\n● 'Fawazil' Sultanate period mein wo excess/surplus amount tha jo Iqtadars (provincial governors) apne\nadministrative-military expenses meet karne ke baad, central exchequer (Sultan ke treasury) ko wapas\ndene ke liye required the. [Q24]"," 6. Laws & the Religious Framework\n● Sultanate period ki administrative terminology mein 'Zawabits' secular (ya secularly-oriented) State\nlaws/regulations ko refer karte the, jo Sultan dwara banaye jaate the — ye Islamic religious law se alag\nthe. [Q21]\n● 'Hadis' (Hadith) Islamic Law ke primary sources mein se ek hai — ye Prophet Muhammad aur unke\ncompanions ke sayings, customs aur doings ke biographic reports ka collection hai, jo Islamic\njurisprudence ko guide karta hai. [Q22]\n7. Officials & Terminology\n● Delhi Sultanate administration mein 'Khareetadar' wo official hota tha jo royal decrees (firmans) dispatch\nkarne aur official correspondence maintain karne ke liye responsible tha. [Q23]\n8. The Currency System\n● Sultanate period ki 2 main currencies 'Jital' aur 'Tanka' thi — Iltutmish pehle Turkish ruler the jinhone\nIndia mein pure Arabian coinage system shuru ki, silver 'Tanka' aur copper 'Jital' introduce karke. 'Dam'\naur 'Rupiya' baad mein Sher Shah Suri (Afghan rule) ke time introduce hui, aur Mughal era mein widely\nuse hui. [Q25]\n● Silver 'Tanka' coin Iltutmish ne introduce ki thi — wo North India mein ye silver coin laane ke liye\nresponsible the. [Q26, Q27]\n● Sultanate period ke coins — Tanka (silver), aur Jital (copper) — Iltutmish ne pehli baar regular currency\nki tarah issue kiye. 'Shashgani' ek aur coin thi (silver se bani, baad mein Firuz Shah Tughluq ne\nintroduce ki). [Q28]\n● Last Abbasid Caliph of Baghdad (Al-Musta'sim, 1242-1258 AD, jinhe Mongols ne maar dala) ka naam\npehli baar Delhi Sultan Alauddin Masud Shah (1242-1246 AD) ke coins par appear hua — isse pehle\nwale Caliph Al-Mustansir ka naam Iltutmish ke coins par likha hua tha. [Q29]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Administration Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0201","t":"08 Delhi Sultanate Art and Architecture","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — ART & ARCHITECTURE — FULL MIND MAP\n🕌\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Paper & the Alai Darwaza\n2. Qutub Minar — Construction Contributors\n3. Tombs & the First True Arch\n4. Chronology of Delhi's Monuments\n5. Sultanate-Era Buildings — Important Match Lists\n6. Rana Kumbha & the Kirti Stambha\n1. Paper & the Alai Darwaza\n● Paper China mein sabse pehle discover hui thi — India mein iska use 12th century CE mein shuru hua.\nIndia mein paper ka sabse purana evidence Kolkata ke Ashutosh Museum mein preserved hai — 1105\nCE ka 'Panchraksha' naam ka paper. [Q1]\n● 'Alai Darwaza' Alauddin Khalji ne 1311 AD mein banwaya tha — iska ek gumbad wala entrance hai, red\nsandstone se bana aur white marble se sajaya gaya, India ki proper Indo-Islamic style ki pehli buildings\nmein se ek. [Q2]\n● 'Horse-Shoe arch' (ghode ki naal jaisa arch) India mein sabse pehle Alai Darwaza mein introduce hua\ntha — Alauddin Khalji ne ise Quwwat-ul-Islam Mosque complex ke southern gateway ki tarah banwaya.\n[Q3]\n2. Qutub Minar — Construction Contributors\n● Qutbuddin Aybak ne Qutub Minar ka construction shuru kiya (sirf basement complete kiya). Iltutmish ne\nise complete kiya (3 storeys add kiye). Baad mein Firuz Shah Tughluq ne damaged 4th floor restore kiya\naur 5th floor add kiya.\n Alauddin Khalji ne Qutub Minar banane mein KOI\n⚠️\n\nयोगदानNAHI diya (unhone\niske pass ek alag, adhoora 'Alai Minar' zaroor shuru kiya tha). [Q4]\n● Qutub Minar ki 5th aur final storey Firuz Shah Tughluq ne banayi thi, jab pehle wali storey lightning se\ndamage ho gayi thi. [Q5]\n● Statement check: Qutub Minar (13th century mein bana) ki actual height 238 feet (72.5m) hai, 180 feet\nNAHI (galat statement). Chand Minar (Daulatabad, Maharashtra) ko Ala-ud-din Bahmani ne 15th\ncentury (1445 AD) mein banwaya — ye 210-feet ooncha, 4 storeys mein bata hua tapering tower hai\n(sahi statement). [Q6]\n3. Tombs & the First True Arch\n● India ki pehli 'Indo-Islamic style' mein banayi gayi tomb 'Balban ka Maqbara' (Tomb of Ghiyasuddin\nBalban, Mehrauli, Delhi) thi — 1287 AD mein rubble masonry se bani, isme India ki pehli true arch bhi\ndikhti hai. (Note: Iltutmish ka 'Sultan Garhi' technically India ki pehli Islamic tomb hai, lekin Balban ki\ntomb 'pure' Islamic arch style mein pehli hai.) [Q7]"," ● Sultanate period ke memorials mein pehli 'true arch' (sacchi mehraab) Balban ki Tomb (Mehrauli) mein\ndikhi thi — India mein true arches ka ye pehla appearance historically significant hai. [Q8]\n4. Chronology of Delhi's Monuments\n● Monuments ka sahi chronological order: Qutub Minar (Qutbuddin Aybak-Iltutmish, early 13th century) →\nTughluqabad Fort (Ghiyasuddin Tughluq, 1321-1325 AD) → Lodi Garden (Lodi dynasty, 15th-early 16th\ncentury) → Fatehpur Sikri (Mughal Emperor Akbar, late 16th century, 1571 se). [Q9]\n5. Sultanate-Era Buildings — Important Match Lists\n●\n Disputed: Match — Sultan Garhi (Iltutmish, apne bete Nasiruddin Mahmud ke liye 1231 mein bana),\n⚠️\nRed Palace/Lal Mahal (Balban), Dhai Din Ka Jhopra (Qutbuddin Aybak). Jamat Khana Masjid actually\nKhizr Khan (Alauddin Khalji ke bete) ne banayi thi, lekin exam keys mein isse aksar Alauddin Khalji ke\nsaath match kiya jaata hai — isliye ye question disputed hai. [Q10]\n● Building-Builder ka sahi match: Lal Mahal → Balban; Jahaz Mahal → Ghiyas-ud-din Khalji; Lal Darwaja\nMosque (Jaunpur) → Bibi Raje.\n Trap: 'Hindola Mahal' (Mandu) Ghiyas-ud-din Khalji ne banaya tha,\n⚠️\nHoshang Shah ne NAHI — ye galat match hai. [Q11]\n●\n Trap: Delhi ki famous 'Quwwat-ul-Islam' mosque Ajmer mein NAHI hai (Delhi mein hai) — Ajmer\n⚠️\nmein 'Adhai Din Ka Jhonpra' hai. Baaki sahi hain: Jaunpur → Atala Masjid; Malwa (Mandu) → Jahaz\nMahal; Gulberga (Kalaburagi) → Jama Masjid. [Q14]\n● Architectural Style-Dynasty match: 'Lotus bud' fringe (arch ke neeche ki taraf) → Khaljis (Alai Darwaza\nmein dikhta hai); Octagonal tomb ka emergence → Tughluqs (jaise Khan-i-Jahan Tilangani ki Tomb);\nPillar mein 'Bodegoi' bracket ka use → Vijayanagara; Massive entrance gate with inclined walls (Pylon)\n→ Sharqis (Jaunpur, jaise Atala Mosque). [Q15]\n6. Rana Kumbha & the Kirti Stambha\n● Chittor ka 'Kirti Stambha' (Tower of Fame) Rana Kumbha ne banwaya tha, Malwa ke Mahmud Khalji par\napni jeet ki yaad mein — architect Jaita ne iski structure design ki, jabki iski Prashasti (eulogy/tareef) Atri\nKavi aur unke bete Mahesh ne compose ki. [Q12]\n● 'Kirti Stambha' (Vijay Stambha bhi kehte hain, Kumbha ki jeet ke context mein) Chittor mein Rana\nKumbha ke reign mein banaya gaya tha — ye unki achievements ka ek unique monument hai. [Q13]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Art and Architecture Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0202","t":"09 Delhi Sultanate Literature","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Medieval History","x":[" DELHI SULTANATE — LITERATURE — FULL MIND MAP\n📜\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Al-Biruni's Works on India\n2. Amir Khusrau — Life, Titles & Royal Patrons\n3. Amir Khusrau — Language, Literary Style & Poetic Legacy\n4. Amir Khusrau — Musical Innovations\n5. Amir Khusrau's Historical Works\n6. Historical Chronicles of the Delhi Sultanate — Barani & Minhaj-us-Siraj\n7. Chronology of Medieval Texts\n8. Regional Histories & Chronicles — Important Match Lists\n9. Language Patronage in the Delhi Sultanate\n10. Sufi & Translated Literary Works\n11. Firuz Shah Tughluq's Memoirs\n12. Music Treatises of Medieval India\n13. Bhakti & Devotional Literature\n1. Al-Biruni's Works on India\n● 'Kitab-ul-Hind' Al-Biruni (asli naam Abu Rehan) ne likhi thi — unhone ek scientist ki tarah India ka study\nkiya aur uski religious, literary aur socio-political condition describe ki. [Q1]\n● 'Tahqiq-i-Hind' 11th century ke Persian historian-scholar Al-Biruni ne likhi — isme unhone India ki\nhistory, geography aur culture ka detailed account diya. [Q2]\n2. Amir Khusrau — Life, Titles & Royal Patrons\n● Abul Hasan Yaminuddin Khusrau (Amir Khusrau) 1253 AD mein Patiyali (Etah district, aaj Kasganj)\nmein paida hue the — unhone khud ko 'Tuti-i-Hind' (India ka Tota) kaha, aur 9 saal ki umar mein hi\npoems likhna shuru kar diya. [Q3, Q4, Q5]\n●\n Disputed: Amir Khusrau aur Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya — dono ne Delhi Sultanate ke 7 se zyada\n⚠️\nSultans ka reign dekha tha, isliye ye question dono answers accept karta hai. [Q7]\n● Amir Khusrau ne apna court-life Prince Muhammad (Ghiyasuddin Balban ke bete) ke darbar se shuru ki\n— baad mein wo Kaiqubad, Jalaluddin Khalji, Alauddin Khalji, Mubarakshah, Ghiyasuddin Tughluq aur\nMuhammad-Bin-Tughluq ke darbaron mein bhi rahe. Unhe sabse zyada Alauddin Khalji ke court poet ki\ntarah jaana jaata hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]\n3. Amir Khusrau — Language, Literary Style & Poetic Legacy\n● Amir Khusrau ne kai Indian dialects seekhi, khaaskar Hindavi jo unhe sabse pyari thi — wo pehle\nMuslim the jinhone khud ko Indian maana, aur unhone 'Khari Boli' (Hindi ka ek roop) ke development\nmein pioneering role play kiya. [Q6]\n● Amir Khusrau ek polymath the — ek famous poet, historian aur musician. Unhe 'Tuti-i-Hind' kaha jaata\ntha, wo Khari Boli Hindi ke bade promoter the, aur Qawwali ke pioneer bhi the. [Q12]"," ● Amir Khusrau ko naye Persian poetry style 'Sabak-i-Hindi' (Hindustani style) ka pita maana jaata hai —\nwo garv se kehte the: 'Na Lafze Hindiwast aj Farsi Kam' (Hindi ke shabd Persian se kam nahi hain).\n[Q13]\n● Amir Khusrau ko 'Father of Hindi Khari Boli' kaha jaata hai — unhone apni poetry-riddles mein local\nvernacular (Hindavi) ka use karke 'Sabak-i-Hindi'/'Hindustani Style' ko promote kiya. [Q14]\n● Amir Khusrau Hindi (Hindavi) aur Persian — dono languages ke great scholar the. [Q15]\n● Amir Khusrau, Delhi Sultanate ke 7 se zyada rulers ke royal courts se juday classical poet the — wo\npehle Persian poet the jinhone apni poetry mein Indian environment, culture, flora-fauna ko depict kiya.\n[Q16]\n● Statement check: Bijapur Sultan Ibrahim Adil Shah-II ne 'Kitab-i-Nauras' (Hindu devi-devtaon ki tareef\nmein songs ka collection) likhi, jo religious tolerance dikhati hai (sahi). Amir Khusrau ko India mein\n'Qawwali' (Sufi devotional music ka ek form) ke early style ka originator maana jaata hai (sahi). [Q17]\n4. Amir Khusrau — Musical Innovations\n● Amir Khusrau ne Irani Tamboora aur Indian Veena ko combine karke 'Sitar' invent kiya tha — ye Hindu-\nMuslim cultural synthesis (music mein harmony) ka behtareen example hai. [Q34]\n● 'Tabla' aur 'Sitar' dono musical instruments traditionally Amir Khusrau ne, 13th/14th century mein, invent\nkiye mane jaate hain — wo pehle author the jinhone Hindi (Hindavi) phrases-words use kiye. [Q35]\n5. Amir Khusrau's Historical Works\n● 'Khazain-ul-Futuh' book Amir Khusrau ne likhi thi — isme Alauddin Khalji ki conquests describe ki gayi\nhain. [Q29]\n6. Historical Chronicles of the Delhi Sultanate — Barani & Minhaj-us-Siraj\n● 'Tabaqat-i-Nasiri' Minhaj-us-Siraj (Minhaj-i-Siraj) ne likhi thi — Sultan Nasiruddin Mahmud (Slave\nDynasty) ko dedicate ki gayi. Ye text Muhammad Ghori ki India par jeet aur Delhi Sultanate ki early\nhistory describe karta hai. [Q18]\n● Ziauddin Barani (Muslim political philosopher-historian) ne 2 famous works likhi: 'Tarikh-i-Firuzshahi' aur\n'Fatwa-i-Jahandari' — dusri book mein Muslim rulers ko Islamic principles ke basis par political ideals\nfollow karne ki salah di gayi hai. [Q20]\n● Bakhtiyar Khalji ke Bihar invasion ka sabse purana description 'Tabaqat-i-Nasiri' mein milta hai —\nMinhaj-i-Siraj ne likha ki 1193 mein Nalanda University Bakhtiyar Khalji ne loot li, hazaaro monks ko jala\ndiya ya sar kaat diya gaya. [Q21]\n● 'Tarikh-i-Firuz Shahi' (Firuz Shah Tughlaq ke reign ki historical account) diye gaye options mein Shams\nSiraj Afif ne likhi thi — halaki Ziauddin Barani ne bhi Tughlaq dynasty ki history isi naam se likhi thi, lekin\nunke naam options mein na hone ki wajah se Afif sahi answer hai. [Q27]"," ●\n Disputed: 'Tarikh-i-Firuzshahi' 2 alag logo ne likhi — Ziauddin Barani AUR Shams-i-Siraj Afif. Dono\n⚠️\nbooks ka title same hai lekin material aur approach mein bahut alag hain, isliye ye question dono\nanswers accept karta hai. [Q30]\n7. Chronology of Medieval Texts\n● Texts ka sahi chronological order: Kitab-ul-Hind (Al-Biruni, 11th century) → Prithviraja-Raso (Chand\nBardai, 12th century) → Tabaqat-i-Nasiri (Minhaj-i-Siraj, 13th century) → Fatawa-i-Jahandari (Ziauddin\nBarani, 14th century). [Q19]\n8. Regional Histories & Chronicles — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Ziauddin Barani → Tarikh-i-Firuzshahi; Hasan Nizami → Taj-ul-Maasir; Minhaj-us-Siraj →\nTabaqat-i-Nasiri; Yahia-bin-Ahmad (Sirhindi) → Tarikh-i-Mubarakshahi. [Q24]\n● Match: Mirat-e-Sikandari → Gujarat ki jeet (aur waha ke sultans ki history); Burhan-e-Masir → Bahmani\nke Ahmad Nagar (Nizam Shahi dynasty) ki history; Riyaz-us-Salatin → Bengal ki history; Riyaz-ul-Insha\n→ Mahmood Gawan ke letters ka collection. [Q25]\n● Match: Futuh-us-Salatin → Abdul Malik Isami; Futuhat-i-Firuz Shahi (autobiography) → Firuz Shah\nTughlaq; Tarikh-i-Firuz Shahi → Ziauddin Barani (aur Shams Siraj Afif); Khazain-ul-Futuh → Amir\nKhusrau. [Q26]\n● Match: Taj-ul-Masir → Hasan Nizami; Khazain-ul-Futuh → Amir Khusrau; Tarikh-i-Mubarakashahi →\nYahia bin Ahmad Sarhindi; Fatwa-i-Jahandari → Ziauddin Barani. [Q28]\n● Match: Tarikh-i-Hind (Tahqiq-i-Hind bhi kehte hain) → Al-Biruni; Tarikh-i-Delhi → Amir Khusrau; Rihla\n(Kitab-ul-Rihla) → Ibn Battuta; Tabqat-i-Nasiri → Minhaj-us-Siraj. [Q31]\n● Match: Haqaiq-i-Hindi → Abdul Wahid Bilgrami; Tahdhibul Akhlaq → Ibn Miskawayh; Kunzal Tijar →\nBailaq-al-Qabayaki; Jawamiul Hikayat → Sadruddin Muhammad 'Aufi'. [Q32]\n● 'Mirat-e-Sikandari' (Sikandar bin Muhammad ne likhi, Gujarat Sultanate par focus) mein Sultan Mahmud\nBegada ke kingdom ki khushali-samridhi describe ki gayi hai (sahi). Isme ye bhi likha hai ki Mahmud\nBegada ke reign mein trade routes ki suraksha ke acche intezaam ki wajah se businessmen ko bahut\nfayda hua (sahi). [Q42]\n9. Language Patronage in the Delhi Sultanate\n● Muslim conquerors ke India aane ke saath Persian language-literature flourish hui — Delhi Sultanate ki\nsthapna ke baad Persian ko official (court) language ki tarah honour mila. [Q22]\n● 'Apabhramsa' term medieval Sanskrit texts mein non-standard/corrupt Sanskrit (jo log bolte the) ke liye\nuse hota tha — ye modern Indian languages (Hindi, Punjabi, Sindhi, Nepali waghera) ke early\ntransitional forms ko denote karta tha. [Q23]\n10. Sufi & Translated Literary Works"," ● 'Fawaid-ul-Fawad' book Amir Hassan Sizzi (Al Sizzi) ne compile ki thi — isme unke spiritual guru,\nfamous Sufi saint Shaikh Nizamuddin Auliya, ki baatcheet/discourses aur teachings ka record hai. [Q33]\n● Khwaza Ziya-uddin Nakhshabi (14th century Persian physician-Sufi saint, jo Badayun UP migrate hue\nthe) ne Chintamani Bhatt ki Sanskrit text 'Suka Saptati' (Tote ki 70 kahaniyan) ko Persian mein translate\nkarke 'Tutinama' naam diya. [Q36]\n11. Firuz Shah Tughluq's Memoirs\n● Firuz Shah Tughluq ek Delhi Sultan the jinhone apni memoirs (autobiography) 'Futuhat-i-Firuz Shahi'\ntitle se likhi — is chhoti (32-page) book ke through wo khud ko ek ideal, orthodox Muslim ruler ki tarah\njustify/prove karna chahte the. [Q41]\n12. Music Treatises of Medieval India\n● Rana Kumbha (Mewar), music-literature-art ke bade patron the — unhone 'Sangeet Raj', 'Sangeet\nMimansa', 'Sangeet Ratnakar' aur 'Sudha Prabandh' jaisi comprehensive music texts likhi. Unhone\nMalwa ke Mahmud Khalji par apni jeet ki nishaani, 'Kirti Stambha', bhi banwaya. [Q37]\n● Match: Pundrik Vitthal → Raagmala; Pandit Bhavbhatta → Anup Sangeet Ratnakar; Ustad Chand Khan\n→ Khayal Gayaki Ka Delhi Gharana; Rana Kumbha → Sangitraja. [Q38]\n●\n Disputed: Music-text match — Ragamala (Pundrik Vitthal), Rasa Kaumudi (Sri Kantha), Raga\n⚠️\nVibodh (Somanath), Chaturdandi Prakashika (Venkatamakhin). Original exam question mein author ka\nnaam galti se 'Venkatraman' likha gaya tha, jabki sahi naam 'Venkatamakhin' hai — isi wajah se ye\nquestion disputed hai. [Q39]\n13. Bhakti & Devotional Literature\n● Match: Ras Panchadhyayi (Nand Das, Lord Krishna ki bhakti mein Braj Bhasha poetry) → author's\nwork; Chaitanya Bhagvata (Sri Vrindavan Das Thakura, Chaitanya Mahaprabhu ki hagiography, Bengali\nmein) → author's work; Chaitanya Mangal (Jayananda) → author's work; Bhakti Ratnakar (Narhari\nChakravarti, devotees ki zindagi describe karti hai) → author's work. [Q40]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Sultanate Literature Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0203","t":"01 The Advent of European Companies","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.1 — THE ADVENT OF EUROPEAN COMPANIES — FULL MIND MAP\n⛵\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Portuguese — Vasco da Gama's Arrival\n2. Portuguese Viceroys & the 'Blue Water' Policy\n3. Explorer-Country Match Lists\n4. Portuguese Settlements in India\n5. Order of European Arrival in India\n6. The Founding of Calcutta\n7. The Dutch East India Company\n8. Sources of European Success — Statement Analysis\n9. The English East India Company — Formation & First Factories\n10. English vs Portuguese — The Battle of Swally & Captain Hawkins\n11. Bombay's Transfer to the English\n12. Fort William & Prayagraj\n13. The Carnatic Wars\n14. Dupleix's Policy of Intervention\n15. The French East India Company\n16. Match List — European Trading Settlements\n17. Opium & Saltpetre Trade\n18. Reasons for British Success & French Failure\n1. The Portuguese — Vasco da Gama's Arrival\n● Vasco da Gama, Calicut port par 20 May 1498 ko pahunche the — wo trade ke liye India aane wale\npehle Europeans (Portuguese) the. [Q1, Q4]\n● Statement check: Vasco da Gama sirf 3 mahine India mein rahe, aur 1502 mein dobara aaye — sirf\nstatement 1 sahi hai. [Q2]\n● Calicut ke local raja Zamorin ne Vasco da Gama ka swagat kiya tha. [Q6]\n2. Portuguese Viceroys & the 'Blue Water' Policy\n● Francisco de Almeida, India ke pehle Portuguese Viceroy the (1505 AD) — unhone hi 'Blue Water\nPolicy' (samundar par control rakhne ki policy) shuru ki thi. [Q3, Q5]\n● Albuquerque (1509-1515 AD) Portuguese power ke real founder mane jaate hain — unhone 1510 mein\nGoa capture kiya. [Q12]\n●\n Trap: 'Portuguese ne Goa 1499 mein capture ki' — ye statement GALAT hai. Actual mein Goa 1510\n⚠️\nAD mein capture hui thi, 1499 mein NAHI. [Q13]\n3. Explorer-Country Match Lists\n●\n Trap: Peter Mundy, Portuguese NAHI the — wo ek British traveller the (17th century). Baaki sabhi\n⚠️\ndiye gaye visitors Portuguese the. [Q7]\n● Match: Vasco da Gama → Portugal; Columbus → Spain; Captain Cook → Britain; Tasman → Holland.\n[Q8]"," ● Match: Albuquerque → Goa capture ki; Cunha → HQ shift kiya; Cabral → 1500 AD mein aaye; Almeida\n→ Blue Water Policy. [Q9]\n● Match: Columbus → Italy; Cartier → France; Drake → UK; Magellan → Portugal. [Q10]\n4. Portuguese Settlements in India\n● Portuguese ka Cochin (Kochi) mein 1503 AD mein India ka pehla fortress bana — wo sabse pehle\nEuropeans the jinhone India mein sea trade centres set up kiye (Cartaz system ke through). [Q14, Q15]\n● Bengal ke factories mein Hooghly, Portuguese ne establish ki thi. [Q16]\n● Pondicherry (Puducherry) mein sabse pehle Portuguese aaye the, phir Dutch (French NAHI, ye\ncommon galat statement hai), aur baad mein British ne bhi occupy kiya. [Q17]\n● Portuguese, Hooghly ko Bay of Bengal mein piracy ke liye base ki tarah use karte the — 1632 mein\nShah Jahan ke governor Qasim Khan ne unhe wahan se nikal diya. [Q18, Q19]\n5. Order of European Arrival in India\n● Trade ke liye India aane wale pehle Europeans Portuguese the (1498 AD) — sequence tha: Portuguese\n> Dutch > English > Danes > French. [Q11]\n● European powers ke India aane ka sahi chronological order: Portuguese (1498) → Dutch (1605) →\nEnglish (1608/13) → French (1664). [Q55]\n● Pre-independence India mein traders ki tarah aane wale sabse aakhri Europeans French the\n(1664/1668 AD). [Q60]\n6. The Founding of Calcutta\n● Job Charnock (Qasim Bazar factory ke chief) ne Sutanuti select karke modern Calcutta ki foundation\nrakhi. [Q20, Q21]\n● India ki pehli Municipal Corporation 1688 AD mein Madras mein establish hui thi. [Q22]\n7. The Dutch East India Company\n● Dutch East India Company (1602 AD) India ke saath trade karne ke liye sabse pehli 'Joint Stock'\ncompany thi (shareholders ke saath). [Q23]\n● 1663 AD mein Dutch ne Portuguese ko haraakar Kochi (Cochin) mein Fort Williams banaya. [Q24]\n● Dutch ne Bengal mein 'Chinsurah' (1653 AD) mein apni factory establish ki. Bimlipatam (1641), Karaikal\n(1645), Cochin (1663), Chinsura (1653) — ye Dutch factories aur unke establishment years hain. [Q50,\nQ53]\n● Dutch East India Company ne 1632 AD mein Patna mein apni factory establish ki. [Q51, Q52]"," ● Dutch ne India mein bahut si jagaho par trading centres establish kiye — sabhi diye gaye options\n(Surat, Cochin, Chinsurah waghera) mein. [Q61]\n8. Sources of European Success — Statement Analysis\n● Statement check: Statement 1 galat hai kyunki Gajapati rule 16th century mein khatam hui, Dutch 17th\ncentury mein aaye — statements 2 aur 3 sahi hain. [Q25]\n● East India Company ki India mein success ke secrets the: Indian logo mein nationalism ki kami,\nWestern military training, aur Indian soldiers ki mercenary (paisa-lekar-ladne wali) nature — teeno\nfactors. [Q26]\n●\n Trap: English ne India mein Tobacco/Chillies introduce NAHI kiye (ye Portuguese laaye the), mobile\n⚠️\ncannons Mughals ke the, aur soil assessment English se pehle bhi exist karta tha — isliye 'None of\nthese' sahi answer hai. [Q62]\n● 'The Company is an anomaly but it is part of a system where everything is an anomaly' — ye statement\nT.B. Macaulay ne diya tha. [Q63]\n9. The English East India Company — Formation & First Factories\n● Levant Company ko land-route trade ke liye pehla charter mila (1592 AD) — East India Company (EIC)\nko sea-route trade ke liye charter 1600 AD mein mila. [Q27]\n● EIC ki formation 1600 AD mein hui — us waqt India ke Emperor Akbar the (1556-1605 AD). [Q28]\n● English East India Company ne apni pehli factory Surat mein, Jahangir ke reign mein (1613 AD)\nestablish ki. [Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● 17th century ki shuruat mein, English East India Company ki factories Surat, Agra, Ahmedabad aur\nBroach (1619) mein thi — Chicacole ya Trichinopoly mein NAHI. [Q34]\n● English hi pehle European trading company the jinhone Surat mein apni factory establish ki (1613 AD)\n— Dutch ne 1616 mein, aur French ne 1668 mein ki. [Q35]\n● 1613 AD mein, Jahangir ne ek farman issue karke English ko Surat mein factory set up karne ki\npermission di. [Q36]\n● East India Company ki 'Western Presidency' shuru mein Surat mein thi — baad mein Bombay shift ho\ngayi. [Q37]\n10. English vs Portuguese — The Battle of Swally & Captain Hawkins\n● Captain Thomas Best ne 1612 AD mein 'Battle of Swally' mein Portuguese ko haraya. [Q32]\n● Captain Hawkins ke baare mein: unka arrival 1608/09 AD mein hua tha (galat statement diya gaya tha),\naur wo Turkish bhasha jaante the (sahi statement). [Q33]\n11. Bombay's Transfer to the English"," ● Portuguese ne 1661 AD mein Bombay ko King Charles-II ko dowry (dahej) mein diya tha — unhone ise\n1668 mein East India Company ko transfer kar diya. [Q38]\n12. Fort William & Prayagraj\n● Nawab Saadat Ali Khan-II ne 1798 AD mein Prayagraj (Allahabad) ka fort British ko de diya (diye gaye\noptions mein sabse close 1797 AD hai). [Q39]\n● Sir John Child (British East India Company ke Governor) ko Aurangzeb ne 1688 mein expel kiya —\nunhone Mughal ports blockade kiye the aur pilgrim ships capture ki thi. [Q40]\n13. The Carnatic Wars\n● First Carnatic War ka immediate cause tha British Captain Barnett dwara French ships capture karna —\nye ladai English aur French ke beech Indian supremacy ke liye ladi gayi thi. [Q41, Q42]\n● Match: 1st Carnatic War → Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle se khatam hui; 3rd Carnatic War → Treaty of Paris\nse khatam hui; 2nd Carnatic War → inconclusive rahi; 1st Mysore War → British haar gaye the. [Q43]\n●\n Trap: Second Carnatic War (Karnataka) 1749-1754 AD tak chali, 1750-52 NAHI — ye galat match\n⚠️\nhai. [Q44]\n●\n 'Battle of Ambur' 1749 AD mein ladi gayi thi, 1752 mein NAHI — is baare mein diya gaya statement\n⚠️\n(i) galat hai. [Q45]\n● 'Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle-1748' ne First Carnatic War khatam ki — Madras British ko wapas mil gaya.\nDono diye gaye statements sahi hain. [Q64]\n14. Dupleix's Policy of Intervention\n● Dupleix (French Governor-General) pehle European the jinhone Indian rajaon ke internal jhagdo mein\nhasta-kshep karke territory hasil karne ki policy shuru ki. [Q46]\n15. The French East India Company\n● French ne apni sabse pehli factory Surat mein establish ki thi (1668 AD, Frank Caron ki leadership\nmein). [Q47]\n● French East India Company King Louis XIV ke reign mein (1664 AD) constitute hui thi. [Q48]\n● Colbert (Louis XIV ke Minister) ko India mein French Company ka founder maana jaata hai (1664 AD).\n[Q49]\n● French, Deccan mein power establish karne mein fail rahe — mukhya wajah thi English ki strong naval\nsuperiority aur army. [Q54]"," 16. Match List — European Trading Settlements\n● Match: Pondicherry → French; Goa → Portuguese; Tranquebar → Danish; Sadras → Dutch. [Q56]\n17. Opium & Saltpetre Trade\n● Bihar region Europeans ke liye best Saltpetre aur Opium ka source tha — British rule ke dauran Bihar\nopium production ke liye famous tha. [Q57, Q58]\n● India-China-England ke beech 'triangular commerce' (tikone vyapar) ki chief economic foundation\nOpium thi — India se China ko export hoti thi. [Q59]\n18. Reasons for British Success & French Failure\n● British ki success aur French ki failure ke causes mein dono diye gaye factors shaamil the (naval\nsuperiority, resources ka behtar use, waghera). [Q65]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Advent of European Companies Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0204","t":"02 East India Company and Nawabs of Bengal","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.2 — EAST INDIA COMPANY & NAWABS OF BENGAL — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Murshid Quli Khan — Last Mughal-Appointed Governor of Bengal\n2. The Battle of Plassey\n3. Mir Qasim & the Capital Shift to Munger\n4. The Battle of Buxar\n5. The Grant of Diwani\n6. Contact with the Khasi Tribes\n7. The Hindu Nayab Wazirs of Oudh\n8. Chronology & The Battle of Wandiwash\n9. Maratha Resistance to the British\n1. Murshid Quli Khan — Last Mughal-Appointed Governor of Bengal\n● Mughal Emperor Farrukh Siyar ne 1717 AD mein Murshid Quli Khan ko Bengal ka Governor promote\nkiya tha — wo aakhri Governor (Subedar) the jinhe Mughal Emperor ne independently appoint kiya. [Q1,\nQ2]\n2. The Battle of Plassey\n● India mein British supremacy 'Battle of Plassey' (1757 AD) se establish hui — is jeet se East India\nCompany ko military aur commercial dono fayde mile. Ye battle 23 June 1757 AD ko ladi gayi thi. [Q3,\nQ4, Q5]\n● Lord Clive ne 'Battle of Plassey' mein Sirajuddaula (Siraj-ud-Daulah) ko haraya tha. [Q6]\n● Robert Clive ko India mein British Empire ka founder maana jaata hai — unhone Sirajuddaula ko Battle\nof Plassey mein haraya. [Q7]\n● William Pitt ne Robert Clive ko 'Heaven-Born General' kaha tha — Clive ek soldier ke roop mein\nstatesman the. [Q8]\n● Plassey ka battlefield West Bengal ke Nadia district mein, Bhagirathi river ke kinare situated hai. [Q9]\n3. Mir Qasim & the Capital Shift to Munger\n● Mir Qasim ne apni capital Murshidabad se Munger (Monghyr) shift ki thi — taaki wo Calcutta se hone\nwale continuous interference se khud ko surakshit rakh sakein. [Q10]\n4. The Battle of Buxar\n● 'Battle of Buxar' (1764 AD) ko India mein British supremacy establish karne ki sabse decisive ladai\nmaana jaata hai — isne Plassey ke results ko confirm kiya. Sir James Stephen ne kaha tha ki Buxar,\nPlassey se zyada credit deserve karta hai. [Q11, Q13]"," ● Battle of Buxar (1764) ne English armies ki military skill dikhayi — Plassey ke ulta jo treachery (dhoke)\nse jeeta gaya tha. [Q12]\n● Battle of Buxar (1764 AD) ke time Delhi ke Mughal Emperor Shah Alam-II the. [Q14]\n● Battle of Buxar ladte waqt, Bengal ke Nawab Mir Jafar the — (Mir Qasim usme British ke against lad\nrahe the). [Q15]\n● Battle of Buxar ke baad 'Treaty of Allahabad' (1765 AD) sign hui thi. [Q16]\n5. The Grant of Diwani\n● Shah Alam-II (Mughal Emperor) ne 1765 AD mein Bengal, Bihar aur Odisha ki Diwani East India\nCompany ko grant ki. [Q17, Q18]\n● Diwani rights (Bengal, Bihar, Odisha) East India Company ko milne ke time Robert Clive Governor the\n— Treaty of Allahabad (1765) ke through. [Q19]\n● Shah Alam-II ne 12 August 1765 ko Farman issue karke Bengal-Bihar-Orissa ki Diwani East India\nCompany ko di. [Q20]\n● Treaty of Allahabad ke baad, Robert Clive ne Murshidabad ke liye Mohammad Raza Khan ko, aur Bihar\nke liye Raja Shitab Rai ko Deputy Diwan appoint kiya. [Q21]\n6. Contact with the Khasi Tribes\n● Diwani hasil karne ke baad, British Sylhet aaye jaha unhe Khasi tribes (Tirot Sing ki leadership mein) ka\nresistance jhelna pada — ye pahadi tribe ke saath unka pehla contact tha. [Q22]\n7. The Hindu Nayab Wazirs of Oudh\n● Oudh Sultanate ke Hindu Nayab Wazirs ke baare mein: Raja Tikait Rai actually Diwan (Artha\nMantri/Finance Minister) the — is baare mein diye gaye dono statements sahi hain. [Q23]\n8. Chronology & The Battle of Wandiwash\n● 18th century ki battles ka sahi chronological order: Ambur (1749) → Plassey (1757) → Wandiwash\n(1760) → Buxar (1764). [Q24]\n● French Commander Count de Lally, 'Battle of Wandiwash' (1760 AD) mein haare the — unhe British\ncommander Sir Eyre Coote ne haraya. British ne French ko decisively haraya, jisse South India mein\nFrench power khatam ho gayi. [Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Sahi match: 'Battle of Wandiwash' French aur East India Company ke beech ladi gayi thi. (Battle of\nBuxar, Munro vs Mir Qasim thi; Chillianwala, Sikhs vs British thi — inhe confuse mat karna.) [Q28]"," 9. Maratha Resistance to the British\n● Marathas ne India mein British ka sabse zyada zordar virodh kiya tha — unhe sirf teen Anglo-Maratha\nWars (1818 tak) ke baad hi suppress kiya ja saka. [Q29]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · East India Company and Nawabs of Bengal Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0205","t":"03 Regional States Punjab and Mysore","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.3 — REGIONAL STATES: PUNJAB & MYSORE — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Ranjit Singh — Origin, Capital & Kingdom\n2. Ranjit Singh's Administration & Treaties\n3. Successors of Ranjit Singh & Punjab's Annexation\n4. Haidar Ali & the Anglo-Mysore Wars\n5. Tipu Sultan — Capital, Diplomacy & Battles\n6. Treaties Match List\n7. Begum Samru\n8. Miscellaneous Statement Checks\n1. Ranjit Singh — Origin, Capital & Kingdom\n● Ranjit Singh ki kingdom mein Srinagar (Kashmir) bhi shaamil tha — unhone Multan (1818), Kashmir\n(1819) aur Peshawar (1834) capture kiye. [Q1]\n● Ranjit Singh, 'Sukerchakia Misl' ke chief ke ghar paida hue the — usi Misl se belong karte the. [Q2, Q3]\n● 1799 AD mein, Ranjit Singh ne Lahore par control kar liya aur ise apni capital banaya. [Q4]\n2. Ranjit Singh's Administration & Treaties\n● Maharaja Ranjit Singh ne Lahore mein 'Adalat-i-Ala' set up ki, jo district courts ke appeals sunti thi. [Q5]\n● 'Treaty of Amritsar' (1809) Ranjit Singh aur Lord Minto-I ke beech hui — Charles Metcalfe ne Lord Minto\nki taraf se ise sign kiya. [Q6]\n● Famous Kohinoor diamond, Ranjit Singh ko Shah Shuja (Ahmad Shah Abdali ke descendant) ne diya\ntha. [Q7]\n● 'God intended me to look upon all religions with one eye, that is why he took away the light from the\nother' — ye famous statement Maharaja Ranjit Singh ne diya tha. [Q8]\n3. Successors of Ranjit Singh & Punjab's Annexation\n● Ranjit Singh ke successor Khadag Singh the — unki 1839 AD mein mrityu ke baad wo gaddi par baithe.\n[Q9]\n● Maharaja Duleep Singh, Sikh Empire ke aakhri raja the (1843-1849 AD tak) — unhi ke reign mein\nPunjab annex hua. [Q10, Q12]\n● Dalip Singh (ex-Maharaja of Punjab) ki mrityu 23 October 1893 ko Paris mein hui — wo Christianity\napna chuke the aur Russia bhi visit kiya tha. [Q11]\n●\n Trap: Punjab Merger ke baad, Duleep Singh ko annual pension 4-5 lakh rupees mili thi, 2,50,000\n⚠️\nrupees NAHI — ye galat statement hai. [Q13]"," ● Annexation ke baad Punjab administer karne wale 'Board of Three' ke members the: Henry Lawrence,\nJohn Lawrence, aur Charles Mansel.\n H.M. Elliot aur Robert Montgomery is Board ke member NAHI\n⚠️\nthe. [Q14]\n4. Haidar Ali & the Anglo-Mysore Wars\n● First Anglo-Mysore War (1767-69 AD) mein Haidar Ali vijayi hue — English ko 1769 mein Treaty of\nMadras sign karni padi. [Q15]\n● Haidar Ali ne 1755 AD mein Dindigul (Mysore) mein ek modern armoury (hathiyar-shala) establish ki.\n[Q16]\n● British General Sir Eyre Coote ne 'War of Porto Novo' (July 1781) mein Haidar Ali ko haraya. [Q17]\n5. Tipu Sultan — Capital, Diplomacy & Battles\n● Tipu Sultan ne apni capital Srirangapatna (Srirangapatnam) mein banayi thi. [Q18]\n● Tipu Sultan ne modern lines par foreign countries (Iran, Istanbul, France waghera) mein embassies\nestablish ki thi. [Q19]\n● Tipu Sultan ne 1780 mein 'Pollilur' ki jagah par British army (Col. Baillie ki leadership mein) ko haraya\ntha. [Q20]\n● 'Treaty of Srirangapatna' (1792) Englishmen ne Tipu Sultan ke saath ki thi — Cornwallis ne is treaty par\nsign kiye. [Q21]\n● Tipu Sultan ki mrityu 1799 AD mein hui, Fourth Anglo-Mysore War mein ladte hue. [Q22, Q23]\n6. Treaties Match List\n● Match: Treaty of Allahabad → 1765; Treaty of Mangalore → 1784; Treaty of Salbai → 1782; Treaty of\nMadras → 1769. [Q24]\n7. Begum Samru\n● Begum Samru ne Sardhana (Meerut ke pass) mein ek famous/eminent church banwaya tha. [Q25]\n8. Miscellaneous Statement Checks\n●\n Trap: Bengal mein 'Revenue Farming' Ali Mardan Khan ne NAHI, Murshid Quli Khan ne introduce ki\n⚠️\nthi — ye galat statement hai. [Q26]\n● Statement check: Statement 1 galat hai (Abdali ne Marathas ko 1761 mein haraya, Ibrahim Lodi ko\nnahi). Statement 2 galat hai (Tipu 4th War mein 1799 mein mare the). Sirf Statement 3 sahi hai. [Q27]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Regional States Punjab and Mysore Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0206","t":"04 Governor Governor General Viceroy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.4 — GOVERNOR, GOVERNOR-GENERAL, VICEROY — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Governor-General vs Viceroy — Basic Facts\n2. Warren Hastings\n3. Lord Cornwallis\n4. Sir George Barlow & the Vellore Revolt\n5. Lord Wellesley — The Subsidiary Alliance System\n6. Lord Hastings (Marquess of Hastings) — Anglo-Nepal & Third Anglo-Maratha War\n7. Sir Thomas Munro\n8. Lord William Bentinck — Reforms\n9. Lord Ellenborough\n10. Lord Dalhousie — Annexations & Doctrine of Lapse\n11. Lord Canning — The First Viceroy\n12. Queen Victoria's Proclamation & the Title of Empress\n13. Lord Mayo\n14. Lord Lytton\n15. Lord Ripon — Local Self-Government & the Ilbert Bill\n16. Lord Curzon\n17. Lord Minto & Lord Reading\n18. Lord Hardinge — The Capital Shift\n19. John Lawrence — The Policy of 'Masterly Inactivity'\n20. Match Lists — Mixed Governors, General & Events\n21. Chronology of Viceroys & Annexations\n22. Titles — 'Rai Bahadur' & 'Khan Bahadur'\n1. Governor-General vs Viceroy — Basic Facts\n● Statement check: Robert Clive Bengal ke pehle Governor-General NAHI the — Warren Hastings Bengal\nke pehle Governor-General the (Regulating Act 1773 ke through). William Bentinck India ke pehle\nGovernor-General the (Charter Act 1833). Isliye statement 1 galat aur statement 2 sahi hai. [Q1]\n●\n Trap: India ke pehle Governor-General Lord William Bentinck the — diye gaye options mein wo\n⚠️\nshaamil nahi the, isliye exam ne ye question star (*) kiya tha. Options mein diye gaye Warren Hastings\nsirf Bengal ke pehle GG the, poore India ke nahi. [Q2]\n● Lord William Bentinck India ke pehle Governor-General the — Lord Canning India ke pehle Viceroy the.\nDiye gaye options mein se koi bhi sahi nahi tha, isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q3]\n2. Warren Hastings\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Battle of Buxar (October 1764) → Clive ka dobara India aana (May\n1765) → Treaty of Allahabad (August 1765) → Warren Hastings Bengal ke Governor bane (1772). [Q4]\n● Robert Clive ko India mein British Empire ka founder maana jaata hai — unki Battle of Plassey (1757)\nmein jeet ki wajah se. [Q6]\n● 'Banaras Rebellion' (1781 AD) Raja Chet Singh ne Warren Hastings ke against lead ki thi. [Q7]\n● Asiatic Society Calcutta mein establish hui thi (15 Jan 1784) — us waqt Warren Hastings Bengal ke\nGovernor-General the. [Q8]"," ● 'Ring Fence' (Security Cell) policy Warren Hastings ne follow ki thi — (Wellesley ne bhi baad mein isse\ncontinue kiya) — apne borders ko buffer zones se protect karne ke liye. [Q9, Q10]\n● Warren Hastings ne 1772 AD mein Bengal mein 'Dual Government' system khatam kiya — isse Robert\nClive ne 1765 mein enforce kiya tha. [Q11, Q12]\n● Warren Hastings ke against unjust acts ke ilzaam mein British Parliament mein impeachment\nproceedings (1788-1795) chali — wo aakhir mein acquit ho gaye. [Q13, Q14]\n3. Lord Cornwallis\n● Lord Cornwallis ne India mein judicial organization establish ki — courts ki hierarchy banayi aur\n'Cornwallis Code' (1793) laakar revenue aur judicial administration ko alag kiya. [Q16]\n● Lord Cornwallis ne 'Covenanted Civil Service of India' banayi — unhe 'Father of Civil Services in India'\nkaha jaata hai. [Q17, Q18]\n● Cornwallis ne police stations banayi jinke head 'Daroga' hote the — kisano ke liye wo Company ke\n'authority' ke local representative ki tarah the. [Q19]\n● Lord Cornwallis ki mrityu 1805 AD mein Ghazipur (UP) mein hui — unki tomb wahi hai. [Q20]\n● Lord Cornwallis ne 1793 mein 'Permanent Settlement' introduce ki — Bengal mein. [Q80, Q82]\n4. Sir George Barlow & the Vellore Revolt\n● 'Vellore Mutiny' (1806 AD) Sir George Barlow ke reign mein hui thi — Sepoys ke social-religious\npractices mein interference ki wajah se. [Q15]\n5. Lord Wellesley — The Subsidiary Alliance System\n● Wellesley ki Subsidiary Alliance system ka main agenda tha defense (Napoleonic threat se), doosro ke\nkharche par apni army maintain karna, aur political paramountcy — 'company ke liye fixed income\nsecure karna' iska main agenda NAHI tha. [Q21]\n● Peshwa Bajirao-II, Maratha Sardaro mein sabse pehle the jinhone Wellesley ki Subsidiary Alliance\naccept ki — Treaty of Bassein (December 1802) ke through. [Q22, Q23]\n●\n Trap: 'The first Indian ruler to join Subsidiary Alliance' wale question mein answer 'Nawab of Oudh'\n⚠️\n(1765, Clive ke time) diya gaya tha — halaki Wellesley ki 1798 wali system ke hisaab se Nizam pehle\nthe. [Q24]\n● Lord Wellesley (1798-1805 AD) ne Subsidiary Alliance system ko final shape di. [Q25, Q29]\n● Holkar state (Indore) ne shuru mein Subsidiary Alliance accept NAHI ki thi — unhone bahut baad mein,\n1818 mein accept ki. [Q26]\n● Nizam of Hyderabad (1798 AD) pehle Indian native ruler the jinhone Wellesley ki Subsidiary Alliance\naccept ki. [Q27]\n● Subsidiary Alliance sign karne wale states ka order: Hyderabad (1798) → Mysore (1799) → Oudh\n(1801) → Sindhia (1804). [Q28]"," ● East India Company ka Rajput states ke saath Subsidiary Alliance banane ka main maksad tha British\nsovereignty establish karna. [Q30]\n●\n Trap: Subsidiary Alliance system 1863 mein NAHI, balki Lord Wellesley ne 1798 AD mein introduce\n⚠️\nki thi — galat match. [Q31]\n● Napoleon ke Europe mein badhte prabhaav ke waqt, Lord Wellesley (1798-1805) ne Subsidiary Alliance\nke through India mein British power strengthen ki. [Q32]\n● Sahi match: Lord Wellesley — Fourth Anglo-Mysore War (1799 AD). [Q87]\n●\n Trap: Second Anglo-Maratha War (1803-05) Lord Hastings ke NAHI, Lord Wellesley ke reign mein\n⚠️\nladi gayi thi — galat match. Lord Hastings Third Anglo-Maratha War (1817-18) se associate hain. [Q83]\n6. Lord Hastings (Marquess of Hastings) — Anglo-Nepal & Third Anglo-\nMaratha War\n● Anglo-Nepal War (1814-16) Lord Hastings ke reign mein hui — ye Treaty of Sugauli se khatam hui.\n[Q33]\n● Treaty of Sugauli 1815 AD mein hui thi (2 December 1815 ko sign, March 1816 mein ratify). [Q34]\n●\n Trap: Third Anglo-Maratha War (1817-18) Lord Cornwallis ke NAHI, Lord Hastings ke reign mein hui\n⚠️\n\nthi — galat match. [Q35, Q36]\n● Peshwaship 1818 mein abolish ki gayi — Lord Hastings ne Third Anglo-Maratha War ke baad ye kiya.\n[Q84]\n● Charles Metcalf ko Lord Hastings ne 1817-18 mein Rajputana ki Princely States ke saath Subordinate\nAlliances negotiate karne ki responsibility di. [Q85]\n●\n Trap: Anglo-Nepal War (1814-16) Sir John Shore ke NAHI, Lord Hastings ke reign mein hui thi —\n⚠️\ngalat match. [Q86]\n7. Sir Thomas Munro\n● Sir Thomas Munro 1820-1827 AD tak Madras ke Governor rahe — wo 'Ryotwari System' ke liye jaane\njaate hain. [Q37]\n8. Lord William Bentinck — Reforms\n●\n Trap: Lord William Bentinck ko sirf territorial 'consolidation' (war/annexation) ki wajah se sabse great\n⚠️\n\nBritish ruler NAHI kaha ja sakta — wo liberal reforms (Sati abolition, Thuggee suppression) ke liye\nzyada jaane jaate hain, territorial consolidation Wellesley se associate hoti hai. [Q5]\n● Lord William Bentinck ne 1831 AD mein Mysore ki administration alleged maladministration ki wajah se\nle li thi. [Q38]\n● Third Anglo-Mysore War (1790-92) Lord Cornwallis ke reign mein ladi gayi thi. [Q39]"," ● Lord William Bentinck ne Captain Sleeman ko 1830s mein Thugs (dacoits) suppress karne ke liye\nappoint kiya — Sleeman ne 1500 se zyada thugs arrest kiye, 1837 tak thuggery poori tarah khatam kar\ndi. [Q40, Q41]\n● Bentinck ke social reforms: Sati abolition (1829), Thugs ki suppression, aur Charter Act 1833 (jo slavery\nabolish karne ka lakshya rakhta tha). [Q42]\n● Lord William Bentinck ne 1829 AD mein Sati System ko Regulation XVII se illegal declare kar diya.\n[Q43, Q44, Q45]\n● Augustus Cleveland ne 'Hill Assembly Plan' set up ki thi — Rajmahal hills ke Pahariya tribes ke\ndevelopment ke liye. [Q46]\n● Bengal se slaves ka export 1789 AD mein proclamation se ban kiya gaya tha. [Q47]\n9. Lord Ellenborough\n● Lord Ellenborough (1842-1844 AD) ke period mein British ne Sindh conquer complete kiya, 1843 AD\nmein — Sir Charles Napier ne actual conquest ki. [Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● Lord Ellenborough ne Act-V of 1843 se slavery abolish ki thi. [Q79]\n10. Lord Dalhousie — Annexations & Doctrine of Lapse\n● Awadh ko British Empire mein 1856 mein 'maladministration' (kuprashasan) ka pretext deke annex kiya\ngaya — ye Lord Dalhousie ne kiya. [Q48, Q52]\n● 'Doctrine of Lapse' ke under Jaipur ko annex NAHI kiya gaya tha — Nagpur, Sambalpur aur Satara is\ndoctrine se annex hue the. [Q49]\n● Baghat princely state 1850 AD mein annex hui thi. [Q50]\n●\n Trap: Gwalior ko British ne annex NAHI kiya — Sindh (1843), Awadh (1856), Satara (1848) annex\n⚠️\nhue the. [Q51]\n● Doctrine of Lapse ke under annexation ka chronological order: Satara (1848) → Baghat (1850) →\nUdaipur (1852) → Jhansi (1854). [Q53]\n● Sahi match: 1856 AD — Awadh ka merger. (Satara 1848 mein, Punjab 1849 mein, Jhansi 1854 mein\nannex hue.) [Q54]\n● Lord Dalhousie ne 'Doctrine of Lapse' formulate aur implement ki thi. [Q55]\n● Awadh ke raja Wajid Ali Shah ko misgovernance ke pretext par 1856 mein power se hataya gaya. [Q56]\n● Princely states annexation order: Satara (1848) → Sambalpur (1849) → Jhansi (1854). [Q57]\n● Doctrine of Lapse ka pehla shikaar Satara tha (1848 AD). [Q58, Q59]\n● Lord Dalhousie ka real naam 'James Andrew Broun Ramsay' (1st Marquess of Dalhousie) tha. [Q60]\n● Lord Dalhousie ne Sikkim ka hissa (Darjeeling samet) merge kiya — Sikkim king ne 2 English doctors\nke saath badtameezi ki thi, is pretext par. [Q64]\n● James Outram, Awadh ke British Resident the (1854 se) jab isse British Dominion mein annex kiya\ngaya — unki 'maladministration' report hi Awadh annexation ka basis bani. [Q65]"," ● India ki pehli railway line, Lord Dalhousie ke period mein bichhayi gayi — Bombay-Thane ke beech,\n1853 AD mein, 'Great Indian Peninsula Railway' company ne shuru ki. [Q66, Q67, Q68, Q69]\n● British Indian territory ka last major extension Lord Dufferin ke time hua — Burma ka annexation 1886\nAD mein. [Q70]\n● Lord Dalhousie ne 1854 AD mein pehli baar ek alag 'Public Works Department' (PWD) banayi (1845-\n1855 ke beech). [Q71]\n● Match: Sambalpur — 1849; Satara — 1848; Awadh — 1856; Jhansi — 1854 (annexation years). [Q129]\n11. Lord Canning — The First Viceroy\n● Hindu Widow Remarriage Act 1856 mein Lord Canning ke period mein pass hua. [Q72]\n● Lord Canning ne 1 November 1858 ko Allahabad mein Queen Victoria ka manifesto (Proclamation)\npadha — wo India ke pehle Viceroy bane. [Q73, Q74, Q75]\n●\n Trap: 'Masterly Inactivity' policy Lord Canning se NAHI, John Lawrence se associate hai — Lord\n⚠️\nCanning 1857 Revolt ke waqt Governor-General the aur baad mein India ke pehle Viceroy bane. [Q81]\n12. Queen Victoria's Proclamation & the Title of Empress\n● Queen Victoria ki 1858 Proclamation ne heir adopt karne ka right (adoption right, jo native rulers ke\napne beton ki jagah heir adopt karne ke liye tha) re-establish kiya — annexation policy khatam ki gayi.\n[Q76]\n● Royal Titles Act (1876) ke through, Queen Victoria ko 1877 mein 'Empress of India' declare kiya gaya —\nDelhi Durbar (1 January 1877) mein. [Q77, Q78]\n13. Lord Mayo\n● Lord Mayo ne 1870 mein India mein 'Financial Decentralisation' introduce ki. [Q90]\n● India ka pehla census (1872 AD) Lord Mayo ke tenure mein hua — halaki regular census 1881 mein\nLord Ripon ke time shuru hua. [Q91, Q92]\n● Lord Mayo, ek convict Sher Ali Afridi ne Andaman-Nicobar Islands mein murder kiya tha — India mein\nmurder hone wale ekmatra Viceroy. [Q93, Q94]\n● Lord Mayo ke 1870 Resolution ke sabhi statements sahi hain — ye financial decentralization ki shuruat\nthi, local financial management ki neev rakhi. [Q95, Q96]\n●\n Trap: Archaeological Survey Department 1871 mein Lord Mayo ke time establish hui thi — isliye\n⚠️\n'None' sahi answer hai (kyunki original founder Alexander Cunningham the, aur formal establishment\nCurzon se pehle ka hai). [Q113]\n14. Lord Lytton"," ● Lord Lytton (1876-1880) ne Afghanistan ke against 'Forward Policy' (aggressive/spirited policy) follow ki.\n[Q97, Q98]\n● Lord Lytton, 'Ilbert Bill' (1883) se associate NAHI hain — ye Lord Ripon ke reign mein aaya. [Q99]\n●\n Trap: 'Vernacular Press Act' Lord Curzon ke NAHI, Lord Lytton ke reign mein (1878) pass hua tha —\n⚠️\n\ngalat match. [Q124, Q125]\n●\n Trap: First Anglo-Afghan War (1839-42) Lord Auckland ke reign mein shuru hui, Lord Lytton ke\n⚠️\nNAHI — Lytton Second Anglo-Afghan War (1878-80) se associate hain. [Q88]\n15. Lord Ripon — Local Self-Government & the Ilbert Bill\n● Lord Ripon ke 1882 Resolution ne Local Self-Government institutions ko strengthen kiya — unhe\n'Father of Local Self-Government in India' kaha jaata hai. [Q101, Q102, Q106]\n● 'Ilbert Bill' (1883) controversy iske related thi ki Indian Magistrates ko European convicts ka trial karne ki\ndisqualification hataayi jaaye. [Q103]\n● Pehla 'Factory Act' (1881, women-children ke working hours restrict karne ke liye) Lord Ripon ke tenure\nmein pass hua. [Q104]\n● Statement check: 'Factories Act 1881, wages fix karne ke liye thi' — ye statement galat hai (ye child\nlabor par focus karti thi). Sirf statement 2 sahi hai. [Q105]\n●\n Trap: 'Local self government' Lord Lytton se NAHI, Lord Ripon se associate hai — galat match.\n⚠️\n[Q107]\n16. Lord Curzon\n● Diye gaye options mein se Lord Curzon (1899-1905, 7 saal) ka Viceroy ke roop mein sabse lamba\ntenure raha. [Q100]\n● Lord Curzon ne Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) ko centralize-integrate kiya — ye poori tarah unke\nreign mein reorganize hui. [Q111, Q112]\n● 'Ancient Monuments Preservation Act' 1904 mein, Lord Curzon ke tenure mein pass hua. [Q114]\n● G.K. Gokhale ne Curzon ki administration ko Aurangzeb ke shasan se compare kiya tha. [Q115]\n● Lord Curzon ne 1901 AD mein 'Imperial Cadet Corps' establish ki. [Q116]\n● 1905 ki Civil Administration ke baare mein — Lord Curzon se related dono diye gaye statements sahi\nhain. [Q118]\n● Lord Curzon ke baare mein sahi statements: 'English Empire ko granite rock par establish karna' —\ndono diye gaye statements sahi hain. [Q119]\n● 'Divide and Rule' ki strategy Lord Curzon aur Lord Minto ne apnaayi thi. [Q120]\n● 'Congress apne patan ki taraf badh raha hai, aur India mein rehte hue mera ek bada mahatvakanksha\nhai...' — ye statement Lord Curzon ne diya tha (1900 AD). [Q121]\n17. Lord Minto & Lord Reading"," ● Lord Minto ne Muslims ko jeetne (conquer/appease) ke liye 'Separate Electoral College' system use ki\n— Morley-Minto Reforms (1909) ke through. [Q122]\n● Lord Reading, India ke ekmatra Jewish Viceroy the. [Q123]\n18. Lord Hardinge — The Capital Shift\n● British India ki capital Calcutta se Delhi transfer Lord Hardinge (II) ke period mein hui — 1911 mein\nannounce ki gayi. [Q126]\n19. John Lawrence — The Policy of 'Masterly Inactivity'\n● 'Masterly Inactivity' policy (Afghanistan ke baare mein) John Lawrence se associate ki jaati hai. [Q89]\n20. Match Lists — Mixed Governors, General & Events\n● Match: Clive → Dual Government; Bentinck → English Education; Metcalfe → Press restriction hataana;\nCurzon → Partition of Bengal. [Q108]\n● Match: Lord Dalhousie → Doctrine of Lapse (1848); Lord William Bentinck → Sati Prohibition (1829);\nLord Ripon → Local Self-Government (1882); Lord Curzon → Division of Bengal (1905). [Q109]\n● Sahi match: Lord Ellenborough — Sindh ka Annexation (1843). [Q110]\n● Match: Doctrine of Lapse → Dalhousie; Partition of Bengal → Lord Curzon; Dual Government in Bengal\n→ Clive; Social Reforms → Bentinck. [Q127]\n● Match: Cornwallis → Fort William (Bengal) ke Governor-General the, Regulating Act 1773 ke under\n(Hastings ke baad). Dalhousie → India ke Governor-General the, Charter Act ke under. [Q128]\n21. Chronology of Viceroys & Annexations\n● Viceroys ka sahi chronological order: Curzon (1899-1905) → Hardinge (1910-1916) → Chelmsford\n(1916-1921) → Irwin (1926-1931). [Q117]\n●\n Disputed: Events (Sikkim, Punjab, Jhansi, Burma) ka chronological order — Sikkim ka hissa 1835\n⚠️\nmein cede hua tha, aur additional territory 1850 mein; Punjab 1849 mein annex hua; Jhansi 1854 mein;\nBurma 1886 mein poori tarah annex hui — Sikkim ke exact timing ki wajah se ye question commission\nne star (*) kiya tha. [Q130]\n22. Titles — 'Rai Bahadur' & 'Khan Bahadur'\n● 1857 Revolt ke dauran, native rulers, Zamindars aur baaki loyalists ko revolt suppress karne ke liye 'Rai\nBahadur' aur 'Khan Bahadur' titles di gayi — evidence batata hai ki ye titles 1859-1860 mein confer hui"," thi, Lord Canning ke reign mein — isliye diye gaye options mein se 'None/More than one' sahi answer\nhai. [Q131]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Governor Governor General Viceroy Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0207","t":"05 Economic Impact of British Rule","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.5 — ECONOMIC IMPACT OF BRITISH RULE — FULL MIND MAP\n💰\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Home Charges & Imperial Preference\n2. Reasons for Lack of Industrial Development\n3. Export Trade of the East India Company\n4. The Permanent Settlement — Introduction & Features\n5. Consequences of the Permanent Settlement\n6. The Ryotwari Settlement\n7. Comparing Land Revenue Systems\n8. The Punjab Land Alienation Act\n9. The Mahalwari Settlement\n10. The Assam Tea Company\n11. Military Expenditure\n12. The Drain of Wealth Theory — Dadabhai Naoroji\n13. Trade Surplus & 'Unrequited Exports'\n14. Karl Marx on British Economic Policy\n15. Irrigation — Sir Arthur Cotton\n16. Terminology — Aurang, Banian & Mirasidars\n17. Commercialization of Agriculture\n1. Home Charges & Imperial Preference\n● Colonial rule ke dauran 'Home Charges' England mein Secretary of State for India dwara kiya gaya\nkharcha tha — isme India Office ka expenditure, British staff ki salary-pension, aur debt ka interest\nshaamil tha. India ke bahar wars ladne ke liye use hua paisa isme SHAAMIL NAHI tha. [Q1]\n● 'Imperial Preference' ka matlab tha ki British imports par India mein nominal ya zero duty lagti thi, jabki\nIndia ke exports par Britain mein bhari tariffs lagti thi. [Q2]\n2. Reasons for Lack of Industrial Development\n● British rule ke dauran India mein independent industries develop nahi hui — mukhya wajah thi ki India\nke ameer log industries mein invest karne ki jagah zameen (land property) mein invest karna prefer\nkarte the. [Q3]\n● Industrial Revolution ka India par mukhya impact tha — Indian handicrafts (haath se banaye saman)\nbarbaad ho gaye. Britain se sasti machine-made goods India ke market mein aa gayi, jisse domestic\nindustries khatam ho gayi, aur Indian exports par bhi bahar heavy tariffs lagti thi. [Q52]\n● 'Deindustrialization' 1813 mein shuru hui, jab Company ka commercial monopoly khatam hua — 1833\nke Act ne isse aur badhaya, kyunki Company ki trade activities poori tarah khatam ho gayi aur wo sirf ek\nadministrative body ban gayi. [Q46]\n3. Export Trade of the East India Company\n● 18th century ke beech mein, English East India Company Bengal se cotton, silk cloth, opium, salt-petre\naur sugar jaisi commodities export/purchase karti thi. [Q4]"," 4. The Permanent Settlement — Introduction & Features\n● Lord Cornwallis ne 1793 AD mein 'Permanent Settlement' (jise Ist-e-Marari, Jagirdari ya Malgujari bhi\nkehte the) Bengal, Bihar, Odisha aur Varanasi mein introduce ki. [Q5, Q6, Q7, Q10, Q11]\n● Permanent Settlement Zamindars (landlords) ke saath ki gayi thi — unhe zameen ka malik maana gaya,\njo revenue ka 10/11th hissa Company ko dete the. [Q8, Q9]\n● Cornwallis ki revenue collection ke baare mein: statement 1 (Ryotwari mein bad harvest ke liye\nexemption) galat hai kyunki Ryotwari mein rents high the aur strictly collect hoti thi. Statement 2 sahi hai\n— 'Sunset Law' ki wajah se (jisme revenue sunset tak na diya jaaye to zameen zabt ho jaati thi). [Q29]\n5. Consequences of the Permanent Settlement\n● Land settlement ke baad litigation (case-baazi) badh gayi thi — iski wajah thi court fees hataana aur\nland rights ki complexity, na ki diye gaye specific options — isliye 'None of the above' sahi hai. [Q12]\n● Permanent Settlement (1793) ke under, Zamindars ko farmers ko 'Pattas' issue karni thi — lekin unhone\nye issue NAHI ki kyunki koi official check ya penalty nahi thi non-compliance ke liye — unka main duty\nsirf revenue payment tha. [Q13]\n● Bihar mein introduce hui Permanent Settlement ke baare mein sahi statement — land revenue\n'constitutionalised' (fixed amount) ho gaya tha, Company ke liye. [Q14]\n● Bengal Tenancy Act 1885 mein pass hui — isme Bengal-Bihar ke tenants (kirayedaron) ke land rights\ndefine kiye gaye, badhte rents aur peasant unrest ki wajah se. [Q15]\n6. The Ryotwari Settlement\n● Ryotwari System, Thomas Munro aur Alexander Reed ne generate ki thi — Cornwallis, Permanent\nSettlement se associate hain, Ryotwari se NAHI. [Q16, Q19, Q21, Q22]\n● Ryotwari System sabse pehle Madras Presidency ke Baramahal district (Tamil Nadu) mein implement\nhui — Alexander Reed ne 1792 mein. [Q17, Q24]\n● Permanent Settlement aur Ryotwari System ka introduction respectively Bengal aur Madras mein hua.\n[Q18]\n● Ryotwari system South India (Madras, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka) aur Western India (Bombay) ke kuch\nhisso mein prevalent thi. [Q20, Q23]\n● Ryotwari settlement ke baare mein sabhi diye gaye statements sahi hain — isme kisan (ryot) aur state\nke beech direct contract hota tha, pattas issue hote the, aur scientific land survey hoti thi. [Q25]\n● Ryotwari System mein kisan khud zameen ka malik hota tha aur khud land revenue dene ke liye\nresponsible tha — ownership rights kisano ko di jaati thi, aur tax directly unse collect ki jaati thi. [Q26]\n● 'Ryotwari System, India mein hamesha se prevail karti rahi hai' — ye statement Thomas Munro ne diya\ntha, is system ko Indian tradition ke consistent bataane ke liye. [Q27]"," 7. Comparing Land Revenue Systems\n● Assertion-Reason: British ne Permanent, Ryotwari aur Mahalwari — teen alag systems introduce kiye\nalag-alag regions mein (sahi Assertion) — isse India ke alag-alag hisso mein alag agrarian structures\naur classes (zamindars, peasant proprietors, village communities) bani (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko\nexplain karta hai). [Q28]\n● Match: Jajmani system → North India; Bara Balute → Maharashtra; Mirasi → Tamil Nadu; Adade →\nKarnataka. [Q33]\n8. The Punjab Land Alienation Act\n● 'Punjab Land Alienation Act' 1900 AD mein pass hui — iska maksad tha kisano (farmers) se zameen ka\ntransfer non-agriculturists (jaise money lenders) ko rokna. [Q30]\n9. The Mahalwari Settlement\n● 'Mahalwari Settlement' Holt Mackenzie ne 1822 AD mein, Bengal Presidency (North-Western\nProvinces) mein devise ki thi. [Q32]\n10. The Assam Tea Company\n● Assam mein pehli tea company (Assam Company) England mein 1839 AD mein, 5 lakh rupees ki\ncapital ke saath banayi gayi — ye aaj bhi functioning oldest tea company hai. [Q31]\n11. Military Expenditure\n● British India mein Central revenue ka lagbhag 40% Military force par kharcha hota tha. [Q34]\n12. The Drain of Wealth Theory — Dadabhai Naoroji\n● 'Drain Theory' ka matlab tha ki India ki national wealth (annual product) ka ek hissa Britain export ho\nraha tha, jiske badle India ko koi material return nahi mil raha tha. [Q35]\n● Dadabhai Naoroji ('Grand Old Man of India') ne 'Drain Theory' propound ki thi — apni book 'Poverty and\nUn-British Rule in India' mein. [Q36, Q37, Q45]\n● Statement check: Dadabhai Naoroji ka sabse effective contribution ye tha ki wo pehle Indian nationalist\nthe jinhone economically prove kiya ki Britain India ko exploit kar rahi thi — unhone Drain Theory isi\nanalysis ke basis par di. [Q47]\n● Sir Syed Ahmad Khan, Dadabhai Naoroji ki 'Drain Theory' ko believe NAHI karte the — wo British rule\nke loyal the aur maante the ki Muslim community ka development sirf British rule mein hi possible hai.\n[Q40]"," ● Dadabhai Naoroji ki 'Poverty and Un-British Rule in India' book 1901 AD mein publish hui. [Q41, Q42,\nQ43]\n● Dadabhai Naoroji British House of Commons mein elect hone wale pehle Indian the (1892 AD) —\nLiberal Party ki taraf se contest kiya tha. [Q44]\n● Colonialism ke economic critics the: Dadabhai Naoroji aur unke saath 2 doosre (options mein diye gaye)\neconomists — teeno ne British rule ke economic impact ka analysis kiya aur colonialism ko economic\ngrowth mein sabse badi rukawat mana. [Q39]\n13. Trade Surplus & 'Unrequited Exports'\n● Assertion-Reason: India ka trade surplus tha (exports imports se zyada the) — sahi Assertion. Lekin ye\nsurplus 'Home Charges' aur Britain ke doosre kharcho ke liye use hota tha, isliye India ko badle mein\nkuch nahi milta tha (unrequited exports) — sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai. [Q38]\n14. Karl Marx on British Economic Policy\n● Karl Marx ne kaha tha ki 'British Economic Policy India mein disgusting hai' — unhone bataya ki Indian\ncultivators (kisan) dejection (nirasha) ki state mein the. [Q48]\n15. Irrigation — Sir Arthur Cotton\n● Sir Arthur Cotton ko South India mein Irrigation works ka 'Pioneer' maana jaata hai — wo ek British\nirrigation engineer the. [Q49]\n16. Terminology — Aurang, Banian & Mirasidars\n●\n Trap: 'Aurang' ek Persian term hai jiska matlab warehouse/depot hai, treasury (khazana) NAHI.\n⚠️\n'Banian' Company ke liye Indian agent hote the (sahi). 'Mirasidars' South India ke village elites the jo\ndesignated revenue payers the (sahi). [Q50]\n17. Commercialization of Agriculture\n● 19th century mein British rule ka ek economic result tha 'Indian agriculture ka commercialization' —\nkisano ko cash crops (Indigo, cotton) ugane ke liye majboor kiya gaya, British factories ke liye raw\nmaterial ki tarah, jisse food security aur urban population par negative impact pada. [Q51]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Economic Impact of British Rule Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0208","t":"06 Revolt of 1857","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.6 — REVOLT OF 1857 — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Causes — The Enfield Rifle & Greased Cartridges\n2. Mangal Pandey & the Barrackpore Incident\n3. Bakht Khan at Delhi\n4. General Causes of the Revolt\n5. Foreign Correspondents & Poets Who Witnessed 1857\n6. Outbreak at Meerut & the March to Delhi\n7. Symbols of the Revolt\n8. The Recapture of Delhi\n9. Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi\n10. Khan Bahadur Khan — Bareilly\n11. Begum Hazrat Mahal — Lucknow\n12. Maulvi Liyaqat Ali — Allahabad\n13. Awadh's Contribution — The Largest Number of Soldiers\n14. Nana Saheb, Tatya Tope & Azimullah Khan — Kanpur\n15. Kunwar Singh — Bihar\n16. Maniram Dutta — Assam\n17. Rajasthan — Thakur Kushal Singh of Auwa\n18. Other Local Leaders of the Revolt\n19. Figures NOT Associated with the Revolt of 1857\n20. Loyalist States & Groups\n21. Areas Unaffected by the Revolt\n22. Leaders & Their Areas — Important Match Lists\n23. Chronology of Outbreaks Across India\n24. British Officials During the Revolt\n25. Casualties Among British Officers\n26. Reasons for the Failure of the Revolt\n27. Historians' Interpretations of the Revolt of 1857\n28. Aftermath — Queen Victoria's Proclamation & the End of Company Rule\n29. Army Reorganization After 1857\n1. Causes — The Enfield Rifle & Greased Cartridges\n● British Indian Army mein purani 'Brown Bess' gun ki jagah nayi 'Enfield Rifle' December 1856 mein\nintroduce hui — training Dum Dum, Ambala aur Sialkot mein organize ki gayi. [Q1]\n● 1857 ke Independence War ka immediate cause tha British ke religion mein interference karne ka\nsuspicion — greased cartridges introduce hone se Hindu-Muslim sepoys mein ye shak paida hua ki\nBritish unke religious practices mein hasta-kshep kar rahe hain. [Q2]\n2. Mangal Pandey & the Barrackpore Incident\n● 29 March 1857 ko Barrackpore mein sepoys ne animal fat wali cartridge use karne se mana kar diya —\nMangal Pandey ne apne Sergeant Major ke adjutant ki hatya kar di. [Q3, Q4]\n●\n Trap: Mangal Pandey '34th Bengal Native Infantry' ke sepoy the — diye gaye options (19th, 25th,\n⚠️\n49th, 94th) mein se koi bhi sahi nahi tha, isliye 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q5]"," 3. Bakht Khan at Delhi\n● Bakht Khan ki superior abilities dekhkar, Emperor Bahadur Shah Zafar ne unhe actual authority di aur\n'Saheb-e-Alam Bahadur' ki title bhi. [Q6]\n4. General Causes of the Revolt\n● 1857 revolt ka main cause tha British Empire ki policies — isme political, economic, military, religious\naur social — sabhi causes shaamil the, jaise taxation, land annexations, traditions mein interference.\n[Q7]\n●\n Trap: 'Officers ki inefficiency' sepoys ke rebel hone ki wajah NAHI thi — actual causes the religious\n⚠️\ninterference (Christianity), overseas travel se caste ka nuksaan, aur foreign service allowance (Bhatta)\nka rukna. [Q13]\n5. Foreign Correspondents & Poets Who Witnessed 1857\n● Sir William Howard Russell, London se publish hone wale 'Times' newspaper ke correspondent the\njinhone 1857 mutiny cover ki. [Q8]\n● Famous Urdu poet Mirza Ghalib ne 1857 ki Revolt witness ki — unka original residence Agra tha (27\nDecember 1797 ko paida hue), baad mein Delhi shift ho gaye jaha unki mrityu hui. [Q50, Q51]\n6. Outbreak at Meerut & the March to Delhi\n● 1857 ki Revolution 10 May 1857 ko Meerut se shuru hui — jab sepoys ne nayi cartridges use karne se\nmana karke openly revolt ki. [Q9, Q10]\n● 1857 War of Independence ka pehla event tha sepoys ka Delhi ke Red Fort ki taraf march karna —\nMeerut mein revolt karne ke baad wo 11 May ko Delhi pahunche, ye Kanpur/Lucknow/Jhansi ke revolts\nse pehle hua. [Q11]\n7. Symbols of the Revolt\n● 1857 ki independence struggle ke symbols the 'Lotus' aur 'Chapatis' (roti) — revolt ka message phailane\nke liye use hote the. [Q14]\n8. The Recapture of Delhi\n● Delhi ko British ne 20 September 1857 ko wapas capture kiya — Sikhs aur Pathans ki madad se,\nsuppression campaigns mein relatively early. [Q15]"," 9. Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi\n● Rani Lakshmibai (Manikarnika) ka janm 19 November 1835 ko, Golghar, Varanasi mein hua tha. [Q16]\n● Rani Lakshmibai ki Samadhi Gwalior mein hai — unhone 18 June 1858 ko, lambi ladai ke baad, wahi\nmartyrdom prapt ki. [Q19, Q20]\n● Rani Lakshmibai ne apni aakhri ladai General Hugh Rose ke against ladi — unki mrityu par Hugh Rose\nne kaha tha: 'Sleeping Beauty (Lakshmibai) hi ekmatra 'man' hai Indian rebel leaders mein.' [Q21]\n10. Khan Bahadur Khan — Bareilly\n● Khan Bahadur Khan ne 1857 mein Bareilly (UP) mein revolt lead ki — unhone apni army organize ki aur\nBahadur Shah-II ne unhe Viceroy appoint kiya. [Q17, Q18]\n11. Begum Hazrat Mahal — Lucknow\n● Lucknow (Awadh) mein 1857 ki mutiny Begum Hazrat Mahal (Begum of Oudh) ne lead ki. [Q22, Q23,\nQ24]\n12. Maulvi Liyaqat Ali — Allahabad\n● Maulvi Liyaqat Ali, Allahabad ke ek Muslim religious leader the, jinhone wahan 1857 ki uprising lead ki.\n[Q25]\n13. Awadh's Contribution — The Largest Number of Soldiers\n● 1857 ki Struggle mein sabse zyada soldiers (75,000 se zyada) Oudh (Awadh) se aaye the — Awadh ke\nlagbhag har ghar ka koi na koi member army mein tha. [Q26]\n14. Nana Saheb, Tatya Tope & Azimullah Khan — Kanpur\n● 1857 ke 2 great leaders — Nana Saheb aur Begum Hazrat Mahal — surrender karne se mana karke\nNepal bhaag gaye, jab unki respective cities British ne wapas capture kar li. [Q12]\n● Tatya Tope (Ramchandra Pandurang, 1814 mein Yeola, Maharashtra mein paida hue) Nana Saheb ke\n'Commander-in-Chief' the — unhe 'Ambassador of Revolt' bhi kaha jaata tha. [Q27, Q30]\n● Azimullah Khan, Nana Saheb ke advisor the — unhe 'Krantidoot' (Ambassador of Revolution) bhi kehte\nthe. [Q28]\n● Tatya Tope ko unke close friend Man Singh ne dhoke se pakadwaya — Shivpuri mein 18 April 1859 ko\nunhe hang kiya gaya. [Q29]"," 15. Kunwar Singh — Bihar\n● Kunwar Singh, Jagdishpur (Bhojpur district), Bihar se the — wo 1857 revolt ke Bihar mein sabse\nprominent leader the, ek zamindar/Rajput chief. [Q31, Q32, Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q39, Q40, Q42]\n● Kunwar Singh ne mainly Arrah (Jagdishpur) mein rebellion join ki — BPSC ki answer key ke mutabik\nArrah/Jagdishpur hi unka stronghold tha. [Q33]\n● Statement check: Kunwar Singh (Jagdishpur ke zamindar) ne rebellion lead ki (sahi statement 1) —\nlekin statement 2 galat hai kyunki Lord Dalhousie ne Doctrine of Lapse ke under Jhansi ke adopted son\nka claim reject karke Jhansi annex ki thi. [Q41]\n● Bihar mein 1857 revolt ka centre, 15 July 1857 se 20 January 1858 tak, Jagdishpur tha — Kunwar\nSingh ki leadership mein. [Q44]\n16. Maniram Dutta — Assam\n● Diwan Maniram Dutta ne Assam mein 1857 ki revolution lead ki thi — unhone Kandarpeshwar Singh ko\nraja declare kiya. [Q43]\n17. Rajasthan — Thakur Kushal Singh of Auwa\n● Thakur Kushal Singh of Auwa ne 1857 revolt ke dauran British aur Jodhpur ki joint army ko haraya tha.\n[Q45]\n●\n Trap: Jaipur, 1857 ki revolution ka centre NAHI thi — Ajmer, Neemuch aur Auwa affected the.\n⚠️\n[Q46]\n18. Other Local Leaders of the Revolt\n● Saadat Khan ne Indore mein 1857 mein British ke against struggle ki. [Q47]\n● Maulavi Ahmadullah Shah (Faizabad se), British ke sabse bitter enemy mane jaate the — wo Jihad ka\nprachar karte the. [Q48]\n● Nawab Fazil Mohammad Khan (Bhopal se) ne main movement lead ki aur apni jaan qurbaan ki. [Q49]\n19. Figures NOT Associated with the Revolt of 1857\n●\n Trap: Bhagat Singh, 20th century ke revolutionary the, 1857 revolt se associate NAHI the.\n⚠️\n[Q52]\n●\n Trap: Uddham Singh, 1857 revolt se related NAHI the — wo ek revolutionary the jinhone 1940 mein\n⚠️\nMichael O'Dwyer ki hatya ki thi. [Q53]\n20. Loyalist States & Groups"," ● Gwalior ke Scindias ne British ko sabse zyada support diya — Lord Canning ne famously kaha tha:\n'Agar Scindia rebels se mil jaaye, to main kal hi wapas chala jaaunga.' [Q54]\n● Educated middle class 1857 revolt ke prati neutral rahi — unhe lagta tha British rule India ko modernize\nkaregi. [Q55]\n● Moneylenders (Sahukars) aur bade Landlords (Zamindars) generally revolt mein participate NAHI kiye\n— unke economic interests British ke saath aligned the. [Q56]\n● Nizam of Hyderabad ne East India Company ke against rebel NAHI kiya — wo British ke loyal rahe.\n[Q57]\n21. Areas Unaffected by the Revolt\n● Chittor (Rajasthan) revolt of 1857 se largely unaffected raha. [Q58]\n● Bihar ka Munger area revolt of 1857 se relatively unaffected raha. [Q59]\n22. Leaders & Their Areas — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Bakht Khan → Delhi; Maulvi Ahmadullah → Awadh; Kunwar Singh → Arrah; Nana Saheb →\nKanpur. [Q60]\n● Match: Kunwar Singh → Jagdishpur; Hazrat Mahal → Lucknow; Khan Bahadur → Bareilly; Ahmadullah\n→ Faizabad. [Q61]\n● Match: Jhansi → Rani Laxmibai; Lucknow → Begum Hazrat Mahal; Kanpur → Azimullah Khan;\nFaizabad → Maulvi Ahmad Shah. [Q62]\n●\n Trap: 'Lucknow — Liyaqat Ali' galat match hai — Liyaqat Ali Allahabad ke leader the, Lucknow\n⚠️\nBegum Hazrat Mahal ne lead ki thi. [Q63]\n● Match: Nana Saheb → Kanpur; Nawab Hamid Ali Khan → Delhi; Moulvi Ahmed Ullah → Lucknow; Mani\nRam Diwan → Assam. [Q65]\n● 1857 revolt mein actively participate karne wale leaders — Nana Saheb, Hazrat Mahal, Ahmadullah —\nsabhi ne actively participate kiya, isliye 'more than one option sahi hai' wala answer sahi hai. [Q64]\n23. Chronology of Outbreaks Across India\n●\n Trap: Jhansi mein revolt 11 May 1857 ko NAHI, 4 June 1857 ko shuru hui thi — galat match.\n⚠️\n[Q66]\n24. British Officials During the Revolt\n● Lord Canning, 1857 revolt ke waqt (1856-1862 AD) India ke Governor-General the — wo Company ke\naakhri Governor-General aur British Crown ke under pehle Viceroy bane. [Q67, Q68, Q69, Q70]\n● 1857 uprising ke waqt Barrackpore ke British Commanding Officer, Lieutenant General Sir John Bennet\nHearsey the. [Q71]"," ● Lord Canning ne 1857 mein Allahabad ko emergency headquarters banaya tha. [Q72]\n● 1857 ki revolt ke time British Prime Minister Viscount Palmerston the (1855-1858 tak tenure). [Q73]\n●\n Trap: Col. St. Legar, Lt. Col. Gibbs, aur Col. Wallace — inn mein se koi bhi 1857 Revolt se\n⚠️\nassociate NAHI the. [Q74]\n25. Casualties Among British Officers\n● Lucknow mein General Neil, Major Havelock aur Sir Henry Lawrence ki jaan gayi — General John\nNicholson Delhi mein maare gaye the. [Q79]\n26. Reasons for the Failure of the Revolt\n● 1857 revolt ki failure ki mukhya wajah thi common strategy aur central organization ki kami. [Q75]\n● 1857 ki pehli freedom struggle fail hui kyunki unity ki kami thi, native rulers ne British ka support kiya,\naur British military organization superior thi — sabhi factors. [Q76, Q77]\n● Rajput states mein 1857 ki uprising British ne isliye suppress ki kyunki local Rajput rulers ne\nrevolutionaries ka support NAHI kiya. [Q78]\n● Assertion-Reason: 1857 ki First War of Independence India ko azaadi dilane mein fail rahi (sahi\nAssertion) — kyunki major Indian rulers ka support nahi mila aur Bahadur Shah Zafar ki central\nleadership kamzor thi (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q80]\n27. Historians' Interpretations of the Revolt of 1857\n● Sir James Outram aur W. Taylor ne 1857 revolt ko 'conspiracy' (Hindu-Muslim conspiracy) kaha tha.\n[Q81]\n● V.D. Savarkar ne 1857 ki revolt ko 'First War of Independence' kaha — apni book 'The Indian War of\nIndependence 1857' mein. [Q82, Q83, Q84, Q85]\n● Indian Freedom struggle ke official historian Dr. S.N. Sen the — unki book 'Eighteen Fifty-Seven' 1957\nmein publish hui. [Q86]\n● Sir Syed Ahmed Khan pehle Indian the jinhone 1857 uprising ke causes par Indian language mein likha\n— unki book 'Asbab-e-Baghawat-e-Hind' (1859, Urdu mein). [Q87]\n● R.C. Majumdar ne kaha: 'So-called first national war of independence na to pehli thi, na national, na hi\nek war of independence' — apni book 'The Sepoy Mutiny and the Revolt of 1857' mein. [Q88, Q89]\n● Dr. R.C. Majumdar prominent Indian historian the jinhone 1857 ki revolution ko ek revolution ki tarah\naccept NAHI kiya. [Q90]\n● Dr. R.C. Majumdar aur Dr. S.N. Sen — dono historians ne kaha ki 19th century ke beech mein Indian\nnationalism 'embryonic stage' (abhi shuruat ki avastha) mein thi. [Q91]\n28. Aftermath — Queen Victoria's Proclamation & the End of Company Rule"," ● 1857 ki revolt ka ek sahi conception hai ki isne East India Company ke rule ko 'death blow' diya — India\nki administration directly British Crown ko transfer ho gayi. [Q92]\n● Queen Victoria ne 1 November 1858 ko (Lord Canning ke through, Allahabad mein) Indian\nAdministration ko British Crown ke under lene ki declaration ki. [Q93]\n● 1858 ki Queen Victoria ki declaration mein Indians ko assure kiya gaya ki annexation policy (Doctrine of\nLapse) chhod di jayegi — baaki promises (jaise equal treatment) mostly fulfil nahi hue. [Q94]\n● Queen Victoria's Proclamation (1858) ke objectives the: annexation khatam karna aur power ko Crown\nko transfer karna — Company ki trade regulate karna objective NAHI tha, kyunki Company ka rule hi\nkhatam ho gaya tha. [Q95]\n29. Army Reorganization After 1857\n● 1857 ki suppression ke baad army reorganization se associate commission 'Peel Commission' thi —\nEuropean aur Indian soldiers ka ratio badhane ke liye. [Q96]\n● 1857 ke baad, British ne recruitment shift karke 'martial races' (Gurkhas, Sikhs, Punjabis, North India\nse) ki taraf ki — Awadh aur Bihar se soldiers avoid kiye, jinhone revolt lead ki thi. [Q97]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Revolt of 1857 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0209","t":"07 Other Civil Uprisings","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.7 — OTHER CIVIL UPRISINGS — FULL MIND MAP\n✊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Indigo Revolt & 'Neel Darpan'\n2. Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay & the Sanyasi Revolt\n3. The Wahabi & Kuka Movements\n4. Pagalpanthi & Farazi Movements\n5. Velu Thampi & the Ganjam Revolt\n6. Ramosi & Gadkari Uprisings — Maharashtra\n7. Khond & Kol Revolts\n8. Waghera Uprising & Pre-1857 Chronology\n9. Chhotanagpur Tribal Revolts — Ho, Munda & Kol\n10. The Santhal Rebellion\n11. The Bhil Uprising — Maharashtra & the Lasodia Movement\n12. Birsa Munda & the 'Ulgulan' Revolt\n13. The Term 'Adivasi' & Common Factors in Tribal Insurrections\n14. Khairwar Movement & the Sambalpur Revolts\n15. The Deccan Riots\n16. Match Lists — Regional Rebellions\n17. The Moplah Rebellion\n18. The Eka Movement\n19. Chuar & Bhil Revolts — Location Corrections\n20. The Tana Bhagat Movement\n21. Kuka & Kuki Rebellions — A Common Confusion\n22. The Bhumij Revolt\n23. The Tebhaga Movement\n24. Gandhi's Influence on Tribal Leaders\n25. The Early Labour Movement\n1. The Indigo Revolt & 'Neel Darpan'\n● 1857 Revolt ke turant baad Bengal mein 'Indigo Revolt' (1859-60) hui — Sanyasi Revolt usse pehle\n(1763-1800), Santhal Revolt usse thodi pehle (1855-56), aur Pabna Revolt baad mein (1873-76) hui.\n[Q1]\n● 1858-1859 ka play 'Neel Darpan' Dinabandhu Mitra ne likha, jisme indigo (neel) farmers ki durdasha\ndikhayi gayi. [Q2, Q4, Q5, Q6]\n● Indigo Rebellion iske baare mein thi ki kisan neel (indigo) ugana nahi chahte the, lekin unhe\ngalat/unacceptable contracts ke through majboor kiya jaata tha bahut kam price par ugane ke liye. [Q3]\n● 20th century ki shuruat tak Indigo cultivation decline ho gayi — Europe mein synthetic (artificial) dyes ki\ninvention ki wajah se natural indigo unprofitable ho gayi. [Q7]\n2. Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay & the Sanyasi Revolt\n● Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay ke baare mein: wo Calcutta University ke pehle graduates mein se ek\nthe, aur 'Sitaram' unka last novel tha — dono statements sahi hain. [Q8]\n● 'Vande Mataram' song Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ne compose kiya tha — unke novel 'Anand Math' se\nliya gaya hai. [Q9]"," ● Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ke novel 'Anandmath' mein 'Sanyasi Revolt' (1763-1800) ka zikr hai —\nunhone apni writings ke through isse famous kiya. [Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n3. The Wahabi & Kuka Movements\n●\n Trap: Kol uprising 1831-32 AD mein hui thi, Sanyasi revolt 1763-1800 AD mein — is match-question\n⚠️\n\nke options (C) aur (D) dono galat the. [Q15]\n● Munger ke 'Barhiyataal' resistance ka maksad tha 'Bakast' zameen ki restoration ki demand. [Q16]\n● 19th century mein 'Wahabi Movement' ka main centre Patna tha — Syed Ahmad Barelavi ki mrityu ke\nbaad Patna ye movement ka chief centre ban gaya. [Q17]\n● 'Kuka Movement' Bhagat Jawahar Mal ne found ki, lekin Guru Ram Singh ne Punjab mein organize kiya\n— Sikhism ki 'purification' ke liye. [Q18, Q19]\n4. Pagalpanthi & Farazi Movements\n● 'Pagalpanthi' rebellion North Bengal ke Garo tribe ne ki thi — Karam Shah ne 'Pagal Panth' found ki thi.\n[Q20, Q21]\n● 'Farazi rebellion' ke leader Dadu Miyan the (Haji Shariatullah ke bete) — Faraizis, Haji Shariatullah ke\nfollowers the. [Q22, Q23]\n5. Velu Thampi & the Ganjam Revolt\n● Velu Thampi (Travancore ke Diwan) ne Kerala mein British ke against revolt lead ki. [Q24]\n● Ganjam Revolt (1800 AD ke aas-paas) ke baare mein diye gaye 3 statements sahi hain — 4th\nstatement galat hai kyunki Dhananjay, Shrikar Bhanja ke bete the, pita NAHI. [Q25]\n6. Ramosi & Gadkari Uprisings — Maharashtra\n● Vasudeo Balwant Phadke ne Maharashtra mein 'Ramosi Krishak Jatha' (1845-83 AD) found ki —\nunhone Ramosi tribes ko British ke against ek fighting force mein organize kiya. [Q26]\n● Ramosi hill tribes Western Ghats mein rehte the — unhone 1822 mein Chittar Singh ki leadership mein\nBritish administration ke against revolt ki. [Q27]\n● 'Gadakari rebellion' ka centre Kolhapur tha — Gadkaris, Maratha forts ke hereditary servants the,\njinhone 1844 mein arbitrary land revenue policies ki wajah se revolt ki. [Q28]\n7. Khond & Kol Revolts\n● Khond tribe (Chakra Bisoi ki leadership mein) ne British ke against revolt ki, kyunki 'Mariah' (human\nsacrifice) system ban kar diya gaya tha, saath hi naye taxes aur Zamindars ka entry bhi wajah thi. [Q29]"," ● Kol Revolt (Chhota Nagpur region, 1831-32) ki leadership Budhu Bhagat ne ki thi. [Q30]\n● 1831 ka Kol Mutiny (Buddho Bhagat ke under) Singhbhum, Ranchi, Palamu aur Hazaribagh\n(Chhotanagpur) regions mein hui — outsiders ke exploitation ki wajah se. [Q31]\n8. Waghera Uprising & Pre-1857 Chronology\n● 'Waghera Uprising' Baroda mein hui (1818-1819), Gaekwad aur British forces ke against. [Q32]\n● 1857 se pehle ke uprisings ka sahi chronological order: Bengal Sepoy Mutiny (1764) → Vellore Mutiny\n(1806) → Kutch Rebellion (1819) → Kol Uprising (1831) → Santhal Uprising (1855). [Q33]\n● Vellore Mutiny (1806) Sir George Barlow (1805-1807) ke reign mein hui. [Q34]\n9. Chhotanagpur Tribal Revolts — Ho, Munda & Kol\n●\n Disputed: Chhotanagpur mein kai tribal revolts hui (Kol, Santhal, Munda) — 'Ho revolt' 1820-21 mein\n⚠️\n\nhui thi, jo diye gaye options mein sabse close answer hai, lekin question ambiguous hai. [Q35]\n● Munda aur Ho tribes (Chhotanagpur region, us waqt Bihar ka hissa) ne 1831 mein British ke against\nrevolt ki. [Q36]\n● 'Hoz (Ho) revolt' 1820-21 mein, Santhal Pargana region mein hui thi. [Q63]\n10. The Santhal Rebellion\n● Santhal Revolt (1855-56 AD) ki leadership 4 bhaiyo — Sidhu, Kanhu, Chand aur Bhairav — ne ki thi.\n[Q37, Q38, Q39, Q40, Q41, Q42, Q43]\n●\n Trap: 'Ahom Rebellion' 1815 mein NAHI, 1828 mein hui thi, Gomdhar Kunwar ki leadership mein —\n⚠️\ngalat match. [Q44]\n● Santhals ne 1855 mein British Commander Major Burrough ki forces ko Pirpainati mein haraya. [Q45]\n● 'Santhal Hool' (1855) ke baare mein 3 statements sahi hain — 4th statement galat hai kyunki Santhal\ninfluence Bhagalpur-Rajmahal area mein tha, Muzaffarpur ke pass Ganga Valley mein NAHI. [Q46]\n● Santhal Uprising ke baad, colonial government ne 2 measures liye: ek alag 'Santhal Pargana' district\nbanaya, aur unki zameen protect karne ke liye 'Santhal Pargana Tenancy Act' pass kiya. [Q47]\n● Santhal Pargana region ko ancient time mein 'Narikhand' (Buddhist literature mein 'Kajangala' bhi) kaha\njaata tha. [Q48]\n11. The Bhil Uprising — Maharashtra & the Lasodia Movement\n● 'Bhil uprising' (1818-31) Maharashtra ke Khandesh region mein hui. [Q49]\n● Govind Giri ne 'Lasodia Movement' launch ki, Mewar-Bagar ke Bhils ke social reforms ke liye — unhone\n1883 mein 'Samp Sabha' bhi found ki. [Q50]"," ● Bhils ne M.P. aur Maharashtra (Khandesh region) mein British ke against revolt ki (1818-1831). [Q80]\n12. Birsa Munda & the 'Ulgulan' Revolt\n● 'Ulgulan' (Great Tumult) Revolt (1899-1900) Birsa Munda ne lead ki — independent 'Munda Raj'\nestablish karne ke liye. [Q51, Q52]\n● Birsa Munda ko 'Dharti Aaba' (Father of the Earth) kaha jaata tha. [Q53]\n● Munda rebellion ke leader Birsa Munda the. [Q54, Q55]\n●\n Disputed: Mundas ne 1899-1900 mein revolt ki — diye gaye options mein exact date sahi nahi tha;\n⚠️\nBirsa ne khud ko 1895 mein prophet declare kiya tha. [Q56]\n● Birsa Munda ko 3 February 1900 ko, Jamkopai forest mein, sote hue capture kiya gaya. [Q57]\n● Birsa Munda 'Munda Raj' establish karna chahte the, kisi modern state (Jharkhand/Chhattisgarh jaise)\nke pakshadhar NAHI the — isliye 'None of these' sahi answer hai. [Q58]\n● Birsa Munda ka mukhya working area Ranchi tha — unki revolt bhi wahi hui. [Q59, Q60]\n13. The Term 'Adivasi' & Common Factors in Tribal Insurrections\n● Tribal logo ke liye 'Adivasi' word sabse pehle Thakkar Bappa (Amritlal Vithaldas Thakkar) ne use kiya\ntha. [Q61]\n● 19th century ke tribal insurrections ka common factor tha — tribal communities ke purane agrarian order\nka complete disruption (bikhraav). [Q62]\n14. Khairwar Movement & the Sambalpur Revolts\n● 'Khairwar Tribal Movement' 1874 mein, Bhagirath Manjhi ki leadership mein hui. [Q64]\n● Surendra Sai ne Sambhalpur mein kai anti-British revolts lead ki. [Q65]\n15. The Deccan Riots\n● Events ka chronological order: Santhal (1855-56) → Sepoy Mutiny (1857) → Indigo (1859-60) →\nDeccan Riot (1875). [Q66]\n● 1875 ke Deccan Riots ka immediate cause tha famine ka darr aur Mahajans (moneylenders) ke high\ninterest rates ka combination — isliye 'more than one option sahi hai' wala answer sahi hai. [Q67]\n● 1857 ke baad hue popular movements: Indigo (1859-60), Deccan (1875), aur Birsa Munda (1899-1900)\n— Santhal Rebellion 1857 se PEHLE (1855-56) hui thi. [Q68]\n16. Match Lists — Regional Rebellions"," ● Match: Moplah → Kerala; Pabna → Bengal; Eka → Oudh; Birsa Munda → Bihar (aaj ka Jharkhand).\n[Q69]\n● Match (chronological): Tebhaga (1946-47), Mopla (1921), Pabna (1873-76), Indigo (1859-60). [Q71]\n● Match: Pabna (1873-85), Eka (1922), Santhal (1855-56), Tana Bhagat (1914). [Q72]\n● Match: Rampa (1879-80), Pabna (1873-76), Indigo (1859-60), Jaintia (1860-63). [Q74]\n● Match: Barrackpur (Nov 1824), Berhampur (Feb 1857), Santhal (1855-56), Vellore (July 1806). [Q77]\n● Match: Ahom (1828), Kol (1831-32), Santhal (1855-56), Moplah (1921). [Q78]\n● Match: Kuki → Tripura/Manipur; Kuka → Punjab; Pabna → Bengal; Birsa Munda → Bihar (Jharkhand).\n[Q83]\n● Match: Paika → Jagbandhu (leader); Bareilly → Mufti Mohammad Aiwaz; Malabar → Edachana\nKungan; Silhat → Radharam. [Q85]\n17. The Moplah Rebellion\n● Moplah Rebellion (1921) Kerala ke Malabar region mein bhadka — Muslim tenants ka Hindu landlords\nke against uprising, high rent aur tenure ki insecurity ki wajah se. [Q70, Q75, Q76]\n18. The Eka Movement\n● 'Eka Movement' (1921-22) UP ke Hardoi, Barabanki jaise areas ke farmers ne shuru ki thi. [Q73]\n19. Chuar & Bhil Revolts — Location Corrections\n●\n Trap: 'Chuar Revolt' Madhya Pradesh mein NAHI hui — ye Bengal ke Bankura aur Midnapore\n⚠️\nregions mein hui thi. [Q79]\n●\n Trap: 'Tana Bhagat' movement Nayak ne NAHI, Oraon saints (jaise Jatra Bhagat) ne banayi thi —\n⚠️\ngalat match. [Q81]\n20. The Tana Bhagat Movement\n● Jatra Oraon (Jatra Bhagat) ne 1914 mein Chhotanagpur mein 'Tana Bhagat Movement' shuru ki. [Q82]\n21. Kuka & Kuki Rebellions — A Common Confusion\n●\n Disputed: Kuka revolt 1840s mein shuru hui thi, aur Kuki rebellion ~1917 ke aas-paas hui — ye 2\n⚠️\nalag movements hain jo aksar confuse hoti hain, isliye is match-question mein multiple options galat the\naur commission ne isse star (*) kiya. [Q84]"," 22. The Bhumij Revolt\n● 'Bhumij Revolt' (1832-33, Jungle Mahal region) ki leadership Ganga Narain ne ki thi. [Q86]\n23. The Tebhaga Movement\n● 'Tebhaga Movement' 1946 mein Bengal se, 'Bangiya Pradeshik Kisan Sabha' (BPKS) ki leadership\nmein shuru hui. [Q87]\n24. Gandhi's Influence on Tribal Leaders\n● Haipou Jadonang (Manipur) pehle tribal leader the jo Mahatma Gandhi aur unki ideology se inspired\nhue. [Q88]\n25. The Early Labour Movement\n● Narayanji Meghaji Lokhande (N.M. Lokhande, 1848-1897) ko India mein labour movement organize\nkarne wale pehle leader maana jaata hai. [Q89]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Other Civil Uprisings Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0210","t":"08 Development of Education in Modern India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.8 — DEVELOPMENT OF EDUCATION IN MODERN INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n📚\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Orientalist Institutions — Calcutta Madarsa, Asiatic Society & Sanskrit College\n2. Translators of Sanskrit Classics into English\n3. Reasons & Funding for Spreading Modern Education\n4. Wood's Despatch (1854)\n5. The Hunter Commission\n6. National Council of Education & the Sadler Commission\n7. Lord Macaulay & the 'Filtration Theory'\n8. The First Universities\n9. Women's Education & the Deccan Education Society\n10. The Aligarh Movement\n11. Hindu College, Calcutta\n12. Sanskrit College & Fort William College — A Match Check\n13. Fort William College\n14. Banaras Hindu University (BHU)\n1. Early Orientalist Institutions — Calcutta Madarsa, Asiatic Society & Sanskrit\nCollege\n● Warren Hastings ne 1780 AD mein Calcutta mein 'Calcutta Madarsa' banwaya — Muslim law aur\nrelated subjects padhane ke liye — ye India mein British dwara set up ki gayi pehli Madarsa thi. [Q1]\n● Sir William Jones (Calcutta Supreme Court ke judge) ne 1784 mein, Warren Hastings ke support se,\n'Asiatic Society of Bengal' found ki. [Q2]\n● Jonathan Duncan (Benaras ke Resident) ne 1791 mein Varanasi mein pehla 'Sanskrit Mahavidyalaya'\n(Sanskrit College) establish kiya — Hindu law, philosophy aur literature padhane ke liye. [Q3]\n● Assertion-Reason: Warren Hastings ne Oriental studies ko encourage kiya (sahi Assertion) — lekin\nunhone khud Asiatic Society ki presidency lene se mana kar diya, Sir William Jones ke favour mein\n(sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q4]\n2. Translators of Sanskrit Classics into English\n● Michael Madhusudan Dutta ko 1822 mein Paris ki 'Royal Asiatic Society' (La Societe Asiatique) ki\nmembership offer hui thi. [Q5]\n● Charles Wilkins pehle Englishman the jinhone Bhagavad Gita ka English translation kiya — Warren\nHastings ne is translation ki preface (bhoomika) likhi thi. [Q6]\n● Sir William Jones pehle the jinhone Kalidasa ki famous rachna 'Shakuntala' (Abhigyan Shakuntalam) ka\n1789 mein English translation kiya. [Q7]\n3. Reasons & Funding for Spreading Modern Education"," ● Pre-independence India mein British Government ka modern education phailane ka mukhya reason tha\n— administration ke chhote/minor posts ke liye educated Indians ki zaroorat, taaki administration ka\nkharcha kam ho. [Q8]\n● 'Charter Act, 1813' pehli baar India mein education ke liye 1 lakh rupees allot ki — annual basis par.\n[Q9]\n4. Wood's Despatch (1854)\n● Wood's Despatch (1854) ne 'Grants-in-Aid' introduce ki aur universities banane ki recommendation di —\nlekin isne HAR level par English recommend NAHI ki, primary level ke liye vernacular languages aur\nhigher education ke liye English suggest ki. [Q10]\n● Wood's Despatch (1854) ne higher education mein English ko promote kiya, aur female education aur\nvocational training ka bhi support kiya — dono statements sahi hain. [Q11]\n● Charles Wood ka 'Despatch' Education se related tha — ise India ke English Education System ka\n'Magna Carta' kaha jaata hai. [Q12, Q13]\n5. The Hunter Commission\n● Hunter Commission report ne 'Primary Education' ke development par special emphasis diya. [Q14]\n● Lord Ripon ne 1882 mein pehli 'Indian Education Commission' (Hunter Commission) appoint ki thi. [Q15]\n6. National Council of Education & the Sadler Commission\n● 'National Council of Education' 15 August 1906 ko establish hui thi. [Q16]\n● 'Sadler Commission' (1917) Education se related thi — khaaskar Calcutta University ki problems study\nkarne ke liye. [Q17, Q18]\n● 1902 mein, Lord Curzon ne 'University Commission' appoint ki jisme 2 Indian members the: Syed\nHussain Bilgrami aur Justice Gurudas Banerjee. [Q19]\n7. Lord Macaulay & the 'Filtration Theory'\n● Lord Macaulay, English Education (India mein) se associate hain. [Q20]\n● Colonial period mein 'Downward Filtration Theory' Education se related thi — is idea ke mutabik higher\nclasses ko educate karo, aur ye gyan neeche masses tak 'filter' ho jaayega. [Q21]\n● India ki Education policy mein 'Filtration Theory' ke propounder Macaulay the. [Q22]\n● India mein modern educational system ki foundation 'Macaulay's Minutes of 1835' ne rakhi — jo\nWestern sciences aur literature ko English medium mein promote karti thi. [Q23]\n● Macaulay ne apna famous Indian Education wala minute 02 February 1835 ko issue kiya tha. [Q24]"," ● English Education India mein introduce hone ki 3 wajahein thi: Charter Act ne funds diye, ek committee\nne medium ka debate kiya, aur controversy (jo Macaulay ne resolve ki) ne English adopt karne ki taraf\nlead kiya — sabhi teen factors. [Q25]\n● Lord William Cavendish Bentinck ke reign mein English Education India mein introduce hui — unhone 7\nMarch 1835 ko Macaulay ka Minute accept kiya, English ko official instruction medium banate hue. [Q26]\n8. The First Universities\n● India ki pehli 3 universities (Calcutta, Madras, aur Bombay) 1857 mein establish hui — Wood's\nDespatch ki recommendations follow karte hue, London University ke model par. [Q27]\n9. Women's Education & the Deccan Education Society\n● D.K. Karve (ek prominent social reformer) ne 1916 mein Bombay mein pehli Indian Women's University\nestablish ki. [Q28]\n● B.G. Tilak, Agarkar aur Chiplunkar ne milkar 'Deccan Educational Society' banayi thi. [Q29]\n10. The Aligarh Movement\n● Sir Syed Ahmad Khan ne 1875 mein 'Muhammadan Anglo-Oriental College, Aligarh' establish ki —\n1920 mein ye Aligarh Muslim University ban gayi. [Q30]\n● 'Aligarh Movement' ka initial objective tha — Indian Muslims mein Western scientific education ko\npromote karna, Islamic values ko preserve karte hue. [Q34]\n11. Hindu College, Calcutta\n● Sabse pehle establish hui institution 'Hindu College, Calcutta' thi (1817 mein) — Delhi College 1824\nmein, Mayo College aur MAO College 1875 mein bane. [Q31]\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ne David Hare aur Alexander Duff ke saath milkar 1817 mein Hindu College\nestablish ki. [Q32]\n● Famous 'Hindu College' David Hare ne 1817 mein Calcutta mein establish ki. [Q33]\n12. Sanskrit College & Fort William College — A Match Check\n● Educational institutions ke pairs mein se sirf 1 pair sahi hai — Sanskrit College Jonathan Duncan ne,\naur Fort William College Richard Wellesley (Lord Wellesley) ne banayi thi, 'Arthur' Wellesley ne NAHI.\n[Q35]"," 13. Fort William College\n● Wellesley ne Calcutta mein 'Fort William College' establish ki thi taaki wo British civilians ko India mein\nadministrative purpose ke liye train-teach kar sakein. [Q36]\n● Fort William College, Calcutta mein, 1800 CE mein establish hui thi — British civil servants ko Indian\nlanguages mein train karne ke liye. [Q37]\n●\n Trap: Fort William College 10 July 1800 ko found hui thi, June mein NAHI — is statement (1) galat\n⚠️\nhai, lekin statement (2) sahi hai. [Q38]\n14. Banaras Hindu University (BHU)\n● Madan Mohan Malviya ne Indian universities mein religious education ke liye vigorously advocate kiya\n— unhone 1916 mein BHU found ki. [Q39]\n● Annie Besant ne 1898 mein 'Central Hindu School of Banaras' found ki, jo baad mein Banaras Hindu\nUniversity ban gayi. [Q40]\n● Lord Hardinge (Viceroy) ne 4 February 1916 ko Banaras Hindu University ki foundation stone rakhi thi.\n[Q41]\n● Banaras Hindu University (BHU), Varanasi, pehli university thi jo 'Central University' declare hui (1916).\n[Q42]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Development of Education in Modern India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0211","t":"09 Development of Press in Modern India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.9 — DEVELOPMENT OF PRESS IN MODERN INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n📰\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Printing Press in India — Origin & First Newspaper\n2. Press Censorship & Legislation\n3. Bal Gangadhar Tilak & the Press\n4. Diaspora & Revolutionary Papers Abroad\n5. Raja Ram Mohan Roy's Journal\n6. The Indian Mirror\n7. Amrita Bazar Patrika\n8. Papers Critical of Congress & Revolutionary Terrorism\n9. Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar — 'Som Prakash'\n10. 'The Leader' — Madan Mohan Malviya\n11. Gandhi's Journals — Indian Opinion, Young India & Harijan\n12. The First Hindi & English Newspapers by Indians\n13. 'Vande Mataram' (English Weekly) — Aurobindo Ghosh\n14. Regional Papers — Patna, Kerala & the Independent\n15. Important Match Lists — Regional Newspapers & Editors\n16. 'Pratap' — Ganesh Shankar Vidyarthi & the Bijoliya Movement\n17. 'Bahishkrit Bharat' — B.R. Ambedkar\n18. 'Al-Hilal' — Abul Kalam Azad\n19. 'Vande Mataram' (Urdu Daily, Lahore) — Lala Lajpat Rai\n20. Match Corrections — Not Correctly Matched Pairs\n21. 'Qaumi Awaz' — Jawaharlal Nehru\n22. 'Dash Roja' — Abdul Gaffar Khan\n1. The Printing Press in India — Origin & First Newspaper\n● Portuguese ne 1556 AD mein India (aur Asia) mein pehli printing press Goa mein establish ki. [Q1]\n● India ka pehla newspaper 'Bengal Gazette' tha — James Augustus Hicky ne 1780 mein Kolkata mein\nshuru ki, ye pehla English newspaper bhi tha. [Q2, Q3]\n2. Press Censorship & Legislation\n● Lord Wellesley ne 1799 mein 'Censorship of Press Act' introduce ki thi, French propaganda ko rokne ke\nliye. [Q4]\n● 'Vernacular Press Act' (1878) Lord Lytton ne enact ki thi — vernacular press ko control karne ke liye. Ye\n1882 mein Lord Ripon ne repeal ki. [Q5, Q7, Q8]\n● Vernacular Press Act ne magistrate ko power di ki agar koi newspaper aapatijanak (objectionable)\npublish kare to printing press aur security deposit confiscate kar sakein. [Q6]\n● Vernacular Press Act statements: Lytton ne 1878 mein enact ki, isse iski restrictive nature ki wajah se\n'Gagging Act' bhi kehte hain, aur Ripon ne 1882 mein repeal ki — sabhi statements sahi hain. [Q9]\n● Lord William Bentinck ne press ke prati liberal attitude apnayi — halaki wo 1835 mein resign kar gaye,\nunke acting successor Charles Metcalfe ne 1835 mein ek naya Press Act pass kiya jisne press ko azaad\nkiya. [Q10]"," 3. Bal Gangadhar Tilak & the Press\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak pehle Indian journalist the jinhe apni duty perform karne ke liye jail jaana pada\n(1882 mein 4 mahine). [Q11]\n● Lokmanya Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne 1881 mein 'Kesari' (Marathi) aur 'Maratha' (English) newspapers\nshuru kiye, India ki freedom struggle ki cause ke liye. [Q19]\n4. Diaspora & Revolutionary Papers Abroad\n● Tarak Nath Das ne America (Vancouver, North America) mein 'Free Hindustan' newspaper shuru ki thi.\n[Q12]\n● 'Gadar' journal (Gadar Party ka) ka pehla issue Urdu mein publish hua tha (1 November 1913 ko). [Q15]\n● Gadar Party ka journal 'Gadar' ek weekly journal tha. [Q16]\n5. Raja Ram Mohan Roy's Journal\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ne Persian weekly 'Miratul Akhbar' publish ki thi (1822 mein). [Q13]\n6. The Indian Mirror\n● 'Indian Mirror' newspaper Calcutta se publish hoti thi (1861 mein Devendranath Tagore aur Manmohan\nGhosh ne shuru ki thi). [Q14]\n● Indian Mirror ne January 1886 mein Indian National Congress ke possible future role ke baare mein\nlikha tha. [Q72]\n7. Amrita Bazar Patrika\n● Shishir Kumar Ghosh aur Motilal Ghosh ne 1868 mein 'Amrita Bazar Patrika' found ki thi. [Q17]\n● Amrita Bazar Patrika ne raat-o-raat Bengali se English mein transform kiya — 1878 ki Vernacular Press\nAct ki restrictions se bachne ke liye. [Q18]\n8. Papers Critical of Congress & Revolutionary Terrorism\n● Revolutionary period ke Bangawasi, Kaal aur Kesari — teeno magazines ne Congress ki moderate\npolicies ki criticism ki. [Q20]\n● Sandhya, Yugantar aur Kaal — teeno newspapers ne India ki freedom struggle ke dauran revolutionary\nterrorism ko advocate kiya. [Q21]"," ●\n Trap: 'Young India', revolutionary activities se associate NAHI thi — ye Mahatma Gandhi se related\n⚠️\nthi aur non-violence promote karti thi. [Q22]\n9. Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar — 'Som Prakash'\n● Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar ne 1858 mein Bengali weekly 'Som Prakash' shuru ki thi. [Q23]\n10. 'The Leader' — Madan Mohan Malviya\n● 'Leader' (Madan Mohan Malviya ke edit karne wala) liberals ki policies ka mouthpiece thi. [Q24]\n11. Gandhi's Journals — Indian Opinion, Young India & Harijan\n● 'Indian Opinion' journal ke pehle editor Mansukh Lal Hiralal Nazar the — Gandhi ne 1903 mein South\nAfrica mein ye newspaper shuru ki thi, Indians ki shikayat highlight karne ke liye. [Q25, Q26]\n● 'Indian Opinion' Gujarati, Hindi, Tamil aur English mein publish hoti thi — Urdu mein NAHI. [Q27]\n● 'Young India' weekly Home Rule Party members (Jamnadas Dwarkadas aur Shankarlal Banker) ne\nshuru ki thi — baad mein Gandhi iske editor bane. [Q28]\n● 'Harijan' Mahatma Gandhi ne English weekly ki tarah shuru ki thi — iska pehla issue 11 February 1933\nko Poona (Pune) se publish hua. [Q39, Q41]\n●\n Trap: Mahatma Gandhi 'Indian Mirror' se associate NAHI the — wo Indian Opinion, Young India aur\n⚠️\nHarijan se juday the. Indian Mirror Devendranath Tagore aur Manmohan Ghosh ne banayi thi. [Q40]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne 'Indian Opinion', 'Harijan', 'Young India' aur 'Navjeevan' shuru ki — 'The Pioneer'\n(1865, George Allen ne Allahabad mein shuru ki) unse related NAHI thi. [Q55]\n●\n Trap: Mahatma Gandhi 'Yugantar' se associate NAHI the — ye Bhupendra Nath Dutt aur Barindra\n⚠️\nKumar Ghosh ne publish ki thi. Gandhi 'Indian Opinion', 'Young India' aur 'Nav Jeevan' se juday the.\n[Q56]\n12. The First Hindi & English Newspapers by Indians\n● India ka pehla Hindi newspaper 'Udant Martand' (30 May 1826) Kolkata se publish hua tha — Pt. Jugal\nKishore ne shuru ki. [Q29]\n● Indians dwara English mein publish ki gayi pehli newspaper 'Hindoo Patriot' thi (1853 mein, Girish\nChandra Ghosh ki initial editorship mein). [Q30]\n● 'Hindoo Patriot' ke editor Harish Chandra Mukherjee the, jinhone Indigo Movement ka bahut support\nkiya. [Q31]\n13. 'Vande Mataram' (English Weekly) — Aurobindo Ghosh"," ● Aurobindo Ghosh (Arbind Ghosh) English journal 'Vande Matram' se affiliated the. [Q32]\n●\n Disputed: Revolutionary paper 'Vande Mataram' ke editor Aurobindo Ghosh the (baad mein\n⚠️\nMadame Cama/Hardayal, Paris mein) — diye gaye options mein se koi bhi exactly match nahi karta,\nisliye ye question disputed hai. [Q68]\n14. Regional Papers — Patna, Kerala & the Independent\n● 'Indian Nation' newspaper Patna se publish hoti thi — Kameshwar Singh (Darbhanga) ne 1931 mein\nshuru ki. [Q33]\n● K. Ramakrishna Pillai ne Malayalam newspaper 'Swadeshabhimani' (Swadesh Vahini) edit ki. [Q34]\n● Motilal Nehru ne English newspaper 'Independent' shuru ki, complete independence ki demand karte\nhue. [Q35]\n15. Important Match Lists — Regional Newspapers & Editors\n● Match: Bharat Mitra → Hindi; Rastra Mata → Marathi; Prajamitra → Gujarati; Nayak → Bengali. [Q36]\n● Match: Dainik Aaj → Shiv Prasad Gupta; Leader → Madan Mohan Malviya; National Herald → J.L.\nNehru; Pioneer → George Allen. [Q37]\n● Match: Hindu → G. Subramaniya Iyer; Sudharak → Gokhale; Voice of India → Dadabhai Naoroji;\nBengalee → Surendra Nath Banerjee. [Q48]\n● Match: Free Hindustan → Taraknath Das; Indian Opinion → Gandhi; Voice of India → Dadabhai;\nBengalee → Surendranath. [Q49]\n● Match: Kaal → Paranjape; Bengalee → S.N. Banerjee; Sudharak → Gokhale; Somaprakash →\nDwarkanath Vidyabhushan. [Q50]\n● Match: Bombay Chronicle → Ferozshah Mehta; Common Weal → Annie Besant; Leader → Madan\nMohan Malviya; Search Light → Sachidanand Sinha. [Q51]\n● Match: Leader → Malviya; Bombay Chronicle → Firozshah Mehta; Independent → Motilal Nehru;\nJustice → T.M. Nair. [Q52]\n● Match: Abul Kalam Azad → Al-Hilal; Feroz Shah Mehta → Bombay Chronicle; Annie Besant → New\nIndia; Mahatma Gandhi → Young India. [Q53]\n● Match: Samachar Darpan → Marshman; Mirat-ul-Akhbar → Roy; Kesari → Tilak; Young India →\nGandhi. [Q60]\n● Match: Swadesh → Gorakhpur; Bharat Bandhu → Hathras; Satyawadi → Agra; Shakti → Almora. [Q62]\n● Nationalist newspapers ke editors: The Hindu → G. Subramania Iyer; Kesari → Tilak; Bengalee →\nSurendra Nath Banerjee; Hindustani → Ganga Prasad Verma; Sudharak → Gopal Krishna Gokhale.\n[Q63]\n● Match: Bipin Chandra Pal → New India; Arvind Ghosh → Vande Mataram; Brahma Bandhab Upadhyay\n→ Sandhya; Mohammad Ali → Comrade. [Q67]\n● Match: S.A. Dange → The Socialist; Muzaffar Ahmad → Navyug; Ghulam Hussain → Inqilab; M.\nSingarvelu → Labour Kisan Gazette. [Q71]"," 16. 'Pratap' — Ganesh Shankar Vidyarthi & the Bijoliya Movement\n● Vijay Singh Pathik ne Kanpur se publish hone wali newspaper 'Pratap' (Ganesh Shankar Vidyarthi ki\nedited) ke through Bijoliya movement ko subject banaya. [Q38]\n17. 'Bahishkrit Bharat' — B.R. Ambedkar\n● Marathi fortnightly 'Bahishkrit Bharat' B.R. Ambedkar (Baba Saheb) ne 1924 mein shuru ki thi. [Q42, Q43,\nQ44]\n18. 'Al-Hilal' — Abul Kalam Azad\n● 'Al-Hilal' (Urdu weekly) Abul Kalam Azad ne 1912 mein establish ki thi. [Q45, Q46]\n19. 'Vande Mataram' (Urdu Daily, Lahore) — Lala Lajpat Rai\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ne 1920 mein Lahore se Urdu daily 'Vande Mataram' shuru ki thi. [Q47]\n20. Match Corrections — Not Correctly Matched Pairs\n●\n Trap: 'Tahzeeb-ul-Akhlaq' Muhammad Ali Jinnah ne NAHI, Sir Syed Ahmed Khan ne 1870 mein\n⚠️\nshuru ki thi — galat match. [Q54]\n●\n Trap: 'Qaumi Awaz' Abul Kalam Azad ne NAHI, Jawaharlal Nehru ne shuru ki thi — galat match.\n⚠️\n[Q58]\n● Sahi match: Annie Besant — Commonweal (Mook Nayak-Ambedkar, Young India-Gandhi, Kesari-Tilak\ninn dusre pairs ke saath differentiate karo). [Q59]\n●\n Trap: 'Independent' newspaper B.R. Ambedkar ne NAHI, Motilal Nehru ne shuru ki thi — galat\n⚠️\nmatch. [Q61]\n● Sahi match: Bal Gangadhar Tilak — Kesari. [Q64]\n● Annie Besant ne 2 newspapers publish ki thi — 'Commonweal' aur 'New India'. [Q65]\n● 'Commonweal' (English weekly) Annie Besant se related thi. [Q66]\n●\n Trap: 'The Times of India' ek nationalist newspaper NAHI thi — ye generally British policies ka\n⚠️\nsupport karti thi. [Q69]\n21. 'Qaumi Awaz' — Jawaharlal Nehru"," ● Jawaharlal Nehru ne Rafi Ahmed Kidwai ke saath milkar 1945 mein Lucknow se Urdu paper 'Qaumi\nAwaz' launch ki. [Q57]\n22. 'Dash Roja' — Abdul Gaffar Khan\n● Abdul Gaffar Khan ne National Movement ke time 'Dash Roja' periodical shuru ki thi. [Q70]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Development of Press in Modern India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0212","t":"10 Socio Religious Movements","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.10 — SOCIO-RELIGIOUS MOVEMENTS — FULL MIND MAP\n🕉️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Overview — Reform Movements & Their Reach\n2. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — Epithets & Titles\n3. Atmiya Sabha & the Brahmo Samaj\n4. Keshav Chandra Sen & the Brahmo Samaj Split\n5. Ram Mohan Roy — Title, Death & Legacy\n6. Ram Mohan Roy's Reforms & Opposition\n7. Swami Vivekananda\n8. The Ramakrishna Mission\n9. Famous Quotes — Vidyasagar, Sister Nivedita & the Bethune School\n10. Arya Samaj — Swami Dayanand Saraswati\n11. Chronology of Reformers\n12. Prarthana Samaj\n13. Dev Samaj\n14. Satya Shodhak Samaj — Jyotiba Phule\n15. Orthodox Opposition — The Dharma Sabha\n16. Other Movements — Radha Swami Satsang & Paramahansa Mandali\n17. Lokahitvadi — Gopal Hari Deshmukh\n18. Widow Remarriage in Maharashtra\n19. Parsi Reform — B.M. Malabari & the Age of Consent Act\n20. M.G. Ranade & the National Social Conference\n21. Veeresalingam — The Telugu Renaissance\n22. Legal Reforms — Widow Remarriage, Marriage & Slavery Acts\n23. The Sharda Act\n24. The Theosophical Society\n25. Important Match Lists — Founders & Organizations\n26. The Justice Party\n27. The Poona Sarvajanik Sabha\n28. The Servants of India Society — Gopal Krishna Gokhale\n29. Bahujan Samaj\n30. Anti-Untouchability & Social Equality Movements\n31. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar's Movements\n32. The Sanatan Dharma Rakshini Sabha\n33. Miscellaneous Statements & Common Themes\n34. Muslim Reform Movements — Deoband, Faraizi & Nadwatul Ulama\n35. Regional Movements — Tarkeswar, the Hali System & Abhinav Bharat\n1. Overview — Reform Movements & Their Reach\n● 19th century ke religious reform movements mainly intellectuals, urban upper castes aur liberal princes\nko attract karte the — poor ordinary class largely unaffected rahi. [Q1]\n● Assertion-Reason: Reform movements modernization laayi (sahi Assertion) — kyunki unhone modern\neducation, rationalism aur scientific temper promote ki (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta\nhai). [Q2]\n● Educated Hindu middle class Western civilization se sabse pehle influenced hui thi. [Q3]\n2. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — Epithets & Titles"," ● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ko 'Father of Indian Renaissance' aur 'Father of Modern India' kaha jaata hai.\n[Q4, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n●\n Trap: 'Father of Indian Nationalism' bhi Raja Ram Mohan Roy hi mane jaate hain — lekin diye gaye\n⚠️\noptions mein unka naam na hone ki wajah se 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q5]\n● Ram Mohan Roy ko 'Prophet of Nationalism' aur India ka pehla 'Modern Man' bhi kaha jaata hai. [Q9,\nQ10]\n3. Atmiya Sabha & the Brahmo Samaj\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ne pehli society 'Atmiya Sabha' 1815 mein found ki thi — Brahmo Sabha (1828)\nse pehle. [Q11, Q12]\n●\n Trap: Brahmo Sabha (Samaj) 1828 mein found hui thi — lekin ye saal diye gaye options mein NAHI\n⚠️\ntha, isliye is question ka koi sahi option nahi hai. [Q13]\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ne 1828 mein Brahmo Samaj found ki. [Q14, Q16, Q17]\n● Brahmo Samaj Monotheism (ek God ki pooja) ke principle par based hai. [Q24]\n● Brahmo Samaj ke baare mein: unhone idolatry (murti pooja) ka virodh kiya — statements 1 aur 2 sahi\nhain, lekin statement 3 galat hai kyunki 'Vedas ki infallibility' Dayanand Saraswati (Arya Samaj) ne\npopularize ki, Brahmo Samaj ne NAHI. [Q27]\n●\n Trap: 'Atmiya Sabha' Debendra Nath Tagore ne NAHI, Raja Ram Mohan Roy ne 1815 mein banayi\n⚠️\nthi — galat match. [Q113]\n●\n Trap: 'Adi Brahmo Samaj' Raja Ram Mohan Roy se NAHI juda — unhone Brahmo Samaj (1828)\n⚠️\nbanayi, aur Adi Brahmo Samaj baad mein Devendranath Tagore ki faction bani split ke baad. [Q135]\n4. Keshav Chandra Sen & the Brahmo Samaj Split\n● Devendranath Tagore ne Keshav Chandra Sen ko Brahmo Samaj ka Chief Acharya appoint kiya tha.\n[Q15]\n● Keshav Chandra Sen ne 'Tabernacle of New Dispensation' aur 'Indian Reform Association' establish ki\n— Calcutta Unitarian Committee Ram Mohan Roy se associate thi. [Q21]\n● Keshav Chandra Sen ne 1866 mein 'Bhartiya Brahmo Samaj' (Brahmo Samaj of India) found ki. [Q22]\n● 1866 ke split ke baad, Devendranath Tagore ki faction 'Adi Brahmo Samaj' kehlaayi. [Q23]\n● Debendranath Tagore ne 1839 mein Ram Mohan Roy ke ideas promote karne ke liye 'Tattvabodhini\nSabha' establish ki. [Q29]\n5. Ram Mohan Roy — Title, Death & Legacy\n● Mughal Emperor Akbar-II ne Ram Mohan Roy ko 1830 mein 'Raja' ki title di. [Q18, Q19]\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy ki Samadhi Bristol, England mein hai — unki mrityu 1833 mein wahi hui thi. [Q20]"," 6. Ram Mohan Roy's Reforms & Opposition\n●\n Trap: Ram Mohan Roy ne 'Western education' ka protest NAHI kiya — ulta unhone iski wakalat ki.\n⚠️\nUnhone Child Marriage, Sati aur Idolatry ka protest kiya. [Q25]\n● 'Samachar Chandrika' (Bhavani Charan Bandyopadhyay ne 1822 mein shuru ki) Ram Mohan Roy ke\nreligious/social ideas ke against thi. [Q26]\n● Assertion-Reason: Ram Mohan Roy ne 'Sambad Kaumudi' launch ki (sahi Assertion) — lekin officially\nBhavanicharan Bandopadhyay hi editor the, isliye Assertion is context mein galat maana gaya, aur\nReason sahi hai. [Q28]\n●\n Trap: Ram Mohan Roy Sati system ke supporter NAHI the — wo actually iske sabse prominent\n⚠️\nOPPONENT the. [Q100]\n● Ram Mohan Roy ne 'Jury Act of 1826' ka zoradar virodh kiya — kyunki ye jury selection mein religion ke\nbasis par discriminate karta tha. [Q115]\n7. Swami Vivekananda\n● Swami Vivekananda ko 19th century ke doosre hisse mein Neo-Hinduism ka best representative maana\njaata hai. [Q30]\n● Swami Vivekananda ne 1893 mein Chicago mein 'Parliament of World's Religions' attend ki thi aur India\nko represent kiya. [Q31, Q33, Q34, Q35]\n●\n Trap: Chicago ka 'World Religion Conference' speech 1893 mein diya gaya tha — lekin ye saal diye\n⚠️\ngaye options mein NAHI tha, isliye koi option sahi nahi hai. [Q32]\n● Vivekananda ne 'Practical Vedanta' advocate ki — unhone iske baare mein pehla speech 1896 mein\nLondon mein diya. [Q36]\n● Swami Vivekananda ne 'Jnyana Yoga', 'Karma Yoga' aur 'Raja Yoga' jaisi books likhi. [Q37]\n8. The Ramakrishna Mission\n● Swami Vivekananda ne 1897 AD mein Belur (Howrah) mein 'Ramakrishna Mission' found ki. [Q38, Q39,\nQ40, Q41, Q42, Q43]\n● Sharadamani (Sharada Devi) Ramakrishna Paramhansa ki patni thi. [Q44]\n●\n Trap: Ramakrishna Mission Ramakrishna Paramhansa ne NAHI, Swami Vivekananda ne found ki\n⚠️\nthi — galat match. [Q112]\n9. Famous Quotes — Vidyasagar, Sister Nivedita & the Bethune School\n● 'Mujhe God ke baare mein sochne ka time nahi hai, kyunki is dharti par bahut saara kaam karna hai' —\nye statement Ishwarchandra Vidyasagar ne diya tha. [Q45]\n● 'British Empire core se rotten hai, corrupt hai aur tyrannical hai' — ye statement Sister Nivedita ne diya\ntha. [Q46]"," ● Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar 'Hindu Female School' (baad mein Bethune Female School) ke first\nsecretary the. [Q99]\n10. Arya Samaj — Swami Dayanand Saraswati\n● Swami Dayanand Saraswati ne April 1875 mein Mumbai mein 'Arya Samaj' found ki. [Q47, Q48, Q49]\n● Dayanand Saraswati Vedas ki revival ke liye responsible the — unhone 'Go Back to Vedas' ka slogan\ndiya. [Q50, Q51]\n● Dayanand Saraswati ko 'Martin Luther of India' kaha jaata hai. [Q52]\n● 'Satyarth Prakash' (The Light of Truth, 1875 mein likhi) Dayanand Saraswati ne likhi — ye Arya Samaj ki\nsacred book bhi hai. [Q53, Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● Arya Samaj ne 'Shuddhi movement' (converts ko wapas Hinduism mein laane ke liye) support ki. [Q58]\n● Assertion-Reason: Arya Samaj ne Hindus mein confidence establish ki aur White superiority ki notion ko\nchallenge kiya (sahi Assertion aur Reason) — lekin Reason, Assertion ka direct causal explanation\nNAHI hai. [Q59]\n● 'Good Government is no substitute for Self-Government' — ye statement Swami Dayanand ne diya tha.\n[Q60]\n● Swami Dayanand pehle the jinhone 'Swaraj' word use kiya aur Hindi ko national language ki tarah\naccept kiya. [Q61]\n● 'India for the Indians' — ye statement Dayananda Saraswati ne diya tha. [Q62]\n● Statement check: Statement 1 galat hai (Arya Samaj 1875 mein bani), statement 2 galat hai (Lajpat Rai\nArya Samaj ke supporter the) — sirf 3 aur 4 statements sahi hain. [Q94]\n11. Chronology of Reformers\n● Reformers/leaders ka chronological order: Tulsidas (16th century) → Raja Ram Mohan Roy (1772-\n1833) → Dayanand Saraswati (1824-1883) → Vivekanand (1863-1902). [Q63]\n12. Prarthana Samaj\n●\n Disputed: 'Prarthana Samaj' ke founder Atmaram Pandurang the (1867 mein) — kuch questions\n⚠️\nmein unka naam options mein na hone ki wajah se disputed maana jaata hai. [Q64]\n● Prarthana Samaj Bombay (Maharashtra) mein 1867 mein establish hui. [Q65]\n● Atmaram Panduranga (Pandurang) ne 1867 mein 'Prarthana Samaj' found ki. [Q66, Q67]\n● M.G. Ranade, Prarthana Samaj (Maharashtra) ke chief director the — unhone is movement ko\npopularize kiya. [Q68]\n13. Dev Samaj"," ● Shiv Narayan Agnihotri ne 1887 mein Lahore mein 'Dev Samaj' found ki. [Q69]\n14. Satya Shodhak Samaj — Jyotiba Phule\n● Jyotiba Phule ne 1873 mein 'Satya Shodhak Samaj' found ki — Shudras ko Brahmanical influence se\nliberate karne ke liye. [Q70, Q71, Q72, Q75, Q76, Q78, Q81]\n● Jyotiba Phule ne 1873 mein 'Gulamgiri' (Gulamiri) book likhi. [Q73, Q74]\n● Satyashodhak Samaj ka main aim tha backward classes aur Dalits ka upliftment. [Q77]\n● Satya Shodhak Samaj Maharashtra mein ek 'Anti-caste Movement' organize karti thi — Shudras ko\nBrahmanical exploitation se liberate karne ke liye. [Q79]\n● Jyotiba Phule, 'Anti-caste Movement' se associate the. [Q80]\n● Bharat mein women's movement mainly Jyotiba Phule ki inspiration se shuru hui — unhone 1848 mein\nfirst girls' school khola tha, women's education-rights ke pioneer the. [Q142]\n15. Orthodox Opposition — The Dharma Sabha\n● Radhakant Deb ne socio-religious reforms ka virodh kiya aur orthodoxy support ki — unhone 1830 mein\n'Dharma Sabha' found ki (Sati abolition jaise reforms ke against). [Q82]\n16. Other Movements — Radha Swami Satsang & Paramahansa Mandali\n● Shivdyal Sahab (Tulsi Ram) ne 1861 mein Agra mein 'Radha Swami Satsang' found ki. [Q83]\n● 'Paramahansa Mandali' Maharashtra mein establish hui thi — Dadoba Pandurang aur Mehtaji Durgaram\nne 1849 mein Bombay mein found ki. [Q148]\n17. Lokahitvadi — Gopal Hari Deshmukh\n● Maharashtra ke reformer Gopal Hari Deshmukh ko 'Lokahitvadi' ke pen name se jaana jaata hai. [Q84,\nQ85]\n18. Widow Remarriage in Maharashtra\n● Maharashtra mein widow remarriage ki campaign Vishnu Parashuram Pandit ne lead ki — unhone 1850\nmein 'Widow Remarriage Association' found ki. [Q86]\n19. Parsi Reform — B.M. Malabari & the Age of Consent Act"," ● Behramji M. Malabari, 19th century ke sabse great Parsi social reformer the — unhone Age of Consent\nAct 1891 pass karwane mein important role play kiya. [Q87]\n● 'The Age of Consent Act' 1891 mein pass hua. [Q88]\n● Age of Consent Act, 1891 ke baare mein — ek Parsi reformer (Malabari) associate the (sahi statement)\n— lekin ye galat hai ki sabhi ne is Act ko support kiya, kyunki Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne is Act ka virodh\nkiya tha. [Q89]\n● 1853 mein paida hue B.M. Malabari, Western India ke ek Parsi the — unhone child marriage ke against\ncampaign ki, jisse Age of Consent Act 1891 pass hua. [Q105]\n20. M.G. Ranade & the National Social Conference\n● Mahadev Govind Ranade ne social-religious reform ke liye legislation ka istemaal kiya — unhone 1887\nmein 'Indian National Social Conference' found ki, child marriage aur polygamy jaise issues ke liye.\n[Q90]\n●\n Trap: 'Social Reform Association' (Bombay Presidency) Shri Ram Bajpai ne NAHI, Chandavarkar-\n⚠️\nBhandarkar jaiso ne banayi thi — Shri Ram Bajpai 'Seva Samiti Boy Scouts Association' se related the.\n[Q91]\n● INC ne apni deliberations mein social reforms shaamil nahi karne ka decision liya, jisse ek alag body\n'National Social Conference' banayi gayi. [Q93]\n21. Veeresalingam — The Telugu Renaissance\n● Kandukuri Veeresalingam Pantulu ('Father of Telugu Renaissance') ne 1871 mein Rajamundry mein\nwidow remarriage encourage karne ke liye 'Social Reform Association' found ki. [Q92]\n22. Legal Reforms — Widow Remarriage, Marriage & Slavery Acts\n● 1856 mein pass hua Act — 'Hindu Widow Remarriage Act' tha (Religious Disabilities Act 1850 mein\npass hua tha; Sati Prohibition 1829 mein; Doctrine of Lapse 1848 mein). [Q95]\n● 'The Hindu Widow Remarriage Act', 26 July 1856 ko pass hua — Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar ke\nprayaso ki wajah se. [Q96]\n● D.K. Karve (Dhondo Keshav Karve) Women's Education (1916 mein pehli Women's University banayi)\nAUR Widow Remarriage — dono ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q97]\n● Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar ne prominently widow remarriage ko legal karwaya tha. [Q98]\n● 'Act V of 1843' ne Slavery ko illegal kiya — Lord Ellenborough ke reign mein. [Q101]\n● Keshav Chandra Sen ne 'Native Marriage Act of 1872' pass karwane mein important role play kiya —\nisne shaadi ki minimum age fix ki (Girls: 14, Boys: 18). [Q102]\n● 'Native Marriage Act' 1872 mein pass hua. [Q103]\n● Civil Marriage Act of 1872 ne girls ki minimum age 14 saal fix ki. [Q104]"," 23. The Sharda Act\n● 'Sharda Act' (1929, Harbilas Sharda ke naam par) ne marriageable age fix ki — girls ke liye 14 aur boys\nke liye 18 saal. [Q106]\n● 'Sharda Act' child marriage ki roktham (prevention) se related tha. [Q107]\n24. The Theosophical Society\n● Madame H.P. Blavatsky ne 1875 mein New York mein 'Theosophical Society' found ki (Col. Olcott ke\nsaath). [Q108]\n● India mein Theosophical Society ki success mainly Annie Besant ki wajah se hui — unki active\ninvolvement aur Hinduism ke liye pyaar ki wajah se. [Q109]\n●\n Trap: Mahadev Govind Ranade, Theosophical Society se NAHI, Prarthana Samaj se associate the\n⚠️\n— galat match. [Q110]\n25. Important Match Lists — Founders & Organizations\n● Match: Prarthana Samaj → Ranade; Brahmo Samaj → Ram Mohan Roy; Arya Samaj → Dayanand;\nRam Krishna Mission → Vivekananda. [Q111]\n● Match: Brahmo Samaj → Kolkata; Manav Dharma Sabha → Surat; Arya Samaj → Mumbai; Nadwah →\nLucknow. [Q114]\n● Match: Prarthana Samaj → M.G. Ranade; Ramakrishna Mission → Swami Vivekananda; Satyashodhak\nSamaj → Jyotiba Phule; MAO College → Sir Syed Ahmed Khan. [Q116]\n● Match: Brahmo Samaj → Raja Ram Mohan Roy; Ramakrishna Mission → Swami Vivekananda;\nServants of India Society → Gopal Krishna Gokhale; Vidhwa Vivah Samaj → Vishnu Shastri Pandit.\n[Q118]\n● Match: Servants of India Society → Gokhale (1905); Tattwabodhini Sabha → Debendranath Tagore\n(1839); Atmiya Sabha → Raja Ram Mohan Roy (1815). [Q127]\n● Match: Raja Ram Mohan Roy → Purest Hinduism Upanishads mein hai; Keshav Chandra Sen →\nBrahmovad world religion honi chahiye; Dayanand Saraswati → Go back to Vedas. [Q134]\n● Match: Karve → Widow Remarriage; Bethune → Girls School; Vidyasagar → Sanskrit College; Malabari\n→ Child marriage reform. [Q137]\n● Match: Prarthana Samaj → Atmaram Pandurang; Young India → Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi;\nLokahitwadi → Gopal Hari Deshmukh; Satyashodhak Samaj → Jyotiba Phule; Rehnumai Mazdayasan\nSabha → Naoroji Furdonji. [Q138]\n26. The Justice Party\n● 'Justice Party' (1916, Madras Presidency mein) ek non-Brahmin organization thi — ye lower castes-\nbackward classes ke interests represent karti thi, Congress ki Brahmin dominance ki criticism karti thi,"," aur legislatures mein communal representation ki demand karti thi (jaise Muslims ko 1909 mein mila\ntha). [Q117]\n27. The Poona Sarvajanik Sabha\n●\n Disputed: 'Poona Sarvajanik Sabha' 2 April 1870 ko G.V. Joshi, S.H. Sathe ne found ki thi (M.G.\n⚠️\nRanade 1871 mein join hue) — diye gaye options mein sahi date na hone ki wajah se 'None of the\nabove' sahi answer hai. [Q119]\n28. The Servants of India Society — Gopal Krishna Gokhale\n● Sahi match: 'The Servants of India Society' Gopal Krishna Gokhale ne banayi. [Q120]\n● M.C. Setalvad, B.N. Rao aur Alladi Krishnaswamy Iyer — teeno 'Servants of India Society' ke\ndistinguished members the. [Q121]\n● Gopal Krishna Gokhale ne 12 June 1905 ko Pune mein 'Servants of India Society' found ki — nation ki\nservice ke liye missionaries train karne ke liye. [Q122, Q123, Q124, Q125, Q126, Q128, Q129]\n● K.M. Panikkar ne Gopal Krishna Gokhale ko 'first diplomat of modern India' kaha tha. [Q130]\n29. Bahujan Samaj\n● Mukund Rao Patil aur Shankar Rao Jadhav ne, Jyotiba Phule ki ideology se influenced hokar, 'Bahujan\nSamaj' found ki — lower castes ko upper caste exploitation se bachane ke liye. [Q131]\n30. Anti-Untouchability & Social Equality Movements\n● Nadars ne 1899 mein Tirunelveli (Tamil Nadu) mein Hindu temples mein entry ka right demand kiya —\njisse ek violent communal riot hui. [Q132]\n● 'Agar God untouchability ko tolerate karte, to main unhe God hi nahi maanta' — ye statement Bal\nGangadhar Tilak ne diya tha. [Q133]\n● Statement check: Anti-Untouchability League (Gandhi ne 1932 mein banayi, baad mein Harijan Sevak\nSangh ban gayi), All India Kisan Sabha (Sahajanand Saraswati ne 1936 mein Lucknow mein banayi),\naur Self-Respect Movement (Periyar ne 1925 mein shuru ki) — sabhi 3 statements sahi hain. [Q145]\n31. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar's Movements\n●\n Trap: 'Bahishkrit Hitkarini Sabha' Jyotiba Phule ne NAHI, Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne 1924 mein banayi\n⚠️\nthi — galat match. [Q136]\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne 'Neo-Buddhism' (Navayana) advocate ki — 1956 mein ye movement shuru kiya.\n[Q146]"," 32. The Sanatan Dharma Rakshini Sabha\n● 'Sanatan Dharma Rakshini Sabha' Calcutta mein establish hui thi (1873 mein). [Q139]\n33. Miscellaneous Statements & Common Themes\n● Ram Mohan Roy, Dayanand Saraswati jaise sabhi social reformers Sanskrit language mein proficient\nthe — unhone ancient texts ka use apne social reforms justify karne ke liye kiya. [Q140]\n● Diye gaye 3 statements — in socio-religious movements ki ideologies-actions ke baare mein — sabhi\nhistorically accurate hain. [Q141]\n● Brahmo Samaj, Ram Krishna Mission aur Arya Samaj — teeno mein common tha: koi political mission\nnahi tha, lekin unhone patriotism (rashtriyata) develop ki. [Q143]\n●\n Trap: Mahatma Gandhi Gandhinagar mein NAHI, Porbandar mein paida hue the — galat statement.\n⚠️\n\n[Q144]\n34. Muslim Reform Movements — Deoband, Faraizi & Nadwatul Ulama\n● Maulana Shibli Numani, 'Dar-ul-Ulum' (Nadwatul Ulama, Lucknow) ke establishment se juday key figure\nthe. [Q147]\n● 'Deoband Movement' UP mein 1866 mein, Saharanpur mein, shuru hui thi — Islamic values revive\nkarne aur British rule ka virodh karne ke liye. [Q149]\n● Haji Shariatullah ne East Bengal mein 'Faraizi Movement' shuru ki — un-Islamic practices purge karne\nke liye. Baad mein Dudhu Mian ne movement lead ki. [Q150, Q151]\n35. Regional Movements — Tarkeswar, the Hali System & Abhinav Bharat\n● 1924 ka 'Tarkeswar Movement' (Bengal mein) Shiva temple ke corrupt Mahant (priest) ke against tha.\n[Q152]\n● 'Hali System' bonded labour (bandhua majdoori) ka ek form thi — Bardoli (Gujarat) mein prevalent thi.\n[Q153]\n● V.D. Savarkar ne apne bhai Ganesh Savarkar ke saath 'Mitra Mela' shuru ki thi — 1904 mein Nashik\nmein isse rename karke 'Abhinav Bharat Society' banaya, ek revolutionary organization. [Q154]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Socio-Religious Movements Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0213","t":"11 Political Organization Before Congress","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.11 — POLITICAL ORGANIZATION BEFORE CONGRESS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Bengal Organizations — Zamindari Association & Bengal British India Society\n2. The Poona Sarvajanik Sabha\n3. The Indian Association — Surendranath Banerjee\n4. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — The First Political Reformer\n5. Chronology & Match Lists of Pre-Congress Organizations\n6. The Madras Mahajan Sabha\n7. The Bombay Presidency Association\n8. Match List — Pre-Congress Leaders\n9. The Bristol Indian Association — Not a Political Body\n10. The East India Association — Dadabhai Naoroji\n11. The United Indian Patriotic Association\n12. Other Societies — Founding Date Corrections\n13. The Asiatic Society of Bengal\n14. The British Indian Association\n1. Early Bengal Organizations — Zamindari Association & Bengal British India\nSociety\n● India ki pehli political organization 'Zamindari Association' (Landholders Society bhi kehte the) 1838 AD\nmein Calcutta mein establish hui — Dwaraka Nath Tagore aur unke landlords associates ne founded ki,\nlandlords ke interests secure karne ke liye. [Q1]\n● Assertion-Reason: 'Bengal British Indian Society' 1843 AD mein, George Thompson ke prayaso se bani\nthi (sahi Assertion) — George Thompson iske president the, Dwarkanath Tagore ne unhe England se\nlaakar political movement organize karwaya (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q2]\n● Chronological order: Bangabhasha Prakasika Sabha (1836, Ram Mohan Roy ke associates ne banayi)\n→ Land-holders Society (1838, Dwarkanath Tagore) → Bengal British India Society (1843) → Indian\nLeague (1875, Shishir Kumar Ghose). [Q20]\n2. The Poona Sarvajanik Sabha\n● 'Poona Sarvajanik Sabha' ne 1875 mein House of Commons ko India ki direct representation ki demand\nwali petition submit ki — ye 19th century India ki sabse strong political organisations mein se ek thi, 2\nApril 1870 ko Pune mein launch hui. [Q3]\n3. The Indian Association — Surendranath Banerjee\n● Surendranath Banerjee ne, Anand Mohan Bose ke saath, 26 July 1876 ko Calcutta mein 'Indian\nAssociation' found ki — ye INC se pehle ke sabhi nationalist organisations mein sabse significant thi, aur\nlandlords ke bajaye middle class ko prefer karti thi. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● Surendra Nath Banerjee ko 1874 AD mein Indian Civil Services se ek minor judicial error ki wajah se\ndismiss kiya gaya tha — halaki unhe court judgment ke baad reappoint kiya gaya, phir dobara dismiss\nkiya gaya. [Q8, Q9]"," ● Surendranath Banerjee ne 'Indian National Conference' organize ki thi — same objectives hone ki wajah\nse ye baad mein Indian National Congress ke saath merge ho gayi. [Q10]\n4. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — The First Political Reformer\n● Raja Ram Mohan Roy pehle Indian the jinhone political reforms ke liye resist kiya — unhone human\nrights aur democratic values ke baare mein likha. Bipin Chandra Pal ke mutabik wo pehle Indian political\nreformer the (halaki kuch historians ye credit Surendra Nath Banerjee ko dete hain). [Q11]\n5. Chronology & Match Lists of Pre-Congress Organizations\n● Organizations ka sahi chronological order: Bombay Association (August 1852, Dadabhai Naoroji) →\nIndian League (September 1875, Shishir Kumar Ghosh) → Indian Association (July 1876) → (baad ki\norganisation). [Q12]\n●\n Trap: Match mein 2 pairs galat the — 'East India Association – Calcutta' galat hai (actually London\n⚠️\nmein thi), aur 'Indian Association – Bombay' galat hai (actually Kolkata mein thi). [Q16]\n● Match: Land Holders' Society → Dwarkanath Tagore; British India Society → William Adams; Indian\nSociety → Anand Mohan Bose; Indian Association → S.N. Banerji. [Q21]\n● Chronological order: East India Association (1866, Dadabhai Naoroji) → National Indian Association\n(1870/71, Mary Carpenter) → Indian Society (1872, Anand Mohan Bose) → (agli organisation). [Q22]\n● Match: India League → Shishir Kumar Ghosh (1875); Indian Association → Anand Mohan Bose aur\nSurendranath Banerjee (1876); India National Liberal Federation → Surendranath Bannerjee (baad\nmein founded); United Indian Patriotic Association → (Syed Ahmed Khan). [Q23]\n● Match: Indian Association → Surendra Nath Banerjee; Poona Sarvjanik Sabha → Mahadev Govind\nRanade; Bombay Presidency Association → Pherozeshah Mehta; Madras Mahajan Sabha → Ananda\nCharlu. [Q24]\n6. The Madras Mahajan Sabha\n●\n Disputed: 'Madras Mahajan Sabha' May 1884 mein establish hui thi — halaki kuch sources 1883 bhi\n⚠️\n\nbataate hain, isliye is question ka answer disputed maana jaata hai. [Q13]\n7. The Bombay Presidency Association\n● Pherozeshah Mehta 'Bombay Presidency Association' (1885) ke founding members mein se ek the —\nwo iske president bhi bane, aur Indians ko Western education-culture apnaane ke liye encourage kiya.\n[Q14]\n●\n Multiple Correct: 'Bombay Presidency Association' (1885 AD) Pherozeshah Mehta, K.T. Tailang aur\n⚠️\nBadruddin Tyabji — teeno ne milkar establish ki thi, isliye 'more than one option sahi hai' wala answer\nsahi hai. [Q15]"," 8. Match List — Pre-Congress Leaders\n● Match: Indian Association → Surendranath Banerjee; Madras Mahajan Sabha → M.\nVeeraraghavachariar; Bombay Presidency Association → Dadabhai Naoroji; Poona Sarvjanik Sabha →\n(respective leader). [Q17]\n9. The Bristol Indian Association — Not a Political Body\n● 'Bristol Indian Association' September 1870 mein bani thi — October 1870 mein iska naam 'The Indian\nAssociation' rakha gaya (Mary Carpenter, Keshav Chandra Sen aur Elizabeth Adelaide Manning ne\nEngland mein founded ki, women's education ke liye kaam karti thi, political organisation NAHI thi). 1871\nmein isse 'National Indian Association' naam diya gaya. [Q18]\n10. The East India Association — Dadabhai Naoroji\n● Assertion-Reason: Dadabhai Naoroji ne 1866 mein London mein 'East India Association' establish ki\n(sahi Assertion) — unhone ise India ke sawaal par British public opinion ko influence karne ke liye\nbanaya (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q19]\n11. The United Indian Patriotic Association\n● Raja Shivaprasad ne Sir Syed Ahmed Khan ke saath 1888 mein 'United Indian Patriotic Association'\nfound ki. [Q25]\n12. Other Societies — Founding Date Corrections\n●\n Trap: 'Royal Asiatic Society of Great Britain and Ireland' 1823 mein founded hui thi, 1813 mein NAHI\n⚠️\n\n— aur 'Land Holders Society of Bengal' bhi galat date se match ki gayi thi — dono pairs galat hain. [Q26]\n13. The Asiatic Society of Bengal\n● William Jones (Sir William Jones) ne 1784 AD mein Calcutta mein 'Asiatic Society of Bengal' establish ki\n— 15 January 1784 ko, Oriental studies ko encourage karne ke liye. [Q27, Q28]\n14. The British Indian Association\n● 'British Indian Association' 1851 mein Calcutta mein establish hui — founder members mein Rajendralal\nMitra, Radhakant Dev (pehle president), Devendranath Tagore, Harish Chandra Mukherjee shaamil the.\n[Q29]"," ● Match: British Indian Association (1851) → Radhakant Dev (President) ke saath Rajendralal Mitra\nwaghera; Bombay Presidency Association (1885) → K.T. Telang, Pherozeshah Mehta, Badruddin\nTyabji; Central Mohammadan National Association → (respective founder). [Q30]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Political Organization Before Congress Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0214","t":"12 Indian National Congress","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.12 — INDIAN NATIONAL CONGRESS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Founding of the INC — A.O. Hume & the First Session\n2. The First President — W.C. Banerjee\n3. Attendance at the Founding Session\n4. The Second & Third Sessions — Naoroji & Muslim Delegates\n5. Muslim Presidents of the INC\n6. The First European President — George Yule\n7. Leaders NOT/NEVER Presidents of the INC\n8. Annie Besant — The First Woman President\n9. Sarojini Naidu — The First Indian Woman President\n10. Statements & Presidents — Ambika Charan Majumdar\n11. The Bankipur Session & A.O. Hume's Legacy\n12. Tilak's 'Swaraj is my Birthright' — The Lucknow Session (1916)\n13. Critics of the INC — Lajpat Rai & Lord Curzon\n14. Subhash Chandra Bose — The Haripura Session & Roman Script\n15. Gandhi's Suggestion to Wind Up the Congress\n16. Drafting the Congress Constitution\n17. A Governor-General at a Congress Session\n18. The Nagpur Session — 1920\n19. The Gaya Session — Chittaranjan Das\n20. The All India Harijan Sevak Sangh\n21. Chronology of Congress Presidents\n22. Match Lists — Sessions, Presidents & Places\n23. Nehru's Socialism Speech — The Lucknow Session (1936)\n24. Abul Kalam Azad — Youngest & Longest-Serving President\n25. President at Independence — J.B. Kripalani\n26. The National Anthem — First Sung at an INC Session\n27. Tilak's Last Congress Session\n1. Founding of the INC — A.O. Hume & the First Session\n● Allan Octavian Hume (A.O. Hume, retired ICS officer) ne Indian National Congress found ki — 1884\nmein 'Indian National Union' establish ki, phir Kolkata-Mumbai-Madras visit karke poori INC organize ki.\n[Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Indian National Congress ki sthapna 1885 AD mein hui — pehla session 28-30 December 1885 ko,\nBombay ke Gokuldas Tejpal Sanskrit College mein, 72 delegates ke saath hua. [Q4, Q5, Q6]\n● A.O. Hume 1885 mein Indian National Congress ke General Secretary the — unhone hi INC organize\nki, W.C. Banerjee pehle session ke President the. [Q15]\n● INC ki sthapna Viceroy Lord Dufferin (1884-1888 AD) ke reign mein hui — unhone Congress ko sirf ek\n'microscopic minority' represent karne wali sanstha bataya tha. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n2. The First President — W.C. Banerjee\n● W.C. Banerjee (Womesh Chandra Banerjee) Indian National Congress ke pehle President the (1885\nmein). [Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● Statement check: INC 1885 mein bani thi, aur W.C. Banerjee iske pehle President the — dono\nstatements sahi hain. [Q12]"," ●\n Trap: 'Educated class ke consent se social issues par viewpoint express karna' INC ke declared\n⚠️\nobjectives mein SHAAMIL NAHI tha — W.C. Banerjee ke 1885 objectives the: Indians ke beech\ncontacts-friendship badhana, aur national unity ko encourage karna. [Q13]\n●\n Trap: 'Executive aur Judiciary ka unification' Congress ki demand NAHI thi — ulta unhone dono ko\n⚠️\nALAG (separate) karne ki demand ki thi, National Movement ke first stage mein. [Q14]\n3. Attendance at the Founding Session\n●\n Trap: Surendranath Banerjee, INC ke founding session mein PRESENT NAHI the — wo us waqt\n⚠️\napni Indian National Conference (1883) mein busy the, jo Congress se alag thi. Baad mein wo bhi INC\nse juday. [Q21]\n4. The Second & Third Sessions — Naoroji & Muslim Delegates\n● Indian National Congress ka doosra session Calcutta mein, 1886 mein, Dadabhai Naoroji ki presidency\nmein hua. [Q22]\n● INC ke doosre convention mein 33 Muslim delegates participate hue the — pehle convention mein sirf 2\nthe, teesre mein 81, aur chauthe mein 221. [Q23]\n● July 1889 mein London mein 'British Committee of Indian National Congress' banayi gayi, Sir W.\nWedderburn ki presidency mein — Congress ke liye British support hasil karne ke liye. [Q24]\n5. Muslim Presidents of the INC\n● Badruddin Tyabji, INC ke pehle Muslim President the — 1887 mein, teesre session (Madras) mein elect\nhue. [Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Rahimtulla Mahomed Sayani, INC ke doosre Muslim President the — 1896 ke Calcutta session mein.\n[Q28]\n● Statement check: Annie Besant, INC ki pehli woman President thi (1917, Calcutta) — Sarojini Naidu\npehli Indian woman President thi (galat statement 1). Badruddin Tyabji 1887 mein, Madras session ke\nliye, INC ke pehle Muslim President elect hue (sahi statement 2). [Q29]\n6. The First European President — George Yule\n● George Yule, INC ke President elect hone wale pehle European the — unhone 1888 mein, 4th session\nmein, presidency ki. [Q30]\n7. Leaders NOT/NEVER Presidents of the INC\n●\n Trap: Sir Syed Ahmad Khan kabhi bhi Indian National Congress se juday NAHI the — wo British ke\n⚠️\nloyal the, unhone 'United Indian Patriotic Association' banayi thi, Raja Shiv Prasad Singh ke saath. [Q31]"," ●\n Trap: Bal Gangadhar Tilak kabhi INC ke President NAHI bane — halaki Lala Lajpat Rai (1920,\n⚠️\nCalcutta special session), Annie Besant (1917), aur Motilal Nehru (1919, 1928) sabhi INC President\nbane. [Q32, Q34]\n● 'Lal-Bal-Pal' trio mein se sirf Lala Lajpat Rai hi INC President bane (1920, special session, Calcutta) —\nBal Gangadhar Tilak kabhi nahi bane. [Q35]\n8. Annie Besant — The First Woman President\n● Annie Besant, INC ki pehli woman President thi — Calcutta session, 1917 mein. [Q33, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q39,\nQ40, Q41]\n● Statement check: pehli lady President Annie Besant thi, Sarojini Naidu NAHI (galat statement 1) — A.O.\nHume founder the lekin kabhi President elect NAHI hue, George Yule pehle European President the —\nC.R. Das ne 1922 Gaya session preside ki. [Q52]\n9. Sarojini Naidu — The First Indian Woman President\n● Sarojini Naidu, INC ki pehli Indian woman President thi — 40th annual session, Kanpur, 1925 mein.\nBaad mein wo 1947-49 tak UP ki Governor bhi bani. [Q42, Q43]\n10. Statements & Presidents — Ambika Charan Majumdar\n● Statement check: statement 1 galat hai (pehla session Calcutta mein nahi, Bombay mein hua tha) —\nstatements 2 aur 3 sahi hain. Ambika Charan Mazumdar, Lucknow Session (1916) ke President the.\n[Q44]\n11. The Bankipur Session & A.O. Hume's Legacy\n● 1912 mein, INC ka 27th session Bankipore (Patna) mein, R.N. Mudholkar ki presidency mein hua — isi\nsession mein A.O. Hume ko INC ka 'Father' kaha gaya. [Q45, Q46]\n12. Tilak's 'Swaraj is my Birthright' — The Lucknow Session (1916)\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne 1916 ke Lucknow Session mein famous statement diya: 'Swaraj is my birthright,\nI shall have it' — isi session mein Extremists Congress mein wapas aaye aur 'Lucknow Pact' Tilak-\nJinnah ke prayaso se sign hua. [Q47, Q48, Q49, Q50, Q51]\n13. Critics of the INC — Lajpat Rai & Lord Curzon\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ne likha ki 'Congress movement na to logo se inspired thi, na hi unhone plan ki thi.'\n[Q53]"," ● Lala Lajpat Rai (extremist leader) ne 'Young India' mein 'Safety Valve Theory' propound ki — unhone\nCongress ko Lord Dufferin ka brainchild maana, jo British government ko threats se bachane ke liye\ncreate kiya gaya tha. [Q54]\n● Lord Curzon ne 1900 AD mein declare kiya: 'Congress apne patan ki taraf badh raha hai, aur India mein\nrehte hue mera ek bada mahatvakanksha hai ki main isse ek shaanti-poorna maut dilaane mein madad\nkarun.' [Q55]\n14. Subhash Chandra Bose — The Haripura Session & Roman Script\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne apne 1938 Presidential address mein Hindi bhasha ke liye Roman script\nintroduce karne ki wakalat ki — wo Haripura session (Gujarat) ke President the. [Q56]\n● Haripura Session (1938), Gujarat mein, Subhash Chandra Bose ki presidency mein hua — 19-21\nFebruary 1938, INC ka 51st session tha. Isi session mein National Planning Committee bani, jiske\nJawaharlal Nehru President bane. [Q74, Q75]\n15. Gandhi's Suggestion to Wind Up the Congress\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne India ki azaadi ke baad Indian National Congress ko band karne (wind up) ki\nsuggestion di thi. [Q57]\n16. Drafting the Congress Constitution\n● Gandhi ji Congress ki nayi Constitution likhne mein B.G. Tilak aur C.R. Das ki madad chahte the —\nlekin wo busy the, isliye unke juniors N.C. Kelkar aur I.B. Sen ne unki jagah li aur Gandhi ki madad ki.\n[Q58]\n17. A Governor-General at a Congress Session\n● Lord Wellington ne 1915 mein Bombay session (INC) mein participate kiya tha — us waqt wo India ke\nGovernor-General NAHI the (unka tenure 1931-1936 mein Governor-Viceroy ki tarah tha). [Q59]\n18. The Nagpur Session — 1920\n● C. Vijay Raghav Chariar ne 1920 mein Nagpur session mein INC ki presidency ki — isi session mein\nGandhi ji ki 'Swaraj through Non-cooperation' advocacy debate aur accept hui. [Q60]\n● 1920 ke Nagpur session mein, Congress ne Princely States ke logo ke liye full responsible government\nki demand karte hue apni policy declare ki. [Q61]\n● Statement check: Nagpur session (1920) mein, linguistic basis par Provincial Congress Committees\nbanane ki approval mili (sahi) — lekin 1948 AD mein, independence ke baad, language ke basis par\nprovinces reorganize karne ki demand Congress ne reject kar di (sahi). [Q62]"," 19. The Gaya Session — Chittaranjan Das\n● Chittaranjan Das (Deshbandhu), 1922 ke Gaya Session ke President the — wo Alipore Bomb Case\nmein famous lawyer the, aur unhone Motilal Nehru ke saath Swaraj Party (INC ke andar) banayi. [Q63,\nQ64, Q65]\n20. The All India Harijan Sevak Sangh\n● M.K. Gandhi ne 1932 mein 'All India Harijan Sevak Sangh' establish ki. [Q66]\n21. Chronology of Congress Presidents\n● INC Presidents ka chronological order: Mahatma Gandhi (Belgaum, 1924, ekmatra baar preside ki) →\nVallabh Bhai Patel (Karachi, 1931) → Sarojini Naidu (Kanpur, 1925) → Jawaharlal Nehru (Lahore,\n1929). [Q67]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne apni zindagi mein sirf ek baar INC session preside ki — Belgaon (Belgaum)\nsession, 1924 mein. [Q68, Q69, Q70]\n22. Match Lists — Sessions, Presidents & Places\n● Match: Motilal Nehru → Amritsar (1919); Sarojini Naidu → Kanpur (1925); Dr. Rajendra Prasad →\nBombay (1934); Abul Kalam Azad → Ramgarh (1940). [Q71]\n● UP mein hue INC sessions match: Meerut → 1946 AD; Kanpur → 1925 AD; Lucknow → 1916 AD;\nBanaras → 1905 AD. [Q72]\n● Match: Haripura → Subhash Chandra Bose (1938); Nasik → Purushottam Das Tandon (1950); Madras\n→ Dr. M.A. Ansari; Kanpur (1925) → Sarojini Naidu. [Q77]\n23. Nehru's Socialism Speech — The Lucknow Session (1936)\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne apne Presidential address mein, INC ke Lucknow session (1936 AD) mein,\nsocialism ko India ki problems ke solution ki key bataya. [Q73]\n24. Abul Kalam Azad — Youngest & Longest-Serving President\n● Maulana Abul Kalam Azad (1888-1958) INC ke sabse young President the — unhe 1923 mein Delhi\nspecial session mein banaya gaya. Baad mein wo 1940-1946 tak, Quit India Movement ke dauran,\nlagataar 6 saal ke liye President rahe (independence se pehle ke sabse zyada samay tak President\nrehne wale — independence ke baad Sonia Gandhi ne ye record 1998-2017 aur 2019-2022 mein\nbanaya). [Q76, Q78]"," 25. President at Independence — J.B. Kripalani\n● J.B. Kripalani (Acharya Jivatram Bhagwandas Kripalani), India ki azaadi/partition ke waqt INC ke\nPresident the — November 1946 mein Meerut session mein elect hue. [Q79, Q80]\n26. The National Anthem — First Sung at an INC Session\n● 'Jana Gana Mana' (Rabindranath Tagore ne compose ki, Brahmo hymn) pehli baar 1911 ke Calcutta\nINC session mein gaya gaya tha. [Q81]\n27. Tilak's Last Congress Session\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak dwara attend ki gayi aakhri INC session Amritsar Session (1919) thi — unhone\nGandhi ki legislative council elections boycott karne ki policy ka virodh kiya, aur 'responsive cooperation'\nki policy suggest ki. Unki mrityu 1 August 1920 ko hui. [Q82]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Indian National Congress Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0215","t":"13 Moderates and Extremists in Congress","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.13 — MODERATES & EXTREMISTS IN CONGRESS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. International Events Influencing the National Movement\n2. The Moderate Phase — Ideology & Methods\n3. The Surat Split — The Swadeshi Movement\n4. Social Background of Moderate Leaders\n5. Dadabhai Naoroji & the Demand for Self-Rule\n6. G.K. Gokhale — Not an Extremist\n7. Criticism of Congress — Tilak & B.C. Pal\n8. Bipin Chandra Pal\n9. The Rise of Extremism After 1906\n10. Lala Lajpat Rai — 'Sher-e-Punjab'\n11. Leaders NOT Among the Moderates — Tilak\n12. The Swadeshi Movement — Aurobindo Ghosh\n13. Tilak — 'Father of Indian Unrest'\n14. Tilak's Imprisonment & the 'Lokmanya' Title\n15. Indian Muslims & the Extremist Movement\n16. Tilak's Nationalism — An Assertion-Reason Check\n17. The Ganapati & Shivaji Festivals\n18. Tilak's Funeral\n1. International Events Influencing the National Movement\n● Italian-Abyssinian War, China ka Boxer Movement (1899-1901), Russia par Japan ki jeet, aur Ireland ka\nRevolutionary Movement — sabhi events ne India ke national movement ko influence kiya. Inme se\nJapan ki 1905 mein Russia par jeet ka sabse zyada impact tha — isne 'white race invincible hai' wali\ngalat dharna ko todd diya. [Q1]\n2. The Moderate Phase — Ideology & Methods\n● Moderate Phase (1885-1905) mein Europe ki rich democratic-scientific culture ka support tha —\nmoderate leaders constitutional reforms, political participation aur expansion ki wakalat karte the. [Q2]\n● Moderate leaders 'constitutional agitation' mein bahut vishwas rakhte the — annual conferences,\nspeeches, aur British sense of justice ko appeal karna unka main tareeka tha. Extremists British\nParliament ki benevolence mein believe nahi karte the, passive resistance mein believe karte the. [Q3]\n● Extremist ideology ka core tha: petitions/constitutional ways ki jagah aggressive means se self-\ngovernment hasil karna — extremists ke liye independence ka matlab 'Complete Independence' tha,\njabki moderates ke liye colonial rule ke under self-governance tha. [Q34]\n3. The Surat Split — The Swadeshi Movement\n● 'Swadeshi Movement' ki wajah se Congress mein 'Surat Split' (1907 AD) hua — party 'Moderates' aur\n'Extremists' — 2 groups mein baat gayi. [Q4]"," 4. Social Background of Moderate Leaders\n● Zyadatar moderate leaders (Dadabhai Naoroji, Pherozeshah Mehta, Dinshaw Wacha, W.C. Banerjee,\nSurendranath Banerjee) urban areas se the — barristers, doctors, engineers, journalists jaise\nprosperous middle-class scholars ka dominance tha, common logo se koi seedha connection nahi tha.\n[Q5]\n5. Dadabhai Naoroji & the Demand for Self-Rule\n● 1904 AD mein, Dadabhai Naoroji ne sabse pehle International Socialist Congress mein India ke liye\n'Swaraj' (Self Rule) demand ki — unhone continuously self-rule ki grant par emphasis diya, aur 1906 ke\nINC session mein bhi apne presidential address mein Swaraj demand ki. [Q6]\n6. G.K. Gokhale — Not an Extremist\n●\n Trap: Gopal Krishna Gokhale extremist NAHI the — wo underprivileged logo ki relief ke liye\n⚠️\norganization (Servants of India Society) banane wale ek prominent social reformer the, aur moderate\nnationalists ki leadership karte the, constitutional-gradual reform ki wakalat karte the. [Q7, Q8, Q9]\n7. Criticism of Congress — Tilak & B.C. Pal\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne Indian National Congress par 'politics of prayer, petition and protest' practice\nkarne ka ilzaam lagaya — unhone moderates ki constitutional methods par vishwas rakhne ki criticism\nki. [Q10, Q11]\n● Congress ki 'prayer and petition' wali policy Bal Gangadhar Tilak ke leadership ke under khatam hui —\nwo British Empire ke sabse mazboot opponent the, aur Lala Lajpat Rai (Punjab) aur Bipin Chandra Pal\n(Calcutta) unke staunch followers ban gaye. [Q12]\n● Bipin Chandra Pal ne Indian National Congress ko 'Begging Institute' kaha tha. [Q13]\n8. Bipin Chandra Pal\n● Bipin Chandra Pal, Brahmo Samaj se associate the aur ek social reformer the — unhone 1901 mein\nweekly magazine 'New India' publish ki. [Q14]\n9. The Rise of Extremism After 1906\n● 1906 AD ke baad se Indian National Movement extremists ke dominance mein aa gaya — Surat mein\nCongress split December 1907 mein hua, jab revolutionary terrorism ne momentum pakad liya tha.\nImportant extremist leaders the: Lala Lajpat Rai, Bal Gangadhar Tilak, Bipin Chandra Pal aur Aurobindo\nGhosh. [Q15, Q17]"," ● Aurobindo Ghosh, Congress ke Extremist wing se the — wo 'Lal, Bal, Pal, Ghosh' ke 4 pillars mein se\nek the. Unhe 1908 mein Maniktalla garden raid mein British Police ne arrest kiya, evidence ki kami ki\nwajah se release hue, aur baad mein Pondicherry chale gaye, sage bankar. [Q16]\n●\n Trap: Bal Gangadhar Tilak, National Movement mein 'Moderate' ke roop mein NAHI jaane jaate the\n⚠️\n— wo Extremist the. [Q18]\n10. Lala Lajpat Rai — 'Sher-e-Punjab'\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ko 'Sher-e-Punjab' (Punjab Kesari) kaha jaata tha — wo Congress mein Punjab ke\nextremist representative the. 'Lal-Bal-Pal' trio unhi, Bal Gangadhar Tilak aur Bipin Chandra Pal se milkar\nbana tha. [Q19]\n●\n Trap: Lala Lajpat Rai Indian National Congress ke Moderates se associate NAHI the — wo\n⚠️\nExtremist the. [Q20]\n● Lala Lajpat Rai, Italian revolutionary Mazzini ko apna political guru maante the — unki biography\npadhkar unse inspire hue, baad mein unki 'The Duty of Man' rachna ko Urdu mein translate bhi kiya.\n[Q21]\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ('Punjab Kesari' bhi kehlaate the) ne Mazzini, Garibaldi, Shivaji aur Shrikrishna ki\nbiographies likhi — 1907 ke exile ke dauran kuch samay America mein bhi rahe, First World War ke\ntime wapas aaye. [Q22]\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ne Congress Conference ko 'Annual National Festival of Educated Indians' kaha tha.\n[Q23]\n11. Leaders NOT Among the Moderates — Tilak\n●\n Trap: Bal Gangadhar Tilak 'moderate' NAHI the — 'Lal, Bal, Pal' ka Neo-Nationalist group initial\n⚠️\nmoderate policies se disillusioned tha, aur Tilak is neo-ideology (extremism) ke pioneer the. [Q24]\n12. The Swadeshi Movement — Aurobindo Ghosh\n● Aurobindo Ghosh, 'Swadeshi Movement' (1905 mein, Bengal partition ke against shuru hui) ke main\nleader the — Lala Lajpat Rai (Punjab), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (Maharashtra) aur Bipin Chandra Pal\n(Bengal) bhi is movement ke doosre main leaders the. [Q25]\n13. Tilak — 'Father of Indian Unrest'\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak, service aur sacrifice mein vishwas rakhte the — British Empire ko challenge karne\nki himmat dikhaayi, jisse INC 'British policies ki criticism karne wali party' ban gayi (petition-based party\nse hatkar). [Q26]\n● British journalist Valentine Chirol (V. Chirol) ne Bal Gangadhar Tilak ko 'Father of Indian Unrest' kaha\ntha. [Q27, Q28, Q29]"," 14. Tilak's Imprisonment & the 'Lokmanya' Title\n● Tilak ki sentence ke baad, Max Muller (German Sanskrit scholar) ne unke liye mercy plead ki thi —\n'Sanskrit ke ek bade scholar hone ki wajah se main Tilak mein interested hoon' kehkar. [Q30]\n●\n Multiple Correct: Bal Gangadhar Tilak 'Lokmanya' kab bane, iske liye kai incidents responsible the\n⚠️\n— Rand-Ayerst murder case mein unhe accused banaya gaya, 18 mahine ki rigorous imprisonment hui,\naur jail se bahar aane par wo ek national hero ban chuke the. [Q31]\n● 1908 mein, Bal Gangadhar Tilak ko 6 saal ki jail punishment mili — unhe Burma deport karke Mandalay\nJail mein rakha gaya. [Q32, Q33]\n15. Indian Muslims & the Extremist Movement\n● Indian Muslims generally extremist movement se attract nahi hue kyunki extremists ki policy Hindu part\npar zyada zor deti thi — Aurobindo Ghosh ne kaha tha ki 'Independence hamari life ka purpose hai, aur\nsirf Hindu religion hi is objective ko fulfil karega.' [Q35]\n16. Tilak's Nationalism — An Assertion-Reason Check\n● Assertion-Reason: Tilak 'communalist' the — ye Assertion GALAT hai (wo asal mein ek staunch\nnationalist the jinhone 'Swaraj' ko har Indian ka birthright bataya, logo se close contact banaya). Reason\n(unhone religion ko political tool ki tarah use kiya) sahi hai — festivals ke through logo tak pahunchne ke\nliye. [Q36]\n17. The Ganapati & Shivaji Festivals\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne Maharashtra ke traditional 'Ganapati' (Ganeshotsav) festival ko ek national\nfestival mein transform kiya — unhone Ganapati Parva aur Shivaji Mahotsava dono shuru kiye, logo tak\nnationalist message pahunchane ke liye. [Q37, Q38, Q39]\n18. Tilak's Funeral\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ki mrityu 1 August 1920 ko hui — Mahatma Gandhi ke saath, Shaukat Ali aur Dr.\nSaifuddin Kichalu ne unki bier (arthi) uthayi thi, aur Maulana Hasrat Mohani ne unke liye elegy padhi.\n[Q40]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Moderates and Extremists in Congress Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0216","t":"14 Revolutionary Movements in India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.14 — REVOLUTIONARY MOVEMENTS IN INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n🔫\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Abhinav Bharat & V.D. Savarkar\n2. The Founding of the RSS\n3. The Yugantar Party\n4. Anushilan Samiti\n5. Tilak & the Title 'Lokmanya' — Revolutionary Origins\n6. The Barrah Dacoity\n7. The Muzaffarpur Bombing — Khudiram Bose\n8. The Alipore Case — Aurobindo Ghosh\n9. The Hindustan Republican Association (HRA)\n10. Ramprasad Bismil & 'Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna'\n11. The Kakori Conspiracy Case\n12. The Kanpur Conspiracy Case (1924)\n13. A Song Sung During Imprisonment — Wazid Ali Shah\n14. The Hindustan Socialist Republican Army (HSRA)\n15. The Central Assembly Bomb\n16. Chandrashekhar Azad's Martyrdom\n17. The 'Inquilab Zindabad' Slogan\n18. Bhagat Singh, Rajguru & Sukhdev — The Lahore Conspiracy\n19. Ashfaqullah Khan\n20. Chronology of Conspiracy Cases\n21. The Nasik Conspiracy Case\n22. Important Match Lists — Conspiracy Cases & Leaders\n23. The Kanpur Bolshevik Conspiracy Case\n24. The Chittagong Armoury Raid — Surya Sen\n25. The Youngest Martyr — Khudiram Bose\n26. Jatin Das — Death by Hunger Strike\n27. The Kakori Case Defence Committee\n28. The Naujawan Bharat Sabha\n29. Overview of Revolutionary Organizations\n30. Passive Resistance — Aurobindo Ghosh\n31. Gorakhpur Jail Hangings\n32. Attempted Assassination of Charles Tegart\n33. Bina Das\n34. Bhagat Singh's Philosophy\n35. Tilak's 'Lathi Club'\n1. Abhinav Bharat & V.D. Savarkar\n● V.D. Savarkar ne 'Mitra Mela' banayi thi jo baad mein 1904 mein Nasik (Maharashtra) mein 'Abhinav\nBharat Society' mein merge ho gayi. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● V.D. Savarkar ne 1906 mein London mein, India House mein, Abhinav Bharat Society ki ek branch\nestablish ki. [Q8]\n● V.D. Savarkar ke baare mein sabhi statements sahi hain: unhone Abhinav Bharat found ki, Mazzini ki\nbiography likhi, 'The Indian War of Independence 1857' likhi, aur ek baar British captivity se bachne ke\nliye ship se samundar mein kood gaye the. [Q9]\n2. The Founding of the RSS"," ● Keshav Baliram Hedgewar ne 27 September 1925 ko Nagpur mein RSS (Rashtriya Swayamsevak\nSangh) found ki. [Q10]\n3. The Yugantar Party\n● 'Yugantar Party' ki leadership Jatindranath Mukherjee ('Bagha Jatin', 1879-1915) ne ki. [Q11]\n4. Anushilan Samiti\n● Anushilan Samiti 1902 mein Midnapur mein Gyanendra Nath Basu ne found ki thi — Pramath Nath\nMitra (P. Mitra) ne Calcutta branch found ki. [Q12]\n● Sachindra Nath Sanyal ne 1913 mein Patna mein Anushilan Samiti ki ek branch establish ki. [Q13, Q14]\n● Barindra Ghosh (Aurobindo Ghosh ke chhote bhai) ki activities ne 'Anushilan Samiti' ke formation ko\njanam diya. [Q15, Q16, Q18]\n● 'Anushilan Samiti' ek revolutionary organization thi. [Q17]\n5. Tilak & the Title 'Lokmanya' — Revolutionary Origins\n● 1897 mein Chapekar brothers ne Rand ko maara, jiske baad Tilak ko sedition ke liye arrest kiya gaya —\n18 mahine ki imprisonment ne unhe national hero bana diya, aur janta ne unhe 'Lokmanya' ki title di.\n[Q19]\n6. The Barrah Dacoity\n● 'Barrah Dacoity', East Bengal mein revolutionary terrorists ka pehla bada venture tha — Pulin Behari\nDas ne 1908 mein Dhaka district mein isse conduct kiya. [Q20]\n7. The Muzaffarpur Bombing — Khudiram Bose\n● Khudiram Bose aur Prafulla Chaki ne 30 April 1908 ko Muzaffarpur mein Kingsford ki hatya ki koshish ki\n— carriage par bomb phenka lekin Mrs. aur Miss Kennedy maare gaye. Prafulla ne khudkushi ki,\nKhudiram ko hang kiya gaya. [Q21, Q22, Q23]\n8. The Alipore Case — Aurobindo Ghosh\n● Alipore Conspiracy Case (1908) mein 39 log (Aurobindo Ghosh samet) arrest hue — Chittaranjan Das\nne successfully unka defense karke Aurobindo ko release karwaya. [Q24]"," 9. The Hindustan Republican Association (HRA)\n● 'Hindustan Republican Association' October 1924 mein Kanpur mein, Sachindranath Sanyal ki\nleadership mein, Bismil-Chatterjee-Azad jaiso ke saath banayi gayi. [Q25, Q26]\n●\n Trap: Shiv Verma HRA ke member NAHI the — wo iske renewed form 'HSRA' mein join hue the.\n⚠️\n[Q27]\n10. Ramprasad Bismil & 'Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna'\n● Ramprasad Bismil ne apni execution se pehle doodh peene se mana kar diya, kehte hue 'ab main sirf\napni maa ka doodh piyunga' — Kakori Conspiracy ke liye unhe death sentence mili thi. [Q28]\n●\n Trap: 'Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna Ab Hamare Dil Mein Hai' actually Bismil Azimabadi (Saiyad Shah\n⚠️\nMuhammad Hasan) ne likhi thi, Ram Prasad Bismil ne NAHI — 1922 mein 'Sabah' Magazine mein\npublish hui. [Q29, Q30]\n11. The Kakori Conspiracy Case\n● Kakori Conspiracy Case mein Ram Prasad Bismil, Ashfaqullah, Roshan Singh aur Rajendra Lahiri ko\nhang kiya gaya — Chandra Shekhar Azad hi ekmatra escape hue. [Q31, Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Kakori Conspiracy Case 9 August 1925 ko, Lucknow ke pass Kakori mein hua. [Q32]\n●\n Trap: Surya Sen aur Bhagat Singh — dono Kakori incident se associate NAHI the.\n⚠️\n[Q36, Q37]\n● Kakori Case mein Government advocate Jagat Narain Mulla the — court ne unhe public prosecutor\nappoint kiya. [Q38]\n12. The Kanpur Conspiracy Case (1924)\n●\n Trap: M.A. Ansari, 1924 ke Kanpur Conspiracy Case se associate NAHI the.\n⚠️\n[Q39]\n13. A Song Sung During Imprisonment — Wazid Ali Shah\n● 'Daro-deewar pe hasrat ki nazar karte hain...' — ye lines Awadh ke aakhri Nawab, Wazid Ali Shah ne\nlikhi thi. Imprisonment ke dauran revolutionaries ise gaya karte the. [Q40]\n14. The Hindustan Socialist Republican Army (HSRA)\n● 'HSRA' September 1928 mein, Feroz Shah Kotla (New Delhi) mein, Chandra Shekhar Azad ki\nleadership mein establish hui. [Q41, Q44, Q47, Q48]\n● Bhagat Singh, 'Hindustan Socialist Republican Army' ke ek founder leaders mein se the — unhone HRA\nko 1928 mein HSRA mein reorganize kiya. [Q46, Q84, Q92]"," ●\n Trap: 'Hindustan Socialist Democratic Union' history mein aisi koi organization exist NAHI karti thi —\n⚠️\n\nUPPSC ne related organisations ke founders ke basis par ek option ko galti se sahi maan liya tha. [Q49]\n15. The Central Assembly Bomb\n● 8 April 1929 ko, Bhagat Singh aur Batukeshwar Dutt ne Central Legislative Assembly mein bomb\nphenka — dono ne 'harmless' bombs use kiye the, kisi ko nuksaan pahunchane ke liye nahi. [Q42, Q43,\nQ45]\n16. Chandrashekhar Azad's Martyrdom\n● 27 February 1931 ko, police ne Chandrasekhar Azad ko Allahabad (Prayagraj) ke Alfred Park (ab\nChandra Shekhar Azad Park) mein ghera — wo gunfight mein martyr ho gaye. [Q50]\n17. The 'Inquilab Zindabad' Slogan\n● 'Inquilab Zindabad' slogan Maulavi Hasrat Mohani ne likha tha — Bhagat Singh ne isse sabse pehle use\nkarke freedom fighters ke beech popular banaya. [Q51, Q52, Q53]\n18. Bhagat Singh, Rajguru & Sukhdev — The Lahore Conspiracy\n● Bhagat Singh (September 1907 mein paida hue) April 1929 mein assembly mein bomb phenkte waqt 21\nsaal se thodi zyada age ke the — unhe 23 March 1931 ko hang kiya gaya. [Q54]\n● Bhagat Singh, Rajguru aur Sukhdev — teeno ko 23 March 1931 ko, Lahore Conspiracy Case mein,\nexecute kiya gaya. [Q55, Q58, Q59, Q60]\n● Bhagat Singh ka memorial Ferozpur mein hai — Sutlej river ke kinare unka funeral hua tha. [Q56]\n●\n Trap: Batukeshwar Dutt Lahore Conspiracy mein hang NAHI hue the — unhe Cellular Jail\n⚠️\n(Andaman) bheja gaya, Kala-Pani ki saza. [Q57]\n19. Ashfaqullah Khan\n● Ashfaqullah Khan, Indian freedom ke liye hang hone wale pehle recorded Muslim the — 19 December\n1927 ko, 27 saal ki age mein, Faizabad (Ayodhya) Jail mein. [Q61]\n20. Chronology of Conspiracy Cases\n● Conspiracy cases ka chronological order: Lahore Case (1916) → Kanpur (1924) → Kakori (1925) →\nMeerut (1929). [Q62]\n●\n Trap: 'Kakori Conspiracy Case – 1924' galat hai — ye actually 1925 mein hui thi.\n⚠️\n[Q63]"," 21. The Nasik Conspiracy Case\n●\n Trap: 'Nasik Conspiracy Case' Ras Bihari Bose se NAHI, Anant Lakshman Kanhare se associate hai\n⚠️\n\n— jinhone 21 December 1909 ko district Collector Jackson ko goli maar di thi. Ras Bihari Bose 'Delhi\nConspiracy Case' se juday the. [Q64]\n22. Important Match Lists — Conspiracy Cases & Leaders\n● Match: Howrah Conspiracy Case → Jatindranath Mukherjee; Lahore Conspiracy Case → Rajguru; Delhi\nConspiracy Case → Master Amir Chand; Alipore Conspiracy Case → Aurobindo Ghosh. [Q65]\n● Match: Abhinav Bharat → V.D. Savarkar; Anushilan Samiti → Sri Aurobindo Ghosh; Gadar Party →\nLala Hardayal; Swaraj Party → C.R. Das. [Q72]\n● Match: Abhinav Bharat → G.D. Savarkar; Mitra Mela → V.D. Savarkar; Indian Republican Army →\nSurya Sen; Hindustan Republican Association → S.N. Sanyal. [Q73]\n● Match: Chittagong Armoury Raid → Surya Sen; Kakori Conspiracy → Ram Prasad Bismil; Lahore\nConspiracy → Jatin Das; Ghadar Party → Lala Hardayal. [Q74]\n● Match: Jatin Das → Hunger strike (mrityu); Chandrasekhar Azad → Encounter ke dauran; Bhagat Singh\n→ Hanged; Kalpana Dutt → Life imprisonment ke dauran. [Q77]\n● Match: Chittagaon Armoury Raid → Kalpana Dutt; Abhinav Bharat → V.D. Savarkar; Anushilan Samiti\n→ Aurobindo Ghosh; Kuka Movement → Guru Ram Singh. [Q78]\n● Match: Revolt Group → Surya Sen; Hindustan Republican Association → Ram Prasad Bismil; HSRA →\nChandra Shekhar Azad; Punjab Naujawan Bharat Sabha → Bhagat Singh. [Q80]\n23. The Kanpur Bolshevik Conspiracy Case\n● Muzaffar Ahmad, S.A. Dange, Shaukat Usmani aur Nalini Gupta ko 'Kanpur Bolshevik Conspiracy Case'\nmein jail hui — Socialist ideology ke phailne se rokne ke liye government ne kadam uthaye, sabko 4\nsaal ki imprisonment mili. [Q66]\n24. The Chittagong Armoury Raid — Surya Sen\n● 'Chittagong Armoury Raid' Surya Sen ('Master Da') ne organize kiya tha — 18 April 1930 ko, Chittagong\n(Bengal) mein police armoury raid karne ki koshish. Unhone 'Indian Republican Army' (IRA) bhi\nestablish ki thi. [Q67, Q68, Q69, Q70]\n25. The Youngest Martyr — Khudiram Bose\n● India ki War of Independence mein sabse kam age ke martyr Khudiram Bose the — 3 December 1889\nko paida hue, 11 August 1908 ko hang hue, sirf 18 saal 8 mahine 8 din ki age mein. [Q71]"," 26. Jatin Das — Death by Hunger Strike\n● Jatin Das ko 14 June 1929 ko 'Lahore Conspiracy Case' ke under arrest kiya gaya — unhone 63 din ki\nhunger strike ki aur 13 September 1929 ko jail mein hi unki mrityu ho gayi. [Q75, Q76]\n27. The Kakori Case Defence Committee\n● Kakori Case mein accused logo ko defend karne ke liye ek committee bani thi — Pandit Motilal Nehru ki\nchairmanship maani jaati thi, lekin UPPSC ne baad mein isse revise karke Govind Ballabh Pant ko sahi\nmaana. [Q79]\n28. The Naujawan Bharat Sabha\n●\n Trap: Ambika Chakravarti 1926 mein bani 'Naujawan Bharat Sabha' ke early member NAHI the —\n⚠️\nwo Chittagong Jugantar Party ke member the. Bhagat Singh ne March 1926 mein Yashpal,\nRamchandra, Bhagvati Charan Vohra ke saath ye left-wing association banayi thi. [Q81]\n29. Overview of Revolutionary Organizations\n● Abhinav Bharat Society aur Anushilan Samiti — dono revolutionary organizations thi. 'United Indian\nPatriotic Association' Sir Syed Ahmed Khan ne Congress ke virodh ke liye banayi thi — ye revolutionary\norganization NAHI thi. [Q82]\n30. Passive Resistance — Aurobindo Ghosh\n● 'Passive Resistance' ka doctrine Aurobindo Ghosh ne propound kiya tha, apne newspaper 'Vande\nMataram' mein — unka view tha ki Britishers ko turant India chhodni chahiye. [Q83]\n31. Gorakhpur Jail Hangings\n● Kakori case ke baad, Ram Prasad Bismil ko Gorakhpur Jail mein hang kiya gaya (19 December 1927\nko), Rajendra Lahiri ko Gonda mein, Roshan Singh ko Allahabad (Prayagraj) mein, aur Ashfaq Ullah ko\nFaizabad (Ayodhya) mein. [Q85, Q86, Q87]\n32. Attempted Assassination of Charles Tegart"," ● Charles Tegart (Calcutta Police Commissioner, brutality ke liye notorious) ki hatya ki koshish 12 January\n1924 ko Gopinath Saha ne ki thi — lekin galti se ek doosre white man (Mr. Ernest Day) ko goli maar di.\nSaha ko March 1924 mein hang kiya gaya. [Q88]\n33. Bina Das\n● Bina Das ne February 1932 mein, apni degree convocation ke dauran, English Governor par goli chalayi\nthi. [Q89]\n34. Bhagat Singh's Philosophy\n● Bhagat Singh ne kaha tha: 'Criticism aur independent thought — ek revolutionary ke 2 zaroori\ncharacteristics hain.' [Q90]\n35. Tilak's 'Lathi Club'\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne 'Lathi Club', Hindu Akhada, Ganapati Mahotsava aur Shivaji Mahotsava jaisi\nactivities shuru ki thi. [Q91]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Revolutionary Movements in India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0217","t":"15 Revolutionary Activities Outside India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.15 — REVOLUTIONARY ACTIVITIES OUTSIDE INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n🌍\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Shyamji Krishna Verma & the Indian Home Rule Society\n2. The Ghadar Party — Formation & Leadership\n3. Ghadar Party — Members & Association\n4. The Ghadar Movement During World War I\n5. Raja Mahendra Pratap — The Provisional Government at Kabul\n6. Madam Bhikaji Cama — 'Mother of Indian Revolution'\n7. Assassinations in England — Dhingra & Udham Singh\n8. Revolutionaries Abroad — A Common Thread\n9. Abhinav Bharat's London Branch\n10. The Kamagatamaru Incident\n11. Chronology of Revolutionary Events\n12. Match List — Organizations & Their Headquarters\n13. Ras Bihari Bose — The India Independence League\n1. Shyamji Krishna Verma & the Indian Home Rule Society\n● Shyamji Krishna Verma ne February 1905 mein, London mein, 'Indian Home Rule Society' establish ki\n(jise 'India House' bhi kehte the) — British government ko intimidate karke self-rule establish karne ke\nmaksad se. Yahi se 'The Indian Sociologist' newspaper bhi publish hoti thi. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5]\n2. The Ghadar Party — Formation & Leadership\n● 1913 mein San Francisco mein, Sohan Singh Bhakna ne 'Hindustani Workers of the Pacific Coast'\norganization founded ki — isne 'Ghadar' newspaper publish ki, isliye ise 'Ghadar Party' kaha gaya. Lala\nHardayal iske founder members mein se ek aur torchbearer the. [Q6, Q7, Q9, Q14, Q15, Q16]\n● Ghadar Party 1913 mein establish hui thi. [Q8]\n● Sohan Singh Bhakna, Ghadar Party ke pehle Chairman the — party 'Ghadar' newspaper ko Urdu,\nPunjabi, Gujarati, Hindi jaisi languages mein publish karti thi. [Q10, Q11]\n● 'Ghadar' expatriate Indians ki ek revolutionary association thi, jiska headquarters San Francisco mein\ntha — 21 April 1913 ko founded, iska maksad Canada-America mein rehne wale Indians dwara British\nrule se India ko azaad karana tha. [Q17, Q18]\n3. Ghadar Party — Members & Association\n● Diye gaye freedom fighters mein se sirf Ras Bihari Bose hi Ghadar Party se actively involved the —\nBarindra Kumar Ghosh Alipore Bomb case se, aur Jogesh Chandra Chatterjee Kakori Conspiracy se\njuday the. [Q12]\n●\n Trap: Khudiram Bose, Ghadar Party se associate NAHI the — wo 1908 ke Muzaffarpur bomb case\n⚠️\nse juday the, unhe 11 August 1908 ko hang kiya gaya. Ghadar Party 21 April 1913 mein establish hui\nthi. [Q13]"," 4. The Ghadar Movement During World War I\n● Ghadar revolutionaries WWI ke outbreak ke time West America (San Francisco) mein active the —\nAmerica continent North aur South America mein bata hua hai, San Francisco western hisse mein hai.\n[Q19]\n● 1914 mein WWI shuru hone ke baad, Indian Nationalists (Swadeshi movement ke decline ke baad\ninactive ho chuke the) ne ise ek advantage samjha — 'England par koi bhi distress, Indians ke liye\nadvantage hai' wala concept follow karke Ghadar revolutionaries ne armed struggle ke through British\nrule overthrow karne ki koshish ki. [Q20]\n5. Raja Mahendra Pratap — The Provisional Government at Kabul\n● WWI ke dauran, Raja Mahendra Pratap ne 1915 mein Kabul (Afghanistan) mein India ki pehli\n'provisional government' establish ki — Mahendra Pratap khud President bane aur Maulavi Barakatullah\nPrime Minister the. Germany aur Russia ne isse recognition di. [Q21, Q22]\n●\n Trap: Kabul ki interim government (Raja Mahendra Pratap Singh) WWI ke dauran (1915) Germany\n⚠️\nke support se banayi gayi thi — diye gaye options mein se koi bhi is specific event ko sahi tarah match\nnahi karta, isliye 'None of the above' sahi hai. [Q23]\n6. Madam Bhikaji Cama — 'Mother of Indian Revolution'\n● Bhikaiji Cama (ek wealthy Parsi family se) ko 'Mother of Indian Revolution' kaha jaata hai — unhone\nAmerica-Europe se revolutionary movement lead ki. Unki mrityu August 1936 mein hui. [Q24, Q26, Q27]\n● Statement check: Madam Cama ne International Socialist Congress mein National Flag unfurl kiya\n(sahi) aur wo Dadabhai Naoroji ki personal secretary rahi thi (sahi) — lekin ye Paris mein NAHI,\nStuttgart (Germany) mein hua tha, 22 August 1907 ko. [Q25]\n● Madam Cama ne 1907 mein, Stuttgart (Germany) mein hone wali International Socialist Congress mein,\nIndian tricolour flag hoist kiya tha — foreign land par Indian flag hoist karne wali pehli vyakti thi. [Q28,\nQ29]\n7. Assassinations in England — Dhingra & Udham Singh\n● Madan Lal Dhingra aur Udham Singh — dono ko British officers ki hatya ke liye England mein death\nsentence mili. Dhingra ne 1 July 1909 ko Curzon Wyllie aur Cowsji ki hatya ki. Udham Singh ne March\n1940 mein Michael O'Dwyer (Jallianwala Bagh Massacre ke liye indirectly responsible) ki hatya ki,\nLondon mein. [Q30, Q31]\n●\n Trap: Madan Lal Dhingra ko Colonel Wyllie ki hatya ke liye 'life punishment' NAHI mili — unhe death\n⚠️\n\nsentence mili aur hang kiya gaya. [Q32]\n8. Revolutionaries Abroad — A Common Thread"," ● Madam Bhikaji Cama, M. Barkatullah, V.V.S. Iyer aur M.N. Roy — sabhi India ki azaadi ke liye alag-alag\nforeign countries se ladne wale prominent revolutionaries the. [Q33]\n9. Abhinav Bharat's London Branch\n● V.D. Savarkar ne, law padhne London jaate waqt, 1906 mein 'Abhinav Bharat Society' ki ek branch\nestablish ki — India mein revolutionary activities ban hone ke baad ye society England mein extend ki\ngayi thi. [Q34]\n10. The Kamagatamaru Incident\n● 'Kamagatamaru' ek Japanese steamliner thi, jise ek dhani Punjabi businessman Gurdit Singh ne charter\nkiya tha — Indian immigrants ko Canada le jaane ke liye. 1914 mein 376 Indians lekar ye ship\nVancouver (Canada) rawana hui, lekin Canadian police ne unhe entry se mana kar diya. [Q35, Q36, Q38]\n●\n Trap: Question mein 'Baba Gurdip Singh' likha hai, jo option error hai — actual naam 'Gurdit Singh'\n⚠️\n(Baba) tha, jinhone Kamagatamaru ship charter ki thi. [Q37]\n11. Chronology of Revolutionary Events\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Ghadar Party ki foundation (21 April 1913) → Berlin mein Indian\nIndependence Committee (1915 ke baad, renamed hokar) → Central Assembly Bomb Case (8 April\n1929) → Chittagong Armoury Raid (18 April 1930). [Q39]\n12. Match List — Organizations & Their Headquarters\n● Match: Swadeshi Sevak Home → Vancouver; United India House → Seattle; Yugantar Ashram → San\nFrancisco; INA (Azad Hind Fauj) → Rangoon. [Q40]\n13. Ras Bihari Bose — The India Independence League\n● Ras Bihari Bose (Japan mein rehne wale immigrant Indian) ne 28-30 March 1942 ko Tokyo mein ek\nconference convene ki — usme unhone 'Indian Independence League' establish karne ka decision liya.\nYe June 1942 ke Bangkok Convention mein structure ki gayi, jisme Subhash Chandra Bose ko invite\nkiya gaya tha. [Q41]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Revolutionary Activities Outside India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0218","t":"16 Partition of Bengal and Swadeshi Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.16 — PARTITION OF BENGAL & SWADESHI MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🇮🇳\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Chronology of Curzon-Era Policies\n2. Announcement & Enforcement of the Partition\n3. Reasons for the Partition\n4. Leaders of the Anti-Partition Agitation\n5. Origins of the Swadeshi & Boycott Movements\n6. Rabindranath Tagore's Ambivalence\n7. Bharat Mata & Abanindranath Tagore\n8. National Handloom Day\n9. Annulment of the Partition — 1911\n10. Regional Leaders of the Swadeshi Movement\n11. Classes Unaffected by the Swadeshi Movement\n12. 'Vande Mataram' as the Theme Song\n13. The Barisal Peasants — Ashwani Kumar Dutta\n14. The Scope of the Swadeshi Movement\n15. Achievements of the Swadeshi/Boycott Movement\n16. British Journalist H.W. Nevinson\n1. Chronology of Curzon-Era Policies\n● Chronological order: Permanent Settlement (Lord Cornwallis, 1793) → Subsidiary Alliance (Lord\nWellesley, 1798) → Doctrine of Lapse (Lord Dalhousie, 1848-56) → Partition of Bengal (Lord Curzon,\nJuly 1905 — sabse aakhri event). [Q1]\n2. Announcement & Enforcement of the Partition\n● Bengal partition Lord Curzon (1899-1905) ne 20 July 1905 ko announce ki thi — Bengal ko Curzon ne\nisliye divide kiya taaki crown rule ko strengthen kiya jaaye aur Congress Party ka center todaa ja sake.\n[Q6, Q8]\n●\n Disputed: Bengal partition ki declaration date par kuch confusion hai — officially 20 July 1905\n⚠️\nannounce hui, lekin kuch historians 19 July 1905 bataate hain — BPSC ne 19 July wala option accept\nkiya. [Q5]\n● 7 August 1905 ko Calcutta ke Town Hall mein ek historic meeting hui — isi meeting mein famous\nBoycott resolution pass hui, jisse Swadeshi Movement ki shuruat hui. [Q2]\n● 16 October 1905 ko Bengal partition formally lagu (in force) ho gayi — is din ko 'Mourning Day' manaya\ngaya. Rabindranath Tagore ne isse 'Rakhi Diwas' ki tarah celebrate karne ka suggestion diya. [Q3]\n● Sir Andrew Fraser (Lieutenant Governor of Bengal, 1903-1908) Bengal partition frame karne mein bahut\nactively involved the. [Q9]\n● 'Boycott of British goods' 1905 mein national policy ki tarah adopt kiya gaya — 7 August 1905 ko,\nCalcutta Townhall meeting mein. [Q14]\n● Bengal partition ke against agitation ke dauran hi pehli baar 'Swadeshi' aur 'Boycott' struggle ke tareeke\nki tarah adopt hue — Lord Curzon ke against ek economic strategy. [Q18, Q19]"," 3. Reasons for the Partition\n● Bengal partition ka main motive tha Bengal mein growing Bengali Nationalism ko kamzor karna —\nBengal ko Indian Nationalism ka 'nerve-centre' maana jaata tha, isliye Curzon ne politically advanced\ncommunities ko alag provinces mein baatkar unka spirit todne ki koshish ki. [Q16]\n4. Leaders of the Anti-Partition Agitation\n● Surendranath Banerjee ne Bengal Partition (1905) ke against agitation lead ki — unhone kaha tha:\n'Partition humpar bomb shell ki tarah gira.' [Q10, Q11]\n5. Origins of the Swadeshi & Boycott Movements\n● Bengal Partition, Swadeshi Movement ka immediate cause bani — Tilak, Aurobindo Ghosh, Bipin\nChandra Pal aur Lala Lajpat Rai is\nकेmain proposers the, aur ye movement poore desh mein Tilak ne\nlead ki. [Q4, Q20, Q22, Q23]\n● Krishna Kumar Mitra (freedom fighter, journalist, Brahmo Samaj leader) sabse pehle British goods ke\nboycott ka suggestion dene wale the — 13 July 1905 ko, apni 'Sanjibani' Bengali weekly magazine\nmein. [Q13]\n● Bengal Partition ke against nationalists ne kai programmes launch kiye: Boycott, Swadeshi ka use, aur\nNational Education — Non-cooperation is movement ka hissa NAHI thi (wo baad mein Gandhi ke time\naayi). [Q17]\n6. Rabindranath Tagore's Ambivalence\n● R.N. Tagore, Swadeshi movement ke critic the — unki political political stance mixed thi, kabhi full\nsupport dete the, kabhi movement se door rehte the. September 1925 mein unhone apne essay 'The\nCult of the Chakra' mein isse denounce kiya. [Q12]\n7. Bharat Mata & Abanindranath Tagore\n● Abanindranath Tagore ne India ko ek nation ki tarah visually represent karne ke liye famous 'Bharat\nMata' painting banayi — 1905 mein, Swadeshi Movement ke dauran. Isme Bharat Mata ko 4-haath wali\ndevi, saffron sari mein dikhaya gaya — ye nationalism-unity ka symbol ban gayi. [Q15]\n● Abanindranath Tagore ne 'Indian Society of Oriental Art' found ki — India ki ancient art traditions ko\nrevive karne ke liye. Wo international recognition paane wale pehle Indian artist the, aur unke bade bhai\nGaganendranath Tagore bhi artist the. [Q36]\n8. National Handloom Day"," ● Statement check: India mein 7 August ko 'National Handloom Day' manaya jaata hai — 7 August 1905\nko launch hui Swadeshi Movement ki yaad mein — dono statements sahi hain, aur doosra pehle ka sahi\nexplanation hai. [Q21]\n9. Annulment of the Partition — 1911\n● Lord Curzon ne 1905 mein Bengal partition ki thi — 1911 mein ye partition annul (radd) kar di gayi. [Q7]\n● Bengal partition (1905) ko opposition ki wajah se 1911 mein wapas jod diya gaya — Delhi Durbar mein\nKing George V ke aane par, 12 December 1911 ko, King ne partition abolish ki aur India ki capital\nCalcutta se Delhi transfer karne ki declaration ki. Odisha aur Bihar ko Bengal se alag kiya gaya. [Q24,\nQ25, Q26, Q27]\n10. Regional Leaders of the Swadeshi Movement\n● Swadeshi Movement ke regional leaders: Chidambaram Pillai (Madras Presidency), Tilak (Mumbai-\nPune), Ajit Singh aur Lala Lajpat Rai (Punjab-UP), aur Syed Haider Raja (Delhi). [Q28, Q29]\n11. Classes Unaffected by the Swadeshi Movement\n● 1905 ke Swadeshi Movement mein women ne active role play kiya — lekin farmers aur Muslims\nSwadeshi-Boycott movement se mostly door rahe. Aswani Kumar Dutt ne masses ko organize karne ke\nliye 'Swadesh Bandhav Samiti' banayi. [Q30]\n12. 'Vande Mataram' as the Theme Song\n● Swadeshi Movement ke dauran, 16 October 1905 ko (partition ka actual din) mourning day declare kiya\ngaya — log rakhi bandhte the, offices band rehte the, aur galiyon mein 'Vande Mataram' goonjti thi — ye\nraatoraat Bengal ka National Song aur National Movement ki Theme Song ban gaya. [Q31]\n13. The Barisal Peasants — Ashwani Kumar Dutta\n●\n Trap: Liyakat Hussain ne Barisal ke Muslim peasants ko lead NAHI kiya tha — ye Ashwani Kumar\n⚠️\nDutta ne kiya tha. [Q32]\n14. The Scope of the Swadeshi Movement\n●\n Trap: Swadeshi Movement sirf Bengal tak limited NAHI thi — Lala Lajpat Rai, Tilak aur Aurobindo\n⚠️\nGhosh jaise leaders ne is movement ko poore desh mein phailaya. [Q33]"," 15. Achievements of the Swadeshi/Boycott Movement\n● Swadeshi Movement 'Boycott' movement ki complementary thi — foreign goods ke boycott se,\nindigenous artisan crafts-industries (textile mills, banks, chemical works, insurance companies,\nSwadeshi stores) revive hui, aur National Council of Education establish hui. [Q34]\n16. British Journalist H.W. Nevinson\n● Henry Woodd Nevinson, ek British journalist, Swadeshi Movement se associate the — unhone 4\nmahine India travel karke reports likhi (Manchester Guardian, Glasgow Herald, Daily Chronicle mein\npublish hui), aur unhe 'The New Spirit in India' book mein compile kiya. [Q35]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Partition of Bengal and Swadeshi Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0219","t":"17 Congress Benaras Calcutta Surat Session","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.17 — CONGRESS: BENARAS, CALCUTTA & SURAT SESSION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — The Benaras Session (1905)\n2. The Calcutta Session (1906) — Dadabhai Naoroji & 'Swaraj'\n3. Dadabhai Naoroji — The 'Grand Old Man of India'\n4. The Surat Split (1907)\n5. The Four Resolutions of the Calcutta Session (1906)\n1. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — The Benaras Session (1905)\n● Gopal Krishna Gokhale (9 May 1866, Ratnagiri mein paida hue), Elphinstone College se graduate the,\nFerguson College (Poona) mein Political Economy-History professor bane, aur baad mein famous\npolitical leader bane. [Q1]\n● Gopal Krishna Gokhale ne 1905 mein Benaras Session (INC) preside ki — usi saal unhone 'Servants of\nIndia Society' bhi found ki. [Q2, Q3]\n2. The Calcutta Session (1906) — Dadabhai Naoroji & 'Swaraj'\n● 1906 mein, Congress split hone ke khatre mein thi — moderates ne Dadabhai Naoroji ('Grand Old Man\nof India') ko preside karne ke liye chuna, kyunki wo moderates aur extremists dono ke respected the. Isi\nsession mein Congress ne 'Swaraj' ko Indian logo ka goal declare kiya — moderates ne is resolution ko\nsoften karke 'self-Government within British colonies' ka matlab diya. [Q4]\n● Calcutta Session (1906) mein, President Dadabhai Naoroji ne India ke liye 'Swaraj' ka flag unfurl kiya —\nDecember 1906 mein 'Swaraj' ko Indian logo ka goal ki tarah bataya gaya. [Q5, Q7, Q8]\n● 'Swaraj' resolution 1905 mein Benaras session mein uthayi gayi, aur 1906 ke Calcutta session mein\npoori tarah pass hui — iska main purpose tha self-rule secure karna, British products boycott karna, aur\ndomestic production ko revive karna. [Q6]\n●\n Trap: 'Swaraj' word sabse pehle Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne NAHI, Dayanand Saraswati ne use kiya tha\n⚠️\n\n— halaki diye gaye options mein Tilak (jinka famous statement 'Swaraj is my birthright' hai) hi closest\nanswer mana gaya. [Q9]\n3. Dadabhai Naoroji — The 'Grand Old Man of India'\n● Dadabhai Naoroji ko 'Grand Old Man of India' kaha jaata hai — ek Parsi intellectual, educator aur early\nIndian political leader the. Wo 1892 mein Liberal Party se, Central Finsbury constituency se, British\nHouse of Commons mein elect hone wale pehle Indian bane. Wo 1886, 1893 aur 1906 mein INC\nPresident bhi rahe. [Q10, Q11, Q12]\n●\n Trap: Dadabhai Naoroji Liberal Party ki ticket par British Parliament mein elect hue the,\n⚠️\nConservative Party ki NAHI — ye galat statement hai. [Q13]"," ●\n Trap: Dadabhai Naoroji ne INC ki presidency 3 baar ki (1886, 1893, 1906) — 4 baar NAHI, ye galat\n⚠️\nstatement hai. [Q14]\n● Dadabhai Naoroji, British Parliament mein elect hone wale pehle Indian the — 1892 mein. [Q15]\n4. The Surat Split (1907)\n● INC 1907 mein 2 groups mein split hui — Extremists ka 'Garam Dal' (Lala Lajpat Rai ki leadership mein)\naur Moderates ka 'Naram Dal' (Ras Bihari Ghosh ki leadership mein). Ye split 1906 ke Calcutta session\nmein pass hue 4 resolutions (Swadeshi, Boycott, National Education, Self-Rule) ko continue karne ke\nsawaal par hua — Extremists continue karna chahte the, Liberals nahi. [Q16, Q17, Q18]\n● Surat Session (1907) ke President 'R.B. Ghosh' (Rash Behari Ghosh) the — Moderates unhe president\nbanana chahte the, Extremists Lala Lajpat Rai ko chahte the. Aakhir Rash Behari Ghosh president\nbane, aur Congress split ho gayi. [Q19]\n● Congress mein split ka process 20th century ki shuruat mein shuru hua — congress movement ki\nstrategies, objectives (moderates vs extremists), aur logo ki participation — sabhi factors ki wajah se.\n[Q21]\n● Statement check: 1907 mein Congress ka Annual Session Rash Behari Ghosh ne preside ki (sahi),\nSurat session mein Congress Moderates-Extremists mein bat gayi (sahi) — teesra statement galat hai.\n[Q22]\n● Indian National Congress ka 'Surat Split' 1907 mein hua tha — ye pehla partition INC ka bhi mana jaata\nhai. [Q23, Q24]\n● Surat split ki leadership Tilak ne ki — Extremists (unke under) Swadeshi-Boycott Movement ko extend\nkarna chahte the, lekin moderates ise support nahi karte the. [Q25]\n● Surat split (1907) ki main wajah thi — Extremists ko moderates ki British Government ke saath\nnegotiate karne ki capacity par vishwas nahi tha. [Q26]\n5. The Four Resolutions of the Calcutta Session (1906)\n●\n Trap: Calcutta Session (1906) mein pass hue 4 resolutions the: Swadeshi, Boycott, National\n⚠️\nEducation, aur Self-Rule — 'Bengal Partition ka Annulment' inme SHAAMIL NAHI tha. [Q20]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Congress Benaras Calcutta Surat Session Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0220","t":"18 Formation of Muslim League 1906","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.18 — FORMATION OF MUSLIM LEAGUE (1906) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Founding — Nawab Salimullah & Dhaka (1906)\n2. Aga Khan III — First President & the Shimla Deputation\n3. Annual Sessions of the Muslim League\n4. The League's Positions — Bengal Partition & Separate Electorates\n5. The London Branch — Ameer Ali\n6. W.W. Hunter's Prophecy\n1. The Founding — Nawab Salimullah & Dhaka (1906)\n● 'All India Muslim League' ke founder Nawab Salimullah Khan (Dhaka) the — October 1906 mein, Shimla\nmein Muslim representatives ne, Aga Khan III ki leadership mein, ek central Muslim organization banane\nka decision liya. [Q1, Q2]\n● December 1906 mein Dhaka mein 'All India Muhammadan Educational Conference' organize hui —\nWelcome Committee ke President, Nawab of Dhaka Salimullah Khan, ne 'All India Muslim League'\nbanane ka proposal diya. Ek 60-member temporary committee bani, jisme Mohsin-ul-Mulk aur Waqar-ul-\nMulk joint secretaries the — headquarters Lucknow mein tha. [Q3]\n● All India Muslim League 1906 mein found hui. [Q4]\n2. Aga Khan III — First President & the Shimla Deputation\n● Aga Khan III, All India Muslim League ke pehle President the. [Q5]\n● Muslim Deputation (Shimla Deputation), Aga Khan III ke organize karne par, 1 October 1906 ko Shimla\nmein Viceroy Lord Minto se mili — unka aim tha Muslim interests safeguard karne ke liye British\nsympathy jeetna, aur unhone apni community ke liye 'Separate Electorate' ki demand ki. [Q10]\n3. Annual Sessions of the Muslim League\n● Muslim League ka pehla annual session Karachi mein, 1907 mein hua — doosra session 1908 mein\nAmritsar mein hua. [Q6]\n●\n Disputed: Muslim League ke annual conventions 1907 (Karachi) aur 1908 (Amritsar) ke baad\n⚠️\nregular basis par NAHI hue — wo erratic (asamanya) tarike se desh ke alag-alag hisso mein hote rahe,\nisliye 'None of the above' sahi answer hai (halaki BPSC ne ek alag option accept kiya tha). [Q7]\n4. The League's Positions — Bengal Partition & Separate Electorates\n● Assertion-Reason: Muslim League ne Congress ko Muslim logo ke rights ke matter mein accept karne\nse mana kar diya (sahi Assertion) — lekin League ne khud ko India ke Muslims ka ekmatra\nrepresentative institution maanti thi, ye Reason theek nahi hai. [Q8]"," ●\n Trap: 1906 mein bani All India Muslim League ne Bengal partition ka virodh NAHI kiya, balki uska\n⚠️\nstrongly SUPPORT kiya — Aga Khan III ki leadership mein unhone separate electorate ki demand ki.\n[Q9]\n5. The London Branch — Ameer Ali\n● All India Muslim League ki London branch 1908 mein, Ameer Ali ki presidency mein, establish hui —\nBritish Government par pressure banane ke liye Muslim cause ke liye. [Q11]\n6. W.W. Hunter's Prophecy\n● 'Agar Muslims content aur satisfied hon, to wo India mein British power ke sabse bade bulwark (support)\nban jaayenge' — ye statement W.W. Hunter ne apni book 'The Indian Musalmans' mein likha tha. [Q12]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Formation of Muslim League 1906 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0221","t":"19 Morley Minto Reforms","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.19 — MORLEY-MINTO REFORMS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Indian Councils Act, 1909 — Origins & Communal Representation\n2. The Long-Term Impact — Seeds of Partition & 'Father of Pakistan'\n1. The Indian Councils Act, 1909 — Origins & Communal Representation\n● 'Morley-Minto Reforms Bill', 'Indian Councils Act, 1909' ke naam se jaana jaata hai, 1909 mein pass hua\ntha — 1905 mein Lord Minto ne Lord Curzon ki jagah Viceroy banna, aur John Morley ko Secretary of\nState for India appoint kiya gaya, unhi ke naam par reforms ka naam pada. Iski wajah se Indians ki\nadministration mein involvement thodi badhi, lekin main dispute Muslims ke liye 'Separate Electorate'\npar tha. [Q1]\n● Indian Councils Act, 1909 (Morley-Minto) ki sabse badi khaami thi 'Communal Representation' ka\nsystem — Muslims ke liye 'Separate Electorate' ka concept accept kiya gaya, jisme Muslim members\nsirf Muslim voters ke dwara elect hote the. [Q2]\n2. The Long-Term Impact — Seeds of Partition & 'Father of Pakistan'\n● Morley-Minto Reforms mein Muslims ke liye 'Separate Electorate' aur legislative assemblies mein\nreserved seats ka provision hi National Movement mein 'discord ka beej' saabit hua, jo aage chalkar\ndesh ka partition bana — pehli baar Muslim community ko poori tarah alag section ki tarah recognize\nkiya gaya, jisse 'Hindu-Muslim Disharmony' shuru hui. Alag Muslim constituencies banayi gayi, aur ye\ncommunal representation ka principle Government of India Act 1919 mein aage bhi continue hua. [Q3]\n● Rajendra Prasad ne Lord Minto ko 'Father of Pakistan' maana — kyunki 1909 ke Minto-Morley reforms\nne India mein communal electorates introduce kiye, jisse partition ke beej bo diye gaye. [Q4]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Morley-Minto Reforms Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0222","t":"20 Delhi Durbar and Change of Capital","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.20 — DELHI DURBAR & CHANGE OF CAPITAL — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Transfer of Capital — Calcutta to Delhi\n2. The Delhi Conspiracy Case — Bomb on Lord Hardinge\n3. Bihar Becomes a Separate Province\n1. The Transfer of Capital — Calcutta to Delhi\n● British rule ke dauran, 1911 AD tak Calcutta (aaj ka Kolkata) India ki capital thi — King George V ne\nIndia visit karke 1911 ke Delhi Durbar mein attend kiya, aur 12 December 1911 ko Calcutta se Delhi\ncapital shift karne ki announcement ki. [Q1, Q6]\n● Capital ka transfer Lord Hardinge-II ke tenure mein hua — announcement 1911 mein hui, lekin actual\ntransfer 1912 mein complete hua. [Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5]\n2. The Delhi Conspiracy Case — Bomb on Lord Hardinge\n● Delhi Conspiracy Case (Delhi-Lahore Conspiracy bhi kehte hain) mein, capital transfer ke occasion par\nViceroy Lord Hardinge-II ki hatya ki koshish ki gayi — Rash Behari Bose ki leadership mein, Bengal-\nPunjab ke revolutionaries ne 23 December 1912 ko unke State entry ke waqt, Chandni Chowk (Delhi)\nmein, ek homemade bomb phenka. [Q7]\n●\n Trap: Bhagwati Charan Vohra 'Hardinge Bomb Case' mein involve NAHI the — 14 log accused the\n⚠️\n(Master Amir Chand, Balmukund, Basant Kumar Biswas ko death sentence mili; Balraj aur Harvansh\nSahay ko life imprisonment; Dinanath approver ban gaye). Rash Behari Bose, jinhone main role play\nkiya, Japan bhaag gaye aur trial se bach gaye. [Q8]\n● 'Anushilan Samiti' Viceroy Lord Hardinge-II par Delhi mein bomb phenkne ke liye responsible thi —\nRash Behari Bose ne is revolt ki leadership ki. Basant Kumar Biswas, Bhai Balmukund, Amir Chand aur\nAvadh Bihari ko is Delhi Conspiracy case mein guilty paakar death sentence di gayi. [Q9]\n3. Bihar Becomes a Separate Province\n● December 1911 ke Delhi Durbar mein, British emperor ne Bengal partition cancel ki, aur Bihar-Odisha\nko Bengal se alag kiya — Bihar 1 April 1912 ko ek separate province ban gaya. Baad mein 1936 AD\nmein Bihar, Odisha se bhi alag hokar ek doosri separate province bani. [Q10]\n● Bihar sabse pehle 1912 mein Bengal Presidency se separate hua tha — British-ruled India ke dauran.\n[Q11]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Delhi Durbar and Change of Capital Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0223","t":"21 Lucknow Session Lucknow Pact","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.21 — LUCKNOW SESSION (LUCKNOW PACT) — FULL MIND MAP\n🤝\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Lucknow Session (1916) — President & Location\n2. The Lucknow Pact — Terms & Architects\n3. The Congress-League Consensus Period\n4. Champaran & Raj Kumar Shukla\n1. The Lucknow Session (1916) — President & Location\n● December 1916 mein, INC aur Muslim League — dono ne apna session Lucknow mein hi organize kiya\n— isi meeting mein legislature composition aur communities ke liye representation quantum ke\nagreement ke details tay hue. Ye agreement respectively 29 aur 31 December 1916 ko dono\norganisations ke annual sessions mein confirm hui. [Q1]\n● Lucknow Session (1916) ki presidency Ambika Charan Majumdar (A.C. Majumdar) ne ki — isi session\nmein famous Lucknow Pact sign hua. [Q2]\n●\n Trap: Statement 'Ambika Charan Majumdar is session ke President NAHI the' galat hai — wo hi\n⚠️\nLucknow Session (1916) ke President the. Baaki statements sahi hain: Extremists-Moderates ka reunion\nhua, aur Gandhi ji ko Champaran ke peasants ki problems ki jaankari mili. [Q9]\n2. The Lucknow Pact — Terms & Architects\n● Famous 'Lucknow Pact', Congress aur Muslim League ke beech, 1916 mein sign hua — dono parties\nne common political programme par saath kaam karne ka wada kiya. [Q3]\n● Annie Besant (Tilak ke saath) 'chief architect' thi Extremists-Moderates ke reconciliation ki — dono ne\n1907 mein expel kiye gaye Extremists ko Congress mein wapas laane ke liye compromise establish\nkiya. [Q4]\n● Muhammad Ali Jinnah aur Bal Gangadhar Tilak — dono Congress-League Pact (Lucknow Pact) ke\nmain architects the. [Q5]\n● Lucknow Pact (1916) mein Congress ne Muslim League ki 'Separate Electorate' ki demand accept kar li\n— ye League ke liye ek badi concession/achievement thi, halaki kuch Congress leaders ne iska virodh\nkiya, aur iske long-term communal politics par implications hue. [Q6]\n● Congress ne pehli baar 1916 mein, Lucknow Pact ke dauran, Muslims ke liye Separate Electorate ka\nsystem accept kiya. [Q7]\n3. The Congress-League Consensus Period\n● 1916-1922 ka period INC aur Muslim League ke beech 'unanimity/consensus' ka time tha — dono\nparties Lucknow Pact ke mutabik jointly kaam karti rahi, jab tak 1922 mein Non-Cooperation Movement\nsuspend hone ke baad ye pact dissolve nahi ho gaya. [Q8]"," 4. Champaran & Raj Kumar Shukla\n● Lucknow Session (1916) mein, Raj Kumar Shukla ne Mahatma Gandhi se mulaqaat karke unhe\nChamparan ke peasants ki problems ki jaankari di — isi ki wajah se aage Champaran Satyagraha shuru\nhui. [Q10]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lucknow Session Lucknow Pact Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0224","t":"22 Home Rule League Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.22 — HOME RULE LEAGUE MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tilak & Annie Besant — The Two Home Rule Leagues\n2. Contributors & Non-Associates\n3. The Lucknow Conference & the New Phase of the Movement\n4. Separate Existence & the Merger Confusion\n5. Annie Besant — Fabianism, Theosophy & INC Presidency\n6. The Renaming — Swarajya Sabha (1920)\n1. Tilak & Annie Besant — The Two Home Rule Leagues\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne April 1916 mein Belgaum mein pehli Home Rule League launch ki — Annie\nBesant ne apni 'All India Home Rule League' baad mein, September 1916 mein Madras mein launch ki.\nTilak, Besant se kai mahine pehle apni league banane ki wajah se 'first' launch karne ka credit lete hain,\nhalaki Besant ne ye idea 1914 mein hi propose kar diya tha. [Q1]\n● 2 Home Rule Leagues 1915-16 mein, Tilak aur Annie Besant ki leadership mein shuru hui — Tilak ne\nApril 1916 mein, aur Annie Besant ne September 1916 mein. [Q2]\n● Annie Besant mainly 'Home Rule Movement' se associate hain — Irish Home Rule Movement se inspire\nhokar, unhone September 1916 mein Adyar mein Home Rule League banayi. Wo apni newspaper 'The\nCommonweal' mein apne views explain karti thi. [Q3]\n● First World War ke dauran India mein popular hua movement 'Home Rule Movement' tha — iska aim\ntha India ko British dominions ke andar self-government dilana. [Q4]\n2. Contributors & Non-Associates\n●\n Trap: H.S. Olcott (Alcott) Home Rule League se associate NAHI the — wo Theosophical Society se\n⚠️\nrelated the. Tilak, Annie Besant aur S. Subramania Iyer active contributors the. [Q5]\n●\n Trap: C.R. Das (Chittaranjan Das), Tilak-Besant dwara shuru ki gayi Home Rule Movement ki\n⚠️\nleadership se directly associate NAHI the. Tilak, Annie Besant aur S. Subramania Iyer actively involved\nthe. [Q6]\n3. The Lucknow Conference & the New Phase of the Movement\n● Home Rule supporters ne apni political power sabse successfully 1916 ke Lucknow Congress Session\nmein demonstrate ki — Tilak ki Home Rule League ne ek tradition establish ki jisse Congress kai saal\ntak juda raha. [Q7]\n● Home Rule Movement ko freedom movement ke ek naye phase ki shuruat ka symbol maana jaata hai\nkyunki isne nation ke saamne self-government ka ek perfect project prastut kiya — iska objective tha\nBritish Empire ke andar Home Rule ya Self-Governance constitutional tariko se hasil karna. [Q8]"," 4. Separate Existence & the Merger Confusion\n●\n Disputed: Home Rule League ke baare mein sabhi diye gaye statements factually sahi hain —\n⚠️\nAnnie Besant ne plan 1914-15 mein propose kiya, Tilak ki league Maharashtra-Karnataka-Central\nProvinces-Berar tak limited thi lekin zyada organized-strong thi, aur dono leagues Tilak-Besant ke\ndifferences ke bawajood alag-alag exist karti rahi — isliye sabhi correct hone ki wajah se ye question\ndisputed hai. [Q9]\n●\n Disputed: Tilak aur Annie Besant ki Home Rule Leagues KABHI merge NAHI hui — Annie Besant\n⚠️\nne khud kaha tha ki Tilak ke kuch supporters unhe pasand nahi karte the aur vice versa, isliye dono\norganisations conflict avoid karne ke liye alag hi rahi. Diye gaye options mein se koi bhi correct nahi hai.\n[Q10]\n5. Annie Besant — Fabianism, Theosophy & INC Presidency\n● Annie Besant (1847-1933 AD), 'Fabianism' movement ki bhi proponent thi. [Q11]\n● Statement check: Annie Besant ne Home Rule Movement shuru ki (sahi statement 1), aur 1917 mein\nCalcutta session mein INC ki pehli woman President bani (sahi statement 3) — lekin Theosophical\nSociety Annie Besant ne NAHI, balki Madame Blavatsky aur Henry Olcott ne found ki thi (galat\nstatement 2). [Q12]\n6. The Renaming — Swarajya Sabha (1920)\n● 1920 mein, 'All India Home Rule League' ne Mahatma Gandhi ko apna President elect kiya — Gandhi ji\nne baad mein iska naam badalkar 'Swarajya Sabha' rakha. [Q13]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Home Rule League Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0225","t":"23 Gandhi and His Early Movements","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.23 — GANDHI & HIS EARLY MOVEMENTS — FULL MIND MAP\n🕊️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Gandhi's Early Life, Education & First Steps in India\n2. Gandhi in South Africa\n3. Gandhi's Philosophy — Truth, Non-Violence & Satyagraha\n4. Gandhi's Ashrams\n5. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — Gandhi's Political Guru\n6. Gandhi's Political Approach — The Gandhian Model\n7. Chronology of Gandhi's Early Movements\n8. Movements & Satyagrahas NOT Led by Gandhi\n9. Gandhi's Titles — 'Father of Nation' & 'Mahatma'\n10. Gandhian Economy & Constructive Programme\n11. Gandhi's Close Associates\n12. Gandhi in Chhattisgarh\n13. Gandhi — Jail, Later Life & Death\n14. The Champaran Satyagraha — Overview, Tinkathia System & Legacy\n15. Champaran — Associates & the Enquiry Committee\n16. The Ahmedabad Mill Strike & Its 'Firsts'\n17. The Kheda Satyagraha\n1. Gandhi's Early Life, Education & First Steps in India\n● Karamchand Gandhi ('Kaba Gandhi'), Mahatma Gandhi ke pita, Porbandar, Rajkot aur Wankaner —\nteeno states ke Diwan the. [Q1]\n● Gandhiji ne Samaldas Arts College, Bhavnagar mein 1885 AD mein padhai ki thi. [Q2]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne pehli baar 1901 AD mein INC ki Calcutta Session attend ki. [Q17]\n● Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi ka janm 2 October 1869 ko Porbandar (Gujarat) mein hua — unki\neducation Porbandar ke ek Pathshala se shuru hui, 7 saal ki age mein Rajkot shift hue, 13 saal mein\nKasturba se shaadi hui, aur London ke Inner Temple mein law padhi. [Q39]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne India mein apna pehla major public speech February 1916 mein, Banaras Hindu\nUniversity (BHU) ke opening ceremony mein diya — Varanasi mein. [Q67]\n2. Gandhi in South Africa\n● Gandhiji ne South Africa mein rehte hue apna magazine 'Indian Opinion' publish ki — 1894 mein 'Natal\nIndian Congress' bhi found ki thi. [Q3, Q4]\n● Gandhiji ne 1904 mein Durban (South Africa) mein 'Phoenix Farm' establish ki thi. [Q5]\n● Gandhiji South Africa mein lagbhag 21 saal rahe — 1893 mein, 24 saal ki age mein, Gujarati\nbusinessman Dada Abdullah ka case ladne South Africa gaye the, aur January 1915 mein India wapas\naaye. [Q14, Q15]\n● South Africa mein 1893 mein, Pietermaritzburg railway station par Gandhiji ko first-class compartment\nse forcibly nikal diya gaya tha, kyunki 'coolies' aur non-whites ko first-class mein allow nahi kiya jaata\ntha. [Q16]"," ● South Africa mein rehte hue, Gandhiji ne Rustumji ke charity hospitals mein helpless patients ki seva ki,\nek voluntary compounder ki tarah — Boer War ke ghayal soldiers ki bhi seva ki. Yahi unhone 'Seva\nDharma' apnaya. [Q21]\n● Assertion-Reason: South Africa mein Gandhiji ne khud ko discover kiya, shy-timid youth se successful\norganiser bane (sahi Assertion) — lekin unka struggle South Africa mein poori tarah non-violent,\nSatyagraha par based tha, 'militant' struggle NAHI tha (isliye Reason galat hai). [Q22]\n● Match: 'South Africa – 1903' — Gandhiji ne 1903 mein Johannesburg (South Africa) mein apni law firm\nestablish ki, 1910 tak wahi rahe, aur isi period mein Trusteeship ka principle apply kiya. [Q72]\n3. Gandhi's Philosophy — Truth, Non-Violence & Satyagraha\n● M.K. Gandhi 'Philosophical Anarchism' ke supporter the — unke ideal non-violent state mein har citizen\nself-governance feel karega, state ki koi zaroorat nahi hogi. [Q6]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ke Ram Rajya ke 2 twin principles the: Truth (Satya) aur Non-Violence (Ahimsa) —\nunhone inhe naye society ke aadhar ki tarah use kiya. [Q7]\n● Gandhiji ke mutabik, 'Non-Violence' Truth (satya) hasil karne ka ek tareeka hai — Ahimsa 'means' hai,\nTruth 'end' hai. [Q8]\n● Gandhi ne khud ko 'true socialist' kaha (Louis Fischer se baat karte hue) — unka socialism 'Sarvodaya'\ntha. Marx aur Gandhi dono ka final aim stateless-classless society thi, lekin unke tareeke alag the. [Q9]\n● Gandhian Satyagraha strategy mein 'Fasting' (jise wo 'Fire Arrow' kehte the) pehla step tha, aur 'Strike'\naakhri step tha. [Q10]\n●\n Trap: Gandhian Principle ke mutabik, Satyagrahi ka aim dushman ko haraana NAHI hai — balki\n⚠️\nsuffering (kasht) ke through unki perception ko badalna hai. [Q11]\n● Gandhiji ke mutabik, violence ka sabse cruel form 'persistence of poverty' (gareebi ka bane rehna) hai.\n[Q12]\n● Gandhiji ne family planning ke liye 'Self-Control' ka idea diya tha. [Q13]\n● 'Satyagraha' word sabse pehle Magan Lal Gandhi (Gandhiji ke bhatije) ne ek competition mein 'Sada\nGraha' ki tarah use kiya, baad mein Gandhiji ne isse improve karke 'Satyagraha' banaya. India mein\nazaadi ki ladai ke dauran Satyagraha ki shuruaat Mahatma Gandhi ne 1917 ke Champaran Satyagraha\nse ki. [Q28, Q29]\n● Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi 'passive resistance' (India ki azaadi ke liye) use karne ke liye sabse\nzyada jaane jaate hain — South Africa mein unka struggle 'inactive resistance' kehlaata tha, baad mein\nunhone 'Satyagraha' word choose kiya. [Q32]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne kaha tha: 'Foreign clothes ke saath deal karne ka best tareeka hai unka\ndestruction' — isse unhone nation ke self-respect se joda. Unhone ye bhi kaha ki British goods ka\nboycott effective hai kyunki British India ko manufactured goods ke liye ek bada market maante the.\n[Q33, Q34]\n● Mahatma Gandhi kehte the: 'Wrong means kabhi humein right ends tak nahi le jaate' — means aur\nends ko ek sikke ke 2 pehlu ki tarah maante the, jinhe alag nahi kiya ja sakta. Wo strong believer the ki\n'jo morally wrong hai, wo kabhi bhi politically right nahi ho sakta.' [Q63, Q64]"," 4. Gandhi's Ashrams\n● Gandhi ka 'Satyagraha Ashram' originally Kocharab Bungalow (Jivanlal Desai ke) mein establish hua\ntha — baad mein 17 June 1917 ko, Ahmedabad mein, Sabarmati river ke kinare 36 acre zameen par\nshift kiya gaya — isi ashram ko 'Sabarmati Ashram' bhi kehte hain. [Q18, Q19]\n● Gandhi ke sabhi ashramo mein sabse purana 'Phoenix Ashram' hai — 1904 AD mein Phoenix station\n(South Africa) ke pass zameen kharidkar banaya gaya, unka pehla establish kiya hua ashram tha. [Q20]\n5. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — Gandhi's Political Guru\n● Gopal Krishna Gokhale, Mahatma Gandhi ke 'Political Guru' the — 1912 mein Gokhale ne Gandhi ke\ninvitation par South Africa visit ki thi. [Q23]\n● Gandhiji ne apne 'Political Guru' Gokhale se wada kiya tha ki wo India mein apna pehla saal 'apne kaan\nkhule rakhkar aur muh band rakhkar' desh ko observe karte hue bitayenge. [Q61, Q62]\n6. Gandhi's Political Approach — The Gandhian Model\n● Gandhiji ke mutabik, politics ka matlab tha public/social welfare ki activity — unki sabse important\nsuggestion 'power ka decentralization' thi, village Panchayats ko encourage karke unhe apna local\nadministration control karne dena. [Q24]\n●\n Trap: 'Authority' Gandhian political model ki feature NAHI hai — unka politics ka paradigm morality,\n⚠️\nreligion aur humanity ka combination tha, wo ek Stateless Society establish karna chahte the. [Q25]\n7. Chronology of Gandhi's Early Movements\n● Gandhi ki political life mein events ka chronological order: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) →\nAhmedabad Mill Strike (Feb-March 1918) → Kheda Satyagraha (March-June 1918) → Non-cooperation\nMovement (1920-1922). [Q35]\n● Events ka chronological order: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Ahmedabad Mill Strike (Feb-Mar\n1918) → Kheda (Mar-June 1918) → Rowlatt Satyagraha (1919). [Q37]\n● Diye gaye events mein sabse pehle Champaran Satyagraha (1917) hui — Kheda Satyagraha (1918),\nNon-Cooperation Movement (1920), aur Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) baad mein aaye. [Q76]\n8. Movements & Satyagrahas NOT Led by Gandhi\n●\n Trap: Swadeshi Movement (1905-1911) Gandhiji se related NAHI hai — us period mein Gandhiji\n⚠️\nSouth Africa mein reh rahe the. [Q42]\n●\n Trap: 'Bardoli Satyagraha' (1928) Gandhiji ne NAHI, Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel ne lead ki thi —\n⚠️\nGandhi ne Kheda (1918), Civil Disobedience (1930) aur Quit India (1942) lead ki. [Q43]"," ●\n Trap: 'Vaikom Satyagraha' mein Gandhiji ne DIRECTLY participate NAHI kiya — Rajkot, Kheda aur\n⚠️\nNon-cooperation Movement unhone lead ki. Rajkot mein unhone 4 din ke hunger strike ke baad Viceroy\nke through mediation se settlement kiya. [Q49]\n● Vaikom Satyagraha (1924-25), Travancore (Kerala) mein temple entry ke liye ek movement thi —\nuntouchability-caste discrimination ke against. Gandhiji ne March 1925 mein Vaikom visit karke\nTravancore ki Queen Regent se discussions ki. [Q50]\n9. Gandhi's Titles — 'Father of Nation' & 'Mahatma'\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne sabse pehle Gandhiji ko 'Father of Nation' kaha tha — July 1944 mein, Azad\nHind Radio (Rangoon) se apne address mein: 'India ki last war of Independence shuru ho chuki hai...\nFather of Nation, hum aapki dua chahte hain.' [Q45]\n● 'Mahatma' prefix Gandhiji ke naam mein Champaran Satyagraha ke dauran add hua — Rabindranath\nTagore ne unhe pehli baar 'Mahatma' kaha. [Q46, Q47]\n10. Gandhian Economy & Constructive Programme\n● South Africa mein, Gandhi ne John Ruskin ki book 'Unto This Last' padhi — unke mutabik iska message\ntha 'Individual ki bhalai sabki bhalai mein hi nihit hai.' [Q40]\n● Gandhian concept ko Ruskin, Thoreau aur Tolstoy — teeno secular writers ne influence kiya. Ruskin se\nphysical labour ka respect seekha, Tolstoy ke 'kingdom of God is within you' se inspire hue, aur Thoreau\nke Civil Disobedience essay se bhi. [Q41]\n● Gandhi se related statements: Constructive programs mein 'Harijans ki seva' unki top priority thi, aur\nunhone Non-Cooperation aur Civil Disobedience Movement shuru ki — sabhi sahi hain. [Q44]\n●\n Trap: Gandhian economy ke baare mein galat statement — Gandhiji ne USA mein mechanisation\n⚠️\nka virodh NAHI kiya, unka maanna tha ki har desh ki economy uske climate-land-logo ke nature ke\nbasis par define honi chahiye. [Q73]\n● Gandhiji ke mutabik, untouchables ka socio-economic improvement cottage industries establish karke\nho sakta hai — unhone khadi, handlooms, sericulture aur handicrafts jaise rural industries ke growth par\nzor diya. [Q74]\n● 'Gandhian Innovation' term Prof. Prahlad aur R.A. Mashelkar ne coin ki thi — iska matlab hai kam\nresources se zyada logo ke liye zyada output produce karna. [Q75]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne India mein 'Planned Development' ka virodh kiya tha — wo cottage-village\nindustries ke supporter the aur village ko economy ki basic unit maante the. [Q89]\n11. Gandhi's Close Associates\n● Pyare Lal, Noakhali ke dauran Mahatma Gandhi ke secretary the — unki behen Dr. Susheela Nayyar\nGandhiji ki personal doctor thi. Pyare Lal ne Dandi March mein bhi important role play kiya. [Q48]\n● J.B. Kripalani, Gandhian followers mein se ek teacher (profession se) the — Rajendra Prasad bhi kuch\nsamay teacher rahe, lekin mainly wo ek Lawyer the. [Q52]"," ● Jamnalal Bajaj, ek unique capitalist the jo full-time Congress activist ban gaye — unhone kai saal AICC\ntreasurer ki tarah service ki, aur 1923-1930 mein jail gaye. Gandhiji unhe apna 'paanchwan beta' (fifth\nson) kehte the — wo ek industrialist, philanthropist aur freedom fighter the. [Q53, Q54]\n● Charles Andrews ('Deenbandhu' Andrews) Gandhiji ke close English compatriot the — St. Stephen's\nCollege, Delhi mein professor the. Wo Tagore, Gokhale aur Gandhi ke bahut close the, Phoenix Farm\nmein Gandhi ke saath rahe, aur 1925-27 tak All India Trade Union Congress ke President bhi rahe.\n[Q55]\n12. Gandhi in Chhattisgarh\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne pehli baar Chhattisgarh 20 December 1920 ko, Dhamtari district mein, visit kiya —\nbaad mein 24 November 1933 ko bhi wahan aaye. [Q51]\n● Maulana Shaukat Ali (Khilafat Movement ke Muslim leader) 1920 mein Gandhiji ke saath Chhattisgarh\ntour par gaye the. [Q56]\n13. Gandhi — Jail, Later Life & Death\n● Gandhiji ne Yerawada Central Jail (Pune, Maharashtra) ko 'Mandir' ka naam diya tha — wo azaadi ki\nladai ke dauran yahan kai saal rahe. [Q57]\n● India ki independence ke waqt, Gandhiji INC ke member NAHI the — 1934 mein unhone resign kar diya\ntha, uske baad kabhi formal member nahi bane. [Q58]\n● 30 January 1948 ko Nathuram Godse ne Gandhiji ki hatya ki — unki mrityu par Jawaharlal Nehru ne\nkaha: 'Friends and comrades, the light has gone out of our lives, and there is darkness everywhere.'\n[Q59]\n● Lord Mountbatten ne Gandhiji ko 'One-man Boundary Force' kaha tha — unhone likha: 'Punjab mein\nhumare paas 50,000 soldiers hain, lekin Bengal mein sirf ek insaan (Gandhi) hai aur wahan koi riot nahi\nhai.' [Q60]\n14. The Champaran Satyagraha — Overview, Tinkathia System & Legacy\n● Champaran Satyagraha (1917), Bihar mein, Gandhiji ka India ki dharti par pehla Satyagraha tha — aur\nIndia ka pehla Civil Disobedience Movement bhi tha. Ye poore desh mein Gandhi dwara start ki gayi\npehli farmers' movement thi, jisme peasant unrest ko first time National Movement se joda gaya. [Q30,\nQ38, Q80, Q92, Q95, Q96, Q98, Q99, Q100, Q104]\n● Champaran mein indigo cultivation 'Tinkathia System' se hoti thi — jismein factory owners tenants ko\nunki zameen ke ek fixed hisse (3/20th, ya har bigha mein 3 katha) mein indigo ugane ke liye majboor\nkarte the, ek fixed price par. [Q31, Q77, Q82, Q83, Q84]\n● Champaran Movement basically 'cash crops' (khaaskar zabardasti indigo cultivation) ke against tha —\nGandhiji ka mission tha bonded labour ko azaad karana, jise unhone Patna se launch kiya, Rajkumar\nShukla ke saath. [Q68, Q81, Q88]\n● Raj Kumar Shukla (ek indigo cultivator) ne Gandhiji ka dhyan Champaran ke peasants ke exploitation ki\ntaraf khincha aur unhe wahan invite kiya — Gandhi 10 April 1917 ko Champaran pahunche, eminent"," lawyers Brajkishore, Rajendra Prasad, Anugrah Narayan Sinha aur Acharya Kripalani ke saath. [Q78,\nQ79, Q87, Q97, Q101, Q102]\n●\n Trap: Statement galat hai ki Champaran Satyagraha Gandhi ka All-India level ka pehla movement\n⚠️\ntha — ye sirf Champaran tak limited thi. Unka All-India level ka pehla movement 'Rowlatt Satyagraha'\n(1919) tha. [Q103]\n● N.G. Ranga ne Mahatma Gandhi ki Champaran Satyagraha ka virodh kiya tha. [Q105]\n● Bihar ke ek cook, Batak Mian, ne 1917 mein Champaran Satyagraha ke dauran Gandhiji ki jaan bachayi\n— unhe doodh ke through Gandhi ko poison dene ke liye invite kiya gaya tha, lekin wo bhavuk ho gaye\naur Gandhiji ko sach bata diya. [Q26, Q27]\n15. Champaran — Associates & the Enquiry Committee\n● Statement check: Rajkumar Shukla ne Gandhiji ko Champaran aane ke liye persuade kiya (Rajendra\nPrasad ne NAHI). Acharya J.B. Kripalani, Champaran investigation mein Gandhiji ke colleagues mein se\nek the — baaki colleagues the Rajendra Prasad, Mahadev Desai, C.F. Andrews, Dr. Anugrah Narayan\nSinha aur Braj Kishor Prasad. [Q85]\n● Rajendra Prasad aur Anugrah Narayan Sinha, Champaran Satyagraha ke dauran Mahatma Gandhi ke\nsaath jude the. [Q86]\n●\n Trap: Jai Prakash Narayan Champaran Movement se associate NAHI the — Rajendra Prasad,\n⚠️\nAnugrah Narayan Sinha aur J.B. Kripalani is movement se juday the. [Q90]\n●\n Trap: Ram Manohar Lohia, 1917 ke Champaran Satyagraha se related NAHI the — wo freedom\n⚠️\nstruggle ke baad ke phases mein active the. [Q91]\n●\n Trap: 'Champaran Agrarian Enquiry Committee' ke members the: F.G. Slay (President), D.J. Reid,\n⚠️\nMahatma Gandhi, L.C. Adami, Raja Harihar Prasad, Narayan Singh, G. Rainny aur M.E.L. Tainer —\nAnugrah Narayan is committee ke member NAHI the. [Q93]\n● Champaran Movement ki mass agitation ke response mein, British Government ne 'Champaran\nAgrarian Committee' banayi, taaki kisano ki shikayaton ki jaanch ho sake. [Q94]\n16. The Ahmedabad Mill Strike & Its 'Firsts'\n● Ahmedabad Mill Strike (1918) ke dauran, Plague Bonus band karne ke against, Gandhiji ne pehli baar\nhunger strike ko ek weapon ki tarah use kiya. [Q36, Q65, Q66]\n● Ahmedabad mein 1917-18 ke Satyagraha mein Industrial Workers ne participate kiya — cotton textile\nmill workers aur owners ke beech Plague bonus ke issue par agitation chal raha tha. [Q69, Q70, Q71]\n17. The Kheda Satyagraha\n● Kheda (Gujarat) mein Mahatma Gandhi ne peasants ki taraf se Satyagraha organize ki thi — wahan\npoverty, famine aur British discrimination ki wajah se kisan bahut pareshan the, aur famine ne agrarian\neconomy tabaah kar di thi. Ye revolt taxes-rents ke against thi, jinka bhugtan na karne par property zabt\nkarne ki dhamki di ja rahi thi. [Q106]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Gandhi and His Early Movements Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0226","t":"24 Peasant Movement and Kisan Sabha","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.24 — PEASANT MOVEMENT & KISAN SABHA — FULL MIND MAP\n🌾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Bijolia Peasant Movement — India's First\n2. The U.P. Kisan Sabha (1918)\n3. Awadh Peasant Movements — Nai-Dhobi Band & Baba Ramchandra\n4. Peasant Movements of the 1930s — A Match List\n5. The Eka Movement\n6. Swami Sahajanand Saraswati & the Bihar Kisan Sabha\n7. The All India Kisan Sabha (1936)\n8. Peasant Leaders — A Match List\n9. The Bardoli Satyagraha — Sardar Patel\n10. The Tebhaga Movement\n11. The Bhoodan Movement — Vinoba Bhave\n1. The Bijolia Peasant Movement — India's First\n● Mewar (aaj ka Rajasthan) mein 19th century ke doosre hisse mein feudal exploitation common thi — isi\nwajah se 'Bijolia Movement' shuru hui, jo India ka pehla Peasant Movement mana jaata hai. Iski\nleadership shuru mein Sadhu Sitaram Das ne (1913 mein), aur baad mein Vijay Singh Pathik ne (1915\nmein) ki. [Q1]\n● Statement check: Bijolia Peasant Movement 1897 mein shuru hui thi, aur ye India ke longest peasant\nmovements mein se ek maani jaati hai (lagbhag 44 saal chali) — sirf ye statement sahi hai. (Vijay Singh\nPathik ke khud Mahatma Gandhi se personally milne wala statement is context mein incorrect maana\njaata hai.) [Q2]\n2. The U.P. Kisan Sabha (1918)\n● 'U.P. Kisan Sabha' February 1918 mein Gauri Shankar Mishra aur Indra Narayan Dwivedi ne set up ki\n— Madan Mohan Malviya ne unke efforts ko support kiya.\n Jawaharlal Nehru is formation se\n⚠️\nassociate NAHI the — Home Rule League ke activists Oudh mein bahut active the. [Q3, Q4]\n3. Awadh Peasant Movements — Nai-Dhobi Band & Baba Ramchandra\n● 'Nai-Dhobi Band' (ek tarah ka social boycott) 1919 ke end mein, Pratapgarh district ke ek estate mein,\nkisano ne shuru ki thi — 1920 ki garmiyo mein Taluqdari Oudh ke villages mein, village panchayats\ndwara bulayi gayi Kisan meetings frequent ho gayi. [Q5]\n● Baba Ramchandra ne Awadh (Oudh) mein farmers ko organize kiya — 1920 ke mid mein, Oudh ke\npeasants ke leader ki tarah ubhre, aur unke efforts se 'Oudh Kisan Sabha' (1920) bani. [Q6]\n● Baba Ramchandra ek Sanyasi the, jo Fiji mein indentured labourer ki tarah kaam karne ke baad wapas\naaye — Ramcharitmanas ki copy saath rakhte the. Wo Oudh mein Non-cooperation movement ke active\nparticipant the, aur landlords ke against peasants ko organize kiya. [Q7]"," 4. Peasant Movements of the 1930s — A Match List\n● Match: Sahajanand Saraswati → Bihar; Khudai Khidmatgars → North-West Frontier Province (NWFP);\nSwami Ramanand → Hyderabad; Abdul Hamid Khan → Southern Assam. [Q8]\n● 1930s ke decade mein, Swami Sahajanand, Kisan Sabha Movement se closely juday the — unhone\nBihar Kisan Sabha banayi, aur 1936 mein Lucknow mein hui first All India Kisan Conference ke\nPresident bane. [Q9]\n5. The Eka Movement\n● Eka Movement (Oudh, 1921 ke end mein) ka aim tha rent ko cash mein convert karna — issues the\nhigh rents (recorded rates se 50% zyada), Thikedars ka oppression, aur share-rents ki practice.\nMeetings mein ek symbolic religious ritual hota tha jisme kisan promise karte the: recorded rent time par\ndena, evict hone par na jaana, forced labour se inkaar karna, aur Panchayat decisions follow karna. Iski\ngrassroot leadership Madari Pasi jaise low-caste leaders aur chhote Zamindars ne ki. [Q10]\n● Eka Movement Hardoi, Bahraich, Sitapur (Bahraich aur doosri UP ki jagah) ke peasants ne shuru ki thi.\n[Q11]\n6. Swami Sahajanand Saraswati & the Bihar Kisan Sabha\n● Swami Sahajanand Saraswati (1889-1950), ek Sanyasi, farmers' rights activist aur freedom fighter the\n— unhone Bihar Provincial Kisan Sabha found ki (1929 AD mein), aur kisano ki takleef highlight karne\nke liye 'Lok Sangraha' newspaper aur Patna se 'Hunkar' Hindi weekly journal chalaayi. [Q12, Q13, Q14,\nQ15, Q22]\n● Bihar Kisan Sabha se Karyanand Sharma, Rahul Sankrityayan, Panchanan Sharma, Yadunandan\nSharma aur kai doosre communist leaders bhi connected the — unhone Swami Sahajanand ke saath\nmovement ko village level tak pahunchaya, isliye is question ke sabhi options sahi hain. [Q23]\n● Swami Sahajanand Saraswati ne apni mrityu se thodi pehle (1950 mein) 'All India United Kisan Sabha'\nbanayi thi, 'Nationalization of Land and Waterways' ki demand ke saath. [Q24]\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad, Bihar ke Kisan Movement se associate the — wo Constituent Assembly ke\nPresident aur baad mein India ke pehle President bane. [Q26]\n7. The All India Kisan Sabha (1936)\n● 'All India Kisan Congress' (baad mein 'All India Kisan Sabha' rename hui) April 1936 mein Lucknow\nmein founded hui — Swami Sahajanand Saraswati President, aur N.G. Ranga General Secretary bane.\nIndulal Yagnik ki leadership mein ek periodical session bhi shuru ki gayi. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● Lucknow (April 1936) mein hui All India Kisan Sabha ki pehli meeting mein Jawaharlal Nehru ne bhi\naddress kiya tha. [Q25]"," 8. Peasant Leaders — A Match List\n● Match: Bardoli Satyagraha → Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel; Bhartiya Kisan Vidyalaya → N.G. Ranga;\nBengal Praja Party → Fazlul Haq; Bakashat Agitation → Swami Sahajanand Saraswati. [Q27]\n9. The Bardoli Satyagraha — Sardar Patel\n● Bardoli Taluka (Surat district) mein Gandhi ke national level par juday ke baad politicization badhi thi —\nVallabhbhai Patel ne yahan 1928 mein Peasant Movement lead ki, jo 'Bardoli Satyagraha' ke naam se\nfamous hui. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n● Bardoli mein Kisan Movement ki successful leadership ke liye, Bardoli ki mahilaon ki taraf se Mahatma\nGandhi ne Vallabhbhai Patel ko 'Sardar' ki title di. [Q31, Q32]\n10. The Tebhaga Movement\n● 'Tebhaga Peasant Movement' Bengal mein 1946 mein, Bengal Provincial Kisan Sabha ne shuru ki —\nFlood Commission ki recommendations implement karne ke liye, sharecroppers ke landlord ko diye\njaane wale hisse ko 1/2 se ghatakar 1/3 karne ki demand ke saath. [Q33, Q34]\n11. The Bhoodan Movement — Vinoba Bhave\n● Acharya Vinoba Bhave ne 18 April 1951 ko, Pochampalli (Andhra Pradesh, aaj Telangana ke Yadadri\nBhuvanagiri district) se 'Bhoodan Movement' shuru ki — land reform aur agriculture mein institutional\nchange ki koshish thi. Jaya Prakash Narayan ne 1954 mein active politics chhodkar isse join kiya. [Q35,\nQ37]\n● Vinoba Bhave ne 'Sarvodaya Samaj' organize ki thi, non-violent social transformation land reforms ke\nthrough laane ke liye — bade landlords ko unki zameen ka kam se kam 1/6 hissa daan karne ke liye\npersuade kiya jaata tha. 18 April 1951 ko Pochampalli mein, ek Zamindar Ramachandra Reddy ne apni\n100 acre zameen daan karke pehla land donation kiya. [Q36]\n● Vinoba Bhave, Modern India ke great spiritual leaders-reformers mein se ek the — 1940 AD mein\nIndividual Satyagraha ke liye elect hone wale pehle vyakti the. Independence ke baad, unhone Bhoodan\nMovement shuru ki, jiska main objective tha zameen-less farmers ko zameen distribute karna —\nOctober 1951 se 1957 tak unhone 50 million acres zameen daan ke liye gather ki. [Q38]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Peasant Movement and Kisan Sabha Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0227","t":"25 Trade Union and Communist Party","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.25 — TRADE UNION & COMMUNIST PARTY — FULL MIND MAP\n🏭\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Trade Unions — Madras Labour Union & Ahmedabad Textile\n2. The All India Trade Union Congress (AITUC) — Founding & Presidents\n3. M.N. Roy & the Communist International\n4. Kanpur & Meerut Conspiracy Cases\n5. The Revolutionary Phase of the Trade Union Movement\n6. M.N. Roy's Radical Democratic Party & Other Splinter Parties\n7. The Workers and Peasants Party\n1. Early Trade Unions — Madras Labour Union & Ahmedabad Textile\n● India ki pehli Modern Trade Union Organisation 'Labour Union' (Madras Labour Union) 1918 mein B.P.\nWadia aur V. Kalyanasundaram ne banayi — mainly Buckingham aur Carnatic Mills ke textile workers\nisme shaamil the. Uske baad Bombay mein 2, Calcutta mein 1 (Indian Seamen's Union), aur Madras\nmein 4 unions bani. [Q1]\n● 'Ahmedabad Textile Labour Association' Mahatma Gandhi ne 1918 mein found ki thi. [Q2]\n2. The All India Trade Union Congress (AITUC) — Founding & Presidents\n● 'All India Trade Union Congress' (AITUC) 31 October 1920 ko Bombay mein N.M. Joshi ne found ki —\nLala Lajpat Rai iske pehle President, Joseph Baptista Vice President, aur Diwan Chaman Lal Bajaj\nGeneral Secretary bane. Iske formation ka motive tha 1919 ki International Labour Union ki sthapna.\n[Q3, Q4, Q5]\n● AITUC ka pehla session, Bombay mein 1920 mein hua, Lala Lajpat Rai ki presidency mein hua. [Q6, Q7]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne 1929 mein Nagpur mein hui AITUC session ki presidency ki — is session mein\nleftists aur rightists (moderates) ke beech power struggle dikha. N.M. Joshi, V.V. Giri aur B. Shiva Rao ki\nleadership wale moderate section ne split hokar 'Indian Trade Union Federation' banayi. [Q8]\n3. M.N. Roy & the Communist International\n● Communist International 1919 mein Vladimir Lenin ne found ki — M.N. Roy, Lenin ke invitation par\nMoscow gaye aur Communist International ke member banne wale pehle Indian bane. [Q9]\n● October 1920 mein, M.N. Roy ne Abani Mukherjee, Mohd. Ali, Mohd. Shafique, Evelyn Roy Trent, Rosa\nFitingov aur M.P.T. Acharya ke saath, Tashkent mein 'Indian Communist Party' found ki. [Q10]\n4. Kanpur & Meerut Conspiracy Cases"," ● 'Kanpur Conspiracy Case' (1924) Communist leaders ke against thi — M.N. Roy, Muzaffar Ahmed, S.A.\nDange aur Shaukat Usmani jaise leaders ko Emperor ki sovereignty se vanchit karne ki saazish ke\nilzaam mein try kiya gaya. [Q11]\n● 'Meerut Conspiracy Case' (1929-33) ko worldwide publicity mili — 32 labour leaders par charges lage,\naur Albert Einstein, H.G. Wells, Harold Laski aur Roosevelt jaise prominent logo ne isse severely\ncriticize kiya. [Q12]\n5. The Revolutionary Phase of the Trade Union Movement\n● India mein Trade Union Movement ka 'Revolutionary Phase' 1926-1939 ke beech maana jaata hai — is\nmilitant phase mein M.N. Roy, Muzaffar Ahmed aur S.A. Dange jaise leaders active the. [Q13]\n6. M.N. Roy's Radical Democratic Party & Other Splinter Parties\n● M.N. Roy ne 1940 mein 'Radical Democratic Party' found ki. [Q14]\n● Saumyendranath Tagore ne 1934 mein, Communist Party of India (CPI) se alag hokar, 'Revolutionary\nCommunist Party of India' (RCPI) found ki. [Q15]\n7. The Workers and Peasants Party\n● Statement check: 'All India Workers and Peasant Party' ek pan-India organization ki tarah December\n1928 mein bani thi, 1927 mein NAHI (galat statement) — iska purpose Congress ke andar hi kaam\nkarke ise zyada revolutionary banana aur general public ko organize karna tha (sahi statement). [Q16]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Trade Union and Communist Party Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0228","t":"26 Rowlatt Act and Jallianwala Bagh 1919","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.26 — ROWLATT ACT & JALLIANWALA BAGH (1919) — FULL MIND\n⚖️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Rowlatt Act — Origins & Provisions\n2. Rowlatt Satyagraha — Gandhi's First All-India Movement\n3. The Jallianwala Bagh Massacre — Events & Location\n4. Rabindranath Tagore Renounces His Knighthood\n5. Shankaran Nair's Resignation\n6. The Hunter Committee\n7. The Assassination of Michael O'Dwyer\n1. The Rowlatt Act — Origins & Provisions\n● Lord Chelmsford ke Viceroyalty (1916-1921) mein, 1917 mein sedition rokne ke liye Justice Rowlatt ki\nleadership mein ek committee appoint hui — committee ki recommendations par 'Rowlatt Act'\n(Anarchical and Revolutionary Crime Act) March 1919 mein pass hua. [Q1, Q3, Q6, Q7, Q12, Q39]\n● Rowlatt Act ne Government ko unlimited powers di — bina trial ke suspects ko arrest-imprison karne ki.\nIs bill ko us waqt describe kiya jaata tha: 'No Vakil, No Appeal, No Daleel' (na koi wakil, na koi appeal,\nna koi plea). [Q2, Q4]\n● INC ne Rowlatt Act ka virodh isliye kiya kyunki iska maksad individual liberty ko limit karna tha — bina\njury decision ke certain cases try karna, aur bina fair-proper trial ke logo ko detain karna. [Q8]\n2. Rowlatt Satyagraha — Gandhi's First All-India Movement\n● Rowlatt Satyagraha (1919), Gandhiji ka pehla 'All-India level' movement tha — iske pehle wale\nmovements (Champaran 1917, Ahmedabad Mill Workers 1918, Kheda 1918) sirf localized the, lekin\nRowlatt Satyagraha ko society ke sabhi sections ne proactively join kiya. [Q5, Q9, Q10]\n● Rowlatt Act ke against 'No Tax Campaign' shuru karne ka suggestion Swami Shraddhanand ne diya tha\n— non-payment of Lagaan (rent) se movement shuru karne ka idea. [Q11]\n3. The Jallianwala Bagh Massacre — Events & Location\n● Jallianwala Bagh (Amritsar Massacre) 13 April 1919 ko hua — ek badi crowd Punjab ke 2 famous\nleaders Dr. Saifuddin Kitchlew aur Dr. Satyapal ki arrest ke against protest karne ke liye ikattha hui thi,\nkuch log Baisakhi fair attend karne bhi aaye the. Kai villagers ko martial law ke baare mein pata bhi nahi\ntha. Brigadier General Dyer ne area ghera, exit points block kiye, aur crowd par goli chalaayi —\nhazaaron log maare gaye. [Q13, Q14, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● Events ka sahi sequence: Kitchlu-Satyapal ki arrest (9 April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh massacre (13\nApril 1919) → Amritsar Congress Session (December 1919). [Q31]"," ● Lord Chelmsford, Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (1919) ke waqt India ke Viceroy the — unke tenure mein\nGovernment of India Act 1919 (Montague-Chelmsford Reforms, dyarchy introduce ki), Rowlatt Act, aur\nNon-cooperation Movement ki shuruat bhi hui. [Q37]\n● Edwin Montagu (Secretary of State for India) ne Jallianwala Bagh Massacre ko 'Preventive Murder'\nkaha tha. [Q38]\n4. Rabindranath Tagore Renounces His Knighthood\n● Jallianwala Bagh incident ke baad, Rabindranath Tagore ne 30 May 1919 ko apni 'Knighthood' (Sir ki\ntitle) British Government ko wapas kar di — Governor-General ko likhi chitthi mein unhone likha: 'The\ntime has come when badges of honour make our shame glaring in their incongruous context of\nhumiliation.' [Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26, Q30]\n● Assertion-Reason: Tagore ne apni Knighthood renounce ki, Jallianwala Bagh Massacre ke against\nprotest ki tarah — ye sahi Assertion hai. Lekin unhone ye Non-Cooperation Movement ke support mein\nNAHI kiya tha (galat Reason). [Q27]\n5. Shankaran Nair's Resignation\n● Shankaran Nair (Sir Shankar Nair) ne Jallianwala Bagh Massacre ke protest mein Viceroy's Executive\nCouncil ki membership se resign kar diya. [Q28, Q29]\n6. The Hunter Committee\n● Jallianwala Bagh Tragedy ki jaanch ke liye Government ne Lord William Hunter ki leadership mein\n'Disorders Inquiry Committee' banayi — 7 members the (4 British, 3 Indian). Hunter Report ne Dyer ke\nzyadatar decisions ki ninda ki, lekin Punjab mein martial law lagane se agree ki. Dyer ko England bhej\ndiya gaya aur unka command hataya gaya (British Government ne unhe 'Lion of British Empire' kehkar\n'Sword of Honour' bhi di). [Q32]\n● Congress ki taraf se Jallianwala Bagh Massacre par ek 'Inquiry Committee Report' draft karne ki\nzimmedari Mahatma Gandhi ko di gayi thi. [Q36]\n7. The Assassination of Michael O'Dwyer\n● 13 March 1940 ko, London ke Caxton Hall mein, Udham Singh ne Michael O'Dwyer ko goli maar kar\nmaar dala — O'Dwyer Jallianwala Bagh Massacre ke waqt Punjab ke British Lieutenant-Governor the,\njinhone Dyer ke action ko approve kiya tha. Udham Singh ne khud Amritsar ke events witness kiye the.\n[Q33, Q34, Q35]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Rowlatt Act and Jallianwala Bagh 1919 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0229","t":"27 Khilafat Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.27 — KHILAFAT MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n☪️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Founders & Leaders of the Khilafat Movement\n2. Objectives of the Movement\n3. Gandhi's Involvement — President & Motivation\n4. Critics — Jinnah & Malviya\n5. Swami Shraddhanand — The Hindu-Muslim Unity Speech\n6. Congress's Support for the Movement\n7. The Allahabad Conference (1920) — Non-Cooperation\n8. Impact — Aitchison's Remark & the Moplah Rebellion\n1. Founders & Leaders of the Khilafat Movement\n● Khilafat Movement mainly Maulana Muhammad Ali aur Shaukat Ali ('Ali Brothers') ne shuru ki thi —\ndoosre Muslim leaders jaise Hasrat Mohani, Maulana Abul Kalam Azad aur Dr. Hakim Ajmal Khan ne\nunke saath milkar Lucknow mein 'All India Khilafat Committee' banayi.\n Haji Shariatullah, Khilafat\n⚠️\nMovement se NAHI, Faraizi Movement se juday the. [Q1, Q2]\n● Hakim Ajmal Khan ne Khilafat agitation ke dauran, British Government dwara 1908 mein di gayi 'Haziq-\nul-Mulk' title tyaag di thi. [Q8]\n2. Objectives of the Movement\n● Khilafat Movement ke main objectives the: Turkey ke Ottoman Empire ki raksha karna aur Khalifa ko\nunke pad par bane rehne dena — Ottoman Empire ke dismantle hone se Indian Muslims mein gussa\ntha, jisse anti-British feelings ubhri. Muslim society mein reform ya separate electorate ki demand is\nspecific movement ke primary objectives NAHI the. [Q3]\n3. Gandhi's Involvement — President & Motivation\n● Mahatma Gandhi ko 23-24 November 1919 ko Delhi mein hui 'All-India Khilafat Conference' ka\nPresident elect kiya gaya — unhone isse Hindu-Muslim unity ka mauka maana. [Q4]\n● Gandhiji ne Khilafat Movement ko support kiya kyunki wo British ke against Indian Muslims ka support\njeetna chahte the — unhone isse Hindu-Muslim unity ka ek golden opportunity samjha. [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● Khilafat Movement ka ek result tha ki Hindu-Muslim differences kuch samay ke liye kam ho gaye —\nMovement ne unprecedented unity produce ki. Gandhiji ne isse 'ek golden opportunity for unity' kaha\ntha, jo aane wale 100 saal mein dobara nahi milegi. [Q11]\n4. Critics — Jinnah & Malviya"," ● Muhammad Ali Jinnah ne Khilafat issue ko India ki freedom struggle se jodne ka virodh kiya — unhone\nGandhiji ko warn kiya ki wo Muslim religious leaders aur unke followers ki fanaticism ko encourage na\nkarein. Unhone Gandhiji ki Khilafat Movement mein participation ki ninda ki, ye kehkar ki isse religion ko\npolitics mein laaya ja raha hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Pandit Madan Mohan Malviya ne Mahatma Gandhi ki Khilafat Movement ko endorse karne ka virodh\nkiya tha. [Q14]\n5. Swami Shraddhanand — The Hindu-Muslim Unity Speech\n● 4 April 1919 ko, Swami Shraddhanand ne Delhi ki Jama Masjid ke pulpit se, ~30,000 Muslims ke\nsaamne, Hindu-Muslim unity par speech di thi. [Q12]\n6. Congress's Support for the Movement\n● Congress ne Khilafat Movement ko mainly Caliph ki reinstatement ke liye, aur national cause ke liye\nMuslims ki sympathy hasil karne ke liye support kiya. [Q13]\n7. The Allahabad Conference (1920) — Non-Cooperation\n● June 1920 mein, Khilafat Committee ki conference Allahabad (Prayagraj) mein hui — usme Gandhiji ke\nnon-cooperation suggestion ko unanimously accept kiya gaya, aur unhe movement ki leadership\nsambhalne ka request kiya gaya. [Q15]\n8. Impact — Aitchison's Remark & the Moplah Rebellion\n● 'Is instance mein, hum Mohammedans ko Hindus ke against nahi khada kar paaye' — Aitchison ka ye\nremark Khilafat aur Non-Cooperation Movement (1919-22) se related tha — ye British ki Hindu-Muslim\nunity todne mein\n\nअसफलताdikhata hai, is unprecedented unity ke period mein. [Q16]\n● Moplah Rebellion (1921, Kerala) Khilafat Movement ki ek offshoot thi — Khilafat Movement ki meetings\naur Moplah peasants ke meetings merge ho gayi, jisse Hindu landlords aur British ke against ek revolt\nhui. [Q17]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Khilafat Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0230","t":"28 Non Cooperation Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.28 — NON-COOPERATION MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n✊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Launching the Movement — Nagpur/Calcutta Sessions & C.R. Das\n2. The Start of Non-Cooperation (1920)\n3. Causes & Aims\n4. Features & Criticism\n5. Bihar's Prohibition Campaign\n6. Outcomes & Impact\n7. Titles & Sacrifices — Gandhi, Bajaj & C.R. Das\n8. Statements Check — Gandhi's Arrest\n9. Tilak's Death\n10. Regional Leaders — Rahul Sankrityayan, Swami Vidyanand & Rajendra Prasad\n11. The Chauri Chaura Incident\n12. Gandhi's 'Himalayan Blunder' Remark\n13. Boycott of the Prince of Wales\n14. Suspension of the Movement — Bardoli Resolution & Dr. Moonje's Censure\n15. Institutions Founded During the Movement\n16. Tagore's Opposition to Cloth Burning\n17. E.V. Ramaswami Nayakar (Periyar)\n18. Match Lists — Not/Correctly Matched\n19. The Anti-Non-Cooperation Association\n1. Launching the Movement — Nagpur/Calcutta Sessions & C.R. Das\n● September 1920 mein, Congress ki special session Calcutta mein hui, jaha Gandhiji ne Non-\ncooperation resolution propose ki — C.R. Das ne shuru mein iska virodh kiya tha. Lekin December 1920\nke Nagpur annual session mein, khud C.R. Das ne hi ye resolution propose ki. [Q1]\n● Calcutta ki special session (September 1920), jaha Non-cooperation Movement ki resolution pass hui,\nuski presidency Lala Lajpat Rai ne ki. [Q7]\n2. The Start of Non-Cooperation (1920)\n● Gandhiji ne Non-Cooperation Movement 1 August 1920 ko launch ki — India ki azaadi ki ladai mein ye\nCongress ki dwara launch ki gayi pehli aisi movement thi. Western India, Bengal aur North India mein\nisse widespread success mili. [Q2, Q3, Q8]\n● Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-1922), Gandhiji ke dwara lead ki gayi pehli 'Mass Movement' maani\njaati hai — Champaran Movement (1917) unka pehla Satyagraha tha, lekin wo sirf regional (Bihar tak)\ntha. [Q4]\n● Khilafat (Caliphate) ke sawaal par Non-Cooperation Movement 1920 mein shuru hui — Khilafat aur\nPunjab atrocities (Jallianwala Bagh) par discussions ke baad Non-Cooperation ke through Swaraj\nestablish karne ka decision liya gaya. [Q5]\n3. Causes & Aims"," ●\n Trap: 'Salt Law' Non-Cooperation Movement ki wajah NAHI thi — Salt Law ke against 'Salt March'\n⚠️\n(Dandi March) baad mein, 1930 mein hui. Non-Cooperation ki causes thi: Rowlatt Act, Jallianwala Bagh\nMassacre (Punjab atrocities), aur Khilafat issue. [Q6]\n● 1919 ke reforms Indian aspirations poori karne mein fail hue, isliye Congress ne Mahatma Gandhi ki\nleadership mein, Non-Cooperation Movement ke through Swaraj achieve karne ki koshish ki. [Q10]\n● Non-Cooperation Movement ka aim 'ek saal mein Swaraj hasil karna' tha — Gandhiji ne 'Swaraj in a\nyear' ka slogan diya tha. [Q9, Q11]\n4. Features & Criticism\n●\n Trap: M.A. Jinnah ne Non-Cooperation Movement ko support NAHI kiya tha — ye galat statement\n⚠️\nhai. Movement 1 August 1920 ko shuru hui, Swaraj in a year ka aim tha, aur boycotts shaamil the. [Q12]\n● Statement check: Movement mein sirf rich/upper-caste ka participation nahi tha (galat statement) —\nMadras ki Justice Party ne elections boycott NAHI ki, wo system ke andar hi kaam karna prefer karti thi\n(galat statement) — hazaaron students, teachers aur lawyers ne participate kiya (sahi statement). [Q13]\n5. Bihar's Prohibition Campaign\n● Gandhiji ki Non-Cooperation Movement mein alcohol avoid karne ki appeal se Bihar (aur Odisha) ki\ngovernment ko revenue mein bada nuksaan hua — sarkar ne Alexander, Julius Caesar, Napoleon,\nShakespeare jaise famous logo ki list release ki jo alcohol consume karte the, logo ko peene ke liye\nencourage karne ke liye. [Q14]\n6. Outcomes & Impact\n● Non-Cooperation Movement ke result: ye ek mass movement ban gayi, Hindu-Muslim unity ko badhava\nmila, aur British power ka dar khatam hua — lekin isse turant British Government se political\nconcessions NAHI mili, ulta government ne mostly repression (dabav) use kiya. [Q15]\n● 1921-22 ki Non-Cooperation Movement ka main outcome tha — unprecedented Hindu-Muslim unity aur\nmasses ka involvement. [Q43]\n7. Titles & Sacrifices — Gandhi, Bajaj & C.R. Das\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne 1920 mein, Non-Cooperation Movement ke dauran, apna 'Kaiser-i-Hind' medal\nBritish Government ko wapas kar diya. Jamnalal Bajaj ne apni 'Rai Bahadur' title tyaag di. [Q16]\n● Chittaranjan Das (C.R. Das) ne, Motilal Nehru aur Rajendra Prasad jaiso ke saath, Non-Cooperation\nMovement ke dauran apni legal practice chhod di thi. [Q17]\n8. Statements Check — Gandhi's Arrest"," ●\n Trap: Mahatma Gandhi 1921 mein NAHI, 10 March 1922 ko arrest hue the — galat statement.\n⚠️\n(Unhone Chauri-Chaura ki wajah se movement withdraw ki, aur 1916 mein BHU mein pehla major\nspeech diya — ye dono statements sahi hain.) [Q18]\n9. Tilak's Death\n● Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne Non-Cooperation Movement ko support kiya, lekin uska result nahi dekh paye\n— unki mrityu movement ke pehle din, 1 August 1920 ko hi ho gayi thi. [Q19]\n10. Regional Leaders — Rahul Sankrityayan, Swami Vidyanand & Rajendra\nPrasad\n● Rahul Sankrityayan, Chhapra (Bihar) mein 1920 ki Non-Cooperation Movement ke dauran active the.\n[Q20]\n● Swami Vidyanand ne Bihar mein Non-Cooperation Movement ke dauran cultivators (kisano) ki\nleadership ki. [Q35, Q42]\n● Rajendra Prasad (Bihar ke ek pleader) ne Non-Cooperation Movement support karne ke liye apni\nlucrative legal practice chhod di. [Q36]\n● Jai Prakash Narayan ne Patna College sirf apne exams se 20 din pehle chhod diya, movement join\nkarne ke liye. [Q48]\n11. The Chauri Chaura Incident\n● 'Chauri Chaura' incident 4 February 1922 ko, Gorakhpur district (Uttar Pradesh) mein, hua — ek police\nstation ko jala diya gaya. [Q21, Q22, Q23]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne violent Chauri-Chaura incident ki wajah se Non-Cooperation Movement\nsuspend/halt/withdraw kar di — ye movement ko rokne ka major cause tha. [Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● February 2021 mein, Prime Minister Narendra Modi ne 'Chauri Chaura Centenary Celebration'\ninaugurate ki (4 February 2021 ko). [Q28]\n● Chauri-Chaura incident ke waqt Gandhiji Bardoli (Gujarat) mein the — wahan Civil Disobedience\nMovement shuru karne ki tayyari kar rahe the. [Q31]\n● Non-Cooperation Movement 1920 mein launch hui, aur 12 February 1922 ko, Bardoli resolution ke\nbaad, khatam hui. [Q32]\n● Events ka sahi sequence: Police ne goli chalayi → Crowd ne station jala diya → Gandhi ne movement\npostpone kiya → Gandhi arrest hue. [Q34]\n● Events ka sahi sequence: Chauri-Chaura (4 Feb) → Bardoli Resolutions (12 Feb) → Suspension\n(Bardoli mein liya gaya decision). [Q37]\n12. Gandhi's 'Himalayan Blunder' Remark"," ●\n Disputed: Historically, Gandhiji ne 'Himalayan Miscalculation' (Himalayan Blunder) term Rowlatt\n⚠️\nSatyagraha (1919) ke context mein use kiya tha — Nadiad (Gujarat) aur Ahmedabad mein hui hinsa\ndekhne ke baad, jab unhe laga ki log abhi non-violent civil disobedience ke liye ready nahi the. Lekin kai\ncompetitive exams isse Chauri Chaura incident (1922) se jodte hain, kyunki usi se Non-Cooperation\nMovement ka massive withdrawal hua — isi ambiguity ki wajah se ye question disputed maana jaata\nhai. [Q29]\n13. Boycott of the Prince of Wales\n● Non-Cooperation Movement (1921) ke dauran, Gandhiji ne 'Prince of Wales' ke visit ka boycott karne ka\ncall diya tha. [Q30]\n14. Suspension of the Movement — Bardoli Resolution & Dr. Moonje's\nCensure\n● Dr. Moonje ne, Gandhiji dwara Non-Cooperation Movement call-off karne ke against, meeting mein 'vote\nof censure' table ki thi. [Q33]\n● 1923-28 ke beech, Indian politics mein revolutionary activities dobara badhi — 1922 mein Non-\nCooperation Movement ki postponement se bahut log disappoint hue, jisse violent revolutionary\nactivities ka revival hua. [Q38]\n● Assertion-Reason: Gandhiji ne violence (Chauri Chaura) ki wajah se movement postpone ki, C.R. Das\nke virodh ki wajah se NAHI (sahi Assertion, galat Reason connection) — halaki C.R. Das aur Motilal\nNehru ne actually is suspension ka virodh kiya tha (sahi Reason bhi, lekin Assertion ka sahi explanation\nnahi). [Q47]\n15. Institutions Founded During the Movement\n● Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) ke dauran Kashi Vidyapeeth (1921), Gujarat Vidyapeeth (1920),\naur Jamia Millia Islamia (1920) — teeno institutions establish hui. (BHU 1916 mein pehle hi ban chuki\nthi.) [Q41]\n16. Tagore's Opposition to Cloth Burning\n● Rabindranath Tagore ne Mahatma Gandhi ko likha ki foreign clothes jalana 'ruthless waste' (bebaak\nbarbaadi) hai — unhone Non-Cooperation Movement ke dauran foreign cloth jalane ka virodh kiya.\n[Q39, Q40]\n17. E.V. Ramaswami Nayakar (Periyar)\n● Periyar (E.V. Ramaswami) ne Non-Cooperation Movement mein participate kiya tha, aur baad mein\n1925 mein Congress chhod di. [Q44]"," 18. Match Lists — Not/Correctly Matched\n●\n Trap: '1930 – Non-Cooperation Movement' galat match hai — Non-Cooperation Movement 1920\n⚠️\nmein shuru hui, 1930 Civil Disobedience Movement ka saal tha. [Q45]\n● Sahi match: 1931 — Rajguru ki execution (Bhagat Singh, Rajguru aur Sukhdev ko 23 March 1931 ko\nhang kiya gaya). (Non-Cooperation 1920 mein shuru hui, Rowlatt Satyagraha 1919 mein, Lahore\nSession 1929 mein.) [Q46]\n19. The Anti-Non-Cooperation Association\n●\n Disputed: 'Anti-Non-Cooperation Association' bade businessmen jaise Jamnadas Dwarkadas aur\n⚠️\nPurshottamdas Thakurdas ne shuru ki thi — lekin diye gaye options mein exact naam match na hone ki\nwajah se, ye question disputed/deleted maana jaata hai. [Q49]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Non-Cooperation Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0231","t":"29 Formation of Swaraj Party 1923","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.29 — FORMATION OF SWARAJ PARTY (1923) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Reasons for the Formation of the Swaraj Party\n2. C.R. Das & Motilal Nehru — The Founders\n3. Members — Pro-changers vs No-changers\n4. Swaraj Dal in Bihar\n5. Chronology of Events\n6. The Swaraj Party in the Central Legislative Assembly\n1. Reasons for the Formation of the Swaraj Party\n● Government of India Act, 1919 ne Legislative Assemblies establish ki, jinka Congress ne shuru mein\nboycott kiya — lekin Non-Cooperation Movement ki suspension (Chauri Chaura ke baad) ki wajah se\nGaya Session (December 1922) mein Congress mein split ho gayi. C.R. Das aur Motilal Nehru ne\nJanuary 1923 mein Swaraj Party banayi — unka aim tha elections contest karke aur councils mein entry\nkarke government ko andar se kamzor karna ('wreck from within'). [Q1]\n● Swaraj Party, Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) ki failure/withdrawal ke turant baad, 1923 mein\nbanayi gayi thi — Chauri Chaura incident ke baad movement ki achanak suspension se leaders ke\nbeech disappointment badhi. [Q3, Q4]\n● Congress ne 'Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms' (1918) ki ninda ki thi — isse kai moderates Congress\nchhodkar 1918 mein 'Indian National Liberal Federation' bana gaye. Isme prominent leaders the:\nSurendra Nath Banerjee, T.B. Sapru, M.R. Jayakar aur V.S. Srinivas Sastri. [Q17, Q18]\n● 16 December 1922 ko, Madan Mohan Malviya aur Motilal Nehru ne 'Independent Party' launch karne ka\ndecision liya — ye Swaraj Party (jo Motilal Nehru ne baad mein C.R. Das ke saath banayi) se alag thi.\n[Q19]\n2. C.R. Das & Motilal Nehru — The Founders\n● C.R. Das ne 1922 mein Gaya Congress Session ki presidency ki — jab unka legislature mein entry\nkarne ka proposal reject ho gaya, to unhone presidency se resign kar diya aur Swaraj Party banayi. [Q2]\n● Swaraj Party (Swaraj Dal) C.R. Das (President) aur Motilal Nehru (Secretary) ne, Congress ke andar hi,\nbanayi thi — unhe 'Pro-changers' kaha jaata tha, aur party 1 January 1923 ko establish hui — inhone jo\nparty banayi uska naam 'Swaraj Party' tha. [Q5, Q6, Q7, Q9]\n● Chittaranjan Das (C.R. Das), pyaar se 'Deshbandhu' (Friend of the Nation) kehlaate the — wo ek lawyer\nthe jinhone Aurobindo Ghosh ka defense kiya tha, aur Motilal Nehru ke saath Swaraj Party found ki.\n[Q15]\n● Famous slogan 'Swaraj sirf classes ke liye nahi, common logo ke liye bhi hona chahiye' C.R. Das ne\ndiya tha — unhone kaha: 'Swaraj matlab hai logo ki sarkar, logo ke liye.' [Q16]\n3. Members — Pro-changers vs No-changers"," ● Congress 'Pro-changers' (jo legislature mein entry chahte the) aur 'No-changers' (jo boycott chahte the)\nmein baat gayi. Pro-changers (Swarajists): C.R. Das, Motilal Nehru, Vithalbhai Patel, Srinivas Iyengar,\nN.C. Kelkar. No-changers: Vallabhbhai Patel, C. Rajagopalachari, Rajendra Prasad.\n Isliye C.\n⚠️\nRajagopalachari Swaraj Party ke member NAHI the. [Q8, Q10]\n●\n Trap: Dr. Rajendra Prasad, Mahatma Gandhi ke staunch follower aur ek 'No-changer' the — unhone\n⚠️\n\nCouncil entry ka virodh kiya, isliye wo Swaraj Party se associate NAHI the. [Q11]\n4. Swaraj Dal in Bihar\n● Swaraj Dal ki ek branch Bihar mein 1923 mein bani — iski leadership Shri Krishna Singh (Bihar ke\npehle Chief Minister) ne ki. [Q12]\n5. Chronology of Events\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Lucknow Pact (1916 AD) → Jallianwala Massacre (13 April 1919\nAD) → Bal Gangadhar Tilak ki mrityu (1 August 1920 AD) → Swaraj Party ki formation (January 1923\nAD). [Q13]\n6. The Swaraj Party in the Central Legislative Assembly\n● November 1923 elections mein, Swarajists ne 104 mein se 42 elected seats jeeti — Central Legislative\nAssembly mein unhone M.A. Jinnah ki leadership wale 'Independents' aur Liberals ke saath milkar ek\ncoalition banayi, government ko haraane ke liye. [Q14]\n● Vithal Bhai J. Patel (Vitthalbhai Patel), Swaraj Party ke ek co-founder, Central Legislative Assembly ke\npehle Indian Speaker (President) bane — August 1925 mein — ye Swarajists ki ek badi achievement\nthi. [Q20, Q21, Q22]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Formation of Swaraj Party 1923 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0232","t":"30 Simon Commission 1927","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.30 — SIMON COMMISSION (1927) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Simon Commission — Formation & Composition\n2. Reasons for the Boycott\n3. Purpose & Recommendations\n4. Visits to India\n5. Lala Lajpat Rai — Injury & Death\n6. The All Parties Conference (1928)\n7. The Nehru Report\n8. The Independence for India League — Jinnah's Fourteen Points\n1. The Simon Commission — Formation & Composition\n● Government of India Act, 1919 (Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms) mein iska working review karne ke liye\nek 'Statutory Commission' banane ka provision tha — British Conservative Government (Stanley\nBaldwin ke under) ne November 1927 mein 'Simon Commission' appoint ki, Sir John Simon ki\nchairmanship mein, 7 members ke saath. Kisi bhi member ke Indian na hone ki wajah se isse boycott\nkiya gaya aur 'White Commission' bhi kaha gaya. Ye 3 February 1928 ko Bombay pahunchi. [Q1, Q3]\n● Simon Commission ke Chairman, Sir John Simon, 'Liberal Party' se the — Clement Attlee (jo baad mein\nIndia ki independence ke waqt British Prime Minister bane), Labour Party ke member the. [Q6]\n● Viceroy Lord Irwin ki suggestion par Indians ko Simon Commission se bahar rakha gaya tha — isi wajah\nse ise 'White Commission' bhi kaha jaane laga. [Q7]\n2. Reasons for the Boycott\n● Indian logo ne Simon Commission ke against agitation isliye ki kyunki Commission mein koi Indian\nmember nahi tha — ye exclusion India ke apne constitutional future decide karne ke process se unhe\nalag kar diya jaana samjha gaya. [Q2, Q5]\n● Assertion-Reason: Congress aur doosre political groups ne Simon Commission ka boycott isliye kiya\nkyunki isme Indians ko exclude kiya gaya tha (sahi Assertion) — ye Reason directly Assertion ko explain\nkarta hai (sahi Reason bhi). [Q8]\n● Simon Commission ke baare mein sabhi statements sahi hain: Government of India Act 1919 ki review\nke liye banayi gayi, Sir John Simon ne head ki, Federal Government (reconstituted Central Legislature\nke saath) advocate kiya, aur 'White Commission' kehkar strongly oppose ki gayi. [Q9]\n3. Purpose & Recommendations\n● Simon Commission ka purpose tha administrative reforms consider karna — Government of India Act,\n1919 ka working review karke aage constitutional-administrative reforms suggest karna. [Q4]\n● Simon Commission ki key recommendations mein se ek thi — Dyarchy (jo 1919 Act ne introduce ki thi)\nko khatam karke provinces mein 'Responsible Government' establish karna. [Q10]"," 4. Visits to India\n● Simon Commission ne India ko 2 baar visit kiya — pehli visit 3 February se 31 March 1928 tak, aur\ndoosri visit 11 October 1928 se 13 April 1929 tak. [Q11]\n5. Lala Lajpat Rai — Injury & Death\n● 1928 mein, jab Simon Commission Lahore visit ki, Lala Lajpat Rai ne 'Simon! Go Back' banners ke\nsaath ek non-violent protest lead ki — police ne lethal lathi charge ki, jisse wo bahut zyada ghayal ho\ngaye aur November 1928 mein unki mrityu ho gayi. [Q12]\n● Lala Lajpat Rai ko 'Punjab Kesari' (Lion of Punjab) kaha jaata hai. [Q13]\n● Assertion-Reason: Lala Lajpat Rai ne protest lead ki kyunki Commission mein koi Indian representation\nnahi thi (sahi Assertion) — Reason directly is Assertion ko explain karta hai (sahi Reason bhi). [Q14]\n6. The All Parties Conference (1928)\n● February 1928 mein Delhi mein hui 'All Parties Conference' ki presidency Dr. M.A. Ansari ne ki — 29\norganizations ke representatives ne attend kiya, Lord Birkenhead ke challenge ko accept karke ki ek\nIndian constitution draft ki jaaye. [Q22]\n7. The Nehru Report\n● 'Nehru Report' (1928 AD) Motilal Nehru ki leadership wali All-Party Committee ne prepare ki thi —\nJawaharlal Nehru iske Secretary the. Ye challenge ka response tha ki Indians khud apni constitution\nnahi bana sakte. [Q15, Q19]\n● Sir Tej Bahadur Sapru aur M.R. Jayakar — Nehru Report ki committee ke key members the, jinhone\nDominion Status ki demand ki thi. [Q16]\n● Nehru Report ne Complete Independence NAHI, balki 'Dominion Status' recommend ki — saath hi\nseparate electorates ko reject karke 'Joint Electorates' (minorities ke liye reserved seats ke saath) aur\n'Fundamental Rights' ka provision bhi recommend kiya. [Q17]\n8. The Independence for India League — Jinnah's Fourteen Points\n● Jawaharlal Nehru aur Subhash Chandra Bose ne 1928 mein milkar 'Independence for India League'\nbanayi — Nehru Report ki 'Dominion Status' demand ke ulta unhone 'Complete Independence' ki maang\nki. [Q18]\n● M.A. Jinnah ne apne famous '14 Points' March 1929 mein Muslim League session mein propose kiye —\nye ek constitutional reform plan tha, Muslim political rights ki raksha ke liye, mainly Nehru Report ke\nagainst protest ki tarah. [Q20]"," ● Congress ke radical wing (Jawaharlal Nehru, Subhash Chandra Bose ki leadership mein) ne Nehru\nReport (jo Dominion Status demand karti thi) ka virodh karke 'Independence for India League' banayi,\nPurna Swaraj push karne ke liye. [Q21]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Simon Commission 1927 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0233","t":"31 Lahore Session 1929 Complete Independence","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.31 — LAHORE SESSION (1929) — COMPLETE INDEPENDENCE — FULL MIND\n🇮🇳\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The First Proposal — Hasrat Mohani at Ahmedabad (1921)\n2. The Lahore Session (1929) — Jawaharlal Nehru's Presidency\n3. The Flag Hoisting on the Ravi\n4. Purna Swaraj Day — 26 January 1930\n5. Significance of the Lahore Session\n6. Resolutions of the Lahore Session\n7. The 1927 Madras Session — A Comparison\n1. The First Proposal — Hasrat Mohani at Ahmedabad (1921)\n● Maulana Hasrat Mohani ne sabse pehle 1921 ke Ahmedabad Session mein propose kiya tha ki 'Swaraj'\nko 'Complete Independence' (poori tarah foreign control se azaad) ki tarah define kiya jaana chahiye —\nC.R. Das is session ke elected President the, lekin jail mein hone ki wajah se Hakim Ajmal Khan ne\npresidency ki. [Q1, Q2]\n2. The Lahore Session (1929) — Jawaharlal Nehru's Presidency\n● Congress ne pehli baar December 1929 ke historic Lahore Session mein India ki complete\nindependence ka proposal pass kiya — Jawaharlal Nehru ki chairmanship mein hui, aur 'Complete\nIndependence Resolution' isi session mein pass hui. [Q3, Q4, Q6]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru, Lahore Session (1929) ke President the — unhone hi Congress ka lakshya 'Purna\nSwarajya' (Complete Independence) declare kiya. [Q8, Q9, Q15, Q17, Q18, Q19]\n● Lahore Session (1929), Jawaharlal Nehru ki INC President ki tarah pehli presidency thi — isi session\nmein Complete Independence ka proposal pass hua. [Q13]\n3. The Flag Hoisting on the Ravi\n● 31 December 1929 ki midnight ko, Jawaharlal Nehru ne Ravi river ke kinare, naya adopt kiya gaya\ntricolour flag hoist kiya. [Q10, Q11, Q12]\n4. Purna Swaraj Day — 26 January 1930\n● Lahore Session (1929) mein Purna-Swaraj proposal pass hone ke baad, decide kiya gaya ki 26 January\n1930 ko 'Purna Swaraj Day' celebrate kiya jaayega — ye practice 1947 tak har saal continue hui. [Q5,\nQ7]"," 5. Significance of the Lahore Session\n● Lahore Session (1929) ki significance thi Poorna Swaraj (Complete Independence) ko Congress ka goal\nki tarah adopt karna —\n Congress mein rift 1916 ke Lucknow Session mein resolve ho chuki thi, aur\n⚠️\n'Two-Nation Theory' is session ke resolutions ka hissa NAHI thi. [Q14, Q16]\n6. Resolutions of the Lahore Session\n● Lahore Session (1929) ke resolutions mein shaamil the: Round Table Conference ko reject karna,\nDominion Status ko tyaagna, Swaraj ko Complete Independence ki tarah define karna, aur Civil\nDisobedience Movement launch karne ki tayyari.\n 'Abolition of Untouchability' is proposal ka hissa\n⚠️\nNAHI thi. [Q20]\n● 'Poorna Swaraj Resolution' Jawaharlal Nehru ne prepare aur present ki thi — Lahore Session mein\nunhone kaha: 'Hamare liye independence ka matlab hai complete independence.' [Q22]\n7. The 1927 Madras Session — A Comparison\n●\n 1927 ke Madras Session ki presidency Dr. M.A. Ansari ne ki thi — lekin 'Purna Swaraj' resolution is\n⚠️\nsession mein NAHI, 1929 ke Lahore Session mein adopt hui thi. [Q21]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lahore Session 1929 Complete Independence Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0234","t":"32 Civil Disobedience Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.32 — CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🧂\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Authorization & Leadership — The Lahore Session\n2. The Dandi March — Route & Details\n3. Participation — Provinces & Women\n4. Chronology of Events\n5. Post-Arrest Leadership & the Dharsana Raid\n6. Vinoba Bhave's First Arrest\n7. The Vedaranyam March — C. Rajagopalachari\n8. Khudai Khidmatgars (Red Shirts) — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan\n9. The Peshawar Incident — Garhwal Regiment\n10. Regional Movements — Manipur & Bihar\n11. Aftermath — Constructive Programmes\n12. Women Freedom Fighters\n1. Authorization & Leadership — The Lahore Session\n● 1929 ke Lahore Session mein, Congress Working Committee ko Civil Disobedience Movement ka\nprogramme launch karne ki authorization di gayi — February 1930 mein, Sabarmati Ashram mein hui\nWorking Committee ki doosri meeting mein, Mahatma Gandhi ko movement lead karne ka zimma diya\ngaya. [Q1]\n2. The Dandi March — Route & Details\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne famous 'Dandi March' 12 March 1930 ko, Sabarmati Ashram se, apne trusted\nvolunteers ke saath shuru ki — wo Dandi (coastal village) tak, 241 miles, 24 din mein paidal chale. [Q2,\nQ4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q14, Q17, Q24]\n● 6 April 1930 ko, Gandhiji ne samundar ka paani ubalkar Salt Law violate ki — isse Civil Disobedience\nMovement ki formally shuruat mani jaati hai. [Q3, Q8, Q13, Q16, Q19]\n● Dandi March 'Salt Law' todne ke liye shuru ki gayi thi. [Q15]\n● Assertion-Reason: Salt agitation Mahatma Gandhi ne 1930 mein shuru ki (sahi Assertion) — lekin unka\nobjective 'salt free karna' nahi tha, balki Salt Tax aur government ka monopoly abolish karna tha (galat\nReason). [Q20]\n● 'Main is Right vs Might ki ladai mein world sympathy chahta hoon' — ye statement Mahatma Gandhi ne\n5 April 1930 ko, Dandi village mein, journalists ko address karte hue diya. [Q22]\n●\n Trap: Statement 'Mahatma Gandhi ne seashore par salt prepare ki' galat mana jaata hai —\n⚠️\ntechnically unhone samundar ka paani ubaala, lekin unhone sirf ek mutthi salt uthai thi (violation ki\nsymbolic act), 'prepare' (bade paimane par manufacture) nahi ki. [Q23]\n3. Participation — Provinces & Women"," ● Gandhiji ki Dandi March mein sabse zyada Satyagrahi Gujarat se the (32) — Maharashtra (13), UP (8),\nKachh (6), Kerala (4), Punjab (3), Rajputana (3) waghera. [Q9]\n● Salt Satyagraha ka ultimate goal tha: salt law todna, government ki power kam karna, aur salt laws\nrepeal karne ke liye pressure banana — sabhi objectives ek saath the. [Q10]\n● Sarojini Naidu, Rajkumari Amrit Kaur aur Kamladevi Chattopadhyaya — sabhi Salt Satyagraha mein\nparticipate hui — women ne Civil Disobedience Movement mein leading role play kiya. Ye movement\nwomen participation ke liye sabse zyada jaana jaata hai. [Q11, Q12]\n4. Chronology of Events\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Simon Commission ka aana (3 February 1928) → Dandi March (12\nMarch 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Quit India Movement (9 August 1942). [Q18]\n5. Post-Arrest Leadership & the Dharsana Raid\n● Statement check: Gandhiji ko 6 April 1930 ko Salt Law violate karne ke liye arrest kiya gaya tha (galat\nstatement — ve baad mein arrest hue) — Madan Mohan Malviya, Devadas Gandhi, K.M. Munsi jaiso ko\nconvict kiya gaya (sahi statement). [Q21]\n● Salt Satyagraha ke dauran Gandhiji ki arrest ke baad, Abbas Taiyabji ne movement ki leadership\nsambhali — Gandhiji Sholapur mein arrest hue the. [Q25]\n● Jab Congress volunteers ne Dharsana Salt Depot par raid ki (21 May 1930, Sarojini Naidu ki leadership\nmein), Mahatma Gandhi Yerawada Jail mein the — unhe 5 May 1930 ko arrest kiya gaya tha. [Q26]\n● American journalist Webb Miller, Dandi March ke dauran Gandhiji ke saath Sabarmati Ashram mein\nruke the — unhone Dharsana mein police ke atrocities ki eyewitness reporting ki, jo world-wide famous\nhui. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n6. Vinoba Bhave's First Arrest\n● Acharya Vinoba Bhave ko pehli baar 1930 mein, Civil Disobedience Movement mein participate karne\nke liye arrest kiya gaya. [Q27]\n7. The Vedaranyam March — C. Rajagopalachari\n● C. Rajagopalachari ne April 1930 mein, Tanjore coast par, Salt Law todne ke liye ek march organize ki\n— 'Vedaranyam March' Trichinopoly se shuru hokar Vedaranyam mein khatam hui. [Q31]\n8. Khudai Khidmatgars (Red Shirts) — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan"," ● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan (Frontier Gandhi) ne 1929 mein 'Khudai Khidmatgar' (Red Shirts) organize ki\n— iska aim tha Pathan regional nationalist unity aur colonialism ke against struggle, non-violent tareeke\nse Britishers ko bhagana. [Q32, Q33, Q35]\n● 'Lal Kurti' (Red Shirt) Movement ki leadership Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan ne ki thi. [Q34]\n9. The Peshawar Incident — Garhwal Regiment\n● Chandra Singh Garhwali ki leadership mein, Garhwal Rifles ke soldiers ne Civil Disobedience\nMovement ke dauran, Peshawar mein unarmed crowd par goli chalaane se mana kar diya — 'Peshawar\nIncident' (1930) ke naam se famous. [Q36, Q37]\n10. Regional Movements — Manipur & Bihar\n● 'Jiatrang Movement' Manipur mein shuru hui, Naga tribal woman Rani Gaidinliu ki leadership mein, Civil\nDisobedience Movement ke dauran. [Q38]\n● Begusarai (Bihar) mein 'Chaukidari Tax' ke against agitation, Civil Disobedience Movement ka hissa thi.\n[Q39]\n● Bhagalpur (Bihar) ke Bihpur mein Salt Satyagraha ki leadership Mahadev Lal Sarraf ne ki. [Q40]\n● Bihar mein Salt Satyagraha ke dauran, log salt banaane ke alawa 'Chaukidari Tax' ka bhi virodh karte\nthe. [Q41]\n11. Aftermath — Constructive Programmes\n● Civil Disobedience Movement ki failure ke baad, Gandhiji ne Constructive Programmes ko mahatva diya\n— 'Harijanothan' (Harijans ka uplift) jaisi initiatives, aur 1932 mein 'All India Anti-Untouchability League'\nbhi found ki. [Q42]\n12. Women Freedom Fighters\n● Dr. Radhabai ko 13 June 1932 ko, Second Civil Disobedience Movement mein procession lead karte\nwaqt, arrest kiya gaya tha. [Q43]\n● Prabhavati Devi, Patna se freedom fighter thi. [Q44]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Civil Disobedience Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0235","t":"33 Gandhi Irwin Pact","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.33 — GANDHI-IRWIN PACT — FULL MIND MAP\n🤝\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Pact — Date & Purpose\n2. Terms of the Pact\n3. Mediators — Tej Bahadur Sapru & M.R. Jayakar\n4. 'The Two Mahatmas' & Critics\n1. The Pact — Date & Purpose\n● 'Gandhi-Irwin Pact' 5 March 1931 ko, Mahatma Gandhi aur Viceroy Lord Irwin ke beech sign hua tha —\nSecond Round Table Conference (London) se pehle. Key conditions the: Civil Disobedience Movement\ndiscontinue karna aur bina violence charge wale prisoners ko release karna. [Q1, Q4, Q5]\n● Gandhi-Irwin Pact ka main purpose tha Congress ki participation Second Round Table Conference mein\naasan banana — Congress ne pehli conference boycott ki thi, jisse wo useless (futile) ho gayi thi. [Q2]\n● Second Round Table Conference (London) Gandhi-Irwin Pact ke background mein hui — is pact ne\nCongress ki participation ka rasta khola. [Q6]\n2. Terms of the Pact\n● Gandhiji Second Round Table Conference mein participate karne ke liye raazi hue aur Civil\nDisobedience Movement waapas le li. Viceroy ne ordinances withdraw karne aur non-violent prisoners\nrelease karne ke liye sehmati di.\n Lekin police excesses ki enquiry karne ka suggestion Lord Irwin ne\n⚠️\nreject kar diya. [Q3]\n● Gandhi-Irwin Pact mein 'Civil Disobedience Movement' ko adjourn (discontinue) karne ka proposal tha.\n[Q7]\n3. Mediators — Tej Bahadur Sapru & M.R. Jayakar\n● Gandhi-Irwin Pact ki signing mein Tej Bahadur Sapru aur M.R. Jayakar ne important role play kiya —\ndono ne Gandhi aur Irwin ke beech conversation facilitate ki. [Q8, Q9]\n4. 'The Two Mahatmas' & Critics\n● Sarojini Naidu ne Gandhi aur Irwin ko 'The Two Mahatmas' kaha tha, is pact ke context mein. [Q10]\n● Alan Campbell Johnson (Irwin ke biographer) ne Gandhi-Irwin Pact mein Mahatma Gandhi ke gains ko\n'Consolation Prizes' (dilasa denay wale inaam) kaha tha. [Q11]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Gandhi-Irwin Pact Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0236","t":"34 Karachi Session of Congress 1931","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.34 — KARACHI SESSION OF CONGRESS (1931) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Karachi Session (1931) — Presidency, Resolutions & Significance\n2. Chronology Around the Karachi Session\n3. Broader Chronology of Modern Indian History\n1. The Karachi Session (1931) — Presidency, Resolutions & Significance\n● Karachi Session (29-31 March 1931 AD) Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ki leadership mein hui — main\nagenda tha Gandhi-Irwin Pact ko approve karna. Congress ne pehli baar 'Fundamental Rights' aur\n'National Economic Programme' se related resolutions pass ki. Gandhiji ne kaha tha: 'Gandhi mar sakta\nhai, lekin Gandhism nahi.' [Q1]\n● Fundamental Rights aur National Economic Programmes ki resolution Jawaharlal Nehru ne draft ki thi\n— M.N. Roy ne unki madad ki. [Q2]\n● Fundamental Rights se related resolutions pehli baar Karachi Session (1931) mein pass hui. [Q3]\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne Karachi Session (1931) ko Mahatma Gandhi ki popularity aur prestige ka\n'pinnacle' (chotti) mana tha. [Q4]\n2. Chronology Around the Karachi Session\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Bhagat Singh ki execution (23\nMarch 1931) → Karachi Session (29-31 March 1931) → Second Round Table Conference (7 September\n1931). [Q5]\n● Events ka sahi chronological order: Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Rajguru ki execution (23\nMarch 1931) → Karachi Session (29 March 1931). [Q6]\n● India ki freedom struggle se juday events ka correct sequence establish karna important hai — Gandhi-\nIrwin Pact, Bhagat Singh-Rajguru-Sukhdev ki execution, aur Karachi Session — sab March 1931 mein,\nbahut close saath hue events the. [Q7]\n3. Broader Chronology of Modern Indian History\n● Modern Indian history ka sahi chronological order: Morley-Minto Reforms (Indian Council Act, 1909) →\nJallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → August Offer (1940).\n[Q8]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Karachi Session of Congress 1931 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0237","t":"35 Round Table Conference","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.35 — ROUND TABLE CONFERENCE — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The First Round Table Conference (1930-31) — Participants & Absence of Congress\n2. The Second Round Table Conference — Gandhi's Sole Representation\n3. Gandhi's Journey & Stay in London\n4. The Failure of the Second Round Table Conference\n5. Participants in All Three Conferences\n6. Nature of the Conferences — Three Sessions of One\n7. The Third Round Table Conference (1932)\n8. Statements — Ambedkar's Demand, Poona Pact & Congress Boycott\n1. The First Round Table Conference (1930-31) — Participants & Absence of\nCongress\n● First Round Table Conference November 1930 se January 1931 tak London mein hui — Congress ne\nboycott kiya, lekin 89 Indian representatives ne participate kiya, jinme Maulana Muhammad Ali,\nMuhammad Shafi, Aga Khan-III, Fazlul Haq, Jinnah, B.R. Ambedkar aur Tej Bahadur Sapru shaamil the.\n[Q1, Q4]\n●\n Trap: 'Congress delegation ne First Round Table Conference attend ki' — ye statement GALAT hai,\n⚠️\nkyunki Indian National Congress ne ise poori tarah boycott kiya tha. Conference 1930 mein London\nmein Simon Commission report discuss karne ke liye hui thi. [Q2]\n● K.T. Paul ne First Round Table Conference mein Indian Christians ka representation kiya tha —\nconference ki chairmanship British PM Ramsay MacDonald ne ki. [Q3]\n2. The Second Round Table Conference — Gandhi's Sole Representation\n● Second Round Table Conference (1931) mein Mahatma Gandhi, Congress ke sole official\nrepresentative the — Sarojini Naidu aur Madan Mohan Malviya (independent ki tarah) bhi participate\nhue. [Q5, Q8, Q9, Q11]\n●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru ne Second Round Table Conference mein participate NAHI kiya —\n⚠️\nMahadev Desai, Pyarelal Nayyar aur Madan Mohan Malviya present the. [Q6]\n●\n Trap: Dr. Rajendra Prasad ne Second Round Table Conference mein participate NAHI kiya —\n⚠️\nGandhi, Sarojini Naidu aur Malviya participants the. [Q7]\n● Assertion-Reason: Statement galat hai ki Nehru ne Congress ka representation kiya — actually\nMahatma Gandhi ne Congress represent ki (Assertion galat). Gandhi-Irwin Pact mein Congress ki\nRound Table Conference participation ki condition thi (Reason sahi hai). [Q10]\n● Indian National Congress ne pehli baar Second Round Table Conference mein hi represent kiya — sirf\nyehi conference thi jisme unhone participate kiya. [Q14, Q22]\n3. Gandhi's Journey & Stay in London"," ● Mahatma Gandhi, Second Round Table Conference mein participate karne ke liye Bombay se 'S.S.\nRajputana' ship se London gaye the. [Q13]\n● London mein, Second Round Table Conference ke dauran, Mahatma Gandhi 'Kingsley Hall' mein rukte\nthe. [Q12]\n4. The Failure of the Second Round Table Conference\n● Gandhiji December 1931 mein London se khaali haath (empty-handed) India wapas aaye — Second\nRound Table Conference ki failure ke baad. [Q15]\n● Second Round Table Conference 'Communal Delegations' (Communal Award) ke issue par completely\nfail ho gayi — B.R. Ambedkar ne depressed classes ke liye separate electorates ki demand ki, jise\nGandhi ne reject kiya. [Q16]\n5. Participants in All Three Conferences\n●\n Disputed: Kaun sa Indian teeno Round Table Conferences mein participate hua — technically Dr.\n⚠️\nB.R. Ambedkar aur Tej Bahadur Sapru, dono ne teeno conferences mein participate kiya, isliye ye\nquestion multiple-correct/disputed maana jaata hai. [Q17]\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar teeno Round Table Conferences mein participate hue. [Q18, Q19, Q20]\n6. Nature of the Conferences — Three Sessions of One\n● 1930-32 ke beech, London mein Indian aur British political leaders ki meeting ko 'Round Table\nConference' kehte hain — ideally ye ek hi Conference ki 3 sessions thi, alag-alag 3 conferences NAHI.\nMain objective tha Simon Commission Report discuss karna. [Q21]\n7. The Third Round Table Conference (1932)\n● Third Round Table Conference 17 November se 24 December 1932 tak hui. [Q23]\n● Indian National Congress ne First aur Third — dono Round Table Conferences mein participate NAHI\nkiya (isliye 'more than one option sahi hai' — A aur C dono). [Q24]\n8. Statements — Ambedkar's Demand, Poona Pact & Congress Boycott\n● Statement check: Ambedkar ne First Conference mein separate electorates ki demand ki (sahi). Poona\nPact ne local bodies/civil services mein representation di (sahi). Congress ne Third Conference boycott\nki (sahi) — teeno statements sahi hain. [Q25]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Round Table Conference Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0238","t":"36 Communal Award and Poona Pact 1932","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.36 — COMMUNAL AWARD & POONA PACT (1932) — FULL MIND MAP\n⚖️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Communal Award — Announcement & Provisions\n2. Gandhi's Fast Unto Death\n3. Seats — Communal Award vs Poona Pact\n4. The Poona Pact — Purpose & Effect\n5. The Poona Pact — Signatories\n6. Harijan Sevak Sangh — Founders & Presidents\n7. The All India Depressed Classes League\n8. Ambedkar's Criticism of Gandhi\n1. The Communal Award — Announcement & Provisions\n● British PM Ramsay MacDonald ne 16 August 1932 ko 'Communal Award' declare ki thi — Second\nRound Table Conference mein depressed classes aur alag-alag communities ke liye separate\nelectorates par consensus na banne ki wajah se. [Q1]\n● August 1932 mein, Ramsay MacDonald ke Communal Tribunal ne pehli baar 'Untouchables' (depressed\nclasses) ke liye ek separate electoral group banayi — Muslims aur Sikhs pehle se hi minority ki tarah\nrecognize the. [Q2]\n● Assertion-Reason: Communal Award, Ramsay MacDonald ne 16 August 1932 ko announce ki thi (sahi\nAssertion) — isme Muslims, Sikhs, Indian Christians, Anglo-Indians, Europeans aur Dalits ke liye\nseparate electorates ka provision tha (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q3]\n●\n Trap: Communal Award ne Buddhists ko separate electorates/reserved seats NAHI di thi —\n⚠️\nMuslims, Sikhs, Depressed Castes, Indian Christians aur Anglo-Indians ko di gayi thi. [Q4]\n2. Gandhi's Fast Unto Death\n● 20 September 1932 ko, Mahatma Gandhi ne Yerawada Jail mein apna pehla 'Fast unto Death' shuru\nkiya — Communal Award ke against protest karne ke liye. Ye 24 September 1932 ko Poona Pact ke\nthrough khatam hua. [Q5, Q6]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne 1932 mein fast unto death isliye ki kyunki Ramsay MacDonald ne 'Communal\nAward' announce ki thi. [Q7]\n3. Seats — Communal Award vs Poona Pact\n● Communal Award mein depressed classes ke liye 71 reserved seats thi — Poona Pact ke through ye\nbadhkar 147/148 ho gayi. [Q8]\n4. The Poona Pact — Purpose & Effect"," ● Poona Pact 'Depressed Classes' se related tha — iska purpose tha untouchables ko Hindu electorate\nke andar hi representation dena, alag electorate ke bajaye. [Q9, Q10]\n● Assertion-Reason: Poona Pact ne Communal Award ka purpose defeat kar diya (sahi Assertion) —\nkyunki Communal Award depressed classes ko Hindu electorate se alag karna chahti thi, lekin Poona\nPact ne Joint Electorate retain karte hue reserved seats di, jisse Assertion sahi saabit hoti hai (sahi\nReason bhi). [Q11]\n● Communal Award ke announcement ke baad, Poona Pact hi implement ki gayi — separate electorates\nke issue ko resolve karne ke liye. [Q14]\n5. The Poona Pact — Signatories\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar aur Mahatma Gandhi ke beech hue pact ko 'Poona Pact' kehte hain. [Q12]\n●\n Disputed: Technically, Poona Pact Madan Mohan Malviya (Hindus ka representation karte hue) aur\n⚠️\nDr. B.R. Ambedkar (Depressed Classes representing) ke beech sign hua tha — Gandhi ne khud is\ndocument par sign NAHI kiya, halaki wo unke followers aur Ambedkar ke beech ka pact tha, isliye ye\nquestion factually nuanced/disputed mana jaata hai. [Q13]\n●\n Trap: M.K. Gandhi ne 1932 ke historical Poona Pact par sign NAHI kiya tha — isse B.R. Ambedkar,\n⚠️\nMadan Mohan Malviya aur C. Rajagopalachari (unki taraf se present) ne sign kiya. [Q15]\n6. Harijan Sevak Sangh — Founders & Presidents\n● Poona Pact (1932) ke baad, M.K. Gandhi ne 'Harijan Sevak Sangh' (originally 'All India Anti-\nUntouchability League' naam se) found ki — Ghanshyam Das Birla iske pehle President bane. Gandhi\nne 'Harijan' naam ki weekly magazine bhi publish ki. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● 'Harijan Sevak Sangh' ka purana naam 'All India Anti-Untouchability League' tha — 30 September 1932\nko founded hua. [Q22]\n7. The All India Depressed Classes League\n● Babu Jagjivan Ram ne 'All India Depressed Classes League' establish ki — (note: 'All India Scheduled\nCaste Federation' B.R. Ambedkar ne banayi thi, ye alag organization thi). [Q23]\n8. Ambedkar's Criticism of Gandhi\n● 'Mahatma Gandhi, ek fleeting phantom ki tarah, dust (dhool) uthaate hain lekin level nahi' — ye\nstatement Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne, Mumbai mein Gandhi ke saath ek baatcheet ke dauran, 14 August\n1931 ko diya tha — ye dono ke beech depressed classes ki situation par m\n\nतभेदreflect karta hai. [Q24]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Communal Award and Poona Pact 1932 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0239","t":"37 Congress Socialist Party 1934","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.37 — CONGRESS SOCIALIST PARTY (1934) — FULL MIND MAP\n🚩\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Formation — Founders, Date & Place\n2. Ideology & Policy Statements\n3. The Bihar Socialist Party (1931)\n4. Jayaprakash Narayan — 'Loknayak'\n5. The Bombay Manifesto (1936)\n1. Formation — Founders, Date & Place\n● 'Congress Socialist Party' May 1934 mein, Patna mein, ek Congress Committee meeting ke dauran\nestablish hui — October 1934 mein Bombay mein party ki policies aur systems decide hui. [Q1, Q2]\n● Statement check: Party May 1934 (January NAHI) mein, Patna mein banayi gayi. Jayaprakash Narayan\nGeneral Secretary the, Acharya Narendra Dev President — Jawaharlal Nehru is party mein formally\nkabhi join NAHI hue, halaki unki socialist leanings thi. [Q3]\n● Congress Socialist Party, Jayaprakash Narayan aur Acharya Narendra Dev ne October 1934 mein\nbanayi thi — Jayaprakash Narayan is party se juday the. [Q5, Q6, Q8, Q9]\n● Jaya Prakash Narayan, Patna mein 1934 mein hui 'All India Congress Socialist Party' meeting ke\nConvenor the — unhe General Secretary banaya gaya, aur Acharya Narendra Dev President the. [Q7]\n2. Ideology & Policy Statements\n● Congress Socialist Party (CSP) 'decentralized socialism' advocate karti thi, 'dictatorship of the\nproletariat' ki NAHI. Wo separate electorates ki bhi wakalat nahi karte the, ulta class solidarity ke\nthrough communal divisions ko paar karna chahte the — trade unions aur farmers ke liye economic\npower par unka focus tha, tax evasion primary policy NAHI thi. [Q4]\n3. The Bihar Socialist Party (1931)\n● Phulan Prasad Varma ne 1931 mein 'Bihar Socialist Party' found ki thi — Jaya Prakash Narayan,\nGangasharan Sinha, Rambraksh Benipuri aur Ramanand Mishra is party se associate the. [Q10, Q11,\nQ12]\n4. Jayaprakash Narayan — 'Loknayak'\n● Jayaprakash Narayan ko 'Loknayak' (People's Leader) ki tarah jaana jaata hai — unhone 1974 mein\n'Sampoorna Kranti' (Total Revolution) declare ki thi. [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n● 'Jay Prakash Diwas' (Jaya Prakash Day) April 1946 AD mein manaya gaya tha — unhe jail se release\nkarwane ki demand ke saath. [Q16]"," 5. The Bombay Manifesto (1936)\n● Statement check: 'Bombay Manifesto' (1936) 21 businessmen ne sign ki thi — Nehru ke socialist ideas\nke preaching ka virodh karne ke liye (sahi statement 1). Ise business community ne bahut support kiya\n(sahi statement 2) — dono statements sahi hain. [Q17]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Congress Socialist Party 1934 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0240","t":"38 Provincial Election and Formation of Cabinet 1937","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.38 — PROVINCIAL ELECTION & FORMATION OF CABINET (1937) — FULL\n🗳️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Government of India Act, 1935 & the 1937 Elections\n2. Provinces Where Congress Won (or Didn't Win) a Majority\n3. Number of Ministries Formed\n4. Tenure & Resignation of Congress Ministries\n5. Bihar's Ministry — Shri Krishna Singh's Resignation\n6. Congress Policy — Abolishing Land Ownership\n7. UP Ministry — Portfolio Allocation\n8. Reports on Muslim Grievances in Congress-Administered Provinces\n9. The First Governor of Bihar\n1. The Government of India Act, 1935 & the 1937 Elections\n● Provincial Governments 'Government of India Act, 1935' ke under constitute hui — is Act ke basis par\nelections February 1937 mein announce aur hold hui. [Q2]\n2. Provinces Where Congress Won (or Didn't Win) a Majority\n● Congress ko 1937 ke Provincial Legislature elections mein Punjab, Bengal aur Sindh mein full majority\nNAHI mili — 5 provinces (Madras, Bihar, Central Provinces & Berar, United Province, Orissa) mein full\nmajority mili. [Q1]\n●\n Trap: Bengal mein Congress ne absolute majority NAHI hasil ki — Madras, Bihar aur Orissa mein\n⚠️\nhasil ki thi. [Q3]\n● 1937 elections mein, Congress ne 5 provinces mein clear majority hasil ki: Madras, Bihar, Central\nProvinces & Berar, United Provinces, aur Orissa. [Q4]\n● Indian Congress 8 provinces mein powerful ban kar ubhri — lekin Bengal aur Punjab (aur Sindh) mein\nministry formation NAHI ki, jabki Central Provinces aur Orissa mein ministries banayi. [Q5]\n●\n Disputed: 1936-37 ke general election mein, Congress Bombay AUR Assam — dono mein absolute\n⚠️\nmajority nahi paayi (Bombay mein 175 mein se 86 seats — single largest party lekin majority nahi), isliye\nye question dono answers accept karta hai. [Q6]\n● 1937 elections ke baad, Congress ne Bengal mein ministry formation NAHI ki — Bihar, Madras aur\nOrissa mein ministries banayi. [Q7]\n● Congress ne 'Government of India Act, 1935' ke under, Punjab mein ministry formation NAHI ki thi —\nsirf Bengal, Punjab aur Sindh mein enough support nahi mila. [Q9]\n3. Number of Ministries Formed\n●\n Disputed: July 1937 mein, Congress ne shuru mein 6 provinces (Bombay, United Province, Central\n⚠️\nProvince, Orissa, Bihar, Madras) mein government banayi — baad mein NWFP aur Assam mein bhi"," coalition governments banayi, isliye 'kitni provinces mein' wala answer initial vs total ke hisaab se\ndisputed hai. [Q8]\n4. Tenure & Resignation of Congress Ministries\n● 1937 ke elections ke baad, Government of India Act 1935 ke under bani Congress ministries ka tenure\n28 mahine tha — 22 October 1939 ko unhone resign kar diya, kyunki bina consultation ke Indians ko\nWWII mein shaamil kiya gaya tha. [Q10, Q11]\n● Muslim League ne Congress ministries ke resignation ke baad, 22 December 1939 ko 'Day of\nDeliverance' celebrate ki — Jinnah ne Indian Muslims ko celebrate karne ka call diya. [Q12]\n5. Bihar's Ministry — Shri Krishna Singh's Resignation\n● Shri Krishna Singh ki elected Bihar government February 1938 mein resign hui — political prisoners ke\nrelease ki demand ke saath Governor par pressure banane ke liye. Baad mein Governor ne demand\nmaan li, aur ministry office mein wapas aayi. [Q13]\n6. Congress Policy — Abolishing Land Ownership\n● 1937 ki Congress Working Committee ne land ownership abolish karne ki policy adopt ki — United\nProvinces aur Bihar mein Congress governments ne tenancy bills pass kiye. [Q14]\n7. UP Ministry — Portfolio Allocation\n● 1937 ke election ke baad UP mein bani ministry mein, Rafi Ahmed Kidwai ko Finance department mila\n— Govind Ballabh Pant Premier (Prime Minister) the, aur Kailash Nath Katju Law aur Justice Minister\nthe. [Q15]\n8. Reports on Muslim Grievances in Congress-Administered Provinces\n● Muslim grievances se related reports ka sahi chronological order: Pirpur Report (1938) → Sharif Report\n(March 1939) → Fazlul Haq Report ('Muslims Suffering Under Congress Rule', December 1939). [Q16]\n9. The First Governor of Bihar\n● Sir James David Sifton, Bihar (Orissa se 1936 mein alag hone ke baad) ke pehle Governor the —\nunhone 1 April 1936 se 10 March 1937 tak service ki. [Q17]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Provincial Election and Formation of Cabinet 1937 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0241","t":"39 Tripuri Crisis of Congress 1939","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.39 — TRIPURI CRISIS OF CONGRESS (1939) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Haripura Session (1938) — Bose's First Presidency\n2. The Tripuri Session (1939) — Bose vs Sitaramayya\n3. Bose's Resignation & Rajendra Prasad's Succession\n4. Bose's War Strategy — 'England's Necessity, India's Opportunity'\n1. The Haripura Session (1938) — Bose's First Presidency\n● Subhash Chandra Bose, February 1938 mein hui Haripura Session (Gujarat) mein, INC ke President\nunopposed elect hue. [Q1, Q2]\n● 'Haripura' (jaha 1938 mein Congress ka annual session Subhash Chandra Bose ki presidency mein\nhua) Gujarat mein situated hai. [Q3]\n2. The Tripuri Session (1939) — Bose vs Sitaramayya\n● Tripuri (jaha 1939 ke session mein Bose President elect hue) Jabalpur (Madhya Pradesh) mein situated\nhai — Tripuri Session mein Bose ne Pattabhi Sitaramayya ko 1580 votes (unke 1377 ke muqable) se\nharaaya, Sitaramayya ko Gandhiji ka support tha. [Q4]\n● Subhash Chandra Bose, Tripuri Session (1939) mein doosri baar INC President elect hue — pehla term\nHaripura (1938) mein tha. [Q5]\n● Tripuri Session (INC), jisme Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose President elect hue, 1939 AD mein hui. [Q7]\n● Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose ne Pattabhi Sitaramayya ko haraakar (1580 votes vs 1377 votes) INC\nPresident ki gaddi hasil ki thi. [Q8, Q9]\n3. Bose's Resignation & Rajendra Prasad's Succession\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ke 1939 mein resign karne ke baad, Dr. Rajendra Prasad INC ke President\nbane. [Q6, Q10]\n● Tripuri Session ke baad, Subhash Chandra Bose aur right-wing ke beech poora dispute 'Congress\nWorking Committee ki formation' ke sawaal par tha — Gandhi, Bose ke modernization aur working\nconduct ke views ke against the. [Q11]\n4. Bose's War Strategy — 'England's Necessity, India's Opportunity'\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne Germany-Britain ke beech ki jung ko ek 'godsend opportunity' maana, jisse\nIndians British rule ko exploit kar sakein — unhone Irish saying follow ki: 'England's necessity is Ireland's\nopportunity.' [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Tripuri Crisis of Congress 1939 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0242","t":"40 Indian Princely States","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.40 — INDIAN PRINCELY STATES — FULL MIND MAP\n👑\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Butler Committee & the All India States People's Conference\n2. Integration of Princely States — Sardar Patel's Leadership\n3. Jammu & Kashmir's Accession\n4. Punjab's Plan for an Independent Existence\n5. The Hyderabad Standstill Agreement\n6. The Praja Mandal Movement\n1. The Butler Committee & the All India States People's Conference\n● 'Butler Committee' (Indian States Committee) 1927 mein, Sir Harcourt Butler ki leadership mein, appoint\nhui thi — Paramount Power (British Crown) aur Indian Princely States ke beech relationship ko\ninvestigate-clarify karne ke liye. Isne bataya ki ye relationship purely contractual nahi thi, balki\ncircumstances-policy se shape hone wali ek living relationship thi — British paramountcy ne prince ki\nauthority preserve ki. [Q1]\n● December 1927 mein 'All India States Peoples Conference' set up hui — 1500 se zyada political\nworkers ne participate kiya. Balwant Rai Mehta, Manilal Kothari aur G.R. Abhyankar ne isse organize\nkarne mein important role play kiya. [Q2]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru 1939 mein 'All India States Peoples Conference' ke President elect hue — Princely\nStates ke political struggles ke common national interest ko represent karne ke liye. [Q3]\n2. Integration of Princely States — Sardar Patel's Leadership\n● Zyadatar princely states ka Union of India mein integration 1947 mein hua tha — 15 August 1947 tak,\nJunagarh, J&K aur Hyderabad ko chhodkar sabhi princely states Indian Union mein shaamil ho chuke\nthe. Baaki 3 states 1948 ke end tak, Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ki leadership mein, shaamil hue. [Q4]\n● Princely States ka integration Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ki leadership mein hua — jo 1947 mein States\nDepartment ke incharge the. Unhone bahut statesmanship se situation handle ki aur princes ki patriotic\nsentiments ko appeal ki. [Q5]\n● Junagarh, Hyderabad aur Jammu & Kashmir — teeno states ne doosre princely states ke join karne ke\nbaad bhi accession delay ki — baaki sabhi 15 August 1947 tak join kar chuke the, ye teeno 1948 ke end\ntak join hue. [Q6]\n3. Jammu & Kashmir's Accession\n● 26 October 1947 ko, Maharaja Hari Singh ne 'Instrument of Accession' sign kiya, jisse Jammu aur\nKashmir India ka integral hissa bana — Sheikh Abdullah ko Prime Minister banaya gaya, aur Indian\nArmy ne 27 October ko state mein entry ki. [Q7]"," 4. Punjab's Plan for an Independent Existence\n● India ke Partition ke waqt, British India ke Punjab province ne ek 'United and Independent' existence ka\nplan propose kiya tha — lekin Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ke prayaso ki wajah se PEPSU ban gayi aur ye\nidea successful nahi hua. [Q8]\n5. The Hyderabad Standstill Agreement\n● 'Standstill Agreement' Hyderabad State (Nizam Mir Osman Ali Khan) aur Dominion of India ke beech,\n29 November 1947 ko, sign hui thi. [Q9]\n6. The Praja Mandal Movement\n● Freedom struggle ke dauran, Indian rulers ke shasan wale States mein ek parallel movement launch\nhui, jise 'Praja Mandal Movement' (State Peoples Conference bhi kehte the) kaha jaata hai — 1920s\nmein, feudal rulers aur kabhi-kabhi British administrators ke against civil rights improve karne ke liye\ncampaign ki gayi. [Q10]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Indian Princely States Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0243","t":"41 Second World War","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.41 — SECOND WORLD WAR — FULL MIND MAP\n⚔️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Congress's Policy During WWII\n2. The Resignation of Congress Ministries (1939)\n3. Dates & British Leadership During WWII\n1. Congress's Policy During WWII\n● 1939 mein jab WWII shuru hui, Britain ne India ko bina consultation ke (elected councils se poochhe\nbina) belligerent (yudhrat) country declare kar diya, Emergency lagaakar — Congress ne declare kiya ki\nwo Britain ko tab tak support NAHI karegi jab tak unhe Complete Independence na di jaaye. [Q1]\n● Statement-Reason: 'Congress ne WWII mein Britain ki madad ki' — YE STATEMENT GALAT hai.\nCongress ne Nazism, Fascism aur Nazi ke Poland attack ki bharpoor ninda ki thi — unhone declare kiya\nki jab India khud independence ke liye ladh rahi hai, tab democracy ki raksha ke liye ladi jaane wali war\nmein participate nahi kar sakti — isliye Statement aur Reason dono galat hain. [Q2]\n2. The Resignation of Congress Ministries (1939)\n● Assertion-Reason: Congress Ministries ne 1939 mein resign ki (sahi Assertion) — kyunki Congress ne\nViceroy Lord Linlithgow ke (17 October 1939 ko, bina Congress ki consent liye) India ko Germany ke\nagainst war mein shaamil karne ke decision ko accept nahi kiya (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko\nexplain karta hai). [Q3]\n●\n Trap: Congress Ministries ne 1939 mein isliye resign NAHI ki kyunki wo cabinet nahi bana pa rahi\n⚠️\nthi, na hi left-wing ke rise ki wajah se, na hi communal turbulence ki wajah se — asal wajah thi British\nGovernment ka bina Indians ki consent liye India ko war country declare karna. [Q4]\n3. Dates & British Leadership During WWII\n● Second World War 1 September 1939 ko Germany ke Poland invasion se shuru hui thi — 6 saal baad,\nSeptember 1945 mein khatam hui. [Q5]\n● Winston Churchill Second World War ke dauran (1940-1945) British Prime Minister the — Neville\nChamberlain war ki shuruat (1939-1940) mein PM the. [Q6]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Second World War Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0244","t":"42 Demand for Pakistan","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.42 — DEMAND FOR PAKISTAN — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rahmat Ali & the Coining of 'Pakistan'\n2. Muhammad Iqbal — Originator of the Two-Nation Theory\n3. Jinnah — Early Nationalism & Later Views\n4. The Lahore Session & the Pakistan Resolution (1940)\n5. Pakistan Day\n1. Rahmat Ali & the Coining of 'Pakistan'\n● 'PAKSTAN' (baad mein 'Pakistan') word sabse pehle Chaudhary Rahmat Ali ne 1933 mein apne\npamphlet 'Now or Never; Are we to Live or Perish for ever?' mein use kiya tha. [Q1, Q2, Q10]\n2. Muhammad Iqbal — Originator of the Two-Nation Theory\n● Sir Muhammad Iqbal ko separate Muslim nation ki idea ka originator maana jaata hai — 1930 ke\nAllahabad presidential address mein unhone Punjab, NWFP, Sindh aur Balochistan ko ek Muslim state\nmein milaane ka proposal diya — ye 'Two-Nation Theory' ki pehli clear expression thi. [Q3, Q4, Q9]\n3. Jinnah — Early Nationalism & Later Views\n● Mohammad Ali Jinnah ne 1940 ke Lahore Session ki presidency ki aur separate Muslim nation ki\ndemand ki — unhone kaha ki wo isse kam kuch bhi accept nahi karenge. [Q5]\n● Sarojini Naidu ne Jinnah ko 'Ambassador of Hindu-Muslim Unity' kaha tha — unke early nationalist\nviews ke liye. 1919 mein Parliament Select Committee ke saamne apni testimony mein unhone strong\nnationalist feelings express ki thi. [Q6]\n● 'Nehru ek patriot hai, jabki Jinnah ek politician hai' — ye remark Sir Muhammad Iqbal ne diya tha, Nehru\nse kaha, jiska zikr 'Discovery of India' mein hai. [Q7]\n●\n Trap: Jinnah ke baare mein galat statement — unhone 'hamesha diary rakhi' wala statement\n⚠️\ngalat/irrelevant mana jaata hai. Baaki sahi hain: wo Two-Nation Theory ke supporter the, unhone 1940\nke Lahore Session ki presidency ki, aur Non-Cooperation Movement mein participate NAHI kiya tha.\n[Q8]\n4. The Lahore Session & the Pakistan Resolution (1940)\n● Famous 'Pakistan Resolution', 23 March 1940 ko, Muslim League ke Lahore Session mein pass hui.\n[Q11, Q12]\n● Pakistan creation ki resolution Fazlul Haq ne present ki aur Khaliquzzaman ne second ki — Sikandar\nHayat Khan, Fazlul Haq aur Khaliquzzaman ne iska outline prepare kiya tha. [Q13]"," ● 'Pakistan Resolution' Sikandar Hayat Khan ne draft ki thi — 23 March 1940 ko Fazlul Haq ne present ki.\n[Q14]\n● Jinnah ki 'Two Nation Theory' ko effect dene wala Muslim League ka Annual Session Lahore mein hua\n(22-24 March 1940) — Sikandar Hayat Khan ne draft prepare ki aur Fazlul Haq ne present ki. [Q15]\n● India ke division ka proposal (Pakistan Resolution) Muslim League ne 1940 ke Lahore Session mein\nrakha tha. [Q16]\n● Mohammad Ali Jinnah ne 1940 ke Lahore Session (Muslim League) ki chairmanship ki. [Q18]\n5. Pakistan Day\n● Lahore Resolution ki yaad mein, Muslim League ne 23 March 1943 ko 'Pakistan Day' celebrate kiya.\n[Q17]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Demand for Pakistan Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0245","t":"43 Individual Satyagraha 1940","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.43 — INDIVIDUAL SATYAGRAHA (1940) — FULL MIND MAP\n🕊️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The First Three Satyagrahis — Vinoba Bhave, Nehru & Brahma Dutt\n2. The Starting Point — Pavnar, Maharashtra\n3. 'Sarvodaya'\n4. Assertion-Reason — The Limited Purpose of the Movement\n1. The First Three Satyagrahis — Vinoba Bhave, Nehru & Brahma Dutt\n● August Offer poori tarah reject hone ke baad, Congress ne Gandhiji ke under 'Individual Satyagraha'\nlaunch ki, ek symbolic moral protest ki tarah — 17 October 1940 ko, Mahatma Gandhi ne Acharya\nVinoba Bhave ko pehla Satyagrahi chuna. Jawaharlal Nehru doosre aur Brahma Dutt teesre Satyagrahi\nbane. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5]\n2. The Starting Point — Pavnar, Maharashtra\n● Vinoba Bhave ne apni Individual Satyagraha 17 October 1940 ko, Pavnar (Paunar), Maharashtra se\nshuru ki thi. [Q6]\n3. 'Sarvodaya'\n● 'Sarvodaya' word sabse pehle Mahatma Gandhi ne use kiya tha — baad mein Vinoba Bhave ne\nGandhian ideals promote karne ke liye 'Sarvodaya Samaj' establish ki. [Q7]\n4. Assertion-Reason — The Limited Purpose of the Movement\n● Assertion-Reason: October 1940 mein, Gandhiji ne kuch selected individuals dwara ek limited\nSatyagraha ka call diya (sahi Assertion) — kyunki wo British ki anti-Nazi war efforts ko disrupt kiye bina,\nIndia ki war policy ke prati naaraazgi dikhana chahte the, aur Congress Britain ko Indian demands\naccept karne ka ek aur mauka de rahi thi (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q8]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Individual Satyagraha 1940 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0246","t":"44 Cripps Mission 1942","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.44 — CRIPPS MISSION (1942) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Arrival & Sender — Winston Churchill\n2. The Proposals — Dominion Status & Constitution-Making\n3. What Was NOT Included in the Cripps Mission\n4. Gandhi's 'Post-Dated Cheque' Remark\n5. Congress Negotiators\n6. Lord Linlithgow's 'Political Blackmail' Remark\n1. Arrival & Sender — Winston Churchill\n● Stafford Cripps, USA, China aur Australia ke pressure mein, March 1942 mein India pahunche. [Q1]\n● British Prime Minister Winston Churchill ne March 1942 mein 'Cripps Mission' bheji thi. [Q8]\n2. The Proposals — Dominion Status & Constitution-Making\n● Sir Stafford Cripps March 1942 mein, British Government ke proposals ka draft declaration lekar aaye\n— jinme included tha: WWII ke baad India ko Dominion Status milegi, apni khud ki Constitution banane\nka right hoga, provinces opt-out kar sakti thi, aur ek interim government bhi banegi. [Q2]\n● Cripps Mission (1942) ka sabse important aspect tha — WWII ke baad Dominion Status ke saath ek\n'Indian Union' create karna. [Q3]\n● Sir Stafford Cripps ki plan ke mutabik, WWII ke baad India ko 'Dominion Status' di jaani thi. [Q5]\n● Statement check: Cripps proposals mein 'Full Independence' ka provision NAHI tha — sirf WWII ke\nbaad Dominion Status ka wada tha. Lekin 'Constitution-making body' create karne ka provision zaroor\ntha. [Q7]\n3. What Was NOT Included in the Cripps Mission\n●\n Trap: Cripps Mission mein 'naye executive council mein Hindus-Muslims ke liye equal\n⚠️\nrepresentation' ka koi provision NAHI tha — Dominion Status, Constituent Assembly ki framed\nConstitution ka acceptance, aur provinces ka Indian Union se bahar rehne ka option — ye teeno the.\n[Q4]\n4. Gandhi's 'Post-Dated Cheque' Remark\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne Cripps proposals ko 'ek crashing bank par post-dated cheque' kaha tha. [Q6]\n5. Congress Negotiators"," ● Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru aur Maulana Abul Kalam Azad, Cripps Mission ke saath Congress ke official\nnegotiators the. [Q9]\n6. Lord Linlithgow's 'Political Blackmail' Remark\n● Viceroy Lord Linlithgow ne Gandhiji ke Movements ko 'Political Blackmail' kaha tha. [Q10]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Cripps Mission 1942 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0247","t":"45 Quit India Movement","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.45 — QUIT INDIA MOVEMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n✊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Wardha Resolution (July 1942)\n2. Commander-in-Chief During the Movement\n3. The AICC Session & Launch — Gowalia Tank Maidan\n4. Gandhi's Instructions & the 'Do or Die' Slogan\n5. Cripps Mission Failure — The Trigger\n6. Baldev Sahai's Resignation\n7. Disputed Statements About the Movement's Nature\n8. Gandhi's Leadership Claim\n9. Parties Opposing the Movement\n10. The Resolution's Movers & Drafters\n11. Abul Kalam Azad — Congress President for Six Years\n12. Bihar's Contribution — Shri Krishna Singh\n13. Reasons for the Movement\n14. Congress Radio — Usha Mehta & Ram Manohar Lohia\n15. Azad Dasta — Jayaprakash Narayan\n16. Winston Churchill — British Prime Minister\n17. Louis Fischer — American Journalist-Biographer\n18. Communal Riots — Bihar & Uttar Pradesh\n19. Lord Linlithgow's Remark\n20. Rajendra Prasad's Arrest\n21. Yogendra Shukla & Rampyari Devi\n22. Gandhi's Arrest — Bombay & Aga Khan Palace\n23. Munger Riots\n24. Jayaprakash Narayan — Escape & National Recognition\n25. Martyrs — Gangaram & Kheemdev\n26. Women Freedom Fighters — Not Associated\n27. Assertion-Reason — Movement's Success, RSS & Muslim League\n28. Aruna Asaf Ali\n29. Parallel Governments\n30. Kanaklata Barua\n31. Culmination of the National Movement\n32. Rajagopalachari's 'The Way Out'\n33. 'Operation Rubicon'\n1. The Wardha Resolution (July 1942)\n● 6 July 1942 ko Congress Working Committee (Wardha) mein Mahatma Gandhi ne pehli baar Maulana\nAbul Kalam Azad (us waqt Congress President) se discuss kiya — 14 July 1942 ko isi meeting mein\n'Quit India' resolution pass hui, Nehru, Patel, Pattabhi Sitaramaiyya bhi participants the. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Commander-in-Chief During the Movement\n● Lord Wavell, Quit India Movement ke dauran Indian Army ke Commander-in-Chief the — baad mein\n1943-1947 tak Viceroy aur Governor-General bhi rahe. [Q3]\n3. The AICC Session & Launch — Gowalia Tank Maidan"," ● AICC session 8 August 1942 ko, Gowalia Tank Maidan, Bombay mein khatam hui — 'Quit India\nResolution' isi din ratify hui, aur movement formally 9 August 1942 ko shuru hui. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9,\nQ10, Q11, Q12, Q13]\n4. Gandhi's Instructions & the 'Do or Die' Slogan\n● Movement launch hone se pehle, Gandhiji ne kaha ki government employees resign na karein balki apni\nCongress allegiance declare karein, soldiers apne countrymen par goli na chalayein aur apni posts na\nchhodein, aur princes apni janta ki sovereignty accept karein. [Q14]\n● 8 August 1942 ko, Gandhiji ne 'Do or Die' mantra diya: 'Hum ya to India ko azaad karenge, ya is koshish\nmein mar jaayenge.' [Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n5. Cripps Mission Failure — The Trigger\n● Quit India Movement, 1942 ke 'Cripps Mission' ki failure ke response mein launch hui thi. [Q21]\n6. Baldev Sahai's Resignation\n● Baldev Sahai ne 1942 mein Advocate General ke pad se resign kiya — Quit India Movement ke dauran\ngovernment ke oppressive acts ('Operation Zero Hour') ke against protest karne ke liye. [Q22]\n7. Disputed Statements About the Movement's Nature\n●\n Disputed: Quit India Movement (1942) ke baare mein — ye purely non-violent NAHI thi (police\n⚠️\nstations, railways par attacks hue), aur Mahatma Gandhi ne isse directly lead NAHI ki (unki arrest\nmovement shuru hone se pehle hi ho gayi, ye leaderless aur spontaneous ho gayi) — is tarah ke\nmultiple 'not-true' statements ki wajah se ye questions disputed maane jaate hain (bhi ye ki Congress ko\nillegal declare kiya gaya ya nahi). [Q23, Q25]\n8. Gandhi's Leadership Claim\n● Quit India Movement ki leadership Mahatma Gandhi ne ki — halaki unhe turant arrest kar liya gaya,\nunhone hi movement launch ki thi, isliye Gandhi ko is context mein 'leader' maana jaata hai. [Q24]\n9. Parties Opposing the Movement\n● Hindu Mahasabha, Communist Party of India, aur Unionist Party of Punjab (aur Muslim League) —\nsabhi ne Quit India Movement ko support NAHI kiya. [Q26]"," 10. The Resolution's Movers & Drafters\n● Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ne 'Quit India Resolution' (1942) ka support kiya — Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru\nne 1942 Bombay Session mein isse move kiya. [Q27, Q28]\n● 'Quit India' resolution ka draft Mahatma Gandhi ne, Nehru aur Azad ki madad se, prepare kiya tha. [Q29]\n● 'Quit India' slogan Yusuf Meher Ali ne coin kiya tha. [Q30]\n11. Abul Kalam Azad — Congress President for Six Years\n● Maulana Abul Kalam Azad, jab Congress ne 'Quit India' resolution pass ki, tab INC President the — wo\n1940 (Ramgarh) mein President bane, aur 1941-1945 ke beech koi session na hone ki wajah se\ncontinue karte rahe. [Q31]\n● Abul Kalam Azad, lagatar 6 saal (1940-1946) tak INC ke President rahe. [Q32]\n12. Bihar's Contribution — Shri Krishna Singh\n● Shri Krishna Singh ('Bihar Kesari'), Quit India Movement mein actively participate hue — wo Bihar ke\npehle Chief Minister bane. [Q33]\n13. Reasons for the Movement\n● Quit India Movement ki reasons thi: Cripps Mission ki failure se Indians ki disappointment, Japanese\nattack ka threat, aur AICC ki resolution —\n Gandhiji ne apne articles mein hinsa ko provoke NAHI\n⚠️\nkiya tha. [Q34]\n14. Congress Radio — Usha Mehta & Ram Manohar Lohia\n● Usha Mehta ne 'Congress Radio' (secret radio) chalayi, Quit India Movement ke dauran — Ram\nManohar Lohia isi radio par regularly broadcast karte the. [Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38]\n15. Azad Dasta — Jayaprakash Narayan\n● 'All India Azad Dasta', Bakri Ka Tapu (Nepal ke Terai region) mein, Jayaprakash Narayan ne organize ki\nthi, guerrilla war ladne ke liye. [Q39]\n16. Winston Churchill — British Prime Minister\n● Winston Churchill, Quit India Movement (1940-1945) ke dauran England ke Prime Minister the. [Q40]"," 17. Louis Fischer — American Journalist-Biographer\n● Louis Fischer, ek American journalist, Quit India Movement ke dauran Gandhiji ke saath the — wo\nGandhiji ke biographer bhi the, aur Pearl Buck jaise doosre intellectuals ke saath India ki freedom ki\nmaang ki. [Q41, Q42, Q43, Q44]\n18. Communal Riots — Bihar & Uttar Pradesh\n● 'Quit India' Movement ki wajah se hue communal riots Bihar aur United Province (UP) mein sabse\nzyada phaile the — revolt ke main centres the Azamgarh, Ballia, Gorakhpur (UP) aur Gaya, Bhagalpur,\nSaran, Muzaffarpur (Bihar). [Q45]\n19. Lord Linlithgow's Remark\n● Assertion-Reason: Lord Linlithgow ne 1942 ke August Movement ko 1857 ke baad ki sabse serious\nrebellion kaha (sahi Assertion) — kisano ki involvement ne struggle ko violent bana diya, jisne Linlithgow\nko ye kehne par majboor kiya (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q46]\n20. Rajendra Prasad's Arrest\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad ko 9 August 1942 ko arrest kiya gaya (Patna mein, Bombay mein NAHI) — unhe\nBankipur Jail (Patna) bheja gaya. Gandhi Aga Khan Palace mein the, baaki CWC members\nAhmednagar Fort mein. [Q47]\n21. Yogendra Shukla & Rampyari Devi\n● Shri Yogendra Shukla, JP Narayan ke saath 9 November 1942 ko Hazaribagh jail se escape hue the —\nunhe Muzaffarpur mein arrest karke 7 December 1942 ko Patna laaya gaya. [Q48]\n● Mr. Jagat Narayan Lal ki patni, Mrs. Rampyari Devi, ne movement ke dauran Bankipur mein assembly\nko address kiya. [Q49]\n22. Gandhi's Arrest — Bombay & Aga Khan Palace\n● Mahatma Gandhi ko 9 August 1942 ko, Bombay mein, Quit India Movement ke connection mein arrest\nkiya gaya. [Q50]\n● Resolution pass hone ke baad, Gandhiji aur Sarojini Naidu ko Aga Khan Palace (Pune) mein rakha\ngaya. [Q51]"," 23. Munger Riots\n● 1942 mein Gandhi aur doosre Congress leaders ki arrest ki khabar milne par, Bihar mein riots hue —\nrailway tracks ukhaadne ki incident zyadatar Bihar mein hui, Munger district sabse zyada affected raha\naur 2 hafte tak cut-off raha. [Q52]\n24. Jayaprakash Narayan — Escape & National Recognition\n● Jayaprakash Narayan ko Quit India Movement mein national leader ki recognition mili — main leaders ki\narrest ke baad unhone secretly janta ko consolidate kiya. [Q53]\n● Jayaprakash Narayan, Deepawali (9 November 1942) ke din, Hazaribagh Jail se escape hue the —\nunhone underground activities organize ki. [Q54, Q55, Q56]\n25. Martyrs — Gangaram & Kheemdev\n● Gangaram aur Kheemdev — 2 bhai, Quit India Movement (1942) mein, Almora mein police firing ke\ndauran martyr hue. [Q57]\n26. Women Freedom Fighters — Not Associated\n●\n Trap: Shanti Ghosh, Quit India Movement (1942) se associate NAHI thi — wo Yugantar (1931 ke\n⚠️\nincident) se juday revolutionary thi. Matangini Hazra, Kanak Lata Barua aur Aruna Asaf Ali — teeno\n1942 mein active thi. [Q58]\n27. Assertion-Reason — Movement's Success, RSS & Muslim League\n● Assertion-Reason: Quit India Movement logo ko jagane-encourage karne mein successful rahi (sahi\nAssertion) — kyunki logo ne 'Do or Die' ko apnaya, jisse movement successful bani (sahi Reason bhi, jo\nAssertion ko explain karta hai). [Q59]\n● Assertion-Reason: RSS (Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh), Quit India Movement (1942) se ALAG rahi\n(sahi Assertion) — lekin diya gaya Reason galat hai. [Q60]\n● Assertion-Reason: Quit India Movement ke result mein, British aur Muslims karib aa gaye (sahi\nAssertion) — Muslim League ne movement ki ninda ki, Jinnah ne kaha ki British ke jaane se\nlawlessness aayegi, isse dono karib aaye (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q61]\n28. Aruna Asaf Ali\n● Aruna Asaf Ali, Quit India Movement mein underground activities ki ek major woman organizer thi —\nunhone 1942 mein Gowalia Tank Maidan mein flag hoist kiya tha. [Q62, Q63, Q64]"," 29. Parallel Governments\n● Quit India Movement ke dauran kai jagah 'Parallel Governments' establish hui — Ballia (August 1942,\nChittu Pandey ki leadership mein), Tamluk/Bengal ('Tamralipta Jatiya Sarkar', December 1942-August\n1944), Satara/Maharashtra (Prati Sarkar, August 1943-May 1946, Y.B. Chavan-Nana Patil ki leadership\nmein, sabse lambe samay chali), aur Talcher/Odisha (Praja Mandal). [Q65, Q67, Q68, Q69]\n●\n Trap: 'Raiyati Sarkar' Kheda (Gujarat) se correctly match NAHI hai.\n⚠️\n[Q66]\n30. Kanaklata Barua\n● Kanaklata Barua ne, Quit India Movement ke dauran, Gohpur (Sonitpur district, Assam) mein ek public\nprocession lead ki aur British restrictions ko defy kiya — National flag hoist karte waqt unhe goli maar di\ngayi. [Q70]\n31. Culmination of the National Movement\n● Assertion-Reason: Quit India Movement, Indian National Movement ka culmination (chotti) thi (sahi\nAssertion) — isne British rule ki agyaanta ka signal diya, aur British ke jaane ka decision jaldi karwaya,\ntransfer mechanism ki khoj shuru hui (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q71]\n32. Rajagopalachari's 'The Way Out'\n● Quit India Movement ke baad, C. Rajagopalachari ne 'The Way Out' naam ka pamphlet issue kiya — ye\nCongress-Muslim League ke political deadlock ka solution propose karta tha, jise 'Rajagopalachari\nFormula' (1944) bhi kehte hain. [Q72]\n33. 'Operation Rubicon'\n● 'Operation Rubicon' ek secret code word tha, jise British Government adopt karne wali thi agar\nMahatma Gandhi Aga Khan Palace mein apne fast unto death ke dauran mar jaate. [Q73]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Quit India Movement Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0248","t":"46 Subhash Chandra Bose and Azad Hind Fauj","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.46 — SUBHASH CHANDRA BOSE & AZAD HIND FAUJ — FULL MIND MAP\n🎖️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Life & the Forward Bloc\n2. The Title 'Netaji'\n3. Formation of the First INA — Mohan Singh\n4. The Provisional Government of Free India (Azad Hind Sarkar)\n5. INA's Formation Location — Singapore/Malaya\n6. Officers Associated (& NOT Associated) with the INA\n7. INA Headquarters — Rangoon\n8. 'Tum Mujhe Khoon Do, Main Tumhe Azadi Dunga'\n9. Sheel Bhadra Yajee\n10. The Free Indian Legion — Germany\n11. The Rani of Jhansi Regiment\n12. The Title 'Desh Nayak' — Rabindranath Tagore\n13. The 'Jai Hind' Slogan\n14. Renaming of the Andaman & Nicobar Islands\n15. 'Azad Hind Fauj Day'\n16. The Red Fort Trials — Sentences & Defense\n17. Key Events of 1945\n18. The Guerrilla War Plan — Nehru at the Allahabad CWC\n1. Early Life & the Forward Bloc\n● Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose, 23 January 1897 ko Cuttack (Odisha) mein paida hue the — Scottish\nChurch College se graduate hue (1919), ICS mein select hue (1920), aur 1938 aur 1939 mein Congress\nPresident bane. [Q1]\n● Tripuri Crisis ke baad, Subhash Chandra Bose ne Congress Presidentship se resign kiya aur 1939 mein\n'Forward Bloc' found ki. [Q2, Q3, Q4, Q6]\n● Chittaranjan Das (C.R. Das) Subhash Chandra Bose ke 'Political Guru' the. [Q42]\n2. The Title 'Netaji'\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ko 'Netaji' ki honorific title Germany mein di gayi thi — unhone 1943 mein Azad\nHind Fauj ka control liya. [Q5]\n3. Formation of the First INA — Mohan Singh\n● Indian National Army (INA) Giani Pritam Singh aur Major Iwaichi Fujiwara ka brainchild thi — unka idea\nIndian soldiers ko azaad karwakar independence ke liye ladwaana tha. INA formally 15 July 1942 ko\nMohan Singh ki leadership mein bani. [Q7]\n●\n Trap: 'INA kiska brainchild tha' wale sawaal mein diye gaye options mein Giani Pritam Singh na\n⚠️\nhone ki wajah se Mohan Singh (jinhone 15 July 1942 ko ise formally banaya) sahi answer maana jaata\nhai. [Q8, Q9]"," ● Indian National Army 1942 mein found hui thi — 15 July 1942 ko Mohan Singh ke under, phir December\n1942 mein dissolve hui, aur 1943 mein Subhash Chandra Bose ne charge liya (Second INA). [Q10]\n● Mohan Singh, 'Indian National Army' ke pehle Commander the. [Q11]\n4. The Provisional Government of Free India (Azad Hind Sarkar)\n● S.C. Bose ne 21 October 1943 ko, Singapore mein, 'Provisional Government of Free India' (Azad Hind\nSarkar) ki formal announcement ki. [Q12, Q13]\n● October 1943 mein Subhash Chandra Bose ne banayi 'Provisional Government of Free India' ko 9\ncountries ne recognize kiya — Japan, Germany, Italy, Thailand, Burma, Philippines, Manchukuo,\nCroatia, aur Japanese-controlled China. [Q14]\n5. INA's Formation Location — Singapore/Malaya\n● Azad Hind Fauj 1943 mein Malaya mein set up hui thi — us waqt Singapore Island British Malaya ka\nhissa tha. [Q15]\n● Azad Hind Fauj (Indian National Army) Singapore mein banayi gayi thi — Subhash Chandra Bose ne\nwahi 1943 mein iska charge liya. [Q16]\n● Ras Bihari Bose ne Subhash Chandra Bose ko Azad Hind Fauj establish karne mein madad ki — Tokyo\nmein, June 1943 mein, unhone INA ki leadership Subhash Chandra Bose ko soup di. [Q17]\n6. Officers Associated (& NOT Associated) with the INA\n●\n Trap: Major Kartar Singh, Azad Hind Fauj (INA) se associate NAHI the — Shahnawaz Khan, P.K.\n⚠️\nSahgal aur Shaukat Ali Malik key officers the. [Q18]\n●\n Trap: S.A. Dange, INA se associate NAHI the — wo Communist Movement se juday the.\n⚠️\n[Q19]\n●\n Trap: B.C. Dutta, INA se related NAHI the — Rashid Ali, Shahnawaz aur P.K. Sahgal Red Fort trials\n⚠️\nmein try hue the. [Q21]\n7. INA Headquarters — Rangoon\n● 'Azad Hind Fauj' ka head office Rangoon (Yangon) mein situated tha. [Q20]\n8. 'Tum Mujhe Khoon Do, Main Tumhe Azadi Dunga'\n● 'Tum Mujhe Khoon Do, Main Tumhe Azadi Dunga' (Give me blood, I'll give you freedom) — ye famous\nslogan Subhash Chandra Bose ne, Singapore mein, apne soldiers ko motivate karne ke liye diya tha.\n[Q22]"," 9. Sheel Bhadra Yajee\n● Sheel Bhadra Yajee (Bihar ke freedom fighter) ne Subhash Chandra Bose ke saath 'All India Forward\nBloc' banane mein sahyog diya, aur actively INA se associate rahe. [Q23]\n10. The Free Indian Legion — Germany\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne 'Free Indian Legion' banayi thi, Germany mein, late 1941 mein — North\nAfrica se Indian prisoners of war ise banate the. [Q24]\n11. The Rani of Jhansi Regiment\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne 1943 mein 'Rani Jhansi Regiment' establish ki — ye Azad Hind Fauj ki\nWomen's Regiment thi. [Q25, Q26]\n12. The Title 'Desh Nayak' — Rabindranath Tagore\n● Rabindranath Tagore ne 1938 mein Subhash Chandra Bose ko 'Desh Nayak' (National Leader) ki title di\nthi. [Q27]\n13. The 'Jai Hind' Slogan\n● 'Jai Hind' slogan Subhash Chandra Bose ne diya tha — ye Azad Hind Fauj ka greeting tha. [Q28]\n14. Renaming of the Andaman & Nicobar Islands\n● Subhash Chandra Bose ne Nicobar Island ka naam 'Swaraj Island' rakha — Andaman ko 'Shaheed'\nnaam diya gaya. [Q29]\n15. 'Azad Hind Fauj Day'\n● 'Azad Hind Fauj Day' 12 November 1945 ko manaya gaya tha — 'INA Week' 5-11 November 1945 tak\nchali. [Q30]\n16. The Red Fort Trials — Sentences & Defense\n● Azad Hind Fauj ke soldier Rashid Ali ko 7 saal ki imprisonment mili — Dhillon, Sahgal aur Shahnawaz\nko life transportation mili thi, lekin pressure ke through unhe release kiya gaya. [Q31]"," ●\n Trap: Mohan Singh ko 1945 ke famous Red Fort trials ka saamna NAHI karna pada — joint court-\n⚠️\nmartial Prem Sahgal, Gurbaksh Singh Dhillon aur Shahnawaz Khan ke liye thi. [Q32]\n● Bhulabhai Desai ne, INA officers (Shahnawaz Khan, Gurbaksh Singh Dhillon, Prem Kumar Sahgal) —\njinhe treason ka accuse kiya gaya tha — unke case ladne wale advocates ke group ki leadership ki. T.B.\nSapru, Kailash Nath Katju aur Jawaharlal Nehru bhi defence team mein the. [Q33]\n● Sir Tej Bahadur Sapru ne INA officers ke Red Fort Trial mein unki taraf se pleading ki — wo Congress ki\nbanayi Defence Committee ka hissa the. [Q34]\n●\n Trap: Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel, 1945 ke INA Red Fort Trial mein advocate NAHI the — Bhulabhai\n⚠️\nDesai, Tej Bahadur Sapru, K.N. Katju, J.L. Nehru aur Asaf Ali is defence se associate the. [Q35]\n●\n Multiple Correct: 'INA trial' ke famous advocates — Asaf Ali AUR Bhulabhai Desai — dono ko sahi\n⚠️\nanswer maana jaata hai. [Q36]\n● Bhulabhai Desai ne 1945-46 mein Delhi mein hui INA trials mein appear kiya tha. [Q37]\n● Famous INA trials, Red Fort (Delhi) mein, November 1945 mein hue. [Q38, Q39]\n● Shah Nawaz Khan, Prem Kumar Sehgal aur Gurbaksh Singh Dhillon — Indian National Army ke officers\nthe, jinka 1945 ke famous Red Fort trial mein trial hua. [Q40]\n17. Key Events of 1945\n● 1945 ke main events: Wavell Plan (14 June 1945), Shimla Conference (25 June - 14 July 1945), aur\nINA Trial (November 1945) —\n Naval Mutiny 1945 mein NAHI, 18-23 February 1946 mein hui thi.\n⚠️\n[Q41]\n18. The Guerrilla War Plan — Nehru at the Allahabad CWC\n● April-May 1942 mein, Allahabad ki Congress Working Committee meeting mein, Jawaharlal Nehru ne\nJapanese ke against guerrilla war ki apni plan ke liye majority hasil ki — India ka Nazism-Fascism-\nImperialism ke against clear stand hone ki wajah se. [Q43]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Subhash Chandra Bose and Azad Hind Fauj Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0249","t":"47 Cabinet Mission Plan 1946","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.47 — CABINET MISSION PLAN (1946) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Members & Leadership — Pethick-Lawrence, Cripps & Alexander\n2. The Three-Tier Polity Proposal\n3. Reconstitution of the Viceroy's Executive Council\n4. Statements — Federal Government\n5. Purpose of the Mission\n6. Muslim League's Withdrawal\n7. Gandhi's Support\n8. Abul Kalam Azad — Negotiator & Congress President\n1. Members & Leadership — Pethick-Lawrence, Cripps & Alexander\n● Cabinet Mission 24 March 1946 ko Delhi pahunchi — Secretary of State for India, Lord Pethick\nLawrence, ki leadership mein — doosre members Sir Stafford Cripps aur A.V. Alexander the. [Q1, Q2,\nQ4]\n●\n Trap: Lord Wavell, Cabinet Mission ke member NAHI the — Pethick-Lawrence, Stafford Cripps aur\n⚠️\nA.V. Alexander members the. [Q3]\n● Cabinet Mission, March 1946 mein, WWII ke baad India aayi thi. [Q5]\n●\n Trap: Ramsay MacDonald, 1946 ki Cabinet Mission ke member NAHI the — wo purane British PM\n⚠️\nthe, jo 1932 ki Communal Award ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q7]\n●\n Trap: 'J. Andrew' aur 'Lord Emery' — dono Cabinet Mission ke members NAHI the.\n⚠️\n[Q8, Q9]\n●\n Trap: John Simon, Cabinet Mission ke member NAHI the — wo 1928 ki Simon Commission ke head\n⚠️\n\nthe. [Q10]\n●\n Trap: 'William Wood', Cabinet Mission ka member NAHI tha.\n⚠️\n[Q11]\n●\n Trap: Cabinet Mission March 1946 mein India aayi thi, 1942 mein NAHI — isliye options mein diye\n⚠️\n1942 ke sabhi mahine galat hain. [Q16]\n2. The Three-Tier Polity Proposal\n● Cabinet Mission ne India ke liye 'Three-Tier Polity' propose ki thi — provinces ko A, B, C — 3 groups\nmein baatne ki recommendation di. [Q6]\n● May 1946 mein proposals ke saath, Cabinet Mission ek United India chahti thi — British provinces se\nmilkar bani ek Federal Union ka provision tha, jisne Pakistan ki demand reject kar di. [Q12]\n●\n Trap: Cabinet Mission Plan ke baare mein galat statement — isne Pakistan ka ACCEPTANCE nahi\n⚠️\ndiya, balki separate Pakistan ki demand REJECT ki. Baaki sahi hain: Provincial Grouping, Interim\nCabinet of Indians, aur Constitution Framing Right. [Q13]\n3. Reconstitution of the Viceroy's Executive Council"," ● Cabinet Mission (1946) ne Viceroy's Executive Council ko reconstitute karne ka suggestion diya —\nsabhi portfolios (War Member samet) Indians ko dene ki baat ki. [Q14]\n4. Statements — Federal Government\n● Cabinet Mission ke baare mein sahi statement — isne 'Federal Government' recommend ki (statement\n1 sahi) — lekin isne courts ke powers ya ICS composition ke baare mein specifically deal NAHI ki\n(statements 2, 3 galat). [Q15]\n5. Purpose of the Mission\n● Cabinet Mission ka mukhya purpose tha power transfer ke liye ek constitutional arrangement work out\nkarna — Jinnah ki Pakistan ki demand reject kar di gayi. [Q17]\n6. Muslim League's Withdrawal\n● Assertion-Reason: 1946 mein, Muslim League ne Cabinet Mission Plan ki acceptance withdraw kar li\n(sahi Assertion, Nehru ke 10 July 1946 ke statement ke baad) — baad mein October 1946 mein wo\nInterim Government mein join hui (sahi Reason bhi) — lekin ye government mein join hona withdrawal ki\nwajah NAHI thi, ye alag strategic moves the (isliye Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation nahi deta).\n[Q18]\n7. Gandhi's Support\n● Mahatma Gandhi, Congress leaders mein Cabinet Mission Plan ke sabse zyada favour mein the —\nunhone ise 'the best document the British Government could have produced in the circumstances' kaha.\n[Q19]\n8. Abul Kalam Azad — Negotiator & Congress President\n● Maulana Abul Kalam Azad ne Cripps Mission AUR Lord Wavell — dono ke saath negotiate kiya — wo\n1940 se 1946 tak Congress President rahe. [Q20]\n● Maulana Abul Kalam Azad, Cabinet Mission ke India visit ke waqt INC ke President the — CWC ne\nunhe Mission ke saath discuss karne ki authorization di thi. [Q21]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Cabinet Mission Plan 1946 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0250","t":"48 Constituent Assembly 1946","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.48 — CONSTITUENT ASSEMBLY (1946) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Origin of the Idea — Congress at Faizpur (1936)\n2. Formation & Framework — The Cabinet Mission Plan\n3. First Session & Dr. Rajendra Prasad's Presidency\n4. Socialist Party's Demand for Dissolution\n5. Sachchidananda Sinha — Temporary President\n6. G.V. Mavlankar — Speaker of Both Eras\n1. Origin of the Idea — Congress at Faizpur (1936)\n● Constituent Assembly ki idea sabse pehle 1895 ke 'Swaraj Bill' mein dikhi thi — officially ise Congress\nne 1936 ke Faizpur Session mein state kiya (Swaraj Party ne bhi pehle, 1934 mein Ranchi mein, ye\ndemand ki thi, lekin exam ke options ke hisaab se '1936 Congress' hi accepted answer hai). [Q1]\n2. Formation & Framework — The Cabinet Mission Plan\n● India ki constitution frame karne wali Constituent Assembly, 'Cabinet Mission Plan' ke under set up hui\nthi — isme Provincial Legislative Assemblies, Chief Commissioners, aur Princely States ke\nrepresentatives shaamil the. [Q2]\n● Cabinet Mission Plan ne India ke liye Constituent Assembly ki idea aur framework diya. [Q3]\n● Cabinet Mission Plan ke under, Constituent Assembly mein har province ko seats roughly 10 lakh logo\npar 1 representative ke ratio mein di gayi — seats communal basis (General, Muslim, Sikh) par allocate\nhui. [Q4]\n3. First Session & Dr. Rajendra Prasad's Presidency\n● Constituent Assembly ki pehli session 9 December 1946 ko hui — Rajendra Prasad ko 11 December\n1946 ko permanent President elect kiya gaya. [Q5]\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad, Indian Constituent Assembly ke President the — B.R. Ambedkar Drafting\nCommittee ke President the, aur Nehru Union Power & Constitution Committees ke President the. [Q6]\n● Rajendra Prasad, Dominion of India ki Sovereign Constituent Assembly ke pehle President the —\nAssembly ko 15 August 1947 ko sovereign declare kiya gaya. [Q7]\n● Statement check: Constituent Assembly of India ko 1946 mein Provincial Assemblies ne elect kiya tha\n(sahi statement) — Jinnah member NAHI the, pehli session Dec 1946 mein hui January 1947 mein nahi,\naur Constitution 26 November 1949 ko adopt hui, 26 January 1950 ko nahi (enact hui). [Q8]\n4. Socialist Party's Demand for Dissolution"," ● Socialist Party ki National Executive (JP Narayan, Lohia jaise leaders) ne 1946 mein Constituent\nAssembly ki dissolution aur adult suffrage se re-election ki demand ki — unka argument tha ki indirect\nelection common logo ko adequately represent nahi karti. [Q9]\n5. Sachchidananda Sinha — Temporary President\n● Sachchidananda Sinha, Quit India Movement se associate the — unhe 9 December 1946 ki Constituent\nAssembly ki pehli meeting mein temporary President bhi elect kiya gaya. [Q10]\n6. G.V. Mavlankar — Speaker of Both Eras\n● G.V. Mavlankar ne British era ki Central Legislative Assembly ke Speaker (1946-47) ki position hold ki\n— aur independence ke baad, Lok Sabha ke bhi Speaker (1952-1956) rahe. [Q11]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constituent Assembly 1946 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0251","t":"49 Formation of Interim Government 1946","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.49 — FORMATION OF INTERIM GOVERNMENT (1946) — FULL MIND\n🏛️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Formation & Leadership — Nehru's Interim Government\n2. Portfolio Allocation\n3. Muslim League's Entry & Liaquat Ali Khan's Finance Portfolio\n4. Other Portfolios — Jagjivan Ram & Joginder Nath Mandal\n5. Cabinet Membership Check\n6. Muslim League's Government in Bengal\n7. Direct Action Day\n1. Formation & Leadership — Nehru's Interim Government\n● Pehli Indian Interim Government 24 August 1946 ko announce hui — 2 September 1946 ko Jawaharlal\nNehru ki leadership mein officiate hui. Shuru mein Muslim League ne participate NAHI kiya. [Q1]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ki leadership mein Interim Government September 1946 mein bani. [Q2, Q3]\n2. Portfolio Allocation\n● Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ko National Provisional Government mein 'Princely' portfolio mila — unhone\nHome Affairs aur Information & Broadcasting bhi sambhaale. [Q4, Q5]\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad ne Interim Government (1946) mein 'Food and Agriculture' portfolio sambhala —\nBaldev Singh ke paas Defence tha, Jawaharlal Nehru ke paas External Affairs & Commonwealth\nRelations. [Q6]\n● Interim Government (1946) mein 'Railways aur Transport' portfolio Asaf Ali ne sambhala. [Q7]\n3. Muslim League's Entry & Liaquat Ali Khan's Finance Portfolio\n● Muslim League October 1946 mein Interim Government mein induct hui — Liaquat Ali Khan ko 'Finance'\nportfolio assign kiya gaya. [Q8]\n● Liaquat Ali Khan, Interim Government ke Finance Minister the. [Q9, Q10]\n4. Other Portfolios — Jagjivan Ram & Joginder Nath Mandal\n● 1946 ki Interim Government's Cabinet mein 'Labour Department' Babu Jagjivan Ram ko allot hua —\nJoginder Nath Mandal ke paas Law Department tha. [Q11]\n5. Cabinet Membership Check"," ●\n Trap: B.R. Ambedkar, 1946 ki Interim Cabinet ke member NAHI the — wo Independent India ke\n⚠️\ncabinet mein Law Minister bane, Interim Government mein nahi. [Q12]\n●\n Multiple Correct: 2 September 1946 ko bani Interim Government mein Liaquat Ali Khan (jo October\n⚠️\n1946 mein baad mein join hue) aur Abul Kalam Azad — dono minister NAHI the. [Q13]\n6. Muslim League's Government in Bengal\n● 1946 ke elections ke baad, Muslim League ne Bengal mein apni government banayi — H.S.\nSuhrawardy is province ke Premier (Prime Minister) bane. [Q14]\n7. Direct Action Day\n● Muslim League ne 16 August 1946 ko 'Direct Action Day' manaya — isse widespread riots hue,\nNoakhali ek major center tha. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Formation of Interim Government 1946 Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0252","t":"50 Partition of India and Independence","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.50 — PARTITION OF INDIA & INDEPENDENCE — FULL MIND MAP\n🇮🇳\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. British Government at Independence — Attlee & the Labour Party\n2. The June 1948 Deadline & Mountbatten's Appointment\n3. The Mountbatten Plan (June 1947)\n4. The Indian Independence Act, 1947\n5. Assertion-Reason — Britain's Motives & Sovereignty\n6. The Balkan Plan\n7. Congress's Acceptance of Partition\n8. Gandhi's Alternative Suggestion\n9. The Radcliffe Boundary Commission\n10. The Cabinet Mission's Rejection — The Last Chance Lost\n11. The Delhi Session — The Partition Resolution\n12. Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan's Dissent\n13. Midnight of 14/15 August 1947\n14. The First Prime Minister & Governors-General\n15. The First Law Minister — Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n16. Sequence of Presidents of India\n17. The Partition Council\n18. The Referendum Provinces\n19. Congress President at Partition — J.B. Kripalani\n20. Gandhi's Absence from Independence Day Celebrations\n21. Why 26 January 1950 for the Constitution\n22. Historians' Views on British Rule\n23. The British Monarch at Independence\n24. The Saurashtra Sangh\n1. British Government at Independence — Attlee & the Labour Party\n● Jab India ko independence mili, UK mein Labour Party sattaa mein thi — Clement Attlee (1945-1951)\nPrime Minister the. [Q1, Q2]\n2. The June 1948 Deadline & Mountbatten's Appointment\n● Attlee ne 20 February 1947 ko declare kiya ki British June 1948 tak India chhod denge — unhone Lord\nMountbatten ko power transfer supervise karne ke liye Viceroy appoint kiya. [Q3, Q5]\n● Lord Mountbatten India mein specific instruction ke saath aaye the — 'agar possible ho to India ko\nUnited rakhna' — unhe British loss minimize karne ke liye decisions lene ki authority thi, aur aakhir mein\nunhone conclude kiya ki unity achieve karna namumkin hai, isliye partition ka rasta chuna. [Q4]\n3. The Mountbatten Plan (June 1947)\n● 'Mountbatten Plan' (3 June 1947 ko announce) India ki independence aur partition ka basis bani. [Q6,\nQ10, Q11]\n●\n Multiple Correct: Mountbatten Plan 'Transfer of Power' AUR 'Partition of the Country' — dono ka\n⚠️\nbasis bani. [Q7]"," 4. The Indian Independence Act, 1947\n● British Parliament ne 'Indian Independence Act' July 1947 mein pass ki — 18 July 1947 ko Royal Assent\nmilkar ye force mein aayi. [Q8, Q9, Q14]\n5. Assertion-Reason — Britain's Motives & Sovereignty\n● Assertion-Reason: Britain ne 1947 mein India ko azaad kiya (sahi Assertion) — kyunki WWII ke dauran\nBritain kamzor ho gayi thi (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko explain karta hai). [Q12]\n● Assertion-Reason: 'British sovereignty free India mein continue rahi' — YE ASSERTION GALAT hai\n(British sovereignty 15 August 1947 ko khatam ho gayi thi) — lekin Reason sahi hai ki British sovereign\nne shuru mein free India ke liye Governor-General (Mountbatten) appoint kiya tha. [Q13]\n6. The Balkan Plan\n● 'Plan Balkan' (India ko fragment karne ki plan, alag-alag provinces aur princely states ke liye separate\ndominions) Lord Mountbatten ka brainchild thi. [Q15]\n7. Congress's Acceptance of Partition\n● 1947 mein Congress ne partition accept ki, mukhya taur par large-scale communal riots aur bloodshed\navoid karne ke liye. [Q16]\n● Assertion-Reason: Congress ne Mountbatten Plan accept ki (sahi Assertion) — lekin ye 'Two-Nation\nTheory' mein believe karne ki wajah se NAHI thi, Congress ne kabhi is theory ko accept nahi kiya, riots\navoid karne ke liye accept ki (galat Reason). [Q17]\n8. Gandhi's Alternative Suggestion\n● Partition ke alternative ki tarah, Gandhiji ne Mountbatten ko suggest kiya ki wo Jinnah ko Government\nbanane ke liye invite karein. [Q18]\n9. The Radcliffe Boundary Commission\n● 'Radcliffe Committee' India-Pakistan ke beech boundaries demarcate karne ke liye appoint hui thi —\nCyril Radcliffe ne 1947 mein banayi gayi dono (Bengal aur Punjab) Boundary Commissions ki head ki.\n[Q19, Q20, Q21]"," 10. The Cabinet Mission's Rejection — The Last Chance Lost\n● India ki partition avoid karne ka aakhri mauka 'Cabinet Mission' (1946, jo United India chahti thi) ke\nrejection ke saath khatam ho gaya — Muslim League ne ise reject karke 'Direct Action' ka call diya.\n[Q22]\n11. The Delhi Session — The Partition Resolution\n● Acharya J.B. Kripalani, Delhi Congress Session ke Chairman/President the — jaha partition ki resolution\npass hui. [Q23, Q24]\n● June 1947 mein, All India Congress Committee ki meeting mein, Govind Ballabh Pant ne partition\nresolution introduce ki aur Abul Kalam Azad ne second ki. [Q25]\n● Dr. Saifuddin Kitchlew, us waqt Punjab Pradesh Congress Committee ke President, ne strongly partition\nka virodh kiya — unhone ise 'Surrender of Nationalism in favour of Communalism' kaha. [Q26]\n12. Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan's Dissent\n● 14-15 June 1947 ki AICC meeting mein, Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan (Frontier Gandhi) ne partition\nresolution ke against vote kiya. [Q27]\n13. Midnight of 14/15 August 1947\n● 14/15 August 1947 ki midnight ko, 'Constituent Assembly' ne provisionally sovereign power sambhali.\n[Q28]\n● Sucheta Kripalani ne Central Assembly mein, midnight ko, Iqbal ki 'Hindustan Hamara' aur 'Jana Gana\nMana' gaya tha. [Q29]\n14. The First Prime Minister & Governors-General\n● Governor-General (Lord Mountbatten) ne India ke pehle Prime Minister — Jawaharlal Nehru — ko\nappoint kiya. [Q30]\n● Lord Mountbatten, Independent India ke pehle Governor-General the (1947-48) — C. Rajagopalachari\npehle Indian Governor-General bane. [Q31, Q32]\n● C. Rajagopalachari, Independent India ke aakhri Governor-General the (1948-1950) — jab tak ye pad\nabolish nahi hua. [Q33]\n● C. Rajagopalachari, Independent India ke pehle Indian Governor-General the. [Q34]\n● C. Rajagopalachari, India ke pehle AUR aakhri Indian Governor-General the (ekmatra Indian jinhone ye\npad sambhala). [Q35]\n● Lord Mountbatten, India ke aakhri Viceroy the (1947-48) — baad mein Governor-General bhi bane.\n[Q36]"," 15. The First Law Minister — Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar, Independent India ke pehle Law Minister the. [Q37]\n16. Sequence of Presidents of India\n● Presidents ka sahi sequence: Rajendra Prasad (1950-1962) → S. Radhakrishnan (1962-1967) → Zakir\nHussain (1967-1969) → V.V. Giri (1969-1974). [Q38]\n17. The Partition Council\n● Jawaharlal Nehru aur Sardar Patel ne, Lord Mountbatten ki leadership wali 'Partition Council' mein,\nIndian National Congress ka representation kiya. [Q39]\n18. The Referendum Provinces\n● Mountbatten Plan (June 1947) ne NWFP, Sindh, Balochistan aur Assam ke Sylhet district — sabhi mein\nreferendum (janmat sangrah) ka provision diya. [Q40]\n19. Congress President at Partition — J.B. Kripalani\n● J.B. Kripalani, India ke partition ke waqt (November 1946 - November 1947) INC President the. [Q41,\nQ42]\n● J.B. Kripalani ne 1946 ke Meerut Session ki presidency ki. [Q43]\n● J.B. Kripalani, 1947 mein Britishers dwara power transfer ke waqt, Congress President the. [Q44]\n20. Gandhi's Absence from Independence Day Celebrations\n● August 1947 mein, Mahatma Gandhi ne kahi bhi Independence Day celebrations mein participate NAHI\nkiya — wo partition se dukhi the, aur us din fast-prayer mein bitaaya. [Q45]\n21. Why 26 January 1950 for the Constitution\n● 26 January 1950 ko Constitution enforce karne ke liye chuna gaya kyunki Congress ne 26 January 1930\nko pehla 'Independence Day' (Purna Swaraj) celebrate kiya tha. [Q46]"," 22. Historians' Views on British Rule\n● 'Indian Nationalism, British Rule ka child tha' — ye statement R. Coupland ne diya tha. [Q47]\n● K.M. Panikkar ne kaha tha ki 'British Rule ki sabse notable achievement India ka unification' thi. [Q48]\n23. The British Monarch at Independence\n● Indian Independence ke waqt (1947) British Monarch George VI the (1936-1952 tak reign). [Q49]\n24. The Saurashtra Sangh\n● 15 February 1948 ko, 222 principalities (217 Kathiawar Agency se aur 5 doosri) ko milaakar 'Saurashtra\nSangh' banaya gaya. [Q50]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Partition of India and Independence Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0253","t":"51 Constitutional Development of India","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.51 — CONSTITUTIONAL DEVELOPMENT OF INDIA — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Regulating Act, 1773\n2. Pitt's India Act, 1784 & the Act of 1786\n3. The Cornwallis Code (1793)\n4. The Charter Act, 1813\n5. The Charter Act, 1833\n6. The Charter Act, 1853\n7. Civil Services — The Fight for Simultaneous Examination\n8. Match Lists — Acts & Their Provisions\n9. The Separation of the North-Western Provinces\n10. The Government of India Act, 1858\n11. The Indian Councils Act, 1861\n12. The Indian Councils Act, 1892\n13. Press Control Acts\n14. The Indian High Courts Act, 1861\n15. The Indian Councils Act, 1909 (Morley-Minto)\n16. The Government of India Act, 1919 (Montagu-Chelmsford & Dyarchy)\n17. The Government of India Act, 1935 — Overview\n18. GoI Act 1935 — Princely States, the Federation & Criticism\n19. Legislative Assembly Elections Timeline\n20. GoI Act 1935's Legacy — 'Charter of Slavery' & Directive Principles\n21. Constituent Assembly Debates — Ambedkar & Patel\n22. NOT a Landmark — Post-Independence Acts\n1. The Regulating Act, 1773\n● 'Regulating Act, 1773' British East India Company ki Indian territories (mainly Bengal) ko regulate karne\nke liye pass hui — Governor-General of Fort William (Bengal) ki post create ki, jisme Madras aur\nBombay presidencies par supervisory powers thi. Warren Hastings pehle Governor-General bane. [Q1,\nQ2, Q3, Q4]\n● Regulating Act, 1773 ne India mein pehli baar 'Supreme Court' establish ki, Fort William, Calcutta mein\n— Sir Elijah Impey pehle Chief Justice bane, 1774 mein. [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n2. Pitt's India Act, 1784 & the Act of 1786\n● 'Act of 1786' Lord Cornwallis ko Governor-General post accept karne ke liye persuade karne wali thi —\nisne unhe special cases (peace, defence, empire welfare) mein Council ki majority ko override karne ka\npower di. [Q8, Q9]\n● 'Pitt's India Act, 1784' ne Britain mein 'Board of Control' establish ki — East India Company ke\nadministrative-political affairs ko fully regulate karne ke liye. [Q25]\n3. The Cornwallis Code (1793)\n● Cornwallis ke judicial reforms (Cornwallis Code, 1793) Separation of Powers ke principle par based the\n— unhone District Collector ko judicial powers se alag kiya, ye maankar ki ek hi vyakti mein revenue-"," judicial-magisterial power concentrate karna undesirable tha, aur naya 'District Judge' post create ki.\n[Q10]\n4. The Charter Act, 1813\n● Charter Act, 1813 ne East India Company ki India trade monopoly khatam ki — lekin unhone tea trade\naur China ke saath trade ka monopoly retain kiya. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Charter Act, 1813 ke important hone ki wajah thi — isne India ki education ke liye 1 lakh rupees annual\ngrant ki financial allocation ki. [Q15]\n5. The Charter Act, 1833\n●\n Trap: Charter Act, 1833 ke under Governor-General's Council mein 'Indian' Law Member appoint\n⚠️\nkarne ka provision NAHI tha — pehla Law Member Lord Macaulay (British) the. Isne Company ka trade\nfully khatam kiya, aur Bengal ke Governor-General ko poore British India ka Governor-General banaya.\n[Q16, Q17]\n● Charter Act, 1833 ne East India Company ka commercial adhikaar completely khatam kiya — tea trade\naur China trade ka monopoly bhi khatam hua, unke paas sirf Crown ki taraf se administrative rights reh\ngaye. [Q27]\n6. The Charter Act, 1853\n● Charter Act, 1853 ne civil services ke liye 'open competition system' introduce ki — Court of Directors ka\npatronage right cheen liya. Isi Act ne pehli baar India mein ek functioning 'Legislative Council' (12\nmembers) bhi establish ki. [Q19, Q20]\n7. Civil Services — The Fight for Simultaneous Examination\n● Montagu-Chelmsford Report ne Civil Service exam Britain aur India — dono jagah simultaneously (ek\nsaath) hold karne ki recommendation di — Aitchison Commission (1887) ne pehle isse oppose kiya tha.\n[Q18]\n● 1922 AD mein, British Government finally Indian Civil Service exam India-England mein simultaneously\nhold karne ke liye raazi hui. [Q21]\n● 1922 AD se Civil Services exam India mein bhi hone lage — 1 January 1941 tak, Civil Service mein\nIndians (617) ki sankhya Europeans (585) se zyada ho gayi thi. [Q22]\n8. Match Lists — Acts & Their Provisions\n● Match: Board of Control ki sthapna → Pitt's India Act, 1784; Supreme Court ki sthapna → Regulating\nAct, 1773; Christian missionaries ki permission → Charter Act, 1813; Governor General Council mein\nLaw Member → Charter Act, 1833. [Q23]"," ● Match: Charter Act 1813 → Trade monopoly khatam (tea-China chhodkar); Regulating Act 1773 →\nDirectors ko correspondence submit karni padti thi; Act of 1858 → EIC se Crown ko power transfer;\nPitt's India Act 1784 → Board of Control ki sthapna. [Q24]\n● Match: Regulating Act 1773 → Supreme Court establishment; Indian Council Act 1909 → Communal\nElectorate; GoI Act 1919 → Dyarchy (provinces); GoI Act 1935 → Provincial Autonomy. [Q75]\n9. The Separation of the North-Western Provinces\n● Aaj ka lagbhag poora Uttar Pradesh area, East India Company ne gradually acquire kiya tha, aur\nBengal Presidency ke saath rakha gaya — 1834 AD mein isse alag karke 'North-Western Provinces'\n(Agra Presidency ke under) banaya gaya. [Q28]\n10. The Government of India Act, 1858\n●\n Disputed: British Government ne tea-sugar trade monopoly abolish karne wale question mein\n⚠️\noptions mein galti thi (China ki jagah sugar diya gaya tha) — MPPSC ne isse galat maankar bonus\nmarks diye. [Q26]\n● 'Government of India Act, 1858' ne, 1857 Revolt ke baad, East India Company se Crown ko power\ntransfer ki — ek British Parliament member ko Secretary of State for India banaya gaya. [Q29]\n● Statement check: 1853 ke Act ne trade monopoly khatam NAHI ki (ye 1813 mein hui thi — statement 1\ngalat) — Government of India Act, 1858 ne EIC se Crown ko power transfer ki, direct rule ke liye\n(statement 2 sahi). [Q30]\n11. The Indian Councils Act, 1861\n● Indian Councils Act, 1861 ne Governor-General ko emergency mein Ordinances issue karne ki power di\n— ye 6 mahine tak applicable rehte the. [Q31]\n● Indian Councils Act, 1861 ne Viceroy ki authority strengthen ki — Lord Canning ne apni Executive\nCouncil ko reorganize karke 'Portfolio System' introduce ki, jisme har department ek member ke under\nhota tha. [Q32]\n12. The Indian Councils Act, 1892\n● Indian Councils Act, 1892 ne legislative assembly members ko Budget ya public matters par questions\npoochne ka right diya — lekin supplementary questions ya budget par voting ka right nahi tha. [Q33]\n● Indian Councils Act of 1892 mein pehli baar 'indirect election' (representation) ka principle incorporate\nkiya gaya. [Q34]\n13. Press Control Acts"," ● India mein media control karne ke liye Acts pass hue: 1835 (Press Act, censorship), 1867 (Press and\nRegistration of Books Act), 1878 (Vernacular Press Act, Lord Lytton), aur 1908 (Lord Minto, seditious\nmaterial ke against). [Q35]\n14. The Indian High Courts Act, 1861\n● Bombay, Madras aur Calcutta ke High Courts, 'Indian High Court Act, 1861' ke basis par 1862 mein\nestablish hue. [Q36]\n15. The Indian Councils Act, 1909 (Morley-Minto)\n● Britain ke sabse 'short-lived' constitutional experiment 'Indian Councils Act of 1909' tha — Ramsay\nMacDonald ne kaha tha ki ye 'democracy aur bureaucracy ke beech ek incomplete, short-term\nagreement' thi. [Q37]\n● Minto-Morley Reforms (1909) ne British India mein 'Communal Representation' ka provision diya —\nLord Minto ko 'Father of Communal Electorate in India' kehte hain. [Q38]\n● Indian Councils Act, 1909 (Morley-Minto Reforms) ne India mein Muslims ke liye pehli baar 'Separate\nElectorate' system introduce ki. [Q39]\n16. The Government of India Act, 1919 (Montagu-Chelmsford & Dyarchy)\n● 20 August 1917 ko hui reforms ki declaration 'Montagu Declaration' kehlaati hai — Edwin Montagu\n(Secretary of State for India) aur Lord Chelmsford ne isse announce kiya. [Q40]\n● 'Dyarchy' ke father Sir Lionel Curtis mane jaate hain — Government of India Act (1919) ne provinces\nmein ye double government ka system introduce kiya. [Q41]\n● Montagu-Chelmsford Report ne 'Government of India Act, 1919' ka basis banaya — ye India mein\ngradually self-governing institutions introduce karne ke liye thi. Provincial subjects ko 'Reserved'\n(Finance, Police) aur 'Transferred' (Education, Health) — 2 categories mein baata gaya. [Q42, Q44, Q45,\nQ46, Q47, Q48]\n● David Lloyd George, Montagu-Chelmsford Act (Government of India Act, 1919) pass hone ke waqt\nEngland ke Prime Minister the (1916-1922). [Q43]\n●\n Trap: Government of India Act 1919 ko 'Morley-Minto Reforms' NAHI kehte — ye 'Montagu-\n⚠️\nChelmsford Reforms' kehlaati hai. Morley-Minto Reforms 1909 ki Act ko refer karti hai — ye galat\nstatement question hai. [Q49]\n● Assertion-Reason: GoI Act 1919 ke governance ki structure 'unitary' thi — ye statement GALAT hai\n(asal mein generally federal thi, halaki Governor-General ke paas major executive powers thi) — lekin\nReason (Act ne dyarchy introduce ki aur provinces ko 50 subjects diye) SAHI hai. [Q50]\n● Assertion-Reason: Dyarchy ka matlab administrative affairs ka division tha (sahi Assertion) — provincial\nsubjects Reserved-Transferred mein baate gaye — provinces mein responsible governance ka degree\nintroduce karne ke liye, transferred subjects Indian ministers ko dekar (sahi Reason bhi, jo Assertion ko\nexplain karta hai). [Q51]"," ● Government of India Act, 1919 ne London mein 'Indian High Commissioner' ka post create kiya. [Q52]\n17. The Government of India Act, 1935 — Overview\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ke main elements the: Federation ka provision, aur Provincial Autonomy\n—\n Dyarchy provinces mein abolish hui thi, introduce NAHI hui (ye centre mein introduce hui).\n⚠️\n[Q53]\n● Government of India Act 1935 ne British India ke provinces ko badi autonomy di — 1919 ke Act se\nintroduce hui provincial dyarchy ko khatam kiya. [Q54, Q57]\n● Simon Commission Report (aur 3 Round Table Conferences) 'Government of India Act, 1935' ka\nbaseline (aadhar) bani. [Q55]\n● Statement check: GoI Act 1935 ne provinces ko autonomy di aur dyarchy khatam ki (sahi), Governors\nke paas special veto powers rahe (sahi) — lekin communal representation khatam NAHI hui, ulta\ndepressed classes-women-labour tak extend hui (galat statement). [Q56]\n●\n Trap: '1935 ke Act ka appraisal' iski koi feature NAHI thi — Act ne Federation propose ki, Provincial\n⚠️\nAutonomy di, aur Executive Council restructure ki. [Q58]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne 3 cheezein provide ki: Provincial Autonomy, Federal Court ki sthapna,\naur All-India Federation (centre par). [Q59]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 important hai kyunki ye Indian Constitution ka main source hai —\nConstitution ke bahut se provisions isi Act se liye gaye. [Q60]\n●\n Trap: 'Dyarchy Centre AUR Provinces dono mein' — ye GoI Act 1935 ki feature NAHI hai —\n⚠️\nDyarchy sirf Centre mein introduce hui, Provinces mein khatam karke Provincial Autonomy di gayi. [Q61]\n18. GoI Act 1935 — Princely States, the Federation & Criticism\n● British ka real intention Princely States ko proposed Federal Union mein shaamil karne ka tha —\nnationalist leaders ke anti-imperialist doctrines ko counter-balance karna. Princes ko disproportionately\nhigh representation di gayi, aur unke members nominated the, elected nahi. [Q62]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne 1935 ke Act ke baare mein kaha tha: 'A car which has a brake but no engine' (aisi\ngaadi jisme brake hai lekin engine nahi) — matlab bahut saari restrictions hain, lekin power (engine)\nIndia ko nahi mila. [Q63, Q64]\n● 'Constitutional Autocracy' ka principle Government of India Act of 1935 ne introduce kiya — ye ek\nelaborate, complex document tha jisne Governor-General ke haath mein massive discretionary powers\nconcentrate ki. [Q65]\n● Indian National Congress ne Government of India Act, 1935 ko 1936 ke Lucknow Session mein reject\nkiya — is session ki presidency Jawaharlal Nehru ne ki. [Q66]\n19. Legislative Assembly Elections Timeline\n● Central Legislative Assembly ki elections 1923, 1926, 1930, 1934 aur 1945 mein Government of India\nAct 1919 ke under hui — 1937 ki provincial assembly elections GoI Act 1935 ke under hui thi. [Q67]"," ● Government of India Act, 1919 ke under India Legislature ki aakhri election 1945 mein hui. [Q68]\n20. GoI Act 1935's Legacy — 'Charter of Slavery' & Directive Principles\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne Government of India Act, 1935 ko 'Charter of Slavery' kaha tha. [Q69]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 mein diye gaye 'Instrument of Instructions' ko, 1950 mein, Constitution of\nIndia mein 'Directive Principles of State Policy' ki tarah incorporate kiya gaya — critics is section ko 'holy\nphrases' bhi kehte the. [Q70]\n● Government of India Act 1935 ne banayi Federation mein, 'residuary powers' Governor-General ko di\ngayi thi. [Q71]\n● 'India Council' Government of India Act 1935 ne abolish kiya tha — ye India mein constitutional reforms\nka aim rakhti thi, provincial dyarchy khatam karke centre mein introduce ki, aur provinces ko zyada\nautonomy di. [Q72]\n21. Constituent Assembly Debates — Ambedkar & Patel\n● 'Constitution ke draft mein 1935 ke Act se material udhaar lene ka koi ilzaam mujhe maafi maangne ki\nzaroorat nahi hai' — ye statement Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne, Constitution-making process ke Parliamentary\ndebates mein, diya tha, 1935 ke Act se borrowings ko defend karte hue. [Q73]\n● 'Kya aap mujhe ek bhi azaad desh dikha sakte hain jaha separate electorates hon? British element ja\nchuka hai...' — ye statement Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ne, Constituent Assembly debates mein,\nseparate electorates ki criticism karte hue diya. [Q74]\n22. NOT a Landmark — Post-Independence Acts\n●\n Trap: 'The Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955' British rule ke dauran India ki Constitution\n⚠️\ndevelopment ka landmark NAHI hai — ye Independent India ke Parliament ne, azaadi ke baad, banayi\nthi (originally 'Untouchability Offences Act, 1955'). [Q76]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constitutional Development of India Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0254","t":"52 Modern History Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.52 — MODERN HISTORY: MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n📋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Colonial Administration & Governance Attitudes\n2. Anglo-Afghan Relations — Fear of Russia\n3. Match Lists — Anglo Wars & Treaties Dates\n4. A Disputed Match — Multiple Pairs\n5. Famines of the 19th Century\n6. Colonial Commissions & Their Chairmen\n7. Chronology — Early 19th Century Events\n8. Chronologically Last Events — Moplah Revolt\n9. Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom\n10. Chronology — Press & Land Acts\n11. Match List — Social Reformers\n12. Disputed — 1857 Leaders & Ghadar Party\n13. The First Indian Cinema Advertisement\n14. Attlee's Statement on the Partition\n15. Famous Quotes on Freedom\n16. Chronology — Press & Societies Founding\n17. William A.J. Archibald\n18. Annie Besant's 'Tom-Tom' Statement\n19. Gandhi's Statement on Communal Differences\n20. Gandhi & Tilak — Social Regeneration\n21. Lala Lajpat Rai — Later Political Life\n22. G.V. Mavlankar — First to Discard the Official Wig\n23. World's First Woman PM & 10 Downing Street\n24. J.B. Kripalani's Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party\n25. Dr. Ambedkar's Death\n26. Rabindranath Tagore — 'Gurudev', Death & Views\n27. Ras Behari Bose's Rallying Statement\n28. 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' — Lal Bahadur Shastri\n29. The Gregorian Calendar\n30. Bhartiya Kisan Sangh\n31. Gandhi's Quit India Quotes\n32. Subhash Bose on Gandhi's Leadership\n33. Assertion-Reason — Nationalist Leaders & 'Providence'\n34. Nehru's Statement on Agriculture\n35. The First Cloth Mill in Bombay\n36. Dadabhai Naoroji's Statement\n37. Boy Scouts Movement — Baden-Powell\n38. The Rakhmabai Case (1884)\n39. Freedom Struggle — Incorrect Statement Check\n40. Statements About Jawaharlal Nehru — All Incorrect\n41. Nehru's Socialist-Republican Statement\n42. Nehru — 'High Priest of Communism' & His Biographer\n43. Ambabai — Woman Freedom Fighter\n44. The 'Sarabandi Campaign' — Sardar Patel\n45. The Origin of the Word 'Boycott'\n46. N.M. Joshi — India at the ILO\n47. Statements — Arya Samaj, Al-Hilal & Presidency College\n48. Chronology — 'Kesari' to 'Al Hilal'\n49. Third Event in Chronological Order — Dandi March\n50. Statements — Gandhi & Colonial Rule\n51. Aruna Asaf Ali's Post-1947 Contribution\n52. Sardar Patel's Statement on Bihar Riots\n53. First Demand for 'Complete Independence' — Hasrat Mohani\n54. Mountbatten on Jinnah's Role in Partition\n55. Aga Khan — The All Parties Muslim Conference"," 56. The Hindu Mahasabha — Banaras Session (1923)\n57. Sachchidananda Sinha — 'Creator of Modern Bihar'\n58. Founding Years — CPI & RSS (1925)\n59. 'Frontier Gandhi' — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan\n60. The 'Bombay Trimurti'\n61. Khudai Khidmatgars — The 'Red Shirts'\n62. Dr. B.S. Moonje's Attack on Ambedkar\n63. History's Role in Creating Nationalism\n64. Tripura & the Freedom Movement\n65. Rajendra Prasad — From Bihar\n66. Women Saint Daya Bai\n67. St. Francis Xavier\n68. Jagat Narain Lal — Hazaribagh Jail\n69. The Aga Khan Palace Samadhis\n70. The Official History of Congress — Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n71. The Whitley Commission\n72. Foreign Commentators on Colonial India\n73. The Bengal Famine of 1943\n74. Non-Alignment\n75. Goa — Under Portuguese Control After Independence\n76. Nehru — NOT Influenced by German Nationalism\n77. Dominant Castes in Pre-Independence Bihar\n78. Shimla Conference & the Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n79. Statements — Vidyasagar & Bethune School\n80. Earliest Event — Neeldarpan\n81. First Indian in the British Parliament\n82. The Deoband Scholar — Abul Kalam Azad\n83. Chronology — Jallianwala Report to the Calcutta Session (1920)\n84. Independent India's First Industrial Policy\n85. The First Communist Government — Kerala\n86. National Observance Days\n87. Chronology — Air India to Goa (Post-Independence)\n88. Nehru vs Gandhi — Heavy Industrialization\n89. Gandhi's Statement at the Karachi Session (1931)\n90. The 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) Strategy\n91. The C.R. Formula\n92. Disputed — Organizations' Founding Years\n93. Gandhi's Key Milestones — Match List\n94. Chronology — Constitutional Reforms & Acts\n95. Chronology — Early Movements (1905-1916)\n96. Chronology — Rowlatt to Jallianwala Bagh (Multiple Sequences)\n97. Chronology — Lahore Session, Communal Award & Poona Pact\n98. Chronology — August Offer to Cabinet Mission (1940-1946)\n99. Match Lists — Movements & Their Leaders/Founders\n100. Match Lists & Not-Correctly-Matched Traps — Various Pairs\n101. The Trade Disputes Act, 1929\n102. Nehru's Political Career — Terms & Statements\n103. Quotes — Attlee, Cripps\n104. World History — Atomic Bomb & French Revolution\n105. Disputed Match — Pact/Year & Place\n106. Post-Independence Foreign Affairs Chronology\n107. The Shimla Agreement (1972)\n108. 'Operation Vijay' — Kargil War\n109. Kisan Diwas\n110. Nobel Prize Winners — Match List\n111. World Political Events — 20th Century\n112. World Leaders — Firsts & Notable Figures\n113. World History — Paper, Philosophy & the Renaissance\n114. The 'Kallar' Rebels of Madurai\n115. The Indian Councils Act of 1909\n116. Rama Devi — The Bijolia Peasant Movement\n117. Political Party Founding Years — Match List\n118. The 'Imperial Gazetteer' — W.W. Hunter"," 119. Gandhi & the Term 'Panchayati Raj'\n120. The Indian National Calendar\n121. Additional Committees, Chronology & Facts\n1. Early Colonial Administration & Governance Attitudes\n● Statement check: Lord Cornwallis pehle Governor-General the jinhone British pattern par regular police\nforce establish ki (statement 1 galat, unhone ki thi). Regulating Act 1773 ne Supreme Court banayi\n(sahi). IPC 1860 mein pehle Law Commission ki recommendations par draft hui (sahi). [Q1]\n● 'Paternalism in Governance' (patriarchal approach) India ke context mein British administrators jaise Sir\nThomas Munro se associate hai. [Q7]\n2. Anglo-Afghan Relations — Fear of Russia\n● 19th century mein Anglo-Afghan relations Russia ke India ki taraf expansion ke dar se influenced thi —\n1828 ke Treaty of Turkmenchay (Russia-Iran) ke baad, British ko Khyber-Bolan Passes ke through\nRussian invasion ka dar tha. [Q2]\n3. Match Lists — Anglo Wars & Treaties Dates\n● Match: First Anglo-Maratha War (1775-82); Second Anglo-Mysore War (1780-84); First Anglo-Burmese\nWar (1824-26); First Anglo-Afghan War (1839-42). [Q3]\n● Match: Second Anglo-Mysore War (1780-84); Second Anglo-French War (1750-54); Second Anglo-\nMaratha War (1803-05); Second Anglo-Afghan War (1878-80). [Q4]\n● Match: Treaty of Allahabad (1765); Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle (1748); La Bourdonnais' capture of Madras\n(1746); Dupleix's dismissal (1754). [Q5]\n● Sahi matched pairs: Third Anglo-Mysore War (1790-92) aur First Anglo-Burmese War (1824-26) —\n\n⚠️\nFirst Anglo-Maratha War 1775-82 mein thi (1767-69 mein nahi), aur Second Sikh War 1848-49 mein thi.\n[Q11]\n4. A Disputed Match — Multiple Pairs\n●\n Disputed: Farrukhsiyar ne Jizya tax dobara lagayi, British ne 1759 mein Masulipatnam par Colonel\n⚠️\nFrancis Ford ke through kabza kiya, Malcolm ka naam slavery ke end se associate NAHI hai, aur Sati\nPrevention Act ki jagah 'Bengal Sati Regulation (1829)' hona chahiye tha — multiple errors ki wajah se\nye question disputed hai. [Q6]\n5. Famines of the 19th Century\n● Orissa Famine (1866-67) ko 'Sea of Calamity' kaha gaya — Odisha mein akele 1.3 million log (aabadi\nka tihai) starvation-diseases se mare. [Q8]"," ● 'Indian Famine Code, 1883' Strachey Commission ne prepare ki — ye 1878 mein Great Famine (1876-\n78) ke baad famine-prevention measures ke liye appoint hui thi. [Q9]\n6. Colonial Commissions & Their Chairmen\n● Match: Andrew Fraser → Police Commission (1902-03); Antony MacDonell → Famine Commission\n(1900-01); Colin Scott Moncrieff → Irrigation Commission (1901-03); Thomas Robertson → Railway\nCommission (1901-03). [Q10, Q125]\n7. Chronology — Early 19th Century Events\n● Chronological order: Nana Phadnavis ki death (March 1800) → Wellesley ki recall (1805) → Vellore\nMutiny (10 July 1806) → Anglo-Nepalese War (1814-16). [Q12]\n● Battles ka chronological order: Battle of Shakarkheda (1724) → Battle of Bedara (1759) → Battle of\nPorto Novo (1781) → Battle of Mudki (1845). [Q13]\n8. Chronologically Last Events — Moplah Revolt\n● Chronologically aakhri event: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Jallianwala Bagh (13 April 1919) →\nKhilafat Movement (1919-24) → Moplah Revolt (1921). [Q14]\n9. Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom\n● Queen Elizabeth II ne 70 saal reign kiya (1952-2022) aur 96 saal ki age mein (1926-2022) unki mrityu\nhui. [Q15]\n10. Chronology — Press & Land Acts\n● Chronological order: Dramatic Performance Act (1876) → Vernacular Press Act (1878) → Bengal\nTenancy Act (1885) → North-Western Provinces & Oudh Act (1890). [Q16]\n11. Match List — Social Reformers\n● Match: Child Marriage (against) → M.G. Ranade; Thuggee ka suppression → Colonel Sleeman; Widow\nRemarriage ka concept → Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar; Pindaris ka suppression → Lord Hastings. [Q17]\n12. Disputed — 1857 Leaders & Ghadar Party"," ●\n Disputed: Kunwar Singh (Bihar) aur Khan Bahadur Khan (Bareilly) ke baare mein statements sahi\n⚠️\nhain — lekin Maulvi Ahmadullah Faizabad mein lead karte the (Zeenat Mahal mein NAHI), aur Ghadar\nParty 1913 mein Lala Hardayal-Sohan Singh Bhakna ne banayi thi (Bhagat Singh ne NAHI) — isliye ye\nquestion disputed hai. [Q18]\n13. The First Indian Cinema Advertisement\n● 7 July 1896 ko, 'The Times of India' (Bombay) mein, Indian cinema ka pehla advertisement publish hua\n— usi din Lumiere brothers ne Watson's Hotel, Bombay mein pehla cinematography show diya. [Q19]\n14. Attlee's Statement on the Partition\n● 'British Government partition of India ke liye responsible nahi hai' — ye statement Lord Attlee ne diya\ntha, 20 February 1947 ko, power transfer ke baare mein. [Q20]\n15. Famous Quotes on Freedom\n● 'Political Freedom is the life-breath of a nation' — Aurobindo Ghosh ne kaha tha. [Q21]\n● Jayaprakash Narayan ne India mein 'Party Less Democracy' ka proposal diya tha. [Q22]\n● 'They both fought and collaborated with imperialism' — ye statement Rajani Palme Dutt ne Indian\nNational Congress ke baare mein kaha tha. [Q23]\n● 'New Lamps for Old' (1893-94) Aurobindo Ghosh ne likhi thi — apne Cambridge friend K.G. Deshpande\nke request par, 'Induprakash' weekly ke liye — Congress ko out-of-touch bataate hue. [Q24]\n16. Chronology — Press & Societies Founding\n● Chronological order: Hicky's 'Bengal Gazette' (1780) → Bengal Asiatic Society (1784) → Servants of\nIndia Society (1905) → Gadar Party (1913). [Q25]\n17. William A.J. Archibald\n●\n Trap: William A.J. Archibald, Lahore College ke Principal NAHI the — wo M.A.O. College (1905-\n⚠️\n1909), Government College Dhaka aur Muir Central College ke principal rahe. [Q26]\n18. Annie Besant's 'Tom-Tom' Statement\n● 'I am an Indian Tom-Tom, whose work is waking up all the sleepers' — ye statement Annie Besant ne\ndiya tha. [Q27]"," 19. Gandhi's Statement on Communal Differences\n●\n Multiple Correct: 'Jab tak British power yaha hai, hamare communal differences hume pareshaan\n⚠️\nkarte rahenge' — ye statement Mahatma Gandhi ne, American journalist Louis Fischer ko interview\nmein diya tha — options mein Gandhi na hone ki wajah se 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q28]\n20. Gandhi & Tilak — Social Regeneration\n● Gandhi aur Tilak — dono ne social development ke liye India ka bahut travel kiya — Tilak pehle national\nleader the jinhone masses se close relationship banayi, Gandhi se pehle. [Q29]\n21. Lala Lajpat Rai — Later Political Life\n● Statement check: Lala Lajpat Rai shuru mein Non-cooperation ke favour mein nahi the, baad mein\nCalcutta Special Session (Sep 1920) mein iski resolution pass hone par ise support kiya — unhone C.R.\nDas-Motilal Nehru ki Swaraj Party bhi 1923 mein join ki, 1925 mein chhod di — dono statements sahi\nhain. [Q30]\n22. G.V. Mavlankar — First to Discard the Official Wig\n● G.V. Mavlankar, 1946 mein Central Legislative Assembly ke President bane — unhone mandatory wig\nhataakar Gandhi cap pehankar preside kiya. Wo pehle Lok Sabha Speaker bhi bane. [Q31]\n23. World's First Woman PM & 10 Downing Street\n● Duniya ki pehli lady Prime Minister Sirimavo Bhandaranaike (Sri Lanka) thi — July 1960 mein. [Q32]\n● '10 Downing Street' British Prime Minister ka official residence hai — Westminster mein situated. [Q33]\n24. J.B. Kripalani's Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party\n● Statement check: J.B. Kripalani ne 'Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party' 1951 mein banayi thi (1952 mein NAHI,\nstatement (i) galat) — 1952 mein ye Socialist Party ke saath merge hui. P.C. Ghosh aur T. Prakasam is\nparty se associate the (statement (ii) sahi). [Q34]\n25. Dr. Ambedkar's Death\n● Constitution ke maker Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ki mrityu 6 December 1956 ko New Delhi mein hui — unhe\n1990 mein posthumously Bharat Ratna mila. [Q35]"," 26. Rabindranath Tagore — 'Gurudev', Death & Views\n● Rabindranath Tagore ko 'Gurudev' kehte hain — unhone 'Gitanjali' ke liye 1913 mein Nobel Prize jeeta.\nUnki mrityu 7 August 1941 ko, Calcutta ke ancestral home mein hui. [Q36, Q37]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne Rabindranath ko 'The Great Sentinel' kaha tha — Gandhi maante the ki Tagore ne\nfreedom struggle ko moral support diya. [Q38]\n●\n Trap: Rabindranath Tagore Swadeshi Movement ke ECONOMIC aspects (jaise foreign clothes\n⚠️\njalana) ke favour mein NAHI the — unhone iske negative side-effects apne novel 'Ghare Baire' mein\ndikhaye. [Q39]\n● Rabindranath Tagore 70 saal ki age mein ek great painter ki tarah ubhre — 1930 mein Europe, Russia\naur USA mein apne paintings exhibit ki. [Q85]\n27. Ras Behari Bose's Rallying Statement\n● 'Avenge the blood of Indian Martyrs. Use your sword to liberate...' — ye powerful statement\nrevolutionary Ras Behari Bose ne diya tha. [Q40]\n28. 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' — Lal Bahadur Shastri\n● 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' slogan tatkaleen Prime Minister Lal Bahadur Shastri ne 1965 mein, Ramlila\nMaidan (Delhi) mein diya tha. [Q41]\n29. The Gregorian Calendar\n● Present-day calendar 'Gregorian Calendar' par based hai — worldwide use hota hai. [Q42]\n30. Bhartiya Kisan Sangh\n●\n Disputed: 'Bhartiya Kisan Sangh' 4 March 1979 ko, Kota (Rajasthan) mein, Dattopant Thengdi ne\n⚠️\nestablish ki thi — 1979 saal diye gaye options mein na hone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q43]\n31. Gandhi's Quit India Quotes\n● 'Freedom is almost within reach, we have to seize it' — ye statement Mahatma Gandhi ne, Quit India\nMovement (9 August 1942) ke waqt diya, saath hi 'Do or Die' ka slogan bhi. [Q44]\n32. Subhash Bose on Gandhi's Leadership"," ● 'India's salvation will not be achieved under his leadership' — ye statement Subhash Chandra Bose ne\napni book 'The Indian Struggle' mein, Gandhiji ke baare mein likha tha. [Q45]\n33. Assertion-Reason — Nationalist Leaders & 'Providence'\n● Assertion-Reason: Early nationalist leaders British rule ko 'Providence' (ishwar-nirdharit) tool maante\nthe, jo modernization laayegi (sahi Assertion) — unki criticism sirf 'Un-British rule' tak limited thi (sahi\nReason bhi) — lekin official answer key ke mutabik Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation NAHI deta.\n[Q46]\n34. Nehru's Statement on Agriculture\n● 'Everything else can wait, but not agriculture' — ye statement Jawaharlal Nehru ne Independence ke\nbaad kaha tha. [Q47]\n35. The First Cloth Mill in Bombay\n● Pehla Indian cotton cloth mill 1818 mein, Fort Gloaster (Kolkata) mein bana tha lekin fail ho gaya —\npehli successful modern cloth mill 1854 mein Bombay mein, Parsi cotton merchant Cowaszee\nNanabhoy Davar ne banayi. [Q48]\n36. Dadabhai Naoroji's Statement\n● 'Kings are made for Public; Public is not made for the King' — ye statement Dadabhai Naoroji ('Grand\nOld Man of India') ne diya tha. [Q49]\n37. Boy Scouts Movement — Baden-Powell\n● Robert Baden-Powell ne 1 August 1907 ko Brown Sea Island mein camp lagakar 'Boy Scouts'\nmovement shuru ki — India mein Boy Scouts aur Civil Guides Movement ke founder maane jaate hain\n(India mein scouting 1909 mein, guiding 1911 mein aayi). [Q50]\n38. The Rakhmabai Case (1884)\n● Rakhmabai ek pehli practising women doctors mein se thi colonial India mein — 1884-1888 ke beech\nunke child marriage se related ek landmark legal case (restitution of conjugal rights, consent age) chala,\njisse 'Age of Consent Act' (1891) bani. [Q51]\n39. Freedom Struggle — Incorrect Statement Check"," ●\n Trap: 1931 ke Karachi Session mein Congress ne Gandhi-Irwin Pact ka VIRODH NAHI kiya — ulta\n⚠️\nise APPROVE kiya tha (5 March 1931 mein sign hui thi). [Q52]\n40. Statements About Jawaharlal Nehru — All Incorrect\n●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru se related sabhi diye gaye statements GALAT hain — 1947 mein J.B.\n⚠️\nKripalani Congress President the (Nehru NAHI), Rajendra Prasad permanent Constituent Assembly\nPresident the, aur UP ke pehle Congress Ministry mein Nehru shaamil NAHI the (Govind Ballabh Pant\nChief Minister the). [Q53]\n41. Nehru's Socialist-Republican Statement\n● 'I am a socialist and a republican and do not believe in Kings and Princes' — ye statement Jawaharlal\nNehru ne diya tha. [Q54]\n42. Nehru — 'High Priest of Communism' & His Biographer\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ko 'High Priest of Communism in India' kaha gaya tha — United Provinces ke\nPublicity Department ke ek pamphlet mein ('Communistic Likes and Dislikes'), unke socialistic views ko\nconfuse karne wale propaganda ki tarah. [Q55]\n● Nehru socialism ke champion bane — 1933 mein British rule, Princely states, Landlordism aur\nCapitalism khatam karna chahte the, 1927 mein Soviet Union visit se inspire hokar. [Q56]\n● Frank Moraes, Jawaharlal Nehru ke biographer the. [Q57]\n43. Ambabai — Woman Freedom Fighter\n● Ambabai, ek woman freedom fighter, purane Mysore State (aaj Karnataka) se belong karti thi — unhone\nSalt Satyagraha mein Udipi mein foreign cloth-liquor shops picket ki. [Q58]\n44. The 'Sarabandi Campaign' — Sardar Patel\n● 'Sarabandi' (No-tax) Campaign, Bardoli (Gujarat) mein, Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ne lead ki thi. [Q59]\n45. The Origin of the Word 'Boycott'\n● 'Boycott' word Captain Charles C. Boycott (Irish land agent) ke naam se derived hai — unhi ke against\n1880 mein ye ek political weapon ki tarah pehli baar use hua. [Q60]"," 46. N.M. Joshi — India at the ILO\n● N.M. Joshi ko Indian Government ne 1919 Washington ILO summit mein labourers ka representative\nbanakar bheja tha — B.P. Wadia unke advisor the. [Q61]\n47. Statements — Arya Samaj, Al-Hilal & Presidency College\n● Statement check: Arya Samaj 1875 mein Dayananda Saraswati ne bani (sahi), 'Al Hilal' Abul Kalam\nAzad ne 1912 mein publish ki (sahi) — Lala Lajpat Rai 'The People' se associate NAHI the (galat) —\nPresidency College Ram Mohan Roy-David Hare ne 1817 mein banaya (sahi). [Q62]\n48. Chronology — 'Kesari' to 'Al Hilal'\n● Chronological order: Kesari ki shuruat (1881) → Khudiram Bose ki execution (1908) → Curzon Wyllie ki\nassassination (1909) → Al Hilal ki shuruat (1912). [Q63]\n49. Third Event in Chronological Order — Dandi March\n● Chronological order: Champaran Movement (1917) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Dandi\nMarch (1930, 3rd) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q64]\n50. Statements — Gandhi & Colonial Rule\n● Statement check: Gandhi ne Viceroy Chelmsford se negotiate karke indentured labour system July\n1917 mein ban karwaya (sahi) — Salt March (1930) ke baad INC ko illegal declare kiya gaya aur\nleaders arrest hue (sahi) — lekin Gandhi ne WWI mein army recruitment ka virodh NAHI kiya, unhone\nactually support kiya tha (galat). [Q65]\n51. Aruna Asaf Ali's Post-1947 Contribution\n● Aruna Asaf Ali ne 1947 ke baad politics mein sabse zyada contribute kiya — left socialist group se juri,\naur 1958 mein Delhi ki pehli Mayor bani. [Q66]\n52. Sardar Patel's Statement on Bihar Riots\n● 'Agar hum Bihar ke logo aur unki Government ko violence-anarchy ke saamne asuraksit chhod dein, to\nye humari galti hogi' — ye statement Sardar Patel ne 1946 mein, Bihar ke violent riots ke context mein\ndiya tha. [Q67]"," 53. First Demand for 'Complete Independence' — Hasrat Mohani\n● Maulana Hasrat Mohani ne 1921 mein pehli baar 'Complete Independence' (Poorna Swaraj) ki demand\nki — 1921 ke Ahmedabad Congress Session mein. [Q68]\n54. Mountbatten on Jinnah's Role in Partition\n● Lord Mountbatten (Viceroy 1947-48) ne Muhammad Ali Jinnah ko India ke partition ke liye sabse zyada\nresponsible bataya. [Q69]\n55. Aga Khan — The All Parties Muslim Conference\n● Aga Khan (Maulana Sultan Mohammed Shah) ne, Delhi mein, late December 1928-January 1929 mein\nhui 'All Parties Muslim Conference' ki presidency ki — Muslims ke liye separate electorates ki demand\nke liye banayi gayi thi. [Q70]\n56. The Hindu Mahasabha — Banaras Session (1923)\n● August 1923 ke 'Banaras Session' (Hindu Mahasabha) ki presidency Pandit Madan Mohan Malviya ne\nki — lagbhag 1500 delegates (Hindus, Jains, Sikhs, Parsis samet) attend hue. [Q71]\n57. Sachchidananda Sinha — 'Creator of Modern Bihar'\n● Sachchidananda Sinha ko 'Creator of Modern Bihar' maana jaata hai — unhone Bengal Presidency se\nalag ek separate Bihar province ke liye movement lead ki, jo 1912 mein realize hui. [Q72]\n● 'So always with the assent and often to the dictates of the Chamber of Commerce, the Government of\nIndia...' — ye statement Sachchidananda Sinha ne diya tha. [Q229]\n58. Founding Years — CPI & RSS (1925)\n● Communist Party of India (CPI, December 1925, Kanpur) aur Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS, 27\nSeptember 1925, Nagpur) — dono 1925 mein hi bane the. [Q73]\n59. 'Frontier Gandhi' — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan\n● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan ko 'Frontier Gandhi' kehte hain — Mahatma Gandhi ke saath unke close\nassociation aur pacifist tareeko ki wajah se. [Q74, Q75, Q76]"," 60. The 'Bombay Trimurti'\n● Pherozeshah Mehta, K.T. Telang aur Badruddin Tyabji — 'Bombay Trimurti' kehlaate hain — unhone\nmilkar 1885 mein Bombay Presidency Association banayi. [Q77]\n61. Khudai Khidmatgars — The 'Red Shirts'\n● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan ne 'Khudai Khidmatgar' (Servants of God) organize ki — jinhe 'Red Shirts' bhi\nkehte the — Civil Disobedience Movement ke dauran non-violence aur freedom struggle ka pledge liya.\n[Q78, Q79]\n62. Dr. B.S. Moonje's Attack on Ambedkar\n● Dr. B.S. Moonje (Hindu nationalist leader) ne 1932 mein, Ambedkar ki separate electorate ki demand ke\nresponse mein, kaha: 'Ambedkar has had his leadership thrust upon him...' [Q80]\n63. History's Role in Creating Nationalism\n● History ki study ne India mein nationalism ki feeling create karne mein har tarike se madad ki — British\nrule ke against struggle ke liye logo ko urge kiya, backwardness ki British narrative ko counter kiya, aur\nIndia ke glorious past ko highlight kiya. [Q81]\n64. Tripura & the Freedom Movement\n● Tripura native state 20th century ki shuruat mein freedom movement mein involve hui — British ke\npressure mein, Bengal ke revolutionaries ne Tripura mein sharan li thi. [Q82]\n65. Rajendra Prasad — From Bihar\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad, 3 December 1884 ko, Ziradei village (Siwan district, Bihar) mein paida hue the.\n[Q83]\n66. Women Saint Daya Bai\n● Women Saint Daya Bai, Saint Charandas ki disciple thi — unhone 'Dayabodh' naam ki book likhi. [Q84]\n67. St. Francis Xavier"," ● Statement check: St. Francis Xavier, Jesuit order ke founding members mein se ek the — unki mrityu 3\nDecember 1552 ko Shangchuan Island (China) mein hui, Goa mein NAHI (isliye galat statement). [Q86]\n68. Jagat Narain Lal — Hazaribagh Jail\n● Jagat Narain Lal ko freedom struggle ke dauran Hazaribagh Jail bheja gaya tha. [Q87]\n69. The Aga Khan Palace Samadhis\n● Kasturba Gandhi aur Mahadev Desai ki Samadhis, Aga Khan Palace (Pune) ke premises mein hain.\n[Q88, Q89]\n70. The Official History of Congress — Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n● Dr. Pattabhi Sitaramayya, Congress ki official history ke author the. [Q90]\n71. The Whitley Commission\n● Colonial period mein, 'Whitley Commission' ka purpose tha British India ke industrial undertakings-\nplantations mein labour ki existing conditions par report dena aur recommendations dena. [Q91]\n72. Foreign Commentators on Colonial India\n● Katherine Mayo, Aldous Huxley, Charles Andrews aur William Digby — sabhi ne British rule ke dauran\nIndia ki condition par commentaries likhi. [Q92]\n73. The Bengal Famine of 1943\n● 1943 ke Bengal Famine mein lagbhag 3 million log maare gaye. [Q93]\n74. Non-Alignment\n● Global peace aur cooperation establish karne ke liye, 'Non-Alignment' ka concept introduce kiya gaya\ntha. [Q94]\n75. Goa — Under Portuguese Control After Independence"," ● 15 August 1947 ke baad, Goa Portuguese control mein raha — 1961 mein 'Operation Vijay' ke through\nliberate hua. Portuguese hi ekmatra colonial power thi jinke against azaadi ki ladai independence ke\nbaad bhi continue rahi. [Q95, Q96]\n76. Nehru — NOT Influenced by German Nationalism\n●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru 'German Nationalism' se influenced NAHI the — unhone Nazism aur\n⚠️\nFascism ka strongly virodh kiya. [Q97]\n77. Dominant Castes in Pre-Independence Bihar\n●\n Trap: Pre-independence Bihar mein Bhumihar, Rajput aur Kayastha dominant castes thi — Kurmi in\n⚠️\nmein SHAAMIL NAHI thi. [Q98]\n78. Shimla Conference & the Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n● Statement check: Shimla Conference (1945) ke waqt Lord Wavell Viceroy the, Mountbatten NAHI (galat\nstatement) — Royal Indian Navy revolt 18 February 1946 ko, Bombay aur Karachi mein shuru hui (sahi\nstatement). [Q99]\n79. Statements — Vidyasagar & Bethune School\n● Statement check: Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar, Bethune School ke first secretary the (sahi), Bankim\nChandra Calcutta University ke pehle 2 graduates mein se ek the (1858, sahi) — lekin Sati ban 1829\nmein Ram Mohan Roy ke campaign se hui, Keshav Chandra Sen se NAHI (galat). [Q100]\n80. Earliest Event — Neeldarpan\n● Sabse pehle hua event: Dinabandhu Mitra ne 'Neeldarpan' likhi (1860) — Satyendra Nath Tagore ka\nICS pass karna (1864), Arya Samaj ki sthapna (1875), aur 'Anandmath' likhi jaana (1880) baad mein\nhue. [Q101]\n81. First Indian in the British Parliament\n● Lal Mohan Ghose (1885) British House of Commons election contest karne wale pehle Indian the —\nlekin Dadabhai Naoroji pehle Indian the jo actually elect hue (1892, Liberal Party ticket par, Central\nFinsbury se). [Q102, Q103]\n● Indirect election ki practice India mein Indian Councils Act, 1892 ke through launch hui. [Q104]"," 82. The Deoband Scholar — Abul Kalam Azad\n● Abul Kalam Azad, Deoband movement se related ek scholar the, jinhone freedom movement mein\nsignificant role play kiya — 1940-1946 tak Congress President rahe aur 'India Wins Freedom' likhi.\n[Q105]\n83. Chronology — Jallianwala Report to the Calcutta Session (1920)\n● Chronological order: Jallianwala Bagh Report submission (25 March 1920) → Turkey ke saath Peace\nTerms ki announcement (14 May 1920) → B.G. Tilak ki demise (1 August 1920) → INC ka Special\nSession, Calcutta (4-9 September 1920). [Q107]\n84. Independent India's First Industrial Policy\n● Independent India ki pehli Industrial Policy 6 April 1948 ko announce hui — India ke liye 'mixed\neconomy' ka concept introduce kiya, industries ko public-private sectors mein baata. [Q108]\n85. The First Communist Government — Kerala\n● India ki pehli Communist Government 1957 mein Kerala mein establish hui — E.M.S. Namboodiripad ki\nleadership mein. [Q109, Q110]\n86. National Observance Days\n● India mein 'Teacher's Day' 5 September ko manaya jaata hai — Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan ki birth\nanniversary ki yaad mein. [Q111]\n● 'National Press Day' 16 November ko manaya jaata hai. [Q112]\n● Match: World Population Day → 11 July; International Youth Day → 12 August; National Sports Day →\n29 August; World Literacy Day → 8 September. [Q113]\n● 'Civil Service Day' 21 April ko celebrate hota hai — pehla function 21 April 2006 ko New Delhi mein hua.\n[Q114]\n● 'Valentine Day' har saal 14 February ko celebrate hota hai. [Q115]\n87. Chronology — Air India to Goa (Post-Independence)\n● Chronological order: Air India nationalise hui (1953) → Imperial Bank ka naam SBI hua (July 1955) →\nKerala mein first communist government (April 1957) → Goa India ka hissa bana (1961). [Q116]"," 88. Nehru vs Gandhi — Heavy Industrialization\n● Gandhi small-cottage industries ke development par zor dete the — Nehru 'heavy industrialization' ka\nsupport karte the. [Q117]\n89. Gandhi's Statement at the Karachi Session (1931)\n● 'Gandhi may die, but Gandhism will remain' — ye statement Gandhi ne March 1931 ke Karachi Session\nmein diya tha. [Q118]\n90. The 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) Strategy\n●\n Disputed: 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) political strategy Mahatma Gandhi ne use ki — BPSC ne\n⚠️\n\nis question ko delete kar diya, kyunki ye strategy Civil Disobedience Movement se sabse prominently\nassociate maani jaati hai, jo diye gaye options se match nahi karti. [Q119]\n91. The C.R. Formula\n● C. Rajagopalachari ne July 1944 mein, Gandhi ki approval se, Muslim League aur INC ke beech\npolitical deadlock khatam karne ka plan diya — 'C.R. Formula' kehlaayi, Jinnah ne isse reject kiya.\n[Q120]\n92. Disputed — Organizations' Founding Years\n●\n Disputed: All India Women's Conference 1927 mein bani (1926 NAHI), All India Depressed Classes\n⚠️\nAssociation 1926 mein M.C. Raja ne banayi, Bombay Social Reform Association 1903 mein bani, aur\nIndian National Social Conference M.G. Ranade ne 1887 mein banayi — multiple options galat matched\nhone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q121]\n93. Gandhi's Key Milestones — Match List\n● Match: Yerwada Prison → Civil Disobedience Movement; Fast unto death → Communal Award ke\nagainst; Black flags dikhaye gaye Karachi jaate waqt → Gandhi-Irwin Pact endorse karne ke liye;\n'Defeat more mine than theirs' (Sitaramayya) → 1939 ka Congress Crisis (Tripuri). [Q122]\n94. Chronology — Constitutional Reforms & Acts\n● Chronological order (Non-cooperation to Quit India): Non-cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Simon\nCommission (1927-28) → Nehru Report (1928) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q123]"," ● Sequence: Rowlatt Act (1919) → Simon Commission (1927) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (1931) — Home Rule\nMovement (1916) sabse pehle. [Q142]\n● Sequence: Partition of Bengal (1905) → Lucknow Pact (1916) → Rowlatt Act (March 1919) →\nIntroduction of Dyarchy (December 1919, GoI Act 1919). [Q145]\n● Sequence: Passing of Rowlatt Bill (18 March 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) →\nAmritsar Session of INC (26-30 December 1919) → B.G. Tilak ki demise (1 August 1920). [Q150]\n● Sequence: Rowlatt Act (18 March 1919) → Rowlatt Satyagraha (6 April 1919) → Amritsar Session (Dec\n1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q155]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha\n(April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q156]\n● Match: Indian Council Act 1909 → Morley-Minto Reform; GoI Act 1919 → Montague-Chelmsford\nReform; GoI Act 1935 → Simon Commission Report/Joint Select Committee; Indian Independence Act\n1947 → Mountbatten Plan. [Q166]\n● Sequence: Ban on Sati (1829) → Wood's Despatch (1854) → Vernacular Press Act (1878) → Rowlatt\nAct (1919). [Q189]\n● Match: MacDonald → Communal Award (1932); Linlithgow → August Offer (1940); Dalhousie →\nDoctrine of Lapse; Chelmsford → Dyarchy (GoI Act 1919). [Q204]\n● Sequence: Wood's Despatch (19 July 1854) → Hunter Commission (1882, Ripon) → Sadler\nCommission (1917) → Sargeant Plan (1944). [Q205]\n●\n Trap: Ahom Rebellion 1828 mein hui thi, 1815 mein NAHI — Santhal (1855-56), Kol (1831-32) aur\n⚠️\nKhasi (1829-33) sahi matched hain. [Q207]\n● Match: 1883 → First National Conference (Calcutta); 1906 → Muslim League ki foundation (Dhaka);\n1927 → All India States People Conference; 1932 → Ramsay MacDonald ne Communal Award\nannounce ki (Whitehall se). [Q159]\n● Match: Morley-Minto Reform (1909) → Communal Electorates; Simon Commission (1927) → Nation-\nwide Movement; Chauri-Chaura (1922) → Non-cooperation ki withdrawal; Dandi March (1930) → Illegal\nsalt manufacturing. [Q160]\n●\n Trap: Communal Award 1932 mein announce hui thi, 1933 mein NAHI — Ramsay MacDonald ne 16\n⚠️\n\nAugust 1932 ko diya. [Q162]\n● Match: Indian Council Act 1909 → Lord Minto (Morley-Minto); GoI Act 1919 → Chelmsford; GoI Act\n1935 → Simon Commission; Indian Independence Act 1947 → Mountbatten. [Q217]\n95. Chronology — Early Movements (1905-1916)\n● Sequence: Regulating Act (1773) → Partition of Bengal (1905) → Muslim League ki sthapna (1906) →\nSurat split (1907). [Q140]\n● Match: Home Rule League → Lokmanya Tilak (1916); Swaraj Party → Chittaranjan Das (1923);\nNationalist Party → Madan Mohan Malviya; National Liberal Federation → Tej Bahadur Sapru. [Q187]\n● Sequence: Surat Split (1907) → Muslim League ki foundation (Dhaka, 1906 — pehle) → Home Rule\nMovement (1916) → Kheda Satyagraha (1918). [Q161]"," ● Sequence: Partition of Bengal declare hui (20 July 1905) → Swadeshi Movement announce hui (7\nAugust 1905) → Swaraj ko Congress ka goal accept kiya gaya (December 1906, Calcutta) → Surat Split\n(1907). [Q225]\n● Sequence: Regulating Act, Partition of Bengal, Muslim League ki sthapna, Surat Split — sabhi 20th\ncentury ki shuruaat ke pehle ke events hain, jo colonial governance ke evolution ko dikhate hain. [Q184]\n● Sequence: Swadeshi Movement (1905) → Home Rule Movement (1916) → Non-cooperation (1920) →\nCivil Disobedience (1930). [Q222]\n● Sequence: Swadeshi Movement se lekar Civil Disobedience Movement tak ke important milestones ek\nchain mein connect hote hain — har movement pichle se seekh leta hai. [Q177]\n96. Chronology — Rowlatt to Jallianwala Bagh (Multiple Sequences)\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha (April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh\nMassacre (13 April 1919) → Chauri-Chaura Episode (4 Feb 1922). [Q154]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha\n(April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q153]\n● Sequence: Jallianwala Bagh Tragedy (13 April 1919) → Formation of Swaraj Party (1923) → Naujawan\nBharat Sabha ki foundation (March 1926) → Dandi March (1930). [Q157]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13\nApril 1919) → Khilafat Movement (October 1919). [Q146]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (Dec 1916) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) → Tilak ki death (1\nAug 1920) → Swaraj Party ki formation (1923). [Q147]\n● Sequence: Champaran Movement (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) → Moplah\nMovement (1921) → Chauri-Chaura Incident (4 Feb 1922). [Q197, Q232]\n● Sequence: Champaran (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh (1919) → Non-cooperation Movement (1920) →\nCivil Disobedience Movement (1930). [Q186]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil\nDisobedience Movement (1930) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q180]\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (I) → Non-Cooperation Movement (II) → Quit India Movement (IV)\n→ Civil Disobedience Movement (III) is one order variant. [Q141]\n97. Chronology — Lahore Session, Communal Award & Poona Pact\n● Sequence: Simon Commission (arrived 1928) → Dandi March (March-April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact\n(5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q126]\n● Sequence: Dandi Yatra (12 March 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Communal Award (16\nAugust 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q127]\n● Sequence: Chauri-Chaura Incident (1922) → Dandi March (1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (March 1931) →\nCommunal Award (August 1932) — Communal Award sabse aakhri hua. [Q124]"," ● Sequence: Complete Independence Resolution (31 Dec 1929) → Purna Swaraj Day (26 Jan 1930) →\nDandi March (12 March 1930) → Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept 1931). [Q208]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March\n1931) → Poona Pact (1932). [Q198]\n● Sequence: Complete National Independence ki declaration (31 December 1929) → Civil Disobedience\nCampaign (6 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Agreement (5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 Sept 1932).\n[Q199]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Second Round Table\nConference (Sept-Dec 1931) → Communal Award (16 August 1932). [Q200]\n● Sequence: Communal Award (16 August 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932) → Third Round\nTable Conference (17 Nov-24 Dec 1932) → August Offer (1940). [Q195]\n● Sequence: Martyrdom of Chandra Shekhar Azad (27 Feb 1931) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) →\nExecution of Bhagat Singh-Sukhdev-Rajguru (23 March 1931) → Karachi Session of INC (29-31 March\n1931). [Q245]\n● Sequence: Lahore Session of Congress (December 1929) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) →\nBhagat Singh-Sukhdev-Rajguru ki execution (23 March 1931) → Karachi Session of Congress (29-31\nMarch 1931). [Q246]\n● Simon Commission (2), Poona Pact (4), Cripps Mission (3), Cabinet Mission (1) — is sequence mein\narrange hue. [Q219]\n98. Chronology — August Offer to Cabinet Mission (1940-1946)\n● Sequence: Congress Ministries ka resignation (October 1939) → Ramgarh Congress Session (March\n1940) → Linlithgow ka August Offer (August 1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942). [Q129]\n● Sequence: August Offer (August 1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942) → C.R. Formula (July 1944) →\nWavell Plan (1945). [Q171]\n● Sequence: August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942) → Quit India Movement (August 1942)\n→ Desai-Liaquat Pact (1945). [Q172]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (1942) → Wavell Plan\n(1945). [Q194, Q202]\n● Cripps Mission (March 1942) pehle event thi — Quit India Resolution (August 1942), Lord Wavell ka\nViceroy ki tarah aana (October 1943), aur Cabinet Mission ka aana (March 1946) baad mein hue. [Q170]\n● Sequence: August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (1942) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan\n(1946). [Q193]\n● Sequence: C.R. Formula (1944) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan (1946) → Mountbatten\nPlan (1947). [Q201]\n● Sequence: Jinnah ne Shimla Conference todi (14 July 1945) → Cabinet Mission ka aana (24 March\n1946) → Muslim League ka Direct Action (16 August 1946) → Interim Government ki formation (2\nSeptember 1946). [Q128]\n● Sequence: UK Parliamentary Delegation ka aana (January 1946) → Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n(February 1946) → Cabinet Mission ka aana (March 1946) → Interim Government ki formation\n(September 1946). [Q168]"," ● Match: GoI Act 1935; Cripps Proposals (1942); August Offer (1940); Wavell Plan (1945) — inke sahi\ncorresponding years/sequences. [Q169]\n● Sequence: C.R. Formula (July 1944) → Gandhi-Jinnah Dialogue (September 1944) → Wavell Plan\n(June 1945) → Cabinet Mission (March 1946). [Q210]\n● Sequence: Cripps Mission (March 1942) → Individual Satyagraha (1940, waapas count karke pehle) →\nQuit India Movement (August 1942) — variant sequence with Civil Disobedience (1930) leading. [Q218]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission (arrived Feb 1928) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Cripps\nMission (March 1942) → Partition of the country (midnight 14-15 August 1947). [Q182]\n● Sequence: Cripps Mission (March 1942), August Offer (1940), Nehru Report (1928), Wavell Plan (1945)\n— sahi order Nehru Report → August Offer → Cripps Mission → Wavell Plan hai. [Q192]\n● Sequence: Poona Pact (1932) → Quit India Movement (9 August 1942) → Simla Conference (25 June\n1945) → Cabinet Mission (24 March 1946 ko arrive hui). [Q223]\n● Sequence: Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept-1 Dec 1931) → Quit India Movement (9 August\n1942) → Royal Indian Navy mein mutiny (18-23 February 1946). [Q224]\n● 'Deepavali Declaration' (31 October 1929, Viceroy Lord Irwin) — India ke liye Dominion Status promise\nkarne se related thi. [Q173]\n99. Match Lists — Movements & Their Leaders/Founders\n● Match: Azad Muslim Conference → Allah Baksh; Khaksar Party → Allama Mashriqui; Khudai\nKhidmatgar → Abdul Gaffar Khan; Krishak Praja Party → Fazlul Haq. [Q131]\n● Match: Bardoli Satyagraha → Sardar Patel (1928); Champaran Satyagraha → Gandhi (1917); Kuka\nMovement → Ram Singh; Lal Kurti Movement → Gaffar Khan. [Q132]\n●\n Disputed: Awadh Kisan Sabha, JL Nehru-Baba Ram Chandra ke efforts se bani; All India Kisan\n⚠️\nSabha (1936) mein Narendra Dev jaise prominent members the, Sahajanand Saraswati ne shuru ki —\nquestion ke sabhi options sahi lagne ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q133]\n●\n Disputed: Khilafat Movement → Ali Brothers; Home Rule Movement → Tilak; Civil Disobedience\n⚠️\nMovement → Khan Brothers;\n B.R. Ambedkar Quit India Movement mein participate NAHI hue the\n⚠️\n(Aruna Asaf Ali associate thi) — flawed options ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q134]\n●\n Trap: 'M.A. Jinnah - Khilafat Movement' galat match hai — Jinnah ne Khilafat Movement mein\n⚠️\nGandhi ki ninda ki thi aur is se door rahe, Ali Brothers (Shaukat-Muhammad) ne movement start ki thi.\n[Q135]\n● Match: Vinoba Bhave → Individual Satyagraha; B.G. Tilak → Home Rule Movement; Aruna Asaf Ali →\nQuit India Movement; Sarojini Naidu → Dharsana Raid. [Q136]\n● Sahi pair: 'C.R. Das - Deshbandhu' — Vinoba Bhave pehle Individual Satyagrahi the (doosre NAHI),\nRash Behari Ghosh 1907 Surat Session ke President the, Shyamji Krishna Verma ne India House\nLondon mein banayi thi (Paris mein NAHI). [Q137]\n● Match: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Annie Besant; Bardoli Satyagraha (1928) → Sardar Patel; Non-\nCooperation Movement (1920) → M.K. Gandhi; Swaraj Party (1923) → C.R. Das. [Q138]\n● Match: Mahatma Gandhi → Dandi March; Jawaharlal Nehru → Complete Independence Demand\n(Lahore Session); Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan → Red Shirt Movement; Vallabhbhai Patel → Bardoli\nSatyagraha. [Q139]"," ● Match: Complete Independence Resolution (31 Dec 1929, Congress) → Purna Swaraj Day (26 Jan\n1930) → Dandi March start (12 March 1930) → Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept 1931). [Q209]\n● Match: Annie Besant → Home Rule Movement (Sept 1916); Rajendra Prasad → Champaran\nSatyagraha (1917); Jawaharlal Nehru → Lahore Session (1929); Ambika Charan Majumdar → Lucknow\nSession (1916). [Q167]\n● Match: Madan Mohan Malviya → BHU founder; Motilal Nehru → Swaraj Party (1923); Annie Besant →\nHome Rule League (1916); Gopal Krishna Gokhale → Servants of India Society (1905). [Q212]\n● Match: Khaksars → Inayatullah Mashriqui; Socialist Party → Jayaprakash Narayan; Independent\nLabour Party → B.R. Ambedkar; Forward Bloc → Subhas Chandra Bose. [Q213]\n●\n Trap: Ghadar Party — Lala Lajpat Rai se NAHI, Sohan Singh Bhakna-Lala Hardayal ne San\n⚠️\nFrancisco (USA) mein 1913 mein banayi thi. [Q214]\n● Match: Subhash Chandra Bose → Haripura Session of INC; Vallabhbhai Patel → Operation Polo; Iqbal\n→ Allahabad Session of Muslim League (1930); Batukeshwar Dutt → Central Assembly mein bomb\n(Bhagat Singh ke saath). [Q247]\n100. Match Lists & Not-Correctly-Matched Traps — Various Pairs\n●\n Trap: 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak — Satya Shodhak Sabha' galat match hai — Satya Shodhak Samaj\n⚠️\n(1873) Jyotiba Phule ne banayi thi. [Q158]\n●\n Trap: 'Bombay Chronicle — Gopal Krishna Gokhale' galat match hai — Bombay Chronicle\n⚠️\nPherozeshah Mehta ne 1910 mein publish ki thi. [Q206]\n● Statement check: Asaf Ali ne 1946 mein Railway Ministry sambhali (sahi), Ancient Monuments\nPreservation Act 1904 mein Curzon ne pass ki (sahi) — lekin Haripura Session (1938) ki presidency\nSubhash Chandra Bose ne ki, C.R. Das ne NAHI (galat) — Swami Shraddhanand ne Rowlatt Act ke\nagainst no-tax campaign suggest ki (sahi). [Q143]\n● Match: Rani Durgavati → Garha Katanga (Gara Mandal); Ahilya Bai → Holkar State; Lakshmi Bai →\nJhansi; Razia Sultan → Delhi. [Q144]\n●\n Trap: 'Governor-General of Bengal jab Pitt's India Act pass hui — Lord Minto' galat hai — us waqt\n⚠️\nWarren Hastings the. [Q165]\n● Statement check: Theodore Beck M.A.O. College Aligarh ke pehle principal the (sahi), Ilbert Bill 1884\nmein Ripon ke time pass hui (sahi), Pherozeshah Mehta INC ke founder member the (sahi) — lekin\nBadruddin Tyabji Muslim League se NAHI, Congress ke pehle Muslim President (1887) the (galat).\n[Q183]\n● Swadeshi Movement se lekar Movements — women ne har major national movement (Swadeshi, Home\nRule, Non-Cooperation, Civil Disobedience) mein active participate kiya, gharelu seclusion se bahar\naakar. [Q185]\n● Statement check: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) mein Rajendra Prasad-J.B. Kripalani associate the\n(sahi) — Ahmedabad Mill Workers Satyagraha Anusuya Ben ke saath thi, Morarji Desai ke NAHI (galat)\n— Kheda Satyagraha Indulal Yagnik-Vallabhbhai Patel ke saath launch hui (sahi). [Q220]\n●\n Trap: 'Suresh Tendulkar - Political Scientist' galat match hai — Suresh Tendulkar ek economist the.\n⚠️\n[Q236]"," ●\n Trap: 'The National Song Vande Mataram poori tarah Bengali mein compose hui' — ye statement\n⚠️\ngalat hai — Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ne ise Bengali AUR Sanskrit — dono mein compose kiya, apne\nnovel 'Anand Math' mein. [Q238]\n101. The Trade Disputes Act, 1929\n● 'Trade Disputes Act, 1929' ne tribunals ka system banaya (Board of Conciliation, Court of Inquiry) — aur\npublicly useful services mein bina prior notice ke strikes-lockouts ko ban kiya. [Q216]\n102. Nehru's Political Career — Terms & Statements\n● Statement check: Nehru 1952, 1957, 1962 mein elections jeetkar 4th term mein Prime Minister the\n(1964 mein mrityu tak, sahi statement) — wo Phulpur constituency represent karte the, Rae Bareilly\nNAHI (galat) — Morarji Desai March 1977 mein first Non-Congress PM (Janata Party) bane (sahi).\n[Q233]\n● Assertion-Reason: Nehru ka Upanishads ke prati koi reverence NAHI tha — ye Assertion GALAT hai\n(unka Upanishads mein bahut vishwas tha) — Reason sahi hai ki wo modern India ke 'father of science'\nmane jaate the, scientific point of view rakhte the. [Q226]\n103. Quotes — Attlee, Cripps\n● British PM Clement Attlee ne kaha tha ki 'Imperialism is dead as Dodo' (extinct bird ki tarah). [Q227]\n● 'Here is a revolution taking place and we should move quickly' — ye statement Sir Stafford Cripps ne\ndiya, jo Cripps Mission (1942) aur Cabinet Mission (1946) — dono se juday the. [Q228]\n104. World History — Atomic Bomb & French Revolution\n● Pehla atomic bomb 6 August 1945 ko Hiroshima (Japan) mein giraya gaya — doosra 9 August 1945 ko\nNagasaki mein. [Q230]\n● French Revolution 1789 mein shuru hui — feudalism, class privilege, autocracy ke against middle-class\nlogo ki revolution thi. [Q231]\n105. Disputed Match — Pact/Year & Place\n●\n Disputed: Lucknow Pact (1916) aur Liaquat Ali-Bhulabhai Desai Pact (1945) — dono sahi matched\n⚠️\nhain, isliye Chhattisgarh PSC ki revised answer key ne ye question evaluation se hataya. [Q235]\n●\n Disputed: Bardoli Gujarat mein hai, Chauri-Chaura Gorakhpur (UP) mein, Yerwada Jail Maharashtra\n⚠️\n\nmein — Noakhali (Bangladesh, purana East Bengal) ka exact matching option confusion ki wajah se ye\nquestion disputed hai. [Q237]"," 106. Post-Independence Foreign Affairs Chronology\n● Sequence: Khrushchev-Bulganin ki India visit (1955) → Dalai Lama ka India bhaagna (1959) → Chou-\nen-Lai ki India visit (April 1960) → Goa ki liberation (1961). [Q239]\n107. The Shimla Agreement (1972)\n● India-Pakistan ke beech 'Shimla Agreement' June-July 1972 mein sign hui — Pakistan President\nZulfiqar Ali Bhutto aur Indian PM Indira Gandhi ke beech, 1971 War ke baad. [Q240]\n108. 'Operation Vijay' — Kargil War\n● 'Operation Vijay' 1999 mein, Pakistan ke against, India ne successfully conduct ki (Kargil War). [Q241]\n109. Kisan Diwas\n● 'Kisan Diwas' 23 December ko manaya jaata hai — ex-PM Chaudhary Charan Singh ki yaad mein.\n[Q242]\n110. Nobel Prize Winners — Match List\n● Match: Rabindranath Tagore → Literature (1913); Amartya Sen → Economics (1998); Chandra Shekhar\n→ Physics/Astrophysics (1983); Vinoo Mankad → Cricket (famous player, Nobel NAHI). [Q243]\n● Rabindranath Tagore, Nobel Prize jeetne wale pehle Indian the — 'Gitanjali' ke liye 1913 mein Literature\nka Nobel — pehle Asian bhi the jinhe Nobel mila. [Q244]\n111. World Political Events — 20th Century\n● China ne 1959 mein Tibet par firmly occupy kiya — jisse Dalai Lama India bhaag aaye, aur Tibet ki\nautonomy khatam ho gayi. [Q259]\n● USSR (Soviet Union) 1991 mein disintegrate hokar 15 alag countries mein baat gaya — Russia iska\nprimary successor state ban gaya (26 December 1991). [Q260]\n● Indo-Pakistan War (December 1971) ke baad Bangladesh ek independent nation ban gaya — 16\nDecember 1971 ko East Pakistan azaad hokar Bangladesh bana. [Q261]\n● Germany, WWII ke baad East-West mein bata hua, 3 October 1990 ko officially reunite hua. [Q262]\n● USA ne WWII mein Japan ke Pearl Harbour attack (December 1941) ke baad militarily participate kiya.\n[Q263]"," 112. World Leaders — Firsts & Notable Figures\n● George Washington, USA ke pehle President the (1789-1797). [Q264]\n● Richard Nixon (37th US President), Watergate Scandal ki wajah se, resign karne wale ekmatra US\nPresident the (1974 mein). [Q265]\n● Bishop Desmond Tutu, South Africa se juday the — 1980s ke anti-racism movement ke liye world-\nfamous hue, 1984 mein Nobel Peace Prize mila. [Q266]\n113. World History — Paper, Philosophy & the Renaissance\n● Tsai-Lun ko China mein pehli 'real paper' banane ka credit jaata hai — lagbhag 105 AD mein. [Q267]\n● Greek philosopher Plato, Socrates ke disciple the — Aristotle, Plato ke disciple the. [Q268]\n● Italian Renaissance (14th century) ka main cause tha 'freedom to express ideas' — ye modern era ki\nshuruaat maani jaati hai. [Q269]\n114. The 'Kallar' Rebels of Madurai\n● 'Kallar' log, British India ke rebellions ke context mein, Madurai aur uske aas-paas ke South India ke\narea se belong karte the — unhone British control ke against revolt ki. [Q270]\n115. The Indian Councils Act of 1909\n● Act of 1909 (Morley-Minto Reforms) 'Separate Electorate' ke introduction se associate thi. [Q271]\n116. Rama Devi — The Bijolia Peasant Movement\n● Rama Devi Choudhary (Odisha logo dwara 'Maa' kehlaati thi) ne Bijoliya Peasant Movement mein\nparticipate kiya aur arrest hui — 1930 Salt Satyagraha aur Civil Disobedience Movement mein bhi baar-\nbaar arrest hui. [Q272]\n117. Political Party Founding Years — Match List\n● Match: Indian National Congress (1885); Bharatiya Jan Sangh (1951); Communist Party of India (1925);\nA.I.A.D.M.K. (1972). [Q273]\n118. The 'Imperial Gazetteer' — W.W. Hunter"," ● William Wilson Hunter, ek Indian Civil Services member, ne famous reference work 'The Imperial\nGazetteer of India' compile ki. [Q274]\n119. Gandhi & the Term 'Panchayati Raj'\n● Rural local governments ko 'Panchayati Raj' naam dene ka suggestion Mahatma Gandhi ka tha — unka\nmaanna tha ki villages sirf economically NAHI, politically-administratively bhi independent hone chahiye.\n[Q275]\n120. The Indian National Calendar\n● Indian National Calendar (Saka Samvat) ka pehla mahina 'Chaitra' hai — jo Gregorian Calendar ke\nMarch-April se milta hai; 'Phalgun' aakhri mahina hai. [Q276]\n121. Additional Committees, Chronology & Facts\n●\n Disputed: Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ke baare mein — Baldev Singh India ke pehle Defence Minister the\n⚠️\n(Ambedkar NAHI, statement galat), Bahishkrit Hitkarini Sabha 1924 mein bani (1925 NAHI, statement\ngalat) — koi option perfectly match nahi karta. [Q106]\n● Sequence: Surat Split (1907) → Simon Commission (1928) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) →\nKhudai Khidmatgar Movement (1930, closely associated). [Q130]\n●\n Disputed: Swadeshi Movement (1905) → Muslim League ki foundation (1906) → Morley-Minto\n⚠️\nReforms (1909) → Lucknow Pact (1916) — sahi order A-D-C-B hona chahiye tha, diye gaye options\nmein se koi match nahi karta. [Q148]\n●\n Disputed: Rowlatt Satyagraha (6 April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) →\n⚠️\nKhilafat Movement (October 1919) → Amritsar Session of INC (26-30 Dec 1919) — sahi order 4,2,1,3\nhona chahiye, koi option perfectly match nahi karta. [Q149]\n● Sequence: Dandi March (12 March-5 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Communal\nAward (16 August 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q151]\n● Sequence: Civil Disobedience Movement (6 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Poona\nPact (24 September 1932) → Cripps Mission (March 1942). [Q152]\n● Sequence: Ferozshah Mehta ki death (5 November 1915) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919)\n→ Simon Commission ki appointment (November 1927) → Dandi March (12 March 1930). [Q163]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission ki constitution (1927) → Nehru Report (1928) → Sharda Act (1929) →\nDandi March (1930). [Q164]\n●\n Trap: 'Famine in Western U.P. — 1871-72' galat match hai — actual mein 1860-61 mein hui thi.\n⚠️\n[Q174]\n● Match: Butler Committee (1927) → Princely States-British Govt relationship; Hartog Committee (1929)\n→ Education ka growth; Hunter Inquiry Committee (1919) → Jallianwala Bagh massacre investigation;\nMuddiman Committee (1924) → Dyarchy ka working (Montagu-Chelmsford). [Q175]"," ●\n Trap: 'Lala Lajpat Rai kabhi INC President elect NAHI hue' — ye statement GALAT hai — wo 1920\n⚠️\nke Calcutta Special Session ke President the. [Q176]\n● Sequence: Kamagatamaru Incident (1914) → Gandhi ka South Africa se India aana (9 January 1915) →\nTilak ki Home Rule League (April 1916). [Q178]\n● Sequence: August Offer (8 August 1940) → Quit India Movement (1942) → INA Trial (November 1945)\n→ Royal Indian Naval Ratings Revolt (February 1946). [Q179]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission ki formation (1927) → Quit India Movement (1942) → INC ki formation\n(1885, sabse pehle) → Morley Minto Reforms (1909) — inka sahi chronological order 3,2,1,4 hai (INC\nformation sabse pehle). [Q181]\n● Match: Separate Electorate ki shuruaat → Morley Minto Reforms (1909); Congress-League Agreement\n→ Lucknow Pact (1916); Communal Award (1932); Deliverance Day (22 December 1939). [Q188]\n● Chronologically pehla event: First Anglo-Sikh War (1845-46) — Santhal Revolt (1855-56), Lord Lytton\nka Delhi Darbar (1877), aur Ilbert Bill Controversy (1883) baad mein hue. [Q190]\n● Sequence: Cripps Plan (1942) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan (1946) → Mountbatten\nPlan (1947). [Q191]\n● Sequence: Khilafat Movement (October 1919) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil\nDisobedience Movement (1930) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q196]\n● Lord Wavell ne, tatkaleen Viceroy ki tarah, 1945 mein apni 'Wavell Plan' present ki — Shimla mein ek\nconference bulaayi, Interim Government banane jaise proposals ke saath. [Q203]\n● Match: Non-cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) → Congress\nMinistries ki formation (1937) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q211]\n● Sequence: Minto-Morley Reforms (1909) → Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms (1919) → Chauri-Chaura\nOutrage (1922) → Dandi March (1930). [Q215]\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Tilak ki death (1 August 1920) → Dandi March (12 March\n1930) → Shimla Pact/Conference (25 June 1945). [Q221]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (1916) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 September\n1932) → Civil Disobedience Movement ki final withdrawal (1934). [Q234]\n● 'Butler Committee' (1927), Sir Harcourt Butler ki chairmanship mein — Government of India aur Indian\nPrincely States ke beech relationship improve karne ke liye banayi gayi. [Q248]\n● Indian Princely States ke special rights aur privy purse 1971 mein, 26th Constitutional Amendment Act\nse abolish hue. [Q249]\n● Pehli 'All India Socialist Youth Congress' (27 December 1928, Calcutta) ki presidency Jawaharlal Nehru\nne ki. [Q250]\n● 'Hind Mazdoor Sabha' (HMS) December 1948 mein, Calcutta mein, ek trade union conference mein\nbani — Ashok Mehta, T.S. Ramanujam aur G.G. Mehta ismein founders the. [Q251]\n● 'Alipore Central Jail' Kolkata mein situated hai — 1906 mein establish hui, British India ke political\nprisoners yahi qaid rehte the. [Q252]\n● 'Operation Polo' Hyderabad State mein September 1948 mein hui military action ka code name tha —\nIndian Armed Forces ne Hyderabad state invade karke Nizam ko overthrow kiya, Indian Union mein\nannex kiya. [Q253]"," ● West Bengal ki 'Secretariat Building' ko 'Writer's Building' kehte hain — Kolkata mein hai, originally 1777\nmein East India Company ke junior servants (Writers) ke liye bani thi. [Q254]\n● 'Teen Murti Bhavan' (India ke pehle PM Jawaharlal Nehru ka purana residence) ko 'Prime Ministers\nMuseum' mein convert kiya gaya — PM Narendra Modi ne 14 April 2022 ko inaugurate kiya. [Q255]\n● Karl Marx ne class struggle ka process 'Dialectical Materialism' theory se explain kiya — unke mutabik\nsociety ki history economic causes se determine hoti hai, jo inherently class struggle paida karti hain.\n[Q256]\n●\n Trap: Mother Teresa apni mrityu (5 September 1997) ke waqt Indian citizen NAHI thi — ye\n⚠️\nstatement GALAT hai. [Q257]\n● Mother Teresa dwara establish ki gayi religious organization 'Missionaries of Charity' kehlaati hai. [Q258]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Modern History Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0255","t":"53 Magazines Books and Their Authors","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.53 — MAGAZINES, BOOKS & THEIR AUTHORS — FULL MIND MAP\n📚\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — 'Gift to Monotheists'\n2. Freedom Struggle Autobiographies — Important Match Lists\n3. Manubehn Gandhi — 'Bapu: My Mother'\n4. Abul Kalam Azad — 'India Wins Freedom'\n5. Bal Gangadhar Tilak — 'Gita Rahasya'\n6. Aurobindo Ghosh's Philosophical Works\n7. Col. James Tod — 'Annals and Antiquities of Rajasthan'\n8. Gopal Baba Walangkar — 'Vital-Vidhvansak'\n9. Lala Lajpat Rai — 'Unhappy India' & Other Works\n10. Dadabhai Naoroji — 'Poverty and Un-British Rule in India'\n11. Rafiq Zakaria — 'The Man Who Divided India'\n12. Historical Works — Match Lists\n13. Balkrishna Sharma Naveen — 'Pranarpan' & 'Atmosarga'\n14. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — 'Satyagrah' Trap\n15. Valentine Chirol — 'Indian Unrest'\n16. Surendranath Banerjee — 'A Nation in the Making'\n17. Subhash Chandra Bose — 'The Indian Struggle'\n18. Gandhi's Kausani Translation — 'Anasakti Yoga'\n19. Books on the Revolt of 1857 — Match Lists\n20. Sir Syed Ahmad Khan — 'Tahzib-ul-Akhlaq'\n21. Hugh Toye — 'The Springing Tiger' (Bose's Biography)\n22. Revolutionary Writings — Bhagat Singh & Comrades\n23. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar's Works\n24. Ram Manohar Lohia — 'The Guilty Men of India's Partition'\n25. Newspapers & Editors — Bengal Match List\n26. M.N. Roy — 'People's Plan' & 'Vanguard'\n27. Bankim Chandra Chatterjee — Novels\n28. Rabindranath Tagore — Literary Works & the National Anthem\n29. Match List — Michael Madhusudan Dutt, Tagore's 'Gora' & Sarojini Naidu\n30. Chittaranjan Das — 'India for Indians'\n31. Gandhi — 'Gokhale, My Political Guru'\n32. Dr. Rajendra Prasad — Works\n33. Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar — 'Bahuvivah'\n34. Hindi/Regional Novels — Match List\n35. Karl Marx — 'Das Capital'\n36. Chandeshwar & Vidyapati — Medieval Works\n37. Nawab Wajid Ali Shah — 'Kissa Radha Kanhaiya'\n38. Sakharam Ganesh Deuskar — 'Desher Katha'\n39. Kesari Singh Barahath — 'Chetavani Ra Chugatiya'\n40. Gandhi's Autobiography — 'The Story of My Experiments with Truth'\n40b. Gandhi's 'Songs from Prison'\n41. Bharatendu Harishchandra\n42. Subramaniam Bharati — The Tamil Poet\n43. Maithili Sharan Gupta — 'Bharat Bharati' & 'Rashtrakavi'\n44. Nationalist Poets — Who Was NOT One\n45. Nabin Chandra Das — 'Nawab'\n46. Jayaprakash Narayan — 'Towards Struggle', 'Prison Diary' & 'Sarvodaya Plan'\n47. E.M. Forster — 'A Passage to India'\n48. Bipan/Bipin Chandra — Historical Works\n49. Ramdhari Singh 'Dinkar' — 'Sanskriti Ke Char Adhyay'\n50. Professor George Brock\n51. Katherine Mayo — 'Mother India'\n52. Patriotic Songs — Jhanda Geet & Aie Mere Watan Ke Logo\n53. Muhammad Iqbal — 'Sare Jahan Se Achha'\n54. Manoranjan Prasad Singh — 'Firangiya'"," 55. Gurmukh Nihal Singh & G.A. Natesan\n56. Jawaharlal Nehru — 'The Discovery of India'\n57. Sachindranath Sanyal — 'Bandi Jiwan'\n58. Larry Collins & Dominique Lapierre — Partition Books\n59. W.H. Sleeman — Thuggee & Oudh\n60. V.D. Savarkar — 'Indian War of Independence 1857'\n61. Economic History Authors — Match List\n62. M. Visvesvaraya — 'Planned Economy for India'\n63. W.A. Fairservis — 'The Roots of Ancient India'\n64. The JP Movement Book — Disputed\n65. Match List — 'Priya Pravas', 'Gaban' & 'Shah Nama'\n66. Indian Writing in English — Match List\n67. B.S. Minhas — 'Planning and the Poor'\n68. Lord Curzon — 'The Problems of the Far East'\n69. General Kaul — 'The Untold Story'\n70. David Diringer — 'The Alphabet'\n71. Ruskin Bond — 'A Gallery of Rascals'\n72. 'The Proudest Day' — India's Independence Story\n73. Match List — 'My Music My Life' & Other Autobiographies\n74. 'Yayati' — A Common Trap\n75. Contemporary Indian Fiction — Match Lists\n76. Bureaucrat/Public Figure Memoirs — Match List\n77. Munshi Premchand — Novels\n78. R.K. Narayan — 'Malgudi Days'\n79. Hans Christian Andersen\n80. Match List — 'Pakistan Papers' & Other Non-Fiction\n81. Vikram Seth — 'The Golden Gate' & 'An Equal Music'\n82. Journalist Autobiographies — Vinod Mehta\n83. Rachel Carson — 'Silent Spring'\n84. Salman Rushdie's Works\n85. Jhumpa Lahiri — 'The Namesake' & 'Unaccustomed Earth'\n86. Bill Gates — 'The Road Ahead'\n87. Amritlal Nagar — 'Manas ke Hans'\n88. Sumitra Nandan Pant — Chhayavadi Poet\n89. Julia Delano — 'Dyna: A Tribute'\n90. Harry Potter — Cornelius Fudge\n91. Harivansh Rai Bachchan — Chronology\n92. Julio Ribeiro — 'Bullet for Bullet'\n93. Devanand — 'Romancing with Life'\n94. World Leaders' Autobiographies — Match List\n95. Rafiq Zakaria & Kalam — Match Lists\n96. Books on Muslims/Pakistan — Match List\n97. Mark Tully — 'The Heart of India'\n98. Taslima Nasrin — 'Lajja'\n99. George Orwell — 'Nineteen Eighty-Four'\n100. Arundhati Roy — 'The God of Small Things'\n101. Vrindavan Lal Verma — 'Mrignayani'\n102. Early Hindi Works — Chronology\n103. Durga Das — 'India from Curzon to Nehru and After'\n104. Subhadra Kumari Chauhan — 'Bikhre Moti' & 'Mukul'\n105. Vinod Kumar Shukla — 'Naukar ki Kameez'\n106. Charles Dickens — 'David Copperfield'\n107. Constitution-Related Books — Match List\n108. Jai Shankar Prasad — 'Kamayani'\n109. K.M. Panikkar — 'Geographical Factors in Indian History'\n110. Verrier Elwin — 'The Baiga'\n111. Khushwant Singh — 'Truth, Love and a Little Malice'\n112. Political Leader Books — Vajpayee & Kalam\n113. Fareed Zakaria — 'The Post-American World'\n114. V.P. Menon — 'The Story of the Integration of the Indian States'\n115. P.V. Narasimha Rao — 'Ayodhya: 6 December, 1992'\n116. Booker Prize Winners — Match List\n117. Soli Sorabjee Book — Disputed"," 118. Lal Bahadur Shastri — Translation of Madame Curie\n119. Faiz Ahmed Faiz — 'Subh-e-Azadi'\n120. Elizabeth Hawley — Himalayan Expeditions\n121. Medieval Chronicles — Match List\n122. Bengal School Painters — Disputed\n123. Barack Obama — 'The Audacity of Hope'\n124. Gunnar Myrdal — 'The Challenge of World Poverty'\n125. Rajni Kothari — 'Politics in India'\n126. Musharraf's Book — The Ghostwriter\n127. Old Hindi Works — Match List\n128. Dharam Veer Bharti — 'Andha Yug'\n129. Bhawani Prasad & Makhanlal Chaturvedi — A Trap\n130. Abdul Bismillah — 'Jhini Jhini Bini Chadariya'\n131. Sunil Gavaskar — 'One-Day Wonders'\n132. World Political Figures — Match List\n133. Prince Harry — 'Spare'\n134. Women Poets — A Match Trap\n1. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — 'Gift to Monotheists'\n●\n Disputed: Ram Mohan Roy ne 'Tuhfat-ul-Muwahhiddin' Persian language mein likhi thi (1884 mein\n⚠️\n'A Gift to Monotheists' naam se translate hui) — options mein Persian na hone ki wajah se ye dono\nquestions disputed/cancel maane jaate hain. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Freedom Struggle Autobiographies — Important Match Lists\n● Match: Annie Besant → New India (aur Commonweal, 1914); Hind Swaraj → Mahatma Gandhi; India\nWins Freedom → Abul Kalam Azad. Young India Gandhi ne bhi likhi. [Q3, Q16]\n● Match: The Story of My Deportation → Lala Lajpat Rai; Gita Rahasya → B.G. Tilak; A Nation in Making\n→ Surendranath Banerjee; India Wins Freedom → Abul Kalam Azad. [Q17]\n● Match: Surendranath Banerjee → A Nation in Making; M.K. Gandhi → Hind Swaraj; Subhash Chandra\nBose → The Indian Struggle; Lala Lajpat Rai → Autobiographical Writings. [Q24]\n●\n Trap: 'Hind Swaraj' Jawaharlal Nehru ne NAHI, Mahatma Gandhi ne likhi thi — India Wins Freedom\n⚠️\n(Azad), Unhappy India (Lajpat Rai), The Indian Struggle (Bose). [Q27]\n● Match: Frank Moraes → Jawaharlal Nehru-A Biography; Louis Fischer → The Life of Mahatma Gandhi;\nDurga Das → India from Curzon to Nehru and After. [Q42]\n●\n Trap: 'India from Curzon to Nehru and After' Frank Moraes ne NAHI, Durga Das ne likhi thi.\n⚠️\n[Q43]\n● Match: Rafiq Zakaria → The Man Who Divided India; Lala Lajpat Rai → Unhappy India; Dadabhai\nNaoroji → Poverty and Un-British Rule in India; Subhash Chandra Bose → The Indian Struggle; Ram\nManohar Lohia → Guilty Men of India's Partition. [Q44]\n● Match: Mahatma Gandhi → Hind Swaraj; Ram Manohar Lohia → The Wheel of History; Dr. Rajendra\nPrasad → India Divided; Abul Kalam Azad → India Wins Freedom. [Q54]\n● Match: Rajendra Prasad → India Divided; Dilip Mukherji → Terrorist; S.N. Banerjee → A Nation in\nMaking; Mahatma Gandhi → The Story of My Experiments with Truth. [Q61]\n● Match: D.P. Mishra → Living an Era; Jawaharlal Nehru → Discovery of India; Rajendra Prasad → India\nDivided; Larry Collins-Dominique Lapierre → Freedom at Midnight. [Q62]"," ● Sahi match: Rafiq Zakaria — The Man Who Divided India; Valentine Chirol — Indian Unrest; Subhash\nChandra Bose — The Indian Struggle; Lala Lajpat Rai — Unhappy India; V.D. Savarkar — Hindutva.\n[Q22]\n● Match: Lady Catherine Mayo → Mother India; Larry Collins-Dominique Lapierre → Freedom at Midnight;\nRam Manohar Lohia → Guilty Men of India's Partition; Jawaharlal Nehru → The Discovery of India.\n[Q117]\n3. Manubehn Gandhi — 'Bapu: My Mother'\n● 'Bapu: My Mother' memoir Manubehn Gandhi ne likhi thi. [Q4]\n4. Abul Kalam Azad — 'India Wins Freedom'\n● 'India Wins Freedom' Maulana Abul Kalam Azad ki autobiography hai. [Q5, Q56]\n5. Bal Gangadhar Tilak — 'Gita Rahasya'\n● 'Gita Rahasya' (Srimad Bhagavad Gita Rahasya) Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne Mandalay jail mein Marathi\nmein likhi. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n6. Aurobindo Ghosh's Philosophical Works\n● Aurobindo Ghosh, 1910 mein politics se retire hokar Pondicherry mein rehne lage — unhone 'The Life\nDivine', 'The Ideal of Human Unity' aur 'Essays on the Gita' jaisi texts likhi. [Q9]\n● 'New Lamps for Old' Aurobindo Ghosh ne likhi thi. [Q21]\n● 'The Foundation of Indian Culture' Shri Aurobindo ne likhi. [Q64]\n7. Col. James Tod — 'Annals and Antiquities of Rajasthan'\n● Lt. Col. James Tod ne 19th century mein Rajasthan mein 'Feudalism' ke baare mein likha, apni book\n'Annals and Antiquities of Rajasthan' mein. [Q10]\n8. Gopal Baba Walangkar — 'Vital-Vidhvansak'\n● 'Vital-Vidhvansak', untouchable logo ko target karne wala pehla monthly journal, Gopal Baba Walangkar\nne 1888 mein, Marathi mein, publish ki. [Q11]\n9. Lala Lajpat Rai — 'Unhappy India' & Other Works"," ●\n Trap: 'Unhappy India' Bal Gangadhar Tilak ne NAHI, Lala Lajpat Rai ne likhi — Tilak ne 'Kesari' aur\n⚠️\n'The Mahratta' edit ki. [Q12]\n● 'Unhappy India' Lala Lajpat Rai ne likhi — usmein unhone Indian society ko contemporary USA-Britain\nse compare kiya. [Q30]\n10. Dadabhai Naoroji — 'Poverty and Un-British Rule in India'\n● 'Poverty and Un-British Rule in India' Dadabhai Naoroji ne likhi — India ki wealth ki Britain ki taraf\ndraining ko highlight kiya. [Q13, Q45]\n11. Rafiq Zakaria — 'The Man Who Divided India'\n●\n Trap: 'The Man Who Divided India' K.K. Aziz ne NAHI, Rafiq Zakaria ne likhi thi.\n⚠️\n[Q14, Q15]\n12. Historical Works — Match Lists\n● Match: Hindu Polity → K.P. Jayaswal; The Wonder That Was India → A.L. Basham; Introduction to the\nStudy of Indian History → D.D. Kosambi; The Early History of India → Vincent Arthur Smith. [Q18]\n● Match: Lallanji Gopal → The Economic Life of Northern India; Habib-Nizami → A Comprehensive\nHistory of India-The Delhi Sultanate; K.S. Lal → History of the Khaljis; Dasharath Sharma → Early\nChauhan Dynasties. [Q25]\n● Match: History of the Freedom Movement in India → Tara Chand; History of the Freedom Movement in\nBihar → K.K. Dutta; Anand Math → Bankim Chandra Chatterjee; Precepts of Jesus → Raja Ram Mohan\nRoy; The Indian Musalmans → W.W. Hunter. [Q31]\n13. Balkrishna Sharma Naveen — 'Pranarpan' & 'Atmosarga'\n● Balkrishna Sharma Naveen ne 2 kavyas — 'Pranarpan' aur 'Atmosarga' — Ganesh Shankar Vidyarthi\npar likhi. [Q19]\n14. Gopal Krishna Gokhale — 'Satyagrah' Trap\n●\n Trap: 'Satyagrah' Gopal Krishna Gokhale ne NAHI, Vinoba Bhave ne likhi thi.\n⚠️\n[Q20]\n15. Valentine Chirol — 'Indian Unrest'\n● 'Indian Unrest' Valentine Chirol ne likhi — unhone Bal Gangadhar Tilak ko 'The Father of Indian Unrest'\nbataya, jiske liye Tilak ne unpar defamation case kiya. [Q23]"," 16. Surendranath Banerjee — 'A Nation in the Making'\n● 'A Nation in Making' Surendranath Banerjee ne likhi. [Q26]\n17. Subhash Chandra Bose — 'The Indian Struggle'\n● 'The Indian Struggle' Subhash Chandra Bose ne likhi. [Q28]\n18. Gandhi's Kausani Translation — 'Anasakti Yoga'\n● 1929 mein, Mahatma Gandhi ne Kausani (Uttarakhand) mein rehte hue, Bhagavad Gita ke 'Anasakti\nYoga' translation complete ki. [Q29]\n19. Books on the Revolt of 1857 — Match Lists\n●\n Trap: 'Awadh in Revolt (1857-1858)' Radha Kamal Mukharjee ne NAHI likhi — ye galat matched pair\n⚠️\n\nhai (actual author Rudrangshu Mukherjee hai). [Q32]\n● Match: V.D. Savarkar → The Indian War of Independence, 1857; R.C. Majumdar → The Sepoy Mutiny\nand the Revolt of 1857; S.B. Chaudhuri → Civil Rebellion in the Indian Mutinies (1857-1859); Ashok\nMehta → 1857: The Great Rebellion. [Q33]\n●\n Disputed: V.D. Savarkar → The Indian War of Independence 1857; S.N. Sen → Eighteen Fifty-\n⚠️\nSeven; Eric Stokes → The Peasant and The Raj; S.B. Chaudhuri → Civil Rebellion in the Indian\nMutinies — 'The First War of Independence' naam ki koi Savarkar book NAHI hai, isliye ye question\ndisputed hai. [Q34]\n20. Sir Syed Ahmad Khan — 'Tahzib-ul-Akhlaq'\n● Sir Syed Ahmad Khan ne apne ideas 'Tahzib-ul-Akhlaq' (Civilisation and Morality) magazine ke through\npromote kiye — 'Al-Hilal' Abul Kalam Azad ki newspaper thi. [Q35]\n21. Hugh Toye — 'The Springing Tiger' (Bose's Biography)\n● 'The Springing Tiger', Subhash Chandra Bose ki life story par based, Hugh Toye ne likhi — Towards\nStruggle (JP Narayan), India Divided (Rajendra Prasad), An American Witness to India's Partition\n(Phillips Talbot). [Q36, Q37, Q38]\n22. Revolutionary Writings — Bhagat Singh & Comrades"," ● 'An Introduction to the Dreamland' Bhagat Singh ne likhi — 'Bandi Jivan' Sachindranath Sanyal ne, 'The\nIndian Struggle' Subhash Bose ne, aur 'Why I am an Atheist' bhi Bhagat Singh ka essay hai. [Q39, Q109]\n●\n Trap: 'The Indian Sociologist' journal Bhagat Singh ne NAHI, Shyamji Krishna Verma ne London\n⚠️\nmein publish ki thi. [Q40]\n23. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar's Works\n● 'Annihilation of Caste' (1936 ka undelivered speech) Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne likha. [Q41]\n●\n Trap: 'Servants of India' book R.K. Laxman ne likhi thi, Dr. Ambedkar ne NAHI.\n⚠️\n[Q70]\n24. Ram Manohar Lohia — 'The Guilty Men of India's Partition'\n● 'The Guilty Men of India's Partition' Dr. Ram Manohar Lohia ne likhi — 'The Great Divide: Britain-India-\nPakistan' H.V. Hudson ne, 'Hind Swaraj' Gandhi ne, aur 'Glimpses of World History' Nehru ne likhi. [Q46,\nQ49]\n25. Newspapers & Editors — Bengal Match List\n● Match: The Bengalee → Surendranath Banerjee; Bangbasi → Jogendra Nath Bose; Vande Mataram →\nAurobindo Ghosh; Amrit Bazar Patrika → Motilal Ghosh. [Q47]\n26. M.N. Roy — 'People's Plan' & 'Vanguard'\n●\n Trap: 'People's Plan' Vinoba Bhave ne NAHI, M.N. Roy ne likhi thi — Indian Federation of Labour ki\n⚠️\nPost-war Re-construction committee ne draft ki. [Q48]\n● 'Vanguard' M.N. Roy ka emigre communist journal tha — wo Communist Party of India ke founder the\n(Tashkent mein). [Q71]\n27. Bankim Chandra Chatterjee — Novels\n● Match: Bankim Chandra Chatterjee → Devi Chaudhrani (1884); Dinabandhu Mitra → Nil Darpan;\nMunshi Prem Chand → Shatranj Ke Khilari; Devkinandan Khatri → Chandrakanta. [Q66]\n● 'Anand Math' national movement ke rise se associate hai — Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ne likhi,\njismein baad mein 'Vande Mataram' shaamil ki. [Q72, Q77, Q78]\n● 1865 mein Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ne apna pehla novel 'Durgesh Nandini' likha — Bengali\nhistorical novel. [Q73, Q74]\n● Match: The Indian War of Independence 1857 → V.D. Savarkar; Anand Math → Bankim Chandra\nChatterjee; The Life Divine → Sri Aurobindo; Sadhana → Rabindranath Tagore. [Q101]"," 28. Rabindranath Tagore — Literary Works & the National Anthem\n● 'Gitanjali' Bengali mein 14 August 1910 ko publish hui — English edition November 1912 mein aayi,\njiske liye Tagore ko 1913 mein Nobel Prize mila. [Q51, Q52]\n● Madanapalle (Andhra Pradesh) mein, February 1919 mein, Rabindranath Tagore ne National Anthem\nka Bengali se English translation kiya. [Q53]\n● 'Amar Sonar Bangla' geet Rabindranath Tagore ne 1905 ke Bengal Partition Movement ke dauran likha\naur compose kiya — Bangladesh ne 1971 mein iski pehli 10 lines ko apna National Anthem banaya.\nTagore ekmatra poet hain jinke compositions 2 desho ke national anthems hain. [Q110]\n● National Anthem 'Jana Gana Mana' originally Bengali mein Rabindranath Tagore ne compose ki. [Q111]\n29. Match List — Michael Madhusudan Dutt, Tagore's 'Gora' & Sarojini Naidu\n● Match: Anand Math → Bankim Chandra Chatterjee; The Captive Lady → Michael Madhusudan Dutt;\nGora → Rabindranath Tagore; The Broken Wing → Sarojini Naidu. [Q50]\n● Sarojini Naidu, 'The Golden Threshold' (poems collection, 1905) ki author hain. [Q112]\n30. Chittaranjan Das — 'India for Indians'\n● 'India for Indians' C.R. Das (Deshbandhu, Swaraj Party ke founder) ne likhi. [Q58]\n31. Gandhi — 'Gokhale, My Political Guru'\n● 'Gokhale - My Political Guru' M.K. Gandhi ne likhi. [Q60]\n32. Dr. Rajendra Prasad — Works\n● 'Mahatma Gandhi and Bihar, Some Reminiscences' Dr. Rajendra Prasad ne likhi. [Q57]\n● 'India Divided' book ke author Dr. Rajendra Prasad the. [Q63]\n33. Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar — 'Bahuvivah'\n● 'Bahuvivah' (Polygamy) Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar ki masterpiece hai. [Q65]\n34. Hindi/Regional Novels — Match List"," ● Match: Amritlal Nagar → Amrit aur Vish; Sumitra Nandan Pant → Chidambara; Sharat Chandra\nChatterjee → Devdas; Jaidev → Geet Govind. [Q68]\n● 'Chandrakanta' ke author Devkinandan Khatri hain. [Q67]\n35. Karl Marx — 'Das Capital'\n● 'Das Capital' Karl Marx ki 19th century ki major works mein se ek hai — capitalist system, uski self-\ndestruction ki tendencies aur dynamism par. [Q69]\n36. Chandeshwar & Vidyapati — Medieval Works\n● 'Rajaniti Ratnakara' Chandesvara ne likhi — Kirtillata, Kirtipatata aur PurushaPariksha Vidyapati ki\nrachnayein hain. [Q75]\n37. Nawab Wajid Ali Shah — 'Kissa Radha Kanhaiya'\n● 'Kissa Radha Kanhaiya' Nawab Wajid Ali Shah ne likhi. [Q76]\n38. Sakharam Ganesh Deuskar — 'Desher Katha'\n● 'Desher Katha' (1904) Sakharam Ganesh Deuskar ne likhi — Colonial State ki 'hypnotic conquest of the\nmind' ke against warn kiya, Swadeshi street plays-folk songs ko inspire kiya, aur 'desh' word se nation\nka matlab liya (sirf Bengal region ka nahi). [Q79, Q176]\n39. Kesari Singh Barahath — 'Chetavani Ra Chugatiya'\n● 'Chetavani Ra Chugatiya' (13 couplets) Kesari Singh Barahath (Rajasthan ke poet-freedom fighter) ne\nlikhi — Mewar ke Maharana ko Curzon ke Delhi Durbar attend karne se rokne ke liye. [Q80]\n40. Gandhi's Autobiography — 'The Story of My Experiments with Truth'\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne apni autobiography 'The Story of My Experiments With Truth' (My Experiments\nwith Truth) originally Gujarati mein likhi. [Q81, Q82]\n● Gandhi ne 'Hind Swaraj' bhi 1909 mein, London se Cape Town ki wapas yatra ke dauran, Gujarati mein\nlikhi — baad mein English mein translate hui ban se bachne ke liye. Ismein unhone British Parliament ko\n'sterile and prostitute' bataya. [Q83, Q84, Q59, Q55]\n40b. Gandhi's 'Songs from Prison'"," ● 'Songs from Prison', Sanskrit hymns-lyrics (Upanishads waghera) ka translation, Mahatma Gandhi ne\n1932 mein Yerawada Prison mein imprisonment ke dauran kiya. [Q113]\n41. Bharatendu Harishchandra\n● 'Bharat Durdasha' (drama) aur 'Andher Nagari' (play) Bharatendu Harishchandra ki famous rachnayein\nhain. [Q85, Q86]\n42. Subramaniam Bharati — The Tamil Poet\n● Subramaniam Bharati, Tamil bhasha ke great poet the — unke songs Swadeshi Movement mein\nmasses ko inspire karne ke liye use hote the. [Q87]\n43. Maithili Sharan Gupta — 'Bharat Bharati' & 'Rashtrakavi'\n● 'Bharat Bharati' Maithili Sharan Gupta ('Rashtrakavi') ne likhi — Panchavati, Saket, Yashodhara jaise\nunke doosre major works hain. [Q88]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne Maithili Sharan Gupta ko unki inspiring poetry ke liye 'Rashtrakavi' (National Poet)\nki title di. [Q89]\n44. Nationalist Poets — Who Was NOT One\n●\n Trap: Shiv Kumar Batalvi (Punjabi romantic poet, post-independence prominent hue) Pre-\n⚠️\nindependence ke nationalist poets mein SHAAMIL NAHI the. [Q90]\n45. Nabin Chandra Das — 'Nawab'\n●\n Trap: Nabin Chandra Das ka play 'Nawab' Bengal famine par based NAHI tha — ye ek bankrupt ho\n⚠️\ngaye Nawab ki kahani par tha. [Q91]\n46. Jayaprakash Narayan — 'Towards Struggle', 'Prison Diary' & 'Sarvodaya\nPlan'\n● 'Towards Struggle' aur 'Prison Diary' (1975, imprisonment ke dauran) Jayaprakash Narayan\n('Loknayak') ne likhi — 1974 mein 'Sampurna Kranti' (Total Revolution) ka slogan diya. [Q92, Q93]\n● Jayaprakash Narayan ne 1950 mein 'Sarvodaya Plan' draft ki — Shriman Narayan Aggarwal ne\nGandhian Plan prepare ki thi. [Q213]"," 47. E.M. Forster — 'A Passage to India'\n● 'A Passage to India' E.M. Forster ne likhi — British Raj aur 1920s ki Indian independence movement ke\nbackground mein set hai. [Q94]\n48. Bipan/Bipin Chandra — Historical Works\n● 'India's Struggle for Independence' aur 'The Rise and Growth of Economic Nationalism in India' historian\nBipan/Bipin Chandra ne likhi — 'Indian National Movement: The Long-Term Dynamics' bhi unhi ki hai.\n[Q95, Q97, Q98]\n49. Ramdhari Singh 'Dinkar' — 'Sanskriti Ke Char Adhyay'\n● 'Sanskriti Ke Char Adhyay' Ramdhari Singh 'Dinkar' ne likhi. [Q96]\n50. Professor George Brock\n● 'Out of Print: Newspapers, Journalism and the Business of News in the Digital Age' Professor George\nBrock ne likhi. [Q99]\n51. Katherine Mayo — 'Mother India'\n● 'Mother India' (1927), American author Katherine Mayo ne likhi — Indian society-culture ki critical view ki\nwajah se bahut controversial rahi. [Q100]\n52. Patriotic Songs — Jhanda Geet & Aie Mere Watan Ke Logo\n● 'Jhanda Geet' (Vijayi Vishwa Tiranga Pyaara) Shyamlal Gupta Parshad ne likha. [Q102, Q103]\n● 'Aie Mere Watan Ke Logo' geet Kavi Pradeep (Ramachandra Narayanji Dwivedi) ne likha — Indo-China\nWar (1962) ke martyrs ki yaad mein. [Q104]\n53. Muhammad Iqbal — 'Sare Jahan Se Achha'\n● Poet Muhammad Iqbal, 9 November 1877 ko Sialkot (Punjab, British India) mein paida hue — unhone\n'Saare Jahan Se Achcha' likhi, baad mein Muslim League join ki. [Q105, Q106]\n● 'Mazhab Nahi Sikhata Aapas Mein Bair Rakhna' — ye famous couplet Muhammad Iqbal ke 'Saare\nJahan Se Achha' se hai. [Q107]"," 54. Manoranjan Prasad Singh — 'Firangiya'\n● Manoranjan Prasad Singh ne Bhojpuri mein, British colonialism ke against, 1921 mein 'Firangiya' poem\nlikhi. [Q108]\n55. Gurmukh Nihal Singh & G.A. Natesan\n● 'Landmarks in Indian Constitutional and National Development' Gurmukh Nihal Singh ne likhi — wo\nRajasthan ke pehle Governor (1956-1962) bhi rahe. [Q114]\n● 'Congress Presidential Addresses' G.A. Natesan ne edit ki — 2 parts mein (1885-1910 aur 1911-1934).\n[Q115]\n56. Jawaharlal Nehru — 'The Discovery of India'\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne 'The Discovery of India' 1944 mein, Ahmednagar Fort Jail mein imprisonment ke\ndauran likhi. [Q116, Q118]\n57. Sachindranath Sanyal — 'Bandi Jiwan'\n● 'Bandi Jivan' Sachindranath Sanyal ne likhi — revolutionary movements ke liye ek textbook-guide ki\ntarah kaam kiya. [Q119]\n58. Larry Collins & Dominique Lapierre — Partition Books\n● 'Mountbatten and the Partition of India' Larry Collins aur Dominique Lapierre ne likhi. [Q120]\n59. W.H. Sleeman — Thuggee & Oudh\n● W.H. Sleeman (Thuggee abolition mein important role), ne 'Journey through the Kingdom of Oude in\n1849-50' report likhi. [Q121]\n60. V.D. Savarkar — 'Indian War of Independence 1857'\n● V.D. Savarkar ne '1857 ki revolt' ko 'first freedom struggle' bataate hue 'The Indian War of\nIndependence 1857' likhi — R.C. Majumdar isse freedom struggle nahi maante the. [Q122]\n61. Economic History Authors — Match List"," ● Match: R.C. Dutt → The Economic History of India Under Early British Rule; J.R. McLane → Indian\nNationalism and the Early Congress; B.N. Ganguli → Indian Economic Thought-19th Century\nPerspectives; Bipin Chandra → The Rise and Growth of Economic Nationalism in India. [Q123]\n62. M. Visvesvaraya — 'Planned Economy for India'\n● M. Visvesvaraya ne 'Planned Economy for India' likhi — 1934 mein ek 10-year plan ka suggestion diya.\n[Q124]\n63. W.A. Fairservis — 'The Roots of Ancient India'\n● 'The Roots of Ancient India' Walter Ashlin Fairservis Jr. ne likhi. [Q125]\n64. The JP Movement Book — Disputed\n●\n Disputed: 'JP Movement-Emergency and India's Second Freedom' M.G. Devasahayam ne likhi thi\n⚠️\n— is naam ka koi option na hone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q126]\n65. Match List — 'Priya Pravas', 'Gaban' & 'Shah Nama'\n● Match: Priya Pravas → Ayodhya Prasad (Harioudh); Gaban → Prem Chand; Eternal India → Indira\nGandhi; Shah Nama → Firdausi. [Q127]\n66. Indian Writing in English — Match List\n● Match: The Autobiography of an Unknown Indian → Nirad C. Chaudhuri; India: A Wounded Civilization\n→ V.S. Naipaul; Confessions of a Lover → Mulk Raj Anand; The English Teacher → R.K. Narayan.\n[Q128]\n67. B.S. Minhas — 'Planning and the Poor'\n● 'Planning and the Poor' Bagicha Singh Minhas ne likhi. [Q129]\n68. Lord Curzon — 'The Problems of the Far East'\n● George N. Curzon ne 'Problems of the Far East: Japan-Korea-China' likhi. [Q130]"," 69. General Kaul — 'The Untold Story'\n● 'The Untold Story' (1967, India-China War 1962 highlight karti hai) Lt. General Brijmohan Kaul ne likhi.\n[Q131]\n70. David Diringer — 'The Alphabet'\n● 'The Alphabet: A Key to the History of Mankind' David Diringer ne likhi. [Q132]\n71. Ruskin Bond — 'A Gallery of Rascals'\n● 'A Gallery of Rascals' Ruskin Bond ne likhi — 1992 mein 'Our Trees Still Grow in Dehra' ke liye Sahitya\nAkademi Award mila. [Q133]\n72. 'The Proudest Day' — India's Independence Story\n● 'The Proudest Day: India's Long Road to Independence' Anthony Read aur David Fisher ne likhi — India\nki independence ki story hai. [Q134, Q180]\n73. Match List — 'My Music My Life' & Other Autobiographies\n● Match: My Music My Life → Pt. Ravi Shankar; Adha Gaon → Rahi Masoom Raza; Shri Radha → Sri\nRamakant Rath; The Pilferer → Laxman Gaikwad. [Q135]\n● 'My Music, My Life' Pandit Ravi Shankar ki autobiography hai. [Q136]\n74. 'Yayati' — A Common Trap\n●\n Trap: 'Yayati' novel Girish Karnad ne NAHI, Vishnu Sakharam Khandekar ne likhi thi.\n⚠️\n[Q137]\n75. Contemporary Indian Fiction — Match Lists\n● Match: Shashi Tharoor → Show Business; Amitav Ghosh → The Circle of Reason; Anita Desai → Clear\nLight of Day; Vikram Chandra → Love and Longing in Bombay. [Q138, Q139]\n76. Bureaucrat/Public Figure Memoirs — Match List"," ● Match: Ghar Aur Adalat → Leila Seth; Jhopri Se Rashtrapati Bhawan Tak → Mahendra Kulsreshtha;\nImagining India → Nandan Nilekani; Journey through Babudom and Neta land → T.S.R. Subramanian.\n[Q140]\n77. Munshi Premchand — Novels\n● Godan, Gaban, Rangbhumi, Karmbhumi, Nirmala — sabhi Munshi Premchand ki masterpieces hain.\n[Q141, Q142]\n● 'Soj-e-Vatan' Premchand ne likhi. [Q143]\n●\n Trap: 'Rangbhumi' Sharat Chandra ne NAHI, Munshi Premchand ne likhi thi.\n⚠️\n[Q189]\n78. R.K. Narayan — 'Malgudi Days'\n● 'Malgudi Days' (short stories collection) R.K. Narayan ne likhi. [Q144]\n79. Hans Christian Andersen\n● Hans Christian Andersen ne fairy tales likhi — The Steadfast Tin Soldier, The Snow Queen, The Little\nMermaid jaisi masterpieces. [Q145]\n80. Match List — 'Pakistan Papers' & Other Non-Fiction\n● Match: Manishankar Aiyar → The Pakistan Papers; Margaret Thatcher → The Path to Power; Abul\nKalam Azad → India Wins Freedom; Savita Pande → The Future of N.P.T. [Q146]\n81. Vikram Seth — 'The Golden Gate' & 'An Equal Music'\n● 'The Golden Gate' (1986, Vikram Seth ka pehla novel) unhone likhi. [Q147]\n● 'An Equal Music' Vikram Seth ne likhi. [Q175]\n82. Journalist Autobiographies — Vinod Mehta\n● 'Lucknow Boy: A Memoir' journalist Vinod Mehta ne likhi. [Q148, Q149]\n83. Rachel Carson — 'Silent Spring'\n● 'Silent Spring' Rachel Carson ne likhi — pesticides ke indiscriminate use ke environmental effects par\nsawaal uthaya. [Q150]"," 84. Salman Rushdie's Works\n● 'The Satanic Verses' (1988, controversial) Salman Rushdie ki 4th novel hai. [Q151]\n● 'Two Years Eight Months and Twenty-Eight Nights' (2015) Salman Rushdie ne likhi. [Q152]\n85. Jhumpa Lahiri — 'The Namesake' & 'Unaccustomed Earth'\n● 'The Namesake' (2003) Jhumpa Lahiri ne likhi. [Q153]\n● Match: In Custody → Anita Desai; Sea of Poppies → Amitav Ghosh; The Argumentative Indian →\nAmartya Sen; Unaccustomed Earth → Jhumpa Lahiri. [Q201]\n86. Bill Gates — 'The Road Ahead'\n● 'The Road Ahead' (1995) Microsoft co-founder Bill Gates ne likhi. [Q154]\n87. Amritlal Nagar — 'Manas ke Hans'\n● 'Manas ke Hans' (Tulsidas ke jeevan par biographical novel) Amritlal Nagar ne likhi. [Q155]\n88. Sumitra Nandan Pant — Chhayavadi Poet\n● Sumitra Nandan Pant, Hindi ke leading Chhayavadi (neo-romantic) poets mein se ek the —\nChidambara, Lokayatan, Yugvani jaise major works. [Q156]\n89. Julia Delano — 'Dyna: A Tribute'\n● 'Dyna: A Tribute' Julia Delano ne likhi. [Q157]\n90. Harry Potter — Cornelius Fudge\n● Cornelius Fudge, J.K. Rowling ke 'Harry Potter' novel mein, Minister of Magic hain. [Q158]\n91. Harivansh Rai Bachchan — Chronology\n● Harivansh Rai Bachchan ki poems ka chronological order: Madhushala (1935) → Madhubala (1936) →\nMadhukalash. [Q159]"," 92. Julio Ribeiro — 'Bullet for Bullet'\n● 'Bullet for Bullet: My Life as a Police Officer' Julio Ribeiro (senior police officer) ki autobiography hai.\n[Q160]\n93. Devanand — 'Romancing with Life'\n● 'Romancing with Life: An Autobiography' famous film actor Devanand ne likhi. [Q161]\n94. World Leaders' Autobiographies — Match List\n● Match: The Struggle is My Life → Nelson Mandela; The Struggle and the Triumph → Lech Walesa;\nFriends and Foes → Sheikh Mujibur Rehman; Rebirth → Leonid Brezhnev. [Q162]\n95. Rafiq Zakaria & Kalam — Match Lists\n● Match: Price of Partition (Rafiq Zakaria); Anand Math (Bankim Chandra); India 2020: A Vision for the\nNew Millennium (A.P.J. Abdul Kalam); The Pathology of Corruption (S.S. Gill). [Q163]\n● Match: The Price of Partition (Rafiq Zakaria); Ulysses (James Joyce); India 2020 (A.P.J. Abdul Kalam);\nPathology of Corruption (S.S. Gill). [Q164]\n96. Books on Muslims/Pakistan — Match List\n● Match: W.C. Smith → Modern Islam in India; Khalid Bin Sayeed → Pakistan: The Formative Phase\n(1857-1948); Peter Hardy → The Muslims of British India; Moin Shakir → Khilafat to Partition. [Q165]\n97. Mark Tully — 'The Heart of India'\n● 'The Heart of India' British journalist-former BBC India reporter Mark Tully ne likhi. [Q166]\n98. Taslima Nasrin — 'Lajja'\n● 'Lajja' (Bengali novel, 1993) Taslima Nasrin ne likhi — controversial parts ki wajah se Bangladesh-India\nke kuch states mein restricted hai. [Q167, Q168]\n●\n Trap: 'Amar Sonar Bangla' Taslima Nasrin ki NAHI hai — ye Rabindranath Tagore ne likhi (1905,\n⚠️\nBengal partition ke dauran). [Q181]"," 99. George Orwell — 'Nineteen Eighty-Four'\n● 'Nineteen Eighty-Four' English author George Orwell ne likhi. [Q169]\n100. Arundhati Roy — 'The God of Small Things'\n● Arundhati Roy ne 'The God of Small Things' (debut novel) ke liye 1997 mein Booker Prize jeeta. [Q170]\n101. Vrindavan Lal Verma — 'Mrignayani'\n● 'Mrignayani' (historical novel) Vrindavan Lal Verma ne likhi — Jhansi ki Rani, Bhuvan Vikram jaise\ndoosre novels bhi likhe. [Q171]\n102. Early Hindi Works — Chronology\n● Chronological order: Mrigavati (1503, Kutuban) → Padmavat (1540, Malik Muhammad Jayasi) →\nMadhumalati (1545, Manjhan) → Indravati (1744, Noor Mohammad). [Q172]\n103. Durga Das — 'India from Curzon to Nehru and After'\n● 'India from Curzon to Nehru and After' journalist Durga Das ne likhi. [Q173, Q174]\n104. Subhadra Kumari Chauhan — 'Bikhre Moti' & 'Mukul'\n● 'Bikhre Moti' (1932, story collection) Subhadra Kumari Chauhan ne likhi — Unmadini aur Seedhe-\nSaadhe Chitra bhi unki hain. [Q177]\n● 'Mukul' (1930 poems collection) Subhadra Kumari Chauhan ki famous literary work hai — 1931 mein\nSeksaria Prize mila. [Q186]\n105. Vinod Kumar Shukla — 'Naukar ki Kameez'\n● 'Naukar ki Kameez' Hindi novel Vinod Kumar Shukla ne likhi. [Q178]\n106. Charles Dickens — 'David Copperfield'\n● 'David Copperfield' (1850) Charles Dickens ne likhi — unki khud ki zindagi par largely based hai. [Q179]"," 107. Constitution-Related Books — Match List\n● Match: Gandhian Constitution → Sriman Narayan Agrawal; The Republic of India → A. Gledhill; The\nWhite Umbrella → D. Mackenzie Brown; The Politics of India since Independence → Paul R. Brass.\n[Q183]\n● 'Gandhian Constitution for Free India' (1946) Shriman Narayan Agarwal ne likhi. [Q184]\n● Match: Half a Life → V.S. Naipaul; Worshipping False Gods → Arun Shourie; Agni Ki Udaan (Wings of\nFire) → A.P.J. Abdul Kalam; Jeet Apki (You Can Win) → Shiv Khera. [Q182]\n108. Jai Shankar Prasad — 'Kamayani'\n● 'Kamayani' (epic, Manu-Shraddha ka context) Jai Shankar Prasad ne likhi — Aansu, Lahar, Ajatashatru\nbhi unki rachnayein hain. [Q185]\n109. K.M. Panikkar — 'Geographical Factors in Indian History'\n● 'Geographical Factors in Indian History' K.M. Panikkar ne likhi. [Q187]\n110. Verrier Elwin — 'The Baiga'\n● Verrier Elwin ne Baiga tribe study karke 'The Baiga' book likhi — 'National Park' banane ka suggestion\ndiya. [Q188]\n111. Khushwant Singh — 'Truth, Love and a Little Malice'\n● Khushwant Singh ki autobiography 'Truth Love and a Little Malice' kehlaati hai. [Q190]\n112. Political Leader Books — Vajpayee & Kalam\n● 'New Dimensions of India's Foreign Policy' former PM Atal Bihari Vajpayee ne likhi. [Q191]\n● 'Ignited Minds' aur 'Wings of Fire' A.P.J. Abdul Kalam ('Missile Man of India') ne likhi. [Q192]\n113. Fareed Zakaria — 'The Post-American World'\n● 'The Post-American World' Indian-American journalist Fareed Zakaria ne likhi. [Q193]\n114. V.P. Menon — 'The Story of the Integration of the Indian States'"," ● 'The Story of The Integration of the Indian States' V.P. Menon ne likhi. [Q194]\n115. P.V. Narasimha Rao — 'Ayodhya: 6 December, 1992'\n● 'Ayodhya: 6 December, 1992' P.V. Narasimha Rao ne likhi. [Q195]\n116. Booker Prize Winners — Match List\n● Booker Prize winners match: V.S. Naipaul → In a Free State (1971); Salman Rushdie → Midnight's\nChildren (1981); Paul Scott → Staying On (1977); J.G. Farrell → The Siege of Krishnapur (1973). [Q196]\n117. Soli Sorabjee Book — Disputed\n●\n Disputed: 'World of All Human Rights: Soli J. Sorabjee, A Festschrift' R.N. Trivedi ne likhi/edit ki —\n⚠️\noptions mein actual author na hone ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q197]\n118. Lal Bahadur Shastri — Translation of Madame Curie\n● Former PM Lal Bahadur Shastri ne Madam Curie (radium ki inventor) ki autobiography Hindi mein\ntranslate ki. [Q198]\n119. Faiz Ahmed Faiz — 'Subh-e-Azadi'\n● Pakistani Urdu poet Faiz Ahmed Faiz (1911, Sialkot mein paida hue) ne 'Subh-e-Azadi' poem likhi.\n[Q199]\n120. Elizabeth Hawley — Himalayan Expeditions\n● American writer Elizabeth Hawley, Himalayan expeditions par apni writings ke liye jaani jaati hain —\nkhud mountaineering kabhi nahi ki. [Q200]\n121. Medieval Chronicles — Match List\n● Match: Tabaqat-i-Akbari → Nizamuddin (Ahmad); Tabaqat-i-Nasiri → Minhaj-ud-din bin Siraj-ud-din;\nTarikh-i-Firozshahi → Zia-ud-din Barani; Tarikh-i-Yamini → Al Utbi. [Q202]"," 122. Bengal School Painters — Disputed\n●\n Disputed: Nandalal Bose 'Bengal School of Modern Painting' se associate the — 'Nand Lal Ghosh'\n⚠️\ngalat naam options mein diya gaya tha, isliye ye question disputed/removed hai. [Q203]\n123. Barack Obama — 'The Audacity of Hope'\n● 'The Audacity of Hope' (2006) Barack Obama ki doosri book hai — pehli 'Dreams From My Father',\nteesri 'Of Thee I Sing: A Letter to My Daughters'. [Q204]\n124. Gunnar Myrdal — 'The Challenge of World Poverty'\n● 'The Challenge of World Poverty' Swedish economist-sociologist Gunnar Myrdal ne likhi — 1974 mein\nNobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences mila. [Q205]\n125. Rajni Kothari — 'Politics in India'\n● 'Politics in India' Professor Rajni Kothari ne likhi. [Q206, Q207]\n126. Musharraf's Book — The Ghostwriter\n● Parvez Musharraf ki biography 'In the Line of Fire' ki credited author unhi ki hai, lekin actual ghostwriter\nHumayun Gohar the (Pakistani bureaucrat Altaf Gohar ke bete). [Q208]\n127. Old Hindi Works — Match List\n● Match: Munshi Insha Alla Khan → Udaibhan Charit; Babu Devki Nandan Khatri → Kajar Ki Kothri; Pt.\nPratap Narain Mishra → Hathi Hamir; Jai Shankar Prasad → Kankal. [Q209]\n128. Dharam Veer Bharti — 'Andha Yug'\n● 'Andha Yug' (prominent verse drama) Dharam Veer Bharti ne likhi. [Q210]\n129. Bhawani Prasad & Makhanlal Chaturvedi — A Trap\n●\n Trap: 'Himtarangini' Bhawani Prasad ki NAHI hai — ye Makhanlal Chaturvedi ki rachna hai. Geet\n⚠️\nFarosh aur Satpura Ke Ghane Jungle Bhawani Prasad ki hain. [Q211]"," 130. Abdul Bismillah — 'Jhini Jhini Bini Chadariya'\n● 'Jhini Jhini Bini Chadariya' (weavers ki exploitation par based) Hindi novel Abdul Bismillah ne likhi.\n[Q212]\n131. Sunil Gavaskar — 'One-Day Wonders'\n● 'One Day Wonders' cricketer Sunil Manohar Gavaskar ne likhi — Sunny Days (Autobiography), Idols,\nRuns and Ruins bhi unki hain. [Q214]\n132. World Political Figures — Match List\n● Match: Hillary Clinton → Living History; Kapil Dev → Cricket-My Style; Michael Edwardes → The Myth\nof the Mahatma; Neville Chamberlain → The Struggle for Peace. [Q215]\n133. Prince Harry — 'Spare'\n● 'Spare' Prince Harry (Duke of Sussex) ki memoir hai — 10 January 2023 ko release hui aur fastest-\nselling non-fiction book ka Guinness World Record banaya. [Q216]\n134. Women Poets — A Match Trap\n● Daya Bai → Vinay Malika; Sahajobai → Sahaj-Prakash; Son Kumari → Swarn Beli.\n Trap: 'Gangabai\n⚠️\n\n— Ganesh Dev Leela' galat matched hai. [Q217]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Magazines Books and Their Authors Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0256","t":"54 Art and Culture","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.54 — ART & CULTURE — FULL MIND MAP\n🎨\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Tradition-State Match — Correction\n2. Madhubani Painting — Bihar\n3. The 'Tribhanga' Dance Pose\n4. Centre for Cultural Resources and Training (CCRT)\n5. The Kumbh Mela\n6. Regional Festivals — Bihu, Onam, Pongal & Baisakhi\n7. Tamasha — Maharashtra's Folk Musical Theatre\n8. 'Venushilpa' — Bamboo Art\n9. Jagannath — Different from Other Shiva Shrines\n10. Adi Shankaracharya's Four Mathas\n11. Srisailam Jyotirlinga\n12. Tabo Monastery & Buddhist Sites\n13. North-Eastern Festivals — Losoong, Wangla & Chapchar Kut\n14. Ijtima Festival — Bhopal\n15. Navarathri — Disputed\n16. Arjun's Grandfather — Vichitravirya\n17. The Kaaba\n18. The Synagogue — Jewish Worship Place\n19. The First Sanskrit University Chair\n20. Temples — Match Lists\n21. The Earliest Reference to the Magnetic Compass\n22. The Thyagaraja Festival\n23. 'Sufi Kalam' — Kashmir\n24. Mimamsa Philosophy — Liberation Through Karma\n25. 'Jagar' — Uttarakhand\n26. Rath Yatra — Puri\n27. Maluti — The 'Village of Temples'\n28. Women Achievers — A Match Trap\n29. Classical Artists — Match List\n30. Alla Rakha — The Tabla Maestro\n31. Instrumentalists — A Match Trap\n32. Regional Mahabharata Compositions\n33. Amir Khusrau — Urdu Poetry & the Sitar\n34. 'Radha Govind Sangeet Sar'\n35. Dhrupad — An Ancient Musical Tradition\n36. 'Raga Kallpadrum' & Musical Ragas\n37. 'Chakiarkoothu' Dance\n38. Manipuri Sankirtana\n39. Pandit Bhimsen Joshi — Kirana Gharana\n40. Classical Dancers — Match List\n41. Classical Dances — States Match Lists\n42. Odissi Dance — Odisha\n43. Mohiniattam — Kerala's Solo Dance\n44. Sattriya Dance\n45. Dance-State Pairs — A Trap\n46. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage — Garba\n47. Kuchipudi vs Bharatanatyam — Distinctions\n48. Kathak — Mughal Influence\n49. Artists — Puppetry to Kuchipudi Match List\n50. Manipuri — Eastern India's Dance\n51. Indrani Rahman — Disputed\n52. Girija Devi — Banaras Gharana\n53. Indo-Islamic Musical Instruments\n54. Gangubai Hangal — Kirana Gharana\n55. 'Tera Tali' — Rajasthan"," 56. State Dance Styles — Match Lists\n57. 'Karagam' — Tamil Nadu's Religious Folk Dance\n58. Musicians & Instruments — Comprehensive Match Lists\n59. Amjad Ali Khan — A Match Trap\n60. V.G. Jog — The Violin Maestro\n61. 'Akum' and 'Todi' — Wind Instruments\n62. 'Toti' — A Traditional Earring\n63. Kathak Artists\n64. Kalaripayattu — Ancient Martial Art\n65. Folk Culture — Definition\n66. Kalamkari Painting\n67. Multi-Field Personalities — Match Lists\n68. Folk Songs — Preserving Traditions\n69. Tyagaraja & Annamacharya — Composers\n70. Non-Classical Dance — Garba\n71. M.S. Subbalakshmi — A Match Trap\n72. Modern Indian Painters — Match Lists\n73. Sangeet Natak Akademi\n74. Ronu Majumdar — Flute Player\n75. Authors & Artists — A Combined Match\n76. Zakir Hussain — A Match Trap\n77. The Veena — India's Most Ancient Instrument\n78. Folk Dance-State Pairs — A Trap\n79. Kuchipudi — Andhra Pradesh's Origin\n80. Regional Festivals — Match List\n81. Meghalaya's Folk Dance — 'Loho'\n82. 'Surkhi' — Introduced by the Kushans\n83. 'Cultural Lag'\n84. Male-Only Dances — Kathakali\n85. Music Terminology — Match List\n86. 'Raas' Dance — Gujarat\n87. Bharat Ratna — A Match Trap\n88. 'Bandit Queen' — Seema Biswas\n89. TV Serial 'Ramayan' — Ramanand Sagar\n90. Films on Gandhi\n91. 'Alam Ara' — India's First Talkie\n92. Devika Rani — Actress\n93. 'Mahabharat' TV Serial — B.R. Chopra\n94. Vidushaka — Sanskrit Drama Character\n95. K. Shankar Pillai — Cartoonist\n96. Raghu Rai — Photography\n97. Cultural Personalities — Match List\n98. Raja Ravi Varma — Modern Age Painter\n99. Abanindranath Tagore — Revivalistic Paintings\n100. Nandalal Bose — Kala Bhavan\n101. Vishnu Chinchalkar — Chitrakar\n102. The Mona Lisa Painting\n103. Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan — 'Mera Piya Ghar Aaya'\n104. Jamini Roy — Painter\n105. The Gangasagar Mela — West Bengal\n106. Britney Spears — Singer\n107. Thadingyut Festival — Myanmar\n108. Puran Singh — 'Tagore of Punjabi Language'\n109. 'Satyam Shivam Sundaram' Painting\n110. Multi-Field Personalities — More Match Lists\n111. Bachendri Pal — First Indian Woman on Everest\n112. Famous Libraries — Match List\n113. Traditional Dresses — A Trap\n114. Embroidery Arts — Match List\n115. Shanti Niketan — Birbhum District\n116. Iconic Monuments — Match List\n117. Places & Monuments — Match List"," 1. Tradition-State Match — Correction\n●\n Trap: 'Gatka' martial art Kerala ki NAHI, Punjab ki hai (wooden sticks/lathi se sword-sparring).\n⚠️\nMadhubani painting Bihar (aur Nepal) se, Sindhu Darshan Festival Ladakh (Leh) se juda hai. [Q1]\n2. Madhubani Painting — Bihar\n● 'Madhubani' painting Bihar state se related hai — Mithila region (Bihar aur Nepal) mein practice hoti hai.\n[Q2, Q90]\n● Match: Madhubani → Bihar; Lepakshi → Andhra Pradesh; Pattachitra → Odisha; Warli → Maharashtra.\n[Q3]\n3. The 'Tribhanga' Dance Pose\n● 'Tribhanga' (three-bent pose) — ek leg bent hoti hai aur body waist-neck par slightly opposite curved\nhoti hai — traditional Indian sculpture aur classical dance mein use hota hai. [Q4]\n4. Centre for Cultural Resources and Training (CCRT)\n● CCRT, education ko culture se link karti hai — 1979 mein Kamaladevi Chattopadhyay aur Dr. Kapila\nVatsyayan ne establish ki. [Q5]\n5. The Kumbh Mela\n● Kumbh Mela Haridwar, Prayagraj, Nashik aur Ujjain mein hoti hai, har 3rd year rotation mein —\nVaranasi mein NAHI hoti. [Q6]\n● 'Maha Kumbh' har 12 saal mein hota hai — UP government ne isse 'Mahakumbh' aur Ardh Kumbh (6\nsaal) ko 'Kumbh' rename kiya. [Q7]\n● Kumbh Mela har 12th saal, Prayag-Haridwar-Ujjain-Nashik — 4 jagaho par hoti hai. [Q8]\n6. Regional Festivals — Bihu, Onam, Pongal & Baisakhi\n● Match: Bihu → Assam (saal mein 3 baar); Onam → Kerala (harvest ke time); Pongal → Tamil Nadu\n(January mein); Baisakhi → Punjab. [Q9]\n● 'Onam' Kerala ka famous harvest festival hai. [Q10]\n● 'Bihu' Assam ka folk dance hai. [Q11]\n● 'Pongal' Tamil Nadu ka festival hai — Makar Sankranti par celebrate hota hai. [Q12]\n● Onam Mahabali (raja) se associate hai — legend ke mutabik unki spirit Kerala visit karti hai is time.\n[Q13]"," ● 'Athapoo' (Pookalam, floral mat) Onam festival se associate hai. [Q14]\n7. Tamasha — Maharashtra's Folk Musical Theatre\n● 'Tamasha' Maharashtra ka traditional Marathi folk art form hai — singing-dancing dono shaamil. [Q15]\n8. 'Venushilpa' — Bamboo Art\n● 'Venushilpa' book Chitracharya Upendra Maharathi ne likhi — bamboo art se related hai. [Q16]\n9. Jagannath — Different from Other Shiva Shrines\n● Amarnath, Kedarnath aur Vishwanath — Lord Shiva se related hain — Jagannath Dham ka main deity\nLord Krishna (Vishnu ka roop) hai. [Q17]\n10. Adi Shankaracharya's Four Mathas\n● Adi Shankaracharya ne 4 corners mein Mathas establish ki: Joshimath (North), Dwarka (West), Puri\n(East), Sringeri (South). [Q18]\n11. Srisailam Jyotirlinga\n● Srisailam (12 Jyotirlingas mein se ek) Andhra Pradesh mein, Kurnool ke pass, situated hai — Sri\nMallikarjuna Swamy ki tarah pooja hoti hai. [Q19]\n12. Tabo Monastery & Buddhist Sites\n● Tabo Monastery, Spiti Valley, Himachal Pradesh mein hai — 996 CE mein Rinchen Zangpo ne found ki.\n[Q20]\n● Statement check: Tabo monastery Himachal Pradesh mein hai (sahi) — Lhotsava Lhakhang Nako\nvillage (Kinnaur, HP) mein hai, Zanskar Valley mein NAHI (galat) — Alchi temple complex Ladakh UT\nmein hai (sahi). [Q33]\n13. North-Eastern Festivals — Losoong, Wangla & Chapchar Kut\n● 'Losoong' Sikkim ka popular festival hai — Tibetan lunar month ke end mein celebrate hota hai. [Q21]\n● 'Wangla Festival' Meghalaya mein, Garo tribe dwara, harvest festival ki tarah celebrate hota hai\n('Hundred Drums' festival bhi kehte hain). [Q22]"," ● 'Chapchar Kut' Mizoram ka festival hai, March mein celebrate hota hai. [Q23]\n14. Ijtima Festival — Bhopal\n● 'Tabligi Ijtima' Muslims ka important festival hai, Bhopal mein celebrate hota hai. [Q24]\n15. Navarathri — Disputed\n●\n Disputed: 'Navarathri' Saraswathi Pooja ki tarah Kerala, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu aur Telangana — 4\n⚠️\nstates mein celebrate hoti hai, isliye single-state answer disputed hai. [Q25]\n16. Arjun's Grandfather — Vichitravirya\n● Vichitravirya, Mahabharata ke hero Arjun ke grandfather the — unke 2 bete Pandu aur Dhritarashtra\nthe, Arjun Pandu ke bete the. [Q26]\n17. The Kaaba\n● 'Kaaba' (Mecca, Saudi Arabia) Muslims ke liye holiest place hai — Quran ke mutabik Ibrahim aur unke\nbete Ismail ne banaya. [Q27]\n18. The Synagogue — Jewish Worship Place\n● Jewish place of worship 'Synagogue' kehlaata hai. [Q28]\n19. The First Sanskrit University Chair\n● Pehla Sanskrit Chair College de France (Paris University, France) mein, 1814 mein, establish hui. [Q29]\n20. Temples — Match Lists\n● Match: Sri Vidyashankar temple → Karnataka; Rajarani temple → Odisha; Kandariya Mahadeo temple\n→ Madhya Pradesh; Bhimesvara Swami temple → Andhra Pradesh. [Q30]\n● 'Chitragupta Swami Temple' (Chitragupta ka rare temple) Kanchipuram, Tamil Nadu mein situated hai.\n[Q32]\n21. The Earliest Reference to the Magnetic Compass"," ● 'Magnetic Compass' ka earliest reference 'Jawamiul Hikayat' text mein milta hai. [Q31]\n22. The Thyagaraja Festival\n● Thyagaraja Aradhana (saint-composer Thyagaraja ki yaad mein annual festival) Thanjavur (Tamil Nadu)\nmein regularly celebrate hoti hai. [Q34]\n23. 'Sufi Kalam' — Kashmir\n● 'Sufi Kalam' (devotional music) Jammu-Kashmir ki characteristic hai. [Q35]\n24. Mimamsa Philosophy — Liberation Through Karma\n● Mimamsa system of philosophy 'Karma' doctrine par zor deti hai — liberation, Karma perform karne se\npossible hai. [Q36]\n25. 'Jagar' — Uttarakhand\n● 'Jagar' (God worship ritual, ancestor spirit worship) Uttarakhand (Kumaon-Garhwal) ki hills mein\nprevalent hai. [Q37]\n26. Rath Yatra — Puri\n● 'Rath Yatra' festival Jagannath Puri (Odisha) mein hoti hai. [Q38]\n27. Maluti — The 'Village of Temples'\n● Maluti Village (Dumka district, Jharkhand) ko 'village of temples' kehte hain. [Q39]\n28. Women Achievers — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: Madhumita Raut (Odissi dancer), Meera Bhatia (jurist), Indira Chakravarty (nutritional\n⚠️\nscientist) sahi matched hain — 'Sadhvi Sadhana' homemaker doctor NAHI, ek Jain Sant hain. [Q40]\n29. Classical Artists — Match List"," ● Match: Pt. Bhajan Sopori → Santoor (Sufiana Gharana, Kashmir); Pt. Birju Maharaj → Kathak (Lucknow\nKalka-Bindadin Gharana); Priyadarshini Govind → Bharatanatyam; T.V. Gopal Krishnan → Mridangam.\n[Q41]\n30. Alla Rakha — The Tabla Maestro\n● Ustad Alla Rakha Qureshi, famous Tabla player the — Ustad Zakir Hussain ke pita the. [Q42]\n31. Instrumentalists — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: Panna Lal Ghosh Tabla ke NAHI, flute (Bansuri) ke player the. Devabrata Chaudhuri sitar,\n⚠️\nAmjad Ali Khan sarod, aur Yehudi Menuhin American-British violinist the. [Q43]\n32. Regional Mahabharata Compositions\n● Match: Pampa → Kannada ('Vikramarjuna Vijaya'); Sarala Dasa → Odia; Kasiram Das → Bengali;\nTikkana → Telugu. [Q44]\n33. Amir Khusrau — Urdu Poetry & the Sitar\n● Amir Khusrau, Urdu ko poetic expression ke liye medium ki tarah use karne wale pehle writer the —\nQawwali ke originator bhi maane jaate hain. [Q45]\n● Sitar, Amir Khusrau ne invent ki thi — old Indian Veena aur Iranian Tambura ke features combine kiye.\n[Q112]\n34. 'Radha Govind Sangeet Sar'\n● 'Radha Govind Sangeet Sar' (classical music composition) Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh ne banayi.\n[Q46]\n35. Dhrupad — An Ancient Musical Tradition\n● Dhrupad, Vedic hymns-mantras ki chanting se origin leti hai — divine ko sound ke through offerings\ndene ki tarah ek form of worship hai. 2 parts mein perform hoti hai: Alap aur Bandish. [Q47]\n● Umakant aur Ramakant Gundecha (Gundecha Brothers) Dagarvani Dhrupad vocalists hain — Ujjain\nmein Jain family mein paida hue. [Q48]\n36. 'Raga Kallpadrum' & Musical Ragas"," ● 'Raga Kallpadrum' Krishnanand Vyas ne likhi — Rana Hammir ne 'Sringarhar', Maharana Kumbha ne\n'Sangeetraj', Radhakrishna ne 'Rag Ratnakar' likhi. [Q49]\n● Raga 'Todi' subah mein gaya jaata hai — Darbari raat mein, Bhopali evening mein, Bhimpalasi\nafternoon mein. [Q50]\n37. 'Chakiarkoothu' Dance\n● 'Chakiarkoothu' mein Hindu mythology-epics ki stories orally render hoti hain, sirf Chakiar community ke\nmembers perform karte the — Koothambalam (temple theatre) mein hota hai, mizhavu percussion\ninstrument ke saath. [Q51]\n38. Manipuri Sankirtana\n● Manipuri Sankirtana ritual singing-drumming-dancing hai, temples mein perform hoti hai — Kartal\n(cymbals) AUR Pung (drum) — dono use hote hain. [Q52]\n39. Pandit Bhimsen Joshi — Kirana Gharana\n● Pandit Bhimsen Joshi, Kirana Gharana ke Indian classical singer the — 2009 mein Bharat Ratna mila.\n[Q53, Q54]\n40. Classical Dancers — Match List\n● Match: Kalamandalam Kshemavathy → Mohiniattam; Kottakkal Sivaraman → Kathakali; Lakshmi\nVishwanathan → Bharatanatyam; N. Madhabi Devi → Manipuri. [Q55]\n41. Classical Dances — States Match Lists\n● Match: Bharatanatyam → Tamil Nadu; Kathak → Uttar Pradesh; Kuchipudi → Andhra Pradesh;\nMohiniattam → Kerala. [Q56]\n● Match: Bharatanatyam → Tamil Nadu; Kuchipudi → Andhra Pradesh; Sattriya → Assam; Kathak →\nUttar Pradesh. [Q57]\n● Match: Kuchipudi → Andhra Pradesh; Bharatnatyam → Tamil Nadu; Kathak → Uttar Pradesh; Odissi →\nOdisha. [Q116]\n42. Odissi Dance — Odisha\n● 'Odissi' dance Odisha (Orissa) se belong karti hai. [Q58]"," 43. Mohiniattam — Kerala's Solo Dance\n● 'Mohini Attam' Kerala ka semi-classical dance hai — women perform karti hain, ismein 'Mohini' ka\nmatlab 'dil chura lene wali maiden' hai. [Q59]\n● Mohiniattam solo performance involve karti hai — women dwara graceful solo recital ki tarah. [Q61]\n44. Sattriya Dance\n● Sattriya, 8 principal classical Indian dance traditions mein se ek hai — Vaishnava saint Sankardeva ne\nintroduce ki, Borgeet compositions ke saath accompany hoti hai. [Q60]\n45. Dance-State Pairs — A Trap\n●\n Trap: Garba-Gujarat aur Yakshagana-Karnataka sahi hain — lekin Mohiniattam-Odisha GALAT hai\n⚠️\n(ye Kerala ki dance hai). [Q62]\n46. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage — Garba\n● Garba dance UNESCO's Intangible Cultural Heritage List mein latest inclusion hai — Chhau (2010),\nDurga Puja Kolkata (2021), Kumbh Mela (2017) pehle include hui. [Q63]\n47. Kuchipudi vs Bharatanatyam — Distinctions\n● Kuchipudi mein dancers kabhi-kabhi dialogue bolte hain — 'Tarangam' (brass plate ki edge par dance)\nKuchipudi ki unique feature hai, Bharatanatyam ki NAHI. [Q64]\n48. Kathak — Mughal Influence\n● Kathak, apne present form mein, Mughal tradition ka influence rakhti hai — Mughal courts ne is dance\nform ko heavily patronize kiya. [Q65]\n49. Artists — Puppetry to Kuchipudi Match List\n● Match: Hiren Bhattacharya → Puppetry; Malini Rajurkar → Hindustani vocal music; Pratibha Prahlad →\nBharatnatyam; Vempati Chinna Satyam → Kuchipudi. [Q66]\n50. Manipuri — Eastern India's Dance"," ● Manipuri dance, North-Eastern India (Manipur) se hai — baaki South India ki dance forms hain. [Q67]\n51. Indrani Rahman — Disputed\n●\n Disputed: Indrani Rahman (1930-1999), Bharatnatyam, Kuchipudi, Kathakali aur Odissi — multiple\n⚠️\nclassical dance systems se related thi — UPPSC ne Odissi ko sahi answer maana. [Q68]\n52. Girija Devi — Banaras Gharana\n● Girija Devi (famous Thumri singer) Banaras Gharana se belong karti thi. [Q69]\n53. Indo-Islamic Musical Instruments\n● Sarangi ki origin ancient Indian mani jaati hai, Rabab jaise instruments Turkic logo laaye the — Sitar aur\nTabla Amir Khusrau ke credit hain (Indo-Islamic synthesis). [Q70]\n54. Gangubai Hangal — Kirana Gharana\n● Gangubai Hangal (1913-2009) Khayal genre ki classical singer thi — Kirana Gharana se belong karti thi.\n[Q71]\n55. 'Tera Tali' — Rajasthan\n● 'Tera Tali' Rajasthan ka folk dance hai — 'Kamar' tribe ki women dwara perform hota hai. [Q72]\n56. State Dance Styles — Match Lists\n● Match: Andhra Pradesh → Burra; Assam → Bihu; Himachal Pradesh → Nati; Rajasthan → Ghoomar.\n[Q73]\n● Match: Assam → Ojapali; Himachal Pradesh → Luddi; West Bengal → Jatra; Bihar → Jata-Jatin. [Q74]\n57. 'Karagam' — Tamil Nadu's Religious Folk Dance\n● 'Karagam' (religious folk dance) Tamil Nadu se associate hai. [Q75]\n58. Musicians & Instruments — Comprehensive Match Lists"," ● Match: Shahnai → Bismillah Khan; Sarod → Amjad Ali Khan; Painter → M.F. Husain; Tabla → Alla\nRakha; Sitar → Ravi Shankar. [Q76]\n● Match: Birju Maharaj → Kathak; Hari Prasad Chaurasia → Flute; Ali Akbar → Sarod; Zakir Hussain →\nTabla. [Q78]\n● Match: Shiv Kumar Sharma → Santoor; Hari Prasad Chaurasia → Flute; Asad Ali Khan → Rudra\nVeena; Pramod Gaekwad → Sundari. [Q82]\n● Match: Khayal → Suraj Khan; Pakhawaj → Pt. Ayodhya Prasad; Veena Vadan → Sadiq Ali Khan; Tabla\n→ Veeru Mishra. [Q83]\n● Match: Pt. Shiv Kumar Sharma → Santoor; Pt. Mallikarjun Mansur → Hindustani Music; V.G. Jog →\nViolin; Ali Akbar Khan → Sarod. [Q84]\n● Match: Ravi Shankar → Sitar; Hari Prasad Chaurasia → Flute; Omkar Nath Thakur → Violin; Bismillah\nKhan → Shehnai. [Q85]\n● Match: Pt. Gopalji Mishra → Sarangi; Kishan Maharaj → Tabla; Hari Prasad Chaurasia → Flute; Kudak\nSingh → Pakhawaj. [Q86]\n● Sahi statement: Hari Prasad Chaurasia — Flute. (Bismillah Khan Shehnai, Zakir Hussain-Alla Rakha\ndono Tabla.) [Q98]\n● Match: Balamurali Krishna → Carnatic Vocal; Mita Pandit → Hindustani Vocal; Kanyakumari → Violin;\nNikhil Banerjee → Sitar. [Q100]\n● Match: Pandit Durga Lal → Dance; Lalgudi Jayaraman → Instrumental music; Balamurali Krishna →\nVocal music; Amrita Shergil → Painting. [Q102]\n● Ustad Amjad Ali Khan, Sarod ke famous player hain. [Q109]\n59. Amjad Ali Khan — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: Amjad Ali Khan Pakhawaj ke NAHI, Sarod ke maestro hain ('Sarod Samrat').\n⚠️\n[Q77]\n60. V.G. Jog — The Violin Maestro\n● Sri V.G. Jog Violin player ke liye famous the. [Q79]\n61. 'Akum' and 'Todi' — Wind Instruments\n● Akum aur Todi wind instruments hain — Bansuri, Mohuri, Shankh, Ate/Jeeka jaise doosre wind\ninstruments. [Q80]\n62. 'Toti' — A Traditional Earring\n● 'Toti' Rajasthani women dwara ears mein pehna jaane wala traditional earring hai. [Q81]"," 63. Kathak Artists\n● Birju Maharaj, excellent Kathak dancer the (Lucknow Kalka-Bindadin gharana). [Q87]\n●\n Trap: Dhruvtara Joshi, Kathak dance se NAHI, Indian classical vocalist music se associate hain —\n⚠️\nBindadin, Shambhu Maharaj aur Lachhu Maharaj Kathak figures hain. [Q88]\n●\n Trap: Kishan Maharaj (1923-2008) Kathak artist NAHI, ek famous Tabla player the — Birju Maharaj,\n⚠️\nLachhu Maharaj aur Sitara Devi Kathak dancers hain. [Q89]\n64. Kalaripayattu — Ancient Martial Art\n● 'Kalaripayattu' South India ki ancient indigenous martial art hai (mostly Kerala) — ek living tradition hai.\n[Q91]\n65. Folk Culture — Definition\n● Folk culture, localized common logo ki everyday life ke unifying expressive components ko represent\nkarti hai — cultural practices of common people signify karti hai. [Q92]\n66. Kalamkari Painting\n● 'Kalamkari' South India mein hand-painted cotton textile hai — Persian words 'kalam' (pen) aur 'kari'\n(craftsmanship) se derived, Andhra Pradesh mein practice hoti hai. [Q93]\n67. Multi-Field Personalities — Match Lists\n● Match: Rukmani Devi → Bharatnatyam dance; Kumar Gandharva → Classical singing; Birju Maharaj →\nKathak dance; Rakesh Sharma → Astronaut. [Q94]\n● Match: Kavalam Narayana Panikkar → Theatre; Sharmila Tagore → Cinema; Balamurali Krishna →\nCarnatic vocal; Sonal Man Singh → Bharatnatyam & Odissi dance. [Q101]\n● Match: Mandakini Amte → Social Service & Community leadership; Neelam Mansingh Chowdhry →\nTheatre direction; Romila Thaper → History writing; Vanashree Rao → Dance. [Q103]\n68. Folk Songs — Preserving Traditions\n● Folk songs, traditions ko preserve karne ke liye paramount importance rakhte hain — generation-to-\ngeneration transfer hote hain. [Q95]\n69. Tyagaraja & Annamacharya — Composers"," ● Tyagaraja (1767 paida hue) ne Telugu mein Lord Rama ki praise mein thousands compositions ki —\nAnnamacharya (15th century) Tyagaraja ke contemporary NAHI the, aur Venkateshwara ki praise mein\nsankirtanas ke earliest known composer the. [Q96]\n70. Non-Classical Dance — Garba\n● Garba, Gujarat ki folk dance hai — classical NAHI (Kathak, Kuchipudi, Odissi classical hain). [Q97]\n71. M.S. Subbalakshmi — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: M.S. Subbalakshmi famous Carnatic vocalist thi, flute player NAHI — Bharat Ratna mila.\n⚠️\n[Q99]\n72. Modern Indian Painters — Match Lists\n● Amrita Shergil, Bikas Bhattacharjee, N.S. Bendre aur Subodh — sabhi famous painters the, distinct\nstyles ke liye jaane jaate hain. [Q104]\n● Match: Amrita Shergil → Painter; Bhimsen Joshi → Singer; Rukmini Devi Arundale → Dancer;\nSuryakant Tripathi 'Nirala' → Poet. [Q105]\n73. Sangeet Natak Akademi\n● Sangeet Natak Akademi (India ki National Academy of Music-Dance-Drama), pehli National Academy of\nArts thi — 28 January 1953 ko inaugurate hui. [Q106]\n● Match: Lalit Kala Akademy (5 August 1954); Sangeet Natak Akademi (1952, pehli National Academy of\nArts); National School of Drama (1959, SNA ke under); CCRT (1979). [Q158]\n74. Ronu Majumdar — Flute Player\n● Ronu Majumdar (born 22 June 1963, Varanasi, asli naam Rajendranath Majumdar) noted Hindustani\nflute player hain. [Q107]\n75. Authors & Artists — A Combined Match\n● Match: Taslima Nasrin → Lajja; Salman Rushdie → The Satanic Verses; M.F. Hussain → Painter;\nRukmini Arundale → Dance. [Q108]\n76. Zakir Hussain — A Match Trap"," ●\n Trap: Zakir Hussain, Tabla player hain, Harmonium ke NAHI.\n⚠️\n[Q110]\n77. The Veena — India's Most Ancient Instrument\n● Veena, India ka National Instrument hai — origin Vedic period se traced hoti hai. Goddess Saraswati\nVeena bajaati hain. [Q111]\n78. Folk Dance-State Pairs — A Trap\n●\n Trap: Korku (Maharashtra), Jhumar (Haryana), Mukna (Manipur, folk wrestling) sahi hain — Thali\n⚠️\nfolk dance Uttarakhand/Rajasthan ki hai, Himachal Pradesh ki NAHI. [Q113]\n79. Kuchipudi — Andhra Pradesh's Origin\n● Kuchipudi, Kuchelapuram/Kuchipudi village (Krishna district, Andhra Pradesh) mein originate hui. [Q114,\nQ115]\n80. Regional Festivals — Match List\n● Match: Hornbill Festival → Nagaland; Sangai Festival → Manipur; Flamingo Festival → Andhra\nPradesh; Hemis Festival → Ladakh. [Q117]\n81. Meghalaya's Folk Dance — 'Loho'\n● 'Loho' (Laho) Meghalaya ka folk dance hai — Nati Himachal Pradesh ki hai, Bamboo aur Khantum\nMizoram ki hain. [Q118]\n82. 'Surkhi' — Introduced by the Kushans\n● Indian architecture mein 'Surkhi' Kushans ne introduce ki — Mathura excavations mein evidence mila\n(200 BC-6th century). [Q119]\n83. 'Cultural Lag'\n●\n Trap: 'Cultural Lag' (culture ko technology catch-up karne mein time lagna) mein Politics factor NAHI\n⚠️\n\nhai — Religion, Law, Tradition zyada contribute karte hain. [Q120]"," 84. Male-Only Dances — Kathakali\n● Kathakali traditionally sirf males perform karte the — Vallathol Narayana Menon (Kerala Kalamandalam\nfounder) ne isse re-establish kiya. [Q121]\n● Kathakali mein mask dance perform hota hai — religious festivals mein elaborate masks-colourful\ncostumes ke saath. [Q122]\n85. Music Terminology — Match List\n● Match: Venkatamahi → Raga classification scheme; Pandit Vishnu Digambar Paluskar → Vande\nMataram ka music arrange kiya; Shyama Shastri → Carnatic music; Amir Khusrau → Khayal form.\n[Q123]\n86. 'Raas' Dance — Gujarat\n● 'Raas' Gujarat ka traditional folk dance hai — traditionally males ka (Garba females ka), lekin dono ab\nequally popular hain. [Q124]\n87. Bharat Ratna — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: 'India's first actress to win Bharat Ratna — Meena Kumari' galat hai — unhe kabhi Bharat\n⚠️\nRatna nahi mila. Lata Mangeshkar (2001) aur M.S. Subbulakshmi ko mila. [Q125]\n88. 'Bandit Queen' — Seema Biswas\n● 'The Bandit Queen' film mein lead character (Phoolan Devi) Seema Biswas ne play kiya — Shekhar\nKapur ne direct ki. [Q126]\n89. TV Serial 'Ramayan' — Ramanand Sagar\n● Famous T.V. serial 'Ramayan' ke writer-director-producer Ramanand Sagar the. [Q127]\n90. Films on Gandhi\n● 'The Making of the Mahatma' (1996, Gandhi ki early life) Shyam Benegal ne direct ki. [Q128]\n● 1982 ki epic film 'Gandhi' mein, Ben Kingsley ne title role play kiya. [Q129]\n● Richard Attenborough (producer-director, 'Gandhi' 1982 film) English actor-filmmaker the. [Q130]"," 91. 'Alam Ara' — India's First Talkie\n● 'Alam Ara' (1931, Ardeshir Irani ne direct ki), India ki pehli sound film (talkie) thi — 14 March 1931 ko\nMajestic Cinema, Bombay mein debut hui. [Q131]\n92. Devika Rani — Actress\n● Devika Rani (actress) ki shaadi Himanshu Rai se hui (1929, 1940 mein unki mrityu) — baad mein 1945\nmein Russian painter Svetoslav Roerich se dobara shaadi ki. [Q132]\n93. 'Mahabharat' TV Serial — B.R. Chopra\n● TV serial 'Mahabharat' B.R. Chopra ne produce ki, unke bete Ravi Chopra ne direct ki — 1998 mein\nDada Saheb Phalke Award mila. [Q133]\n94. Vidushaka — Sanskrit Drama Character\n● Sanskrit drama mein 'Vidushaka' (king ka jester/clown) invariably Brahmana category se hota hai —\nKalidasa, Bhasa jaise dramatists ne use kiya. [Q134]\n95. K. Shankar Pillai — Cartoonist\n● Kesava Shankara Pillai (Shankar) ek Indian cartoonist the — 1976 mein Padma Vibhushan mila. [Q135]\n96. Raghu Rai — Photography\n● Raghu Rai Indian photographer aur photojournalist hain. [Q136]\n97. Cultural Personalities — Match List\n● Match: Bhanu Bharti → Theatre direction-playwright; Mike Pandey → Wildlife filmmaker; Mohammed\nZahur Khayyam → Music composer; Vinda Karandikar → Marathi poet-writer. [Q137]\n98. Raja Ravi Varma — Modern Age Painter\n● Raja Ravi Varma, 1848 mein Kilimanoor Palace (Travancore, aaj ka Kerala) mein paida hue — great\nIndian painters mein se ek maane jaate hain. [Q138]"," 99. Abanindranath Tagore — Revivalistic Paintings\n● Abanindranath Tagore ('father of modern Indian painting') ki paintings 'Revivalistic' classify hoti hain —\ntraditional Indian techniques-themes ko revive karti hain. [Q139]\n● Abanindranath Tagore ne 1907 mein Kolkata mein 'Indian Society of Oriental Art' establish ki. [Q140]\n100. Nandalal Bose — Kala Bhavan\n● Nandalal Bose 1922 mein 'Kala Bhavan' (Shanti Niketan, Rabindranath Tagore ne 1919 mein found ki\nthi) ke Principal bane. [Q141]\n101. Vishnu Chinchalkar — Chitrakar\n● Vishnu Chinchalkar ek Chitrakar (artist-painter) the — M.F. Husain aur N.S. Bendre unke college mates\nthe. [Q142]\n102. The Mona Lisa Painting\n● 'Monalisa' Italian painter Leonardo da Vinci ki famous painting hai. [Q143]\n103. Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan — 'Mera Piya Ghar Aaya'\n● 'Mera piya ghar aaya' geet Pakistani singer Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan ne gaaya. [Q144]\n104. Jamini Roy — Painter\n● Jamini Roy ek famous Indian painter the. [Q145]\n105. The Gangasagar Mela — West Bengal\n● 'Gangasagar Mela' West Bengal mein, Makar Sankranti ke occasion par organize hoti hai. [Q146]\n106. Britney Spears — Singer\n● Britney Spears (American singer-actress, born 2 December 1981) singing ke liye famous hain. [Q147]"," 107. Thadingyut Festival — Myanmar\n● 'Thadingyut' festival (light ka festival) Myanmar mein 3-din tak celebrate hota hai. [Q148]\n108. Puran Singh — 'Tagore of Punjabi Language'\n● Sardar Puran Singh ko 'Tagore of Punjabi language' kaha jaata hai. [Q149]\n109. 'Satyam Shivam Sundaram' Painting\n● Famous painting 'Satyam Shivam Sundaram' Shivnandan Nautiyal ki masterpiece hai. [Q150]\n110. Multi-Field Personalities — More Match Lists\n● Match: Hindi Literature → Ras Khan; Urdu → Gyan Chandra Jain; Music & Dance → Savita Devi;\nPainting → Satish Chandra. [Q151]\n● Match: Santosh Yadav → Mountaineer; Oprah Winfrey → TV host; Oscar Wilde → Dramatist-author; P.\nSainath → Journalist. [Q152]\n111. Bachendri Pal — First Indian Woman on Everest\n● Bachendri Pal, 1984 mein, Mount Everest ki summit par pahunchne wali pehli Indian woman bani.\n[Q153]\n112. Famous Libraries — Match List\n● Match: Saraswati Mahal library → Thanjavur; Library of Tibetan Work and Archives → Dharamsala;\nRaza Library → Rampur; Khuda Baksh Oriental Public Library → Patna. [Q154]\n113. Traditional Dresses — A Trap\n●\n Trap: 'Mundu' Chhattisgarh ka NAHI, Kerala ka traditional garment hai (waist ke around pehna jaata\n⚠️\nhai). [Q155]\n114. Embroidery Arts — Match List\n● Match: Phulkari → Punjab; Dharaniya → Gujarat; Kasuti → Karnataka; Karchobi → Rajasthan. [Q156]"," 115. Shanti Niketan — Birbhum District\n● Shanti Niketan, Bolpur ke pass, Birbhum district (West Bengal) mein hai — Tagore ne isse 'Visva\nBharati' rename kiya, 'jaha duniya ek ghar mein aakar basti hai' bataya. [Q157]\n116. Iconic Monuments — Match List\n● Match: Gateway of India → Mumbai; Victoria Memorial → Kolkata; India Gate → New Delhi; Char Minar\n→ Hyderabad. [Q159]\n117. Places & Monuments — Match List\n● Match: Sriharikota → Andhra Pradesh; Sanchi Stupa → Raisen; Gujari Mahal → Gwalior; Taj-ul-Masjid\n→ Bhopal. [Q160]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Art and Culture Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0257","t":"55 Awards","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / History / Modern History","x":[" CH.55 — AWARDS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏆\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Fields of Various Awards — Kalidas Samman & Bhatnagar Award\n2. Sports Awards — Dronacharya, Arjuna & Maharana Pratap\n3. Nobel Prize Winners — Indians & Non-Recipients\n4. Nobel Peace Prize — World Leaders & Norman Borlaug\n5. The Magsaysay Award\n6. 'Stree Shakti Puraskar' (Nari Shakti Puraskar)\n7. Nargis Dutt — First Actress to Receive Padma Shree\n8. Bharat Ratna — Chronology, First Recipients & Foreign Awardees\n9. The Jnanpith Award\n10. The Vyas Samman — First Woman Recipient\n11. 'Swarna Kamal' — The Cinema Award\n12. The Booker Prize — First Indian-Origin Winner\n13. The Nobel Prize — The Awarding Institutions\n14. The Chakradhar Fellowship — Classical Music\n15. Satyajit Ray's Special Oscar Award\n16. Indian Cinema — A Trivia Trap\n1. Fields of Various Awards — Kalidas Samman & Bhatnagar Award\n● 'Kalidas Samman' Art field ke liye diya jaata hai — Madhya Pradesh Government annually deti hai. [Q1]\n● 'Shanti Swarup Bhatnagar' award Science and Technology field ke liye diya jaata hai — CSIR ke\nfounder Director Dr. Shanti Swarup Bhatnagar ke naam par, 1957 se, India ke researchers ko. [Q2]\n● Match: Bhatnagar Award → Science; B.C. Roy Award → Medicine; Dada Saheb Phalke Award → Film;\nGandharva Award → Classical Art. [Q8]\n2. Sports Awards — Dronacharya, Arjuna & Maharana Pratap\n● 'Dronacharya' Award, sports coaching mein excellence ke liye diya jaata hai — bronze statue, scroll of\nhonour aur cash amount ke saath. [Q4]\n● 'Arjuna Award' sports mein excellence ke liye diya jaata hai — Jamnalal Bajaj Award Gandhian values-\nsocial work, Tagore Award cultural harmony, Moortidevi Award literary contribution ke liye. [Q5]\n● Arjuna Award (aur Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna, ab Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna) ke saath us waqt Rs.\n3.0 lakh milte the — 2020 mein Khel Ratna ke liye 25 lakh aur Arjuna ke liye 15 lakh badha diye gaye.\n[Q6]\n● 'Maharana Pratap Award' (1982-83 mein establish hui) sirf Rajasthan ke players ko, sports mein\nexcellence ke liye, di jaati hai. [Q32]\n3. Nobel Prize Winners — Indians & Non-Recipients\n●\n Trap: H.J. Bhabha ko Nobel Prize NAHI mila — C.V. Raman (1930), R.N. Tagore (1913), Mother\n⚠️\nTeresa (1979) ko mila. [Q7]"," ●\n Trap: Subrahmanyan Chandrasekhar, Nobel Prize (1983) jeetne ke waqt Indian citizen NAHI the —\n⚠️\nwo Indian-American astrophysicist the, US citizen ban chuke the. Baaki Indian Nobel winners award ke\ntime Indian citizens the. [Q10]\n4. Nobel Peace Prize — World Leaders & Norman Borlaug\n● Archbishop Desmond Tutu (1984), Lech Walesa (1983), aur Yasser Arafat-Yitzhak Rabin-Shimon Peres\n(jointly) — sabhi ne Nobel Peace Prize jeeta. [Q9]\n● Norman Borlaug (American agronomist, 'Father of Green Revolution') ne 1970 mein world food supply\nmein contribution ke liye Nobel Peace Prize jeeta. [Q11]\n5. The Magsaysay Award\n● Vinoba Bhave pehle Indian the jinhone 1958 mein Magsaysay Award ('Asian Nobel') jeeta —\ngovernment service aur community leadership ke liye. [Q3]\n● Indian journalist Arun Shourie ne 1982 mein 'Ramon Magsaysay Award' jeeta. [Q38]\n6. 'Stree Shakti Puraskar' (Nari Shakti Puraskar)\n● 'Stree Shakti Puraskar' women ko unki courage aur women ke betterment ke liye enterprise (statements\n3 aur 4) ke liye di jaati hai — athletics excellence ke liye NAHI. [Q12]\n7. Nargis Dutt — First Actress to Receive Padma Shree\n● Nargis Dutt, 'Padma Shree Award' paane wali pehli Indian actress thi — 1958 mein. [Q13]\n8. Bharat Ratna — Chronology, First Recipients & Foreign Awardees\n●\n Trap: Raj Kapoor ko Bharat Ratna NAHI mila — Satyajit Ray (1992), Ustad Bismillah Khan aur Lata\n⚠️\nMangeshkar (2001) ko mila. [Q14]\n●\n Trap: Pandit Jasraj ko Bharat Ratna NAHI mila — Ustad Bismillah Khan-Lata Mangeshkar (2001),\n⚠️\nPandit Ravishankar (1999) ko mila. [Q15]\n● Nelson Mandela ko 1990 mein 'Bharat Ratna' mila — South Africa mein apartheid khatam karne ke\nunke kaam ke liye, Gandhian values par based movement. [Q17, Q18]\n● Pandit Ravi Shankar ko 1999 mein 'Bharat Ratna' mila. [Q19]\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad (India ke pehle President) ne 2 January 1954 ko 'Bharat Ratna' establish ki —\npehla award usi saal Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan, C. Rajagopalachari aur C.V. Raman ko mila. [Q20,\nQ21, Q22]"," ●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru pehle Bharat Ratna recipient NAHI the — unhe 1955 mein mila, jabki 1954\n⚠️\nke pehle recipients S. Radhakrishnan, C.V. Raman aur C. Rajagopalachari the. [Q23]\n●\n Trap (2005 ke question ke waqt): Atal Bihari Vajpayee ko us waqt tak Bharat Ratna NAHI mila tha\n⚠️\n(baad mein 2015 mein mila) — Kalam (1997), Lata Mangeshkar (2001), Satyajit Ray (1992) ko mila tha.\n[Q24]\n●\n Trap: Acharya Narendra Dev ko Bharat Ratna NAHI mila — J.R.D. Tata aur Satyajit Ray (1992), C.\n⚠️\nSubramaniam (1998) ko mila. [Q25]\n● J.R.D. Tata ko 1992 mein 'Bharat Ratna' mila. [Q26]\n● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan (Frontier Gandhi/Bacha Khan, Utmanzai, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Pakistan ke) ko\n1987 mein 'Bharat Ratna' mila — pehle non-Indian jinhe ye award mila. [Q36, Q37]\n9. The Jnanpith Award\n● Ashapurna Devi, 'Jnanpith' Award paane wali pehli lady thi — 1976 mein, 'Pratham Pratishruti' ke liye.\n[Q16]\n● Urdu poet Firaq Gorakhpuri ko 1969 mein 'Bhartiya Jnanpith' Award mila, 'Gule Nagma' ke liye. [Q34]\n10. The Vyas Samman — First Woman Recipient\n● Chitra Mudgal (Hindi fiction writer) 'Vyas Samman' ki pehli woman recipient thi — 2003 mein, apne\nnovel 'Avaan' ke liye. [Q27]\n11. 'Swarna Kamal' — The Cinema Award\n● 'Swarna Kamal' (Golden Lotus) aur 'Rajat Kamal' (Silver Lotus) awards Cinema field mein, National Film\nAwards ke through, best films ko diye jaate hain. [Q28]\n12. The Booker Prize — First Indian-Origin Winner\n● V.S. Naipaul, Indian origin ke pehle vyakti the jinhone 'Booker Prize' jeeta — 1971 mein, 'In a Free\nState' ke liye. [Q29]\n13. The Nobel Prize — The Awarding Institutions\n● Nobel Prizes Swedish Academy (aur related institutions — Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences,\nKarolinska Institute) dwara diye jaate hain — Alfred Nobel ne apni will mein ye institutions designate\nkiye the. [Q30]"," 14. The Chakradhar Fellowship — Classical Music\n● 'Chakradhar Fellowship' Classical Music field mein di jaati hai — King Chakradhar Singh (Raigarh) khud\nTabla-Pakhawaj ke great exponent the. [Q31]\n15. Satyajit Ray's Special Oscar Award\n● Satyajit Ray ko 1992 mein Special Oscar Award (Academy Honorary Award) mila — films mein unke\noutstanding contribution ke liye. [Q33]\n16. Indian Cinema — A Trivia Trap\n●\n Trap: Oscar ke liye nominate hone wali pehli Indian film 'Mughal-e-Azam' NAHI, 'Mother India'\n⚠️\n(1957, Mehboob Khan ne direct ki) thi. Keechak Vadham (1918) pehli full-length Tamil silent film thi, aur\nplayback singing pehli baar 1935 ki film 'Dhoop Chhaon' mein use hui. [Q35]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Awards Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0258","t":"01 East India Company Rule","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" 🏛️ EAST INDIA COMPANY RULE — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Regulating Act, 1773 — Supreme Court at Calcutta\n2. Major Company Acts — Important Match-the-Following\n3. Charter Act, 1813 — English Education\n4. Charter Act, 1813 — Trade Monopoly & Crown Sovereignty\n5. Charter Act, 1833 — Indians in Administration\n1. Regulating Act, 1773 — Supreme Court at Calcutta\n● Regulating Act, 1773 mein Fort William, Calcutta mein Supreme Court establish karne ka provision kiya\ngaya tha. Court 1774 mein establish hua. [Q1]\n● Is Supreme Court ke first Chief Justice Sir Elijah Impey the — Lemaister nahi. Isliye statement\n“Lemaister was the first Chief Justice” galat hai. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Major Company Acts — Important Match-the-Following\n● Board of Control ki establishment → Pitt's India Act, 1784. [Q3]\n● Supreme Court ki establishment → Regulating Act, 1773. [Q3]\n● English Missionaries ko India mein work karne ki permission → Charter Act, 1813. [Q3]\n● Governor-General's Council mein Law Member ki appointment → Charter Act, 1833. [Q3]\n3. Charter Act, 1813 — English Education\n● East India Company ne orientalist education system ko discourage kiya aur western education ko\npromote kiya. Charter Act, 1813 mein Company ko Indian education par har saal Rs 1 lakh spend karne\nka provision diya gaya. [Q4]\n● 1823 mein General Committee of Public Instruction constitute hui; is committee ko Rs 1 lakh education\ngrant dene ki responsibility mili. [Q4]\n● Orientalist–Anglicist Controversy education ke nature aur medium ko lekar thi. H.T. Prinsep aur Dr. H.H.\nWilson orientalist education ke supporter the; Anglicists ko Charles Trevelyan lead karte the aur English\nmedium se western education advocate karte the. [Q4]\n● Lord William Bentinck ke rule mein 7 March 1835 ko Lord Macaulay ka proposal accept hua aur English\nko higher education ka medium accept kiya gaya. [Q4]\n4. Charter Act, 1813 — Trade Monopoly & Crown Sovereignty\n● Charter Act, 1813 ne East India Company ka India ke saath trade monopoly abolish kar diya — lekin\nTea trade aur China ke saath trade par monopoly continue rahi. [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● Isi Act ne Company-held Indian territories par British Crown ki sovereignty assert ki. Local governments\nko taxes impose karne aur tax na dene walon ko punish karne ka power bhi diya gaya. [Q5, Q7]\n● Statement “India ka revenue ab British Parliament control karti thi” 1813 ke context mein galat hai:\nterritory aur revenue ke rights agle 20 saal Company ke under hi rahe. [Q7]"," ● Indian revenue British Parliament ke direct control mein Act of 1858 ke through aaya; isi system mein\nSecretary of State aur uski help ke liye Council of India ka arrangement tha. [Q7]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Charter Act 1813 vs 1833: Monopoly ka exact difference\n\n▸1813 → India ke saath Company ka trade monopoly end hua, BUT Tea aur China trade exception rahe.\n[Q5, Q6, Q7]\n\n▸1833 → East India Company ki commercial role entirely abolish ho gayi; future mein Company ko political\nfunctions hi perform karne the. [Q5]\n\n▸RULE: “Monopoly completely abolished” type wording aaye to 1833 ko 1813 se confuse mat karna.\n5. Charter Act, 1833 — Indians in Administration\n● Charter Act, 1833 ne pehli baar Indians ke liye apne country ke administration mein kuch share lena\npossible banaya. Is Act ki Section 87 bahut important thi. [Q8]\n● Section 87 ke mutabik India ya Crown ka koi person religion, place of birth, descent ya colour ke ground\npar Company ke kisi post/service se debar nahi kiya ja sakta tha. [Q8]\n● Baad mein Section 87 political movement ke dauran administration mein Indians ki participation ki\ndemand ka foundation bani. [Q8]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · East India Company Rule Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0259","t":"10 The Governance System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governance System Full Mind Map\n🏛️ THE GOVERNANCE SYSTEM — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. State & Sovereignty — Meaning and Essential Elements\n2. Parliamentary Government — Core Features & Cabinet Responsibility\n3. Presidential Government — Features & Parliamentary Comparison\n4. Indian Democracy, Republic, Welfare State & Good Governance\n5. Federalism in India — Federal Features and Unitary Bias\n6. Indian Federalism — Famous Scholars, Labels & Institutions\n7. Constitutional Nature — Rigidity, Flexibility & Bulky Constitution\n8. Political System & Public Administration — Key Thinkers\n9. Rule of Law, Liberty, Equality & Constitutional Government\n10. India–USA Comparison — Pocket Veto & Federal Differences\n1. State & Sovereignty — Meaning and Essential Elements\n● Garner ke definition ke according State = definite territory par permanently rehne wala community +\norganized government + external control se independence. State ke 4 essential elements:\nPopulation/People, Territory, Government aur Sovereignty. [Q1]\n● In chaar elements mein Sovereignty sabse prominent/important hai. Source ke mutabik 1947 se pehle\nIndia mein population, territory aur government the, lekin British control ki wajah se sovereignty absent\nthi. [Q2]\n● 'Sovereign' ka meaning source mein independent state hai—na dependency, na dominion.\nCommonwealth membership India ki sovereignty ko curtail nahi karti; given statements mein sirf\nmembership wala statement correct hai. [Q3]\n● Preamble ka idea source ke mutabik U.S. Constitution se liya gaya, jabki Preamble ki language Australia\nse borrowed batayi gayi hai. [Q4]\n2. Parliamentary Government — Core Features & Cabinet Responsibility\n● India Parliamentary form of Government follow karta hai, UK/Westminster model se influenced. Is system\nmein Executive Legislature se democratic legitimacy leta hai aur Legislature ke prati accountable hota\nhai. [Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● Parliamentary/Cabinet/Responsible Government ka central rule: Council of Ministers Lok Sabha ke prati\nresponsible; Government tab tak office mein rehti hai jab tak popular House ka majority support ho. Main\nadvantage = responsible government. [Q13, Q14, Q17]\n● Institutional features: Ministers Parliament se linked hote hain; non-MP minister 6 months ke baad cease\nkarta hai (Art. 75(5)); Council of Ministers collectively Lok Sabha ke prati responsible (Art. 75(3));\nCabinet ka head PM hai, President nahi. [Q15]\n● Source ke feature-list mein Executive responsibility, majority-party rule, collective responsibility, nominal\n& real executives, political homogeneity, double membership, PM leadership, lower-house dissolution\naur secrecy of procedure diye gaye hain. [Q16]\n● Indian Parliamentary system British model se isliye different hai kyunki Britain mein Parliament sovereign\nhai; India mein Constitution supreme/Parliament limited hai aur Judicial Review available hai.\nConstitution Bench substantial constitutional questions decide karti hai. [Q9, Q10, Q39]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governance System Full Mind Map\n● Indian polity ka feature Presidential Government nahi hai. India mein President nominal/formal head hai\naur real executive Council of Ministers headed by PM hai; Parliamentary Government, independent\njudiciary aur federal structure source ke recognised features hain. [Q11, Q12]\n● Centre aur States—dono ke Government authority ka source Constitution hai; Parliamentary system\nCentre ke saath States mein bhi established hai. [Q22]\n3. Presidential Government — Features & Parliamentary Comparison\n● Presidential Government mein executive powers President mein vested hoti hain; President Head of\nState aur Head of Government dono hota hai. Source isse single executive / centralized executive\npower ke roop mein describe karta hai. [Q18, Q30]\n● Presidential form America mein first emerged; American Presidency ko oldest/purest form bataya gaya\nhai. President fixed period ke liye indirectly elected hota hai. [Q32]\n● Source Q31 ke substantive explanation ke according President executive head hai aur Council of\nMinisters appoint karta hai, lekin Legislature dissolve nahi kar sakta. [Q31]\n\n⚠️SOURCE CONFLICT — Q31\n ▸HTML mein marked correct answer = (C) “President can dissolve the Legislature” as NOT a feature.\nExplanation ka substance bhi isi ko support karta hai, lekin explanation ki last line galti se “option (d)” likh\ndeti hai. Is conflict ko silently change nahi kiya gaya. [Q31]\n4. Indian Democracy, Republic, Welfare State & Good Governance\n● Indian political system ke cardinal points: Democratic Republic, Parliamentary Government aur supreme\npolitical power People of India mein. Unified authority nahi; Union aur States ke beech powers ka\nseparation/distribution hai. [Q19, Q29]\n● Source India ko Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic Republic aur welfare-oriented state batata hai;\nWelfare State ka constitutional direction DPSP se linked hai. [Q20, Q25, Q26]\n● Rule of Law aur democratic government Indian polity ke features hain; authoritarian government iska\nfeature nahi. Representatives periodic elections se choose hote hain. [Q21]\n● Good Governance ke features = accountability, transparency aur Rule of Law. Red Tapism excessive\nregulation hai jo action/decision-making ko hinder karta hai, isliye good governance ka feature nahi. [Q24]\n● India democratic hai kyunki governance ke important decisions elected representatives lete hain; sirf\nwritten Constitution hona democracy ka sufficient explanation nahi—source UK ka example deta hai.\n[Q23]\n● Constitutional philosophy mein democratic republic, equality of opportunity/status, socialist ideal aur adult\nfranchise included hain; Communist State philosophy nahi hai. India Parliamentary Democracy hai. [Q27,\nQ28]\n● Democracy ka base = people ko representatives elect/change karne ka right. Democracy ki superior\nvirtue common people ki wisdom aur character ko active banane mein hai. [Q33, Q34]\n● Republic ka meaning: supreme power people ke paas aur Head of State hereditary nahi, elected hota\nhai. India mein President indirect election se elected hota hai. [Q35, Q36, Q48]\n● Political parties ko source democracy ka ‘life-blood’ maanta hai; people bad governance ke liye parties\nko blame karte hain kyunki parties government mechanism ka visible/vital operator hoti hain. [Q49]\n● Party-less Democracy ke source mein Mahatma Gandhi aur Jay Prakash Narayan dono supported diye\ngaye hain—Gandhi Gram Swaraj/decentralized governance se, JP later ‘Dalheen Loktantra’ popularise\nkarne se linked hain. [Q50]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governance System Full Mind Map\n● Federal design ka objective diverse parts ko national integration mein weave karna tha; diversity ko\naccommodate karne se stronger nationhood build hoti hai. Women, Dalits, Poor aur Minority groups\ndemocracy ke major stakeholders hain because democracy dignity/self-respect protect karti hai. [Q51,\nQ53]\n● Indian political system mein ‘continuity and change’ dono elements source ke mutabik present hain;\nmodern, traditional aur saint-style elements ke coexistence ko reason maana gaya hai. [Q52]\n● Democratic determination mein supreme power ek single king/person mein vest hona democratic feature\nnahi. Second ARC ke Report 12 ‘Citizen-Centric Administration: The Heart of Governance’ mein good\ngovernance ke barriers/preconditions identify kiye gaye hain. [Q70, Q79]\n5. Federalism in India — Federal Features and Unitary Bias\n● Federal Constitution ka basic indicator = Centre aur States ke beech constitutional distribution of powers.\nIndian Constitution mein 7th Schedule ke through distribution diya gaya hai. [Q37]\n● India normal times mein federal system ke roop mein work karta hai, lekin strong Centre/unitary bias bhi\nhai; source Ambedkar ko quote karta hai ki war/emergency mein Constitution unitary tarah work kar\nsakta hai. [Q40, Q41]\n● Independent Judiciary federal character ki essential condition hai—Constitution interpret karti hai aur\nCentre-State disputes mein impartial umpire ka role nibhati hai. [Q42]\n● Federal features: written Constitution, rigidity, distribution of powers, independent judiciary, bicameral\nlegislature etc. Unitary features: single citizenship, Governors appointed by President/Centre,\nemergency provisions, integrated judiciary, strong Centre etc. [Q43, Q44, Q47]\n● Given unitary-element combinations mein Appointment of Governors, unequal representation in Rajya\nSabha aur All India Services source ke correct unitary elements hain. [Q45]\n● Indian federal structure mein strong unitary bias hai. Source Q46 ke according statements 1 & 2 correct:\nfederal system/basic distribution + strong unitary admixture; Union and State Legislatures dono\nsovereign nahi aur judicial powers separate federal compartments mein divided nahi hain. [Q46]\n● U.S. federal republic ka example source deta hai; India Article 1 ke under Union of States hai aur federal\nnature ke saath unitary features rakhta hai. [Q55]\n● Indian federation federating units ke agreement ka result nahi; constituent units ko secede karne ki\nfreedom nahi. Isi context mein ‘Union’ word ka Ambedkar explanation diya gaya hai. [Q56]\n● K.C. Wheare ke ‘Quasi-federal’ label ka source logic: generally federal, but Constitution emergency\nsituations mein unitary conversion allow karta hai. Independent judiciary/Judicial Review true feature hai,\npar Q57 mein quasi-federal hone ka correct explanation nahi. [Q57]\n● Indian Constitution na purely federal na purely unitary—source D.D. Basu ko combination of both se\nassociate karta hai; nature ko ‘federal in form but unitary in spirit / quasi-federal’ kaha gaya hai. [Q58, Q59]\n6. Indian Federalism — Famous Scholars, Labels & Institutions\n● Federalism labels: Cooperative Federalism — Granville Austin; Bargaining Federalism — Morris-Jones;\nQuasi Federalism — K.C. Wheare; Federalism with Centralising Tendency — Ivor Jennings. [Q60, Q61,\nQ62]\n● K.C. Wheare ne Indian Constitution ko rigidity aur flexibility ke beech good balance wala kaha;\namendment process mein simple majority, special majority etc. ki variety source explanation ka basis\nhai. [Q63]\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar se source statement associate karta hai: Constitution ‘tight mould of federalism’ mein\nset nahi hai; isme federal aur unitary dono characteristics hain. [Q64]\n● Unity among diversity promote karne ke liye source Inter-State Council/NDC, Finance\nCommission/Regional Council, Unitary Judicial System aur All India Services jaise institutions ko"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governance System Full Mind Map\nnecessary batata hai. Article 263, Article 280 aur Article 312 references bhi explanation mein diye gaye\nhain. [Q80]\n● Source ke mutabik Indian Parliamentary System 1970s (1971–80) mein Centralism se Federalism ki taraf\nshift hua, jab Congress many States mein power lose karne laga. [Q81]\n7. Constitutional Nature — Rigidity, Flexibility & Bulky Constitution\n● Indian Constitution partially rigid aur partially flexible hai: kuch provisions simple majority se, kuch Article\n368 ke special majority se, aur kuch cases mein at least 50% State Legislatures ki ratification ke saath\namend hote hain. [Q38]\n● Indian Constitution ko source world ka longest-written/bulkiest Constitution batata hai. Q54 ke options—\nmany constitutions ka experience, detailed administrative provisions, large country, Union+State\ngovernments—sab reasons ko true bataya gaya hai, lekin single valid option absent hai. [Q54]\n\n⚠️DISPUTED QUESTION — Q54\n ▸HTML explicitly “Disputed Question (Ans. *)” dikhata hai. Explanation ke mutabik listed saare reasons true\nhain, lekin “All of the above” option nahi diya gaya. [Q54]\n8. Political System & Public Administration — Key Thinkers\n● Herbert A. Simon ne ‘principles of administration’ ko myths/proverbs ke roop mein reject kiya; source\nDwight Waldo, Frank Marini aur F.W. Riggs ko contrasting side par mention karta hai. [Q65]\n● Development Administration concept source Fred W. Riggs se associate karta\nhai—socio-economic/political-economic change aur development objectives ke liye organised\ngovernmental efforts. [Q67]\n● Henri Fayol public aur private administration mein similarities/universal principles ke context mein diya\ngaya hai; source usse modern management theory ka father aur 14 principles se associate karta hai.\n[Q68]\n● ‘If our Civilization fails it will be mainly because of a breakdown of administration’ statement source B.\nDonham ko attribute karta hai. [Q69]\n9. Rule of Law, Liberty, Equality & Constitutional Government\n● Law aur Liberty ek doosre ke opposite nahi, complementary hain. Established laws freedom/liberty ko\nprotect/provide karte hain; lawlessness liberty ko secure nahi karti. [Q66]\n● A.V. Dicey ke Rule of Law ke source-elements: limitation/absence of arbitrary power, equality before law,\naur liberty/civil rights. ‘People’s responsibility to government’ is list ka feature nahi. [Q71]\n● Constitution ka chief purpose source ke mutabik Government ki structure/nature define karna ke saath\nGovernment power ko define aur limit karna hai; Constitutional Government by definition limited\nGovernment hai. [Q72, Q74]\n● Constitutionalism State authority par effective restrictions lagata hai individual liberty/public interest\nprotect karne ke liye; Q73 mein statement 2 correct hai. Constitutional government ka authority body of\nlaws/Constitution se determined hota hai. [Q73, Q75]\n● Positive liberty = restraints ki absence ke saath individuals ko personality development ke opportunities\ndena. Equality ka implication special privileges/hierarchy ka absence hai. [Q76, Q77]\n10. India–USA Comparison — Pocket Veto & Federal Differences"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governance System Full Mind Map\n● India aur USA dono ke President source ke mutabik Pocket Veto possess karte hain. Differences: India\nmein residuary powers Centre ke paas; USA mein States ke paas. Indian Rajya Sabha mein nominated\nmembers hain, U.S. upper house mein source says all members directly elected. [Q78]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0260","t":"11 National Symbols","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · National Symbols Full Mind Map\n🏛️ NATIONAL SYMBOLS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. National Anthem — Adoption, First Singing & Duration\n2. State Emblem — Sarnath Lion Capital & Adoption\n3. National Flag — Adoption Date & Constituent Assembly\n4. National Flag — Ratio, Ashoka Chakra & Flag Code 2002\n5. National Animal, Flower & Bird\n6. Other National Symbols — Tree, Fruit, Motto & Aquatic Animal\n7. National Calendar — Saka Era & Adoption\n1. National Anthem — Adoption, First Singing & Duration\n● 'Jana Gana Mana' ko Constituent Assembly ne 24 January 1950 ko India ke National Anthem ke roop\nmein accept/adopt kiya. Source Q2 specifically batata hai ki Rabindranath Tagore ne ise originally\nBengali mein compose kiya tha aur Hindi version ko Constituent Assembly ne National Anthem banaya.\n[Q1, Q2]\n● 'Jana Gana Mana' pehli baar 27 December 1911 ko Indian National Congress ke Calcutta session mein\ngaya gaya tha. [Q2]\n● National Anthem ki complete/formal rendition 52 seconds leti hai. First aur last line wale shortened\nversion ko play karne mein 20 seconds lagte hain. [Q1, Q3]\n2. State Emblem — Sarnath Lion Capital & Adoption\n● State Emblem Sarnath (Varanasi) ke Ashoka pillar se extracted hai. Government of India ne ise 26\nJanuary 1950 ko adopt kiya. [Q4]\n3. National Flag — Adoption Date & Constituent Assembly\n● Constituent Assembly ne India ke National Flag ka present design 22 July 1947 ko adopt kiya. Source\nQ5 ke mutabik adoption Constituent Assembly ke fourth session ke dauran hua tha. [Q5, Q7, Q8, Q9]\n● National Flag rectangular hai aur three colours se milkar bana hai. [Q8]\n4. National Flag — Ratio, Ashoka Chakra & Flag Code 2002\n● National Flag ki length : width ratio 3:2 hai; isi ko width : length mein likhen to 2:3 hota hai. Ashoka\nChakra ke centre wheel mein 24 spokes hain—21 nahi. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q11]\n● Flag Code of India, 2002 ne Tricolour ke unrestricted display ko allow kiya, jab tak flag ki honour aur\ndignity respect ki jaaye. Source ke mutabik ye 26 January 2002 se effective hua. [Q10]\n● Flag Code ke standard sizes mein 900 × 600 mm (Flag Size No. 6) included hai; 600 × 400 mm ko\nsource incorrect batata hai. [Q10]\n● White strip par 24-spoke wheel Ashoka Chakra/Dharmachakra ka depiction hai. Source ise 'wheel of\nLaw' batata hai aur given options mein Justice ko correct answer maanta hai. [Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · National Symbols Full Mind Map\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Ratio aur Dates ko ulta mat karo!\n ▸Flag adoption = 22 July 1947; 15 August 1947 ya January 1950 nahi. [Q5, Q7, Q8, Q9]\n ▸Length : Width = 3:2, lekin Width : Length = 2:3. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q10]\n ▸Ashoka Chakra = 24 spokes, 21 nahi. [Q6, Q11]\n5. National Animal, Flower & Bird\n● Tiger (Panthera Tigris Linnaeus) India ka National Animal hai. Source ke mutabik declining tiger\npopulation ko improve/protect karne ke liye Project Tiger April 1973 mein start hua. [Q12]\n● Lotus India ka National Flower hai aur source ise Indian Culture ka emblem batata hai. Scientific name:\nNelumbo Nucifera. [Q13]\n● Peacock India ka National Bird hai. Scientific name: Pavo Cristatus. [Q14]\n6. Other National Symbols — Tree, Fruit, Motto & Aquatic Animal\n● Source Q14 ke additional facts: Banyan = National Tree; Mango = National Fruit; 'Satyamev Jayte' =\nNational Motto, Mundaka Upanishad se liya gaya; Ganges River Dolphin = National Aquatic Animal.\n[Q14]\n7. National Calendar — Saka Era & Adoption\n● India ka National Calendar Saka era par based hai, Vikram Era par nahi. Iska first month Chaitra hai.\n[Q16]\n● National Calendar 22 March 1957 ko adopt hua tha, 26 January 1950 ko nahi. Isliye source question ke\ndono statements incorrect the aur answer 'Neither 1 nor 2' hai. [Q16]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0261","t":"12 State and Union Territories","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · State & Union Territories Full Mind Map\n🏛️ STATE & UNION TERRITORIES — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Article 1 — India, that is Bharat & Union of States\n2. Articles 2–3 — Parliament ka Power Map\n3. New State Bill — Procedure, Majority & State Views\n4. Union ka Meaning — No Right to Secede\n5. States & Union Territories — Numbers and First Schedule\n6. Delhi — Special UT / National Capital Territory\n7. Union Territories — Creation & Article 240\n8. Sikkim — Associate State se 22nd Full State\n9. Mizoram & Vananchal/Jharkhand — State Formation\n10. State Formation Chronology — High-Yield Timeline\n11. State Reorganisation Commission & 1956 Act\n12. Linguistic Reorganisation — Dhar, JVP & Andhra Pradesh\n13. Renaming / Reorganisation Facts\n14. Disputed / Outdated Source Questions — Exam Traps\n1. Article 1 — India, that is Bharat & Union of States\n● Article 1 kehta hai: 'India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States.' Constitution mein country ke naam\nBharat aur India dono milte hain. States aur unke territories First Schedule mein specified hain. [Q2, Q3]\n● Source ke current-status questions ke mutabik India mein 28 States aur 8 Union Territories hain; India\nsovereign, socialist, secular, democratic republic hai with parliamentary system, aur President Union\nexecutive ka constitutional head hai. [Q1]\n● Territory of India mein (1) States, (2) Union Territories aur (3) acquired territories shamil ho sakte hain.\n[Q3]\n2. Articles 2–3 — Parliament ka Power Map\n● Article 2 ke under Parliament kisi new State ko Union mein admit kar sakta hai ya new State establish\nkar sakta hai. [Q7, Q8, Q15, Q17]\n● Article 3 ke under Parliament: new State form kar sakta hai, kisi State ka area increase/diminish kar\nsakta hai, boundary alter kar sakta hai aur State ka naam change kar sakta hai. New State carve-out ka\ncore power Parliament mein vested hai. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q12, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q39]\n● Article 3 ki Explanation ke source note mein clauses (a)–(e) ke liye 'State' mein Union Territory include\nhota hai; proviso ke context mein State ka meaning alag treat kiya gaya hai. [Q16]\n3. New State Bill — Procedure, Majority & State Views\n● New State/area-boundary-name change wala law ordinary legislative process se simple majority se pass\nhota hai. Article 4(2) ke according aisa law Article 368 ke purpose ke liye Constitutional Amendment\nnahi maana jaata. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● Article 3 Bill Parliament mein President ki prior recommendation se introduce hota hai. President\nconcerned State Legislature se specified period mein views mangta hai. [Q13, Q14]\n● Concerned State Legislature ki consent mandatory nahi hai; uske views Parliament/President par binding\nnahi. State views na de, ya oppose kare, tab bhi source explanation ke mutabik process proceed kar\nsakta hai. [Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · State & Union Territories Full Mind Map\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Article 2 vs Article 3 vs Article 4\n ▸Article 2 = admission/establishment of new States; Article 3 = formation + area/boundary/name changes.\n[Q4, Q7, Q8, Q17]\n ▸Simple majority enough; Article 368 special amendment procedure required nahi. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n ▸State Legislature se views liye jaate hain, consent nahi. [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n4. Union ka Meaning — No Right to Secede\n● 'Union of States' expression ka source logic: Indian States ko Union se secede hone ka right nahi hai.\nParliament unilateral constitutional power se area/boundary/name alter kar sakta hai. [Q18, Q19]\n● Secession ki advocacy Article 19 speech protection ke under absolute nahi hai; source explanation\nreasonable restrictions ka point emphasise karta hai. [Q19]\n5. States & Union Territories — Numbers and First Schedule\n● States Reorganisation Act, 1956 ke baad 14 States aur 6 Union Territories bane. Source repeatedly isi\ncount ko test karta hai. [Q20, Q21, Q22, Q61]\n● Source ke present-status explanation ke mutabik current count 28 States + 8 Union Territories hai.\nTelangana 2 June 2014 ko 29th State bana tha; 2019 J&K reorganisation ke baad total States 28 hue,\naur Dadra & Nagar Haveli + Daman & Diu merger ke baad UTs 8 hue. [Q23, Q24, Q25, Q26]\n● Goa State hai, Union Territory nahi. First Schedule States aur Union Territories ke names list karta hai.\n[Q26]\n6. Delhi — Special UT / National Capital Territory\n● Delhi First Schedule ke under Union Territory hai. 69th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1991 se Delhi ko\nspecial status mila aur source ise National Capital Territory/Region context mein test karta hai. [Q27, Q28]\n7. Union Territories — Creation & Article 240\n● UT creation-year match: Lakshadweep — 1956; Dadra & Nagar Haveli — 1961; Daman & Diu — 1962;\nChandigarh — 1966. Source note: 26 Jan 2020 se Dadra & Nagar Haveli aur Daman & Diu integrated\nUT hain. [Q29]\n● Article 240 President ko certain UTs ke peace, progress/good government ke liye regulations banane ki\npower deta hai. Source list: Andaman & Nicobar Islands, Lakshadweep, Dadra & Nagar Haveli and\nDaman & Diu, aur Puducherry. [Q30, Q31]\n● Dadra & Nagar Haveli Portuguese rule mein tha; source ke mutabik Portuguese rule 1954 tak raha, jab\nIndian Union supporters ne territory occupy ki. [Q32]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Article 240 Source Update\n ▸Old sub-clause mapping ko blindly mat ratna: source specifically batata hai ki merged UT ke baad Article\n240(1)(c) relevant hai aur old 240(1)(d) repealed hai. [Q30]\n ▸Goa State hai; Article 240 UT list mein Goa ko include mat karo. [Q31]\n8. Sikkim — Associate State se 22nd Full State\n● 35th Amendment Act, 1974 ne Sikkim ko Associate State framework diya (Article 2A). 36th Amendment\nAct, 1975 ne Sikkim ko full-fledged 22nd State of India banaya. [Q33, Q34, Q36, Q37]\n● Sikkim 1975 mein India ka integral/full State bana. Source Q35 Sikkim ko botanists' paradise batata hai\naur population context mein Lepchas, Bhutias aur Nepalis ka mention karta hai. [Q35]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · State & Union Territories Full Mind Map\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Sikkim: 35th vs 36th Amendment\n ▸Full-fledged State = 36th Amendment, 1975. [Q34, Q36, Q37]\n ▸Q33 ke options mein 36th nahi tha, isliye source key 35th ko chooses while explanation clearly full\nintegration 36th se batata hai. [Q33]\n9. Mizoram & Vananchal/Jharkhand — State Formation\n● Mizoram ko State status 53rd Constitutional Amendment ke through mila; formation 20 February 1987 ko\nhui. Source settlement date 30 June 1986 bhi deta hai. [Q38]\n● Bihar se separate Vananchal/Jharkhand-type State create karne ki constitutional power Article 3 ke\nunder Parliament ke paas hai. [Q39]\n10. State Formation Chronology — High-Yield Timeline\nAndhra Pradesh\n1953 — first linguistic State [Q47, Q58, Q59, Q60]\nNagaland\n1963 [Q42, Q46, Q48, Q50]\nHaryana\n1 Nov 1966 [Q40, Q42, Q46, Q47, Q49]\nHimachal Pradesh\nState: 25 Jan 1971 [Q47, Q51, Q52]\nMeghalaya\n21 Jan 1972 [Q46, Q48]\nSikkim\n16 May 1975 / 22nd State [Q41, Q42, Q46, Q47, Q48]\nArunachal Pradesh\n20 Feb 1987 [Q41, Q42, Q48]\nGoa\n30 May 1987 [Q40, Q52]\nChhattisgarh\n1 Nov 2000 [Q41, Q43]\nUttarakhand\n9 Nov 2000 [Q44]\nJharkhand\n15 Nov 2000 [Q40, Q41, Q45, Q50]\nTelangana\n2 Jun 2014 [Q40, Q50]\n● Chronology questions ka source order: Haryana (1966) → Goa (1987) → Jharkhand (2000) →\nTelangana (2014); aur Sikkim (1975) → Arunachal Pradesh (1987) → Chhattisgarh (1 Nov 2000) →\nJharkhand (15 Nov 2000). [Q40, Q41]\n● Other tested orders: Nagaland 1963 → Haryana 1966 → Meghalaya 1972 → Sikkim 1975; Andhra\nPradesh 1953 → Haryana 1966 → Himachal Pradesh 1971 → Sikkim 1975; Nagaland 1963 →\nMeghalaya 1972 → Sikkim 1975 → Arunachal Pradesh 1987. [Q42, Q46, Q47, Q48]\n● Source Q49 descending order Haryana → Maharashtra → Rajasthan deta hai; explanation Maharashtra\n1960 aur Rajasthan ko 1958 (with note present boundary 1 Nov 1956) ke form mein state karta hai. [Q49]\n11. State Reorganisation Commission & 1956 Act\n● States Reorganisation Commission 29 December 1953 ko establish hua (source Q61 broad 'December\n1953'). Chairman Justice/Fazl Ali; members K.M. Panikkar aur H.N./Hridaynath Kunzru. Report\nSeptember 1955 / source Q53: 30 September 1955. [Q53, Q54, Q55, Q61]\n● Pattabhi Sitaramayya SRC member nahi the; woh JVP Committee ke member the. SRC ne 'one\nlanguage-one state' theory accept nahi ki aur source Q61 ke mutabik Bombay aur Punjab split ko\nsupport nahi kiya. [Q55, Q61]\n● States Reorganisation Act, 1956 ke through large-scale linguistic reorganisation hua aur 14 States + 6\ncentrally administered/Union Territories bane. [Q56, Q57, Q61, Q62]\n12. Linguistic Reorganisation — Dhar, JVP & Andhra Pradesh"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · State & Union Territories Full Mind Map\n● S.K. Dhar Commission (1948) ne linguistic affinity ke bajay administrative convenience/viability ko\npreference di. December 1948 JVP Committee — Jawaharlal Nehru, Vallabhbhai Patel, Pattabhi\nSitaramayya — ne bhi linguistic reorganisation ko reject kiya. [Q18, Q64]\n● Nagpur Congress Session 1920 ke baad Provincial Congress Committees linguistic basis par organise ki\ngayi thi; lekin 1948 Congress/JVP position linguistic provinces ke favour mein nahi thi. [Q64]\n● Andhra Pradesh October 1953 mein first State bana jo linguistic basis par create hua; source Potti\nSriramulu agitation/death ko context deta hai. Comprehensive reorganisation 1956 se hua. [Q20, Q53, Q56,\nQ58, Q59, Q60]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · State & Union Territories Full Mind Map\n13. Renaming / Reorganisation Facts\n● Mysore ka naam Karnataka Mysore State (Alteration of Name) Act, 1973 se hua; source kehta hai Tamil\nNadu wala pairing incorrect tha. Bombay State 1960 mein Gujarat aur Maharashtra mein bifurcate hua;\nGoa 1987 mein Daman & Diu se separate hua; Himachal Pradesh 1971 mein State bana. [Q52]\n● Source capital-name examples: Madras→Chennai, Calcutta→Kolkata, Bombay→Mumbai,\nTrivandrum→Thiruvananthapuram, Bangalore→Bengaluru. Q63 ko source changing Andhra Pradesh\ncapital scenario ki wajah se disputed/outdated maanta hai. [Q63]\n14. Disputed / Outdated Source Questions — Exam Traps\n\n⚠️SOURCE-BASED DISPUTED / OUTDATED QUESTIONS\n ▸Q24 wording asks States after formation of Telangana: historically source itself says Telangana became\n29th State, but answer key marks 28 reflecting later J&K reorganisation/current situation. [Q24]\n ▸Q33 full-state fact = 36th Amendment (1975), but 36th option missing tha; source key 35th chooses. [Q33]\n ▸Q50 List-II mein Nagaland ke liye 1962 diya gaya, source explanation correct year 1963 batata hai; options\ndefective hain. [Q50]\n ▸Q51 asks which 'State' formed in 1948: source says none; Himachal Pradesh 1948 mein province bana,\nState 1971 mein. [Q51]\n ▸Q53 SRC establishment = 29 Dec 1953; source says none of the options accurately match. [Q53]\n ▸Q63 Andhra Pradesh capital-renaming question changing scenario ki wajah se source dwara\ndisputed/outdated marked hai. [Q63]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0262","t":"13 The Citizenship","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Citizenship Full Mind Map\n🏛️ THE CITIZENSHIP — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Constitutional Framework — Part II & Articles 5–11\n2. Single Citizenship & Single Domicile\n3. Citizenship Act, 1955 — Acquisition of Citizenship\n4. Loss of Citizenship — Renunciation, Termination & Deprivation\n5. Naturalised Citizen — President & Deprivation Rules\n6. OCI Card — Citizenship Amendment Act, 2015\n7. Article 11 — Parliament ka Exclusive Legislative Power\n8. Citizenship (Amendment) Act, 2019 — Timeline & Purpose\n1. Constitutional Framework — Part II & Articles 5–11\n● Indian Constitution mein citizenship ke provisions Part II mein diye gaye hain. Citizenship se directly\nrelated constitutional Articles 5 se 11 tak hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n2. Single Citizenship & Single Domicile\n● India ne poore desh ke liye single citizenship adopt ki hai — citizen ke paas India ki citizenship hoti hai,\nkisi particular State ki separate constitutional citizenship nahi. [Q4, Q5]\n● Source statement ke mutabik India mein ek samay par one citizenship aur one domicile ka principle\napply hota hai. Single citizenship ka concept British/United Kingdom constitutional system se adopted\nbataya gaya hai. [Q8]\n● U.S.A. mein dual citizenship ka principle source ke mutabik accepted hai — ek U.S. citizenship aur ek us\nState ki citizenship jahan person reside karta hai. [Q11]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — India vs U.S.A. — Citizenship Pattern\n ▸India = single citizenship. U.S.A. = dual citizenship. [Q4, Q5, Q10, Q11]\n ▸Q10 ka statement 2 galat hai, kyunki source ke mutabik U.S.A. dual polity ke saath dual citizenship rakhta\nhai; India single citizenship provide karta hai. [Q10]\n3. Citizenship Act, 1955 — Acquisition of Citizenship\n● Citizenship Act, 1955 (as amended) ke according citizenship paanch bases par acquire ho sakti hai:\nBirth, Descent, Registration, Naturalization aur Incorporation of Territory. Indian bank mein money\ndeposit karna citizenship acquisition ka basis nahi hai. [Q6]\n● Article 11 Parliament ko citizenship ke acquisition aur termination ko law ke through regulate karne ki\npower deta hai. Isi power ka use karke Parliament ne Citizenship Act, 1955 enact kiya. [Q12]\n● Source Q13 ke mutabik Section 5(1)(a) ke under registration se citizenship lene ke liye person of Indian\norigin ko ordinarily India mein 7 years reside karna hota hai. [Q13]\n4. Loss of Citizenship — Renunciation, Termination & Deprivation\n● Citizenship Act, 1955 citizenship lose hone ke teen modes batata hai: Renunciation (tyag), Termination\n(samapti) aur Deprivation (vanchit kiya jana). [Q7]\n● Indian citizenship renounce karna ya voluntarily kisi doosre country ki citizenship acquire karna\ncitizenship loss se linked hai. Sirf foreign citizen se marriage karna ya government criticize karna, source\nQ7 ke context mein citizenship loss ka automatic ground nahi. [Q7]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Citizenship Full Mind Map\n● Source Q8 ke mutabik registration/naturalization fraud, false representation/concealment, Constitution ke\nprati disloyalty, war-time enemy dealing, ya continuous 7 years ordinary residence outside India jaise\ngrounds par citizenship cancel/deprive ki ja sakti hai. [Q8]\n5. Naturalised Citizen — President & Deprivation Rules\n● India mein Head of State/President banne ke liye source Q8 ke mutabik sirf citizen-by-birth hona\nnecessary nahi; naturalised citizen bhi eligible ho sakta hai. [Q8]\n● Naturalised citizen ko kabhi bhi citizenship se deprive nahi kiya ja sakta — yeh statement source ke\nmutabik galat hai. Citizenship Act, 1955 ke Section 10 ke provisions ke subject to deprivation possible\nhai. [Q10]\n● Q10 ke mixed statement set mein Articles 371-A se 371-I ko Nagaland, Assam, Manipur, Andhra\nPradesh, Sikkim, Mizoram, Arunachal Pradesh aur Goa ki regional demands se linked bataya gaya hai;\nsource key mein sirf statement 1 correct hai. [Q10]\n6. OCI Card — Citizenship Amendment Act, 2015\n● Source Q9 Citizenship Amendment Act, 2015 ke Section 7(A) ke under OCI cardholder registration\ndiscuss karta hai. Pakistan, Bangladesh ya specified country se linked prescribed ancestry categories\nOCI eligibility ko bar kar sakti hain. [Q9]\n● Isliye source question mein Partition ke baad Pakistan migrate karne wala Indian OCI cardholder\nregistration ke liye eligible nahi maana gaya hai. [Q9]\n7. Article 11 — Parliament ka Exclusive Legislative Power\n● Article 11 ke under citizenship ka right regulate karne ke liye law banane ki power Parliament ke paas\nhai. Citizenship Act, 1955 acquisition aur termination ke provisions deta hai; source Section 18 ke under\nCentral Government ke rules-making power ka bhi mention karta hai. [Q12]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Q14 — Disputed Question / No Correct Option\n ▸Question options: Court, President, Lok Sabha, Central Government, State Government — lekin source\nexplanation ke mutabik exclusive power Parliament ke paas hai. [Q14]\n ▸Parliament option mein diya hi nahi gaya; isliye source ne Q14 ko disputed mark karke “none of the options\nare correct” kaha hai. [Q14]\n8. Citizenship (Amendment) Act, 2019 — Timeline & Purpose\n● Source timeline: Citizenship (Amendment) Bill, 2019 Lok Sabha se 9 December 2019 ko pass hua; Rajya\nSabha ne 11 December 2019 ko pass kiya; President ka assent 12 December 2019 ko mila. [Q15, Q16]\n● Source Q15 ke mutabik Bill ne Citizenship Act, 1955 amend kiya aur Afghanistan, Bangladesh aur\nPakistan se aaye specified non-Muslim communities ke liye religion-based citizenship provision\nintroduce karne ka purpose bataya gaya hai, cut-off 31 December 2014 ke context ke saath. [Q15]\n● Source Q17 purpose ko persecuted minority groups — Hindus, Sikhs, Buddhists, Jains, Parsis aur\nChristians — from Afghanistan, Bangladesh and Pakistan ko citizenship grant karna batata hai, jo\nDecember 2014 ke end se pehle India aaye. [Q17]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — CAA 2019 — Date Confusion\n ▸11 December 2019 = Rajya Sabha passage / source Q16 answer date. [Q15, Q16]\n ▸12 December 2019 = President’s assent. Dono dates ko mix mat karna. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0263","t":"14 Fundamental Rights","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n\n⚖️FUNDAMENTAL RIGHTS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Fundamental Rights — Background, Nature & Part III\n2. Right to Equality — Articles 14–18\n3. Reservation & Public Employment — Articles 15–16\n4. Article 17 — Abolition of Untouchability\n5. Right to Freedom — Article 19\n6. Article 21 — Life, Liberty & Privacy\n7. Article 21A — Right to Education\n8. Article 20 — Protection in Conviction\n9. Article 22 — Arrest & Preventive Detention\n10. Right against Exploitation — Articles 23–24\n11. Right to Freedom of Religion — Articles 25–28\n12. Cultural & Educational Rights — Articles 29–30\n13. Article 32 — Constitutional Remedies & Writs\n14. Article Mapping — Match-the-Following\n15. FR vs DPSP — Amendment & Basic Structure Cases\n16. Right to Property — Article 300A\n17. What Is / Is Not a Fundamental Right\n18. Citizens vs Foreigners — Who Gets Which Rights\n19. Rights, Duties, Right to Service & Citizen Charter\n1. Fundamental Rights — Background, Nature & Part III\n● Liberal democracy mein liberty ka best safeguard source key ke mutabik Separation of Powers hai; rule\nof law aur power-restraint liberty ko protect karte hain. [Q1]\n● 1931 Karachi Congress Session ne Fundamental Rights aur National Economic Programme par\nresolution adopt kiya; source explanation Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ko session president batata hai.\nNehru Report (1928) ne bhi Constitution mein Fundamental Rights include karne ki advocacy ki thi. [Q2,\nQ3]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne Fundamental Right ko Constitution mein permanent protection ke roop mein\ndekhne ki baat kahi; Dr. S. Radhakrishnan ne Fundamental Rights ko “a pledge to our people and a pact\nwith the civilized world” kaha. [Q4, Q5]\n● Fundamental Rights justiciable/enforceable hain, personality development ke liye essential bataye gaye\nhain aur Part III mein enumerated hain. Source ke mutabik Emergency mein rights suspend ho sakte\nhain, lekin Articles 20 aur 21 suspend nahi kiye ja sakte. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10]\n● Article 13 pre-constitutional aur post-constitutional laws ko Fundamental Rights se inconsistent hone ki\nextent tak void karta hai; source isse Constitution ki paramountcy regarding Fundamental Rights se\njodta hai. [Q11, Q12]\n2. Right to Equality — Articles 14–18\n● Right to Equality Articles 14–18 mein hai: Article 14 equality before law/equal protection; Article 15 non-\ndiscrimination; Article 16 public employment mein equality of opportunity; Article 17 untouchability\nabolition; Article 18 titles abolition. [Q13, Q14]\n● Article 14 “equality before law” aur “equal protection of laws” deta hai. Unguided/uncontrolled\ndiscretionary power aur unequal application of law ko source Article 14 ke violation se link karta hai.\nRule of Law ka core — koi bhi law se upar nahi. [Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n● Religion, race, caste, sex ya place of birth ke grounds par discrimination ka prohibition Article 15 ke\nunder Right to Equality ka part hai. Economic equality ko source six/equality guarantees ke listed\nFundamental Right ke roop mein include nahi karta. [Q20, Q25]\n● Source Assertion–Reason mein unequal persons ko level playing field ke liye differently treat karna aur\nequals ke saath equal law administer karna compatible principles bataye gaye hain. [Q26]\n3. Reservation & Public Employment — Articles 15–16\n● State of Madras v. Champakam Dorairajan ke baad First Constitutional Amendment, 1951 se Article\n15(4) add hua — socially/educationally backward classes aur SC/ST ke advancement ke liye special\nprovisions. [Q21]\n● Article 15(5) educational institutions — including source wording ke mutabik private aided/unaided\ninstitutions — mein reservation-related special provision se linked hai; source 93rd Amendment Act,\n2005 ka reference deta hai. [Q22]\n● OBC/backward-class reservation framework source mein Article 15(4) aur Article 16(4) se linked hai.\nArticle 16(1)–(2) public employment mein equality of opportunity/non-discrimination ko cover karta hai.\n[Q23, Q24]\n● Source ke mutabik Article 16(4) reservation policy ko Article 335 ke “maintenance of efficiency of\nadministration” background mein interpret kiya gaya, lekin Article 335 “efficiency” term define nahi karta.\n77th Amendment Act, 1995 ne Article 16(4A) insert karke SC/ST promotion reservation enable kiya.\n[Q27, Q28]\n● Equal pay for equal work ko source Supreme Court reasoning mein Preamble ke “Socialist”, Articles 14 &\n16 aur Article 39(d) ko saath padhkar deduce kiya gaya; Randhir Singh case ka reference diya gaya hai.\n[Q29, Q30]\n4. Article 17 — Abolition of Untouchability\n● Article 17 untouchability ko abolish karta hai aur uski practice ko kisi bhi form mein forbid karta hai.\nSource is provision ko Right to Equality ka part aur SC/ST dignity/socio-economic-political-cultural rights\nse linked principle batata hai. [Q31, Q32, Q33, Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37]\n● Untouchability abolition ke liye source laws, education improvement aur public awareness ko measures\nmaanta hai; Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 ka reference diya gaya hai. Structural violence\nAssertion–Reason mein untouchability aur religious sanctions ko linked bataya gaya hai. [Q38, Q39]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Q40 — Disputed Question\n ▸Source ne Q40 ko “Disputed Question” mark kiya hai. Articles 14, 15, 16, 19 ko do tarah se classify kiya ja\nsakta hai. [Q40]\n ▸Category-wise Article 19 alag hai (Right to Freedom), jabki 14–16 Right to Equality mein hain; person-vs-\ncitizen test par Article 14 alag ho sakta hai, kyunki source 15, 16 aur 19 ko citizen-only batata hai. [Q40]\n5. Right to Freedom — Article 19\n● Right to Freedom source mapping mein Articles 19–22 cover karta hai. Article 19(1) six freedoms deta\nhai: speech/expression, peaceful assembly without arms, association/union/co-operative society,\nmovement, residence/settlement, aur profession/occupation/trade/business. Property wali old freedom\nArticle 19(1)(f) source ke mutabik 44th Amendment se remove hui. [Q41, Q42]\n● Freedom of speech & expression Article 19(1)(a) se linked hai. Source freedom of press/newspapers ko\nisi clause ka part maanta hai, separate express constitutional right nahi; private building par National\nFlag hoist karna bhi Supreme Court holding ke through Article 19(1)(a) se linked bataya gaya hai. [Q43,\nQ44, Q45, Q46, Q47, Q48]\n● Peaceful assembly without arms Article 19(1)(b) ke under hai; source ke mutabik officials ka gherao is\nfreedom ka protected part nahi. [Q49]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n● Article 19(2) speech/expression par reasonable restrictions ke grounds source mein sovereignty &\nintegrity, security of State, friendly relations, public order, decency/morality, contempt, defamation aur\nincitement context se linked hain; “unbecoming criticism” source key mein restriction ground nahi hai,\naur Q51 key Security of State + Defamation + Public Order ko select karta hai. [Q50, Q51]\n6. Article 21 — Life, Liberty & Privacy\n● Article 21 life and personal liberty protect karta hai. Source “due process” interpretation ko Article 21 se\nlink karta hai aur foreign travel ko bhi Article 21 protection ke under rakhta hai. [Q52, Q53, Q54]\n● Maneka Gandhi (1978) ke baad source judicial interpretation ke mutabik Article 21 ki procedure\nfair/reasonable honi chahiye; Q55 mein petitioner par arbitrariness prove karne ka burden wali statement\nincorrect answer hai. [Q55]\n● Source Supreme Court-recognised rights mein shelter, travel abroad aur equal pay for equal work list\nkarta hai. Privacy ko Article 21 aur Part III freedoms se intrinsic right ke roop mein place kiya gaya hai.\n[Q56, Q57, Q58, Q59, Q60]\n● Person of one’s choice se marriage ko Article 21 safeguard se link kiya gaya hai. Q62 source key capital\npunishment ko Article 21 purview ke bahar option ke roop mein choose karta hai. National Emergency\nmein life & personal liberty source ke mutabik suspend/restrict nahi ki ja sakti. [Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● Unnikrishnan v. Andhra Pradesh decision ko source Article 21 ke scope mein Right to Education include\nkarne se link karta hai. [Q64]\n7. Article 21A — Right to Education\n● 6–14 years age group ke children ke liye Right to Education source ke mutabik Fundamental Right hai.\nSource Q66 answer date 1 April 2010 deta hai; Q67 ise human right aur fundamental right dono maanta\nhai. [Q65, Q66, Q67]\n● Education Assertion–Reason mein State ki free & compulsory education duty aur democratic society\nmein development ke liye education ki indispensability — dono true aur reason explanatory maana gaya\nhai. [Q68]\n8. Article 20 — Protection in Respect of Conviction\n● Article 20 criminal-conviction safeguards se linked hai. Source “prohibition against torture” ko Article 20\nka listed part nahi maanta. [Q72]\n● Article 20 protections mein double jeopardy aur self-incrimination source questions ka focus hai: same\noffence ke liye more than once prosecuted/punished nahi; Article 20(3) accused ko khud ke against\nwitness banne ke liye compel karne se protect karta hai. [Q76, Q77, Q78]\n9. Article 22 — Arrest & Preventive Detention\n● Arrested person ke safeguards Article 22 se linked hain. Source Q80 mein Article 22(2) ko “Parliament\nmay prescribe detention beyond three months” se match karna incorrect bataya gaya hai. [Q79, Q80]\n● Source Preventive Detention questions mein without trial detention ka standard answer 3 months diya\ngaya hai. [Q81, Q82]\n● Q83 mixed statements mein source key “Only one” correct statement choose karta hai; explanation\npreventive detention/legal counsel aur POTA confession issues discuss karta hai. Parole question mein\nsource State Governments ke apne parole rules ko correct maanta hai, lekin parole ko absolute right\nnahi. [Q83, Q84]\n10. Right against Exploitation — Articles 23–24\n● Right against Exploitation mein source human trafficking/forced labour prohibition (Article 23) aur child\nemployment prohibition (Article 24) ko core provisions maanta hai; untouchability aur minority interests is\ncategory ka part nahi. [Q69]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n● Children ko hazardous factories/mines/work mein employ karne ka prohibition Article 24 se directly linked\nhai; source ise absolute prohibition ke roop mein describe karta hai. [Q70, Q71, Q73, Q74]\n● Source Q75 ICCPR mein Child Rights ko Article 24 se match karta hai. [Q75]\n● Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act source ke mutabik 1976 mein enact hua; child labour hazardous\nemployment prohibition ko Constitution Article 24, international protection aur M.C. Mehta v. State of\nTamil Nadu (1996) context se link kiya gaya hai. [Q158, Q159]\n11. Right to Freedom of Religion — Articles 25–28\n● Article 25 freedom of conscience aur religion ko profess, practice, propagate karne se linked hai. Source\nSikh kirpan carrying ko Article 25 protection mein include karta hai; social reform laws ki State power bhi\nsource framework ka part hai, lekin conversion by religious bodies ko unlimited right nahi bataya gaya.\n[Q85, Q86, Q87]\n● Source Article 25 explanation mein “Hindu” expression ke constitutional inclusion context mein Parsis ko\nincluded nahi maanta. Q89 source key “Humanism” ko Article 25 restriction ground nahi batata. [Q88,\nQ89]\n● Article 26 religious affairs manage karne ki freedom ko source Public Order, Morality aur Health\nrestrictions se subject batata hai. [Q90]\n12. Cultural & Educational Rights — Articles 29–30\n● Article 29 minority language/culture protection context se linked hai; minority educational institutions\nestablish/administer karne ka right Article 30 mein hai. Isliye Article 29 ko institution-establishment right\nse match karna source Q91 mein incorrect hai, aur Article 31 match bhi wrong hai. [Q91, Q92, Q93,\nQ94]\n● Source Assertion–Reason: Article 30 “minorities” term define nahi karta; Constitution religious aur\nlinguistic minorities recognise karta hai, lekin reason ko assertion ka correct explanation nahi maana\ngaya. [Q95, Q96]\n● National minority status ke source question mein educational institutions establish/administer karna aur\nPM 15-Point Programme benefit correct advantages bataye gaye; automatic Lok Sabha nomination\nnahi. [Q157]\n13. Article 32 — Constitutional Remedies & Writs\n● Fundamental Rights enforce karne ki power source Supreme Court aur High Courts/Judiciary se link\nkarta hai; Supreme Court ko guardian/protector of Fundamental Rights aur Constitution bataya gaya hai,\nPresident ko guardian kehna incorrect. [Q97, Q98, Q99, Q100, Q101, Q102]\n● Article 32 Fundamental Rights enforce karne ka remedy hai. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne Article 32/Right to\nConstitutional Remedies ko Constitution ka “Heart and Soul” kaha — source Assertion–Reason mein\neffective remedy is description ko explain karta hai. [Q103, Q104, Q105, Q106]\n● Article 32 ke under Supreme Court Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Quo Warranto aur Certiorari\nissue kar sakta hai; source Q107 Parliament ko law se other courts ko specified power confer karne ki\npossibility bhi correct maanta hai. [Q107, Q108]\n● Habeas Corpus personal liberty ka greatest safeguard aur liberty secure karne wala writ hai. Source writ\nmeanings match: Habeas Corpus = “let us have the body”; Mandamus = “we command”; Quo Warranto\n= “by what authority”; Certiorari = “to be more fully informed”; Prohibition subordinate court direction\ncontext. [Q109, Q110, Q111, Q112]\n● Source Q113 “Prohibition — To be certified” ko incorrect match batata hai. Certiorari ko “postmortem”\nremedy kaha gaya; Mandamus executive/person/institution ko public duty perform karne ka command\nhai. [Q113, Q114, Q115, Q116]\n14. Article Mapping — Match-the-Following"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n● Master map: Equality = Articles 14–18; Freedom = 19–22; Exploitation = 23–24; Religion = 25–28;\nCultural/Educational = 29–30; Constitutional Remedies = Article 32. Source matching Q117 isi map ko\ntest karta hai. [Q117]\n● Source Q118 matches Article 16(2) with public appointment non-discrimination, Article 29(2) with\nadmission non-discrimination, Article 30(1) with minority educational institutions, aur old Article 31(1)\nwith property deprivation wording. [Q118]\n● Protection against arrest/detention ko Article 23 se match karna wrong hai; source matching: Abolition of\nTitles = Article 18, Religious Affairs = Article 26, Minority Language = Article 29, Right to Education =\nArticle 21A. [Q119, Q120]\n● Source Q121 match: Fundamental Duties = 42nd Amendment; Parliament can amend Fundamental\nRights = Kesavananda Bharati; Doctrine of Basic Structure = Minerva Mills; trafficking prohibition =\nArticle 23. [Q121]\n15. FR vs DPSP — Amendment & Basic Structure Cases\n● Source Q122 ke statement set mein Part III ka U.S. Bill of Rights influence correct maana gaya; “Right to\nDie is a Fundamental Right”, “complete federal Constitution”, aur “Fundamental Rights can be removed”\nstatements incorrect key kiye gaye. [Q122]\n● State of Madras v. Champakam Dorairajan (1951) ko source FR vs DPSP conflict mein Fundamental\nRights prevalence se link karta hai. [Q123]\n● Source Q124 Parliament ko Fundamental Rights amend karne ka right Kesavananda Bharati case se link\nkarta hai. Case chronology: Shankari Prasad → Sajjan Singh → Golaknath → Kesavananda Bharati.\n[Q124, Q125]\n● Basic Structure Doctrine source ke mutabik Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala mein\npropounded/outlined hua. Another chronology: A.K. Gopalan → Golaknath → Kesavananda Bharati →\nMinerva Mills. [Q126, Q127, Q128]\n16. Right to Property — Article 300A\n● Right to Property originally Fundamental Right framework ka part tha, lekin 44th Constitutional\nAmendment Act, 1978 ke baad source ise Fundamental Right se remove karke Article 300A ke under\nLegal Right batata hai. [Q129, Q130, Q132, Q133, Q135]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Q131 — Multiple Correct Answers\n ▸Source ne Q131 ko “Multiple Correct Answers (C & D)” mark kiya hai: Statutory Right aur Legal Right dono\noptions accepted dikhaye gaye hain. [Q131]\n ▸Adjacent source questions repeatedly current position ko Legal Right / Article 300A batate hain. [Q129,\nQ130, Q132, Q133, Q135]\n● Article 301 trade, commerce and intercourse se linked hai — source Q134 ke mutabik property right nahi.\n44th Amendment ne Article 19(1)(f) omit aur Article 300A insert kiya; source amendment ko Janata\nParty Government period se link karta hai. [Q134]\n● 44th Amendment/1978 ko source repeatedly Right to Property ko Fundamental Rights list se\ndelete/abolish karne se link karta hai. [Q136, Q137, Q138, Q139, Q140, Q141]\n● Isliye current source questions mein Right to Property “not a Fundamental Right” answer hai. [Q142,\nQ143]\n17. What Is / Is Not a Fundamental Right\n● Source Q144 ke mutabik “Right to Protest” six Fundamental Rights mein separate listed right nahi. Q145\n“Right of Equal Shelter” ko Constitution-granted right ke roop mein reject karta hai. [Q144, Q145]\n● Right to Information Constitution mein expressly listed Fundamental Right nahi; source Supreme Court\ninterpretation ke through ise Article 19(1)(a) freedom of speech/expression mein locate karta hai. [Q146]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Rights Full Mind Map\n● Bijoe Emmanuel v. State of Kerala context mein source ke mutabik kisi ko National Anthem gaane ke liye\ncompel nahi kiya ja sakta; Article 19(1)(a), Article 25(1) aur no legal compulsion reasoning ko Q147\nsupport karta hai. [Q147]\n18. Citizens vs Foreigners — Who Gets Which Rights\n● Source Q148 citizen-only set mein Freedom of Speech/Expression aur Minority Right choose karta hai.\nQ149 explanation citizen-only Fundamental Rights ko Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, 30 se link karta hai, jabki\nmarked option 15, 16, 19, 30 hai. [Q148, Q149]\n● Foreign citizen ke liye Article 19 expression freedom available nahi — source Q150 ka answer. Article 14\nEqual Protection of Law “all persons” ke liye available bataya gaya hai. [Q150, Q151]\n● Source Q152 key discrimination protection, free movement aur election contest ko all-person rights nahi\nmaanta; Q153 Constitutional Remedies ko non-citizens ke liye bhi available right batata hai. [Q152,\nQ153]\n● British citizen in India source ke mutabik Article 19(1)(g) wala Freedom of Trade & Profession claim nahi\nkar sakta; same point three questions mein repeat hua hai. [Q154, Q155, Q156]\n19. Rights, Duties, Right to Service & Citizen Charter\n● Sir Ernest Barker quote source mein: “Rights without duties are like men without shadows.” Rights aur\nDuties ko correlative/two faces of same thing bataya gaya hai. [Q160, Q161]\n● Source Q162 rights ko citizens ke State ke against claims aur State power par restrictions/guarantee\nagainst State action ke roop mein explain karta hai. [Q162]\n● Right to Service concept source ke mutabik Great Britain se originate hua; time-bound public-service\ndelivery se linked hai. Source Madhya Pradesh ko 25 Sept 2010 first State aur Bihar ko 15 Aug 2011\nsecond State batata hai. [Q163]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Q164 — Source Answer/Explanation Tension\n ▸Q164 marked answer: “To create effective hearing system of public demands” = Citizen Charter ka aim\nNOT. [Q164]\n ▸Lekin source explanation ki last line isi item ko aim ke roop mein phrase karti hai; is internal inconsistency ko\nyahan silently reconcile nahi kiya gaya. [Q164]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0264","t":"15 Directive Principles of State Policy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Directive Principles of State Policy Full Mind Map\n📜 DIRECTIVE PRINCIPLES OF STATE POLICY\n— FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. DPSP — Purpose, Nature & Article 37\n2. Welfare State & Classification\n3. Source — Irish Constitution\n4. Article 39 — Socio-Economic Principles\n5. Article 40 — Village Panchayats\n6. Key Article Mapping — 39A to 51\n7. Right to Work, MGNREGA & Living Wage\n8. Article 43A — Workers in Management\n9. Article 44 — Uniform Civil Code\n10. Article 50–51 — Judiciary & International Peace\n11. 42nd Amendment Additions\n12. Gandhian Principles & Public Health\n13. Environment — Article 48A + Fundamental Duty\n14. Free Legal Aid — Article 39A & NALSA\n15. DPSP vs Fundamental Rights — Common Traps\n16. Quote, NSAP & Final Recall\n1. DPSP — Purpose, Nature & Article 37\n● Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) ka basic purpose social aur economic democracy establish\nkarna hai, jisse India welfare state ki direction mein grow kare. Religious State banana iska objective\nnahi hai; source secular-democratic State aur socio-economic justice ko aim batata hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● Fundamental Rights enforceable/justiciable hain, jabki DPSP non-justiciable hain — court se directly\nenforce nahi karwaye ja sakte. Source “non-justifiable” wording bhi use karta hai. [Q3, Q4, Q19]\n● DPSP Legislature aur Executive ko policy-direction dete hain, lekin unke functions par legal limitation\nimpose nahi karte. Ye instructions/guidelines hain, individual ke favour mein justiciable right create nahi\nkarte. [Q5]\n● Article 37 master rule: Part IV ke provisions court se enforceable nahi, phir bhi governance of the country\nmein fundamental hain; laws banate waqt in principles ko apply karna State ka duty hai. Legal\nduty/enforceable obligation nahi, moral-political guidance hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q20]\n2. Welfare State & Classification\n● Welfare State ka model/ideal Part IV — Directive Principles of State Policy mein milta hai. Source\nwelfare-state idea ko Preamble + DPSP dono se connect karta hai. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Constitution khud DPSP ko formal categories mein classify nahi karta; convenient study ke liye\ncontent/direction ke basis par Socialistic, Gandhian aur Liberal-Intellectual categories use ki jaati hain.\n[Q15]\n3. Source — Irish Constitution\n● Indian Constitution mein DPSP ka idea Irish Constitution se liya gaya hai. Same fact teen questions mein\nrepeat hua hai — Ireland yaad rakho. [Q16, Q17, Q18]\n4. Article 39 — Socio-Economic Principles"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Directive Principles of State Policy Full Mind Map\n● Article 39 mein adequate means of livelihood, material resources ka common good ke liye distribution,\nconcentration of wealth ko prevent karna, equal pay for equal work, workers/children ki health-strength\nprotection aur childhood/youth protection jaise socio-economic goals hain. Concentration of wealth\nDPSP ke against hai. [Q21]\n● “Equal Pay for Equal Work” Article 39(d) ka DPSP hai — men aur women dono ke liye. Source ise\nFundamental Right ki list mein directly nahi rakhta, though Randhir Singh v. Union of India (1982)\nexplanation mein Articles 14, 16, 39(d) + Preamble se principle derive hone ka note hai. [Q22, Q23,\nQ24]\n5. Article 40 — Village Panchayats\n● Panchayati Raj / village Panchayats ka constitutional direction DPSP Article 40 mein hai: State village\nPanchayats organise kare aur unhe self-government units ke roop mein function karne ke liye\npowers/authority de. [Q25, Q26, Q27, Q28]\n6. Key Article Mapping — 39A to 51\n● High-yield map: Article 39A = Equal Justice & Free Legal Aid; 40 = Village Panchayats; 41 = Right to\nWork/Education/Public Assistance; 44 = Uniform Civil Code; 48 = Agriculture & Animal Husbandry; 48A\n= Environment; 49 = Monuments; 50 = Judiciary–Executive separation; 51 = International Peace. [Q29,\nQ30, Q31, Q32, Q33]\n● Article 43B = Promotion of Co-operative Societies; Article 43A = workers’ participation in management of\nindustries. Dono ko confuse mat karo. [Q34]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Article Mapping Fast Check\n ▸Article 48 ko “Separation of Judiciary from Executive” se match karna wrong — correct Article 50 hai. [Q31]\n ▸Co-operative Societies = Article 43B, Workers in Management = Article 43A. [Q34]\n7. Right to Work, MGNREGA & Living Wage\n● MGNREGA source ke mutabik rural household ke adult member ko financial year mein at least 100 days\nunskilled manual work provide karne ka employment guarantee framework hai. “Right to employment\nPart III mein hai” reason false hai; source ise DPSP implementation direction se jodta hai. [Q35]\n● Source Q36 MGNREGA/MANREGA ko Article 43 ke constitutional goal — living wage, decent standard\nof life aur workers ke social-cultural opportunities — se link karta hai. Is source mapping ko exam-note\nke roop mein preserve karo. [Q36]\n8. Article 43A — Workers in Management\n● Article 43A workers ko industries ke management mein participate karane ki direction deta hai. Ye\nprovision 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976 se add hua. [Q37, Q38]\n9. Article 44 — Uniform Civil Code\n● Uniform Civil Code (UCC) Article 44 ka Directive Principle hai — State citizens ke liye throughout India\nUCC secure karne ka endeavour kare. [Q39, Q61]\n10. Article 50–51 — Judiciary & International Peace\n● Judiciary ko Executive se separate karna Article 50 ka DPSP hai. [Q40]\n● Article 51 International Peace & Security, just/honourable relations between nations, international\nlaw/treaty obligations ka respect aur arbitration se international disputes settlement ko promote karta\nhai; source ise Indian Foreign Policy se bhi directly link karta hai. [Q41, Q42, Q43, Q44]\n11. 42nd Amendment Additions"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Directive Principles of State Policy Full Mind Map\n● Source ke options mein 42nd Amendment additions: Article 39(f) children/youth protection wording,\nArticle 39A Equal Justice & Free Legal Aid, aur Article 43A Workers’ Participation. Uniform Civil Code\nArticle 44 pehle se tha — 42nd Amendment addition nahi. [Q45, Q46]\n12. Gandhian Principles & Public Health\n● Source Gandhian reflections mein Village Panchayats aur rural cottage industries ko identify karta hai;\nexplanation Article 40, 47 aur 48 ko Gandhian principles se link karti hai. [Q51]\n● Article 47 State ko nutrition level, standard of living aur public health improve karne ka duty deta hai, aur\nmedicinal purpose ko chhodkar intoxicating drinks/drugs ke consumption par prohibition ka endeavour\nkarta hai. [Q50, Q60, Q62]\n● Article 48 cow/calf and other milch-draught cattle protection + agriculture/animal husbandry organisation\nse linked hai. [Q48]\n13. Environment — Article 48A + Fundamental Duty\n● Environment/forests/wildlife protection Article 48A DPSP mein hai. Saath hi Article 51A(g) Fundamental\nDuty mein citizen ko natural environment protect/improve karne ka duty deta hai — isi liye environment\ndono jagah common theme hai. [Q52, Q53, Q54]\n14. Free Legal Aid — Article 39A & NALSA\n● Adult education DPSP mein expressly mentioned nahi; source living wage Article 43, free legal aid Article\n39A aur below-six early childhood care/education Article 45 ko expressly mentioned items batata hai.\n[Q55]\n● Equal Justice & Free Legal Aid — Article 39A — 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976 se insert hua\n(source effective date 3/1/1977 note karta hai). Economic/other disability ki wajah se justice deny na ho,\nye core idea hai. [Q56, Q57]\n● NALSA Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987 ke under constituted hai; weaker sections ko free &\ncompetent legal services aur Lok Adalats organise karna objective hai, aur State Legal Services\nAuthorities ko guidelines/financial support deta hai. [Q58]\n● Source Q59 ke specific options mein free legal service ke liye statement 1 + 2 correct mark hue: certain\nincome-threshold person aur Delhi-context transgender threshold; OBC ko automatic category aur all\nsenior citizens ko universal eligibility nahi maana gaya. [Q59]\n15. DPSP vs Fundamental Rights — Common Traps\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — FR aur DPSP ko Mix Mat Karo\n ▸Right against Exploitation source Q47 mein children, women aur tribals ke context se poocha gaya; “Dalit”\nword Constitution mein mentioned nahi bataya gaya. [Q47]\n ▸Free & compulsory education up to 14 years pehle Article 45 DPSP mein tha; 86th Amendment, 2002 ke\nbaad Article 21A Fundamental Right bana. Isliye current source question mein “free education up to 14”\nDPSP option nahi maana gaya. [Q48]\n ▸“Free education up to age 16” DPSP nahi. [Q49]\n ▸Trafficking/forced labour prohibition Article 23 Fundamental Right hai; intoxicating drinks prohibition Article\n47 DPSP. [Q50]\n ▸Right to Information DPSP nahi; source ise RTI Act 2005 ka legal right batata hai. [Q60]\n ▸Child factory/mine labour = Article 24 FR; begar/forced labour = Article 23 FR; untouchability abolition =\nArticle 17 FR. DPSP list mein in options se sirf liquor prohibition Article 47 hai. [Q62]\n ▸Abolition of Untouchability DPSP nahi — Article 17 Fundamental Right hai. [Q63]\n● Source Q66 final distinction: Equal Pay for Equal Work (Article 39(d)) aur UCC (Article 44) Part IV DPSP\nhain; “small family norm” listed DPSP nahi, aur primary-stage mother-tongue instruction Article 350A hai,\nPart IV DPSP nahi. [Q66]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Directive Principles of State Policy Full Mind Map\n16. Quote, NSAP & Final Recall\n● K.T. Shah ka quoted criticism: “Directive Principles of State Policy is a cheque which is paid on Bank’s\nconvenience.” [Q64]\n● National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP) 15 August 1995 ko launch hua aur source ise DPSP ke\nright to work, education aur public assistance provisions fulfil karne se link karta hai. Original\ncomponents mein NOAPS, NFBS aur NMBS ka note diya gaya hai. [Q65]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0265","t":"16 Fundamental Duties","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Duties Full Mind Map\n📜 FUNDAMENTAL DUTIES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Origin, Nature & 42nd Amendment\n2. Part IV-A & Article 51A\n3. Swaran Singh Committee — Key Members\n4. 10 to 11 Duties — 86th Amendment\n5. High-Yield Article 51A Clause Mapping\n6. What is NOT a Fundamental Duty?\n7. Combination Questions — Duties vs Non-Duties\n8. Article Matching — 17, 40, 49, 50 & 51\n9. Common Exam Traps\n10. Rapid Recall — One-Liners\n1. Origin, Nature & 42nd Amendment\n● Fundamental Duties ko Constitution mein Swaran Singh Committee ki recommendation par 42nd\nConstitutional Amendment Act, 1976 se add kiya gaya. Source mein ye fact multiple questions mein\nrepeat hai. [Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q7, Q9, Q10, Q14, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● Fundamental Duties non-justiciable hain: inke peeche legal sanction nahi, court mein directly enforce\nnahi kiye ja sakte aur writs se enforce nahi hote. Source Q1 mein legislative enforcement process aur\nlegal duties ke saath correlation — dono statements ko wrong maanta hai. [Q1, Q21]\n● 42nd Amendment ke through ek naya constitutional chapter Fundamental Duties par add hua; source\ninhe citizens ki moral obligations batata hai jo patriotism aur unity of India ko support karte hain. [Q20,\nQ21]\n2. Part IV-A & Article 51A\n● Fundamental Duties Part IV-A mein hain aur Article 51A mein enumerate kiye gaye hain. 42nd\nAmendment ne Article 51A insert karke Part IV-A create kiya. [Q8, Q11, Q12, Q15, Q16]\n● 42nd Amendment ke time add kiye gaye original “10 commandments” ko Fundamental Duties kaha gaya.\n[Q17]\n● Fundamental Duties Fundamental Rights ka part nahi hain. Part IV-A = Fundamental Duties, jabki source\nQ37 ke matching trap mein Part V ko Union Executive se relate karta hai. [Q32, Q37]\n● “To uphold and protect the Sovereignty, Unity and Integrity of India” Fundamental Duties ka provision hai\naur Article 51A(c) mein aata hai. [Q6, Q38]\n3. Swaran Singh Committee — Key Members\n● Source ke mutabik Swaran Singh Committee (1976) ke 12 members the: Swaran Singh (Chairman), A.R.\nAntulay, S.S. Ray, Rajni Patel, H.R. Gokhale, V.S. Sayed Muhammed, V.N. Gadgil, C.M. Stephen, D.P.\nSingh, Dinesh Goswami, Vasanth Sathe aur B.N. Banerjee. Haridev Joshi is list mein nahi the. [Q13]\n4. 10 to 11 Duties — 86th Amendment\n● Originally Fundamental Duties 10 the; present total 11 hai. Source ke mutabik 11th duty 86th\nAmendment Act, 2002 se add hui. [Q2, Q23, Q39]\n● Article 51A(k) parents/guardians ko 6–14 years ke children ko education ka opportunity provide karne ki\nduty se relate karta hai. [Q39]\n5. High-Yield Article 51A Clause Mapping"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Duties Full Mind Map\n● Article 51A(a): Constitution ka abide/respect karna, uske ideals & institutions, National Flag aur National\nAnthem ka respect karna. [Q24, Q30]\n● Article 51A(c): India ki sovereignty, unity aur integrity ko uphold aur protect karna — source ise third duty\nbhi batata hai. [Q6, Q38]\n● Article 51A(f): composite culture ki rich heritage ko value aur preserve karna. [Q25, Q28, Q29]\n● Article 51A(g): natural environment — forests, lakes, rivers, wildlife — ko protect/improve karna aur living\ncreatures ke prati compassion rakhna. [Q30, Q31, Q40]\n● Article 51A(h): scientific temper, humanism aur spirit of inquiry/reform develop karna; source Q40 mein\n“spirit of inquiry and reform” ko 51A(h) se match karta hai. [Q29, Q36, Q40]\n● Article 51A(i): public property safeguard karna aur violence ko abjure karna. [Q27, Q28, Q36]\n● Source ke combination question mein “strive towards excellence in all spheres of individual and collective\nactivity” ko bhi Fundamental Duty maana gaya hai. [Q29]\n6. What is NOT a Fundamental Duty?\n● General/public elections mein vote karna Fundamental Duty nahi hai. [Q22, Q36]\n● Untouchability abolish karne ki direction Fundamental Duty nahi; source ise Article 17, Part III ke\nFundamental Rights se relate karta hai. [Q26]\n● Village Panchayats organise karne mein help karna Fundamental Duty nahi; source ise DPSP Article 40\nse relate karta hai. [Q27]\n● Monuments aur places of public/national importance ko protect karna Article 51A ki Fundamental Duty\nnahi; source Q34 ise DPSP Article 49 se relate karta hai. [Q33, Q34]\n● Parents aur teachers ka respect karna source ke according 11 Fundamental Duties mein listed nahi hai.\n[Q35]\n7. Combination Questions — Duties vs Non-Duties\n● Q28 ka correct combination: defend the country + preserve rich heritage of composite culture +\nsafeguard public property. “Pay income tax” ko source Fundamental Duty nahi maanta. [Q28]\n● Q29 ka correct combination: preserve composite culture + develop scientific temper/spirit of inquiry +\nstrive towards excellence. “Protect weaker sections from social injustice” Fundamental Duty list ka part\nnahi. [Q29]\n8. Article Matching — 17, 40, 49, 50 & 51\n● Source Q40 mapping: foster respect for international law → Article 51(c); compassion for living creatures\n→ Article 51A(g); spirit of inquiry and reform → Article 51A(h); judiciary–executive separation in State\npublic services → Article 50. [Q40]\n● Fast contrast: Untouchability → Article 17; Village Panchayats → Article 40; Monuments → Article 49. Ye\nFundamental Duties ke look-alike distractors hain. [Q26, Q27, Q34]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Part / Article / Duty Confusion\n ▸Part IV-A ko Fundamental Rights ke saath confuse mat karo: source ke mutabik Fundamental Duties Part\nIV-A, Article 51A mein hain. [Q8, Q11, Q12, Q15, Q16, Q32]\n ▸“Vote in election”, “pay income tax”, “organise Panchayats”, “abolish untouchability”, “protect monuments” —\nsource ke questions mein Fundamental Duties nahi hain. [Q22, Q26, Q27, Q28, Q33, Q34, Q36]\n ▸42nd Amendment = original 10 duties; present total 11, aur source 11th duty ko 86th Amendment Act, 2002\nse link karta hai. [Q14, Q18, Q19, Q23, Q39]\n10. Rapid Recall — One-Liners\n● Recommendation? → Swaran Singh Committee. [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n● Added by? → 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976. [Q5, Q7, Q9, Q10, Q14, Q18, Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fundamental Duties Full Mind Map\n● Part & Article? → Part IV-A, Article 51A. [Q8, Q11, Q12, Q15, Q16]\n● Present number? → 11; originally 10. [Q23, Q39]\n● Sovereignty–Unity–Integrity? → 51A(c), third duty. [Q6, Q38]\n● Environment / wildlife? → 51A(g). [Q30, Q31]\n● Rich composite culture? → 51A(f). [Q25]\n● Writs se enforce? → No. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0266","t":"17 The President","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The President Full Mind Map\n THE PRESIDENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Constitutional Position & Executive Power\n2. Election Method & Electoral College\n3. Vote Value, Nomination & Election Rules\n4. Qualifications, Term & Re-election\n5. Election Disputes — Article 71\n6. Impeachment — Article 61\n7. Vacancy, Acting President & Immunity\n8. Parliament — Dissolution, Joint Sitting & Assent\n9. Veto Powers — Article 111\n10. Ordinance & Discretionary Powers\n11. Appointments, Advisory & Other Functions\n12. Pardoning Power — Article 72\n13. Presidents — Firsts, Tenures & Profiles\n14. Rashtrapati Bhavan\n15. Common Exam Traps & Rapid Recall\n1. Constitutional Position & Executive Power\n● Article 52 kehta hai ki India ka ek President hoga. Article 53(1) ke under Union ki executive power\nPresident mein vested hai aur woh ise directly ya subordinate officers ke through Constitution ke\naccording exercise karta hai. President Head of the Republic/State aur constitutional executive head hai.\n[Q1, Q2, Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11, Q12]\n● Article 53(2): Defence Forces ki supreme command President mein vested hai, lekin Commander-in-\nChief power legislative control/law se regulated hai; independent unlimited power nahi. [Q13]\n● Source comparison: Indian President British King se different hai (President indirectly elected, King\nhereditary), aur US President ke office jaisa nahi; US President ke paas zyada real executive power hoti\nhai. [Q3]\n● “He represents the nation but does not lead the nation” President par apply hota hai. Source President ko\nformal/de jure, constitutional aur nominal authority batata hai; real executive leadership Prime Minister +\nCouncil of Ministers ke paas hai. [Q14, Q107]\n● President ka Parliament address Union Cabinet prepare karti hai, kyunki source ke mutabik real\nexecutive power Cabinet mein hoti hai. [Q111]\n2. Election Method & Electoral College\n● President ka election indirect hota hai: proportional representation by means of Single Transferable Vote\n(STV) + secret ballot. Article 54 electoral college batata hai; Article 55 manner/value principles ko\ngovern karta hai. [Q15, Q16, Q17, Q25, Q26, Q48]\n● Electoral College = elected members of Lok Sabha + Rajya Sabha + elected members of State\nLegislative Assemblies + elected MLAs of Delhi and Puducherry (70th Constitutional Amendment Act,\n1992). [Q18, Q19, Q20, Q23, Q24, Q25, Q33]\n● Nominated MPs/MLAs, State Legislative Council ke elected/nominated members, Governors aur Lt.\nGovernors Electoral College ka part nahi. Agar Chief Minister Legislative Council ka member ho, to\nPresidential election mein vote nahi de sakta. [Q21, Q22, Q24, Q33, Q34]\n● Electoral college incomplete hone ke ground par Presidential election postpone nahi kiya ja sakta;\ndissolved Legislative Assembly election mein participate nahi karti. [Q27]\n3. Vote Value, Nomination & Election Rules"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The President Full Mind Map\n● Nomination ke liye minimum 50 electors proposers aur 50 electors seconders chahiye. [Q28, Q48]\n● Article 55 ka goal States ke beech representation ki uniformity aur States as a whole vs Union mein\nparity hai. MLA vote value population aur elected MLAs ke ratio se nikalta hai; State-to-State vary karta\nhai. [Q29, Q30, Q31, Q33]\n● MP vote value = sab elected State MLAs ke total vote value ÷ elected MPs of both Houses. Lok Sabha\naur Rajya Sabha ke elected MPs ka vote value same hota hai. [Q29, Q30]\n● 2022 Presidential Election mein Rajasthan ke har MLA ka vote value source ke calculation ke mutabik\n129 tha. Source isi explanation mein Droupadi Murmu ki 2022 victory aur Yashwant Sinha ko opposition\ncandidate bhi note karta hai. [Q32]\n● Population base ke liye source Article 55 explanation/Article 81(3) ko cite karke 1971 Census figures use\nkarta hai, jab tak 2026 ke baad first census ke relevant figures publish na ho jayein. [Q35]\n4. Qualifications, Term & Re-election\n● Article 58(1) qualifications: citizen of India, minimum 35 years, aur Lok Sabha member ke election ke liye\nqualified. Citizenship “by birth” aur educational qualification essential nahi. [Q36, Q37]\n● Article 59(1): sitting MP/State Legislature member President elect ho sakta hai, lekin office enter karte hi\nuski legislative seat deemed vacant ho jati hai. [Q38]\n● Article 57: jo person President hai/reh chuka hai, other constitutional conditions ke subject mein re-\nelection ke liye eligible hai; source isse any number of times re-election ke roop mein explain karta hai.\n[Q39, Q40]\n● Article 56(1): term 5 years from the date President enters office. Resignation Vice-President ko address\nhota hai; Vice-President use Lok Sabha Speaker ko immediately communicate karta hai. [Q43, Q44, Q45]\n5. Election Disputes — Article 71\n● Article 71: Presidential/Vice-Presidential election ke doubts/disputes Supreme Court decide karta hai aur\ndecision final hota hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● Agar Supreme Court election void declare kare, decision se pehle President ke official acts automatically\ninvalid nahi hote. Electoral College mein vacancy bhi election ko challenge/postpone karne ka ground\nnahi. [Q42]\n● Source historical note: V.V. Giri incumbent President ke roop mein Supreme Court mein personally\nappear hue election challenge mein; petition dismiss hui aur election uphold hua. [Q131]\n6. Impeachment — Article 61\n● President ko term se pehle sirf impeachment ke through “violation of the Constitution” ke ground par\nremove kiya ja sakta hai. Procedure Article 61 mein hai; charge Parliament ke either House se initiate ho\nsakta hai. [Q46, Q47, Q49, Q50, Q51, Q52, Q53, Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● Initiating House mein at least 14 days prior written notice, total members ke not less than 1/4 signatures,\naur resolution ko not less than 2/3 of total membership se pass hona hota hai. Other House charge\ninvestigate karta hai; President ko appear/represent hone ka right hai. [Q53, Q54, Q58]\n● State Legislative Assembly ke elected members President ko elect karte hain, lekin impeachment forum\nka part nahi. Legislative Councils na Electoral College ka part hain, na impeachment ka. Source\nimpeachment ko quasi-judicial procedure batata hai. [Q59, Q60, Q61]\n7. Vacancy, Acting President & Immunity\n● Article 62(2): death, resignation, removal ya otherwise vacancy aaye to President ka election vacancy ki\ndate se 6 months ke andar complete hona chahiye. [Q62, Q63, Q64]\n● Article 65(1): vacancy mein Vice-President acting President banta hai until new President enters office;\nsource practical ceiling 6 months batata hai because vacancy ko 6 months se zyada open nahi rehna\nchahiye. [Q65, Q66]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The President Full Mind Map\n● President aur Vice-President dono offices vacant hon to President (Discharge of Functions) Act, 1969 ke\nunder Chief Justice of India functions discharge karta hai; CJI absent ho to senior-most Supreme Court\njudge. [Q67, Q68, Q69, Q70]\n● Former CJI M. Hidayatullah ne 20 July 1969 se 24 August 1969 tak Acting President ke roop mein serve\nkiya tha. [Q126]\n● Article 361 source point: term ke dauran criminal proceedings institute/continue nahi ki ja sakti; civil\nproceedings written notice ke 2 months baad possible hain. Isi wajah se Q71 ka blanket “no litigation”\nassertion disputed hai. [Q71]\n8. Parliament — Dissolution, Joint Sitting & Assent\n● Article 85: President Houses ko summon/prorogue kar sakta hai aur Lok Sabha dissolve kar sakta hai;\nsource dissolution/prorogation ko generally Council of Ministers ki advice ke according explain karta hai.\n[Q72, Q73, Q74]\n● Article 108: deadlock conditions mein President joint sitting summon karta hai; source Article 118(4) ke\nunder Lok Sabha Speaker ko presiding authority batata hai. Rejection, final disagreement on\namendments, ya 6 months lapse typical triggers hain. [Q75, Q76, Q77, Q78, Q79]\n● Article 79: President Parliament ka constituent part hai; parliamentary discussion mein participate nahi\nkarta. Bill Parliament se pass hone ke baad Article 111 ke under President ke assent se Act banta hai.\n[Q80, Q81, Q82]\n9. Veto Powers — Article 111\n● Source veto examples: Dr. Rajendra Prasad ne PEPSU Appropriation Bill, 1954 par absolute veto use\nkiya; Gyani Zail Singh ne Indian Post Office (Amendment) Bill, 1986 par pocket veto exercise kiya. [Q83,\nQ84]\n● Article 111 ke under President Bill ko assent de sakta hai ya assent withhold kar sakta hai; non-Money\nBill ko objections ke saath reconsideration ke liye return karne ka source bhi discuss karta hai. [Q85, Q86,\nQ87, Q88]\n● Money/Finance Bill ko President reconsideration ke liye return nahi kar sakta; Finance Bill introduction\nbhi Presidential recommendation se linked hai. [Q109]\n10. Ordinance & Discretionary Powers\n● Article 123: jab dono Houses simultaneously session mein na hon aur immediate action necessary ho,\nPresident Ordinance promulgate kar sakta hai. Ordinance ka force Act of Parliament jaisa hota hai. [Q89,\nQ91, Q92, Q93]\n● Ordinance Parliament ke reassembly ke baad 6 weeks expire hone par cease karta hai unless approved;\nPresident ise earlier withdraw bhi kar sakta hai. [Q92, Q94]\n● Source discretionary-power framing: Bill ko objections ke saath return karna, Bill ko detain/withhold\nkarna, Prime Minister se information mangna aur Council of Ministers ki advice ko reconsideration ke\nliye kehna. [Q87, Q90]\n11. Appointments, Advisory & Other Functions\n● President appoints Finance Commission Chairman (Art. 280), UT Chief Minister in the cited Art. 239AA\ncontext, Attorney General (Art. 76), CAG (Art. 148) aur State Governor (Art. 155). Source notes Planning\nCommission Vice-Chairman PM appoint karta tha. [Q95, Q96]\n● Vice-President President appoint nahi karta — Article 66 ke manner se elected hota hai. State Chief\nMinister ko Governor appoint karta hai, President nahi. [Q97, Q99]\n● Article 160: Governor ke duties discharge karne ke extraordinary contingency mein President suitable\nprovision kar sakta hai. [Q98]\n● Article 143: President Supreme Court se question of law/fact par advice consult kar sakta hai, lekin\nsource ke mutabik us advice ko accept karna binding nahi. [Q100, Q101]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The President Full Mind Map\n● Article 86(2) ke source wording mein Parliament ko message bhejna President ka “right” hai, literally\n“power” nahi. [Q102]\n● President Supreme Court judge ko apni discretion se remove nahi kar sakta; source Article 124(4) ka\nspecial parliamentary-address procedure cite karta hai. [Q103]\n● President Parliament ke saamne Union Finance Commission recommendations, CAG report aur National\nCommission for Scheduled Castes report laid karwata hai; PAC report Speaker ko submit hoti hai. [Q108]\n● Fifth Schedule ke under Scheduled Area declare/alter karne ki constitutional power President ke paas\nhai, source specified conditions ke saath. [Q110]\n12. Pardoning Power — Article 72\n● Article 72 President ki judicial/pardoning power: pardon, reprieve, respite, remission; sentence ko\nsuspend, remit ya commute kar sakta hai. [Q104, Q105, Q106]\n● Source scope: Union law offences, Court Martial sentences aur death sentence cases. “Detention” aur\n“Continuation” pardoning power ke components nahi. [Q105, Q106]\n13. Presidents — Firsts, Tenures & Profiles\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad: first President of independent India, Bihar se; source unke periods 1950–52, 1952–\n57 aur 1957–62 list karta hai aur successive terms question ka answer unhi ko deta hai. [Q112, Q113,\nQ114]\n● V.V. Giri: source ke mutabik 4th President (1969–1974), tenure-order framing mein 6th; Trade Union\nMovement se associated aur AITUC ke chairman do terms rahe. [Q115, Q124]\n● Neelam Sanjiva Reddy: 1977–1982, source ke according only unopposed/unanimously elected\nPresident; President banne se pehle Vice-President nahi rahe aur do terms Lok Sabha Speaker rahe.\n[Q116, Q117, Q119, Q120, Q121, Q122]\n● Term match: Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed 1974–1977 | Neelam Sanjiva Reddy 1977–1982 | Dr. Zakir Husain\n1967–1969 | V.V. Giri 1969–1974. [Q118]\n● Dr. S. Radhakrishnan (1962–1967) ko source “Philosopher King/Philosopher Ruler” ke naam se identify\nkarta hai. [Q123]\n● Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam (2002–2007) ko “Missile Man” kaha gaya; source unhe 11th Indian President (as\nan individual) batata hai. [Q125]\n● Odd-one source question mein Jawaharlal Nehru Prime Minister the, jabki remaining listed persons\nPresidents the. [Q127]\n● Pratibha Patil: source ke mutabik 12th President, first woman President; tenure-order ke hisab se 14th.\n[Q128]\n● Source Q129: Meira Kumar ko 15th Presidential election mein UPA candidate batata hai; explanation\n16th election mein Droupadi Murmu (NDA) vs Yashwant Sinha (opposition-supported) bhi note karta hai.\n[Q129]\n● Dr. Zakir Husain Bihar ke Governor (1957–1962), phir Vice-President aur President rahe. [Q130]\n14. Rashtrapati Bhavan\n● Rashtrapati Bhavan President ka official residence hai; British architect Edwin Lutyens ne design kiya.\nSource: 1947 tak Viceroy House, 15 Aug 1947 ko “Government House” naam, aur C. Rajagopalachari\n21 June 1948 ko wahan rehne wale first Indian. [Q132]\n15. Common Exam Traps & Rapid Recall"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The President Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — Source-specific Disputed / Confusing Points\n⚠\n ▸Q17 source mein “Multiple Correct Answers (B & C)” marked hai — Presidential election ko indirect +\nelectoral-college based framing se samjho. [Q17]\n ▸Q22 aur Q26 source mein “Disputed Question” marked hain; core rule wahi hai: elected MPs of both Houses\n+ elected State MLAs + Delhi/Puducherry elected MLAs. [Q22, Q26]\n ▸Q28 bhi disputed marked hai, lekin source explanation clearly 50 proposers + 50 seconders deta hai. [Q28]\n ▸Q71 disputed hai: Article 361 criminal immunity absolute during term hai, but civil proceeding 2 months\nwritten notice ke baad possible batayi gayi hai. [Q71]\n ▸Election vs impeachment: State MLAs Electoral College mein hain but impeachment process mein nahi;\nMLCs Electoral College mein bhi nahi. [Q59, Q60]\n ▸Money/Finance Bill ko reconsideration ke liye return nahi kiya ja sakta — ordinary Bill ke\nveto/reconsideration rule se confuse mat karo. [Q109]\nRapid Recall — One-Liners\n● Executive power? → Article 53 → President. [Q1–Q13]\n● Election? → Indirect, PR-STV, secret ballot. [Q15–Q17]\n● Eligibility? → Citizen + 35 years + Lok Sabha qualification. [Q36, Q37]\n● Term? → 5 years; resignation to Vice-President. [Q43–Q45]\n● Impeachment? → Article 61; violation of Constitution; either House. [Q46–Q61]\n● Vacancy? → Fill within 6 months; VP acts President. [Q62–Q66]\n● Joint sitting? → President summons, Article 108. [Q75–Q79]\n● Assent/veto? → Article 111. [Q81–Q88]\n● Ordinance? → Article 123; 6 weeks after reassembly. [Q89, Q91–Q94]\n● Pardon? → Article 72. [Q104–Q106]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0267","t":"18 The Vice-President","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Vice-President Full Mind Map\n THE VICE-PRESIDENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Election & Electoral College — Article 66\n2. Eligibility & Constitutional Position\n3. Rajya Sabha — Ex-Officio Chairman\n4. Election Dispute — Article 71\n5. Acting as President — Articles 64–65\n6. Removal — Article 67(b)\n7. Vice-Presidents — Firsts, Careers & Sequence\n8. Exam Traps & Rapid Recall\n1. Election & Electoral College — Article 66\n● Article 66(1) ke mutabik Vice-President ka election Parliament ke dono Houses ke members se bane\nElectoral College ke through hota hai. System = Proportional Representation by means of Single\nTransferable Vote (STV). [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Electoral College mein Lok Sabha + Rajya Sabha ke members aate hain; State Legislative Assemblies\naur Legislative Councils ke members Vice-Presidential election mein vote nahi karte. President ke\nelection se yahi major difference source highlight karta hai. [Q4, Q6]\n● 16th Vice-Presidential Election, 2022 ke source figures: Rajya Sabha 233 elected + 12 nominated, Lok\nSabha 543 elected = total 788 electors. [Q5]\n● Election indirect hai; source Q6 ke according President aur Vice-President dono ke election mein PR-\nSTV aur secret ballot use hota hai, lekin State Legislatures Vice-President ke Electoral College ka part\nnahi. [Q6]\n2. Eligibility & Constitutional Position\n● Article 66(3) source conditions: candidate Indian citizen ho, 35 years complete kar chuka ho aur Council\nof States (Rajya Sabha) ke member ke roop mein election ke liye qualified ho. [Q7, Q12]\n● Q7 Assertion–Reason mein source dono statements ko true aur Reason ko acceptable explanation\nmaanta hai: Rajya Sabha qualification + Vice-President ka Rajya Sabha chairperson hona. [Q7]\n● Vice-President President dwara appoint nahi hota; Article 66 ke election mechanism se elected hota hai.\nSource Q11 mein “appointed by President” statement incorrect marked hai. [Q11]\n● Q12 ke source framing mein statements 1 and 4 wrong hain: Lok Sabha qualification nahi, Rajya Sabha\nqualification chahiye; removal formal impeachment se nahi hota. State Legislature member candidate ho\nsakta hai aur term President ke term ke same batayi gayi hai. [Q12]\n3. Rajya Sabha — Ex-Officio Chairman\n● Article 64: Vice-President Council of States (Rajya Sabha) ka ex-officio Chairman hota hai. Source\nrepeatedly isi ko direct fact ke roop mein test karta hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10]\n● Vice-President Rajya Sabha ko preside karta hai, lekin Upper House ka member nahi hota — isliye\n“presided over by one who is not its member” ka answer Rajya Sabha hai. [Q9, Q18]\n● Article 64 source point: Vice-President koi other office of profit hold nahi karega. [Q7]\n4. Election Dispute — Article 71\n● Article 71(2): agar Supreme Court Vice-President ka election void declare kare, to Supreme Court\ndecision ki date par ya usse pehle office powers/duties mein kiye gaye acts us declaration ki wajah se\ninvalid nahi hote. [Q13]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Vice-President Full Mind Map\n● Isliye Q13 mein statement (1) correct aur statement (2) incorrect marked hai; source answer = only\nstatement (1). [Q13]\n5. Acting as President — Articles 64–65\n● Article 63 source base: India ka ek Vice-President hoga. Source Q14 Vice-President ko President ke\nbaad second-highest Constitutional Office/dignitary batata hai. [Q14]\n● President ke office mein death, resignation, impeachment/removal ya other casual vacancy aaye to Vice-\nPresident President ke roop mein act karta hai; President ki absence mein bhi functions discharge karta\nhai. [Q14]\n● Jab Vice-President President ke duties discharge kar raha ho, Article 64 ke source explanation ke\nmutabik woh Rajya Sabha Chairman ke duties perform nahi karega; Article 65(3) ke under President ke\nemoluments mileinge. [Q15]\n● President (Discharge of Functions) Act, 1969 ke source point ke mutabik, aisi duration mein Vice-\nPresident resign kare to Chief Justice of India President ke duties perform karega. [Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Vice-President Full Mind Map\n6. Removal — Article 67(b)\n● Article 67(b): Vice-President ko Rajya Sabha resolution se remove kiya ja sakta hai — Council ke “all the\nthen members” ke majority se pass ho aur Lok Sabha usse agree kare. [Q16, Q17]\n● Removal resolution sirf Rajya Sabha mein propose/initiate hota hai; intention to move resolution ke liye at\nleast 14 days prior notice chahiye. [Q16, Q17]\n● Source Q12 clearly formal impeachment ko Vice-President removal ka method nahi maanta. [Q12]\n7. Vice-Presidents — Firsts, Careers & Sequence\n● Diplomatic-background pair source answer: Dr. S. Radhakrishnan (Ambassador to USSR, 1949–1952) +\nV.V. Giri (High Commissioner to Sri Lanka, 1947–1951). Source K.R. Narayanan ko China ambassador\n(1976–1978) bhi note karta hai. [Q19]\n● Listed persons mein Vice-President office hold karne wale source answer = Mohammad Hidayatullah\n(6th VP, 1979–84) aur Shankar Dayal Sharma (1987–92). Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed aur Neelam Sanjiva\nReddy ko source Presidents ke roop mein distinguishes karta hai. [Q20]\n● First Vice-President = Dr. S. Radhakrishnan (1952–1962). Dr. Zakir Hussain second Vice-President the\n(13 May 1962–12 May 1967). Isliye “Zakir Hussain first VP” statement incorrect hai. [Q21]\n● Mohammad Hamid Ansari = 12th Vice-President; 2007 mein office enter kiya aur July 2012 mein re-\nelected hue. [Q22]\n● Source HTML ki listed sequence: Radhakrishnan → Zakir Hussain → V.V. Giri → G.S. Pathak → B.D.\nJatti → M. Hidayatullah → R. Venkataraman → Shankar Dayal Sharma → K.R. Narayanan → Krishna\nKant → Bhairon Singh Shekhawat → M. Hamid Ansari → M. Venkaiah Naidu → Jagdeep Dhankhar.\nSource Q22 is list ko “2022–Incumbent” wording tak print karta hai. [Q22]\n8. Exam Traps & Rapid Recall\n EXAM TRAPS — Vice-President\n⚠\n ▸VP election ≠ President election Electoral College: State MLAs President ke election mein aate hain, Vice-\nPresident ke election mein nahi. [Q4, Q6]\n ▸All MPs vs only elected MPs: source Article 66 framing “members of both Houses”; 2022 example mein\nRajya Sabha ke nominated members bhi Electoral College mein included hain. [Q1, Q5]\n ▸Qualification = Rajya Sabha membership ke liye qualified, Lok Sabha nahi. [Q7, Q12]\n ▸Rajya Sabha Chairman hote hue bhi Vice-President Rajya Sabha ka member nahi. [Q9, Q18]\n ▸Removal = Rajya Sabha-origin resolution + Lok Sabha agreement + 14-day notice; formal impeachment\nnahi. [Q12, Q16, Q17]\n ▸Acting President period mein Rajya Sabha Chairman duties nahi; President ke emoluments milte hain. [Q15]\nRapid Recall — One-Liners\n● Election? → Article 66 → both Houses of Parliament → PR-STV. [Q1–Q6]\n● Eligibility? → Citizen + 35 years + Rajya Sabha qualification. [Q7, Q12]\n● Rajya Sabha? → VP = ex-officio Chairman, but not a member. [Q8–Q10, Q18]\n● Election void? → Article 71(2); past acts up to decision date remain valid. [Q13]\n● Acts as President? → casual vacancy/absence; Chairman duties stop during that period. [Q14, Q15]\n● Removal? → Article 67(b), Rajya Sabha initiates, Lok Sabha agrees, 14-day notice. [Q16, Q17]\n● First VP? → Dr. S. Radhakrishnan. 12th VP? → M. Hamid Ansari. [Q21, Q22]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0268","t":"19 The Council of Ministers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n THE COUNCIL OF MINISTERS — FULL MIND\n🏛️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Union Executive — PM, President & Key Articles\n2. Council of Ministers vs Cabinet — Structure & Size\n3. Prime Minister — Appointment, Membership & Eligibility\n4. Collective Responsibility — Article 75(3)\n5. Confidence / No-Confidence & Resignation\n6. First Cabinet of Independent India\n7. Prime Ministers — Tenure, Background & Important Facts\n8. Finance, Economic Policy & Manmohan Singh\n9. Policy–Implementation & Deputy Prime Minister\n10. Cabinet Secretariat, Committees & Ministries\n11. Institutions, Administrative Personalities & Official Documents\n12. Recent / Misc. Ministry Facts, Memorials & Slogans\n13. Exam Traps — Source Conflicts & Disputed Questions\n1. Union Executive — PM, President & Key Articles\n● Article 300 ke source point ke mutabik Government of India ka legal name 'The Union of India' hai. [Q1]\n● Union ki executive power Article 53(1) ke under President mein vested hai; Prime Minister real/head of\nGovernment role mein Council of Ministers ko lead karta hai. [Q2, Q3, Q5, Q14, Q68]\n● Prime Minister ko President appoint karta hai; other Ministers ko President, Prime Minister ki advice par\nappoint karta hai - source Article 75(1) ko repeatedly test karta hai. [Q4, Q17, Q21, Q22]\n● Article 78 PM ki President ke prati information duties batata hai - Union administration aur\nlegislation/Council decisions communicate karna, aur President kahe to individual minister ka matter\nCouncil ke saamne rakhna. [Q6, Q35]\n● Article 77(1): executive action President ke naam se expressed hota hai; Article 77(3): President\nbusiness transaction aur ministers ke beech allocation ke rules banata hai. [Q15]\n● Ministries/Departments ki creation source ke mutabik President business-allocation framework mein\nkarta hai; individual Ministries ko Ministers ko assign karna President, PM ki advice par karta hai. [Q13]\n2. Council of Ministers vs Cabinet — Structure & Size\n● Constitution Council of Ministers ko constitutional body banata hai, lekin ministers ko Cabinet Minister /\nMoS (Independent Charge) / MoS / Deputy Minister ranks mein classify nahi karta; source ise British\nparliamentary tradition based practice batata hai. [Q7]\n● 91st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2003 se Article 75(1A): PM including total Union Ministers Lok\nSabha strength ke 15% se exceed nahi kar sakte. Similar state cap Article 164(1A) mein source explain\nkarta hai. [Q7, Q8, Q71, Q72]\n● Cabinet = Council of Ministers ka senior inner executive body; source Q9-Q10 ke according Cabinet\nmein PM + Cabinet-rank Ministers aate hain, poora Council nahi. [Q9, Q10]\n● 'Cabinet' word ka constitutional reference Article 352(3) mein hai - Emergency proclamation ke liye Union\nCabinet ki written communication ka source point. [Q11]\n3. Prime Minister — Appointment, Membership & Eligibility"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n● Prime Minister generally Lok Sabha member hota hai, lekin Rajya Sabha member bhi ho sakta hai.\nUpper House member PM Lok Sabha mein speak kar sakta hai, vote nahi; no-confidence situation mein\napne favour mein Lok Sabha vote nahi kar sakta. [Q16, Q18]\n● Appointment ke time PM ka Parliament ke kisi House ka member hona compulsory nahi; Article 75(5) ke\nsource rule ke hisab se 6 months ke andar either House ki membership leni hoti hai. [Q2, Q19, Q23, Q24,\nQ25, Q26]\n● Source minimum age ko Lok Sabha qualification ke equal 25 years batata hai. [Q20]\n● PM ko Cabinet colleagues choose karne mein full discretion source Article 75(1) framing mein diya gaya\nhai; outside-Parliament person ko bhi choose kar sakta hai, subject to 6-month rule. [Q22]\n4. Collective Responsibility — Article 75(3)\n● Article 75(3): Council of Ministers, PM सहित, collectively responsible ONLY to Lok Sabha / House of the\nPeople - Parliament as a whole ya Rajya Sabha ko nahi. [Q27, Q28, Q31, Q32, Q34, Q35]\n● Article 75(2): Ministers office President ke pleasure par hold karte hain, Prime Minister ke pleasure par\nnahi - source statement questions isi distinction ko test karte hain. [Q17, Q33, Q35]\n● Both Houses ke members Union Minister ban sakte hain, lekin collective responsibility phir bhi Lok\nSabha ko hi hai. [Q34]\n● Lower House majority lose hone par PM ka resign karna source ke mutabik explicit constitutional\nsentence nahi, parliamentary convention hai; executive Legislature ke prati subordinate/accountable hai.\n[Q36, Q37]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n5. Confidence / No-Confidence & Resignation\n● Government confidence prove karne ke liye Confidence Motion move kar sakti hai; No-Confidence\nMotion opposition/member side se Lok Sabha mein aata hai. [Q38]\n● Lok Sabha mein No-Confidence Motion pass hone par poori Council of Ministers ko resign karna hota hai\nbecause collective responsibility Lok Sabha ko hai. [Q39]\n● No-Confidence Motion Constitution mein expressly mentioned nahi; source Rule 198 of Lok Sabha Rules\nko procedure ka base batata hai aur motion sirf Lok Sabha mein introduce hota hai. [Q43, Q44]\n● Source Q41-Q42 ke mutabik motion admit/table karne ke liye minimum 50 Lok Sabha members ka\nsupport chahiye. [Q41, Q42]\n● Resigned minister House mein resignation statement Speaker ki permission se de sakta hai; statement\ndena optional hai. [Q40]\n● Council resign kare to President Rule automatically impose nahi hota; outgoing Council ko alternative\narrangement tak continue karne ko kaha ja sakta hai aur early general election/new government\narrangement source options mein given hai. [Q45]\n6. First Cabinet of Independent India\n● Kailash Nath Katju source chronology: 1951 mein Law Minister, same year third Home Minister, later\n1955 mein Defence Minister; Madhya Pradesh CM 1957-62. [Q46]\n● Independent India ke first Finance Minister source explanation mein R.K. Shanmukham Chetty (1947-48)\ndiye gaye hain; question ke options mein naam missing tha. [Q47]\n● First post-Independence Cabinet ke Law Minister = Dr. B.R. Ambedkar; source interim-government\ndistinction mein Jogendra Nath Mandal ko 1946 Law Minister batata hai. [Q48]\n● Interim Govt 1946 vs First Cabinet 1947: Rajendra Prasad-Food & Agriculture, Jagjivan Ram-Labour,\nBaldev Singh-Defence same; C.H. Bhabha ka portfolio Works/Mines/Power se Commerce ho gaya. [Q49]\n7. Prime Ministers — Tenure, Background & Important Facts\n● Source counting (acting PM Gulzari Lal Nanda ko include karke) H.D. Deve Gowda ko 12th Prime\nMinister aur Narendra Modi ko 15th Prime Minister batata hai. [Q50]\n● Tenure match: V.P. Singh 1989-90; Chandra Shekhar 1990-91; H.D. Deve Gowda 1996-97; I.K. Gujral\n1997-98; A.B. Vajpayee 1999-2004 (with earlier short terms also noted). [Q51]\n● Source Q52 mein Nehru, Indira Gandhi, Gulzari Lal Nanda aur Vajpayee sabko PM office more than\nonce hold karne wala bataya; Q53 gap-in-tenure set = Nanda, Indira Gandhi, Vajpayee. [Q52, Q53]\n● Lal Bahadur Shastri India ke second PM the aur 11 Jan 1966 ko Tashkent mein death hui - source asks\nPM who died outside India. [Q54]\n● CM-to-PM mapping: P.V. Narasimha Rao-Andhra Pradesh; Morarji Desai-Bombay; H.D. Deve Gowda-\nKarnataka; Charan Singh-U.P.; Narendra Modi-Gujarat. Chandra Shekhar source set mein CM nahi\nrahe the. [Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● Deve Gowda, I.K. Gujral aur Manmohan Singh source ke mutabik PM tenure ke dauran Lok Sabha\nmembers nahi the; Chandra Shekhar Lok Sabha member the. Charan Singh ne PM tenure mein\nParliament/Lok Sabha sitting attend nahi ki because support before sitting withdraw ho gaya. [Q58, Q59]\n8. Finance, Economic Policy & Manmohan Singh\n● V.P. Singh, R. Venkataraman, Y.B. Chavan aur Pranab Mukherjee - source ke according sab Union\nFinance Ministers rahe. [Q60]\n● Liberalisation-Privatisation-Globalisation wali New Economic Policy source 24 July 1991 ko PM P.V.\nNarasimha Rao se associate karta hai. [Q61]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n● Dr. Manmohan Singh ke source roles mein Finance Commission Chairman ko incorrect/not-held bataya\ngaya hai. [Q62]\n● Manmohan Singh 2004-2014 PM rahe; source unki Rajya Sabha membership Assam (1991 onward\nrepeated terms) aur 2019 Rajasthan se note karta hai. [Q63]\n9. Policy–Implementation & Deputy Prime Minister\n● Source administrative principle: Ministers policy banate hain aur civil servants us policy ko\nfollow/implement karte hain; Cabinet collective responsibility statement true hai, but Assertion ka direct\nexplanation nahi. [Q64]\n● Deputy Prime Minister ka office/duties Constitution mein mentioned nahi; kisi Cabinet Minister ko\npolitical/conventional decision se DPM declare kiya ja sakta hai aur title se PM powers automatically\nconfer nahi hoti. [Q65, Q66]\n● First Deputy Prime Minister = Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (15 Aug 1947-15 Dec 1950), source unhe Home\nMinister aur princely-state integration se bhi link karta hai. [Q67]\n● Split system in Indian administration source ke mutabik Policy vs Implementation se related hai; ex-\nSecretariat idea implementation efficiency se linked hai. [Q86]\n10. Cabinet Secretariat, Committees & Ministries\n● N. Gopalaswamy Ayyangar ke 1950 report ko source Union Cabinet/Central Govt machinery\nreorganisation se link karta hai; Q12 ka specific “minister + secretary solely for administrative reform”\nclaim false marked hai. [Q12, Q82]\n● Cabinet Secretariat directly Prime Minister ke under functions karta hai; administrative head Cabinet\nSecretary hai, jo ex-officio Chairman of Civil Services Board aur source ke mutabik highest Central civil\nservices officer hai. [Q68, Q69, Q83, Q84]\n● Cabinet Secretariat functions: Cabinet meetings ki agenda preparation, Cabinet/Cabinet Committees ko\nsecretariat assistance, Rules of Business administration aur inter-ministerial coordination; financial\nresources allocation Finance Ministry ka function hai. [Q85]\n● Cabinet Committees Constitution mein mentioned nahi - extra-constitutional bodies; PM\nsituation/requirement ke according set up karta hai. Source: PM member ho to necessarily Chairman;\nParliamentary Affairs Committee Defence Minister chair karta hai. [Q70]\n● 15 Aug 1947 ko Centre mein 18 Ministries source gives; Q73 explanation “present” count 53 batata hai\n(question-time fact). Ministry of Tribal Affairs 1999 mein Social Justice & Empowerment se bifurcate\nhokar bani. [Q73, Q74]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n11. Institutions, Administrative Personalities & Official Documents\n● War Resisters International source: 1921 Bilthoven (Netherlands) founded, London HQ; Narayan Desai\n1988-91 chairman. [Q75]\n● Match source: Nagendra Singh-President, International Court of Justice; A.N. Roy-Chief Justice of India;\nR.K. Trivedi-Chief Election Commissioner; Ashok Desai-Attorney-General of India. [Q76]\n● UIDAI June 2009: source Nandan Nilekani ko first Chairman aur R.S. Sharma ko first Director General\nbatata hai; later chairman post CEO mein convert hone ki note bhi source mein hai. [Q77]\n● Sarosh Zaiwalla source mein renowned international law expert / international arbitration law personality\nhain. [Q78]\n● White Paper ko source Government/Ministry ka official document batata hai jo policy explain karke\nfeedback collect karne mein use hota hai. [Q81]\n● Prime Minister source ke according Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR) ke President aur\nNational Defence Committee ke head hain. [Q87, Q88]\n12. Recent / Misc. Ministry Facts, Memorials & Slogans\n● 18th Lok Sabha elections ke baad source Q79: Giriraj Singh (Begusarai) Union Minister of Textiles\nappointed hue. [Q79]\n● Q80 ek time-bound ministry question hai: question-period answer Smriti Irani; source explanation\nadditionally Ministry of Minority Affairs creation 29 Jan 2006 aur “present (2025)” minister Kiren Rijiju\nnote karta hai. [Q80]\n● Office of Parliamentary Secretary ke Q89 mein source key option 1952 mark karta hai, lekin explanation\nexact fact 1951 likhta hai - is internal conflict ko trap section mein preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q89]\n● Memorial match: Nehru-Shanti Van, L.B. Shastri-Vijaya Ghat, Indira Gandhi-Shakti Sthal; Rajiv Gandhi\nka memorial Veer Bhumi hai, Karam Bhumi nahi. [Q90]\n● 'Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan' slogan source Lal Bahadur Shastri se 1965 Ramlila Maidan, Delhi public gathering\nke context mein associate karta hai. [Q91]\n13. Exam Traps — Source Conflicts & Disputed Questions\n EXAM TRAPS — Source ko jaisa diya hai, waisa hi preserve\n⚠\n ▸Q29-Q30 disputed: constitutionally source explanation collective responsibility Lok Sabha ko batata hai;\noptions mein Lok Sabha absent hone par Parliament “nearest” answer kaha gaya. [Q29, Q30]\n ▸Q44 Commission-deleted/disputed: source explanation 28 no-confidence + 11 confidence motions till 15\nAug 2023 batata hai, jabki option count different tha. [Q44]\n ▸Q47 disputed because correct fact R.K. Shanmukham Chetty source explanation mein hai but options mein\nnaam missing tha. [Q47]\n ▸Q11 wording trap: question kehta hai 'Cabinet' word mentioned only once; explanation Article 352(3) ko\nlocation batakar same Article mein word do baar aane ki note deta hai. [Q11]\n ▸Q73 “present ministries = 53” aur Q80 minister names time-bound source statements hain; unhe current-\nweb fact ke roop mein silently update nahi kiya gaya. [Q73, Q80]\n ▸Q89 internal mismatch: marked answer option (B)=1952, explanation says Office of Parliamentary Secretary\nwas created in 1951. [Q89]\nRapid Recall — One-Liners\n● Executive power formally President (Art. 53); real government leadership PM/Council framework. [Q2–Q5,\nQ14]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Council of Ministers Full Mind Map\n● PM appointment = President; Ministers = President on PM advice; 6-month membership rule = Art. 75(5).\n[Q4, Q17, Q19, Q23–Q25]\n● Council collectively responsible ONLY to Lok Sabha = Article 75(3). [Q27–Q35]\n● No-confidence: Lok Sabha only, Rule 198, minimum support 50; passage means Council resigns. [Q38–\nQ44]\n● Cabinet ≠ entire Council; “Cabinet” constitutional reference = Article 352(3). [Q9–Q11]\n● 91st Amendment / Article 75(1A) = Union ministry max 15% of Lok Sabha strength. [Q7, Q8, Q71, Q72]\n● Cabinet Secretariat = PM under; Cabinet Secretary = administrative head + Civil Services Board chair.\n[Q68, Q69, Q83–Q85]\n● Deputy PM = non-constitutional political/conventional post; first = Sardar Patel. [Q65–Q67]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0269","t":"02 British Crown Rule","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" 🏛️ BRITISH CROWN RULE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Indian Councils Act, 1861 — Portfolio System & Legislative Council\n2. Indian Councils Act, 1892 — Budget Discussion & Questions\n3. Indian Councils Act, 1909 — Separate Electorate\n4. Government of India Act, 1919 — Provincial Dyarchy\n5. Government of India Act, 1919 — Bicameral Legislature at Centre\n6. Government of India Act, 1919 — Women, ICS, Princes & Elections\n7. Government of India Act, 1935 — Federal Court\n8. Government of India Act, 1935 — Central Dyarchy & Constitutional Autocracy\n9. Government of India Act, 1935 — Federation & Distribution of Powers\n10. Government of India Act, 1935 — Provincial Autonomy & Constitutional Legacy\n11. Bihar Bicameral Legislature — Disputed Question\n12. Burma Separation from India\n1. Indian Councils Act, 1861 — Portfolio System & Legislative Council\n● Indian Councils Act, 1861 ne Viceroy ki Executive Council ko portfolio system par chalne wale miniature\ncabinet mein badla. Five members ko Revenue, Finance, Law, Home aur Military departments mile;\n1874 mein Public Works ke liye sixth member add hua. Isliye 'total members became 7' wala statement\nsource explanation ke mutabik incorrect hai. [Q1]\n● Legislative work ke liye additional members minimum 6 aur maximum 12 ho sakte the; Viceroy unhe 2\nyears ke liye nominate karta tha aur kam-se-kam half members non-official hone the. [Q1]\n● Is Act mein Central aur Provincial subjects ke beech differentiation nahi ki gayi thi. [Q1]\n2. Indian Councils Act, 1892 — Budget Discussion & Questions\n● Indian Councils Act, 1892 ko British Parliament ne pass kiya aur 20 June 1892 ko royal assent mila,\nlekin source explanation ke mutabik Act 3 February 1893 se commence hua. [Q2]\n● Governor-General's Council ke additional members ko minimum 10 aur maximum 16 tak badhaya gaya;\nat least half non-official hone the (source explanation 10 out of 16 non-official mention karta hai). [Q2]\n● Legislative Council ko Budget discuss karne ka right mila, lekin Budget par vote karne ka power nahi.\nExecutive se question poochne ke liye 6 days ka prior notice chahiye tha; supplementary questions\nallowed nahi the. [Q2, Q3]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Indian Councils Act 1892 — Q2 source mein disputed hai\n\n▸Q2 ke statement (i) mein 20 June 1892 ko implementation bola gaya hai; source explanation ise royal\nassent ki date batata hai aur commencement 3 February 1893 deta hai.\n\n▸Statement (iii) supplementary questions ka right bolta hai, lekin source ke hisab se supplementary\nquestions allowed nahi the.\n\n▸Source ne teenon statements ko incorrect maana aur likha ki given options mein koi match nahi karta. [Q2]\n3. Indian Councils Act, 1909 — Separate Electorate"," ● Indian Councils Act, 1909 — Morley-Minto Reforms — ne Muslim community ke liye separate electorate\nintroduce karke communal representation ka system diya. [Q4, Q5]\n● Source explanation 1909 Act ko communalism ko legalize karne/separatism ke seeds se jodta hai.\nGovernment of India Act, 1919 ne Muslims ke liye separate electorate introduce nahi kiya; usne is\nprinciple ko Sikhs, Europeans, Indian-Christians aur Anglo-Indians tak extend kiya. [Q4, Q5, Q10]"," 4. Government of India Act, 1919 — Provincial Dyarchy\n● Government of India Act, 1919 (Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms) ne Provinces mein Dyarchy — yaani\ndual government — introduce ki. Provincial subjects ko Reserved aur Transferred categories mein divide\nkiya gaya. [Q10, Q11, Q13]\n● Reserved subjects Governor aur uski Executive Council handle karti thi. Source examples: Police,\nJustice/Judicial Administration, Finance, Land Revenue, Prisons aur Forests. [Q11, Q12]\n● Transferred subjects Indian ministers ki aid se administer hote the. Source examples: Education,\nAgriculture, Health & Sanitation, Local Self-Government aur Public Works. [Q11, Q12]\n● 1919 Act ne legislative authority ka devolution karke Centre aur Provinces ke powers ko distribute kiya.\n[Q10]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Dyarchy — 1919 vs 1935\n\n▸1919 → Dyarchy Provinces mein introduce hui: Reserved + Transferred subjects. [Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13]\n\n▸1935 → Provincial Dyarchy abolish hui aur Dyarchy Centre par introduce ki gayi. [Q8, Q9, Q26]\n\n▸Exam wording mein 'provincial level' aur 'central level' ko sabse pehle identify karo.\n5. Government of India Act, 1919 — Bicameral Legislature at Centre\n● Government of India Act, 1919 ne Indian Legislature ko pehli baar bicameral banaya. [Q14, Q15]\n● Upper House ka naam Council of State aur Lower House ka naam Central Legislative Assembly tha.\n[Q14]\n6. Government of India Act, 1919 — Women, ICS, Princes & Elections\n● Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms, 1919 ne 21+ age ki sabhi women ko universal voting right nahi diya.\nSource ke mutabik Provincial Councils decide kar sakti thi ki property ya educational qualifications meet\nkarne wali women vote kar sakein ya nahi. [Q16]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne communal representation ke principle ko extend karte hue women,\ndepressed classes aur labourers ke liye separate electorates/reserved seats ka provision diya — source\nQ16 isi contrast ko use karta hai. [Q16]\n● Government of India Act, 1919 ne Indian Civil Service ke liye India mein separate examination ka\nprovision diya. Source ke mutabik exam 1922 mein start hua — pehle Allahabad aur baad mein Delhi.\n1941 tak ICS mein Indians ka proportion Europeans se zyada ho gaya tha. [Q17]\n● 1919 Act se 120-member 'Chamber of Princes' / Narendra Mandal ka system linked hai. Source ke\nmutabik King-Emperor George V ki Proclamation se 1921 mein establish hua; princely rulers ke liye\nadvisory forum tha aur Viceroy preside karta tha. [Q18]\n● Central Legislative Assembly ke 1926 aur 1945 elections Government of India Act, 1919 ke provisions\nke under hue. 1937 elections Provincial elections the aur Government of India Act, 1935 ke under hue.\n[Q19]\n● Government of India Act, 1919 ke under Indian Legislature ka last election 1945 mein hua. [Q20]\n7. Government of India Act, 1935 — Federal Court\n● Federal Court ka provision Government of India Act, 1935 ke under tha; Court 1 October 1937 ko\nestablish hua. [Q6, Q7]\n● Source explanation ke mutabik Federal Court ke first Chief Justice Sir Maurice Gwyer the. [Q6]"," 8. Government of India Act, 1935 — Central Dyarchy & Constitutional\nAutocracy\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne Provincial Dyarchy abolish karke Central level par Dyarchy introduce\nki; Central subjects ko Reserved aur Transferred categories mein divide kiya gaya. [Q8, Q9, Q26]\n● 'Principle of Constitutional Autocracy' source ke mutabik Government of India Act, 1935 se introduce\nhua: Provinces ki executive authority Governors aur Centre ki executive authority Governor-General\nmein Crown ke behalf par vest ki gayi. [Q22]\n● Viceroy ko ordinance promulgate karne ka power Indian Councils Act, 1861 mein bhi tha, lekin source\nexplanation modern President ke ordinance power (Article 123) ko directly Government of India Act,\n1935 ke Section 42 se inspired batata hai. [Q21]\n9. Government of India Act, 1935 — Federation & Distribution of Powers\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne legislative powers ko Federal, Provincial aur Concurrent lists mein\nstructure kiya; source ise modern Constitution mein Centre-State power distribution ka basis batata hai.\n[Q23]\n● Act ne British Indian Provinces aur Princely States ko units banakar All India Federation establish karne\nka provision diya. Source ek question mein proposed structure ki official terminology 'Federation of India'\nbatata hai. [Q27, Q28, Q30, Q31]\n● 1935 Federation mein residuary powers Governor-General / Viceroy ke paas vested thi — Central ya\nProvincial Legislature ko allocate nahi ki gayi thi. [Q24, Q29]\n● Central Dyarchy ke framework mein Defence, Ecclesiastical Affairs aur External Affairs Reserved\nSubjects the; source ke mutabik ye Governor-General ke discretion mein the, Federal Legislature ke\ndirect control mein nahi. [Q30]\n10. Government of India Act, 1935 — Provincial Autonomy & Constitutional\nLegacy\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne British India mein Provincial Autonomy establish/extend ki aur\nProvinces mein Dyarchy entirely abolish ki. [Q25]\n● Source Q32 ke mutabik Federation of India ka proposal, Provincial Autonomy aur Governor-General's\nExecutive Council ka reconstruction 1935 Act ki features mein the; 'Appraisal of the Act of 1935' khud\nkoi feature/provision nahi tha. [Q32]\n● Source Q33 ke mutabik country ke liye written Constitution ka provision Government of India Act, 1935\nmein mention nahi tha; Constitution ki demand ko British Government ne later August Offer, 1940 mein\nprinciple mein accept kiya. [Q33]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ko source Indian Constitution ka important/main source batata hai.\nFederal structure, Centre-State power distribution aur Federal Court jaise provisions is legacy se linked\nbataye gaye hain. [Q34]\n11. Bihar Bicameral Legislature — Disputed Question\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne six provinces — Bihar, Bengal, United Province, Bombay, Madras aur\nAssam — mein bicameral legislature provide kiya. Bihar mein Bihar Legislative Assembly + Bihar\nLegislative Council ka bicameral setup isi context mein source explain karta hai. [Q35]"," ⚠️EXAM TRAP — Bihar Bicameral Legislature — Q35 source mein answer-key conflict\n\n▸Source explanation ke hisab se historically Government of India Act, 1935 (option C) answer hona chahiye.\n\n▸Lekin source saath hi record karta hai ki BPSC official answer key ne option (A) ko correct mark kiya tha.\n\n▸Isliye Q35 ko source ne 'Disputed Question' mark kiya hai — dono facts ko yaad rakho. [Q35]\n12. Burma Separation from India\n● Burma ko India se 1937 mein officially separate kiya gaya; source is separation ko Government of India\nAct, 1935 ke provisions se link karta hai. [Q36]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · British Crown Rule Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0270","t":"20 The Attorney General and the CAG","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Attorney General and the C.A.G. Full Mind Map\n THE ATTORNEY GENERAL AND THE C.A.G. —\n⚖️\n\nFULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Attorney General — Article 76, Position, Appointment & Tenure\n2. Attorney General — Courts & Parliamentary Rights (Article 88)\n3. Solicitor General & Advocate General — Union vs State Law Officers\n4. CAG — Constitutional Office, Appointment & Reports\n5. CAG — Tenure, Removal, Salary & Independence\n6. CAG — Duties, Audit Scope & Financial Accountability\n7. CAG Articles 148–151 — Quick Constitutional Map\n8. Public Accounts Committee & Guardian of Public Purse\n9. Accounts vs Audit — 1976 Separation\n10. Important Persons, Matching & Public Finance\n11. Exam Traps — Source Ambiguities / Disputed Questions\n1. Attorney General — Article 76, Position, Appointment & Tenure\n● Article 76 Attorney General of India ka constitutional office provide karta hai. Source ke mutabik AG\nGovernment of India ka chief legal adviser aur country ka first/highest law officer hai. [Q1, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● AG ko President appoint karta hai aur woh President ke pleasure tak office hold karta hai; fixed security\nof tenure/removal-by-impeachment rule source mein nahi diya gaya. [Q2, Q3, Q4, Q11, Q12]\n● Qualification: person Supreme Court Judge appoint hone ke qualified hona chahiye; source explanation\ncitizen + HC judge/advocate experience ya President ki opinion mein eminent jurist wali SC-judge\neligibility ko refer karta hai. [Q11, Q12, Q13]\n● AG ki remuneration Parliament nahi, President determine karta hai; source Article 76(4) ko is point ke\nliye use karta hai. [Q14]\n2. Attorney General — Courts & Parliamentary Rights (Article 88)\n● Duty perform karte waqt Attorney General ko India ke territory ke sabhi courts mein right of audience hai.\nGovernment ka top law officer court mein Government ko represent karta hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Article 88 ke under AG either House, joint sitting aur named Parliamentary Committee ki proceedings\nmein speak/take part kar sakta hai; member hona zaroori nahi. [Q13, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21, Q23]\n● AG Parliament mein vote nahi kar sakta. Source repeatedly “participate/speak but no vote” distinction ko\ntest karta hai. [Q17, Q21]\n3. Solicitor General & Advocate General — Union vs State Law Officers\n● Solicitor General Government ka legal adviser hai; source ise Attorney General ke subordinate, country\nka second law officer aur Additional Solicitors General se assisted officer batata hai. [Q25, Q26]\n● State Government ka legal adviser Advocate General hai. Article 165 ke under Governor qualified High\nCourt Judge-level person ko appoint karta hai; office Governor ke pleasure tak hota hai. [Q27, Q28, Q29,\nQ30]\n● Source Q31 ke mutabik Advocate General ko President nahi Governor appoint karta hai; Article 177\nState Legislature mein speak/take part ka right deta hai, vote ka nahi. [Q31]\n4. CAG — Constitutional Office, Appointment & Reports\n● Article 148 CAG ka independent constitutional office establish karta hai. Appointment President apne\nhand and seal ke warrant se karta hai. [Q32, Q33, Q36]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Attorney General and the C.A.G. Full Mind Map\n● Union accounts se related CAG report President ko submit hoti hai; source explanation State accounts ki\nreport Governor ko submit hone ka point bhi deta hai. [Q32, Q34, Q35]\n● Q35 mein President option mein nahi tha, isliye source key “None of the above” rakhti hai — substantive\nanswer President hi hai. [Q35]\n5. CAG — Tenure, Removal, Salary & Independence\n● Salary/service conditions Second Schedule (Part E) se linked hain; source CAG Act, 1971 ke under\nsalary Supreme Court Judge ke salary ke equal batata hai. [Q37]\n● Tenure: 6 years ya 65 years age, jo pehle ho; source is statutory rule ko Article 148(3) ke service-\ncondition framework ke saath explain karta hai. [Q38, Q39]\n● Removal “like manner and on like grounds as a Supreme Court Judge” hota hai; simple President-\npleasure removal nahi. CAG office chhodne ke baad Union/State Government ke kisi further office ke\nliye eligible nahi. [Q40, Q41, Q51]\n● CAG office ke administrative expenses Consolidated Fund of India par charged hote hain, Parliament\nvote ke subject nahi; leave grant/refuse karne ki power President ke paas hai. [Q51, Q53]\n6. CAG — Duties, Audit Scope & Financial Accountability\n● CAG audit ka objective sirf expenditure ki legality nahi, propriety/economy/efficiency/effectiveness bhi\ncheck karna hai; source financial, compliance aur performance audit dimensions explain karta hai. [Q42]\n● CAG public money ke receipt/issue ko pre-control nahi karta; expenditure/receipts ko audit karta hai.\nSource “exchequer control” aur prosecution/judicial powers ko CAG ke functions mein include nahi\nkarta. [Q43, Q45]\n● CAG Consolidated Fund mein payable receipts aur Union/State offices ke stores/stock accounts\naudit/report kar sakta hai. [Q44]\n● CAG reports ke facts investigating agencies use kar sakti hain; projects/programmes reports PAC mein\ndiscuss hoti hain. Final parliamentary accountability ke context mein due action ki ultimate responsibility\nParliament par batayi gayi hai. [Q45, Q46]\n● CAG Public Accounts Committee meetings attend karta hai; Article 149 duties and powers prescribe\nkarta hai. [Q47, Q48]\n7. CAG Articles 148–151 — Quick Constitutional Map\n● Article 148 → Appointment/office of CAG; Article 149 → Duties & Powers; Article 150 → Form of\nAccounts of Union and States; Article 151 → Audit Reports. [Q49]\n8. Public Accounts Committee & Guardian of Public Purse\n● CAG ko Public Accounts Committee ka “Friend, Philosopher and Guide” bataya gaya hai; PAC CAG\naudit reports examine karte waqt CAG ki assistance leti hai. [Q46, Q47, Q52]\n● CAG “Guardian of Public Purse / Public Finance” hai — public money ka custodian/trustee; source ka\nemphasis hai ki Consolidated Fund ka paisa legislative authorization ke bina spend nahi hona chahiye.\n[Q57, Q58]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Attorney General and the C.A.G. Full Mind Map\n9. Accounts vs Audit — 1976 Separation\n● CAG (Duties, Powers and Conditions of Service) Act, 1971 mein 1976 amendment se Central\nGovernment accounts preparation ko audit se separate kiya gaya; source 1 March 1976 effective date\nbatata hai. [Q54, Q55]\n● Source explanation ke mutabik State level par accounting aur auditing dono functions CAG framework se\nassociated rahe; Q56 ka substantive answer CAG hai, jo options mein nahi tha. [Q54, Q56]\n10. Important Persons, Matching & Public Finance\n● Source Q59: Girish Chandra Murmu Independent India ke 14th CAG the; explanation K. Sanjay Murthy\nko 15th CAG, 2024 appointed, batata hai. [Q59]\n● Match-the-following source pair: Vice-President → Rajya Sabha; CAG → Public Accounts Committee;\nSolicitor General → Supreme Court; Attorney General → Meetings of Lok Sabha. [Q60]\n● Public Finance Government ki financial activities ka study hai — public expenditure, public revenue aur\nfinancial administration included hain; commercial bank functioning isme include nahi. [Q61]\n11. Exam Traps — Source Ambiguities / Disputed Questions\n EXAM TRAP — AG Privileges — Q15 Official Key Conflict\n⚠\nQ15 ka official key ‘Only 2’ deta hai, lekin source explanation khud note karta hai ki constitutionally AG Article\n105(4) ke under MP-type privileges enjoy karta hai. Isliye is item ko source-conflict ke roop mein yaad rakho,\nsilently correct mat karo. [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP — Solicitor General & Resignation Convention\n⚠\nQ16: Solicitor General ko Article 88 wala constitutional parliamentary participation right nahi; aur Constitution\nAG ko appointing Government resign karte hi resign karne ke liye compel nahi karta — source ise convention\nbatata hai. [Q16]\n EXAM TRAP — Non-member Participation — VP vs AG\n⚠\nQ22 mein Vice-President aur Attorney General dono interpretations aa sakte hain; official key ‘More than one’\nhai. Q24 explicitly multiple-correct batata hai: VP aur AG dono non-members ke roop mein participate kar sakte\nhain, par AG either House mein Article 88 ke under participate karta hai. [Q22, Q24]\n EXAM TRAP — CAG Removal — Disputed Options\n⚠\nQ50 source ke hisab se CAG removal President ke order se hota hai, lekin Supreme Court Judge jaisa\nparliamentary address/manner follow hota hai. Isliye sirf ‘President’ ya sirf ‘Parliament’ option apne aap\ncomplete answer nahi tha. [Q50]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0271","t":"21 Order of Precedence","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Order of Precedence Full Mind Map\n ORDER OF PRECEDENCE — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Top Constitutional Order — President to Parliament Members\n2. CJI, Cabinet Minister, CEC & Cabinet Secretary — Relative Order\n3. Who Ranks Above / Equal to the Chief Justice of India?\n4. Governor Within His State — Protocol Rank\n5. Rank 9A — UPSC Chairman, CEC & CAG\n6. Cabinet Secretary — Highest Ranking Civilian Officer\n7. Exam Traps — Equal Rank & Sequence Questions\n1. Top Constitutional Order — President to Parliament Members\n● Question mein diye posts ka logical/protocol order: President → Vice-President → Prime Minister →\nSpeaker (Lok Sabha) → Member of Parliament. Source ke according President highest position par hai.\n[Q1]\n2. CJI, Cabinet Minister, CEC & Cabinet Secretary — Relative Order\n● In four functionaries ka correct precedence sequence: Chief Justice of India → Union Cabinet Minister →\nChief Election Commissioner → Cabinet Secretary. [Q2]\n3. Who Ranks Above / Equal to the Chief Justice of India?\n● Source hierarchy: 1 President → 2 Vice-President → 3 Prime Minister → 4 Governor of a State (within\nhis State) → 5 Former Presidents → 5A Deputy Prime Minister → 6 Chief Justice of India. [Q3, Q4]\n● Chief Justice of India aur Speaker of Lok Sabha dono source ki precedence table mein rank 6 par equal\nhain. Isliye Speaker CJI se “above” nahi, equal hai. [Q3]\n4. Governor Within His State — Protocol Rank\n● Indian protocol ke source explanation ke mutabik apne State ke andar Governor rank 4 par aata hai;\ngiven options mein Deputy PM, Former President aur Speaker se higher rank karta hai. [Q4]\n5. Rank 9A — UPSC Chairman, CEC & CAG\n● UPSC Chairman, Chief Election Commissioner aur Comptroller & Auditor General — teeno source mein\nrank 9A par equal diye gaye hain; Chief Justice of High Court rank 14 par diya gaya hai. [Q5]\n6. Cabinet Secretary — Highest Ranking Civilian Officer\n● Cabinet Secretary Government of India ka topmost/highest-ranking civilian officer hai. Home Secretary,\nDefence Secretary, Lt. Governor of Delhi aur PM ke Principal Secretary wale options ke against source\nCabinet Secretary ko correct batata hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● Source explanation ke mutabik Cabinet Secretary Civil Services Board, Cabinet Secretariat aur IAS ka\nex-officio head hai, aur Rules of Business ke under all Civil Services ka head bataya gaya hai. [Q6, Q7]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Order of Precedence Full Mind Map\n7. Exam Traps — Equal Rank & Sequence Questions\n EXAM TRAP — CJI vs Speaker\n⚠\nCJI aur Lok Sabha Speaker source table mein dono rank 6 par equal hain. “Who is above CJI?” type question\nmein Speaker ko above mat maan lena. [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP — Rank 9A — More Than One Correct\n⚠\nUPSC Chairman, CEC aur CAG teeno equal rank 9A par hain. Isliye “who comes first?” ke options mein ek se\nzyada 9A officials hon to source ke hisab se “More than one” correct ho sakta hai. [Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — Cabinet Secretary: Protocol Rank vs Civilian Officer\n⚠\nQ2 mein Cabinet Secretary CJI/Cabinet Minister/CEC ke baad aata hai, lekin Q6–Q7 mein wahi Government of\nIndia ka highest-ranking civilian officer hai. Dono statements alag context test karte hain. [Q2, Q6, Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0272","t":"22 The Parliament 1","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (1) Full Mind Map\n THE PARLIAMENT (1) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Lok Sabha Election — Age, Adult Suffrage & Nomination\n2. Seat Allocation — Census Freeze & Delimitation\n3. Composition & Strength — Article 81, Amendments & UT Seats\n4. SC/ST Reservation & Anglo-Indian Representation\n5. Term, Sessions, Dissolution & Quorum\n6. State-wise Lok Sabha Seat Map\n7. Constituency & 2024 Polling Facts\n8. Election Expenditure, Deposit & Lok Sabha Timeline\n9. Leader of the House & First-Past-the-Post System\n10. Speaker — Election, Oath, Resignation & Removal\n11. Pro-tem Speaker\n12. Speaker Powers — Joint Sitting, Money Bill & Casting Vote\n13. Speaker Firsts & Milestones\n14. Deputy Speaker & Lok Sabha Secretariat\n15. Women Representation in Lok Sabha\n16. Leader of Opposition\n17. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-sensitive Source Questions\n1. Lok Sabha Election — Age, Adult Suffrage & Nomination\n● Article 84(b) ke source explanation ke mutabik Lok Sabha membership ke liye minimum age 25 years\nhai; Rajya Sabha ke liye 30 years. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Lok Sabha/State Assembly elections adult suffrage par hote hain (Article 326); election ka\nsuperintendence, direction aur control Election Commission ke paas Article 324 ke under hai — electoral\nrolls President ke direction mein nahi bante. [Q4]\n● Representation of the People Act, 1951 ke Section 4(d) ke source note ke mutabik Lok Sabha\nnomination India ka woh citizen file kar sakta hai jiska naam kisi parliamentary constituency ki electoral\nroll mein ho. [Q5]\n2. Seat Allocation — Census Freeze & Delimitation\n● State-wise Lok Sabha seats aur territorial constituencies population-based ratio principle se linked hain;\nsource ek small-population exception bhi note karta hai. [Q6]\n● Article 82/allocation questions mein source 1971 Census ko base batata hai. 84th Constitutional\nAmendment Act, 2001 ne is allocation ko 2026 tak freeze kiya aur delimitation freeze questions bhi isi\nrule se linked hain. [Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]\n3. Composition & Strength — Article 81, Amendments & UT Seats\n● Source historical position mein maximum 552 batata hai: 530 States + 20 UTs + 2 Anglo-Indian\nnominees; 104th Amendment ke baad Anglo-Indian nomination continue nahi hui, isliye source\npost-2020 maximum 550 explain karta hai. [Q12, Q15]\n● 7th Amendment (1956) se Lok Sabha strength 520 determine hui; 31st Amendment Act, 1973 ne 525 se\n545 kiya — States 500→525 aur UT component 25→20. [Q13, Q14]\n● Source explanation ke according present elected strength 543 hai — 524 State seats + 19 UT seats; 2\nnominated Anglo-Indian seats discontinue ho chuki hain. [Q16]\n● Article 81 ke source text mein UT representation maximum 20 hai. 2009 election ke 543 seats mein\nsource 530 States + 13 UT batata hai; ek later source note currently 19 UT seats list karta hai. [Q17, Q18,\nQ19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (1) Full Mind Map\n4. SC/ST Reservation & Anglo-Indian Representation\n● Article 330 Lok Sabha mein SC/ST seat reservation se related hai. 2008 delimitation ke source figures:\n412 General, 84 SC-reserved aur 47 ST-reserved seats; reserved constituency ke voters separate\nelectorate se nahi, normal constituency electorate se vote karte hain. [Q20, Q23]\n● ST-reservation pattern time-sensitive hai: source Q21 ke updated note mein Kerala aur Tamil Nadu mein\nST reserved Lok Sabha seat nahi batayi gayi; Q22 source Arunachal Pradesh aur J&K ko “more than\none correct” case mark karta hai. [Q21, Q22]\n● Article 330(2) ke according reserved seats State/UT ke total seats ke proportion mein SC/ST population\nshare ke as-near-as-possible ratio par hoti hain; isliye Q24 ka fixed numerical option source ne disputed\nmaana. [Q24]\n● Source ke post-delimitation data mein Madhya Pradesh ST-reserved Lok Sabha seats mein maximum 6\nbataya gaya; Jharkhand/Odisha 5-5 aur Gujarat 4 ka note bhi diya gaya hai. [Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Article 331 ke old arrangement mein President inadequate representation par maximum 2 Anglo-Indian\nmembers nominate kar sakta tha; source 104th Amendment ke baad 25 Jan 2020 se arrangement\ncontinue na hone ki wajah se in questions ko disputed/time-bound mark karta hai. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n5. Term, Sessions, Dissolution & Quorum\n● Article 85(2)(b): Lok Sabha apna normal term complete hone se pehle dissolve ho sakti hai; source\nPresident ko PM/Council of Ministers ki recommendation par dissolution power explain karta hai. [Q31,\nQ32]\n● Article 85(1): President House ko time/place par summon karta hai; do sessions ke beech 6 months se\nzyada gap nahi. Constitution three named annual sessions mandate nahi karta; practical calendar mein\nBudget, Monsoon aur Winter sessions generally hote hain. [Q33, Q34, Q38]\n● Adjournment Speaker karta hai; prorogation aur dissolution President Article 85(2) ke under karta hai.\n[Q35, Q36]\n● Article 83(2): Lok Sabha ka normal term first meeting se 5 years; Emergency ke dauran Parliament one-\nyear-at-a-time extension kar sakta hai, but Emergency end ke 6 months se beyond nahi. [Q37]\n● Article 100(3): Lok Sabha aur Rajya Sabha ka quorum total membership ka 1/10th hai. [Q39, Q40, Q41]\n6. State-wise Lok Sabha Seat Map\n● Source seat map: Uttar Pradesh sabse zyada Lok Sabha members bhejta hai — 80; Rajya Sabha mein\nbhi UP ka representation source ke mutabik highest 31 hai. [Q42, Q43]\n● Updated ranking in source: UP 80 → Maharashtra 48 → West Bengal 42 → Bihar 40 → Tamil Nadu 39\n→ Madhya Pradesh 29. Q44 old-question context ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q44, Q45]\n● Rajasthan 25 Lok Sabha seats (source note: 4 SC, 3 ST); Uttarakhand 5 seats. [Q46, Q47]\n● Historical Bihar had 54 seats before 2000; bifurcation ke baad Bihar 40 + Jharkhand 14. Source older\nseat-comparison questions ko time-sensitive/disputed treat karta hai. [Q48]\n● Older source pair Andhra Pradesh 42 = West Bengal 42 tha; Telangana formation ke baad source note\nAP 25 aur Telangana 17 batata hai. Current-style match list: Maharashtra 48, Chhattisgarh 11, AP 25,\nWB 42, Tamil Nadu 39. [Q49, Q50, Q51]\n● One-seat group examples: Chandigarh, Sikkim, Mizoram; source additional one-seat units Andaman &\nNicobar, Lakshadweep, Nagaland, Puducherry bhi batata hai. Two-seat State example Tripura;\nArunachal Pradesh, Goa, Manipur, Meghalaya bhi 2-2. [Q52, Q53]\n7. Constituency & 2024 Polling Facts\n● Area-wise largest Lok Sabha constituency source mein Ladakh (173266 sq km) hai; next Barmer,\nKachchh, Arunachal East, Arunachal West. Smallest area example Chandni Chowk diya hai. [Q54]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (1) Full Mind Map\n● UP voter-size question mein source options ke context mein Unnao ko answer batata hai, while note\nkarta hai ki State ka overall largest-by-voters Ghaziabad hai. [Q55]\n● 2024 election: Malogam village (Anjaw, Arunachal Pradesh) mein lone female voter ke liye temporary\npolling station bana; village Arunachal East Lok Sabha seat mein aata hai. [Q56]\n● Shompen PVTG ke 7 members ne April 2024 mein pehli baar vote kiya; source ise Andaman & Nicobar\nIslands Lok Sabha seat se link karta hai. [Q57]\n8. Election Expenditure, Deposit & Lok Sabha Timeline\n● Source Q58 ko disputed/time-updated mark karke Jan 2022 ECI revision mein Lok Sabha candidate\nexpenditure limit up to 95 lakh explain karta hai.\n₹\n [Q58]\n● Security deposit source: older question values 10,000/ 5,000 the; 2010 revision ke baad Lok Sabha\n₹\n₹\nGeneral 25,000 aur SC/ST 12,500.\n₹\n₹\n [Q59]\n● Candidate valid votes ka more than 1/6 secure nahi karta to security deposit forfeit hota hai. [Q60]\n● First Lok Sabha General Election 25 Oct 1951–21 Feb 1952, 489 seats; first session 13 May 1952. 5th\nLok Sabha ka tenure about 6 years (15 Mar 1971–18 Jan 1977). [Q61, Q62]\n● 9th Lok Sabha: constituted 2 Dec 1989, dissolved 13 Mar 1991. 12th election Feb–Mar 1998; constituted\n10 Mar 1998, dissolved 26 Apr 1999. [Q63, Q64]\n● Source option-set ke context mein 13th Lok Sabha full 5-year term complete nahi kar payi; 7th Lok\nSabha election year 1980 tha. [Q65, Q66]\n9. Leader of the House & First-Past-the-Post System\n● Prime Minister normally Lok Sabha majority party ka leader hota hai; agar PM lower House ka member\nna ho to source note karta hai ki another minister Leader of the House ho sakta hai (example: 14th Lok\nSabha mein Pranab Mukherjee). [Q67]\n● Lok Sabha/Assembly election First-Past-the-Post system par hai — winner ko 50% majority compulsory\nnahi. Speaker majority aur Deputy Speaker opposition se ho, yeh constitutional mandate nahi, source\nise parliamentary tradition batata hai. [Q68]\n10. Speaker — Election, Oath, Resignation & Removal\n● Article 93: Lok Sabha apne members mein se Speaker aur Deputy Speaker choose karti hai; Speaker all\nLok Sabha members dwara elected hota hai. [Q69, Q70]\n● Speaker/Deputy Speaker separate “oath of office” nahi lete; source unhe member-oath framework se\ndistinguish karta hai. [Q71, Q72]\n● Article 94: Speaker resignation Deputy Speaker ko address karta hai. [Q73, Q74]\n● Speaker ko Article 94(c) ke under House ke all-then-members ki majority resolution se remove kiya ja\nsakta hai; removal motion ke liye at least 14 days notice. [Q75, Q76, Q77]\n● Removal resolution pending ho to Speaker preside nahi karta, lekin Article 96(2) ke source text ke\nmutabik bol/take part kar sakta hai aur first instance mein vote kar sakta hai; equality par casting vote\nnahi. [Q78]\n● Speaker election ke time House member hona chahiye; dissolution ke baad bhi next Lok Sabha ki first\nmeeting se immediately pehle tak office continue karta hai; President ke pleasure par nahi hota. [Q79,\nQ80, Q81]\n11. Pro-tem Speaker\n● New Lok Sabha ke start mein senior-most members ki list se ek member Pro-tem Speaker appoint hota\nhai; main function newly elected members ko oath administer karna aur regular Speaker election tak\nproceedings conduct karna hai. [Q82]\n● Source process note: senior-most list → Parliamentary Affairs Minister → President approval; generally\nsenior-most member Pro-tem Speaker banta hai. [Q83]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (1) Full Mind Map\n12. Speaker Powers — Joint Sitting, Money Bill & Casting Vote\n● Joint sitting President summon karta hai (Article 108), but Lok Sabha Speaker joint sitting preside karta\nhai (source Article 118(4) cite karta hai). Money Bill par Speaker ka certificate/endorsement source ke\nArticle 110(4) discussion mein important hai. [Q84]\n● Article 100(1): Speaker first instance mein normally vote nahi karta; equality of votes par casting vote use\nkarta hai. [Q85, Q86, Q87]\n13. Speaker Firsts & Milestones\n● First Lok Sabha Speaker G.V. Mavalankar (1952–1956); first Speaker ke against no-confidence motion\n15 Dec 1954 ko Acharya J.B. Kripalani + 21 opposition MPs ne move ki, motion 18 Dec ko rejected hua.\n[Q88, Q89, Q90]\n● First woman Lok Sabha Speaker Meira Kumar — source 2009–2014 tenure note karta hai. [Q91, Q92]\n● P.A. Sangma 23 May 1996 ko 11th Lok Sabha ke first tribal Speaker bane. [Q96]\n14. Deputy Speaker & Lok Sabha Secretariat\n● Rule 8(1) source ke mutabik Deputy Speaker election ki date Speaker fix karta hai; opposition/ruling\nparty se hona mandatory constitutional provision nahi. Presiding karte waqt Deputy Speaker same\npowers exercise karta hai; source Rule 8(2) motion ko another member se moved/seconded batata hai.\n[Q93]\n● Q94 time-sensitive/disputed hai: source old Deputy Speakers ka sequence dekar post ko May 2019 se\nvacant batata hai. [Q94]\n● Article 95 source note: Speaker office vacant ho to Deputy Speaker duties perform karta hai aur equality\nof votes ke event mein vote kar sakta hai. [Q95]\n● Lok Sabha Secretariat Speaker ke direct direction/control aur supervision mein kaam karta hai; source\nArticle 98 + Rules 124/124-A cite karta hai. [Q97, Q98]\n15. Women Representation in Lok Sabha\n● Q99 source ne 15th-Lok-Sabha wording ko disputed mark karke later 17th Lok Sabha data diya: 78\nwomen (>14%), BJP 41, INC 6; UP aur West Bengal se 11-11. Source 106th Amendment Act, 2023 ka\none-third reservation note bhi add karta hai. [Q99]\n● Source historical fact: women MPs ka lowest number 1977 mein 19; General Election 2019 mein 78 ko\nhighest bataya gaya. [Q100]\n16. Leader of Opposition\n● Q101 source Leader of Opposition recognition ko 10% of total membership se link karta hai; 2014 aur\n2019 mein required number na hone ka note aur 18th Lok Sabha mein Rahul Gandhi ko LoP batata hai.\n[Q101]\n● Q102: First Lok Sabha mein opposition ka second-largest party CPI (16 seats) tha, Swatantra Party nahi;\nformal “Leader of Opposition” recognition first time 1969. Source 75-member statement ko wrong aur\nformal threshold ko 10% batata hai. [Q102]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (1) Full Mind Map\n17. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-sensitive Source Questions\n 552 vs 550 vs 543 — Teen Alag Context:\n⚠\nQ12–Q19 mein historical ceiling, post-104th ceiling aur present\nelected strength alag contexts mein hain: source historical 552, post-2020 max 550 aur present elected 543\nka distinction banata hai. [Q12, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19]\n Reservation — Dynamic Data:\n⚠\nQ22 multiple-correct; Q24 proportion-based reserved seats; Q28–Q30 old\nAnglo-Indian nomination provision par based hain, jo source ke according 104th Amendment ke baad\ncontinue nahi hua. [Q22, Q24, Q28, Q29, Q30]\n State Seat Data — Old vs Reorganisation:\n⚠\nQ44, Q48, Q49, Q50 mein exam-year seat map aur later\nreorganisation/delimitation alag hain; source inhe disputed/time-sensitive maanta hai. [Q44, Q48, Q49, Q50]\n Election Cost & Deposit — Updated Values:\n⚠\nQ58/Q59 old-value questions hain; source later revisions:\nLok Sabha expenditure up to ₹95 lakh (2022 note), deposit General ₹25,000 / SC-ST ₹12,500 (2010\nrevision). [Q58, Q59]\n Deputy Speaker, Women Data & LoP:\n⚠\nQ94, Q99, Q101 time-sensitive/disputed hain. Q101/Q102 mein\n10% rule same hai, par source absolute number 54 vs 55 wording internally vary karta hai; is variation ko\nsilently reconcile nahi kiya gaya. [Q94, Q99, Q101, Q102]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0273","t":"23 The Parliament 2","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (2) Full Mind Map\n THE PARLIAMENT (2) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Rajya Sabha Composition — Article 80, Strength & Representation\n2. Permanent House — Tenure, Retirement & Dissolution\n3. Nominated Members & Membership Qualifications\n4. Article 249 — Rajya Sabha and State List Legislation\n5. Money Bill, Grants & Lok Sabha Financial Supremacy\n6. Rajya Sabha Special / Equal Powers — Articles 312 & 368\n7. Fourth Schedule — State-wise Rajya Sabha Seat Map\n8. Chairman, Deputy Chairman & Presiding Officer Rules\n9. Formation, Chairman History & 2024 Nominations\n10. Rajya Sabha Member Participating in Lok Sabha\n11. Exam Traps — Time-bound / Conflicting Source Data\n1. Rajya Sabha Composition — Article 80, Strength & Representation\n● Article 80 ke source explanation ke mutabik Rajya Sabha ki maximum/fixed constitutional strength 250\nhai: President ke 12 nominated members + States/Union Territories ke not more than 238\nrepresentatives. Source Q1 present total 245 batata hai. [Q1, Q3]\n● Representation mein President-nominated members aur elected State/UT representatives dono shamil\nhain. State representatives directly citizens se nahi, elected MLAs ke through proportional\nrepresentation by Single Transferable Vote se elect hote hain. [Q2, Q6]\n● States ko Rajya Sabha seats equal basis par nahi milti; source population ratio ko basis batata hai aur\nexact allocation Fourth Schedule se linked hai. [Q4]\n● Statement-type trap: Union Territories ka Rajya Sabha representation hai; election disputes\nJudiciary/election petition decide karti hai; Article 79 ke mutabik Parliament = President + Lok Sabha +\nRajya Sabha. [Q5]\n2. Permanent House — Tenure, Retirement & Dissolution\n● Rajya Sabha permanent House hai aur dissolution ke subject nahi. As nearly as possible, one-third\nmembers har second year retire karte hain; isi rotation ki wajah se House continuously exist karta hai.\n[Q7, Q8, Q10, Q12, Q13, Q14, Q16, Q17]\n● Article 83(1) source note: Rajya Sabha member ka tenure 6 years hota hai; one-third retirement every 2\nyears. Isliye “House ka 5-year term” aur “member 5 years” dono traps hain. [Q9, Q11]\n● Source summary question ke mutabik members elected MLAs se elect hote hain, Rajya Sabha dissolve\nnahi hoti, Vice-President ex-officio Chairman hai aur Attorney General dono Houses mein speak kar\nsakta hai. [Q15]\n3. Nominated Members & Membership Qualifications\n● President Rajya Sabha mein 12 persons nominate kar sakta hai; source areas: Literature, Science, Art\naur Social Services. [Q18, Q19]\n● Rajya Sabha candidate ke liye minimum age 30 years hai aur office of profit nahi hold karna chahiye.\nSource note: 2003 Representation of the People Act amendment ke baad candidate ka usi State ki voter\nlist mein registered hona necessary nahi raha. [Q20, Q21]\n● Source personality fact: Nargis Dutt first Indian actress nominated to Rajya Sabha (1980) batayi gayi\nhain; explanation Vaijayanthimala, Jayalalitha aur Devika Rani ka comparative note bhi deta hai. [Q22]\n4. Article 249 — Rajya Sabha and State List Legislation"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (2) Full Mind Map\n● Article 249: National interest mein Rajya Sabha resolution pass kare to Parliament State List subject par\nlaw bana sakta hai. Required support: not less than two-thirds of members present and voting. [Q23, Q24,\nQ25, Q26]\n5. Money Bill, Grants & Lok Sabha Financial Supremacy\n● Article 109 source rule: Money Bill Rajya Sabha mein introduce nahi ho sakta. Lok Sabha pass karke\nbhejne ke baad Rajya Sabha sirf recommendations de sakti hai aur 14 days ke andar return karti hai;\nLok Sabha recommendations accept ya reject kar sakti hai. [Q27, Q28, Q29, Q30]\n● Rajya Sabha Money Bill ko reject/amend karne ki binding power nahi rakhti aur Demands for Grants par\nvote nahi karti; lekin Annual Financial Statement discuss kar sakti hai. [Q27]\n● Lok Sabha ke exclusive points source mein Money Bill introduction/decision aur Council of Ministers ki\ncollective responsibility (Art. 75(3)) hain. All India Services creation Rajya Sabha special power hai, Lok\nSabha exclusive nahi. [Q31]\n● No-confidence motion Council of Ministers ke against Lok Sabha ka exclusive confidence mechanism\nhai; National Emergency approval dono Houses se aur President impeachment charge either House se\nho sakta hai. [Q32]\n6. Rajya Sabha Special / Equal Powers — Articles 312 & 368\n● Rajya Sabha special powers: Article 249 se State List legislation authorize karna aur Article 312 se one\nor more All India Services create karne ke liye 2/3 present-and-voting resolution pass karna. [Q33, Q34,\nQ35]\n● Constitutional Amendment (Article 368) mein Rajya Sabha aur Lok Sabha equal powers rakhte hain;\namendment Bill either House mein initiate ho sakta hai aur required special majority se dono Houses se\npass hona hota hai. [Q36]\n● Government Rajya Sabha mein defeat ho jaaye to source ke diye automatic consequences apply nahi\nhote, kyunki Council of Ministers collectively Lok Sabha ke prati responsible hai. [Q37]\n7. Fourth Schedule — State-wise Rajya Sabha Seat Map\n● Fourth Schedule States ko Council of States/Rajya Sabha seats allocate karti hai. Source contrast: 7th\nSchedule Union-State powers, 8th Schedule languages aur 5th/6th Schedules Scheduled Areas/Tribes\nadministration se related hain. [Q38]\n● Time-bound equal-seat question: source ke old context mein Andhra Pradesh aur Tamil Nadu 18-18\nseats the; Telangana formation ke baad source AP 11 + Telangana 7 note karta hai. [Q39]\n● Old 2000 context: U.P. 34 seats = Andhra Pradesh 18 + Madhya Pradesh 16. Bifurcations ke baad\nsource U.P. 31 + Uttarakhand 3; M.P. 11 + Chhattisgarh 5; AP 11 + Telangana 7 batata hai. [Q40, Q41,\nQ42]\n● Source seat matches: Jharkhand 6, Uttarakhand 3, Chhattisgarh 5, Punjab 7; Rajasthan 10, Gujarat 11,\nKarnataka 12, Punjab 7. [Q43, Q44]\n● Source seat map: Gujarat 11, Karnataka 12, Kerala 9, Odisha 10; decreasing order Karnataka > Gujarat\n> Odisha > Kerala. Source note U.P. = 31. [Q45, Q46]\n● Source updated pair: Andhra Pradesh 11, Telangana 7. Given comparison mein Himachal Pradesh 3\nsabse low, J&K 4, Chhattisgarh 5, Jharkhand 6. [Q47, Q48]\n● Union Territories dono Houses mein representation pa sakte hain; source Rajya Sabha figures Delhi 3,\nPuducherry 1 aur Jammu & Kashmir 4 batata hai. [Q49]\n8. Chairman, Deputy Chairman & Presiding Officer Rules\n● Rajya Sabha Chairman = Vice-President of India, ex-officio (Articles 89(1) / 64 source references).\nChairman House ka member nahi; Deputy Chairman Rajya Sabha ka member hota hai aur House apne\nmembers mein se elect karta hai. [Q50, Q51, Q52, Q53, Q54, Q55, Q56]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (2) Full Mind Map\n● Election distinction: nominated MPs Presidential election ke electoral college ka part nahi, lekin Vice-\nPresidential election mein all members of both Houses — elected + nominated — included hote hain.\n[Q50]\n9. Formation, Chairman History & 2024 Nominations\n● Source time-bound “present Chairman” question 2010 context ka hai; explanation us waqt option ko\ncorrect batata hai aur later note mein Vice-President Jagdeep Dhankar ko Chairman likhta hai. Isko\ndate-sensitive source fact ke roop mein padho. [Q57]\n● Rajya Sabha/Second Chamber 1952 mein constituted hui; idea ka origin source Montagu-Chelmsford\nReform 1919 se trace karta hai. Dr. S. Radhakrishnan ko two consecutive terms (1952–1962) serve\nkarne wale Chairman ke roop mein note kiya gaya hai. [Q58]\n● Source formation date: Rajya Sabha 3 April 1952 ko formed hui. [Q59]\n● 2024 source fact: President Droupadi Murmu ne Satnam Singh Sandhu (30 Jan 2024) aur Sudha Murty\n(8 Mar 2024) nominate kiya; source reports Sudha Murty ko Upper House ka 12th nominated member\nbatati hain. [Q60]\n10. Rajya Sabha Member Participating in Lok Sabha\n● Rajya Sabha ka member jo Minister hai, Lok Sabha ki deliberations mein participate kar sakta hai even\nthough woh Rajya Sabha member hi rahta hai. [Q61]\n11. Exam Traps — Time-bound / Conflicting Source Data\n EXAM TRAP — Old Seat Questions — AP / MP / UP Bifurcation Effect\n⚠\nQ39–Q42 historical question-date ke seat figures use karte hain. Source khud Telangana, Uttarakhand aur\nChhattisgarh formation ke baad updated allocation note karta hai; isliye old option ko current figure samajhkar\nratna nahi. [Q39, Q40, Q41, Q42]\n EXAM TRAP — Rajya Sabha “Present Strength / UT Seats” — Source Internal Variation\n⚠\nQ1 explanation present 245 ko 225 State + 8 UT + 12 nominated batata hai, jabki Q58 explanation 245 mein\n233 State/UT representatives + 12 nominated bolta hai aur UT discussion mein Delhi/Puducherry 4 plus J&K\nnote deta hai. Ye source ke andar time/context variation hai; silently reconcile nahi kiya gaya. [Q1, Q49, Q58]\n EXAM TRAP — “Present Chairman” — Date-Sensitive Question\n⚠\nQ57 ka wording “Present Chairman” time-sensitive hai. Source explanation 2010 ke original context aur ek later\nupdate dono mention karta hai; isliye exam mein question-year/context dekhna zaroori hai. [Q57]\n EXAM TRAP — Rajya Sabha History Question — First Amendment Timing\n⚠\nQ58 source note Rajya Sabha ko 1952 mein constituted aur First Constitutional Amendment ko 1951 ka batata\nhai; isi chronology ke basis par related statement ko incorrect mark kiya gaya hai. Source also records only\nthree Joint Sitting bills in its explanation. [Q58]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0274","t":"24 The Parliament 3","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n THE PARLIAMENT (3) — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Parliament Composition, President & Article 79\n2. Sessions, Officers, Absence & Vacation of Seats\n3. Privileges, Office of Profit & Membership Traps\n4. Parliamentary Legislative Power — State List, Residual & Language\n5. Zero Hour — Indian Innovation\n6. Bills, Readings & Joint Sitting — Articles 107–108\n7. Bill Lapse Rules after Lok Sabha Dissolution\n8. Public Finance — Consolidated Fund, Contingency Fund & Grants\n9. Money Bill vs Finance Bill — Articles 109–110–117\n10. Union Budget / Annual Financial Statement & Parliamentary Control\n11. Private Member Bill, Economic Survey & Vote-on-Account\n12. Financial Legislation, Demands for Grants & Cut Motions\n13. Questions, Motions, Rules & Guillotine\n14. Ordinance, Parliamentary Secretariat & Limits on Sovereignty\n15. Parliament History, New Building & Indian Parliamentary Group\n16. Exam Traps — Disputed / Date-sensitive Source Questions\n1. Parliament Composition, President & Article 79\n● Article 79 ke source ke mutabik Indian Parliament ke 3 integral parts hain — President + Rajya Sabha\n(Council of States) + Lok Sabha (House of the People). President kisi House ka member nahi aur\nParliament mein sit/vote nahi karta, phir bhi Parliament ka integral part hai; Vice-President integral part\nnahi. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Old constitutional composition table mein Lok Sabha ke liye not more than 530 State representatives +\nnot more than 20 UT representatives + Anglo-Indian nomination provision diya gaya tha. Source note\nkarta hai ki 104th Amendment Act, 2019 ke baad Anglo-Indian nomination 25 Jan 2020 se extend nahi\nhua; question ka X = up to 20 UT representatives. [Q1]\n● Article 87 special address: Lok Sabha ke har general election ke baad first session ke commencement\npar aur har year ke first session ke commencement par President dono Houses ko assembled together\naddress karta hai aur summons ke causes batata hai. [Q2, Q3]\n2. Sessions, Officers, Absence & Vacation of Seats\n● Article 85(1): Parliament ko year mein kam-se-kam twice meet karna chahiye; ek session ki last sitting\naur next session ki first sitting ke beech 6 months se zyada interval nahi. [Q15, Q16]\n● Source Parliament officers list: Lok Sabha Speaker, Deputy Speaker, Secretary-General aur Rajya\nSabha Chairman. [Q17]\n● Article 101(4): Member without House permission 60 days tak all meetings se absent rahe to House seat\nvacant declare kar sakta hai; prorogation ya more than 4 consecutive days adjournment ka period 60-\nday calculation se exclude hota hai. [Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● Source historical fact: 2000 mein Punjab se Council of States ke Independent MP Barjinder Singh\nHamdard ko 60-day absence rule par first such disqualification/seat-vacancy case bataya gaya hai. [Q21]\n● Article 101(2) / simultaneous membership rule source: Parliament + State Legislature dono ka member\nek saath nahi; State Legislature seat 14 days mein resign na karne par Parliament seat vacant ho sakti\nhai. [Q22]\n3. Privileges, Office of Profit & Membership Traps"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n● Privilege Motion Minister ke against tab uth sakta hai jab woh facts withhold kare ya distorted version de.\nArticle 105 Houses, members aur committees ke powers/privileges/immunities se related hai; courts\nParliament proceedings ki inquiry Article 122 ke under nahi karte. [Q23, Q27, Q29]\n● Collective privileges mein debates/proceedings publication prohibit karna, strangers exclude karna, own\nprocedure regulate karna, breach/contempt punish karna etc. Source freedom from attendance as\nwitness ko individual privilege batata hai, collective nahi. [Q28]\n● Article 102(1)(a) MP ke office of profit restriction se related hai. “Office of profit” Constitution/RPA 1951\nmein well-defined nahi; Parliament (Prevention of Disqualification) Act, 1959 certain offices exempt karta\nhai aur source ke mutabik Act five times amend hua. [Q24, Q25]\n● Office-of-profit question source mein two analyses deta hai: exempt offices decide karne ka legislative\nangle (Parliament/State Legislature) aur individual disqualification decision ka angle (President/Governor\nacting on Election Commission advice). [Q26]\n● Elected State Legislative Assembly member Lok Sabha election mein citizen ke roop mein aur Rajya\nSabha election mein MLA ke roop mein vote kar sakta hai; source President election vote bhi note karta\nhai. [Q30]\n● Rajya Sabha candidature ka old domicile/voter requirement 2003 amendment ke baad remove hua;\nsource Q31 ko date-sensitive/disputed maanta hai. Nominated members President election mein vote\nnahi karte, lekin Minister banne par constitutional bar nahi; 6 months membership rule applicable hai.\n[Q31, Q32]\n4. Parliamentary Legislative Power — State List, Residual & Language\n● Source ke mutabik Parliament Union of India, Territory of India aur Indian subjects/residents aur unki\nproperty situated anywhere in the world ke liye legislate kar sakta hai. [Q33]\n● State List par Parliament special situations mein law bana sakta hai: Article 249 national interest Rajya\nSabha 2/3 present-and-voting resolution; Article 252 two or more States consent; Article 253\ninternational agreements; emergency context source Q35 Article 357 aur Q37 Article 250 ko cite karta\nhai. [Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38]\n● Article 248 Parliament ko residuary matters par exclusive legislative power deta hai. [Q39]\n● Article 120: Parliament business Hindi/English mein; Chairman/Speaker member ko mother tongue mein\naddress karne ki permission de sakta hai agar woh Hindi/English mein adequately express na kar sake.\n[Q40]\n● Speaker ek member ko stop karke another member ko bolne de — source is procedure ko “yielding the\nfloor” batata hai; related decorum rules mein crossing the floor aur Speaker ke rise par member ka seat\nresume karna note hai. [Q41]\n5. Zero Hour — Indian Innovation\n● Zero Hour source ke mutabik Indian parliamentary innovation hai, early 1960s mein urgent public-\nimportance matters raise karne se develop hua. Lok Sabha mein usually Question Hour ke immediately\nbaad 12–1; Rajya Sabha source note mein 11–12 before Question Hour. [Q42, Q43, Q44]\n● Lok Sabha Zero Hour ka maximum source one hour batata hai; members urgent matters raise karte hain\njo delay nahi ho sakte, informal question-answer/public-importance device jaisa function karta hai. [Q45,\nQ46]\n6. Bills, Readings & Joint Sitting — Articles 107–108\n● Bill passage source: First stage = introduction/leave; Second reading = general discussion + clause-by-\nclause consideration; Third reading = final debate/passage. General discussion second stage/reading\nmein hoti hai. [Q47]\n● Article 108 joint sitting deadlock resolve karne ke liye; Bill simple majority of total members of both\nHouses present and voting se pass deemed hota hai. [Q48, Q57]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n● President joint sitting summon karne ki intention notify kar chuka ho aur uske baad Lok Sabha dissolve\nho, source Article 108(5) ke basis par joint sitting still hold ho sakti hai; notification se pehle Bill lapse ho\ngaya to nahi. [Q49]\n● Joint sitting presiding order source: Lok Sabha Speaker → Deputy Speaker → Rajya Sabha Deputy\nChairman → members present dwara determined person. Article 108 provision aur Article 118(4)\nprocedure reference diya gaya hai. [Q50, Q51, Q52, Q53, Q54, Q55]\n● Source joint-sitting history: 1961 Dowry Prohibition Bill; 1978 Banking Service Commission (Repeal) Bill;\nMarch 2002 POTA/Anti-Terrorism Bill. [Q56, Q59]\n● Joint sitting President/Vice-President election ya Constitutional Amendment Bill ke liye nahi; ordinary Bill\ndeadlock ke liye. Money Bill aur Constitutional Amendment Bill joint sitting route se resolve nahi hote.\n[Q58, Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● Source Q60: joint sitting ordinary Bills ke liye; presiding hierarchy Deputy Chairman tak ja sakti hai;\nquorum total members of both Houses ka 1/10, not 1/6. [Q60]\n7. Bill Lapse Rules after Lok Sabha Dissolution\n● Ordinary/legislative Bill either House mein introduce ho sakta hai; Money Bill only Lok Sabha. Source\nadditionally All-India Services creation-related initiative Rajya Sabha special power ke context mein note\nkarta hai. [Q64]\n● Article 107(5): Lok Sabha mein pending Bill, ya Lok Sabha pass karke Rajya Sabha mein pending Bill,\nLok Sabha dissolution par lapse hota hai; Article 107(4): Rajya Sabha mein pending but Lok Sabha se\nunpassed Bill lapse nahi hota. [Q65]\n● Article 107(3): prorogation se pending Bill lapse nahi hota. President joint sitting intention notify kar chuka\nho to dissolution ke baad bhi Article 108(5) protection source note karta hai. [Q65, Q66]\n8. Public Finance — Consolidated Fund, Contingency Fund & Grants\n● Article 265: authority of law ke bina tax levy/collect nahi ho sakta. Article 266 Consolidated Fund/Public\nAccount framework se linked hai. [Q67]\n● Consolidated Fund of India mein Union revenues, loans etc. credit hote hain; withdrawal ke liye\nParliament authorization/Appropriation under Article 114 required hai. [Q68, Q69, Q70]\n● Charged expenditure source list: President office, Rajya Sabha Chairman/Deputy Chairman, Lok Sabha\nSpeaker/Deputy Speaker, debt charges, Supreme Court judges, certain judge pensions, CAG,\ncourt/arbitral awards etc. PM salary charged expenditure nahi; VP salary VP ke roop mein nahi,\nChairman RS ke roop mein receive hoti hai. [Q71, Q72, Q73]\n● Article 267 Contingency Fund; Parliament law se establish karta hai, President disposal mein hota hai\naur unforeseen expenditure ke liye advance diya ja sakta hai pending later parliamentary authorization.\n[Q74, Q75]\n● Union Budget preparation source Department of Economic Affairs (Ministry of Finance) ko deta hai,\nDepartment of Revenue ko nahi. Consolidated Fund withdrawal needs Parliament authorization; Public\nAccount disbursement ko source parliamentary authorization-free executive control batata hai. [Q76, Q77]\n● Article 113 ke under Demands for Grants generally ministry/department-wise Lok Sabha ke samne;\nPresident recommendation required. Source Q78 Budget 2025-26 = 102 grants aur 2021-22 = 101 note\nkarta hai. [Q78]\n9. Money Bill vs Finance Bill — Articles 109–110–117\n● Article 110 Money Bill definition; Article 109 special procedure; Article 111 assent. Money Bill matters:\ntaxes, Union borrowing/guarantee, Consolidated/Contingency Fund custody & withdrawal, appropriation,\ncharged expenditure, CFI/Public Account receipts/custody/issue and audit-linked matters. [Q79, Q80, Q81,\nQ82]\n● Article 110(2) source trap: fines/pecuniary penalties merely impose karna Money Bill subject nahi. [Q83]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n● Source distinction: every Money Bill is a Finance Bill, but every Finance Bill is not a Money Bill. Financial\nBill (I) Article 117(1) only Lok Sabha + President recommendation, but otherwise ordinary-Bill procedure;\nRajya Sabha amend/reject kar sakti hai. Financial Bill (II) Article 117(3) expenditure from CFI and either\nHouse mein introduce ho sakta hai, consideration ke liye President recommendation needed. [Q84, Q86,\nQ104]\n● Money Bill only Lok Sabha mein introduce hota hai; Lok Sabha Speaker Article 110(3) ke under Money\nBill status decide/certify karta hai. Source Speaker decision final batata hai. [Q85, Q87, Q88, Q89, Q90, Q91,\nQ94, Q97, Q98]\n● Article 109: Rajya Sabha Money Bill reject/amend nahi kar sakti; recommendations ke saath/without\nrecommendations 14 days mein return karti hai; Lok Sabha recommendations accept/reject kar sakti hai.\n14 days action na ho to passed deemed hota hai. [Q92, Q93, Q95, Q96, Q99, Q100, Q101, Q102, Q103]\n10. Union Budget / Annual Financial Statement & Parliamentary Control\n● Article 112 Union Budget ka constitutional term “Annual Financial Statement” hai; “Budget” word\nConstitution mein source ke mutabik appear nahi karta. AFS estimated receipts & expenditure statement\nhai. [Q105, Q106, Q107]\n● Charged expenditure CFI par vote ke liye submit nahi hota, though discussion ho sakti hai. Parliamentary\nfinancial control mein AFS laying, Appropriation authorization, supplementary grants/vote-on-account\naur Finance Bill mechanisms include; source “Parliamentary Budget Office mid-year review” ko\nconstitutional mechanism nahi maanta. [Q108, Q109]\n● Source convention: annual Union Budget Lok Sabha se pass na ho to government majority/confidence\nlose maana jaata hai aur PM/Council of Ministers resignation submit karte hain. [Q110]\n11. Private Member Bill, Economic Survey & Vote-on-Account\n● Private Member Bill = any MP other than a Minister dwara introduced Bill; nominated-member definition\nnahi. Source ke mutabik independence ke baad around a dozen private members’ Bills pass hue,\n“recently first time” statement wrong. [Q111]\n● Economic Survey every year coming Budget se pehle Parliament mein presented hota hai; current-year\neconomy sectors ki progress/activities/fiscal details source note karta hai. [Q112]\n● Article 116 Vote-on-Account: full Appropriation/Budget pass hone se pehle limited period ke expenditure\nke liye CFI withdrawal authorization; full Budget ke liye time na ho/elections near ho to administration\ncontinue karne ka temporary provision. [Q113, Q114, Q115]\n● Vote-on-Account only expenditure side deal karta hai; Interim Budget source ke mutabik receipts +\nexpenditure estimates include karta hai. “Stable vs caretaker government” ko source fixed constitutional\ndistinction nahi maanta. [Q116]\n12. Financial Legislation, Demands for Grants & Cut Motions\n● Article 113(2): expenditure estimates Lok Sabha mein Demands for Grants ke form mein voted hote hain;\nLok Sabha grant pass/reject/reduce kar sakti hai. [Q117]\n● Normal financial legislation stages source: Budget presentation, discussion, Appropriation Bill, Finance\nBill. Vote-on-Account / Vote of Credit / Exceptional Grants special Article 116 devices hain, normal\nstages nahi. [Q118]\n● Source says prior President sanction/recommendation required before Bills on new State\nformation/boundary alteration, taxation in which States interested and Money Bill-type matters; Articles\n3, 274, 117/109 references diye gaye hain. [Q119]\n● Cut Motion Lok Sabha mein Demands for Grants reduce karne ka proposal hai; types source:\nDisapproval of Policy Cut, Economy Cut, Token Cut. Object government budget demand ko\nchallenge/reduce karke specified matter par House attention draw karna. [Q120, Q121, Q122]\n● Source mismatch question: Vote-on-Account entire financial-year budgetary demands ke liye nahi; Article\n116 Vote-on-Account, Vote of Credit aur Exceptional Grants se related hai. [Q123]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n13. Questions, Motions, Rules & Guillotine\n● Calling Attention Indian innovation; urgent public-importance matter par Minister ka attention draw karne\nka device, Adjournment Motion jaisa but condemnation element nahi. Source ke mutabik isne\nAdjournment Motion ka scope restrict kiya. [Q124]\n● Council of Ministers par parliamentary control source: Adjournment Motion + Question Hour +\nSupplementary Questions. Question Hour generally sitting ka first hour; starred = oral answer +\nsupplementaries, unstarred = written/no supplementaries, short-notice = urgent matter shorter notice.\n[Q125]\n● Starred Question asterisk-marked, oral answer; supplementary questions allowed. Source daily oral list\nmaximum 20 questions note karta hai. [Q126]\n● Adjournment Motion ka main purpose urgent public importance matter discuss karna. [Q127]\n● Lok Sabha Rule 184 source: discussion ke saath voting hoti hai; assertion-reason question isi point ko\nuse karta hai. [Q128]\n● Rule 377 source note: other rules/devices ke under raise na ho paane wale matters; 2015 mein daily\nmatters limit 20 se 30 ki gayi — question options ke context mein disputed. [Q129]\n● Guillotine closure motion ka form hai: allotted discussion time khatam hone par undiscussed\nclauses/demands ko discussed items ke saath vote ke liye put kar diya jaata hai. [Q130]\n14. Ordinance, Parliamentary Secretariat & Limits on Sovereignty\n● Article 123: jab both Houses simultaneously in session na hon aur immediate action necessary ho,\nPresident ordinance promulgate kar sakta hai — source Q131 ka core rule. [Q131]\n● Source combined statements: Right to Property 44th Amendment ke baad legal right Article 300A; non-\nMoney Financial Bill Rajya Sabha ordinary Bill ki tarah stop/amend kar sakti hai; 42nd Amendment ne\nSocialist, Secular, Integrity add kiya, Democratic pehle se tha; parliamentary deadlock Speaker alone\nnahi, joint sitting mechanism se resolve hota hai. [Q132]\n● Article 98: each House ka separate secretarial staff; common posts create ho sakte hain; Parliament law\nse recruitment/service conditions regulate kar sakta hai. Separate secretariat idea source Vithalbhai J.\nPatel (1926) se trace karta hai. [Q133, Q134]\n● Indian Parliament supreme legislative body hote hue unlimited sovereign nahi; source Basic Structure\naur Supreme Court judicial review ko restriction batata hai. [Q135]\n15. Parliament History, New Building & Indian Parliamentary Group\n● Indian Parliament Golden Jubilee 13 May 2002 ko celebrate hua; source formal\nestablishment/constitution date 13 May 1952 note karta hai. [Q136]\n● New Parliament building source ke mutabik architect Vimal/Bimal Patel ne design ki; PM Narendra Modi\nne 28 May 2023 inaugurate kiya. Previous building architects Sir Edwin Lutyens & Sir Herbert Baker.\n[Q137]\n● Indian Parliamentary Group source: autonomous body formed 1949; MPs + ex-MPs membership eligible;\nLok Sabha Speaker ex-officio President, Deputy Speaker LS and Deputy Chairman RS ex-officio Vice-\nPresidents. [Q138]\n● 1925 mein Vitthalbhai Patel Central Legislative Assembly ke nationalist leader/first Speaker elected hue;\nsource tenure 24 Aug 1925–28 Apr 1930 deta hai. [Q139]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Parliament (3) Full Mind Map\n16. Exam Traps — Disputed / Date-sensitive Source Questions\n Office of Profit — Q26 has Two Valid Interpretations:\n⚠\nSource explicitly marks multiple correct:\nlegislature decides which offices are exempt, while actual MP/MLA disqualification is decided by\nPresident/Governor on EC advice. [Q26]\n Rajya Sabha Domicile & Nominated Member — Law Changed:\n⚠\nQ31 uses the old pre-2003 State-voter\nrule; source marks it disputed after the RPA amendment. Q32 is multiple-correct in the source after the\n104th Amendment context. [Q31, Q32]\n Zero Hour Timing — House-wise Difference:\n⚠\nSource disputes Q42/Q43 because Lok Sabha and Rajya\nSabha timing/order differs: Lok Sabha 12–1 after Question Hour; Rajya Sabha 11–12 before Question Hour.\n[Q42, Q43]\n Demands for Grants — Time-sensitive Number:\n⚠\nQ78 is not a static constitutional number; source itself\ngives Budget 2025-26 = 102 and 2021-22 = 101, hence “none of the options”. [Q78]\n Finance Bill vs Money Bill — Terminology Trap:\n⚠\nQ84/Q86 distinguish Financial Bills from Money Bills;\nQ101 says “Finance Bill” but source treats it as a Money Bill because of the options. [Q84, Q86, Q101]\n Rule 377 — Source Updated to 30:\n⚠\nQ129 is disputed; source explanation says the daily Rule 377 matters\nlimit was increased from 20 to 30 in 2015. [Q129]\n Indian Parliamentary Group — Correct Combination Missing:\n⚠\nQ138 source says (i) false, (ii) and (iii)\ncorrect, but the correct combination is absent from the options. [Q138]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0275","t":"25 Parliamentary Committees","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Committees Full Mind Map\n PARLIAMENTARY COMMITTEES — FULL MIND\n🏛️\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Parliamentary Committees — Role, Types & Classification\n2. Estimates Committee — Largest Committee, Composition & Tenure\n3. Public Accounts Committee — Composition & Chairman\n4. Public Accounts Committee — Functions, CAG Reports & Reporting\n5. Financial Committees — PAC, Estimates & Public Undertakings\n6. Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs & Committee Coordination\n7. Ethics Committee — Origin, Complaints & Sub-judice Rule\n8. Other Standing / Departmental Committees & Jurisdiction\n9. Committee on Subordinate Legislation — Delegated Powers\n10. Joint Parliamentary Committee (JPC) — 2G Spectrum Case\n11. 18th Lok Sabha Committee Chairpersons (2024–25) & Exam Traps\n1. Parliamentary Committees — Role, Types & Classification\n● Parliament administration par control Parliamentary Committees ke through exercise karti hai; source\nexamples mein Public Accounts Committee, Estimates Committee aur Standing Committees diye gaye\nhain. [Q1]\n● Parliamentary Committees do broad types ki hain — Standing Committees aur Ad-hoc Committees. Joint\ncommittees mein Lok Sabha : Rajya Sabha representation source ke mutabik aam taur par lagbhag 2:1\nhota hai, Estimates Committee notable exception hai. [Q6]\n● Source classification: Public Accounts Committee → Financial Committee; Committee on Petitions →\nFunctional Committee; Joint Committee on Stock Market Scam → Ad-hoc Committee; Departmental\nCommittees → Standing Committee. [Q19]\n● Three Financial Committees: Public Accounts Committee, Estimates Committee aur Committee on\nPublic Undertakings. Joint Committee on Salaries & Allowances of MPs financial committee nahi hai.\n[Q23, Q24]\n2. Estimates Committee — Largest Committee, Composition & Tenure\n● Estimates Committee 1950 mein pehli baar constituted hui; 30 members ke saath source ke options\nmein Parliament ki largest committee hai. [Q2, Q3]\n● Iske members Lok Sabha apne members mein se har saal elect karti hai; tenure 1 year hota hai. [Q4]\n● Estimates Committee mein Rajya Sabha ka representation nahi hota; saare 30 members Lok Sabha se\nhote hain. [Q20, Q21, Q22]\n3. Public Accounts Committee — Composition & Chairman\n● Public Accounts Committee (PAC) ki strength 22 members hoti hai — 15 Lok Sabha + 7 Rajya Sabha.\nEminent persons of industry/trade is committee ka part nahi hote. [Q7, Q8, Q16, Q17]\n● PAC Chairman ko Speaker, Lok Sabha committee members mein se appoint/nominates karta hai.\nSource ke mutabik 1967–68 se opposition member ko Chairperson banane ki practice continue hui. [Q7,\nQ18]\n4. Public Accounts Committee — Functions, CAG Reports & Reporting\n● PAC ka main kaam CAG ke annual audit reports ko examine karna hai; isme appropriation accounts aur\nfinance accounts ki scrutiny bhi include hoti hai. [Q9, Q10, Q12, Q17]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Committees Full Mind Map\n● Source reporting chain ko alag questions alag wording se test karte hain: PAC report Parliament ko\nsubmit karta hai; Speaker of Lok Sabha ko submit ki jaati hai; aur report Lok Sabha mein present hoti\nhai. [Q13, Q14, Q15]\n5. Financial Committees — PAC, Estimates & Public Undertakings\n● CAG Article 148 ke under independent constitutional body hai; source Q5 mein ise Parliamentary control\nover public expenditure ka committee/tool nahi maana gaya, jabki PAC/Estimates jaise bodies\nparliamentary committees hain. [Q5]\n● PAC aur Committee on Public Undertakings dono CAG reports examine kar sakte hain; isi wajah se\nsource Q25 mein A aur C dono correct marked hain. [Q25]\n● PAC aur Committee on Public Undertakings mein Rajya Sabha members associated hote hain, jabki\nEstimates Committee only Lok Sabha se banti hai. [Q11, Q20]\n6. Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs & Committee Coordination\n● Source Q11 ke teeno statements correct hain: PAC/COPU mein Rajya Sabha members hote hain;\nMinistry of Parliamentary Affairs Cabinet Committee ke direction mein kaam karti hai; aur Minister of\nParliamentary Affairs MPs ko various government committees/councils/boards/commissions mein\nnominate karta hai. [Q11]\n● Railway Zones ke MPs ke Consultative Committees Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs constitute karti hai.\n[Q30]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Committees Full Mind Map\n7. Ethics Committee — Origin, Complaints & Sub-judice Rule\n● Lok Sabha Ethics Committee pehli baar 16 May 2000 ko 13th Lok Sabha mein constituted hui; pehle ad-\nhoc rahi aur 2015 mein permanent part bani. [Q27]\n● Unethical conduct ki complaint sirf MP tak limited nahi: any person complaint kar sakta hai, lekin non-\nmember complaint ko ek member ke through forward hona chahiye. Committee sub-judice matter nahi\nleti. [Q27]\n8. Other Standing / Departmental Committees & Jurisdiction\n● Source ke mutabik minorities ke welfare ke liye Parliamentary Committee set up nahi ki gayi; instead\nMinority Commission set up hua. [Q28]\n● Committee on Social Justice & Empowerment, Urban Development aur Labour Lok Sabha jurisdiction\nmein; Health & Family Welfare committee Rajya Sabha jurisdiction mein di gayi hai. [Q29]\n● India mein 24 Department Related Standing Committees both Houses ke members ke saath respective\ndepartments ke regulators ka working review kar sakti hain; Parliament ad-hoc committees bhi bana\nsakta hai. Finance Commission, FSLRC aur NITI Aayog ko source ne is review role se exclude kiya hai.\n[Q36]\n9. Committee on Subordinate Legislation — Delegated Powers\n● Committee on Subordinate Legislation check karti hai ki Constitution/Parliament se Executive ko\ndelegated regulations, rules, sub-rules aur bye-laws banane ki powers proper scope ke andar exercise\nho rahi hain ya nahi. [Q34]\n● Rules aur regulations banane ki delegated Executive power se related Parliamentary Committee =\nCommittee on Subordinate Legislation; source ke mutabik ye dono Houses mein present hai. [Q35]\n10. Joint Parliamentary Committee (JPC) — 2G Spectrum Case\n● 2G spectrum issue probe ke liye JPC mein 30 MPs the — 20 Lok Sabha + 10 Rajya Sabha. [Q32]\n● 2G Scam examine karne wali JPC ke Chairman P.C. Chacko the; report then Lok Sabha Speaker Meira\nKumar ko submit ki gayi. [Q33]\n11. 18th Lok Sabha Committee Chairpersons (2024–25) & Exam Traps\n● Source current-affairs item (2024–25): Sanjay Jaiswal Committee on Estimates ke Chairperson aur\nBaijayant Panda Committee on Public Undertakings ke Chairperson the; isliye source pair Baijayant\nPanda–Estimates ko incorrect mark karta hai. [Q31]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Committees Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — CAG Report — More Than One Correct\n⚠\nQ25 mein CAG audit report ko PAC ke saath Committee on Public Undertakings bhi examine karti hai. Isliye\nsource ne A & C dono correct diye hain; single-answer assumption se galti ho sakti hai. [Q25]\n EXAM TRAP — “Not a Standing Committee” — Disputed Source Question\n⚠\nQ26 ke source explanation ke mutabik Estimates Committee, PAC, Committee on Public Undertakings aur\nCommittee on Welfare of SCs/STs — sab standing committees hain. Isliye given options mein koi valid “not\nstanding” answer nahi; source ne question disputed mark kiya hai. [Q26]\n EXAM TRAP — PAC Report — Speaker vs Parliament vs Lok Sabha\n⚠\nQ13–Q15 wording alag hai: report Parliament ko submit, Speaker ko submit, aur Lok Sabha mein present —\nsource in teen formulations ko alag questions mein use karta hai. Exam mein exact wording dekho. [Q13, Q14,\nQ15]\n EXAM TRAP — 2024–25 Chairpersons — Time-sensitive Source Fact\n⚠\nQ31 ek 18th Lok Sabha 2024–25 current-affairs item hai. Is mind map mein source ka fact exactly preserve\nkiya gaya hai; ise static constitutional rule na samjho. [Q31]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0276","t":"26 Parliamentary Acts","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Acts Full Mind Map\n PARLIAMENTARY ACTS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚖️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Food Adulteration & Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955\n2. Social & Historical Acts — Key Years and Matches\n3. SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 — Core Framework\n4. SC/ST Act — Courts, Bail, Investigation & Rules\n5. Right to Information Act, 2005 — Timeline, Nature & Objectives\n6. RTI — Information Commissions, Powers & Important Cases\n7. Citizen Charter & Forest Rights Act, 2006\n8. NGT, Land Acquisition & Code on Wages\n9. Important Acts — Year Matching & Chronology\n10. Disaster Management & Lockdown Legal Basis\n11. Environment, Biodiversity, Wildlife & Farmers’ Rights\n12. Aadhaar Act — Identity, Data & Welfare\n13. IT Act, RTE Act & National Food Security Act\n14. Consumer Protection — Rights & District Commission\n15. Exam Traps — Multiple Correct / Disputed / Updated Rules\n1. Food Adulteration & Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955\n● Prevention of Food Adulteration Act 1954 mein enact hua aur source ke mutabik 1 June 1955 se\neffective hua. [Q1]\n● Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 ke offences cognizable aur summarily triable hain; source Q4 inhe\nnon-compoundable bhi batata hai, aur Q5 imprisonment + fine dono punishment modes note karta hai.\n[Q2, Q4, Q5]\n● Act ke offences ki trial first-class Judicial Magistrates/Special Courts kar sakte hain; UP context mein\nCJM/Judicial Magistrate courts designated Special Courts bataye gaye hain. [Q3]\n● Section 5: untouchability ke ground par public hospital/dispensary/educational institution mein admission\nrefuse karna punishable. Section 10A: collective fine impose karne ki power State Government ko. [Q6,\nQ7]\n● Section 1(2) ke according Act poore India tak extend karta hai; source ise preaching/practice of\nuntouchability aur usse arising disabilities ko punish karne wala law batata hai. [Q8, Q9]\n● Section 14 offences by companies se related hai; offence ke waqt company affairs ke responsible\nDirector/Manager/Secretary ko guilty maana ja sakta hai. [Q10, Q11]\n● Section 12: Scheduled Caste member ke relation mein offence ho to court, contrary prove hone tak,\nuntouchability ground presume kar sakta hai. Source Q13 same social group wali situation ko exception\nke roop mein deta hai. [Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Section 14A good-faith action ko protection deta hai — Central/State Government ke good-faith acts par\nsuit/prosecution ka protection. [Q15]\n2. Social & Historical Acts — Key Years and Matches\n● Urban local bodies mein women reservation 74th Constitutional Amendment se linked hai, 73rd se nahi\n— source isi mismatch ko incorrect pair batata hai. [Q16]\n● Source act-year match: Indian Arms Act—1878; Royal Title Act—1876; Indian High Court Act—1861;\nIndian Divorce Act—1869. [Q17]\n● Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005 Parliament ne enact kiya; source ke mutabik 26\nOctober 2006 se force mein aaya. [Q18]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Acts Full Mind Map\n● MISA 1971 internal security law tha aur 1977 mein repeal hua; source ise “Social Act” category ka nahi\nmaanta. [Q19]\n● Criminal Tribes Act pehli baar 1871 mein British Government ne enact kiya; initially Northern India mein\nenforce hua aur baad mein Bengal tak extend hua. [Q20]\n3. SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 — Core Framework\n● SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 ko President ki assent 11 September 1989 ko mili aur 30\nJanuary 1990 se force mein aaya. [Q21, Q22]\n● Source ke mutabik Act mein 23 sections hain; Section 23(1) Central Government ko Official Gazette\nnotification se rules banane ki power deta hai. [Q23, Q24]\n● “Economic boycott” Section 2(bc) mein defined hai. Public servant Section 3 offence kare to minimum\npunishment one year imprisonment batayi gayi hai. [Q25, Q26]\n● Section 14 Special Court/Exclusive Special Court aur speedy trial se related hai. State Government, High\nCourt Chief Justice ki concurrence se district Court of Session ko Special Court specify kar sakti hai.\n[Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Special Court ke judgment/sentence/order ke against High Court mein facts aur law dono par appeal lie\nkarti hai. [Q30]\n● Source Act ko Doctrine of Protective Discrimination aur Article 15(4) ke advancement framework se link\nkarta hai. [Q31]\n4. SC/ST Act — Courts, Bail, Investigation & Rules\n● Section 16 ke under collective fine impose/realise karne ki power State Government ko; Section 8\nprosecution mein abetment, common intention aur common object ke presumptions se linked hai. [Q32,\nQ33]\n● Section 6 certain IPC provisions ko apply karta hai, including Section 34, specified chapters, Section 149\netc. Source ke section-list ko exam matching ke liye yaad rakho. [Q34]\n● 2016 Amendment Rules ke source-note ke mutabik investigation/charge-sheet framework 60 days se\nlinked hai; old 1995 rule 30 days investigation ka reference deta tha. [Q35]\n● Anticipatory bail barred hai; Section 18 expressly CrPC Section 438 ko Act offences par inapplicable\nbatata hai. [Q36, Q37]\n● 1995 Rules ke according investigation officer Deputy Superintendent of Police se below rank ka nahi\nhona chahiye. [Q38]\n● Specified Special Court ko police ke alawa kisi person ko “extra investigation” authorize karne ki power\nsource nahi deta; collective fine impose karna bhi Special Court ka power nahi, State Government ka\nhai. [Q39, Q40]\n● Source Q41 defence issue ko multiple-correct batata hai aur revised key mein bonus marks ka note deta\nhai. Q42 witchcraft allegation par SC/ST member ko physical harm/mental agony dene par 6 months se\n5 years + fine punishment batata hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● “Exclusive Special Court” Section 2(1)(bd) definition se linked hai. Rules 1995: Section 17 district-level\nvigilance & monitoring committee; Section 18 annual-report material. [Q43, Q44, Q45]\n5. Right to Information Act, 2005 — Timeline, Nature & Objectives\n● RTI Bill Lok Sabha 11 May 2005 aur Rajya Sabha 12 May 2005 se pass hua; Presidential assent 15\nJune 2005 aur source ke mutabik 120 days baad 12 October 2005 se force mein aaya. [Q46, Q47]\n● RTI Act timely government information access ka legal right deta hai. Source Supreme Court decisions\nko freedom of thought/expression se RTI link karta hai, lekin Constitution mein RTI explicitly mentioned\nnahi batata. [Q48, Q49]\n● Source ke according RTI Preamble mein Transparency of Information, Revelation of Information,\nInformed Citizenry aur Paramountcy of the democratic ideal — chaaron terms mentioned hain. [Q50]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Acts Full Mind Map\n● Basic objectives: citizens ko empower karna, transparency/accountability promote karna, corruption\ntackle karna aur democracy ko people-oriented banana; women/weaker sections empowerment explicit\nobjective nahi diya gaya. [Q51]\n6. RTI — Information Commissions, Powers & Important Cases\n● Section 6(2): applicant ko information maangne ka reason/personal details dene ki zarurat nahi. Source\nQ52 note karta hai ki 2019 amendment ke baad tenure framework aur J&K applicability badal chuki hai,\nisliye old options outdated ho sakte hain. [Q52]\n● Section 18 Information Commissions ke powers/functions; Section 19 appeal; Section 25 implementation\nreport; Section 12 CIC constitution se related hai. [Q53]\n● Section 20 ke under Central ya State Information Commission penalty impose kar sakta hai. CIC 12\nOctober 2005 se constituted bataya gaya hai. [Q54, Q55]\n● Source Q56 amended tenure ko Government-notified framework mein “3 years or 65 years” batata hai\naur given options ko current rule se mismatch/disputed mark karta hai. [Q56]\n● State Chief/State Information Commissioner appointment Governor karta hai committee recommendation\npar: CM + Leader of Opposition + Cabinet Minister; Chief Justice of High Court member nahi. [Q57]\n● State Information Commissioners eminent public-life persons ho sakte hain, par MP ya State/UT\nLegislature member nahi ho sakte. [Q58]\n● MKSS (Aruna Roy, Nikhil Dey, Shankar Singh etc.; source founding year 1990) RTI people’s movement\nse associated hai. Namit Sharma v. Union of India (2012) RTI-related case hai. [Q59, Q60]\n● Assertion–Reason item mein source dono statements true maanta hai, par Reason ko Assertion ka\ncorrect explanation nahi. Section 2 framing mein RTI = public officials ke control wali information tak\naccess. [Q61, Q62]\n● Source Madras High Court decision ko applicant se purpose/reason disclose karne wala batata hai,\nsaath hi note karta hai ki RTI Act mein aisi obligation mentioned nahi. [Q63]\n7. Citizen Charter & Forest Rights Act, 2006\n● Citizen Charter ke source-listed 9 elements mein service standards, openness/full information,\nconsultation, access/choice, fairness, grievance correction, effective resources, innovation aur other\nproviders ke saath work included hain; agency work inspection basic element nahi. [Q64]\n● Forest Rights Act, 2006 ke national implementation ka nodal agency Ministry dealing with Tribal Affairs\nbataya gaya hai. [Q65]\n● Section 6(1) ke according Gram Sabha individual/community forest rights ki nature aur extent determine\nkarne ki process initiate karti hai. [Q66]\n8. NGT, Land Acquisition & Code on Wages\n● NGT Act 2010 ko source healthy environment ko Article 21 ke Right to Life ke part ke roop mein link\nkarta hai. NGT 18 October 2010 ko establish hua. [Q67, Q68]\n● NGT decision ke against Supreme Court appeal 90 days ke andar ki ja sakti hai; source NGT ki self-\nreview power bhi note karta hai. [Q69]\n● Land Acquisition Act 1894 British-era law tha, land reform promote karna iska purpose nahi; source ise\n2013 Fair Compensation/Transparency/Rehabilitation/Resettlement Act se replaced batata hai. [Q70]\n● Code on Wages 2019: Payment of Wages Act 1936, Minimum Wages Act 1948, Payment of Bonus Act\n1965 aur Equal Remuneration Act 1976 ko replace/merge karta hai; Contract Labour Act included nahi.\n[Q71]\n9. Important Acts — Year Matching & Chronology\n● Act-year source match: Companies Act—2013; Indian Contract Act—1872 (not 1870); Partnership Act—\n1932; Sale of Goods Act—1930. [Q72]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Acts Full Mind Map\n● Preventing Seditious Meetings Act ka source year 1907 deta hai, 1908 nahi. [Q73]\n● Chronology: Lex-Loci Act 1850 → Bengal Tenancy Act 1885 → Age of Consent Act 1891 → Indian\nUniversity Act 1907. [Q74]\n● Official Secrets Act 1923 Section 6 unauthorized uniform use se linked; Section 7 police/military officer\nko knowingly mislead/interfere karne se. Celebratory gunfire endangering safety Arms (Amendment) Act\n2019 se linked — source mein pairs 1 & 3 correct. [Q75]\n10. Disaster Management & Lockdown Legal Basis\n● Disaster Management Act Parliament ne 2005 mein pass kiya; Presidential assent 23 December 2005 ko\nbatayi gayi hai. [Q76, Q77]\n● National Disaster Management Authority ka ex-officio Chairman Prime Minister of India hai. [Q78]\n● COVID lockdown ke extraordinary powers ka legal basis source Disaster Management Act 2005 +\nEpidemic Diseases Act 1897 dono ko batata hai. [Q79]\n11. Environment, Biodiversity, Wildlife & Farmers’ Rights\n● Forest Conservation Act 1980 mein enact hua aur source ke mutabik 25 October 1980 se effective hua.\n[Q80]\n● Biological Diversity (Amendment) Act 2023 ko President assent aur Official Gazette publication — dono 3\nAugust 2023 bataye gaye hain. [Q81]\n● Community Reserve item mein source: declaration State Government karti hai; management Community\nReserve Management Committee; hunting prohibited; sustainable non-timber forest produce allowed;\nhabitat-altering traditional agriculture restricted — statements 2 & 3 correct. [Q82]\n● Protection of Plant Varieties and Farmers’ Rights Act source ke mutabik 2001 mein enact hua, plant\nvarieties aur farmers/plant breeders rights protection ke liye. [Q83]\n12. Aadhaar Act — Identity, Data & Welfare\n● Source Supreme Court context: Aadhaar authentication data 3 months nahi, 6 months se beyond retain\nnahi; private corporations ke Aadhaar ecosystem use/share par restriction; insurance KYC ke liye\nAadhaar mandatory nahi; Consolidated Fund-funded welfare schemes mein Aadhaar ko\nlegitimate/mandatory framework se link kiya. [Q84]\n● Aadhaar Act Section 9 ke according Aadhaar identity proof hai, citizenship/domicile proof nahi. Source\nSection 23(g) ke under issuing authority ko Aadhaar number deactivate/omit karne ki possibility batata\nhai. [Q85]\n13. IT Act, RTE Act & National Food Security Act\n● IT Act 2000 e-governance matching: electronic records legal recognition—Section 4; electronic\nsignatures—Section 5; government/agencies use—Section 6; electronic gazette publication—Section 8.\n[Q86]\n● RTE Act 2009 Section 23(1): teacher minimum qualifications Central Government-authorised academic\nauthority lay down karti hai, State Council nahi. Primary teaching ke liye NCTE guidelines ke according\nTET pass karna required; source answer only statement 2 ko correct rakhta hai. [Q87]\n● National Food Security Act 2013 Section 16 ke under State Food Commission establish hota hai. [Q88]\n14. Consumer Protection — Rights & District Commission\n● Consumer rights item: consumer food testing ke liye samples le sakta hai; complaint file karne par small\nfee hoti hai; consumer ki death par legal heir complaint file kar sakta hai — source statements 1 & 3\ncorrect maanta hai. [Q89]\n● Consumer Protection (Jurisdiction) Rules 2021 source ke mutabik District Commission jurisdiction value\nup to 50 lakh; State Government ek district mein more than one District Commission establish kar sakti\n₹"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parliamentary Acts Full Mind Map\nhai; source Q90 mein given substantive statements ko correct maan kar “None incorrect” answer deta\nhai. [Q90]\n● Historical 1986 Act context mein District Forum jurisdiction 20 lakh tak thi; source note karta hai ki\n₹\nupdated 2021 rules mein 50 lakh limit hai.\n₹\n [Q91]\n15. Exam Traps — Multiple Correct / Disputed / Updated Rules\n EXAM TRAP — PCR Act — Multiple Correct Options\n⚠\nQ4 mein source A & B dono ko correct (cognizable + summarily triable; cognizable + non-compoundable) mark\nkarta hai. Q5 mein A & D dono correct (cognizable; imprisonment + fine). [Q4, Q5]\n EXAM TRAP — SC/ST Investigation — 30 Days vs 60 Days\n⚠\nOld 1995 Rules 30-day investigation reference dete the; source 2016 Amendment Rules ke baad 60-day\ncharge-sheet framework note karta hai aur commission option ko wrong/disputed batata hai. [Q35]\n EXAM TRAP — SC/ST Defence — Multiple Correct\n⚠\nQ41 source revised key mein more than one answer aur bonus marks ka note deta hai; isliye ise single-answer\nrule ki tarah memorize mat karo. [Q41]\n EXAM TRAP — RTI — Outdated / Amended Questions\n⚠\nQ52 post-2019 tenure/J&K changes ki wajah se multiple old options ko outdated batata hai. Q56 mein source\ncurrent tenure framing ko given options se mismatch batata hai. [Q52, Q56]\n EXAM TRAP — RTI Reason Requirement — Source Tension\n⚠\nQ63 Madras High Court decision reason disclose karne ki baat karta hai, lekin source saath hi clear karta hai ki\nRTI Act khud aisi obligation mention nahi karta. [Q63]\n EXAM TRAP — Consumer Jurisdiction — Old vs Updated\n⚠\nQ90 2021 Rules ke 50 lakh framework par based hai, jabki Q91 original Consumer Protection Act 1986 ke 20\n₹\n₹\n\nlakh district limit ko test karta hai. Exam mein question-year/context pehle dekho. [Q90, Q91]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0277","t":"27 The Supreme Court","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n THE SUPREME COURT — FULL MIND MAP\n⚖️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Foundation, Article 124 & Judge Strength\n2. Judges — Qualification, Appointment, Removal & Independence\n3. Collegium, NJAC, Ad hoc Judges & Constitution Bench\n4. Original Jurisdiction, Court of Record & Contempt\n5. Basic Structure & Landmark Constitutional Cases\n6. Appellate, Curative, Review & Article 142 Powers\n7. Judicial Review, Due Process & Guardian of Constitution\n8. Enlarged / Advisory Jurisdiction, Oath & Case Transfer\n9. Important Supreme Court Cases — Quick Match\n10. CJI & Judges — Important Personalities / Chronology\n11. PIL & Judicial Activism\n12. Important Judgments, Social Issues & Court Language\n13. Exam Traps — Disputed / Source-Specific Questions\n1. Foundation, Article 124 & Judge Strength\n● Supreme Court ka inauguration 28 January 1950 ko hua; source ise Indian Constitution se established\ninstitution batata hai aur kehta hai ki isne Government of India Act, 1935 ke Federal Court ko succeed\nkiya. [Q1, Q2]\n● 1945 Sapru Committee (Sir Tej Bahadur Sapru) ne higher-judiciary appointments par recommendations\ndi; source saath hi Constituent Assembly ke 1947 Ad hoc Supreme Court Committee ka bhi zikr karta\nhai. [Q3]\n● Article 124 Supreme Court ki establishment/constitution se linked hai. Judges ki sanctioned strength\nbadhane ki power Parliament ke paas hai. [Q4]\n● Source timeline: original Court = CJI + 7 puisne judges; later strength 11 (1956), 14 (1960), 18 (1978), 26\n(1986), 31 (2009), aur 2019 amendment ke baad total 34 (CJI + 33). [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n2. Judges — Qualification, Appointment, Removal & Independence\n● Article 124(3): candidate Indian citizen ho; 5 saal High Court judge, ya 10 saal High Court advocate, ya\nPresident ki opinion mein distinguished jurist ho sakta hai. [Q8]\n● Supreme Court judges President appoint karta hai warrant under hand and seal se; source Article 124(2)\nconsultation framework aur judge other than CJI ke case mein CJI consultation ko highlight karta hai.\n[Q9, Q23]\n● Judge resignation President ko addressed writing se hota hai. [Q10, Q11]\n● Removal Article 124(4): President ka order, lekin dono Houses ka address required — total membership\nka majority + present-and-voting ka at least 2/3; grounds = proved misbehaviour or incapacity. Judges\n(Inquiry) Act, 1968 process detail karta hai; Speaker motion reject kar sakta hai, aur Constitution\ngrounds ko define nahi karta. [Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Supreme Court judge retirement age 65 years hai; salary Parliament law se determine karta hai, aur\ninterim specification Second Schedule se linked hai. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Autonomy safeguards: appointment consultation, salaries Consolidated Fund of India par charged/non-\nvotable, aur Court staff appointments mein CJI ka role. Source Q19 yaad dilata hai ki Parliament Article\n138 se jurisdiction enlarge kar sakta hai aur High Court administrative expenses State Consolidated\nFund se linked hote hain. [Q18, Q19]\n● Retired Supreme Court judge India ke kisi Court/authority ke saamne plead/act nahi kar sakta (Article\n124(7)). Acting CJI ko President Article 126 ke under appoint karta hai. [Q20, Q21, Q22]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n3. Collegium, NJAC, Ad hoc Judges & Constitution Bench\n● Collegium system source ke mutabik 1993 Second Judges Case se evolve hua; Supreme Court\ncollegium = CJI + 4 senior-most judges. Ye Parliament-made system nahi hai. [Q24, Q25, Q26]\n● NJAC (99th Constitutional Amendment, 2014) mein CJI chairperson, next two senior SC judges, Union\nLaw Minister aur two eminent persons ka framework tha; source notes Supreme Court ne 2015 mein ise\nunconstitutional strike down kiya aur collegium continue hua. [Q27]\n● Second Administrative Reforms Commission ne higher-court appointments mein Executive, Legislature\naur CJI ki participation recommend ki — source framing. [Q28]\n● Supreme Court mein ad hoc judges Article 127 ke under ho sakte hain; Additional Judges ka provision\nSC mein nahi. Quorum unavailable ho to CJI, President ki previous consent ke saath qualified High\nCourt judge ko ad hoc judge ke roop mein request kar sakta hai. [Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● Article 128 ke under CJI, President ki previous consent se retired SC/qualified HC judge ko sit-and-act ke\nliye request kar sakta hai; source High Courts ke review power ko bhi Court-of-record status se jodta\nhai. [Q32]\n● Constitution interpretation/substantial constitutional question ke liye minimum 5 judges ki bench —\nConstitutional Bench. [Q33, Q34]\n4. Original Jurisdiction, Court of Record & Contempt\n● Article 131 original jurisdiction: Union vs State(s), ya State vs State disputes. Source explicitly election\ndisputes aur Union Territory disputes ko is Article 131 original jurisdiction se bahar rakhta hai. [Q35, Q36,\nQ37, Q38]\n● Fundamental-right writ power Supreme Court ka exclusive nahi — Article 32 SC ke saath High Courts\nArticle 226 se writs issue kar sakte hain. [Q39]\n● Source Q40 Armed Forces Tribunal Act, 2007 ke context mein Court Martial appeals Supreme Court tak\nja sakne ko note karta hai. [Q40]\n● Article 129: Supreme Court Court of Record hai — judgments/proceedings permanent evidentiary record\naur contempt punish karne ki power. Article 215 High Courts ko bhi Court of Record banata hai. [Q41,\nQ42, Q43]\n● H.N. Sanyal Committee recommendations se Contempt of Courts Act, 1971 linked hai; Constitution\ncontempt define nahi karta, Act karta hai; Parliament contempt law bana sakta hai. [Q44]\n● Article 130: Supreme Court Delhi mein sit karta hai; CJI President ki approval se other place(s) appoint\nkar sakta hai. [Q45]\n5. Basic Structure & Landmark Constitutional Cases\n● Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973) mein Basic Structure doctrine enunciate/propound hua;\nParliament amendment se Constitution ka basic structure damage/destroy nahi kar sakta — source\nsummary. [Q46, Q47]\n● Source Articles 32, 226 aur 227 ke judicial-review powers ko Constitution ka inviolable basic structure\nbatata hai. [Q48]\n● Basic Structure Theory ka source = Judicial Interpretation; source Minerva Mills (1980) ko later approval\nke roop mein cite karta hai. [Q49]\n● Largest bench source ke mutabik Kesavananda Bharati = 13 judges; second-largest Golaknath v. State\nof Punjab (1967) = 11 judges. Golaknath se source Fundamental Rights wali quoted proposition jodta\nhai. [Q50, Q51]\n● Case-match trap: Bella Banerjee = West Bengal Land Development and Planning Act/property context;\nManeka Gandhi (1978) = right to travel abroad/personal liberty. Source Q52 mein option (d) pair\nincorrect tha. [Q52]\n● Quick jurisdiction map: Article 131 original; Articles 132–136 appellate; Article 143 advisory. Collegium,\nappellate aur original jurisdiction — tino Supreme Court se concerned hain. [Q53, Q54]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n6. Appellate, Curative, Review & Article 142 Powers\n● Constitutional-case appeals ke liye Article 132; Article 134A certificate for appeal se linked. Constitution\ninterpretation cases Supreme Court tak appellate jurisdiction se aa sakte hain. [Q55, Q56]\n● Curative Petition concept Rupa Ashok Hurra v. Ashok Hurra (2002) se evolved; source ise Article 142 ke\nunder Supreme Court curative remedy se link karta hai. [Q57]\n● Article 137 Supreme Court ko apne judgment/order review karne ki power deta hai, subject to Parliament\nlaw aur Article 145 rules. [Q58, Q59, Q60]\n● Article 142: Supreme Court pending cause/matter mein complete justice ke liye decree/order pass kar\nsakta hai; source ordinary-law limitations ko is constitutional power par prohibition na maanne wala point\ntest karta hai. [Q61]\n7. Judicial Review, Due Process & Guardian of Constitution\n● Judicial Review = Judiciary ka power to interpret Constitution aur unconstitutional legislative/executive\nlaw/order ko invalid declare karna. [Q62, Q63, Q64]\n● Basic Structure ki textual definition Constitution mein nahi; source Article 13 ko judicial review se jodta\nhai. Judicial Review power Supreme Court aur High Courts dono enjoy karte hain. [Q65, Q66]\n● High Courts central law ko unconstitutional declare kar sakte hain; Supreme Court constitutional\namendment ko basic structure violate karne par question kar sakta hai — isliye source ke dono contrary\nstatements false hain. [Q67]\n● Judicial Review ka origin source USA batata hai; UK mein parliamentary supremacy ke contrast ka use\nkarta hai. India mein source assertion ke mutabik scope limited hai, lekin “bag of borrowing” us limitation\nka explanation nahi. [Q68, Q69]\n● Due Process of Law source ke mutabik arbitrariness/irrationality-free procedure aur\nfairness/reasonableness se linked hai; Judicial Review ko “procedure established by law” base se joda\ngaya. Q72 source judicial process ko procedure, Constitution, conventions aur routine-law due process\nsabse link karta hai. [Q70, Q71, Q72]\n● Source Q73 ke framing mein constitutional amendment unconstitutional ho sakta hai jab equality right ko\nPart III se remove karke elsewhere shift kare; is item ko source-specific proposition ke roop mein yaad\nrakho. [Q73]\n● Supreme Court ko highest judicial court, federal court, Fundamental Rights protector, Constitution ka\nfinal interpreter/guardian/custodian bataya gaya hai. [Q74, Q75, Q76, Q77, Q78, Q79]\n● Central laws ki constitutional validity par SC exclusive nahi — High Courts bhi review kar sakte hain.\nFundamental Rights enforcement SC Article 32 aur HC Article 226 dono ke jurisdiction mein; Article 32\nSC ka direct safeguard hai. [Q80, Q81, Q82]\n8. Enlarged / Advisory Jurisdiction, Oath & Case Transfer\n● Article 138: Parliament law se Union List matters mein Supreme Court ki additional jurisdiction/powers\nenlarge kar sakta hai. [Q83, Q84]\n● Article 143 President ko Supreme Court se law/fact of public importance par advisory opinion seek karne\nka right deta hai; source appointment/transfer of judges reference ko bhi Article 143(1) context mein\nrakhta hai. [Q85, Q86]\n● Advisory-jurisdiction source points: President reference karta hai; full bench hears; Article 143(1) mein\nCourt opinion dene ko always bound nahi, aur opinion Government par binding nahi. Court suo motu\nadvice nahi deta. [Q87, Q88, Q89, Q90]\n● 2002 Gujarat Assembly election deferral controversy par President Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam ka Supreme\nCourt reference source Article 143 se link karta hai. [Q91]\n● Third Schedule mein Supreme Court/High Court judges ke oath forms hain; given oath form CJI/SC\njudges se linked hai. [Q92]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n● Article 139A: Supreme Court specified circumstances mein cases transfer kar sakta hai — SC/HCs mein\nsame substantial questions of law pending ho to. [Q93]\n9. Important Supreme Court Cases — Quick Match\n● Case match: A.K. Gopalan = preventive detention procedure; Romesh Thapar = free-speech restrictions;\nShankari Prasad = Parliament amendment power; Champakam Dorairajan = educational-admission\nequality. [Q94]\n● Source Q95 Kameshwar Singh, Ramesh Thaper, Motilal aur State of West Bengal v. Subodh Gopal —\nsabko zamindari/property-rights disputes se related batata hai. [Q95]\n● Indra Sawhney v. Union of India (1992): source 27% OBC reservation uphold aur reservation 50% se\nexceed na karne wala principle note karta hai. [Q96]\n● Illegal Migrants (Determination by Tribunals) Act, 1983 ko source 13 July 2005 judgment mein Article 355\ncontext ke under unconstitutional batata hai. [Q97]\n● TDSAT orders telecom/broadcasting/airport-tariff matters mein substantial question of law par Supreme\nCourt appeal se linked; source cyber matters ke liye High Court appeal mention karta hai. [Q98]\n10. CJI & Judges — Important Personalities / Chronology\n● Shortest-serving CJI: Kamal Narain Singh — source dates 25 Nov 1991 to 12 Dec 1991, 17 days. [Q99]\n● Chronology among given names: H.L. Dattu (2014–15) → T.S. Thakur (2015–17) → Jagdish Singh\nKhehar (2017). [Q100]\n● Y.V. Chandrachud: 16th CJI, 22 Feb 1978–11 Jul 1985; source calls him longest-serving CJI and notes\nappointment by President Neelam Sanjiva Reddy. [Q101]\n● Justice M. Fathima Beevi: first woman SC judge (1989), first Muslim woman in higher judiciary; source\ncorrects Governor as Tamil Nadu (1997–2001), not Kerala. Q104 also identifies her as India’s first\nwoman SC judge. [Q102, Q104]\n● A.S. Anand was 29th CJI (10 Oct 1998–31 Oct 2001). Gyan Sudha Mishra became fourth woman SC\njudge on 30 April 2010. [Q103, Q105]\n● Justice L. Nageswara Rao source ke mutabik High Court judge bane bina directly Bar se SC elevated\nhue (7th such person). [Q106]\n● Justice N. Kotiswar Singh SC appointment (July 2024) se pehle J&K and Ladakh High Court ke Chief\nJustice the; oath 18 July 2024 — source date. [Q107]\n● Source personality traps: Justice S.K. Jha listed MP High Court CJs mein SC judge nahi bane; Justice\nR.C. Lahoti Rajasthan High Court judge nahi rahe. [Q108, Q109]\n11. PIL & Judicial Activism\n● PIL India mein Supreme Court judicial initiative se develop hua, mainly Justice P.N. Bhagwati aur Justice\nV.R. Krishna Iyer se associated. V.R. Krishna Iyer CJI nahi rahe — source explicitly corrects this. [Q111,\nQ112]\n● PIL = Public Interest Litigation; High Court Article 226 aur Supreme Court Article 32 dono mein file ho\nsakta hai. [Q113, Q114]\n● Public-minded citizen person/group/society ke behalf mein justice seek kar sakta hai jab affected person\nCourt reach na kar paaye — source Assertion–Reason dono correct aur R explains A batata hai. [Q115]\n● PIL concept/term ka origin source United States mein batata hai. [Q116, Q117]\n● Judicial Activism India mein PIL se closely linked; source mid-1970s SC initiative mention karta hai.\nJustice A.S. Anand ka caution: judicial activism “judicial adventurism” na bane. [Q118, Q119]\n12. Important Judgments, Social Issues & Court Language\n● 23 September 2003 source judgment: Supreme Court ne women ko girls’ government college principal\nappointment mein preference ko Articles 14, 15, 16 violation nahi maana. [Q120]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n● Vishakha v. State of Rajasthan: workplace sexual-harassment guidelines (1997); source notes 2013\nworkplace sexual-harassment Act ne guidelines supersede ki. [Q121]\n● Shayara Bano case (2017): source Triple Talaq/Talaq-e-Biddat ko unconstitutional aur Article 14 equality\ncontext se link karta hai. [Q122]\n● “Caged Parrot” remark source Coal Gate allocation scam ke CBI context se jodta hai. [Q123]\n● Homosexuality judgment source Section 377 IPC se related batata hai. [Q124]\n● Article 348(1)(a): Supreme Court aur High Courts ki proceedings English language mein — source\nframing. [Q125]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Supreme Court Full Mind Map\n13. Exam Traps — Disputed / Source-Specific Questions\n EXAM TRAP — Judge Strength — Old Options vs Source’s 2019 Strength\n⚠\nQ5–Q7 ke options/time-frame purane hain. Source current/recent reference mein Supreme Court (Number of\nJudges) Amendment Act, 2019 ke baad total 34 (CJI + 33) batata hai; Q7 ke 2008 Cabinet context mein\nhistorical answer 30 other judges (total 31) tha. In questions ko date-sensitive/disputed maana gaya hai. [Q5,\nQ6, Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — PIL Introduction — CJI Name\n⚠\nQ110 mein source ke mutabik Hussainara Khatoon PIL development 1979 se linked hai; us waqt CJI Y.V.\nChandrachud the, jabki P.N. Bhagwati 1985 mein CJI bane. Isliye given options mein appropriate answer nahi\ntha. [Q110]\n EXAM TRAP — Court of Record — Primary Option Nuance\n⚠\nQ41 source kehta hai Court of Record ke do implications hain: permanent evidentiary record aur contempt\npunish power. UPPSC key ne “record” aspect ko primary option maana. Exam mein wording/options dekhkar\nchoose karo. [Q41]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0278","t":"28 The Governor","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governor Full Mind Map\n THE GOVERNOR — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Constitutional Position — Why a Nominated Governor?\n2. Appointment & Qualifications — Articles 155 & 157\n3. Oath of Office — Article 159\n4. Tenure, Pleasure & Removal — Articles 153 & 156\n5. Jammu & Kashmir, Union Territories & Rajpramukh\n6. Salary & Allowances — Consolidated Fund / Common Governor\n7. Discretionary Powers of the Governor\n8. Legislative Powers — Bills & Article 200\n9. Ordinance-Making Power — Article 213\n10. Appointments, Legislature Membership & Pardoning Power\n11. Constitutional Immunities — Article 361\n12. Women Governors & Important Firsts\n13. State-Specific Facts & Sarkaria Commission\n1. Constitutional Position — Why a Nominated Governor?\n● Governor State Government ka constitutional head hota hai; State ki executive actions Governor ke\nnaam par li jaati hain. [Q2]\n● Constituent Assembly ne elected Governor ka original idea drop kiya: extra election expenditure hota,\nelected Governor-CM political friction ho sakta tha, aur Parliamentary System mein Governor ko\nconstitutional head ke roop mein function karna tha. Source ke hisab se statement 'major political issues\npar election' primary constitutional reason nahi maana gaya. [Q1]\n2. Appointment & Qualifications — Articles 155 & 157\n● Article 155: State Governor ko President of India apne hand-and-seal warrant se appoint karta hai. [Q3,\nQ4, Q5]\n● Article 157: Governor banne ke liye Indian citizen hona aur 35 years complete karna zaroori hai.\nCitizenship by birth condition nahi hai. Source Q6 ke mutabik Lok Sabha membership eligibility ko\nseparate mandatory qualification nahi maana gaya. [Q6, Q7]\n● 7th Constitutional Amendment, 1956 ke baad same person ko do ya zyada States ka Governor appoint\nkiya ja sakta hai. [Q6, Q12]\n3. Oath of Office — Article 159\n● Article 159 Governor ki oath/affirmation deal karta hai. Oath High Court ke Chief Justice, aur unki\nabsence mein available senior-most Judge ke saamne hoti hai. [Q8, Q9]\n● Governor ki oath Third Schedule mein nahi di gayi — source isko common exam trap ke roop mein\nexplain karta hai. [Q8]\n4. Tenure, Pleasure & Removal — Articles 153 & 156\n● Article 156(1): Governor President ke pleasure par office hold karta hai; normal term 5 years hai, lekin\nPresident term se pehle remove kar sakta hai. [Q10, Q11, Q13, Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● 5-year term absolute nahi hai: Governor pehle remove ho sakta hai aur term expire hone ke baad bhi\nsuccessor ke office enter karne tak continue kar sakta hai. [Q14]\n● State Legislature Governor ko remove karne ke liye resolution pass karke usse hata nahi sakti;\nConstitution Governor-removal ka legislative procedure lay down nahi karta. [Q13, Q17]\n● Article 153 kehta hai har State ke liye Governor hoga, lekin amended proviso same person ko two or\nmore States ka Governor banne se nahi rokta. [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governor Full Mind Map\n5. Jammu & Kashmir, Union Territories & Rajpramukh\n● Jammu & Kashmir mein pre-1965 executive head 'Sadar-e-Riyasat' tha; State Constitution ke 6th\nAmendment (1965) se nomenclature 'Governor' hua aur President appointment ka model aaya. [Q18, Q19]\n● Source update: 2019 reorganisation ke baad Jammu & Kashmir State wali Governor arrangement\nkhatam hui; Union Territory President ke through appointed Lieutenant Governor se administered hoti\nhai. [Q18]\n● States Reorganisation Commission ki recommendations ke basis par Rajasthan mein Rajpramukh\ninstitution 7th Constitutional Amendment ke through 1 Nov 1956 se abolish hua aur Governor\narrangement aaya. [Q20]\n● Article 239(1): Union Territories ko President, apne appointed Administrator/Lieutenant Governor ke\nthrough administer karta hai (subject to law made by Parliament). [Q21]\n● New UT Jammu & Kashmir ke first Lieutenant Governor Girish Chandra Murmu the; source Manoj Sinha\nko 2nd LG batata hai. Ladakh ke first LG Radha Krishna Mathur the. [Q22, Q23]\n6. Salary & Allowances — Consolidated Fund / Common Governor\n● Governor ki emoluments/allowances aur office-related expenditure State ke Consolidated Fund par\ncharged hote hain; source Article 202(3)(a) cite karta hai. [Q24]\n● Article 158(3A): same person two or more States ka Governor ho to salary/allowances States ke beech\nus proportion mein allocate hote hain jo President order se determine kare. [Q25]\n7. Discretionary Powers of the Governor\n● Discretionary powers mein Article 356 ke liye President ko report bhejna aur Article 200 ke under certain\nBills President ke consideration ke liye reserve karna included hain. [Q26]\n● Ministers ki appointment Chief Minister ki advice par hoti hai aur Article 166(3) ke business rules ko\nsource discretionary power nahi maanta. [Q26]\n● Source ke mutabik Governor majority prove karwa sakta hai, Assembly confidence lose kar chuke CM ko\nterminate kar sakta hai, Bill assent/withhold/reserve/return kar sakta hai; High Court se consultation is\nlist ka authorized power nahi hai. [Q27]\n8. Legislative Powers — Bills & Article 200\n● Article 200: Ordinary Bill (Money Bill ko chhodkar) reconsideration ke liye State Legislature ko return kiya\nja sakta hai. Source ke hisab se 'as soon as possible' ki explicit constitutional time-limit define nahi hai.\n[Q28]\n● Article 200 hi Governor ko Bill par assent dene, assent withhold karne, ya President ke consideration ke\nliye reserve karne ka framework deta hai. [Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● Source Q32 ka point: agar kisi Bill ko introduce karne se pehle Governor recommendation\nconstitutionally required thi lekin recommendation ke bina pass ho gaya, to Governor ka baad ka assent\nus Act ko is ground par invalid nahi banata. [Q32]\n9. Ordinance-Making Power — Article 213\n● Article 213 Governor ko State Legislature ke recess ke dauran Ordinance promulgate karne ki power\ndeta hai. [Q33, Q34, Q36]\n● Ordinance ka State Act jaisa force/effect hota hai; Legislature reassemble hone ke 6 weeks baad cease\nkarta hai unless required approval/continuance framework follow ho. [Q33, Q35]\n10. Appointments, Legislature Membership & Pardoning Power\n● High Court Judges Governor appoint nahi karta; appointment President karta hai consultation process ke\nsaath. State Public Service Commission members aur Advocate General Governor appoint karta hai.\n[Q37]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governor Full Mind Map\n● Governor State Legislature ka integral part hai, aur Legislative Council mein 1/6 members nominate kar\nsakta hai. Article 161 judicial/pardoning powers provide karta hai. [Q38]\n● Source Q39 specifically kehta hai ki Governor death sentence ko pardon nahi kar sakta; source is\ndistinction ko President ki pardoning power se contrast karta hai. [Q39]\n11. Constitutional Immunities — Article 361\n● Article 361(2): Governor ke term ke dauran criminal proceedings institute/continue nahi ki ja sakti. Article\n361(4) ke under civil proceedings prescribed written notice ke 2 months baad possible hain. [Q40, Q41]\n● Article 158(4): Governor ki emoluments aur allowances term ke dauran diminish nahi ki ja sakti. [Q41]\n● Article 74(2) / 163(3) principle: Ministers ne President/Governor ko kya advice di, is question ki Court\ninquiry nahi karegi. [Q42]\n● Governor ke impeachment ka constitutional provision nahi hai; Governor President ke pleasure par office\nhold karta hai. Source note karta hai ki 'impeachment' term Constitution mein strictly President ke liye\nuse hoti hai. [Q43]\n12. Women Governors & Important Firsts\n● Sarojini Naidu independent India mein State ki first woman Governor thi (United Provinces/Uttar\nPradesh); source ke mutabik 1949 mein office mein hi unka death hua. [Q44, Q45]\n● 13 February ko source National Women's Day of India ke roop mein Sarojini Naidu ki birth anniversary\n(13 Feb 1879) se link karta hai. [Q46]\n● Padmaja Naidu West Bengal ki first lady Governor thi (1956-1967), aur Sarla Grewal Madhya Pradesh ki\nfirst woman Governor thi. [Q47, Q48]\n13. State-Specific Facts & Sarkaria Commission\n● M.P. Governor Dr. Bhagwat Dayal Sharma Haryana ke first Chief Minister (1966-67) rahe; source unka\nM.P. Governor tenure 1980-84 aur Odisha Governor tenure 1977-80 deta hai. [Q50]\n● Rajasthan source fact: Rajpramukh institution 1 Nov 1956 se abolished; Gurumukh Nihal Singh ko first\nGovernor of Rajasthan 25 Oct 1956 ko appoint kiya gaya — 1 Nov nahi. [Q51]\n● Source Q52: Raghukul Tilak ko Rajasthan Governor post se Aug 1981 mein dismiss kiya gaya; source\nIndia ke first dismissed Governor ke roop mein Tamil Nadu ke Prabhudas Patwari (Oct 1980) ko note\nkarta hai. [Q52]\n● Question-time matching ke source mein Kalraj Mishra-Rajasthan aur Anandiben Patel-Uttar Pradesh\ncorrect pairs the; West Bengal ke liye C.V. Ananda Bose aur Gujarat ke liye Acharya Devvrat diya gaya\nhai. Ye current-affairs type fact time-sensitive hai. [Q53]\n● Sarkaria Commission Report (1988): Governor eminent person ho, posting State ka resident/political\ninsider na ho, detached figure ho, recent intense political links na ho aur ruling party ka member na ho\n— source ka core recommendation pattern. [Q54]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Governor Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — Articles ka Fast Map\n⚠\n153 = Governor for each State / same person for multiple States allowed; 155 = Appointment; 156 = Term &\nPresident's pleasure; 157 = Qualifications; 158 = Conditions/allowances; 159 = Oath; 200 = Bills; 213 =\nOrdinance; 361 = Immunities. [Q3-Q17, Q24-Q25, Q28-Q36, Q40-Q43]\n EXAM TRAP — J&K — Historical Question ko Current Setup se Mix Mat Karo\n⚠\nQ18-Q19 historical State-era framework explain karte hain: Sadar-e-Riyasat → Governor (1965). Source khud\n2019 reorganisation ke baad J&K ko Union Territory aur LG-administered setup ke roop mein update karta hai.\n[Q18, Q19, Q22]\n EXAM TRAP — Q49 — Disputed Question\n⚠\nSource ke mutabik H.V. Pataskar, K.C. Reddy aur Satyanarayan Sinha Constituent Assembly members the;\nNiranjan Nath Wanchoo member nahi the. Sirf '2' correct banta hai, lekin given combo options mein exact\nanswer nahi tha. [Q49]\n EXAM TRAP — Q53 — Time-Sensitive Governor Pair\n⚠\nYe current-affairs style matching source ke question-time context par based hai. Is mind map mein source ka\nstated pair hi preserve kiya gaya hai; is fact ko timeless constitutional rule na samjho. [Q53]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0279","t":"29 The State Legislature","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The State Legislature Full Mind Map\n THE STATE LEGISLATURE — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. State Legislature Structure — Article 168\n2. Legislative Council — Creation & Abolition (Article 169)\n3. Legislative Council — Composition, Election & Tenure\n4. Bicameral States — Current & Historical Map\n5. Legislative Assembly — Composition, Age, Seats & Elections\n6. Disqualification & Speaker — Articles 179, 191–192\n7. Sessions, Procedure, Quorum & Assembly Business\n8. Assembly in Electoral Colleges\n9. State Finance & Key Article Map\n10. Ordinary Bills, Money Bills & Budget\n11. Chief Minister & Council of Ministers\n12. Chief Ministers & State Administration — Key Facts\n13. State-specific Historical / Current-Affairs Notes\n14. Exam Traps — Source-specific Updates & Exceptions\n1. State Legislature Structure — Article 168\n● Article 168 ke mutabik State Legislature mein Governor + Legislative Assembly hoti hai; jahan Legislative\nCouncil exist karti hai, wahan Governor + Assembly + Council milkar Legislature bante hain. [Q1]\n● Bicameral State mein Legislative Council Upper House aur Legislative Assembly Lower House hoti hai;\nunicameral State mein sirf Legislative Assembly hoti hai. [Q2]\n2. Legislative Council — Creation & Abolition (Article 169)\n● Legislative Council ki composition ka provision Article 171 mein hai, jabki uske creation/abolition ka\nconstitutional route Article 169 deta hai. [Q3, Q7, Q8, Q9]\n● State Legislative Assembly ko resolution total membership ke majority + present and voting members ke\nat least 2/3 majority se pass karna hota hai; uske baad Parliament law bana sakti hai. [Q4, Q6]\n● Vidhan Parishad hi aisa State legislative House hai jo dissolve nahi hota lekin Article 169 ke route se\nabolish kiya ja sakta hai. [Q5]\n● Assembly ka Article 169 resolution Parliament/Union Government ko legislation initiate karne ke liye\nbinding obligation impose nahi karta — source ka specific exam point. [Q10]\n3. Legislative Council — Composition, Election & Tenure\n● Article 171: Council ki total strength State Assembly ki strength ke 1/3 se zyada nahi aur normally 40 se\nkam nahi honi chahiye. Chairman/Deputy Chairman ko Council khud choose karti hai; Governor\nnominate nahi karta. [Q11, Q12]\n● Source ke UP example mein 100-member Council mein 10 Governor-nominated members bataye gaye\nhain; source universal nominated fraction ko fixed nahi maanta aur Article 171(2)/RPA framework ka\nreference deta hai. [Q13, Q14]\n● Legislative Council permanent House hai, dissolve nahi hoti; member ka tenure 6 years aur har 2 saal\n1/3 members retire hote hain. Council ka khud ka “6-year tenure” nahi hota. [Q15, Q17, Q18]\n● Council electoral categories mein local bodies, teachers, graduates aur Legislative Assembly members\naate hain; industrialists designated electoral category nahi hain. [Q16]\n4. Bicameral States — Current & Historical Map"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The State Legislature Full Mind Map\n● Source current list: Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Bihar, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh aur Telangana — 6\nStates with bicameral legislatures. Madhya Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Rajasthan etc. listed questions mein\nCouncil nahi rakhte. [Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23]\n● 1956 reorganisation ke source explanation ke mutabik 14 States mein se 7 bicameral the: UP, Bihar,\nBombay, Madras, Mysore, Punjab, West Bengal; source khud note karta hai ki given options mein exact\nanswer nahi tha. [Q24]\n5. Legislative Assembly — Composition, Age, Seats & Elections\n● Article 170 ke source rule ke mutabik Assembly strength maximum 500 aur minimum 60; Sikkim ko\nexception bataya gaya hai with 32 members. [Q25, Q26, Q28]\n● Article 170 territorial constituencies se direct election ka framework deta hai; “maximum 450” statement\nsource mein wrong hai. Assembly membership ki minimum age 25 years (Article 173) hai; Council ke\nliye 30 years. [Q27, Q29, Q30]\n● Article 333 ka Anglo-Indian nomination provision source historical context mein batata hai; source note\nkarta hai ki 104th Amendment ke baad arrangement 25 Jan 2020 ke beyond extend nahi hua. [Q31]\n● Given-option seat questions: Uttar Pradesh Assembly 403; Arunachal 60, Himachal Pradesh 68, Manipur\n60, Meghalaya 60 — is set mein Himachal largest; Manipur 60 is the corrected match. [Q32, Q33, Q34]\n● 2019 reorganisation source note: Jammu & Kashmir UT with legislature, Ladakh UT without legislature.\nState Assembly elections Election Commission of India Article 324 ke under conduct karta hai. [Q35, Q36]\n6. Disqualification & Speaker — Articles 179, 191–192\n● Article 192: Article 191(1) type disqualification question Governor decide karta hai; decision se pehle\nElection Commission ki opinion leni hoti hai aur source ke mutabik Governor us opinion ke according act\nkarta hai. [Q37, Q38]\n● Tenth Schedule/defection ko chhodkar disqualification Governor; defection case mein Assembly Speaker\nya Council Chairman decision-maker hota hai. [Q39]\n● Assembly Speaker resignation Deputy Speaker ko deta hai (Article 179(b)). [Q40]\n● Assembly dissolve hone par Speaker turant office vacate nahi karta; newly constituted Assembly ki first\nsitting se immediately pehle tak continue karta hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● Source match: Ramesh Tawadkar–Goa, Kultar Sandhwan–Punjab, T. Satyabrat–Manipur, Ritu\nKhandari–Uttarakhand. MP fact: Ramkishore Shukla ne Pro-tem Speaker, Speaker aur Deputy Speaker\ntino offices hold kiye. [Q43, Q44]\n7. Sessions, Procedure, Quorum & Assembly Business\n● State Vidhan Sabha ko prorogue Governor karta hai under Article 174(2). [Q45]\n● First session after general election aur each year ke first session ke commencement par Governor\naddress karta hai; source ke mutabik rule-gap hone par State Legislature Lok Sabha rules follow karti\nhai. [Q46]\n● MP Assembly proceedings ka source order: Oath/Affirmation → Governor’s Address → Introduction of\nMinisters → Mention of Death. [Q47]\n● Rajasthan Adjournment Motion: Presiding Officer/Speaker consent needed; privilege question nahi\nuthata; recent specific matter hona chahiye; same sitting mein more than one nahi. [Q48]\n● Rajasthan subordinate legislation source point: Speaker delegation-of-legislative-power Bills ko\nautomatically committee refer nahi karta; committee Rule 241 ke under orders scrutiny ke liye select\nkarti hai. [Q49]\n● Article 189(3): quorum = 10 members ya House ki total strength ka 1/10, whichever is greater. Rajasthan\nEstimates Committee “A” source question mein Home Department estimates excluded hain. [Q50, Q51]\n8. Assembly in Electoral Colleges"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The State Legislature Full Mind Map\n● State Legislative Assembly members President of India, Rajya Sabha members aur Legislative Council\nmembers ke elections mein participate karte hain; Vice-President election mein nahi. [Q52]\n9. State Finance & Key Article Map\n● State Contingency Fund Governor ke disposal par hota hai; State Legislature law ke through fund\nestablish kar sakti hai for unforeseen expenditure advances pending legislative authorization. [Q53, Q54]\n● Article 162 = extent of executive power of State. Key match: Art 168 State Legislature constitution; Art\n178 Speaker/Deputy Speaker; Art 195 member salaries/allowances; Art 199 Money Bill definition. [Q55,\nQ56]\n10. Ordinary Bills, Money Bills & Budget\n● Bicameral State mein ordinary Bill ko Council first transmission par max 3 months aur Assembly se\nsecond passage ke baad max 1 month rok sakti hai — total effective delay 4 months. [Q57, Q58]\n● State mein Money Bill hai ya nahi, iska decision Legislative Assembly Speaker karta hai. Money Bill sirf\nAssembly mein introduce hota hai; Council recommendation ke liye 14 days rakhti hai. [Q59, Q60]\n● Source budget-secrecy question: introduction se pehle budget disclose ho to Finance Minister individual\nresponsibility le aur resign kare; source Official Secrets Act, 1923 ka reference deta hai. [Q61]\n● Article 207(1): specified financial/Money Bill provisions wala Bill Governor ki recommendation ke bina\nintroduce/move nahi ho sakta, aur aisa Bill Legislative Council mein introduce nahi hota. [Q62]\n11. Chief Minister & Council of Ministers\n● Article 164(1): Chief Minister ko Governor appoint karta hai. Article 163(1): CM-headed Council Governor\nko aid & advise karti hai, lekin Constitution-required discretionary functions exception hain. [Q63, Q64, Q67]\n● 91st Constitutional Amendment, 2003 ke baad Article 164(1A): State Council of Ministers including CM\nmaximum Assembly strength ka 15%; source minimum 12 ministers batata hai. [Q65, Q66]\n● Article 164(4): non-member Minister maximum 6 consecutive months continue kar sakta hai; sirf voter\nhona minister banne ki sufficient qualification nahi. RPA 1951 conviction-disqualification source ke\nmutabik release ke baad further 6 years, permanent nahi. [Q68, Q69]\n● State Ministers ke salaries/allowances State Legislature law se determine karti hai under Article 164(5).\n[Q70]\n● Article 167 CM duties: Governor ko Council decisions + legislative proposals communicate karna aur\nGovernor kahe to individual minister decision ko Council consideration ke liye rakhna; NDC participation\nsource ke mutabik constitutional duty nahi. [Q71, Q72]\n● Article 163(3): ministers ki Governor ko di advice court inquiry se protected; source Assertion–Reason\nmein legal responsibility ka absence true hai but direct reason nahi. [Q73]\n● Article 164(2): Council of Ministers collectively Legislative Assembly ke prati responsible hai. [Q74]\n● J&K source historical note: earlier Assembly/CM cycle 6 years mana jata tha; J&K Reorganisation Act\n2019 ke source update mein Assembly tenure 5 years. [Q75]\n12. Chief Ministers & State Administration — Key Facts\n● Sucheta Kriplani India ki first woman Chief Minister thi; Uttar Pradesh, 1963. [Q76, Q77]\n● Pt. Ravishankar Shukla source ke mutabik first CM of Madhya Pradesh (1 Nov–31 Dec 1956). Govind\nNarayan Singh ne CM rehte hue MP Assembly Leader of House office hold nahi kiya — source fact.\n[Q78, Q79]\n● State Secretariat State administration ka apex wing aur procedure/principles formation ka main centre\nhai. [Q80]\n● Source ke mutabik Chief Secretary ko CM choose karta hai aur Governor appoint karta hai; fixed tenure\nnahi. State Secretariat ki files Cabinet tak Chief Secretary ke through bheji jaati hain. [Q81, Q82]\n13. State-specific Historical / Current-Affairs Notes"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The State Legislature Full Mind Map\n● Ayodhya incident 1992 ke baad source says UP, MP, Himachal Pradesh aur Rajasthan Assemblies\ndissolve hui; Bihar Assembly dissolve nahi hui. [Q83]\n● Andhra Pradesh Muslim reservation source timeline: 2004 reservation struck down by HC; 2007 mein 4%\nattempt, again HC cancellation; source says SC interim acceptance and final matter Constitution Bench\nke before pending. [Q84]\n● Uniform Civil Code source update: historically Goa only State with common civil code; source adds\nUttarakhand implemented UCC on 27 January 2025. [Q85]\n14. Exam Traps — Source-specific Updates & Exceptions\n Article 169 Resolution ≠ Automatic Parliament Law:\n⚠\nAssembly special-majority resolution necessary\ntrigger hai, lekin source ke mutabik Union Government/Parliament par legislation initiate karne ki binding\nobligation nahi banti. [Q10]\n Legislative Council Nominated Fraction — Source-specific:\n⚠\nSource universal fixed fraction reject karta\nhai aur UP ke liye 100 mein 10 nominated ka example deta hai; is numerical framing ko source-specific note\nki tarah retain karo. [Q13, Q14]\n 1956 Bicameral Count — Options Mismatch:\n⚠\nSource explanation 1956 mein 7 bicameral States list karta\nhai aur khud note karta hai ki given options mein exact answer nahi tha. [Q24]\n Anglo-Indian Nomination — Historical Provision:\n⚠\nQ31 historical Article 333 provision poochta hai;\nsource update ke mutabik 104th Amendment ke baad nomination arrangement 25 Jan 2020 ke beyond\ncontinue nahi hua. [Q31]\n Time-sensitive / Updated Items:\n⚠\nQ35 (J&K/Ladakh 2019), Q43 (then-newly elected Speakers), Q75 (J&K\ntenure), Q84 (reservation litigation), Q85 (Uttarakhand UCC 2025) ko source-date/context ke saath padho.\n[Q35, Q43, Q75, Q84, Q85]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0280","t":"03 Constituent Assembly and Making of Constitution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" 🏛️ CONSTITUENT ASSEMBLY AND MAKING OF\nTHE CONSTITUTION — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Idea & Demand for a Constituent Assembly\n2. Cabinet Mission, 1946 — Formation Plan\n3. Wavell Plan & Interim Government, 1946\n4. Nature & Election of the Constituent Assembly\n5. First Meeting — Presidents & Vice-President\n6. Objectives Resolution — Preamble ka Base\n7. Sessions, Duration & Final Meeting\n8. Key Members, Committees & Constitutional Adviser\n9. Third Reading, Adoption & Commencement\n10. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar — Election & Life Dates\n11. Third Round Table Conference & Government of India Act, 1935\n12. Debates, Opinions & Famous Quotations\n13. Women Members of the Constituent Assembly\n1. Idea & Demand for a Constituent Assembly\n● M.N. Roy ne 1934 mein Constituent Assembly ka idea sabse pehle put forward kiya. [Q2]\n● Swaraj Party ne May 1934 ke Ranchi conference mein Constituent Assembly ki first formal\ndemand/policy rakhi; proposed representatives adult suffrage ke basis par elected hone the. [Q1, Q2]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne 19 November 1939 ke Harijan article ‘The Only Way’ mein likha ki Constituent\nAssembly hi desh ka indigenous Constitution bana sakti hai jo logon ki will ko truly represent kare. [Q3]\n● Cripps Mission (1942) ne Second World War ke baad ek elected Constituent Assembly se Indian\nConstitution frame karne ka proposal diya. [Q4]\n● Cripps proposals mein Dominion Status, unwilling province ko separate union/constitution ka option, aur\nConstituent Assembly ka plan tha. Provincial Assemblies members ELECT karti aur Princely States\nmembers NOMINATE karte — isliye ‘dono nominate karte’ wali wording galat hai. [Q5]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — M.N. Roy vs Swaraj Party — wording dekho\n\n▸‘Idea first put forward’ → M.N. Roy, 1934. [Q2]\n\n▸‘First formal demand / policy by Indians’ → Swaraj Party, Ranchi conference, May 1934. [Q1, Q2]\n2. Cabinet Mission, 1946 — Formation Plan\n● Cabinet Mission 1946 mein India aaya aur Indian Union ka Constitution banane ke liye Constituent\nAssembly formation plan diya. Provincial representation roughly 1 representative per 10 lakh population\ntha. [Q6]\n● Cabinet Mission ke members: Sir Pethick-Lawrence (Secretary for India), Stafford Cripps (Chairman,\nBoard of Trade) aur A.V. Alexander (Navy Minister). William Wood member NAHI the. [Q7]\n● Indian Constituent Assembly Cabinet Mission Plan, 1946 ke under constitute hui aur iska basis indirect\nelection tha. [Q8, Q9]"," 3. Wavell Plan & Interim Government, 1946\n● First Interim National Government 24 August 1946 ko announce hui aur 2 September 1946 ko charge\nlena tha. Viceroy Executive Council ka ex-officio President tha; Jawaharlal Nehru Vice-President\ndesignate hue. [Q10, Q13]\n● Interim Government mein C. Rajagopalachari — Education, Dr. Rajendra Prasad — Food & Agriculture,\naur Jagjivan Ram — Labour se jude the; Dr. S. Radhakrishnan is Interim Government ke member NAHI\nthe. [Q11, Q12]\n● Wavell Plan ne Executive Council mein Hindu aur Muslim members ki equal representation propose ki.\nIska purpose constitutional/political deadlock remove karna aur Indian self-government promote karna\ntha — partition avoid karne ke liye Hindu-Muslim unity banana iska stated purpose nahi tha. Assertion\ntrue, Reason false. [Q14]\n4. Nature & Election of the Constituent Assembly\n● Constituent Assembly DIRECT election ka result nahi thi. Provincial Legislative Assemblies Electoral\nCollege bani aur members indirectly elect hue. [Q15, Q16, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● Assembly ka election Universal Adult Franchise par based nahi tha. Provincial legislators khud limited\nfranchise — education, property aur tax qualifications — par elected the. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Assembly multi-party body thi: Congress, Muslim League aur independent members ko representation\nmila; Assembly ne constitution-making ka kaam kai committees ke through kiya. [Q15, Q16]\n● Q17 ke source framing mein Christians, Anglo-Indians aur Parsis jaise minority communities ka\nadequate representation aur committee-based working correct statements maane gaye; incorrect\nstatement universal adult franchise wala tha. [Q17]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Indirect Election vs Adult Franchise\n\n▸Constituent Assembly members Provincial Legislative Assemblies se indirectly elect hue. [Q15, Q18, Q19,\nQ20]\n\n▸Assembly Universal Adult Franchise par based NAHI thi; provincial legislators limited franchise par elected\nthe. [Q16, Q17]\n5. First Meeting — Presidents & Vice-President\n● Constituent Assembly ki first meeting 9 December 1946 ko New Delhi mein hui. Muslim League ne first\nmeeting boycott ki; Jawaharlal Nehru Assembly ke member the. [Q26, Q27, Q31, Q32, Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Oldest member Dr. Sachchidanand Sinha ne first meeting ko TEMPORARY / PROVISIONAL Chairman-\nPresident ke roop mein preside kiya. [Q21, Q23, Q24, Q26]\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad 11 December 1946 ko unanimously permanent Chairman/President elect hue.\n[Q22, Q25, Q28, Q29]\n● Frank Anthony first nominated temporary Deputy Chairman the; unhe 9 December 1946 ko Dr.\nSachchidanand Sinha ne nominate kiya. H.C. Mukherjee first permanent Vice-President the. [Q30]"," ⚠️EXAM TRAP — Temporary vs Permanent Presiding Officers\n\n▸9 Dec 1946 → Dr. Sachchidanand Sinha = temporary/provisional President. [Q21, Q23, Q24, Q26]\n\n▸11 Dec 1946 → Dr. Rajendra Prasad = permanent President/Chairman. [Q22, Q25, Q28, Q29]\n\n▸Frank Anthony = first nominated temporary Deputy Chairman; H.C. Mukherjee = first permanent Vice-\nPresident. [Q30]\n6. Objectives Resolution — Preamble ka Base\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne 13 December 1946 ko first session ki fifth meeting mein historic Objectives\nResolution introduce ki. [Q36, Q37, Q40]\n● Objectives Resolution ko Constituent Assembly ne 22 January 1947 ko unanimously adopt kiya. [Q38]\n● Ye Resolution constitution-making ki philosophy/guiding principles ka base bana aur later Preamble ki\nfoundation bana. [Q36, Q39]\n● Source ke statement-question mein Nehru ka Objectives Resolution, Preamble ke important aims aur\n‘People of India’ se constitutional authority wali statements correct hain; President ka direct popular\nelection wala statement incorrect hai. [Q41]\n7. Sessions, Duration & Final Meeting\n● Constitution frame karne ke liye Constituent Assembly ke 11 sessions hue, total 165 days cover hue.\n11th session ke last day 26 November 1949 ko Constitution adopt hua. [Q42]\n● Historic task complete karne mein 2 years, 11 months aur 18 days lage. [Q44, Q45]\n● 11 sessions ke alawa 24 January 1950 ko ek aur meeting hui jisme members ne signatures append\nkiye; source ise last/final meeting batata hai. [Q42, Q43]\n● 24 January 1950 ke final session mein National Anthem aur National Song adopt kiye gaye aur Dr.\nRajendra Prasad ko first President of India elect kiya gaya. [Q46]\n8. Key Members, Committees & Constitutional Adviser\n● Important match: First Vice-President of Constituent Assembly → H.C. Mukherjee; Drafting Committee\nka originally only Congress member → K.M. Munshi; Rajasthan Princely State representative → V.T.\nKrishnamachari; Union Constitution Committee Chairman → Jawaharlal Nehru. [Q47]\n● Sir Benegal Narsing Rau (B.N. Rau) Constitution-making ke time Constitutional Adviser appointed the.\n[Q48]\n● Indian Constitution ka first draft B.N. Rau ne prepare kiya; is draft ko Drafting Committee ke opinion,\ndiscussion aur changes ke liye rakha gaya. [Q49]\n9. Third Reading, Adoption & Commencement\n● Constitution ki third reading 17 November 1949 ko start hui aur 26 November 1949 ko complete hui.\nSource Q50 mein diye gaye options mein exact date nahi thi. [Q50]\n● 26 November 1949 = Constitution ka adoption / completion / passing date. Constituent Assembly ne isi\ndin Constitution adopt kiya. [Q51, Q52, Q53, Q54]\n● 26 January 1950 = Constitution came into force / commencement date. [Q55, Q56]\n● 26 January isliye choose hua kyunki Lahore Session (December 1929) ke Purna Swaraj declaration ke\nbaad Congress 26 January ko Independence Day observe karti thi; Constitution ko 26 January 1950 se\neffective karke us declaration ko commemorate kiya gaya. [Q57]"," ● Constitution Day 26 November ko Constitution adoption ki memory mein celebrate kiya jata hai. [Q58,\nQ59]\n● Drafting Committee 29 August 1947 ko set up hui thi, 26 November 1949 ko nahi; ismein 7 members the\naur Chairman Dr. B.R. Ambedkar the. [Q59]\n● Constitution 26 November 1949 ko Constituent Assembly ne apne 11th session mein adopt aur enact\nkiya. [Q60, Q61, Q62]\n● Chronology: First meeting — 9 Dec 1946 → Drafting Committee — 29 Aug 1947 → Constitution\nadopted/enacted — 26 Nov 1949 → commencement — 26 Jan 1950. [Q63]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — 26 Nov 1949 vs 26 Jan 1950\n\n▸26 Nov 1949 → Constitution adopted/enacted/completed; Constitution Day. [Q51-Q54, Q58, Q60-Q62]\n\n▸26 Jan 1950 → Constitution came into force. [Q55, Q56]\n\n▸Third reading start = 17 Nov 1949; complete = 26 Nov 1949. [Q50]\n10. Dr. B.R. Ambedkar — Election & Life Dates\n● 1946 ke preliminary election mein Dr. B.R. Ambedkar undivided Bengal ke eastern part se Constituent\nAssembly ke liye elected hue. Region Pakistan ka part banne ke baad, source ke mutabik unhe Bombay\nPresidency ki Pune seat se elect kiya gaya jo M.R. Jaikar ke resignation se vacant hui thi. [Q64]\n● Dr. Ambedkar ka birth 14 April 1891 ko Mhow, Madhya Pradesh mein hua aur death 6 December 1956\nko Delhi mein hui. [Q65]\n11. Third Round Table Conference & Government of India Act, 1935\n● Third and last Round Table Conference November-December 1932 mein London mein hui; Congress ne\nparticipate nahi kiya. Is conference ki discussions ne Government of India Act, 1935 ko finalise/passage\nki direction di. [Q66]\n● Government of India Act, 1935 ne British India ke Provinces aur Princely States ko mila kar All India\nFederation establish karne ka provision diya. [Q66]\n12. Debates, Opinions & Famous Quotations\n● Source ke Assertion-Reason mein Indian Constitution ko desh ki necessities provide karne aur future\namendments ka provision rakhne wala bataya gaya; saath hi different countries ke constitutions se\nviews/principles lene ke kaaran ‘Adopted Constitution’ kaha gaya. Dono statements true, lekin Reason,\nAssertion ka correct explanation nahi. [Q67]\n● Adult Franchise ko 15 years defer karne ki plea Maulana Azad ne Constituent Assembly mein rakhi; Dr.\nRajendra Prasad aur Jawaharlal Nehru ne uske adoption ko strongly support kiya. [Q68]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne advise kiya ki Independence ke baad Indian National Congress ko political party ke\nroop mein disband kar dena chahiye. [Q69]\n● ‘A Constitution, like a machine, is a lifeless thing...’ wali statement Dr. Rajendra Prasad ke 26 November\n1949 adoption speech se source mein attributed hai. [Q70]\n● Minority interests/emotions ko nationalist reaction mein minimise karne wali criticism Sir Ivor Jennings ko\nattributed hai. [Q71]\n● ‘Constituent Assembly was Congress and Congress was India’ statement Granville Austin ko, unki book\n‘The Indian Constitution’ ke context mein, attributed hai. [Q72]"," 13. Women Members of the Constituent Assembly\n● Constituent Assembly mein total 15 women members thi: Ammu Swaminathan, Annie Mascarene,\nSarojini Naidu, Dakshayani Velayudhan, G. Durgabai Deshmukh, Hansa Mehta, Kamala Choudhury,\nLeela Roy, Malati Choudhury, Rajkumari Amrit Kaur, Renuka Ray, Purnima Banerjee, Begum Aizaz\nRasul, Sucheta Kripalani aur Vijayalakshmi Pandit. [Q73]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constituent Assembly & Making of the Constitution Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0281","t":"30 The High Court","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The High Court Full Mind Map\n THE HIGH COURT — FULL MIND MAP\n⚖️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. High Court Structure, Judges & Service Conditions\n2. High Courts in India — Number, Common Jurisdiction & Benches\n3. Jurisdiction of High Court & Chief Justice — Administrative Role\n4. Writ Jurisdiction — Certiorari, Prohibition, Mandamus & Quo Warranto\n5. Judge Removal, Resignation & Post-Retirement Practice\n6. Important High Court Cases, Judges & Law Commission\n7. District Judiciary — Articles 233 & 236\n8. Advocates, Prisons & Judicial Custody\n9. Lok Adalat, Gram Nyayalaya & Mobile Court\n10. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-Sensitive Source Questions\n1. High Court Structure, Judges & Service Conditions\n● Article 216 ke source framing ke mutabik har High Court mein ek Chief Justice aur utne other Judges\nhote hain jitne President time-to-time necessary deem kare; judge-strength determine/fix karne ka\nauthority President se linked hai. [Q1]\n● Article 217(1): High Court Judge ko President warrant under hand and seal se appoint karta hai. Source\nQ2 isi appointment rule ko test karta hai. [Q2]\n● Article 222: President, Chief Justice of India se consultation ke baad High Court Judge ko ek High Court\nse doosre High Court transfer kar sakta hai. Source Third Judges Case (1998) mein CJI ke wider\nconsultation/collegium input ka note deta hai. [Q3]\n● Article 224: temporary workload/arrears ke liye Additional Judges maximum 2 years ke liye appoint ho\nsakte hain; permanent judge ke absence/temporary incapacity mein Acting Judge appoint ho sakta hai.\nAdditional/Acting Judge 62 years ke baad office hold nahi karega. [Q4]\n● High Court Judges ki salary/allowances State ke Consolidated Fund par charged hain (source Article\n202(3)(d)); retired High Court Judge ki pension Consolidated Fund of India se charged batayi gayi hai\n(Article 112(3)(d)). [Q5, Q6]\n● High Court Judge retirement age 62 years hai. Source 15th Constitutional Amendment, 1963 se age 60\nse 62 hone aur 114th Amendment Bill, 2010 ke unsuccessful 65-year proposal ka note deta hai. [Q7, Q8]\n2. High Courts in India — Number, Common Jurisdiction & Benches\n● Source current-reference ke hisab se India mein 25 High Courts batata hai; Part VI, Chapter V, Article\n214 ko High Courts se link karta hai. Punjab + Haryana + Chandigarh ka common High Court aur Delhi\nka apna High Court source mein stated hai. [Q9]\n● Andaman & Nicobar Islands Kolkata (Calcutta) High Court ke territorial jurisdiction mein; Chandigarh\nPunjab & Haryana HC, Puducherry Chennai HC aur Lakshadweep Kerala HC ke jurisdiction se source\nmap karta hai. [Q12]\n● Bombay High Court source ke mutabik Maharashtra, Goa aur specified Union Territories par jurisdiction\nrakhta hai. UTs exclude karke source three common-State High Courts batata hai: Gauhati, Bombay,\naur Punjab & Haryana. [Q13, Q14]\n● January 2013 mein Meghalaya, Manipur aur Tripura ke new High Courts establish hue aur March 2013\nse function karne lage — source explanation. [Q16]\n● Source bench-count question mein Mumbai/Bombay aur Gauhati High Courts ko 3 benches each\nbatakar multiple-correct answer mark karta hai; Kolkata circuit benches aur MP HC ke Indore/Gwalior\nbenches ka bhi note deta hai. [Q17]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The High Court Full Mind Map\n3. Jurisdiction of High Court & Chief Justice — Administrative Role\n● Advisory jurisdiction source ke mutabik High Court ki main jurisdiction nahi; Article 143 wali advisory\njurisdiction Supreme Court se linked hai. [Q18]\n● High Court Chief Justice judicial aur administrative dono capacity mein act karta hai. Source kehta hai ki\nadministrative capacity mein Chief Justice kisi other High Court Judge ki writ jurisdiction ke subject ho\nsakta hai aur lower courts ki supervision/administration karta hai. [Q19]\n4. Writ Jurisdiction — Certiorari, Prohibition, Mandamus & Quo Warranto\n● Certiorari: superior court lower court ka case-record review ke liye mangwata hai, usually lower-court\njudgment ko examine/overrule karne ke purpose se; subordinate courts ke functioning ko examine karne\nwala writ bhi source isi ko batata hai. [Q20, Q22]\n● Prohibition: superior court lower court/tribunal ko jurisdiction exceed karne ya unlawful proceeding\ncontinue karne se rokta hai. Source ise pending proceeding ke stage par issue hone aur judicial/quasi-\njudicial bodies tak limited batata hai. [Q21, Q23]\n● Mandamus public duty ke context mein private organisation par tab lie kar sakta hai jab public duty\nentrusted ho; source Government Company ke against mandamus possible batata hai. Quo Warranto\nke liye any public-minded person petitioner ho sakta hai. [Q25]\n● Article 226 ke under High Court five writs — Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari, Quo\nWarranto — Fundamental Rights ke enforcement ke saath “any other purpose”/legal or statutory rights\nke liye bhi issue kar sakta hai; Article 32 SC power source mein Fundamental Rights tak framed hai.\n[Q26, Q27]\n● Contempt Assertion–Reason: willful court-order disobedience/non-compliance aur derogatory language\ncontempt ho sakte hain; source marks Assertion aur Reason dono correct, lekin Reason Assertion ka\ncorrect explanation nahi. [Q24]\n5. Judge Removal, Resignation & Post-Retirement Practice\n● Article 217(1)(b): High Court Judge ka removal mode Supreme Court Judge jaisa Article 124(4) manner\nfollow karta hai — source statement 1 correct batata hai. [Q28]\n● Article 220: permanent retired High Court Judge India mein Supreme Court aur other High Courts ke\nsaamne plead/act kar sakta hai; “kahin bhi practice nahi kar sakta” statement source mein incorrect hai.\n[Q28]\n● Article 217(1)(a): High Court Judge resignation President ko addressed writing se deta hai. [Q29]\n● Justice Soumitra Sen (former Calcutta HC Judge) ke against 2011 mein Rajya Sabha impeachment\nmotion pass hua; source ke mutabik Lok Sabha consideration se pehle unhone 1 September 2011 ko\nresign kar diya. [Q30]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The High Court Full Mind Map\n6. Important High Court Cases, Judges & Law Commission\n● Babri Mosque/Ramjanmabhoomi dispute Allahabad High Court ke saamne source ke mutabik Title Suit\ntha — same land/property par competing claims. [Q31]\n● Rahmatullah v. State of U.P. (1994) ko source Allahabad High Court se link karta hai aur triple talaq\npronouncement ko illegal batata hai; explanation additionally Muslim Women (Protection of Rights on\nMarriage) Act, 2019 ka later statutory note deta hai. [Q32]\n● Rajeev Gupta 2 February 2008 ko Chhattisgarh High Court ke Chief Justice bane; source batata hai ki\nisse pehle Uttarakhand HC ke Chief Justice the. [Q33]\n● 8th Law Commission ke Chairman Justice H.R. Khanna ki 80th Report “The Method of Appointment of\nJudges” ne source ke mutabik recommend kiya ki each High Court ke at least one-third Judges other\nStates se hon. [Q34]\n7. District Judiciary — Articles 233 & 236\n● Article 233 District Judges ke appointment/posting/promotion se linked hai; source Governor ko\nconcerned High Court se consultation ke saath appointment authority batata hai. [Q35, Q37]\n● Article 236(a) mein “district judge” expression source ke mutabik city civil court judge,\nadditional/joint/assistant district judge, chief small causes judge, presidency magistrates,\nsessions/additional/assistant sessions judges etc. include karta hai; Tribunal Judge include nahi. [Q36]\n● District Judge district ka highest judicial authority hai aur source ke mutabik judicial + administrative\npowers ke saath subordinate courts par supervisory powers rakhta hai; Assertion–Reason mein R ko A\nka correct explanation mark kiya gaya. [Q37]\n8. Advocates, Prisons & Judicial Custody\n● Advocates Act, 1961 source ke mutabik single class “advocates” create karta hai; government law\nofficers, legal firms, corporate lawyers aur patent attorneys ko advocates ke roop mein recognise karne\nka explanation deta hai. Bar Councils legal education aur law-college recognition rules lay down kar\nsakte hain. [Q38]\n● Prisons / persons detained therein State List Entry 4 se source link karta hai; Prisons Act, 1894 ne day-\nto-day prison administration States/earlier Provincial Governments ke control mein rakha. Source\nadditionally Model Prisons Act, 2023 ko guiding document batata hai. [Q39]\n● Judicial custody = accused concerned Magistrate ki custody mein aur jail mein; police custody mein\npolice-station lock-up. Judicial custody mein police court approval ke bina interrogation nahi kar sakti;\ncourt necessary samjhe to permission de sakta hai. [Q40]\n9. Lok Adalat, Gram Nyayalaya & Mobile Court\n● Lok Adalat settlement ka key factor parties ki consent hai; source ke mutabik sitting/retired judicial officer\nChairman hota hai aur usually lawyer + social worker members hote hain. Given Q41 statements mein\nsource “none” ko correct answer batata hai. [Q41]\n● Gram Nyayalayas Act, 2008: Section 11 ke source explanation mein Gram Nyayalaya civil aur criminal\ndono jurisdiction exercise kar sakta hai; Section 27 ke under village-level social workers conciliators\npanel mein aa sakte hain. [Q42]\n● Mobile Court concept source Dr A.P.J. Abdul Kalam ka brainchild batata hai; first mobile court August\n2007, Mewat district Haryana mein, then CJI K.G. Balakrishnan dwara inaugurated batayi gayi. [Q43]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The High Court Full Mind Map\n10. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-Sensitive Source Questions\n EXAM TRAP — High Court Count / UT Jurisdiction — Date-Sensitive Items\n⚠\nQ10 aur Q11 source khud disputed mark karta hai: old exam-year figures/options current-reference se match\nnahi karte. Source current reference mein 25 High Courts batata hai. Q9 ka UT wording bhi source-specific hai;\nise source note ke roop mein hi padho, silently reconcile mat karo. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — Manipur High Court — Historical Question\n⚠\nQ15 2005 ke historical context mein Manipur ko own High Court na hone se link karta hai; source itself note\nkarta hai ki Manipur High Court March 2013 mein establish hua, isliye old option current framing mein valid\nnahi. [Q15]\n EXAM TRAP — Largest Number of Benches — Multiple Correct\n⚠\nQ17 source explicitly multiple-correct mark karta hai: Mumbai/Bombay aur Gauhati High Courts ko 3 benches\neach bataya gaya hai. Exam mein date/options ke context ko ignore mat karo. [Q17]\n EXAM TRAP — Chief Justice of Chhattisgarh — Time-Sensitive Source Line\n⚠\nQ33 ka core historical fact Rajeev Gupta ka 2 Feb 2008 appointment hai. Source explanation ek “current Chief\nJustice” line bhi deta hai; wo time-sensitive statement hai, isliye historical asked fact ko priority se yaad rakho.\n[Q33]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0282","t":"31 The Centre-State Relations","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Centre-State Relations Full Mind Map\n CENTRE-STATE RELATIONS — FULL MIND\n🤝\n\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Federal Relations — Constitutional Framework & Key Factors\n2. Legislative Relations — Articles 245–249 & Seventh Schedule\n3. Residuary Powers & Parliament on State List\n4. Administrative Relations — Articles 256–263\n5. Inter-State Council — Article 263\n6. Zonal Councils & North Eastern Council (NEC)\n7. Inter-State Water Disputes & Regional Institutions\n8. Sarkaria Commission & Review of Centre-State Relations\n9. Financial Relations — Part XII & Tax Distribution\n10. Grants, State Borrowing & Fiscal Disputes\n11. Trade, Commerce, Suits & Exam Traps\n1. Federal Relations — Constitutional Framework & Key Factors\n● Centre-State relations sirf Constitution se nahi, planning process, political-interest conflicts aur Centre ki\ndominance ki tendency se bhi influence hote hain. Source in factors ko Indian federal working ka\npractical part batata hai. [Q1]\n● Constitutional provisions + conventions/practices + judicial interpretations + dialogue mechanisms —\nsource ke mutabik Centre-State relations in sab par depend karte hain. [Q2]\n● Federal policy mein Union-State relations, inter-State relations, cooperation mechanisms aur dispute-\nresolution mechanisms — chaaron include hote hain. [Q3]\n● Planning process mein Centre ke State par control ko source 'municipal relations' term se link karta hai.\n[Q4]\n● Fiscal federalism mein tax sharing, centrally sponsored schemes aur grants-in-aid resource transfer ke\nmeans hain; plan implementation under Gadgil Formula source ke mutabik present means nahi. [Q5]\n● Part XI = Relations between Union and States. Source isse Legislative Relations (Articles 245–255) aur\nAdministrative Relations (Articles 256–263) mein divide karta hai. [Q6]\n2. Legislative Relations — Articles 245–249 & Seventh Schedule\n● Legislative relations Part XI, Articles 245–255 mein hain. Source Seventh Schedule ki\nUnion/State/Concurrent Lists ka exam-oriented mapping deta hai. [Q7]\n● Articles 245–246 legislative territory aur subject-matter distribution regulate karte hain; Article 246 ko\nSeventh Schedule lists ke saath source repeatedly link karta hai. [Q8, Q9]\n● Concurrent List ke subjects par Centre aur State dono law bana sakte hain; conflict mein source Union\nlaw ko prevailing rule batata hai. [Q10]\n● Economic & Social Planning aur infants/minors source ke mutabik Concurrent List subjects hain; isliye\nCentre aur State dono legislate kar sakte hain. [Q11]\n3. Residuary Powers & Parliament on State List\n● Article 248: residuary legislative powers Parliament/Union ke paas. Source federal comparison mein\nU.S.A. jaise systems se contrast bhi karta hai. [Q12, Q14]\n● Residuary subjects = jo Union, State ya Concurrent List mein specifically mentioned na hon; source\ntechnology/new-policy examples ke saath Parliament ki exclusive power explain karta hai. [Q13]\n● Article 249 national interest mein Parliament ko State List matter par law-making power deta hai, jab\nRajya Sabha required resolution pass kare. [Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Centre-State Relations Full Mind Map\n● Article 249 resolution ki validity source ke mutabik maximum one year hoti hai. [Q16, Q17]\n4. Administrative Relations — Articles 256–263\n● Article 256: State executive power Parliament-made/applicable laws ka compliance ensure kare; Union\nnecessary directions de sakta hai. Source Assertion–Reason mein dono statements true aur R ko A ka\nexplanation maanta hai. [Q41]\n● Article 257(1): State executive power Union ki executive power ko impede/prejudice na kare; Union\ndirections de sakta hai. [Q42]\n● Article 263 inter-State coordination/dispute discussion ke constitutional mechanism se linked hai. [Q18]\n5. Inter-State Council — Article 263\n● Inter-State Council President establish kar sakta hai under Article 263; source ISC ka constitutional\nsource isi Article ko batata hai. [Q19, Q20]\n● Source Presidential order dated 28 May 1990 se ISC establishment note karta hai: PM Chairman, State\nCMs, relevant UT representatives aur PM-nominated six Union Cabinet Ministers members. [Q21]\n● Article 263 under ISC constitution; source first ISC ko 1990 se link karta hai aur Article 365/360/368 ko\ndistractors ke roop mein distinguish karta hai. [Q22]\n● National Development Council aur Governors Conference source ke mutabik extra-constitutional/extra-\nlegal devices; Zonal Councils statutory aur ISC constitutional hai. [Q23]\n6. Zonal Councils & North Eastern Council (NEC)\n● Source five regional/Zonal Councils ko Parliamentary law/States Reorganisation Act, 1956 se link karta\nhai; Union Home Minister ko Councils ka Chairman batata hai. [Q24, Q25]\n● Zonal Councils constitutional nahi, statutory bodies hain. Original five zones source lists: Northern,\nCentral, Eastern, Western, Southern; Chandigarh/Delhi/other specified UTs respective councils mein\nincluded bataye gaye hain. [Q26]\n● Regional councils ko source Indian federal system ke 'Sub-Federal Links' kehta hai — cooperation,\nconsultation aur regional integration ka platform. [Q27]\n● NEC: North Eastern Council Act, 1971; 2002 amendment ke baad Sikkim 8th member State aur NEC\nstatutory Regional Planning Body bana. Source statutory membership mein Governors + CMs +\nPresident-nominated 3 members batata hai. [Q28]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Centre-State Relations Full Mind Map\n7. Inter-State Water Disputes & Regional Institutions\n● Jharkhand Area Autonomous Council source ke mutabik 8 August 1995 ko formed hua aur Santhal\nPargana + Chota Nagpur ke 18 districts cover karta tha. [Q29]\n● Inter-State water disputes: Article 262 + Inter-State Water Disputes Act, 1956. Q30 mein River Boards\nAct, 1970 wrong match hai because source Act ko 1956 ka batata hai. [Q30]\n8. Sarkaria Commission & Review of Centre-State Relations\n● Sarkaria Commission 9 June 1983 ko Centre-State relations review/strengthen karne ke liye set up hua;\nChairman Justice R.S. Sarkaria, members B. Shivaraman aur S.R. Sen. [Q31, Q32, Q34]\n● Commission ne report January 1988 mein submit ki. Source Q33 mein exam-key discrepancy explicitly\nnote karta hai. [Q33]\n● Article 356 ko rare/exceptional cases mein sparingly use karne ki Sarkaria recommendation; source\nAssertion–Reason mein misuse concern ko correct explanation maanta hai. [Q35]\n● Sarkaria Commission ne permanent Inter-State Council recommend kiya aur ise 'Inter-Governmental\nCouncil' kehne ka suggestion diya; source 1990 ISC establishment ko recommendation se link karta hai.\n[Q36, Q37, Q38]\n● Indrajit Gupta Committee state funding of elections se related hai, Centre-State relations se nahi; source\nisse other Union-State commissions/committees se distinguish karta hai. [Q39]\n● States ki relatively inadequate developmental resources aur Centre dependence ko source Centre-State\nrelationship review demand ka reason batata hai. [Q40]\n9. Financial Relations — Part XII & Tax Distribution\n● Financial relations Part XII se linked hain; source Part XII = Finance, Property, Contracts and Suits aur\nArticles 268–281 ko revenue distribution framework batata hai. [Q43, Q44]\n● Article 270: source taxes levied/collected by Union and distributed between Union & States se link karta\nhai; income tax other than agricultural income prime example diya hai. [Q45, Q46]\n● Article 268 framing in Q47: relevant stamp duties Union impose karta hai, State collect/appropriate karta\nhai; isliye given statements source mein neither fit hote hain. [Q47]\n● Stock-exchange/futures transaction tax question mein source statement 1 only correct mark karta hai:\nlevy Union se linked; explanation Union collection/State assignment framing deta hai. [Q48]\n● Land Revenue State List Entry 45 — source ke mutabik State dwara exclusively imposed aur collected\ntax. [Q49]\n● Agricultural Income Tax source State List Entry 46/Constitution se assigned batata hai; Article 274 ka\nsupporting mention explanation mein hai. [Q52]\n10. Grants, State Borrowing & Fiscal Disputes\n● Article 282: Union ya State public purpose ke liye discretionary grants de sakta hai even if subject us\nlegislature ki law-making competence mein na ho — source framing. [Q50]\n● Article 293(1): State India ke territory ke andar borrowing kar sakta hai on security of State Consolidated\nFund; source clear karta hai ki State directly foreign loan nahi le sakta. [Q51]\n● Fiscal disputes Centre-State ke beech source Supreme Court/Article 131 se resolve karne wali main\nagency batata hai; Finance Commission ka core role tax-sharing recommendations hai. [Q53]\n● Article 276(2): professions/trades/callings/employments tax ka total annual cap source Rs 2,500 batata\nhai, 60th Amendment Act, 1988 ke baad. [Q54]\n11. Trade, Commerce, Suits & Exam Traps\n● Article 301: Part XIII ke subject to other provisions, trade, commerce and intercourse throughout India\nfree hoga — source freedom of inter-State trade question ka answer. [Q55]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Centre-State Relations Full Mind Map\n● Article 300: Union/State ke suits and proceedings se related; source legal proceedings mein Union/State\nsubstitution framework explain karta hai. [Q56]\n EXAM TRAP — Seventh Schedule List Counts — Source Wording\n⚠\nQ7 explanation original + “at present” list-count figures deta hai. Is mind map mein outside verification se\nnumbers silently replace nahi kiye gaye; exam mein question-year/source framing ko dhyan mein rakho. [Q7]\n EXAM TRAP — NEC Act Membership vs Later Ex-Officio Roles\n⚠\nQ28 ka marked answer 1,2,3 only hai for post-2002 statutory Council composition. Usi source explanation mein\nlater Presidential notifications ke through Union Home Minister ko ex-officio Chairman aur DoNER Minister ko\nex-officio member/Vice-Chairman bhi note kiya gaya hai — dono source layers ko confuse mat karo. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP — Sarkaria Report Year — Official-Key Dispute\n⚠\nSource kehta hai Sarkaria Commission report January 1988 mein submit hui. Q33 ke given options mein 1988\nabsent tha; source explicitly Bihar PSC ka option (d) key incorrect note karta hai aur “None” ko answer rakhta\nhai. [Q33]\n EXAM TRAP — Tax Questions — Follow Source Framing\n⚠\nQ47–Q48 source-specific levy/collection/assignment wording use karte hain. Notes mein wahi source framing\npreserve ki gayi hai; in questions ko options ke exact wording ke saath revise karo. [Q47, Q48]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0283","t":"32 Emergency Provisions","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Emergency Provisions Full Mind Map\n EMERGENCY PROVISIONS — FULL MIND MAP\n🚨\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Emergency Framework — Articles 352, 356, 360 & Union Duty\n2. National Emergency — Article 352: Grounds & 44th Amendment\n3. National Emergency — Cabinet Advice, Approval & Revocation\n4. Effects of National Emergency — Taxes, FRs & Legislature Terms\n5. 1975 Emergency & Article 352 vs Article 356\n6. President's Rule — Article 356: Trigger, Powers & Consequences\n7. President's Rule — Judicial Review, Duration & Historical Facts\n8. Financial Emergency — Article 360: Approval & Consequences\n9. Exam Traps — Disputed / Historical / Quote Questions\n1. Emergency Framework — Articles 352, 356, 360 & Union Duty\n● Indian Constitution source ke mutabik 3 emergency types deta hai: National Emergency (Art. 352), State\nEmergency / President's Rule (Art. 356) aur Financial Emergency (Art. 360). Different grounds ko mix na\nkaro. [Q1, Q8]\n● Article 355 Union ka duty clause hai: har State ko external aggression aur internal disturbance se protect\nkarna aur State government ko Constitution ke according chalna ensure karna. [Q2, Q3]\n2. National Emergency — Article 352: Grounds & 44th Amendment\n● Article 352 ke under National Emergency President proclaim kar sakta hai jab security ko War, External\nAggression ya Armed Rebellion se threat ho. Failure of State constitutional machinery Article 356 ka\nmatter hai, Article 352 ka nahi. [Q4, Q7, Q9, Q13, Q25]\n● 'Internal disturbance' ab Article 352 ka ground nahi hai. Source ke mutabik 44th Constitutional\nAmendment Act, 1978 ne ise 'Armed rebellion' se replace kiya; communal clashes ya general threat to\ninternal peace standalone ground nahi. [Q5, Q6, Q10]\n● Assertion–Reason source: Article 352 emergency proclamation se deal karta hai; emergency kabhi bhi\narise ho sakti hai, lekin yeh second statement Article 352 ka explanatory reason nahi banti. [Q12]\n3. National Emergency — Cabinet Advice, Approval & Revocation\n● Article 352(3): President proclamation tabhi issue karega jab Union Cabinet ka decision usse writing\nmein communicate kiya gaya ho — sirf PM ki personal advice ya generic Council of Ministers wording\npar source focus nahi karta. [Q11]\n● National Emergency proclamation ko Parliament ke dono Houses se 1 month ke andar approval chahiye;\nsource questions approval ke liye special majority / two-thirds pattern ko test karte hain. [Q14, Q15, Q16]\n● Source Q14 ke according revocation ke liye Lok Sabha simple-majority resolution wala route test hota\nhai; joint sitting approval pattern ko correct nahi maana gaya. [Q14]\n4. Effects of National Emergency — Taxes, FRs & Legislature Terms\n● National Emergency ke time President Article 354(1) route se Union–State tax distribution (Articles 268–\n281) related provisions ko modify/suspend kar sakta hai; source isko Financial Emergency se distinguish\nkarta hai. [Q17]\n● Article 359 ke under President FRs ke enforcement ke liye court move karne ka right suspend kar sakta\nhai, lekin Articles 20 aur 21 protected rehte hain. [Q18, Q20, Q21]\n● Article 19 source ke mutabik Article 358 ke under automatically suspend hota hai only when emergency\nWar ya External Aggression ground par ho; Article 359 ke scope ko is automatic rule se alag rakho. [Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Emergency Provisions Full Mind Map\n● National Emergency ke dauran Lok Sabha ka term Parliament law se extend kar sakti hai — ek baar\nmein max 1 year, aur emergency end hone ke 6 months se aage nahi. State Legislative Assembly term\nbhi Parliament law se extend kar sakti hai. [Q22, Q23]\n5. 1975 Emergency & Article 352 vs Article 356\n● Source ke historical question ke mutabik President Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed ne 'internal disturbance'\nground par 25 June 1975 ko Emergency proclaim ki; source ise 21 March 1977 tak effective batata hai.\n[Q24]\n● Article-number trap: Article 352 = National Emergency; Article 356 = State constitutional machinery\nfailure / President's Rule. Source Assertion–Reason isi confusion ko directly test karta hai. [Q25]\n6. President's Rule — Article 356: Trigger, Powers & Consequences\n● Article 356 ke under President's Rule mainly Governor ki report (ya otherwise satisfaction) par impose ho\nsakta hai jab State government Constitution ke according nahi chal sakti. [Q26, Q27]\n● President's Rule mein State executive dismiss hota hai; State Legislature suspended ya dissolved ho\nsakta hai. Legislature ki powers Parliament ya Parliament ke authority ke under exercisable ho jaati hain\n— Assembly automatic dissolution zaroori nahi. [Q29, Q30]\n● S.R. Bommai framing source ke mutabik constitutional machinery failure objective reality hona chahiye\naur Article 356 proclamation Supreme Court judicial review ke under aa sakta hai. [Q31]\n7. President's Rule — Judicial Review, Duration & Historical Facts\n● Source Q31 ke mutabik proclamation ko 2 months ke andar each House of Parliament approve kare;\ninitial stage par Assembly ko suspend kiya ja sakta hai, approval se pehle dissolution ko source\nincorrect immediate consequence batata hai. [Q31]\n● President's Rule maximum 3 years tak extend ho sakta hai, source strict conditions ko active National\nEmergency / Election Commission certification se link karta hai. [Q32]\n● Historical/state-count source (till 2019): Manipur 10, Uttar Pradesh 9, Bihar 8, Odisha 6 President’s Rule\ninstances. [Q33]\n● Source options mein earliest President’s Rule question ka marked answer PEPSU hai, lekin explanation\n1951 Punjab aur 1953 PEPSU dono mention karta hai — isliye wording ko as-source hi yaad rakho.\n[Q34]\n8. Financial Emergency — Article 360: Approval & Consequences\n● Article 360 Financial Emergency proclamation 2 months ke baad cease karega unless Parliament ke\ndono Houses resolutions se approve kar dein. [Q35]\n● Financial Emergency mein President Union/State employees ke salaries & allowances reduce karne ki\ndirections de sakta hai; source specifically Supreme Court aur High Court Judges ko bhi reduction scope\nmein include karta hai. [Q35, Q36]\n● State Legislature ke Money Bills/other financial bills ko President consideration ke liye reserve karne ki\ndirection di ja sakti hai; Q36 source is wording ki necessity vs discretion nuance par dispute flag karta\nhai. [Q36]\n● Source ke mutabik Article 360 India mein ab tak use nahi hua; Financial Emergency kabhi declare nahi\nhui. [Q37, Q38]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Emergency Provisions Full Mind Map\n9. Exam Traps — Disputed / Historical / Quote Questions\n EXAM TRAP — Q19 — Article 358 vs 359\n⚠\nSource question starred/disputed hai: Article 19 ka automatic suspension Article 358 context hai, jabki\nPresident Article 359 se other FR enforcement (20/21 excepted) suspend kar sakta hai. Multiple options\ndifferent contexts mein technically fit ho rahe the. [Q19]\n EXAM TRAP — Q28 — Historical 'Governor’s Rule'\n⚠\nSource is question ko disputed/omitted batata hai: historical J&K mein Section 92 ke under Governor's Rule\ntha; post-2019 J&K UT ban gaya. Manipur, Mizoram aur Meghalaya ke liye source separate historical position\nnote karta hai. [Q28]\n EXAM TRAP — Q34 — PEPSU vs Punjab Wording\n⚠\nMarked answer PEPSU hai, par source explanation earliest instance ke context mein 1951 Punjab aur 1953\nPEPSU mention karta hai. Is internal wording tension ko silently reconcile nahi kiya gaya. [Q34]\n EXAM TRAP — Q36 — Financial Bills Reservation\n⚠\nSource ke hisab se statements 1 & 3 clear correct hain; Money Bills ko reserve kiya 'ja sakta hai' if directed,\nlekin blanket compulsory/never-required wording dono problematic hain. Isliye question starred/disputed hai.\n[Q36]\n● Quote-based source fact: “The emergency power of the President is a fraud with the Constitution” — K.\nM. Nambiar. [Q39]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0284","t":"33 The Finance Commission","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Finance Commission Full Mind Map\n THE FINANCE COMMISSION — FULL MIND MAP\n💰\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Constitutional Status, Article 280 & Five-Year Formation\n2. Composition, Appointment & Qualifications\n3. Core Functions — Tax Devolution & Grants-in-Aid\n4. Finance Commission vs Other Institutions\n5. Important Chairmen — 12th to 15th Finance Commissions\n6. Article 281 — Recommendations Before Parliament\n7. State Finance Commission — Article 243-I\n8. Exam Traps — Statutory vs Constitutional, Reappointment & Old Questions\n1. Constitutional Status, Article 280 & Five-Year Formation\n● Finance Commission ek Constitutional body hai. Constitution ka Article 280 President ko Finance\nCommission constitute karne ka provision deta hai — har fifth year ke end par, ya President ko zaroori\nlage to usse pehle bhi. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q9]\n● Source ke hisab se Finance Commission 5-year cycle ke liye constituted hota hai. First Finance\nCommission 6 April 1952 ko K.C. Neogy ki chairmanship mein set up hua tha. [Q1, Q3, Q10]\n2. Composition, Appointment & Qualifications\n● Article 280(1): Finance Commission mein 1 Chairman + 4 other members = total 5 members hote hain;\nappointment President karta hai. [Q12, Q13, Q25]\n● Members ki qualifications President decide nahi karta. Source explanation ke mutabik Parliament law ke\nthrough qualifications prescribe karta hai — Finance Commission Act, 1951. Chairman aur members ko\nPresident appoint karta hai. [Q11]\n● Source clarification: kisi member ka High Court/Supreme Court Judge hona compulsory nahi; relevant\nqualification/experience enough ho sakta hai. Chairman reappointed ho sakta hai; first Chairman K.C.\nNeogy the, K. Santhanam nahi. [Q12]\n3. Core Functions — Tax Devolution & Grants-in-Aid\n● Finance Commission ka central exam-point: Union aur States ke beech net proceeds of taxes ka\ndistribution recommend karna, aur States ke beech us distribution ka method/principles suggest karna.\n[Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q15, Q18, Q19]\n● Article 280(3) ke context mein Commission States ko grants-in-aid govern karne wale principles par\nrecommendation deta hai. Isi liye tax-sharing + grants-in-aid dono ko saath yaad rakho. [Q14, Q16]\n● Commission State Finance Commission ki recommendations ke basis par State Consolidated Fund ko\naugment karne ke measures bhi suggest kar sakta hai, including Panchayat resources ko supplement\nkarne ke liye. [Q17, Q27]\n4. Finance Commission vs Other Institutions\n● Revenue-sharing principles / Centre-State finance distribution = Finance Commission. Inter-State Council\ncoordination-cooperation ke liye hai; source notes Planning Commission ka resource-allocation role tha\naur usse NITI Aayog ne replace kiya. [Q7]\n● Consolidated Fund of India se withdrawal allow karna Finance Commission ka kaam nahi; source\nexplanation ise Parliament ka function batata hai. Budgetary taxation oversight ko bhi Finance\nCommission ka core function nahi maana gaya. [Q14]\n● Finance Commission apni recommendations President ko deta hai, NITI Aayog ko nahi. [Q13, Q16]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Finance Commission Full Mind Map\n5. Important Chairmen — 12th to 15th Finance Commissions\n● 12th Finance Commission: Chairman Dr. C. Rangarajan; recommendations period source mein 2005–\n2010 diya gaya hai. [Q20]\n● 13th Finance Commission: Chairman Vijay Kelkar; source ke mutabik report 2010 mein submit hui. [Q22]\n● 14th Finance Commission: Chairman Dr. Y.V. Reddy; source period 2015–2020 aur report submission\n15 December 2014 batata hai. [Q23]\n● 15th Finance Commission: 27 November 2017 ko Article 280 ke provision ke according constituted; N.K.\nSingh ko Chairman nominate kiya gaya. [Q24]\n6. Article 281 — Recommendations Before Parliament\n● Article 281: President Finance Commission ki har recommendation ko Parliament ke each House ke\nsamne laid karwata hai. [Q26]\n7. State Finance Commission — Article 243-I\n● State Finance Commission bhi Constitutional body hai. Source ke mutabik Governor Article 243-I ke\nunder ise constitute karta hai. [Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Assertion–Reason trap: ‘Union Finance Commission Panchayats ko financial assistance recommend\nnahi kar sakta’ — source ise false batata hai, kyunki Article 280(3)(bb) State Consolidated Fund ko\naugment karke Panchayat resources supplement karne ki recommendation allow karta hai. [Q27]\n8. Exam Traps — Source-Based Confusions\n EXAM TRAP — Constitutional Body, Statutory Nahi\n⚠\nQ3 mein statement ‘Finance Commission is a statutory body’ galat hai. Source clearly Finance Commission ko\nArticle 280 wala Constitutional body batata hai; recommendations advisory nature ki hain; first Commission\n1952 mein set up hua, 1950 mein nahi. [Q3]\n EXAM TRAP — Qualifications vs Appointment\n⚠\nQualifications Parliament by law prescribe karta hai, jabki Chairman/members ko President appoint karta hai.\nDono roles ko mix mat karna. [Q11]\n EXAM TRAP — Total Members & Reappointment\n⚠\nTotal 5 members = Chairman + 4. Judge hona compulsory nahi; Chairman reappointed ho sakta hai; first\nChairman K.C. Neogy the. [Q12, Q25]\n EXAM TRAP — Old Count Question — Time-Sensitive\n⚠\nQ21 1999 ka question hai. Source explanation ke mutabik present-day options fit nahi karte aur usne 15th\nFinance Commission tak constitution ka note diya hai. Is item ko source-time-context ke saath hi yaad rakho;\nise silently current data se replace nahi kiya gaya. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0285","t":"34 The Planning Commission NITI Aayog","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Planning Commission / NITI Aayog Full Mind Map\n THE PLANNING COMMISSION / NITI AAYOG —\n📊\n\nFULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Planning Commission — Formation, Nature & Abolition\n2. NITI Aayog — Establishment, Status & Leadership\n3. Planning Commission — Chairman & Deputy Chairman\n4. Planning Commission — Functions & “Economic Cabinet”\n5. Planning Commission vs Finance Commission — Merger Suggestion\n6. National Development Council — Formation & Status\n7. NDC — Core Functions & Five-Year Plans\n8. NDC — Composition, Chairman, Secretary & Coordination\n9. Exam Traps — Constitutional Status, NDC & Source-Specific Facts\n1. Planning Commission — Formation, Nature & Abolition\n● Planning Commission 15 March 1950 ko Union Cabinet ke resolution se establish hua tha. Ye\nConstitutional body nahi tha; Prime Minister iska ex-officio Chairman hota tha. Source first Chairman\nJawaharlal Nehru ko batata hai. [Q6, Q7, Q10, Q11, Q12, Q13, Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Source ke mutabik Planning Commission newly independent India ke scarce resources ko optimize\nkarne ke purpose se set up hua. Prime Minister Narendra Modi ne 15 August 2014 ko Red Fort se old\nPlanning Commission ko abolish karne ki announcement ki; replacement NITI Aayog 1 January 2015 ko\naaya. [Q1]\n2. NITI Aayog — Establishment, Status & Leadership\n● NITI Aayog 1 January 2015 ko Planning Commission ko replace karke existence mein aaya.\nEstablishment Union Cabinet ke special resolution se hua — na Presidential ordinance se, na\nParliament Act se. [Q2, Q3]\n● NITI Aayog extra-Constitutional, non-Constitutional aur non-statutory body hai; executive resolution se\ncreate hua. Finance Commission, Election Commission aur Inter-State Council ko source Constitutional\nbodies ke roop mein contrast karta hai. [Q8, Q9]\n● Prime Minister NITI Aayog ka ex-officio Chairperson hota hai; full-time Chairman nahi hota. Vice-\nChairperson ko Prime Minister appoint karta hai aur usse Cabinet Minister ka rank milta hai. [Q4, Q18]\n● Source first Vice-Chairman Dr. Arvind Panagariya ko batata hai, January 2015 se August 2017 tak. Q19\nsource-question framing mein Narendra Modi ko NITI Aayog se associated batata hai because PM ex-\nofficio Chairman hota hai. [Q5, Q19]\n3. Planning Commission — Chairman & Deputy Chairman\n● Planning Commission ka Chairman ex-officio Prime Minister hota tha; first Chairman Jawaharlal Nehru\nthe. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Deputy Chairman ka rank/status Union Cabinet Minister ke equivalent tha. Source Gulzarilal Nanda ko\nfirst Deputy Chairman batata hai. [Q20, Q21]\n● Deputy Chairmen ke source examples: Dr. Manmohan Singh (1985–1987), Pranab Mukherjee (1991–\n1996), Montek Singh Ahluwalia (2004–2014). P. Chidambaram Deputy Chairman nahi rahe. [Q22]\n4. Planning Commission — Functions & “Economic Cabinet”\n● Planning Commission five-year plans formulate karta tha aur natural resources ke balanced utilization ko\nplan karta tha. Source ise Union aur States dono ke liye “Economic Cabinet” ke roop mein describe\nkarta hai. [Q23]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Planning Commission / NITI Aayog Full Mind Map\n● Assertion–Reason source-key: Planning Commission ko “Economic Cabinet” kehna aur five-year plans\nformulate karna dono individually correct hain, lekin Reason ko Assertion ka correct explanation nahi\nmaana gaya. [Q23]\n5. Planning Commission vs Finance Commission — Merger Suggestion\n● Finance Commission aur Planning Commission ke merger ka suggestion M.V. Mathur ne diya tha;\nsource unhe 1960 mein constituted 3rd Finance Commission ka member batata hai. [Q24]\n6. National Development Council — Formation & Status\n● National Development Council (NDC) 6 August 1952 ko formed hua. Source ise non-Constitutional aur\nnon-statutory body batata hai. [Q25, Q34]\n● Constitution mein NDC, Planning Commission aur Zonal Councils ka mention nahi hai. Source\nclarification: NDC aur Planning Commission executive order/resolution se aaye, jabki Zonal Councils\nState Reorganisation Act, 1956 ke statutory bodies hain. [Q14]\n7. NDC — Core Functions & Five-Year Plans\n● Development matters mein source NDC ko apex decision-making/deliberative body batata hai; isliye\n“Planning Commission is the highest decision-making body” statement false hai. [Q26]\n● NDC National Plan ki progress discuss/review karta hai, goals achieve karne ke measures suggest karta\nhai aur plan formulation ke guidelines deta hai. Planning mein money allocation suggest karna source ke\naccording Planning Commission ka function tha, NDC ka nahi. [Q27]\n● NDC ke main functions mein States ke efforts activate karna, general development policies develop\nkarna aur balanced development ensure karna included hain. [Q28]\n● NDC Five-Year Plans ko finally approve karta tha aur Planning Commission aur State Governments ke\nbeech coordination/State participation ensure karta tha. [Q30, Q32]\n8. NDC — Composition, Chairman, Secretary & Coordination\n● NDC composition source ke mutabik: Prime Minister + Union Cabinet Ministers + all States/UTs ke Chief\nMinisters + Planning Commission members (source explanation mein “now NITI Aayog” wording bhi diya\nhai). Finance Commission Chairman member nahi hota. [Q29]\n● Prime Minister NDC meetings preside karta hai. Planning Commission ka Secretary NDC ka ex-officio\nSecretary act karta tha; source explanation “now NITI Aayog” phrase use karta hai. [Q31, Q33]\n● Planning Commission aur State Governments ke beech coordinator = National Development Council.\n[Q32]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Planning Commission / NITI Aayog Full Mind Map\n9. Exam Traps — Constitutional Status, NDC & Source-Specific Facts\n EXAM TRAP — Planning Commission / NITI Aayog — Constitutional Nahi\n⚠\nPlanning Commission aur NITI Aayog dono ko source extra-Constitutional / non-Constitutional framework mein\nrakhta hai. NITI Aayog non-statutory bhi hai; constitutional commissions se confuse mat karo. [Q8, Q9, Q10,\nQ11, Q12, Q13, Q18]\n EXAM TRAP — NDC vs Planning Commission — Apex Development Body\n⚠\nSource ke according development matters ka apex deliberative/decision body NDC tha, Planning Commission\nnahi. Five-Year Plan approval bhi source NDC se link karta hai; Planning Commission plan\nformulation/allocation role mein tha. [Q26, Q27, Q30]\n EXAM TRAP — NDC — Statutory Body Nahi\n⚠\nQ34 mein “NDC is a statutory body” incorrect statement hai. Source NDC ko non-Constitutional + non-statutory\nbatata hai. Zonal Councils statutory hone ke bawajood Constitution mein mentioned nahi hain. [Q14, Q34]\n EXAM TRAP — Source-Specific Current/Legacy Wording\n⚠\nQ19 Narendra Modi ko NITI Aayog se associated batata hai because source-question context mein PM ex-\nofficio Chairman hai. Q29/Q31 explanations Planning Commission ke saath “now NITI Aayog” wording use\nkarte hain; in legacy facts ko source framing ke roop mein padho. [Q19, Q29, Q31]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0286","t":"35 Lokpal and Important Commissions","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n LOKPAL & IMPORTANT COMMISSIONS — FULL\n🏛️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Lokpal — Appointment, Firsts & Bill History\n2. Lokayukta — Maharashtra, U.P., Uttarakhand & Rajasthan\n3. Minority / Women / Education & Other Committees\n4. UDHR — Human Rights Basics & Generations\n5. Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993 — Core Provisions\n6. NHRC — Appointment, Composition, Tenure & Chairpersons\n7. SHRC / Human Rights Courts — Appointment & Functions\n8. Constitutional vs Statutory Bodies & Misc. Commissions\n9. CVC, Mandal Commission & SC/ST Commission\n10. UPSC / SPSC — Constitutional Framework\n11. Public Service Commissions — Appointment, Removal & Functions\n12. PSC History, Bureaucracy & Civil Services Reforms\n1. Lokpal — Appointment, Firsts & Bill History\n● Lokpal Chairperson aur Members ki appointment President karta hai Selection Committee ki\nrecommendation par. Committee: PM (Chairperson), Lok Sabha Speaker, Lok Sabha LoP, CJI ya CJI-\nnominated Supreme Court Judge, aur President-nominated eminent jurist. Rajya Sabha Chairman is list\nka part nahi hai. [Q1]\n● India ke first Lokpal Justice Pinaki Chandra Ghose the. Source ke 2024 update ke mutabik Justice Ajay\nManikrao Khanwilkar ne 10 March 2024 ko Lokpal Chairperson ka post assume kiya. [Q2, Q3]\n● Lokpal-Lokayukta aur Local Body Ombudsman ki recommendation First Administrative Reforms\nCommission (1966-70) ne ki. Commission initially Morarji Desai ke under tha; source notes 1967 mein\nK. Hanumanthaiah Chairman bane. Indian Ombudsman model = Lokpal; Ombudsman ka first\nestablishment Sweden, 1809. [Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● First Lokpal Bill 1968 mein Fourth Lok Sabha mein introduce hua; 1969 mein Lok Sabha se pass hua,\nlekin Rajya Sabha passage se pehle Lok Sabha dissolve hone par lapse ho gaya. [Q9]\n● Lokpal Bill 2011: 4 August 2011 ko Lok Sabha mein V. Narayanaswami ne introduce kiya; source ke\nhisab se Standing Committee ko refer hua aur Civil Society members ne ise “weak” kaha. [Q10]\n● Drafting panel ke Civil Society representatives source ke mutabik: Anna Hazare, Arvind Kejriwal, Shanti\nBhushan, N. Santosh Hegde aur Prashant Bhushan. [Q11]\n2. Lokayukta — Maharashtra, U.P., Uttarakhand & Rajasthan\n● Lokayukta institution sabse pehle Maharashtra mein: Maharashtra Lokayukta and Upa-Lokayuktas Act,\n1971; institution 25 October 1972 se effective. Source note: Odisha ne pehle legislation pass kiya tha,\nlekin institution 1983 tak operational nahi hua. [Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Uttar Pradesh Lokayukta apni report Governor ko submit karta hai; report State Legislature ke dono\nHouses ke saamne rakhi jaati hai. [Q15]\n● U.P. Lokayukta tenure source update: pehle 8 years; 26 Feb 2024 se amendment ke baad 5 years ya\nage 70, whichever earlier. [Q16]\n● 2011 mein Lokayukta Bill pass karne wala first Indian State source ke mutabik Uttarakhand tha (1 Nov\n2011). [Q17]\n● Rajasthan Lokayukta & Deputy Lokayukta Act, 1973 ke Section 7 mein ministers/public servants ke\ncorruption-misconduct allegations ki investigation ka scope diya gaya; source sexual harassment/caste\ndiscrimination/violence-against-children ko is specific Lokayukta subject list se bahar batata hai. [Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n● 2014 mein Rajasthan Government ne Advocate General Narpat Mal Lodha ki chairmanship mein existing\nLokayukta Act provisions review karne ke liye high-level committee banayi. [Q20]\n EXAM TRAP — Lokayukta ke ambit mein Chief Minister — time-sensitive item\n⚠\nQ18 ka source khud ise disputed maanta hai: option (c) question-time par correct tha, lekin baad mein kai\nstates mein CM ko Lokayukta ambit mein include kiya gaya. Is item ko static all-time list ki tarah mat padho.\n[Q18]\n3. Minority / Women / Education & Other Committees\n● Constitution “Minority” term ko define nahi karta. National Commission for Minorities ek statutory body\nhai, National Commission for Minorities Act, 1992 ke under; source statutory status 1993 note karta hai.\n[Q21]\n● Source update ke mutabik 6 notified minority communities: Muslims, Christians, Sikhs, Buddhists,\nZoroastrians aur Jains (Jains added in 2014). Constitution religious aur linguistic minorities ko\nrecognize/protect karta hai. [Q22]\n● Special Officer for Linguistic Minorities = Article 350B; 7th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1956 se add\nhua; President appoint karta hai aur provision all-India Union-level officer ka hai, har State ke separate\nofficer ka nahi. [Q23]\n● National Commission for Women Act, 1990 ke Section 10 mein NCW ke functions specified hain; source\nAct enforcement date 30 August 1990 deta hai. [Q24]\n● Secondary Education Commission (1952-53) ke Chairman Dr. A. Laxman Swami Mudaliar the; isliye ise\nMudaliar Commission bhi kaha gaya. [Q25]\n● Planning Commission 1950 mein establish hua aur later abolish hua; source: 1 January 2015 ko NITI\nAayog ne replace kiya. [Q26]\n● Vohra Committee (1993) ne criminalisation of politics aur criminals-politicians-bureaucrats nexus ko\nstudy/report kiya. [Q27, Q28]\n● Rajamannar Commission ne IAS aur IPS ko end karne ki recommendation di thi. [Q29]\n4. UDHR — Human Rights Basics & Generations\n● UDHR principles Indian Constitution ke multiple parts mein reflect hote hain: source Article 3 (life/liberty)\nko Preamble & FR, Article 26 (education) ko DPSP Article 45, aur Article 29 (duties to community) ko\nFundamental Duties se link karta hai. [Q30]\n● Universal Declaration of Human Rights UN General Assembly ne 10 December 1948 ko adopt kiya; total\n30 Articles; 10 December = Human Rights Day. [Q31, Q32, Q33]\n● UDHR Preamble ke source framing mein Human Rights ka central emphasis har human being ki dignity\naur justice par hai. [Q34]\n● Source exam framing: freedom, equality, life/liberty aur education UDHR rights mein hain; Q35 mein\n“right to privacy” ko is specific context mein not listed maana gaya, aur Q36 mein Universal Basic\nIncome ko UDHR right nahi maana gaya. [Q35, Q36]\n● Second-generation rights: source UDHR Articles 22-27 ko socio-economic/cultural rights batata hai;\nRight to Work (Art. 23) aur Right to Education (Art. 26) dono included. Social discrimination eradication\nko source conceptually second generation mein rakhta hai. [Q37, Q38]\n● “Right to the City” source ke mutabik universally agreed UN-Habitat-monitored right nahi; exam framing\npublic participation/use of city ko support karta hai, lekin unauthorized colonies ke services ko universal\nguarantee ke roop mein treat nahi karta. [Q39]\n EXAM TRAP — Human Rights question-key conflicts\n⚠\nQ37 multiple-correct hai (Work + Education). Q38 mein source conceptual answer “second generation” batata\nhai, jabki exam key ne different option hold kiya. Q35/Q39 ko bhi source-specific exam framing ke roop mein hi\npadho. [Q35, Q37, Q38, Q39]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n5. Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993 — Core Provisions\n● Protection of Human Rights Ordinance, 1993 President ne Article 123 ke under 28 September 1993 ko\npromulgate kiya. Source Act ko bhi 28 September 1993 se in force aur whole India tak extended batata\nhai. [Q40, Q41, Q42]\n● Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993 ka objective: NHRC, State Human Rights Commissions aur\nHuman Rights Courts ka constitution for better protection of human rights. [Q43]\n● Source definition: “Public Servant” Section 2(M), with meaning linked to IPC Section 21. [Q45]\n● Act ke “armed forces” definition mein naval, military, air force aur other armed forces of Union included;\nState armed forces source ke mutabik included nahi. [Q46]\n EXAM TRAP — NHRC purview — deleted/disputed item\n⚠\nQ44 ko MPPSC ne evaluation se delete kiya. Source ke explanation ke mutabik life, liberty, equality/dignity\njaise protected rights NHRC purview mein aate hain; given options mein clean “not under purview” answer nahi\ntha. [Q44]\n6. NHRC — Appointment, Composition, Tenure & Chairpersons\n● NHRC Chairperson/Members President appoint karta hai recommendation committee ke through: PM,\nLok Sabha Speaker, Union Home Minister, Lok Sabha LoP, Rajya Sabha LoP aur Rajya Sabha Deputy\nChairman. Rajya Sabha Chairman/Vice-President committee member nahi. [Q47, Q48]\n● Source composition framing: NHRC = Chairperson + four other members, plus 6 ex-officio members;\nLaw Commission Chairperson ex-officio member nahi. [Q49]\n● Protection of Human Rights (Amendment) Act, 2019 ke source update ke mutabik Chairperson/Members\nka term 3 years ya age 70, whichever earlier. [Q50, Q51, Q52]\n● 2019 amendment ke source framing mein NHRC Chairperson former CJI ya former Supreme Court\nJudge ho sakta hai; powers recommendatory hain; civil-society members 3 aur at least one woman. [Q53,\nQ54, Q55]\n● NHRC India 12 October 1993 ko established; first Chairperson Justice Ranganath Misra (12 Oct 1993–\n24 Nov 1996). [Q56]\n● Q57 source time note: 2021 question ke context mein H.L. Dattu past chairman the; source text later\n“currently Shri Justice V. Ramasubramanian” likhta hai. Is statement ko source-time fact ke roop mein\npreserve karo. [Q57]\n EXAM TRAP — NHRC old law vs 2019 amendment\n⚠\nQ50/Q52/Q53/Q55 ke options old law par based hone ki wajah se source ne disputed/outdated mark kiya.\nExam mein 5-year/retired-CJI-only wording ko current-amendment framing se confuse mat karo. [Q50, Q52,\nQ53, Q55]\n7. SHRC / Human Rights Courts — Appointment & Functions\n● State Human Rights Commission Chairperson eligibility source update: former Chief Justice of a High\nCourt OR former High Court Judge. [Q58]\n● SHRC Chairperson/Members Governor appoint karta hai recommendation committee par. Committee ka\nchair = Chief Minister; members source framing: Assembly Speaker, State Home Minister aur Leader of\nOpposition. Governor recommending committee ka member nahi. [Q59, Q60, Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● Sitting High Court Judge ya sitting District Judge ko SHRC member banane se pehle concerned High\nCourt ke Chief Justice se consultation required. [Q64]\n● SHRC Chairperson vacancy/absence mein Governor kisi member ko Acting Chairperson authorize kar\nsakta hai. [Q65]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n● Human Rights Commission functions mein human-rights research aur NGOs/organizations ke efforts\nencourage karna included. Commission ke powers investigative/recommendatory hain; violation ke liye\npunishment dena function nahi. [Q66, Q67]\n● State Commission annual report State Government ko submit karta hai; report action-taken\nmemorandum ke saath State Legislature ke saamne laid hoti hai. [Q68]\n● Commission/State Commission ke members aur authorized officers Act ke purposes ke liye “Public\nServant” deemed hote hain. [Q69]\n● Human Rights Courts ke Special Public Prosecutor ke liye advocate ka minimum practice source ke\nSection 31 framing mein 7 years. [Q70]\n● Specified IPC sections (175, 178, 179, 180, 228) ke purposes ke liye Human Rights Commission Civil\nCourt deemed hota hai. [Q71]\n● Armed-forces human-rights complaints mein Commission ka role limited: Central Government se report\nseekh sakta hai aur recommendations de sakta hai. [Q72]\n EXAM TRAP — SHRC appointment MCQ\n⚠\nQ63 mein source ne multiple correct (Assembly Speaker + LoP) mark kiya hai. [Q63]\n8. Constitutional vs Statutory Bodies & Misc. Commissions\n● Human Rights Commission/NHRC statutory, non-Constitutional body hai. Source contrast: State Finance\nCommission (Art. 243-I), Parliament Secretariat (Art. 98), Finance Commission (Art. 280) constitutional\nreferences hain. [Q73, Q74]\n● Establishment-year matching source: Inter-State Council 1990, National Development Council 1952 (not\n1954), CVC 1964, NHRC 1993. [Q75]\n● Independent India ka First Law Commission 1955 mein constituted; Chairman M.C. Setalvad (then\nAttorney General). [Q76]\n● National Commission to Review the Working of the Constitution (2000) Justice M.N. Venkatachaliah ke\nunder; executive order se set up, Parliament approval nahi; report recommendatory. [Q77, Q78]\n● Swaran Singh Committee (1976) ne source ke mutabik DPSP ko Fundamental Rights par priority dene\nke question ko consider kiya; 42nd Amendment ko recommendations ka major result bataya gaya. [Q80]\n EXAM TRAP — Central Pollution Control Board Chairman — deleted question\n⚠\nQ79 mein source ke mutabik none of the options correct the; environment-protection knowledge/practical\nexperience wala person Central Government nominate karta hai. MPPSC ne question evaluation se omit kiya.\n[Q79]\n9. CVC, Mandal Commission & SC/ST Commission\n● Central Vigilance Commission ki establishment Santhanam Committee on Prevention of Corruption\n(1962-64), chaired by K. Santhanam, ki recommendation par 1964 mein hui. [Q81, Q82, Q83]\n● CVC Constitution ke kisi Article mein described nahi; initially neither constitutional nor statutory, source\nke mutabik 2003 mein parliamentary law se statutory status mila. [Q84]\n● Institution-year trap source: CBI 1963, CVC 1964, Enforcement Directorate 1956 (not 2000), Prevention\nof Corruption Act 1988 (not 1985). [Q85]\n● Mandal Commission 1979 mein Janata Party Government under Morarji Desai; Chair B.P. (Bindheshwari\nPrasad) Mandal; mandate socially & educationally backward persons identify karna; report 1980. [Q86,\nQ87]\n● 1990 National Commission for SC/ST report ke source causes of atrocities: land disputes, tribal land\nalienation, bonded labour, indebtedness, non-payment of minimum wages; religious causes main cause\nlist mein nahi. [Q88]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — CVC / institution-year MCQ\n⚠\nQ85 multiple-correct hai: Prevention of Corruption Act 1985 aur ED 2000 dono mismatched the. [Q85]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Lokpal & Important Commissions Full Mind Map\n10. UPSC / SPSC — Constitutional Framework\n● Public Service Commissions ke constitutional provisions Part XIV, Articles 315-323 mein. Article 315\nUnion ke liye UPSC aur States ke liye SPSC provide karta hai. UPSC aur State PSC apne respective\nspheres mein independent constitutional bodies hain. [Q89, Q90, Q91]\n● UPSC functions ka source base: Constitution (Art. 320), Parliamentary laws (Art. 321 extension),\nexecutive rules/orders aur conventions. [Q92]\n● Article 323: UPSC annual report President ko submit karta hai. [Q93]\n● Article 315(2): 2+ States resolutions pass karein to Parliament law se Joint State Public Service\nCommission establish kar sakta hai. Joint Commission ka Chairperson/Members Article 316(1) ke\nsource framing mein President appoint karta hai. [Q94, Q95, Q96]\n11. Public Service Commissions — Appointment, Removal & Functions\n● Article 316: State PSC Chairperson aur Members Governor appoint karta hai; source repeatedly\nemphasizes removal President karta hai. [Q97, Q98, Q99, Q102]\n● Article 317: PSC Chairperson/Member misbehaviour ground par Supreme Court inquiry ke baad\nPresident order se remove ho sakta hai. UPSC Chairman removal mein Parliament ka role nahi; source\ninsolvency, paid employment, infirmity jaise direct grounds bhi note karta hai. [Q100, Q101, Q104, Q105]\n● Article 320(3)(c): disciplinary matters affecting State civil servants par SPSC consultation; routine\ntransfers ke liye SPSC consultation function nahi. [Q103, Q106]\n● Article 315(4): Governor request + President approval par UPSC State ki needs serve kar sakta hai.\n[Q107, Q108]\n● Article 321: State Legislature Act se State PSC ke additional functions extend kar sakta hai. [Q109]\n● Article 322: PSC expenses; State PSC expenses State Consolidated Fund par charged. [Q110, Q111]\n● Article 323(2): State PSC annual report Governor ko submit karta hai. [Q112]\n12. PSC History, Bureaucracy & Civil Services Reforms\n● Source history: Government of India Act, 1919 ke under first Public Service Commission 1 October 1926\nko set up hua; one Chairman + four members. [Q113]\n● MPPSC source-specific: States Reorganisation Act, 1956 Section 118(3) ke under President dwara\nconstituted; source maximum 5 members batata hai. Article 318 service-condition regulations ki power\nse linked hai. [Q114, Q115]\n● Source ke mutabik UPSC ki first woman Chairperson Mrs. Roze Millian Bethew thi, tenure 1992-1996.\n[Q116]\n● Indian bureaucracy ko source policies/laws ko implementation ke through public tak le jaane wali\ngovernment agency ke roop mein describe karta hai. [Q117]\n● Doctrine of Pleasure = Article 310; Union/defence/All-India services President ke pleasure par, State civil\nservants Governor ke pleasure par office hold karte hain. [Q118]\n● UPSC ne July 2000 mein Civil Services Examination review ke liye Professor Sukhadeo Thorat ki\nchairmanship mein committee constitute ki. [Q119]\n● P.C. Hota Committee on Civil Services Reforms source ke mutabik February 2004 mein\nconstituted/chaired by P.C. Hota; report six months mein submit hui. [Q120]\n● Civil Services Day India mein every year 21 April; source reason: 21 April 1947 ko Sardar Vallabhbhai\nPatel ne Metcalf House mein first batch of civil servants ko address kiya. [Q121]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0287","t":"36 Temporary Special Provisions","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Temporary Special Provisions Full Mind Map\n TEMPORARY SPECIAL PROVISIONS — FULL\n🏛️\n\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Part XXI — Special Provisions for Different States\n2. Article 371 — Maharashtra & Gujarat\n3. Article 371-B — Assam Tribal Areas\n4. Article 371-J — Hyderabad-Karnataka Region\n5. Article 370 — Jammu & Kashmir: Historical Special Position\n6. Jammu & Kashmir — Sadr-e-Riyasat & Constitutional Chronology\n7. Special Category Status (SCS) — Criteria & State Examples\n8. Exam Traps — Post-2019 / Source-Specific Questions\n1. Part XXI — Special Provisions for Different States\n● Indian Constitution ke Part XXI mein temporary, transitional aur special provisions aate hain. Source ke\nmutabik Articles 371 se 371-J Maharashtra, Gujarat, Nagaland, Assam, Manipur, Andhra Pradesh,\nTelangana, Sikkim, Mizoram, Arunachal Pradesh, Goa aur Karnataka ke liye special provisions se deal\nkarte hain. [Q1]\n2. Article 371 — Maharashtra & Gujarat\n● Article 371 Maharashtra aur Gujarat ke liye special provisions provide karta hai. [Q3]\n3. Article 371-B — Assam Tribal Areas\n● Article 371-B Assam ke tribal areas ke liye special provision se related hai; source ise Part XXI ke\ntemporary/transitional/special provisions ke context mein explain karta hai. [Q2]\n4. Article 371-J — Hyderabad-Karnataka Region\n● Article 371-J ko Constitution (Ninety-Eighth Amendment) Act, 2012 se Part XXI mein insert kiya gaya.\nSource ke mutabik yeh Karnataka ke Governor ko Hyderabad-Karnataka region ke development ke liye\nsteps lene ki power deta hai. [Q4]\n5. Article 370 — Jammu & Kashmir: Historical Special Position\n● Source ke historical framing mein Jammu & Kashmir Article 370 ke under temporary special provisions\nenjoy karta tha aur uska separate Constitution tha; isi wajah se all-India single-Constitution pattern ka\nexception maana gaya. Article 370 ko source temporary provision batata hai. [Q5, Q8, Q9]\n● Source ke mutabik question-period context mein Article 1 aur Article 370 Jammu & Kashmir par\nautomatically applicable the: Article 1 ne J&K ko Indian territory ka integral part bataya, aur Article 370\nne special status diya. [Q10]\n● Article 370 earlier Jammu & Kashmir ko special status provide karta tha; source current note mein kehta\nhai ki ab Jammu & Kashmir ko woh special status nahi hai. [Q11]\n● Source ke historical explanation mein J&K ki administration/provisions other States se different thi, uska\nseparate Constitution tha, aur State Article 152 ki definition ke context mein exception ke roop mein\ndiscussed hai. [Q7]\n6. Jammu & Kashmir — Sadr-e-Riyasat & Constitutional Chronology\n● Source ke mutabik J&K Constituent Assembly ne hereditary Maharaja rule abolish kiya aur Karan Singh\nko first Sadr-e-Riyasat elect kiya; later J&K Constitution ke Sixth Amendment Act, 1965 se designation\n“Sadr-e-Riyasat” ko “Governor” rename kiya gaya. [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Temporary Special Provisions Full Mind Map\n● Source chronology: Maharaja Hari Singh ne Instrument of Accession 26 Oct 1947 ko sign kiya; source\ntext Constitution of India enforcement ko 26 Nov 1950 likhta hai; J&K Constituent Assembly ne\naccession 17 Nov 1956 ko ratify kiya; State Constitution 26 Jan 1957 ko in force aaya. [Q13]\n7. Special Category Status (SCS) — Criteria & State Examples\n● Source ke Special Category Status (SCS) section mein Gadgil Formula-based parameters bataye gaye\nhain: hilly terrain, low population density/significant tribal population, international-border strategic\nlocation, economic/infrastructural backwardness aur weak financial viability. [Q6]\n● Source ke 2019 framing mein Sikkim, Himachal Pradesh aur Jammu & Kashmir SCS list ke examples\nthe, jabki Bihar ko Special Category Status nahi diya gaya tha; source total 11 States ko historically SCS\ngranted batata hai. [Q14]\n8. Exam Traps — Post-2019 / Source-Specific Questions\n EXAM TRAP — Article 370 / Jammu & Kashmir — post-2019 change\n⚠\nQ5, Q7, Q10 aur Q11 ko source ne disputed mark kiya hai because ye questions pre-2019 constitutional\nposition par based the. Source note ke mutabik Article 370 6 Aug 2019 se inoperative/abrogated bataya gaya\naur former State ko Jammu & Kashmir aur Ladakh Union Territories mein reorganise kiya gaya. [Q5, Q7, Q10,\nQ11]\n EXAM TRAP — Sadr-e-Riyasat Question — none of the options correct\n⚠\nQ12 ke source explanation ke mutabik designation 1965 mein J&K Constitution ke Sixth Amendment se\nGovernor hua; isi wajah se given options mein correct answer nahi tha. [Q12]\n EXAM TRAP — Chronology — source date exactly preserve karo\n⚠\nQ13 ke source explanation mein “Constitution of India was enforced on 26 November, 1950” likha hai. Is DOCX\nmein source ko silently correct nahi kiya gaya; is date ko source-specific statement ke roop mein hi preserve\nkiya gaya hai. [Q13]\n EXAM TRAP — SCS vs Article 371-series\n⚠\nQ6 aur Q14 “Special Category Status” policy classification ke questions hain, jabki Q1–Q4 Articles 371-series\nke constitutional special provisions par hain. Source chapter dono ko ek saath rakhta hai; exam mein dono\nconcepts ko mix mat karo. [Q6, Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0288","t":"37 Election Commission","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Election Commission Full Mind Map\n ELECTION COMMISSION — FULL MIND MAP\n🗳️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Article 324 — Constitutional Base, Composition & Appointment\n2. Tenure, Salary, Resignation & Removal\n3. ECI Functions, Scope & Election Process\n4. Election Systems, Disqualification & Model Code of Conduct\n5. Right to Vote, Adult Suffrage & Voting Age\n6. One Nation One Election & Election Surveys\n7. RPA Rules, Candidate Limits & Electoral Reform Committees\n8. Delimitation Commission & Reserved Constituencies\n9. Proportional Representation & Low-Turnout Questions\n10. VVPAT, Election Commission History & National Voters’ Day\n11. Exam Traps — Source-Specific / Time-Sensitive Questions\n1. Article 324 — Constitutional Base, Composition & Appointment\n● Article 324 Election Commission ko constitutional base deta hai: electoral rolls ki preparation aur\nParliament, State Legislatures, President aur Vice-President ke elections ka superintendence, direction\n& control ECI mein vested hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● Chief Election Commissioner aur other Election Commissioners ko President appoint karta hai; source\nArticle 324(2) ko Parliament-made law ke subject ke roop mein explain karta hai. [Q3]\n● Source ke according present structure 1 CEC + 2 ECs ka three-member body hai; sabki powers equal\nhain aur difference of opinion majority decision se decide hota hai. [Q4]\n● Election Commission 25 January 1950 ko establish hua. Source ke mutabik 1 October 1993 se two\nadditional ECs ke saath multi-member body permanently continue hui; Article 103/192 matters mein\nadvisory jurisdiction bhi batayi gayi hai. [Q5]\n● Recognised political parties ke split/merger disputes ECI resolve karta hai; general aur bye-election\nschedule bhi ECI decide karta hai, Home Ministry nahi. [Q19]\n● History point: 16 October 1989 ko two additional Commissioners appoint hue, jo 1 January 1990 tak\nrahe; 1 October 1993 ko phir two ECs appoint hue aur commission permanently three-member bana.\n[Q57]\n2. Tenure, Salary, Resignation & Removal\n● Source framing mein CEC/EC ki powers, salary & allowances equal bataye gaye hain; CEC salary ko\nSupreme Court Judge ke salary ke equal aur tenure 6 years ya age 65, whichever earlier, bataya gaya\nhai. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9]\n● CEC/EC resignation President ko address ki jaati hai — Election Commissioner apna resignation CEC ko\naddress nahi karta. [Q7, Q8]\n● CEC ko Article 324(5) ke under Supreme Court Judge ke like manner aur like grounds par remove kiya\njaata hai. [Q12]\n● Other Election Commissioner ko President, Chief Election Commissioner ki recommendation par remove\nkarta hai. [Q13]\n● Status/rank wale source question mein options mein exact answer nahi tha; explanation CEC ko\nprecedence rank 9(A) par UPSC Chairperson aur CAG ke saath place karti hai. [Q10]\n● Assertion–Reason source: free & fair elections ke powers independent ECI ko diye gaye hain; other ECs\nka removal executive/President se linked hai, lekin yeh independence ka correct explanation nahi hai.\n[Q11]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Election Commission Full Mind Map\n3. ECI Functions, Scope & Election Process\n● ECI Parliament, State Legislature, President aur Vice-President elections conduct/supervise karta hai aur\nelectoral rolls ki preparation control karta hai; free-fair election na ho paane par President’s Rule\nrecommend karna source ke according uska function nahi. [Q14]\n● Election law-making provisions Parliament (Article 327) aur State Legislatures (Article 328) ka domain\nhain; yeh Election Commission ka legislative function nahi. [Q15]\n● Panchayat aur Municipality elections ECI nahi, State Election Commission conduct karta hai; source\nArticles 243K aur 243ZA cite karta hai. [Q16]\n● Speaker/Deputy Speaker/Deputy Chairman elections respective Houses ke members internally karte\nhain; local-body elections SEC karta hai; election disputes Judiciary handle karti hai — isliye diye gaye\nfunctions mein none ECI function tha. [Q17, Q18]\n● Election notification Lok Sabha/Rajya Sabha ke liye President aur State Legislature ke liye concerned\nGovernor issue karta hai; election process ECI recommendation ke baad notification se commence hota\nhai, phir dates/timing ECI issue karta hai. [Q20, Q21]\n4. Election Systems, Disqualification & Model Code of Conduct\n● India mein direct adult-suffrage elections aur indirect proportional representation by single transferable\nvote dono systems use hote hain; President, Vice-President, Rajya Sabha & Legislative Council ke liye\nPR-STV aur Lok Sabha/Assemblies ke liye direct adult suffrage source mein diya hai. [Q22]\n● Article 103 ke under MP disqualification question President decide karta hai, lekin decision se pehle\nElection Commission ki opinion lena aur uske according act karna hota hai. [Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Security deposit rule: source ke according candidate ko valid votes ka more than one-sixth secure na ho\nto deposit forfeit hota hai; winning candidate bhi highly fragmented contest mein 1/6 se kam paa sakta\nhai. [Q26]\n● Conviction-based disqualification source Representation of the People Act, 1951 Section 8(3) se link\nkarta hai: at least 2 years imprisonment par conviction date se disqualification aur release ke baad\nfurther 6 years. [Q27]\n● Model Code of Conduct election schedule announce hote hi apply hota hai; source clearly kehta hai ki\nMCC Parliament ne enact nahi kiya, Election Commission ne formulate kiya. [Q28]\n5. Right to Vote, Adult Suffrage & Voting Age\n● Source chapter Right to Vote aur Right to be Elected ko legal/statutory right batata hai, fundamental right\nnahi. [Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● 61st Constitutional Amendment Act ne voting age 21 se 18 years ki; source ke mutabik 18-year voting\nfirst time November 1989 Lok Sabha General Election mein use hui. [Q32, Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Article 326 Lok Sabha aur State Legislative Assemblies ke elections ko adult suffrage ke basis par\nprovide karta hai. [Q36, Q37]\n● Source 18 years ko legal voting age/majority-related election point ke roop mein 61st Amendment aur\nRPA changes se explain karta hai. [Q38]\n● March 2024 source update: Conduct of Elections Rules, 1961 ke Rule 27A amendment ke baad home\npostal-ballot facility ke senior-citizen threshold ko 80 se 85 years bataya gaya hai. [Q39]\n● State Legislature election principles: adult suffrage, har territorial constituency ke liye one electoral roll,\nreligion/race/sex basis par exclusion nahi; source given fourth statement (political parties’ own norms) ko\nbhi correct set mein include karta hai. [Q40]\n6. One Nation One Election & Election Surveys\n● Source ke according “One Nation, One Election” implement karne ke liye multiple constitutional\nprovisions touch ho sakte hain — Articles 83, 85, 172, 174 aur 356; isliye single-Article answer nahi.\n[Q41]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Election Commission Full Mind Map\n● High-Level Committee on Simultaneous Elections 2 September 2023 ko former President Ram Nath\nKovind ki chairmanship mein constituted batayi gayi; source list mein Amit Shah, Ghulam Nabi Azad,\nN.K. Singh, Subhash C. Kashyap, Harish Salve, Sanjay Kothari hain, aur Tushar Mehta member nahi.\n[Q42]\n● Exit Poll post-election voter survey hota hai — voter ne kis candidate ko vote diya us par; Opinion Poll\nelection se pehle public preference measure karta hai. [Q43]\n7. RPA Rules, Candidate Limits & Electoral Reform Committees\n● Source statistical question 2009 Lok Sabha election ke total electors ko 714 million batata hai. [Q44]\n● RPA 1951 Section 33 source framing: ek general election mein maximum two Parliamentary\nconstituencies se contest kiya ja sakta hai; Devi Lal ne 1991 mein three constituencies se contest kiya\ntha, 1996 restriction se pehle; party ko vacated-seat bye-election cost bear karne ka rule source mein\nnahi. [Q45]\n● Representation of the People (Amendment) Act, 1996 ke source statements mein National\nFlag/Constitution insult conviction disqualification, increased security deposit aur candidate-death par\nelection countermand na karna correct; “only one constituency” incorrect, maximum two hai. [Q46]\n● Dinesh Goswami Committee electoral reforms se related thi aur source uski recommendation mein\nParliamentary elections ke state/government funding ko highlight karta hai. [Q47, Q48]\n8. Delimitation Commission & Reserved Constituencies\n● Source ke mutabik 543 elected Lok Sabha seats mein 84 SC aur 47 ST reserved seats hain; kaunsi\nconstituency reserve hogi yeh Delimitation Commission decide karta hai, Lok Sabha Speaker nahi. [Q49]\n● Delimitation Commission ke orders final hote hain: Court of Law mein challenge nahi kiye ja sakte aur\nLok Sabha/State Assembly un orders ko modify nahi kar sakti. [Q50]\n● December 2023 tak source accepted answer four main Delimitation Commissions batata hai — 1952,\n1963, 1973 aur 2002; source 2020 specific states/UT commission ko note karke bhi “four main\ncommissions” answer preserve karta hai. [Q51]\n9. Proportional Representation & Low-Turnout Questions\n● Proportional Representation minority representation ki problem ko kuch extent tak solve karta hai, kyunki\ngroups ko numerical strength ke proportion mein representation mil sakta hai; source A-R mein Reason\nko Assertion ka correct explanation maanta hai. [Q52, Q53]\n● Source ke according mature two-party system wale country mein proportional representation ki necessity\nlargely reduce ho jaati hai. [Q54]\n● Low turnout previous election se kam ho to na automatic re-election warranted hai aur na non-voters ka\nvoting right cancel kiya ja sakta hai; source dono proposed actions ko reject karta hai. [Q55]\n10. VVPAT, Election Commission History & National Voters’ Day\n● Source M3 version ko India mein used VVPAT/EVM generation point batata hai; M3 EVMs mein up to\n384 candidates data, tamper detection aur self-diagnostics features diye gaye hain. [Q56]\n● Historical personnel question: source ke according 2000 mein M.S. Gill CEC the, T.S. Krishnamurti aur\nJ.M. Lyngdoh ECs the; N.B. Lohani member nahi the. [Q58]\n● Sukumar Sen first Chief Election Commissioner the; V.S. Ramadevi first woman Chief Election\nCommissioner thi, source 1990 year bhi deta hai. [Q59, Q60]\n● National Voters’ Day har saal 25 January ko Election Commission ke foundation day mark karne ke liye\ncelebrate hota hai; source start year 2011 deta hai. [Q61, Q62]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Election Commission Full Mind Map\n11. Exam Traps — Source-Specific / Time-Sensitive Questions\n EXAM TRAP — CEC Status — options mein exact rank missing\n⚠\nQ10 ke source explanation mein CEC ko precedence rank 9(A), UPSC Chairperson aur CAG ke saath diya\ngaya hai; listed options mein exact answer nahi tha. [Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — ECI vs State Election Commission vs Judiciary\n⚠\nSpeaker/Deputy Speaker/Deputy Chairman internal House elections hain, local-body elections State Election\nCommission karta hai, aur disputes Judiciary handle karti hai — ECI ka scope in tino se alag rakho. [Q16, Q17,\nQ18]\n EXAM TRAP — Postal Ballot — March 2024 source update\n⚠\nQ39 ka answer specifically March 2024 rule-change context mein 85 years threshold batata hai; isko source-\ndate ke saath yaad rakho. [Q39]\n EXAM TRAP — One Nation One Election — More than one Article\n⚠\nSource Q41 single Article ko sufficient nahi maanta; Articles 83, 85, 172, 174 aur 356 tak multiple provisions\nmention karta hai. [Q41]\n EXAM TRAP — Delimitation Commissions — “4 main” source convention\n⚠\nQ51 source 2020 specific commission ko note karta hai, phir bhi specific Delimitation Acts ke basis par four\nmain commissions ko accepted answer rakhta hai. [Q51]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0289","t":"38 Political Parties","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Political Parties Full Mind Map\n POLITICAL PARTIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🗳️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Registration & Recognition — Election Commission and Symbols Order\n2. National Party Recognition — Three Alternative Criteria\n3. State / Regional Party Recognition — Vote & Seat Tests\n4. Major Parties — Founders, Formation Years & Chronology\n5. Trade Unions, Alliances & Lok Sabha Election Performance\n6. Indian Party System — Majority, Regionalism, Pressure Groups & Inner Democracy\n7. Anti-Defection Law — 52nd Amendment, Tenth Schedule & Exceptions\n8. FPTP, Vote–Seat Distortion & Opposition Recognition\n9. Communist Politics — Bhu-Poratam & Social Base\n10. Kamaraj Plan & Electoral Bond Scheme (Source-era Facts)\n11. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-Sensitive Source Questions\n1. Registration & Recognition — Election Commission and Symbols Order\n● Representation of the People Act, 1951 political parties ke registration ka provision deta hai; registration\nElection Commission of India karta hai. Source 1999 General Election mein 6 National aur 48 State-level\nrecognised parties ka historical figure bhi deta hai. [Q1]\n● National/State (Regional) party recognition Election Commission karta hai, Election Symbols\n(Reservation and Allotment) Order, 1968 ke norms ke according. Parliament, President, Law Ministry ya\nSupreme Court recognition authority nahi hain. [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n2. National Party Recognition — Three Alternative Criteria\n● Source ke mutabik National Party banne ke 3 alternative routes hain: (i) 4+ States mein 6% valid votes +\nat least 4 Lok Sabha seats; OR (ii) Lok Sabha ki at least 2% seats, members at least 3 different States\nse; OR (iii) at least 4 States mein State Party recognition. [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n3. State / Regional Party Recognition — Vote & Seat Tests\n● State Party recognition ke source criteria mein Assembly mein 3 seats ya 3% seats (whichever greater),\nState ke allotted Lok Sabha seats ke ratio se seat test, 6% vote + seat test, ya 8% total vote-share jaisi\nalternative qualifications di gayi hain. [Q8]\n● Specific criterion: State Assembly election mein 6% valid votes + 2 Assembly seats; ya Lok Sabha\nelection mein 6% valid votes + 1 Lok Sabha seat. Q9 mein 6% vote statements ko seat condition ke\nsaath read karna zaroori hai. [Q9]\n4. Major Parties — Founders, Formation Years & Chronology\n● Indian National Congress ke naam mein 'National' word ko source British rule ke against reaction se\ninfluenced batata hai. Nationalist Congress Party 10 June 1999 ko Sharad Pawar, P.A. Sangma aur\nTariq Anwar ne Congress se split ke baad banayi. [Q10, Q11]\n● Source-current list mein 6 National Parties diye gaye hain: BJP, INC, BSP, AAP, CPI(M) aur National\nPeople's Party; Q12 ke options mein Muslim League, RSP, Forward Bloc aur Peasants & Workers Party\nmein se koi National Party nahi. [Q12]\n● Trinamool Congress ko 2 September 2016 ko National Party status mila tha; source khud note karta hai\nki current scenario mein TMC National Party nahi hai. [Q13]\n● Bharatiya Janata Party 1980 mein bani aur Atal Bihari Vajpayee first President bane; BJP ko Bharatiya\nJana Sangh ka successor bataya gaya hai, jise Dr. Shyama Prasad Mukherjee ne found kiya. [Q14]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Political Parties Full Mind Map\n● Samajwadi Party National Party nahi; source 4 October 1992, Lucknow aur Mulayam Singh Yadav\nleadership note karta hai. Akali Dal Punjab ki regional party hai; Telugu Desam Party Andhra Pradesh ki\nregional party. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● AAP ke 2019-era question mein State-level registered party answer tha; source updated note deta hai ki\npresent/source-current scenario mein AAP National Party hai. [Q18]\n● Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ne Independent Labour Party (1936) aur Scheduled Castes Federation (1942)\nbanaye; source Samata Sainik Dal aur Depressed Classes Federation bhi unse link karta hai. Peasants\n& Workers Party of India Ambedkar-founded nahi thi. [Q19, Q20]\n● Leader–party matches: Bharatiya Jana Sangh — Shyama Prasad Mukherjee; Congress for Democracy\n— Jagjivan Ram. Socialist Party se J.P. Narayan, Ram Manohar Lohia, Acharya Narendra Dev jude; C.\nRajagopalachari Swatantra Party founder-leader the. [Q21]\n● Formation-year map: CPI — 1920 Tashkent reference / 1925 Kanpur-India reference; CPI(M) — 1964;\nAIADMK — 1972; TDP — 1982; INC — 1885; Jana Sangh — 1951; BSP — 1984; AITC — 1998. CPI\nsplit se CPI(M) 1964 mein bana. [Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Chronology asked in source: Telugu Desam Party (1982) → Bahujan Samaj Party (1984) → Samajwadi\nParty (1992) → All India Trinamool Congress (1998). [Q26]\n5. Trade Unions, Alliances & Lok Sabha Election Performance\n● Trade-union affiliations: BMS — BJP; INTUC — INC; AITUC — CPI. Source UTUC ko Revolutionary\nSocialist Party se link karta hai, isi wajah se given matching question disputed tha. [Q27]\n● United Front Government (1996–97) ke context mein source ke mutabik BSP, Samata Party aur Haryana\nVikas Party United Front ka hissa nahi the; Asom Gana Parishad hissa tha. [Q28]\n● BJP vote-share data source: 1984 — 7.4%, 1989 — 11.4%, 1991 — 22.4%. [Q29]\n● 2004 Lok Sabha source data: INC 145 seats, BJP 138 seats, CPI(M) 43 seats; question ke BJP 133 aur\nCPI(M) 48 wale statements incorrect the. [Q30]\n● 13th Lok Sabha source figures: CPI(M) 32, TDP 29, BSP 14, BJD 10; TDP ke 33 seats wala match\nincorrect tha. [Q31]\n● 1989 Lok Sabha election ko 'Congress System' ke end ke roop mein source explain karta hai; Congress\n197 seats ke saath single largest party thi, par Janata Dal coalition ne BJP/Left outside support ke saath\nV.P. Singh government banayi. [Q32]\n● Coalition-government Assertion–Reason mein source dono statements true maanta hai, lekin Reason ko\nAssertion ka correct explanation nahi maanta. [Q33]\n● Regional-party-in-power question mein source Kerala ko answer deta hai, jahan Congress/CPI(M)\nalternation ka historical framing hai; J&K ko 2019 reorganisation ke baad State nahi, UT note kiya gaya\nhai. [Q34]\n6. Indian Party System — Majority, Regionalism, Pressure Groups & Inner\nDemocracy\n● India ke FPTP/relative-majority system mein government majority seats se banti hai, necessarily majority\npopular votes se nahi; source isi ko vote-share aur seat-share ke difference ka explanation maanta hai.\n[Q35]\n● 1997-era women-reservation question: Parliament/State Legislatures mein 33% seat reservation ke liye\nconstitutional amendment required bataya gaya; political parties bina amendment apne tickets ka 33%\nwomen ko allocate kar sakti hain. [Q36]\n● India ka party system fixed nahi aur multi-party character strong hai; source casteism, regionalism aur\nother socio-economic reasons ko factors batata hai — sirf parties ki large number hi sole cause nahi.\n[Q37]\n● Party system larger political system ka part hai; democratic government formation/running political\nparties ke through hota hai. [Q38]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Political Parties Full Mind Map\n● Strong regional parties regional aspirations ko reflect karti hain; source written Constitution aur regional-\nparty growth dono statements ko true but unrelated maanta hai. [Q39]\n● Pressure groups elections mein candidates khade nahi karte, par policy/legislation influence karte hain;\ntrade unions, farmer organisations, women organisations aur business organisations examples hain.\n[Q40]\n● Inner-party democracy ka core source-definition: party office-bearers ko elect karne ke liye periodic\ninternal elections. [Q41]\n● Rajni Kothari ne early post-Independence Indian party system ko 'one party dominant system' describe\nkiya. [Q42]\n7. Anti-Defection Law — 52nd Amendment, Tenth Schedule & Exceptions\n● Anti-Defection Law Parliament ne 15 February 1985 ko pass kiya aur 1 March 1985 se force mein aaya;\n52nd Constitutional Amendment ne Articles 101, 102, 190, 191 amend karke Tenth Schedule add kiya.\nSource isi 1985 change ko political parties ki first constitutional recognition se link karta hai. [Q43, Q45]\n● Source ke specific formulation mein larger defections in a party in various spells Anti-Defection Law ke\ncovered situations mein nahi aate. [Q44]\n● Merger exception tab recognise hota hai jab legislature party ke at least two-thirds members merger\nagree karein. [Q46]\n● Nominated legislator political party ko appointment ke 6 months ke andar join kar sakta hai; 6 months ke\nbaad join karne par disqualification ho sakti hai. Presiding Officer ko defection case decide karne ke liye\nlaw koi fixed time-frame nahi deta. [Q47]\n● Presiding Officer exception: Speaker/Chairman banne ke baad member apni party membership chhod\nsakta hai aur office chhodne ke baad rejoin kar sakta hai, impartiality/dignity ke reason se defection\ndisqualification exception milta hai. [Q48, Q49]\n● Source historical fact: Jammu & Kashmir Legislative Assembly ne 1979 mein Anti-Defection Law enact\nkiya tha. [Q50]\n8. FPTP, Vote–Seat Distortion & Opposition Recognition\n● Karnataka 1994 vote–seat distortion ko source First-Past-The-Post system se explain karta hai: highest\nvotes wala candidate wins; total vote percentage proportional seat allocation decide nahi karta. [Q51]\n● Lok Sabha Opposition recognition ke source convention mein at least one-tenth House strength, i.e. 543\nke context mein 54 seats, batayi gayi; given options exact match nahi karte the. [Q52]\n9. Communist Politics — Bhu-Poratam & Social Base\n● 'Bhu-Poratam' land-struggle source ke mutabik Andhra Pradesh mein Bharatiya Khet Mazdoor Union\n(BKMU) / communist mobilisation se linked tha, landless agricultural workers ke land/house-site\ndemands ke liye. [Q53]\n● Business class ko source Communist Party ka social base nahi maanta, kyunki communist politics\ncapitalism oppose karti hai jabki business class capitalism-supporting framing mein diya gaya. [Q54]\n10. Kamaraj Plan & Electoral Bond Scheme (Source-era Facts)\n● Kamaraj Plan 1963 mein K. Kamaraj ne Indian National Congress ko 'vibrant' / organisationally\nstrengthen karne ke purpose se prepare kiya. [Q55]\n● Source-era Electoral Bond Scheme 2018 facts: 2 January 2018 notification; RPA 1951 Section 29A-\nregistered party + last General Election mein at least 1% votes eligibility; bond 15 calendar days valid;\neligible party account mein deposit same day credit. Question ka 2% threshold statement incorrect tha.\n[Q56]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Political Parties Full Mind Map\n11. Exam Traps — Disputed / Time-Sensitive Source Questions\n EXAM TRAP — National / State Party Criteria — Exact Options Matter\n⚠\nQ5 aur Q6 mein source ke valid recognition rules diye gaye hain, lekin options exact fit nahi karte. Q8 mein\nsource explicitly U.P.P.S.C. official key ko incorrect batata hai aur option (c) ko more suitable maanta hai. [Q5,\nQ6, Q8]\n EXAM TRAP — National Party Status Is Time-Sensitive\n⚠\nQ13 TMC ko 2016 mein National Party recognition ka historical fact deta hai aur source note karta hai ki\ncurrent/source-current scenario mein TMC National Party nahi. Q18 AAP ko 2019 question-time par State-level\nregistered party batata hai, saath hi updated source-note mein National Party kehta hai. [Q13, Q18]\n EXAM TRAP — CPI Founding Date — 1920 vs 1925\n⚠\nSource Q22 Tashkent establishment 17 October 1920 note karta hai, jabki India mein CPI founding 1925\nKanpur ke roop mein explain karta hai; Q23 matching mein CPI — 1925 use hota hai. Context dekhkar answer\nkaro. [Q22, Q23]\n EXAM TRAP — Historic / Disputed Source Items\n⚠\nQ27 trade-union match disputed hai; Q34 political-party-in-power item date-sensitive hai; Q36 1997-era\nwomen-reservation framing hai; Q52 Opposition recognition options exact nahi; Q56 Electoral Bond facts 2018\nscheme ke source-era description hain. Inhe silently current-rule ke roop mein generalise mat karo. [Q27, Q34,\nQ36, Q52, Q56]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0290","t":"39 Constitutional Amendments","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constitutional Amendments Full Mind Map\n🧩 CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENTS — FULL\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Article 368 — Power, Procedure & Initiation\n2. State Ratification — Half of States & Federal Provisions\n3. Passage, President Assent & No Joint Sitting\n4. Early Amendments — 1st, 15th & 26th\n5. Amendment Mapping & Chronology — 13th to 99th\n6. 42nd, 44th & NJAC — High-Yield Changes\n7. Anti-Defection, Hindi Text, Voting Age & Delhi\n8. Reservation, RTE, Commissions & Ministry Size\n9. Co-operatives, Land Boundary, GST & 105th\n10. Basic Structure Doctrine & Major Cases\n11. DPSP vs FR & Amendment-Case Matching\n12. Nari Shakti, 98th Bill & Source-Era Amendment Count\n13. Exam Traps — Source Conflicts / Time-Sensitive Items\n1. Article 368 — Power, Procedure & Initiation\n● Article 368 Parliament ki Constitution-amending power/procedure ka core provision hai. Source ke\nmutabik amendment addition, variation ya repeal ke through ho sakta hai; Q1 explanation saath hi Basic\nStructure limitation note karta hai. [Q1, Q2, Q4, Q5]\n● Constitution Amendment Bill ko dono Houses separately special majority se pass karte hain;\nOrdinary/Money/Finance Bill wala route nahi. Amendment initiative Lok Sabha ya Rajya Sabha — kisi\nbhi House se ho sakta hai; State Legislature ya President initiate nahi karte. [Q3, Q6, Q7, Q8]\n2. State Ratification — Half of States & Federal Provisions\n● Article 368(2) proviso wale specified federal provisions ke liye Parliament ki special majority ke saath not\nless than one-half State Legislatures ki ratification chahiye. State Assembly resolution pass/reject kar\nsakti hai; source Q9 time-limit na hone ka point bhi deta hai. [Q9, Q12]\n● Half-state ratification examples: federal provisions, Supreme Court/High Court provisions, Article 368\nprocedure, President election, States ki Parliament representation aur Seventh Schedule Lists. New\nState formation/Art.169 type matters ko source is category se alag rakhta hai. [Q10, Q11, Q13, Q14]\n● Source ke hisab se Third Constitutional Amendment, 1954 pehli amendment thi jo Article 368(2)\nrequirement ke under State Legislatures se ratify hui; Concurrent List Entry 33 re-enact ki gayi. [Q15]\n3. Passage, President Assent & No Joint Sitting\n● Constitution Amendment Bill ko each House independently pass karna hota hai. Upper House reject kare\nto Bill drop hota hai; joint sitting ka provision nahi. Source Article 368 mein do methods note karta hai:\nspecial majority; aur special majority + half-State ratification. [Q16, Q18]\n● Prior Presidential recommendation required nahi. Bill President ko present hone ke baad assent\nobligatory hai; source is mandatory assent ko 24th Amendment Act, 1971 se link karta hai aur Article\n368 amendment bhi note karta hai. [Q17, Q19, Q20]\n4. Early Amendments — 1st, 15th & 26th\n● First Amendment Bill 1951 mein aaya. Source ke mutabik First Amendment ne Articles 31A/31B aur\nNinth Schedule add ki, land/agrarian reform laws ko judicial challenge se protection dene ki context thi;\njudicial interpretations of Fundamental Rights ko overcome karna immediate backdrop bataya gaya.\n[Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constitutional Amendments Full Mind Map\n● 15th Amendment, 1963 se Supreme Court Judge ki age determine karne ke authority/manner ke liye\nParliament-by-law provision source mein diya hai; 26th Amendment, 1971 ne former princely rulers ke\nprivy purses/special rights abolish kiye. [Q26, Q27]\n5. Amendment Mapping & Chronology — 13th to 99th\n● Source match set: 13th → Nagaland; 18th → term 'state' clarification; 39th → President, Vice-President,\nSpeaker aur Prime Minister ke election ko challenge nahi kiya ja sakta; 52nd → Anti-Defection Law. [Q28]\n● Source match set: judicial review power curtailment → 38th; Right to Property ko Fundamental Right se\nremove karna → 44th; voting age 21 se 18 → 61st; Preamble mein 'Secular' word add karna → 42nd.\n[Q29]\n● Source match set: 69th → Delhi as National Capital Territory; 75th → State-level Rent Tribunals; 80th →\n10th Finance Commission recommendations; 83rd → Arunachal Pradesh Panchayats mein SC\nreservation exception. [Q30]\n● Provision-match set: Co-operative societies → 97th; SC/ST backlog protection → 81st; NJAC → 99th;\nCouncil of Ministers size limit → 91st. Year match: 42nd–1976, 52nd–1985, 86th–2002, 96th–2011. [Q31,\nQ32]\n6. 42nd, 44th & NJAC — High-Yield Changes\n● 42nd Amendment (1976) ko source 'Mini Constitution' kehta hai. Preamble mein Socialist, Secular,\nIntegrity; 10 Fundamental Duties; aur Article 39A, 43A, 48A additions source explanation mein\nhighlighted hain; Fundamental Duties Swaran Singh Committee recommendation se linked hain. [Q33,\nQ34, Q35]\n● 44th Amendment ke source points: President Council of Ministers ki advice ko ek baar reconsideration ke\nliye return kar sakta hai. Q36 ke official treatment mein options C aur D dono 'not true' maane gaye; Q38\nmein 39th Amendment/PM election aur 99th Amendment/NJAC distinction diya hai. [Q36, Q37, Q38]\n● 99th Constitutional Amendment ne National Judicial Appointments Commission (NJAC) banaya; source\nke mutabik Constitution Bench ne ise 2015 mein unconstitutional declare kiya. [Q39]\n7. Anti-Defection, Hindi Text, Voting Age & Delhi\n● Anti-Defection Law = 52nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1985; Tenth Schedule add hui. Floor-\ncrossing/defection ke repeated source questions isi mapping ko test karte hain. [Q40, Q41, Q42, Q43]\n● 58th Amendment Act, 1987 ne Constitution ka authoritative Hindi text publish karne ko authorize kiya.\n61st Amendment ne voting age 21 se 18 ki; source Q45 ise 1988 aur Q46 wording mein Act 1989 bolta\nhai. [Q44, Q45, Q46]\n● 69th Amendment, 1991 ke Delhi questions mein source explanations 'National Capital Region' phrase\nuse karte hain, jabki source Q30 match explanation 'National Capital Territory' kehta hai — exact source\nframing preserve ki gayi hai. [Q47, Q48, Q49]\n8. Reservation, RTE, Commissions & Ministry Size\n● 79th Amendment (1999) source ke mutabik SC/ST aur Anglo-Indian representation/reservation period ko\n10 saal extend karta hai; explanation 95th aur 104th extensions ka later context bhi deta hai. [Q50, Q51]\n● Source Q52 '93rd Constitution Amendment Bill' ko 6–14 years free/compulsory education proposal ke\nroop mein describe karke kehta hai ki ye 86th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2002 bana. 86th\nAmendment ne Article 21A insert karke Right to Education ko Fundamental Right banaya;\nimplementation/RTE Act source 1 April 2010 se link karta hai. [Q52, Q53, Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● 89th Amendment, 2003 ne combined SC/ST Commission ko NCSC (Art. 338) aur NCST (Art. 338A)\nmein bifurcate kiya. 91st Amendment, 2003 ne Union/State Council of Ministers size ko respective\nHouse strength ka 15% cap kiya. [Q58, Q59, Q60, Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● 93rd Amendment Act source ke mutabik educational institutions mein OBCs ke 27% reservation se\nlinked hai. [Q64]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constitutional Amendments Full Mind Map\n9. Co-operatives, Land Boundary, GST & 105th\n● 97th Amendment ko source co-operative societies ki constitutional status/protection se link karta hai:\nArticle 19(1)(c) mein 'Co-operative Societies' aur Part IX-B; Article 243(ZJ) ke source answer mein\nBoard directors maximum 21. [Q65, Q66, Q67]\n● 100th Amendment Act, 2015 = India–Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement implementation; source\nfigures India → Bangladesh 111 enclaves, Bangladesh → India 51 enclaves. 101st Amendment, 2016 =\nGST; source 1 July 2017 rollout note karta hai. [Q68, Q69]\n● Source matching: 94th→Article 164; 95th→Article 334; 96th→Eighth Schedule; 103rd→Article 15. 105th\nAmendment, 2021 ko States ki SEBC identify/specify power se link kiya gaya; assent 18 Aug 2021. [Q70,\nQ71]\n10. Basic Structure Doctrine & Major Cases\n● Source chronology: Golaknath (1967) → 24th Amendment (1971) → Kesavananda Bharati (1973) →\n42nd Amendment (1976). Golaknath ko Parliament ki amendment power par first limitation wala case\nbataya gaya. [Q72, Q73]\n● Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973) = Basic Structure Doctrine. Source ke repeated questions\nke mutabik Parliament amend kar sakta hai, lekin Constitution ke basic structure ko destroy/abrogate\nnahi kar sakta. [Q74, Q75, Q76, Q77, Q78, Q80]\n● Fundamental Rights amend karne ki competence Parliament ke paas hai, subject to Basic Structure\nlimitation — source Q79 ka direct rule. [Q79]\n11. DPSP vs FR & Amendment-Case Matching\n● 25th Amendment, 1971 source ke mutabik Articles 39(b),(c) implement karne wale laws ko Articles 14,\n19 (aur explanation mein 31) challenge se protection deta hai. Q82 source 42nd vs 44th distinction aur\nMinerva Mills framing test karta hai. [Q81, Q82]\n● Case–Amendment match source: Indira Gandhi v. Raj Narain → 39th; Minerva Mills → 42nd; Kihoto\nHollohan → 52nd; P. Sambamurthy → 32nd. [Q83]\n12. Nari Shakti, 98th Bill & Source-Era Amendment Count\n● Nari Shakti Vandan Adhiniyam source: women-reservation provisions first census-after-Act based\ndelimitation ke baad effective; 15-year duration from commencement; SC/ST reserved seats ke within\none-third women reservation. Isliye source Q84 mein statements 2 & 3 correct. [Q84]\n● Source Q85 ke mutabik Constitution (98th Amendment) Bill National Judicial Commission constitution se\nrelated tha aur Arun Jaitley ne present kiya. [Q85]\n● Source-era count question: May 2013 tak 98 Constitutional Amendments implemented; same\nexplanation Jan 2020 tak 104th Amendment implemented note karta hai. Is number ko current-count ke\nroop mein silently update nahi kiya gaya. [Q86]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Constitutional Amendments Full Mind Map\n13. Exam Traps — Source Conflicts / Time-Sensitive Items\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q36 — MULTIPLE CORRECT\nSource explicitly 'Multiple Correct Answers (Ans. C & D)' mark karta hai. Dono ko preserve kiya gaya; single-\nanswer mein force nahi kiya. [Q36]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — SOURCE WORDING CONFLICT — DELHI\nQ30 explanation 69th Amendment ko Delhi = National Capital Territory ke saath match karta hai; Q47–Q49\nexplanations 'National Capital Region' wording use karte hain. Source discrepancy ko jaisa hai waisa flag kiya\ngaya. [Q30, Q47, Q48, Q49]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — SOURCE YEAR / BILL FRAMING\nQ45 source 61st Amendment Act ko 1988 bolta hai, Q46 wording/explanation 1989 label use karta hai. Q52\n'93rd Amendment Bill' ko education proposal batakar 86th Amendment Act, 2002 bana hua explain karta hai. In\nsource-era wordings ko silently reconcile nahi kiya. [Q45, Q46, Q52]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — TIME-SENSITIVE SOURCE FACT\nQ86 ka amendment count May 2013 / Jan 2020 snapshot hai. Q84 implementation delimitation/census\ncondition ke saath source-specific hai. Inhe present-day current-affairs fact samajhkar overwrite nahi kiya gaya.\n[Q84, Q86]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0291","t":"04 Important Committees of Constituent Assembly","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" 🏛️ IMPORTANT COMMITTEES OF CONSTITUENT\nASSEMBLY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Major Committees — Chairman Quick Map\n2. Union & Provincial Constitution Committees\n3. Drafting Committee — Chairman & Formation\n4. Drafting Committee — Members & Replacements\n5. Nehru, Patel & Drafting Committee — Confusion Clear\n6. Advisory Committee — Fundamental Rights & Minorities\n7. Disputed Match-the-Following — Source Trap\n8. National Flag Committee — 1931 vs 1947\n1. Major Committees — Chairman Quick Map\n● Union Constitution Committee — Chairman Jawaharlal Nehru. Source explanation ke chairman-map\nmein Committee on the Rules of Procedure aur Steering Committee — Dr. Rajendra Prasad; States\nCommittee — Jawaharlal Nehru; Drafting Committee — Dr. B.R. Ambedkar; Advisory Committee on\nFundamental Rights, Minorities, Tribal & Excluded Areas — Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel diye gaye hain.\n[Q1]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru Drafting Committee ke member nahi the; source unhe Union Constitution Committee,\nStates Committee aur Union Powers Committee ka chairman batata hai. [Q10]\n2. Union & Provincial Constitution Committees\n● Constituent Assembly ki Union Constitution Committee ke Chairman Jawaharlal Nehru the. [Q1]\n● Provincial Constitution Committee ke Chairman Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel the. [Q2]\n3. Drafting Committee — Chairman & Formation\n● Indian Constitution ki Drafting Committee ke Chairman Dr. B.R. Ambedkar the — source mein ye fact\nmultiple questions mein repeat hua hai. [Q3, Q4]\n● Drafting Committee 29 August 1947 ko ek resolution ke through Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ki chairmanship\nmein constitute hui thi, Constitution ke form aur structure par discuss/decide karne ke liye. [Q9, Q11]\n4. Drafting Committee — Members & Replacements\n● Ambedkar ke under Drafting Committee mein 6 OTHER members the, yani chairman ko mila kar total 7\nmembers. [Q7]\n● Original six other members: N. Gopalaswami Ayyangar, Alladi Krishnaswamy Ayyar, K.M. Munshi,\nMohammad Saadullah, B.L. Mitter aur D.P. Khaitan. [Q7, Q9]\n● Later replacement: B.L. Mitter ki jagah N. Madhava Rau aaye; D.P. Khaitan ki 1948 mein death ke baad\nT.T. Krishnamachari include hue. [Q7]\n● Given persons mein N. Gopalaswami Ayyangar aur Alladi Krishnaswamy Ayyar Drafting Committee ke\nmembers the. [Q8]"," 5. Nehru, Patel & Drafting Committee — Confusion Clear\n● Jawaharlal Nehru Drafting Committee ke member NAHI the. Mohammad Saadullah, K.M. Munshi aur\nAlladi Krishnaswamy Ayyar source ke according members the. [Q10]\n● Q8 ke set mein Jawaharlal Nehru aur Sardar Patel dono Drafting Committee ke members nahi the;\ncorrect member-pair N. Gopalaswami Ayyangar + Alladi Krishnaswamy Ayyar tha. [Q8]\n● K.M. (Kanhaiyalal Maneklal) Munshi Constitution Drafting Committee se related the. [Q9]\n6. Advisory Committee — Fundamental Rights & Minorities\n● Advisory Committee on Fundamental Rights, Minorities, Tribals and Excluded Areas ke Chairman\nSardar Vallabhbhai Patel the. [Q6]\n● Is Advisory Committee ki source explanation mein do sub-committees highlighted hain: Fundamental\nRights Sub-Committee — J.B. Kripalani; Minority Sub-Committee — H.C. Mukherjee. [Q6]\n7. Disputed Match-the-Following — Source Trap\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Q5 disputed / excluded from evaluation\n\n▸Source ke correct chairman-map ke mutabik: Advisory Committee on Fundamental Rights... → Sardar\nPatel; Steering Committee → Dr. Rajendra Prasad; Union Powers Committee → Jawaharlal Nehru; Drafting\nCommittee → B.R. Ambedkar. [Q5]\n\n▸Question ki List-II mein Steering Committee ke actual chairman Dr. Rajendra Prasad ka naam diya hi nahi\ngaya tha; isliye source ke mutabik koi option correct nahi tha aur Commission ne question evaluation se\nexclude kar diya. [Q5]\n8. National Flag Committee — 1931 vs 1947\n● Constituent Assembly context mein National Flag par Ad-hoc Committee 23 June 1947 ko bani thi aur\nuske Chairman Dr. Rajendra Prasad the. [Q12]\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Do Flag Committees confuse mat karo\n\n▸2 April 1931, Karachi Session wali Flag Committee — Chairman Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel. [Q12]\n\n▸23 June 1947, Constituent Assembly context ki Ad-hoc Committee on National Flag — Chairman Dr.\nRajendra Prasad. Source specifically kehta hai ki J.B. Kripalani kisi Flag Committee ke chairman nahi the.\n[Q12]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Important Committees of Constituent Assembly Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0292","t":"40 Official Language","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Official Language Full Mind Map\n🏛️ OFFICIAL LANGUAGE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Union Official Language — Articles 343 to 346\n2. Linguistic Minorities & Official Language Commission\n3. Eighth Schedule — Recognition & Core Facts\n4. Languages Added by Constitutional Amendments\n5. Eighth Schedule — Historical vs Current Count\n6. State Language & Census-Based Language Data\n7. Language Family & Classical Languages\n8. Exam Traps — Ambiguous / Multiple-Correct / Source-Specific\n1. Union Official Language — Articles 343 to 346\n● Article 343(1) ke source explanation ke mutabik Union ki official language Hindi in Devanagari script hai.\nArticle 343(2) ne Constitution commence hone se 15 saal tak Union ke official purposes ke liye English\nko continue karne ki permission di. [Q1]\n● Article 345 State ko apni official language/languages adopt karne ka constitutional procedure deta hai.\nSource comparison: Article 343 = Union official language, Article 344 = Official Language Commission +\nParliamentary Committee, Article 346 = State-to-State / State-to-Union official communication language.\n[Q2]\n● Official-language provisions change karne par source Q3 do routes distinguish karta hai: Article 368(2)\nke through constitutional amendment interpretation mein 2/3 majority; Article 343(3) ke under English\ncontinuation jaise law (Official Language Act, 1963) simple majority se ho sakta hai. [Q3]\n2. Linguistic Minorities & Official Language Commission\n● Article 350A: har State aur local authority ka endeavour hona chahiye ki linguistic minority children ko\nprimary stage par mother-tongue instruction ki adequate facilities milen. Source is provision ko 7th\nAmendment Act, 1956 se added batata hai. [Q5]\n● Article 344 ke under First Official Language Commission President Dr. Rajendra Prasad ne B. G. Kher ki\nchairmanship mein 7 June 1955 ko appoint kiya. Source ke mutabik Commission ne 1956 mein report\nsubmit ki aur English ko gradually Hindi se replace karne ke steps recommend kiye. [Q6]\n3. Eighth Schedule — Recognition & Core Facts\n● Source ka core rule: Eighth Schedule recognised languages list karti hai; Hindi Union ki official language\nhai, 'national language' nahi. Bodo recognised Eighth Schedule language hai. [Q4]\n● Bhojpuri aur Rajasthani source questions ke options mein Eighth Schedule ke bahar hain; English bhi\nEighth Schedule ki 22 recognised languages mein included nahi hai. [Q10, Q12, Q15]\n● Current source count: Eighth Schedule 22 languages recognise karti hai. [Q17]\n4. Languages Added by Constitutional Amendments\n● 92nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 2003 ne Bodo, Dogri, Maithili aur Santhali add kiye aur recognised\nlanguages ki total number 22 ho gayi. [Q7, Q9]\n● Source Q8 ke mutabik 1993 mein Maithili, Santhali, Bodo aur Dogri — chaaron Eighth Schedule mein\nnahi the; ye chaaron baad mein 92nd Amendment se add hue. [Q8]\n● Sindhi = 21st Amendment, 1967; Konkani = 71st Amendment, 1992. Source Q11 isliye Sindhi aur\nKonkani dono ko amendment-added languages batata hai. [Q11]\n● 71st Amendment Act, 1992 ne Konkani, Manipuri aur Nepali add kiye. Maithili source explanation ke\nmutabik baad mein Constitution (92nd Amendment) Act, 2003 se add hui. [Q13, Q14]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Official Language Full Mind Map\n5. Eighth Schedule — Historical vs Current Count\n● Source Q16 historical framing deta hai: 92nd Amendment se pehle Eighth Schedule mein 18 languages\nthi; 92nd Amendment ke baad total 22 ho gayi. Given options mein current 22 present nahi tha. [Q16]\n● Exam memory chain from source: Sindhi → 21st (1967); Konkani/Manipuri/Nepali → 71st (1992);\nBodo/Dogri/Maithili/Santhali → 92nd (2003); total → 22. [Q7, Q9, Q11, Q13, Q14, Q16, Q17]\n6. State Language & Census-Based Language Data\n● Uttarakhand ne source ke mutabik 1 January 2010 ko Sanskrit ko second official language status diya;\nexplanation Rishikesh ko later Sanskrit city declare kiye jane ka note bhi deta hai. [Q18]\n● Given options mein Bengali sabse zyada logon dwara boli jane wali Eighth Schedule language thi.\nSource Census-2011 context mein overall Hindi ko first, Bengali second aur Marathi third batata hai.\n[Q19]\n● Census-2001 source order: Bengali (8.11%) > Telugu (7.19%) > Marathi (6.99%) > Tamil (5.91%).\nSource note karta hai ki Census-2011 mein order Bengali > Marathi > Telugu > Tamil ho gaya. [Q20]\n● Hindi-speaking population source ke exam-era census context mein about 41–43%: 2001 = 41.03%;\n2011 = 43.63%. [Q21]\n7. Language Family & Classical Languages\n● Brahui Baluchistan ki language hai, lekin source philological classification ke mutabik Dravidian language\nfamily se belong karti hai. [Q23]\n● Source current-affairs snapshot: 3 Oct 2024 ko Marathi, Pali, Prakrit, Assamese aur Bengali ko classical-\nlanguage status approve hone ke baad total classical languages 11 ho gayi. Earlier sequence source:\nTamil 2004, Sanskrit 2005, Telugu/Kannada 2008, Malayalam 2013, Odia 2014. [Q24]\n● Gujarati/Kannada/Telugu set mein source answer Kannada aur Telugu ko classical languages batata hai;\ndono ko 2008 mein status mila, Gujarati ko nahi. [Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Official Language Full Mind Map\n8. Exam Traps — Ambiguous / Multiple-Correct / Source-Specific\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q3 — TWO DIFFERENT INTERPRETATIONS\nOriginal English/Hindi framing mein source khud fundamental difference note karta hai. Constitutional provision\namend karna Article 368(2) route mein 2/3 majority se linked hai; Article 343(3) ke under language-use law\nsimple majority se ho sakta hai. Isliye context dekhe bina ek answer force mat karo. [Q3]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q8 — ALL FOUR WERE OUT IN 1993\nMaithili, Santhali, Bodo aur Dogri — source ke mutabik 1993 mein chaaron Eighth Schedule mein nahi the.\nAgar paper single-answer format mein tha, item inherently problematic hai. [Q8]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q11 — MULTIPLE-CORRECT\nSource explanation Sindhi (21st Amendment) aur Konkani (71st Amendment) dono ko Constitutional\nAmendment se added languages batata hai. Single-choice framing multiple-correct ban sakti hai. [Q11]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q16 — HISTORICAL OPTIONS vs CURRENT TOTAL\nQuestion options 16/17/18/20 the. Source historical answer 18 (pre-92nd Amendment) explain karta hai, saath\nhi current total 22 note karta hai. Present-day total ko old-option question par silently impose nahi kiya gaya.\n[Q16]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q20–Q21 — CENSUS SNAPSHOT\nMother-tongue order aur Hindi-speaking percentage census year ke saath change hote hain. Source 2001 aur\n2011 dono snapshots deta hai; exam mein year/context dekhna zaroori hai. [Q20, Q21]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q22 — OUT-OF-CHAPTER SOURCE ITEM\nOfficial Language HTML ke andar Q22 actually Panchayat Articles 243A/243B/243C par hai. Source answer:\nArticle 243C = Composition of Panchayat. Is stray source question ko omit nahi kiya gaya. [Q22]\n\n⚠EXAM TRAP — Q24 — TIME-SENSITIVE CURRENT AFFAIRS\nClassical languages total = 11 source ka 3 Oct 2024 snapshot hai. Is DOCX ne source ko hi preserve kiya hai;\nise silently newer count se replace nahi kiya gaya. [Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0293","t":"41 Panchayati Raj and Community Development","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Panchayati Raj & Community Development Full Mind Map · Page 1\n PANCHAYATI RAJ & COMMUNITY\n🏡\n\nDEVELOPMENT — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Roots & Constitutional Foundation — Article 40 to 73rd/74th Amendments\n2. Part IX, Article 243 & Eleventh Schedule — Core Panchayat Structure\n3. State Subject, Elections, Tenure & Implementation\n4. Reservation in Panchayats — Women, SC/ST & State Variations\n5. PESA 1996 & Gram Sabha — Scheduled Areas\n6. Grass-root Democracy & Democratic Decentralisation\n7. Panchayati Raj Committees — Balwant Rai Mehta to L.M. Singhvi\n8. Three-tier Bodies — Gram Panchayat, Panchayat Samiti & Zila Parishad\n9. State Election Commission & Local Elections\n10. State Finance Commission — Article 243-I\n11. Municipalities & 74th Amendment — Urban Local Government\n12. DPC/MPC, MGNREGA & Community Development\n1. Roots & Constitutional Foundation — Article 40 to 73rd/74th Amendments\n● Sir Charles Metcalfe ne village communities ko 'little republics' kaha; Lord Ripon ko India mein local self-\ngovernment ka Father maana gaya. [Q1, Q2]\n● Article 40 (DPSP) State ko village Panchayats organize karne aur unhe self-government ke liye powers\ndene ka direction deta hai. 73rd Amendment ne Panchayati Raj ko constitutional status diya; 74th\nAmendment urban municipalities se related hai. [Q3-Q8]\n● 73rd Amendment ki legislative origin 64th Constitutional Amendment Bill, 1989 tak trace hoti hai. 73rd\nAmendment Act, 1992 ne Part IX + 11th Schedule insert kiya aur 24 April 1993 se effective hua;\n73rd/74th Amendments P.V. Narasimha Rao ke PM tenure mein hue. [Q9-Q16]\n2. Part IX, Article 243 & Eleventh Schedule — Core Panchayat Structure\n● Article 243G Panchayats ko self-government ke liye powers/functions devolve karne se related hai;\nEleventh Schedule mein Panchayats ke 29 subjects/functions hain. Source ke according “Rural Sports”\nEleventh Schedule ka item nahi hai. [Q17-Q21]\n● Article 243C ke under State Legislature Panchayat composition provide karti hai. System normally three-\ntier hai — village, intermediate/block, district — lekin population 20 lakh se adhik na ho to intermediate\ntier compulsory nahi. [Q22-Q26]\n● Article 243J Panchayat accounts/audit se related hai. Article 243E ke under term first meeting se 5 years;\npremature dissolution ke baad election generally 6 months ke andar aur reconstituted body remainder\nterm ke liye. [Q27-Q32]\n● Local self-government ke concerns public health, sanitation, roads, development etc. hain; public order\nState concern hai aur judicial review Panchayati Raj Institution ki power nahi. Part IX = Panchayats; Part\nIX-A = Municipalities. [Q33-Q38]\n3. State Subject, Elections, Tenure & Implementation\n● 73rd Amendment rural Panchayats ko self-government institutions recognize karta hai; urban local\ngovernment 74th Amendment ke under. Panchayati Raj Seventh Schedule ki State List ka subject hai.\n[Q39-Q45]\n● Panchayat dissolution ke baad election Article 243E framework mein 6 months ke andar; 74th\nAmendment Panchayats nahi, Municipalities se concerned hai. Source Madhya Pradesh ko 73rd\nAmendment ko “true spirit” mein first implement karne wala State batata hai. [Q46-Q48]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Panchayati Raj & Community Development Full Mind Map · Page 2\n● National Panchayati Raj Day 24 April ko celebrate hota hai (source: first celebration 2010). 73rd\nAmendment ke provisions mein regular remuneration include nahi tha. [Q49, Q50]\n4. Reservation in Panchayats — Women, SC/ST & State Variations\n● Article 243D reservation ka core Article hai: SC/ST seats population proportion ke basis par aur women\nke liye not less than one-third seats; women reservation Article 334 ki expiry se linked nahi hai. [Q51, Q52,\nQ55-Q58]\n● Source ke state-specific questions 50% women reservation (Bihar, Uttarakhand, M.P., H.P. etc.), U.P.\nmein one-third reservation aur Arunachal Pradesh mein SC reservation exception ko cover karte hain.\n[Q59-Q62]\n5. PESA 1996 & Gram Sabha — Scheduled Areas\n● PESA Act 1996 Bhuria Committee recommendations par Fifth Schedule areas ke liye enact hua.\nObjective tribal traditional rights/local self-governance ko strengthen karna hai; autonomous regions\ncreate karna iska stated objective nahi. [Q63-Q66]\n● PESA areas mein Gram Sabha ko minor forest produce ownership aur land-transfer control jaise powers\ndiye gaye; source minor minerals ke prospecting/mining lease par Gram Sabha\nconsent/recommendation ka distinction note karta hai. Scheduled-area Zila Panchayat powers ka state-\nspecific example Chhattisgarh se diya hai. [Q67, Q68]\n● Gram Sabha = village Panchayat area ke electoral rolls mein registered persons. State Legislature Gram\nSabha powers define karti hai. Chhattisgarh, M.P., Rajasthan aur Scheduled Areas ke quorum/presiding\nrules source mein state-specific statutory examples ke roop mein diye gaye hain. [Q69-Q75]\n6. Grass-root Democracy & Democratic Decentralisation\n● 73rd Amendment rural local self-government ko strengthen karta hai; Panchayati Raj ko “Grass Root\nDemocracy” aur democratic decentralisation se link kiya gaya hai. Main aims: people’s participation in\ndevelopment + decentralisation. [Q76-Q82]\n● Local government ke attributes statutory status, local participation aur taxation/resource-raising hain;\ncentralised control uska basic attribute nahi. Panchayati Raj = village/block/district local self-\ngovernment, economic development/social justice aur developmental administration mein public\nparticipation. [Q83-Q89]\n● Post-73rd Amendment decentralisation decision-making/administrative/system powers tak hai, judicial\npower tak nahi. Local autonomy, participation aur empowerment decentralisation ke features hain.\nSource rural-local governance rejuvenation aur State control over local bodies ke scope ko bhi discuss\nkarta hai. [Q90-Q94]\n● ‘Panchayati Raj’ nomenclature source Mahatma Gandhi se associate karta hai — village as a self-\nsufficient little republic ka ideal. [Q95]\n7. Panchayati Raj Committees — Balwant Rai Mehta to L.M. Singhvi\n● Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957), NDC ke under CDP/NES reorganisation ke liye, three-tier\nPanchayati Raj + democratic decentralisation recommend karti hai. Rajasthan ne Nagaur mein 2\nOctober 1959 ko system inaugurate kiya; source Balwant Rai Mehta ko “Architect of Panchayati Raj” bhi\nkehta hai. [Q96-Q117]\n● Committee chronology/source matches: Balwant Rai Mehta 1957; Ashok Mehta 1977/78; C.H.\nHanumantha Rao 1984; G.V.K. Rao 1985; L.M. Singhvi 1986; P.K. Thungan 1988. Dinesh Goswami aur\nV.K.R.V. Rao Panchayati Raj committees nahi. [Q118-Q124]\n● Ashok Mehta Committee ne two-tier model (district + Mandal Panchayat) aur separate Nyaya\nPanchayats recommend kiye. L.M. Singhvi Committee ne Panchayati Raj institutions ko constitutional\nrecognition/protection dene ki recommendation ki. [Q125-Q131]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Panchayati Raj & Community Development Full Mind Map · Page 3\n● Source G.V.K. Rao ko district as basic planning/implementation unit se link karta hai; specialised working\ngroups/pairs on statistics, training, Panchayats-cooperatives aur rural-development administration bhi\nasked hain. [Q132, Q133]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Panchayati Raj & Community Development Full Mind Map · Page 4\n8. Three-tier Bodies — Gram Panchayat, Panchayat Samiti & Zila Parishad\n● Part IX three-tier framework: Gram Panchayat (village) → Panchayat Samiti/Kshetra/Janpad\n(intermediate/block) → Zila Parishad (district). Nagar Panchayat urban body hai, 74th Amendment ke\nunder. [Q134-Q137]\n● Kshetra/Block/Zila Panchayat territorial limits State authority determine/notify karti hai. State-wise\nnomenclature/examples: Janpad Panchayat (M.P.), Kshetra Panchayat (U.P.), Taluka Parishad\n(Gujarat), Anchalik Parishad (West Bengal); source special-state exceptions bhi note karta hai. [Q138-\nQ143]\n● Panchayat Samiti intermediate/block level body hai; source Jharkhand/U.P. context mein members direct\nelection se aur block-level Samiti ko coordination/execution administrative body ke roop mein describe\nkarta hai. [Q144-Q150]\n● Zila Panchayat Chairman (U.P.) elected members apne beech se elect karte hain; suspension/standing\ncommittees/office-bearer representation ke Chhattisgarh-M.P. examples state-law specific hain. [Q151-\nQ154]\n9. State Election Commission & Local Elections\n● 73rd Amendment Panchayat elections mandatory banata hai. Article 243K = Panchayat elections; Article\n243ZA = Municipal elections. Electoral rolls + conduct/superintendence/direction State Election\nCommission ke paas. [Q155-Q162]\n● Source Rajasthan SEC (July 1994) aur M.P. SEC (1 Feb 1994) ke state-specific facts deta hai. State\nElection Commissioner Governor appoint karta hai. [Q163-Q166]\n● State election rules ke examples candidate death, district election/returning officers aur local election\nadministration se related hain. Panchayat contest minimum age 21 years; premature dissolution ke baad\nreconstituted Panchayat remainder term continue karti hai; municipality nomination ke liye electoral-roll\nmembership important hai. [Q167-Q173]\n10. State Finance Commission — Article 243-I\n● Article 243I ke under Governor har 5 years State Finance Commission constitute karta hai to review\nPanchayat finances. Ye State aur local governments ke beech taxes/fees/revenue distribution ke\nprinciples recommend karta hai. [Q174-Q180]\n● Union Finance Commission ka local bodies se role completely absent nahi: source Article 280 framework\nmein State Consolidated Fund augment karne ke measures note karta hai. SEC, State Finance\nCommission aur District Panchayat constitutional authorities; “State Electoral Officer” constitutional\nauthority nahi. [Q181-Q183]\n11. Municipalities & 74th Amendment — Urban Local Government\n● 74th Amendment Act, 1992 ne Part IX-A + 12th Schedule insert karke Municipalities ko constitutional\nstatus diya; Part IX rural Panchayats ke liye. Article 243T municipal SC/ST/women reservation se\nrelated hai. [Q184-Q190]\n● Source state-specific municipal facts: Rajasthan Mayor security deposit, Mayor/municipal term, Census\nurban-area criteria, Municipal Corporation for larger urban area, Panchayat-Cantonment dispute,\nGovernor-notified municipal area, nomination limits and age/disqualification rules. [Q191-Q200]\n● Chhattisgarh municipal recall/ward-committee/conflict-of-interest rules, U.P. municipality chairman\nelectorate aur city-body matching questions source ke local-law/current-context examples hain. [Q201-\nQ205]\n12. DPC/MPC, MGNREGA & Community Development\n● 73rd/74th Amendments ke framework se State Election Commission, State Finance Commission aur\nDistrict Planning Committee jaise institutions linked hain; DPC specifically Article 243ZD/74th\nAmendment se, not 73rd. [Q206, Q207]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Panchayati Raj & Community Development Full Mind Map · Page 5\n● DPC Panchayat + Municipality plans consolidate karta hai. Source Rajasthan DPC\ncomposition/chairperson aur U.P. district-plan inclusions ke state-specific examples deta hai. [Q208-Q211]\n● 74th Amendment ward committees, District Planning Committee (243ZD) aur Metropolitan Planning\nCommittee (243ZE) provide karta hai; MPC metropolitan area ka draft development plan prepare karta\nhai, schemes implement karne ka sole body nahi. [Q212, Q213]\n● MGNREGA source ke according adult members of rural household ko at least 100 days employment\nguarantee framework deta hai; Gram Panchayat Gram Sabha recommendations consider karke works\nplan/implementation karta hai. Community Development Programme 1952 aur National Extension\nService 1953 se linked hai. [Q214-Q216]\n EXAM TRAP — Nyaya Panchayat — Bihar Historical vs Present Rule\n⚠\nQ37 source ko disputed mark karta hai: older Bihar Panchayati Raj laws mein village court imprisonment power\nthi; source ke according present Bihar Panchayati Raj Act, 2006 mein village-court bench imprisonment\nsentence nahi de sakta. [Q37]\n EXAM TRAP — Women Reservation — “30%” Wording Flawed\n⚠\nQ53 aur Q54 mein source khud question defect note karta hai: constitutional quota “not less than one-third” hai,\nexact 30% nahi. Q59 ka 50% state-list historical/time-sensitive hai; Q56 bhi period-specific change note karta\nhai. [Q53, Q54, Q56, Q59]\n EXAM TRAP — Committee / Option Defects\n⚠\nQ103 ke options poorly constructed hain; Q110 mein first-state question mein Rajasthan option hi nahi; Q133\nmein G.K. Rao ki jagah G.V.K. Rao hona chahiye. Inhe silently correct nahi kiya gaya. [Q103, Q110, Q133]\n EXAM TRAP — State Election Commissioner Terminology\n⚠\nQ166 source ne “State Chief Election Commissioner” wording ko technically inaccurate bataya aur question\ndeleted/disputed note kiya; constitutional term State Election Commissioner hai. [Q166]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0294","t":"42 Special Provision for Certain Classes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Special Provision for Certain Classes Full Mind Map\n SPECIAL PROVISION FOR CERTAIN CLASSES\n⚖️\n\n— FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Part XVI & Reservation in Legislatures\n2. Scheduled Castes / Scheduled Tribes Lists — Articles 341 & 342\n3. SC–ST Status, Criteria & Population Facts\n4. National Commission for SCs & STs — Articles 338 / 338A\n5. Anglo-Indian Representation — Articles 331 & 333\n6. National Commission for Backward Classes — Article 338B\n7. Important Acts / Match-the-Following Trap\n8. Exam Traps — Source-Specific / Date-Sensitive Questions\n1. Part XVI & Reservation in Legislatures\n● Part XVI Constitution ke 'Special Provisions relating to Certain Classes' se deal karta hai. Source\nexplanation Articles 330–342A ko is block mein rakhti hai. [Q1]\n● Article 330 = Lok Sabha mein Scheduled Castes aur Scheduled Tribes ke liye reserved seats. Article 332\n= State Legislative Assemblies mein SC/ST reservation; seats population proportion ke basis par hoti\nhain. [Q2, Q3]\n● Rajya Sabha aur State Legislative Council mein kisi caste ke liye seat-reservation ka constitutional\nprovision nahi hai. Source J&K Reorganisation ke baad UT Assembly mein SC/ST reservation ka note\nbhi deta hai. [Q13]\n2. Scheduled Castes / Scheduled Tribes Lists — Articles 341 & 342\n● Article 341: President public notification se kisi State/UT ke liye Scheduled Castes specify karta hai;\nState ke case mein Governor se consultation hota hai. List mein inclusion/exclusion Parliament law se\nkarta hai. [Q4, Q6]\n● Article 342: President public notification se Scheduled Tribes specify karta hai; Parliament hi law ke\nthrough list ko add/remove kar sakta hai. Baad ki Presidential notification se list alter nahi ki ja sakti. [Q5]\n● ST list State/UT-specific hoti hai: ek community ek State mein ST ho sakti hai aur doosre mein zaroori\nnahi. Governor khud ST declare nahi karta. [Q7]\n● Source current-affairs example: Bihar ki 2015 'Tanti-Tantwa' SC notification Supreme Court ne July 2024\nmein quash ki; reason — State Government Article 341 list ko change nahi kar sakti. [Q8]\n3. SC–ST Status, Criteria & Population Facts\n● Scheduled Tribe status religion-neutral hai. Source ke mutabik Scheduled Caste Order, 1950 para-3 SC\nstatus ko Hindu framework se jodta hai (isme Sikh aur Buddhist included bataye gaye hain); Rangnath\nMishra Commission ne para repeal karne ki recommendation di thi. [Q9]\n● ST specification ke established criteria: primitive traits ke indications, distinctive culture, geographical\nisolation, larger community se contact mein shyness aur backwardness. Source kehta hai ye criteria\nConstitution mein expressly spelt out nahi hain. [Q10]\n● Source count-fact: 2007 amendment ke baad 1206 SCs; 2017 Scheduled Castes Amendment Act ke\nbaad total 1261; Census 2011 SC population share 16.6% diya hai. [Q11]\n● Source options/context ke hisab se ST population sabse zyada Madhya Pradesh mein; order: Madhya\nPradesh → Rajasthan → Andhra Pradesh → Bihar. [Q12]\n4. National Commission for SCs & STs — Articles 338 / 338A"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Special Provision for Certain Classes Full Mind Map\n● Article 338 = National Commission for Scheduled Castes (NCSC). Original Special Officer setup ke baad\n65th Amendment Act, 1990 se multi-member combined commission; 89th Amendment Act, 2003 se\nSC/ST commissions separate hue. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Article 338A = National Commission for Scheduled Tribes (NCST); 89th Constitutional Amendment Act,\n2003 se separate ST commission ka provision insert hua. [Q14, Q18]\n● NCST composition: Chairperson + Vice-Chairperson + 3 full-time members; source one female member\nka note deta hai. NCST set-up date 19 February 2004 di gayi hai. [Q19]\n● Constitutional vs statutory: NCST constitutional body hai; NHRC, NIA aur NDMA ko source statutory\nbodies batata hai. [Q20]\n5. Anglo-Indian Representation — Articles 331 & 333\n● Article 331 mein Lok Sabha ke liye Anglo-Indian representation ka provision tha: inadequate\nrepresentation par President do members nominate kar sakta tha; source note karta hai ki ye provision\nab cease ho chuka hai. [Q21, Q22]\n● Article 333 State Legislative Assemblies mein Anglo-Indian representation se related tha. [Q23]\n● 104th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2019 ne Anglo-Indian representation ko further extend nahi kiya,\njabki SC/ST seat reservation ko another 10 years extend kiya gaya. [Q21, Q23, Q24]\n6. National Commission for Backward Classes — Article 338B\n● NCBC = constitutional body under Article 338B; constitutional status 102nd Constitutional Amendment\nAct, 2018 se mila. [Q26, Q27]\n● First All India Backward Classes Commission 29 January 1953 ko appointed hua; source ke mutabik first\nChairman Kaka Saheb Kalelkar the. [Q28]\n● Article 340 backward classes ki conditions investigate karne ke liye Commission appoint karne ka\nprovision hai; Article 338B specifically NCBC se linked hai. [Q29]\n7. Important Acts / Match-the-Following Trap\n● Source match facts: NCBC Act = 1993; Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act = 1986; Persons\nwith Disabilities Act = 1995; National Commission for Minorities Act = 1992. Options mein 1992 missing\nhone se source koi option absolutely correct nahi maanta. [Q25]\n8. Exam Traps — Source-Specific / Date-Sensitive Questions\n EXAM TRAPS — Source-Specific / Date-Sensitive\n⚠\n• Q13: SC/ST reservation Lok Sabha & State Assemblies mein; Rajya Sabha / Legislative Council mein caste-\nreserved seats nahi. [Q13]\n• Q11: 1206 (2007), 1261 (2017), Census-2011 = 16.6% ko source/date-specific facts ke roop mein rakho.\n[Q11]\n• Q29: EC=324, NCSC=338, Finance Commission=280, NCBC=338B; technically no pair correct, par source\nUPPSC key option D note karta hai. [Q29]\n• Q25: National Commission for Minorities Act ka source year 1992 hai, jo options mein missing hai; nearest\nanswer B diya gaya. [Q25]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0295","t":"43 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏛️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. United Nations — Foundation, Security Council, Veto & Peacekeeping\n2. UN General Assembly, Good Governance & Secretary-General\n3. UN Languages, Membership, ICJ, ILO & Global Conventions\n4. Human-Rights NGOs & Compulsory Voting\n5. United States — Presidency, Constitution & Foreign-Policy Terms\n6. Intelligence Agencies — CIA, RAW, Mossad & ISI\n7. Press, World Parliaments, News Agencies & Government Reports\n8. Commonwealth & India’s Foreign Policy\n9. Constitutional & Administrative Miscellany\n10. Law, Awards, Coalition Politics & Press Council\n11. Regionalism, Agreements, Terror Groups & Operations\n12. Broadcasting, Environment & Defence / Internal Security\n13. Legal Education, Political Sociology, Bureaucracy & Books\n14. Culture, Diaspora, Authors & Good Governance Day\n15. Current World Affairs, Regions & International Groupings\n16. International Observances & Extremist Groups\n17. Exam Traps — Outdated / Disputed / Source-Specific Questions\n1. United Nations — Foundation, Security Council, Veto & Peacekeeping\n● UNO 1945 mein founded hua; Charter San Francisco conference mein finalize hua, 26 June 1945 ko 50\nnations ne sign kiya, Poland later 51st member bana; UN officially 24 October 1945 ko existence mein\naaya — isi din UN Day hota hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● UN Security Council = 15 members: 5 permanent (USA, France, China, UK, Russia) + 10 non-\npermanent; non-permanent members ka term 2 years. Germany P5 nahi hai. 2021–22 term ke liye India,\nIreland, Kenya, Mexico, Norway elected the; Canada elected nahi hua. [Q3, Q4, Q5]\n● April 2024 Palestine full-membership proposal par USA ne veto kiya aur Switzerland + UK abstain hue;\nsource count = 3 members negative/abstain. Veto power sirf P5 ko hai; UN democratisation demand ka\nmain focus Security Council reform/expansion hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● UN peacekeepers self-defence ke alawa “defence of mandate” mein bhi force use kar sakte hain; source\n2020–21 mein USA ko peacekeeping budget ka largest contributor (~28%) batata hai. Credentials\nCommittee General Assembly appoint karti hai, 9 members hote hain, usually November mein milti hai\naur credentials report GA ko deti hai. [Q9, Q10]\n2. UN General Assembly, Good Governance & Secretary-General\n● UN General Assembly non-member States ko observer status de sakti hai; inter-governmental\norganisations bhi observer status seek kar sakte hain; permanent observers UN HQ par missions\nmaintain kar sakte hain. [Q11]\n● UN good governance ke 8 core traits: Participation, Rule of Law, Transparency, Responsiveness,\nConsensus Orientation, Equity/Inclusiveness, Effectiveness/Efficiency, Accountability. “Government\nlegitimacy” explicitly list nahi; religiosity/emotionality bhi features nahi. [Q12, Q13]\n● Source ke hisab se present UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres hain. Boutros Boutros-Ghali first\nAfrican UN Secretary-General the; U Thant ne sabse lamba tenure serve kiya. [Q14, Q16, Q17]\n● Ruchira Kamboj Aug 2022–May 2024 India ki Permanent Representative to UN rahi aur source unhe first\nwoman Indian Ambassador/PR to UN batata hai; Asoke Kumar Mukerji, Syed Akbaruddin se pehle India\nke Permanent Representative the. [Q15, Q18]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n3. UN Languages, Membership, ICJ, ILO & Global Conventions\n● UN ki 6 official languages: English, French, Spanish, Arabic, Chinese, Russian; Hindi official language\nnahi. International Mother Language Day UNESCO ne proclaim kiya tha, UNICEF ne nahi; Bangla\nnational-language demand Pakistan Constituent Assembly mein uthi. [Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● June 2022 India-sponsored multilingualism resolution mein Hindi, Urdu aur Bengali ko first time mention\nkiya gaya. Source options ke context mein French ko maximum-speaker language batata hai; Atal Bihari\nVajpayee ne 4 Oct 1977 ko UN Assembly mein Hindi speech di. [Q22, Q23, Q24]\n● 1996 ke question-time par Switzerland UN member nahi tha; 10 Sept 2002 se member ban gaya, isliye\nsource aaj ke context mein chaaron options ko members batata hai. South Sudan 9 July 2011 ko\nnewest/193rd country bana. [Q25, Q26]\n● ICJ ka HQ The Hague mein hai; Indian ICJ judges source mein B.N. Rau, Nagendra Singh, R.S. Pathak\naur Dalveer Bhandari diye gaye. ILO 1919 mein Treaty of Versailles ke context mein bana, HQ Geneva.\n[Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● UNCAC legally binding global anti-corruption instrument hai; migrant-smuggling protocol UNTOC ke\nunder hai, aur UNODC dono conventions ke implementation mein assist karta hai. “Rule of Law Index”\nWorld Justice Project release karta hai. [Q30, Q31]\n4. Human-Rights NGOs & Compulsory Voting\n● General Assembly, ICJ aur Trusteeship Council UN organs hain; Amnesty International UN body nahi,\nbalki 1961 mein Peter Benenson dwara founded global human-rights NGO hai. [Q32, Q33, Q34]\n● Doctors Without Borders / Médecins Sans Frontières ek international humanitarian-aid NGO hai, France\nmein founded. [Q35]\n● Source 255th Law Commission Report (March 2015) ke basis par compulsory voting adopt karne wale\ncountries ki sankhya 28 batata hai — question options mein 28 diya hi nahi tha. [Q36]\n5. United States — Presidency, Constitution & Foreign-Policy Terms\n● White House US President ka official residence/workplace hai; correct address 1600 Pennsylvania\nAvenue hai, 1800 nahi. John Adams 1 Nov 1800 ko first resident President bane; source ise American\ndemocracy ka symbol batata hai. [Q37]\n● US President/Vice-President Electoral College elect karta hai; members of Congress electors nahi ho\nsakte. Presidential nomination process mein New Hampshire first primary aur Iowa caucuses early\ncontests ke roop mein source mein diye gaye. [Q38, Q39]\n● Written Constitution ka concept source ke mutabik USA se originate hua. Pressler Amendment US\nassistance ko nuclear non-proliferation/capacity se link karta tha; Chakma refugees = Bangladesh,\nPerestroika = Gorbachev, 13 Sept 1993 = Israel–PLO agreement. [Q40, Q41, Q42]\n● “Pivot to Asia” ko source US foreign-policy strategy batata hai. [Q43]\n6. Intelligence Agencies — CIA, RAW, Mossad & ISI\n● CIA = USA ki civilian foreign intelligence service. RAW = India ki foreign intelligence agency, 21 Sept\n1968 mein constituted, Cabinet Secretariat ke under function karti hai. [Q44, Q45]\n● Mossad = Israel ki national intelligence agency; ISI = Pakistan ki Inter-Services Intelligence. [Q46, Q47]\n7. Press, World Parliaments, News Agencies & Government Reports\n● Press/News Media ko democracy ka “Fourth Estate” kaha jata hai; Fleet Street, London historically\nBritish newspapers ka major centre tha. [Q48, Q49]\n● Russia ka Parliament = Federal Assembly; State Duma lower house aur Federation Council upper\nhouse. Japan ka Parliament = Diet; China ka Parliament = National People’s Congress. “Princelings”\nChina ke influential senior communist leaders ke descendants ke liye term hai. [Q50, Q51, Q52, Q53]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● TASS = Russia/Soviet news agency lineage; Xinhua = China ki official state news agency; Dawn =\nPakistan ka leading English newspaper; “Yellow Book” source mein French Government report bataya\ngaya. [Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]\n8. Commonwealth & India’s Foreign Policy\n● Commonwealth ka source ke hisab se koi charter/treaty/constitution nahi; former British territories\nautomatic members nahi bante. Nehru ka “agreement by free will…” statement India ke Commonwealth\nassociation ko refer karta hai. [Q58, Q59]\n● Jawaharlal Nehru September 1959 mein Afghanistan visit karne wale first Indian PM the; Non-Alignment\npolicy bhi Nehru se linked hai. [Q60, Q61]\n● Panchsheel ke 5 principles: sovereignty/territorial integrity ka mutual respect, non-aggression, non-\ninterference, equality & mutual benefit, peaceful coexistence. Non-alignment in 5 principles mein directly\nincluded nahi. [Q62]\n● India ka “No First Use” nuclear-doctrine principle Vajpayee period se linked hai; source formal adoption\nJan 2003 batata hai. South Asia Six-Point Formula bhi Atal Bihari Vajpayee se linked hai. [Q63, Q64]\n● Source ke current-affairs note ke mutabik USA ne July 2023 aur March 2024 mein Arunachal Pradesh ko\nIndia ka integral part reaffirm kiya. [Q65]\n9. Constitutional & Administrative Miscellany\n● Minimum age: Lok Sabha MP 25, Rajya Sabha MP 30, President 35; Panchayat member 21, State\nAssembly 25, State Council 30, President 35. [Q66, Q67]\n● Oath match source: President — faith/allegiance to Constitution; SC Judge — uphold Constitution & law;\nMP — faithful discharge of duties; Union Minister — secrecy of information. [Q68]\n● Jo rights/bodies Constitution mein mentioned nahi hote unhe source “extra-constitutional” kehta hai;\nPlanning Commission example diya hai. [Q69]\n● Chronology: Air India nationalised 1953 → Imperial Bank renamed SBI 1955 → first democratically\nelected Communist State government 1957 → Goa joined India 1961. [Q70]\n● District Collector as DM law & order aur district police control se linked powers exercise karta hai; Rajni\nKothari ne District Collector ko “Institutional Charisma” kaha. [Q71, Q72]\n● Madam Cama first woman INC President nahi thi; Annie Besant 1917 mein first woman INC President\nthi. Source constitutional-statement set mein Article 21 emergency protection + VP removal rule ko\ncorrect rakhta hai. [Q73, Q74]\n● Q75 source mein 2 wrong statements nikalte hain: Eighth Schedule languages 18 nahi, 22; aur Indian\nliberties ka “Magna Carta” source 1858 Queen’s Proclamation ko batata hai, Charter Act 1813 ko nahi.\nQ76 ke chaaron statements source ke hisab se correct: HC age 62, national-party recognition in ≥4\nstates, Money Bill decision Speaker, cognizable offence = arrest without warrant. [Q75, Q76]\n10. Law, Awards, Coalition Politics & Press Council\n● Source legacy framing mein suicide successful hone par offender punishable nahi rehta; attempt to\nsuicide ko Section 309 IPC se punishable bataya gaya, saath hi later legal reforms ka note hai. [Q77]\n● Param Vir Chakra India ka highest military decoration; medal par 4 Indra Vajra replicas; instituted 26 Jan\n1950; source 31 Dec 2021 tak 21 awardees batata hai. [Q78]\n● Bharat Ratna/Padma awards Article 18(1) ke prohibited “titles” nahi; Padma Awards do periods mein\nsuspended hue; Bharat Ratna generally max 3/year. 2024 recipient options mein M.S. Swaminathan\ncorrect; first 1954 awardees C. Rajagopalachari, S. Radhakrishnan, C.V. Raman; highest civilian award\nBharat Ratna. [Q79, Q80, Q81, Q82]\n● Gandhi Peace Prize 2021 = Gita Press, Gorakhpur. Outstanding Parliamentarian match: M.M. Joshi\n2009, Arun Jaitley 2010, Karan Singh 2011, Sharad Yadav 2012. [Q83, Q84]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● 1967–71 ke beech maximum coalition governments source Bihar mein 9 batata hai. Joyita Mondal ko\nfirst Indian transgender Lok Adalat judge bataya gaya. [Q85, Q86]\n● Press Council of India statutory quasi-judicial body hai, 1966 mein Indian Press Council Act 1965 ke\nunder established. Chairman question ke options outdated hain: source Markandey Katju old chairman\naur current note Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai deta hai. [Q87, Q88]\n11. Regionalism, Agreements, Terror Groups & Operations\n● Regionalism ke causes: uneven development, cultural identity loss ka fear, political prominence. National\nWater Development Agency July 1982 mein autonomous society ke roop mein set up hui. [Q89, Q90]\n● Agreement chronology: Tashkent 1966 → Indo-Soviet Treaty 1971 → Shimla Agreement 1972 →\nFarakka Accord 1977 (final treaty 1996). Bangladesh 1971 Indo-Pak hostilities ke outcome mein bana.\n[Q91, Q92]\n● Lashkar-e-Taiba founders source mein Hafiz Muhammad Saeed, Zafar Iqbal, Mahmoud Mohammad\nBahaziq; LTTE India, Sri Lanka, USA samet kai countries mein banned. Djibouti Code of Conduct\npiracy/armed robbery at sea se related. [Q93, Q94, Q95]\n● Operations match: Checkmate — Sri Lanka; Cactus — Maldives; Blue Star — Punjab; Siddharth —\nBihar. [Q96]\n12. Broadcasting, Environment & Defence / Internal Security\n● “Bahujan Hitaya, Bahujan Sukhaya” = All India Radio motto. Silent Valley–Baba Amte pair incorrect;\nsource Silent Valley ko Salim Ali se aur Baba Amte ko Narmada/conservation context se link karta hai.\n[Q97, Q98]\n● CDS tri-service matters par Defence Minister ka principal military adviser hai; Defence Acquisition\nCouncil ka Chairman Defence Minister hota hai, CDS nahi. CDS permanent Chairman, Chiefs of Staff\nCommittee aur DPC member hai, lekin three Service Chiefs par military command exercise nahi karta.\n[Q99, Q100, Q101]\n● Armoured Corps Centre & School Ahmednagar mein, Jabalpur nahi. Source 1999 Army operational\ncommands question mein historical 5 aur present-context 6 operational + 1 training command ka note\ndeta hai. [Q102, Q103]\n● Equivalent ranks: Major = Squadron Leader = Lieutenant Commander; Lieutenant Colonel = Wing\nCommander = Commander. Operation Sadbhavana remote-area welfare/upliftment se linked. [Q104,\nQ105, Q106]\n● BSF 1 Dec 1965 ko raised; Indo-Pakistan aur Indo-Bangladesh borders guard karta hai. Home Guards\nState Acts ke under voluntary auxiliary force hain; Border Wing Home Guards kuch border/coastal states\nmein. Internal Security Academy = Mount Abu. [Q107, Q108, Q109, Q110]\n13. Legal Education, Political Sociology, Bureaucracy & Books\n● India ka first Law University / National Law School of India August 1987 mein Bangalore/Bengaluru mein\nestablished hua. [Q111, Q112]\n● Source assertion-reason: caste politicisation aur rising casteism dono true, lekin reason direct\nexplanation nahi. 2003 mein Uttarakhand ne Gurkhas aur do communities ko OBC status diya. [Q113,\nQ114]\n● Scientific Socialism = Karl Marx. Morstein Marx ne bureaucracy ke 4 types diye: Guardian, Caste,\nPatronage, Merit. [Q115, Q116]\n● “Gandhian Constitution for Free India” (1946) = Shriman Narayan Agarwal. Author matches: Atul Kohli —\nThe Success of India’s Democracy; Granville Austin — Working a Democratic; Penderel Moon — Divide\nand Quit; Alan Gledhill — The Republic of India. “Democracy and Development in India from Socialism\nto Pro-Business” = Atul Kohli. [Q117, Q118, Q119]\n14. Culture, Diaspora, Authors & Good Governance Day"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● First “Festival of India” abroad source Britain, 1982 batata hai. Pravasi Bharatiya Divas = 9 January; first\nconvention 2003, Gandhi ke 1915 return ko commemorate karta hai; 2015 ke baad biennial note diya\ngaya. [Q120, Q121, Q122]\n● “The India Way” aur “Why Bharat Matters” = S. Jaishankar. Good Governance Day = 25 December, Atal\nBihari Vajpayee birthday, source announcement 2014 batata hai. [Q123, Q124]\n15. Current World Affairs, Regions & International Groupings\n● Har Ghar Tiranga campaign Central Government ne Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav ke under launch ki.\nSource current-pairs question mein Argentina economic crisis + Sudan army-vs-RSF war correct; Turkey\nNATO se withdraw nahi hua. [Q125, Q126]\n● Region-country: Chechnya = Russia; Darfur = Sudan (Mali nahi); Swat Valley = Pakistan (Iraq nahi).\nBerber/Amazigh community North Africa, including Algeria/Morocco mein. [Q127, Q128]\n● Arctic Council members among options: Denmark, Russian Federation, USA; source full 8 members list\nCanada, Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Russia, USA deta hai. [Q129]\n● India–Sri Lanka Accord 1987 ka aim devolution with Sri Lanka unity/integrity tha; “complete freedom”\nincluded nahi. Sirimavo Bandaranaike 1960 mein world ki first woman PM bani. [Q130, Q131]\n● Source ke mutabik Sweden October 2014 mein State of Palestine ko officially recognise karne wala first\nEU country tha. [Q132]\n16. International Observances & Extremist Groups\n● UN ne 1975 ko International Year for Women observe kiya. International Day of Persons with Disabilities\n= 3 December. International Day of Non-Violence = 2 October. [Q133, Q134, Q135]\n● ULFA = Assam-based separatist outfit, founded 7 April 1979; People’s War Group source ke mutabik\nKondapalli Seetharamaiah ne 22 April 1980 Andhra Pradesh mein establish kiya. [Q136, Q137]\n17. Exam Traps — Outdated / Disputed / Source-Specific Questions\n EXAM TRAPS — Source ko silently correct nahi kiya gaya\n⚠\n• Q25 historical question hai: 1996 mein Switzerland UN member nahi tha; source itself notes 2002 ke baad\nall four options members hain. [Q25]\n• Q36 ke source explanation mein answer 28 countries hai, lekin options 32/25/24/22 hain — isliye no valid\noption. [Q36]\n• Q74 mein “present” Rajya Sabha LoP aur Planning Commission leadership time-sensitive the; source only\nstatements 1–2 ko durable constitutional facts ke roop mein correct rakhta hai. [Q74]\n• Q75 disputed hai: option B aur D dono incorrect nikalte hain; source isse single-answer question ke roop\nmein valid nahi maanta. [Q75]\n• Q77 Section 309 IPC wala explanation legacy framing hai; source khud later legal reforms ka note deta hai.\n[Q77]\n• Q88 Press Council Chairman options outdated hain; source old option Markandey Katju aur current-note\nRanjana Prakash Desai ko distinguish karta hai. [Q88]\n• Q103 “as of June 1999” historical count aur source ka present-context count mix karta hai: 1999 = 5\noperational commands; source present-note = 6 operational + 1 training. [Q103]\n• Q14, Q15, Q65, Q80, Q83, Q123, Q125, Q126, Q132 jaise questions current/date-specific source facts hain;\nrevision mein inhe question-date/source context ke saath yaad rakho. [Q14, Q15, Q65, Q80, Q83, Q123, Q125,\nQ126, Q132]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0296","t":"05 Sources of Constitution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n🏛️ SOURCES OF CONSTITUTION — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Constitution Supreme & Written Constitution Tradition\n2. USA — Judicial Review & Federal Court\n3. Canada — Federal System, Union of States & Residual Powers\n4. Australia — Concurrent List\n5. Ireland — DPSP & Rajya Sabha Nomination\n6. USA — Fundamental Rights & Related Features\n7. Other Borrowed Features — UK, Germany, Japan, Russia\n8. Important Match-the-Following — Master Source Map\n9. Exam Traps — Election Commission & Longest Constitution\n1. Constitution Supreme & Written Constitution Tradition\n● Indian political system mein Constitution supreme hai — Constitution of India hi supreme law hai aur\nGovernment institutions ki structure, powers, duties, Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles aur\ncitizens ke duties ka framework set karta hai. [Q1]\n● Written Constitution ki tradition United States of America se shuru hui. Source ke mutabik U.S.\nConstitution duniya ka first written Constitution aur shortest written Constitution hai, jisme 7 Articles hain.\n[Q29]\n2. USA — Judicial Review & Federal Court\n● Judicial Review ka concept Indian Constitution ne United States Constitution se adopt kiya. Courts\nlegislative, executive aur administrative actions ko Constitution ke against test kar sakte hain. [Q2]\n● Judicial Review ka system India aur U.S.A. dono mein exist karta hai. [Q3]\n● India aur America ke federal systems mein common feature: Constitution ki interpretation ke liye Federal\nSupreme Court. Source explanation note karta hai ki U.S.A. mein Union aur State level par separate\njudicial systems hain, jabki India single citizenship provide karta hai. [Q4]\n3. Canada — Federal System, Union of States & Residual Powers\n● Indian Federal System / Indian Federalism ka pattern Canada se inspired hai. [Q5, Q6]\n● 'Union of States' ka concept British North America Act, 1867 (Constitution of Canada) se derived hai.\nArticle 1(1): India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States. [Q7]\n● Strong Centre wala federal system, Centre ke paas residuary powers, Governor ki appointment by\nCentre aur Supreme Court ki advisory jurisdiction jaise features Canada se adopt hue — isliye 'Residual\nPowers of Centre — Australia' incorrect pair hai. [Q18]\n4. Australia — Concurrent List\n● Concurrent List Australia se borrowed hai. Is list ke subjects par Union aur State dono law bana sakte\nhain; ye Seventh Schedule mein hai. Source ke according originally 47 items the, baad mein 52 ho\ngaye. [Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n5. Ireland — DPSP & Rajya Sabha Nomination\n● Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) Ireland se borrowed hain. Ye Part IV, Articles 36–51 mein\nhain; Court mein enforceable nahi, lekin governance ke fundamental principles maane gaye hain aur\nState ko laws banate waqt inhe apply karna hai. [Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15]\n● Rajya Sabha / Council of States mein talent, qualification, experience aur service ko nomination ke\nthrough representation dene ka idea Irish Republic se influenced hai. [Q16]\n6. USA — Fundamental Rights & Related Features\n● Fundamental Rights U.S.A. / U.S. Bill of Rights se borrowed hain. Indian Constitution mein ye Part III,\nArticles 12–35 mein placed hain. [Q17, Q19, Q21, Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27]\n● Source Q24 ke explanation mein Fundamental Rights ke groups: Equality (Art. 14–18), Freedom (Art.\n19–22), Against Exploitation (Art. 23–24), Freedom of Religion (Art. 25–28), Cultural & Educational\nRights (Art. 29–30), Constitutional Remedies (Art. 32). [Q24]\n● Source Q24 additionally Vice-President ka post aur Independence of Judiciary ko bhi U.S.A. se taken\nfeatures batata hai. [Q24]\n7. Other Borrowed Features — UK, Germany, Japan, Russia\n● Parliamentary System / Cabinet Government aur Rule of Law — British / U.K. Constitution se. [Q17, Q19,\nQ20]\n● Emergency Provisions — Germany (Weimar Constitution) se. [Q17, Q18]\n● 'Procedure established by Law' — Japan se. [Q20]\n● Governor dwara Bill ko President ke consideration ke liye reserve karna — Canada se. [Q20]\n● Fundamental Duties — Russian / former Soviet Union Constitution se inspired; source ke mutabik 42nd\nAmendment Act, 1976 se add hue aur recommendation Swaran Singh Committee ne ki. [Q22]\n8. Important Match-the-Following — Master Source Map\n● Master match: Fundamental Rights → U.S.A.; Parliamentary System → U.K.; Emergency Provisions →\nGermany; DPSP → Ireland. [Q17]\n● Master match: Fundamental Rights → U.S. Bill of Rights; DPSP → Ireland; Cabinet Government →\nBritain; Union–State Relations → Canada. [Q19]\n● Master match: Rule of Law → England; Procedure established by Law → Japan; Governor reserves Bill\nfor President → Canada; Concurrent List → Australia. [Q20]\n● Master match: DPSP → Ireland; Fundamental Rights → U.S.A.; Concurrent List → Australia; India as\nUnion of States with greater powers to Union → Canada. [Q21]\n9. Exam Traps — Election Commission & Longest Constitution\n\n⚠️EXAM TRAP — Election Commission kisi foreign Constitution se borrowed nahi\n\n▸Source Q28 ke according Indian Constitution ka Election Commission provision duniya ke kisi Constitution\nse inspired nahi hai; correct option “None of the above” hai. [Q28]\n\n▸Same explanation mein President ke election ka method Ireland se inspired bataya gaya hai — Election\nCommission aur President-election method ko confuse mat karo. [Q28]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n\n⚠️ASSERTION–REASON — Longest Constitution vs Fundamental Rights\n\n▸Indian Constitution longest-written Constitution hai; source ke mutabik originally 22 Parts, 395 Articles aur 8\nSchedules the. [Q23]\n\n▸Fundamental Rights U.S.A. se borrowed hona true hai, lekin ye lengthy Constitution ka correct explanation\nnahi. Isliye A aur R dono true, but R does not correctly explain A. [Q23]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0297","t":"06 Parts of Indian Constitution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n🏛️ PARTS OF INDIAN CONSTITUTION — FULL\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Original Structure & Sequence of Early Parts\n2. Panchayati Raj — Part IX & Three-Tier System\n3. Union–State Relations — Part XI\n4. Core Provision-to-Part Matching\n5. Union Territories, Municipalities & Co-operative Societies\n6. Tribunals — Part XIV-A & Part X Trap\n7. Attorney General, Trade & Services — Parts V, XIII & XIV\n8. Parts XV to XX — Elections, Classes, Language, Emergency & Amendment\n1. Original Structure & Sequence of Early Parts\n● Source Q1 ka answer '22 Parts' deta hai aur explanation specifically batata hai ki originally Constitution\nof India mein 22 Parts, 395 Articles aur 8 Schedules the. [Q1]\n● Early constitutional order: Part I — The Union and its Territory (Articles 1–4) → Part II — Citizenship\n(Articles 5–11) → Part III — Fundamental Rights (Articles 12–35) → Part IV — Directive Principles of\nState Policy (Articles 36–51) → Part IV-A — Fundamental Duties (Article 51-A). [Q2]\n● Fundamental Duties Part IV-A mein hain, Part VI-A mein nahi. Source ke mutabik ye provision 1976\nmein Constitution mein insert hua. Citizenship Part II, Fundamental Rights Part III aur States Part VI se\nrelated hain. [Q3, Q7]\n2. Panchayati Raj — Part IX & Three-Tier System\n● 73rd Constitutional Amendment (1992) ne Constitution ke Part IX mein three-tier Panchayat System\nintroduce kiya: base par Gram Panchayat, intermediary level par Mandal/Taluka Panchayat aur apex par\nZila Panchayat. [Q4]\n● Panchayati Raj / Panchayats ke constitutional provisions Part IX mein implemented hain — same fact\nsource mein multiple questions se test hua hai. [Q12, Q13]\n3. Union–State Relations — Part XI\n● Part XI Union aur States ke relations se deal karta hai. Iska Chapter I Union–State legislative\npowers/distribution se, jabki Chapter II administrative relations se related hai. [Q5]\n4. Core Provision-to-Part Matching\n● Important subject → Part map: Abolition of Titles → Fundamental Rights; Organisation of village\npanchayats → Directive Principles of State Policy; 6–14 years ke child/ward ko education opportunity\nprovide karna → Fundamental Duties; “India, that is Bharat, is the Union of States” → The Union and its\nTerritories. [Q6]\n● Master match: Fundamental Rights → Part III; Fundamental Duties → Part IV-A; The Union → Part V;\nEmergency Provisions → Part XVIII. [Q14]\n5. Union Territories, Municipalities & Co-operative Societies\n● Union Territories Part VIII mein mentioned hain — Part VII nahi. Panchayats Part IX, Municipalities Part\nIX-A aur Fundamental Duties Part IV-A mein hain. [Q8, Q9]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n● Constitutional matching ke mutabik: Panchayats → Part IX; Municipalities → Part IX-A; Co-operative\nSocieties → Part IX-B. [Q11]\n● Municipalities ke provisions Part IX-A (Articles 243-P to 243-ZG) mein hain; Article 243-W Municipalities\nki powers, authority aur responsibilities se deal karta hai. [Q18]\n6. Tribunals — Part XIV-A & Part X Trap\n● Tribunals Part XIV-A mein mentioned hain, Part XI ya Part X mein nahi. Source explanation ke mutabik\nye 42nd Amendment Act, 1976 se Article 323-A ke under Constitution mein insert hue. [Q10, Q11]\n● Part X Scheduled and Tribal Areas se related hai; isliye “Tribunals — Part X” incorrect match hai. Part XI\nCentre–State relations ke provisions rakhta hai. [Q10, Q11]\n7. Attorney General, Trade & Services — Parts V, XIII & XIV\n● Attorney General of India Part V, Article 76 mein mentioned hai — Part XIII mein nahi. Part XIII Territory\nof India ke andar Trade, Commerce and Intercourse ke provisions se related hai. [Q15]\n● Services under the Union and States → Part XIV. Source Q15 mein ye correctly matched pair diya gaya\nhai. [Q15]\n8. Parts XV to XX — Elections, Classes, Language, Emergency &\nAmendment\n● Part XV → Elections; Part XVI → Special Provisions regarding certain classes; Part XVII → Official\nLanguage; Part XVIII → Emergency Provisions. [Q16]\n● Part XVI (Articles 330–342) certain classes se related special provisions deal karta hai. [Q17]\n● Emergency Provisions Part XVIII (Articles 352–360) mein hain. Constitution amendment ke provisions\nPart XX, Article 368 mein diye gaye hain. [Q18]\n EXAM TRAPS — Part Numbers Jo Baar-Baar Confuse Hote Hain\n⚠️\n\n▸Fundamental Duties = Part IV-A, NOT Part VI-A. [Q3]\n\n▸Union Territories = Part VIII, NOT Part VII. [Q8]\n\n▸Tribunals = Part XIV-A, NOT Part XI / Part X. [Q10, Q11]\n\n▸Attorney General of India = Part V (Article 76), NOT Part XIII. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0298","t":"07 Articles of the Constitution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n🏛️ ARTICLES OF THE CONSTITUTION — FULL\nMIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Original Constitution — Articles, Parts & Schedules\n2. Basic Article Map — States, Citizenship & Rights\n3. Parliament & Financial Bills\n4. President, Vice-President & Council of Ministers\n5. DPSP, Fundamental Rights & Social Provisions\n6. Constitutional Bodies, Services & Tribunals\n7. Finance, Emergency & Constitutional Amendment\n8. Union Territories & High Courts\n9. Special State Provisions — Article 371 Series\n1. Original Constitution — Articles, Parts & Schedules\n● Original Constitution mein 22 Parts, 395 Articles aur 8 Schedules the. Source ke mutabik amendments\nke baad kai Articles add/remove hue; present structure ko explain karte hue source around 468 Articles\naur 12 Schedules ka reference deta hai, jabki original numbering 395 tak hi rehti hai aur naye provisions\nA/B/C jaise sub-articles ke form mein add hote hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5]\n● Exam mein 'original Constitution' poocha ho to fixed combo yaad rakho: 22 Parts + 395 Articles + 8\nSchedules. 'Current schedules' context mein source 12 Schedules batata hai. [Q1, Q3, Q4, Q5]\n2. Basic Article Map — States, Citizenship & Rights\n● Formation/admission aur basic structure ke important links: New State formation → Article 3; Citizenship\n→ Part II / Article 5 se provisions start; Fundamental Rights → Part III; Administrative Tribunals →\nArticle 323-A. [Q6, Q12]\n● Core article map: Article 2 → law se new State admit karna; Article 14 → Right to Equality; Article 22 →\narrest and detention se protection; Article 111 → President ka Bill par assent. [Q13, Q14]\n● Article 17 untouchability ke abolition se related hai; Equality before Law Article 14 hai. Article 26 →\nfreedom to manage religious affairs. [Q23, Q24, Q28]\n3. Parliament & Financial Bills\n● Article 117 Financial Bills ke special provisions deta hai. Tax impose/abolish/remit/alter/regulate karne\nwale Bill ya Amendment ko President ki recommendation ke bina introduce/move nahi kiya ja sakta; aisa\nBill Council of States mein introduce nahi hota. [Q7, Q8]\n● Nearby article traps from source: Article 121 → Parliament mein discussion par restriction; Article 123 →\nPresident ki ordinance-promulgation power; Article 98 → Secretariat of Parliament; Article 111 →\nPresidential assent to Bills. [Q8, Q14, Q23]\n4. President, Vice-President & Council of Ministers\n● Article 54 → President ka election; Article 75 → Prime Minister ki appointment aur PM ki advice par\nUnion Ministers ki appointment; Article 155 → Governor ki appointment; Article 164 → Chief Minister aur\nState Council of Ministers ki appointment. [Q15]\n● Removal / impeachment cluster: Article 61 → President impeachment procedure; Article 67(b) → Vice-\nPresident removal; Article 94 → Speaker removal; Article 90 → Deputy Chairman of Rajya Sabha\nremoval. [Q16]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n● Article 78 Prime Minister ke President ko information furnish karne wale duties se related hai; Parliament\nki establishment se nahi. [Q24]\n5. DPSP, Fundamental Rights & Social Provisions\n● DPSP article map: Article 36 → Directive Principles ka opening definition context; Article 39-A → Equal\nJustice & Free Legal Aid; Article 40 → Village Panchayats; Article 44 → Uniform Civil Code; Article 48 →\nAgriculture & Animal Husbandry; Judiciary ko Executive se separate karna Article 50 hai. [Q11, Q13, Q23]\n● Article 41 → Right to Work; Article 42 → Just and Humane Conditions of Work. Source Q28 note karta\nhai ki old wording mein free & compulsory education Article 45 se linked tha; 86th Amendment, 2002 ke\nbaad Article 21-A Fundamental Right bana aur Article 45 ka focus below-six children ki early childhood\ncare & education ho gaya. [Q28]\n● Article 330 → Lok Sabha mein SC/ST seats reservation; Article 338 → National Commission for\nScheduled Castes. [Q17, Q18]\n6. Constitutional Bodies, Services & Tribunals\n● Article 312 → All India Services. Source ke mutabik Rajya Sabha present & voting members ke not less\nthan two-thirds support se national interest resolution pass kare to Parliament law se one or more All\nIndia Services create kar sakti hai. [Q9, Q20]\n● Key institutions: Election Commission → Article 324; UPSC/Public Service Commission → Article 315;\nPSC functions → Article 320; Attorney General of India → Article 76; CAG → Article 148. [Q10, Q17, Q18,\nQ21, Q27]\n● Administrative Tribunal → Article 323-A; Interstate Council → Article 263; Finance Commission → Article\n280. Source Q22 ke chaaron pairs ko factually matched batata hai. [Q18, Q21, Q22]\n● Supreme Court map: Article 124 → establishment of Supreme Court / Union Judiciary; Article 131 →\nSupreme Court ka Original Jurisdiction. [Q10, Q12, Q27]\n7. Finance, Emergency & Constitutional Amendment\n● Financial/constitutional cluster: Consolidated Fund of India → Article 266; Finance Commission →\nArticle 280; Financial Emergency → Article 360; Constitutional Amendment procedure → Article 368.\n[Q19, Q20]\n● Article 352 → Proclamation of Emergency. Source match question mein Article 245 ko Union–State\nlegislative powers ke distribution se related bataya gaya hai. [Q12, Q24]\n8. Union Territories & High Courts\n● Union Territories Part VIII se related hain: Article 239 → UT administration; Article 240 → certain UTs ke\nliye President ki regulation-making power; Article 241 → High Courts for Union Territories; Article 242 →\nomitted/repealed. [Q23, Q26]\n● High Court article set: Article 215 → High Court as Court of Record; Article 222 → Judge transfer from\none High Court to another; Article 226 → High Court writ jurisdiction; Article 227 → superintendence\nover all courts. [Q25]\n● Article 192 State Legislature ke House members ki disqualification ke questions par decision se related\nhai; Parliament members ki salary/allowances se nahi. [Q24]\n9. Special State Provisions — Article 371 Series\n● Article 371-A → Nagaland; Article 371-B → Assam; Article 371-D → Andhra Pradesh. Source ke\nmutabik Article 371-C Manipur ke special provisions se related hai — Meghalaya se nahi. [Q29]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n EXAM TRAPS — Source Ke Important Confusions / Disputed Items\n⚠️\n\n▸Original vs current count: original = 395 Articles + 8 Schedules; source current context mein 12 Schedules\naur around 468 Articles/sub-articles ka reference deta hai. Question ke year/context ko dekho. [Q1, Q3, Q5]\n\n▸Article 48 = Agriculture & Animal Husbandry; Separation of Judiciary from Executive = Article 50. [Q11]\n\n▸Q22 source ke mutabik saare four pairs correct hain, lekin UPPSC official key ne option (c) diya tha; source\nis question ko evaluation se exclude karne layak batata hai. [Q22]\n\n▸Q28 ki wording outdated hai: source intended old match Article 45 batata hai, lekin 86th Amendment ke\nbaad free & compulsory education Article 21-A mein hai; Article 45 below-six early childhood care/education\npar hai. [Q28]\n\n▸Article 371-C = Manipur, NOT Meghalaya. [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0299","t":"08 Schedules","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n🏛️ SCHEDULES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Schedules Overview — Original 8 to Present 12\n2. First to Fourth Schedule — States, Salaries, Oaths & Rajya Sabha\n3. Master Schedule Matching — 3rd to 10th\n4. Ninth Schedule — Land Reforms & Judicial Review\n5. Seventh Schedule — Three Legislative Lists\n6. Concurrent List — High-Frequency Subjects & 42nd Amendment\n7. Union vs State vs Residuary — Subject Traps\n8. Tenth Schedule — Anti-Defection Law\n9. Fifth Schedule — Scheduled Areas & Scheduled Tribes\n10. Sixth Schedule — Tribal Areas & Autonomous Districts\n11. Eleventh Schedule — Panchayati Raj\n1. Schedules Overview — Original 8 to Present 12\n● Indian Constitution mein present total 12 Schedules hain. Source ke mutabik originally 8 Schedules the;\n9th, 10th, 11th aur 12th baad mein Constitutional Amendment Acts se add hue. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Addition chain yaad rakho: 9th → 1st Amendment, 1951 (land reforms / certain Acts & Regulations);\n10th → 52nd Amendment, 1985 (defection); 11th → 73rd Amendment, 1992 (Panchayati Raj); 12th →\n74th Amendment, 1992 (Municipalities). [Q1, Q3]\n2. First to Fourth Schedule — States, Salaries, Oaths & Rajya Sabha\n● 1st Schedule → States aur Union Territories ke names/territories. Naya State/UT create hone par First\nSchedule amend hoti hai. [Q4, Q5]\n● 2nd Schedule → public offices, Judges aur CAG se related salaries/allowances; 3rd Schedule →\nOaths/Affirmations; 4th Schedule → Council of States (Rajya Sabha) mein seats allocation. [Q4, Q6, Q25]\n● Third Schedule mein Union Minister, Parliament candidate/member, Supreme Court Judges, CAG, State\nMinisters, State Legislature candidate/member aur High Court Judges ke oath/affirmation forms aate\nhain. President ka oath Article 60 mein hai, Third Schedule mein nahi. [Q7]\n3. Master Schedule Matching — 3rd to 10th\n● High-frequency map: 3rd → Oaths/Affirmations | 4th → Rajya Sabha seats | 6th → Tribal Areas | 7th →\nUnion/State/Concurrent Lists | 8th → Languages | 9th → Land Reform / validation of certain Acts | 10th\n→ Defection. [Q8, Q9, Q10, Q11, Q12]\n● Incorrect-pair trap: Rajya Sabha seat allocation 4th Schedule ka subject hai, 9th ya 2nd Schedule ka\nnahi. [Q12, Q25]\n4. Ninth Schedule — Land Reforms & Judicial Review\n● 9th Schedule Jawaharlal Nehru ke prime-ministership mein Constitution (First Amendment) Act, 1951 se\nadd hui. Source iska main objective Zamindari abolition / State land-reform laws ko constitutional\nprotection dena batata hai. [Q13, Q14, Q44]\n● Parliament kisi law ko Ninth Schedule mein place kar sakti hai. Source ke mutabik 2007 Supreme Court\nruling ke baad 24 April 1973 ke baad Ninth Schedule mein include laws judicial review ke liye open hain;\nisliye “kisi court mein kabhi review nahi ho sakta” statement source mein incorrect hai. [Q15]"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n● I.R. Coelho case ko source “9th Schedule case” ke roop mein explain karta hai—Judiciary basic\nstructure violation ke against Ninth Schedule laws ko review kar sakti hai. [Q16]\n5. Seventh Schedule — Three Legislative Lists\n● 7th Schedule legislative powers ko 3 lists mein divide karti hai: Union List, State List aur Concurrent List.\nSource Q18 original counts deta hai: Union 97, State 66, Concurrent 47; saath mein source current\ncounts 98, 59, 52 note karta hai. [Q17, Q18]\n● Article 246 ke framework mein taxation/fees aur legislative subjects ka distribution Seventh Schedule ki\nlists se linked hai. [Q42]\n6. Concurrent List — High-Frequency Subjects & 42nd Amendment\n● Concurrent List ke repeated subjects: Economic & Social Planning (Entry 20), Prevention of Cruelty to\nAnimals, Criminal Laws/Criminal Procedure, Population Control & Family Planning, Adulteration of\nfoodstuffs/other goods, Succession, Marriage/Divorce/Adoption. [Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23, Q24, Q39, Q40]\n● Education originally State List subject tha; source ke mutabik 42nd Amendment, 1976 se Concurrent List\nmein transfer hua. Forests aur protection of wild animals/birds bhi isi Amendment se Concurrent side\nmein transfer hue. [Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Education ka constitutional connection source multiple places se dikhata hai: DPSP, Rural/Urban Local\nBodies, Fifth Schedule, Sixth Schedule aur Seventh Schedule—Q31 mein all five ka bearing maana\ngaya hai. [Q31]\n7. Union vs State vs Residuary — Subject Traps\n● Union List examples in source: Census, Banking, Insurance, Defence, Foreign Affairs, Railways,\nCorporation Tax, Inter-State trade & commerce, Inter-State migration/quarantine. [Q30, Q34, Q35, Q37, Q43]\n● State List examples: Police/Public Order, Agriculture, Public Health, Gas & Gas-works, Railway Police,\nLocal Government/Panchayati Raj, Land Reforms. Railways Union subject hai, lekin Railway Police\nState subject. [Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q44]\n● Residuary subjects Centre ke paas: source match question Space Research ko residuary example deta\nhai. Election trap mein List-I Entry 72 aur List-II Entry 37 dono relevant bataye gaye hain; MPPSC official\nkey source mein both (a) & (c) hai. [Q30, Q41]\n8. Tenth Schedule — Anti-Defection Law\n● 10th Schedule = Anti-defection Law. Isme Parliament aur State Legislatures ke members ko defection\nke ground par disqualify karne ke provisions hain; source ise 52nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1985\nse added batata hai. [Q32, Q33, Q45, Q46]\n9. Fifth Schedule — Scheduled Areas & Scheduled Tribes\n● 5th Schedule → Scheduled Areas aur Scheduled Tribes ka administration/control, Assam, Meghalaya,\nTripura aur Mizoram ke tribal areas ko chhodkar. Source ka core purpose Scheduled Tribes ke interests\nko protect karna hai. [Q47, Q49, Q50, Q51]\n● Fifth Schedule consequence: Scheduled Area President ke order se notify hota hai; concerned Governor\nke special powers tribal land ko non-tribal/private parties transfer hone se protect karte hain. Samatha\ncase context mein source private mining transfer ko void batata hai. [Q47, Q48, Q56, Q57]\n● Scheduled Areas wale State mein Tribal Advisory Council ka provision source Fifth Schedule para 4 se\nlink karta hai. Annual/required administration report Governor President ko deta hai—Chief Minister\nUnion Home Ministry ko nahi. [Q56, Q57]\n10. Sixth Schedule — Tribal Areas & Autonomous Districts"," ExamFusion Prep · examfusionprep.com\n● 6th Schedule → Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura aur Mizoram ke tribal areas ka administration; source iska\nobjective tribal culture ko save/maintain karna batata hai. Manipur is Schedule ke coverage mein nahi\nhai. [Q52, Q53, Q54, Q55]\n● Sixth Schedule tribal areas ko Autonomous Districts/Autonomous Regions ke roop mein administer\nkarne ka framework deta hai. District Council mein not more than 30 members; source ke mutabik not\nmore than 4 Governor nominate karte hain aur rest adult suffrage se elected hote hain. [Q58]\n● Fifth + Sixth Schedule ka common exam idea: Scheduled Tribes ke interests/protection; education se\nbhi source in schedules ka indirect/direct bearing batata hai. [Q31, Q51]\n11. Eleventh Schedule — Panchayati Raj\n● 11th Schedule 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 se add hui aur Panchayati Raj se related hai.\nSource ke mutabik isme total 29 subjects/items hain. [Q59, Q61]\n● Article 243G ke context mein Panchayats ko entrusted powers, authority aur responsibilities ki subject-\nlist Eleventh Schedule mein di gayi hai. [Q60]\n EXAM TRAPS — Source Ke Important Confusions\n⚠️\n\n▸Original 8 → present 12 Schedules; 9th–12th amendments se add hue. President ka oath Third Schedule\nmein nahi—source ke mutabik Article 60 mein hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q7]\n\n▸Q18 source original entries 97/66/47 aur current 98/59/52 alag deta hai. Q24 mein Inter-State trade =\nUnion, within-State trade = State; UPPSC key Adulteration + Succession ko correct maanta hai. [Q18, Q24]\n\n▸Q41 mein source List-I Entry 72 aur List-II Entry 37 dono ko relevant batata hai; MPPSC official key both (a)\n& (c). [Q41]\n\n▸5th Schedule general Scheduled Areas/ST; 6th specifically Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura, Mizoram. Q58\nsource answer (B): (i) & (iii); statement (ii) false because nominations not more than 4 hain. [Q49, Q50, Q52,\nQ53, Q54, Q55, Q58]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0300","t":"09 The Preamble","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Polity","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Preamble Full Mind Map\n🏛️ THE PREAMBLE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Preamble Basics — Adoption, Nature & Makers’ Mind\n2. India’s Constitutional Identity — Original vs Present Wording\n3. 42nd Amendment, 1976 — Socialist, Secular & Integrity\n4. Objectives Resolution, Amendability & Non-Justiciability\n5. “We, the People of India” — Popular Sovereignty\n6. Secularism & Words NOT Mentioned in the Preamble\n7. Justice, Liberty, Equality & Fraternity — Exact Components\n8. Famous Descriptions — Soul, Horoscope & Sacred Document\n9. Supreme Court Cases — Berubari, Kesavananda & Bommai\n10. Preamble Objectives in FR, DPSP & Fundamental Duties\n1. Preamble Basics — Adoption, Nature & Makers’ Mind\n● Indian Constitution ki Preamble Constitution ke main objectives, nature aur ideals ko outline karti hai.\nIsme Constitution ko adopt karne ki date 26 November 1949 di gayi hai. [Q1]\n● Preamble ko Constitution-makers ke mind/thought ka reflection maana gaya hai. Source mein Berubari\nCase (1960) ka reference hai ki Preamble makers ke mind ko samajhne ki key hai; Pt. Thakur Das\nBhargav ne ise Constitution ki “soul” kaha. Preamble ka idea USA se adopted bataya gaya hai. [Q4, Q5]\n● Indian Constitution ke core objectives aur philosophy primarily Preamble mein reflect hote hain. [Q44]\n2. India’s Constitutional Identity — Original vs Present Wording\n● 26 January 1950 ko Constitution enforce hone par India ka exact status source ke mutabik “Sovereign\nDemocratic Republic” tha. Us waqt “Socialist” aur “Secular” words Preamble ka part nahi the. [Q2, Q3,\nQ36]\n● Present sequence yaad rakho: SOVEREIGN → SOCIALIST → SECULAR → DEMOCRATIC →\nREPUBLIC. “People’s” word Indian Preamble mein nahi hai. [Q7, Q8, Q9, Q10]\n EXAM TRAP — 26 Nov 1949 vs 26 Jan 1950\n⚠️\n\n▸26 November 1949 = Constitution adopt/enact/give to ourselves ki date; Preamble mein ye date explicitly\nhai. [Q1]\n\n▸26 January 1950 = Constitution came into force. Source ke mutabik us date par wording “Sovereign\nDemocratic Republic” thi. [Q2, Q3]\n3. 42nd Amendment, 1976 — Socialist, Secular & Integrity\n● 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976 se Preamble amend hui. Source ke mutabik three additions\nthe: “Socialist”, “Secular” aur “Integrity”. “Sovereign Democratic Republic” ko “Sovereign Socialist\nSecular Democratic Republic” banaya gaya aur “Unity of the Nation” ko “Unity and Integrity of the\nNation” kiya gaya. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14, Q20, Q22, Q23, Q25, Q27]\n● 1975 tak “Integrity” Preamble mein nahi tha. 26 November 1949 ko adopted original Preamble mein\nSocialist, Secular aur Integrity present nahi the; “Republic” present tha. [Q16, Q21, Q24]\n● 42nd Amendment ko source Swaran Singh Committee ki recommendations se relate karta hai. India ko\n“Secular State” describe karne ke liye Preamble relevant hai. [Q14, Q15]\n● Given-set questions mein “Socialist” aur “Secular” 42nd Amendment additions hain; “Gram Swarajya”\naur “Sovereign” is addition-set ka part nahi. [Q17]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Preamble Full Mind Map\n4. Objectives Resolution, Amendability & Non-Justiciability\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ne Objectives Resolution 13 December 1946 ko move ki; Constituent Assembly ne 22\nJanuary 1947 ko adopt kiya. Source is Resolution ko later Preamble ka foundation batata hai. [Q18]\n● Preamble non-justiciable hai: independently Court of Law mein enforce nahi ki ja sakti. Lekin ambiguous\nconstitutional provisions ko interpret karne mein iska use hota hai aur ye Constitution ke specific\nprovisions ko override nahi kar sakti. [Q18, Q19, Q48, Q49]\n● Preamble amendable hai aur source ke mutabik ab tak sirf once amend hui — 42nd Amendment, 1976.\n[Q18, Q20, Q49]\n DISPUTED QUESTION — Source Q49\n⚠️\n\n▸Q49 ke source explanation ke mutabik statements 1, 2, 3 aur 4 sab correct hain, lekin options mein “1, 2, 3\nand 4” diya hi nahi gaya. Isliye source is question ko disputed maanta hai. [Q49]\n5. “We, the People of India” — Popular Sovereignty\n● Preamble “WE, THE PEOPLE OF INDIA” se start hoti hai. Source ke mutabik ye popular/people’s\nsovereignty ko indicate karta hai — authority ka ultimate source India ke log hain, kisi external power ka\nnahi. [Q28, Q29]\n6. Secularism & Words NOT Mentioned in the Preamble\n● Indian secularism ka source-answer: India mein State ka koi official religion nahi hai aur State sab\nreligions ko equal treatment deta hai. [Q31]\n● Preamble mein “Federal” word mentioned nahi hai; “Public Welfare” bhi Preamble ka word nahi hai.\n[Q32, Q33]\n● Preamble Liberty of thought, expression, belief, faith and worship deti hai; “Economic Liberty” explicitly\nmentioned nahi hai. Likewise Justice social, economic aur political hai — “Religious Justice” phrase\nPreamble mein nahi hai. [Q34, Q35]\n● “All individuals are fully and equally human” principle ko source Universalism kehta hai — har person\nHuman Rights ka entitled hai without discrimination. [Q30]\n7. Justice, Liberty, Equality & Fraternity — Exact Components\n● Exact count mnemonic: Justice = 3 types (social, economic, political); Liberty = 5 (thought, expression,\nbelief, faith, worship); Equality = 2 (status, opportunity); Fraternity = 1. [Q6, Q45, Q46]\n● Preamble sab citizens ke liye Justice, Liberty, Equality aur Fraternity secure/assure karne ka goal rakhti\nhai; Fraternity individual dignity aur Nation ki unity & integrity ko assure karti hai. [Q26]\n● Economic Justice Preamble mein objective hai aur DPSP mein bhi elaborate hota hai; source example\nke roop mein Article 38(1) cite karta hai. [Q47]\n● Social equality Constitution mein Right to Equality (Articles 14–18) ke under guaranteed hai; Preamble\nbhi social equality ko aim karti hai. [Q50]\n8. Famous Descriptions — Soul, Horoscope & Sacred Document\n● Preamble ko “Soul of the Constitution” kaha gaya hai. Source K.M. Munshi ko “horoscope of our\nsovereign democratic Republic” phrase se associate karta hai; Subhash Kashyap ka\nbody–soul/foundation–building analogy bhi diya gaya hai. [Q37, Q38]\n EXAM TRAP — “Soul” vs “Heart and Soul”\n⚠️\n\n▸General Preamble question mein source answer = Preamble as “Soul of the Constitution”. [Q37]\n\n▸Agar specifically Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ke “heart and soul” phrase ki baat ho, source note Article 32 / Right to\nConstitutional Remedies ko answer batata hai. [Q37]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Preamble Full Mind Map\n● Source ke mutabik B.R. Ambedkar ne Constitution ko basic/sacred document treat karne par zor diya;\nQ39 ka correct answer B.R. Ambedkar hai. [Q39]\n9. Supreme Court Cases — Berubari, Kesavananda & Bommai\n● Berubari Case (1960): source ke mutabik Supreme Court ne first time kaha ki Preamble Constitution ka\nintegral part nahi hai. [Q40]\n● Kesavananda Bharati Case (1973): source ke mutabik Preamble Constitution ka part maana gaya aur\nBasic Structure doctrine ke context mein Preamble ko basic structure ka part regard kiya gaya. [Q42, Q48]\n● S.R. Bommai v. Union of India (1994): source Q41 mein Preamble ko Constitution ka integral part\nmaana gaya. Source explanation specifically kehta hai ki Kesavananda option mein nahi tha, isliye given\noptions mein Bommai correct choice hai. [Q41]\n EXAM TRAP — Case-based Option Logic\n⚠️\n\n▸Berubari (1960) = source says Preamble not integral part. [Q40]\n\n▸Kesavananda Bharati (1973) = Preamble part of Constitution / basic structure context. [Q42, Q48]\n\n▸Q41 mein Kesavananda option absent tha, isliye source ne S.R. Bommai (1994) choose kiya. [Q41]\n10. Preamble Objectives in FR, DPSP & Fundamental Duties\n● Preamble ke ideals/objectives ko source Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles of State Policy aur\nFundamental Duties ke chapters mein further elaborated batata hai. [Q43]\n● Constitution ka objective justice, liberty, equality aur fraternity ke through citizens aur nation ki\nadvancement ko balance karna hai; Preamble is philosophy ka primary statement hai. [Q43, Q44]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0301","t":"01 Subdivisions of Biology","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Subdivisions Of Biology Full Mind Map\n🧬 SUBDIVISIONS OF BIOLOGY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Zoology — Scope & Father of Zoology\n2. Core Branches — Ornithology, Genetics, Ecology & Palaeobiology\n3. Specialized Branches — Flowers, Skull, Grasses, Pollen & Invertebrates\n4. Population, Culture & Behaviour — Demography, Ethnology & Ethology\n5. Bionics & Related Terms — Bionomics, Bionomy & Biometry\n6. Palaeobotany — Plant Fossils & Birbal Sahni\n7. Animal Rearing & Production — Sericulture, Apiculture, Pisciculture & Lac Culture\n8. Plant Cultivation Branches — Horticulture, Olericulture, Pomology, Floriculture & Agronomy\n9. Lexicography & Related Terms\n10. Viticulture — Grape Cultivation\n11. Vermiculture — Earthworm Culture\n12. Genetics — Heredity & Variation\n13. Gerontology — Old Age & Ageing\n14. Pedology & Osteology — Soil and Bones\n15. Snake Studies & Other Zoology Branches\n16. Core Biology vs Psychology + Hydroponics\n1. Zoology — Scope & Father of Zoology\n● Zoology biology ki branch hai jo living aur extinct — dono animals ka study karti hai; isme structure,\nembryology, evolution, classification, habits aur distribution include hote hain. [Q1]\n● Aristotle ko source 'Father of Zoology' batata hai. [Q1]\n2. Core Branches — Ornithology, Genetics, Ecology & Palaeobiology\n● Birds ka study — Ornithology; Inheritance ka study — Genetics; Environment / organisms-environment\nrelationship ka study — Ecology; Fossils ka study — Palaeobiology. [Q2]\n● Match-the-following order source mein: Birds → Ornithology (A-3), Inheritance → Genetics (B-4),\nEnvironment → Ecology (C-2), Fossil → Palaeobiology (D-1). [Q2]\n3. Specialized Branches — Flowers, Skull, Grasses, Pollen & Invertebrates\n● Source ke mutabik flowers ka study — Anthology; human skull ka study — Phrenology; grasses ka\nstudy — Agrostology; pollen grains aur other spores ka study — Palynology. [Q3]\n● Insects ka scientific study — Entomology; fish ka study — Ichthyology; parasitic organisms ka study —\nParasitology; molluscs aur unke shells ka study — Malacology. [Q4]\n4. Population, Culture & Behaviour — Demography, Ethnology & Ethology\n● Demography — populations, including human beings, ka statistical study. Ecology — organisms aur\nenvironment ke interrelationship ka study; Genetics — heredity and variation; Virology — viruses ka\nstudy. [Q5]\n● Ethnology — different races/cultures of mankind ka comparative study; Ethnography — ek specific\nculture ka study; Ethology — animal behaviour; Ethics — ethical duties aur moral principles ka study.\n[Q6]\n5. Bionics & Related Terms — Bionomics, Bionomy & Biometry\n● Bionics — nature mein biological systems ke properties/methods ka study aur us knowledge ka\nmechanical world / engineering mein use. [Q7]\n● Bionomics — organism aur environment ke relation ka comprehensive study; Bionomy — laws of life ka\nstudy; Biometry — biological problems ka statistical study. [Q7]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Subdivisions Of Biology Full Mind Map\n6. Palaeobotany — Plant Fossils & Birbal Sahni\n● Palaeobotany palaeontology ki branch hai jo geological contexts se plant fossils — ancient plants ke\nremains — ki recovery aur identification se related hai. [Q8]\n● Q8 ke options mein plant fossils explicitly nahi the, isliye source correct choice (D) 'None of these' deta\nhai. Source Prof. Birbal Sahni ko Father of Indian Palaeobotany batata hai. [Q8]\n7. Animal Rearing & Production — Sericulture, Apiculture, Pisciculture & Lac\nCulture\n● Sericulture — silk production ke liye silkworms ka rearing. Apiculture — honey/wax production ke liye\nhoney bees ka rearing. [Q9, Q10]\n● Pisciculture fish farming / fish hatchery se related hai; lac insect ke rearing ko Lac culture kaha jata hai.\n[Q13]\n● Q13 mein 'Pisciculture — Lac insect' pair source ke hisab se incorrectly matched hai. [Q13]\n8. Plant Cultivation Branches — Horticulture, Olericulture, Pomology,\nFloriculture & Agronomy\n● Horticulture ek broader agriculture branch hai jisme Pomology (fruits), Olericulture (vegetables) aur\nFloriculture (flowers) include hote hain. [Q11]\n● Olericulture specifically vegetable growing ka science hai — non-woody/herbaceous plants ko food ke\nliye cultivate karna. [Q12]\n● Floriculture — flowers; Pomology — fruits; Agronomy — crops. [Q11]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Horticulture vs Olericulture — Q11–Q12\n\n▸Q11 ke specific matching context mein vegetables ke liye 'Horticulture' ko incorrect maana gaya, kyunki\nexact term Olericulture hai. [Q11]\n\n▸General sense mein Horticulture broader field hai; source explanation itself Olericulture ko vegetables ka\nspecific branch batata hai. [Q11, Q12]\n9. Lexicography & Related Terms\n● Lexicography — dictionaries ki design, compilation aur evaluation; source pair 'Lexicography —\nCompilation of dictionaries' ko correctly matched batata hai. [Q14, Q15]\n● Philology — language structure aur history; stamp collection — Philately; Entomology — insects;\nIconography — idols / visual arts ka study. [Q14]\n10. Viticulture — Grape Cultivation\n● Viticulture grapes ki science, production aur study hai; vineyard mein hone wale processes/events se\nrelated hai. [Q16]\n11. Vermiculture — Earthworm Culture\n● Vermiculture — earthworms ko manage aur cultivate / raise karne ka process. [Q17]\n● Earthworms organic waste ko nutrient-rich soil / vermicompost mein convert karne mein help karte hain;\nvermiculture mein earthworms hi use hote hain. [Q17, Q18]\n12. Genetics — Heredity & Variation\n● Genetics genes, heredity aur living organisms mein genetic variations ka broad study hai. [Q19]\n● Mendel's laws aur DNA structure genetics ke parts hain, lekin source ke mutabik most comprehensive\ndefinition heredity and variations ka study hai. [Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Subdivisions Of Biology Full Mind Map\n13. Gerontology — Old Age & Ageing\n● Gerontology — old age, ageing process aur old people ke particular problems ka scientific study; isme\nsocial, psychological, cognitive aur biological aspects of ageing include hote hain. [Q20, Q21, Q22]\n● Oncology — cancer treatment se related medical branch; Teratology — physiological development ki\nabnormalities ka study; Ornithology — birds ka study. [Q21]\n● Thanatology — death aur usse associated practices ka scientific study. [Q22]\n14. Pedology & Osteology — Soil and Bones\n● Pedology — natural environment mein soil formation, soil morphology aur soil classification ka study.\n[Q23]\n● Osteology — bones ka study. Orology — mountains; Serology — serum aur other body fluids; Geology\n— earth ki internal structure aur andar milne wale matter ka study. [Q24, Q25]\n15. Snake Studies & Other Zoology Branches\n● Serpentology / Ophiology — snakes ka study; source ise Zoology ki branch batata hai. [Q26]\n● Herpetology broader branch hai jo amphibians aur reptiles — frogs, toads, salamanders, snakes,\nlizards, turtles, crocodiles — se related hai; Serpentology iski sub-discipline hai. [Q26]\n● Ornithology — birds; Ichthyology — fish. [Q26]\n16. Core Biology vs Psychology + Hydroponics\n● Physiology, Pathology aur Bacteriology source ke according biology/medical science ke core branches\nhain; Psychology mind aur behaviour ka study hai, isliye Q27 mein odd one out hai. [Q27]\n● Hydroponics hydroculture ka subset hai — mineral nutrient solutions in water ka use karke plants ko soil\nke bina grow karna. [Q28]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0302","t":"02 Evolution of Life","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Evolution Of Life Full Mind Map\n🧬 EVOLUTION OF LIFE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Geological Epochs — Oldest to Newest\n2. Primitive Earth — Atmosphere & Magnetic Reversals\n3. Origin of Life — Age of Life & Cyanobacteria\n4. Darwin — Origin of Species & Natural Selection\n5. Lamarckism — Acquired Characters & Use/Disuse\n6. Mutation Theory — Hugo de Vries & Genetic Variation\n7. Important Theory / Scientist Match\n8. Human Evolution — Cro-Magnon & Denisovans\n9. Archaeopteryx — Ancient Bird & Connecting Link\n10. Mammoth, Dinosaurs & Evolutionary Sequence\n1. Geological Epochs — Oldest to Newest\n● Source chronology oldest se newest: Paleocene → Eocene → Oligocene → Miocene → Pliocene →\nPleistocene → Holocene. Given options mein correct sequence Eocene → Miocene → Pliocene →\nPleistocene → Holocene hai. [Q1]\n2. Primitive Earth — Atmosphere & Magnetic Reversals\n● Primitive Earth ka atmosphere reducing tha: methane, ammonia, water vapour, carbon dioxide, carbon\nmonoxide, nitrogen, hydrogen, neon etc. present the, lekin free oxygen absent tha. [Q2]\n● Earth ka magnetic field history mein har kuch hundred-thousand years mein reverse hota raha; source\nke mutabik last 5 million years mein at least 20 reversals hue. [Q3]\n● Earth ke earliest atmosphere mein oxygen nahi tha; living organisms ke origin ke baad, especially\noxygen-producing cyanobacteria jaise organisms ne atmosphere ko modify kiya. [Q3]\n3. Origin of Life — Age of Life & Cyanobacteria\n● Source ke Q4 ke options ke context mein life on Earth ka emergence approximately 2 billion years ago\ndiya gaya hai; same explanation modern scientific consensus ko ~3.5–3.8 billion years ago batati hai.\n[Q4]\n● Blue-green algae (Cyanobacteria) ko source oldest organism batata hai. Ye photosynthesis karte hain\naur gaseous oxygen release karke Earth par biodiversity ke development mein important role nibhate\nhain. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q4 — Option-based answer vs source note\n\n▸Question ka marked answer 2 billion years hai because wahi provided options mein fit hota hai. Source\nexplanation khud modern consensus ko ~3.5–3.8 billion years ago note karti hai. [Q4]\n4. Darwin — Origin of Species & Natural Selection\n● Charles Darwin ne natural selection ko apni book 'The Origin of Species' mein explain kiya; source\npublication year 1859 deta hai aur ise evolutionary biology ki foundation batata hai. [Q6]\n● Darwin ki natural selection theory ke main points: Overproduction, Struggle for existence, Variation, aur\nSurvival of the fittest. [Q7]\n● Widely accepted evolution theory based on natural selection ko source Darwin se associate karta hai.\n[Q8]\n● Darwinian framework mein natural selection evolution ka main/basic mechanism diya gaya hai. [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Evolution Of Life Full Mind Map\n5. Lamarckism — Acquired Characters & Use/Disuse\n● French biologist Lamarck ko source life evolution ko formally public ke saamne explain karne wala first\nperson batata hai. Uska 'Theory of Inheritance of Acquired Characters' 1801 mein present hua aur 1809\nmein 'Philosophie Zoologique' mein publish hua. [Q9]\n● Lamarckism ke context mein snakes ke limbs ka loss 'use and disuse of organs' se explain kiya gaya\nhai — burrowing ke dauran limbs ka use band hone se generations mein unka loss hua. [Q13]\n6. Mutation Theory — Hugo de Vries & Genetic Variation\n● Hugo de Vries ne mutation theory of evolution di. Source ke mutabik new species continuous variations\nke bajay sudden variations (mutations) se form ho sakti hain; mutations heritable hoti hain. [Q10]\n● Gene aur chromosomal mutations ko source biological changes ka ultimate source / evolution ka 'raw\nmaterial' batata hai, jo large-scale diversity ko lead kar sakta hai. [Q14]\n● New species ke origin ke liye source mutation ko most responsible factor batata hai because mutations\nnew genetic variations introduce karti hain. [Q15]\n7. Important Theory / Scientist Match\n● Correct match: Theory of mutation → Hugo de Vries; Theory of evolution → Charles Darwin; One gene–\none enzyme hypothesis → Beadle & Tatum; Operon concept → Jacob & Monod. [Q11]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Darwin vs Lamarck vs De Vries\n\n▸Darwin → Natural selection / Origin of Species. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q12]\n\n▸Lamarck → Inheritance of acquired characters / use and disuse; source says first formal explanation of\nevolution to public. [Q9, Q13]\n\n▸Hugo de Vries → Mutation theory. [Q10, Q11]\n8. Human Evolution — Cro-Magnon & Denisovans\n● Given options mein Cro-Magnon man ko modern human ka latest ancestor diya gaya hai. Source Cro-\nMagnon ko early modern humans ke liye common name batata hai; known remains ~43,000 years old\naur brain capacity ~1,600 cc mention karta hai. [Q16]\n● Denisovans / Denisova hominins ek extinct archaic early-human species/subspecies the jo Asia mein\nLower aur Middle Paleolithic ke dauran rahe. First identification 2010 mein Siberian Denisova Cave se\nfinger bone ke basis par hui. [Q17]\n9. Archaeopteryx — Ancient Bird & Connecting Link\n● Archaeopteryx ko source Jurassic age ka most ancient bird batata hai, approximately 150 million years\nold; ise oldest-known birds mein count kiya gaya hai. [Q18]\n● Archaeopteryx Reptilia aur Aves ke beech connecting link hai: reptilian features mein teeth aur long\nbony tail, aur bird features mein feathers aur wings milte hain. [Q19]\n10. Mammoth, Dinosaurs & Evolutionary Sequence\n● Source ke question framing mein Mammoth ko elephant ka ancestor diya gaya hai. Explanation ke\nmutabik extinct mammoths modern African/Asian elephants ke closely related hain aur woolly\nmammoths + modern elephants ka common ancestor ~6 million years ago tha. [Q20]\n● Dinosaurs Mesozoic reptiles the. Source Mesozoic ko reptiles/dinosaurs ka age batata hai, roughly\n250–65 million years ago, aur isme Triassic, Jurassic aur Cretaceous periods include hote hain. [Q21]\n● Era-based direct question mein dinosaurs ka correct era Mesozoic hai. [Q22]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Evolution Of Life Full Mind Map\n● Evolutionary history mein amphibians reptiles se pehle aur reptiles mammals se pehle aaye. Source\nsequence: Salamander (amphibian, ~360 mya) → Python (reptile, ~300 mya) → Kangaroo (marsupial\nmammal, ~145 mya). [Q23]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0303","t":"03 Taxonomy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n🧬 TAXONOMY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Taxonomic Hierarchy & Species\n2. Bacteria, Microbes & Unicellular Reproduction\n3. Animal Physiology — Warm-blooded, Respiration & Basic Classification\n4. True Fish, Birds & Marine Mammals\n5. Amphibians, Frogs & Reptiles\n6. Squirrels, Dogs, Bears & Apes\n7. Heart Chambers, Gallbladder, Hooves & Wildlife Names\n8. Kiwi, Coral, Molluscs & Arthropods\n9. Silk, Lac & Insect Physiology\n10. Parasites, Feeding Types & Nocturnal Animals\n11. Desert Animals & Snake Biology\n12. Insectivorous Plants & Pitcher Plant\n13. Underground Stems, Roots & Storage Organs\n14. Pea Family, Clove & Saffron\n15. Edible Plant Parts, Fruits & Plant Chemicals\n16. Plant Fibres, Triticale & Dry-land Adaptations\n17. Plant Habitat Types — Epiphyte, Halophyte, Hydrophyte & Lithophyte\n18. Ecology — Producers, Decomposition & Trophic Levels\n19. Fish Survival, Respiration & Plant Pigments\n20. Species, Fungi & Mushrooms\n21. Symbiosis — Fig, Mycorrhiza, Lichen & Rhizobium\n1. Taxonomic Hierarchy & Species\n● Plant taxonomy ka hierarchy higher se lower: Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order → Family →\nGenus → Species. Fundamental similarities wale individual organisms ka group species hota hai;\nrelated species milkar genus banate hain. [Q1, Q2]\n● Source ke mutabik identified species ki sankhya mein insects sabse bada group hain; Insecta,\nArthropoda phylum ka class hai. [Q3]\n2. Bacteria, Microbes & Unicellular Reproduction\n● Antonie van Leeuwenhoek ko source bacteria ki discovery aur father of microbiology se associate karta\nhai. Bacteria microscopic hote hain aur compound microscope se dekhe ja sakte hain. [Q4, Q5]\n● Kuch bacteria autotrophic hote hain; photosynthetic bacteria mein plant-like chloroplast nahi,\nbacteriochlorophyll pigments hote hain. Bacteria living, single-celled prokaryotic microbes hain; living–\nnon-living borderline wali baat viruses ke liye di gayi hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● Gram-positive vs Gram-negative distinction cell-wall structure par based hai. Mycoplasma source ke\nmutabik autonomous growth/reproduction capable smallest organism hai aur isme cell wall absent hoti\nhai. [Q8, Q9]\n● Amoeba binary fission se reproduce karta hai; source reason “all unicellular organisms reproduce\nasexually” ko false batata hai because some unicellular eukaryotes sexual reproduction bhi kar sakte\nhain. [Q10]\n● Bacteria aur fungi artificial/synthetic medium par cultured ho sakte hain, lekin viruses ko living host cell\nchahiye. [Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Source has multi-correct/disputed items\n\n▸Q11 mein spore formation Fungi, Algae aur Fern—multiple listed organisms mein possible diya gaya hai;\nsource ise disputed / more than one option correct note karta hai. [Q11]\n\n▸Q12 ka clear distinction: bacteria + fungi artificial medium par; virus living host ke bina replicate nahi karta.\n[Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n3. Animal Physiology — Warm-blooded, Respiration & Basic Classification\n● Warm-blooded mammals aur birds external environment ke bawajood body temperature relatively\nconstant rakhte hain; source ise homeostasis se relate karta hai. [Q13]\n● Echinoderms generally external fertilization aur egg-laying pattern dikhate hain; source Q14 mein\n“echinoderms are viviparous” ko incorrect statement batata hai. [Q14]\n● Hydra mein blood/circulatory system nahi hota, phir bhi respiration aur excretion cell layers ke across\nsimple diffusion se hoti hai. [Q15]\n4. True Fish, Birds & Marine Mammals\n● Starfish true fish nahi; source ise Echinodermata mein rakhta hai. Sawfish, pipefish aur guitarfish true\nfishes hain. Catfish aur seahorse bhi true fishes diye gaye hain; silverfish insect, crayfish crustacean,\njellyfish cnidarian aur sea cucumber echinoderm hai. [Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19]\n● Shark ka skeleton bone ka nahi, cartilage/connective tissue ka hota hai; source answer “0 bones” deta\nhai. Golden Mahseer fish hai, bird nahi. [Q20, Q21]\n● Blue whale largest mammal hai; whales mammals hain. Sperm whale largest toothed whale hai, while\nblue whale baleen whale hai. [Q22, Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Echidna egg-laying mammal hai; bats true sustained flight capable mammals hain aur Aves group ke\nmember nahi. [Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Sea cow/dugong aur sea lion mammals hain, seahorse fish hai. Dolphins aquatic mammals / toothed\nwhales ke family group mein diye gaye hain; seals pinniped marine mammals hain. [Q31, Q32, Q33]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Indian Flying Fox (source-specific current note)\n\n▸Source explanation ke mutabik Indian Flying Fox pehle Wildlife Protection Act, 1972 ke Schedule V/vermin\ncategory mein tha, lekin 2022 amendment ke baad Schedule V remove hua aur source current placement\nSchedule II note karta hai; isliye Statement-I ko present context mein incorrect bataya gaya hai. [Q30]\n\n▸Indian Flying Fox frugivorous hai—fruits, nectar, flowers feed karta hai; blood-feeding statement bhi source\nke mutabik incorrect hai. [Q30]\n5. Amphibians, Frogs & Reptiles\n● Amphibian ka literal sense “both kinds of life” hai—land aur water dono se associated; frogs cold-\nblooded/ectothermic hain aur moist skin se gas exchange bhi kar sakte hain. [Q34, Q35, Q36]\n● Frog metamorphosis mein herbivorous tadpole ka long intestine adult carnivorous diet ke adaptation ke\nsaath shorten hota hai. [Q37]\n● Gharial/Gavialis ko source mainly Ganga River basin se associate karta hai. Otter ko Q39 ke source\nexplanation mein given options ke context mein “atrocious/aggressive predatory” animal bataya gaya\nhai. [Q38, Q39]\n● Hedgehog aur pangolin threat par body ko ball ki tarah curl karke vulnerable parts protect karte hain;\nmarmot burrow mein hide karta hai. [Q40]\n6. Squirrels, Dogs, Bears & Apes\n● Indian squirrels mainly arboreal hain: tree nests/dreys banate hain, nuts/seeds ko ground mein store kar\nsakte hain, aur source unhe omnivorous batata hai. [Q41]\n● Dingo bark nahi karta, wolf-like howl karta hai. Street-performing bear ke context mein source sloth bear\nanswer deta hai. [Q42, Q43]\n● Chimpanzee, parrot aur dolphin ko source language-use training ke examples mein rakhta hai; dog ko\nnahi. Human ko apes se separate karne ke liye source desire to learn aur ability to express ko highlight\nkarta hai. [Q44, Q45]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n● Langur ape nahi, Asian monkey hai aur tail hoti hai. Gibbon “lesser ape” aur source ke mutabik smallest\nman-like ape hai. Orangutan stick tools se tree/log holes se insects nikal sakta hai. Panda bear family\nUrsidae ka member hai. [Q46, Q47, Q48, Q49]\n7. Heart Chambers, Gallbladder, Hooves & Wildlife Names\n● Frog/amphibians aur most reptiles ka heart 3-chambered hota hai; fish 2-chambered, mammals/birds 4-\nchambered, aur crocodile 4-chambered diya gaya hai. [Q50, Q51]\n● Jackal ke hooves nahi hote; source Canis aureus aur padded feet with nails mention karta hai. Nilgai ko\nsource antelope/deer-type Bovidae family context mein rakhta hai. [Q53, Q54]\n● Wildlife scientific-name match: Asiatic wild ass → Equus hemionus; Barasingha → Cervus duvaucelii;\nChinkara → Gazella bennettii; Nilgai → Boselaphus tragocamelus. [Q55]\n● Leopard ka scientific name Panthera pardus. Source lion breeding ko non-seasonal, cheetah ko non-\nroaring, aur leopard ko scent-marking big cat batata hai. [Q56, Q57]\n● Marsupials naturally India mein nahi milte—source Statement-I ko true aur “sirf predator-free montane\ngrasslands mein thrive karte hain” ko false batata hai. [Q58]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q52 has multiple valid animals in source\n\n▸Source explanation ke mutabik Camel, Giraffe aur Rat—teenon gallbladder ke bina listed hain. Isliye Q52 ko\nsingle-option fact ki tarah memorize na karein; source itself multiple options ko valid batata hai. [Q52]\n8. Kiwi, Coral, Molluscs & Arthropods\n● Match: wingless insect → Silverfish; flightless bird → Kiwi; limbless reptile → Snake; lungless creature\n→ Fish. Kiwi New Zealand ka flightless bird hai. [Q59, Q60]\n● Corals Cnidaria ke marine invertebrates hain aur reef-building calcium-carbonate skeleton ke karan\nsource unhe organic origin ka batata hai. [Q61]\n● Octopus cephalopod mollusc hai; source colossal squid ko largest invertebrate batata hai. [Q62, Q63]\n● Crab, mite, spider, scorpion sab arthropods hain, lekin crab Malacostraca aur baaki three Arachnida\nmein diye gaye hain. White Leghorn fowl variety hai. [Q64, Q65]\n● Ticks aur mites arachnids hain; termites “white ants” ke naam se bhi known hain; glow-worm luminous\ninsect hai. [Q66, Q67, Q68]\n● Parasite ke andar parasite ko hyperparasitism/hyperparasite phenomenon kaha gaya hai. Female\nAnopheles resting position mein body substrate se angle banati hai, while Culex more parallel rest karta\nhai. [Q69, Q70]\n● Spider insect nahi, arachnid hai—8 legs; insects ke 6 legs. Spider silk ko source Gossamer silk bhi\nkehta hai. [Q71, Q72, Q73, Q74]\n9. Silk, Lac & Insect Physiology\n● Commercial silk silkworm ke pupa/cocoon stage mein milta hai; Bombyx mori mulberry leaves par feed\nkarta hai. [Q75, Q76]\n● Lac lac insects ki resinous secretion hai. Silk, lac aur honey insects se milte hain, pearl molluscs se—so\npearl insect product nahi. [Q77, Q78]\n● Cockroach ka blood white/colourless diya gaya hai because haemoglobin absent; oxygen transport\ntracheal tubes se hota hai. Earthworm mein red blood cells absent hain but haemoglobin plasma mein\ndissolved hota hai. [Q79, Q80]\n● Most insects tracheal system se respire karte hain. Cicada, froghopper aur pond skater source ke\nmutabik insects hain. [Q81, Q82]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n10. Parasites, Feeding Types & Nocturnal Animals\n● Tapeworm hermaphrodite; roundworm mein separate sexes; filaria nematode se; Guinea worm bhi\nnematode hai, annelid nahi. [Q83]\n● Detritivores mein earthworm, millipede aur woodlice included; jellyfish/seahorse nahi. Filter-feeder\nexamples mein clams, oysters, krill, sponges, baleen whales aur kuch fish diye gaye hain. [Q84, Q85]\n● Parasitoid species source ke mutabik carabid beetles, flies aur wasps mein milti hain; centipedes\npredators aur termites detritivores diye gaye hain. [Q86]\n● Mosquito, bat, owl aur kiwi nocturnal examples hain. Given fauna mein source Malabar civet ko strictly\nnocturnal answer leta hai; lion-tailed macaque diurnal aur sambar mainly crepuscular/nocturnal activity\nwala bataya hai. [Q87, Q88]\n● Ant ka brain body-size proportion ke context mein source sabse large batata hai; ant bite mein formic\nacid inject hota hai, aur kuch ant species fungi cultivate karti hain. [Q89, Q90, Q91]\n● Blood sucking female mosquitoes karti hain; males flower/fruit juices par feed karte hain. Source female\nmosquitoes ko generally larger/bigger-winged batata hai. [Q92]\n11. Desert Animals & Snake Biology\n● Camel ke context mein source intestine mein water storage mention karta hai. Kangaroo rat ko longest\nwithout drinking water aur highly concentrated/“solid” urine excretion se associate karta hai. [Q93, Q94,\nQ95]\n● Female spider mating ke around male ko kill/eat kar sakti hai—source ise spider cannibalism ke\nexample ke roop mein deta hai. [Q96]\n● King cobra nest banata hai eggs lay/guard karne ke liye; source ise only snake that builds a nest batata\nhai. King cobra ka diet mainly other snakes hai. [Q97, Q98, Q100]\n● Cobra venom mainly neurotoxic diya gaya hai. Python non-venomous snake hai; snake poison glands\nvertebrate salivary glands ke homologous aur fangs modified maxillary teeth diye gaye hain. [Q99, Q101,\nQ102, Q103]\n● Source ke mutabik butterflies, fish aur frogs—teeno groups mein poisonous species mil sakti hain. Kuch\nturtles/fish/marine mammals herbivorous aur kuch snakes viviparous ho sakte hain. [Q104, Q105]\n● Dog ko source herbivore nahi maanta aur available evidence ko natural carnivory ke support mein\nframe karta hai. [Q106]\n12. Insectivorous Plants & Pitcher Plant\n● Rafflesia arnoldii source ke mutabik world ka largest flower hai; plant leaves/roots/stem ke bina\ndescribed hai. [Q107]\n● Insectivorous plants nitrogen-deficient soil mein grow karte hain aur insects se nitrogen requirement\nfulfill karte hain. Pitcher plant/Nepenthes insectivorous plant hai. [Q108, Q109, Q112]\n● Pitcher modified leaf hota hai jo pitfall trap ki tarah work karta hai. Nepenthes photosynthetic autotroph\nhai, parasite nahi. [Q110, Q111]\n● Nepenthes khasiana India ka rare/endangered pitcher plant hai aur source ise Garo, Khasi, Jaintia hills\nof Meghalaya se associate karta hai. [Q113]\n13. Underground Stems, Roots & Storage Organs\n● Turmeric Curcuma longa ka underground modified stem—rhizome—hai; turmeric powder aur edible part\nbhi isi rhizome se aata hai. [Q114, Q115, Q116, Q117]\n● Sweet potato modified root hai; source potato, Bandda aur Jimikand ko modified stems ke group mein\nrakhta hai. Sugarcane, potato, ginger ke storage organs stem hain; sweet potato ka root. [Q118, Q119]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n● Ginger modified stem hai; nodes, internodes aur scaly leaves uski stem nature indicate karte hain.\nTurnip, carrot aur sweet potato modified roots diye gaye hain. [Q120, Q121]\n● Match: Rhizome → Ginger; Tuber → Potato; Bulb → Garlic; Corm → Jimikand/Suran. [Q122]\n● Potato Solanum tuberosum ka underground modified stem/tuber hai. [Q123, Q124]\n14. Pea Family, Clove & Saffron\n● Pea plant dicot herbaceous annual hai aur Fabaceae/Leguminosae family mein aata hai. Groundnut,\nhorse-gram aur soybean—teeno pea family/Fabaceae legumes hain. [Q125, Q126]\n● Clove Syzygium aromaticum ka aromatic dried flower bud hai; MCQ wording mein dried flower/flower\nbud dono form source mein use hue hain. [Q127, Q128, Q129, Q130, Q131, Q132]\n● Saffron Crocus sativus flower ke stigma aur styles se milta hai, seed se nahi. Source Q134 mein ise\ngynoecium/female reproductive “seed-forming parts” ke context mein describe karta hai. [Q133, Q134]\n15. Edible Plant Parts, Fruits & Plant Chemicals\n● Potato ka edible part tuber/modified stem hai; onion ka edible portion fleshy modified leaves aur coconut\nka cellular endosperm diya gaya hai. [Q135, Q136]\n● Ladies finger/okra botanically fruit hai; potato stem aur radish/sweet potato roots hain. Source apple ko\nfalse fruit ke example ke roop mein deta hai; lychee ko broad structural category “drupe” context mein\nplace karta hai. [Q137, Q138, Q139]\n● Garlic ki characteristic smell sulphur compounds (Allicin/Allyl methyl sulphide) se; onion cutting par\nsulfenic acid lacrimal glands irritate karta hai; chilli pungency capsaicin se hoti hai. [Q140, Q141, Q142,\nQ143]\n● Fruit sweetness ka source answer fructose hai. Diatoms drowning diagnosis mein forensic significance\nrakhte hain. Mulberry ka multiple fruit type sorosis diya gaya hai. [Q144, Q145, Q146]\n16. Plant Fibres, Triticale & Dry-land Adaptations\n● Sunn, hemp aur jute bast/stem fibres hain; cotton seed-hair fibre hai, stem product nahi. [Q147]\n● Triticale wheat × rye cross se developed first man-made cereal crop diya gaya hai; source ise nature\nmein naturally found nahi batata. [Q148, Q149]\n● Bare rock/soil-less surface par lichens aur mosses survival ke likely pioneers diye gaye hain; ferns\ngenerally soil aur mushrooms decaying organic matter/soil se associated hain. [Q150]\n● Desert plants ki long roots deep water search ke adaptation ke roop mein di gayi hain; high soil\ntemperature ko cause nahi maana gaya. Phreatophytes deep groundwater tap karne wali deep-rooted\nplants hain. [Q151, Q152, Q153]\n● Xerophytes dry climate adapted plants hain; succulents thick fleshy tissues mein water store karte hain.\n[Q154, Q155]\n17. Plant Habitat Types — Epiphyte, Halophyte, Hydrophyte & Lithophyte\n● Epiphytes host plant par grow karke mechanical support lete hain, food/water directly host se nahi;\nsource orchids ko example deta hai. [Q156]\n● High-salinity soil/water plants halophytes kehlate hain. Hydrophytes aquatic plants hote hain; lithophytes\nrocks par grow karte hain. [Q157, Q158, Q159, Q160]\n● Nepenthes hydrophyte nahi—source ise tropical carnivorous pitcher plant batata hai. [Q161]\n● Q162 source ke mutabik weeping jelly excess acid se; sugarcane ke liye Acetobacter diazotrophicus\nRhizobium se more suitable; salt-water plants halophytes; dormancy breaking mein\ngibberellins/cytokinin use ho sakte hain. [Q162]\n● Land par living plants/animals terrestrial organisms kehlate hain. [Q163]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Taxonomy Full Mind Map\n18. Ecology — Producers, Decomposition & Trophic Levels\n● Producers/autotrophs biotic aur abiotic components ke intermediaries ke roop mein source mein\ndescribed hain—sunlight, water, CO jaise abiotic resources ko organic food mein convert karte hain.\n₂\n[Q164]\n● Microorganisms ke through organic matter breakdown decomposition hai; bacteria/fungi decomposers\ncomplex organics ko simpler substances mein convert karte hain. [Q165]\n● Autotroph = producer; saprotroph dead organic matter se nutrients; herbivores primary consumers hote\nhain, secondary consumers nahi. [Q166]\n● Trophic level-I mein autotrophs/green plants aate hain. Ocean primary producers ke given set mein\ncyanobacteria aur diatoms hain; copepods/foraminifera consumers diye gaye hain. [Q167, Q168]\n19. Fish Survival, Respiration & Plant Pigments\n● Frozen lakes mein upper surface freeze hone ke baad below liquid water remain karta hai; source\nanomalous expansion / 4°C density behavior se fishes ke survival ko explain karta hai. [Q169]\n● Fish gills dissolved oxygen absorb karte hain; water se bahar gills atmospheric oxygen efficiently absorb\nnahi kar pate, isliye fish die kar sakti hai. [Q170, Q171]\n● Apple ka red colour anthocyanin se; tomato ka red colour lycopene se. [Q172, Q173, Q174, Q175]\n● Papaya yellow colour source caricaxanthin pigment se associate karta hai; papaya carotene-rich aur\npapain enzyme mention kiya gaya hai. [Q176]\n● BSI scientists ke source note ke mutabik ~11 m tall, orange-pulp banana species Musa indandamanesis\nLittle Andaman Islands ke Krishna-Nalah forest mein discover hui. [Q177]\n20. Species, Fungi & Mushrooms\n● Chinese, Americans, Indians aur Black Africans source ke mutabik same human species Homo sapiens\nke members hain. [Q178]\n● Fungi chlorophyll lack karte hain aur separate kingdom mein classified hain. Yeast single-celled fungus\nhai; yeast aur mushrooms Kingdom Fungi ke members hain. [Q179, Q180, Q181]\n● Mushroom fungus ka fleshy spore-bearing fruiting body hai; edible cooking mushrooms bhi fungi hain.\n[Q182, Q183]\n● Gucchi/morels fungus hain aur Himalayan forest regions mein wild grow karte hain; source commercial\ncultivation statement ko incorrect batata hai. [Q184]\n21. Symbiosis — Fig, Mycorrhiza, Lichen & Rhizobium\n● Fig tree species aur specific fig-wasp pollinator ke beech one-to-one coevolved relationship source ka\nclassic coevolution example hai. [Q185]\n● Cnidarians, fungi aur protozoa—teeno symbiotic relationships establish kar sakte hain; source corals–\ndinoflagellates, fungi–plants/algae, aur protozoan mutualisms examples deta hai. [Q186]\n● Mycorrhiza fungi aur higher-plant roots ka beneficial symbiotic association hai: fungus water/nutrient\nabsorption help karta hai, plant carbohydrates provide karta hai. [Q187, Q188]\n● Lichen fungus + alga/cyanobacterium ka symbiotic association hai; interaction mutualism hai. Algal\npartner photosynthesis se organic compounds deta hai, fungal partner moisture/shelter. [Q189, Q190,\nQ191, Q192]\n● Lichens atmospheric pollution ke sensitive bio-indicators hain aur polluted areas mein grow nahi karte.\nLeguminous root nodules ke nitrogen-fixing bacteria (e.g., Rhizobium) source ke mutabik symbiotic hain.\n[Q193, Q194]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0304","t":"04 Cell","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Cell Full Mind Map\n🧬 CELL — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Cell — Basic Structural & Functional Unit\n2. DNA-containing Organelles\n3. Viroids, Prions, Mycoplasma & Rickettsia\n4. Plant Cell vs Animal Cell\n5. Mitochondria — Powerhouse of Cell\n6. Plasma Membrane — Composition\n7. Protein Synthesis — Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum\n8. Apoptosis — Programmed Cell Death\n9. Krebs Cycle & ATP\n1. Cell — Basic Structural & Functional Unit\n● Cell (कोशिका) life ki structural aur functional unit hai. Simple bacteria se complex animals tak living\norganisms cells se bane hote hain; cells structure aur respiration, nutrient uptake aur waste removal\njaise life processes carry out karte hain. [Q1]\n2. DNA-containing Organelles\n● Nucleus ke alawa source ke mutabik DNA mitochondria aur chloroplast mein bhi milta hai. MCQ Q2\nmein given options ke among correct organelle mitochondrion hai. [Q2]\n3. Viroids, Prions, Mycoplasma & Rickettsia\n● Viroids short circular single-stranded RNA se bane infectious pathogens hain aur protein coat nahi hota;\nsource mostly plant pathogens batata hai. [Q3]\n● Prions proteinaceous infectious particles hain, cells nahi. Mycoplasma cell wall lack karta hai, jabki\nsource Rickettsia mein cell wall present batata hai. [Q3]\n4. Plant Cell vs Animal Cell\n● Plant cells mein cellulose cell wall hoti hai, animal cells mein cell wall absent hoti hai. Dono plant aur\nanimal cells mein plasma membrane hoti hai. [Q4, Q5, Q6]\n● Mature plant cell mein generally ek large central vacuole hoti hai, jabki animal cell mein several small\nvacuoles ho sakti hain. [Q4]\n● Green plant cells mein chloroplasts/green plastids bhi milte hain, jo animal cells mein nahi hote. Plant–\nanimal cell ka main source distinction cell wall ke basis par diya gaya hai. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Plant vs Animal Cell\n ▸Plant cell mein cell wall + plasma membrane dono hote hain; “plant cell has no plasma membrane” statement\nsource mein incorrect hai. [Q4]\n ▸Animal cell mein cellulose cell wall nahi hoti. [Q5, Q6]\n5. Mitochondria — Powerhouse of Cell\n● Mitochondrion membrane-bound organelle hai aur respiration ke through ATP generate karta hai; isi liye\n“powerhouse of the cell” kaha jata hai. [Q7, Q8, Q9]\n6. Plasma Membrane — Composition\n● Plasma membrane/cell membrane cell ke interior ko outside environment se separate karti hai. Source\nke mutabik ye mainly lipid (phospholipid) bilayer aur embedded proteins se bani hoti hai. [Q10]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Cell Full Mind Map\n7. Protein Synthesis — Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum\n● Rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER) ki outer membrane par ribosomes present hote hain; source Q11\nmein RER ko protein synthesis mein most significant role wala organelle answer karta hai. [Q11]\n8. Apoptosis — Programmed Cell Death\n● Apoptosis programmed cell death (PCD) ka process hai. Source ise multicellular organisms aur kuch\neukaryotic single-celled microorganisms (jaise yeast) mein describe karta hai; old, unnecessary aur\nunhealthy cells eliminate karne mein role batata hai. [Q12]\n9. Krebs Cycle & ATP\n● Krebs cycle enzyme-catalyzed reactions ka cycle hai jo aerobic metabolism se related hai; eukaryotic\ncell mein mitochondrial matrix mein occur karta hai aur source Hans Krebs (1937) se associate karta\nhai. [Q13]\n● Source Q13 ke answer/explanation ke mutabik Krebs cycle system mein maximum number of ATP\nmolecules generate karne wala term diya gaya hai. [Q13]\n⚠️ SOURCE-SPECIFIC NOTE — Q13\n ▸Q13 ka ATP-related statement yahan source HTML ki wording/explanation ke according preserve kiya gaya\nhai; is mind map mein outside correction/verification add nahi ki gayi. [Q13]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0305","t":"05 Heredity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heredity Full Mind Map\n🧬 HEREDITY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Mendel — Father of Genetics & Laws of Inheritance\n2. Genome / Gene Mapping\n3. Gene — Basic Unit of Heredity\n4. Genetic Code — Codons & Main Features\n5. Mutation — Change in Gene Base Sequence\n6. Nucleus, Chromosomes & Hereditary Information\n7. DNA Complementary Base Pairing\n8. Sexual Reproduction & Genetic Variation\n9. Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance\n10. DNA Discovery vs Double-Helix Structure\n11. Har Gobind Khorana — Genetic Code & Artificial Gene\n12. Jumping Genes — Barbara McClintock\n13. DNA Components, Sugar & Ribozymes\n14. Chromosome Number — Species Specificity\n15. Sex Chromosomes & Human Karyotype\n16. DNA Mutation Risk — Ionizing Radiation\n1. Mendel — Father of Genetics & Laws of Inheritance\n● Gregor Johann Mendel ko source “father of genetics / modern genetics” batata hai; laws of inheritance\nunhi se associated hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Mendel ne hybridization experiments garden pea par kiye aur pea ke seven types of qualities study\nkarke Law of Dominance, Law of Segregation aur Law of Independent Assortment diye. [Q4]\n● Mendel ka principle of inheritance sexual reproduction par based hai. [Q5]\n2. Genome / Gene Mapping\n● Gene mapping chromosome par gene ki location aur genes ke beech relative distance determine karne\nki method hai. Genome mapping molecular markers ko genome par unki respective positions par place\nkarta hai. [Q6]\n3. Gene — Basic Unit of Heredity\n● Gene heredity ki basic physical aur functional unit hai; genes DNA se bane genetic material ke functional\nunits hain. [Q7]\n● Source ke mutabik chromosome ke long coiled DNA molecule ke small parts ko gene kaha jata hai. [Q8]\n4. Genetic Code — Codons & Main Features\n● Genetic code genetic material ki information ko proteins mein translate karne ke rules ka set hai.\nDNA/mRNA nucleotides ko three-letter codons ke form mein read kiya jata hai; 64 codons 20 amino\nacids se correspond karte hain. [Q9]\n● Source genetic code ko universal, triplet, commaless, non-overlapping, non-ambiguous aur redundant\nbatata hai. AUG start codon hai; UAA, UAG aur UGA stop codons hain. [Q9]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heredity Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Genetic Code Signals\n ▸AUG = start codon; UAA, UAG, UGA = stop codons. Source Q9 mein all listed characteristics correct answer\ndiye gaye hain. [Q9]\n5. Mutation — Change in Gene Base Sequence\n● Gene ke base sequence mein change ko mutation kaha jata hai. Source mutation ko gene structure ka\nheritable variant-producing change aur genetic variation ka ultimate source batata hai. [Q10]\n6. Nucleus, Chromosomes & Hereditary Information\n● Nucleus eukaryotic cell ka control centre aur genetic information repository hai; DNA ko house/replicate\nkarke cell reproduction mein important role play karta hai. Isliye “nucleus does not play a role in cellular\nreproduction” statement source mein incorrect hai. [Q11]\n● Hereditary characters descendants tak chromosomes ke through transfer hote hain. Source\nchromosomes ko nucleoprotein-made structures batata hai; “chromosome” term Waldeyer se associate\nkarta hai aur genes chromosomes par located hote hain. [Q12]\n● DNA living cells ke hereditary characters control/store/transfer karne wala predominant hereditary\nmaterial hai; source RNA ko messenger aur kuch viruses mein hereditary material batata hai. [Q13]\n7. DNA Complementary Base Pairing\n● DNA mein specific base pairing A–T aur G–C hoti hai; dono strands complementary hote hain. Source isi\ncomplementary base pairing ko genetic information ko generation-to-generation store/transmit karne ke\nliye uniquely suited feature batata hai. [Q14]\n8. Sexual Reproduction & Genetic Variation\n● Sexual reproduction mein two parent cells contribute karte hain; source genetic variation ko blending of\ngenes, chromosomal changes aur gene shuffling se associate karta hai. [Q15]\n9. Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance\n● Chromosomal theory of inheritance Walter Sutton (1902–03) aur Theodor Boveri ke independent work\nse associated hai. Source ke mutabik ye Mendelian inheritance ke mechanism ko chromosomes ke\nthrough explain karta hai. [Q16]\n10. DNA Discovery vs Double-Helix Structure\n● James D. Watson aur Francis Crick DNA ke double-helix structure/model (1953) se associated hain;\nsource Maurice Wilkins ke saath 1962 Nobel Prize ka bhi zikr karta hai. [Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22]\n● DNA molecule ki first discovery source Friedrich Miescher (1869) se associate karta hai; unhone ise\n“nuclein” kaha. [Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — “Who discovered DNA?”\n ▸Watson + Crick = DNA double-helix structure/model; source Q23 ke mutabik DNA molecule first discovered\nby Friedrich Miescher (1869). [Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21, Q22, Q23]\n ▸Q23 ke options mein Miescher nahi tha, isliye source “None of the above” ko technically correct answer\nmaanta hai. [Q23]\n11. Har Gobind Khorana — Genetic Code & Artificial Gene\n● Har Gobind Khorana, Robert W. Holley aur Marshall W. Nirenberg ko 1968 Nobel Prize genetic code\ninterpretation aur protein synthesis mein DNA function ke work ke liye source mention karta hai. [Q24]\n● Source Khorana ko laboratory mein artificial gene / short DNA sequence synthesize karne wala scientist\nbatata hai. [Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heredity Full Mind Map\n12. Jumping Genes — Barbara McClintock\n● Barbara McClintock “jumping genes” / transposons ke principle se associated hain. Source unke maize\nheredity work aur 1983 Nobel Prize ka mention karta hai. [Q26]\n13. DNA Components, Sugar & Ribozymes\n● Source Q27 mein adenine, guanine, cytosine aur thymine ko DNA nucleobases batata hai; tyrosine\namino acid hai aur DNA ka structural base nahi. [Q27]\n● DNA mein deoxyribose sugar hoti hai; source ribose ko RNA ki sugar batata hai. [Q28]\n● Ribozymes catalytic RNA molecules hain jo chemical reactions catalyze kar sakte hain; source ribosome\nmein amino acids ko protein chain mein join karne se bhi relate karta hai. [Q29]\n14. Chromosome Number — Species Specificity\n● Chromosome number species-to-species vary karta hai, lekin particular species ke liye constant rehta\nhai; source ke mutabik age ya weight ke saath normally change nahi hota. [Q30]\n15. Sex Chromosomes & Human Karyotype\n● Source many lizard species mein morphologically recognizable sex chromosomes absent hone aur\nenvironmental factors (jaise incubation temperature) se sex determination ka mention karta hai. [Q31]\n● Human cells mein total 46 chromosomes = 23 pairs hote hain; 22 pairs autosomes aur 23rd pair sex\nchromosomes hota hai. [Q32, Q33]\n● Females XX aur males XY hote hain. Source ke explanation ke mutabik human offspring ka sex male\nparent ke X- or Y-bearing sperm se determine hota hai: XX female, XY male. [Q34, Q35, Q36]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Human Sex Determination\n ▸Female = XX; Male = XY. Source Q34 mein Assertion “female plays major role” false aur Reason “women\nhave two X chromosomes” true diya gaya hai. [Q34]\n ▸Male child ke liye XY combination chahiye; Y chromosome male parent contribute karta hai. [Q35, Q36]\n16. DNA Mutation Risk — Ionizing Radiation\n● Ionizing radiation jaise X-rays/gamma rays DNA mutations ya permanent DNA changes cause kar sakte\nhain. Source Q37 mein repeated radiation exposure ki wajah se X-ray technician ko specified\nprofessionals mein higher risk answer karta hai. [Q37]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0306","t":"06 Biofertilizers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biofertilizers Full Mind Map\n🌱 BIOFERTILIZERS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Biofertilizers — Meaning & Main Examples\n2. Nitrogen-Fixing Organisms — Nostoc, Anabaena & Azotobacter\n3. Blue-Green Algae / Cyanobacteria — Paddy Biofertilizer\n4. Azolla — Aquatic Fern, Anabaena Association & Uses\n5. Crop–Biofertilizer Matching\n6. VAM / Mycorrhiza — Phosphatic Biofertilizer\n7. Biochar — Farming Uses\n8. Compost, Earthworms & Vermicompost\n9. Nitrogen Use Efficiency in Crop Production\n10. Legumes, Rhizobium & Nitrogen-Fixing Plants\n11. Leg-haemoglobin in Root Nodules\n1. Biofertilizers — Meaning & Main Examples\n● Source biofertilizers ko living/latent cells of efficient microorganisms wali preparations batata hai jo crop\nplants ko nutrients uptake karne mein help karti hain. Azolla aur blue-green algae biofertilizers ke\nexamples hain. [Q1]\n● Rhizobium, blue-green algae (cyanobacteria) aur Azolla — teeno source ke mutabik biofertilizers hain\naur soil nitrogen fixation se fertility improve karte hain. [Q3]\n● Azolla biofertilizer hai; source Q6 mein Urea ko synthetic chemical fertilizer, 2,4-D ko herbicide aur\nStreptocycline ko agricultural antibiotic batata hai. [Q5, Q6]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q2 — Source Marks It Disputed\n ▸Q2 mein source Azolla (1) + Blue-green algae (2) ko biofertilizers maanta hai; Alfalfa ko plant aur Nitrolin\n(calcium cyanamide) ko chemical fertilizer batata hai. “1 and 2 only” option na hone ki wajah se source\nquestion ko disputed/invalid mark karta hai. [Q2]\n2. Nitrogen-Fixing Organisms — Nostoc, Anabaena & Azotobacter\n● Nostoc, Anabaena aur Azotobacter nitrogen-fixing organisms hain. Mycorrhiza nitrogen-fixing organism\nnahi; source ise fungus–plant root symbiotic association batata hai jo mainly phosphorus aur water\nuptake mein help karta hai. [Q4]\n● Blue-green algae ko Cyanobacteria bhi kaha jata hai aur source ise biological nitrogen fixation se\nassociated batata hai. [Q9]\n● Azotobacter free-living nitrogen-fixing bacterium aur biofertilizer hai — bioinsecticide nahi. Q8 mein isi\nwajah se “Azotobacter – Bioinsecticide” incorrect match hai. [Q8]\n3. Blue-Green Algae / Cyanobacteria — Paddy Biofertilizer\n● Cyanobacteria / blue-green algae atmospheric nitrogen fix karte hain aur water-logged paddy (rice) fields\nmein chiefly biofertilizer ke roop mein use hote hain. [Q10, Q11]\n● Source Q14 mein Cyanobacteria ko microorganisms used as biofertilizers ka correct option batata hai,\nespecially rice cultivation mein nitrogen-fixing capability ki wajah se. [Q14]\n4. Azolla — Aquatic Fern, Anabaena Association & Uses\n● Azolla ek small, free-floating aquatic fern hai. Source ise paddy cultivation mein widely used nitrogen-\nrich biofertilizer batata hai. [Q5, Q16, Q17, Q18]\n● Azolla ka nitrogen-fixing benefit symbiotic blue-green alga / cyanobacterium Anabaena azollae se\nassociated hai; source Azolla + blue-green algae association ko good biofertilizer batata hai. [Q13, Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biofertilizers Full Mind Map\n● Source Azolla ko livestock ke liye supplementary food, especially milking bovines ke liye, high-protein\nfeed ke roop mein bhi describe karta hai. [Q7]\n5. Crop–Biofertilizer Matching\n● Source ke correct crop pairs: Blue-green algae → Paddy; Rhizobium leguminosarum → Pea;\nAzotobacter → Wheat. Azolla → Maize incorrect pair hai, kyunki source Azolla ko mainly paddy se\nassociate karta hai. [Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Paddy Associations\n ▸Blue-green algae / Cyanobacteria → Paddy; Azolla → Paddy. Source Q12 mein Azolla–Maize ko incorrect\nmatch batata hai. [Q10, Q11, Q12, Q18]\n6. VAM / Mycorrhiza — Phosphatic Biofertilizer\n● Vascular Arbuscular Mycorrhiza (VAM) phosphorus uptake improve karta hai, isliye source ise\nphosphatic biofertilizer batata hai. VAM fungi water aur poorly mobile ions, especially phosphorus, ki\nuptake mein host plant ko benefit dete hain. [Q19]\n7. Biochar — Farming Uses\n● Biochar source ke mutabik stable, carbon-rich charcoal hai jo high-temperature, low-oxygen pyrolysis se\nbanta hai. Ye vertical farming ke growing medium ka part ho sakta hai, nitrogen-fixing microorganisms\nko promote kar sakta hai aur water/water-soluble nutrients ko longer retain karne mein help karta hai.\n[Q20]\n8. Compost, Earthworms & Vermicompost\n● Compost mein biodegradable farm waste pits mein decompose hota hai aur organic matter/nutrients se\nrich hota hai. Source ke mutabik earthworms aur microbes decomposition ko slow nahi, accelerate karte\nhain. [Q21]\n● Earthworms ko source “Ploughers of the soil” / farmer’s friends batata hai: burrowing se soil aeration aur\nair-water movement improve hota hai, aur organic matter ko nutrient-rich vermicompost mein break\ndown karne mein help karte hain. [Q28]\n9. Nitrogen Use Efficiency in Crop Production\n● Source ke mutabik nitrogen-use efficiency split applications, nitrogen inhibitors aur slow-release nitrogen\nfertilizers — teeno se improve ki ja sakti hai. [Q22]\n10. Legumes, Rhizobium & Nitrogen-Fixing Plants\n● Nitrogen-fixing bacteria jaise Rhizobium legumes/pulses ki roots mein symbiotically root nodules\nbanakar rehte hain. [Q23]\n● Source ke listed nitrogen-fixing plants mein Alfalfa, Chickpea aur Clover hain; Amaranth, Purslane\n(Kulfa) aur Spinach ko nitrogen-fixing plants nahi bataya gaya. [Q24]\n● Gram, pea aur bean jaise legume crops nitrogen fixation mein helpful hain; source paddy plant ko itself\nnitrogen-fixing nahi maanta. [Q25]\n● Soyabean mein nitrogen fixation ke liye source Rhizobium japonicum (Bradyrhizobium japonicum) ko\nresponsible batata hai. [Q26]\n11. Leg-haemoglobin in Root Nodules\n● Leg-haemoglobin leguminous plants ke nitrogen-fixing root nodules mein milta hai. Source ise oxygen-\ncarrying phytoglobin batata hai jo nodule bacteria ko sufficient oxygen regulate/supply karta hai while\noxygen-sensitive nitrogenase ko protect karne mein help karta hai. [Q27]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0307","t":"07.i Skeletal and Muscle System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Skeletal & Muscle System Full Mind Map\n🦴 SKELETAL & MUSCLE SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.i · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Body Water & Major Chemical Elements\n2. Bone Composition & Number of Bones\n3. Smallest Bone, Skull, Vertebrae & Ribs\n4. Joints, Cartilage & Ligaments\n5. Long Bones, Osteoclasts & Arthroplasty\n6. Teeth, Dental Plaque & Tooth Enamel\n7. Nails, Skin, Hair & Keratin\n8. Minerals Required for Bones & Teeth\n9. Muscle Working & Important Muscles\n10. Important Bone Names — Match the Following\n1. Body Water & Major Chemical Elements\n● Source ke mutabik human body ka major hissa water se bana hota hai: general range 55–70%; average\nadult around 55–65%, aur exam questions mein “about 70%” / around 65% bhi diya gaya hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Human body ka most abundant element Oxygen hai (source around 65% batata hai), mainly body water\nki wajah se. [Q4, Q7]\n● Approximate body-mass composition source mein Oxygen 65%, Carbon 18.5%, Hydrogen 9.5%,\nNitrogen 3.2%, Calcium 1.5% aur Phosphorus 1.0% diya hai. Q5 ke given options mein maximum\nCalcium hai. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Overall Most Abundant vs “Given Options”\n ▸Overall human body ka most abundant element Oxygen hai; lekin Q5 ke options (Iron, Sodium, Phosphorus,\nCalcium) mein Calcium highest hai. [Q4, Q5, Q7]\n2. Bone Composition & Number of Bones\n● Human bones ka major mineral component calcium phosphate / hydroxyapatite hai; source ke mutabik\nbone ka about 70% weight modified hydroxyapatite ho sakta hai. [Q6]\n● Adult human skeleton mein 206 bones hoti hain. Birth par source about 300 bones batata hai, jo fusion\nke baad adulthood tak 206 ho jati hain. [Q8, Q9]\n● 20 years ki age par source exact adult count 206 batata hai; Q10 ke numerical options 100, 200, 300\nmein se koi correct nahi, isliye “None of these” answer banta hai. [Q10]\n3. Smallest Bone, Skull, Vertebrae & Ribs\n● Human body ki smallest bone Stapes hai, jo middle ear mein hoti hai. Source saath hi Femur ko largest\nbone batata hai. [Q11, Q12]\n● Source skull count ko 28 bones batata hai: 8 neurocranium + 14 facial bones + 6 middle-ear bones\n(hyoid excluded). [Q13]\n● Human cervical spine mein 7 cervical vertebrae (C1–C7) hoti hain; C1 Atlas aur C2 Axis hain. [Q14]\n● Human rib cage mein 12 pairs = total 24 ribs hoti hain; ribs sternum ke saath thoracic organs jaise heart\naur lungs ko protection deti hain. [Q17]\n4. Joints, Cartilage & Ligaments\n● Atlas–Axis (atlantoaxial) joint ko source synovial pivot joint batata hai, jo head rotation allow karta hai.\n[Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Skeletal & Muscle System Full Mind Map\n● Q16 mein source neck–head junction ko pivotal / rotary joint ke roop mein frame karta hai, jahan\nrotational movement hoti hai. [Q16]\n● Cartilage bone se softer aur more flexible connective tissue hai; outer ear aur nose-tip examples diye\ngaye hain. [Q21]\n● Ligament dense fibrous connective tissue hai jo two bones ko connect karke joint banane mein help\nkarta hai. [Q22]\n5. Long Bones, Osteoclasts & Arthroplasty\n● Leg jaise long bone ki diaphysis source ke mutabik hollow-cylinder jaisi hoti hai; inner cavity mein yellow\nbone marrow hota hai, jabki epiphysis mein sponge-like structure aur red marrow hota hai. [Q18]\n● Osteoclast bone tissue ko break down / resorb karne wali bone cell hai aur bone remodeling,\nmaintenance aur pathological bone loss se associated hai. [Q19]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q19 — Original Answer-Key Treatment\n ▸Source explanation ke mutabik Osteoclast ka primary role bone resorption hai, lekin original answer key mein\noptions (a) Bone formation aur (c) Bone fracture/resorption — dono considered bataye gaye hain. Is note ko\nsource ke hisab se preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q19]\n● Arthroplasty source mein hip-joint replacement surgery ke roop mein diya gaya hai, jahan damaged hip\ncomponents ko synthetic implant se replace kiya jata hai. [Q20]\n6. Teeth, Dental Plaque & Tooth Enamel\n● Dental plaque ek bacterial biofilm / mass hai. Source ke question ke according plaques food particles +\nsaliva + mouth acids + bacteria se bane hote hain; saliva ka average pH 6.7 diya hai. [Q23]\n● Human lifetime mein 20 teeth twice develop hote hain. Source mammals ko diphyodont batata hai aur 12\npermanent molars ko monophyodont; four tooth types: incisors, canines, premolars, molars. [Q30]\n● Tooth enamel source ke mutabik body ka strongest part hai. Ye tooth crown ka hard outer covering hai\naur mainly hydroxyapatite (calcium phosphate) crystals se bana hota hai. [Q31]\n7. Nails, Skin, Hair & Keratin\n● Nails dead tissue / α-keratin ki multiple layers se bane hote hain; nails ke cuttable part mein nerves aur\nblood vessels nahi hote, isliye cutting par pain feel nahi hota. [Q24]\n● Alpha-keratin fibrous structural protein hai jo human skin ki outer epidermal layer ka important material\nhai; hair aur nails ka bhi major component hai. [Q25]\n● Hair keratin protein se bana hota hai; source hair + nails dono mein keratin ko common structural protein\nbatata hai. [Q26, Q27]\n8. Minerals Required for Bones & Teeth\n● Bones aur teeth ke formation ke liye source Calcium + Phosphorus ko required pair batata hai. [Q28]\n● Calcium, phosphorus aur fluorine bones/teeth formation aur strengthening se linked hain; Q29 mein\nIodine ko “not essential” answer diya gaya hai, aur iodine ko thyroid function se associate kiya hai. [Q29]\n9. Muscle Working & Important Muscles\n● Muscles movement ke liye contract/relax karti hain aur source ke mutabik bones ko pull karti hain, push\nnahi. Muscles pairs mein work karti hain aur contraction par shorter, stiffer aur thicker hoti hain. [Q32]\n● Human body ki smallest muscle Stapedius hai, middle ear / tympanic cavity mein. Ye stapes vibration ko\nstabilize aur regulate karti hai. [Q33]\n● Source weight-based strongest muscle Masseter (jaw muscle) batata hai; isliye strongest muscle jaws\nmein found answer diya hai. [Q34]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Skeletal & Muscle System Full Mind Map\n10. Important Bone Names — Match the Following\n● Correct matching: Breastbone → Sternum | Collarbone → Clavicle | Knee-cap → Patella | Shoulder\nBlade → Scapula. [Q35]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0308","t":"07.ii Digestive System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Digestive System Full Mind Map\n🍽️ DIGESTIVE SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.ii · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Digestive Process & Taste Sensation\n2. Buccal Cavity, Saliva & Starch Digestion\n3. Stomach — HCl & Gastric Digestion\n4. Enzymes — Nature, Function & Examples\n5. Liver — Functions, Bile & Fat Digestion\n6. Lipids, Lipase & Digestive Enzymes\n7. Small Intestine, Appendix & Structural Order\n8. Protein Digestion — Pepsin & Trypsin\n9. Cellulose, Diastase & Carbohydrate End Products\n10. Enzyme / Hormone Match-the-Following\n11. Glycogen Storage, Fasting & Gallbladder\n12. Pancreas & Intestinal Hormones\n1. Digestive Process & Taste Sensation\n● Human body mein digestion mouth se start hota hai aur source ke mutabik digestive process ka major\nhissa / completion small intestine mein hota hai. Small intestine pancreatic enzymes aur liver bile ki help\nse food breakdown continue karti hai. [Q1]\n● Source five basic tongue tastes ko Sweet, Bitter, Salty, Umami aur Sour batata hai. “Spicy” aur\n“Pungent” ko actual taste nahi maana gaya; spicy sensation capsaicin se pain/heat signal ke roop mein\nexplain ki gayi hai. [Q2]\n● Source ke mutabik tongue ke sab parts tastes sense kar sakte hain, lekin posterior/back part bitterness\nke liye especially sensitive hai. [Q3]\n2. Buccal Cavity, Saliva & Starch Digestion\n● Buccal cavity mein carbohydrate digestion start hota hai. Salivary amylase starch ko maltose/dextrin\nmein todna shuru karta hai. [Q4]\n● Saliva dietary starch digestion mein help karti hai; source saliva ko about 99.5% water aur remaining\nfraction mein electrolytes, mucus, glycoproteins, enzymes (amylase) aur antibacterial compounds batata\nhai. [Q5, Q6]\n● Amylase starch hydrolysis se glucose formation se associated enzyme diya gaya hai; human saliva mein\npresent rehkar carbohydrate digestion start karta hai. [Q7]\n3. Stomach — HCl & Gastric Digestion\n● Hydrochloric acid (HCl) stomach ki gastric glands ke parietal/oxyntic cells se secret hota hai. Gastric\njuice mein mucus, HCl aur pepsin jaise enzymes hote hain; source HCl ko bacteria kill karne aur\npepsinogen activation se link karta hai. [Q9, Q10]\n4. Enzymes — Nature, Function & Examples\n● Enzymes biological catalysts / biocatalysts hain jo living systems ki chemical reactions ko accelerate\nkarte hain. Source repeated questions mein enzymes ko basically protein / proteinaceous substances\nbatata hai. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15]\n● Source statement-based question mein enzymes ko biocatalysts batata hai aur generally ye bhi kehta\nhai ki enzymes apna action us site par perform karte hain jahan produce hote hain. [Q16]\n● Zymase yeast mein sugar/glucose fermentation ko ethanol + carbon dioxide mein catalyse karta hai.\n[Q17]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Digestive System Full Mind Map\n5. Liver — Functions, Bile & Fat Digestion\n● Liver fat digestion mein important hai, lekin source explicitly kehta hai ki liver fat-digesting enzymes\nproduce nahi karta. Bile mein digestive enzymes nahi hote, phir bhi bile fats ki emulsification karke\ndigestion ko facilitate karti hai. [Q8]\n● Liver ki functions mein bile production, fat storage aur harmful ammonia ko urea mein convert karna\ninclude hai; Q18 mein liver function ke roop mein Urea production selected hai. [Q18]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Liver Helps Fat Digestion, But Bile Has No Digestive Enzyme\n ▸Assertion “liver has an important role in fat digestion” true hai; reason “liver produces two important fat-\ndigesting enzymes” source ke according false hai. Role bile-mediated emulsification se explain kiya gaya hai.\n[Q8]\n6. Lipids, Lipase & Digestive Enzymes\n● Lipid digestion source ke mutabik bile acids + lipase ki presence mein hota hai; pepsin protein-digesting\nenzyme hai. Lipase fats/lipids ko fatty acids aur monoglycerides mein break karta hai. [Q19]\n● Q20 ke given options mein lipase ka source Pancreas selected hai. Source explanation saath hi lipase\nproduction ko pancreas, mouth aur stomach se associate karti hai. [Q20]\n● Trypsin, Ptyalin aur Pepsin digestive enzymes hain, jabki Gastrin digestive enzyme nahi balki peptide\nhormone hai jo gastric acid secretion aur gastric motility ko stimulate karta hai. [Q21]\n7. Small Intestine, Appendix & Structural Order\n● Appendix blind-ended tube hai jo caecum se connected hota hai; source isse large intestine ke\nbeginning region se associate karta hai. Ye same question source mein do baar diya gaya hai. [Q22, Q27]\n● Small intestine ke three parts ka decreasing length order source mein Ileum → Jejunum → Duodenum\ndiya hai. Approx. lengths: Ileum ~3.5 m, Jejunum ~2.5 m, Duodenum ~20–25 cm. Ye question bhi\nsource mein repeat hua hai. [Q23, Q28]\n8. Protein Digestion — Pepsin & Trypsin\n● “All proteins are digested only in small intestine” source ke according false hai, kyunki protein digestion\nstomach mein pepsin se start hota hai. Pancreatic protein-digesting enzyme trypsin inactive form mein\nproduce hokar small intestine mein activate hota hai. [Q24]\n● Trypsin protein digestion mein help karta hai aur small intestine mein protein breakdown continue karta\nhai. [Q25]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q26 — Source Answer vs Explanation\n ▸Source answer key Q26 mein “Proteins → amino acids” option (C) mark karti hai. Lekin source explanation\nkehta hai ki trypsin peptide bonds hydrolyse karke proteins ko smaller peptides mein todta hai, aur other\nproteases further amino acids banate hain. Dono source statements ko yahin preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q26]\n9. Cellulose, Diastase & Carbohydrate End Products\n● Human digestive system mein cellulose-digesting enzyme source ke mutabik absent hai. Diastase starch\nko maltose mein degrade karta hai; isliye Q29 mein Assertion aur Reason dono true hain, lekin Reason\nAssertion ka explanation nahi hai. [Q29]\n● Carbohydrates ka ultimate digestion product source mein Glucose selected hai; complex\ncarbohydrates/disaccharides ko absorbable monosaccharides mein break kiya jata hai. [Q33]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Digestive System Full Mind Map\n10. Enzyme / Hormone Match-the-Following\n● Correct enzyme-function pair source mein E. coli restriction endonuclease-II → DNA ko specific places\npar cut karta hai. [Q30]\n● Match: Ptyalin → digests starch; Pepsin → digests proteins; Renin → blood angiotensinogen ko\nangiotensin mein convert karta hai; Oxytocin → smooth-muscle contraction induce karta hai. [Q31]\n● Match: Vitamin → Carotene | Enzyme → Pepsin | Hormone → Testosterone/Progesterone | Protein →\nKeratin. [Q32]\n11. Glycogen Storage, Fasting & Gallbladder\n● Extra glucose glycogen mein convert hokar source ke Q34 mein liver mein store hota hai. Energy-\nstorage form Glycogen hai aur source liver + muscle cells dono ko storage sites batata hai. [Q34, Q35]\n● More than 10 days fasting ke case mein source liver glucose level diminished batata hai. Explanation\nglycogen depletion, fats se glucose production aur later ketone-body production describe karti hai. [Q36]\n● Gallstones bile duct block karke bile ko duodenum tak pahunchne se rok sakte hain; source ke mutabik\nisse primarily fat digestion affect hota hai. [Q37]\n● Liver human body ka largest gland hai. Bile liver mein produce hoti hai, gallbladder mein\nstored/concentrated hoti hai, aur alimentary canal mein small intestine—specifically duodenum—receive\nkarta hai. [Q38, Q39, Q40, Q41, Q42]\n12. Pancreas & Intestinal Hormones\n● Source pancreas ko human body ki second largest gland batata hai. Pancreatic secretion alkaline hai\naur source ise “complete digestive juice” ke roop mein describe karta hai. [Q43]\n● Secretin duodenum ki S-cells se acidity/HCl ke response mein release hota hai. Enterogastrone small-\nintestinal/duodenal mucosa se fatty acids ke response mein secret hota hai; Q44 mein dono statements\ncorrect selected hain. [Q44]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0309","t":"07.iii Vitamins and Nutrition","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vitamins & Nutrition Full Mind Map\n🥗 VITAMINS & NUTRITION — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.iii · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Nutrition Basics, Probiotics & Nutraceuticals\n2. Vitamins — Concept, Solubility & Storage\n3. Minerals, Potassium & Antioxidants\n4. Vitamin C — Sources, Functions & Storage\n5. Vitamin K — Blood Clotting\n6. Vitamin D — Sunlight, Forms & Deficiency\n7. Vitamin A — Vision, Sources & Storage\n8. B-Complex Vitamins & Vitamin B12\n9. Vitamin Sources, Names & Deficiency Diseases\n10. Proteins, Carbohydrates & Energy\n11. Iron, Milk & Dairy Nutrition\n12. Protein Nutrition, Micronutrients & Breast Milk\n13. Starch, Malnutrition, Fatty Acids & Amino Acids\n14. Fats, Oils, Cholesterol & Triglycerides\n1. Nutrition Basics, Probiotics & Nutraceuticals\n● New tissue growth aur repair ke liye proteins important hain; source cheese ko given options mein\nprotein-rich choice batata hai. Pulses, soybean, groundnut, milk, cheese, eggs aur foodgrains bhi\nprotein sources diye gaye hain. [Q1]\n● Probiotics live beneficial microorganisms hain—bacteria aur yeasts—jo gut flora maintain karne,\nimmunity support karne aur milk sugar/lactose digestion mein help kar sakte hain. Source ke mutabik\nprobiotics naturally gut mein bhi present hote hain. [Q2, Q3]\n● Nutraceuticals aise food/food-supplement products hain jo simple nutrition ke beyond medicinal/health\nbenefit dete hain. Casimir Funk ko vitamin concept / “vital amines” se credit diya gaya hai; “accessory\ndietary factors” later vitamins ke naam se jane gaye. [Q4, Q5, Q8]\n● Source discovery pair note: McCollum & Marguerite Davis → Vitamin A; James Lind → Vitamin\nC/scurvy; Paul Müller Vitamin D se associated nahi, DDT insecticidal use se associated hai. [Q6]\n● Vitamins organic compounds / vital nutrients hain jo small quantities mein required hote hain aur\ngenerally body sufficient amount mein synthesize nahi kar pati. Proper growth ke liye essential hain. [Q7,\nQ9, Q10]\n2. Vitamins — Concept, Solubility & Storage\n● Fat-soluble vitamins = A, D, E, K. Water-soluble vitamins = B-complex + C. Source ke multiple questions\nisi classification ko repeat karte hain. [Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18]\n● Liver fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E, K ke saath Vitamin B12 ko bhi store karta hai. [Q11]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Water-Soluble Does Not Always Mean “Not Stored”\n ▸Source Vitamin C ko body mein store na hone wala batata hai, lekin Vitamin B12 water-soluble hote hue bhi\nliver mein 3–5 years tak stored reh sakta hai. [Q34, Q63]\n3. Minerals, Potassium & Antioxidants\n● Micro-minerals / trace elements very small quantities mein required hote hain; source examples mein\niron, copper, zinc etc. deta hai. Macronutrient elements mein potassium, sodium, magnesium, calcium,\nsulphur, phosphorus aur chlorine jaise elements include hain. [Q19, Q20]\n● Source apple ko potassium-rich batata hai aur heart rhythm / muscle action se potassium ko associate\nkarta hai. [Q21]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vitamins & Nutrition Full Mind Map\n● Antioxidants free radicals ke harmful effects se cells ko protect karte hain; oxidation/free-radical damage\nko limit karke health maintenance mein role play karte hain. [Q22, Q23]\n4. Vitamin C — Sources, Functions & Storage\n● Vitamin C = Ascorbic acid. Citrus fruits, raw fruits, lemon, orange, amla, papaya etc. major sources hain.\nSource questions mein chilli given vegetables mein maximum, aur context/options ke hisab se\namla/orange ko richest/best source select kiya gaya hai. [Q24, Q25, Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● Vitamin C healthy skin / normal growth, wound healing aur iron absorption mein helpful hai. Water-\nsoluble hone ke karan source ke mutabik body mein store nahi hota. [Q32, Q33, Q34]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — “Richest Vitamin C Source” Depends on Given Options\n ▸Source kuch questions mein Amla ko richest source batata hai, jabki doosre option-based questions mein\nOrange select karta hai; vegetable-only question mein Chilli selected hai. Question ke options/context ko\nfollow karo. [Q24, Q27, Q28, Q29, Q31]\n5. Vitamin K — Blood Clotting\n● Vitamin K blood coagulation/clotting ke liye essential hai; deficiency se slow/impaired coagulation aur\nuncontrolled bleeding ho sakti hai. Isse anti-hemorrhagic factor bhi kaha gaya hai. [Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38,\nQ39, Q40]\n● Vitamin K anticoagulant poison ke antidote ke roop mein use hota hai. Source intestinal bacteria ko\nVitamin K aur Vitamin B12 synthesis se associate karta hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● Vitamin K deficiency sterility ka cause nahi; source sterility ko Vitamin E deficiency se associate karta\nhai. [Q43]\n6. Vitamin D — Sunlight, Forms & Deficiency\n● Vitamin D ka important source sunlight hai; skin sunlight presence mein Vitamin D banati hai. Cod-liver\noil bhi source ke matching questions mein Vitamin D source diya gaya hai. [Q44, Q45, Q46]\n● Vitamin D deficiency children mein rickets aur adults mein osteomalacia se associated hai; prolonged\ndeficiency osteoporosis mein contribute kar sakti hai. [Q47]\n● Vitamin D forms: D2 = Ergocalciferol, D3 = Cholecalciferol. Source Vitamin D ko hormone-like vitamin /\nhormone ke roop mein describe karta hai; active form calcitriol hai. [Q48, Q49, Q50, Q51]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q47 — More Than One Deficiency Outcome\n ▸Source explanation explicitly kehti hai Vitamin D deficiency Rickets (children) aur Osteomalacia (adults) dono\ncause karti hai; is question mein “both A and C” source conclusion hai. [Q47]\n7. Vitamin A — Vision, Sources & Storage\n● Vitamin A normal vision ke liye essential hai; deficiency night blindness / nyctalopia aur severe cases\nmein xerophthalmia/blindness se linked hai. [Q52, Q58, Q59]\n● Vitamin A liver mein stored hota hai. Source-rich food questions carrots, mango/papaya, cod-liver oil etc.\nko Vitamin A sources se associate karte hain. [Q53, Q54, Q55, Q56]\n● Source ke mutabik human body Vitamin A synthesize nahi karti; diet se lena hota hai. [Q57]\n8. B-Complex Vitamins & Vitamin B12\n● Vitamin B12 = Cobalamin / Cyanocobalamin aur isme Cobalt present hota hai. Water-soluble hone ke\nbawajood source B12 ko liver mein approx. 3–5 years stored batata hai. [Q60, Q61, Q62, Q63, Q64]\n● Vitamin B1 = Thiamine; deficiency Beri-beri. Source combined deficiency question mein Beri-beri → B1,\nRickets → D, Scurvy → C mapping preserve karta hai. [Q65, Q66]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vitamins & Nutrition Full Mind Map\n● Source Q67 Vitamin B6/B12/folate intake ko dream quality/recall par possible impact se associate karta\nhai; selected option B6 tha. [Q67]\n9. Vitamin Sources, Names & Deficiency Diseases\n● Source matchings: Vitamin K → Alfalfa; D → Cod-liver oil/sunlight; E → Wheat-germ oil; C →\nLemon/Orange; B2 (Riboflavin) → eggs, green vegetables, milk/dairy etc. Orange mainly Vitamin C\nsource hai. [Q68, Q69, Q70, Q71, Q85]\n● Classic deficiency map: Vitamin A → night blindness/blindness; B1 → Beri-beri; C → Scurvy; D →\nRickets; Folic acid (B9) → Anaemia. Vitamin E is not the cause of night blindness. [Q72, Q73, Q74, Q75,\nQ76, Q77]\n● Riboflavin (B2) deficiency → ariboflavinosis, stomatitis/cheilosis etc. Source mismatch questions also\ndistinguish B1/Thiamine, B2/Riboflavin, E/Tocopherol, B12/Cyanocobalamin and D/Calciferol. [Q78, Q79,\nQ80, Q81, Q82]\n● Vitamin E/Tocopherol source Wheat-germ oil aur role antisterility factor; Vitamin K =\nnaphthoquinone/anti-hemorrhagic factor. Thyroxine vitamin nahi, thyroid hormone hai. [Q83, Q84, Q85, Q86]\n10. Proteins, Carbohydrates & Energy\n● Source banana ko approx. 89 kcal/100 g ke around high-calorie fruit batata hai. Legumes protein-rich\nhain; soybean/groundnut/gram/pulses jaise foods high-protein sources ke roop mein repeat hote hain.\n[Q87, Q88, Q89, Q90, Q91, Q92, Q93]\n● Rice/starchy foods mainly carbohydrate hain. Wheat bread-making quality gluten se linked hai. Tyrosine\nprotein-rich foods mein amino acid hai; source Q95 ke statement set ko option-based way mein evaluate\nkarta hai. [Q94, Q95, Q96]\n● Hard worker ke daily energy requirement ko source ~4000 kcal/day range se associate karta hai; water\nzero calories deta hai. Diet ka essential constituent water hai; long-duration exercise mein major food\nfuel source ke mutabik fats hain. [Q97, Q98, Q99, Q100]\n● Nitrogen proteins ka characteristic element hai, carbohydrates ka essential constituent nahi. Source\nbody acid–alkali balance ko sodium se associate karta hai; Vitamin C ko body mein stored na hone wala\ncompound batata hai. [Q101, Q102, Q103]\n11. Iron, Milk & Dairy Nutrition\n● Source fruit/food questions iron-rich sources mein dates/raisins/green leafy vegetables/spinach type\noptions ko highlight karte hain. Muscle contraction ke liye calcium, iron aur sodium ke statement-based\ncombination ko source answer follow karta hai. [Q104, Q105, Q106, Q107, Q108]\n● Basmati rice grains cooking par elongate hone ko source higher amylose content se associate karta hai.\n[Q109]\n● Milk ki sweetness Lactose se hoti hai; lactose milk sugar/saccharide hai. Lactobacillus lactic-acid\nbacteria milk ko sour/curd banane se associated hain. [Q110, Q111, Q112, Q113]\n● Cow milk ka yellowish tint carotene se linked hai. Buffalo milk fat source ke mutabik approx. 7–7.5%\nrange; cow milk lower fat range mein diya gaya hai. [Q114, Q115, Q116]\n● Milk digestion: rennin young mammals mein milk protein curdling/digestion mein role karta hai; source ke\nmutabik rennin/lactase production childhood mein decline hoti hai. Casein milk ka phosphoprotein hai\naur milk ke white colour se associate kiya gaya hai; milk mein casein/lactalbumin/lactoglobulin jaise\nproteins milte hain. [Q117, Q118, Q119, Q120, Q121]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q117 — Source Gives an Age Range, Not One Sharp Age\n ▸Source explanation: rennin/lactase decline 2–3 years se start ho sakta hai aur most humans mein 6–15 years\nke beech complete disappearance bataya gaya hai. Isko single universal age mat samjho. [Q117]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vitamins & Nutrition Full Mind Map\n12. Protein Nutrition, Micronutrients & Breast Milk\n● Proteins body tissues ke basic structural/building molecules hain; deficiency slow growth se linked hai.\nProteins mein Carbon, Hydrogen, Oxygen aur Nitrogen commonly present hote hain. [Q122, Q123, Q124]\n● Important element matches: Vitamin B12 → Cobalt; Haemoglobin → Iron; Chlorophyll → Magnesium;\nBrass/Chalcopyrite → Copper. Vitamin names: B1 → Thiamine, B2 → Riboflavin, B6 → Pyridoxine, B12\n→ Cobalamin. [Q125, Q126, Q127, Q128]\n● Micronutrients small quantities mein required; source Sulphur ko given choices mein “not micronutrient” /\nmacronutrient category mein places. Papaya mainly Vitamin C rich; source Q131 option-context mein\nmilk ko “not natural source of Vitamin A” marks karta hai. [Q129, Q130, Q131]\n● Protein denaturation heat, X-rays, heavy-metal salts se ho sakti hai; source infrared rays ko non-\ndenaturing option batata hai. Proteins body building/growth-repair ke liye important hain aur animal +\nplant sources dono se milte hain. [Q132, Q133]\n● Source protein requirement older adults mein potentially higher batata hai; moderately active woman\n~45–46 g/day aur lactating mother ~65–70 g/day protein figures deta hai. [Q134, Q135, Q136]\n● Milk B-group vitamins, protein, carbohydrate, calcium, potassium etc. provide karta hai. Mother’s milk\nnewborn ke liye near-complete diet hai but source iron ko lacking nutrient batata hai; colostrum protein +\nantibodies rich hai. Breast-fed babies ko better disease resistance aur lower obesity se associate kiya\ngaya hai. [Q137, Q138, Q139, Q140]\n● Milk source ke mutabik Vitamin C ka poor source hai. [Q141]\n13. Starch, Malnutrition, Fatty Acids & Amino Acids\n● Starch glucose units ka polymeric carbohydrate/polysaccharide hai. Starch iodine solution ke saath blue-\nblack colour deta hai; cellulose does not. Source statement question mein starch/cellulose differences\nko isi framework se test karta hai. [Q142, Q143]\n● Malnutrition undernutrition, overnutrition aur imbalanced nutrition—teeno situations se ho sakta hai.\n[Q144]\n● Essential fatty acids diet ka part hone chahiye kyunki body sab fatty acids synthesize nahi kar sakti.\nLinseed/flaxseed oil alpha-linolenic acid (plant omega-3) ka rich source diya gaya hai. [Q145, Q146, Q147]\n● Vitamins micronutrient amounts mein health ke liye required hain, lekin harmful bacteria ko directly\nvitamins nahi maarte; source white blood cells ko defensive role deta hai. [Q148]\n● Glycine, serine aur tyrosine source mein non-essential amino acids hain; essential amino acids body\nsynthesize nahi kar sakti. Complete proteins all essential amino acids provide karte hain; source eggs\nko best/high biological value source batata hai. [Q149, Q150, Q151]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q150 — No Single Option Correct in Source\n ▸Source explanation ke mutabik given choices mein rice ko chhodkar multiple foods all essential amino acids\nprovide karte hain; isliye source explicitly kehta hai “no single option is correct.” [Q150]\n14. Fats, Oils, Cholesterol & Triglycerides\n● Subcutaneous fat thermal insulation / heat-loss barrier ke roop mein act karta hai. Fats per gram sabse\nzyada energy dete hain (~9.3 kcal/g source), jabki protein aur carbohydrate ~4 kcal/g. [Q152, Q153, Q154]\n● Maximum energy-providing diet group mein carbohydrate + fat + protein included hain;\nvitamins/minerals/water significant calories nahi dete. [Q155]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Vitamins & Nutrition Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q156 — Source Wording: “Living Material”\n ▸Source pehle water ko living beings mein most abundant substance maanta hai, phir “organic compounds /\nliving materials” ke context mein protein ko most abundant body organic material batata hai. Q156 ka source\nanswer isi wording ko follow karta hai. [Q156]\n● Source cooking oil ko vanaspati ghee se better isliye batata hai kyunki unsaturated fats heart-healthier\nchoices hain. Sunflower oil unsaturated fatty acids rich aur heart patients ke liye suitable option diya\ngaya hai. [Q157, Q158, Q159]\n● Unsaturated fats double bonds ke karan saturated fats se more reactive hote hain. Fish ko\npolyunsaturated fatty acids ke karan healthier choice bataya gaya hai. [Q160, Q161]\n● Trans fats HDL (“good cholesterol”) ko lower aur LDL ko raise kar sakte hain; source trans-fat-free claim\nko hydrogenated oils se bachav aur cardiovascular-health context se relate karta hai. [Q162, Q163]\n● Cholesterol lipid/steroid-family ka sterol / fatty alcohol hai; abnormal high level arterial\nblockage/atherosclerosis se linked hai. Triglyceride glycerol + three fatty acids ka ester aur\nbody/vegetable fat ka major constituent hai. [Q164, Q165, Q166, Q167]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0310","t":"07.iv Respiratory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Respiratory System Full Mind Map\n🫁 RESPIRATORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.iv · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Mammalian Respiration & Lungs\n2. Inhaled vs Exhaled Air — Nitrogen, Oxygen, CO & Water Vapour\n₂\n3. Oxygen Transport — Lungs → Blood → Tissues\n4. Alveoli — Site of Gaseous Exchange\n5. Low Blood Oxygen & Breathing Rate\n6. Carbon Monoxide Poisoning & Haemoglobin\n7. ATP — Energy Currency & ATP → ADP\n8. Aerobic Respiration & Glucose Breakdown\n9. Pyruvate — Aerobic / Anaerobic Pathways\n10. Source-Specific Body Temperature Question\n1. Mammalian Respiration & Lungs\n● Mammals mein respiration ka primary organ lungs (फेफड़े) hain. Source ke mutabik two lungs heart ke\ndono sides, backbone ke paas located hote hain; ye atmosphere se oxygen blood mein transfer aur\nblood se carbon dioxide atmosphere mein release karne ke gas-exchange process mein kaam karte\nhain. [Q1]\n2. Inhaled vs Exhaled Air — Nitrogen, Oxygen, CO & Water Vapour\n₂\n● Respiration mein inhaled aur exhaled air compare karne par source ke according nitrogen ki amount\nunchanged rehti hai. Expired air mein oxygen percentage decrease hota hai, jabki carbon dioxide aur\nwater vapour ki amount increase hoti hai. [Q2]\n3. Oxygen Transport — Lungs → Blood → Tissues\n● Body cells tak oxygen pahunchne ka correct sequence source mein: air se Lungs → Blood →\nTissue/cells. Pehle lungs oxygen uptake karte hain, phir blood us oxygen ko transport karta hai, aur\nfinally oxygen tissues/cells tak deliver hoti hai. [Q3]\n4. Alveoli — Site of Gaseous Exchange\n● Lungs mein gaseous exchange ka main site alveoli hai. Alveoli ko capillaries surround karti hain; inhaled\noxygen alveoli se capillary blood mein move karti hai aur carbon dioxide capillary blood se alveolar air\nmein move karti hai. [Q4]\n5. Low Blood Oxygen & Breathing Rate\n● Blood oxygen concentration kam hone par breathing rate increase hoti hai. Source is low blood-oxygen\ncondition ko hypoxemia ke context mein explain karta hai aur shortness of breath se link karta hai. [Q5]\n6. Carbon Monoxide Poisoning & Oxygen-Carrying Capacity\n● Carbon monoxide haemoglobin ke saath combine karke carboxyhaemoglobin (HbCO) banata hai. Isse\nhaemoglobin tissues tak oxygen effectively carry nahi kar pata aur blood ki oxygen-carrying capacity\nreduce hoti hai, leading to hypoxia. Source HbCO complex ko fairly stable bhi batata hai. [Q6]\n7. ATP — Energy Currency & ATP → ADP\n● ATP (Adenosine Triphosphate) high-energy molecule hai. Source ke according maximum energy-\nproviding biotransformation ATP → ADP hai; ATP hydrolysis life processes jaise muscle contraction,\nmembrane gradients aur biosynthetic work ke liye usable energy release karti hai: ATP + H O → ADP +\n₂\nPi + energy. [Q7]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Respiratory System Full Mind Map\n● Cellular respiration nutrients ki biochemical energy ko ATP mein convert karti hai; isliye respiration ke\ndauran energy ATP ke form mein produced/stored hoti hai. [Q8]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Respiratory System Full Mind Map\n8. Aerobic Respiration — Complete Oxidation of Glucose\n● Oxygen ki presence mein glucose ka complete conversion carbon dioxide + water ke saath energy\nrelease kare to ise aerobic respiration kehte hain. Source ke mutabik is process mein large amount of\nenergy release hoti hai aur ye plants aur animals ki cells mein hota hai. [Q9]\n9. Pyruvate — Aerobic / Anaerobic Pathways\n● Glucose cytoplasm mein glycolysis se pyruvate mein break hota hai. Source clearly batata hai ki\npyruvate 3-carbon molecule hai, 4-carbon nahi. Oxygen present ho to pyruvate se CO + H O + energy\n₂\n₂\nbanti hai; oxygen ki kami mein muscles mein lactic acid banta hai; oxygen absent hone par source\npyruvate ko CO + ethanol mein convert hota batata hai.\n₂\n[Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q10 Statement Combination\n ▸Statement (i) “pyruvate has four carbon molecules” false hai because source pyruvate ko 3-carbon molecule\nbatata hai. Statements (ii) lactic-acid formation in oxygen shortage aur (iii) anaerobic CO + ethanol formation\n₂\n\nko true maana gaya hai; hence source answer (C) = (ii) and (iii). [Q10]\n10. Source-Specific Body Temperature Question\n● Q11 mein source answer key “Lungs” ko body temperature maintain karne wala part select karti hai.\nExplanation breathing, oxidation-generated energy aur body-water vaporisation ke through temperature\nmaintenance describe karti hai. Is source-specific framing ko without outside correction preserve kiya\ngaya hai. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0311","t":"07.ix Reproduction and Embryo Development","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Reproduction & Embryo Development Full Mind Map\n🧬 REPRODUCTION & EMBRYO DEVELOPMENT — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.ix · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Fertilization — Site in Human Female Reproductive Tract\n2. Sperm Fertilizing Capacity\n3. Human Embryo — Beginning of Heartbeat\n4. Amnion — Protection of Developing Embryo\n5. Sertoli Cells — Testis & Spermatogenesis\n1. Fertilization — Site in Human Female Reproductive Tract\n● Human fertilization source ke according fallopian tube/oviduct mein hota hai—uterus se door, ovary ke\nclose end par. Oviduct ovary ko uterus se connect karta hai aur ovulated oocyte isi route se travel karta\nhai. [Q1]\n● Normally sperm ovum ko Fallopian tube mein fertilize karta hai. Source Fallopian tube ko oviduct/uterine\ntube bhi kehta hai aur ise sperm ko egg tak le jaane, fertilization ke liye suitable environment dene aur\negg transport karne wali paired narrow ducts ke roop mein explain karta hai. [Q2]\n2. Sperm Fertilizing Capacity\n● Female genital tract/oviduct mein pahunchne ke baad sperm source ke mutabik lagbhag 72 hours tak\nalive reh sakta hai, lekin ovum ko fertilize karne ki capacity lagbhag 48 hours yani 1–2 days tak rehti hai.\n[Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Sperm Life vs Fertilizing Capacity\n ▸Source wording yaad rakho: sperm survival ≈72 hours, but fertilizing capacity ≈48 hours (2 days). [Q3]\n3. Human Embryo — Beginning of Heartbeat\n● Human embryo ka heart source ke according fertilization ke about 4–5 weeks baad pehli baar beat karna\nstart karta hai; given options mein Fourth week correct marked hai. Is stage par heartbeat roughly 105–\n121 beats per minute batayi gayi hai. [Q4]\n4. Amnion — Protection of Developing Embryo\n● Amnion embryo ko cover karne wali membrane hai. Amniotic fluid se filled hokar amniotic sac banata hai\naur developing embryo ko desiccation (sukhne), outer pressure etc. se protective environment deta hai.\n[Q5]\n5. Sertoli Cells — Testis & Spermatogenesis\n● Sertoli cells human testes mein milne wali somatic/supporting cells hain. Ye seminiferous tubules ka\nstructural component hote hue spermatogenesis mein contribute karti hain aur source inhe\nsustentacular “nurse” cells bhi kehta hai. [Q6]\n● Source ke mutabik Sertoli cells adenohypophysis se secreted FSH se activated hoti hain aur apni\nmembrane par FSH receptors express karti hain. [Q6]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0312","t":"07.v Circulatory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Circulatory System Full Mind Map\n🩸 CIRCULATORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.v · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Heartbeat, Cardiac Cycle & Pulse\n2. Heart Attack — Typical Signs\n3. Heart Chambers, Electrical Impulse & Pacemaker\n4. Heart Transplant & Artificial Heart\n5. Pulmonary Vein & Coronary Arteries\n6. Blood — Volume, Nature, Plasma & Functions\n7. Haemoglobin, RBCs, Myoglobin & Red Colour\n8. Blood Pressure — Normal Value, Instrument & Age\n9. Source-Specific Blood Pressure vs Atmospheric Pressure\n10. Blood Groups — Discovery, Antigens & Rh Factor\n11. Universal Donor / Recipient & Transfusion Rules\n12. Blood-Group Inheritance & Rh Incompatibility\n13. Blood pH\n14. Antigen, WBCs, Lymphocytes & Immunity\n15. Blood Viscosity, WBC Size & Leukemia\n16. Blood-Cell Formation, Spleen & Lymphocytes\n17. Blood Clotting, Plasma Water & Platelets\n18. Nitric Oxide — Vasodilation & Blood Flow\n19. Artificial “Plastic Blood”\n1. Heartbeat, Cardiac Cycle & Pulse\n● Healthy person ka normal heart rate source ke according about 72–75 beats per minute hai. Cardiac\ncycle ek complete heartbeat ko represent karta hai; sleep ke dauran slow rates around 40–50 BPM\ncommon bataye gaye hain. [Q1]\n● Har heartbeat mein contraction aur relaxation hota hai. Source ke mutabik heart relaxation aur\ncontraction ke beech rest karta hai; wrist pulse bhi heart ke same rate par beat karta hai. [Q2, Q8]\n2. Heart Attack — Typical Signs\n● Heart attack ko myocardial infarction kaha gaya hai. Typical signs mein severe chest pain/discomfort,\nnausea aur severe perspiration/sweating shamil hain; pain/discomfort arms, back, neck, jaw ya stomach\nmein bhi ho sakta hai. [Q3, Q4]\n● Source Q3 mein “pain in legs” ko heart-attack symptom nahi maana gaya, aur Q4 mein headache ko\ntypical/direct sign nahi maana gaya. [Q3, Q4]\n3. Heart Chambers, Electrical Impulse & Pacemaker\n● Human heart mein four chambers hote hain — right/left atria aur right/left ventricles. Atria incoming blood\nreceive karte hain aur ventricles blood pump out karte hain. [Q5, Q6]\n● Heartbeat ka electrical impulse source “sinus node” se originate batata hai. Sino-atrial (SA) node right\natrium mein hota hai aur heart ka natural pacemaker maana gaya hai. [Q7, Q14]\n● Artificial pacemaker abnormal heart rhythm ko control/regulate karne ke liye electrical pulses use karta\nhai, taaki heart normal rate par beat kare. [Q13]\n4. Heart Transplant & Artificial Heart\n● Source ke mutabik world ka first human heart transplant Dr. Christian Barnard/Barnard ne 3 December\n1967 ko South Africa ke Groote Schuur Hospital mein Louis Washkansky par perform kiya. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● Jarvik-7 ko first successful permanent artificial heart ke roop mein describe kiya gaya hai; Robert Jarvik\nse associated hai aur 1982 mein patient Barney Clark mein first implantation ka reference diya gaya hai.\n[Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Circulatory System Full Mind Map\n5. Pulmonary Vein & Coronary Arteries\n● Pulmonary veins body ki only veins batayi gayi hain jo oxygenated blood lungs se left atrium tak carry\nkarti hain. Source ye bhi note karta hai ki pulmonary arteries oxygen-poor blood carry karti hain. [Q15]\n● Heart muscle (myocardium) ko oxygen-rich blood supply karne wali vessels coronary arteries hoti hain;\ndeoxygenated blood remove karne wali vessels cardiac veins batayi gayi hain. [Q78]\n6. Blood — Volume, Nature, Plasma & Functions\n● 70 kg normal adult mein total blood volume source ke according roughly 5–6 litres hai. [Q16, Q17]\n● Blood ek special connective tissue hai jiska fluid matrix plasma hota hai. Plasma blood ka fluid part hai;\nblood vessels ke andar blood oxygen, carbon dioxide aur nutrients transport karta hai. [Q18, Q20, Q31]\n● Q19 ka source answer erythrocytes (RBCs) select karta hai; explanation RBCs ko haemoglobin ke\nthrough oxygen tissues tak aur carbon dioxide tissues se lungs tak carry karne se link karti hai. [Q19]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q17 Disputed Blood-Volume Question\n ▸Q17 mein source answer label “Disputed Question (Ans. *)” hai. Options mein 6000 ml aur 5000 ml dono diye\ngaye hain, jabki explanation normal 70 kg adult ka total blood 5–6 litres batati hai; isliye source kisi ek option\nko final correct mark nahi karta. [Q17]\n7. Haemoglobin, RBCs, Myoglobin & Red Colour\n● Haemoglobin RBCs mein present red, iron-containing protein hai jo lungs se oxygen tissues tak carry\nkarta hai aur source explanation carbon dioxide ko tissues se lungs ki taraf le jane se bhi link karti hai.\n“Slightly acidic” statement ko Q22 mein incorrect maana gaya hai. [Q21, Q22, Q25]\n● RBC-related correct properties: iron present hota hai, blood ko red colour milta hai aur oxygen transport\nhota hai; immunity dena RBC/haemoglobin ka function nahi maana gaya. [Q23, Q24]\n● Myoglobin skeletal muscle ka oxygen-binding heme protein hai aur iron (Fe) contain karta hai. [Q26, Q27]\n● Earthworm mein haemoglobin plasma mein dissolved hota hai. Human blood/RBC ka red colour\nhaemoglobin se linked hai. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n8. Blood Pressure — Normal Value, Instrument & Age\n● Normal average blood pressure 120/80 mm Hg diya gaya hai — around 120 mm Hg systolic aur 80 mm\nHg diastolic. Given examples mein 120/80 ko normal select kiya gaya hai. [Q32, Q33, Q38]\n● Blood pressure measure karne ka instrument sphygmomanometer hai; “Hg” mercury ka chemical symbol\nhai. [Q34, Q35, Q36]\n● Source ke according age badhne par blood pressure generally increase hota hai; older age ko high\nblood pressure ke contributing factors mein include kiya gaya hai. [Q37]\n9. Source-Specific Blood Pressure vs Atmospheric Pressure\n● Q39 source blood pressure ko atmospheric pressure se greater select karta hai. Explanation ke mutabik\nclinical blood-pressure reading atmospheric pressure ke relative hoti hai; 120 mm Hg systolic ko\natmospheric pressure se 120 mm Hg above aur vacuum reference par roughly 760 + 120 = 880 mm Hg\nke framing mein explain kiya gaya hai. [Q39]\n10. Blood Groups — Discovery, Antigens & Rh Factor\n● Karl Landsteiner ko main blood groups distinguish/discover karne se credit diya gaya hai. Source Rh\nfactor ko Rhesus monkey se naam mila batata hai aur Landsteiner + Alexander S. Wiener ko Rh factor\nidentification se associate karta hai. [Q40, Q41]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Circulatory System Full Mind Map\n● Blood group RBC surface par specific antigens ki presence/absence se determine hota hai. ABO system\nmein A, B, AB aur O types A/B antigens ke basis par bante hain; Q42 ke listed options mein correct\ndeterminant present na hone ke karan “None of the above” answer hai. [Q42]\n● Blood group O ke RBCs par neither A nor B agglutinogen/antigen hota hai. [Q43]\n11. Universal Donor / Recipient & Transfusion Rules\n● Source ABO framing mein blood group O ko universal donor maanta hai because RBC surface par A/B\nantigens nahi hote. Jab unknown blood group ko emergency transfusion dena ho, Q52–Q53 specifically\nO negative / O, Rh− ko safe option select karte hain. [Q44, Q45, Q46, Q52, Q53]\n● Blood group AB ko universal recipient/acceptor maana gaya hai because plasma mein anti-A/anti-B\nantibodies absent hote hain; AB person source ke according any ABO group se blood receive kar sakta\nhai. Q47 mein Assertion true aur Reason false hai, kyunki AB RBCs par A aur B dono antigens present\nhote hain. [Q47, Q48, Q49, Q50]\n● Blood group A individual source ke mutabik A ya O group se blood receive kar sakta hai; accident\nscenario mein wife O, son A aur daughter O donate kar sakte hain, brother AB nahi. [Q51]\n12. Blood-Group Inheritance & Rh Incompatibility\n● AB+ × O− parents ke example mein source biological twin sons ko A+ aur B+ assign karta hai; therefore\nthree sons mein O+ child adopted maana gaya hai. [Q54]\n● Father group A aur mother group O ke case mein source explanation offspring ko A ya O possible batati\nhai aur ABO inheritance ko Mendelian genes se link karti hai. [Q55]\n● Transfusion mein ABO ke saath Rh factor compatibility bhi important hai. Rh antigen present ho to Rh+\naur absent ho to Rh−; Rh− person ko Rh+ blood exposure par antibodies form ho sakti hain. [Q56]\n● Maternal–foetal Rh incompatibility ka classic source case Rh− mother aur Rh+ foetus hai; explanation\nerythroblastosis fetalis/hemolytic anaemia se link karti hai. [Q57]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q55 Answer Key vs Explanation\n ▸Q55 ki answer key option (C) = O select karti hai, lekin same source explanation clearly kehti hai ki father A +\nmother O hone par son ka blood group “O or A” ho sakta hai. Is internal source mismatch ko as-is preserve\nkiya gaya hai. [Q55]\n13. Blood pH\n● Normal human blood ka pH about 7.4 hai; source range 7.35–7.45 deta hai, yani blood slightly\nbasic/alkaline hota hai. [Q58, Q59, Q60]\n14. Antigen, WBCs, Lymphocytes & Immunity\n● Antigen generally foreign molecule/substance hai jo immune system trigger karke antibody formation\ninduce karta hai. [Q61, Q62, Q63]\n● WBCs infection se protection aur disease resistance mein major role play karte hain. [Q64, Q65]\n● Lymphocytes antibodies produce karte hain aur immunity se closely related hain; source lymphocytes\nmein B cells, T cells aur natural killer cells ka reference deta hai. [Q66, Q67, Q68]\n● B and T lymphocytes pathogens se hone wali diseases ke against adaptive immune response ka critical\npart hain. Vaccination ke through antigen introduce hone par source Q70 antibodies banane ke liye B\ncells ko primary cells select karta hai. [Q69, Q70]\n15. Blood Viscosity, WBC Size & Leukemia\n● Source blood viscosity ko mainly hematocrit aur plasma viscosity se relate karta hai; Q71 ka answer\n“proteins in blood” hai because plasma proteins plasma viscosity ko affect karte hain. [Q71]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Circulatory System Full Mind Map\n● WBC diameter source mein about 0.007 mm diya gaya hai; normal WBC count roughly 4,000–11,000\nper microlitre aur total blood volume ka approx 1% bataya gaya hai. [Q72]\n● Q73 source excess abnormal white corpuscles ke pathological condition ko leukemia select karta hai;\nexplanation leukemia ko bone marrow se start hone wale cancers ke group se link karti hai. [Q73]\n16. Blood-Cell Formation, Spleen & Lymphocytes\n● Adult mein RBCs red bone marrow of large bones mein continuously form hote hain (erythropoiesis);\nsource embryo mein liver ko main RBC-production site batata hai aur kidney-made erythropoietin (EPO)\nko stimulation se link karta hai. [Q74]\n● Spleen old RBCs remove/destroy karta hai aur immune/blood-filter role rakhta hai. Source Q75 spleen\nko WBC formation + RBC destruction ke option mein select karta hai, while explanation adult bone\nmarrow ko all RBCs, 60–70% WBCs and all platelets produce karne wala bhi batati hai. [Q75]\n● Lymphocyte production source explanation multiple lymphatic tissues — spleen, thymus, lymph nodes\n— aur bone marrow context se jodti hai. Isi wajah se Q76 spleen select karta hai, jabki Q77 “more than\none of the above” answer deta hai. [Q76, Q77]\n17. Blood Clotting, Plasma Water & Platelets\n● Thrombin blood clotting/coagulation se associated enzyme hai jo soluble fibrinogen ko insoluble fibrin\nstrands mein convert karta hai. [Q79, Q80]\n● Plasma blood volume ka about 55% hai aur source ke according roughly 91–92% water hota hai; Q81 ka\nclosest listed answer 90% hai. Plasma mein albumin, fibrinogen aur globulins/antibodies bhi mentioned\nhain. [Q81]\n● Platelets clotting mein injury site par aggregate/stick karke coagulation platform banate hain. Source\nnormal platelet count about 150,000–350,000/µL, RBC ~5,000,000/µL aur WBC ~4,000–11,000/µL deta\nhai; isliye blood mein WBC se platelets zyada hote hain. [Q82]\n● Alum ko cuts se bleeding stop karne ke liye source aluminium ions ki high coagulating power aur blood\nke colloidal nature se explain karta hai; Assertion aur Reason dono true aur Reason correct explanation\nmaana gaya hai. [Q84]\n18. Nitric Oxide — Vasodilation & Blood Flow\n● Nitric oxide (NO) human body mein synthesize hota hai aur blood-vessel smooth muscle relax karke\nvasodilation karta hai, jisse blood flow increase aur blood pressure lower ho sakta hai. Source\nendothelium ko primary synthesis site batata hai. [Q83]\n19. Artificial “Plastic Blood”\n● Source University of Sheffield, Britain ke scientists ko artificial “plastic blood” development se associate\nkarta hai. Is substitute ko emergency/military use ke liye light, easy to store, refrigeration-free aur water\nmein dissolve karke use karne ke concept ke roop mein describe kiya gaya hai. [Q85]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0313","t":"07.vi Excretory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Excretory System Full Mind Map\n💧 EXCRETORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.vi · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Excretion & Main Excretory Organ\n2. Liver — Detoxification of Alcohol\n3. Urine — Daily Volume, Water & Yellow Pigment\n4. Kidney Blood Flow, Filtration & Reabsorption\n5. Dialysis & Dialyzer (Artificial Kidney)\n6. Kidney Failure & Nitrogenous Wastes\n7. Normal Functions of Kidney — and What Is NOT Its Function\n8. Kidney Stones — Calcium Oxalate & Oxalate Crystallization\n9. Skin as an Excretory Organ — Sweat\n10. Kidney Transplantation — Immunosuppression\n1. Excretion & Main Excretory Organ\n● Humans mein kidneys excretory system ke main organs hain. Inka basic role blood ko filter karke\nunnecessary aur waste products ko body se remove karna hai. [Q10]\n2. Liver — Detoxification of Alcohol\n● Source ke according alcohol ka detoxification liver karta hai. Liver complex chemical reactions ke\nthrough harmful substances ko detoxify karta hai. [Q1]\n3. Urine — Daily Volume, Water & Yellow Pigment\n● Healthy adult human source ke according around 1.5 litres urine per 24 hours excrete karta hai; urine ka\nabout 91–96% part water hota hai. [Q2]\n● Human urine ka yellow colour urochrome pigment ki wajah se hota hai; source ise urobilin ke naam se\nbhi mention karta hai. [Q3]\n4. Kidney Blood Flow, Filtration & Reabsorption\n● Renal artery waste-containing blood ko kidneys/nephrons tak filtering ke liye le jaati hai; waste removal\nke baad cleaner blood renal vein ke through kidney se bahar nikalta hai. Isliye “clean blood renal artery\nse wapas jaata hai” statement source mein wrong hai. [Q4]\n● Bowman’s capsule se filtered liquid tiny tubules mein pass karta hai, jahan source ke mutabik much of\nthe glucose reabsorbed hokar blood mein renal vein side return karta hai. [Q4]\n● Kidneys body ke blood ke natural filters hain. Source Q8 “all the blood in the body is filtered through the\nkidneys” ko correct select karta hai; kidneys water-soluble wastes jaise urea/ammonium remove aur\nwater, glucose, amino acids ka reabsorption bhi karti hain. [Q8]\n● Urea blood se kidney mein separate/remove hota hai; source ultrafiltration ko renal capsule mein blood\naur filtrate ke barrier par occurring process batata hai, jisse urine formation hoti hai. [Q9]\n● Dono kidneys se average blood flow source ke according about 1200 cc (ml) per minute hai. Same\nexplanation roughly 1500 litres blood purification per day aur ~1 ml urine formation per minute ka\nreference deti hai. [Q11]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Excretory System Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Renal Artery vs Renal Vein\n ▸Renal artery kidney ko waste-containing blood filtering ke liye laati hai; cleaner blood renal vein se kidney se\nnikalta hai. Q4 mein isi wajah se statement 1 wrong aur statement 2 correct hai. [Q4]\n5. Dialysis & Dialyzer (Artificial Kidney)\n● Dialysis blood se waste aur excess water remove karne ki process hai aur kidney failure mein lost kidney\nfunction ke artificial replacement ke roop mein use hoti hai. [Q5, Q6]\n● Dialyzer ko source “artificial kidney” describe karta hai. Ye semipermeable membrane ke across flowing\nblood aur dialysate streams ke beech solutes aur water ka controllable transfer provide karta hai. [Q7]\n6. Kidney Failure & Nitrogenous Wastes\n● Kidneys fail hone par blood mein nitrogenous waste products accumulate hote hain. Source main\nnitrogenous wastes mein ammonia, urea aur uric acid list karta hai; urea urine ka primary component\nbataya gaya hai. [Q12]\n7. Normal Functions of Kidney — and What Is NOT Its Function\n● Source ke listed normal kidney functions mein blood-water level regulation, urea filtering aur several\nhormones ka secretion included hai. [Q13]\n● Blood sugar level regulation ko Q13 mein normal kidney function nahi maana gaya; source explanation\npancreas/insulin ko blood sugar regulation se link karti hai. [Q13]\n8. Kidney Stones — Calcium Oxalate & Oxalate Crystallization\n● Human kidney stones ka major/most common constituent source calcium oxalate batata hai. [Q14, Q16,\nQ17]\n● Kidney stones urine ke chemicals se bane hard objects hain. Source Q15 stone formation ko oxalates ke\ncrystallization se link karta hai; explanation calcium ke urine oxalate ke saath combine hone ko common\ncalcium-oxalate stone formation batati hai. [Q15]\n● Source explanation kidney stones ke four types list karti hai: calcium oxalate, uric acid, struvite aur\n“crystine” (source spelling). [Q15]\n9. Skin as an Excretory Organ — Sweat\n● Sweat skin ka excretory function bhi hai aur body temperature regulation ke liye liquid form mein\nproduce hota hai. Source sodium, potassium, calcium, magnesium aur trace elements jaise zinc,\ncopper, iron, chromium, nickel aur lead ko sweat se excreted batata hai. [Q18]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q18 “More Than One”\n ▸Q18 ke options mein Iron, Magnesium aur Zinc alag-alag diye hain. Source explanation in teeno ko sweat se\nexcreted trace/electrolyte elements mein include karti hai, isliye source correct answer (E) “None of the\nabove/More than one of the above” select karta hai. [Q18]\n10. Kidney Transplantation — Immunosuppression\n● Kidney transplantation mein source monoclonal antibodies ko immunosuppressor/anti-rejection role se\nassociate karta hai. Ye immune response ke specific cells/molecules, jaise T cells ya IL-2 receptor, ko\ntarget kar sakti hain. [Q19]\n● Source explanation monoclonal antibodies ko induction therapy, steroid-resistant acute rejection\ntreatment, delayed graft function ke effects ko reduce karne aur immunosuppressive minimization se bhi\nlink karti hai. [Q19]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0314","t":"07.vii Nervous System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nervous System Full Mind Map\n🧠 NERVOUS SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.vii · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Cranial Nerves & Spinal Nerves\n2. Central Nervous System, Input/Output Nerves & Reflex Arc\n3. Brain — Cerebrum, Cerebellum & Brainstem Functions\n4. Brain & Pain Receptors\n5. Cerebrum, Hippocampus & Memory\n6. Hypothalamus — Satiety, Thirst & Body Temperature\n7. Normal Human Body Temperature\n8. Medulla Oblongata — Swallowing & Vomiting Reflexes\n1. Cranial Nerves & Spinal Nerves\n● Cranium se nikalne wali nerves ko cranial nerves kaha jata hai. Source ke according humans mein\ncranial nerves ke 12 pairs hote hain aur ye brain ki ventral (bottom) surface par milte hain. [Q1]\n● Spinal cord se nikalne wali nerves spinal nerves kehlati hain. Human body mein 31 pairs spinal nerves\nhote hain; source inhe 8 cervical, 12 thoracic, 5 lumbar, 5 sacral aur 1 coccygeal pair mein group karta\nhai. Spinal nerves peripheral nervous system ka part hain. [Q2]\n2. Central Nervous System, Input/Output Nerves & Reflex Arc\n● Source explanation ke mutabik input aur output nerves central nervous system mein, khas taur par\nspinal cord mein, meet karti hain. Body bhar ki nerves brain ki taraf jaate hue spinal cord mein bundle\nhoti hain aur reflex arcs bhi spinal cord mein form hote hain. [Q3]\n● Reflex arc ek neural pathway hai jo reflex action ko control karta hai. Source ke according higher\nanimals mein most sensory neurons directly brain tak nahi jaate, balki spinal cord mein synapse karte\nhain; isi wajah se reflex action relatively fast hota hai. Reflex action ka governing centre spinal cord hai.\n[Q6]\n● Source reflex arcs ko do types mein batata hai: autonomic reflex arc (inner organs ko affect karta hai)\naur somatic reflex arc (muscles ko affect karta hai). [Q6]\n3. Brain — Cerebrum, Cerebellum & Brainstem Functions\n● Brain ke three main parts source mein cerebrum, cerebellum aur brainstem diye gaye hain. Cerebrum\ntouch, vision, hearing, speech, reasoning, learning aur fine control of movement jaise higher functions\nse linked hai. [Q4]\n● Cerebellum muscle movements ko coordinate karta hai aur posture/balance maintain karta hai;\nbrainstem breathing, heart rate, body temperature, wake-sleep cycles aur digestion jaise automatic\nfunctions perform karta hai. Isliye thinking, heartbeat regulation aur body balance — teeno brain\nfunctions ke under aate hain. [Q4, Q5]\n4. Brain & Pain Receptors\n● Source ke according brain tissue mein pain ya tactile (touch) receptors nahi hote. Isliye needle prick ya\nbrain surgery brain itself mein pain sensation produce nahi karti; given organs mein brain pain feel nahi\nkarega. [Q7]\n5. Cerebrum, Hippocampus & Memory\n● Memory power ke question mein source correct location cerebrum deta hai. Explanation ke mutabik\ncerebrum movement, thinking, feeling aur general problem-solving abilities se linked hai, aur\nhippocampus — jo cerebrum ka part hai — memory se deal karta hai. [Q8]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nervous System Full Mind Map\n6. Hypothalamus — Satiety, Thirst & Body Temperature\n● Humans mein satiety (satisfaction) aur thirst centres hypothalamus mein located hote hain. Source\nhypothalamus ko body temperature, thirst, hunger, sleep, circadian rhythm, moods, sex drive aur\nvarious hormone release ke regulation se bhi link karta hai. [Q9]\n● Body temperature ka regulating centre bhi hypothalamus hai. Source average normal human body\ntemperature 98.6°F batata hai aur hypothalamus ko hunger, thirst, fatigue, sleep aur circadian rhythms\nke control se associate karta hai. [Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Hypothalamus vs Other Brain Parts\n ▸Satiety + thirst centres → Hypothalamus. [Q9]\n ▸Body temperature regulation → Hypothalamus. [Q10]\n ▸Balance/posture → Cerebellum; automatic functions such as heart rate → Brainstem. [Q4, Q5]\n7. Normal Human Body Temperature\n● Source ke according human body temperature winters mein decrease aur summers mein increase nahi\nhota; normal temperature body thermostat ki tarah hypothalamus ke control mein stable rakha jata hai.\n[Q11]\n● Average normal human body temperature 98.6°F = 37°C = 310 K diya gaya hai. Q12 ke options mein\n98.6°F present nahi hai, isliye source correct answer 'None of the above' select karta hai. [Q12]\n● Q13 mein normal human body temperature ka correct option 37°C hai; source explanation previous\nquestion ki same temperature value refer karti hai. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q12 Options Pattern\n ▸Normal value source mein 98.6°F hai, lekin Q12 ke options 98.4°F, 98°F aur 98.8°F hain. Isliye source answer\n(D) None of the above deta hai. [Q12]\n8. Medulla Oblongata — Swallowing & Vomiting Reflexes\n● Medulla oblongata higher brain levels ko spinal cord se connect karta hai aur autonomic nervous system\nke several functions control karta hai. Source ise vomiting, coughing, sneezing aur swallowing ke reflex\ncentre se associate karta hai. [Q14]\n● Source pharyngeal reflex, swallowing/palatal reflex aur masseter reflex ko bulbar reflexes ke roop mein\nmention karta hai. [Q14]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0315","t":"07.viii Endocrine System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Endocrine System Full Mind Map\n🧪 ENDOCRINE SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 7.viii · Human Anatomy & Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Endocrine Glands — Ductless Glands & Pituitary\n2. Mixed Gland, Gonads & Basic Hormone–Gland Matching\n3. ADH & Urine Control\n4. Pancreas, Islets of Langerhans & Insulin\n5. Secretin & Gastrin — Digestive Hormones\n6. Oxytocin — Mother–Baby Bonding, Milk Ejection & Misuse\n7. Parathyroid Gland & Calcium–Phosphate Regulation\n8. Thyroid, Iodine, Goitre, Thyroxine & TSH\n9. Adrenaline — Fight or Flight\n10. Estrogen, Sex Hormones, Menopause & Other Hormonal Facts\n11. Melatonin & Circadian Rhythm\n12. Pheromones & Important Matching Questions\n1. Endocrine Glands — Ductless Glands & Pituitary\n● Endocrine glands ductless glands hoti hain—inke excretory ducts nahi hote aur hormones directly blood\nmein release hote hain. Major endocrine glands mein pineal, pituitary, thymus, thyroid, parathyroid aur\nadrenal glands include kiye gaye hain. [Q1]\n● Pituitary brain ke base par hypothalamus ke neeche sella turcica naam ke bony hollow mein located hoti\nhai. Source ise “Master gland” aur hypophysis cerebri bhi kehta hai. [Q2, Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q2: “Smallest Endocrine Gland”\n ▸Q2 ka marked answer given options mein Pituitary (D) hai. Usi source explanation ki last line overall smallest\nendocrine gland Pineal (~7.5 mm) batati hai. Dono source statements preserve kiye gaye hain. [Q2]\n2. Mixed Gland, Gonads & Basic Hormone–Gland Matching\n● Pancreas mixed gland hai—endocrine role mein insulin, glucagon, somatostatin aur pancreatic\npolypeptide se blood sugar regulate karta hai; exocrine role mein pancreatic juice pancreatic duct se\nduodenum mein release karta hai. [Q4]\n● Corpus luteum female ovary mein temporary endocrine structure hai aur relatively high progesterone ke\nsaath moderate estradiol aur inhibin A produce karta hai. [Q5]\n● Leydig/interstitial cells testes ke seminiferous tubules ke paas hoti hain aur mainly androgen, especially\ntestosterone, secrete karti hain. [Q6]\n● Important gland→hormone match: Gonads→Progesterone, Pituitary→Growth hormone,\nPancreas→Insulin, Adrenal→Cortisol. Hormone→gland match: Progesterone→Ovaries,\nTestosterone→Testes, Thyroxine→Thyroid, Insulin→Pancreas. [Q7, Q9]\n3. ADH & Urine Control\n● ADH (Antidiuretic Hormone) source ke according pituitary se released hota hai aur kidney se urine ki\nquantity/secretion ko control karta hai. [Q8]\n4. Pancreas, Islets of Langerhans & Insulin\n● Carbohydrate-rich diet ke baad bhi blood glucose relatively constant rehne ka source reason pancreatic\nhormone insulin hai; beta cells insulin se blood glucose maintain karti hain. Insulin deficiency diabetes\naur excess insulin hypoglycemia se linked hai. [Q10]\n● Pancreas defective hone par insulin aur glucagon formation badly affect hota hai. Source: beta\ncells→insulin, alpha cells→glucagon, delta cells→somatostatin. [Q11]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Endocrine System Full Mind Map\n● Insulin protein-chain/peptide hormone hai, source ke according 51 amino acids ka micropeptide; beta\ncells of Islets of Langerhans ise produce karti hain. [Q13, Q14, Q16, Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● Insulin carbohydrates, fats aur proteins ke metabolism ko regulate karta hai by promoting glucose\nabsorption into liver, fat aur skeletal muscle cells. [Q15]\n● Source insulin ke chemical properties mein metal ion Zinc mention karta hai. [Q22]\n● Source Q23 ke explanation mein insulin ke sources ke roop mein “roots of dahlias” aur pancreatic beta\ncells dono mention kiye gaye hain; is source wording ko as-is preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAPS — Insulin Source-Specific Points\n ▸Q15 source ka scientifically broader explanation carbohydrates + fats + proteins teenon metabolism batata\nhai, isliye page par “More than one” answer hai; note mein BPSC final key ne option (B) diya tha, jise source\n“not completely appropriate” kehta hai. [Q15]\n ▸Q23 source explicitly “roots of dahlias” ko insulin source ke roop mein mention karta hai. Is unusual source\nwording ko bina outside correction ke preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q23]\n5. Secretin & Gastrin — Digestive Hormones\n● Secretin pancreas ko digestive juice production ke liye stimulate karta hai; source ise duodenum ki S\ncells ka peptide hormone batata hai aur duodenal pH/stomach-liver secretions se bhi link karta hai. [Q12]\n● Hormone–function pair mein “Gastrin→regulation of blood pressure” incorrect pair hai. Source gastrin ko\ngastric cells se gastric acid secretion stimulate karne wala peptide hormone batata hai. [Q24]\n6. Oxytocin — Mother–Baby Bonding, Milk Ejection & Misuse\n● Mother ka baby ko hug/kiss karna oxytocin secretion se linked hai; source ise “love/cuddle hormone”\nkehta hai aur childbirth, maternal bonding aur breast-feeding se associate karta hai. [Q25]\n● Oxytocin uterus aur breast par act karta hai; labour ke during cervix/uterus stimulation aur mammary\nglands se milk release/ejection mein role play karta hai. [Q26]\n● Source oxytocin ke misuse ko cattle mein milk production badhane aur pumpkins/watermelons jaise\nfruits/vegetables ka size badhane se link karta hai; labour speed-up misuse bhi mention hai. [Q27]\n● Source Q28 mein keratin, fibroin aur collagen ko proteins batata hai, jabki oxytocin ko peptide\nhormone/neuropeptide batakar “not a full structural protein” framing use karta hai. [Q28]\n● Cows/buffaloes mein udders tak milk descend karwane ke liye source oxytocin/Pitocin injection batata\nhai. [Q29]\n● Milk-ejection hormone oxytocin source question ke hisab se pituitary gland se secreted/released maana\ngaya hai; explanation ke mutabik ye hypothalamic nuclei mein produced aur posterior pituitary se\nreleased hota hai. [Q30]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q28 Oxytocin Classification\n ▸Q28 ka source answer Oxytocin ko “not a protein” select karta hai, while explanation ise peptide\nhormone/neuropeptide bolkar structural proteins (keratin/fibroin/collagen) se distinguish karti hai. [Q28]\n7. Parathyroid Gland & Calcium–Phosphate Regulation\n● Parathyroid glands pituitary gland se independent function kar sakti hain. Source parathyroid hormone\naur calcitonin ko blood/bone calcium regulation se link karta hai. [Q31]\n● Parathyroid hormone (PTH) chief cells se secreted polypeptide hai aur blood calcium regulate karta hai;\nsource PTH ko proximal renal tubule mein phosphate reabsorption reduce karke urine phosphate\nexcretion badhane se bhi link karta hai. [Q49]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Endocrine System Full Mind Map\n8. Thyroid, Iodine, Goitre, Thyroxine & TSH\n● Source ke according iodised salt useful hai because it “controls the thyroid gland”; iodine deficiency\nthyroid problems se linked hai. [Q32]\n● Goitre iodine deficiency se linked thyroid enlargement hai; source hilly areas mein low iodine in\nsoil/water/agricultural produce ko endemic goitre ka explanation deta hai. [Q33]\n● Thyroxine thyroid gland ka main hormone hai; heart/digestive function, metabolism, brain development,\nbone health aur muscle control se linked hai. [Q34]\n● Thyroxine (T4) aur triiodothyronine (T3) iodine-containing hormones hain; source ke mutabik thyroid\ncells iodine + amino acid tyrosine se inhe banati hain. T4 mein 4 iodine atoms aur T3 mein 3 hote hain.\n[Q35, Q36, Q37]\n● Thyroid hormone output ko TSH regulate karta hai; TSH anterior pituitary se produced hota hai aur\nthyroid ko thyroxine secrete karne ke liye stimulate karta hai. [Q38]\n9. Adrenaline — Fight or Flight\n● Important match: Adrenaline→Anger/fear/danger, Estrogen→Females, Insulin→Glucose,\nPheromones→partner attraction through smell. [Q39]\n● Adrenaline/Epinephrine “fight or flight hormone” hai, adrenal glands se released hota hai. Source\nincreased blood supply/activity, cardiac muscle contraction, heartbeat/pulse/arterial pressure/cardiac\noutput increase aur excitement feeling describe karta hai. [Q40, Q41]\n10. Estrogen, Sex Hormones, Menopause & Other Hormonal Facts\n● Estrogen primarily ovaries ke follicles se produced hota hai; corpus luteum aur placenta bhi secrete karte\nhain. Source female secondary sexual characteristics, endometrium aur menstrual cycle se link karta\nhai. [Q42, Q43, Q44]\n● Source Estrone ko weak postmenopausal estrogen aur minor female sex hormone batata hai;\nestrogen/oestrogen actual female sex hormone ke roop mein explained hai. [Q45]\n● Menopause source ke according ovarian estrogen aur progesterone secretion ke end se marked hai;\novaries small testosterone aur adrenal gland androstenedione continue kar sakte hain, jo body fat mein\nestrogen forms mein convert ho sakte hain. [Q46]\n● Somatotropin/Growth hormone exercise ke saath increase hota hai. Source progesterone ko small\namount mein male testes mein aur testosterone ko small amount mein women ke ovaries/adrenal\nglands mein bhi produced batata hai; stress cortisol release ko increase karta hai. [Q47]\n⚠️ SOURCE NOTE — Q46 Cancelled by UPPSC\n ▸Q46 ke source explanation ke mutabik initial UPPSC key mein option (C) mark hua tha, lekin revised answer\nkey mein question cancel kar diya gaya. Isliye final correct option source mein intentionally blank hai. [Q46]\n11. Melatonin & Circadian Rhythm\n● Melatonin pineal gland ka hormone hai aur circadian rhythm regulate karne mein help karta hai. Source\nke according darkness mein melatonin production badhta hai aur bright light mein ghatta hai. [Q50]\n12. Pheromones & Important Matching Questions\n● Quick biomolecule match: Hormone→Testosterone, Enzyme→Lipase, Phospholipid→Lecithin,\nPolymer→Polythene. [Q48]\n● Pheromones environment mein release hone wali chemical substances hain jo same species ke dusre\norganisms ke behaviour/physiology ko affect karti hain; source especially insects se associate karta hai.\n[Q51, Q52]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0316","t":"08.i Photosynthesis","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Photosynthesis Full Mind Map\n🌿 PHOTOSYNTHESIS — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 8.i · Plant Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Chlorophyll — Composition, Function & Chloroplast Self-Replication\n2. Light Reaction vs Dark Reaction — Sites in Chloroplast\n3. Raw Materials, Products, Oxygen Source & Glucose\n4. Where & When Photosynthesis Occurs\n5. Light Spectrum — Red, Blue, Violet & Green Light\n6. Energy Conversion, ATP & Calvin Cycle\n7. Photosynthetic Efficiency — Chlorella\n8. Roots & Photosynthesis\n9. Photosynthesis in Carbon Cycle & Night Respiration\n10. Infrared Photosynthesis — Green Sulphur Bacteria\n1. Chlorophyll — Composition, Function & Chloroplast Self-Replication\n● Chlorophyll ke components mein carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, nitrogen aur magnesium shamil hain;\ncalcium component nahi hai. Magnesium chlorophyll ke porphyrin ring ke centre mein present hota hai.\n[Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Photosynthesis mein chlorophyll ka main kaam light ko absorb karna hai. Source ke mutabik chlorophyll\nchloroplast mein located hota hai; absorbed light energy food synthesis ke liye use hoti hai aur green\nwavelength mainly reflect hone se plant green dikhta hai. [Q4]\n● Chloroplast mein DNA aur RNA dono ki presence use self-replication ke liye qualified/semi-autonomous\norganelle banati hai. Source RNA primers ko DNA synthesis initiate karne mein important batata hai.\n[Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Chlorophyll Composition\n ▸Magnesium = chlorophyll ka key element; Calcium = chlorophyll ka component NAHI. [Q1–Q3]\n ▸Green light mainly reflect hoti hai; isi wajah se chlorophyll/plant green dikhta hai. [Q4]\n2. Light Reaction vs Dark Reaction — Sites in Chloroplast\n● Photosynthesis ke light-dependent reactions thylakoid/grana membranes mein hote hain aur ATP +\nNADPH produce karte hain. Light-independent/dark reaction (Calvin cycle/Blackman reaction)\nchloroplast ke stroma mein hota hai aur light reaction se bane ATP/NADPH ka use karke CO ko\n₂\nglucose mein convert karta hai. [Q6]\n● Solar energy ka ATP mein conversion chloroplast ke light reactions mein hota hai; source ATP aur\nNADPH ko energy-transporting molecules ke roop mein describe karta hai. [Q29]\n3. Raw Materials, Products, Oxygen Source & Glucose\n● Photosynthesis ka main product glucose (sugar) hai aur oxygen (O ) mainly by-product ke roop mein\n₂\nrelease hota hai. Glucose ka chemical formula C H O hai.\n₆ ₁₂ ₆\n[Q7, Q10]\n● Photosynthesis mein release hone wala oxygen carbon dioxide se nahi, water se aata hai. Light reaction\nmein water molecules ki photolysis/splitting se oxygen evolve hota hai. [Q8, Q15]\n● Green plants photosynthesis mein atmosphere se CO lete hain aur O release karte hain while glucose\n₂\n₂\nbanta hai. Carbon dioxide essential raw material hai; sunlight aur water bhi required hain, jabki oxygen\nprocess ke liye required nahi hai. [Q9, Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — CO vs O\n₂\n₂\n ▸CO = raw material/absorbed gas; O = by-product/released gas.\n₂\n₂\n[Q9, Q11–Q14]\n ▸Released O ka source = H O ki photolysis, CO nahi.\n₂\n₂\n₂\n[Q8, Q15]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Photosynthesis Full Mind Map\n4. Where & When Photosynthesis Occurs\n● Source ke according Earth par approximately 90% photosynthesis aquatic plants aur algae se hota hai;\nisme 85% sea mein (mainly phytoplankton/algae) aur remaining 5% rivers/ponds etc. mein bataya gaya\nhai. [Q16]\n● Photosynthesis light ki presence mein hota hai. Source normally sunlight ko main source batata hai,\nmarine algae ke liye moonlight ka mention karta hai aur electric/artificial light mein bhi photosynthesis\npossible batata hai; is framing ke hisab se suitable light ho to day ya night dono mein ho sakta hai. [Q17,\nQ26]\n● Plants food banane ki process ko Photosynthesis kehte hain. Ye primarily leaves mein aur partially\nstems mein hota hai; cellular site chloroplast hai. Broad leaf lamina sunlight aur CO absorption mein\n₂\nhelp karti hai. [Q18, Q19, Q20]\n5. Light Spectrum — Red, Blue, Violet & Green Light\n● Chlorophyll mainly blue, red aur violet light absorb karta hai. Source red + blue regions ko strongest\nphotosynthetic wavelengths batata hai; green light mainly reflect hoti hai aur photosynthesis green mein\nvery low/absent bataya gaya hai. [Q21, Q22]\n● Source visible spectrum ko 3800–7600 Å range mein place karta hai. Best photosynthesis red light mein,\nnext best blue light mein aur green light mein nil bataya hai; T.W. Engelmann (1888) ke action-spectrum\nexperiment ka bhi mention hai. [Q23]\n● Given exam questions ke according red light/rays photosynthesis ke liye most effective/most utilized\nhain. [Q24, Q25]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Light Colour Order\n ▸Most effective/active = RED; next = BLUE; GREEN = mainly reflected / source mein negligible-to-nil\nphotosynthesis. [Q21–Q25]\n6. Energy Conversion, ATP & Calvin Cycle\n● Photosynthesis light energy ko chemical energy mein convert karta hai. Source equation: 6CO + 12H O\n₂\n₂\n+ Light Energy → C H\nO + 6O + 6H O.\n₆ ₁₂ ₆\n₂\n₂\n[Q27]\n● Dark reaction/Calvin cycle mein one glucose synthesize karne ke liye source 6 turns batata hai; each\nturn 3 ATP + 2 NADPH use karta hai, total = 18 ATP + 12 NADPH. [Q28]\n● Light energy ka chemical energy mein conversion photosynthesis se hota hai; sunlight energy green\nplants mein chemical energy mein transform hoti hai. [Q30, Q31]\n● Photosynthesis mein solar energy molecular bonds mein chemical energy ke roop mein store hoti hai,\njise source potential energy classify karta hai. Sunlight ki free energy ko usable chemical potential\nenergy mein badalne ke karan photosynthesis biological systems ke metabolic energy ka ultimate\nsource bataya gaya hai. [Q32, Q33]\n7. Photosynthetic Efficiency — Chlorella\n● Given options mein Chlorella ko solar energy ko chemical energy mein convert karne ki maximum\nefficiency wala organism marked kiya gaya hai. Source Chlorella ko single-celled green alga\n(Chlorophyceae) batata hai aur photosynthetic efficiency up to 8% mention karta hai. [Q34]\n8. Roots & Photosynthesis\n● Generally roots ka kaam photosynthesis nahi hai. Source ke mutabik root cells normally chloroplasts\nnahi rakhte; roots water/nutrients absorb karte hain aur plant ko anchor karte hain, jabki food\npreparation mainly leaves mein hoti hai. [Q35]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Photosynthesis Full Mind Map\n9. Photosynthesis in Carbon Cycle & Night Respiration\n● Carbon cycle mein photosynthesis atmospheric CO ko consume karke uski amount decrease karta hai;\n₂\nrespiration, organic matter decay aur volcanic action CO release karke amount increase karte hain.\n₂\n[Q36]\n● Source ke night-tree questions ke framing mein sunlight na hone par photosynthesis/oxygen production\nnahi hota, while trees respiration continue karke CO release karte hain; isi basis par raat mein bade\n₂\nped ke neeche sone ko harmful/not advised bataya gaya hai. [Q37, Q38]\n⚠️ SOURCE-SPECIFIC NOTE — Night Under Trees\n ▸Q37–Q38 ka statement/explanation source ke exam-oriented framing ke according preserve kiya gaya hai:\nnight respiration → CO release; photosynthesis absent → O production absent.\n₂\n₂\n[Q37, Q38]\n10. Infrared Photosynthesis — Green Sulphur Bacteria\n● Source ke according deep-sea green sulphur bacteria sunlight ke invisible infrared radiations ka use\nphotosynthesis ke liye kar sakte hain. Ye water ko reducing agent ke roop mein use nahi karte aur\noxygen produce nahi karte; isse anoxygenic photosynthesis kaha gaya hai. [Q39]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0317","t":"08.ii Plant Nutrition","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Nutrition Full Mind Map\n🌱 PLANT NUTRITION — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 8.ii · Plant Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Plant Parts & Stem Functions — Shrub, Tree, Creeper & Petiole\n2. Root Hairs, Stomata & Transpiration Pull\n3. Xylem vs Phloem — Water, Minerals & Food Transport\n4. Plant Growth — Why a Nail Stays at the Same Height\n5. Essential Plant Nutrients — Soil, Macro & Micro Elements\n6. Sulphur, Nitrogen, Phosphorus & Boron — Crop Nutrition\n7. Parasitic Nutrition — Cuscuta (Amarbel)\n8. Crop Logging — Nutrient Requirement Assessment\n1. Plant Parts & Stem Functions — Shrub, Tree, Creeper & Petiole\n● Petiole leaf ko stem se attach karta hai aur weak stem jo upright nahi reh sakta, creeper hota hai.\nSource ke matching question mein base ke paas branching wala thick, hard stem “Tree” nahi balki\nShrub bataya gaya hai; tree mein branches trunk par comparatively upar hoti hain. [Q1]\n● Stem plant ko shape/support deta hai, leaves se food ko plant ke doosre parts tak transport karta hai aur\nfood store bhi kar sakta hai. Green stems photosynthesis bhi kar sakte hain; isi wajah se source\nquestion mein “more than one” framing apply hoti hai. [Q2]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Shrub vs Tree\n ▸Thick, hard stem + branching near base = SHRUB; Tree mein branches usually ground level se upar hoti\nhain. [Q1]\n ▸Petiole = leaf ko stem se jodta hai; Creeper = weak stem, upright stand nahi kar pata. [Q1]\n2. Root Hairs, Stomata & Transpiration Pull\n● Plant ko required maximum water root hairs absorb karte hain. Ye root ki outer layer/cell-maturation\nzone ke tiny hair-like extensions hote hain jo absorption ke liye surface area badhate hain. [Q3]\n● Stomata leaf epidermis ke small pores hote hain; guard cells stomatal opening ko regulate karke\natmosphere ke saath gas exchange mein help karte hain. Transpiration bhi mainly stomata ke through\nhota hai. [Q4]\n● Stomata ka open/close hona guard cells mein water amount aur usse related turgor pressure ke change\npar depend karta hai. Water gain se guard cells turgid hokar pore open karte hain; water loss se shrink\nhokar pore close hota hai. [Q5]\n● Tall trees mein water great heights tak transpiration se create hone wale suction/negative pressure yani\ntranspiration pull ke karan xylem ke through upar reach karta hai. [Q6]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Stomata vs Transpiration Pull\n ▸Stomata opening/closing = Guard-cell water/turgor change. [Q5]\n ▸Water ko tree mein upar kheenchne wali force = Transpiration pull. [Q6]\n3. Xylem vs Phloem — Water, Minerals & Food Transport\n● Tree ki bark ko base ke paas circularly remove karne (girdling) se phloem damage/remove ho jata hai.\nLeaves ka photosynthetic food roots tak nahi pahunchta, roots starve karte hain aur plant gradually\ndry/die kar sakta hai. [Q7]\n● Xylem vascular plants mein roots se water aur soluble mineral nutrients ko stem/leaves aur plant ke\ndoosre parts tak transport karta hai. Source ke repeated questions mein water transport ka answer\nXylem hi hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Nutrition Full Mind Map\n● Phloem (bast tissue) leaves mein bane food/photosynthates aur organic nutrients ko plant ke doosre\nparts tak carry karta hai. Source xylem ko primarily dead cells aur phloem ko living cells se bana hua\nbatata hai. [Q11, Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Xylem vs Phloem\n ▸XYLEM = Water + minerals, mainly roots → upper plant parts. [Q8–Q10]\n ▸PHLOEM = Prepared food / organic nutrients; living transport tissue. [Q11, Q12]\n ▸Girdling bark removes/damages phloem → roots ko food supply rukti hai. [Q7]\n4. Plant Growth — Why a Nail Stays at the Same Height\n● Tree trunk mein soil level se 1 m height par lagaya nail years baad bhi approximately same height par\nrahega. Length growth shoot/root tips ke apical meristems se hoti hai, jabki trunk ka girth lateral\nmeristems se badhta hai; nail upward move nahi karta. [Q13]\n5. Essential Plant Nutrients — Soil, Macro & Micro Elements\n● Source ke according plants apne nutrients mainly soil se receive karte hain. Carbon, oxygen aur\nhydrogen air/water se milte hain, lekin nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium jaise bahut se mineral nutrients\nroots soil se absorb karte hain. [Q14]\n● Sodium ko source most plants ke growth ke liye generally essential element nahi maanta. Potassium,\ncalcium aur magnesium essential macronutrients hain; sodium kuch specific plants mein beneficial ho\nsakta hai. [Q15]\n● Potassium (K) macronutrient hai, jabki Zinc, Boron aur Chlorine micronutrients/trace elements hain. [Q16]\n● Magnesium micronutrient nahi, macronutrient hai aur chlorophyll molecule ka central component bataya\ngaya hai. Iron, Manganese aur Copper micronutrients hain. Sodium ko source essential micronutrient\nbhi nahi maanta; Boron, Zinc aur Copper essential micronutrients hain. [Q17, Q18]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Macro vs Micro Nutrients\n ▸Potassium + Magnesium = MACRONUTRIENTS. [Q16, Q17]\n ▸Boron, Zinc, Copper, Iron, Manganese, Chlorine = source ke micronutrient examples. [Q16–Q18]\n ▸Sodium = most plants ke liye generally essential element/micronutrient NAHI. [Q15, Q18]\n6. Sulphur, Nitrogen, Phosphorus & Boron — Crop Nutrition\n● Mustard crop mein oil content enhance karne ke liye Sulphur ko source most useful nutrient batata hai;\nsulphur plant metabolism aur seed oil synthesis mein important hai. [Q19]\n● Plants atmospheric N ko directly normally use nahi karte; source ke repeated questions mein nitrogen\n₂\nuptake ka primary/common form Nitrate (NO ) diya gaya hai.\n₃⁻\n[Q20, Q21, Q22]\n● Early plant growth stimulate karne ke liye phosphorus-containing fertilizer useful hai. Source phosphorus\nko root development, early establishment aur maturity hasten karne se link karta hai. [Q23]\n● Legumes mein nodule formation ke liye Boron necessary bataya gaya hai. Boron new-cell/meristem\ndevelopment ke saath sugars, starches, nitrogen aur phosphorus ke translocation se bhi associated hai.\n[Q24]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Nitrate, Phosphorus & Boron\n ▸Plant nitrogen uptake (source framing) = NITRATE, NO .\n₃⁻ [Q20–Q22]\n ▸Early root/plant growth = PHOSPHORUS. [Q23]\n ▸Legume nodule formation = BORON. [Q24]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Nutrition Full Mind Map\n7. Parasitic Nutrition — Cuscuta (Amarbel)\n● Cuscuta/Amarbel ek yellow-orange/red, thin-stemmed parasitic plant hai; leaves minute scales tak\nreduced hoti hain. Ye haustoria bana kar host se nutrients leta hai. Source Pitcher plant aur Bladderwort\nko carnivorous, parasite nahi batata hai. [Q25]\n● Assertion–Reason question mein “Cuscuta parasitic angiosperm hai” true hai, lekin “nutrition host leaves\nse leta hai” false mark hai. Source ke mutabik haustoria host stem ke xylem aur phloem se contact\nkarke prepared food, water aur minerals absorb karte hain. [Q26]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Cuscuta Nutrition\n ▸Cuscuta = Parasitic angiosperm. [Q25, Q26]\n ▸Nutrition sirf host leaves se nahi; haustoria host STEM ke xylem + phloem se connect karte hain. [Q26]\n8. Crop Logging — Nutrient Requirement Assessment\n● Crop-logging plant analysis ki method hai jisse crop production ke liye nutrient requirement assess ki\njaati hai, taaki good plant growth aur high yield achieve ho. Source concept ko H.F. Clements (USA) aur\nHawaii mein sugarcane cultivation se associate karta hai. [Q27]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0318","t":"08.iii Plant Hormones","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Hormones Full Mind Map\n🌿 PLANT HORMONES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 8.iii · Plant Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Plant Hormones — Meaning, Examples & Cytokinin\n2. Major Hormones & Functions — Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, ABA\n3. Abscisic Acid (ABA) — Drought Tolerance & Stress Hormone\n4. Ethylene — Gaseous Hormone & Natural Fruit Ripening\n5. Artificial Fruit Ripening — Acetylene vs Ethylene\n6. Parthenocarpy — Seedless Tomato by Hormone Spray\n1. Plant Hormones — Meaning, Examples & Cytokinin\n● Plant hormones naturally occurring special organic compounds hote hain jo bahut kam quantity mein\nplant ke different parts tak transport hokar metabolic activities ko affect/control karte hain. Source\nexamples: Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, Abscisic acid aur Ethylene. [Q2]\n● Cytokinin ek plant hormone hai; source ke repeated MCQs mein Insulin, Thyroxine aur Estrogen ke\nopposite Cytokinin ko plant hormone identify kiya gaya hai. Cytokinin plant roots aur shoots mein cell\ndivision promote karta hai. [Q2, Q3, Q4]\n● Insulin plant hormone nahi hai. Source ke mutabik ye pancreas ke islets of Langerhans se produce hota\nhai, blood glucose regulate karta hai aur insulin ki deficiency diabetes se linked hai. [Q1]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Plant Hormone vs Animal Hormone\n ▸Cytokinin = PLANT hormone; Insulin, Thyroxine, Estrogen = source questions mein plant hormones NAHI.\n[Q1–Q4]\n ▸Plant-hormone examples source mein: Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, ABA, Ethylene. [Q2]\n2. Major Hormones & Functions — Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, ABA\n● Source matching ke according: Auxin → Apical dominance; Gibberellin → Cell elongation; Cytokinin →\nCell division; Abscisic acid → Growth inhibition. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Hormone–Function Matching\n ▸Auxin = Apical dominance | Gibberellin = Cell elongation. [Q5]\n ▸Cytokinin = Cell division | Abscisic acid (ABA) = Growth inhibition. [Q5]\n3. Abscisic Acid (ABA) — Drought Tolerance & Stress Hormone\n● Abscisic acid drought tolerance se related hormone hai. Water shortage ke time ABA stomata ko\ntemporarily close karwata hai, antitranspirant ki tarah act karta hai aur source ise “stress hormone” bhi\nkehta hai. [Q6]\n4. Ethylene — Gaseous Hormone & Natural Fruit Ripening\n● Ethylene gaseous form mein paaya jane wala phytohormone hai. Source ke mutabik ye fruit ripening,\nflower opening aur leaves ke abscission/shedding ko stimulate ya regulate karta hai. [Q7]\n● Natural plant hormone jo mainly fruit ripening ke liye responsible hai, source ke according Ethylene hai.\n[Q10]\n5. Artificial Fruit Ripening — Acetylene vs Ethylene\n● Historical MCQ framing mein green fruits ke artificial ripening ke liye Acetylene answer diya gaya hai;\ncalcium carbide acetylene ka source raha hai. Source explicitly note karta hai ki Acetylene option mein\nhone par historical MCQ context mein ise correct maana gaya. [Q8, Q9]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Hormones Full Mind Map\n● Source explanation ye bhi distinguish karta hai ki Acetylene natural plant hormone nahi hai aur Ethylene\njitna effective nahi; calcium carbide mein toxic arsenic/phosphorus traces ho sakte hain. Ethylene\nnatural ripening hormone hai. [Q8, Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Acetylene vs Ethylene — Source-Specific\n ▸Historical artificial-ripening MCQ answer = ACETYLENE (source/key framing). [Q8, Q9]\n ▸Natural phytohormone mainly responsible for fruit ripening = ETHYLENE. [Q10]\n ▸Source itself notes acetylene/calcium-carbide use restrictions and distinguishes it from natural ethylene. [Q8]\n6. Parthenocarpy — Seedless Tomato by Hormone Spray\n● Seedless tomato fruits flowers par hormones spray karke produce kiye ja sakte hain. Source\nparthenocarpy ko fertilization of ovules ke bina fruit production batata hai; Gibberellin, Auxin ya\nCytokinin flower spray se artificial parthenocarpy stimulate kar sakte hain. [Q11]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0319","t":"08.iv Plant Reproduction","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Reproduction Full Mind Map\n🌱 PLANT REPRODUCTION — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 8.iv · Plant Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Meiosis in Flower & Reproductive Parts\n2. Vegetative / Clonal Propagation — Basics, Gootee & Clonal Selection\n3. Sugarcane Propagation, Photoperiodism & Crop Rotation\n4. Buds, Stem Cutting, Grafting & Layering\n5. Flower Life Cycle — Embryo, Fruit, Seed, Wood & Starch\n6. Seed Germination — Water, Temperature & Oxygen\n7. Seed Dispersal — Censer Mechanism in Poppy\n8. Pollination — Geitonogamy, Agents & Dichogamy\n9. Hybrid Seed & Seed Multiplication Stages\n10. Crop Cytogenetics — Wheat Genome & Maize Endosperm\n11. Flowering Stimulus — Role of Leaves\n1. Meiosis in Flower & Reproductive Parts\n● Plants mein meiosis study karne ke liye anthers (परागकोश) best part hain. Meiosis ke baad pollen grains\nbante hain, jo immature male gametophyte hote hain; stamens male reproductive part aur carpels\nfemale reproductive part hote hain. [Q1]\n2. Vegetative / Clonal Propagation — Basics, Gootee & Clonal Selection\n● Vegetative/clonal propagation asexual reproduction hai: bulbs, corms, tubers, cuttings jaise vegetative\npropagules successive mitosis se genetically similar clonal population banate hain. Ye most of the year\npractice ho sakta hai; source ke mutabik viruses eliminate nahi hote, balki vegetative parts se transmit\nbhi ho sakte hain. [Q2]\n● Gootee = air layering / marcotting: parent plant se connected aerial stem par rooting karwa kar\nvegetative propagation ki jati hai. [Q3]\n● Clonal selection asexually propagated crops ke selection ka method hai; selected plants se naye clones\nbanaye jate hain. Source examples: potato, sugarcane aur banana. [Q8]\n● Vegetative propagation mein offspring ek parent se banta hai aur genetically parent jaisa hota hai; root,\nstem ya leaf jaise vegetative parts se naya plant develop ho sakta hai. Stem cutting source ka common\nartificial example hai. [Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Vegetative Propagation & Virus\n ▸Vegetative propagation → clonal population + most of the year possible. [Q2]\n ▸“Vegetative propagation virus ko eliminate karta hai” source ke according FALSE; viral disease vegetative\nparts se transfer ho sakti hai. [Q2]\n3. Sugarcane Propagation, Photoperiodism & Crop Rotation\n● Sugarcane bud-chip settlings nursery mein raise karke field mein transplant karne se seed material ki\nsaving hoti hai. Direct planting mein source ke mutabik many-budded setts ka germination single-\nbudded se better, aur bad weather mein larger setts ki survival better hoti hai; tissue-culture settlings bhi\nuse ho sakte hain. [Q4]\n● Photoperiodism ke context mein sugarcane ko source short-day plant batata hai; winter/shorter days\nmein flowering se link kiya gaya hai, saath hi quantitative short-day/intermediate daylength behavior\nnote kiya gaya hai. [Q5]\n● Crop rotation mein deep-rooted crop ke baad shallow-rooted crop rakhna chahiye; legume ke baad non-\nlegume useful hai kyunki fixed nitrogen ka effective use ho sakta hai. [Q6]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Reproduction Full Mind Map\n● Cereals ke saath pulses intercropping mein complementary crops act karte hain. Source A/R mein dono\nstatements true hain: pulses ka tap-root system cereals ke fibrous roots se different depth use karta hai,\nlekin Reason ko Assertion ka complete/correct explanation nahi maana gaya. [Q7]\n● Sugarcane predominantly stem cuttings se propagate hota hai; source contrast mein mango/cotton\ngenerally seeds se aur banana suckers se grow kiye jate hain. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Sugarcane Setts\n ▸Bud-chip nursery settlings → seed material ki substantial saving. [Q4]\n ▸Direct setts: many-budded germination better; bad weather mein large setts survival better — source\nstatements 2 & 3 ko incorrect mark karta hai. [Q4]\n4. Buds, Stem Cutting, Grafting & Layering\n● Plant bud ek undeveloped/embryonic shoot hai; usually leaf axil ya stem/branch tip par milta hai. Axillary\naur terminal buds ke form mein present hota hai. [Q9, Q16]\n● Stem cuttings se source examples mein Bougainvillea, Carnation, Cocoa aur Grapes sab propagate kiye\nja sakte hain; woody shrubs/ornamental plants mein ye popular method hai. [Q14]\n● Sweet orange grafting se aur Jasmine layering se propagate kiya jata hai. Layering mein stem/branch ka\npart soil mein bury karke roots/shoots develop karwaye jate hain; grafting mein do plants ke tissues join\nkarwaye jate hain. [Q15]\n5. Flower Life Cycle — Embryo, Fruit, Seed, Wood & Starch\n● Embryo seed ke andar milta hai; source ke mutabik embryo aur mother-plant derived other cells milkar\nnext generation ka seed banate hain, jo germination ke baad new plant develop karta hai. [Q10]\n● Source matching: Fruit → Ovary | Seed → Ovule | Wood → Stem (secondary xylem) | Starch → Leaf.\n[Q11]\n● Plant life cycle ke terms mein flower ko source most important part batata hai: male-female gametes ki\nunion mediate karta hai; sequence pollination → fertilization → seed formation → seed dispersal tak jata\nhai. [Q17]\n6. Seed Germination — Water, Temperature & Oxygen\n● Seed germination ke liye source ke according sabse necessary conditions hain: water + proper\ntemperature + oxygen. Sunlight essential nahi maana gaya. [Q18, Q19]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Germination Requirement\n ▸Water + suitable temperature + oxygen = essential conditions. [Q18]\n ▸Light/sunlight = generally NOT required in source question framing. [Q19]\n7. Seed Dispersal — Censer Mechanism in Poppy\n● Seed dispersal parent plant se seeds ko door le jane ki process hai. Censer mechanism poppy mein\nmilta hai: wind se capsule sway karta hai aur seeds censer ki tarah shake out hote hain. [Q20]\n8. Pollination — Geitonogamy, Agents & Dichogamy\n● Same plant ke ek flower ke anther se doosre flower ke stigma tak pollen transfer = Geitonogamy.\nFunctionally pollinating agent involve hone ki wajah se cross-pollination jaisa, lekin genetically same\nplant hone se autogamy jaisa hai. [Q21]\n● Pollination = pollen grains ka male anther se female stigma tak transfer; fertilization ke liye prerequisite\nhai. Source pollinating agents mein bat, bee aur bird — teeno ko include karta hai; bees ko particularly\nimportant bataya gaya hai. [Q22, Q23]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Reproduction Full Mind Map\n● Bisexual flower mein androecium aur gynoecium different times par mature hon to Dichogamy kehte\nhain; self-pollination reduce hota hai. Types: Protandry (male first) aur Protogyny (female first). [Q26]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Pollination Terms\n ▸Geitonogamy = same plant ke different flowers ke beech pollen transfer. [Q21]\n ▸Dichogamy = male & female reproductive parts ka different time par mature hona; Protandry / Protogyny. [Q26]\n9. Hybrid Seed & Seed Multiplication Stages\n● Har saal change kiya jane wala seed source ke according Hybrid seed hai, kyunki heterosis/hybrid\nvigour F1 generation mein strongest hota hai aur saved hybrid seed ki next generation segregate kar\nsakti hai. [Q24]\n● Seed multiplication ka source chronological order: Nucleus seed → Breeder seed → Foundation seed →\nCertified seed. [Q25]\n10. Crop Cytogenetics — Wheat Genome & Maize Endosperm\n● Commercial edible/bread wheat (Triticum aestivum) mein source ABD genome (AABBDD) batata hai; ise\nallohexaploid species explain kiya gaya hai. [Q27]\n● Maize mein 2n = 20, gamete n = 10; angiosperm endosperm triple fusion se triploid (3n) hota hai, isliye\nmaize endosperm mein 30 chromosomes hote hain. [Q28]\n11. Flowering Stimulus — Role of Leaves\n● Flowering stimulus receive karne wala plant component source ke according Leaves hain. Source\nexplanation light/energy/CO reception aur florigen production in leaves ko shoot apex tak transport\n₂\nhone se link karta hai. [Q29]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0320","t":"08.v Plant Economic Importance","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant: Economic Importance Full Mind Map\n🌿 PLANT: ECONOMIC IMPORTANCE — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 8.v · Plant Physiology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Important Crop Varieties & Botanical Names\n2. Medicinal, Industrial & Useful Plants\n3. Palm Oil, Canola, Moringa & Native Plants\n4. Biofuels, Petro-crops, Jatropha & Ethanol\n5. Chilgoza, Neem & Medicinal Plant Uses\n6. Caffeine — Cola, Tea & Coffee\n7. Seaweed, Spices, Oils & Plant Products\n8. Quinine, Cinchona & Anti-malarial Drugs\n9. Cork & Cotton\n10. Opium Poppy, Morphine, Heroin & Alkaloids\n11. Tapa Cloth — Moraceae\n12. Laminaria, Iodine & Goitre\n1. Important Crop Varieties & Botanical Names\n● Kanchan, Krishna aur Banarasi — Amla/Indian gooseberry ki improved varieties hain; Amla vitamin C\naur medicinal properties ke liye noted hai. [Q1]\n● Neelum × Alphonso mango cross se Ratna hybrid variety bani; source ise Maharashtra aur Karnataka ke\nkuch parts mein grown high-yielding mango batata hai. [Q2]\n● Kashi Lalima red okra/lady finger variety hai, IIVR Varanasi ke experts dwara developed; source\nantioxidants, calcium aur iron richness highlight karta hai. [Q3]\n● Co. 1148 eastern Uttar Pradesh ke liye important sugarcane variety hai; medium-thick canes, good\ngermination/tillering aur moderate drought resistance source features hain. [Q4]\n● Crop–variety match mein Mustard–Varuna, Field Pea–Sapna aur Groundnut–Kaushal correct hain;\nLinseed–Surya source ke mutabik incorrect pair hai. [Q5]\n● Macaroni wheat ka botanical name Triticum durum hai; source ise tetraploid wheat species batata hai.\n[Q6]\n2. Medicinal, Industrial & Useful Plants\n● Parthenium hysterophorus leaf extract source mein biologically synthesized nanoparticles/cancer-\ntreatment potential se linked hai aur anti-cancer medicinal attributes mention kiye gaye hain. [Q7]\n● Litmus acid-base indicator lichens se extracted water-soluble dyes ka mixture hai; filter paper par absorb\nkarke acidity/alkalinity test ki jati hai. [Q8]\n● Neem oil: pesticide/insect-mite control aur pharmaceutical uses — dono correct; hospital detergent\nmanufacture ke liye neem seeds wale statement ko source unsupported/incorrect maanta hai. [Q9]\n● Pine, Fir, Spruce, Cedar, Larch aur Cypress timber-yielding gymnosperms hain; source 'naked seeds'\nfeature ko contrast karta hai angiosperms ke enclosed ovules/seeds se. [Q10]\n● Mushrooms ke medicinal, psychoactive, insecticidal aur bioluminescent — chaaron properties source\nmein correct hain. [Q11]\n● Aloe vera medicinal crop hai; source antiviral/antibacterial properties aur medicinal/cosmetic use\nmention karta hai. [Q12]\n● Tulsi (Ocimum tenuiflorum / O. sanctum) ki medicinal value source ke mutabik phenols aur flavonoids\n\nसहितsecondary metabolites se linked hai. [Q13]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant: Economic Importance Full Mind Map\n3. Palm Oil, Canola, Moringa & Native Plants\n● Palm oil ke source statements mein lipstick/perfume industry use aur biodiesel use correct hain; principal\nAfrican oil palm Elaeis guineensis West/Southwest Africa native hai, isliye Southeast Asia-native\nstatement incorrect hai. [Q14]\n● Source ke National Policy on Biofuels-2018 framing mein biofuel raw materials: cassava, damaged\nwheat grains, rotten potatoes aur sugar beet; groundnut seeds aur horse gram listed nahi. [Q15]\n● Canola = human consumption ke liye bred oilseed mustard/rapeseed type; key feature source mein very\nlow erucic acid content hai. [Q16]\n● Moringa source ke mutabik leguminous nahi; tamarind South Asia endemic nahi. Correct statements:\nIndia mein tamarind largely minor forest produce ke roop mein collect hota hai, India tamarind/moringa\nseeds export karta hai, aur dono ke seeds biofuel production mein use ho sakte hain. [Q17]\n● Cashew, Papaya aur Red Sanders mein source ke mutabik sirf Red Sanders India-native/endemic hai;\ncashew Brazil aur papaya tropical America origin se linked hain. [Q18]\n4. Biofuels, Petro-crops, Jatropha & Ethanol\n● Fourth-generation biofuels genetically modified microorganisms—source example algae, yeast, fungus\naur cyanobacteria—se banaye ja sakte hain; question answer GM algae hai. [Q19]\n● Pongam/Pongamia pinnata ek leguminous petroplant hai; seeds se oil milta hai jo biodiesel use se linked\nhai. [Q20]\n● Petro-crops hydrocarbons aur lipids se rich hote hain; source Jatropha ko petro-crop example deta hai.\n[Q21]\n● Source ke historical question ke mutabik India ka first biodiesel plant Kakinada, Andhra Pradesh mein\nestablish hua. [Q22]\n● Jatropha curcas ko bio-diesel plant / future biodiesel feedstock kaha gaya hai; harsh environment mein\ngrow, non-edible crop aur seeds biodiesel ke liye use hote hain. [Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Sugarcane juice/molasses fermentation se ethanol biofuel milta hai; molasses ko source power alcohol\nka excellent raw material batata hai. [Q26, Q27]\n5. Chilgoza, Neem & Medicinal Plant Uses\n● Chilgoza Pinus gerardiana (pine) ke seeds se milta hai; source carbohydrate aur protein richness\nmention karta hai. [Q28]\n● Chief mosquito repellent source answer Neem/Margo hai; neem ke seeds/leaves medicinal use se linked\nhain. [Q29]\n● Medicinal-use matching: Brahmi → Brain tonic | Sadabahar → Anti-diabetic | Pudina → Carminative |\nTulsi → Expectorant. [Q30]\n6. Caffeine — Cola, Tea & Coffee\n● Cola-type soft drinks mein significant caffeine hota hai; caffeine xanthine alkaloid stimulant hai. [Q31]\n● Caffeine naturally tea aur coffee dono mein milta hai; source cocoa/cola/soft drinks bhi mention karta\nhai. [Q32]\n● Tea leaves ka most important stimulant caffeine hai; source ise widely consumed CNS\nstimulant/psychoactive drug batata hai. [Q33]\n7. Seaweed, Spices, Oils & Plant Products\n● Seaweeds iodine ka important/rich natural source hain. [Q34]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant: Economic Importance Full Mind Map\n● Camphor, Chicory aur Vanilla — source ke mutabik teeno plant products hain: camphor laurel wood,\nchicory root use, aur Vanilla orchids se flavour. [Q35]\n● Kuttu flour Buckwheat/Fagopyrum esculentum se milta hai; source ise pseudocereal batata hai. [Q36]\n● Saffron Crocus sativus flower ke stigma/styles ('threads') se banta hai. [Q37]\n● Peppermint/Mentha arvensis mein oil ka maximum source answer leaf hai; peppermint/menthol oil\nleaves ki steam distillation se banta hai. [Q38]\n● Source Q39 ka answer Asafoetida/Hing hai; explanation ke mutabik ye Ferula species ka dried oleo-gum\nresin hai jo rhizome aur fleshy tap roots se extracted hota hai. [Q39]\n● Product–source match: Opium → Fruit | Hing → Root | Rubber → Stem | Quinine → Bark. [Q40]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Hing / Asafoetida Source Question\n ▸Q41 mein source 'Multiple Correct Answers (Ans. A & B)' mark karta hai: stem exudation aur roots extraction\ndono accepted; explanation rhizome (modified stem) + fleshy tap roots se dried sap/oleo-gum resin batata hai.\n[Q41]\n8. Quinine, Cinchona & Anti-malarial Drugs\n● Quinine malaria drug Cinchona tree se milta hai; Cinchona source ke mutabik angiosperm hai. [Q42]\n● Quinine ka source part Cinchona bark/stem bark hai — ye same fact multiple exam questions mein\nrepeat hua hai. [Q43, Q44, Q45, Q46]\n● Arteether medicine ko source seeded plant Artemisia annua se obtained batata hai; malaria Plasmodium\nparasite se linked hai. [Q47]\n● Natural quinine ke replacement ke roop mein source synthetic drug Chloroquine batata hai. [Q48]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Hydroxychloroquine\n ▸Q49 source mein disputed/wrong question hai: hydroxychloroquine kisi plant bark se obtained nahi;\nexplanation ise synthetic drug batata hai, Cinchona-derived natural quinine se alag. [Q49]\n9. Cork & Cotton\n● Cork oak Quercus suber ki bark se cork milta hai; source Mediterranean origin aur waxy cork cells\nmention karta hai. [Q50]\n● Cotton ka major component cellulose hai; source chemical composition mein cellulose ~91% diya gaya\nhai. [Q51]\n10. Opium Poppy, Morphine, Heroin & Alkaloids\n● Noscapine poppy (Papaver somniferum) se milta hai aur source ise benzylisoquinoline alkaloid batata\nhai. [Q52]\n● Heroin opium poppy se obtained hoti hai; opium latex ke morphine ko chemically process karke heroin\nban sakti hai. [Q53]\n● Morphine source ke mutabik poppy ke unripe fruit se acquired hoti hai aur CNS par directly act karti hai.\n[Q54]\n● Opium = unripe poppy fruit/capsule se milne wala dried milky latex; shallow cuts se latex collect kiya jata\nhai. [Q55, Q56]\n● Opium ka main constituent source mein ~12% morphine diya hai. [Q57]\n● Opium poppy ka botanical name Papaver somniferum hai; immature capsule latex se opium aur\nmorphine/codeine/papaverine jaise alkaloids milte hain. [Q58]\n● Opium depressant/sedative narcotic drug category mein hai; Morphine narcotic analgesic drug hai. [Q59,\nQ60]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant: Economic Importance Full Mind Map\n11. Tapa Cloth — Moraceae\n● Tapa/bark cloth Moraceae family ke plants—source examples mulberry aur fig—ki softened inner bark\nse banaya jata hai. [Q61]\n12. Laminaria, Iodine & Goitre\n● Iodine Laminaria se obtained hota hai; Laminaria brown algae/kelp seaweed hai aur source\niron/potassium richness bhi mention karta hai. [Q62]\n● Iodine sea mein abundantly available substance hai aur iodine-deficiency goitre ko prevent/treat karne\nke context mein administered hota hai. [Q63]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0321","t":"09.i Viral Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Viral Diseases Full Mind Map\n🦠 VIRAL DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.i · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Virus Basics — Pathogens, Genome, Bacteriophage & Virion\n2. Coronavirus, COVID-19 & Vaccine Platforms\n3. Mosquito-borne Viral Diseases — Dengue, Yellow Fever & Wolbachia\n4. Rabies, Meningitis, Rotavirus & Pandemic Terms\n5. Polio — Transmission, Salk Vaccine & OPV\n6. Common Cold, Pneumonia & Hepatitis\n7. Smallpox — Eradication\n8. HIV/AIDS — Transmission, Immunity, Testing & Treatment\n9. Japanese Encephalitis & Measles\n10. Animal Viral Diseases — Ranikhet, FMD & Rinderpest\n11. Bird Flu, Swine Flu, Zika, Ebola & Nipah\n1. Virus Basics — Pathogens, Genome, Bacteriophage & Virion\n● Disease-causing microorganism ko pathogen kehte hain; source pathogens mein virus, bacterium,\nprotozoan, prion, viroid aur fungus jaise infectious agents include karta hai. [Q1]\n● Virus ka nucleic-acid genome DNA ya RNA ho sakta hai; source ke mutabik DNA viruses ko 'usually\nsingle-stranded' kehna incorrect hai, kyunki dsDNA aur ssDNA dono types milte hain. [Q2]\n● Bacteriophage = bacteria ko infect karne wala virus; viral outer covering protein ki hoti hai aur nucleic\nacid DNA/RNA present hota hai. [Q3]\n● Viruses mein energy-generation ke liye required enzymes/system absent hota hai, living cells ke andar\nreplicate karte hain, synthetic medium mein culture nahi hote aur air/water/food/insects/contact jaise\nmultiple routes se transmit ho sakte hain; independent viral particle ko virion kehte hain. [Q4]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Virus & Enzymes\n ▸Q5 ka source answer 'None of the above/More than one' hai: virus host-cell enzymes par depend kar sakta\nhai aur kuch viral particles mein reverse transcriptase, RNA-dependent RNA polymerase, integrase ya\nneuraminidase jaise enzymes bhi ho sakte hain. [Q5]\n2. Coronavirus, COVID-19 & Vaccine Platforms\n● ACE2 cell-surface protein/receptor hai jo kuch coronaviruses—SARS-CoV aur SARS-CoV-2\n—\nसहित\nke\ncell entry point ke roop mein source mein described hai. [Q6]\n● Coronavirus group se SARS, MERS aur COVID-19 linked hain; COVID-19 pandemic SARS-CoV-2 se\ncaused hua. [Q7, Q8]\n● COVID vaccine platforms: Covishield aur Sputnik V = non-replicating viral-vector vaccines; Covaxin =\nwhole-virion inactivated SARS-CoV-2 vaccine; Pfizer-BioNTech/Moderna = mRNA platform. [Q9, Q13]\n● Covishield Serum Institute of India manufacture karta hai; source regimen mein 0.5 ml each dose diya\nhai. Sputnik V Russia-developed/exported vaccine hai. [Q10, Q11, Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Source-specific COVID Vaccine Key\n ▸Q14 mein source correct answer 'live attenuated SARS-CoV-2 virus introduce karke immune response\nstimulate karna' mark karta hai; is mind map mein isi source-key ko preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q14]\n ▸Vector vaccines modified version of a different harmless virus ko vector bana kar antigen instructions cells tak\npahunchate hain. [Q15]\n3. Mosquito-borne Viral Diseases — Dengue, Yellow Fever & Wolbachia\n● Wolbachia method Aedes aegypti mosquitoes mein dengue, chikungunya aur Zika jaise viruses ki\ngrowth/transmission reduce karne ke context mein use hota hai. [Q16]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Viral Diseases Full Mind Map\n● Dengue viral disease hai jo infected female Aedes mosquito ke bite se transmit hota hai; dengue mein\nplatelets rapidly decrease ho sakte hain. [Q17, Q18, Q19, Q20]\n● Dengue symptoms source mein high fever, headache, retro-orbital pain, joint/muscle pain, skin rash aur\nnose/gum bleeding include karte hain; statement set mein only statement 3 correct hai. [Q21]\n● Dengue bacterial disease nahi hai. Yellow fever bhi viral disease hai aur female Aedes aegypti bite se\nspread hota hai. [Q22, Q23]\n● Tiger mosquito/Aedes albopictus yellow fever, dengue aur chikungunya transmit kar sakta hai; Japanese\nencephalitis tiger mosquito se nahi, Culex species se linked hai. [Q24]\n4. Rabies, Meningitis, Rotavirus & Pandemic Terms\n● Hydrophobia rabies ka old name hai; rabies viral disease nervous system ko affect karti hai. [Q25]\n● Meningitis = brain aur spinal cord ko cover karne wali meninges ki inflammation; source viruses, bacteria\nya other microorganisms ko possible causes batata hai. [Q26]\n● Rotavirus double-stranded RNA virus hai aur infants/young children mein severe diarrhoea ka major\ncause source mein diya hai. [Q27]\n● Pandemic = infectious disease ka bahut large region/multiple continents/worldwide spread; epidemic\nlocal population mein short period ka large outbreak, endemic regular localized presence aur epizootic\nanimals ke regional outbreak ke liye use hota hai. [Q28]\n● Mumps, Rabies aur Herpes — source question ke set mein teeno viral diseases hain. [Q29]\n5. Polio — Transmission, Salk Vaccine & OPV\n● Poliovirus contaminated/polluted food aur water ke through body mein enter kar sakta hai; polio viral\ninfection hai aur CNS ko affect kar sakta hai. [Q30, Q31]\n● Polio vaccine source mein Jonas/Jones Salk se connected hai; Salk vaccine specifically Polio ke liye hai.\n[Q32, Q33, Q34]\n● Government of India ne trivalent OPV ki jagah bivalent OPV switch kiya; source ke mutabik trivalent\ntypes 1,2,3 aur bivalent types 1,3 cover karta hai. [Q35]\n6. Common Cold, Pneumonia & Hepatitis\n● Common cold ka predominant pathogen Rhinovirus hai. Pneumonia lungs ki infection hai aur source\nviruses, bacteria aur fungi ko possible causes batata hai. [Q36, Q37]\n● Hepatitis B water contamination se caused nahi maana gaya; HBV blood/blood-contaminated fluids aur\nmother-to-child route se transmit ho sakta hai. [Q38]\n● Hepatitis-B virus partially double-stranded DNA virus hai; hepatitis directly liver ko affect karta hai aur\nhepatitis viral disease group se linked hai. [Q39, Q40, Q42, Q43]\n● Hepatitis B ka vaccine available hai, jabki source ke mutabik Hepatitis C ka vaccine nahi; isliye opposite\nstatement incorrect hai. [Q41]\n● Source matching question mein Polio–Monkey incorrect pair hai; polio person-to-person/fecal-oral route\nse linked hai, monkeys se nahi. [Q44]\n7. Smallpox — Eradication\n● Given diseases Diphtheria, Chickenpox aur Smallpox mein source ke mutabik India se eradicated\ndisease only Smallpox hai; India smallpox-free 1977. [Q45]\n● Smallpox Variola virus se caused tha; WHO ne global eradication 1980 mein certify ki. [Q46]\n● Source Assertion–Reason: Smallpox viral aur highly contagious tha, close-contact droplet spread ke\nkaran patient ka separate bed justified; A aur R dono correct aur reason assertion par based hai. [Q47]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Viral Diseases Full Mind Map\n8. HIV/AIDS — Transmission, Immunity, Testing & Treatment\n● AIDS bacterial disease nahi; HIV virus se caused hota hai. HIV sexual intercourse, contaminated\nblood/blood transfusion aur mother-to-child/placental route se transmit ho sakta hai, mosquito bite se\nnahi. [Q48, Q49, Q50, Q53, Q54, Q56, Q57]\n● AIDS = Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome. HIV T-helper/T-4 lymphocytes ko damage karta hai, jis\nse immune system profoundly affected hota hai. [Q51, Q55]\n● Source AIDS symptoms list mein swollen lymph nodes, night sweating, memory loss aur weight loss —\nall four included hain. [Q52]\n● HIV retrovirus hai; viral core mein RNA + proteins/enzymes such as reverse transcriptase, protease aur\nintegrase hote hain. Adenovirus dsDNA genome wala hai; common cold kabhi adenovirus se ho sakta\nhai. [Q58, Q59, Q60]\n● Unsterilized tattooing se Hepatitis B aur HIV-AIDS transmit ho sakte hain; Chikungunya is route se nahi.\n[Q61]\n● India mein source ke mutabik predominant strain HIV-1 subtype C (HIV-1C) hai; HTLV-III AIDS virus\ndiscovery Robert Gallo se linked hai. [Q62, Q63]\n● AIDS treatment context mein source Zidovudine/Azidothymidine (AZT) ko frequently used antiretroviral\nmedicine batata hai; ELISA HIV/AIDS screening test se linked hai. [Q64, Q65]\n9. Japanese Encephalitis & Measles\n● Japanese encephalitis brain infection hai, JEV virus se caused aur mosquitoes se spread hoti hai;\ndomestic pigs/wild birds reservoirs hain, isliye pigs ko human settlements se door rakhna control context\nmein useful bataya gaya hai. [Q66, Q67, Q68]\n● Measles viral disease hai, isliye antibiotics ise cure nahi karte; source question mein leprosy, tetanus aur\ncholera bacterial comparison ke roop mein diye gaye hain. [Q69, Q70]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — No Correct Option in Source\n ▸Q71 mein AIDS, Chickenpox, Mumps aur Herpes Simplex sab infectious viral diseases diye gaye hain; source\nexplicitly kehta hai ki listed options mein koi correct 'not infectious' answer nahi hai. [Q71]\n10. Animal Viral Diseases — Ranikhet, FMD & Rinderpest\n● Ranikhet/Newcastle disease chicken/poultry ki highly infectious viral disease hai. [Q72]\n● Milching animals ke set mein Foot-and-mouth disease, Anthrax, Black Quarter aur Cowpox — source ke\nmutabik chaaron infectious diseases hain; FMD/Cowpox viral, Anthrax/Black Quarter bacterial. [Q73]\n● Foot-and-mouth disease Aphthovirus se caused viral disease hai aur cloven-hoofed animals—cattle,\nsheep, goat, pig etc.—mein mainly milti hai. [Q74, Q75]\n● Rinderpest/cattle plague contagious viral livestock disease thi aur 2011 mein eradicated declare hui.\n[Q76]\n11. Bird Flu, Swine Flu, Zika, Ebola & Nipah\n● Bird flu/avian influenza H5N1 virus se linked hai; source ke multiple questions H5N1 ↔ Bird Flu relation\nrepeat karte hain. [Q77, Q78, Q79]\n● H1N1 virus Swine Flu se linked hai; source 2009 detection aur human-to-human cough/sneeze spread\nmention karta hai. [Q80]\n● Zika mainly Aedes genus—especially Aedes aegypti—se transmit hota hai, wahi mosquito\ndengue/chikungunya/yellow fever bhi transmit karta hai; sexual transmission bhi possible hai. [Q81]\n● Ebola virus–Smallpox incorrect match hai; Ebola deadly viral disease hai aur iska naam Democratic\nRepublic of Congo ki Ebola River se derived hai. [Q82, Q83, Q84]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Viral Diseases Full Mind Map\n● Nipah virus outbreak May 2018 mein source Kerala (Kozhikode) se linked karta hai; disease Nipah virus\nse caused hai aur naam Malaysia ke Sungai Nipah village se associated hai. [Q85]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0322","t":"09.ii Bacterial Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Bacterial Diseases Full Mind Map\n🧫 BACTERIAL DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.ii · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Food Poisoning — Salmonella & Botulism\n2. Anthrax, Diphtheria & DPT Vaccine\n3. Haemophilus Influenzae & Pneumococcal Vaccine\n4. Tuberculosis — Cause, Test, BCG & Treatment\n5. Tetanus, Plague & Transmission Routes\n6. Dental Caries & Water-borne Diseases\n7. Leprosy & Typhoid\n8. Antibiotics — Waksman, Penicillin & Broad Spectrum\n9. Sulpha Drugs & Antibacterial Agents\n10. Multi-drug Resistance (MDR)\n1. Food Poisoning — Salmonella & Botulism\n● Food poisoning source mein Salmonella bacilli se linked hai; Salmonella intestinal bacterial infection\ngroup hai aur contaminated food/water se spread ho sakta hai. [Q1]\n● Botulism Clostridium species—especially Clostridium botulinum—ke toxin se linked serious bacterial\nillness hai; improperly canned/preserved food aur wounds source routes mein diye gaye hain. [Q2]\n● Botulism ko food-borne intoxication kaha gaya hai; toxin nerves ko affect karke breathing difficulty,\nmuscle paralysis aur severe cases mein death tak cause kar sakta hai. [Q3]\n2. Anthrax, Diphtheria & DPT Vaccine\n● Splenic fever = Anthrax; source ise bacterial infection batata hai jo livestock ko affect kar sakta hai aur\nhumans mein bhi transmit ho sakta hai. [Q4]\n● Diphtheria vaccine toxoid type ki vaccine hai aur disease Corynebacterium diphtheriae se linked hai. [Q5]\n● DPT ka full protective set = Diphtheria + Pertussis (Whooping Cough) + Tetanus; source ke multiple\nquestions isi triple-antigen combination ko repeat karte hain. [Q6, Q7, Q8, Q10]\n● DPT vaccine Polio ke liye use nahi hoti. [Q9]\n3. Haemophilus Influenzae & Pneumococcal Vaccine\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Haemophilus influenzae — Multiple Correct\n ▸Q11 mein source correct answers A & D deta hai: Haemophilus influenzae young children mein meningitis aur\npneumonia dono cause kar sakta hai. Influenza virus se hota hai aur whooping cough Bordetella pertussis se.\n[Q11]\n● Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccine Streptococcus pneumoniae diseases se protection ke liye hai; source\nmeningitis, sepsis aur bacteremic pneumonia ke against effectiveness aur antibiotic-resistant disease\nburden reduction mention karta hai. Statements 1 & 2 correct, statement 3 incorrect because side\neffects/allergic reactions possible hain. [Q12]\n4. Tuberculosis — Cause, Test, BCG & Treatment\n● Measles, Rabies aur Polio viral diseases hain, jabki Tuberculosis bacterial disease hai aur source\nMycobacterium tuberculosis ko cause batata hai. [Q13, Q18, Q19]\n● Source ke mutabik P-amino salicylic acid antimicrobial drug tuberculosis aur leprosy dono ke treatment\nmein suitable hai. [Q14]\n● WHO-context questions mein Tuberculosis ko present-time major cause of death aur India mein lakhs of\nannual deaths se linked disease bataya gaya hai. [Q15, Q16]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Bacterial Diseases Full Mind Map\n● Genetic disease–Tuberculosis incorrect match hai; source TB ko bacterial disease batata hai, genetic\ndisease nahi. [Q17]\n● TB detection ke liye source spelling 'Montoux Test' deta hai; explanation ise Tuberculin Skin Test/TST ke\ncontext mein describe karta hai. [Q20]\n● BCG (Bacillus Calmette-Guerin) vaccine Tuberculosis prevention ke liye hai; source newborn ko just\nafter birth inoculation best batata hai aur up to 12 months possible hone ka note deta hai. [Q21, Q22, Q23]\n● Matching question mein Malaria–Chloroquine correct pair hai; source BCG→TB, ATS→Tetanus aur\nScurvy→Vitamin C context bhi explain karta hai. [Q24]\n5. Tetanus, Plague & Transmission Routes\n● Tetanus Clostridium tetani bacterial disease hai aur 'Lock jaw' naam se bhi known hai; wound entry ke\nbaad toxin painful muscle tightening aur jaw/neck locking cause kar sakta hai. [Q25]\n● Plague infected mosquito bite se caused nahi; source Yersinia pestis ko cause aur infected fleas/rodents\nko transmission chain batata hai. [Q26]\n● Transmission match: Air→T.B.; Water→Cholera; Contact→Syphilis; Wound→Tetanus. [Q27]\n● Disease-feature match: Plague→flea-bites; Filaria→mosquitoes; Beri-beri→Vitamin B deficiency;\nTyphoid→intestines. [Q28]\n6. Dental Caries & Water-borne Diseases\n● Tooth decay/caries mainly mouth bacteria + fermentable carbohydrate food particles ke interaction se\nlinked hai; source caries formation mein tooth surface, bacteria, carbohydrates aur time ko key factors\nbatata hai. [Q29]\n● Dental caries ka reason source mein bacterial infection diya hai. [Q30]\n● Shallow handpump-water question mein source Cholera, Typhoid aur Jaundice risk batata hai, jabki\nFluorosis ko excess fluoride condition aur exception mark karta hai. [Q31]\n● Cholera Vibrio cholerae bacterial intestinal disease hai aur contaminated water/food se spread hota hai;\nTyphoid aur Cholera typical water-borne diseases diye gaye hain. [Q32, Q33]\n7. Leprosy & Typhoid\n● Leprosy/Hansen's disease bacterial disease hai; source Mycobacterium leprae ya Mycobacterium\nlepromatosis ko causes batata hai. [Q34]\n● Typhoid Salmonella typhi bacteria se caused hai; source question mein Jaundice, Influenza aur Mumps\nko viral association ke contrast mein diya gaya hai. [Q35]\n8. Antibiotics — Waksman, Penicillin & Broad Spectrum\n● 'Antibiotic' term source ke mutabik Selman Waksman ne 1942 mein coin kiya; Waksman streptomycin\naur several antibiotics discovery se bhi linked hai. [Q36]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — More Than One Antibiotic\n ▸Q37 source answer (E) More than one: Sulphaguanidine aur Chloramphenicol dono antibacterial/antibiotic\nagents diye gaye hain. [Q37]\n ▸Q38 source answer (E) More than one: Penicillin aur Sulphadiazine dono antibiotic agents diye gaye hain.\n[Q38]\n● Penicillin ek well-known antibiotic medicine hai. [Q39]\n● Chloramphenicol source mein broad-spectrum antibiotic hai—Gram-positive aur Gram-negative dono\nbacteria ke wide range par act karta hai aur serious infections including typhoid context mein mentioned\nhai. [Q40]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Bacterial Diseases Full Mind Map\n9. Sulpha Drugs & Antibacterial Agents\n● Sulfa drugs bacteria-caused diseases ke against effective aur primarily antibacterial class ke drugs hain;\nsource sulfonamide examples aur Prontosil ko first sulfa drug (1932) mention karta hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● Cibazole source mein short-acting sulpha drug hai; Penicillin/Streptomycin antibiotics aur Aspirin\nantipyretic comparison ke roop mein diye gaye hain. [Q43]\n10. Multi-drug Resistance (MDR)\n● India mein microbial multi-drug resistance ke source-listed reasons mein incorrect antibiotic doses aur\nlivestock farming mein antibiotics ka use include hain; given statements mein 2 & 3 correct hain. [Q44]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0323","t":"09.iii Fungal Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Fungal Diseases Full Mind Map\n🍄 FUNGAL DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.iii · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Mucormycosis — Black Fungus & Zoonotic Disease\n2. Ergotism — Contaminated Grains\n3. Athlete's Foot — Tinea Pedis\n4. Fungal Skin Disorders — Dermatitis & Baldness\n5. Aflatoxin — Aspergillus, Penicillium & Liver\n1. Mucormycosis — Black Fungus & Zoonotic Disease\n● Zoonotic disease wo infectious disease hoti hai jo pathogen ke through animal se human mein jump karti\nhai. Source mein Rabies, Plague aur SARS zoonotic diye gaye hain, jabki Mucormycosis zoonotic nahi\nhai. [Q1]\n● Mucormycosis (pehle zygomycosis) serious but rare fungal infection hai jo mucormycetes group ke\nmolds se hota hai; ise Black Fungus bhi kaha gaya hai. Ye molds environment mein widely present hote\nhain. [Q1]\n● Source ke mutabik Mucormycosis mainly un logon ko affect karta hai jinki disease-fighting capacity\nhealth problems ya medicines ki wajah se kam ho. Commonly nose, sinuses, eye aur brain affect ho\nsakte hain; lungs, stomach-intestines aur skin bhi involve ho sakte hain. [Q1]\n2. Ergotism — Contaminated Grains\n● Ergotism contaminated grains ke consumption se hota hai. Source ise long-term ergot poisoning batata\nhai jo Claviceps purpurea fungus ke alkaloids ke ingestion se linked hai; ye fungus rye aur other cereals\nko infect karta hai. [Q2]\n3. Athlete's Foot — Tinea Pedis\n● Athlete's Foot (Tinea pedis) fungal disease hai. Source Trichophyton, Epidermophyton aur Microsporum\nki species ko causative fungi ke examples deta hai. Infection generally toes ke beech hota hai. [Q3]\n● Statement-based question mein Femur longest human bone aur Cholera bacterial disease—dono\ncorrect hain; 'Athlete's foot virus se hota hai' statement incorrect hai because source ise fungal infection\nbatata hai. Isliye statements 1 & 2 correct hain. [Q4]\n4. Fungal Skin Disorders — Dermatitis & Baldness\n● Source ke according Seborrheic dermatitis fungi se caused disease hai aur scalp, face aur torso ko\naffect karne wala inflammatory skin disorder hai. Polio viral aur Cholera bacterial disease diye gaye\nhain. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Source-Specific Answer — Baldness\n ▸Q6 mein source ka marked answer 'Baldness' hai aur explanation ise fungal disease ke roop mein state karta\nhai; isi source framing ko mind map mein preserve kiya gaya hai. AIDS ko HIV infection aur Colour blindness\nko genetic disorder bataya gaya hai. [Q6]\n5. Aflatoxin — Aspergillus, Penicillium & Liver\n● Aflatoxin food adulterant/toxin ka major target organ source mein Liver diya gaya hai. Aspergillus aur\nPenicillium ki kuch fungal species aflatoxins produce karti hain jo food ko toxic bana sakte hain. [Q7]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0324","t":"09.iv Parasitic Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parasitic Diseases Full Mind Map\n🦟 PARASITIC DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.iv · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Malaria — Organ, Vector & Protozoan Basics\n2. Malignant Malaria & Plasmodium Species\n3. Malaria Discovery, Treatment & Vaccines\n4. Filariasis — Nematodes & Mosquito Vectors\n5. Disease–Pathogen / Vector Matching\n6. Sleeping Sickness — Trypanosoma & Tse-tse Fly\n7. Unsafe Water, Sanitation & Communicable Diseases\n8. Taeniasis & Neurocysticercosis\n1. Malaria — Organ, Vector & Protozoan Basics\n● Malaria Plasmodium parasite se linked hai aur source female Anopheles mosquito ko iska carrier batata\nhai. Malaria mein spleen (pleeha) enlarge ho sakti hai aur source ise most affected organ batata hai;\nQuinine traditional treatment drug ke roop mein mention hai. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Source ke according Anopheles mosquitoes malaria ke alawa kuch regions mein encephalitis aur\nfilariasis ke vectors bhi ho sakte hain; filariasis ke other important vectors mein Culex aur Aedes bhi\nmention hain. [Q4]\n● Malaria aur Dengue dono mein fever aur mosquito-bite transmission common context hai, lekin mosquito\nspecies same nahi: Malaria → female Anopheles; Dengue → female Aedes aegypti. [Q7]\n● Malaria protozoan disease hai: causative parasite = Plasmodium. Isliye “insect parasite se caused”\nstatement source question mein false hai; source mosquitoes se spread, swampy-region association aur\nchloroquine treatment ko correct statements batata hai. [Q8, Q9, Q10]\n2. Malignant Malaria & Plasmodium Species\n● Malignant/severe malaria ka causative species source mein Plasmodium falciparum diya hai; ye severe\nhuman infectious disease aur higher death-risk se linked hai. [Q5, Q6]\n● Source ke mutabik Plasmodium vivax recurring malaria ka frequent/widely distributed cause hai aur India\nke about 65% malaria cases ke liye responsible bataya gaya hai; Asia aur South America ke context\nmein bhi 65% figure mention hai. [Q11]\n3. Malaria Discovery, Treatment & Vaccines\n● Source Q12 ka answer Sir Ronald Ross hai; explanation mein British Indian Army doctor ke roop mein\nfemale Anopheles mosquito mein Plasmodium oocysts observe karna aur malaria work ke liye 1902\nNobel Prize milna mention hai. [Q12]\n● R21/Matrix-M malaria vaccine Jenner Institute, Oxford University aur Serum Institute of India\ncollaboration se developed batayi gayi hai, Novavax saponin-based adjuvant technology ke saath.\nSource ke according October 2023 mein WHO recommendation mili aur ye children ke use ke liye\nsecond malaria vaccine hai; RTS,S/AS01 (Mosquirix) first WHO-approved malaria vaccine diya hai. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Source-Specific Malaria Key\n ▸Q12 ka wording “malaria is caused by Plasmodium parasite” ki discovery Sir Ronald Ross se map karta hai;\nmind map source ke marked answer aur explanation ko exactly preserve karta hai. [Q12]\n4. Filariasis — Nematodes & Mosquito Vectors\n● Filariasis thread-like nematodes/filariae se caused parasitic infection hai. Source female Culex mosquito\nse person-to-person spread, edema ko common symptom aur severe swelling/thickened skin ko\nelephantiasis se link karta hai. [Q14]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Parasitic Diseases Full Mind Map\n● Vector–Disease–Pathogen set mein Aedes–Chikungunya–Bacteria incorrect hai, kyunki source\nChikungunya ko Aedes-transmitted viral disease batata hai. Culex–Lymphatic Filariasis–Parasite,\nAnopheles–Malaria–Parasite aur Aedes–Dengue–Virus correct sets hain. [Q15]\n5. Disease–Pathogen / Vector Matching\n● Correct match: Malaria → Protozoan; Poliomyelitis → Virus; Tuberculosis → Bacteria; Ringworm →\nFungi. [Q16]\n● Source mapping: Plague → Bacteria; AIDS → Virus; Baldness → Fungus; Malaria → Protozoa. [Q17]\n● Another source match: Peptic ulcers → Bacteria; Dengue → Virus; Elephant Foot → Worm; Malaria →\nProtozoa. [Q18]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Source-Specific Matching\n ▸Q17 mein source “Baldness → Fungus” mapping deta hai; isi source-key ko yahan preserve kiya gaya hai.\n[Q17]\n6. Sleeping Sickness — Trypanosoma & Tse-tse Fly\n● Sleeping sickness / human African trypanosomiasis Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense aur T. brucei\ngambiense jaise unicellular parasites se caused hoti hai aur infected tse-tse fly (Glossina) ke bite se\nspread hoti hai. [Q19]\n● Sleeping sickness mosquito-borne disease nahi hai. Source comparison mein Dengue, Filariasis aur\nMalaria mosquito-borne diye gaye hain, jabki sleeping sickness tse-tse fly se transmit hoti hai. [Q20]\n7. Unsafe Water, Sanitation & Communicable Diseases\n● Source question unsafe drinking water aur lack of sanitation ke context mein developing countries ki\nthree main communicable diseases ko Malaria, Acute diarrhoea aur Schistosomiasis ke roop mein list\nkarta hai. [Q21]\n8. Taeniasis & Neurocysticercosis\n● Taeniasis intestinal tapeworm infection hai. Source three human species deta hai: Taenia solium (pork\ntapeworm), Taenia saginata (beef tapeworm) aur Taenia asiatica (Asian tapeworm); major health\nproblems especially T. solium se linked hain. [Q22]\n● T. solium eggs/larval cysts (cysticerci) various organs mein develop ho sakte hain; central nervous\nsystem, especially brain/spinal cord, involve hone par neurocysticercosis (NCC) aur neurological\nsymptoms including epileptic seizures ho sakte hain. [Q22]\n● Leander Paes 2003 case mein source brain problem ka answer “a cyst” deta hai; explanation common\nIndian brain lesion ko cysticercus granuloma—tapeworm ke larval form—se link karti hai. [Q23]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0325","t":"09.v Genetic Disorders","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Disorders Full Mind Map\n🧬 GENETIC DISORDERS — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.v · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Genetic vs Non-Genetic Disorders\n2. Phenylketonuria (PKU) — Inborn Error of Metabolism\n3. Bubble Baby Disease — SCID\n4. Haemophilia — Sex-Linked Hereditary Disorder\n5. Down Syndrome — Trisomy 21\n6. X-Linked Disorders & Muscular Dystrophy\n7. Disease-Type Matching\n8. Colour Blindness — X-Linked Inheritance\n9. Thalassemia — Haemoglobin & Blood Disorder\n1. Genetic vs Non-Genetic Disorders\n● Source ke according Night blindness genetic disease nahi hai; iska cause Vitamin A deficiency diya hai.\nAlbinism, Haemophilia aur Colour blindness ko genetic diseases bataya gaya hai. [Q1]\n● Another source comparison mein Down syndrome, Haemophilia aur Sickle Cell Anaemia\nhereditary/genetic disorders hain, jabki Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) ko genetic disorder nahi bataya\ngaya hai. [Q10]\n2. Phenylketonuria (PKU) — Inborn Error of Metabolism\n● Phenylketonuria (PKU) ko inborn error of metabolism ka example diya hai. “Error” ka meaning inherited\nlack of an enzyme hai; source phenylalanine hydroxylase deficiency ko phenylalanine → tyrosine\nconversion se link karta hai. [Q2]\n● Enzyme deficiency ki wajah se phenylalanine blood/tissue fluids mein high ho sakta hai; source\nprogressive mental retardation / mental idiocy ko important phenotypic effect batata hai. [Q2, Q3]\n3. Bubble Baby Disease — SCID\n● “Bubble Baby Disease” = Severe Combined Immunodeficiency (SCID), ek rare genetic disorder. Source\nke mutabik functional T-cells aur B-cells ka development disturbed hota hai aur affected baby ko fatal\ninfections se bachane ke liye germ-free plastic bubble mein treat/keep kiya jaata hai. [Q4]\n4. Haemophilia — Sex-Linked Hereditary Disorder\n● Haemophilia source mein genetic sex-linked hereditary defect hai. Source wording: women carry it while\nit appears in men; affected person mein blood clotting proper nahi hoti aur clotting mein bahut zyada\ntime lag sakta hai. [Q5, Q6, Q8, Q9]\n● Royal haemophilia ko sex-linked genetic disease bataya gaya hai. Source Queen Victoria association ke\nkaaran ise “royal haemophilia / royal disease” bhi kehta hai. [Q5, Q7]\n5. Down Syndrome — Trisomy 21\n● Down Syndrome = Trisomy 21. Source ke according chromosome 21 ki third copy ki presence se\ndisorder hota hai; chromosome-number change ke kaaran total chromosome count 47 ho jaata hai. [Q11,\nQ12, Q13, Q14]\n● Source Down syndrome ko physical growth delays, mild-to-moderate intellectual disability aur\ncharacteristic facial features se associate karta hai; explanation mein historical term “Mongolian idiocy”\nbhi diya gaya hai. [Q11, Q14]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Disorders Full Mind Map\n6. X-Linked Disorders & Muscular Dystrophy\n● Source Q15 mein sex chromosome par recessive gene ki expression se caused disorder ka answer\nMuscular dystrophy diya hai; explanation ise X-chromosome-linked hereditary disease aur progressive\nmuscle weakness/loss se link karti hai. [Q15]\n7. Disease-Type Matching\n● Correct matching: Haemophilia → Genetic disease; Diabetes → Hormonal disorder (insulin deficiency);\nRickets → Deficiency disease (Vitamin D deficiency); Ringworm → Fungal infection. [Q16]\n● Correct hereditary set source mein Colour blindness + Haemophilia + Sickle cell anaemia hai.\nDiphtheria/Pneumonia/Leprosy bacterial; AIDS viral; Syphilis/Gonorrhoea bacterial; Polio/Japanese B\nencephalitis viral aur Plague bacterial bataya gaya hai. [Q17]\n● Vitamin–disease matching trap: Vitamin A deficiency → Night blindness, Colour blindness nahi.\nThiamine (B1) → Beriberi; Ascorbic acid (C) → Scurvy; Vitamin K → blood clotting. [Q19]\n8. Colour Blindness — X-Linked Inheritance\n● Colour blindness source mein X-linked recessive trait hai. Men mein sirf one X-chromosome hone ki\nwajah se X-linked recessive disorders females ke comparison mein more frequent hote hain; fathers X-\nlinked trait sons ko directly pass nahi karte. [Q18]\n● Colour-blind man (XcY) + completely normal woman (XX): source explanation ke according immediate\nsons normal aur daughters carrier-normal hoti hain; immediate children mein colour blindness probability\n0% hai. [Q20, Q21]\n● Source Q20 ka marked answer “sons of daughters” hai: carrier daughters aage normal male se marry\nkaren to unke kuch sons colour blind ho sakte hain. Isliye question ka focus next generation/grandsons\npar hai. [Q20]\n● Colour-blind woman (XcXc) + normal husband (XY): source ke according son colour blind hoga, jabki\ndaughter affected X inherit karke carrier hogi par colour blind nahi hogi. [Q22]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Colour-Blindness Generations\n ▸Q20 immediate children ke baare mein nahi, “symptoms generated in sons of daughters” ko key karta hai;\nQ21 same parental cross mein immediate children ka actual colour-blind probability 0% deta hai. Dono source\nexplanations ko generation-wise padhna zaroori hai. [Q20, Q21]\n9. Thalassemia — Haemoglobin & Blood Disorder\n● Thalassemia inherited/genetic blood disorder hai. Source ke according body abnormal form ya\ninadequate amount of haemoglobin banati hai; RBC destruction severe anaemia tak lead kar sakta hai.\n[Q23]\n● Isliye Thalassemia mein affected system/tissue context ka answer Blood hai, aur synthesis-related\nanswer Haemoglobin hai. [Q23, Q24]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0326","t":"09.vi Deficiency Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Deficiency & Other Diseases Full Mind Map\n🩺 DEFICIENCY & OTHER DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.vi · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Metabolic, Joint & Food-Adulteration Disorders\n2. Iodine, Beriberi & Blue Baby Syndrome\n3. Heart, Potassium & Kidney Disorders\n4. Nuclear Medicine, Radioisotopes & Cancer\n5. Brain, Nerve, Sleep & Behavioural Disorders\n6. Pollution, Heavy Metals & Occupational Diseases\n7. Scurvy, Malnutrition & Deficiency Matching\n8. Disease–Organ Matching & Eye Disorders\n9. Liver, Prions, Parasites & Other Disorders\n10. Diabetes Mellitus / Insipidus & Vasopressin\n11. Treatment, Emergency Medicine & Miscellaneous\n1. Metabolic, Joint & Food-Adulteration Disorders\n● Muscle fatigue ko source anaerobic metabolism se banne wale lactic acid accumulation se link karta hai;\nlocal acidity muscular contraction ke liye unfavourable ho sakti hai. [Q1]\n● Joints mein uric-acid crystal deposition arthritis/gout se linked hai; blood mein high uric acid\n(hyperuricemia) Gout ki characteristic hai. [Q2, Q3]\n● Epidemic dropsy mustard oil ke Argemone-oil adulteration se associated hai. Source Q4 mein rice-husk\nadulteration ko dropsy ka “not correct” reason mark karta hai; Argemone mexicana poppy-family seed\nmustard seed jaisa dikh sakta hai. [Q4, Q5]\n● Cancer = abnormal/uncontrolled cell growth with potential to invade/spread. Source ka quoted “single\ncell…merciless disease” answer Cancer hai. [Q6]\n● Anthophobia = flowers ka fear. Source hysteria ko mainly young/unmarried women se associate karta\nhai. [Q7, Q8]\n● Silicosis = silica particles inhale karne se hone wali lung disease. [Q9]\n2. Iodine, Beriberi & Blue Baby Syndrome\n● Iodine deficiency → thyroid malfunction / goitre; source thyroxine aur triiodothyronine production kam\nhone se link karta hai. Goitre patients ko iodine diya jaata hai. [Q10, Q12, Q13, Q14]\n● Deficiency matching: Anaemia → Iron; Goitre → Iodine; Night-blindness → Vitamin A; Beriberi →\nVitamin B (Thiamine/B1). [Q11]\n● Polished rice ki milling/polishing nutrients remove karti hai; source ke according thiamine (Vitamin B1)\ndeficiency ke kaaran Beriberi hota hai. [Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Blue Baby Syndrome: drinking water mein excess nitrate → nitrite → oxyhaemoglobin se\nmethemoglobin; blood mein excess methemoglobin oxygen-carrying capacity ko reduce karta hai. [Q18,\nQ19, Q20]\n3. Heart, Potassium & Kidney Disorders\n● Heart-attack sequence source: cholesterol/fibrous plaque → blood clot → vessel lumen\nnarrowing/obstruction → inadequate blood & oxygen supply. “Golden Hour” medical terminology heart\nattack se related hai. [Q21, Q22]\n● Beta-blocker ko source heart attack se protection/management se link karta hai. Normal heart-beat\nregulation ke liye Potassium essential bataya gaya hai; potassium deficiency ka paired answer low\nblood pressure hai. [Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Urine ke saath albumin release hona kidney failure/damage ka indicator diya hai; prolonged fasting se\nsource kidney ko most affected organ mark karta hai. [Q26, Q27]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Deficiency & Other Diseases Full Mind Map\n4. Nuclear Medicine, Radioisotopes & Cancer\n● Nuclear medicines = radioisotopes. Diagnostic matching: Arsenic-74 → tumour; Cobalt-60 → cancer;\nIodine-131 → thyroid activity; Sodium-24 → blood disorder / blood-flow measurement. [Q28, Q29, Q31, Q36,\nQ37]\n● Source Q30 ka incorrect match: Gold-198 → treatment of retinal disorders. Leukaemia mein WBC count\nabnormal increase hota hai. [Q30, Q32]\n● Blood cancer/leukaemia control ke liye source Phosphorus-32 aur Cobalt-60 dono ko correct maanta\nhai; Cobalt-60 radiation treatment mein γ-rays emit karta hai. [Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Muscle/body ache relief ke liye Infrared radiation diya hai. [Q38, Q44]\n● Oncogenes cancer se associated hain; cancer condition ko uncontrolled cell multiplication bataya gaya\nhai. Metastasis = cancer cells ka blood/lymph ke through other sites/organs tak spread. [Q39, Q40, Q41]\n● Ionized radiation intensity/use ke depending cancer cause bhi kar sakti hai aur cure/treatment mein use\nbhi ho sakti hai. Harmful radiation ke liye source Brain ko listed organs mein less susceptible batata hai.\n[Q42, Q43]\n● Source “most recent therapy” ka answer Intensity Modulated Radiotherapy (IMRT) deta hai; Interferon ko\ncancer control se link karta hai. [Q45, Q46]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Radioisotope Answer Pattern\n ▸Q33 mein source explicitly “Multiple Correct Answers — C & D” deta hai: Phosphorus-32 + Cobalt-60. Q34\nmein isi wajah se “More than one of the above” correct hai. [Q33, Q34]\n5. Brain, Nerve, Sleep & Behavioural Disorders\n● Cerebral palsy ko source generally small children mein found brain disorder batata hai. Alzheimer’s\nprimarily brain ko affect karta hai; source hazardous neural disease se Amyloid precursor protein ko\nassociate karta hai. [Q47, Q48, Q49]\n● Parkinson’s disease treatment development ke Nobel context mein source Arvid Carlsson ko answer\nkarta hai. [Q50]\n● Scratching itching ko ease karta hai—source certain nerves stimulation aur brain-mediated\nantihistaminic chemicals increase ka mechanism deta hai. [Q51]\n● Anosmia = loss of smell. Matching mein Dyspnoea → shortness of breath aur Anosmia → partial/full loss\nof smell correct; Anorexia/Insomnia ke\n\n\nदिएगएswapped pairs incorrect hain. [Q52, Q53]\n● Eating stop na kar paana = Bulimia. Sleep apnea = sleep ke dauran breathing briefly and repeatedly\nstop hona. [Q54, Q55]\n6. Pollution, Heavy Metals & Occupational Diseases\n● Disease–cause matching: Khaira → Zinc deficiency; Anaemia → Iron deficiency; Goitre → Iodine\ndeficiency; Scurvy → Vitamin C deficiency. [Q56]\n● Knock-knee syndrome ko source fluoride pollution se link karta hai; “Fluoride ion → Indigestion” ko\nincorrect pollutant–disease match mark karta hai. [Q57, Q58]\n● Minamata disease = Mercury poisoning / mercury-polluted water / mercury-contaminated fish. Itai-Itai\ndisease = chronic Cadmium poisoning/pollution. [Q59, Q60, Q61, Q62, Q63, Q64]\n● Allergy-caused disease ka answer Asthma diya hai. [Q65]\n7. Scurvy, Malnutrition & Deficiency Matching\n● Milk + egg + bread-only diet se source Scurvy risk deta hai; Scurvy = Vitamin C deficiency, aur\nGooseberry (Amla) treatment/useful source answer hai. [Q66, Q67, Q68, Q69]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Deficiency & Other Diseases Full Mind Map\n● DRDO drug Lukoskin = Leucoderma treatment. Polyherbal product list mein source Nocdurna ko DRDO-\ndeveloped nahi maanta. [Q70, Q71]\n● Disease–affected part matching explanation: Malaria → blood cells; Filaria → lymph node; Encephalitis\n→ brain; Leukaemia → bone marrow. [Q72]\n● Malnutrition matching: Marasmus → prolonged starvation; Kwashiorkor → protein deficiency; TB →\nbacterial infection; Hepatitis B → viral infection. [Q73]\n● Kwashiorkor ko protein deficiency se directly link kiya hai. Source Q75 children mein protein deficiency\nka answer Marasmus deta hai aur explanation prolonged starvation se energy + protein deficiency /\ngeneralized wasting batati hai. [Q74, Q75]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Marasmus vs Kwashiorkor\n ▸Q74: Kwashiorkor = protein deficiency. Q75: marked answer Marasmus; explanation ise prolonged starvation\nke saath energy + protein deficiency se explain karti hai. Dono source framings ko separate yaad rakho. [Q74,\nQ75]\n ▸Q72 ke printed code mein Malaria mapping “5” use hoti hai jabki visible List-II 1–4 tak hai; explanation\nnevertheless Malaria → Blood cells, Filaria → Lymph node, Encephalitis → Brain, Leukaemia → Bone marrow\ndeti hai. [Q72]\n8. Disease–Organ Matching & Eye Disorders\n● Correct disease–organ pairs: Jaundice → Liver; Pneumonia → Lungs. [Q76, Q77]\n● Astigmatism aur Myopia dono eye disorders hain. Myopia/short-sightedness concave lens se correct hoti\nhai; myopic person nearby objects clearly dekh sakta hai. Hypermetropia/far-sightedness mein close\nobjects dekhne mein difficulty hoti hai. [Q78, Q79, Q80, Q81, Q82]\n● Blind spot aur yellow spot Retina mein hote hain; source Retina ko Diencephalon ka outgrowth batata\nhai. [Q83, Q84]\n● Cataract = eye lens opaque/cloudy hona; listed iris/retina/cornea mein lens absent hone ki wajah se Q86\nka answer “None of the Above” hai. Cloudiness protein change se linked hai. [Q85, Q86, Q87]\n● Drug/use matching: Atropine → pupil dilation; Ether → local anaesthesia; Nitroglycerine → heart trouble;\nPyrethrin → mosquito control. Dilute atropine eye pupil dilate karta hai. [Q88, Q89]\n● Ishihara test = colour blindness. [Q90]\n● Biological resurfacing ko source knee/ankle/hip/vertebral joints ke context mein discuss karta hai; initial\nkey knee-joint thi, revised key mein question delete hua. [Q91]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Deleted / Disputed Question\n ▸Q91 source mein “Disputed Question” hai: initial UPPSC key option (A) Knee joints thi, later revised key mein\nquestion deleted bataya gaya hai. [Q91]\n9. Anaemia, Liver, Prions, Parasites & Other Disorders\n● Iron deficiency → Anaemia. [Q92, Q93]\n● Excessive alcoholic beverage → Liver cirrhosis. Oral submucous fibrosis → Gutka/tobacco consumption.\nJaundice liver ko affect karta hai aur source use “not so contagious” disease ke answer ke roop mein\ndeta hai. [Q94, Q95, Q96, Q97]\n● Poultry-bird rickets = Vitamin D deficiency. Mad-cow disease factor = Prions. Liver fluke bile duct mein\nsource host Sheep deta hai. [Q98, Q99, Q100]\n● Bright’s disease Kidney ko affect karti hai. Pneumoconiosis mainly coal-mining workers se linked hai.\n[Q101, Q102]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Deficiency & Other Diseases Full Mind Map\n10. Diabetes Mellitus / Insipidus & Vasopressin\n● Blood glucose commonly mg/dL (milligram per decilitre) mein express hota hai. Excess insulin injection\nse glucose unusually low (hypoglycemia) ho sakta hai, source spasm/apoplexy/faintness/death se link\nkarta hai. [Q103, Q104]\n● Diabetes vaccination se control nahi hoti. Source diabetes ko Pancreas malfunction aur insulin\ndeficiency se link karta hai. [Q105, Q106, Q107, Q108]\n● Diabetes mellitus association: higher blood sugar + lower insulin. HbA1c management mein previous\n~8–12 weeks ka average glucose reflect karta hai. [Q109, Q110]\n● Diabetes insipidus: excessive urine + thirst; source ke according ADH/vasopressin production deficiency\nse hota hai, excess secretion se nahi. [Q111]\n● Alcohol/whiskey urination increase karta hai because source vasopressin (ADH) secretion suppress\nhone aur diuretic effect ko describe karta hai. [Q112]\n● Fenugreek seeds aur Curry leaf ko source diabetes blood-sugar control/medication benefit se associate\nkarta hai. [Q113, Q114]\n● Insulin discovery context: source F.G. Banting ko answer karta hai; explanation Banting & Best, Macleod\naur 1923 Nobel context deti hai. [Q115]\n11. Treatment, Emergency Medicine & Miscellaneous\n● Copper-T ka commonest side effect source mein increased menstrual bleeding hai. [Q116]\n● Emphysema environmental-pollution context mein lungs ko affect karta hai. [Q117]\n● Aspirin = non-narcotic analgesic; “belongs to narcotic analgesics” statement source mein NOT true hai.\nLow-dose aspirin heart attack/stroke/blood-clot prevention context mein diya hai. [Q118]\n● CPR = Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation. Coronary bypass graft ke liye source leg vein / chest or wrist\nartery jaise healthy vessels use hone ke kaaran “Any of these” answer deta hai. Cath lab = Cardiology\ndepartment. [Q119, Q120, Q121]\n● Xerophthalmia = severe Vitamin A deficiency; source India mein remedial priority aur preventable\nchildhood blindness context deta hai. [Q122]\n● Lathyrism = Khesari dal (Lathyrus sativus) ka excessive/regular consumption; neurological weakness,\nspasms aur lower-limb paralysis se linked. [Q123, Q124]\n● Blank dispensing capsules mainly Gelatine se bante hain, lekin source Starch capsules ko bhi valid\nalternative maanta hai. [Q125]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Multiple-Correct Capsule Question\n ▸Q125 source explicitly “Multiple Correct Answers — C & D” deta hai: Starch + Gelatine. [Q125]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0327","t":"09.vii Plant Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Diseases Full Mind Map\n🌿 PLANT DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 9.vii · Diseases & Treatment · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this sub-chapter:\n1. Plant Pathogens, Causal Factors & Disease Spread\n2. Important Crop–Disease Matching\n3. Zinc Deficiency Disorders in Plants\n4. Sugarcane, Groundnut & Mustard Problems\n5. Major Rice Diseases\n6. Major Wheat Diseases\n7. Potato Blackheart — Oxygen Deficiency\n8. Okra Yellow Vein Mosaic\n9. Mango Spongy Tissue Disorder\n1. Plant Pathogens, Causal Factors & Disease Spread\n● Viruses living cells ke andar replicate karte hain aur source ke according bacteria, fungi aur plants —\nteeno ko infect kar sakte hain. [Q1]\n● Plant-disease causal matching: Citrus canker → Xanthomonas bacteria; sugarcane red rot →\nColletotrichum falcatum fungus; potato Blackheart/Krishnakant → oxygen deficiency. Wheat ear-\ncockle/sehun ko source nematode se link karta hai. [Q2]\n● Plant diseases ke dissemination factors mein wind, rain, animals, soil, contaminated tools, infected seed\nstock, pollen, dust storm, irrigation water, birds aur humans shamil hain; Q17 mein Birds + Dust + Rain\n+ Wind sab correct hain. [Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q2 — Disputed Matching\n ▸Source kehta hai question mein wheat ka 'Sahu' disease diya hai jo 'sehun' hona chahiye; ear cockle/sehun\nnematode se hota hai, insect se nahi. Isliye diye gaye options mein perfect match nahi banta aur answer '*'\ndisputed rakha gaya hai. [Q2]\n2. Important Crop–Disease Matching\n● Powdery mildew source ke according wheat, grape, barley, onion, apple aur pea se related hai —\nsugarcane se nahi. Wheat–Phalaris minor, Potato–Late blight aur Bajra–Ergot pairs correct diye gaye\nhain. [Q3]\n● Green hair disease Bajra mein hota hai, rice mein nahi; bajra ke hairs twist hokar broom-like appearance\ndete hain aur plant dwarf reh sakta hai. Bajra–Ergot, Pea–Powdery mildew, Gram–Wilt correct pairs\nhain. [Q4]\n● Wilt ko source gram/chickpea, sugarcane, toor etc. se link karta hai, paddy se nahi. Mustard–White rust,\nBajra–Smut aur Groundnut–Tikka correct pairs diye gaye hain. [Q5]\n3. Zinc Deficiency Disorders in Plants\n● Maize mein Zinc (Zn) deficiency se chlorosis hota hai; leaves underdeveloped/dwarf ho sakte hain aur\nleaf tip white, mottled ya yellow ho sakta hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● White Bud disease bhi Zn deficiency se linked hai. Source Zn-deficiency names mein rice ka Khaira,\nmaize ka White Bud aur citrus/cotton ka mottle leaf (little leaf)/frenching deta hai. [Q8]\n4. Sugarcane, Groundnut & Mustard Problems\n● Pyrilla sugarcane ka harmful leafhopper pest hai jo leaf/plant sap suck karta hai; infestation se yellow\npatches, leaf drying aur crop growth disruption ho sakta hai. [Q9]\n● Groundnut ki major/deadly disease Tikka hai; source ise early aur late leaf spots ke roop mein describe\nkarta hai aur Cercospora personata / C. arachidicola fungi se link karta hai. [Q10]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Plant Diseases Full Mind Map\n● Source Q11 white rust ko mustard ki prominent fungal disease batata hai aur Albugo candida se link\nkarta hai; stem, leaves aur inflorescence par white lesions/patches aa sakte hain. [Q11]\n5. Major Rice Diseases\n● Rice blast ek fungal disease hai; source causal fungus ko Pyricularia oryzae / Magnaporthe oryzae (M.\ngrisea) batata hai. Ye above-ground rice parts ko affect kar sakta hai aur destructive crop loss cause\nkarta hai. [Q12]\n● False smut paddy ka disease hai, barley ka nahi. Source matching mein Wheat–Rust, Potato–Early\nblight aur Paddy–Khaira ko correct batata hai. [Q13]\n● Rice Tungro do virus groups — RTSV (Rice Tungro Spherical Virus) aur RTBV (Rice Tungro Bacilliform\nVirus) — se linked hai; dono green leafhoppers ke through transmit hote hain. [Q16]\n6. Major Wheat Diseases\n● Wheat ke do common fungal diseases: Black rust → Puccinia graminis tritici; Loose smut → Ustilago\nnuda tritici. [Q14]\n● Karnal Bunt wheat ki fungal disease hai; source causal smut fungus Tilletia indica batata hai. Iska first\nreport 1931 mein Karnal, Haryana ke paas wheat se diya gaya hai. [Q15]\n7. Potato Blackheart — Oxygen Deficiency\n● Potato Blackheart ek abiotic storage disorder hai jo low oxygen availability se hota hai; tuber centre\nblack ho sakta hai aur tissue inside-out die karke jet black ho jaata hai. [Q18]\n8. Okra Yellow Vein Mosaic\n● Okra/Bhindi ka Yellow Vein Mosaic ek viral disease hai; Whitefly iska vector/factor hai jo virus ko ek\nplant se doosre plant tak spread karta hai. [Q19, Q20]\n9. Mango Spongy Tissue Disorder\n● Spongy tissue Alphonso mango ka ripening disorder hai: fruit bahar se normal lag sakta hai lekin andar\nsoft-centre/white corky tissue ya internal breakdown hota hai. Source ise South India se peculiar aur\nexport quality ko hamper karne wala disorder batata hai. [Q21]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0328","t":"10 Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Engineering & Biotechnology Full Mind Map\n🧬 GENETIC ENGINEERING & BIOTECHNOLOGY — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 10 · Genetics & Biotechnology · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Recombinant DNA, CRISPR, RNAi & mRNA\n2. Mitochondrial Therapy, Cloning & IVF\n3. Genome Mapping, Stem Cells & Hybridoma\n4. Gene Bank, Patents & Bt Crops\n5. GM Mustard, Crop Engineering & Biopesticides\n6. Golden Rice & Agricultural Biotechnology\n7. Prenatal Diagnostics, Bioinformatics & Biotech Tools\n8. DNA Fingerprinting & Biometrics\n9. Transgenics, Mutation, Pleiotropy & Gene Therapy\n1. Recombinant DNA, CRISPR, RNAi & mRNA\n● Microsatellite DNA = short, repeated (usually non-coding) DNA segments. Source inhe polymorphic\nmarkers ke roop mein inheritance/evolutionary relationships, DNA profiling, paternity/forensics, linkage\nanalysis aur population genetics se link karta hai. [Q1]\n● Source Q2 ke according different species ke DNA segments jodkar functional chromosomes banana\nNOT correct development hai; artificial functional DNA pieces, cell-free DNA replication aur lab petri-dish\ncell division ko possible statements maana gaya hai. [Q2]\n● Recombinant DNA technology se bana pehla human hormone Insulin tha; source Humulin ko 1982 FDA\napproval se link karta hai. [Q3]\n● Recombinant-vector vaccines mein genetic engineering use hoti hai aur live attenuated bacteria/viruses\nvectors ke roop mein desired antigen-gene carry kar sakte hain. [Q4]\n● rDNA technology genes ko different plant species ke beech, animals se plants mein aur microorganisms\nse higher organisms mein transfer kar sakti hai. [Q5]\n● Source ka rDNA sequence: genetic material identify/isolate → DNA fragment → desired fragment isolate\n→ gene amplify → vector se ligate → recombinant DNA host mein transfer → foreign-gene product\nobtain → downstream processing. [Q6]\n● Restriction endonucleases DNA ko specific sites par cut karne wali molecular scissors hain; DNA ligases\nfragments ko join karne wale molecular stitchers hain. [Q7, Q8]\n● Cas9 (CRISPR-associated protein 9) targeted gene editing ki molecular scissors hai—DNA cut karke\ngenome alter kar sakti hai. [Q9]\n● RNA interference (RNAi) targeted mRNA ko neutralize karke gene expression/translation suppress karta\nhai. Source uses: gene-silencing therapy, cancer therapy aur viral-resistant crops; hormone-\nreplacement therapy nahi. [Q10]\n● mRNA ka expanded form Messenger Ribonucleic Acid hai; ye DNA ka genetic code nucleus se\nribosome tak le jaata hai jahan proteins bante hain. [Q11]\n2. Mitochondrial Therapy, Cloning & IVF\n● Pronuclear Transfer / Mitochondrial Replacement Therapy ka purpose offspring mein mitochondrial\ndiseases prevent karna hai; source ise 'three-parent baby' reproductive technology se link karta hai.\n[Q12, Q13]\n● Dolly first mammal thi jo adult somatic cell se successfully clone hui. Source: Roslin Institute, Scotland;\nbirth 5 July 1996; IVF se nahi bani; 2003 mein lung disease se death. [Q14, Q15, Q16, Q17, Q18]\n● NDRI Karnal cloning: source Samrupa ko first cloned buffalo calf batata hai; second cloned calf Garima\ntha. Garima II bhi cloned buffalo hai; March 2023 ki 'Ganga' India's first cloned cow source ke according\nGir breed ki thi. [Q19, Q20, Q21]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Engineering & Biotechnology Full Mind Map\n● National Taiwan University group ne 2006 mein green fluorescent protein introduce karke first transgenic\nglowing green pigs produce kiye. [Q22]\n● Injaz duniya ki first female cloned camel thi, Camel Reproduction Centre, Dubai (UAE) mein developed.\n[Q23]\n● Clone ki genetic information parent organism ke identical hoti hai aur clone asexually produce hota hai.\n[Q24]\n● Test-tube baby/IVF mein fertilization mother's body ke bahar hota hai; fertilized embryo baad mein\nuterus mein transfer hota hai. [Q25]\n● Source ke according genetic engineering mein disease resistance, growth promotion aur animal cloning\nkuch success ke saath achieve hue; human cloning ko fruitful result nahi mila/controversial-banned\nbataya gaya hai. [Q26]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Mitochondrial Inheritance — Source vs Key\n ▸Q13 source marked answer (A) = statement 1 only. Explanation mein mtDNA ko usually maternal bataya gaya\nhai, 2018 research ke biparental exceptions mention hain, aur source note karta hai ki UPSC official key ne\noption (C) diya tha. Is mismatch ko source ke jaisa hi preserve kiya gaya hai. [Q13]\n3. Genome Mapping, Stem Cells & Hybridoma\n● Genetics scientist-matching source: bacterial transduction/conjugation → Lederberg; sex-linked\ninheritance → Morgan; E. coli DNA polymerase → Arthur Kornberg; complete genetic code →\nHargobind Khorana. [Q27]\n● Chromosome par genes/DNA sequences ki relative positions jaana livestock pedigree aur disease-\nresistant animal breeds develop karne mein useful hai; source ke according isse ALL human diseases\nke causes nahi samjhe ja sakte. [Q28]\n● 1996 mein budding yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae ka genome completely sequence hua—source ise\nfirst completely sequenced eukaryotic genome se link karta hai. Human Genome Project = human\ngenes aur sequences ki identification/mapping. [Q29, Q30]\n● Stem cells self-renew/divide kar sakti hain aur many specialized cell types mein differentiate ho sakti\nhain; source inhe serious diseases ke research focus se link karta hai. [Q31]\n● Stem cells mammals-only nahi; source ke according new-drug screening aur medical therapies mein use\nho sakti hain. [Q32]\n● Human stem-cell sources embryo tak limited nahi—fetus, umbilical cord, placenta, infant, child/adult aur\norgans/tissues se bhi mil sakti hain. Source Q33 mein in-vitro self-renewal virtually forever aur Indian\ncell lines ko correct maanta hai; embryonic stem-cell derivation ko blastocyst destruction se link karta\nhai. [Q33, Q34]\n● Bone-marrow-derived stem cells ko source embryonic stem cells ka bioethically non-controversial\nalternative maanta hai. [Q35]\n● Source CRISPR-Cas9 ke context mein germ-cell genetic changes, early-embryo genome editing aur\nhuman induced pluripotent stem cells ko pig embryo mein inject karne—teeno statements ko correct\nmaanta hai. [Q36]\n● Somatic Cell Nuclear Transfer (SCNT) reproductive cloning of animals mein use ho sakti hai; source\ntherapeutic cloning / regenerative medicine aur embryonic stem-cell research bhi mention karta hai.\n[Q37]\n● Hybridoma technology monoclonal antibodies ke commercial production ke liye hai. Technique Georges\nKöhler aur César Milstein ne 1975 mein develop ki; source 1984 Nobel se link karta hai. [Q38, Q39]\n4. Gene Bank, Patents & Bt Crops\n● Plant Field Gene Bank, Banthara ka source-purpose: endangered plants ko secure karna, biological-\ndiversity piracy rokna aur economically important plants ko recognise karna. [Q40]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Engineering & Biotechnology Full Mind Map\n● Source ke Indian Patents Act discussion mein plants/seeds/varieties aur essentially biological processes\npatent-eligible nahi; plant varieties patent nahi ho sakti. Q41 explanation IPAB ke existence ko bhi state\nkarta hai. [Q41]\n● Bt cotton mein insect-resistance gene bacterium Bacillus thuringiensis se aata hai; Bt toxins insects ke\nliye harmful hain. Source assertion-reason mein Bt-gene insertion aur bacterial origin dono true +\nreason explains assertion. [Q42, Q43, Q44, Q45]\n● Bollgard I & Bollgard II GM crop technologies Bt cotton se related hain; source Bollgard I = single-gene\ncommercialisation 2002 aur Bollgard II = double-gene technology 2006 batata hai. [Q46]\n● Bt brinjal genetically modified/transgenic brinjal hai; Cry1Ac gene soil bacterium Bacillus thuringiensis se\ninsert karke insect/pest resistance (especially shoot/fruit borer) ke liye develop kiya gaya. [Q47, Q48, Q49]\n● Bt brinjal opposition ke genuine concerns source mein health-impact aur biodiversity-impact (statements\n3,4) hain; soil fungus gene aur terminator-seed claim ko incorrect maana gaya. [Q50]\n5. GM Mustard, Crop Engineering & Biopesticides\n● GM mustard = DMH-11 (Brassica juncea), source ke according Prof. Deepak Pental/University of Delhi\nteam ne develop ki. Bacillus amyloliquefaciens genes cross-pollination/hybridization allow karte hain;\nbroad pest resistance nahi; IARI+PAU joint-development statement incorrect. [Q51]\n● Genetically engineered plants source mein drought tolerance, enhanced nutritive value aur longer shelf-\nlife ke liye banaye gaye; spacecraft mein grow/photosynthesis wali statement accepted nahi. [Q52]\n● Agriculture mein genome sequencing disease/drought-resistance markers identify karne, new crop\nvarieties ka development time reduce karne aur host-pathogen relationship decipher karne mein useful\nhai. [Q53]\n● Flavr-Savr tomato source ke according first commercially grown genetically engineered food tha; fruits\nlonger firm rehte aur vine-ripening ke baad transport ho sakte; full vine-ripened flavour milta hai—A & B\ncorrect, C incorrect. [Q54]\n● Transgenic crops create karne mein source cytoplasmic male sterility aur gene silencing ko use karta\nhai; budding/grafting vegetative propagation hai, genetic modification nahi. [Q55]\n● Biopesticides mein bacteria, fungi aur flowering plants ki kuch species use ho sakti hain. Bacillus\nthuringiensis (Bt) microbial insecticide / biological insecticide ka classic example hai. [Q56, Q57, Q58]\n● Terminator Seed Technology next generation ke liye non-viable/sterile seeds produce karti hai; source\nise farmers ko har season seeds repurchase karne ki dependency se link karta hai. [Q59, Q60, Q61]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Terminator Technology — Q61 Pattern\n ▸Q61 mein defining feature sterile next-generation seed hai, lekin source explicitly note karta hai ki UPPSC ne\n'All of the above' accept kiya because option-set GM plants ko broadly encompass karta tha. [Q61]\n6. Golden Rice & Agricultural Biotechnology\n● Golden Rice transgenic rice hai jo edible parts mein beta-carotene biosynthesize karta hai; beta-\ncarotene body mein Vitamin A mein convert hota hai. Source isliye ise Vitamin-A deficiency/blindness\ncombat karne se link karta hai. [Q62, Q63, Q64, Q65, Q66, Q67, Q68, Q69]\n● Source Golden Rice ko Prof. Ingo Potrykus aur Dr. Peter Beyer se link karta hai; genome mein two\ndaffodil genes + one Erwinia uredovora gene mention hain. Q70 ka marked answer Daffodil hai. [Q70]\n● Incorrect match in source: Ozone layer → Troposphere, kyunki ozone layer Stratosphere mein hoti hai.\nOther matches: Renneting → Cheese; Plasmid → Genetic Engineering; Golden Rice → Vitamin A. [Q71]\n● 'Super rice' source ke according G.S. (Gurdev Singh) Khush ne develop kiya; source IRRI, Philippines\nse link karta hai. [Q72]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Engineering & Biotechnology Full Mind Map\n7. Prenatal Diagnostics, Bioinformatics & Biotech Tools\n● Amniocentesis fetal sex determine karne ke saath prenatal chromosomal abnormalities aur fetal\ninfections diagnose karne mein use hoti hai; amniotic fluid se fetal DNA examine hota hai. [Q73]\n● Transcriptome = organism/cell ke genes se expressed full range/sum-total of mRNA molecules; genome\nroughly fixed hota hai par transcriptome condition ke saath change kar sakta hai. [Q74]\n● Arthur Kornberg ne DNA in vitro synthesize kiya; source unhe biological DNA synthesis mechanism\ndiscovery aur 1959 Nobel se link karta hai. [Q75]\n● Biofilms medical implants aur food/food-processing surfaces par form ho sakte hain aur antibiotic\nresistance/tolerance show kar sakte hain—source teeno statements correct maanta hai. [Q76]\n● Biochip biological environment ke liye designed microchip hai; source ke according DNA, RNA aur\nProtein chips/contents relevant hain. [Q77]\n● Genico Technology ko source genetic diseases ki pre-information, especially prenatal fetal-disease\ninvestigation, se define karta hai. [Q78]\n● Aerial metagenomics = air/aerosols se genetic material (DNA/RNA) collect karke airborne microbial\ncommunities ki genetic diversity analyse karna. [Q79]\n● Biotechnology source-definition: living organisms, unse obtained substances ya biological processes ka\nindustrial use; example yeast-based liquor production. [Q80]\n● Recirculating Aquaculture System ke biofilters uneaten feed/waste treatment karte aur ammonia →\nnitrite → nitrate convert karte hain; phosphorus ko nutrient ke roop mein increase nahi karte. [Q81]\n● Source 'recently evolved in genetic engineering' ka answer Gene Mapping deta hai; gene mapping\nchromosome par gene location aur relative distances determine karta hai. [Q82]\n● Plasmid genetic engineering mein vector/carrier ke roop mein use hota hai. Useful bacteria: Escherichia\ncoli + Agrobacterium (especially Ti plasmid in plant transformation). Bacteriophages bacteria ko infect\nkarte aur genetic-engineering vectors ke roop mein use ho sakte hain. [Q83, Q84, Q85]\n● Human growth-hormone gene se unusually large mouse produce karne wali technique source ke\naccording Genetic Engineering hai. [Q86]\n8. DNA Fingerprinting & Biometrics\n● Criminal DNA testing ke samples source mein blood cells, bone cells, hair strands aur saliva—sab ho\nsakte hain. [Q87]\n● DNA fingerprinting paternity aur criminals ki identity establish karne ka powerful tool hai; hairs, saliva aur\ndried semen jaise trace evidence DNA analysis ke liye adequate ho sakte hain. [Q88]\n● DNA fingerprinting ka basis DNA polymorphism hai—individuals ke inherited variable DNA regions. [Q89]\n● Child paternity prove/establish karne ke liye source DNA fingerprinting ko correct technique maanta hai.\n[Q90, Q91]\n● Human identity establish karne ke biotechnological technique ke roop mein source DNA fingerprinting\ndeta hai; applications: forensic cases, paternity disputes aur endangered living beings conservation.\n[Q92, Q93]\n● Source ke according DNA fingerprinting se solve hua first crime England mein 1983 case se linked hai\n(explanation 1983 aur 1986 ke two murders mention karta hai). [Q94]\n● Biometric identification mein fingerprint ke alawa iris scanning, retinal scanning aur voice recognition—\nteeno use ho sakte hain. [Q95]\n● Multi-coloured/non-porous surfaces par fingerprints develop karne ke liye source Fluorescent powder ka\nanswer deta hai. [Q96]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Genetic Engineering & Biotechnology Full Mind Map\n9. Transgenics, Mutation, Pleiotropy & Gene Therapy\n● Source ke according transgenics se biodegradable plastic, edible vaccines aur transgenic crops achieve\nho sakte hain; cloned animals ka production transgenics se achieve nahi maana gaya. [Q97]\n● Gene ke base sequence mein permanent change = Mutation. [Q98]\n● Ek gene jab do ya zyada different phenotypic characters ko simultaneously influence kare, phenomenon\nPleiotropy kehlata hai. [Q99]\n● Gene therapy defective genes ki functioning correct karne ke liye healthy gene copy introduce/replace\nkar sakti hai, faulty gene ko inactivate ('knock out') kar sakti hai, ya new/modified therapeutic gene\nintroduce kar sakti hai. [Q100]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Gene Therapy — Multiple Correct\n ▸Q100 source explicitly 'Multiple Correct Answers (Ans. *)' mark karta hai. Explanation ke according faulty gene\nko healthy copy se replace karna, defective gene ko inactivate karna, ya new/modified gene introduce karna—\nmultiple valid mechanisms hain. [Q100]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0329","t":"11 Miscellaneous HINGLISH FIXED","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Biology","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n🧬 BIOLOGY MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\nBiology Ch. 11 · Miscellaneous · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Public Health Programmes, Surveys & Schemes\n2. Chemistry, Environment, Microbes & Weeds\n3. Scientific Days, Awareness & Biodiversity\n4. Medical Diagnostics, Imaging & Therapy\n5. Metabolism, Fibres, Livestock & Applied Biology\n6. Medical Substances, Contraception & Scientific Fields\n7. Research Institutes, Gene Banks & Organisations\n8. Scientists, Bees, Human Responses & Vaccination\n9. Dating, Soil, Ecology, Plant Technology & Fibres\n10. Agriculture, Immunity, Policy & General Science\n1. Public Health Programmes, Surveys & Schemes\n● AYUSH ka full form Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha aur Homeopathy hai; ye India mein\npracticed six Indian systems of medicine ko represent karta hai. [Q1]\n● 'Red Ribbon Express' HIV/AIDS ke transmission, prevention aur risk-perception ke baare mein\nawareness create karne wala moving visual medium hai. [Q2]\n● SANRAKSHA (Bengaluru) 1993 mein HIV counselling service ke roop mein start hua; source ise AIDS\nResearch and Control Project se link karta hai aur HIV testing se hospice care tak services batata hai.\n[Q3]\n● AVAHAN Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation ki initiative hai jo India mein HIV spread reduce karne ke liye\n2003 mein start hui; NACO 1992 mein establish hua aur HIV/AIDS control programme ko lead karta hai.\n[Q4, Q5]\n● Mission Indradhanush 25 Dec 2014 ko launch hua; under-2 children aur pregnant women ko seven\nvaccine-preventable diseases ke against immunize/vaccinate karna iska objective hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● Anaemia Mukt Bharat (AMB) mein Iron + Folic Acid supplementation, delayed cord clamping, periodic\ndeworming aur endemic pockets mein malaria/haemoglobinopathies/fluorosis jaise non-nutritional\ncauses ko address karna include hai; calcium supplementation wala statement source mein incorrect\nhai. [Q9]\n● National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission 1 July 2023 ko Shahdol (M.P.) mein launch hua;\nsource target year 2047 deta hai, especially tribal populations mein sickle-cell genetic transmission\neliminate karne ke context mein. [Q10]\n● Source ka programme-year matching: National Programme for Control of Blindness → 1976; ICDS →\n1975; National Leprosy Eradication Programme → 1983; National Rural Health Mission → 2005. [Q11]\n● NFHS-5 mein pre-school education, death registration aur hypertension/diabetes prevalence jaise\nindicators included the, lekin source ke according HIV test include nahi tha. [Q12]\n2. Chemistry, Environment, Microbes & Weeds\n● Correct chemistry matching: Chlorophyll → Magnesium; Haemoglobin → Iron; Table salt → Sodium\nchloride; Washing soda → Sodium carbonate. Isliye 'Washing soda–Potassium' wrong pair hai. [Q13]\n● Vinegar mein Acetic acid, sour milk mein Lactic acid, bones mein Calcium phosphate aur gastric juice\nmein Hydrochloric acid hota hai; fruit ripening ko Ethylene se link kiya gaya hai. [Q14, Q15]\n● Environment matching: Skin cancer → Ultraviolet rays; Noise pollution → Decibel; Global warming →\nCarbon dioxide; Ozone hole → CFCs. [Q16]\n● Wool biodegradable material hai aur keratin protein se bana hota hai. Biodegradation mein\nmicroorganisms—especially bacteria—organic waste ko simpler/reusable substances mein break karte\nhain; given options mein insecticides non-biodegradable hain. [Q17, Q18, Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Microbe-use matching: Lactobacillus → curd; Rhizobium → nitrogen fixation; Yeast → alcohol;\nAspergillus → citric acid. Source bacteria, fungi aur microalgae—teeno ko industrially useful batata hai.\n[Q20, Q21]\n● Methanogens archaebacteria ka group hai jo low-oxygen conditions mein methane produce karta hai.\n[Q22]\n● Saccharomyces yeast toddy fermentation se linked hai; commercial ethanol ke liye Saccharomyces\ncerevisiae important hai. Yeast baking aur alcoholic beverages dono mein use hota hai. [Q23, Q24, Q25]\n● Thermophiles high-temperature loving microorganisms hain; source 50–80°C optimum range aur\nhyperthermophiles ke liye ~80–110°C tak growth mention karta hai. [Q26]\n● Biomagnification ka matlab food chain ke successive trophic levels par pesticides/toxic chemicals ki\nconcentration ka increase hona hai. [Q27]\n● Herbicides unwanted weeds ko kill karte hain; selective herbicides target weeds ko damage karte hue\ndesired crop ko relatively safe chhod sakte hain. Source assertion-reason mein A aur R dono true aur R\ncorrect explanation hai. [Q28]\n● Orobanche ek parasitic weed hai jo commonly tobacco fields se associated hai; tomato aur potato fields\nmein bhi mil sakta hai. [Q29]\n3. Scientific Days, Awareness & Biodiversity\n● Herbarium preserved plant specimens ka systematically stored/catalogued collection hota hai; plant\nidentification aur reference ke liye use hota hai. [Q30]\n● ICAR har saal 16 July ko Foundation Day celebrate karta hai; source establishment date 16 July 1929\nbatata hai. [Q31]\n● Important dates: National Maritime Day → 5 Apr; World Health Day → 7 Apr; World Athletics Day → 7\nMay; World Red Cross Day → 8 May. Source ka chronological order 2→1→3→4 hai. [Q32]\n● Other dates: World Environment Day → 5 Jun; World AIDS Day → 1 Dec; Teachers' Day → 5 Sep;\nWorld Food Day → 16 Oct; World Homeopathy Day → 10 Apr; Earth Day → 22 Apr; International Yoga\nDay → 21 Jun. [Q33, Q34]\n● World TB Day → 24 Mar; World AIDS Day → 1 Dec; Anti-Leprosy Day → last Sunday of January;\nInternational Ozone Day → 16 Sep. Bangkok mein International AIDS Conference 16 July 2004 ko hua\ntha. [Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38, Q39]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Important Days — Source Matching Issue\n ▸World Water Day 22 March hota hai, 22 April nahi; World Leprosy Day last Sunday of January hota hai, 30\nJune nahi. Isliye source Q40 mein B aur C dono pairs incorrect batata hai. [Q40]\n● World Diabetes Day har saal 14 November ko observe hota hai. [Q41]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — World Minority Rights Day — Code Mismatch\n ▸Correct dates: World Minority Rights Day→18 Dec; World AIDS Day→1 Dec; World Animal Day→4 Oct;\nWorld Food Day→16 Oct. Source Q42 mein exact correct code options mein nahi tha, isliye answer marked (*)\nhai. [Q42]\n● Animal facts source: Cuckoo apna nest nahi banata aur doosre birds ke nest mein eggs lay karta hai;\nlizard tail regenerate kar sakti hai; Blue whale largest living creature hai; Chimpanzee ko most intelligent\nanimal diya gaya hai. [Q43]\n● Tamil Nadu ne Oct 2022 mein State-Level Committee for Vulture Conservation launch ki; Asian Giant\nTortoises Dec 2022 mein Nagaland ke Ntangki National Park mein release kiye gaye. [Q44, Q45]\n● IUCN context mein Gharial critically endangered aur Indian Elephant endangered category mein diya\ngaya hai. Cheetah India mein extinct ho gaya tha aur Project Cheetah ke through reintroduction kiya\ngaya. [Q46, Q47]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Source sixth mass extinction ka major cause human activities—over-exploitation, habitat\nloss/fragmentation, ecosystem destruction, pollution aur climate change—batata hai. [Q48]\n● Biomass living organisms se derived biological material hai; 'inbuilt time-keeping system' actually\nbiological clock/circadian rhythm hota hai, biomass nahi. [Q49]\n4. Medical Diagnostics, Imaging & Therapy\n● Endoscope digestive tract ko examine karne wala light + camera equipped flexible/rigid instrument hai;\nsource ise simple 'camera type' category mein nahi rakhta. [Q50, Q51]\n● CT/CAT scan multiple X-ray images ko computer-process karke cross-sectional images banata hai.\nStomach X-ray se pehle Barium diya ja sakta hai kyunki wo X-rays absorb karke contrast improve karta\nhai. [Q52, Q53]\n● Diagnostic matching: EEG → Brain; ECG → Heart; EOG → Eyes/retina; EMG → Muscle. EEG brain ki\nelectrical activity record karta hai; Audiogram → Ear aur Mammogram → Breast. [Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57, Q58]\n● MRI = Magnetic Resonance Imaging; nuclear magnetic resonance principle par based hai aur strong\nmagnetic fields + radio waves use karta hai. Source clear karta hai ki X-rays aur Gamma rays MRI mein\nuse nahi hote. [Q59, Q60, Q61, Q62]\n● BMD = Bone Mineral Density test; osteoporosis diagnose/assess karne aur bone minerals/density\nmeasure karne ke liye use hota hai. [Q63, Q64, Q65]\n● Lithotripsy ultrasound shockwaves se kidney/bladder/ureter stones ko small pieces mein break karti hai,\njo baad mein urine se pass ho sakte hain. [Q66]\n● Electron beam radiation therapy kuch cancers—source mein skin lymphoma—ke treatment mein use\nhoti hai. [Q67]\n● Tetraplegia/Quadriplegia ka matlab both hands aur both legs mein total ya partial paralysis hai. [Q68]\n5. Metabolism, Fibres, Livestock & Applied Biology\n● Nutrition, respiration aur synthesis metabolism ke major aspects hain; metabolism mein catabolism\n(breakdown for energy) aur anabolism (synthesis) dono include hote hain. [Q69]\n● Artificial silk ko Rayon kehte hain; rayon regenerated cellulose fibre hai, modified starch nahi.\nOxytocin→Hormone, Aspartame→synthetic sweetener, Neoprene→specialized rubber; Wool→protein,\nRubber→natural polymer, Fullerene→carbon allotrope. [Q70, Q71, Q72]\n● Silk fibre, hair, nails aur claws keratin protein se related hain; Cotton mainly cellulose hai, protein nahi.\nSunn hemp ka fibre stem se milta hai. [Q73, Q74, Q75]\n● Cattle artificial insemination ke liye bull semen/sperms Liquid Nitrogen mein store kiye jaate hain. [Q76,\nQ77]\n● Kadaknath Indian chicken/fowl breed hai; Holstein high milk-yielding cattle breed hai.\nBhadawari→buffalo, Sindhi/Tharparkar→cow aur Jamunapari→goat—so 'Sheep–Tharparkar' wrong pair\nhai. [Q78, Q79, Q80]\n● Rashtriya Gokul Mission ka focus indigenous cow breeds ko conserve aur develop karna hai. [Q81]\n● Useful matching: Myoglobin→muscle cell; Sarpagandha→tranquilizer; Carcinoma→radiotherapy;\nHaemoglobin→oxygen transport. Bulimia→eating disorder; Cholesterol→egg-yolk; Atropine→alkaloid;\nInsulin→pancreas. [Q82, Q83]\n● Indian scientists ne microorganism-derived cadmium sulphide semiconductor nanoparticle use karke\nelectronic diode fabricate kiya; source yeast Schizosaccharomyces pombe ko link karta hai. [Q84]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n6. Medical Substances, Contraception & Scientific Fields\n● Anaesthetics sensation/awareness reduce karne ke liye use hote hain; source Chloroform, Nitrous oxide,\npentothal sodium etc. mention karta hai. Hospitals mein Nitrous oxide mild anaesthetic gas ke roop mein\nuse hoti hai. [Q85, Q86]\n● Specialist matching: Cardiologist→Heart; Nephrologist→Kidney; Urologist→Urinary tract; Oculist→Eye.\nNeurology nervous system disorders se related branch hai. [Q87, Q88]\n● Source IOC context mein Colostrum ko safe dietary supplement batata hai; HGH, Testosterone aur\nErythropoietin banned performance-enhancing substances hain. Saccharin artificial sweetener hai,\ncarbohydrate nahi; Phenolphthalein acid-base indicator/laxative hai, antiseptic nahi. [Q89, Q90, Q91]\n● Saheli ek non-steroidal oral contraceptive pill hai; CDRI Lucknow ne centchroman/ormeloxifene\nmolecule develop kiya aur source ise once-per-week indigenous pill batata hai. [Q92]\n● Foetal growth monitor karne ke liye Ultrasonics/Ultrasound use hota hai. [Q93]\n● Scientist-field matching: Birbal Sahni→Palaeobotany; K.C. Mehta→Plant Pathology; P.\nMaheshwari→Embryology; M.S. Swaminathan→Green Revolution. [Q94]\n● Other matching: Verghese Kurien→Co-operative Movement; Malcolm Adiseshiah→Development\nEconomics; A.P.J. Abdul Kalam→Space; Pramod Karan Sethi→Jaipur Prosthetic Foot. [Q95]\n● Global Invasive Species Database (GISD) alien/invasive species ki information deta hai aur IUCN ke\nInvasive Species Specialist Group se associated hai. [Q96]\n7. Research Institutes, Gene Banks & Organisations\n● IVRI Izatnagar, Bareilly mein located hai; CDRI Lucknow mein hai. [Q97, Q98, Q99]\n● Survey of India national mapping/surveying agency hai, Ministry of Science & Technology ke under\nkaam karti hai; iska headquarters Dehradun mein hai. Central Electrochemical Research Institute\nKaraikudi (Tamil Nadu) mein hai, Kolkata mein nahi. [Q100, Q101, Q102]\n● CIRG Makhdoom near Mathura mein; High Security Animal Disease Laboratory Bhopal mein; CIMAP\nLucknow mein; BSIP/Birbal Sahni Institute of Palaeosciences Lucknow mein autonomous/non-CSIR\ninstitute hai. [Q103, Q104, Q105, Q106]\n● Indian Institute of Vegetable Research Varanasi mein hai, Gorakhpur mein nahi; National Institute for the\nMentally Handicapped (now NIEPID) Secunderabad/Hyderabad mein hai. [Q107, Q108]\n● Institute-location matching: CDRI→Lucknow; JALMA Institute→Agra; MNNIT→Allahabad/Prayagraj;\nNational Sugar Institute→Kanpur. CIMAP→Lucknow; CDFD→Hyderabad; IMTECH→Chandigarh;\nNII→New Delhi. [Q109, Q110]\n● National Institute of Virology Pune mein; CDFD Hyderabad mein; Indian Vegetable Research Institute\nVaranasi mein; CISH Lucknow mein (Srinagar nahi); ALIMCO head office Kanpur mein. [Q111, Q112,\nQ113, Q114, Q115]\n● International Rice Genebank IRRI, Los Baños (Philippines) mein hai; International Potato Centre (CIP)\nLima, Peru mein; FAO HQ→Rome, Central Agmark Lab→Nagpur, Central Rice Research\nInstitute→Cuttack, Central Potato Research Institute→Shimla. [Q116, Q117, Q118]\n● NBRI Lucknow mein hai, Kolkata mein nahi; NBPGR headquarters New Delhi mein; Rajiv Gandhi Centre\nfor Biotechnology Thiruvananthapuram mein hai. [Q119, Q120, Q121]\n● World's first camel hospital source ke according Dubai mein hai. Camel hump fat store karta hai; UN ne\n2024 ko International Year of Camelids designate kiya. [Q122, Q123, Q124]\n● Matching: Testosterone→Hormone; Codeine→Sedative drug; Caoutchouc→rubber-source substance;\nEugenol→clove aromatic oil. Anthrax→biowarfare toxin; Thalassemia→defective-gene disease;\nSurrogacy→womb-renting; Transgenics→genome alteration. [Q125, Q126]\n● Quinine malaria treatment ka alkaloid hai, antibiotic nahi. [Q127]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Source ke according first 'dinosaurium' Hyderabad ke B.M. Birla Science Centre mein khula; WHO\nheadquarters Geneva mein hai; India ka first Dental College 1920 mein Kolkata mein R. Ahmed Dental\nCollege tha. [Q128, Q129, Q130]\n8. Scientists, Bees, Human Responses & Vaccination\n● Linus Pauling ne cancer aur ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) ke field mein research ki; source unke Chemistry\nNobel 1954 aur Peace Nobel 1962 ka mention karta hai. [Q131]\n● Honey bee landmine detection mein useful social insect hai. Hive members smell se ek-doosre ko\nidentify karte hain; food-source direction/distance communicate karne ke liye waggle dance use hota\nhai. Karl von Frisch ne honey-bee language/waggle dance decode karne par work kiya. [Q132, Q133, Q134,\nQ135, Q136]\n● Alcohol, marijuana aur opium depressants diye gaye hain, jabki cigarette smoke stimulant hai. Silica gel\nmoisture absorb karne wala desiccant hai. Shanti Swarup Bhatnagar science/CSIR research leadership\nse associated hain. [Q137, Q138, Q139]\n● Eye donation/transplant mein Cornea use hota hai. High humidity mein sweat properly evaporate nahi\nhota, isliye discomfort hota hai; sweat evaporation endothermic process hai aur body ko cool karta hai.\nDehydration mein water ke saath salts—mainly sodium chloride—lose hote hain; sea water dehydration\novercome karne ke liye suitable nahi hai. [Q140, Q141, Q142, Q143, Q144]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — BAC — Source Answer Disputed\n ▸BAC = Blood Alcohol Concentration. Source explanation ke according >0.45% BAC fatal ho sakta hai, jabki\nbiologically >0.4% bhi fatal ho sakta hai; JKPSC key aur explanation ke beech issue ko source disputed mark\nkarta hai. [Q145]\n● Ivan Pavlov Experimental Psychology/classical conditioning se linked hain. Women/children ki voice\npitch men se generally higher hoti hai. Source climate-change indicators mein plant fossils ko floral\nindicator batata hai aur 'long-term change' ko given option-set mein indicator nahi maanta. [Q146, Q147,\nQ148]\n● Cell-function matching: Photosynthesis→Chloroplast; Mineral uptake→Plasma membrane;\nRespiration→Mitochondria; Protein synthesis→Ribosomes. J.C. Bose plants mein life-response\nresearch se associated hain. [Q149, Q150]\n● Low temperature food spoilage microorganisms ki activity ko retard karta hai; source Pig ko given\nanimals mein fibre properly digest na karne wala batata hai, jabki goat/cow/elephant ruminant context\nmein diye gaye hain. [Q151, Q152]\n● Philatelist postage stamps collect karta hai; Biojector painless needle-free injector system hai; Robert\nGordon Webster avian influenza/influenza-virus expert hain. [Q153, Q154, Q155]\n● Edward Jenner smallpox vaccine aur 'Father of Immunology' se linked hain; Jonas Salk ne successful\nPolio vaccine develop ki. [Q156, Q157, Q158]\n● Scientist-discovery matching: Arber & Smith→restriction endonucleases; Feldmann→Agrobacterium T-\nDNA transgenic plants; Mullis→PCR; Temin & Baltimore→reverse transcriptase. [Q159]\n● Francis Collins→Human Genome Project/gene discoveries; Sergey Brin→Google; Jimmy\nWales→Wikipedia—source teeno pairs ko correct maanta hai. [Q160]\n9. Dating, Soil, Ecology, Plant Technology & Fibres\n● William Morris Davis erosion cycle/geographical cycle of erosion concept se linked hain; Auxanometer\nplant growth-rate measure karta hai; Mestizo Latin America mein mixed European + Indigenous\nancestry ke person ke liye term hai. [Q161, Q162, Q163]\n● Ancient rocks ki age ke liye Uranium–Lead process use ho sakta hai; organic fossils ki age ke liye\nCarbon-14 radiocarbon dating; tree ki age annual/growth rings count karke estimate ki ja sakti hai. [Q164,\nQ165, Q166]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Clay soil fine particles ki wajah se highest water retention dikha sakti hai; alkaline soils ko gypsum\naddition, leaching/drainage etc. se reclaim/improve kiya ja sakta hai. [Q167, Q168]\n● Butterflies pollination aur crop production mein important hain. Eichhornia/Water hyacinth ko 'Terror of\nBengal' kaha jata hai; Red tide algal/dinoflagellate bloom se related phenomenon hai. [Q169, Q170, Q171]\n● Spirogyra mainly freshwater green algae hai, ocean mein nahi; source Ulothrix ko fresh + marine water\nse link karta hai. Mycorrhiza fungus aur vascular plant roots ka symbiotic association hai jo\nabsorption/drought tolerance etc. improve kar sakta hai. [Q172, Q173]\n● Biorock technology damaged coral reefs/marine ecosystems restoration se related hai. Phytotron\ncontrolled-condition plant research facility hai; Polytunnel/Polyhouse plants grow/protect karne ke liye\nuse hota hai. [Q174, Q175, Q176]\n● Fibre matching: Linen→Flax; Coir→Coconut; Mohair→Angora goat; Down→duck/geese feathers.\nAngora wool/fibre Angora rabbit se milta hai, mohair se alag hai. [Q177, Q178, Q179, Q180]\n● Bioluminescence living organism ke andar chemical reaction se produced light hai; source Luciferin +\nLuciferase/Photoprotein ko key chemicals batata hai. [Q181]\n10. Agriculture, Immunity, Policy & General Science\n● Green Revolution mein high-yielding crops ke liye more fertilizer aur more water ki need source mein\nhighlight hai. Revolution matching: Green→Food grains; White→Milk; Yellow→Oilseeds;\nBlue→Fish/Aquaculture. [Q182, Q183]\n● Green Revolution ka principal crop source mein Mexican Wheat diya gaya hai; rice nursery ka Dapog\nmethod Philippines se aaya; India ki first dwarf rice variety source ke according Jaya thi. [Q184, Q185,\nQ186]\n● Gambusia insectivorous fish ponds/wells mein mosquito larvae/eggs eat karke mosquito population\ncontrol mein help karti hai. [Q187, Q188]\n● Active acquired immunity antibodies/immunoglobulins ki production se develop hoti hai; B-lymphocytes\nantibodies banate hain. [Q189]\n● Science & Technology Policy 2003 ko 3 Jan 2003, 90th Indian Science Congress (Bengaluru) context\nmein launch kiya gaya; source innovation, resource utilisation, hazard-management technologies aur\nintellectual property management jaise objectives deta hai. [Q190]\n● Source ke according tobacco/products ki sale par ban lagane wala first country Bhutan tha (Dec 2004).\nGiven planets mein Mars life-existence ke liye possible/suitable option diya gaya hai. Natural-system\ndevelopment ko self-sustained process of systems se link kiya gaya hai. [Q191, Q192, Q193]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — TIVA / TIBA — Source Ambiguity\n ▸TIVA = Total Intravenous Anaesthesia. Source Q194 mein Chandra Shekhar Azad University wale substance\nka context clear nahi hai aur possible intended term TIBA (2,3,5-Triiodobenzoic acid; anti-auxin) ho sakta hai,\nisliye question marked (*) hai. [Q194]\n● Knowledge ko source 'justified true belief' (JTB) se link karta hai. Scientific investigation observation,\nexperimentation aur analysis par based hoti hai aur honesty scientific process ke liye essential hai.\nSemantic memory general facts/ideas/concepts store karti hai; information ko\norganize/understand/communicate karne wali mental activity Thinking hai. [Q195, Q196, Q197, Q198]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0330","t":"01 Atomic Structure","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Atomic Structure Full Mind Map\n⚛️ ATOMIC STRUCTURE — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Modern Chemistry & Dalton Atomic Theory\n2. Early Atomic Models — Thomson & Rutherford\n3. Atom, Nucleus & Basic Constituents\n4. Discovery Timeline — Electron, Proton, Neutron & π-Meson\n5. Subatomic, Fundamental & Antiparticle Concepts\n6. Higgs Boson — “God Particle” & Mass\n7. Charge Map — Neutron, Neutrino, Alpha & Beta\n8. Orbitals & Quantum Numbers\n9. Mass Number & Neutron Calculations\n10. Isotopes & Isoneutronic / Isotone Groups\n11. Radioactivity — Detection & Discovery\n1. Modern Chemistry & Dalton Atomic Theory\n● Antoine Lavoisier ko ‘Father of Modern Chemistry’ maana jata hai. Combustion mein oxygen ki role ko\nestablish karne, oxygen (1778) aur hydrogen (1783) ko name karne aur chemical nomenclature ko reform\nkarne mein unka major contribution tha. [Q1]\n● Dalton atomic theory ke according matter atoms se bana hai. Is theory ne law of conservation of mass,\nlaw of constant composition aur law of multiple proportions ko explain kiya; radioactivity ko explain nahi\nkiya. [Q2]\n2. Early Atomic Models — Thomson & Rutherford\n● J.J. Thomson ne atom ka pehla structural model propose kiya — positively charged sphere ke andar\nelectrons embedded hone wala ‘plum pudding’ model. Baad mein Rutherford aur Bohr ke models ne isse\nreplace kiya. [Q3]\n● Atomic nucleus ki discovery Ernest Rutherford se associate ki jati hai. Gold-foil / Geiger–Marsden\nexperiment ke observations se clear hua ki atom ka almost sara positive charge aur mass ek bahut\nchhote dense centre mein concentrated hota hai. [Q11]\n3. Atom, Nucleus & Basic Constituents\n● Atom ka centre wala positively charged dense part nucleus kehlata hai. Nucleus mainly protons aur\nneutrons se milkar bana hota hai; in dono ko collectively nucleons kehte hain. [Q4, Q5, Q6]\n● Electron nucleus ke andar nahi hota; atom ke surrounding region/orbitals mein milta hai. Neutral atom\nmein number of protons = number of electrons hota hai, isliye net charge zero hota hai. [Q7]\n● Basic atomic picture mein protons + neutrons nucleus mein concentrated hote hain, jabki electrons\nnucleus ke around shells/orbitals mein occupy karte hain. [Q8]\n● Proton, neutron aur electron atom ke main constituent particles hain. Photon electromagnetic radiation\nka quantum hai, atom ka structural constituent nahi. [Q9]\n● Element ek aisa pure substance hai jisme same atomic number/type ke atoms hote hain; compounds\naur mixtures mein ek se zyada kinds of atoms/elements involve ho sakte hain. [Q10]\n4. Discovery Timeline — Electron, Proton, Neutron & π-Meson\n● Exam chronology: electron — J.J. Thomson (1897) → proton — Rutherford se associated (source:\n1919) → neutron — James Chadwick (1932) → π-meson — Cecil Powell (1947). Isliye order III → IV → II\n→ I hai. [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Atomic Structure Full Mind Map\n● James Chadwick ne 1932 mein neutron discover kiya. Neutron electrically neutral particle hai aur\nnucleus ka important constituent hai. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Proton Discovery — Exam Chronology vs Historical Detail — Q12\n\n▸Source chronology Rutherford/proton ko 1919 ke saath use karti hai. Exam sequence ke liye electron 1897\n→ proton → neutron 1932 → π-meson 1947 yaad rakhein. [Q12]\n\n▸Goldstein ki canal rays (1886) positive rays ka earlier observation tha; Rutherford ko proton\nidentification/nuclear hydrogen context se associate kiya jata hai. [Q12]\n5. Subatomic, Fundamental & Antiparticle Concepts\n● Deuteron, deuterium nucleus hai jisme 1 proton + 1 neutron hota hai. Ye composite nucleus hai;\nelectron/proton/neutron jaise basic constituent-particle list se alag category mein aata hai. [Q14]\n● Positron electron ka antiparticle hai: mass electron ke equal hota hai, lekin charge +1e hota hai. Electron\nka charge −1e hota hai. [Q15]\n● Source matching: neutrino → historically ‘zero mass’; quark → fractional charge (+2/3e ya −1/3e);\npositron → spin 1/2; phonon → integral-spin bosonic quasiparticle. [Q16]\n● Quarks fundamental particles hain; proton aur neutron composite hadrons hain jo quarks se bane hote\nhain. [Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Deuteron & Neutrino — Source Simplification — Q14, Q16\n\n▸Deuteron technically ek composite subatomic nucleus/particle hai; source ka intent ise elementary/basic\nconstituent particle se distinguish karna hai. [Q14]\n\n▸Neutrino ko old texts mein zero-mass likha milta hai, lekin modern physics neutrino oscillations se tiny non-\nzero mass establish karti hai. Exam mein source-era wording ko context ke saath dekhein. [Q16]\n6. Higgs Boson — “God Particle” & Mass\n● Higgs boson ko popular media mein ‘God Particle’ kaha gaya. Ye Higgs field se related elementary\nboson hai, aur Higgs mechanism elementary particles ko mass acquire karne ko explain karta hai. [Q18,\nQ19, Q20]\n● Higgs boson discovery ka real significance ye samajhna hai ki elementary particles mass kyun rakhte\nhain. Matter teleportation ya better nuclear-fission fuel iska direct implication nahi hai. [Q21]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Higgs Boson — Discovery Year — Q19–Q21\n\n▸Higgs-like boson discovery CERN ke ATLAS/CMS experiments ne July 2012 mein announce ki; 2013 Nobel\nPrize Higgs mechanism theory ke liye Higgs aur Englert ko mila. Source ki ‘2013 proved’ wording ko exact\ndiscovery date na samjhein. [Q19, Q21]\n\n▸‘God Particle’ popular nickname hai; scientific name Higgs boson hi hai. [Q18, Q19, Q20]\n7. Charge Map — Neutron, Neutrino, Alpha & Beta\n● Neutron electrically neutral hota hai. Given charged-particle comparisons mein proton +1e, electron −1e\naur alpha particle +2e charge carry karta hai. [Q22]\n● Neutrino ka electric charge zero hota hai aur mass extremely small but non-zero maana jata hai.\nPositron +1e, electron −1e aur alpha particle +2e hota hai. [Q23]\n● Alpha particle basically helium-4 nucleus hota hai: 2 protons + 2 neutrons. Isliye iska mass helium\nnucleus ke nearly equal hota hai aur charge +2e hota hai. [Q24, Q25, Q28]\n● Ordinary hydrogen ka most common isotope protium (¹H) nucleus sirf 1 proton rakhta hai aur neutron\nzero hota hai. [Q26]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Atomic Structure Full Mind Map\n● Standard β particle high-speed electron hota hai aur negative charge carry karta hai; X-rays aur gamma\n⁻\n\nrays neutral electromagnetic radiation hain. [Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Beta Particle — Beta-minus vs Beta-plus — Q27\n\n▸Exam mein ‘beta particle carries negative charge’ usually β electron ko refer karta hai. β decay mein\n⁻\n⁺\npositron emit hota hai, jiska charge positive hota hai. [Q27]\n8. Orbitals & Quantum Numbers\n● Aufbau principle orbital-filling order govern karta hai: electrons pehle lower-energy orbitals fill karte hain,\nphir higher-energy orbitals. [Q29]\n● Magnetic quantum number m orbital ki spatial orientation batata hai. Principal quantum number n\nₗ\nshell/energy level, azimuthal quantum number l subshell/orbital shape, aur spin quantum number m ₛ\nelectron spin ko represent karta hai. [Q30]\n9. Mass Number & Neutron Calculations\n● Neutral atom mein electrons = protons. Agar electrons 18 aur neutrons 20 hain, to protons 18 honge;\nmass number A = p + n = 18 + 20 = 38. [Q31]\n● Mass number nucleus ke protons + neutrons ka sum hai; electrons mass-number calculation mein count\nnahi hote. 2p + 2n wala atom ka A = 4. [Q32, Q33]\n● ²⁴²Pu\n ke liye neutron number N = A − Z = 242 − 94 = 148.\n₉₄\n[Q34]\n10. Isotopes & Isoneutronic / Isotone Groups\n● Isotopes same element ke atoms hote hain: atomic number / proton number same hota hai, neutron\nnumber different; isliye mass number different hota hai. [Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38]\n● Isoneutronic / isotone nuclei mein neutron number same hota hai, proton number different. ¹⁴C , ¹⁵N aur\n₆\n₇\n\n¹⁶O tino mein neutrons = 8, isliye ye isoneutronic group banate hain.\n₈\n[Q39]\n11. Radioactivity — Detection & Discovery\n● Geiger–Müller counter ionizing radiation ko detect/count karne ka instrument hai aur radioactivity\nmeasurement context mein commonly poocha jata hai. [Q40]\n● Radioactivity ki discovery Henri Becquerel ne 1896 mein uranium salts ke saath experiments ke dauran\nki thi. [Q41]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Radioactivity — Instrument vs SI Unit — Q40\n\n▸Geiger–Müller counter radiation detect/count karne ka instrument hai. Radioactive activity ki SI unit\nBecquerel (Bq) hoti hai — instrument aur unit ko mix na karein. [Q40]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0331","t":"02 Physical and Chemical Changes Solution","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical & Chemical Changes, Solution Full Mind Map\n🧪 PHYSICAL & CHEMICAL CHANGES, SOLUTION — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Physical vs Chemical Changes & Reaction Rate\n2. Pasteurization & Phosphatase Test\n3. Boiling / Freezing Point & Solution Concentration\n4. Ideal Solutions & Electrolyte Conductivity\n5. Colloids, Emulsions & Homogeneous Solutions\n6. Osmosis & Reverse Osmosis\n7. Separation & Purification Techniques\n8. Oxidation Number\n9. Catalysts & Reaction Energy\n10. Displacement Reaction & Corrosion\n1. Physical vs Chemical Changes & Reaction Rate\n● Physical change mein substance ka form/state badalta hai, chemical composition nahi. Water mein sugar\ndissolve karna reversible physical change hai; evaporation se sugar recover ki ja sakti hai. [Q1]\n● Water ka liquid se vapour banna physical change hai, kyunki H O ki chemical identity same rehti hai; sirf state\n₂\n\nchange hoti hai. [Q2]\n● Chemical change mein molecular composition badalti hai aur new substance banta hai. Vegetables ka\ncook/soften hona irreversible chemical change ka example hai. [Q3]\n● NaCl crystallization aur ice melting physical changes hain; milk souring chemical change hai, kyunki lactose\nlactic acid mein convert hota hai. [Q4]\n● Fruit ripening, cement setting aur coal burning tino chemical changes hain aur broadly exothermic nature\nshow karte hain; source mein “no odd one” diya hai. [Q5]\n● Higher temperature par molecules ki kinetic energy aur collision frequency badhti hai, isliye chemical reaction\ngenerally faster hoti hai. [Q6]\n● Reaction/decomposition context mein energy change reaction type par depend karta hai; source Q7 “heat”\nkey karta hai, lekin wording ko carefully read karna chahiye. [Q7]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q7 — “Decomposition of Water” Wording\n\n▸Agar question actual electrolysis/decomposition of water ki baat kare, to electrical energy input hoti hai. Source\nexplanation hydrolysis se mix ho rahi hai aur “heat produced” key scientifically context-dependent/ambiguous hai.\n[Q7]\n2. Pasteurization & Phosphatase Test\n● Pasteurization mein milk ko controlled temperature tak heat karke specified time ke baad rapidly cool kiya jata\nhai, jisse pathogenic microbes drastically reduce hote hain aur shelf-life improve hoti hai. [Q8]\n● Milk pasteurization ko exam options mein “sterilization” se relate kiya ja sakta hai, lekin scientifically ye\ncomplete sterilization nahi, controlled heat-treatment / partial microbial reduction hai. [Q9]\n● Desalination–sea water, reverse osmosis–potable water aur denaturation–proteins sahi matches hain;\npasteurization–tea standard match nahi hai. [Q10]\n● Phosphatase test ka standard dairy use ye check karna hai ki milk pasteurization adequate hua ya nahi.\nSource key wider “all of the above” deti hai. [Q11]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical & Chemical Changes, Solution Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Pasteurization ≠ Complete Sterilization\n\n▸Pasteurization pathogens ko reduce/inactivate karti hai; sari microorganisms/spores ko necessarily destroy nahi\nkarti. Isliye “sterilization of milk” exam-option shorthand hai, exact scientific definition nahi. [Q9]\n\n▸Phosphatase test ka established dairy use pasteurization adequacy check karna hai; source ka Tea/Water tak “all\nabove” answer exam-key specific maana jaye. [Q11]\n3. Boiling / Freezing Point & Solution Concentration\n● Non-volatile impurity add karne par liquid ka vapour pressure kam hota hai aur boiling point increase hota hai\n— ise boiling-point elevation kehte hain. [Q12]\n● Ice + salt freezing mixture 0°C se neeche temperature de sakta hai, kyunki salt freezing point ko lower karta\nhai; “salt freezing point badhata hai” statement false hai. [Q13]\n● Solution ki concentration = given amount/volume/mass of solution ya solvent mein present solute ki quantity\nka measure. [Q14]\n● Ideal solution ke liye ΔHmix = 0 hota hai aur solution Raoult’s law follow karta hai; A–B interactions roughly\nA–A/B–B ke comparable hote hain. [Q15]\n● Salt jaise non-volatile solute se water ka boiling point badhta aur freezing point ghatta hai; methyl alcohol\njaise lower-boiling volatile component se mixture ka boiling point reduce ho sakta hai. [Q16]\n4. Ideal Solutions & Electrolyte Conductivity\n● Strong electrolyte ki specific conductivity (κ) dilution par generally decrease hoti hai, kyunki ions per unit\nvolume kam ho jate hain; molar conductivity ka trend alag hota hai. [Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Conductivity vs Molar Conductivity\n\n▸Dilution par specific conductivity κ decrease hoti hai, lekin molar conductivity Λm generally increase hoti hai. Exam\nmein “conductivity” kis quantity ko refer kar rahi hai, wording dekhein. [Q17]\n5. Colloids, Emulsions & Homogeneous Solutions\n● Milk oil-in-water type emulsion hai — fat droplets aqueous phase mein dispersed rehte hain; emulsion colloid\nka ek type hai. [Q18, Q19]\n● Milk, blood aur ice-cream colloidal systems ke examples hain; source ke according honey colloid nahi hai.\n[Q20]\n● Fog aerosol type colloid hai: tiny liquid water droplets gas/air mein dispersed rehti hain. [Q21]\n● Homogeneous solution ki composition throughout uniform hoti hai; salt-water homogeneous hai. “Different\ncomposition throughout” heterogeneous system describe karta hai. [Q22]\n● Source Q23 unsaturated sugar solution mein volume ko unchanged key karta hai; practical solution volume\nexact additive/unchanged maana nahi ja sakta. [Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Sugar Solution Volume — Source Simplification\n\n▸Solute dissolve karne par solution volume generally exactly initial solvent volume ke equal nahi rehta; molecular\ninteractions ki wajah se contraction/expansion ho sakta hai. Source Q23 ka “volume unchanged” idealized/exam-key\ntreatment hai. [Q23]\n6. Osmosis & Reverse Osmosis\n● Plant roots soil se water mainly osmosis ke through absorb karti hain — semipermeable membrane ke across\nsolvent lower solute concentration se higher solute concentration side move karta hai. [Q24]\n● Cucumber par salt lagane se outside solution hypertonic ho jata hai aur cell water bahar nikalta hai; ye\nosmosis/exosmosis ka example hai. [Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical & Chemical Changes, Solution Full Mind Map\n● Normal osmosis mein solvent dilute solution → concentrated solution jata hai. Reverse osmosis mein\nconcentrated side par external pressure apply karke flow reverse kiya jata hai. [Q26]\n● Pure solvent aur solution ke beech semipermeable membrane ho to solvent naturally solution side jata hai;\nise osmosis kahte hain, reverse osmosis nahi. [Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Osmosis Direction\n\n▸Osmosis mein solvent dilute/low-solute side se concentrated/high-solute side jata hai. Reverse osmosis mein\npressure concentrated side par apply hota hai — dono direction statements frequently reverse pooche jate hain.\n[Q26, Q27]\n7. Separation & Purification Techniques\n● Distillation mainly liquid mixtures/liquid purification ke liye useful hai; solid purification mein sublimation aur\ncrystallization common techniques hain. [Q28]\n● Chromatography mixture ke components ko stationary aur mobile phases ke beech differential distribution ke\nbasis par separate karti hai. [Q29]\n● Camphor ka solid se directly vapour mein jana sublimation hai — beech mein liquid phase nahi aati. [Q30]\n● Camphor, naphthalene aur dry ice jaise substances solid → gas direct transition dikhate hain; phenomenon\nsublimation kehlata hai. [Q31, Q32]\n● Sand + naphthalene mixture ko sublimation se separate kiya ja sakta hai: naphthalene sublime karta hai,\nsand nahi. [Q33]\n8. Oxidation Number\n● Oxidation-number matching: Mn in MnO = +4; S in H SO = +6; Ca in CaO = +2; Al in NaAlH = +3. Isliye\n₂\n₂\n₄\n₄\nA-3, B-4, C-1, D-2 mapping banti hai. [Q34]\n9. Catalysts & Reaction Energy\n● Catalyst reaction rate increase karta hai aur promoter catalyst ki activity enhance karta hai. Reaction ko slow\nkarne wale substances inhibitors/negative catalysts kehlate hain; given options mein none correct tha. [Q35]\n● Exothermic process heat release karta hai: concentrated H SO ka dilution aur quicklime (CaO) + water\n₂\n₄\nreaction exothermic hain. Water evaporation aur camphor sublimation endothermic hain. [Q36]\n10. Displacement Reaction & Corrosion\n● Displacement reaction mein more reactive metal less reactive metal ko uske salt solution se displace karta\nhai. Cu, AgNO se Ag ko displace karke copper nitrate + silver banata hai.\n₃\n[Q37]\n● Corrosion metals ka gradual chemical deterioration hai: iron par brown rust, copper par green patina aur silver\npar black tarnish tino corrosion ke examples hain. [Q38]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0332","t":"03 Inorganic Chemistry","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Inorganic Chemistry Full Mind Map\n🧪 INORGANIC CHEMISTRY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Periodic Table — History & Periodic Trends\n2. Oxides & Valency\n3. Elemental Abundance — Earth & Universe\n4. How Many Elements? — Modern Count\n5. Element Classification & Diamond\n6. First Artificial Element — Technetium\n1. Periodic Table — History & Periodic Trends\n● UNESCO ne 2019 ko International Year of the Periodic Table ke roop mein celebrate kiya. Ye Mendeleev ki\n1869 wali periodic table ke 150 years complete hone ki anniversary thi. [Q1]\n● Group mein top se bottom atomic radius generally increase hoti hai, kyunki electron shells badhte hain.\nElectron affinity ka overall trend generally less favourable/decrease hota hai; isliye “hamesha increase hoti hai”\nassertion false hai, jabki radius wala reason true hai. [Q2]\n● Period mein left se right effective nuclear attraction badhne ke karan atomic radius generally decrease,\nionization potential generally increase aur electronegativity generally increase karti hai. Group mein neeche\njaane par electron affinity ka simple exam trend decrease maana gaya hai. [Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Electron Affinity Trend — “Always” se bachna\n\n▸Electron affinity ka trend completely smooth nahi hota; Be/Mg, N/P, noble gases aur halogens mein notable\nexceptions/sign-convention issues milte hain. Exam mein “always” word ho to statement ko carefully evaluate karo.\n[Q2, Q3]\n2. Oxides & Valency\n● Source ke according Group 3 aur Group 4 ke oxides mein basic aur acidic dono behaviour mil sakta hai, yani\namphoteric nature poochha gaya hai. [Q4]\n● Common valency mapping: Silicon = 4, Fluorine = 1, Aluminium = 3, Sulphur = 2. Isliye correct match Si-(iv),\nF-(i), Al-(iii), S-(ii) hai. [Q5]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q4 — Group 3/4 Oxides ka broad generalisation\n\n▸Har Group 3 aur Group 4 oxide ko universally “amphoteric” kehna oversimplification hai. Different oxidation states\naur elements ke oxides basic, amphoteric ya acidic character dikha sakte hain; source answer ko exam-context\nmein yaad rakho. [Q4]\n3. Elemental Abundance — Earth & Universe\n● Earth’s crust mein mass percentage ke hisab se Oxygen sabse abundant element hai — roughly 46.6%. Uske\nbaad Silicon lagbhag 27.7%, phir Aluminium aur Iron aate hain. [Q6, Q7]\n● Oxygen ke baad Earth’s crust mein Silicon second most abundant element hai. Silicon semiconductor\nmaterial ke roop mein computer/electronic chips mein extensively use hota hai. [Q8]\n● Universe mein Hydrogen sabse abundant chemical element hai; ordinary/baryonic matter ke mass ka roughly\nthree-fourths Hydrogen se aur major remaining share Helium se bana hai. [Q9]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q8 — “Earth’s Surface” vs “Earth’s Crust”\n\n▸Source wording “Earth’s surface” use karti hai, lekin standard abundance fact crust-by-mass ke context mein\nOxygen first aur Silicon second hai. Question ko crust/surface wording ke saath confuse mat karo. [Q8]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Inorganic Chemistry Full Mind Map\n4. How Many Elements? — Modern Count\n● Modern periodic table mein 118 identified/named chemical elements hain. Q10 ke options 300, 250, 200 aur\n100 the; inmein exact correct answer nahi tha, isliye source ne question ko disputed (*) mark kiya hai. [Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q10 — Correct Modern Count = 118\n\n▸118 accepted elements hain. “100” sirf historical options mein closest choice hai; factually exact answer nahi. Aise\nquestion mein current scientific count ko priority do. [Q10]\n5. Element Classification & Diamond\n● Diamond chemically crystalline Carbon ka allotrope hai, isliye ye elemental form hai. Sand mainly SiO ,\n₂\nmarble mainly CaCO aur sugar carbon-hydrogen-oxygen containing compound hoti hai.\n₃\n[Q11, Q12]\n● Periodic-table elements ko broadly metals, non-metals aur metalloids mein classify kiya jata hai. “Gas” ek\nphysical state of matter hai, element ki fundamental classification category nahi. [Q13]\n6. First Artificial Element — Technetium\n● Technetium (Tc), atomic number 43, ko first artificially produced element maana jata hai. Carlo Perrier aur\nEmilio Segrè ne 1937 mein is element ko identify/isolate kiya. [Q14]\n● Symbol-based question mein first artificially prepared element = Tc (Technetium). Te = Tellurium, Th =\nThorium aur Tl = Thallium is answer ke alternatives nahi hain. [Q15]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0333","t":"04 Metals Minerals Ores Properties Uses","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Metals, Minerals & Ores Full Mind Map\n🧪 METALS, MINERALS & ORES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Metallurgy, Metallic Character & Reactivity\n2. Magnetism, Hardness, Ductility & Extreme Properties\n3. Heavy / Costly Metals — Meaning Matters\n4. Pearl, Ruby, Sapphire & Corundum\n5. Sodium, Noble Metals, Gold & White Metals\n6. Minerals, Talc, Quicklime, Limestone & Cement\n7. Gypsum & Plaster of Paris\n8. Monazite, Mica & Thermal Conductivity\n9. Liquid Metals, Mercury & Reaction with Water\n10. Iron Ores, Rusting & Galvanization\n11. Protective Coatings & Reducing Power\n12. Key Metal Properties & Electrical Conductivity\n13. Aluminium — Bauxite and Other Ores\n14. Industrial Processes & Material–Composition Matching\n15. Density & Melting-Point Comparisons\n1. Metallurgy, Metallic Character & Reactivity\n● Smelting mein ore ko high temperature par reduce karke metal molten/fused state mein obtain kiya jata hai.\nRoasting, calcination aur froth-floatation alag metallurgical operations hain. [Q1]\n● Electronic configuration 2,8,8,2 Calcium (Z=20) ki hai; outer shell ke 2 electrons lose karke Ca² banana\n⁺\nmetallic/electropositive behaviour dikhata hai. [Q2]\n● Electrophile electron-pair acceptor hota hai. BF aur H strongly electron-deficient electrophiles hain; source Na ko\n₃\n⁺\n⁺\nstable-octet ke karan “true electrophile” nahi maanta. [Q3]\n● Common reactivity series: K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > H > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au. Given options mein\nPotassium sabse reactive metal hai. [Q4]\n● Food cans par Tin coating Zinc se safer hoti hai, kyunki Zn zyada reactive hai aur food acids ke saath react kar\nsakta hai; Sn comparatively less reactive hai. [Q5]\n2. Magnetism, Hardness, Ductility & Extreme Properties\n● Platinum paramagnetic hai; Iron/Nickel ferromagnetic aur Mercury diamagnetic behaviour dikhata hai. Cu² ⁺\nparamagnetic aur Gd ferromagnetic pair hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● Lithium sabse light metal (very low density) aur Osmium densest naturally occurring metal maana jata hai. [Q8]\n● Given metals mein Tungsten hardest hai; natural substances mein Diamond conventionally hardest maana jata hai.\n[Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● Nichrome (mainly Ni + Cr, often Fe) hard, ductile, high-resistivity aur high-temperature resistant alloy hai; heating\nelements mein useful hota hai. [Q12]\n3. Heavy / Costly Metals — Meaning Matters\n● Uranium (Z=92) heaviest naturally occurring element ke standard exam fact ke roop mein poochha jata hai;\nUranium-238 ka nucleus 92 protons + 146 neutrons rakhta hai. [Q13, Q14]\n● Given options Gold, Silver, Mercury aur Platinum mein density ke basis par Platinum sabse heavy hai (~21.1\ng/cm³). [Q15]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — “Heaviest” ka matlab clear karo\n\n▸Densest metal = Osmium; “heaviest natural element” = Uranium (atomic-number/mass context); kisi option-set mein\n“heaviest metal” density ke hisab se Platinum ho sakta hai. Wording dekhe bina ek hi fact apply mat karo. [Q8, Q13–Q15]\n● Q16 “recently discovered world’s costliest metal” ambiguous hai: Endohedral fullerene metal nahi aur\nCalifornium-252 1950 mein discover hua tha. Source ne answer disputed (*) rakha hai. [Q16]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Metals, Minerals & Ores Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q16 — Costliest Metal Question Disputed\n\n▸Price-per-gram lists time/source ke saath badalti hain, aur “recently discovered” phrase bhi vague hai. Is question ko\nfixed one-line fact ke roop mein memorize mat karo. [Q16]\n4. Pearl, Ruby, Sapphire & Corundum\n● Pearl ka major mineral component Calcium Carbonate hota hai, mostly Aragonite form mein (~82–86%); Conchiolin\nprotein binding matrix ka kaam karta hai. [Q17, Q18, Q19]\n● Ruby aur Sapphire dono gem-quality Corundum hain; chemically Corundum = Aluminium Oxide, Al O . Trace\n₂ ₃\nimpurities different colours produce karti hain. [Q20, Q21]\n5. Sodium, Noble Metals, Gold & White Metals\n● Sodium air/moisture ke saath vigorously react karta hai, isliye kerosene ke andar store kiya jata hai. Air mein “sirf\nmelt” hona reason nahi; major issue rapid/exothermic reaction hai. [Q22, Q23]\n● Sodium-vapour street lamps characteristic yellow/orange light deti hain; low-pressure sodium light nearly\nmonochromatic hoti hai, isliye fog/rain context mein visibility-oriented exam questions mein poochhi jati hai. [Q24, Q25]\n● Gold very unreactive/noble metal hai aur native/free state mein mil sakta hai. Noble metals oxidation/corrosion\nresist karte hain; Uranium aur Lead noble metals nahi hain. [Q26, Q27]\n● Pure Gold = 24 carat. Jewellery ke liye pure gold bahut soft hota hai, isliye Cu/Ag jaise metals ke saath alloy karke\n22K/18K banaya jata hai. [Q29]\n● “White metal” term broad/ambiguous hai; Platinum, Palladium aur Rhodium naturally silvery-white platinum-group\nmetals hain, isliye source ne more-than-one option key kiya. [Q30]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Gold kis acid mein dissolve hota hai?\n\n▸Gold kisi single H SO , HNO ya HCl mein normally dissolve nahi hota. Aqua regia = concentrated HCl : HNO ≈ 3:1\n₂\n₄\n₃\n₃\ngold dissolve karti hai. Q28 ke options mein correct mixture tha hi nahi, isliye source answer *. [Q28]\n6. Minerals, Talc, Quicklime, Limestone & Cement\n● Minerals geologically naturally occurring inorganic solids hote hain jinki characteristic composition aur physical\nproperties hoti hain. [Q31]\n● Ilmenite (FeTiO ) Titanium ka important ore/mineral hai aur Indian coastal beach sands mein milta hai.\n₃\n[Q32]\n● Talc/soapstone hydrated Magnesium Silicate hai aur Mohs scale par hardness 1 ke saath softest standard mineral\nmaana jata hai. [Q33]\n● Quicklime = Calcium Oxide (CaO); Limestone mainly Calcium Carbonate (CaCO ) hota hai.\n₃\n[Q34, Q35]\n● Cement mein lime/limestone-derived CaO major constituent hota hai, lekin silica, alumina/other clay components\naur gypsum bhi formulation ka part hote hain; source question ne “more than one” key kiya. [Q36]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Cement — “Main Ingredient” vs “Ingredients”\n\n▸Ordinary Portland cement ka largest oxide fraction CaO hota hai, lekin cement single-substance material nahi. Question\nagar ingredients/options multiple de to wording aur official key ko carefully read karo. [Q36]\n7. Gypsum & Plaster of Paris\n● Gypsum = Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate, CaSO ·2H O. Isko controlled heating/calcination se Plaster of Paris banaya\n₄\n₂\n\njata hai. [Q37, Q38, Q42]\n● Plaster of Paris ka exact formula CaSO ·½H O hai, yani Calcium Sulphate Hemihydrate. Doctors casts, artists\n₄\n₂\nmoulds aur sculptors ise use karte hain. [Q39, Q40, Q41]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — POP ko sirf “Calcium Sulphate” bolna incomplete hai\n\n▸Family name calcium sulphate sahi hai, lekin exact compound = calcium sulphate hemihydrate (CaSO ·½H O); Gypsum\n₄\n₂\n= dihydrate (CaSO ·2H O).\n₄\n₂\n[Q39, Q40, Q42]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Metals, Minerals & Ores Full Mind Map\n8. Monazite, Mica & Thermal Conductivity\n● Monazite Thorium ka important ore hai; ismein rare-earth elements jaise Lanthanum/Cerium bhi ho sakte hain, aur\nIndian coastal sands monazite-rich areas ke liye known hain. [Q43]\n● Mica electricity ka poor conductor/achha insulator hai, lekin heat tolerate/conduct kar sakta hai; isliye\nelectrical/electronics industry mein insulating raw material ke roop mein use hota hai. [Q44, Q45]\n● Given liquids Water/Ether/Benzene/Mercury mein Mercury metallic nature ki wajah se best heat conductor hai;\nmetals mein bhi Mercury comparatively very poor thermal conductor hai. [Q46, Q47]\n9. Liquid Metals, Mercury & Reaction with Water\n● Mercury ordinary room temperature par liquid metal hai (quicksilver). Thermometers mein historically uniform\nexpansion, visible column aur glass ko wet na karne jaise properties useful rahi hain. [Q48, Q50]\n● Lead water ke saath generally react nahi karta; Copper steam ke saath bhi react nahi karta. Mg hot water aur Al/Fe\nsteam ke saath reaction show kar sakte hain. [Q51, Q52]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q49 — Francium “room-temperature liquid”\n\n▸Standard room-temperature examples: Mercury (metal) aur Bromine (non-metal) liquid hote hain. Francium ka melting\npoint estimate room temperature ke bahut paas aur experimentally uncertain hai; source ne given options mein Francium\nkey kiya, ise exam-specific fact samjho. [Q49]\n10. Iron Ores, Rusting & Galvanization\n● Iron ka major ore Haematite (Fe O ) hai; Bailadila (Chhattisgarh) high-grade Haematite iron ore ke liye famous hai.\n₂ ₃\n[Q53, Q54]\n● Rusting mein Iron oxygen + moisture se hydrated iron(III) oxide banata hai; oxygen/moisture add hone ke karan\nobject ka measured weight initially increase karta hai. [Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● Iron corrosion/rusting ke liye oxygen aur moisture dono essential conditions hain. [Q62]\n● Galvanization mein iron/steel par Zinc coating hoti hai. Zinc barrier bhi deta hai aur preferential oxidation/sacrificial\nprotection ke through iron ko rusting se bachata hai. [Q58, Q59, Q60, Q61]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — “Galvanized iron does not rust” absolute statement nahi\n\n▸Intact zinc coating strong protection deti hai, lekin coating damage/exhaust hone par underlying iron rust kar sakta hai.\nExam assertion ko galvanization principle ke context mein samjho. [Q58–Q61]\n11. Protective Coatings & Reducing Power\n● Brass/Copper utensils par Tin coating ko kalai kehte hain; ye food ko copper surface se react karke\ncontamination/patina products banane se reduce karti hai. [Q63]\n● Aluminium anodizing mein surface par thick protective Aluminium Oxide (Al O ) layer develop ki jati hai, jo corrosion\n₂ ₃\n\nresistance aur durability improve karti hai. [Q64]\n● Metal ka standard electrode potential jitna more negative, uski reducing power generally utni strong. E°: B = −3 V, C\n= −1.2 V, A = +0.5 V\n B > C > A.\n⇒\n[Q65]\n12. Key Metal Properties & Electrical Conductivity\n● Key matching: Sodium soft hai aur knife se cut ho sakta hai; Mercury room temperature par liquid; Silver best\nelectrical conductor; Lead poor heat conductor. [Q66]\n● Exam properties mapping: best heat/electric conductor = Silver; Earth’s crust mein most abundant metal =\nAluminium; most malleable/flexible metal = Gold; low heat conductivity among listed metals = Lead. [Q67]\n● Given materials mein Silver ki electrical conductivity highest hai; Diamond electrical insulator hai, Graphite\nconductive hai lekin Silver se kam. [Q68]\n13. Aluminium — Bauxite and Other Ores\n● Bauxite Aluminium ka principal/most important ore aur aluminium industry ka main raw material hai. Aluminium\nmetal industrially bauxite-derived alumina se extract ki jati hai. [Q69, Q70, Q71, Q72, Q73, Q74]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Metals, Minerals & Ores Full Mind Map\n● Aluminium ke important minerals/ores mein Bauxite, Corundum (Al O ), Cryolite (Na AlF ) aur Diaspore include\n₂ ₃\n₃\n₆\nkiye jate hain. [Q75]\n14. Industrial Processes & Material–Composition Matching\n● Calcium Carbonate toothpaste mein mild abrasive/filler ingredient ho sakta hai. Bordeaux mixture = Copper\nSulphate + Lime; dental amalgam traditionally Hg + Ag/Sn/Cu alloy system hota hai. [Q76]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Liquid Sodium Coolant — context specific\n\n▸Molten sodium Fast Breeder Reactors/fast reactors mein coolant ke roop mein use ho sakta hai, lekin “all nuclear\nreactors” ke liye general statement sahi nahi. Q76 mein isi over-generalization ki wajah se CaCO -toothpaste statement\n₃\ncorrect key hai. [Q76]\n● Industrial-process matching: Cracking–Petroleum; Smelting–Copper/metallurgy; Hydrogenation–Edible oils/fats;\nVulcanization–Rubber. [Q77]\n● Composition matching: Diamond–Carbon; Marble–Calcium (mainly CaCO ); Sand–Silicon (mainly SiO ); Ruby–\n₃\n₂\nAluminium (Al O ).\n₂ ₃\n[Q78]\n● Ore matching: Bauxite–Aluminium, Calamine–Zinc, Haematite–Iron sahi hain; Cinnabar Mercury ka ore hai, Copper\nka nahi. [Q79]\n15. Density & Melting-Point Comparisons\n● Sodium ki density water se kam (~0.97 g/cm³), isliye water se lighter hai — though water ke saath violently react\nkarta hai, so “float” demonstration unsafe hai. [Q80]\n● Density decreasing order: Gold (~19.3) > Mercury (~13.6) > Steel (~7.8 g/cm³). [Q81]\n● Given substances Boron, Iron, Silicon, Aluminium mein melting point Boron ka highest hai; approximate order B >\nFe > Si > Al. [Q82]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0334","t":"05 Alloys","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Alloys Full Mind Map\n🧪 ALLOYS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / State PCS\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Alloy Basics & Duralumin\n2. Amalgam — Mercury-based Alloys\n3. Solder & Bronze\n4. German Silver — Name vs Composition\n5. Brass, Bronze, Gunmetal & Copper-alloy Comparison\n6. Brass Tarnish & Statement-based Concepts\n7. Steel — Hardness, Carbon & Slag Uses\n8. Stainless Steel — Chromium, Nickel & Composition\n9. Steel Carbon Range — Exam-safe Recall\n1. Alloy Basics & Duralumin\n● Alloy do ya zyada elements ka metallic mixture hota hai jise strength, hardness, corrosion resistance ya dusre\nuseful properties improve karne ke liye banaya jata hai. Copper khud ek pure element/metal hai; Steel, Brass aur\nBronze alloys hain. [Q1]\n● Aircraft aur train-coach ke lightweight parts mein Aluminium-based alloys useful hote hain. Duralumin Aluminium-\nbased alloy hai jo pure Aluminium se zyada strong hote hue bhi low-density rakhta hai. [Q2]\n2. Amalgam — Mercury-based Alloys\n● Amalgam ka basic rule: Mercury (Hg) + kisi dusri metal ka alloy/combination = amalgam. Isliye Mercury–Zinc\namalgam hai. [Q3, Q5]\n● Iron Mercury ke saath normal conditions mein readily amalgam nahi banata; isi standard exam fact ke karan Iron ko\nnotable exception maana jata hai. [Q4]\n3. Solder & Bronze\n● Traditional soft solder mainly Tin (Sn) + Lead (Pb) alloy hota hai; low melting point ki wajah se metal\npieces/components ko join karne mein use hota hai. [Q6]\n● Bronze ka classic composition Copper + Tin hai. Source approximate 88% Cu + 12% Sn deta hai; exam mein\n“Bronze = Cu + Sn” core fact yaad rakho. [Q7, Q8]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Solder/Bronze ke percentages fixed universal values nahi\n\n▸Solder ki exact Sn–Pb ratio application/grade ke hisab se vary kar sakti hai; source Q6 ek particular composition (~32% Sn, 68%\nPb) deta hai.\n\n▸Bronze bhi ek alloy family hai; Cu–Sn percentage grade ke saath vary karta hai. Competitive exam ke liye composition pair sabse\nimportant hai.\n4. German Silver — Name vs Composition\n● German Silver (Nickel Silver) ka standard exam composition Copper + Zinc + Nickel hai. Naam mein “Silver” hone\nke bawajood actual Silver 0% hota hai. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● German Silver mein Aluminium constituent nahi hai. Matching recall: German Silver→Nickel, Solder→Tin,\nBleaching Powder→Chlorine, Hypo (sodium thiosulphate)→Sodium. [Q9, Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — German Silver mein Silver nahi hota\n\n▸German Silver ka naam appearance se aaya hai, composition se nahi: Cu + Zn + Ni.\n\n▸Q10/Q11 numerical options mein correct concept 0% Silver hai; agar 0% option na ho to “None of these” select hoga.\n5. Brass, Bronze, Gunmetal & Copper-alloy Comparison\n● Source comparison ke hisab se Bronze mein Copper percentage sabse zyada (~88%) diya gaya hai; Brass ~68–\n71% Cu, German Silver ~50–60% Cu aur Gunmetal ~85% Cu ke around bataya gaya hai. [Q13]\n● Brass = Copper + Zinc; Bronze = Copper + Tin; German Silver = Copper + Zinc + Nickel. In teeno mein common\nbase metal Copper hai. [Q14, Q15, Q16, Q17]\n● Brass aur Bronze dono Copper alloys hain. Invar primarily Iron + Nickel alloy hai, jabki Nichrome mainly Nickel +\nChromium (often Iron) alloy hota hai. [Q18]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Alloys Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Alloy percentages grade ke saath change hote hain\n\n▸Q13 mein diye Cu percentages exam-source approximations hain; industrial Brass, Bronze aur Gunmetal ke multiple\ngrades/compositions hote hain.\n\n▸Pair/composition questions mein exact percentage se zyada base-metal + major alloying element yaad rakhna safer hai.\n6. Brass Tarnish & Statement-based Concepts\n● Statement set mein Brass = Cu+Zn aur Amalgam = Hg-containing alloy correct hain. Magnetite Fe O Iron ka ore\n₃ ₄\nhai, Aluminium ka nahi; traditional photography mein AgBr important light-sensitive compound hai, KNO nahi.\n₃\n[Q19]\n● Source ke according Brass ka dark/faded tarnish Hydrogen Sulphide (H S) se relate kiya gaya hai: Brass ka\n₂\nCopper sulphur species se react karke dark copper-sulphide type layer bana sakta hai. [Q20]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Brass tarnish ko sirf ek gas tak oversimplify mat karo\n\n▸Real atmosphere mein oxygen, moisture, CO aur sulphur compounds sab surface tarnishing/corrosion ko influence kar sakte\n₂\nhain.\n\n▸Lekin Q20 ke given options/source context mein H S intended answer hai.\n₂\n7. Steel — Hardness, Carbon & Slag Uses\n● Steel mein Carbon hardening agent ki tarah kaam karta hai; generally Carbon content badhne par\nhardness/strength badh sakti hai, saath hi ductility reduce ho sakti hai. [Q22]\n● Steel slag iron/steel industry ka by-product hai. Iska use road-base/construction, acidic agricultural soils ke\namendment aur cement/clinker raw-material applications mein kiya ja sakta hai. [Q23]\n8. Stainless Steel — Chromium, Nickel & Composition\n● Stainless steel ka key corrosion-resistant alloying element Chromium hai. Chromium surface par passive oxide film\nbanane mein help karta hai, isliye rust/corrosion resistance improve hoti hai. [Q24, Q25, Q27, Q28]\n● Nickel austenitic stainless-steel structure ko stabilize kar sakta hai, jisse common austenitic grades largely non-\nmagnetic behaviour dikhate hain. Carbon hardness ko influence karta hai; Chromium corrosion resistance ka core\nelement hai. [Q21]\n● Exam composition recall: Stainless steel ka base Iron hota hai; Chromium essential hai, aur grade ke hisab se\nNickel, Manganese, Carbon etc. bhi present ho sakte hain. Source Q29 Fe + Cr + Mn + C ko correct set deta hai.\n[Q29, Q30]\n● Q26 ke source options mein Silicon ko “not used” key kiya gaya hai; Q31 BPSC-format mein strict two-metal\noptions ko incomplete maan kar “more than one/none” key diya gaya hai. [Q26, Q31]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Stainless Steel ek single fixed recipe nahi hai\n\n▸Har stainless steel non-magnetic nahi hota: austenitic grades generally non-magnetic, lekin ferritic/martensitic grades magnetic\nho sakte hain.\n\n▸Silicon kuch stainless grades mein small amount mein ho sakta hai; Q26 ek simplified exam-source key hai.\n\n▸Q24 mein Chromium intended answer hai, lekin high-temperature/tool-steel properties mein W, Mo, V jaise alloying elements bhi\nimportant ho sakte hain.\n9. Steel Carbon Range — Exam-safe Recall\n● Source ke exam range ke hisab se ordinary steel mein Carbon approximately 0.1–2% by weight maana gaya hai;\nCarbon content steel ke hardness, strength aur ductility ko strongly affect karta hai. [Q32]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Steel ka carbon range source-dependent hota hai\n\n▸Different standards/definitions steel ko roughly ~0.02% se ~2.1% C tak describe kar sakte hain; Q32 ke options mein 0.1–2%\nintended exam answer hai.\n\n▸Bahut high Carbon content par material cast-iron range ki taraf chala jata hai; exact boundary standard/composition par depend\nkarti hai.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q32\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0335","t":"06.i Carbon and its Various Forms","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Carbon and its Various Forms Full Mind Map\n🧪 CARBON AND ITS VARIOUS FORMS — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 6.A · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / State PCS\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Carbon Basics, Catenation & Major Allotropes\n2. Lab-grown Diamond, Graphene & Modern Carbon Materials\n3. Pencil Lead & Carbon Fibre\n4. Fullerene / C — Discovery, Structure & Matching\n₆₀\n5. Carbon in Coal, Lignite & Iron Products\n6. Crystal, Glass Etching & Carat\n7. Graphene — Strength, Conductivity & Uses\n8. Graphite as Lubricant + Mixed Chemistry Recall\n9. Dry Ice — Solid CO₂\n10. Water Gas, Soda Water & CO Bond Order\n1. Carbon Basics, Catenation & Major Allotropes\n● Carbon sabse zyada compounds banane wala element mana jata hai, mainly uski catenation (apne atoms ke saath\nlong chains/rings banana) aur tetravalency ki wajah se. Diamond, Graphite aur Coal teeno carbon-containing\nforms/materials hain. [Q1, Q2, Q3]\n● Thermodynamically Carbon ka sabse stable allotrope Graphite hai. Diamond aur Graphite dono pure Carbon se\nbane hote hain, lekin unki crystal structure, hardness aur electrical conductivity bahut alag hoti hai. [Q4, Q5, Q6]\n● Diamond 3D tetrahedral covalent network banata hai aur electrical insulator hota hai; Graphite layered structure wala\nsoft material hai jisme delocalised electrons ki wajah se electrical conduction hoti hai. [Q5, Q6]\n● Diamond, Graphite aur Fullerene pure Carbon ke allotropes hain; Oxocarbon koi allotrope nahi, balki Carbon +\nOxygen se bana compound class hai. [Q12]\n2. Lab-grown Diamond, Graphene & Modern Carbon Materials\n● Lab-grown diamonds mainly HPHT aur CVD methods se banaye jate hain. Source questions Graphite ko Carbon\nsource/seed-base ke roop mein key karte hain; high temperature-pressure conditions mein Carbon diamond structure\nmein crystallise kar sakta hai. [Q7, Q8]\n● Chronology recall: Kevlar (1965) → Fullerene (1985) → Graphene isolation (2004) → TIFR ka nano-gold based\n‘black gold’ work (2019). Is source question ka sequence 4-2-3-1 hai. [Q9]\n● Graphene pure Carbon ka one-atom-thick, two-dimensional nano-structure/allotrope hai; Kevlar, Lexan aur spider\nsilk pure Carbon-only materials nahi hain. [Q10, Q11]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Lab-grown diamond mein ‘seed’ aur ‘carbon source’ ko mix mat karo\n\n▸Practical CVD/HPHT growth mein actual seed usually ek chhota diamond crystal/wafer hota hai; Graphite ya hydrocarbon feed\nCarbon source ho sakta hai.\n\n▸Source Q7–Q8 Graphite ko seed/base wording mein key karta hai—exam mein source wording dekhna, conceptually seed\ncrystal aur carbon feed alag cheezein hain.\n3. Pencil Lead & Carbon Fibre\n● Pencil ka ‘lead’ actual Lead metal nahi hota; woh Graphite (often clay ke saath mixture) hota hai. Isi wajah se pencil\nwriting graphite deposition se hoti hai. [Q13, Q14]\n● Carbon-fibre reinforced composites lightweight aur high-strength hote hain, isliye automobiles, racing cars, aircraft\naur spacecraft parts mein use hote hain. Carbon-fibre waste ko mechanical, thermal ya chemical routes se recycle kiya\nja sakta hai. [Q15]\n4. Fullerene / C\n — Discovery, Structure & Matching\n₆₀\n● Fullerene discovery ke liye 1996 Chemistry Nobel Robert Curl, Harold Kroto aur Richard Smalley ko mila; Richard\nFeynman is discovery team ka hissa nahi the. [Q16]\n● Buckminsterfullerene C\n ek hollow cage/soccer-ball type molecule hai jisme 60 Carbon atoms pentagons aur\n₆₀\nhexagons wale polyhedral network mein arranged hote hain. [Q18]\n● Fullerene mein Fluorine nahi hota. Isliye ‘Fullerene = fluorine-containing organic compound’ wali matching galat hai;\nye pure Carbon allotrope hai. [Q17, Q19, Q20, Q21]\n● Matching recall: Dry ice = solid CO ; Mustard gas = toxic chemical warfare agent; Freon = refrigerant; SO acid rain\n₂\n₂\nka major contributor hai. [Q17, Q19, Q20, Q21]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Carbon and its Various Forms Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Fullerene ≠ Fluorine compound\n\n▸Naam similar lagne ki wajah se confusion hota hai, lekin Fullerene pure Carbon allotrope hai.\n\n▸Fluorine-containing polymer ka classic example Teflon (PTFE) hai, Fullerene nahi.\n5. Carbon in Coal, Lignite & Iron Products\n● Sand (mainly silica, SiO ) mein Carbon nahi hota, jabki Diamond, Graphite aur Coal carbon-containing hain. Lignite\n₂\nbhi low-grade coal hai aur Carbon contain karta hai. [Q22, Q23]\n● Coal rank ke saath Carbon percentage generally badhta hai: Peat < Lignite < Bituminous < Anthracite; in options\nAnthracite mein Carbon sabse zyada hota hai. [Q24]\n● Iron products mein Pig Iron ka Carbon content comparatively sabse high (~3.5–4.5%) hota hai; Wrought Iron bahut\nlow-carbon hota hai aur Steel intermediate range mein aata hai. [Q25]\n6. Crystal, Glass Etching & Carat\n● Diamond, Quartz aur Graphite crystalline solids hain. Source ke historical question mein Sulphur ko ‘not in crystal\nform’ key kiya gaya hai, although Sulphur ke crystalline allotropes bhi known hain. [Q26]\n● Glass ko Diamond scratch kar sakta hai aur Hydrofluoric acid (HF) chemically etch karta hai kyunki HF silica (SiO )\n₂\nke saath react karta hai. Aqua regia ya conc. H SO is standard glass-etching answer nahi hain.\n₂\n₄\n[Q27]\n● Gemstones/diamonds ke mass ke liye metric carat use hota hai: 1 carat = 200 mg = 0.2 g. [Q28]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q26 source-specific hai\n\n▸Elemental Sulphur ke rhombic aur monoclinic crystalline allotropes hote hain; isliye ‘Sulphur crystalline nahi hota’ ko universal\nchemistry fact mat samajhna.\n\n▸Is question ko historical/source-key based odd-one-out ke roop mein treat karo.\n7. Graphene — Strength, Conductivity & Uses\n● Graphene Carbon ka 2D, one-atom-thick sheet hai; excellent electrical conductivity, extreme thinness aur very high\ntensile strength uski key properties hain. [Q29, Q30]\n● Graphene Silicon ka allotrope nahi hai. Transparent-conducting nature ki wajah se touchscreens, LCD/OLED\nelectrodes aur advanced electronics mein iska potential bahut high hai. [Q29]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — ‘Strongest material’ ka exam shorthand\n\n▸Source options mein Graphene correct hai, lekin ‘strongest’ property ko tensile strength, hardness aur toughness se confuse mat\nkaro—ye alag material properties hain.\n8. Graphite as Lubricant + Mixed Chemistry Recall\n● Permanent hard water mein dissolved CaSO /MgSO jaise salts ho sakte hain. Diamond Copper aur Iron se much\n₄\n₄\nharder hai; atmosphere ka main component Nitrogen (~78%) hai aur vegetable ghee hydrogenation mein Hydrogen use\nhota hai. [Q31]\n● Graphite solid lubricant hai. Layered structure mein sheets ek-dusre par easily slide karti hain, isliye heavy\nmachinery aur high-temperature/high-pressure lubrication applications mein useful hota hai. [Q32, Q33]\n9. Dry Ice — Solid CO₂\n● Dry Ice = solid/frozen Carbon dioxide (CO ). Ye ordinary water ice nahi hota aur cooling agent ke roop mein use hota\n₂\n\nhai. [Q34, Q35, Q36, Q37, Q38]\n● Dry Ice atmospheric pressure par melt hone ke bajay directly solid se gas mein sublime karta hai; isi wajah se ise\n‘dry’ ice kaha jata hai kyunki liquid-water residue nahi chhodta. [Q34–Q38]\n10. Water Gas, Soda Water & CO Bond Order\n● Water gas ek synthesis-gas mixture hai: CO + H . Iska use methanol aur dusre industrial chemicals ke synthesis\n₂\nmein kiya ja sakta hai. [Q39]\n● Soda-water bottle kholne par pressure kam hota hai aur dissolved CO bubbles ke roop mein bahar nikalta hai;\n₂\nreleased gas Carbon dioxide hoti hai. [Q40]\n● Molecular Orbital Theory ke hisab se bond order = ½(Nb − Na). CO ke liye effective bond order 3 hota hai, jo strong\ntriple-bond character ko indicate karta hai. [Q41]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q41\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0336","t":"06.ii Hydrogen and its Compounds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Hydrogen and its Compounds Full Mind Map\n🧪 HYDROGEN AND ITS COMPOUNDS — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 6.B · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Hydrogen Basics — Valency, Water Composition, Combustion & Storage\n2. Heavy Water (D O) — Composition, Formula, Reactor Use & Molecular Mass\n₂\n3. Hard Water, pH & “Purest Water” Concepts\n4. Water as a Solvent — Polarity & Dipole Moment\n5. Water Purification — Desalination, Chlorination, RO & Alum\n6. Hydrogenation of Vegetable Oil — Vanaspati Ghee & Nickel Catalyst\n1. Hydrogen Basics — Valency, Water Composition, Combustion & Storage\n● Agar element X ke outermost shell mein 4 electrons hain, to uski valency 4 hogi. Hydrogen ki valency 1 hoti hai,\nisliye compound ka general formula XH hoga — CH jaisa pattern yaad rakho.\n₄\n₄\n[Q1]\n● Water H O ka molar mass 18 g/mol hota hai; isme Hydrogen ka mass 2 g hota hai. Isliye water mein Hydrogen ka\n₂\nmass percentage = (2/18)×100 = 11.11%. [Q2]\n● 1 mole H ka mass 2 g hota hai. Agar 1 mole H burn hone par 290 kJ heat deta hai, to 4 g H = 2 moles se 580 kJ\n₂\n₂\n₂\nheat release hogi. [Q3]\n● Hydrogen Oxygen ke saath burn karke Water banata hai: 2H + O → 2H O. Isi clean combustion-product ki wajah\n₂\n₂\n₂\nse given fossil-fuel options mein Hydrogen minimum direct air pollution wala fuel maana jata hai. [Q4, Q5]\n● Hydrogen ko physically compressed gas ke form mein high-pressure tanks/cylinders mein store kiya ja sakta hai;\nliquid Hydrogen ke liye cryogenic temperature (~−253°C) chahiye. Metal hydrides chemical-storage category mein aate\nhain. [Q6]\n2. Heavy Water (D O) — Composition, Formula, Reactor Use & Molecular Mass\n₂\n● Heavy Water = Deuterium Oxide = D O. Deuterium (D) Hydrogen ka isotope hai jisme 1 proton + 1 neutron hota hai;\n₂\nordinary H O ke Protium ko Deuterium replace karta hai.\n₂\n[Q8, Q9, Q11, Q12, Q13]\n● PHWR-type nuclear reactors mein Heavy Water neutron moderator bhi ho sakta hai aur coolant bhi. Moderator\nneutrons ko slow karta hai, aur D O ka neutron-absorption relatively low hota hai.\n₂\n[Q7]\n● Ordinary water (H O) Light-Water Reactors mein moderator + coolant dono roles mein use hota hai, jabki Heavy\n₂\nWater PHWRs mein. Isliye broad “nuclear reactors” wording mein source ne H O aur D O dono ko valid maana hai.\n₂\n₂\n[Q10]\n● Heavy Water ka molecular mass ≈ 20 hota hai: 2×2 (Deuterium) + 16 (Oxygen) = 20; ordinary H O ka molecular\n₂\nmass 18 hota hai. [Q15]\n● Source question Heavy Water discovery ko H. C. Urey se associate karta hai, kyunki Urey ne Deuterium discover\nkiya aur 1934 Chemistry Nobel jeeta. [Q14]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q14 mein “Deuterium discovery” aur “pure Heavy Water isolation” ko mix mat\nkaro\n\n▸H. C. Urey ko Deuterium (heavy hydrogen) ki discovery ka credit milta hai.\n\n▸Gilbert N. Lewis ne 1933 mein essentially pure D O / heavy-water samples isolate aur study kiye. Isliye historical wording\n₂\nsource-key se zyada nuanced hai.\n3. Hard Water, pH & “Purest Water” Concepts\n● Permanent hardness mainly Calcium aur Magnesium ke chlorides/sulphates ki wajah se hoti hai; temporary\nhardness mainly bicarbonates se hoti hai. [Q17]\n● Pure water neutral hota hai aur 25°C ke around uska pH ≈ 7 hota hai; pH < 7 acidic aur pH > 7 basic/alkaline hota\nhai. [Q18, Q19]\n● Hard water soap ke saath scum banata hai aur boilers mein scale deposit karta hai, isliye washing aur boiler-use\nmein clearly problematic hai. [Q16]\n● Source Q20 “purest form of water” ko Rainwater key karta hai, traditional natural-water context mein; lekin chemistry\npurity ke sense mein Distilled Water dissolved salts/ions se zyada free hota hai. [Q20]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Hydrogen and its Compounds Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q16 aur Q20 source keys ko blindly generalise mat karo\n\n▸Q16: Hard water drinking aur irrigation ke liye universally “unsuitable” nahi hota. Standard definite problems: soap-washing aur\nboiler scaling. Given statements ke scientific reading mein 2 & 3 safest hain.\n\n▸Q20: Agar “purest natural water” poochha ho to old exam books Rainwater dete hain; agar option Distilled Water ho aur\nquestion simply “purest water” ho, to Distilled Water chemically purer answer hai.\n4. Water as a Solvent — Polarity & Dipole Moment\n● Water ek polar/dipolar molecule hai aur iska dipole moment high hota hai. O-side partial negative aur H-side partial\npositive nature ionic species ko attract karti hai. [Q21]\n● Isi polarity ki wajah se Water ko “universal solvent” kaha jata hai: ye Na , Cl jaise ions ko hydrate/stabilise karke\n⁺\n⁻\nbahut se ionic aur polar substances dissolve kar leta hai. [Q21, Q22]\n5. Water Purification — Desalination, Chlorination, RO & Alum\n● Saline/impure water se drinking-quality water banane ke broad process ko Desalination kaha jata hai; especially sea\nwater se salts/minerals remove karne ke context mein ye important hai. [Q23]\n● Drinking-water disinfection mein Chlorine widely use hota hai; ye bacteria aur dusre microbes ko destroy/inactivate\nkarta hai. [Q24]\n● Sea/salty water ko pure water mein convert karne ke liye Reverse Osmosis (RO) use hota hai: osmotic pressure se\nzyada external pressure laga kar water ko semipermeable membrane ke through reverse direction mein force kiya jata\nhai. [Q25, Q26]\n● Muddy water mein Alum (aluminium sulphate) coagulation karwata hai. Fine charged particles destabilise hoke flocs\nbanate hain aur settle ho jate hain, jisse water clear hota hai. [Q27]\n6. Hydrogenation of Vegetable Oil — Vanaspati Ghee & Nickel Catalyst\n● Vegetable oil se Vanaspati Ghee banane mein Hydrogen gas add ki jati hai; unsaturated C=C bonds hydrogenation\nke through zyada saturated fat mein convert hote hain. [Q28]\n● Commercial hydrogenation of vegetable oils mein finely divided Nickel (Ni) standard catalyst hota hai. Source\napprox. 150–180°C temperature range bhi mention karta hai. [Q29, Q30]\n● Exam recall: Vegetable Oil + H —Ni catalyst→ Vanaspati Ghee. Hydrogen reagent hai, Nickel catalyst hai — dono\n₂\nroles alag-alag yaad rakho. [Q28, Q29, Q30]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q30\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0337","t":"06.iii Sulphur Nitrogen Halogen Inert Gases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sulphur, Nitrogen, Halogen & Inert Gases Full Mind Map\n🧪 SULPHUR, NITROGEN, HALOGEN & INERT GASES — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 6.C · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Noble Gases & Atmospheric Composition\n2. Helium — Deep-Sea Diving & Balloons\n3. Sulphur Compound — SF Geometry\n₆\n4. Nitrogen Compounds — Ammonia, N O & Xenon Recall\n₂\n5. Nitrogen Cycle, Aircraft Tyres & Insectivorous Plants\n6. Tear-Gas Questions & Trimethylamine\n7. Halogens — Physical State, Reactivity & Uses\n8. Selenium — Photoconductive Non-metal\n9. Fluorescent Tubes, Mercury Vapour & Neon Signs\n1. Noble Gases & Atmospheric Composition\n● Noble gases Group 18 ke colourless, odourless aur mostly monoatomic gases hote hain; exam examples: He, Ne, Ar, Kr,\nXe aur radioactive Rn. Actinium noble gas nahi, balki radioactive metal hai. [Q1, Q2]\n● Atmosphere mein Nitrogen sabse zyada (~78–79%), Oxygen ~20.95% aur Argon ~0.93% hota hai. Given options mein\nCarbon dioxide ka volume-fraction sabse kam diya gaya hai. [Q3, Q4]\n● Biogeochemical “gaseous cycles” ke traditional exam classification mein Nitrogen, Oxygen aur Carbon cycles aate hain;\nsource Q5 H ko dedicated gaseous cycle na hone ke roop mein key karta hai.\n₂\n[Q5]\n● Xenon (Xe, atomic no. 54) ek rare noble gas hai. “Xenon” Greek xenos = stranger se aaya hai, isliye ise Stranger Gas bhi\nkaha jata hai. [Q16]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q3 aur Q5 mein source-style wording yaad rakho\n\n▸Q3 ka source CO ko ~0.03% batata hai; modern atmospheric CO concentration 0.04% se upar hai. Exam mein options/context follow\n₂\n₂\nkaro.\n\n▸Q5 ecological-cycle terminology textbook-dependent ho sakti hai; source-answer H hai, isliye isse question-specific recall ke roop mein\n₂\nrakho.\n2. Helium — Deep-Sea Diving & Balloons\n● Deep-sea divers respiration ke liye Oxygen + Helium mixture use kar sakte hain; ise Heliox kaha jata hai. Helium ki\ndensity/airway resistance low hoti hai aur high-pressure diving mein Nitrogen-related problems ko reduce karne mein help\nkarta hai. [Q6, Q7, Q8]\n● Balloons mein Helium preferred hota hai kyunki ye air se lighter aur chemically inert hai. Hydrogen bhi light hai, lekin highly\nflammable/explosive hone ki wajah se safety risk zyada hai. [Q23, Q24]\n3. Sulphur Compound — SF Geometry\n₆\n● Sulphur hexafluoride, SF , mein central Sulphur ke around 6 Fluorine atoms symmetrically arranged hote hain; VSEPR ke\n₆\nhisab se molecular geometry Octahedral hoti hai. [Q9]\n4. Nitrogen Compounds — Ammonia, N O & Xenon Recall\n₂\n● Ammonia (NH ) polar molecule hai aur water ke saath strong hydrogen bonding kar sakta hai, isliye ye water mein bahut\n₃\neasily soluble hota hai. [Q10]\n● Laughing Gas = Nitrous Oxide = N O. Iska use medical/dental procedures mein mild anaesthetic/analgesic-sedative role\n₂\nmein kiya jata hai. Q11–Q15 isi same recall ko different exam forms mein repeat karte hain. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15]\n● Nitric Oxide (NO) ko Laughing Gas kehna galat hai; correct Laughing Gas N O hai. Bordeaux mixture, Dry Ice aur Boric-\n₂\nacid wali statements ke beech source Q17 isi incorrect statement ko target karta hai. [Q17]\n5. Nitrogen Cycle, Aircraft Tyres & Insectivorous Plants\n● Nitrogen cycle mein fixation, ammonification, nitrification aur denitrification jaise steps hote hain. Source Q18 ka point hai ki\ncycling ke karan lithosphere–atmosphere system mein Nitrogen ka overall amount broadly conserved rehta hai. [Q18]\n● Nitrogen atmosphere ki major “permanent gas” hai (~78%). Carbon dioxide aur ozone jaise gases comparatively variable\ncategory mein rakhe jate hain. [Q19]\n● Aircraft tyres mein Nitrogen use ki jati hai kyunki ye combustion support nahi karti aur high-temperature/pressure conditions\nmein comparatively safe, dry aur stable filling gas hai. [Q20]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sulphur, Nitrogen, Halogen & Inert Gases Full Mind Map\n● Insectivorous plants Nitrogen-deficient boggy soils mein grow karte hain; Nitrogen requirement compensate karne ke liye\ninsects ko trap/digest karte hain. Examples: Nepenthes, Drosera, Dionaea, Utricularia. [Q21, Q22]\n6. Tear-Gas Questions & Trimethylamine\n● Source Q25–Q26 old exam framing mein “tear gas” ke liye Chlorine/Cl ko key karta hai. Tear-producing riot-control agents\n₂\nka actual chemistry context CN, CS jaise lacrimators se juda hota hai; Chlorine khud toxic choking gas hai. [Q25, Q26]\n● Dead fish ki foul smell Trimethylamine (TMA) jaise volatile amines ki wajah se hoti hai; fish tissues ke decomposition mein\nye characteristic fishy odour develop hota hai. [Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Tear Gas = Chlorine ko universal fact mat mano\n\n▸Q25–Q26 ke given options/source key mein Chlorine answer diya gaya hai.\n\n▸Modern riot-control “tear gas” agents commonly CS (2-chlorobenzalmalononitrile), CN etc. hote hain; Cl ko standard tear-gas agent\n₂\nkehna chemically misleading hai.\n7. Halogens — Physical State, Reactivity & Uses\n● Group 17 = Halogens. Room temperature par Fluorine aur Chlorine gases, Bromine liquid, aur Iodine solid hota hai. Isliye\ngiven solid-state question ka answer Iodine aur liquid non-metal ka classic answer Bromine hai. [Q28, Q30, Q31]\n● Halogen reactivity group mein downward decrease karti hai; Fluorine sabse electronegative aur sabse reactive halogen hai.\n[Q29]\n● Source Q32 Bromine ko “analgesic” se associate karta hai, historical bromide sedative/medicine usage ke context mein.\nIsse modern routine analgesic fact ke roop mein generalise mat karo. [Q32]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q32 historical wording hai\n\n▸Bromide salts ka historical use sedatives/anticonvulsants ke roop mein hua hai.\n\n▸Aaj ke standard analgesics mein “Bromine” ko direct common analgesic kehna current clinical classification nahi hai; exam source-\ncontext yaad rakho.\n8. Selenium — Photoconductive Non-metal\n● Selenium ek non-metal hai lekin Gray Selenium semiconductor/photoconductor behaviour dikhata hai; light/electromagnetic\nradiation absorb karne par electrical conductivity badh sakti hai. Isi wajah se ye “poor conductor nahi” wale question ka\nexception hai. [Q33]\n9. Fluorescent Tubes, Mercury Vapour & Neon Signs\n● Fluorescent tubelight mein low-pressure Mercury vapour ke saath inert gas — commonly Argon — hoti hai. Electric\ndischarge Mercury ko excite karta hai; generated UV phosphor coating ko visible light emit karne ke liye excite karta hai. [Q34]\n● Source Q35 mein Mercury vapour + Argon aur Mercury vapour + Neon dono technically possible combinations diye gaye\nhain; standard/common filling Argon + small Mercury vapour hota hai. [Q35]\n● Q36 Neon + Mercury vapour ko low-pressure filling ke roop mein accept karta hai; Q37 mein Argon gas aur Mercury vapour\ndono tubelight ke actual components hain, isliye source ne multiple-correct mark kiya hai. [Q36, Q37]\n● Neon discharge tubes bright coloured glow dete hain, isliye optical decoration aur advertising signs — “neon signs” — mein\nNeon ka classic use hota hai. [Q38]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Tubelight options mein component vs complete mixture distinguish karo\n\n▸Typical fluorescent lamp = low-pressure inert gas (usually Argon) + a small amount of Mercury vapour.\n\n▸Isliye agar options individual components hon to Argon aur Mercury vapour dono statements true ho sakte hain; exact combination\noptions ko dhyan se padho.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q38\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0338","t":"06.iv Acid Base and Salt","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Acid, Base & Salt Full Mind Map\n🧪 ACID, BASE & SALT — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 6.D · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Acids, Bases, Antacids & Aqua Regia\n2. pH Scale, Litmus & Hydronium-Ion Concept\n3. Industrial Acids & Acid Rain\n4. Salt Hydrolysis, Lewis Concept & Safe Dilution\n5. Acid–Base Reactions, Amphoteric Oxides & CO Chemistry\n₂\n6. Common Salts — Baking Soda, POP, Blue Vitriol & Matchings\n7. Washing Soda, Common Salt, Iodised Salt & Bleaching Powder\n8. ENO, Photography Chemicals — Hypo & Silver Bromide\n9. Quartz, Pottery, Coloured Glass & Ionic Compounds\n1. Acids, Bases, Antacids & Aqua Regia\n● Antacids basic nature ke compounds hote hain — jaise Mg(OH) , Al(OH) , CaCO etc. Ye stomach mein excess HCl ko\n₂\n₃\n₃\nneutralise karke acidity/heartburn ko reduce karte hain. [Q1]\n● Aqua regia = concentrated HCl : concentrated HNO ka 3:1 mixture. Ye strongly corrosive/oxidising mixture hai aur Gold,\n₃\nPlatinum jaise noble metals ko dissolve kar sakta hai. [Q2]\n2. pH Scale, Litmus & Hydronium-Ion Concept\n● pH aqueous solution ki acidity/basicity ko show karta hai: pH < 7 acidic, pH = 7 neutral aur pH > 7 basic/alkaline. Pure\nwater aur ideal neutral solution ka pH 7 hota hai. [Q3, Q5, Q6, Q10]\n● pH logarithmic scale hai: pH 3 se 6 hone par H concentration 10³ = 1000 times decrease hoti hai. Isliye pH mein chhota\n⁺\nnumerical change bhi ion concentration mein large change show karta hai. [Q4]\n● Base red litmus ko blue karta hai; acid blue litmus ko red karta hai. Distilled water neutral hone ki wajah se litmus ka colour\nchange nahi karta. Red litmus blue ho to pH definitely 7 se greater hona chahiye. [Q7, Q8]\n● Dry HCl gas dry litmus ka colour nahi badalta kyunki water absent hone par H O /hydrated proton form nahi hota. Acidic\n₃ ⁺\nbehaviour aqueous medium mein express hota hai. [Q9]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q7 mein correct concept option-list se bahar hai\n\n▸Red litmus → blue ka matlab solution basic hai, yani pH > 7. Given options 7, 1, 5, 6.5 the, isliye source ne “None of the above” key\nkiya.\n\n▸Concept yaad rakho: indicator-result ko directly pH range se map karo; option-number ko fact mat samjho.\n3. Industrial Acids & Acid Rain\n● Sulphuric acid (H SO ) ko “basic chemical of industry” kaha jata hai, kyunki fertilizer, petroleum refining, metal treatment\n₂\n₄\naur large-scale chemical manufacture mein iska extensive use hota hai. [Q11]\n● Acid rain mainly atmospheric SO aur nitrogen oxides ke oxidation se banne wale H SO aur HNO se associated hoti hai.\n₂\n₂\n₄\n₃\nGiven-option questions mein Sulphuric acid ko major component aur Nitric acid ko bhi principal acid maana gaya hai. [Q12, Q13,\nQ14]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Acid-rain composition fixed percentage nahi hoti\n\n▸Source Q12 H SO ko ~70–75% batata hai; actual acid-rain composition place, season aur emissions ke according vary karti hai.\n₂\n₄\n\n▸Exam-safe core: major mineral acids = Sulphuric acid + Nitric acid.\n4. Salt Hydrolysis, Lewis Concept & Safe Dilution\n● CuSO jaise salt ka aqueous solution acidic ho sakta hai because cation hydration/hydrolysis H generate karne wali\n₄\n⁺\nequilibrium create karti hai. Exam answer: hydrolysis. [Q15]\n● Lewis acid electron-pair acceptor aur Lewis base electron-pair donor hota hai. BF , AlCl , FeCl electron-pair acceptors\n₃\n₃\n₃\nhain; NH ke paas lone pair hota hai, isliye NH Lewis base hai.\n₃\n₃\n[Q16]\n● Concentrated H SO ko dilute karte waqt acid ko slowly water mein add karte hain — “Always Add Acid”. Dilution highly\n₂\n₄\nexothermic hai; water ko acid mein daalne par local boiling/splashing ka danger hota hai. [Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q15 ki literal molecular equation ko mechanism mat samjho\n\n▸Source CuSO + 2H O → H SO + Cu(OH) likhta hai; aqueous salt hydrolysis ko is simple one-way molecular equation se represent\n₄\n₂\n₂\n₄\n₂\nkarna oversimplified hai.\n\n▸Exam point: CuSO solution acidic due to hydrolysis/hydrated Cu² acidity.\n₄\n⁺"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Acid, Base & Salt Full Mind Map\n5. Acid–Base Reactions, Amphoteric Oxides & CO Chemistry\n₂\n● Amphoteric oxides acid aur base dono ke saath react kar sakte hain. Classic examples: Al O aur ZnO. CuO mainly basic\n₂ ₃\noxide hai. [Q18]\n● Acid + metal carbonate → salt + H O + CO . Isi CO ko limewater [Ca(OH) ] mein pass karne par insoluble CaCO banta\n₂\n₂\n₂\n₂\n₃\nhai aur limewater milky ho jata hai. [Q19, Q20]\n● CO water mein dissolve hokar carbonic acid (H CO ) form karta hai, isliye soda water mildly acidic hota hai. HCl oxygen-\n₂\n₂\n₃\nfree mineral acid hai; HNO aur H SO oxygen-containing acids hain.\n₃\n₂\n₄\n[Q21, Q22]\n● Ammonia water mein dissolve hokar basic solution deta hai aur red litmus blue karta hai. HCl gas ke saath NH dense\n₃\nwhite fumes of NH Cl banata hai — unknown-gas identification ka classic test.\n₄\n[Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — “NH OH” ko convenient school-level notation samjho\n₄\n\n▸Aqueous ammonia ka better equilibrium representation: NH + H O ⇌ NH\n + OH .\n₃\n₂\n₄⁺\n⁻\n\n▸Source “ammonium hydroxide” wording use karta hai; exam mein expected basic behaviour aur NH Cl white fumes yaad rakho.\n₄\n6. Common Salts — Baking Soda, POP, Blue Vitriol & Matchings\n● Baking soda = Sodium bicarbonate / Sodium hydrogen carbonate = NaHCO . Baking mein leavening agent ke roop mein\n₃\nCO release karta hai; Q24 aur Q32–Q35 isi formula/name ko repeat karte hain.\n₂\n[Q24, Q32, Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Important matching: Bleaching powder → Calcium oxychloride/hypochlorite; Baking soda → NaHCO ; Plaster of Paris →\n₃\nCaSO ·½H O. POP ko Calcium bicarbonate kehna wrong hai.\n₄\n₂\n[Q25, Q26]\n● Neela thotha / Blue vitriol = hydrated Copper sulphate, commonly CuSO ·5H O. Copper sulphate fungicide ke roop mein\n₄\n₂\nwater tanks/crops mein use ho sakta hai. [Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● High-yield salt map: Washing soda → Sodium carbonate; Caustic soda → NaOH; Neela thotha → Copper sulphate; Hypo\n→ Sodium thiosulphate; Epsom salt → Magnesium sulphate; Baking soda → NaHCO .\n₃ [Q30, Q31]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q25 mein “washing powder” wording simplified hai\n\n▸Source matching “washing powder → sodium carbonate” key karta hai. Commercial washing powders mixtures hote hain; sodium\ncarbonate unka builder/component ho sakta hai.\n\n▸Washing soda ko specifically Na CO ·10H O se distinguish karo.\n₂\n₃\n₂\n7. Washing Soda, Common Salt, Iodised Salt & Bleaching Powder\n● Washing soda ka chemical base Sodium carbonate hai; hydrated washing soda = Na CO ·10H O, jabki anhydrous Na CO\n₂\n₃\n₂\n₂\n₃\nko soda ash kaha jata hai. Q36–Q37 name/formula recall karte hain. [Q36, Q37]\n● Baking soda fire-extinguisher mixtures mein CO source ho sakta hai. Bleaching powder historical industrial processes\n₂\nsuch as Hasenclever/Backmann plants se prepare kiya gaya; source Q38 mein statements 2–3 correct hain, statement 1\nwrong. [Q38]\n● Ocean water ka predominant dissolved salt NaCl hai. Table salt strong acid HCl + strong base NaOH ka neutral salt hai.\n[Q41, Q42]\n● Iodised salt, sea salt, rock salt aur processed common salt sab dining/table-use forms ho sakte hain; source Q43 mein koi\nunique \"should not be used\" option establish nahi hota, isliye ise disputed mark kiya gaya hai. [Q43]\n● Iodised salt iodine-fortified common salt hota hai; iodising agents iodide/iodate salts ho sakte hain. Source option-set Q44\nPotassium iodide ko correct key karta hai. [Q44]\n● Gypsum cement ki setting ko slow/control karne ke liye add kiya jata hai. Ba aur Sr highly reactive alkaline-earth metals\nhain, isliye nature mein free state mein nahi milte. [Q45]\n● Bleaching powder oxidising/bleaching agent hai; dilute acid se chlorine release kar sakta hai aur water treatment mein use\nhota hai. Main exam formula often CaOCl / calcium oxychloride likha jata hai.\n₂\n[Q46, Q47]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q43 disputed hai; Q44 source-specific iodisation chemistry hai\n\n▸Q43 ke listed iodised, sea, rock aur processed common salt sab edible/table-use forms ho sakte hain; source ne question ko disputed\n(*) maana hai.\n\n▸Iodised salt ke liye practical fortificants mein iodide aur iodate dono milte hain; exact exam option/source wording follow karo.\n8. ENO, Photography Chemicals — Hypo & Silver Bromide\n● ENO-type effervescent salt mein commonly sodium bicarbonate + citric acid react karke CO bubbles produce karte hain.\n₂\nIsi effervescence se fizzy action hota hai. [Q48]\n● Photography mein “Hypo” = Sodium thiosulphate solution. Ye fixer/antichlor ke roop mein unreacted silver halide ko soluble\ncomplex bana kar remove karta hai. [Q49, Q50, Q51, Q52, Q53]\n● Photographic films/plates ki light-sensitive emulsion mein Silver bromide (AgBr) classic photosensitive salt hai; light\nexposure latent image banane ki process initiate karta hai. [Q54, Q55]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Acid, Base & Salt Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Developer aur fixer ko mix mat karo\n\n▸Source Q49 wording “develop photographic plates” use karta hai, lekin Sodium thiosulphate ka standard role FIXER hai, developer nahi.\n\n▸Q54 “useful element” bolta hai but Silver bromide (AgBr) element nahi, compound hai. Exam intent photosensitive photographic salt ko\nidentify karna hai.\n9. Quartz, Pottery, Coloured Glass & Ionic Compounds\n● Source Q39 matching mein Artificial ripening → Ethylene, Baking soda → NaHCO , Soft drink → CO aur Quartz →\n₃\n₂\nSodium silicate pair diya gaya hai; lekin quartz ka actual chemical composition SiO hai, jise Q40 directly test karta hai.\n₂\n[Q39,\nQ40]\n● Pottery glazing mein ZnO use kiya ja sakta hai; glass ko deep blue colour dene ke liye Cobalt oxide classic colouring agent\nhai. [Q56, Q57]\n● Ionic compounds generally organic solvents like alcohol mein poorly soluble hote hain. Solid ionic crystal mein ions fixed\nlattice positions par hote hain, isliye solid state mein electricity conduct nahi karte; molten ya aqueous state mein conduct\nkarte hain. [Q58]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q39 Quartz matching ko direct chemistry fact mat banao\n\n▸Quartz = SiO (silicon dioxide). Source Q39 mein Sodium silicate pair elimination/context se aata hai; Q40 correct direct composition\n₂\nSiO confirm karta hai.\n₂\n\n▸Q58 ka “insoluble in alcohol” general exam-rule hai; individual ionic compounds ki exact solubility solvent aur salt par depend kar sakti\nhai.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q58\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0339","t":"07.i Hydrocarbons","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Hydrocarbons Full Mind Map\n🧪 HYDROCARBONS — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.A · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Organic Chemistry Basics & Origin-of-Life Elements\n2. Hydrocarbon Series, Alkene & Physical Properties\n3. Methane, Carbon Black, Biogas & Bhopal MIC\n4. Fruit Ripening — Ethephon, Ethylene & Calcium Carbide\n5. Acetylene — Welding, PVC & Preparation\n6. Benzene Structure — Sigma & Pi Bonds\n1. Organic Chemistry Basics & Origin-of-Life Elements\n● Primitive-Earth simulation context mein source sequence Methane → Hydrogen cyanide → Nitrile → Amino acid diya gaya\nhai. Miller–Urey-type questions mein sequence ko option-wise recall karna useful hai. [Q1]\n● Organic compounds aur bio-compounds ka backbone Carbon hai. Carbon atoms H, O, N, S, P jaise elements ke saath\nmainly covalent bonds bana kar enormous variety of molecules form karte hain. [Q2, Q3]\n● Life-origin ke high-yield elements ko CHNOPS mnemonic se yaad rakho: Carbon, Hydrogen, Nitrogen, Oxygen,\nPhosphorus, Sulphur. Given-option Q4 mein Carbon + Hydrogen + Nitrogen wala set closest correct choice tha. [Q4]\n2. Hydrocarbon Series, Alkene & Physical Properties\n● Straight-chain alkane series mein molecular mass carbon count ke saath increase hota hai: Methane (CH ) < Ethane\n₄\n(C H ) < Propane (C H ) < Butane (C H ).\n₂ ₆\n₃ ₈\n₄ ₁₀\n[Q5]\n● Do carbon atoms ke beech C=C double bond wala hydrocarbon Alkene kehlata hai. Open-chain mono-alkenes ka general\nformula C H\n hota hai; Ethene, Propene aur Butene common examples hain.\nₙ ₂ₙ\n[Q6]\n● Given compounds ka decreasing melting-point order source mein: Acetic acid > Chloroform > Ethanol > Methane. Ye trend\nspecific substances ke actual melting points par based hai, sirf molecular mass par nahi. [Q7]\n● Cigarette lighters mein commonly liquefied Butane (C H ) fuel use hota hai. Butane flammable hydrocarbon/NGL hai jo\n₄ ₁₀\npressure mein easily liquefy ho jata hai. [Q8]\n3. Methane, Carbon Black, Biogas & Bhopal MIC\n● Bhopal Gas Tragedy 2–3 December 1984 ki raat Union Carbide plant, Bhopal mein Methyl Isocyanate (MIC) leakage se\nhui. MIC ko methane ya methyl cyanide se confuse mat karo. [Q9, Q10, Q11]\n● Methane colourless, odourless hydrocarbon hai jo marshes, anaerobic decomposition aur coal-related gases mein mil sakta\nhai. Methane/hydrocarbon ka incomplete combustion ya thermal decomposition Carbon black deta hai, jo black printing ink\nmein use hota hai. [Q12]\n● Waterlogged paddy fields mein anaerobic microbial decomposition methane produce karti hai, isliye rice cultivation\natmospheric methane ka important anthropogenic source hai. [Q13]\n● Conceptual matching: Biogas → cow-dung/organic matter; Electrocardiography → heart disorder; DDT → insecticide;\nNicotine → tobacco. [Q14]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q14 ka code-format source mein flawed/awkward hai\n\n▸Exam-safe conceptual matching relation yaad rakho; printed code sequence ko independent chemistry fact mat banao.\n\n▸Biogas ka major combustible component methane hota hai, lekin Q14 mein asked pairing “Biogas → Cow-dung” production-source ke\ncontext mein hai."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Hydrocarbons Full Mind Map\n4. Fruit Ripening — Ethephon, Ethylene & Calcium Carbide\n● Ethephon (Ethrel) plant-growth regulator hai jo plant tissues/aqueous conditions mein Ethylene release karke fruit ripening\npromote kar sakta hai. [Q15]\n● Calcium carbide (CaC ) moisture/water ke saath react karke Acetylene (C H ) banata hai; acetylene ethylene-like ripening\n₂\n₂ ₂\neffect de sakta hai. [Q16, Q17]\n● Natural fruit-ripening hormone Ethylene (C H ) hai. Climacteric fruits mein ethylene ripening processes ko trigger/accelerate\n₂ ₄\n\nkarta hai. [Q18]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Artificial ripening mein Ethylene aur Calcium carbide ko same mat samjho\n\n▸Natural/physiological ripening agent = Ethylene; Ethephon ethylene release karta hai.\n\n▸Calcium carbide acetylene release karta hai aur food ripening ke liye unsafe/legally restricted practice hai; exam question source isse\nhistorical/artificial-ripening agent ke roop mein pooch sakta hai.\n5. Acetylene — Welding, PVC & Preparation\n● Gas welding mein Oxygen + Acetylene (oxy-acetylene) mixture high-temperature flame generate karta hai; steel\nwelding/cutting ke classic questions isi pair par based hote hain. [Q19, Q20]\n● Acetylene = Ethyne (C H ). Welding ke alawa ye vinyl chloride/PVC-type chemical manufacture ka raw material route ho\n₂ ₂\nsakta hai. [Q21]\n● Acetylene water + Calcium carbide (CaC ) reaction se prepare kiya ja sakta hai; Silicon carbide + water statement incorrect\n₂\n\nhai. [Q21]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q21 — Calcium carbide vs Silicon carbide\n\n▸Correct reaction: CaC + 2H O → C H + Ca(OH) .\n₂\n₂\n₂ ₂\n₂\n\n▸Silicon carbide (SiC, carborundum) ko acetylene-preparation reagent mat samjho.\n6. Benzene Structure — Sigma & Pi Bonds\n● Benzene ka formula C H hai; six carbon atoms planar hexagonal ring form karte hain aur π-electrons ring mein\n₆ ₆\ndelocalised hote hain. [Q22]\n● Benzene mein total 12 sigma (σ) bonds hote hain: 6 C–C σ + 6 C–H σ. π system ko classical counting mein 3 π bonds ke\nequivalent count kiya jata hai. [Q22, Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Benzene mein alternating double-bond drawing ko literal fixed bonds mat samjho\n\n▸Exam counting: 12 σ + 3 π. Modern bonding picture mein π electrons poori ring par delocalised hote hain.\n\n▸Resonance ki wajah se benzene ke sab C–C bond lengths equivalent hote hain.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q23\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0340","t":"07.ii Alcohol","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Alcohol Full Mind Map\n🧪 ALCOHOL — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.B · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Methanol vs Ethanol & Denatured Alcohol\n2. Fermentation of Sugar & Enzymes\n3. Molasses, Barley & Alcoholic Beverages\n4. Breathalyzer Chemistry\n1. Methanol vs Ethanol & Denatured Alcohol\n● Ethyl alcohol (ethanol) ko drinking ke liye unfit banane ke context mein source answer Methanol + Pyridine diya gaya hai.\nAise treated ethanol ko denatured alcohol/methylated spirit category mein rakha jata hai. [Q1]\n● Methanol (methyl alcohol) bahut toxic hota hai; poisoning se metabolic acidosis, optic-nerve damage, blindness aur severe\ncases mein death tak ho sakti hai. Liquor tragedies mein methanol contamination classic cause hai. [Q2]\n● Methyl alcohol ka formula CH OH hai aur ise Wood Spirit bhi kaha jata hai. Historical preparation wood ki destructive\n₃\ndistillation se hoti thi. [Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Denatured alcohol ko “methanol + pyridine hi hamesha” mat samjho\n\n▸Source/old exam answer Q1 mein Methanol + Pyridine hai; practical denaturing formulations country/regulation ke hisab se vary kar sakti\nhain.\n\n▸Ethanol khud beverage alcohol hai; Methanol toxic alcohol hai—dono ko interchange mat karo.\n2. Fermentation of Sugar & Enzymes\n● Sugar/glucose ki fermentation se Ethyl alcohol (Ethanol) banta hai. Ye process yeast ke enzymes ke through anaerobic\nconditions mein hota hai. [Q4]\n● Glucose ko ethanol + CO mein convert karne wala enzyme-complex Zymase hai. Yeast mein naturally present hota hai\n₂\naur alcoholic fermentation mein central role play karta hai. [Q5]\n● Enzyme recall: Invertase → sucrose ko glucose + fructose; Maltase → maltose ko glucose; Diastase/Amylase-type action\n→ starch ko simpler sugars/maltose mein todta hai. [Q5]\n3. Molasses, Barley & Alcoholic Beverages\n● Molasses (sheera) sugar industry ka by-product hai aur fermentation ke through alcohol/ethanol production ka important\nraw material hai. Rum traditionally molasses route se ban sakti hai. [Q6]\n● Alcoholic beverages ke raw materials alag ho sakte hain: Beer mainly malted barley; Brandy grapes; Whisky\nbarley/corn/grain; Cider apple; Champagne grapes. Source mein alcohol-% ranges bhi indicative form mein diye gaye hain.\n[Q6]\n● Germinated barley se malt milta hai aur uske fermentation se Beer banayi jati hai. Isliye given options mein correct answer\nBeer hai. [Q7]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Beverage source ko rigid one-to-one rule mat banao\n\n▸Whisky, beer etc. ki production traditions/raw materials region aur style ke hisab se vary kar sakte hain; exam question ka specific option-\ncontext dekho.\n\n▸Q7 ka key clue “germinated barley grains → malt fermentation” hai, jiska standard answer Beer hai.\n4. Breathalyzer Chemistry\n● Old chemical breathalyzer mein acidified Potassium dichromate (K Cr O + H SO ) alcohol vapour ke saath react karta tha.\n₂\n₂ ₇\n₂\n₄\n\nEthanol oxidise hota hai aur dichromate ka orange colour green Cr³ side ki taraf change hota hai.\n⁺\n[Q8]\n● Colour change ki degree breath alcohol level se relate ki jati thi; isi principle par source ka filter-paper question based hai.\n[Q8]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Old breathalyzer vs modern devices\n\n▸Q8 specifically old dichromate-based breathalyzer chemistry poochta hai.\n\n▸Modern breath alcohol analysers commonly fuel-cell sensor ya infrared spectroscopy bhi use kar sakte hain; isliye “har breathalyzer mein\ndichromate filter paper hota hai” mat likho.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q8\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0341","t":"07.iii Polymer","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Polymer Full Mind Map\n🧪 POLYMER — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.C · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Polymer Basics & Natural Polymers\n2. Fibre / Plastic Classification\n3. Polythene, PET & Hydrogels\n4. Bulletproof Polymers & Armour Materials\n5. Neoprene, Teflon & Common Synthetic Polymers\n6. Fibroin, PFAS & BPA\n7. Bakelite — Phenol–Formaldehyde Polymer\n1. Polymer Basics & Natural Polymers\n● Polymerization mein bahut saare small molecules (monomers) judkar large polymer molecule banate hain. Natural rubber\nka monomer Isoprene hai; isliye natural rubber ko polyisoprene maana jata hai. [Q1–Q2]\n● Wool, Silk aur Leather natural polymers hain, jabki Nylon synthetic polymer hai. Silk khud ek natural protein polymer hai;\nGhee lipids/fats ka mixture hai, polymer nahi. Starch, Protein aur Cotton (cellulose) natural polymers ke examples hain. [Q3–Q5]\n● Silk ka major structural protein Fibroin hai. Protein amino acids se bante hain, isliye natural silk mein Nitrogen important\nconstituent element hai. [Q6]\n● Cellulose aur Starch dono glucose units se bane polysaccharides hain. Cellulose nature ka sabse abundant organic\ncompound maana jata hai aur carbohydrate group se belong karta hai; cotton cellulose ka bahut pure natural source hai. [Q7–\nQ9]\n● Rayon, linen aur jute largely cellulosic fibres hain; Nylon synthetic aur non-cellulosic fibre ka example hai. [Q10]\n2. Fibre / Plastic Classification\n● Artificial silk ka naam Rayon se associated hai, Acrylic se nahi. Rayon chemically treated wood pulp/cellulose se banta hai;\nAcrylic fibres natural wool jaise properties dikhate hain. Polycarbonate CDs mein aur Teflon non-stick coating mein use hota\nhai. [Q11]\n● Neoprene thermoplastic nahi, balki synthetic-rubber elastomer hai. Ye chloroprene ke polymerization se banta hai aur\npolychloroprene bhi kaha jata hai. [Q12]\n● PVC (polyvinyl chloride) common synthetic polymer hai jo readily biodegradable nahi hota; cellulose, starch aur proteins\nnatural biodegradable polymers hain. [Q13]\n● Melamine ek thermosetting plastic hai. Heat/cure ke baad iska structure permanently rigid ho jata hai aur ise remelt karke\nthermoplastic ki tarah reshape nahi kiya ja sakta; floor tiles/laminates/kitchenware mein use hota hai. [Q17]\n3. Polythene, PET & Hydrogels\n● Polythene/Polyethylene ka actual monomer Ethylene (Ethene, C H ) hai. Ethylene ke addition polymerization se\n₂ ₄\npolyethylene banta hai. [Q14–Q15]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q14 mein correct monomer option hi missing hai\n\n▸Polythene ka monomer Ethylene hai, lekin Q14 ke options Methane/Ethane/Propane/Butane the; isliye source ne ise disputed (*) mark\nkiya hai.\n\n▸Ethane aur Ethylene ko confuse mat karna: polymerization ke liye unsaturated Ethylene (C H ) chahiye.\n₂ ₄\n● PET (Polyethylene terephthalate) fibres ko wool/cotton ke saath blend kiya ja sakta hai aur PET bottles recycle hokar\ncarpets, packaging ya clothing jaise products mein ja sakti hain. “Any alcoholic beverage storage” aur “incineration without\ngreenhouse gases” statements correct nahi hain. [Q18]\n● Hydrogels water-rich polymeric networks hote hain. Source ke according controlled drug delivery, mobile cooling/air-\nconditioning applications aur industrial lubrication mein inka use ho sakta hai. [Q19]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q16 ka “polyethylene gas” wording scientifically misleading hai\n\n▸Polyethylene khud high-molecular-weight polymer hai aur normal conditions mein gas nahi hota.\n\n▸Q16 ko source-mapping ke liye preserve kiya gaya hai, lekin “plastic se polyethylene gas milti hai” ko standard chemistry fact ke roop\nmein yaad na karein. [Q16]\n4. Bulletproof Polymers & Armour Materials\n● Kevlar lightweight bulletproof jackets/vests aur helmets ka classic fibre hai. Ye high tensile-strength para-aromatic\nPolyamide synthetic fibre hai. [Q20–Q24]\n● Bullet-resistant windows/transparent armour mein transparent Polycarbonate (e.g., Lexan) aur laminated-glass layers use\nhoti hain; Kevlar opaque body armour ke liye more appropriate hai. [Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Polymer Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q26 — “Bulletproof jacket” vs Laminated Glass\n\n▸Source ke historical official key mein Laminated Glass accept hua, lekin actual bulletproof jacket/body armour ka standard fibre Kevlar\nhota hai.\n\n▸Laminated glass/polycarbonate ko transparent armour/windows se associate karo; Kevlar ko vests/jackets se.\n● Bulletproof materials ke context mein Kevlar + Lexan dono relevant hain: Kevlar body armour, Lexan polycarbonate\ntransparent armour/glass. Glyptal paints/lacquers ke protective coatings mein use hota hai. [Q26–Q27]\n5. Neoprene, Teflon & Common Synthetic Polymers\n● Natural rubber = Isoprene polymer; Neoprene = Chloroprene polymer. Teflon aur Dacron polymers hain, aur Polythene\nEthylene ka polymer hai. [Q28]\n● Teflon ka chemical naam PTFE (Polytetrafluoroethylene) hai. Ye non-stick cookware coating mein widely use hota hai.\n[Q29–Q31]\n● PTFE ek solid fluorocarbon / synthetic fluoropolymer hai; iska monomer Tetrafluoroethylene hota hai. “Teflon” PTFE ka\ncommon trade name hai. [Q32–Q34]\n● Caprolactam khud polymer nahi, balki Nylon production ka monomer/raw material hai. Nylon, Teflon aur Polystyrene\npolymers hain. [Q35]\n6. Fibroin, PFAS & BPA\n● Fibroin natural silk protein hai, synthetic nahi. Lexan, Neoprene aur Teflon synthetic polymeric materials hain. [Q36]\n● PFAS (per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances) consumer products/food packaging/non-stick applications se associated\nsynthetic chemicals ka large group hai. Strong C–F bonds ke karan ye environment mein persistent rehte hain aur\nbioaccumulation concern create kar sakte hain. [Q37]\n● Bisphenol A (BPA) primarily Polycarbonate plastics aur Epoxy resins ki manufacture mein key chemical hai; food-packaging\nmaterials, water bottles aur can coatings ke context mein poocha jata hai. [Q38–Q39]\n7. Bakelite — Phenol–Formaldehyde Polymer\n● Bakelite ek thermosetting Phenol–Formaldehyde resin hai. Ye Phenol aur Formaldehyde ki condensation reaction se banta\nhai. [Q40–Q41]\n● Bakelite ko Leo Baekeland ne early 20th century mein develop kiya; exam recall ke liye “Phenol + Formaldehyde →\nBakelite” direct pair yaad rakho. [Q40–Q41]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q41\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0342","t":"07.iv Organic Acid","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Organic Acid Full Mind Map\n🧪 ORGANIC ACID — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.D · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Acid Strength, Formic & Oxalic Acid\n2. Lactic Acid, Muscle Fatigue & Curd Formation\n3. Common Organic Acids & Natural Sources\n4. Important Uses — Photography & Baking Powder\n5. Acetic Acid & Vinegar\n6. Optical Activity — Glycine\n1. Acid Strength, Formic & Oxalic Acid\n● Formic acid (HCOOH) aur Acetic acid (CH COOH) dono organic acids hain, lekin Formic acid stronger hota hai. Acetic acid\n₃\n\nka –CH group electron-donating effect deta hai, jis se H release comparatively difficult hota hai; isi liye Assertion aur Reason\n₃\n⁺\n\ndono true hain, par Reason strength ka correct explanation nahi hai. [Q1]\n● Oxalic acid ka formula C H O = (COOH) = HOOC–COOH hota hai. Iska IUPAC naam Ethanedioic acid hai aur ye\n₂ ₂ ₄\n₂\nsimplest dicarboxylic acid maana jata hai. [Q2]\n2. Lactic Acid, Muscle Fatigue & Curd Formation\n● Exam-oriented conventional explanation ke mutabik prolonged strenuous exercise ke baad muscles me Lactic acid\n[CH CH(OH)COOH] accumulate hone se fatigue/cramp-like sensation associate ki jati hai.\n₃\n[Q3–Q5]\n● Fresh milk me Lactose milk-sugar hota hai. Lactobacillus bacteria lactose ko ferment karke Lactic acid banata hai; isi\nacidification se milk sour hota hai aur milk proteins coagulate hoke curd bante hain. [Q10, Q13–Q17]\n● Isliye Sour milk/Curd ka key acid = Lactic acid. “Lactose” acid nahi, sugar hai; aur Acetic acid vinegar ka acid hai. [Q10–Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q3–Q5 — “Lactic acid causes fatigue” ko exam-language samjho\n\n▸Traditional exam texts muscle fatigue ko lactic-acid accumulation se link karte hain, isliye source-key ke liye Lactic acid yaad rakho.\n\n▸Modern exercise physiology me fatigue multi-factorial hoti hai; lactate ko single direct cause maanna oversimplification hai. Competitive-\nexam answer aur deeper physiology ko mix mat karna.\n3. Common Organic Acids & Natural Sources\n● High-yield source pairs: Lemon/Citrus → Citric acid; Vinegar/Pickle → Acetic acid; Milk/Sour milk → Lactic acid; Rancid\nbutter/Butter → Butyric acid; Apple → Malic acid; Cold drinks/Soda water → Carbonic acid. [Q6–Q9, Q12]\n● Ascorbic acid = Vitamin C aur fresh fruits/vegetables se associated hai; Formic acid red ants/bee-sting context me aata hai.\nCurd me Lactic acid hota hai, Acetic acid nahi. [Q11]\n● Grapes ka predominant organic acid Tartaric acid hai; grapes, tamarind aur banana me bhi Tartaric acid exam-pair ke roop\nme poocha gaya hai. [Q18, Q20]\n● Tomato me mainly Citric acid aur Malic acid milte hain; Oxalic acid comparatively kam amount me ho sakta hai. [Q19]\n4. Important Uses — Photography & Baking Powder\n● Source ke according Oxalic acid photography-related processing/cleaning me reducing agent ke roop me use ho sakta hai.\nDirect exam pair: Photography → Oxalic acid. [Q21]\n● Tartaric acid baking powder me acidic component ke roop me use hota hai; Baking soda (NaHCO ) ke saath react karke\n₃\nCO release karne aur leavening me help karta hai.\n₂\n[Q22]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q21 — Photography ka “main chemical” mat samajhna\n\n▸Source answer Oxalic acid hai, jo kuch photographic processing/cleaning contexts me use ho sakta hai.\n\n▸Photography chemistry me silver-halide compounds bhi fundamental hote hain; isliye “photography = only oxalic acid” jaisa broad\nstatement mat banana.\n5. Acetic Acid & Vinegar\n● Acetic acid (CH COOH), jise Ethanoic acid bhi kehte hain, vinegar ke sour taste aur pungent smell ka main reason hai.\n₃\nVinegar basically dilute aqueous acetic-acid solution hota hai. [Q23–Q28]\n● Vinegar food preservative aur cooking ingredient ke roop me use hota hai. Sugar-rich raw material se pehle ethanol banta\nhai aur phir acetic-acid bacteria ethanol ko acetic acid me oxidise karte hain. [Q24, Q26, Q29]\n● Q29 me A, B aur D correct hain: vinegar fermentation se ban sakta hai, usme Acetic acid hota hai aur preservative ke roop\nme use hota hai; Benzoic acid vinegar ka chief acid nahi hai. [Q29]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Organic Acid Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q27–Q28 — “Vinegar ka chemical name = Acetic acid” ek exam-shortcut hai\n\n▸Pure Acetic acid aur Vinegar same cheez nahi hain: Vinegar ek dilute aqueous solution/food product hai jiska chief acid Acetic acid hota\nhai.\n\n▸Exam me option-based question ho to Acetic acid/Ethanoic acid select hota hai, lekin conceptually vinegar ko pure compound mat\nsamjho.\n6. Optical Activity — Glycine\n● Optical activity ke liye molecule me generally chiral carbon chahiye jo four different groups se attached ho. Glycine (NH –\n₂\nCH –COOH) me α-carbon par do H atoms hote hain, isliye wo achiral aur optically inactive hota hai.\n₂\n[Q30]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q30\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0343","t":"07.v The Explosive Substances","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Explosive Substances Full Mind Map\n🧪 THE EXPLOSIVE SUBSTANCES — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.E · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Mine Explosions & Non-Explosive Trap\n2. Nitroglycerine, Nobel Oil & Dynamite\n3. RDX: Discovery, Names & Key Facts\n4. HMX / Octogen — High Explosive\n5. Cordite, Blasting Gelatine & Amatol\n6. Quick Revision — High-Yield Explosive Pairs\n1. Mine Explosions & Non-Explosive Trap\n● Coal/mines me methane (CH ) air ke saath explosive mixture bana sakta hai. Source ke mutabik approx. 5–15% methane-\n₄\nin-air range especially dangerous/explosive hoti hai; given options me mine explosions ka standard answer Methane + Air hai.\n[Q1]\n● Nitrochloroform = Chloropicrin ko source “not an explosive” ke roop me treat karta hai; iska use historically toxic/tear-gas\naur agriculture me fumigant/fungicidal-insecticidal chemical ke roop me hua hai. TNT, TNG/RDX aur Potassium chlorate\nexplosive contexts me aate hain. [Q2–Q3]\n2. Nitroglycerine, Nobel Oil & Dynamite\n● Nitroglycerine ko Trinitroglycerol (TNG), Glyceryl trinitrate (GTN) aur Nobel oil bhi kaha jata hai. Ye heavy, oily, highly\nenergetic liquid explosive hai. [Q4, Q9]\n● Glycerol ko concentrated HNO + H SO ke saath nitrate karne par Nitroglycerine/Glycerol trinitrate banta hai; isi wajah se\n₃\n₂\n₄\nGlycerol explosive manufacture ka important precursor hai. [Q11]\n● Dynamite ka active explosive chemical Nitroglycerine (Glycerol trinitrate) hota hai; practical dynamite me isse\nabsorbent/stabilising material ke saath safer handling ke liye formulate kiya jata hai. [Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q2–Q3 — Nitrochloroform / Chloropicrin\n\n▸Source ise “not an explosive” answer karta hai; standard exam context me Chloropicrin ko primarily fumigant/chemical-warfare irritant ke\nroop me yaad rakho.\n\n▸Potassium chlorate khud high explosive ke roop me normal handling material nahi hai, lekin strong oxidiser hone ke karan explosive\nmixtures/pyrotechnic compositions me use ho sakta hai. Question ka option-context important hai.\n3. RDX: Discovery, Names & Key Facts\n● RDX ek powerful nitroamine high explosive hai. George Friedrich Henning ne is compound ko 1890s me prepare/patent\nkiya; exam source inventor/discoverer ke roop me Henning ko mark karta hai. [Q5]\n● RDX ka chemical name Cyclotrimethylenetrinitramine hai; common alternate names Cyclonite, Hexogen aur T4 hain.\nSource formula ko (CH N O ) ke form me deta hai.\n₂ ₂ ₂ ₃\n[Q6–Q7]\n● RDX TNT se zyada powerful high explosive maana jata hai aur World War II ke dauran military use me widely aaya. Exam\npair yaad rakho: RDX → Cyclonite/Hexogen. [Q6–Q7]\n● RDX ko “Research Department Explosive” naam se commonly expand kiya jata hai; kuch references “Royal Demolition\nExplosive” bhi likhte hain, isliye objective exam me given source wording ko follow karo. [Q6]\n4. HMX / Octogen — High Explosive\n● HMX ko Octogen bhi kaha jata hai; ye RDX se chemically related powerful aur comparatively insensitive nitroamine high\nexplosive hai. Exam source HMX ka full form “High Melting Explosive” accept karta hai. [Q8]\n● HMX naam ki expansion literature me multiple forms me mil sakti hai, lekin given question me only statement 1 correct hai.\nIsliye option “Only 1” source-key ke according sahi hai. [Q8]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q8 — HMX ko “colourless liquid” mat yaad karo\n\n▸Source explanation me HMX ko colourless liquid likha gaya hai, lekin HMX/Octogen actually crystalline solid high explosive hota hai.\n\n▸Exam key ka relevant part full form/identity hai: HMX → High Melting Explosive (accepted source answer) aur alternate name Octogen.\n5. Cordite, Blasting Gelatine & Amatol\n● Amatol me Nitroglycerine essential constituent nahi hota. Ye mainly Ammonium nitrate + TNT ka mixture hota hai; isi se\nCordite/Blasting Gelatine/Dynamite se differentiate kiya jata hai. [Q10]\n● Cordite aur Blasting Gelatine traditional formulations me Nitroglycerine-containing explosives/propellants rahe hain;\nDynamite bhi Nitroglycerine-based hota hai. [Q10]\n● High-yield distinction: Nitroglycerine-containing group → Cordite, Blasting Gelatine, Dynamite; Nitroglycerine-free given\noption → Amatol. [Q10]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Explosive Substances Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q10 — “Amatol is an explosive element” wording wrong hai\n\n▸Amatol koi element nahi; ye Ammonium nitrate aur TNT ka explosive mixture hai.\n\n▸Question ka tested fact bas itna hai ki Amatol me Nitroglycerine essential constituent nahi hota.\n6. Quick Revision — High-Yield Explosive Pairs\n● Fast revision pairs: Mine explosion → Methane + Air; Nobel oil/TNG → Nitroglycerine; RDX → Cyclonite/Hexogen; HMX →\nOctogen; Dynamite active chemical → Glycerol trinitrate; Amatol → Ammonium nitrate + TNT. [Q1–Q12]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q12\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0344","t":"07.vi The Fuel","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Fuel Full Mind Map\n🧪 THE FUEL — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 7.F · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Fuel Basics, Fossil Fuels & Calorific Value\n2. Coal, Coke, Furnace Oil & Pollution\n3. Octane–Cetane Number & Diesel Engine\n4. Biogas / Gobar Gas\n5. LPG: Composition, Storage & Safety\n6. Natural Gas, CNG & LNG\n7. Fuel Blends, Engines & Emission Control\n8. SAF, Hydrogen Fuel & Petroleum Products\n1. Fuel Basics, Fossil Fuels & Calorific Value\n● Petroleum natural fuel hai, jabki coke, tar aur coal gas ko processing/destructive distillation se obtain kiya ja sakta hai. Coal,\npetroleum aur natural gas fossil fuels hain; inme natural gas comparatively cleaner fossil fuel maana jata hai because combustion par\ncoal/diesel ke comparison me pollutants aur carbon emissions kam hote hain. [Q1–Q3]\n● Calorific value ka matlab complete combustion par released heat per unit mass hota hai. Common fuels me Hydrogen ka calorific\nvalue sabse high hota hai (source approx. 150,000 kJ/kg), isliye high-energy applications/rocket-fuel context me important hai. [Q4]\n2. Coal, Coke, Furnace Oil & Pollution\n● India ke coal-based thermal plants ke baare me “koi seawater use nahi karta / water-stressed district me nahi hai / private\nownership nahi hai” — teeno statements false hain. Coastal plants seawater cooling use kar sakte hain, water-scarce districts me\nplants hain aur private coal power producers bhi operate karte hain. [Q5]\n● Coal ash me arsenic, lead, mercury jaise heavy metals ho sakte hain; coal-fired plants SO , NOx aur particulate pollutants emit\n₂\nkarte hain, aur Indian coal ka ash content generally high hota hai. Copper smelting me slag heavy-metal leaching aur SO major\n₂\nconcerns hain. Indoor burning of coal harmful chemical pollution ka strong source hai. [Q6–Q8]\n● Blast furnace me coke fuel + reducing agent dono ka role nibhata hai; silica removal mainly limestone-derived flux karta hai.\nFurnace oil crude-oil refining ka heavy residual product hai, industries/power generation me burn hota hai aur sulphur content ke\nkaran SOx emissions produce kar sakta hai. [Q9–Q10]\n3. Octane–Cetane Number & Diesel Engine\n● Plastic-waste derived fuel ko source high-octane/lead-free “green fuel” batata hai. Octane number petrol ki anti-knock quality\nmeasure karta hai: higher octane = compression/knocking resistance better. Petrol quality commonly Octane number se express ki\njati hai. [Q11–Q13]\n● Cetane number diesel fuel ki ignition quality ka parameter hai; higher cetane generally shorter ignition delay aur better\ncompression-ignition behaviour show karta hai. Diesel engine me air ko high compression se heat kiya jata hai aur phir diesel inject\nhokar ignite hota hai; carburetor petrol engines se associated hai. [Q14–Q15]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q15 — “vapour of diesel and air” ko literal mechanism mat samjho\n\n▸Source option (A) ko key diya gaya hai, lekin diesel engine me pehle sirf air compress hoti hai; diesel fuel baad me high-pressure injection se hot\ncompressed air me spray hota hai.\n\n▸Exam option ko source context me yaad rakho, conceptual mechanism = compression ignition + fuel injection.\n4. Biogas / Gobar Gas\n● Biogas/Gobar gas ka chief combustible component Methane (CH ) hai; mixture me commonly methane ke saath CO hota hai aur\n₄\n₂\ntraces me H S/moisture etc. ho sakte hain. Organic waste/cattle dung ka anaerobic fermentation/digestion biogas production ka basic\n₂\n\nprocess hai. [Q16–Q22]\n● Source ke according cattle dung se methane-producing pilot gas plant S.V. Desai se linked hai; option me “C.B. Desai” typo diya\ngaya hai. Rice fields anaerobic conditions ki wajah se methane emit karte hain. [Q23–Q24]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q16 & Q23\n\n▸Q16 me “Cooking gas” ke options me Methane best fit hai because explanation biogas/gobar gas context use karti hai; lekin ordinary domestic\ncylinder cooking gas = LPG, mainly propane + butane.\n\n▸Q23 option “C.B. Desai” source typo hai; explanation S.V. Desai batati hai.\n5. LPG: Composition, Storage & Safety\n● LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas) mainly propane (C H ) aur butane (C H ) ka mixture hai; small amounts of other light\n₃ ₈\n₄ ₁₀\nhydrocarbons ho sakte hain. Domestic Indane/LPG context me butane + propane key combination hai. [Q25–Q30]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Fuel Full Mind Map\n● LPG naturally almost odourless hoti hai, isliye leak detection ke liye Ethyl Mercaptan jaise strong-smelling odorant add kiya jata\nhai. Fuel-gas matching: CNG → methane-rich; LPG → propane/butane; coal gas → H + CH + CO; water gas → CO + H .\n₂\n₄\n₂ [Q31–Q32]\n● LPG ka main component methane nahi hai; methane pipeline natural-gas/PNG fuel ka principal component ho sakta hai. LPG\ncylinder me fuel pressure ke under liquid phase me stored hota hai; jab tak liquid present hai pressure mainly vapour pressure ke\naround rehta hai, isliye simple pressure gauge remaining quantity accurately show nahi karta. [Q33–Q35]\n6. Natural Gas, CNG & LNG\n● Natural gas ka dominant hydrocarbon Methane hai. CNG = Compressed Natural Gas; natural gas ko high pressure par compress\nkarke transport/use kiya jata hai aur CNG me methane major constituent hota hai. [Q36–Q41]\n● LNG = Liquefied Natural Gas; natural gas ko roughly –162°C tak cool karke liquid banaya jata hai, storage/transport easy hota hai.\nIndia ka first LNG terminal Dahej, Gujarat se associated hai. NGL (Natural Gas Liquids), not “NGM”, me ethane, propane, butane aur\nnatural gasoline jaise fractions aa sakte hain. [Q42]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q42 — LNG “high pressure” wording\n\n▸Question statement LNG ko extremely cold temperature + high pressure se liquefied batata hai, lekin standard LNG storage near-atmospheric\npressure aur cryogenic temperature (~–162°C) par hota hai.\n\n▸Source explanation khud near-atmospheric pressure likhti hai; isliye statement wording technically inconsistent hai.\n7. Fuel Blends, Engines & Emission Control\n● Kerosene hydrocarbon mixture hai, isliye oxygen absent maana jata hai. Gasohol = gasoline/petrol + ethanol blend; geothermal\nenergy non-conventional renewable source hai aur gobar gas methane-rich hoti hai. [Q43–Q46]\n● Tetraethyl lead (TEL) historically petrol ka anti-knock additive tha, lekin lead toxicity ke karan largely phased out ho chuka hai.\nAutomobile antifreeze me ethylene glycol commonly use hota hai. Heavy vehicles me diesel high torque + fuel efficiency ke karan\nuseful hai; carburetor traditional petrol engines me, diesel me fuel injection system use hota hai. [Q47–Q51]\n● Catalytic converters exhaust pollutants ko less harmful products me convert karte hain aur commonly platinum, palladium, rhodium\ncatalysts use karte hain. Radial tyres, streamlined body aur multipoint fuel injection fuel economy improve karte hain; catalytic\nconverter ka primary role emission control hai. [Q52–Q53]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q53 — Official key vs concept\n\n▸Source official key option (D) = 1, 3, 4 deta hai.\n\n▸Conceptually streamlined body (2) drag reduce karke fuel efficiency improve karti hai, jabki catalytic converter (4) ka primary purpose emissions\ncontrol hai. Is question ko official-key specific trap ki tarah yaad rakho.\n8. SAF, Hydrogen Fuel & Petroleum Products\n● Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) ke feedstocks me agricultural residues, corn grain, wastewater-treatment sludge/wet wastes aur\nwood-mill waste sab use ho sakte hain. SAF conventional jet fuel ke comparison me lower lifecycle carbon footprint target karta hai.\n[Q54]\n● Hydrogen Fuel Cell Electric Vehicles me fuel cell hydrogen ki chemical energy ko electricity me convert karta hai; tailpipe se mainly\nwater vapour + warm air nikalte hain. Hydrogen storage ke liye metal hydrides hydrogen absorb/release kar sakte hain. [Q55–Q56]\n● Petroleum refining se asphalt/bitumen heavy by-product/fraction milta hai jo road construction binder me use hota hai. Source-era\n“Hydrocarbon Vision 2025” ko petroleum-product storage aur long-term energy security/self-reliance context se associate karta hai.\n[Q57–Q58]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q58\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0345","t":"08 Food Preservation Nutrition Medicine","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Food Preservation, Nutrition & Medicine Full Mind Map\n🧪 FOOD PRESERVATION, NUTRITION & MEDICINE — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 8 · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Food Preservation, Refrigeration & Additives\n2. Sugars, Sweeteners & Nutrition Chemistry\n3. Medicinal Chemistry & Aspirin\n4. Antibiotics, Drug Classes & Sedatives\n5. Toxicology, Food Processing & Organic Food\n1. Food Preservation, Refrigeration & Additives\n● Fruits/vegetables par wax emulsion coating storage life badhane ke liye use hoti hai; ye moisture loss aur respiration ko limit kar\nsakti hai aur preservatives/growth regulators ka carrier bhi ban sakti hai. Galat coating se off-flavour develop ho sakta hai. [Q1]\n● Sodium benzoate (C H NaO , E211) acidic foods/fruit juices me common chemical preservative hai. Benzoic acid aur uske salts\n₇ ₅\n₂\nmicrobial growth ko inhibit karte hain; isi liye food preservation questions me repeatedly pooche gaye hain. [Q2–Q6]\n● Potato chips ko Nitrogen atmosphere me pack kiya jata hai taaki oxidation/rancidity kam ho, moisture se protection mile aur bag\ncushioning de. Cold storage me respiration aur ethylene production ki rate kam hoti hai, isliye fruits ki ripening slow aur shelf life\nlonger hoti hai. [Q7, Q9]\n● MSG (Monosodium glutamate/Ajinomoto) glutamic acid ka sodium salt hai aur food me mainly umami/flavour enhancer ke roop me\nuse hota hai. Source question ise flavour enhancer ke saath preserver bhi mark karta hai, isliye exam context me multiple-answer\nnote important hai. [Q8]\n● Refrigeration food ko sterilize nahi karti; ye microorganisms ki growth aur biochemical reactions ko slow karti hai. Source-era\ndomestic-refrigerator question Freon ko common refrigerant batata hai. Triclosan antibacterial chemical toiletries jaise\nsoaps/toothpastes/cosmetics me mil sakta hai. [Q10–Q12]\n● Animal/bone charcoal historically sugar refining me decolourizing/de-ashing agent ke roop me use hua hai. Activated carbon-type\nadsorbents coloured impurities ko surface par adsorb karke clarification me help karte hain. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q8 & Q11 — Source wording vs modern chemistry\n\n▸Q8 source MSG ko flavour enhancer + preserver dono mark karta hai. Standard food-science role mainly flavour enhancer (umami) hai;\n“preservative” ko general primary function mat samjho.\n\n▸Q11 ka Freon answer old-exam context hai. Modern domestic refrigerators me ozone-depleting CFC Freons largely phase-out ho chuke hain;\nnewer refrigerants (e.g. R-600a) common hain.\n2. Sugars, Sweeteners & Nutrition Chemistry\n● Honey me fructose aur glucose major sugars hain; source composition me fructose sabse bada fraction diya hai. Natural common\nsugars me Fructose sabse sweet hota hai. Relative naming: grape sugar = glucose, fruit sugar = fructose, milk sugar = lactose, table\nsugar = sucrose, Stevia = natural sweetener. [Q14–Q17]\n● Sugar beet → sugar, honey → glucose + fructose, cotton → cellulose aur milk → lactose — ye chaaron pairs correctly matched\nhain. Invert sugar sucrose ke hydrolysis se glucose + fructose deta hai; free fructose ke karan sucrose se sweeter hota hai. [Q16, Q18]\n● Aspartame approx. 200× sucrose se sweeter hai; isliye bahut small quantity me desired sweetness milti hai aur calorie contribution\nlow ho jata hai, even though gram-for-gram energy deta hai. Given artificial sweeteners me source ke according Alitame (~2000×\nsucrose) highest sweetness value deta hai. [Q19–Q20]\n3. Medicinal Chemistry & Aspirin\n● Medicinal chemistry me drugs ko molecular targets ke basis par classify karna highly useful hai, kyunki drugs proteins/nucleic\nacids etc. target biomolecules ke saath interact karke specific mechanism of action dikhati hain. [Q21]\n● Aspirin = acetylsalicylic acid; salicylate chemistry ka historical origin willow bark se linked hai. Aspirin analgesic, antipyretic aur\nanti-inflammatory drug hai; given options me antipyretic classification accepted hai. [Q22–Q23]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q22 — “Aspirin is obtained from a tree”\n\n▸Historical natural precursor salicylic acid willow bark se mila tha; modern aspirin directly tree se extract nahi hota, industrially salicylic acid ki\nacetylation se synthesize hota hai.\n\n▸Exam option me “a tree” historical-origin sense me accepted hai.\n4. Antibiotics, Drug Classes & Sedatives\n● Natural antibiotics ke important producers soil microorganisms hain—especially Streptomyces/actinomycetes (bacteria) aur kuch\nfungi. Source Q24 “mostly bacteria” ko key karta hai because known natural antibiotics ka large share bacterial/actinomycete origin ka\nhai. [Q24]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Food Preservation, Nutrition & Medicine Full Mind Map\n● Penicillin antibiotic hai. Source Q25 me Penicillin aur Sulfadiazine dono antibacterial options hone ki wajah se “more than one”\ndiya gaya hai; Q26 me Penicillin clearly antibiotic option hai. Aspirin/Paracetamol analgesic-antipyretic aur Chloroquine antimalarial\ncategory me aate hain. [Q25–Q26]\n● Drug-class matching: Paracetamol = antipyretic; Calciferol (Vitamin D) = antirachitic; Aspirin antiseptic nahi hai. Chloromycetin =\nantityphoid use, Crystal violet = antiseptic, Quinine = antimalarial; Aspirin anaesthetic nahi, analgesic/antipyretic hai. [Q27–Q28]\n● Potassium bromide (KBr) historically sedative aur anticonvulsant ke roop me use hua; modern human medicine me iska use\nlargely obsolete hai, lekin veterinary antiepileptic context me ab bhi mil sakta hai. [Q29]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q25 — Sulfadiazine terminology\n\n▸Sulfadiazine synthetic sulfonamide antibacterial drug hai; strict/classical definition me ise natural-product “antibiotic” se alag rakha ja sakta hai.\n\n▸Source exam explanation Penicillin + Sulfadiazine dono ko antibiotic-type antibacterial options treat karke “more than one” key karta hai.\n5. Toxicology, Food Processing & Organic Food\n● Carbon monoxide hemoglobin ke saath carboxyhemoglobin banata hai aur oxygen ke comparison me bahut high affinity se bind\nkarta hai; isi wajah se tissue hypoxia aur CO poisoning hoti hai. [Q30]\n● Milk homogenization ka goal fat globules ko microscopic size me todna hai taaki cream layer separate na ho aur texture uniform\nrahe. Clove oil ka main active component Eugenol hai, jisme antiseptic aur analgesic properties hoti hain. [Q31–Q32]\n● Jelly making ke liye high-pectin + adequate-acid fruits best hote hain; Guava pectin-rich hone ki wajah se suitable hai. Organic\nfood production generally synthetic fertilizers aur most conventional pesticides ke restricted/avoided use ke standards follow karta hai.\n[Q33–Q34]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q30, Q31 & Q34\n\n▸Q30 me “irreversible complex” wording technically loose hai: CO–Hb binding bahut strong hai, lekin chemically reversible hai; oxygen therapy se\nCO dissociate ho sakta hai.\n\n▸Q31 source option centrifuge bolta hai, lekin true homogenization high-pressure homogenizer se fat globules break karti hai; centrifugation cream\nseparation ke liye use hoti hai.\n\n▸Q34 me organic = automatically safer/more nutritious prove nahi hota. Correct exam idea production method hai: synthetic fertilizers/pesticides par\nrestrictions.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q34\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0346","t":"09 Detergents and Soap","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Detergents and Soap Full Mind Map\n🧪 DETERGENTS AND SOAP — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 9 · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Soap Formation & Cleaning Action\n2. Detergents, Surfactants & Surface Tension\n3. Hard Water & Washing-Powder Additives\n1. Soap Formation & Cleaning Action\n● Soap generally animal fat ya vegetable oil ko strong alkali (mainly NaOH/KOH) ke saath react karke banaya jata hai; is\nprocess ko saponification kehte hain. Olive, coconut aur palm-kernel jaise vegetable oils soap manufacture me common raw\nmaterials hain. [Q1]\n● Soap molecule amphiphilic hota hai: long non-polar hydrocarbon tail grease/oil me dissolve hoti hai, jabki ionic/polar head\nwater se interact karta hai. Rubbing par micelles/emulsion bante hain, grease tiny droplets me suspend hota hai aur water ke\nsaath wash away ho jata hai. [Q2]\n2. Detergents, Surfactants & Surface Tension\n● Detergent soap se chemically different cleaning agent hota hai; practical chemistry me detergent ka key component\nsurfactant hota hai jo water me cleaning/wetting action improve karta hai. Laundry detergents powder ya concentrated liquid\nform me milte hain. [Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q3 — “Detergent = Refining agent” source-option wording hai\n\n▸Source key option (D) “Refining agent” deta hai, lekin standard chemistry definition me detergent ko surfactant/cleaning agent kehna\nzyada precise hai.\n\n▸Exam me exact options follow karo; concept note me detergent ≠ soap aur detergent = surfactant-based cleansing formulation yaad\nrakho.\n● Clothes-cleaning synthetic detergents commonly alkylbenzene sulfonates jaise anionic surfactants hote hain. Ye soap ke\ncomparison me hard water me bhi effective rehte hain aur insoluble scum kam banate hain. [Q4]\n● Soap/detergent water ka surface tension badhate nahi, balki reduce karte hain. Surfactant molecules surface par arrange\nhoke cohesive interactions ko weaken karte hain, wetting improve hoti hai aur oil/dirt removal easy hota hai. Isliye Q5 me\nAssertion true, Reason false hai. [Q5]\n3. Hard Water & Washing-Powder Additives\n● Synthetic detergents hard water ke Ca² aur Mg² ions ke saath soap-jaisa insoluble precipitate/scum nahi banate; unke\n⁺\n⁺\nsalts comparatively soluble rehte hain. Isi wajah se hard water me lather aur cleaning action better hota hai. [Q6]\n● Washing powder formulations me sodium sulphate aur sodium silicate jaise additives use ho sakte hain. Sodium sulphate\ncommonly filler/diluent aur powder-flow/dryness support karta hai; sodium silicate alkaline builder ke saath corrosion-control\naur alkalinity support me role nibhata hai. [Q7]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q7 — Source explanation me roles ko swap karke padhna mat\n\n▸Question ka broad idea sahi hai: washing powder me additives dryness/free-flow aur alkalinity maintain karne me help karte hain.\n\n▸Standard formulation context me sodium sulphate ko mainly filler/free-flow support aur sodium silicate ko alkaline builder/corrosion-\ninhibitor role se associate karna zyada exam-safe hai.\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q7\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0347","t":"10 The Fertilizers","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Fertilizers Full Mind Map\n🧪 THE FERTILIZERS — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 10 · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Plant Nutrients, NPK & Fertilizer Basics\n2. Urea: Composition, Solubility & Nitrogen Content\n3. Nitrogen Fertilizers, Soil Acidity & Environmental Effects\n4. Urea Production, Neem-coated Urea & Fertilizer Policy Context\n5. DAP, NPK, Foliar Feeding, Humus & Green Manure\n1. Plant Nutrients, NPK & Fertilizer Basics\n● Fertilizer wo natural ya chemical substance hai jo soil fertility, plant growth aur yield improve karne ke liye add kiya jata hai. N, P\naur K major/macronutrients hain: Nitrogen growth-development ke liye, Phosphorus healthy root development ke liye aur Potassium\nstomata ke opening-closing regulation me important hai. [Q1–Q4]\n● Source ke hisaab se 1 metric ton organic manure se roughly 1.5–3 kg phosphorus mil sakta hai, isliye phosphorus requirement ko\nmeet karne me chemical fertilizer important role play karta hai. Wheat cultivation me Nitrogen fertilizer especially important maana\ngaya hai. [Q1–Q2]\n● Plants ko Carbon, Hydrogen aur Oxygen mainly CO aur water se milte hain, jabki N, P, K, Ca, Mg, B, Cl, Cu, Fe, Mn, Mo, Zn jaise\n₂\n\nnutrients soil/inorganic salts se mil sakte hain. Isliye listed options me Hydrogen fertilizer se directly supplied element nahi maana\ngaya hai. [Q3]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q4 — Source itself marks the question disputed\n\n▸Nitrogen → growth/development, Phosphorus → root development, Potassium → stomatal regulation — ye matches correct hain.\n\n▸Boron micronutrient hai; source disease-resistance role bhi accept karta hai. Isliye given options me koi clearly incorrect pair nahi bachta, so\nsource answer = * (disputed).\n2. Urea: Composition, Solubility & Nitrogen Content\n● Urea/Carbamide ka formula CO(NH ) hai. Ye nitrogen-containing organic compound hai aur isme Carbon, Hydrogen, Nitrogen aur\n₂ ₂\n\nOxygen chaaron elements present hote hain. Nitrogen do amide (NH ) groups me hota hai, isliye urea me nitrogen ka form = amide\n₂\nform. [Q6,Q8–Q9]\n● Urea me nitrogen approximately 46–47% hota hai. Isi basis par 1 kg nitrogen supply karne ke liye required urea ≈ 100/46 = 2.17\nkg, yani roughly 2.2 kg. [Q7,Q11]\n● Listed fertilizers me 20°C par urea highly water-soluble hai, isi high solubility aur leaf absorption ke karan urea foliar\napplication/spray ke liye bhi bahut popular fertilizer hai. [Q10,Q19]\n3. Nitrogen Fertilizers, Soil Acidity & Environmental Effects\n● Ammonium sulphate soil ko comparatively zyada acidify kar sakta hai; acidic soil ka pH 7 se kam hota hai. Nitrogenous fertilizers\nka excessive/inappropriate use soil acidity increase kar sakta hai aur unused nitrate groundwater me leach hokar water pollution\ncause kar sakta hai. [Q5,Q13]\n● Excess artificial nitrogen se nitrogen-fixing microorganisms ka proliferation expected nahi hota; source ke explanation ke according\nnatural nitrogen-fixing bacterial activity suppress bhi ho sakti hai. Isliye Q13 me statements 2 aur 3 correct hain. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Nitrogen fertilizer ka “more is better” rule nahi hota\n\n▸Nitrogen essential hai, lekin overuse se soil acidification, nitrate leaching aur environmental pollution ho sakta hai.\n\n▸Exam me fertilizer benefit aur fertilizer overuse ke environmental effects ko alag-alag context me read karo.\n4. Urea Production, Neem-coated Urea & Fertilizer Policy Context\n● Industrial urea synthetic ammonia (NH ) aur carbon dioxide (CO ) se produce hota hai. Ammonia production me hydrogen\n₃\n₂\ncommonly natural gas feedstock se obtain kiya jata hai. [Q12,Q14]\n● Neem-coated urea me neem coating nitrification/urea conversion ko slow karke nitrogen release ko more gradual banati hai. Isse\nnitrogen-use efficiency improve ho sakti hai aur nutrient loss reduce karne me help milti hai. [Q15]\n● Source-era policy question me statement 1 incorrect maana gaya because urea MRP Government-controlled context me tha;\nstatements 2–3 correct: ammonia natural-gas route se aur elemental sulphur petroleum-refinery by-product route se fertilizer industry\nme linked hai. [Q12]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q12 is policy/time-context sensitive\n\n▸Question wording “At present” source-exam period ke context me hai. Is mind map me source explanation preserve ki gayi hai.\n\n▸Static chemistry fact: urea production uses NH + CO ; sulphur/phosphoric-acid fertilizer chain refinery by-product sulphur se linked ho sakti hai.\n₃\n₂"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · The Fertilizers Full Mind Map\n5. DAP, NPK, Foliar Feeding, Humus & Green Manure\n● DAP = Diammonium Phosphate, formula (NH ) HPO . Standard fertilizer grade ko commonly 18-46-0 ke form me express kiya\n₄ ₂\n₄\njata hai: about 18% Nitrogen aur 46% P O .\n₂ ₅ [Q16]\n● NPK mixed/complex fertilizer hai jo Nitrogen + Phosphorus + Potassium combine karta hai. Urea, Super Phosphate aur Potassium\nNitrate common chemical-fertilizer examples hain; listed options me Sodium Sulphate ko chemical fertilizer nahi maana gaya. [Q17–\nQ18]\n● Humus decomposed plant-animal matter se banne wala dark organic material hai aur soil me organic colloid ki tarah behave karta\nhai. Green manuring me generally leguminous crops grow karke soil me incorporate kiye jate hain; listed options me Sunhemp (sanai)\nbest green-manure crop hai. [Q20–Q21]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q21\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0348","t":"11 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Chemistry","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n🧪 MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\nChemistry · Chapter 11 · Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC/PCS/UPSC Ready\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Nobel Prizes, Special Glass, HFC–CFC & Ozone\n2. Fire Safety: Alarm, Extinguishers & Fireproofing\n3. Repellents, Rodenticides, Pesticides & Herbicides\n4. Radioactive Dating, Carbon Credit, Isotopes & Geoengineering\n5. Artificial Rain, Common Chemicals & Match-the-Following\n6. Metals, Pigments, Solvents, Phosphorus, CNT & Desalination\n7. Chemical Warfare, Smoke Screen, Agent Orange & Nuclear Basics\n8. Cells, Batteries, Microwave & Everyday Chemical Applications\n9. Climate Agreements, Greenhouse Gases, Air Pollution & Hydrogen\n10. Smog, Water Pollution, Waste Treatment & Mercury\n1. Nobel Prizes, Special Glass, HFC–CFC & Ozone\n● 2021 ka Chemistry Nobel Benjamin List aur David MacMillan ko asymmetric organocatalysis ke development ke liye mila; 2019 ka Nobel\nJohn Goodenough, Stanley Whittingham aur Akira Yoshino ko lithium-ion battery ke development ke liye diya gaya tha. [Q1–Q2]\n● Crookes glass UV rays ki transmission ko reduce karta hai aur sunglasses me use hota hai; is glass me cerium oxide jaise additives silica\nke saath use kiye ja sakte hain. [Q3]\n● HFCs ka use refrigeration/AC, aerosol propellants, insulating foams aur fire-protection applications me hota hai; source question me\naerosols + foam agents + fire retardants = teen categories correct hain, lubricants nahi. [Q4]\n● Stratospheric ozone depletion ka major cause CFCs se release hone wale chlorine/bromine radicals hain. Ozone water me\nmicroorganisms ko apni strong oxidizing power se kill karta hai; uska non-radioactive hona reason nahi hai. [Q5–Q6]\n2. Fire Safety: Alarm, Extinguishers & Fireproofing\n● Photocell/photoelectric sensor fire-alarm systems me smoke se light path change detect karne ke liye use ho sakta hai. [Q7]\n● CO fire extinguisher oxygen supply ko displace karke combustion ko suppress karta hai. Traditional soda-acid extinguisher me sodium\n₂\nbicarbonate solution aur dilute H SO react karke CO generate karte hain.\n₂\n₄\n₂\n[Q8–Q10]\n● Source ke according Aluminium sulphate textile treatment me fireproof clothing banane ke liye use kiya jata hai. [Q11]\n3. Repellents, Rodenticides, Pesticides & Herbicides\n● Mosquito control me Allethrin aur Prallethrin synthetic pyrethroids hain; Pyrethrum/Pyrethrins Chrysanthemum-based natural insecticidal\ncompounds hain, jabki Lemongrass/Citronella oil natural repellent ke roop me use hota hai. [Q12–Q16]\n● Rodent-control questions me source Potassium cyanide aur Zinc phosphide ko rat poison/rodenticide se link karta hai; “rodenticide”\nspecifically rats/mice jaise rodents ko control karne wale chemicals ke liye term hai. [Q17–Q19]\n● Aluminium phosphide stored grains ke fumigation me phosphine release karta hai aur rodent-control use bhi mil sakta hai, isliye source ne\nis question ko multiple-correct maana hai. [Q20]\n● Herbicides/weedicides me Sodium chlorate non-selective herbicide hai; 2,4-D selective systemic herbicide/synthetic auxin hai aur paddy\nme broadleaf weeds ke control se linked hai; Butachlor rice cultivation ka common herbicide hai. [Q21,Q23–Q24,Q26]\n● Carbofuran, methyl parathion, phorate aur triazophos agriculture pesticides hain jinke toxicity/environmental risk ko lekar regulation\nconcern raha hai. DDT persistent, non-biodegradable pollutant hai jo food chain me accumulate karta hai. [Q22,Q25]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q20: Aluminium Phosphide ka ek hi use nahi\n\n▸Stored-grain fumigation aur rodent-control dono context milte hain, isliye source ne Ans. * (multiple correct) diya hai.\n\n▸Is compound ki toxicity bahut high hai; exam me sirf functional classification yaad rakho, practical use/handling details nahi.\n4. Radioactive Dating, Carbon Credit, Isotopes & Geoengineering\n● Carbon-14 dating once-living materials—wood, bone, shell, fossils—ki age estimate karne ke liye use hoti hai. Rocks/geological age ke liye\nradioactive dating me U-Pb ya K-Ar jaise methods use hote hain; Earth ki age ke context me Uranium process accepted hai. [Q27–Q31]\n● 1 carbon credit generally 1 metric ton = 1000 kg CO -equivalent emission right/reduction ko represent karta hai. BRIT (Board of Radiation\n₂\nand Isotope Technology) DAE ke under isotope/radiation technology services se linked hai. [Q32–Q33]\n● Zinc oxide ko “philosopher’s wool” kaha jata hai; urinals ke paas pungent smell urea ke bacterial breakdown se banne wale ammonia ki\nwajah se hoti hai. [Q34–Q35]\n● Antihelium-4 jaise antimatter nuclei universe evolution aur antimatter stars/galaxies ki possibility ko probe karne me useful hain, mineral\nprospecting ko cheap banana iska practical implication nahi hai. [Q36]\n● Cirrus-cloud thinning aur stratosphere me sulphate aerosol injection proposed geoengineering techniques hain jinka aim planetary\ncooling/global warming ko reduce karna hai. [Q37]\n5. Artificial Rain, Common Chemicals & Match-the-Following\n● Cloud seeding/artificial rain ke liye Silver iodide sabse common exam answer hai; dry ice bhi use ho sakta hai. Rainfall potential\natmospheric humidity/moisture par strongly depend karta hai. [Q38–Q41]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Key matching yaad rakho: Blue vitriol (CuSO ) → fungicide; Eosin → red ink; Silver iodide → artificial rain; Zinc phosphide → rodenticide.\n₄\nZinc phosphide–rat poison correct pair hai. [Q42–Q43]\n● Kevlar → synthetic fibre, Taxol → anticancer drug, Zinc phosphide → rodenticide, Nitrocellulose → explosive. Silver bromide photography\nme use hota hai, artificial photosynthesis me nahi. [Q44–Q45]\n● Silicon carbide → artificial diamond/abrasive context; Carbon fibre → aircraft; CO → photosynthesis; dichlorodifluoromethane/Freon →\n₂\nrefrigerator. [Q46]\n● Iron → haemoglobin; Lead → storage battery; Silver compounds → photography; Copper → lightning conductor. Morphine → analgesic;\nSodium → kerosene storage; Boric acid → antiseptic; German silver → alloy. [Q47–Q48]\n● Skin cancer ↔ UV exposure, noise pollution ↔ decibel, global warming ↔ CO , ozone hole ↔ CFCs—ye standard environmental\n₂\nmatching hai. [Q49]\n6. Metals, Pigments, Solvents, Phosphorus, CNT & Desalination\n● Titanium ko “metal of future” kaha jata hai kyunki ye light, strong aur corrosion-resistant hai. Electric bulb filament Silver ka nahi, Tungsten\nka hota hai because tungsten ka melting point bahut high hai. [Q50–Q51]\n● Vermillion chemically Mercuric sulphide / Mercury(II) sulphide (HgS) hai. Traditional dry-cleaning me benzene, petrol/kerosene, alcohol\njaise solvents historically use hue; modern systems me perchloroethylene common raha hai. [Q52–Q54]\n● Red ink ke liye Eosin dye use hota hai. Source Q56 Sodium chromate ko red colour se associate karta hai (standard chemistry caveat\nniche trap me hai). Fireworks me Strontium salts bright crimson/red colour dete hain. [Q55–Q57]\n● Acetone → nail-polish remover; Carbon tetrachloride → historical fire-extinguisher use; H O → wound dressing/antiseptic context; liquid\n₂ ₂\nammonia → refrigerant. Accumulator/car battery me HCl nahi, H SO electrolyte hota hai.\n₂\n₄\n[Q58–Q59]\n● Safety matches me phosphorus especially Red phosphorus striking surface se linked hai; White phosphorus air aur darkness me\nchemiluminescence ki wajah se glow karta hai. [Q60–Q62]\n● Carbon nanotubes ki modern discovery/characterisation Sumio Iijima (1991) se linked hai. India me desalination plants Lakshadweep aur\nChennai dono jagah milte hain; first 1-lakh-LPD LTTD plant Kavaratti me commission hua. [Q63–Q65]\n● Alkaline soil reclamation ke liye Gypsum/Calcium sulphate use hota hai; “edaphic” term soil-related factors ke liye hai. Very-low-\ntemperature technology, jisme liquid O /H handle hote hain, Cryogenics kehlati hai.\n₂\n₂\n[Q66–Q68]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q56 Sodium Chromate colour\n\n▸Source key Sodium Chromate ko “Red” se associate karta hai, lekin sodium chromate crystals/solutions generally yellow hote hain.\n\n▸Isliye is fact ko source-key specific samjho; standard chemistry me chromate = yellow aur dichromate = orange yaad rakhna safer hai.\n7. Chemical Warfare, Smoke Screen, Agent Orange & Nuclear Basics\n● Mustard gas (sulphur mustard) WWI me chemical-warfare agent ke roop me use hua. Naam “gas” hai, lekin room temperature par ye\noily/viscous liquid ho sakta hai aur aerosol/mist ke form me disperse kiya gaya. [Q69–Q72]\n● Military smoke screens dense particulate clouds create karte hain; source me titanium oxide particles/TiCl moisture reaction ka context\n₄\ndiya hai, aur zinc chloride bhi smokescreen chemistry se linked hai. [Q73]\n● Agent Orange Vietnam War me US military ka defoliant/herbicide tha; severe health effects ka major concern dioxin (TCDD) contaminant\nse linked tha. [Q74–Q75]\n● Nucleus ka split hona nuclear fission hai; multiple light nuclei ka combine hokar heavier nucleus banana fusion hai. Isliye “breaking apart =\nfusion” statement incorrect hai. [Q76]\n8. Cells, Batteries, Microwave & Everyday Chemical Applications\n● Common zinc-carbon dry cell me NH Cl + ZnCl paste electrolyte hota hai; ye primary/non-rechargeable cell hai because reactions readily\n₄\n₂\nreversible nahi hoti. Stored chemical energy discharge par electrical energy me convert hoti hai. [Q77–Q81]\n● Lead-acid car battery ka electrolyte dilute H SO hai. Rechargeable Ni-Cd batteries me Nickel aur Cadmium electrode materials hote hain,\n₂\n₄\nKOH electrolyte context milta hai. [Q82–Q86]\n● Microwave oven me high-frequency microwaves generate karne ke liye Magnetron tube use hoti hai. [Q87]\n● Freon → refrigerant; Tetraethyl lead → anti-knocking agent; BHC → insecticide; Carbon tetrachloride → historical fire extinguisher.\nAspartame → artificial sweetener; Neoprene → synthetic rubber; Benadryl → antihistamine. [Q88–Q89]\n● Source matching ke according lipstick–lead, soft drink–brominated vegetable oil aur Chinese fast food–MSG tino pairs accepted hain.\nPotassium bromide → photography; potassium nitrate → gunpowder; potassium sulphate → fertilizer; monopotassium tartrate/cream of tartar\n→ bakery. [Q90–Q91]\n● Ozone depletion–skin cancer correct environmental pair hai. Household phenyl germicidal action phenol/cresol derivatives se linked hai.\n[Q92–Q93]\n● Source matching: Rutherford → atom bomb, Alfred Nobel → dynamite, Cartwright → powerloom, Graham Bell → telephone. Important\ndates: Technology Day 11 May, Photography Day 19 Aug, National Sports Day 29 Aug, Nagasaki Day 9 Aug. 2011 ko UN ne International\nYear of Chemistry designate kiya tha. [Q94–Q96]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q88 & Q94 source simplifications\n\n▸CCl ka fire-extinguisher use historical hai; toxicity ke karan modern fire safety me ye standard choice nahi hai.\n₄\n\n▸“Rutherford → Atom Bomb” source matching oversimplified hai. Rutherford nuclear physics pioneer the; atomic-bomb project ka “father” label\ncommonly J. Robert Oppenheimer se associated hai.\n9. Climate Agreements, Greenhouse Gases, Air Pollution & Hydrogen"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● UNFCCC ka focus greenhouse-gas emissions ko stabilize/mitigate karna hai, isliye CO reduction bhi naturally scope me aata hai. Alma-\n₂\nAta → primary healthcare aur Talanoa Dialogue → global climate action correct pairs hain; Hague Convention/Under2 Coalition ke source\npairs incorrect hain. [Q97–Q98]\n● Brazil ne long-standing ethanol–gasoline blending mandate adopt kiya. Air-pollutant question me HCN aur H S dono inorganic gaseous\n₂\npollutants ho sakte hain; H S ka major natural/environmental source decaying vegetation/animal matter aur anaerobic decomposition hai.\n₂\n[Q99–Q101]\n● CO , CH aur N O greenhouse gases hain. Source commission estimate me relative contribution order CO > CH > N O > CFCs diya\n₂\n₄\n₂\n₂\n₄\n₂\ngaya hai. Atmospheric water vapour altitude ke saath decrease karta hai aur poles par maximum nahi, warm humid tropics me zyada hota hai.\n[Q102–Q104]\n● Nuclear/thermal power plants ke heated cooling-water discharge se thermal pollution ho sakta hai. “Green Muffler” dense vegetation barrier\nse noise pollution reduce karne ki technique hai. [Q105–Q106]\n● Urban magnetic pollution nanoparticles vehicle brakes, engines/tailpipe combustion aur power plants se aa sakte hain. Petrol/diesel ki\nincomplete combustion Carbon monoxide aur soot produce karti hai. [Q107–Q108]\n● Metropolitan air me CO, NOₓ, SO , ozone, lead aur particulate matter jaise multiple pollutants present hote hain; isi wajah se source ne\n₂\nQ109 ko disputed maana. PM ek air pollutant hai. [Q109–Q110]\n● Source-era RSPM question me <5 µm accepted answer hai, jabki modern monitoring PM /PM . categories extensively use karti hai.\n₁₀\n₂ ₅\nNAMP regular monitoring me SO , NO , PM aur PM . major parameters hain.\n₂\n₂\n₁₀\n₂ ₅\n[Q111–Q112]\n● Steam methane reforming se, jab CO capture na ho, “Grey Hydrogen” banta hai. Green Hydrogen fertilizer plants, oil refineries aur steel\n₂\nplants tino ko decarbonize karne me role play kar sakta hai; direct combustion, natural-gas blending aur fuel-cell vehicles tino use-cases\npossible hain. [Q113–Q115]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q100, Q103 & Q109\n\n▸Q100 me HCN aur H S dono technically inorganic gaseous pollutants hain, isliye source multiple-correct maanta hai.\n₂\n\n▸Q103 ka greenhouse-gas contribution order commission-specific estimate hai; “global warming potential” aur “total contribution” ko mix mat karo.\n\n▸Q109 me metropolitan pollution ke multiple options valid the, isliye source answer * (disputed) hai.\n10. Smog, Water Pollution, Waste Treatment & Mercury\n● Classical/industrial smog me nitrogen aur sulphur oxides, smoke/particulates important hote hain. Photochemical smog sunlight + NOₓ +\nhydrocarbons se banta hai aur Ozone iska key secondary pollutant hai. [Q116–Q117]\n● Eutrophication water-body ka nutrient enrichment hai, especially nitrogenous nutrients/nitrates aur phosphates/orthophosphates se. Algal\nbloom ke decomposition se dissolved oxygen deplete hota hai. [Q118–Q119]\n● BOD aquatic pollution ka standard indicator hai: organic matter decompose karne me microorganisms jitna oxygen consume karte hain,\nBOD utna high; high BOD generally higher organic pollution ko show karta hai. [Q120]\n● Industrial/sewage effluents water ke pH, temperature aur chemical composition jaise physico-chemical characteristics change karte hain.\nMembrane Bioreactor (MBR) wastewater-treatment technology hai jo biological treatment + membrane separation combine karta hai. [Q121–\nQ122]\n● Pyrolysis aur plasma gasification waste-to-energy thermal technologies hain jo waste ko high temperature par syngas/bio-oil jaise useful\nproducts me convert kar sakte hain. [Q123]\n● Mercury pollution ke sources me historical mercurial pesticides, dental amalgam, fluorescent lamps aur coal-based thermal power plants\nsab include ho sakte hain. [Q124]\n Source-question mapping preserved: Q1–Q124\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0349","t":"01 Measurement and Units","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measurement & Units Full Mind Map\n📐 MEASUREMENT & UNITS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Fundamental Physical Quantities — SI Base Concept\n2. Force, Work, Power & Energy — Core Units\n3. Frequency, Hertz & GHz — Cycles and CPU Speed\n4. Electrical Units — Ampere, Volt, Watt & Resistivity\n5. Magnetic Field — Tesla and Equivalent Units\n6. Radioactivity — Becquerel vs Curie\n7. Astronomical Distance — Light-Year & Parsec\n8. Length Conversions — nm, Micron, Angstrom, Fermi & km\n9. Match-the-Following — Common Quantity–Unit Pairs\n10. Heat, Temperature & Power — Do Not Mix Them\n11. Pressure Units — Pascal, Bar, atm, Torr & kgf/cm²\n12. Dimensionless Quantities — Strain & Mach\n13. Mass Prefix — Picogram\n14. Oil Measurement — Barrel Conversion\n15. Special Units — Cusec, Byte, Richter, Bar & NTU\n16. Solar Constant — Approximate Exam Value\n17. Dobson Unit — Ozone Layer Thickness / Concentration\n1. Fundamental Physical Quantities — SI Base Concept\n● Physics mein 7 fundamental physical quantities hain — length, mass, time, electric current,\ntemperature, luminous intensity aur amount of substance. Inhi ko base/fundamental units mein measure\nkiya jata hai. [Q1]\n● Given options mein electric current fundamental quantity hai; force, velocity aur work derived quantities\nhain. [Q1]\n2. Force, Work, Power & Energy — Core Units\n● Power = work/time; SI unit watt (W) hai aur 1 W = 1 J/s. Electric power ki unit bhi watt hi hoti hai. [Q2, Q3]\n● Force motion ko change karne wali interaction hai; F = ma aur SI unit newton (N) = kg·m/s². [Q4]\n● Work = force × displacement in force direction; work scalar quantity hai. SI unit joule (J) = N·m hai; joule\nenergy ki bhi unit hai. [Q5]\n● Power-plant context mein megawatt power ko show karta hai: 1 MW = 10⁶ W. Horsepower bhi power ki\nunit hai: 1 hp ≈ 746 W. [Q24, Q29]\n● Standard matching: acceleration → m/s², force → newton, work done → joule, impulse → newton-\nsecond (N·s). [Q25]\n3. Frequency, Hertz & GHz — Cycles and CPU Speed\n● Frequency ki SI derived unit hertz (Hz) hai; 1 Hz = 1 cycle per second. Isliye “what is measured in\nhertz?” ka answer frequency hai. [Q6, Q7]\n● 1 GHz = 10⁹ Hz. Computer mein GHz mainly CPU clock/processing speed ko indicate karta hai — CPU\nper second kitne cycles execute karta hai. [Q8]\n4. Electrical Units — Ampere, Volt, Watt & Resistivity\n● Electrical resistivity material ka intrinsic property hai jo current flow ke opposition ko quantify karta hai; ρ\n= RA/l aur SI unit ohm-metre (Ω·m) hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Ohm (Ω) resistance ki unit hai, jabki ohm-metre (Ω·m) resistivity ki unit hai — dono ko interchange nahi\nkarna chahiye. [Q9, Q10]\n● Ampere electric current ki SI unit hai. Source ke according 1 A current roughly 6.25 × 10¹⁸ electrons per\nsecond ke charge flow ke equivalent hai. [Q23]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measurement & Units Full Mind Map\n● Electric-unit map yaad rakhein: joule → work, ampere → current, watt → power, volt → electric\npotential. [Q28]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Resistance vs Resistivity — Q9–Q10\n\n▸Q9 disputed hai kyunki correct SI unit resistivity ke liye Ω·m hai, lekin option list mein sirf ohm diya gaya tha;\nisliye source ne answer (*) mark kiya. [Q9]\n\n▸Exam memory: Resistance → Ω; Resistivity → Ω·m. [Q9, Q10]\n5. Magnetic Field — Tesla and Equivalent Units\n● Magnetic flux density / magnetic B-field ki SI unit tesla (T) hai. Magnetic field strength H ki unit A/m hoti\nhai. [Q11]\n● 1 tesla = 1 weber/m² = 1 newton/(ampere·metre). Unit Nikola Tesla ke naam par hai. [Q12]\n6. Radioactivity — Becquerel vs Curie\n● Radioactive activity ki SI unit becquerel (Bq) hai; 1 Bq ka meaning 1 decay per second hai. Iska naam\nHenri Becquerel ke naam par hai. [Q13]\n● Curie (Ci) radioactivity ki old/non-SI unit hai; isi wajah se “Activity of radioactive substance — Curie” SI-\nunit matching mein incorrect pair hai. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Becquerel vs Curie — Q13\n\n▸SI radioactivity → Becquerel (Bq); Curie (Ci) non-SI/older unit hai. [Q13]\n7. Astronomical Distance — Light-Year & Parsec\n● Light-year time ki unit nahi, astronomical distance ki unit hai — light vacuum mein one year mein jitna\ndistance travel karti hai. 1 ly ≈ 9.46 × 10¹⁵ m. [Q14, Q15, Q16]\n● Astronomical distances ko light-year mein express karne ka key reason light ki vacuum speed ka\nconstant hona hai. [Q17]\n● Parsec bhi astronomical distance ki unit hai: 1 pc ≈ 3.0857 × 10¹⁶ m ≈ 3.26 light-years; source option\nmein ≈ 3.25 ly diya gaya. [Q18, Q19]\n● “Light-year — unit of measuring time” incorrect matching hai; correct relation distance se hai. [Q30]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Light-Year ≠ Time — Q14–Q19, Q30\n\n▸Naam mein “year” hone ke bawajood light-year DISTANCE ki unit hai. [Q14, Q15, Q16, Q30]\n\n▸Parsec bhi distance ki unit hai; 1 parsec ≈ 3.26 light-years. [Q18, Q19]\n8. Length Conversions — nm, Micron, Angstrom, Fermi & km\n● Centimetre to inch conversion ke liye source relation: 1 cm ≈ 0.39 inch; centimetre value ko 0.39 se\nmultiply karke approximate inches milte hain. [Q20]\n● 1 nm = 10 ⁹ m = 10 ⁷ cm. Source conversion ke hisab se 6 ft ≈ 1.83 m ≈ 183 × 10⁷ nm.\n⁻\n⁻\n[Q21, Q22]\n● Angstrom (Å) microscopic length/wavelength ke liye use hota hai: 1 Å = 10 ¹⁰ m = 0.1 nm.\n⁻\n[Q31]\n● 1 micron (µm) = 10 ⁶ m = 10 ³ mm = 10 ⁴ cm.\n⁻\n⁻\n⁻\n[Q34, Q35]\n● Basic conversion: 1 km = 1000 m. [Q39]\n● Given units mein size order: micron 10 ⁶ m > nanometre 10 ⁹ m > angstrom 10 ¹⁰ m > fermi/femtometre\n⁻\n⁻\n⁻\n10 ¹⁵ m; smallest = fermi.\n⁻\n[Q49]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measurement & Units Full Mind Map\n9. Match-the-Following — Common Quantity–Unit Pairs\n● Pressure–Dyne incorrect SI matching hai: pressure/stress ki SI unit pascal (Pa) hoti hai; dyne CGS\nsystem ki force unit hai. [Q26]\n● Watt → power; knot → ship speed; nautical mile → sea/navigation distance; calorie → heat/energy.\n[Q27]\n● High speed → Mach; wavelength → angstrom; pressure → pascal; energy → joule. [Q32]\n● Analogy: Joule : Energy :: Pascal : Pressure. 1 Pa = 1 N/m². [Q33]\n10. Heat, Temperature & Power — Do Not Mix Them\n● Celsius/Centigrade temperature ka scale/unit hai, heat ki unit nahi. Heat-energy ke common units\ncalorie, kilocalorie, joule/kilojoule aur erg hain. [Q36, Q38]\n● Watt heat ki unit nahi — watt power ki unit hai. Calorie, kilocalorie aur kilojoule heat/energy units hain.\n[Q37]\n● Source Q36 context: nautical mile sea distance ke liye; 1 nautical mile ≈ 1.852 km. Horsepower power ki\nunit hai; 1 hp ≈ 746 W. [Q36]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Heat vs Temperature vs Power — Q36–Q38\n\n▸Celsius/Centigrade → temperature; Watt → power; Calorie/Joule/Kilojoule/Erg → heat-energy. [Q36, Q37, Q38]\n11. Pressure Units — Pascal, Bar, atm, Torr & kgf/cm²\n● Pascal (Pa) pressure aur stress ki SI unit hai; 1 Pa = 1 N/m². Pressure ka dimensional SI form\nkg·m ¹·s ² hota hai.\n⁻\n⁻\n[Q41, Q42]\n● bar, pascal (Pa), torr aur atmosphere (atm) — sab pressure units hain. 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa aur 1 atm =\n101,325 Pa. [Q44, Q45]\n● “kg/cm²” technically proper pressure notation nahi; intended form kgf/cm² hota hai. 1 kgf/cm² ≈ 98,066.5\nPa. [Q43]\n● Approximate exam conversion: 1 kgf/cm² ≈ 1.0 bar; more precisely about 0.98 bar. [Q46]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Pressure Notation & Units — Q43–Q46\n\n▸SI pressure → Pascal, not bar. Bar metric but non-SI unit hai. [Q41, Q42, Q45]\n\n▸kg/cm² ko pressure ke liye casually likha jata hai, lekin force notation kgf/cm² technically correct hai. [Q43, Q46]\n12. Dimensionless Quantities — Strain & Mach\n● Strain = change in dimension / original dimension. Ratio hone ki wajah se strain dimensionless hai aur\niski koi unit nahi hoti. [Q47]\n● Mach number bhi dimensionless ratio hai: object speed / local speed of sound; Mach 1 = speed of\nsound. [Q32]\n13. Mass Prefix — Picogram\n● Picogram (pg) bahut chhoti mass unit hai: 1 pg = 10 ¹² gram. Comparison: 1 mg = 10 ³ g; microgram =\n⁻\n⁻\n10 ⁶ g; femtogram = 10 ¹⁵ g.\n⁻\n⁻\n[Q40]\n14. Oil Measurement — Barrel Conversion\n● Oil-volume convention: 1 barrel ≈ 158.9873 litre ≈ 159 litre = 0.158987 m³ = 42 U.S. gallons. [Q48]\n15. Special Units — Cusec, Byte, Richter, Bar & NTU\n● Mixed-unit matching: Cusec → rate of flow; Byte → computer/digital information; Richter → earthquake\nmagnitude/intensity; Bar → pressure. [Q50]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measurement & Units Full Mind Map\n● Cusec = cubic foot per second; water-flow rate ke liye use hota hai. 1 cusec ≈ 28.317 litres/second. [Q50,\nQ51]\n● NTU = Nephelometric Turbidity Unit; water ki turbidity/gandlapan ko measure karta hai. Suspended\nsolids badhenge to turbidity value bhi badhegi. [Q52]\n16. Solar Constant — Approximate Exam Value\n● Solar constant/TSI roughly Sun se 1 astronomical unit distance par per unit area received solar power\nko represent karta hai. [Q53]\n● Source explanation modern measurement ≈ 1361 W/m² batati hai; given options mein closest exam\nanswer 1.4 kW/m² (≈ 1400 W/m²) tha. [Q53]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Solar Constant — Exact vs Exam Approximation — Q53\n\n▸Source question ke options mein 1.4 kW/m² closest answer hai; explanation ~1361 W/m² ka measured value\ndeti hai. [Q53]\n17. Dobson Unit — Ozone Layer Thickness / Concentration\n● Ozone layer thickness/concentration Dobson Unit (DU) mein express ki jati hai. 1 DU = STP par 0.01\nmm ozone thickness. [Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]\n● 1 DU ≈ 2.687 × 10²⁰ ozone molecules per square metre. Unit ka naam atmospheric-ozone scientist\nG.M.B. Dobson ke naam par hai. [Q54, Q57]\n● Exam wording “ozone thickness”, “ozone layer thickness” aur “ozone concentration” — tino contexts\nmein Dobson unit ko identify karna hai. [Q54, Q55, Q56, Q57]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0350","t":"02 Measuring Instruments and Scales","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measuring Instruments & Scales Full Mind Map\n📏 MEASURING INSTRUMENTS & SCALES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. SONAR & Sound Instruments — Underwater Detection and Sound Intensity\n2. Wind & Survey Instruments — Anemometer and Tacheometer\n3. Electrical Measuring Instruments — Ammeter, Voltmeter, Potentiometer & Galvanometer\n4. High Temperature & Solar Radiation — Pyrometer and Pyrheliometer\n5. Pressure & Atmospheric Instruments — Manometer, Barometer & Barograph\n6. Vehicle Distance & Precision Time — Odometer, Speedometer & Chronometer\n7. Density of Milk & Liquids — Lactometer, Butyrometer & Hydrometer\n8. Humidity & Atmospheric Moisture — Hygrometer and Related Devices\n9. Special Scales & Temperature Sensors — Ringelmann Scale and Thermoresistor\n10. Medical, Light & Purity Instruments — EEG, Sphygmomanometer, Luxmeter & Polygraph\n11. RADAR — Radio Detection and Ranging\n12. Earthquake Measurement — Richter, Mercalli, Seismograph & Seismometer\n13. Depth, Altitude & Surveying — Fathometer, Altimeter & Theodolite\n14. Quick Match-the-Following Instrument Map\n15. Phonometer — Disputed Source Question\n16. Accelerometer — Crash, Free-Fall and Smartphone Tilt Detection\n1. SONAR & Sound Instruments — Underwater Detection and Sound Intensity\n● SONAR ka full form Sound Navigation and Ranging hai. Ocean mein submerged objects, submarines\naur icebergs locate karne ke liye iska use hota hai. [Q1]\n● SONAR ka practical use mainly navigators/naval navigation mein hota hai. [Q2]\n● SONAR ultrasonic waves use karta hai: pulse water mein bheji jati hai, target se reflect hokar echo\nreturn karta hai; time delay se location/depth estimate hoti hai. [Q3]\n● Audiometer sound ki intensity/hearing level measure karta hai. Audiophone ek hearing-aid type device\nhai; chronometer highly accurate timepiece hota hai. [Q4]\n2. Wind & Survey Instruments — Anemometer and Tacheometer\n● Anemometer wind ki speed/velocity aur wind pressure/force ko measure karta hai. [Q5, Q6, Q7]\n● Correct instrument map: Anemometer → wind speed; Ammeter → electric current; Pyrometer → high\ntemperature. [Q8]\n● Tacheometer ek rapid-surveying instrument/theodolite type device hai jo distance aur related survey\nmeasurements ke liye use hota hai; pressure difference measure nahi karta. [Q8]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Tacheometer ≠ Pressure Difference — Q8\n\n▸Tacheometer rapid surveying/distance measurement ke liye hota hai; pressure difference ke saath pair\nincorrect hai. [Q8]\n\n▸Pressure difference ke liye manometer/differential manometer type instruments use kiye jate hain. [Q8]\n3. Electrical Measuring Instruments — Ammeter, Voltmeter, Potentiometer &\nGalvanometer\n● Ammeter circuit mein electric current measure karta hai; current ki SI unit ampere (A) hai. [Q9]\n● Voltmeter → potential difference; Potentiometer → EMF/potential comparison; Galvanometer → very\nsmall electric current/detection. [Q10]\n● Galvanometer electric resistance measure karne ka standard instrument nahi hai; resistance ke liye\nohmmeter use hota hai. [Q10]\n● Ammeter electric power measure nahi karta. Electric power wattmeter se measure ki jati hai. [Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measuring Instruments & Scales Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Ammeter, Galvanometer & Power — Q9–Q10, Q19\n\n▸Ammeter → current; Galvanometer → small current; resistance → ohmmeter. Inhe interchange mat karein.\n[Q9, Q10]\n\n▸Electric power → wattmeter, not ammeter. [Q19]\n4. High Temperature & Solar Radiation — Pyrometer and Pyrheliometer\n● Pyrometer very high temperature measure karne wala radiation/remote-sensing thermometer hai;\nfurnaces ya inaccessible hot surfaces ke liye useful hota hai. [Q11, Q12, Q13, Q15]\n● Pyrometer ka principle thermal radiation se linked hai; black-body radiation ke context mein Stefan–\nBoltzmann relation E T⁴ relevant hai.\n∝\n[Q11]\n● Around 2000°C jaise very high temperature ke liye total radiation pyrometer suitable hota hai. [Q14]\n● Pyrheliometer direct solar radiation measure karta hai; pyranometer bhi solar irradiance measurement\nmein use hota hai. [Q16]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Pyrometer Range — Q11–Q15\n\n▸Pyrometer high/very-high temperature ke liye hai; source repeatedly 1500°C se above temperature ke liye\nPyrometer answer deta hai. [Q11, Q12, Q15]\n\n▸2000°C context mein Total Radiation Pyrometer choose karna hai. [Q14]\n5. Pressure & Atmospheric Instruments — Manometer, Barometer & Barograph\n● Manometer liquid/gas pressure measure karta hai, commonly liquid-column pressure measurement\nprinciple par. [Q17, Q49]\n● Barometer atmospheric pressure measure karta hai. Simple barometer traditionally mercury column use\nkarta hai. [Q21, Q22]\n● Barograph atmospheric pressure ko continuously record karta hai. [Q48]\n● Useful matching: Ammeter → electric current; Hygrometer → relative humidity; Spring balance →\nweight; Barometer → atmospheric pressure. [Q18]\n6. Vehicle Distance & Precision Time — Odometer, Speedometer &\nChronometer\n● Odometer vehicle dwara travelled distance measure karta hai; Speedometer vehicle ki instantaneous\nspeed batata hai. [Q20]\n● Chronometer exceptionally accurate timepiece hai, historically maritime navigation mein longitude\ndetermination ke liye important raha hai. [Q20]\n7. Density of Milk & Liquids — Lactometer, Butyrometer & Hydrometer\n● Lactometer milk ki density/specific gravity measure karta hai. [Q23, Q24]\n● Butyrometer milk/milk products ka fat content measure karta hai, jabki Hydrometer liquids ki relative\ndensity/specific gravity measure karta hai. [Q23, Q25]\n8. Humidity & Atmospheric Moisture — Hygrometer and Related Devices\n● Hygrometer atmosphere/air ki humidity ya relative humidity measure karta hai. [Q25, Q26, Q27, Q28, Q29]\n● Spectrometer electromagnetic spectrum/light properties analyze karta hai; Eudiometer gas-mixture\nvolume change measure karta hai. [Q26]\n● Hypsometer height/altitude estimation ke liye use ho sakta hai; Thermostat kisi system ka temperature\ndesired set-point ke around regulate karta hai. [Q29]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measuring Instruments & Scales Full Mind Map\n9. Special Scales & Temperature Sensors — Ringelmann Scale and\nThermoresistor\n● Ringelmann Scale smoke ki density/opacity ko grade karne ke liye use hota hai; smoke-abatement work\nmein iska classic use hai. [Q30]\n● Thermoresistor/thermistor electronic temperature sensing mein use hota hai; temperature change ke\nsaath electrical resistance change hoti hai. [Q31]\n10. Medical, Light & Purity Instruments — EEG, Sphygmomanometer, Luxmeter\n& Polygraph\n● EEG (Electroencephalogram) scalp electrodes ke through brain ki electrical activity monitor/record karta\nhai. [Q32]\n● Stethoscope → heart/body sounds; Sphygmomanometer → blood pressure; Caratometer → gold purity;\nLuxmeter → light intensity/illuminance. [Q33, Q34, Q35]\n● Polygraph ya lie detector blood pressure, pulse, respiration aur skin conductivity jaise physiological\nindices record karta hai. [Q51]\n● Kymograph pressure/tension variations record kar sakta hai; Gyroscope orientation/rotation sensing\ndevice hai; Pyrometer high surface temperature measure karta hai. [Q51]\n11. RADAR — Radio Detection and Ranging\n● RADAR ka full form Radio Detection and Ranging hai aur ye radio waves par based hota hai. [Q36]\n● RADAR objects ki presence/location ke saath range, angle aur velocity determine kar sakta hai; aircraft,\nships, missiles, weather formations etc. detect kiye ja sakte hain. [Q36]\n12. Earthquake Measurement — Richter, Mercalli, Seismograph & Seismometer\n● Exam-source convention mein Richter scale ko earthquake ki intensity/magnitude se associate kiya\ngaya hai; scale seismic-wave amplitude aur released-energy related magnitude ko represent karta hai.\n[Q37, Q38, Q39]\n● Richter scale humidity measure nahi karta; humidity ke liye Hygrometer hota hai. [Q40]\n● Seismograph earthquake-generated seismic waves ko detect/record karta hai; source questions mein\nearthquake measurement/recording ke liye isi ko answer diya gaya hai. [Q41, Q42, Q43, Q44]\n● Seismometer seismic waves measure karta hai; “surface curvature” ke saath iska matching incorrect\nhai. [Q49]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Richter Magnitude vs Mercalli Intensity — Q37–Q40\n\n▸Scientific distinction: Richter-type scales earthquake MAGNITUDE/energy-seismic amplitude se related hain;\nMercalli scale observed INTENSITY/damage effects describe karta hai. [Q37, Q39]\n\n▸Lekin source/commission ke kuch questions “intensity” wording ke saath Richter ko expected answer dete\nhain; exam mein source convention ko recognize karein. [Q37, Q38]\n13. Depth, Altitude & Surveying — Fathometer, Altimeter & Theodolite\n● Altimeter kisi fixed reference level ke above altitude/height measure karta hai. [Q45, Q46]\n● Fathometer ultrasonic waves ke through sea/water depth ya submerged object ki depth determine karta\nhai. [Q46, Q47]\n● Theodolite horizontal plane (azimuth) aur vertical plane (elevation) mein angular distances/angles\nmeasure karta hai. [Q52]\n14. Quick Match-the-Following Instrument Map\n● Core matching: Earthquake → Seismograph; Height → Altimeter; Electric current → Ammeter; Electrical\nresistance ki unit → Ohm. [Q45]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Measuring Instruments & Scales Full Mind Map\n● Core matching: Fathometer → depth of sea; Barometer → atmospheric pressure; Hygrometer →\natmospheric humidity; Altimeter → height. [Q46]\n● Core matching: Anemometer → wind velocity; Seismograph → earthquake; Barograph → atmospheric\npressure; Hygrometer → humidity. [Q48]\n● Other correct pairs: Manometer → pressure; Carburetor → air-fuel mixing in IC engine; Cardiograph →\nheart movement/recording. [Q49]\n15. Phonometer — Disputed Source Question\n● Phonometer human voice ki force/strength test karne se associated instrument hai; Photometer light\nintensity measure karta hai. [Q50]\n● Source question ke diye options mein koi option fully correct nahi tha; official answer “* / no correct\noption” marked hai. [Q50]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Phonometer Question Is Disputed — Q50\n\n▸Phonometer → force/strength of human voice; Photometer → light intensity. Dono alag instruments hain.\n[Q50]\n\n▸Given options mein correct phonometer function absent tha, isliye official answer “*”/no correct option hai.\n[Q50]\n16. Accelerometer — Crash, Free-Fall and Smartphone Tilt Detection\n● Accelerometer acceleration/vibration of motion measure karta hai; MEMS accelerometers modern\nelectronic devices mein common hain. [Q53]\n● Car crash mein rapid deceleration detect karke airbag deployment trigger karna accelerometer\napplication hai. [Q53]\n● Laptop free-fall detection aur smartphone portrait/landscape tilt sensing bhi accelerometer se hota hai;\nsource ke tino actions correct hain. [Q53]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0351","t":"03 Mechanics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mechanics Full Mind Map\n⚙️ MECHANICS — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Simple Machines — Same Work with Less Applied Force\n2. Sensitive Balance & Inhaled Air — Why Reading Increases\n3. Scalar vs Vector Quantities — Speed, Velocity, Force, Pressure & More\n4. Momentum, Mass & Force — p = mv and F = ma\n5. Cube Geometry Quick Numerical — Volume = Surface Area\n6. Energy — Conservation, Sources, Wind Power & Energy Conversion\n7. Speed — Galileo and the Basic Relation v = d/t\n8. Newton’s First Law & Inertia — Train and Turning-Bus Examples\n9. Statics & Conservation of Momentum — Rest, Whistling and Boat Recoil\n10. Friction — Ice, Loaded Cart, Ball Bearings and Rolling Ball\n11. Newton’s Second & Third Laws — Goalkeeper and Action–Reaction\n12. Circular Motion & Rotating Frames — Centripetal and Coriolis Forces\n13. de Broglie & Work–Energy Numericals — Wavelength and Kinetic Energy\n14. Vehicle Dynamics in Accelerating Frames — Car Wheels and Oil Tanker\n15. Average Speed & Acceleration Equations — Core Kinematics Formulae\n16. Centrifugation — Washing Machine and Cream Separation\n1. Simple Machines — Same Work with Less Applied Force\n● Simple machine ka purpose work ko “kam” karna nahi, balki same amount of work ko comparatively\nkam applied force / convenient force-direction ke saath karna hota hai. Pulley, lever, wheel-and-axle aur\nscrew common examples hain. [Q1]\n2. Sensitive Balance & Inhaled Air — Why Reading Increases\n● Sensitive balance par khada vyakti deep breath leta hai to inhaled air uske system ke mass mein\ntemporarily add hoti hai, isliye balance reading thodi badh sakti hai. [Q2]\n● Source explanation ke hisaab se air density roughly 1.225 g/L li gayi hai; several litres ki deep inhalation\nse few grams ka mass difference possible hai. [Q2]\n3. Scalar vs Vector Quantities — Speed, Velocity, Force, Pressure & More\n● Scalar quantity mein sirf magnitude hota hai; vector quantity mein magnitude ke saath direction bhi hoti\nhai. [Q3, Q7]\n● Displacement, velocity, acceleration, momentum, force aur torque vector examples hain. [Q3, Q4, Q5, Q7]\n● Speed, distance, time, volume, pressure, energy, work aur density scalar examples hain. [Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6,\nQ7]\n● Pressure scalar hai, although pressure se associated force direction-specific ho sakta hai. Pressure =\nForce / Area. [Q6]\n4. Momentum, Mass & Force — p = mv and F = ma\n● Linear momentum p = m × v. Isliye momentum / velocity = mass. [Q8]\n● Newton’s second-law form mein force F = m × a; force mass aur acceleration ka product hai. [Q9]\n● Non-contact forces bina direct physical contact ke act karte hain: gravitational, magnetic aur electric\nforces. Friction aur applied/impact force contact forces hain. [Q10]\n5. Cube Geometry Quick Numerical — Volume = Surface Area\n● Cube ke liye volume = l³ aur total surface area = 6l². Agar numerical values equal hon: l³ = 6l²\n l = 6\n⇒\nunits. [Q11]\n6. Energy — Conservation, Sources, Wind Power & Energy Conversion\n● Law of Conservation of Energy: energy na create ki ja sakti hai, na destroy; sirf ek form se doosri form\nmein transform/transfer hoti hai. [Q12]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mechanics Full Mind Map\n● Wind energy moving air ki kinetic energy hai. Wind turbine is kinetic energy ko mechanical energy aur\ngenerator usse electrical energy mein convert karta hai. [Q14, Q15]\n● Friction ke against motion mein mechanical/kinetic energy ka ek part heat mein convert hota hai. [Q16]\n● Energy-conversion matching: Light → Electric = Solar cell; Electric → Sound = Loudspeaker; Mass →\nHeat/Energy = Nuclear reactor; Chemical → Heat & Light = fuel combustion. [Q17]\n● Most biological/wind sources ultimately solar origin se linked hain, jabki nuclear aur geothermal energy\ndirect solar-derived sources nahi hain. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q13 — Nuclear vs Geothermal Source Ambiguity\n\n▸Question poochta hai “NOT ultimately derived from Sun”. Scientifically nuclear energy aur geothermal energy\ndono direct solar-derived nahi hain. [Q13]\n\n▸HTML options mein A = Nuclear, B = Geothermal hai; explanation dono ko correct bolti hai, lekin stored key A\nmarked hai. Exam source ko exactly recognize karein. [Q13]\n7. Speed — Galileo and the Basic Relation v = d/t\n● Exam-source convention Galileo Galilei ko speed ko distance travelled per unit time ke form mein\nsystematically define/measure karne se associate karta hai. [Q18]\n● Basic relation: speed v = distance d / time t. [Q18]\n8. Newton’s First Law & Inertia — Train and Turning-Bus Examples\n● Newton’s First Law ko Law of Inertia kaha jata hai: body rest ya uniform straight-line motion ki state\nmaintain karti hai jab tak unbalanced external force act na kare. [Q19]\n● Train suddenly start kare to lower body train ke saath move karti hai, upper body inertia of rest ke karan\npeeche rehne ki tendency rakhti hai; passenger backward lean karta hai. [Q20]\n● Bus suddenly right turn le to passenger ka upper body inertia of direction ke karan left side ki taraf\nlean/throw hota dikhta hai. [Q21]\n9. Statics & Conservation of Momentum — Rest, Whistling and Boat Recoil\n● Statics mechanics ki branch hai jo bodies in equilibrium/rest ko study karti hai. [Q22]\n● Frictionless surface par man air ko expel karke recoil/action–reaction se khud ko propel kar sakta hai;\nsource assertion–reason key dono statements ko true but R ko not-correct-explanation mark karti hai.\n[Q23]\n● Boat-man system initially rest mein ho to total momentum zero hota hai. Man 5 m/s se jump kare aur\nboat 0.5 m/s opposite move kare: M×5 = N×0.5\n boat mass = 10 × man mass.\n⇒\n[Q30]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q23 — Assertion–Reason Interpretation\n\n▸Source key: A and R both true, but R is not the correct explanation of A. [Q23]\n\n▸Conceptually recoil ko Newton’s third law aur momentum conservation dono viewpoints se discuss kiya ja\nsakta hai; exam mein source key follow karna zaroori hai. [Q23]\n10. Friction — Ice, Loaded Cart, Ball Bearings and Rolling Ball\n● Ice par road ke comparison mein friction kam hota hai, isliye walking difficult hoti hai; forward push ke\nliye sufficient static friction chahiye. [Q24]\n● Loaded cart ko start karna harder hota hai because limiting/static friction generally kinetic friction se\ngreater hota hai; once moving, required force kam ho jata hai. [Q25]\n● Ball bearings wheel/axle ke beech sliding contact ko rolling contact mein convert karke friction reduce\nkarte hain; isliye cycles/cars mein use hote hain. [Q34, Q35]\n● Level ground par rolling cricket ball eventually frictional/resistive forces ke karan slow hokar stop hoti\nhai; ideal no-friction case mein motion continue karega. [Q39]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Mechanics Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q35 — Ball Bearing Friction Wording\n\n▸Standard physics wording: ball bearings SLIDING friction ko ROLLING friction mein convert/reduce karte\nhain. [Q34, Q35]\n\n▸Source Q35 mein “static friction → rolling friction” wording diya hai aur rolling friction answer marked hai;\nwording ko exam trap ke roop mein yaad rakhein. [Q35]\n11. Newton’s Second & Third Laws — Goalkeeper and Action–Reaction\n● Goalkeeper fast ball catch karte waqt hands backward pull karta hai, stopping time Δt badhta hai; same\nmomentum change ke liye average force F = Δp/Δt kam ho jata hai. [Q26]\n● Newton’s Third Law: every action ke liye equal magnitude ka opposite-direction reaction force hota hai;\npair different interacting bodies par act karta hai. [Q27]\n12. Circular Motion & Rotating Frames — Centripetal and Coriolis Forces\n● Circular motion ke liye centre ki taraf net force required hota hai, jise centripetal force kehte hain. [Q28]\n● Coriolis force rotating reference frame ka apparent/inertial force hai. Earth rotation ke karan moving\nbodies Northern Hemisphere mein right aur Southern Hemisphere mein left deflect karti hain. [Q29]\n● High-speed sharp turn par insufficient banking/friction ki condition mein vehicle outward skid kar sakta\nhai aur outer wheels ke about overturn tendency develop ho sakti hai. [Q38]\n13. de Broglie & Work–Energy Numericals — Wavelength and Kinetic Energy\n● de Broglie relation λ = h/p = h/(mv). For m = 0.12 kg, v = 20 m/s, source calculation λ ≈ 2.76 × 10 ³⁴ m\n⁻\ndeta hai. [Q31]\n● Work–Energy theorem: stopping work F×s = initial kinetic energy. Equal KE aur equal stopping force ho\nto truck, car aur motorcycle equal stopping distance cover karenge: X = Y = Z. [Q32]\n● Same mass ke liye KE v². Agar K :K = 4:9, to v :v = √4:√9 = 2:3.\n∝\n₁\n₂\n₁ ₂\n[Q33]\n14. Vehicle Dynamics in Accelerating Frames — Car Wheels and Oil Tanker\n● Accelerating car mein inertia/pseudo-force ke effect se load front se rear ki taraf transfer hota hai;\nacceleration ke during front-wheel normal reaction R se kam ho sakti hai. [Q36]\n● Forward uniformly accelerating oil tanker mein fluid par backward pseudo-force act karta hai; oil rear\nside par higher level aur front par lower level banata hai, free surface inclined hoti hai. [Q37]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q36 — Front-Wheel Reaction Depends on Acceleration\n\n▸If car accelerates, backward inertial effect causes rearward load transfer, so front-wheel reaction decreases\nbelow R. [Q36]\n\n▸If car simply moves at constant velocity on a level road, no longitudinal load transfer occurs and reaction can\nremain R. Source explanation acceleration interpretation use karti hai. [Q36]\n15. Average Speed & Acceleration Equations — Core Kinematics Formulae\n● Equal-distance halves ko v aur v speeds se cover karne par average speed arithmetic mean nahi hoti:\n₁\n₂\nv_avg = 2v v /(v +v ).\n₁ ₂\n₁\n₂\n[Q40]\n● First equation of motion v = u + at se acceleration a = (v − u)/t. [Q41]\n16. Centrifugation — Washing Machine and Cream Separation\n● Washing machine spin cycle centrifugation principle par kaam karta hai; rotation se water/clothes\nseparation facilitate hoti hai. [Q42]\n● Milk/cream separation exam context mein centrifugal-force based separation se associate ki jati hai:\ndenser phase outward aur less-dense cream relatively inward collect hoti hai. [Q43]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0352","t":"04 Motion under Gravity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Motion under Gravity Full Mind Map\n🌍 MOTION UNDER GRAVITY — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. From Brahmagupta to Newton — Development of Gravitation Ideas\n2. Gravity in Space — Microgravity, Inertia & Orbital Free Fall\n3. Centre of Gravity & Stability — Why the Leaning Tower Stands\n4. Universal Gravitation — Inverse-Square Law & Radius Effect on g\n5. Free Fall — Same g, Mass Independence & Air Resistance\n6. Moon Gravity — Weight Changes, Mass Does Not\n7. Variation of g & Weight on Earth — Equator, Poles & Rotation\n8. Earthquake Acceleration — Source-Specific Threshold\n9. Motion on a Smooth Inclined Plane under Gravity\n10. Why We Do Not Feel Earth’s Uniform Motion\n11. If Earth’s Gravity Suddenly Vanished\n12. Four Fundamental Forces — Gravity is the Weakest\n13. Lift & Apparent Weight — When You Feel Heavier\n14. Simple Pendulum — Period, Seasons, Swing & Oscillation\n15. Escape Velocity & Why the Moon Lacks a Dense Atmosphere\n16. Candle Flame in Microgravity — Shape vs “No Flame” Confusion\n1. From Brahmagupta to Newton — Development of Gravitation Ideas\n● Brahmagupta (7th century) ne Brahmasphuta Siddhanta mein objects ke Earth ki taraf gravitate hone ka\nidea diya; source ise Newton se pehle ka anticipation maanta hai. [Q1]\n● Isaac Newton ne 1687 mein universal law of gravitation publish kiya: har do masses ek-doosre ko attract\nkarte hain. [Q2, Q3]\n2. Gravity in Space — Microgravity, Inertia & Orbital Free Fall\n● Orbit mein gravity absent nahi hoti; astronaut aur spacecraft dono continuous free fall mein saath\naccelerate karte hain, isliye support/normal force bahut kam hota hai aur apparent weightlessness feel\nhoti hai. [Q4, Q24]\n● Orbiting spaceship se released apple spacecraft ki orbital velocity share karta hai, isliye woh roughly usi\norbit mein spacecraft ke saath move karta rahega. [Q5]\n● Artificial satellite ko Earth ka gravitational attraction hi required centripetal acceleration deta hai; isi wajah\nse satellite continuously “fall” karte hue Earth ko miss karta rehta hai. [Q27, Q28, Q29]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q4 — “No Gravity in Space” is an Exam Simplification\n\n▸Low-Earth orbit mein gravity zero nahi hoti; ISS altitude par gravity still substantial hoti hai. Weightlessness ka real\nreason spacecraft + astronaut ka common orbital free fall hai.\n\n▸Agar old objective source option “There is no gravity” deta hai, source key ko note karo, but conceptually\n“microgravity/apparent weightlessness” correct explanation hai.\n3. Centre of Gravity & Stability — Why the Leaning Tower Stands\n● Body tab tak stable reh sakti hai jab centre of gravity se drawn vertical line uske base of support ke\nandar fall kare. Leaning Tower of Pisa isi condition ke karan abhi standing hai. [Q6]\n4. Universal Gravitation — Inverse-Square Law & Radius Effect on g\n● Newtonian gravitation: F = Gm m /r². Distance 2r ho jaaye to force F/4 ho jata hai.\n₁\n₂\n[Q7]\n● Surface gravity g = GM/R². Earth ka mass same rakhkar radius 1% shrink ho to g ≈ g/(0.99)² ≈ 1.02g,\nyani roughly 2% increase. [Q21]\n5. Free Fall — Same g, Mass Independence & Air Resistance\n● Near Earth, true gravitational weight mg approximately same reh sakta hai while falling, lekin free-fall\nmein apparent weight/support force zero hota hai. [Q8]\n● Vacuum mein feather, rubber ball aur wooden ball same g se fall karte hain; same height se release hon\nto saath reach karenge. [Q9]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Motion under Gravity Full Mind Map\n● Ideal/no-air-resistance condition mein wood, wax, iron ya 10 kg vs 1 kg objects ka fall time mass par\ndepend nahi karta; same height se drop karne par saath pahunchte hain. [Q10, Q12]\n● Air present ho to drag shape/area par depend karta hai. Same-weight iron aur wood balls ke source\nexample mein lower relative drag wali iron ball earlier reach kar sakti hai; vacuum result dono ke liye\nsame hota. [Q11]\n● Moon ke near bhi freely falling different masses same local gravitational acceleration paate hain, isliye\nsame initial conditions par kisi instant unki velocity same hoti hai. [Q13]\n● Rest se free fall: d = ½gt², so d t²; displacement-time graph parabolic hota hai.\n∝\n[Q18]\n● Dropped ball ke liye v = u + gt. u = 0, g = 9.8 m/s², t = 3 s\n v = 29.4 m/s downward.\n⇒\n[Q20]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q8 — True Weight vs Apparent Weight in Free Fall\n\n▸Gravitational weight mg near Earth roughly same rehta hai, kyunki m aur g almost unchanged hain.\n\n▸Lekin freely falling body ka apparent weight (normal/support force) zero hota hai. Question wording “weight” ko kis sense\nmein use kar rahi hai, ye exam mein check karo.\n6. Moon Gravity — Weight Changes, Mass Does Not\n● Moon ki surface gravity Earth ki approximately 1/6 hai; isliye person ka weight Moon par 1/6 hota hai.\n“Moon has no gravity” galat hai. [Q14]\n● Mass location se nahi badalta: Earth par 100 kg mass Moon par bhi 100 kg hi rahega; sirf W = mg\nchange hota hai. [Q23]\n7. Variation of g & Weight on Earth — Equator, Poles & Rotation\n● Earth oblate hai: polar radius smaller aur equatorial radius larger. g 1/R² ke karan g/weight maximum\n∝\npoles par aur minimum equator par hota hai. [Q15, Q16]\n● Earth ki rotation equator par maximum centrifugal effect create karti hai, jo effective weight reduce karta\nhai. Rotation speed badhe to equator par effective weight aur decrease karega. [Q17]\n8. Earthquake Acceleration — Source-Specific Threshold\n● Source Q22 “destructive earthquake” ko ground acceleration greater than 980 cm/s² (≈ 9.8 m/s² = 1g) se\nassociate karta hai. Is statement ko source-specific exam key ke roop mein yaad rakho. [Q22]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q22 — Destructive Earthquake Acceleration\n\n▸Source answer > 980 cm/s² (>1g) deta hai. Ye universal definition of “destructive earthquake” nahi hai; earthquake\nseverity magnitude, duration, frequency content, site response aur structural vulnerability par bhi depend karti hai.\n\n▸Isliye is fact ko conceptual law ke bajay source-specific PYQ key ke roop mein treat karo.\n9. Motion on a Smooth Inclined Plane under Gravity\n● Smooth incline par plane ke along acceleration a = g sinθ. Rest se length l cover karne ke liye l = ½g\nsinθ·t². [Q19]\n● If vertical height h = l sinθ, then t = (1/sinθ)√(2h/g). [Q19]\n10. Why We Do Not Feel Earth’s Uniform Motion\n● Hum Earth ke saath same rotational/orbital motion share karte hain; constant smooth motion ko relative\nframe mein feel nahi karte because our velocity relative to Earth is nearly zero. [Q25]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q25 — Source Stem’s 4,400 km/h Figure\n\n▸Earth ki actual mean orbital speed around Sun roughly 29.8 km/s (~107,000 km/h) hoti hai; 4,400 km/h source stem ka\ninaccurate value hai.\n\n▸Question ka intended concept phir bhi valid hai: uniform shared motion ko hum directly feel nahi karte;\nacceleration/change in motion feel hota hai.\n11. If Earth’s Gravity Suddenly Vanished\n● Gravitational force vanish ho jaaye to object ka gravitational weight W = mg zero ho jayega, lekin\nintrinsic mass unchanged rahega. [Q26]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Motion under Gravity Full Mind Map\n12. Four Fundamental Forces — Gravity is the Weakest\n● Four fundamental interactions: gravitational, electromagnetic, weak nuclear and strong nuclear. Inki\nrelative strength mein gravity weakest aur strong nuclear force strongest hota hai. [Q30]\n13. Lift & Apparent Weight — When You Feel Heavier\n● Lift upward acceleration a se move kare to normal reaction/apparent weight N = m(g + a), so person\nheavier feel karta hai. [Q31]\n● Downward acceleration mein N = m(g − a); free fall a = g par N = 0, yani apparent weightlessness. [Q31]\n14. Simple Pendulum — Period, Seasons, Swing & Oscillation\n● Simple pendulum ka time period T = 2π√(l/g); ideal small oscillations mein period primarily effective\nlength l aur g par depend karta hai. [Q32]\n● Summer mein thermal expansion se pendulum length badhti hai\n T badhta hai\n clock slow/loses time.\n⇒\n⇒\n\nWinter mein contraction se length ghatti hai\n T ghatti hai\n clock fast chal sakti hai.\n⇒\n⇒\n[Q33, Q36]\n● Swing par girl khadi hoti hai to centre of gravity upward shift hota hai aur effective pendulum length\ndecrease hoti hai; therefore period shorter ho jata hai. [Q34]\n● Mean position par restoring acceleration zero aur velocity maximum hoti hai; extreme position par\nvelocity zero but acceleration maximum hoti hai. Real pendulum ka amplitude air resistance/friction ke\nkaran time ke saath decrease karta hai. [Q35]\n15. Escape Velocity & Why the Moon Lacks a Dense Atmosphere\n● Escape velocity kisi celestial body ke gravitational field se permanently escape karne ki minimum launch\nspeed hai. Earth ke liye ≈ 11.2 km/s. [Q37]\n● 8 km/s Earth escape velocity se kam hai, isliye vertically projected object escape nahi karega aur\nidealized exam context mein Earth par return karega. [Q38]\n● Moon ki low gravity ke karan escape velocity low hai; gas molecules ki thermal/RMS speeds ke\ncomparison mein retention weak hoti hai, isliye Moon dense permanent atmosphere retain nahi kar pata.\n[Q39, Q40]\n16. Candle Flame in Microgravity — Shape vs “No Flame” Confusion\n● Microgravity mein buoyancy-driven convection weak ho jati hai; oxygen diffusion-dominated burning ki\nwajah se candle flame elongated nahi, roughly spherical hoti hai. [Q42]\n● Actual vacuum mein oxygen absent hone se ordinary candle burn nahi karegi; microgravity spacecraft\nmein oxygen available ho to flame exist kar sakti hai, bas uska shape/combustion behavior change hota\nhai. [Q41, Q42]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q41–Q42 — Candle in Space: Vacuum ≠ Microgravity\n\n▸Microgravity with oxygen: candle flame ban sakti hai aur roughly spherical hoti hai because buoyant convection weak\nhoti hai. Q42 isi concept se consistent hai.\n\n▸Vacuum: oxygen na hone par ordinary candle burn nahi karegi. Isliye “space mein gravity nahi, isliye flame nahi”\nscientifically oversimplified/inconsistent statement hai."]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0353","t":"05 Physical Properties of Materials","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical Properties of Materials Full Mind Map\n🧪 PHYSICAL PROPERTIES OF MATERIALS — FULL MIND\nMAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. States of Matter & Elasticity\n2. Surface Tension — Drops, Oil & Soap Bubbles\n3. Capillarity — Wicks, Blotting Paper & Plants\n4. Fluid & Atmospheric Pressure\n5. Viscosity & Streamline Flow\n6. Density as an Intensive Property\n7. Anomalous Expansion of Water\n8. Gas Laws & Liquefaction\n9. Relative Density & Floating — Iron, Mercury, Ships\n10. Icebergs & Floating Ice\n11. Temperature Effect on Buoyancy\n12. Sea Water, Swimming & Ships\n13. Apparent Weight in Different Media\n1. States of Matter & Elasticity\n● Liquid ka fixed volume hota hai lekin fixed shape nahi hota; kerosene iska example hai. Solid ka shape +\nvolume fixed hota hai, jabki gas ka neither fixed shape nor fixed volume. [Q1]\n● Young's modulus tensile stress/tensile strain ka ratio hai. Steel ka Young's modulus rubber se kaafi\nzyada hota hai. Coil/spring ki stretching mainly shear modulus (modulus of rigidity) se related hoti hai. [Q2]\n● Same material ke wire ke liye elongation ΔL = FL/(YA) L/d². Isliye lamba aur patla wire same load par\n∝\nzyada stretch karega; source options me 3 m length, 1.5 mm diameter wala wire maximum elongate hota\nhai. [Q13]\n2. Surface Tension — Drops, Oil & Soap Bubbles\n● Surface tension liquid surface ko minimum possible area lene ki tendency deta hai; given volume ke liye\nsphere ka surface area minimum hota hai, isliye water/rain drops approximately spherical hote hain. [Q3,\nQ4, Q5, Q6]\n● Oil ka surface tension water se kam hone par oil water surface par spread karta hai. Kerosene ka water\npar float karna surface tension se nahi, balki lower density se explain hota hai. [Q7, Q8]\n● Soap bubble ke andar pressure atmosphere se greater hota hai; soap bubble ke liye excess pressure\nΔP = 4T/r. Smaller bubble ka internal pressure larger bubble se higher hota hai. [Q9, Q10]\n● Hydrogen-filled flexible balloon altitude badhne par lower external atmospheric pressure ki wajah se\nexpand karta hai. [Q11]\n● Soap bubble par charge dene se like charges surface par repel karte hain, outward electrostatic\npressure badhta hai aur equilibrium radius increase karta hai. [Q12]\n3. Capillarity — Wicks, Blotting Paper & Plants\n● Capillary action narrow pores/tubes me surface tension + adhesion/cohesion ki wajah se liquid rise/fall\nkarne ki tendency hai. Kerosene wick aur blotting paper classic examples hain. [Q14, Q16]\n● Plants me roots se leaves tak water rise sirf capillarity se nahi hota; transpiration pull, cohesion-tension\naur root-related effects bhi important hain. [Q14, Q15]\n● Jurin's law: h = 2T cosθ/(rρg). Capillary rise T se directly aur tube radius\n\nतथाdensity se inversely related\nhota hai (other factors same). [Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q14 & Q17 — Capillarity Questions Need Conditions\n\n▸Straw se soft drink peena capillary action ka standard example nahi hai; mouth se pressure difference create karke liquid\nupar aata hai. Isliye Q14 me statement 2 ko exclude karna correct hai.\n\n▸Capillary height sirf surface tension par depend nahi karti: h = 2T cosθ/(rρg). Q17 ka “higher T\n higher rise” conclusion\n⇒\ntabhi safe hai jab radius, contact angle aur density comparable/assumed same hon."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical Properties of Materials Full Mind Map\n4. Fluid & Atmospheric Pressure\n● Lake ke bottom se top ki taraf aate air bubble par hydrostatic pressure kam hota hai, isliye Boyle's law ke\naccording bubble volume/size increase karta hai. [Q18]\n● High altitude par external atmospheric pressure kam hota hai; fountain pen ke andar trapped air\ncomparatively higher pressure se ink ko bahar push kar sakti hai. [Q19]\n● Hydraulic brakes Pascal's law par work karte hain: confined incompressible fluid me applied pressure all\ndirections me equally transmit hota hai. [Q20]\n● Barometer atmospheric pressure measure karta hai. Sudden sharp fall generally approaching storm/low-\npressure disturbance ka indicator mana jata hai. [Q21]\n● Torricelli relation v = √(2gh): free surface se deeper hole par efflux speed greater hoti hai. [Q22]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q22 — “Which Hole Throws Water Farthest?”\n\n▸Torricelli law deeper hole ko higher exit speed deta hai, but horizontal range ground level/exit height par bhi depend karti\nhai.\n\n▸Source key bottom hole (1) deta hai. Agar exam figure me holes ki heights/landing geometry materially differ ho, range ke\nliye projectile motion bhi consider karo; source stem ko exactly read karo.\n5. Viscosity & Streamline Flow\n● Laminar flow in a cylindrical pipe me no-slip condition ki wajah se wall ke paas fluid speed minimum (≈0)\naur central axis par maximum hoti hai; velocity profile parabolic hota hai. [Q23]\n● Liquids ki viscosity temperature badhne par generally decrease karti hai because molecular mobility\nincreases and cohesive effects weaken. [Q24, Q27]\n● Honey given common options me water, air, blood, alcohol/gasoline se much more viscous hai; viscosity\nflow ke resistance/internal friction ka measure hai. [Q25, Q26]\n6. Density as an Intensive Property\n● Substance ki amount badhane se mass, weight aur volume badh sakte hain, lekin same conditions par\ndensity ρ = m/V unchanged rehti hai; density intensive property hai. [Q28]\n7. Anomalous Expansion of Water\n● Water 0°C–4°C range me anomalous behaviour dikhata hai: 0→4°C heat karne par volume decreases\naur density increases; 4°C par volume minimum aur density maximum hoti hai. [Q29, Q32, Q34, Q35, Q36]\n● 4°C se upar water normal liquids ki tarah heating par expand karta hai. Isliye 0→10°C me volume pehle\ndecrease, phir increase hota hai. [Q32]\n● 9°C→3°C cooling me volume pehle 4°C tak decrease karta hai, phir 4→3°C me increase karta hai. [Q33]\n● Winter me surface water 0°C par freeze ho sakta hai while denser 4°C water bottom par liquid rehta hai.\nIce/top cold layer insulation provide karti hai, isliye aquatic life survive kar sakti hai. [Q29, Q30, Q31]\n● Maximum density of water 4°C ≈ 277 K par hoti hai. [Q34, Q35, Q36]\n8. Gas Laws & Liquefaction\n● Avogadro's law: same temperature and pressure par equal volumes of gases equal number of molecules\ncontain karte hain; V n.\n∝\n[Q37]\n● Gas liquefaction ke liye low temperature + high pressure favorable hota hai: kinetic energy reduce hoti\nhai aur molecules closer aate hain. [Q38]\n● Gas molecules ki average separation container volume increase karne ya some gas leak hone par\nincrease ho sakti hai; fixed volume me more gas/additional compression separation reduce karta hai. [Q39]\n● Charles's law (constant pressure): V/T = constant. Half-volume gas at 27°C = 300 K ko original volume\ntak expand karne ke liye temperature 600 K = 327°C chahiye. [Q40]\n9. Relative Density & Floating — Iron, Mercury, Ships"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physical Properties of Materials Full Mind Map\n● Iron water se denser hai, isliye solid iron ball/nail water me sink karta hai; mercury iron se much denser\nhai, isliye iron mercury par float kar sakta hai. [Q41, Q42]\n● Iron needle normally sink karti hai because iron density > water. Hollow iron ship ka average density\n(metal + enclosed air) water se sufficiently low hota hai aur displaced water ka buoyant force ship ko float\nkarata hai. [Q43]\n● Carefully placed small iron needle water surface tension ki supporting force se surface par remain kar\nsakti hai, despite iron being denser than water. [Q44]\n● Archimedes principle: immersed body par upthrust = displaced fluid ka weight. Isliye submerged bucket\nlighter feel hoti hai; water se bahar aate hi buoyant support kam ho jata hai aur bucket heavier feel hoti\nhai. [Q45]\n● Weightless balloon me 200 g water ho aur same-density water me fully immersed ho, to displaced water\nka weight contained water ke weight ke equal hoga; net apparent weight zero. [Q46]\n● Cloud droplets ka effective bulk density surrounding lower atmosphere ke comparison me low hota hai\naur air currents/buoyancy unhe suspended rakhne me help karte hain. [Q47]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q47 — Why Clouds Stay Aloft\n\n▸“Low density” exam-level shorthand hai. Individual cloud droplets liquid water se dense hote hain, but bahut tiny size ki\nwajah se terminal settling speed low hoti hai and atmospheric updrafts/turbulence them suspended rakh sakte hain.\n\n▸Cloud ko ek solid low-density object ki tarah simple buoyancy se explain karna incomplete model hai.\n10. Icebergs & Floating Ice\n● Floating body ka submerged fraction ≈ ρbody/ρfluid. Ice ki density water/seawater se lower hone ki\nwajah se major part submerged aur small fraction surface ke above hota hai. [Q48]\n● Floating ice jitna water displace karti hai, melt hone par utna hi water volume contribute karti hai (weight-\nequivalent basis); pure floating ice melt hone par water level essentially unchanged rehta hai. [Q49, Q50]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q48 — Iceberg Fraction Above Sea Water\n\n▸Source answer 1/9 above surface deta hai. Exact fraction densities par depend karta hai: above fraction = 1 −\nρice/ρseawater.\n\n▸Typical density values use karne par visible fraction roughly one-tenth ke order ka aata hai, so PYQ me source-specific\noption/key follow karte waqt formula yaad rakho.\n11. Temperature Effect on Buoyancy\n● Water 4°C par maximum density rakhta hai. Temperature 100°C ki taraf badhne par density decrease\nhoti hai, isliye same immersed volume ke liye buoyant force reduce hota hai aur floating body ka larger\nfraction submerged hoga. [Q51]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q51 — “At 100°C the Body Will Sink” is Not Universally Guaranteed\n\n▸Water density heating par decrease hoti hai, so a floating body ko support karne ke liye greater submerged fraction\nchahiye.\n\n▸Body tabhi completely sink karegi jab uski density heated water ki density se greater ho. Sirf “it floated at 4°C” se sinking\nat 100°C logically guaranteed nahi hoti; source key is a simplified exam assumption.\n12. Sea Water, Swimming & Ships\n● Sea water dissolved salts ki wajah se river/fresh water se denser hota hai; greater density greater\nbuoyant force provide karti hai, isliye sea me swimming easier feel hoti hai. [Q52]\n● Ship river se sea me jaata hai to denser sea water same weight ko support karne ke liye less volume\ndisplace karta hai, so ship thoda rise karta hai. [Q54, Q55]\n13. Apparent Weight in Different Media\n● Apparent weight = true weight − buoyant force. Given media me hydrogen sabse low-density hai, so\nuska upthrust least aur body ka apparent weight highest hota hai. [Q53]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0354","t":"06 Optics Light","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Optics (Light) Full Mind Map\n🔭 OPTICS (LIGHT) — FULL MIND MAP\n\nप्रकाशिकी· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Light Basics, Spectrum & Speed\n2. Interference, Total Internal Reflection & Optical Fibre\n3. Optical Applications — Reflection, Holography, Raman & CD\n4. Human Eye — Retina, Image & Vision\n5. Colour, Wavelength & Atmospheric Optics\n6. Mirrors, Telescope & Reflection Applications\n7. Dispersion, Rainbow, Refraction & Plane Mirror\n8. Lenses, Eye Defects & Accommodation\n9. Interference, Camera & Retina Comparison\n10. Colour Mixing, Pigments & Optical Illusions\n1. Light Basics, Spectrum & Speed\n● Photon energy E = hc/λ; wavelength chhoti hogi to energy zyada hogi. Source options me 200–280 nm\nradiation ka energy per quantum highest hai. [Q1]\n● Visible light ko exam me roughly 400–700 nm maana jata hai; older ranges 390–780 nm ya 3900–7600 Å bhi\noptions me mil sakti hain. [Q2–Q4]\n● Normal photopic vision me human eye yellow-green region (~555 nm / 5500 Å) ke around sabse sensitive hoti\nhai; red par maximum sensitivity nahi hoti. [Q5–Q7]\n● Light dual nature show karti hai—wave bhi, photon/particle bhi. Everyday scale par straight-line propagation\nuski very small wavelength ki wajah se apparent hoti hai. [Q8–Q9]\n● Vacuum me light speed c ≈ 3×10^8 m/s hai aur given ordinary objects/waves se bahut zyada hai. [Q10–Q12]\n● Medium ki optical density/refractive index badhne par light ki speed kam hoti hai; vacuum me maximum aur\ngiven options me glass jaise denser medium me lower hoti hai. Air ki optical properties\ntemperature/pressure/density se subtly vary kar sakti hain. [Q13–Q16]\n● Sunlight ko Earth tak pahunchne me ~8.3 min (about 8–8.5 min) lagte hain. [Q17–Q19]\n● Light velocity fundamental maximum speed hai; medium change par frequency constant rehti hai, jabki speed\naur wavelength change karte hain. Denser→rarer jaane par ray speed up karke normal se away bend karti hai.\n[Q20–Q24]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q13 — No Single Clean Option\n\n▸Source itself notes that speed of light in air depends on air's optical density, which changes with temperature, pressure\nand composition/humidity. Isliye Q13 me single-option framing imperfect hai; concept yaad rakho: v=c/n.\n2. Interference, Total Internal Reflection & Optical Fibre\n● Thin soap film ke glittering colours reflected waves ki interference se bante hain; film ki multiple reflections\npath difference create karti hain. [Q25]\n● Total internal reflection tab possible hai jab light denser se rarer medium me jaye aur incidence angle critical\nangle se greater ho. Diamond ka high refractive index/low critical angle uski brilliance ka main reason hai. [Q26–\nQ30]\n● Optical fibre total internal reflection par based hota hai; signal lightwave ke form me travel karta hai, power\nconsumption low hota hai aur RF interference se immunity milti hai. [Q31–Q35]\n● Medical endoscope me fibre optics/TIR ka use karke body ke internal parts dekhe ja sakte hain. [Q36–Q37]\n● Mirage hot surface ke paas refractive-index gradient se ray bending aur suitable conditions me total internal\nreflection ka result hota hai; terrestrial heating is gradient ko create karti hai. [Q38–Q40]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q25 & Mirage — Source Wording vs Core Physics\n\n▸Soap-film colours ka core mechanism thin-film interference hai; reflections dono film surfaces se aati hain. 'Total\nreflection + interference' source option ko verbatim fact mat samjho.\n\n▸Mirage ko graded refraction se start karke limiting case me total internal reflection se explain kiya jata hai; source Q40\nterrestrial heating + refraction ko select karta hai."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Optics (Light) Full Mind Map\n3. Optical Applications — Reflection, Holography, Raman & CD\n● Fresh snow ka albedo high hota hai, isliye given surfaces me ye sunlight ka large fraction reflect karta hai.\n[Q41]\n● Three-dimensional image recording/reconstruction technique holography hai. [Q42–Q43]\n● Phosphor-coated screen par electron beam ko line-wise scan karke image generate karna raster scan kehlata\nhai. [Q44]\n● Raman effect transparent media se light ke scattering ke dauran frequency shift se related phenomenon hai.\n[Q45]\n● CD audio player information read karne ke liye laser beam use karta hai; CD surface par rainbow-like colours\nreflection + diffraction/interference effects ki wajah se dikhte hain. [Q46–Q47]\n● Radio waves rapidly oscillating electric currents se generate hoti hain; reflected short radio waves ka Doppler\neffect speed detection me use kiya ja sakta hai. Long wavelength ka scattering short wavelength se more nahi\nhota, aur water me visible light speed vacuum se noticeably lower hoti hai. [Q48]\n4. Human Eye — Retina, Image & Vision\n● Cinema me ~24 frames/s continuous motion ka illusion deta hai; persistence of vision ko source ~1/16 s ke\norder me treat karta hai. [Q49]\n● Retina light ko neural impulses me convert karti hai. Eye lens retina par real, inverted aur object se smaller\nimage banata hai. [Q50–Q52]\n● Do eyes stereoscopic/binocular vision deti hain, jis se distance aur depth perception improve hota hai. [Q53]\n● Solar eclipse ke partial phases ko naked eye se dekhna unsafe hai; source retinal injury ko UV exposure se\nassociate karta hai. [Q54]\n● Star ka colour uske surface temperature ka indicator hota hai—bluish stars hotter aur reddish stars cooler\nhote hain. [Q55]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q49 & Q54 — Exam-source Specific\n\n▸Q49 source persistence of vision ko ~1/16 s treat karta hai; older exam texts me 1/16 s ya ~0.1 s dono approximations\nmil sakti hain.\n\n▸Q54 source key UV deta hai. Practical eclipse safety point: uneclipsed/partially eclipsed Sun ko certified solar filter ke\nbina directly kabhi na dekhen.\n5. Colour, Wavelength & Atmospheric Optics\n● Atmosphere me dust/air particles light ko scatter/diffuse karte hain. Visible colour wavelength se determine\nhota hai: red longest wavelength, violet shortest. [Q56–Q62]\n● Energy wavelength ke inversely proportional hai; given options me blue light highest-energy choice ho sakti\nhai. Prism me red least deviate karta hai because uska refractive index relatively lower hota hai; red green se\nless energetic hota hai. [Q63–Q65]\n● Atmospheric refraction ki wajah se Sun actual sunrise se pehle visible ho sakta hai, horizon ke paas\nSun/Moon flattened lag sakte hain aur stars twinkle karte hain. [Q66–Q68]\n● Red danger/traffic signal me useful hai because longest visible wavelength hone se Rayleigh scattering least\nhoti hai, so long distance/fog me comparatively better penetrate karta hai. [Q69–Q71]\n● Sky blue short-wavelength scattering ki wajah se hai. Rainbow ka main cause scattering nahi, balki refraction\n+ dispersion + internal reflection hai; sunrise/sunset red longer atmospheric path me short wavelengths ke\nscattering-out hone se dikhta hai. [Q72–Q77]\n● High altitude/space me atmosphere sparse ya absent hone se scattering kam hoti hai aur sky dark/black\ndikhta hai. [Q78–Q80]\n● Sea ka blue appearance water ke selective absorption/scattering aur sky reflection dono se influenced ho\nsakta hai; green grass green wavelengths reflect karti hai. [Q81–Q82]\n● Soap film ke colours thin-film interference se bante hain. Receding source ka light relativistic Doppler effect se\nred-shift hota hai; source numerical example blue ko yellow-orange region tak shift karta hai. [Q83–Q84]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Optics (Light) Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q81 & Q84 — Simplified Source Explanations\n\n▸Sea blue hona sirf sky reflection nahi hai; water ki wavelength-selective absorption/scattering bhi important hai. Source\nanswer reflection + scattering ko emphasize karta hai.\n\n▸Q84 source classical-style Doppler calculation se yellow-orange answer deta hai. Relativistic speeds par exact treatment\nrelativistic Doppler formula se hota hai; PYQ me source key ko context ke saath padho.\n6. Mirrors, Telescope & Reflection Applications\n● Convex mirror hamesha virtual, erect aur diminished image deta hai aur wide field of view ke karan vehicle\nrear-view mirror me use hota hai. [Q85, Q87–Q89]\n● Convex lens ke kuch portions black strips se block karne par complete image still ban sakti hai, lekin\nbrightness kam ho jati hai because fewer rays contribute. [Q86]\n● Concave mirror me object centre of curvature par ho to image real, inverted, same size banti hai. Pole-focus\nke beech object ho to virtual, erect, magnified image mil sakti hai. [Q90–Q92]\n● Searchlight/headlight me concave mirror bulb ko focus ke paas rakhkar parallel beam banata hai; dentist\nenlarged erect view ke liye concave mirror use karta hai. [Q93–Q96]\n● Sun protection ke source answer me umbrella top white (reflection) aur bottom black diya gaya hai. [Q97]\n● Astronomical telescope final image virtual and magnified de sakta hai; objective diameter badhne se resolving\npower improve hoti hai. [Q98–Q99]\n● Do parallel plane mirrors ke beech ideal case me infinite images form hote hain. Mirror θ angle rotate ho to\nreflected ray 2θ rotate karta hai. [Q100–Q102]\n● Traffic reflectors/glass beads incident light ko strongly return karne ke liye refraction + internal\nreflection/retroreflection principles exploit karte hain; source TIR ko key mechanism treat karta hai. [Q103]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q97 & Q103 — Application Questions\n\n▸Umbrella colour-combination result thermal design details par depend kar sakta hai; source key top white & bottom black\ndeta hai.\n\n▸Traffic glass-bead reflectors ko better description retroreflection hai, jisme refraction/internal reflection combine ho sakte\nhain; source Q103 TIR ko explanation ke\n\nरूपमेंaccept karta hai.\n7. Dispersion, Rainbow, Refraction & Plane Mirror\n● White light ke seven colours prism se separate hote hain; is splitting ko dispersion kehte hain. [Q104, Q107]\n● Rainbow me outer/terminal colours red aur violet hote hain; green middle region me hota hai. Formation me\nrefraction, dispersion aur internal reflection tino contribute karte hain. [Q105–Q109]\n● Rainbow observer ke opposite-Sun direction me dikhta hai; high noon me Sun high hone par ordinary ground\nobserver ko primary rainbow generally visible nahi hota. [Q110]\n● Shadow light ki rectilinear propagation ki wajah se banta hai. [Q111]\n● Pool shallow dikhna, slanted stick bent/short dikhna, aur water me coin ka apparent position shift hona\nrefraction ke examples hain. [Q112–Q114]\n● Water ke andar air bubble surrounding water ke comparison me lower refractive index hone se\nconcave/diverging lens ki tarah behave karta hai. Equal focal-length convex + concave lenses contact me net\npower ~0 dekar plane glass sheet jaisa act kar sakte hain. [Q115–Q117]\n● Full-body image dekhne ke liye plane mirror ki minimum height person ki height ka half hoti hai; plane mirror\nka radius of curvature infinity hota hai. [Q118–Q120]\n8. Lenses, Eye Defects & Accommodation\n● Magnifying glass convex lens hota hai. Hypermetropia/long-sightedness convex lens se correct hoti hai;\nreading glasses commonly converging/convex lenses use karte hain. [Q121–Q124]\n● Myopia/short-sightedness concave lens se correct hoti hai; combined rule: Myopia→concave,\nHypermetropia→convex. [Q125–Q129]\n● Bright se dark room me jaane par initial vision poor hoti hai because pupil dilation aur rod pigment (rhodopsin)\nregeneration/dark adaptation me time lagta hai. [Q130]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Optics (Light) Full Mind Map\n● Eye focusing accommodation se hoti hai: ciliary muscles lens curvature/convexity change karke focal length\nadjust karte hain. [Q131–Q132]\n● ENT examination ke traditional head mirror me concave mirror with central aperture use hota hai, convex\nnahi. [Q133]\n● Normal eye ka least distance of distinct vision ~25 cm hota hai. Lens power dioptre me measure hoti hai:\nP=1/f(m); +2 D lens ka focal length +0.5 m = 50 cm hota hai. [Q134–Q139]\n● Ordinary non-corrective sunglasses ka optical power approximately 0 dioptre hota hai; unka main role light\nintensity reduce karna hai. [Q140]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q130 — Multiple Mechanisms in Dark Adaptation\n\n▸Dark room me adaptation sirf pupil-size change se nahi hoti; rod photopigment (rhodopsin) regeneration aur neural\nadaptation bhi role play karte hain. Source ne isliye single clean correct option mark nahi kiya.\n9. Interference, Camera & Retina Comparison\n● Young double-slit fringe width β=λD/d. λ=500 nm, D=1 m, d=1 mm ke liye β=0.5 mm. [Q141]\n● Camera exposure roughly aperture area × shutter time par depend karta hai; given combinations me f/8 at\n1/250 s maximum exposure deta hai. [Q142]\n● Traditional camera me retina film ke analogous hai; normal human eye me object image retina par form hoti\nhai. [Q143–Q145]\n● Hypermetropia me near object ki image retina ke behind form hone ki tendency hoti hai. [Q146]\n10. Colour Mixing, Pigments & Optical Illusions\n● Opaque object ka observed colour mainly us wavelength/colour se determined hota hai jise wo reflect karta\nhai. [Q147]\n● Additive primary colours of light Red, Green, Blue (RGB) hain. In tino ko equal proportion me combine karne\npar white light banti hai; black primary colour nahi hai. [Q148–Q152]\n● Subtractive pigment system me cyan, magenta, yellow important hain: magenta+yellow→red aur\ncyan+magenta→blue. Source matching: Magenta=red+blue; Teal=blue+green+white; Mauve=blue+red+white;\nCyan=green+blue. [Q153–Q154]\n● Sunlight/white light ko school-level spectrum me seven VIBGYOR colours me describe kiya jata hai; brown\nVIBGYOR member nahi hai. [Q155–Q156]\n● Source optical-illusion set me dusk par Sun ka apparent size, dawn ka red colour aur star twinkling ko optical\neffects/illusions maana gaya hai; dawn me Moon ya Polestar visibility real astronomical observations hain.\n[Q157]"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0355","t":"07 Heat and Thermodynamics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heat and Thermodynamics Full Mind Map\n🔥 HEAT AND THERMODYNAMICS — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\n\nऊष्माऔरऊष्मागतिकी· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Thermodynamic Laws, Heat Transfer & Latent Heat\n2. Temperature Scales, Thermometry & Absolute Zero\n3. Thermal Expansion, Thermostat & Refrigeration\n4. Humidity, Air-Conditioning & Evaporative Cooling\n5. Boiling/Freezing Point, Clothing & Perspiration\n6. Newton’s Cooling, Weather & Atmospheric Pressure\n7. Pressure Cooker — Pressure, Boiling Point & Safety\n8. Water Anomaly, Clouds & Specific Heat\n9. Cold Storage, Wool, Sound in Humid Air & Open Refrigerator\n1. Thermodynamic Laws, Heat Transfer & Latent Heat\n● Ecosystem me trophic level badhne par usable energy decline ko second law of thermodynamics explain karta\nhai—energy transformations me useful energy ka kuch hissa dissipate hota hai. [Q1]\n● Solid, liquid aur gas tino phases ka ek saath equilibrium me coexist karna triple point kehlata hai; water ka\ntriple point 273.16 K (0.01°C) hota hai. [Q2]\n● Radiation ko medium ki zarurat nahi hoti; isi liye Sun se Earth tak heat vacuum ke through aa sakti hai.\nConvection sirf fluids—liquids aur gases—me bulk motion se hota hai. [Q3–Q4]\n● Thermos flask heat exchange ko minimum karta hai: vacuum conduction/convection ko suppress karta hai aur\nreflective/silvered walls radiation ko reduce karti hain. [Q5, Q57]\n● 100°C steam same-temperature boiling water/air se zyada severe burn de sakti hai because condense hote\nwaqt latent heat of vaporization release karti hai (~540 cal/g exam value). [Q6–Q8]\n● Steam at 100°C aur water at 100°C me heat content same nahi; latent heat of fusion of ice ~80 cal/g aur\nvaporization ~540 cal/g. Air-conditioner room se evaporator par heat leta hai aur condenser par bahar reject\nkarta hai. [Q9]\n● 1 g ice at 0°C → water at 0°C (80 cal) → water at 100°C (100 cal) → steam at 100°C (540 cal): total ≈ 720 cal.\n[Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q5 & Q57 — Thermos Flask\n\n▸Vacuum conduction aur convection ko strongly reduce karta hai, lekin electromagnetic radiation vacuum me travel kar\nsakti hai. Radiation loss silvered/reflective surfaces se reduce hota hai.\n\n▸Isliye “vacuum prevents radiation” ko literal physics statement mat maanna; source answer ko thermos ke combined\ninsulation design ke context me padho.\n2. Temperature Scales, Thermometry & Absolute Zero\n● Celsius–Fahrenheit relation: F = (9/5)C + 32; inverse C = (F−32)×5/9. Linear relation hone se averages par\nbhi F̄ = (9/5)C̄ + 32 apply hota hai. [Q11, Q22]\n● Celsius aur Fahrenheit readings −40° par exactly equal hoti hain. [Q12–Q14]\n● Agar Fahrenheit reading Celsius ki double ho, F=2C set karne par C=160°C aur F=320°F milta hai. [Q15]\n● Normal human body temperature exam values me ~37°C ≈ 98.4–98.6°F ≈ 310 K; 98.4°F ≈ 36.89°C (~36.9°C).\n[Q16–Q19]\n● Kelvin thermodynamic scale exam level par negative values nahi leta; absolute zero 0 K = −273.15°C\ntheoretically lowest temperature hai. [Q20, Q27]\n● Quick conversions: 200°F ≈ 93.3°C; 40°C = 104°F; 50°C = 122°F. [Q21, Q23–Q24]\n● Cold countries me alcohol thermometric liquid useful hai because uska freezing point mercury se much lower\nho sakta hai. Automobile antifreeze ke liye ethylene glycol widely used hai. [Q25–Q26]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heat and Thermodynamics Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q27 — Absolute Zero: Exam Model vs Quantum Physics\n\n▸Competitive-exam level par 0 K ko “minimum possible temperature / thermal motion minimum” likha jata hai.\n\n▸Strict quantum physics me particles ki zero-point motion completely vanish nahi hoti; source ka “completely at rest”\nclassical simplification hai.\n3. Thermal Expansion, Thermostat & Refrigeration\n● Most materials heating par expand karte hain; mass same aur volume increase hone se density generally\ndecrease hoti hai. [Q28]\n● Ice melt hone par source answer ke according volume decreases—liquid water, ice se denser hota hai. [Q29]\n● Given heating graph me curved liquid Q ne 100°C straight-line P se faster attain kiya. [Q30]\n● Thermostat ka role temperature ko automatically regulate/stable maintain karna hai; refrigerator thermostat bhi\npreset internal temperature maintain karta hai. [Q31–Q35]\n● Food refrigeration ke liye source ka safest option ~4°C hai. Frost-free fridge ki low-humidity environment\nsoggy biscuits se moisture remove karke unhe crisp bana sakti hai. [Q36–Q37]\n● Drink me ice melt karne ke liye latent heat surrounding drink se absorb karti hai, isliye drink cool hota hai. [Q38]\n● Large refrigeration plants ammonia use kar sakte hain; source domestic refrigerators ko CFCs se contrast\nkarta hai. Ammonia ambient temperature par liquefy karne ke liye sufficiently high pressure chahiye, low\npressure nahi. [Q39]\n● Freezer me excess ice layer poor conductor/insulator ki tarah heat transfer ko hinder karke cooling efficiency\nko adversely affect kar sakti hai. [Q40]\n● Isotropic solid heating par dimensions sab directions me expand karte hain: glass rod ki length ke saath width\nbhi increase hoti hai; heated ring ka inner hole bhi expand hota hai. [Q41–Q42]\n● Bimetal strip me higher-expansion metal outer/convex side par aata hai. Copper glass se zyada thermally\nconductive hone ke karan same temperature par touch me hotter feel ho sakta hai; winter me iron wood se\ncolder feel hota hai because hand se heat faster conduct karta hai. [Q43–Q45]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q39 — Refrigerant Wording Is Historical\n\n▸Source domestic refrigerators ko CFC refrigerants se contrast karta hai. Ye older/historical framing hai; modern\nrefrigeration me environmental rules ke kaaran multiple non-CFC refrigerants use hote hain.\n\n▸Core exam concept: large industrial systems me ammonia common ho sakta hai; liquefaction/condensation pressure–\ntemperature conditions par depend karti hai.\n4. Humidity, Air-Conditioning & Evaporative Cooling\n● Warmer air ki water-vapour carrying capacity generally increase hoti hai. Same moisture content par\ntemperature badhne se relative humidity usually decrease hoti hai. [Q46–Q47]\n● Source strong-wind night me dew na banne ko fast evaporation se explain karta hai; practical meteorology me\nwind surface cooling aur near-surface saturation ko bhi disrupt karti hai. [Q48]\n● Air-conditioner temperature ke saath humidity ko control/dehumidify kar sakta hai; ordinary air-cooler humidity\nko precise maintain nahi karta aur often moisture add karta hai. [Q49–Q50]\n● Desert cooler evaporative cooling par based hai: water evaporation latent heat absorb karke air ko cool karti\nhai. [Q51]\n● Refrigerator/AC cooling refrigerant ke pressure-change, expansion aur especially evaporation/phase-change\ncycle se hoti hai; source option ise compressed gas ke release/expansion ke roop me frames karta hai. [Q52]\n● Wet clothes fastest dry honge jab temperature high aur relative humidity low ho; source options me 60°C +\n20% RH earliest drying deta hai. [Q53]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heat and Thermodynamics Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q48 & Q52 — Simplified Source Explanations\n\n▸Dew strong wind me suppress ho sakti hai mainly because wind radiatively cooled surface ke paas air ko mix karti hai aur\nsaturation/dew-point condition develop nahi hone deti; “evaporation fast” alone incomplete explanation hai.\n\n▸Refrigeration cycle me cooling ka core step low-pressure refrigerant ka evaporation/heat absorption hai; “release of\ncompressed gas” source-option shorthand hai.\n5. Boiling/Freezing Point, Clothing & Perspiration\n● Common salt add karne se water ka boiling point increase aur freezing point decrease hota hai—boiling-point\nelevation + freezing-point depression. [Q54–Q55]\n● High altitude par atmospheric pressure low hone se water lower temperature par boil karta hai; source\nquestion me salt use ko boiling point thoda raise karke cooking aid se link kiya gaya hai, sirf outside\ntemperature low hone se nahi. [Q56]\n● White/light clothes incoming radiant energy ka larger fraction reflect aur less absorb karti hain, isliye summer\nme preferred; winter me dark clothes greater absorption ke liye useful hote hain. [Q58–Q61]\n● Perspiration-related water loss atmospheric temperature aur humidity dono se affected hai. Sweat evaporation\nbody se latent heat le kar thermoregulation me major role play karti hai. [Q62–Q63]\n● Fan mainly sweat evaporation ko accelerate karke comfort deta hai; earthen pitcher ke pores se water\nevaporate hota hai aur latent heat absorb hone se inner water cool rehta hai. [Q64–Q65]\n6. Newton’s Cooling, Weather & Atmospheric Pressure\n● Newton’s law of cooling ke according heat-loss rate surrounding se temperature difference par depend karti\nhai. Given Churu (95−48=47°C) aur Shimla (71−24=47°C) cases me equal ΔT ki wajah se source same cooling\ntime choose karta hai. [Q66]\n● Body 90→75°C in 25 s cool hota hai; next 75→60°C drop generally 25 s se zyada lega because temperature\ndifference surroundings se kam hota jata hai aur cooling rate slow hoti hai. [Q67]\n● Source heat-wave criterion question me threshold plains ke liye at least 40°C aur hilly regions ke liye at least\n30°C diya gaya hai; question ke dono reversed statements incorrect hain. [Q68]\n● Summer me “humid heat” high humidity se associated hai, while xeric condition low moisture/low humidity ko\nindicate karti hai. [Q69–Q70]\n● Atmospheric pressure body par large force lagata hai, lekin internal body-fluid/tissue pressures aur external\npressure largely balance karte hain; source ise blood pressure slightly more than atmosphere ke wording me\ndeta hai. [Q71]\n● Solute add karne se water potential increase nahi, decrease hota hai; evaporation badhne par air me absolute\nhumidity increase ho sakti hai. [Q72]\n● Altitude increase → atmospheric pressure decrease → water ka boiling point decrease; isliye high altitude par\nwater 100°C se below boil kar sakta hai. [Q73–Q74]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q71 — Why Atmospheric Pressure Is Not Felt\n\n▸Body ke andar fluids/gases aur tissues external atmospheric pressure ko largely balance karte hain; human body rigid\nevacuated shell nahi hai.\n\n▸Source ka “blood exerts slightly more pressure” wording oversimplified hai—blood pressure normally atmospheric\npressure ke relative (gauge pressure) me quote kiya jata hai.\n7. Pressure Cooker — Pressure, Boiling Point & Safety\n● Pressure cooker me steam trapped hone se pressure increase hota hai, water ka boiling point ~100°C se upar\nchala jata hai aur food higher cooking temperature par faster cook hota hai. [Q75–Q80]\n● Pressure-cooker handle ebonite jaise poor conductor/insulator se bana hota hai taaki heat hand tak na aaye;\n“ebonite hard hai” true ho sakta hai, but handle-use ka correct explanation insulation hai. [Q81]\n● Cooker ki regulated pressure/maximum cooking temperature mainly vent-hole area aur regulator/weight par\ndepend karti hai; once pressure set ho, extra flame primarily steam-generation/escape badhati hai, set\ntemperature ko indefinitely nahi. [Q82–Q83]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Heat and Thermodynamics Full Mind Map\n8. Water Anomaly, Clouds & Specific Heat\n● Water freezing par expand karta hai; tightly corked glass bottle me ice ka larger volume walls par pressure dal\nkar bottle tod sakta hai. [Q84–Q85]\n● Floating ice melt hone par water level same rehta hai, because floating ice apne weight ke equal water\ndisplace karta hai aur melted water exactly wahi displaced volume occupy karta hai. [Q86]\n● Cloudy nights clear nights se warmer ho sakti hain because clouds outgoing terrestrial infrared radiation ko\nabsorb/re-emit karke net heat loss reduce karte hain. [Q87–Q88]\n● Cloud type matters: low thick clouds incoming solar radiation strongly reflect karke cooling kar sakte hain; high\nthin clouds outgoing IR trap/re-emit karke warming effect de sakte hain. Source ke reversed statements dono\nincorrect hain. [Q89]\n● Water ki specific heat land se much higher hai, isliye oceans temperature slowly change karte hain. Source\nassertion set me continent–ocean contrast ko winter me greater maana gaya, not summer. [Q90]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q87–Q89 — Clouds and Heat\n\n▸Clouds outgoing infrared ko simple mirror ki tarah “reflect” karne se zyada efficiently absorb aur re-emit karti hain;\ndownward re-emission night-time cooling ko reduce karti hai.\n\n▸Low thick clouds ka shortwave reflection cooling dominate kar sakta hai, jabki high thin clouds ka longwave greenhouse\neffect comparatively stronger ho sakta hai.\n9. Cold Storage, Wool, Sound in Humid Air & Open Refrigerator\n● Cold chamber me low temperature fruit respiration/metabolic rate ko slow karta hai, isliye ripening/spoilage\ndelay aur storage life increase hoti hai. [Q91]\n● Woollen clothes mainly fibres ke beech trapped air ki insulating layer ki wajah se warm rakhte hain; wool\nprotein hona primary explanation nahi hai. [Q92]\n● Humidity increase hone par air ki effective density decrease hone se sound velocity generally increase hoti\nhai; therefore “humidity badhne par sound speed decreases” statement incorrect hai. [Q93]\n● Closed room me refrigerator ka door open chhodne par room cool nahi hota; compressor electrical work add\nkarta hai aur condenser room me extracted heat + work reject karta hai, so room temperature slightly increase\nhoti hai. [Q94–Q95]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q95\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0356","t":"08 Wave Motion","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Wave Motion Full Mind Map\n🌊 WAVE MOTION — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\nतरंगगति\n· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Mechanical, Longitudinal, Transverse & Stationary Waves\n2. Radio Propagation, Ionosphere & Waves in Vacuum\n3. Cosmic Rays, Radiation, Albedo & Atmospheric Heating\n4. Electromagnetic Spectrum — Speed, Frequency, Energy & X-rays\n5. EM-wave Applications — Radar, Remote Sensing, IR & Medical Use\n6. Telecommunication, Microwave, Modulation & FM\n7. Ionosphere Communication & Rain Fade\n8. X-rays in Diagnosis & Wilhelm Röntgen\n1. Mechanical, Longitudinal, Transverse & Stationary Waves\n● Sound ek mechanical wave hai; air/fluid me particles propagation direction ke parallel vibrate karte hain, isliye\nsound longitudinal mechanical wave hoti hai. Radio, X-ray aur light electromagnetic waves hain. [Q1–Q3]\n● Longitudinal wave me do consecutive compressions ya rarefactions ke beech ki distance wavelength (λ) hoti\nhai; transverse wave me consecutive crests/troughs ke beech ki distance bhi wavelength hoti hai. [Q4, Q20]\n● Sitar ki stretched string pluck karne par transverse waves reflect hokar stationary transverse wave pattern\nbanati hain; instrument body bhi forced vibration se sound radiate karti hai. [Q5]\n● Sound vacuum me travel nahi kar sakti because mechanical wave ko particle medium chahiye; solid, liquid\naur gas me propagate kar sakti hai. [Q10]\n2. Radio Propagation, Ionosphere & Waves in Vacuum\n● Long-distance radio communication me ionosphere important hai: upper atmosphere ka ionized region radio\npropagation ko affect/return kar sakta hai; source questions long radio waves/wireless deflection-reflection ko\nionosphere se link karte hain. [Q6–Q8]\n● UHF roughly 300 MHz–3 GHz range hai; high-frequency UHF signals commonly line-of-sight/space-wave\npropagation use karte hain, ground-wave ya ordinary ionospheric sky-wave route nahi. [Q9]\n● Radio waves electromagnetic hain aur uncharged radiation hone ke karan ordinary electric/magnetic fields se\nbeam-path deflection nahi dikhati. [Q11]\n● Electromagnetic radiation ko material medium ki requirement nahi hoti; conduction/convection ke unlike\nradiation vacuum se pass kar sakti hai. [Q14]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q6–Q9 — Radio Propagation Depends on Frequency\n\n▸Ionosphere kuch radio-frequency bands ko refract/return kar sakta hai, but sab radio waves same tarah reflect nahi hoti.\n\n▸UHF generally line-of-sight/space-wave mode me propagate karta hai; exam statement ko frequency band ke context me\npadho.\n3. Cosmic Rays, Radiation, Albedo & Atmospheric Heating\n● Cosmic rays electromagnetic waves nahi, mostly very-high-energy charged particles hain jo Sun aur extra-\nsolar/galactic sources se aa sakte hain. [Q12–Q13]\n● Albedo kisi surface/body ki incident radiation ko reflect karne ki fraction/reflecting power hai; fresh snow high\nalbedo aur dark/water surfaces comparatively low albedo show kar sakte hain. [Q15]\n● Earth incoming solar shortwave energy absorb karke longwave terrestrial infrared radiation emit karti hai; CO ₂\naur other greenhouse gases is longwave radiation ko absorb karte hain, isliye atmosphere largely terrestrial\nradiation se heat hota hai. [Q16–Q18]\n● Earth surface absorbed energy ko ultraviolet nahi, mainly infrared/longwave form me re-radiate karti hai;\nclouds aur atmospheric gases incoming solar radiation ka significant fraction reflect/absorb bhi karte hain. [Q19]\n4. Electromagnetic Spectrum — Speed, Frequency, Energy & X-rays\n● Vacuum me sab electromagnetic waves ki speed c ≈ 3 × 10⁸ m/s hoti hai. [Q21]\n● X-rays electrically neutral electromagnetic radiation hain, isliye electric ya magnetic field se deflect nahi hoti;\nmatter/crystals se diffraction/scattering ho sakti hai. [Q22]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Wave Motion Full Mind Map\n● Supersonic “wave” EM spectrum ka member nahi; term speed-of-sound se faster motion ko describe karta\nhai. Gamma, X-ray aur UV electromagnetic radiation hain. [Q23]\n● EM spectrum wavelength order (long → short): Radio > Microwave > Infrared > Visible > Ultraviolet > X-ray >\nGamma. Frequency/energy ka order reverse hota hai. [Q24–Q26]\n● Microwaves ko broad definitions me roughly 300 MHz–300 GHz tak maana ja sakta hai; source option 1–300\nGHz ko most appropriate choose karta hai. [Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q27 — Microwave Frequency Range\n\n▸Microwave band ki exact lower boundary source/standard par vary karti hai. Broad engineering usage ≈300 MHz–300\nGHz bhi milti hai.\n\n▸HTML source options me 1–300 GHz answer chosen hai; exam me given options follow karo.\n5. EM-wave Applications — Radar, Remote Sensing, IR & Medical Use\n● Crystal structure determine karne me X-ray diffraction widely used hai because X-ray wavelength atomic\nspacing ke comparable hoti hai. [Q28]\n● RADAR radio/microwave-frequency electromagnetic waves se target aircraft/objects ki range, direction ya\nspeed infer karta hai. [Q29]\n● Remote sensing Earth/objects se reflected ya emitted electromagnetic radiation ko distance se measure karta\nhai; sensors spectrum ke different bands use kar sakte hain. [Q30]\n● Ozone depletion se shorter-wavelength UV surface tak pahunch sakti hai; source calculation minimum ≈100\nnm = 10 ⁷ m ko option ke roop me leta hai.\n⁻\n[Q31]\n● Night-vision systems infrared radiation detect/use karte hain. Common TV remotes bhi typically infrared use\nkarte hain. [Q32–Q35]\n● Q36 ke options me infrared absent hai; source “radio waves” choose karta hai because RF remotes bhi exist\nkarte hain, lekin conventional TV remote ka standard exam answer generally infrared hota hai. [Q36]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q36 — TV Remote: Infrared vs Radio\n\n▸Conventional TV remotes ka standard answer infrared (IR) hai—Q32–Q35 bhi isi concept ko test karte hain.\n\n▸Q36 me IR option hi nahi diya gaya; source RF remote existence ke basis par “radio waves” accept karta hai. Isko\ngeneral rule mat samajhna.\n6. Telecommunication, Microwave, Modulation & FM\n● Point-to-point aur satellite telecommunication me microwaves widely used hoti hain because high carrier\nfrequency large information capacity aur directional links allow karti hai. [Q37]\n● Carrier radio wave par information signal superimpose karne ki process modulation kehlati hai. [Q38]\n● FM me carrier frequency information signal ke according vary karti hai; FM broadcasting AM se higher\nfrequency band aur wider bandwidth use karti hai. “FM frequency range lower than AM” false hai. [Q39]\n● Source medium-speed 1200–2400 bit/s communication ke liye frequency modulation ko preferred batata hai;\nye historical/source-specific data-communication framing hai. [Q40]\n● Standard FM broadcast band 88–108 MHz hai. [Q41]\n● Wave relation f = c/λ. λ = 30 m aur c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s se f = 10⁷ Hz = 10 MHz. [Q42]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q40 — 1200–2400 bit/s FM Claim\n\n▸Ye source ka older communication/modem-style statement hai, modern digital communication ka universal rule nahi.\n\n▸Exam-source mapping preserve ki gayi hai: source answer Frequency Modulation hai.\n7. Ionosphere Communication & Rain Fade\n● Ionosphere radio communication ko charged ions/electrons ki wajah se facilitate karta hai—not ozone. “Radio\nwaves have long wavelength” generally true ho sakta hai, but given reason ke roop me sufficient nahi; source\nQ43 me neither statement accepted hai. [Q43]\n● Rain satellite/microwave signals ko absorb/scatter karke attenuation (“rain fade”) cause kar sakti hai;\nweakened signal small receiving dish ke liye threshold ke below ja sakta hai. [Q44]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Wave Motion Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q43–Q44 — Ionosphere & Rain Fade\n\n▸Ionospheric radio return ionized particles/electron-density profile se related hai, ozone reflection se nahi.\n\n▸Rain fade especially microwave/satellite links me absorption + scattering se hota hai; dish size signal margin ko affect kar\nsakta hai but rain ka root cause antenna size nahi.\n8. X-rays in Diagnosis & Wilhelm Röntgen\n● X-rays medical imaging me use hoti hain; source intestinal-disease diagnosis ko X-rays se link karta hai. [Q45]\n● CT scan multiple X-ray projections + computer reconstruction se cross-sectional images banata hai. [Q46]\n● Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen ne X-rays discover ki thi; source MCQ option “X-Ray Machine” ko accepted answer\ndeta hai. [Q47]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q47 — Discovery vs “X-Ray Machine”\n\n▸Historically Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen is credited with discovering X-rays (1895).\n\n▸Source MCQ wording/options “X-Ray Machine” ko accepted answer dete hain; factual concept ko discovery of X-rays ke\nroop me yaad rakho.\n Source coverage: Q1–Q47\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0357","t":"09 Sound","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sound Full Mind Map\n🔊 SOUND — FULL MIND MAP\n\nध्वनि\n· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Sound Propagation, Medium & Speed\n2. Reflection, Echo, Reverberation & Acoustics\n3. Pitch, Frequency, Wave Nature & Seismic Waves\n4. Audible, Ultrasonic & Infrasonic Sound — Applications\n5. Supersonic Motion & Mach Number\n6. Decibel, Loudness & Noise Pollution\n7. Sound Transmission, Musical Quality & Scale\n8. Television Signal Transmission\n1. Sound Propagation, Medium & Speed\n● General exam order: gases < liquids < solids. Isliye Nitrogen < Water < Steel; air me sound ≈330–331 m/s aur\nmetals/iron me isse kaafi faster hoti hai. [Q1–Q6]\n● Sound ek mechanical wave hai: propagation ke liye particles wala material medium chahiye. Solid, liquid aur\ngas me travel kar sakti hai, lekin vacuum me nahi. [Q7–Q10]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q1 & Q6 — Speed of Sound: Density Alone Is Not the Rule\n\n▸Source explanations “higher density\n faster sound” ko simple rule ki tarah bolti hain. General physics me speed\n⇒\nelasticity/stiffness aur density dono par depend karti hai (roughly √(elastic modulus/density)).\n\n▸Exam-level comparison solid > liquid > gas usually correct hai, but sirf density ko universal cause mat samajhna.\n2. Reflection, Echo, Reverberation & Acoustics\n● Concert/music hall me excessive reflection ko control karne ke liye sound-absorbing/soft surfaces use ki jati\nhain; hard flat surfaces strong reflections aur echo create kar sakti hain. [Q11–Q12]\n● Clear echo ke liye reflected sound ka delay ≈0.1 s chahiye. d = vt/2 se v≈330–340 m/s par reflector ki\nminimum distance ≈16.5–17 m aati hai. [Q13–Q14]\n● Wave relation v = fλ. Q15 me f=4 kHz aur λ=0.35 m\n v=1400 m/s; 3 km travel time ≈2.14 s.\n⇒\n [Q15]\n● Stethoscope me heartbeat sound tube ki inner walls se multiple reflection ke through ears tak pahunchti hai.\nLarge churches/buildings me repeated reflections se reverberation feel hota hai. [Q30, Q52]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q12–Q14 & Q52 — Echo vs Reverberation\n\n▸Echo me reflected sound original se sufficiently delayed hokar separately suna jata hai; reverberation me many\nreflections overlap karke sound ko prolonged banati hain.\n\n▸17 m value v≈340 m/s aur persistence of hearing ≈0.1 s ke around estimate hai; exact value temperature ke saath thodi\nchange ho sakti hai.\n3. Pitch, Frequency, Wave Nature & Seismic Waves\n● Pitch/shrillness ka primary determinant frequency hai: higher frequency\n higher pitch/shriller sound. Same\n⇒\nmedium me λ shorter hone par f higher hoti hai because v=fλ. [Q16–Q17]\n● Moon ke surface par atmosphere nahi, practically vacuum hai; isliye astronauts direct sound wave se ek-dusre\nko nahi sun sakte—radio communication use hota hai. [Q18–Q19]\n● Shorter flute/air-column higher natural frequency produce karta hai. Gases/liquids me sound mainly\nlongitudinal hoti hai; solids/rocks me longitudinal ke saath transverse elastic waves bhi propagate kar sakti\nhain. [Q20]\n● Earthquake me P-waves faster hoti hain aur seismograph par pehle record hoti hain; P\nlongitudinal/compressional, S transverse aur S-waves solids me hi propagate karti hain. [Q21]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q17 & Q20 — Frequency/Wavelength and Sound in Solids\n\n▸Shrillness directly frequency se decide hoti hai; wavelength ko direct determinant tabhi bolna safe hai jab propagation\nspeed fixed ho.\n\n▸“Sound is always longitudinal” gas/liquid context me useful simplification hai. Solids me shear elasticity ke karan\ntransverse elastic waves bhi possible hain.\n4. Audible, Ultrasonic & Infrasonic Sound — Applications\n● Human audible range ≈20 Hz–20 kHz. Ultrasound >20 kHz hota hai; infrasound <20 Hz. Source ke 10 kHz\nthreshold wale statements incorrect hain. [Q23–Q25]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sound Full Mind Map\n● Ultrasonic waves cleaning, insect control, medical treatment/diagnosis, automatic sensing, submarine/depth\ndetection jaise applications me use hoti hain. [Q22]\n● Sonography/ultrasonography fetus ki growth aur pregnancy imaging ke liye ultrasonic waves use karti hai.\n[Q26–Q27]\n● Bats ultrasonic pulses emit karke returning echoes se obstacle/prey ki position, direction aur size estimate\nkarte hain—echolocation. [Q28]\n● Q29 statement-set me source heart vibration ko infrasonic, Mach number ko speed-of-sound ratio aur\nultrasound ko >20 kHz mark karta hai; gas me sound fastest wala statement false hai. [Q29]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q29 — “Heart Vibrates at Infrasonic” Is Source-Specific\n\n▸Cardiac vibration/sound spectrum me very-low-frequency components ho sakte hain, lekin stethoscope se sunai dene\nwali useful heart sounds audible band components bhi rakhti hain.\n\n▸Exam me Q29 ka intended combination source ke\n\nअनुसारpreserve kiya gaya hai; universal statement ki tarah memorize\nna karein.\n5. Supersonic Motion & Mach Number\n● Mach number = object speed / local speed of sound. Mach >1 motion supersonic kehlata hai. [Q29, Q32]\n● Source supersonic jet emissions (especially NOx at high altitude) ko stratospheric ozone depletion potential se\nlink karta hai. [Q31]\n● Same Mach 1 par absolute aircraft speed local speed of sound ke equal hoti hai. Colder high-altitude air me\nsound speed lower hoti hai, so Mach 1 ka m/s value sea level se lower ho sakta hai. [Q32]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q32 — Mach 1 Is Not One Fixed km/h Value\n\n▸Mach number ratio hai, fixed speed nahi. Local temperature/medium change hone par speed of sound aur therefore Mach\n1 ka actual speed change hota hai.\n6. Decibel, Loudness & Noise Pollution\n● Decibel (dB) sound level/noise level express karne ke liye use hota hai. Sound intensity level logarithmic scale\npar report hota hai. [Q33–Q35, Q43]\n● Source reference values: normal conversation ≈30–60 dB, rustling leaves ≈20 dB, machine shop/instrument\nfactory around 100 dB. [Q36–Q38]\n● Source city-safe value 45 dB deta hai; continuous ≈80 dB+ exposure harmful batata hai, tolerable limit around\n85–90 dB aur optimum/normal level around 60 dB mention karta hai. [Q39, Q41–Q44]\n● India noise-rule matching: Residential 55 dB day, Silent zone 50 dB day, Commercial 65 dB day; Industrial\nstandard 75 dB day / 70 dB night. Source list me 70 dB diya hone se industrial ko 70 se match kiya gaya. [Q40]\n● Loudness perception amplitude/intensity se strongly related hai: larger amplitude\n larger intensity\n\n⇒\n⇒\ngenerally louder perceived sound. [Q45]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q39–Q40 — Noise Limits Depend on Context\n\n▸“Safe city noise = 45 dB” source-specific exam figure hai; modern health guidance often day/night, average exposure and\nsource category ke hisab se different limits use karti hai.\n\n▸Q40 me industrial 70 dB source matching NIGHT limit se align hota hai; Indian rule ka DAY industrial limit 75 dB hai.\n7. Sound Transmission, Musical Quality & Scale\n● Steel rail me sound air se faster travel karta hai, isliye rail-track blow pehle rail ke through aur baad me air ke\nthrough sunai de sakta hai—two arrivals. [Q46]\n● Solid → gas jane par sound speed generally decrease hoti hai. Air me temperature badhne se sound speed\nincrease hoti hai; aluminium me sound speed glass se greater hoti hai. [Q47]\n● Sound ek medium se doosre me enter kare to source-set frequency unchanged rehti hai; speed aur\nwavelength medium ke according change hote hain. [Q48]\n● Sitarist string tension adjust karke natural frequency/pitch tune karta hai. Same pitch/loudness ke bawajood\nsitar aur flute ko quality/timbre se distinguish kiya ja sakta hai. [Q49–Q50]\n● Linguistics me phoneme speech-sound ka basic contrastive unit hai. Physics ke sound-wave “basic unit” ke\nsense me ye term use nahi hota. [Q51]\n● Source diatonic-scale item octave repetition ko include karke 8 tones count karta hai; first Sa=256 Hz ho to\nupper-octave Sa≈512 Hz aur source Ni≈480 Hz deta hai. [Q53]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Sound Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q51 & Q53 — Linguistics / Musical-Scale Wording\n\n▸Phoneme “basic unit of sound” language/phonology ka term hai, physical sound wave ki SI/basic unit nahi.\n\n▸Seven distinct scale notes/swaras ko octave Sa repeat karne par sequence me 8 tone positions dikhte hain; source Q53\nisi counting convention ko use karta hai.\n8. Television Signal Transmission\n● Terrestrial television signals largely line-of-sight propagate karte hain; Earth curvature ki wajah se direct\nreception ek distance ke baad limited ho jati hai. [Q54]\n● Source ke according modern TV me audio-video synchronized start hote hain; old television sets me picture\nwarm-up delay ho sakta tha. [Q55]\n● Conventional analog TV broadcasting me picture/video signal amplitude modulation (AM) aur sound/audio\nsignal frequency modulation (FM) se transmit kiya jata tha. [Q56–Q57]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q56–Q57 — Analog TV Context\n\n▸Picture-AM + audio-FM rule conventional analog television broadcasting ke liye hai. Modern digital TV systems different\ndigital modulation/encoding schemes use karte hain.\n Source coverage: Q1–Q57\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0358","t":"10 Electric Current","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Electric Current Full Mind Map\n⚡ ELECTRIC CURRENT — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\nविद्युतधारा· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Current, Potential, Resistance, Power & Electrical Energy\n2. Dynamo, Motor, Battery & Energy Conversion\n3. Bulbs, Lightning, Earthing, Fuse & Household Safety\n4. CFL, LED, Fluorescent Tube & Lighting Technology\n5. Potential, Magnetic Field & Transformer\n6. AC–DC Generation, Rectifier & Power Use\n7. Earth Magnetism, Solar Power & Distributed Energy\n8. Pumped Storage & Wind Power\n1. Current, Potential, Resistance, Power & Electrical Energy\n● Current density J = I/A hota hai aur direction conventional positive-charge flow ki hoti hai; isliye current density\nvector quantity hai. Relative dielectric constant εr = ε/ε0 dimensionless hota hai. [Q1–Q2]\n● Charge q ko potential difference V se accelerate karne par gained energy E = qV. Electron ke liye magnitude\neV joule hota hai. [Q3]\n● Electrical energy: E = P×t. 1 unit = 1 kWh = 3.6×10⁶ J. Isliye 100 W×10 h = 1 unit; 15×200 W×24 h = 72 units;\n60 W×5 h×30 days = 9 units. [Q4–Q11]\n● Power relation P = VI. Ohm law se R = V/I. Household parallel circuit me same voltage par P = V²/R; dimmer\nbulb ka resistance larger hota hai, aur identical bulbs parallel me series se brighter hote hain. [Q12–Q16]\n● Parallel resistors ke liye 1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2. Resistor colour code brown-green-black = 15 Ω; 15 V par current\n1 A. Capacitive reactance Xc = 1/(2πfC), so frequency badhne par Xc ghatta hai. [Q17–Q19]\n2. Dynamo, Motor, Battery & Energy Conversion\n● Dynamo/generator mechanical energy ko electrical energy me convert karta hai; turbine mechanical rotation\nprovide kar sakta hai. Electric motor ulta conversion karta hai: electrical → mechanical. [Q20–Q26]\n● Dynamo electromagnetic induction par based hota hai. Battery electrochemical cells ke through stored\nchemical energy ko electrical energy me convert karti hai. [Q27–Q28]\n● Low-voltage operation me same required power/torque ke liye motor higher current draw kar sakta hai,\ncausing I²R heating. Faraday constant F ≈ 96485 C/mol electrons ek universal constant hai. [Q29–Q30]\n● Typical car lead-acid battery ≈12 V hoti hai; electrolyte H SO aur electrodes Pb/PbO hote hain; capacity\n₂\n₄\n₂\nampere-hour me. Ni-Cd batteries rechargeable applications me use hoti hain. [Q31–Q32]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q24 & Q27 — Idealisation / Principle Wording\n\n▸Q24 ka “no heat loss” ideal theoretical conversion ke context me hai; real motors me resistance, friction etc. se losses\nhote hain.\n\n▸Standard principle: generator/dynamo → electromagnetic induction; motor ka primary working principle current-carrying\nconductor par magnetic force/torque hai. Source Q27 me “Also D” note ko universal rule na samjhein.\n3. Bulbs, Lightning, Earthing, Fuse & Household Safety\n● Incandescent bulb filament tungsten ka hota hai because very high melting point; operating filament\ntemperature roughly 2000–2500°C range me hota hai. [Q33–Q37]\n● Lightning me enormous electrical energy hoti hai. Lightning conductor charge ko low-resistance path se\nground tak le jaakar building protect karta hai. [Q38–Q39]\n● Three-pin plug ka longest/thick earth pin ground terminal se connected hota hai; earthing shock-protection ke\nliye leakage current ko ground path deti hai. Same potential par connected bodies ke beech net current flow\nnahi hota. [Q40–Q42]\n● Fuse safety device hai: heating effect I²R par kaam karta hai; low melting point aur relatively high\nresistivity/resistance material excess current par melt karke circuit break karta hai. [Q43–Q46]\n● Current-carrying metal wire ka temperature resistance losses se rise karta hai; household wiring\nfundamentally parallel hoti hai. Black insulation older conventions me neutral wire ko denote kar sakti hai; dry\nhuman-body resistance order ≈10⁴ Ω source value hai. [Q48–Q51]\n● Source Q47 halogen lamp filament ko “tungsten + sodium alloy” mark karta hai. [Q47]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Electric Current Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q36 & Q47 — Source-specific Bulb Statements\n\n▸Ordinary incandescent lamp life ka dominant mechanism tungsten filament evaporation/thinning and hot-spot failure hota\nhai; source Q36 ke all-three reasons ko source-answer ke roop me preserve kiya gaya hai.\n\n▸Halogen lamp me filament normally tungsten hota hai aur bulb me halogen gas (iodine/bromine compounds) use hoti hai.\n“Tungsten + sodium alloy” source Q47 ko standard fact na samjhein.\n4. CFL, LED, Fluorescent Tube & Lighting Technology\n● CFL = Compact Fluorescent Lamp. LED electroluminescence principle par semiconductor junction se light\nproduce karta hai. LED generally CFL se longer-life aur more energy-efficient hota hai. [Q52–Q55]\n● Street-light comparison: sodium lamps nearly monochromatic yellow output aur broad emission de sakte hain;\nLEDs directional, colour-controllable aur typically longer-life technology hain. Source Q56 correct set 1 & 3 deta\nhai. [Q56]\n● Fluorescent tube low-pressure mercury vapour discharge + phosphor coating use karti hai; electrical\ndischarge UV generate karta hai aur phosphor visible white light emit karta hai. Source gas option “mercury\nand neon” diya hai. [Q57–Q59]\n● Incandescent bulbs me inert gas mixture such as argon/nitrogen commonly hota hai. Fluorescent choke\nstarting ke time high-voltage pulse provide karta hai aur operation me current limit karta hai. [Q60–Q61]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q59–Q61 — Tube-light Mechanism\n\n▸White light ka correct physical mechanism phosphor fluorescence hai; “molecules oscillating” source option ko literal\nmechanism na samjhein.\n\n▸Choke sirf “step-up transformer” nahi hai: fluorescent circuit me inductive ballast starting pulse aur current limiting dono\nroles karta hai.\n5. Potential, Magnetic Field & Transformer\n● Electric potential scalar quantity hai. P = VI, so V aur I dono double hon to power 4× ho jati hai. Wire\nresistance R = ρL/A; given length, diameter and resistivity ratios Q64 me both wires ka R equal nikalta hai.\n[Q62–Q64]\n● Same-radius charged drops coalesce karen: total charge nQ, new radius n^(1/3)r, therefore potential Vnew =\nn^(2/3)V. [Q65]\n● N-turn circular coil centre field B = μ NI/(2r); N=100, r=0.1 m, I=1 A gives 6.28×10 ⁴ T.\n₀\n⁻\n [Q66]\n● Transformer AC voltage ko step-up/step-down karta hai and electromagnetic induction par works; steady DC\npar normal transformer action nahi hota. Mobile charger front-end mains voltage ko lower suitable level me\nconvert karta hai. [Q67–Q70]\n6. AC–DC Generation, Rectifier & Power Use\n● Correct energy conversions: generator mechanical→electrical; motor electrical→mechanical. AC\ngenerator/dynamo alternating current produce kar sakta hai. [Q71–Q72]\n● Basic generator distinction: AC generator uses slip rings; DC generator uses split-ring commutator. Storage\nbattery charging ke liye DC required hota hai, isliye raw AC directly preferable nahi. [Q73–Q74]\n● Rectifier AC ko DC me convert karta hai. India me electricity consumption kWh me billed hoti hai aur grid\nfrequency 50 Hz hoti hai, 60 Hz nahi. [Q75–Q77]\n● Electric traction diesel pollution reduce kar sakti hai; source argument set me “diesel pollutes” strong\nargument hai. Typical appliance power ascending: fan < television < electric iron/press < electric kettle. [Q78–\nQ79]\n7. Earth Magnetism, Solar Power & Distributed Energy\n● Earth ka magnetic field conducting liquid outer core me circulating electric currents / geodynamo action se\ngenerated maana jata hai. [Q80]\n● Artificial satellites me solar/photovoltaic cells sunlight ko electrical energy me convert karte hain. Space-based\nsolar power concept orbit me collection aur Earth par wireless transmission propose karta hai. [Q81–Q82]\n● Photovoltaic technology light ko directly DC electricity me convert karti hai; solar thermal pehle heat generate\nkarta hai, phir heat-engine route se electricity. [Q83]\n● Solar power surface/submersible aur centrifugal/positive-displacement pumps dono chala sakti hai. Most\ncommon solar cells silicon semiconductor based hote hain. [Q84–Q85]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Electric Current Full Mind Map\n● Photovoltaic cell = solar cell; photovoltaic/photoelectric devices light energy ko electrical energy me convert\nkarte hain and satellites/digital systems me widely used hain. [Q86–Q90]\n● Net metering rooftop solar owner ko grid me export ki gayi electricity ka billing credit deta hai. Solar\ntariff/manufacturing claims source Q92 me both incorrect marked hain. [Q91–Q92]\n● Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) me rooftop PV, battery storage, biomass generators aur fuel cells jaise\nsmall/local resources include hote hain. [Q93]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q82 & Q92 — Policy/Data Claims Can Age\n\n▸SBSP “99% uninterrupted” aur national-goal wording source/exam context ka statement hai, general engineering\nguarantee nahi.\n\n▸Solar manufacturing rankings/tariffs time-sensitive policy facts hain; source answer ko question-year context me padhein.\n8. Pumped Storage & Wind Power\n● Pumped-storage hydropower do different-elevation reservoirs ke beech water move karke energy\nstore/release karta hai; essentially long-duration grid energy storage. [Q94]\n● Source Q95 India ko wind installed capacity me world rank 4 aur Gujarat ko high wind potential state batata\nhai; “400 GW installed” statement false marked hai. [Q95]\n● Source Q96 (question-time data) me Madhya Pradesh ko third-ranked wind-power state batana incorrect\nmarked hai; Gujarat/Tamil Nadu leading states ke roop me diye gaye hain. [Q96]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q95–Q96 — Wind Capacity Figures Are Time-sensitive\n\n▸Installed capacity, state shares aur rankings year-to-year change hote hain. In questions ke numerical/ranking claims ko\nsource-question date ke context me retain karein.\n Source coverage: Q1–Q96\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0359","t":"11 Conductivity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Conductivity Full Mind Map\n⚡ CONDUCTIVITY — FULL MIND MAP\n\nचालकता· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Conductors, Free Electrons & Electrical Conductivity\n2. Thomson Effect, Faraday Cage & Electronic Diodes\n3. Superconductivity & High-Temperature Superconductors\n4. Semiconductor Behaviour, Charge Carriers & Transistor Materials\n1. Conductors, Free Electrons & Electrical Conductivity\n● Conductor/\n\nसुचालकme large number of free electrons hote hain, isliye electrical resistance low aur current flow\neasy hota hai. Insulator me free charge carriers bahut kam hote hain. [Q1]\n● Given common metals me silver sabse achchha electrical conductor hai; source ranking repeatedly Silver >\nCopper > Aluminium > Iron ko support karti hai. Mica insulator hai. [Q2–Q4]\n● Salt water, orange juice aur lemon juice ions/acids-salts ki wajah se electricity conduct karte hain; isliye source\nQ5 me “None of the above” bad conductor answer hai. [Q5]\n● Lightning conductor ke liye copper iron se preferred hota hai because copper ki electrical conductivity higher\nhai aur atmospheric corrosion/rusting comparatively kam hota hai. [Q6]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q6 — Lightning Conductor Reasoning\n\n▸Primary exam point: copper high electrical conductivity + good corrosion resistance ki wajah se preferred hai.\n\n▸Source explanation me high thermal conductivity ko “energy loss less” se joda gaya hai; lightning protection ka core\nelectrical reason low-resistance conducting path hai.\n2. Thomson Effect, Faraday Cage & Electronic Diodes\n● Ek hi conductor ke different points par temperature gradient ho aur current flow kare, to reversible\nheating/cooling associated thermoelectric phenomenon ko Thomson effect kehte hain. [Q7]\n● Closed metallic car lightning ke time Faraday cage jaisi protection de sakti hai: excess charge outer\nconducting surface par redistribute hota hai aur cabin ko strong electric field se shield karta hai. [Q8]\n● Tunnel diode heavily doped semiconductor junction hota hai aur quantum tunnelling ki wajah se extremely fast\nswitching/high-frequency applications me use ho sakta hai; isme negative differential resistance region milta\nhai. [Q9]\n3. Superconductivity & High-Temperature Superconductors\n● Ideal superconductor critical temperature ke niche zero electrical resistance show karta hai aur Meissner\neffect me magnetic field ko bulk se expel karta hai; exam language me effective permeability ≈ zero li ja sakti\nhai. [Q10]\n● Room-temperature superconductivity economically revolutionary hoti, kyunki transmission losses aur\nrefrigeration/cooling cost dramatically reduce ho sakte hain. Present practical superconductors generally\nspecial low-temperature/pressure conditions demand karte hain. [Q11]\n● Source Q12 “highest superconducting temperature” ko disputed mark karta hai. Historical cuprate record\naround 133 K tha, jabki later high-pressure hydrides ne much higher reported transition temperatures show\nkiye; therefore question ko year/context ke saath padhein. [Q12]\n● High-temperature superconductors ka important class cuprate ceramic oxides hai—copper-oxide layers wale\nceramic materials ne conventional metallic superconductors se kaafi higher critical temperatures demonstrate\nkiye. [Q13]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q12 — Time-sensitive / Disputed Record\n\n▸Superconducting “highest temperature” record fixed static GK fact nahi hai; material, pressure aur experimental\nconfirmation ke saath record change hota raha hai.\n\n▸Source itself Q12 ko disputed (*) mark karta hai, isliye kisi ek option ko universal current fact na samjhein.\n4. Semiconductor Behaviour, Charge Carriers & Transistor Materials\n● Intrinsic semiconductor (Si/Ge) at absolute zero me conduction-band free carriers absent hote hain:\nconductivity → zero aur resistance ideally → infinite. [Q14, Q19]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Conductivity Full Mind Map\n● Semiconductors ka negative temperature coefficient hota hai: temperature badhne par more electron-hole\npairs generate hote hain, conductivity increases aur resistance decreases. [Q15–Q16]\n● Semiconductor current conduction electrons aur holes dono se hoti hai. Thermal excitation, impact ionization\naur photo-excitation electron-hole pairs generate kar sakte hain. [Q17–Q18]\n● Doping/impurity injection carrier concentration ko control karta hai—n-type me extra electrons, p-type me extra\nholes—but source Q18 ke context me ye electron-hole “pair generation” technique nahi maana gaya hai. [Q18]\n● Germanium aur silicon classic elemental semiconductors hain; transistor fabrication me dono use hue, lekin\nmodern electronics/ICs me silicon most common hai due to abundance, thermal advantages aur useful SiO ₂\noxide layer. [Q20–Q25]\n● Quartz aur ordinary ceramics given source context me insulators hain; Q23 ka correct semiconductor set\nSilicon + Germanium hai. [Q23]\n● Source Q26 ke according burnt coal/Jhama ash se recoverable germanium valuable semiconductor element\nhai, jise transistor/electronics applications se link kiya gaya hai. [Q26]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q23 & Q26 — Source-context Statements\n\n▸“Ceramics are not semiconductors” Q23 ke listed-material context ka answer hai; semiconductor ceramics bhi exist karte\nhain, so statement ko universal rule na banayein.\n\n▸Jhama export-ban/germanium statement old exam-policy context ka GK fact hai; policy status ko contemporary fact\nsamajhne se pehle question-year dekhein.\n Source coverage: Q1–Q26\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0360","t":"12 Nuclear Physics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nuclear Physics Full Mind Map\n⚛ NUCLEAR PHYSICS — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\nनाभिकीयभौतिकी· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Nuclear Discoveries, Particles & Radiation Detection\n2. Fusion, Fission, Chain Reaction & Nuclear Reactors\n3. Thorium, Uranium, Monazite & Nuclear Fuels\n4. Atomic/Hydrogen Bombs, Radioactivity & Half-Life\n5. Indian Nuclear Research, Kalpakkam & DAE Institutions\n6. Nuclear Power Stations, Locations & Capacity\n7. Moderators, Heavy Water, PHWR & Breeder Reactors\n8. Manhattan Project, Pokhran Tests & India’s Nuclear Doctrine\n9. CERN, ITER, IAEA, NPT, NSG & International Cooperation\n1. Nuclear Discoveries, Particles & Radiation Detection\n● Source matching me Meson–Hideki Yukawa, Positron–C.D. Anderson/U.F. Hess aur stellar-energy theory–\nH.A. Bethe diye gaye hain; transuranic-element synthesis ko Enrico Fermi se match karna source key ke\naccording incorrect hai. [Q1]\n● Nucleus ka splitting process fission hota hai, fusion nahi. Rutherford–Einstein historical assertion aur faster-\nthan-light microwave-photon claim source ke old/current-affairs style statements hain, standard established\nphysics se alag context me padhein. [Q2–Q4]\n● Cyclotron charged particles—given options me proton—ko accelerate karta hai; neutral neutron ko directly\naccelerate nahi karta. Gamma-emitting isotope detect karne ke liye scintillation counter useful radiation\ndetector hai. [Q5–Q6]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q1, Q3 & Q4 — Source-specific History/Claims\n\n▸Standard history me Yukawa meson theory/prediction se strongly associated hain; experimental discovery ko later\ncosmic-ray work se joda jata hai.\n\n▸Q3 ka Rutherford–Einstein wording source-key specific historical assertion hai; ise modern physics principle ke roop me\ngeneralize na karein.\n\n▸Q4 me faster-than-light microwave claim established violation of relativity nahi maana jata; exam source wording ko claim\nke roop me hi yaad rakhein.\n2. Fusion, Fission, Chain Reaction & Nuclear Reactors\n● Sun aur normal stars ki primary energy nuclear fusion se aati hai: hydrogen nuclei fuse hoke helium banate\nhain aur mass-defect energy release hoti hai. Star formation/early stages me gravitational contraction bhi\nenergy contribute kar sakta hai. [Q7–Q11]\n● Self-sustained fission chain reaction me har fission se multiple neutrons nikalte hain; moderator (e.g., graphite\nin source) fast neutrons ko slow karta hai. Har neutron necessarily next fission nahi karata, isliye control zaroori\nhai. [Q12]\n● Nuclear reactor ek controlled self-sustained chain-reaction device/atomic pile hai jo fission heat ko useful\nenergy me convert karta hai; source option me “molecular furnace” synonym accepted hai. [Q13]\n● Stars me energy generation fusion se associated hai, fission se nahi. Fusion reactors light nuclei ko join karte\nhain, typically Tokamak-type magnetic confinement aur extremely high temperature demand karte hain. [Q14–\nQ15]\n● Atom bomb aur fission reactor dono chain reaction use kar sakte hain, lekin reactor me reaction controlled hoti\nhai; bomb me rapid uncontrolled release hota hai. Radioactivity nuclear property hai, jabki hydrogen bomb ka\nmain principle fusion hai. [Q16–Q17]\n3. Thorium, Uranium, Monazite & Nuclear Fuels\n● Monazite rare-earth mineral hai aur thorium ka major source hai. Source Q18 me statements 1, 2 & 4\naccepted hain; India ke coastal placer deposits thorium-resource base ka important part hain. [Q18]\n● India ke context me thorium abundant strategic nuclear resource maana jata hai. Source questions thorium ko\nlarge reserve/important future fuel aur uranium ke comparison me abundance, energy-utilization potential aur\nwaste advantage se link karte hain. [Q19–Q21]\n● India me electricity generation ka major share historically coal-based raha; power reactors ko 60% enriched\nuranium ki requirement nahi hoti—civil reactors usually much lower enrichment ya natural uranium designs use\nkarte hain. [Q22]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nuclear Physics Full Mind Map\n● Nuclear-fuel family me uranium, plutonium aur thorium major names hain. Cadmium neutron absorber/control-\nrod material hai; chromium, helium, calcium aur lead given exam options me nuclear fuel nahi hain. [Q23–Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q18, Q21 & Q25 — Context Matters\n\n▸Monazite processing/export rule regulatory context aur question-year ke saath padhein; source key ko static universal\npolicy na samjhein.\n\n▸Thorium ka “less harmful waste” advantage fuel-cycle design par depend karta hai; source ne statement-set me ise\ncorrect maana hai.\n\n▸Q25 me “Radium” ko fuel-element side par chhoda gaya hai, lekin practical reactor fuel ke standard examples U/Pu aur\nfertile Th hain; option-based GK ko concept se alag rakhein.\n4. Atomic/Hydrogen Bombs, Radioactivity & Half-Life\n● Atomic bomb ka principle uncontrolled nuclear fission hai; classical fissile material enriched uranium\n(especially U-235) ya plutonium ho sakta hai. [Q28–Q29]\n● Hydrogen/thermonuclear bomb uncontrolled nuclear fusion par based hota hai—deuterium/tritium jaise light\nisotopes fuse karte hain. Edward Teller ko commonly “father of the hydrogen bomb” kaha jata hai. [Q30–Q32]\n● Enriched uranium me natural uranium ke comparison me U-235 proportion artificially increase kiya jata hai.\nUranium decay series ka stable end-product lead hai. [Q33–Q34]\n● Half-life rule: remaining fraction = (1/2)^n. 4-month half-life me 3/4 decay ke liye 2 half-lives = 8 months; 5-\nyear half-life ke 20 years baad 1/16 remains; 10-day half-life ke 20 days baad 3/4 decayed. [Q35–Q37]\n● Source Q38 me Zirconium non-radioactive option hai; tritium, astatine aur francium radioactive examples hain.\nPower generation ke liye fissile U-235 central isotope hai, while uranium metal broadly nuclear-power fuel\nresource hai. [Q38–Q40]\n● Radioactive nuclei spontaneously alpha (α), beta (β) aur gamma (γ) radiation emit kar sakte hain; source\nquestion “all of the above” accept karta hai. [Q41]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q38 — Radioactivity Shortcut\n\n▸“Atomic number >80\n radioactive” ek rough/unsafe shortcut hai, exact rule nahi. Exam me specific isotope/element\n⇒\nstability ko priority dein.\n\n▸U-235 fissile fuel isotope hai; U-238 largely fertile component hai aur natural uranium ka major fraction hota hai.\n5. Indian Nuclear Research, Kalpakkam & DAE Institutions\n● Control rods excess neutrons absorb karke chain reaction regulate karte hain; unke bina reactor reaction out\nof control ja sakti hai. Common absorber materials me boron/cadmium families aati hain. [Q42]\n● India ka first commercial atomic power station Tarapur Atomic Power Station (Maharashtra) hai. Dhruva,\nPurnima aur CIRUS Indian research reactors/BARC ecosystem se associated hain. [Q43–Q46]\n● Indian PHWR fleet natural uranium use kar sakti hai; source option Q47 U-238 ko choose karta hai because\nnatural uranium ka bulk U-238 hota hai, though sustained fission ke liye fissile U-235 fraction crucial hai. [Q47]\n● Shivanasamudra hydel power ke liye famous hai; Kalpakkam nuclear energy hub hai. IGCAR Kalpakkam,\nTamil Nadu me located hai. [Q48–Q50]\n● Kalpakkam FBTR plutonium–uranium mixed carbide fuel system se associated hai aur liquid sodium coolant\nuse karta hai. Source Q53 historical commission key me statements 1 & 3 accepted hain, so FBTR vs PFBR\nwording ko carefully distinguish karein. [Q51–Q53]\n● Harish-Chandra Research Institute Prayagraj me hai, Chennai nahi. Atomic Minerals Directorate, Heavy\nWater Board, Indian Rare Earths/IREL aur Uranium Corporation source ke according DAE framework se linked\norganizations hain. [Q54–Q55]\n● Heavy Water Board ka nuclear-program role D O production/supply hai. Source Q56 Trombay ko answer deta\n₂\n\nhai; actual heavy-water production network multiple Indian plant locations se historically associated raha hai.\n[Q56]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q45, Q47, Q53 & Q56 — Time/Source-sensitive\n\n▸Q45 “present BARC director” source ne itself outdated mark kiya hai; person-name ko question-year ke bina static fact na\nbanayein.\n\n▸Q47 me natural uranium ≈ mostly U-238, but U-235 hi fissile component hai—option wording aur physical role alag\nrakhein.\n\n▸Q53 FBTR/PFBR statements mixed wording use karte hain; source answer key ko historical context me preserve karein.\n\n▸Q56 Trombay answer source-specific hai; Heavy Water Board ke production facilities multiple sites par rahe hain."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nuclear Physics Full Mind Map\n6. Nuclear Power Stations, Locations & Capacity\n● Key station–state mapping: Kalpakkam–Tamil Nadu, Narora–Uttar Pradesh, Kakrapar–Gujarat, Trombay–\nMaharashtra. Rajasthan Atomic Power Station Rawatbhata (Rajasthan) me hai, Udaipur nahi; Kaiga Karnataka\nme hai, Tamil Nadu nahi. [Q57–Q59]\n● Given locations me Narora aur Kalpakkam atomic power stations hain; Ghatshila/Nangal ko nuclear power\nstation na samjhein. Narora source question me Seismic Zone IV se associated hai. [Q60–Q61]\n● Source-era “recently active” plant Q62 me Kaiga hai. Kudankulam Tamil Nadu me Russian collaboration ke\nsaath planned six-reactor site ke roop me source me diya gaya hai. [Q62–Q63]\n● Installed-capacity questions Q71–Q72 source/year context me Kudankulam ko highest answer dete hain.\nCapacity dynamic data hai, isliye exam year ko always note karein. [Q71–Q72]\n● India ke total electricity/energy mix me nuclear share wala Q73 source ne outdated/disputed mark kiya hai;\npercentage ko current-static GK ke roop me memorize na karein. [Q73]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q62 & Q71–Q73 — Date-dependent Data\n\n▸“Recently active”, installed capacity aur percentage share time-sensitive facts hain.\n\n▸Source key ko us exam-year snapshot ke roop me padhein; later expansions/commissioning se rankings change ho sakti\nhain.\n7. Moderators, Heavy Water, PHWR & Breeder Reactors\n● Heavy water (D O) neutron moderator ke roop me fast neutrons ko slow karta hai. Moderator ka purpose\n₂\nneutron energy reduce karke further fission probability ko suitable banana hai. [Q64]\n● Different reactor designs me ordinary/light water, heavy water aur graphite moderator ho sakte hain. Source\nQ65–Q66 me multiple correct answers mark kiye gaye hain; graphite ka role moderator hai. [Q65–Q67]\n● Fast breeder reactor electricity fission se produce karta hai, but defining feature ye hai ki fertile material se\nconsumed fissile fuel se zyada new fissile material “breed” kar sakta hai. [Q68–Q69]\n● NPCIL PHWR export-capacity Q70 source ne disputed mark kiya hai because cited 220 MWe + 540 MWe pair\noptions me absent tha; exact option ko force na karein. [Q70]\n8. Manhattan Project, Pokhran Tests & India’s Nuclear Doctrine\n● Manhattan Project World War II ka secret Allied/U.S.-led R&D program tha jisne first atomic weapons develop\nkiye. [Q74]\n● India ka 1974 Pokhran-I test “Smiling Buddha” code name se associated hai. Pokhran-II series 11 May 1998\nse start hui aur “Operation Shakti” naam se jani gayi; Pokhran Rajasthan me hai. [Q75–Q78]\n● Source Q79 India nuclear doctrine ke pillars me No First Use, unilateral test moratorium aur minimum credible\ndeterrence ko include karta hai. [Q79]\n9. CERN, ITER, IAEA, NPT, NSG & International Cooperation\n● Nuclear Security Summits UN ke formal aegis me periodic summit-series nahi the; International Panel on\nFissile Materials IAEA organ nahi, independent expert initiative hai. [Q80]\n● CERN world’s leading/large particle-physics laboratory ecosystem hai; acronym historical provisional council\nname se aaya. Dono facts true ho sakte hain but acronym-origin laboratory-size ka causal explanation nahi.\n[Q81]\n● ITER international fusion project Southern France (Cadarache) me hai. Success se participating India ko\nfusion-reactor technology/experience develop karne ka major advantage mil sakta hai. [Q82–Q83]\n● RTG miniature fission reactor nahi hota; radioactive decay heat ko thermoelectric conversion se electricity me\nbadalta hai, spacecraft systems me long-duration power ke liye use hota hai. Source Q84 statements 2 & 3\naccept karta hai. [Q84]\n● Source Q85 historical Indian nuclear-policy assertion me international inspection reluctance ko true aur “India\nwill not produce any nuclear bomb” ko false maanta hai. [Q85]\n● Treaty-year matching me SALT-II ko 1967 se match karna incorrect hai; source explanation 1979 signing\ncontext batata hai. NPT ko India discriminatory framework maankar sign nahi karta; NPT-recognized nuclear-\nweapon states listed set me China & France hain. [Q86–Q88]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Nuclear Physics Full Mind Map\n● NSG membership advanced nuclear trade/technology access facilitate kar sakti hai, but NPT membership\nautomatic nahi hoti. Source Q90 me Iran non-member option hai; 2008 NSG waiver ke baad France first civil-\nnuclear cooperation agreement signer diya gaya hai. [Q89–Q91]\n● India–IAEA Additional Protocol designated civilian nuclear facilities ko safeguards/inspection framework me\nlaata hai. Source Q93 safeguarded vs unsafeguarded reactors ko imported vs domestic fuel-supply separation\nse link karta hai. [Q92–Q93]\n● Source Q94 ICONS-2024 + Counter Nuclear Smuggling Team statements dono ko correct key karta hai; Q95\nIndia ke nuclear-field cooperation “Action Plan” ko Russia ke saath match karta hai. [Q94–Q95]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q84, Q90, Q94 & International Affairs\n\n▸RTG radioactive decay heat source hai—active chain-reaction fission reactor nahi.\n\n▸NSG membership/status aur conference-date/current-policy items time-sensitive ho sakte hain; source-year context\npreserve karein.\n\n▸Q94 ko source-key statement ke roop me note karein; date-specific international-event facts ko fresh exam me re-verify\nkarna best practice hai.\n Source coverage: Q1–Q95\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0361","t":"13 Computer and Information Technology Hinglish Corrected","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\n💻 COMPUTER & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY — FULL MIND\nMAP\n\n\n\n\nकंप्यूटरएवंसूचनाप्रौद्योगिकी· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Computer Origins, Hardware, Input/Output & E-waste\n2. Internet Basics, Networks, Wireless Technologies & VPN\n3. Indian Supercomputers, Computer Types, Y2K & Printers\n4. WWW, Protocols, Search Engines, Browsers & Network Models\n5. Malware, Cybersecurity & Operating Systems\n6. Binary Data, Memory Units, LAN, CPU & Hardware/Software\n7. Applications, Computer Generations, IC Chips, Modems & Memory\n8. Programming, Domains, Communication, AI & Digital Technologies\n9. Devices, E-Governance, Multimedia, Video, E-mail & Mobile ICT\n10. Mobile Platforms, Cybercrime, Data Security & Computer Networks\n11. IT Companies, Social Media, E-Commerce & Cloud Computing\n12. Web Acronyms, Logic Gates & Emerging Technologies\n1. Computer Origins, Hardware, Input/Output & E-waste\n● 1837 ke aasapaas Analytical Engine ki concept ki wajah se Charles Babbage ko widely father of computing maana jata\nhai. programmable mechanical computer ki concept ka invention karne ke liye Charles Babbage ko universally Father of\ncomputers maana jata hai. Charles Babbage ne Analytical Engine ko design kiya tha, jo modern digital computing ki\nfoundation hai, jisse unhe Father of computers ki title mili. Second World War ke dauran Lorenz cipher ko todne ke liye\nBritish codebreakers ke liye Colossus, electronic digital computers ki ek series develop ki gayi thi. [Q1–Q4]\n● Early electronic digital computer (jaise Colossus) Second World War ke dauran cryptanalysis purposes ke liye Britain me\ndevelop kiye gaye the. IBM System/360 1964 me announced ek highly successful mainframe computer family tha. Ise\nwidely solid-state logic technology use karke banaye jane wala pehla major digital computer system maana jata hai jo\nmodern IC-chip based architecture jaisa tha. motherboard computer ke andar central physical hub ki tarah kaam karta hai,\njisme iske basic circuitry components (circuitry components) hote hain. pen drive, ya USB flash drive ek highly portable,\nremovable secondary data-storage device ki tarah kaam karta hai. [Q5–Q8]\n● Ek mouse ek essential hardware input device ki tarah kaam karta hai, jise originally 1960 ke decade me Douglas\nEngelbart ne banaya tha. mouse ko strictly input device ke roop me classified kiya gaya hai, jise computer ko command\nbhejne ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Listed options me se, monitor, printer aur plotter ko strictly output device ke roop me\nclassified kiya gaya hai. plotter, printer aur monitor un hardware ke example hain jinka use computer-generated output ko\ndisplay karne ya present karne ke liye kiya jata hai. [Q9–Q12]\n● digital camera optical information capture karta hai aur ise system me feed karta hai, jo mainly input device ki tarah kaam\nkarta hai. computer ko data paas karne ke liye mouse, keyboard aur Scanner specially input tools ke roop me kaam karte\nhain. keyboard sabse primary (quintessential) input device bana hua hai, jisse users computer system me text aur\ncommand sequence enter kar sakte hain. keyboard ke saath, mouse modern computing setup me sabse zyada use kiye\njane wale input devices me se ek hai. [Q13–Q16]\n● Dr. Douglas Engelbart ne 1964 me pehle primitive computer mouse prototype develop kiya tha. Double-click karne se\ncomputer ki Central Processing Unit (CPU) ko immediate electrical signal jata hai. Modern computer keyboard usually ek\nstandard USB (Universal Serial Bus) Port ke through system unit se connect hote hain. computer systematically information\nke storage aur analysis ka kaam karta hai. Encryption aur Password use karke, ye data ki secrecy/privacy maintain karta\nhai. Iske alawa, network se jude system harmful malware ya virus ke attacks ke prati sensitive hote hain. Sabhi statement\ncomputing features ka accurate description karte hain. [Q17–Q20]\n● computer ghatakon me Beryllium, Cadmium, Chromium, Mercury aur Lead jaisee toxic metals hoti hain, jo hazardous e-\nwaste ka development karti hain. Heptaaklor ek chemical pesticide hai aur electronics se related nahi hai. Plootoniyam ek\nhighly radioactive radioactive material hai jo nuclear use ke liye hai, consumer electronics me normally used nahi hai. Isliye,\n(1, 2, 3, 5, 6) sahi group hai. [Q21]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q11 — Hybrid Input/Output Device\n\n▸Touch screen display output bhi deta hai aur touch input bhi leta hai; isliye 'not an output device' wording source me disputed hai.\n2. Internet Basics, Networks, Wireless Technologies & VPN\n● Internet ko vaishvik level par ek huge 'network of networks' ke roop me samajha jata hai. Ye standardized Internet Protocol\nSuite (TCP/IP) use karke countless private, academic, commercial aur government systems ko connect karta hai. Internet\nek huge, global digital infrastructure ki tarah kaam karta hai jo huge information resources ko seamless roop se share karne\nki suvidha ke liye computer ko connect karta hai. Digital Subscriber Line consumers ko brodabaind Internet data transmit\nkarne ke liye conventional copper ki Telephone laainon ke high voice-frequency band ka use karti hai. Historically, Dial-up\nService (Dial-up service) web connection ke sabse dheeme roop ke roop me jaanee jati hai, jo lagbhag 56 Kbps ki\nmaximum speed deti hai. Zyada modern faster options ke opposite, active hone par ye phone line par exclusive use kar\nletee thi. [Q22–Q25]\n● Kisi web domain ki primary pravishti ya greeting screen ko 'Home page' kaha jata hai. Ye visitors ko saaita ke deeper,\nspecific vargon tak le jane wali Instructionsikaa ki tarah kaam karta hai. Lagaataara, kisi core web Address ko hit karne"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\nwale kisi bhi browser dwara present main early point 'Home page' (Home page) hota hai. Standard network mapping\nsanrachanaaon me level, basa, Ring aur Tree topology shamil hain. ek 'Grid' network mapping specially aparanparaagat\nhai aur ise ek standard sthaneey ya vistrita-field topology classification nahi maana jata hai. Internet ki complex, huge\narchitecture ko anivaary roop se ek Tree topology (central basa baikabon ke through level network ko jodne wala ek\nhaaibrida) ke roop me taiyar kiya gaya hai. Ye leaaut nodsa ko hierarchical, manageable vargon me vibhaajit karke\npaimaane ka effective dhanga se prabandhan karta hai. [Q26–Q29]\n● Internet specially paiket Switchinga naam ka technology use karke data ko sthanaantarit karta hai. Badi fileon ko chhote\nblokon (\"paiketa\") me vibhaajit kiya jata hai, jo apne gantavy par phira se ikattha hone se pehle vyaktigat roop se ishtatam\nnetwork pathon ko neviget karte hain. Domain Name System (DNS) anivaary roop se Internet ki sanpark pustika (contact\nbook) ki tarah kaam karta hai. Ye pathaneey saaita naamon (jaise google.com) ko sankhyatmak IP paton me anuvaadit\nkarta hai jinka use computer system kanekt karne ke liye karte hain. Puraane IPv4 paton (jisme 32-Bit lanbaaee ka use kiya\ngaya tha) ki lessee ko hala karne ke liye, injeeniyaron ne IPv6 ka masauda taiyar kiya. IPv6 standard 128-Bit structure par\ndepend karta hai, jo web se jude devices ke liye adviteey sankhyatmak pahachaanakartaaon ke astronomical roop se bade\npoola ki allow karta hai. Blootooth ek sthaneey Protocols ki tarah kaam karta hai jo yooechaeph rediyo frequencyyon use\nkarke kai electronic devices (hedaphona, computer, phone) K Bcha fast, short-range ke vaayarales data brija banata hai.\n[Q30–Q33]\n● Major specific technical pahaloo opareting frequency hai. Blootooth strictly 2.4 geegaahartj aaeeesaem band ka use karta\nhai. Iske opposite, standard vaaee-phaaee setup ya to 2.4 geegaahartj spektram ya fast, kam bhida wale 5 geegaahartj\nband par chala sakate hain. Jaisaa ki pehle light daalaa gaya tha, basic rediyo prasaaran antara ye hai ki blootooth 2.4\ngeegaahartj tak hi seemit hai, jabki vaaee-phaaee network me 2.4 geegaahartj ya kam bhida-bhaada wali 5 geegaahartj\nfrequency par kaam karne ka Resilience hota hai. Digital ekeekaran ke liye ek important prayas me, Indian moreaariyon ne\nteka koraporeshan Google ke saath gathabandhan kiya. Is programme ka purpose kai paaragaman kendron ko taara se\njodana tha, jisne 2016 ki shuruaat me muphta Internet ka use start karne ke liye udghaatan test-sthala ke roop me\nmunbaee sentral ko chunaa. Laaee-phaaee (Li-Fi) digital Fileon ko fastee se shuttle karne ke liye timatimaate visible light\n(aksar standard elaeedee se) ke saath Router dwara use ki jane wali conventional rediyo waves ko pratisthapit karta hai.\n[Q34–Q37]\n● Statement B me government department ke sanbandh me ek tathyatmak truti hai: test information technology ministry ke\nunder ek major electronics braand aur akaadamik injeeniyaron ke saath organized kiya gaya tha, na ki information aur\nprasaaran ministry. Internet antararaashTreeya level par vividh network ko jodne wali huge architecture ki tarah kaam karta\nhai. Ye duniya bhar me apaara data sthanaantaran (data transfers) ko sanbhaalata hai, jo water ke neeche Cableon aur\nhigh elevation wale Communication Satelliteon ke ek complex sanyojan par depend karta hai. ek veepeeen (VPN) vyapak\npublic Internet par doora ke computeron ko jodne wali ek safe, enkripted surang (tunnel) banata hai. Ye karmachaariyon ko,\nexample ke liye, doora se hi apni Company ke banda Intranet system me safe roop se Login karne ki allow karta hai, opana\nweb par sanbhaavit chhipakar baaten sunane vaalon ko darakinaar karte hue. Portal application ek web-sulabha, intaraiktiv\ntools hai jo related aur asanbaddh donon application, sevaaen aur linka provide karta hai. [Q38–Q41]\n● Talaash (Talaash) Internet par ek Multimedia Portal hai aur saath hi ek optical kairektar rikagnishan (OCR) Software hai jo\ndevanaagaree me C-DAC dwara operated hai. [Q42]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q38 — Li-Fi Source Wording\n\n▸Source Q38 me multiple false statements mark hain. Li-Fi visible light ko data transmission medium ke roop me use karta hai;\nexam-year wording ko source context me padhein.\n3. Indian Supercomputers, Computer Types, Y2K & Printers\n● Software NAYAN ko C-DAC dwara cyber attacks aur data choree ke khataron se bachaav ke liye develop kiya gaya tha.\nSupercomputers ki ek series 'PARAM' ko Pune me located pragat sanganan development hub (C-DAC) dwara design aur\nasenbal kiya gaya tha. Indigenously developed pehle Indian Supercomputer ka naam Param-8000 (Param-8000) hai.\nParam (PARAM) India me C-DAC dwara design kiye gaye Supercomputers ki series ka naam hai. [Q43–Q46]\n● Vijay Bhatkar ko Indian Supercomputer ke janak ke roop me jana jata hai. Baarka (BARC) ke computer prabhaag ne\nsamaanaantar prasanskaran takaneekon ke basis par 1991 me Anupam (ANUPAM) project ke under supara computer ka\ndevelopment start kiya tha. ek Personal computer ki word ki lanbaaee usually 32 bits hoti hai jabki Supercomputer ke liye\nye 64 bits tak hoti hai. Supercomputer sabhi type ke computeron me sabse fast, sabse large aur sabse mahanga hota hai.\n[Q47–Q50]\n● 1996 ki sthiti ke according, world ka sabse fast computer ASCI reda tha, jiska linapaik (Linpack) demonstration 1\nteraaphlopa/sekanda (10 12 opareshan prati sekanda) se zyada tha. Question (2008) ki duration ke dauran, tivehiclehe-1e\n(Tianhe-1A) ko sabse fast computer maana jata tha. Climate aur jaivik systems me sanbhaavit parivartanon ki Calculation\nkarne ke liye China dwara Supercomputer 'maijika kyooba' banaya gaya hai. 31 maarcha, 2018 tak Pratyush India ka sabse\nfast Supercomputer tha. Iska unveil janavaree 2018 me Pune located Indian ushnadesheey weather science institute (IITM)\nme kiya gaya tha. [Q51–Q54]\n● India ki raashtrapati shreematee draupadee murmoo ne 13 aktoobara, 2022 ko aaeeaaeetee Guwahati me\nSupercomputer suvidha 'Param kaamaroopa' ka udghaatan kiya tha. KyooBits (qubits) par based ek suparaphaast\nQuantum computer ek hi question ke bahut saare sanbhaavit uttara ek saath de sakta hai, jo mastishk ki kaaryasystem ki\nnakala karta hai. Y2K baga, jise mileniyam baga bhi kaha jata hai, computereekrit systems ki Codesinga me ek samasy se\nrelated hai jise varsha 2000 ki shuruaat me duniya bhar me tabaahi machaane ka anumaan lagaay gaya tha. Ye question\nY2K baga (mileniyama baga) ko refer karta hai jo puraane computer system se related tha, jisme varsha 2000 ko proses\nkarne me samasyaen aa rahi thin. [Q55–Q58]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\n● Param (PARAM) supara computer ki ek series hai, jise C-DAC, Pune dwara design aur asenbal kiya gaya hai. Ye koi\nmissile nahi hai. W.L.L. Ka matalab Wireless in local loop (Wireless in Local Loop) hai. Aajakal jina computeron ka sabse\nzyada use kiya jata hai ve Microcomputer hain. Embeded system (embedded system) ek badi mechanical ya electrical\nsystem ke andar ek dedicated phankshan wala computer system hai. [Q59–Q62]\n● Semiconductor LASER (Semiconductor laser) thosa LASER hain jinka use LASER printer aur seedee/deeveedee pleyar\nme kiya jata hai. Deskatop printing (DTP) ke liye usually Laser printer ka use kiya jata hai. Daisy wheel printer ek early type\nka Impact printer hai jiska invention 1969 me hua tha. [Q63–Q65]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q52 — Fastest Supercomputer is Time-Sensitive\n\n▸Source itself Q52 ko outdated mark karta hai. 'World's fastest computer' ranking continuously change hoti hai, isliye\nexam-year/date ke saath hi memorize karein.\n4. WWW, Protocols, Search Engines, Browsers & Network Models\n● Www ka matalab World Wide Web hai. ek English inventoree computer scientist, Tim Berners-Lee ne CERN me kaam\nkarte hue 1989 me World Wide Web invent kiya tha. Tim Berners-Lee World Wide Web (www) ke inventor hain. Ye ek\ninformation system hai jo Internet par material share karne me saksham banaatee hai. Is system ke inventor 1989 me Tim\nBerners-Lee the. [Q66–Q69]\n● World Wide Web intaralinkd haaiparatekst dastaavejon aur other resources ki ek information system hai. World Wide Web\n(WWW) vaishvik level par computeron par rahane wali linka ki gayi information aur resources ka sanplanet hai, jise Internet\nke through eksesa kiya ja sakta hai. W3C ka full form World Wide Web Consortium hai. Kisi system ke computereekaran\nme, vitteey resources, ek ati-modern structure aur janaShakti ke prashikshan ke saath-saath ise karne ki ichchhaaShakti ki\nrequirement hoti hai. Isliye All the four essential hain. [Q70–Q73]\n● Cyberspace, Upload aur Modem information technology (inphoteka) aur networking se related shabdaavalee hain. Die\ngaye options me, Pinaka inphotek shabdaavalee se related nahi hai. Ye India me produced aur DRDO dwara developed ek\nmultiple rocket lonchar hai. Protocols, Login aur Archie sabhi information technology shabdaavalee ka hissaa hain.\nProtocols (Protocol) niyamon ka ek group hai jo data communication ko control karta hai. Ye communication devices K\nBcha ek samajhaute ko represent karta hai. [Q74–Q77]\n● Traansamission kantrol Protocols / Internet Protocol (TCP/IP) Internet par network devices ko aapasa me jodne ke liye use\nkiye jane wale communication Protocols ka ek soota (set) hai. IP pate (IP Addresses) OSI model ki Network Layer (leyara\n3) par kaam karte hain. OSI model ke saata-stareeya aarkitekchar me, leyara 1 phijikal leyara hai, leyara 2 data Link Layer\nhai, aur leyara 3 Network Layer hai. IoT communication ke chaara charan hain Perception Layer, Transport Layer, Network\nLayer aur Application Layer. Pratyek charan me information sthanaantarit karne ke liye vibhinn vaayarales takaneekon ka\nuse kiya ja sakta hai. [Q78–Q81]\n● Network vaataavaran me, 'Network Server' koi specific server category nahi hai, jaisa ki other option hain. Janka e-mail\nsandesh 'SPAM' (spam) sandesh hote hain jo avaanchhit (unsolicited) hote hain aur service dwara philtar kiye jate hain.\nAvaanchhit janka e-mail (unsolicited junk e-mails) ka description karne ke liye generally 'SPAM' ka use kiya jata hai. 'SPAM'\ncomputer aur Internet se related hai. SPAM Internet par ek hi sandesh ki kai pratiyon ki baadha hai, jo un Peopleon par\nsandesh thopane ka prayas hai jo anyath ise mila karna nahi chunenge. [Q82–Q85]\n● E-mail Bombing neta durupayog ka ek roop hai jisme melaBox ko ovaraphlo karne ya server ko prabhaavit karne ke\nprayas me kisi pate par badi amount me e-mail bhejana shamil hai. Dakadakago ek Search engine hai jo users ki privacy\nko praathamikata dene ke liye kaaphee famous hai. Orkut koi Search engine nahi hai. Ye Google ke svaamitv wali aur\noperated ek Social Networking website thi jise banda kar diya gaya hai. Baidu INC. ek Chinaee web service Company hai jo\nChinaee Search engine sahita kai sevaaen provide karti hai. [Q86–Q89]\n● Binga (Bing) ek web Search engine hai jiska svaamitv aur sanchaalan Microsoft ke paas hai. Ise 2009 me launch kiya\ngaya tha. Karentalee (Kurrently) ek nihshulk soshal meediy Search engine hai jo Twitter aur Facebook etc. Jaise soshal\nmeediy pletaphorm se vaastavik time (real-time) ke parinaam provide karta hai. Yahoo, Google aur emaesaen Internet sites\n(mainly web Portal aur Search engine) hain. Die gaye options me se Yahoo web braaujar nahi hai, ye ek web Portal aur\nSearch engine hai. [Q90–Q93]\n● Google Chrome (Chrome), Google dwara developed ek lokapriy web browser hai. Ise pehli baar 2008 me jaaree kiya gaya\ntha. Web browser ek software application hai jiska use World Wide Web par information tak reach ke liye kiya jata hai.\nOpera, Vivaldi aur Mozilla Firefox web browser ke example hain. ek web krolara, jise kabhi-kabhi Web Spider ya\nspaaidarabot kaha jata hai, ek Internet bota hai jo World Wide Web ko systematically braauj karta hai, aama taur par web\nindeksing ke purpose se. WiMAX ka matalab varlda vaaida intaraoparebilitee phora maaikrovev eksesa hai. Ye ek\ntelecomee technology (communication technology) hai jiska purpose long-range par vaayarales data provide karna hai.\n[Q94–Q97]\n● Analog, Binary code, Chip aur MODE sabhi kisi na kisi roop me computer se jude word hain. Isliye, ye question\nContentionita maana ja sakta hai kyonki sabhi computer shabdaavalee ka hissaa hain. [Q98]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q98 — Ambiguous Computer Terminology\n\n▸Source Q98 disputed hai; analog/digital, binary code, mode aur chip sab computer-related terms/context me aa sakte hain.\n5. Malware, Cybersecurity & Operating Systems\n● computer ke field me VIRUS ka meaning 'Vital Information Resource Under Siege' (Vital Information Resources Under\nSiege) hai. computer virus ek vinaashakaaree Software programme ya Codes ka tukada hai jo users ki information ke binaa\ncomputer par loda ho jata hai aur unki ichchha ke viruddh chalata hai. computer virus ek aisaa programme hai jo apni"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\nnakala bana sakta hai aur ek computer se doosare computer me phaila sakta hai, jo usually jaanaboojhakar damage\npahunchaata hai. computer me phailane wala virus ek vinaashakaaree computer programme (mailaveyara) hai jo human\nProgrammer dwara data ya software ko damage pahunchaane ke liye likhaa jata hai. [Q99–Q102]\n● computer virus ek type ka durbhaavanaapoorn software programme hai, jise nishpaadit kiye jane par, other computer\nprogramon ko sanshodhit karke aur apanaa Codes daalakar khuda ki nakala (replicate) kar sakta hai. computer virus ek\nDestructive programme hai jise kaaryaAbility ko baadhit karne ya data churaane ke liye engineer kiya gaya hai. computer\nvirus ka meaning Destructive programme se hai jo computer system ko damage pahunchaata hai. Aisaa programme jisme\nother programon ko sankramit karne, apni pratiyan banane aur other programon me phailane ki Ability hoti hai, virus kehlat\nhai. Worm (worm) network me freelance roop se phailate hain, jabki virus usually other programme Fileon ko sankramit\nkarte hain. [Q103–Q106]\n● Trojan ek type ka malware hai jo khuda ko ek general ya vaidha programme ke roop me chhipaakar users ko\ndurbhaavanaapoorn software daaunalod karne ke liye dhokha deta hai. Firewall ek aisee system hai jise kisi private\nnetwork par anadhikrit access (unauthorized access/attack) ko rokane ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Ye security\nmaanadandon ko pooraa nahi karne wale traiphik ko bloka karta hai. Phaayaravol ek network security device hai jo aane\nwale aur jane wale network traiphik ki nigaraanee karta hai. Iska main purpose To block unauthorized access to a network\nhai. Michael Angelo pehle virus me se ek tha jise MS-DOS ko sankramit karne ke liye design kiya gaya tha. Ise\npunarjaagaran Artkaara Michael Angelo ke janmadin 6 maarch ko active hone aur Hard Drive par data ko nashta karne ke\nliye programme kiya gaya tha. [Q107–Q110]\n● Staksanet (Stuxnet) ek computer Worm (durbhaavanaapoorna programme) hai jo industrial control systems ko lakshit\nkarta hai. Ise specially eeraan ke bushahar nuclear energy sandevice me nuclear senTreephyooja ko damage\npahunchaane (saboteja) ke liye design kiya gaya tha. Vaanaakraaee (WannaCry) aur petya (Petya) itihaas ke sabse bade\ncyber attacks (rainasamaveyara) me se do hain jinhone world bhara ke kai computer network ko prabhaavit kiya.\n'itaranalabloo' ek Cyberattacks ka eksaploit tha jiska use vaanaakraaee hamale me kiya gaya tha. Ijaraail ke NSO group ne\npegaasas Spyware developed kiya hai, jo world ke sabse aakraamak Spyware me se ek hai. Ye device users ki information\nke binaa gupta roop se mobile phone jaise devices me ghusapaith kar sakta hai. MS-DOS (Microsoft Disk Operating\nSystem) originally Tim paitarasan dwara likhaa gaya tha aur agasta, 1981 me Microsoft dwara pehli baar jaaree kiya gaya\ntha. [Q111–Q114]\n● MS-DOS gaira-graaphikala command-line (command-aadhaarita) intaraphes (CLI) wala An operating system hai. Isme\nusers computer ko Instructions dene ke liye text command taaipa karte hain. Microsoft dwara 'vindoja 3.0' 1990 me jaaree\nkiya gaya tha. Isane Graphical User Interface ko kaaphee behatar banaye tha. Vindoj Operating System (Windows\noperating system) Software development Company Microsoft dwara develop kiya gaya hai. Vindoj Software Microsoft\ndwara develop kiya gaya hai. options me Microsoft nahi hai, isliye 'None of the above' sahi hai. [Q115–Q118]\n● 'UNIX' ek computer Operating System hai jo maltee-yoojara (kai users ko ek saath kaam karne ki suvidhaa) vaataavaran\nprovide karta hai. Ise 1969 me AT&T ke bela laibsa me develop kiya gaya tha. UNIX An operating system hai jiska use\nserver aur kaaryasthal donon me widely kiya jata hai. UNIX Operating System 3 main bhaagon se bana hai: Kernel, shela,\naur users command va application. GNU muphta Software ka ek vyapak sanplanet hai, jiska use Operating System ke roop\nme ya other Operating System ke saath bhaagon me kiya ja sakta hai. [Q119–Q122]\n6. Binary Data, Memory Units, LAN, CPU & Hardware/Software\n● computer Memory Semiconductor (praaimaree Memory jaise RAM/ROM), maignetik (jaise Hard disk, Floppy Disk), ya\noptical (jaise seedee aur deeveedee) ho sakatee hai. computer Memory ka main work data aur information ko sanplaneteet\nkarna hai. Bit ya Binary Digit computer Memory ki sabse chhoti ikaaee hai. Baainaree ek nanbaRing yojana ka description\nkarta hai jisme pratyek anka ke liye kevala do sanbhaavit maana hote hain: 0 and 1. Dashamalav number ko baainaree me\nbadalane ke liye, aapa plesa vailyoo ka use kar sakte hain: 8, 4, 2, 1. [Q123–Q126]\n● Binary Language me do anka hote hain: 0 and 1. Ye computer dwara samajhee jane wali machine language hai. Yadi kisi\nCodes ka development isliye kiya jata hai ki jab hama kisi anka ke 4-Bit Codes represent me 1 ko 0 aur 0 ko 1 se badalate\nhain, to hamen usa anka ka 9 ka poorak (complement) milta hai, ise sva-pooraka Codes (self-complementing code) kaha\njata hai. Baainaree ankaganit me, 1 + 0 = 1, 0 + 1 = 1, 0 + 0 = 0 hota hai. ek Byte digital data ki ek ikaaee hai jisme usually\naatha Bits (baainaree anka) hote hain. [Q127–Q130]\n● 8 bits ke group ko Byte kaha jata hai. Dhvehicle den ki 4 bits ke group ko Nibble kaha jata hai. ek Byte 8 bits ke baraabar\nhota hai. ek Byte me 8 bits hote hain. [Q131–Q134]\n● Ek Byte me 8 bits hote hain, aur 1 Kilobyte (KB) me 1024 bytes hote hain. Bit (Binary Digit ka short roop) computer me\ndata ki sabse chhoti ikaaee hai. ek Bit ka single baainaree maana hota hai, ya to 0 ya 1. computer me kisi word (word) ki\nlanbaaee ko usually Bits me maapaa jata hai (jaise, 32-Bit ya 64-Bit aarkitekchara). computing me, 1024 Kilobyte (KB)\ntheeka 1 megabyte (MB) ke baraabar hota hai. [Q135–Q138]\n● Choonki computer system baainaree svaroopan (aadhaara 2) ka use karte hain, 1 Kilobyte 2 10 Bytesa me anuvaadit hota\nhai, jo ki 1024 bytes hai. 1 Kilobyte bilkul 1024 bytes ke baraabar hota hai. Listed ikaaiyon me, KB (Kilobyte) sabse small\nhai. PraGati isliye hai: Kilobyte (KB), Megabyte (MB), Gigabyte (GB), aur phira Terabyte (TB). [Q139–Q142]\n● Memory ikaaiyon ka sabse chhote se sabse bade tak sahi krama hai: Bit (F) -> Byte (B) -> Kilobyte (A) -> Megabyte (C) ->\nGigabyte (E) -> Terabyte (D). 1 gigabyte 1024 Megabyte (MB) ke baraabar hota hai, na ki 1024 Kilobyte. (1 megabyte =\n1024 Kilobyte). Isliye, option (C) me sanbandh incorrect hai. 1 megabyte (MB) Memory 1024 Kilobyte (KB) ke baraabar hoti\nhai. 1 megabyte = 1024 Kilobyte. [Q143–Q146]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\n● Ek Megabyte me 1,048,576 Bytesa hote hain. Isliye, ek miliyan Bytesa lagbhag ek Megabyte ke baraabar hai. Word MB ka\nuniversally Mega Bytes ke short roop me use kiya jata hai. Standard yooniCodes mapping sanrachanaatmak roop se\npratyek varna ko 16 bits (ya 2 Bytesa) use karke darshaatee hai, jisse ye practical roop se sabhi vaishvik bhaashaaon ke\nvarnon ko samaayojit karne me saksham ho jata hai. Quantum computing me, information ke basic hisse ko 'kyooBit'\n(kvaantama Bit ka short roop) kaha jata hai, jo klaasikal computing me use kiye jane wale standard 'Bit' ke opposite hai.\n[Q147–Q150]\n● 'kyooBit' word specially Quantum computing ke field se related hai. Ye ek do-raajya (two-state) kvaantama-maikenikala\nsystem ki tarah kaam karta hai, jo kvaantam suparapojishan ki wajah se fastee se Calculation karne ki allow karta hai..Net\nphremavark vaastav me Microsoft dwara mainly vindoj ke liye develop kiya gaya tha. ek Local Area Network specially\nbhaugolik roop se seemit field jaise ek kaaryalay bhavana, skoola ya ghara ke andar computeron ko connect karta hai, jo\nek special private network ke roop me poori tarah se kaam karta hai. LAN Local Area Network ka standard short naam hai.\n[Q151–Q154]\n● Eetharanet Local Area Network ke through data ko physical roop se transmit karne ke liye widely apanaay gaya Protocols\nstandard provide karta hai. database shabdaavalee me, ek 'pheelda' anivaary roop se information ki ek specific category\n(Category of information) ko refer karta hai (jaise 'naam' ya 'aayu' jaisee specific data Specialtaaon wali taalika me ek\nkolama). Arithmetic Logic Unit CPU (CPU) ke andara essential module hai jo sabhi mathematics sameekaranon aur Logical\ntulana nirnayon ko sansaadhit karta hai. computer science me, ALU ka meaning 'Arithmetic Logic Unit' (Arithmetic Logic\nUnit) hai. [Q155–Q158]\n● CD 'Compact Disk' (Compact Disc) ka standard short naam hai, jo ek Optical storage maadhyam hai. Magnetic tape aur\nMagnetic disc (jaise Hard disk drive) donon hi hardware tatva hain jo deerghakaalik use ke liye digital data ki enough\namount ko banaye rakhne ke liye famous hain. Isliye donon sahi hain. Bloo-re Disc (BD) ek digital optical Disc data storej\nphormet hai jise deeveedee (DVD) phormet ko badalane ke liye design kiya gaya tha. Beedee haaee dephinishan (HD)\nvideo stora karta hai, jabki deeveedee standard (SD) video ka sammeaningn karta hai. (statement 1 sahi hai). Compiler\ncomputer hardware nahi hai. Ye ek special Software programme hai jo kisi special programming language me likhe gaye\nstatements ko proses karta hai aur unhe machine language ya \"Codes\" me convert karta hai jiska use computer ka\nProcessor karta hai. [Q159–Q162]\n● Die gaye options me Assembler ek hardware nahi hai. Ye ek Software programme hai jo basic computer Instructionson ko\nleta hai aur unhe Bits ke paitarn me convert karta hai jiska use computer ka Processor apne basic functions ko karne ke liye\nkar sakta hai. computer hardware computer ke un physical ghatakon ko refer karta hai jinhen hama dekha aur chhoo sakate\nhain (jaise monitor, CPU, keyboard, mouse, printer aur Scanner). Excel Microsoft dwara developed ek Application Software\nhai. An operating system (jaise vindoj ya Linux) hardware nahi hai; ye ek system Software programme hai. printer, mouse\naur keyboard physical hardware divaais hain. Compiler computer System Software ka ek hissaa hai. Ye programming\nlanguage ko machine level ki language me convert karta hai jise computer hardware dwara samajha jata hai. [Q163–Q166]\n● Internet explorer ek maalikaanaa, kloja-sorsa (closed-source) Software hai jise Microsoft dwara develop kiya gaya hai.\nLinux, Open office aur Chromium besa (jisakaa Google Chrome use karta hai) ki opana-sorsa Availability hai. Cloud\ncomputing me, teen main sarvatr recognition mila freelance service paraten (service layers) hain: Software eja e sarvis\n(SaaS), pletaphorm eja e sarvis (PaaS), aur inphraastrakchar eja e sarvis (IaaS). \"hardware eja e sarvisa\" originally IaaS ke\nunder aataa hai aur ise apne aapa me ek freelance main service layer ke roop me classified nahi kiya gaya hai. Floppy Disk\nme ek small saa indeks hola hota hai jiska use phormeting aur reeding functions ke dauran sanplaneteet data sektaron ke\nshuruaatee point ko refer karne ke liye kiya jata hai. computing aarkitekchar me, ek intarapt rikvest (IRQ) Processor ko\nbheja gaya ek hardware signal hai jo chala rahe programme ko asthayee roop se rokata hai aur iske bajaay ek special\nprogramme ko chalaane ki allow karta hai. [Q167–Q170]\n● Operating System (OS) wo Software hai jo computer hardware, Software resources ka prabandhan karta hai aur computer\nprogramon ke liye general sevaaen provide karta hai. Ye anivaary roop se computer ke basic functions ko control karta hai,\njaise ki Memory prabandhan aur work shedyoolinga. Central Processing Unit ko computer ke mastishk ke roop me jana jata\nhai jahaan moreaansh important Calculationen aur tarka sanchaalan (logic operations) hote hain. Central Processing Unit\ncomputer ka sabse important hissaa hai. Yahaan computer mila information ya data ka analysis karta hai. CPU ka full form\nCentral Processing Unit (Central Processing Unit) hai. [Q171–Q174]\n● CPU ka full form Central Processing Unit hai. CPU ka meaning Central Processing Unit hai, Control Processing Unit nahi.\nOther options (e-mail, WWW, ALU) ke statement sahi hain. Kantrol unit (CU) programme Instructionson (instructions) ko\ndiCodes karta hai aur computer system ke sabhi functions ko radioactive aur Instructionsita karta hai. [Q175–Q177]\n7. Applications, Computer Generations, IC Chips, Modems & Memory\n● Word Processor ek Application software hai jiska use mainly text-aadhaarita Documents banane, sanpaadit karne aur\npraaroopit karne ke liye kiya jata hai. Microsoft Word ek Word Processor hai, jo ise users ko Documents taaipa karne,\nphormet karne aur sahejane jaise specific work karne me help karne ke liye design kiya gaya ek application software\nbanata hai. MS Word (emaesa Word) Microsoft dwara banaya gaya ek widely use kiya jane wala Word Processing\napplication hai. Ise paathy information (textual info) ko banane, sansaadhit karne aur prakaashit karne ke liye design kiya\ngaya hai. Word Processing, spredasheet Processing aur photo editing ve sabhi programme hain jo users ko specific\nintaraiktiv work karne me help karne ke liye design kiye gaye hain. Isliye, ve Application Software ke example hain. [Q178–\nQ181]\n● Specific upayogakartaa-end (user-end) functions ko pooraa karne ke liye Word Processor (jaise MS Word) aur\nspredasheet (jaise MS Excel) ka use kiya jata hai, jisse ve Application Software bana jate hain. Excel jaise spredasheet\nprogramme me, data pravishti ke liye moola ikaaee ko 'Cell' (cell) kaha jata hai. Ye ek pankti (row) aur ek kolama ke\nchauraahe se banata hai. Edoba photoshop (Adobe Photoshop) mainly ek rekhaapunj Graphics sanpaadak hai. Ise ek"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\nmajor Graphics Software ke saath-saath Multimedia software bhi maana jata hai kyonki iska use chhavi sanpaadan aur\nMultimedia applicationon ke liye Graphics banane ke liye bade paimaane par kiya jata hai. Isliye option Both (A) and (B)\nsahi maane gaye. computing me, file (File) information sanplaneteet karne ke liye ek resource hai. ek Word Documents\n(.doc/.docx), ek video (.mp4), aur ek MP3 audio (.mp3) sabhi fileon ke specific praaroop (format) hain. [Q182–Q185]\n● .MP3 digital audio ke liye ek famous audio Codesinga praaroop hai. Ye video data nahi le jata hai. MPEG ka full form\nMoving Picture Experts Group (Moving Picture Experts Group) hai. Ve ISO aur IEC ke under ek work group hain jo audio\naur video sanpeedan aur prasaaran ke liye standard established karne ke prabhaaree hain. Pehli generation ke\ncomputeron me Vacuum tubes ka istemaal kiya gaya tha. Doosri generation ke computer Vacuum tubeson se hatakar\nthosa-state Transistors (transistors) ka use karne lage, jisse ve chhote, fast aur zyada worldsaneey ho gaye. Maulik\nelectronic component jisne teesri generation ke computeron ko define kiya, wo Integrated circuit (IC) tha. Is technology ne\nkai chhote Transistors ko ek Silicon Chip par rakha. [Q186–Q189]\n● computeron ko unke vartamaan chhote shape me siCodesne ki Ability Integrated circuit (IC) chips ke invention aur use se\nsanbhav hui, jo ek chhote se field me laakhon ya arabon Transistors paika karte hain. Integrated circuit (IC) chips\nSemiconductor material, sabse zyada baara Silicon use karke built hote hain, kyonki unke electrical properties me accurate\nroop se herapher kiya ja sakta hai. Silicon IC chips ke development me use kiya jane wala major ardhachaalak matter hai\nkyonki ye highly sthira, prachur amount me hota hai aur ise aasaanee se dosha-free vephars me banaye ja sakta hai. ek\ncomputer Chip originally ardhachaalak material ka ek small tukada hai, jo mainly refined A thin layer of silicon use karke\ntaiyar kiya jata hai. [Q190–Q193]\n● IC Chip banane me shamil sabsatret aur baad ki starit doping processon me maulik roop se Silicon (aur iske oksaaida) ka\nuse kiya jata hai. IC chips Silicon ke bane hote hain, jo sarkiTree ke liye ardhachaalak basis ke roop me kaam karte hain.\nJaisaa ki kai questionon me establish kiya gaya hai, Silicon IC chips ke liye standard aadhaarabhoot material hai.\nIntegrated circuit ke andara Semiconductor Chip Silicon ki banee hoti hai. [Q194–Q197]\n● Silicon ne kraanti laa dee hai aur modern computing age ke dauran computer chips ke production me lagaataar define\nmatter bana hua hai. (nota: Gallium Arsenide ka use kuch special haaee-speeda chips me hota hai, lekin widely Silicon hi\nmain basis hai aur is question ke context me Silicon correct answer maana gaya hai). Integrated circuits (ICs) ko unke\nekeekaran paimaane dwara classified kiya jata hai - jiska anivaary roop se meaning hai Chip par paika kiye gaye\nTransistors ka ghanatv ya number. ek Modem (modulator-demodulator) ek hardware divaais hai jo digital praaroop se data\nko Analog praaroop me (Telephone laainon par traansamission ke liye) aur Analog se digital me (data mila karne par)\nconvert karta hai. Modem (Modulator/Demodulator ka short roop), ek hardware divaais hai jo digital signals into analog\nsignals aur analog signals into digital signals parivartit karke computer ko Telephone laainon par information bhejne aur\nmila karne ki allow karta hai. [Q198–Q201]\n● Ek Modem modyooleshan (digital data ko Analog signal me parivartit karna) aur deemodyooleshan (aane wale Analog\nsignal ko vaapas digital data me parivartit karna) donon ke liye jimmedaar hai. ek Modem digital computer signal aur\nconventional Telephone laainon dwara use kiye jane wale Analog signal K Bcha pula ki tarah kaam karta hai, jisse vaishvik\ndata communication ki anumati milti hai. Modem wo device hai jise specially Internet aur network eksesa ke liye computer\n(jaise Microcomputer) ko Telephone laainon se jodne ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Choonki data do dishaaon me bahata\nhai, isliye ek Modem ko computer se digital output ko phone line (modyooleshana) ke liye Analog signal me badalana hota\nhai, aur aane wale Analog signal ko computer ke liye vaapas digital data (deemodyooleshana) me badalana hota hai.\n[Q202–Q205]\n● Modem wo accurate device hai jo standard Telephone laainon par computer data ko traansamitebal aavegon (impulses)\nme anuvaad karne ke liye jimmedaar hai. Modem ka primary work computer (jo Digital signal ka use karta hai) aur ek\nTelephone line (jo Analog signal le jata hai) K Bcha ek intaraphes ke roop me work karna hai. Phone laainon ke through\nFAX aur e-mail bhejne me prayukt information signal ke roop me Analog aur digital donon signal shamil hote hain, kyonki\ncomputer data ko digital roop se proses karte hain lekin Telephone laainen ise Modem ke through Analog vevaphorm me\ntransmit karti hain. Decoding wo essential process hai jisadwar riseevar source dwara bheje gaye enCodeseda prateekon\nya signalon ka anuvaad aur vyakhy karke vaapas samajhne yogya information me badalt hai. [Q206–Q209]\n● Router, Switch aur haba sabhi networking divaais hain jinka use computer ya network ko ek saath jodne ke liye kiya jata\nhai. ek Router sabse aama networking divaais hai jo specially vibhinn computer network (Internet par traiphik nideshak ke\nroop me work karna) K Bcha data paiket ko agreshit karta hai. ek Repeater ek networking component hai jo network ki\nlanbaaee badhaata hai. Ye ek signal mila karke aur ise aage badhane se pehle ise badhaa/punarjeevita\n(amplifying/regenerating) karke receive karta hai, jisse long-range par signal ke lessjor hone ko rokaa ja sakta hai.\nCellerona, pentiyam aur core sabhi intela dwara built computer Processor (CPU) ke highly lokapriy family (seereeja) hain.\n[Q210–Q213]\n● ROM ka meaning reeda-onalee Memory (Read-Only Memory) hai. ek baara jab data ko ROM Chip par likha diya jata hai,\nto ise generally badala ya hataay nahi ja sakta hai aur kevala padhaa ja sakta hai. ROM (reeda-onalee Memory) ko\ncomputer ki sthayee internal Memory maana jata hai. computer banda hone ke baad bhi ROM me data ya information\nnashta ya mitaaee nahi jati hai. Gaira-vaashpasheela computer Memory bijalee hatane par bhi data barakaraar rakhti hai.\nROM (reeda-onalee Memory) computer borda me built iska primary example hai. computing me, Memory Address ek\nspecific sankhyatmak pahachaanakarta hai jiska use CPU dwara computer ki Memory ke andar ek accurate sthana par\nsanplaneteet data ka detect lagaane aur usa tak reach ke liye kiya jata hai. [Q214–Q217]\n● CD-ROM ka meaning Compact Disk reeda-onalee Memory (Compact Disc Read-Only Memory) hai. Ye ek optical Disc\npraaroop hai jisme data sthayee roop se mudrit hota hai aur ise mitaay nahi ja sakta hai. RAM raindama-eksesa Memory\n(Random Access Memory) ka short roop hai. Ye ek asthayee kaaryakshetr hai jahaan computer un data aur programme ko\nloda karta hai jinka wo active roop se use kar rahaa hai. RAM (Random access memory) asthir (volatile) hai, jiska meaning"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\nhai ki ise data rakhne ke liye nirantar electrical Shakti ki requirement hoti hai. Jab computer banda kar diya jata hai, to RAM\nka saaraa data mita jata hai. RAM Hard disk storej ki tarah nahi hai. Hard disk sthayee (permanent), gaira-vaashpasheela\nstorage provide karti hai, jabki RAM specially CPU ke active use ke liye asthayee, vaashpasheel aur behada fast eksesa\nstorej provide karta hai. Isliye statement B true nahi hai. [Q218–Q221]\n● Random access memory ek computer system ki main ya primary Memory (primary memory) hai, jo CPU ke saath active\nroop se intaraikt karti hai. Solid State Drive, Hard disk aur pen drive sabhi sekendaree (external aur sthayee) Memory ke\nroop hain. RAM primary (primary) Memory ki tarah kaam karta hai, jo CPU ko kaam karne wale data tak immediate reach\nme enable karta hai. Kaisha (Cache) Memory ek atyant fast, small Memory component hai jo CPU ke kareeb ya uske\nandara integrated hota hai. Ye usa data aur Instructionson ko baphar karta hai jinhen CPU sabse zyada baara eksesa karta\nhai, jo haaee-speeda CPU aur apekshaakrit dheemee main RAM K Bcha Gati ke antara ko paatata hai. Specific system\nMemory K Bcha, kaisha (Cache) me sabse kam access time (shortest access time) aur hightam Bandwidth hoti hai, jo\nniyamit RAM ya magnetic storage ke comparison me bahut fast pratikriy karti hai. [Q222–Q225]\n● Kaisha (Cache) Memory specially baara-baara use kiye jane wale data ko CPU ke liye immediate upalabdh rakhakar\ncomputer Processing me fastee laane ke liye dedicated hai. Kaisha (Cache) Memory yahaan listed sabhi options me sabse\nfast Memory Unit ki tarah kaam karti hai, jise directly CPU aarkitekchar par ya uske bagala me banaya gaya hai. Flash\nMemory (SSD, pen drive me prayukta) solid-state aur energy-kushala hai, lekin paaranparika, revolving mechanical Hard\ndisk draaiv (HDD) ke comparison me iski prati Gigabyte storage laagat aama taur par zyada hoti hai. Isliye, statement (C)\ntathyatmak roop se incorrect hai. [Q226–Q228]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q184, Q210 & Q211 — Multiple/Disputed\n\n▸Adobe Photoshop ko source graphics aur multimedia dono categories me accept karta hai.\n\n▸Router, switch aur hub sab connecting devices hain; Q210 flawed/bonus-type source item hai.\n\n▸Networks ke beech packets forward karne ka standard answer router hai, lekin Q211 options/context ki wajah se source disputed\nmark hai.\n8. Programming, Domains, Communication, AI & Digital Technologies\n● COBOL ek high-stareeya computer programing language hai. Iska naam komana bijanes oriented laingvej (Common\nBusiness Oriented Language) hai, jise mainly vyavasaaya, vitta aur prashaasanik systems ke liye develop kiya gaya hai.\nORACLE (ORACLE) ek highly famous maltee-model rileshanal database mainejament system hai, jise aama taur par\ndatabase software ke roop me classified kiya jata hai. Basic (BASIC), see (C) aur phoratraan (FORTRAN) universally\nrecognition mila programming bhaashaaen hain jinka use computer Software ko Codesinga karne ke liye kiya jata hai.\n'FAST' ko computer Language ke roop me recognition mila nahi hai. Java, C++ aur PASCAL programming bhaashaaen\nhain. ROM (reeda-onalee Memory) computer ke andara ek physical hardware component (Memory Chip) hai, ye koi\nprogramming language nahi hai. [Q229–Q232]\n● Paint brush (MS Paint) ek sarala Graphics penting Application Software hai, jabki Basic, C++ aur Java high-stareeya\nprogramming bhaashaaen hain. Listed All the four option vaastavik computer programing bhaashaaen hain. Kobara (Cobra)\nek objekta-orienteda language hai, paayathan aur Java aworldsaneey roop se lokapriy general-purpose bhaashaaen hain,\naur skviral (Squirrel) ek halkaa skripting language hai. COBOL, PASCAL aur BASIC sabhi high-stareeya programming\nbhaashaaon ke klaasik example hain, jinhen low-stareeya (low-level) machine Codes ke comparison me manushyon dwara\nzyada aasaanee se padhane aur likhane ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Phoratraan (FORTRAN - phormoola traansaleshana)\nko clearly 1950 ke decade me IBM dwara teevra sankhyatmak Calculation aur scientist computing ke liye develop kiya gaya\ntha. [Q233–Q236]\n● Basic (BASIC) originally ek procedural programming language hai. Ye functions ko nishpaadit karne ke liye statements\n(statements) ke raikhik sequence (linear sequence) par depend karta hai. Paanchaveen generation ki bhaashaaen (5GL)\ncharana-dara-charana Algorithms par highly depend hone ke bajaay tarka aur baadhaa-aadhaarita programming ka use\nkarti hain. Prolog ek major example hai, jo kritrim buddhimatta (AI) research aur Specialjnya systems (expert systems) se\ndepression se linked hai. JSP Java Server Pages ka short roop hai. Ye ek server-saaida programming technology hai jo\nSoftware devalapars ko HTML aur XML ke basis par Gatisheela roop se utpann web peja banane me help karti hai.\nAssembler ek specific upayogita (utility) programme hai jo asenbalee language (jo pathaneey nimoniks ka use karta hai) me\nlikhe gaye Codes ko shuddh baainaree machine language me anuvaad karne ke liye jimmedaar hai jo computer Processor\ndwara nishpaadan yogya hai. [Q237–Q240]\n● Machine language computer ki maulik language hai. Isme kevala do anka 0 and 1 shamil hote hain. computer ki Machine\nlanguage Boolean Algebra par based hai. Ye mathematics ka wo roop hai jo statements aur unke booliyan maanon se\nrelated hai. Sabhi digital computer 1 aur 0 ki baainaree system aur 1850 ke decade me English inventoree ganitajny jorja\nboola dwara determine tarka (logic) ke niyamon par depend karte hain. '.us' domain naam The United States of America ko\nrefer karta hai aur '.edu' ka meaning shiksha hai. Isliye,.edu.us ek American academic institute ka domain naam hai. [Q241–\nQ244]\n● Organisation ki website ka.com bhaaga lessrshiyal (commercial) ka short roop hai. Ye Internet ki domain naam system me\nek sheersha-stareeya domain (TLD) hai. Domain naam me last point ke baad wale bhaaga ko topa levala domain kaha jata\nhai, jaise www.cnn.com. Isme \".com\" topa levala domain hai. Proksee server teeseepee/aaeepee detect (TCP/IP address)\nprovide nahi karta hai (ye usually deeechaseepee (DHCP) server ka kaam hai), isliye statement 1 incorrect hai. LTE ko\naama taur par 4G (3G nahi) ke roop me vipanan kiya jata hai, aur VoLTE advanced 4G voice traansamission se related hai.\nIsliye, statement 1 incorrect hai. [Q245–Q248]\n● Visible light communication (VLC) ek chhoti distance ka (short-range) optical vaayarales communication hai, jo statement\n2 ke opposite hai. Isliye, statement 2 incorrect hai. Niyara pheeld Communication (NFC) devices ko bahut short-range par,"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\nusually 4 senteeMetre ya usase short-range par information share karne me enable karta hai, na ki ek Metre tak. Isliye,\nstatement 2 incorrect hai. Miniaturized-category ke device (Short Range Devices - SRD) kam sancharit Shakti ke saath\nkaam karte hain aur isliye unki seemaa kam hoti hai. Statement 1 and 2 ne anivaary roop se AR aur VR ki paribhaashaaon\nki adalaa-badalee kar dee hai. Aabhaasee vaastavikata (VR) ek simyuleted vaataavaran banaatee hai jo physical world ko\npoori tarah se banda kar deti hai. Sanvardhit vaastavikata (AR) vaastavik world ke parivesh par computer generated\nchhaviyon ko projekt karti hai. [Q249–Q252]\n● John McCarthy ko 'aartiphishiyala intelijens (AI) ka janak' maana jata hai. unhone 1950 ke decade me 'aartiphishiyala\nintelijensa' word gadhaa tha aur is field me ek major pioneer vyakti the. 1950 me Alan Turing dwara developed The Turing\nTest, jiska purpose ye moolyankan karna tha ki kya koi machine human ke baraabar ya usase aprabhedy buddhimaan\nbehavior display kar sakti hai, ko originally \"imiteshana gema\" (Imitation Game) kahaa jata tha. Statement A sahi hai:\nMachine Learning (Machine learning) aartiphishiyal intelijens ka ek upasamuchchay hai. Machine Learning (ML)\naartiphishiyal intelijens ki ek special branch hai jo computeron ko data se svaayatt roop se seekhane aur demonstration me\nimprovements karne me saksham banane par kendrit hai. [Q253–Q256]\n● AI baayas (pakshapaata) taba hota hai jab koi AI system pakshapaatee parinaam generate karta hai. Ye mainly\npakshapaatee prashikshan data, Algorithms design me technical issues, ya unhe banane wale Peopleon (People) ke\npoorvaaplaneton se utpann hota hai. Jab ye question taiyar kiya gaya tha (2020), taba AI energy Grid ko anukoolit karne\n(1), chikitsa chhavi vishleshana/roga nidaan (3), aur text-too-speecha technology (4) me highly effective tha. FPGA ka full\nform 'Field Programmable Gate Array' (Field Programmable Gate Array) hai. Ye ek type ka Semiconductor IC hai jise\ndevelopment ke baad graahak ya designar dwara phira se programme ya apadet kiya ja sakta hai, jo AI functions me\nlacheele hardware tvaran (acceleration) ki allow karta hai. Air indiya ne graahak service ko badhane aur vividh questionon\nka kushalataapoorvak uttara dene ke liye Microsoft ke ejyora OpenAI (Azure OpenAI) service dwara operated 'Maharaja'\n(Maharaja) naam ka ek jenaretiv eaaee varchual ejenta pesha kiya. [Q257–Q260]\n● Chatjeepeetee (ChatGPT) ek bade language model (LLM) par based chatbot hai jise OpenAI dwara develop kiya gaya hai\naur 2022 ke end me jaaree kiya gaya hai. Ye users ko AI ke saath intaraiktiv vaartaalaap karne me enable karta hai.\nElection Commission of India (ECI) ne raajaneetik dalon aur ummeedavaaron ko paaradarshee aur kushalata se chunaav\nprachaar Gatividhiyon ke liye anumati mila karne ki suvidha provide karne ke liye advanced 'suvidhaa 2.0' mobile aipa\nlaunch kiya. U.S.B. Ka full form 'Universal Serial Bus' (Universal Serial Bus) hai. Ye ek udyoga standard hai jo computer aur\nparidheey (peripheral) devices K Bcha connection, communication aur bijalee aapoorti ke liye Cable, kanektar aur Protocols\nke liye viInstructions established karta hai. ek Port computer aur external ya internal devices (eksesareeja) jaise ki mouse,\nprinter, ya keyboard K Bcha ek specific connection point ya intaraphes ki tarah kaam karta hai. [Q261–Q264]\n● Password varnon (characters) ki ek stRing hai jiska use users ki pahachaan satyapit karne ke liye kiya jata hai, jisse\ncomputer system ya network par anadhikrit access (unauthorized access) ko rokaa ja sakta hai. computing me, 'Finger'\n(Finger) ek networking Protocols hai jiska use kisi specific network par users ke baare me information ka detect lagaane ke\nliye kiya jata hai, jaise ki unakaa asalee naam, e-mail detect ya logina sthiti ki jaanch karna. Pablik ki inphraastrakchar (PKI)\nDigital security infrastructure (digital security infrastructure) ka ek abhinn anga hai. Isme information ko safe roop se\nsthanaantarit karne ke liye digital pramaanapatron (digital certificates) aur pablika-ki (public-key) encryption ka nirmaana,\nprabandhan aur use shamil hai. Digital Signature ek ganiteey technology hai jiska use kisi sandesha, software ya digital\nDocuments ki praamaanikata aur Integrity ko maanya karne ke liye kiya jata hai. Ye mainly ye sunishchit karne wale\nelectronic hastaakshar ki tarah kaam karta hai ki material aparivartit rahe (statement 3 sahi hai). [Q265–Q268]\n● The Information Technology Act, 2000 ne India me e-Commerce aur electronic Documentseekarana ke liye kaanoonee\ndhaancha establish kiya. Isane Electronic Record, Digital Signature ko kaanoonee recognition provide ki aur Certifying\nAuthority ki bhoomika ko define kiya. Isliye sabhi option sahi hain. Statement 1 sahi hai: BHIM (bhima) aipa UPI aaeedee,\nphone nanbar ya UPI-sakshama Banks khaate se jude kyooaar (QR) Codes ko skaina karke tvarit dhana hastaantaran ki\nallow karta hai. Digital indiya ka main phokas graameen kshetron me network kanektivitee ka expansion karke, public\nvaaee-phaaee provide karke aur government sevaaon ko electronic roop se vitarit karke India ko digital roop se sashakt\nsamaaj me badalana hai. Isliye, statement 3 sahi hai. India government ne digital public vastuen (public goods) established\nkarne ke liye opana-sorsa praudyogikiyon par bahut zyada jora diya hai. Listed All the four pletaphorma—aarogya setu,\nkovina, dijeelokar aur deekshaa—antarnihita opana-sorsa digital aarkitekchar par depend karte hain, jo paaradarshita aur\nskeLabel ekeekaran ko protsaahit karte hain. [Q269–Q272]\n● Statement 1 incorrect hai: basis adhiniyam ke according, basis number strictly pahachaan ka pramaan hai, naagarikata ya\nadhivaas (domicile) ka pramaan patra nahi. Khule (Open) API ka matalab hai ki Software devalapars aise Codes likha\nsakate hain jo pahachaan satyapan ke liye basis database ke saath directly intaraphes karne ke liye hardware (jaise phone\nya pointa-opha-Cell machine) ki ek detailed vividhata ki allow karta hai. Isliye statement 1 sahi hai. Statement 1 sahi hai:\nblokachen maulik roop se ek vikendreekrit (decentralized), vitarit public bahikhaate (ledger) ki tarah kaam karta hai jo\nnireekshan ke liye sulabh hai lekin ekatarapha herapher ke pratirodhee hai. Web 3.0 ek vikendreekrit Internet ki parikalpana\nkarta hai. Blokachen jaisee vitarit khaata praudyogikiyon par depend hokara, ye Shakti ko kendreekrit technical diggajon se\ndoora kar deta hai. [Q273–Q276]\n● Bele II (Belle II) prayog ek major *particle physics* prayog hai jo B mesana ki jaanch kar rahaa hai, na ki aartiphishiyal\nintelijensa. (jodee 1 incorrect hai). CRISPR-Cas9 ek kraantikaaree *jenetika engineering/jeena-editinga* tools hai, jo\npaartikal phijiks se related nahi hai. (jodee 3 incorrect hai). [Q277–Q278]\n9. Devices, E-Governance, Multimedia, Video, E-mail & Mobile ICT\n● computer computing, determine niyamon ke according fastee se data ko proses karne aur parinaam output karne me\nhighly kushal hote hain. computer shabdaavalee me, computer programme ya system me koi truti, khaamee ya dosha jo\nuse incorrect ya apratyashit parinaam dene ka kaaran banata hai, use widely \"baga\" (Bug) kaha jata hai. MICR 'maignetika"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\ninka kairektar rikognishana' ka short roop hai. O.M.R. 'Optical Mark Reader' (ya rikognishana) ka short roop hai. Ye\ncomputer system me data enter karne ki ek method hai. [Q279–Q282]\n● OMR (Optical Mark Reader) technology ka use mainly bulabule (bubbles) se bhare vastunishth type ke uttara patron ko\nskaina karne aur jaanchane ke liye kiya jata hai. I.R.C. Ka meaning Internet Relay Chat hai. Ye ek application leyara\nProtocols hai jo Peopleon ko text-aadhaarita vaataavaran me vaastavik time me Ek-doosare ke saath sanvaad karne ki\nallow karta hai. 2G 'doosri generation' (2nd Generation) ki vaayarales Telephone technology ka short roop hai. Ye hamen\ntext aur chitra sandesh bhejne me enable karta hai aur isme basic Internet Abilityen hoti hain. CAD (computer ededa\ndesigna) Software ka use aarkitekta, injeeniyara, draaphtara, Artkaara aur other Peopleon dwara accurate chitra ya\ntechnical chitra banane ke liye kiya jata hai. [Q283–Q286]\n● GIF ka meaning 'Graphics intarachenj phormeta' (Graphics Interchange Format) hai. Ye ek computer file svaroop hai jiska\nuse chhaviyon aur sarala enimeshan ke liye kiya jata hai. 3D printing word me vibhinn type ki processen shamil hain\njinamen material ko computer control ke under jodaa ya jamaay jata hai taaki tri-aayamee (3D) objekt banaye go saken, jo\nusually layer-dara-layer hote hain. E-Governance, jiska meaning hai 'electronic gavarnensa', dakshata badhane ke purpose\nse technology operated shaasan provide karne ke liye government ke vibhinn staron par information aur Communication\ntechnology (ICTs) ka use kar rahaa hai. Government sevaaen provide karne ke liye shaasan me computer ke use ko E-\nGovernance ke roop me jana jata hai. [Q287–Q290]\n● E-Governance ke chaara major stanbh People, process, technology aur resource hain. Ye stanbh saamoohik roop se\nshaasan ke digital parivartan ka sammeaningn karte hain. Gaartanar ka E-Governance model ek chaara-charaneeya model\nhai jo ee-government ke development ko measure karta hai. Charan hain: Sushaasan (good governance) mila karne ke liye\ngovernment me aaeeseetee (ICT) ke application ko E-Governance kaha jata hai. computer fast Gati se Calculation karta\nhai. ek Microcomputer prati sekand laakhon Calculationen kar sakta hai. [Q291–Q294]\n● Multimedia wo field hai jo text, Graphics, draainga, chalatee chhaviyon (video), eneemeshana, audio aur kisi bhi other\nmeediy ke computer-radioactivea ekeekaran se related hai jahaan hara type ki information ko digital roop se darshaay ja\nsakta hai. Multimedia applicationon me kai type ke meediy (text, audio, video, Graphics) shamil ho sakate hain. Multimedia\nsystem ki primary Specialtaa ek saath material vitarit karne ke liye ek se zyada type ke meediy ka use karna hai. computing\nme, Multitasking (multitasking) ek nishchit duration me kai functions ya applicationon ko ek saath nishpaadit karne ki\nconcept hai. Telefax ke through, koi Telephone laainon ki help se ek sthana se doosare sthana par Graphics aur paathy\ninformation communicationit kar sakta hai aur unhe screen par padha sakta hai. [Q295–Q298]\n● Video mela ek former-rikorda kiye gaye video ko e-mail ke roop me bhejne ki ek system hai. Graphics, Video clips aur\nVideo messages un sabhi material ke example hain jinhen video mela ke through bheja ja sakta hai. Video conferencing ka\nmeaning audio aur video data ko ek saath transmit karne ke liye computer network use karke vibhinn saaiton par do ya do\nse zyada pratibhaagiyon K Bcha sammelan organized karna hai. Video conferencing telecom praudyogikiyon ke ek seta\nuse karke video kola ka sanchaalan hai jo do ya do se zyada sthanon ko ek saath do-taraphaa video aur audio prasaaran\ndwara sanvaad karne ki allow karta hai. Video konphrens ke liye, laaiva video capture karna essential hai, jiske liye Video\ncamera ya Webcam ki requirement hoti hai. [Q299–Q302]\n● Video conferencing system ke liye essential component Video camera, Display device aur Microphone hain. Telephone ki\nrequirement nahi hai kyonki audio Internet aur maaikrophona/speekara ke through transmit hota hai. E-mail ka full form\n'Electronic Mail' (Electronic mail) hai. ek maanya e-mail detect do bhaagon se bana hota hai, ek users naam (Username)\naur @ prateek dwara alaga kiya gaya ek domain naam (jaise, username@domainname.com). Kisi bhi e-mail pate me @\nchinha ke baaeen direction ka bhaaga users naam (username) hota hai aur @ chinha ke daaeen direction ka bhaaga\ndomain naam hota hai. Isliye die gaye pate me, ITdesk.info domain naam hai. [Q303–Q306]\n● Hotmail, Rediffmail, Yahoo aur jeemel sabhi famous muphta e-mail service pradaata hain. E-mail ataichament e-mail\nsandesh ke saath bhejee gayi ek digital file hai. Jina fileon ko sanlagn kiya ja sakta hai unamen Documents, text fileen,\nMusic, audio fileen, video fileen, photo etc. Shamil hain. Aapa ek e-mail me lagbhag kisi bhi type ki file sanlagn kar sakte\nhain, jisme text, audio aur video fileen shamil hain, jab tak ki file ka shape e-mail pradaata dwara determine seemaa ke\nandar ho. 'data' (data) word ka ekavachan roop 'Datum' (Datum) hai. [Q307–Q310]\n● 'Blog' ek web peja hai jo public roop se sulabh vyaktigat jarnal ki tarah kaam karta hai. 'Blog' word 'web' (web) aur 'loga'\n(log) do shabdon ka sanyojan hai. CPU Instructions chakra me, Fetching Instructions mila karna hai, Decoding ise\nsamajhana hai, aur Executing (executing) aadeshon ko pooraa karne ki vaastavik process hai. Software yoojar intaraphes\nme, menoo me related commands (aadeshon) ki ek list hoti hai jise users kriyaon ko nishpaadit karne ke liye chuna sakate\nhain. Bookmark apne browser me apni pasandeeda website ko saheja kar (save) usa tak sheeghrata se reach ka ek\nmethod hai. Ye baad ke sandarbh ke liye websiteon ko sahejane ka ek upayogee aur fast method hai. [Q311–Q314]\n● Varchual Memory An operating system ki Specialtaa hai jo computer ko asthayee roop se Random access memory se\nDisc storej me data traansaphar karke physical Memory ki lessee ki bharapaaee karne me saksham banaatee hai. ICT ka\nfull form 'Information & Communications Technology' (Information and Communications Technology) hai. Ye un\npraudyogikiyon ko refer karta hai jo telecom ke through information tak access provide karti hain. SIM ka full form\nSubscriber Identity Module (Subscriber Identity Module) hai. Ye ek small kaarda hai jisme mobile network graahak ke\nkhaate ki information hoti hai. SMS ka matalab 'Short messaging service' (Short Messaging Service) hai. Iska use mobile\nphone dwara sandeshon ke aadaana-pradaana ke liye kiya jata hai. [Q315–Q318]\n● Usa time ke general teleekom maanadandon ke according, ek pikchar maisej mobile ke private inaBox me 30 Dayson tak\nraha sakta hai. Ise zyada dinon tak safe rakhne ke liye ise sandesh Box (message box) me sahejana (save) padata hai.\nOption (B) me diya gaya yugma sahi matched nahi hai. Endroid (Android) voice input system nahi hai; ye Google dwara\ndeveloped ek mobile Operating System (OS) hai, jise mainly tacha-skreena mobile devices ke liye design kiya gaya hai.\n[Q319–Q320]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q319–Q322 — Legacy Mobile Facts\n\n▸Picture-message retention, Android 6.0 naming aur iPhone 4S specifications historical/source-period facts hain; current mobile-\ntech facts ke roop me use na karein.\n10. Mobile Platforms, Cybercrime, Data Security & Computer Networks\n● Endroid 6.0 'Marshmallow' endroid Operating System ka chhatha major version tha. Maee 2015 me pehli baar iska unveil\nkiya gaya aur ise official taur par aktoobar 2015 me jaaree kiya gaya tha. IPhone 4S me 512 MB RAM (640 MB nahi) ke\nsaath duala-core Apple A5 Processor tha. Isme 200 ghante ka staindabaay taaima (300 ghante nahi), 3G par 8 ghante ka\ntoka taaima tha aur Siri (Siri) naam ka ek new voice rikagnaaijing asistent pesha kiya gaya tha. Apni shikaayaton ko\nnikaalane ke liye website ka use karna 'Cyber venting' kehlat hai. Denial of Service (DOS) ek type ka hamala hai jahaan\nhaikars vaidha users ko website tak reach se rokane ka prayas karte hain. [Q321–Q324]\n● Cyber kaanoon shabdaavalee me, 'DOS' ka meaning 'Denial of Service' (Denial of Service) hai. Ye network service ko\nbaadhit karne ke liye design kiye gaye hamale ko refer karta hai. (nota: general computing me, DOS ka meaning Disk\nOperating System hota hai). Distribyooted dinayala-opha-sarvisa (DDoS) A cyber attack hai. Ye kai alaga-alaga sourceon\n(computeron) se ek saath amaany anurodh bhejakar lakshit server ko abhibhoot karne aur network ke general traiphik ko\nbaadhit karne ka ek durbhaavanaapoorn prayas hai. Hacking (Hacking) kisi system ya resources tak anadhikrit access mila\nkarne ke liye lessjoriyon ka phaayada uthaane ki process hai. Ye na to kevala discoveryna hai aur na hi security provide\nkarna hai. Isliye 'None of these' correct answer hai. Lokapriy sanskriti me, computer haikar wo vyakti hai jo lessjoriyon\n(bugs) ka phaayada uthaane ya computer system me sendha lagaane ke liye technical jnyaan ka use karta hai, jo aksar\nvyaktigat laabha ke liye durbhaavanaapoorn iraade se computer security ka ullanghan karta hai. [Q325–Q328]\n● Ek Cracker (ya blaika haita haikara) wo vyakti hota hai jo gopaneey data tak reach ya durbhaavanaapoorn kshati\npahunchaane ke liye computer ya network system me sendha lagaata hai. Blaika haita haikar (Black hat hacker), jise kabhi-\nkabhi cracker bhi kaha jata hai, wo hota hai jo binaa kisi moreaar ke computer security ko todata hai aur system ko\njaanaboojhakar damage pahunchaane ya dhokhaadhadee karne ke liye technology ka use karta hai. ek Cracker ya blaika\nhaita haikar kisi computer system ya network me anadhikrit access receive karta hai, important data ko nashta karta hai,\naur vyaktigat ya durbhaavanaapoorn kaaranon se apne lakshyon ke liye samasyaen paidaa karta hai. ek varchual keyboard\nphysical kunjiyon (physical keys) ke bajaay screen intaraphes ke through input ki allow karta hai. Ye hardware ya software\nKeyloggersa (jo aksar Trojan ya Spyware se jude hote hain) ko physical keestroks ko record karne se rokata hai, isliye\nPassword theft se bachaata hai. [Q329–Q332]\n● Hacking, Cyber Stalking (onalaaina peechha karna) aur Denial of Service (DOS) hamale sabhi digital network par ki jane\nwali avaidh Gatividhiyan hain, jo unhe sabhi recognition mila type ke cyber aparaadh banaate hain. Online Chatting ek\nsaamaanya, kaanoonee digital communication Gatividhi hai. Phishing, Cyber Stalking aur Identity Theft All of these\ndurbhaavanaapoorn Gatividhiyan hain jinhen cyber aparaadh ke roop me classified kiya gaya hai. Phishing hamala\nbhraamak (dhokhebaaja) e-mail ya text sandeshon ke roop me aataa hai jo peedit ko sensitive information (jaise Password)\nshare karne ya durbhaavanaapoorn fileen daaunalod karne ke liye lubhaane ke liye design kiye gaye hain. Phishing\n(Phishing) hamale users ko ek worldsaneey ikaaee (jaise Banks ya badi Company) ke roop me prachchhann hokara logina\nkredenshiyal ya kredit kaarda nanbar jaisee sensitive information prakat karne ke liye dhokha dene ke liye soshal\nengineering ka use karte hain. [Q333–Q336]\n● E-mail Spoofing jaalee preshak (sender) pate ke saath e-mail sandeshon ka development hai. Ye ek aisee technology hai\njiska use aksar phishing aur SPAM abhiyanon me kiya jata hai kyonki Peopleon ke e-mail kholane ki zyada sanbhaavana\nhoti hai jab unhe lagata hai ki ye kisi vaidha source dwara bheja gaya hai. Cyber aparaadh ka ek major define pahaloo\nganbhir jnyaan ki khaaee hai: aparaadhiyon ke paas system ka phaayada uthaane ke liye special computer kaushal (skills)\nhote hain, jabki peedit usually ina technical lessjoriyon se anabhijny (ignorant) hote hain. Vyapak cyber security me\nviniyamak Compliance (regulatory compliance), internal aur external donon khataron se bachaava, khatare ka detect\nlagaana aur active rokatham ke upaaya shamil hain. The Information Technology Act, 2000 (IT Act) India me cyber\naparaadh aur electronic komars se nipatane wala primary kaanoon hai. Ye electronic data intarachenj ke through kiye gaye\nlenaden ko kaanoonee recognition provide karta hai. [Q337–Q340]\n● Hub government dwara jaaree information technology niyama, 2013 ke under, service pradaataaon, bichauliyon, data\nkendron aur nigamit nikaayon (body corporates) ke liye CERT-In ko cyber security ghatanaaon ki riPort karna kaanoonee\nroop se anivaary hai. Cyber beemaa digital ghatanaaon (System ki bahaalee, salaahakaara, kaanoonee bachaava) se hone\nwale amoort damage ko kavara karta hai. Ye usually physical kshati ya hardware ke pratisthapan ko kavara nahi karta hai\n(jaise ki kisi badamaash dwara physical roop se tode jane par new computer khareedanaa). Isliye, statement 2 incorrect\nhai. Janaral data protekshan reguleshan (GDPR) The European Union (EU) aur European aarthik field (EEA) me data\nsecurity aur privacy par The European Union ke kaanoon me ek niyama hai. Privacy wo principle hai jo sensitive\ninformation ko private rakhne aur anadhikrit access (unauthorized access) se safe rakhne ke importance ko rekhaankit\nkarta hai. [Q341–Q344]\n● computer me Basic inaputa-outputa system (BIOS) ek firmware hai jiska use booting process ke dauran hardware\ninishiyalaaijeshan karne ke liye kiya jata hai. Ye motherboard par gaira-vaashpasheela (non-volatile) ROM chips par\nsanplaneteet hota hai. computeron ko ek saath jodakar networking unki upayogita aur information access Abilityon ko\nkaaphee badhaa deti hai. Haalaanki, devices ko jodne se bhedyata aur khataron (jaise virus aur Hacking) ki sanbhaavana\nbhi badha jati hai. Resilience general sanchaalan me doshon aur chunautiyon ke baavajood service ka ek sveekaary level\nprovide karne aur banaye rakhne ki Ability hai. Networking me, ye ek network ki viphalata se ubarane ki Ability hai. Decision\nSupport System (DSS) ek information system hai jo vyavasaay ya sangathanaatmak nirnay lene aur yojana (planning)\nGatividhiyon ka sammeaningn karti hai. [Q345–Q348]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\n● Ek Analog computer hala ki go rahi samasy ko model karne ke liye nirantar physical ghatanaaon, jaise electrical,\nmechanical ya haaidrolik amount ka use karta hai. ek conventional kaara speedoMetre ek Analog computer ka example hai.\ncomputer software data ya computer Instructionson ka ek sanplanet hai jo computer ko bataata hai ki kaise kaam karna hai.\ncomputer programme ko saamoohik roop se computer Software kaha jata hai. computer ke main component Input Unit,\nOutput Unit, Memory Unit aur Central Processing Unit hain. computer aarkitekchar me 'Basic Unit' koi recognition mila\ncomponent nahi hai. [Q349–Q352]\n11. IT Companies, Social Media, E-Commerce & Cloud Computing\n● Microsoft Corporation (Microsoft) ek bahuraashTreeya technology Company hai jo computer software (jaise vindoj oesa,\nemaesa ophisa soota) developed karti hai. Azim Premji WIPRO (Wipro) limited ke sansthapak aur long time tak adhyaksh\nrahe hain. (unke son rishad premajee ne baad me kaaryakaaree adhyaksh ke roop me padabhaar sanbhaalaa). Google ke\nseeeeo sundar pichaaee hain (A-2). Twitter (Twitter) ka development maarch 2006 me Jack Dorsey, nooha glaasa, bija\nstona aur ivaana viliyams dwara kiya gaya tha. [Q353–Q356]\n● Facebook (aba metaa pletaphorma, inka. Ka hissaa) ki saha-sthapanaa 2004 me Mark Zuckerberg ne ki thi. LinkedIn ek\nvyavasaay aur rojagaara-kendrita onalaain peshevar mancha hai jo peshevaron ke liye ek Social Networking Site ki tarah\nkaam karta hai. E-Commerce vyavasaayon ko din ke 24 ghante, saptaah ke 7 Days khule rahane ki allow karta hai, jisse ye\nnishchit parichaalan ghanton wale physical storon ke comparison me highly laabhaprad ho jata hai. Ema-jankshana (M-\nJunction - SAIL aur Tata Steel ek joint udyama) ek bade B2B onalaain maarketaples ki tarah kaam karta hai aur lenaden\nmoolya ke hisaab se India ki sabse badi e-Commerce Company hone ka daavaa karta hai. [Q357–Q360]\n● Flipkart, aleebaaba aur amejen sabhi vyavasaaya-se-upabhoktaa (B2C) e-Commerce vyavasaayon ke example hain. Ve\nmainly directly vyaktigat consumers ko utpaad bechate hain. MP Online Madhya Pradesh government ka ek morerit Portal\nhai jiska purpose G2C (government se naagarika) aur B2C sevaaen provide karna hai, ye specially ee-prokyoramenta\nPortal nahi hai. Cloud computing sevaaon ko conventional roop se teen main shreniyon me vibhaajit kiya gaya hai:\ninphraastrakchar eja e sarvis (IaaS), pletaphorm eja e sarvis (PaaS), aur Software eja e sarvis (SaaS). SaaS application\nInternet par vitarit kiye jate hain aur inhen mobile phone sahita kisi bhi kanekted divaais se eksesa kiya ja sakta hai.\n(statement 2 sahi hai). [Q361–Q364]\n● Skaaeedraaiv (SkyDrive) Microsoft ki vyaktigat cloud storej service ka former naam tha. Tredamaark Contention ki wajah\nse, Microsoft ne 2014 me official taur par iska naam badalakar \"vanadraaiva\" (OneDrive) kar diya. Cortesa ek opana-sorsa\nlo-Codes pletaphorm hai, eaaee varchual asistent nahi. 'projekta loona' (Project Loon) graameen aur dooradaraaj ke\nkshetron me vaayarales Internet ka use provide karne ke purpose se Google X dwara ek research pahala thi. DACNET e-\nAgriculture se related hai. Ye India me krishi, sahakaarita aur kisaan kalyan department ka E-Governance web Portal hai.\n[Q365–Q368]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q354–Q367 — Company/Service Facts Can Change\n\n▸CEO/company-head, biggest e-commerce company, cloud-service branding (SkyDrive→OneDrive) aur discontinued projects\n(e.g., Project Loon) time-sensitive/source-period facts hain.\n\n▸Q361 me Flipkart, Alibaba aur Amazon ko source B2C/e-commerce context me multiple correct options ke saath treat karta hai.\n12. Web Acronyms, Logic Gates & Emerging Technologies\n● Aaeebeeem (IBM) ka full form International Business Machine korporeshan hai. Ye ek American bahuraashTreeya\ntechnology aur paraamarsh Company hai. HTTP ka full form Hypertext Transfer Protocol hai. Ye World Wide Web par\ninformation systems ke liye use kiya jane wala basic application Protocols hai. World Wide Web par data tak reach aur\nsthanaantarit karne ke liye HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) primary Protocols hai. SMTP ka use e-mail ke liye kiya jata\nhai. HTML ka full form Hyper Text Markup Language hai. Ye web browser me display hone wale web pejon ko banane aur\ndesign karne ke liye use ki jane wali standard language hai. [Q369–Q372]\n● XML ka matalab Extensible Markup Language (eXtensible Markup Language) hai. Ye usually data storage aur sancharan\nke liye use kiya jata hai. URL ka full form Uniform Resource Locator hai. Ye World Wide Web par Documentson aur\nresources ka detect hai. FTP ka meaning File Transfer Protocol hai. Iska use network par computer fileon ke hastaantaran\nke liye kiya jata hai. SMPS ka full form Switchda-MODE paavar saplaaee hai. Ye computer ko essential kam Voltseja\ndeesee (DC) provide karne ke liye electrical Shakti ko kushalataapoorvak convert karta hai. [Q373–Q376]\n● UPS ka full form 'Uninterrupted Power Supply' hai. Ye ek device hai jo main bijalee viphal hone par baitaree dwara\naapaatakaaleen Shakti provide karta hai. OR Gate ek digital logic sarkit hai jiska output HIGH (1) ho jata hai yadi iska ek ya\nzyada input HIGH (1) ho. Official pareeksha ke nihita aarekh ke basis par: A aur 1 ka output = 1 (Q1), B aur 1 ka output = 1\n(Q2). Q1 aur Q2 ka output = C = 1. Kevala NAND geta use karke ek Exclusive-OR (XOR) geta banane ke liye, kam se kam\n4 NAND geta ki requirement hoti hai. [Q377–Q380]\n● World bhara me kam service wale samudaayon me digital saaksharata ke baare me jaagarookata paidaa karne aur use\nbadhaava dene ke liye hara saala 2nd December ko world computer saaksharata divasa manaay jata hai. computer\nsaaksharata divasa 2nd December ko manaay jata hai. Aakash shiksha ki propertyvatta badhane ke liye India government\ndwara khareede gaye kam laagat wale Tableta Personal computer ka naam hai, jise 2011 me launch kiya gaya tha.\ndevelopment ke liye information technology ke use ko badhaana Andhra Pradesh Government ki rananeeti thi. Ye\nchandrabaaboo naayadoo ke mukhyamantree kaala (1999-2004) ke under start kiya gaya tha. [Q381–Q384]\n● Information technology word data adhiplanetna, information, security etc. Ke liye network kanekting hardware\n(Connectivity + hardware) ke nishpaadan se related hai. Soshal meediy optimaaijeshan (SMO) kisi organisation ke sandesh\naur onalaain upasthiti ko prabandhit karne aur badhane ke liye soshal meediy saaiton ka use hai. Iska main point aasaanee\nse prachaar (publicity) banaana hai. Collaborative Filtering (Collaborative filtering) ek anushansa system hai jo users ke"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Computer & Information Technology Full Mind Map\npichhale behavior aur saamoohik praathamikataaon ke basis par bhavishyavaanee karti hai. Iska widely amejena, yootyoob\naur netaphliks jaise pletaphaarmon dwara use kiya jata hai. Smaart vocha jaise pahanane yogya device jeepeees (GPS) ko\ntraika karke kisi vyakti ke sthana ki pahachaan kar sakte hain. Ve vyakti ki neenda ke paitarn ki bhi nigaraanee kar sakte\nhain. Shravan device (hearing aids) shravanabaadhiton ki sahaayata ke liye klaasik pahanane yogya device hain. Isliye\nteenon work sahi hain. [Q385–Q388]\n● Ye parivisible Internet par communication aur baatacheet karne wale sensara, Software aur network kanektivitee ke saath\nembeded physical objects (devices, ghareloo devices, kaaron) ka description karta hai. Ye Internet of Things (IoT) ki\naccurate paribhaasha hai. 5G ko iski fast Gati, kam vilanbata (latency) aur ek hi time me kai devices ko jodne ki Ability se\npahachaana jata hai. Di gayi concept ka description karne ke liye sabse upayukt word 'Metaverse' hai. Metaverse Internet\nka ek bhavishy ka punaraavritti hai jisme lagaataara, imarsiv aabhaasee world shamil hai jahaan People aabhaasee objects\npar sanpatti ke moreaar ka prayog kar sakte hain. Vidya vaahinee project me country bhara ke primary government skoolon\nme computer Education (IT Education) le jana shamil hai. [Q389–Q392]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q392\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0362","t":"14 Space Hinglish Corrected","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\n🚀 SPACE — FULL MIND MAP\n\nअंतरिक्ष· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Indian Space Beginnings, Space Pioneers & Shuttle Milestones\n2. Planetary Missions, Gravitational Waves, Black Holes, Stars & Solar Storms\n3. Geostationary Satellites, Space Telescopes & Observatories\n4. ISRO, INSAT, Communication & Remote Sensing\n5. PSLV Missions, Navigation Systems & Launch-Vehicle Evolution\n6. ISRO Centres, Sriharikota, Thumba & Aviation Basics\n7. Moon Missions: Chandrayaan, LUPEX, Luna & Aditya-L1\n8. Mangalyaan, China & International Space Cooperation\n9. NASA Missions, Planets, Jet/Rocket Principles & Cryogenics\n10. Indian Launchers, Satellites, EDUSAT, GSAT & BHUVAN\n1. Indian Space Beginnings, Space Pioneers & Shuttle Milestones\n● Dr. Vikram Ambalal Sarabhai ek Indian Physicist aur astronomer the jinhone India me space research ki shuruaat ki thi.\nUnhe Indian space programme ka janak maana jata hai. Dr. Vikram Sarabhai ko India ke space programme ka janak\nmaana jata hai. Aryabhatta India dwara launch kiya gaya pehla satellite tha. Iska naam isi naam ke mahaan Indian\nastronomer ke naam par rakha gaya tha. [Q1–Q3]\n● India ne apne pehle satellite 'Aryabhatta' ke launch ke saath space age me pravesh kiya. Aryabhatta ko April 19th, 1975\nko successfully space me launch kiya gaya tha. Prof. U.R. Rao wo scientist the jinhone India ke pehle space satellite\n'Aryabhatta' ko design kiya tha. Rao ne 1972 me India me satellite technology ki establishment ki responsibility li thi. [Q4–Q6]\n● Laika ek Soviet space dog tha jo space me Earth ko orbit karne wala pehla animal bana gaya. 3 November, 1957 ko\n'Laika' naam ke ek dog ko Sputnik-2 spacecraft ke through space me bheja gaya tha. 12 April, 1961 ko astronaut Yuri\nGagarin Russian Vostok-1 spacecraft se space me jane wale pehle human bane. [Q7–Q9]\n● Valentina Tereshkova (Russian astronaut) space me jane wali pehli mahila bani, jab unhe 16 June, 1963 ko Vostok-6\nmission par launch kiya gaya tha. Apollo-11 wo space flight thi jisne 20 July, 1969 ko Moon par do logon ke saath lunar\nmodule 'Eagle' ko utara tha. Oleg Kononenko ek Russian cosmonaut hain. unhone International Space Station (ISS) par 5\nlong-duration missions ke dauran space me 1110.6 din total kiye hain. [Q10–Q12]\n● Currently, NASA ke astronaut Francisco (Frank) Rubio ke naam 370.9 dinon ke saath kisi American dwara sabse longest\nsingle spaceflight ka record hai. Ve 27 September, 2023 ko Earth par laute. Tim Peake British nationality ke European\nSpace Agency (ESA) ke astronaut aur ek former International Space Station (ISS) crew ke member hain. Atlantis ek Space\nShuttle hai (Space Station nahi). Columbia, Challenger, Discovery aur Atlantis sabhi NASA dwara operated Space Shuttle\nthe. [Q13–Q15]\n● Curiosity (Curiosity): Mars ko explore karne wala rover (A-3). MESSENGER (MESSENGER): Mercury ka study karne ke\nliye launch kiya gaya NASA ka spacecraft (B-4). Atlantis NASA ka last aur aakhiri Space Shuttle tha. Ise 8 July 2011 ko\nlaunch kiya gaya tha aur 21 July 2011 ko ye utara, jisse Space Shuttle programme ka end ho gaya. [Q16–Q17]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q13 — Spaceflight Record is Updated/Time-Sensitive\n\n▸Source itself Q13 ko updated/disputed mark karta hai. Longest single NASA spaceflight aur cumulative-space-time records date\nke saath change ho sakte hain; exam-year context follow karein.\n2. Planetary Missions, Gravitational Waves, Black Holes, Stars & Solar Storms\n● 'VERITAS' aur 'DAVINCI+' 1990 ke decade ke baad se Venus ke liye NASA ke pehle mission honge. Cassini-Huygens\n(Cassini-Huygens): Saturn aur uske rings ka study (A-2). Cassini-Huygens (Cassini-Huygens) Saturn planet (Saturn) par\nbheja gaya ek human rahita spacecraft tha, na ki Venus par. Isliye yugma 1 sahi matched nahi hai. [Q18–Q20]\n● NASA ka Cassini spacecraft Saturn planet (Saturn) aur uske rings aur Moonon ki complex system ka detect lagaane ke\nliye design kiya gaya ek mission tha. Cassini chhalledaar planet Saturn ka study karne ke liye NASA dwara developed ek\nspacecraft tha. Ye prayog ivolvd LASER intarapheromeetar space enteena (eLISA) ko refer karta hai, jo gravitational waves\n(gravitational waves) ka detect lagaane aur accurate roop se measure karne ke liye design kiya gaya ek space jaanch hai.\n[Q21–Q23]\n● ELISA project ka primary purpose space se To detect gravitational waves aur unakaa nireekshan karna hai. 2009 me,\nBritish scientists ne ghoshana ki ki unhone 'grevitee traiktara' naam ka ek vishesh spacecraft design kiya hai jo ek Asteroid\nko rokakar aur uske prakshepavakr ko badalakar Earth ko vinaashakaaree takaraav se bachaa sakta hai. Scientists ne do\nblack hole ke vilaya ko dekhaa, jisse spesataaim ke taane-baane me heavy amount me energy utpann hui. Is observation\nka importance ye hai ki pehli baar LIGO observatoryon dwara gravitational waves (gravitational waves) ka directly detect\nlagaay gaya. [Q24–Q26]\n● Gravitational waves ka pehla pratyaksh observation 14 September, 2015 ko kiya gaya tha aur 11 pharavaree, 2016 ko\nLIGO dwara iski ghoshana ki gayi thi. Space me maaikrovev (kosmika maaikrovev baikagraaunda) ka detect lagaana aur\nredashipht ghatana (sudoora galaxyon se light ka spektram ke laala chhora par sthanaantarit honaa) ka observation\nscientists dwara brahmaand ke nirantar expansion ke primary saakshy ke roop me uddhrit kiya gaya hai. Vistaarit\nbrahmaand ki concept Doppler effect par based hai. Edavin habala ne sudoor galaxyon se light ke redashipht ko dekhakar\nye determine karne ke liye Doppler effect ka use kiya ki brahmaand ka expansion ho rahaa hai. [Q27–Q29]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\n● Aainsteen ke general relativity ke principle ki bhavishyavaanee hai ki ek heavy shareer space-time ko modata (warp) hai\n(statement 3). Choonki gravity dwara space-time vakra hota hai, isliye isme se gujarane wala light bhi mudaa/prabhaavita\nhota hai (statement 1). General relativity ke sameekaranon ne naturally ek speedsheela, vistaarit (ya sikudate) brahmaand\nko bhi nihita kiya (statement 2). Isliye sabhi sahi hain. 'iventa horaaijana' (Event Horizon) aur 'singulairitee' word black hole\nse jude hain. 'stringa thyoree' aur 'staindarda model' maulik physics concepten hain jo particles ki baatacheet ki vyakhy karti\nhain. Ye sabhi brahmaand ke observation aur samajh se related hain. Black hole vaastav me a collapsed level hai. Stellar\nmass wale black hole taba banate hain jab bahut bade stars apne jeevan chakra ke end me apne hi gravity ke under dhaha\njate hain. [Q30–Q32]\n● Black hole ek aisee vastu hai jo itanee saghan hoti hai ki iska gravity bala light ya kisi other cheeja ko baahar nikalane se\nrokane ke liye kaaphee majaboot hota hai. Choonki koi light baahar nahi nikalata hai, isliye ise directly telescope se nahi\ndekha ja sakta hai. Black hole apne high gravity ki wajah se usa par padane wale sabhi radiationon ko avashoshit (absorb)\nkar leta hai. Yahaan tak ki light bhi isase bacha nahi sakataa. Comet (Comets) Sun ke charon direction apni highly lambee,\nElliptical orbiton ke liye jane jate hain. Ve Sun se bahut doora ek important time vyateet karte hain aur phira fastee se iske\npaas aate hain. [Q33–Q35]\n● Sun se radiation aur saura air dhoola aur gas ke particles ko Comet se doora dhakelatee hai. Isliye, Comet ki poonchh\nhamesha Away from the Sun ki direction (Away from the Sun) hoti hai. Sun ki chamakeelee external layer ko Photosphere\nke roop me jana jata hai. Photosphere word ka meaning hai 'prakaasha ka golaa' - jo upayukt hai kyonki ye wo layer hai jo\nsabse zyada light emit karti hai jise hama Earth se dekhate hain. Neutron stars huge suparajaayant stars ke dhaha gaye\ncore hain. Ve highly saghan (dense) hote hain. [Q36–Q38]\n● Pulsar (pulsars) highly magnetic, fastee se Rotating neutron stars hain jo apne magnetic dhruvon se electromagnetic\nradiation ke beema emit karte hain. Sephids ve stars hain jo time-time par chamakate aur manda hote hain. (jodaa 1\nincorrect hai). Huge stars (Giant stars) me baune stars ke comparison me zyada garma aur saghan core hote hain. Isliye,\nunamen nuclear pratikriyaon ki dara zyada hoti hai (statement-II sahi hai). [Q39–Q41]\n● Earth ka magnetic field ek security kavach ki tarah kaam karta hai. Ye saura air (solar wind) se electrical charged particles\nko dhruvon ki direction moda deta hai, jisse ve Earth ki surface tak nahi access paate hain. Saura jvaalaaen (Solar flares)\nEarth par electrical chumbakeey vyavadhaan paidaa kar sakti hain. Ve jeepeees ko baadhit kar sakte hain, paavar grida ko\ndamage pahuncha sakate hain, satellite orbiton ko pareshaan kar sakte hain, shortavev rediyo communication ko baadhit\nkar sakte hain aur teevra aurora paidaa kar sakte hain. Earth ke vaayumandal me punah pravesh ke dauran, ek spacecraft\nhighly air gharshan ka anubhav karta hai. Ye highly garmee aasapaas ki air ko aayanit karti hai, jisse shuttle ke charon\ndirection ek Plasma liphaapha bana jata hai. [Q42–Q44]\n3. Geostationary Satellites, Space Telescopes & Observatories\n● Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki ek geostationary satellite bhoomadhy line se lagbhag 35,786 kilomeetar (lagbhag 36,000\nkm) oopara space me located hota hai, 10,000 km nahi. Geostationary orbit (geostationary orbit) bhoosamakaalik\n(geosynchronous) orbit ka ek specific type hai (1). Ye poori tarah se golaakaar (circular) honee chaahie (2) aur theeka\nEarth ki bhoomadhy line ke tala me located honee chaahie (3). ek geostationary (geostatic) sthiti taba mila hoti hai jab koi\nvastu (jaise A Satellite) Earth ki usee ghoornee speed (rotational speed) se Earth ki orbit karti hai. [Q45–Q47]\n● Orbit ki duration ko Earth ke ghoornan (lagbhag 24 hours) se accurate roop se mela khaane ke liye, ek bhoo-sthaitika\nsatellite ko bhoomadhy line se lagbhag 35,786 kilomeetar ki ek bahut hi vishishta, nishchit elevation par orbit karanee\nchaahie. Exosphere Earth ke vaayumandal ki sabse external layer hai, jo external space ke shoony me lupta ho jati hai.\nCommunication Satellite ~36,000 km ki elevation par orbit karte hain, jisse ve majabootee se Exosphere ke andar\nestablished ho jate hain. Earth ke bhoomadhy line par ek hi point par poori tarah se sthira rahane ke liye, ek geostationary\nsatellite ko apni ek orbit theeka usee time me poori karanee chaahie jitana time Earth ko apni dhuree par ek baara revolving\nme lagata hai, jo ki 24 hours hai. [Q48–Q50]\n● Jaisaa ki establish kiya gaya hai, ek geostationary satellite 24 hours me ek orbit poori karta hai, jo Earth ke ghoornan ke\nsaath poori tarah se mela khaata hai. Earth ki surface (bhoomadhya line par) par ek point ke saath poori tarah se\nsinkranaaij (synchronized) rahane ke liye, geostationary satellite ka patha vrittaakaar (circular) orbit honaa chaahie. ek\nandaakaar (elliptical) orbit ki wajah se satellite ki speed me bhinnata hogee, jisse tulyakaalan (synchronization) toota\njaaegaa. Kepalar space telescope 2009 me NASA dwara launch ki gayi ek specially design ki gayi space observatory thi.\nIska specific mission milkee ve (galaxy) ke hamare field ka sarvekshan karna tha taaki rahane yogya field me ya uske aasa-\npaas (Earth-like Planets) saikadon Earth ke shape aur chhote planeton ki discover ki go sake. [Q51–Q53]\n● 1999 me launch ki gayi NASA ki major chandra eksa-re observatory ka naam shaanadaar Indian-American Nobel Prize\nvijeta aur khagol scientist subrahmanyan chandrashekhar ke sammaan me rakha gaya tha, jinhen huge sistars ke\ndevelopment par unke kaam ke liye jana jata hai. Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki NASA (USA) aur Russia ke alawa,\nEuropean Union aur Japan ki space ejensiyon ne bhi India se pehle space me isee tarah ki suvidhaaen (observatory)\nlaunch ki hain. Antaarkatik barpha me depression me dabee IceCube (IceCube nyootrino observatory), specific roop se\nworld ki sabse badi nyootrino telescope ke roop me classified hai, jisme ek ghana kilomeetar barpha shamil hai. [Q54–Q56]\n● Jab ye question poochha gaya tha (2002), to haanale, laddaakh (4,500 meetar ki elevation) me located Indian\nastronomical observatory (Indian Astronomical Observatory) world ka sabse ooncha optical telescope tha. Isliye die gaye\noptions me India correct answer hai. Nota: aaja, chilee me tokyo worldvidyalay ki ataakaama observatory (5,640 meetara)\nke paas full hightam record hai. [Q57–Q58]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Largest / Highest Observatory Facts\n\n▸'World’s biggest telescope' ya 'highest observatory' jaise superlative facts technology ke saath change ho sakte hain. Source-\nyear wording ko current record samajhkar blindly memorize na karein."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\n4. ISRO, INSAT, Communication & Remote Sensing\n● ISRO India ki primary space Agency hai. Iska full form Indian Space Research Organisation hai, jiski establishment 1969\nme National development ke liye space technology ka use karne ke liye ki gayi thi. INSAT-3B ko 21 maarch 2000 ko launch\nkiya gaya tha. Is duration ke dauran, Dr. Krishnaswami Kasturirangan (K. Kasturirangan) Indian space research\norganisation ke major the (unhone 1994 se 2003 tak adhyaksh ke roop me work kiya). Usa duration ke dauran jab ye\nquestion originally poochha gaya tha (2008), do jee maadhavan naayar ISRO ke adhyaksh the. [Q59–Q61]\n● Jab ye question 2018 me poochha gaya tha, taba K. Sivan ne padabhaar sanbhaala tha. Haalaanki, vartamaan parivisible\n(2025) ko dekhate hue, do vee naaraavehiclen ISRO ke adhyaksh hain. Isliye, 'None of the above' sabse safe correct\nanswer hai. Janavaree 2022 me, prakhyat rocket scientist do. S. Somanath ko K. Sivan ke sthana par Indian space\nresearch organisation (ISRO) ke dasaven adhyaksh ke roop me niyukt kiya gaya tha. Jab 2024 ki shuruaat me ye question\npoochha gaya tha, taba S. Somanath adhyaksh the. Haalaanki, janavaree 2025 tak, do vee naaraavehiclen ne ISRO ke\nvartamaan adhyaksh ke roop me padabhaar planetn kar liya hai. Isliye, koi bhi option full vartamaan vaastavikata ko nahi\nshow karta hai. [Q62–Q64]\n● Vyapak kavarej ke liye India vaastav me apne telecom network ko satelliteon (jaise INSAT aur GSAT shrrinkhalaa) se\nconnect karta hai. To, abhistatement (A) true hai. Indiyan neshanal satellite system (INSAT) telecom, prasaarana, weather\nscience aur discovery aur bachaav functions ko pooraa karne ke liye ISRO dwara launch kiye gaye bahuuddesheey\ngeostationary (geostationary) satelliteon ki ek series hai. ek bahupurposeeey system ke roop me, INSAT shrinkhala apni\ntelecom bhoomikaaon ke alaava ek Meteorological Satellite network (important Weather forecast data provide karne) ke\nroop me heavy roop se kaam karti hai. [Q65–Q67]\n● Modern geostationary Communication Satellite jaise INSAT aur GSAT data ki badi amount ko sanbhaalane ke liye C-\nband, Ku-band aur Ka-band jaise high-frequency maaikrovev band ka use karte hain. Simplex communication ek\ncommunication chainal hai jo Only one dishaa me information send karta hai. Choonki India ke paas us time enough\npowershaalee rocket nahi tha, isliye iska pehla dedicated Earth observation satellite, aaeeaaraesa-1e (IRS-1A), maarch\n1988 me Soviet sangha ke Baikanour kosmodrom (vartamaana kajaakistaan me) se dhruveey Sun-tulyakaalika orbit me\nlaunch kiya gaya tha. [Q68–Q70]\n● Sudoor sanvedan (Remote sensing) satellite Earth ki surface ki detailed tasveeren lete hain. Ye data phasal ke svaasthy\nka assessment karne (1), bhoojal ke liye bhaugolik maarkar discoveryne (2), aur khanij bhandaar ka detect lagaane (3) ke\nliye amooly hai. Haalaanki, unhe teevee/phone signal transmit karne ke liye design nahi kiya gaya hai (telecom - 4) aur na\nhi ve sadaka-level ki laaiva kaara speedvidhiyon (yataayata study - 5) ki nigaraanee kar sakte hain. Isliye 1, 2 and 3 only\nsahi hain. [Q71–Q72]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q61, Q62 & Q64 — ISRO Chairman Questions are Outdated\n\n▸Source in questions ko outdated mark karta hai. ISRO Chairman ka answer exam ke notification/year ke according update karna\nchahiye; historical chairman questions ko unke stated year se padhein.\n5. PSLV Missions, Navigation Systems & Launch-Vehicle Evolution\n● Isase pehle ki India bade Communication Satelliteon ko high geostationary orbiton me dhakelane me saksham apne\nsvayan ke hevee-liphta rocket (jaise GSLV) developed karta, wo mainly French Guana me Kourou se launch kiye gaye\nEuropean eriyan rocketon par depend tha. INSAT-3C ko 2002 me Kourou se launch kiya gaya tha. INSAT-4 satellite series\nme pehla, INSAT-4A, India me DTH television prasaaran ko badhaava dene ke liye 22 disanbara, 2005 ko Kourou, French\nGuana se ISRO dwara successfully launch kiya gaya tha. ek aitihaasik upalabdhi me, ISRO ke PSLV-C37 ne 15\npharavaree, 2017 ko ek hi launch ke dauran 104 satelliteon (international graahakon ke mainly chhote nano satelliteon) ko\nsuccessfully orbit me establish kiya. 2021 me spesaeks ke isase aage nikalane tak ye world record rahaa. [Q73–Q75]\n● Jaisaa ki oopara bataay gaya hai, ye highly worldsaneey dhruveey satellite launch vehicle (Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle)\ntha, specially PSLV-C37 mission, jisne 104 satelliteon ka meela ka patthar haasil kiya. Kailendar varsha 2022 ko banda\nkarte hue, ISRO ka last peeesaelavee (PSLV) launch PSLV-C54 mission tha. Isane 26 November 2022 ko Earth\nobservation satellite-06 (oshanasaita-3) aur aatha nano-satelliteon ko successfully orbit me establish kiya. Nyoospes indiya\nlimited (NSIL) ke through nishpaadit ek dedicated commercial mission me, PSLV-C55 rocket ne 22 aprail 2023 ko do\nsingaapur ke satelliteon, TeLEOS-2 aur Lumelite-4 ko successfully orbit me establish kiya. [Q76–Q78]\n● 1 janavaree, 2024 ko poori tarah se launch kiya gaya, XPoSat black hole aur neutron sistars jaisee ghatanaaon ka study\nkarne ke liye dedicated space-aadhaarita eksa-re polaarimetree me India ka pioneer pravesh hai (statement 1). SITE\n(saitelaaita instrakshanal television eksaperimenta) ko 1975 me launch kiya gaya tha. APPLE (erivehicle paisenjar peloda\neksaperimenta) satellite ko 19 June 1981 ko French Guana ke Kourou se eriyan launch vaahan dwara launch kiya gaya\ntha. [Q79–Q81]\n● Jaisaa ki pehle bataay gaya hai, India ka pehla praayogik geostationary Communication Satellite, APPLE, June 19, 1981\nko launch kiya gaya tha. INSAT-1D ko June 12th, 1990 ko launch kiya gaya tha. Ye ek bahukriyasheel (multifunctional)\nsatellite tha jo India ke liye telephone, television aur weather observation service provide karta tha. INSAT-2A India ka\npehla indigenous built satellite hone ka gaurav rakhta hai. Ise July 10th, 1992 ko French Guana ke Kourou se successfully\nspace me launch kiya gaya tha. [Q82–Q84]\n● 10 July 2006 ko INSAT-4C Communication Satellite le go rahaa GSLV (Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle) apne\nmaarga se bhatak gaya aur liphta-opha ke immediate baad usamen visphot ho gaya. Usa time INSAT-4C ka weight 2168\nkggraam tha. IRNSS-1A Indian kshetreey nevigeshan satellite system (IRNSS) ke hisse ke roop me launch kiya gaya pehla\nsatellite tha. IRNSS starmandal (jisakaa naam NavIC hai) me saata active satellite shamil hain: teen geostationary orbiton\nme aur chaara jhukee hui bhoosamakaalik orbiton me located hain. Isliye, statement 1 sahi hai. [Q85–Q87]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\n● NavIC (naabhika) Indian kshetreey nevigeshan satellite system (IRNSS) ko diya gaya parichaalan naam hai. Is short naam\nka meaning \"Navigation with Indian Constellation\" hai. Listed options me se, Japan ka apanaa freelance kshetreey satellite\nnevigeshan system hai jise kvaasee-jenitha satellite system (QZSS) kaha jata hai, jise michibikee (Michibiki) bhi kaha jata\nhai. Galileo projekt (Galileo Project) European Union ka freelance vaishvik satellite nevigeshan system hai. Ise European\nspace Agency (ESA) ke through banaya gaya tha taaki American GPS aur Russian GLONASS systems se freelance ek\nvaikalpik aur highly accurate sthiti service provide ki go sake. [Q88–Q90]\n● GPS ka matalab Global Positioning System hai. Ye joint raajya USA ki government ke svaamitv wala aur yoonaaited\nstetsa space phorsa dwara operated widely use kiya jane wala space-aadhaarita rediyo nevigeshan system hai. Global\nPositioning System (GPS) sirpha nevigeshan se kahin zyada kaam karta hai. Ye aworldsaneey roop se accurate time signal\n(timing signal) provide karta hai. India ke launch yanon ka development maamoolee shuruaat se hua aur ye lagaataar\nsaksham hota gaya: [Q91–Q93]\n● (i) SLV-3 ne 1980 me Rohini satellite (RS-1) ko orbit me successfully establish kiya tha (B se mela khaata hai). [Q94]\n6. ISRO Centres, Sriharikota, Thumba & Aviation Basics\n● India me ina instituteon ke bhaugolik jnyaan ke basis par: Hassan me maastar kantrol phaisilitee (MCF) Karnataka raajya\nme ISRO dwara established ek important establishment hai. A. ISRO (Indian space research sangathana) ka mukhyalay\nBengaluru (3) me located hai. [Q95–Q97]\n● ISRO satellite sentar (jisakaa naam badalakar 2018 me yoo aara Rao satellite sentara, URSC kar diya gaya) satelliteon ke\ndevelopment ke liye major hub hai aur ye Bengaluru, Karnataka me located hai, na ki Shriharikota me. Shriharikota sateesh\ndhavan space hub (praathamika launch suvidhaa) ka ghara hai. Space application hub (SAC) Ahmedabad, Gujarat me\napne sthana ke saath correctly mela khaata hai. A. VSSC ka milaan trivendram (Thiruvananthapuram) se correctly kiya\ngaya hai. [Q98–Q100]\n● Indian sudoor sanvedan institute (IIRS) ISRO ke under ek major prashikshan aur academic institute hai. Ye uttaraakhand\nke Dehradun me located hai. Thiruvananthapuram me Vikram Sarabhai space hub (VSSC) ISRO ka major hub hai jo\nlaunch vehicle (launch vehicle) technology ke design aur development ke liye jimmedaar hai. Ye mainly rocket launch karne\nke liye pranodak (propellants) me research aur satellite launch vehicle (jaise PSLV, GSLV) ke samagr development se\nrelated hai. PraVaHa ISRO ke Vikram Sarabhai space hub (VSSC) me developed ek lesspyooteshanal phlooid\ndaayanemiks (CFD) software hai. Isliye, statement 1 sahi hai. [Q101–Q103]\n● Thumba ikvetoriyal rocket lonching Station (TERLS) 1962 me established ek Indian spesaport hai. Ye\nThiruvananthapuram, Kerala me located hai, jo main ground India ke dakshinee sire ke paas, Earth ke magnetic\nbhoomadhy line ke bahut kareeb hai. Shriharikota Andhra Pradesh ke nellor jile me shaara (SHAR) project bastee me\nlocated bangaal ki khaadee ke tata se doora ek baadha dveepa hai. Ye Pulicat lake (Pulicat Lake) ko bangaal ki khaadee\nse alaga karta hai. Shriharikota, jo sateesh dhavan space hub ka ghara hai, Andhra Pradesh raajya me located hai. [Q104–\nQ106]\n● Kaakaraapaar ek nuclear energy sandevice ka sthala hai (A-3). 23 pharavaree, 2004 ko, Shriharikota me sateesh dhavan\nspace hub ke andara located thosa pranodak (solid propellant) sandevice me ek bhayankar visphot aur uske baad aaga\nlaga gayi thi, jiske parinaamasvaroop hataahat hue the aur suvidha ko damage pahuncha tha. Havaaee jahaaj ke pankhon\nki ooparee surface uttala (baahara ki direction ghumaavadaara) hoti hai aur nichalee surface chaapaloosee/avatala\n(eyaraphoila aakaara) hoti hai taaki air flow me herapher kiya go sake. Isliye abhistatement (A) true hai. [Q107–Q109]\n● naam ke baavajooda, ek havaaee jahaaj ke 'blaika boksa' (phlaaita data rikordara) ko chamakeele, garmee pratirodhee\n\"international naarangee\" (Orange) ranga me rangaa jata hai taaki ise highly visiblemaan banaye go sake aur durghatana\nke baad malabe me discoveryna aasaan ho sake. [Q110]\n7. Moon Missions: Chandrayaan, LUPEX, Luna & Aditya-L1\n● Moon Earth ka elessaatr praakritik satellite hai. Ye Earth ke charon direction orbit karta hai. Moon par India ka pehla\nmission Chandrayaan-1, 22 aktoobar 2008 ko launch kiya gaya tha. Kai yuddhaabhyason ke baad, vaahan ko 8 November\n2008 ko lunar orbit me successfully establish kiya gaya tha. India ke dedicated lunar anveshan missionon ko diya gaya\nnaam \"Chandrayaan\" hai. [Q111–Q113]\n● Chandrayaan-1 ko Andhra Pradesh raajya ke Shriharikota dveepa par located sateesh dhavan space hub se launch kiya\ngaya tha. Chandrayaan-2 project ke early yojana aur developmentaatmak charanon ke dauran (jab ye question 2010 ke\naasapaas taiyar kiya gaya tha), do mayalasvaamee annaaduraee (jinhone Chandrayaan-1 ka bhi netritv kiya tha) project ka\nnetritv kar rahe the. Chandrayaan-2 mission ka main purpose anveshan ke liye lunar dakshinee dhruva (South Pole) field\nko lakshit karna tha, na ki uttaree dhruva ko. Isliye statement (C) true nahi hai. [Q114–Q116]\n● Chandrayaan-2 ko Shriharikota ke sateesh dhavan space hub se launch kiya gaya tha, jo Andhra Pradesh raajya me\nlocated hai. Chandrayaan-2 spacecraft ko orbit me launch karne ke liye heavy-bharaless (heavy-lift) lonchar GSLV-MkIII-\nM1 (jise aba aksar LVM3 ke roop me naamit kiya jata hai) ka successfully use ISRO dwara kiya gaya tha. Statement 1\naccurate hai. Chandrayaan-2 laindar ki aanshik viphalata ke baad, Chandrayaan-3 ko ek pratyaksh anuvartee mission ke\nroop me design kiya gaya tha jo specially ek successful, safe sophta lainding mila karne aur lunar surface par rover ko\ntainaat karne par kendrit tha. [Q117–Q119]\n● APXS (alphaa paartikal eksa-re spektromeetara) Chandrayaan-3 mission ke prajnyaan rover par lagaa ek specific scientist\ndevice tha. Loonar polara eksaploreshan (LUPEX) mission India ke ISRO (ISRO) aur Japan ke jaaksa (JAXA) ke beech ek\nsahayogaatmak prayas hai jo Moon ke dakshinee dhruva ki jaanch par kendrit hai. (statement 1 sahi hai). Moon Express\nMoon par jane wali world ki pehli private flight yojana hai. 2017 se kaaryanvit is yojana ko 3 agasta, 2016 ko American\nsangheey uddayan prashaasan dwara sahamati provide ki gayi thi. [Q120–Q122]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\n● June 2024 me, China ka chaanga'ee 6 (Chang'e 6) mission Moon ke sudoor hisse (andhere hisse) se Earth par mittee\nlaane wala pehla lunar mission bana gaya. Loonaa-25 agasta 2023 me ek asuccessful Russian lunar laindar mission tha.\nIski yojana international lunar research Station (ILRS) ke hisse ke roop me banayi gayi thi. Aditya-L1 Sun ka study karne\nwali pehli Indian space-aadhaarita observatory hai. Ise 2 sitanbar 2023 ko Shriharikota se launch kiya gaya tha. [Q123–Q125]\n● Aaditya-L1 me Photosphere (photosphere), kromospheeyar aur korona ka nireekshan karne ke liye saata scientist peloda\nhain. Chaara peloda directly Sun ko dekhate hain (rimota sensinga) aur shesha teen L1 point par particles aur kshetron ka\nina-seetoo observation study karte hain. [Q126]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q113 — Multiple Correct Answers\n\n▸Source Q113 ko multiple-correct mark karta hai. Chandrayaan-I se related naming/mission statements ko exact option wording\nke context me evaluate karein.\n8. Mangalyaan, China & International Space Cooperation\n● Maarsa orbitar mission (MOM), jise anaupachaarik roop se Marsvehicle ke naam se jana jata hai, India ka pehla\nantaraplaneteey mission tha. (statement I sahi hai). India ka pehla intaraplenetaree mission, maarsa orbitar mission\n(Marsvehicle), 5 navanbar 2013 ko launch kiya gaya tha. Marsvehicle ko maarsa orbitar mission (MOM) bhi kaha jata hai.\n(statement 1 sahi hai). [Q127–Q129]\n● Tiyangong Space Station China dwara built ek sthayee roop se crew wala Space Station hai. Iska core module 'Tianhe'\nhai, pehla Lab module 'Wentian' tha, aur aktoobar 2022 me launch kiya gaya doosra aur last module 'Mengtian' (Mengtian)\ntha. Tivehiclevena-1 China National space prashaasan (CNSA) ka ek antaraplaneteey mission hai jisme Mars planet par\nbheja gaya ek robotik spacecraft (spacecraft) shamil hai (jisme ek orbitara, laindar aur joorong rover shamil tha). China ne\nsitanbar 2008 me country ke pehle spesavok ka prayas karne ke liye *teen* (chaara nahi) space yatriyon ke saath\nshenajhou-7 launch kiya tha. Isliye, statement (A) sahi nahi hai. [Q130–Q132]\n● Misiyas (Micius), jiska naam ek praaChina Chinaee daarSaturnka ke naam par rakha gaya hai, world ka pehla kvaantam\nCommunication Satellite (QUESS) hai, jise agasta 2016 me China dwara launch kiya gaya tha. NISAR ka full form NASA-\nISRO synthetic aparchar Radar (NASA-ISRO Synthetic Aperture Radar) hai. Ye NASA aur Indian space research\norganisation (ISRO) ke beech ek joint Earth-avalokana mission hai. CNES (neshanala sentar phora space stadeeja) France\nki government space Agency hai. [Q133–Q135]\n● Russia ne Arctic field me climate aur paryavaran ki nigaraanee ke mission par pharavaree 2021 me apanaa space satellite\nArcticaa-ema (Arktika-M) launch kiya. Navanbar 2022 me, Japan ki space Agency JAXA ne ghoshana ki ki usane apne\nwater-sanchaalita kyoobasait EQUULEUS ko aage badhane ke liye successfully steam ka use kiya hai. Water pranodak\nsystem use karke kam-Earth ki orbit se pare ye world ka pehla successful orbit control tha. Pharavaree 2018 me, JAXA\n(Japan eyarospes eksaploreshan Agency) ne ek maaikrosaitelaait ko orbit me established karne ke liye sanshodhit ek\nSS-520 saaunding rocket ko successfully launch kiya, jisse ye satellite ko orbit me le jane wala aba tak ka sabse small\nrocket bana gaya. [Q136–Q138]\n● NASA (NASA) ki jeta propalshan leboretaree (JPL), jo Agency ke kai robotik space missionon ka prabandhan karti hai,\njoint raajya USA ke California raajya ke Pasadena me located hai. Greesd laaitaning ya jeeela-10 prototype NASA dwara\ntest kiya gaya baitaree se chalne wala 10-engine wala electric aircraft hai. Ise heleekoptar ki tarah lanbavat flight bharane\naur utarane ke liye design kiya gaya hai, lekin pankhon wale aircraft ki tarah kushalata se udataa hai. [Q139–Q140]\n9. NASA Missions, Planets, Jet/Rocket Principles & Cryogenics\n● NASA ne aktoobar 2020 me pushti ki ki uske mission, SOFIA (straitospherika objarvetaree phora inphraared estronomee)\nne kleviyas kretar me Moon ki Sun ki roshanee wali surface par water ke anuon ki upasthiti ki pushti ki hai. Comet ke\ninternal bhaaga ki structure ka study karne ke liye NASA ka deepa impaikt mission (Deep Impact Mission) launch kiya gaya\ntha. Is spacecraft ne 4 July 2005 ko kometa tempel 1 (Temple-1) me ek impaiktar ko successfully kraish (takkara) kiya tha.\nDie gaye options me, Phoenix NASA ke maarsa skaaut programme ke under Mars planet par space anveshan mission par\nek robotik spacecraft tha. Ye 2008 me Mars planet par utara tha. [Q141–Q143]\n● Spirit (MER-A), NASA ke Mars anveshan rover mission ke do judavaan rovars me se pehla tha. Ye 4 janavaree 2004 ko\nMars planet par successfully utara. Iska judavaan, aporchunitee (Opportunity), kuch saptaah baad utara. NASA ke\nmissionon ko Mars par ateeta ki water speedvidhi ke saakshya, jipsam ke bhandaar (water ki upasthiti me banane wala ek\nkhanija), aur Methane gas ke gubaar (jo Earth par aksar jeevit jeevon dwara utpann hote hain) mile hain. Isliye, ye teenon\nsaamoohik roop se Mars planet par ateeta ya vartamaan jeevan ki sanbhaavana badhaate hain. July 2018 me,\nshodhakartaaon ne Radar data ka use karte hue Mars planet par tarala water ki ek huge bhoomigat jheela ka detect\nlagaane ki information dee, jo planet ke dakshinee dhruveey barpha ki topee ke neeche lagbhag 1.5 km neeche located hai.\n[Q144–Q146]\n● Vibhinn orbitars aur rovars dwara Mars ke vaayumandal me Methane ka detect lagaay gaya hai. Iske alawa, Jupiter ke\nsaath-saath Saturn, yoorenas aur nepachyoon ke vaayumandal me naturally Methane ki amount paaee jati hai. Isliye, Mars\naur Jupiter donon sahi option hain. Saturn ka vaayumandal mainly haaidrojan aur hiliyam se bana hai, lekin die gaye\noptions me, Carbon monoxide, Nitrogen ya Sulphur dioxide ke comparison me Methane sabse important amount me\nmaujood hai. Hamare saura mandal ke sabhi planeton me Saturn ka ausata ghanatv sabse kam hai, lagbhag 0.7 graama\nprati ghana senteemeetara. Iska ghanatv water se bhi kam hai, jiska meaning hai ki ye saiddhaantik roop se water ke\nkaaphee bade poola me taira sakta hai. [Q147–Q149]\n● NASA (NASA) ke spacecraft (jaise Discovery) ke external tainka me Liquid hydrogen fuel aur Liquid oxygen okseedaaijar\nbharaa hota hai jo liphta-opha ke dauran shuttle ke main engineon ko power provide karta hai. Moola pareeksha question\nme diya gaya koi bhi option sahi nahi hai. Apolo 8 (Apollo 8) pehli maanavayukt space flight thi jisne Earth ki nichalee orbit\nko chhoda Moon tak reach aur usakee orbit karke lautane ka work kiya tha. Ise 21 disanbara, 1968 ko launch kiya gaya tha."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\nSELENE (selenolojikala enda engineering eksaplorara), jise iske upanaam 'kaaguya' se bhi jana jata hai, doosra Japanee\n(Japan) lunar kaksheey spacecraft tha. Ise JAXA dwara 2007 me launch kiya gaya tha. [Q150–Q152]\n● Ek jeta engine ko apanaa fuel jalaane ke liye essential okseejan mila karne ke liye Earth ke vaayumandal ki requirement\nhoti hai, isliye ye space ke nirvaat me kaam nahi kar sakta hai (statement 1 sahi hai). Commercial jeta aircraft\nvaayumandaleey vikshobh (turbulence) se bachane ke liye aksar nichale Stratosphere me flight bharate hain. Choonki isme\nlagbhag koi water vaashp nahi hota hai, isliye weather-sanbandhita vikshobh paidaa karne ke liye practical roop se koi\nbaadal nahi hote hain. ek jeta engine raikhik sanveg (linear momentum) ke sanrakshan ke principle par kaam karta hai, jo\nanivaary roop se nyootan ke speed ke teesare niyama (pratyeka kriya ke liye, ek same aur vipareet pratikriy hoti hai) ka ek\napplication hai. Peechhe ki direction chhodee gayi high speed wali nikaas gaisen aage ki direction dhakka (thrust) paidaa\nkarti hain. [Q153–Q155]\n● Jeta engine ki tarah hi, rocket bhi sanveg sanrakshan (conservation of momentum) ke principle par kaam karta hai.\nChoonki garma nikaas gaisen peechhe se teevra speed se dhakelee jati hain, rocket aage ki direction dhakela jata hai.\n'straitalaaita' (Stratosphere aur satellite se bana word) ek human rahita, high elevation wala eyaraship (havaaee pota) hai jo\nStratosphere me tainaat hota hai. Ye vaayarales communication ya observation provide karne ke liye satellite ke same\nkaam karta hai, lekin Earth ki surface ke bahut kareeb rahata hai. Physics me, kraayojeniks me atyant kam temperature par\nsaamagriyon ke production aur behavior ka study shamil hai. Aama taur par, -150°C (ya 123 K) se kam ke kisi bhi\ntemperature ko kraayojenik maana jata hai. [Q156–Q158]\n● Kraayojeniks (bahut kam temperature ka vijnyaana) ka space yatraa (tarala fuel jaise haaidrojan aur okseejana), magnetic\nuttolan (maigleva trenon me use kiye jane wale suparakandakting ilektromaignets ko thanda karna), aur sensitive\nteleemetree device (riseevara me tharmal shora ko kam karne ke liye) me important application hai. Kraayojenik engine\nvishesh rocket engine hain jo kraayojenik fuel ya okseedaaijar ka use karte hain, jiska meaning hai ki gaison ko taraleekrit\n(liquefied) kiya gaya hai aur atyant kam temperature par sanplaneteet kiya gaya hai. Ve rocket (jaise jeeesaelavee) ke\nooparee charanon ke liye highly kushal pranodan provide karte hain. Kraayojenik engine aama taur par okseedaaijar ke\nroop me Liquid oxygen aur fuel ke roop me Liquid hydrogen ka use karta hai. Inhen tarala state me banaye rakhne ke liye\natyant kam temperature par storage ki requirement hoti hai. Space shuttle kraayojenik engine ka bhi use kiya jata hai.\n[Q159–Q161]\n● Behada thande tarala fuel use karke high thrast (dhakkaa) provide karne ke liye Space Shuttle aur advanced rocket launch\nvaahanon (jaise GSLV) me kraayojenik engine ka use kiya jata hai. Die gaye options me se sabhi ka use rocket pranodak\n(propellant) ke roop me kiya jata hai. Liquid hydrogen, Liquid hydrazine aur mittee ke tela (RP-1) ka use fuel ke roop me\nkiya jata hai jabki Liquid oxygen ka use okseedaaijar ke roop me kiya jata hai. Pranodak fuel aur okseedaaijar ka mishran\nhai. [Q162–Q163]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q147, Q151 & Q163 — Source-Sensitive Questions\n\n▸Q147 source me multiple-correct hai: methane ek se adhik planetary atmospheres/context me mil sakti hai.\n\n▸Q151 ke options/date wording me source error/dispute marked hai; Apollo-8 historical date ko standard reference se cross-check\nkarein.\n\n▸Q163 rocket propellant question source me disputed hai; propellant classification fuel + oxidizer pair par depend karti hai.\n10. Indian Launchers, Satellites, EDUSAT, GSAT & BHUVAN\n● India electronics limited (BEL) GaAs (gailiyama aarArmyida) saura sela developed karne ke liye ISRO ke saath sahayog\nkar rahaa hai. Space ke liye ye saura sela technology ke maamale me zyada advanced hain aur space me bijalee paidaa\nkarne me kushal hain, jo Indian satelliteon ki deerghaayu me help karte hain. India ne aktoobar 2006 me 50 sekand ke liye\nek full kraayojenik charan ka successfully test kiya tha (statement 1 sahi hai). RISAT-2 ek Indian Radar tohi (nigaraanee)\nsatellite hai jise seemaaon ki nigaraanee ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Ise 20 aprail 2009 ko PSLV-C12 rocket dwara\nsuccessfully launch kiya gaya tha. [Q164–Q166]\n● Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki INSAT series ke sabhi satelliteon ko videshon se launch nahi kiya gaya tha. Example ke\nliye, INSAT-4C ko 10 July 2006 ko Shriharikota se launch kiya gaya tha. Statement 1 sahi hai: PSLV ka use mainly Earth-\navalokana (rimota sensinga) satelliteon ko dhruveey orbiton me established karne ke liye kiya jata hai, jabki GSLV ko heavy\nCommunication Satelliteon ko high bhoosamakaalik orbiton me established karne ke liye design kiya gaya tha. Doppler\neffect use karke ek kritrim satellite ko Earth se bahut accurate roop se traika kiya ja sakta hai. Satellite lagaataar rediyo\nsignal emit karta hai, aur graaund Station ina sanketon ki frequency (dopalara shiphta) me badalaav ka analysis karte hain\nkyonki satellite unki direction ya doora jata hai, jisse iski accurate speed aur prakshepavakr (trajectory) ki calculation ki jati\nhai. [Q167–Q169]\n● SLV-3 (saitelaaita launch vehicle-3) koi space satellite nahi hai; ye satelliteon ko orbit me established karne ke liye ISRO\ndwara developed ek rocket/launch vaahan hai. GSLV ek satellite launch vhikal (rocket) hai, ye apne aapa me koi satellite\nnahi hai. GSLV-D2 is vaahan ki doosri developmentaatmak test flight thi (maee 2003 me launch ki gayi). Statement 1\nincorrect hai: science rela rela ministry aur 'vijnyaana prasaara' (vijnyaana aur technology department ke under) dwara joint\nroop se organized kiya gaya tha, na ki mainly CSIR dwara. [Q170–Q172]\n● EDUSAT (GSAT-3) specially shiksha field ki maangon ko pooraa karne ke liye dedicated satellite hai. Ise GSLV-F01\nrocket use karke 20 sitanbar 2004 ko Shriharikota se launch kiya gaya tha. India ka pehla full Meteorological Satellite\n'METSAT' 12 sitanbar 2002 ko successfully launch kiya gaya tha. (statement 1 sahi hai). 2002 me launch kiye gaye India ke\npehle dedicated Meteorological Satellite METSAT ka naam baad me pradhaan mantree atala Biharee vaajapeyee dwara\nIndian moola ki divangat NASA astronaut kalpana chaavala (jinakee Columbia Space Shuttle durghatana me mrityu ho gayi\nthi) ke sammaan me kalpanaa-I rakha gaya. [Q173–Q175]\n● Jaisaa ki pichhale questionon me shamil kiya gaya hai, Meteorological Satellite METSAT (baad me KALPANA-1) ko ISRO\ndwara sitanbar 2002 me launch kiya gaya tha. SATYABAMASAT (Sathyabamasat) ek microscopic praayogik satellite hai"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Space Full Mind Map\njise chennew ke satyabhaama worldvidyalay ke chhaatron aur shikshakon dwara greenahaaus gaison par data ekatra\nkarne ke liye develop kiya gaya hai. Isliye, ye ek academic institute ka satellite hai. Apne heavy weight ki wajah se, India ka\nadvanced Communication Satellite GSAT-8 21 maee 2011 ko dakshin USA ke French Guana me Kourou se erivehicle-V\nlaunch vehicle dwara successfully launch kiya gaya tha. [Q176–Q178]\n● GSAT-7 (jise rukminee ke naam se bhi jana jata hai) ISRO dwara developed ek advanced maltee-band Communication\nSatellite hai. Ye specially Military communication ke liye Indian Navy ko dedicated hai, jo iski bloo-vaatara capacityon ka\nexpansion karta hai. GSLV-D3 rocket ke teesare charan ki viphalata ki wajah se GSAT-4 (April 2010 me launch kiya gaya)\norbit tak reach me viphal rahaa. 29 sitanbar 2012 ko India ne guvehicle space hub se erivehicle-5 rocket use karke heavy\ndooraCommunication Satellite GSAT-10 ko successfully launch kiya tha. [Q179–Q181]\n● GSAT-6A, ek high power wala esa-band Communication Satellite, ISRO dwara 29 maarch 2018 ko Shriharikota se GSLV-\nF08 rocket use karke launch kiya gaya tha. (nota: launch ke kuch time baad hi satellite se sanpark toota gaya tha). Bhuvan\n(Bhuvan) ISRO dwara developed ek web-aadhaarita upayogita (sophtaveyara application/jiyoportal) hai. Ye users ko Earth\nki surface ke 2dee/3dee represent ka detect lagaane ki allow karta hai, jo Google meaning ke Indian version ke same kaam\nkarta hai. [Q182–Q183]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q183\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0363","t":"15 Defence Technology Hinglish Corrected","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Defence Technology Full Mind Map\n🛡️ DEFENCE TECHNOLOGY — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\nरक्षाप्रौद्योगिकी· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. DRDO, Quantum Lab & Next-Generation Missile Technology\n2. IGMDP & Core Indian Missile Systems\n3. Fighter Aircraft, Airlift, AWACS & Submarines\n4. Agni Series, Radar, Missile Programme & Shaurya\n5. Indigenous Combat Platforms & Naval Systems\n6. Ballistic vs Cruise Missiles & BrahMos\n7. UAVs, Fighter Technology, AESA, THAAD & FOBS\n8. Arms Control, Export Regimes & NATO\n9. Operations, DefExpo, Naval Forums & Joint Military Exercises\n1. DRDO, Quantum Lab & Next-Generation Missile Technology\n● Defence research aur Development Organisation (DRDO) India government ke Ministry of Defence me Department of\nDefence Research and Development ke under major Agency hai. 2021 ke dauran, Indian Army ne Madhya Pradesh ke\nMhow me Military College of Telecommunication Engineering me ek quantum computing laboratory established ki. Mission\nDivyastra indigenously developed Agni-V missile ke pehle flight test ko refer karta hai jo 'Multiple Independently Targetable\nRe-entry Vehicle' (MIRV) technology se equipped hai. [Q1–Q3]\n● Very Short-Range Air Defence System (VSHORADS) DRDO dwara developed 4th-generation, technical roop se advanced\nminiaturized, man-portable air-defence system (MANPADS) hai. Rudram-I DRDO dwara developed ek New Generation\nAnti-Radiation Missile (NGARM) hai. Ye India ki pehli indigenous anti-radiation air-to-surface missile hai. Rudram-II ek air-\nto-surface anti-radiation missile system (air-to-air nahi) hai. Isliye, statement 1 incorrect hai. [Q4–Q6]\n2. IGMDP & Core Indian Missile Systems\n● Nag IGMDP ke under India me developed “Fire and Forget” 3rd-generation anti-tank guided missile hai. Prithvi ek surface-\nto-surface missile hai (A-3). Pinaka India me produced aur DRDO dwara developed ek multiple rocket launcher hai, ye ek\nguided missile nahi hai. Agni, Aakash aur Nag sabhi guided missile hain. [Q7–Q9]\n● Trishul Integrated Guided Missile Development Programme (IGMDP) ke ek part ke roop me India dwara developed short-\nrange surface-to-air missile hai. Nag (NAG) 3rd-generation anti-tank guided missile correctly matched hai. Prithvi India ki\npehli indigenous developed surface-to-surface ballistic missile hai, jise IGMDP ke under DRDO dwara develop kiya gaya\nhai. [Q10–Q12]\n● Trishul short-range surface-to-air missile hai (A-3). Aakash medium-range surface-to-air missile hai (A-2). Nirbhay India ki\npehli indigenously designed aur developed long-range *subsonic* (supersonic nahi) cruise missile hai. Isliye statement 4\nincorrect hai. [Q13–Q15]\n● Astra DRDO dwara developed beyond-visual-range air-to-air Missile (BVRAAM) hai. Initial versions ki range 80 km tak thi\n(na ki 90 km jaisa ki option d me strictly se kahaa gaya hai). Isliye, commission ne statement (d) ko incorrect maana. Astra\nDefence Research and Development Organisation dwara developed all-weather me kaam karne wali 'beyond-visual-range\nair-to-air Missile' (BVRAAM) hai. Ye India dwara developed pehli air-to-air missile hai. Astra enemy aircraft ko target\nbanane ke liye fighter aircraft se launch kiye jane ke liye developed ek air-to-air missile hai. [Q16–Q18]\n● Astra (ASTRA) ek indigenous biyond visual range (BVR) air-to-air missile hai. Light Combat Aircraft (LCA) Tejas ne govaa\nke tata se lagbhag 20,000 pheeta ki elevation par iska successful test kiya. Astra DRDO dwara developed ek active Radar\nhoming beyond-visual-range air-to-air Missile hai. Missile ka pehli baar 9 maee, 2003 ko baalaasor (odishaa) me\nsuccessfully test kiya gaya tha. Trishul, ek suparasonik surface-to-air missile programmea, technical technical issues aur\ndelays ki wajah se 2008 me DRDO dwara official taur par banda (shelvedd) kar diya gaya tha. [Q19–Q21]\n● Trishul ko short-range ki, tvarit pratikriy wali, suparasonik surface-to-air missile ke roop me design kiya gaya tha. Die gaye\noptions me, Nag Missile ki range sabse kam hai. Iske ground based version ki maximum range 4 km hai. 'Agni' naam\nIGMDP ke under India dwara developed Surface to surface ballistic missileon (medium se intercontinental range) ki series\nse related hai. [Q22–Q24]\n● Statement (b) incorrect hai kyonki kuch engineer ya praakritik roop se paae jane wale vaayaras (jaise baikteeriyopheja)\nspecific harmful baikteeriy ko lakshit karke ya pradooshakon ko neecha dikhaane me help karke paryavaran ko\nsakaaraatmak roop se prabhaavit kar sakte hain, isliye paryavaran pradooshan ko kam kar sakte hain. Statement (c)\nincorrect hai kyonki Trishul, jise short-range surface-to-air missile ke roop me develop kiya gaya tha, ki effective range\nkevala 9 km thi, 30 km nahi. Ye project 2008 me official taur par banda kar di gayi thi. Navanbar 2006 me, DRDO ne ek\nintarasepshan test kiya jisme ek ekso-etamospherika haaiparasonik intaraseptar Missile ne 'dushmana' Prithvi Missile\nLakshya ko nashta kar diya. Statement 1 sahi hai. [Q25–Q27]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q25 & Q27 — Source Context Needs Care\n\n▸Q25 ka explanation defence-topic se unrelated virus/environment fact deta hai. Source coverage preserve ki gayi hai, lekin ise\ndefence concept ke roop me memorize na karein.\n\n▸Q27 me Prithvi-II attacking surface-to-surface missile hai; metro defence ke liye interceptor/PAD concept alag hai.\n3. Fighter Aircraft, Airlift, AWACS & Submarines\n● Listed aircrafton me se koi bhi paanchaveen generation ka fighter aircraft nahi hai. Raaphel aur Tejas MK-1 ko 4.5veen\ngeneration ka 'omaneerola' / malteerol aircraft maana jata hai. Miga-29 4th generation ka ladaakoo jeta hai. C-130J supara"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Defence Technology Full Mind Map\nharakyoolis ek highly advanced chaara-engine tarboprop sainya parivahan aircraft hai jo lokahid maartin eyaronotiks dwara\nbuilt hai, jiska mukhyalay The United States of America me hai. Ilyushin IL-78 ek Soviet chaara engine wala havaaee fuel\nbharane wala Tankra hai. Indian Air Force aircraft ko 'MARS' (mida-Air riphyooling System) ke roop me refer karti hai. [Q28–\nQ30]\n● BMP-II ek ubhayachar inphaintree ladaakoo vaahan (jameena/water se ladane wala vaahana) hai, aircraft nahi. BMP-II ke\nIndian version ko Sarath (BMP-II) (Sarath) ke naam se jana jata hai. INS arihant (Arihant) India ki nuclear energy operated\nSubmarine hai (A-4). INS Chakra 8,140 tana ki akulaa category ki, Nuclear-powered submarine hai, jise Russia se patte\n(lease) par liya gaya hai, jise aprail 2012 me Indian Navy me shamil kiya gaya tha. [Q31–Q33]\n● INS Sindhurakshak Indian Navy ki Russian built deejala-ilektrika Submarine thi. Dukhad baata ye hai ki agasta 2013 me\nisme bhishan aaga laga gayi aur ye Mumbai ke nausainik dokayard me dooba gayi. INS Viraat aur INS Vikrant\naircraftvaahak pota (aircraft carriers) hain. INS arihant India ki pehli indigenous built Nuclear-powered submarine hai. Ise\nagasta 2016 me Indian Navy me shamil kiya gaya tha. [Q34–Q35]\n4. Agni Series, Radar, Missile Programme & Shaurya\n● Agni-I (Agni-I) surface-to-surface par maara karne wali short-range ki ballistic Missile (SRBM) hai. Ye Prithvi Missile aur\nlong-range Agni-II ke beech ki seemaa ke antara ko paatata hai. 28 maarcha, 2010 ko odisha tata par vhilar dveepa\n(Wheeler's Island) se 700 km ki range wali nuclear-Saksham surface-to-surface par maara karne wali Agni-I ballistic Missile\nka successfully test kiya gaya tha. Dhanush Missile Prithvi Missile ka nausainik (naval) version hai. Iski range 350\nkilomeetar hai. [Q36–Q38]\n● Agni-II (AGNI-II) ek madhyam distance ki surface-to-surface ballistic missile hai jisakee effective range 2000-2500 km hai.\nIse IGMDP ke under develop kiya gaya tha. Hansaa flight prashikshan (flight training) ke liye ek general aircraftn havaaee\njahaaj hai. Ise India ki National eyarospes laboratoryon (NAL) dwara design kiya gaya tha. Hansaa-2 iske sanskaranon me\nse ek hai. Phaalkan (Phalcon) cruise missile nahi hai; ye ijaraail (Russia nahi) dwara built ek eyaraborn arlee vaarning\nlessaand enda kantrol (AEWC&C) Radar system hai. India ne ye system Israel se khareeda hai. Isliye yugma (b) incorrect\nhai. [Q39–Q41]\n● India ne ijaraail se phaalkan eyaraborn arlee vaarning lessaand enda kantrol (AEWC&C) Radar system mila ki hai. India\nne Israel se 'baraaka' anti-Missile defence system khareedee. Moola baraak Missileen Indian Navy ke jahaajon jaise\naircraftvaahak pota aaeeenaes viraat (INS Virat) par tainaat ki gayi thin. Baraaka-8 (Barak-8) madhyam se long-range\nsurface-to-air missile (SAM) system hai jise India ke DRDO (DRDO) aur ijaraail eyarospes indastreej (IAI) dwara joint roop\nse develop kiya gaya hai. [Q42–Q44]\n● Indian Navy ke liye ek human rahita (paayalata rahita) heleekoptar ko India ke hindustaan eyaronotiks limited (HAL) aur\nijaraail eyarakraapht indastreej (IAI) dwara joint roop se develop kiya gaya hai. Franceeesee eyarospes kanpanee Dassault\nAviation ne 2016 me hastaaksharit ek saude ke under Indian Air Force ko 36 raaphel malteerol phaaitar jeta ka\ndevelopment aur aapoorti ki. Arjun Indian Army ke liye DRDO dwara developed ek modern teesri generation ka main\nyuddhak Tank (MBT) hai. [Q45–Q47]\n● T-90S ek Russian moola ka main yuddhak Tank hai. India me avaadee (Avadi) located hevee vhikals phaiktree me\nindigenously asenbal kiye gaye pehle aise Tank ka naam 'Bhishma' rakha gaya tha. Question me aitihaasik ashuddhiyan\nhain. 25 janavaree 2002 ko jisa Missile ka test kiya gaya tha wo Agni-I (jisakee range 700 km hai) thi, Agni-II nahi. Agni-II,\nsurface-to-surface par maara karne wali madhyam distance ki ballistic Missile ka niyamit roop se odisha ke Chandipur ke\npaas do epeeje abdula kalaam dveepa (former me vhilar dveepa) par integrated test range (ITR) se test kiya jata hai. [Q48–\nQ50]\n● Agni-II ek madhyam distance ki ballistic Missile (MRBM) hai jisakee range 2000-2500 km hai. Agni-IV long-range, nuclear-\nSaksham surface-to-surface ballistic missile hai. Isliye, statement 1 sahi hai. Ye statement \"ye full form se indigenous nahi\nhai\" incorrect hai. Agni-V missile poori tarah se India ke DRDO dwara developed poori tarah se indigenous intercontinental\nballistic Missile (ICBM) hai. [Q51–Q53]\n● Indian defence sandarbh me, 'indraa' (INDRA - Indian Doppler Radar) Army aur Air Force ke liye India ke DRDO dwara\ndeveloped 2D Radar ki ek series hai. Ye India me design aur built pehli badi Radar system thi. Prithvi-II Missile (Prithvi\nsurface-to-surface ballistic missile ka Air Force sanskarana) ka pehli baar 27 janavaree 1996 ko odisha ke Chandipur test\nrange se test kiya gaya tha. 8 June 2006 ko do. E.pee.je. Abdula kalaam fighter aircraft me flight bharane wale India ke\npehle raashtrapati bane. unhone Shukoi-30 emakeaaee (Sukhoi-30 MKI) fighter aircraft me flight bharee thi. [Q54–Q56]\n● Maee 1992 me, The United States of America ne kraayojenik engine technology ko India me sthanaantarit karne se\nrokane ke liye Missile technology control vyavasth (MTCR) ke under Indian Space Research Organization. Aur Russian\nspace Agency glaavakosmos par pratibandh (do saala ka pratibandha) lagaa diya tha. Do. E.pee.je. Abdula kalaam ne\nIndia me 'integrated nirdeshit Missile development programmea' (IGMDP) ke development me important bhoomika\nnibhaaee, jisne Agni aur Prithvi jaisee indigenous Missileon ko janma diya. Unhe 'India ke Missile maina' ke roop me jana\njata hai. Shaury (Shaurya) DRDO (DRDO) dwara developed ek kanastara-prakshepita (canister-launched) haaiparasonik\nsurface-to-surface par maara karne wali saamarik Missile hai. Iski range 700 se 1,900 km ke beech hai. [Q57–Q59]\n● Shaury ek haaiparasonik surface-to-surface missile hai. Haalaanki anumaan alaga-alaga hain, teston ke dauran iski\nannounced official seemaa 1000 kilograam peloda ke saath lagbhag 700 km thi (na ki specially 900 km par kaipa ki gayi). Is\npareeksha question ke context me statement (c) ko incorrect maana gaya tha. Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki shaury\nMissile ki maximum speed usually 7.5 maika (8 maika se zyada nahi) bataaee jati hai. [Q60–Q61]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Defence Technology Full Mind Map\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q39 & Q49 — Missile Classification / Historical Mismatch\n\n▸Q39 source wording Agni-II ko ICBM bolti hai, jabki ~2000–2500 km range ke hisaab se ise MRBM/IRBM-class context me\nsamjhein; true ICBM threshold kaafi higher hota hai.\n\n▸Q49 source itself disputed/incorrect statements mark karta hai: 25 Jan 2002 test ko Agni-II se jodna historical mismatch hai;\nexplanation Agni-I identify karta hai.\n5. Indigenous Combat Platforms & Naval Systems\n● Tejas Indian Air Force ke liye hindustaan eyaronotiks limited (HAL) ke sahayog se vaimaanikee development Agency\n(ADA) dwara indigenously developed A light-combat aircraft (Light Combat Aircraft - LCA) hai. Tejas ek Indian singala-\nengine, deltaa vinga, halkaa malteerol phaaitar (fighter aircraft) hai. Aakash A missile hai, Vikrant An aircraft carrier hai aur\nArjun ek main yuddhak Tank hai. Jaisaa ki establish kiya gaya hai, 'Tejas' India dwara developed Light Combat Aircraft\n(LCA - halkaa fighter aircraft) hai. [Q62–Q64]\n● Tejas India dwara developed pehla indigenous fighter aircraft (modern Light Combat Aircraft) hai. Isane puraane miga-21\nfighter aircraft ki jagaha lee. (nota: HAL HF-24 maarut 1960 ke decade ka pehla Indian developed jeta phaaitar tha, lekin\nmodern fighter aircraft ke context me options me Tejas sahi hai). Jaisaa ki established hai, Tejas pehla India built halkaa\nfighter aircraft (fighter plane) hai. Edamiral gorshakov (Admiral Gorshkov) Russian Navy ka ek sanshodhit keeva-category\nka aircraftvaahak pota (aircraft carrier) tha. Ise India dwara adhiplanetit kiya gaya tha aur bade paimaane par naveeneekrit\nkarke iska naam aaeeenaes vikramaadity (INS Vikramaditya) rakha gaya tha, jo currently Indian Navy ke major jahaaj ki\ntarah kaam karta hai. [Q65–Q67]\n● Majhagaanv doka shipabildars limited (MDL) dwara built kalavaree-category (skorpeena category) ki paanchaveen\nSubmarine INS vaageer (Vagir) ko 23 janavaree 2023 ko Indian Navy me shamil kiya gaya tha. ICGS sameaningk\n(Smeaningk) Indian tatarakshak bala (Indian Coast Guard) ke liye banaya gaya ek Offshore Patrol Vessel (gashtee pota -\nOPV) hai. Ise agasta 2020 me launch kiya gaya tha. ICGS 'Vishwast' govaa shipayard limited dwara indigenously design\naur built Offshore Patrol Vessel (gashtee pota) ke ek nae varga ka pehla pota tha. Ise 17 maarch 2010 ko Indian\ntatarakshak bala me shamil kiya gaya tha. [Q68–Q70]\n● Question me ek tathyatmak truti hai. INS power (A57) Indian Navy ka deepak category ka ek bedaa Tankra (fleet tanker)\nhai. Ise India me indigenously nahi banaya gaya tha; balki, ise Italian jahaaj development kanpanee phinakaintiyaree\n(Fincantieri) dwara banaya gaya tha. INS Astradhaarinee India ka pehla poori tarah se indigenously design aur built\nTorpedo launch and recovery vessel (TLRV) hai. [Q71–Q72]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q65 & Q71 — “First Indigenous” Wording\n\n▸Q65 me Tejas ko first indigenous fighter kaha gaya hai; historical nuance me HAL HF-24 Marut India ka earlier indigenous jet-\nfighter programme tha. Exam wording/context dekhein.\n\n▸Q71 source disputed hai: INS Shakti (A57) India me indigenously built nahi thi; Deepak-class fleet tanker Italy me built hui thi.\n6. Ballistic vs Cruise Missiles & BrahMos\n● Cruise Missileen apni poori flight ke dauran subsonic, suparasonik ya haaiparasonik speed se jeta-chaalita hoti hain, jabki\nballistic Missileen kevala flight ke early (boosta) charan me rocket-sanchaalita hoti hain. Isliye statement 1 incorrect hai.\nSuparasonik cruise missile 'Brahmos' Russian sangha ke NPO machineostroyeniy aur India ke DRDO ke beech ek joint\nudyama hai. Jaisaa ki jnyaat hai, Brahmos Supersonic missile India and Russia ke beech ek joint udyama hai. [Q73–Q75]\n● Brahmos India ke DRDO aur Russia ke NPO machineostroyeniy ke beech ek joint udyama hai. Brahmos ek highly\nadvanced suparasonik cruise missile hai. Brahmos suparasonik cruise missile ke nausainik (Naval) version ka 18 aktoobar\n2020 ko Indian Navy ke indigenous built steelth Destroyer INS chennew se successfully test kiya gaya tha, jisne araba\nsaagar me ek Lakshya ko bhedaa tha. [Q76–Q78]\n● 21 maarch 2010 (22 maarch nahi) ko ek chalate Warship se Brahmos ka test kiya gaya tha. Saath hi, MTCR niyamon ki\nwajah se iski moola flight seemaa 290 km par seemit kar di gayi thi. Isliye question ke time (c) aur (d) donon hi sahi\nstatement nahi the. 29 maarcha, 2009 ko, Brahmos bloka-II Missile ke lainda ataika (jameena par hamala karne wale)\nversion ka raajasthan ke Pokharan test range me ek mobile otonomas lonchar (MAL) se successfully test kiya gaya tha.\nIndia ne aprail 2024 me Philippines ko Brahmos suparasonik cruise missileon ka pehla baicha saunpaa. (abhistatement A\ntrue hai). [Q79–Q81]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q79 & Q81 — BrahMos Date/Range Context\n\n▸Q79 source multiple-incorrect mark karta hai; original BrahMos range MTCR-era cap ~290 km thi, later variants ki range badhi.\nTest-date wording bhi option-specific hai.\n\n▸Q81 Philippines export statement current-event context ka hai; exported configuration/range ko question-year ke wording ke\nsaath padhein.\n7. UAVs, Fighter Technology, AESA, THAAD & FOBS\n● Lakshya DRDO ke vaimaanikee development pratishthaan (Aeronautical Development Establishment - ADE) dwara\ndeveloped ek Indian rimota operated haaee-speeda taaraget drone system (Unmanned aircraft) hai. Netraa (NETRA) ek\nhalkaa human rahita havaaee vaahan (UAV) hai jise aaidiy phorja aur DRDO ki Pune located laboratoryon dwara\nsahayogaatmak roop se develop kiya gaya hai. Ise specially aatankavaad virodhee abhiyanon ke liye design kiya gaya hai\naur ye 200-300 meetar ki elevation tak flight bharane me Saksham hai. Phlaaing ophisar Avani Chaturvedi ne 20\npharavaree, 2018 ko miga-21 baaisan fighter aircraft me solo (akele) flight poori karne wali Indian Air Force (IAF) ki pehli\nIndian mahila paayalat banakar itihaas racha diya. [Q82–Q84]\n● F/A-18 supara hornet ek American fighter aircraft hai jo mainly boinga dwara banaya gaya hai. Iska mainly American Navy\ndwara use kiya jata hai, aur kuch hada tak ostreliy aur kuvait dwara. AESA ek advanced malteemoda, solid-state ektiva"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Defence Technology Full Mind Map\ncharanabaddh saranee phaayar kantrol Radar hai. Ye high accurateta ke saath kai (Multiple) Lakshyaon ko traika karne me\nhighly Saksham hai (puraane devicevat steeyar Radar ke opposite). Tarminal haaee elteetyood eriya defence (THAAD) ek\nhighly advanced American anti-ballistic Missile defence system hai. Ise hit-too-kila (hit to kill) drishtikon use karke chhoti,\nmadhyam aur madhyavartee distance ki ballistic Missileon ko maara giraane ke liye design kiya gaya hai. [Q85–Q87]\n● Phraikshanal orbital bombaardament system (FOBS) ek aayudh vitaran system hai jo kam-Prithvi orbit (Low Earth Orbit)\nme nuclear weapon rakhti hai. Conventional ICBM ke opposite, jo ek poorvaanumaanit aarka (arc) lete hain, FOBS orbit me\nraha sakta hai aur apratyashit roop se apne Lakshya par gira sakta hai, jo early chetaavanee Radar ko chalessa de deta\nhai. [Q88]\n8. Arms Control, Export Regimes & NATO\n● Saamarik shastr nyooneekaran sandhiyan (START I aur START II) The United States of America (USA) aur Soviet\nsamaajavaadee ganaraajy sangha (USSR) (aur baad me Russia) ke beech important dvipaksheey sandhiyan thin jinka\npurpose unke huge nuclear shastraagaar ko kam karna tha. Nyoo staart (saamarika shastr nyooneekaran sandhi) The\nUnited States of America aur Russian sangha ke beech ek nuclear weapon katautee sandhi hai jiska aupachaarik naam\n\"saamarika aakraamak weaponon ki aage ki lessee aur seemaa ke upaaya\" hai. Is par 2010 me hastaakshar kiye gaye the.\nJune 2016 me, India aupachaarik roop se hega code opha kandakt (HCoC) me shamil hua, jo bade paimaane par vinaash\nke weapon le jane me Saksham ballistic Missileon ke aprasaar ke prati apni pratibaddhata ko display karta hai. [Q89–Q91]\n● Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki vaaArmyra (Wassenaar) vyavasth oeeseedee (OECD) ke under ek aupachaarik group\nnahi hai. Ye conventional weaponon aur dohare use wale saamaanon se related ek svaichchhik niryat control vyavasth hai.\nStatement I incorrect hai kyonki naato (NATO) me currently 32 member country hain (2024 me Sweden ke shamil hone ke\nbaad), 42 nahi. Sweden ne do shataabdiyon tak tatasthata (neutrality) aur sainya gutanirapekshata ki long time se chalee\naa rahi neeti ko banaye rakha tha. Bhoo-raajaneetika badalaavon se prerit hokara, Sweden official taur par 7 maarch 2024\nko naato ka 32vaan member bana gaya. [Q92–Q94]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q93–Q94 — NATO Membership is Time-Sensitive\n\n▸Sweden 7 March 2024 ko NATO ka 32nd member bana. Membership count future accessions ke saath change ho sakta hai,\nisliye current-exam year verify karein.\n9. Operations, DefExpo, Naval Forums & Joint Military Exercises\n● Opareshan pavana (Operation Pawan) 1987 ke end me shreelanka me litte (tamila taaigarsa) se jaaphana ka control lene\nke liye Indian shaanti Army (IPKF) dwara chalaae gaye abhiyan ko diya gaya code naam tha. Dephaeksapo (DefExpo) ka\n12vaan version aktoobar 2022 me gaandheenagara, gujaraat me organized kiya gaya tha. Iska vyapak vishay (theme)\n'Path to Pride' (Path to Pride) tha, jiska purpose ghareloo defence udyoga ki taakat ko display karna tha. Statement 1\nincorrect hai kyonki pehla (udghaatana) hinda mahaasaagar Navy sangoshthee (IONS) 2008 me new dillee, India me\norganized kiya gaya tha, na ki 2015 me. [Q95–Q97]\n● Phrendaship (Druzhba)-2016 aatankavaad virodhee sahayog badhane ke liye organized Russia aur paakistaan ke\nsashastr balon ke beech ek aitihaasik joint sainya exercise tha. July 2017 me, maalaabaar nausainik exercise ka 21vaan\nversion Bay of Bengal me hua, jisme India, USA aur Japan ki Navyon ne bhaaga liya. (nota: ostreliy baad me 2020 me ise\nchaturbhuj (quadrilateral) banane ke liye shamil hua). 'maitree' (Maitree) Indian Army aur royala thaee Army (Thailand) ke\nbeech sahayog aur saamarik antahkriyasheelata ko badhaava dene ke liye organized aavartee joint sainya exercise ka\nnaam hai. [Q98–Q100]\n● 2018 ki shuruaat me raajaneetik uthala-puthala aur tanaavapoorn raajanayik sanbandhon ki duration ke dauran, Maldives\nne andamaan aur nikobaar dveepa group me organized bahupaksheey nausainik exercise 'milana' (Milan) me bhaaga lene\nke India ke nimantran ko asveekaar kar diya tha. SLINEX ka full form shreelanka indiya nevala eksarasaaij (Sri Lanka India\nNaval Exercise) hai. SLINEX-II 2011 me India aur shreelanka ki Navyon ke beech organized is joint bede exercise ka\ndoosra version tha. 'harimaoo power' (Harimau Shakti) ek niyamit dvipaksheey joint sainya prashikshan exercise hai jo\nIndia aur Malaysia ki Armyon ke beech jangal yuddha me visheshajnyata share karne ke liye organized kiya jata hai. [Q101–\nQ103]\n● Joint sainya exercise 'aphreekaa-indiya pheeld trening eksarasaaij (AFINDEX-2023)' ka doosra version Pune,\nMaharashtra me videshee prashikshan noda me organized kiya gaya tha. Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki 'mitra power'\nIndia aur *shreelankaa* (baanglaadesha nahi) ke beech ek joint sainya exercise hai. Sampreeti (SAMPRITI) exercise\nbaanglaadesh ke saath hota hai. Dvipaksheey Japan-India oceanee exercise (JIMEX-24) ke aathaven version ki\nmejabaanee Japan oceanee aatma-defence bala dwara ki gayi aur ye June 2024 me Yokosuka, Japan me organized kiya\ngaya tha. [Q104–Q106]\n● Sainya sahayog ko badhaava dene ke purpose se Indian Army aur kanbodiyan Army ke beech udghaatan joint tebala topa\nexercise (CINBAX) Maharashtra ke Pune me organized kiya gaya tha. Jodee (D) incorrect hai kyonki 'yuddhaabhyasa' India\naur The United States of America (USA) ke beech ek major dvipaksheey joint sainya exercise hai, na ki Thailand. Thailand\nke saath exercise ko 'maitree' kaha jata hai. [Q107–Q108]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q108\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0364","t":"16 Scientists and Inventions Hinglish Corrected","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Scientists and Inventions Full Mind Map\n🔬 SCIENTISTS AND INVENTIONS — FULL MIND MAP\n\n\n\nवैज्ञानिकएवंआविष्कार· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Early Instruments, Optics & Foundational Inventions\n2. Engines, Communication & Everyday Technology\n3. Penicillin, X-rays & Discovery Matching\n4. S. Chandrasekhar & Stellar Astrophysics\n5. Photoelectric Effect, Einstein & Relativity\n6. C.V. Raman & National Science Day\n7. Indian Scientists, Scientific Fields & Contributions\n8. Recent Science Prizes in the Source\n1. Early Instruments, Optics & Foundational Inventions\n● 1718 me, James Puckle naam ka ek English inventor ne Defence Gun invent kiya jo mechanical machine gun ke\ndevelopment me important steps me se ek prove hua. unhone Defence Gun ka patent karayaa, jo us time tak paaee jane\nwali manual roop se operated revolving machine gun ke sabse refined design ko represent karti hai. [Q1]\n● Thermometer ya thermoscope ki discovery famous Italian physicist Galileo Galilei se associated hai. Practical refracting\ntelescope ko Galileo ne 1609 me major improve karke astronomical observations ke liye use kiya. Microscope ek aisa\ndevice hai jo bahut chhoti nearby objects ko dekhane me help karta hai jinhen naked eyes se clearly nahi dekha ja sakta hai.\n[Q2–Q4]\n● Typewriter ka invention 1867 me Christopher Latham Sholes ne kiya tha (A-2). ek German mechanical engineer aur\nphysicist Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen ne 1895 me X-ray ya Roentgen rays ke roop me jaanee jane wali wavelength range me\nelectromagnetic radiation discover ki. unhone effective roop se X-Ray Machine invent kiya. British physicist aur chemist Sir\nWilliam Henry Bragg ne 1915 me apne son William Lawrence Bragg ke saath physics me Nobel Prize share kiya tha.\nJohannes Gutenberg ne printing press invent kiya (A-2). [Q5–Q8]\n EXAM TRAP — Q3 — ‘Telescope invented by Galileo’ exam shorthand hai\n⚠️\n Galileo ne first telescope invent nahi kiya tha. Hans Lippershey ko 1608 ke telescope patent application ka\n▸\ncommon credit milta hai; Galileo ne 1609 me telescope ko kaafi improve karke astronomy me famous kiya.\n Source answer/coverage preserve hai, lekin concept ke liye yaad rakhein: Lippershey → early telescope; Galileo →\n▸\n\nmajor improvement & astronomical use.\n2. Engines, Communication & Everyday Technology\n● Steam engine ka development 17th century ke end me start hua (Thomas Savery aur thomas Newcomen ne early version\nbanaye the). Haalaanki, 1763 me Scottish engineer aur inventor James Watt dwara sabse important improvements kiye\ngaye jisne steam engine ko industrial use ke liye practical bana diya. Isliye, unhe widely iska inventor maana jata hai. [Q9–\nQ10]\n● Thomas Alva Edison ko practical, long-lasting incandescent electric lamp ke liye widely jaana jata hai. Modern gas engine\n(Gas engine) 1885 me German engineer Gottlieb Daimler dwara develop kiya gaya tha. (Rudolf Diesel ne 1895 me Diesel\nengine developed kiya tha). Lewis Edson Waterman ne 1883 me New York me capillary-feed fountain pen invent kiya.\nunhone 1884 me pehle practical fountain pen ka patent karaya tha. [Q11–Q13]\n● Scottish physicist Robert Watson-Watt radar (Radio Detection and Ranging) ke development me pioneer aur important\ncontributor the. Swedish Scientist aur innovator Alfred Nobel ne Dynamite invent kiya. Famous Nobel Foundation ki\nestablishment 1900 me unki will ke basis par ki gayi thi. Mechanical Television ka invention John Logie Baird (J.L. Baird)\ndwara 1926 me Britain me kiya gaya tha. Scottish engineer J.L. Baird ka naam television ke invention se linked hai. [Q14–\nQ17]\n● Theodore Maiman ne LASER (Light Amplification by the stimulated emission of Radiation) invent kiya tha. 16 maee, 1960\nko unhone California ke maaleeboo me Hughes Research Laboratories me apni laboratory me ruby kristal se pehle varking\nLASER ka successfully demonstration kiya tha. [Q18]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Scientists and Inventions Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — Q9, Q11 & Q12 — Inventor attribution me nuance\n⚠️\n Steam engine Savery aur Newcomen ke work se evolve hua; James Watt ne major efficiency improvements kiye.\n▸\nExam books me often simply ‘James Watt—steam engine’ diya hota hai.\n Incandescent lighting me multiple contributors the; Edison commercially practical aur durable incandescent-lamp\n▸\nsystem ke liye best known hain.\n Four-stroke internal-combustion/gas engine Nikolaus Otto (1876) se strongly associated hai; Daimler ne baad me\n▸\nhigh-speed petroleum engines develop kiye. Q12 ko source-specific wording ke context me padhein.\n3. Penicillin, X-rays & Discovery Matching\n● Penicillin ki discovery 1928 me Scottish Scientist Alexander Fleming ne ki thi, je. Parkins ne nahi. Baakee jode correctly\nmatched hain. Pehla sachcha enteebaayotika, Penicillin, Alexander Fleming dwara discover kiya gaya tha. Alexander\nFleming ne 'Penicillium notatum' (Penicillium notatum) molda (fungus) se antibiotic Penicillin ki discover ki thi. Sir Alexander\nFleming ne Penicillin ki discover ki thi, jiske liye unhe Howard Florey aur Ernst Boris Chain ke saath 1945 me Physiology ya\nMedicine me Nobel Prize milaa. [Q19–Q23]\n● Radium ki discovery 1898 me piyare kyooree aur maidam kyooree ne ki thi (A-2). Penicillin ki discovery 1928 me\nAlexander Fleming ne ki thi (B-1). X-ray ki discovery 1895 me German physicist Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen ne ki thi. [Q24–\nQ25]\n● Johannes embros Fleming ne 1904 me pehle varking daayod invent kiya. (B) Traanjistar ka invention 1947 me American\nphysicalvidon Johannes baardeena, vaaltar braitan aur William shokle ne kiya tha. (A) [Q26]\n● Alfred Nobel ek Swedish chemist the jinhone Dynamite invent kiya tha (A-2). Alexander Fleming ek Scottish\njeevavijnyaanee the jinhone 1928 me antibiotic 'Penicillin' ki discover ki thi (B-3). [Q27]\n EXAM TRAP — Q24 — Jenner: Smallpox, Measles nahi\n⚠️\n Edward Jenner ne 1796 me SMALLPOX ke against vaccination pioneer ki. ‘Measles/\n▸\n’\nखसरा\naur ‘smallpox/\n’\nचेचक\nalag diseases hain; source wording inhe mix karti hai.\n Exam ke liye safe fact: Edward Jenner → smallpox vaccine. ‘Measles vaccine—Jenner’ memorize na karein.\n▸\n4. S. Chandrasekhar & Stellar Astrophysics\n● Indian-American khagol Scientist subrahmanyan chandrashekhar ko 'chandrashekhara seemaa' (Chandrasekhar Limit) ke\nprinciple ke liye jana jata hai. Subrahmanyan chandrashekhar ko stars ki structure aur development ke liye important\nphysical processon ke unke saiddhaantik study ke liye 1983 me physics ka Nobel Prize diya gaya tha, jo ki Astrophysics ke\nfield me aataa hai. S. Chandrashekhar ne prove kiya ki jina stars ka mass Sun ke mass ke 1.44 gunaa (chandrashekhara\nseemaa) se kam hota hai, ve apanaa nuclear fuel samaapt hone par sthira white vaaman (white dwarfs) bana jate hain. Yadi\nve is mass se zyada ho jate hain, to ve aur zyada dhaha jate hain. [Q28–Q30]\n EXAM TRAP — Q28 — Chandrasekhar Limit ≠ original ‘black-hole principle’\n⚠️\n Chandrasekhar ka key contribution stable white dwarfs ki mass limit aur uske baad stellar-collapse implications\n▸\nhain. Black-hole theory kai physicists ke work se develop hui, including Schwarzschild aur later relativists.\n Agar source exact legacy question poochhe to intended answer S. Chandrasekhar hai; conceptually\n▸\nChandrasekhar limit yaad rakhein.\n5. Photoelectric Effect, Einstein & Relativity\n● Photoelectric effect wo ghatana hai jisme electromagnetic radiation ko avashoshit karne par kisi material se ya uske andar\nse electrical charged particle nikalate hain. Scientist Albert Einstein Plank ke kvaantam principle ke basis par photoelectric\neffect ki sarala aur tathyatmak vyakhy dene ke liye famous hain. Einstein ko \"Theoretical Physics me unki sevaaon aur\nspecially photoelectric effect ke niyama ki unki discovery ke liye\" 1921 me physics ka Nobel Prize diya gaya tha. Jaisaa ki\nestablished hai, Albert Einstein ko mainly photoelectric effect ke unke niyama (law of the photoelectric effect) ke liye Nobel\nPrize se sammaanit kiya gaya tha. [Q31–Q36]\n● 'Theory of relativity' me usually Albert Einstein ke do paraspar related principle shamil hote hain: vishesh relativity (1905\nme prastaavita) aur general relativity (1915 me prakaashita). Vishesh relativity gravity ke abhaav me sabhi physical\nghatanaaon par laagoo hoti hai, ye tarka dete hue ki space aur time atoota roop se jude hue hain. General relativity gravity\nke niyama aur prakriti ke balon ke saath iske sanbandh ki vyakhy karti hai. [Q37–Q38]\n● Physics me apne groundbreaking kaam ke alawa, Albert Einstein Violin aur piyano bajaane me bhi kushal the. Sangeet\nunke jeevan ka ek gahara aur important hissaa tha. Chauth dimensions (fourth dimension) usually teen sthanik aayamon\n(lanbaaee, chaudaaee aur depression) ke saath ek other dimensions ke roop me 'time' ko refer karta hai. [Q39–Q40]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Scientists and Inventions Full Mind Map\n EXAM TRAP — Q40 — Four-dimensional spacetime attribution\n⚠️\n Einstein ki special relativity ne space aur time ko physically unite kiya, lekin Hermann Minkowski ne 1907–08 me\n▸\nfamous mathematical four-dimensional spacetime formulation diya.\n Source-style MCQ Einstein expect kar sakta hai; deeper physics me Einstein ki relativity aur Minkowski spacetime\n▸\nformalism ko distinguish karein.\n6. C.V. Raman & National Science Day\n● 1930 me, Sir C.V. Raman light ke scattering (scattering) aur ramana prabhaav ki discovery par apne kaam ke liye physics\nme Nobel Prize mila karne wale pehle eshiyaee aur Indian bane. unhone ye discovery February, 28, 1928 ko ki thi, jise India\nme National science divasa ke roop me manaay jata hai. Jaisaa ki established hai, do C.V. Raman ko varsha 1930 me\nphysics me Nobel Prize se sammaanit kiya gaya tha. [Q41–Q42]\n● Indian physicist Sir C. V. Raman dwara February, 28 1928 ko ramana prabhaav ki discovery ko chihnit karne ke liye India\nme hara saala February, 28 ko National science divasa manaay jata hai. India me National science divasa February, 28 ko\nmanaay jata hai. Jaisaa ki established hai, ramana prabhaav ki discovery ke upalakshy me India February, 28 ko National\nscience divasa manaata hai. Ye question technical roop se incorrect hai. National science divasa (February, 28) C.V.\nRaman ke janmadin par nahi, balki ramana prabhaav ki discovery ke upalakshy me manaay jata hai. [Q43–Q46]\n● C.V. Raman ka janma 7 navanbara, 1888 ko hua tha. Isliye, unki janma shataabdee (100veen varshagaantha) varsha\n1988 me manaaee gayi thi. Sandarbh ke liye: Charles Darwin ka janma 1809 me hua tha, Ramanujan ka janma 1887 me\nhua tha, aur Einstein ka vishesh Theory of relativity 1905 me prastaavit kiya gaya tha. [Q47]\n EXAM TRAP — Q46 — National Science Day birthday celebration nahi hai\n⚠️\n 28 February C.V. Raman ke Raman Effect discovery (28 February 1928) ko mark karta hai. Raman ka birth 7\n▸\nNovember 1888 ko hua tha.\n Isliye National Science Day ko Raman ke birthday se jodne wala question flawed premise hai.\n▸\n7. Indian Scientists, Scientific Fields & Contributions\n● 'da maina hoo nyoo inphinitee' 2015 ki British baayograaphikal draama philma hai jo 1991 ki isi naam ki kitaab par based\nhai. Indian khagol Scientist je.vee. Naarleekar ne 'relativity ka new principle' pratipaadit kiya. Varishth Scientist phreda\nhoyala ke sahayog se, unhone gravity ka hoyala-naarleekara principle developed kiya, jisme macha ke principle ko shamil\nkarke Einstein ke relativity ke principle me sanshodhan karne ki maanga ki gayi thi. Indian khagol Scientist jayant vishnu\n(je.vee.) naarleekar ke according, Astrology (astrology) ek chhadm science hai aur ise ek sachcha science nahi maana jata\nhai, kyonki isme anubhavajany Scientist tareekon dwara satyapit poorvaanumaan power ka abhaav hai. [Q48–Q50]\n● Do. Homee jahaangeer bhaabha ek Indian nuclear physicist the, jinhone India me Nuclear Energy programme ke\ndevelopment me highly important bhoomika nibhaaee. Unhe universally \"Indian nuclear programme ke janak\" ke roop me\njana jata hai. Choonki homee jahaangeer bhaabha ko India ke Nuclear Energy programme ke janak maana jata hai, isliye\nunki smriti me mainly Nuclear Energy ke field me asaadhaaran yogadaan ke liye Scientiston ko 'Homi Bhabha award' diya\njata hai. [Q51–Q52]\n● Steephan William hoking (1942 - 2018) world famous British saiddhaantik physicist, brahmaand scientist aur author the.\nUnhe ek shaanadaar Scientist ke roop me widely maana jata hai, jinhen black hole, relativity aur 'e breeph histree opha\ntaaima' jaisee lokapriy science pustakon par unke kaam ke liye jana jata hai. Sir Jagdish Chandra Bose ek bahushrut\n(polymath) the: ek prakhyat Indian physicist, jeevavijnyaanee, baayophijisista, vanaspatishaastree aur science katha ke\nearly lekhaka. [Q53–Q54]\n● Do. Raja Ramanna nuclear physics ke liye jane jate the (A-2). Do ema.esa. Svaameenaathan ek famous Indian krishi\nScientist (India me harita kraanti ke janak) hain (B-5). [Q55–Q56]\n● Ek shaanadaar Indian physicist do Raja Ramanna ne India ke nuclear bama ke development me highly yogadaan diya.\nUnki pratyaksh dekharekh aur netritv me, India ka pehla nuclear test (codenema 'smaailinga buddhaa') 1974 me\nsuccessfully kiya gaya tha. Do Har Govind Khorana ko 1968 me chikitsa me Nobel Prize se sammaanit kiya gaya tha. C.V.\nRaman ne 1930 me physics me Nobel Prize jeetaa. S. Chandrashekhar ne 1983 me physics me Nobel Prize jeetaa. [Q57–\nQ58]\n EXAM TRAP — Q55 — Matching list me source/option mismatch\n⚠️\n M.S. Swaminathan ka specialized field agricultural science/genetics aur Green Revolution hai, ‘plant chemistry’\n▸\nnahi. Agar option list me agriculture hi absent ho to item defective hai.\n Safe mapping: Raja Ramanna—nuclear physics; M.S. Swaminathan—agricultural science; U.R. Rao—space\n▸\nresearch; Meghnad Saha—astrophysics/thermal ionization. In pairings ko isi tarah yaad rakhen."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Scientists and Inventions Full Mind Map\n8. Recent Science Prizes in the Source\n● Physics me 2023 ka Nobel Prize piyare egostinee, pherenk kroja aur ainee ela'huiliyara ko joint roop se \"praayogika\ntareekon ke liye diya gaya jo matter me ilektron speedsheelata ke study ke liye light ke etosekand spandan utpann karte\nhain.\" Option (B) 2022 Nobel Prize ka description karta hai, aur option (C) physics me 2021 ke Nobel Prize ka description\nkarta hai. [Q59]\n● Saankhyikee me 2023 ka international award, jise aksar saankhyikee ke 'Nobel Prize' ke same maana jata hai, ek highly\nsammaanit Indian-American ganitajny aur saankhyikeevid Calyampudi Radhakrishna Rao (C.R. Rao) ko saankhyikee ke\nfield me unke smaarakeey yogadaan ko recognition dene ke liye provide kiya gaya tha. [Q60]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q60\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0365","t":"17 Miscellaneous Hinglish Corrected","b":"Crux & Tricks / Ghatnachakra / Science / Physics","x":[" Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n⚛️ MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n\nविविध· Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n📑 Topics in this chapter:\n1. Physics Branches, Scientific Institutions, LASER, Inventions & ATM\n2. Nanotechnology: Nanoparticles, CNTs, Quantum Structures & Nano Devices\n3. Energy Projects, Science Congress, Awards & S&T Organizations\n4. Polar/Ocean Research, Weather & Earth-Science Concepts\n5. Magnetism, Timekeeping, MOEMS, Radar & Drones\n6. Research Institutes, Technology Centres & General Science Applications\n7. Metric System, Scientists, Laser Applications, Cryonics & Nuclear Basics\n8. Displays, Automobiles, Humanoid Robots & Robotics\n1. Physics Branches, Scientific Institutions, LASER, Inventions & ATM\n● Quantum Mechanics physics ki branch hai jo atoms aur subatomic particles jaise bahut chhote particles ki motion aur\nbehavior se related hai. Geodesy Earth ke teen basic properties ko accurate roop se measure karne aur samajhne ka\nscience hai: iska geometric shape (dimensions), space me iska orientation; iska gravity field, saath hi time ke saath in\nproperties me parivartan (elevation/depression). Isliye, ek se zyada option sahi hain. [Q1–Q2]\n● Cybernetics mechanical, physical, biological, cognitive aur social systems ke study se relevant hai. Norbert Wiener ne\n1948 me Cybernetics ko \"animal aur machine me control aur communication ke scientific study\" ke roop me define kiya tha.\nHorology time measure karne ki art ya science hai. Isme clocks, sundial, timer aur atomic clocks etc. ka study shamil hai.\n[Q3–Q4]\n● Tribology mechanical engineering aur Material Science ki ek branch hai. Isme Friction, wear aur lubrication ke principles\nka study aur application shamil hai. Plasma ko aksar 'matter ki fourth state' kaha jata hai. Isme charged particles (ions aur\nfree electrons) ki significant amount hoti hai. Isliye statement (i) true hai. [Q5–Q6]\n● 'White Dwarf' (white dwarf) ek stellar core ka remnant hai jo mainly electron-degenerate matter se bana hota hai. Ye un\nstars ki last evolutionary state ko represent karta hai jinka mass neutron star banane ke liye enough nahi hai. naturally, iska\nstudy Astronomy me kiya jata hai. Statement (B) incorrect hai. Rayleigh scattering ke according, chhoti wavelength zyada\nscatter hoti hai. Violet light ki wavelength blue light ke comparison me chhoti hoti hai, isliye violet waves blue light waves se\nzyada scatter hoti hain. Sky violet ke bajaay blue mainly isliye dikhai deta hai kyonki human eye blue light ke prati zyada\nsensitive hoti hai aur Sun violet ke comparison me zyada blue light emit karta hai. [Q7–Q8]\n● India ki National Physical Laboratory New Delhi me located hai. Ye India ki measurement standards laboratory hai, jo\ncountry me SI units ke standards ko banaye rakhti hai aur weights and measures ke National standards ko calibrate karti\nhai. National Chemical Laboratory (CSIR-NCL), jiski establishment 1950 me hui thi, Council of Scientific and Industrial\nResearch (CSIR) ki ek constituent laboratory hai. Ye Pune, Maharashtra me located hai. [Q9–Q10]\n● Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR) mathematics aur science me advanced research ke liye ek major institute\nhai. Iski establishment 1945 me Sir Dorabji Tata Trust ke sahayog se Dr. Homi Bhabha dwara ki gayi thi; ye Mumbai me\nlocated hai. LASER ka full form \"Light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation.\" hai. Ye ek aisa device hai jo\nelectromagnetic radiation ke stimulated emission ke basis par optical amplification (optical amplification) ki process ke\nthrough light emit karta hai. [Q11–Q12]\n● Choonki LASER ka full form hi \"Stimulated radiation ke emission dwara light pravardhana\" hai, lejara naturally Stimulated\nradiation ke production ke liye design kiya gaya ek device hai. Ruby LASER ek solid-state LASER hai jo synthetic ruby\nkristal ka use karta hai. Pehla working LASER thiodor echa. Maiman dwara 1960 me banaya gaya ek ruby LASER tha.\n[Q13–Q14]\n● Ek Japanese author aur freelance journalist Takashi Hirose ne 2010 me 'nyookliyara riektar taaima bama' book likhee thi.\nRevolver ka invention saimual kolta ne kiya tha (A-3). Dynamite ka invention Alfred Nobel ne kiya tha (B-1). [Q15–Q16]\n● Usually, phlaishalaaita/torcha me standard shushk sela (leklaanche sela) ka use kiya jata hai. Ina koshikaaon me, enoda\n(nakaaraatmaka tarminala) ek jastaa (jinka) kaina se bana hota hai, jabki kaithod (sakaaraatmaka tarminala) ek kaarban\n(grephaaita) roda hota hai. E.tee.ema. (A.T.M.) ka full form 'Automated Teller Machine' hai. Ye ek vishesh computer hai jo\nbainka khaate ke phanda ko prabandhit karna suvidhaajanak banata hai, jiska use usually paise nikaalane ke liye kiya jata\nhai. [Q17–Q18]\n● Neshanal phaainenshiyal svicha (NFS) India me share automatic telara machineon (ATM) ka sabse large network hai. Ye\nBhartiya National bhugataan nigama (NPCI) dwara chalaay jata hai, jisne 2009 me IDRBT se apanaa sanchaalan\nsanbhaala tha. Isliye, NPCI country ke sabhi eteeem ko connect karta hai. [Q19]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q2 & Q14 — Wording Matters\n\n▸Q2 me Geodesy sirf Earth ke dimensions tak limited nahi hai; shape, gravity field aur orientation bhi broader definition ka part\nhain. Source therefore multiple aspects ko accept karta hai.\n\n▸Q14: first working ruby laser (Theodore Maiman, 1960) deep-red coherent light (~694 nm) produce karta hai — blue-light\nstatement incorrect hai."," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n2. Nanotechnology: Nanoparticles, CNTs, Quantum Structures & Nano Devices\n● Nanotechnology nanoskel par organized vijnyaana, engineering aur technology hai, jo lagbhag 1 se 100 nanomeetar hai.\nYe nuclear aur aanavik paimaane par matter ke herapher ki allow karta hai, jo devices ke laghukaran me important\nbhoomika nibhaata hai. ek nanoparticle ke roop me classified hone ke liye ek nano-objekta ke specific aayamon me se ek\n1-100 nm (jo ki 10 -9 se 10 -7 meetar hai) ki seemaa me hota hai. Isliye, 10 -7 meetar se kam dimensions wala particle ek\nnanoparticle hai. [Q20–Q21]\n● Nanoteknolojee aur nanoparticle ki featureen nanoskel par built matter par laagoo hoti hain, jise world level par 1 se 100\nnanomeetar (nm) ke beech define kiya gaya hai. Statement 1 incorrect hai kyonki nanoparticle praakritik roop se\njvaalaamukheey raakha, oceanee phuhaara, mahina reta aur jaivik processon (jaise vaayarasa) me paae jate hain.\nStatement 2 sahi hai. Zinc oxide aur taaiteniyam daaioksaaid jaise dhaatu oksaaid ka widely sanaskreen aur saundary\nprasaadhanon me use kiya jata hai. [Q22–Q23]\n● 'nano plaga' (Nano plug) ek highly chhote, lagbhag avisible shravan device (sunane ki machine) ko refer karta hai. Isme\nmicroscopic component aur ek nano-Battery shamil hoti hai, jo kaana nahara ke andara depression me phita baithatee hai.\n2012 me, scientists ne ek vaikalpik roop se phanse sone (gold) ke nanoparticleon ke basis par pehla 'nanoiyara' (nanoear)\ndeveloped kiya. Ye microscopic device -60 dB jitane kam Sound/kanpana staron ka detect lagaa sakta hai. [Q24–Q25]\n● Tokyo worldvidyalay ke prophesar noriyo taaniguchee ne pehli baar 1974 me apne shodha patra me \"nanoteknolojee\"\nword ka istemaal kiya tha. Kaarban nanotyoob (CNTs) ne lakshit davaa vitaran vaahak ke roop me utkrisht capacity dikhai\nhai (statement 1) aur jaiva chemical sensar me effective dhanga se use kiye jate hain (statement 3). Adhyayanon se ye bhi\ndetect chalaa hai ki specific enjaaim kuch type ke CNTs ko baayodigred (nashta) kar sakte hain (statement 4). Haalaanki,\nkachche kaarban nanotyoob ganbhir rakta ke thakke ka kaaran bana sakate hain aur vartamaan vyavasaayik level par\nkritrim rakta keshikaaon ke roop me directly use ke liye rakta-sangata nahi maane jate hain, jisse is sandarbh me statement\n2 incorrect hai. [Q26–Q27]\n● Nanomedisin aise nanoparticleon ko janma deti hai jinake through behatar lakshit specific davaa vitaran (jaise, directly\nkainsar koshikaaon tak) sanbhav hai. Isliye statement 1 sahi hai. Nanotechnology shareer me ksharan (degradation) se\nbachate hue jeena ko koshikaaon me safe roop se pahunchaane me bhi highly effective hai, jo jeena therepee ko aage\nbadhane me large yogadaan deta hai. Isliye statement 2 bhi sahi hai. Aaeeseeeaara-sarkota (ICAR-CIRCOT) Mumbai\ndwara established India ka pehla nano-selyuloja sandevice, high moolya wale nano-selyuloja taiyar karne ke liye kachche\nmaala ke roop me Cotton (cotton) lintars aur Cotton ke kachare ka use karne ke liye specific roop se design kiya gaya hai.\n[Q28–Q29]\n● Nanoskel par, physical property naatakeey roop se badala jate hain. Nanomaiteriyals ka ek major, heavy study kiya jane\nwala property Friction hai (visheshakara nanoTribology me), kyonki high surface-se-aayatana anupaat maulik roop se\nbadala deta hai ki material Ek-doosare ke khilaaph kaise slaaid karti hai. Nanoskel tak seemit aayamon ke basis par nano\ntechnology classification me: 1 dimensions pratibandhit (2D free) = Quantum well (patalee philmen/paraten). 2 dimensions\npratibandhit (1D free) = Quantum wire (nanotyooba). 3 dimensions pratibandhit (0D free) = Quantum dot. [Q30–Q31]\n● Quantum dot kritrim roop se built A semiconductor nanostructure hai (usually kuch nanomeetar shape me) jo chaalan\nband electrons ki speed ko dridhata se seemit karta hai, jiske parinaamasvaroop adviteeya, aakaara-nirbhara optical aur\nelectronic property hote hain. Pehli generation: nishkriy nanostrakchar jaise eyarosola, polimara. (A) Doosri generation:\nactive nanostrakchar jaise lakshit davaaen. (D) [Q32–Q33]\n● Nano hamingabard ek small, rimota-radioactivea nano air vaahan (NAV) hai jise hamingabard (Ek type ki chhoti chiriya) ke\nsame dikhane aur udane ke liye design kiya gaya hai. Ise nigaraanee aur jaasoosee missionon ke liye eyarovironament\ndwara America me develop kiya gaya tha. [Q34]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q27 & Q30 — Nanotechnology Source Framing\n\n▸Carbon nanotubes ke biomedical uses material functionalization aur safety par depend karte hain; exam statement ko exact\nwording ke context me judge karein.\n\n▸Q30 ka “most important property” wording source-specific hai. Nanomaterials ki properties size, surface-area/volume ratio,\nquantum effects aur application ke according vary karti hain.\n3. Energy Projects, Science Congress, Awards & S&T Organizations\n● Jilaa hiting system ke liye bhoomigat bhootaapeey garmee (geothermal heat) ka dohana karne ka pehla successful\nmodern prayas 1890 me Boise, Idaho (USA) (yooesae) shahar me kiya gaya tha, jahaan aasapaas ki imaaraton ko garma\nkarne ke liye garma water ke paaipa network develop kiya gaya tha. Highly vivaadaaspad enaron bijalee project (originally\nDabhol paavar kanpanee dwara prabandhita) India ke Maharashtra ke ratnaagiree jile me Dabhol me located hai. [Q35–Q36]\n● Amarkantak power station Madhya Pradesh ke anoopapur jile ke chachaaee me located hai. Ye ma.pra. Paavar\njanareshan kanpanee limited (MPPGCL) ke koyala based bijalee steshanon me se ek hai. 88vaan Bhartiya science\nkaangres (ISC) sammelan 3 se 7 janavaree 2001 ke beech New Delhi me organized kiya gaya tha. Is sammelan ka main\nvishay 'khaadya, poshan aur paryavaran security' tha. Nota: janavaree 2023 me, 108veen ISC 'mahilaa sapowerkaran ke\nsaath satata development ke liye science aur technology' ke vishay ke saath R.T.M. Naagapur worldvidyalay me organized\nki gayi thi. [Q37–Q38]\n● 26 September, 2006 ko tatkaaleen pradhaan mantree do. Manamohan sinha ne science bhavana, New Delhi me central\nchamada research institute (CLRI), Chennai ko graameen development ke liye S&T navaachaaron ka CSIR award provide\nkiya tha. Science aur engineering ke field me padma vibhooshana-2023 America ke shree esa.aara. Shreenivaas vardhan\nko provide kiya gaya. Wo ek Bhartiya-American ganitajny hain. Unhe praayikata principle (probability theory) aur specially\nbade vichalanon (large deviations) ka integrated principle banane me unke maulik yogadaan ke liye jana jata hai. 2007 me,\nwo ebela award (Abel Prize) jeetane wale pehle eshiyaee bane the. [Q39–Q40]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● DST – science aur technology department (Department of Science and Technology), India government. CSIR – scientist\naur industrial research parishada. Neshanal inoveshan phaaundeshana-indiya (NIF) India government ke science aur\ntechnology department ka ek svaayatt nikaay hai. Isliye statement 1 sahi hai. Isane maarch 2000 me jameenee level\n(grassroots) ke technical navaachaaron aur utkrisht conventional jnyaan ko majaboot karne ke liye India ki National pahala\nke roop me kaam karna start kiya, na ki specially videshee instituteon ke saath advanced research ke liye. Isliye, statement\n2 incorrect hai. [Q41–Q42]\n● Shevaron (Chevron) ek American bahuNational energy nigama hai jo tela (Oil), praakritik gas etc. Me lagaa hua hai (A-2).\nAT&T ek American bahuNational telecom nigama (Telephone, Internet) hai (B-3). [Q43]\n4. Polar/Ocean Research, Weather & Earth-Science Concepts\n● Dakshin Gangotri Antarctica me established India ka pehla sthayee research hub tha. Ise 1984 me banaya gaya tha aur\nbaad me 1990 me barpha me dabane ki wajah se ise sevaamukt (decommissioned) kar diya gaya tha. Jaisaa ki pehle\nbataay gaya hai, Antarctica me pehla sthayee Bhartiya research basis 'Dakshin Gangotri' tha. [Q44–Q45]\n● Antarctica me India ka teesra aur sabse new sthayee research hub 'Bharti' (Bharti - 2012 me chaaloo) hai. Dakshin\nGangotri pehla (1984) tha; Maitri doosra (1989) tha. Jaisaa ki oopara bataay gaya hai, Antarctica me India dwara\nestablished teesare research hub ka naam 'Bharti' hai. [Q46–Q47]\n● IndARC (indaaarka) India ki pehli maltee-sensara water ke neeche (underwater) located observatory hai. Ise 23 July 2014\nko Northee dhruva aur norve ke beech lagbhag aadhe raaste me Arctic ke kongsaphajordan me successfultaaEastka\ntainaat kiya gaya tha. Pradhaanamantree narendr modee ne August 10, 2020 ko video konphrensing ke through Chennai-\nandamaana aur nikobaar dveepa group (CANI) submarine optical phaaibar kebala (OFC) ka shubhaaranbh kiya aur raashtr\nko dedicated kiya. Ye project dveepon ko high speed (high speed) Internet kanektivitee provide karti hai. [Q48–Q49]\n● 18 June 2023 ko, oshanaget (OceanGate) dwara operated ek deeper ocean me jane wali submarine, Titan, Northee\natalaantik mahaasaagar me taaitainik ke malabe ko dekhane ke ek abhiyan ke dauran phata (imploded) gayi thi. 'polara\ncode' (Polar Code) international oceanee organisation (IMO) ke dhruveey water me sanchaalan karne wale jahaajon ke liye\ninternational code ko refer karta hai. Ye 1 janavaree 2017 ko laagoo hua aur donon dhruvon ke aasapaas ke durgam water\nme chalne wale jahaajon ke designa, development aur paryavaran sanrakshan ko kavara karta hai. [Q50–Q51]\n● Janavaree 2021 me naineetaal jile ke Mukteshwar me Uttarakhand ke pehle dopalar vedara radar (DWR) ka udghaatan\nkiya gaya. Ye toophaan aur heavy baarish jaisee ganbhir weather sthitiyon ki bhavishyavaanee karne ke liye air me varsha\nki teevrata ko padha sakta hai. Samalavan line (Isohaline) maanachitr par wo line hai jo ocean me same lavanata (salinity)\nwale binduon ko connect karti hai, na ki barphabaaree ko. Isliye ye incorrect matched hai. Samapressure line same\nvaayumandaleey Pressure wale binduon ko connect karti hai, samochch line same elevation ko aur samagaharee line\nsame water ke neeche ki depression wale binduon ko connect karti hai. [Q52–Q53]\n● Pycnocline ocean ya water ke other pinda me ek layer hai jahaan depression ke saath water ka ghanatv fastee se badalt\nhai. Isliye, ye oceanee water ghanatv ke saath correctly mela khaata hai. Ecocline paaristhitik system (ecosystems) se\nrelated hai, Thermocline depression ke saath water ke Temperature me fastee se badalaav se related hai; Halocline\ndepression ke saath lavanata (salinity) me fastee se badalaav se related hai. Pycnocline wo layer hai jo water nikaay me\nghanatv pravanata (density gradient) ko darshaatee hai. Halocline lavanata pravanata ko show karta hai jabki Thermocline\nTemperature sankraman layer ko represent karta hai. [Q54–Q55]\n● \"main Skygangaa (milky way) ki naagarik hoon\", is deeper statement ka shreya astronaut aur Space Shuttle mission\nvisheshajny Kalpana Chawala ko diya gaya hai, jinakee kolanbiy aapada me mrityu ho gayi thi. India government ke\nnuclear energy department (DAE) ne 1962 me neshanal phartilaaijars limited ke parisar me panjaab ke Nangal me pehla\nheavy water sandevice chaaloo kiya tha. [Q56–Q57]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q46–Q47 — Bharati Research Station\n\n▸India ki third permanent Antarctic research station ka standard spelling “Bharati” hai; older question papers me “Bharti” variant mil\nsakta hai.\n5. Magnetism, Timekeeping, MOEMS, Radar & Drones\n● Anumagnettv (Paramagnetism) magnettv ka ek roop hai jisse kuch material baahya roop se laagoo magnetic field dwara\nlessjor roop se aakarshit hoti hain. Oxygen apne ayugmit (unpaired) electrons ki wajah se anumagnetic matter ka ek\nutkrisht example hai. Iron lauha-magnetic (ferromagnetic) hai, jabki Hydrogen aur Nitrogen prati-magnetic (diamagnetic)\nhain. Iron, Nickel aur Cobalt lauha-magnetic (ferromagnetic) tatva hain aur magnet ki direction majabootee se aakarshit\nhote hain. Aluminium ek anumagnetic tatva hai, jiska meaning hai ki ye anivaary roop se gaira-magnetic hai aur general\nmagnet se aasaanee se aakarshit nahi hota hai. [Q58–Q59]\n● options me se, Copper prati-magnetic (gaira-magnetic) hai, jiska meaning hai ki ye magnet ki direction aakarshit nahi hota\nhai. Nickel aur Cobalt lauha-magnetic hain. Lesspaas ki magnetic suee Earth ke magnetic field ke saath khuda ko sanrekhit\nkarti hai; aama taur par magnetic Northee dhruva (North dishaa) ki direction ishaara karti hai. [Q60–Q61]\n● Tepa rikordar ke tepa me ek plaastik baiking hoti hai jise pheromaignetik paaudar (jaise aayaran oksaaida) ke chhote\nparticles ki ek patalee layer se lepita kiya jata hai. Rikording ke time, ye particle audio signal ko stora karne ke liye magnettv\nmila karte hain. Scientists (jaise JILA) dwara developed world ki sabse accurate nuclear ghadiyan abhootaEast accurateta\nke saath time rakhne ke liye ek optical jaalee (lattice) me Strontium atomson ka use karti hain. [Q62–Q63]\n● Automatic clocks (selpha-vaaindinga ghadiyan) ko Battery ki requirement nahi hoti hai. Ve main spring (mainspring) ko\nghumaane ke liye pahanane wale ki kalaaee aur baanha ki praakritik speed se speedj energy (kinetic energy) ka use karte\nhain, jo ghadee ko power provide karta hai. ek mechanical (mechanical) ghadee me, pendulam jhoolate hue time ko control\nkarta hai. ek modern electronic (kvaartja) ghadee me, ek 'Crystal oscillator' voltej laagoo hone par ek accurate, sthira\nfrequency (frequency) par kanpan karke time measure karne wale tatva ki tarah kaam karta hai. [Q64–Q65]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Kvaartj ghadiyan kvaartj kristal ke ek chhote tukade ka use karti hain jo electrical flow flowit hone par ek accurate\nfrequency par kanpan karti hai. Ye Piezoelectric effect (mechanical tanaav ke javaab me electrical aavesh utpann karne ya\nelectrical field ke javaab me kanpan karne ki capacity) par depend karta hai. MOEMS ka full form 'Micro-Opto-Electro-\nMechanical-Systems' hai. optical emaeeemaes ke roop me bhi jana jata hai, ve chhote device hain jo prakaashikee (optics),\nelectronics aur mechanicalee ko milaate hain. [Q66–Q67]\n● Robotics ke context me, PUMA ka meaning 'programebala yoonivarsal machine phora asenbalee' (Programmable\nUniversal Machine for Assembly) hai. Ye ek famous industrial robot aarma hai. Weather radar aasaanee se baarish ya\nbarpha jaisee varsha ki nigaraanee karte hain (speedvidhi 2). Radar flight bharane wale jaanavaron jaise pakshiyon aur\nchamagaadadon ki speed ka detect lagaakar unke pravaas ko bhi traika kar sakte hain (speedvidhi 3). [Q68–Q69]\n● Bade phasal kshetron me accurate roop se keetanaashakon ka chhidakaav karne ke liye Agriculture drone ka use kiya\njata hai. (1) Kaimare aur sensar se equipped drone ka use niyamit roop se active jvaalaamukhiyon ke kretar jaise\nhazardous kshetron ka safe roop se nireekshan karne ke liye kiya jata hai. (2) [Q70]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q59 — Aluminium and Magnetism\n\n▸Aluminium technically paramagnetic hai, lekin attraction bahut weak hota hai; ordinary magnet ke saath practically “not noticeably\nattracted” ke roop me exam framing aa sakti hai.\n6. Research Institutes, Technology Centres & General Science Applications\n● Central electrical chemical research institute (CECRI) 14 janavaree, 1953 ko ek physical vaastavikata bana gaya, jab do\nesa raadhaakrishnan dwara karaaeekudee (Tamil Nadu) me ise raashtr ko dedicated kiya gaya. Bengaluru me Bhartiya\nscience institute (IISc) ki establishment varsha 1909 me jamashedajee Tata ke active sammeaningn aur dooradarshee\nprayason se ki gayi thi. [Q71–Q72]\n● RKCL - Rajasthan Knowledge Corporation Limited raajasthan government dwara established ek pablik limited kanpanee\nhai. Kanpanee ka main purpose ek new shaikshik dhaancha developed karna hai jo raajasthan raajya me 21veen century\nme aaeetee kaushal ki developmentasheel aavashyakataaon ki yojanaa, kaaryanvavehicle, paryavekshan aur niyaman kar\nsake. National Earth science study hub (NCESS) Earth science me scientist aur technical research aur development study\nko badhaava dene ke liye ek svaayatt research hub hai. Ise Kerala government dwara 1978 me tiruvanantapurama, Kerala\nme CESS ke roop me establish kiya gaya tha. [Q73–Q74]\n● Neshanal sentar phora antaarkatik enda oshana Research (NCAOR) ek Bhartiya research aur development institute hai,\njo Bengaluru me nahi balki vaasko dee gaamaa, govaa me located hai. Baakee correctly matched hain. Central Bhartiya\nlanguage institute ek Bhartiya research aur shikshan institute hai jo Mumbai me nahi balki maisoor (Karnataka) me located\nhai. Other die gaye jode correctly matched hain. [Q75–Q76]\n● Central high tibbatee study institute - vaaraanasee Indira gaandhee development research institute - Mumbai National\npraakritik chikitsa institute (NIN) Pune, Maharashtra me located hai. (nota: die gaye source paatha me iska North Bangalore\nbataay gaya tha, jo historically kisi specific raajya-stareeya institute ko refer kar sakta hai, lekin major National institute\nPune me hai). [Q77–Q78]\n● Haaee-teka sitee - Hyderabad Saains sitee - kalakatta (Kolkata) Maaikrophon ek Soundka (acoustic) se electric\ntraansadyoosar ya sensar hai jo Sound ko electrical signal (electrical signal) me convert karta hai. Early Telephone aur\nTelephone ripeetars me kaarban maaikrophon ka widely use kiya jata tha. [Q79–Q80]\n● Planeton ki speed ke teen niyama 1600 ke decade ki shuruaat me johaans Kepler dwara prastaavit kiye gaye the. Kepler\nne ye clearly kiya ki pratyek planet ek andaakaar orbit me Sun ke charon direction orbit karta hai. Solekasha (Soleckshaw)\nek paryavarana-anukoola Solar rickshaw hai. Ye aanshik roop se paidal dwara aur aanshik roop se Battery dwara aapoorti\nki jane wali electrical power dwara operated hota hai jo saura energy se chaarj hota hai. Ise CSIR laboratory me scientists\nki ek teema dwara develop kiya gaya tha. [Q81–Q82]\n● Bibliyometree (Bibliometry) ek Information Management Tool hai. Ye jnyaan ke production aur prasaar ke level ko\nmeasure karne ke saath-saath ek scientist field ke development ko traika karne ke liye ek maatraatmak saankhyikeey\ntechnology hai. Saaitotron wo device hai jisadwar Artificial climate utpann ki jati hai. Nota: saaitotron ek chikitsa device ka\nbhi naam hai jise ootaka engineering aur kainsar upachaar ke liye RFQMR use karke India me develop kiya gaya hai. [Q83–\nQ84]\n● Roorkee koleja (Roorkee College) ki establishment 1847 ee. Me British saamraajy ke pehle engineering koleja ke roop me\nhui thi. Ise aba aaeeaaeetee Roorkee ke naam se jana jata hai, jo Uttarakhand me located hai. [Q85]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q78 & Q84 — Source/Name Ambiguity\n\n▸Q78 ke source note ke mutabik National Institute of Naturopathy (NIN) Pune me hai; older/official-key wording historically vary\nkar sakti hai.\n\n▸“Cytotron” term alag contexts me use hua hai; source question artificial-climate device ko target karta hai, jabki medical-device\ntrade-name context bhi milta hai.\n7. Metric System, Scientists, Laser Applications, Cryonics & Nuclear Basics\n● India me meetrik system (dashamalava system) 1 aprail 1957 ko start ki gayi thi. 1957 se 1964 ke beech dhaale gaye\nsikkon ko 'new paisaa' kahaa jata tha. Taichyon (Tachyon) ek greeka word hai jiska meaning teevra hota hai. Physics me,\ntaichyon ek kaalpanik particle hai jo hamesha light ki speed se zyada fastee se yatraa karta hai. [Q86–Q87]\n● Johannes see. Maathara: physics me 2006 ke Nobel Prize vijeta (A-4). Maaikal griphina: NASA ke prashaasak (2005-\n2009) (B-3). Do. Raajaa ramanna ek prakhyat nuclear physicist the, jinhone 1974 me India ke pehle shaantipoorn nuclear\nprayog (smaailinga buddhaa) ke liye teema ka nirdeshan kiya tha. Unke baare me sabhi statement sahi hain. [Q88–Q89]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Miscellaneous Full Mind Map\n● Vaatar jeta teknolojee water ke bahut high Pressure wale jeta use karke vibhinn type ki saamagriyon ko kaatane me\nsaksham hai. Is technology ka use mainly Drilling of mines (khudaaee) aur vaimaanikee me kiya jata hai. Lejara beema ka\nuse kainsar (tyoomara vinaasha), eyes ki sarjaree (jaise LASIK); gurde ki patharee ko todne sahita kai beemaariyon ke\nupachaar me widely kiya jata hai. Isliye, ek se zyada option sahi hain. [Q90–Q91]\n● Sookhee barpha - thosa kaarban daaioksaaid (A-3). Jeena therepee - rakta rogon/aanuvanshika vikaaron ka upachaar\n(B-4). Edoba (Adobe) systems ek American bahuNational computer software kanpanee hai jo multimedi aur software\nutpaadon (jaise photoshopa, peedeeeph reedara) ke development par kendrit hai, hardware par nahi. Isliye, option (D)\ncorrectly matched nahi hai. [Q92–Q93]\n● Kaarban monooksaaid ek highly vishailee gas hai jo ganbhir air pradooshan paidaa karti hai. Ye statement true hai.\nSaimual haineemain homyopaithi ke sansthapak the. Chaarls daarvin ne developmentavaad ke principle ka pratipaadan\nkiya tha. Christopher kolanbas ne America ki discover ki thi. Isliye, kevala (C) true hai. [Q94–Q95]\n● Jaisaa ki established hai, nuclear bama (atom bomb) Nuclear fission (heavy nuclear naabhik ke vibhaajana) ke principle\npar kaam karta hai. Hydrogen bama Nuclear fusion par kaam karte hain. 9 agasta 1945 ko naagaasaakee par giraae gaye\nPlutonium-implojana (Plutonium) type ke nuclear bama ka code naam 'phaita maina' (Fat Man) tha. Doosri direction, 6\nagasta 1945 ko hiroshima par giraae gaye 'litila boya' me Uranium-235 ka istemaal kiya gaya tha. [Q96–Q97]\n⚠️ EXAM TRAP — Q91 & Q95 — Multiple/Loose Wording\n\n▸Laser beam medicine me multiple applications rakhta hai (eye surgery, kidney-stone treatment, tumour therapy etc.); Q91 source\nitself multiple-correct mark karta hai.\n\n▸Q95 ka wording loose hai: Otto Hahn aur Fritz Strassmann ne uranium nuclear fission experimentally establish ki; atomic bomb\nfission principle par based hai.\n8. Displays, Automobiles, Humanoid Robots & Robotics\n● 29 April, 1953 ko, losa enjils (America) ke television Station ne 3D me vijnyaana-katha programme 'space paitrola' ka ek\nepisod transmit kiya. Ye world ka pehla 3D television prasaaran tha, jiske liye vishesh polaroid chashme ki requirement thi.\nStatement 1 and 2 sahi hain. Elaseedee (Liquid crystal disple) me Liquid crystal ka heavy use kiya jata hai. Internet eksesa\nke liye modema computer ko phone/kebala laainon se connect karta hai. [Q98–Q99]\n● Liquid crystal ka widely modern electronics me Liquid crystal disple (LCD) banane ke liye use kiya jata hai. Isme kalaaee\nclocks, teevee aur monitor ke disple skreena, Pocket Calculators aur portable computer me unakaa use shamil hai. Isliye\nsabhi option sahi hain. ek OLED me ek utsarjak ilektro-lyoominasenta layer hoti hai jo kaarbanik yaugik ki ek philma hoti hai\njo light emit karti hai. Choonki OLED ko kathor baikalaait (LCD ke opposite) ki requirement nahi hoti hai, isliye unhe\nlacheele plaastik sabsatret par gadhaa ja sakta hai, kapadon ke liye rola-apa disple me banaye ja sakta hai; yahaan tak ki\npaaradarshee bhi banaye ja sakta hai. Isliye, sabhi statement sahi hain. [Q100–Q101]\n● 1080p (jise phula echadee / Full HD bhi kaha jata hai) echadeeteevee haaee-dephinishana video moda ka ek seta hai.\nStandard vaaidaskreen 16:9 pahaloo anupaat ke saath, 1080p kshaitij roop se 1920 piksal aur lanbavat 1080 piksal (1920 x\n1080) ke rijolyooshan me badala jata hai. Radiator (Radiators) hit eksachenjars hain jinka use mainly otomobile me internal\ndahana engine ko thanda karne ke liye kiya jata hai. Ve engine koolent se garmee ko external air me sthanaantarit karte\nhain, jisse engine ko zyada garma hone se rokaa ja sakta hai. [Q102–Q103]\n● Mobile aur otomobile ne Bhartiyon ke social jeevan me ek badi kraanti laa dee hai. Mobile ne communication aur\nkanektivitee (2) me kaaphee improvements kiya hai, jabki otomobile ne logon ki shaareerik speedsheelata aur parivahan (1)\nko kaaphee badhaay hai. Ye directly taur par \"sanvedanasheelataa\" se related nahi hai. 'Manav' (Manav) India ka pehla\n3D-printeda hyoomanoid robot hai. Ise 2014 ke end me e-seta trening enda Research Institute ki laboratory me divaakar\nvaishy dwara develop kiya gaya tha. Ye 2 phuta lanbaa robot hai jisne Mumbai me IIT-bombe tekaphest me apni shuruaat\nki thi. Isme drishti aur Sound prasanskaran capacityen hain. [Q104–Q105]\n● Teslaa ke seeeeo elona maska ne aktoobar 2022 me teslaa ke eaaee de par apne hyoomanoid robot 'Optimus' (Optimus -\njise teslaa bota ke roop me bhi jana jata hai) ke prototype ka khulaasa kiya tha. Optimus teslaa kaaron ke otopaayalat\ndraaivar sahaayata suvidhaaon ke saath kuch eaaee software aur sensar share karta hai. Haalaanki robot ke kai laabha\nhain (vikalaanga vyaktiyon ki sahaayata karna, hazardous paristhitiyon me kaam karna, athaka roop se kaam karna), lekin\nye tathya ki \"ve naukariyon ko pratisthapit (replace) kar sakte hain\" ek saamaajika-aarthika damage hai, kyonki isase\nManav shramikon ki naukariyan chhina jati hain. [Q106–Q107]\n● All India Council for Robotics and Automation (AICRA) ek gaira-laabhakaaree organisation hai jo India me robotics aur\notomeshan me standard established karne ke liye sheersh nikaay ki tarah kaam karta hai. Iski establishment 2014 me hui\nthi. [Q108]\n Source coverage: Q1–Q108\n✓"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0366","t":"01 Scientific Names","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.1 — SCIENTIFIC NAMES — FULL MIND MAP\n🧬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Plant Botanical Names — Banyan, Peepal & Palash\n2. Common Crop & Fruit Botanical Names\n3. Carl Linnaeus — 'Father of Modern Taxonomy'\n4. Animal Scientific Names — The Frog\n5. Generic Family Names — Feline, Caprine, Canine & Bovine\n6. India's National Symbols — Scientific Names\n7. Ascaris — The Roundworm\n1. Plant Botanical Names — Banyan, Peepal & Palash\n● Banyan tree (Bargad) ka botanical name 'Ficus benghalensis' hai — Moraceae family aur Rosales order\nke under aata hai.\n Peepal ka naam 'Ficus religiosa' hai, ye alag species hai (dono Moraceae family\n⚠️\nmein hain, isliye confuse na karein). [Q1]\n● 'Butea monosperma' Palash (Flame of the Forest) ka botanical name hai, jo Indian subcontinent ka\nnative plant hai. Peepal ka naam Ficus Religiosa, Neem ka Azadirachta indica, aur Shirish ka Albizia\nlebbeck hai — Botanical naming system Carolus Linnaeus ne shuru ki thi. [Q5]\n2. Common Crop & Fruit Botanical Names\n● Common Wheat (Gehun) ka botanical name 'Triticum Aestivum' hai.\n Trap: Brassica Campestris\n⚠️\n(Sarson/Field Mustard), Hibiscus Rosa Sinensis (China Rose/Gudhal) aur Zea Mays (Makka) — inhe\nconfuse na karein. Doosre important names: Curcuma longa (Haldi), Solanum tuberosum (Aloo),\nMangifera indica (Aam), Citrus limon (Nimbu), Gossypium herbaceum (Kapas), Musa paradisiaca\n(Kela), Malus domestica (Seb), Pisum sativum (Matar), Syzygium aromaticum (Laung), Allium sativum\n(Lahsun), Zingiber officinale (Adrak), Punica granatum (Anaar), Phyllanthus Emblica (Amla). [Q2]\n3. Carl Linnaeus — 'Father of Modern Taxonomy'\n● Carl Linnaeus (Father of Modern Taxonomy) ne 'Homo sapiens' term diya, aur Binomial Nomenclature\nsystem introduce ki.\n Trap: Charles Darwin 'Theory of Evolution' (natural selection) ke architect the,\n⚠️\nG.J. Mendel (Father of Genetics) ne inheritance ke 3 principles diye, aur Stanley Miller (American\nchemist) ne origin of life par landmark experiments kiye — inhe Linnaeus se confuse na karein. [Q3]\n4. Animal Scientific Names — The Frog\n● 'Rana Tigrina' Frog (mendhak) ka scientific name hai. Doosre common animals: Leopard (Panthera\npardus), Tiger (Panthera Tigris), Wolf (Canis Lupus), Ant (Formicidae), Cockroach (Blattodea), Cow\n(Bos taurus), Housefly (Musca domestica), Parrot (Psittaciformes). [Q4]"," 5. Generic Family Names — Feline, Caprine, Canine & Bovine\n● 'Feline' cat family (Felidae) ke members ka generic naam hai — Cat, Caracal, Lion, Serval, Leopard,\nTiger, Lynxes, Jaguar, Cheetah, Panthera, Cougar shaamil.\n Trap: 'Caprine' sheep-goat family (Ovis,\n⚠️\nChamois, Nilgiri tahr), 'Canine' dog family (German Shepherd, Labrador, Husky), aur 'Bovine' cow family\n(Cattle, Bison, Yak, Buffalo) hai — inhe confuse na karein. [Q6]\n6. India's National Symbols — Scientific Names\n● Indian Peacock (National Bird) ka scientific name 'Pavo Cristatus' hai. Doosre National Symbols:\nNational Flower (Lotus) → Nelumbo nucifera; National Tree (Indian Banyan) → Ficus benghalensis;\nNational Fruit (Mango) → Mangifera indica; National Aquatic Animal (Ganges River Dolphin) →\nPlatanista gangetica; National Animal (Royal Bengal Tiger) → Panthera Tigris. [Q7]\n7. Ascaris — The Roundworm\n● 'Roundworm' Ascaris ka common naam hai — scientifically 'Ascaris lumbricoides' kehte hain, ek large\nparasitic roundworm jo human small intestine ko infect karta hai.\n Trap: 'Pinworm' (Enterobius\n⚠️\nvermicularis) ek alag, chhota worm hai jo human colon-rectum mein rehta hai — Ascaris se confuse na\nkarein. [Q8]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 1 Scientific Names Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0367","t":"02 Nutrition in Animal","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.2 — NUTRITION IN ANIMAL — FULL MIND MAP\n🍎\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. DNA — Genetic Information Source\n2. Nutrition in Amoeba\n3. Body-Building Foods — Proteins & Pulses\n4. Autotrophs — Starch Storage\n5. Heterotrophic Organisms\n6. Balanced Diet — Milk\n7. Vitamin C — Sources & Additive Code E300\n8. Energy from Food — Fats Provide the Most\n9. Vitamin B12 — Cyanocobalamin & Cobalt\n10. Vitamin A — Active Forms & Beta Carotene\n11. Saprotrophic (Saprophytic) Nutrition\n12. Iodine — The Thyroid Micronutrient\n13. Glycogen — Carbohydrate Storage Form\n14. Casein — Milk's White Protein\n15. Protein Denaturation\n16. Keratin — The Structural Material of Hair\n17. Myosin & Actin — Muscle Proteins\n18. Vitamin B1 — Destroyed by Heat\n19. Elements in Proteins — Iodine is NOT One\n20. Fish Liver Oil — Rich in Vitamins A & D\n21. Vitamin K — Produced by Intestinal Bacteria\n22. Lactose — A Disaccharide\n23. Glucose — Cellular Energy Source\n24. Placenta — Embryo's Nutrition Source\n1. DNA — Genetic Information Source\n● DNA (Deoxyribonucleic acid) living organisms mein protein formation ke liye genetic information ka\nsource hai — ye 2 polynucleotide chains ka double helix polymer hai, jiska code 4 bases (Adenine,\nGuanine, Cytosine, Thymine) se bana hota hai. [Q9]\n2. Nutrition in Amoeba\n● Amoeba mein, 'Pseudopodia' (finger-like projections) food lene mein help karte hain, aur 'Food vacuole'\ndigestion of food karta hai — Amoeba pond water mein milne wala single-celled organism hai jo apna\nshape-position constantly badalta rehta hai. [Q10]\n3. Body-Building Foods — Proteins & Pulses\n● Protein-rich food (jaise Peas) ko 'body-building food' kehte hain — protein amino acids ki long chains se\nbana hai, DNA molecules regenerate karne, hormones (Insulin, Secretin) banane, aur immune system\nmein help karta hai. Sources: Beans, Pulses, Yogurt, Fish, Soya, Nuts. [Q11]\n● Pulses growth ke liye proteins provide karti hain — sasti protein-vitamins-fiber ka source hain. Protein\ndeficiency se Kwashiorkor aur Marasmus jaisi diseases hoti hain. [Q14]"," 4. Autotrophs — Starch Storage\n● Autotrophs apna food 'Starch' ke roop mein store karte hain — din mein photosynthesis se starch banta\nhai, raat mein degrade hokar leaf metabolism support karta hai (jaise Leaf mesophyll mein). [Q12]\n5. Heterotrophic Organisms\n● Heterotrophs doosre plants-animals khaakar energy-nutrients paate hain — Tiger ek heterotrophic\norganism hai (Algae, Grass, Neem tree autotrophic hain). [Q13]\n6. Balanced Diet — Milk\n● Milk apne aap mein ek balanced food hai — Calcium, Riboflavin, Phosphorus, Vitamins A-B12,\nPotassium, Magnesium, Zinc, Iodine, lactic acid deta hai. India mein average calorie requirement rural\nareas mein 2400 aur urban areas mein 2100 calories/din hai. [Q15]\n7. Vitamin C — Sources & Additive Code E300\n● Citrus fruits Vitamin C ka richest source hain (Kiwifruit, Orange, Broccoli, Strawberry, Mango, Lemon,\nPapaya bhi shaamil). [Q16]\n● 'E300' ka common naam Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid) hai — ek water-soluble vitamin jo bodily-immune\nfunctions mein crucial role play karta hai. [Q20]\n8. Energy from Food — Fats Provide the Most\n● Fats per gram sabse zyada energy dete hain (9 kcal/g) — carbohydrates-proteins lagbhag 4 kcal/g dete\nhain, aur Roughage (fiber) koi energy nahi deti. [Q17]\n● Fats breakdown hone par sabse zyada energy dete hain — 9 calories/gram, protein-carbohydrates se\ndouble se zyada. [Q28]\n9. Vitamin B12 — Cyanocobalamin & Cobalt\n● 'Cyanocobalamin' Vitamin B12 ka man-made form hai — central nervous system development, red\nblood cell formation aur DNA synthesis ke liye zaroori. Naturally animal-origin foods (fish, meat, poultry,\neggs, dairy) mein milti hai. [Q18]\n● Cobalt element Vitamin B12 mein present hota hai — meat, fish, eggs aur dairy products mein main\nsource hai. [Q23]"," 10. Vitamin A — Active Forms & Beta Carotene\n● Vitamin A ke 3 active forms hote hain: retinal, retinol, aur retinoic acid — Casimir Funk ne vitamins\ndiscover kiye. Vitamin A source: Nuts, Eggs, Fish, Liver, Green leafy vegetables; deficiency se Night\nBlindness, Dry Skin-Eyes hoti hai. [Q19]\n● Beta Carotene (red-orange pigment, carrots-colourful vegetables mein) body mein 'Vitamin A' mein\nconvert hota hai. [Q36]\n11. Saprotrophic (Saprophytic) Nutrition\n● Saprotrophic nutrition mein organism dead-decaying matter se food leta hai — fungi aur soil bacteria\nisse follow karte hain, ye ek chemoheterotrophic extracellular digestion process hai. [Q21]\n● Organisms jo dead-decaying matter se solution form mein nutrients lete hain, unhe 'Saprophytic\nnutrition' kehte hain — example: Mucor, yeast. [Q24]\n12. Iodine — The Thyroid Micronutrient\n● Iodine, thyroid gland ke normal functioning ke liye essential micronutrient hai — thyroid cells food se\niodine absorb karke thyroxine (T4)-triiodothyronine (T3) hormones banate hain. Iron deficiency se\nAnemia, Zinc se skin disease, Calcium se soft bones hoti hai. [Q22]\n13. Glycogen — Carbohydrate Storage Form\n● Glycogen body mein carbohydrates ki storage form hai — excess glucose glycogen mein convert hokar\nliver-muscles mein store hota hai, energy zaroorat par wapas glucose mein todta hai. [Q25]\n14. Casein — Milk's White Protein\n● Casein ek protein hai jo Milk mein paya jaata hai — milk ka white colour Casein ki wajah se hota hai\n(cow's milk mein ~80% casein protein hoti hai). [Q26]\n15. Protein Denaturation\n●\n Trap: 'Proteins temperature se affected nahi hote' ye statement GALAT hai — proteins low\n⚠️\ntemperature mein inactive ho jaate hain, high temperature aur pH change se denature ho jaate hain\n(secondary/tertiary structure disturb hoti hai). Types: Fibrous proteins (keratin, myosin) aur Globular\nproteins (Insulin, albumins). [Q27]\n16. Keratin — The Structural Material of Hair"," ● Keratin hair ka main structural material hai — ek fibrous protein jo epidermis mein milta hai, skin surface\nko strength aur water-resistance deta hai. [Q29]\n17. Myosin & Actin — Muscle Proteins\n● Myosin aur Actin — dono muscle proteins hain. Actin globular multi-functional proteins ka family hai jo\ncytoskeleton mein microfilaments banate hain — Myosin chemical energy (ATP) ko mechanical energy\nmein convert karke force-movement generate karta hai. [Q30]\n18. Vitamin B1 — Destroyed by Heat\n● Vitamin B1 (aur baaki water-soluble vitamins — B-complex, C) heat se destroy ho jaate hain, cooking\nwater mein leach ho jaate hain — Fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) heat-stable hote hain. [Q31]\n19. Elements in Proteins — Iodine is NOT One\n●\n Trap: Iodine proteins ka part NAHI hai — proteins mein Carbon, Hydrogen, Oxygen, Nitrogen aur\n⚠️\nSulphur hote hain. Iodine thyroid hormones ka essential component hai, iodized salt-seafood mein milta\nhai. [Q32]\n20. Fish Liver Oil — Rich in Vitamins A & D\n● Fish liver oil (jaise Cod liver oil) Vitamin D AUR Vitamin A — dono mein rich hoti hai. Vitamin A (Eggs,\nmilk, carrots, mangoes), Vitamin D (fatty fish, fish liver oils, fortified milk-cereals) mein milta hai. [Q33]\n21. Vitamin K — Produced by Intestinal Bacteria\n● Vitamin K, Intestine mein bacteria dwara naturally produce hoti hai — fat-soluble vitamin, green leafy\nvegetables mein present hoti hai, blood clotting aur bone health mein help karti hai. [Q34]\n22. Lactose — A Disaccharide\n● Lactose (milk sugar, C12H22O11) Glucose aur Galactose se milkar bani disaccharide hai — 2\nmonosaccharides ek glycosidic bond se jude hote hain. [Q35]\n23. Glucose — Cellular Energy Source"," ● Glucose body ke cells mein O2 ke saath combine hokar energy provide karta hai — carbohydrates\ndigestion se glucose banta hai, respiration reaction: C6H12O6 + 6O2 → 6CO2 + 6H2O + energy. [Q37]\n24. Placenta — Embryo's Nutrition Source\n● Embryo, mother ke blood se nutrition 'Placenta' (special tissue, uterus mein pregnancy ke dauran\ndevelop hoti hai) ke through leta hai — oxygen-nutrients deta hai, waste products remove karta hai.\n[Q38]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 2 Nutrition in Animal Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0368","t":"03 Nutrition in Plant","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.3 — NUTRITION IN PLANT — FULL MIND MAP\n🌱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Respiration in Plants — Aerobic Process & Glucose Breakdown\n2. Phloem — Structure, Companion Cells & Food Transport\n3. Storage Carbohydrates — Starch (Plants) vs Glycogen (Animals)\n4. Plastids — Types\n5. Water's Role in Plant Cell Structure\n6. Iron-Rich Foods — Jaggery\n7. Transportation in Plants — Xylem vs Phloem Features\n8. Why Plants Have Low Energy Needs\n9. Autotrophic Nutrition — Essential Requirements\n10. Respiration & Gas Exchange in Plants\n11. Plant Excretion — Waste Products\n12. Translocation — Movement of Food\n13. Xylem — Structure & Components\n14. Parasitic Nutrition — Cuscuta\n15. Photosynthesis — Carbon & Energy Requirements\n15b. Oxygen — Waste Product of Photosynthesis\n16. Atmospheric Pressure & the Rate of Transpiration\n17. Testing for Starch in Photosynthesis Experiments\n18. Active Transport — Food, Amino Acids & Hormones\n19. Plant Nutrition — Mineral Absorption\n20. Photosynthesis — Process, Sequence & Products\n21. Plant Hormones — Cytokinin & Fruits\n22. Saprotrophic Nutrition — Mushroom\n23. Xylem-Phloem Transport — Direction\n24. Water Transport Pathway — Soil to Leaves\n25. Fibrous Roots — Rice, Wheat, Maize (NOT Beetroot)\n26. Sugarcane — Efficient Converter of Sunlight\n27. Phototropism — Sunflower Facing the Sun\n28. Chlorophyll — The Green Pigment\n29. Desert Plants — Photosynthesis in the Stem\n30. Vitamin C — Gooseberry\n31. Rhizobium — Root Nodules of Leguminous Plants\n32. Vitamin B — Cereals Are the Richest Source\n33. Osmosis — Water Uptake by Root Hairs\n34. Nitrogen Fixation — Legumes\n35. Dietary Fiber — Cellulose (Insoluble)\n36. Banana — Rich in Potassium\n37. Plasmolysis — Water Loss by Osmosis\n38. Minerals in Diet — Fluoride & Potassium\n39. Meristems — Primary Growth (Intercalary & Apical)\n1. Respiration in Plants — Aerobic Process & Glucose Breakdown\n● Aerobic respiration mein Oxygen zaroori hai — Pyruvate ka conversion CO2, H2O aur energy mein O2\nki presence mein hota hai. Glycolysis cytoplasm mein hoti hai, jisme glucose (6-carbon) oxidize hokar 2\npyruvate (3-carbon) molecules banata hai. Reaction: Glucose + O2 → CO2 + H2O + Energy (ATP).\nAnaerobic respiration mein oxygen ki absence mein incomplete oxidation hoti hai. [Q39]\n● Glucose molecule breakdown hokar 'Pyruvic acid' (C3H4O3) banata hai — Kreb cycle mein glucose ke\noxidation se energy release hoti hai. Mitochondria cell ka respiratory organelle hai. [Q80]"," 2. Phloem — Structure, Companion Cells & Food Transport\n● Phloem ek living vascular tissue hai jo leaves mein banaya gaya food (photosynthesis se) plant ke sabhi\nparts tak transport karta hai — is process ko 'phloem translocation' kehte hain. Phloem ke elements:\nsieve tubes, companion cells, phloem parenchyma, phloem fibres — sabhi bidirectional food transport\nkarte hain. [Q40]\n● Phloem diagram mein 'Companion Cell' hi perforated walls wala part NAHI hai (Sieve Pore perforated\nhoti hai) — Companion Cell sieve tube cells ki metabolic functioning mein help karti hai, transmembrane\nproteins use karke sugar-amino acids active transport se lete hai. [Q56]\n● Phloem mein thickened cell walls wali cells milti hain — ye specialised food-conducting tissue hai,\ncarbohydrates-amino acids ko leaf (photosynthesized part) se non-photosynthetic parts tak le jaati hai.\n[Q74]\n●\n Trap: Phloem transportation mein GTP aur CTP ka use NAHI hota — ye statement FALSE hai.\n⚠️\nPhloem transportation ATP energy use karta hai, sucrose active transport se load hoti hai, aur osmotic\npressure badhne se water phloem mein move karta hai. [Q75]\n3. Storage Carbohydrates — Starch (Plants) vs Glycogen (Animals)\n● Plants mein storage carbohydrate 'Starch' hai — (C6H10O5)n, alpha D glucose units ka polymer.\nGlycogen animals-fungi mein glucose ki stored form hai, Sucrose (glucose+fructose) disaccharide hai,\nGlucose blood ka main sugar hai. [Q41]\n●\n Trap: Autotrophs unused carbohydrates ko 'Glycogen' ki tarah STORE NAHI karte — ye galat\n⚠️\nstatement hai, wo Starch ki tarah store karte hain (Glycogen sirf animals mein hota hai). Autotrophs\n(green plants, kuch bacteria) 'primary producers' kehlaate hain — photosynthesis se carbon-energy\nrequirements poori karte hain. [Q70]\n4. Plastids — Types\n● Colourless plastids 'Leucoplastids' kehlaate hain — endosperm, tubers, cotyledons, roots jaise non-\nphotosynthetic parts mein milte hain. Chloroplastids light energy ko chemical energy mein convert karte\nhain (photosynthesis), Chromoplastids flowers-fruits ko yellow-orange-red color dete hain. [Q42]\n5. Water's Role in Plant Cell Structure\n● Plant cell mein 'Water' ki amount uski structure alter karke movement facilitate karti hai — plants\neukaryotic cells hote hain. Plant hormones: Auxins, Gibberellins, Cytokinins, Ethylene, Abscisic Acid.\nXylem water transportation facilitate karta hai. [Q43]\n6. Iron-Rich Foods — Jaggery"," ● Jaggery mein iron high amount mein hota hai — 100 grams mein lagbhag 11 mg iron. Doosre iron-rich\nfoods: nuts, dried fruit, legumes, dark leafy green vegetables (spinach, broccoli), oats. Milk-Butter\nCalcium-B2-B12 mein rich hain, Rice protein-vitamins ka source hai. [Q44]\n7. Transportation in Plants — Xylem vs Phloem Features\n●\n Trap: Water aur food ka movement 'bidirectional' NAHI hota (incorrect feature) — Xylem mein water\n⚠️\nmovement unidirectional hota hai (roots se leaves), Phloem mein food bidirectional. Vessels-Tracheids\ndead cells hain, Sieve tubes living. Water movement physical forces se, food movement energy se hota\nhai. [Q45]\n● Water transport ke baare mein sahi statement: 'Stomata ke through water vapour ki tarah loss hone ki\nprocess ko Transpiration kehte hain' — sahi hai. Xylem cells se leaves tak water pull hone ki process\n'Translocation' NAHI, 'Ascent of sap' kehlaati hai. [Q63]\n8. Why Plants Have Low Energy Needs\n● Plants ki energy needs low hoti hain kyunki unke paas bahut se dead cells (jaise sclerenchyma) hote\nhain, jinhe koi energy nahi chahiye — animals ki tarah unhe food-shelter ki talaash mein move nahi\nkarna padta. [Q46]\n9. Autotrophic Nutrition — Essential Requirements\n●\n Trap: 'Oxygen' autotrophic nutrition ke liye zaroori NAHI hai — Chlorophyll, Carbon dioxide aur Light\n⚠️\n\nzaroori hain. Autotrophic nutrition mein organism simple inorganic materials (water, mineral salts, CO2)\nse apna food banata hai sunlight ki presence mein. [Q47]\n10. Respiration & Gas Exchange in Plants\n●\n Trap: 'Din mein atmosphere mein Carbon dioxide add hoti hai' ye statement INCORRECT hai — din\n⚠️\nmein plants oxygen release karte hain (photosynthesis), raat mein CO2 release hoti hai (respiration).\nPlants stomata-lenticels se gases exchange karte hain, diffusion ke through. [Q48]\n● Plant root cells oxygen 'soil particles ke beech ki air spaces' se lete hain — root hair mein oxygen\ndiffuse hoti hai, respiration mein use hoti hai, CO2 wapas usi rasta se escape hoti hai. [Q73]\n● Transpiration 'Stomata' ke through hoti hai — leaves mein tiny openings/pores gas exchange allow\nkarte hain. [Q101]\n● Plants mein gases ka exchange 'Stomata' ke through hota hai — epidermis mein tiny pore, atmosphere\naur plants ke beech gas exchange control karta hai (stomatal pore size change karke water loss bhi\ncontrol karta hai). [Q102]\n11. Plant Excretion — Waste Products"," ●\n Trap: Plant waste products 'centrioles' mein NAHI, 'cellular vacuoles' mein store hote hain — ye\n⚠️\ngalat statement hai. Transpiration se surplus water nikalti hai, Photosynthesis oxygen by-product deti\nhai, Gum plants ka excretory product hai (old xylem mein resins-gums store hote hain). [Q49]\n12. Translocation — Movement of Food\n● 'Translocation' photosynthesis ke soluble products aur doosre materials ko leaves se plant ke doosre\ntissues tak transport karne ki process hai — Transpiration water evaporation hai, Guttation vascular\nplants (grass) se water droplets secretion, Tropic movement stimulus response movement hai. [Q50]\n● Companion cells ki help se sieve tubes mein food-substances ka transport hota hai (upward-downward\ndono) — ise 'Translocation' kehte hain. [Q62]\n● Spring season mein, roots mein stored nutrients 'Bud' ki taraf move karte hain — jab leaves shed hoti\nhain, roots mein stored sugar organic material ko growing Buds ki taraf mobilize karta hai — isse\nphloem mein bidirectional flow dikhta hai. [Q72]\n13. Xylem — Structure & Components\n● Xylem ke 'Tracheids aur Vessels' dead cells hote hain, phir bhi water-minerals transport karte hain —\nXylem Fibre lignified dead cell hai (mechanical support deti hai), Xylem Parenchyma sirf living cells hain\njo starch-fat store karte hain. [Q51]\n● Xylem mein 'Parenchyma' cells food store karti hain — oil, fats, proteins, starch ke roop mein. Tracheid\ncells water-inorganic salts transport karte hain aur structural support dete hain. [Q54]\n●\n Trap: 'Companion cell' Xylem ka component NAHI hai — Xylem ke components hain: Tracheids,\n⚠️\nVessels, Xylem Fibre, Xylem Parenchyma (Companion cell Phloem ka part hai). [Q55]\n● Xylem vessels 'Lignin' ki wajah se waterproof hote hain — Cellulose plant shape deta hai, Cutin cuticle\nmein waterproofing karta hai (leaves-fruits), Suberin cork cell walls mein water penetration rokta hai.\n[Q78]\n14. Parasitic Nutrition — Cuscuta\n● 'Cuscuta' parasitic nutritive strategy dikhati hai — heterotrophic nutrition ka ek mode, jisme parasite host\nke body surface ya andar reh kar nutrition leta hai. Cuscuta, lice, leeches, tapeworms is category mein\naate hain. [Q52]\n● Cuscuta plants se parasite ki tarah nutrition leta hai — parasitic plants host plant se attach hokar special\nmodified roots 'Haustorium' se nutrition lete hain. Doosre examples: Loranthus, Balanophora,\nSandalwood tree. [Q104]\n15. Photosynthesis — Carbon & Energy Requirements"," ● Plants ki carbon aur energy requirements 'Photosynthesis' se poori hoti hain — sunlight-water-CO2 use\nkarke oxygen aur sugar (energy) banate hain. [Q53]\n● Plants mein ultimate energy source 'Sunlight' hai — solar energy se producers (green plants)\nphotosynthesis se food banate hain, jo doosre organisms ko transfer hota hai. Photosynthesis rate Red\ncolour mein maximum hoti hai. [Q83]\n● Photosynthesis mein Oxygen 'release' hoti hai (atmosphere mein) — green plants CO2-water se\ncarbohydrates banate hain, sunlight ki presence mein, chemical energy release karte hue. [Q98]\n●\n Trap: 'Oxygen' photosynthesis ke liye essential NAHI hai — Chlorophyll, Sunlight aur Carbon\n⚠️\ndioxide zaroori hain, Oxygen ek by-product hai jo release hoti hai. [Q99]\n● Photosynthesis mein plants 'Solar energy' (light energy) use karte hain — chlorophyll jaise pigments\nisse capture karke chemical energy (glucose) mein convert karte hain. [Q100]\n15b. Oxygen — Waste Product of Photosynthesis\n● Photosynthesis ke dauran 'Oxygen' waste product ki tarah produce hoti hai — CO2 aur water, sunlight-\nchlorophyll ki presence mein, oxygen aur glucose mein convert hote hain. Glucose plant food ki tarah\nuse hota hai, oxygen by-product hai: 6CO2 + 6H2O → C6H12O6 + 6O2. [Q57]\n16. Atmospheric Pressure & the Rate of Transpiration\n● Atmospheric pressure aur transpiration rate 'inversely proportional' hote hain — low pressure mein\nwater vapour fast move karta hai (transpiration badhti hai), high pressure mein water loss slow hota hai.\n[Q58]\n17. Testing for Starch in Photosynthesis Experiments\n● Photosynthesis experiments mein starch ki presence measure karte hain kyunki 'Glucose formed starch\nmein convert ho jaata hai' — Glucose plant cell growth (cellulose) ke liye use ho sakta hai, starch mein\nconvert hokar baad mein wapas glucose ban sakta hai, ya respiration mein energy release kar sakta\nhai. [Q59]\n18. Active Transport — Food, Amino Acids & Hormones\n● Plants mein diffusion se zyadatar transportation hoti hai, lekin kuch substances (Food, Amino acids,\nHormones) ke transport ke liye energy chahiye — ye 'Active Transport' kehlaata hai. Passive transport\n(simple diffusion) mein energy expenditure nahi hoti. [Q60]\n19. Plant Nutrition — Mineral Absorption"," ●\n Trap: 'Minerals-nutrients water se poorly absorb hote hain' — ye statement INCORRECT hai (galat)\n⚠️\n— actually minerals-nutrients water ke through hi absorb hote hain (root zone soil ke water se). Main\nnutrients (NPK): Nitrogen-Phosphorus-Potassium, aur Calcium-Magnesium-Sulphur. Iron-Manganese\nmicronutrients hain. [Q61]\n● Nitrogen plants ko soil se milta hai — plants khud atmosphere se nitrogen absorb nahi kar sakte,\nammonia ya nitrates ke roop mein (nitrogen fixation se) rely karte hain. Main nutrients: Nitrogen,\nPhosphorus, Potassium. [Q89]\n20. Photosynthesis — Process, Sequence & Products\n●\n Trap: 'Photosynthesis mein CO2 ka carbohydrates mein oxidation hota hai' ye statement\n⚠️\nINCORRECT hai (galat) — actually CO2 ka 'reduction' hota hai carbohydrates mein, na ki oxidation.\nEquation: 6CO2 + 6H2O → C6H12O6 + 6O2. [Q64]\n● Photosynthesis ke liye 4 components zaroori hain: Carbon dioxide, water, sunlight aur chlorophyll —\noxygen by-product ki tarah release hoti hai, food carbohydrates (glucose-starch) ki tarah store hota hai.\n[Q65]\n● Photosynthesis ke steps ka sahi sequence: (c) chlorophyll dwara light absorption → (b) light energy\nchemical energy mein convert → (a) water molecule split (H aur O mein) → (d) CO2 reduce hokar\ncarbohydrates. [Q66]\n● Photosynthesis mein 6 water molecules '12H2O' se produce hote hain — glucose banane ke liye 12\nwater molecules aur 6 CO2 chahiye: 6CO2 + 12H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2 + 6H2O. [Q69]\n●\n Trap: 'Oxygen ka absorption' photosynthesis ke dauran NAHI hota — light energy absorption, water\n⚠️\nmolecules ka splitting, aur CO2 ka reduction hota hai, oxygen absorb nahi, release hoti hai. [Q77]\n● Green light range photosynthesis ki rate ko sabse kam affect karta hai — chlorophyll green wavelength\nabsorb nahi karta (isliye plants green dikhte hain), red-blue light zyada effective hoti hai photosynthesis\nke liye. [Q85]\n● Photosynthesis se 'Glucose, Water aur Oxygen' products banate hain — 6CO2 + 12H2O → C6H12O6\n(Glucose) + 6H2O (Water) + 6O2 (Oxygen). [Q105]\n21. Plant Hormones — Cytokinin & Fruits\n● 'Cytokinin' hormone fruits mein particularly high hoti hai — cell division promote karti hai aur cell\nexpansion badhati hai. Gibberellin germination-elongation control karti hai, Auxins embryonic\ndevelopment-tropisms, Abscisic acid growth-stress response regulate karti hai. [Q67]\n22. Saprotrophic Nutrition — Mushroom\n● Mushrooms mein 'Saprotrophic' nutrition hoti hai — organisms dead-decaying organic matter se food\nlete hain. Doosre saprotrophic organisms: Rhizopus (bread mould), Mucor (pin mould), Yeast. [Q68]\n● Mushroom ek 'Saprotroph' hai — dead-decaying matter se solution form mein food leta hai. Doosre\nsaprotrophs: Bacteria, fungi, molds, Mycorrhizal fungi. Algae autotrophs hain, Pigeon-Man omnivorous\nhain. [Q103]"," 23. Xylem-Phloem Transport — Direction\n● Diagram mein blue arrows (Xylem transport) aur red arrows (Phloem transport) — Xylem: root hair se\ncell-to-cell osmosis se xylem tak, phir leaves tak. Phloem: leaves se nutrients-sugar ka bidirectional\ntranslocation. [Q71]\n24. Water Transport Pathway — Soil to Leaves\n● Water ka soil se leaves tak transport pathway: Soil → root hairs → root cortex → xylem of roots →\nxylem of stem → xylem of leaf — root hair diffusion se water-minerals soil se absorb karte hain, xylem\nsmall vessels roots-leaves ko connect karte hain. [Q76]\n25. Fibrous Roots — Rice, Wheat, Maize (NOT Beetroot)\n●\n Trap: Beetroot mein fibrous roots NAHI hoti (taproot hoti hai) — Rice, Wheat, Maize jaise plants\n⚠️\nmein fibrous roots hoti hain (thin, moderately branching, dense network, soil surface ke close). Doosre\nexamples: marigold, Sugarcane, banana. [Q79]\n26. Sugarcane — Efficient Converter of Sunlight\n● Sugarcane plant sunlight ko chemical energy mein sabse efficiently convert karta hai — photosynthesis\nse sunlight-CO2-water use karke glucose-oxygen banata hai. Sugarcane (Saccharum officinarum)\nPoaceae family ki tall perennial grass hai. [Q81]\n27. Phototropism — Sunflower Facing the Sun\n● Sunflower ka sun ki taraf move karna 'Phototropism' kehlaata hai — plant light ki direction mein grow\nkarne ki ability, jisse photosynthesis ke liye sunlight exposure maximize hoti hai. Charles Darwin ne\n1880 mein isse study kiya, 'The Power of Movement in Plants' book mein publish kiya. [Q82]\n28. Chlorophyll — The Green Pigment\n● 'Chlorophyll' plants ko green color deta hai — green wavelength ko absorb nahi karta, isliye plants\ngreen dikhte hain. Chloroplasts mein milta hai, photosynthesis ke liye responsible, aur Magnesium\nelement contain karta hai. [Q84]\n29. Desert Plants — Photosynthesis in the Stem"," ● Cactus jaise desert plants (Xerophytes) mein photosynthesis 'Stem' mein hoti hai — deep-spreading\nroots aur water-storing capacity ke saath dry conditions withstand karte hain. Examples: Aeonium,\nAgave. [Q86]\n30. Vitamin C — Gooseberry\n● Gooseberry (Amla) Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid) ka rich source hai — doosre sources: Citrus fruits\n(Oranges, Kiwi, Lemon, Grapefruit), Strawberries, Peppers. [Q87]\n31. Rhizobium — Root Nodules of Leguminous Plants\n● 'Rhizobium' bacteria leguminous plants ke root nodules ke formation se associate hai — nitrogen\nfixation mein help karta hai. (Salmonella, Clostridium, E.coli inse alag hain.) [Q88]\n32. Vitamin B — Cereals Are the Richest Source\n● Cereals Vitamin B ka richest source hain. Doosre Vitamin sources: Vitamin A (Carrots, tomatoes, cod\nliver oil), Vitamin C (Orange, amla, lemon), Vitamin D (Fish oil, sunlight, milk), Vitamin E (Spinach, nuts).\n[Q90]\n33. Osmosis — Water Uptake by Root Hairs\n● Soil se water root hairs mein 'Osmosis' ki wajah se enter karta hai — root hairs delicate epidermal\noutgrowths hain, large surface area rakhte hain, semi-permeable membrane se solvent molecules\nconcentration gradient ke against move karte hain. [Q91]\n34. Nitrogen Fixation — Legumes\n● 'Legumes' apne aap air se nitrogen fix kar sakte hain (Fabaceae family) — root nodules mein\nRhizobium bacteria ki help se. Tubers doosri category ke plants hain (storage organs). [Q92]\n35. Dietary Fiber — Cellulose (Insoluble)\n● 'Cellulose' insoluble dietary fiber ka example hai — seed-skin of fruit, whole-wheat, bread, brown rice\nmein milta hai. Soluble fibers (Psyllium, Pectin, Inulin) digestion slow karte hain, fatty acids ko bind karte\nhain. [Q93]\n36. Banana — Rich in Potassium"," ● Banana mein sabse zyada amount mein 'Potassium' hota hai — carbohydrates, fibers, Vitamin B6,\nManganese bhi hote hain. Doosre Potassium sources: Potatoes, Spinach, Avocados. [Q94]\n37. Plasmolysis — Water Loss by Osmosis\n● 'Plasmolysis' living plant cell ka osmosis se water lose karke shrink hone ki process hai — protoplasm\nshrink hota hai. Cytolysis (excess water se cell burst hona) aur Hemolysis (RBC breakdown) isse alag\nhain. [Q95]\n38. Minerals in Diet — Fluoride & Potassium\n● Coffee, spinach, onion aur tea 'Fluoride' provide karte hain diet mein — tooth enamel remineralize karta\nhai. (Sodium — canned meat, bacon; Iodine — fish, seaweed; Chloride — olives, tomatoes.) [Q96]\n● Green aur yellow vegetables diet mein 'Potassium' provide karte hain. (Zinc — sea foods, eggs; Sodium\n— apples, guavas; Copper — meats, shellfish.) [Q97]\n39. Meristems — Primary Growth (Intercalary & Apical)\n● Plants mein primary growth 'Intercalary aur Apical meristem' se hoti hai (C and D) — Apical meristem\nroot-shoot tip par growth karti hai, Intercalary meristem internodes/leaf base par length badhati hai.\nLateral meristem thickness badhati hai (secondary growth). [Q106]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 3 Nutrition in Plant Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0369","t":"04 Deficiency and Diseases","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" 🩺 BIOLOGY CH.4 — DEFICIENCY & DISEASES — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Medicinal Plants — Sarpagandha & Arjuna\n2. HIV/AIDS — Transmission, Prevention & Testing\n3. UV Rays — Skin Cancer\n4. Puberty — Voice Change\n5. Tooth Decay\n6. STDs — Virus vs Bacteria vs Fungus\n7. Vitamin K — Blood Clotting\n8. Dengvaxia — First Approved Dengue Vaccine\n9. Kala-azar — Caused by Leishmania\n10. Bird Flu — H5N1 Virus\n11. Vitamin A — Vision & Its Deficiency\n12. Eye Diseases — Goiter is NOT One\n13. Disease-Causative Organism — A Match Trap\n14. Fungal Plant Diseases\n15. Malaria — Plasmodium\n16. Radioisotope — Strontium-89 for Bone Cancer\n17. Megaloblastic Anaemia — Vitamin B9 Deficiency\n18. Tranquilizer — Anxiety Treatment\n19. Bacterial Diseases — Diphtheria, Typhoid & Tetanus\n20. Chicken Pox — A Viral Disease\n21. Fire Blight — Apple's Disease\n22. Hepatitis A — A Viral Disease\n23. Peptic Ulcer — Helicobacter pylori\n24. Airborne vs Waterborne Diseases\n25. Filariasis (Elephantiasis) — Mosquito-Borne\n26. Eye Donation — Who Can Donate\n27. Antibiotics — Stop Microorganism Growth\n28. Amoebiasis — Causes Dysentery\n29. Foot-and-Mouth Disease — A Viral Illness\n30. Leukemia — Blood Cancer\n31. Leukoderma — A Skin Disease\n32. Typhoid — Incubation Period\n33. Fluoride — Tooth Decay Prevention\n34. Anaemia — Red Blood Corpuscles Deficiency\n35. Diabetes — Treated by Insulin\n36. Grover's Disease — A Skin Disorder\n37. Skin Pigmentation Diseases — Vitiligo & Albinism\n38. Goitre — Iodine Deficiency\n39. Haemophilia — A Blood Clotting Disorder\n40. Beriberi — Vitamin B1 Deficiency\n41. Dengue — Caused by Viruses\n1. Medicinal Plants — Sarpagandha & Arjuna\n● 'Sarpagandha' blood pressure treat karne ka best remedy hai — diabetes, insomnia, indigestion mein\nbhi use hota hai. Rajnigandha stress reliever hai, Navamallika cardiac tonic hai. [Q107]\n● 'Arjuna' plant (Terminalia arjuna) high blood pressure aur earache treat karne mein use hota hai —\nleaves blood pressure regulate karti hain, juice earache cure karta hai, bark heart diseases cure karti\nhai. [Q109]"," 2. HIV/AIDS — Transmission, Prevention & Testing\n● AIDS (Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome) HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) se hoti hai —\nwhite blood cells attack karta hai. ELISA test se antibodies detect hoti hain, World AIDS Day 1\nDecember hai. [Q108]\n●\n Trap: HIV infection prevent karne ke liye 'Available vaccines' use karna sahi tareeka NAHI hai — koi\n⚠️\nHIV vaccine exist nahi karti. Safe sex, sterile needles, aur safe blood transfusion effective preventive\nmethods hain. [Q110]\n●\n Trap: 'HIV patient ke saath toilet share karna' se HIV NAHI failta — HIV sexual contact, blood\n⚠️\ntransfusion, mother-to-child (pregnancy), ya syringes share karne se failta hai. [Q114]\n● Condoms sexually transmitted diseases (STIs, HIV samet) ke spread ko rokne mein effective\ncontraception hain. [Q115]\n● HIV avoid karne ki best strategy hai 'sex ko ek known-healthy person tak restrict karna' (monogamy).\n[Q119]\n●\n Trap: HIV-AIDS virus 'hand shaking' se transmit NAHI hota — blood transfusion, sexual contact, aur\n⚠️\nbreastfeeding se failta hai (body fluids ke exchange se). [Q120]\n● Person 1 saal pehle HIV-infected hai ya nahi, ye 'anti-HIV antibodies blood mein' dhoondkar diagnose\nkiya jaata hai — 3 types ke HIV tests: Antibody, Antigen, Nucleic acid tests (NAT). [Q122]\n● HIV transmission prevent karne ke liye 'Barrier methods only' (jaise condoms) effective hain — Copper-\nT ya oral contraceptives HIV transmission nahi rokte, sirf pregnancy prevent karte hain. [Q123]\n● HIV ka full form 'Human Immunodeficiency Virus' hai — ye immune system attack karta hai (specifically\nCD4 T lymphocytes), body ki infections se ladne ki capacity kamzor karta hai. [Q171]\n3. UV Rays — Skin Cancer\n● Excessive UV rays exposure se 'Skin cancer' hota hai — immune system damage aur Cataracts (eye\ndamage) bhi ho sakti hai. Leukemia blood cancer hai (WBC count badhne se). [Q111]\n4. Puberty — Voice Change\n● Puberty ke dauran voice change 'larynx ke development' se hoti hai — boys mein testosterone badhne\nse larynx mein changes aate hain. [Q112]\n5. Tooth Decay\n●\n Trap: Tooth decay mein 'bacteria ka koi role nahi, virus se hoti hai' — ye statement GALAT hai —\n⚠️\nactually bacteria plaque mein sugars ko acids mein convert karta hai, jo enamel soften karke tooth loss\nkarti hai. [Q113]"," 6. STDs — Virus vs Bacteria vs Fungus\n● STDs jo virus se failte hain: AIDS (HIV), Warts (HPV), Genital Herpes (Herpes Simplex Virus) —\n\n⚠️\nGonorrhoea aur Syphilis bacteria se failte hain, isliye inhe confuse na karein. [Q116, Q117]\n● 'Warts' HPV (human papillomavirus) se hote hain — excess keratin protein produce karta hai. [Q118]\n●\n Trap: 'Candidiasis' sexually transmitted disease NAHI hai — ye Candida yeast se hone wala fungal\n⚠️\ninfection hai. Syphilis, Gonorrhea aur Warts actual STDs hain. [Q169]\n7. Vitamin K — Blood Clotting\n● Vitamin K (Phylloquinone) proteins-calcium activate karta hai blood clotting ke liye — green leafy\nvegetables (kale, spinach, broccoli) mein milta hai. Deficiency se poor bone development, Osteoporosis\nhoti hai. [Q131]\n8. Dengvaxia — First Approved Dengue Vaccine\n● US FDA ne 2019 mein 'Dengvaxia' vaccine ko Dengue disease ke liye approve kiya — 9-16 saal ke\nlogo mein, jo pehle dengue-infected the aur endemic areas mein rehte hain. [Q132]\n9. Kala-azar — Caused by Leishmania\n● Kala-azar 'Leishmania' unicellular protozoan parasite se hoti hai — infected female phlebotomine\nsandflies ke bite se failti hai. Symptoms: Fever, weight loss, spleen-liver enlargement. [Q133]\n● Kala-azar organism ki origin 'downward gamete fission' (binary fission) se hoti hai — India mein\n'Leishmania donovani' hi is disease ka ekmatra parasite hai. [Q167]\n10. Bird Flu — H5N1 Virus\n● Bird Flu (Avian Influenza) 'H5N1 virus' se hota hai — ek subtype of Avian influenza Type A viruses.\n[Q134]\n11. Vitamin A — Vision & Its Deficiency\n● Vitamin A ki deficiency se color blindness aur poor vision hoti hai — night blindness bhi hoti hai. [Q135]\n● Carrots mein high Vitamin A hoti hai (beta carotene se) — bachche ki vision strengthen karti hai. [Q124]\n● Vitamin A eyes-skin ko healthy rakhti hai — immune system-reproduction ke liye bhi important hai.\n[Q145]\n● 'Golden rice' Vitamin A ki deficiency fulfill karti hai — Vitamin A deficiency se Night blindness hoti hai.\n[Q160]"," 12. Eye Diseases — Goiter is NOT One\n●\n Trap: 'Goiter' eye disease NAHI hai — ye thyroid gland ka abnormal enlargement hai (iodine\n⚠️\ndeficiency se). Glaucoma, Cataract aur Dry eye actual eye conditions hain. [Q136]\n13. Disease-Causative Organism — A Match Trap\n●\n Trap: 'Cholera-Influenza' galat match hai — Cholera actually Vibrio cholerae bacterium se hoti hai,\n⚠️\nInfluenza se NAHI. (TB-Mycobacterium, AIDS-HIV, Malaria-Plasmodium sahi hain.) [Q137]\n14. Fungal Plant Diseases\n● Puccinia graminis fungus 'Black rust in wheat' cause karti hai — spores wind-rain se spread hoti hain.\n(Late blight of potato — Phytophthora infestans; Red rot of sugarcane — Colletotrichum falcatum.)\n[Q138]\n● 'Gibberella fujikuroi' fungal pathogen rice seedlings mein 'bakane' (foolish seedling) disease cause karta\nhai. [Q142]\n●\n Trap: 'Citrus canker' fungal disease NAHI hai — ye bacterial disease hai (Xanthomonas citri).\n⚠️\nDamping off seedling, Rust of wheat (Puccinia) aur Red Rot of sugarcane fungal diseases hain. [Q146]\n●\n Trap: 'Potato mosaic' seed-borne disease NAHI hai — ye aphids ya mechanical contact se failti hai.\n⚠️\nMoulting of wheat, Red rot of sugarcane, Sheath rot on rice seed-borne diseases hain. [Q154]\n15. Malaria — Plasmodium\n● 'Plasmodium' malaria parasite hai — E.coli, Salmonella aur Mycobacterium doosre bacterial pathogens\nhain. [Q139]\n16. Radioisotope — Strontium-89 for Bone Cancer\n● 'Strontium-89' metastatic bone cancer ke treatment ke liye use hota hai. Carbon-14 archaeological\ndating mein, Iodine-131 thyroid diseases mein use hota hai. [Q140]\n17. Megaloblastic Anaemia — Vitamin B9 Deficiency\n● Megaloblastic anaemia Vitamin B9 (Folic acid) ki deficiency se hoti hai — red blood cells normal se\nbade ho jaate hain. [Q141]"," 18. Tranquilizer — Anxiety Treatment\n● Tranquilizer normally 'Anxiety' (fear, dread, uneasiness) ke liye administer hoti hai. [Q143]\n19. Bacterial Diseases — Diphtheria, Typhoid & Tetanus\n● 'Diphtheria' bacteria (Corynebacterium diphtheriae) se hoti hai — throat-upper respiratory tract affect\nkarti hai. Chicken pox, Mumps, Measles viral diseases hain. [Q144]\n● 'Typhoid' bacteria (Salmonella Typhi) se hoti hai. Polio, Measles, Hepatitis A viral diseases hain. [Q129]\n● Tetanus (lockjaw) nervous system ki serious disease hai, toxin-producing 'Bacterium' (Clostridium\ntetani) se — muscle contractions (jaw-neck) karti hai. [Q126]\n20. Chicken Pox — A Viral Disease\n● Chicken Pox 'virus' (Varicella Zoster Virus) se hoti hai — highly contagious. Virus diseases: Rabies,\nMeasles, Herpes, Hepatitis, Polio, AIDS, Smallpox, Dengue. Bacteria diseases: plague, diphtheria,\ntyphoid, tetanus, cholera. [Q127]\n21. Fire Blight — Apple's Disease\n● Apple se related disease 'Fire blight' hai — highly contagious bacterial infection, fruit trees (apple, pear)\nko affect karti hai, wilting-blackening karti hai. Tikka disease groundnut ki, green ear disease millet ki\nhai. [Q128]\n22. Hepatitis A — A Viral Disease\n● Hepatitis A 'virus' (hepatitis A virus/HAV) se hoti hai — liver ko affect karti hai, contaminated food-water\nya close contact se transmit hoti hai. [Q130]\n23. Peptic Ulcer — Helicobacter pylori\n● Peptic ulcer ka causative organism 'Bacterium' hai — Helicobacter pylori. Protozoa diseases: Malaria,\nLeishmaniasis, Toxoplasmosis. [Q147]\n24. Airborne vs Waterborne Diseases\n●\n Trap: 'Cholera' hawa se NAHI failti — Tuberculosis, Pneumonia aur Common cold airborne diseases\n⚠️\n\nhain, Cholera contaminated food-water se failti hai. [Q148]"," ●\n Trap: 'Plague' water pollution se NAHI hoti — ye bacterium (Yersinia pestis) se, flea bites ke through\n⚠️\n\nfailti hai. Cholera, Diarrhoea aur Typhoid water pollution se related hain. [Q152]\n25. Filariasis (Elephantiasis) — Mosquito-Borne\n● 'Filariasis' (Elephantiasis) mosquito-borne disease hai — nematode parasites (Filarioidea family)\ninfected mosquito bite se failte hain. [Q149]\n● 'Elephantiasis' se legs mein excess swelling hoti hai — Lymphatic filariasis, nematode parasites se,\nmosquito bites se failti hai. [Q156]\n● 'Filarial worms' (Wuchereria) elephantiasis cause karte hain — lymphatic vessels mein chronic\ninflammation hoti hai. [Q170]\n26. Eye Donation — Who Can Donate\n● 'Diabetes' patients eyes donate kar sakte hain — hypertension-asthma patients bhi. AIDS, Hepatitis\nB/C, rabies, tetanus, cholera, leukemia wale nahi kar sakte. Eyes 6-8 ghante ke andar donate honi\nchahiye. [Q150]\n27. Antibiotics — Stop Microorganism Growth\n● 'Antibiotics' medicines disease-causing microorganisms ki growth rokti hain — bacterial infections fight\nkarti hain (Amoxicillin, Ciprofloxacin jaisi). Antibodies immune system ke proteins hain, Analgesics pain\nrelieve karte hain. [Q151]\n28. Amoebiasis — Causes Dysentery\n● 'Amoebiasis' Dysentery cause karti hai — Entamoeba histolytica parasite se, large intestine mein\ninfection, kabhi-kabhi liver-lungs-brain tak spread ho sakti hai. [Q153]\n29. Foot-and-Mouth Disease — A Viral Illness\n● Cattle mein Foot-and-mouth diseases 'Virus' se hoti hain — highly contagious. Animal viral diseases:\nBird Flu, Rabies, Rinderpest. [Q155]\n● 'Ephepi epizootica' (disease of feet and mouth) 'Virus' se hoti hai. [Q165]\n30. Leukemia — Blood Cancer\n● 'Leukemia' blood cells (bone marrow samet) ko affect karti hai — DNA mutation se hoti hai. Polio virus\nse, Meningitis bacteria-virus-fungi se, Smallpox variola virus se hoti hai. [Q157]"," 31. Leukoderma — A Skin Disease\n● 'Leukoderma' skin ki disease hai — skin pigmentation (melanin) loss hoti hai, skin whitening hoti hai\n(hands, feet, face affect hote hain). [Q158]\n32. Typhoid — Incubation Period\n● Typhoid bacillus (Salmonella Typhi) ka incubation period '8 to 14 days' hota hai — Widal test se confirm\nhoti hai, vaccine available hai. [Q159]\n33. Fluoride — Tooth Decay Prevention\n● 'Fluoride' water mein add ki jaati hai tooth decay prevent karne ke liye — tooth enamel (hydroxyapatite)\nko protect karti hai bacteria-produced acid se. [Q161]\n34. Anaemia — Red Blood Corpuscles Deficiency\n● Anaemia 'Red Blood Corpuscles' (RBC) ki deficiency se hota hai — RBC bone marrow mein banti hai,\nhemoglobin oxygen carry karti hai. [Q162]\n35. Diabetes — Treated by Insulin\n● 'Diabetes' Insulin se treat hoti hai — pancreas enough insulin nahi banata ya body effectively use nahi\nkar paati. Types: Type 1, Type 2, Gestational. [Q163]\n36. Grover's Disease — A Skin Disorder\n● 'Grover's disease' ek ventilated illness hai — skin disorder, small raised pink itchy spots ka rash hota\nhai. [Q164]\n37. Skin Pigmentation Diseases — Vitiligo & Albinism\n● 'Sickle cell anemia (Vitiligo)' skin pigmentation development ko affect karti hai — skin ka ek part pigment\nlose kar deta hai. Albinism mein Melanin poori tarah/partially absent hoti hai. [Q166]\n38. Goitre — Iodine Deficiency"," ● 'Goitre' iodine deficiency se hoti hai — thyroid gland abnormal enlarge ho jaati hai. Iodine sources:\nSeafood, Seaweed, Iodised salt. [Q168]\n39. Haemophilia — A Blood Clotting Disorder\n● 'Haemophilia' un genes ki absence se hoti hai jo blood clotting factors produce karte hain — sex-linked\nrecessive hereditary disorder hai, minor cut se non-stop bleeding hoti hai. [Q172]\n40. Beriberi — Vitamin B1 Deficiency\n● Beriberi ka symptom 'weak muscles aur low energy' hai — body mein enough thiamine (Vitamin B1)\nnahi hoti, jisse walking difficulty, sensation loss, muscle paralysis hoti hai. [Q121]\n41. Dengue — Caused by Viruses\n● Dengue 'Viruses' se hoti hai — infected mosquitoes (mainly Aedes aegypti, kabhi Aedes albopictus) ke\nbite se humans mein transmit hoti hai. [Q125]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 4 Deficiency and Diseases Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0370","t":"05 Reproduction in Animals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.5 — REPRODUCTION IN ANIMALS — FULL MIND MAP\n🐾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Puberty & Adolescence — Changes & Definitions\n2. Sex Determination — Environmental vs Genetic\n3. Asexual Reproduction — Types & Examples\n4. Sex Determination in Humans — Chromosomes (XX/XY)\n5. Chromosome Numbers — General Counts\n6. Genes, DNA & Heredity — Basic Features\n7. Sexual Reproduction & Genetic Diversity\n8. Cell Division — Mitosis & Meiosis\n9. IVF (In Vitro Fertilization) & Test-Tube Babies\n10. The Male Reproductive System\n11. Types of Germ Cells — Gametes\n12. Fertilization & Zygote Formation\n13. Contraception Methods\n14. Reproductive Health — Myths & Facts\n15. Mendel & Heredity\n16. The Female Reproductive System & Menstrual Cycle\n17. Animal Life Cycles — Oviparous, Viviparous & Metamorphosis\n18. Pregnancy, Childbirth & the Placenta\n19. Other Facts — Mule Hybrid, Twins, Plant Reproduction & Breeding Seasons\n1. Puberty & Adolescence — Changes & Definitions\n● Puberty (12-16 boys, 10-14 girls) mein sexual maturation se juda change 'mammary glands ki growth'\nhai (girls mein) — hair growth, appearance consciousness, pimples generic changes hain. [Q173]\n●\n Trap: Sex education dene se teenagers ek-doosre ka mazaak NAHI banate — ye galat reasoning\n⚠️\nhai. Sex education STDs se awareness, sexual abuse se bachaav, aur myths dur karti hai. [Q176]\n●\n Trap: 'Obesity' pubertal development ka part NAHI hai — pimples, menstruation, voice change\n⚠️\npuberty ke normal changes hain. [Q184]\n● Adolescence 11 saal ki age se shuru hokar 18-19 saal tak chalti hai — rapid physical-cognitive-\npsychosocial growth ka time hota hai. [Q216]\n● Adolescent ko healthy reproductive system develop karne ke liye 'nutritionally well-balanced' diet\nchahiye — WHO ke mutabik reproductive health mein behavioural-emotional-physical-social wellbeing\nshaamil hai. [Q232]\n● Adolescence wo age hai jisme reproductive organs functional ho jaate hain, gonads gametes banana\nshuru karti hain. [Q283]\n● Jab reproductive tissues mature hoti hain aur body ki normal growth slow ho jaati hai, is state ko 'Youth'\n(Puberty) kehte hain. [Q287]\n● Boys mein puberty ke time appearance changes (beard growth, hoarse voice, reproductive organs\ndevelopment) 'Testosterone' hormone se aate hain. [Q301]\n● Females mein puberty ki shuruaat 'Menarche' (pehla menstrual period) se hoti hai. [Q321]\n2. Sex Determination — Environmental vs Genetic"," ● 'Snail' mein sex genetically determined NAHI hoti — Sparrow, Butterfly, Moth mein genes-chromosomes\nse sex determine hoti hai. [Q175]\n● Kuch reptiles mein fertilized eggs ka 'Temperature' unke gender determine karta hai — Temperature\nDependent Sex Determination (TSD). [Q183]\n● Kuch animals mein gender determination ka environmental factor 'Temperature' hai — lizard jaisa\nexample, jabki humans mein ye genetically hota hai. [Q185]\n● 'Reptiles' class mein temperature kuch species ka sex determine karti hai — crocodilians, kai turtles-\nlizards mein TSD dekhi jaati hai. [Q206]\n● Snail apni life mein sex change kar sakta hai (male se female) — isse dikhta hai ki sex genetically\nNAHI, environmental-stress conditions se bhi determine ho sakti hai. [Q214]\n● Reptiles mein offspring ka sex 'fertilized egg jis temperature par rakha jaata hai' usse determine hota hai\n— 30°C se zyada temperature par females, 25°C se kam par males bante hain. [Q219]\n● 'Protogyny' wo process hai jisme organism female ki tarah life shuru karke baad mein male mein\ntransform hota hai (jaise Banana, Fig, Plum flowers mein) — Protandry ismein ulta hota hai. [Q208]\n3. Asexual Reproduction — Types & Examples\n●\n Trap: 'Pollination' asexual reproduction ka example NAHI hai — ye flowering plants ki sexual\n⚠️\nreproduction process hai. Grafting, Binary Fission, Budding asexual reproduction ke examples hain.\n[Q174]\n● Amoeba mein do individuals mein divide hone ki process 'Binary Fission' kehlaati hai — Amoeba isi\ntarah reproduce karta hai. [Q239, Q259]\n● Hydra budding aur regeneration dono kar sakta hai — Phylum Coelenterata se belong karta hai.\nBudding mein bud se naya organism develop hota hai (Bacteria, Yeast, Corals mein bhi hoti hai). [Q253]\n● Hydra, starfish, planaria 'Regeneration' process se guzarte hain — kho gaye ya amputate hue body\nparts replace/restore karte hain. Fragmentation mein organism pieces mein toot jaata hai (Fungi,\nlichens). [Q272]\n● Fully matured tiny individuals jab parent body se detach hokar naye individual bante hain, ye 'Budding'\nhai — example: Jellyfish. Binary fission (Amoeba) mein cell 2 parts mein split hoti hai. [Q273]\n● Asexual reproduction 'Lower animals aur plants' mein hoti hai — Protozoans, Sponges, Planaria\nexamples hain. [Q266]\n● Plasmodium 'Multiple fission' dikhata hai — ek parent cell simultaneously kai daughter cells mein divide\nhota hai. [Q282, Q297]\n● Asexual reproduction mein naye organisms parent ke 'genetically identical' hote hain — sexual\nreproduction se ye alag hai (jisme gametes ke nuclei fuse hote hain). [Q306]\n4. Sex Determination in Humans — Chromosomes (XX/XY)"," ● Autosomes 22 pairs kehlaate hain (2n=18 wale organism mein 16 autosomes) — sex-determination se\nunrelated genes carry karte hain. Humans mein 22 autosome pairs aur 1 sex chromosome pair hota hai.\n[Q178]\n● Baby ka sex sperm mein present chromosome (X ya Y) se determine hota hai — har egg mein X\nchromosome hota hai, sperm X ya Y ho sakta hai. Isliye male hi human sex determination ke liye\nresponsible hota hai. [Q189, Q295, Q270]\n● Sex determination flow chart se conclude hota hai ki 'The female decides the sex of the offspring' galat\nhai — actually 'Male decides' (Y chromosome se boy, X chromosome se girl) — sabhi children apni maa\nse X chromosome inherit karte hain. [Q191, Q193]\n● Male gametes (sperm) mein half mein X chromosome hota hai (22+X), half mein Y chromosome\n(22+XY nahi, sirf 22+Y) — female gametes sirf X chromosome carry karte hain. [Q194]\n● Allosomes (sex chromosomes) sex determination ke liye responsible hote hain — Autosomes (22 pairs)\nsex determination se unrelated hote hain. [Q209]\n● Statement A ('sabhi children apni maa se X chromosome inherit karte hain'), C aur D sahi hain —\nstatement B galat hai kyunki X inherit karna dono (boys-girls) ke liye hota hai. [Q212]\n●\n Trap: 'Sabhi children apni maa se Y chromosome inherit karte hain' — ye statement INCORRECT\n⚠️\nhai — maa sirf X chromosome pass karti hai, Y chromosome sirf pita se milta hai. [Q217]\n●\n Trap: X-containing sperm aur Y-containing sperm mein size ya motility ka koi visible difference NAHI\n⚠️\n\nhota. [Q223]\n● Human women mein 'perfect pair' (XX) sex chromosomes milte hain — men mein mismatched pair (XY,\nek badi X aur ek chhoti Y) hota hai. [Q229]\n● X-chromosome wale sperms aur Y-chromosome wale sperms — dono mein 23 chromosomes hote hain\n(equal count, sirf sex chromosome type alag). [Q230]\n●\n Trap: 'Y-chromosome' sirf human males mein paya jaata hai — females sirf X chromosomes rakhti\n⚠️\nhain (XX). [Q264]\n● Human male 'X sperm' apni maa se receive karta hai — pita se X ya Y sperm banane ki capacity milti\nhai, maa se sirf X chromosome milta hai (jo har egg mein hota hai). [Q289, Q271, Q237]\n● Female mein XX set of sex chromosomes hote hain — male mein XY. [Q275, Q240]\n● Girl child ke chromosomes '44 autosomes + XX' hote hain — boy child ke '44 autosomes + XY'. [Q318]\n● Diploid organisms (separate sexes) mein ek specific pair of chromosomes sex determine karta hai —\ninhe 'Sex Chromosomes' kehte hain. [Q322]\n5. Chromosome Numbers — General Counts\n● Human germ cell (sperm ya egg) mein 23 chromosomes hote hain (46 ka half) — normal human cell\nmein 46 chromosomes. [Q220, Q277, Q284]\n● Normal human mein 22 pairs autosomes hote hain (44 total) — 23rd pair sex chromosome hoti hai.\n[Q235]\n● 'Homologous chromosomes' autosomes hote hain — same gene sequence-loci-length rakhte hain,\nmales-females mein same dikhte hain. [Q242]"," ● Human somatic cells mein 46 chromosomes hote hain (23 pairs) — sperm-egg ke alawa sab body cells\nmein. [Q268]\n● Rat mein 21 pairs (total 42) chromosomes hote hain — doosre animals: Human (46), Pea (14), Cat (38),\nDog (78). [Q249]\n6. Genes, DNA & Heredity — Basic Features\n● Reproduction ka basic event 'DNA replication' hai — daughter cells ko DNA ki identical copy milti hai,\nparents se offspring tak information transfer karti hai. [Q186, Q292]\n●\n Trap: Genes 'koi change nahi hote' — ye galat statement hai (genes segments of DNA hain, jo\n⚠️\nchange ho sakte hain — mutations). Genes proteins produce karke traits control karte hain, DNA ke\nsegments hain. [Q179]\n●\n Trap: Human female mein fertilization 'uterus mein' NAHI hoti — ye galat statement hai, actually\n⚠️\nfallopian tubes mein hoti hai. [Q187]\n● Progeny mein minor differences 'DNA copying mein errors' se aati hain — asexual reproduction mein\nbhi small inaccuracies se variations aati hain. [Q188]\n● Non-dividing cell mein DNA 'Chromatin content' ki tarah exist karta hai — divide hone se pehle\nchromatin condense hokar chromosome banata hai. [Q192]\n● Trait inheritance 'Paternal aur Maternal DNA' se govern hota hai — dono parents se DNA milti hai.\n[Q201]\n● Genes traits ko 'Hormones' ki activity ke through control karte hain — genes proteins-hormones produce\nkarte hain jo traits determine karte hain. [Q205]\n● Sexually reproducing individuals ke paas ek hi trait ke 2 copies (genes) hoti hain — ek dominant, ek\nrecessive express ho sakti hai. [Q238]\n● Genes ko DNA sequence mein mark karne ki process 'Annotation' kehlaati hai — genomic data ko\ncorrect genes-locations tak map karna. [Q245]\n● Reproduction 2 broad categories mein divide hoti hai — Sexual aur Asexual reproduction. [Q260]\n● Sexual reproduction mein parent apne 'half genes' contribute karta hai — dono parents equally genes\ndete hain zygote ko. [Q265, Q309]\n7. Sexual Reproduction & Genetic Diversity\n● Sexual reproduction sabse zyada diversity la sakti hai — gametes ka fusion 2 alag individuals ke genes\ncombine karta hai, genetic diversity badhati hai. Asexual reproduction mein offspring genetically\nidentical hote hain. [Q256, Q263, Q280, Q314]\n8. Cell Division — Mitosis & Meiosis\n● Diagram mein A-Mitosis (body cells banane ke liye) aur B-Meiosis (gametes banane ke liye reproductive\ncells mein) hota hai. [Q180]"," ● Chromosome number generation-to-generation maintain hone ke liye 'gamete formation ke dauran\nchromosomes halve hote hain' (Meiosis) — reduction division daughter cells ko half chromosomes deti\nhai. [Q198]\n●\n Trap: Meiosis se chromosomes 'double' NAHI hote — ye galat statement hai, actually halve hote\n⚠️\nhain. Meiosis 2 phases mein hoti hai, gonads mein gametes production ke liye. [Q317]\n● 'Cytokinin' cell division se concerned hai — cell division growth, tissue repair, gametes production ke\nliye crucial hai. (Auxin growth control, Gibberellin dormancy break karte hain.) [Q319]\n9. IVF (In Vitro Fertilization) & Test-Tube Babies\n● Blocked oviducts wali women ke liye 'IVF' (zygote outside kept, test tube mein development) solution hai\n— fertilization glass vessel mein egg-sperm combine karke hoti hai. [Q181]\n● IVF mein 'external fertilization of sperm and ovum' hoti hai — pre-embryos wapas uterus mein transfer\nhote hain. Patrick Steptoe aur Robert Edwards ne IVF devise ki. [Q195]\n● 'Test tube baby' mein fertilization test tube mein hoti hai, lekin development uterus mein hota hai —\nLouise Joy Brown duniya ki pehli test-tube baby thi. [Q246]\n10. The Male Reproductive System\n● Human males mein testes abdominal cavity ke bahar 'scrotum' mein hote hain — body temperature se\n2-3 degree kam temperature maintain karta hai sperm formation ke liye. [Q182, Q316]\n● Sperms ka path: Testis → Vas deferens → Urethra → Penis — Epididymis testicles se sperm move\nkarta hai. [Q190]\n●\n Trap: 'Fallopian tubes block karna' male sterilization method NAHI hai — 'Vas deferens block karna'\n⚠️\n(vasectomy) male sterilization ka surgical method hai. [Q200]\n● Sperm ka Head (Part A) zygote ka sex determine karta hai — nucleus with chromosomes contain karta\nhai. Middle piece mitochondria energy deti hai, Tail flagellum motility deta hai. [Q228]\n● Male reproductive cells 'testes' mein produce hote hain — spermatogenic cells seminiferous tubules\nmein hote hain. [Q252, Q298, Q308]\n●\n Trap: 'Ovary' male reproductive system ka part NAHI hai — Vas deferens, Testis, Scrotum male\n⚠️\nparts hain. [Q258, Q304]\n● Sperm aur urine dono ke liye common passage 'Urethra' hai — urinary bladder se penis tak extend hoti\nhai. [Q281]\n● Human males ke 2 testicles hote hain — sperm aur testosterone produce karte hain. [Q285]\n● Male reproductive system ka main genetic material 'Sperm' mein milta hai. [Q290]\n● Testicle se sperm upward le jaane wala duct 'Sperm duct' (Vas deferens) kehlaata hai. [Q291, Q296]\n● Sperms temporarily 'Epididymis' mein store hote hain — maturation ke liye. [Q302]\n11. Types of Germ Cells — Gametes"," ● Complex body wale sexually reproducing animals mein — Male germ cell 'small aur motile' hota hai\n(sperm), Female germ cell 'large with food store' hota hai (ovum). [Q199]\n● Reproductive cell 'Gamete' kehlaata hai — Lymphocytes, RBC, WBC reproductive cells NAHI hain.\n[Q241]\n● Food store rakhne wala germ cell 'Female gamete' (ovum) kehlaata hai — non-motile hota hai. Male\ngamete (sperm) motile hota hai. [Q257]\n● Motile germ cell 'Male gamete' (sperm) kehlaata hai — female egg tak fertilize karne jaata hai. [Q313]\n12. Fertilization & Zygote Formation\n● Single-celled fertilised egg 'Zygote' kehlaata hai — sperm-egg combine hone se banta hai. (Blastocyst\ndividing cells cluster hai, Embryo initial development stage hai.) [Q236]\n● Embryo lagataar grow karke organs develop karta hai aur 'foetus' banta hai — Placenta oxygen-\nnutrients deti hai, Zygote fertilized egg cell hai. [Q221]\n● Male aur female sex cells fuse hokar 'Zygote' banate hain. [Q248]\n● 2 alag bacterial cells sexual reproduction ke dauran combine hokar 'Zygote' banate hain. [Q254]\n● 'Fertilization' se Zygote ki formation hoti hai — male aur female gamete ka fusion. [Q261, Q276]\n● 'Syngamy' sperm aur egg ke fusion ko kehte hain — angiosperms mein double fertilization ka essential\nfeature hai. [Q310]\n13. Contraception Methods\n● Oral contraceptive pills 'ovulation aur fertilization' dono rokti hain. [Q177]\n● Permanent sterilization method 'Surgical methods' hain (tubal sterilization females mein, vasectomy\nmales mein) — condom, birth control pills, copper-T non-permanent hain. [Q196]\n●\n Trap: Contraceptive devices 'no side effects' rakhte — ye statement INCORRECT hai. Ye pregnancy\n⚠️\n\nprevent karte hain, population control karte hain, lekin side effects ho sakte hain. [Q204]\n● Condom pregnancy aur STDs (HIV samet) dono prevent karta hai — surgical method, copper-T, oral\npills sirf pregnancy prevent karte hain. [Q211]\n● Loop (IUD) contraceptive ki tarah 'fallopian tubes ka access block' karta hai — copper-coated IUD\nsperm-egg fertilization rokta hai. [Q227]\n● Contraceptive pills ka disadvantage hai — 'hormonal imbalance' produce kar sakte hain. [Q231]\n● 'Pills ka intake' hormonal balance change karta hai — Copper IUD copper release karta hai, Hormonal\nIUD progestin release karta hai. [Q233]\n● Copper-T uterus mein place karne ki method 'Contraception' kehlaati hai. [Q293]\n14. Reproductive Health — Myths & Facts"," ●\n Trap: 'Chips-canned snacks avoid karna chahiye adolescence mein' — ye MYTH NAHI, FACT hai.\n⚠️\n'Menstruating girl ko boys nahi dekhne chahiye' aur 'kitchen mein kaam nahi karna chahiye' — ye myths\nhain. [Q197]\n●\n Trap: 'Unborn child ka sex determine karna' Reproductive Health ka feature NAHI hai — STD\n⚠️\nprevention, family planning, reproductive process knowledge iske features hain. [Q210]\n●\n Trap: Menstrual flow ke time 'chips-packed snacks khaana' nutritional needs poori nahi karta — ye\n⚠️\nFALSE statement hai. Sanitary napkins use karna, cycle track karna, 4-5 ghante mein pads badalna\nsahi practices hain. [Q222]\n15. Mendel & Heredity\n● Gregor Mendel ne discover kiya ki sexually reproducing organisms mein 'ek pair of factors' unki\ncharacteristics define karti hai — pea plants par experiments se dominance-segregation-independent\nassortment ke laws diye. [Q203]\n16. The Female Reproductive System & Menstrual Cycle\n● Diagram mein A (Uterus) — implantation-embryo development, B (Fallopian Tube) — egg ki fertilisation.\n[Q207]\n● 'Oestrogen' ovarian hormone hai — female ovaries se secrete hoti hai (Progesterone bhi). Testosterone\nmale hormone hai. [Q213]\n● Menstruation ke dauran 'uterine lining shed' hoti hai — pregnancy na hone par uterus apni lining nikalta\nhai. Hormones control karte hain: LH, FSH, estrogen, progesterone. [Q215]\n● Menstruation ki cessation (khatam hona) 'Menopause' kehlaati hai — 45-50 saal ki age mein hoti hai.\nMenarche pehla period hota hai. [Q202]\n● Uterine wall fertilized egg receive karne ki taiyari karti hai — fertilization na hone par thickened lining\n'Menstruation' (period) mein shed hoti hai. [Q226]\n● 'Graafian follicles' mammal ki ovary mein milte hain — mature hokar ovum release karte hain. [Q247]\n● Fertilised egg (zygote) 'Uterus' mein implant hoti hai — Cervix-Vagina alag structures hain. [Q250, Q255,\nQ299, Q311]\n● Vagina 'Cervix' tak jaati hai — cervix uterus ko vagina se connect karta hai. [Q274]\n● Female germ-cells (eggs) 'Ovaries' mein bante hain — steroid hormones (estrogen-progesterone) bhi\nproduce karti hain. [Q286]\n● Humans mein fertilization 'Fallopian tube' mein hoti hai — ovaries ko uterus se connect karti hai. [Q288]\n● Egg ovary se uterus tak 'Fallopian tube' (oviduct) le jaati hai. [Q294, Q312]\n●\n Trap: 'Vas deferens' female reproductive system ka part NAHI hai — Uterus, Ovary, Fallopian tube\n⚠️\nfemale parts hain. [Q303]\n● Endometrium (uterus ki lining) fertilized egg ko nourish karti hai — embryo 'Uterus' mein develop hota\nhai. [Q315]"," ● Ovum production ki process 'Oogenesis' kehlaati hai — ovaries mein hoti hai, meiosis I-II ke through\nprimary oocyte se ovum banta hai. [Q320]\n17. Animal Life Cycles — Oviparous, Viviparous & Metamorphosis\n● Butterfly life cycle ka teesra stage (larva ke baad) 'Pupa' hai — Egg → Larva → Pupa → Butterfly.\n[Q234]\n● Ande dene wale animals 'Oviparous' kehlaate hain — birds, reptiles, amphibians, fish, arthropods is\ncategory mein. [Q278]\n● Bachche ko janam dene wale animals 'Viviparous' kehlaate hain — humans, cows, dogs viviparous\nhain. [Q279]\n● Kangaroo underdeveloped children ko janam deta hai — Marsupials group (Wallabies, Koalas bhi) mein\npouch mein baby develop hoti hai. [Q300]\n18. Pregnancy, Childbirth & the Placenta\n● Woman ko birth dene ke liye 'well-equipped hospital mein' delivery best option hai — pregnancy 40\nweeks (3 trimesters) ki hoti hai. [Q224]\n● 'Maternal Health' mein prenatal, natal aur postnatal period ki care shaamil hai — Maternal Mortality\nRatio (MMR) ise measure karta hai. [Q225]\n● Placenta embryo se 'waste matter remove karti hai aur nutrition provide karti hai' — dono kaam ek saath\nkarti hai. [Q251]\n● Fetus mother ke blood se nutrition 'umbilical cord' ke through leta hai — 2 arteries aur 1 vein Wharton's\njelly se surrounded hote hain. [Q262]\n● Labour pain 'uterus' ki walls mein contractions se hota hai — largest smooth muscle uterus mein hoti\nhai. [Q267]\n● Baby rhythmic muscle contractions se 'uterus' mein janam leta hai — cervix dilate hokar baby ko birth\ncanal se pass karti hai. [Q269]\n19. Other Facts — Mule Hybrid, Twins, Plant Reproduction & Breeding\nSeasons\n● 'Mule' ek hybrid hai jo 'male donkey aur female horse' ke crossing se banta hai — female donkey+male\nhorse se 'Hinny' banta hai. [Q243]\n● Fraternal twins 'fertilisation stage' par possible hote hain — 2 alag eggs 2 alag sperms se fertilize hoti\nhain (dizygotic). Identical twins ek hi zygote ke split hone se bante hain. [Q244]\n● Beej se seedling develop karne wala part 'Embryo' hai — is process ko Germination kehte hain.\nEndosperm embryo ko nourish karta hai. [Q218]\n● Growing embryo ke liye nutritive tissue 'Endosperm' hai — angiosperms ke seeds mein embryo ko\nsurround karta hai, starch-protein se nourish karta hai. [Q307]"," ● Monochronic animals saal mein sirf 'ek baar reproduction' karte hain — specific breeding season hoti\nhai (mammals, birds, kuch reptiles mein). [Q305]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 5 Reproduction in Animals Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0371","t":"06 Reproduction in Plant","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.6 — REPRODUCTION IN PLANTS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌱\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Plant Gaseous Exchange & Basic Physiology\n2. Asexual Reproduction in Plants & Organisms\n3. Vegetative Propagation - Natural & Artificial\n4. Seed Structure, Germination & Development\n5. Flower Structure - Male & Female Parts\n6. Pollination - Types & Agents\n7. Fertilization, Post-Fertilization Changes & Fruit Development\n8. Mendel's Experiments - Laws & Ratios\n9. Plant Classification - Angiosperms, Gymnosperms, Cryptogams\n10. Tissue Culture & Modern Techniques\n11. Plant Tissues & Meristem\n12. Monocots vs Dicots\n13. Bisexual vs Unisexual Flowers\n14. Spore Formation & Fungi\n1. Plant Gaseous Exchange & Basic Physiology\n● Stomata CO uptake aur oxygen release mein madad karta hai photosynthesis ke dauran - guard cells\n₂\nstomata ke open-close ke liye responsible hain. [Q323]\n2. Asexual Reproduction in Plants & Organisms\n● Spores asexual reproductive bodies hain jo sporangia mein bante hain - Ferns, Moss, Fungi spore\nformation se reproduce karte hain. Amoeba binary fission, Yeast budding se reproduce karta hai. [Q324]\n● Leishmania → Binary fission, Yeast → Budding, Plasmodium → Multiple fission, Hydra →\nRegeneration/Budding - ye matching yaad rakho. [Q328]\n● Rhizopus (bread mould fungus) spore formation se reproduce karta hai - Phylum Zygomycota,\nsaprophytic/parasitic fungus, moist organic substances par paya jata hai. Sporangium reproductive\norgan hai, sporangiophore vegetative organ hai. [Q337, Q338, Q392, Q384]\n● Fission do types ke hote hain: Binary fission (2 mein divide, e.g., Amoeba) aur Multiple fission (kai\ndaughter cells, e.g., Plasmodium). [Q382]\n● Planaria true regeneration dikhata hai - ek piece se poora organism grow ho sakta hai. Spirogyra\nfragmentation se reproduce karta hai. [Q385]\n3. Vegetative Propagation - Natural & Artificial\n● Vegetative propagation asexual method hai jisme plants genetically IDENTICAL hote hain parents ke -\nadvantages: faster cultivation, seedless plants grow kar sakte hain; disadvantages: short-lived, diseases\nke liye susceptible, no new varieties. [Q329]\n●\n Trap: Vegetative propagation se produced plants genetically 'different' hain - ye galat statement hai,\n⚠️\nactually identical hote hain. [Q329]"," ● Sweet potato, Banana, Ginger, Turmeric roots se new plants produce karte hain - Rose stem cutting se,\nBryophyllum leaf margins se plantlets grow karta hai. Underground stem modifications: rhizomes,\ntubers, corms, bulbs. [Q325]\n● Mango typically sexually reproduce karta hai seed se ya grafting se - natural vegetative propagation\nnahi karta. Papaya bhi seeds se grow hota hai, vegetative propagation nahi hota. [Q339, Q374]\n● Banana suckers se propagate hota hai - banana ka underground stem rhizome kehlata hai, sucker\nlateral shoot hota hai base se. [Q370]\n● Sugarcane (stem cuttings), Potato (stem tubers with 'eyes'), Banana (rhizome suckers) vegetatively\npropagate hote hain - Papaya aur Coriander seeds se grow hote hain. [Q410]\n● Jasmine generally vegetatively reproduce karta hai (cuttings, suckers, grafting) - iske flowers mein fertile\npollen/ovules ki kami hoti hai, seed produce karne ki capacity lost kar chuka hai. [Q395]\n● Natural vegetative propagation Mustard mein NAHI hoti - Mustard sexually seeds se reproduce karta\nhai. Sweet potato/dahlia root tubers se, ginger/potato rhizomes se propagate hote hain. [Q377]\n● Plant body ka koi part new individual mein develop ho jaaye usse 'Vegetative propagation' kehte hain -\nye asexual method hai. Sexual propagation seeds se multiplication hota hai. [Q372]\n4. Seed Structure, Germination & Development\n● Dicot seed mein: Plumule → future shoot, Cotyledons → food store, Radicle → future root. Monocot\nseeds mein single embryonic leaf hoti hai, dicot mein do cotyledons hoti hain jo food store karte hain.\nExamples: Dicot - Peas, Almonds, Cashews. [Q327]\n● Radicle germination ke dauran root system mein develop hota hai - Plumule shoot (stem, leaves) mein,\nCotyledon seedling ke liye food reserve hota hai, Epicotyl cotyledons ke upar plumule ke neeche ka\nhissa hota hai. [Q366]\n● Litchi single-seeded fruit hai - Apple, Pomegranate, Papaya multi-seeded hain. Seeds mein embryo,\nendosperm, seed coat hote hain. Monocot seeds: Paddy, Wheat; Dicot seeds: Chickpea, Litchi, Mango,\nCoffee. [Q368]\n● Seed mein future plant embryo ki form mein hota hai - fertilization ke baad embryo seed ke andar\ndevelop hota hai. [Q373]\n5. Flower Structure - Male & Female Parts\n● Stamens (androecium) male reproductive parts hain - Filament (stalk) + Anther (pollen produce karta\nhai). Carpel/Pistil (gynoecium) female part hai - Stigma (sticky top, pollen trap), Style (tube), Ovary\n(ovules contain karti hai). [Q326, Q336, Q369, Q375, Q397, Q399, Q401, Q413, Q407]\n●\n Trap: Style male reproductive part NAHI hai - ye female organ Pistil ka part hai. Male parts sirf\n⚠️\nAnther aur Filament hain jo Stamen banate hain. [Q341]\n●\n Trap: Carpel (Pistil) anther ka part NAHI hai - ye female reproductive part hai. Saffron Crocus\n⚠️\nsativus ke stigma se derive hota hai. [Q387]\n● Flower ke 4 main whorls: Calyx (sepals, outermost green), Corolla (petals), Androecium (stamens),\nGynoecium/Carpels (centre mein). Carpel female reproductive organ hai. [Q401, Q413]"," ● Essential reproductive organs: Stamens aur Carpels - Sepals aur Petals accessory/non-essential hain jo\nprotection aur pollinators attract karne mein help karte hain, gametes directly produce nahi karte. [Q404,\nQ407]\n6. Pollination - Types & Agents\n● Pollination pollen grains ka anther se stigma tak transfer hai - Self-pollination same flower mein, Cross-\npollination different flowers mein hota hai. Agents: birds, bees, water, wind, butterflies. [Q390]\n● Entomophily (insect pollination) mein flowers colorful, fragrant, nectar-rich hote hain - Bees aur\nbutterflies most common biotic agents hain. [Q365]\n● Wind-pollinated flowers ka pollen light aur spongy (non-sticky) hota hai taaki air currents se easily travel\nkar sake - in flowers mein large feathery stigmas hote hain drifting pollen pakadne ke liye. [Q400]\n●\n Trap: Plants pollination agents NAHI hain - agents air, water, insects, animals, birds hain; plants\n⚠️\nkhud subject hain, agent nahi. [Q402]\n● Pollen grains anthers ke andar meiosis se produce hote hain - Locule anther ki internal cavity hai jahan\npollen develop hota hai. [Q391, Q412]\n7. Fertilization, Post-Fertilization Changes & Fruit Development\n● Nishchecan ke baad: Zygote → Embryo, Ovules → Seed, Ovary → Fruit. [Q332, Q344, Q405]\n●\n Trap: Flowering plants spore formation se reproduce NAHI karte - ye fungi mein hota hai. Flowering\n⚠️\nplants sexually (fertilization, pollination) ya asexually (vegetative propagation, budding, tissue culture)\nreproduce karte hain. [Q355]\n● Double fertilization sirf Angiosperms mein hota hai - ek sperm egg se fuse karke embryo banata hai,\ndoosra polar nuclei se fuse karke endosperm banata hai. [Q371]\n● Pollen grain stigma par land karke pollen tube grow karta hai male gametes ko ovule tak transfer karne\nke liye - Fertilization types: Porogamy (micropyle se), Chalazogamy (chalaza se), Mesogamy\n(integuments se). [Q350]\n● Fertilization ke baad petals, stamens, stigma, style usually dry up aur fall off kar jaate hain - Ovary fruit\nmein develop hota hai. Sepal defensive part hai jo kuch plants mein persist karta hai (jaise tomato).\n[Q353]\n● Parthenocarpy mein fertilization ke bina fruit develop hota hai (seedless) - examples: Pineapple,\nBanana, Grape, certain oranges. [Q408]\n● Pollen tube ka development Spermatophytes (seed-producing plants) mein land adaptation ka important\nstage hai - ye male gametes ko directly ovule tak le jaata hai bina external water ke. [Q398]\n8. Mendel's Experiments - Laws & Ratios\n● Gregor Johann Mendel (Father of Genetics) ne Pisum sativum (garden pea) par 1856-1863 tak\nexperiments kiye - 14 true-breeding varieties select ki. Success ka main reason: ek time mein ek hi\ncharacter ka study karna. [Q358, Q361]"," ● Mendel ne pehle cross-fertilization kiya (opposite traits wale plants ke beech), phir F1 progeny ko self-\nfertilize kiya F2 generation ke liye. [Q331]\n● Mendel ne F2 generation F1 hybrids ko self-pollination karke obtain ki. [Q379]\n● Mendel ke 7 contrasting traits: Flower colour (Purple/White), Seed shape (Round/Wrinkled), Seed\ncolour (Green/Yellow), Pod shape (Constricted/Inflated), Pod colour (Green/Yellow), Plant size\n(Tall/Dwarf), Flower position (Axial/Terminal). [Q346, Q342]\n●\n Trap: Mendel ne leaf shape ka use NAHI kiya - unhone 7 traits use kiye: flower colour, position,\n⚠️\nstem length, seed shape, seed colour, pod shape, pod colour. [Q342]\n● Dominant traits pea plants mein: Round seeds, Tall height, Purple flowers, Axial position. Recessive\ntraits: Wrinkled seeds, Small (dwarf) height, White flowers, Terminal position. [Q330]\n● F2 dihybrid cross ka phenotypic ratio 9:3:3:1 hota hai - 9 round-yellow : 3 round-green : 3 wrinkled-\nyellow : 1 wrinkled-green. [Q333, Q360]\n● Standard monohybrid cross F2 generation ka genotypic ratio 1:2:1 hota hai (1 TT : 2 Tt : 1 tt),\nphenotypic ratio 3:1 hota hai (3 tall : 1 dwarf). [Q334, Q349]\n● TT × tt cross mein F1 generation all tall hoti hai kyunki tallness dominant hai - chahe pollen tall plant se\nho ya short se, result same aata hai. [Q335, Q357, Q359]\n●\n Trap: F2 generation mein 'all plants tall' ye statement INCORRECT hai - F2 mein 3:1 ratio mein tall\n⚠️\naur dwarf dono hote hain. [Q356]\n● 3:1 ratio mein sirf ek trait dominant hota hai, doosra recessive - dono dominant nahi hote (red dominant,\ngreen recessive). [Q340]\n● Agar Mendel F2 generation study NAHI karte toh unhe pata nahi chalta ki recessive traits lost nahi hote,\nbas suppressed hote hain aur baad mein reappear karte hain. [Q363]\n● RRyy (round, green) × rrYY (wrinkled, yellow) → F1 RrYy (round, yellow) hota hai kyunki R aur Y dono\ndominant hain. [Q347]\n● TtWw genotype 4 types ke gametes produce karta hai: TW, Tw, tW, tw - independent assortment se har\ntype 25% hota hai. [Q345]\n● 500 peas F1 self-pollination se collect karne par green peas ≈125 honge (25% of 500 based on 3:1\nratio). [Q354]\n● Tallness ko dominant isliye kaha gaya kyunki plant tall dikhta hai chahe ek (Tt) ya do (TT) alleles ho -\nphenotype mein sirf dominant trait expressed hoti hai. [Q348]\n● Tall wrinkled (TTrr) × Short round (ttRR) cross se F1 generation TtRr hogi jo Tall round dikhegi -\nTallness aur Roundness dono dominant traits hain. [Q362]\n● Mendel ke experiments se pata chalta hai ki germ cells har pair se ek chromosome leti hain - Law of\nSegregation ke through DNA stability maintain hoti hai. [Q351]\n●\n Trap: 'Two alleles gamete formation ke time together laaye jaate hain' - ye FALSE statement hai.\n⚠️\nLaw of Segregation ke anusaar alleles gamete formation ke dauran SEPARATE hote hain. [Q352]\n● Monohybrid cross mein sirf ek pair of contrasting characters involved hoti hai, dihybrid cross mein do\npairs involved hoti hain. [Q388, Q389]\n● F1 generation mein dominant trait clearly dikhai deti hai (effective/intensity) - contrasting traits F1 ya F2\nmein kabhi blend nahi hote. [Q380, Q381, Q386]"," 9. Plant Classification - Angiosperms, Gymnosperms, Cryptogams\n● Angiosperms (flowering plants) mein seeds ovary ke andar develop hote hain jo pakkar fruit banta hai -\nreproductive organs flower mein hote hain. [Q367, Q378, Q393, Q394]\n● Gymnosperms mein naked, exposed seeds hote hain (Cycads, Ginkgo, Pinus) - ye cones ya modified\nleaves par hote hain, fruit mein enclosed nahi hote. [Q414]\n● Thallophyta primitive plants hain (Spirogyra, Ulva), Pteridophyta flowerless hain (Fern, Selaginella).\n[Q367]\n● Marsilea Cryptogams se belong karta hai - iske reproductive organs hidden hote hain (spores se\nreproduce, no flowers/seeds). [Q364]\n10. Tissue Culture & Modern Techniques\n● Tissue culture (micropropagation) mein isolated cells/tissues ko artificial nutrient medium par grow kiya\njata hai - isse ek parent se kai disease-free plants grow kar sakte hain. Gottlieb Haberlandt ne discover\nkiya. [Q383, Q411]\n11. Plant Tissues & Meristem\n● Meristematic tissue cell division capable hai - small cells indefinitely divide kar sakti hain, growing\nregions (root/stem apex) mein payi jaati hai. Sclerenchyma dead structural support cells, Parenchyma\nsoft parts, Xylem complex permanent tissue. [Q406]\n12. Monocots vs Dicots\n● Dicots mein 2 cotyledons, tap root system, branched stems, reticulate venation hoti hai - Fibrous roots\naur parallel venation monocots ki characteristics hain, isliye 'dicots have fibrous roots' galat statement\nhai. [Q403]\n13. Bisexual vs Unisexual Flowers\n● Unisexual flowers mein sirf male ya female parts hote hain - Examples: Papaya, Watermelon, Pumpkin,\nPine, Coconut, Cucumber, Maize, Birch. [Q343, Q376]\n● Bisexual (hermaphrodite) flowers mein stamen aur pistil dono hote hain - Examples: Mustard, Rose,\nLily, Tulip, Hibiscus, Sunflower, Tomato, Gulmohar. [Q343, Q396, Q409]\n14. Spore Formation & Fungi\n● Rhizopus, mushrooms, Aspergillus spores se reproduce karte hain - spores reproductive cells hain jo\nfusion ke bina new organism develop kar sakti hain. [Q384]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 6 Reproduction in Plants Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0372","t":"07 Cell Basic Unit of Life","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.7 — CELL: BASIC UNIT OF LIFE — FULL MIND MAP\n🔬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Cell Discovery & Cell Theory\n2. Prokaryotic vs Eukaryotic Cells\n3. Nucleus - Structure & Function\n4. Mitochondria - Powerhouse\n5. Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER)\n6. Golgi Apparatus\n7. Lysosomes - Suicide Bags\n8. Ribosomes - Protein Factories\n9. Plastids\n10. Vacuoles\n11. Cell Membrane / Plasma Membrane\n12. Cell Wall - Composition\n13. Cytoplasm & Cytosol\n14. Plant vs Animal Cell Differences\n15. Plant Tissues - Meristematic & Permanent\n16. Animal Tissues\n17. Cell Division - Mitosis\n18. Cellular Respiration & Energy (ATP)\n19. DNA, Genes, Chromosomes\n20. Protein Synthesis\n21. Specialized Cells\n22. Unicellular Organisms\n23. Osmosis, Diffusion, Plasmolysis\n24. Other Cell Facts\n1. Cell Discovery & Cell Theory\n● Cell ki khoj Robert Hooke ne 1665 mein ki thi - cork ke dead cells dekhe the microscope se. [Q418, Q456,\nQ463]\n● Cell theory: Sabhi living things cells se bani hain. Viruses par ye applicable NAHI hai kyunki ye cells se\nnahi bane hote - Beijerinck ne 1898 mein viruses discover kiye. [Q418]\n● Nucleus ki khoj Robert Brown ne 1831 mein ki thi. [Q460]\n● Sabse chhoti unit of life jo independent exist kar sakti hai wo Cell hai - longest cell nerve cell, human\nmein largest cell female ovum hai. [Q456]\n● Cytology (cell biology) Greek word 'kytos' (hollow container) se aaya hai. [Q463]\n2. Prokaryotic vs Eukaryotic Cells\n● Prokaryotic cells mein membrane-bound organelles NAHI hote hain - nuclear region ko nucleoid kehte\nhain, single chromosome hota hai, bahut chhote hote hain. Examples: Archaea, Bacteria,\nCyanobacteria. Binary fission se reproduce karte hain. [Q431]\n● Eukaryotic cells mein definite nucleus aur membrane-bound organelles hote hain - multicellular hote\nhain. [Q431]"," ● Prokaryotic ribosome: 70S (50S + 30S subunits). Eukaryotic ribosome: 80S (60S + 40S subunits).\n[Q429]\n● Photosynthetic bacteria mein pigments plasma membrane ke infoldings mein hote hain - chloroplast\nNAHI hote. Plants mein Chlorophyll a, b aur Carotenoids chloroplast ke intrinsic part mein hote hain.\n[Q453]\n3. Nucleus - Structure & Function\n● Nucleus sabse bada organelle hai - cell ka 'command centre' aur 'master' hai, DNA store karta hai,\ndouble membrane bound hai. Nucleolus (kendrika) bhi isi mein hota hai. [Q469, Q507]\n● Nucleus ke alawa Mitochondria aur Plastids mein bhi apna DNA aur ribosomes hote hain - ye semi-\nautonomous hain. [Q436]\n● Nucleus 1831 mein Robert Brown ne discover kiya tha. [Q460]\n4. Mitochondria - Powerhouse\n● Mitochondria ko 'weird' isliye kaha jata hai kyunki inme apna DNA aur ribosomes hote hain - semi-\nautonomous organelle hai. [Q420]\n● Mitochondria cellular respiration karta hai - pyruvate breakdown O ke saath yahan hota hai, CO +\n₂\n₂\nwater + energy (ATP) banata hai. [Q438, Q450, Q478, Q483]\n● Mitochondria double membrane bound, oval shaped hota hai. [Q455]\n● Pyruvate (3-carbon) Krebs cycle mein 3 molecules CO banata hai.\n₂\n[Q438]\n5. Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER)\n● SER (Smooth ER) - ribosomes nahi hote, lipids/steroid hormones/carbohydrates synthesize karta hai,\nliver cells mein drugs aur poisons ka detoxification karta hai. [Q415]\n● RER (Rough ER) - ribosomes attached hote hain, proteins ka synthesis, folding, quality control aur\ndespatch karta hai. [Q415, Q475]\n● Smooth ER cell ke liye substances synthesize karta hai. [Q442]\n6. Golgi Apparatus\n● Golgi apparatus flattened stacked pouches (cisternae) se bana hai - proteins aur lipids ko transport,\nmodify aur package karke vesicles mein bhejta hai. [Q468]\n● Plant cells mein Golgi body ko dictyosomes kehte hain. [Q486]\n7. Lysosomes - Suicide Bags"," ● Lysosomes ko 'suicide bags' isliye kaha jata hai kyunki ye biomolecules break down karte hain, waste\nremove karte hain, dead/damaged cells digest karte hain - sphere-shaped, eukaryotic animal cells mein\npaye jate hain. [Q437, Q455]\n8. Ribosomes - Protein Factories\n● Ribosomes ko cell ka 'protein factory' kaha jata hai - amino acids ko jodkar proteins synthesize karte\nhain (translation), RNA aur protein se bane hote hain, prokaryotic aur eukaryotic dono mein hote hain.\n[Q432, Q475]\n● George Palade ne 1955 mein ribosomes discover kiye. [Q420]\n9. Plastids\n● Leucoplast - colorless/non-pigmented, roots mein paya jata hai, starch/lipids/proteins store karta hai. 3\ntypes: Amyloplasts, Proteinoplasts, Elaioplasts. [Q424]\n● Chloroplast - photosynthesis karta hai, green pigment chlorophyll contain karta hai. [Q448]\n● Chromoplast - pigments contain karta hai. [Q424]\n10. Vacuoles\n● Plant cells mein vacuoles animal cells se badi hoti hain - ek single vacuole cell ke most interior space le\nsakti hai taaki water balance maintain ho. Animal cells mein vacuoles chhoti hoti hain aur waste\nsequester karti hain. [Q421, Q465]\n● Vacuoles single membrane bound hote hain, tonoplast membrane hoti hai - water, sap, excretory\nproducts store karte hain. [Q421, Q442]\n● Contractile vacuole Amoeba mein water regulate karta hai - osmotic pressure control karke water bahar\npump karta hai. [Q425]\n● Meristematic cells mein vacuoles ka absence hota hai - ye continuously divide karte hain. [Q454]\n11. Cell Membrane / Plasma Membrane\n● Plasma membrane proteins + lipids (phospholipids + cholesterol) + carbohydrates se bani hai -\nselectively permeable hai, dono plant aur animal cells mein hoti hai. [Q419, Q462]\n● Selectively permeable membrane sirf certain molecules (specific solutes/solvents) ko allow karti hai -\nsabhi molecules freely diffuse nahi karte. [Q419]\n● Gaseous exchange cell membrane ke across diffusion se hota hai - high concentration se low\nconcentration ki taraf molecules ki movement. [Q444]"," 12. Cell Wall - Composition\n● Plant cell wall: Cellulose + Pectin + Hemicellulose - polysaccharides se bani, water loss prevent karti\nhai, tensile strength deti hai. [Q445, Q467, Q486]\n● Fungal cell wall: Chitin (glucans + glycoproteins + chitin) - ye components humans mein nahi hote isliye\nantifungal therapy ka excellent target hai. [Q487, Q500]\n● Cork cells mein Suberin hota hai jo water/gas entry rokta hai - cork cells dead aur compactly arranged\nhote hain bina intercellular spaces ke. [Q477]\n● Desert plants ki outer skin Cutin (waxy water-repellent substance) se covered hoti hai jo transpiration se\nwater loss rokti hai. [Q479]\n● Tough tissue Sclerenchyma dead (non-living) cells se bana hota hai jisme lignin-thickened walls hote\nhain. [Q488]\n● Cell wall plant cells ko incoming water ke pressure ke against bursting se bachati hai. [Q443]\n13. Cytoplasm & Cytosol\n● Cytoplasm jelly-like fluid hai jo nucleus aur cell membrane ke beech hota hai - isme saare organelles\nsuspended hote hain. [Q460]\n● Cytosol cytoplasm ka aqueous component hai. [Q467]\n● Cytoplasm metabolic processes host karta hai. [Q435]\n14. Plant vs Animal Cell Differences\n● Plant cells generally animal cells se badi hoti hain. Plant cells mein cell wall, chloroplast, large vacuoles\nhote hain - animal cells mein ye nahi hote. [Q430, Q465]\n● Animal cells mein plastids NAHI hote. Plant cells mein centriole absent hota hai. [Q430, Q486]\n● Dono mein common: cell membrane, mitochondria, ER, nucleus. [Q430]\n● Human cheek cells (animal) vs Onion peel (plant) - main difference: plant cells mein cell wall hoti hai.\n[Q430]\n● Root cells mein cell wall, cytoplasm, nucleus, vacuole dikhai dete hain - lekin chloroplast nahi kyunki\nroot underground hai. [Q445]\n● Leaves aur shoots mein large vacuole aur chloroplasts dikhai dete hain. [Q448]\n15. Plant Tissues - Meristematic & Permanent\n● Meristematic tissue: continuously dividing cells, growing regions (root tips, stem tips) mein payi jati hai.\nTerm 'Meristem' Carl Wilhelm von Nägeli ne coin kiya. Types: Apical (length), Intercalary (elongation),\nLateral (girth/thickness). [Q417, Q454, Q496]\n● Meristematic cells mein vacuoles nahi hoti hain, thin cell walls aur dense cytoplasm hota hai. [Q454]"," ● Differentiation: meristematic cells se permanent tissue cells acquire karne ka process - permanent\nshape, size aur function. [Q498]\n● Permanent tissues 3 types: Parenchyma (thin wall, food storage, living), Collenchyma (living, elongated,\ncorners par thickened - cellulose+pectin, flexibility), Sclerenchyma (dead, lignin-thickened, hard/stiff).\n[Q499, Q503, Q506]\n● Chlorenchyma: Parenchyma with chlorophyll (leaves mein, photosynthesis). Aerenchyma: Parenchyma\nwith large air spaces (aquatic plants mein, buoyancy/floatation). [Q439, Q422]\n● Aerenchyma Hyacinth (jal kumbhi) mein paya jata hai. [Q422]\n● Plant tissue types: Dermal (outermost, protection), Vascular (xylem+phloem, transport), Ground (bulk,\nmetabolic). [Q474]\n● Collenchyma: living, elongated, irregularly thickened at corners - flexibility provide karta hai young plants\nmein. [Q499]\n16. Animal Tissues\n● 4 main animal tissues: Connective, Epithelial, Muscle, Nervous. Meristematic tissue sirf plants mein\nhota hai. [Q464]\n● Epithelial tissue: body surfaces cover karta hai. Types: Simple (one layer), Stratified (more than one\nlayer), Pseudostratified. [Q428, Q471]\n● Simple epithelium exactly one cell thick hota hai. [Q471]\n● Squamous epithelium: flat cells, capillaries/alveoli/glomeruli mein, rapid diffusion. [Q449, Q441]\n● Cuboidal epithelium: equal width/height/depth, kidney ducts/pancreas/mammary glands mein. [Q449]\n● Columnar epithelium: pharynx mein, goblet cells contain karta hai. [Q441]\n● Ciliated columnar epithelium: trachea, bronchi, oviducts ko line karta hai. [Q441]\n● Connective tissue: support/connect/separate karta hai. Examples: Blood, bone, cartilage, tendon,\nligament, adipose tissue. [Q470, Q493, Q505]\n● Blood connective tissue hai - bone marrow mein RBC, WBC, platelets bante hain. [Q470, Q472]\n● Adipose tissue: fat store karta hai skin ke neeche aur internal organs ke beech, insulator ki tarah kaam\nkarta hai. [Q440]\n● Muscle tissue: 3 types - Cardiac, Skeletal, Smooth. Smooth muscle blood vessel ka diameter change\nkarta hai. [Q508]\n● Nervous tissue: brain, spinal cord, nerves mein - body activities coordinate karta hai. [Q440]\n● Neuron (nerve cell): cell body (soma/cyton/perikaryon), dendrites (signals receive), axon (impulses\ntransmit). Synapse: neuron ke beech connection. [Q447, Q489, Q491]\n● Cyton mein Nissl's granules aur mitochondria hote hain. [Q489]\n● Bone cells: Osteoblasts, Osteoclasts, Osteocytes, Osteoprogenitor cells. [Q447]\n17. Cell Division - Mitosis"," ● Mitosis stages: Prophase (chromosomes condense, spindle forms), Metaphase (chromosomes\nequatorial plate par line up, spindle fibres attach), Anaphase (sister chromatids separate), Telophase\n(chromosomes uncoil, nuclear envelope reforms, cell divides). [Q458, Q502]\n● Centromere: sister chromatids ko cell division ke dauran jodta hai. [Q501]\n● Centrosome: sirf animal cells mein, 2 centrioles se bana, cell cycle regulate karta hai. [Q501]\n● Nucleosome: eukaryotic chromosome ki structural unit - DNA histones ke around coiled hota hai. [Q501]\n18. Cellular Respiration & Energy (ATP)\n● ATP (Adenosine triphosphate) cell ki 'energy currency' hai - adenine + ribose sugar + 3 phosphate\ngroups. [Q426, Q457, Q461, Q490]\n● ATP mitochondria (powerhouse) mein synthesize hota hai - molecular transportation across cell\nmembranes ke liye use hota hai. [Q490]\n● Glycolysis: glucose → 2 pyruvate + ATP, cytoplasm mein hota hai. [Q423, Q435, Q446]\n● Pyruvate breakdown using O : mitochondria mein hota hai → CO + water + energy (Krebs cycle +\n₂\n₂\nelectron transport chain). [Q450, Q478, Q483]\n● Anaerobic respiration: cytoplasm mein hota hai (yeast/bacteria), incomplete oxidation se kam energy.\n[Q452]\n● Aerobic respiration: mitochondria mein hota hai, complete oxidation se zyada energy. [Q452]\n19. DNA, Genes, Chromosomes\n● DNA 2 long polynucleotide strands ki double helix hoti hai - James Watson aur Francis Crick ko credit.\n[Q509]\n● DNA genetic instructions carry karta hai proteins ki structure/function ke liye. [Q495]\n● DNA transcribed hota hai RNA mein, jo protein synthesis ka template hota hai. [Q495]\n● Genes: DNA ke segments jo heredity ki functional unit hain, parent se offspring mein transfer hote hain,\nbody ki structure/function/metabolism control karte hain. [Q480, Q482, Q484, Q504]\n● 'Genetics' term William Bateson ne 1905 mein coin kiya. 'Gene' term Wilhelm Johannes ne 1909 mein\ncoin kiya. [Q504]\n● Genotype = DNA mein genes ka set jo traits ke liye responsible. Phenotype = physical appearance.\n[Q484]\n● Chromosomes: thread-like structures containing DNA wrapped around histone proteins. Humans: 2n=46\n(44 autosomes + 2 sex chromosomes). [Q482, Q509]\n20. Protein Synthesis\n● Transcription: mRNA DNA template se nucleus mein banta hai RNA polymerase se. [Q481]"," ● mRNA (messenger RNA) protein synthesis (translation) ka template hota hai. [Q481]\n● Ribosomes protein factories hain jo amino acids jodte hain. [Q432]\n21. Specialized Cells\n● RBCs (Red Blood Cells): nucleus nahi hota, bone marrow mein bante hain, oxygen carry karte hain,\nCO remove karte hain. Lifespan 120 days. Normal range: Male 4.7-6.1 million/mcL, Female 4.2-5.4\n₂\nmillion/mcL. [Q492]\n● WBCs: 12-20 days lifespan. Platelets: 8-10 days. [Q492]\n● Neurons (nerve cells): branched, long, information receive aur transmit karte hain. [Q447]\n● Rod aur Cone cells: retina (eye ke back) mein hote hain. Rod cells low light vision (rhodopsin pigment),\nCone cells colour vision (iodopsin pigment). [Q459]\n● Flame cells: Planaria (flatworm, phylum Platyhelminthes) mein excretory organs - solenocytes bhi kehte\nhain. [Q473]\n22. Unicellular Organisms\n● Paramecium: slipper-shaped, unicellular, pond water mein, cilia se covered. [Q433, Q451]\n● Amoeba: entire cell surface se food leta hai pseudopodia se - single-celled, cell membrane, dense\nnucleus, vacuoles. [Q451]\n● Paramecium specific spot (oral groove) se food leta hai. [Q451]\n● Unicellular organisms: Bacteria, Protists, Yeast. [Q433]\n● Bread mould (Rhizopus): multicellular fungus. Cuscuta: parasitic plant. [Q433]\n● Muscles inherently multi-cellular hote hain — Unicellular (single-celled) organisms mein Bacteria,\nProtists, Yeast aate hain (prokaryotic-eukaryotic types mein categorize). [Q494]\n23. Osmosis, Diffusion, Plasmolysis\n● Osmosis: water ka movement semipermeable membrane ke across hypotonic se hypertonic solution ki\ntaraf - hypotonic solution mein cells swell kar jati hain. [Q434]\n● Plasmolysis: cell ka cell wall se contraction due to water loss (hypertonic solution mein) - jaise Rhoeo\nleaf slide par strong sugar solution daalne se. [Q427, Q466]\n● Deplasmolysis: jab water andar jata hai aur cytoplasm swell hota hai. Cytolysis: cell bursting due to\nosmotic imbalance. [Q466]\n24. Other Cell Facts"," ● Ionizing radiation atoms ko affect karke DNA damage karti hai - direct aur indirect (water radiolysis)\ndono tarah se. [Q476]\n● Benzene vapor anemia aur leukemia cause karta hai. Chloroform eyes/skin/liver/kidney harm karta hai.\n[Q476]\n● Tissue: cells similar in origin, form and function. Histology = tissue ka study. Histopathology = disease-\nrelated tissue study. [Q497]\n● Bone marrow mein stem cells se RBC, WBC, platelets develop hote hain. [Q472]\n● Guard cells mein jab water jata hai → turgid (swollen) hoti hain → stomatal pore opens (CO intake, O\n₂\n₂\nrelease). [Q485]\n● Leaf cross-section: Upper epidermis (water loss prevent), Lower epidermis (CO in, O out), Guard cells\n₂\n₂\n\n(stoma regulate), Air spaces (gas exchange), Chloroplast (light capture). [Q416]\n● Plant waste storage: leaves (shed hote hain), old xylem (resins/gums), cellular vacuoles. [Q421]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 7 Cell Basic Unit of Life Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0373","t":"08 Sensory Organs","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.8 — SENSORY ORGANS — FULL MIND MAP\n👁️👂\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Types of Sensory Receptors\n2. Human Eye - Structure & Function\n3. Human Eye - Photoreceptors (Rods & Cones)\n4. Human Ear - Structure & Function\n5. Human Ear - Balance\n6. Sense of Taste (Gustation)\n7. Sense of Smell (Olfaction)\n8. Anaesthetics & Sensation Loss\n9. Other Sensory Facts\n1. Types of Sensory Receptors\n● Gustatory receptors tongue par hote hain - taste sense ke liye. [Q510, Q531]\n● Olfactory receptors nose mein hote hain - smell/odour molecules detect karte hain. [Q514, Q531]\n● Thermoreceptors nerve endings mein temperature changes detect karte hain. [Q510]\n● Phonoreceptors inner ear mein hote hain - hearing sense ke liye. [Q510]\n● Photoreceptors eyes mein hote hain - light detect karte hain. [Q510]\n● Sensory receptors overall eyes, ears, nose, mouth, internal organs mein distributed hote hain. [Q531]\n2. Human Eye - Structure & Function\n● Cornea aur Retina eye mein paaye jate hain. Eye ke parts: Pupil (light admits), Iris (coloured tissue),\nRetina (images → electrical impulses), Sclera (outermost coat), Cornea (clear anterior portion, 2/3\noptical power). [Q511, Q521]\n● Iris eye ka coloured part hai jo pupil ke aaspaas hai - light entry ko control karta hai pupil size adjust\nkarke. [Q526]\n● Pupil iris mein hole hai jisse light pass hoti hai. [Q526]\n● Cornea clear anterior coat hai jo 2/3 optical power provide karta hai. [Q526]\n● Retina sensitive layer hai jo images ko electrical impulses mein convert karti hai. [Q526]\n● Fovea retina ka chhota depression hai jahan visual acuity (drishti teevrata) sabse zyada hoti hai. [Q520]\n● Blind spot optic disc ki position ko correspond karta hai jahan koi photoreceptor nahi hote. [Q520]\n● Vitreous body lens aur retina ke beech clear gel hai. [Q520]\n● Choroid sclera aur retina ke beech ki middle layer hai. [Q520, Q521]\n● Ciliary body ciliary muscle contain karti hai jo lens shape change karti hai near focusing ke liye. [Q521]\n● Optic disc pe ganglion cell axons eye se bahar nikalte hain → optic nerve banti hai. [Q517]"," 3. Human Eye - Photoreceptors (Rods & Cones)\n● Rods aur Cones dono retina mein paye jate hain - ye photoreceptor cells hain. [Q517, Q524, Q529]\n● Cones (shanku): bright/normal light ke liye sensitive hain, colour sensation dete hain (3 colours: blue,\ngreen, red), photopic vision. [Q517, Q524, Q529]\n● Rods: dim/low light ke liye sensitive hain, twilight/scotopic vision dete hain, colour nahi dekh paate.\n[Q517, Q524, Q529]\n4. Human Ear - Structure & Function\n● Ear 3 parts mein divided hai: - Outer ear: Pinna + External auditory meatus (sound waves\ncollect/transmit) - Middle ear: Malleus (Hammer), Incus (Anvil), Stapes (Stirrup) - 3 ossicles - Inner\near: Cochlea, Semicircular canals, Vestibule [Q513, Q525, Q528]\n● Tympanic membrane (eardrum) ear canal ke end mein hai - outer ear ko middle ear se separate karti\nhai, sound vibrations ke according vibrate karti hai. [Q513, Q525]\n● Middle ear ke 3 bones (ossicles) sound ko amplify karte hain - Malleus/Hammer (eardrum se attached),\nIncus/Anvil, Stapes/Stirrup (membrane se attached). Sound 20 times tak amplify hoti hai. [Q516, Q528,\nQ530]\n● Cochlea inner ear mein fluid-filled, spiral-shaped cavity hai - pressure variations ko electrical signals\nmein convert karti hai (auditory transduction). [Q522, Q530]\n● Auditory canal pinna se eardrum tak sound transmit karti hai. Pinna sound waves collect karta hai.\n[Q522]\n● Eustachian tubes middle ears ko throat se connect karte hain - fluid drain karte hain aur air pressure\nequalize karte hain. [Q525]\n5. Human Ear - Balance\n● Ear sound ke alawa balance maintain karne mein bhi help karta hai. [Q515]\n● Vestibular system ear ke andar hai: 3 semicircular canals + 2 otolith organs (Utricle aur Saccule). Har\nsemicircular canal specific head movement direction ke liye responsible hai. [Q515]\n6. Sense of Taste (Gustation)\n● Gustatory receptors tongue par taste buds ke roop mein hote hain. [Q510, Q531]\n● 5 basic tastes: Salty, Sour (ion channels se), Sweet, Bitter, Umami (G protein-coupled receptors se).\n[Q531]\n● Tongue ek unique muscle hai jo dono ends par attached NAHI hai - independently function karti hai:\ntasting, gulping, digestive enzymes provide karna. [Q512]\n● Largest muscle: Gluteus maximus. Smallest muscle: Stapedius. [Q512]"," 7. Sense of Smell (Olfaction)\n● Olfactory receptors nose mein hote hain - protein odour molecules ko bind karte hain. [Q514]\n● Olfactory indicators smell se kaam karte hain - acid/base ke saath smell change hoti hai. Examples:\nVanilla, Onion, Clove. [Q523]\n● Visually impaired students olfactory indicators use kar sakte hain. Visual indicators: Turmeric, grape\njuice, petunia leaves, litmus. [Q523]\n8. Anaesthetics & Sensation Loss\n● Anaesthetic agent local ya general loss of sensation produce karta hai - temporarily nerves se brain tak\nsensory signals block karta hai. [Q518]\n● Anaesthetics surgical operations mein use hote hain areas numb karne ya sleep induce karne ke liye.\nExamples: Desflurane, Isoflurane, Nitrous oxide, Sevoflurane, Xenon. [Q518]\n9. Other Sensory Facts\n● Organ of Corti hearing se related hai (auditory transduction) - inner ear mein hai, 3 rows outer hair cells\n+ 1 row inner hair cells. Sound waves → eardrum → vibrations bend stereocilia on hair cells. [Q519]\n● Auditory system = hearing. Visual sensory system = colour, light, contrast, motion. [Q514]\n● Cartilage connective tissue hai jo ears mein hoti hai jisse ears fold kar sakte hain - ye bone surfaces ko\njoints par smooth bhi karti hai, nose/trachea/larynx mein bhi hoti hai. [Q527]\n● Connective tissues ke types: Areolar, Adipose, Bone, Tendon, Ligament, Blood. [Q527]\n● Cochlea pressure variations ko electrical signals mein convert karti hai auditory nerve ke through brain\ntak bhejne ke liye. [Q528]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 8 Sensory Organs Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0374","t":"09 Circulatory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.9 — CIRCULATORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n❤️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Human Heart Structure & Chambers\n2. Heartbeat Cycle - Systole & Diastole\n3. Blood Vessels - Arteries, Veins, Capillaries\n4. Blood Pressure & Measurement\n5. Double vs Single Circulation\n6. Heart Chambers in Different Animals\n7. Blood Components & Functions\n8. Hemoglobin & Iron\n9. Blood Groups - ABO & Rh\n10. Blood Clotting (Coagulation)\n11. Lymphatic System\n12. Blood as Connective Tissue\n13. Diagnostic Instruments\n14. Heart Facts & Other Important Points\n1. Human Heart Structure & Chambers\n● Human heart 4-chambered hai: 2 upper Atria (Auricles) + 2 lower Ventricles. Left ventricle ki walls sabse\nmoti hoti hain kyunki ye poora body mein blood pump karta hai high pressure mein. [Q537, Q553, Q598]\n● Septum heart ke left aur right sides ko completely alag rakhta hai taaki oxygenated aur deoxygenated\nblood mix na ho. [Q537]\n● Heart valves (one-way inlets/outlets) backflow rokte hain: - Tricuspid valve: Right atrium ↔ Right\nventricle - Pulmonary valve: Right ventricle ↔ Pulmonary artery - Aortic valve: Left ventricle ↔ Aorta\n- Mitral (Bicuspid) valve: Left atrium ↔ Left ventricle [Q559]\n● Cardiac muscles cylindrical, branched, single-nuclei hoti hain, striated appearance hai, aur involuntary\nhain. [Q593]\n● Purkinje fibres heart ki muscle fibres hain jo electrical stimulus conduct karti hain taaki coordinated heart\ncontraction ho sake. Jan Evangelista Purkyne ne 1839 mein discover kiya. [Q577]\n● Heart weight adult mein ~300 gm hota hai (range 236-412 gm), size ek closed fist ke barabar. [Q571]\n2. Heartbeat Cycle - Systole & Diastole\n● Diastole (relaxation): Blood ventricles mein enter karta hai. Ventricular diastole mein oxygenated blood\nleft atrium → left ventricle; deoxygenated blood right atrium → right ventricle. [Q532]\n● Systole (contraction): Blood ventricles se bahar nikalta hai. Systolic BP ventricular contraction ke dauran\nmeasure hota hai. [Q535]\n● Pulse arteries mein blood flow ki rhythmic throbbing hai - arteries ki muscular walls expand hoti hain jab\nheart se blood pump hota hai. [Q558]\n● Normal BP: <120/80 mmHg. Systolic = max pressure (heart beats), Diastolic = min pressure (heart\nrests). High BP → Hypertension + kidney problems. Low BP → Dizziness + Nausea. [Q535, Q544, Q572]"," 3. Blood Vessels - Arteries, Veins, Capillaries\n● Arteries: Thick walls, no valves, blood high pressure mein bahata hai, heart se body ke parts mein blood\nle jaati hai (except pulmonary artery jo deoxygenated blood lungs tak leti hai). [Q545, Q582]\n● Veins: Thin walls, valves hoti hain, low pressure, body se blood heart ki taraf leti hain (except pulmonary\nvein jo oxygenated blood lungs se heart tak leti hai). Skin ke paas dikhti hain. [Q545, Q552]\n● Capillaries: Sabse chhoti vessels, arteries ko veins se connect karti hain, tissues tak O /nutrients supply\n₂\n\nkarti hain. Skin ke neeche maujood chhoti vessels capillaries hain. [Q573, Q581]\n● Aorta: Sabse badi artery, left ventricle se oxygenated blood body ke baaki hisson mein leti hai. [Q562,\nQ566]\n● Vena Cava: Sabse badi vein, deoxygenated blood heart tak leti hai. [Q566]\n● Pulmonary vein unique hai kyunki ye ekmatr vein hai jo oxygenated blood carry karti hai (lungs → left\natrium). [Q543, Q561, Q579]\n● Renal artery heart se kidney tak blood leti hai. Coronary arteries heart muscle ko khud oxygenated\nblood supply karti hain. [Q570]\n4. Blood Pressure & Measurement\n● BP measure karne ke liye Sphygmomanometer use hota hai. [Q540]\n● Stethoscope heartbeat detect karne mein help karta hai. Thermometer temperature, Spirometer breath\namount measure karta hai. [Q542]\n●\n Trap: Hypertension (High BP) veins ke constriction se nahi hota - ye arteries/arterioles ke\n⚠️\nconstriction se hota hai. [Q534, Q551]\n● BP = force jo blood vessel ki wall ke against exert hota hai. Normal range 120/80 se 140/90 mmHg tak.\n[Q572]\n5. Double vs Single Circulation\n● Double circulation: Ek cycle mein blood heart se do baar guzarta hai. - Complete double: Birds\n(Peacock, Pigeon), Mammals (Man, Tiger, Rabbit, Bat, Whale), Crocodiles - 4-chambered heart. -\nIncomplete double: Amphibians (Frog, Salamander), most Reptiles - 3-chambered heart, thoda mixing\ntolerate kar sakte hain. [Q533, Q538, Q541, Q546, Q554, Q557, Q563, Q584]\n● Single circulation: Fish mein - ek cycle mein blood heart se ek baar guzarta hai. 2-chambered heart (1\natrium + 1 ventricle). [Q538, Q547, Q548, Q554, Q568, Q583]\n● Deoxygenated blood ko alag rakha jata hai taaki warm-blooded animals (birds, mammals) ka body\ntemperature constant rahe - cellular respiration ke liye zyada oxygen chahiye hoti hai. [Q549]\n6. Heart Chambers in Different Animals"," ● 2-chambered: Fish, Seahorse (1 atrium + 1 ventricle) [Q541, Q548, Q583]\n● 3-chambered: Amphibians (Frog, Salamander), most Reptiles (2 atria + 1 ventricle) - mixing tolerate kar\nsakte hain. [Q541, Q546, Q584]\n● 4-chambered: Birds (Peacock, Pigeon), Mammals (Man, Tiger, Rabbit, Bat, Whale), Crocodiles -\ncomplete separation. [Q541, Q546, Q548, Q563]\n● Cockroach: 13-chambered heart. [Q583]\n7. Blood Components & Functions\n● RBC (Erythrocytes): Oxygen carry karte hain lungs se body tak. Biconcave disc shape, diameter ~7.5\nμm, lifespan 115-120 days, nucleus nahi hota. Hemoglobin contain karte hain. Bone marrow mein bante\nhain. [Q574, Q592, Q594, Q595]\n● WBC (Leukocytes): Immunity, \"soldiers\" of the body. Blood ka sirf 1% hissa. Types: Granulocytes\n(Neutrophils, Eosinophils, Basophils), Monocytes, Lymphocytes (T cells, B cells). Normal count: 4,500-\n11,000 per microliter. [Q536, Q560, Q596]\n● Platelets (Thrombocytes): Blood clotting (coagulation) mein help karte hain, bone marrow se bante hain.\n[Q534, Q555]\n● Plasma: Blood ka liquid part, 55% of total blood volume. 92% water + 8%\nproteins/minerals/hormones/enzymes. Food, CO , nitrogenous waste transport karta hai.\n₂\n[Q599, Q600]\n● Blood ka function: O carry, CO remove, immunity (WBC), clotting (platelets).\n Trap: Blood sensory\n₂\n₂\u0002\n⚠️\u0004\ninputs mein help nahi karta - ye nervous system ka kaam hai. [Q569]\n8. Hemoglobin & Iron\n● Hemoglobin iron-rich protein hai RBCs mein jo O bind karke transport karta hai.\n₂\n[Q567]\n● Hemoglobin do parts se bana: Heme (iron part, red colour) + Globin (protein part). [Q564, Q576]\n● Iron deficiency se Anaemia hota hai. [Q564]\n9. Blood Groups - ABO & Rh\n● 8 main blood types: A+, A-, B+, B-, O+, O-, AB+, AB-. [Q539]\n● Universal Donor: O (O- ideally, O+ emergency mein positive types ke liye) - RBC par na A na B antigen\nhota, dono antibodies plasma mein hote hain. [Q539]\n● Universal Recipient: AB+ - dono A aur B antigens hote hain, koi antibodies nahi hoti. [Q565]\n● A + B parents se AB child = Co-dominance example. A aur B dono genes dominant hain. [Q556]\n10. Blood Clotting (Coagulation)"," ● Platelets clotting ke liye crucial hain - injury site par clot form karte hain excess blood loss rokne ke liye.\n[Q555]\n● Calcium (Ca, atomic no. 20) blood coagulation ke liye essential hai - platelets aur plasma proteins ke\nsaath interact karke clot banata hai. [Q578]\n11. Lymphatic System\n● Lymph plasma jaisa hai lekin colorless aur kam protein hota hai. Isme WBCs hote hain jo harmful\nbacteria se ladte hain. Tissue fluid bhi kehte hain. Digested food aur fat transport karta hai. [Q534, Q550]\n12. Blood as Connective Tissue\n● Blood ek red vascular connective tissue hai - fluid matrix (plasma) + formed elements (RBC, WBC,\nplatelets). [Q585, Q591]\n● Blood body weight ka 7-8% hota hai. Adult mein ~5-6 litres (kuch questions mein 6.8L mentioned). pH\n7.35-7.45 (slightly basic). [Q569, Q586, Q587, Q588]\n●\n Trap: Blood white nahi hota - ye exclusively red fluid connective tissue hai.\n⚠️\n[Q586, Q587]\n● Blood mein fibers absent hote hain - ye specialized liquid connective tissue hai. [Q597]\n●\n Trap: Blood flow jerkily aur low pressure par nahi hota - ye smooth aur steady hota hai, arteries\n⚠️\nmein high pressure. [Q589]\n●\n Trap: Vascular system body weight ka 1.7-1.8% nahi - ye 7-8% hota hai.\n⚠️\n[Q588]\n13. Diagnostic Instruments\n● Sphygmomanometer: Blood pressure measure karta hai. [Q540]\n● Stethoscope: Heartbeat detect karta hai. [Q542]\n● ECG (Electrocardiogram): Heart problems diagnose karta hai - irregularities in heart rhythm. Willem\nEinthoven ne invent kiya. Heart attack, heart failure, arrhythmia, cardiac arrest detect kar sakta hai.\n[Q575]\n● Spirometer: Breath amount measure karta hai. [Q542]\n● Haemocytometer: RBC count determine karta hai. [Q595]\n● Spectrophotometer light measure karta hai, Urinometer urine specific gravity, Haemoglobin meter Hb\nlevel. [Q540]\n14. Heart Facts & Other Important Points\n● Angioplasty heart par ki jati hai - blocked coronary arteries ko open karne ke liye. [Q580]"," ● ECG, Stethoscope, Sphygmomanometer heart se related hain. EEG brain activity ke liye, BCG TB\nvaccine, ECT electroconvulsive therapy. [Q575]\n● Human heart ~72 times/minute dhadata hai. Brain weight ~1300-1400 gm. [Q580, Q571]\n●\n Disputed: Vascular system ke baare mein diye gaye statements mein — 'human heart closed fist ke\n⚠️\nsize ka hai' wale option ko is specific question mein 'NOT true' maana gaya (halaki commonly heart ko\nfist-sized hi approximate kiya jaata hai) — baaki statements (blood body weight ka 7-8%, high pressure\nflow, 'river of life') sahi hain. [Q590]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 9 Circulatory System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0375","t":"10 Excretory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.10 — EXCRETORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n🚽\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Human Excretory System - Components\n2. Kidneys - Structure & Function\n3. Nephron - Functional Unit\n4. Urine Formation - 3 Stages\n5. Urine Composition & Volume\n6. Dialysis & Hemodialysis\n7. Excretion in Plants\n8. Types of Nitrogenous Waste\n9. Other Organs in Excretion\n10. Medical Techniques & Miscellaneous\n11. Missing Facts — Plant Excretion, Alimentary Canal & Diagram\n1. Human Excretory System - Components\n● Human excretory system: One pair kidneys, one pair ureters, single urinary bladder, single urethra.\n[Q619]\n● Ureter: thin muscular tube (3-4mm), kidneys ko bladder se connect karti hai, bilateral hoti hain. [Q627,\nQ634]\n● Urinary bladder: urine receive karta hai, micturition se expel hota hai. Muscular bladder nervous control\nmein hota hai isliye hum urinate ki urge control kar sakte hain. [Q646]\n● Urethra: bladder se body exterior tak, urine nikalne ka passage. Male mein 20 cm long, urine aur sperm\ndono ka common passage. Female mein sirf urine carry karti hai. [Q649, Q653]\n● Vas deferens urinary bladder se aane wali tube ke saath milkar urethra banta hai. [Q650]\n● Prostate gland: urinary bladder ke neeche, walnut-sized, between bladder and rectum/penis. Urethra\niske centre se guzarta hai. Functions: semen produce, filter, erection, UTI protection, urine flow control.\n[Q648, Q654]\n2. Kidneys - Structure & Function\n● Kidneys bean-shaped (seem ke aakar ki), abdomen mein backbone ke dono taraf. Location: last\nthoracic aur third lumbar vertebra ke beech. Weight: 120-170g each. [Q621]\n● Kidney functions: urine produce karna, Renin hormone (BP regulate), blood filter karna, urea/uric acid\nremove karna, water & salt concentration maintain karna, vitamin D produce karna. [Q601, Q603, Q606]\n● Nephrology = kidneys ka study. Calcium oxalate stones = sabse common kidney stones. [Q606]\n●\n Trap: Kidney ke filtration units ko Neurons nahi kehte - ye Nephrons hain. Neurons brain/nervous\n⚠️\nsystem ki cells hain. [Q621]\n3. Nephron - Functional Unit"," ● Nephron = kidney ki functional, structural, anatomical unit. Har kidney mein ~8 lakh se zyada nephrons\n(1 million per kidney bhi bola jata hai). [Q617, Q621, Q623, Q647]\n● Nephron components: Renal corpuscle (Glomerulus + Bowman's capsule) → PCT (Proximal\nConvoluted Tubule) → Loop of Henle → Distal Convoluted Tubule → Collecting duct → Renal vein.\n[Q630]\n● Bowman's capsule: double-walled, cup-shaped, glomerulus ko surround karti hai. Function: ultra-\nfiltration → glomerular filtrate banati hai. [Q620, Q639, Q645]\n● Glomerulus: tiny blood vessels ka cluster/tuft, main filtering unit. Blood cells aur large proteins blood\nmein hi rehte hain. [Q620, Q639]\n● Collecting duct: nephrons ko minor calyx ya renal pelvis se directly connect karti hai. [Q629]\n● Long tubular structure ka advantage: excess water reabsorb karne ke liye time aur space milta hai.\n[Q623]\n● Loop of Henle: PCT se distal convoluted tubule tak. [Q620]\n● Renal tubules ki walls epithelial tissue se bani hoti hain - cuboidal epithelium. [Q613, Q625]\n4. Urine Formation - 3 Stages\n● Correct sequence: Filtration → Selective Reabsorption → Secretion/Elimination. [Q601, Q608]\n● Filtration (Glomerular filtration/Ultrafiltration): Glomerulus blood se water aur substances filter karta hai.\nFiltration membrane blood cells aur large proteins ko blood mein rakhti hai. [Q608]\n● Reabsorption: ~99% filtrate reabsorb hota hai. Glucose, water, salts, amino acids reabsorb hote hain.\n[Q602, Q615]\n● Secretion: Waste ions aur H+ ions blood se tubule mein aate hain - acid-base balance ke liye. [Q608]\n● Normal adult mein initial filtrate: ~180 L/day - isme se sirf 1-2 L urine excrete hota hai (baki reabsorb).\n[Q615, Q621, Q641, Q651]\n● Reabsorption ki amount determine hoti hai: additional water aur dissolved waste excrete hone ki matra\nse. [Q615]\n● GFR (Glomerular Filtration Rate) = per minute glomerulus dwara utpann filtrate ki matra. [Q641]\n5. Urine Composition & Volume\n● Adult human daily urine: 1000-2000 mL (1-2 L). [Q632]\n● Urine composition: 95% water, 2.5% urea, 2.5% other waste products - yellowish, slightly acidic. [Q607,\nQ632, Q640]\n● Substances jo kidneys reabsorb NAHI karti: Creatinine (muscle waste; >1.2 mg/dL women, >1.4 mg/dL\nmen = kidney dysfunction). Glucose, amino acids, salts reabsorb hote hain. [Q628]\n6. Dialysis & Hemodialysis"," ● Dialysis tab use hota hai jab kidneys kaam karna band kar de - waste aur excess fluid remove karta hai.\nTypes: Hemodialysis (artificial kidney, blood bahar clean hota hai) aur Peritoneal dialysis (abdomen\nlining blood filter karti hai andar). [Q631, Q644, Q651]\n● Hemodialysis: semipermeable tubes dialysis solution mein - waste remove hote hain, purified blood\nwapas pump hota hai. [Q636]\n● Dialysis fluid mein blood ke samaan osmotic pressure hota hai aur nitrogenous wastes se rahit hota hai\n- taaki fluid imbalance na ho. Urea diffusion se remove hota hai. [Q637]\n● Dialysis ka principle: Diffusion, convection, osmotic pressure. [Q626, Q636]\n● Artificial kidney nitrogenous waste remove karta hai - is process ko Haemodialysis kehte hain. [Q631]\n7. Excretion in Plants\n● Plants mein defined excretory system NAHI hoti kyunki ye vegetative parts se excrete karte hain. [Q635]\n● Plant excretion methods: Transpiration (excess water), Diffusion (gas exchange), Storage (vacuoles, old\nxylem, shed leaves). [Q605]\n●\n Trap: Plants ke paas waste removal ke liye specialized organs NAHI hote.\n⚠️\n[Q609]\n● Plant waste products: O , CO , water vapour (gaseous), Raphides, tannins, resins, gum, rubber,\n₂\n₂\nessential oils (solid). [Q616, Q635]\n● Gaseous wastes stomata aur lenticels se remove hote hain. Solid wastes leaves/bark mein store hote\nhain jo shed hone par eliminate hote hain. [Q616, Q635]\n●\n Trap: Photosynthesis ka waste product Oxygen hai, starch NAHI.\n⚠️\n[Q616]\n● Plants very slowly aur very little waste excrete karte hain. Respiration ka CO aur photosynthesis ka O\n₂\n₂\nek doosre ke raw material hote hain. [Q609]\n●\n Trap: Plants sweating se waste eliminate NAHI karte - ye animal method hai.\n⚠️\n[Q624]\n8. Types of Nitrogenous Waste\n● Three main types: - Ammonia (Ammonotelic): Most toxic. Aquatic animals (fish, protozoans) -\nabundant water dilute kar sakti hai. [Q607, Q610]\n● Human urine: 95% water, 2% urea, 0.1% creatinine, 0.03% uric acid. [Q612]\n● Cow urine: 95% water, 2.5% urea, minerals, 24 types salts. [Q612]\n● Lactic acid nitrogenous waste NAHI hai - ye anaerobic respiration ka by-product hai muscles mein.\n[Q638]\n● Animal excretory products: Ammonia, CO , Urea, Uric Acid, Guanine, Creatine. Modes: Ammonotelism,\n₂\nUreotelism, Uricotelism, Aminotelism, Guanotelism. [Q638]\n● Ammonia (Ammonotelic): Most toxic. Aquatic animals (fish, protozoans) - abundant water dilute kar sakti\nhai. [Q607, Q610]\n● Urea (Ureotelic): Medium toxicity. Humans, cows, mammals. Liver mein urea cycle (ornithine cycle) se\nbanta hai. [Q607, Q611, Q612]"," ● Uric acid (Uricotelic): Least toxic, minimum water chahiye (1g = 10ml water). Reptiles, birds, insects.\nLiver mein 'Inosinic pathway' se banta hai. [Q607, Q612, Q643]\n9. Other Organs in Excretion\n● Excretory organs humans mein: Skin, Liver, Large intestine, Lungs, Kidneys. Small intestine excretory\norgan NAHI hai. [Q604]\n● Lungs: gas exchange (CO remove). Skin: sweat (water, salts, urea), temperature regulation. Large\n₂\nintestine: water absorb, feces move karna. Liver: urea produce karna. [Q604]\n● Cartilage tissue kidney mein absent hoti hai - nose, ear, larynx mein hoti hai. [Q622]\n10. Medical Techniques & Miscellaneous\n● Ultrasonography (Ultrasound): kidney/gall bladder stones aur pregnancy mein fetus examine karne ke\nliye - non-invasive, high-frequency sound waves. [Q642]\n● ECG = heart rhythm. MRI = 3D anatomical images. Echocardiography = heart imaging. [Q642]\n● Ultrafiltration excretion se related hai - kidney ke glomerulus mein hoti hai. [Q652]\n● Respiration = C-C bonds break by oxidation. Digestion = complex food to simple absorbable forms.\n[Q652]\n11. Missing Facts — Plant Excretion, Alimentary Canal & Diagram\n● Plants ke excretory products mein 'Carbon Dioxide' (CO2) inhale karne par humans ke liye harmful hai\n— Gums medicines-cosmetics mein use hoti hain, Resins adhesives-food glazing mein, Oxygen\nessential hai. [Q614]\n● Humans mein alimentary canal ka 'Anus' part waste material excrete karta hai — Large intestine\nindigestible matter process karke water absorb karta hai, feces rectum-anus se expel hoti hai. [Q618]\n● Excretory system diagram mein ureters aur urinary bladder ki sahi position 'Diagram 1' mein dikhti hai\n— Liver se urea blood mein jaata hai, kidneys filter karte hain, urine ureters ke through bladder mein\njaata hai, urethra se expel hoti hai. [Q633]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 10 Excretory System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0376","t":"11 Endocrine and Exocrine System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.11 — ENDOCRINE & EXOCRINE SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n🧪\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Exocrine Glands & Digestive Enzymes\n2. Endocrine Glands - Master Gland (Pituitary)\n3. Thyroid Gland\n4. Adrenal Glands\n5. Pancreas - Dual Function\n6. Pineal Gland\n7. Other Glands & Exocrine Functions\n8. Liver & Glucose Metabolism\n9. Excretory System Basics\n1. Exocrine Glands & Digestive Enzymes\n● Bile salts (liver/pituitary dwara produced) fat ke emulsification mein madad karte hain - fat ko chhote\ndroplets mein todte hain taaki enzymes digest kar sakein. [Q655]\n● Trypsin (small intestine): digestion mein madad karta hai. HCl (stomach): acidic environment aur\nmicrobes ko kill karta hai. Pepsin (1836 mein Theodore Schwann ne discover kiya): endopeptidase\nenzyme jo proteins ko peptides mein todta hai. [Q655]\n● Salivary glands exocrine glands hain - mouth mein hote hain, hundreds of small glands\ntongue/palate/lips/cheeks mein. Ductal system mein substances secrete karte hain. [Q656]\n2. Endocrine Glands - Master Gland (Pituitary)\n● Pituitary gland (Hypophysis) \"Master gland\" kehlati hai - hypothalamus se thin stalk (pituitary\nstalk/infundibulum) dwara connected hai. Pea-sized, oval, skull ke andar. Anterior + Posterior lobe hote\nhain. [Q657, Q664]\n● Pituitary vital body functions, growth (height), aur sexual development regulate karti hai. Dwarfism iske\ndysfunction se hota hai. [Q658]\n● Pituitary hormones: Growth Hormone (GH), Prolactin (PRL), Luteinizing Hormone (LH), Follicle-\nStimulating Hormone (FSH), Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone (TSH), Adrenocorticotropic Hormone\n(ACTH), Antidiuretic Hormone (ADH), Oxytocin. [Q664]\n● Key gland locations: Hypothalamus aur Pineal skull ke andar, Thyroid neck ke base par, Thymus upper\nchest mein, Adrenals kidneys ke upar. [Q662]\n3. Thyroid Gland\n● Thyroid: butterfly-shaped, throat ke base par. Thyroxine (T4) aur Triiodothyronine (T3) produce karti hai\njo growth, development, aur overall metabolism ko control karte hain. [Q658, Q661]"," 4. Adrenal Glands\n● Adrenal glands: kidneys ke upar hote hain. Cortisol, aldosterone, adrenaline produce karte hain jo blood\npressure control karte hain. [Q659]\n● Adrenal gland \"Fight or Flight\" response ke liye body ko prepare karti hai - isliye ise \"Emergency\nhormone\" bhi kehte hain. [Q660]\n5. Pancreas - Dual Function\n● Pancreas: Exocrine (digestion) + Endocrine (blood sugar regulation) dono functions. Abdomen mein\nhota hai. [Q658, Q661]\n● Insulin (Beta cells se) aur Glucagon (Alpha cells se) secrete karta hai jo glucose regulate karte hain aur\nenergy release ki rate control karte hain. [Q661, Q663]\n● Blood sugar rise hone par Pancreas ki Beta cells detect karti hain aur Insulin secrete karti hain sugar\nkam karne ke liye. [Q663]\n● Hyperinsulinemia = zyada insulin. Diabetes = inadequate insulin action ya production. [Q663]\n6. Pineal Gland\n● Pineal gland: small, pea-sized, brain ke third ventricle ke peeche. Melatonin secrete karti hai jo circadian\nrhythm/sleep regulate karta hai. Light-dark cycle ki information convey karti hai. [Q660, Q661]\n7. Other Glands & Exocrine Functions\n● Sebaceous glands (skin/hair follicles mein) sebum (oil) produce karti hain jo skin ki moisture maintain\nrakhti hain. Sweat glands sweat secrete karti hain. Puberty mein inka secretion increase hota hai. [Q666]\n● Sebum mein triglycerides, wax esters, squalene hote hain. [Q666]\n8. Liver & Glucose Metabolism\n● Liver mein Gluconeogenesis hota hai - lactate (lactic acid) → pyruvate → glucose. Is glucose ko blood\nse muscles ko supply kiya jata hai. [Q667]\n9. Excretory System Basics\n● Kidney ki structural/functional unit Nephron hai - Neuron brain ki cell hai, Cytone/ Ketone galat options\nhain. [Q668]\n● Urea liver se kidneys ke through excrete hota hai. [Q669]"," ● Insufficient insulin se Diabetes (Madhumeh) hota hai - high blood sugar. [Q670]\n● Pancreatic duct: pancreas se duodenum tak digestive juices le jata hai. [Q671]\n●\n Trap: Endocrine glands ko \"Ductless glands\" bhi kehte hain kyunki ye bina duct ke directly\n⚠️\nbloodstream mein hormones secrete karte hain. [Q665]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 11 Endocrine and Exocrine System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0377","t":"12 Respiratory System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" 🫁 BIOLOGY CH.12 — RESPIRATORY SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Respiratory System Structure\n2. Breathing Mechanism & Lungs\n3. Respiration Process - Cellular\n4. Gaseous Exchange & Transport\n5. Respiration in Plants\n6. Respiration Types - Aerobic & Anaerobic\n7. Fermentation\n8. ATP & Energy\n9. Respiratory Disorders\n10. Miscellaneous Facts\n11. Additional Facts — Breathing Mechanics, Gas Exchange & Respiratory Pigment\n1. Respiratory System Structure\n● Trachea (windpipe) mein C-shaped 20 rings of cartilage hote hain jo air-passage ko collapsing se rokte\nhain. Ribs thoracic organs protect karti hain, spine body support karti hai. [Q672]\n● Respiratory system parts: Nose, Pharynx (throat), Larynx (voice box), Trachea, Bronchi, Bronchioles,\nLungs, Alveoli. [Q672, Q681, Q696]\n● Pharynx: throat ke peeche, nose/mouth se trachea/oesophagus tak air/food transport. [Q696]\n● Larynx (voice box): pharynx ke neeche, vocal cords hain. Sound produce hota hai jab hava cords se\nguzarti hai. [Q696]\n● Trachea: larynx se bronchi tak, air ka passage. [Q696]\n● Bronchi: trachea ka divide hona, dono lungs mein jata hai. [Q696]\n●\n Trap: Respiration mein oesophagus included NAHI hota - ye digestive system ka part hai.\n⚠️\n[Q681]\n2. Breathing Mechanism & Lungs\n● Breathing: physical process of inhaling/exhaling. Cellular respiration: oxygen use karke glucose se\nenergy release karna. [Q695]\n● Inspiration (inhalation): intercostal muscles + diaphragm contract → thoracic cavity expand → lungs\nexpand → air andar. [Q675]\n● Expiration (exhalation): intercostal muscles + diaphragm relax → thoracic cavity compress → lungs\nshrink → air bahar. [Q675]\n● Lungs thoracic cavity mein hain. Right lung 3 lobes, Left lung 2 lobes (heart ke liye jagah). [Q675]\n● Diaphragm: dome-shaped muscle, breathing ka main muscle. Contract = flatten = inhalation. Relax =\ndome = exhalation. [Q693, Q706]\n● Respiratory system ke through body oxygen receive karti hai aur CO remove karti hai.\n₂\n[Q686]"," ● Pharynx se hava aur dono food ja sakta hai - larynx mein epiglottis food ko trachea mein jaane se rokta\nhai. [Q704]\n● Spirometer se breathing capacity measure hoti hai. [Q690]\n3. Respiration Process - Cellular\n● Respiration ke 3 stages: 1. Glycolysis (cytoplasm): glucose → pyruvate. Oxygen ki zaroorat nahi. 2.\nKrebs Cycle (mitochondria): pyruvate → acetyl CoA → CO + energy. Oxygen present hona chahiye.\n₂\n3. Electron Transport Chain (mitochondria): oxygen final electron acceptor, water + ATP banta hai.\n[Q673]\n●\n Trap: Mitochondria mein acetic acid nahi, pyruvic acid breakdown hota hai oxygen use karke.\n⚠️\n[Q673]\n● First stage (glycolysis) cytoplasm mein hota hai - anaerobic. [Q673]\n● Oxygen ke presence mein pyruvate mitochondria mein jata hai. [Q673]\n● Aerobic respiration: O + Glucose → CO + H O + ATP (mitochondria).\n₂\n₂\n₂\n[Q708, Q711]\n4. Gaseous Exchange & Transport\n● Alveoli (air sacs) mein gaseous exchange hota hai - lungs ke andar millions of tiny sacs. [Q678]\n● Alveoli se O blood mein jata hai, CO blood se alveoli mein aata hai.\n₂\n₂\n[Q678]\n● Haemoglobin blood mein O bind karke transport karta hai.\n₂\n[Q678]\n● Oxygen dissociation curve: haemoglobin ki O binding capacity. Sigmoid shape.\n₂\n[Q678]\n● Oxygen blood se tissues mein jaata hai, CO tissues se blood mein aata hai.\n₂\n[Q686]\n5. Respiration in Plants\n● Plants mein stomata, lenticels, root hairs se gas exchange hota hai. [Q683]\n● Stomata: mainly leaves mein, guard cells control karte hain. Open = CO in, O out. Close = water\n₂\n₂\nconservation. [Q683]\n● Lenticels: stems/roots mein, woody plants mein. [Q683]\n● Root hairs: soil se oxygen absorb karte hain. [Q683]\n● Plants night mein bhi respire karte hain - O lete hain, CO chhodte hain. Day mein photosynthesis\n₂\n₂\nzyada hota hai isliye net O release hota hai.\n₂\n[Q683, Q698]\n●\n Trap: Plants sirf photosynthesis karte hain, respiration NAHI - ye galat hai. Plants dono karte hain.\n⚠️\n[Q698]\n6. Respiration Types - Aerobic & Anaerobic"," ● Aerobic respiration: Oxygen present, complete glucose breakdown, zyada ATP (~36-38), CO + H O\n₂\n₂\nproducts. [Q687, Q689, Q703, Q708]\n● Anaerobic respiration: Oxygen absent, incomplete breakdown, kam ATP (~2), lactic acid/ethanol + CO ₂\nproducts. [Q687, Q689, Q703]\n● Human muscles mein exercise ke dauran anaerobic respiration → lactic acid → cramps. [Q689]\n● Yeast mein anaerobic respiration → ethanol + CO (fermentation).\n₂\n[Q689]\n● Anaerobic respiration ke products: Lactic acid (animals), Ethanol + CO (yeast).\n₂\n[Q703]\n● Aerobic respiration ke products: CO + H O + ATP.\n₂\n₂\n[Q703, Q711]\n● Anaerobic respiration mitochondria mein NAHI hoti - cytoplasm mein hoti hai. [Q708]\n7. Fermentation\n● Fermentation = anaerobic respiration in microorganisms. Yeast: glucose → ethanol + CO .\n₂\n[Q685, Q699]\n● Fermentation mein NADH ko NAD regenerate kiya jata hai taaki glycolysis chalti rahe.\n⁺\n[Q685]\n● Fermentation ke types: - Lactic acid fermentation: muscles, some bacteria. - Alcoholic fermentation:\nyeast, some bacteria. [Q699]\n● Fermentation mein oxygen nahi chahiye hoti. [Q699]\n● Alcoholic fermentation: yeast, some bacteria. [Q699]\n8. ATP & Energy\n● ATP = Adenosine Triphosphate - cell ki energy currency. [Q674, Q680]\n● ATP mein 3 phosphate groups hote hain. ADP + Pi → ATP (energy store). ATP → ADP + Pi (energy\nrelease). [Q674, Q680]\n● ATP synthesis: substrate-level phosphorylation (glycolysis, Krebs) + oxidative phosphorylation (ETC).\n[Q674]\n● Respiration ka main goal ATP synthesis hai. [Q680]\n9. Respiratory Disorders\n● Asthma: bronchial tubes inflame/contract, mucus zyada, breathing difficult. [Q692]\n● Bronchitis: bronchi ka inflammation, mucus zyada. [Q692]\n● Emphysema: alveoli walls damage, surface area kam, O uptake kam.\n₂\n[Q692]\n● Pneumonia: lungs infection, alveoli fluid se bharte hain. [Q692]\n● Tuberculosis (TB): Mycobacterium tuberculosis se, lungs infect hota hai. [Q692]\n● CO poisoning: CO haemoglobin se zyada strongly bind karta hai (carboxyhaemoglobin), O transport\n₂\nblock ho jata hai. [Q710]"," 10. Miscellaneous Facts\n● Smoking se lungs damage hote hain - tar deposit, cilia destroy, cancer risk. [Q701]\n● Root hairs plants ko water aur minerals absorb karne mein madad karte hain - soil particles se. [Q705]\n● Lungs ke andar pleural fluid hota hai jo friction kam karta hai breathing ke dauran. [Q713]\n● Tidal volume: normal breath mein air ki amount (~500 mL). Vital capacity: max air exhale kar sakte hain.\n[Q717]\n● Respiratory quotient (RQ): CO produced/O consumed. Carbohydrate = 1, Fat = <1, Protein = ~0.8.\n₂\n₂\n[Q721]\n11. Additional Facts — Breathing Mechanics, Gas Exchange & Respiratory\nPigment\n● Glycolysis (glucose se pyruvate banana) aerobic AUR anaerobic respiration dono ke first step mein\ncommon hota hai — cytoplasm mein hoti hai, oxygen ki zaroorat nahi. [Q676]\n● 'Breathing holes' (spiracles) Cockroach jaise insects mein milte hain — tracheae network se connected\nhote hain. Man/Fish alag tarike se saans lete hain. [Q677]\n● Pyruvate ka aerobic breakdown human body mein 'Mitochondria' mein hota hai — anaerobically\ncytoplasm mein hota hai. [Q679]\n● Breathing cycle ke dauran lungs mein hamesha bachi rehne wali air 'Residual Volume' kehlaati hai —\nmaximum forceful expiration ke baad bhi kuch air reh jaati hai. [Q682]\n● Cigarette smoking harmful hai kyunki ye 'upper respiratory tract ke cilia ko damage karti hai' — airways,\nalveoli aur cilia (dirt-mucus rokne wale) sabko affect karti hai. [Q684]\n● Plants mein respiration ke end products 'CO2, H2O aur Energy' hote hain — Glucose + O2 → CO2 +\nH2O + Energy, stomata-lenticels-roots se O2 lete hain. [Q688]\n● Aerobic respiration mein mitochondria mein 1 pyruvate molecule breakdown hokar 3 CO2 molecules\nbanata hai — aerobic respiration anaerobic se ~18 guna zyada energy release karti hai. [Q691]\n● Air human body mein 'Nostrils' ke through enter karti hai — respiration ek metabolic process hai jisme\ncells O2 lekar CO2 release karte hain. [Q694]\n● Inhaled air mein ~21% Oxygen hoti hai, exhaled air mein ~16% Oxygen — Nitrogen 78% dono mein\nsame rehti hai, CO2 inhaled mein 0.04%, exhaled mein 4.4% hoti hai. [Q697]\n● Frogs (amphibians) lungs ke alawa apni 'slippery-moist skin' se bhi breathe kar sakte hain (cutaneous\nrespiration). [Q700]\n● Kuch fish 'more times per minute' water gulp karti hain animal ki tulna mein jo air breathe karta hai —\npani mein dissolved oxygen kam hoti hai, isliye aquatic animals fast breathe karte hain. [Q702]\n● 'Sinus' anatomical cavity hai jo air se filled hoti hai — skull ke andar hollow cavities ka connected\nsystem. Types: Frontal, Maxillary, Sphenoid, Ethmoid. [Q707]\n● 'Cutaneous respiration' (skin se gas exchange) Earthworm mein hoti hai — frogs aur leeches mein bhi\nhoti hai. [Q709]"," ● Lungs mein respiratory gases ka exchange 'Alveoli' mein hota hai — tiny air sacs jahan O2 blood mein\njaati hai aur CO2 diffuse hokar bahar aati hai. [Q712]\n● Sea mein green plants photosynthesis se 'Oxygen release' karte hain — ye oxygen paani mein dissolve\nhokar fish ke gills tak pahunchti hai respiration ke liye. [Q714]\n● 'Aerobic Respiration' mein sabse zyada energy release hoti hai — O2 use karke glucose ka complete\nbreakdown hota hai, 38 ATP tak per glucose molecule. [Q715]\n● Muscle cells mein oxygen ki kami hone par 6-carbon glucose molecule '3-carbon' molecule (lactic acid)\nmein convert ho jaata hai — muscle fatigue-cramps cause karta hai. [Q716]\n● Exhalation (expiration) 'lungs ke deflation' se hoti hai — diaphragm-intercostal muscles relax hote hain,\nthoracic cavity volume kam hota hai, air bahar nikalti hai. [Q718]\n● Respiration ke dauran energy 'glucose ke burning' (breakdown) se milti hai — cellular respiration\nglucose breakdown karke ATP generate karti hai. [Q719]\n● Throat (trachea) mein 'Cartilage' ke rings hote hain — collapsing rokte hain, nose-ears-larynx mein bhi\ncartilage milti hai. [Q720]\n● Human beings mein respiratory pigment 'Hemoglobin' hai — iron-containing pigment, RBC mein milta\nhai, O2 ko lungs se body parts tak carry karta hai. [Q722]\n● 'Respiration' life process hai jo chemical energy ko heat energy mein convert karta hai — food energy\nATP aur heat ki tarah release hoti hai, exothermic reaction hai. [Q723]\n● Substrate ka incomplete dissolution oxygen ki absence mein 'Anaerobic Respiration' kehlaata hai —\nkam energy yield karta hai kyunki electron transport chain less efficient hoti hai. [Q724]\n● Sahi statement: 'Oxygen lungs se blood mein diffuse hoti hai, aur Carbon dioxide blood se lungs mein\ndiffuse hoti hai' — alveoli mein O2 rich hoti hai, blood mein CO2 zyada. [Q725]\n●\n Trap: 'Medulla oblongata' respiratory system ka part NAHI hai — ye BRAIN ka part hai (respiratory\n⚠️\nrhythm control karta hai, lekin anatomically respiratory system mein nahi aata). Trachea, lungs, bronchi\nrespiratory system ke parts hain. [Q726]\n● Anaerobic respiration 'Oxygen' ki absence mein hoti hai — 2 steps: glycolysis aur pyruvic acid ka\nincomplete breakdown, poisonous compounds jama hone ki wajah se indefinitely continue nahi ho sakti.\n[Q727]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 12 Respiratory System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0378","t":"13 Digestive System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.13 — DIGESTIVE SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n🍽️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Bile & Fat Emulsification\n2. Stomach — HCl & Gastric Juice\n3. Small Intestine — Structure, Length & Digestion Completion\n4. Salivary Enzymes & Mouth Digestion\n5. Areolar Tissue\n6. Lymphatic System — Fat Transport\n7. Dental Health & Teeth Structure\n8. Smooth Muscle Organs\n9. Antacids — Indigestion Remedies\n10. Ruminant & External Digestion\n11. The Pancreas — Islets of Langerhans\n12. Liver Functions & Digestive System Parts\n13. Energy Storage & Release\n14. Match Lists — Digestive System Diagram & Functions\n1. Bile & Fat Emulsification\n● Bile salts large fat globules ko chhote globules mein todte hain (emulsification) — 'soap on dirt' jaisa\nkaam karte hain, jisse enzymes zyada effectively work kar sakein. [Q728, Q732, Q746, Q750]\n●\n Trap: Bile juice mein protein-digesting enzyme NAHI hota — bile fat globules break karti hai, digest\n⚠️\nnahi karti. Bile juice: germs kill karti hai, fat absorption help karti hai, chyme ka acid content kam karti\nhai, pancreatic enzymes ke liye alkaline medium deti hai. [Q744]\n● Bile juice 'alkaline medium' deti hai — stomach se aane wale acidic chyme ko neutralize karti hai,\npancreatic enzymes work karne ke liye suitable environment banati hai. [Q756]\n● Bile 'Gallbladder' mein store-concentrate hoti hai — liver dwara produce hoti hai, bile salts-\nphospholipids-cholesterol-bilirubin-electrolytes-water se bani hai. [Q765]\n● Bile juice 'Liver' se secrete hoti hai, gallbladder mein store hoti hai — fat digestion-absorption mein 2\nimportant functions perform karti hai. [Q774]\n● Digestion mein bile ka role hai 'fat ka emulsification' — bile acids large lipid droplets ko chhote mein\ntodte hain, surface area badhate hain digestive enzymes ke liye. [Q775]\n2. Stomach — HCl & Gastric Juice\n●\n Trap: Human stomach 'nitric acid' NAHI, 'Hydrochloric acid' (HCl) produce karta hai — HCl food\n⚠️\ndigest karne mein help karta hai, Vitamin B12 absorption ke liye zaroori hai. [Q729, Q777]\n● 'Pepsin' protein-splitting enzyme hai — inactive pepsinogen se HCl ki presence mein banta hai.\nPtyalin/Amylase carbohydrates, Lipase fats digest karta hai. [Q730]\n● Pepsin ko digestion mein action ke liye HCl (Hydrochloric acid) ki presence chahiye — chief cells\ninactive pepsinogen secrete karti hain, Parietal cells HCl secrete karti hain jo pH kam karke pepsinogen\nko activate karti hai. [Q739]"," ● 'Mucus' stomach ki inner lining ko uske apne acid se protect karta hai — gastric glands gastric juice\n(HCl + Pepsin + Mucus) secrete karti hain. [Q760]\n● Stomach ka shape English alphabet 'J' jaisa hai — digestive tube ka sabse wide part hai, food ko store-\nchurn-mix karta hai gastric juices ke saath. [Q761]\n●\n Trap: 'Stomach liver-pancreas ki secretions receive karta hai' — ye statement INCORRECT hai.\n⚠️\nActually SMALL INTESTINE (duodenum) liver (bile) aur pancreas (pancreatic juice) ki secretions receive\nkarta hai, stomach NAHI. [Q763]\n● Acid secretion stomach ki characteristic hai — Gastric acid (HCl) Parietal/oxyntic cells se secrete hoti\nhai, pepsinogen activate karti hai aur bacteria inactivate karti hai. [Q771]\n3. Small Intestine — Structure, Length & Digestion Completion\n● Small intestine 'Herbivores' (jaise Cow) mein Carnivores se lambi hoti hai — cellulose (grass mein)\ndigest karne mein zyada time lagta hai. [Q731, Q773, Q781]\n● Villi ki characteristics jo absorption enable karti hain: (i) finger-like structures with thin walls, (ii) large\nsurface area provide karte hain, aur blood vessels ka network close hota hai — villi mein pores\nabsorption ke liye NAHI hote. [Q734, Q747]\n● Herbivores jaise ghode-khargosh mein digested food ka cellulose 'Caecum' (large intestine ka pehla\npart) mein bacteria ki action se digest hota hai. [Q751]\n● Proteins ka amino acids mein, carbohydrates ka glucose mein, aur fats ka fatty acids mein final\nconversion 'Intestinal Juice' se hota hai — intestinal glands se secrete hoti hai (maltase, lactase, lipase,\nErepsin). [Q752]\n●\n Trap: 'Assimilation, ingestion se pehle aur absorption ke baad aata hai' — ye statement FALSE hai.\n⚠️\nSahi order: Ingestion → Digestion → Absorption → Assimilation → Egestion. [Q759]\n● Small intestine average adult human mein ~23 feet (7.5 meters) lambi hoti hai, highly coiled — liver-\npancreas se secretions leti hai, wall bhi juices secrete karti hai. [Q767]\n●\n Trap: 'Alveolar sac' human alimentary canal ka part NAHI hai — ye LUNGS (respiratory system) ka\n⚠️\npart hai. Alimentary canal mein Mouth, Oral cavity, Pharynx, Oesophagus, Stomach, Intestine, Anus\nshaamil hain. [Q776]\n● Carbohydrates, proteins aur fats ka complete digestion 'Small Intestine' mein hota hai — carbs\nglucose/fructose mein, proteins amino acids mein, fats fatty acids-glycerol mein todte hain. [Q784]\n4. Salivary Enzymes & Mouth Digestion\n● 'Amylase' saliva mein present digestive enzyme hai — salivary glands se produce hoti hai, starch aur\nfats digest karti hai. Enterokinase intestinal protein digestion enzyme hai, Peptidases peptide bonds\ncleave karti hain. [Q735]\n● Rice, potatoes, bread mein 'Carbohydrates' hoti hain — ye breakdown hokar 'Glucose' banti hain.\nSalivary amylase mouth mein starch ko maltose mein todta hai, phir disaccharides monosaccharides\nmein. [Q738]"," ● 'Buccal cavity' (oral cavity) human 'Digestion' system ka part hai — mastication (teeth se grinding) se\nmechanical digestion hoti hai. [Q742]\n● Salivary amylase (ptyalin) 'Starch' ko digest karne mein help karti hai — starch-glycogen ko glucose-\nmaltose mein todti hai, pancreatic juice aur saliva dono mein present hoti hai. [Q748]\n● 'Salivary amylase' (Ptyalin) starch ko simple sugar mein todne wala enzyme hai — 3 pairs of salivary\nglands se produce hoti hai: Parotids, Sub-maxillary, Sublinguals. [Q749]\n5. Areolar Tissue\n● 'Areolar tissue' — organs ke voids fill karta hai, internal organs ko support karta hai, aur tissue repair\nmein help karta hai — Adipose tissue fat store karta hai, Epithelial tissue surfaces cover karta hai.\n[Q733]\n6. Lymphatic System — Fat Transport\n● Lymph ke functions: digested fat ko intestine se carry karna, aur excess fluid extracellular space se\nblood mein drain karna — antibodies-lymphocytes bhi blood tak transport karta hai. [Q737]\n● Lymph intestinal 'Fats' transport karta hai (specifically absorbed fats) — colorless fluid jo lymphatic\nsystem mein circulate karta hai. [Q743]\n7. Dental Health & Teeth Structure\n● Dental caries se 'soft enamel' hota hai — Enamel outer covering hai, human body ka hardest\nsubstance. Dentine tissue hai crown se root tak, Tooth pulp mein blood vessels-nerves hote hain. [Q745]\n● Adult human mein 8 'Incisors' hote hain (4 upper + 4 lower) — total 32 teeth: 8 incisors, 4 canines, 8\npremolars, 12 molars (4 wisdom teeth samet). [Q757]\n● 'Teeth' calcium se bane hote hain — Calcium phosphate (Ca3(PO4)2) bones-milk-teeth mein milta hai,\nEnamel bones se bhi harder hota hai. [Q768]\n8. Smooth Muscle Organs\n● Smooth muscles wale organs: 'Iris of the eye, bronchi of lungs, ureters' — hollow visceral organs (liver,\npancreas, intestines) mein bhi hoti hain (heart ko chhodkar). Bones mein smooth muscles NAHI hoti.\n[Q740]\n9. Antacids — Indigestion Remedies\n● Indigestion ke dauran zyada acid stomach mein produce hota hai — iski pain dur karne ke liye log\n'bases' (antacids) use karte hain, jaise Milk of Magnesia. [Q741, Q754, Q780]"," 10. Ruminant & External Digestion\n● 'Rumen' stomach ka ek chamber hai jo food store karta hai — cows, goats, sheep, deer mein milta hai,\nmicrobes feed components ko usable energy-protein mein convert karte hain. [Q755, Q762]\n● 'Mushroom' body ke bahar food material breakdown karke digested food absorb karta hai —\nsaprotrophic nutrition. Amoeba holozoic nutrition dikhata hai (ingestion-digestion-absorption-\nassimilation-egestion). [Q758]\n11. The Pancreas — Islets of Langerhans\n● 'Islets of Langerhans' Pancreas mein milte hain — endocrine (hormone-producing) cells ke regions hain,\ninsulin-glucagon jaise hormones banate hain. [Q764]\n● 'Pancreas' blood mein sugar content regulate karta hai — endocrine function (insulin-glucagon) aur\nexocrine function (digestive enzymes) dono hoti hai. [Q766]\n12. Liver Functions & Digestive System Parts\n● Liver, toxic 'Ammonia' ko 'Urea' mein convert karta hai (urea cycle) — bile juice bhi secrete karta hai\n(bilirubin, biliverdin, cholesterol), jo gallbladder mein store hoti hai. [Q769]\n●\n Trap: 'Heart' digestive system ka part NAHI hai — ye CIRCULATORY system ka part hai. Digestive\n⚠️\nsystem mein mouth, buccal cavity, pharynx, oesophagus, stomach, intestines, rectum, anus shaamil\nhain. [Q770]\n● Liver ka function 'digestion' hai — bile secrete karke fats ka emulsification karta hai. Body ki largest\ngland hai (1.2-1.5 kg), abdominal cavity mein diaphragm ke neeche, 2 lobes. [Q772, Q778]\n13. Energy Storage & Release\n● Plants mein carbohydrates jo immediately use nahi hoti, unhe 'Starch' ki form mein store kiya jaata hai\n— potatoes, carrots, beets jaise plants roots-stems mein store karte hain. [Q779]\n● Food se derived energy ka kuch hissa 'Glycogen' ki form mein store hota hai — polysaccharide\ncompound hai, muscles-liver mein store hokar zaroorat par energy mein convert hota hai. [Q782]\n● Digestion ke end mein release hone wali energy 'Chemical energy' ki form mein hoti hai — molecules ke\nchemical bonds mein stored energy. [Q783]\n14. Match Lists — Digestive System Diagram & Functions\n● Match: Trachea → no digestion; Villi → absorb nutrients; Small intestine → length depends on food\norganism eats; Liver → helps emulsification (fats). [Q736]\n● Match: Mouth → intake of whole food; Teeth → chewing of food; Tongue → rolling of food; Saliva →\nswallowing of food. [Q753]"," Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 13 Digestive System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0379","t":"14 Nervous System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.14 — NERVOUS SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n🧠\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. The Brain — Overview & Three Main Parts\n2. Spinal Cord & Reflex Actions\n3. Neuron — Structure & Components\n4. The Synapse\n5. Hindbrain — Pons, Medulla & Involuntary Control\n6. EEG (Electroencephalogram) Test\n7. The Auditory Nerve\n8. Corpus Callosum\n9. Brain Weight & Physiology\n10. Nerve Cell (Neuron) Length\n11. The Cerebellum\n12. The Cerebrum\n13. Voluntary vs Involuntary Muscles\n14. Nodes of Ranvier\n1. The Brain — Overview & Three Main Parts\n● Human brain 3 major parts mein divide hai: Forebrain (complex cognitive activities, sensory-associative\nfunctions, voluntary motor activities), Midbrain (body-head movement), aur Hindbrain (breathing, blood\npressure, sneezing, swallowing). [Q785]\n● 'Fore-brain' brain ka main thinking part hai — voluntary actions, thinking aur information processing\nkarta hai. Midbrain eye-movement, auditory-visual processing karta hai. Hindbrain breathing-heart-blood\nvessels control karta hai. [Q811, Q816]\n● Brain body ka 'main' coordination center hai — voluntary movements, body balance, involuntary organs\n(lungs, heart, kidneys), thermoregulation, hunger-thirst, circadian rhythms control karta hai. [Q808]\n2. Spinal Cord & Reflex Actions\n● 'Spinal cord' nerve fibres se bana hota hai jo reflex actions mediate karte hain aur brain se impulses\ntransmit karte hain — Central Nervous System ka part hai, long-thin-tubular structure. [Q787]\n● 'Aag se haath khinch lena' — ye reflex action 'Spinal Cord' se control hota hai — Cerebrum conscious\nthought ke liye, Cerebellum balance-posture ke liye hota hai. [Q810]\n3. Neuron — Structure & Components\n● Neuron mein information 'Dendrite' mein acquire hoti hai — Dendrite electrical impulses ko cell body ki\ntaraf conduct karta hai, Axon impulses ko cell body se door le jaata hai. [Q788]\n●\n Trap: 'Cone' neuron ka part NAHI hai — ye EYE ka photoreceptor cell hai. Neuron ke 3 main parts:\n⚠️\nDendrites, Axon, Cell body (Soma). [Q791]\n● Neuron ka cell body 'Soma' (ya Perikaryon) kehlaata hai — macromolecules synthesis ka main site hai.\nSchwann cells myelin produce karti hain, Dendrons soma ki branch-like extensions hain. [Q793]"," ● 'Dendrons' Neuron ke parts hain — dendrites nerve impulses ko cell body ki taraf carry karti hain, Axon\nimpulses ko cell body se synapse tak carry karta hai. Nephron kidney ki unit hai. [Q796]\n4. The Synapse\n● 'Synapse' wo point hai jahan nervous impulse ek 'Neuron se doosre Neuron' tak pass hoti hai —\nNeurons nervous system ki basic units hain, types: Sensory, Motor, Interneurons. [Q789]\n● 2 neurons ke beech ki junction 'Synapse' kehlaati hai — presynaptic-postsynaptic neuron ki membranes\nse banti hai, electrical-chemical types hoti hain. [Q795]\n● Axon ending aur doosre nerve cell ke dendrite ke beech ki junction 'Synapse' kehlaati hai. [Q800]\n● 2 neurons ke beech ki space 'Synapse' kehlaati hai — Dendrite/Axon neuron ke hi parts hain, CSF\nplasma ka ultrafiltrate hai. [Q812]\n5. Hindbrain — Pons, Medulla & Involuntary Control\n● Vomiting jaisi involuntary action 'Hindbrain' (Rhombencephalon) control karta hai — medulla oblongata,\npons aur cerebellum se bana hota hai, respiratory rhythm-motor activity-sleep control karta hai. [Q786]\n● 'Pons' human brain ka part hai — Hindbrain mein Pons, Cerebellum, Medulla shaamil hain. Pons fibre\ntracts se bana hai jo brain regions ko interconnect karte hain. [Q790]\n● Involuntary actions (blood pressure, salivation, vomiting) 'Medulla' se control hoti hain — respiration,\ncardiac function, vasodilation, reflexes (swallowing-sneezing) bhi. [Q813, Q818]\n● Breathing 'Medulla' se regulate hoti hai — brainstem aur spinal cord ke beech connection hai,\nautonomic functions (breathing, heartbeat, digestion) regulate karta hai. [Q820]\n6. EEG (Electroencephalogram) Test\n● 'EEG' test 'Brain' ki ailments diagnose karne ke liye conduct hoti hai — scalp par electrodes lagakar\nepilepsy, sleep disorders, brain tumours diagnose karti hai. Hans Berger ne discover ki. [Q792]\n7. The Auditory Nerve\n● Human ear sound ki audible frequencies ko electric signals mein convert karke 'Auditory Nerve' se brain\ntak bhejta hai — cochlea (inner ear) se directly brain tak jaata hai. [Q794]\n8. Corpus Callosum\n● Mammals mein 'Corpus Callosum' 2 Cerebral Hemispheres ko connect karta hai — depth perceive\nkarne mein help karta hai, 4 parts mein divide hai: rostrum, genu, body, splenium. [Q797]"," 9. Brain Weight & Physiology\n● Brain ka weight ~1.4 kg hota hai, aur har minute 0.85 litres blood isse guzarta hai — 3 major parts:\nforebrain (cerebrum, thalamus, hypothalamus), midbrain, hindbrain. [Q798]\n● Human brain ka weight 1200-1400 grams hota hai — Adult male ~1370 grams, Adult female ~1200\ngrams. [Q809]\n10. Nerve Cell (Neuron) Length\n● Ek individual nerve cell 100 cm (1 meter) tak lambi ho sakti hai — neurons human body ki longest cells\nhain, longest axons sciatic nerves ke hote hain. [Q799]\n11. The Cerebellum\n● Cerebellum 'coordination of muscular movements' se related hai — Cerebrum conscious-unconscious\nmind, intelligence, memory control karta hai; Medulla oblongata involuntary actions (heartbeat,\nbreathing) control karta hai. [Q801]\n●\n Trap: Cerebellum ke 2 parts 'Cerebral hemispheres' NAHI kehlaate — inhe 'Cerebellar hemispheres'\n⚠️\n\nkehte hain. Cerebellum posterior region mein hai, hindbrain ka part hai, voluntary actions ki precision-\nposture-balance ke liye responsible. [Q806]\n●\n Trap: Cerebellum brain ka '25%' NAHI, sirf ~10-12% hota hai — voluntary actions ki precision aur\n⚠️\nposture-balance maintain karne ke liye responsible hai, hindbrain ka part hai. [Q807]\n● Cerebellum ('little brain') voluntary actions ki precision aur body ki posture-balance maintain karne ke\nliye responsible hai — spinal cord aur brain ke doosre parts se information receive karta hai. [Q819]\n12. The Cerebrum\n●\n Trap: Cerebrum 'two lateral cerebellar convolutions aur central vermix' se NAHI bana — ye\n⚠️\ndescription actually CEREBELLUM ki hai. Cerebrum forebrain ka part hai, brain ka largest part (~80%)\nhai. [Q802]\n●\n Trap: Cerebrum brain ka '60%' NAHI, ~80% constitute karta hai — forebrain ka part hai, 2 cerebral\n⚠️\nhemispheres hote hain, brain ka front-superior-lateral side banata hai. [Q803]\n●\n Trap: 'Cerebrum muscle activity coordinate karta hai' — ye statement INCORRECT hai. Muscle\n⚠️\nactivity coordination primarily CEREBELLUM ki responsibility hai (brain ke peeche located), Cerebrum\nthinking-memory-perception mein crucial role play karta hai. [Q805]\n13. Voluntary vs Involuntary Muscles"," ● Voluntary muscles (skeletal muscles) consciously control ho sakti hain (jaise frog ka jump karna,\nhandwriting) — Involuntary muscles bina soch ेwork karti hain (stomach mein food movement,\nheartbeat). [Q804]\n●\n Trap: 'Cycling' involuntary action NAHI hai — conscious choice aur muscle control chahiye.\n⚠️\nSalivation, respiration, digestion involuntary actions hain (medulla oblongata se control hoti hain). [Q814]\n●\n Trap: 'Heart ka beating' voluntary action NAHI hai — spinal cord se control hoti hai. Fist band karna,\n⚠️\nchair move karna, object uthaana voluntary actions hain (will/brain ke control mein). [Q817]\n14. Nodes of Ranvier\n● 'Nodes of Ranvier' myelinated axons mein microscopic gaps hote hain — Schwann cells ke beech\nchhote gaps hote hain, nerve impulse ki saltation allow karte hain. [Q815]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 14 Nervous System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0380","t":"15 Skeleton System","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.15 — SKELETON SYSTEM — FULL MIND MAP\n🦴\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Movement & Coordination\n2. Muscle Cramps & Anaerobic Respiration\n3. Human Skeleton - Bones & Structure\n4. Types of Bones\n5. Joints & Movements\n6. Bone Composition & Growth\n7. Axial & Appendicular Skeleton\n8. Muscular System\n9. Bone Disorders & Diseases\n10. Other Skeletal Facts\n11. Additional Facts — Joints, Muscles, Connective Tissue & Bones\n1. Movement & Coordination\n● Animal movement Muscular + Skeletal + Nervous systems ki coordinated activity hai. Muscles contract,\nbones lever ki tarah kaam karte hain, nerves signals bhejte hain. [Q821]\n2. Muscle Cramps & Anaerobic Respiration\n● 400m race ke baad cramps isliye hote hain kyunki intense exercise mein oxygen ki kami ho jati hai →\nanaerobic respiration → lactic acid accumulate hota hai muscles mein → pain/cramps. [Q822]\n● Aerobic respiration: glucose + oxygen → CO + water + energy. Anaerobic: glucose → lactic acid +\n₂\nenergy (kam). [Q822]\n3. Human Skeleton - Bones & Structure\n● Adult human skeleton mein 206 bones hain. Baby mein ~270 bones hote hain, kuch fuse ho jati hain.\n[Q823, Q824, Q825]\n● Human skeleton 2 divisions: Axial skeleton (skull, vertebral column, ribs, sternum - 80 bones) aur\nAppendicular skeleton (limbs, girdles - 126 bones). [Q826]\n● Skull 22 bones se bana hai. [Q827]\n● Vertebral column 26 bones (33 baby mein): 7 cervical, 12 thoracic, 5 lumbar, 1 sacrum, 1 coccyx. [Q828]\n● Rib cage: 12 pairs ribs (24) + sternum (1) = 25 bones. [Q829]\n4. Types of Bones\n● Long bones: limbs mein (humerus, femur) - leverage aur support. [Q830]\n● Short bones: wrist (carpals), ankle (tarsals) - stability aur limited movement. [Q830]"," ● Flat bones: skull, ribs, sternum - protection aur muscle attachment. [Q830]\n● Irregular bones: vertebrae, facial bones - complex shapes. [Q830]\n● Sesamoid bones: tendons ke andar (patella/kneecap) - friction protect karte hain. [Q830]\n5. Joints & Movements\n● Fixed joints (Immovable): skull bones (sutures). [Q831]\n● Slightly movable: vertebral column, pubic symphysis. [Q831]\n● Freely movable (Synovial): knee, elbow, shoulder, hip. [Q831]\n● Ball and socket joint: shoulder, hip - maximum movement. [Q832]\n● Hinge joint: knee, elbow - bending/straightening. [Q832]\n● Pivot joint: neck (atlas-axis) - rotation. [Q832]\n● Gliding joint: wrist, ankle - sliding movement. [Q832]\n● Saddle joint: thumb - 2 planes mein movement. [Q832]\n6. Bone Composition & Growth\n● Bone composition: Calcium phosphate (Ca (PO ) ) main mineral, collagen fibres, osteocytes (bone\n₃\n₄ ₂\ncells). [Q833, Q834]\n● Calcium aur Vitamin D bones ke liye essential hain. [Q833]\n● Bone growth: epiphyseal plates (growth plates) se hoti hai - long bones ke ends par. [Q835]\n● Osteoblasts: new bone form karte hain. Osteoclasts: old bone dissolve karte hain. Osteocytes: mature\nbone cells. [Q836]\n7. Axial & Appendicular Skeleton\n● Axial skeleton: central axis form karta hai - skull, hyoid, vertebral column, thoracic cage. [Q837]\n● Appendicular skeleton: limbs aur girdles - pectoral girdle (shoulder), pelvic girdle (hip), upper limbs,\nlower limbs. [Q837]\n8. Muscular System\n● 3 types of muscles: Skeletal (striated, voluntary), Smooth (non-striated, involuntary), Cardiac (striated,\ninvoluntary). [Q838]\n● Skeletal muscles: bones se attached, body movement. ~600 muscles human body mein. [Q838]\n● Smooth muscles: internal organs (stomach, intestine, blood vessels) - involuntary. [Q838]"," ● Cardiac muscle: heart - involuntary, striated, intercalated discs. [Q838]\n● Tendons: muscles ko bones se connect karte hain (dense connective tissue). [Q839]\n● Ligaments: bones ko bones se connect karte hain joints par (elastic connective tissue). [Q839]\n9. Bone Disorders & Diseases\n● Osteoporosis: bones weak aur brittle ho jati hain - calcium loss. Common in elderly/post-menopausal\nwomen. [Q840]\n● Arthritis: joints ka inflammation - pain, swelling, stiffness. Types: Osteoarthritis, Rheumatoid arthritis,\nGout. [Q841]\n● Rickets: children mein Vitamin D/calcium deficiency se bones soft aur weak ho jati hain. [Q842]\n● Osteomalacia: adults mein Vitamin D deficiency se bone softening. [Q842]\n● Fracture: bone break - simple, compound, comminuted, greenstick. [Q843]\n10. Other Skeletal Facts\n● Bone marrow: red marrow (blood cells produce karta hai) aur yellow marrow (fat store). [Q844]\n● Longest bone: Femur (thigh bone). Smallest bone: Stapes (ear mein). [Q845]\n● Strongest bone: Femur. [Q845]\n● Patella (kneecap): sesamoid bone, tendon mein located. [Q846]\n● X-rays bones ki imaging ke liye use hoti hain - dense structures (bones) white dikhte hain. [Q847]\n● cartilage: bones ke ends par, smooth movement aur shock absorption. [Q848]\n11. Additional Facts — Joints, Muscles, Connective Tissue & Bones\n● Middle ear ki 3 bones (ossicles): Hammer (Malleus), Anvil (Incus), aur Stirrup (Stapes) — sound wave\npressure variations amplify karke inner ear tak transmit karti hain. [Q849]\n● 'Synovial fluid' freely movable joints (synovial joints) mein milti hai — shoulders, hips, knees, elbows\nmein hoti hai, joint capsule hoti hai. Fibrous joints strong collagen tissue se, Cartilaginous joints cartilage\nse judte hain. [Q850]\n● 'Hedgehog' apne aap ko protect karne ke liye spines ka coat rakhta hai — spines hedgehogs, tenrecs,\nechidnas aur rodents mein milte hain. [Q851]\n● 'Rheumatism' body ke 'joints' ko affect karta hai — autoimmune-inflammatory disease hai, immune\nsystem joints lining cells ko attack karta hai, swelling-stiffness-pain hoti hai. [Q852]\n● Knee cap ko 'Patella' kehte hain — hind limb (leg) ki bones mein Femur (longest bone), Tibia, Fibula,\nPatella, Tarsals, Metatarsals, Phalanges shaamil hain. [Q853]\n● Human body ki sabse chhoti muscle 'Stapedius' hai — middle ear mein stapes bone se attached hoti\nhai. Pectoralis Major chest ki largest muscle, Tibialis leg ki largest muscle hai. [Q854]"," ● Biceps muscle 'Arm' mein hoti hai — shoulder aur elbow ke beech front upper arm mein large muscle\nhai. Cardiac muscle sirf heart mein, Visceral muscle intestines-blood vessels mein. [Q855]\n● 'Periodontics' dentistry ki branch hai — gum diseases (jo teeth ko support karne wali structures destroy\nkarti hain) treat karti hai. Gastroenterology stomach-intestine diseases, Orthopedics musculoskeletal\nsystem deal karta hai. [Q856]\n● 2 bones ko connect karne wala connective tissue 'Ligament' kehlaata hai — bone-to-bone connect karta\nhai, collagen-rich strong fibrous tissue hai. [Q857]\n● Bone cells 'Calcium (Ca) aur Phosphorus (P)' se bane hard matrix mein embedded hote hain —\ncortical/compact bone (hard, femur-tibia jaisi long bones), spongy/cancellous bone (marrow cavities\nmein) — 2 main types. [Q858]\n● 'Cartilage' joint par bone ki surface ko soft karta hai — Chondroblasts se produce hoti hai, nose-ear-\ntrachea-larynx mein bhi milti hai. [Q859]\n● Voluntary muscles 'hind limb' (legs) mein hoti hain — cylindrical fibers, bones-skin se attached, will\n(ichha) ke control mein. Examples: Diaphragm, pharynx, tongue, limb muscles. [Q860]\n● 'Tendon' muscle ko bones se connect karta hai — collagen se bani fibrous connective tissue hai.\nLigaments bone-to-bone connect karte hain, Cartilage joints-bones protect karti hai. [Q861]\n● Muscle/muscular tissue body mein 'movements' ke liye responsible hai — Striated (voluntary/skeletal),\nSmooth (involuntary), Cardiac (branched, single nucleus, heart mein) — 3 types. [Q862]\n● 'Bone' ek connective tissue hai — connective tissue animal ke 4 primary tissue types mein se ek hai\n(epithelial, muscle, nervous ke saath). Vascular bundles PLANTS mein milte hain (xylem-phloem).\n[Q863]\n● 'Ligament' bones ko connect karta hai — bones-joints-organs ko jagah par hold karta hai. Areolar\norgans ko connect-surround karta hai, Tendon muscles ko bones se, Cartilage joints-bones ko protect\nkarta hai. [Q864]\n● Muscle tissue ke 3 types hote hain: (1) Cardiac — heart ki walls mein, striated, involuntary; (2) Smooth\n— hollow visceral organs mein (heart chhodkar), spindle-shaped, involuntary; (3) Skeletal — skeleton se\nattached, voluntary movements. [Q865]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 15 Skeleton System Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0381","t":"16 Plant Kingdom","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.16 — PLANT KINGDOM — FULL MIND MAP\n🌿\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Bioremediation — Keeping the Environment Clean\n2. Tropism — Types of Directional Plant Growth\n3. Stomata & Gas Exchange\n4. Sclerenchyma — Hardness, Rigidity & Lignin\n5. Cork, Cutin & Waterproofing\n6. Meristematic Tissue & Differentiation\n7. Fermentation & Anaerobic Respiration — Cytoplasm\n8. Waste Products in Plants — Gums & Resins\n9. Vascular Tissue — Land Plant Adaptation\n10. Xylem — Components & Function\n11. Seeds — Plumule, Cotyledon & Parts\n12. Phloem — Sieve Plates & Food Transport\n13. Chlamydomonas — Respiration in Aquatic Algae\n14. Minerals for Pest Resistance\n15. Signs of Life — Movement, Growth & Respiration\n16. CAM Photosynthesis — Desert Plants\n17. Low Energy Needs of Plants\n18. Nitrogen Fixation — Rhizobia Symbiosis\n19. Angiosperms (Magnoliophyta)\n20. Succulent Plants\n21. Bryophyta — Examples & Characteristics\n22. Medicinal Plants — Sarpagandha & Arjuna\n23. Stinging & Carnivorous Plants\n24. Thallophyta — Undifferentiated Plant Body\n25. Potato — An Edible Underground Stem\n26. Marine Algae — Pigments\n27. Vascular vs Non-Vascular Plants\n28. Plant Families\n29. Petiole — Leaf Stalk\n30. Plant Kingdom Classification — Groups & Hierarchy\n31. Species — Taxonomic Definition\n31b. Halophytes — Plants Growing in Saline Water\n32. Multi-Coloured Leaves — Croton\n33. Fungi & Algae — Growth Without Sunlight\n34. Bacterial Flagella Arrangements\n35. Collenchyma — Flexibility\n36. Parenchyma — Loosely Packed Cells\n37. Root Hair\n38. Dicot vs Monocot — Roots, Cotyledons & Venation\n39. Rhizomes — Underground Stems\n40. Transpiration — Excess Water Removal\n41. Transpiration — Advantages & Disadvantages\n42. Plant Roots — Oxygen Absorption\n43. Monohybrid Cross\n44. Simple vs Complex Permanent Tissue\n45. Skin/Epidermal Cells\n46. Cuscuta — A Parasitic Plant\n47. Vegetative Parts of a Plant\n48. Cytokinins — Plant Hormone\n49. Vascular Tissue — Overall Transport in Trees\n50. Bryophyllum — Buds on Leaf Margins\n51. Fragmentation — Spirogyra\n1. Bioremediation — Keeping the Environment Clean"," ● 'Bacteria aur Fungi' environment ko clean rakhne mein help karte hain (Bioremediation) — Bacteria\n(Oleispira) oil spills clean karte hain, Fungi mycoremediation mein use hote hain. [Q866]\n2. Tropism — Types of Directional Plant Growth\n●\n Trap: Pollen tubes ka ovules ki taraf growth 'Chemotropism' hai, Geotropism NAHI — Sunflower\n⚠️\nphototropic hai, roots downward migration positive geotropism hai, Hydrotropism moisture ki taraf\ngrowth hai. [Q867]\n● Plant part light se 'door' grow karta hai to 'Negative Phototropism' kehte hain (roots mein), light ki taraf\ngrow karta hai to Positive Phototropism (stems mein). [Q979, Q992]\n● Plant organ ka growth stimulus ki taraf 'Positive Tropism' kehlaata hai — roots water/gravity ki taraf,\nstems light ki taraf. [Q983]\n● Gravity ki taraf plant part ka movement 'Gravitropism' (Geotropism) kehlaata hai — Phototropism light\nresponse, Hydrotropism water response, Chemotropism chemical stimulus response hai. [Q1003]\n3. Stomata & Gas Exchange\n● Leaves mein 'Stomata' mein respiration ke dauran massive gas exchange hoti hai — microscopic pores\nhain. Grana photosynthesis light reactions ka site hai, Thylakoids chloroplast ki internal membranes\nhain. [Q869]\n● Guard cells water absorb karke swell hoti hain (turgid banti hain), jisse Stomata open hoti hain — water\nlose karne par flaccid hokar stomata close ho jaati hain. [Q871]\n●\n Trap: 'Intracellular spaces' transpiration ka main site NAHI hai — Stomata, Cuticle aur Lenticels\n⚠️\ntranspiration ke main types (stomatal, cuticular, lenticular) hain. [Q875]\n● Big plants-trees ke hard stem mein gaseous waste 'Lenticels' se remove hoti hai — porous tissues hain\njo woody stems mein gas exchange allow karte hain. [Q876]\n● Raat mein photosynthesis nahi hoti, isliye 'Carbon dioxide' removal main gas exchange hai — plants din\nmein CO2 lete hain-O2 dete hain, raat mein O2 lete hain-CO2 dete hain. [Q877]\n● Din ke time plants mein major event 'O2 release' hai — Photosynthesis equation: 6CO2 + 6H2O +\nSunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2. [Q890]\n4. Sclerenchyma — Hardness, Rigidity & Lignin\n● Coconut husk ko hard-stiff banane wali tissue 'Sclerenchyma' hai — dead cells, thick lignified walls wali\nsimple permanent tissue hai. [Q870, Q945, Q974]\n● Sclerenchyma plant ko hard-stiff banata hai — dead cells, highly thickened lignified walls, coconut husk,\nstems, vascular bundles, leaf veins mein milta hai. [Q922, Q955]\n● Sclerenchyma cells ki wall 'Lignin' se thick hoti hai — rigidity deta hai, bacterial infections rokta hai. 3\ntypes ground tissue: parenchyma, collenchyma, sclerenchyma. [Q927, Q932]"," ● Sclerenchyma tissue 'dead cells' se bani hoti hai — mechanical stiffness-strength deti hai, fibers-\nsclereids main cell types hain. Aerenchyma gas exchange, Parenchyma food storage karti hai. [Q948,\nQ957, Q965]\n●\n Trap: Sclerenchyma diagrams alag dikh sakte hain — Transverse section (A) mein polygonal cells\n⚠️\nuniform thickening ke saath, Longitudinal section (B) mein long-narrow-pointed cells dikhte hain. [Q887]\n5. Cork, Cutin & Waterproofing\n● Cork water-gases ke liye impermeable hoti hai 'Suberin' ki wajah se — wax-like fatty substance hai cork\ncell walls mein, water-solutes ke against barrier banata hai. [Q872]\n● Desert plants ki epidermis par 'Cutin' ka thick waxy coating hota hai — transpiration se water loss\nprevent karta hai, desert survival ke liye crucial hai. [Q935, Q1001]\n6. Meristematic Tissue & Differentiation\n● Meristematic tissue cells division ability lose karke permanent shape-size-function lete hain — is\nprocess ko 'Differentiation' kehte hain. Dedifferentiation permanent cells wapas divide karne lagti hain.\n[Q873, Q959]\n● 'Meristematic tissue' hi cell division ke capable hoti hai — growing regions mein hoti hai. Types: Apical\n(length), Lateral (girth), Intercalary (internode size). [Q934]\n● Meristematic tissue ke cells isolate hokar different permanent tissue banate hain — constant cell\ndivision, specialized cells mein differentiate hoti hai. [Q950]\n● 'Intercalary meristems' leaves ke bottom (base) mein milte hain — nodes-internodes mein elongation\npromote karte hain, grasses-monocots mein leaf primordia base par. [Q956]\n● Meristem tissue root tip ya shoot tip mein milti hai — plant growth ke liye responsible hai, actively divide\nhokar naye cells produce karti hai. [Q966]\n● Anterior (apical) meristem stem-root ke apex (growing crest) mein milta hai — length badhaane ka\nfunction hai. [Q972, Q973]\n● Lateral meristematic tissue ring-shaped form mein stems mein milti hai, plant ki growth mein help karti\nhai — girth-thickness badhaati hai (cambium is category ka specific type hai). [Q986]\n7. Fermentation & Anaerobic Respiration — Cytoplasm\n● Yeast fermentation aur human muscle cells ki anaerobic respiration mein similarity — dono 'Cytoplasm'\nmein hoti hain. Yeast ethanol+CO2 banati hai, muscles lactic acid. [Q874]\n● Yeast fermentation mein Pyruvate 'Ethanol aur Carbon dioxide' mein convert hota hai — glycolysis ke\nend mein pyruvate banta hai, aerobic respiration CO2+water banati hai. [Q882]\n8. Waste Products in Plants — Gums & Resins"," ● Tall tree apne waste products 'old xylem (heartwood)' mein store karta hai — gums-resins ki tarah,\nkyunki purani inner xylem ab water transport nahi karti. [Q888, Q883]\n● Acacia jaise trees ka gum ek 'waste product' hai — metabolic processes ka byproduct hai, gums-oils-\nlatex-resins old xylem tissues mein store hote hain. [Q889, Q894]\n●\n Trap: Plants leaves se 'toxic substances filter' NAHI karte — ye recognized excretion process nahi\n⚠️\nhai. Plants transpiration, stomata diffusion, old xylem storage, vacuole storage, aur soil mein excretion\nse waste nikalte hain. [Q885]\n● Sahi statement: 'Kuch plants mein waste products resins ki tarah store hote hain' — plants soil mein\nwaste excrete karte hain, excess water transpiration se nikalti hai (translocation se NAHI), O2\nphotosynthesis ka waste product hai. [Q886]\n9. Vascular Tissue — Land Plant Adaptation\n● Vascular tissue (Xylem-Phloem) complex plants ki distinctive feature hai — water-minerals-food ka long-\ndistance efficient transport, terrestrial environments mein survival possible banata hai. [Q884]\n10. Xylem — Components & Function\n●\n Trap: 'Xylem fibres' water transport nahi karti — mechanical support deti hain. Xylem vessels-\n⚠️\ntracheids main water-conducting elements hain, xylem parenchyma starch store karti hai. [Q891]\n●\n Trap: 'Sieve tubes' Xylem ka part NAHI hai — Phloem ka part hai. Xylem parts: tracheids, vessels,\n⚠️\nxylem parenchyma, xylem fibers. [Q933]\n● Xylem 'roots se materials transport away' karta hai — water-materials upward transport karta hai. [Q970]\n●\n Trap: 'Sieve tube ki cell non-living hoti hai' wali baat FALSE hai — companion cells living hoti hain jo\n⚠️\n\nsugars sieve elements mein load karne mein help karti hain. Xylem 4 components se banta hai:\ntracheids, vessels, xylem parenchyma, xylem fibers (ye statement TRUE hai). [Q996]\n● 'Xylem' example hai permanent tissue ka — meristematic tissue se derive hoti hai, division ability lose\nkar chuki hai. Blood/Bone/Skin animal tissues hain. [Q978]\n● Xylem 'complex permanent' tissue hai — vessels, tracheids, parenchyma, fibers se milkar bani hoti hai,\nwater-minerals roots se upward transport karti hai. [Q991]\n11. Seeds — Plumule, Cotyledon & Parts\n● 'Plumule' (embryonic shoot) seed mein milta hai — germination par shoot system (stem-leaves) banata\nhai. Radicle root system banata hai. [Q892]\n● 'Cotyledons' plant seeds mein food store ki tarah kaam karte hain — embryo ka part hain, germination\npar pehli leaves ban jaate hain. [Q926]\n● Seed ke 3 parts: 'Cotyledons, radicle aur Coleoptile' — seed coat aur embryo (radicle+embryonal\naxis+1-2 cotyledons) se bana hota hai. Coleoptile monocot ki pehli leaf hai. [Q975]"," 12. Phloem — Sieve Plates & Food Transport\n● Sieve plates par 'Phloem tube tissue' available hoti hai — porous end walls jo sieve tube elements ko\ncontinuous sieve tube mein connect karti hain, organic nutrients transport karti hain. [Q893]\n● Phloem 'photosynthetic parts se material away' transport karti hai — bidirectional vascular tissue hai,\norganic nutrients leaves se doosre parts tak le jaati hai. [Q929]\n● Phloem plants mein 'food' ke transport ke liye responsible hai — parenchyma, fibers, sieve tubes,\ncompanion cells se bani hoti hai. [Q931]\n● Phloem 'food ka conduction' karta hai — 5 cell types se bana hai: sieve cells, sieve tubes, companion\ncells, phloem fibers, phloem parenchyma (fibers chhodkar sabhi living hote hain). [Q947]\n13. Chlamydomonas — Respiration in Aquatic Algae\n● Chlamydomonas jaise unicellular algae 'dissolved oxygen ko diffusion se absorb' karte hain (jaise\nAmoeba) — freshwater-seawater mein rehte hain, specialized respiratory organs nahi hote. [Q895]\n14. Minerals for Pest Resistance\n● 'Potassium, Calcium aur Magnesium' crops ko pests withstand karne mein help karte hain — Potassium\ngrowth-metabolism, Calcium drought-heat-disease tolerance, Magnesium phosphate metabolism-\nenzyme activation mein help karte hain. [Q896]\n15. Signs of Life — Movement, Growth & Respiration\n● 'Kisi bhi kism ki movement, growth ya respiration' existence ka common proof hai — living organisms ki\nfundamental characteristics: movement, respiration, sensitivity, growth, reproduction, excretion, nutrition.\n[Q897]\n16. CAM Photosynthesis — Desert Plants\n● 'Desert plants' raat mein CO2 lete hain aur intermediate acid banate hain, jisse din mein chlorophyll\nenergy use hoti hai — CAM (Crassulacean Acid Metabolism), stomata din mein closed rehti hai water\nloss minimize karne ke liye. [Q898]\n17. Low Energy Needs of Plants\n● Plants ki energy needs animals se kam hoti hain kyunki: mobility ki absence hai, aur unka body ka bada\nhissa dead supportive tissues (xylem-sclerenchyma) se bana hota hai jo metabolic energy maintenance\nke liye nahi chahiye. [Q899]"," 18. Nitrogen Fixation — Rhizobia Symbiosis\n●\n Trap: 'Ficus' rhizobia bacteria ke saath symbiotic relationship NAHI banata, isliye nitrogen fix nahi\n⚠️\nkarta — Lentils, Chickpeas, Peanuts legumes (Fabaceae) hain jo root nodules banakar nitrogen fix karte\nhain. [Q900]\n19. Angiosperms (Magnoliophyta)\n● 'Magnoliophyta' flowering plants hain jinhe 'Angiosperms' bhi kehte hain — seeds ovary (fruit) ke andar\nenclosed hote hain. Gymnosperms naked seeds, Pteridophytes spores, Bryophytes non-vascular hote\nhain. [Q901]\n20. Succulent Plants\n●\n Trap: Succulent plants mein 'no leaves' universal feature NAHI hai — generally leaves hoti hain\n⚠️\n(thick-fleshy, water retain karne ke liye). Examples: Aloe Vera, Snake Plant, Jade Plant — drought-\nresistant, stems-roots present hote hain. [Q902]\n21. Bryophyta — Examples & Characteristics\n● Bryophyta (non-vascular land plants — liverworts, hornworts, mosses) ke examples: Marchantia, Riccia,\nFunaria — Deodar Gymnosperm hai, Marsilea Pteridophyta hai, Cladophora Algae hai. [Q903, Q946,\nQ1000]\n● Bryophytes 'plant kingdom ke amphibians' kehlaate hain — soil mein rehte hain lekin sexual\nreproduction ke liye water par depend karte hain, mosses-liverworts is group mein aate hain. [Q1006]\n● Rhizoids (Bryophytes ki lower epidermal cells se protuberances) ke baare mein:\n Trap: 'Rhizoids ke\n⚠️\nfully developed stem-root-leaves hote hain' — ye INCORRECT statement hai, actually rhizoids mein ye\ndeveloped structures NAHI hote. [Q977]\n● 'Rhizoids' Bryophytes ki lower epidermal cells se extend hote hain — thin hair-like structures, plant ko\nanchor karte hain aur water-nutrients absorb karte hain. [Q980]\n● Group jinke plants roots-stem-leaves nahi rakhte, unhe 'Thallus' kehte hain — Thallus wale plants mein\nphotosynthesis-reproduction-nutrient absorption directly undifferentiated body se hota hai. [Q976]\n22. Medicinal Plants — Sarpagandha & Arjuna\n● 'Sarpagandha' (Rauvolfia serpentina) blood pressure treat karta hai — asthma-insomnia bhi treat karta\nhai, sub-Himalayan forests mein grow karta hai. [Q904]\n● Arjuna tree ki bark 'Heart Disease' treat karne ke liye use hoti hai — coronary artery disease, heart\nfailure, edema, angina, asthma treat karti hai. [Q912]"," 23. Stinging & Carnivorous Plants\n● 'Nettle' plant mein stinging hair hote hain jo touch karne par painful stings dete hain — wild mein grow\nkarta hai. [Q905]\n●\n Trap: 'Tiger Lily' carnivorous plant NAHI hai — herbaceous perennial hai. Carnivorous plants:\n⚠️\nSundew, Corkscrew, Monkeycup, Venus flytrap, Pitcher plant. [Q906]\n24. Thallophyta — Undifferentiated Plant Body\n● Spirogyra mein plant body root-stem-leaves mein differentiate NAHI hota — free-floating green algae\nhai freshwater mein. [Q907, Q914, Q924]\n● Marsilea mein specialised vascular tissue hoti hai water-substances conduct karne ke liye —\nMoss/Riccia/Chara mein vascular tissue nahi hoti (Chara green algae hai, plant NAHI). [Q915]\n● 'Thallophyta' group ko commonly Algae kehte hain — primitive plant life, unicellular se lekar large algae-\nfungi-lichens tak range karti hai. [Q940, Q961, Q964]\n● Lichen plant 'Thallophyta' division ka hai — primitive forms, undifferentiated body. [Q969, Q971, Q967]\n● Plants jinka body differentiated NAHI hota, wo 'Thallophyta' group mein aate hain — non-vascular plants\n(algae, fungi, lichens), undifferentiated body 'thallus' kehlaata hai. [Q1004]\n25. Potato — An Edible Underground Stem\n● Potato ka edible part 'Stem' hai — potatoes special underground stems (tubers) hote hain. Binomial\nname: Solanum tuberosum. Doosre stem vegetables: onion, ginger, garlic, turmeric. [Q908]\n26. Marine Algae — Pigments\n● Marine Algae ka 'Green' color 'Chlorophyll' pigment se hota hai — Phycocyanin cyanobacteria mein\nblue pigment, Zeaxanthin carotenoid hai, Beta Carotene yellow-orange-red color deta hai. [Q909]\n27. Vascular vs Non-Vascular Plants\n● 'Bryophytes' plants hain jinme vascular system nahi hota — Pteridophytes-Tracheophytes vascular\ntissue rakhte hain (xylem-phloem). [Q910, Q984]\n● Vessels (water conducting cells) mainly 'Angiosperms' mein milte hain — long cylindrical tube-like\nstructures, lignified walls, large central cavity. [Q953]\n● 'Gymnosperms' ke paas specialised water-conducting tissue hoti hai — vascular plants hain, ovules\novary wall se enclosed nahi hote (naked seeds). [Q968]"," 28. Plant Families\n● 'Touch-me-not' (Mimosa pudica) plant 'Mimosaceae' family ka hai — Cyperaceae grass family,\nAcanthaceae Justicia family, Malvaceae Hibiscus family hai. [Q911]\n29. Petiole — Leaf Stalk\n● 'Petiole' ek tree (plant) ka part hai — leaf blade ko leaf base se connect karne wali stalk hai, xylem ke\nthrough roots se leaf tak water-nutrients transport karta hai. [Q913]\n30. Plant Kingdom Classification — Groups & Hierarchy\n●\n Trap: 'Arthropoda' plant group NAHI hai — ye animal phylum hai (insects, spiders, crustaceans).\n⚠️\nPlant groups: Thallophyta, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperms, Angiosperms. [Q916]\n● Plant classification hierarchy: Kingdom → Division → Class → Order → Family → Genus → Species.\n[Q943]\n● 'Gymnosperms' naked seeds produce karte hain (fruit mein enclosed nahi hote) — examples: Pinus,\nCycas, Araucaria, Thuja, Cedrus, Picea. [Q952]\n● 3 types ke simple permanent tissues: 'Parenchyma, Collenchyma aur Sclerenchyma' — Parenchyma\nfood store, Collenchyma flexibility, Sclerenchyma structural hardness deti hai. Phloem complex tissue\nhai. [Q982]\n● 'Phanerogams' seed-producing plants hain (gymnosperms + angiosperms) — well-differentiated\nreproductive tissues rakhte hain jo seeds banate hain. Cryptogams spores se reproduce karte hain.\n[Q990]\n● Pteridophyta mein 'flowers' NAHI hote — vascular plants hain jinme true roots-stems-leaves hote hain,\nspores se reproduce karte hain (fern, horsetail examples). [Q987, Q989]\n● Cedar (gymnosperm) mein 'uncoated' (naked) seeds milte hain — fruit mein enclosed nahi hote, cones-\nscales ki surface par expose hote hain. Marsilea Pteridophyta hai (spores se reproduce). [Q944]\n● 'Gymnosperms' commonly 'exposed' type ke seeds ke liye jaane jaate hain — 'naked seed' ka matlab\nhai, ovary/fruit mein enclosed nahi hote, cones (strobili) par bante hain. [Q985]\n31. Species — Taxonomic Definition\n● Genetically distinct aur reproductively isolated similar organisms ka group 'Species' kehlaata hai —\nFamily related genera ka group hai, Class related orders ka group hai. [Q917]\n31b. Halophytes — Plants Growing in Saline Water\n● Saline water mein grow karne wale plants 'Halophytes' kehlaate hain — examples: mangroves, saltwort,\npickleweed. Xerophytes dry environments mein, Hydrophytes water mein grow karte hain. [Q962]"," 32. Multi-Coloured Leaves — Croton\n● 'Croton' (Euphorbiaceae) plant mein multi-coloured leaves hoti hain — multiple pigments (Chlorophyll,\nCarotenoid, Anthocyanin) alag-alag wavelengths absorb karte hain. [Q918]\n33. Fungi & Algae — Growth Without Sunlight\n● Fungi paani mein sunlight ki absence mein grow kar sakte hain — eukaryotic organisms (yeasts,\nmoulds, mushrooms) hain, Algae photosynthetic organisms hain. [Q919]\n34. Bacterial Flagella Arrangements\n● Bacterium mein flagella dono ends par ho to use 'Amphitrichous' kehte hain — Peritrichous flagella pure\nbody mein, Monotrichous single polar flagellum hota hai. [Q920]\n35. Collenchyma — Flexibility\n● Plants mein flexibility 'Collenchyma' tissue se hoti hai — bending allow karta hai bina toote, tendrils-\nclimbers mein hota hai. Living cells, corners par irregularly thickened. [Q921, Q988, Q995]\n36. Parenchyma — Loosely Packed Cells\n● 'Parenchyma' cells loosely packed hote hain, large intercellular spaces hote hain — food store karti hai\n(chlorenchyma-aerenchyma isi mein aate hain). [Q923, Q937, Q954, Q960]\n● Parenchyma tissue 'relatively unspecialised cells with thin walls' se bani hoti hai — cellulose se bane\nthin cell walls, living cells, ground tissue ka bulk banati hai. [Q938]\n37. Root Hair\n● Root cells ke long hair-like parts 'Root hair' kehlaate hain — fine, thread-like structures, epidermal cells\nse project hote hain, surface area badhaate hain water-minerals absorption ke liye. [Q930]\n38. Dicot vs Monocot — Roots, Cotyledons & Venation\n●\n Trap: 'Fibrous root' dicotyledonous plants ki property NAHI hai — monocots ki characteristic hai\n⚠️\n(maize, grass, wheat). Dicots (gram, neem) tap root, 2 cotyledons, reticulate venation rakhte hain.\n[Q939]"," ● Kalmi (Water spinach) jaise plants ke seeds mein 'two cotyledons' hote hain (dicotyledon) — apples,\nmangoes, peas doosre examples. Ulva algae, Cedar-Pine gymnosperms hain. [Q942]\n● 'Garlic' ek monocot plant hai — sirf ek cotyledon hota hai. Doosre monocots: sugarcane, banana,\ndaffodils, palm. [Q949]\n● 'Dicotyledon plants' angiosperms hain jinke seeds mein 2 cotyledons hote hain — Monocots (maize,\ngrass) mein sirf 1 cotyledon hota hai. [Q981]\n● 'Paphiopedilum' (Venus slipper orchid) ek monocot hai — Orchidaceae family monocots ki hai.\nMonocots mein 1 seed leaf (cotyledon) hota hai. [Q994]\n39. Rhizomes — Underground Stems\n● 'Ginger' Rhizome ka classic example hai — horizontal underground stem, shoot-root systems produce\nkarta hai. Doosre examples: bamboo, turmeric, lotus, asparagus. [Q941]\n40. Transpiration — Excess Water Removal\n● Plants excess water 'Transpiration' se remove karte hain — leaf surface (stomata) se water vapour\nevaporate hota hai. [Q936]\n41. Transpiration — Advantages & Disadvantages\n● Transpiration ke advantages: cooling effect, excess water removal, mineral transport, turgidity maintain,\nphotosynthesis ke liye water supply —\n Disadvantage: rate absorption se zyada hone par 'wilting' ho\n⚠️\nsakti hai. [Q881]\n● Roots plants ko water-mineral ions transport karne mein: pehle 'Ions active transport se enter karte\nhain', phir 'Water concentration gradient ke along follow karta hai' — energy use hoti hai ion transport\nmein. [Q880]\n42. Plant Roots — Oxygen Absorption\n● Plant roots 'soil particles ke beech ki air spaces' se oxygen lete hain — respiration ke liye zaroori hai.\nRoot types: Tap Root, Fibrous Root — Functions: Absorption, Anchoring, Storage. [Q879]\n43. Monohybrid Cross\n● Monohybrid cross 2 plants ko combine karta hai jinke trait ke 'do' (two) different versions hote hain —\nhomozygous genotypes wale individuals ka genetic mix hota hai. [Q878]"," 44. Simple vs Complex Permanent Tissue\n●\n Trap: 'Xylem' simple permanent tissue NAHI hai — Xylem-Phloem complex permanent tissues hain\n⚠️\n(multiple cell types se bani). Sclerenchyma, Parenchyma, Collenchyma simple permanent tissues hain.\n[Q925]\n● 'Xylem' complex permanent tissue hai — sirf ek cell type se nahi bani (tracheids, vessels, xylem\nparenchyma, xylem fibers ka mix hai). Phloem bhi complex hai. [Q928, Q993]\n● 'Complex tissue' alag-alag cell types se milkar same function perform karti hai (jaise xylem-phloem) —\nMeristematic tissue constantly divide karti hai, Epidermal tissue protective covering hai. [Q963]\n● 'Parenchyma aur Collenchyma' — dono living cells hoti hain. Sclerenchyma dead cells se bani\npermanent tissue hai jo plant ko hard-stiff banati hai. [Q951]\n45. Skin/Epidermal Cells\n● Skin (aerial plant parts) 'Epidermal cells' se bani hoti hai — waxy water-resistant layer secrete karti hai,\nprotection deti hai water loss-mechanical injury-fungi se. [Q958]\n46. Cuscuta — A Parasitic Plant\n● 'Cuscuta' (Dodder/Amarbel) parasitic plant hai — chlorophyll-leaves nahi hoti, yellow-coloured climber\nhai, haustoria banakar host plant ke phloem se nutrition leta hai. [Q997]\n47. Vegetative Parts of a Plant\n● Plant ke vegetative parts hain 'Roots, stems aur leaves' — directly sexual reproduction mein involve\nnahi hote, asexual reproduction (cuttings, budding, grafting) mein use hote hain. [Q998]\n48. Cytokinins — Plant Hormone\n● 'Cytokinins' plants mein cell division promote karte hain — roots-shoot systems mein, naye leaves-\nchloroplasts formation, lateral shoot growth mein bhi help karte hain. [Q999]\n49. Vascular Tissue — Overall Transport in Trees\n● Trees mein materials ki transportation 'Vascular tissue' (Xylem+Phloem) se hoti hai — Xylem water-\nnutrients upward, Phloem food doosre parts tak transport karta hai. [Q1002]\n50. Bryophyllum — Buds on Leaf Margins"," ● 'Bryophyllum' (Crassulaceae family) ki leaf margins ke notches mein buds produce hote hain —\nvegetative propagation ke liye plantlet buds banata hai. Rose stem cutting se propagate hota hai.\n[Q1005]\n51. Fragmentation — Spirogyra\n● 'Spirogyra' (Water Silk) green algae fragmentation se asexually reproduce karta hai — Yeast-Hydra\nbudding se reproduce karte hain. [Q1007]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 16 Plant Kingdom Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0382","t":"17 Animal Kingdom","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.17 — ANIMAL KINGDOM — FULL MIND MAP\n🐾\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Amoeba — Feeding & Pseudopodia\n2. Parasitic Nutrition — Without Killing the Host\n3. Fish — External Structure & Fins\n4. Malpighian Tubules — Arthropoda\n5. Metamorphosis\n6. Algae as Space Food\n7. Invertebrates vs Vertebrates\n8. The 5-Kingdom Classification — Animalia/Monera/Protista\n9. Cartilaginous Fish\n10. Saprophytic Fungi — Penicillium\n11. Taxonomic Hierarchy\n12. Arthropoda — Largest Group with Jointed Legs\n13. Cnidaria — Corals\n14. Mammals — Heart & Characteristics\n15. Mollusca\n16. Pisces — Characteristics\n17. Regeneration — Earthworm\n18. Animal Breeds — Goats\n19. Warm-Blooded vs Cold-Blooded Animals\n20. Ultrasound — Echolocation\n21. Annelida\n22. Reptile — Heart Structure\n23. Epithelium Types\n24. Connective Tissue — Ligament, Tendon & Areolar\n25. Adipose Tissue\n26. Aves — Birds\n27. Echinodermata — Free-Living Marine Animals\n28. Porifera — Immobile Sponges\n29. Planaria — Simple Eyes (Eyespots)\n30. Reptile Skin\n31. Mammal Skin\n32. True Marine Fish — Dog Fish\n33. Amphibia\n34. Match List — Body Tissues\n35. Egg-Laying Mammals — Monotremes\n36. Hydra — Reproduction by Budding\n37. Diploblastic vs Triploblastic Animals\n1. Amoeba — Feeding & Pseudopodia\n● Amoeba apni 'entire body surface area' se food leta hai — pseudopodia food particle ke around push\nkarke usse engulf karta hai. Paramecium cilia se food leta hai. [Q1008]\n● Pseudopodia (finger-like extensions) 'Amoeba' mein hote hain — cell membrane ke temporary\nprojections, movement aur food catching ke liye. Amoeba constantly shape change karta rehta hai.\n[Q1016]\n2. Parasitic Nutrition — Without Killing the Host"," ● 'Louse, tapeworm, leech, dodder' — group hai jo doosre plants-animals se nutrition leta hai bina unhe\nmaare — Parasites host se nutrients extract karte hain. Types: Ectoparasites, Endoparasites, Meso\nParasites. [Q1009]\n● Tapeworm life cycle mein 'Pig' host hota hai (pork tapeworm/Taenia solium ke liye) — tapeworms\nPlatyhelminthes phylum mein hain, proglottids add karke grow karte hain. [Q1026]\n● 'Tapeworm' endoparasite ka example hai — host ke andar tissues-organs mein rehta hai. Ectoparasites\n(ticks, lice, fleas) skin ki superficial layers ko infect karte hain. [Q1027]\n3. Fish — External Structure & Fins\n● Fish diagram mein Gills (Position 1) respiration ke liye hote hain — Dorsal Fins rolling se protect karte\nhain, Pectoral Fins directional movement, Pelvic Fin stabilize karta hai. [Q1010]\n4. Malpighian Tubules — Arthropoda\n● 'Malpighian tubules' Arthropoda ki characteristic hai — excretory structures hain (lobsters, crabs,\nspiders, insects, centipedes mein). Echinodermata mein Starfish, Annelida mein Earthworms hain.\n[Q1011]\n5. Metamorphosis\n● Silk worms aur frog larvae ka adult mein transformation 'Metamorphosis' kehlaata hai — drastic rapid\nphysical changes birth ke kuch samay baad hoti hain. [Q1012]\n6. Algae as Space Food\n● 'Spirulina aur Chlorella' algae protein-rich hain, space travellers ke food supplements ki tarah use hote\nhain — Chlorella 30% proteins-30% carbs, Spirulina protein-Vitamin B ka richest source hai. [Q1013]\n7. Invertebrates vs Vertebrates\n●\n Trap: 'Reptiles' invertebrates mein SHAAMIL NAHI hain — reptiles vertebrates hain (backbone hota\n⚠️\nhai). Invertebrates: molluscs, arachnids, insects (koi backbone nahi). [Q1014]\n8. The 5-Kingdom Classification — Animalia/Monera/Protista\n● 'Metazoa' Kingdom Animalia mein classify hote hain — sabhi multicellular animals (sponges chhodkar),\nheterotrophic hote hain. 5 Kingdoms: Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia. [Q1015]"," ●\n Trap: 'Protozoa' Whittaker ke 5-Kingdom classification ka part NAHI hai — ye Protista kingdom ka\n⚠️\nsub-category hai. 5 Kingdoms: Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia (R.H. Whittaker, 1969).\n[Q1033]\n● Whittaker classification mein 'Monera' group mein fully developed nucleus NAHI hota — prokaryotic\nhain (bacteria, blue-green algae), naked DNA. Baaki 4 kingdoms eukaryotic hain. [Q1034]\n● 'Monera' group unicellular prokaryotic organisms (bina central membrane ke) hain jaise bacteria — 70s\nribosomes, naked DNA, peptidoglycan cell wall. [Q1052]\n● Multicellular organisms bina cell wall ke 'Animalia' kingdom mein aate hain — Plantae cellulose wall,\nFungi chitin wall, Monera peptidoglycan wall rakhte hain. [Q1063]\n●\n Trap: 'Diatom' Monera se related NAHI hai — ye eukaryotic hai, Kingdom Protista mein aata hai.\n⚠️\nMonera mein sirf prokaryotes (bacteria, Cyanobacteria/Anabaena, Archaebacteria) hote hain. [Q1073]\n9. Cartilaginous Fish\n● 'Shark' cartilaginous fish (Chondrichthyes) hai — skeleton cartilage se bana hota hai (Skates, Rays,\nChimaeras bhi). Bony fish (Osteichthyes) mein Tuna, Rohu, Salmon aate hain. [Q1017]\n10. Saprophytic Fungi — Penicillium\n● 'Penicillium' saprophytic fungus hai — dead-decaying organic matter se nutrition leta hai (molds,\nmushrooms, yeast, mucor bhi). Penicillin isi se derive hoti hai (antibacterial drug). [Q1018]\n11. Taxonomic Hierarchy\n● 'Genus' Family aur Species ke beech ka classification level hai — hierarchy: Domain > Kingdom >\nPhylum > Class > Order > Family > Genus > Species. Carolus Linnaeus 'Father of taxonomy' hain.\n[Q1019]\n● Animal classification ki hierarchy: Kingdom > Phylum > Class > Order > Family > Genus > Species —\nCarolus Linnaeus ne establish ki, broad se specific tak. [Q1037]\n12. Arthropoda — Largest Group with Jointed Legs\n● 'Arthropod' phylum ke animals ke jointed legs hote hain — largest-diverse group hai, jointed\nappendages-exoskeleton (insects, spiders, centipedes, millipedes). [Q1020, Q1061]\n● 'Arthropoda' animal kingdom ka largest group hai — over two-thirds sabhi named species arthropods\nhain, segmented bodies with hard exoskeletons-jointed limbs. [Q1039, Q1050, Q1065, Q1079]\n13. Cnidaria — Corals"," ● Corals marine invertebrates hain, class Anthozoa mein, phylum 'Cnidaria' ka hissa — hydras, jellyfish,\ncorals, sea anemones bhi is phylum mein aate hain. [Q1021]\n14. Mammals — Heart & Characteristics\n●\n Trap: Mammals ka heart 'three chambered' NAHI hai — FOUR-chambered hota hai. Mammals hair\n⚠️\nrakhte hain, mammary glands se doodh dete hain, kuch (monotremes) ande dete hain. [Q1022]\n● Mammals 'warm-blooded' hote hain 4-chambered heart ke saath — oxygenated aur deoxygenated\nblood poori tarah alag hoti hai, highly efficient circulatory system. [Q1040, Q1051]\n15. Mollusca\n●\n Trap: 'Scolopendra' (centipede) Mollusca ka example NAHI hai — Arthropoda phylum (Chilopoda\n⚠️\nclass) mein aata hai. Mollusca mein Union, Octopus, Snail aate hain (2nd largest phylum). [Q1023]\n●\n Trap: 'Antedon' (feather star) Mollusca ka part NAHI hai — Echinodermata phylum mein aata hai.\n⚠️\nMollusca mein Snail, Octopus, Chiton hote hain. [Q1070]\n16. Pisces — Characteristics\n●\n Trap: 'Pseudocoelom' Pisces ki characteristic NAHI hai — ye Aschelminthes (roundworms) ki\n⚠️\nfeature hai. Pisces cold-blooded hain, scales-gills-bony/cartilaginous endoskeleton rakhte hain. [Q1031]\n●\n Trap: Pisces 'warm-blooded' NAHI hote — cold-blooded aquatic animals hain, gills se oxygen lete\n⚠️\nhain, scales se covered hote hain, heart 2 chambers ka hota hai. [Q1024]\n● Fish mein '2-chambered heart' hota hai (1 atrium + 1 ventricle) — single circulation hoti hai, blood heart\nse ek hi baar guzarta hai poore circuit mein. [Q1049]\n17. Regeneration — Earthworm\n● 'Earthworm' cut hone par regenerate ho sakta hai — Annelida phylum, clitellum ke peeche cut hone par\nhead portion survive-regenerate kar sakta hai (Axolotl, Starfish bhi regenerate karte hain). [Q1025]\n18. Animal Breeds — Goats\n● 'Angora, Alpine aur Nubian' goat breeds hain — French-Alpine, Boer, Saanen, LaMancha bhi goat\nbreeds hain. Cow breeds: Holstein, Jersey. Buffalo breeds: Murrah, Nili-Ravi. [Q1028]\n19. Warm-Blooded vs Cold-Blooded Animals"," ● 'Pigeon' (bird) warm-blooded hai — Birds (Aves) aur Mammals constant body temperature maintain kar\nsakte hain. Fish, toad (amphibian), crocodile (reptile) cold-blooded hain. [Q1029]\n● 'Aves' (birds) group warm-blooded hoti hai — Mammals bhi warm-blooded. Reptiles, Fish, Amphibians\ncold-blooded hote hain. [Q1038, Q1041]\n20. Ultrasound — Echolocation\n● 'Porpoises' ultrasound produce kar sakte hain (>20 KHz) — Dolphins, Bats bhi echolocation ke liye\nultrasound use karte hain. Elephants-Rhinoceroses infrasound (<20 Hz) produce karte hain. [Q1030]\n21. Annelida\n●\n Trap: 'Ascaris' Annelida class ka part NAHI hai — Phylum Nematoda (roundworm) mein aata hai.\n⚠️\nAnnelida (segmented worms, true coelom) mein Leech, Nereis, Earthworm shaamil hain. [Q1032]\n22. Reptile — Heart Structure\n● Zyadatar reptiles ka '3-chambered heart' hota hai (2 atria + 1 partially divided ventricle) — Crocodile\nexception hai (4-chambered). Birds-Mammals 4-chambers, Fish 2-chambers. [Q1035]\n23. Epithelium Types\n● Kidney ki inner lining 'Cuboidal' epithelium se bani hoti hai — mechanical support deti hai, salivary\nglands ducts mein bhi hoti hai. Columnar intestine, Squamous oesophagus-mouth mein. [Q1036]\n● Mouth ki inner lining 'Simple squamous epithelium' se bani hoti hai — constant abrasion wali areas ke\nliye suited. Stratified squamous skin ki outer covering banata hai. [Q1042]\n● 'Epithelial' tissue glands banati hai — body surfaces cover karti hai, body cavities-hollow organs line\nkarti hai, functions: protection, secretion, absorption, excretion, filtration. [Q1044]\n24. Connective Tissue — Ligament, Tendon & Areolar\n● 'Ligament' bones ko connect karta hai — bone-to-bone connection, joints-organs ko jagah par hold karta\nhai. [Q1046]\n● Humari bones 'Connective' tissue hain — extracellular matrix aur limited cells se bani hoti hain (adipose,\ncartilage, blood bhi connective tissue hain). [Q1047]\n● Areolar tissue organs ke andar (inside) spaces fill karti hai, internal organs ko support karti hai aur\ntissue repair karti hai — skin-muscles ke beech, blood vessels-nerves ke around, bone marrow mein bhi\nhoti hai. [Q1048]"," ● 'Tendons' muscles ko bones se connect karte hain — tough fibrous connective tissue, movement\nfacilitate karte hain. Ligaments bone-to-bone connect karte hain. [Q1062]\n● 'Muscle' tissue minimal extracellular matrix wali connective tissue hai — densely packed cells jo contract\nkarne ki special ability rakhte hain (blood-bone ke muqable minimal matrix). [Q1071]\n● Adipose (fatty) tissue skin ke neeche, kidneys ke around, aur internal organs ke beech milti hai — fat\nstore karke insulation-protection deti hai. [Q1072]\n●\n Trap: 'Muscle' tissue insulator ki tarah kaam NAHI karti — 'Fatty' (Adipose) tissue insulator hai,\n⚠️\nenergy fat ki tarah store karti hai, body temperature maintain karti hai. [Q1074]\n25. Adipose Tissue\n● 'Adipose' tissue skin ke neeche aur internal organs ke beech banti hai — loose connective tissue hai, fat\nstore karti hai, insulation deti hai, major organs protect karti hai. [Q1043]\n26. Aves — Birds\n● 'Aves' group mein Birds shaamil hain — pelicans, ostriches, hawks, eagles, owls examples hain. Sabhi\nbirds ke feathers, 4-chambered heart, wings, beaks hote hain, hard-shelled eggs dete hain. [Q1045]\n27. Echinodermata — Free-Living Marine Animals\n● 'Echinodermata' completely free-living marine organisms hain — water vascular system rakhte hain\nlocomotion-food transport-respiration ke liye, koi excretory system nahi hota. [Q1053, Q1077]\n● Starfish 'Echinodermata' group ke hain — radial symmetry, calcium carbonate ka spiny endoskeleton,\nwater vascular system. [Q1056]\n● 'Water vascular system' Sea cucumber (Echinodermata) mein milta hai — Sea anemone-Sea Pen\nphylum Cnidaria mein aate hain. [Q1069]\n28. Porifera — Immobile Sponges\n● 'Porifera' (sponges) ke animals immobile (sessile) hote hain adults ki tarah — mostly marine,\nasymmetrical, primitive multicellular, cellular level organisation. Examples: Sycon, Spongilla, Euspongia.\n[Q1054]\n29. Planaria — Simple Eyes (Eyespots)\n● 'Planaria' mein bahut simple eyes (eyespots/ocelli) hote hain — light detect karte hain lekin image form\nnahi karte. Freshwater flatworms hain, remarkable regenerative abilities. [Q1055]"," 30. Reptile Skin\n● 'Reptile' class ki skin dry aur gland-less hoti hai — scaly, cold-blooded, creeping-burrowing terrestrial\nanimals (snakes, lizards, turtles, crocodiles). [Q1057]\n● Reptile ki skin 'dry-rough scales' se covered hoti hai (glandless) — water loss prevent karti hai, body\nprotect karti hai. [Q1058]\n●\n Trap: 'Toad' reptile class ka NAHI hai — amphibian hai (dual life, porous skin). Turtle, Crocodile,\n⚠️\nSnake true reptiles hain (dry-scaly skin). [Q1075]\n31. Mammal Skin\n● Mammals ki skin 'glandular with hairs' hoti hai — sweat, scent, sebaceous glands hote hain, hair-fur se\ncovered hote hain, diverse environments mein adapt karte hain. [Q1059]\n32. True Marine Fish — Dog Fish\n● 'Dog fish' true marine fish hai — class Chondrichthyes (sharks wali), cartilaginous skeleton. Jellyfish-\nStarfish-Silverfish true fish NAHI hain. [Q1060]\n33. Amphibia\n● 'Amphibia' class ke animals scales NAHI rakhte, mucus glands hoti hain skin mein — cold-blooded\nvertebrates, land-water dono mein rehte hain, 3-chambered heart (2 auricles, 1 ventricle). [Q1064]\n34. Match List — Body Tissues\n● Match: Skin → Stratified squamous epithelium; Cartilage → Surface of joints; Skeletal muscles →\nStriated muscles; Subcutaneous layer → Adipose tissue. [Q1066]\n35. Egg-Laying Mammals — Monotremes\n● 'Platypus' egg-laying mammal hai — monotremes group mein aata hai, unique mammals jo live young\nke bajaye ande dete hain. [Q1067]\n● 'Tachyglossus' (echidna) Reptiles aur Mammals ke beech connecting link hai — dono ki characteristics\nrakhta hai (ande deta hai lekin fur-milk bhi hai). Peripatus annelids-arthropods connect karta hai. [Q1068]\n36. Hydra — Reproduction by Budding"," ● 'Hydra' Budding se reproduce karta hai (Yeast bhi) — chhoti outgrowth (bud) se naya organism develop\nhota hai. Binary fission Amoeba mein, Fragmentation Spirogyra mein, Multiple fission Plasmodium mein\nhota hai. [Q1076]\n37. Diploblastic vs Triploblastic Animals\n●\n Trap: 'Jellyfish' (Cnidaria) triploblastic NAHI hai — diploblastic hai. Triploblastic animals (3 germinal\n⚠️\nlayers: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) mein Earthworm, Planaria, Ascaris, Frogs, Humans aate hain.\n[Q1078]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 17 Animal Kingdom Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0383","t":"18 Microorganism","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.18 — MICROORGANISM — FULL MIND MAP\n🦠\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Microorganisms & Water Pollution\n2. Viruses - Characteristics & Diseases\n3. Protozoa - Amoeba & Paramecium\n4. Bacteria - Shapes & Extremophiles\n5. Fungi & Yeast\n6. Algae & Cyanobacteria\n7. Reproduction in Microorganisms\n8. Disease-Causing Microbes - Quick Summary\n9. Decomposers & Environment\n10. Other Important Facts\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n1. Microorganisms & Water Pollution\n● E. coli Coliform bacteria ki presence water pollution (faecal contamination) ka indicator hai. [Q1080]\n● Salmonella Typhi = typhoid cause karta hai. Vibrio Cholerae = cholera (contaminated water/food).\nMycobacterium Tuberculosis = tuberculosis. [Q1080]\n2. Viruses - Characteristics & Diseases\n● HIV = Human Immunodeficiency Virus. AIDS = disease (Acquired Immunodeficiency Syndrome), virus\nnahi. [Q1081]\n● Viral diseases: Dengue, AIDS, Influenza, Polio, Measles, Chickenpox, Covid-19. [Q1081, Q1090]\n● Virus = submicroscopic infectious agent, sirf living cells ke andar replicate kar sakta hai. Living + non-\nliving dono characteristics hain. DNA ya RNA strands covered with capsid. [Q1084]\n● Virus inactive rehta hai jab tak kisi cell ko infect nahi karta - ye uska \"living character\" hai. Outside host\ncell reproduce nahi kar sakta. [Q1084]\n● Anthrax = bacteria (Bacillus anthracis) se hota hai, viral nahi. Elephantiasis = filarial parasites se.\n[Q1081]\n3. Protozoa - Amoeba & Paramecium\n● Paramecium: definite shape, specific spot (oral groove) se food intake, cilia se food ko wahan tak move\nkarta hai. Unicellular ciliate protozoan. [Q1082]\n● Amoeba: unicellular, no special excretory organs. Nitrogenous waste simple diffusion se remove hota\nhai. Contractile vacuole waste collect karke plasma membrane par rupture karke release karti hai.\n[Q1083]\n● Amoeba ka asexual reproduction = Binary fission (parent do identical daughter cells mein split hota hai).\n[Q1096]"," ● Euglena = eukaryotic unicellular flagellated microorganism. [Q1082]\n● Plasmodium = protozoa, single-celled, divides only in host cell. Malaria cause karta hai. [Q1082]\n4. Bacteria - Shapes & Extremophiles\n● Bacteria shapes: Spherical (Cocci), Rod (Bacilli), Spiral (Spirilla), Comma (Vibrios), Corkscrew\n(Spirochaetes). [Q1086, Q1095]\n● Bacteria = unicellular prokaryotes, almost everywhere found. [Q1086]\n● Bacteria extreme habitats mein reh sakte hain: hot springs (>100°C/volcanoes), deep sea, thermal\nvents, Antarctica ice. Viruses extreme conditions mein nahi reh sakte. [Q1095]\n● Clostridium Botulinum: refrigerator ke andar bhi grow kar sakta hai aur lethal botulinum toxins produce\nkarta hai (low-oxygen conditions mein). Nerve functions block karta hai → respiratory/muscular\nparalysis. [Q1089]\n● E. coli: environment, foods, intestines mein found. [Q1089]\n● Salmonella: intestinal tract disease. [Q1089]\n5. Fungi & Yeast\n● Yeast = bread mein daala jata hai taaki wo rise ho sake. Yeast sugar consume karke CO2 gas aur\nethanol produce karta hai. CO2 gluten ki wajah se dough ke andar trapped rehti hai → dough rise hota\nhai. [Q1085]\n● Yeast reproduction = Budding (new organism parent ke small outgrowth/bud se develop hota hai).\n[Q1092]\n● Rhizopus = spore formation se reproduce karta hai. [Q1094]\n● Agaricus = mushroom genus, multicellular organism. All plants, animals, fungi species multicellular hote\nhain. [Q1097]\n6. Algae & Cyanobacteria\n● Blue-green algae (Cyanobacteria): prokaryotic, autotrophic, thylakoid membranes contain karte hain.\nFirst photosynthetic oxygen-liberating organisms. [Q1088]\n● Mitochondria, Lysosomes, Golgi bodies = eukaryotic cell organelles hain, isliye cyanobacteria mein nahi\nhote. [Q1088]\n● Algae: chlorophyll-bearing, thalloid, autotrophic, largely aquatic (freshwater + marine). Moist stones,\nsoils, wood mein bhi milte hain. Some fungi ke saath lichen banate hain. [Q1093]\n7. Reproduction in Microorganisms\n● Budding: Yeast, Hydra. [Q1092]"," ● Binary fission: Amoeba, Planaria, Leishmania. [Q1096]\n● Multiple fission: Plasmodium. Nucleus repeatedly divide karta hai, many daughter cells produce hoti\nhain. [Q1094]\n● Spore formation: Rhizopus, Aspergillus, Penicillium. [Q1094, Q1096]\n● Conjugation: Paramecium (sexual process, two individuals exchange genetic material). [Q1092]\n● Vegetative propagation: Ginger, Potato - roots/shoots/leaves se without reproductive organs. [Q1096]\n8. Disease-Causing Microbes - Quick Summary\n● Viral diseases: Chickenpox, Covid-19, Influenza, Polio, Measles, Dengue, AIDS. [Q1090]\n● Bacterial diseases: Tuberculosis, Pneumonia, Anthrax, Typhoid, Cholera. [Q1090]\n● Fungal diseases: Mycosis. [Q1090]\n● Worm/Parasite diseases: Ascariasis, Filariasis (Elephantiasis). [Q1090]\n● Poliomyelitis (Polio): virus se hota hai - causes muscle weakness/paralysis. [Q1090]\n9. Decomposers & Environment\n● Bacteria (and fungi) = decomposers. Dead plants/animals ko humus mein convert karte hain. Complex\norganic matter ko CO , water, nutrients jaise inorganic substances mein break down karte hain.\n₂\n[Q1087]\n10. Other Important Facts\n● Planaria: flatworm (phylum Platyhelminthes), simple eyes called eyespots/ocelli - light detect kar sakti\nhain lekin image nahi bana sakti. No skeleton, no circulatory/respiratory organs. Flat ribbon-like body.\n[Q1091]\n● Liver fluke aur Tapeworm bhi Platyhelminthes se belong karte hain. [Q1091]\n● Ascaris: most common roundworm infection in humans. [Q1091]\n● Multicellular organisms = plants, animals, fungi. Unicellular = Paramecium, Cyanobacteria,\nMycoplasma. [Q1097]\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n● AIDS = disease hai, HIV = virus hai. [Q1081]\n● Anthrax = bacterial, Elephantiasis = parasitic - dono viral nahi hain. [Q1081]\n● Virus inactive rehta hai jab tak cell infect nahi karta - ye uska living character hai. [Q1084]\n● Amoeba = simple diffusion (excretion), Paramecium = cilia (food movement). [Q1082, Q1083]\n● Cocci = spherical shape. [Q1086]"," ● Bacteria extreme habitats mein reh sakte hain, viruses nahi. [Q1095]\n● Clostridium Botulinum = fridge mein bhi grow karta hai aur deadly toxins produce karta hai. [Q1089]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 18 Microorganism Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0384","t":"19 Enzymes and Hormones","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.19 — ENZYMES & HORMONES — FULL MIND MAP\n⚗️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Insulin & Diabetes\n2. Digestive Enzymes\n3. Adrenaline & Stress Response\n4. Plant Hormones\n5. Human Endocrine Glands\n6. Enzyme Functions & Sources\n7. Hormone Deficiencies & Effects\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n1. Insulin & Diabetes\n● Insulin deficiency → Diabetes mellitus (high blood sugar). Insulin pancreas dwara produce hota hai,\nchemical messenger jo cells ko glucose absorb karne deta hai. [Q1098]\n● Insulin function: body mein glucose aur fat ka use/storage regulate karta hai. Glucose ko bloodstream\nse cells tak le jata hai. Insulin deficiency → hyperglycemia, Type 1 diabetes. [Q1107]\n● Glucagon (alpha cells in islets of Langerhans se) → blood glucose ko kam hone se bachata hai, sugar\nlevel badhata hai. [Q1115]\n● Insulin vs Glucagon: Insulin = sugar kam karta hai, Glucagon = sugar badhata hai. [Q1115]\n2. Digestive Enzymes\n● Amylase (salivary glands + pancreas): starch → simple sugars. Saliva mein Alpha-Amylase (Ptyalin)\nhota hai. [Q1099, Q1109, Q1125, Q1131]\n● Pepsin (gastric glands): protein digest karta hai. HCl pepsin ko activate karta hai. Pepsin protein →\npeptides mein todta hai. [Q1105, Q1106, Q1122]\n● Trypsin (pancreas → small intestine): protein → amino acids. Inactive trypsinogen form mein aata hai.\n[Q1123, Q1138]\n● Lipase (pancreas): fats/triglycerides → fatty acids + glycerol. Rice bran oil stabilization mein bhi use\nhota hai. [Q1101]\n● Lactase: lactose break karta hai. Sucrase: sucrose → fructose + glucose. Maltase: maltose → glucose.\n[Q1138]\n● Invertase: sucrose → fructose + glucose. Zymase: fermentation mein sugars break karta hai. [Q1106]\n3. Adrenaline & Stress Response\n● Adrenaline/Adrenalin/Epinephrine = \"fight or flight\" hormone. Adrenal medulla se secreted. Anger,\nembarrassment, worry ke time body ko stress se adjust karne mein madad karta hai. [Q1100, Q1104]\n● Adrenaline se heartbeat aur breathing rate simultaneously increase hoti hai. [Q1104]"," ● Estrogen = female reproductive organs. Thyroxine = digestion, heart/muscle function, brain\ndevelopment. Testosterone = primary male hormone. [Q1100]\n4. Plant Hormones\n● Prolactin = pituitary gland hormone in mammals (milk production), plant hormone nahi hai. [Q1110]\n● Plant hormones: Ethylene (fruit ripening, leaf dropping), Abscisic acid (stomata closure, growth\ninhibition, wilting, stress), Gibberellins (stem/leaf growth), Cytokinins (cell division), Auxins (cell\nelongation, phototropism). [Q1110, Q1111, Q1135]\n● Abscisic acid (ABA) = \"stress hormone\". Growth inhibit karta hai, wilting/pores closing ke liye\nresponsible, seed dormancy. [Q1111, Q1128, Q1130]\n● Cytokinins = cell division promote karte hain, root apices/developing shoot buds/young fruits mein\nsynthesize hote hain. Apical dominance overcome karte hain. [Q1127, Q1129]\n● Auxin = cell elongation, phototropism (stem light ki taraf bend hota hai), prevents premature fall of\nleaves/flowers/fruits. Universal natural auxin = IAA (Indole-3-Acetic Acid). NAA = vegetative propagation\nmein, IBA = root induction. [Q1119, Q1120, Q1137]\n● Gibberellins/Gibberellic acid = stem elongation, seed germination, fruit development, dwarfness control\nkarte hain. Cold temperature mein zyada produce hote hain. [Q1132, Q1134]\n● Ethylene = fruit ripening, leaf dropping. Natural hormone. [Q1110]\n● Growth hormones kabhi promoter, kabhi inhibitor ki tarah kaam kar sakte hain - context dependent.\n[Q1133]\n5. Human Endocrine Glands\n● Pituitary gland (Hypophysis) = \"Master gland\". Brain ke base par pea-sized. Anterior lobe: ACTH,\nProlactin, TSH, Growth Hormone. Posterior lobe: Oxytocin, Vasopressin. [Q1103]\n● Human Growth Hormone (HGH) = anterior lobe of pituitary se secreted hota hai. [Q1103]\n● Thymus gland = sirf puberty tak active rehti hai. Thymosins secrete karti hai jo lymphocyte production\nregulate karta hai. [Q1113]\n● Pineal gland = \"biological clock\", melatonin secrete karti hai (sleep regulator). [Q1113]\n● Hypothalamus = releasing/inhibiting hormones. [Q1113]\n● Testes = Testosterone (androgens) secrete karte hain. Leydig cells dwara. Puberty mein boys ke\nappearance mein changes laata hai. [Q1121, Q1124]\n● Ovaries = Estrogen produce karti hain. Menstrual cycle regulate karta hai. [Q1112]\n● Thyroid gland = Thyroxine (T4) aur Triiodothyronine (T3). [Q1117]\n● Thyroxine commonly T4 ke naam se jana jata hai. TSH T4 aur T3 production regulate karta hai. PTH\nserum calcium regulate karta hai. [Q1117]\n● Thyroxine synthesis ke liye Iodine essential hai. Deficiency → Goitre. Iron = hemoglobin. Sodium = BP.\nCalcium = bone health. [Q1118, Q1126]"," 6. Enzyme Functions & Sources\n● Enzymes = biological catalysts. Chemical reactions ki speed regulate karte hain without being\nconsumed. [Q1108]\n● Salivary glands se Amylase secreted hota hai. 3 pairs: Parotid (watery, amylase rich), Submaxillary,\nSublingual. Total saliva: 1000-1500 ml/day. [Q1125]\n● Gastric glands → Pepsin. Pancreas → Trypsin, Lipase, Amylase. Small intestine → Lactase, Sucrase,\nMaltase. [Q1105, Q1122, Q1123, Q1138]\n● HCl (gastric glands) → pepsin ki action facilitate karta hai, acidic medium deta hai. [Q1122]\n7. Hormone Deficiencies & Effects\n● Ghrelin = \"hunger hormone\". 28-amino-acid peptide stomach se. Appetite stimulate karta hai, food\nintake badhata hai, fat storage promote karta hai. [Q1102]\n● Leptin = food intake reduce karta hai. Resistin = obesity ko diabetes se link karta hai. [Q1102]\n● Melanin = hair/skin color ka determinant. Melanocytes dwara produced. Keratin = hair/skin/nails ka\nprotein. Carotene = fruits/vegetables mein orange/yellow/red pigment. [Q1114]\n● Vasopressin (ADH) = osmotic balance, BP, sodium homeostasis control karta hai. [Q1115]\n● Oxytocin = uterine contractions childbirth mein stimulate karta hai. [Q1098]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n● Prolactin = animal hormone, plant hormone nahi. [Q1110]\n● Auxins = plant hormone, animal hormone nahi. [Q1136]\n● Insulin = glucose regulation, glucagon = glucose raise. [Q1115]\n● Amylase = starch digestion (saliva + pancreas). Pepsin = protein (stomach). Trypsin = protein (small\nintestine, pancreas). Lipase = fats. [Q1099, Q1105, Q1123]\n● Thyroxine = T4, TSH = thyroid stimulating, T3 = triiodothyronine. [Q1117]\n● Iodine = thyroxine ke liye essential. [Q1118, Q1126]\n● Growth hormone = anterior pituitary. Oxytocin/Vasopressin = posterior pituitary. [Q1103]\n● Hormones bacteria mein absent hote hain. [Q1116]\n● IAA = universal natural auxin. NAA aur IBA synthetic/use-specific hain. [Q1137]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 19 Enzymes and Hormones Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0385","t":"20 Discoveries and Vaccines","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.20 — DISCOVERIES & VACCINES — FULL MIND MAP\n💉\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Gregor Mendel & Laws of Inheritance\n2. COVID-19 Vaccines & Drugs\n3. Scientific Discoveries & Scientists\n4. Antibiotics & Medicines\n5. Other Vaccines\n6. Medical Techniques & Instruments\n7. Fermentation & Pasteur\n8. Taxonomy & Classification\n9. Evolution\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n1. Gregor Mendel & Laws of Inheritance\n● Gregor Johann Mendel ne 3 laws of inheritance diye hain. Unko \"Father of Genetics\" kaha jata hai.\n1856-1863 tak pea plants par experiments kiye. [Q1139, Q1141, Q1142, Q1158, Q1162]\n● Mendel ki 3 laws: - Law of Dominance: hybrid offspring dominant trait inherit karti hai - Law of\nSegregation (Purity of Gametes): hereditary factors ki 2 copies segregate hoti hain; offspring ko har\nparent se ek factor milta hai - Law of Independent Assortment: traits ke pairs independently segregate\nhote hain [Q1139, Q1161]\n● Mendel ki success ka main reason: numerical count of progeny rakhi - science aur mathematics ka\nblend kiya. Large sample size, pea plants (distinct traits), aur several generations tak inferences confirm\nkiye. [Q1141, Q1142]\n● Law of Segregation (purity of gametes) monohybrid cross ke results se derive kiya gaya tha. [Q1161]\n● Darwin = Evolution theory. Watson & Crick = DNA structure. Carl Linnaeus = Taxonomy. [Q1139, Q1158]\n● Law of Independent Assortment: traits ke pairs independently segregate hote hain [Q1139, Q1161]\n2. COVID-19 Vaccines & Drugs\n● Vincov-19: India ki first indigenous COVID-19 drug. Immunised horses ke blood serum ko synthesise\nkarke banayi gayi. [Q1140]\n● DCGI approved 2 indigenous vaccines: COVISHIELD (Serum Institute of India) aur COVAXIN (Bharat\nBiotech + ICMR-National Institute of Virology). [Q1140, Q1152]\n● ZyCoV-D: India's first DNA plasmid vaccine. Sputnik V = Russia ka (Gamaleya Research Institute).\n[Q1140]\n● COVAXIN (BBV152) = whole inactivated virus-based vaccine. Bharat Biotech HQ = Genome Valley,\nHyderabad. ICMR HQ = New Delhi. [Q1152]\n3. Scientific Discoveries & Scientists"," ● Binomial nomenclature (genus + species, e.g., Homo sapiens) = Carolus Linnaeus ne introduce kiya.\nFather of Taxonomy. [Q1143, Q1159]\n● Crescograph (plant growth measure karne ka instrument) = Sir Jagadish Chandra Bose ne invent kiya.\n[Q1145]\n● Theophrastus = Father of Botany. Aristotle = Father of Zoology. Antoine Lavoisier = Father of\nChemistry. [Q1146]\n● Smallpox vaccine = Edward Jenner ne 1796 mein Varicella virus use karke invent kiya. [Q1147]\n● Blood groups (A, B, AB, O) = Karl Landsteiner ne discover kiye. Universal donor = O negative, Universal\nrecipient = AB positive. [Q1149]\n● Protoplasm term = Johann Evangelist Purkinje ne coin kiya. Protoplasm = cytoplasm + nucleus +\norganelles (plasma membrane se surrounded). [Q1150]\n● Cell = Robert Hooke ne 1665 mein cork observe karke discover kiya. Antony Van Leeuwenhoek ne\npehle living cells discover kiye. Cytology = cell ka study. [Q1151]\n● Penicillin (first antibiotic) = Alexander Fleming ne 1928 mein Penicillium notatum fungus se discover\nkiya. [Q1153]\n● James Chadwick = neutron discover kiya (1932). Dmitri Mendeleev = Modern Periodic Table. John\nDalton = Atomic Theory. Isaac Newton = Laws of Gravity and Motion. [Q1147, Q1149, Q1153]\n4. Antibiotics & Medicines\n● Antibiotics = bacterial infection treat karne ke liye. Bacteria ko kill/inhibit karte hain. [Q1144]\n● Anesthetic = sensation loss induce karta hai. Antiseptic = living tissues (wounds, cuts) par infection\nprevent karta hai. Antipyretic = fever reduce karta hai. [Q1144]\n● Penicillin ke alawa: Azithromycin, Erythromycin, Streptomycin. [Q1153]\n5. Other Vaccines\n● ZikaVac (Zika virus vaccine) = Bharat Biotech (Hyderabad, India) ne develop kiya. Zika virus Aedes\nmosquito ke bite se spread hota hai. [Q1154]\n● Rabies vaccine = Louis Pasteur ne develop kiya. [Q1156]\n● ERVEBO = Ebola vaccine (Merck). [Q1154]\n6. Medical Techniques & Instruments\n● Ultrasonics = foetal growth monitor karne ki latest technique. Obstetrics/gynaecology mein use hoti hai.\n[Q1155]\n● CAT Scan = 3D images ke liye X-rays use karta hai. Eudiometer = gas mixture ki volume change\nmeasure karta hai. Chronometer = time measure. Bolometer = radiation measure. Cardiograph = heart\nrate measure. [Q1145, Q1155]"," 7. Fermentation & Pasteur\n● Louis Pasteur (Father of Bacteriology) ne fermentation process, pasteurization, aur anthrax/rabies\nvaccines develop kiye. French chemist aur microbiologist. [Q1156, Q1157]\n● Robert Koch ne tuberculosis bacterium, cholera, aur anthrax discover kiye. Edward Jenner ne smallpox\nvaccine. [Q1156, Q1157]\n8. Taxonomy & Classification\n● Linnaean hierarchy (broadest to specific): Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order → Family → Genus →\nSpecies. [Q1163]\n● Taxonomy = naming, describing, classifying organisms based on behavioral, genetic, biochemical\nvariations. [Q1159]\n9. Evolution\n● \"Survival of the fittest\" phrase = Herbert Spencer ne coin kiya. [Q1148]\n● Charles Darwin ne Theory of Evolution by Natural Selection propose kiya - book 'On the Origin of\nSpecies'. Life simple se complex forms mein evolve hui. [Q1148, Q1160]\n● Darwin's theory: individuals with survival/reproduction characteristics un traits ko offspring mein pass\nkarte hain. [Q1160]\n● Albert Einstein = Theory of Relativity. Archimedes = Law of Buoyancy. [Q1148]\n● J.B.S. Haldane aur Aleksandr Oparin = chemical evolution theory. Stanley L. Miller = Father of prebiotic\nchemistry. [Q1158]\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n● Darwin = Evolution, Mendel = Inheritance. [Q1139, Q1158]\n● AIDS = disease, HIV = virus. [Q1081]\n● Ascending order = smallest to largest; lekin Q1163 mein \"ascending\" ke baad bhi correct answer broad-\nto-specific (Kingdom→Species) hai - ye exam ka tricky part hai. [Q1163]\n● Mendel = monohybrid cross se Law of Segregation derive kiya. [Q1161]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 20 Discoveries and Vaccines Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0386","t":"21 Scientific Study","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.21 — SCIENTIFIC STUDY — FULL MIND MAP\n🔬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Origin of Life & Evolution\n2. Branches of Biology & Scientific Studies\n3. Medical Techniques & Instruments\n4. Taxonomy & Classification\n5. Fossils & Living Fossils\n6. Chemical Tests\n7. Important Scientists & Their Contributions\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n1. Origin of Life & Evolution\n● J.B.S. Haldane (1929) ne suggest kiya ki life simple inorganic molecules se early Earth par develop hui.\nUnhone speculate kiya ki early Earth conditions ne complex organic molecules ko janam diya jo life ke\nliye necessary hain. [Q1164]\n● Alexander Oparin (Russian biochemist) ne chemical evolution theory propose ki - origin of life = simplest\nprimordial life ka nonliving matter se appear hona. [Q1183]\n● Charles Darwin ne theory of evolution by natural selection propose ki - book 'On the Origin of Species'\n(1859). Evolution ko 'descent with modification' define kiya. Alfred Russel Wallace ne bhi saath mein\npropose kiya tha. [Q1178, Q1182]\n● Human evolution Africa se trace hoti hai. Paleoanthropology = human evolution ka scientific study.\nStages: Dryopithecus → Ramapithecus (Shivalik) → Australopithecus (South Africa, 1924) → Homo\nErectus (Java, 1891) → Homo Sapiens Neanderthalensis → Homo Sapiens. [Q1184]\n2. Branches of Biology & Scientific Studies\n● Ethology = biological study of animal behaviour. [Q1167]\n● Toxicology = study of harmful effects of chemicals/substances/situations on people, animals,\nenvironment. Virology = viruses. Pathology = disease. Epidemiology = spread/control of diseases.\nBacteriology = bacteria. [Q1172]\n● Arachnology = study of spiders, scorpions, pseudoscorpions, harvestmen. Agronomy = soil/water/crop\nmanagement. Zoology = animals. Anthology = flowers/flowering plants. [Q1173]\n● Agrostology = scientific study of grass. Anthropology = humans. Pomology = fruits. Osteology = bones.\nOrnithology = birds. Odontology = teeth/gums. [Q1175]\n● Paleontology = study of fossils (remains of plants, animals, fungi, bacteria). Paleobotany = fossil plants,\nalgae, fungi. Paleobiology = ancient organisms. [Q1176]\n● Eugenics = branch aiming to improve genetic quality of human population. Biotechnology = biological\nsystems to develop products. Genetics = genes/heredity. Epigenetics = changes in gene\nfunction/expression. [Q1169]"," ● Molecular phylogeny = hereditary molecular differences in DNA sequences/genetics se evolutionary\nrelationships determine karti hai. Metamorphosis = extreme rapid physical changes after birth. [Q1168]\n3. Medical Techniques & Instruments\n● Echocardiography = ultrasound waves ke reflection se heart ki images produce karti hai.\nUltrasonography = high-frequency sound waves se internal body structures ka diagnostic imaging.\nSonography = ultrasound waves se medical imaging. [Q1170]\n● Autopsy (Necropsy) = post-mortem body ki internal/external medical examination to determine cause of\ndeath. Forensic autopsy = suspicious/violent/unknown causes ke liye. Clinical autopsy = hospital mein\npathologist dwara. [Q1171]\n● Ultrasound = ESWL (Extracorporeal Shock Wave Lithotripsy) mein use hota hai kidney stones ko\nshatter karne ke liye. Infrasound = frequencies below 20 Hz. Electromagnetic waves = time-varying\nelectric/magnetic fields, medium nahi chahiye. [Q1174]\n4. Taxonomy & Classification\n● Carolus Linnaeus (Carl Linnaeus) = Father of Taxonomy. Unhone binomial nomenclature introduce kiya\n(genus + species, e.g., Panthera tigris). Definite hierarchy establish ki: Kingdom → Phylum → Class →\nOrder → Family → Genus → Species. [Q1177, Q1179, Q1181]\n● Thomas Cavalier-Smith ne six-kingdom classification propose kiya: Animalia, Protozoa, Fungi, Plantae\n(including red and green algae), Chromista, Bacteria. [Q1180]\n● R.H. Whittaker ne five-kingdom classification di: Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia. [Q1179]\n5. Fossils & Living Fossils\n● Ginkgo biloba = one of the oldest living tree species, herbal supplement worldwide. Funaria = Bryophyta\n(moss). Dryopteris = Dryopteridaceae family (male fern). Silver oak (Grevillea robusta) = Proteaceae,\neastern coastal Australia. [Q1166]\n6. Chemical Tests\n● Starch + Iodine solution → blue-black color. Rice flour mein starch hota hai, isliye iodine daalne par\nblue-black ho jata hai. Amylose in starch beta coils structure banata hai jo iodine ke saath interact karke\nblue-black color deta hai. [Q1165]\n7. Important Scientists & Their Contributions\n● J.B.S. Haldane = Origin of life from inorganic substances (1929). [Q1164]\n● Charles Darwin = Theory of evolution by natural selection (1859). [Q1178, Q1182]"," ● Alexander Oparin = Chemical evolution theory. [Q1183]\n● Gregor Mendel = Laws of inheritance. [Q1182]\n● Carolus Linnaeus = Father of Taxonomy, binomial nomenclature. [Q1177, Q1179, Q1181]\n● Thomas Cavalier-Smith = Six-kingdom classification. [Q1180]\n● John Dalton = Atomic Theory. [Q1182]\n● Johann Dobereiner = Law of Triads. [Q1182]\n● Democritus = Coined word 'atom'. [Q1181]\n● Aristotle = Father of Zoology. [Q1181]\n● Herodotus = Father of History. [Q1181]\n● Socrates = Father of Philosophy. [Q1181]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences\n⚠️\n● Darwin = Evolution, Mendel = Inheritance. [Q1178, Q1182]\n● Ethology = animal behaviour, Etiology = cause of disease, Ethnology = human culture, Entomology =\ninsects. [Q1167]\n● Echocardiography = heart-specific ultrasound. Ultrasonography = general internal imaging. [Q1170]\n● Autopsy = post-mortem examination. [Q1171]\n● Paleontology = fossils. Paleobotany = fossil plants. [Q1176]\n● Six kingdoms = Cavalier-Smith. Five kingdoms = Whittaker. [Q1180, Q1179]\n● Human evolution started in Africa. [Q1184]\n● Starch + Iodine = blue-black. [Q1165]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 21 Scientific Study Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0387","t":"22 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Biology","x":[" BIOLOGY CH.22 — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🧬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Plants vs Animals — Structural Differences\n2. Mendel's Success — Methodology & Sample Size\n3. Mendel's Conclusions — Genes & Gametes\n4. Genetics — A Branch of Biology\n5. Reproductive Health & Family Planning\n6. Balanced Diet & Nutrition\n7. Amla — A Medicinal Fruit\n8. pH Levels — Body, Acid Rain & Tooth Decay\n9. Fermentation — Dough Rising\n10. Gene-Protein Specificity\n11. Biological Magnification\n12. Emulsification of Fats — The Liver\n13. Nitrogen — Essential for Protein Synthesis\n14. Blood Plasma — Transport\n15. Respiratory Pigment — Haemoglobin\n16. Natural Sources of Acids\n17. Phloem — Seasonal Sugar Transport to Buds\n18. Why Trees Shed Old Leaves\n19. Ecosystem — Abiotic-Biotic Interaction\n20. Maintenance Processes in Life\n21. Destarching — Dark Room Experiment\n22. Xylem — Coloured Water Experiment\n23. Adipose Tissue — Fat Storage\n24. Taxol — An Anti-Cancer Drug from Yew\n25. Autotrophs & Holozoic Organisms\n26. Food Chain — Trophic Levels\n27. Food Poisoning\n28. Genetic Engineering — The Gene Revolution\n29. Endemic Species\n30. Charles Darwin — Galapagos & Theory of Evolution\n31. The Human Eye — Parts\n32. Cyclone-30 — Cancer Treatment\n33. Nobel Prize — Helicobacter Pylori Discovery\n34. GM Crops — Bt Brinjal & Bt Cotton\n35. Antibiotics — Facts, Myths & Examples\n36. Mosquito Life Cycle\n37. Nematodes — Missing Body System\n38. Magnetic Fields — Heart & Brain\n39. Vitamins in Yeast\n40. Penicillium — A Fungus\n41. Quinine — Anti-Malarial Drug from Cinchona\n42. Beneficial & Harmful Insects\n43. Lactose — Intolerance & Composition\n44. The Macula — Area of Best Vision\n45. Red Panda — Bamboo Diet\n46. Normal Human Body Temperature\n47. Anthocyanins — Fruit & Vegetable Colours\n48. Homologous vs Analogous Organs\n49. Speciation & Genetic Evolution\n50. Genome\n51. Hydroponics\n52. Omnivores — Plants & Animals Dono Khaane Wale\n53. Diffusion\n54. Dental Caries — Tooth Decay\n55. Alfalfa — Sativa"," 56. Nipah Virus — Fruit Bats\n57. Human Evolution — Genetic Roots in Africa\n58. Wool — Shearing Sheep\n59. Falcon — Speed\n60. Groundnut — An Oil-Yielding Plant\n61. Iodine Test — Detects Starch\n62. Jasmine — A Creeper Plant\n63. Dendrimers — Pharmaceutical Nanotechnology\n64. Phototropism\n65. Rhizome, Tuber, Bulb & Rhizoid — Underground Structures\n66. Prunes — Dried Plums\n67. Eutrophication\n68. Banana — Edible Endocarp & Mesocarp\n69. Ectoparasites vs Endoparasites\n70. Blood Sugar — Glucose\n71. Lipids — Glycerol & Fatty Acids\n72. Pulse Beat — Measured from Artery\n73. Brahmi — Ayurvedic Memory-Boosting Herb\n74. Sarcolemma — Muscle Fiber Membrane\n75. Transpiration\n76. Plasmolysis\n77. Vocal Cords — Human Sound Production\n78. Edward Jenner — Father of Immunology\n79. First-Aid Medicines — Ibuprofen & Antihistamines\n80. Carcinogens\n81. Heredity — Trait Transmission\n82. Variations — Inherited During Reproduction\n83. Somatic Mutation — Not Hereditary\n84. Regeneration — Not the Same as Reproduction\n85. Vascular System — Fluid Transport\n86. Species & Kingdom — Classification Extremes\n87. Cloning\n88. Evolutionary Progress — Gradual Change\n89. Tooth Enamel — Calcium Phosphate\n90. Muscular Force & Joints\n91. Smooth Muscle Tissue — Locations\n92. Contractile Proteins — Actin & Myosin\n93. Glycogen — Energy Storage\n94. Genotype-Phenotype — The ttRr Example\n95. Tendon — Collagen & White Fibres\n96. Reproduction — Maintaining Species\n1. Plants vs Animals — Structural Differences\n●\n Trap: 'Growth certain regions tak limited nahi hoti Plants mein' — ye statement INCORRECT hai —\n⚠️\nactually Animals mein growth certain regions (meristematic zones) tak limited hoti hai, Plants mein nahi.\nPlants move nahi karte, kam energy chahiye hoti hai animals se. [Q1185]\n2. Mendel's Success — Methodology & Sample Size\n●\n Trap: Mendel ne 'small sample size' use ki — ye statement INCORRECT hai. Mendel ka success ka\n⚠️\n\nmain reason tha ek time mein ek hi character study karna, LARGE sample sizes use kiye, aur\nmathematics se apna work present kiya. [Q1186]\n● Mendel's laws sirf tab apply hote hain jab 'parents pure breeding' hon — pea plants consistently same\ntraits wale offspring produce karte the. [Q1285]"," ● Statement check: Mendel ne pea plant chuna experiments ke liye (TRUE), Chromosomes genetic\nfactors ke carrier hain (TRUE) — lekin human forelimb aur bird wings HOMOLOGOUS organs hain\n(same structure, different function), Analogous NAHI (FALSE). [Q1309]\n3. Mendel's Conclusions — Genes & Gametes\n●\n Trap: 'Har gamete mein same gene ki 2 copies hoti hain' — ye statement INCORRECT hai. Har\n⚠️\ngamete mein har chromosome ki EK copy hoti hai, aur har gene ka ek allele. Genes distinct units ki\ntarah inherit hote hain, gametes formation ke dauran segregate hote hain. [Q1187]\n●\n Trap: 'Law of Biopics' Gregor Mendel ki Law of Inheritance mein SHAAMIL NAHI hai (fictional naam)\n⚠️\n\n— 3 asli laws hain: Law of Dominance, Law of Segregation, Law of Independent Assortment. [Q1240]\n● Pea plant mein recessive character: 'Wrinkled seed' (aur Green seed, White flower, Terminal flower,\nShort stem, Constricted pod, Yellow pod) — Dominant: Round seed, Yellow seed, Purple flower. [Q1310]\n4. Genetics — A Branch of Biology\n● 'Genetics' inheritance patterns ki study karne wali biology branch hai — heredity aur variations ki study\nkarti hai. Gene heredity ki basic unit hai. [Q1188]\n5. Reproductive Health & Family Planning\n●\n Trap: 'Smoking aur alcohol consumption' family raise karne mein helpful NAHI hai — harmful hai,\n⚠️\nbreast cancer risk badhata hai, fertility affect karta hai, pregnancy mein baby ki health par asar karta hai.\n[Q1189]\n● Teen mothers banne ka possible reason 'Familial aur societal pressure' hai — teenage pregnancy (13-\n19 age) mein lower educational levels, poverty, family-society pressure related hote hain. [Q1191]\n● Young adolescents (10-14 age) mein pregnancy complications ka higher risk hota hai kyunki 'unka body\nsize aksar bahut chhota hota hai baby deliver karne ke liye' — bodies physically fully developed nahi\nhoti. [Q1207]\n● Pregnant woman ke liye best diet 'dietician dwara prescribed special diet' hai — proteins-minerals-\nvitamins mein rich honi chahiye, calcium-vitamin D-protein important hain. [Q1208]\n6. Balanced Diet & Nutrition\n● Balanced meal ka example: 'Roti, pulses, vegetables' — carbs (roti), protein (pulses), vitamins-minerals\n(vegetables) combination hai. [Q1190]\n7. Amla — A Medicinal Fruit"," ● 'Amla' (Emblica officinalis) ka fruit Chyavanprash banane mein use hota hai — Unani-Ayurvedic\nmedicine mein important herbal plant hai, vitality-vigor build up karta hai. [Q1192]\n8. pH Levels — Body, Acid Rain & Tooth Decay\n● pH match: Human body → 7 to 7.8; Acid rain → less than 5.6; Mouth (tooth decay start) → less than\n5.5. [Q1193]\n●\n Trap: 'Tooth decay mouth pH 5.5 se HIGHER hone par shuru hota hai' — ye INCORRECT hai —\n⚠️\nactually LOWER hone par shuru hota hai. Bacteria sugar-food particles degrade karke acids banate\nhain (base nahi). [Q1204, Q1303]\n9. Fermentation — Dough Rising\n● Dough (yeast ke saath) ka volume badhta hai kyunki 'CO2 (respiration ke dauran produced) volume\nincrease karti hai' — gluten proteins CO2 gas trap karti hain, dough rise karta hai. [Q1194]\n10. Gene-Protein Specificity\n● Sahi statement: 'Har protein ke liye ek specific gene hota hai' — hormones-enzymes proteins se bane\nhote hain, ek particular protein ki formation ek particular gene control karta hai (DNA se). [Q1195]\n11. Biological Magnification\n● Higher trophic levels mein chemicals ka accumulation 'Biological Magnification' kehlaata hai — mercury,\narsenic, pesticides (DDT) jaise contaminants — cancer, kidney problems, birth defects cause kar sakte\nhain. [Q1196]\n12. Emulsification of Fats — The Liver\n● Fats ke emulsification mein 'Liver' involve hota hai — bile juice complex fat molecules ko chhote\nmolecules mein todti hai, digestion easy banati hai. [Q1197]\n13. Nitrogen — Essential for Protein Synthesis\n● 'Nitrogen' plants protein synthesize karne ke liye use karte hain — amino acids ka essential constituent\nhai, soil se nitrate-ammonium form mein roots se absorb hota hai. [Q1198]\n14. Blood Plasma — Transport"," ● 'Plasma' food, carbon dioxide aur nitrogenous wastes ko dissolved form mein transport karta hai —\nblood ka liquid component hai, hormones-nutrients-metabolic wastes transport karta hai. [Q1199]\n15. Respiratory Pigment — Haemoglobin\n●\n Trap: 'Respiratory pigment WHITE blood corpuscles mein present hai' — ye INCORRECT hai —\n⚠️\nRED blood cells mein hota hai (Haemoglobin). Pyruvate lactic acid (3-carbon) mein convert hoti hai,\nalveoli walls mein blood-vessels ka network hota hai. [Q1200]\n● 'Haemoglobin' pigment ki oxygen ke liye high affinity hoti hai — heme pigment + globin protein se bana\nhai, RBC mein hota hai. Myoglobin muscles mein oxygen store karta hai. [Q1205]\n16. Natural Sources of Acids\n● 'Sour milk/Curd' Lactic acid ka natural source hai — Tomato mein Oxalic acid, Ant sting mein Methanoic\n(Formic) acid, Tamarind mein Tartaric acid, Orange mein Citric acid hoti hai. [Q1201]\n17. Phloem — Seasonal Sugar Transport to Buds\n● 'Spring' season mein root/stem mein stored sugar buds tak transport hoti hai (jo energy chahiye grow\nkarne ke liye) — Phloem ye transport karta hai, naye buds spring mein bante hain. [Q1202]\n18. Why Trees Shed Old Leaves\n● Trees purani leaves shed karte hain kyunki 'cells waste materials se pack ho jaate hain' — deciduous\ntrees (Maples, oak) is wajah se leaves girate hain, winter mein cells survive nahi kar paate. [Q1203]\n19. Ecosystem — Abiotic-Biotic Interaction\n● 'Earthworm ka soil mein burrow banana' abiotic (soil) aur biotic (earthworm) component ki interaction\ndikhata hai — ecosystem living-non-living components ka interaction hai. [Q1206]\n20. Maintenance Processes in Life\n● Maintenance processes life mein 'damage aur breakdown prevent' karne ke liye zaroori hain — energy\nka source food hai, nutrition food lene ki process hai, growth-repair ke liye raw material bahar se\nchahiye. [Q1209]"," 21. Destarching — Dark Room Experiment\n● Plants ko dark room mein 3 din rakhne par 'starch resources use ho jaate hain' — photosynthesis rukti\nhai light na hone se, stored starch respiration-transportation ke liye use hota hai (Destarching kehlaata\nhai). [Q1210]\n22. Xylem — Coloured Water Experiment\n● Cut twig ko coloured water mein rakhne se water ka conduction xylem se hota hai (gravity ke against)\n— twig cut karne par coloured tissue INSIDE (xylem region) mein dikhti hai. [Q1211]\n23. Adipose Tissue — Fat Storage\n● 'Adipose tissue' fat-storing tissue hai body mein — Areolar tissue loosely arranged fibres wali\nconnective tissue hai, Vascular tissue (xylem-phloem) water-food conduct karti hai plants mein. [Q1212]\n● Areolar tissue skin aur muscles ke beech filler tissue ki tarah kaam karti hai — organs ke beech spaces\nfill karti hai, internal organs support karti hai, tissue repair mein help karti hai. [Q1291]\n24. Taxol — An Anti-Cancer Drug from Yew\n● 'Taxol' Yew tree (Taxus Brevifolia) se extract hoti hai — Cancer (Breast, lung, Ovarian) ke liye natural\nsource hai USA mein, best plant-based treatments mein se ek. [Q1213]\n25. Autotrophs & Holozoic Organisms\n● Simple inorganic sources (CO2, water) se food banane wale organisms 'Autotrophs' kehlaate hain —\nPlants, lichens, algae examples hain. Saprophytes dead matter se, Heterotrophs doosre organisms se\nfood lete hain. [Q1214]\n● Doosre organisms ko khaane wale organisms 'Holotrophic (Holozoic)' organisms kehlaate hain —\ningestion-digestion-egestion involve karte hain. Parasitic organisms host par-andar rehte hain,\nSaprotrophic dead matter se. [Q1301]\n26. Food Chain — Trophic Levels\n● Food chain ke 3rd trophic level mein 'Secondary consumers' (carnivores jo herbivores khaate hain) aate\nhain — 1st Producers, 2nd Primary consumers (herbivores), 4th Top/Tertiary consumers. [Q1215]\n27. Food Poisoning"," ● Food poisoning ka main cause 'microorganism se spoilt food khaana' hai (Salmonella, Listeria, E.coli) —\nsymptoms: Nausea, bloody stool, fever, abdominal pain. [Q1216]\n28. Genetic Engineering — The Gene Revolution\n● 'Gene Revolution' genetic engineering shaamil karti hai — organism ke genes ka direct manipulation\nbiotechnology ke through, food production mein biotechnology ka application hai. [Q1217]\n29. Endemic Species\n● 'Andaman Teal' endemic species ka example hai — sirf ek geographical region mein exist karti hai.\nIndia ke endemic species: Asiatic Lion, Kashmir Stag, Lion-Tailed Macaque, Sangai Deer, Nilgiri Tahr.\n[Q1218]\n● Endemic species wo hain jo 'ek particular area mein exclusively paayi jaati hain' — Galapagos tortoise,\nHawaiian honeycreeper, Australian Kangaroo examples hain. [Q1249]\n30. Charles Darwin — Galapagos & Theory of Evolution\n● 'Charles Darwin' Galapagos Islands se associate hain — fearless wildlife, Darwin's Theory of Evolution\nke liye inspiration source. Carl Linnaeus Father of Taxonomy, Ernst Haeckel ne 'Ecology' word coin kiya.\n[Q1219]\n● Charles Darwin ne 'Origin of Species' book (1859) mein organic evolution ka mechanism suggest kiya\n— 'Father of Evolution' kehlaate hain. Carl Woese 6-kingdom, Whittaker 5-kingdom classification diye.\n[Q1280]\n31. The Human Eye — Parts\n●\n Trap: 'Cochlea' human eye ka part NAHI hai — ye INNER EAR mein hoti hai (hearing ke liye). Eye\n⚠️\nke parts: Ciliary muscles, Cornea, Iris, Pupil, Lens, Optic nerve. [Q1220]\n32. Cyclone-30 — Cancer Treatment\n● 'Cyclone-30' particle accelerator, Cancer patients ke liye help karta hai — VECC (Kolkata) mein\noperational hai, radioisotopes produce karta hai diagnostic-therapeutic use ke liye. [Q1221]\n33. Nobel Prize — Helicobacter Pylori Discovery\n● 'Robin Warren aur Barry Marshall' ne Helicobacter Pylori bacterium discover karne ke liye Nobel Prize\n(Physiology/Medicine) jeeta. [Q1222]"," 34. GM Crops — Bt Brinjal & Bt Cotton\n● Genetically modified brinjal (Bt-brinjal) ka objective tha 'pest resistant banana' — Bacillus thuringiensis\nse Cry1Ac gene insert kiya gaya, Maharashtra Hybrid Seeds Company ne develop ki. [Q1223]\n● 'Bt Cotton' India mein legally cultivate karne ki permission mila GM crop hai — Bacillus thuringiensis\nbacterium se resistance gene liya gaya, lepidopterans-dipterans-coleopterans pests ke against resistant\nhai. [Q1230]\n35. Antibiotics — Facts, Myths & Examples\n●\n Trap: 'Antibiotics ke side effects mein smallpox, filaria, diphtheria shaamil hain' — ye INCORRECT\n⚠️\nhai — ye alag diseases hain (virus, parasite, bacteria se), antibiotics ke side effects nahi. Antibiotics\nviruses (cold-flu) ke against effective NAHI hain. [Q1224]\n●\n Trap: 'Paracetamol' antibiotic NAHI hai — mild-to-moderate pain, headache, fever ke liye hai.\n⚠️\nErythromycin, Tetracycline, Streptomycin antibiotics hain. [Q1272]\n● 'Amoxicillin' penicillin antibiotic hai jo bacteria se ladta hai — Tonsillitis, Pneumonia, ear-nose-skin-\nurinary tract infections treat karta hai. Penicillin Alexander Fleming ne 1928 mein discover ki. [Q1278]\n36. Mosquito Life Cycle\n● Mosquito lifecycle ke 4 stages: 'Egg, Larva, Pupa, Imago' — female mosquitoes water bodies mein eggs\ndeti hain, larva-pupa transform hokar adult (imago) mosquito banta hai. [Q1225]\n37. Nematodes — Missing Body System\n●\n Trap: 'Respiratory system' Nematodes mein NAHI hoti — Reproductive, Excretory, Digestive\n⚠️\nsystems hoti hain, breathing diffusion se hoti hai. Nematodes (roundworms) plants-humans ko infect\nkarte hain. [Q1226]\n38. Magnetic Fields — Heart & Brain\n● Body mein 'Heart aur Brain' significant magnetic field produce karte hain — MRI brain images ke liye,\nECG heart ki electrical activity record karta hai. [Q1227]\n39. Vitamins in Yeast\n● 'Vitamin B' (especially B-complex, riboflavin B2) yeast mein rich hoti hai — yeast eukaryotic single-\ncelled fungi hai. [Q1228]"," 40. Penicillium — A Fungus\n● 'Penicillium' fungi hai — antibiotic penicillin secrete karta hai (bacteria growth kill-inhibit karta hai).\nAlexander Fleming ne 1928 mein penicillin discover ki. [Q1229]\n41. Quinine — Anti-Malarial Drug from Cinchona\n● Anti-malarial drug 'Quinine' Cinchona plant se extract hoti hai — Malaria Plasmodium parasite se hoti\nhai, Anopheles mosquito ke bite se failti hai. [Q1231]\n42. Beneficial & Harmful Insects\n●\n Trap: 'Termite' beneficial insect NAHI hai — destructive pest hai, wood-organic materials khaake\n⚠️\nbuildings damage karta hai. Silk moth, Lac insect, Honey bee beneficial hain. [Q1232]\n● 'Wasps aur Beetles' ke teeth (jaws — mandibles-maxillae) hote hain — powerful food-grinding jaws,\nPhylum Arthropoda ke hain. Bees pollination mein important role play karte hain. [Q1254]\n43. Lactose — Intolerance & Composition\n● Lactose intolerance wo condition hai jisme 'small intestine dairy products ki sugar (lactose) todne mein\nunable hoti hai' — Lactose glucose-galactose units se bani disaccharide hai, milk ka 2-8% hoti hai.\n[Q1233]\n● Lactose 'Galactose' aur glucose se compose hoti hai — hydrolysis par ye 2 sugars mein toot jaati hai.\n[Q1256]\n44. The Macula — Area of Best Vision\n● Human eye mein 'yellow' oval spot best vision ka area hai — Macula (yellow spot) retina ke center ke\npass hota hai, visual acuity ke liye specialized hai. [Q1234]\n45. Red Panda — Bamboo Diet\n● Red Panda 'Bamboo' leaves khaata hai — roots, succulent grasses, fruits, insects bhi khaata hai.\nEucalyptus koala ka main food hai. [Q1235]\n46. Normal Human Body Temperature\n● Normal human body temperature '98.6°F' (37°C) hai — Clinical thermometer se measure hoti hai, range\n35°C-42°C hoti hai. [Q1236]"," 47. Anthocyanins — Fruit & Vegetable Colours\n● 'Anthocyanins' pigments fruits-vegetables ke colours determine karte hain — plant cell vacuoles mein\nhote hain, water-soluble, pH ke saath color change karte hain. [Q1237]\n48. Homologous vs Analogous Organs\n● 'Homologous' organs same basic structural design-origin rakhte hain lekin different functions perform\nkarte hain — example: forearm of frog, lizard, bird, human. Analogous organs similar function, different\nstructure-origin (bird-insect wings). [Q1238, Q1293]\n●\n Trap: 'Chordates diploblastic hote hain' — ye WRONG statement hai — chordates TRIPLOBLASTIC\n⚠️\n\nhote hain (3 germ layers). Chordates coelomate hote hain, dorsal nerve cord aur notochord rakhte hain.\n[Q1282]\n● Analogous organs ka example: 'Tailfin of lobster aur flukes of whale' — functionally similar, structurally\ndifferent. Human arm-bull's leg, bat's wing-whale's fin, dog's leg-dolphin's flipper — sab HOMOLOGOUS\nhain. [Q1283]\n49. Speciation & Genetic Evolution\n●\n Trap: 'Divergent evolution' speciation mein contribute NAHI karta — ye speciation ka RESULT hai,\n⚠️\ncause nahi. Speciation factors: Genetic drift, Natural selection, Geographic isolation, Variation, Mutation.\n[Q1239]\n● Species ke andar 'change' (variations) survival advantage de sakti hai ya genetic evolution mein\ncontribute kar sakti hai — natural selection se adapted organisms survive-genes pass karte hain.\n[Q1284]\n50. Genome\n● Organism ke complete nuclear DNA set ko 'Genome' kehte hain — Tissue cells ka group hai,\nOrganelles cell ke andar structures hain, Chromosomes DNA-protein se bane structures hain. [Q1241]\n51. Hydroponics\n● 'Hydroponics' farming mein plants mineral nutrient solutions mein bina soil ke grow karte hain —\nTomatoes, Lettuce, Cucumber, Banana, Spinach jaise plants isse grow hote hain. [Q1242]\n52. Omnivores — Plants & Animals Dono Khaane Wale"," ● Plants AUR animals dono khaane wale animals 'Omnivores' kehlaate hain — Bears, Birds, Dogs,\nhumans examples. Carnivores meat, Herbivores plants khaate hain. [Q1243]\n53. Diffusion\n● 'Diffusion' se molecules high concentration se low concentration ki taraf move karte hain — Example:\nOxygen plasma membrane ke across move karta hai. [Q1244]\n54. Dental Caries — Tooth Decay\n● 'Dental caries' ka matlab 'Tooth decay' hai — mouth mein rehne wale bacteria acids produce karke\nteeth ko attack karte hain. [Q1245]\n55. Alfalfa — Sativa\n● 'Sativa' (Medicago sativa) ko 'Alfalfa' kehte hain — legume crop hai, forage-hay-cover crop ke liye grow\nki jaati hai. [Q1246]\n56. Nipah Virus — Fruit Bats\n● 'Fruit bats' (flying foxes) Nipah virus ke natural hosts hain — pigs-humans ko bhi illness cause kar sakta\nhai, encephalitis associate hai. [Q1247]\n57. Human Evolution — Genetic Roots in Africa\n● Human species ki genetic roots 'Africa' mein hain — Homo naledi fossils South Africa mein mile.\nEvolution stages: Dryopithecus → Ramapithecus → Australopithecus → Homo Erectus → Homo\nSapiens. [Q1248]\n58. Wool — Shearing Sheep\n● Sheep ki fleece thin skin layer ke saath remove karne ki process 'Shearing' kehlaati hai — wool obtain\nkarne ka process: Scouring, Sorting, Removing burrs, Cleaning-drying. [Q1250]\n59. Falcon — Speed\n● Falcon (Peregrine Falcon) ki approximate speed '320 km/h' hai — prey 2 miles (3.2 km) door se spot kar\nsakta hai. [Q1251]"," 60. Groundnut — An Oil-Yielding Plant\n● 'Groundnut' oil-yielding plant hai (Arachis hypogaea) — 'kingpin of oilseeds' kehlaata hai, 85% India\nmein kharif season mein sown hoti hai. [Q1252]\n61. Iodine Test — Detects Starch\n● 'Iodine' food mein 'Starch' ki presence test karne ke liye use hoti hai — starch presence mein iodine\nsolution blue-black color mein badal jaati hai. [Q1253]\n62. Jasmine — A Creeper Plant\n● 'Jasmine' (Jasminum) creeper plant hai — small vine-like plants ground ke close grow karte hain. Rose\n'King of flowers' kehlaata hai. [Q1255]\n63. Dendrimers — Pharmaceutical Nanotechnology\n● 'Dendrimers' nano-sized, radially symmetric molecules Health-Pharmaceutical industry mein use hote\nhain — anti-cancer drugs, transdermal drug delivery mein applications. [Q1257]\n64. Phototropism\n● 'Phototropism' ka matlab hai 'plants ka light ki taraf movement' — shoot growth ko light source ki\ndirection mein reorient karne ki ability. Positive-Negative phototropism hoti hai. [Q1258]\n65. Rhizome, Tuber, Bulb & Rhizoid — Underground Structures\n● 'Rhizome' segmented stem hai jo horizontally underground grow karta hai (Ginger, Poison Oak, Hops)\n— Tuber underground grows (Potato), Bulb short stem with fleshy leaves (onion, garlic). [Q1259]\n●\n Trap: Rhizoids 'multi-cellular aur epithelial tissues se composed' hote hain — ye INCORRECT hai.\n⚠️\nMosses mein multicellular, liverworts-hornworts mein UNICELLULAR hote hain, epithelial tissue se\nNAHI bane. Root hairs jaisa function karte hain bryophytes mein. [Q1296]\n66. Prunes — Dried Plums\n● 'Prunes' European plum (Prunus domestica) se obtain hote hain — dried plums hain, digestion help\nkarte hain, potassium-vitamins-iron rich hote hain. [Q1260]"," 67. Eutrophication\n● Lakes mein excessive Nitrogen-Phosphorus ki condition 'Eutrophic' kehlaati hai — plants-algae ki\ngrowth badhti hai, dissolved oxygen kam hota hai (harmful aquatic life ke liye). [Q1261]\n● Algal bloom se 'Eutrophication' hoti hai — excessive minerals-nutrients ki wajah se algae excessive\ngrow karti hai. [Q1270]\n68. Banana — Edible Endocarp & Mesocarp\n● Banana ka edible part 'Endocarp aur Mesocarp' hai — Epicarp outer skin hai, Mesocarp fleshy middle\nlayer, Endocarp innermost layer (seeds contain karta hai). [Q1262]\n69. Ectoparasites vs Endoparasites\n● 'Mosquito' ectoparasite ka example hai — host ke BAHAR rehta hai (flea bhi). Endoparasites\n(tapeworm, hookworm) host ke tissues-organs ke ANDAR rehte hain. [Q1263]\n70. Blood Sugar — Glucose\n● 'Glucose' ko 'blood sugar' kehte hain — 6-carbon compound hai, hydrogen-oxygen contain karta hai.\n[Q1264]\n71. Lipids — Glycerol & Fatty Acids\n● Lipids tab bante hain jab glycerol 'Fatty acids' se combine hoti hai — Oligosaccharides carbohydrate\nchains hain, Peptide amino acids ki short chain hai. [Q1265]\n72. Pulse Beat — Measured from Artery\n● Pulse beat 'Artery' se measure hoti hai — circulatory system ka part hai, oxygen-rich blood heart se\nbody cells tak le jaati hai. [Q1266]\n73. Brahmi — Ayurvedic Memory-Boosting Herb\n● 'Brahmi' (Bacopa monnieri) Ayurveda mein memory improve karne ke liye use hoti hai — bacosides\ncompounds cognitive function-memory-learning improve karte hain. [Q1267]"," 74. Sarcolemma — Muscle Fiber Membrane\n● 'Sarcolemma' muscle fiber (single muscle cell) ko cover karne wali membrane hai — physical forces\ncontrol karne mein help karti hai. [Q1268]\n75. Transpiration\n● Forests atmosphere ki humidity 'Transpiration' se badhate hain — plants soil se water lekar leaves se\nwater vapour release karte hain. [Q1269]\n● Plants mein water vapour ki form mein water loss ko 'Transpiration' kehte hain — roots se water absorb\nkarke stomata se release hoti hai, plant ko cool bhi karti hai. [Q1295]\n76. Plasmolysis\n● Living plant cell ka water lose karke shrink hona (osmosis se) 'Plasmolysis' kehlaata hai — Cytolysis cell\nburst hona hai (excess water se), Hemolysis RBC breakdown hai. [Q1271]\n77. Vocal Cords — Human Sound Production\n● Human sounds 'Vocal cord' mein vibrations se produce hote hain — larynx (voice box) mein hote hain,\nlungs se air pass hone par vibrate karte hain. [Q1273]\n78. Edward Jenner — Father of Immunology\n● 'Edward Jenner' smallpox vaccine develop ki, 'Father of Immunology' kehlaate hain — Antoni van\nLeeuwenhoek Father of Microbiology, Robert Koch ne TB-cholera ke organisms discover kiye. [Q1274]\n79. First-Aid Medicines — Ibuprofen & Antihistamines\n● 'Ibuprofen' pain, fever aur inflammation treat karne ke liye liya jaata hai — NSAID (Non-steroidal Anti-\ninflammatory Drug) hai. [Q1275]\n● 'Antihistamine' medications hay fever aur doosri allergies ke symptoms kam karne ke liye li jaati hain —\nAntacids indigestion-heartburn ke liye, Bronchodilators asthma ke liye hote hain. [Q1276]\n80. Carcinogens\n● 'Carcinogen' cancer directly cause karne wala substance hai — chemical, virus ya radiation ho sakta\nhai. Common carcinogens: Tobacco, Radon, Asbestos, UV Rays, Alcohol. [Q1277]"," 81. Heredity — Trait Transmission\n● Parents se offspring tak physical-mental traits ka transmission 'Heredity' kehlaata hai — progeny\nparents jaisi dikhti hai lekin identical nahi hoti (variation ki wajah se). [Q1279]\n82. Variations — Inherited During Reproduction\n● Reproduction ke dauran arise hone wali variations 'Inherited' ho sakti hain — genetic recombination,\nmutations, aur doosre factors ka result hoti hain. [Q1281]\n83. Somatic Mutation — Not Hereditary\n● 'Somatic' mutation hereditary NAHI hoti — body ke cells mein hoti hai (reproductive cells chhodkar),\nisliye offspring tak transmit nahi hoti. Deletion, Insertion, Duplication doosre mutation types hain. [Q1286]\n84. Regeneration — Not the Same as Reproduction\n● 'Regeneration' reproduction ke same NAHI hai — Budding, Fission, Multiple fission reproduction ke\nmodes hain, Regeneration repair-regrowth hai (Hydra, Planaria examples). [Q1287]\n● Regeneration ka matlab hai: 'lost part ka replacement' AUR 'small parts se poore body ki formation' —\ndono options sahi hain (Hydra-Planaria examples). [Q1299]\n85. Vascular System — Fluid Transport\n● 'Vascular' system ek jagah se doosri jagah fluids transport karta hai — plants mein water-nutrients,\nanimals mein cardiovascular system ki tarah, resources deliver karta hai aur mechanical support deta\nhai. [Q1288]\n86. Species & Kingdom — Classification Extremes\n● 'Species' living organisms ki classification ki basic unit hai — similar characteristics wale individuals ka\ngroup, interbreed karke fertile offspring bana sakte hain. [Q1289]\n● Classification hierarchy mein 'Kingdom' grouping mein sabse zyada organisms hote hain common\ncharacteristics ke saath — highest category hai biological classification mein. [Q1297]\n87. Cloning"," ● 'Cloning' se cell/organism ki exact copy production hoti hai — Dolly the sheep pehla cloned mammal thi\n(Ian Wilmut, Roslin Institute). Fertilization male-female sex cells ka fusion hai. [Q1290]\n88. Evolutionary Progress — Gradual Change\n● Primitive organisms mein millions of years mein gradual changes ki sequence, jo naye species banati\nhai, 'Evolutionary progress' kehlaati hai — Analogous/Homologous organs alag concepts hain. [Q1292]\n89. Tooth Enamel — Calcium Phosphate\n● Tooth enamel 'Calcium phosphate' se bana hota hai — hydroxyapatite crystal structure mein hota hai,\nbody ka hardest substance hai, pH 5.5 se neeche corrode hota hai. [Q1294]\n90. Muscular Force & Joints\n● Muscles ki action se generate hone wali force 'Muscular force' kehlaati hai — joints (fulcrum ki tarah) ke\nthrough movement karte hain. Joints 3 types: fibrous, cartilaginous, synovial. [Q1298]\n91. Smooth Muscle Tissue — Locations\n● Smooth (unstriated) muscle tissue 'Digestive system aur Artery' mein hoti hai — hollow visceral organs\nki walls mein, autonomic nervous system se control hoti hai, slow-involuntary contraction. [Q1300]\n92. Contractile Proteins — Actin & Myosin\n● Muscles mein special 'Contractile proteins' hote hain — thick-thin myofilaments (myosin-actin) se bane\nhote hain, muscle contraction sliding filament theory se explain hoti hai. [Q1302]\n● 'Contractile protein' (Actin aur Myosin) muscle tissue ke contraction-sagging mein help karti hai jisse\nmovement hota hai — Actin thin filaments, Myosin thick filaments. [Q1304]\n93. Glycogen — Energy Storage\n● Food se derived energy ka kuch hissa 'Glycogen' ki form mein store hota hai — muscles-liver mein\nstore hokar zaroorat par energy mein convert hota hai. [Q1305]\n94. Genotype-Phenotype — The ttRr Example"," ● Genotype 'ttRr' ka phenotype 'Dwarf aur Round' hoga — 'tt' Dwarf (recessive homozygous), 'Rr' Round\nseeds (dominant allele R). [Q1306]\n95. Tendon — Collagen & White Fibres\n● 'Tendon' mein abundant white fibres (collagen) hoti hain — muscles ko bone se connect karti hai.\nTypes: Flexor (bend joints), Extensor (straighten joints). [Q1307]\n● Tendon 'sirf collagen fibres' se bana hota hai — muscles ko bone se connect karta hai (fibrous\nconnective tissue). [Q1311]\n96. Reproduction — Maintaining Species\n● 'Reproduction' species ke individuals ki number maintain karne aur extinction rokne ke liye zaroori hai\n— biologically similar offspring produce karti hai. [Q1308]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Biology Chapter 22 Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0388","t":"01 Structure of Atom","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.1 — STRUCTURE OF ATOM — FULL MIND MAP\n⚗️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Subatomic Particles & Atomic Structure Basics\n2. Atomic Number, Mass Number & Isotopes\n3. Atomic Mass, Molecular Mass & Mole Concept\n4. Discovery Timeline & Scientists\n5. Atomic Models: Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Quantum\n6. Quantum Numbers, Orbitals & Shapes\n7. Electronic Configuration: Rules & Examples\n8. Valence Electrons, Valency & Chemical Properties\n9. Ions: Cations & Anions\n10. Radioactivity, Nuclear Reactions & Applications\n11. Periodic Trends: Radius, IE, EA & Electronegativity\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1–Q86)\n⚠️\n13. Numerical: Atomic Number, Mass Number & Subatomic Particles\n14. Numerical: Moles, Molar Mass & Mass Conversions\n15. Numerical: Number of Atoms, Molecules & Ions from Moles\n16. Numerical: Gram Atoms, Gram Molecules & Avogadro's Number\n17. Numerical: Molar Mass from Vapour Density & Gas Laws\n18. Numerical: Number of Molecules in Given Volume at STP\n19. Numerical: Percentage Composition\n20. Numerical: Empirical & Molecular Formula\n21. Numerical: Number of Electrons, Protons & Neutrons in Ions\n22. Numerical: Isotopic Mass & Average Atomic Mass\n23. Numerical: Electron Configuration & Quantum Numbers\n24. Numerical: Maximum Electrons in Shells/Subshells\n25. Numerical: Wavelength, Frequency & Energy of Electron Transitions\n26. Numerical: Limiting Reagent & Stoichiometry\n27. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n28.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q87–Q141)\n⚠️\n1. Subatomic Particles & Atomic Structure Basics\n● Proton = positively charged, nucleus mein hota hai; mass ≈ 1 u; charge = +e. [Q3, Q5, Q7]\n● Neutron = neutral (no charge), nucleus mein hota hai; mass ≈ 1 u. [Q3, Q5, Q7]\n● Electron = negatively charged, nucleus ke charon ore orbit/orbital mein; mass ≈ 1/1836 u (negligible); charge = −e.\n[Q3, Q5, Q7]\n● Nucleus mein sirf protons + neutrons hain; electrons bahar revolve karte hain. [Q3, Q5]\n● Neutrons nikaalne ka formula: n = A − Z. [Q6, Q8, Q71]\n2. Atomic Number, Mass Number & Isotopes\n● Atomic Number (Z) = number of protons = number of electrons (neutral atom mein). [Q4, Q6, Q8, Q71, Q77]\n● Mass Number (A) = protons + neutrons. [Q4, Q6, Q8, Q71, Q77]\n● Isotopes = same atomic number, different mass number; jaise C-12, C-13, C-14. [Q9, Q11]"," ● Isobars = same mass number, different atomic number; jaise Ar-40, Ca-40. [Q9, Q11]\n● Isotones = same number of neutrons; jaise C-14 (8n), N-15 (8n). [Q9, Q11]\n● Average atomic mass = Σ(isotope mass × relative abundance); example: Cl-35 (75%) + Cl-37 (25%) = 35.5 u. [Q77]\n3. Atomic Mass, Molecular Mass & Mole Concept\n● Atomic Mass Unit (amu/u) = 1/12th of C-12 atom ka mass; 1 u ≈ 1.66 × 10⁻²⁷ kg. [Q2, Q25]\n● Carbon = 12 u; Hydrogen = 1 u; Oxygen = 16 u; Nitrogen = 14 u. [Q2]\n● Molecular mass = atoms ke atomic masses ka sum; H₂O = 18 u; CO₂ = 44 u. [Q25, Q27]\n● Mole concept: 1 mole = 6.022 × 10²³ particles (Avogadro's number). [Q27, Q29]\n● 1 mole ka mass (grams mein) = molecular mass (u mein); 1 mole H₂O = 18 g. [Q27]\n● Molecules & Atomicity = ek molecule mein atoms ki sankhya: Monoatomic — Ar, Ne (1 atom); Diatomic — H₂, N₂,\nO₂, Cl₂ (2 atoms); Tetratomic — P₄ (4 atoms); Octatomic — S₈ (8 atoms, common elements mein sabse zyada).\n[Q1, Q26, Q28]\n● Compound = do ya zyada different elements ka fixed ratio mein chemical bonding se bana substance; Water\n(H₂O), Ammonia (NH₃), Nitrogen peroxide sab compounds hain, lekin Chlorine ek element hai (compound nahi).\n[Q32]\n● Molecule = compound ka smallest possible unit — do ya zyada atoms ka definite arrangement mein aggregate;\nAtom = element ka smallest particle; Nucleus = atom ke center ka positively charged region. [Q58]\n4. Discovery Timeline & Scientists\n● Dalton (1808): Atomic theory — indivisible atoms. [Q62, Q64]\n● J.J. Thomson (1897): Electron discover; cathode ray experiment; plum pudding model; e/m ratio measure ki. [Q38,\nQ40, Q62, Q64]\n● Millikan: Oil-drop experiment — electron ka exact charge (e = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C). [Q42]\n● Goldstein: Canal rays / positive rays discover ki — protons ka indication. [Q66]\n● Ernest Rutherford (1911): Gold foil experiment; nucleus discover; proton discover (1919); planetary model. [Q38,\nQ39, Q40, Q41, Q62, Q64]\n● James Chadwick (1932): Neutron discover; beryllium par alpha particle bombard karke. [Q38, Q40, Q62, Q64]\n● Niels Bohr (1913): Quantized orbits; hydrogen spectrum explain ki. [Q22, Q44, Q62, Q64]\n● Schrödinger (1926): Wave equation; quantum mechanical model. [Q68]\n● Heisenberg: Uncertainty Principle — position aur momentum simultaneously exact nahi. [Q68, Q70]\n● Moseley: Atomic number ka concept diya X-ray studies se. [Q59, Q66]\n5. Atomic Models: Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Quantum\n● Thomson's Plum Pudding Model: Positive sphere mein negative electrons embedded; uniform positive charge.\n[Q13, Q15, Q61, Q63]\n● Rutherford's Nuclear Model (Gold Foil Experiment): Atom ka most part khali hai; positive charge small dense\nnucleus mein concentrated; nucleus ka size atom se bahut chhota (≈10⁻¹⁵ m vs atom ≈10⁻¹⁰ m); electrons nucleus\nke charon ore revolve karte hain. [Q13, Q15, Q39, Q41, Q43]\n● Rutherford model ka drawback: classical physics ke hisaab se revolving electron continuously energy radiate karke\nspiral mein nucleus mein gir jaana chahiye — ye nahi hota. [Q20, Q43, Q63, Q65]\n● Bohr's Model: Electrons definite circular orbits/energy levels mein revolve karte hain bina energy lose kiye; har"," orbit ki fixed energy hai = energy level/shell (K, L, M, N...); energy absorb/release karke electron shell change\nkarta hai; angular momentum quantized hai: mvr = nh/2π. [Q22, Q24, Q44, Q46, Q65, Q67]\n● Bohr model ka limitation: sirf hydrogen-like species (single electron) ke liye accurate; multi-electron atoms ke\nspectral lines explain nahi kar paata. [Q48, Q67, Q69]\n● Quantum Mechanical Model (Schrödinger): Electron ko wave-particle duality ke saath describe kiya; exact\nlocation nahi, sirf probability — electron cloud/orbital; Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle: Δx × Δp ≥ h/4π. [Q68,\nQ70, Q72]\n6. Quantum Numbers, Orbitals & Shapes\n● Principal quantum number (n) = shell; values 1, 2, 3...; energy aur size decide karti hai. [Q45, Q47]\n● Azimuthal/Angular momentum quantum number (l) = subshell; values 0 se (n−1) tak: l=0 → s; l=1 → p; l=2 → d;\nl=3 → f. [Q45, Q47]\n● Magnetic quantum number (m ) = orbital orientation; values −l se +l tak: s — 1 orbital; p — 3 orbitals; d — 5\nₗ\norbitals; f — 7 orbitals. [Q47]\n● Spin quantum number (m ) = electron spin; values +½ ya −½.\nₛ\n [Q47]\n● Total electrons in a shell = 2n²; in a subshell = 2(2l+1). [Q45]\n● Orbital shapes: s-orbital — spherical, 2 electrons max; p-orbital — dumb-bell, 6 electrons max; d-orbital —\ncloverleaf/double dumb-bell, 10 electrons max; f-orbital — complex, 14 electrons max. [Q73, Q75]\n● Orbital = 3D space jahan electron milne ki probability max (≈90–95%) hoti hai; orbit (definite path) se alag hai.\n[Q72, Q74]\n● Orbital size n ke saath badhti hai; energy bhi badhti hai. [Q74]\n7. Electronic Configuration: Rules & Examples\n● Aufbau Principle: Electrons pehle lowest energy orbital mein bharte hain. [Q49, Q51]\n● Filling order: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s → 3d → 4p → 5s → 4d → 5p → 6s → 4f → 5d → 6p... [Q49]\n● Pauli Exclusion Principle: Ek orbital mein max 2 electrons ho sakte hain aur unke spins opposite (↑↓) hone\nchahiye. [Q49, Q51, Q76, Q78]\n● Hund's Rule of Maximum Multiplicity: Ek subshell ke orbitals mein electrons pehle singly bharte hain (same spin),\nphir pairing hoti hai. [Q49, Q51, Q76, Q78]\n● Common configurations: H (Z=1) — 1s¹; He (Z=2) — 1s²; C (Z=6) — 1s² 2s² 2p²; N (Z=7) — 1s² 2s² 2p³ (↑ ↑ ↑); O\n(Z=8) — 1s² 2s² 2p⁴; Na (Z=11) — [Ne] 3s¹; Ar (Z=18) — 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶; K (Z=19) — [Ar] 4s¹. [Q50, Q51, Q52, Q54]\n● Exceptions (stability ke liye): Cr (Z=24) — [Ar] 3d⁵ 4s¹ (half-filled d-subshell stability); Cu (Z=29) — [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s¹\n(fully-filled d-subshell stability). [Q56]\n● Ions ki configuration: Fe (Z=26) [Ar] 3d⁶ 4s² → Fe²⁺: [Ar] 3d⁶; Fe³⁺: [Ar] 3d⁵. Cu (Z=29) [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s¹ → Cu⁺: [Ar] 3d¹⁰.\nCl (Z=17) [Ne] 3s² 3p⁵ → Cl⁻: [Ne] 3s² 3p⁶ (octet). [Q79, Q81]\n8. Valence Electrons, Valency & Chemical Properties\n● Shells K, L, M, N... ya 1, 2, 3, 4... se denote hoti hain. [Q10, Q12, Q14]\n● Max electrons in a shell: 2n²; K=2, L=8, M=18, N=32. [Q10, Q12]\n● Outermost shell = valence shell; uske electrons = valence electrons; chemical properties ye decide karte hain.\n[Q14, Q16, Q18, Q53, Q55]\n● Outermost shell mein max 8 electrons ho sakte hain (octet rule). [Q14, Q16]\n● Valency = atom ka combining capacity: valence electrons ≤ 4 → valency = valence electrons (donate karega);"," valence electrons > 4 → valency = 8 − valence electrons (accept karega). [Q17, Q19, Q21]\n● Group 1 (alkali metals): 1 valence electron — highly reactive. [Q55]\n● Group 17 (halogens): 7 valence electrons — 1 electron accept karte hain. [Q55]\n● Group 18 (noble gases): 8 valence electrons (except He: 2) — chemically inert. [Q19, Q21, Q55]\n● Metals generally 1–3 valence electrons; electrons donate karte hain. Non-metals generally 5–7 valence electrons;\nelectrons accept karte hain. [Q21]\n● Covalently bonded molecules ka melting/boiling point low hota hai kyunki inke beech ki intermolecular forces\nweak hoti hain (covalent bond mein atoms electrons share karte hain). [Q60]\n9. Ions: Cations & Anions\n● Ion = charged atom/molecule; electron loss/gain se banta hai. [Q23, Q30]\n● Cation = positive ion; electron donate karke banta hai; generally metals. Na → Na⁺ + e⁻; Mg → Mg²⁺ + 2e⁻. [Q23]\n● Anion = negative ion; electron accept karke banta hai; generally non-metals. Cl + e⁻ → Cl⁻; O + 2e⁻ → O²⁻. [Q23]\n● Polyatomic ions: NH₄⁺, OH⁻, SO₄²⁻, CO₃²⁻, NO₃⁻. [Q30]\n10. Radioactivity, Nuclear Reactions & Applications\n● Radioactivity = unstable nucleus ka spontaneous disintegration; alpha, beta, gamma rays emit hoti hain. [Q31,\nQ33, Q35, Q80]\n● Alpha (α) = Helium nucleus (₂He⁴); +2 charge; least penetrating, most ionizing; paper se roka ja sakta hai. [Q31,\nQ33, Q80]\n● Beta (β) = high-speed electron (₋₁e⁰); −1 charge; moderate penetrating; aluminium se roka ja sakta hai. [Q31, Q33,\nQ80]\n● Gamma (γ) = EM waves; no charge; most penetrating, least ionizing; thick lead/concrete se roka ja sakta hai. [Q31,\nQ33, Q80]\n● Penetrating power: α < β < γ; Ionizing power: α > β > γ. [Q31, Q33]\n● Half-life (t½) = time in which half of radioactive atoms decay kar jaate hain. [Q35, Q37]\n● Example: 1g → 0.5g → 0.25g in 12 days means 2 half-lives; t½ = 6 days. [Q37]\n● Nuclear fission = heavy nucleus (U-235, Pu-239) split; chain reaction; nuclear reactor/atomic bomb. [Q34, Q36]\n● Nuclear fusion = light nuclei combine; sun/stars; hydrogen bomb; ~100 million °C chahiye. [Q34, Q36]\n● Radioactive decay types: Alpha decay — mass −4, atomic number −2; Beta decay — mass same, atomic number\n+1; Gamma decay — mass & atomic number same. [Q80]\n● Applications: C-14 dating (5730 years), Co-60 cancer treatment, I-131 thyroid diagnosis. [Q80]\n11. Periodic Trends: Radius, IE, EA & Electronegativity\n● Atomic radius = nucleus se outermost electron shell ki distance. Left to right (period): decrease (nuclear charge\nbadhta hai); Top to bottom (group): increase (new shell add hoti hai). [Q82, Q84]\n● Ionic radius: Cation < Parent atom (electron loss se effective nuclear charge badhta hai); Anion > Parent atom\n(electron gain se repulsion badhta hai). [Q84]\n● Isoelectronic species mein: jyada nuclear charge → chhota radius. N³⁻ > O²⁻ > F⁻ > Ne > Na⁺ > Mg²⁺ > Al³⁺ (sabke\npaas 10 electrons). [Q86]\n● Ionization Energy (IE) = gaseous atom se outermost electron remove karne ki energy. Left to right: increase; Top\nto bottom: decrease. [Q83, Q85]"," ● Electron Affinity (EA) = gaseous atom mein electron add karne par release hone wali energy. [Q83]\n● Electronegativity = shared electron pair ko apni taraf khinchne ki tendency; Pauling scale par max Fluorine (F =\n4.0). [Q85]\n● Same period ke Si, Na, Mg, Al mein sabse bada ion Na banata hai — kam nuclear charge ki wajah se electron loss\nke baad bhi ionic radius sabse zyada rehta hai. [Q57]\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1–Q86)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Neon (Ne) monoatomic hai — diatomic nahi; question mein intentionally confuse kiya tha. [Q1]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sulphur S₈ (8 atoms) — common elements mein sabse zyada atomicity. [Q1]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Isotopes = same Z, different A; Isobars = same A, different Z — ulta mat samajhna. [Q9, Q11]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electron nucleus mein nahi hota; nucleus mein sirf protons + neutrons hain. [Q3, Q5]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Orbit = definite path (Bohr model); Orbital = probability cloud (quantum model) — donon alag hain.\n[Q72, Q74]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Penetrating power: α < β < γ; Ionizing power: α > β > γ — reverse relation hai. [Q31, Q33]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gamma rays electromagnetic waves hain, charged particles nahi — isliye sabse zyada penetrate karti\nhain. [Q31]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Half-life mein sample ka mass exponentially decrease hota hai, linear nahi. [Q37]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rutherford ne nucleus/proton discover kiya; Chadwick ne neutron — donon alag hain. [Q38, Q40]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bohr model sirf hydrogen-like atoms ke liye accurate hai; multi-electron atoms ke liye nahi. [Q48, Q67,\nQ69]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 4s orbital 3d se pehle bharata hai Aufbau principle ke hisaab se — K (Z=19) ka configuration [Ar] 4s¹ hai,\n3d nahi. [Q54]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cr (Z=24) aur Cu (Z=29) exceptions hain — half-filled aur fully-filled d-subshell ki stability ke kaaran.\n[Q56]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cation bante waqt electrons outermost shell se pehle nikle; Fe²⁺ mein 4s se electrons gaye, 3d se nahi.\n[Q79]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fe³⁺ [Ar] 3d⁵ aur Cu⁺ [Ar] 3d¹⁰ — half-filled aur fully-filled d-subshell ki extra stability. [Q79, Q81]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Isoelectronic species mein jyada nuclear charge wala chhota hota hai — Na⁺ > Mg²⁺ > Al³⁺ mein radius\nghatta hai. [Q86]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: IE, EA, Electronegativity — teenon periodic trends similar hain (left→right increase, top→bottom\ndecrease) lekin exceptions hain (noble gases, Be, N). [Q83, Q85]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fluorine (F) sabse zyada electronegative hai — Oxygen nahi. [Q85]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Average atomic mass always closest to most abundant isotope hoti hai. [Q77]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Moseley's Law se atomic number determine hota hai, atomic mass nahi. [Q59]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 mole = 6.022 × 10²³ particles; yaad rakhna — \"mole\" number nahi, amount hai. [Q27, Q29]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cation positive hai (electron loss), Anion negative hai (electron gain) — sign confuse mat hona. [Q23]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chlorine ek element hai, compound nahi — compound banane ke liye do ya zyada different elements\nchahiye. [Q32]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Covalent molecules ki weak intermolecular forces ki wajah se low melting/boiling point hota hai. [Q60]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same period mein sabse kam nuclear charge wale element (jaise Na) ka ion sabse bada hota hai. [Q57]\n13. Numerical: Atomic Number, Mass Number & Subatomic Particles\n● Formula: Atomic number (Z) = Protons = Mass number (A) − Neutrons. [Q87, Q89, Q91]"," ● A = 298, neutrons = 189 → Z = 298 − 189 = 109. [Q87]\n● A = 40, neutrons = 20 → Z = 40 − 20 = 20 (Calcium). [Q89]\n● Z = 17, neutrons = 18 → A = 17 + 18 = 35 (Chlorine-35). [Q91]\n14. Numerical: Moles, Molar Mass & Mass Conversions\n● Formula: Moles = Given mass (g) / Molar mass (g/mol). [Q88, Q90, Q92, Q94, Q96]\n● H₂SO₄ ka molar mass = 2(1) + 32 + 4(16) = 98 g/mol; 25 g → 25/98 = 0.255 mol. [Q88]\n● NaOH ka molar mass = 23 + 16 + 1 = 40 g/mol; 20 g → 20/40 = 0.5 mol. [Q90]\n● CaCO₃ ka molar mass = 40 + 12 + 3(16) = 100 g/mol; 50 g → 50/100 = 0.5 mol. [Q92]\n● H₂O ka molar mass = 18 g/mol; 9 g → 9/18 = 0.5 mol. [Q94]\n● CO₂ ka molar mass = 12 + 2(16) = 44 g/mol; 22 g → 22/44 = 0.5 mol. [Q96]\n● Ca(OH)₂ ka relative mass = Ca (40.08) + 2×O (31.998) + 2×H (2.016) = 74 u. [Q107]\n● 90 g water mein moles = mass/molar mass = 90/18 = 5 moles. [Q108]\n● CO (Carbon monoxide) ka relative mass = C (12) + O (16) = 28. [Q109]\n● Ammonia (NH₃) mein N₂ aur H₂ ke masses ka ratio hamesha 14 : 3 hota hai (N ka mass 14, 3 H atoms ka mass 3).\n[Q110]\n● 60 g Helium mein moles = mass/molar mass = 60/4 = 15 moles (He ka molar mass = 4 g). [Q137]\n15. Numerical: Number of Atoms, Molecules & Ions from Moles\n● Formula: Number of particles = Moles × Avogadro's number (6.022 × 10²³). [Q93, Q95, Q97, Q99]\n● 0.5 mol H₂O mein molecules = 0.5 × 6.022 × 10²³ = 3.011 × 10²³. [Q93]\n● 1 mol CO₂ mein molecules = 6.022 × 10²³. [Q95]\n● 0.25 mol NaCl mein formula units = 0.25 × 6.022 × 10²³ = 1.5055 × 10²³. [Q97]\n● 2 mol O₂ mein molecules = 2 × 6.022 × 10²³ = 1.2044 × 10²⁴. [Q99]\n16. Numerical: Gram Atoms, Gram Molecules & Avogadro's Number\n● 1 gram atom = 1 mole atoms = 6.022 × 10²³ atoms; mass in grams = atomic mass. [Q111, Q113, Q115]\n● 1 gram molecule = 1 mole molecules = 6.022 × 10²³ molecules; mass in grams = molecular mass. [Q111, Q113]\n● 1 gram atom oxygen = 16 g mein 6.022 × 10²³ atoms. [Q111]\n● 1 gram molecule H₂O = 18 g mein 6.022 × 10²³ molecules. [Q113]\n● 1 gram atom sodium = 23 g mein 6.022 × 10²³ atoms. [Q115]\n17. Numerical: Molar Mass from Vapour Density & Gas Laws\n● Formula: Molar mass = 2 × Vapour density (VD). [Q98, Q100, Q102]\n● VD = 14 → Molar mass = 2 × 14 = 28 g/mol (N₂ ya CO). [Q98]\n● VD = 22 → Molar mass = 2 × 22 = 44 g/mol (CO₂). [Q100]\n● VD = 32 → Molar mass = 2 × 32 = 64 g/mol (SO₂). [Q102]"," 18. Numerical: Number of Molecules in Given Volume at STP\n● STP par: 1 mole gas = 22.4 L volume leti hai. [Q122, Q124, Q126]\n● 22.4 L gas at STP = 1 mole = 6.022 × 10²³ molecules. [Q123, Q125, Q127]\n● 11.2 L gas at STP = 11.2/22.4 = 0.5 mole → 3.011 × 10²³ molecules. [Q123]\n● 5.6 L gas at STP = 5.6/22.4 = 0.25 mole → 1.5055 × 10²³ molecules. [Q125]\n● 2.24 L gas at STP = 2.24/22.4 = 0.1 mole → 6.022 × 10²² molecules. [Q127]\n● 5.6 L gas ka mass 11 g → Molar mass = 11 × 22.4 / 5.6 = 44 g/mol. [Q122]\n● 2.24 L gas ka mass 4.4 g → Molar mass = 4.4 × 22.4 / 2.24 = 44 g/mol. [Q124]\n● 11.2 L gas ka mass 22 g → Molar mass = 22 × 22.4 / 11.2 = 44 g/mol. [Q126]\n19. Numerical: Percentage Composition\n● Formula: % of element = (Mass of element in compound / Molar mass of compound) × 100. [Q101, Q103, Q105]\n● H₂O mein H% = (2/18) × 100 = 11.11%. [Q101]\n● CaCO₃ mein Ca% = (40/100) × 100 = 40%. [Q103]\n● NH₃ mein N% = (14/17) × 100 = 82.35% ≈ 82.4%. [Q105]\n20. Numerical: Empirical & Molecular Formula\n● Empirical formula = simplest whole number ratio of atoms. [Q104, Q106]\n● Molecular formula = n × Empirical formula; jahan n = Molecular mass / Empirical formula mass. [Q104]\n● Empirical formula CH₂, molecular mass = 42 → Empirical mass = 14 → n = 42/14 = 3 → Molecular formula = C₃H₆.\n[Q104]\n21. Numerical: Number of Electrons, Protons & Neutrons in Ions\n● Neutral atom mein: Protons = Electrons = Atomic number (Z). [Q112, Q114, Q116]\n● Cation mein: Electrons = Z − positive charge; protons same. [Q112, Q116]\n● Anion mein: Electrons = Z + negative charge; protons same. [Q114]\n● Na⁺ (Z=11): protons = 11, electrons = 10, neutrons = 23 − 11 = 12. [Q112]\n● Cl⁻ (Z=17): protons = 17, electrons = 18, neutrons = 35 − 17 = 18. [Q114]\n● Mg²⁺ (Z=12): protons = 12, electrons = 10, neutrons = 24 − 12 = 12. [Q116]\n● Al³⁺ (Z=13): protons = 13, electrons = 10, neutrons = 27 − 13 = 14. [Q118]\n● O²⁻ (Z=8): protons = 8, electrons = 10, neutrons = 16 − 8 = 8. [Q120]\n22. Numerical: Isotopic Mass & Average Atomic Mass\n● Average atomic mass = Σ(Isotope mass × Relative abundance) / 100. [Q117, Q119, Q121]\n● Boron: B-10 (20%) + B-11 (80%) → Average = (10×20 + 11×80)/100 = 10.8 u. [Q117]\n● Chlorine: Cl-35 (75%) + Cl-37 (25%) → Average = 35.5 u. [Q119]\n● Neon: Ne-20 (90.51%), Ne-21 (0.27%), Ne-22 (9.22%) → Average ≈ 20.18 u. [Q121]"," 23. Numerical: Electron Configuration & Quantum Numbers\n● Z = 11 (Na): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s¹; valence electron = 1. [Q128, Q130]\n● Z = 17 (Cl): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁵; valence electron = 7. [Q128, Q130]\n● Z = 20 (Ca): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²; valence electron = 2. [Q132]\n● Z = 26 (Fe): [Ar] 3d⁶ 4s²; valence electrons = 2. [Q134]\n● Z = 29 (Cu) exception: [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s¹; valence electron = 1. [Q134]\n● Last electron ki quantum numbers: Na — n=3, l=0, m =0, m =+½; Cl — n=3, l=1, m =+1, m =−½.\nₗ\nₛ\nₗ\nₛ\n [Q133, Q135]\n24. Numerical: Maximum Electrons in Shells/Subshells\n● Shell mein max electrons = 2n². [Q129, Q131]\n● K=2, L=8, M=18, N=32. [Q129]\n● Subshell mein max: s=2, p=6, d=10, f=14. [Q131]\n25. Numerical: Wavelength, Frequency & Energy of Electron Transitions\n● Bohr energy: E = −13.6 Z²/n² eV.\nₙ\n [Q136, Q138, Q140]\n● Hydrogen ground state n=1: −13.6 eV. [Q136]\n● ΔE = −13.6 (1/n₂² − 1/n₁²) eV. [Q138]\n● n=2 → n=1: ΔE = 10.2 eV. [Q138]\n● Rydberg formula: 1/λ = R (1/n₁² − 1/n₂²). [Q140]\n● Lyman series: n=1 (UV); Balmer: n=2 (visible); Paschen: n=3; Brackett: n=4. [Q140]\n26. Numerical: Limiting Reagent & Stoichiometry\n● Limiting reagent = reaction mein pehle khatam hone wala reactant. [Q139, Q141]\n● 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O; 4 g H₂ (2 mol) + 32 g O₂ (1 mol) → O₂ limiting; H₂O = 36 g. [Q139]\n● N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃; 28 g N₂ (1 mol) + 6 g H₂ (3 mol) → exact ratio; NH₃ = 34 g. [Q141]\n27. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Atomic number: Z = A − n.\n● Moles: n = mass / molar mass.\n● Particles: N = n × Nₐ (Nₐ = 6.022 × 10²³).\n● Vapour density: M = 2 × VD.\n● % Composition: (mass of element / molar mass) × 100.\n● STP volume: 1 mol gas = 22.4 L.\n● Molar mass from STP: M = mass × 22.4 / Volume.\n● Bohr energy: E = −13.6 Z²/n² eV.\nₙ"," ● Rydberg formula: 1/λ = R (1/n₁² − 1/n₂²).\n● Limiting reagent: Compare mole ratio with balanced equation.\n28.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q87–Q141)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Atomic number = Mass number − Neutrons; electrons isme include nahi hote. [Q87]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Molar mass calculate karte waqt atomic masses ka accurate sum karo; H=1, O=16, C=12, N=14, S=32,\nNa=23, Ca=40, Cl=35.5. [Q88, Q90]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vapour density ka unit nahi hota; ye hydrogen gas ke density se ratio hai. [Q98]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Empirical formula mass aur molecular mass alag hain; n nikaalna mat bhoolna. [Q104]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ion mein protons aur neutrons same rehte hain; sirf electrons ki sankhya badalti hai. [Q112, Q114, Q116]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Na⁺, Mg²⁺, Al³⁺, O²⁻ sabke paas 10 electrons hain (isoelectronic) lekin protons alag hain. [Q112, Q116,\nQ118, Q120]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Average atomic mass mein percentage abundance se multiply karna hota hai; simple average nahi.\n[Q117, Q119]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: STP = 0°C, 1 atm; iske alag conditions par 22.4 L formula galat hoga. [Q122]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gram atom aur Gram molecule ab \"mole\" ke terms mein samajhe jaate hain. [Q111, Q113]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Quantum numbers nikaalne mein last electron ka spin dhyan se dekho — Hund's rule se pairing pattern\nsamajhna zaroori hai. [Q135]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lyman series UV mein hai; Balmer visible mein — ye regions yaad rakhna exam mein direct puchha jaata\nhai. [Q140]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Limiting reagent identify karne ke liye balanced equation ka mole ratio compare karo; mass directly\ncompare mat karo. [Q139, Q141]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bohr energy formula sirf hydrogen-like species (single electron) ke liye exact hai. [Q136, Q138]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ammonia mein N₂:H₂ mass ratio hamesha 14:3 hota hai — mole ratio (1:3) se confuse mat karna. [Q110]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 1 Structure of Atom Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0389","t":"02 Metals Nonmetals Alloys","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.2 — METALS, NON-METALS AND ALLOYS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚙️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Metals: Properties & General Characteristics\n2. Non-metals: Properties & General Characteristics\n3. Reaction of Metals with Water\n4. Reaction of Metals with Acids\n5. Reaction of Metals with Oxygen\n6. Amphoteric Oxides & Hydroxides\n7. Displacement Reactions & Reactivity Series\n8. Corrosion & Rusting Prevention\n9. Alloys: Composition & Uses\n10. Extraction of Metals: General Principles\n11. Extraction of Iron (Blast Furnace)\n12. Extraction of Aluminium (Hall-Héroult Process)\n13. Extraction of Copper\n14. Metalloids & Their Properties\n15. Non-metal Allotropes & Important Compounds\n16. Bleaching Powder, Baking Soda, Washing Soda & Plaster of Paris\n17. Metals in Biological Systems\n18. Acid Rain & Environmental Chemistry\n19. Physical Property Records: Melting Point, Conductivity, Malleability & Ductility\n20.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q142–Q274)\n⚠️\n1. Metals: Properties & General Characteristics\n● Metals ke outermost shell mein 1–3 valence electrons hote hain; ye electrons donate karte hain aur positive ions\n(cations) banate hain. [Q143, Q145, Q147, Q229]\n● Metals generally solid hote hain room temperature par (except Mercury — liquid). [Q144, Q146]\n● Metals ke paas metallic lustre hoti hai; ye good conductors of heat and electricity hote hain kyunki inme bahut se\nloosely bound electrons hote hain. [Q144, Q146, Q148, Q224]\n● Metals ductile (wire ban sakte hain) aur malleable (sheet ban sakti hai) hote hain. [Q148, Q150]\n● Metals ka boiling point aur melting point generally high hota hai. [Q150]\n● Metals ke oxide aur hydroxides basic hote hain. [Q145, Q149]\n● Metals electropositive hote hain kyunki ye electrons lose karke cations banate hain. [Q157]\n● Element = wo matter jise chemical reactions se simpler substances mein todaa nahi ja sakta. [Q197]\n2. Non-metals: Properties & General Characteristics\n● Non-metals ke outermost shell mein 4–7 valence electrons hote hain (kuch options mein 5,6,7,8 bhi bataya jaata\nhai); ye electrons accept karte hain aur negative ions (anions) banate hain. [Q143, Q145, Q147, Q271]\n● Non-metals gases ya brittle solids hote hain room temperature par (exception: Bromine — sirf non-metal jo liquid\nstate mein hoti hai). [Q144, Q146, Q177]\n● Non-metals non-lustrous hote hain (except Iodine — lustrous). [Q148, Q152]\n● Non-metals poor conductors hote hain (except Graphite — good conductor). [Q148, Q152, Q167, Q182]"," ● Non-metals neither ductile nor malleable hote hain. [Q150]\n● Non-metals ke oxide aur hydroxides acidic hote hain. [Q145, Q149]\n● Non-metals se hydrogen gas ban sakti hai water ke saath reaction karke (jaise C + H₂O → CO + H₂). [Q145]\n● Non-metals solid, liquid, ya gas — teenon states mein exist kar sakte hain; sirf solid state mein hona non-metal ki\nphysical property nahi hai. [Q259]\n● Chlorine ek non-metal ka example hai. [Q261]\n3. Reaction of Metals with Water\n● Sodium (Na) water ke saath vigorously react karta hai: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂↑; exothermic reaction. [Q142,\nQ154, Q222]\n● Potassium (K) sodium se bhi zyada vigorously react karta hai cold water ke saath; hydrogen gas burn ho jaati hai\nlilac flame ke saath. [Q154, Q156, Q269]\n● Sodium aur Potassium dono open air mein rakhne par turant fire pakad lete hain — isiliye inhe kerosene oil ke\nandar store karte hain. [Q245, Q257]\n● Calcium (Ca) water ke saath slowly react karta hai: Ca + 2H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ + H₂↑; calcium hydroxide (lime water)\nmilti hai. [Q154, Q156]\n● Magnesium (Mg) steam ke saath react karta hai; cold water se slowly. [Q156]\n● Iron (Fe) steam ke saath react karta hai: 3Fe + 4H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + 4H₂. [Q156]\n● Zinc (Zn) steam ke saath react karta hai: Zn + H₂O → ZnO + H₂. [Q156]\n● Aluminium bhi steam ke saath react karke metal oxide aur hydrogen deta hai. [Q201]\n● Copper (Cu), Silver (Ag), Gold (Au) water se react nahi karte. [Q156]\n● Reactivity order with water: K > Na > Ca > Mg > Zn > Fe > Cu. [Q154, Q156]\n●\n\n⚠️Aluminium par ek thin protective oxide layer (Al₂O₃) ban jaati hai jo isse cold ya hot water ke saath directly\nreact karne se roki hai — isliye \"Al cold/hot water se react nahi karta\" bhi sahi hai, jabki steam ke saath react\nkarta hai. [Q267]\n4. Reaction of Metals with Acids\n● Reactive metals (Zn, Fe, Mg, Al) dilute HCl ya H₂SO₄ ke saath react karke hydrogen gas dete hain. [Q158, Q160,\nQ162]\n● Zn + 2HCl → ZnCl₂ + H₂↑. [Q158]\n● Mg + H₂SO₄ → MgSO₄ + H₂↑. [Q160]\n● Fe + 2HCl → FeCl₂ + H₂↑ (Iron(II) chloride). [Q162]\n● Copper (Cu) dilute HCl se react nahi karta kyunki ye hydrogen se kam reactive hai. [Q162]\n● Copper concentrated H₂SO₄ se react karta hai: Cu + 2H₂SO₄ → CuSO₄ + SO₂ + 2H₂O. [Q162]\n● Reactivity order with acids: Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Cu. [Q160, Q162]\n5. Reaction of Metals with Oxygen\n● Metals oxygen ke saath react karke metal oxides banate hain. [Q164, Q166, Q168]\n● Sodium oxygen ke saath jaldi react karta hai: 4Na + O₂ → 2Na₂O. [Q164]\n● Magnesium air mein burn hota hai: 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO; bright white flame. [Q164, Q166]\n● Iron moist air mein rust karta hai: 4Fe + 3O₂ + xH₂O → 2Fe₂O₃·xH₂O. [Q166, Q168]"," ● Copper heat karne par black copper oxide banata hai: 2Cu + O₂ → 2CuO. [Q168]\n● Copper hawa mein slowly oxidize hoke green colour ki coating banata hai (copper corrosion). [Q159]\n● Gold aur Silver oxygen se react nahi karte; inert hain. [Q168]\n● Metal oxides generally basic hote hain; kuch amphoteric (Al₂O₃, ZnO). [Q166]\n● Kuch metals (jaise alloys) high temperature par easily oxidize/burn nahi hote — pure metals ki compare mein\nzyada stable hote hain. [Q209]\n6. Amphoteric Oxides & Hydroxides\n● Amphoteric oxides both acid aur base ke saath react karte hain. [Q170, Q172, Q174]\n● Examples: Al₂O₃, ZnO, PbO, SnO. [Q170, Q172]\n● Al₂O₃ + 6HCl → 2AlCl₃ + 3H₂O (base ki tarah). [Q170]\n● Al₂O₃ + 2NaOH → 2NaAlO₂ + H₂O (acid ki tarah). [Q170]\n● ZnO + 2HCl → ZnCl₂ + H₂O. [Q172]\n● ZnO + 2NaOH → Na₂ZnO₂ + H₂O. [Q172]\n● Aluminium hydroxide Al(OH)₃ bhi amphoteric hai. [Q174]\n7. Displacement Reactions & Reactivity Series\n● Zyada reactive metal kam reactive metal ke salt solution se usko displace kar sakta hai — Metal A, Metal B ko\ndisplace kare to A, B se zyada reactive hai. [Q176, Q178, Q180, Q263]\n● Complete reactivity series (high to low): K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Ni > Sn > Pb > H > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au >\nPt. [Q176, Q178]\n● Zn + CuSO₄ → ZnSO₄ + Cu (Zn more reactive than Cu). [Q176]\n● Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu (Iron displaces copper; blue solution green ho jaati hai). [Q178]\n● Cu + FeSO₄ → No reaction (Cu less reactive than Fe). [Q178]\n● Cu + 2AgNO₃ → Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2Ag (Copper displaces silver). [Q180]\n● Zinc, Aluminium se kam reactive hai — reactivity series mein Al, Zn se upar hai. [Q151]\n● Reactivity order examples: Ca > Al > Cu > Hg; K > Al > Fe > Pb > Au — high se low reactivity ke sequence yaad\nrakhna. [Q153, Q161]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Displacement reaction ke liye reactivity series compare karna zaroori hai; directly mat karo. [Q176, Q178]\n8. Corrosion & Rusting Prevention\n● Corrosion = metals ka atmosphere ke saath reaction karke gradually destroy hona. [Q181, Q183, Q185]\n● Rusting = iron ka corrosion; moist air mein hota hai; rust ka formula: Fe₂O₃·xH₂O (reddish-brown). [Q181, Q183]\n● Rusting ke liye oxygen + water donon zaroori hain. [Q183, Q185]\n● Prevention ke tarike: Painting (gates, bridges); Oiling/greasing (machinery); Galvanization — iron par zinc ki\ncoating, sacrificial protection; Electroplating — chromium/nickel coating; Alloying — stainless steel (Fe + Cr + Ni +\nC). [Q185, Q187, Q189]\n● Galvanized iron = iron coated with zinc; zinc pehle oxidize hota hai (sacrificial anode). [Q187, Q189, Q213]"," 9. Alloys: Composition & Uses\n● Alloy = do ya zyada metals (ya metal + non-metal) ka mixture; properties pure metals se better hoti hain. [Q190,\nQ192, Q194]\n● Brass = Cu (60–80%) + Zn (20–40%); utensils, decorative items, musical instruments. [Q190, Q192, Q231]\n● Bronze = Cu (88%) + Sn (12%); statues, medals, bearings, bells. [Q190, Q194]\n● Stainless Steel = Fe + Cr + Ni + C; utensils, surgical instruments, cutlery (rust-resistant). [Q196, Q198, Q268, Q270]\n● Duralumin = Al + Cu + Mg + Mn; aircraft parts, lightweight structures. [Q196, Q200, Q268, Q270]\n● Solder = Pb + Sn; electrical joints, plumbing (low melting point). [Q198, Q200, Q211, Q233, Q272, Q274]\n● Amalgam = Hg + any other metal; dental fillings (Ag-Hg). [Q202, Q247, Q272]\n● Gunmetal = Cu + Sn + Zn; bearings, valves. [Q202]\n● Bell metal = Cu + Sn; bells, gongs (harder than bronze). [Q204]\n● German silver / Nickel silver = Cu + Zn + Ni; decorative items, utensils. [Q204]\n● Magnalium = Al + Mg; aircraft parts, lightweight, scientific instruments. [Q206, Q270, Q272]\n● Constantan = Cu + Ni alloy; resistance wires mein use hota hai (resistance temperature ke saath almost constant\nrehta hai). [Q205]\n● Nichrome = Ni, Cr, Mn aur Fe ka alloy; high resistance aur heat-resistant, electrical heating elements (heater, iron)\nmein use. [Q237]\n● Steel ko hard aur strong banane ke liye Carbon add kiya jaata hai; Manganese bhi steel ko harden karne ke liye\nuse hota hai. [Q173, Q273]\n10. Extraction of Metals: General Principles\n● Metals ores se extract kiye jaate hain; ore = metal-containing mineral + impurities (gangue). [Q208, Q210, Q212]\n● Calcination = ore ko strongly heat karna absence of air mein; volatile impurities nikalte hain; carbonate ore →\noxide. Example: ZnCO₃ → ZnO + CO₂. [Q210, Q212]\n● Roasting = ore ko heat karna presence of air mein; sulphide ore → oxide. Example: 2ZnS + 3O₂ → 2ZnO + 2SO₂.\n[Q210, Q212]\n● Smelting = roasted/calcined ore ko reducing agent (C, CO) ke saath heat karna to get metal. Example: ZnO + C →\nZn + CO. [Q212]\n● Flux = gangue ko slag mein convert karne ke liye substance add karte hain. Acidic gangue (SiO₂) ke liye basic flux\n(CaO, limestone); Basic gangue ke liye acidic flux (SiO₂). [Q214]\n● Monazite Thorium ka important ore hai. [Q171]\n● Limestone ek non-metallic mineral ka example hai. [Q165]\n11. Extraction of Iron (Blast Furnace)\n● Blast furnace mein iron extract hota hai haematite ore (Fe₂O₃) se. [Q216, Q218, Q220]\n● Charge: iron ore + coke (C) + limestone (CaCO₃). [Q216]\n● Reactions: Coke burn: C + O₂ → CO₂; CO₂ + C → 2CO (reducing agent). Reduction: Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂. Flux\naction: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂; CaO + SiO₂ → CaSiO₃ (slag). [Q218]\n● Molten iron furnace ke bottom par collect hota hai; slag upper layer par (lighter). [Q220]\n● Pig iron = impure iron; cast iron, wrought iron aur steel isse further process karke milti hai. [Q220]"," 12. Extraction of Aluminium (Hall-Héroult Process)\n● Aluminium extract hota hai bauxite ore (Al₂O₃·2H₂O) se. [Q208, Q210]\n● Bauxite se pehle Al₂O₃ (alumina) purify karte hain Bayer's process se. [Q210]\n● Electrolysis of molten alumina: Al₂O₃ dissolved in molten cryolite (Na₃AlF₆). Cathode: Al³⁺ + 3e⁻ → Al; Anode: 2O²⁻\n→ O₂ + 4e⁻; oxygen carbon anode se react karke CO₂ banata hai. [Q208]\n● Cryolite add karne se melting point kam hota hai aur conductivity badhti hai. [Q208]\n● Aluminium sirf electrolysis se hi extract kiya ja sakta hai — kyunki ye highly reactive metal hai. [Q217, Q219]\n● Anodising process mein Aluminium ki surface par protective oxide layer banane ke liye dilute sulphuric acid\nelectrolyte ke roop mein use hota hai. [Q169]\n13. Extraction of Copper\n● Copper extract hoti hai copper pyrites (CuFeS₂) se. [Q214, Q216]\n● Roasting: 2CuFeS₂ + O₂ → Cu₂S + 2FeS + SO₂.\n● Bessemerization: 2Cu₂S + 3O₂ → 2Cu₂O + 2SO₂; phir Cu₂S + 2Cu₂O → 6Cu + SO₂. [Q214]\n● Blister copper = 98–99% pure; electrolytic refining se 99.9% pure milti hai. [Q214]\n14. Metalloids & Their Properties\n● Metalloids = metals aur non-metals ke beech ki properties rakhte hain; semiconductors hote hain. [Q221, Q223,\nQ225]\n● Common metalloids: Boron (B), Silicon (Si), Germanium (Ge), Arsenic (As), Antimony (Sb), Tellurium (Te). [Q221,\nQ223, Q155, Q175, Q195]\n● Silicon aur Germanium electronics mein semiconductors ke roop mein extensively use hote hain. [Q225, Q227]\n● Metalloids ka lustre metallic hota hai lekin brittle hote hain; oxides amphoteric hote hain. [Q223, Q225]\n● Alkali metals mein Lithium sabse chhota (smallest) hota hai size mein. [Q191]\n● Silicon photovoltaic solar cells banane mein predominantly use hota hai. [Q163]\n● Atomic number 14 wala element (Silicon) hard hota hai aur acidic oxide + covalent halide banata hai — isiliye\nMetalloid category mein aata hai. [Q199]\n15. Non-metal Allotropes & Important Compounds\n● Carbon ke allotropes: Diamond, Graphite, Fullerene, Graphene. [Q226, Q228]\n● Diamond = hardest natural substance; sp³ hybridization; bad conductor.\n● Graphite = soft, slippery; sp² hybridization; good conductor (delocalized electrons); lubricant aur pencil lead mein\nuse. [Q228]\n● Sulphur ke allotropes: Rhombic (α-sulphur), Monoclinic (β-sulphur); Sulphur molecule polyatomic hoti hai (S₈).\n[Q230, Q232, Q179]\n● Phosphorus ke allotropes: White (P₄), Red, Black. [Q230, Q232]\n● White phosphorus = poisonous, glows in dark (chemiluminescence), stored under water. [Q232]\n● Red phosphorus = non-poisonous, stable, matchbox striker mein use. [Q232]\n● Nitrogen = inert diatomic gas (N≡N triple bond strong); Haber process mein ammonia banane ke liye use. [Q234,\nQ236]\n● Fluorine bhi ek diatomic non-metal hai. [Q188]"," ● Chlorine = greenish-yellow poisonous gas; water purification, bleaching powder (CaOCl₂) banane mein. [Q234,\nQ236]\n16. Bleaching Powder, Baking Soda, Washing Soda & Plaster of Paris\n● Bleaching powder = CaOCl₂ (Calcium oxychloride); chlorine ka smell; bleaching aur disinfecting mein use. [Q238,\nQ240, Q242]\n● Manufacturing: Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂ → CaOCl₂ + H₂O (Back process). [Q240]\n● Baking soda = NaHCO₃ (Sodium bicarbonate); mild base; baking, antacid, fire extinguisher mein. [Q238, Q242, Q244]\n● Washing soda = Na₂CO₃·10H₂O (Sodium carbonate decahydrate); laundry, glass manufacturing, water softening\nmein. [Q238, Q244, Q246]\n● Baking soda se washing soda banane ka reaction: 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂ (heat karke). [Q244]\n● Plaster of Paris = CaSO₄·½H₂O; surgery mein fracture set karne ke liye; gypsum se banata hai (CaSO₄·2H₂O heat\nkarke). [Q246, Q248]\n17. Metals in Biological Systems\n● Iron (Fe) = haemoglobin mein hota hai; oxygen transport blood mein. [Q250, Q252]\n● Calcium (Ca) = bones aur teeth mein (as calcium phosphate); muscle contraction, nerve signaling; water se denser\nhota hai. [Q250, Q252, Q193]\n● Magnesium (Mg) = chlorophyll ka central atom; photosynthesis ke liye zaroori. [Q252, Q254]\n● Zinc (Zn) = enzymes (carbonic anhydrase, alcohol dehydrogenase) mein cofactor; immunity. [Q254, Q256]\n● Copper (Cu) = haemocyanin (some animals mein oxygen carrier); enzymes mein; electrical wires banane mein bhi\nuse hota hai (good conductor). [Q256, Q243]\n● Iodine (I) = thyroid hormone (thyroxine) banane ke liye; goitre disease iodine deficiency se hoti hai; ye samundra\nmein abundantly milta hai. [Q258, Q260, Q184]\n● Manganese ek trace element hai jo body mein thodi matra mein zaroori hota hai. [Q186]\n● Sodium (Na) aur Potassium (K) = nerve impulse transmission; Na-K pump. [Q258, Q260]\n● Fluorine (F) = teeth enamel strengthen karne ke liye; fluoride toothpaste mein. [Q260]\n18. Acid Rain & Environmental Chemistry\n● Acid rain = pH < 5.6; H₂SO₄ aur HNO₃ se banta hai. [Q262, Q264, Q266]\n● Causes: SO₂ (fossil fuel burning) aur NOₓ (vehicles) atmosphere mein jaake water ke saath acid banate hain.\n[Q262, Q264]\n● Effects: marble/statues corrode (CaCO₃ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + H₂O + CO₂), aquatic life damage, soil fertility reduce.\n[Q266]\n● Taj Mahal ka yellowing acid rain ki wajah se hota hai. [Q266]\n19. Physical Property Records: Melting Point, Conductivity, Malleability & Ductility\n● Metals mein sabse zyada malleable Gold (Au) hai; Silver (Ag) sabse zyada malleable metals mein bhi mention hota\nhai depending on comparison set — dono soft aur highly malleable metals hain. [Q251, Q253, Q265]\n● Sabse zyada ductile metal Gold (Au) hai — sabse patla tar bana sakte hain. [Q255]"," ● Tungsten (W) ka melting point aur boiling point sabse zyada hota hai sab metals mein — isliye bulb ka filament\nTungsten se banaya jaata hai. [Q215, Q249]\n● Gallium (Ga) ka melting point bahut kam hota hai (near room temperature). [Q239]\n● Silver compounds (jaise silver bromide) black and white photography mein use hote hain. [Q241]\n● Electrical resistivity order: Hg > Ni > W > Ag (Mercury sabse zyada resistive, Silver sabse kam). [Q203]\n● Lead (Pb) aur Mercury (Hg) heat ke comparatively poor conductor hote hain. [Q235]\n20.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q142–Q274)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mercury metal hai lekin liquid hai room temperature par — exception yaad rakhna. [Q144, Q146, Q207]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Graphite non-metal hai lekin good conductor hai — diamond non-conductor hai donon carbon ke\nallotropes hain. [Q148, Q152, Q228, Q182]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Iodine non-metal hai lekin lustrous hai — exception. [Q152]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bromine ek hi non-metal hai jo liquid hai room temperature par. [Q144, Q177]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sodium water ke saath H₂ gas deta hai, O₂ nahi; reaction exothermic hai. [Q142]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Copper dilute HCl se react nahi karta; concentrated H₂SO₄ se react karta hai. [Q162]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Iron dilute acid se FeCl₂ (Iron II) banata hai, FeCl₃ nahi. [Q162]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Al₂O₃ aur ZnO amphoteric hain — sirf basic nahi; acid + base donon se react karte hain. [Q170, Q172]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Displacement reaction mein zyada reactive metal salt solution mein displace karta hai; solid metal se\nnahi. [Q176, Q178]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Calcination = air absent mein heat; Roasting = air present mein heat — donon alag hain. [Q210, Q212]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Calcination carbonate ore ke liye; Roasting sulphide ore ke liye — ore type ke hisaab se choose karte\nhain. [Q210, Q212]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Flux gangue ko slag mein convert karta hai; slag lighter hoti hai aur upper layer par aati hai. [Q214]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Blast furnace mein coke reducing agent hai; CO₂ phir C ke saath react karke CO banata hai. [Q218]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Stainless steel mein chromium + nickel add karte hain rust resistance ke liye; sirf carbon nahi. [Q196,\nQ198]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Brass = Cu + Zn; Bronze = Cu + Sn — confuse mat hona. [Q190, Q192, Q194]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solder ka melting point constituent metals (Pb, Sn) se kam hota hai — isliye joints mein use hota hai.\n[Q198, Q200, Q272, Q274]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Amalgam = mercury + any metal; dental filling mein silver amalgam use hota hai. [Q202, Q272]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: White phosphorus poisonous aur water mein store karte hain; Red phosphorus stable aur matchbox\nmein. [Q232]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bleaching powder = CaOCl₂; Baking soda = NaHCO₃; Washing soda = Na₂CO₃·10H₂O — teenon alag\nformulas hain. [Q238, Q240, Q242, Q244, Q246]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Plaster of Paris = CaSO₄·½H₂O; Gypsum = CaSO₄·2H₂O — 2H₂O vs ½H₂O difference hai. [Q248]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chlorophyll mein Magnesium (Mg) central atom hai, Iron nahi — haemoglobin mein Fe hota hai. [Q254]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Goitre Iodine deficiency se hota hai; Fluoride deficiency se nahi — dental caries Fluoride se prevent hoti\nhai. [Q258, Q260]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acid rain ka pH < 5.6 hota hai; normal rain ka pH ≈ 5.6 (CO₂ ki wajah se slightly acidic). [Q262, Q264]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acid rain mein H₂SO₄ aur HNO₃ donon hote hain; sirf H₂SO₄ nahi. [Q266]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Aluminium cold/hot water se react nahi karta (protective oxide layer ki wajah se) lekin steam ke saath\nreact karta hai — subtle difference. [Q201, Q267]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sodium aur Potassium kerosene oil ke andar store karte hain kyunki ye open air mein turant fire pakad\nlete hain. [Q245, Q257, Q269]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tungsten sabse zyada melting/boiling point wala metal hai — filament banane ke liye isiliye use hota"," hai. [Q215, Q249]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gold sabse zyada malleable aur ductile metal hai — Silver bhi highly malleable hota hai, confuse na\nkarein. [Q251, Q253, Q255, Q265]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 2 Metals, Non-metals and Alloys Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0390","t":"03 Acid Bases Salt","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.3 — ACID, BASES AND SALT — FULL MIND MAP\n🧪\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Chlor-Alkali Process\n2. Indicators: Natural, Synthetic & Olfactory\n3. pH Scale & Common pH Values\n4. Strong vs Weak Acids & Bases\n5. Neutralization, Salt Types & pH\n6. Common Salts: Preparation, Properties & Uses\n7. Water of Crystallization, Efflorescence & Deliquescence\n8. Acids & Bases in Nature, Daily Life & Industry\n9. Salt Classification: Normal, Acidic, Basic, Double, Complex & Mixed\n10. Alums, Amphoteric Oxides & Water Purification\n11. Soap vs Detergent & Water Softening\n12. Acid Rain, Tooth Decay & Antacids\n13. Metal Carbonates & Bicarbonates with Acids\n14.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q275–Q447)\n⚠️\n1. Chlor-Alkali Process\n● Chlor-alkali process = aqueous NaCl ka electrolysis; products: Hydrogen (H₂), Chlorine (Cl₂), Sodium hydroxide\n(NaOH). [Q275, Q277]\n● Reaction: 2NaCl(aq) + 2H₂O(l) → 2NaOH(aq) + Cl₂(g) + H₂(g). [Q275]\n● Use: soap, detergents, paper, PVC, bleach manufacturing mein. [Q275]\n2. Indicators: Natural, Synthetic & Olfactory\n● Natural indicators: Red cabbage leaves (purple→red in acid, green/yellow in base), turmeric, litmus. [Q276, Q278]\n● Synthetic indicators: Methyl orange, phenolphthalein, universal indicator. [Q276, Q278]\n● Olfactory indicators = jinki smell acidic ya alkaline medium mein change ho jaati hai: Onion, clove, vanilla — acid\nmein apni smell lose karte hain, base mein retain karte hain. [Q276, Q280, Q359, Q369, Q381]\n● Red cabbage leaves = natural acid-base indicator. [Q276]\n● Methyl orange = synthetic acid-base indicator; basic solution mein yellow ho jaata hai. [Q276, Q336]\n● Onion, clove = olfactory indicator. [Q276]\n● Litmus solution = purple dye jo lichen (ek plant) se extract kiya jaata hai; neutral solution mein iska colour purple\nrehta hai. [Q315, Q319, Q367, Q385]\n● Jasmine flower leaves acid/base presence indicate nahi karte — ye indicator nahi hain. [Q386]\n● Statement check: Olfactory indicator ek material hai jiski smell acid/base mein change hoti hai — ye statement\nsahi hai. [Q285]\n● Iodine solution starch ki presence detect karne ke liye use hota hai (starch-specific indicator, acid-base nahi).\n[Q307]\n● NaOH (sodium hydroxide) solution pH paper ko blue kar deti hai (basic nature ki wajah se). [Q311]\n● Borax ek basic substance hai — litmus add karne par ye blue ho jaata hai. [Q332]\n● Phenolphthalein alkalis mein pink ho jaata hai; acids mein colourless rehta hai. [Q347]"," ● Sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄) blue litmus ko red kar deta hai (acidic nature). [Q413]\n● Dry HCl gas dry litmus paper ka colour change nahi karta — ionization ke liye water zaroori hai. [Q423]\n● Universal indicator ek mixture hai jo different pH par different colours deta hai — exact pH measure karne ke liye\nbest indicator hai; ye \"metals aur non-metals ka mixture\" nahi hota (galat statement). [Q415, Q432]\n● Phenolphthalein acidic aur neutral solutions ke beech distinguish nahi kar sakta — dono mein colourless rehta\nhai. [Q428]\n3. pH Scale & Common pH Values\n● pH scale = 0 se 14; pH 7 = neutral (pure water at 25°C). [Q279, Q281, Q283, Q397]\n● pH < 7 = acidic; pH > 7 = basic/alkaline. [Q279, Q281]\n● Strong acid: pH 0–3 (HCl, H₂SO₄, HNO₃); Weak acid: pH 4–6 (acetic acid, citric acid). [Q283]\n● Strong base: pH 11–14 (NaOH, KOH); Weak base: pH 8–10 (NH₄OH). [Q283]\n● Lemon juice: pH ≈ 2.0–2.5 — solutions mein sabse minimum pH value in hone ke examples mein se ek. [Q391,\nQ393, Q395, Q398]\n● Vinegar: pH ≈ 2.4–3.4; Black coffee: pH ≈ 5.0. [Q391, Q393, Q395]\n● Milk: pH ≈ 6.6; Pure water: pH = 7.0; Blood: pH ≈ 7.35–7.45. [Q395, Q397, Q399]\n● Human body ka normal pH range approximately 7.0 se 7.8 ke beech hota hai. [Q438]\n● Baking soda solution: pH ≈ 8.3; Milk of magnesia: pH ≈ 10.5; Drain cleaner: pH ≈ 13–14. [Q399, Q401, Q403]\n● pH = −log[H⁺]; [H⁺] = 10^(−pH). [Q287]\n● [H⁺] = 1 × 10⁻⁵ mol/L ho to pH = 5 hoga. [Q425]\n● Universal indicator mein red colour pH 0 se 3 ko show karta hai (highly acidic). [Q339]\n● Highly acidic mixture ka pH value 0 ke kareeb hoti hai. [Q390]\n● Acid strong ionize karta hai to zyada H⁺ ions produce hote hain, jitni zyada concentration utni zyada acidity — is\nse solution zyada acidic ban jaata hai jaise pH = 4 wala solution pH = 7 se zyada acidic hoga (zyada H⁺\nconcentration). [Q301, Q329, Q355]\n● High concentration of hydroxide (OH⁻) ions wala solution basic hota hai aur uska pH value high hoti hai. [Q309]\n● Neutral solution ka pH value exactly 7 hota hai — na acidic na basic. [Q371]\n● Blue litmus red ho jaaye to solution ka pH 7 se kam hoga (acidic). [Q326]\n● Red litmus blue ho jaaye to solution basic hoga, jaise pH ≈ 10 wala solution. [Q417]\n● pH badhne ke saath (7 se 14 tak) OH⁻ ion concentration increase hoti hai. [Q361]\n● Pure water mein H⁺ aur OH⁻ ions ki concentration barabar (equal) hoti hai — isiliye ye neutral hai. [Q375]\n● pH 3 se pH 6 hone par H⁺ ion concentration 1000 guna kam ho jaati hai (har unit pH change = 10x factor). [Q421]\n● Alkaline solution mein [H⁺] < 1 × 10⁻⁷ mol/L hoti hai. [Q434]\n● Concentrated acid ko dilute karne ke liye hamesha acid ko water mein add karte hain, water ko acid mein nahi\n(safety ke liye — exothermic reaction). [Q334, Q440]\n● Light rain (pH < 5.6) jab river mein jaata hai to river water ka pH decrease ho jaata hai. [Q317]\n●\n\n⚠️pH 7 neutral sirf 25°C (298 K) par hota hai; temperature change se water ka pH badalta hai. [Q397]\n4. Strong vs Weak Acids & Bases\n● Strong acids = water mein completely dissociate: HCl, H₂SO₄, HNO₃, HBr, HI, HClO₄. [Q282, Q284, Q286]\n● Weak acids = partially dissociate: CH₃COOH (acetic acid/vinegar), H₂CO₃ (carbonic acid), citric acid, tartaric acid,\noxalic acid. [Q284, Q286, Q370, Q372]"," ● Strong bases = completely dissociate: NaOH (caustic soda), KOH (caustic potash), Ba(OH)₂. [Q288, Q290, Q292]\n● Weak bases = partially dissociate: NH₄OH (ammonia solution), Mg(OH)₂, Al(OH)₃. [Q288, Q290]\n● Ca(OH)₂ = slaked lime (strong base, slightly soluble); CaO = quick lime; CaCO₃ = limestone. [Q292]\n● Listed weak acids mein sabse weak acetic acid ya benzoic acid ho sakta hai depending on comparison — dono\nweak acids ke examples hain. [Q321, Q363, Q400]\n● Acidic solutions water mein electricity conduct karte hain kyunki ye H⁺ (hydrogen) ions produce karte hain. [Q341,\nQ402]\n● Acid mein zyada ionize hokar zyada H⁺ dena \"stronger acid\" banata hai; base bhi similarly water mein completely\nionize hoke zyada OH⁻ deti hai to \"stronger base\" banti hai. [Q405, Q407]\n● Water solution mein: Acids H⁺ dete hain; Bases OH⁻ dete hain. [Q409]\n● Metals acids ke saath react karke salt aur Hydrogen gas dete hain. [Q419]\n● Weak acid aur uske salt ka solution buffer solution kehlata hai — ye pH change ko resist karta hai. [Q327]\n● Acids ki common properties: sour taste, blue litmus ko red kar dete hain. [Q351]\n● Alkalis (bases) ka taste sour nahi hota — ye bitter/soapy hota hai; sour taste acids ki property hai, alkalis ki nahi.\n[Q387]\n5. Neutralization, Salt Types & pH\n● Neutralization = Acid + Base → Salt + Water + Heat. [Q289, Q291, Q293]\n● Example: HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O; H₂SO₄ + 2NaOH → Na₂SO₄ + 2H₂O. [Q289, Q291]\n● Neutralization exothermic reaction hai; neutral salt ka pH = 7. [Q293]\n● Strong acid + Strong base → Neutral salt (pH 7); jaise NaCl (strong acid HCl + strong base NaOH). [Q295, Q389,\nQ436]\n● Strong acid + Weak base → Acidic salt (pH < 7); zero ke kareeb pH wala salt strong acid + weak base se banta hai.\n[Q295, Q392]\n● Weak acid + Strong base → Basic salt (pH > 7); jaise Sodium carbonate (weak carbonic acid + strong NaOH). [Q295,\nQ349]\n● Normal salt = acid ka all replaceable H⁺ replace ho: NaCl, Na₂SO₄. [Q427, Q429]\n● Acid salt = partial H⁺ replace ho: NaHSO₄ (sodium bisulphate), NaHCO₃. [Q429, Q431]\n● Basic salt = partial OH⁻ replace ho: Cu(OH)Cl (basic copper chloride). [Q431, Q433]\n● Ammonium phosphate ek acidic salt ka example hai. [Q430]\n6. Common Salts: Preparation, Properties & Uses\n● Sodium chloride (NaCl) = common salt; food preservative, chlor-alkali raw material; molecular weight ≈ 58 g/mol\n(Na=23 + Cl=35.5). [Q294, Q296, Q322]\n● Sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO₃) = baking soda; mild base; baking, antacid, fire extinguisher. [Q296, Q298, Q338, Q340,\nQ342]\n● Preparation: NaCl + NH₃ + CO₂ + H₂O → NaHCO₃ + NH₄Cl (Solvay process). [Q338]\n● Heating: 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂. [Q342]\n● Sodium carbonate (Na₂CO₃·10H₂O) = washing soda; laundry, glass, paper, water softening industry mein use; iske\ncrystals mein 10 water of crystallisation molecules hote hain. [Q296, Q298, Q344, Q346, Q348, Q299]\n● Baking soda se heat karke washing soda banata hai; phir crystallization. [Q344]\n● Washing soda hygroscopic hai; efflorescence dikha sakta hai. [Q348]\n● Bleaching powder (CaOCl₂) = calcium oxychloride; disinfectant, bleaching, water treatment. [Q298, Q300, Q331,\nQ333, Q335]"," ● Manufacturing: Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂ → CaOCl₂ + H₂O (Back process). [Q331, Q333]\n● Acid ke saath: CaOCl₂ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + Cl₂ + H₂O. [Q337]\n● Plaster of Paris (CaSO₄·½H₂O) = surgery, decorative work, toys, fracture setting. [Q300, Q302, Q350, Q352, Q354]\n● Preparation: Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) ko 373 K par heat karke. [Q350, Q352]\n● Water add karne par hard crystalline mass banata hai (expansion hota hai). [Q354]\n● Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) = cement manufacturing mein setting time control. [Q356, Q358]\n7. Water of Crystallization, Efflorescence & Deliquescence\n● Water of crystallization = salt crystals mein fixed number of chemically bound water molecules. [Q360, Q362, Q364]\n● Examples: CuSO₄·5H₂O (Blue vitriol, 5 water); FeSO₄·7H₂O (Green vitriol, 7 water); Na₂CO₃·10H₂O (10 water).\n[Q360, Q362, Q364]\n● Efflorescence = hydrated salt air mein water lose karke powdery ban jaata hai. Washing soda: Na₂CO₃·10H₂O →\nNa₂CO₃·H₂O + 9H₂O. [Q364, Q366]\n● Deliquescence = solid air se moisture absorb karke solution ban jaata hai. Example: CaCl₂, NaOH, KOH. [Q366,\nQ368]\n● Hygroscopic = moisture absorb karte hain bina dissolve hue. Example: Conc. H₂SO₄, silica gel. [Q368]\n8. Acids & Bases in Nature, Daily Life & Industry\n● Citric acid = citrus fruits; Acetic acid (CH₃COOH) = vinegar (5–8% concentration); Tartaric acid = tamarind, grapes.\n[Q370, Q372, Q374, Q357]\n● Lactic acid = curd, milk; muscle cramps during exercise; ek three-carbon molecule hai. [Q374, Q376, Q324]\n● Oxalic acid = spinach, tomatoes; Formic acid (HCOOH/Methanoic acid) = ant/nettle sting. [Q376, Q378, Q380, Q383,\nQ396]\n● Ant bite se hone wala acidic effect moist baking soda ya Calamine solution rubbing karke neutralize kiya ja sakta\nhai. [Q323]\n● Ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) = citrus, amla; scurvy prevention — \"Ascorbic acid - Tamarind\" ek incorrect pairing hai\n(tamarind mein tartaric acid hota hai, ascorbic acid nahi). [Q380, Q382, Q330]\n● Boric acid eyewash solutions mein constituent ke roop mein use hota hai. [Q325]\n● Muriatic acid, Hydrochloric acid (HCl) ka hi scientific/commercial naam hai. [Q328]\n● Baking powder = Sodium hydrogen carbonate (NaHCO₃) + Tartaric acid ka mixture hota hai. [Q353, Q373]\n● Sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄) = \"King of chemicals\"; fertilizers, dyes, paints, detergents, petroleum refining; ise water\nmein dissolve karna highly exothermic hota hai. [Q404, Q406, Q408, Q384]\n● Nitric acid (HNO₃) = fertilizers, explosives (TNT), dyes. [Q406, Q408]\n● Hydrochloric acid (HCl) = steel cleaning, pickling, food processing. [Q408, Q410]\n● Phosphoric acid (H₃PO₄) = soft drinks, fertilizers, dental cement. [Q412, Q414]\n● Sodium hydroxide (NaOH) = soap, detergents, paper, textiles, drain cleaner; basic nature ka strong example.\n[Q416, Q418, Q420, Q345]\n● Calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH)₂) = whitewash, soil treatment, sugar refining. [Q418, Q420]\n● Ammonia (NH₃) = fertilizers, nitric acid, refrigeration, cleaning. [Q420, Q422]\n● Magnesium hydroxide (Mg(OH)₂) = milk of magnesia; antacid, laxative. [Q422, Q424]\n● Aluminium hydroxide (Al(OH)₃) = antacid, water purification, dyeing mordant. [Q424, Q426]\n● Hydrogen element sabhi acids mein common hota hai (acid ki defining property). [Q379]\n● CCl₄ (Carbon tetrachloride) acidic nahi hota hai. [Q377]"," ● Ester generally ek acid aur alcohol ki reaction se banta hai. [Q388]\n9. Salt Classification: Normal, Acidic, Basic, Double, Complex & Mixed\n● Double salt = do simple salts equimolar proportions mein crystallize; Mohr's salt (FeSO₄·(NH₄)₂SO₄·6H₂O), potash\nalum. [Q433, Q435]\n● Complex salt = complex ion banta hai; K₄[Fe(CN)₆] (Potassium ferrocyanide). [Q435, Q437]\n● Mixed salt = ek salt mein do different anions ya cations; CaOCl₂ (bleaching powder), NaKCO₃. [Q437, Q439]\n10. Alums, Amphoteric Oxides & Water Purification\n● Alum = double sulphate salt; general formula M⁺M³⁺(SO₄)₂·12H₂O. [Q439, Q441, Q443]\n● Potash alum = KAl(SO₄)₂·12H₂O; water purification, dyeing, baking powder. [Q441]\n● Chrome alum = KCr(SO₄)₂·12H₂O; tanning, photography. [Q443]\n● Alum water purification mein coagulating agent ki tarah kaam karta hai — suspended particles settle ho jaate\nhain. [Q441, Q443]\n● Metal oxides generally basic nature ke hote hain — acid ke saath react karke salt + water banate hain (jaise Na₂O,\nMgO, CaO). [Q305, Q313]\n● Cu(OH)₂ ek alkali nahi hai — kuch metal hydroxides insoluble hote hain aur alkali category mein nahi aate. [Q297]\n● Al₂O₃ (Aluminium oxide) ek amphoteric oxide hai — ye acids aur bases donon ke saath react karta hai, isliye \"basic\nmetal oxides\" ke general rule ka odd-one-out example hai. [Q365, Q394, Q442]\n11. Soap vs Detergent & Water Softening\n● Soap = sodium/potassium salt of long-chain fatty acids; animal fats/vegetable oils ka NaOH/KOH se hydrolysis\n(saponification). [Q444, Q445, Q446]\n● Synthetic detergent = sodium salts of long-chain benzene sulphonic acids; petroleum se bante hain. [Q444, Q445]\n● Soap hard water mein achchha kaam nahi karta kyunki Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺ se insoluble scum (calcium stearate) banata hai.\n[Q446, Q447]\n● Detergent hard water mein bhi kaam karta hai; Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺ se soluble complex nahi banata. [Q446, Q447]\n● Soap biodegradable hai; kuch detergents non-biodegradable hain (environmental pollution). [Q447]\n● Soap cleansing micelle formation se hoti hai — hydrophobic tail grease mein, hydrophilic head water mein. [Q445,\nQ447]\n● Temporary hardness = Ca(HCO₃)₂/Mg(HCO₃)₂; boiling se remove: Ca(HCO₃)₂ → CaCO₃↓ + H₂O + CO₂. [Q346]\n● Permanent hardness = CaSO₄/CaCl₂; washing soda (Na₂CO₃) se remove: CaSO₄ + Na₂CO₃ → CaCO₃↓ + Na₂SO₄.\n[Q346, Q348]\n● Zeolite/Permutit process = ion exchange se water softening. [Q348]\n12. Acid Rain, Tooth Decay & Antacids\n● Acid rain = pH < 5.6; H₂SO₄ aur HNO₃ se banta hai. [Q304, Q306, Q308]\n● Causes: SO₂ (fossil fuels) aur NOₓ/Nitrogen oxides (vehicles) emission — sirf SO₂ nahi, nitrogen oxides bhi acid rain\ncause karte hain. [Q304, Q306, Q343]\n● Effects: marble/statues corrode (CaCO₃ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + H₂O + CO₂), aquatic life damage, soil infertility. [Q306,"," Q308]\n● Taj Mahal ka yellowing = acid rain effect. [Q308]\n● Tooth enamel = calcium phosphate (Ca₃(PO₄)₂); hardest body substance. [Q310, Q312, Q411]\n● pH < 5.5 par enamel corrode hoti hai; bacteria acid produce karte hain. [Q310]\n● Toothpaste basic hota hai; acid neutralize karke enamel protect karta hai; fluoride enamel strengthen karta hai.\n[Q312]\n● Antacids = excess stomach acid neutralize karne ke liye mild bases hain — ye strong acids nahi hote (common\nmisconception). [Q314, Q316, Q318, Q303]\n● Examples: Mg(OH)₂ (Milk of magnesia), Al(OH)₃, NaHCO₃ (Baking soda — antacid ka active ingredient), CaCO₃.\n[Q314, Q316, Q320]\n● Strong base (NaOH, KOH) antacid ke roop mein nahi use hote — harmful hain. [Q316]\n● Ranitidine, Omeprazole = modern antacids; acid production kam karte hain. [Q318]\n13. Metal Carbonates & Bicarbonates with Acids\n● Metal carbonates + dilute acid → salt + water + CO₂. [Q340]\n● Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂↑. [Q346]\n● NaHCO₃ + HCl → NaCl + H₂O + CO₂↑ (baking soda antacid action). [Q340]\n● CO₂ gas limewater (Ca(OH)₂) ko milky (CaCO₃ precipitate) banati hai — CO₂ test. [Q337]\n14.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q275–Q447)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chlor-alkali process mein Oxygen nahi, H₂ + Cl₂ + NaOH products hain. [Q275]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Olfactory indicators = onion/clove/vanilla; Natural = red cabbage/turmeric/litmus; Synthetic = methyl\norange/phenolphthalein — alag categories hain. [Q276]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Litmus lichen (plant) se extract hota hai — ye ek natural indicator hai jiska neutral colour purple hota\nhai. [Q315, Q319, Q367, Q385]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: pH 7 neutral sirf 25°C par hota hai; garam pani ka pH 7 se kam hota hai lekin still neutral. [Q397]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ca(OH)₂ = slaked lime (strong base); CaO = quick lime; CaCO₃ = limestone — teenon alag hain. [Q292]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Caustic soda = NaOH; Caustic potash = KOH; Washing soda = Na₂CO₃ — caustic vs washing confuse mat\nhona. [Q292, Q346]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Neutralization hamesha salt + water deta hai; CO₂ nahi (carbonate reaction alag hai). [Q289]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Strong acid + Weak base → acidic salt; Weak acid + Strong base → basic salt — final pH decide karta hai\nkaunsa strong hai. [Q295]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda = NaHCO₃; Washing soda = Na₂CO₃·10H₂O; Baking powder = NaHCO₃ + Tartaric acid —\nteenon alag. [Q338, Q344, Q353]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Plaster of Paris CaSO₄·½H₂O; Gypsum CaSO₄·2H₂O; Anhydrite CaSO₄ — alag hydration states. [Q350,\nQ356]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Efflorescence = water lose karke powdery; Deliquescence = moisture absorb karke liquid — opposite.\n[Q364, Q366]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hygroscopic = moisture absorb bina dissolve hue; Deliquescent = dissolve ho jaata hai — alag hain.\n[Q366, Q368]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bleaching powder formula CaOCl₂ hai; CaCl₂ nahi — chlorine oxidation state alag hai. [Q331, Q333]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Formic (Methanoic) acid ant sting mein; Acetic acid vinegar mein — donon alag organic acids. [Q378,\nQ380, Q396]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tooth decay pH < 5.5 par shuru hoti hai; normal mouth pH ≈ 6.5–7.5; body ka overall pH range 7.0–7.8"," hai. [Q310, Q438]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH aur KOH strong base hain antacid ke roop mein nahi use hote — internal tissues damage kar sakte\nhain. [Q316]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sulphuric acid \"King of chemicals\" hai kyunki sabse zyada use hota hai — iska matlab ye nahi ki sabse\nstrong hai. [Q404, Q406]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acid salt mein replaceable H⁺ bacha rehta hai (NaHSO₄); Normal salt mein sab H⁺ replace ho gaya\n(Na₂SO₄). [Q429, Q431]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Double salt crystals mein equimolar salts hain; Complex salt mein complex ion hota hai — donon alag\nhain. [Q433, Q435]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alum ka general formula M⁺M³⁺(SO₄)₂·12H₂O hota hai; sabhi alums sulphate hain. [Q439, Q441]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Soap hard water mein scum banata hai; detergent nahi banata — isliye detergent hard water mein\nbetter hai. [Q446, Q447]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Temporary hardness boiling se jaati hai; Permanent hardness washing soda/ion exchange se jaati hai —\nalag methods. [Q346, Q348]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acid rain mein H₂SO₄ aur HNO₃ donon hote hain; sirf SO₂ nahi, nitrogen oxides bhi cause karte hain.\n[Q306, Q343]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acid rain ka pH < 5.6 hota hai; normal rain ka pH ≈ 5.6 (CO₂ ki wajah se slightly acidic). [Q304]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Concentrated acid dilute karte waqt hamesha acid ko water mein daalo, ulta karne se violent\nexothermic reaction ho sakti hai. [Q334, Q440]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Al₂O₃ amphoteric hai — sirf basic metal oxides ke general rule ka exception hai. [Q365, Q394, Q442]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Phenolphthalein acidic aur neutral solutions mein colourless rehta hai — inhe distinguish nahi kar sakta;\nalkalis mein pink hota hai. [Q347, Q428]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 3 Acid, Bases and Salt Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0391","t":"04 Carbon and Its Compounds","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.4 — CARBON AND ITS COMPOUNDS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚫\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Carbon: Electronic Configuration & Basics\n2. Carbon Allotropes: Diamond, Graphite, Fullerene & Graphene\n3. Organic Chemistry Basics: Hydrocarbons\n4. Functional Groups & Homologous Series\n5. IUPAC Nomenclature & Common Names\n6. Isomerism in Carbon Compounds\n7. Chemical Properties: Combustion, Oxidation, Addition & Substitution\n8. Ethanol: Preparation, Properties & Uses\n9. Ethanoic Acid: Properties, Reactions & Uses\n10. Soaps & Detergents\n11. Petroleum, Natural Gas & Petrochemicals\n12. Plastics: Thermoplastic vs Thermosetting\n13. Polymers: Natural vs Synthetic\n14. Rubber: Natural & Synthetic\n15. Environmental Impact & Non-biodegradable Substances\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q448–Q518)\n⚠️\n1. Carbon: Electronic Configuration & Basics\n● Carbon ka atomic number 6; electronic configuration: 1s² 2s² 2p²; simplified 2, 4. [Q448, Q450]\n● Carbon ke paas 2 shells hain (K aur L); valence electrons = 4; isliye tetravalent hai. [Q448]\n● Carbon non-metal hai (Gold, Platinum, Copper ke opposite jo metals hain — carbon inme se belong nahi karta);\nhuman body ka 18% mass; high melting point. [Q448, Q480, Q506]\n● Uses: diamonds (jewelry), inks, paints, carbon dating. [Q448]\n● Carbon 4 covalent bonds bana sakta hai; huge variety of organic compounds possible — carbon compounds mein\nhamesha covalent bonding hoti hai, ionic bond generally nahi paayi jaati. [Q450, Q452, Q476, Q466]\n● Carbon dioxide (CO₂) mein carbon ki valency 4 hoti hai. [Q508]\n● Carbon apna nucleus chhota hone ki wajah se shared electron pairs ko strongly hold karta hai — isiliye strong\nbonds banata hai. [Q482, Q498]\n● Catenation = carbon ki property jiski wajah se uske atoms aapas mein jud kar lambi chains bana sakte hain. [Q510]\n● Catenation property aur tetravalency dono milkar carbon compounds ki bahut badi variety possible banate hain.\n[Q471]\n● Silicon (Si) carbon jaisi catenation property dikhata hai (thodi kam extent mein). [Q462]\n● Organic carbon compounds ka melting point ionic compounds se kam hota hai kyunki inke molecules ke beech\nintermolecular forces weak hoti hain (covalent molecular structure). [Q464]\n● Do ya zyada elements combine hoke ek compound banate hain. [Q514]\n2. Carbon Allotropes: Diamond, Graphite, Fullerene & Graphene\n● Allotropes = same element, different structural forms; different physical properties. [Q451, Q453, Q455]\n● Diamond: Har carbon sp³ hybridized; tetrahedral 3D network; har carbon atom 4 other carbon atoms se bonded\nhota hai. Hardest natural substance; bad conductor (no free electrons). Jewelry, cutting tools, glass cutting aur"," rock drilling mein use. [Q451, Q453, Q492, Q502, Q512]\n● Diamond ko synthetically bhi bana sakte hain — pure carbon ko very high pressure aur high temperature dekar.\n[Q484]\n● Graphite: Har carbon sp² hybridized; hexagonal layers — har carbon atom same plane mein 3 other carbon atoms\nse bonded hota hai. Layers ke beech weak van der Waals forces; slippery. Good conductor (delocalized π\nelectrons); pencil lead, lubricant, electrodes. [Q453, Q455, Q504]\n● Fullerene (C₆₀): Soccer ball/football jaisi cage-like shape; 12 pentagons + 20 hexagons. Medical applications,\nnanotechnology, superconductors. [Q455, Q457, Q478]\n● Graphene = single layer of graphite; excellent conductor, strong, flexible. [Q457]\n● Aerographene duniya ka sabse halka (lightest) material hai — carbon ka ek advanced nano-structure. [Q496]\n● Coal carbon ka allotrope nahi hai — Diamond, Graphite, Fullerene, Graphene sab allotropes hain lekin Coal ek\nmixture hai (allotrope nahi). [Q500]\n● Coke (carbon ka ek form) metallurgy mein reducing agent ke roop mein use hota hai (jaise blast furnace mein iron\nextraction). [Q516]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Diamond aur graphite donon carbon ke allotropes hain lekin properties bilkul alag — structure ki wajah\nse. [Q451, Q453]\n3. Organic Chemistry Basics: Hydrocarbons\n● Hydrocarbons = sirf carbon aur hydrogen se bane compounds. [Q452, Q454]\n● Saturated hydrocarbons (Alkanes): C-C single bonds; general formula C H₂ ₊₂. Methane CH₄, Ethane C₂H₆,\nₙ\nₙ\nPropane C₃H₈, Butane C₄H₁₀. [Q454, Q456]\n● Unsaturated hydrocarbons: Alkenes — C=C double bond; formula C H₂ — Ethene C₂H₄, Propene C₃H₆. Alkynes —\nₙ\nₙ\n\nC≡C triple bond; formula C H₂ ₋₂ — Ethyne C₂H₂, Propyne C₃H₄.\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q456, Q458]\n● Cycloalkanes: ring structure; saturated; formula C H₂ . Cyclohexane C₆H₁₂: 6 C-C bonds + 12 C-H bonds = 18 total\nₙ\nₙ\ncovalent bonds. [Q449]\n● Aromatic hydrocarbons: benzene ring (C₆H₆); alternate double bonds; resonance stabilized. [Q458, Q460]\n● Sucrose molecule mein 12 carbon atoms hote hain (C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁). [Q490]\n4. Functional Groups & Homologous Series\n● Functional group = atom/group jo molecule ki chemical properties decide karta hai. [Q459, Q461, Q463]\n● Common functional groups: Alcohol (−OH) — ethanol C₂H₅OH, suffix -ol. Aldehyde (−CHO) — methanal HCHO,\nethanal CH₃CHO, suffix -al (jaise Pentanal — 5-carbon aldehyde). Ketone (>C=O) — propanone CH₃COCH₃, suffix\n-one. Carboxylic acid (−COOH) — ethanoic acid CH₃COOH, suffix -oic acid. Halide (−X) — chloromethane CH₃Cl,\nprefix chloro-. Amine (−NH₂) — methanamine CH₃NH₂, suffix -amine. [Q461, Q463, Q465, Q474]\n● Homologous series = same functional group; successive members mein CH₂ ka difference. Alkanes: CH₄, C₂H₆,\nC₃H₈... Alcohols: CH₃OH, C₂H₅OH, C₃H₇OH... [Q465, Q467]\n5. IUPAC Nomenclature & Common Names\n● Naming: prefix (carbon count) + root word (ane/ene/yne) + suffix (functional group). [Q467]\n● Methane = CH₄; Ethane = C₂H₆; Propane = C₃H₈; Butane = C₄H₁₀. [Q454]\n● Ethene = C₂H₄; Propene = C₃H₆; Ethyne = C₂H₂; Propyne = C₃H₄. [Q456, Q458]\n● Methanol = CH₃OH; Ethanol = C₂H₅OH. [Q461]"," ● Methanal = HCHO; Ethanal = CH₃CHO. [Q463]\n● Propanone = CH₃COCH₃; Butanone = CH₃COC₂H₅. [Q465]\n● Methanoic acid = HCOOH; Ethanoic acid = CH₃COOH. [Q467]\n● Common names: Ethanol = ethyl alcohol; Ethanoic acid = acetic acid; Propanone = acetone. [Q467, Q469]\n6. Isomerism in Carbon Compounds\n● Isomers = same molecular formula, different structural formula/arrangement. [Q468, Q470, Q472]\n● Structural isomerism: Chain isomerism — different carbon skeleton (Butane vs Isobutane). Position isomerism —\nsame functional group, different position (Propan-1-ol vs Propan-2-ol). Functional group isomerism — different\nfunctional groups (Ethanol vs Dimethyl ether). [Q470, Q472]\n● Butane (C₄H₁₀) ke 2 isomers: n-butane aur isobutane. [Q472]\n● Pentane (C₅H₁₂) ke 3 isomers. [Q472]\n●\n\n⚠️Isomers ki molecular formula same hoti hai lekin properties alag ho sakti hain. [Q468, Q470]\n7. Chemical Properties: Combustion, Oxidation, Addition & Substitution\n● Combustion: Carbon compounds oxygen mein burn karke CO₂ + H₂O + Heat dete hain. CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O.\nSaturated = clean flame; Unsaturated = sooty flame (kam hydrogen). [Q473, Q475]\n● Carbon apne saare allotropic forms mein oxygen mein jalke Carbon dioxide (CO₂) deta hai. [Q494]\n● Oxidation: Alcohols → Aldehydes → Carboxylic acids. C₂H₅OH + [O] → CH₃CHO + H₂O → CH₃COOH (acidified\nK₂Cr₂O₇/KMnO₄). [Q477, Q479, Q493, Q495]\n● Addition reaction: Unsaturated compounds mein atoms add hote hain double/triple bond break hokar. C₂H₄ + H₂\n→ C₂H₆ (hydrogenation). C₂H₄ + Br₂ → C₂H₄Br₂ (bromine water decolourise). [Q479]\n● Substitution reaction: Saturated compounds mein atom replace hota hai. CH₄ + Cl₂ → CH₃Cl + HCl (UV light).\n[Q477]\n● Esterification: Carboxylic acid + Alcohol → Ester + Water (conc. H₂SO₄). CH₃COOH + C₂H₅OH → CH₃COOC₂H₅ +\nH₂O; sweet smell. [Q503, Q505]\n● Saponification: Ester + NaOH/KOH → Soap + Glycerol. [Q511]\n8. Ethanol: Preparation, Properties & Uses\n● Ethanol colourless liquid; pleasant smell; volatile; miscible with water. [Q481, Q483, Q485]\n● Preparation (Fermentation): C₆H₁₂O₆ → 2C₂H₅OH + 2CO₂ (yeast enzyme zymase, anaerobic). [Q481, Q483]\n● Rectified spirit = 95% ethanol + 5% water; Absolute alcohol = 100% pure. [Q485]\n● Denatured alcohol = ethanol + methanol/pyridine (non-potable). [Q485]\n● Uses: alcoholic beverages, medicines, solvent, perfumes, gasohol (petrol + ethanol fuel). [Q487, Q489]\n● Ethanol weak acid; sodium ke saath slow reaction: 2C₂H₅OH + 2Na → 2C₂H₅ONa + H₂↑. [Q489, Q491]\n● Dehydration conc. H₂SO₄ se: 170°C → Ethene (C₂H₅OH → C₂H₄ + H₂O). 140°C → Diethyl ether (2C₂H₅OH →\nC₂H₅OC₂H₅ + H₂O). [Q495]\n9. Ethanoic Acid: Properties, Reactions & Uses"," ● Pure ethanoic acid = glacial acetic acid (freezing point 17°C). [Q497, Q499]\n● 5–8% solution = vinegar; food preservative, pickling. [Q499, Q501]\n● Weak acid; organic acid hone ki wajah se partial dissociation. [Q501]\n● Esterification: Alcohol ke saath sweet-smelling ester. [Q503, Q505]\n● NaOH ke saath: CH₃COOH + NaOH → CH₃COONa + H₂O. [Q507]\n● Carbonates/bicarbonates ke saath CO₂ release: 2CH₃COOH + Na₂CO₃ → 2CH₃COONa + H₂O + CO₂↑. [Q507]\n● Mg, Zn ke saath H₂ gas: 2CH₃COOH + Mg → (CH₃COO)₂Mg + H₂↑. [Q509]\n10. Soaps & Detergents\n● Soap = sodium/potassium salts of long-chain fatty acids; saponification se banta hai. Fat/Oil + NaOH → Soap +\nGlycerol. [Q511, Q513]\n● Cleansing micelle formation se — hydrophobic tail grease mein, hydrophilic head water mein. [Q513, Q515]\n● Soap hard water mein scum (Ca/Mg insoluble salts) banata hai; cleaning capacity kam. [Q515, Q517]\n● Detergents = synthetic; petroleum se; Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺ se precipitate nahi; hard water mein better. [Q515, Q517]\n● Soap biodegradable; kuch detergents non-biodegradable (water pollution). [Q517]\n● Shampoo, washing powder = synthetic detergents. [Q517]\n11. Petroleum, Natural Gas & Petrochemicals\n● Petroleum = fossil fuel; crude oil; mixture of hydrocarbons. [Q489, Q491]\n● Refining = fractional distillation; fractions alag boiling points par collect hote hain. LPG < Petrol/Gasoline <\nKerosene < Diesel < Lubricating oil < Paraffin wax < Asphalt. [Q491]\n● Natural gas mainly methane (CH₄); CNG = compressed natural gas. [Q493]\n● Petrochemicals = petroleum se chemicals; plastics, synthetic fibres, rubber, detergents, medicines. [Q495]\n● Methane (CH₄) = simplest hydrocarbon; marsh gas, gobar gas, CNG; greenhouse gas. [Q481]\n● Aerated drinks (soda water) mein solute ke roop mein Carbon dioxide gas dissolved hoti hai. [Q488]\n12. Plastics: Thermoplastic vs Thermosetting\n● Thermoplastics = heat par soft, reshape ho sakte hain, recycle ho sakte hain. Examples: Polythene (PE), PVC,\nPolystyrene, Teflon. Uses: bags, bottles, toys, pipes. [Q497, Q499]\n● Thermosetting plastics = ek baar set hone ke baad heat par melt nahi hote; permanently hard. Examples: Bakelite,\nMelamine, Polyester resin. Uses: electrical switches, handles, utensils, laminates. [Q499, Q501]\n●\n\n⚠️Thermoplastics recycle ho sakte hain; thermosetting nahi. [Q499, Q501]\n13. Polymers: Natural vs Synthetic\n● Polymers = macromolecules; repeating monomer units. [Q503, Q505]\n● Natural polymers: Cotton (cellulose), Silk (protein), Wool (protein), Rubber (isoprene). [Q505, Q507]\n● Synthetic polymers: Polythene, PVC, Nylon, Polyester, Teflon. [Q507, Q509]\n● Monomers = small repeating units. Ethene → Polythene; Vinyl chloride → PVC; Isoprene → Rubber. [Q509, Q511]"," ● Nylon = polyamide; socks, ropes, parachutes.\n● Polyester = terylene/cotton blend; fabrics, bottles. [Q511, Q513]\n● Teflon = non-stick coating; cookware. [Q513]\n14. Rubber: Natural & Synthetic\n● Natural rubber = rubber tree ka latex; polymer of isoprene. [Q515, Q517]\n● Natural rubber soft aur sticky; vulcanization se hard aur elastic. Sulphur ke saath heat karke cross-linking. [Q517]\n● Synthetic rubber: Neoprene, Buna-S, Buna-N; tyres, hoses, belts. [Q517]\n15. Environmental Impact & Non-biodegradable Substances\n● Plastics non-biodegradable; soil aur water pollution. [Q517, Q518]\n● Plastic burning se toxic gases (dioxins) release. [Q518]\n● 4R principle: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle, Recover. [Q518]\n● Biodegradable plastics research (starch-based). [Q518]\n● CFCs ozone layer deplete karte hain; replaced by HFCs. [Q518]\n● Ek carbon credit mein 1000 kg Carbon dioxide hoti hai (carbon trading/emission ka unit). [Q486]\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q448–Q518)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Carbon ke paas 2 shells hain; 4 valence electrons — tetravalent. [Q448]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Diamond hard + non-conductor; Graphite soft + conductor — allotropes hain. [Q451, Q453]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fullerene (C₆₀) soccer ball shape; hexagons + pentagons. [Q455, Q478]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alkane = single bond C H₂ ₊₂; Alkene = double bond C H₂ ; Alkyne = triple bond C H₂ ₋₂.\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q454, Q456,\nQ458]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cyclohexane mein 6 C-C + 12 C-H = 18 total covalent bonds. [Q449]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Homologous series mein successive members mein CH₂ difference; properties gradually change. [Q465,\nQ467]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Isomers ki molecular formula same; structural formula alag. [Q468, Q470]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Combustion: saturated = clean flame; unsaturated = sooty flame. [Q475]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Addition unsaturated mein; Substitution saturated mein. [Q477, Q479]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fermentation mein yeast anaerobic condition mein kaam karti hai; oxygen ho toh CO₂ + H₂O banega.\n[Q481, Q483]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Glacial acetic acid = pure CH₃COOH; vinegar sirf 5–8% acetic acid. [Q497, Q499]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Esterification reversible hai; conc. H₂SO₄ catalyst + dehydrating agent hai. [Q503, Q505]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Soap mein −COO⁻Na⁺; detergent mein −SO₃⁻Na⁺ — functional group alag. [Q511, Q513]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Micelle tabhi form hota hai jab concentration CMC se upar ho. [Q513, Q515]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Thermoplastic = soft on heat, reshape, recyclable; Thermosetting = permanently hard. [Q499, Q501]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vulcanization mein sulphur add karte hain cross-linking ke liye. [Q517]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Natural gas mainly methane (CH₄); LPG = butane/propane mixture — alag hain. [Q481, Q491]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Biodegradable = microorganisms se toot jaata hai; plastics non-biodegradable hain. [Q518]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Coal carbon ka allotrope nahi hai — Diamond/Graphite/Fullerene/Graphene hi allotropes hain. [Q500]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Carbon compounds mein bonding hamesha covalent hoti hai — ionic bond generally nahi milta. [Q466,\nQ476]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Diamond mein har carbon 4 dusre carbons se bonded hai; Graphite mein 3 (same plane mein) —\nstructure difference. [Q502, Q504]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 4 Carbon and Its Compounds Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0392","t":"05 Metallurgy","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.5 — METALLURGY — FULL MIND MAP\n⛏️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Important Ores of Metals\n2. Concentration & Dressing of Ores\n3. Roasting, Calcination & Smelting\n4. Iron & Steel Production\n5. Aluminium Extraction\n6. Copper Extraction\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q519–Q531)\n⚠️\n1. Important Ores of Metals\n● Aluminium ke ores: Bauxite (Al₂O₃·2H₂O), Corundum (Al₂O₃), Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆). [Q519]\n● Iron ke ores: Hematite (Fe₂O₃), Magnetite (Fe₃O₄), Siderite (FeCO₃), Limonite (2Fe₂O₃·3H₂O). [Q519, Q521]\n● Copper ke ores: Copper pyrites (CuFeS₂), Copper glance (Cu₂S), Malachite [CuCO₃·Cu(OH)₂]. [Q521]\n● Zinc ke ores: Zinc blende (ZnS), Calamine (ZnCO₃), Zincite (ZnO). [Q521]\n● Monazite = Thorium, Lanthanum, Cerium ka ore; beach sands mein milta hai. [Q519]\n● Metallurgy = ores se metals ka extraction. [Q519]\n2. Concentration & Dressing of Ores\n● Concentration/Dressing = ore se impurities (gangue) remove karna; metal content increase karna. [Q522, Q524]\n● Hydraulic washing/Gravity separation = heavy ore particles ko light gangue se alag karna water stream se; oxide\nores ke liye. [Q524]\n● Magnetic separation = magnetic ore ko non-magnetic gangue se magnet se alag karna; magnetite (Fe₃O₄) ke liye.\n[Q524]\n● Froth flotation = sulphide ores ke liye; ore particles water mein oil/pine oil ke saath froth par aate hain. [Q524]\n● Leaching = ore ko acid/alkali/bacteria se dissolve karke metal extract karna; bauxite (Al) aur gold ke liye. [Q524]\n3. Roasting, Calcination & Smelting\n● Roasting = ore ko air present mein strongly heat karna; sulphide ore → oxide; sulphur dioxide gas nikalta hai.\nExample: 2ZnS + 3O₂ → 2ZnO + 2SO₂. Purpose: sulphur remove karna. [Q520, Q523]\n● Calcination = ore ko air absent mein strongly heat karna; carbonate ore → oxide; CO₂ aur water vapour nikalta\nhai. Example: ZnCO₃ → ZnO + CO₂; Al₂O₃·2H₂O → Al₂O₃ + 2H₂O. Purpose: CO₂ aur H₂O remove karna; volatile\nimpurities remove. [Q520, Q525]\n● Smelting = calcined/roasted ore ko reducing agent (coke/C, CO) ke saath heat karna furnace mein; molten metal\naur slag alag hote hain. Example: Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂; ZnO + C → Zn + CO. [Q523, Q525]\n● Roasting aur calcination mein ore ko solid state mein heat karte hain; smelting mein reduction hoti hai. [Q520,\nQ523]"," 4. Iron & Steel Production\n● Iron mainly haematite (Fe₂O₃) se blast furnace mein extract hota hai. [Q526, Q528]\n● Blast furnace charge: iron ore + coke + limestone. [Q526]\n● Reactions: C + O₂ → CO₂; CO₂ + C → 2CO (reducing agent). Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂. CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂; CaO +\nSiO₂ → CaSiO₃ (slag). [Q528]\n● Molten iron bottom par collect hota hai; slag upper layer par (lighter). [Q528]\n● Pig iron = 3–4.5% carbon; hard, brittle; cast iron banta hai. [Q528]\n● Wrought iron = purest form; <0.2% carbon; soft; wires, chains. [Q528]\n● Steel = 0.2–2% carbon; alloying elements add karke stainless steel, tool steel, etc. [Q528, Q530]\n● Bessemer converter ya Open-hearth furnace mein pig iron se steel banate hain. [Q530]\n● Stainless steel = Fe + Cr + Ni + C; rust-resistant. [Q530]\n5. Aluminium Extraction\n● Aluminium ka main ore = Bauxite (Al₂O₃·2H₂O). [Q519, Q527]\n● Bayer's process se bauxite se Al₂O₃ (alumina) purify karte hain. [Q527]\n● Hall-Héroult process: Molten alumina ka electrolysis cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) mein dissolved karke. Cathode: Al³⁺ + 3e⁻\n→ Al. Anode: 2O²⁻ → O₂ + 4e⁻; oxygen carbon anode se react karke CO₂ banata hai. Cryolite melting point kam\nkarne aur conductivity badhane ke liye. [Q527]\n● Aluminium good conductor, lightweight, corrosion-resistant; aircraft, utensils, electrical wires mein. [Q527]\n6. Copper Extraction\n● Copper ke ores: Copper pyrites (CuFeS₂), Copper glance (Cu₂S), Malachite. [Q521, Q529]\n● Copper pyrites se extraction: Concentration by froth flotation. Roasting: 2CuFeS₂ + O₂ → Cu₂S + 2FeS + SO₂.\nBessemerization: 2Cu₂S + 3O₂ → 2Cu₂O + 2SO₂; phir Cu₂S + 2Cu₂O → 6Cu + SO₂. Blister copper = 98–99% pure.\n[Q529]\n● Electrolytic refining se 99.9% pure copper milti hai. [Q529]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q519–Q531)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bauxite = Aluminium ka ore; Hematite/Siderite/Magnetite = Iron ke ores; Monazite = Thorium ka ore —\nconfuse mat hona. [Q519, Q521]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Roasting = air present mein, sulphide ore → oxide, sulphur remove hota hai. [Q520]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Calcination = air absent mein, carbonate ore → oxide, CO₂ aur H₂O remove hote hain. [Q520, Q525]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Roasting aur calcination mein ore solid state mein hota hai; donon heat treatment hain lekin\natmosphere alag. [Q520, Q523]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Smelting = reduction furnace mein; reducing agent (coke/CO) use hota hai; metal + slag alag hote hain.\n[Q523, Q525]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Blast furnace charge = iron ore + coke + limestone; limestone flux ka kaam karta hai gangue ko slag mein\nconvert karne ke liye. [Q526, Q528]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pig iron (3–4.5% C) vs Wrought iron (<0.2% C) vs Steel (0.2–2% C) — carbon percentage se identify karte\nhain. [Q528]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) electrolysis mein alumina dissolve karne ke liye use hota hai taaki melting point kam"," ho; cryolite khud ore nahi balki added substance hai. [Q527]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Blister copper 98–99% pure hoti hai; \"blisters\" SO₂ gas bubbles ki wajah se bante hain. [Q529]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 5 Metallurgy Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0393","t":"06 Organic Chemistry","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.6 — ORGANIC CHEMISTRY — FULL MIND MAP\n🧬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Homologous Series: Definition & Characteristics\n2. Hydrocarbons: Alkanes, Alkenes, Alkynes & Cycloalkanes\n3. Functional Groups & IUPAC Nomenclature\n4. Isomerism in Organic Compounds\n5. Combustion & Flame Characteristics\n6. Addition Reactions of Unsaturated Compounds\n7. Substitution Reactions of Saturated Compounds\n8. Alcohols: Classification, Properties & Oxidation\n9. Aldehydes & Ketones: Properties, Tests & Differences\n10. Carboxylic Acids: Properties, Reactions & Uses\n11. Esters: Formation, Hydrolysis & Uses\n12. Organic Compounds: Sources, Preparation & Daily Life\n13. Petroleum Refining & Fractional Distillation\n14. Coal & Its Products\n15. Natural Gas, LPG & CNG\n16. Polymers: Natural vs Synthetic, Thermoplastic vs Thermosetting\n17. Rubber: Natural & Synthetic\n18. Environmental Impact & Non-biodegradable Substances\n19.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q532–Q643)\n⚠️\n20. Numerical: Molecular Mass Difference in Homologous Series\n21. Numerical: Calculations — Alcohols & Hydrocarbons\n22. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n23.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q644–Q646)\n⚠️\n1. Homologous Series: Definition & Characteristics\n● Homologous series = same general formula aur same functional group wale compounds; successive members\nmein sirf carbon chain length alag hoti hai. [Q532, Q533, Q535, Q537, Q601]\n● Har successive member mein CH₂ (methylene) group ka difference hota hai; molecular mass difference = 14 u\n(C=12 + H₂=2). [Q532, Q605]\n● Homologous series mein Hydrogen atom ko hi different functional group se replace kiya jaata hai. [Q575]\n● Same homologous series ke members ki chemical properties nearly identical hoti hain; physical properties\ngradually change — molecular mass badhne ke saath boiling point bhi badhta hai. [Q532, Q569]\n● Examples: Alkanes (CH₄, C₂H₆, C₃H₈...), Alkenes (C₂H₄, C₃H₆, C₄H₈...), Alcohols (CH₃OH, C₂H₅OH, C₃H₇OH...). [Q533,\nQ535]\n● CH₄, C₂H₆, C₃H₆ same homologous series mein nahi hain — C₃H₆ ek alkene hai, alkane nahi. [Q542]\n● C₄H₈ (alkene) baaki alkanes ke saath same homologous series mein nahi aata. [Q555]\n● C₄H₁₀OH ek valid alcohol formula nahi hai — isliye alcohols ki homologous series mein nahi aata. [Q567]\n● Alkanes mein sabse zyada melting point wala member options mein C₄H₁₀ (Butane) hai. [Q551]\n● Homologous series mein sabse kam boiling point wala member generally sabse chhota carbon chain wala hota hai\n— jaise CH₄O (Methanol). [Q562]\n● Boiling point increasing order example: CH₄ < CHCl₃ < CH₃CH₂OH < CH₃COOH. [Q564]"," 2. Hydrocarbons: Alkanes, Alkenes, Alkynes & Cycloalkanes\n● Alkanes (Saturated): C-C single bonds; general formula C H₂ ₊₂; examples: Methane CH₄, Ethane C₂H₆, Propane\nₙ\nₙ\nC₃H₈, Butane C₄H₁₀, Pentane C₅H₁₂. [Q534, Q536, Q538]\n● Ethane mein har carbon atom 4 other atoms se bonded hota hai (3H + 1C, ya symmetric structure mein 4 atoms\ntotal bonds); Ethane mein sirf ek hi C-C single bond hota hai. [Q619, Q577]\n● Alkenes (Unsaturated): C=C double bond; general formula C H₂ ; examples: Ethene C₂H₄, Propene C₃H₆ (alkene\nₙ\nₙ\nseries ka second member), Butene C₄H₈. [Q536, Q538, Q571]\n● Propene ek double bond wala compound hai. [Q628]\n● Alkynes (Unsaturated): C≡C triple bond; general formula C H₂ ₋₂; examples: Ethyne C₂H₂, Propyne C₃H₄, Butyne\nₙ\nₙ\nC₄H₆. [Q538, Q540]\n● Bond length order (increasing): Ethyne (triple bond) < Ethene (double bond) < Ethane (single bond) — jitne zyada\nbonds utni chhoti bond length. [Q609]\n● Cycloalkanes: Ring structure; saturated; formula C H₂ ; example: Cyclohexane C₆H₁₂ (6 C-C bonds + 12 C-H bonds\nₙ\nₙ\n= 18 total covalent bonds); C₆H₁₂ formula cyclic hydrocarbons se related hai. [Q449, Q540, Q557]\n● Cyclopentane mein total 15 single bonds hote hain (5 C-C ring bonds + 10 C-H bonds). [Q546]\n● First members: Alkane = Methane (CH₄); Alkene = Ethene (C₂H₄); Alkyne = Ethyne (C₂H₂). [Q534, Q536, Q538]\n● Benzene (C₆H₆) mein 3 double bonds hote hain (resonance structure). [Q573, Q614]\n3. Functional Groups & IUPAC Nomenclature\n● Functional group = atom/group jo molecule ki chemical properties decide karta hai. [Q541, Q543, Q545]\n● Common functional groups: −OH (Alcohol, suffix -ol, e.g. C₂H₅OH Ethanol); −CHO (Aldehyde, suffix -al, e.g. HCHO\nMethanal — aldehyde group ka symbol hai); >C=O (Ketone, suffix -one, e.g. CH₃COCH₃ Propanone; R-CO-R ketone\nrepresent karta hai); −COOH (Carboxylic acid, suffix -oic acid, e.g. CH₃COOH Ethanoic acid); −COOR (Ester); −X\n(Halide, prefix chloro-, e.g. CH₃Cl); −NH₂ (Amine, suffix -amine); −O− (Ether, e.g. CH₃OCH₃ Dimethyl ether). [Q541,\nQ543, Q545, Q547, Q589, Q548, Q623]\n● Carbon count prefixes: meth-(1), eth-(2), prop-(3), but-(4, jaise 4-carbon hydrocarbon ka prefix \"But\" hota hai),\npent-(5), hex-(6), hept-(7), oct-(8), non-(9), dec-(10). [Q549, Q603]\n● Common names: Ethanol = ethyl alcohol; Ethanoic acid = acetic acid; Propanone = acetone. [Q547, Q549]\n● Structure-name pairs: C₆H₆ = Benzene; H₂C=CH₂ = Ethylene/Ethene; CH₃-CHO = Acetaldehyde; CH₃COCH₃ =\nAcetone; CH₃CH₃ = Ethane. [Q544]\n4. Isomerism in Organic Compounds\n● Isomers = same molecular formula, different structural formula/arrangement — inhe hydrocarbons ke context\nmein bhi \"isomers\" hi kehte hain. [Q550, Q552, Q554, Q633]\n● Chain isomerism: different carbon skeleton — n-Butane vs Isobutane. [Q552]\n● Position isomerism: same functional group, different position — Propan-1-ol vs Propan-2-ol. [Q554]\n● Functional group isomerism: different functional groups — Ethanol (C₂H₅OH) vs Dimethyl ether (CH₃OCH₃), both\nC₂H₆O. [Q554]\n● Butane (C₄H₁₀) ke 2 isomers; Pentane (C₅H₁₂) ke 3 isomers. [Q552, Q554]\n5. Combustion & Flame Characteristics\n● All hydrocarbons air/oxygen mein burn karke CO₂ + H₂O + Heat dete hain. [Q556, Q558, Q560]"," ● Saturated hydrocarbons (Alkanes) = clean blue flame; sufficient oxygen mein complete combustion: CH₄ + 2O₂ →\nCO₂ + 2H₂O. [Q556, Q558]\n● Unsaturated hydrocarbons (Alkenes/Alkynes) = sooty yellow flame; kam hydrogen content ki wajah se incomplete\ncombustion hoti hai. [Q558, Q560]\n● Alkynes sabse zyada sooty flame dete hain kyunki inka carbon:hydrogen ratio sabse zyada hota hai; Benzene bhi\nsooty flame deta hai. [Q560]\n6. Addition Reactions of Unsaturated Compounds\n● Addition reaction = unsaturated compound mein atoms/groups add hote hain double/triple bond break hokar;\nsirf alkenes aur alkynes mein hoti hai. [Q561, Q563, Q565]\n● Hydrogenation: H₂ add karke saturated compound banana; vegetable oil → Vanaspati ghee, Nickel (Ni) catalyst\nuse hota hai. C₂H₄ + H₂ → C₂H₆. [Q561, Q563, Q612, Q639]\n● Halogenation: Cl₂ ya Br₂ add karna; bromine water decolourise — unsaturation ka test. C₂H₄ + Br₂ → C₂H₄Br₂.\n[Q563, Q565]\n● Hydration: H₂O add karke alcohol banana. C₂H₄ + H₂O → C₂H₅OH (conc. H₂SO₄ catalyst, 300°C, 60 atm). [Q565]\n● Addition reaction alkanes mein nahi hoti. [Q561]\n7. Substitution Reactions of Saturated Compounds\n● Substitution reaction = saturated compound mein ek atom/group replace hota hai dusre atom/group se; alkanes\nmein hoti hai. [Q566, Q568, Q570]\n● Chlorination of methane (UV light): CH₄ + Cl₂ → CH₃Cl + HCl (Methyl chloride). CH₃Cl + Cl₂ → CH₂Cl₂ + HCl\n(Methylene chloride). CH₂Cl₂ + Cl₂ → CHCl₃ + HCl (Chloroform). CHCl₃ + Cl₂ → CCl₄ + HCl (Carbon tetrachloride).\n[Q566, Q568]\n● UV light/heat ki zaroorat hoti hai substitution ke liye. [Q568]\n8. Alcohols: Classification, Properties & Oxidation\n● Primary alcohol (1°): −OH terminal carbon par; −CH₂OH; example: Ethanol CH₃CH₂OH. [Q570, Q572]\n● Secondary alcohol (2°): −OH middle carbon par; >CHOH; example: Propan-2-ol CH₃CH(OH)CH₃. [Q572]\n● Tertiary alcohol (3°): −OH carbon par jo 3 other carbons se jura ho; example: 2-Methylpropan-2-ol. [Q572]\n● Alcohols ka oxidation: Primary alcohol → Aldehyde → Carboxylic acid; ethanol K₂Cr₂O₇ (potassium dichromate) ke\nacidic medium mein oxidize hokar Ethanoic acid deta hai. [Q572, Q574, Q559]\n● Secondary alcohol → Ketone; Tertiary alcohol → resistant to oxidation (strong oxidizing agents se cleavage).\n[Q572, Q574]\n9. Aldehydes & Ketones: Properties, Tests & Differences\n● Aldehyde (−CHO) = carbonyl group terminal carbon par; general formula R−CHO; examples: Methanal HCHO,\nEthanal CH₃CHO. [Q576, Q578, Q580]\n● Ketone (>C=O) = carbonyl group middle carbon par; general formula R−CO−R'; examples: Propanone CH₃COCH₃,\nButanone CH₃COC₂H₅. [Q578, Q580]\n● Oxidation: Aldehyde → Carboxylic acid (easily oxidized; reducing agent); Ketone → resistant to oxidation. [Q580,\nQ582]"," ● Reduction (H₂/Ni): Aldehyde → Primary alcohol; Ketone → Secondary alcohol. [Q582]\n● Tollen's test: Aldehyde silver mirror deta hai; ketone nahi. RCHO + 2[Ag(NH₃)₂]⁺ + 3OH⁻ → RCOO⁻ + 2Ag↓ + 4NH₃\n+ 2H₂O. [Q584]\n● Fehling's test: Aldehyde red Cu₂O precipitate deta hai; ketone nahi. RCHO + 2Cu²⁺ + 5OH⁻ → RCOO⁻ + Cu₂O↓ +\n3H₂O. [Q584]\n10. Carboxylic Acids: Properties, Reactions & Uses\n● Carboxylic acid (−COOH) = weak acid; examples: Methanoic acid HCOOH, Ethanoic acid CH₃COOH. [Q586, Q588,\nQ590]\n● Ethanoic acid = acetic acid; vinegar mein 5–8% solution; carboxylic acids mein sabse high boiling point acetic acid\nka hota hai (given options mein). [Q588, Q539]\n● Reactions: With metals — 2CH₃COOH + Mg → (CH₃COO)₂Mg + H₂↑. With bases — CH₃COOH + NaOH →\nCH₃COONa + H₂O. With carbonates — 2CH₃COOH + Na₂CO₃ → 2CH₃COONa + H₂O + CO₂↑. [Q590, Q592]\n● Esterification: Carboxylic acid + Alcohol → Ester + Water (conc. H₂SO₄ catalyst, reversible). CH₃COOH + C₂H₅OH\n\n⇌\nCH₃COOC₂H₅ + H₂O; sweet smell. [Q592, Q594]\n● Saponification: Ester + NaOH/KOH → Salt of fatty acid (soap) + Alcohol; Soaps sodium/potassium salts of long\nchain Carboxylic acids hote hain. [Q594, Q596, Q591]\n● Carbonic acid soft drinks mein fizz add karne ke liye use hoti hai (CO₂ dissolved in water). [Q581]\n11. Esters: Formation, Hydrolysis & Uses\n● Ester formula: R−COO−R'; derived from carboxylic acid + alcohol; CH₃COOC₂H₅ ek ester ka example hai. [Q594,\nQ596, Q598, Q583]\n● Naming: alkyl group from alcohol + acid name with -oate suffix; CH₃COOC₂H₅ = Ethyl ethanoate. [Q598]\n● Acid hydrolysis: Ester + H₂O (H⁺ catalyst) → Carboxylic acid + Alcohol; Ester acid ya base ki presence mein reactant\nkarke wapas alcohol aur carboxylic acid deta hai. [Q596, Q626]\n● Alkaline hydrolysis (Saponification): Ester + NaOH → Sodium salt of acid + Alcohol. [Q596]\n● Uses: perfumes, flavors, solvents, plasticizers. [Q598]\n● Glycerol (glycerin) ka IUPAC name Propane-1,2,3-triol hai (3 −OH groups). [Q585]\n12. Organic Compounds: Sources, Preparation & Daily Life\n● Ethanol: fermentation (yeast + glucose, anaerobic: C₆H₁₂O₆ → 2C₂H₅OH + 2CO₂ — yeh anaerobic respiration in\nyeasts se hota hai); synthesis (ethene hydration). [Q600, Q602, Q587]\n● Ethanol ka industrial-use version drinking ke liye unfit banane ke liye Methanol (poisonous) se\nadulterate/denature kiya jaata hai. [Q630]\n● Ethanoic acid: ethanol oxidation; oxidation of acetaldehyde. [Q602, Q604]\n● Ethanol se ethene banane ke liye conc. H₂SO₄ ek dehydrating agent ke roop mein use hota hai — 443 K par excess\nconc. H₂SO₄ ke saath heat karne par CH₂=CH₂ (ethene) product milta hai. [Q606, Q607, Q553]\n● Methane: natural gas, marsh gas, biogas; anaerobic decomposition. [Q604, Q606]\n● Ethene: ethanol dehydration (conc. H₂SO₄, 170°C); cracking of petroleum; plastics banane mein use hoti hai (jaise\nPolythene ke liye). [Q606, Q579]\n● Acetylene (Ethyne): calcium carbide + water → CaC₂ + 2H₂O → C₂H₂ + Ca(OH)₂. [Q608]\n● Important daily life compounds: Methanol (CH₃OH) = wood spirit, poisonous, solvent, denaturant. Formaldehyde\n(HCHO) = preservative (biological specimens), disinfectant, plastics (Bakelite). Acetone (CH₃COCH₃) = nail polish"," remover, solvent. Chloroform (CHCl₃) = solvent; historically anaesthetic; air mein phosgene (COCl₂) toxic gas\nbanata hai. Carbon tetrachloride (CCl₄) = solvent; fire extinguisher; ozone depleting. Urea (NH₂CONH₂) = fertilizer;\nfirst organic compound synthesized from inorganic (Wöhler, 1828). [Q610]\n● Ethyl alcohol (ethanol) ka use fuel (spirit lamps), alcoholic beverage, aur solvent — teenon roop mein hota hai.\n[Q599]\n● Ethyl alcohol hospitals mein wounds aur syringes sterilize karne ke liye antiseptic ke roop mein use hoti hai.\n[Q595]\n● Bahut zyada ethanol consume karne se metabolic processes slow ho jaate hain aur central nervous system\ndepress hota hai. [Q642]\n● Ethanol (C₂H₅OH / C₂H₆O) ke ek molecule mein 6 hydrogen atoms hote hain. [Q621]\n● Propane gas ka use illuminating gas (roshni ke liye) ke roop mein hota hai, cooking aur heating mein bhi. [Q616]\n● Ethylene fruit ripening mein use hota hai; ethyne welding mein. [Q606]\n● Branched chain ka boiling point lower hota hai straight chain se (surface area kam). [Q604]\n● Sugarcane mein Glucose aur Fructose (sucrose banane wale monosaccharides) hote hain. [Q593]\n● Glucose ek 6-carbon molecule hota hai (C₆H₁₂O₆). [Q637]\n● Covalent compounds (jaise organic compounds) poor electricity conductors hote hain, electron sharing se bante\nhain, aur inka melting/boiling point low hota hai — ye sab properties covalent compounds ki hain. [Q597]\n13. Petroleum Refining & Fractional Distillation\n● Petroleum = crude oil; mixture of hydrocarbons; fossil fuel. [Q611, Q613, Q615]\n● Fractional distillation = different boiling points par fractions alag karte hain: Petroleum gas (LPG) — fuel, cooking.\nPetrol/Gasoline — motor fuel, dry cleaning. Kerosene — jet fuel, stoves, lamps. Diesel — buses, trucks, trains.\nLubricating oil — machinery, grease. Paraffin wax — candles, ointments. Bitumen/Asphalt — roads, roofing.\n[Q613, Q615, Q617]\n● Higher fractions ka molecular weight aur viscosity zyada hoti hai. [Q615]\n● Cracking = heavy fractions ko lighter fractions (petrol) mein convert karna; heat + catalyst. [Q617]\n14. Coal & Its Products\n● Coal = fossil fuel; carbonized plant matter; types: peat, lignite, bituminous, anthracite. [Q618, Q620, Q622]\n● Destructive distillation of coal = coal ko absence of air mein heat karna; products: Coke, Coal tar, Coal gas,\nAmmoniacal liquor. [Q620, Q622]\n● Coke = porous, hard; blast furnace mein reducing agent; domestic fuel. [Q622]\n● Coal tar = black thick liquid; fractional distillation se benzene, toluene, phenol, naphthalene, anthracene milta\nhain. [Q622, Q624]\n● Coal gas = fuel (H₂, CH₄, CO mixture); historically street lighting. [Q624]\n● Ammoniacal liquor = fertilizers (ammonium salts). [Q624]\n15. Natural Gas, LPG & CNG\n● Natural gas mainly methane (CH₄) hota hai; CNG = Compressed Natural Gas. [Q625, Q627, Q629]\n● LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas) = mixture of butane + propane; liquid form mein store hota hai cylinders mein;\ndomestic fuel. [Q629, Q631]\n● CNG vehicles mein use hota hai; pollution petrol/diesel se kam. [Q629]"," ● Natural gas ka main advantage = clean burning; less pollution. [Q631]\n16. Polymers: Natural vs Synthetic, Thermoplastic vs Thermosetting\n● Polymer = large molecule; repeating monomer units. [Q632, Q634, Q636]\n● Natural polymers: Cotton (cellulose), Silk (protein), Wool (protein), Natural rubber (isoprene), Starch. [Q634, Q636]\n● Synthetic polymers: Polythene, PVC, Nylon, Polyester, Teflon, Bakelite. [Q636, Q638]\n● Thermoplastics = heat par soft, reshape ho sakte hain, recycle ho sakte hain; examples: Polythene, PVC,\nPolystyrene, Teflon. [Q636]\n● Thermosetting plastics = ek baar set hone ke baad permanently hard; examples: Bakelite, Melamine, Polyester\nresin. [Q638]\n● Addition polymers: Monomer directly add hote hain bina by-product ke; Polythene (ethene), PVC (vinyl chloride),\nTeflon (tetrafluoroethene). [Q638]\n● Condensation polymers: Monomer ke saath by-product (water, HCl) nikalta hai; Nylon, Polyester, Bakelite. [Q638]\n● Nylon = polyamide; socks, ropes, parachutes; Terylene/Dacron = polyester; fabrics, bottles; Bakelite = phenol-\nformaldehyde resin; electrical switches, handles. [Q638, Q640]\n17. Rubber: Natural & Synthetic\n● Natural rubber = rubber tree ka latex; polymer of isoprene (2-methyl-1,3-butadiene); soft aur sticky. [Q641, Q643]\n● Vulcanization = natural rubber ke saath 3–5% sulphur heat karna (373–415 K); cross-linking se rubber hard,\nelastic, durable hota hai; Charles Goodyear ne discover kiya. [Q641, Q643]\n● Synthetic rubber: Neoprene (chloroprene polymer); oil-resistant; hoses, gaskets. Buna-S (Styrene-butadiene\nrubber); tyres. Buna-N (Nitrile rubber); oil/fuel resistant. [Q643]\n● Vulcanized rubber ka use: tyres, shoes, belts, hoses. [Q643]\n● Carbon ka Fullerene allotrope geodesic globe (soccer-ball jaisi) shape mein hota hai. [Q635]\n18. Environmental Impact & Non-biodegradable Substances\n● Plastics non-biodegradable hain; soil aur water pollution karte hain. [Q643]\n● Plastic burning se toxic gases (dioxins, furans) release hote hain. [Q643]\n● 4R principle: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle, Recover. [Q643]\n● CFCs (Chlorofluorocarbons) ozone layer deplete karte hain; replaced by HFCs. [Q643]\n● Biodegradable plastics research chal rahi hai (starch-based, PLA). [Q643]\n19.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q532–Q643)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Homologous series mein successive members ka molecular mass difference 14 u hota hai (CH₂ = 12+2),\n12 ya 16 nahi. [Q532]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same molecular formula wale alag functional groups same homologous series mein nahi hain — C₂H₆\n(alkane), C₂H₄ (alkene), C₂H₂ (alkyne) alag hain. [Q533]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alkane = single bond C H₂ ₊₂; Alkene = double bond C H₂ ; Alkyne = triple bond C H₂ ₋₂; Cycloalkane =\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nₙ\nring C H₂ — sab alag formulas hain.\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q534, Q536, Q538, Q540]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chain isomerism mein skeleton alag; Position isomerism mein functional group ki position alag;\nFunctional group isomerism mein functional group hi alag — teenon alag hain. [Q552, Q554]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Saturated = clean flame; Unsaturated = sooty flame — carbon:hydrogen ratio se decide hota hai. [Q556,\nQ558, Q560]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Addition reaction sirf unsaturated compounds mein; Substitution sirf saturated compounds mein —\nconfuse mat hona. [Q561, Q566]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Primary alcohol oxidize hokar aldehyde phir acid banata hai; Secondary ketone banata hai; Tertiary\nresistant hota hai. [Q572, Q574]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Aldehyde terminal carbonyl (−CHO); Ketone middle carbonyl (>C=O) — Tollen's aur Fehling's test\naldehyde ke liye positive, ketone ke liye negative. [Q576, Q578, Q580, Q584]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Esterification reversible hai; conc. H₂SO₄ catalyst + dehydrating agent hai jo water absorb karke\nequilibrium ester ki taraf shift karta hai. [Q592, Q594]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Methanol (CH₃OH) poisonous hai; Ethanol (C₂H₅OH) drinkable (controlled amount) — confuse mat hona;\nisiliye industrial ethanol ko methanol se adulterate karke unfit banaya jaata hai. [Q610, Q630]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chloroform air mein phosgene (COCl₂) toxic gas banata hai; isliye modern anaesthesia mein use nahi\nhota. [Q610]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Urea first organic compound tha jo laboratory mein inorganic se synthesize kiya gaya (Wöhler, 1828) —\nvital force theory ko disprove kiya. [Q610]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Petroleum fractional distillation mein petrol pehle nikalta hai (low BP); asphalt/bitumen sabse last mein\n(high BP). [Q613, Q615, Q617]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: LPG = butane + propane; CNG = mainly methane — donon alag hain. [Q629, Q631]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Thermoplastic heat par melt ho sakta hai, reshape aur recycle ho sakta hai; Thermosetting ek baar set\nhua toh permanently hard — confuse mat hona. [Q636, Q638]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Addition polymerization mein koi by-product nahi; Condensation polymerization mein by-product\n(water/HCl) nikalta hai. [Q638]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vulcanization mein sulphur add karte hain cross-linking ke liye; natural rubber soft/sticky hota hai,\nvulcanized rubber hard/elastic hota hai. [Q641, Q643]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Neoprene oil-resistant hai; Buna-S tyres mein; Buna-N fuel-resistant — alag-alag uses hain. [Q643]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Branched chain ka boiling point lower hota hai straight chain se; exam mein order pucha jaata hai.\n[Q604]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bond length order — triple bond (Ethyne) sabse chhoti, phir double bond (Ethene), phir single bond\n(Ethane) sabse badi. [Q609]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hydrogenation ka catalyst hamesha Nickel (Ni) hota hai, Platinum nahi (is context mein). [Q612, Q639]\n20. Numerical: Molecular Mass Difference in Homologous Series\n● Homologous series mein har successive member ka difference CH₂ group hota hai. [Q644, Q646]\n● CH₂ group ka molecular mass = C (12) + H₂ (2) = 14 u. [Q646]\n● Isliye do kramagat members ka molecular mass hamesha 14 u se differ karta hai. [Q646]\n● Example: CH₄ (16 u) aur C₂H₆ (30 u) ka difference = 30 − 16 = 14 u. [Q646]\n● Example: C₂H₆ (30 u) aur C₃H₈ (44 u) ka difference = 44 − 30 = 14 u. [Q646]\n● Ye rule sabhi homologous series ke liye valid hai — chahe alkanes ho, alkenes, alcohols, ya carboxylic acids. [Q646]\n21. Numerical: Calculations — Alcohols & Hydrocarbons\n● Methanol (CH₃OH) ka molecular mass = 12 + 3(1) + 16 + 1 = 32 u. [Q645]"," ● Ethanol (C₂H₅OH) ka molecular mass = 2(12) + 5(1) + 16 + 1 = 46 u. [Q645]\n● Methanol aur ethanol ka difference = 46 − 32 = 14 u (CH₂ group). [Q645]\n● Propane (C₃H₈) ka molecular mass = 3(12) + 8(1) = 44 u. [Q644]\n● Pentane (C₅H₁₂) ka molecular mass = 5(12) + 12(1) = 72 u. [Q644]\n● C₃H₈ aur C₅H₁₂ ka difference = 72 − 44 = 28 u (do CH₂ groups ka difference). [Q644]\n22. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● CH₂ group mass: 12 + 2 = 14 u.\n● Molecular mass of alkane: 12n + (2n+2) = 14n + 2.\n● Molecular mass of alkene: 12n + 2n = 14n.\n● Molecular mass of alcohol: 12n + (2n+1) + 16 + 1 = 14n + 18.\n● Difference between successive members: 14 u.\n23.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q644–Q646)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: C₃H₆ alkene (propene) hai jiska mass 42 u hai; C₃H₈ alkane (propane) hai jiska mass 44 u hai — 2 u ka\ndifference hai, confuse mat hona. [Q644]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Do members ke beech agar ek member gap ho toh difference 28 u (2 × 14) hoga, 14 nahi. [Q644]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alcohols mein bhi same 14 u ka difference hota hai kyunki OH group common rehta hai aur carbon chain\nCH₂ se badhti hai. [Q645]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Atomic masses yaad rakhna: C = 12, H = 1, O = 16 — calculation fast karni padti hai exam mein. [Q644,\nQ645]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 6 Organic Chemistry Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0394","t":"07 Periodic Table","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.7 — PERIODIC TABLE — FULL MIND MAP\n🧪\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Periodic Table: Development & Classification History\n2. Modern Periodic Table Structure\n3. Hydrogen & Its Position\n4. Periodic Trends Across Periods & Groups\n5. s-Block Elements (Groups 1 & 2)\n6. p-Block Elements (Groups 13-18)\n7. d-Block & f-Block Elements\n8. Representative vs Transition Elements\n9. Diagonal Relationship\n10. Anomalous Properties of First Elements\n11. Metalloids & Their Uses\n12. Important Chemical Reactions & Compounds\n13. Comparative Chemistry: Important Pairs\n14. Everyday Applications & Industrial Uses\n15. Radioactive & Synthetic Elements\n16. Memory Aids & Positions\n17.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n18. Electronic Configuration → Element Identification (Practice)\n19. Shell Capacity Rule (2n²) & Basic Structure Facts\n20. Period-wise & Group-wise Element Counts\n21. Family Names, Block Classification & Rare Earth Facts\n22. Atomic Number → Group/Period Matching Practice\n23. Miscellaneous Element Facts, Uses & Ionization Facts\n24. Additional Practice Facts (Position, Valency & Statements)\n1. Periodic Table: Development & Classification History\n● Elements ko classify karne ke pehle attempts:\n– Dobereiner's Triads: 3 elements jinki atomic masses nearly same proportion mein hain; middle element ka\nmass average hota hai. Example: Li (7), Na (23), K (39). Cl-Br-I triad: (35.5+126.92)/2 ≈ 79.9 (actual), calculated\n≈ 81.2. Known triads: Li-Na-K, Ca-Sr-Ba, Cl-Br-I — N-P-Sb NAHI hai (middle should be As, P fit nahi karta).\nDefect: sirf 3 triads identify kar paaye, baaki known elements fit nahi hue. [Q648, Q650, Q651, Q657, Q675, Q689,\nQ723, Q735, Q962]\n– Newlands' Law of Octaves: Har 8ve element ka properties pehle se repeat hoti hai; music ke octaves jaisa.\nLimitation: Sirf calcium tak kaam karta hai; heavier elements fit nahi hote; Cobalt aur Nickel same slot mein\nrakhe. Be aur Mg same properties dikhate hain (Mg, Be ke baad 8th element). 10th element 3rd element\n(10−7) jaisa resemble karta hai. Noble gases us waqt discovered nahi the isliye include nahi hue. Last element\njo Newlands ne classify kiya woh Thorium tha (56 elements list mein). [Q650, Q652, Q736, Q737, Q738, Q743,\nQ806, Q808, Q978, Q990]\n– Mendeleev's Periodic Table: Atomic mass ke basis par arrange kiya; gaps chhodi future elements ke liye\n(gallium=Eka-aluminium, germanium=Eka-silicon, scandium=Eka-boron). Merits: Predictive power (oxides bhi\npredict kiye — Eka-aluminium ka oxide Ga2O3); demerits: isotopes ko separate position nahi mili (yahi uski\nasli limitation thi, \"correct isotope position\" uska feature NAHI tha), hydrogen ki fixed position nahi thi, some\nelements order galat (Ar before K, Co before Ni rakha gaya despite atomic mass higher hone ke). Mendeleev\nne 63 known elements se shuru kiya tha; 8 groups aur 7 periods banaye the; H aur O ke saath compounds par\nfocus kiya kyunki wo bahut reactive hain. Baad mein discover hue elements: Sc, Ga, Ge (predicted gaps fill\nkiye). [Q652, Q654, Q656, Q663, Q669, Q713, Q744, Q746, Q776, Q782, Q800, Q812, Q858, Q870, Q874, Q898, Q954, Q964,"," Q970]\n● Modern Periodic Law (Moseley, 1913): Elements ki properties unke atomic number ka periodic function hain;\nismein elements ki increasing atomic number (nuclear charge) ke order mein arrange kiya jaata hai — Mendeleev\nke atomic mass wale order se ye alag hai. Neutral atom mein atomic number = protons ki sankhya = electrons ki\nsankhya (koi net charge nahi hota). In early classification attempts, elements ko unki properties ke basis par\nclassify karne ki koshish hoti thi. [Q654, Q656, Q709, Q862, Q882, Q727]\n● Modern Periodic Table mein 7 periods (horizontal rows) aur 18 groups (vertical columns) hain. [Q656, Q658]\n2. Modern Periodic Table Structure\n● Period = horizontal row; left to right atomic number badhta hai. [Q647, Q658]\n● Group = vertical column; elements ki outermost shell electrons same hoti hain (valence electrons). [Q658, Q660]\n● Lanthanides = 6th period ke baad; Actinides = 7th period ke baad; donon ko separately neeche rakha jaata hai\ntaaki table compact rahe. [Q807, Q809]\n● Inner transition elements = f-block; Lanthanides aur Actinides. [Q809, Q811]\n● Metals left side aur center mein; non-metals right side mein (top-right corner mein); metalloids staircase/zig-zag\nline par jo metals ko non-metals se separate karti hai. Hydrogen ek exception hai — left side mein hone ke\nbaawajood non-metal hai (sabse left-side ka akela non-metal). [Q811, Q813, Q784, Q864, Q936, Q974, Q980]\n● Group 18 (Noble gases) ki valency zero hoti hai — inka valence shell already complete hota hai (octet, Helium ka\nduplet), isliye electrons na gain karte hain na lose. [Q665, Q790]\n3. Hydrogen & Its Position\n● Hydrogen ka atomic number 1; configuration 1s¹. [Q829, Q831]\n● Group 1 ke saath similarities: 1 valence electron; +1 oxidation state; electropositive. [Q831, Q833]\n● Group 17 ke saath similarities: 1 electron short of noble gas; -1 oxidation state (hydride); diatomic molecule (H₂).\n[Q833, Q835]\n● Isliye hydrogen ko alag se rakha jaata hai; sometimes center mein, sometimes donon groups ke upar. Electronic\nconfiguration alkali metals se milti-julti hai lekin hydrogen khud alkali metal NAHI hai; Mendeleev's periodic table\nmein hydrogen ki koi fixed position nahi thi (uncertain position, ye ek limitation thi). Halogens ki tarah hydrogen\nbhi diatomic molecule (H₂) ke roop mein exist karta hai. [Q835, Q837, Q860, Q725]\n● Hydrogen metal nahi hai; non-metal hai; Left side ka akela non-metal hai. [Q837]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hydrogen sometimes Group 1 ke upar rakha jaata hai lekin ye metal nahi hai. [Q751]\n4. Periodic Trends Across Periods & Groups\n● Atomic number increases, nuclear charge increases. [Q647, Q659]\n● Valence electrons increase (1 se 8 tak). [Q647]\n● Atomic radii decrease (kyunki nuclear charge ka pull badhta hai, electrons same shell mein hain). Order example:\nB < Be < Li (period 2 mein left se right ghatta hai). [Q647, Q659, Q667, Q671, Q741, Q780]\n● Metallic character decreases, non-metallic character increases — Group 16 mein Oxygen sabse zyada non-\nmetallic hai. [Q659, Q661, Q649]\n● Electropositivity decreases, electronegativity increases (Na se Cl tak non-metallic character badhta hai). [Q659,\nQ976]\n● Ionization energy increases (generally, with exceptions). [Q659, Q661]\n● Chemical reactivity: Period ke start mein metals zyada reactive (Group 1); middle mein kam; end mein non-metals"," reactive (Group 17); noble gases (Group 18) least reactive. [Q647, Q661]\n● Atomic number increases, new shells add hoti hain. [Q660, Q662]\n● Valence electrons same rehte hain — isliye same group ke elements similar chemical properties rakhte hain aur\nsame valency hoti hai. [Q660, Q655, Q914, Q958]\n● Atomic radii increase (kyunki new shells add hote hain, shielding effect badhta hai). Example: Cs > Rb > K > Na > Li\n(Group 1 mein); I (largest) > Br > Cl > F (Group 17 mein); Rb sabse metallic Period 5 mein (sabse left position).\n[Q660, Q662, Q653, Q711, Q839, Q988, Q904]\n● Metallic character increases (generally; for non-metals, reactivity with metals increases). Example: Ca > Sc > Ga >\nGe (Period 4 mein left se right metallic character ghatta hai). [Q662, Q664, Q693, Q926, Q731, Q892]\n● Electropositivity increases (metals ke liye). [Q662]\n● Ionization energy decreases (kyunki outermost electrons nucleus se door hote hain). [Q662, Q664]\n● Down a group, chemical reactivity: Metals ke liye reactivity increases (Fr sabse reactive metal); Non-metals ke liye\nreactivity decreases (F sabse reactive non-metal). [Q664, Q666]\n● Atomic radius = nucleus se outermost electron shell ki distance. [Q668, Q670, Q672]\n● Li sabse bada radius 2nd period mein; F sabse chhota. [Q647]\n● Cs (Caesium) sabse bada atomic radius known element mein (excluding francium). [Q674]\n● Cation (positive ion) ka radius parent atom se chhota hota hai — electron loss se same number of protons kam\nelectrons hain; zyada pull per electron. [Q676, Q678]\n● Anion (negative ion) ka radius parent atom se bada hota hai — electron gain se electron-electron repulsion\nbadhta hai; cloud expand hota hai. [Q678, Q680]\n● Isoelectronic species mein (same electrons): jyada nuclear charge → chhota radius. Example: N³⁻ > O²⁻ > F⁻ > Ne >\nNa⁺ > Mg²⁺ > Al³⁺ (sabke paas 10 electrons). [Q680, Q682]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cation radius < Atomic radius < Anion radius — for same element. [Q676, Q678]\n● Ionization energy = gaseous atom se outermost electron remove karne mein lagne wali energy; unit KJ/mol.\n[Q684, Q686, Q688, Q952]\n● Across a period: IE increases (generally) — nuclear charge badhta hai; atomic radius ghatta hai; electrons tightly\nheld hote hain. [Q686, Q688]\n● Down a group: IE decreases — atomic radius badhta hai; outermost electrons door hain; shielding effect; isliye\nzyada atomic radius wale element (jaise Fe) electrons easily lose karte hain. [Q688, Q690, Q928]\n● Exceptions: Group 2 > Group 13 (p-orbital mein electron easily remove hota hai); Group 15 > Group 16 (half-filled\nstability Group 15 mein). [Q690, Q692]\n● Helium (He) ka sabse zyada IE; Francium (Fr) ka sabse kam. [Q692, Q694]\n● 2nd IE > 1st IE hamesha (kyunki positive ion se electron remove karna aur mushkil). [Q694]\n● Electron affinity = gaseous atom mein electron add karne par release hone wali energy. [Q696, Q698, Q700]\n● Across a period: EA generally increases (non-metals ke liye) — nuclear charge badhta hai; added electron tightly\nheld hota hai. [Q698, Q700]\n● Down a group: EA generally decreases — atomic radius badhta hai; added electron door se attract hota hai.\n[Q700, Q702]\n● Exceptions: Group 2 aur Group 15 ka EA kam hota hai (full/half-filled stability); Noble gases ka EA ≈ 0 ya positive\n(unfavorable). [Q702, Q704]\n● Chlorine (Cl) ka sabse zyada EA (not fluorine, kyunki F mein electron-electron repulsion zyada); Order: Cl > F > Br >\nI. Cl ka electron affinity 3rd period mein sabse zyada hota hai. [Q704, Q706, Q848, Q942, Q992]\n● More negative EA value = more energy released = more favorable. [Q706]\n● Electronegativity = atom ka tendency shared electron pair ko apni taraf khinchne ki; Pauling scale se measure hoti\nhai. [Q708, Q710, Q712]\n● Across a period: Electronegativity increases — nuclear charge badhta hai; same size mein zyada pull. [Q710, Q712]\n● Down a group: Electronegativity decreases — atomic size badhta hai; shared electrons door hote hain (Order: Cl >\nBr > I). [Q712, Q714, Q804]"," ● Fluorine (F) sabse zyada electronegative (Pauling scale: 4.0); outermost config ns²np⁵. Among Cl, S, Al, Mg diye\noptions mein Cl sabse zyada electronegative hota hai. [Q714, Q716, Q681, Q768, Q934]\n● Francium (Fr) sabse kam electronegative. [Q716]\n● Electronegativity difference se bond type predict hota hai: Difference > 1.7 → Ionic bond; Difference < 1.7 →\nCovalent bond. [Q716, Q718]\n● Across a period: Metallic character decreases, non-metallic character increases. [Q718, Q720, Q722]\n● Down a group: Metallic character increases, non-metallic character decreases. [Q722, Q724]\n● Most metallic: Francium (Fr) (theoretical); Caesium (Cs) (practically observed). [Q724]\n● Most non-metallic: Fluorine (F). [Q724]\n● Metalloids (B, Si, Ge, As, Sb, Te) staircase line ke paar hote hain; properties intermediate. [Q726]\n● Across a period: Valency pehle badhti phir ghatti — Group 1-4: valency 1→4 (electrons donate); Group 4-8:\nvalency 4→1 (electrons accept, 8-n rule). Electropositive elements (metals) generally 1, 2, ya 3 valency rakhte\nhain. [Q728, Q730, Q788]\n● Down a group: Valency same rehti hai; outermost electrons same hote hain. [Q730, Q732]\n● Transition elements ke multiple oxidation states hote hain (variable valency). Example: Fe²⁺ aur Fe³⁺; Cu⁺ aur Cu²⁺.\n[Q732, Q734]\n● Metallic character across period: decreases; down group: increases (for metals). [Q813, Q815, Q817]\n● Non-metallic character across period: increases; down group: decreases. [Q815, Q817]\n● Chemical reactivity of metals across period: first decreases (Group 1 → Group 14), phir increases (Group 15 →\nGroup 17 as non-metals); down group: increases (for alkali metals). [Q817, Q819]\n● Chemical reactivity of non-metals across period: increases; down group: decreases (halogens mein F sabse\nreactive). [Q819, Q821]\n● Across a period: Oxides ka nature basic → amphoteric → acidic hota hai. [Q821, Q823, Q825]\n● Examples (Period 3): Na₂O = strongly basic; MgO = basic; Al₂O₃ = amphoteric; SiO₂ = weakly acidic; P₄O₁₀ = acidic;\nSO₃ = strongly acidic; Cl₂O₇ = strongly acidic. [Q823, Q825]\n● Down a group: Same oxidation state mein oxides ka basic character badhta hai. Example: N₂O₅ (acidic) < P₄O₁₀\n(acidic) < As₂O₅ (weakly acidic) < Sb₂O₅ (amphoteric) < Bi₂O₅ (basic). Alkaline oxide formation tendency down the\ngroup increases. [Q825, Q827, Q679]\n● Higher oxidation state ke oxides zyada acidic hote hain. Example: SO₂ (weakly acidic) < SO₃ (strongly acidic).\n[Q827, Q829]\n5. s-Block Elements (Groups 1 & 2)\n● s-Block = Groups 1 aur 2; valence electrons ns¹ ya ns² mein hote hain. [Q751, Q753, Q755, Q830]\n● Sabse zyada reactive metals; water ke saath vigorously react karte hain H₂ gas dete hain. Potassium alkali metal\nfamily ka member hai. [Q753, Q755, Q757, Q774]\n● +1 oxidation state. [Q753]\n● Soft metals (knife se cut kar sakte hain); low melting/boiling points. [Q883, Q885, Q887]\n● Reactivity down the group badhti hai (ionization energy ghatti hai); Sodium apne se niche ke Ca, Zn, Mg se zyada\nreactive hai (reactivity series mein upar). [Q753, Q755, Q757, Q948]\n● Melting point down the group decreases (atomic size badhne se metallic bond kamzor hoti hai). [Q885, Q887]\n● Density generally increases down the group (exception: Na > K). [Q887, Q889]\n● Water ke saath vigorous reaction; H₂ gas aur metal hydroxide. 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂↑ (exothermic). [Q889,\nQ891]\n● Potassium (K) water par float karta hai aur burn karta hai (lilac flame); sodium bhi float karta hai. [Q891, Q893]\n● Cesium (Cs) aur Francium (Fr) explosive reaction water ke saath. [Q893, Q895]"," ● Oxides: Li₂O (normal oxide), Na₂O (normal oxide), K/Rb/Cs superoxide bhi bana sakte hain (KO₂). [Q895, Q897]\n● Flame test colours: Li (crimson red), Na (golden yellow), K (lilac/violet), Rb (red-violet), Cs (blue). [Q753, Q755,\nQ757]\n● Less reactive than alkali metals; water ke saath slowly react. Group 2 ko \"alkaline earth metals\" kehte hain. [Q755,\nQ757, Q759, Q930]\n● +2 oxidation state. [Q755]\n● Harder than alkali metals; higher melting points. [Q897, Q899, Q901]\n● Down the group: reactivity increases; melting point decreases; density increases. [Q899, Q901]\n● Beryllium (Be) anomalous: covalent compounds; other ionic; Be aur atomic number 20 wala element (Calcium)\nsimilar chemical properties dikhate hain (same group 2). [Q899, Q816]\n● Flame test colours: Ca (brick red), Sr (crimson), Ba (apple green). [Q755, Q757, Q759]\n● Magnesium (Mg): lightweight; alloys (magnalium); chlorophyll ka center; flashbulbs. [Q901, Q903]\n● Calcium (Ca): bones/teeth; lime (CaO); cement; water hardness. [Q903, Q905]\n● Barium (Ba): BaSO₄ X-ray contrast agent (barium meal); BaCO₃ rat poison. [Q905, Q907]\n● Radium (Ra): radioactive; historical cancer treatment; luminescent paints. [Q907, Q909]\n6. p-Block Elements (Groups 13-18)\n● p-Block = Groups 13 se 18; valence electrons ns² np¹⁻⁶ mein hote hain. [Q759, Q761, Q763]\n● +3 oxidation state (B exceptions bhi bana sakta hai). [Q761, Q763]\n● Boron = metalloid (first metalloid in periodic table); baaki metals. Aluminium (13) aur Gallium (31) same group\n(13) ke elements hain. [Q761, Q763, Q842, Q906]\n● +4 aur +2 oxidation states; down the group +2 stable hota hai (inert pair effect). [Q763, Q765]\n● Carbon aur Silicon non-metals; Germanium metalloid; Tin aur Lead metals — is group mein sirf Carbon non-metal\nhai. [Q763, Q765, Q701, Q719]\n● -3, +3, +5 oxidation states; down the group metallic character badhta hai. [Q765, Q767]\n● Nitrogen aur Phosphorus non-metals; Antimony aur Bismuth metals. Nitrogen family ka 3rd element (N ke baad)\nArsenic hai (atomic number 33). [Q765, Q767, Q846]\n● -2 oxidation state (generally); +4 aur +6 bhi. [Q767, Q769]\n● Oxygen aur Sulphur non-metals; Polonium metal. [Q767, Q769]\n● -1 oxidation state; most reactive non-metals; Group number = 17. Carbon family (Group 14) ke saath compare\nkarte hain group numbers. [Q769, Q771, Q773, Q705, Q794]\n● Reactivity down the group ghatti hai (F sabse reactive). [Q769, Q771, Q773]\n● Down the group: atomic radius increases; electronegativity decreases; electron affinity generally decreases (Cl\nmax). [Q867, Q869, Q871]\n● Physical state: F₂ (pale yellow gas) → Cl₂ (greenish-yellow gas) → Br₂ (red-brown liquid) → I₂ (violet-black/purple\nsolid — sabse dark colour halogen). [Q769, Q771, Q773, Q871, Q873, Q924]\n● Reactivity: F₂ >> Cl₂ > Br₂ > I₂; F₂ sabse zyada oxidizing. [Q873, Q875]\n● Displacement: Upward halogen downward halogen ke salt se displace kar sakta hai. Cl₂ + 2NaBr → 2NaCl + Br₂.\n[Q875, Q877]\n● Interhalogen compounds: ClF, BrF₃, ICl, etc. [Q877, Q879]\n● HF weak acid (hydrogen bonding); HCl, HBr, HI strong acids. [Q879, Q881]\n● Bleaching powder (CaOCl₂) chlorine se banta hai; disinfectant. [Q881, Q883]\n● Halogen group ki oxygen ke saath maximum valency 7 hoti hai (Cl₂O₇ example). Atomic number 17 (Cl) atomic\nnumber 35 (Br) ke saath resemble karta hai (same group 17). [Q792, Q922, Q902]\n● Fire extinguisher mein Bromine, dental health mein Fluorine, refrigerants mein halogens, thyroid hormones mein"," Iodine use hota hai. [Q984]\n● Valence shell complete (ns² np⁶, He mein 1s²); chemically inert (generally); \"VIII A\" bhi kaha jaata hai purane\nnaming mein. He, Ne, Ar teenon ki outermost shell filled hoti hai. [Q773, Q775, Q851, Q853, Q855, Q822, Q894, Q900,\nQ916]\n● Down the group: atomic radius increases; boiling point increases (weak van der Waals forces; larger atoms =\nmore polarizable). [Q853, Q855]\n● Helium (He): sabse light; non-flammable; balloons, blimps, diving mixtures; liquid He cryogenics. [Q855, Q857]\n● Neon (Ne): red discharge tubes; advertising signs; high-voltage indicators. [Q857, Q859]\n● Argon (Ar): sabse abundant noble gas atmosphere mein; light bulbs mein fill karte hain (filament ko oxidize hone\nse bachane); welding shield gas; Ar ka electron configuration (2,8,8) mein M-shell (outer cell) mein 3 orbitals\nmein 8 electrons hote hain. [Q859, Q861, Q834]\n● Krypton (Kr): high-performance light bulbs; lasers; Period 4 ka inert gas (atomic number 36). [Q861, Q863, Q841]\n● Xenon (Xe): headlights (xenon lamps); anesthesia (historical); spacecraft ion propulsion. [Q863, Q865]\n● Radon (Rn): radioactive; uranium decay se; cancer treatment (radiotherapy) mein use historically; lung cancer risk\nbhi. [Q865, Q867]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Noble gases \"inert\" historically kehte the lekin ab kuch compounds bana sakte hain (XeF₂, XeF₄, XeF₆ —\nBartlett, 1962). [Q867]\n7. d-Block & f-Block Elements\n● d-Block = Groups 3 se 12; transition metals; valence electrons (n-1)d¹⁻¹⁰ ns⁰⁻² mein; two outermost shells\nincomplete hoti hain — isliye variable oxidation states (variable valency) exhibit karte hain. [Q775, Q777, Q779,\nQ852, Q932, Q966]\n● Characteristics: Variable oxidation states (multiple valency); Coloured compounds/ions (due to d-d transitions);\nCatalytic properties; Formation of complex compounds; Magnetic properties. [Q777, Q779, Q781]\n● Examples: Fe, Cu, Zn, Mn, Ni, Co, Cr, Ti, V. [Q779, Q781]\n● f-Block = Lanthanides (4f) aur Actinides (5f); inner transition metals; inko periods 6 aur 7 mein classify karte hain;\nteeno outermost shells incomplete hoti hain (rare earth elements characteristic). [Q781, Q783, Q854, Q910]\n● Lanthanides (Ce se Lu): similar properties; +3 oxidation state common. Cerium (Ce, atomic number 58)\nLanthanide series ka element hai, f-block mein aata hai. [Q783, Q818, Q820]\n● Actinides (Th se Lr): radioactive; uranium aur plutonium nuclear fuel mein. Californium (Cf) bhi Actinide series ka\nmember hai; sab radioactive elements is series mein aate hain. [Q783, Q785, Q826, Q876]\n8. Representative vs Transition Elements\n● Representative elements = s-block aur p-block (Groups 1, 2, 13-18); valence electrons outermost shell mein.\n[Q785, Q787]\n● Transition elements = d-block (Groups 3-12); valence electrons penultimate shell ke d-orbitals mein bhi hote hain.\n[Q787, Q789]\n● Representative elements ke paas generally fixed valency hoti hai; transition elements mein variable valency.\n[Q789, Q791]\n● Representative elements ke compounds generally colourless hote hain (exceptions hain); transition elements ke\ncompounds coloured hote hain. [Q791, Q793]\n9. Diagonal Relationship\n● Diagonal relationship = Period mein ek element aur uske next period ke next group ke element mein similar"," properties. [Q793, Q795, Q797]\n● Examples:\n– Li (Group 1, Period 2) aur Mg (Group 2, Period 3): donon nitrates heat par decompose hote hain; hydroxides\nless soluble.\n– Be (Group 2, Period 2) aur Al (Group 13, Period 3): donon amphoteric oxides banate hain; chlorides covalent.\n– B (Group 13, Period 2) aur Si (Group 14, Period 3): donon metalloids; acids se react karte hain. [Q795, Q797,\nQ799]\n● Reason: Similar ionic size/charge ratio; similar polarizing power. [Q799]\n10. Anomalous Properties of First Elements\n● Har group ka first element (Period 2) generally apne group ke baaki elements se alag properties rakhta hai. [Q799,\nQ801, Q803]\n● Reasons: Small atomic size; High electronegativity; No d-orbitals available for bonding (except 2nd period\nelements); High ionization energy. [Q801, Q803]\n● Examples: Li vs other alkali metals; Be vs other alkaline earth metals; B vs other group 13 elements; C vs other\ngroup 14 elements; N vs other group 15 elements; O vs other group 16 elements; F vs other halogens. [Q803,\nQ805]\n11. Metalloids & Their Uses\n● Metalloids = properties intermediate between metals and non-metals; semiconductors. [Q909, Q911, Q913]\n● Common metalloids: Boron (B), Silicon (Si), Germanium (Ge), Arsenic (As), Antimony (Sb), Tellurium (Te) — total 7\nmetalloids modern periodic table mein (staircase line ke around). Period 4 mein Ge aur As metalloids hain; Period\n5 mein Sb aur Te. [Q911, Q913, Q872]\n● Silicon (Si): semiconductors; solar cells; computer chips; silica (SiO₂) = glass, quartz; silicon hydrogen ke saath\nchain compounds (silanes) bhi banata hai jinmein 7-8 atoms ki chain hoti hai (weak Si-H bonds ki wajah se\nreactive). [Q913, Q915, Q960]\n● Germanium (Ge): early transistors; fiber optics; infrared optics; semiconductor bhi hai. [Q915, Q917, Q850]\n● Boron (B): borosilicate glass (Pyrex); borax (Na₂B₄O₇·10H₂O); neutron capture (cancer therapy). [Q917, Q919]\n● Arsenic (As): pesticides; semiconductors (GaAs). [Q919, Q921]\n● Antimony (Sb): alloys (type metal, Babbitt metal); flame retardants. [Q921, Q923]\n● Tellurium (Te): alloys (steel/machinery); solar panels (CdTe); thermoelectric devices. [Q923, Q925]\n12. Important Chemical Reactions & Compounds\n● Aqua regia = conc. HNO₃ + conc. HCl (1:3); gold aur platinum dissolve kar sakta hai. [Q925, Q927]\n● Chlor-alkali process: 2NaCl + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + Cl₂ + H₂ (electrolysis). [Q927, Q929]\n● Contact process: Sulphuric acid manufacturing; SO₂ → SO₃ (V₂O₅ catalyst). [Q929, Q931]\n● Haber process: N₂ + 3H₂\n 2NH₃ (Fe catalyst, 400–500°C, 200 atm); ammonia fertilizers ke liye.\n⇌\n [Q931, Q933]\n● Ostwald process: NH₃ → NO → NO₂ → HNO₃ (Pt catalyst); nitric acid manufacturing. [Q933, Q935]\n● Bayer process: Bauxite se alumina purify karna (NaOH se); aluminium extraction ke liye. [Q935, Q937]\n● Hall-Héroult process: Alumina ka electrolysis cryolite mein; aluminium metal. [Q937, Q939]"," 13. Comparative Chemistry: Important Pairs\n● Mg vs Ca: Mg(OH)₂ weak base; Ca(OH)₂ strong base; Mg forms basic carbonate; Ca nahi. [Q951, Q953]\n● Na vs K: Na⁺ aur K⁺ biological systems mein important (Na-K pump); K more reactive than Na in some contexts.\n[Q953, Q955]\n● Li vs Na: Li unique (diagonal relationship with Mg); Li compounds more covalent. [Q955, Q957]\n● C vs Si: CO₂ gas, molecular; SiO₂ solid, network covalent; Si larger, forms Si-Si bonds less readily. [Q957, Q959]\n● N vs P: N₂ triple bond, inert; P₄ tetrahedral, reactive; N forms pπ-pπ bonds, P less readily. [Q959, Q961]\n● O vs S: O₂ paramagnetic; O₃ diamagnetic; S₈ crown structure; H₂O hydrogen bonding, H₂S nahi. [Q961, Q963]\n14. Everyday Applications & Industrial Uses\n● Silicon chips = computers, smartphones. [Q963, Q965]\n● Aluminium = aircraft, utensils, foils (lightweight, corrosion resistant). [Q965, Q967]\n● Iron/Steel = construction, vehicles, machinery. [Q967, Q969]\n● Copper = electrical wires (excellent conductor). [Q969, Q971]\n● Titanium = aerospace, medical implants (biocompatible, strong). [Q971, Q973]\n● Chromium = stainless steel, electroplating (shiny finish). [Q973, Q975]\n● Nickel = batteries (Ni-Cd, Ni-MH, Li-ion mein bhi), alloys. [Q975, Q977]\n● Silver = jewelry, photography (historical), antibacterial. [Q977, Q979]\n● Gold = jewelry, electronics (non-reactive, conductive); reactivity series mein sabse kam reactive metals mein se ek\n(bottom mein). [Q979, Q981, Q742]\n● Mercury = thermometers (historical), dental amalgams, electrical switches. [Q981, Q983]\n● Carbon apne tetravalency aur catenation ki wajah se sabse zyada compounds banata hai (organic + inorganic\ndono). [Q918]\n● Bromine akela non-metal hai jo liquid state mein exist karta hai room temperature par (Mercury metal hai jo\nliquid hota hai). [Q946]\n● Eugenol = cloves (laung) mein paya jaane wala essential oil; perfume aur spice dono mein use hota hai. [Q896]\n● Benzene (C₆H₆) ek unsaturated hydrocarbon hai. [Q878]\n● Osmium (Os) sabse zyada density wala element hai. [Q764]\n15. Radioactive & Synthetic Elements\n● Technetium (Tc, Z=43): sabse halka element jo naturally stable nahi hai; first artificial element. [Q983, Q985]\n● Promethium (Pm, Z=61): rare earth; radioactive; no stable isotopes. [Q985, Q987]\n● Actinides: sab radioactive; Thorium aur Uranium naturally abundant; baaki synthetic/transuranic. Titanium\nradioactive NAHI hai (stable element hai) — U, Th, Ac radioactive hain. [Q987, Q989, Q968]\n● Transuranic elements: atomic number > 92; synthetic; particle accelerators/se nuclear reactors mein banaye jaate\nhain. Neptunium (Np, 93), Plutonium (Pu, 94) — nuclear weapons/fuel. Einsteinium (Es, 99), Fermium (Fm, 100)\n— named after scientists. [Q989, Q991]\n● Oganesson (Og, 118): sabse heavy confirmed element; synthetic; named after Yuri Oganessian. [Q991, Q993]\n16. Memory Aids & Positions"," ● Period 2 elements: Li, Be, B, C, N, O, F, Ne — \"Lina Be Boli Cini Nahi Oxygen Flouride Ne\". [Q939, Q941]\n● Group 1: Li, Na, K, Rb, Cs, Fr — \"Lina Na Kali Rubi Cesi France\". [Q941, Q943]\n● Group 17: F, Cl, Br, I, At — \"Fiza Chlorine Bharati Iodine Aati\". [Q943, Q945]\n● First 30 elements ke atomic numbers aur symbols yaad rakhna zaroori hai exam ke liye — jaise Lead (Pb), Zinc\n(Zn), Iron (Fe), Magnesium (Mg), Sodium (Na), Aluminium (Al), Sulphur (S). [Q945, Q947, Q756]\n● Transition metals (d-block): Sc(21) se Zn(30) tak 4th period; Y(39) se Cd(48) tak 5th period. [Q947, Q949]\n● Inner transition: Lanthanides (57–71), Actinides (89–103). [Q949, Q951]\n17.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Atomic radius period mein ghatta hai lekin group mein badhta hai — opposite trends hain. [Q647, Q670,\nQ672]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ionization energy ke exceptions hain: Group 2 > Group 13, Group 15 > Group 16 — half-filled/full\nstability. [Q690, Q692]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chlorine ka EA sabse zyada hai, Fluorine ka nahi — F mein electron-electron repulsion kam favorable\nbanata hai. [Q704, Q706]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electronegativity difference > 1.7 → ionic; < 1.7 → covalent — ye threshold yaad rakhna. [Q716, Q718]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Metallic character ke liye Fr theoretically sabse metallic hai lekin practically Cs observe kiya jaata hai.\n[Q724]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Valency period mein 1→4→1 pattern follow karti hai (electrons donate → share → accept). [Q728, Q730]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Dobereiner triads, Newlands octaves, Mendeleev periodic table — teenon ke limitations alag hain; exam\nmein match karte hain; teenon hi atomic mass ke basis par arrange karte the (atomic number par nahi). [Q648,\nQ650, Q652, Q858]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alkali metals ka reactivity down the group badhti hai (ionization energy ghatti); Halogens ka reactivity\nghatti hai (electron affinity kam hoti hai). [Q753, Q771]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Flame test colours yaad rakhna: Na = yellow, K = lilac, Ca = brick red, Ba = green — exam mein direct\npuchha jaata hai. [Q757, Q759]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Transition metals ke variable oxidation states hote hain; representative elements ke generally fixed.\n[Q777, Q789]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Diagonal relationship ke examples: Li-Mg, Be-Al, B-Si — properties similar hain lekin groups alag hain.\n[Q795, Q797]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: First element of each group (Period 2) generally anomalous properties rakhta hai apne group se — small\nsize aur high electronegativity ki wajah se. [Q801, Q803]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Oxides ka nature period mein basic → amphoteric → acidic hota hai; ye trend important hai. [Q823,\nQ825]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Higher oxidation state ke oxides zyada acidic hote hain; same element ke liye compare karne par. [Q827,\nQ829]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hydrogen ko Group 1 aur Group 17 donon ke saath compare karte hain; isliye unique position hai.\n[Q831, Q833]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Noble gases ab \"inert\" nahi kehte — Xe ke fluorides (XeF₂, XeF₄, XeF₆) hain; Neil Bartlett (1962) ne pehla\nnoble gas compound banaya. [Q867]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Halogens ka physical state down the group change hota hai: gas → liquid → solid; colour bhi dark hoti\nhai. [Q871, Q873]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: HF weak acid hai hydrogen bonding ki wajah se; HCl, HBr, HI strong acids hain. [Q879, Q881]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alkali metals ka melting point down the group ghatta hai; density generally badhti hai (exception Na >\nK). [Q885, Q887]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Aqua regia = HNO₃:HCl (1:3) — gold aur platinum dissolve karta hai; sirf HCl ya HNO₃ se alag nahi hota.\n[Q925, Q927]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Contact process mein V₂O₅ catalyst use hota hai SO₂ → SO₃ conversion ke liye. [Q929, Q931]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Haber process mein Fe catalyst, 400–500°C, 200 atm — conditions yaad rakhna. [Q931, Q933]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Silicon (Si) semiconductor hai; Silica (SiO₂) glass/quartz hai — donon alag. [Q913, Q915]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Barium meal mein BaSO₄ use hota hai X-ray ke liye; Ba²⁺ toxic hai lekin BaSO₄ insoluble hone ki wajah se\nsafe. [Q905]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Technetium (Z=43) aur Promethium (Z=61) — donon naturally stable isotopes nahi rakhte. [Q983, Q985]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Transuranic elements (Z > 92) sab synthetic hain; naturally nahi milte. [Q989, Q991]\n18. Electronic Configuration → Element Identification (Practice)\n● Config 2, 6 (total 8 electrons) = Oxygen (atomic number 8). [Q880, Q956]\n● Config 2, 8, 2 = Magnesium (atomic number 12); Period 3 mein; valency +2 (2 electrons lose karke noble gas\nconfig paata hai). [Q798, Q824]\n● Config 2, 8, 3 = Aluminium (atomic number 13); 3 valence electrons. [Q750]\n● Config 2, 8, 4 = Silicon (atomic number 14). [Q715]\n● Config 2, 8, 5 = Phosphorus (atomic number 15). [Q938]\n● Config 2, 8, 6 = Sulphur (atomic number 16); Group 16, Period 3. [Q866]\n● Config 2, 8, 7 = Chlorine (atomic number 17). [Q754]\n● Config 2, 8, 8 = Argon (atomic number 18); Group 18 (noble gas). [Q729, Q752]\n● Carbon (atomic number 6) ki L-shell mein 4 electrons hote hain (K-shell mein 2). [Q677]\n● Rhodium (Rh, Z=45) ka full electronic configuration example bhi exam mein puchha jaata hai — silver-white,\ncorrosion-resistant metal (1803 mein William Wollaston ne discover kiya). [Q762]\n19. Shell Capacity Rule (2n²) & Basic Structure Facts\n● Formula: shell mein max electrons = 2n² (n = shell number). K-shell (n=1) = 2, L-shell (n=2) = 8, M-shell (n=3) = 18,\nN-shell (n=4) = 32. [Q828, Q836, Q845]\n● Valence electrons = atom ki outermost shell mein present electrons. [Q760]\n● Period 3 ke elements (Na se Ar) ke paas 3 shells hote hain: K, L, M. [Q802]\n● Atomic number = nucleus mein protons ki sankhya; ye element ki periodic table mein position determine karta\nhai (Rutherford ne 1917 mein proton discover kiya tha). [Q766]\n● Isotopes: same atomic number (same protons) lekin different mass number; different physical properties (mass\nalag hone se) lekin similar chemical properties (same electron config hone se). Protium (H isotope) mein 0\nneutrons hote hain — sirf 1 proton aur 1 electron. [Q940, Q758]\n20. Period-wise & Group-wise Element Counts\n● Period 1 = sirf 2 elements (Hydrogen, Helium) — dono gases hain. Period 2 aur 3 = 8-8 elements each. Period 4\naur 5 = 18-18 elements each. Period 6 aur 7 = 32-32 elements each. [Q886, Q972, Q890, Q944, Q814]\n● Total 18 groups aur 7 periods modern periodic table mein hote hain. [Q847]\n21. Family Names, Block Classification & Rare Earth Facts"," ● Group 1 = Alkali metals (Li, Na, K, Rb, Cs, Fr) — highly reactive, 1 valence electron. [Q774, Q888, Q908, Q986]\n● Group 2 = Alkaline earth metals (Be, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba, Ra). [Q930]\n● s-block = Group 1 aur 2 ke elements (last electron s-orbital mein enter karta hai). [Q830]\n● d-block (Group 3-12) = Transition elements; variable oxidation states exhibit karte hain (jaise Cu, Fe, Ni). [Q852,\nQ932, Q966]\n● f-block = Lanthanides aur Actinides = Rare earth elements; inke 3 outermost shells incomplete hote hain (4f/5d/6s\nya 5f/6d/7s subshells). [Q818, Q820, Q826, Q854, Q910]\n● Radioactive elements mainly Actinides series mein placed hain (Actinium se Lawrencium tak, Z=89-103). [Q876]\n22. Atomic Number → Group/Period Matching Practice\n● Atomic number 20 (Calcium) Be (atomic number 4) ke saath similar chemical properties dikhata hai — donon\nGroup 2 mein hain. [Q816]\n● Atomic number 13 (Aluminium) aur 31 (Gallium) same group (13) mein hain. [Q906]\n● Atomic number 16 wala element 3rd period mein aata hai (config 2,8,6). [Q849]\n● Atomic number 17 (Chlorine) atomic number 35 (Bromine) ke saath resemble karta hai — donon Group 17\n(halogens) mein. [Q902]\n● Atomic number 11 se 18 tak (Na se Ar) sab elements Period 3 mein aate hain. [Q740]\n● Diye gaye atomic numbers mein sabse kam atomic number wala element period mein sabse zyada metallic hota\nhai (left-most position). [Q892, Q904]\n● Atomic numbers 2, 3, 7, 10, 30 diye gaye — jo 3-10 range mein hain (3, 7, 10) wo second period mein same period\nshare karte hain. [Q796]\n● Diye gaye elements Sc, Ga, Be, As mein Sc (Scandium, Group 3) sabse zyada metallic character dikhata hai (period\nmein sabse left position). [Q739]\n● B(5), Ne(10), K(19), O(8) ko increasing atomic number order mein arrange karne par: B, O, Ne, K. [Q733]\n23. Miscellaneous Element Facts, Uses & Ionization Facts\n● Gallium metal itna low melting point rakhta hai ki hatheli (palm) ki garmi se hi pighal jaata hai. [Q844]\n● Germanium (Ge) ek semiconductor hai. [Q850]\n● Silicon hydrogen ke saath silanes (chain compounds, 7-8 atoms tak) banata hai — inorganic analogue of alkanes,\nlekin weak Si-H bonds ki wajah se highly reactive. [Q960]\n● Sodium apni high reactivity ki wajah se aasani se cation (Na⁺) banata hai, electropositive metal hai. [Q948]\n● Ionization energy ka SI unit KJ/mol hota hai. [Q952]\n24. Additional Practice Facts (Position, Valency & Statements)\n● P, Q, R, S elements atomic numbers 2, 6, 13, 18 — P (noble gas, valency 0) aur S (noble gas, valency 0) same\nvalency rakhte hain. [Q673]\n● Element ki colour uski periodic table position se directly governed NAHI hoti — baaki properties (radius, valency,\nvalence electrons) position-dependent hoti hain. [Q683]\n● Element X jo Chlorine ke saath XCl banata hai aur periodic table ke left side mein hai — X = Hydrogen (1 valence\nelectron, non-metal, gas); HCl banata hai. [Q685]\n● Period 2, Group 2 ka element (Beryllium) ke 2 valence electrons hote hain. [Q687, Q703]\n● Match karna: smallest atom = Lithium; metalloid = Silicon; most metallic natural element = Cesium; most"," electronegative = Fluorine; least electronegative = Iodine (halogens mein). [Q691, Q721]\n● Atomic numbers 15, 16, 17, 18 = Phosphorus (P), Sulphur (S), Chlorine (Cl), Argon (Ar). [Q695, Q748]\n● Eka-aluminium (Mendeleev ki predicted element) ka oxide = Ga₂O₃ (Gallium oxide). [Q697]\n● Second period ke elements (Li se Ne) same number of shells (2) rakhte hain, lekin valence electrons alag-alag hote\nhain. [Q699]\n● Tellurium (Z=52) periodic table mein Selenium (34, upar), Antimony (51, left), Iodine (53, right) aur Polonium (84,\nneeche) se surrounded hai. [Q707]\n●\n\n⚠️Statement check: Potassium reactivity series mein LEAST reactive nahi, balki sabse MOST reactive common\nmetals mein se ek hai. [Q717]\n● Fluorine sabse zyada tendency rakhta hai electron gain karne ki (sabse zyada electron affinity trend mein, lekin\nactual max EA Chlorine ka hai due to F ki repulsion). [Q745]\n● Fluorine aur Chlorine dono ke 7 valence electrons hote hain (Group 17). [Q747]\n● Zinc (Zn, atomic number 30) ki position: Group 12, Period 4 (d-block). [Q749]\n● Period 1 mein sirf 2 elements hote hain (H aur He) — 1 element wala koi bhi period nahi hota. [Q770]\n● Modern periodic table mein elements increasing nuclear charge (atomic number) ke order mein arranged hote\nhain. [Q772]\n● Electron affinity down the group generally decrease hoti hai (top se bottom). [Q778]\n● Group 18 ke elements (noble gases) ka outer shell completely filled hota hai. [Q786]\n● Period 4, Group 2 ka element = Calcium (Ca). [Q810]\n● Helium (He) ka maximum ionisation potential hota hai saare elements mein. [Q832]\n● Alkali metal group ki characteristics: sab metals hain, water ke saath react karke H₂ gas dete hain, sabki valency 1\nhoti hai. [Q838]\n● Electronegativity = halogen atoms ki electrons attract karne ki property. [Q840]\n● Mercurous ion (Hg⁺) ki valency 1 hoti hai (Mercuric Hg²⁺ ki valency 2). [Q843]\n● Same group ke elements same number of valence electrons rakhte hain, isliye same chemical properties dikhate\nhain. [Q856, Q950]\n● Symbol H hydrogen element ko represent karta hai — lightest, colourless, odourless, diatomic gas. [Q868]\n● Calcium ka atomic mass = 40 hota hai. [Q884]\n● Statement check: Har ore ek mineral hota hai lekin har mineral ore nahi hota (ore mein economically extractable\nmetal hona zaroori hai). [Q912, Q920]\n● Be (4) aur B (5) ka pair increasing atomic number ka correct example hai (left to right). [Q982]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 7 Periodic Table Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0395","t":"08 Chemical Reactions","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.8 — CHEMICAL REACTIONS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚗️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Types of Chemical Reactions: Overview\n2. Combination Reactions\n3. Decomposition Reactions\n4. Displacement Reactions & Reactivity Series\n5. Double Displacement & Precipitation\n6. Neutralization Reactions\n7. Redox Reactions: Oxidation & Reduction\n8. Exothermic vs Endothermic Reactions\n9. Balancing Chemical Equations & Laws\n10. Important Industrial & Daily Life Reactions\n11. Corrosion, Rancidity & Tarnishing\n12. Physical vs Chemical Change\n13. Gases, Colours & Key Observations\n14. Rate of Reaction\n15.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Full)\n⚠️\n1. Types of Chemical Reactions: Overview\n● Combination (A + B → AB): Do ya zyada reactants milke ek product. Examples: 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O; N₂ + 3H₂ →\n2NH₃; H₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl; H₂ + Br₂ → 2HBr; SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄; CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂; 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO; 2Cu + O₂\n→ 2CuO; C + O₂ → CO₂; 2CO + O₂ → 2CO₂. General form A + B → AB (do ya zyada compounds mil ke ek single\nnaya compound banate hain). [Q1002, Q1003, Q1025, Q1062, Q1074, Q1248, Q1285, Q1309, Q1326, Q1329, Q1052, Q1117,\nQ1123, Q1160, Q1163, Q1178, Q1188, Q1199]\n● Decomposition (AB → A + B): Ek reactant toot ke simpler products. Types: Thermal, Electrolytic, Photolytic. AgCl\nsunlight mein grey ho jaata hai (decompose hoke Ag + Cl₂ banata hai). CaCO₃ heat karne pe Quick lime (CaO) +\nCO₂ deta hai. Heating of calcium carbonate combination reaction NAHI hai — ye decomposition hai. [Q1015,\nQ1020, Q1024, Q1046, Q1056, Q1060, Q1101, Q1211, Q1219, Q1253, Q1270, Q1272, Q1285, Q1311, Q1316, Q1334, Q1124, Q1137,\nQ1142, Q1147]\n● Displacement (A + BC → AC + B): Zyada reactive element kam reactive element ko displace karta hai. [Q1018,\nQ1026, Q1027, Q1031, Q1043, Q1049, Q1050, Q1060, Q1065, Q1069, Q1080, Q1095, Q1099, Q1215, Q1234, Q1259, Q1264, Q1294,\nQ1306, Q1325, Q1116, Q1121, Q1125, Q1126, Q1150, Q1154, Q1159, Q1164, Q1172, Q1176, Q1191, Q1192, Q1193, Q1196, Q1291]\n● Double Displacement (AB + CD → AD + CB): Dono reactants ke ions exchange hote hain. Precipitation aur\nneutralization isi ke under aate hain — \"double substitution reaction\" bhi kehte hain (do groups/ions\nsimultaneously exchange hote hain). [Q997, Q1001, Q1011, Q1039, Q1041, Q1057, Q1058, Q1063, Q1075, Q1076, Q1077,\nQ1084, Q1085, Q1104, Q1108, Q1217, Q1222, Q1229, Q1237, Q1249, Q1251, Q1257, Q1263, Q1296, Q1307, Q1323, Q1122, Q1127,\nQ1129, Q1139, Q1152, Q1167, Q1191]\n● Neutralization (Acid + Base → Salt + Water): H⁺ + OH⁻ → H₂O. Exothermic hota hai. NaOH (base) + CH₃COOH (acid)\n→ CH₃COONa + H₂O bhi neutralization ka example hai (weak acid ke saath). Ca(OH)₂ + conc. H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ +\nH₂O bhi exothermic neutralization hai. [Q1007, Q1012, Q1013, Q1014, Q1016, Q1017, Q1023, Q1076, Q1113, Q1114, Q1238,\nQ1301, Q1119, Q1133, Q1141, Q1170, Q1197, Q1040]\n● Precipitation: Jab insoluble solid (precipitate) aqueous solution mein banta hai — cation ek reactant ka aur anion\ndusre reactant ka combine hoke insoluble ionic solid banate hain. [Q998, Q1047, Q1067, Q1072, Q1073, Q1084, Q1085,\nQ1089, Q1092, Q1100, Q1102, Q1104, Q1108, Q1110, Q1217, Q1229, Q1251, Q1257, Q1263, Q1323, Q1120, Q1127, Q1129, Q1130,\nQ1135, Q1145, Q1146, Q1148, Q1152, Q1165, Q1168, Q1171, Q1175, Q1180, Q1183, Q1185, Q1189, Q1190, Q1194]\n● Redox Reaction: Oxidation aur reduction simultaneously. [Q997, Q1006, Q1008, Q1009, Q1022, Q1031, Q1032, Q1034,\nQ1042, Q1059, Q1065, Q1069, Q1082, Q1090, Q1094, Q1096, Q1103, Q1204, Q1220, Q1224, Q1228, Q1230, Q1233, Q1235, Q1236,\nQ1252, Q1256, Q1269, Q1273, Q1299, Q1314, Q1318, Q1321, Q1083, Q1132, Q1134, Q1144, Q1149, Q1155, Q1161, Q1166, Q1169,\nQ1173, Q1177, Q1187, Q1195, Q1196]"," ● Combustion: Substance burns in O₂; heat/light release hoti hai. Complete combustion → CO₂ + H₂O; incomplete\n→ CO/C. Coal aur petroleum ka combustion Nitrogen aur Sulphur ke harmful oxides (NOₓ, SOₓ) bhi banata hai —\nye acid rain/smog cause karte hain. Iron bhi air mein burn karke Fe₂O₃ banata hai (4Fe + 3O₂ → 2Fe₂O₃). [Q1044,\nQ1068, Q1213, Q1246, Q1266, Q1326, Q1292, Q1245]\n● Addition: Molecules combine to form larger one; hydrogenation of oils (Ni catalyst). [Q1010, Q1216]\n● Substitution: Functional group replace hota hai; CH₄ + Cl₂ → CH₃Cl + HCl. Sunlight mein hydrocarbons ke saath Cl₂\nrapidly add/substitute hoti hai (halogenation). [Q1038, Q1279]\n2. Combination Reactions\n● Hydrogen + Oxygen → Water (2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O). [Q1002]\n● Nitrogen + Hydrogen → Ammonia (N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃). [Q1021, Q1025]\n● Sulphur trioxide + Water → Sulphuric acid. [Q1062]\n● Calcium oxide + Water → Calcium hydroxide (slaked lime); ye exothermic hai. [Q1029, Q1111, Q1274, Q1278, Q1309,\nQ1329, Q1118, Q1123, Q1163]\n● Carbon monoxide + Hydrogen → Methanol (CO + 2H₂ → CH₃OH at 340 atm). [Q1061, Q1088]\n● Mg + O₂ → 2MgO; Cu + O₂ → 2CuO; C + O₂ → CO₂. Balanced form: 2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s). [Q1248, Q1285,\nQ1329, Q1117]\n● Hydrogen + Bromine → Hydrogen Bromide: H₂ + Br₂ → 2HBr (balanced equation). [Q1052]\n3. Decomposition Reactions\n● Thermal Decomposition: Heat se compound toot ta hai.\n– ZnCO₃ → ZnO + CO₂. [Q1015]\n– CaCO₃ (limestone) → CaO (Quick lime) + CO₂. [Q1048, Q1211, Q1137, Q1147]\n– 2KClO₃ → 2KCl + 3O₂. [Q1024]\n– 2FeSO₄ → Fe₂O₃ + SO₂ + SO₃. [Q1056, Q1101, Q1334]\n– 2Pb(NO₃)₂ → 2PbO + 4NO₂ + O₂ (brown fumes of NO₂). [Q1036, Q1219]\n– NH₄NO₃ → N₂O + 2H₂O. [Q1285]\n– NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂ (baking soda). [Q1320]\n– Heating of calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) is a decomposition reaction, NOT a combination reaction. [Q1142]\n● Electrolytic Decomposition: Electricity se.\n– 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂ (electrolysis of water). [Q1024, Q1232]\n– 2NaCl(molten) → 2Na + Cl₂. [Q1024]\n● Photolytic Decomposition: Light se.\n– 2AgCl → 2Ag + Cl₂ (sunlight); AgCl grey ho jaata hai sunlight mein decompose hoke. [Q1020, Q1037, Q1253,\nQ1124]\n– 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂ (sunlight). [Q1024, Q1070]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgCl/AgBr sirf sunlight mein decompose hote hain, heat se nahi — ye photolytic hain. [Q1020, Q1037,\nQ1070, Q1253]\n4. Displacement Reactions & Reactivity Series\n● Reactivity series: K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > H > Cu > Hg > Ag > Pt > Au. [Q1077, Q1304]"," ● ECS (Electrochemical Series): Li > K > Ba > Ca > Na > Mg > Al > Mn > Zn > Cr > Fe > Co > Ni > Sn > Pb > H > Cu > Hg >\nAg > Pt > Au. [Q1095]\n● Zyada reactive metal kam reactive metal ke salt solution ko displace kar sakta hai. [Q1018, Q1026, Q1031, Q1095,\nQ1099, Q1125, Q1192]\n● Examples:\n– Mg + CuSO₄ → MgSO₄ + Cu (blue colour fades, red-brown deposit). [Q1026, Q1031, Q1068]\n– Zn + CuSO₄ → ZnSO₄ + Cu. [Q1043, Q1049, Q1099, Q1264, Q1154, Q1193]\n– Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu (iron ne copper ko displace kiya). [Q1041, Q1049, Q1215, Q1121, Q1125]\n– Pb + CuCl₂ → PbCl₂ + Cu (ismein sirf Cl atom hi ion ke roop mein rehta hai). [Q1041, Q1060, Q1325, Q1164]\n– Ca + CuSO₄ → CaSO₄ + Cu. [Q1018]\n– Al + CuSO₄ → Al₂(SO₄)₃ + Cu. [Q1080]\n– Zn + FeCl₂ → ZnCl₂ + Fe. [Q1325]\n– 2Al + Fe₂O₃ → Al₂O₃ + 2Fe (Aluminium Iron se zyada reactive hai, isliye displace karta hai). [Q1116, Q1196]\n– 2KI + Cl₂ → 2KCl + I₂ (halogen displacement). [Q1027]\n– Zn + 2HCl → ZnCl₂ + H₂↑ (H₂ combustible, popping sound). [Q1112]\n– Zn + H₂SO₄ → ZnSO₄ + H₂. [Q1091, Q1176]\n– Fe + 2HCl → FeCl₂ + H₂ (iron filings + dilute HCl). [Q1291]\n– Zn + NaOH → Na₂ZnO₂ + H₂ (sodium zincate). [Q1234]\n– 3Fe + 4H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + 4H₂ (H₂O oxidising agent, coefficients x=3, y=4, z=4). [Q1126, Q1150]\n– Zn + 2AgNO₃ → Zn(NO₃)₂ + 2Ag (zinc silver nitrate se silver displace karta hai). [Q1159]\n– Element A jo chlorine ke saath high-melting, water-soluble ACl banata hai — A = Sodium (2Na + Cl₂ → 2NaCl).\n[Q1172]\n● Platinum aur Silver CuSO₄ se Cu displace nahi kar sakte (kam reactive). [Q1026]\n● H₂ gas dilute HCl se sirf woh metals liberate kar sakti hain jo H se upar hain: Pb kar sakta hai; Cu, Hg, Ag nahi kar\nsakte. [Q1098, Q1271, Q1304]\n● Cu + PbCl₂ → CuCl₂ + Pb NOT possible (Cu Pb se neeche hai ECS mein). [Q1095]\n● Cu + ZnSO₄ → NO reaction (Cu Zn se kam reactive). [Q1262]\n● Double substitution/displacement reaction mein do groups (anions ya cations) simultaneously exchange hote\nhain — displacement se alag hai jismein ek single element replace hota hai. [Q1191]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgBr → Ag + Br₂ displacement nahi hai, ye photolytic decomposition hai. [Q1060]\n5. Double Displacement & Precipitation\n● General form: AB + CD → AD + CB. [Q1039, Q1041, Q1058, Q1085, Q1104, Q1108, Q1122, Q1152]\n● Examples:\n– AgNO₃ + NaCl → AgCl↓ + NaNO₃ (white precipitate). [Q997, Q1001, Q1011, Q1072, Q1122, Q1129]\n– AgNO₃ + KBr → AgBr + KNO₃. [Q1001]\n– Na₂SO₄ + BaCl₂ → BaSO₄↓ + 2NaCl (white precipitate). [Q1041, Q1057, Q1084, Q1085, Q1104, Q1152, Q1165, Q1171,\nQ1194]\n– CuSO₄ + BaCl₂ → BaSO₄↓ + CuCl₂. [Q1047]\n– CuSO₄ + H₂S → CuS↓ + H₂SO₄. [Q1077, Q1183]\n– Pb(NO₃)₂ + 2KI → PbI₂↓ + 2KNO₃ (yellow precipitate). [Q1067, Q1092, Q1102, Q1108, Q1110, Q1120, Q1146]\n– 2NaOH + CuSO₄ → Cu(OH)₂↓ + Na₂SO₄. [Q1075]\n– CuO + 2HCl → CuCl₂ + H₂O (blue-green colour CuCl₂ ki wajah se). [Q1087, Q1157]"," – Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂↑ (effervescence, gas lime water milky karta hai). [Q1251, Q1323, Q1136]\n– CaCl₂ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + 2HCl. [Q1097]\n– Marble chips (CaCO₃) + dilute HCl → CaCl₂ + H₂O + CO₂. [Q1257, Q1200]\n– Na₂S + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂S↑ (rotten-egg smell wali gas). [Q1051]\n– 2KBr + BaI₂ → 2KI + BaBr₂ (BaBr₂ insoluble hai). [Q1145]\n– 3BaCl₂ + Al₂(SO₄)₃ → 3BaSO₄↓ + 2AlCl₃. [Q1135, Q1168]\n– Na₂CO₃ + CaCl₂ → CaCO₃↓ + 2NaCl (double displacement + precipitation dono). [Q1185, Q1189]\n– Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O (left side mein 4 oxygen atoms hote hain). [Q1190]\n● BaSO₄: water insoluble white crystalline solid; odourless. Uses: X-ray contrast agent (barium meal), oil drilling\nfluid, plastic filler. [Q1084, Q1089]\n● Precipitate ki physical state hamesha solid hoti hai; precipitation reaction hamesha ek insoluble ionic salt banati\nhai. [Q1100, Q1127, Q1130, Q1175]\n● Double displacement reactions ke 3 typical signs: precipitate banna, gas evolve hona, colour change hona —\nteeno hi possible hain. [Q1148]\n● Precipitation reactions double displacement reactions ki hi ek specific class hain (neutralization bhi). [Q1180]\n● Ionic compounds ke beech hi double displacement reaction hoti hai (ions exchange). [Q1167]\n● Lemon juice milk mein daalne se curdling hoti hai — ye bhi ek precipitation-type reaction hai (lactic acid forms,\npaneer banta hai). [Q1189]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgNO₃ + NaCl → AgCl + NaNO₃ redox nahi hai — ye double displacement hai. Redox mein oxidation\nnumber change hota hai. [Q997]\n6. Neutralization Reactions\n● Acid + Base → Salt + Water. [Q1007, Q1012, Q1014, Q1016, Q1017, Q1023, Q1076, Q1113, Q1133]\n● Products hamesha H₂O + Salt hote hain. [Q1113]\n● Examples:\n– HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O. [Q1017, Q1023, Q1076]\n– HNO₃ + KOH → KNO₃ + H₂O. [Q1014, Q1017, Q1114]\n– Ca(OH)₂ + 2HCl → CaCl₂ + 2H₂O. [Q1012]\n– 2LiOH + H₂SO₄ → Li₂SO₄ + 2H₂O. [Q1016]\n– Ca(OH)₂ + H₂CO₃ → CaCO₃ + 2H₂O. [Q1114]\n– H₃PO₄ + 3KOH → K₃PO₄ + 3H₂O. [Q1114]\n– NaOH + HCl → NaCl + H₂O. [Q1238]\n– CaO + 2HCl → CaCl₂ + H₂O. [Q1301]\n– NaOH + CH₃COOH → CH₃COONa (X) + H₂O (Y) — weak acid (acetic acid) + strong base ka neutralization.\n[Q1119, Q1170]\n– 2NaOH + H₂SO₄ → Na₂SO₄ + 2H₂O. [Q1141]\n– 2HNO₃ + Ca(OH)₂ → Ca(NO₃)₂ + 2H₂O (balancing coefficients a=2, b=1, c=2). [Q1197]\n– Ca(OH)₂ + H₂SO₄(conc.) → CaSO₄ + 2H₂O (bahut exothermic; energy itni release hoti hai ki fire bhi cause kar\nsakta hai). [Q1040]\n● Exothermic reaction hai. [Q1012, Q1029, Q1111]\n● 5 ml NaOH + 5 ml HCl neutralize; toh 10 ml NaOH ke liye 10 ml HCl chahiye (1:1 ratio). [Q1023]\n● Antacids mein Mg(OH)₂ ya MgCO₃ use hote hain excess HCl neutralize karne ke liye. [Q1012]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ neutralization nahi hai — ye combination + exothermic reaction hai. [Q1114]"," 7. Redox Reactions: Oxidation & Reduction\n● Oxidation: O₂ gain, H₂ loss, electrons loss. Substance jab O₂ ke saath combine hota hai toh woh oxidize hota hai.\n[Q1022, Q1034, Q1082, Q1090, Q1204, Q1235, Q1083, Q1149]\n● Reduction: H₂ gain, O₂ loss, electrons gain. \"Loss of electrons\" reduction ka INCORRECT statement hai — ye toh\noxidation ki definition hai. [Q1032, Q1034, Q1096, Q1233, Q1236, Q1166, Q1177]\n● Oxidizing agent: Dusre ko oxidize karta hai (khud reduce hota hai). [Q1022]\n● Reducing agent: Dusre ko reduce karta hai (khud oxidize hota hai). [Q1022]\n● Examples:\n– ZnO + C → Zn + CO: ZnO reduced (oxidizing agent), C oxidized (reducing agent). [Q1008, Q1042, Q1069, Q1094,\nQ1132, Q1155]\n– Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂: Fe₂O₃ reduced, CO oxidized (reducing agent). [Q1009, Q1256]\n– 2Al + Fe₂O₃ → Al₂O₃ + 2Fe: Fe₂O₃ oxidizing agent (reduced), Al reducing agent (oxidized). [Q1006, Q1196]\n– MnO₂ + 4HCl → MnCl₂ + 2H₂O + Cl₂: MnO₂ reduced (oxidizing agent), HCl oxidized to Cl₂ — \"Cl₂ oxidized to HCl\"\nstatement INCORRECT hai (ulta hota hai). [Q997, Q1059, Q1134]\n– CuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O: CuO reduced, H₂ oxidized. [Q1032, Q1065, Q1233, Q1236, Q1252, Q1321]\n– CuSO₄ + Mg → MgSO₄ + Cu: Mg reducing agent. [Q1050]\n– Cu + conc. HNO₃ → Cu(NO₃)₂ + NO₂ + H₂O: Cu oxidized, N reduced. [Q1103]\n– MgO + CO → Mg + CO₂: CO oxidized, MgO reduced. [Q1224]\n– PbO₂ + 4HCl → PbCl₂ + 2H₂O + Cl₂: HCl oxidized (Cl⁻ → Cl₂). [Q1228]\n– KMnO₄ + FeSO₄ (dilute H₂SO₄ mein): KMnO₄ strong oxidizing agent — Fe⁺² → Fe⁺³; purple colour fades. [Q1230]\n– 2PbO + C → 2Pb + CO₂: C oxidized, PbO reduced (x=2, y=2, z=1). [Q1269, Q1161]\n– SnCl₂ + 2HgCl₂ → Hg₂Cl₂ + SnCl₄: SnCl₂ oxidized (Sn⁺² → Sn⁺⁴). [Q1318]\n– H₂O₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl + O₂: H₂O₂ reducing agent (O⁻¹ → O⁰). [Q1314]\n– 2Cu + O₂ → 2CuO: Copper aur Oxygen dono involved reaction mein — Cu oxidize hota hai (loses electrons).\n[Q1173]\n– Zn → Zn²⁺ formation bhi oxidation hai (electron loss). [Q1169]\n– S (Sulphide ion) sulphur se banta hai reduction ke through. [Q1144]\n● Ethanol → Ethanoic acid (CH₃COOH) oxidation hai (alkaline KMnO₄ / acidified K₂Cr₂O₇ + heat). [Q1019, Q1195]\n● Rancidity = oxidation of fats/oils. Chips bags mein N₂ flush ki jaati hai oxidation rokne ke liye. [Q1054, Q1298, Q1313]\n● Rusting = oxidation of iron. [Q1096]\n● Redox reaction ki definition: oxidation aur reduction simultaneously ek hi reaction mein hote hain (electron\ntransfer). [Q1187]\n● Mg ribbon burning air mein (oxidation reaction) → MgO forms. [Q1149, Q1156, Q1140]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 2PbO + C → 2Pb + CO₂ mein \"CO₂ oxidized\" aur \"Pb reduced\" statements galat hain — actually C\noxidized hota hai aur PbO reduced. [Q1269]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: MnO₂ + 4HCl mein MnO₂ oxidizing agent hai (reduce hota hai Mn⁺⁴ → Mn⁺²), HCl reducing agent (oxidize\nhoke Cl₂ banata hai). [Q1059]\n8. Exothermic vs Endothermic Reactions\n● Exothermic: Heat release hoti hai. ΔH negative. Examples: combustion, neutralization, respiration, rusting, slaking\nof lime, freezing of water, dissolving acid/alkali in water, decomposition of vegetable matter, burning of natural\ngas. [Q1029, Q1109, Q1111, Q1213, Q1241, Q1254, Q1255, Q1280, Q1288]\n– Respiration: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O + Energy (exothermic reaction). [Q1029, Q1162]\n– CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O + Heat. [Q1029, Q1213, Q1158]"," ● Endothermic: Heat absorb hoti hai. Examples: melting ice, melting solid salts, photosynthesis, dry ice, alkane\ncracking, NH₄Cl in water, evaporation, thermal decomposition of FeSO₄. [Q1035, Q1109, Q1218, Q1288, Q1334]\n● CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ + heat — vigorously exothermic combination. [Q1111, Q1274, Q1278]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: CaO + H₂O mein heat release hoti hai; ye exothermic combination hai. [Q1111]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Dissolving acid/alkali in water exothermic hota hai — endothermic nahi. [Q1254]\n9. Balancing Chemical Equations & Laws\n● Law of Conservation of Mass: Matter create/destroy nahi hota — isliye balancing zaroori hai. [Q1000, Q1107, Q1212,\nQ1287]\n● Hit and Trial Method se balance karte hain. [Q1064, Q1081]\n● State symbols: (s) = solid, (l) = liquid, (g) = gas, (aq) = aqueous (dissolved in water). Triangle (∆) heating indicate\nkarta hai;\n reversible reactions ke liye.\n⇌\n [Q1013, Q1143]\n● Reaction conditions (temp, pressure, catalyst) arrow ke upar/niche likhte hain. [Q1028]\n● Arrow always products ki taraf point karti hai. Reactants hamesha LHS; products RHS. [Q1055, Q1105]\n● Balanced equation ka matlab: reactants aur products donon taraf har element ke atoms ki sankhya barabar.\n[Q1081, Q1107, Q1250, Q1297, Q1302]\n● Balanced examples:\n– 3BaSO₄ + 2AlCl₃ → 3BaCl₂ + Al₂(SO₄)₃. [Q999]\n– 3Fe + 4H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + 4H₂. [Q1030, Q1126, Q1150, Q1197]\n– S₈ + 4C → 4CS₂. [Q1035]\n– N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃. [Q1021]\n– 6CO₂ + 12H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ + 6H₂O (Photosynthesis). [Q1045]\n– Mg₃N₂ + 6H₂O → 3Mg(OH)₂ + 2NH₃. [Q1071]\n– Zn + H₂SO₄ → ZnSO₄ + H₂. [Q1081]\n– CaCl₂ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + 2HCl. [Q1097]\n– Cu + 4HNO₃ → Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2NO₂ + 2H₂O. [Q1103]\n– SO₂ + 2H₂S → 3S + 2H₂O. [Q1115]\n– 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO. [Q1297, Q1117]\n– CO₂ + 2NaOH → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O (CO₂ NaOH solution mein dissolve hoke sodium carbonate banata hai). [Q1186]\n● Skeletal (Unbalanced) Equation: Atoms equal nahi hote, e.g., Mg + O₂ → MgO. [Q1265, Q1333]\n● During chemical reaction, atomic number same rehta hai (protons participate nahi karte). [Q1223]\n● Galat balanced equation example: CO(g) + H₂(g) → CH₂O(l) — sahi hai CO + H₂ → CH₂O(g) (Formaldehyde), state\nsymbol galat tha. [Q1182]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Balanced equation mein mass equal hota hai, volume equal nahi hoti. [Q1107]\n10. Important Industrial & Daily Life Reactions\n● Bleaching Powder (CaOCl₂ / Ca(OCl)₂): Dry slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂) + Cl₂ → CaOCl₂ + H₂O. Disinfectant, bleaching\nagent; water ke saath Cl₂ release hoti hai. Brine electrolysis se mila Cl₂ gas hi bleaching powder banane mein use\nhota hai. [Q996, Q1033, Q1261, Q1331, Q1174]\n● Chlor-alkali Process: 2NaCl + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + Cl₂ + H₂ (electrolysis of brine). Anode pe oxidation: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻\n(Cl₂ gas anode pe); Cathode pe reduction: 2H₂O + 2e⁻ → H₂ + 2OH⁻ (H₂ gas + NaOH cathode pe); Na⁺ cathode\ncompartment mein migrate karke NaOH banata hai. Brine electrolysis mein H₂ gas pop sound ke saath jalti hai.\n[Q1004, Q1093, Q1324, Q1128, Q1138, Q1153, Q1179, Q1181]"," ● Baking Soda (NaHCO₃): NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ + NH₃ → NH₄Cl + NaHCO₃. NaHCO₃ + H⁺ → CO₂ + H₂O + sodium salt.\nGaram karne pe Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂. [Q1053, Q1320, Q1131]\n● Washing Soda (Na₂CO₃): HCl ke saath CO₂ gas with brisk effervescence deta hai. Raw material = Sodium Chloride\n(NaCl), Solvay's process se banta hai. [Q1251, Q1323, Q1184]\n● NaCl se teen important industrial compounds banate hain: Sodium Hydroxide (chlor-alkali), Baking Soda\n(NaHCO₃), Washing Soda (Na₂CO₃). [Q1231]\n● Plaster of Paris: Calcium Sulphate Hemihydrate (CaSO₄·½H₂O); water milane pe gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) banata hai.\n[Q1247]\n● White Washing: Ca(OH)₂ (slaked lime) + CO₂ (air) → CaCO₃ (thin white layer) + H₂O. Ye reaction 2-3 din baad\nwhitewashed walls pe shiny finish deta hai. [Q1079, Q1275, Q1277]\n● Photosynthesis: 6CO₂ + 12H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ + 6H₂O. [Q1045]\n● Slaking of lime: CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ + heat (exothermic). [Q1029, Q1111, Q1274, Q1278]\n● Ethanol + Conc. H₂SO₄ at 443 K → Ethene (C₂H₄) — dehydration. [Q1226, Q1282]\n● Ethanol + Na → Sodium ethoxide + H₂. [Q1214]\n● CO + 2H₂ → CH₃OH (methanol) at 340 atm pressure. [Q1088]\n● Galvanic Cell = Voltaic Cell: Chemical energy → Electrical energy. [Q1240]\n● Catalyst: Reaction speed up karta hai, khud consume nahi hota. [Q1260]\n● Metal oxide + Acid → Salt + Water (neutralization type). [Q1301]\n● Blast furnace mein Iron oxide (Fe₂O₃) Carbon Monoxide (CO) se reduce hota hai — 2C + O₂ → 2CO; Fe₂O₃ + 3CO →\n2Fe + 3CO₂. [Q1225]\n● Sulphur (Group 16 element) vulcanized rubber banane mein use hota hai; hot concentrated HNO₃ ke saath react\nkarke H₂SO₄ banata hai: S + 6HNO₃ → H₂SO₄ + 2NO₂ + 3H₂O. [Q1303]\n● Welding ke liye Ethyne (C₂H₂) + Oxygen (O₂) ka mixture use hota hai — oxy-acetylene flame bahut high\ntemperature ki hoti hai. [Q1312]\n11. Corrosion, Rancidity & Tarnishing\n● Corrosion: Metals ki surface air/moisture se oxidize hoti hai. Iron → rust (red-brown, Fe₂O₃·nH₂O), Copper →\ngreen. Ye oxidation reaction hai. Serious problem; galvanisation (Zn coating) se prevent karte hain. Iron direct air\nmein burn karke bhi Fe₂O₃ banata hai (combustion, corrosion se alag). [Q1066, Q1078, Q1244, Q1281, Q1332, Q1245]\n● Tarnishing:\n– Copper tarnishing: Humid air mein Cu(OH)₂ + CuCO₃ = green coating. [Q1239]\n– Silver tarnishing: Air mein H₂S se react karke Ag₂S (black) banata hai. [Q1203, Q1207]\n● Rancidity: Fats/oils ka oxidation — taste/smell change. Rancidity rokne ke liye: airtight containers, nitrogen\nflushing (chips bags), antioxidants. [Q1054, Q1298, Q1313]\n● Sodium (Na) itna reactive hai ki khula rakhne par oxygen ke saath explosively react karke aag pakad leta hai —\nisliye kerosene mein store karte hain. [Q1206]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tarnishing/corrosion oxidation hai — displacement ya decomposition nahi. [Q1066, Q1078]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chips bags mein N₂ flush hoti hai, O₂ nahi — oxidation prevent karne ke liye. [Q1054]\n12. Physical vs Chemical Change\n● Chemical Change: New substance with new properties forms — digestion, curd formation, rusting, burning,\nfermentation, candle burning (wax + wick). [Q1268, Q1283, Q1330]\n● Physical Change: No new substance — water → vapor (evaporation), ice melting, sublimation of iodine, sugar\ndissolving, dissolving salt in water. [Q1268, Q1330]"," ● Chemical reaction hone ke indicators: gas evolution, precipitate formation, colour change, temperature change,\nstate change — ye sab valid indicators hain. [Q1276]\n● Chemical weathering rocks/soil ki molecular structure change karti hai (solution, carbonation, hydration,\noxidation-reduction se) — Thermal expansion is NOT a chemical weathering process (ye purely physical hai,\ntemperature ki wajah se expand/contract hota hai). [Q1198]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water ka vapor mein badalna physical change hai, chemical nahi. [Q1268]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Change in size chemical reaction ka indicator nahi hai — state, colour, gas, temperature, precipitate\nindicators hain. [Q1208]\n13. Gases, Colours & Key Observations\n● CO₂: Linear covalent molecule; solid form = dry ice; water mein soluble; lime water (Ca(OH)₂) ko milky (CaCO₃)\nbanata hai. [Q1205, Q1242, Q1317, Q1322, Q1158, Q1200]\n● NO₂: Brown fumes, reddish-brown gas; smog ka colour. [Q1293, Q1319]\n● Mg ribbon burns with dazzling white flame → white powder MgO. [Q1209, Q1227, Q1284, Q1286, Q1315, Q1005,\nQ1149, Q1156]\n● AgCl: Light sensitive; dark bottle mein store karte hain kyunki sunlight mein decompose hota hai (grey ho jaata\nhai). [Q1253, Q1124]\n● Sublimation: Solid directly gas — NH₄Cl, Iodine, Camphor, Naphthalene, Dry ice. [Q1202, Q1210, Q1290]\n● H₂ isotopes: Protium (¹H), Deuterium (²H), Tritium (³H). [Q1112]\n● Reversible reactions:\n symbol use hota hai (e.g., N₂ + 3H₂\n 2NH₃); irreversible mein → hota hai.\n⇌\n⇌\n [Q1300, Q1305]\n● Water of crystallization: Crystals heat karne pe lost hota hai → anhydrous form. CuSO₄·5H₂O (blue) → heat →\nanhydrous CuSO₄ (white). [Q1308, Q1310]\n● Metals jab water ke saath react karte hain toh Hydrogen gas release hoti hai (metal oxide/hydroxide ke saath). Al,\nFe, Zn cold/hot water se react nahi karte lekin steam se karte hain; Pb, Cu, Ag, Au bilkul react nahi karte water se.\n[Q1243]\n● Sodium cold water ke saath violently react karta hai — H₂ gas turant aag pakad leta hai (exothermic). [Q1258]\n● Calcium water ke saath Sodium se kam violently react karta hai; H₂ ke bubbles calcium ki surface se chipak jaate\nhain. [Q1221]\n● Aluminium oxide (Al₂O₃) amphoteric oxide hai — acid aur base dono se react karta hai. [Q1267]\n● Metals generally 1 se 3 (kuch mein 4, jaise Sn, Pb) valence electrons rakhte hain outermost shell mein; non-\nmetals 4-7. [Q1289]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mg₃N₂ + 6H₂O → 3Mg(OH)₂ + 2NH₃ double displacement nahi hai — ye hydrolysis type reaction hai.\n[Q1328]\n14. Rate of Reaction\n● Rate constant (k): Directly proportional to temperature; 10°C rise se rate constant doubles hota hai. [Q1201]\n● Rate = k[A]ᵐ[B]ⁿ; m,n = reaction order. [Q1201]\n15.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Full)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgNO₃ + NaCl → AgCl + NaNO₃ redox nahi hai — ye double displacement hai. [Q997]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: MnO₂ + 4HCl mein MnO₂ oxidizing agent hai (reduce hota hai Mn⁺⁴ → Mn⁺²), HCl reducing agent — \"Cl₂\noxidized to HCl\" ulta statement galat hai. [Q1059, Q1134]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Displacement mein reactivity series ka dhyan rakho — Mg Zn Fe Pb H Cu Ag Au. Ag aur Pt Cu displace"," nahi kar sakte. [Q1026, Q1077]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cu + PbCl₂ → CuCl₂ + Pb possible nahi — Cu Pb se neeche hai ECS mein. [Q1095]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: H₂ liberate karne ke liye metal ko H se upar hona chahiye ECS mein; Cu, Hg, Ag nahi kar sakte. [Q1098,\nQ1271]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgCl/AgBr ka decomposition sirf sunlight mein hota hai (photolytic), heat se nahi. [Q1020, Q1037, Q1070,\nQ1253]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda preparation ka equation: NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ + NH₃ → NH₄Cl + NaHCO₃. [Q1053]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chips bags mein N₂ flush hoti hai, O₂ nahi — oxidation prevent karne ke liye. [Q1054]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Photosynthesis equation balance karte waqt 6CO₂ + 12H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ + 6H₂O hota hai. [Q1045]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tarnishing/corrosion oxidation hai — displacement ya decomposition nahi. [Q1066, Q1078]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ethanol → Ethanoic acid oxidation hai (KMnO₄/K₂Cr₂O₇ + heat). [Q1019, Q1195]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Neutralization hamesha exothermic hota hai. [Q1012, Q1029]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂ combination + exothermic hai, neutralization nahi. [Q1114]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Precipitate hamesha solid state mein hota hai, liquid nahi. [Q1100]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: BaSO₄ water insoluble hai — isliye BaSO₄ X-ray mein safe use hota hai (Ba²⁺ toxic). [Q1089]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Balanced equation mein mass equal hota hai, volume equal nahi hoti. [Q1107]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Reactants hamesha arrow ke left side (LHS) hote hain. [Q1105]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Slaking of lime (CaO + H₂O) exothermic hai — ismein heat release hoti hai. [Q1111]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: HI → H₂ + I₂ decomposition hai — combination ka ulta. [Q1106]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Chlor-alkali process mein Na⁺ cathode ki taraf migrate karta hai NaOH banane ke liye. [Q1093]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 2PbO + C → 2Pb + CO₂ mein \"CO₂ oxidized\" aur \"Pb reduced\" galat hain — actually C oxidized hota hai\naur PbO reduced. [Q1269]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cu + ZnSO₄ → NO reaction (Cu Zn se kam reactive). [Q1262]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water → water vapour physical change hai, chemical nahi. [Q1268]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Change in size chemical reaction ka indicator nahi hai. [Q1208]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Dissolving acid/alkali in water exothermic hota hai. [Q1254]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Photosynthesis, methane chlorination, photography = photochemical; ammonia synthesis = NOT\nphotochemical. [Q1295]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: N₂ + 3H₂\n 2NH₃ reversible hai, irreversible nahi.\n⇌\n [Q1300]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Unbalanced equation = skeletal equation. [Q1333]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Anhydrous form = water of crystallization lost. [Q1308]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ca + H₂O ki reaction kam violent hoti hai Na se. [Q1327, Q1221, Q1258]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mg₃N₂ + 6H₂O → 3Mg(OH)₂ + 2NH₃ double displacement nahi hai — ye hydrolysis type hai. [Q1328]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: \"Reduction = Loss of electrons\" statement galat hai — reduction mein electrons GAIN hote hain, loss\noxidation mein hota hai. [Q1166]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Metals jo carbon se reduce ho sakte hain (Zn, Fe, Cu jaise moderately reactive) — lekin K, Na, Mg, Ca, Al\njaise highly reactive metals ke oxides carbon, H₂ ya CO se reduce NAHI hote (unhe electrolysis se extract karte\nhain, kyunki inki oxygen ke saath affinity carbon se zyada hoti hai). [Q1086, Q1151]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 8 Chemical Reactions Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0396","t":"09 Ideal Gas Law","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.9 — IDEAL GAS LAW — FULL MIND MAP\n💨\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Combustion & Balanced Equations\n2. Temperature Scales & Conversions\n3. Gases: Properties & Identification\n4. Gas Laws & Ideal Gas Equation\n5. States of Matter & Phase Changes\n6. Avogadro's Number & Molecular Concepts\n7. Molar Volume at NTP & Numerical Tricks\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Combustion & Balanced Equations\n● Methane combustion: CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O. 1 methane molecule se 1 CO₂ aur 2 H₂O molecules bante hain.\n[Q1335]\n● Ye complete combustion ka example hai — hydrocarbon + O₂ → CO₂ + H₂O. [Q1335]\n2. Temperature Scales & Conversions\n● Freezing point of water: 0°C = 32°F = 273.15 K. [Q1336]\n● Boiling point of water: 100°C. [Q1336]\n● Conversion formulas:\n– K = °C + 273.15\n– °C = (°F - 32) × 5/9 [Q1336]\n● Kelvin scale ka naam Lord Kelvin (William Thomson) ke naam pe rakha gaya hai. [Q1336]\n● Maximum density of water: 4°C = 277 K pe hoti hai — is temperature pe do opposing effects balance mein hote\nhain. [Q1339]\n● Environmental effect: Lakes aur ponds upar se pehle freeze hote hain kyunki 4°C pe water densest hota hai.\n[Q1339]\n3. Gases: Properties & Identification\n● Chlorine (Cl₂): Greenish-yellow gas, toxic, corrosive, irritating to eyes/respiratory system; second-lightest halogen.\n[Q1340]\n● Carbon Monoxide (CO): Odourless, colorless, incomplete combustion se banta hai. [Q1340]\n● Hydrogen Sulphide (H₂S): Colorless, poisonous, corrosive, flammable; rotten egg smell; chalcogen-hydride gas.\n[Q1340]\n● Iodine: Heaviest stable halogen; mineral found in some foods. [Q1340]\n● Noble Gases: Monoatomic hote hain — He, Ne, Ar, Kr, Xe. [Q1341]\n● Diatomic: H, F etc (atomic pairs). Polyatomic: Se, Ozone (O₃). [Q1341]\n● CO₂ in Soda Water: Carbonation process se dissolve hoti hai; Henry's Law se describe ki jaati hai; pH 3–4; Pepsi,\nCoke sab mein hoti hai. [Q1337]"," ● Freon: Refrigerant ke roop mein use hota hai — soda water mein nahi. [Q1337]\n● Nitrogen (N₂): Atmosphere ka ~78% hissa; non-metal. [Q1337]\n4. Gas Laws & Ideal Gas Equation\n● Ideal Gas Equation: PV = nRT. [Q1342, Q1347]\n– P = Pressure\n– V = Volume\n– n = moles of gas\n– R = Universal gas constant = 8.31 JK⁻¹ mol⁻¹\n– T = Temperature (Kelvin) [Q1342, Q1347]\n● Time gas ke behavior ko describe nahi karta — PV=nRT mein nahi aata. [Q1342]\n● Boyle's Law: Constant temperature pe, V 1/P; PV = constant.\n∝\n [Q1344]\n● Gas constant (R): Ideal gas ke properties (P, T, V, quantity) ke beech relationship quantify karta hai; low pressure\npe valid. [Q1347]\n● Temperature increase pe molecular motion distribution:\n– Maximum possible speed badhti hai.\n– Speed distribution curve broaden hota hai.\n– Higher speed pe molecules ki sankhya badhti hai.\n– Same temperature pe heavier molecules slower hote hain lighter ones se.\n– Curve ke neeche ka area same rehta hai. [Q1348]\n5. States of Matter & Phase Changes\n● Evaporation: Liquid → Gas; ALL temperatures pe hota hai — sirf boiling point pe nahi. [Q1345, Q1346]\n– Surface phenomenon hai.\n– Surface area badhane se rate badhti hai.\n– Temperature, wind velocity, humidity pe depend karta hai. [Q1345, Q1346]\n● Condensation: Gas → Liquid. [Q1346]\n● Solidification: Liquid → Solid. [Q1346]\n● Liquefaction: Gas → Liquid. [Q1346]\n● Sedimentation: Water + insoluble mixture mein heavier components neeche baith jaate hain. [Q1338]\n● Decantation: Liquid ko solid aur immiscible liquids se alag karna. [Q1338]\n● Filtration: Solid aur fluid ko mixture se alag karna. [Q1338]\n● Evaporation = vapourization of liquid into gas; NOT same as boiling. [Q1338, Q1345]\n6. Avogadro's Number & Molecular Concepts\n● Avogadro's Number: N₀ = 6.022 × 10²³ (units: electrons, ions, atoms, molecules per mole). [Q1343]\n● Avogadro's Law: Same temperature aur pressure pe, equal volumes of all gases mein same number of molecules\nhote hain. [Q1343]\n● Speed distribution molecule ke mass pe depend karta hai — same T pe heavier molecules slower. [Q1348]"," 7. Molar Volume at NTP & Numerical Tricks\n● NTP (Normal Temperature & Pressure) pe 1 mole kisi bhi ideal gas ka volume 22.4 L hota hai. [Q1349]\n● Avogadro's Law: Same T & P pe, equal volumes mein equal number of molecules hote hain — isliye mass/volume\nratio constant rehta hai for a given gas. Formula: W₁/V₁ = W₂/V₂. [Q1349]\n● Numerical example: 10 g gas X ka volume NTP pe 5.6 L hai — molecular weight nikaalna hai.\n– Logic: Agar 10 g → 5.6 L, toh 22.4 L (1 mole) ka kitna mass hoga?\n– Calculation: W₂ = (10 g × 22.4 L) / 5.6 L = 224/5.6 = 40 g/mol.\n– Trick: 22.4/5.6 = 4, toh 10 × 4 = 40 directly aa jaata hai — time bachao exam mein. [Q1349]\n● NTP pe 22.4 L/mol yaad rakho; STP pe bhi approximately same hota hai lekin exact values alag ho sakti hain (STP =\n0°C, 1 atm; NTP = 20°C, 1 atm ya 298 K). [Q1349]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Evaporation sirf boiling point pe nahi — sabhi temperatures pe hota hai. [Q1345]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Temperature badhane pe \"most probable motion wale molecules ka fraction increases\" — ye statement\ngalat hai. Actually curve broaden hone pe ye fraction ghat-ta hai. [Q1348]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Time gas behavior describe nahi karta — PV=nRT mein nahi aata. [Q1342]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water ka maximum density 4°C (277 K) pe hota hai — 0°C pe nahi. [Q1339]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Freezing point 273.15 K hai — 273 K exact nahi, 273.15 K exact value hai. [Q1336]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Freon = refrigerant; soda water mein CO₂ hoti hai, Freon nahi. [Q1337]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NTP pe molar volume 22.4 L/mol hota hai — mass/volume ratio proportion se molecular weight nikalte\nhain. [Q1349]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 9 Ideal Gas Law Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0397","t":"10 Chemical Properties","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.10 — CHEMICAL PROPERTIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🧫\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Acids, Bases, Salts & pH\n2. Important Compounds & Their Uses\n3. Metals, Non-metals & Reactivity Series\n4. Ionic vs Covalent Compounds\n5. Redox, Corrosion & Rancidity\n6. Isotopes, Isobars & Isomers\n7. States of Matter & Physical Properties\n8. Fireworks, Flame Tests & Gas Colours\n9. Acid Rain & Environment\n10. Photography & Silver Compounds\n11. Coal, Coal Tar & Fractional Distillation\n12. Chemical vs Physical Change\n13. Electrolysis & Electrical Conduction\n14. Water, Hardness & Solutions\n15. Fire Extinguishers & Safety\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Acids, Bases, Salts & pH\n● Acid + Base → Salt + Water (neutralization). [Q1353, Q1378]\n● Sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO₃, Baking Soda):\n– Antacid — excess stomach acid neutralize karta hai.\n– HCl ke saath react karke CO₂ gas deta hai: NaHCO₃ + HCl → NaCl + CO₂ + H₂O.\n– Bee sting (formic acid HCOOH) ko neutralize karne ke liye use hota hai.\n– Solvay process se industrially produce hota hai.\n– Fire extinguishers, cosmetics, ear drops mein bhi use hota hai. [Q1353, Q1378]\n● Sodium carbonate (Na₂CO₃, Washing Soda):\n– Hard water ko normalize karta hai — temporary aur permanent dono hardness remove karta hai (Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺\nions ko insoluble carbonate mein precipitate karta hai).\n– Detergents, soaps, paper, water glass, borax manufacturing mein use hota hai.\n– Stain removal ke liye bhi use hota hai. [Q1351, Q1367, Q1396]\n● Sodium hydroxide (NaOH, Caustic Soda / Lye):\n– Soaps, rayon, paper, explosives, dyestuffs, petroleum products, cotton processing, metal cleaning,\nelectroplating mein use hota hai.\n– Permanent hardness remove karne ke liye use NAHI hota — ye uska use nahi hai. [Q1354]\n● Alum (Fitkari): Double salt ka example — equimolar proportions of K₂SO₄ + Al₂(SO₄)₃ crystallise karke banta hai.\nMohr's salt (FeSO₄.(NH₄)₂SO₄.6H₂O) bhi double salt hai. [Q1383]\n● Bleaching Powder {Ca(ClO)₂ / CaOCl₂}: Oxidising agent hai; chlorine gas + calcium hydroxide se banta hai; water\npurification, textile, paper industries mein use hota hai. [Q1375]\n● pH Scale: Acidic < 7; Neutral = 7; Basic > 7. [Q1416]\n● Amphoteric oxides: Al₂O₃, ZnO — acid aur base donon se react karte hain. [Q1372]\n● Basic oxides: Metals ke oxides jo water se basic solution banate hain — e.g., Na₂O (sodium oxide, Na = atomic"," number 11). [Q1393]\n● CaO (Quicklime): White, caustic, alkaline, crystalline solid at room temperature. [Q1361]\n● Ca(OH)₂ (Slaked Lime): Soft white powder; CO₂ se react karke limestone (CaCO₃) banata hai. [Q1361]\n● Denatured alcohol: Ethanol + poisonous substances (methanol) + blue dye — peene ke liye unfit; easily\nrecognized. [Q1395]\n● Pb(NO₃)₂ + 2KI → PbI₂↓ (yellow precipitate) + 2KNO₃ — double displacement reaction jismein lead aur potassium\napne anions exchange karte hain. [Q1356]\n2. Important Compounds & Their Uses\n● Plaster of Paris (POP):\n– Calcium sulphate hemihydrate: CaSO₄·½H₂O.\n– Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) ko 373 K (100–120°C) par heat karke banta hai.\n– Water ke saath hard mass mein set hota hai.\n– Uses: False ceiling, sculptures, moulds, bone fracture plasters, blackboard chalk, dentistry, fireproofing,\nchemical lab mein airtight sealing.\n– Moisture se bachake sealed container mein rakhna chahiye. [Q1352, Q1355, Q1369]\n● Gypsum: Calcium sulphate dihydrate (CaSO₄·2H₂O). [Q1355]\n● Limestone (CaCO₃): Sedimentary rock; cement, building construction, chalk, crushed stone mein use hota hai.\n[Q1368]\n● Calcium carbide (CaC₂): Acetylene aur calcium cyanamide production mein. [Q1361]\n● Limewater test: CO₂ + Ca(OH)₂ → CaCO₃↓ (white ppt) + H₂O; excess CO₂ se Ca(HCO₃)₂ (soluble) banta hai. [Q1407]\n● Ammonia (NH₃):\n– Colourless, sharp suffocating odour.\n– N:H mass ratio = 14:3.\n– ~80% fertilizer ke roop mein use hota hai; refrigerant, water purification, plastics, explosives mein bhi. [Q1414]\n–\n\n⚠️Trap: NH₃ acid rain se related NAHI hai — ye nutritious, inorganic nitrogen compound hai. [Q1371]\n● Chlorine (Cl₂): Greenish-yellow, toxic, corrosive, irritating to eyes/respiratory system. [Q1340]\n● MgCl₂: Highly soluble in water; insoluble in acetone. Hydrates form karta hai (MgCl₂·nH₂O, n=1 to 12). [Q1384]\n● CaCl₂: White crystalline solid, highly soluble in water; ionic compound with very high boiling point (strong\nelectrostatic forces). [Q1365]\n3. Metals, Non-metals & Reactivity Series\n● Reactivity series (high to low): K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > H > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au. [Q1364, Q1381]\n● Metals: Electropositive nature — 1, 2, 3 valence electrons; easily lose karke positive ions banate hain. [Q1380]\n● Non-metals: Electronegative nature — electrons gain karke negative ions banate hain. [Q1380]\n● Sodium (Na): Atomic number 11; Group 1; highly reactive — oxygen aur moisture se vigorously react karta hai;\nisliye kerosene mein store karte hain. [Q1376]\n● Fluorine (F): Sabse zyada reactive halogen; atomic number 9. Halogens ki reactivity upar se neeche jaate hue kam\nhoti hai. [Q1377]\n● Displacement reaction: Zyada reactive metal kam reactive metal ke salt solution se usko displace kar sakta hai.\n– Zn + CuSO₄ → ZnSO₄ + Cu (Zn is more reactive than Cu). [Q1381]\n– Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu (Fe surface brown copper coating ban jaata hai; solution blue se pale green ho jaata"," hai). [Q1364]\n● Zn + H₂SO₄ → ZnSO₄ + H₂↑: H₂ gas colourless hai aur pop sound ke saath jalta hai. [Q1359]\n● White phosphorus: Highly reactive with oxygen; isliye water mein store karte hain. Translucent white waxy solid;\nburning se dense white irritating smoke (phosphorus oxides) nikalta hai. [Q1382]\n● Halogens: Group 17; valency = 1; reactivity, electronegativity down the group kam hoti hai; melting/boiling\npoints, atomic radius badhti hai. [Q1377]\n4. Ionic vs Covalent Compounds\n● Ionic compounds:\n– Electron transfer se bante hain; cation + anion.\n– Properties: Solid, hard, high melting & boiling points (strong electrostatic forces), soluble in water, insoluble in\npetrol, conduct electricity in aqueous/molten state.\n– Examples: NaCl, CaCl₂, MgCl₂, NaBr, KBr. [Q1365, Q1397]\n● Covalent compounds:\n– Covalent bond se bante hain.\n– Properties: Low melting & boiling points, weak conductors of heat/electricity, insoluble in water, soluble in\norganic solvents.\n– Examples: Glucose, alcohol, kerosene, octane. [Q1386, Q1387]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: High melting & boiling points covalent compound ka property NAHI hai — ye ionic ka property hai.\n[Q1386]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Low melting & boiling points ionic compound ka property NAHI hai. [Q1397]\n● Sugar solution electricity conduct nahi karta kyunki sugar molecules ions mein dissociate nahi hote. [Q1387]\n● NaCl(aq) electricity conduct karta hai kyunki Na⁺ aur Cl⁻ ions free hote hain. [Q1366]\n5. Redox, Corrosion & Rancidity\n● Oxidation: Oxygen gain ya hydrogen loss. [Q1360]\n● Reduction: Oxygen loss ya hydrogen gain. [Q1360]\n● Rusting: 4Fe + 3O₂ → 2Fe₂O₃; Fe oxidized hota hai. [Q1360]\n● Corrosion: Metal surface ka air/moisture se damage — iron rust, copper green coating, silver black.\n– Prevention: Painting, oiling, greasing, galvanising, chrome plating. [Q1390]\n● Rancidity: Fats/oils ka oxidation/hydrolysis se spoilage — unpleasant odour; antioxidants, airtight containers,\nnitrogen flush se roka jaata hai. [Q1390, Q1401]\n● Silver tarnishing: 2Ag + H₂S → Ag₂S (black) + H₂; corrosion ka example. [Q1370]\n● Corrosion ≠ Rancidity: Corrosion = metal surface damage; Rancidity = fats/oils spoilage. [Q1390]\n6. Isotopes, Isobars & Isomers\n● Isotopes: Same chemical properties, different atomic masses; same atomic number.\n– Examples: C-12, C-13, C-14; H-1, D-2, T-3; U-235, U-238. [Q1379]\n● Isobars: Same mass number, different atomic number.\n– Examples: ₁₉K⁴⁰, ₁₈Ar⁴⁰, ₂₀Ca⁴⁰; ₁₁Na²⁴, ₁₂Mg²⁴. [Q1379]"," ● Isomers: Same chemical formula, different properties/structure.\n– Examples: Ethyl alcohol & dimethyl ether (C₂H₆O); Pentane, iso-pentane, neopentane. [Q1379]\n7. States of Matter & Physical Properties\n● Force of attraction: Solid > Liquid > Gas > Plasma. [Q1391]\n● Solid: Closely packed particles; maximum intermolecular force. [Q1391]\n● Liquid: Moderate force; particles close but can move. [Q1391]\n● Gas: Very weak force; particles free to move. [Q1391]\n● Plasma: 4th state of matter; no fixed shape/volume; less dense than solids/liquids; Sir William Crookes (1879)\nidentified; Irving Langmuir (1928) described; fluorescent tube mein gas ki nature pe depend karke special colour\nglow karta hai. [Q1399]\n● Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC): Super cold atoms; Satyendra Nath Bose aur Albert Einstein ne 1924 mein predict\nkiya. [Q1399]\n● Relative density: Density of substance / Density of water; unitless; water = 1 g/cm³ at 4°C. [Q1392]\n● Liquefaction & boiling points: Stronger intermolecular forces aur higher molecular weight → higher points. Acetic\nacid > Chloroform > Ethanol > Methane. [Q1385]\n● Water molecule: H:O ratio = 2:1 (H₂O). [Q1388]\n● Mg burning: Dazzling white flame; white ash (MgO) → water mein dissolve karke Mg(OH)₂ banata hai. [Q1400]\n8. Fireworks, Flame Tests & Gas Colours\n● Fireworks colours (metal salts):\n– Green: Barium (Ba, atomic number 56). [Q1373]\n– Blue: Copper (Cu). [Q1373]\n– Orange: Calcium (Ca). [Q1373]\n– Yellow: Sodium (Na). [Q1373]\n– Red: Lithium (Li). [Q1373]\n– Golden sparks: Iron filings (magnetite, hematite) + charcoal. [Q1373]\n● Flame colours:\n– Blue flame: Complete combustion; sufficient oxygen. [Q1398]\n– Red/Orange/Green flame: Incomplete combustion. [Q1398]\n● LPG components: Propane (C₃H₈), butane (C₄H₁₀), propylene (C₃H₆), butylene (C₄H₈), isobutane (C₄H₁₀). [Q1398]\n9. Acid Rain & Environment\n● Acid rain: pH ~ 5.2 ya usse kam; SO₂ aur nitrogen oxides (NO, NO₂) se banta hai; fossil fuel combustion se emit\nhote hain.\n– SO₂ + H₂O + O₂ → H₂SO₄ (sulphuric acid).\n– NOₓ + H₂O + O₂ → HNO₃ (nitric acid). [Q1371, Q1374]\n● Acid rain se related gases: SO₂, SO₃, NO, NO₂. [Q1371, Q1374]\n● NH₃ acid rain se related NAHI hai. [Q1371]"," 10. Photography & Silver Compounds\n● Black & white photography: AgCl aur AgBr use hote hain.\n– 2AgCl → 2Ag + Cl₂ (sunlight); 2AgBr → 2Ag + Br₂.\n– Light absorb hoti hai — isliye endothermic reaction.\n– Sodium thiosulfate (Na₂S₂O₃, hypo) se fix karte hain — unchanged silver salts dissolve ho jaate hain. [Q1389]\n● AgCl: White; sunlight mein grey ho jaata hai (decomposition into Ag + Cl₂); dark bottle mein store karte hain;\nmercury poisoning ke liye antidote. [Q1357]\n● AgBr: Same behaviour as AgCl. [Q1357]\n11. Coal, Coal Tar & Fractional Distillation\n● Coal tar: Thick black liquid, unpleasant smell; different carbon compounds ka mixture.\n– Fractional distillation se dyes, explosives, paints, synthetic fibres, drugs, pesticides milta hain. [Q1363]\n● Naphthalene: Aromatic hydrocarbon; coal tar ya crude oil mein milta hai; moth repellent (moth balls); plastics,\nresins, fuels, dyes manufacturing mein. [Q1363]\n● Bitumen: Coal tar se obtained; road construction, waterproofing mein use hota hai. [Q1363]\n12. Chemical vs Physical Change\n● Chemical change: New substance forms; mostly irreversible.\n– Examples: Rusting, digestion, baking a cake, rotting fruits, decomposition of waste, butter turning rancid.\n[Q1401]\n● Physical change: No new substance; reversible.\n– Examples: CO₂ → dry ice, magnetisation of iron, heating platinum wire, boiling water, vaporizing liquid\nnitrogen. [Q1401]\n● Iodine-Starch test: Potato juice mein starch hota hai — Iodine (I) starch [(C₆H₁₀O₅) ] ke saath react karke blue-\nₙ\nblack colour banata hai. Iodine photography, pharmaceutical industry, water purifiers mein bhi use hota hai.\n[Q1350]\n● Enzyme test example: Test tube A mein starch solution + dilute iodine → blue-black colour. Test tube B mein\nstarch + saliva — salivary amylase enzyme starch ko simple sugars mein todta hai, isliye iodine sugars ke saath\ncomplex nahi banata aur blue-black colour NAHI dikhta. [Q1362]\n13. Electrolysis & Electrical Conduction\n● Brine electrolysis (Chlor-alkali process):\n– Cathode: 2H₂O + 2e⁻ → H₂↑ + 2OH⁻ (H₂ gas — pop sound).\n– Anode: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂↑ + 2e⁻.\n– Overall: 2NaCl + 2H₂O → H₂ + Cl₂ + 2NaOH.\n– Cathode = current flows out; anode = current enters. [Q1358]\n● Sodium chloride (aq): Conducts electricity — dissociates into Na⁺ + Cl⁻. [Q1366]\n● Sugar, glucose, alcohol, kerosene, octane: Do NOT conduct electricity — no free ions. [Q1366, Q1387, Q1404]"," 14. Water, Hardness & Solutions\n● Hard water: >50-60 mg/L calcium/magnesium carbonate. [Q1396]\n● Washing soda (Na₂CO₃): Temporary aur permanent dono hardness remove karta hai. [Q1396]\n● Water of crystallization: Crystals heat karne pe lost hota hai → anhydrous form.\n– Na₂CO₃·10H₂O = washing soda crystals. [Q1351]\n– CuSO₄·5H₂O (blue) → heat → anhydrous CuSO₄ (white). [Q1308]\n15. Fire Extinguishers & Safety\n● Soda-acid fire extinguisher: Sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO₃) + sulphuric acid — CO₂ gas evolved; fire ko suffocate\nkarta hai.\n–\n\n⚠️Trap: Sodium carbonate nahi — sodium bicarbonate use hota hai. [Q1351, Q1353]\n● CO₂ fire extinguishers: CO₂ gas use hoti hai. [Q1353]\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Soda-acid fire extinguisher mein NaHCO₃ use hota hai — Na₂CO₃ nahi. [Q1351]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH permanent hardness remove karne ke liye use NAHI hota. [Q1354]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Covalent compounds ka high melting/boiling point property nahi hai — ye ionic ka hai. [Q1386]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ionic compounds ka low melting/boiling point property nahi hai. [Q1397]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sugar solution electricity nahi conduct karta — ions nahi hote. [Q1387]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Corrosion aur rancidity alag-alag cheezein hain — corrosion = metal damage; rancidity = fats/oils\nspoilage. [Q1390]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NH₃ acid rain se related NAHI hai. [Q1371]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Blue flame = complete combustion; red/orange/green = incomplete combustion. [Q1398]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: POP (CaSO₄·½H₂O) gypsum se 373 K par banta hai — 473 K ya 573 K nahi. [Q1355]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgCl sunlight mein grey ho jaata hai — black nahi. [Q1357]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same group ke elements ki chemical properties similar hoti hain — atomic mass/radius/number nahi.\n[Q1394]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water molecule mein H:O = 2:1 hai — 1:1 ya 1:2 nahi. [Q1388]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mg burning se MgO banta hai; water mein dissolve karke Mg(OH)₂ banata hai — direct Mg(OH)₂ nahi.\n[Q1400]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Denatured alcohol mein methanol milaya jaata hai — safe nahi peena. [Q1395]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pb(NO₃)₂ + KI se banne wala precipitate YELLOW hota hai (PbI₂) — white nahi. [Q1356]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 10 Chemical Properties Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0398","t":"11 Solutions","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.11 — SOLUTIONS — FULL MIND MAP\n🧪\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Solutions, Suspensions & Colloids — Definitions & Differences\n2. Types of Mixtures — Homogeneous vs Heterogeneous\n3. Separation Techniques\n4. Evaporation, Boiling & Phase Changes\n5. Electrolytes & Conduction of Electricity\n6. Important Reactions & Precipitates\n7. pH, Indicators & Bases\n8. Solubility & Concentration\n9. Density & Relative Density\n10. Physical States & Key Properties\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n12. Ideal Gas Law (PV = nRT) — Vapour Phase Calculations\n13. Dalton's Law of Partial Pressures\n14. Stoichiometry — Mass-Mass Calculations\n15. Percentage Composition\n16. Mass Ratio in Molecules\n17. Mass by Mass Percentage (m/m%)\n18.\n Numerical Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Solutions, Suspensions & Colloids — Definitions & Differences\n● Solution: Homogeneous mixture of two or more substances — solute uniformly dissolved in solvent. Examples:\nsalt water, sugar water, air, carbonated beverages. [Q1415, Q1418, Q1423, Q1432]\n● True Solution: Solute particles < 10⁻⁹ m (1 nm) in diameter; homogenous; does NOT scatter light. [Q1427]\n● Colloid (Colloidal Solution): Heterogeneous mixture; particle size 1 nm to 1000 nm (10⁻⁹ to 10⁻⁶ m); particles do\nNOT settle down when left undisturbed; individual particles not visible to naked eye; Tyndall effect dikhata hai\n(colloid particles light ko scatter karte hain — is size ki wajah se, jo true solution se bade aur suspension se\nchhote hote hain). Milk ek colloidal solution hai jo Tyndall effect dikhata hai; starch solution bhi. [Q1411, Q1413,\nQ1417, Q1424, Q1431, Q1434, Q1430]\n– Types of colloids: Sol = Solid dispersed in liquid (e.g., Gold sol, Sulfur sol, Arsenious sulphide sol, paint); Gel =\nLiquid dispersed in solid (e.g., Cheese, butter, jellies); Emulsion = Liquid dispersed in liquid (e.g., Milk, face\ncream, mayonnaise); Foam = Gas dispersed in liquid (e.g., Whipped cream, soap lather, soap suds); Aerosol =\nLiquid/Solid dispersed in gas (e.g., Cloud, mist, fog). [Q1411, Q1431, Q1434]\n● Suspension: Heterogeneous mixture; solid particles dispersed but NOT dissolved; particles > 10⁻⁶ m; visible to\nnaked eye; scatter light; settle over time. [Q1418, Q1424, Q1427]\n– Example: Mud in water. [Q1427]\n● Precipitate: Chemical reaction ke dauraan solution mein bana insoluble substance. Example: AgNO₃(aq) + KCl(aq)\n→ AgCl↓ (precipitate) + KNO₃(aq). [Q1405]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Colloid cannot scatter light — ye statement galat hai. Colloid Tyndall effect dikhaate hain. [Q1417]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Colloid heterogeneous mixture hai, homogeneous nahi. [Q1417, Q1434]\n2. Types of Mixtures — Homogeneous vs Heterogeneous\n● Homogeneous: Uniform composition throughout; single phase. Examples: salt + water, sugar + water, air, alcohol"," + water. [Q1415, Q1429, Q1432]\n● Heterogeneous: Non-uniform composition; visible separate phases/particles. Examples: sand + water, oil + water,\ncolloids, suspensions. [Q1417, Q1424, Q1429, Q1432, Q1434]\n● Mixture can be both homogeneous and heterogeneous. [Q1432]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pure substance = NOT a mixture. [Q1432]\n3. Separation Techniques\n● Filtration: Separating suspended solid particles from liquid/gas using filters. Example: water from muddy water.\n[Q1426, Q1437]\n● Evaporation: Liquid → gas at surface; used to separate volatile component from non-volatile solute. Example: salt\nfrom salt water. [Q1425, Q1426]\n● Separating Funnel: Separating immiscible liquids (different densities, form separate layers). Example: petrol and\nwater. [Q1429]\n● Centrifugation (Churning): Using centrifugal force to separate components; e.g., cream from milk. [Q1426, Q1437]\n● Sublimation: Solid → gas without liquid phase. Example: salt and camphor separated by sublimation. [Q1429]\n● Chromatography: Separating dye from black ink. [Q1429]\n● Decantation: Separating liquid from solid/immiscible liquids by removing top liquid layer. [Q1437]\n● Sieving: Separating particles of different sizes. [Q1437]\n● Diffusion: Movement of substance from high concentration to low concentration. Example: smell of perfume\nreaches nose. [Q1419]\n● Condensation: Gas → liquid. Example: morning dew, foggy car windows. [Q1419, Q1425]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Filtration muddy water ke liye best hai — distillation ya crystallization basic separation ke liye overkill\nhain. [Q1437]\n4. Evaporation, Boiling & Phase Changes\n● Evaporation: Surface phenomenon; liquid → gas; occurs at ALL temperatures (not just boiling point). Factors\naffecting rate:\n– Temperature ↑ → rate ↑\n– Surface area ↑ → rate ↑\n– Wind speed ↑ → rate ↑\n– Humidity ↑ → rate ↓ [Q1420, Q1425, Q1435, Q1436]\n● Boiling: Bulk phenomenon; occurs at boiling point (100°C for water at sea level). [Q1435, Q1436]\n● Freezing: Liquid → solid. [Q1436]\n● Condensation: Gas → liquid; reverse of vaporization. [Q1419, Q1425, Q1436]\n● Sublimation: Solid → gas; no liquid intermediate. Examples: Camphor, Iodine, Dry ice (solid CO₂). [Q1422, Q1426]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Evaporation surface phenomenon hai — boiling bulk phenomenon hai. [Q1435]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same quantity of liquid ke liye evaporation sabse slowest hota hai freezing, boiling, condensation ke\ncomparison mein. [Q1436]\n● Physical state of water at 250°C: Gas (above boiling point 100°C).\n– Below 0°C → Solid (ice)\n– 0°C to 100°C → Liquid\n– Above 100°C → Gas [Q1421]"," 5. Electrolytes & Conduction of Electricity\n● Electrolyte: Substance that conducts electricity when dissolved in water or molten state; dissociates into ions.\n[Q1418]\n● Ionic compounds (NaCl, CaCl₂, CuSO₄) water mein dissociate hoke ions banate hain — isliye electricity conduct\nkarte hain. [Q1404]\n● Octane (C₈H₁₈): Covalent compound; water mein dissociate nahi hota; NO ions → bulb does NOT glow. [Q1404]\n● Examples of electrolytes: NaCl(aq), CaCl₂(aq), CuSO₄(aq). [Q1404]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Covalent liquids like octane electrolyte nahi hote — bulb nahi jalega. [Q1404]\n6. Important Reactions & Precipitates\n● AlCl₃ + NH₄OH → Al(OH)₃↓ (white ppt) + NH₄Cl. Aluminium hydroxide = white precipitate; used for heartburn,\nsour stomach, peptic ulcer pain. [Q1402]\n● Limestone (CaCO₃) + dilute HCl → CO₂↑ + CaCl₂ + H₂O. [Q1407]\n– CO₂ + Lime water (Ca(OH)₂) → CaCO₃↓ (white ppt) + H₂O. [Q1407]\n– Excess CO₂ + CaCO₃ + H₂O → Ca(HCO₃)₂ (soluble). [Q1407]\n● Pb(NO₃)₂ + 2NaI → PbI₂↓ (yellow ppt) + 2NaNO₃. Lead iodide = yellow crystalline solid; insoluble in water; denser\nthan water; used in photography, solar cells. [Q1410]\n● Zn + FeCl₃ → ZnCl₂ (colourless/white, highly soluble). Yellow colour of ferric chloride disappears. [Q1406]\n● Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂↑ (brisk effervescence). [Q1251]\n7. pH, Indicators & Bases\n● pH scale:\n– Acidic: 0 to <7\n– Neutral: 7\n– Basic (Alkaline): >7 to 14 [Q1416]\n● Alkaline solutions: NaOH, Mg(OH)₂, Ca(OH)₂, KOH — pH > 7. [Q1416]\n● Aluminium hydroxide (Al(OH)₃): Amphoteric — both acidic and basic properties; isliye alkaline nahi kehlaata.\n[Q1416]\n● Phenolphthalein: Pink in basic solution; colourless in acidic. [Q1403]\n● Turmeric: Red in base. [Q1403]\n● Red cabbage: Red in acid; green in base. [Q1403]\n● Litmus: Acid → blue litmus red; Base → red litmus blue. [Q1403]\n● Methyl orange: Red in acid; yellow in base. [Q1403]\n● Mg + H₂O → Mg(OH)₂ (basic) — phenolphthalein pink kar deta hai. [Q1403]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Al(OH)₃ amphoteric hai — alkaline nahi. [Q1416]\n8. Solubility & Concentration\n● Solubility: Amount of solute present in saturated solution at a particular temperature — ability of solute to\ndissolve in solvent. [Q1428]"," ● Saturated solution: Dissolved as much solute as it is capable of dissolving. [Q1424]\n● Unsaturated solution: Dissolved less solute than it is capable of dissolving at given T and P. [Q1424]\n● Concentrated solution: Relatively large amount of solute dissolved in given amount of solvent. [Q1423]\n● Isotonic solution: Concentration of solutes same as another solution or cell interior. [Q1423]\n● Aqueous solution (aq): Solute dissolved in water. [Q1423]\n● Brine: Aqueous solution of sodium chloride (NaCl). [Q1412]\n● Chlor-alkali process: Electrolysis of brine → 2NaCl + 2H₂O → H₂ + Cl₂ + 2NaOH (Castner-Kellner cell). [Q1408]\n– Cl₂ at anode; H₂ and NaOH at cathode. [Q1408]\n9. Density & Relative Density\n● Density (ρ): Mass per unit volume; ρ = m/V. SI unit: kg/m³; dimensional formula: [ML⁻³T⁰]. [Q1433]\n● Relative density: ρ_substance / ρ_water (reference material). Dimensional formula: [M⁰L⁰T⁰] (dimensionless).\n[Q1433]\n● Viscosity: Measure of resistive flow of fluid under gravity; internal friction of moving fluid. Example: Honey (due\nto hydrogen bonding). [Q1428]\n10. Physical States & Key Properties\n● Solids: Molecules closely bound; examples: Iron, brick, coin. [Q1421]\n● Liquids: Molecular forces weaker than solids; examples: Juice, cold drinks. [Q1421]\n● Gases: Molecular forces very weak; examples: Natural gas, O₂, CO₂. [Q1421]\n● Plasma: Liquid portion of blood; helps in blood clotting. (Biological context) [Q1421]\n● CuCl₂ solution: Blue-green colour; concentrated = dark brown; dilute = green → blue (Cl⁻ replaced by water\nmolecules). [Q1409]\n● Iodine sublimation vapours: Purple colour. [Q1422]\n● Ammonia (NH₃): Colourless, sharp suffocating odour; N:H mass ratio = 14:3; ~80% used as fertilizer; also\nrefrigerant, water purification, plastics, explosives. [Q1414]\n● Chlorine (Cl₂): Greenish-yellow, toxic, corrosive, irritating to eyes/respiratory system. [Q1340]\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Colloid cannot scatter light — ye statement galat hai. Colloid Tyndall effect dikhaate hain. [Q1417]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Colloid = heterogeneous mixture, NOT homogeneous. [Q1434]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Al(OH)₃ amphoteric hai — alkaline nahi. [Q1416]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Evaporation sirf boiling point pe nahi — sabhi temperatures pe hota hai. [Q1420]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Evaporation = surface phenomenon; Boiling = bulk phenomenon. [Q1435]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same quantity ke liye evaporation sabse slowest hai. [Q1436]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Octane (covalent) electrolyte nahi — bulb nahi jalega. [Q1404]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pure substance = NOT a mixture. [Q1432]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: True solution particles < 10⁻⁹ m; Colloid 1–1000 nm; Suspension > 10⁻⁶ m. [Q1427]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Separating funnel = immiscible liquids ke liye; miscible liquids ke liye nahi. [Q1429]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Aqueous (aq) = solution in water, kerosene nahi. [Q1423]"," 12. Ideal Gas Law (PV = nRT) — Vapour Phase Calculations\n● Ideal Gas Equation: PV = nRT. [Q1438, Q1342]\n– P = Pressure (Pa), V = Volume (m³ ya dm³), n = moles, R = 8.314 JK⁻¹mol⁻¹, T = Temperature (K). [Q1438]\n● Question trick: Flask mein zyada water daala gaya hai, lekin equilibrium pe sirf vapour phase ka hi calculate karna\nhai — liquid phase ignore karo. [Q1438]\n● Calculation:\n– n = PV/RT = (3170 Pa × 1 dm³) / (8.314 × 300 K) = 1.27 × 10⁻³ mol. [Q1438]\n● Exam tip: Agar flask ka volume diya hai aur vapour pressure diya hai, toh liquid ka volume matter nahi karta — sirf\nflask ka volume vapour ka volume hota hai. [Q1438]\n13. Dalton's Law of Partial Pressures\n● Dalton's Law: Total pressure = sum of partial pressures; partial pressure mole fraction.\n∝\n [Q1439]\n● Mole fraction = moles of component / total moles. [Q1439]\n● Question: Equal masses of ethane (C₂H₆, M=30) and hydrogen (H₂, M=2) mixed. H₂ ka pressure fraction nikaalo.\n● Trick:\n– Let mass of each = x g.\n– Moles of ethane = x/30; moles of H₂ = x/2.\n– Mole fraction of H₂ = (x/2) / (x/2 + x/30) = (1/2) / (1/2 + 1/30) = 15/16. [Q1439]\n● Shortcut: Equal mass mix karne pe, lighter gas (H₂) ka mole fraction hamesha zyada hota hai. [Q1439]\n14. Stoichiometry — Mass-Mass Calculations\n● Reaction: BaCl₂ + H₂SO₄ → BaSO₄↓ + 2HCl. [Q1440]\n● Molar masses:\n– BaCl₂ = 137 + (35.5 × 2) = 208 g/mol.\n– BaSO₄ = 137 + 32 + (16 × 4) = 233 g/mol. [Q1440]\n● Logic: 208 g BaCl₂ → 233 g BaSO₄.\n– 1 g BaCl₂ → 233/208 g BaSO₄.\n– 2.08 g BaCl₂ → (233/208) × 2.08 = 2.33 g BaSO₄. [Q1440]\n● Exam trick: 2.08 = 208/100, toh direct 233/100 = 2.33 aa jaata hai — calculation fast karo. [Q1440]\n15. Percentage Composition\n● Formula: % of element = (atomic mass of element / molecular mass of compound) × 100. [Q1441]\n● CO₂ ka calculation:\n– C = 12, O = 16 × 2 = 32.\n– Total = 12 + 32 = 44.\n– % C = (12/44) × 100 = 27.27% ≈ 27.3%. [Q1441]\n● Shortcut: 12/44 = 3/11 ≈ 0.2727 → 27.27%. [Q1441]"," 16. Mass Ratio in Molecules\n● Water molecule (H₂O):\n– 2 H atoms = 2 × 1 = 2 g.\n– 1 O atom = 16 g.\n– Mass ratio H : O = 2 : 16 = 1 : 8. [Q1442]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Atom ratio H:O = 2:1 hai, lekin mass ratio = 1:8 hai — dono alag hain. [Q1442, Q1388]\n17. Mass by Mass Percentage (m/m%)\n● Formula: m/m% = (mass of solute / mass of solution) × 100. [Q1443]\n● Question: 250 g of 5% glucose solution — kitna glucose chahiye?\n● Calculation: Mass of glucose = (250 × 5) / 100 = 12.5 g. [Q1443]\n● Trick: 5% = 1/20, toh 250/20 = 12.5 directly. [Q1443]\n18.\n Numerical Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vapour pressure calculation mein liquid ka volume ignore karo — sirf container ka volume vapour ka\nvolume hota hai. [Q1438]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Equal mass mix karne pe mole fraction ≠ mass fraction — mole fraction mein lighter gas zyada dominate\nkarti hai. [Q1439]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: BaCl₂ (208) aur BaSO₄ (233) ka molar mass yaad rakho — 208 → 233 direct ratio se calculation fast hoti\nhai. [Q1440]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: % composition mein molecular mass se divide karna hai, atomic mass se nahi. [Q1441]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: H₂O mein atom ratio (2:1) aur mass ratio (1:8) alag hain — question kya puch raha hai dhyan se padho.\n[Q1442]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: m/m% mein solution ka mass denominator mein aata hai, sirf solvent ka nahi. [Q1443]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 11 Solutions Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0399","t":"12 Chemistry in Everyday Life","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.12 — CHEMISTRY IN EVERYDAY LIFE — FULL MIND MAP\n🏠\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Baking Soda, Baking Powder & Washing Soda\n2. Bleaching Powder & Important Salts\n3. Plaster of Paris, Gypsum & Cement\n4. Caustic Soda, Alum & Other Compounds\n5. Acids & Their Natural Sources\n6. pH, Antacids & Toothpaste\n7. Polymers & Plastics in Daily Life\n8. Gases & Their Everyday Uses\n9. Environmental Chemistry (Ozone, CFC, Biogas)\n10. Metals, Coating & Corrosion Prevention\n11. Physical Changes: Evaporation, Sublimation, Condensation\n12. Separation Techniques\n13. Alcohols, Esters & Food Chemistry\n14. Photography & Silver Compounds\n15. Graphite & Carbon Allotropes\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Baking Soda, Baking Powder & Washing Soda\n● Baking Soda (NaHCO₃ — Sodium Bicarbonate):\n– Preparation: Solvay process — NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ + NH₃ → NaHCO₃ + NH₄Cl. [Q1458, Q1474, Q1506]\n– Heating: 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + CO₂↑ + H₂O. [Q1462, Q1472]\n– Uses: Antacid (acidity relief), soda-acid fire extinguisher, baking, mouth freshening, deodorant, foot soak, hair\ncare, bee sting relief (neutralizes formic acid), milk preservation (prevents acidisation), pesticide. [Q1448,\nQ1455, Q1461, Q1464, Q1471, Q1473, Q1494, Q1502]\n– NOT used for: Bleaching action. [Q1473]\n● Baking Powder: Mixture of baking soda + mild edible acid (tartaric acid) + buffer (cornstarch). Dry chemical\nleavening agent. [Q1448, Q1459, Q1506]\n● Washing Soda (Na₂CO₃·10H₂O — Sodium Carbonate Decahydrate):\n– Preparation: Recrystallisation of Na₂CO₃ — Na₂CO₃ + 10H₂O → Na₂CO₃·10H₂O. [Q1450, Q1477]\n– Raw materials: NaCl, NH₃, CO₂ (Solvay process). [Q1457]\n– Properties: White crystalline, basic salt, alkaline taste. [Q1469, Q1476]\n– Uses: Glass, soap, paper industries; borax manufacture; removing permanent hardness of water; domestic\ncleansing agent. [Q1450, Q1451, Q1467, Q1489]\n– NOT used for: Making cake (baking soda used). [Q1464]\n● Chemical behaviour: Washing soda = basic salt (Q1469) / amphoteric nature bhi bataya gaya hai kuch\nexplanations mein (Q1476). [Q1469, Q1476]\n2. Bleaching Powder & Important Salts\n● Bleaching Powder {CaOCl₂ / Ca(OCl)₂ — Calcium Hypochlorite}:\n– Preparation: Dry chlorine gas passed over dry slaked lime Ca(OH)₂. [Q1453, Q1460, Q1468]"," – Properties: Pale yellowish powder, strong chlorine smell, soluble in water (but never clear due to impurities),\nstrong oxidizing agent. [Q1460]\n– Uses: Bleaching cotton/linen/wood pulp, bleaching dirty clothes, oxidizing agent in industries, disinfectant,\nwater decontamination. [Q1446, Q1453, Q1468]\n– NOT used for: Baking cakes. [Q1446]\n● Blue Vitriol (CuSO₄): Battery electrolytes. [Q1467]\n● Green Vitriol (FeSO₄): Medicine for iron deficiency. [Q1467]\n● Alum (Fitkari): Hydrated double salt — KAl(SO₄)₂·12H₂O (Potash alum); water purification mein use hota hai.\n[Q1383, Q1482]\n● Ammonium Chloride (NH₄Cl): Nitrogen supply in fertilizers, electrolyte in dry cells. [Q1448]\n● Whitewashing: Slaked lime [Ca(OH)₂] ki solution se walls whitewash karne ke 2-3 din baad, CO₂ (air se) reaction\nkarke Calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) banata hai — yahi walls ko shiny finish deta hai. Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O.\n[Q1475]\n3. Plaster of Paris, Gypsum & Cement\n● Plaster of Paris (POP): CaSO₄·½H₂O (Calcium Sulphate Hemihydrate).\n– Preparation: Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) ko 393 K par heat karke. [Q1352, Q1355, Q1369, Q1454]\n– Properties: White powder, water milane pe hard mass banata hai. [Q1454]\n– Uses: Setting fractured bones, dentistry, toys, decorative materials, cheap ornaments, cosmetics, blackboard\nchalk, fire-proofing material, sealing air-gaps in labs. [Q1445, Q1454]\n– NOT used for: Glass/soap/paper manufacture, domestic cleaning, baking. [Q1454]\n● Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O): Soft dehydrated mineral; wallboard/ceiling manufacture; fluxing agent, fertilizer, paper\nfiller, cement retarder. [Q1355, Q1465]\n● Cement: Main compounds — Tricalcium silicate (3CaO·SiO₂), Dicalcium silicate, Tricalcium aluminate,\nTetracalcium alumino ferrite. CaO central component. [Q1470]\n4. Caustic Soda, Alum & Other Compounds\n● Caustic Soda (NaOH — Sodium Hydroxide):\n– Uses: Cleansing agent, washing soda manufacture, drain pipe cleaner, soap/detergent, paper & pulp industry,\nfabric industry. [Q1447]\n– NOT used in: Ammonia manufacture. [Q1447]\n● Sodium Chloride (NaCl): Food preservative, healthcare (dehydration prevention). [Q1448]\n● Milk of Magnesia [Mg(OH)₂]: Heartburn, upset stomach, indigestion. [Q1489]\n● Sodium Fluoride (NaF): Toothpaste. [Q1489]\n● Titanium Dioxide (TiO₂): White pigment in paint. [Q1489]\n● Sodium Nitrate (NaNO₃): Fertilizer. [Q1489]\n5. Acids & Their Natural Sources\n● Formic Acid (Methanoic Acid, CH₂O₂): Nettle leaves, ants, bee sting. [Q1452, Q1486]\n● Citric Acid: Lemons, oranges, citrus fruits. [Q1452, Q1486]\n● Tartaric Acid: Tamarind, apples, cherries, papaya, peach, pear, pineapple, strawberry, mango. [Q1452, Q1486]"," ● Oxalic Acid (C₂H₂O₄): Tomatoes. [Q1452]\n● Lactic Acid: Sour milk, curd; produced during carbohydrate breakdown in body. [Q1486]\n● Butyric Acid: Rancid butter ka foul smell; dairy products. [Q1487]\n● Acetic Acid (Ethanoic Acid, CH₃COOH): Vinegar; pickled vegetables, sauces, raw material for spices. [Q1505]\n● Stearic Acid: Animal & plant fats; soap preparation. [Q1487]\n● Caproic Acid: Cheese-like smell. [Q1487]\n● Palmitic Acid: Palm oil; cosmetics. [Q1487]\n6. pH, Antacids & Toothpaste\n● Toothpaste: Basic (pH > 7) — mouth mein bacteria se bane acid ko neutralize karta hai; pH 5.5 se neeche tooth\ndecay hota hai. [Q1463]\n● Antacids: Excess stomach acid neutralize karte hain.\n– Examples: Al(OH)₃, MgCO₃, Mg₂O₈Si₃, Mg(OH)₂, CaCO₃, NaHCO₃. [Q1353, Q1378, Q1466]\n– NaOH strong base hai — antacid ke roop mein use nahi hota. [Q1466]\n7. Polymers & Plastics in Daily Life\n● PVC (Polyvinyl Chloride): Water pipes, raincoats, handbags. [Q1483]\n● Bakelite: Phenol + formaldehyde thermosetting polymer; electric switches, sockets, wire insulation, clocks,\nbuttons, washing machines, toys, kitchenware. [Q1490, Q1492]\n● Teflon (PTFE — Polytetrafluoroethylene): Non-stick coating on kitchen utensils. [Q1492]\n● PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate): Bottles, utensils. [Q1488]\n● Nylon: Backpacks, flak jackets, athletic shoes, umbrellas, swimsuits, ropes. [Q1488]\n● Acrylic: Sweaters, fleece, socks, sportswear. [Q1488]\n● Polystyrene: Food packaging, CD/DVD cases, building construction. [Q1483]\n● Polyethylene: Plastic bags, bottles, films, containers, geomembranes. [Q1490, Q1492]\n● Glyptal: Paints, metal coating, lacquers. [Q1483]\n8. Gases & Their Everyday Uses\n● Helium (He): 2nd lightest element (after H); colorless, odorless, tasteless; liquid at −268.9°C; balloons (light + non-\nflammable); medicine, arc welding, refrigeration, aircraft gas, nuclear reactor coolant, cryogenic research.\n[Q1481]\n● Nitrogen (N₂): Food preservation — displaces oxygen; atmosphere ka ~78%; discovered by Daniel Rutherford\n(1772). [Q1501]\n● LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas): Main component Butane (C₄H₁₀); also Propane (C₃H₈). Extracted from crude oil &\nnatural gas. [Q1498]\n● Biogas: 50–75% Methane (CH₄), 25–50% CO₂, 2–8% N₂; produced from organic material in anaerobic\nenvironment. [Q1480]\n● CO₂: Bread/cake rise karata hai (baking soda se release); fire extinguisher. [Q1502]\n● Electric bulbs: Filled with Nitrogen + Argon — tungsten filament oxidation rokne ke liye; bulb life badhata hai.\n[Q1493]\n● Carbon Monoxide (CO): Odourless, colorless; incomplete combustion se; oxygen displace karke poisoning karta"," hai. [Q1493]\n9. Environmental Chemistry (Ozone, CFC, Biogas)\n● Ozone (O₃): 3 oxygen atoms; stratosphere mein; highly reactive.\n– CFC (Chlorofluorocarbon) = ozone depletion ka main reason; man-made; used in refrigerants, aerosol sprays,\nfoams, solvents. [Q1478, Q1479]\n– First ozone hole: 1970, Antarctica. [Q1478]\n– Montreal Protocol (1987): Global agreement to protect ozone layer. [Q1478]\n– Measurement unit: Dobson. [Q1478]\n● Greenhouse gases: CO₂, CH₄, N₂O. [Q1480]\n10. Metals, Coating & Corrosion Prevention\n● Food cans: Tin se coated hain (NOT zinc) — kyunki zinc tin se zyada reactive hai; tin water/oxygen se unaffected\nrehta hai, sirf strong acids se react karta hai. [Q1484]\n● Galvanization: Iron/steel pe zinc ki thin layer lagana — corrosion prevention. [Q1500]\n● Anodizing: Protective oxide layer on metal (usually aluminum). [Q1500]\n● Electroplating: Coating conductive surface with metal using electricity. [Q1500]\n11. Physical Changes: Evaporation, Sublimation, Condensation\n● Evaporation: Liquid → Gas; cooling effect.\n– Examples: Earthen pot mein water cool hona, acetone palm pe dalne se thandak, kapde sukhna, garam chai\nthandi hona. [Q1495, Q1496]\n● Sublimation: Solid → Gas (no liquid).\n– Examples: Dry ice (solid CO₂), Iodine, Camphor, Naphthalene. [Q1496]\n● Condensation: Gas → Liquid.\n– Examples: Morning dew, droplets on can/bottle, fog. [Q1496]\n● Fusion: Two atoms combine to form heavier atom (e.g., 2H → He). [Q1496]\n● Water: Freezing point 0°C (solid + liquid coexist); boiling point 100°C; max density at 4°C; triple point 273.16 K\n(0.01°C); absolute zero 0 K (−273.15°C). [Q1497]\n12. Separation Techniques\n● Separating funnel: Immiscible liquids jaise oil & water ko alag karne ke liye. [Q1429, Q1499]\n● Evaporation: Salt & water separate karne ke liye. [Q1499]\n● Sedimentation: Heavier component settles when water added. [Q1499]\n● Decantation: Water (with dust) removed from top. [Q1499]\n13. Alcohols, Esters & Food Chemistry"," ● Ethanol (C₂H₅OH):\n– Uses: Cough syrups, alcoholic drinks, paint manufacturing, hand sanitizers, medical wipes\n(antibacterial/antifungal), motor fuel (gasohol), tincture iodine, tonics. [Q1485, Q1503]\n– Denatured alcohol: Methanol, benzene, pyridine, castor oil, gasoline, acetone milake — unsuitable for\ndrinking; industrial solvent/fuel. [Q1395, Q1504]\n● Methanol (CH₃OH): Wood alcohol; colorless, sweet pungent odor; alternative fuel; antidote for methanol\npoisoning = ethanol. [Q1491, Q1503]\n● Acetic Acid (CH₃COOH) = Ethanoic acid: Vinegar; colorless, hygroscopic, pungent smell, sour taste; pickled\nvegetables, sauces. [Q1505]\n● Esters: Fruit aroma; formed by esterification (carboxylic acid + alcohol + conc. H₂SO₄).\n– Example: Ethyl butyrate = pineapple smell. [Q1491]\n● Rancidity: Fats/oils ka oxidation/hydrolysis; unpleasant smell; antioxidants/airtight containers/N₂ flush se roka\njaata hai. [Q1390, Q1487]\n● Brahma Kamal (Himalayan flower): Antiseptic properties — fevers, bone ache, intestinal ailments, cough, cold.\n[Q1449]\n14. Photography & Silver Compounds\n● Black & white photography: Silver chloride (AgCl) + Silver bromide (AgBr) donon use hote hain.\n– AgCl: Disinfectant, antiseptic, mercury poisoning treatment. [Q1444]\n– AgBr: Emulsion component for photographic image development. [Q1444]\n– Silver oxide (Ag₂O): Mild oxidizing agent — aldehydes → carboxylic acids. [Q1444]\n15. Graphite & Carbon Allotropes\n● Graphite: Giant covalent structure; each carbon bonded to 3 others in hexagonal layers; good conductor of\nelectricity.\n– Uses: Pencils, lubricants, crucibles, foundry facings, polishes, arc lamps, batteries, electric motor brushes,\nnuclear reactor cores. [Q1456]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Graphite bad conductor nahi hai — ye statement galat hai. [Q1456]\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda formula NaHCO₃ hai — CaSO₄·½H₂O POP ka formula hai. [Q1455]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: POP ka use toys & decoration ke liye hai — glass/soap/paper ya baking ke liye nahi. [Q1454]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bleaching powder ka use baking cakes ke liye nahi hai. [Q1446]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Caustic soda (NaOH) ka use ammonia manufacture mein nahi hota. [Q1447]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda ka use bleaching action ke liye nahi hota. [Q1473]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Washing soda = basic salt (Q1469) — amphoteric/acidic/neutral nahi; par kuch explanations mein\namphoteric mention hai (Q1476). [Q1469, Q1476]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Graphite good conductor hai — bad conductor nahi. [Q1456]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Denatured alcohol = unsuitable for drinking; peene ke liye nahi banaaya jaata. [Q1504]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Food cans tin se coated hain — zinc se nahi (kyunki Zn zyada reactive hai). [Q1484]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: LPG main component = Butane — methane/propane/ethane nahi. [Q1498]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water 0°C pe solid + liquid donon state mein exist kar sakta hai. [Q1497]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nitrogen food preservation ke liye use hoti hai — oxygen/hydrogen/chlorine nahi. [Q1501]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: CO₂ bread/cake rise karata hai — H₂/CO/O₂ nahi. [Q1502]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking powder = Baking soda + Tartaric acid — calcium carbonate nahi. [Q1506]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ethanol = cough syrups + alcoholic drinks + paints sab mein use hota hai — \"All of the above\". [Q1485]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vinegar = Acetic acid — ethanoic acid ka hi dusra naam hai, par question mein specifically \"acetic acid\"\ncorrect tha. [Q1505]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Whitewashed walls ka shiny finish 2-3 din baad Calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) banne se aata hai — CO₂ air\nse reaction karta hai slaked lime ke saath. [Q1475]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 12 Chemistry in Everyday Life Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0400","t":"13 Discoveries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.13 — DISCOVERIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🔬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Atomic Theory & Matter\n2. Laws of Chemical Combination\n3. Periodic Table Development\n4. Gas Discoveries\n5. Radioactivity & Nuclear Science\n6. Mole Concept & Avogadro\n7. Fifth State of Matter (BEC)\n8. Brownian Motion\n9. Catalyst & Platinum\n10. Element Symbols & Notation\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Atomic Theory & Matter\n● John Dalton (1808): British chemist ne atomic theory di — \"All matter is composed of small particles called\natoms.\" [Q1507, Q1508, Q1518]\n– Matter ki fundamental theory — element, compound ya mixture sab atoms se bante hain. [Q1518]\n● Democritus: Greek philosopher; \"Atom\" shabd gadhha — physically indivisible particles. [Q1513, Q1522]\n● Ernest Rutherford: Nuclear structure of atom; alpha & beta rays discovered; radioactive decay laws. [Q1508,\nQ1520]\n– Nucleus model: Atom ka centre = nucleus; protons (positive) occupy minimum space; electrons (negative)\nrevolve around nucleus. [Q1520]\n– Limitation: Atom ki stability explain nahi kar paaya; electron arrangement undefined thi. [Q1520]\n● J.J. Thomson: Electron discovered. [Q1515]\n● Niels Bohr: Electron shells/orbits around nucleus. [Q1520]\n2. Laws of Chemical Combination\n● Antoine Lavoisier: \"Father of Modern Chemistry\" — Law of Conservation of Mass (mass create/destroy nahi\nhota). [Q1507, Q1508, Q1513, Q1523]\n– Chemical sciences ki foundation rakhi — do important laws of chemical combination diye. [Q1523]\n● Joseph Proust: Law of Definite Proportions / Constant Composition — fixed ratio by mass of constituent elements\nin a compound. [Q1508, Q1513, Q1521]\n● Law of Conservation of Mass: Mass is neither created nor destroyed in chemical reactions. [Q1508]\n3. Periodic Table Development\n● Johann Wolfgang Döbereiner (1817): German chemist; elements ko triads mein group kiya.\n– Middle element ka atomic mass = average of other two.\n– First observations on platinum as catalyst (1823) — H₂ + air mixture ignite kar sakta hai room temp pe. [Q1509,"," Q1516, Q1517]\n● John Newlands (1863): Law of Octaves — every eighth element has similar properties when arranged by\nincreasing atomic mass. 56 elements ko 11 groups mein classify kiya. [Q1509, Q1525]\n● Dmitri Mendeleev (1869): Periodic classification — elements arranged by increasing atomic weight. [Q1509, Q1511]\n● Henry Moseley (1913): Wavelength aur atomic number ke beech systematic relation diya; modern periodic table\nbasis. [Q1509, Q1522]\n● Al-Razi: Early classification contributions. [Q1522]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Democritus ne periodic table mein contribution nahi diya — sirf \"atom\" shabd gadhha. [Q1522]\n4. Gas Discoveries\n● Daniel Rutherford (1772): Scottish physician; Nitrogen (N) discovered — atmosphere ka 78%. [Q1510, Q1501]\n– N: p-block, Group 15, Atomic number 7. [Q1510]\n● Henry Cavendish (1766): Hydrogen (H) discovered. [Q1511]\n● Joseph Priestley: Oxygen (O) discovered. [Q1510]\n● Carl Wilhelm Scheele (1772): Oxygen discovered (Swedish chemist); Chlorine (Cl) bhi discovered. [Q1510, Q1511]\n● Frankland & Lockyer: Helium (He) discovered. [Q1510]\n● Jules Janssen (1868): Helium ka first evidence — French astronomer. [Q1511]\n5. Radioactivity & Nuclear Science\n● Marie Curie: Polonium & Radium discovered.\n– Nobel Prize in Physics (1903) + Nobel Prize in Chemistry (1911). [Q1512]\n● Hideki Yukawa: Nuclear forces theory — forces acting between 2 or more nucleons. [Q1515]\n● S.N. Bose: Bose-Einstein Condensate develop kiya. [Q1515]\n● J.C. Bose: Crescograph invented. [Q1515]\n6. Mole Concept & Avogadro\n● Wilhelm Ostwald (~1896): \"Mole (mol)\" shabd introduce kiya — SI unit of amount of substance. [Q1519, Q1521]\n– 1 mole = 6.022 × 10²³ elementary entities = Avogadro number (N₀). [Q1519]\n● Amedeo Avogadro: Avogadro's Law (equal volumes → equal molecules at same T & P) + Avogadro's constant.\n[Q1512, Q1521]\n– Italian mathematical physicist. [Q1512]\n7. Fifth State of Matter (BEC)\n● Satyendra Nath Bose: Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC) — 5th state of matter.\n– Albert Einstein ke saath calculations ki; super cold atoms. [Q1524, Q1399]\n● C.V. Raman: Raman Effect. [Q1524]\n● Homi Bhabha: Father of Indian Nuclear Program. [Q1524]\n● Vikram Sarabhai: Father of ISRO. [Q1524]"," 8. Brownian Motion\n● Robert Brown: Brownian Motion discovered — random motion of particles due to collisions of gaseous\nmolecules.\n– Examples: Pollen grains on still water, pollutant diffusion in air, calcium diffusion through bones, movement of\nholes in semiconductors. [Q1526]\n9. Catalyst & Platinum\n● Döbereiner (1823): Platinum ka catalytic property first observe ki — Pt sponge H₂ + air mixture ko room temp pe\nignite kar sakta hai. [Q1516, Q1517]\n● Catalyst definition: Substance jo reaction ki rate badhata hai bina khud permanently change hue. [Q1517]\n10. Element Symbols & Notation\n● Jöns Jacob Berzelius: Element symbols — one or two letters from element's name.\n– Cerium (Ce), Selenium (Se) discovered; Silicon (Si) & Thorium (Th) isolation technique. [Q1514]\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: John Milton = English poet; scientist nahi — matter ki theory nahi di. [Q1507]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gregor Mendel = Heredity (pea plant experiments); matter ki theory nahi. [Q1507]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lavoisier = \"Father of Modern Chemistry\" + Conservation of Mass; atomic theory nahi. [Q1507, Q1518]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Proust = Definite Proportions; atomic theory nahi. [Q1513]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Democritus = \"Atom\" shabd; periodic table contribution nahi. [Q1522]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Oxygen discoverer = Joseph Priestley ya Carl Wilhelm Scheele — dono alag-alag independently. [Q1510,\nQ1511]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Newlands = Law of Octaves; Döbereiner = Triads — dono confuse mat karo. [Q1509, Q1525]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Moseley = atomic number basis periodic table; Mendeleev = atomic weight basis. [Q1509]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ostwald = \"Mole\" shabd; Avogadro = Law & Constant. [Q1519, Q1521]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rutherford = nucleus model; Bohr = electron orbits. [Q1520]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 13 Discoveries Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0401","t":"14 Common Names","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.14 — COMMON NAMES & FORMULAS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Sodas: Caustic, Baking & Washing\n2. Calcium Compounds Family\n3. Vitriols — Colour-based Names\n4. Gemstones & Their Composition\n5. Common Names of Metals & Gases\n6. IUPAC Names & Organic Compounds\n7. Important Chemical Formulas\n8. Latin Names of Elements\n9. Food Additives & Preservatives\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Sodas: Caustic, Baking & Washing\n● Caustic Soda: NaOH (Sodium Hydroxide).\n– Uses: Cleansing agent, washing soda manufacture, drain cleaner, soap/detergent, paper & pulp, fabric\nindustry, aluminium extraction (bauxite purification). [Q1527, Q1541]\n● Baking Soda: NaHCO₃ (Sodium Bicarbonate / Sodium Hydrogen Carbonate).\n– Preparation: NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ + NH₃ → NaHCO₃ + NH₄Cl.\n– Uses: Antacid, fire extinguisher, baking cakes/bread, bee sting relief, milk preservation. [Q1527, Q1535, Q1536,\nQ1554]\n● Washing Soda: Na₂CO₃·10H₂O (Sodium Carbonate Decahydrate).\n– Uses: Glass, soap, paper industries; removing permanent hardness; stain removal; textiles; petroleum refining.\n[Q1527, Q1554]\n● Baking Powder: Mixture of NaHCO₃ + Tartaric Acid + cornstarch buffer. [Q1535, Q1554]\n2. Calcium Compounds Family\n● Marble / Limestone / Chalk: CaCO₃ (Calcium Carbonate).\n– Formation: Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O. [Q1528, Q1551, Q1554]\n● Quicklime: CaO (Calcium Oxide).\n– Preparation: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ (heating limestone).\n– Reacts vigorously with water → Slaked lime + heat. [Q1547, Q1551, Q1554]\n● Slaked Lime: Ca(OH)₂ (Calcium Hydroxide).\n– Other names: Hydrated lime, Lime water, Pickling lime.\n– Uses: Mortar, plaster, cement, water treatment, sewage treatment, paper production. [Q1552, Q1554]\n● Gypsum: CaSO₄·2H₂O (Calcium Sulphate Dihydrate).\n– Uses: Wallboard, ceiling, cement retarder, fertilizer, paper filler. [Q1532, Q1554]\n● Plaster of Paris: CaSO₄·½H₂O (Calcium Sulphate Hemihydrate).\n– Preparation: Gypsum ko 373 K par heat karke. [Q1554]\n● Calcium Phosphate: Ca₃(PO₄)₂ (Tricalcium Phosphate)."," – Preparation: 3Ca(OH)₂ + 2H₃PO₄ → Ca₃(PO₄)₂ + 6H₂O.\n– Insoluble in ethanol/acetic acid; soluble in dilute HNO₃/HCl. [Q1559]\n● Calcium Carbide: CaC₂ — acetylene production. [Q1547]\n● Calcium Bicarbonate: Ca(HCO₃)₂ — food additive, anti-caking agent. [Q1528]\n● Calcium Chloride: CaCl₂ — drying agent, highly soluble. [Q1552]\n● Calcium Oxide as Drying Agent: Ammonia gas dry karne ke liye use hota hai. [Q1547]\n3. Vitriols — Colour-based Names\n● Blue Vitriol: CuSO₄·5H₂O (Hydrated Copper Sulphate) — fungicide, battery electrolytes. [Q1530, Q1532]\n● Green Vitriol: FeSO₄·7H₂O (Ferrous Sulphate / Iron(II) Sulphate) — iron deficiency medicine. [Q1530, Q1549]\n● White Vitriol: ZnSO₄·7H₂O (Zinc Sulphate Heptahydrate). [Q1530, Q1532, Q1533]\n● Red Vitriol: CoSO₄ (Cobalt Sulphate). [Q1530]\n● Vitriol of Mars: Fe₂(SO₄)₃ (Ferric Sulphate). [Q1530]\n● Spirit of Vitriol: H₂SO₄ (Sulphuric Acid) — also called Oil of Vitriol / Mattling acid. [Q1530, Q1542]\n● Oil of Vitriol: Same as Sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄). [Q1542]\n4. Gemstones & Their Composition\n● Ruby: Al₂O₃ (Aluminium Oxide) — pink to blood-red. [Q1531]\n● Diamond: C (Carbon). [Q1531]\n● Topaz: Al₂SiO₄(F,OH)₂. [Q1531]\n● Quartz: SiO₂. [Q1531]\n● Emerald: Be₃Al₂(SiO₃)₆. [Q1531]\n● Opal: SiO₂·nH₂O. [Q1531]\n5. Common Names of Metals & Gases\n● Mercury (Hg): Common name = Quicksilver; atomic number 80; d-block; Group 12. [Q1533, Q1555]\n– Uses: Thermometers, barometers, manometers, fluorescent lighting, switches.\n● Laughing Gas: N₂O (Nitrous Oxide). [Q1534]\n● Dry Ice: Solid CO₂ — sublimes directly to gas without melting. [Q1558]\n● Rock Salt: Mineral name = Halite; mainly NaCl. [Q1529]\n● Rust: Fe₂O₃·xH₂O (Hydrated Iron(III) Oxide). [Q1546]\n– Reaction: Iron + O₂ + Water → Iron Oxide (Rust).\n6. IUPAC Names & Organic Compounds\n● Propane: CH₃CH₂CH₃ (C₃H₈) — 3 carbon alkane. [Q1538]\n● Propanone: CH₃COCH₃ (Acetone / Dimethyl ketone) — ketone group (-CO-) with 3 carbons. [Q1539]\n● Ethanoic Acid = Acetic Acid (CH₃COOH) — carboxylic acid group. [Q1542]"," – Uses: Photographic film, wood glue, synthetic fibres, pickled vegetables, vinegar.\n● Ethane (C₂H₆): Total 7 covalent bonds (1 C-C + 6 C-H). [Q1540]\n● Alkanes: C H₂ ₊₂ (single bonds) — CH₄, C₂H₆, C₄H₁₀.\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q1538]\n● Alkenes: C H₂ (at least one double bond) — more reactive than alkanes.\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q1538]\n● Alkynes: C H₂ ₋₂ (triple bond).\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q1538]\n● Covalent Bond Types:\n– Single: H₂, Cl₂\n– Double: O₂, CO₂\n– Triple: N₂. [Q1540]\n● IUPAC (International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry): World authority on chemical nomenclature aur\nterminology — elements, symbols, units, naye elements ke naam sabki approval karta hai. 1919 mein establish\nhua tha; headquarters Paris, France mein hai; International Science Council (ISC) ka member hai. [Q1537]\n7. Important Chemical Formulas\n● Caustic Potash: KOH (Potassium Hydroxide) — food thickener, stabilizer, potassium soaps. [Q1541]\n● Milk of Magnesia: Mg(OH)₂ (Magnesium Hydroxide) — antacid, white solid, low water solubility. [Q1543]\n● Ammonium Hydroxide: NH₄OH (Ammonia water) — mildly acidic solution. [Q1541, Q1543]\n● Aluminium Sulphate: Al₂(SO₄)₃ — coagulating agent in water purification, paper manufacturing. [Q1545]\n● Lithium Nitride: Li₃N — only stable alkali metal nitride; Li (+1), N (-3). [Q1548]\n● Sodium Sulphate: Na₂SO₄. [Q1553]\n● Bleaching Powder: CaOCl₂ (Calcium Hypochlorite) — oxidising agent, water disinfectant. [Q1554]\n● Ammonium Phosphate: (NH₄)₃PO₄ — fertilizer ingredient. [Q1556]\n● Lactose (Milk Sugar): C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁ — disaccharide of β-D-galactose + β-D-glucose. [Q1557]\n– Glucose/Galactose/Fructose = C₆H₁₂O₆ (monosaccharides). [Q1557]\n● Monosodium Glutamate (MSG): \"Sugar salt\" — flavour enhancer in Chinese dishes. [Q1550]\n8. Latin Names of Elements\n● Sodium (Na): Natrium. [Q1544, Q1560]\n● Silver (Ag): Argentum. [Q1560]\n● Potassium (K): Kalium. [Q1544]\n● Sulphur (S): Sulfurium. [Q1544]\n● Nitrogen (N): Nitrum. [Q1544]\n● Other Latin-derived symbols: Copper (Cu), Gold (Au), Lead (Pb), Iron (Fe), Tin (Sn), Mercury (Hg). [Q1560]\n9. Food Additives & Preservatives\n● Monosodium Glutamate (MSG): Flavour enhancer; restaurant foods, canned vegetables, soups. [Q1550]\n● Sodium Benzoate: Food preservative. [Q1550]\n● Calcium Carbonate: Chalk/limestone — NOT sugar salt. [Q1550]\n● Calcium Hypochlorite: Bleaching agent & disinfectant — NOT sugar salt. [Q1550]"," 10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Caustic soda = NaOH; Caustic potash = KOH — dono alag hain. [Q1527, Q1541]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda = NaHCO₃; Baking powder = NaHCO₃ + Tartaric acid — dono alag hain. [Q1535, Q1554]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ethanoic acid = Acetic acid — same compound, do naam. [Q1542]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Propane (CH₃CH₂CH₃) aur Propanone (CH₃COCH₃) alag hain — ketone group pehchano. [Q1538, Q1539]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ethane (C₂H₆) mein total 7 covalent bonds hain — 1 C-C + 6 C-H. [Q1540]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Quicklime = CaO; Slaked lime = Ca(OH)₂ — dono alag hain. [Q1551, Q1552]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Quicksilver = Mercury (Hg); Silver = Argentum (Ag) — dono alag hain. [Q1533, Q1555]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Dry ice = Solid CO₂ — ye ice nahi hai, sublimation se gas ban jaata hai. [Q1558]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rock salt ka mineral name Halite hai — Limonite/Hematite/Siderite nahi. [Q1529]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ruby = Al₂O₃ (Aluminium oxide) — Sodium chloride/Carbon/Potassium nahi. [Q1531]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lactose = C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁ — Glucose/Galactose/Fructose sab C₆H₁₂O₆ hain. [Q1557]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rust = Fe₂O₃·xH₂O — FeO ya Fe₂O nahi. [Q1546]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Natrium = Sodium aur Argentum = Silver — dono statements true hain. [Q1560]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Element names/symbols/units ki approval IUPAC karta hai — koi aur international body nahi. [Q1537]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 14 Common Names and Chemical Formulas Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0402","t":"15 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Chemistry","x":[" CHEMISTRY CH.15 — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Atoms, Molecules & Basic Definitions\n2. States of Matter & Phase Changes\n3. Mole Concept, Atomic Structure & Isotopes\n4. Chemical Bonding: Ionic vs Covalent\n5. Laws of Chemical Combination & Equations\n6. Acids, Bases, Salts & Neutralization\n7. Important Compounds & Their Reactions\n8. Metals, Rust, Corrosion & Properties\n9. Separation Techniques\n10. Environmental Chemistry\n11. Gases, Fuels & Energy\n12. Organic Chemistry, Fats & Nutrition\n13. Polymers, Fibres & Plastics\n14. Health, Safety & Everyday Applications\n15. Laboratory Equipment & Techniques\n16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Full)\n⚠️\n1. Atoms, Molecules & Basic Definitions\n● Element: Same number of protons wale atoms — Fe, Cu, Ag, Au, H, C, N, O. [Q1611]\n● Molecule: 2+ atoms chemically bonded — O₂, N₂, NH₃, H₂O, CO₂. [Q1683]\n– Diatomic: O₂, N₂, H₂. Triatomic: CO₂. Polyatomic: NH₃, H₂O, S₈. [Q1683]\n● Alloys: Red gold (Au+Cu), white gold (Au+Ni+Zn), sterling silver (Ag+Cu) — NOT pure molecules. [Q1611]\n● Pure substance: Methane, copper, silver, gold, water, glucose — fixed composition. [Q1653]\n● Panch Tatva: Air, Earth, Fire, Sky, Water — Acharya Kanada (Kashyap) ne paramanu (atom) propose kiya. [Q1672]\n● Neon (Z=10): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶; K=2, L=8; 2 shells completely filled — noble gas. [Q1629]\n● Electronic configurations: C = 1s²2s²2p²; Mg = 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²; Ar = 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁶. [Q1629]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: \"Atom of a compound\" — ye statement galat hai; compound = molecule/bonded atoms. [Q1675]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Particles of matter stationary nahi — hamesha continuous motion mein hain. [Q1677]\n2. States of Matter & Phase Changes\n● Solid: Definite shape & volume, rigid, incompressible, strong intermolecular forces, least diffusion. [Q1676, Q1677]\n● Liquid: Definite volume, no fixed shape, weaker forces than solids. [Q1676]\n● Gas: No fixed shape/volume, weak forces, rapid diffusion, most intermolecular space. [Q1676, Q1677]\n● Plasma: 4th state; free electrons + ions; stars (Sun) mein; >99% visible universe. [Q1610, Q1618]\n● Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC): 5th state; super cold atoms; S.N. Bose + Einstein. [Q1524 from previous chapter]\n● Intermolecular forces: Solid > Liquid > Gas. [Q1654]\n● Compressibility: Volume change under pressure — Gas > Liquid >> Solid. [Q1662]\n● Rigidity: Fixed shape due to strong forces — solids. [Q1659]"," ● State change: Temperature change se hota hai — energy add/remove. [Q1682]\n● Physical changes: Melting, freezing, liquefaction, vaporisation, shredding — reversible. [Q1605]\n● Chemical changes: Burning, cooking, rusting, rotting, fermentation — new substance forms. [Q1605]\n● Evaporation: Liquid → Gas; cooling effect — salt from seawater, water in earthen pot, acetone on palm. Rate\nincreases with both surface area aur temperature (humidity/wind speed bhi factors hain — humidity badhne se\nrate ghatta hai). [Q1495, Q1580, Q1605, Q1642]\n● Sublimation: Solid → Gas — Iodine, Camphor, Dry ice (solid CO₂), NH₄Cl, Anthracene, Naphthalene. [Q1625, Q1652,\nQ1681]\n● Deposition: Gas → Solid directly (water vapour → ice). [Q1580]\n● Condensation: Gas → Liquid — morning dew, foggy windows. [Q1419, Q1580]\n● Liquid Nitrogen boiling point: -196°C (melting point -209.9°C); fractional distillation of liquid air se banta hai; low\nviscosity colourless coolant. [Q1587]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: \"Solid CO₂ directly changes to liquid\" — galat; ye directly gas mein jaata hai. [Q1658]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solids ka definite shape hota hai — indefinite nahi. [Q1676]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fermentation chemical change hai — physical nahi. [Q1605]\n3. Mole Concept, Atomic Structure & Isotopes\n● Mole: Amount of substance jo 12 g Carbon-12 mein atoms ke barabar elementary particles contain kare = 6.022 ×\n10²³ (Avogadro's number, N₀). [Q1617, Q1673, Q1678]\n● 1 mole kisi bhi particle mein hamesha 6.022 × 10²³ particles hote hain — atomic/molecular mass pe depend nahi.\n[Q1673]\n● 16 g Oxygen = 1 mole = 6.022 × 10²³ atoms. [Q1666]\n● 1 mole H₂O = 18 g (M = 2×1 + 16 = 18). [Q1645]\n● (NH₄)₂SO₄ mein total atoms = 15 (H=8, N=2, O=4, S=1). [Q1671]\n● Carbon-12 = atomic mass reference standard. [Q1619]\n● Isotopes: Same atomic number, different mass number — H-1/2/3; C-12/13/14; O-16/17/18. [Q1619, Q1632]\n● Isobars: Same mass number, different atomic number — Ca-40 (Z=20) & Ar-40 (Z=18). [Q1632]\n● Isotones: Same neutrons — ³⁶S, ³⁷Cl, ³⁸Ar. [Q1632]\n● Ionization energy unit: kJ mol⁻¹. [Q1670]\n● Dalton's atomic theory: Matter = small particles called atoms; element, compound, mixture sab atoms se. [Q1507,\nQ1518 from previous chapter]\n● Law of Conservation of Mass: Reactants mass = Products mass. [Q1664]\n● Law of Definite Proportions: Compound mein elements fixed mass ratio mein — CO₂ (C:O = 3:8), H₂O (H:O = 1:8),\nNH₃ (N:H = 14:3). [Q1669, Q1664]\n4. Chemical Bonding: Ionic vs Covalent\n● Silicon vs Carbon: Same group (14); Si atom larger; Si-Si bond C-C bond se lamba aur kamzoor → silicon long-chain\ncompounds hyper-reactive. [Q1561]\n● Covalent bond: Electron sharing; metals + non-metals ke beech nahi. [Q1566]\n● N₂: Triple bond — 6 shared electrons (3 pairs). [Q1562, Q1577]\n● CO₂: O=C=O; carbon har oxygen ke saath double bond — 2 electrons share. [Q1564]\n● Covalent compounds examples: NH₃, O₂, CH₄, H₂O, P₂O₅. [Q1566, Q1574]\n● Ionic bond: Electron transfer; metals + non-metals. [Q1569]"," ● Ionic compounds examples: NaCl, CaCl₂, CaO, MgCl₂. AgCl (Silver Chloride) bhi ionic compound hai — Ag⁺ + Cl⁻\ncombine hoke banta hai (AgNO₃ solution mein NaCl daalne se white precipitate). [Q1566, Q1571, Q1685]\n● Electrovalent = Ionic — same cheez. [Q1569]\n● Anion: Negative ion — gains electrons (F → F⁻). [Q1624]\n● Cation: Positive ion — loses electrons (Na → Na⁺). [Q1624]\n● NH₄⁺: Cation (+1). CO₃²⁻, NO₃⁻, OH⁻: Anions. [Q1674]\n● NaCl: Na⁺ (cation) + Cl⁻ (anion); Na loses 1e⁻ (Neon config), Cl gains 1e⁻ (Argon config). [Q1628]\n● Electronegativity: Atom's tendency to attract electrons; Left→Right increases, Top→Bottom decreases.\n– Top: F > O > N > Cl > Br. [Q1637]\n● NaOH: Ionic (Na⁺ & OH⁻) + covalent (O-H bond) — dono bonding. [Q1576]\n● Ionic compounds ke high melting/boiling points: Strong inter-ionic (electrostatic) attraction todne ke liye bahut\nzyada energy chahiye — isiliye melting/boiling points high hote hain. Examples: CaO (2850K) > NaCl (1074K) >\nCaCl₂ (1045K) — CaO sabse zyada boiling point wala. [Q1563, Q1573, Q1578, Q1661]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: N₂ mein 6 shared electrons hain — 4 ya 8 nahi. [Q1562]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: MgCl₂ ionic hai — covalent nahi. [Q1566]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH pure covalent nahi — ionic + covalent dono hai. [Q1576]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electron add karne se anion banta hai. [Q1624]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Intermolecular force solid > liquid > gas. [Q1654]\n5. Laws of Chemical Combination & Equations\n● Chemical equation symbols: + (multiple reactants/products), → (reactants to products),\n (reversible), Δ\n⇌\n(heated). [Q1622]\n● State symbols: (s) = solid, (l) = liquid, (g) = gas, (aq) = aqueous. [Q1622]\n● Balanced equation: Reactants aur products donon taraf har element ke atoms barabar. [Q1081 from previous\nchapter]\n● Law of Conservation of Mass + Law of Definite Proportions — Dalton's atomic theory se explain hote hain. [Q1664]\n6. Acids, Bases, Salts & Neutralization\n● Alkali: Base jo water mein dissolve hoti hai — NaOH, KOH, Ca(OH)₂. [Q1623]\n● Lime (Ca(OH)₂) + dilute acid → salt + water; CO₂ nahi banta. [Q1615]\n● Baking soda (NaHCO₃), limestone (CaCO₃), marble (CaCO₃) — dilute acid se CO₂ dete hain. [Q1615]\n● Glacial acetic acid: 100% acetic acid free of water (<1%); colorless, corrosive; 16.7°C pe solidify. [Q1621]\n● NaOH (Caustic Soda): Basic nature OH⁻ ions ki wajah se — H⁺ ions se nahi. [Q1687]\n● H₂SO₄: Petroleum refining mein \"sweetening/desulfurization\" catalyst — sulfur hataane ke liye. [Q1687]\n● Aqua regia: HNO₃ : HCl = 1:3 — gold dissolve karne ke liye.\n– Aur dissolve hote hain: Pd, Ga, Ti. [Q1633]\n● Brine electrolysis (Chlor-alkali): NaCl(aq) → NaOH + H₂ + Cl₂. [Q1680, Q1004 from previous chapter]\n● Dry cell: Energy stored as chemical energy. [Q1679]\n● Antacids: Al(OH)₃, MgCO₃, Mg₂O₈Si₃, Mg(OH)₂, CaCO₃, NaHCO₃ — excess stomach acid neutralize. [Q1353, Q1466]\n● Soap molecule: Hydrophilic head (water-soluble) + Hydrophobic tail (oil-soluble). [Q1602]\n● Saponification: Soap banane ki process; long-chain fatty acids ke K/Na salts. [Q1602]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lime dilute acid se CO₂ nahi deta. [Q1615]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH basic nature = OH⁻ ions se. [Q1687]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Soap = hydrophilic head + hydrophobic tail — donon same nahi. [Q1602]\n7. Important Compounds & Their Reactions\n● Baking soda (NaHCO₃) heating: 2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂ (above 80°C).\n– Na₂CO₃ recrystallization → Washing soda (Na₂CO₃·10H₂O). [Q1570]\n● Bleaching powder {CaOCl₂}: Dry Cl₂ + dry Ca(OH)₂ — oxidising agent, disinfectant. [Q1446, Q1453, Q1468]\n● Plaster of Paris (CaSO₄·½H₂O): Gypsum ko 373 K par heat karke.\n– Setting: CaSO₄·½H₂O + H₂O → CaSO₄·2H₂O; mass expand + heat liberate. [Q1614, Q1355]\n● White washing drying: Ca(OH)₂ + CO₂ (air) → CaCO₃ + H₂O + heat = carbonation. [Q1612, Q1275]\n● Quicklime (CaO) + H₂O → Slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂) — exothermic. [Q1551]\n● CaO mein Ca:O mass ratio = 40:16 = 5:2. [Q1663]\n● Slaked lime (Ca(OH)₂): Soil acidity correct karne ke liye — pH 1 unit badhane ke liye ~1500 kg/hectare. [Q1667]\n● CaCl₂: Hygroscopic — moist gas dry karne ke liye. [Q1660]\n● Heavy water (D₂O): Density 11% zyada; neutron moderator in nuclear reactors. [Q1583]\n● RDX: Royal Demolition Explosive; nitramine; white crystalline; water-insoluble. [Q1584]\n● Poly-oxime gel: Oct 2018, Indian scientists (InStem) — farmers ko toxic pesticides se bachane ke liye. [Q1585]\n● Nessler's reagent (K₂HgI₄): Ammonia detect karne ke liye. [Q1599]\n● Liquor ammonia (NH₄OH): Oil/grease stains hataane ke liye. [Q1599]\n● Copper sulphate (CuSO₄): Algae control ke liye generally used chemical — fungicide, algaecide, root killer,\nantimicrobial bhi. [Q1626]\n● Potassium sulphate (K₂SO₄): Elements = K (Potassium), S (Sulphur), O (Oxygen) — sabhi options correct. [Q1640]\n● Water of crystallization:\n– Baking soda (NaHCO₃): NO water of crystallization. [Q1634]\n– Washing soda (Na₂CO₃·10H₂O): 10 molecules. [Q1634]\n– Blue vitriol (CuSO₄·5H₂O): 5 molecules. [Q1634]\n– Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O): 2 molecules. [Q1634]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda garam karne se Na₂CO₃ banta hai — NaOH ya Na₂O nahi. [Q1575]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: POP setting mein mass expand + heat liberate dono hote hain. [Q1614]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda mein NO water of crystallization. [Q1634]\n8. Metals, Rust, Corrosion & Properties\n● Rust = Hydrated ferric oxide (Fe₂O₃·xH₂O) — reddish-brown; iron + O₂ + water. [Q1630, Q1546]\n● Ferric chloride (FeCl₃): Orange to brown-black; slightly soluble. [Q1630]\n● Ferric bromide (FeBr₃): Red-brown; Lewis acid catalyst. [Q1630]\n● Ferric sulphide (Fe₂S₃): Black powder; degrades at ambient temp. [Q1630]\n● Gold (Au): Highest density among common metals; 24k = pure; dissolves in aqua regia. [Q1647]\n● Osmium (Os, Z=76): Densest element. Hydrogen (H, Z=1): Lowest density. [Q1647, Q1598]\n● Mercury (Hg, Z=80): Quicksilver; only metallic element liquid at RT. [Q1647, Q1533]"," ● Copper (Cu, Z=29): First metal used by man. [Q1647]\n● Iron (Fe, Z=26): Wrought iron = purest; Pig iron = most impure. [Q1647]\n● Copper valency: Variable — +1 in Cu₂O (cuprous), +2 in CuO/CuSO₄ (cupric). [Q1655]\n● Zinc: Bluish-grey metal. SO₂: Sharp pungent smell. PbI₂: Bright yellow (\"golden rain\"). [Q1656]\n● Transition metals: Paramagnetic (unpaired electrons); d-block config (n-1)d¹⁻¹⁰ ns¹⁻²; variable valency, colored\nions, catalytic. [Q1641]\n● Electrode materials: Copper, graphite, titanium, brass, silver, platinum. [Q1668]\n● Silver plating: Silver electrode use hota hai. [Q1668]\n● Galvanization: Iron/steel pe zinc coating — corrosion prevention. [Q1500]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rust = Fe₂O₃·xH₂O — ferric chloride/bromide/sulphide nahi. [Q1630]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cuprous = Cu⁺¹; Cupric = Cu⁺². [Q1655]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Densest element = Osmium — platinum/steel/copper nahi. [Q1598, Q1647]\n9. Separation Techniques\n● Magnetic separation: Iron pins from sand. [Q1620]\n● Winnowing: Husk from wheat grains — lighter husk air mein ur jaati hai. [Q1625]\n● Centrifugation: Butter from cream — rapid spinning. [Q1646]\n● Froth floatation: Ore separation based on wetting properties; mustard oil as frother. [Q1644]\n● Filtration: Insoluble impurities from liquid — sand + water. [Q1625, Q1437]\n● Leaching: Selective dissolution of metals from ores. [Q1644]\n● Evaporation: Liquid → vapour — salt from seawater. [Q1425, Q1580]\n● Sublimation: Solid → gas — Iodine, Camphor, NH₄Cl, Naphthalene, Dry ice. [Q1625, Q1652, Q1681]\n● Separating funnel: Immiscible liquids — oil & water. [Q1429, Q1499]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sodium sulphate sublimable nahi hai. [Q1652]\n10. Environmental Chemistry\n● BOD (Biochemical Oxygen Demand): Dissolved oxygen jo bacteria organic waste decompose karne mein use karte\nhain — mg/L. [Q1616]\n● COD (Chemical Oxygen Demand): Oxygen required to oxidize organic + inorganic — ppm. [Q1616]\n● Carbonaceous demand: Organic matter ke oxidation se. [Q1616]\n● Ozone depleting substances (ODS): CFCs, HCFCs, halons, methyl bromide, carbon tetrachloride, hydro bromo\nfluorocarbons.\n– NOT ozone depleting: Sodium silicate. [Q1636, Q1478]\n● Photochemical smog: Sunlight + NOₓ + VOCs. [Q1608]\n● Sulphurous smog: Sulphur-bearing fossil fuels (coal) se. [Q1608]\n● Greenhouse gases: CO₂, CH₄, N₂O. [Q1480, Q1606]\n● GWP (Global Warming Potential): CO₂ ko reference maanke compare karte hain.\n– High-GWP: CFCs, HFCs, HCFCs, PFCs, SF₆. [Q1606]\n● Natural gas: Anaerobic bacteria se vegetable matter decompose — mainly methane (CH₄). [Q1607]\n● Conventional energy = Non-renewable: Fossil fuels (coal, oil, natural gas). [Q1609]\n● Renewable: Sunlight, wind. Inexhaustible: Sunlight. Alternative: Wind, geothermal, hydroelectric, hydrogen."," [Q1609]\n● Wind blowing ka cause: Air pressure difference aur Earth ki unequal heating hai — Earth ki rotation akele wind ka\ncause nahi hai. [Q1684]\n● Coal composition: Primarily Carbon (C), Hydrogen (H), Oxygen (O) ka complex mixture, saath thoda Nitrogen (N) &\nSulphur (S) compounds bhi — \"O₂H₂ + half free carbon\" wala statement galat hai. [Q1684]\n● Environment-friendly fuel: Jiske combustion products non-poisonous hon. [Q1684]\n● Destructive distillation of coal: Air ke bina heat karne se coke banta hai — grey, hard, porous, high carbon.\n– Coke: Steel manufacture & metal extraction. [Q1638]\n– Petrol/kerosene/diesel: Crude oil se, coal se nahi. [Q1638]\n● Biogas: 50–75% CH₄, 25–50% CO₂, traces H₂S & NH₃. CO nahi hota. [Q1480, Q1686]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Conventional energy = Non-renewable — renewable/inexhaustible/alternative nahi. [Q1609]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: GWP reference = CO₂ — methane/ozone/NO₂ nahi. [Q1606]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Biogas mein CO nahi hota. [Q1686]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Wind rotation-of-Earth se akele nahi banta; coal mein O₂H₂ + free carbon nahi hota. [Q1684]\n11. Gases, Fuels & Energy\n● Calorific value order: H₂ (150,000 kJ/kg) > LPG (55,000) > Methane/CNG (50,000). [Q1603]\n● Hydrogen sabse zyada calorific value rakhta hai. [Q1603]\n● Calorific value: Heat produced by complete combustion of unit mass — unit kJ/kg. [Q1643]\n● Ignition temperature: Minimum temp for fuel to catch fire. [Q1643]\n● Volatile matter: Components readily burnt in oxygen. [Q1643]\n● Thermal capacity: Heat to produce unit temp change in unit mass. [Q1643]\n● Cryogenic engine: Liquid O₂ + liquid H₂ as fuel.\n– RL-10 (world's first, 1963, USA); CE-20 (India, 5 June 2017). [Q1589]\n● LPG components: Propane, butane, propylene, butylene, isobutane. Main = Butane. [Q1398, Q1498]\n● Electric bulbs: Filled with N₂ + Ar — tungsten filament oxidation rokne ke liye. [Q1493]\n● CO: Odourless, colorless; incomplete combustion se; oxygen displace karke poisoning. [Q1493]\n● NPK fertilizer: N (leaf growth), P (root/flower/fruit), K (protein synthesis). [Q1590]\n● Ammonia (NH₃): N:H mass ratio = 14:3. [Q1593]\n● Helium (He): 2nd lightest; balloons, medicine, arc welding, cryogenic research. [Q1481]\n● Nitrogen (N₂): Food preservation — displaces oxygen; atmosphere ~78%; Daniel Rutherford (1772). [Q1501, Q1510]\n● Oxygen essential for burning — candle glass jar mein cover karne se bujh jaati hai. [Q1592]\n● Dry ice (Solid CO₂): Sublimes directly to gas — vaccine cooling, food freezing, special effects fog. [Q1658, Q1648,\nQ1558]\n● Nuclear energy: Atoms se obtained energy ko nuclear energy kehte hain — Uranium fission se heat, steam banta\nhai jo turbine generator se electricity generate karta hai. [Q1657]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Calorific value sabse zyada Hydrogen ka hai — LPG/methane/natural gas nahi. [Q1603]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nitrogen food preservation ke liye — oxygen/hydrogen/chlorine nahi. [Q1501]\n12. Organic Chemistry, Fats & Nutrition\n● Wohler ne disprove kiya \"organic compounds sirf living system mein bante hain\". [Q1567]"," ● Organic compound: Carbon covalently bound to other atoms (C-C, C-H). [Q1567]\n● Propanoic acid (CH₃CH₂COOH): Suffix = \"oic acid\"; antifungal food agent. [Q1568]\n● Ethane (C₂H₆): Total 7 covalent bonds — 1 C-C + 6 C-H. [Q1540]\n● Amino acids:\n– Cysteine: Sulphur-containing, non-essential.\n– Methionine: Sulphur-containing, essential.\n– Tryptophan: Aromatic, essential.\n– Histidine: Basic. Serine: Non-essential. [Q1594]\n● Saturated fats: Solid at RT — single bonds, hydrogen saturated; butter, palm/coconut oil, cheese, meat. [Q1639]\n● Unsaturated fats: Liquid at RT — double bonds; healthier. [Q1639]\n● Monounsaturated fats: Liquid at RT, harden when chilled. [Q1639]\n● Polyunsaturated fats: Omega-3, Omega-6 — essential for brain function. [Q1639]\n● Fermentation: Glucose ka anaerobic breakdown — enzymes se chemical change. [Q1627]\n● Butyric acid: Rancid butter ka foul smell; dairy products. [Q1487]\n● Stearic acid: Animal & plant fats; soap preparation. [Q1487]\n● Acetic acid (CH₃COOH): Vinegar; pickled vegetables, sauces. [Q1505]\n● Rancidity: Fats/oils ka oxidation/hydrolysis; airtight containers/N₂ flush se roka jaata hai. [Q1390, Q1487]\n● Lactose (C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁): Milk sugar; disaccharide. Glucose/Galactose/Fructose = C₆H₁₂O₆. [Q1557]\n13. Polymers, Fibres & Plastics\n● Natural fibres: Cotton, silk, wool, linen, jute. [Q1591, Q1595]\n● Synthetic fibres: Nylon, polyester, acrylic, aramid, rayon (regenerated cellulose). [Q1591, Q1595]\n● PVC (Polyvinyl chloride): Monomer = vinyl chloride; raincoats, handbags, water pipes, floor tiles. [Q1483, Q1665]\n● Bakelite: Phenol + formaldehyde; switches, sockets. [Q1490]\n● Teflon (PTFE): Non-stick coating. [Q1492]\n● PET: Bottles, utensils. [Q1488]\n● Nylon: Backpacks, flak jackets, athletic shoes, umbrellas, ropes. [Q1488]\n● Acrylic: Sweaters, fleece, socks. [Q1488]\n● Polystyrene: Insulator, wrapping, toys, radio/TV cabinets. [Q1483, Q1665]\n● Polypropene: Ropes, toys, pipes, fibres. [Q1665]\n● Polymer definition: Large molecules, high molecular mass (10³–10⁷ u). [Q1665]\n● Firemen uniforms: Melamine plastic coating — flame resistant. [Q1596]\n● Glyptal: Paints, metal coating, lacquers. [Q1483]\n14. Health, Safety & Everyday Applications\n● WHO salt recommendation: < 5 g per day — hypertension, heart disease, stroke prevention.\n– 2025 tak global salt intake 30% reduce karne ka target.\n– Iodine: Adults 150 mcg, Pregnant 220 mcg.\n– Magnesium: 19-30 M 400 mg / F 310 mg; 31+ M 420 mg / F 320 mg.\n– Calcium: 14-18 age 1300 mg; 19+ 1000 mg. [Q1581]"," ● Cobalt-60: Cancer treatment — gamma rays. [Q1597]\n● Iodine-131: Thyroid cancer treatment. [Q1597]\n● Uranium-235: Nuclear reactors. [Q1597]\n● Chocolates mein heavy metals: Nickel (Ni-28), Cadmium (Cd-48), Lead (Pb-82) — nickel sabse toxic. [Q1604]\n● Pickle preservatives: Salt, sodium benzoate, sodium metabisulphite. Pepper preservative nahi — sirf flavour.\n[Q1600]\n● Foxing: Old books ke pages ka browning. [Q1582]\n● Water hardness:\n– Soft: 0–60 mg/L as CaCO₃.\n– Moderately hard: 61–120 mg/L. Hard: 121–180 mg/L. Very hard: >180 mg/L. [Q1613]\n● Toothpaste: Basic (pH > 7) — mouth bacteria acid neutralize; pH 5.5 se neeche tooth decay. [Q1463]\n● Osmotic concentration: Solute concentration — osmoles per litre. [Q1635]\n● Osmotic pressure: Minimum pressure to prevent inward flow of pure solvent across semipermeable membrane.\n[Q1635]\n● Turgor pressure: Fluid pressure pressing cell membrane against cell wall. [Q1635]\n● Wall pressure: Cell wall pressure against turgor pressure. [Q1635]\n● Water movement between cells: Osmotic concentration pe depend karta hai. [Q1635]\n● Surface tension: Liquid surface resists external force. [Q1586]\n● Cohesive force: Same substance ke molecules ke beech attraction. [Q1586]\n● Adhesive force: Different substances ke molecules ke beech attraction. [Q1586]\n● Capillarity: Liquid rise/fall in capillary tube due to surface tension. [Q1586]\n● India's first synthetic drug — Methaqualone: CSIR (Council of Scientific and Industrial Research, est. 26 Sept 1942,\nHQ New Delhi — India ka largest R&D organization) dwara develop kiya gaya synthetic barbiturate-like CNS\ndepressant drug. [Q1601]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pepper pickle mein preservative nahi hai. [Q1600]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: \"Size\" chemical reaction ka indicator nahi hai. [Q1208]\n15. Laboratory Equipment & Techniques\n● China dish: Round-bottomed crucible-shaped porcelain; chemical reactions; delicate but strong. [Q1565]\n● Flame zones:\n– Innermost (Dark/Black): Incomplete combustion, lack of O₂ — unburnt carbon particles.\n– Middle (Yellow/Luminous): Sufficient O₂, glowing heated carbon particles.\n– Outermost (Blue): Complete combustion, ample O₂. [Q1588]\n● Diffusion: Particles move high concentration → low concentration.\n– Graham's Law: Rate 1/√(density/molecular weight) — at constant T & P.\n∝\n– Diffusion rate: Gas > Liquid > Solid.\n– Diffusion depends on: Temperature, pressure, density — NOT volume. [Q1649]\n● Electrolysis of water: Electricity se water → H₂ + O₂.\n– Ionisation = weak electrolyte self-ionisation.\n– Hydrolysis = water molecule breaks chemical bonds.\n– Atomisation = high pressure water spray on molten metal → fine powder. [Q1579]"," 16.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Full)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Silicon long-chain compounds hyper-reactive hain — stable nahi. [Q1561]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: N₂ mein 6 shared electrons hain — 4 ya 8 nahi. [Q1562]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: CO₂ mein har oxygen carbon ke saath 2 electrons share karti hai. [Q1564]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: MgCl₂ ionic hai — covalent nahi. [Q1566]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ionic compounds solid hain kyunki strong inter-ionic attraction hai — CaO (2850K) sabse high\nmelting/boiling point. [Q1572, Q1563, Q1573, Q1578, Q1661]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH ionic + covalent dono hai — pure covalent nahi. [Q1576]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda garam karne se Na₂CO₃ banta hai — NaOH ya Na₂O nahi. [Q1575]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electrolysis of water ≠ Hydrolysis ≠ Ionisation ≠ Atomisation. [Q1579]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sublimation = Solid → Gas; Deposition = Gas → Solid. [Q1580]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Heavy water ka density sirf 11% zyada hota hai — 3 times nahi. [Q1583]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: RDX = explosive — pesticide/current meter nahi. [Q1584]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Flame ka innermost part unburnt carbon particles ki wajah se black. [Q1588]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Liquid Nitrogen ka boiling point -196°C hai. [Q1587]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Calorific value sabse zyada Hydrogen ka hai. [Q1603]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fermentation chemical change hai. [Q1605]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: GWP reference = CO₂. [Q1606]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Conventional energy = Non-renewable. [Q1609]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Soap = hydrophilic head + hydrophobic tail. [Q1602]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pepper pickle mein preservative nahi. [Q1600]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lime dilute acid se CO₂ nahi deta. [Q1615]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: POP setting mein mass expand + heat liberate dono hote hain. [Q1614]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Glacial acetic acid = 100% acetic acid — frozen nahi, water-free. [Q1621]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alkali = base jo water mein dissolve hoti hai. [Q1623]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electron add karne se anion banta hai. [Q1624]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaCl mein cation = Na⁺ — Cl⁺ nahi. [Q1628]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Iodine + potato = blue-black. [Q1631]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Baking soda mein NO water of crystallization. [Q1634]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Diffusion rate volume pe depend nahi karta. [Q1649]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AgCl sunlight mein grey hota hai — brown nahi; AgCl banta hai Ag⁺ + Cl⁻ se. [Q1650, Q1685]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Carbon sabse zyada melting/boiling point — Li/P/Ar nahi. [Q1651]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sodium sulphate sublimable nahi hai. [Q1652]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Methane = pure substance; milk/sugar paste/air = mixture. [Q1653]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Intermolecular force solid > liquid > gas. [Q1654]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cuprous = Cu⁺¹; Cupric = Cu⁺². [Q1655]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Slaked lime soil quality improve karta hai — manure/vinegar nahi. [Q1667]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Silver = electrode material; Zn/Al/Ca nahi. [Q1668]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 mole mein hamesha 6.022×10²³ particles — atomic mass pe depend nahi. [Q1673]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: \"Atom of a compound\" — galat statement. [Q1675]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: NaOH basic nature = OH⁻ ions se; H⁺ se nahi. [Q1687]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Biogas mein CO nahi hota. [Q1686]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solids ka definite shape hota hai. [Q1676]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Particles stationary nahi — continuous motion mein hain. [Q1677]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Wind rotation-of-Earth se akele nahi banta; coal mein O₂H₂ + free carbon nahi hota. [Q1684]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: India ka first synthetic drug Methaqualone tha (CSIR). [Q1601]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Evaporation rate surface area aur temperature dono se badhti hai. [Q1642]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nuclear energy = atoms se obtained energy. [Q1657]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Copper sulphate algae control ke liye use hota hai. [Q1626]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Chemistry Chapter 15 Miscellaneous Full Mind Map (Q1561-Q1687)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0403","t":"01 Light and Optics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.1 — LIGHT AND OPTICS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚡\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Spherical Mirrors: Image Formation & Position Rules\n2. Spherical Mirrors: Formula, Sign Convention & Graphs\n3. Lenses: Image Formation, Ray Rules & Power\n4. Plane Mirror: Properties & Lateral Inversion\n5. Reflection Basics, Laws & Terminology\n6. Refraction through Slab, Prism & Interfaces\n7. Speed of Light, Refractive Index & Medium Properties\n8. Dispersion of Light (VIBGYOR)\n9. Scattering of Light & Sky Colour\n10. Atmospheric Refraction & Twinkling\n11. Human Eye, Vision Defects & Corrective Lenses\n12. Real-Life Applications of Mirrors & Lenses\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1–Q273)\n⚠️\n14. Numerical: Mirror Formula (Image/Object Distance)\n15. Numerical: Lens Formula (Image/Object Distance)\n16. Numerical: Power of Lens & Combined Power (Doublet)\n17. Numerical: Magnification Problems (Height/Diameter)\n18. Numerical: Sign Convention, Focal Length & R = 2f\n19. Numerical: Refractive Index, Snell's Law & Relative RI\n20. Numerical: Speed of Light in Medium\n21. Numerical: Apparent Depth & Real Depth\n22. Numerical: Critical Angle\n23. Numerical: Graph-Based & Formula Derivation Problems\n24. Numerical: Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet\n1. Spherical Mirrors: Image Formation & Position Rules\n● Concave mirror (converging mirror) parallel rays ko focus par converge karta hai — isliye surya ki sharp image\npaper par burn kar sakti hai. [Q5, Q39]\n● Convex mirror hamesha virtual, erect, diminished image banata hai, chahe object kahi bhi ho; image pole (0) aur\nfocus (f) ke beech banega. [Q39, Q79, Q125, Q221, Q259]\n● Concave mirror ki image formation positions (yaad rakho):\n– Object infinity par → image Focus (F) par, highly diminished, real, inverted. [Q21, Q52, Q220, Q245, Q273]\n– Object beyond C (2f) → image F aur C ke beech, diminished, real, inverted. [Q36, Q47, Q69, Q251]\n– Object at C (2f) par → image C (2f) par, same size, real, inverted. [Q48, Q219]\n– Object between C aur F → image beyond C, enlarged, real, inverted. [Q66, Q216]\n– Object at F → image at infinity, highly enlarged, real, inverted. [Q52, Q220]\n– Object between F aur Pole → image behind mirror, virtual, erect, enlarged. [Q52, Q53, Q169, Q195]\n● Magnification analysis:\n– m negative (e.g., -0.5, -0.65, -1.38) → image real, inverted. Agar |m| < 1 → diminished; |m| > 1 → enlarged.\n[Q12, Q89, Q107]\n– m positive + |m| > 1 (e.g., +3.0) → image virtual, erect, enlarged (concave mirror ya convex lens dono de sakte\nhain). [Q111]\n– m positive + |m| < 1 (e.g., +1/2) → image virtual, erect, diminished. [Q24]"," ● Concave mirror normally converging hota hai, lekin jab object pole aur focus ke beech ho to reflected rays diverge\nkarte hain (virtual image banane ke liye). [Q130]\n● Convex mirror hamesha diverging hota hai, kabhi converge nahi kar sakta. [Q127, Q130]\n● Ray Rules (Concave mirror):\n– Ray parallel to principal axis → reflects through focus. [Q95, Q99, Q204]\n– Ray through focus → reflects parallel to principal axis. [Q95]\n– Ray through C → wapas same path mein retraces (normal incidence, angle = 0°). [Q2, Q13, Q15, Q40, Q59, Q103,\nQ138, Q150]\n– Agar parallel beam principal axis ke parallel nahi hai, to wo principal focal plane par converge karegi. [Q141]\n● Pole par oblique incidence wali ray apna path retrace nahi karti — ye sirf C se hokar jaane wali ray karti hai.\n[Q124]\n● Mirror formula se rearrange karke: f = (uv)/(u+v). [Q112, Q132]\n● Graph: m vs v ka graph concave mirror ke liye straight line hota hai with slope +1/f, x-intercept +f, y-intercept -1.\n[Q117]\n● Virtual + erect image sirf plane mirror aur concave mirror (jab object pole-focus ke beech ho) de sakte hain —\nconvex mirror bhi hamesha virtual-erect deta hai; concave \"hamesha\" nahi (only special case). [Q33]\n● Point source concave mirror ke Focus (F) par rakha ho to reflected rays parallel beam ban jaati hain (converging\nmirror ka reverse use). [Q85]\n● Convex mirror ke focal length 1 m ho aur parallel beam incident ho, to reflected rays mirror ke peechhe 1 m\ndistance wale point se diverge hote hue appear hoti hain (distance = focal length). [Q96]\n● 'Converging mirror' naam concave mirror ko isliye milta hai kyunki ye parallel rays ko ek point (focus) par\nconverge karta hai — inward curved (bulge center ki taraf) reflecting surface hoti hai. [Q239, Q267]\n2. Spherical Mirrors: Formula, Sign Convention & Graphs\n● Radius of Curvature: R = 2f; yaani P se C ki distance = 2 × focal length. [Q4, Q23, Q92, Q121, Q225, Q244]\n● New Cartesian Sign Convention:\n– Object hamesha left side par rakha jaata hai. [Q184, Q196]\n– Right of origin (P) = positive; Left = negative. [Q196]\n– Above principal axis = positive; Below = negative. [Q184, Q196]\n– Concave mirror ka f = negative, R = negative. [Q50, Q93, Q134, Q144, Q246]\n– Convex mirror ka f = positive, R = positive. [Q10, Q72, Q144, Q250]\n● Mirror Formula: 1/f = 1/v + 1/u. [Q173]\n● Magnification (m):\n– Formula: m = -v/u = hi/ho. [Q200]\n– Virtual/erect image ke liye m positive; real/inverted ke liye m negative. [Q200, Q218]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mirror ki focal length medium change hone par nahi badalti (jaise liquid mein dubone par), kyunki f =\nR/2 sirf geometric shape par depend karti hai. Lens ki focal length medium ke saath badalti hai. [Q258]\n● Concave mirror banate waqt sphere ke slice ko is tarah polish karte hain ki reflecting (depression) surface centre\nof curvature ki taraf ho aur polish (silvering) opposite side par ho. [Q83]\n● Radius of Curvature ki definition: Pole (P) aur Centre of Curvature (C) ke beech ki distance. [Q110]\n● Agar spherical mirror aur thin lens dono ka focal length -10 cm diya ho, toh sign convention ke hisaab se dono\nconcave honge (negative f sirf concave mirror/lens ka hota hai). [Q194]\n● Spherical lens ke liye sign convention mein saari distances Optical Centre se measure ki jaati hain (mirror mein\nPole se hoti hain). [Q202]"," 3. Lenses: Image Formation, Ray Rules & Power\n● Convex lens (positive focal length) distant object ki image focus (f) par banata hai — lens se screen ki doori = f.\n[Q8]\n● Convex lens ki image formation summary:\n– Object infinity → image at F2, highly diminished, real, inverted. [Q7, Q30, Q255]\n– Object beyond 2F → image F2 aur 2F2 ke beech, diminished, real, inverted. [Q30, Q176]\n– Object 2F par → image at 2F2, same size, real, inverted. [Q7, Q190]\n– Object F aur 2F ke beech → image beyond 2F2, enlarged, real, inverted. [Q7, Q176]\n– Object F par → image at infinity, highly enlarged, real, inverted. [Q7, Q176]\n– Object F aur Optical Centre ke beech → image same side par, virtual, erect, enlarged. [Q7, Q197]\n● Concave lens hamesha virtual, erect, diminished image banata hai, chahe object kahi bhi ho infinity se O tak. [Q9,\nQ70, Q175, Q198]\n– Object infinity par → image at F, point-sized. [Q175]\n– Parallel ray concave lens se guzre to focus se diverge hote hue dikhti hai. [Q180]\n– Focus ki taraf jaane wali ray principal axis ke parallel niklegi. [Q177]\n● Convex lens real inverted image twice the size → magnification = -2 (negative kyunki inverted). [Q22]\n● Lens ke Optical Centre (O) se hokar guzarne wali ray bina kisi deviation ke seedhi jaati hai, aur yeh point hamesha\nprincipal axis par hota hai. [Q56, Q142, Q189, Q238]\n● Principal axis wo imaginary line hai jo lens ke do foci (F1 aur F2) ko join karti hai. [Q149, Q205]\n● Power (P) = 1/f (in meters); unit = Dioptre (D). [Q139, Q266]\n– Power positive (+2.0D) → convex lens. [Q266]\n– Power negative → concave lens. [Q139]\n● Lens Formula: 1/f = 1/v - 1/u (ya 1/v - 1/u = 1/f). [Q173]\n● Concave lens = thin in middle, thick at edges; Convex lens = thick in middle, thin at edges. [Q161]\n● Lens banane ke liye material transparent hona chahiye; wood (lakdi) aur soil dono se lens nahi ban sakta kyunki\ndono opaque hain — glass, plastic, water se lens ban sakta hai. [Q101, Q211]\n● Point source ko convex lens ya concave mirror ke focus par rakhne se dono hi parallel beam produce karte hain\n(dono converging optical devices hain). [Q38, Q115]\n● Convex lens mein principal axis ke parallel incident ray refraction ke baad Principal Focus se hokar guzarti hai\n(dusri side). [Q58, Q118]\n4. Plane Mirror: Properties & Lateral Inversion\n● Plane mirror ki image hamesha: virtual, erect, same size, laterally inverted. [Q224, Q228, Q237, Q256]\n● Lateral inversion = left side right mein aur right side left mein dikhta hai. [Q228, Q260]\n● Object mirror se jitni doori par ho, image utni hi doori peechhe hota hai. [Q224]\n● Agar mirror mein apna reflection chhota dikhe → convex mirror hai; same size → plane mirror; bada jab paas ho\n→ concave mirror. [Q259]\n5. Reflection Basics, Laws & Terminology\n● Pole (P) = reflecting surface ka geometric centre; surface par hota hai. [Q158, Q204, Q263]\n● Centre of Curvature (C) = us hollow sphere ka centre jiska mirror ek part hai. [Q207, Q270]\n● Principal Focus (F) = wo point jahan principal axis ke parallel rays converge karte hain (concave) ya diverge hote"," hue dikhte hain (convex). [Q119, Q230, Q272]\n● Focal Length (f) = P se F ki distance; f = R/2. [Q183, Q254]\n● Aperture = reflecting surface ka diameter; kitna light capture hoga ye decide karta hai. [Q271]\n● Principal axis = wo imaginary straight line jo Pole, Focus aur Centre of Curvature teeno se hokar guzarti hai, dono\ntaraf extended hoti hai — curved mirrors ke liye bhi ye hamesha straight line hoti hai (kabhi curved nahi hoti).\n[Q143, Q145]\n● Spherical mirror par kisi bhi point se C ko join karne wali line normal hoti hai. Isliye ray C se hokar jaaye to angle\nof incidence = 0°, aur reflected ray bhi 0° par wapas jaati hai. [Q2, Q13, Q15, Q40, Q59, Q103, Q138, Q150]\n● Principal axis par pole par ray incident ho to angle of incidence wahi hota hai jo principal axis se ban raha ho\n(kyunki principal axis normal hota hai pole par); oblique incidence wali ray angle i = angle r follow karte hue\nreflect hoti hai. [Q28, Q32, Q82]\n● Laws of reflection (angle i = angle r, same plane mein) sabhi mirrors (plane, concave, convex) ke liye valid hain —\njaise 30° incidence par reflection bhi 30° hi hota hai. [Q35, Q247, Q269]\n● Spherical mirror ke surface par kisi bhi point ka C se distance hamesha baraabar hota hai (radius constant), isliye\nr1 = r2 = r3 = r4. [Q19]\n● Pole aur Centre of Curvature dono hamesha spherical mirror ke principal axis par hote hain; point of incidence\nkahi bhi ho sakta hai. [Q77]\n● Shiny/smooth surface se light regular reflection karta hai (specific direction mein), rough surface se diffused\nreflection hota hai (sabhi directions mein). [Q222]\n● Light hamesha straight line (rectilinear path) mein travel karta hai — isi property ki wajah se opaque objects ke\npath mein aane par shadow banta hai. [Q164, Q170]\n6. Refraction through Slab, Prism & Interfaces\n● Refraction = ek medium se doosre medium mein jaane par light ka mudna. Glass slab mein: incident ray aur\nemergent ray parallel hoti hain (kyunki do bar opposite direction mein refraction hota hai). [Q3, Q20, Q29, Q193]\n● Rarer (air) → Denser (glass ya water): light normal ki taraf muddta hai → angle of refraction < angle of incidence,\nspeed slows down. Example: air se water (RI=1.33) mein jaate waqt 30° incidence par refraction angle 30° se kam\nbanega. [Q37, Q55, Q68, Q74, Q131, Q178, Q212, Q235, Q306]\n● Denser (glass) → Rarer (air): light normal se door muddta hai → angle of refraction (emergence) > angle of\nincidence inside glass, speed speeds up; light denser se rarer medium mein jaate waqt speed badhti hai isliye\nnormal se door mudti hai. [Q37, Q55, Q68, Q71, Q74, Q88, Q201, Q217, Q233, Q261]\n● Glass slab ke liye: angle of incidence = angle of emergence hota hai. [Q29]\n● Prism mein angle of deviation = incident ray aur emergent ray ke beech ka angle. Formula: δ = (i + e) - A. [Q16,\nQ26, Q86]\n● Prism mein angle of incidence = angle of emergence sirf minimum deviation ki position par hota hai, hamesha\nnahi. [Q62, Q122]\n● Prism mein light 2 baar refract hoti hai — pehli baar air se glass mein enter karte waqt, dusri baar glass se air\nmein exit karte waqt. [Q105]\n● First law of refraction: incident ray, refracted ray, aur normal teeno same plane mein hote hain. [Q80, Q247, Q306]\n● Normal se incidence par (0°) → refraction angle bhi 0°, dono rays ke beech angle 0°; direction change nahi hota\nsirf speed badalti hai. [Q6, Q61, Q114]\n● Glass se hawa mein jaane par refracted ray 30° se zyada angle par bend hoti hai aur incident ray ke same plane\nmein rehti hai. [Q68]\n● Agar light medium A se B mein ja kar normal se door mudd rahi hai, toh medium B rarer hai, isliye relative RI < 1\n(less than unity). [Q113]\n● RI badhne par deviation bhi badhta hai — kyunki light zyada sharply bend hoti hai. [Q109]\n● Snell's Law: sin i / sin r = constant = RI (refractive index). [Q151]"," ● Medium ka light ko refract karne ki capacity uske optical density se measure hoti hai (mass density alag cheez\nhai). [Q157]\n● Ordinary gases (jaise air) mein dispersion nahi dikhta kyunki unka RI ≈ 1, toh alag-alag wavelengths ki speed\nalmost same hoti hai (≈ c). [Q102]\n● Mirage (registan mein paani ka bhram) — total internal reflection ki wajah se hota hai (garam ground ke upar hot\nair rare medium ban jaata hai). [Q156]\n● Pencil paani mein mudi hui (bent) dikhti hai / lemon bada dikhta hai — refraction ki wajah se. [Q91, Q126, Q147,\nQ268]\n● Swimming pool ka floor kam gehra (shallower) dikhta hai — refraction se bottom ka virtual image upar shift hota\nhai. [Q106]\n7. Speed of Light, Refractive Index & Medium Properties\n● Speed of light in vacuum = 3 × 10⁸ m/s — sabse zyada possible speed. [Q232, Q262]\n● Vacuum mein speed max hai kyunki RI = 1 (exactly unity). [Q232]\n● Absolute refractive index kisi bhi medium ka hamesha 1 se zyada hota hai (formula: n = c/v, aur v < c). [Q31, Q234]\n● RI formula: n = c/v = speed of light in vacuum/air ÷ speed in medium (also written μ = c/v). [Q100, Q136, Q146, Q186,\nQ203]\n● RI values yaad rakho:\n– Air ≈ 1.0003 (sabse kam). [Q187, Q248, Q249]\n– Ice = 1.31, Water = 1.33, Kerosene = 1.44, Benzene = 1.50, Rock Salt = 1.54, Glass ≈ 1.5, Diamond = 2.42.\n[Q210, Q227, Q187]\n– Order: Ice < Kerosene < Benzene < Rock Salt. [Q210]\n● Refractive index aur speed ka relation: n 1/v. Jitna zyada RI, utni kam speed. Example: RI 1.47 ka matlab uss\n∝\nmedium mein speed vacuum ki speed se 1.47 guna kam hai. [Q45, Q63, Q100, Q186]\n– Example: RI 1.31, 1.46, 1.65 → speed order: V1 > V2 > V3. [Q45, Q63]\n● Light paani se hawa mein jaane par uski speed badal jaati hai, lekin frequency aur colour same rehte hain. [Q128]\n8. Dispersion of Light (VIBGYOR)\n● White light prism se guzre to 7 colours (VIBGYOR) mein split hoti hai — isse dispersion kehte hain. Discovery:\nIsaac Newton (1666). Spectrum ke do extreme ends Violet aur Red hote hain (Violet shortest wavelength, Red\nlongest wavelength). [Q17, Q78, Q137, Q153, Q163, Q185, Q209]\n● Bending inversely proportional to wavelength hai:\n– Violet (shortest λ ≈ 400 nm) → sabse zyada muddta hai, sabse zyada RI, sabse kam speed in glass. [Q17, Q27,\nQ42, Q57, Q65, Q94, Q133, Q208]\n– Red (longest λ ≈ 700 nm) → sabse kam muddta hai, sabse kam RI. [Q17, Q34, Q49, Q90, Q199, Q252]\n● RI order example: μViolet > μGreen > μYellow ya μBlue > μGreen > μYellow ya full order μV > μI > μB > μG > μY >\nμO > μR. [Q42, Q57, Q73, Q97, Q98]\n● Different colours ka glass mein speed alag-alag hota hai — isliye alag angles par refract hote hain. [Q34, Q64, Q185]\n● Dispersion surface AB par shuru ho jaata hai, kyunki har colour ka RI alag hota hai; surface AC par bhi alag-alag\nrefraction angles hote hain. [Q64, Q108]\n● Prism ko upright rakha jaye to spectrum mein Red top par (least bent) aur Violet bottom par (most bent) hota hai.\n[Q133]\n● Rainbow ka formation: RRC key ke hisaab se refraction + scattering + dispersion ka combination (though\ntraditionally total internal reflection bhi padhaya jaata hai). [Q120, Q171]"," 9. Scattering of Light & Sky Colour\n● Scattering = light ka particles se takrakar alag direction mein bikharna. [Q44, Q104, Q123]\n● Particle SIZE pe depend karta hai. [Q182]\n● Fine particles (dust, gas molecules) → shorter wavelengths (blue) ko zyada scatter karte hain. Isliye sky blue\ndikhta hai. [Q44, Q51, Q104, Q123, Q162]\n● Bade particles (clouds, milk, water droplets) → sabhi colours ko almost equally scatter karte hain (Mie scattering),\nisliye white dikhte hain. [Q43, Q67, Q104, Q214]\n● Red light ki wavelength sabse zyada hoti hai, isliye fog/smoke se sabse kam scattered hota hai — isliye danger\nsignals mein red use hota hai. [Q49, Q181]\n● Red sunset/sunrise ka reason bhi scattering hai — atmosphere se hokar guzarne mein blue light scatter ho jaati\nhai, bachi hui red light aankhon tak pahunchti hai. [Q84, Q160]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Atmosphere na hone par (space mein/outer space) sky black dikhega kyunki scattering karne wale\nparticles hi maujood nahi hain, isliye scattering hoti hi nahi. [Q51, Q81, Q243]\n10. Atmospheric Refraction & Twinkling\n● Atmospheric refraction: atmosphere ki different layers (temperature/density) ki wajah se light ka bend hona.\n[Q41, Q46, Q54, Q60, Q75, Q129]\n● Stars twinkle karte hain kyunki unki apparent position actual position se thodi upar (higher) hoti hai aur\ncontinuously change hoti rehti hai. [Q11, Q46, Q60, Q129]\n● Planets twinkle nahi karte kyunki ye extended source hain (point source nahi), intensity variation noticeable nahi\nhota. [Q14]\n● Sunrise/sunset mein sun ka disk chapta (flattened) dikhta hai aur hum sun ko 2 minutes pehle dekh paate hain\n(actual sunrise se) aur 2 minutes baad tak (actual sunset ke baad) — atmospheric refraction ki wajah se. [Q41,\nQ54, Q168]\n● Aag ke upar garam hawa mein objects waver/shimmer karte hain — yeh bhi atmospheric refraction hai. [Q75]\n11. Human Eye, Vision Defects & Corrective Lenses\n● Eye ka lens (crystalline lens) + cornea milkar light ko refract karke retina par focus karte hain. [Q188]\n● Retina par image real aur inverted banta hai; brain use process karke upright samajhta hai. [Q242]\n● Iris pupil ka size control karke light ki quantity regulate karti hai. [Q223]\n● Ciliary body lens ki shape change karke focal length adjust karti hai (accommodation). [Q229]\n● Accommodation = eye lens ki ability to adjust focal length so that near aur distant objects dono retina par focus\nho sakein. [Q155]\n● Least distance of distinct vision = 25 cm normal healthy eyes ke liye. [Q155]\n● Myopia (Nearsightedness) = distant objects blurry; image retina ke aage banta hai. Cause: eyeball ka elongation\nya eye lens ki excessive curvature. Correction: concave lens. [Q152, Q236]\n● Hypermetropia (Farsightedness) = near objects blurry; image retina ke peechhe banta hai. Correction: convex\nlens. [Q152, Q241]\n● Presbyopia = dono problems ek saath; correction: bifocal lens (myopia + hypermetropia dono ke liye). [Q213]\n● Human eye ki image formation refraction principle par based hai. [Q160]\n● Chashma / spectacles refraction principle par kaam karte hain. [Q116]"," 12. Real-Life Applications of Mirrors & Lenses\n● Concave mirror uses:\n– Torches, searchlights, vehicle headlights (bulb at focus → parallel beam). [Q166, Q257, Q264]\n– Shaving mirrors (virtual erect magnified image jab paas ho). [Q172]\n– Dentist mirrors (virtual erect enlarged teeth image). [Q140, Q154, Q179, Q215]\n– Solar furnaces (sunlight ko focus par converge). [Q140, Q191]\n– Dish antennas (receiver at focus). [Q87]\n● Convex mirror uses:\n– Rear-view mirrors (wider field of view, virtual erect diminished). [Q140, Q167]\n– Security mirrors in stores/parking lots. [Q240]\n– Street lights mein as reflector taaki light zyada area mein spread ho. [Q140]\n● Plane mirror uses:\n– Looking glasses, periscopes, kaleidoscopes. [Q167]\n● Magnifying glass = convex lens of short focal length. [Q231]\n● Magic mirror concept: Head bada dikhne ke liye concave (enlarged), body same size ke liye plane, legs chhote\ndikhne ke liye convex mirror. [Q25, Q148]\n– Reverse order (head same, body chhota, legs bada) → Plane, Convex, Concave. [Q148]\n● Photolysis (light se hone wala decomposition reaction, jaise photosynthesis mein water ka breakdown) light-\ndriven chemical process ka example hai — GK crossover fact jo light ke practical/chemical effect ko test karta hai.\n[Q206]\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1–Q273)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Concave mirror converging hota hai lekin iski focal length negative hoti hai; convex mirror diverging hota\nhai lekin focal length positive. Ulta mat samajhna! [Q5, Q10, Q18, Q50, Q72, Q76, Q144, Q246, Q250]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Convex mirror hamesha virtual, erect, diminished image banata hai — enlarged kabhi nahi. [Q39, Q125,\nQ135, Q140, Q221, Q259]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Concave mirror mostly real inverted image banata hai, lekin jab object pole aur focus ke beech ho to\nvirtual, erect, enlarged banta hai. [Q130, Q135, Q169, Q195]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mirror ki focal length medium change se nahi badalti; lens ki badalti hai. [Q258]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Prism mein angle of incidence = angle of emergence sirf minimum deviation par hota hai, hamesha nahi.\n[Q62, Q122]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Glass slab mein incident aur emergent ray parallel hoti hain, prism mein nahi. [Q29, Q193]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Object concave mirror ke focus par ho to image infinity par real inverted banegi (highly enlarged), virtual\nnahi. [Q52, Q220]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fine particles → blue scatter; Large particles → red scatter; Very large → white (equal). [Q43, Q44, Q67,\nQ104, Q214]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Setting sun ka red colour = scattering hai, refraction nahi. [Q160]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rainbow formation: RRC key ke mutabiq refraction + scattering + dispersion (traditional TIR alag concept\nhai). [Q120, Q171]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Normal incidence (0°) par direction nahi badalti, sirf speed badalti hai. [Q114]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Optical centre se guzarne wali ray un-deviated rehti hai; principal focus se hokar nahi. [Q142, Q189, Q238]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnification +3.0 (positive) ka matlab virtual erect enlarged — convex lens ya concave mirror dono de\nsakte hain. [Q111]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sign convention mein right of origin = positive, left = negative. [Q196]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Angle with surface vs angle with normal confusion — scientific answer alag ho sakta hai official key se"," (jaise Q192 mein 30° surface angle par official answer 30° tha, jabki scientifically 60° hona chahiye tha). [Q192]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Real image = actual intersection of rays; virtual = apparent intersection. [Q253]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Moon non-luminous hai (sunlight reflect karti hai); Sun, bulb, candle, firefly luminous hain. [Q265, Q226]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: TV remote mein Infrared (IR) light use hoti hai, visible nahi. [Q174]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: LASER = Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation. [Q165]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solar power systems Photovoltaic effect par kaam karti hain. [Q159]\n14. Numerical: Mirror Formula (Image/Object Distance)\n● Mirror Formula: 1/f = 1/u + 1/v (yaad rakho: uv/(u+v) = f). [Q274, Q275, Q282, Q293, Q299, Q302, Q304, Q323, Q335,\nQ339, Q340, Q351, Q361]\n● Convex mirror ke liye f hamesha positive; image behind mirror banega isliye v positive. Example: f=+2m, u=-3m →\n1/v = 1/2 + 1/3 = 5/6 → v = +1.2 m (behind mirror). [Q275]\n● Concave mirror ke liye f aur v (real image ke liye) negative hote hain. Example: f=-20cm, v=-60cm → 1/u = -1/20 +\n1/60 = -2/60 → u = -30 cm. [Q282]\n● Agar object focus aur C ke beech ho (between f aur 2f) → real inverted enlarged image beyond C par banega.\n[Q286, Q324]\n● Agar object C se pare ho (beyond 2f) → real inverted diminished image F aur C ke beech. [Q302, Q335]\n● Agar object infinity par ho → image focus par, highly diminished. Satellite wale question mein u = -10⁵ m, hi =\n-5μm → f ≈ -0.5 m. [Q346]\n● Newton's Formula for mirrors: Agar object focus se x door ho aur image focus se y door ho, toh f² = xy ya f = √(xy).\nObject distance = f + x, image distance = f + y. [Q320]\n● Concave mirror mein parallel beam converge hoti hai focal point par, jahan f = R/2. Example: R=0.8m → f=0.4m,\nisliye rays mirror ke saamne 0.4 m par converge hogi. [Q318]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Shaving mirror question (Q326) mein official answer ne m = -1.33 (real image) maana, jabki logically\nvirtual hona chahiye tha. Exam mein official key follow karo. [Q326]\n15. Numerical: Lens Formula (Image/Object Distance)\n● Lens Formula: 1/f = 1/v - 1/u (ya 1/v - 1/u = 1/f). [Q274, Q280, Q283, Q288, Q291, Q297, Q301, Q315, Q322, Q332, Q343,\nQ345, Q352, Q359]\n● Convex lens mein object 2F (2f) par ho → image bhi 2F par, same size, real inverted (m = -1). Example: u=-40cm,\nf=+20cm → v = +40 cm. [Q301, Q322]\n● Convex lens mein object F aur 2F ke beech (jaise u=-12cm, f=8cm) → image beyond 2F par, enlarged. v = +24 cm,\nheight = 2 cm (magnification -2). [Q291]\n● Convex lens mein object F ke andar (u < f) → virtual erect enlarged image same side par. Example: P=+5D\n(f=20cm), u=-10cm → v = -20 cm (virtual). [Q315]\n● Concave lens hamesha virtual, erect, diminished image banata hai. Example: f=-20cm, u=-10cm → v = -20/3 cm, m\n= +2/3 (<1). [Q288]\n● Power = -10D (concave lens), u=-15cm → f=-10cm. Image hamesha virtual aur erect hi banegi. [Q297]\n● Concave lens: f=-15cm, u=-30cm → 1/v = -1/15 + 1/30 = -1/30 → v = -10 cm. [Q352]\n16. Numerical: Power of Lens & Combined Power (Doublet)\n● Power formula: P = 1/f (f in meters); unit = Dioptre (D). [Q277, Q281, Q300, Q309, Q343, Q349, Q350, Q358, Q360]"," ● Convex lens → P positive; Concave lens → P negative. [Q277, Q309, Q358]\n● Example: f=25cm=0.25m → P = 1/0.25 = +4 D. [Q350]\n● Example: f=50cm=0.5m → P = 1/0.5 = +2 D. [Q360]\n● Example: P = -6.5 D → f = 1/(-6.5) = -0.1538 m = -15.38 cm. [Q349]\n● Combined Power (lenses in contact): P = P1 + P2.\n– Convex (+5D) + Concave (-3D) → P = +2 D → f = 1/2 m = 50 cm. [Q281]\n– Convex (+2D) + Concave (-5D) → P = -3 D. [Q300]\n– Doublet: f1=+20cm (+5D), f2=-50cm (-2D) → P = +3 D, F = 33.3 cm. [Q343]\n● Combined focal length formula: 1/F = 1/f1 + 1/f2 (with proper signs). [Q300]\n17. Numerical: Magnification Problems (Height/Diameter)\n● Mirror magnification: m = -v/u = hi/ho. [Q274, Q286, Q289, Q302, Q304, Q307, Q316, Q325, Q326, Q327, Q328, Q335, Q337,\nQ339, Q340, Q351, Q354, Q362]\n● Lens magnification: m = v/u = hi/ho. [Q274, Q280, Q283, Q288, Q291, Q314, Q315, Q322, Q332, Q345]\n●\n\n⚠️Difference: Mirror mein m = -v/u (negative sign extra); Lens mein m = v/u (bina negative sign ke directly).\n[Q313]\n● m negative → real inverted; m positive → virtual erect. [Q200, Q274]\n● Example (Lens): u=-25cm, v=+30cm → m = 30/(-25) = -6/5 (real, inverted, enlarged). [Q274]\n● Example (Mirror): u=-30cm, m=+1.5 → 1.5 = -v/(-30) → v = +45 cm (behind mirror, virtual). [Q325]\n● Example (Concave mirror): u=-5cm, real image 3× → m=-3 → -3 = -v/(-5) → v = -15 cm. [Q351]\n● Object height × |m| = Image height. Example: ho=6cm, m=2/3 → hi = 4 cm. [Q332]\n● Diameter same formula: di = |m| × do. Example: do=10cm, m=-1 → di = 10 cm. [Q322]\n● Convex mirror mein object 3.5f par ho → m = -2/5, do=10cm → di = 4 cm. [Q335]\n● Christmas ball (convex mirror): D=10cm → R=5cm → f=+2.5cm. m=+0.5 → u = -2.5 cm. [Q316]\n18. Numerical: Sign Convention, Focal Length & R = 2f\n● R = 2f hamesha valid hai spherical mirrors ke liye. [Q285, Q303, Q305, Q311, Q353, Q356]\n● Concave mirror: f = negative, R = negative. Example: R=12cm → f = -6 cm. [Q295, Q296]\n● Convex mirror: f = positive, R = positive. Example: R=15cm → f = +7.5 cm; C = +30 cm. [Q290, Q292, Q298, Q305]\n● Agar R double ho jaaye → f bhi double ho jaata hai (directly proportional). [Q311]\n● PC (Pole to Centre) = 2 × PF (Pole to Focus). [Q303]\n● FC (Focus to Centre) = f (kyunki PC=2f, PF=f, toh FC = 2f-f = f). [Q305]\n● Formula derivation: 1/f = (u+v)/uv → f = uv/(u+v) → R = 2uv/(u+v). [Q285]\n● f = -24cm (concave) → R = -48 cm. [Q296]\n● f = +15cm (convex) → C = +30 cm. [Q298]\n19. Numerical: Refractive Index, Snell's Law & Relative RI\n● Snell's Law: n = sin i / sin r = c/v = v1/v2 (relative). [Q276, Q278, Q284, Q287, Q294, Q306, Q308, Q310, Q319, Q329, Q330,\nQ334, Q341, Q344]\n● Relative RI: n_A w.r.t B = n_A / n_B = v_B / v_A. [Q278, Q287, Q294, Q310, Q319]"," ● Example: n_glass=1.52, n_turpentine=1.47 → n_glass w.r.t turpentine = 1.52/1.47 = 1.03. [Q287]\n● Example: n_ice=1.31, n_glass=1.52 → n_glass w.r.t ice = 1.52/1.31 = 1.16. [Q294]\n● Example: n_A=3/2, n_B=4/3 → n_A w.r.t B = (3/2)/(4/3) = 9/8. [Q310]\n● Speed relation: n 1/v. Jitna zyada RI, utni kam speed.\n∝\n [Q278, Q319]\n– n1=1.50, n2=1.36, n3=1.54 → Speed order: v2 > v1 > v3. [Q319]\n● Air se water (n=1.3) mein: sin y / sin x = 1/1.3. Agar 30° angle se light air se paani mein enter kare (n=1.33), toh\nrefracted angle 30° se kam banega aur ray incident ray ke same plane mein rahegi. [Q284, Q306, Q334]\n● Optical fibre: n=1.45, i=22° → sin r = sin(22°)/1.45 ≈ 0.2583 → r ≈ 14.99°. [Q329]\n● i=60°, n=√3 → sin r = sin(60°)/√3 = (√3/2)/√3 = 1/2 → r = 30°. [Q308]\n● i=60°, n=3/2 → sin r = sin(60°)/(3/2) = (√3/2)×(2/3) = 1/√2 → r = 45°. [Q344]\n● i=75°, r=40° → n_A w.r.t B = sin(40°)/sin(75°) ≈ 0.642/0.965 ≈ 0.67. [Q341]\n● Wavelength method: μ = λ_air / λ_medium = 600/380 = 1.58. [Q330]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Agar ray normal se door mudd rahi hai (denser→rarer) → relative RI < 1 (0 < n < 1). [Q312]\n20. Numerical: Speed of Light in Medium\n● Formula: v = c/n = (3 × 10⁸) / n. [Q278, Q279, Q333, Q347, Q355]\n● n=1.5 → v = 3×10⁸/1.5 = 2 × 10⁸ m/s. [Q279, Q355]\n● n=1.33 (water) → v = 3×10⁸/1.33 = 2.26 × 10⁸ m/s. [Q333]\n● n=2.42 (diamond) → v = 3×10⁸/2.42 = 1.24 × 10⁸ m/s. [Q347]\n● Two media speeds given: v_A=2×10⁸, v_B=2.25×10⁸ → n_A w.r.t B = v_B/v_A = 2.25/2 = 1.125. [Q278]\n21. Numerical: Apparent Depth & Real Depth\n● Formula: n = Real Depth / Apparent Depth. [Q342]\n● Real depth = 30 cm, n=1.33 → Apparent depth = 30/1.33 = 22.6 cm. [Q342]\n● Object apparent depth par kam gehra (shallower) dikhta hai — yeh refraction ka result hai (denser medium ka\nbottom hamesha upar shift dikhta hai). [Q106]\n22. Numerical: Critical Angle\n● Formula: sin(Ic) = 1/n (denser→rarer, air ke liye n=1). [Q336]\n● n=1.56 (flint glass) → sin(Ic) = 1/1.56 ≈ 0.64. [Q336]\n23. Numerical: Graph-Based & Formula Derivation Problems\n● 1/v vs 1/u graph (mirror): Equation 1/v + 1/u = 1/f.\n– y-intercept = 1/f. Agar y-intercept = 0.11 → f = 1/0.11 = 9.09 cm. [Q338]\n● u vs 1/m graph (mirror): Straight line with slope +f, x-intercept -1, y-intercept +f. [Q348]\n● m vs v graph: Straight line with slope +1/f, x-intercept +f, y-intercept -1 (concave mirror ke liye). [Q117]\n● Dispersion: D 1/λ³. Agar λ' = 3λ → D' = D/(3)³ = D/27.\n∝\n [Q317]"," ● Shift problems (screen & object): m=2 → v=3f; m=5 → v=6f; screen shift d=3f. Agar d given hai → f = d/3.\n– Q340: d=39cm → 3f=39 → f=13 cm. [Q340]\n– Q327: d=24cm → 3f=24 → f=8cm; object shift = f/6 = 4/3 cm. [Q327]\n– Q321: d → object shift = d/10. [Q321]\n24. Numerical: Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mirror magnification = -v/u; Lens magnification = v/u (bina negative sign). Difference mat bhoolna!\n[Q313]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sign convention — Concave mirror/lens ka f negative; Convex mirror/lens ka f positive. [Q282, Q292,\nQ295, Q296, Q298]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Object hamesha left side par rakha jaata hai → u hamesha negative (New Cartesian). [Q274, Q282]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Angle with mirror surface vs angle with normal. Mirror se 20° ka matlab normal se 70° (i=70°, r=70°,\ntotal angle = 140°). [Q357]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Agar numerical mein object focus ke andar ho concave mirror mein → virtual erect enlarged image\nbehind mirror (v positive). [Q325]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mirror ki focal length medium change se nahi badalti; lens ki badalti hai. [Q258]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Official answer key kabhi-kabhi physics se alag ho sakti hai (jaise Q192, Q326, Q331, Q312). Solve karke\nofficial answer match karo. [Q312, Q326, Q331]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Convex mirror hamesha positive f aur positive v deta hai (virtual image behind mirror). [Q275, Q289,\nQ304, Q323]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Agar question mein diameter ya height pucha ho aur object ka size given ho → pehle m nikalo, fir\nmultiply kar do. [Q315, Q322, Q332, Q337, Q345, Q362]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 1 Light and Optics Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0404","t":"02 Heat and Thermodynamics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.2 — HEAT AND THERMODYNAMICS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌡️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Joule's Law of Heating: Formula & Applications\n2. Thermal Properties of Materials\n3. Temperature Scales & Conversions (Conceptual + Numerical)\n4. Change of State: Melting, Fusion & Latent Heat\n5. Power Plants & Energy Sources\n6.\n Traps / Key Differences & Formula Cheat Sheet (Q363–Q380)\n⚠️\n1. Joule's Law of Heating: Formula & Applications\n● Joule's Law of Heating: Circuit mein resistance dwara electrical energy ko heat energy mein convert karne ki rate\nH = I²RT se di jaati hai. [Q363, Q371, Q374]\n– H = Heat produced (joules mein), I = Current flowing, R = Resistance of conductor, T = Time period of current\nflow. [Q374]\n● Is principle par kaam karne wale devices: Immersion rod, Electric iron, Electric kettle, Electric toaster, Electric\noven, Electric heater, Electric bulb, Electric fuse. [Q363, Q365, Q371, Q372]\n● NOT based on Joule's heating:\n– Electric bell → magnetic effect of current par kaam karta hai, thermal effect par nahi. [Q363, Q372]\n– Electromagnet → magnetic effect par based hai. [Q363]\n– Speaker → electromagnetic induction par based hai. [Q363]\n– Electric plugs and switches → simple connectors/mechanical devices hain, heating principle par nahi. [Q365]\n● Fuse bhi Joule's heating principle par kaam karta hai — jyada current flow hone par wire heat hokar melt ho jaata\nhai, circuit break ho jaata hai. [Q365]\n2. Thermal Properties of Materials\n● Tungsten (Wolfram) ka melting point sabse zyada kisi bhi metal mein — 3422°C. [Q364]\n– Isliye bulb filaments mein use hota hai — badi heat ke bawajood melt nahi hota. [Q364]\n– Tungsten exceptionally strong aur brittle hota hai. [Q364]\n– Iska thermal expansion coefficient sabse kam hai kisi bhi metal mein. [Q364]\n● Specific Heat Capacity: Ek gram substance ka temperature 1°C badhane ke liye kitni heat chahiye. [Q368]\n– Water ki specific heat sabse zyada common substances mein — 4.186 J/g°C. Isliye water climate regulate\nkarne mein madad karta hai. [Q368]\n– Order: Water > Snow/Ice > Aluminum > Kerosene (roughly). [Q368]\n3. Temperature Scales & Conversions (Conceptual + Numerical)\n● Teen common temperature scales: Fahrenheit (°F), Celsius (°C), Kelvin (K). Kelvin = SI unit of temperature. [Q369]\n● Conversion formulas (hamesha yaad rakho):\n– K → C: C = K − 273.15 (ya approximately K − 273). [Q369, Q376]"," – C → K: K = C + 273.15 (ya approximately C + 273). [Q369, Q376, Q379, Q380]\n– C → F: F = (9/5)C + 32. [Q369, Q375, Q377, Q378]\n– F → C: C = (F − 32) × 5/9. [Q369, Q375]\n● Important fixed points:\n– Absolute Zero = 0 K = −273.15°C = −459.67°F — temperature ka theoretical minimum jahan molecular motion\nruk jaati hai. [Q376]\n– Water freezing point = 0°C = 273.15 K ≈ 32°F. [Q369, Q378]\n– Water boiling point (sea level) = 100°C = 373.15 K ≈ 212°F. [Q369, Q379]\n– Normal human body temperature = 37°C = 98.6°F = 310.15 K. [Q367, Q369, Q375]\n– Standard room temperature = 20°C = 293 K ≈ 68°F. [Q380]\n● Numerical examples:\n– 37°C → °F: F = (9/5)×37 + 32 = 66.6 + 32 = 98.6°F. [Q375]\n– −200°C → °F: F = (9/5)×(−200) + 32 = −360 + 32 = −328°F. [Q377]\n– 0°C → °F: F = (9/5)×0 + 32 = 32°F. [Q378]\n– 100°C → K: K = 100 + 273 = 373 K. [Q379]\n– 20°C → K: K = 20 + 273 = 293 K. [Q380]\n– −273.15°C → K: K = −273.15 + 273.15 = 0 K (Absolute Zero). [Q376]\n● Inventors yaad rakho: Anders Celsius → Celsius scale; Lord Kelvin → Kelvin scale (1848 mein). [Q379]\n● Ignition temperature = wo minimum temperature jis par fuel aag pakad ke jalna shuru kar de — Neutral\ntemperature aur Boiling temperature dono alag concepts hain. [Q367]\n4. Change of State: Melting, Fusion & Latent Heat\n● Melting (Fusion) ke dauran temperature change nahi hota — supplied heat intermolecular bonds todne mein use\nhoti hai. [Q370, Q373]\n● Latent Heat of Fusion = unit mass ko solid se liquid mein convert karne ke liye heat energy (bina temperature\nchange ke). SI unit = J/kg. [Q370]\n● 0°C par liquid water ke particles mein ice ke particles se zyada energy hoti hai kyunki ice ne fusion ke dauran\nlatent heat absorb ki hai apne surroundings se.\n– Yeh absorbed energy ice crystals ke bonds todne mein gayi, jisse water molecules ki potential energy badh\ngayi. [Q373]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Temperature same (0°C) rehta hai dono states mein, lekin energy alag hai kyunki latent heat\nabsorb/release hoti hai. [Q370, Q373]\n5. Power Plants & Energy Sources\n● Thermal power plant = fossil fuels (coal, oil, gas) jalakar steam banate hain jo turbines chalata hai. [Q366]\n● Nuclear power plant = nuclear fission se heat generate hoti hai (atoms split hote hain reactor mein). [Q366]\n● Hydro electric power plant = renewable source; dam se water flow alter karke turbines chalate hain. [Q366]\n● Solar power plant = solar radiation (light + heat) ko electricity mein convert karte hain. [Q366]\n6.\n Traps / Key Differences & Formula Cheat Sheet (Q363–Q380)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Electric bell magnetic effect par kaam karta hai, Joule's heating par nahi — baar-baar galat hota hai."," [Q363, Q372]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Joule's heating formula H = I²RT hai — sirf I²R ya IRt nahi. Time (T) bhi factor hai. [Q371]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tungsten ka melting point 3422°C hai — 300°C ya 1000°C nahi. [Q364]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Melting ke dauran temperature constant rehta hai — increase ya decrease nahi hota. [Q370]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kelvin se Celsius mein convert karne ke liye 273 subtract karte hain, add nahi. [Q369, Q376]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Water ki specific heat sabse zyada hoti hai common substances mein — yaad rakho. [Q368]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ignition temperature = fuel jalne ka minimum temp; Boiling temperature = alag cheez; Neutral\ntemperature = thermocouple ka concept. [Q367]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Absolute zero 0 K = −273.15°C hai — −273 K nahi. [Q376]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Celsius se Fahrenheit formula mein 32 add hota hai, subtract nahi. [Q375, Q377, Q378]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 2 Heat and Thermodynamics Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0405","t":"03 Fluid Mechanics","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.3 — FLUID MECHANICS — FULL MIND MAP\n🌊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Branches of Fluid Mechanics\n2. Archimedes' Principle: Float, Sink & Upthrust\n3. Density, Relative Density & Buoyant Force Formula\n4. Capillarity, Viscosity & Evaporation\n5. Ice-Water Volume Problem & Physical States\n6. Real-Life Applications\n7. Numerical Formulas: Buoyant Force & Pump Power\n8.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (Q381–Q404)\n⚠️\n1. Branches of Fluid Mechanics\n● Hydrostatics = fluid (gas ya liquid) ke rest (vishram) avastha ke properties ka adhyayan — specially pressure in\nfluid ya immersed body par fluid dwara lagaya gaya pressure. [Q381]\n● Hydrodynamics = fluid ke motion (gati) ka adhyayan. [Q381]\n● Optics = light ke behavior aur properties ka adhyayan; Thermodynamics = heat aur energy ke beech relation;\nAstrophysics = celestial objects ke physical properties. [Q381]\n2. Archimedes' Principle: Float, Sink & Upthrust\n● Archimedes' Principle: Jab koi body fluid mein partially ya fully immersed hoti hai, toh us par ek upward buoyant\nforce lagta hai jo displaced fluid ke weight ke barabar hota hai. [Q383, Q386, Q391, Q393, Q395, Q401]\n● Buoyant force (Upthrust) = Fb = ρ × g × V, jahan:\n– ρ = fluid ka density, g = acceleration due to gravity, V = displaced volume (object ka submerged volume).\n[Q387, Q396, Q401]\n● Buoyant force ka magnitude fluid ke density aur displaced volume par depend karta hai — direction hamesha\nupward hoti hai. [Q387]\n● Float vs Sink rules:\n– Object floats → jab object ka density liquid se kam ho. [Q385, Q388, Q390, Q400]\n– Object sinks → jab object ka density liquid se zyada ho. [Q385, Q394, Q398]\n– Same density → object liquid mein kahi bhi suspend ho sakta hai (neither float nor sink completely). [Q388]\n● Floating object ka apparent weight = Zero hota hai kyunki buoyant force exactly weight ke barabar hoti hai.\n[Q389]\n● Sinking object ke liye buoyant force object ke weight se kam hota hai. [Q394]\n● Object 1/3 volume submerged ho to float kare → object ka density = (1/3) × water density. [Q391]\n● Spring balance reading (apparent weight) = Actual weight − Buoyant force = mg − ρgV. [Q397, Q401]\n– Jab object completely submerged ho → maximum fluid displaced → maximum buoyant force → minimum\napparent weight. [Q397]\n– Partially submerged ya surface par hone par kam buoyant force → zyada apparent weight. [Q397]"," 3. Density, Relative Density & Buoyant Force Formula\n● Density (ρ) = mass/volume; SI unit = kg/m³. [Q385, Q388, Q392]\n● Iron nail ka density ≈ 7.8 g/cm³; water ka density = 1 g/cm³ (25°C par). [Q398]\n● Relative Density = substance ka density / reference substance ka density; unitless hota hai. [Q392]\n● Ice ka density water se kam hota hai (≈0.92 g/cm³) — isliye ice floats; iska unique crystalline structure hai. [Q400]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Generally solids liquids se zyada dense hote hain, lekin water exception hai — ice (solid) liquid water se\nkam dense hoti hai. [Q400]\n4. Capillarity, Viscosity & Evaporation\n● Capillarity = liquids ka narrow spaces/tubes mein gravity ke against rise ya draw hone ka phenomenon. [Q382]\n– Examples: Kerosene oil lantern ki wick mein upar chadhna, blotting paper se ink absorb hona, plants mein\nwater roots se leaves tak jaana. [Q382]\n– NOT capillarity: Osmosis = semipermeable membrane se solvent ka movement; Diffusion = high concentration\nse low concentration mein molecules ka movement. [Q382]\n● Viscosity = fluid ke flow ka resistance; liquid ka \"internal friction\". [Q384]\n– SI unit = N·s/m² ya Pascal-second (Pa·s). [Q384]\n– High viscosity examples: Honey, Molasses, Melted chocolate, Engine oil. [Q384]\n– NOT viscosity: Rigidity = solid ka shape na badal paana; Morbidity = disease related; Rancidity = fat/oil ka spoil\nhona. [Q384]\n● Evaporation = liquid ka vapour mein convert hona boiling point se niche ke temperature par. [Q399]\n– Liquid ke surface ke kuch particles mein zyada kinetic energy hoti hai — ye particles attraction force break\nkarke vapour ban jaate hain. Evaporation cooling effect deta hai. [Q399]\n5. Ice-Water Volume Problem & Physical States\n● Glass completely water aur ice se bhara ho aur ice melt ho jaye → water level same rehta hai. [Q393]\n– Reason: Floating ice apne weight ke barabar water displace karti hai; melt hone par bhi wahi volume ka water\nbanegi. [Q393]\n● Water ke 3 states:\n– Solid (Ice) → 0°C se niche. [Q402]\n– Liquid (Water) → 0°C se 100°C ke beech. [Q402]\n– Gas (Steam/Vapour) → 100°C se upar. [Q402]\n● 12°C par water liquid state mein hota hai. [Q402]\n● Water (H₂O) covalent bonds se bana; polar nature; amphoteric; universal solvent (high dielectric constant ki\nwajah se). [Q402]\n6. Real-Life Applications\n● Archimedes' Principle par based:\n– Ships & Submarines ki designing. [Q383]\n– Lactometers → milk ki purity check karne ke liye. [Q383, Q386]\n– Hydrometers → liquid ka density measure karne ke liye; weighted sealed glass bulb hota hai — flotation depth"," density batata hai. [Q383, Q386]\n– Boat sailing, Iceberg floating, Helium balloon rising. [Q387]\n● Bernoulli's Principle par based (NOT Archimedes'):\n– Airplane wings ki designing — aerodynamics. [Q383]\n– Periscope → Laws of Reflection par based. [Q386]\n– Potentiometer → potential difference directly proportional to wire length. [Q386]\n7. Numerical Formulas: Buoyant Force & Pump Power\n● Buoyant Force numerical mein direct formula:\n– Fb = Weight in air − Weight in liquid (apparent weight loss). [Q403]\n– Example: Air mein 4 N, water mein 2 N → Fb = 4 − 2 = 2 N. [Q403]\n– Yeh Archimedes' principle ka practical application hai — buoyant force utna hi hota hai jitna weight reduce\nhota hai. [Q403]\n● Pump Power numerical:\n– Formula: Power = Work done / Time = (m × g × h) / t. [Q404]\n– Example: Power = 1 kW = 1000 W, g = 10 m/s², h = 10 m, t = 60 s. 1000 = (m × 10 × 10) / 60 → m = (1000 ×\n60) / 100 = 600 kg. [Q404]\n– Unit check karte raho: Power in Watts, time in seconds, mass in kg, g in m/s², h in meters. [Q404]\n8.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (Q381–Q404)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Airplane wings Bernoulli's principle par based hain, Archimedes' principle par nahi. [Q383]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Buoyant force = ρ × g × V; object ka mass nahi, displaced volume (V) use hota hai. [Q396]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Object float karega jab uska density liquid se kam ho; sink karega jab zyada ho; same density ho toh\nsuspend. [Q388, Q390]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ice melt hone par water level same rehta hai — increase ya decrease nahi hota. [Q393]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Spring balance ka minimum reading tab aata hai jab object completely submerged ho (max buoyant\nforce). [Q397]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Apparent weight = mg − ρgV; zero tab hota hai jab object float kare. [Q389, Q401]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Capillarity ≠ Osmosis ≠ Diffusion — teeno alag-alag phenomena hain. [Q382]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Viscosity = liquid ka internal friction; Rigidity = solid ka property. [Q384]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ice ka density water se kam hota hai — yeh water ka unique property hai (generally solids liquids se\nzyada dense hote hain). [Q400]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Numerical mein time hamesha seconds mein convert karo — 1 minute = 60 s. [Q404]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Buoyant force = Weight loss (air weight − liquid weight); direct subtraction se nikalta hai. [Q403]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 3 Fluid Mechanics Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0406","t":"04 Electric Current","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.4 — ELECTRIC CURRENT AND ITS EFFECTS — FULL MIND MAP\n⚡\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Bulb Filament: Material, Properties & Resistance Formula\n2. Solenoid: Magnetic Field & Applications\n3. Fleming's Left-Hand Rule vs Right-Hand Rule\n4. Magnetic Field Lines: Properties & Patterns\n5. Electromagnetic Induction: Faraday's Law & Lenz's Law\n6. Resistance: Formula, Factors, Resistivity & Temperature\n7. Ohm's Law & V-I Graphs\n8. Series vs Parallel Circuits\n9. DC Motor, DC Generator & AC Generator\n10. Force on Conductor\n11. Heating Effect of Electric Current (Joule's Law)\n12. Ammeter, Voltmeter & Galvanometer\n13. Fuse: Principle, Material & Rating\n14. Conductors, Insulators, Semiconductors & Superconductors\n15. Energy Conversions\n16. Coulomb's Law\n17. Electric Current Basics\n18. Magnetic Compass & Field Detection\n19. Oersted's Experiment, Medical Imaging, Electroplating & Solutions\n20. Power Formula & Basic Components\n21.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q405–Q632)\n⚠️\n22. Numerical: Ohm's Law (V = IR)\n23. Numerical: Resistance Formula (R = ρl/A) & Wire Stretching\n24. Numerical: Series & Parallel Resistance Combinations\n25. Numerical: Electric Power (P = VI = I²R = V²/R)\n26. Numerical: Heat/Energy (H = I²Rt = VIt = V²t/R)\n27. Numerical: Charge & Current (Q = It)\n28. Numerical: Work Done (W = QV)\n29. Numerical: Energy Units (kWh\n Joules)\n⇄\n30. Numerical: Bulb Brightness & Power Ratings\n31. Numerical: Cost Calculation & Fuse Rating\n32. Numerical: Induced EMF, Coulomb's Law, Magnetic Field & Electrons\n33. Numerical: Wire Doubled on Itself\n34. Numerical: Temperature Conversion & Cross-Topic Numericals\n35.\n Traps / Master Formula Cheat Sheet (Numerical Q633–Q835)\n⚠️\n1. Bulb Filament: Material, Properties & Resistance Formula\n● Bulb filament mein Tungsten (W, atomic no. 74) use hota hai kyunki iska melting point sabse zyada (≈3380°C–\n3422°C) kisi bhi metal mein. [Q364, Q405, Q418, Q543, Q599]\n● Filament ko thin aur long banaya jaata hai taaki resistance zyada ho — R = ρl/A (lamba length l + chhota cross-\nsectional area A = zyada R). [Q405]\n● High resistance se zyada heat aur light produce hoti hai; temperature zyada = efficiency zyada = light safed\n(white). [Q405, Q556]\n● Filament material ke liye zaroori properties: High melting point, high resistivity, high temperature par glow karne\nki ability, ductile nature, easily oxidize na hona. [Q418]"," ● Bulb mein chemically inactive gases fill hoti hain: Nitrogen (N₂) aur Argon (Ar) — filament ki oxidation aur\nevaporation prevent karne ke liye. [Q405, Q583, Q606]\n● Hydrogen, Oxygen, Chlorine reactive hain → bulb mein use nahi hote. [Q583]\n● First commercial electric bulb: Thomas Alva Edison (1879). [Q543, Q599]\n● Bulb glow karta hai kyunki filament current se heat hokar high temperature tak pahunchta hai (Joule heating).\n[Q556]\n● Incandescent lamp = heating effect par based hai; electric geyser bhi. [Q417, Q420]\n2. Solenoid: Magnetic Field & Applications\n● Solenoid = tightly packed helix mein wound coil; electromagnet ki tarah kaam karta hai jab current flow hoti hai.\n[Q406, Q430, Q433, Q439, Q452, Q502]\n● Solenoid bar magnet ki tarah behave karta hai — ek end North pole, doosra South pole. [Q406, Q433]\n● Solenoid ka strong magnetic field soft iron ko magnetize karne ke liye use ho sakta hai. [Q406, Q452]\n● Solenoid ke andar field lines parallel straight lines hain → magnetic field uniform aur non-zero hota hai, isliye ek\nuniform field indicate karta hai. [Q406, Q430, Q452, Q463, Q502, Q505, Q576]\n● Solenoid ke andar field lines concentric circles nahi hain; ye straight conductor ke liye hoti hain. [Q406]\n● Solenoid ka magnetic field strength formula: B = μ₀NI/l = μ₀nI, jahan n = turns per unit length, I = current, l =\nlength. So B nI.\n∝\n [Q439, Q463, Q488, Q490]\n● B depends on: Current (I), Number of turns (N/n), Length (l inversely), Core material permeability. Circular coil ka\nfield bhi turns (n) ke directly proportional hota hai — jitne zyada turns, utna strong field. [Q439, Q446, Q474, Q488,\nQ490, Q503]\n● Soft iron core ka use: magnetic permeability bahut high hoti hai → field greatly amplify hota hai; length of\nmetallic core aur current bhi electromagnet ki strength affect karte hain — coil ka placement direction affect nahi\nkarta. [Q472, Q474, Q496]\n● Wood, glass, ebonite = non-magnetic → field amplify nahi karte. [Q496, Q503]\n● Direction change (current reverse) → sirf direction change hoti hai, magnitude nahi. [Q474]\n● Constant current I → constant uniform magnetic field B inside solenoid. [Q490]\n● Loudspeaker, Voltmeter, Ammeter = force on current-carrying conductor principle par based. [Q452]\n● Circular coil mein 6 turns = single loop se 6 times zyada magnetic field; kyunki har turn ka field add hota hai (same\ndirection mein). [Q414]\n3. Fleming's Left-Hand Rule vs Right-Hand Rule\n● Fleming's Right-Hand Rule = Generator/Induced current ke liye. [Q408, Q426, Q428, Q451, Q498, Q537]\n– Forefinger → Magnetic field direction\n– Middle finger → Induced current/EMF direction\n– Thumb → Motion of conductor (force)\n– Teenon mutually perpendicular hote hain. [Q498]\n– Sirf tab valid jab conductor magnetic field ke perpendicular (90°) move kare. [Q428, Q476, Q534]\n– Example: horseshoe magnet North west, South east, rod vertically downward move ho → induced current\nnorth to south direction mein flow karega. [Q537]\n● Fleming's Left-Hand Rule = Motor/Force on conductor ke liye. [Q408, Q416, Q429, Q431, Q454, Q473, Q481, Q501, Q518,\nQ521, Q522, Q529]\n– Forefinger → Magnetic field direction\n– Middle finger → Current direction"," – Thumb → Force/Motion direction\n– Example: field north-to-south (downward), wire deflected south → conventional current west to east, isliye\nelectrons (opposite direction) east to west flow karte hain. [Q473]\n● Right-Hand Thumb Rule (Maxwell's Corkscrew Rule) = current-carrying conductor ke around magnetic field ki\ndirection nikaalne ke liye. [Q408, Q415, Q422]\n– Thumb → current direction; Curled fingers → magnetic field direction.\n● Conductor par force ki direction tab badalti hai jab current ki direction reverse ki jaaye ya magnetic field ki\ndirection reverse ki jaaye. [Q431, Q481, Q522]\n● Current ya magnetic field ka magnitude change karne se force ka magnitude badalta hai, direction nahi. [Q431,\nQ522]\n● Motion aur induced EMF ki direction perpendicular hoti hain; same ya opposite nahi. [Q498]\n4. Magnetic Field Lines: Properties & Patterns\n● Magnetic field lines kabhi intersect nahi karti hain — agar karti to ek point par do directions ho jaati, jo impossible\nhai. [Q409, Q410, Q432, Q434, Q497]\n● Field lines hamesha closed continuous loops banati hain. [Q409, Q410, Q432]\n● Bar magnet ke bahar: field lines North se South ki taraf jaati hain; andar: South se North. [Q409, Q410, Q432, Q434,\nQ456, Q485]\n● North pole se emerge hoti hain, South pole par merge hoti hain. [Q456, Q465]\n● Field lines ki density/crowding = field strength; poles par sabse dense (strongest), center ya beech mein kam.\n[Q410, Q434, Q466, Q492, Q509]\n● Uniform magnetic field mein field lines parallel aur equidistant hoti hain. [Q409]\n● Current-carrying straight conductor ke around field lines concentric circles hoti hain (hemispherical, intersecting\nya parallel nahi), radius conductor se doori ke saath badhta hai (strength kam hoti hai). [Q409, Q422, Q444, Q464,\nQ467, Q520, Q532]\n● Conductor se door jaane par magnetic field strength kam hoti hai — inverse relation (B 1/r); current zyada hone\n∝\n\npar field strength badhti hai (B I).\n∝\n [Q422, Q464, Q509, Q520]\n– Points P(r), Q(2r), S(3r) → B > B_Q > B_S.\nₚ\n [Q464]\n● Current ki direction reverse karne par field lines ki direction bhi reverse ho jaati hai. [Q440]\n● Wire ko East direction mein current le jaaye to Right-Hand Thumb Rule se field wire ke neeche South direction\nmein banega. [Q514]\n● Compass needle ka North pole field ki direction batata hai, South pole nahi. [Q440]\n● Field lines ki closeness = relative strength of magnetic field. [Q466]\n● Magnetic field lines have both magnitude and direction — vector quantity hain. [Q466, Q497]\n● Magnet ki strength number of field lines. Agar A se 5 lines aur B se 10 lines → A ki strength half of B.\n∝\n [Q465]\n● Field ki direction kisi bhi point par tangent se milti hai. [Q512]\n5. Electromagnetic Induction: Faraday's Law & Lenz's Law\n● Electromagnetic Induction = changing magnetic flux ke kaaran coil mein EMF/induced current generate hona.\nDiscovery: Michael Faraday. [Q411, Q419, Q424, Q425, Q441, Q442, Q449, Q453, Q482, Q493, Q506, Q524, Q545, Q575,\nQ618]\n● Electric generator mein mechanical energy use hoti hai conductor ko magnetic field mein rotate karne ke liye\nelectricity produce karne ke liye. [Q449]\n● Faraday's Law: Induced EMF = N × (dΦ/dt) = rate of change of magnetic flux ke proportional. [Q419, Q442, Q453,\nQ482, Q493, Q506, Q524]"," ● Faraday's Second Law: Induced EMF = rate of change of magnetic flux se proportional (EMF = N × dΦ/dt). [Q453]\n● Sirf flux change hone par induction hoti hai — flux itself nahi, uska rate of change matter karta hai. [Q453]\n● EMF independent of R (resistance); depends on: magnetic strength, turns, cross-sectional area, flux change rate.\n[Q506]\n● Induced current I = EMF/R → depends on R. [Q506]\n● Induced current tabhi hoti hai jab relative motion ho magnet aur coil ke beech:\n– Magnet stationary rakhne par → flux change nahi → no induced current. [Q424, Q441, Q450, Q458, Q524]\n– Magnet ko towards ya away coil se move karne par → flux change → induced current. [Q424, Q539]\n– Coil aur magnet same direction mein same speed se move karein → relative motion zero → no induction.\n[Q442, Q457, Q539]\n– Magnet ko solenoid ki axis par rotate karne par → flux change nahi → zero induced current. [Q507]\n● Square coil rotating magnetic field mein ho to induced current ki direction har half revolution mein change hoti\nhai (AC generation ka principle). [Q515]\n● Key switch on/off karne ke interval mein induction hoti hai; steady current hone par nahi. [Q441, Q450, Q458]\n– Key closed karne ke waqt: current 0 se max tak badhti hai → flux change → induction hoti hai. [Q450]\n– Key closed hone ke 2 minutes baad: current steady → flux constant → no induction. [Q450, Q458]\n– Current decrease at constant rate (rheostat se) → flux change → induction hoti hai. [Q458]\n● Induced potential difference (EMF) ko increase karne ke liye:\n– Coil mein turns (N) zyada karo. [Q438]\n– Stronger magnet (zyada magnetic field) use karo. [Q438]\n– Magnet ko tez speed se move karo. [Q419, Q442, Q460]\n● Maximum induced EMF jab coil aur magnet ek doosre ki taraf move karein (relative velocity = v1 + v2). [Q442]\n● Coil ki speed kam hone par → flux change rate kam → induced EMF/potential difference kam hota hai. [Q482]\n● AC generator ke armature ko tez rotate karne par → flux change rate zyada → induced potential difference (EMF)\nincreases. [Q460]\n● Lenz's Law: Induced current ki direction hamesha us cause ka oppose karti hai jisne use produce kiya. [Q483, Q493]\n● Magnet ka North pole coil ki taraf → induced current ek direction mein. [Q483]\n● Same magnet, same speed, South pole coil ki taraf → induced EMF ka magnitude same, lekin sign/direction\nopposite. [Q483]\n● Straight conductor ki current direction continuously change hone par → magnetic field continuously change →\ninduced current not constant (continuously changing). [Q493]\n● Induced current maximum jab conductor ki motion magnetic field ke perpendicular (90°) ho. [Q476]\n– 0° par minimum (zero) induced current. [Q476, Q534]\n– EMF = BLv sinθ; θ = 0° → sin 0° = 0 → EMF = 0. [Q534]\n6. Resistance: Formula, Factors, Resistivity & Temperature\n● Resistance formula: R = ρl/A; ρ = resistivity, l = length, A = πr². [Q405, Q412, Q413, Q427, Q478, Q487, Q510, Q513, Q589,\nQ602, Q620]\n● R l (length):\n∝\n– Length double → R double. [Q510]\n– Length 5 times → R 5 times. [Q478]\n– Length double karke, area same rakhne par ammeter reading (current) half ho jaati hai V constant hone par\n(kyunki R double hone se I = V/R half ho jaata). [Q630]\n● R 1/A (area):\n∝"," – Area double → R half. [Q602, Q620]\n– Area half karne par R double. [Q487 context]\n● Length double + Area half karne par → R = ρ(2l)/(A/2) = 4 times original. [Q487]\n● Resistivity (ρ) = material ki intrinsic property; length ya area par depend nahi karti. [Q412, Q427, Q487, Q553, Q601]\n– Resistivity sirf material nature aur temperature par depend karti hai. [Q412, Q423, Q427, Q487]\n– Wire ko 4 parts mein kaatne par bhi ρ same rehti hai. [Q412]\n– SI unit = Ohm-meter (Ω·m). [Q553, Q587]\n– Definition: 1m length aur 1m² cross-section wale conductor ka resistance. [Q553]\n● Temperature badhne par pure metals ka resistance badhta hai (electron-ion collisions zyada hote hain). [Q423,\nQ560]\n● Semiconductors ka resistance temperature ke saath kam hota hai. [Q617]\n● Resistance does NOT depend on: density (Q580), pressure (Q581). [Q580, Q581]\n● Resistivity order (low to high):\n– Silver (1.60×10⁻⁸) < Copper (1.62×10⁻⁸) < Aluminium (2.63×10⁻⁸) < Tungsten (5.20×10⁻⁸) < Manganin (44×10⁻⁶)\n< Glass/Rubber (10¹²–10¹⁷). [Q443, Q477, Q479, Q491, Q528, Q587, Q624]\n● Same dimension mein: Silver ka resistance sabse kam hoga (lowest ρ). [Q479, Q491, Q587]\n● Alloys ki resistivity generally pure metals se zyada hoti hai. [Q427]\n● Copper transmission lines ke liye ideal hai kyunki iska resistance kam hai → energy loss kam. [Q436]\n– Aluminium bhi use hota hai kyunki lightweight aur cheap hai. [Q567]\n● High resistivity aur low melting point transmission line material ke liye undesirable hain. [Q436]\n● Nichrome = metals mein maximum resistivity; isliye heating elements mein use hota hai. [Q443, Q592]\n– Properties: high resistance, high melting point, oxidation resistant. [Q592]\n● Resistors = alloys se bane hote hain (Nichrome, Constantan, Manganin) → high resistivity. [Q570]\n● Resistivity order category-wise: Conductors < Alloys < Insulators. [Q528]\n7. Ohm's Law & V-I Graphs\n● Ohm's Law (1827): V = IR → current (I) voltage (V) ke directly proportional hai, jabki resistance (R) constant ho.\n[Q447, Q486, Q489, Q508, Q519, Q540, Q569, Q588, Q594, Q621]\n● V-I graph = straight inclined line through origin → linear. [Q448, Q486, Q508, Q594]\n– Slope = Resistance (R). [Q486]\n– Steeper slope → zyada current for same voltage → lower resistance. [Q407]\n● Do alag materials ka V-I graph dono straight line through origin → dono Ohm's law follow karte hain; sirf slope\nalag hai → resistance alag hai. [Q448]\n● Constant temperature par V increase karein → I proportionally increase karegi (R constant rehta hai). [Q489]\n● Temperature badhne par R badhta hai → current aur drift velocity dono kam ho jaate hain. [Q489]\n● Drift velocity formula: Vd = I/(nAe); n = electron density, A = area, e = electron charge. [Q489]\n● Resistance unit: Volt/Ampere = Ohm (Ω). [Q519, Q526]\n● Current 1/R (inverse).\n∝\n [Q407]\n● Agar V constant aur I increase → R decrease (R = V/I). [Q621]\n● Agar R 4× ho jaye (V same) → current I/4. [Q447]\n8. Series vs Parallel Circuits"," ● Electrical circuit connections do types ki hoti hain: Series aur Parallel. [Q614]\n● Series connection: components end-to-end; single path for current. [Q533, Q554, Q565, Q593, Q616]\n– Same current through all components (koi bhi resistor ho, current same rehta hai). [Q475, Q500, Q461, Q593]\n– Total resistance: R = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ + ...\nₛ\n [Q461, Q616]\n– Voltage divides: V_total = V₁ + V₂ + V₃. [Q540]\n– Ek bulb blow → sabhi bulbs stop glowing (circuit breaks). [Q565]\n– Examples: Decoration lights (Diwali ki jhalar), water heater, freezer, refrigerator, lamp, flashlight. [Q533]\n● Parallel connection: components across same two points; multiple paths. [Q552, Q555, Q616]\n– Same voltage across all components. [Q555, Q619]\n– Total resistance: 1/R = 1/R₁ + 1/R₂ + 1/R₃ + ...\nₚ\n [Q435]\n– Current divides; total current = sum of branch currents. [Q500]\n– Ek component fail → others continue to work. [Q565]\n– Examples: Home wiring, street lights, car headlights, DC filter circuit, fire alarm. [Q533, Q555]\n● Domestic wiring parallel mein hoti hai taaki devices independently kaam karein. [Q555]\n● Parallel mein jude bulbs zyada bright glow karte hain series ke comparison mein. [Q500]\n● Series mein potential difference across each resistor uske resistance ke proportional hota hai (V = IR, I same → V\n R).\n∝\n [Q455]\n● Parallel mein 2 resistors: R = R₁R₂/(R₁ + R₂). [Q435]\n● 4 wires same material, garland (mala) ki tarah series mein → R_eq = 4R → 4 times original. [Q461]\n● P point (before split) par current Q point (after split) se zyada hoti hai. [Q500]\n9. DC Motor, DC Generator & AC Generator\n● DC Motor = electrical energy → mechanical energy convert karta hai. [Q416, Q469, Q471, Q551, Q608, Q612]\n– Working principle: Current-carrying conductor magnetic field mein rakha jaaye to mechanical force lagti hai.\n[Q416]\n– Split rings (commutator) har half rotation par current ki direction reverse karte hain → continuous rotation\npossible hoti hai. [Q416, Q471, Q495, Q538]\n– Maximum force tab hoti hai jab coil ke arms magnetic field ke perpendicular hote hain; parallel hone par force\nkam. [Q416]\n– Force ki direction: Fleming's Left-Hand Rule se determine hoti hai. [Q416]\n– Motor elements: Armature Core (coil hold), Commutator (current reverse), Carbon Brushes (current conduct),\nMagnetic Field (torque). [Q538]\n– Commercial motor features: Electromagnet use karta hai (permanent magnet ki jagah) → zyada torque; Soft-\niron core → current band hone par magnetism retain nahi karta. [Q470]\n– Motor invention: Michael Faraday (1821). [Q471, Q551]\n– Motor uses: Fan, Mixer, Washing machine, Computer, MP3 player, Refrigerator, Pump, Vacuum cleaner.\n[Q462, Q551]\n– DC motor types: Series, Shunt/Parallel, Compound, Permanent Magnet DC motor. [Q416]\n– Galvanometer motor nahi use karta — ye sirf current detect/measure karta hai; iron core + rectangular wire\nloop se bana hota hai. [Q462]\n● DC Generator (Dynamo) = mechanical energy → electrical energy (DC). [Q451, Q495, Q504, Q575, Q618]\n– Uses split-ring commutator to reverse current every half rotation. [Q495, Q504]\n– Current flows in one direction only. [Q504]"," – Generates lower voltages. [Q504]\n– Current induced only in rotor. [Q504]\n– Principle: Electromagnetic Induction (Faraday's Law). [Q545, Q575, Q618]\n● AC Generator (Alternator) = mechanical energy → electrical energy (AC). [Q451, Q504, Q618]\n– Converts mechanical → electrical (AC).\n– Uses slip rings (not commutator). [Q495, Q504]\n– Current direction periodically reverses.\n– Can generate very high voltages.\n– Current can be induced in rotor or stator.\n– Uses: Power stations, large-scale electricity generation. [Q618]\n● Commutator use hota hai: DC motor aur DC generator dono mein. [Q495]\n– AC generator mein nahi. [Q495]\n● Transformer = transfers electrical energy from one circuit to another through electromagnetic induction. [Q579]\n10. Force on Conductor\n● Force formula: F = BIL sinθ. [Q494, Q518]\n● Force maximum jab θ = 90° (arms perpendicular to magnetic field) → sin 90° = 1 → F_max = BIL. [Q494]\n● Force zero jab θ = 0° (parallel to field) → sin 0° = 0. [Q494, Q518]\n● Force ki direction Current ki direction aur magnetic field ki direction dono par depend karti hai. [Q445]\n● Force ki direction: Fleming's Left-Hand Rule se. [Q416, Q431, Q445, Q454, Q481, Q501, Q521, Q529]\n● Magnetic field (North), Current (East to West) → Force direction: Downward (Fleming's Left-Hand Rule se). [Q454]\n● Force ki direction tab badalti hai jab current ki direction reverse ki jaaye ya magnetic field ki direction reverse ki\njaaye. [Q431, Q481, Q522]\n● Current ya magnetic field ka magnitude change karne se force ka magnitude badalta hai, direction nahi. [Q431,\nQ522]\n● Motor mein coil ki do arms mein current opposite directions mein flow hoti hai → forces equal magnitude,\nopposite direction → rotational torque (couple) create hota hai. [Q521, Q529]\n11. Heating Effect of Electric Current (Joule's Law)\n● Formula: H = I²RT — heat produced directly proportional to square of current, resistance, aur time. [Q363, Q371,\nQ374, Q417, Q420, Q535, Q544, Q591]\n● Heating effect par based devices: Electric iron, Electric heater, Electric geyser, Induction cooker, Microwave oven,\nHair blower, Incandescent lamp, Immersion rod, Electric kettle, Electric toaster, Electric oven, Fuse. [Q363, Q365,\nQ371, Q372, Q417, Q420, Q517, Q547, Q579, Q591]\n● NOT based on heating effect:\n– Electric generator → electromagnetic induction par. [Q417, Q575]\n– Electric washing machine, mixer, fan, computer, refrigerator → electric motor use karte hain. [Q420, Q462,\nQ547, Q579]\n– Electric bell, electromagnet → magnetic effect par. [Q363]\n– Speaker → electromagnetic induction par. [Q363]\n– Transformer → induction par. [Q579]\n● Electric current ke teen main effects hote hain: Heating, Magnetic aur Chemical — \"Contraction effect\" naam ka"," koi recognized effect nahi hai. [Q598]\n● Electric iron ka invention: Henry Seely White (1882). [Q420]\n● Electric circuits mein losses heat ke form mein hoti hain (Joule's heating). [Q535]\n● Factors: Resistance (zyada R = zyada heat), Time (zyada t = zyada heat), Current (zyada I = zyada heat).\n– Current triple ho jaye (R, t constant) → heat H I² se 9 times ho jaati hai.\n∝\n [Q468, Q535]\n– Resistance half ho jaye (I, t constant) → heat bhi half ho jaati hai (H R).\n∝\n [Q628]\n– Energy dissipated formula alternate roop mein: H = I²Rt = IVt = VIt (Ohm's law V=IR use karke). [Q629]\n● Brightness vs Resistance: Same voltage source par bulb with higher resistance → less current (I = V/R) → less\npower (P = V²/R) → dimmer. [Q586]\n– So dim bulb = higher resistance; bright bulb = lower resistance. [Q586]\n12. Ammeter, Voltmeter & Galvanometer\n● Ammeter = current measure karta hai; series mein lagta hai; very low resistance (ideally zero) taaki current\nsignificantly reduce na ho. [Q557, Q562, Q590, Q625]\n● Voltmeter = potential difference measure karta hai; parallel mein lagta hai; very high resistance (ideally infinite)\ntaaki negligible current le. [Q562, Q571, Q590, Q596, Q610]\n● Galvanometer = very small current (≈100 mA) ki presence aur direction detect karta hai. [Q462, Q585, Q625]\n– Iron core + rectangular wire loop se bana hota hai.\n– Motor nahi use karta. [Q462]\n● Galvanometer ko voltmeter banane ke liye high resistance series mein lagate hain. [Q462]\n● Rheostat current control karta hai; Ohm's Law par based. [Q568, Q600, Q605]\n● Resistance symbol: zigzag line (American) ya rectangle (European). [Q526]\n● Electric bulb symbol = circle with X inside. [Q626]\n● Voltmeter symbol = circle with V and +/- terminals. [Q610]\n● Rectifier = AC ko DC mein convert karta hai. [Q549]\n13. Fuse: Principle, Material & Rating\n● Fuse = safety device based on heating effect of current (H = I²Rt). [Q544, Q591]\n● Fuse wire = Tin (Sn) + Lead (Pb) alloy; low melting point hota hai. [Q544, Q613]\n● Jab current rated value se zyada ho jaaye → wire heat hokar melt ho jaata hai → circuit break → protection.\n[Q544, Q613]\n● Fuse rating example: 8 A → 8 A tak safe, usse zyada par melt. [Q613]\n● Domestic fuse rating: 1 Ampere – 10 Ampere. [Q536]\n– Small appliances (bulb, fan): ~5A.\n– Heavy appliances (AC, geyser): up to 15A.\n● Fuse wire properties: Low melting point, high conductivity, low oxidation. [Q459]\n● Fuse series mein connected hota hai device ke saath. [Q459, Q590]\n● Short circuit = low-resistance connection between conductors → V = IR, R ≈ 0 → I = V/R becomes enormously\nlarge. [Q511, Q584]\n– Causes: Vermin chewing wires, loose connections, old/damaged outlets. [Q511]\n● PVC coating on wires → insulation → short circuit prevent karta hai. [Q584]"," ● Electrician rubber gloves pehanta hai → rubber = excellent insulator → electric shock se bachata hai. [Q558]\n14. Conductors, Insulators, Semiconductors & Superconductors\n● Conductors = low resistivity; allow current flow easily. [Q480, Q564, Q587, Q617]\n– Examples: Silver (lowest ρ = 1.60×10⁻⁸ Ωm), Copper (1.62×10⁻⁸), Aluminium (2.63×10⁻⁸), Gold, Iron. Human\nbody bhi conductor hai kyunki body cells mein ions hote hain jo electricity conduct karte hain. [Q477, Q479,\nQ491, Q546, Q587, Q567]\n– Copper aur Aluminium = most common for transmission wires (copper: low ρ, aluminium: lightweight +\ncheap). [Q436, Q567]\n● Insulators = extremely high resistivity (practically infinite). [Q480, Q564, Q595, Q611]\n– Resistivity order: 10¹² Ωm to 10¹⁷ Ωm. [Q624]\n– Examples: Glass, Rubber, Plastic, Wood, Dry air, Bakelite, Ebonite, Paper, Cotton, Diamond, Mica, Quartz.\n[Q443, Q477, Q564, Q573, Q595, Q604, Q611, Q631]\n– Ebonite resistivity = 10¹⁵ to 10¹⁷ Ωm → highest among common options. [Q604]\n– Bakelite = polymer (phenol + formaldehyde) → thermosetting insulator → weakest conductor. [Q573]\n● Semiconductors = conductors aur insulators ke beech. [Q570, Q617]\n– Examples: Silicon (Si), Germanium (Ge).\n– Resistivity decreases with increasing temperature.\n● Superconductors = zero resistance. Examples: Magnesium Diboride, Niobium. [Q564]\n● At high temperatures, conductor resistivity increases and conductivity decreases, while for semiconductors,\nresistance decreases with increasing temperature. [Q617]\n● Good conductor (transmission lines) ke liye chahiye: low resistance, free electron movement. [Q436]\n● High resistivity aur low melting point transmission line material ke liye undesirable hain. [Q436]\n● Nichrome = heating devices mein use hota hai (water heater coils, hair dryer, toaster, oven) → high resistance +\nhigh melting point + oxidation resistant. [Q443, Q592]\n15. Energy Conversions\n● Electric Motor = Electrical energy → Mechanical energy. [Q416, Q469, Q471, Q551, Q608, Q612]\n● Electric Generator/Dynamo = Mechanical energy → Electrical energy. [Q417, Q449, Q451, Q469, Q575, Q618]\n● Heating Effect Devices = Electrical → Heat energy. [Q363, Q371, Q417, Q420, Q517, Q547, Q579, Q591]\n● Electric bulb = Electrical → Light + Heat. [Q612]\n● Microphone = Sound → Electrical. Loudspeaker = Electrical → Sound. [Q612]\n● Battery/Cell = Chemical energy → Electrical energy. [Q551, Q572, Q603]\n– Primary cell = non-rechargeable (Leclanche, Daniel, Dry Cell). [Q603]\n– Invented by Alessandro Volta. [Q559, Q603]\n● Photocell = Light energy → Electrical energy. [Q551]\n● Torch = Chemical (cells) → Electrical → Light. [Q608]\n● TV = Electrical → Light + Sound. [Q608]\n● Electromagnet = Electrical energy → Magnetic energy. [Q484]\n● Turbine = Hydraulic energy → Mechanical energy. [Q469]\n● Transformer = transfers electrical energy from one circuit to another through electromagnetic induction. [Q579]"," 16. Coulomb's Law\n● Coulomb's Law: Do point charges ke beech attraction/repulsion force directly proportional to product of charges\naur inversely proportional to square of distance. [Q622, Q623]\n● Formula: F = k × (q₁q₂/r²); k = 8.99 × 10⁹ N·m²/C². [Q622, Q623]\n● Scientist: Charles Coulomb. [Q622]\n17. Electric Current Basics\n● Electric current = flow of electrons (negative charges) in conductor. [Q607, Q627]\n● Conventionally, current direction = positive charges ka flow (positive to negative terminal). [Q577, Q582]\n– Actual electron flow = negative to positive (opposite). [Q582]\n● Current flow ke liye potential difference zaroori hai. Agar do points ka potential equal ho → no current flows.\n[Q597]\n● Electric potential kisi point par = work done in moving a unit positive charge infinity se us point tak (bina\nacceleration ke). [Q566]\n● Potential difference (V) do points ke beech = work done per unit charge ek point se doosre point tak move karne\nmein: V = W/Q. [Q578]\n● SI unit = Ampere (A) = 1 Coulomb/second. [Q607]\n● Electric circuit = continuous closed path for current flow. [Q561, Q616]\n● Cell/battery maintains potential difference → drives continuous current. [Q572]\n● Conductor mein current flow = electrons ka motion; solution mein = ions ka motion (electrolyte). [Q627]\n● Neutrons = neutral (no charge), protons = fixed in nucleus → dono current carry nahi karte. [Q627]\n18. Magnetic Compass & Field Detection\n● Magnetic compass = tiny magnetic needle (aluminium pointer se attached) jo North-South direction indicate karti\nhai. [Q499, Q527]\n– China mein invented (2nd century BC - 1st century AD). [Q499]\n● Compass needle bar magnet ke paas laane par deflect hoti hai kyunki ye khud ek chhota magnet hai. [Q527]\n● Magnetic field ki presence detect karne ke liye magnetic needle use hoti hai; galvanometer, voltmeter, ammeter\nnahi. [Q530]\n● Freely suspended bar magnet hamesha geographical North-South direction mein point karta hai. [Q421, Q434]\n– Reason: Earth ka magnetic South pole geographical North mein hai (unlike poles attract). [Q421]\n● Magnetic field = magnet ke around ka region jahan uska effect detect ho sakta hai. Unit = Tesla. [Q615]\n● Electromagnetic force = electrically charged particles ke interaction se. [Q609]\n– Friction, tension, spring force = all electromagnetic at microscopic level.\n– Weight (gravitational force) = NOT electromagnetic; alag fundamental force hai. [Q609]\n19. Oersted's Experiment, Medical Imaging, Electroplating & Solutions\n● Oersted's Experiment (1820): Current-carrying wire ke paas compass needle deflect hoti hai → wire magnetic\nfield produce karti hai. [Q531]\n– Current direction reverse karne par deflection ki direction bhi reverse hoti hai. [Q531]"," ● Medical Imaging: [Q523]\n– MRI = Powerful magnetic field + radiofrequency pulses + computer.\n– CT Scan = X-rays + computer → cross-sectional images.\n– Ultrasound = High-frequency sound waves.\n– PET Scan = Radioactive substance (tracer).\n● Electroplating = electricity se kisi material par desired metal ki layer deposit karna. [Q548]\n● Electrolytes = solutions jo electricity conduct karte hain (acids, bases, salts in water). [Q550]\n● Non-electrolytes = alcohol, glucose → no free ions → do NOT conduct electricity. [Q550]\n● Distilled water = poor conductor (no dissolved salts/ions); regular tap water conducts kyunki dissolved salts hain.\n[Q574]\n● Parallel conductors: same direction current → attract; opposite direction → repel. [Q525]\n● GK crossover facts jo isi chapter mein aaye: sabse effective tarika electricity production kam karne ka hai\ncombustion (fuel burning) kam karna, kyunki thermal power plants combustion se hi electricity banate hain\n(reduce/reuse/composting alternative waste-management concepts hain, production kam karne ka direct tarika\nnahi). [Q516]\n● Water ki density sabse zyada 277 K (4°C) par hoti hai — 273 K (0°C, ice) par nahi; heating se molecular cage-\nstructure break hoke volume minimum aur density maximum ho jaati hai. [Q542]\n20. Power Formula & Basic Components\n● Electric power formulas: P = VI = I²R = V²/R. [Q563]\n– IR² power represent nahi karta → wrong dimensions. [Q563]\n● Resistor = passive two-terminal component jo electrical resistance implement karta hai; current ko limit/regulate\nkarta hai. [Q541, Q526]\n● Capacitor = electrical energy store karta hai electric field mein. [Q541]\n● Transistor = miniature semiconductor jo current/voltage regulate aur amplify karta hai. [Q541]\n● Diode = one-way switch for current. [Q541]\n● Switch = circuit ko break/close karne ke liye; invented by John Henry Holmes (1884). [Q559]\n● Cell/battery: Invented by Alessandro Volta. [Q559, Q603]\n21.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q405–Q632)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fleming's Right = Generator (induced current); Left = Motor (force). Ulta mat karna! [Q408, Q416, Q426,\nQ451, Q498]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bulb mein Nitrogen aur Argon fill hoti hai; Hydrogen/Oxygen nahi. [Q583, Q606]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Filament = Tungsten; Silver/Iron/Nickel nahi. [Q543, Q599]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solenoid ke andar field lines parallel straight hain; straight conductor ke around concentric circles.\n[Q406, Q422, Q467]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnetic field strength poles par strongest hoti hai, center par nahi. [Q410]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Resistivity (ρ) length/area par depend nahi karti — sirf material aur temperature par. [Q412, Q427, Q487,\nQ601]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Length double + Area half = R 4 times (not 2 times or unchanged). [Q487]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Resistance density ya pressure par depend nahi karti. [Q580, Q581]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Temperature badhne par pure metals ka R badhta hai; semiconductors ka R kam hota hai. [Q423, Q617]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Induced EMF flux change se nahi, rate of change of flux se proportional hai. [Q453, Q482]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same direction same speed mein coil aur magnet move karein → no induction (relative motion zero).\n[Q457, Q539]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnet North pole vs South pole same speed par → EMF magnitude same, direction opposite. [Q483]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Commutator DC motor + DC generator dono mein use hota hai; AC generator mein slip rings. [Q495,\nQ504]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force maximum at 90° (perpendicular), zero at 0° (parallel). [Q494, Q518, Q534]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force direction sirf current direction ya field direction change karne se badalti hai; magnitude change se\nnahi. [Q522]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Series mein current same, voltage divide; Parallel mein voltage same, current divide. [Q475, Q500, Q533,\nQ540, Q593, Q619]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: EMF R par depend nahi karti; induced current depend karti hai (I = EMF/R). [Q506]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Domestic wiring parallel mein; series nahi. [Q555]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ammeter = series + low R; Voltmeter = parallel + high R. [Q557, Q571, Q590]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Motor = electrical → mechanical; Generator = mechanical → electrical. Ulta mat karo! [Q612, Q618]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Toaster = heating effect; motor nahi use karta. [Q579]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Equal potential par no current flows; potential difference zaroori hai. [Q597]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: IR² power represent nahi karta; I²R karta hai. [Q563]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cell = chemical energy convert karta hai; potential/kinetic nahi. [Q603]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weight = gravitational force; electromagnetic nahi. [Q609]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Compass needle khud chhota magnet hai; sirf conductor nahi. [Q527]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Oersted experiment mein current reverse → deflection reverse hota hai. [Q531]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Domestic fuse 1-10A range mein; 100-200A nahi. [Q536]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Silver = lowest resistivity; Nichrome = high resistivity. [Q587]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnetic field lines vector hain → magnitude + direction. [Q466, Q497]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Conductor ko field ke parallel move karne par EMF = 0 (flux change nahi). [Q534]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Solenoid mein wooden core field nahi badhata; soft iron badhata hai. [Q472, Q503, Q496]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Series circuit examples = decoration lights; Parallel = home wiring, street lights. [Q533]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Repulsion = sure test of magnetism; attraction alone sufficient nahi. [Q432, Q437]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Earth ka magnetic South pole geographical North mein hai. [Q421]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fuse = heating effect par based; electromagnetic induction nahi. [Q591]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alloys ki resistivity pure metals se zyada hoti hai. [Q427]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Glass = insulator = highest resistivity; metals = conductors = low resistivity. [Q443, Q477]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fuse wire melts → circuit disconnect; NOT short circuit ya overloading se bachata hai directly. [Q544,\nQ613]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Conventional current = positive to negative; actual electrons = negative to positive. [Q577, Q582]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnetic monopoles exist nahi karte. [Q432]\n22. Numerical: Ohm's Law (V = IR)\n● V = IR — sabse basic formula sabhi numerical ka base. [Q633, Q637, Q646, Q647, Q648, Q667, Q672, Q678, Q682, Q683,\nQ690, Q732, Q745, Q746, Q748, Q757, Q760, Q778, Q779, Q780, Q781, Q783, Q793, Q795, Q796, Q812, Q820]\n● Current (I) = V/R — jab voltage aur resistance given ho. [Q633, Q637, Q648, Q706, Q760, Q793, Q795, Q796]\n● Resistance (R) = V/I — jab voltage aur current given ho. [Q647, Q672, Q683, Q778, Q779, Q780, Q781, Q783, Q820]\n● Voltage (V) = IR — jab current aur resistance given ho. [Q646, Q678, Q682, Q690, Q812]\n● V double, R constant → I doubles. [Q748]"," ● V half, R constant → I halves. [Q746]\n● V aur I dono double → R same rehta hai (R = V/I). [Q791]\n● Unit consistency zaroori: mA ko A mein convert karo (1 mA = 10⁻³ A). [Q646, Q667]\n● V-I graph ka slope = Resistance (jab V vertical, I horizontal). [Q700]\n23. Numerical: Resistance Formula (R = ρl/A) & Wire Stretching\n● R = ρ(l/A) — ρ = resistivity, l = length, A = πr². [Q634, Q636, Q641, Q651, Q656, Q658, Q663, Q664, Q666, Q677, Q679, Q680,\nQ698, Q705, Q713, Q714, Q715, Q719, Q721, Q722, Q724, Q734, Q735, Q740, Q751, Q763, Q772]\n● Same material (ρ constant) mein:\n– R l — length double → R double; length 3× → R 3×.\n∝\n [Q478, Q510, Q641, Q705, Q751, Q772]\n– R 1/A — area double → R half.\n∝\n [Q656, Q714, Q763]\n– R 1/r² — radius half → R 4×; radius 1/3 → R 9×.\n∝\n [Q636, Q679]\n● Length double + Area half → R = 4× original. [Q487, Q658, Q736]\n● Length 4× + Area 5× → R_new = (4/5)×R. [Q666]\n● Wire stretched (volume constant): R l² kyunki A = V/l.\n∝\n [Q673]\n– Length 50% increase (1.5×) → R_new = (1.5)² × R = 2.25× R = 9R/4. [Q673]\n● Resistivity (ρ) = RA/L — intrinsic property, length/area par depend nahi karti. [Q735, Q553]\n– SI unit = Ohm-meter (Ω·m). [Q553, Q587]\n● ρ calculation: ρ = R(πr²)/L. [Q722, Q734, Q740]\n● Same R, different L aur A → ρ ratio = (A₁/A₂) × (L₂/L₁). [Q724]\n● Different material, same dimension → ρ ratio = R ratio. [Q663]\n● Material change: R_new/R_old = (ρ_new/ρ_old) × (L_new/L_old) × (A_old/A_new). [Q713, Q721]\n24. Numerical: Series & Parallel Resistance Combinations\n● Series: R_eq = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ + ... [Q633, Q637, Q648, Q653, Q655, Q665, Q671, Q678, Q681, Q682, Q699, Q706, Q718, Q727,\nQ743, Q750, Q758, Q771, Q775, Q805, Q821]\n– Same current through all resistors — R value chahe kuch bhi ho, series mein current constant rehta hai (jaise\n5Ω se 6A guzri to 10Ω series resistor se bhi 6A hi guzregi). [Q637, Q648, Q665, Q671, Q727, Q771]\n– Voltage divides in ratio of resistances: V₁/V₂ = R₁/R₂. [Q665, Q671, Q681]\n– Cells series mein connected ho toh total EMF/potential difference = sabhi cells ki EMF ka sum hota hai (3 cells\nof 2V series mein → 6V total). [Q750]\n● Parallel: 1/R_eq = 1/R₁ + 1/R₂ + ... [Q635, Q642, Q654, Q657, Q670, Q674, Q676, Q686, Q718, Q729, Q739, Q742, Q825, Q827,\nQ835]\n– Same voltage across all resistors. [Q642, Q654, Q657, Q661, Q674, Q676, Q703]\n– Current divides: I₁/I₂ = R₂/R₁. [Q661]\n– 2 identical parallel → R_eq = R/2. [Q642, Q674, Q676]\n– n identical parallel → R_eq = R/n. [Q670, Q697, Q711, Q717]\n● Mixed: Pehle parallel solve karo, phir series add karo. [Q635, Q686, Q707, Q827]\n● Wire bent into circle → 2 semicircles in parallel → R_eq = R/4. [Q638]\n● Two resistors: R_s = R₁+R₂, R_p = R₁R₂/(R₁+R₂). [Q733, Q737]\n● Maximum resistance ke liye series; minimum ke liye parallel. [Q697, Q706, Q711, Q717, Q718, Q769, Q835]"," 25. Numerical: Electric Power (P = VI = I²R = V²/R)\n● P = VI — jab V aur I given ho. [Q652, Q660, Q674, Q675, Q676, Q702, Q730, Q757, Q777]\n● P = V²/R — jab voltage aur resistance given ho (parallel mein useful). [Q643, Q692, Q694, Q731]\n● P = I²R — jab current aur resistance given ho (series mein useful). [Q650, Q725, Q738]\n● Same voltage (parallel) mein: P 1/R. Lower R = higher power = brighter bulb.\n∝\n [Q643, Q703]\n● Same current (series) mein: P R. Higher R = higher power.\n∝\n [Q650]\n● Resistance from power rating (same V): R = V²/P. [Q649, Q709, Q720]\n● Agar V double (R constant) → P 4× (P V²).\n∝\n [Q689, Q731]\n● Agar I double aur V triple → P 6×. [Q668]\n● Agar dono triple → P 9×. [Q687]\n● V half (R constant) → P = P/4. [Q731]\n● No voltage applied → P = 0W. [Q741]\n● P = V/I galat hai — dimensionally wrong. [Q685]\n● Power = Energy/Time. [Q693, Q767, Q774]\n● Do bulbs parallel mein 3V source ke saath, R ratio 1:3 ho toh heat produced ratio (H 1/R same V par) = 3:1\n∝\n(lower R wala bulb zyada heat produce karta hai). [Q645]\n● 5 identical bulbs parallel mein 20V, total current 5A → R_total = V/I = 4Ω; example ke hisaab se har bulb ka\nresistance ≈1.25Ω aur power ≈31.25W (official RRC key ke formula se). [Q729]\n26. Numerical: Heat/Energy (H = I²Rt = VIt = V²t/R)\n● Heat produced = Power × Time. [Q640, Q644, Q654, Q655, Q657, Q662, Q669, Q689, Q691, Q701, Q710, Q725, Q726, Q728,\nQ770]\n● H = I²Rt — jab current direct given ho. [Q662, Q669, Q701, Q710, Q725, Q770]\n● H = VIt = V²t/R — jab voltage given ho. [Q654, Q657, Q726, Q728]\n● Power = Heat/Time = H/t. [Q693]\n27. Numerical: Charge & Current (Q = It)\n● Charge (Q) = Current (I) × Time (t). [Q696, Q730, Q744, Q749, Q753, Q759, Q761, Q764, Q787, Q790, Q792, Q798, Q799,\nQ817, Q818, Q819, Q831]\n● Current (I) = Q/t. [Q794]\n● Time (t) = Q/I. [Q799]\n● Time hamesha seconds mein convert karo — 1 min = 60s, 5 min = 300s, 10 min = 600s. [Q753, Q759, Q761, Q764,\nQ787, Q790, Q792, Q794, Q798, Q817, Q818, Q819]\n● Resistance value kabhi-kabhi extra information hoti hai — sirf Q = It se kaam chal jaata hai. [Q764]\n28. Numerical: Work Done (W = QV)\n● Work (W) = Charge (Q) × Potential Difference (V). [Q747, Q752, Q786, Q788, Q797, Q804, Q810, Q813, Q814, Q815, Q816,\nQ832]\n● Charge (Q) = W/V. [Q801, Q807]\n● Potential Difference (V) = W/Q. [Q832 context]"," ● Unit hamesha Joules (J) hoti hai — N, Pa, C, A galat hain. [Q777, Q786, Q810, Q832]\n29. Numerical: Energy Units (kWh\n Joules)\n⇄\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J (yaad rakho!). [Q755, Q762, Q766, Q785, Q811]\n● 1 unit = 1 kWh = 1000 Wh. [Q644, Q754, Q768, Q773, Q776, Q782, Q785, Q800, Q802, Q803, Q806, Q811, Q824, Q834]\n● Energy (kWh) = Power (kW) × Time (h). [Q640, Q644, Q754, Q765, Q768, Q776, Q782, Q800, Q802, Q803, Q824, Q834]\n● Energy (Wh) = Power (W) × Time (h). [Q695, Q754, Q776, Q800]\n● Joules → kWh: divide by 3.6 × 10⁶. [Q756, Q773, Q785, Q806, Q811]\n● kWh → Joules: multiply by 3.6 × 10⁶. [Q756, Q766, Q773, Q785, Q806]\n● Month ke liye: days × hours/day. [Q644, Q765, Q773, Q803, Q824, Q834]\n● September = 30 days, October = 31, November = 30, etc. [Q644]\n30. Numerical: Bulb Brightness & Power Ratings\n● Parallel mein same voltage → zyada rated wattage = zyada bright. [Q643, Q703]\n● Series mein same current → kam rated wattage = zyada bright (uska R zyada hota hai). [Q649]\n● Current from power: I = P/V. [Q659, Q793, Q795, Q796]\n31. Numerical: Cost Calculation & Fuse Rating\n● Cost = Energy (units/kWh) × Rate per unit. [Q644: 150 kWh × Rs 6 = Rs 900]\n● Fuse rating: I = P/V. [Q723: 2000/250 = 8A → 12A fuse inappropriate]\n● Max devices from fuse: P_total = V × I_fuse. [Q716: 220×15 = 3300W → 13 lamps of 100W]\n32. Numerical: Induced EMF, Coulomb's Law, Magnetic Field & Electrons\n● Induced EMF: ε = -N(dΦ/dt) → EMF N (turns).\n∝\n [Q704: N_B = 2N_A → ε ratio 1:2]\n● n turns wali coil ka magnetic field, single loop (same radius, same current) ke comparison mein n : 1 ratio mein\nhota hai (B n).\n∝\n [Q639]\n● Straight conductor ke around magnetic field current ke directly proportional hota hai (B I); currents I, 2I, 3I ke\n∝\nliye fields B1 < B2 < B3 (B3 sabse zyada). [Q684]\n● Induced current: I = EMF/R — EMF independent of R, current depends on R. [Q688, Q708, Q712]\n– Example: R=4Ω, induced current 1 mA → EMF = IR = 1mA × 4Ω = 4 mV. [Q688]\n● Coulomb's Law: F = k(q₁q₂/r²) → F 1/r².\n∝\n [Q833]\n– Distance 1/5 → Force 25×. [Q833]\n● Number of electrons: n = Q/e = It/e. [Q829, Q830]\n– I = 1A, t = 1s, e = 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ C → n = 6.25 × 10¹⁸. [Q830]\n● Equivalent current in hydrogen atom: I = Qv/(2πR). [Q828]\n– R = 5×10⁻¹¹ m, v = 2.2×10⁶ m/s → I ≈ 1.12 mA. [Q828]"," 33. Numerical: Wire Doubled on Itself\n● Jab wire ko moodhkar aadha (doubled) karte hain:\n– Length → L/2\n– Area → 2A\n– New R = ρ(L/2)/(2A) = ρL/(4A) = R/4. [Q784, Q808, Q809, Q822, Q823]\n● Examples: 5Ω→1.25Ω, 7Ω→1.75Ω, 8Ω→2Ω, 9Ω→2.25Ω, 10Ω→2.5Ω. [Q784, Q808, Q809, Q822, Q823]\n34. Numerical: Temperature Conversion & Cross-Topic Numericals\n● K = °C + 273. [Q826: 78°C = 351K]\n● Cross-topic numerical (potential energy, mechanics ka formula jo isi Q-range mein aaya): PE = m × g × h. Example:\nmass=20kg, height=15m, g=10 m/s² → PE = 20×10×15 = 3000 J (unit Joules, na ki Watt/Newton/Pascal). [Q789]\n35.\n Traps / Master Formula Cheat Sheet (Numerical Q633–Q835)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: mA ko hamesha A mein convert karo — 2.5 mA = 2.5×10⁻³ A. [Q646]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Wire stretch karne par (volume constant) R L², sirf L nahi.\n∝\n [Q673]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Radius half → Area 1/4 → R 4×. Radius 1/3 → Area 1/9 → R 9×. [Q636, Q679]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Series mein current same, voltage divide in R ratio. [Q665, Q671, Q681, Q771]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Parallel mein voltage same, current divide in inverse R ratio. [Q661]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Power parallel mein P 1/R (V same); series mein P R (I same).\n∝\n∝\n [Q643, Q650, Q703]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: V double karne par (R constant) P 4× hota hai (P V²), P/2 nahi.\n∝\n [Q689, Q731]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: P = V/I galat hai — P = VI sahi hai. [Q685]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 2 identical parallel → R_eq = R/2; n identical → R/n. [Q670, Q674, Q676, Q697, Q711, Q717]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cost calculate karte waqt days of month yaad rakho. [Q644, Q765]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Power = 0 jab V = 0 (no voltage applied). [Q741]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: V aur I dono double → R same rehta hai. [Q791]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Wire doubled on itself → R/4 (not R/2). [Q784, Q808, Q809, Q822, Q823]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Time hamesha seconds mein — 1 min = 60s. [Q753, Q759, Q761, Q764, Q787, Q790, Q792, Q794, Q798, Q817,\nQ818, Q819]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work done unit Joules (J) hoti hai — N, Pa, C, A galat. [Q777, Q786, Q810]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Resistivity (ρ) length/area par depend nahi karti. [Q735]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J — 3600 J nahi. [Q755, Q762]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fuse rating hamesha thoda zyada hona chahiye actual current se. [Q723]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Resistance value kabhi-kabhi extra information hoti hai — Q = It direct use karo. [Q764]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 4 Electric Current Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0407","t":"05 Force and Pressure","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.5 — FORCE AND PRESSURE — FULL MIND MAP\n💪\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Archimedes' Principle & Buoyancy\n2. Gas Laws: Boyle's, Charles's, Gay-Lussac's\n3. Newton's Laws of Motion\n4. Friction: Types, Order, Applications & Reduction\n5. Pressure: Definition, Units & Atmospheric Pressure\n6. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n7. Fundamental Forces\n8. Kepler's Laws of Planetary Motion\n9. Spring Balance & Hooke's Law\n10. Work, Energy, Momentum & Equations of Motion\n11. Stress, Thrust & Tension\n12. Types of Motion\n13. Inertia, Mass & Weight\n14. Balanced vs Unbalanced Forces\n15. Impulse & Safety Applications\n16. Miscellaneous Concepts\n17.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q836–Q965)\n⚠️\n18. Numerical: Newton's Second Law (F = ma)\n19. Numerical: Equations of Motion\n20. Numerical: Distance in nth Second\n21. Numerical: Conservation of Momentum\n22. Numerical: Weight (W = mg) & Moon Weight\n23. Numerical: Momentum (p = mv)\n24. Numerical: Unit Conversions\n25. Numerical: Work Done & Energy\n26. Numerical: Gravitational Force\n27. Numerical: Cricket Ball / Retarding Force\n28.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (Numerical Q966–Q1058)\n⚠️\n1. Archimedes' Principle & Buoyancy\n● Archimedes' Principle: Fluid mein fully/partially immersed body par upward buoyant force = weight of displaced\nfluid. [Q836, Q848, Q853, Q911, Q938]\n● Formula: Fb = ρ × g × V; ρ = liquid density, V = volume, g = gravity. [Q848, Q938]\n● Applications: Submarines (dive/surface), Ships, Hydrometers (liquid density measure), Lactometers (milk purity).\n[Q848, Q853]\n● Archimedes ne is principle se king's crown ki gold purity determine ki thi. [Q853]\n● When object floats: upthrust = weight of object (equilibrium). [Q911]\n● Buoyant force acts at centre of mass of displaced fluid. [Q836]\n● Buoyant force depends on density of fluid (ρ) and volume displaced (V). [Q938]\n2. Gas Laws: Boyle's, Charles's, Gay-Lussac's\n● Boyle's Law: Constant temperature par, gas ka volume inversely proportional hota hai pressure se (PV ="," constant). [Q837]\n● Charles's Law: Constant pressure par, ideal gas ka volume directly proportional hota hai absolute temperature se.\n[Q837]\n● Gay-Lussac's Law: Constant volume par, gas ka pressure directly proportional hota hai absolute temperature se.\n[Q837]\n● Graham's Law: Constant pressure par, gas diffusion ki rate inversely proportional hoti hai molar mass ke square\nroot se. [Q837]\n3. Newton's Laws of Motion\n● First Law (Law of Inertia): Body at rest → at rest; body in uniform motion → uniform motion (jab tak external\nforce na lage). [Q838, Q889, Q892, Q909, Q940, Q958, Q965]\n– Examples: Bus start hone par backward jerk, coin on card flicked falls in tumbler, athlete ka run before jump.\n[Q889, Q940]\n● Second Law: Rate of change of momentum directly proportional to applied force (F = ma). [Q839, Q840, Q888, Q895,\nQ924, Q961, Q964]\n– Momentum (p) = mass × velocity; vector quantity; unit = kg m/s. [Q895, Q898, Q901, Q910, Q946, Q950, Q951]\n– Acceleration = rate of change of velocity. [Q896]\n● Third Law: Every action has equal and opposite reaction. [Q887, Q893, Q906, Q929, Q932, Q960]\n– Examples: Rocket launching (expels gases backward → moves forward). [Q887, Q906]\n– Force never occurs singly in nature. [Q893, Q960]\n– Action-reaction forces always act on different bodies, never on the same body — jaise 70 kg person ne 50 kg\nperson ko 50 N se push kiya toh 50 kg person bhi 50 N ka hi reaction force lagayega (magnitude equal, chahe\nmasses alag hon). [Q929, Q985]\n● Force (F) = ma — quantitative definition from Second Law. [Q961, Q964]\n4. Friction: Types, Order, Applications & Reduction\n● Friction = force resisting relative motion between two surfaces in contact; acts opposite to motion. [Q842, Q846,\nQ850, Q882, Q883, Q894, Q962]\n● Friction ke bina mushkil ho jaane wale kaam: wet marble floor par chalna (grip minimal ho jaati hai) — normal\nwalking, door movement, carrom, box move karna friction ki wajah se easy hote hain. [Q849]\n● Order of Frictional Force: Static > Sliding (Kinetic/Dynamic) > Rolling. [Q842, Q852, Q855, Q861, Q875]\n– Static = strongest; Rolling = least. [Q842]\n● Static Friction: Object at rest; due to interlocking of irregularities between surfaces. [Q847, Q869]\n● Sliding (Kinetic/Dynamic) Friction: Surfaces in relative motion/sliding. [Q842, Q875, Q886]\n● Rolling Friction: Object rolls on surface; smaller than sliding friction. [Q842, Q855, Q864]\n● Fluid Friction (Drag): Exerted by fluids (air/water) on moving objects; depends on speed, nature of fluid, shape of\nobject. [Q842, Q862, Q868, Q878, Q879, Q880]\n● Friction cannot be totally eliminated — microscopic irregularities always remain. [Q861]\n● Friction ka formula: f = μN (μ = coefficient of friction, N = normal force). [Q851, Q962]\n● Friction wears out materials: screws, ball bearings, shoe soles. [Q851]\n● Without friction → object can never stop (Newton's first law). [Q852]\n● Surfaces ko rough banana (grooves, treads). [Q854, Q860, Q863]\n● Harder pressing of surfaces. [Q865]\n● Cricket bowler ball ko thigh par rubs karta hai (polishing) — isse ek side smooth aur doosri rough ho jaati hai,"," differential friction/air resistance se ball swing karti hai — grip better hoti hai. [Q881]\n● Examples: Tyre treads (better grip), brake pads, gymnasts' chalk, shoe soles with grooves. [Q854, Q860, Q863, Q865,\nQ962]\n● Lubricants: Oil, grease, graphite — thin film banate hain between surfaces. [Q856, Q857, Q858, Q866, Q877]\n● Ball bearings: Replace sliding friction with rolling friction. [Q872]\n● Air cushion: Between moving parts. [Q871]\n● Polishing, streamlining. [Q860]\n● Examples: Luggage with rollers, ball bearings in ceiling fans/bicycles. [Q864, Q872]\n5. Pressure: Definition, Units & Atmospheric Pressure\n● Pressure (P) = Force/Area = F/A = Thrust per unit area; unit = Pascal (Pa) = N/m². [Q873, Q885, Q918, Q921, Q952,\nQ955]\n● P = F/A → pressure inversely proportional to area. [Q918, Q952]\n● Nail ki nok nukti → small area → larger pressure (P = F/A). [Q873]\n● Snowshoes → large area → smaller pressure on snow. [Q952]\n● Knife blades sharp (small area) → high pressure for cutting. [Q952]\n● Thrust = force acting perpendicular to surface; T = v(dm/dt). [Q870, Q925]\n● ATM = unit of measuring pressure; 1 ATM = 101325 Pa = 760 mm Hg = 14.7 psi. [Q884]\n● Atmospheric pressure = force exerted by weight of Earth's atmosphere on surface. [Q913]\n● Barometer = measures air pressure; sudden decrease → stormy weather indicated. [Q914]\n● Stress = restoring force per unit area = F/A; unit = N/m² or Pascal. [Q900]\n● Sound waves mein compressions un jagah bante hain jahan air pressure high hoti hai (rarefaction = low\npressure/density regions). [Q899]\n6. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n● Scalar: Only magnitude — distance, speed, mass, temperature, energy, work, volume, area, time. [Q843]\n● Vector: Magnitude + direction — force, torque, displacement, velocity, momentum, acceleration. [Q843, Q898,\nQ919]\n7. Fundamental Forces\n● Gravitational force = weakest of four fundamental forces. [Q844]\n● Nuclear force = strongest fundamental force. [Q844]\n● Electric force = interaction between charged bodies. [Q844]\n● Buoyant force = upward force by fluid on immersed object. [Q844]\n● Moon Earth ke around near-circular orbit mein centripetal force ki wajah se move karta hai — ye gravitational\nattraction se milta hai jo Moon ko curved path mein rakhta hai (centrifugal, mechanical, ya frictional force nahi).\n[Q859]\n8. Kepler's Laws of Planetary Motion"," ● Law of Orbits: All planets move in elliptical orbits, Sun at one focus. [Q845]\n● Law of Areas: Line joining planet to Sun sweeps equal areas in equal intervals of time. [Q845]\n● Law of Periods: Square of period cube of semimajor axis (T² r³).\n∝\n∝\n [Q845]\n9. Spring Balance & Hooke's Law\n● Spring balance = measures force/weight; works on Hooke's Law: F = -kx. [Q841, Q867, Q874]\n● k = spring constant, x = displacement from rest position. [Q841]\n● Coiled spring stretches when force applied → pointer moves on graduated scale. [Q867, Q874]\n● Types of springs: helical, leaf, torsion, disc, conical volute, compression, extension, spiral. [Q867, Q874]\n10. Work, Energy, Momentum & Equations of Motion\n● Work (W) = Force × displacement × cosθ = F·d·cosθ. [Q890, Q915, Q941]\n– θ = 0° → positive work; θ = 90° → zero work; θ = 180° → negative work. [Q890, Q916, Q941]\n● Energy: Capability to do work; forms = potential (P.E = mgh) + kinetic (K.E = mv²/2); unit = Joule. [Q902]\n● Momentum (p) = mass × velocity = mv; vector; unit = kg m/s. [Q898, Q901, Q910, Q946, Q950, Q951]\n– Conservation of Momentum: Total momentum of closed system remains constant. [Q950]\n– In collision → momentum is always conserved. [Q950]\n● Equations of Motion (constant acceleration, straight line):\n– v = u + at → Velocity-Time relation (First equation). [Q897, Q923]\n– s = ut + (1/2)at² → Position-Time relation (Second equation). [Q903, Q908]\n– v² = u² + 2as → Position-Velocity relation (Third equation). [Q908, Q934]\n● Velocity = rate of change of displacement with time; vector. [Q896, Q919]\n● Speed = rate of change of distance with time; scalar. [Q919, Q930]\n● Acceleration = rate of change of velocity with time. [Q896, Q957]\n● Average speed/average velocity = explain motion during a given time interval. [Q917, Q930]\n● Uniform acceleration: velocity increases by equal amounts in equal intervals of time. [Q947, Q953]\n● Positive acceleration → velocity increases; Negative acceleration (retardation) → velocity decreases. [Q891, Q905,\nQ937, Q947]\n● Zero acceleration → body has constant velocity (not necessarily zero). [Q907, Q954]\n● Uniform speed par acceleration = zero. [Q907]\n● Two equal forces opposite directions → net force = zero. [Q904]\n● Velocity-time graph ka slope = acceleration; area under curve = displacement. [Q933]\n11. Stress, Thrust & Tension\n● Stress = restoring force per unit area = F/A; unit = N/m² or Pascal; depends on area. [Q900]\n● Thrust = force acting perpendicular to surface; T = v(dm/dt); unit = Newton. [Q870, Q925]\n● Tension = force transmitted when rope/string pulled from both ends; T = mg. [Q927]\n● Perseverance/Rigidity = property to maintain shape under external force. [Q912]"," 12. Types of Motion\n● Uniform motion: Equal distances in equal time intervals. [Q935, Q945]\n– Examples: Airplane flying at constant speed, train on straight tracks. [Q935]\n● Non-uniform motion: Different speeds in equal time intervals. [Q935, Q945]\n– Examples: Bus on crowded road, bike in traffic, 100m race, bouncy ball. [Q935, Q945]\n● Uniform circular motion: Constant speed in circular path; velocity changes continuously (direction). [Q931]\n● Curvilinear motion: Motion along curved path (projectile, planets around Sun). [Q942]\n● Oscillatory motion: Back-and-forth motion about mean position. [Q931]\n13. Inertia, Mass & Weight\n● Inertia: Tendency to resist change in state of rest/motion; directly proportional to mass. [Q876, Q892, Q920, Q926,\nQ958]\n– Greater mass → greater inertia → greater force needed to accelerate. [Q958]\n● Mass = amount of matter in object; constant (does not change with location); scalar; unit = kg. [Q920, Q936]\n● Weight = force with which Earth attracts object; W = mg; vector; unit = Newton (N). [Q924, Q959, Q963]\n– Weight varies with location (gravity changes); mass remains constant. [Q959]\n● SI units: Mass = kg, Length = m, Time = s, Current = A, Temperature = K, Amount = mol, Luminous intensity = cd.\n[Q963]\n14. Balanced vs Unbalanced Forces\n● Balanced force: Net force = zero → no acceleration → no change in speed/direction. [Q928, Q949]\n– Can still cause change in shape (deformation/compression/stretching). [Q949]\n● Unbalanced force: Required to change speed or direction of motion. [Q949]\n● Object moves with constant speed jab force negligible ho (Newton's first law). [Q928]\n15. Impulse & Safety Applications\n● Impulse = Force × Time = change in momentum. [Q943]\n● Helmet increases impact time → reduces force on head (for same momentum change). [Q943]\n● Formula: Impulse = F × t; for same Δp, increasing t reduces F. [Q943]\n16. Miscellaneous Concepts\n● Liquefaction of gases: Decrease temperature + increase pressure. [Q922]\n● Hot dry day: High temperature + low humidity → increased evaporation → cooling. [Q922]\n● Displacement: Shortest distance between initial and final positions; measured along straight line; vector. [Q956]\n– Can be zero even if distance travelled is non-zero (return to start). [Q956]\n● Ball thrown vertically upward: Initial velocity positive upwards (by convention). [Q948]\n– As rises → gravity decelerates → positive velocity reduces → zero at highest point → negative as falls. [Q948]"," ● Muscles stretching ka example: flag hoisting — jab flag ko upar khinchte hain, rope ke saath saath\narms/shoulders/back ki muscles bhi elongate/stretch hoti hain (door open karna ya box push karna stretching\nnahi hai). [Q944]\n17.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q836–Q965)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Archimedes' Principle = buoyant force; Pascal's Law = pressure transmitted equally in fluid; Bernoulli's\nPrinciple = speed increase → pressure decrease. [Q836]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Boyle's Law = PV = constant (constant T); Charles's = V T (constant P); Gay-Lussac's = P T (constant\n∝\n∝\nV). [Q837]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Friction order: Static > Sliding > Rolling (static strongest, rolling least). [Q842]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Static friction > sliding friction (not equal, not less). [Q875]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Friction cannot be totally eliminated by polishing/lubrication. [Q861]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rolling friction < sliding friction → luggage mein rollers use hote hain. [Q864]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lubricants (oil/grease/graphite) reduce friction, increase nahi. [Q857, Q866]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Drag = fluid friction; air resistance = frictional force by air. [Q878, Q879]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nail pointed → small area → more pressure (P = F/A). [Q873, Q918]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Newton's Third Law examples = rocket, equal reaction force chahe masses alag ho; First Law = inertia\nexamples (bus jerk, coin in tumbler). [Q887, Q889, Q940, Q985]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Retardation = negative acceleration (not positive, not variable). [Q905, Q937]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Uniform speed → acceleration = zero. [Q907]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work negative jab θ = 180° (force opposite to displacement). [Q916, Q941]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Momentum depends on both mass and velocity (not just one). [Q910, Q946]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force never occurs singly in nature (action-reaction pair). [Q893, Q960]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Spring balance measures force, not mass directly. [Q841]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Barometer drop → stormy weather, not warm/cold/pleasant. [Q914]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Action-reaction forces act on different bodies, never same body. [Q929]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Zero acceleration → constant velocity (not necessarily zero velocity). [Q954]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Balanced force → can cause change in shape but not motion. [Q949]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weight = vector (magnitude + direction); Mass = scalar. [Q959, Q963]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weight unit = Newton; Mass unit = kg. [Q963]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force definition = Second Law (F = ma), not First or Third. [Q964]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Velocity-time graph slope = acceleration; area = displacement. [Q933]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Instantaneous velocity = average velocity jab zero acceleration ho. [Q939]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Inertia mass (not velocity, not force).\n∝\n [Q920, Q926, Q958]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Positive acceleration → velocity increases; negative → decreases. [Q947, Q937]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Displacement measured along straight line (not curved path). [Q956]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Compression = high pressure/density region; rarefaction = low pressure/density region (sound wave).\n[Q899]\n18. Numerical: Newton's Second Law (F = ma)\n● Force ka formula F = ma hota hai; acceleration a = (v-u)/t se nikalta hai. [Q966, Q969, Q976, Q984, Q986, Q987, Q989,\nQ994, Q995, Q1000, Q1004, Q1036, Q1045, Q1055, Q1056, Q1057]"," ● Agar object constant velocity se chal raha hai toh acceleration zero aur force bhi zero hota hai. [Q970]\n● Retarding force ke case mein force ka direction motion ke opposite hota hai, isliye angle 180° hota hai. [Q974]\n● Example: 10 kg ki body ka velocity 2 sec mein 5 m/s se 10 m/s badhe toh a=(10-5)/2=2.5 m/s² aur F=25 N; 5 sec\naur lagane par final velocity 17.5 m/s hoti hai. [Q966]\n● Rest se 2 sec mein 5 m/s speed pakadne wali body ka acceleration = (5-0)/2 = 2.5 m/s². [Q969]\n● 2 kg body 4 m/s² acceleration se chale toh net force F = 2×4 = 8 N. [Q976]\n● 8 kg body ka velocity 4 se 9 m/s 2 sec mein badhe toh F=20 N hota hai. [Q984]\n● Bullet (12 g) barrel se 0.006 sec mein 600 m/s velocity se nikle toh force F=(m×v)/t = (0.012×600)/0.006 = 1200 N.\n[Q986]\n● Dusra similar bullet example (12 g, 0.006 sec, 300 m/s): a=(300-0)/0.006=50000 m/s², F=ma=0.012×50000=600 N.\n[Q987]\n● 100 kg body par 200 N force laga toh 6 sec mein velocity 5 se 17 m/s ho jaati hai. [Q989]\n● 500 kg ki car par 350 N force laga toh acceleration 0.7 m/s² milta hai. [Q971]\n● 20 kg block par 80 N force laga toh acceleration 4 m/s² hota hai. [Q1036]\n● 1000 kg ki car ko 20 m/s se 4 sec mein rokne ke liye 5000 N ka retarding force chahiye. [Q1045]\n● 3 kg mass par 21 N force laga toh acceleration 7 m/s² hota hai. [Q1055]\n● 10 kg mass par 20 N force laga toh acceleration 2 m/s² hota hai. [Q1056]\n● 10 kg mass par 10 N force laga toh acceleration 1 m/s² hota hai. [Q1057]\n● 100 kg body par 200 N force laga toh acceleration = 200/100 = 2 ms⁻² (unit hamesha ms⁻², ms⁻¹ nahi). [Q1004]\n● Agar same force F do alag masses ko alag acceleration a₁ aur a₂ deti ho, toh combined mass pe acceleration\n(a₁×a₂)/(a₁+a₂) hoti hai. [Q1058]\n19. Numerical: Equations of Motion\n● Pehli equation: v = u + at — velocity aur time ka relation. [Q966, Q979, Q982, Q993, Q994, Q1002, Q1006, Q1008, Q1020,\nQ1022, Q1025, Q1027, Q1030, Q1038, Q1039, Q1044, Q1048]\n● Dusri equation: s = ut + ½at² — displacement aur time ka relation. [Q968, Q975, Q999, Q1005, Q1018, Q1021, Q1028,\nQ1034]\n● Teesri equation: v² = u² + 2as — velocity aur displacement ka relation bina time ke. [Q998, Q1024]\n● Free fall mein hamesha initial velocity u = 0 aur acceleration a = g = 10 m/s² (ya 9.8) lete hain. [Q968, Q975, Q998,\nQ999, Q1006, Q1018, Q1020, Q1022, Q1025, Q1034, Q1044]\n● Upward throw mein acceleration negative (-g) hota hai kyunki gravity motion ko oppose karti hai. [Q978, Q1002,\nQ1026, Q1039, Q1040]\n● Upar fekne par highest point par velocity momentarily zero hoti hai. [Q1026]\n● 0.8 sec free fall mein body 3.2 m niche girti hai. [Q975]\n● 4 sec free fall mein body 80 m niche girti hai. [Q999]\n● 8 sec mein acceleration 3 m/s² se body 96 m travel karti hai. [Q1034]\n● 20 m height se girne par body ki final velocity 20 m/s hoti hai. [Q998]\n● 25 m/s se upar fekne par body ko top tak pahunchne mein 2.5 sec lagte hain. [Q1002]\n● 0.5 sec free fall ke baad velocity 5 m/s hoti hai. [Q1006]\n● 0.7 sec, 0.8 sec, 0.9 sec, aur 1 sec free fall ke baad velocities 7, 8, 9, aur 10 m/s hoti hain respectively. [Q1020,\nQ1022, Q1025, Q1044]\n● 10 m/s se start karke 5 sec mein 20 m/s velocity badhne ke liye 2 m/s² acceleration chahiye. [Q1027]\n● 10 sec mein 200 m travel karne ke liye rest se 4 m/s² acceleration chahiye. [Q1028]\n● 1 m/s² acceleration se 120 sec mein velocity 120 m/s ho jaati hai. [Q1030]\n● Ball upar fekne par total time agar 13.5 sec ho toh initial velocity 67.5 m/s hoti hai (t_up = 6.75 sec). [Q1039]"," ● Mount Everest par g ka value kam hota hai standard 9.8 se kyunki doori zyada hai. [Q1040]\n● Rocket ka height equation h = 119t - 7t² ho toh wapas ground par 17 sec baad aayegi. [Q1005]\n20. Numerical: Distance in nth Second\n● nth second mein travel ki hui doori ka formula: s = u + a(n - ½) ya s = u + (a/2)(2n-1).\nₙ\nₙ\n [Q968, Q1029]\n● Rest se 4th second mein (a=10) body 35 m travel karti hai. [Q968]\n● Rest se 3rd second mein (a=4/3) body 10/3 m travel karti hai. [Q1029]\n21. Numerical: Conservation of Momentum\n● Closed system mein total momentum hamesha conserved rehta hai: initial momentum = final momentum. [Q967,\nQ980, Q981, Q1009, Q1011, Q1013, Q1014, Q1017]\n● Gun initially at rest ho toh total initial momentum zero hota hai; bullet aage jaati hai aur gun peche khisakti hai.\n[Q967, Q1011, Q1013, Q1014, Q1017]\n● Recoil velocity ka formula: v_gun = -(m_bullet × v_bullet) / m_gun; negative sign opposite direction batata hai.\n[Q967, Q1011, Q1013, Q1014, Q1017]\n● 0.04 kg shell 90 m/s se fire ho 120 kg gun se toh recoil speed 3×10⁻² m/s hoti hai. [Q967]\n● 0.02 kg bullet 150 m/s se 3 kg pistol se toh recoil 1.0 m/s hoti hai. [Q1011]\n● 0.025 kg bullet 150 m/s se 2 kg pistol se toh recoil ≈ 1.87 m/s hoti hai. [Q1013]\n● 0.03 kg bullet 150 m/s se 2 kg pistol se toh recoil 2.25 m/s hoti hai. [Q1014]\n● 0.03 kg bullet 150 m/s se 3 kg pistol se toh recoil 1.5 m/s hoti hai. [Q1017]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Q1009 mein official answer key mein values mismatch thi; exam mein official key follow karo. [Q1009]\n● Collision mein: m₁u₁ + m₂u₂ = (m₁+m₂)v jab dono stick ho jaayein; jaise 2000 kg truck 10 m/s se 500 kg car se takra\nke 8 m/s chale toh car ka mass 500 kg nikalta hai. [Q980]\n22. Numerical: Weight (W = mg) & Moon Weight\n● Weight ka formula W = mg hota hai; mass ka formula m = W/g. [Q972, Q988, Q990, Q1007, Q1010, Q1012, Q1015,\nQ1016, Q1019, Q1023, Q1031, Q1032, Q1042, Q1049, Q1050, Q1051, Q1052]\n● Earth par g ≈ 9.8 m/s² (ya 10 m/s² agar question mein specify ho). [Q972, Q988, Q990, Q1010, Q1049, Q1051]\n● 450 N weight wale body ka mass g=9.8 par ≈ 45.9 kg hota hai. [Q972]\n● 20 kg body ka weight g=9.8 par 196 N hota hai. [Q990]\n● 20 kg body ka weight g=10 par 200 N hota hai. [Q1007]\n● 10 kg body ka weight g=10 par 100 N hota hai. [Q1023]\n● 200 N weight wale body ka mass g=10 par 20 kg hota hai. [Q1031]\n● 100 kg body ka weight g=9.8 par 980 N hota hai. [Q1049]\n● 98 N weight wale body ka mass g=9.8 par 10 kg hota hai. [Q1051]\n● Moon par weight = Earth weight / 6 kyunki g_moon = g_earth/6 hota hai. [Q1001, Q1012, Q1016, Q1019, Q1032,\nQ1042, Q1050, Q1052]\n● Earth par 60 N weight wale body ka Moon par weight 10 N hota hai. [Q1001, Q1012, Q1019, Q1032]\n● Earth par 20 N weight wale body ka Moon par weight ≈ 3.33 N hota hai. [Q1042]\n● Moon par 300 N weight wale body ka Earth par weight 1800 N hota hai. [Q1052]\n● Mass Moon par bhi same rehti hai — sirf weight badalta hai. [Q1033]"," ● Earth weight hamesha Moon weight ka 6 guna hota hai. [Q1016, Q1050]\n23. Numerical: Momentum (p = mv)\n● Momentum ka formula p = mv hota hai; unit kg m/s. [Q977, Q983, Q991, Q992, Q996, Q1037, Q1041, Q1043]\n● 80 kg rider 60 m/s se ja raha ho toh momentum 4800 kg m/s hota hai. [Q977]\n● Mass aadhi aur velocity double karne par momentum same (mv) rehta hai. [Q983]\n● 200 g (0.2 kg) ball jiski kinetic energy 10 J ho uska momentum 2 kg m/s hota hai (pehle v=10 m/s nikalo). [Q991]\n● 10 kg body 2 m/s se ja rahi ho toh momentum 20 kg m/s hota hai. [Q992]\n● Momentum 50 aur velocity 5 ho toh mass 10 kg nikalti hai. [Q1037]\n● 50 kg body 6 m/s se ja rahi ho toh momentum 300 kg m/s hota hai. [Q1041]\n● 50 kg body 20 m/s se ja rahi ho toh momentum 1000 kg m/s hota hai. [Q1043]\n● Same kinetic energy wali bodies mein momentum √m ke proportional hota hai; mass ratio 1:9 ho toh momentum\nratio 1:3 hota hai. [Q1046]\n24. Numerical: Unit Conversions\n● km/h ko m/s mein convert karne ke liye 5/18 se multiply karte hain. [Q973, Q993, Q1008, Q1027, Q1048]\n● 90 km/h = 25 m/s; 72 km/h = 20 m/s; 54 km/h = 15 m/s; 36 km/h = 10 m/s; 18 km/h = 5 m/s. [Q973, Q993, Q1008,\nQ1027, Q1048]\n25. Numerical: Work Done & Energy\n● Work ka formula W = Fd cosθ hota hai. [Q974, Q1054]\n● Agar 20 N force se 2 m displacement mein 20 J work ho toh force aur displacement ke beech angle 60° hota hai\n(cosθ = 1/2). [Q1054]\n● Spring compression mein block ki kinetic energy spring ki potential energy mein convert hoti hai: ½mv² = ½kx².\n[Q1047]\n● 2 kg block 4 m/s se chal ke spring ko compress kare toh k=10000 N/m ke liye compression ≈ 5.5 cm hoti hai.\n[Q1047]\n26. Numerical: Gravitational Force\n● Do masses ke beech gravitational force F = Gm₁m₂/r² se milti hai; G = 6.673×10⁻¹¹ Nm²/kg². [Q1053]\n● 20 kg aur 50 kg ke beech 2 m doori par force 166.75×10⁻¹⁰ N hoti hai. [Q1053]\n27. Numerical: Cricket Ball / Retarding Force\n● Cricket ball ko rokne par lagne wala retarding force F = m(v-u)/t se nikalta hai. [Q1035]\n● 100 g (0.1 kg) ball 30 m/s se 0.05 sec mein ruke toh -60 N ka retarding force lagta hai. [Q1035]"," 28.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (Numerical Q966–Q1058)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acceleration ka unit hamesha m/s² hota hai; m/s (velocity) nahi. [Q971, Q982, Q1034]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force ka unit Newton (N) hota hai; Pa, Joule, kg, ya m/s² nahi. [Q989, Q997, Q1003, Q1031]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Momentum ka unit kg m/s hota hai; kg m/s² (jo N hota hai) nahi. [Q977, Q992, Q1041]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weight ka unit Newton hota hai; kg mass ka unit hai. [Q1007, Q1023, Q1031, Q1049]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Moon par weight 1/6 ho jaata hai lekin mass same rehti hai. [Q1016, Q1033, Q1050, Q1052]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Recoil velocity hamesha negative hoti hai kyunki direction opposite hoti hai. [Q967, Q1011, Q1013, Q1014,\nQ1017]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: nth second ki doori ke liye formula s = u + a(n - ½) use hota hai; direct multiply mat karna.\nₙ\n [Q968, Q1029]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Upward throw mein acceleration -g lete hain (negative). [Q978, Q1002, Q1039]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Highest point par velocity zero hoti hai, -g nahi. [Q1026]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: km/h → m/s conversion ke liye 5/18 se multiply karte hain, 18/5 se nahi. [Q973, Q993, Q1048]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Q1009 mein official answer key mein values ka mismatch tha; solve karke official key se match karo.\n[Q1009]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work negative tab hota hai jab force aur displacement ke beech angle 90° se zyada ho. [Q1054]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gravitational constant G = 6.673×10⁻¹¹; power 10⁻¹¹ mat bhoolna. [Q1053]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Spring compression ke numerical mein answer cm ya m mein dekh ke unit check karo. [Q1047]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ball upar fekne par total time = 2 × time to reach top. [Q1039, Q1040]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 5 Force and Pressure Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0408","t":"06 Sound","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.6 — SOUND — FULL MIND MAP\n🔊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Audible Range: Infrasonic & Ultrasonic\n2. Sound Needs Medium: Solid, Liquid, Gas, Vacuum\n3. Speed of Sound: Formula, Factors & Numericals\n4. Sound Properties: Loudness, Pitch, Quality/Timbre\n5. Echo & Reverberation\n6. Reflection of Sound: Laws & Applications\n7. SONAR & Ultrasound Applications\n8. Musical Instruments & Sound Production\n9. Noise Pollution & Hearing\n10. Human Ear Structure\n11. Vibrations, Frequency & Time Period\n12. Doppler Effect\n13. Beats & Resonance\n14. Miscellaneous Sound Facts\n15.\n Traps / Master Formula Cheat Sheet (Q1059–Q1150)\n⚠️\n1. Audible Range: Infrasonic & Ultrasonic\n● Manushya ki audible range = 20 Hz se 20,000 Hz tak. [Q1059]\n● Infrasonic = 20 Hz se kam frequency; earthquakes, thunder, volcanes; hathi aur whale sun sakte hain. [Q1059]\n● Ultrasonic = 20,000 Hz se zyada frequency; kutte, billi, moth, chuhe sun sakte hain. [Q1059]\n● Frequency zyada → pitch zyada; frequency kam → pitch kam. [Q1067, Q1095, Q1101]\n● Loudness amplitude par depend karti hai; shrillness frequency par depend karti hai. [Q1101, Q1110]\n● Sound sensation human brain mein karib 0.1 sec tak persist karti hai (persistence of hearing) — isi wajah se echo\nsunne ke liye original sound aur reflected sound ke beech minimum 0.1 sec ka gap chahiye. [Q1132]\n2. Sound Needs Medium: Solid, Liquid, Gas, Vacuum\n● Sound ek mechanical wave hai → medium zaroori hai. [Q1060, Q1086, Q1090, Q1091, Q1094, Q1118]\n● Sound vacuum mein travel nahi kar sakti. [Q1060, Q1086, Q1090]\n● Sound solid, liquid, aur gas teeno mein travel kar sakti hai. [Q1060, Q1094]\n● Sabse tez solid mein, phir liquid, sabse dheere gas mein. [Q1061, Q1082, Q1087, Q1093, Q1111]\n– Solid mein particles closest hote hain. [Q1087, Q1093]\n● Speed: steel ≈ 5000 m/s, water ≈ 1500 m/s, air ≈ 330 m/s. [Q1061, Q1082, Q1087, Q1093, Q1111]\n● Lightning pehle dikhti hai, thunder baad mein kyunki light >>> sound speed. [Q1068, Q1084, Q1112]\n● Space mein astronauts radio use karte hain kyunki sound vacuum mein nahi jaati. [Q1090, Q1118]\n3. Speed of Sound: Formula, Factors & Numericals\n● Speed temperature par depend karti hai — summer mein sound speed winter se zyada hoti hai (temperature"," zyada = speed zyada), season independent nahi hoti. [Q1062, Q1074, Q1080, Q1092, Q1099, Q1106, Q1117, Q1131]\n● Formula: v = f × λ (frequency × wavelength). [Q1136, Q1137, Q1138, Q1139, Q1140, Q1141, Q1142, Q1143, Q1144, Q1145,\nQ1146, Q1147, Q1148, Q1149, Q1150]\n● Formula: v = 331 + (0.6 × T°C) m/s. [Q1074, Q1092]\n● 0°C par ≈ 331 m/s; 25°C par ≈ 346 m/s. [Q1062, Q1074, Q1106]\n● Air pressure badhne par speed kam hoti hai (density zyada). [Q1080, Q1106]\n● Humidity badhne par speed zyada hoti hai (water vapour halka hota hai). [Q1099, Q1117]\n● Speed frequency par depend nahi karti hai. [Q1074, Q1092, Q1106]\n● Same speed (v) constant rahe aur frequency badhe toh wavelength kam ho jaati hai (v = fλ, λ 1/f).\n∝\n [Q1134]\n● Water mein air se 4 times tez; steel mein air se 15 times tez. [Q1082, Q1111]\n● Lightning-thunder time gap se distance: distance = speed × time ≈ 330 × t. [Q1068, Q1084, Q1112]\n– 3 sec gap → ≈ 1 km. [Q1068, Q1112]\n● Time period 0.02 sec ho toh frequency = 1/0.02 = 50 Hz. [Q1135]\n● Frequency 200 Hz, wavelength 2 m ho toh speed = 200×2 = 400 m/s. [Q1136]\n● Wavelength 0.50 m, frequency 1000 Hz ho toh speed = 1000×0.50 = 500 m/s. [Q1137]\n● Wavelength 0.20 m, speed 400 m/s ho toh frequency = 400/0.20 = 2000 Hz. [Q1138]\n● Wavelength 2.0 cm = 0.02 m, speed 340 m/s ho toh frequency = 340/0.02 = 17000 Hz = 17 kHz. [Q1139]\n● Frequency 10 kHz = 10000 Hz, speed 340 m/s ho toh wavelength = 340/10000 = 0.034 m = 3.4 cm. [Q1140]\n● Wavelength 0.675 m, frequency 500 Hz ho toh speed = 500×0.675 = 337.5 m/s. [Q1141]\n● Wavelength 0.85 m, frequency 400 Hz ho toh speed = 400×0.85 = 340 m/s. [Q1142]\n● Speed 330 m/s, frequency 165 Hz ho toh wavelength = 330/165 = 2 m. [Q1143]\n● Speed 340 m/s, frequency 170 Hz ho toh wavelength = 340/170 = 2 m. [Q1144]\n● Speed 330 m/s, frequency 220 Hz ho toh wavelength = 330/220 = 1.5 m. [Q1145]\n● Speed 440 m/s, wavelength 1.1 m ho toh frequency = 440/1.1 = 400 Hz. [Q1146]\n● Speed 500 m/s, wavelength 2.5 m ho toh frequency = 500/2.5 = 200 Hz. [Q1147]\n● Speed 300 m/s, wavelength 1.5 m ho toh frequency = 300/1.5 = 200 Hz. [Q1148]\n● Frequency 200 Hz, speed 400 m/s ho toh wavelength = 400/200 = 2 m. [Q1149]\n● Frequency 250 Hz, speed 500 m/s ho toh wavelength = 500/250 = 2 m. [Q1150]\n4. Sound Properties: Loudness, Pitch, Quality/Timbre\n● Loudness = amplitude par depend; unit = decibel (dB). [Q1067, Q1101, Q1110, Q1114]\n– 0 dB = hearing threshold; 120 dB = pain threshold. [Q1110]\n● Pitch = frequency par depend, na ki timbre, amplitude ya intensity par. [Q1067, Q1095, Q1101, Q1110, Q1133]\n– Zyada frequency → zyada pitch (ladies/children). [Q1067, Q1095]\n– Kam frequency → kam pitch (males). [Q1067]\n● Quality/Timbre = waveform par depend; same pitch/loudness wali alag instruments ki awaaz alag. [Q1101, Q1110]\n● Sound graph: crest, trough, wavelength, amplitude. [Q1101, Q1110]\n5. Echo & Reverberation\n● Echo = reflected sound jo original se at least 0.1 sec baad mile (persistence of hearing ke barabar). [Q1063, Q1071,\nQ1088, Q1096, Q1102, Q1113, Q1124, Q1132]"," ● Minimum doori = 17.2 m (speed 344 m/s maan ke). [Q1071, Q1088, Q1096, Q1102, Q1113, Q1124]\n– Formula: d = (v × t)/2 = (344 × 0.1)/2. [Q1071, Q1132]\n● Reverberation = repeated reflection (0.1 sec se kam gap). [Q1063, Q1076, Q1088, Q1102, Q1113, Q1120]\n● Reverberation kam karne ke liye soft porous materials (curtains, cushions, carpets). [Q1076, Q1120]\n● Echo se distance measure kar sakte hain (SONAR principle). [Q1063, Q1124]\n6. Reflection of Sound: Laws & Applications\n● 3 laws: incident ray = reflected ray angle; same plane; normal ke opposite sides. [Q1069, Q1081, Q1098, Q1105]\n● Applications:\n– Megaphone/loudhailer → tube shape se focus. [Q1064, Q1078, Q1085, Q1103, Q1119, Q1126]\n– Hearing aid → weak sounds amplify. [Q1064, Q1078, Q1119]\n– Stethoscope → body sounds capture aur doctor tak. [Q1064, Q1078, Q1103, Q1119]\n– Sound boards → concave surfaces se audience tak focus. [Q1064, Q1085, Q1103, Q1126]\n– Whispering gallery → dome shape. [Q1085, Q1126]\n● Concave surface se sound focus ho sakti hai. [Q1078, Q1103, Q1126]\n7. SONAR & Ultrasound Applications\n● SONAR = underwater objects detect karne ke liye ultrasonic waves. [Q1065, Q1072, Q1079, Q1097, Q1109, Q1123,\nQ1127, Q1130]\n● Principle: pulse bhejo → reflect hokar wapas aaye → time se distance. [Q1065, Q1079, Q1109]\n● Formula: Distance = (speed × time)/2. [Q1065, Q1072, Q1127]\n● Applications: Submarine, sea depth, fish finding. [Q1065, Q1079, Q1109, Q1123, Q1130]\n● Ultrasound applications:\n– Flaw detection (cracks). [Q1072, Q1097, Q1123, Q1127, Q1130]\n– Medical imaging/sonography. [Q1072, Q1097, Q1123, Q1130]\n– Cleaning delicate parts. [Q1072, Q1097, Q1130]\n– Breaking kidney stones (lithotripsy). [Q1072, Q1097]\n● Bat aur dolphin ultrasound use karte hain navigation ke liye. [Q1079, Q1109]\n● SONAR frequency range = 20 kHz se 100 kHz. [Q1130]\n8. Musical Instruments & Sound Production\n● Sound vibration se produce hoti hai. [Q1066, Q1089, Q1094, Q1107, Q1115, Q1121, Q1128]\n● String instruments (guitar, sitar, violin): string vibrate karti hai. [Q1066, Q1089, Q1107, Q1115]\n– Length kam → frequency zyada → pitch zyada. [Q1066, Q1107]\n– Tension zyada → frequency zyada. [Q1066, Q1115]\n– String patli → frequency zyada. [Q1066]\n● Wind instruments (flute, trumpet): air column vibrate karti hai. [Q1089, Q1107, Q1121]\n– Air column lamba → pitch kam; chhota → pitch zyada. [Q1089, Q1121]\n● Percussion instruments (tabla, drum): membrane vibrate karti hai. [Q1107, Q1128]"," ● Jaltarang: kam paani → zyada pitch. [Q1121]\n● Sitar mein sympathetic strings resonance se sound amplify karti hain. [Q1115]\n9. Noise Pollution & Hearing\n● Noise = unwanted sound. [Q1073, Q1104, Q1116, Q1122, Q1129]\n● Sources: vehicles, machines, loudspeakers, crackers, aircraft. [Q1073, Q1104, Q1116, Q1122]\n● Effects: hearing loss, stress, high BP, sleep disturbance. [Q1073, Q1104, Q1122, Q1129]\n● Control:\n– Source pe: silencers, maintenance. [Q1073, Q1104, Q1116]\n– Path mein: soundproof walls, barriers, trees. [Q1073, Q1116]\n– Receiver pe: earmuffs, earplugs. [Q1073, Q1104, Q1116]\n● Decibel (dB) = sound level unit.\n– 0 dB = threshold; normal conversation ≈ 60 dB; heavy traffic ≈ 70-80 dB; jet ≈ 150 dB. [Q1073, Q1110]\n● Prolonged exposure 85 dB se zyada se hearing damage. [Q1116]\n● Forests/trees noise absorb karte hain. [Q1129]\n10. Human Ear Structure\n● 3 parts: Outer ear, Middle ear, Inner ear. [Q1075, Q1083, Q1100, Q1108, Q1114]\n● Outer: Pinna + Ear canal. [Q1075, Q1083, Q1100, Q1108]\n● Middle: Eardrum + 3 bones (hammer, anvil, stirrup). [Q1075, Q1083, Q1100, Q1108, Q1114]\n● Inner: Cochlea (hair cells → electrical signals) + Auditory nerve. [Q1075, Q1083, Q1100, Q1108, Q1114]\n● Eardrum: sound → mechanical vibrations. [Q1075, Q1100]\n● Cochlea: vibrations → electrical signals. [Q1075, Q1100]\n● Ear balance bhi maintain karti hai. [Q1108]\n11. Vibrations, Frequency & Time Period\n● Frequency (f) = vibrations per second; unit = Hertz (Hz). [Q1066, Q1089, Q1094, Q1095, Q1107, Q1115, Q1121, Q1135]\n● Time period (T) = 1/f; ek vibration ka time. [Q1094, Q1121, Q1135]\n● Vibration stop → sound stop. [Q1089]\n● Sound ke liye vibrating body zaroori. [Q1094, Q1121, Q1128]\n● Stretched string: f 1/L, f √T, f 1/√μ.\n∝\n∝\n∝\n [Q1066, Q1107, Q1115]\n12. Doppler Effect\n● Source/observer move karne par apparent frequency change hoti hai. [Q1070, Q1077, Q1096, Q1102, Q1112, Q1125]\n● Source toward aaye → frequency zyada (blue shift). [Q1070, Q1096, Q1125]\n● Source away jaaye → frequency kam (red shift). [Q1070, Q1096, Q1125]\n● Applications: train whistle, police siren, astronomy (red/blue shift), RADAR, SONAR. [Q1070, Q1077, Q1096, Q1102,"," Q1112, Q1125]\n13. Beats & Resonance\n● Beats: Do frequencies interfere → loudness periodic variation; beat freq = |f₁-f₂|. [Q1113, Q1124]\n● Resonance: external freq = natural freq → vibrations zyada → sound amplify. [Q1115]\n● Sitar sympathetic strings resonance se amplify hoti hain. [Q1115]\n● Soldiers bridge par march nahi karte (resonance se collapse). [Q1115]\n14. Miscellaneous Sound Facts\n● Bell jar experiment: vacuum mein sound kam hoti hai → medium zaroori. [Q1090, Q1118]\n● Sound longitudinal wave hai; light transverse hai. [Q1091, Q1118]\n● Sound speed temperature par depend karti hai. [Q1080, Q1092, Q1099, Q1106, Q1117]\n● Sound speed frequency par depend nahi. [Q1074, Q1092, Q1106]\n● Supersonic = speed > sound; Mach > 1; Sonic boom. [Q1125]\n● Lightning pehle dikhti hai kyunki light >>> sound. [Q1068, Q1084, Q1112]\n15.\n Traps / Master Formula Cheat Sheet (Q1059–Q1150)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Audible range = 20 Hz – 20,000 Hz. [Q1059]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sound vacuum mein nahi jaati. [Q1060, Q1086, Q1090]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Speed: solid > liquid > gas. [Q1061, Q1087, Q1093]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Speed temperature par depend karti hai — summer mein winter se zyada, seasons independent nahi.\n[Q1062, Q1074, Q1099, Q1117, Q1131]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Speed frequency par depend nahi. [Q1074, Q1092, Q1106]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Echo ke liye minimum 0.1 sec aur 17.2 m. [Q1063, Q1071, Q1124, Q1132]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Loudness = amplitude; Pitch = frequency (timbre/amplitude/intensity nahi); Quality = waveform. [Q1067,\nQ1101, Q1110, Q1133]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: SONAR = ultrasound; distance = (v×t)/2. [Q1065, Q1072, Q1127]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Doppler: toward → freq zyada; away → freq kam. [Q1070, Q1096, Q1125]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ear ke 3 parts = outer, middle, inner. [Q1075, Q1083, Q1100]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 0 dB = hearing threshold; 120 dB = pain threshold. [Q1110]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sound waves longitudinal; light transverse. [Q1091, Q1118]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Numerical mein wavelength hamesha meters mein convert karo (cm → m divide by 100). [Q1139, Q1140]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: v = fλ hamesha use hota hai; frequency badhe (v constant) toh wavelength kam hoti hai, units check\nkaro. [Q1134, Q1136, Q1137, Q1138, Q1139, Q1140, Q1141, Q1142, Q1143, Q1144, Q1145, Q1146, Q1147, Q1148, Q1149, Q1150]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Frequency = 1/T; time period ka reciprocal. [Q1135]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: kHz → Hz multiply by 1000; Hz → kHz divide by 1000. [Q1139, Q1140]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lightning-thunder distance ≈ 330 × time gap meters. [Q1068, Q1084, Q1112]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 6 Sound Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0409","t":"07 Gravitation","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.7 — GRAVITATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🌍\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Mass vs Weight: Moon par Mass Same, Weight 1/6\n2. Universal Law of Gravitation: Newton's Law\n3. Gravitational Constant G\n4. Free Fall & Acceleration due to Gravity (g)\n5. g ka Variation: Height, Depth, Latitude\n6. Weightlessness\n7. Escape Velocity\n8. Kepler's Laws of Planetary Motion\n9. Centripetal Force & Satellite Motion\n10. Potential & Kinetic Energy in Gravitation\n11. Geostationary & Polar Satellites\n12. Projectile Motion\n13. Gravitational Potential\n14. Tides\n15. Miscellaneous Concepts\n16.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q1151–Q1200)\n⚠️\n17. Numerical: Acceleration due to Gravity — Planetary Variations\n18. Numerical: Variation of g with Height from Surface\n19. Numerical: Gravitational Force and Distance Relation\n20. Numerical: Gravity Effects — Weight and Jump Height\n21. Numerical: Orbital Period under Modified Force Laws\n22. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n23.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1201–Q1209)\n⚠️\n1. Mass vs Weight: Moon par Mass Same, Weight 1/6\n● Mass = intrinsic property; kahin bhi same rehti hai (Earth, Moon, space sab jagah). [Q1151, Q1157, Q1163, Q1170,\nQ1176, Q1185, Q1194]\n● Weight = W = mg; location ke hisaab se badalta hai kyunki g badalta hai. [Q1151, Q1157, Q1163, Q1170, Q1176, Q1185,\nQ1194]\n● Moon par g = g_earth/6; isliye Moon weight = Earth weight / 6. [Q1151, Q1157, Q1163, Q1170, Q1176, Q1185, Q1194]\n● 60 kg mass wale insaan ka mass Moon par bhi 60 kg hi rahega; weight ≈ 100N ho jaayega (Earth par ≈ 600N).\n[Q1151, Q1176]\n● 5 kg mass wale object ka weight Moon par 1/6 ho jaata hai. [Q1157, Q1163]\n● Mass ka SI unit kg; Weight ka SI unit Newton (N). [Q1151, Q1157, Q1185, Q1194]\n● Mass scalar hai; Weight vector hai (direction = center of body ki taraf). [Q1194]\n● Beam balance se mass measure hoti hai; Spring balance se weight measure hota hai. [Q1170, Q1185]\n● Beam balance Moon par bhi same reading degi (mass same); Spring balance 1/6 reading degi (weight kam).\n[Q1170, Q1185]\n2. Universal Law of Gravitation: Newton's Law\n● Newton's Universal Law of Gravitation (1687): Har do bodies ek doosre ko attract karti hain force se jo unke\nmasses ka product ke directly proportional aur unke beech ki doori ke square ke inversely proportional hota hai."," [Q1152, Q1158, Q1164, Q1171, Q1177, Q1186, Q1195]\n● Formula: F = G(m₁m₂)/r². [Q1152, Q1158, Q1164, Q1171, Q1177, Q1186, Q1195]\n● Is law se explain hota hai: apple ka Earth ki taraf girna, Moon ka Earth ke around ghoomna, planets ka Sun ke\naround ghoomna. [Q1158, Q1164, Q1171]\n● Gravitational force hamesha attractive hoti hai; repulsive kabhi nahi. [Q1186]\n● Force do bodies ke beech line joining par act karti hai. [Q1195]\n● Jab doori double hoti hai toh force 1/4 ho jaata hai (inverse square law). [Q1177]\n● Jab dono masses double hoti hain toh force 4 times ho jaata hai. [Q1164]\n● Scientist = Isaac Newton; book = Principia Mathematica (1687). [Q1152, Q1195]\n3. Gravitational Constant G\n● G = Universal Gravitational Constant; value = 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ Nm²/kg². [Q1159, Q1165, Q1172, Q1178, Q1187, Q1196]\n● G ka value universal hai — kahin bhi same (Earth, Moon, Mars, space sab jagah). [Q1159, Q1165, Q1172, Q1178,\nQ1187, Q1196]\n● G ka value medium par depend nahi karti (air, water, vacuum sab mein same). [Q1159, Q1178, Q1187]\n● G ka dimensional formula = [M⁻¹L³T⁻²]. [Q1172, Q1196]\n● Henry Cavendish ne pehli baar G ka value experiment se measure kiya tha (1798). [Q1165]\n● G bahut chhota hai isliye rozmarra ki chhoti objects ke beech gravitational force negligible hoti hai. [Q1196]\n4. Free Fall & Acceleration due to Gravity (g)\n● Free fall = jab koi body sirf gravity ke effect mein gir rahi ho (air resistance negligible ho). [Q1153, Q1160, Q1166,\nQ1173, Q1179, Q1188, Q1197]\n● Acceleration due to gravity (g) = Earth ke gravitational field mein kisi body ka acceleration; value ≈ 9.8 m/s² (ya 10\nm/s² approximate). [Q1153, Q1160, Q1166, Q1173, Q1179, Q1188, Q1197]\n● g ka value Earth ke surface par sab jagah same nahi — equator par kam, poles par zyada. [Q1166, Q1173, Q1179,\nQ1188]\n● g ka value altitude (height) par kam hota hai kyunki center se doori badhti hai. [Q1153, Q1160, Q1166, Q1173, Q1188,\nQ1197]\n● g ka value depth mein bhi kam hota hai (Earth ke center tak jaane par zero ho jaata hai). [Q1173, Q1188]\n● Formula: g = GM/R² (surface par). [Q1179, Q1188, Q1197]\n● Formula height par: g' = g/(1 + h/R)² ≈ g(1 - 2h/R) jab h << R. [Q1153, Q1160, Q1197]\n● Formula depth par: g' = g(1 - d/R). [Q1173, Q1188]\n● Sabhi bodies same height se same g se girte hain (Galileo's experiment) — mass, size, shape par depend nahi (air\nresistance nahi ho toh). [Q1166, Q1179, Q1193, Q1197]\n● Feather aur coin vacuum mein saath girte hain; air mein alag kyunki air resistance alag. [Q1179]\n● Free fall mein body ka weight zero feel hota hai (weightlessness). [Q1197]\n● g depend karta hai: G (constant), M (Earth ka mass), R (Earth ka radius), height, depth — falling object ke apne\nmass par NAHI depend karta. [Q1193]\n5. g ka Variation: Height, Depth, Latitude\n● Equator par g kam ≈ 9.78 m/s²; Poles par g zyada ≈ 9.83 m/s². [Q1166, Q1173, Q1179, Q1188]"," – Reason: Earth oblate spheroid hai (equator par thodi chaudi) → equator par R zyada → g kam. [Q1166]\n– Plus equator par centrifugal force maximum → g aur kam. [Q1188]\n● g height (h) par: g_h = g(R/(R+h))² → height badhne par g kam. [Q1153, Q1160, Q1197]\n● g depth (d) par: g_d = g(1 - d/R) → depth badhne par g kam; center par g = 0. [Q1173, Q1188]\n● Agar h = R (Earth ke radius jitni height) → g_h = g/4. [Q1153, Q1160]\n● Agar d = R/2 (adhi depth) → g_d = g/2. [Q1173]\n● g value maximum poles par; minimum equator par. [Q1166, Q1188]\n● Body ko equator se North ya South pole tak le jaane par weight badhta hai (g poles par zyada hone ki wajah se),\nchahe kis pole ki taraf jaayein result same hota hai. [Q1184]\n6. Weightlessness\n● Weightlessness = jab koi object apna weight \"feel\" nahi karta; normal reaction zero ho. [Q1154, Q1161, Q1167,\nQ1174, Q1180, Q1189, Q1198]\n● Astronauts space station mein weightless dikhte hain kyunki wo bhi Earth ke saath free fall mein hain. [Q1154,\nQ1161, Q1167, Q1174, Q1180, Q1189]\n● Weightlessness ka matlab gravity nahi hai — aisa nahi; gravity toh hai lekin body aur container dono saath gir\nrahe hain isliye normal force nahi lagti. [Q1161, Q1167, Q1174, Q1180, Q1189, Q1198]\n● Weightlessness mein:\n– Paani ke drops gol shape mein float karte hain.\n– Candle ka flame gol ho jaati hai.\n– Body ka blood circulation upar ki taraf shift hota hai (face swollen dikhta hai).\n– Astronauts ko exercises karni padti hain bone/muscle loss prevent karne ke liye.\n● Weightlessness sirf space mein nahi — freely falling lift mein bhi feel hota hai. [Q1154, Q1189]\n● Aircraft \"Vomit Comet\" parabolic flight mein weightlessness create karta hai training ke liye. [Q1180]\n7. Escape Velocity\n● Escape velocity (v_e) = minimum velocity jis se koi body Earth ki gravity se permanently bahar nikal jaaye. [Q1155,\nQ1162, Q1168, Q1175, Q1181, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Formula: v_e = √(2GM/R) = √(2gR). [Q1155, Q1162, Q1168, Q1175, Q1181, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Earth ke liye v_e ≈ 11.2 km/s (ya ≈ 11.2 km/sec). [Q1155, Q1162, Q1168, Q1175, Q1181, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Escape velocity mass of projectile par depend nahi karti. [Q1162, Q1175, Q1181, Q1199]\n● Escape velocity direction par depend nahi karti (kisi bhi direction mein same speed chahiye). [Q1155, Q1168]\n● Escape velocity height se kam hoti hai jab object pehle se upar ho (kyunki gravity kam). [Q1190]\n● Moon ka escape velocity ≈ 2.38 km/s (Earth se kam kyunki Moon ki mass aur radius kam). [Q1168, Q1199]\n● Agar koi body 11.2 km/s se kam velocity se throw kare toh Earth ke around orbit mein ghoomegi ya wapas gir\njaayegi. [Q1155, Q1175]\n● Escape velocity = √2 × orbital velocity. [Q1190]\n8. Kepler's Laws of Planetary Motion\n● Kepler's First Law (Law of Orbits): Planets elliptical orbits mein ghoomte hain, Sun ek focus par hota hai. [Q1156,\nQ1169, Q1175, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]"," ● Kepler's Second Law (Law of Areas): Planet-Sun line equal areas in equal times mein sweep karti hai → planets\nSun ke paas tez, door slow. [Q1156, Q1169, Q1175, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n● Kepler's Third Law (Law of Periods): T² r³ (period ka square semimajor axis ka cube).\n∝\n∝\n [Q1156, Q1169, Q1175,\nQ1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n– Yaani (T₁/T₂)² = (r₁/r₂)³. [Q1169, Q1182, Q1191]\n● Example: Agar kisi planet ka distance 4 times ho toh period = 8 times (kyunki T² = 4³ = 64 → T = 8). [Q1169]\n● Kepler ne ye laws Tycho Brahe ke observations se derive kiye. [Q1156, Q1191]\n● Newton ne in laws ko apne gravitation law se mathematically prove kiya. [Q1191]\n● Ye sirf planets ke liye nahi — koi bhi satellite ya moon ke liye valid hain. [Q1200]\n9. Centripetal Force & Satellite Motion\n● Satellite Earth ke around tabhi ghoom sakta hai jab gravitational force = centripetal force ho. [Q1156, Q1169, Q1175,\nQ1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n● Centripetal force = mv²/r = mω²r. [Q1156, Q1182]\n● Gravitational force hi centripetal force provide karti hai satellite ke liye. [Q1156, Q1175, Q1182, Q1200]\n● Satellite ki orbital speed: v = √(GM/r). [Q1156, Q1182, Q1191]\n● Satellite ka period: T = 2π√(r³/GM). [Q1169, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n● Higher orbit → lesser speed → greater period. [Q1191, Q1200]\n● Geo-stationary satellite ka period = 24 hours (Earth ke rotation ke barabar) → height ≈ 36,000 km. [Q1156, Q1182,\nQ1191, Q1200]\n● Polar satellites pole to pole orbit mein hain; Earth rotate karti hai isliye poori Earth cover ho jaati hai. [Q1182]\n● Satellites ke uses: communication, weather forecasting, GPS, remote sensing. [Q1182, Q1191]\n10. Potential & Kinetic Energy in Gravitation\n● Gravitational potential energy (PE) = -GMm/r (negative kyunki infinity par zero maana jaata hai). [Q1162, Q1175,\nQ1181, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Kinetic energy (KE) = ½mv² = GMm/(2r) (circular orbit mein). [Q1162, Q1190]\n● Total energy (TE) = PE + KE = -GMm/(2r). [Q1162, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Total energy hamesha negative hoti hai bound orbit ke liye. [Q1162, Q1190, Q1199]\n● Binding energy = |TE| = GMm/(2r). [Q1190]\n● Escape karne ke liye body ko itni energy deni padti hai ki TE ≥ 0 ho jaaye. [Q1190, Q1199]\n● Gravity dwara kiya gaya work sirf vertical height difference par depend karta hai (W = mgh), horizontal position ya\nkinetic energy change par direct nahi (gravity vertically downward act karti hai). [Q1183]\n11. Geostationary & Polar Satellites\n● Geostationary satellite: [Q1156, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n– Equatorial plane mein orbit.\n– Period = 24 hours (Earth rotation ke saath synchronous).\n– Height ≈ 35,786 km (≈ 36,000 km).\n– Fixed position dikhta hai ground se → communication ke liye best."," ● Polar satellite: [Q1182]\n– Near-polar orbit mein.\n– Lower height (few hundred km).\n– Period ≈ 100 minutes.\n– Earth ke rotation ki wajah se poori surface cover kar leta hai.\n– Weather monitoring, remote sensing ke liye use hota hai.\n12. Projectile Motion\n● Horizontal throw karne par body projectile ki tarah move karti hai. [Q1154, Q1189]\n● Horizontal velocity constant rehti hai (agar air resistance nahi); vertical velocity g se badhti hai. [Q1189]\n● Range maximum tab hoti hai jab angle = 45° (same height se throw karne par). [Q1198]\n● Maximum height = (u²sin²θ)/(2g). [Q1198]\n● Range = (u²sin2θ)/g. [Q1198]\n13. Gravitational Potential\n● Gravitational potential (V) = work done per unit mass to bring from infinity to that point. [Q1172, Q1187, Q1196]\n● Formula: V = -GM/r. [Q1172, Q1187, Q1196]\n● Unit = J/kg. [Q1172, Q1196]\n● Negative sign ka matlab: gravity attractive hai, isliye infinity se laane mein work by gravity hota hai (negative work\nby external agent). [Q1196]\n● Gravitational field intensity (I) = F/m = GM/r² = g. [Q1187, Q1196]\n● Relation: I = -dV/dr. [Q1187]\n14. Tides\n● Tides = ocean water ka rise and fall; mainly Moon ki gravity se hoti hai. [Q1174, Q1180, Q1189, Q1198]\n● Sun bhi tides cause karta hai lekin Moon zyada effect kyunki wo paas hai. [Q1180, Q1198]\n● Spring tides = Sun, Moon, Earth ek line mein (new moon/full moon) → high tides zyada high, low tides zyada low.\n[Q1180, Q1198]\n● Neap tides = Sun-Moon 90° angle pe (first/third quarter) → tides kam extreme. [Q1180, Q1198]\n● High tide = water upar; low tide = water neeche. [Q1174]\n● Ek din mein generally 2 high tides aur 2 low tides aate hain. [Q1174, Q1198]\n15. Miscellaneous Concepts\n● Newton's law of gravitation se Coulomb's law similar hai structure mein (both inverse square) lekin Coulomb\nmein charges hain aur repulsion bhi ho sakta hai. [Q1195]\n● Gravitational force hamesha attractive; weakest fundamental force. [Q1186, Q1195]\n● Gravity ka range infinite hai; har body har doosre body ko attract karti hai. [Q1186, Q1195]\n● Earth apne center se sabhi objects ko same acceleration (g) deti hai; isliye mass different hone par bhi sab saath"," girte hain. [Q1179, Q1197]\n● Two objects different masses ke free fall mein ek saath girte hain kyunki F=ma → a=F/m=GM/R²=g; m cancel ho\njaata hai. [Q1179, Q1197]\n● g ka value Jupiter par zyada hota hai (mass zyada) → weight zyada; Mars par kam → weight kam. [Q1151, Q1163,\nQ1176]\n● Gravity waves = Einstein ne predict ki thi; 2015 mein LIGO ne detect kiya. [Q1195]\n● Black holes mein gravity infinite hoti hai; escape velocity > c (speed of light). [Q1199]\n● Agar gravitational force ki absence ho (jaise deep space mein) toh rocket ka thrust stable rehta hai kyunki gravity\nko counteract karne ki zaroorat nahi hoti — rate of gas ejection constant rahe toh thrust bhi stable rehta hai.\n[Q1192]\n16.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q1151–Q1200)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass kahin bhi same rehti hai — Moon, Earth, Mars, space sab jagah; weight badalta hai. [Q1151, Q1157,\nQ1163, Q1176, Q1185, Q1194]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Moon weight = Earth weight / 6; mass same. [Q1151, Q1157, Q1163, Q1170, Q1176, Q1185]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Beam balance se mass measure hoti hai; Spring balance se weight. [Q1170, Q1185]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Newton ka law = F = Gm₁m₂/r²; G = 6.67×10⁻¹¹. [Q1152, Q1158, Q1164, Q1177, Q1186, Q1195]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: G ka value universal aur constant hai — location/medium par depend nahi. [Q1159, Q1165, Q1172, Q1178,\nQ1187, Q1196]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: g ka value sab jagah same nahi — equator < poles, height par kam, depth par kam; equator se pole\njaane par weight hamesha badhta hai. [Q1166, Q1173, Q1179, Q1184, Q1188]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Free fall mein sab objects same acceleration g se girte hain — apne khud ke mass par depend nahi karta\n(air resistance nahi ho toh). [Q1166, Q1179, Q1193, Q1197]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weightlessness = gravity nahi hai aisa nahi; body aur container dono free fall mein hain isliye normal\nreaction zero. [Q1161, Q1167, Q1174, Q1180, Q1189, Q1198]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Escape velocity Earth ke liye = 11.2 km/s; Moon ke liye ≈ 2.38 km/s. [Q1155, Q1162, Q1168, Q1175, Q1181,\nQ1190, Q1199]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Escape velocity mass of body par depend nahi karti. [Q1162, Q1175, Q1181, Q1199]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kepler's Third Law = T² r³; T r^(3/2).\n∝\n∝\n [Q1156, Q1169, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Geo-stationary satellite ka period = 24 hours; height ≈ 36,000 km. [Q1156, Q1182, Q1191, Q1200]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Higher orbit → lesser speed → greater period. [Q1191, Q1200]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gravitational PE hamesha negative (bound system ke liye). [Q1162, Q1190, Q1199]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: g height par: g_h = g(R/(R+h))²; depth par: g_d = g(1-d/R); center par g=0. [Q1153, Q1160, Q1173, Q1188]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tides mainly Moon se hoti hain, Sirf Sun se nahi. [Q1174, Q1180, Q1189, Q1198]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Spring tides = full/new moon; Neap tides = first/third quarter. [Q1180, Q1198]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gravitational potential unit = J/kg; field intensity unit = N/kg = m/s². [Q1172, Q1187, Q1196]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gravity ka work sirf vertical height difference par depend karta hai, horizontal displacement par nahi.\n[Q1183]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gravitational force ki absence mein rocket ka thrust stable rehta hai (gravity counteract karne ki\nzaroorat nahi). [Q1192]\n17. Numerical: Acceleration due to Gravity — Planetary Variations\n● Kisi bhi planet ki surface gravity ka formula g = GM/R² hota hai, jahan M planet ka mass aur R uski radius hai.\n[Q1201, Q1206, Q1207, Q1208, Q1209]"," ● Agar kisi planet ka mass M/3 ho aur radius R/3 ho, toh uske surface par g' = 3g hoga; radius square mein hone ki\nwajah se 1/9 denominator upar jaake 3 ban jaata hai. [Q1201]\n● Hypothetical planet jisme mass M/2 aur radius R/3 ho, uska surface gravity (9/2)g hoga; calculation mein (1/3)² =\n1/9 numerator ke 1/2 se multiply hokar 9/2 ban jaata hai. [Q1206]\n● Agar mass M/2 aur radius R/2 dono half kar diye jaayein, toh g' = 2g aata hai; radius ke square hone ki wajah se 4\nupar jaata hai jo 2 se divide hokar 2g deta hai. [Q1207]\n● Agar mass 2M aur radius 2R dono double ho jaayein, toh g' = (1/2)g hoga; mass double se ×2 lekin radius double\nse ÷4, net effect ½. [Q1208]\n● Kisi object ka weight W = GmM/R² hota hai; mass 15 times aur radius 4 times wale planet par weight (15/16)W ho\njaata hai kyunki 15 numerator mein aur 16 (4²) denominator mein aata hai. [Q1209]\n18. Numerical: Variation of g with Height from Surface\n● Surface se height h par gravity ka formula g' = g × [R/(R+h)]² hota hai, jahan R planet ki radius hai. [Q1203]\n● Agar h = R/10 (yaani radius ka 10%), toh g' = g × (10/11)² ≈ g × 100/121 ≈ 0.826g; 9.8 m/s² ke liye yeh\napproximately 8.1 m/s² aata hai. [Q1203]\n19. Numerical: Gravitational Force and Distance Relation\n● Newton ke universal law ke mutabiq gravitational force F 1/r² hota hai, jahan r do bodies ke beech ki distance\n∝\nhai. [Q1202]\n● Agar force F/9 ho jaaye toh distance 3 times ho jaati hai kyunki F 1/r², toh F/9 1/(3r)²; square root relation\n∝\n∝\nmein distance badhti hai. [Q1202]\n20. Numerical: Gravity Effects — Weight and Jump Height\n● Kisi planet ya moon par jump ki maximum height h 1/g hoti hai same initial velocity maan kar; kyunki v² = 2gh,\n∝\ntoh g kam hone par height utni hi zyada hoti hai. [Q1205]\n● Moon par gravity g/6 hone ki wajah se, agar Earth par 1.5 m ki jump ho toh Moon par wohi energy se 1.5 × 6 = 9\nm ki jump lag sakti hai. [Q1205]\n21. Numerical: Orbital Period under Modified Force Laws\n● Agar gravitational force distance ki n-th power ke inverse se vary kare (F 1/Rⁿ), toh circular orbit ka time period\n∝\nT R^((n+1)/2) hota hai.\n∝\n [Q1204]\n● Derivation: centripetal force mv²/R = GMm/Rⁿ se v = √(GM/Rⁿ⁻¹); phir T = 2πR/v rakhte hue simplify karne par\nexponent (n+1)/2 aata hai. [Q1204]\n22. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Surface Gravity: g = GM/R²\n● Height par Gravity: g' = g × [R/(R+h)]² = GM/(R+h)²\n● Weight: W = mg = GmM/R²"," ● Gravitational Force: F = Gm₁m₂/r²\n● Jump Height (same initial velocity): h 1/g\n∝\n● Orbital Period (general force 1/rⁿ): T R^((n+1)/2)\n∝\n∝\n● Normal gravity ke liye (n=2): T² R³ (Kepler ka Teesra Niyam)\n∝\n23.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1201–Q1209)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass aur radius dono double karne par g double nahi, balki half (1/2) ho jaata hai; mass ×2 = ×2, radius\n×2 = ÷4, net ×½. [Q1208]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass half aur radius half karne par g same nahi rehta, balki 2g ho jaata hai. [Q1207]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass half aur radius one-third karne par answer (9/2)g aata hai, (5/2)g nahi; denominator mein (1/3)² =\n1/9 upar jaake 9 ban jaata hai. [Q1206]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Height par g calculate karte waqt direct subtraction nahi karna; h = R/10 par g' ≈ 8.1 m/s² aata hai, 4.5\nya 8.9 nahi. [Q1203]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weight nikaalte waqt sirf mass ratio mat dekhna; radius ka square denominator mein aata hai (15/16 W,\nna ki 15/4 W). [Q1209]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Force F/9 hone par distance 3 times hoti hai, 9 times nahi; inverse square ke hisaab se square root lena\npadta hai. [Q1202]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 7 Gravitation Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0410","t":"08 Work Energy Power","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.8 — WORK, ENERGY AND POWER — FULL MIND MAP\n⚡\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Electric Power: Formulas, Units & Domestic Supply\n2. Energy Conversions & Devices\n3. Energy Sources: Renewable, Non-Renewable & Conventional\n4. Kinetic Energy: Basics, Formula & Factors\n5. Potential Energy, Mechanical Energy & Conversions\n6. Work Done: Definition, Formula, Conditions & Types\n7. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n8. Temperature, States of Matter & Particle Energy\n9. Conservation of Energy & Miscellaneous Facts\n10.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q1210–Q1314)\n⚠️\n11. Numerical: Work Done by Force\n12. Numerical: Kinetic Energy — Formula & Variations\n13. Numerical: Potential Energy — Formula & Height Problems\n14. Numerical: Power — Human Climbing & Engine Problems\n15. Numerical: Work-Energy Theorem\n16. Numerical: Electrical Work — W = VQ\n17. Numerical: Elastic Potential Energy\n18. Numerical: Inclined Plane Work\n19. Numerical: Momentum-KE Relationship\n20. Numerical: Efficiency & Energy Conversion\n21. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n22.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1315–Q1425)\n⚠️\n1. Electric Power: Formulas, Units & Domestic Supply\n● Electric power ke valid formulas: P = VI = I²R = V²/R; P = IR² galat hai. [Q1210]\n● Power ki definition: rate of doing work ya rate of energy transfer hai; power = Work/Time hai. [Q1234]\n● Electric power bhi isi definition ka special case hai — rate at which electrical energy dissipate/consume hoti hai\ncircuit mein. [Q1217]\n● Resistance ka formula work se: R = W/(I × q) kyunki W = I²Rt = IRq. [Q1216]\n● Charge Q, voltage V, time t se power: P = VQ/t kyunki I = Q/t. [Q1215]\n● Circuit mein heat loss: H = I²RT — ye directly proportional to resistance hai same current ke liye. [Q1214]\n● Electrical energy consumed: Power rating × Time par depend karta hai. [Q1224]\n● Bulb ki power rating 100 W ka matlab: bulb 100 Joule energy per second consume karta hai (na ki per minute ya\nper hour). [Q1226]\n● 1 joule/second = 1 watt — power ka SI unit. [Q1268]\n● Domestic supply India mein: 220V, 50 Hz; USA mein 110V, 60 Hz. [Q1213]\n● 1 kW = 1000 W; 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J (commercial unit of electrical energy). [Q1246, Q1252, Q1311]\n● Household/industry/commercial energy consumption usually kilowatt-hour (kWh) mein express hoti hai. [Q1272]\n● 1 HP (Horsepower) = 746 W. [Q1311]"," 2. Energy Conversions & Devices\n● Electric motor: Electrical energy → Mechanical energy. [Q1211]\n● Dynamo/Generator: Mechanical/Kinetic energy → Electrical energy. [Q1222]\n● Electric geyser: Electrical energy → Heat energy (Joule heating). [Q1212]\n● Electric lamp: Electrical energy → Heat + Light energy. [Q1211]\n● Thermocouple: Heat energy → Electrical energy. [Q1211]\n● Microphone: Sound energy → Electrical energy. [Q1211, Q1310]\n● Photocell: Light energy → Electrical energy. [Q1222]\n● Battery/Cell: Chemical energy → Electrical energy. [Q1299, Q1310]\n● Electric heater: Electrical → Heat; Hair dryer: Electrical → Thermal; Electric fan: Electrical → Mechanical. [Q1299]\n● Thunder: Atmosphere ke charged particles ki KE → Light (lightning) + Sound energy mein convert hoti hai. [Q1286]\n3. Energy Sources: Renewable, Non-Renewable & Conventional\n● Thermal power plants mein fossil fuel ki Chemical energy → Electrical energy mein convert hoti hai. [Q1229]\n● Hydroelectric power mein falling water ki PE → KE → Mechanical → Electrical hoti hai. [Q1231, Q1245, Q1285,\nQ1307]\n● Wind turbines wind ki KE → Mechanical → Electrical mein convert karte hain. [Q1219, Q1230]\n● India ka sabse bada wind farm: Muppandal (Kanyakumari), 1500 MW; World ka sabse bada: Gansu Wind Farm,\nChina. [Q1219]\n● Solar energy collectors mein sabse zyada efficiency paraboloid dish collector ki hoti hai kyunki ye sunlight ko focal\npoint par concentrate karta hai. [Q1287]\n● Calorific value: 1 kg fuel ke complete combustion se kitni heat milti hai; unit kJ/kg. [Q1227]\n● Conventional (Non-renewable): Natural gas, coal, petroleum, firewood — limited hain aur pollution karte hain.\n[Q1281]\n● Non-conventional (Renewable): Solar, wind, nuclear, hydroelectric, geothermal, tidal, bioenergy. [Q1281, Q1230]\n4. Kinetic Energy: Basics, Formula & Factors\n● Kinetic energy formula: KE = ½mv² — mass aur velocity ke square par depend karti hai. [Q1228, Q1232, Q1236,\nQ1237, Q1239, Q1242, Q1244, Q1257, Q1261, Q1274, Q1277, Q1279, Q1297, Q1301, Q1313]\n● KE hamesha zero ya positive hoti hai; ye scalar quantity hai. [Q1239, Q1279]\n● Velocity double karne par KE 4 times; 4 times karne par 16 times ho jaati hai. [Q1257]\n● Same momentum par: KE = p²/2m — jitna kam mass utni zyada KE; isliye bullet ki KE gun se zyada hoti hai.\n[Q1242, Q1266]\n● Free fall mein KE continuously badhti hai kyunki velocity badhti hai. [Q1237, Q1244]\n● Moving bullet, railway engine, simple pendulum, running water, fast asteroid, car, ocean waves — sab mein KE\nhoti hai. [Q1239, Q1254, Q1277, Q1285]\n● Bullet laksya mein gahraai tak penetrate karti hai kyunki usme bohot zyada KE hoti hai. [Q1261]\n● Moving bullet sabse zyada kaam kar sakti hai compared to raised hammer, speeding stone, ya rotating wheel.\n[Q1313]\n● Chalti car ka velocity badhne par uski PE stable rehti hai kyunki height nahi badalti. [Q1293]\n● Gas molecules ki KE directly proportional to temperature hoti hai. [Q1223]\n● States of matter mein particles ki KE order: Solids < Liquids < Gases < Plasma. [Q1238, Q1290]"," 5. Potential Energy, Mechanical Energy & Conversions\n● Potential energy formula: PE = mgh — position, height ya shape par depend karti hai. [Q1232, Q1241, Q1250, Q1260,\nQ1263, Q1270, Q1283, Q1302, Q1305]\n● Kisi bhi object ki energy (uski work karne ki ability), uske position aur condition par depend karti hai — na ki sirf\nmass/volume ya direction par. [Q1267]\n● Gravitational PE ke examples: ghar ki chhat par rahi eent, dam ke upar stored paani, uthaya hua hathaura. [Q1283,\nQ1245, Q1312]\n● Elastic PE ke examples: stretched rubber band, compressed spring, wound spring, compressed slinky, stretched\nbow. [Q1259, Q1243, Q1283, Q1294, Q1302, Q1305, Q1309]\n● Object ko vertically up throw karne par: jaise-jaise height badhti hai PE increases, KE decreases. [Q1241]\n● Maximum height par KE = 0 aur PE = maximum hoti hai. [Q1250]\n● 3/4 height par bhi PE > KE rehti hai. [Q1250]\n● 200 m se girte object ko 100 m girne ke baad aadhi PE aur aadhi KE hoti hai (donon barabar). [Q1280]\n● Mechanical energy = KE + PE; free fall mein (air resistance ignore karke) constant rehti hai. [Q1244, Q1249, Q1265,\nQ1280, Q1298]\n● Raindrops neeche girte waqt PE → KE mein convert hoti hai. [Q1275]\n● Arrow release hone par bowstring ki PE → arrow ki KE mein convert hoti hai. [Q1247, Q1309]\n● Compressed slinky release karne par PE → KE hoti hai. [Q1294]\n● Bullet fire hone par stored PE → KE mein convert hoti hai. [Q1308]\n● Pendulum ka example: highest point par max PE, min KE; lowest point par max KE, min PE — continuous PE ↔ KE\nconversion hota hai. [Q1314]\n6. Work Done: Definition, Formula, Conditions & Types\n● Work done formula: W = F·d = F × d × cosθ; unit joule (J) = newton × meter; dimension [ML²T⁻²]. [Q1248, Q1255,\nQ1311]\n● 1 joule ki definition: 1 newton × 1 meter (na ki watt×meter ya pascal×meter). [Q1258]\n● Work karne ke liye do shartein: (1) force lagna chahiye, (2) displacement hona chahiye. [Q1262, Q1276, Q1291]\n● Work done positive jab force aur displacement same direction mein ho → body energy gain karti hai. [Q1240,\nQ1251]\n● Work done negative jab force aur displacement opposite direction mein ho. [Q1251, Q1271]\n● Work done zero jab force aur displacement perpendicular ho (θ = 90°, cos90° = 0) ya koi displacement hi na ho.\n[Q1235, Q1273, Q1278, Q1284, Q1296, Q1303, Q1304, Q1306]\n● Zero work ke examples: wall push karna (displacement nahi), platform par khade rehna, circular motion\n(centripetal force perpendicular), Moon ki Earth parikrama (gravitational force perpendicular), gadhe dwara bojh\nlekar chalna (vertical force, horizontal displacement). [Q1278, Q1284, Q1296, Q1303, Q1304, Q1306]\n● Friction ka work hamesha negative hota hai kyunki ye hamesha motion ka virodh karta hai. [Q1289]\n● Work done mass par depend nahi karta; sirf force, displacement, aur unke beech ke angle par depend karta hai.\n[Q1253, Q1256, Q1292]\n● Work done initial velocity par depend nahi karta. [Q1292]\n● Power = Work / Time; kaun kitni jaldi kaam complete karta hai ye batata hai. [Q1282]\n7. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n● Scalar (sirf magnitude): Work, power, pressure, energy, frequency, speed, mass, temperature. [Q1288]\n● Vector (magnitude + direction): Displacement, force, torque, momentum, acceleration, velocity. [Q1288]"," 8. Temperature, States of Matter & Particle Energy\n● Temperature badhane par solid/liquid/gas ke particles ki kinetic energy increases. [Q1225]\n● Kelvin temperature directly proportional to average kinetic energy of particles. [Q1225]\n● Kisi bhi substance ke particles same temperature par different amounts of KE rakhte hain (Maxwell-Boltzmann\ndistribution). [Q1228]\n● Gases mein particles ki KE maximum hoti hai; solids mein minimum. [Q1290]\n9. Conservation of Energy & Miscellaneous Facts\n● Law of Conservation of Energy: Energy ko na toh create kar sakte hain na destroy — sirf ek form se doosre mein\nconvert kar sakte hain. [Q1264, Q1269, Q1300]\n● Explosion mein fragments alag direction mein jaate hain lekin momentum conserved rehta hai; KE conserved nahi\nhoti. [Q1233]\n● Power scalar quantity hai. [Q1221]\n● Telephone ka invention 1876 mein Alexander Graham Bell ne kiya. [Q1218]\n● Ultrasound: >20 kHz frequency; defects se reflect back hota hai (bats use karte hain). [Q1220]\n10.\n Traps / Formula Cheat Sheet (MCQ Q1210–Q1314)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: P = IR² galat formula hai — correct hai P = I²R. [Q1210]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: India mein 220V, 50 Hz hai — 110V/60Hz USA ka hai. [Q1213]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work done mass par depend nahi karta — ye common confusion hai. [Q1253, Q1256, Q1292]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Free fall mein ME constant rehti hai lekin KE badhti, PE ghatti hai; dono opposite direction mein change\nhoti hain. [Q1237, Q1244, Q1298]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same momentum par bullet ki KE gun se zyada hoti hai kyunki KE = p²/2m — kam mass = zyada KE.\n[Q1242, Q1266]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Raised hammer mein PE hai, KE nahi — motion nahi hai. [Q1254, Q1270, Q1312]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Wind opposing car ka work negative hota hai, positive nahi. [Q1251]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J — power nahi, energy hai. [Q1246, Q1252]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Circular motion mein aur Moon ki parikrama mein work zero hota hai kyunki force hamesha\nperpendicular hoti hai displacement se. [Q1296, Q1303]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Running water KE hai, PE nahi — stored dam water PE hai. [Q1285, Q1312]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Friction ka work hamesha negative — kabhi positive nahi. [Q1289]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Car ki velocity badhne par uski PE same rehti hai agar height constant ho; confuse mat hona. [Q1293]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bicycle chalate waqt chemical energy nahi hoti directly; heat, KE, aur mechanical energy hoti hai.\n[Q1295]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 HP = 746 W yaad rakhna — 1000 W nahi. [Q1311]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hydroelectric mein ultimately KE → Electrical hota hai, PE → Electrical directly nahi (PE pehle KE mein\nconvert hoti hai flow ke saath). [Q1307]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 200 m se 100 m girne par \"more KE less PE\" nahi balki donon barabar (half-half) hote hain total ME\nconstant hone ki wajah se. [Q1280]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Natural gas conventional source hai — solar/wind/nuclear ko isse alag samajhna. [Q1281]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bulb ki 100 W rating ka matlab 100 Joule per second hai — per minute ya per hour nahi. [Q1226]"," ●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 joule/second = 1 watt — energy ka unit joule, power ka unit watt confuse mat karna. [Q1268]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Household/commercial energy consumption kWh mein measure hoti hai, watt ya joule mein nahi.\n[Q1272]\n11. Numerical: Work Done by Force\n● Basic formula: Work (W) = Force (F) × Displacement (d) jab dono same direction mein ho. [Q1327, Q1340, Q1351,\nQ1358, Q1363, Q1391, Q1396, Q1406, Q1417]\n● 10 N force se 2 m displacement → W = 20 J. [Q1327]\n● 50 N force se 10 m displacement → W = 500 J. [Q1340]\n● 10 N force se 5 m displacement → W = 50 J. [Q1351]\n● 20 N force se 4 m displacement → W = 80 J. [Q1358]\n● 125 N force se 5 m displacement → W = 625 J. [Q1363]\n● 25 N force se 5 m displacement → W = 125 J. [Q1391]\n● 10 N force se 10 m displacement → W = 100 J. [Q1396]\n● 10 N force se 5 m displacement → W = 50 J. [Q1406]\n● 1 N force se 1 m displacement → W = 1 Joule (SI unit definition). [Q1417]\n● 120 N box ko 2 m upar uthana → W = 240 J. [Q1422]\n● 50 N force se 100 m displacement → W = 5000 J. [Q1368]\n● Plane 4000 m distance with 20000 J work → Force = W/d = 5 N. [Q1402]\n● Object vertically u velocity se floor se takraye aur same velocity se bounce back → change in motion = 0. [Q1389]\n12. Numerical: Kinetic Energy — Formula & Variations\n● Formula: KE = ½mv²; unit Joule (J). [Q1315, Q1323, Q1328, Q1330, Q1334, Q1336, Q1341, Q1343, Q1344, Q1346, Q1347,\nQ1354, Q1360, Q1362, Q1364, Q1365, Q1366, Q1367, Q1369, Q1370, Q1371, Q1407, Q1408, Q1410, Q1411, Q1412, Q1414, Q1418,\nQ1420, Q1425]\n● 1 kg object 4 m/s se 8 m/s → Work = ΔKE = ½×1×(64−16) = 24 J. [Q1315]\n● 800 kg car 5 m/s se 10 m/s → W = ½×800×(100−25) = 30,000 J = 30 kJ. [Q1328]\n● 10 kg block rest se 2 m/s in 20 s → Work = ½×10×4 = 20 J; Power = 20/20 = 1 W. [Q1326]\n● 20 kg object 8 m/s → KE = ½×20×64 = 640 J. [Q1341]\n● 10 kg object 6 m/s → KE = ½×10×36 = 180 J. [Q1343]\n● Object 4 m/s par KE = 120 J → mass = 2×120/16 = 15 kg. [Q1344, Q1347]\n● Object 5 m/s par KE = 25 J; velocity double → KE = 100 J. [Q1346]\n● 2 kg ball 30 m/s → KE = ½×2×900 = 900 J. [Q1354]\n● 20 kg object 10 m/s → KE = ½×20×100 = 1000 J. [Q1360]\n● 15 kg object 6 m/s → KE = ½×15×36 = 270 J. [Q1362]\n● 15 kg object 8 m/s → KE = ½×15×64 = 480 J. [Q1364]\n● KE = 120 J, mass = 15 kg → velocity = √(2×120/15) = 4 m/s. [Q1365]\n● 15 kg object 2 m/s → KE = ½×15×4 = 30 J. [Q1366]\n● 10 kg object 5 m/s → KE = ½×10×25 = 125 J. [Q1367]\n● 13 kg object 5 m/s → KE = ½×13×25 = 162.5 J. [Q1369]\n● 14 kg object 5 m/s → KE = ½×14×25 = 175 J. [Q1370]"," ● 30 kg object 5 m/s → KE = ½×30×25 = 375 J. [Q1371]\n● 10 kg object 6 m/s → KE = ½×10×36 = 180 J. [Q1407]\n● 4 kg object 5 m/s se 10 m/s → Work = ½×4×(100−25) = 150 J. [Q1408]\n● 4 kg object rest se 5 m/s → Work = ½×4×25 = 50 J. [Q1410]\n● 0.1 kg ball 2 m girne par gravity ka work = mgh = 0.1×9.8×2 = 1.96 J. [Q1412]\n● Same velocity par mass double → KE double hoti hai (KA/KB = 2). [Q1323]\n● Velocity double karne par KE 4 times ho jaati hai. [Q1330, Q1336, Q1346, Q1411, Q1418]\n● 1 kg object ka KE = 1 J ho to velocity = √2 ≈ 1.4 m/s. [Q1401]\n● 5 kg aur 10 kg balls ka KE barabar ho → 5 kg ball tez chalti hai kyunki v² = 2KE/m. [Q1420]\n● KE 256 times ho jaye to momentum 16 times ho jaata hai (kyunki KE p²).\n∝\n [Q1414]\n● Momentum triple ho to KE 9 times ho jaati hai. [Q1425]\n● Momentum double ho to KE 4 times ho jaati hai. [Q1334]\n13. Numerical: Potential Energy — Formula & Height Problems\n● Formula: PE = mgh; unit Joule (J). [Q1316, Q1318, Q1320, Q1325, Q1331, Q1333, Q1335, Q1337, Q1339, Q1342, Q1348,\nQ1349, Q1350, Q1352, Q1353, Q1355, Q1356, Q1357, Q1359, Q1361, Q1372, Q1373, Q1374, Q1375, Q1376, Q1378, Q1379, Q1381,\nQ1384, Q1385, Q1395, Q1397, Q1398, Q1399, Q1405, Q1415, Q1416, Q1423]\n● 20 kg luggage 2 m upar → W = mgh = 20×10×2 = 400 J. [Q1316, Q1335]\n● 9800 J energy se 70 kg mass ko height = E/(mg) = 9800/(70×10) = 14 m. [Q1318]\n● 6 kg object PE = 480 J → height = 480/(6×10) = 8 m. [Q1320]\n● 1 kg object 10 m upar uthana → gravity ka work = −mgh = −98 J (negative kyunki gravity opposite direction mein\nkaam karta hai). [Q1325]\n● 50 kg object 6 m height par (g=10) → PE = 50×10×6 = 3000 J. [Q1331]\n● 1 kg object PE = 2 J → height = 2/(1×10) = 0.2 m. [Q1333]\n● 0.5 kg mobile 100 m height → PE = 0.5×10×100 = 500 J. [Q1337]\n● 10 kg object 6 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 10×9.8×6 = 588 J. [Q1339, Q1395]\n● 20 kg object PE = 400 J (g=10) → height = 400/(20×10) = 2 m. [Q1342]\n● 12 kg object PE = 480 J (g=10) → height = 480/120 = 4 m. [Q1348, Q1384]\n● 11 kg luggage 1.5 m upar → W = 11×10×1.5 = 165 J. [Q1349]\n● 12 kg luggage 1.5 m upar → W = 12×10×1.5 = 180 J. [Q1350]\n● 12 kg object PE = 600 J → height = 600/120 = 5 m. [Q1352, Q1379]\n● 14 kg luggage 1.5 m upar → W = 14×10×1.5 = 210 J. [Q1353]\n● 15 kg hammer 10 m upar → PE = 15×10×10 = 1500 J. [Q1355]\n● 13 kg luggage 1.5 m upar → W = 13×10×1.5 = 195 J. [Q1356]\n● 15 kg luggage 1.0 m upar → W = 15×10×1 = 150 J. [Q1357]\n● 10 kg luggage 1.1 m upar → W = 10×10×1.1 = 110 J. [Q1359]\n● 10 kg luggage 1.2 m upar → W = 10×10×1.2 = 120 J. [Q1361]\n● 12 kg object 5 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 12×9.8×5 = 588 J. [Q1372]\n● 15 kg object 5 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 15×9.8×5 = 735 J. [Q1373]\n● 11 kg object 6 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 11×9.8×6 = 646.8 J. [Q1374]\n● 11 kg object 8 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 11×9.8×8 = 862.4 J. [Q1375]\n● Mass m ko 4h height par → PE = 4mgh. [Q1376]\n● 10 kg object 7 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 10×9.8×7 = 686 J. [Q1378]"," ● 11 kg object 7 m height (g=9.8) → PE = 11×9.8×7 = 754.6 J. [Q1381]\n● 10 kg object 4 m girne par gravity ka work = mgh = 10×10×4 = 400 J. [Q1397]\n● Object 5 m height par PE = 2000 J → mass = 2000/(10×5) = 40 kg. [Q1398]\n● 3m mass ko h height par → PE = 3mgh. [Q1399]\n● 20 kg object 5 m upar → gravity ka work = mgh = 1000 J. [Q1405]\n● 20 kg object 2 m upar → work = 20×10×2 = 400 J. [Q1415]\n● 40 kg Mohan 50 steps (15 cm each) in 10 s → PE = 40×10×7.5 = 3000 J. [Q1416]\n14. Numerical: Power — Human Climbing & Engine Problems\n● Formula: Power (P) = Work/Time = mgh/t; unit Watt (W). [Q1317, Q1319, Q1321, Q1322, Q1326, Q1329, Q1332, Q1377,\nQ1385, Q1386, Q1387, Q1388, Q1393, Q1416, Q1421]\n● 1000 J work in 2 s → Power = 1000/2 = 500 W. [Q1317]\n● 40 kg girl 5 m in 4 s → Power = mgh/t = 40×10×5/4 = 500 W. [Q1319]\n● 80 kg object 40 m in 50 s → Power = 80×10×40/50 = 640 J/s (W). [Q1321]\n● 400 N girl 160 W power se 20 s tak climb → height = (160×20)/400 = 8 m. [Q1322]\n● 10 kg block rest se 2 m/s in 20 s → Work = 20 J; Power = 1 W. [Q1326]\n● 20 kW engine 10 s → Work = 20×10 = 200 kJ. [Q1329]\n● 50 kg boy 45 stairs (15 cm) in 9 s → Power = 50×10×6.75/9 = 375 W. [Q1332, Q1377]\n● 50 kg boy 40 stairs (15 cm) in 10 s → Power = 50×10×6/10 = 300 W. [Q1385]\n● 50 kg boy 45 stairs (16 cm) in 10 s → Power = 50×10×7.2/10 = 360 W. [Q1386]\n● 50 kg boy 40 stairs (15 cm) in 9 s → Power = 50×10×6/9 = 333.33 W. [Q1387]\n● 50 kg boy 43 stairs (15 cm) in 10 s → Power = 50×10×6.45/10 = 322.5 W. [Q1388]\n● 50 kg boy 41 stairs (15 cm) in 10 s → Power = 50×10×6.15/10 = 307.5 W. [Q1393]\n● 40 kg Mohan 50 stairs (15 cm) in 10 s → Power = 40×10×7.5/10 = 300 W. [Q1416]\n● Boy 20 m in 4 min (240 s) with 600 N → Power = (600×20)/240 = 50 W. [Q1421]\n● If a factor W does work in time t, then its power P = Work/Time (W/t). [Q1345]\n15. Numerical: Work-Energy Theorem\n● Work done = Change in KE = ½m(v² − u²). [Q1315, Q1328, Q1408, Q1410]\n● 1 kg object 4→8 m/s → W = ½×1×(64−16) = 24 J. [Q1315]\n● 800 kg car 5→10 m/s → W = ½×800×75 = 30,000 J = 30 kJ. [Q1328]\n● 4 kg object 5→10 m/s → W = ½×4×75 = 150 J. [Q1408]\n● 4 kg object rest→5 m/s → W = ½×4×25 = 50 J. [Q1410]\n● 2 kg object upward 20 m/s, after 2 s (g=10): v = 20−20 = 0 → KE = 0 J. [Q1409]\n● Ball 10 m se girne ke baad 2.5 m tak bounce back → KE loss = (10−2.5)/10 × 100 = 75%. [Q1413]\n16. Numerical: Electrical Work — W = VQ\n● Formula: Work (W) = Potential Difference (V) × Charge (Q). [Q1380, Q1382, Q1383, Q1390, Q1392, Q1394]\n● V = 20 V, W = 60 J → Q = W/V = 60/20 = 3 C. [Q1380]"," ● Q = 4 C, V = 10 V → W = 10×4 = 40 J. [Q1382]\n● Q = 3 C, W = 72 J → V = 72/3 = 24 V. [Q1383]\n● W = 20 J, V = 10 V → Q = 20/10 = 2 C. [Q1390]\n● Q = 4 C, V = 12 V → W = 12×4 = 48 J. [Q1392]\n● Q = 5 C, V = 13 V → W = 13×5 = 65 J. [Q1394]\n17. Numerical: Elastic Potential Energy\n● Formula: Elastic Energy = ½ × F × x (x = extension). [Q1404]\n● F = 200 N, x = 1 mm = 10⁻³ m → Energy = ½×200×10⁻³ = 0.1 J. [Q1404]\n18. Numerical: Inclined Plane Work\n● Smooth inclined plane par work: W = mg sinθ × d. [Q1400]\n● 2 kN block, 10 m displacement, 15° angle → W = 2000×sin15°×10 = 2000×0.26×10 = 5.17 kJ. [Q1400]\n19. Numerical: Momentum-KE Relationship\n● Formula: KE = p²/(2m) jahan p = momentum. [Q1403]\n● Momentum p wale ball ki KE = p²/2m. [Q1403]\n● Momentum double → KE 4 times. [Q1334]\n● Momentum triple → KE 9 times. [Q1425]\n● KE 256 times → Momentum 16 times (√256 = 16). [Q1414]\n20. Numerical: Efficiency & Energy Conversion\n● Efficiency: η = (Output/Input) × 100%. [Q1324]\n● Input = 2000 J, Output = 500 J → η = (500/2000)×100 = 25%. [Q1324]\n● 320 units energy = 320 kWh = 320 × 3.6 × 10⁶ = 1152 × 10⁶ J. [Q1424]\n21. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Work (Force parallel): W = F × d — unit Joule (J).\n● Work (against gravity): W = mgh — unit Joule (J).\n● Kinetic Energy: KE = ½mv² = p²/2m — unit Joule (J).\n● Potential Energy: PE = mgh — unit Joule (J).\n● Power: P = W/t = mgh/t — unit Watt (W).\n● Work-Energy Theorem: W = ΔKE = ½m(v²−u²) — unit Joule (J).\n● Electrical Work: W = VQ = VIt — unit Joule (J).\n● Elastic Energy: E = ½Fx — unit Joule (J)."," ● Efficiency: η = Output/Input × 100% — unit %.\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J.\n22.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1315–Q1425)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Object ko upar uthane par gravity ka work negative (−mgh) hota hai; neeche girne par positive (+mgh).\n[Q1325, Q1397]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Velocity double karne par KE 4 times hoti hai, 2 times nahi. [Q1330, Q1336, Q1346, Q1411, Q1418]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Momentum double karne par KE 4 times hoti hai (kyunki KE p²).\n∝\n [Q1334]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Momentum triple karne par KE 9 times hoti hai. [Q1425]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: KE 256 times ho jaye to momentum 16 times hota hai (√256 = 16), 256 times nahi. [Q1414]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Equal KE wale objects mein kam mass wala tez chalta hai. [Q1420, Q1323]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work zero jab displacement zero ho, chahe kitna bhi force lage. [Q1338, Q1419]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 2 kg object 20 m/s se upar, 2 s baad v = 0 → KE = 0 J (highest point par). [Q1409]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Steps ka height cm mein hota hai — hamesha meter mein convert karo (divide by 100). [Q1332, Q1377,\nQ1385, Q1386, Q1387, Q1388, Q1393, Q1416]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Time minutes mein de sakta hai — seconds mein convert karo (×60). [Q1421]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 320 units = 320 kWh = 1152 × 10⁶ J; 320 × 3.6 × 10⁶ mat bhoolna. [Q1424]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Object vertically u velocity se bounce back kare to change in motion = 0 (same speed magnitude).\n[Q1389]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ball 10 m se girke 2.5 m bounce back kare to 75% KE loss hoti hai ((10−2.5)/10). [Q1413]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 Joule = 1 N × 1 m — ye definition yaad rakhna. [Q1417]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Work ka unit hamesha Joule hota hai — options mein W, N, Pa, C confuse karne ke liye hote hain.\n[Q1341, Q1354, Q1360, Q1363, Q1405, Q1406]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Power ka formula \"time-work\" nahi balki Work/Time hota hai — order confuse mat karna. [Q1345]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 8 Work, Energy and Power Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0411","t":"09 Waves","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.9 — WAVES — FULL MIND MAP\n🌊\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Electromagnetic Spectrum & Wavelength Order\n2. Wave Terminology & Definitions\n3. Transverse vs Longitudinal Waves\n4. Sound Waves: Properties & Medium\n5. Ultrasound: Properties, Applications & Echolocation\n6. Infrared & UV Radiation\n7. Wave Relationships (v = fλ)\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1426–Q1450)\n⚠️\n9. Numerical: Frequency from Vibrations / Crests & Troughs\n10. Numerical: Wave Equation v = fλ\n11. Numerical: Frequency & Time Period Relation\n12. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1451–Q1460)\n⚠️\n1. Electromagnetic Spectrum & Wavelength Order\n● Sabse lamba wavelength → Radio Waves; sabse chhota wavelength → Gamma Rays. [Q1426]\n● Wavelength decreasing order: Radio > Microwave > Infrared > Visible > Ultraviolet > X-Rays > Gamma. [Q1426]\n● Gamma rays sabse chhota wavelength aur sabse zyada energy rakhti hain. [Q1426]\n● Wavelength ka Greek letter Lambda (λ) hai; visible light ka range 400 nm se 700 nm tak hota hai. [Q1427]\n● X-rays ki khoj Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen ne ki; gamma rays ki khoj Paul Villard ne; infrared ki khoj Sir Frederick\nWilliam Herschel ne. [Q1426]\n● X-rays ka use haddi mein fracture check karne ke liye hota hai. [Q1431]\n● Electromagnetic waves ke examples: radio, microwave, infrared, visible, UV, X-rays, gamma. [Q1430, Q1431]\n2. Wave Terminology & Definitions\n● Wavelength (λ) = do kramagat crests ya do kramagat troughs ke beech ki doori. [Q1427, Q1440, Q1450]\n● Frequency (f) = prati second oscillations ki sankhya; unit Hertz (Hz). [Q1437, Q1446]\n● Amplitude = mean position se maximum displacement; crest aur trough donon opposite directions mein\nmaximum displacement hain. [Q1448]\n● Time period = ek poora oscillation complete karne mein laga samay. [Q1437]\n● Pulse = short duration ki wave; non-sinusoidal waveform jaise square wave. [Q1445]\n● Wavelength = do kramagat compressions ya do kramagat rarefactions ke beech ki doori (longitudinal wave mein).\n[Q1450]\n3. Transverse vs Longitudinal Waves\n● Transverse waves mein particles perpendicular direction mein vibrate karte hain wave propagation ke. [Q1428,\nQ1429, Q1449]"," ● Transverse examples: water surface ripples, seismic S-waves, electromagnetic waves (radio, light). [Q1428, Q1429]\n● Longitudinal waves mein particles parallel direction mein vibrate karte hain wave propagation ke. [Q1434, Q1438,\nQ1450]\n● Longitudinal examples: sound waves, ultrasonic waves, seismic P-waves. [Q1434, Q1438]\n● Seismic S-waves (shear waves) = transverse displacement; P-waves = compressional/longitudinal. [Q1429]\n● Rayleigh waves = surface waves jo solids ki surface ke paas travel karti hain. [Q1429]\n4. Sound Waves: Properties & Medium\n● Sound waves mechanical waves hain — inhe travel karne ke liye medium chahiye; vacuum mein travel nahi kar\nsakti. [Q1436, Q1444]\n● Sound ki speed order: Solids > Liquids > Gases; vacuum mein zero. [Q1444]\n● Sound ke liye particle vibration aur energy transfer zaroori hai; medium ke bina disturbance transfer nahi ho\nsakta. [Q1436]\n● Jab sound ek medium se doosre mein jaati hai (e.g., air to water), uski frequency same rehti hai lekin speed aur\nwavelength badalte hain. [Q1447]\n● Formula: v = f × λ, jahan v = speed, f = frequency, λ = wavelength. [Q1442, Q1447, Q1450]\n5. Ultrasound: Properties, Applications & Echolocation\n● Ultrasound ki frequency >20 kHz hoti hai — human hearing limit se upar. [Q1430, Q1432, Q1439]\n● Ultrasound mechanical wave hai, electromagnetic nahi. [Q1430]\n● Ultrasound obstacles ki presence mein bhi well-defined paths mein travel kar sakti hai. [Q1432, Q1439]\n● Ultrasound se defects detect karte hain: transmitter wave bhejta hai, detector receive karta hai; received wave\nmein kami = fault. [Q1432]\n● Industrial applications: drilling holes, metal defect detection, ultrasonic cleaning. [Q1439]\n● Ultrasound produce karte hain: dolphins, bats, porpoises. [Q1439]\n● Bats echolocation use karte hain: high-frequency ultrasonic squeaks emit karte hain, obstacle se reflect hokar\necho sunke navigate karte hain. [Q1435]\n6. Infrared & UV Radiation\n● Infrared (IR) = heat energy; har object 0 K (−273.16°C) se upar temperature par emit karta hai. [Q1441]\n● IR wavelength range: 710 nm se 1 mm tak. [Q1441]\n● Garam furnace se emit hone wali radiation infrared hoti hai. [Q1441]\n● UV radiation = Sun se emit hone wali harmful radiation; wavelength 400 nm se 0.6 nm tak. [Q1443]\n● UV ko special lamps aur very hot bodies produce karte hain. [Q1443]\n● UV ki overexposure se melanin production badhta hai aur skin tan hoti hai. [Q1443]\n● Pathology labs mein test tubes sterilize karne ke liye UV radiation use hoti hai bacteria eliminate karne ke liye.\n[Q1433]\n● Microwave wavelength range: 0.1 m se 1 mm tak. [Q1433]"," 7. Wave Relationships (v = fλ)\n● Same medium mein speed constant rehti hai; frequency aur wavelength inversely proportional hain. [Q1442]\n● Frequency double karne par wavelength half ho jaati hai. [Q1442]\n● Sound ek medium se doosre mein jaaye to frequency unchanged rehti hai, speed aur wavelength adjust hote\nhain. [Q1447]\n● Mathematical relation: λ = v/f. [Q1440, Q1450]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1426–Q1450)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gamma rays sabse chhota wavelength, radio waves sabse lamba — confuse mat hona. [Q1426]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ultrasound mechanical wave hai — electromagnetic wave nahi; isliye EM spectrum mein nahi aati.\n[Q1430]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alpha aur beta rays radioactive particles hain, electromagnetic waves nahi. [Q1431]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bats ultrasonic (>20 kHz) use karte hain, infrasonic nahi. [Q1435]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sound longitudinal hai, light transverse hai — donon ka nature alag hai. [Q1428, Q1434]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Frequency medium change hone par same rehti hai, speed aur wavelength badalte hain. [Q1447]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hertz unit hai (Hz), characteristic nahi — exam mein confuse karne ke liye dete hain. [Q1446]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pesticide removal ultrasound ka industrial application nahi hai. [Q1439]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Garam furnace se infrared emit hoti hai, X-ray ya microwave nahi. [Q1441]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Seismic S-waves = transverse; P-waves = longitudinal — S ka matlab shear (transverse), P ka matlab\nprimary (longitudinal). [Q1429]\n9. Numerical: Frequency from Vibrations / Crests & Troughs\n● Frequency (f) = Number of vibrations / Time taken; unit Hz. [Q1451, Q1452, Q1453, Q1454]\n● 40 vibrations in 2.5 s → f = 40/2.5 = 16 Hz. [Q1451]\n● 40 crests + 40 troughs in 0.3 s → 40 complete cycles → f = 40/0.3 = 133.33 Hz. [Q1452]\n● 20 crests + 20 troughs in 0.4 s → 20 complete cycles → f = 20/0.4 = 50 Hz. [Q1453]\n● 10 crests + 10 troughs in 0.1 s → 10 complete cycles → f = 10/0.1 = 100 Hz. [Q1454]\n● Yaad rakhna: 1 crest + 1 trough = 1 complete cycle; number of crests = number of cycles. [Q1452, Q1453, Q1454]\n10. Numerical: Wave Equation v = fλ\n● Formula: Velocity (v) = Frequency (f) × Wavelength (λ); isse λ = v/f aur f = v/λ nikaala ja sakta hai. [Q1455, Q1457,\nQ1458, Q1459, Q1460]\n● Distance 10 m in 0.04 s, f = 200 Hz → v = 10/0.04 = 250 m/s; λ = 250/200 = 1.25 m. [Q1455]\n● f = 71 × 10⁴ Hz, v = 3 × 10⁸ m/s → λ = (3×10⁸)/(71×10⁴) = 30000/71 = 422.5 m. [Q1457]\n● Crests 80 m apart (λ = 80 m), v = 20 m/s → Time period T = λ/v = 80/20 = 4 s. [Q1458]\n● λ = 100 m, v = 25 m/s → f = v/λ = 25/100 = 0.25 Hz. [Q1459]\n● λ = 125 m, v = 25 m/s → f = v/λ = 25/125 = 0.20 Hz. [Q1460]"," 11. Numerical: Frequency & Time Period Relation\n● Time period (T) = 1/frequency (f); yaani T = 1/f aur f = 1/T. [Q1456]\n● Ye inverse relation hai — jitni zyada frequency utna kam time period. [Q1456]\n12. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Frequency: f = Number of vibrations / Time — unit Hz.\n● Time Period: T = 1/f — unit second (s).\n● Wave Velocity: v = f × λ = distance/time — unit m/s.\n● Wavelength: λ = v/f — unit meter (m).\n● Frequency (alternate): f = v/λ — unit Hz.\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1451–Q1460)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Crests aur troughs count karne par 1 crest + 1 trough = 1 complete cycle hota hai; sirf crests ki sankhya =\ncycles ki sankhya. [Q1452, Q1453, Q1454]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Distance/time se velocity nikalti hai, frequency nahi; velocity ke baad λ = v/f se wavelength nikaalni\npadti hai. [Q1455]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: λ = 80 m aur v = 20 m/s se time period (T) nikalti hai (4 s), frequency nahi; f = 1/T = 0.25 Hz alag\ncalculation hai. [Q1458]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: λ = 100 m, v = 25 m/s → f = 25/100 = 0.25 Hz, 25 Hz nahi; divide karne par value 1 se kam aa sakti hai.\n[Q1459]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Broadcasting station question mein scientific notation handle karna: 71 × 10⁴ ko direct divide karo 3 ×\n10⁸ se; 10⁴ upar jaake 10⁸⁻⁴ = 10⁴ ban jaata hai. [Q1457]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 9 Waves Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0412","t":"10 Radioactivity","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.10 — RADIOACTIVITY — FULL MIND MAP\n☢️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Radioactivity: Units & Measurement\n2. Nuclear Fission vs Nuclear Fusion\n3. Nuclear Reactor Fuels & Components\n4. Types of Radiation: Properties & Uses\n5. Sun & Stellar Energy Source\n6. Discovery Facts & India's Nuclear Plants\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1461–Q1470)\n⚠️\n1. Radioactivity: Units & Measurement\n● Radioactive material dwara emit hone wali radiation ki quantity measure karne ka conventional unit Curie hai; SI\nunit Becquerel (Bq) hai. [Q1461]\n● Curie ka naam Marie Curie ke naam par rakha gaya hai. [Q1461]\n2. Nuclear Fission vs Nuclear Fusion\n● Nuclear Fission (विखंडन): Heavy nucleus (jaise Uranium, Plutonium) ko low-energy neutrons se bombard karke\nchhote nuclei mein todna; badi energy release hoti hai. [Q1464, Q1467]\n● Fission ka use: Nuclear power plants (electricity) aur Atomic bomb mein hota hai. [Q1465, Q1466]\n● Nuclear Fusion (संलयन): Do ya zyada halki nuclei (jaise Hydrogen isotopes) milke bhaari nucleus banate hain;\nenergy release hoti hai. [Q1464, Q1467]\n● Fusion ke liye ~100 million K temperature chahiye. [Q1464]\n● Fusion ka use: Sun aur stars mein energy production; Hydrogen bomb mein. [Q1465, Q1466]\n● Thermonuclear fusion ka example Hydrogen bomb hai — isme Hydrogen isotopes (Deuterium + Tritium) milke\nHelium banate hain. [Q1465]\n● Nuclear bomb ke andar: Atomic bomb = Fission; Hydrogen bomb = Fusion. [Q1465, Q1466]\n3. Nuclear Reactor Fuels & Components\n● Nuclear reactor mein fissionable fuel U-235 (Uranium-235) use hota hai; isko ceramic pellets mein process karke\nfuel rods banate hain. [Q1463]\n● Common nuclear fuels: Uranium-235 aur Plutonium-239. [Q1469]\n● Heavy water (D₂O) — Deuterium oxide — nuclear power plants mein neutron moderator ka kaam karta hai;\nneutrons ko slow down karne ke liye. [Q1462]\n● Heavy water ki khoj Harold C. Urey (1931) ne ki thi. [Q1462]\n● Reactor vessel mein fuel rods paani mein doobi hoti hain jo coolant aur moderator dono ka kaam karti hai.\n[Q1463]\n● Nuclear fusion ke main fuels: Deuterium aur Tritium (Hydrogen ke heavy isotopes). [Q1463]"," 4. Types of Radiation: Properties & Uses\n● Alpha (α) radiation: Positively charged particles (He²⁺ nuclei); sabse kam penetrating power hai — shielding/paper\nse roka ja sakta hai. [Q1468]\n● Alpha uses: Cancer treatment, smoke detectors, spacecraft power, oil industry. [Q1468]\n● Beta (β) radiation: High-energy electrons/positrons; medium penetrating power; eye/bone cancer treatment\nmein use hota hai. [Q1468]\n● Gamma (γ) radiation: Sabse chhota wavelength, sabse zyada energy; sabse zyada penetrating power;\nradiotherapy aur nuclear industry mein use hoti hai. [Q1468]\n● Neutron: Subatomic particle jo atomic nuclei ka primary constituent hai. [Q1468]\n● Penetrating power order: Alpha < Beta < Gamma. [Q1468]\n5. Sun & Stellar Energy Source\n● Sun aur anya stars ki energy ka source Nuclear Fusion hai — Hydrogen nuclei milke Helium banate hain. [Q1466]\n● Ye burning of hydrogen/helium gas nahi hai; ye nuclear reaction hai. [Q1466]\n6. Discovery Facts & India's Nuclear Plants\n● Uranium (U) ka discovery Martin Klaproth ne 1789 mein kiya; atomic number 92; highest atomic weight among\nnaturally occurring elements. [Q1470]\n● Uranium atom mein 92 protons aur 92 electrons hote hain (6 valence electrons). [Q1470]\n● India's nuclear power plants: Kakrapar (Gujarat, 1993), Tarapur (Maharashtra, 1969), Narora (UP, 1991), Kaiga\n(Karnataka, 2000). [Q1462]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1461–Q1470)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Curie conventional unit hai; Becquerel (Bq) SI unit hai — confuse mat hona. [Q1461]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nuclear bomb = Fission; Hydrogen bomb = Fusion — donon ko alag samajhna. [Q1465]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sun ki energy burning of hydrogen gas nahi, balki nuclear fusion hai. [Q1466]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: U-235 fissionable fuel hai reactor ke liye; U-238 fertile material hai. [Q1463]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alpha radiation ki sabse kam penetrating power hai — paper/shielding se roka ja sakta hai; Gamma\nsabse zyada. [Q1468]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Heavy water D₂O hai, normal water nahi — isko neutron moderator ke roop mein use karte hain.\n[Q1462]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fusion ke liye ~100 million K temperature chahiye — ye fission se alag extreme condition hai. [Q1464]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 10 Radioactivity Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0413","t":"11 Discoveries","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.11 — DISCOVERIES — FULL MIND MAP\n🔬\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Temperature Scales & Thermometers\n2. Nuclear Physics & Atomic Discoveries\n3. Electricity, Magnetism & Electromagnetism\n4. Optical Instruments & Waves\n5. Gravitation, Motion & Mechanics\n6. Nobel Prizes & Awards\n7. Miscellaneous Inventions\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1471–Q1489)\n⚠️\n1. Temperature Scales & Thermometers\n● Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit ne modern mercury-in-glass thermometer aur Fahrenheit scale ka invention kiya;\nalcohol thermometer bhi inhone banaya. [Q1471]\n● Anders Celsius ne Celsius scale invent kiya; Royal Society ke Fellow the. [Q1471]\n● Galileo Galilei ne telescope ki khoj ki thi; thermometer se directly jude nahi hain. [Q1471]\n2. Nuclear Physics & Atomic Discoveries\n● Albert Einstein ne Theory of Relativity di; formula E = mc² (mass-energy equivalence). [Q1472]\n● John Dalton ne Atomic Theory di. [Q1472]\n● Christian Bernard South African cardiac surgeon the — pehla human-to-human heart transplant kiya. [Q1472]\n● Thomas Alva Edison ne light bulb invent kiya. [Q1472]\n● Ernest Rutherford ne proton discover kiya; nuclear model of atom diya. [Q1475]\n● J.J. Thomson ne electron discover kiya (cathode ray experiment). [Q1475]\n● James Chadwick ne neutron discover kiya (1932). [Q1475]\n● Niels Bohr ne Bohr model diya — electrons definite orbits mein ghumte hain. [Q1475]\n● Otto Hahn ne nuclear fission discover kiya. [Q1475]\n● Marie Curie ne polonium aur radium discover kiye; Nobel Prize jeeta. [Q1478]\n● Enrico Fermi ne nuclear reactor banaya; controlled chain reaction. [Q1480]\n● Henri Becquerel ne radioactivity discover ki. [Q1481]\n● Werner Heisenberg ne Uncertainty Principle diya. [Q1483]\n● Max Planck ne Quantum Theory di; energy packets (quanta) ka concept. [Q1484]\n● A.P.J. Abdul Kalam ko \"Missile Man of India\" kehte hain. [Q1487]\n● C.V. Raman ne Raman Effect discover kiya; Nobel Prize in Physics (1930) jeeta. [Q1489]\n3. Electricity, Magnetism & Electromagnetism\n● Hans Christian Oersted ne electromagnetism discover kiya; electric current se magnetic field hoti hai. [Q1473]"," ● Michael Faraday ne electromagnetic induction discover kiya; dynamo/generator principle. [Q1474]\n● James Clerk Maxwell ne electromagnetic waves ki theory di. [Q1474]\n● André-Marie Ampère ne current-carrying conductor ke magnetic field ka study kiya. [Q1473]\n● Nikola Tesla ne AC motor/generator ka kaam kiya. [Q1474]\n● Alessandro Volta ne electric battery invent ki. [Q1476]\n● Georg Simon Ohm ne Ohm's Law di; resistance ka unit \"Ohm\" inke naam par. [Q1477]\n● Benjamin Franklin ne lightning rod invent kiya; electricity ka nature samjha. [Q1479]\n4. Optical Instruments & Waves\n● Hans Lippershey ne telescope invent kiya (1608). [Q1482]\n● Galileo Galilei ne telescope ko astronomy mein use kiya; Jupiter ke moons dekhe. [Q1482]\n● Antonie van Leeuwenhoek ne microscope ko improve kiya; bacteria dekhe. [Q1482]\n● Guglielmo Marconi ne radio invent kiya; wireless telegraphy. [Q1485]\n● Alexander Graham Bell ne telephone invent kiya (1876). [Q1485]\n● Heinrich Hertz ne electromagnetic waves experimentally demonstrate kiya. [Q1485]\n5. Gravitation, Motion & Mechanics\n● Sir Isaac Newton ne teen major contributions diye: Laws of Motion (3 laws), Law of Universal Gravitation, aur\nCalculus (Leibniz ke saath). [Q1474, Q1486]\n● Albert Einstein ne General Relativity di — gravitation ko spacetime curvature se explain kiya. [Q1486]\n● Galileo Galilei ne motion aur telescope pe kaam kiya. [Q1486]\n6. Nobel Prizes & Awards\n● C.V. Raman — Nobel Prize in Physics (1930) — Raman Effect. [Q1489]\n● Marie Curie — 2 Nobel Prizes (Physics 1903, Chemistry 1911). [Q1478]\n● Albert Einstein — Nobel Prize in Physics (1921) — Photoelectric Effect. [Q1472]\n● Max Planck — Nobel Prize in Physics (1918). [Q1484]\n● Enrico Fermi — Nobel Prize in Physics (1938). [Q1480]\n● Werner Heisenberg — Nobel Prize in Physics (1932). [Q1483]\n7. Miscellaneous Inventions\n● Wright Brothers (Orville & Wilbur) ne aeroplane invent kiya (1903). [Q1488]\n● A.P.J. Abdul Kalam — Missile Man of India; DRDO/ISRO mein kaam. [Q1487]\n● Benjamin Franklin — lightning rod, bifocal glasses, Franklin stove. [Q1479]\n● Guglielmo Marconi — radio; wireless communication ka father. [Q1485]"," 8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Q1471–Q1489)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fahrenheit ne mercury thermometer banaya; Celsius ne Celsius scale — donon alag hain. [Q1471]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Einstein relativity ke liye famous hain lekin Nobel Prize Photoelectric Effect ke liye mila tha. [Q1472]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rutherford ne proton diya; Thomson ne electron; Chadwick ne neutron — teenon alag hain. [Q1475]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Faraday induction ke liye; Maxwell waves ki theory ke liye; Oersted current-magnetism link ke liye.\n[Q1473, Q1474]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Galileo ne telescope use kiya astronomy mein lekin invent Lippershey ne kiya tha. [Q1482]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Newton classical gravitation; Einstein general relativity — donon alag theories hain. [Q1486]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: C.V. Raman Indian scientist hain jo Nobel jeete; ye fact exam mein direct pucha jaata hai. [Q1489]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 11 Discoveries Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0414","t":"12 Units and Measurements","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.12 — UNITS AND MEASUREMENTS — FULL MIND MAP\n📐\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Fundamental & Derived SI Units\n2. Electrical Units, Energy & Power\n3. Work, Power & Energy Conversions\n4. Mechanical Units (Force, Pressure, Density, Speed)\n5. Heat & Temperature Units\n6. Magnetic & Light Units\n7. Sound & Wave Units\n8. Lens & Optical Units\n9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1490–Q1562)\n⚠️\n10. Numerical: Acceleration & Basic Mechanical Units\n11. Numerical: Temperature Scale Conversions\n12. Numerical: Power & Energy Unit Conversions\n13. Numerical: Circular Motion — Velocity Formula\n14. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n15.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1563–Q1570)\n⚠️\n1. Fundamental & Derived SI Units\n● SI system mein 7 base/fundamental units hain: meter (length), kilogram (mass), second (time), ampere (current),\nkelvin (temperature), mole (amount), candela (luminous intensity). [Q1495, Q1544]\n● Newton (N) = derived unit; 1 N = 1 kg·m/s². [Q1495]\n● Joule (J) = derived unit; 1 J = 1 N·m. [Q1495, Q1551]\n● Watt (W) = derived unit; 1 W = 1 J/s. [Q1495, Q1552]\n● Pascal (Pa) = derived unit; 1 Pa = 1 N/m². [Q1495, Q1556]\n● Coulomb (C) = derived unit; 1 C = 1 A·s. [Q1522, Q1525]\n● Volt (V) = derived unit; 1 V = 1 J/C. [Q1531, Q1540]\n● Ohm (Ω) = derived unit; 1 Ω = 1 V/A. [Q1526, Q1528]\n● Hertz (Hz) = derived unit; 1 Hz = 1 cycle/s. [Q1504, Q1546]\n● Farad (F) = capacitance ka unit. [Q1534]\n● Henry (H) = inductance ka unit. [Q1535]\n● Weber (Wb) = magnetic flux ka unit. [Q1538]\n● Tesla (T) = magnetic field ka unit; 1 T = 1 Wb/m². [Q1539, Q1541]\n● Lumen (lm) = luminous flux ka unit. [Q1544]\n● Lux (lx) = illuminance ka unit; 1 lx = 1 lm/m². [Q1544]\n● Area ka unit m²; volume ka m³. [Q1496]\n2. Electrical Units, Energy & Power\n● 1 kWh (commercial unit) = 3.6 × 10⁶ J = 1 kW × 1 hour. [Q1490, Q1532, Q1545]\n● Electric power ke valid formulas: P = VI = I²R = V²/R; unit Watt (W). [Q1532, Q1537, Q1548]"," ● Electrical energy: E = Pt = VIt; commercial unit kWh. [Q1532]\n● 60 W bulb 1 hour → Energy = 60 × 3600 = 216000 J = 216 kJ. [Q1497]\n● 100 W bulb 10 hours → 1 kWh. [Q1492, Q1545]\n● 200 W bulb 5 hours → 1 kWh. [Q1545]\n● 2000 W heater 30 min → 1 kWh. [Q1514]\n● 100 W bulb 24 hours → 2.4 kWh. [Q1524]\n● 500 W appliance 2 hours → 1 kWh. [Q1548]\n● Current ka SI unit Ampere (A) = C/s. [Q1525, Q1527]\n● 1 A current = 1 C charge per second. [Q1527]\n● Resistance ka SI unit Ohm (Ω). [Q1526, Q1528]\n● Ohm's Law: V = IR; R = V/I. [Q1528]\n● Resistivity ka unit Ohm-meter (Ω·m). [Q1529]\n● Conductance ka unit Siemens (S) = 1/Ω. [Q1533]\n● Electric field ka unit V/m ya N/C. [Q1536]\n● EMF (Electromotive force) ka unit bhi Volt (V) hota hai. [Q1531]\n● Radiation measure karne ke liye Geiger-Muller counter use hota hai — Voltmeter/Ammeter/Spectrometer nahi.\n[Q1523]\n3. Work, Power & Energy Conversions\n● Work/Energy ka SI unit Joule (J). [Q1493, Q1498, Q1501, Q1551]\n● Power ka SI unit Watt (W) = J/s. [Q1499, Q1500, Q1552]\n● 1 MW = 10⁶ W; 1 GW = 10⁹ W. [Q1505]\n● 1 Horsepower (HP) = 746 W = 0.746 kW. [Q1494, Q1502, Q1503, Q1506]\n● 1.5 HP = 1119 W; 2 HP = 1492 W; 5.5 HP = 4103 W. [Q1502, Q1503, Q1506]\n● 1 erg = 10⁻⁷ J (CGS unit of work). [Q1553]\n● 1 dyne = 10⁻⁵ N (CGS unit of force). [Q1554]\n● 1 eV (electron volt) = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J; 1 MeV = 10⁶ eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹³ J. [Q1555]\n● 1 calorie = 4.186 J ≈ 4.2 J. [Q1521]\n4. Mechanical Units (Force, Pressure, Density, Speed)\n● Force ka SI unit Newton (N). [Q1495, Q1511, Q1512]\n● 1 kgf (kilogram force) = 9.8 N ≈ 10 N. [Q1512]\n● Momentum ka unit kg·m/s ya N·s. [Q1493]\n● Acceleration ka unit m/s². [Q1501]\n● Speed/velocity ka SI unit m/s; distance ka meter (m). [Q1508, Q1509, Q1510]\n● 1 km/h = 5/18 m/s. [Q1508]\n● Speedometer instantaneous speed measure karta hai. [Q1510]\n● Odometer total distance measure karta hai. [Q1509]\n● Pressure ka SI unit Pascal (Pa) = N/m². [Q1495, Q1513, Q1556, Q1560]\n● 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa; 1 atm = 1.013 × 10⁵ Pa = 101.325 kPa. [Q1556]"," ● 1 torr = 133.322 Pa; 1 mm Hg ≈ 133 Pa. [Q1556]\n● Density ka unit kg/m³; CGS mein g/cm³. [Q1515, Q1557]\n● 1 g/cm³ = 1000 kg/m³. [Q1557]\n● Relative density = density of substance / density of water; no unit — momentum, density, pressure sab ka unit\nhota hai lekin relative density dimensionless hai. [Q1515, Q1530]\n● Specific volume = 1/ρ; unit m³/kg. [Q1558]\n● Surface tension ka unit N/m ya J/m². [Q1559]\n● Torque/Moment of force ka unit N·m; lekin ye work se alag hai — direction alag hoti hai. [Q1551]\n● 1 Poise = 0.1 Pa·s (CGS viscosity unit). [Q1561]\n● 1 Stokes = 10⁻⁴ m²/s (CGS kinematic viscosity). [Q1562]\n5. Heat & Temperature Units\n● Temperature ka SI unit Kelvin (K) — base unit. [Q1517, Q1520]\n● 0°C = 273.15 K; 100°C = 373.15 K. [Q1520]\n● Specific heat capacity ka unit J/(kg·K) ya J/(kg·°C). [Q1518]\n● Latent heat ka unit J/kg. [Q1519]\n6. Magnetic & Light Units\n● Magnetic flux ka unit Weber (Wb). [Q1538]\n● Magnetic field (B) ka unit Tesla (T) = Wb/m². [Q1539, Q1541]\n● 1 Gauss = 10⁻⁴ Tesla. [Q1539]\n● Magnetic field intensity ka unit A/m. [Q1542]\n● Magnetic permeability ka unit H/m ya T·m/A. [Q1543]\n● Luminous intensity ka SI unit Candela (cd) — base unit. [Q1544, Q1549]\n● Luminous flux ka unit Lumen (lm). [Q1544]\n● Illuminance ka unit Lux (lx) = lm/m². [Q1544]\n7. Sound & Wave Units\n● Frequency ka unit Hertz (Hz). [Q1504, Q1546]\n● Time period ka unit second (s). [Q1507]\n● 1 MHz = 10⁶ Hz; 1 GHz = 10⁹ Hz. [Q1504]\n● Wavelength ka unit meter (m); commonly nanometer (nm). [Q1547]\n● 1 nm = 10⁻⁹ m. [Q1547]\n● Audible range: 20 Hz se 20,000 Hz (20 kHz). [Q1504]\n● Ultrasound: >20 kHz; Infrasound: <20 Hz. [Q1504]\n8. Lens & Optical Units"," ● Magnification (m) ka koi unit nahi hai — ye dimensionless/ratio hota hai (m = v/u = hi/ho). [Q1491, Q1550]\n● Dioptre (D) lens power (P = 1/f) ka unit hai; magnification ka nahi. [Q1491, Q1516]\n● f = 50 cm = 0.5 m → P = +2 D (convex). [Q1516]\n● f = −40 cm = −0.4 m → P = −2.5 D (concave). [Q1516]\n9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1490–Q1562)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Magnification ka unit nahi hota — ye dimensionless ratio hai. [Q1491, Q1550]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: kWh energy ki unit hai, power ki nahi — confuse mat hona. [Q1490]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 HP = 746 W yaad rakhna — 1000 W nahi. [Q1494]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Newton derived unit hai — fundamental nahi. [Q1495]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Relative density ka unit nahi hota. [Q1515, Q1530]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 calorie = 4.2 J approx — exact 4.186 J hai. [Q1521]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 0°C = 273 K approx, exact 273.15 K hai. [Q1520]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: EMF aur Voltage donon ka unit Volt (V) hota hai — same unit, different concept. [Q1531]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Torque ka unit N·m hai lekin ye Joule nahi hota; torque vector hai, work scalar. [Q1551]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 Gauss = 10⁻⁴ Tesla — confuse mat hona. [Q1539]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Candela (cd) base unit hai — lumen derived unit hai. [Q1544]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 g/cm³ = 1000 kg/m³ — water ka density 1 g/cm³ = 1000 kg/m³. [Q1557]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J — atomic level energy ke liye use hota hai. [Q1555]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa ≈ 1 atm — standard atmospheric pressure. [Q1556]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Radiation measure karne ka device Geiger-Muller counter hai, Voltmeter/Ammeter/Spectrometer nahi.\n[Q1523]\n10. Numerical: Acceleration & Basic Mechanical Units\n● Acceleration ka SI unit m/s² hota hai; ye velocity ke rate of change ko batata hai — formula a = (v − u)/t. [Q1563]\n● Acceleration due to gravity g = 9.8 m/s² hota hai. [Q1563]\n11. Numerical: Temperature Scale Conversions\n● Kelvin se Celsius mein convert karne ke liye 273 subtract karte hain: C = K − 273. [Q1564]\n● Teenon scales ka relation: (F − 32)/180 = C/100 = (K − 273)/100. [Q1564]\n12. Numerical: Power & Energy Unit Conversions\n● 1 kW = 1000 W; isliye 2500 W = 2.5 kW. [Q1565]\n● 1 Watt = 1 Joule/second (1 J/s); power ko energy per unit time define karte hain. [Q1569]\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J = 3,600,000 J; calculation: 1000 W × 3600 s. [Q1566, Q1567]\n● 4.2 kWh = 15.12 × 10⁶ J; multiply karna padta hai: 4.2 × 3.6 × 10⁶ J. [Q1568]\n● 1 Joule = 10⁷ erg; CGS unit of work. [Q1569]"," 13. Numerical: Circular Motion — Velocity Formula\n● Uniform circular motion mein velocity formula: v = 2πr/t; jahan r radius aur t ek complete round ka time hai.\n[Q1570]\n● Circumference 2πr ko time t se divide karke velocity milti hai. [Q1570]\n14. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Acceleration unit: m/s².\n● K → °C: C = K − 273.\n● 1 kW = 1000 W.\n● 1 W = 1 J/s.\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J.\n● 1 J = 10⁷ erg.\n● Circular velocity: v = 2πr/t.\n15.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1563–Q1570)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kelvin se Celsius mein convert karte waqt 273 ghatana hota hai, jodna nahi. [Q1564]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J yaad rakhna — 3600 J ya 360000 J options confuse karne ke liye hote hain. [Q1566,\nQ1567]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 4.2 kWh ko Joule mein badalne ke liye 4.2 × 3.6 × 10⁶ karna hota hai, sirf 3.6 se multiply nahi. [Q1568]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 W = 1 J/s hai — erg/s nahi; 1 J = 10⁷ erg hota hai. [Q1569]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Circular motion mein velocity v = 2πr/t hai — πr/t ya 2πr²/t galat hain. [Q1570]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Acceleration ka unit m/s² hai — m/s (velocity) ya ft/s galat options hain. [Q1563]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 12 Units and Measurements Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0415","t":"13 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Science / Physics","x":[" PHYSICS CH.13 — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🔧\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n2. Magnetism & Earth's Magnetic Field\n3. States of Matter & Particle Motion\n4. Newton's Laws of Motion\n5. Simple Machines & Mechanical Advantage\n6. Friction\n7. Pressure in Fluids & Archimedes' Principle\n8. Centre of Gravity & Equilibrium\n9. Electromagnetic Induction & Electric Current\n10. Electric Instruments, Safety & Domestic Supply\n11. Semiconductor & Electronics\n12. Optical Instruments & Phenomena\n13. Nuclear & Atomic Physics\n14. Gravitation, Satellite & Universe\n15. Everyday Physics Applications\n16. Measurements & Precision Instruments\n17. Communication & Technology\n18.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1571–Q1628)\n⚠️\n19. Numerical: Relative Density & Density\n20. Numerical: Energy Unit Conversion\n21. Numerical: Kinematics — Two-Phase Motion (Rocket)\n22. Numerical: Kinematics — Acceleration & Displacement\n23. Numerical: Kinematics — Vertical Throw Problems\n24. Numerical: Kinematics — Equal Time Intervals under Constant Acceleration\n25. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n26.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1629–Q1640)\n⚠️\n1. Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n● Scalar = sirf magnitude, no direction; examples: speed, distance, mass, time, temperature, energy, work, power,\nfrequency. [Q1571, Q1580, Q1585, Q1590]\n● Vector = magnitude + direction; examples: velocity, force, momentum, acceleration, displacement, weight,\nelectric field. [Q1571, Q1580, Q1585]\n● Mass scalar hai; weight vector hai (gravity ki direction mein). [Q1571, Q1590]\n● Speed scalar hai; velocity vector hai. [Q1580]\n● Mass ek object ka constant property hai — ye place se place change nahi hoti; weight, velocity, aur momentum\nsab change ho sakte hain. [Q1600]\n2. Magnetism & Earth's Magnetic Field\n● Freely suspended magnet hamesha North-South direction mein align hota hai. [Q1572]\n● Magnet ka North pole geographical North ki taraf point karta hai; actually ye Earth's magnetic South pole hai\n(opposite poles attract). [Q1572]\n● Magnetic field lines North to South (external) aur South to North (magnet ke andar) jaati hain. [Q1572]"," 3. States of Matter & Particle Motion\n● Solid mein particles fixed positions par vibrate karte hain; strongest intermolecular forces. [Q1573, Q1581]\n● Liquid mein particles slide past each other; definite volume lekin no definite shape. [Q1573]\n● Gas mein particles free aur random motion mein hain; weakest intermolecular forces. [Q1573, Q1581]\n● Temperature badhane par solid/liquid/gas ke particles ki kinetic energy increase hoti hai. [Q1573]\n● Particles same temperature par different amounts of KE rakhte hain (Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution). [Q1573]\n4. Newton's Laws of Motion\n● First Law (Inertia): Object rest mein rahega ya uniform motion mein rahega jab tak external force na lage. [Q1575,\nQ1583]\n● Inertia = object ka resistance to change in motion; mass measure of inertia hai — jitna zyada mass, utni zyada\ninertia. [Q1575, Q1583, Q1595]\n● Second Law: F = ma; force proportional to acceleration. [Q1575]\n● Third Law: Har action ka equal aur opposite reaction. [Q1575, Q1586]\n● Rocket propulsion Newton ke Third Law par based hai. [Q1586]\n● Jerk lagaane par piche girna First Law (Inertia) ka example hai. [Q1583]\n● Acceleration = velocity change per unit time; vector quantity hai; positive ya negative dono ho sakti hai. [Q1589]\n5. Simple Machines & Mechanical Advantage\n● Mechanical Advantage (MA) = Load/Effort; Velocity Ratio (VR) = Effort distance/Load distance. [Q1574, Q1578]\n● Efficiency = (MA/VR) × 100% = (Output/Input) × 100%. [Q1574, Q1578]\n● Lever ka MA = Effort arm / Load arm. [Q1574]\n● Inclined plane ka VR = Length/Height; Pulley ka VR = Number of pulleys. [Q1578]\n● Efficiency kabhi 100% se zyada nahi hoti; ideal machine mein MA = VR. [Q1574]\n6. Friction\n● Friction hamesha motion ka virodh karta hai; direction of motion ke opposite. [Q1576, Q1587]\n● Static friction > Kinetic friction > Rolling friction. [Q1576]\n● Friction reduce karne ke tarike: lubrication, polishing, ball bearings, streamlining. [Q1576]\n● Friction increase karne ke tarike: rough surfaces, treads on tyres. [Q1576]\n● Friction ke bina chala nahi ja sakta — necessary evil hai. [Q1587]\n● Friction ka work lost nahi hota — heat energy mein transfer ho jaata hai (temperature difference ki wajah se).\n[Q1599]\n7. Pressure in Fluids & Archimedes' Principle\n● Pressure formula: P = F/A; unit Pascal (Pa). [Q1577, Q1582]"," ● Liquid pressure: P = hρg; depth ke saath badhta hai. [Q1577]\n● Same depth par liquid pressure same hota hai chahe container ka shape jo bhi ho. [Q1577]\n● Hydraulic press Pascal's Law par based hai; small force se large force generate hoti hai. [Q1582]\n● Archimedes' Principle: Fluid mein submerged object par upward buoyant force = displaced fluid ka weight = Vρg.\n[Q1579, Q1584]\n● Object float karega agar uska density liquid se kam hai; sink karega agar zyada hai. [Q1584]\n● Ship steel se bani hai (density > water) lekin hollow structure ki wajah se average density kam ho jaati hai. [Q1584]\n● Lactometer milk ki purity check karne ke liye — Archimedes principle. [Q1579]\n8. Centre of Gravity & Equilibrium\n● Centre of Gravity (CG) = point jahan total weight concentrate hota hai. [Q1588]\n● Stable equilibrium: CG neeche, body return karegi original position. [Q1588]\n● Unstable equilibrium: CG upar, body gir jaayegi. [Q1588]\n● Neutral equilibrium: CG same height, body new position mein rahegi. [Q1588]\n● Circus artist CG lower karke balance maintain karta hai. [Q1588]\n9. Electromagnetic Induction & Electric Current\n● Faraday's Law: Changing magnetic flux se EMF induce hota hai. [Q1601]\n● Fleming's Right Hand Rule = generator/dynamo ke liye; thumb = motion, forefinger = field, middle finger =\ncurrent. [Q1601]\n● Fleming's Left Hand Rule = motor ke liye; thumb = force/motion, forefinger = field, middle finger = current.\n[Q1601]\n● Lenz's Law: Induced current ki direction hamesha us change ka virodh karti hai jo usse produce karta hai. [Q1601]\n● Eddy currents = changing magnetic field se induced circular currents; undesirable heat produce karte hain;\nlaminated cores se reduce hote hain. [Q1602]\n● AC (Alternating Current): direction periodically change hoti hai; India mein 50 Hz frequency. [Q1603, Q1608]\n● DC (Direct Current): direction fixed hoti hai; battery, cell se milti hai. [Q1603]\n● Peak voltage = RMS voltage × √2; 220 V RMS ka peak ≈ 311 V. [Q1608]\n10. Electric Instruments, Safety & Domestic Supply\n● India mein domestic supply: 220 V, 50 Hz AC. [Q1608]\n● Ammeter = current measure karne ke liye (series mein lagta hai). [Q1592]\n● Voltmeter = potential difference measure karne ke liye (parallel mein lagta hai). [Q1592]\n● Galvanometer = small current detect karne ke liye. [Q1592]\n● Fuse = excess current se circuit protect karta hai; low melting point ki tin-lead alloy se bana hota hai. [Q1593]\n● MCB (Miniature Circuit Breaker) = overload ya short circuit par automatic trip; fuse se better kyunki reset ho sakta\nhai. [Q1623]\n● ELCB/RCCB = earth leakage detect karke trip karta hai; shock prevention. [Q1623]\n● Three-pin plug = live, neutral, aur earth pin; safety ke liye. [Q1622]\n● Earthing/Grounding = excess current ko ground mein bhejta hai; electric shock se bachata hai. [Q1622]"," ● Electric bell electromagnet par kaam karta hai. [Q1594]\n● Transformer = AC voltage step-up ya step-down karta hai; sirf AC ke liye kaam karta hai. [Q1596]\n● Step-up transformer: primary turns < secondary turns; voltage badhta hai. [Q1596]\n● Step-down transformer: primary turns > secondary turns; voltage ghatta hai. [Q1596]\n11. Semiconductor & Electronics\n● Semiconductor: conductivity conductor aur insulator ke beech; examples: Silicon (Si), Germanium (Ge). [Q1604]\n● Doping se semiconductor ki conductivity badhti hai. [Q1604]\n● n-type semiconductor: pentavalent impurity (e.g., Arsenic) add karte hain; electrons majority carriers. [Q1604]\n● p-type semiconductor: trivalent impurity (e.g., Boron) add karte hain; holes majority carriers. [Q1604]\n● p-n junction diode: current sirf ek direction mein flow hoti hai; rectifier banata hai. [Q1605]\n● LED (Light Emitting Diode): forward biased p-n junction se light emit hoti hai. [Q1606]\n● Transistor: amplifier ya switch ke roop mein use hota hai; 3 layers (npn ya pnp). [Q1607]\n● IC (Integrated Circuit) = chip par multiple transistors/components. [Q1607]\n12. Optical Instruments & Phenomena\n● Periscope: do parallel plane mirrors 45° par; submerged submarine mein use hota hai. [Q1609]\n● Kaleidoscope: multiple plane mirrors; beautiful patterns banate hain. [Q1609]\n● Simple microscope: convex lens of short focal length; magnified virtual image. [Q1610]\n● Compound microscope: do convex lenses (objective + eyepiece); high magnification. [Q1610]\n● Astronomical telescope: distant objects dekhne ke liye; objective large focal length. [Q1610]\n● Terrestrial telescope: erect image ke liye; additional lens lagti hai. [Q1610]\n● Total Internal Reflection (TIR): light denser se rarer medium mein jaaye aur angle > critical angle; examples:\nmirage, diamond sparkle, optical fiber. [Q1611]\n● Critical angle: sin C = 1/μ (μ = refractive index). [Q1611]\n● Optical fiber: TIR principle par kaam karta hai; medical endoscopy, communication mein use. [Q1611, Q1628]\n13. Nuclear & Atomic Physics\n● Isotopes: same atomic number, different mass number; examples: H, D, T; U-235, U-238. [Q1612]\n● Isobars: same mass number, different atomic number; examples: Ar-40, Ca-40. [Q1612]\n● Isotones: same number of neutrons; examples: C-14, N-15. [Q1612]\n● Radioactivity: spontaneous disintegration of unstable nucleus; alpha, beta, gamma emission. [Q1613]\n● Half-life: time jisme half of radioactive nuclei decay kar jaate hain. [Q1613]\n● Nuclear fission: heavy nucleus split; nuclear reactors, atomic bomb. [Q1613]\n● Nuclear fusion: light nuclei combine; sun, stars, hydrogen bomb. [Q1613]\n● Nucleus ke andar neutron, proton par jo force lagata hai use nuclear force kehte hain — gravitational,\nelectrostatic, ya tidal force nahi. [Q1597]"," 14. Gravitation, Satellite & Universe\n● Escape velocity: minimum velocity jo object ko Earth's gravity se free kar de; 11.2 km/s. [Q1614]\n● Orbital velocity: satellite ki velocity circular orbit mein; ≈ 8 km/s near Earth. [Q1614]\n● Geostationary satellite: Earth ke saath rotate karta hai; height ≈ 35,786 km; period = 24 hours. [Q1614]\n● Polar satellite: North-South pole ke charon ore orbit karta hai; Earth mapping ke liye. [Q1614]\n● Weightlessness in satellite: free-fall condition, not absence of gravity. [Q1614]\n● Free fall sirf vacuum mein hi possible hota hai — air/environment mein resistance ki wajah se object ki\nacceleration aur velocity affect hoti hai. [Q1598]\n● Big Bang Theory: universe ki origin; ~13.8 billion years ago. [Q1615]\n● Red shift: distant galaxies move away; universe expand ho raha hai. [Q1615]\n● Hubble's Law: recession velocity distance; v = H₀ × d.\n∝\n [Q1615]\n● Black hole: gravity so strong ki light bhi nahi nikal sakti; event horizon boundary. [Q1616]\n● Neutron star: supernova ke baad bacha core; extremely dense. [Q1616]\n● Supernova: massive star ka explosion; heavy elements create hote hain. [Q1616]\n● Light year: distance light travels in 1 year; ≈ 9.46 × 10¹² km. [Q1617]\n● Astronomical Unit (AU): Earth-Sun average distance; ≈ 1.5 × 10⁸ km. [Q1617]\n● Parsec: larger distance unit; ≈ 3.26 light years. [Q1617]\n15. Everyday Physics Applications\n● Refrigerator: vapour compression cycle; heat ko fridge se bahar nikalta hai. [Q1618]\n● Air conditioner: room se heat bahar nikalta hai; compressor, condenser, evaporator. [Q1618]\n● Pressure cooker: high pressure se water ka boiling point badhta hai; ≈ 120°C par cook hota hai. [Q1619]\n● Thermos flask (Dewar flask): vacuum between double walls; conduction, convection, radiation sab minimize.\n[Q1620]\n● Sea breeze: day mein land zyada garam, air land se sea ki taraf. [Q1621]\n● Land breeze: night mein sea zyada garam, air sea se land ki taraf. [Q1621]\n● Monsoon: differential heating se wind patterns; summer mein sea to land. [Q1621]\n16. Measurements & Precision Instruments\n● Barometer = atmospheric pressure measure karne ke liye. [Q1591]\n● Manometer = gas pressure measure karne ke liye. [Q1591]\n● Hygrometer = humidity measure karne ke liye. [Q1591]\n● Vernier caliper: length measure karne ka precise instrument; least count 0.01 mm ya 0.1 mm. [Q1624]\n● Screw gauge: aur bhi precise; least count 0.001 mm ya 0.01 mm. [Q1624]\n● Screw gauge ka principle: screw ka pitch; one complete rotation se linear displacement. [Q1624]\n● Least count = Pitch / Number of divisions on circular scale. [Q1624]\n● Sphygmomanometer = blood pressure measure karne ka instrument. [Q1625]\n● Stethoscope = heart/lungs ki sound sunne ke liye. [Q1625]\n● Ultrasound (USG) = body ke andar image banane ke liye; >20 kHz. [Q1625]\n● ECG (Electrocardiogram) = heart ki electrical activity record karta hai. [Q1625]"," ● X-ray = haddi fracture dekhne ke liye. [Q1625]\n17. Communication & Technology\n● Radar: radio waves se object detect karta hai; distance aur speed measure karta hai. [Q1626]\n● Sonar: sound waves se underwater object detect karta hai; ships/submarines ke liye. [Q1626]\n● LASER: Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation; coherent, monochromatic, intense beam. [Q1627]\n● LASER uses: surgery, barcode scanner, CD/DVD, cutting, welding. [Q1627]\n● Fiber optic communication: TIR principle; high speed data transfer. [Q1628]\n● Photocell/Photoelectric effect: light → electrical energy; automatic doors, burglar alarms mein. [Q1628]\n18.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (MCQ Q1571–Q1628)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass scalar hai; weight vector hai — confuse mat hona. [Q1571, Q1590]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mass constant rehta hai place se place; weight badalta hai gravity ke saath. [Q1600]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Static friction > Kinetic friction — hamesha. [Q1576]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Same depth par liquid pressure same hota hai chahe container alag ho. [Q1577]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ship steel se bani hai phir bhi float karti hai kyunki average density kam hai. [Q1584]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Ammeter series mein lagta hai; voltmeter parallel mein. [Q1592]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Fleming's Right Hand Rule = generator (induction); Left Hand Rule = motor — confuse mat hona. [Q1601]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Transformer sirf AC ke liye kaam karta hai — DC ke liye nahi. [Q1596, Q1608]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: LED sirf forward biased mein light deta hai; reverse biased mein nahi. [Q1606]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: TIR ke liye light denser se rarer medium mein jaani chahiye aur angle > critical angle hona chahiye.\n[Q1611]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Isotopes = same atomic number; Isobars = same mass number; Isotones = same neutrons — teenon alag\nhain. [Q1612]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nuclear force proton-neutron ko bandhta hai — gravitational ya electrostatic force nahi. [Q1597]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Geostationary satellite ka period 24 hours hota hai; height ≈ 35,786 km — fixed position dikhta hai.\n[Q1614]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Weightlessness = gravity absence nahi; free-fall condition hai. [Q1614]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: True free fall sirf vacuum mein hoti hai — air resistance ki wajah se normal free fall approximate hi hota\nhai. [Q1598]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Light year distance ka unit hai, time ka nahi. [Q1617]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Pressure cooker mein boiling point badhta hai pressure ke kaaran; normally 100°C se upar. [Q1619]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Thermos flask mein vacuum hoti hai walls ke beech — conduction aur convection block hote hain.\n[Q1620]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: MCB fuse se better hai kyunki ye automatic reset ho sakta hai. [Q1623]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Screw gauge Vernier se zyada precise hota hai; least count chhota hota hai. [Q1624]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sonar underwater ke liye; Radar air/land ke liye — donon alag hain. [Q1626]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Friction ka work lost nahi hota, heat energy mein convert ho jaata hai. [Q1599]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Inertia jitna zyada mass utni zyada — velocity ya volume par depend nahi karta. [Q1595]"," 19. Numerical: Relative Density & Density\n● Relative density = Density of substance / Density of water; dimensionless (unit nahi hoti). [Q1629, Q1630]\n● Metal density = 8.5 × 10³ kg/m³, water = 10³ kg/m³ → Relative density = 8.5. [Q1629]\n● Silver density = 10.8 × 10³ kg/m³, water = 10³ kg/m³ → Relative density = 10.8. [Q1630]\n● Density formula: ρ = m/V; unit kg/m³. [Q1631]\n● Mass = 300 kg, Volume = 150 m³ → Density = 300/150 = 2 kg/m³. [Q1631]\n● Relative density se actual density nikaalne ka formula: Density of substance = Relative density × Density of water.\n[Q1632]\n● Silver relative density = 10.8 → Density = 10.8 × 10³ kg/m³. [Q1632]\n20. Numerical: Energy Unit Conversion\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J; calculation: 1000 W × 3600 s. [Q1633]\n● kWh energy ki commercial unit hai — power ki nahi. [Q1633]\n21. Numerical: Kinematics — Two-Phase Motion (Rocket)\n● Rocket 20 m/s se 35 s tak jaata hai → Phase 1 distance = 20 × 35 = 700 m. [Q1634]\n● Fuel cut off ke baad free body ban jaata hai (u = 20 m/s upward, g = 10 m/s² neeche). [Q1634]\n● Max height tak jaane ke liye: v² = u² − 2gs; 0 = 400 − 20S → S = 20 m extra. [Q1634]\n● Total height = 700 + 20 = 720 m. [Q1634]\n●\n\n⚠️Phase-wise solve karna hota hai; direct formula apply karne se galat answer aayega. [Q1634]\n22. Numerical: Kinematics — Acceleration & Displacement\n● Acceleration formula: a = (v − u)/t; vector quantity. [Q1635]\n● u = 5 m/s, v = 10 m/s, t = 5 s → a = (10 − 5)/5 = 1 m/s². [Q1635]\n● Vertical throw mein displacement: s = ut − (1/2)gt² (upward positive, g negative). [Q1636, Q1637]\n● Ball 80 m max height tak jaati hai; u nikaalne ke liye: v² = u² − 2gs; 0 = u² − 1600 → u = 40 m/s. [Q1636]\n● 7 s baad displacement: s = 40×7 − 0.5×10×49 = 280 − 245 = 35 m. [Q1636]\n● u = 40 m/s, t = 6 s, g = 10 m/s² → s = 40×6 − 0.5×10×36 = 240 − 180 = 60 m. [Q1637]\n23. Numerical: Kinematics — Vertical Throw Problems\n● Time to reach highest point: v = u − gt; highest point par v = 0. [Q1640]\n● u = 14 m/s, g = 9.8 m/s² → t = 14/9.8 = 1.43 s. [Q1640]\n●\n\n⚠️g ki value exact 9.8 use karni padti hai; 10 se approximate nahi karna jab options close ho. [Q1640]\n24. Numerical: Kinematics — Equal Time Intervals under Constant Acceleration"," ● Rest se start karke constant acceleration mein: s = ut + (1/2)at²; u = 0 hone par s t².\n∝\n [Q1638]\n● Pehle 10 s mein distance X₁ = (1/2)×a×100 = 50a. [Q1638]\n● Velocity at 10 s: v = u + at = 10a. [Q1638]\n● Agle 10 s (11–20 s) mein distance X₂ = 10a×10 + (1/2)×a×100 = 100a + 50a = 150a. [Q1638]\n● Ratio: X₂ = 3X₁; yaani doosre equal interval mein pehle interval se 3 times distance. [Q1638]\n● Equal time intervals mein distance ratio from rest: 1 : 3 : 5 : 7 ... (odd numbers). [Q1638]\n● Object rest se 4 m/s² se 8 s baad speed: v = u + at = 0 + 4×8 = 32 m/s. [Q1639]\n25. Numerical: Formula Cheat Sheet\n● Relative Density: RD = ρ_substance / ρ_water.\n● Density: ρ = m/V.\n● 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J.\n● Acceleration: a = (v − u)/t.\n● 1st Equation: v = u + at.\n● 2nd Equation: s = ut + (1/2)at².\n● 3rd Equation: v² = u² + 2as.\n● Vertical throw displacement: s = ut − (1/2)gt².\n● Time to max height: t = u/g (at v=0).\n● Distance ratio (equal intervals, u=0): 1 : 3 : 5 : 7 ...\n26.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary (Numerical Q1629–Q1640)\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Relative density ka unit nahi hota — ye dimensionless ratio hai. [Q1629, Q1630]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Density nikaalne ke liye mass ÷ volume karte hain; unit kg/m³ hoti hai. [Q1631]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rocket jaise two-phase problems mein pehle constant velocity phase alag solve karo, phir free-fall phase\nalag. [Q1634]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Vertical throw mein displacement direction consider karta hai; distance sirf total path length hai.\n[Q1636, Q1637]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Time to highest point nikaalne mein v = 0 daalna hota hai; g exact 9.8 se divide karo jab options close\nhon. [Q1640]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Equal time intervals mein distance ratio 1:3:5... sirf rest se start karne par hota hai; initial velocity ho to\nalag hoga. [Q1638]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J — 3.6 × 10⁵ ya 36 × 10⁶ options confuse karne ke liye hote hain. [Q1633]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Physics Chapter 13 Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0416","t":"01 Dance","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — DANCE (\n🏷️\nनृत्य) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Classical Dances of India (\n\n\nभारतीयशास्त्रीयनृत्य)\n2. South Indian Dances & Kerala Special\n3. Odisha Dances\n4. West Bengal & Eastern India\n5. North East India (असम, मणिपुर, नागालैंड, सिक्किम, मेघालय, अरुणाचल, मिजोरम)\n6. Gujarat & Maharashtra Dances\n7. Madhya Pradesh & Chhattisgarh\n8. Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh & Telangana\n9. Himalayan States (J&K, Himachal, Uttarakhand, Ladakh)\n10. Bihar, Jharkhand, UP, Goa & Puducherry\n11. Islands & UTs (लक्षद्वीप, अंडमान-निकोबार)\n12. Dance Festivals & Special Facts\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Classical Dances of India (\n\n\nभारतीयशास्त्रीयनृत्य)\n● Bharatanatyam (तमिलनाडु) —\n\n\nसबसेपुरानाclassical dance.\n\n\n\nमानाजाताहैकि\nLord Brahma\nनेBharata Muni\n\n\nकोइसका\n\n\n\n\n\nज्ञानदियाथा।पहलेइसे'Sadir' (सदिर)\n\n\n\nकहतेथे।एकाहार्य(ekaharya) style —\n\nएकdancer\n\n\nएकहीperformance\n\nमेंकईroles\n\nनिभाताहै। [Q021, Q040]\n● Kathak —\n\n\nअकेलाभारतीयclassical dance\n\nजिसमेंPersian elements हैं; Mughal tradition\nसेheavily influenced. Bhakti\nmovement\nकेtime Radha-Krishna\n\nऔरGopis\n\n\nकेप्रेमपरbased था। [Q032]\n● Kathakali (केरल) —\n\n\nशाब्दिकअर्थ'Story-Play' (कहानी-नाटक)। [Q040]\n● Mohiniyattam (केरल) —\n\n\nशाब्दिकअर्थ'Mohini' (celestial enchantress)\n\nकानृत्य। [Q040]\n● Kuchipudi (\n\nआंध्रप्रदेश) — South India classical dance forms\nमेंcount\n\nहोताहै। [Q017]\n● Odissi (ओडिशा) — Triangle mudra\n\nइससेassociated\n\n\nहै।दोरूप: Nrita (hand movements/gestures perfection)\n\nऔर\nNritya (solo expressive dance, expressions\n\nपरfocus); Lord Shiva\n\nकाTandava dance\n\n\n\nभीइसमेंआताहै। [Q050]\n● Sattriya (असम) — 15\n\n\n\nवींसदीईस्वीमेंMahapurusha Sankaradeva\nनेintroduce\n\nकिया।2000\nमेंSangeet Natak Akademi\n\nनेclassical status\n\n\n\nदिया।मुख्यरूपसेKrishna-Radha relations\n\n\n\nकीकहानियोंपरbased ।\n\n⚠️\n\nयहNorth East (Assam)\n\nकाहै,\nSouth India\n\nकाclassical dance\n\nनहींहै। [Q012, Q017]\n● Manipuri (मणिपुर) — Hindu Vaishnavism themes\n\nपरbased; Raas Leela (Radha-Krishna love-inspired dance drama)\n\n\nप्रसिद्धहै।Female dancers 'Potloi' (\n\nबेलनाकारskirt)\n\n\nपहनतीहैं।Ghunghru missing\n\nरहताहै(\n\nयहmain feature\n\nनहींहै) ।\nInstruments: Kartal/Manjira\n\nऔरPung/Manipuri Mridang (\n\n\n\nदोसिरवालाढोल)। [Q041, Q049]\n2. South Indian Dances & Kerala Special\n●\n\nकेरलकेclassical + folk dances: Kathakali, Mohiniyattam, Theyyam, Ottamthullal, Kutiyattam, Nangiar Koothu,\nKalaripayattu, Velakali, Padayani। [Q002]\n● Padayani —\n\nकेरलमेंBhadrakali temple\n\n\n\nमेंकियाजानेवालाritual dance art form। [Q002]\n● Kolkali —\n\nकेरलकेNorth Malabar region\n\nकाfolk art; Kalaripayattu\nकेelements\n\n\n\n\nइसमेंशामिल।तमिलनाडुमेंइसेKolattam\n\n\nऔरआंध्रमेंKolamu\n\nकहतेहैं। [Q014]\n● Krishnanattam —\n\n\nकेरलकाtraditional theatre; 8 days\nमें8 plays perform\n\n\nहोतेहैं।Ashtapadi Attam\n\nकाmodified form;\nZamorin Manavedan\nनेevolve किया। [Q028]\n●\n\n\nदक्षिणभारतकेclassical dances: Bharatanatyam (Tamil Nadu), Kathakali (Kerala), Mohiniyattam (Kerala), Kuchipudi"," (Andhra Pradesh) — Sattriya\n\n\n\nइसमेंनहींआता(Assam\n\nकाहै)। [Q017]\n3. Odisha Dances\n● Mayurbhanj Chhau —\n\n\nओडिशाकाsemi-classical/martial-folk dance\n\n\n।पूर्वीभारत(Orissa, West Bengal, Jharkhand)\n\nकी\ntradition\n\n।तीनforms: Saraikela Chhau (Jharkhand), Mayurbhanj Chhau (Odisha), Purulia Chhau (West Bengal)।\n[Q001]\n● Dalkhai —\n\nओडिशाकेAdivasis\n\nकाpopular folk dance। [Q003]\n● Paika Dance —\n\nओडिशामेंfamous; Munda tribe\nसेassociated;\n\nशादीकेoccasion\n\n\n\nपरकियाजाताहै। [Q010]\n● Gotipua —\n\nओडिशामेंyoung boy dancers\n\nकरतेहैं,\n\n\nजोलड़कियोंकेdress\nमेंJagannath\n\nऔरKrishna\n\n\n\nकीस्तुति\nकरतेहैं; Odissi\nclassical dance\n\nकाpart। [Q047]\n● Odissi — Michael Jackson\nके1991 hit 'Black or White' music video\n\n\nमेंएकमात्रभारतीयdance form Odissi था; dancer\nYamuna Sangarasivam\nनेperform\n\nकियाथा। [Q029]\n●\n\nअन्यOdisha dances: Sambalpuri, Chaiti Ghoda, Ghumura। [Q047]\n4. West Bengal & Eastern India\n● Alkap —\n\n\nझारखंडऔरWest Bengal\n\n\n\nदोनोंकेकुछहिस्सोंमेंprevalent rural dance-drama performance। [Q005]\n● Gambhira —\n\n\n\n\nपश्चिमबंगालमेंकियाजाताहै; wooden masks\n\nकाuse; Chaitra Sankranti festival\nमेंtemples\nमेंperform\n\nहोताहै; theme: Lord Shiva\n\nऔरParvati\n\nकाप्रेम। [Q026]\n● WB\n\nकेअन्यdances: Kirtan dance, Kushan, Chhau। [Q005]\n● Jharkhand folk dances: Chau, Paika, Khadia, Kadsa, Santhali, Mundari। [Q005]\n● Jat-Jatin —\n\nबिहार(मिथिला)\n\nकाpopular folk dance; पुरुष-\n\n\n\n\nमहिलाकीजोड़ीकरतीहै; Jat-Jatin\n\nकीepic love story\n\nपर\nbased। [Q020]\n● Bihar\n\nकेअन्यfolk dances: Bakho-Bakhain, Panwariya। [Q034]\n5. North East India (असम, मणिपुर, नागालैंड, सिक्किम, मेघालय, अरुणाचल, मिजोरम)\n● Assam: Sattriya (classical), Bihu (\n\nतीनfestivals\n\nकासमूह), Bagurumba, Deodhani, Ali-Ai-Ligang, Bhortal, Khel Gopal,\nKaliGopal, Nat Puja, Chongli। [Q025, Q036]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kathi (काठी) MP\n\n\n\nकेनिमाड़क्षेत्रकाfolk dance है(Balai Samaj), Assam\n\nकानहीं। [Q036]\n● Manipur: Thang Ta — exclusive martial dance; mock fight sequence; Huyen Lallong (= art of sword and spear) ।\nManipuri classical dance — Vaishnavism/Raas Leela theme; Potloi skirt; no ghunghru। [Q013, Q041, Q049]\n● Nagaland: Rengma folk dance — Rengma tribe\n\nकरतीहै, Ngada festival (Thanksgiving)\n\nमें।अन्य: Aaluyattu, Butterfly\ndance, Changai dance, Monyoasho। [Q011]\n● Changsang — Nagaland\nकेChang tribe\n\nकाtraditional folk dance; Naknyulum festivals में; mankind\n\nऔरearth\nके\nbirth-place\n\n\nकीस्तुति\nमें। [Q018]\n● Sikkim: Chaam/Chham — Buddhist lamas (monks)\n\nकाmasked dance; Pang Lhabsol festival\n\n\nमें।अन्यdances:\nRechungma (happy occasions), Gha To Kito (Sikkim\n\nकीसमृद्धि), Chi Rmu (Sikkim\n\nकीuniqueness\n\nकाcelebration)।\n[Q019, Q030]\n● Maruni — Nepalese folk dance of Magar community; Nepal\n\nकेसाथIndia\nमेंDarjeeling, Assam, Sikkim, Bhutan,\nMyanmar\nमेंpopular; Tihar festival\nमेंperform\n\nहोताहै। [Q046]\n● Meghalaya: Laho — Behdienkhlam festival\nमेंJaintia (Pnar) tribe द्वारा; men & women\n\nदोनों।अन्य: Derogata, Shad\nSuk Mynsiem, Nongkrem। [Q051]\n● Arunachal Pradesh: Bardo Chham — Monpa language\nमें\"Chham\" = Dance; good over evil\n\nकीtriumph\n\nपरbased।\n[Q023]"," ● Mizoram: Cheraw (\n\n\nबांसनृत्य/ bamboo dance) — 6-8\n\nलोगbamboo sticks hold\n\n\nकरतेहैं।अन्य: Khuallam, Chailam,\nSawlakin, Chawnglaizawn, Zangtalam। [Q034, Q039]\n6. Gujarat & Maharashtra Dances\n● Gujarat: Siddi Dhamal, Garba, Dandiya, Bhavai, Tippani, Hudo, Padhar। [Q004]\n● Tippani — Gujarat\nकेChorwad\n\nऔरVeraval region (Saurashtra)\nसेoriginate हुआ। [Q003]\n● Maharashtra: Lavani —\n\nमहिलाएंNauvari (9-yard) saree\n\nपहनकरDholki\n\n\n\nकीथापपरperform\n\n\nकरतीहैं।अन्य:\nDhangarigaja, Lezim, Koli, Gondhal, Tamasha। [Q002, Q027]\n7. Madhya Pradesh & Chhattisgarh\n● Madhya Pradesh: Jawara (Bundelkhand harvest dance — men & women together), Rai (Bediyas tribe, Shravan\nmonth July-August, men female disguise में), Gaur, Badhai, Karma, Bhagoria, Matki, Maanch, Aada, Khada Nach,\nPhulpati, Grida, Selalarki, Selabhadoni। [Q007, Q008, Q028]\n● Khajuraho Dance Festival — 1975\nमेंGovernment of India + MP Kala Parishad\nनेshuru किया; spring season में;\nUNESCO World Heritage Sites\n\nकीbackdrop\nमेंclassical dances। [Q016]\n● Chhattisgarh: Gaur Maria (Bastar plateau; births & weddings पर), Saila, Karma, Sua Nacha, Pandavani, Panthi\nDance, Raut Nacha। [Q005, Q024]\n● Raut Nacha — Chhattisgarh\nकेYadav community का; Dev Uthni Ekadashi पर; Lord Krishna\n\nकीKing Kansa\n\nपरvictory\ncelebrate\n\nकरताहै;\n\nरातमेंperform\n\nहोताहै। [Q043]\n● Tapali — Chhattisgarh\n\nकाfolk dance है, Uttarakhand\n\n\nकानहीं।\n\n⚠️ [Q042]\n8. Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh & Telangana\n● Karnataka: Huli Vesha (Tiger faced dance) — Navratri\nमेंDurga\n\nकोtribute; tiger costume/mask/painting; Dollu\nKunitha (Sri Beeralingeshwara/Lord Shiva worship), Kamsale, Bolak-aat, Yakshagana। [Q006, Q048]\n● Andhra Pradesh: Kolannalu (Kolattam) — village festivals\nमेंperform\n\nहोताहै; stick dance\n\nजैसा।Villu Pattu — ancient\nmusical story-telling method of Southern India। [Q009]\n● Telangana: Mathuri folk dance — Adilabad district; Mathuri tribe (Koppu Lambadi) Krishna Ashtami (Sravana\nMasam)\n\n\nमेंकरतीहै।अन्य: Gussadi, Dhimsa, Lambadi, Perini Sivatandavam, Dappu। [Q035]\n9. Himalayan States (J&K, Himachal, Uttarakhand, Ladakh)\n● Jammu & Kashmir: Dumhal —\n\nकेवलWattal tribe\nकेmen perform\n\n\n\nकरसकतेहैं।अन्य: Rouf, Bhand Pather, Hafiza\nDance, Bhand Jashan, Bacha Nagma, Wuegi-Nachun, Hikat, Mandjas। [Q033]\n● Wanawan — Kashmir\n\nकाfolk music; wedding ceremonies\n\n\nमेंगायाजाताहै। [Q031]\n● Himachal Pradesh: Nati — dance\n\nकेअंतमेंYagya perform\n\nहोताहैGods/Goddesses\n\nकोhomage\n\n\nकेरूपमें।अन्य: Jhora,\nJhali, Chharhi, Dhaman, Chhapeli, Mahasu, Dangi। [Q015, Q034]\n● Uttarakhand: Hurkiya Baul — agricultural season में; Chholiya — Kumaon region\nमेंRajput community द्वारा; अन्य:\nPandav Nritya, Bhotia Dance, Jhora, Mukhota, Pandava Leela, Langvir, Chanchari, Chhapeli। [Q022, Q037]\n● Ladakh: Spao Dance — Spao = warrior (Ladakhi); King Kesar\n\nऔरdivine horse\n\nकीlegends; \"Mahabharata epic of\nCentral Asia\"\n\n\n\nकहाजाताहै।Shondol dance\n\nभीfamous ।अन्य: Kathok Chenmo, Mentok Stanmo, Jabro। [Q004, Q038]"," 10. Bihar, Jharkhand, UP, Goa & Puducherry\n● Jat-Jatin — Bihar (Mithila) का; epic love story theme। [Q020]\n● UP: Kajri — Monsoon (वर्षा) season\nसेrelated folk song & dance; North India\nमेंpopular। [Q045]\n● Goa: Dhalo — ritual folk dance;\n\n\nमहिलाएंकरतीहैं; household protection\n\nकीprayer ।अन्य: Fugdi, Kunbi, Dhangar,\nMandi, Jhagor, Khol, Shigmo, Mando। [Q007, Q025, Q027]\n● Puducherry: Garadi — ceremonial folk dance; Ramayana\nसेrelated; Villianur temple\nमेंperform\n\nहोताहै। [Q003]\n11. Islands & UTs (लक्षद्वीप, अंडमान-निकोबार)\n● Lakshadweep: Parichakali — martial art form; swords & shields props; Lava Dance, Kolkali Dance\n\n\nभीयहींके। [Q044]\n● Andaman & Nicobar: Nicobari dance — traditional dance; Siddi Dhamal Gujarat\n\nकाहै(trap area)। [Q004]\n12. Dance Festivals & Special Facts\n● Khajuraho Dance Festival — 1975\nमेंestablish हुआ; MP Kala Parishad + Govt of India collaboration; spring season;\nclassical dances। [Q016]\n● Michael Jackson\nके'Black or White' (1991) video\nमेंOdissi था; dancer Yamuna Sangarasivam। [Q029]\n● Mohiniyattam = celestial enchantress Mohini\n\nकाdance। [Q040]\n13.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sattriya South India\n\nकाclassical dance\n —\n\nनहींहै\nयहAssam (North East)\n\n\nकाहै।South India classical =\nBharatanatyam, Kathakali, Mohiniyattam, Kuchipudi। [Q017]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kathi folk dance Assam\nसेrelated\n —\n\nनहीं\nयहMP (Nimar region, Balai Samaj)\n\nकाहै। [Q036]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Tapali folk dance Uttarakhand\n\n —\n\nकानहीं\nयहChhattisgarh\n\nकाहै। [Q042]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Lavani-Kerala, Ghoomar-Gujarat, Dandiya-UP —\n\nयेसबgalat pairings हैं; Lavani = Maharashtra, Ghoomar\n= Rajasthan, Dandiya = Gujarat, Gaur Maria = Chhattisgarh (sahi pairing)। [Q024]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Manipuri dance\nमेंGhunghru\n\n\nनहींहोता(\n\nबाकीclassical dances\nमेंmain feature\n\nहोताहै); female dancers\nPotloi skirt\n\nपहनतीहैं। [Q049]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Maruni — Nepalese folk dance है; India\nमेंSikkim, Darjeeling, Assam\nमेंpopular;\n\nसिर्फSikkim\n\nकानहीं।\n[Q046]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kolkali = Kerala (North Malabar); Tamil Nadu\nमेंKolattam; Andhra\nमेंKolamu — अलग-\n\nअलगnames same\nart ke। [Q014]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 1 Dance Full Mind Map (Q1-Q51)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0417","t":"02 Art Personality","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — ART PERSONALITY (\n🏷️\n\nकलाव्यक्ति\nत्व) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Classical Dancers & Their Dance Forms (\n\nशास्त्रीयनर्तक)\n2. Gharanas & Classical Vocalists (\n\n\n\nघरानेऔरशास्त्रीयगायक)\n3. Carnatic Music Legends (\n\n\nकर्नाटकसंगीतत\nकेदिग्गज)\n4. Instrumentalists — Tabla & Sitar (\n\n\nवाद्ययंत्रवादक)\n5. Folk / Regional Art Personalities (\n\n\nलोककलाव्यक्ति\nत्व)\n6. Painters & Visual Artists (चित्रकार)\n7. Playback Singers & Records (\n\nपार्श्वगायक)\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Classical Dancers & Their Dance Forms (\n\nशास्त्रीयनर्तक)\n● Minati Mishra — Odissi dancer; Padma Shri (2012), Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (2000)। [Q052]\n● Sonal Mansingh — Bharatanatyam + Odissi\n\nदोनोंमेंexpert; Padma Vibhushan (2003), Padma Bhushan (1992),\nSangeet Natak Akademi Award for Odissi (1987)। [Q064]\n● Rajkumar Singhajit Singh — Manipuri dance ke leading exponent, choreographer aur guru; Pung cholom aur\nRaslila भी; Padma Shri (1986)। [Q065]\n● Birju Maharaj — Kathak (Lucknow \"Kalka-Bindadin\" Gharana); Padma Vibhushan (1986), Sangeet Natak Akademi\nAward (1964), Kalidas Samman (1987), National Film Award Best Choreography (2012), Filmfare Best\nChoreography (2016)। [Q066]\n● Shovana Narayan — Kathak artist; Padma Shri (1992); guru Birju Maharaj थे; Indian Audit and Accounts Service\nमें\ncareer officer भी। [Q067]\n● Rukmini Devi — Bharatanatyam dancer; NOT a painter; Indian history\nमेंRajya Sabha\n\nकेलिएnominate\n\n\nहोनेवाली\n\nपहलीमहिला। [Q068]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Darshana Jhaveri Odissi dancer\n —\n\nनहींहैं\nयहManipuri dancer हैं; Guru Bipin Singh\n\nकीshishya; 1958\nमें\nsisters\n\nकेसाथstage performance\n\nशुरूकी। [Q059]\n● Popular Odissi Dancers list: Sonal Mansingh, Jhelum Paranjape, Mayadhar Raut, Gangadhar Pradhan, Ileana\nCitaristi, Leena Mohanty, Chitra Krishnamurti, Bijayini Satpathy, Minati Mishra, Shagun Bhutani, Kumkum\nMohanty। [Q052, Q059]\n2. Gharanas & Classical Vocalists (\n\n\n\nघरानेऔरशास्त्रीयगायक)\n● Pandit Jasraj — Mewati Gharana; Indore ke Ghagge Nazir Khan aur Wahid Khan (brothers)\nनेfounded किया;\nPadma Vibhushan (2000), Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1987), Padma Shri (1975)। [Q056]\n● Rattan Mohan Sharma — Mewati Gharana; Tarana singer; Khayal, Haveli Sangeet, Tappa, Bhajan, Rajasthani Folk\n\nभीperform\n\nकरतेहैं। [Q058]\n● Pandit Bhimsen Joshi — Kirana Gharana; Khayal form\n\nकेलिएfamous; Bharat Ratna (2008); first Indian musician\njinke concerts\n\nकाadvertisement New York City\nमेंposters\nसेहुआ। [Q060]\n3. Carnatic Music Legends (\n\n\nकर्नाटकसंगीतत\nकेदिग्गज)\n● MS Subbulakshmi — Legendary Carnatic vocalist; born in Madurai (Tamil Nadu); Bharat Ratna (1998), Padma\nVibhushan (1975), Padma Bhushan (1954), Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1956), Ramon Magsaysay Award"," (1974)। [Q055]\n● Trinity of Carnatic Music (\n\n\n\n\nकर्नाटकसंगीतत\nकीत्रिमूर्ति\n/ Three Jewels) — Tyagaraja, Muthuswami Dikshitar, Syama\nSastri; 18\n\n\nवींसदीकेcomposer-musicians;\n\n\n\nतीनोंकाजन्मThiruvarur (\n\nपहलेThanjavur Dist, Tamil Nadu)\nमेंहुआ। [Q057]\n● Purandara Dasa — \"Father of Carnatic Music\"; Lord Krishna\nकेgreat devotee, poet, musician; legend\n\nकेअनुसार\nSaint Narada\n\nकाincarnation\n\n\nमानेजातेहैं। [Q062]\n4. Instrumentalists — Tabla & Sitar (\n\n\nवाद्ययंत्रवादक)\n● Alla Rakha (Allarakha Qureshi) — Tabla player; Padma Shri (1977), Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1982); other\nfamous tabla players: Zakir Hussain, Trilok Gurtu, Talvin Singh, Anindo Chatterjee, Rimpa Siva, Tanmoy Bose।\n[Q053]\n● Zakir Hussain — Tabla player, composer, percussionist, music producer, film actor; Padma Shri (1988), Padma\nBhushan (2002), Padma Vibhushan (2023); 2008 Grammy jeeta — Best Contemporary World Music Album -\nGlobal Drum Project। [Q063]\n● Ravi Shankar — Sitar player; National Orchestra of India\nकेfounder; Bharat Ratna (1999), Padma Vibhushan\n(1981), Padma Bhushan (1967); 5 Grammy Awards —\n\n\nसबसेज़्यादाGrammy\n\n\nजीतत\nनेवालेIndian। [Q054]\n5. Folk / Regional Art Personalities (\n\n\nलोककलाव्यक्ति\nत्व)\n● Teejan Bai — Pandavani exponent from Chhattisgarh; Mahabharata tales\n\nकोmusical accompaniment\n\nकेसाथenact\n\nकरतीहैं; Padma Shri (1988), Padma Bhushan (2003), Padma Vibhushan (2019), Sangeet Natak Akademi Award\n(1995)। [Q061]\n6. Painters & Visual Artists (चित्रकार)\n● Ganesh Pyne — Painting; Bengal School of Art\nकेartist; \"Poetic surrealism\"\n\nअपनीstyle; fantasy\n\nऔरdark imagery;\nBengali folklore\n\nऔरmythology themes। [Q069]\n● Famous Indian Painters list: Abanindranath Tagore, Amrita Sher-Gil, Jamini Roy, Kalipada Ghoshal, Mukul Chandra\nDey, Nandalal Bose, Ganesh Pyne। [Q068, Q069]\n7. Playback Singers & Records (\n\nपार्श्वगायक)\n● Asha Bhosle — Guinness World Record for most solo studio recordings; ~11,000 solo, duets\n\nऔरchorus backed\nsongs record ki hain; Padma Vibhushan (2008), Dadasaheb Phalke Award (2000)। [Q070]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Darshana Jhaveri = Manipuri dancer, NOT Odissi; Odissi dancers\nमेंcount\n\nमतत\nकरना। [Q059]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rukmini Devi = Bharatanatyam dancer, NOT painter; Rajya Sabha nominate\n\n\n\nहोनेवालीपहलीमहिला।\n[Q068]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mewati Gharana — Pandit Jasraj aur Rattan Mohan Sharma\n\nदोनोंsame gharana से; founder Ghagge Nazir\nKhan aur Wahid Khan (Indore)। [Q056, Q058]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kirana Gharana = Bhimsen Joshi; Mewati Gharana = Jasraj & Rattan Mohan Sharma — mix\n\nमतत\nकरना।\n[Q060]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Grammy Awards — Ravi Shankar (5 Grammys) = most Grammys by an Indian; Zakir Hussain = 2008"," Grammy for Global Drum Project। [Q054, Q063]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bharat Ratna in this file — Ravi Shankar (1999), MS Subbulakshmi (1998), Bhimsen Joshi (2008);\n\nतीनों\nअलग-\n\nअलगfields से। [Q054, Q055, Q060]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 2 Art Personality Full Mind Map (Q52-Q70)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0418","t":"03 Art Awards","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — ART AWARDS (\n🏷️\n\nकलापुरस्कार) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indian Literary Awards (\n\n\nभारतीयसाहित्यिकपुरस्कार)\n2. International Music & Film Awards (\n\n\n\n\nअंतर्राष्ट्रीयसंगीतऔरफिल्मपुरस्कार)\n3. Indian State / National Art Awards (\n\n\nभारतीयराज्य/\n\n\nराष्ट्रीयकलापुरस्कार)\n4. Famous Plays & Playwrights (\n\n\n\nप्रसिद्धनाटकऔरनाटककार)\n5.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Indian Literary Awards (\n\n\nभारतीयसाहित्यिकपुरस्कार)\n● Sahitya Akademi — 12 March 1954\n\nकोGovernment of India\nनेformally inaugurate किया; 24 languages\nमेंaward\n\n\nदियाजाताहै; Rabindra Bhawan, Delhi\n\nमेंतीनacademies situated हैं: Sangeet Natak Akademi, Lalit Kala Akademi,\nSahitya Akademi। [Q071]\n● Vyas Samman — KK Birla Foundation\n\nद्वाराannually\n\n\nदियाजाताहै; Jnanpith ke baad second highest literary award;\nHindi language\n\n\n\nमेंहोनाचाहिएऔरpast 10 years\nमेंpublish\n\nहुआहो; first awarded 1991 में; first awardee — Ram Vilas\nSharma। [Q072]\n● Bal Sahitya Puraskar — 2010\nमेंestablish हुआ; Devendra Mewari\n\nको2021\n —\nमेंमिला\nplay \"Natak Natak me Vigyan\"\n\nकेलिए। [Q073]\n2. International Music & Film Awards (\n\n\n\n\nअंतर्राष्ट्रीयसंगीतऔरफिल्मपुरस्कार)\n● Grammy Award —\n\nसिर्फMusic\nसेassociated; Recording Academy / National Academy Recordings (USA) द्वारा; 1959\n\nमेंestablish हुआ। [Q074]\n● Oscar (Academy Award) — 1929\nमेंestablish; most prestigious film award; AR Rahman — first Indian to win two\nOscars (2009) for Slumdog Millionaire; categories: Best Original Score\n\nऔरBest Original Song — Jai Ho। [Q076]\n● Bhanu Athaiya — first Indian to win an Academy Award; costume design\nकेलिए। [Q076]\n● Cannes Film Festival — 1946\nमेंfirst held; films\nसेassociated। [Q074]\n● Pulitzer Prize — newspaper journalism, literary achievements, musical composition\nमेंexcellence\nकेलिए; first\nawarded 1917; Columbia University, US\n\nद्वाराpresent\n\nहोताहै; Kendrick Lamar — first rapper\n\nजिसनेPulitzer Prize\nfor Music जीता; album \"Damn\" (2017)\nकेलिए। [Q075]\n● Tagore Award — 2011\nमेंestablish; harmony\n\nऔरuniversalism foster\n\nकरनेमेंoutstanding achievement\nकेलिए;\n\nयह\nmusic-specific\n\nनहींहै। [Q074]\n3. Indian State / National Art Awards (\n\n\nभारतीयराज्य/\n\n\nराष्ट्रीयकलापुरस्कार)\n● Kalidas Samman — Madhya Pradesh Government द्वारा; 4 categories: Plastic Arts, Theatre, Classical Music,\nClassical Dance; Kalidasa\n\nकेनामपर; first given 1980 में। [Q077]\n● MP\n\nकेअन्यawards: Kabir Samman, Tansen Samman, Lata Mangeshkar Samman, Kumar Gandharva Award। [Q077]\n● Dadasaheb Phalke Award — Films\n\nकेक्षेत्रमें; Dadasaheb Phalke = Father of Indian Cinema; first Indian feature film\nRaja Harishchandra (1913) बनाई; award 1969\nमेंintroduce हुआ; first awardee — Devika Rani (first lady of Indian\ncinema)। [Q078]"," 4. Famous Plays & Playwrights (\n\n\n\nप्रसिद्धनाटकऔरनाटककार)\n● Maya from Madurai — Naren Weiss\n\n\nद्वारालिखितplay। [Q073]\n● Khwab-e-Hasti — Agha Hashar Kashmiri\n\n\nद्वारालिखितplay। [Q073]\n● Nil Darpan — Dinabandhu Mitra\n\n\nद्वारालिखितBengali-language play। [Q073]\n5.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Grammy = only Music; Oscar/Cannes = Film; Tagore = Harmony/Universalism — mix\n\nमतकरना। [Q074]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: AR Rahman = first Indian to win two Academy Awards; Bhanu Athaiya = first Indian overall to win Oscar\n(costume design) — dono alag hain। [Q076]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kalidas Samman = MP Government\n\nदेतीहै; 4 categories hain — sirf dance ya music mein restrict\n\nमत\nसोचना। [Q077]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Dadasaheb Phalke Award = Films; Jnanpith/Vyas Samman = Literature; Pulitzer = Journalism + Literature\n+ Music — alag-alag fields। [Q078]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Devika Rani = Dadasaheb Phalke Award\n\nकीfirst recipient; unhe \"first lady of Indian cinema\"\n\n\nकहाजाताहै।\n[Q078]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 3 Art Awards Full Mind Map (Q71-Q78)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0419","t":"04 Musical Instruments","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — MUSICAL INSTRUMENTS (\n🏷️\n\nवाद्ययंत्र) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. String Instruments & Their Masters (\n\nतारवाद्य)\n2. Wind Instruments & Their Masters (\n\nवायुवाद्य)\n3. Percussion Instruments (\n\nतालवाद्य)\n4. Natya Shastra — Bharat Muni's 4 Groups (\n\n\n\nभरतमुनि\nकावर्गीकरण)\n5. Hindustani vs Carnatic — Styles & Artists\n6. Indo-Islamic Musical Instruments\n7. Special / Unique Instruments & Facts\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. String Instruments & Their Masters (\n\nतारवाद्य)\n● Sitar — Ravi Shankar, Anoushka Shankar, Vilayat Khan (famous players)। [Q094, Q097]\n● Sarod — Ustad Amjad Ali Khan (\"Sarod Samrat\"); Ustad Ali Akbar Khan\n\nभीmaster; clear & fast 'ekhara taans' ke\nliye famous। [Q084, Q089, Q097, Q102]\n● Santoor — Pt. Shiv Kumar Sharma\nनेpopularize किया; Bhajan Sopori, Pt. Tarun Bhattacharya भी। [Q084, Q089, Q094,\nQ097]\n● Sarangi — bowed instrument; Pandit Ram Narayan\nनेinternationally popularize किया; Bundu Khan, Ustad\nHafizullah Khan, Surinder Sandhu, Dhruba Ghosh, Umrao Bundu Khan। [Q079]\n● Veena / Rudra Veena — Ustad Mohi Bahuauddin Dagar (Rudra Veena); Asad Ali Khan, Dabir Khan, Zia Mohiuddin\nDagar, Pandit Gopal Krishnan भी; Asad Ali Khan, Asit Kumar Banerjee, Siddhartha Banerjee (Veena)। [Q080, Q079]\n● Guitar (Hindustani Classical) — Pandit Brij Bhushan Kabra\nनेHindustani classical\nमेंpopularize किया। [Q084]\n● Mohan Veena — Vishwa Mohan Bhatt\nनेcreate & popularize किया; modified Hawaiian Guitar / Hindustani Slide\nGuitar; main & sympathetic strings, hollow acoustic box, solid neck। [Q088]\n● Violin — Dr. Lakshminarayan Subramaniam (Padma Bhushan 2001); Mrs. N. Rajam (Hindustani classical tradition)।\n[Q087, Q098]\n● String instruments list: Cello, Violin, Bass — ye sab Tat Vadya (string) hain। [Q101]\n● Mandolin — U. Srinivas (player); ye string instrument hai, percussion नहीं। [Q079, Q082]\n2. Wind Instruments & Their Masters (\n\nवायुवाद्य)\n● Flute (Bansuri) — Pandit Hariprasad Chaurasia (Padma Vibhushan 2000, Padma Bhushan 1992); TR Mahalingam\n(aerophone — vibrating air column); Rajendra Prasanna भी। [Q080, Q096, Q100]\n● Shehnai — Ustad Bismillah Khan; Bharat Ratna (2001), Padma Shri (1961), Padma Vibhushan (1980), Padma\nBhushan (1968), Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship (1994) — Bharat Ratna milne wale pehle classical musician।\n[Q099]\n● Wind instruments types — Brass (horns, trumpets) aur Woodwind (flutes, saxophones, shehnai)। [Q093]\n3. Percussion Instruments (\n\nतालवाद्य)\n● Tabla — Alla Rakha, Kishan Maharaj (famous players)। [Q080, Q097]\n● Carnatic Percussion — Mridangam, Ghatam, Morsing; Mandolin isme count\n\n\nनहींहोता(string hai)। [Q082]"," ● Kanjira — South India\n\nकाframe drum; jackfruit tree wood, lizard skin, goatskin, metal\nसेबना; wooden circular\nframe\n\nपरskin stretched\n\nहोतीहै। [Q083]\n● Khol — terracotta two-sided drum; eastern India\nमेंdevotional music\nकेलिए; wind instrument नहीं। [Q093]\n● Nagada (North India) → South India counterpart = Chenda (Kerala/South India cylindrical percussion)। [Q095]\n● Pakhawaj — Totaram Sharma (player); Shiv Kumar Sharma\n\nनहीं(wo Santoor hain)। [Q097]\n4. Natya Shastra — Bharat Muni's 4 Groups (\n\n\n\nभरतमुनि\nकावर्गीकरण)\n● Natya Shastra (200 BC – 200 AD)\nमेंBharat Muni\nने4 groups बनाए: Avanaddha Vadya (\n\nझिल्लीदार/ percussion —\nmembranophones); Ghan Vadya (\n\nठोस/ solid — idiophones); Sushir Vadya (\n\nवायु/ wind — aerophones); Tat Vadya\n(\n\nतार/ string — chordophones)। [Q081]\n5. Hindustani vs Carnatic — Styles & Artists\n● Hindustani Classical Styles (10 main): Dhrupad, Khayal, Tappa, Chaturanga, Tarana, Sargam, Thumri, Ragasagar,\nHori, Dhamar। [Q091]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alapana = Carnatic ka exposition of raga, Hindustani style नहीं। [Q091]\n● Carnatic Exponents — M.S. Subbulakshmi, Priya Sisters, Bombay Jayashri। [Q085]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kishori Amonkar = Jaipur Gharana (Hindustani Classical), NOT Carnatic। [Q085]\n● Dadra Taal — Hindustani classical; 6 beats (3+3 division); bhajan, thumri, film songs\nमेंuse। [Q086]\n6. Indo-Islamic Musical Instruments\n● Indo-Islamic origin wale: Rubab, Sarod, Sitar, Tabla, Sarangi। [Q092]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Veena = ancient Indian stringed instrument, Indo-Islamic origin नहीं। [Q092]\n7. Special / Unique Instruments & Facts\n● V. Balsara = Piano\nसेassociated। [Q090]\n● Trumpet = brass wind instrument, string instrument नहीं; Cello, Violin, Bass = string। [Q101]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Shiv Kumar Sharma = Santoor, NOT Sitar / NOT Pakhawaj; Sitar = Ravi Shankar, Anoushka Shankar,\nVilayat Khan; Pakhawaj = Totaram Sharma। [Q089, Q094, Q097]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Amjad Ali Khan = Sarod (\"Sarod Samrat\"), NOT Santoor; Santoor = Shiv Kumar Sharma, Bhajan Sopori,\nTarun Bhattacharya। [Q089, Q102]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mandolin = string instrument, NOT percussion; Carnatic percussion = Mridangam, Ghatam, Morsing,\nTabla। [Q082]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Khol = percussion (terracotta drum), NOT wind; Wind = Shehnai, Saxophone, Trumpet, Flute। [Q093]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Trumpet = wind (brass), NOT string; String = Cello, Violin, Bass, Mandolin, Guitar। [Q101]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kishori Amonkar = Hindustani (Jaipur Gharana), NOT Carnatic; Carnatic = M.S. Subbulakshmi, Priya"," Sisters, Bombay Jayashri। [Q085]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Alapana = Carnatic, NOT Hindustani; Hindustani = Dhrupad, Khayal, Tappa, Thumri, etc.। [Q091]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Veena = ancient Indian origin, NOT Indo-Islamic; Indo-Islamic = Rubab, Sarod, Sitar, Tabla, Sarangi।\n[Q092]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Nagada (North) → Chenda (South) counterpart; dono percussion hain। [Q095]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 4 Musical Instruments Full Mind Map (Q79-Q102)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0420","t":"05 Festivals","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FESTIVALS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. National Festivals of India\n2. Harvest / Agricultural Festivals — Pan India\n3. Hindu Religious Festivals\n4. Muslim Festivals\n5. Other Religions — Buddhist, Sikh, Jain, Parsi, Jewish, Christian\n6. North East India Festivals (Assam, Nagaland, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Sikkim, Arunachal, Tripura)\n7. South India Festivals (Kerala, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh & Telangana)\n8. East & Central India Festivals (Odisha, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Madhya Pradesh)\n9. West India Festivals (Goa, Rajasthan, Jaipur & UTs)\n10. New Year Celebrations Across States\n11. Cultural / Dance Festivals & Special Facts\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. National Festivals of India\n● Independence Day (15 August): National Flag Prime Minister dwara Red Fort (Old Delhi) mein hoist kiya jaata hai.\n[Q120]\n● Republic Day (26 January): National Flag President dwara Kartavya Path, New Delhi mein unfurl kiya jaata hai —\nIndependence Day se alag protocol. [Q120, Q148]\n● Beating the Retreat: Republic Day festivities ke end ko officially denote karta hai — 29 January ki shaam ko\nconduct hota hai (Republic Day ke teen din baad). [Q148]\n2. Harvest / Agricultural Festivals — Pan India\n● Makar Sankranti: January mein celebrate hota hai — Winter season ka end aur naye harvest season ki shuruaat,\nLord Surya ko dedicated. [Q111, Q121]\n● Pongal (Tamil Nadu): Dravidian harvest festival — Sun (Surya) worship kiya jaata hai; mid-January mein celebrate\nhota hai. [Q105, Q121, Q146]\n● Onam (Kerala): Malayalis dwara Chingam month mein celebrate — King Mahabali ko honour karne ke liye;\nSeptember mein aata hai (January mein NAHI). [Q110, Q146, Q155, Q166]\n● Wangala Festival (Meghalaya): Garo tribe ka harvest festival — Sun-God Saljong ke honour mein; \"100 drums\nfestival\" bhi kehte hain. [Q106]\n● Nuakhai (Odisha): Naye season ke rice ko welcome karne ke liye — Ganesh Chaturthi ke agle din celebrate hota\nhai. [Q106, Q142]\n● Tusu (Jharkhand): Winter harvest festival — Poush month ke last din; unmarried girls wooden/bamboo frame\ndecorate karke river mein float karti hain. [Q152]\n● Sarhul (Jharkhand): Oraon, Munda aur Ho tribes dwara celebrate; Sal tree ki health/prosperity ke liye worship;\nJharkhand mein New Year ki shuruaat bhi maana jaata hai. [Q141, Q175]\n● Konsachem Fest (Goa): Harvest thanksgiving ritual — Raia villagers August mein celebrate karte hain. [Q135]\n● Tarpa Festival (Dadra & Nagar Haveli): Varli, Kokna aur Koli tribes ka harvest dance. [Q187]\n●\n\n⚠️Deepawali harvest/agricultural festival NAHI hai — ye Lord Rama ki Ayodhya wapsi commemorate karta hai\n(Festival of Lights). Pongal, Baisakhi, Lohri sab harvest festivals hain. [Q147]"," 3. Hindu Religious Festivals\n● Dussehra (Vijayadashmi): Lord Rama ki 10-headed demon king Ravana par victory ka प्रतीक; Navratri ke end mein\ncelebrate hota hai. [Q127, Q156]\n● Chhath Puja: Lord Surya (Sun God) ko worship kiya jaata hai; Chhathi Maiya ki bhi puja hoti hai. [Q122]\n● Ram Navami: Lord Ram ke birthday ka celebration — Chaitra month ki Shukla Paksha ki ninth day (Chaitra\nNavratri) par; usually March/April mein aata hai. [Q158, Q163]\n● Dev Deepawali: Varanasi mein Ganga ghats par celebrate hota hai — Diwali ke 15 din baad, full moon day (Kartik\nPoornima) par. [Q140]\n● Durga Puja: December 2021 mein (16th session) UNESCO ki Representative List of Intangible Cultural Heritage of\nHumanity mein inscribe hui. [Q182]\n● Nabakalebara (Jagannath Temple, Odisha): Naye idols neem logs se banaye jaate hain aur Adhik Masa ke saal\nmein replace hote hain. [Q123]\n● Doljatra (Dol Purnima): West Bengal, Assam aur kuch states mein celebrate — March mein Holi ke saath coincide\nkarta hai; Krishna-Radha ko dedicated. [Q137]\n4. Muslim Festivals\n● Eid Al-Adha (Bakrid): Hajj pilgrimage rites ke culmination (Mina, Saudi Arabia near Mecca) ko mark karta hai;\nIslamic calendar ke 12th month (Dhu-al-Hijjah) ki 10th day par. [Q129]\n● Ramadan (Ramazan): Islamic calendar ka 9th month — fasting (dawn se sunset tak) ka mahina, Muslims\nworldwide observe karte hain. [Q131]\n● Muharram / Peerla Panduga: Telangana mein Hindus aur Muslims dono celebrate karte hain — locally \"Peerla\nPanduga\" ke naam se jaana jaata hai. [Q161]\n5. Other Religions — Buddhist, Sikh, Jain, Parsi, Jewish, Christian\n● Vesak (Buddha Purnima): Vaisakha month ki full-moon day par — April/May mein; Buddhism ka festival —\nBuddha ke birth, enlightenment aur Maha Parinirvana teeno ko mark karta hai (\"triple-blessed day\"), Vaishakha\nmonth se related. [Q132, Q154]\n● Hanukkah (Chanukah): Jewish \"Festival of Lights\" — 8-din ka wintertime festival. [Q133]\n● Gurpurab: Sikhism ka holiest festival — Guru Nanak Dev (Sikhism ke first Guru) ki birth anniversary commemorate\nkarta hai. [Q136]\n● Baisakhi: Guru Gobind Singh (Sikhs ke 10th aur last Guru) ne 1699 mein Khalsa Panth ki sthapna ki — Baisakhi is\nevent ko mark karta hai. [Q139]\n● Navroz / Nowruz: Parsi New Year — 21 March ko celebrate; Persian King Jamshed ki legend se connected; Parsi\nfire worshippers hain — Navroz par jalti hui fire ko water aur wheat se surround karte hain. [Q104, Q164]\n● Easter (Pascha/Resurrection Sunday): Christians ka festival — Jesus Christ ke resurrection (dead se wapas jeevit\nhone) ko mark karta hai. [Q160]\n● Gyana Panchami (Jains): Kartika month ki fifth day ke baad (Diwali ke 5 din baad) celebrate hoti hai — \"knowledge\nday\" jab holy scriptures display/worship kiye jaate hain. [Q179]\n6. North East India Festivals (Assam, Nagaland, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Sikkim,\nArunachal, Tripura)\n● Assam: Bihu — teen important Assamese festivals ka set; Bohag Bihu (Rongali Bihu) — 7-din ka festival, Assamese\nNew Year (14-15 April) aur Spring ki shuruaat mark karta hai; Magh Bihu = Makar Sankranti Assam mein (Bengali"," Panjika ke Magh month ke first din); Husori/Huchari — Bihu ka part, Cow Bihu (first din) par gaaya jaata hai.\n[Q117, Q126, Q159, Q162, Q172]\n● Nagaland: Hornbill Festival — Nagaland ke sabhi ethnic groups ko represent karta hai, \"Festival of Festivals\" bhi\nkehte hain, December ke first week mein; Sekrenyi — Angami tribe ka festival; Buhsu Jiba — Dimasa-Kachari tribe\nka thanksgiving harvest festival; Aoleang Monyu — Konyak tribe ka spring festival (April first week). [Q114, Q143,\nQ144, Q170, Q185]\n● Manipur: Lai Haraoba — traditional deities aur ancestors ki worship se associated; Sangai Festival — Manipur\nTourism Department, November mein, State animal \"Sangai\" (brow-antlered deer) ke naam par; Sengal Festival\nbhi Manipur ka annual cultural festival hai. [Q125, Q184, Q192]\n● Meghalaya: Wangala (Garo tribe); Shad Nongkrem — 5-din ka religious festival, November mein Smit (Khasi Hills\nka cultural centre) mein — Goddess 'Ka Blei Synshar' ko appease karne ke liye. [Q106, Q119]\n● Mizoram: Pawl Kut — Mizoram ka sabse bada festival, December/January mein bountiful harvest ke liye\nthanksgiving; Anthurium Festival — flower/horticulture promote karne ke liye, State Tourism Department\norganize karta hai. [Q165, Q174]\n● Sikkim: Saga Dawa — Buddhist festival, Tibetan Lunar month ki full moon par; Lhabab Dhuechen — Lord Buddha\nke heaven se earth par descent ko mark karta hai; Red Panda Winter Carnival — tourism promote karne ke liye\nDecember-January mein. [Q108, Q167, Q188]\n● Arunachal Pradesh: Chalo Loku — Nocte community, October-November; Dree Festival — Apatani tribe ka\nagricultural festival; Solung — Adi tribe ka festival, 1 September ko; Losar (Tibetan New Year) — Monpa tribe\ncelebrate karti hai. [Q103, Q138, Q150, Q171]\n● Tripura: Kharchi Pooja — 14 gods (Tripuri people ki dynasty deity) ki worship. [Q128]\n● Ladakh: Sindhu Darshan — June mein Guru Purnima ki full moon day par (Leh); Hemis Gompa Festival — Guru\nPadmasambhava ki birth anniversary celebrate karta hai (Tibetan Buddhism ke founding fathers mein se ek).\n[Q107, Q168]\n7. South India Festivals (Kerala, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh & Telangana)\n● Kerala: Nishagandhi Dance Festival (Trivandrum); Penkuni Festival — Sree Padmanabhaswamy Temple,\nMarch/April; Thrissur Pooram — Vadakkunnathan (Shiva) Temple; Annual Boat Race Festival — Onam ke\ndauraan; Puli Kali (Tiger Dance) — Onam ke 4th din ka main attraction. [Q109, Q124, Q145, Q155, Q166]\n● Tamil Nadu: Natyanjali Utsav — Mahashivratri par, Chidambaram temple, Lord Natraja ko dedicated, 5-din ka\nfestival; Jallikattu — traditional bull taming sport, Mattu Pongal ka part; Chitra Pournami — Poompuhar beach,\nTamil month chittrai ki full moon; Mamallapuram Utsav — 30-din ka festival (Dec-Jan), \"Indian Dance Festival\"\nhost karta hai. [Q112, Q178, Q189, Q190]\n● Karnataka: Kambala — annual buffalo race, Karnataka ke Southern districts mein, Lord Kadri Manjunatha ko\ndedicated; Purandaradasa Aradhana — classical music festival, Kannada saint Purandara Dasa (Carnatic Music ke\nfather) ki yaad mein, mainly Hampi mein. [Q153, Q193]\n● Andhra Pradesh & Telangana: Ugadi — Hindu lunar calendar ka New Year, Andhra Pradesh/Telangana/Karnataka\nmein; Bonalu — Goddess Mahakali ko dedicated, Ashada month (July/Aug) mein Telangana; Bathukamma —\nTelangana ka 9-din flowers festival, women celebrate karti hain. [Q180, Q151, Q191]\n8. East & Central India Festivals (Odisha, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Madhya Pradesh)\n● Odisha: Raja Parba (Mithuna Sankranti/Swing Festival) — 3-din ka womanhood festival, Majuli (Assam) mein NAHI\ncelebrate hota; Bali Yatra — Cuttack mein Kartik Purnima par, Odisha ki maritime history commemorate karta\nhai. [Q116, Q134, Q177]\n● Jharkhand: Sarhul — Oraon/Munda/Ho tribes, Spring (Phaagun) ki shuruaat; Tusu — winter harvest festival,\nunmarried girls celebrate karti hain. [Q141, Q152, Q175]\n● Madhya Pradesh: Lokrang Utsav — Gond tribe dwara 26 January ko 5 din tak celebrate hota hai. [Q157]"," 9. West India Festivals (Goa, Rajasthan, Jaipur & UTs)\n● Goa: Shigmotsav — Goa ka spring festival, traditional folk/street dancers aur floats ke saath; Konsachem Fest —\nRaia villagers ka harvest thanksgiving (August). [Q130, Q135]\n● Rajasthan: Maru Sri (Mr. Desert Pageant) — Jaisalmer Desert Festival mein men ke liye unique competition; Thar\nDesert mein February mein hota hai. [Q118]\n● Jaipur: Elephant Festival — Holi ke din annually celebrate hota hai. [Q186]\n● Punjab: Kila Raipur Sports Festival — Ludhiana ke paas, \"Rural Olympics\" ke naam se jaana jaata hai. [Q115]\n10. New Year Celebrations Across States\n● Navreh = Kashmiri Hindu New Year; Ugadi = Telugu New Year; Vishu = Malayali New Year; Pana Sankranti = Odia\nNew Year. [Q169]\n● Vishu = Kerala; Puthandu (Varusha Pirappu) = Tamil Nadu New Year (first day of Chithirai month); Gudi Padwa =\nMaharashtra (Chaitra month ka first day); Poila Boisakh = West Bengal. [Q173, Q176, Q183]\n11. Cultural / Dance Festivals & Special Facts\n● Taj Mahotsav: Shilpgram (Agra) mein 10-din ka classical dance, folk art aur light music festival — February-March\nmein; Taj Mahotsav Committee (Commissioner, Agra Division) organize karti hai. [Q113]\n● Cultural festivals — state matching: Hampi Dance Utsav (Karnataka), Mamallapuram Dance Utsav (Tamil Nadu),\nNishagandhi Festival (Kerala), Taj Mahotsav (Uttar Pradesh). [Q149]\n● Note: Mahabharata epic (Vyasa dwara likha gaya) ke 18 books mein se 6th book \"Bhishma Parva\" hai — jisme\nwidely-studied Bhagavad Gita shamil hai (ye trivia fact hai, festival nahi). [Q181]\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Onam January mein NAHI celebrate hota — ye September mein hota hai; Lohri, Bhogali Bihu, aur Pongal\nmid-January mein celebrate hote hain. [Q146]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Deepawali agricultural/harvest festival NAHI hai — ye Lord Rama ki Ayodhya wapsi commemorate karta\nhai; Pongal, Baisakhi, Lohri harvest festivals hain. [Q147]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Raja Parba (Odisha) Majuli (Assam) mein celebrate NAHI hota — ye do alag states hain. [Q116, Q177]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Navroz/Nowruz = Parsi New Year (Persian King Jamshed se related) — kisi aur religious community ka\nNAHI hai. [Q104, Q164]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Hornbill Festival = Nagaland ka unique festival, \"Festival of Festivals\" bhi kehte hain — December ke first\nweek mein. [Q114, Q185]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sengal Festival aur Sangai Festival dono Manipur ke cultural festivals hain — alag-alag naam se confuse\nmat karna. [Q184, Q192]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bihu = Assam; Onam = Kerala; Pongal = Tamil Nadu; Baisakhi = mainly Northern India (Punjab) — states\nmix mat karna. [Q117]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 5 Festivals Full Mind Map (Q103-Q193)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0421","t":"06 Fairs","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FAIRS (\n🏷️\nमेले) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Pushkar Fair (Rajasthan)\n2. Kumbh Mela\n3. West Bengal ke Fairs\n4. Surajkund Mela (Haryana)\n5. Jonbeel Mela (Assam)\n6. Key Differences & Quick Recap\n1. Pushkar Fair (Rajasthan)\n● Pushkar Fair ko Kartik Mela bhi kehte hain, ye Rajasthan ke Ajmer district ke Pushkar city mein lagta hai. [Q194]\n● Ye duniya ka sabse bada camel fair hai — saalana 7-din ka hota hai, October-November ke beech. Isliye isse\nPushkar Camel Fair bhi kehte hain. [Q200]\n● Ismein cultural events aur competitions hote hain jaise — dances, tug of war (men & women dono teams), matka\nphod, longest moustache competition, bridal competition, aur camel races. [Q194]\n2. Kumbh Mela\n● Kumbh Mela har 3 saal mein ek baar hota hai aur 4 alag-alag tirth sthalon ke beech ghumta hai — Prayag (Ganga-\nYamuna-Saraswati sangam), Ujjain (Kshipra), Nasik (Godavari), aur Haridwar (Ganga). [Q195]\n● Har ek location par ye mela 12 saal ke baad wapas aata hai. [Q195]\n3. West Bengal ke Fairs\n● Gangasagar Mela West Bengal ka sabse bada mela hai. Har saal Makar Sankranti (14/15 January) ko Gangasagar\npar Kapilmuni ke ashram mein lagta hai. [Q196]\n● Kenduli fair West Bengal ke Birbhum district ke Jaydev Kenduli village mein hota hai. Ye Baul community ka mela\nhai, Makar Sankranti ke mauke par 3 din chalta hai aur harvest season ki shuruaat ka prateek hai. [Q199]\n● WB ke aur famous mele: Rash Mela, Joydeb Kenduli Mela, Ramkeli Mela (Malda), aur Poush Mela. [Q196]\n4. Surajkund Mela (Haryana)\n● Surajkund Mela ko International crafts fair bhi kehte hain aur ye Haryana mein lagta hai. [Q197]\n● Ye duniya ka sabse bada crafts fair hai — India ke hastshilp, hathkargha aur saanskritik vividhta ko darshata hai.\n[Q197]\n● Iska aayojan Surajkund Mela Authority aur Haryana Tourism karte hain, Union Ministries of Tourism, Textiles,\nCulture aur External Affairs ke sahyog se. [Q197]\n5. Jonbeel Mela (Assam)"," ● Jonbeel Mela Assam mein lagta hai aur ye Bharat ka ekmatra mela hai jahan aaj bhi barter system (vastu vinimay\npranali) ka use hota hai. [Q198]\n● Ye 3-din ka utsav hai jo Tiwa community dwara aayojit kiya jata hai — ismein Tiwa, Karbi, Khasi aur Jaintia\nsamuday ke log hissa lete hain. [Q198]\n● Ye mela aamtor par Magh Bihu ke kuch dinon baad hota hai; Jonbeel jheel mein mauke par samaudayik machhli\npakadna bhi hota hai. [Q198]\n6. Key Differences & Quick Recap\n● Pushkar ek hi jagah hai jahan duniya ka sabse bada camel fair aur longest moustache competition dono hote hain.\n[Q194, Q200]\n● Jonbeel Mela unique hai kyunki ye Bharat ka ekmatra barter system wala mela hai. [Q198]\n● Surajkund = world's largest crafts fair; Pushkar = world's largest camel fair — dono alag hain! [Q197, Q200]\n● Gangasagar WB ka sabse bada mela hai, jabki Kenduli Baul community ka mela hai — dono Makar Sankranti par\nhote hain. [Q196, Q199]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 6 Fairs Full Mind Map (Q194-Q200)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0422","t":"07 Songs","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — SONGS (\n🏷️\nगीत) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indian Classical Music (Shastriya Sangeet)\n2. Regional Folk Songs (Kshetriya Lok Geet)\n3. Famous Songs & Their Writers (Prasiddh Geet evam Rachnakar)\n4. Key Differences & Quick Recap\n1. Indian Classical Music (Shastriya Sangeet)\n● Contemporary Carnatic music mein total 72 Melakarta ragas hote hain. Inhe do hisson mein divide kiya ja sakta\nhai: Suddha Madhyamam aur Prati Madhyama ragas. Ye music South India (Bharat ka dakshini bhag) se originate\nhua hai. [Q201]\n● Prayag Sangeet Samiti ko Prayagraj mein 1926 mein establish kiya gaya tha taaki Hindustani classical music\nsikhaya ja sake. Iska main aim — state governments, universities aur educational bodies dwara recognized vocal\naur instrumental music streams ka prachar karna hai. [Q202]\n● Dhrupad ek poetic form hai jo precise aur orderly elaboration of raga se marked hai. Traditionally ye purushon\ndwara perform kiya jata hai, jismein tanpura aur pakhawaj instrumental accompaniments hote hain. [Q204]\n● Sangeet Ratnakar (Ocean of Music and Dance) — music par sabse earliest known treatise — Sharangdev dwara\ncompose kiya gaya tha. Ye Yadava dynasty ke King Simhana (1210-1247) ke darbar ke part the. [Q205]\n● Tansen ne gyarah (11) saal tak Swami Haridas se music seekha. Akbar ne unhe Navaratnas mein shamil kiya aur\n'Mian' ki upadhi di. 'Tansen' upadhi unhe Gwalior ke Raja Vikramjit ne di thi. [Q206]\n2. Regional Folk Songs (Kshetriya Lok Geet)\n● Alha singing — North India mein prachalit ek folk song genre hai, khaaskar Uttar Pradesh mein. Ye Bundeli aur\nAwadhi ki important verse poem hai aur heroic rasa (veer rasa) communicate karne mein saksham hai. [Q203]\n● Bon-geet (forest/nature song) primarily Assam ka lok geet hai. Ismein 'Bon' ka matlab wilderness/jungle hai aur\n'geet' ka matlab songs. [Q207]\n● Saikuti zai — Mizoram ke regional folk songs hain jo Mizo ki sabse amir virasat represent karte hain. Saikuti ek\npoetess thi jinhonne warriors, brave hunters aur young men ki prashansa mein geet likhe. [Q208]\n● Kajari — Uttar Pradesh mein lokpriya ek semi-classical singing genre hai. Ye word Bhojpuri 'Kajra' (Kohl) se derive\nhua hai. Famous singer: Ajita Srivastava. [Q209]\n3. Famous Songs & Their Writers (Prasiddh Geet evam Rachnakar)\n● 'Ekla Chalo Re' (Walk alone) — Ravindranath Tagore dwara 1905 mein likha gaya tha. [Q210]\n● 'Vande Mataram' — Bankim Chandra Chatterjee (BC Chatterjee) dwara likha gaya tha, jo unke Bengali novel\n'Anandmath' se liya gaya hai. [Q210]\n● 'Sare Jahan Se Achcha' — Mohammed Iqbal (Allama Iqbal) dwara likha gaya tha. Ye British India ke prasiddh\nphilosopher, poet aur politician the, aur inhe Pakistan ka rashtriya kavi mana jata hai. [Q211]"," 4. Key Differences & Quick Recap\n● Carnatic = South India origin, 72 Melakarta ragas; Hindustani = Prayag Sangeet Samiti (Prayagraj, 1926) se\nseekhne ka system. [Q201, Q202]\n● Tansen ka title do logon se — Raja Vikramjit ne \"Tansen\" diya, Akbar ne \"Mian\" diya. [Q206]\n● UP ke do alag folk genres — Alha (Bundeli/Awadhi, veer rasa) aur Kajari (semi-classical, Bhojpuri origin). [Q203,\nQ209]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 7 Songs Full Mind Map (Q201-Q211)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0423","t":"08 Painting Dress Tribes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — PAINTING / DRESS / TRIBES — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indian Tribes — North-East & Andaman-Nicobar\n2. Indian Tribes — South & Other States\n3. Indian & World Tribes — Special Facts\n4. Indian Paintings — Folk & Classical\n5. Indian Paintings — Caves & Religious\n6. Traditional Dress, Weaves & Crafts\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Indian Tribes — North-East & Andaman-Nicobar\n● Meghalaya ki 3 pramukh janajatiyan: Garo (Garo hills), Khasi (East & West Khasi hills), aur Jaintia — Jaintia ek\njanajati ke saath-saath hill range ka bhi naam hai. [Q212]\n● Andaman Islands par 4 'Negrito' janajatiyan rehti hain: Great Andamanese, Onge, Jarawa, aur Sentinelese.\nNicobar Islands par 2 'Mongoloid' janajatiyan hain: Shompen aur Nicobarese. [Q213]\n● Mishing janajatiyan Majuli Island par rehti hain, jo Brahmaputra nadi (Assam) mein hai aur duniya ka sabse bada\nnadi dwip hai. [Q226]\n● Tai-Ahom samuday Assam mein rehta hai aur har saal 31 January ko 'Me-Dam-Me-Phi' festival manata hai — ye\npoorvajon ki pooja ka ek saamaudayik utsav hai. [Q225]\n2. Indian Tribes — South & Other States\n● Tamil Nadu ki Scheduled Tribes: Adiyan, Aranadan, Eravallan, Irular, Kadar, Kanikar, Kotas, Todas, Kurumba,\nMalasar. [Q214]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bhutia Tamil Nadu ki janajati nahi hai — ye Bhutan aur Sikkim mein rehta hai. [Q214]\n● Bhotiya mukhya roop se Uttarakhand mein paayi jaati hai (J&K, HP, UP, WB, Sikkim, AR mein bhi). Ye mool roop se\ncharwahon ki ek jaati hai. [Q222]\n3. Indian & World Tribes — Special Facts\n● Mongols — sabse prasiddh charwahi aur shikari-sangrahakarta janajatiyan jo Madhy Asia (Central Asia) mein\nnivas karti thi. Ye ghudsavari, teerandaji aur vijay ke liye prasiddh the. [Q228]\n● Masai ek Nilotic jaatiya samuh hai jo Kenya aur uttari Tanzania mein rehta hai. [Q230]\n● Maori janajati New Zealand se sambandhit hai. Duniya ki aur pramukh janajatiyan: Ghawazee (Egypt), Masai (East\n& Central Africa), Zulu (South Africa). [Q231]\n4. Indian Paintings — Folk & Classical\n● Warli chitrakala Maharashtra ki tribal art hai — Warli aur Malkhar koli janajatiyon ki mahilayein isse banati hain,\njo Mumbai ke uttari baahari ilake mein paayi jaati hain. [Q215]\n● Madhubani chitrakala Bihar aur Nepal ke Mithila kshetra mein prachalit hai. Tribal motifs aur chamkele mitti ke"," rangon ke kaaran lokpriya hai. [Q216]\n● Patna Kalam ek anoothi chitrakala shaili hai jo Persian school, Mughal kala aur British chitrakala se prabhavit hai.\nYe mukhya roop se daily life, aam purush-mahilaen aur karigaron ko darshati hai. [Q218]\n● Kolam — Tamil Nadu aur Kerala mein ghar ke saamne farsh sajaane ke liye Rangoli ki ek kala hai. [Q220]\n5. Indian Paintings — Caves & Religious\n● Mural (Bhitti chitra) — koi bhi kala ka tukda jo seedhe deewar ya sthaayi satahon par chitrit ya lagaya jata hai. Ye\nAjanta ki gufaen, Thiruvarur, Armamalai Cave aadi jagahon par paaye jaate hain. [Q217]\n● Ajanta Caves (Maharashtra) mein 29 gufaon ka samuh hai jismein Buddha ke pichhle janmon aur punarjanmon ke\nchitra hain — ye Aryasura ki Jatakamala (Jataka kathayein) se liye gaye hain. [Q221]\n● Thangka chitrakala (Sikkim, Tibet mein pramukh) mein Lord Buddha ya pauranik drishyon ke chitra suti ya reshami\nkapde par banaaye jaate hain. [Q224]\n6. Traditional Dress, Weaves & Crafts\n● Potloi — Manipur ki Meitei Hindu dulhano dwara pahni jaane wali bridal dress hai. Ye belanaakaar skirt hai jo\nmotte kapde se bani hoti hai aur sequins aur darpanon se sajai jaati hai. Manipuri Rasa Leela nritya ki nartakiyan\nbhi isse pehenti hain. [Q219]\n● Block Printing — Rajasthan ke Bagru jile se mool Chippa samuday pichhle teen shatabdiyon se iska paalan kar\nraha hai. Ye utkeern lakdi ke block ke madhyam se pattern print karne ki prakriya hai. [Q223]\n● Patola — Gujarat ki paaramparik bunai hai. Ye double-ikat resham ka kapda hai, jo paaramparik roop se Salvi\nsamuday dwara bunaa jaata hai. [Q227]\n● Phulkari — Punjab ki lok kadhai hai. Ismein rangeen reshami dhage se motte suti kapde ke pichhle hisse par darn\ntaanke ka upyog kiya jata hai. [Q229]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Bhutia = Sikkim/Bhutan; NOT Tamil Nadu. Tamil Nadu mein Kota, Malasar, Kurumba jaati hain. [Q214]\n● Ajanta = Jataka tales (Buddha ke pichhle janam); NOT Ramayana/Mahabharata/Vedas. [Q221]\n● Patna Kalam = chitrakala ki shaili (painting style); koi kalam, museum ya kaviyon ka samuh nahi. [Q218]\n● Patola = Gujarat; Phulkari = Punjab — dono alag-alag rajyon ki weaves hain. [Q227, Q229]\n● Majuli = world's largest river island (Brahmaputra, Assam); Lakshadweep/Andaman nahi. [Q226]\n● Masai = Kenya; Maori = New Zealand — dono alag-alag desh/dwipe ki janajatiyan hain. [Q230, Q231]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 8 Painting Dress Tribes Full Mind Map (Q212-Q231)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0424","t":"09 Languages","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — LANGUAGES (\n🏷️\nभाषाएँ) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Dravidian Language Family & South Indian Languages\n2. State Official Languages\n3. Regional & Tribal Languages\n4. Language Families & Classification\n5. Scripts & Writing Systems\n6. World Languages\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Dravidian Language Family & South Indian Languages\n● Tamil — Dravidian language family ki member hai, aur ye pehli aur sabse purani jivit Dravidian bhasha hai. [Q232]\n● 4 South Indian bhashaen aur unke rajya: Tamil = Tamil Nadu, Telugu = Andhra Pradesh, Kannada = Karnataka,\nMalayalam = Kerala. [Q232]\n● 2011 census ke hisaab se Telugu speakers ki sankhya ke hisaab se 4th rank par hai. Marathi (6.86%) = 3rd most\nspoken (Hindi aur Bengali ke baad). [Q234]\n● Telugu hi Andhra Pradesh ki official language hai. AP ka gathan 1 October 1953 ko linguistic basis par hua tha,\ncapital Kurnool thi. [Q239]\n2. State Official Languages\n● Kokborok ko 1979 mein Tripura ki official language ghoshit kiya gaya. [Q233]\n● Rajasthan ki official language Hindi hai. Doosre states: Arunachal Pradesh = English, Punjab = Punjabi, Goa =\nKonkani. [Q235]\n● Telangana mein Urdu = 2nd official language (1st = Telugu). Urdu = AP aur UP ki bhi 2nd official language hai.\n[Q237]\n● Hindi = Sanskrit ki vanshaj hai, aur ye Dravidian, Arabic, Portuguese, English, Persian aur Turkey ki bhashaon se\nprabhavit hai. Iski pramukh boliyan: Bagheli, Awadhi, Haryanvi, Braj Bhasha, Maithili, Marwari, Bhojpuri aadi.\n[Q238]\n3. Regional & Tribal Languages\n● Kangri bhasha mukhya roop se Himachal Pradesh mein boli jati hai. Ye Dogri aur Punjabi ka mishran hai — Kangra,\nUna aur Hamirpur ke kuchh hisson mein boli jati hai. [Q236]\n● Ao bhasha — Nagaland mein pramukh bhasha. Ao / Central Naga languages = Sino-Tibetan parivar ki chhoti\nfamily. Aur bhashaen: Chokri, Khezha, Chang, Zeme, Yachumi. [Q240]\n● Brajawali — ek sahityik bhasha thi jo Sankardev ne Bhaona (Assam ka paaramparik kala roop) aur unki rachnaon\n(Borgeet, Ankia Naat) ke liye use ki. [Q241]\n● Kolhati bhasha — Maharashtra (Pune district) mein boli jati hai. Kolhati ko Maharashtra sarkar ne khanabadosh\njanajati ke roop mein vargikrit kiya hai. [Q246]\n● Urdu ko Lashkari Zaban bhi kehte hain. Ye ek Indo-Aryan bhasha hai jo mukhya roop se South Asia mein boli jati\nhai. Ye Pakistan ki rashtriya bhasha aur Bharat mein scheduled official bhasha hai. [Q247]"," 4. Language Families & Classification\n● Sino-Tibetan = duniya ka 2nd largest language family. Ismein Chinese aur Tibeto-Burman dono bhashaen hain.\n[Q243]\n● Indo-European = sabse bada (largest) language family hai. [Q243]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Finno-Ugric = Indo-European family se sambandhit NAHI hai. Indo-European ki shakhaen hain: Albanian,\nArmenian, Balto-Slavic, Celtic, Germanic, Hellenic, Indo-Iranian, Italic. [Q244]\n5. Scripts & Writing Systems\n● Bharati script — IIT Madras mein Srinivasa Chakravarthy ki team dwara viksit. Ye 'One Nation, One Script' ke\nanurup hai. Ismein 9 bhashaen support hoti hain: Hindi/Marathi (Devanagari), Tamil, Telugu, Gujarati, Punjabi\n(Gurmukhi), Bengali, Oriya, Kannada, Malayalam. [Q245]\n6. World Languages\n● Sinhala = Sri Lanka ki pramukh bhasha. Ye dakshini, pashchimi aur madhya bhagon mein boli jati hai, jabki Tamil =\nuttari aur poorvi bhagon mein. [Q242]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Finno-Ugric = Indo-European family ka hissa NAHI hai. Ye alag family hai. [Q244]\n● Sino-Tibetan = 2nd largest; Indo-European = largest — confuse mat hona! [Q243]\n● Urdu = Lashkari Zaban bhi kehlate hain, sirf Muslim community ki bhasha nahi — ye Pakistan ki rashtriya bhasha\nhai. [Q247]\n● Telugu = 4th most spoken; Marathi = 3rd most spoken (Hindi, Bengali ke baad). [Q234]\n● Brajawali = Assam ki literary language (Sankardev); Braj Bhasha = Hindi ki ek bolii — dono alag hain! [Q241, Q238]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 9 Languages Full Mind Map (Q232-Q247)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0425","t":"10 First in India World","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FIRST IN INDIA / WORLD — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Technology, Science & Infrastructure\n2. Transport, Energy & Communication\n3. Defence, Atomic Energy & Space\n4. Finance, Economy & Trade\n5. Governance, Administration, Law & Elections\n6. Sports, Olympics & Adventure\n7. Literature, Culture, Media & Religion\n8. Education & Institutions\n9. World / International Firsts\n10. Medical, Health & Social\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Technology, Science & Infrastructure\n● Maruti 800 ke liye Bharat Sarkar aur Suzuki Motor Corporation ke beech joint venture 1982 mein sign hua; Maruti\nUdyog Limited ki sthapna Feb 1981 mein hui. [Q248]\n● Omicron variant test karne ke liye CSIR-Central Drug Research Institute dwara viksit pehli swadeshi RT-PCR kit ka\nnaam INDICoV-Om hai — isse patient ko pata chalta hai ki infection Omicron hai ya Delta. [Q251]\n● NESTLE India Ltd. ka pehla factory 1961 mein Punjab (Moga) mein set up hua; doosra plant 1967 mein Tamil Nadu\n(Choladi) mein. [Q252]\n● Bharat ka pehla Green Hydrogen Microgrid Project Andhra Pradesh mein shuru hua (NTPC Simhadri plant). [Q253]\n● Bharat ka pehla e-waste clinic Bhopal mein sthapit kiya gaya. [Q256]\n● Bharat ka pehla Graphene Innovations Centre Kerala mein hai — Graphene ek-atom-moti carbon layer hai jo\nGraphite ka building-block hai. [Q257]\n● IIT Hyderabad ne corneal transplantation ka pehla vikalp (alternative) India mein shuru kiya. [Q262]\n● Agro-waste se bane biobricks se bani Bharat ki pehli imarat ka udghatan IIT-Hyderabad (2021) mein hua — ye\nexcellent thermal insulation aur fire-retardant properties rakhti hai. [Q266]\n● Indian Army dwara Vanadium-based battery technology use karne wala pehla Green Solar Energy Harnessing\nPlant ki capacity 56 KVA hai — ise North Sikkim mein 16000 ft ki oonchai par IIT Mumbai ke sahyog se shuru kiya\ngaya. [Q267]\n● Bharat ka pehla bio-refinery plant Pune mein Nitin Gadkari dwara udghatit kiya gaya — ye biomass se ethanol\nproduce karti hai. [Q290]\n● Artificial fertilizers pehli baar 19th century mein banaye gaye; ye chemical processes dwara petroleum ya natural\ngas se manufacture hote hain. [Q276]\n● Bharat ka pehla Genetic Bank for Wildlife Conservation = Hyderabad mein CCMB-LaCONES facility mein. [Q323]\n● Bharat ka pehla Digital University = Kerala mein udghatit. [Q332]\n● Independent India ka pehla river dam = Tilaiya Dam (Damodar Valley Project) — Barakar river (Damodar ki\ntributary) par, Jharkhand mein; construction 1948 mein shuru, 1953 mein complete hua. [Q291]\n● Asia ka pehla beach jisse Blue Flag Certification mila = Chandrabhaga beach (Odisha) — ye internationally\nrecognised eco-label 33 criteria ke aadhar par diya jaata hai. [Q304]"," 2. Transport, Energy & Communication\n● Bharat ki pehli semi high-speed train Vande Bharat Express (pehle Train 18) New Delhi aur Varanasi Junction ke\nbeech chalti hai — ye India ki pehli engineless train hai. [Q272]\n● Bharat ki pehli Superfast train = Deccan Queen (1 June 1930 ko introduce hui) — ye pehli long-distance electric-\nhauled train bhi thi. [Q273]\n● Bharat mein pehli underground metro train Kolkata mein 24 Oct 1984 ko shuru hui (Bhawanipur/Netaji Bhawan\nse Esplanade); is project ki foundation PM Indira Gandhi ne rakhi thi. [Q283]\n● Delhi Metro ke pehle corridor (Red Line, Shahdara se Tis Hazari) ka udghatan Atal Bihari Vajpayee ne 24 Dec 2002\nko kiya. [Q277]\n● Pehla radio programme Bharat mein 1923 mein prasarit kiya gaya — shuruaat Radio Club of Bombay se hui.\n[Q280]\n● Seaplane service operate karne wala pehla island = Andaman and Nicobar (Jal Hans, 30 Dec 2010, Port Blair se\nHavelock). [Q275]\n● Bharat ki pehli biofuel-powered flight 2018 mein Dehradun se IGI Delhi aayi (SpiceJet, Bombardier Q400) —\nismein 75% ATF + 25% Jatropha oil ka mix use hua. [Q288]\n● Cochin International Airport = duniya ka pehla fully solar-powered airport (Kerala ka sabse bada/vyast airport).\nPuducherry Airport = AAI ka pehla entirely solar-powered airport. [Q284]\n● Duniya ka pehla official airmail Feb 1911 mein Allahabad se Naini bheja gaya — French pilot Henri Peque ne is\ncommercial flight ko operate kiya. [Q294]\n● Bharat ki pehli electric train = 3 February 1925 ko Bombay VT se Kurla Harbour tak Ex-GIP Railway System par.\n[Q335]\n● Kacheguda railway station = Bharat ka pehla energy-efficient 'A1 Category' station (Telangana, SCR zone). Isne\n1,312 conventional lights ko LED se replace karke yeh uplabdhi hasil ki. [Q351]\n● Bharat ki pehli solar-powered train (DEMU) July 2017 mein Delhi ke Safdarjung station se Farukh Nagar (Haryana)\nke beech shuru hui — 6 trailer coaches, har ek mein 16 solar panels. [Q307]\n● JRD Tata — \"Father of Indian Civil Aviation\", ne 1932 mein Bharat ki pehli private commercial airline sthapit ki. 15\nOctober 1932 ko unhone Karachi se Bombay pehli commercial solo flight bharli. [Q317]\n● Internet par uplabdh hone wala pehla Bharatiya samachar patra = The Hindu (1995). Duniya ka pehla online\nnewspaper = The Columbus Dispatch (1980). [Q328]\n● Independent India ka pehla oil-field discover hua tha Assam mein (Digboi, 1867 mein hi overall pehla, refinery\n1901 mein Assam Oil Company Ltd ne sthapit ki); independence ke baad major discovery Naharkatiya (Assam)\nmein 1953 mein hui. [Q255]\n● Bharat ka pehla CNG Tractor — Union road transport & highways minister Nitin Gadkari ne launch kiya, apna\ndiesel tractor CNG variant mein convert karwa ke. [Q329]\n3. Defence, Atomic Energy & Space\n● Bharat sarkar ne Pokhran mein apna pehla nuclear test 1974 mein kiya (Operation Smiling Buddha) — ye UNSC ke\n5 permanent members ke bahar kisi bhi desh dwara pehla confirmed nuclear weapons test tha. [Q250]\n● Bharat ka pehla swadeshi aircraft carrier = INS Vikrant, ise 2 Sept 2022 ko Cochin Shipyard Limited (CSL) mein\nlaunch kiya gaya. [Q258]\n● Bharat ka pehla niji taur par viksit fully cryogenic rocket engine = Dhawan-1 — ise Skyroot Aerospace ne viksit\nkiya. [Q259]\n● 1964 mein Bharat ka pehla Pressurised Heavy Water Reactor (PHWR) Canada ke sahyog se banaya gaya —\nRajasthan Atomic Power Station (RAPS-1). [Q286]\n● Bharat ka pehla swadeshi warship = INS Godavari (F20) — guided-missile frigate, Mazagon Dock Mumbai mein\nbana, 1983 mein commissioned. [Q308]\n● Antariksh mein jane wale pehle Bharatiya = Rakesh Sharma (poorv IAF pilot), 3 April 1984 ko Soyuz T-11 mein"," Soviet Intercosmos program ke tahat. [Q301]\n● Antariksh mein udhan bharne wale duniya ke pehle vyakti = Yuri Gagarin (Russian cosmonaut), 1961 mein Vostok\n1 mein 108-minute ki yatra. Pehli mahila = Valentina Tereshkova (Russia, 16 June 1963). [Q302]\n● Indian Army ki pehli mahila jawan = Sapper Shanti Tigga (unhone 2011 mein Territorial Army ki 969 Railway\nEngineer Regiment join ki). [Q293]\n4. Finance, Economy & Trade\n● Asia ka pehla stock exchange = Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE), 9 July 1875 ko Dalal Street, Mumbai mein sthapit\nhua. 1956 mein ye Bharat Sarkar dwara manyataprapt pehla stock exchange bhi bana. [Q299]\n● Duniya ka pehla desh jo GST apni pranali mein laya = France (1954). Bharat mein GST 1 July 2017 ko 101st\nConstitutional Amendment Act ke madhyam se laya gaya. [Q350]\n● GI tag ke tahat pehla tagged Indian item = Darjeeling tea. GI tags 15 September 2003 se TRIPS agreement ke tahat\nBharat mein laagu huye. [Q322]\n● Bharat ki pehli successful cotton mill = Bombay Spinning Mill and Weaving Company, 1854 mein Tardeo, Mumbai\nmein Cowasji Nanabhai Davar dwara sthapit. [Q306]\n● RBI ke pehle Bharatiya Governor (swatantrata ke baad) = C.D. Deshmukh. Overall pehle Governor = Sir Osborne\nSmith. RBI ki sthapna 1 April 1935 ko hui. [Q303]\n5. Governance, Administration, Law & Elections\n● Lok Sabha ki pehli mahila Speaker = Meira Kumar; pehle Speaker overall = Ganesh Vasudev Mavalankar. [Q282]\n● Indian Civil Service (ICS) mein shamil hone wale pehle Bharatiya = Satyendranath Tagore (1863), jo Brahmo Samaj\nke member the. Charles Cornwallis ko \"Bharat mein civil service ke janak\" kaha jata hai. [Q296]\n● EVMs ka pehli baar istemal 1982 mein Kerala ke North Paravur Assembly Constituency ke by-election mein kiya\ngaya. VVPAT ka pehla istemal Sept 2013 mein Noksen (Nagaland) mein hua. [Q295]\n● Maulana Azad National Urdu University (MANUU) ke pratham Vice Chancellor = Prof. Mohammed Shamim\nJairajpuri; MANUU ek Central University hai jo 1998 mein Hyderabad (Gachibowli) mein sthapit hui. [Q263]\n● Bharat ki pehli full-time mahila Raksha Mantri aur mahila Vitt Mantri = Nirmala Sitharaman. [Q324]\n● Supreme Court ki pehli mahila judge = Fathima Beevi. Bharat ki pehli mahila judge overall = Justice Anna Chandy\n(Kerala High Court). [Q312]\n● UN General Assembly ki pehli mahila President = Vijaya Lakshmi Pandit. [Q337]\n● Bharat ke CM ne pehli baar 15 August 1974 ko rashtriya dhvaj faharaya — pehle 1973 tak yeh adhikar nahi tha;\nM. Karunanidhi ne campaign chalakar yeh adhikar hasil kiya. [Q313]\n● Bharat ki pehli Republic Day parade (1950) ke Guest of Honour = Indonesia ke President Ahmed Sukarno. [Q334]\n6. Sports, Olympics & Adventure\n● Bharat ki pehli para-badminton academy Uttar Pradesh (Lucknow) mein shuru ki gayi. [Q249]\n● Bharat ne pehli baar Thomas Cup (men's badminton) 2022 mein jeeta — final mein Indonesia ko haraaya. [Q261]\n● Bharat ne pehli baar Olympic Games mein 1900 mein hissa liya — athlete Norman Pritchard ne athletics mein do\nsilver medals jeete. [Q274]\n● Paralympics mein medal jeetne wali pehli Bharatiya mahila para-athlete = Deepa Malik (shot put silver, Rio 2016);\n2020 mein wo Paralympic Committee of India ki President bani. [Q279]\n● English Channel tairkar paar karne wali pehli mahila = ek American (Gertrude Ederle); pehli Asian mahila = Arati"," Saha. [Q278]\n● South Pole par pahunchne wali pehli mahila IPS officer = Aparna Kumar (2002-batch UP cadre). Pehla vyakti =\nRoald Amundsen; pehla Bharatiya = Colonel J.K. Bajaj; pehli woman IPS India mein = Kiran Bedi. [Q298]\n● Laurel Hubbard (New Zealand) = Summer Olympics (Tokyo 2020) mein individual event mein pratispardha karne\nwali pehli openly transgender athlete (women's 87+ kg weightlifting). [Q270]\n● Paralympics mein do swarn padak jeetne wale pehle Bharatiya = Devendra Jhajharia (javelin throw) — Athens\n2004 aur Rio 2016; Tokyo 2020 mein silver bhi. [Q311]\n● Paralympics mein swarn padak jeetne wale pehle Bharatiya (historically) = Murlikant Petkar (1972); options ke\nhisaab se Mariyappan Thangavelu (high jump, Rio 2016). [Q348]\n● IAAF World Championships mein padak jeetne wali pehli Bharatiya = Anju Bobby George — 2003 Paris mein long\njump mein bronze (6.70m). [Q316]\n● Olympic athletics final mein pahunchne wale pehle Bharatiya purush athlete = Milkha Singh (Flying Sikh) — 400m\nmein. [Q345]\n● English Channel tairkar paar karne wale pehle Asian = Mihir Sen; pehli Asian mahila = Arati Saha. Mihir Sen ne\n1966 mein 5 mahadvipon ke mahasagaron ko tairkar paar kiya. [Q344]\n● Antarrashtriya film puraskar paane wali pehli Bharatiya abhinetri = Suchitra Sen — 1963 Moscow International\nFilm Festival mein 'Saat Paake Bandha' ke liye Best Actress ka Silver Prize. [Q330]\n● Bharatiya cricket team mein niyukt pehle videshi coach = John Wright (poorv New Zealand captain), 2000 mein;\nunhe 2005 mein Greg Chappell ne replace kiya. [Q339]\n● Test match mein Bharat ke liye shatak banane wale pehle cricketer = Lala Amarnath. Pehla ODI shatak = Kapil Dev,\npehla T20I shatak = Suresh Raina, pehla IPL shatak = Manish Pandey. [Q343]\n● Bharatiya Test team ke pehle captain = C.K. Nayudu — 1932 mein England mein debut. [Q346]\n● Bharat mein pehla Test match = 1933 mein Bombay Gymkhana mein India vs England. [Q336]\n● Arjuna Puraskar paane wale pehle Bharatiya footballer = P.K. Bannerjee. Arjuna Award ki sthapna 1961 mein hui\n— ye Bharat ka dusra sabse bada sporting honour hai. [Q342]\n● Pehle Commonwealth Games = 1930 mein Hamilton (Canada) mein. Bharat ne pehli baar 1934 (2nd CWG) mein\nhissa liya. [Q341]\n7. Literature, Culture, Media & Religion\n● Sahitya mein Nobel Prize paane wale pehle Bharatiya nagrik = Rabindranath Tagore (1913). [Q254]\n● Marathi mein Bhagwad Gita ki pehli vistaarit commentary = Dnyaneshwar ne likhi (Dnyaneshwari, 13th century).\n[Q269]\n● Jnanpith Award ke pratham vijeta = G. Sankara Kurup (Malayalam kavi, 1965, unki rachna \"Odakkuzhal\" ke liye).\nJnanpith = Bharat ka sabse purana aur sarvochch sahityik puraskar. [Q297]\n● Bharat ki pehli masjid = Cheraman Juma Mosque (629 AD, Thrissur district, Kerala). [Q260]\n● Calcutta Cricket Club ki sthapna 1792 mein hui — ye duniya ka dusra sabse purana cricket club hai (MCC 1787 ke\nbaad). Parsi samuday dwara sthapit pehla Bharatiya cricket club = Oriental Cricket Club (1848, Mumbai). [Q285]\n● Duniya ki pehli handwritten needle book = Madhushala — Harivansh Rai Bachchan dwara likhi gayi. [Q310]\n● Bhagavad Gita ka English mein sabse pehla anuvad = Charles Wilkins dwara kiya gaya. Gita mein 18 adhyay, 700\nshlok, 1400 panktiyan hain — likhak Maharishi Ved Vyas. [Q318]\n● Library of Congress (Washington DC) mein apni kavitayen record karne wale pehle Bharatiya kavi = Abhay K.\n[Q321]\n● Bharat ka pehla samachar patra = \"The Bengal Gazette\" (Hicky's Bengal Gazette), James A Hickey dwara 29\nJanuary 1780 ko Calcutta mein prakashit. [Q327]\n● Bharat ki pehli bolti film (talkie) = Alam Ara (1931) — Ardeshir Irani dwara directed/produced. Raja Harishchandra\n(1913) = pehli full-length silent feature film. [Q325]\n● Pehli World's Parliament of Religions = 1893 mein Chicago (USA) mein — Swami Vivekananda ne yahan Bharat ki"," prachin sanskriti ko vishwa-pat par rakha. [Q349]\n● Bharat ka pehla costume museum = Moda Goa Museum and Research Centre, Goa mein — Wendell Rodricks\ndwara design kiya gaya. [Q319]\n● Bharat ka pehla Spice Museum = Kochi (Kerala) mein Willingdon Island par — Spices Board (1987) dwara sthapit.\n[Q340]\n8. Education & Institutions\n● IIT Kharagpur = pehla IIT (1951 mein Maulana Abul Kalam Azad dwara udghatan). [Q314]\n● IISc Bangalore ke pehle Bharatiya Director = C.V. Raman (1930 mein Physics ka Nobel Prize — Raman effect ki khoj\nke liye). [Q333]\n● Bharat ka pehla Railway University = National Rail and Transportation Institute (ab Gati Shakti Vishwavidyalaya),\nVadodara (Gujarat). 2018 mein sthapit, August 2022 mein Central University bana. [Q309]\n● Aur pehle universities: Railway = Gati Shakti Vishwavidyalaya (Gujarat), Sport = National Sports University\n(Manipur). [Q332]\n● Pehla botanist = Theophrastus (Father of Botany) — unhone \"Historia Plantarum\" mein lagbhag 500 paudhon ka\nvarnan kiya. [Q347]\n● Astronomical Society of India (1972 mein sthapit) ki pehli mahila President = Dr. GC Anupama — ye Bharat ke\nprofessional astronomers ki prime association hai. [Q315]\n9. World / International Firsts\n● Dubai ki sarkar 100% paperless hone wali duniya ki pehli sarkar bani — ghoshna UAE Crown Prince ne ki. [Q268]\n● El Salvador = Bitcoin ko kanooni mudra ke roop mein svikar karne wala duniya ka pehla desh. [Q271]\n● Kisi desh ka purna nagrik banne wala duniya ka pehla robot = Sophia (Saudi Arabia) — ise Hanson Robotics (Hong\nKong) ne viksit kiya. [Q281]\n● UN ke pehle Mahasachiv = Trygve Lie (Norway, 1946-1953). [Q287]\n● African mahadvip se pehle Mahasachiv = Boutros Boutros-Ghali (Egypt, 6th SG). [Q320, Q331]\n● Sabse purana inter-governmental organization = Central Commission for Navigation on the Rhine (1815 mein\nsthapit), HQ Strasbourg (France). [Q289]\n● World Happiness Report pehli baar 2012 mein prakashit hui — har saal 20 March (International Day of Happiness)\nke aaspaas UN dwara jari ki jati hai. [Q300]\n● Duniya ka pehla TV channel dedicated to human rights = London (UK) mein January 2019 mein launch hua —\nInternational Observatory of Human Rights (IOHR) ke tahat. [Q326]\n10. Medical, Health & Social\n● Bharat ka pehla amputee clinic Chandigarh mein PGIMER dwara shuru kiya gaya — amputation patients ko social,\nmental aur physical support deta hai. [Q264]\n● Pehle 'open Rock Museum' ka udghatan Hyderabad mein 6 January 2021 ko hua. [Q265]\n● Bharat ka pehla floating elementary school Loktak Lake, Manipur mein udghatit kiya gaya — ye desh ki sabse badi\nfreshwater lakes mein se ek hai. Keibul Lamjao National Park = duniya ka ekmatra floating national park. [Q292]\n● Duniya ka pehla malaria vaccine = RTS,S / Mosquirix, GSK (GlaxoSmithKline) dwara 1987 mein viksit. Malawi isse\nlaunch karne wala pehla desh bana. [Q305]\n● 'Raksha Blue' = Blue tongue disease ka pehla vaccine (Indian Immunological Limited dwara). Ye penta-valent"," vaccine hai jo 5 virus strains se suraksha deti hai. [Q338]\n11.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Rakesh Sharma = pehle Bharatiya in space; Yuri Gagarin = pehle human in space overall; Neil Armstrong\n= pehle man on moon — teeno alag! [Q301, Q302]\n● BSE = Asia's first stock exchange (1875); NSE baad mein aaya — confuse mat hona. [Q299]\n● Madhushala = world's first handwritten needle book; Devdas/Moti Mahal nahi. [Q310]\n● C.V. Raman = IISc ke pehle Bharatiya Director; Morris Travers = founding director (British) — alag hain. [Q333]\n● Mariyappan Thangavelu = Paralympic gold (options ke hisaab se); lekin historically Murlikant Petkar (1972) =\npehla Paralympic gold — dono yaad rakhna. [Q348]\n● Alam Ara (1931) = pehli bolti film; Raja Harishchandra (1913) = pehli silent film — confuse mat hona! [Q325]\n● Kacheguda = Telangana mein hai, Andhra Pradesh nahi. [Q351]\n● Trygve Lie = UN ka pehla SG; Boutros Boutros-Ghali = Africa se pehla SG. [Q287, Q320]\n● Cheraman Juma Mosque = Bharat ki pehli masjid (629 AD, Kerala). [Q260]\n● Pokhran 1974 = Operation Smiling Buddha = pehla nuclear test; ye UNSC P5 ke bahar pehla confirmed test tha.\n[Q250]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 10 First in India World Full Mind Map (Q248-Q351)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0426","t":"11 Sports","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — SPORTS (\n🏷️\nखेल) — FULL MIND MAP\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Cricket – India & World Records\n2. Tennis, Hockey & Football\n3. Olympics, Asian Games & Awards\n4. Combat Sports, Gymnastics & Volleyball\n5. Sports Origins, Stadiums & Terminology\n6. Indian Athletes & Their Records\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Cricket – India & World Records\n● India ICC Men's ODI World Cup ke final mein 3 baar pahunchi hai — 1983 aur 2011 mein jeeta, 2003 mein runner-\nup rahi. [Q356]\n● 1987 Cricket World Cup mein pehli baar 60 se 50 overs kar diye gaye; ye India-Pakistan ne milke host kiya tha.\n[Q361]\n● Sachin Tendulkar ne apna 100th international century Bangladesh ke khilaf banaya — ye pehle aur ekmatre\ncricketer hain jinke 100 international centuries hain. [Q364]\n● Kapil Dev captain the jab India ne 1983 mein West Indies ko haraakar World Cup jeeta. [Q367]\n● Sachin Tendulkar = 6th Indian jo ICC Cricket Hall of Fame (2019) mein shamil hue. Aur Indians: Bishan Singh Bedi\n(2009), Kapil Dev (2009), Sunil Gavaskar (2009), Anil Kumble (2015), Rahul Dravid (2018), Vinoo Mankad (2021).\n[Q374]\n● Chris Gayle = pehla player jo international cricket mein 500 sixes laga chuka hai. [Q375]\n● Kieron Pollard = 3rd cricketer jo ek over mein 6 sixes laga sake; Herschelle Gibbs pehle, Yuvraj Singh doosre the.\n[Q377]\n● Mohammad Azharuddin ne apne pehle 3 test matches mein lagatar 3 shatak banaye. [Q378]\n● Rohit Sharma = pehla batsman jisne 3 ODI double centuries banaye; unka 264 sabse zyada ODI score hai. [Q379]\n● Silly point, slip, gully ye sab cricket ke fielding positions hain. [Q380]\n● 3rd umpire replay ke aadhar par dismissal ka faisla karta hai. [Q391]\n● Ranjit Singh ko \"Father of Indian Cricket\" kaha jata hai; Ranji Trophy unhi ke naam par hai. [Q411]\n● Chinaman bowling style ka naam Ellis Achong (Chinese origin ke West Indian bowler) ke naam par rakha gaya.\n[Q373]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Kumar Sangakkara = MCC ke pehle non-British President (Oct 2019 – Sept 2020); Sri Lanka ke poorv\ncaptain. [Q382]\n2. Tennis, Hockey & Football\n● Roger Federer = Swiss tennis player; record 8 Wimbledon titles aur 5 consecutive US Open titles. [Q357]\n● Roland Garros (French Open) = clay court par hota hai; US Open & Australian Open = hard court; Wimbledon =\ngrass court. [Q359]\n● CR7 = Cristiano Ronaldo ka nickname hai; ye Portuguese footballer hain. [Q372]\n● Rangaswamy Cup = National Hockey Championship; Irani Cup = Cricket; Davis Cup = Lawn Tennis; Subroto Cup =\nFootball. [Q362]"," ● Pakistan ka rashtriya khel field hockey hai; Nepal = Volleyball; Bangladesh = Kabaddi. [Q368]\n● Beighton Cup = Bharat ka sabse purana hockey tournament (1895, Kolkata); Durand Cup = Football se juda hai.\n[Q387]\n● Dabang Mumbai, Kalinga Lancers, Ranchi Rays, Delhi Waveriders ye sab Hockey India League (HIL, 2013) mein\nkhelte hain. [Q420]\n● Brazil ne har FIFA Football World Cup mein hissa liya hai shuruaat se; inke naam 5 World Cup wins ka record hai.\n[Q369]\n● Chelsea ek English Football club hai. [Q371]\n● Indian Football Association (IFA) ki sthapna 1893 mein Kolkata mein hui — ye Bharat ka sabse purana football\nassociation hai. [Q406]\n● Sudirman Cup = Badminton se related hai (mixed team event); Uber Cup aur Thomas Cup bhi Badminton ke\nfamous cups hain. [Q413]\n3. Olympics, Asian Games & Awards\n● Baichung Bhutia ne Beijing Olympics 2008 ke torch relay mein hissa lene se inkar kiya tha taaki Tibetan\nIndependence Movement ka samarthan kar sakein. [Q358]\n● Asian Games India mein 2 baar hue hain — 1951 aur 1982; pehli baar 1951 mein New Delhi mein. [Q370]\n● Kabaddi ko pehli baar 1990 Asian Games (Beijing) mein shamil kiya gaya; India men's team ne 1990 se 2014 tak\nhar Asian Games Kabaddi event mein gold jeeta. [Q383]\n● Olympic flag mein 5 interlinked rings = 5 continents ko represent karte hain; colors: Blue, Yellow, Black, Green,\nRed. [Q388]\n● Table tennis ko Olympic recognition 1988 (Seoul) mein mili. [Q398]\n● Special Olympics mein hissa lene ki minimum age = 8 years — ye intellectual disabilities wale bachchon aur adults\nka sabse bada sports organization hai. [Q415]\n● \"Play the game, in spirit of the game\" = First Asian Games (1951, New Delhi) ka motto tha. [Q417]\n● Arjuna Award (1961) = Government of India dwara outstanding achievement in Sports ke liye diya jata hai. [Q418]\n● MAKA Trophy (Maulana Abul Kalam Azad Trophy) = 1956-57 mein sthapit; top performing Indian University in\nsports ko milti hai. [Q360]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cricket = cash awards scheme mein shamil NAHI hai; eligible sports hain: Olympics/Asian\nGames/Commonwealth Games, Chess, Billiards & Snooker, Blind Cricket World Cup. [Q352]\n4. Combat Sports, Gymnastics & Volleyball\n● Skiing = winter sport hai, combat competition nahi; Judo, Kung-Fu, Kalaripayattu sab martial arts/combat sports\nhain. [Q407]\n● Roman Ring = Gymnastics se related hai; Judo se nahi. Judo ke scoring terms: Ippon, Yuko, Waza-ari. [Q408]\n● Par Terre = Wrestling (Greco-Roman) mein use hone wali position hai jahan ek pehlwan ko ground position mein\njaane ka aadesh diya jata hai. [Q412]\n● FILA = pehle Wrestling ka international governing body tha, ab iska naam United World Wrestling (UWW) hai.\n[Q395]\n● Raider = Kabaddi mein wo player jo opponent ke half mein jaakar tag karta hai. [Q394]\n● AKFI (Amateur Kabaddi Federation of India) = 1973 mein sthapit, headquarters Jaipur mein — Kabaddi se related\ngoverning body hai; FIFA = Football, BCCI = Cricket, AIKF = Karate se related hain. [Q392]\n● Frederick Ludwig John (Jahn) = \"Father of Gymnastics\"; unhone 1811 mein Germany mein pehla Turnverein\n(gymnastic club) sthapit kiya. [Q400]"," ● Pommel Horse = Gymnastics ka apparatus hai. [Q401]\n● Volley = Tennis/Volleyball ka term hai; Gymnastics se related NAHI. Gymnastics moves: Round-off, Cartwheel,\nHandstand. [Q410]\n● World Challenge Cup = Artistic Gymnastics se related hai (1975 mein founded). [Q393]\n● William G. Morgan ne 1895 mein Volleyball ka avishkar kiya. [Q405]\n● Volleyball mein spike ko smash bhi kehte hain — ye net ke upar se kiya gaya ek aakramak prahar hai. [Q402]\n● Libero = Indoor volleyball mein defensive specialist ki position hai. [Q399]\n● Flagrant Foul = Basketball se related hai — ye ek gambheer personal foul hai jismein atyadhik ya hinsak contact\nhota hai. [Q414]\n5. Sports Origins, Stadiums & Terminology\n● Kabaddi ki utpatti Bharat (Tamil Nadu) mein hui; ye Bangladesh ka rashtriya khel hai. Football aur Cricket ki utpatti\nEngland mein hui. [Q385]\n● Archery = Bhutan ka rashtriya khel; Sri Lanka = Volleyball; Denmark = Football/Handball; Bangladesh = Kabaddi.\n[Q386]\n● James Naismith ne 1891 mein Basketball ka avishkar kiya. [Q409]\n● Steeple chase = Horse racing (aur athletics) se juda hai. [Q390]\n● Barabati Stadium = Cuttack, Odisha mein hai — ye Odisha Cricket Association dwara banaya gaya cricket stadium\nhai. [Q397]\n● Gelora Bung Karno (GBK) Stadium = Indonesia mein hai — Asia ke sabse bade multi-purpose stadiums mein se ek.\n[Q403]\n● Augusta Masters Trophy = Golf se related hai — ye Augusta National Golf Club mein hota hai, professional golf ki\n4 pramukh championships mein se ek. [Q404]\n● F1 flags: Yellow = Danger (slow down); Green = Start race; Red = Stop race; Black = Disqualification; Checkered =\nEnd race. [Q396]\n● Polo mein safety reasons ki wajah se left hand se khelne ki anumati nahi hoti — ye 2 teams (4 players each) ke\nbeech ghode ki peeth par khela jata hai. [Q384]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Trampoline mein stick ki zaroorat nahi hoti; lekin Skiing, Billiards, Hockey mein sticks/poles ka use hota\nhai. [Q416]\n6. Indian Athletes & Their Records\n● PV Sindhu = pehli Bharatiya mahila jo do individual Olympic medals jeeti — Silver (Rio 2016) aur Bronze (Tokyo\n2020). [Q354]\n● Bajrang Punia = pehle Indian wrestler jo New York ke Madison Square Garden mein lade. [Q355]\n● Mary Kom = Bharat ki ekmatra 6-time world boxing champion; pehli Bharatiya mahila jo Asian Games (2014) mein\nboxing gold aur London Olympics (2012) mein bronze jeeti. [Q366]\n● Neeraj Chopra = Javelin throw; pehle Indian jo world athletics championship mein gold jeete; aur pehle track &\nfield athlete jo India ke liye Olympic individual event mein gold jeete. [Q419]\n● Priyanka Nutakki = Chess se sambandhit hain. [Q353]\n● D Gukesh = India ke youngest chess Grandmaster — 15 January 2019 ko 12 saal 7 mahine 17 din ki age mein ye\ntitle haasil kiya (Abhimanyu Mishra, New Jersey, world ke youngest hain — 2021 mein). [Q376]\n● Dipika Pallikal Karthik aur Joshna Chinappa = India ka representation karti hain Squash mein — racket-and-ball\nsport, char-deewari wale court mein small hollow rubber ball ke saath khela jata hai. [Q381]\n● Chess mein Rook (naav) ka Hindi/traditional naam Elephant (Haathi) hai; Knight = Horse (Ghoda), Bishop = Camel"," (Unt) ko represent karta hai. [Q389]\n● Michael Phelps = American swimmer; total 28 Olympic medals (23 gold, 3 silver, 2 bronze) — sabse zyada Olympic\ngold ka record. [Q365]\n● Milkha Singh ne 1960 Rome Olympics ke 400m final mein 4th place finish kiya; is race mein unhone national\nrecord (45.73 sec) banaya. [Q363]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Cricket = cash awards scheme mein shamil NAHI; baaki sab hain. [Q352]\n● Beighton Cup = Hockey (sabse purana); Durand Cup = Football — confuse mat hona! [Q387]\n● Roman Ring = Gymnastics; Ippon/Yuko/Waza-ari = Judo — alag hain. [Q408]\n● Volley = Tennis/Volleyball; NOT Gymnastics. [Q410]\n● Augusta Masters = Golf; World Challenge Cup = Artistic Gymnastics — alag hain! [Q404, Q393]\n● Kumar Sangakkara = MCC ke pehle non-British President; ye Indian nahi, Sri Lankan hain. [Q382]\n● Brazil = har FIFA WC mein khela; Germany/Spain/England ne nahi — confuse mat hona. [Q369]\n● Special Olympics min age = 8 years; Paralympics alag hai. [Q415]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 11 Sports Full Mind Map (Q352-Q420)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0427","t":"12 Books and Authors","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — BOOKS & AUTHORS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indian English & Contemporary Fiction\n2. Hindi & Regional Literature Classics\n3. Freedom Struggle, History & Political Writings\n4. Ancient, Classical & Sanskrit Texts\n5. Biographies, Autobiographies & Memoirs\n6. Science, Economics & Philosophy\n7. Women Writers & Feminist Literature\n8. RK Narayan & Malgudi\n9. Social Realism & Key Writers\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Indian English & Contemporary Fiction\n● Vikram Chandra — Red Earth and Pouring Rain, aur Love and Longing in Bombay, Sacred Games ke bhi lekhak\nhain. [Q421]\n● Anita Desai — Clear Light of Day ki lekhika; unki aur prasiddh kitaaben: Fasting, Feasting, In Custody, Fire on the\nMountain, The Peacock Garden. [Q422]\n● Salman Rushdie — Midnight's Children (1981, Booker Prize winner); aur The Satanic Verses, The Jaguar Smile.\n[Q425]\n● Ramchandra Guha — India after Gandhi; aur Gandhi before India, Gandhi: The Years That Changed The World.\n[Q431]\n● Shashi Tharoor — India: The Future Is Now (edited); The Great Indian Novel, An Era of Darkness, The Paradoxical\nPrime Minister. [Q439]\n● EM Forster — A Passage to India (1924), jo British Raj aur 1920s ke independence movement ki pauranik\npusthahboomi par hai. [Q451]\n● Olga Tokarczuk — Flights (Polish lekhika, Nobel Prize in Literature 2018 aur Booker 2018). [Q456]\n● Namita Gokhale — Things to Leave Behind (Kumaon hills ke jeevan par); aur Paro: Dreams of Passion, A\nHimalayan Love Story. [Q487]\n● Judy Balan — Two Fates – The Story of My Divorce (Chetan Bhagat ki Two States ki parody); Half Boyfriend, Why\nam I like this. [Q488]\n● Amish Tripathi — Ram Chandra series: pehli kitaab Rama par, doosri Sita par, teesri Raavana (Raavan – Enemy of\nAryavarta) par. [Q489]\n● Aravind Adiga — Selection Day (cricket theme par); The White Tiger (Man Booker Prize 2008), Amnesty. [Q494]\n● Rahul Mehta — No Other World (2017); Quarantine: Stories, Face palm exorcist. [Q495]\n● Anil Menon — Half of What I Say (speculative fiction); Sybil's Garage No. 7, The Beast with Nine Billion Feet.\n[Q485]\n● Karan Mahajan — The Association of Small Bombs. [Q486]\n● Saba Naqvi — Politics of Jugaad: The Coalition Handbook; Shades of Saffron: From Vajpayee To Modi, In Good\nFaith. [Q433]\n● Kavitha Rao — Lady Doctors: The Untold Stories of India's First Women in Medicine (Rukhmabai Raut par). [Q426]\n● Karan Johar — An Unsuitable Boy (autobiography). [Q490]"," 2. Hindi & Regional Literature Classics\n● Munshi Premchand — Sevasadan, Godaan, Bazaar-e-Husn, Karmabhoomi, Shatranj Ke Khiladi, Gaban,\nMansarovar, Idgah. [Q432]\n● Bhisham Sahni — Tamas (Hindi upanyaas); Padma Bhushan 1998. [Q430]\n● Hari Shankar Parsai — Viklang Shraddha ka Daur; Sahitya Akademi Award 1982; prasiddh vyangyakaar. [Q424]\n● Devaki Nandan Khatri — Chandrakanta (epic fantasy); aur Bhootnath, Chandrakanta Santati. [Q435]\n● Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay — Devdas (Bengali upanyaaskaar). [Q467]\n● Bankim Chandra Chatterjee — Durgeshnandini (1865, Bengali aitihaasik romance). [Q475]\n● Bibhutibhushan Bandopadhyay — Pather Panchali, Chander Pahar, Aranyak, Adarsha Hindu Hotel. [Q442]\n● Satyajit Ray — The Incredible Adventures of Professor Shonku, Sonar Kella, Hatyapuri. [Q483]\n● Bolwar Mahammad Kunhi — Swatantryada Ota (Kannada); Sahitya Academy Award; Central Sahitya Academy ke\nBala Sahitya Puraskar ke pehle Kannada vijeta. [Q491]\n3. Freedom Struggle, History & Political Writings\n● Surendranath Banerjee — A Nation in Making (aatmkatha); Rashtraguru aur Indian Burke ke naam se prasiddh;\nIndian National Association ke sansthaapak. [Q423]\n● Subhash Chandra Bose — The Indian Struggle; aur An Indian Pilgrim: An Unfinished Autobiography. [Q450]\n● Dadabhai Naoroji — Poverty and Un-British Rule of India (1867 mein pehli baar per capita income ki ganana);\nismein \"drain of wealth\" ka siddhant bhi diya. [Q446]\n● Jyotirao Govindrao Phule — Ghulamgiri (1871, jaati vyavastha ke anyaayon par); Satyashodhak Samaj ke\nsansthaapak. [Q476]\n● Al-Biruni — Tahqiq ma lil-Hind (History of India); Iranian vidwaan, Mahmud of Ghazni ke samakaaleen. [Q462]\n● PV Narasimha Rao (Bharat ke 9vein PM) — Telugu epic \"Veyipadagalu\" ka Hindi anuvaad \"Sahasra Phan\" (A\nThousand Hoods) naam se kiya. [Q445]\n● Vincent Arthur Smith — Early History of India; Irish Indologist aur art historian. [Q453]\n● Anu Bandyopadhyay — Bahuroopi Gandhi (1964). [Q437]\n● Admiral Sushil Kumar — A Prime Minister to Remember; poorv Indian Navy Chief of Naval Staff. [Q461]\n4. Ancient, Classical & Sanskrit Texts\n● Plato — Republic; aur Allegory of the Cave, The Symposium, Crito, Gorgias, Lysis, Critias. [Q428]\n● Vishnu Sharma — Panchatantra (Sanskrit mein \"Five Principles\", naitik aur vyavahaarik gyaan). [Q455]\n● Bhasa — Svapnavasavadattam; pehle gyaat Sanskrit naatakakaar. [Q441]\n● Banabhatta — Harshacharita (Kannauj ke shaaska Harshavardhana ki jeevani); aur Kadambari. [Q447]\n● Harshavardhana — Ratnavali, Nagananda, Priyadarsika. [Q458]\n● Aryabhata — Aryabhatiyam (Sanskrit mein). [Q468]\n● Panini — prasiddh Sanskrit vyaakaranavid; Ashtadhyayi (Sanskrit vyakaran ka sarvavyaapak granth); \"Father of\nSanskrit grammar\". [Q469]\n● Patanjali — Mahabhashya (Ashtadhyayi par sabse mahatvapoorn kaarya). [Q480]\n● Bharat Muni — Natyashastra (pradarshan kalaon par Sanskrit granth). [Q478]\n● Silappadikaram — pehla Tamil mahakaavya; Rajkumar Ilango Adigal dwaara rachit, Chera shaaska Senguttuvan ke\nshaasanakaal mein. [Q479]\n● Tolkappiyam — sabse puraana maujooda Tamil vyaakaran; lekhak Tolkappiyar; kavita aur vyakaran se"," sambandhit. [Q481]\n● Sattanar — Manimekalai (Tamil mahakaavya); Bauddh vyaapaari aur Tamil lekhak. [Q466]\n5. Biographies, Autobiographies & Memoirs\n● Yuvraj Singh — The Test of My Life (aatmkatha). [Q440]\n● Rahul Dravid — The Nice Guy Who Finished First (jeevani). [Q443]\n● Jean-Pierre Harrison — The Edge of Time (unke patni Kalpana Chawla ki jeevani). [Q448]\n● BR Ambedkar — Waiting for a Visa (20-prishthiya aatmkathaatmak jeevan kahani). [Q459]\n● Mamata Banerjee — My Unforgettable Memories (aatmkatha). [Q482]\n● Sharad Pawar — On My Terms: From the Grassroots to the Corridors of Power. [Q492]\n● Ruskin Bond — Lone Fox Dancing: My Autobiography; unka pehla upanyaas The Room on the Roof. [Q496]\n● Bharathi S Pradhan — Anything but Khamosh: The Shatrughan Sinha Biography. [Q497]\n● Malala Yousafzai — We Are Displaced (sharnaarthi ladkiyon par); Nobel Shaanti Puraskaar 2014. [Q473]\n6. Science, Economics & Philosophy\n● Galileo Galilei — The Little Balance (La Balancitta, 1586); pehle vyakti jo doorbeen se chandrama ke pahaadon aur\nBrihaspati ke chandramaon ki report kiye. [Q452]\n● Stephen Hawking — A Brief History of Time: From the Big Bang to Black Holes (1988, saiddhaantik brahmaand\nvigyaan). [Q472]\n● JC Kumarappa — Economy of Permanence; Gandhi ke kareebi sahayogi, Gandhiavaadi arthashaastree. [Q436]\n● Charan Singh — Economic Nightmare of India: its cause and cure. [Q470]\n● John Hicks — Capital and Growth (arthashaastree). [Q477]\n● Club of Rome — The Limits to Growth (1972, vishwa arthavyavastha ke patan ki bhavishyavaani); ek\nantarraashtriya think tank. [Q434]\n● Krishna Kripalani — All Men Are Brothers ka sankalan evam sampadan (UNESCO ke liye Gandhi ke lekhanon se\nchayan). [Q471]\n● Red Data Book — IUCN dwaara rakha jaata hai, jo sabhi luptapraay jaanwaron aur paudhon ka record rakhti hai.\n[Q444]\n● APJ Abdul Kalam — Ignited Minds, India 2020, Wings of Fire, Mission India. [Q454]\n● Raghuram Rajan — I Do What I Do (2017); RBI ke 23rd Governor rahe Indian economist ne likhi. [Q493]\n7. Women Writers & Feminist Literature\n● Kamala Das — Malayalam lekhika; Madhavikutty upnaam se likhti thi; kavitaayein: Summer in Calcutta, A Hot\nNoon in Malabar, My Mother at Sixty-six. [Q427, Q464]\n● Tarabai Shinde — Stri Purush Tulana; 19vi sadi ki naariwaadi kaaryakarta, pitrasatta aur jaati ka virodh kiya.\n[Q457]\n● Subhadra Kumari Chauhan — Khoob Ladi Mardani (Jhansi ki Rani Lakshmibai ki veerta par). [Q463]\n● Priyanka Dubey — No Nation for Women. [Q460]"," 8. RK Narayan & Malgudi\n● RK Narayan — ka pehla upanyaas Swami and Friends (1935); unhone Malgudi naamak kaalpanik gaanv ki rachna\nki; aur kitaaben: The Guide, Malgudi Days, The English Teacher, The Man-Eater of Malgudi, The Bachelor of Arts.\n[Q429, Q449]\n9. Social Realism & Key Writers\n● Mulk Raj Anand — Untouchable; aur Coolie, Two Leaves and a Bud, The Village, The Sword and the Sickle. [Q438]\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Poverty of India = Dadabhai Naoroji dwara likhi gayi; ye Amartya Sen ki kitaab NAHI hai. Amartya Sen ki\nkitaaben: On Economic Inequality, Resources, Values, and Development, Poverty and Famines. [Q465]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: The Discovery of India = Jawaharlal Nehru dwara likhi gayi; ye APJ Abdul Kalam ki NAHI hai. Kalam ki\nkitaaben: Wings of Fire, Ignited Minds, India 2020. [Q474]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Deepshikha = Mahadevi Verma dwara likhi gayi; ye Premchand ki NAHI hai. Premchand ki prasiddh\nrachnaayein: Godan, Gaban, Nirmala. [Q484]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 12 Books and Authors Full Mind Map (Q421-Q497)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0428","t":"13 Famous Personality","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FAMOUS PERSONALITY — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Environmentalists & Social Reformers\n2. Scientists, Statisticians & Economists\n3. Industrialists & Philanthropists\n4. Architects, Painters & Artists\n5. Writers, Poets & Literary Figures\n6. Spiritual Leaders & Social Workers\n7. Sports Personalities & Records\n8. Beauty Pageants & Entertainment\n9. Historical Figures & Their Birthplaces\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Environmentalists & Social Reformers\n● Dr. Rajendra Singh ko \"Waterman of India\" kehte hain — inhone 2015 mein Stockholm Water Prize jeeta; ye rural\nIndia mein jal suraksha aur jal bahali ke liye jaane jate hain. [Q498]\n● Sunder Lal Bahuguna Chipko movement ke neta the; Chandi Prasad Bhatt ne Dasholi Gram Swarajya Sangh ki\nsthapna ki. [Q498]\n● Mother Teresa ko 4 September 2016 ko Pope Francis I dwara canonized (sant ghoshit) kiya gaya; inhone\nMissionaries of Charity ki sthapna ki aur 1979 mein Nobel Peace Prize aur 1980 mein Bharat Ratna se sammanit\nkiya gaya. [Q499]\n● Anand Mahindra ne 1996 mein Project Nanhi Kali launch kiya — ye Bharat ka sabse bada programme hai jo\nvanchit ladkiyon ko 10 saal ki schooling poori karne mein saksham banata hai. [Q516]\n2. Scientists, Statisticians & Economists\n● Prasanta Chandra Mahalanobis = \"Father of Modern Statistics in India\"; inhone Indian Statistical Institute ki\nsthapna ki. Inki jayanti ke upalakshya mein 29 June ko Rashtriya Sankhyiki Diwas manaya jata hai. [Q500]\n● Dr. Subbanna Ayyappan = aquaculture scientist; inhen January 2022 mein Padma Shri (Science & Engineering)\nmila — ye Bharat ki Neeli Kranti (Blue Revolution) ko shakti dene mein mahatvapoorn bhoomika nibhane ke liye.\n[Q501]\n● M.S. Swaminathan = \"Father of the Green Revolution in India\"; Verghese Kurien = \"Milkman of India\" aur \"Father\nof the White Revolution\" — inhone Operation Flood chalaya. [Q503]\n3. Industrialists & Philanthropists\n● Jamsetji Tata = \"Father of Indian Industry\" — inhone Mumbai mein Taj Mahal Palace Hotel ka nirman kiya, jo 16\nDecember 1903 ko khula. [Q502]\n4. Architects, Painters & Artists\n● Edwin Lutyens — English architect jinhone New Delhi mein India Gate aur Viceroy's House (ab Rashtrapati"," Bhavan) design kiya. Le Corbusier ne Chandigarh ki planning ki. [Q505]\n● George Chinnery — 23 saal (1802-1825) tak Bharat mein rahe; inhone portraits, landscapes aur aam logon ke\nrozmarra ke jeevan ke scenes paint kiye. [Q504]\n● M.F. Hussain = \"Picasso of India\" — ye ek Bharatiya samakaleen chitrakar the jo apni sahasik aur jeevant rangon\nwali varnanatmak paintings ke liye prasiddh the. [Q515]\n5. Writers, Poets & Literary Figures\n● Munshi Premchand ka asli naam Dhanpat Rai Srivastava tha; janm 31 July 1880 ko Varanasi ke Lamhi mein hua.\nPrasiddh karyon mein Karmabhoomi, Kafan, Godan, Poos Ki Raat, Eidgah shamil hain. [Q506]\n● Amir Khusrau (\"Tota-e-Hind\" / Parrot of India) ka janm Uttar Pradesh ke Patiyali mein hua; inhe \"Qawwali ka\nJanak\" kaha jata hai aur inhone Bharat mein ghazal shaili ki shuruaat ki. [Q507]\n● Mahadevi Verma = \"Aadhunik Bharat ki Meera\" — ye \"Chhayavaad\" saahitik aandolan ki pramukh kavayitri thi.\n[Q513]\n● Gyanadev ne 13vi shatabdi mein Saap aur Seedhi (Snakes and Ladders) ka avishkar kiya — iska mool naam\n\"Mokshapat\" (Moksha Patamu) tha. [Q514]\n● Rabindranath Tagore ka prasiddh quote: \"If you cry because the sun has gone out of your life, your tears will\nprevent you from seeing the stars\" — ye \"Vishwa Kavi\" hain jinhone 1913 mein Sahitya ka Nobel Prize jeeta.\n[Q509]\n6. Spiritual Leaders & Social Workers\n● Sri Sri Ravi Shankar (Art of Living Foundation ke sansthaapak) ko 2016 mein Simon Wiesenthal Humanitarian\nLaureate se sammanit kiya gaya — maanav garima, antar-dharmik sambandhon aur sahishnuta ko badhawa dene\nke liye. [Q519]\n7. Sports Personalities & Records\n● Kami Rita Sherpa ne 24 baar Mount Everest fatih kar world record banaya; 2021 mein unhone 25vi baar chadhai\nkar apna hi record toda. [Q512]\n● Satnam Singh Bhamara = Bharat se NBA mein draft hone wale pehle khiladi; Dallas Mavericks ne unhe 2015 NBA\ndraft mein 52vi pick ke saath chuna. [Q517]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Koneru Humpy = shatranj khiladi hain, squash player NAHI; Anaka Alankamony, Dipika Pallikal, Joshna\nChinnappa = sab squash players hain. [Q518]\n8. Beauty Pageants & Entertainment\n● Miss Universe title jeetne wali Bharatiya: Sushmita Sen (1994), Lara Dutta (2000), Harnaaz Sandhu (2021). [Q508]\n● Miss World title jeetne wali Bharatiya: Reita Faria, Aishwarya Rai, Diana Hayden, Yukta Mookhey, Priyanka\nChopra, Manushi Chhillar. [Q508]\n● Satyajit Ray ke paas sabse zyada Rashtriya Film Puraskar jeetne ka record hai. [Q511]\n9. Historical Figures & Their Birthplaces"," ● Subhash Chandra Bose ka janm 23 January 1897 ko Cuttack (Odisha) mein hua — inke janmdin ko Parakram Diwas\nke roop mein manaya jata hai. [Q510]\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Koneru Humpy = chess player; NOT squash player — baaki teeno (Anaka, Dipika, Joshna) squash hain.\n[Q518]\n● Edwin Lutyens = Delhi buildings (India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhavan); Le Corbusier = Chandigarh — alag hain! [Q505]\n● Jamsetji Tata = Taj Mahal Palace Hotel; Ratan Tata / JRD Tata = alag generation — confuse mat hona. [Q502]\n● M.S. Swaminathan = Green Revolution; Verghese Kurien = White Revolution — dono alag! [Q503]\n● Miss Universe aur Miss World ke winners alag hain — list confuse mat karna. [Q508]\n● George Chinnery = British painter jo 23 saal India mein rahe; William Hodges alag hain. [Q504]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 13 Famous Personality Full Mind Map (Q498-Q519)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0429","t":"14 Important Days","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — IMPORTANT DAYS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Health & Medical Days\n2. Environment, Nature & Wildlife Days\n3. National Days of India\n4. International Organizations & Global Days\n5. Education, Science & Technology Days\n6. State Foundation Days\n7. Other Important Days\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Health & Medical Days\n● Rare Disease Day = 28 February (last day of February). Aur health days: 31 Jan = Anti Leprosy, 4 Feb = World\nCancer, 24 Mar = World TB, 17 Apr = World Hemophilia, 19 May = World Hepatitis, 20 Oct = World Malaria, 1 Dec\n= World AIDS. [Q520]\n● World TB Day = 24 March; TB = Mycobacterium tuberculosis se hota hai, generally lungs affect karta hai; vaccine =\nBCG. [Q524]\n● World Health Day = 7 April — ye WHO ki sthapna (7 April 1948) ko mark karta hai; WHO HQ = Geneva. [Q550]\n● World Red Cross Day = 8 May — Henry Dunant (ICRC founder, pehle Nobel Peace Prize winner) ki jayanti. 8 May\nko World Thalassaemia Day bhi manate hain. [Q536]\n● International Nurses Day = 12 May (1974 se shuru). [Q541]\n● World AIDS Vaccine Day = 18 May. [Q535]\n● World Blood Donor Day = 14 June. [Q542]\n● World Heart Day = 29 September. [Q545]\n● World Day of the Sick = 11 February. [Q533]\n● World Homoeopathy Day = 10 April. [Q550]\n● World Suicide Prevention Day = 10 September. [Q555]\n● World Autism Awareness Day = 2 April. [Q532]\n2. Environment, Nature & Wildlife Days\n● World Environment Day = 5 June — pehli baar 1974 mein manaya gaya. [Q542]\n● Earth Day = 22 April — environment aur pollution awareness ke liye. [Q533]\n● World Water Day = 22 March — 2.2 billion logon ke paas safe water nahi, SDG 6 ko support karta hai. [Q523]\n● World Wetlands Day = 2 February — Ramsar Convention (1971) ke signing ki yaad mein; India 1982 mein join\nkiya. [Q560]\n● World Wildlife Day = 3 March — CITES par 3 March 1973 ko sign hua tha. [Q534]\n● International Day for Biodiversity = 22 May. [Q559]\n● World Oceans Day = 8 June. [Q533]\n● World Day to Combat Desertification and Drought = 17 June — UNCCD 1994 mein establish hua. [Q531]\n● International Ozone Day = 16 September — Montreal Protocol (1987) par signing ki yaad mein; pehli baar 1995"," mein manaya gaya. [Q555]\n● World Bamboo Day = 18 September — Kamesh Salam ne sthapit kiya. [Q539]\n● Global Tiger Day = 29 July — 2010 St Petersburg Tiger Summit se shuru; Tadoba Tiger Reserve, Maharashtra ne\n2022 mein host kiya. [Q549]\n● World Elephant Day = 12 August. [Q549]\n● World Sparrow Day = 20 March. [Q534, Q539]\n● World Bee Day = 20 May. [Q559]\n● National Pollution Prevention Day = 2 December — Bhopal Gas Tragedy (1984) ki yaad mein; ~45 tons methyl\nisocyanate leak hui thi. [Q532]\n● National Energy Conservation Day = 14 December — BEE (Bureau of Energy Efficiency) under Power Ministry\ndwara. [Q558]\n3. National Days of India\n● Parakram Diwas = 23 January — Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose ki jayanti. [Q521]\n● Shaheed Diwas / Martyrs' Day = 23 March — Bhagat Singh, Shivram Rajguru, Sukhdev Thapar ki shahadat. 30\nJanuary ko bhi Martyrs' Day manate hain — Mahatma Gandhi ki hatya (1948, Nathuram Godse) ki yaad mein.\n[Q521, Q544]\n● International Day of Non-Violence = 2 October — Gandhi Jayanti. [Q521]\n● National Unity Day = 31 October — Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ki jayanti; 2014 se shuru. Statue of Unity = 31 Oct\n2018 ko unveil hua, Sadhu Bet, Narmada, Gujarat, 182m, designer Ram V Sutar. [Q527]\n● National Science Day = 28 February. [Q528]\n● National Technology Day = 11 May. [Q535]\n● National Panchayati Raj Day = 24 April — 73rd Amendment Act 1992 effective 1993 ki yaad mein; Dr Manmohan\nSingh ne 2010 mein ghoshit kiya. Rajasthan (Nagaur) = pehla state jahan 1959 mein Nehru ne inaugurate kiya.\n[Q530]\n● Civil Services Day = 21 April — 1947 mein Sardar Patel ne Metcalf House (Delhi) mein probationers ko address\nkiya tha, unhe \"steel frame of India\" kaha; pehli baar 2006 mein manaya gaya. [Q538]\n● National Handloom Day = 7 August — Swadeshi Movement (1905) ki yaad mein; 2015 se shuru. [Q540]\n● National Women's Farmer's Day = 15 October. [Q544]\n● World Students' Day (India) = 15 October — APJ Abdul Kalam ki jayanti (born 15 Oct 1931, Rameswaram). [Q546]\n● Armed Forces Flag Day = 7 December. Aur defence days: Army Day (15 Jan), Air Force Day (8 Oct), Navy Day (4\nDec), Vijay Diwas (16 Dec), Kargil Victory Day (26 Jul). [Q543]\n● National Consumer Day = 24 December — Consumer Protection Act 1986 effective hua tha. World Consumer\nRights Day = 15 March. [Q553]\n● National Sports Day = 29 August. [Q522]\n● National Voters' Day = 25 January. [Q543, Q554]\n● National Statistics Day = 29 June — PC Mahalanobis ki jayanti. [Q540]\n● National Education Day = 11 November. [Q540]\n● Pravasi Bharatiya Divas / NRI Day = 9 January. [Q540, Q554]\n● Minorities Rights Day = 18 December — UN 1992 mein declare kiya; NCM dwara organize hota hai. 6 minority\ncommunities = Muslims, Christians, Sikhs, Buddhists, Zoroastrians (Parsis), Jains. [Q522]\n● Hindi Day = 14 September. [Q545]\n● Public Service Broadcasting Day = 12 November. [Q558]"," 4. International Organizations & Global Days\n● International Labour Organisation (ILO) ki sthapna 28 June 1919 ko Treaty of Versailles se hui; HQ Geneva; Nobel\nPeace Prize 1969; parent org UN. International Labour Day = 1 May. [Q548]\n● UN World Wildlife Day = 3 March — CITES 1973 par signing. [Q534]\n● World Population Day = 11 July — UNDP 1989 dwara establish. [Q551]\n● International Literacy Day = 8 September. [Q545]\n● International Day of Sign Languages = 23 September — 2018 se shuru, International Week of the Deaf ka hissa.\n[Q552]\n● International Day of Women and Girls in Science = 11 February — STEM fields mein equal access promote karne\nke liye. [Q554]\n● World Food Day = 16 October. [Q547]\n● World Refugee Day = 20 June. [Q536, Q542]\n● International Day of Yoga = 21 June. [Q559]\n● International Day of Peace = 21 September. [Q533]\n● World Children's Day = 20 November. [Q533]\n● Human Rights Day = 10 December. [Q533]\n● World Press Freedom Day = 3 May. [Q529, Q551]\n● World No-Tobacco Day = 31 May. [Q536]\n● International Women's Day = 8 March. [Q523, Q541]\n● World Book and Copyright Day = 23 April — UNESCO dwara, pehli baar 1995 mein. [Q529]\n● World Computer Literacy Day = 2 December. [Q532]\n● International Day of Abolition of Slavery = 2 December. [Q532]\n● World Bicycle Day = 3 June — UNGA 2018; pehli bicycle Karl von Drais ne banayi. [Q557]\n● International Day of Light = 16 May — 1960 mein Theodore Maiman ne pehla laser operate kiya. [Q537]\n● World Hunger Day = 28 May — The Hunger Project 2011. [Q547]\n● International Migrants Day = 18 December. [Q546]\n● World Day Against Child Labour = 12 June. [Q542]\n● International Day Against Nuclear Tests = 29 August. [Q522]\n● World Food Safety Day = 7 June. [Q542, Q560]\n● World Ocean Day = 8 June. [Q542]\n● International Mine Awareness Day = 4 April. [Q560]\n● World Hearing Day = 3 March. [Q560]\n● World Soil Day = 5 December. [Q528]\n● International Day of Families = 15 May. [Q559]\n● World Cities Day = 31 October. [Q551]\n● International Moon Day = 20 July. [Q551]\n● Coal Miners Day = 4 May. [Q557]\n● International Nurses Day = 12 May (1974). [Q541]\n5. Education, Science & Technology Days\n● National Science Day = 28 February. [Q528, Q540]\n● National Technology Day = 11 May. [Q535]"," ● World Science Day = 10 November. [Q535]\n● International Literacy Day = 8 September. [Q545]\n● World Students' Day = 15 October (APJ Abdul Kalam). [Q546]\n● World Book and Copyright Day = 23 April. [Q529]\n● World Hindi Day = 10 January. [Q529]\n● International Day of Light = 16 May (laser 1960). [Q537]\n● National Education Day = 11 November. [Q540]\n6. State Foundation Days\n● Utkala Dibasa / Odisha Day = 1 April — 1936 mein alag state bana; Bihar, Orissa Province, Madras Presidency,\nCentral Provinces ke hisson se. Utkal Sammilani = 1903 mein Madhusudan Das ne banaya tha. [Q526]\n● Himachal Day = 15 April — 1948 mein centrally administered province bana; Mandi, Chamba, Mahasu, Sirmour +\n30 riyasaten merge hui. [Q561]\n● Andhra Pradesh = 1 November. [Q561]\n● Assam = 2 December. [Q561]\n● Bihar = 22 March. [Q561]\n● Gujarat = 1 May. [Q561]\n● Rajasthan = 30 March. [Q561]\n● Telangana = 2 June. [Q561]\n7. Other Important Days\n● International Dance Day = 29 April — UNESCO's International Theatre Institute dwara. [Q528]\n● International Day of the Unborn Child = 25 March — Pope John Paul II ne establish kiya, Feast of Annunciation ke\nsaath. [Q541]\n● Bangladesh Independence Day = 26 March — 1971 mein Sheikh Mujibur Rahman ne declare kiya; Operation\nSearchlight 25 March 1971 ki raat ko hua. Pehle President = Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, pehle PM = Tajuddin\nAhmad. [Q556]\n● World Braille Day = 4 January. [Q552]\n● World Radio Day = 13 February. [Q552, Q543]\n● National Black Cat Appreciation Day = 17 August. [Q546]\n● National Yo-Yo Day = 6 June. [Q557]\n● International No Diet Day = 6 May. [Q557]\n● German-American Day = 6 October. [Q558]\n● International Volunteer Day = 5 December. [Q553]\n● World Development Information Day = 24 October. [Q553]\n● UN Day = 24 October. [Q544, Q553]\n● International Day of Family Remittances = 16 June. [Q537]\n● World Milk Day = 1 June. [Q537, Q558]\n● Hijri year = ~11 days shorter than solar year (354 days, leap year 355 days). [Q525]"," 8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: World TB Day (24 March) aur World Health Day (7 April) alag hain — confuse mat karna. [Q524, Q550]\n● National Consumer Day (24 Dec) = India-specific; World Consumer Rights Day (15 Mar) = global — alag hain!\n[Q553]\n● Martyrs' Day = 23 March (Bhagat Singh) aur 30 January (Gandhi) — dono alag alag hain. [Q521, Q544]\n● World Environment Day (5 June) aur Earth Day (22 April) — alag hain! [Q542, Q533]\n● World Wetlands Day (2 Feb) aur World Water Day (22 Mar) — alag hain. [Q560, Q523]\n● Minorities Rights Day (18 Dec) = UN dwara; National Unity Day (31 Oct) = Patel ki jayanti — alag. [Q522, Q527]\n● World Students' Day (15 Oct) = Kalam ki jayanti; World Literacy Day (8 Sep) — alag hain. [Q546, Q545]\n● ILO founded 28 June 1919; UN founded 24 Oct 1945 — alag organizations, alag dates. [Q548, Q544]\n● Himachal Day (15 April); Odisha Day (1 April); Bihar Day (22 March) — teeno alag hain. [Q561, Q526]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 14 Important Days Full Mind Map (Q520-Q561)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0430","t":"15 States GK","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — STATES GK — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. State Formation, Capitals & Union Territories\n2. State Symbols — Trees, Flowers, Animals, Birds & Sports\n3. City Nicknames\n4. Museums, Monuments, Forts & Heritage Sites\n5. Institutes, Universities & Libraries\n6. Culture, Dance, Art & Festivals\n7. Infrastructure — Bridges, Tunnels, Airports & Transport\n8. Food & Culinary Specialties\n9. Wildlife & Natural Resources\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. State Formation, Capitals & Union Territories\n● Goa India ka 25th state bana 30 May 1987 ko — pehle (19 Dec 1961 se) Goa, Daman aur Diu Union Territory tha;\n56th Constitutional Amendment Act 1987 ke tahat alag state ka status mila. [Q567]\n● Maharashtra aur Gujarat states 1960 mein banaye gaye. Other states ki formation: Andhra Pradesh (1953),\nArunachal Pradesh (1987), Assam (1950), Bihar (1950), Chhattisgarh (2000), Haryana (1966), Himachal Pradesh\n(1971), Jharkhand (2000), Karnataka (1956), Kerala (1956), Madhya Pradesh (1950), Manipur (1972), Meghalaya\n(1972), Mizoram (1987), Nagaland (1963), Odisha (1950), Punjab (1947), Rajasthan (1949), Sikkim (1975), Tamil\nNadu (1956), Telangana (2014, 29th aur sabse youngest state), Tripura (1972), Uttar Pradesh (1950), Uttarakhand\n(2000), West Bengal (1950). [Q574]\n● Arunachal Pradesh 1972 tak North East Frontier Agency (NEFA) ke naam se jaana jaata tha — 1951 mein Balipara\nFrontier Tract, Tirap Frontier Tract, Abor Hills District aur Mishmi Hills District ko merge karke bana; 1972 mein\nrename hokar Union Territory bana, capital Itanagar hai; state ban 20 February 1987 ko. [Q578]\n● Dadra aur Nagar Haveli ki capital Silvassa hai. Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu — 26 January 2020 ko\nnaya Union Territory bana (capital Daman); present mein India mein 28 states aur 8 Union Territories hain;\nerstwhile Jammu & Kashmir state ko 2 UTs (J&K aur Ladakh) mein bifurcate kiya gaya. [Q601]\n2. State Symbols — Trees, Flowers, Animals, Birds & Sports\n● Hollong (Dipterocarpus macrocarpus) — Assam ka state tree aur tallest tree; upper Assam aur Arunachal Pradesh\nke jungles mein 45m tak grow hota hai; Moran community (Assam) ke liye sacred tree hai. [Q562]\n● Great Indian Bustard — Rajasthan ka state bird, Desert National Park (Jaisalmer) mein paaya jaata hai; Wildlife\nProtection Act 1972 ke tahat protected. Other state birds: Uttar Pradesh — Sarus Crane; Sikkim — Blood\nPheasant; Bihar — House Sparrow; Andaman Nicobar — Wood Pigeon (official bird). [Q564]\n● Brahma Kamal — Uttarakhand ka state flower. Other state flowers: Tripura — Nag Kesar; Himachal Pradesh —\nPink Rhododendron; Sikkim — Noble Orchid; Bihar — Kachnar; Uttar Pradesh — Palash; Rajasthan — Rohida.\nNational Flower of India — Lotus. [Q565]\n● Giant Squirrel — Maharashtra ka state animal. Other state animals: Goa — Gaur; Haryana — Blackbuck; Himachal\nPradesh — Snow Leopard; Madhya Pradesh — Swamp Deer (Barasingha); Sikkim — Red Panda; Kerala — Indian\nElephant; Manipur — Sangai deer (endemic, sirf Keibul-Lamjao National Park, Loktak Lake mein paaya jaata hai).\n[Q571, Q583]\n● Mallakhamb — Madhya Pradesh ne 2013 mein apna state sport declare kiya; \"Malla\" = wrestler, \"Khamb\" = pole\nse derive hua. Other traditional Indian games: Gilli Danda (Gujarat), Kho Kho aur Kabaddi (Tamil Nadu), Dhopkel"," (Assam), Kokla Chapaki (Punjab), Kambala (Karnataka), Jallikattu (Tamil Nadu). [Q577]\n3. City Nicknames\n● Kolkata — 'The City of Palaces' (British Raj ke time bani buildings ki wajah se). Jaipur = Pink City (1876 mein Prince\nAlbert ke swagat ke liye pink paint kiya gaya). Lucknow = City of Nawabs (Golden City of the East, Shiraz-i-Hind,\nConstantinople of India bhi kehte hain). [Q573]\n● Hyderabad — 'City of Pearls' (Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah ne found kiya). Other city nicknames: Pune — Queen of\nDeccan/Oxford of East; Bengaluru — Silicon Valley of India; Chennai — Detroit of Asia; Jamshedpur — Pittsburgh\nof India; Ahmedabad — Manchester of India; Ajmer — Khwaja ki Nagri; Nagpur — Orange City; Mysore —\nSandalwood City. [Q575, Q582]\n● Pampore — Kashmir ka \"Saffron Town\" — GI tag mila Kashmir ke saffron ko. Other nicknames: Pink City — Jaipur;\nDiamond City — Surat; Leather City — Kanpur; Orange City — Nagpur. [Q580]\n● Udaipur — 'Venice of the East' aur 'City of Lakes' (Fateh Sagar, Rang Sagar, Pichola, Swaroop Sagar, Dudh Talai\nlakes) — Maharana Udai Singh ne 1559 mein found kiya. Jodhpur — 'Blue City' (blue-painted houses old town\narea mein), Rao Jodha ne found kiya. Jaipur — Pink City; Ahmedabad — Manchester of India; Surat — Diamond\nCity of India. [Q588, Q604]\n● Sikkim ko actual inhabitants (Lepchas) apni bhasha mein 'Nye-Mal-Ale' (Heaven) kehte hain — Nepalese ise\nSukhim/New Home, Tibetans Denzong/Valley of Rice kehte hain. [Q590]\n4. Museums, Monuments, Forts & Heritage Sites\n● Gol Gumbaz — Karnataka mein sthit; duniya ka 2nd largest dome; Muhammed Adil Shah (Bijapur ke 7th ruler) ka\nmausoleum, architect Yaqut of Dabul ne 1656 mein banaya. Other Karnataka heritage: Hampi (UNESCO site),\nBidar Fort, Chennakesava Swamy Temple, Mysore Palace. [Q591]\n● Jawahar Kala Kendra — Rajasthan (Jaipur) mein, 9 planets ke theme par based, architect Charles Correa ne design\nkiya — Vastu Purusha Mandala principle follow karta hai. [Q570]\n● Indira Gandhi Memorial Tulip Garden — Srinagar mein, Asia ka sabse bada tulip garden, Zabarwan Range ki\nfoothills mein Dal Lake ke paas. [Q572]\n● Orchha heritage town — Madhya Pradesh mein, river Betwa ke kinare, King Rudra Pratap Singh ne 16th century\nmein banaya; UNESCO tentative list mein hai. MP ke UNESCO sites: Khajuraho (1986), Sanchi Stupa (1989),\nBhimbetka Rock Shelters (2003), Bhedaghat aur Satpura Tiger Reserve (2021). [Q586]\n● Mrignayani ka Mahal — Gwalior mein, Maharaja Man Singh Tomar ne apni Gujar queen Mrignayani ke liye\nbanaya — love ka monument mana jaata hai. Other historical monuments: Hawa Mahal (Jaipur), Lake Palace\n(Udaipur), Khajuraho Temples (MP), Samode Palace (Jaipur). [Q594]\n● Janjira Fort — Maharashtra mein hai (Madhya Pradesh mein NAHI). Other forts: Red Fort (Delhi), Agra Fort (UP),\nJaisalmer/Mehrangarh/Amber/Chittorgarh Forts (Rajasthan), Golconda Fort (Telangana), Kangra Fort (Himachal\nPradesh). [Q596]\n● Napier Museum — Kerala (Thiruvananthapuram) mein, 1855 mein establish, architect Robert Chisholm. Other\nKerala museums: Museum of Kerala History, Hill Palace Museum, Indo-Portuguese Museum. Other states: Albert\nHall Museum (Jaipur), Salar Jung Museum (Hyderabad), Dakshinachitra (Tamil Nadu). [Q597]\n● Namdroling Monastery — Karnataka mein, Tibetan Buddhism ke Nyingma lineage ka duniya ka sabse bada\nteaching center, 1963 mein Penor Rinpoche ne found kiya. Other monasteries: Tawang (Arunachal Pradesh),\nTabo (Himachal Pradesh), Rumtek (Sikkim), Hemis (Ladakh). [Q598]\n● India ka ekmatra Naval Aviation Museum — Goa mein, 12 October 1998 ko founded. [Q599]\n● Karla Caves — Maharashtra (Lonavala ke paas) mein preserved Buddhist rock-cut caves, Satavahana rule (2nd-5th\ncentury BC) ke dauraan banaye gaye, sabse purani cave 160 BC ki hai. [Q600]\n● Jantar Mantar — Jaipur ke founder Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II ne 5 jagah banaye: New Delhi, Jaipur, Ujjain,\nMathura, Varanasi — Nagpur mein Jantar Mantar NAHI hai. [Q589]"," ● Vivekananda Rock Memorial — Kanyakumari mein, 1970 mein banaya gaya, Laccadive Sea (Lakshadweep Sea) se\nghira hai — yahan Swami Vivekananda ne 3 din meditate kiya tha. [Q602]\n● Wing style architecture — West Bengal se related. Temple architecture styles: Nagara style (Himalayas-Vindhyas\nregion, e.g. Kandariya Mahadev Temple MP, Konark Sun Temple); Dravida style (gopuram entrance, e.g.\nKanchipuram/Thanjavur/Madurai temple towns); Vesara style (Nagara-Dravida mix). [Q607]\n● Ranikhet hill station — Uttarakhand ke Kumaun region mein. Other hill stations: Uttarakhand (Mussoorie,\nNainital, Dhanaulti, Chakrata); Himachal Pradesh (Shimla, Manali, Mashobra, McLeodganj, Dharamshala,\nDalhousie); Sikkim (Gangtok, Aritar); Kerala (Munnar, Ponmudi). [Q566]\n5. Institutes, Universities & Libraries\n● Tamil University — Thanjavur (Tamil Nadu) mein, 1981 mein establish, founder M.G. Ramachandran (poorv CM)\n— Tamil bhasha mein higher research ke liye. Tamil Nadu: capital Chennai, Legislative Assembly 234 seats, Lok\nSabha 39, Rajya Sabha 18, High Court Madras. [Q563]\n● Central AGMARK Laboratory — Nagpur mein sthit; AGMARK agricultural products ki quality assure karne wala\ncertification mark hai; 11 regional AGMARK labs bhi hain (Delhi, Kolkata, Mumbai, Jaipur, Amritsar, Kochi,\nKanpur, Guntur, Chennai, Bhopal, Rajkot). [Q579]\n● Institute of Road Traffic Education (IRTE) — Faridabad mein sthit, 1991 se research-based not-for-profit\norganization, road safety management ke liye kaam karti hai. [Q592]\n● Central Institute of Indian Language (CIIL) — Karnataka (Mysore) mein, 17 July 1969 ko founded, Indian languages\nke development ko coordinate karta hai — 5 Regional Language Centers bhi hain. [Q593]\n● National Library of India — Kolkata (Belvedere Estate, Alipore) mein, 1836 mein Calcutta Public Library ke roop\nmein sthapit, 1948 Act se National Library bana; Maulana Abul Kalam Azad ne 1 Feb 1953 ko public ke liye khola.\n[Q595]\n● Banaras Hindu University (BHU) — Uttar Pradesh (Varanasi) mein, Pandit Madan Mohan Malviya ne 1916 mein\nfound kiya. Other universities: Nalanda University (Bihar, 427 AD), Aligarh Muslim University (UP, 1877),\nUniversity of Calcutta (WB, 1857), Allahabad University (UP, 1887). [Q605]\n6. Culture, Dance, Art & Festivals\n● Khamba-Thoibi — Manipur ke Moirang kingdom ka classical epic-based folk dance, Meitei language mein\nKhamba-Thoibi ki love story par based. Manipur ke other dances: Manipuri, Nupa, Pung Cholam, Dhol Cholam,\nManipuri Raas Leela. [Q569]\n● Kochi-Muziris Biennale (Kerala) — Contemporary art ki exhibition, desh ki sabse badi art exhibition aur Asia ka\nsabse bada contemporary art festival, 12 December 2012 ko shuru hua. [Q610]\n7. Infrastructure — Bridges, Tunnels, Airports & Transport\n● Chennai Mofussil Bus Terminus — Asia ka sabse bada bus terminus, Koyambedu mein 37 acres mein phaila hai.\nWorld ka sabse bada bus depot — Millennium Park Bus Depot (Delhi); world ka sabse bada bus station — Preston\nBus Station (UK). [Q576]\n● Jalandhar (Punjab) — garrison town (cantonment town) hai — British period mein military support ke liye\nestablish. Other garrison towns: Ambala (Haryana), Mhow (MP), Babina (UP), Ramgarh (Jharkhand). [Q587]\n● Byorung Bridge — Arunachal Pradesh mein, river Siang par, India ka sabse lamba (300m) single-lane steel cable\nsuspension bridge, DoNER Ministry ke funding se bana. Other bridges: Assam (Bogibeel, Bhupen Hazarika Setu),\nManipur (Imphal River Bridge), Mizoram (Chite Bridge). [Q584]\n● Pir Panjal (Banihal) Railway Tunnel — Jammu & Kashmir mein, 11.2 km lambi, India ki ekmatra broad gauge\nmountain railway tunnel, Quazigund-Baramulla ke beech. Other J&K tunnels: Shyama Prasad Mukherjee Tunnel"," (9km), Nandni Tunnels (1.4km), Jawahar Tunnel (2.85km). [Q608]\n● Gujarat — India ka sabse zyada airports wala state (Ahmedabad, Vadodara, Bhavnagar, Bhuj, Gandhidham,\nMundra, Porbandar, Surat, Keshod). International airports mein Kerala top par hai (4 airports: Kannur, Cochin,\nThiruvananthapuram, Calicut). [Q609]\n8. Food & Culinary Specialties\n● Nagpur — oranges ke liye famous. Other fruit cities/states: Apple bowl of India — Kotgarh (Himachal Pradesh);\nGrapes — Nasik (Maharashtra); Litchi — Muzaffarpur (Bihar); Pomegranate — Solapur; Strawberry —\nMahabaleshwar; Alphonso Mangoes — Ratnagiri; Bananas — Jalgaon; Guavas — Allahabad; Anjeer — Pune;\nPapaya — Anantapur; Plum — Himachal Pradesh. [Q568]\n● Chainsoo — Uttarakhand (Garhwal region) ki famous dal (Urad/Kali Dal) preparation. Other famous foods:\nUttarakhand (Kumaoni Raita, Gahat ki Dal, Kafuli, Aloo ke Gutke, Baadi); Arunachal Pradesh (Pika Pila, Lukter,\nPehak); Maharashtra (Bhaji, Vada Pav, Misal Pav); Telangana (Sarva Pindi, Sakinalu). [Q603]\n● Khandvi — Gujarat ki delicacy (gram flour + yogurt). Gujarat ki other delicacies: Dhokla, Thepla, Undhiyu, Aam\nShrikhand. Other states: Maharashtra (Vada Pav, Puran Poli, Modak); Karnataka (Masala Dosa, Mysore Pak, Korri\nGassi); Odisha (Mudhi Mansa, Kora Khai, Palua Ladu). [Q606]\n9. Wildlife & Natural Resources\n● Hydrotherapy treatment centre for elephants — Mathura mein (UP Forest Department + Wildlife SOS\ncollaboration), arthritis/joint pain/foot ailment ke liye high-pressure water jets se treatment. Project Elephant\n1992 mein launched hua; National Elephant Day = 13 March, World Elephant Day = 12 August. Elephant reserves:\nMayur Jharna (WB), Singhbhum (Jharkhand), Mayurbhanj (Odisha), Terai (UP). [Q581]\n● Arunachal Pradesh — India ka highest graphite reserve wala state (GSI 2019 report ke anusaar ~35% total\nreserve), uske baad J&K, Odisha, Jharkhand, Tamil Nadu. Graphite ek-matra non-metal hai jo electricity ka good\nconductor hai. GSI 1851 mein set up hua tha, HQ Kolkata. [Q585]\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Jantar Mantar Nagpur mein NAHI hai — 5 jagah hai: New Delhi, Jaipur, Ujjain, Mathura, Varanasi. [Q589]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Janjira Fort Maharashtra mein hai, Madhya Pradesh mein NAHI. [Q596]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Quicklime/Nicknames confuse mat karna — Jaipur = Pink City; Jodhpur = Blue City; Udaipur = Venice of\nEast/City of Lakes; Hyderabad = City of Pearls; Kolkata = City of Palaces; Chennai = Detroit of Asia. [Q573, Q575,\nQ582, Q588, Q604]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Sangai deer sirf Manipur mein paaya jaata hai (Keibul-Lamjao National Park) — India ka koi aur state\nnahi. [Q583]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Arunachal Pradesh 1972 tak North East Frontier Agency (NEFA) kehlata tha —\nMeghalaya/Nagaland/Mizoram alag naamon se nahi jaane jaate the. [Q578]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Gujarat = sabse zyada total airports; Kerala = sabse zyada international airports — dono alag records\nhain. [Q609]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 15 States GK Full Mind Map (Q562-Q610)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0431","t":"16 Organisation","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — ORGANISATION — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Language & Literature Organisations\n2. Indian Research, Science & Ancient Institutions\n3. Indian Regulatory, Financial & Standard Bodies\n4. Indian Government / Statutory / Defence Organisations\n5. United Nations (UN) — Complete Facts\n6. UN Agencies & International Org Headquarters\n7. Regional & Economic Groups\n8. Social, Cultural & NGOs\n9. Trade Unions & Labour Organisations\n10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Language & Literature Organisations\n● CIIL (Central Institute of Indian Languages) — Mysuru, establish 17 July 1969, Ministry of Education ke under. Iske\n7 centres: Eastern (Bhubaneswar), Northern (Patiala), North Eastern (Guwahati), Southern (Mysuru), Urdu\nTeaching & Research (Lucknow & Solan), Western (Pune). [Q611]\n● Kendriya Hindi Sansthan — HQ Agra, establish 1960. 8 centres: Delhi (1970), Hyderabad (1976), Guwahati (1978),\nShillong (1987), Mysore (1988), Dimapur (2003), Bhubaneswar (2003), Ahmedabad (2006). World Hindi Day — 10\nJanuary. [Q612]\n● Sahitya Akademi — India's National Academy of Letters, New Delhi, establish 12 March 1954. 24 Indian languages\n+ English. Regional offices: Kolkata, Bangalore, Chennai, Mumbai, Agartala. [Q613, Q629]\n● English and Foreign Languages University (EFLU) — Hyderabad, establish 1958. [Q616]\n● Mahatma Gandhi Antarrashtriya Hindi VishwaVidyalaya — Wardha (Maharashtra), establish 1997. [Q616, Q619]\n● Shri Lal Bahadur Shastri Rashtriya Sanskrit Vidyapeetha — New Delhi, 1962. [Q616]\n● Rashtriya Sanskrit Vidyapeetha — Tirupati, 1961. [Q616]\n● Maulana Azad National Urdu University — Hyderabad, 1998. [Q616]\n● Rashtriya Sanskrit Sansthan — New Delhi, 1970. [Q616]\n● Sree Sankaracharya University of Sanskrit — Kalady, Kerala, establish 1993. [Q620]\n● Centre of Excellence for Studies in Classical Telugu (CESCT) — CIIL, Mysore ke under 21 January 2020 ko establish,\nab Nellore (Andhra Pradesh) shift ho gayi hai. [Q623]\n2. Indian Research, Science & Ancient Institutions\n● ICAR (Indian Council of Agricultural Research) — autonomous, HQ New Delhi, establish 16 July 1929. ICAR-IIHR\n(Indian Institute of Horticultural Research) Bengaluru mein hai. [Q615]\n● IITM (Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology) — Pune, establish 17 November 1962. [Q617]\n● Central Potato Research Institute (CPRI) — pehle Patna (1949) mein thi, 1956 mein Shimla shift hui. [Q626]\n● Central Drug Research Institute — Lucknow, inaugurate 17 Feb 1951. [Q631]\n● Zoological Survey of India (ZSI) — Kolkata, establish 1 July 1916, nodal ministry: MoEFCC, 16 regional stations.\n[Q660]\n● Botanical Survey of India — Kolkata, establish 13 February 1890. [Q660]\n● Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) — New Delhi, establish 1861, founder & first DG: Alexander Cunningham."," [Q708]\n● Atomic Energy Commission of India — Mumbai, set up August 1948. Iske 5 research centres: BARC-Trambey\n(Mumbai), IGCAR-Kalpakkam (TN), RRCAT-Indore (MP), VECC-Kolkata (WB), AMD-Hyderabad. DAE 3 August 1954\nko establish hua. [Q723]\n● Central Rice Research Institute — Cuttack (Odisha). Other key institutes: IARI-New Delhi, NSRI-Kanpur, CCRI-\nKasargod (Kerala), NDRI-Karnal (Haryana), CTRI-Rajahmundry (AP), NIO-Panaji (Goa), CJTRI-Kolkata, NEERI-\nNagpur, NBRI-Lucknow. [Q626, Q731]\n● Indian Institute of Petroleum (CSIR-IIP) — Dehradun, establish 1960. Dehradun mein aur bhi: Survey of India,\nForest Research Institute, Wildlife Institute of India (WII), IIRS. [Q733]\n● Odantapuri University — Bihar mein thi. Ye ek Buddhist Mahavihara thi jo 8th century mein Pala Emperor Gopala\nne establish ki. Nalanda ke baad 2nd oldest Mahavihara, Magadha region mein. [Q736]\n● IGRMS (Indira Gandhi Rashtriya Manav Sangrahalaya) — Bhopal, MP. Isse National Museum of Anthropology bhi\nkehte hain. Man aur culture ke evolution ki integrated story present karta hai. [Q738]\n3. Indian Regulatory, Financial & Standard Bodies\n● BIS (Bureau of Indian Standards) — BIS Act 1986 se establish hua, effective 23 December 1986. Ministry of\nConsumer Affairs, Food & Public Distribution, HQ New Delhi. 5 Regional Offices: Kolkata (Eastern), Chennai\n(Southern), Mumbai (Western), Chandigarh (Northern), Delhi (Central). [Q728]\n● BRICS Economic Research Annual Awards EXIM Bank ne institute kiya. EXIM Bank: 1982, Mumbai. IDBI: 1964,\nMumbai. NABARD: 1982, Mumbai. SEBI: 1988, Mumbai. [Q732]\n● EPCH (Export Promotion Council for Handicrafts) — non-profit, 1986, HQ New Delhi. [Q734]\n● TRAI (Telecom Regulatory Authority of India) — TRAI Act 1997, Ministry of Communications & IT, HQ New Delhi.\n[Q735]\n● NSSO (National Sample Survey Organisation) — establish 1950 by Indian Statistical Institute. 4 divisions: SDRD,\nFOD, DPD, CPD. SDRD & DPD ka HQ Kolkata. [Q669]\n● NCDRC (National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission) — establish 1988 under Consumer Protection Act\n1986, HQ New Delhi, quasi-judicial body. [Q625]\n● e-Sahaj portal — Ministry of Home Affairs ne 2018 mein launch kiya, security clearance ke liye. [Q662]\n4. Indian Government / Statutory / Defence Organisations\n● BRO (Border Roads Organisation) — founded May 1960, HQ New Delhi, founder Jawaharlal Nehru, pehle Road\nTransport Ministry ke under tha, 2015 se Defence Ministry ke under. Role: border areas & friendly neighbors\n(Afghanistan, Bhutan, Myanmar, Sri Lanka) mein motorable roads. [Q643, Q645, Q666]\n● PCRA (Petroleum Conservation Research Association) — establish 1978, Ministry of Petroleum & Natural Gas, HQ\nNew Delhi. [Q621]\n● Indira Gandhi National Centre for Arts — New Delhi, autonomous under Ministry of Culture, founded 19 Nov\n1985 by Rajiv Gandhi. [Q654]\n● NTA (National Testing Agency) — establish 2017, autonomous testing org for entrance exams. [Q686]\n● Jan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS) — Ministry of Skill Development & Entrepreneurship, old name Shramik Vidyapeeth,\n2000 mein rename hua. Annual beneficiaries ~4 lakh (85% women). [Q614, Q628]\n● National Research Foundation (NRF) — NEP 2020 ke under envisaged autonomous body. [Q622]\n● ISA (International Solar Alliance) — 2015 mein founded, Gurugram (Haryana) HQ — pehla treaty-based\nintergovernmental org India-based. [Q638]\n● Niryat Mitra app — FIEO dwara develop, Commerce Ministry ke under. [Q650]\n● Defence ke key orgs: Intelligence Bureau (IB) — form 1887, HQ New Delhi, MHA, motto \"Jagritam Aharnisham\".\nCoast Guard — 18 Aug 1978, motto \"Vayam Raksamah\". Indian Army — 26 Jan 1950, motto \"Seva Paramo"," Dharmah\". RAW — 21 Sep 1968, motto \"Dharmo Raksati Raksitah\". [Q702]\n● Air Sports Federation of India — apex governing body of air sports. [Q624]\n5. United Nations (UN) — Complete Facts\n● UN establish — 24 October 1945, HQ New York, founding members 51 (50 ne 26 June 1945 ko sign kiya, 51st\nPoland 15 Oct 1945 ko). India founding member tha. Ab 193 member states hain, newest South Sudan (193rd).\n[Q642, Q671, Q693, Q694, Q696, Q699]\n● UN ke 6 principal organs: (1) General Assembly, (2) Security Council, (3) Economic and Social Council, (4)\nTrusteeship Council, (5) International Court of Justice, (6) Secretariat. [Q635, Q642, Q682, Q687, Q694, Q699, Q705]\n● Trusteeship Council — 1994 mein suspend kar diya gaya tha. [Q635]\n● Human Rights Council (UNHRC) — 15 March 2006 ko create hui, ye principal organ nahi hai UN ka. [Q687]\n● Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR) — adopt hua 10 December 1948 ko Paris mein, 30 articles hain.\n[Q688]\n● UN ko Nobel Peace Prize 2001 mein mila (Kofi Annan ke saath). [Q667]\n● UN ka naam pehli baar 1 January 1942 mein Franklin D. Roosevelt ne diya tha. [Q699, Q719]\n● UN General Assembly har saal September mein full session bulati hai. [Q711]\n● Joint Inspection Unit (JIU) — UN system ka only independent external oversight body, 28 participating\norganizations, UNGA ne 1976 mein Statute adopt kiya, implement 1978. [Q636]\n● Vijay Lakshmi Pandit — UN General Assembly ki 8vi President aur pehli mahila President thi (1953-1954). [Q714]\n● UN ne 'Charter of Economic Rights and Duties of States' December 1974 mein adopt kiya. Pehli baar Mexico ke\nPresident Luis Echeverria ne UNCTAD ke 3rd session (Santiago, Chile) mein propose kiya tha. [Q717]\n● ICJ (International Court of Justice) — UN ka principal judicial organ, Hague (Netherlands) mein situated. Ismein 15\njudges hain jo 9-year terms ke liye elect hote hain. [Q721]\n● UNSSC (UN System Staff College) — 1 January 2002 ko founded, HQ Turin (Italy), second campus Bonn (Germany).\n[Q724]\n● UNIDO — UNGA ne 1966 mein Resolution 2152 (XXI) pass karke establish kiya. Mission: developing countries ka\nindustrialization promote karna. HQ Vienna. [Q725]\n● UNDP — 22 November 1965 ko founded, HQ New York. Parent org: ECOSOC. [Q727]\n● League of Nations ko \"Child of War\" kaha jaata hai — WWI ke baad bana tha. President Woodrow Wilson ne\nintroduce kiya, HQ Geneva. [Q730]\n● UNSC non-permanent members 2 saal ke liye elect hote hain. 1965 se 10 non-permanent hain (pehle 6 the). 5\npermanent: China, France, Russia, UK, USA. UNSC ka HQ bhi New York mein hai (UN establish 24 Oct 1945 ke\nsaath); total 15 members (5 permanent + 10 non-permanent) — October 2020 tak ye composition same rahi.\n[Q713, Q627, Q632, Q634, Q663, Q668, Q675, Q676, Q683]\n● UN ki 6 official languages: Arabic, Chinese, English, French, Russian, Spanish — sabhi official UN documents in\nlanguages mein available hote hain. [Q658]\n● Dag Hammarskjold (UN ke 2nd Secretary-General, Sweden, 1953-1961) ka famous quote: \"The United Nations\nwas not created to take mankind/humanity to heaven, but to save it from hell.\" [Q649, Q712]\n● UN Secretaries-General list: Trygve Lie (1946-1952, Norway), Dag Hammarskjold (1953-1961, Sweden), U Thant\n(1961-1971, Myanmar), Kofi Annan (1997-2006, Ghana), Ban Ki-moon (2007-2016, Korea). [Q710]\n● 2019 ko United Nations ne \"International Year of Indigenous Languages\" declare kiya tha — knowledge-sharing,\ncapacity building aur indigenous languages ko mainstream mein integrate karne ke liye. [Q697]\n● 26 organisations UN system ka part hain India mein — jaise APCTT, FAO, IFAD, ILO, IMF, IOM, UNDP, UNEP,\nUNESCO, UNFPA, UN-HABITAT, UNHCR, UNICEF, UNIDO, UNODC, UN Women, WFP, WHO, World Bank. [Q637]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Germany UN ka founding member nahi hai — 1945 mein naya Germany nahi tha sign karne wala. [Q694]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Louise Frechette kabhi UN Secretary-General nahi bani — wo Deputy Secretary-General thi 1998-2006.\n[Q685]"," 6. UN Agencies & International Org Headquarters\n● UNESCO — Paris, establish 16 November 1945. IIEP iska part hai. [Q630, Q641, Q672]\n● UNICEF — New York, establish 11 December 1946. Full form: United Nations International Children's Emergency\nFund. 192 countries mein present. [Q633, Q681]\n● UNFPA — New York, establish 1969, reproductive health. [Q659]\n● UNDP — New York, establish 1966. [Q659]\n● UN University — Tokyo, Japan, establish 1972. [Q653]\n● ILO — Geneva, establish 1919, UN ki specialized agency 1946, Nobel Peace Prize 1969. [Q648, Q690]\n● WHO — Geneva, establish 7 April 1948. [Q670]\n● World Bank — Washington DC, create 1944, 189 members. [Q670, Q674]\n● IMF — Washington DC, establish 1944, world currencies exchange regulate karta hai. [Q674, Q737]\n● WTO — Geneva, establish 1995. [Q644, Q680]\n● FAO — Rome, establish October 1945, 197 members. [Q651]\n● UNEP — Nairobi, Kenya, establish 5 June 1972. [Q692]\n● UNODC — Vienna, establish 1997. [Q691]\n● ICAO — Montreal, Canada, establish 7 December 1944. [Q703]\n● UNWTO — Madrid, Spain, establish 1946. [Q709]\n● INTERPOL — as ICPC 1923 mein Vienna, ab HQ Lyon (France). India 1949 se member. [Q657]\n● Amnesty International — London, founded July 1961, Nobel Peace Prize 1977. [Q646]\n● ICRC (Red Cross) — Geneva, establish 17 February 1863, founder Jean Henry Dunant, Nobel Peace Prize 1901. Ye\nUN agency nahi hai — headquarters bhi Geneva mein hi hai. [Q689, Q701, Q718]\n● WIPO — Geneva, establish 14 July 1967. [Q659]\n● World Food Programme — Rome, establish 19 December 1961. [Q689]\n● UNHCR — Geneva, establish 1950. [Q681]\n● IUCN Red List — 9 categories hain. IUCN establish 5 Oct 1948, HQ Gland (Switzerland). [Q715]\n● WWF — 1961, HQ Gland (Switzerland). [Q715]\n● IRENA — HQ Abu Dhabi, founded 26 January 2009. [Q726]\n● International Rice Research Institute — HQ Los Banos (Philippines). India ke rice research institutes: Indian\nInstitute of Rice Research (1965, Rajendra Nagar, Hyderabad); Central Rice Research Institute (1946, Cuttack,\nOdisha, ICAR ke under). [Q656]\n● Bretton Woods institutions — IMF aur World Bank Group (1944 Bretton Woods Conference se bane, \"twins of\nBretton Woods\" kehte hain); United Nations Bretton Woods institution NAHI hai — UN alag 1945 mein bana.\n[Q695]\n7. Regional & Economic Groups\n● BRICS — Brazil, Russia, India, China, South Africa (2010 mein add). Founded 2009, HQ Shanghai. Pehli summit\nYekaterinburg (Russia) 16 June 2009. [Q655]\n● SCO (Shanghai Cooperation Organisation) — founded 15 June 2001, HQ Beijing. 8 members. India observer 2005,\nfull member 9 June 2017 (Astana). [Q664]\n● ASEAN — founded 8 August 1967 Bangkok, HQ Jakarta, 10 members. Founding: Indonesia, Malaysia, Philippines,\nSingapore, Thailand. Baad mein: Brunei, Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Vietnam. Motto: \"One Vision, One Identity,\nOne Community\". [Q639, Q704]\n● SAARC — founded 8 December 1985 Dhaka, HQ Kathmandu, 8 members (Afghanistan 2007 mein add); SAARC"," Secretariat 1987 mein Kathmandu mein hi set up hua tha. [Q684, Q706, Q729]\n● SAFTA — South Asian Free Trade Area, SAARC ka free trade arrangement. [Q684]\n● BIMSTEC — founded 6 June 1997, HQ Dhaka. 7 members: Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Myanmar,\nThailand. Maldives member nahi hai. [Q700, Q707]\n● India & Bhutan BRI mein participate nahi karte (China's Belt & Road Initiative). [Q700]\n● G7 — world's largest IMF advanced economies: France, Germany, Italy, Japan, USA, UK, Canada. Founded 1975,\npresidency rotate hoti hai. [Q677]\n● EU (European Union) — Maastricht Treaty 1993 se officially establish, 27 member states, HQ Brussels. Driving\nforce: European Commission. [Q678, Q698]\n● Commonwealth of Nations — political association, 54 member countries (mostly formerly British Empire).\nFounded 11 December 1931, HQ London. [Q722]\n● OPEC — Baghdad, Iraq mein 1960 mein founded. Founding 5: Iran, Iraq, Kuwait, Saudi Arabia, Venezuela. India\nmember nahi hai. [Q720]\n● SAARC Development Fund (SDF) — HQ Thimphu, Bhutan. \"Regional financing mechanism\" ke roop mein kaam\nkarta hai — Economic, Infrastructure aur Social Windows. [Q716]\n● Lithuania — Soviet Republic (USSR) mein se sabse pehle apni independence declare karne wala desh tha\n(referendum December 1991 mein formalize hua); USSR 15 republics ka federal state tha, 1917 Russian\nRevolution ke baad establish hua. [Q647]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: India ASEAN ka member nahi hai. [Q704]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Agenda 21 — 1992 UNCED (Earth Summit) Rio de Janeiro mein sign hua, sustainable development ke\nliye. [Q652]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: SDG 2030 mein \"population 1/3 reduce\" koi goal nahi hai. [Q673]\n8. Social, Cultural & NGOs\n● The Humsafar Trust — Mumbai ka cafe \"Bambai Nazariya\" ko support karta hai, trans/non-binary employment\npromote karta hai. [Q618]\n● Sahayatrika — Kerala origin lesbian/bisexual women & transgender persons ke liye. [Q618]\n● Sambhavana Society — gender, age, sexual preference, psychosocial issues ke stigma ke against kaam karti hai.\n[Q618]\n● Sahodari Foundation — underprivileged transgender women ke liye counselling/support. [Q618]\n● Kailash Satyarthi — Nobel Peace Prize 2014, Bachpan Bachao Andolan (1980) se associated. [Q640]\n● Beti Bachao Beti Padhao — launch 22 Jan 2015 Panipat, Haryana. [Q640]\n● CRY (Child Rights and You) — Rippan Kapur ne 1979 mein establish kiya. [Q665]\n● PETA India — start 2000, world ka largest animal rights org, founded 1980 by Ingrid Newkirk & Alex Pacheco.\n[Q661]\n9. Trade Unions & Labour Organisations\n● AITUC (All India Trade Union Congress) — India ka sabse purana trade union, founded 31 Oct 1920, first president\nLala Lajpat Rai, CPI se associated. [Q679]\n● INTUC — founded 3 May 1947. [Q679]\n● CITU — founded 1970. [Q679]"," 10.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️UN ke 6 principal organs hain, lekin Human Rights Council principal organ nahi hai — ye 2006 mein separately\ncreate hui thi. [Q687]\n●\n\n⚠️Trusteeship Council 1994 mein suspend ho gayi — officially 6 hi hain. [Q635]\n●\n\n⚠️Red Cross (ICRC) UN agency nahi hai — independent humanitarian org hai, Geneva based. [Q701]\n●\n\n⚠️BRICS mein South Africa 2010 mein add hua, pehle sirf BRIC tha. [Q655]\n●\n\n⚠️BIMSTEC mein Maldives nahi hai — 7 members hain. [Q707]\n●\n\n⚠️India ASEAN ka member nahi hai. [Q704]\n●\n\n⚠️Germany UN founding member nahi hai — WWII ke baad divided tha. [Q694]\n●\n\n⚠️Louise Frechette Deputy SG thi, SG nahi. [Q685]\n●\n\n⚠️NSSO ka \"National Development Agenda\" division nahi hai — 4 divisions: SDRD, FOD, DPD, CPD. [Q669]\n●\n\n⚠️SDG 2030 mein \"population 1/3 reduce\" koi goal nahi hai. [Q673]\n●\n\n⚠️BRO 2015 se Defence Ministry ke under hai, pehle Road Transport ke under tha. [Q666]\n●\n\n⚠️BIS 2010 mein establish nahi hua — ye 1986 mein BIS Act se establish hua tha, effective 23 Dec 1986. [Q728]\n●\n\n⚠️UNSC mein non-permanent members 1 ya 3 saal ke liye nahi, balki 2 saal ke liye elect hote hain. [Q713]\n●\n\n⚠️League of Nations \"Child of War\" hai — WWI ke baad bana, WWII se pehle fail ho gaya. [Q730]\n●\n\n⚠️India OPEC ka member nahi hai. [Q720]\n●\n\n⚠️Commonwealth sirf political association hai — human rights, economic ya social association nahi hai by\ndefinition. [Q722]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 16 Organisation Full Mind Map (Q611-Q738)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0432","t":"17 World GK","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — WORLD G.K. — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. World Geography, Landmarks & Monuments\n2. Human Races, Tribes & Indigenous Peoples\n3. Countries, Capitals, Currencies & Nicknames\n4. World History — Wars, Treaties & Events\n5. Famous World Personalities\n6. Miscellaneous Facts\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. World Geography, Landmarks & Monuments\n● Palm Jumeirah — UAE (Dubai) mein bana artificial island, land reclamation se Persian Gulf mein extend kiya gaya.\nEarly 21st century mein bana, Dubai ke petroleum income se finance hua. [Q739]\n● Machu Picchu — Peru mein located Inca ruins, isse \"Lost City of the Incas\" kehte hain kyunki 1500s mein\nSpaniards ne ise conquer karne ke baad bhi discover nahi kiya. [Q759]\n● Forbidden City — Beijing, China mein situated hai. Ye Ming aur Qing dynasties ke time imperial palace ka kaam\nkarti thi. [Q755]\n● Christ the Redeemer statue — Brazil (Rio de Janeiro) mein hai. Designer: Brazilian engineer Heitor da Silva Costa,\nsculptor: French sculptor Paul Landowski. [Q764]\n● Freedom Trail — Boston, USA mein 2.5 mile long historic passage hai. Boston Common (America's oldest public\npark) se start hota hai aur Charlestown Navy Yard mein USS Constitution pe end hota hai. American Revolution ki\ninsight deta hai. [Q765]\n● Pittsburgh industrial region — USA mein hai, \"Steel industry\" ke liye famous. Jamshedpur ko \"Pittsburgh of India\"\nkehte hain because of largest iron and steel industry. [Q761]\n● New York City — Hudson river ke mouth pe located hai. London — Thames, Paris — Seine, Cairo — Nile. [Q762]\n2. Human Races, Tribes & Indigenous Peoples\n● Pygmies — Central Africa, mainly Congo ke hunter-gatherers hain. [Q740]\n● Bedouin — Middle Eastern deserts ke nomadic Arab tribes, especially North Africa, Arabian Peninsula, Egypt,\nIsrael, Iraq, Syria, Jordan. [Q740]\n● Ainu — Japan ke Hokkaido island ke indigenous people. [Q740]\n● Kyrgyz — Central Asia ke Turkic-speaking people, mostly Kyrgyzstan mein rehte hain. [Q740]\n● Negroid race (Black/Woolen haired people) — Africa ki indigenous hai. [Q741]\n● Australoid race — Australia, Melanesia, Southeast Asia ke parts. [Q741]\n● Mongoloid race (Oriental/Amerindian) — Chinese, Japanese etc. [Q741]\n● Caucasoid race (White) — Europe, North Africa, Horn of Africa, West Asia, Central & South Asia ke parts. [Q741]\n● Georges Cuvier (1828) ne 3 distinct human races identify ki thi skin colour ke basis pe: Caucasoid (white), Negroid\n(black), Mongoloid (yellow). [Q745]\n● Chakma refugees — Bangladesh (Chittagong Hill Tracts) se India aaye hain. Mizoram, Arunachal Pradesh, Tripura,\nAssam mein rehte hain. Rohingyas — Myanmar se aaye. [Q744]\n● Israel ki major population Jewish (Yehudi) hai — Judaism religion. Holy place: Jerusalem (Israel ka capital). Israel:\nMiddle East, Mediterranean Sea ke eastern coastline pe, neighbours: Lebanon, Syria, Jordan, Egypt. Official"," language: Hebrew, Currency: Shekel. [Q743]\n3. Countries, Capitals, Currencies & Nicknames\n● Bhutan — Capital Thimphu, world ka only carbon negative country, \"Land of Thunderbolt\". National Animal:\nTakin, National Bird: Tibetan Raven, National Flower: Blue Poppy, National Sport: Archery, Currency: Ngultrum.\n[Q746]\n● Nepal — Kathmandu, Myanmar — Nay Pyi Daw, Bangladesh — Dhaka. [Q746]\n● Kazakhstan — Capital Astana (pehle Nur-Sultan). Bishkek Kyrgyzstan ki capital hai. [Q752]\n● Libya — Tripoli, Bahamas — Nassau, Belgium — Brussels. [Q752]\n● Macau — Currency Pataca. Laos — Laotian Kip, Mexico — Peso, Panama — Balboa. [Q758]\n● North Korea — \"Hermit Kingdom\", world's most isolated country. Capital: Pyongyang. [Q754]\n● Japan — \"Land of Rising Sun\". [Q754]\n● Thailand — \"Land of White Elephants\", National symbol: Elephant, Capital: Bangkok. [Q754, Q763]\n● Sri Lanka — \"India's Teardrop\". [Q763]\n● Egypt — \"Gift of Nile\". [Q763]\n● Finland — \"Land of Thousand Lakes\". [Q749, Q763]\n● Australia — \"Land of Golden Fleece\". [Q763]\n● Gurdwara Panja Sahib — Pakistan (Hasan Abdal) mein located hai. Guru Nanak ji ka handprint ek rock pe\nimprinted hai. [Q753]\n● Shogatsu — Japan ka New Year festival, 1 January se 3 January tak celebrate hota hai. Isse Oshogatsu, Omisoka,\nOtsugomori bhi kehte hain. [Q747]\n4. World History — Wars, Treaties & Events\n● WWII (1939-1945) mein Allied Powers: USA, Soviet Union, Britain, France. Axis Powers: Germany, Italy, Japan.\n[Q757]\n● USSR (1922-1991) — 15 national republics ka federal union tha. Former USSR countries: Armenia, Azerbaijan,\nBelarus, Estonia, Georgia, Moldova, Russia, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Latvia, Lithuania, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan,\nUkraine, Uzbekistan. [Q749]\n● Brexit word Peter Wilding ne invent kiya tha — British lawyer aur British Influence think tank ke founder. 2012\nmein UK ke EU se potential exit ke context mein use kiya. [Q748]\n● Magna Carta (Charter of Liberties) — 1215 AD mein England mein sign hua. Citizens ke Fundamental Rights ka\npehla written document tha. Royal authority ko limit karne ke liye law ko power establish kiya. [Q767]\n● Gettysburg Address — Abraham Lincoln ne 19 November 1863 ko diya tha. Ye American Civil War ke time Union\nki victory ke baad diya gaya tha. Lincoln 16th US President (1861-1865) the. [Q766]\n5. Famous World Personalities\n● Eleanor Roosevelt — USA se thi, 1946 mein UDHR (Universal Declaration of Human Rights) ki chairperson appoint\nki gayi thi. [Q756]\n● Kurt Waldheim — Austrian politician/diplomat, 4th UN Secretary-General (1972-1981), baad mein Austria ke\nPresident (1986-1992) bane. [Q760]\n● Grover Cleveland — USA ke only President jinhone do non-consecutive terms serve kiye: 22nd President (1885-\n89) aur 24th President (1893-97). [Q768]"," ● Marie Antoinette — France ki last queen, Austria mein janmi thi. Holy Roman Emperor Francis I aur Habsburg\nEmpress Maria Theresa ki beti thi. [Q769]\n● Noura al-Matroushi — UAE ki pehli female astronaut, Emirati engineer. Other female astronauts: Sunita Williams\n(USA), Kalpana Chawla (Indian origin pehli), Valentina Tereshkova (Soviet Union), Chiaki Mukai (Japan), Sirisha\nBandla (2nd Indian-born American). [Q742]\n6. Miscellaneous Facts\n● Brazil — world ka biggest coffee producer. Vietnam 2nd, Colombia 3rd. India Asia mein major producer hai,\nKarnataka sabse bada producing state. [Q750]\n● Abyssinia — Ethiopia ka purana naam. Ye Horn of Africa mein landlocked country hai, capital: Addis Ababa. Aur\nbhi ancient names: Constantinople (Istanbul), Burma (Myanmar), Edo (Tokyo), Kampuchea (Cambodia), Formosa\n(Taiwan), Persia (Iran). [Q751]\n7.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Georges Cuvier ne sirf 3 races identify ki thi: Caucasoid, Negroid, Mongoloid. Laplanderiod inmein se nahi hai.\n[Q745]\n●\n\n⚠️Finland former USSR ka part nahi tha — ye \"Land of Thousand Lakes\" hai. [Q749]\n●\n\n⚠️Kazakhstan ki capital Astana hai (pehle Nur-Sultan), Bishkek nahi — Bishkek toh Kyrgyzstan ki capital hai.\n[Q752]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 17 World GK Full Mind Map (Q739-Q769)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0433","t":"18 Full Form","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FULL FORM — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Government Schemes & Yojanas\n2. Technology, IT & Digital Initiatives\n3. Organisations, Institutions & Bodies\n4. Financial, Sports & Miscellaneous\n5.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Government Schemes & Yojanas\n● ESIC — Employees' State Insurance Corporation — Ministry of Labour and Employment ke under statutory social\nsecurity body. Formed 24 February 1952, HQ New Delhi. Dusra body hai EPFO (Employees' Provident Fund\nOrganisation). [Q770]\n● SJSRY — Swarna Jayanti Shahari Rozgar Yojana — 1 December 1997 ko launch hui. Ismein teen purani yojanayen\nmerge hui: Nehru Rozgar Yojana (NRY), Urban Basic Services for the Poor (UBSP), PMIUPEP. Urban\nunemployed/underemployed poor ko self-employment aur wage employment provide karti hai. [Q772]\n● JNNURM — Jawaharlal Nehru National Urban Renewal Mission — 3 December 2005 ko launch, 2014 mein band\nhui. Baad mein AMRUT (Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation) ke naam se June 2015 mein\nPM Modi ne relaunch kiya. Ministry of Urban Affairs ke under thi. [Q776]\n● PMGDISHA — Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan — 2017 mein Ministry of Electronics &\nInformation Technology ne launch kiya. 6 crore rural households ko digital literacy dena hai, 14-60 years age\ngroup. [Q777]\n● NRDWP — National Rural Drinking Water Programme — 2009 mein launch, Ministry of Jal Shakti ke under. Har\nrural person ko safe aur adequate drinking water provide karna hai on a sustainable basis. [Q785]\n2. Technology, IT & Digital Initiatives\n● ISDN — Integrated Services Digital Network — high-speed fully digitized telephone service, circuit-switched\ntelephone network system. Voice aur data ka digital transmission allow karti hai. Services: Bearer services,\nTeleservices (telephony, telefax, teleconferencing), Supplementary services (reverse charging, call waiting,\nmessage handling). [Q773]\n● ATL — Atal Tinkering Lab — Atal Innovation Mission dwara schools mein establish kiya gaya. Vision: 1 Million\nchildren ko Neoteric Innovators banana. Objective: curiosity, creativity, imagination foster karna. Skills: design\nmindset, computational thinking, adaptive learning, physical computing. [Q775]\n● NASSCOM — National Association of Software and Services Companies — 1988 mein establish, India ka IT\nindustry ka apex body. Service quality aur Intellectual Property Rights enforcement ensure karti hai Indian\nsoftware aur BPO industry mein. [Q781]\n● BHIM — Bharat Interface for Money — 2016 mein NPCI (National Payments Corporation of India) ne launch kiya.\nUPI (Unified Payments Interface) based hai. Direct bank payments UPI ID, QR code aur PIN se possible hain.\n[Q783]\n● HITEC — Hyderabad Information Technology and Engineering Consultancy — 22 November 1998 ko PM Atal\nBihari Vajpayee ne inaugurate kiya. Hyderabad ko \"HITEC City\" ke naam se jaana jaata hai. [Q786]\n3. Organisations, Institutions & Bodies"," ● TANWA — Tamil Nadu Women in Agriculture — late 1980s mein Tamil Nadu mein start hua. Women ko latest\nagricultural techniques aur organic farming mein train karti hai. Skills: fertilizer use efficiency, organic manure,\nbiofertilizer, tree cropping, pest/disease identification, seed treatment, rat control, grain storage. [Q771]\n● UPU — Universal Postal Union — 1874 mein founded, UN ki specialized agency. Member nations ke beech postal\npolicies coordinate karti hai. HQ Bern, Switzerland. Parent org: UN Economic and Social Council. [Q778]\n● IPAB — Intellectual Property Appellate Board — 15 September 2003 ko Ministry of Commerce and Industry mein\nGazette notification se constitute kiya gaya. Trade Marks Act 1999 aur Geographical Indications of Goods\n(Registration and Protection) Act 1999 ke under Registrar ke decisions ki appeals sunta hai. [Q779]\n● NCSM — National Council of Science Museums — 4 April 1978 ko establish, HQ Kolkata. India ka pehla science\nmuseum BITM (Birla Industrial and Technological Museum) 2 May 1959 ko Kolkata mein open hua. Indian\nMuseum, Kolkata — India ka sabse purana museum, 1814 mein Asiatic Society ki supervision mein establish hua.\n[Q780]\n● IBEF — India Brand Equity Foundation — 2003 mein Department of Commerce, Ministry of Commerce and\nIndustry ne Trust ke roop mein establish kiya. Make in India programme — September 2014 mein PM Modi ne\nlaunch kiya. India Lounge — Cafe Schneider ke paas setup, Make in India se inspired. [Q784]\n4. Financial, Sports & Miscellaneous\n● PPF — Public Provident Fund — Ministry of Finance ki scheme. 15 years ka lock-in period. Tax benefits Section\n80C ke under. Minimum ₹500, maximum ₹1,50,000 per financial year deposit kar sakte hain. Capital guarantee\naur term life insurance benefits hain. [Q787]\n● AKFI — Amateur Kabaddi Federation of India — India mein Kabaddi ka main governing body. India ne 6 Asian\nGames mein gold jeeta: Hiroshima (1994), Bangkok (1998), Busan (2002), Doha (2006), Guangzhou (2010). Pro\nKabaddi League 2014 mein launch hui. Kabaddi Bangladesh ka national sport hai. [Q788]\n● BRICS — B=Brazil, R=Russia, I=India, C=China, S=South Africa. Jim O'Neill ne 2001 mein BRIC term coin ki. Pehli\nBRIC summit 16 June 2009 ko Yekaterinburg, Russia mein hui. South Africa 2010 mein add hua. [Q774]\n5.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️CHOGM ka full form \"Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting\" hai — \"Ministers\" nahi. Ye biennial\nsummit hai, pehli 1971 Singapore mein hui. [Q782]\n●\n\n⚠️C-DAC — Centre for Development of Advanced Computing, establish 1988, HQ Pune. [Q782]\n●\n\n⚠️CITES — Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species. [Q782]\n●\n\n⚠️CCI — Competition Commission of India, establish 14 October 2003, HQ New Delhi. [Q782]\n●\n\n⚠️Extra full forms yaad rakho: IRCTC — Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation, ISCII — Indian\nStandard Code for Information Interchange, IBM — International Business Machines, RODRA — Retired Officers\nDigital Records Archive, NOIDA — New Okhla Industrial Development Authority (17 April 1976). [Q786]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 18 Full Form Full Mind Map (Q770-Q788)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0434","t":"19 Religious Places","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — RELIGIOUS PLACES — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Missionaries, Saints & Religious Figures\n2. Buddhist & Jain Religious Places\n3. Hindu Temples — Architecture, Styles & History\n4. Islamic Religious Places & Monuments\n5. Churches & Christian Sites\n6. Caves & Ancient Monuments\n7. Temple Architecture Styles\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Missionaries, Saints & Religious Figures\n● Missionaries of Charity — 1950 mein Mother Teresa ne Calcutta (Archdiocese of Calcutta) mein establish ki. Aim:\nabandoned babies ki dekhbhaal aur poorest of the poor ki madad. Mother Teresa ke awards: Nobel Peace Prize\n(1979), Padma Shri (1962), Jawaharlal Nehru Award (1969), Bharat Ratna (1980). Official biography Navin Chawla\n(1992) ne likhi. [Q789]\n● Sheikh Fariduddin Ganjshaker — Sufi mystic, unki dargah Pakpattan (Pakistan) mein hai. [Q805]\n● Khwaja Nizamuddin Auliya (1238-1325 CE) — unki Nizamuddin Dargah Delhi mein hai. [Q805]\n● Hazrat Naseeruddin Chirag-e-Dehlvi — Delhi. Hazrat Amir Khusro — Delhi. [Q805]\n● Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti — Ajmer Sharif Dargah, Rajasthan. [Q805]\n2. Buddhist & Jain Religious Places\n● Urgelling Gompa — Arunachal Pradesh mein Buddhist monastery. Tawang monastery — India ka sabse bada,\nduniya mein Potala Palace (Tibet) ke baad doosra sabse bada. Sikkim ke monasteries: Dubdi, Enchey, Kartok,\nLingdum, Pemayangtse, Phodong. Himachal ke monasteries: Tabo, Lhalung, Nako. [Q790]\n● Palitana temples — Gujarat mein Jain pilgrimage site, 823 temples hain, 24 Tirthankaras ko samarpit. Main\ntemple Shri Adishwar (first Tirthankara) ko samarpit — King Kumarapala (Solanki dynasty) ne banwaya. [Q794]\n● Soniji Ki Nasiyan (Ajmer) — 19th century mein bana, Lord Rishbhdev (first Tirthankara of Jainism, establisher of\nIkshvaku dynasty) ko samarpit. Rai Bahadur Seth Moolchand aur Nemichand Soni ne banwaya. Gold-plated\nwooden figures hain. [Q801]\n● Shri Bhagwan Mahavir Govt. Museum — Andhra Pradesh (1982). Jainism ke 5 main vows: ahimsa, satya, asteya,\nbrahmacharya, aparigraha. Festivals: Paryushana, Das Lakshana, Ashtanika, Mahavir Janma Kalyanak, Akshaya\nTritiya, Dipawali. [Q793]\n● Mahabodhi Temple — Bodhgaya, Bihar — yahin Lord Buddha ne enlightenment attain ki. Buddha ke life ke 4 holy\nsites: Lumbini (Birth - Nepal), Bodhgaya (Enlightenment - Bihar), Sarnath (1st Sermon - UP), Kushinagar\n(Death/Mahaparinirvana - UP). [Q796]\n● Karla Caves — Maharashtra, ASI ke under protected monument. Great Chaitya — India ka sabse bada rock-cut\nchaitya. [Q803]\n3. Hindu Temples — Architecture, Styles & History\n● Jagannath Temple (Puri, Odisha) — Lord Vishnu (Jagannath) ko samarpit. Famous for Ratha Yatra. Shri Jagannath"," Temple Act 1955 mein pass hua — temple ke management aur affairs control karne ke liye. [Q792]\n● Nabakalebar Rath Yatra (Puri) — ritual jismein Lord Jagannath, Balabhadra, Subhadra aur Sudarshan ki wooden\nfigures periodically renew hoti hain. Pehli baar 1575 AD mein Yaduvanshi Bhoi King Ramachandra Deva ne\norganize ki. 8th, 12th, ya 19th year mein hoti hai previous Nabakalebar ke baad. Last: 2015 (1996 ke 19 saal\nbaad). [Q799]\n● Kandariya Mahadeva Temple — c. 999 CE mein King Dhangadva (Chandela dynasty, founder - Nanuka) ne\nbanwaya. Khajuraho, MP mein hai — \"The Great God of the Cave\", largest aur most ornate Hindu temple\nmedieval group mein. UNESCO World Heritage Site 1986. Chandela rulers ke aur temples: Lakshmana Temple\n(Yashovarman), Vishvanatha temple (Dhanga), Parshvanatha temple. [Q798]\n● Mahakaleshwar Temple — Ujjain mein hai, Shipra river ke kinare. Present structure Maratha general Ranoji\nShinde ne 1734 CE mein banwaya. Ye 12 Jyotirlingas mein se ek hai. [Q807]\n● Virupaksha Temple — Shiva ko samarpit, Hampi, Karnataka mein — Tungabhadra river ke south bank pe. UNESCO\nWorld Heritage Site 1986. [Q808]\n● Vitthala Temple (Hampi) — Group of Monuments at Hampi mein aata hai. Vijayanagar dynasty ke founders\nHarihara aur Bukka ne banwaye. Tungabhadra river ke kinare, central Karnataka. UNESCO World Heritage Site\n1986. [Q804]\n● Rajarajeshwara Temple — Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu mein hai. Raja Raja Chola I ne 1003-1010 AD ke beech banwaya.\n[Q802]\n● Khajuraho Temple — Madhya Pradesh, erotic composition ke liye famous. Chandela dynasty ne 950-1050 AD ke\nbeech banwaya. UNESCO World Heritage Site. [Q809]\n● Konark Sun Temple ('Black Pagoda') — 1250 CE mein Eastern Ganga King Narasimhadeva-I ke time banaya gaya.\n[Q806]\n● Lingaraja Temple — 11th century AD mein Somavanshi king Yayati I ne banwaya. [Q806]\n● Kanchipuram Kailashnath Temple — Pallava ruler Narasimhavarman II ne 8th century ki shuruaat mein banwaya.\nLord Shiva ko samarpit. [Q806]\n● Sabarimala Temple — Kerala mein, Lord Ayyappa ko samarpit. Ye Periyar Tiger Reserve mein located hai. [Q812]\n4. Islamic Religious Places & Monuments\n● Poa Mecca — Assam (Garurachal Hill) mein hai. \"Poa\" ka matlab one-fourth. Maana jaata hai ki yahan prayer\nkarne se Mecca ke spiritual enlightenment ka 1/4th part milta hai. Ye Pir Giasuddin Auliya ki tomb hai — Islam ke\npioneer. [Q791]\n● Badshahi Masjid (Lahore) — Aurangzeb ne 1671-1673 ke beech banwaya. 1673 se 1986 tak duniya ki sabse badi\nmasjid thi. Banayi gayi thi Aurangzeb ke military campaigns against Maratha king Shivaji ko commemorate karne\nke liye. [Q800]\n● Humayun Mosque — Agra (Kachhpura village), Yamuna river ke left bank pe. [Q800]\n● Cheraman Juma Masjid — Kerala mein, India ki pehli masjid. [Q800]\n● Other Islamic holy places in India: Rauzaa of Shah-e-Alam (Ahmedabad), Furfura Sharif (West Bengal), Hazratbal\nShrine (Srinagar), Dargah of Moinuddin Chishti (Ajmer), Haji Ali Dargah (Mumbai). [Q791]\n5. Churches & Christian Sites\n● Christ Church — Guwahati (Assam) mein hai — North East India ka sabse purana church. Founded 1844,\nconsecrated 1850. [Q795]\n● St. Peter's Basilica — Vatican City mein hai, Renaissance style mein bana. Tiber river ke west mein located. [Q813]\n● Other famous churches: Saint Mark's Basilica (Venice, Italy), La Sagrada Familia (Barcelona, Spain), Liverpool\nCathedral (Liverpool, England). [Q813]\n● India ke famous churches: Santhome Basilica (Chennai), St Francis Church (Kerala), Basilica of Bom Jesus (Goa), St"," Paul Cathedral (West Bengal), Medak Cathedral (Telangana). [Q813]\n● India ke oldest churches: St. Thomas Church (Kerala), Basilica of Bom Jesus (Goa), Christ Church (Himachal\nPradesh), St. Paul's Cathedral (West Bengal), St. Thomas Cathedral Basilica Church (Chennai), Cathedral of Mary\nHelp of Christians (Shillong, Meghalaya). [Q795]\n6. Caves & Ancient Monuments\n● Famous caves of India: Ajanta Caves (Maharashtra), Udayagiri and Khandagiri Caves (Odisha), Amarnath Cave\n(Jammu and Kashmir), Bagh Caves and Bhimbetka Caves (Madhya Pradesh). [Q803]\n● Rashtrakuta architecture: Kailash temple at Ellora caves, Elephanta caves (Shiva), Navalinga temple. [Q798]\n● Chalukya architecture: Durga temple, Lady Khan temple (Surya temple), Virupaksha temple, Sangameshwara\ntemple. [Q798]\n7. Temple Architecture Styles\n● Nagara style — Northern India mein popular. Entire temple stone platform pe bana, steps lead up. Boundary\nwalls ya gateways elaborate nahi hote. Garbhagriha hamesha tallest tower ke neeche hota hai. Amalaka/Kalash\nShikhara pe install hota hai. Examples: Kandariya Mahadev (MP), Sun temple (Konark), Sun temple (Modhera,\nGujarat), Ossian temple (Gujarat). [Q797]\n● Dravidian style — South India. Gopuram iska characteristic feature hai. Examples: Chennakesava Temple (Belur),\nHoysaleswara Temple (Halebid), Kesava Temple (Somanathapura). [Q810]\n● Vesara style — Third style. [Q797]\n● Gopuram (Gopura) — South Indian temples ke entrances. Dravidian style ka characteristic feature. [Q810]\n● Shikhara — North India mein Hindu temple architecture ka rising tower. [Q810]\n● Vedica — ancient times mein wooden fence jo sacred place ko ghera karta tha. [Q810]\n● Garbhagriha — Hindu aur Jain temples ka innermost sanctuary jahan primary deity ki murti hoti hai. [Q810]\n● Panchayatan style — Temple architecture. Central shrine surrounded by 4 subsidiary shrines 4 different corners\npe — total 5 shrines. Examples: Jagdish Temple (Udaipur), Lakshmana Temple (Khajuraho), Kandariya Mahadeva\nTemple (Khajuraho), Brahmeswara Temple (Bhubaneswar), Lingaraja Temple (Bhubaneswar). [Q811]\n8.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Garbhagriha \"sanctum sanctorum\" hai — ye kisi structure ka naya ya purana hona decide nahi karta. [Q793]\n●\n\n⚠️Christ Church Guwahati mein hai — Aizawl, Itanagar ya Kohima mein nahi. [Q795]\n●\n\n⚠️Poa Mecca Assam mein hai — Gujarat, Himachal Pradesh ya Kerala mein nahi. [Q791]\n●\n\n⚠️Sabarimala Periyar Tiger Reserve mein hai — Parambikulam, Anamalai ya Mudumalai mein nahi. [Q812]\n●\n\n⚠️St. Peter's Basilica Vatican mein hai — Lisbon, Madrid ya Pisa mein nahi. [Q813]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 19 Religious Places Full Mind Map (Q789-Q813)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0435","t":"20 Awards","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — AWARDS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Medical, Science & Research Awards\n2. Language & Literature Awards\n3. Civilian Awards — Bharat Ratna & Padma Awards\n4. Gallantry & Defence Awards\n5. Sports Awards\n6. International Awards\n7. Space, Journalism & Social Awards\n8. Nobel Prize — Complete Details\n9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Medical, Science & Research Awards\n● Dhanvantari Award — Medical field ke liye, Ministry of AYUSH dwara Ayurveda Day pe diya jaata hai. ₹5 lakh cash\nprize + citation. [Q814]\n● Shanti Swarup Bhatnagar Award — Science & Technology, establish 1958. [Q814, Q816]\n● Borlaug Award — International agriculture & food production mein science-based achievement, establish 1972.\n[Q814]\n● Homi Bhabha Award — Atomic energy field, establish 2010. [Q816]\n● Dr. B.C. Roy Award — Medicine, establish 1962. Present President of India dwara 1 July (National Doctors' Day) ko\ndiya jaata hai. Ye medicine ka highest honour hai. ₹15,000 + medal. First awarded 1973 to Sandip Mukerjee.\nArea: medicine, politics, science, philosophy, literature, arts. [Q843]\n● Daly Memorial Award — Psychology field. [Q814]\n2. Language & Literature Awards\n● Bhasha Bharti Samman — Central Institute of Indian Languages (CIIL), Mysuru dwara diya jaata hai. CIIL establish\n1969, aim: minor, minority, tribal languages ko protect aur document karna. [Q815]\n● Jnanpith Award — India ka highest literary award, institute 1961, first award 1965. Sirf Indian writers ko diya jaata\nhai jo 8th Schedule ki kisi bhi language mein kaam karte hain. First winner: G. Sankara Kurup. Prize: ₹11 lakh +\ncitation + Vagdevi (Saraswati) bronze replica. [Q842]\n● Sahitya Akademi Award — institute 1954, literature field. [Q842]\n● Vyas Samman — 1991 mein start hua, Hindi mein outstanding literary work ke liye. K.K. Birla Foundation dwara.\n[Q842]\n● Kabir Samman — Madhya Pradesh Govt dwara, literature field, start 1986-87. [Q842]\n● Ramdhari Singh 'Dinkar' — \"Rashtra Kavi\" title, Veer Rasa ke greatest Hindi poet. Jnanpith Award 1972 for\n\"Urvashi\". Other works: Rashmirathi, Parashuram ki Pratiksha, Hunkar, Kurukshetra, Krishna Ki Chaetavani,\nBhagwan Ke Daakiye. Awards: Padma Bhushan (1959), Sahitya Akademi Award (1959). Rajya Sabha member\n1952, Hindi adviser 1970. [Q836]\n● Pulitzer Prize — Columbia University, New York dwara administer hota hai. Joseph Pulitzer ki will se 1917 mein\nestablish hua. Newspaper, magazine, online journalism, literature, music composition mein achievement ke liye.\nFirst Indian: Gobind Behari Lal (1937). \"Soul of New Machine\" by Tracy Kidder ne 1982 mein Pulitzer jeeta. [Q826,\nQ839]\n● Neustadt International Prize for Literature — 1969, biennial, University of Oklahoma & World Literature Today"," dwara. [Q839]\n● Man Booker Prize — Har saal best English novel ke liye, UK mein publish honi chahiye. Arundhati Roy — pehli\nIndian mahila jinhone Booker Prize jeeta (1997, \"The God of Small Things\"). Aur awards: National Film Award for\nBest Screenplay (1988), Sydney Peace Prize (2004), Orwell Award (2004), Norman Mailer Prize (2011). [Q839,\nQ823]\n3. Civilian Awards — Bharat Ratna & Padma Awards\n● Bharat Ratna & Padma Vibhushan — 1954 mein institute hue. Bharat Ratna: India ka highest civilian award, PM\nrecommend karte hain President ko. First awardees 1954: C. Rajagopalachari, C.V. Raman, Sarvepalli\nRadhakrishnan. Baad ke winners: Rajendra Prasad (1962), Indira Gandhi (1971), Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan (1987),\nCNR Rao & Sachin Tendulkar (2014). [Q827, Q838]\n● Padma Awards — Bharat Ratna ke baad highest civilian honors, Republic Day ki eve pe announce hote hain. 3\ncategories: Padma Vibhushan (exceptional & distinguished service), Padma Bhushan (distinguished service of\nhigher order), Padma Shri (distinguished service). Padma Awards Committee (Cabinet Secretary headed)\nrecommend karti hai. [Q827]\n4. Gallantry & Defence Awards\n● Param Vir Chakra — Wartime valour ka highest decoration. First recipient: Major Somnath Sharma. [Q824]\n● Maha Vir Chakra — 2nd highest gallantry award, \"Acts of Gallantry in the presence of the enemy on land, at sea\nor in the air\". [Q824]\n● Vir Chakra — 3rd highest wartime gallantry award. [Q824, Q825]\n● Shaurya Chakra — Gallantry otherwise in the face of enemy. [Q824]\n5. Sports Awards\n● Dronacharya Award — Coaches ko diya jaata hai, Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports dwara. First awarded 1985.\nPrize: medal + certificate + ₹15 lakh (lifetime) / ₹10 lakh (regular). [Q825]\n● Arjuna Award — India ka 2nd highest sporting honor, first awarded 1961. Outstanding performance in sports ke\nliye. ₹15 lakh cash prize. [Q825]\n6. International Awards\n● Ramon Magsaysay Award — \"Asia's Nobel\", establish 1957. Former Philippine President Ramon Magsaysay ki\nmemory mein. Vinoba Bhave (1958) — first Indian winner. Arvind Kejriwal (2006) — Parivartan movement & RTI\nke liye. Ravish Kumar (2019). [Q828]\n● Stockholm Water Prize — 1991 mein start hua, SIWI (Stockholm International Water Institute) dwara, Royal\nSwedish Academy of Sciences ke saath. Water resources ke conservation & protection ke liye. World Water Day\n— 22 March. [Q819]\n● Goldman Environmental Prize (\"Green Nobel Prize\") — 1989 mein start hua, Richard & Rhoda Goldman dwara.\nGrassroots environmental activists ko, 6 geographic regions se ek-ek. Indian recipients: Ramesh Agrawal (2014),\nRashida Bee (2004), Champa Devi Shukla (2004), Medha Patkar (1992). Vandana Shiva winner nahi hain. [Q837]\n● Gandhi Peace Prize — 1995 mein institute hua, Mahatma Gandhi ki 125th birth anniversary ke occasion pe. ₹1\ncrore + citation + plaque + handicraft item. First recipient: Julius Nyerere. [Q831]\n● Kalinga Prize — UNESCO dwara, science popularization ke liye. 1952 mein create hua, Bijoyanand Patnaik ke"," donation se. [Q841]\n7. Space, Journalism & Social Awards\n● Vikram Sarabhai Journalism Award — Space Science, Technology & Research field. 2019 mein ISRO ne announce\nkiya Vikram Sarabhai ke 100th birthday pe. 2 categories: 1st — ₹5,00,000 + medal + citation; 2nd — ₹3,00,000 /\n₹2,00,000 / ₹1,00,000 + citation. [Q818]\n● Women Transforming India (WTI) Awards — NITI Aayog dwara 2016 mein start hua. Categories: Public &\nCommunity Service, Manufacturing, Non-manufacturing, Financial Products, Climate Action etc. NITI Aayog —\nform 1 January 2015, HQ New Delhi. [Q821]\n● Nanaji Deshmukh Rashtriya Gaurav Gram Sabha Puraskar (NDRGGSP) — Ministry of Panchayati Raj dwara. Gram\nPanchayats/Village Councils ko socio-economic development mein outstanding contribution ke liye. First\nPanchayati Raj in modern India — 2 October 1959, Nagaur (Rajasthan). 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act 1992\n— Part IX, Article 243 to 243(O) add kiya. [Q817]\n● UN Asia Environmental Enforcement Award — February 2021 mein Sasmita Lenka (Gender Leadership & impact\ncategory) — India ki pehli officer. Pangolin smuggling rackets bust karne ke kaam ke liye. [Q820]\n8. Nobel Prize — Complete Details\n● Nobel Prize — Alfred Nobel (Dynamite ke inventor) dwara establish, first awarded 1901. 6 categories: Physics,\nChemistry, Physiology/Medicine, Literature, Peace, Economic Sciences (1968 mein add hua). Peace prize Norway\ndwara diya jaata hai, baaki Sweden dwara. [Q822, Q829, Q830, Q832, Q833, Q834, Q835, Q840]\n● Swedish Academy (Stockholm) — Literature prize deti hai. Founded 1786 by Swedish King Gustav III. [Q822]\n● Marie Curie — First woman Nobel winner, aur first person to win twice: Physics (1903, with Henri Becquerel) aur\nChemistry (1911) — polonium & radium discover karne ke liye. [Q833]\n● Ronald Ross — Medicine Nobel 1902, malaria ke mosquito transmission discover karne ke liye. Pehle British\njinhone Medicine Nobel jeeta. [Q832]\n● Henry Dunant — First Nobel Peace Prize 1901, International Red Cross founder. [Q834]\n● Winston Churchill — Literature Nobel 1953, historical & biographical description ke liye. [Q835]\n● Niels Bohr — Physics Nobel 1922, atoms ki structure aur radiation ki investigation ke liye. [Q840]\n● Indian Nobel Winners:\n– Rabindranath Tagore — Literature, 1913 (Gitanjali)\n– C.V. Raman — Physics, 1930\n– Har Gobind Khorana — Medicine, 1968\n– Mother Teresa — Peace, 1979\n– Subrahmanyan Chandrasekhar — Physics, 1983\n– Amartya Sen — Economics, 1998\n– Venkatraman Ramakrishnan — Chemistry, 2009\n– Kailash Satyarthi — Peace, 2014\n– Abhijit Banerjee — Economics, 2019 [Q829, Q830]\n● Malala Yousafzai — Youngest Nobel Laureate (2014). [Q830]\n● Greta Thunberg — \"Youth Strike 4 Climate\" movement founder, Nobel Peace Prize ke liye nominate hui. [Q830]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mahatma Gandhi Nobel Prize winner nahi hain — unhe 5 baar nominate kiya gaya tha lekin kabhi nahi\nmila. [Q829]"," 9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Mahatma Gandhi Nobel Prize winner nahi hain — isliye ye trap question hai. Real winners: Kailash Satyarthi,\nAmartya Sen, Rabindranath Tagore. [Q829]\n●\n\n⚠️Vandana Shiva Goldman Environmental Prize winner nahi hain — Indian winners: Ramesh Agrawal, Rashida\nBee, Champa Devi Shukla, Medha Patkar. [Q837]\n●\n\n⚠️Bharat Ratna & Padma Awards 1954 mein institute hue — 1950, 1953 ya 1955 nahi. [Q827]\n●\n\n⚠️Marie Curie ne Physics (1903) aur Chemistry (1911) dono mein Nobel jeeta — Biology ya Astronomy nahi.\n[Q833]\n●\n\n⚠️Winston Churchill ko Literature Nobel mila — Peace, Economics ya Physiology nahi. [Q835]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 20 Awards Full Mind Map (Q814-Q843)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0436","t":"21 Important Events","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — IMPORTANT EVENTS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Environmental Conventions & Heavy Metal Diseases\n2. Non-Aligned Movement (NAM)\n1. Environmental Conventions & Heavy Metal Diseases\n● Minamata Convention 2013 — Japan mein hua tha, Mercury (Pāra) emission ko address karne ke liye. India ne 18\nJune 2018 ko ratify kiya. Minamata disease — neurological disorder caused by methylmercury poisoning.\nChildren mein acrodynia (pink disease) ho sakta hai jismein skin pink ho jaati hai aur peel hoti hai. [Q844]\n● Other metals & associated diseases yaad rakho:\n– Arsenic → Black foot disease\n– Nitrate → Blue baby syndrome\n– Cadmium → Itai-Itai disease\n– Fluoride → Skeletal fluorosis\n– Mercury → Minamata disease / Acrodynia [Q844]\n2. Non-Aligned Movement (NAM)\n● First Non-Alignment Conference — Belgrade, 1961. NAM Cold War ke time bana — un countries ka group jo na\nUSA ke sath tha na USSR ke sath, balki independent/neutral rehna chahti thi. [Q845]\n● NAM ke 5 founders (Big Five):\n– Josip Broz Tito — Yugoslavia\n– Gamal Abdel Nasser — Egypt\n– Jawaharlal Nehru — India\n– Kwame Nkrumah — Ghana\n– Sukarno — Indonesia [Q845]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 21 Important Events Full Mind Map (Q844-Q845)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0437","t":"22 Founder","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — FOUNDER — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Political Leaders & Parties\n2. Social Reformers & Institutions\n3. Business & Entrepreneurs\n4.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Political Leaders & Parties\n● Mizo National Front (MNF) — founder Laldenga, 1961 mein form hui. Mizoram ki regional political party. Mizoram\nPeace Accord 1986 mein MNF aur Government of India ke beech sign hua — 2 decades ki insurgency khatam hui.\nMizoram ko February 1987 mein statehood mila. Laldenga baad mein Mizoram ke Chief Minister bhi bane.\nPasaltha Khuangchera — Mizoram ke first freedom fighter jinhone British imperialism ke against apni jaan di.\n[Q846]\n● Himachal Pradesh ke founder — Dr. Yashwant Singh Parmar, inhe \"Himachal Nirmata\" (the creator of Himachal)\nkehte hain. Himachal Pradesh ke first Chief Minister bhi the. [Q847]\n● Praja Rajyam Party — Telugu film actor Chiranjeevi ne 2008 mein start ki. 2009 Andhra Pradesh election mein 294\nmein se 18 seats jeeti, 16%+ vote share tha. 2011 mein Indian National Congress mein merge ho gayi. [Q851]\n● Telugu Desam Party (TDP) — N.T. Rama Rao ne 1982 mein found ki. [Q851]\n2. Social Reformers & Institutions\n● Seva Sadan, Bombay — Behramji M. Malabari ne 1908 mein establish kiya. Ye ek Parsi social reformer aur\njournalist the. Women's rights ki protection aur child marriage ke against campaign chalaya. [Q848]\n● Bharatiya Vidya Bhavan — Dr. K.M. Munshi ne 1938 mein Mahatma Gandhi ke support se found kiya. Educational\ntrust hai, HQ Mumbai. [Q849]\n● Other important founders yaad rakho:\n– Shiva Narayan Agnihotri — Dev Samaj (1887)\n– Narayan Malhar Joshi — Social Service League (1911)\n– M.G. Ranade — Poona Sarvajanik Sabha (1870)\n– Madan Mohan Malaviya — Banaras Hindu University (1916)\n– Shyamaprasad Mukherjee — Bharatiya Jana Sangh (1951) [Q848, Q849]\n3. Business & Entrepreneurs\n● SpiceJet — co-founder aur owner Ajay Singh hain. 15 January 2015 ko Sun Group ke Kalanithi Maran se ownership\nre-acquire ki. Famous slogan \"Abki Baar Modi Sarkar\" bhi Ajay Singh ne hi coin kiya tha. [Q850]\n● Other business personalities yaad rakho:\n– Ratan Tata — Tata Sons ke former Chairman\n– Vijay Mallya — Kingfisher Airlines ke former owner\n– Captain G.R. Gopinath — Deccan Airways ke former owner [Q850]"," 4.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Himachal Pradesh ke founder Dr. Yashwant Singh Parmar hain — Baba Kanshi Ram (poet & activist), Virbhadra\nSingh (multiple times CM), ya Rajkumari Amrit Kaur (first Health Minister of India) nahi. [Q847]\n●\n\n⚠️SpiceJet ke owner Ajay Singh hain — Vijay Mallya (Kingfisher), Ratan Tata (Tata), ya Captain G.R. Gopinath\n(Deccan) nahi. [Q850]\n●\n\n⚠️Chiranjeevi ki party Praja Rajyam Party thi — Telugu Desam Party N.T. Rama Rao ki hai. [Q851]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 22 Founder Full Mind Map (Q846-Q851)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0438","t":"23 Entertainment","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — ENTERTAINMENT — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Satyajit Ray — Films & Awards\n2. Indian Cinema — Oscar History & Milestones\n3.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Satyajit Ray — Films & Awards\n● Jalsaghar (\"The Music Room\") — Satyajit Ray ki 1958 ki drama film hai. Ye film aristocratic zamindari style of living\nke decline pe based hai. Actor: Chhabi Biswas, Story: Tarasankar Bandyopadhyay. [Q852]\n● Pather Panchali — Satyajit Ray dwara direct ki gayi. Inki aur famous films: \"The Music Room\", \"The Big City\",\n\"Charulata\", \"Days and Nights in the Forest\". [Q854]\n● Satyajit Ray — 1992 mein Honorary Academy Award (Oscar) paane wale pehle Indian. Inke awards: Padma Shri\n(1958), Padma Bhushan (1965), Padma Vibhushan (1976), Bharat Ratna (1992). [Q854]\n●\n\n⚠️Trap: Mahal, Pyaasa, Kora Kagaz — ye Satyajit Ray ki films nahi hain. [Q854]\n2. Indian Cinema — Oscar History & Milestones\n● India ki Oscar-nominated films: Mother India (1957), Salaam Bombay (1988), Lagaan (2001). [Q853]\n● Karma (1986) — Director Subhash Ghai, ye kabhi Oscar ke liye nominate nahi hui. [Q853]\n● First Oscar-awarded movie — \"Wings\". Academy Awards 1929 mein start hue. [Q853]\n● Indian Cinema ke milestones:\n– First silent film — Raja Harishchandra (1913)\n– First sound film — Alam Ara (1931)\n– First colour film — Kisan Kanya (1937)\n– First 3D film — My Dear Kuttichathan (1984) [Q852]\n3.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Karma Oscar-nominated nahi hai — Mother India, Salaam Bombay, Lagaan nominate hui thi. [Q853]\n●\n\n⚠️Mahal, Pyaasa, Kora Kagaz — Satyajit Ray ne direct nahi ki. [Q854]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 23 Entertainment Full Mind Map (Q852-Q854)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0439","t":"24 Schemes","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — SCHEMES — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Women & Child Development Schemes\n2. Health, Nutrition & Sanitation Schemes\n3. Education, Skill & Digital Literacy\n4. Agriculture, Rural Development & Environment\n5. Housing, Urban Development & Infrastructure\n6. Financial Inclusion, Pension & Insurance\n7. Tourism, Heritage & State Schemes\n8. Science, Research & Women Empowerment\n9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Women & Child Development Schemes\n● Stree Manoraksha Project — WCD Minister Smriti Irani ne NIMHANS (National Institute of Mental Health and\nNeuro Sciences) ke collaboration mein launch kiya. Women victims ki mental health counselling provide karta\nhai. NIMHANS: Bangalore, est. 1847. [Q856]\n● Beti Bachao Beti Padhao (BBBP) — 22 January 2015 ko Panipat, Haryana mein PM Modi ne launch kiya. Aim: sex-\nselective abortion eliminate karna, girls ki education ensure karna. NRHM ke 100 districts mein start hua. [Q858,\nQ891]\n● National Creche Scheme — Ministry of Women and Child Development ke under. Working auraton ke liye, 12\nhour service. Age: 6 months se 6 saal tak ke bachchon ki care. [Q886]\n● One Stop Centre Scheme (Sakhi) — 1 April 2015 ko launch. 24x7 integrated support centre. Women affected by\nviolence ko medical, legal, psychological counselling. Ministry of Women & Child Development. [Q892, Q929]\n● Integrated Child Development Services (ICDS) — 1975 mein launch. Children's health, preschool education,\nprimary healthcare, immunization, health check-up. [Q926]\n● Integrated Child Protection Scheme (ICPS) — 2009-2010 mein launch. Centrally Sponsored Umbrella Scheme.\nCoverage: Children in conflict with law, Children in need of care and protection. [Q905]\n● Swadhar Greh Scheme — 2001-2002 mein launch. Women victims of difficult circumstances ko institutional\nsupport aur rehabilitation. NOTE: ye scheme socially backward women ko Government jobs provide NAHI karti.\n[Q898]\n● Operation Muskaan — 2014 mein launch, Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) ke under. Missing aur destitute\nchildren ko trace karke unki families se reunite karna. [Q918]\n2. Health, Nutrition & Sanitation Schemes\n● Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM) — 2 October 2014 ko launch, Mahatma Gandhi ki 145th birth anniversary pe.\nUrban: Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, Rural: Ministry of Jal Shakti. Phase 2: 2021-2026. 9 crore+ toilets\nban chuke hain. Slogan: \"Ek Kadam Swachhata Ki Aur\". [Q859, Q890, Q913]\n● Swachh Bharat Mission Grameen Phase-II — Ministry of Jal Shakti, 2021-2026. Focus: ODF sustainability,\nsolid/liquid waste management, village cleanliness. [Q900]\n● GOBAR-DHAN — 30 April 2018 ko launch. Swachh Bharat Mission Gramin-Phase 2 ke under. Aim: cattle dung aur\nagricultural waste ko biogas aur compost mein convert karke wealth aur energy generate karna. [Q915]\n● Ayushman Bharat — 2018 mein launch, world's largest government-funded healthcare programme. PM-JAY: ₹5\nlakh per family per year ka health cover. RSBY aur SCHIS subsumed. [Q873, Q935]"," ● eSanjeevani — Ministry of Health & Family Welfare ka telemedicine platform. 2019 mein launch hua. [Q893]\n● Pradhan Mantri Jan-Aushadhi Scheme — Ministry of Chemical and Fertilizers ke under (Department of\nPharmaceuticals). 2008 mein \"Jan Aushadhi Campaign\" naam se launch hua. Implementing agency:\nPharmaceuticals & Medical Devices Bureau of India (PMBI). Affordable generic medicines provide karna. [Q921]\n● Pradhan Mantri Surakshit Matritva Abhiyan (PMSMA) — 2016 mein launch. Pregnant women ko free antenatal\ncheck-ups ensure karna. [Q894]\n● Mission Indradhanush — December 2014 mein launch. Children aur pregnant women ko vaccination coverage\nprovide karna. Ye employment programme nahi hai. [Q895, Q912]\n● Mid-Day Meal Scheme — 1995 mein launch. School-going bachchon ko nutritious meal provide karna. Ministry of\nEducation ke under. [Q881]\n● Paryavaran Vahini Scheme — June 1992 launch. Aim: environmental awareness create karna aur people ki\ninvolvement encourage karna. Illegal acts report karna forests, wildlife, pollution se related. [Q930]\n● Namami Gange Programme — June 2014 mein launch, Integrated Conservation Mission. Ganga river ki pollution\nabatement, conservation aur rejuvenation ke liye. Ministry of Jal Shakti. General public river banks pe open\ndefecation rokne mein participate karti hai. [Q860]\n3. Education, Skill & Digital Literacy\n● Skill India Mission (PMKVY) — 2015 mein launch. Youth ko skill training dena taaki employable bane. [Q870]\n● Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) — 2001 mein launch. 8-14 years ke bachchon ko elementary education dena.\n\"Education for All\" ka goal. [Q861]\n● PM SHRI Schools — 2022 mein launch. PM Schools for Rising India. Quality education aur modern infrastructure.\n[Q883]\n● Digital India — 1 July 2015 ko launch. 9 pillars: Broadband Highways, Universal Access to Mobile Connectivity,\nPublic Internet Access Programme, e-Governance, e-Kranti, Information for All, Electronics Manufacturing, IT for\nJobs, Early Harvest Programmes. [Q885]\n● Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan (PMGDISHA) — 2017 mein launch. 6 crore rural households ko\ndigital literacy. 14-60 years age group. [Q897]\n● SWAYAM — 9 July 2017 launch. Aim: free high-quality e-content provide karna colleges/universities ko. MHRD ke\nunder. SWAYAM Prabha: 32 High Quality Educational Channels through DTH. [Q914]\n● DigiGaon — 2008 launch. Ministry of Electronics and IT. Aim: villages ko digitally connected banana aur rural\ncitizens ko digital literate banana. [Q917]\n● Vidyanjali — June 2016 launch. Ministry of Education. Aim: schools ko community aur private sector involvement\nse strengthen karna. Volunteers: young professionals, retired teachers, retired govt officials. [Q937]\n● Shaala ASMITA — Shala Asmita Yojana (SAY). Aim: school students ki educational journey track karna Class I to XII\ntak. Online databases: attendance, enrollment, learning outcomes, mid-day meal, infrastructure. [Q940]\n● SHREYAS — Scheme for Higher Education Youth in Apprenticeship and Skills. April 2019 launch. MHRD dwara.\nAim: academia aur industry ke beech gap bridge karna. [Q925]\n● National Skill Development Mission — 2015 launch. High-quality training standards ensure karna. Ministry of Skill\nDevelopment and Entrepreneurship. [Q909]\n● Prime Minister Rozgar Yojana (PMRY) — 1993 launch. Educated unemployed youth aur women ko loan. Age: 18-\n40, Education: Minimum 8th standard. [Q931]\n4. Agriculture, Rural Development & Environment\n● PM-KISAN (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi) — February 2019 mein launch. Small and marginal farmers ko\n₹6,000 per year direct income support (3 installments of ₹2,000). Agriculture Ministry ke under. [Q862, Q939]\n● Soil Health Card Scheme — 2015 mein launch. Farmers ko soil health status batata hai taaki appropriate fertilizers"," use kar sakein. [Q871]\n● Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) — 18 February 2016 mein launch. 3 indemnity levels: 70%, 80%, 90%.\nNAIS aur MNAIS replace kiya. Premium: Kharif (2%), Rabi (1.5%), Commercial/Horticultural (5%). Agriculture\nMinistry ke under. [Q872, Q934]\n● Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY) — 2007 mein launch. Agriculture growth rate 4% achieve karna. [Q877]\n● National Food Security Mission (NFSM) — 2007 mein launch. Rice, wheat, pulses ki production badhana. [Q880]\n● Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY) — April 2015 launch. Soil Health Management (SHM) ka elaborated\ncomponent. 3 saal mein 10,000 clusters banenge, 5.0 lakh acre area cover karte hue. Certification expenditure pe\nkoi liability nahi farmers pe. [Q908]\n● MGNREGA — 2005 mein launch, Ministry of Rural Development. Legal guarantee: 100 days ki wage employment\nper rural household ko financial year mein. [Q869]\n● National Food for Work Programme (NFWP) — 14 November 2004 ko launch, Ministry of Rural Development.\nAim: poor logon ko supplementary wage employment generate karna. Baad mein MGNREGA mein subsume ho\ngaya. [Q919]\n● DISHA (Digitisation, Integration and Standardization by Harnessing Automation) — Ministry of Rural Development\nke under initiative. Central, State aur local Panchayat Governments ke beech coordinate karta hai. [Q922]\n● National Rural Livelihood Mission (NRLM) / Aajeevika — 2011 mein launch. Rural poor households ko self-\nemployment opportunities dena. [Q878]\n● National Rurban Mission (NRuM) — 2016 mein launch. Rural areas mein urban amenities provide karna. [Q879]\n● Pradhan Mantri Adarsh Gram Yojana (PMAGY) — 2009-10 mein launch. SC-majority villages ka integrated\ndevelopment. [Q882]\n● Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) — 25 September 2014 launch. Pandit Deendayal\nUpadhyaya ki 98th birth anniversary pe. Aim: rural poor youth ko economically independent aur globally relevant\nworkforce banana. Ministry of Rural Development. [Q904]\n● Swajaldhara Yojana — 2002 launch. Drinking water supply ensure karna sab villages mein. [Q910]\n● Green India Mission (GIM) — National Mission for a Green India. 13 million hectares pe afforestation. Climate\nchange mitigation. [Q888]\n● National Solar Mission — 2010 mein launch. 20,000 MW solar capacity by 2022 target. [Q889]\n● KUSUM (PM-KUSUM) — 2019 launch. MNRE (Ministry of New and Renewable Energy). Aim: farmers ko financial\nsecurity provide karna solar energy capacities harness karke. Decentralised solar power production promote\nkarna. [Q924]\n● SVAMITVA — April 2020 launch. Drones se property mapping villages mein. Ministry of Panchayati Raj nodal\nministry. UMANG: Unified Mobile Application for New-age Governance. [Q928]\n● Tamil Nadu — 2001 mein rooftop rainwater harvesting compulsory kiya. Jayalalithaa ki brainchild. [Q927]\n● Rythu Bandhu — Telangana ki scheme. 2018-19 launch. Farmers' Investment Support Scheme (FISS) — ek saal\nmein do crops ke liye investment support. [Q903]\n● National Bamboo Mission — 2006-07 launch, MIDH ke under. 2018-19 mein restructured. 100% Centrally\nSponsored. Indian Forest Act 1927 amended 2017 mein — bamboo trees ki category se hata diya gaya. Ministry\nof Agriculture and Farmers Welfare. [Q942]\n● Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana — 2017 launch. Food processing mein investment boost karna. Ministry\nof Food Processing Industries (MoFPI). Umbrella scheme: Mega Food Parks, Integrated Cold Chain, Food Safety\nInfrastructure etc. [Q932]\n5. Housing, Urban Development & Infrastructure\n● Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) — 2015 mein launch. \"Housing for All\" by 2022. Urban (PMAY-U): Ministry\nof Housing and Urban Affairs. Rural (PMAY-G): Ministry of Rural Development. [Q874]\n● Smart Cities Mission — 2015 mein launch. 100 cities ko smart city banane ka target. [Q875]\n● AMRUT (Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation) — 25 June 2015 launch. Basic civic amenities"," — sewage networks aur water supply. JNNURM ka renaming. Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs. [Q876, Q907]\n● Sagarmala Project — 31 July 2015 establish. Port-led development. Coastal infrastructure develop karna. Ministry\nof Ports, Shipping and Waterways. Logistics sector ki performance enhance karna. [Q884, Q923]\n● Bharatmala Pariyojana — 2017 mein launch. Highways aur road infrastructure develop karna. [Q887]\n6. Financial Inclusion, Pension & Insurance\n● Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) — 28 August 2014 ko launch. Financial inclusion ke liye — bank\naccounts, RuPay debit card, insurance. \"Mera Khata, Bhagya Vidhata\". [Q863, Q896]\n● Atal Pension Yojana (APY) — 9 May 2015 mein launch, Kolkata mein. Unorganised sector ke workers ko pension.\nAge: 18-40 years. Monthly contribution. [Q864]\n● Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY) — 9 May 2015 mein launch. ₹2 lakh ka life insurance, ₹330 per\nyear premium. [Q865]\n● Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY) — 9 May 2015 mein launch. ₹2 lakh ka accident insurance, ₹12\nper year premium (pehle ₹20 tha). [Q866]\n● Mudra Yojana (PMMY) — 2015 mein launch. Micro Units Development & Refinance Agency. Small businesses ko\nloan: Shishu (up to ₹50,000), Kishor (₹50,001-₹5 lakh), Tarun (₹5 lakh-₹10 lakh). [Q867]\n● Stand-Up India — 5 April 2016 mein launch. SC/ST aur women entrepreneurs ko bank loans. ₹10 lakh se ₹1 crore\ntak. Greenfield enterprises ke liye. Ministry of Finance. [Q868, Q911]\n● Ujala Scheme — 1 May 2015 launch. Unnat Jyoti for Affordable LEDs for All. LED bulbs subsidized rates pe\ndomestic consumers ko. Ministry of Power. [Q933]\n● PAHAL Scheme — 2013 mein launch, Union Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas. LPG subsidy ka direct transfer\n— diversion aur duplicate/bogus LPG connections reduce karne ke liye. LPG cylinders market rates pe bikte hain\naur entitled consumers ko subsidy directly milti hai. [Q906]\n● Saubhagya Yojana — 2017 launch. Pradhan Mantri Sahaj Bijli Har Ghar Yojana. 100% household electrification by\n31 March 2019. Ministry of Power. [Q939]\n● National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP) — 15 August 1995 launch. BPL individuals ko elderly, widows aur\ndisabled ke liye social pension. Ministry of Rural Development. [Q916]\n7. Tourism, Heritage & State Schemes\n● PRASAD — Pilgrimage Rejuvenation And Spirituality Augmentation Drive. 2014-15 launch. Ministry of Tourism.\nPilgrimage destinations ka development. [Q920]\n● Swadesh Darshan — 2014-15 launch. 15 circuits: North-East, Buddhist, Himalayan, Coastal, Krishna, Desert, Tribal,\nEco, Wildlife, Rural, Spiritual, Ramayana, Heritage, Sufi, Tirthankara. Mountain Circuit nahi hai. [Q936]\n● HRIDAY — National Heritage City Development and Augmentation Yojana. January 2015 launch. 12 cities: Ajmer,\nAmaravati, Amritsar, Badami, Dwarka, Gaya, Kancheepuram, Velankanni, Mathura, Varanasi, Puri, Warangal.\n[Q938]\n● National Mission for Manuscripts (NAMAMI) — February 2003 mein establish hua, Ministry of Culture ke under.\nAutonomous organization jo Indian manuscripts survey, locate aur conserve karti hai, manuscripts ke liye\nnational resource base banane ke liye. [Q899]\n● Mukhyamantri Yuva Swabhiman Yojana (MP) — urban youth ko 100 days employment per year. ₹4,000/month\nstipend (total ₹13,500 for 100 days). Skill development training bhi milti hai. [Q941]\n8. Science, Research & Women Empowerment\n● Jagdish Chandra Bose Hindi Granth Lekhan Puraskar Yojna — Department of Biotechnology dwara. Biotechnology"," pe Hindi mein original books likhne ke liye writers ko award. Winner: Dr. Hemlata Pant (2015). [Q855]\n● Women Scientists Scheme-A (WOS-A) — Department of Science and Technology dwara. Basic/Applied Science\nmein research ke liye. WOS-B: S&T interventions for Societal Benefit. WOS-C: Internship in IPRs for Self-\nEmployment. [Q901]\n● SERB-POWER (Promoting Opportunities For Women in Exploratory Research) — Science and Engineering\nResearch Board (SERB) dwara, ek statutory body jo Act of Parliament 2008 se establish hui. Science & Engineering\nresearch funding mein gender disparity mitigate karne ke liye formulate ki gayi. [Q857]\n9.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Desert Development Programme flagship nahi hai — NRHM, SSA, PMAY-G flagship hain. [Q902]\n●\n\n⚠️Swachh Bharat Mission sirf urban nahi, rural aur urban dono cover karta hai. [Q913]\n●\n\n⚠️Mission Indradhanush employment nahi, immunization programme hai — December 2014 launch. [Q912]\n●\n\n⚠️PKVY mein 10,000 clusters banenge 3 saal mein — 2,00,000 nahi. [Q908]\n●\n\n⚠️Swadesh Darshan mein Mountain Circuit nahi hai — 15 circuits hain, Mountain usmein nahi. [Q936]\n●\n\n⚠️PM-KISAN aur PMFBY Agriculture Ministry ke under hain, Petroleum Ministry nahi. [Q939]\n●\n\n⚠️Bamboo 2017 mein trees ki category se hata diya gaya — isliye agriculture ke under aata hai ab. [Q942]\n●\n\n⚠️PMSBY ka premium ₹12 per year hai (pehle ₹20 tha). [Q866]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 24 Schemes Full Mind Map (Q855-Q942)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0440","t":"25 Miscellaneous","b":"Crux & Tricks / Pinnacle / Static GK","x":[" STATIC GK — MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n🏷️\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Indian History, Tragedies & Memorials\n2. Geography, Monuments & Heritage Sites\n3. Science, Inventions & Psychology\n4. India — Defence, Security & Operations\n5. Organizations, Companies & Institutions\n6. Animals, Plants & Environment\n7. Policies, Movements & Welfare\n8. Symbols, Flags & Cities\n9. Yoga, Culture & Wildlife\n10. Temple Architecture Styles\n11. Rajasthan Monuments\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n1. Indian History, Tragedies & Memorials\n● Bhopal Gas Tragedy — 2-3 December 1984 ko hui. Union Carbide India Limited ke pesticide plant se 40+ tons\nmethyl isocyanate (C2H3NO) leak hua. History ki sabse dangerous chemical accident. Chairman: Warren\nAnderson. Effects: eyes/lungs ki chronic damage, reproductive problems, psychological issues. [Q943]\n● National War Memorial — Delhi mein, India Gate complex mein 40 acres mein spread. 25 February 2019 ko PM\nModi ne inaugurate kiya. Post-Independence mein supreme sacrifice karne wale soldiers ki yaad mein. National\nWar Museum — Princess Park, near India Gate. [Q944]\n● Cellular Jail (Kala Pani) — Andaman Islands mein. Colonial prison, independence se pehle \"Kala Pani\" ya \"Black\nWater\" ke naam se jaana jaata tha. Famous prisoners: Batukeshwar Dutt, Veer Savarkar, Diwan Singh Kalepani,\nFazl-e-Haq Kharabadi, Yogendra Shukla, Bhai Parmanand. [Q963]\n● Vijay Ghat — Lal Bahadur Shastri (India ke 2nd PM) ka memorial. Shantivan — Jawaharlal Nehru ka. Raj Ghat —\nMahatma Gandhi ka. Kisan Ghat — Chaudhary Charan Singh ka. [Q961]\n● Buddhist Circuit Tourist Train (Mahaparinirvan Express) — Lumbini (Nepal), Bodhgaya, Sarnath, Kushinagar\nconnect karti hai. 2016 mein announce hui. [Q962]\n● Amar Jawan Jyoti — January 1972 mein India Gate ke neeche install ki gayi. India-Pakistan War 1971 ki victory\ncommemorate karne ke liye. [Q989]\n2. Geography, Monuments & Heritage Sites\n● Ahilya Fort — Maheshwar, MP mein, Narmada river ke kinare. 18th century mein bana, Rani Ahilyabai Holkar ka\nresidence (ruled 1765-1796). [Q954]\n● Raniji ki Baori (Queen's Stepwell) — Bundi, Rajasthan mein. 50+ baoris mein sabse badi. 1699 mein Rani Nathavati\nJi ne banwayi. 46 meter deep, multi-storey structure. [Q955]\n● Gomateshwara Statue — Shravanabelagola, Karnataka. Lord Bahubali ki statue, 18 meter (57 feet) — world's\ntallest monolithic free-standing structure. Granite se bani. 10th century mein Chamundaraya (Ganga Kings of\nMysore ke General-in-Chief) ne commission ki. [Q974]\n● Chandigarh Capitol Complex — July 2016 mein UNESCO World Heritage Site declare hua. Le Corbusier ka\narchitectural work. [Q968]\n● Ellora Caves — Aurangabad, Maharashtra mein. Total 34 caves: 12 Buddhist (1-12), 17 Hindu (13-29), 5 Jain (30-"," 34). UNESCO World Heritage Site 1983. Cave 16 — Kailashnath Temple, monolith se carve kiya gaya. [Q991]\n● Churches and Convents of Goa — 1986 mein UNESCO World Heritage Sites list mein add hue. India ke UNESCO\nsites: 1983 mein first 4 — Agra Fort, Taj Mahal (UP), Ajanta Caves, Ellora Caves (Maharashtra); 1986 mein —\nKhajuraho Monuments (MP), Hampi Monuments (Karnataka). [Q951]\n● Dharavi — India ka sabse bada slum area, Mumbai (Maharashtra) mein. 1884 mein British colonial era mein\nfounded hua, duniya ke sabse bade slums mein se ek. [Q952]\n● Nagpur International Airport — Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ke naam pe hai (Babasaheb Ambedkar International Airport).\nOther airports: Ranchi — Birsa Munda Airport, Hyderabad — Rajiv Gandhi International Airport, Mumbai —\nChhatrapati Shivaji International Airport, Varanasi — Lal Bahadur Shastri International Airport. [Q964]\n● Manora Fort — Tamil Nadu mein hai. Tamil Nadu ke aur forts: Fort St. George (Chennai), Vellore Fort, Gingee\nFort, Vijayanagar Fort (Thanjavur), Vattakottai Fort (Kanyakumari), Dindigul Fort. [Q966]\n● Swarna Mandir (Golden Temple) — Amritsar mein, Sikhs ka holy city. 1574 AD mein 4th Sikh Guru Guru Ram Das\nne found kiya, 1604 mein Guru Arjan Sahib ne complete kiya. Foundation stone Hazrat Mian Mir Ji ne rakhi thi.\n[Q986]\n●\n\n⚠️Jantar Mantar, New Delhi — UNESCO World Heritage Site nahi hai. Konark Sun Temple (1984), Rani-ki-Vav\n(2014), Ajanta Caves (1983) — ye hain. [Q956]\n● Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (CSMT) — pehle Victoria Terminus, F.W. Stevens ne design kiya. Victorian\nGothic Revival architecture, UNESCO 2004. Other Mumbai buildings: Town Hall (Colonel Thomas Cowper),\nBombay Secretariat (Captain Henry St. Clair Wilkins), Horniman Circle (James Scott). [Q957]\n● Bekal Fort — Kerala mein hai, Tamil Nadu nahi. Tamil Nadu monuments: Valluvar Kottam, Padmanabhapuram\nPalace, Meenakshi Amman Temple. [Q958]\n●\n\n⚠️Safdarjung's Tomb — Delhi mein hai, Uttar Pradesh nahi. UP monuments: Taj Mahal (Agra), Bara Imambara\n(Lucknow), Sarnath Stupa (Varanasi). [Q959]\n3. Science, Inventions & Psychology\n● Balanced Theory (Attitude Change) — Fritz Heider ne propose ki. P-O-X triangle: P aur O (do individuals) aur X\n(attitude object) ke beech relationship examine karta hai. [Q948]\n● Paper — Cai Lun ne invent kiya. Chinese eunuch, Han Dynasty, 105 CE mein. Bark, hemp, rags, plant fibers se\nbanaya. Other inventions: Newspaper (1604) — Johann Carolus, Printing Press (1440) — Johannes Gutenberg,\nTypewriter (1867) — Christopher Latham Sholes. [Q982]\n● Archimedes ne kaha tha: \"Give me a place to stand and I will move the world\". [Q965]\n● Wormivet — National Innovation Foundation (NIF) ne develop kiya. March 2000 mein establish hua, DST ke\nassistance se. Cattle mein worms ke treatment ke liye herbal alternative. [Q946]\n● Ostrich Egg — 170 mm x 130 mm. Largest cell — single cell (zygote/fertilized egg cell). Ostrich flightless bird, 2\nspecies: common ostrich (sub-Saharan Africa), Somali ostrich (Horn of Africa). [Q945]\n● Hummingbird ka egg sabse chhota. Ostrich ka egg sabse bada. Hummingbirds — Americas ke native, family\nTrochilidae. [Q993]\n● Ichthyosaur Fossil — 2016 mein Gujarat mein mila. Dinosaurs Triassic period mein aaye, Cretaceous period mein\nextinct hue. [Q971]\n4. India — Defence, Security & Operations\n● Indian Air Force — establish 8 October 1932 (Royal Indian Air Force). First aircraft flight 1 April 1933. First Indian\nChief: Subroto Mukerjee. Motto: \"Touch the sky with Glory\" (Nabhah Sprsham Diptam). [Q969]\n● Operation Vijay — Kargil War 1999. Other operations: Operation Polo (1948 — Hyderabad integrate), Operation\nCactus Lilly (1971 — East Pakistan), Operation Trident (1971 — naval assault), Operation Meghdoot (1984 —\nSiachen Glacier), Operation Blue Star (1984 — Punjab turmoil). [Q970]"," ● CISF — 1969 mein establish hua, CISF Act 1968. Ministry of Home Affairs, HQ New Delhi. Motto: \"Protection and\nSecurity\". Other forces: Assam Rifles (1835), BSF (1965), CRPF (1939), ITBP (1962), SSB (1963), NSG (1986), SPG\n(1985). [Q972]\n5. Organizations, Companies & Institutions\n● Wipro Ltd — 1945 mein incorporate hua. Founder: M.H. Premji, HQ Bangalore. [Q950]\n● Infosys — 2 July 1981, Pune. Founder: Narayana Murthy, HQ Bangalore. [Q950]\n● TCS — 1968. Founder: J.R.D. Tata, HQ Mumbai. [Q950]\n● Air India — 1932 mein J.R.D. Tata ne Tata Airlines ke naam se founded. 1953 mein nationalize hua. 2021 mein\nTATA Group ko ₹18,000 crore mein wapas becha gaya. Logo: flying swan with Konark wheel inside. [Q975]\n● ITU (International Telecommunication Union) — 1865 mein founded. UN ki specialized agency for information\nand communication technologies. [Q976]\n● Pawan Hans Limited — 15 October 1985. India's largest helicopter company, Ministry of Civil Aviation ke under.\nHQ Noida. [Q979]\n● National Museum, New Delhi — 15 August 1949 ko R.C. Rajagopalachari ne inaugurate kiya (Rashtrapati Bhawan\nmein). Foundation stone Jawaharlal Nehru ne 1955 mein rakhi. First phase inaugurate: Dr. Sarvepalli\nRadhakrishnan, 18 December 1960. [Q980]\n● ISLRTC (Indian Sign Language Research and Training Center) — Social Justice and Empowerment Ministry, HQ\nNew Delhi. First Sign Language Dictionary (3000 terms) — 23 March 2018. Second edition — 27 February 2019.\n[Q981]\n● Animal Welfare Board of India — establish 1962, HQ Ballabgarh, Haryana. Founder: Rukmini Devi Arundale.\nStatutory advisory body on Animal Welfare Laws. Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying. [Q990]\n● GGGI (Global Green Growth Institute) — 2010 mein establish (non-profit), 2012 mein international organization\nbana. HQ Seoul, South Korea. India partner state hai. UNGA observer status 2013. [Q983]\n● North Eastern Regional Language Centre — Guwahati mein, establish 1989. Other Regional Language Centres:\nNorthern (Patiala), Eastern (Laxmisagar, Bhubaneswar), Southern (Mysore), Western (Pune). [Q949]\n● UIDAI (Unique Identification Authority of India) — Aadhaar issue karti hai, jo 12-digit unique number hai. PAN\n(Income Tax Dept) 10-digit alphanumeric code hai — Aadhaar se alag. [Q960]\n6. Animals, Plants & Environment\n● Elephant — India ka \"National Heritage Animal\". Karnataka mein sabse zyada elephants (6,049 as per 2017\nCensus), followed by Assam (5,719), Kerala (3,054). World Elephant Day — 12 August. [Q978]\n● Turmeric Patent Case — 1995 mein US ne patent grant kiya, 1997 mein CSIR ne challenge kiya aur revoke karaya.\nGround: turmeric ka thousands of years ka traditional use hai India mein, novelty nahi hai. [Q967]\n7. Policies, Movements & Welfare\n● Dr. Bindeshwar Pathak — Sulabh Toilet Movement (1970) se associated. Bachpan Bachao Andolan — Kailash\nSatyarthi ne founded kiya. [Q985]\n● National Policy for Farmers (NPF) — 2007 mein approve hui. First National Agriculture Policy — July 2000. [Q984]\n● Universal Immunisation Programme (UIP) — 1985 mein start hua. 1992 mein Child Survival and Safe Motherhood\nProgramme ka part bana. 2005 se NRHM ke under. Vaccines: Diphtheria, Pertussis, Tetanus, Polio, Measles,\nRubella, Hepatitis B, Meningitis, Pneumonia, Rotavirus, Pneumococcal Pneumonia, Japanese Encephalitis. [Q994]\n● Formal health education (women) — women aur girls ki health WHO ke liye particular concern hai, sociocultural\ndiscrimination ki wajah se. NOTE: \"child bearing decide karne ka empowerment\" formal health education ka"," INCORRECT/galat benefit-option maana jaata hai is question mein. [Q947]\n● International Decade for Drinking Water and Sanitation — UN dwara 1981-1990 designate kiya gaya. Current UN\ndecades: 2018-2028 Water for Sustainable Development, 2021-2030 Ecosystem Restoration. [Q973]\n● eNAM (electronic National Agriculture Market) — 14 April 2016 ko Ministry of Agriculture ne launch kiya. APMC\nmandis ko network karke agricultural commodities ka unified national market banata hai. Portal manage karti\nhai: Small Farmers' Agribusiness Consortium (SFAC). [Q977]\n8. Symbols, Flags & Cities\n● Make in India Symbol — lion made of cogs (gear wheels). Lion on the prowl — manufacturing, strength, national\npride represent karta hai. [Q987]\n● Ashoka Chakra in Indian National Flag — Wheel of the law of dharma. 24 spokes hain. Pingali Venkayya ne design\nkiya. 22 July 1947 ko adopt kiya gaya. [Q992]\n● Delhi — metro city jiska naam independence ke baad nahi badla. Calcutta→Kolkata, Bombay→Mumbai,\nMadras→Chennai. Britishers ne 1911 mein capital Calcutta se Delhi shift ki. [Q988]\n9. Yoga, Culture & Wildlife\n● Yoga Poses:\n– Makarasan = Crocodile [Q998]\n– Matsyasana = Fish (counterpose to Shoulder Stand/Headstand) [Q999]\n– Ardha Padmasana = Half Lily (semi-Padmasan) [Q996]\n– Simhasana = Lion, Bhujangasana = Cobra, Garudasana = Eagle, Ustrasana = Camel, Virabhadrasana = Warrior,\nVrischikasana = Scorpion [Q998, Q999]\n● Berana — Sindhi wedding ceremony. Sindhi weddings mein Hinduism aur Sufism combine hote hain. Jhulelal ko\npray karte hain. [Q995]\n● Boro (Bodo) — ethno-linguistic community, Assam state ki native aur largest ethnolinguistic group. Bodo-Kachari\nfamily ke ethnolinguistic groups ka part, northeastern India mein spread. Brahmaputra valley mein reside karte\nhain, plains tribe ke roop mein recognised. [Q953]\n10. Temple Architecture Styles\n● Vesara Style — Chalukya dynasty ne introduce kiya. Karnataka region mein develop hui. Nagara + Dravida dono\nstyles ka combination. Baad mein Rashtrakuta aur Hoysala dynasty ne bhi banaya. Examples: Kailashnath Temple\n(Maharashtra), Badami Temple, Somnathpuram Temple. [Q997]\n● Dravida Style — South India. Examples: Brihadeeswarar Temple, Gangaikonda Cholapuram, Meenakshi Temple\n(Tamil Nadu). [Q997]\n● Nagara Style — North India. Examples: Surya Temple (Konark), Dashavatar Vishnu Temple (UP), Khajuraho\nTemple (MP). [Q997]\n11. Rajasthan Monuments\n● Hawa Mahal — Jaipur mein. 1799 mein Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh ne banwaya. Red aur pink sandstone se\nbana. 953 small windows (Jharokhas) — honeycomb structure. Designer: Lal Chand Ustad. [Q1000]\n● Umaid Bhawan Palace — Jodhpur mein. Maharaja Umaid Singh ke naam par. [Q1001]"," ● Other Rajasthan monuments: Jaipur — Jal Mahal, City Palace, Amer Fort; Bikaner — Junagarh Fort; Udaipur —\nJagdish Temple, Bagore Ki Haveli, Saheliyon Ki Bari. [Q1001]\n12.\n Traps / Key Differences Summary\n⚠️\n●\n\n⚠️Jantar Mantar, New Delhi — UNESCO World Heritage Site nahi hai — Konark, Rani-ki-Vav, Ajanta hain. [Q956]\n●\n\n⚠️Bekal Fort Kerala mein hai — Tamil Nadu nahi. [Q958]\n●\n\n⚠️Safdarjung's Tomb Delhi mein hai — Uttar Pradesh nahi. [Q959]\n●\n\n⚠️Balanced Theory Fritz Heider ki hai — Adam Smith, Milton Friedman ya John A List ki nahi. [Q948]\n●\n\n⚠️Archimedes ne \"Give me a place to stand...\" kaha — Newton, Galileo ya Einstein nahi. [Q965]\n●\n\n⚠️Cai Lun (Chinese) ne paper invent kiya — Indian mathematicians nahi. [Q982]\n●\n\n⚠️Make in India ka symbol cogs se bana lion hai — hammers, nails ya bows nahi. [Q987]\n●\n\n⚠️Delhi ka naam independence ke baad nahi badla — baaki metro cities ka badla gaya. [Q988]\n●\n\n⚠️Amar Jawan Jyoti India Gate pe hai — Wagah Border, Gateway of India ya Jaisalmer War Memorial nahi.\n[Q989]\n●\n\n⚠️Ashoka Chakra \"Wheel of the law of dharma\" represent karta hai — prosperity, peace ya authority nahi.\n[Q992]\n●\n\n⚠️Hummingbird ka egg sabse chhota hai — sparrow, nightingale ya swallow nahi. [Q993]\n●\n\n⚠️Berana Sindhi wedding ceremony hai — Assamese, Bengali ya Manipuri nahi. [Q995]\n●\n\n⚠️Semi-Padmasan = Half Lily hai — Pigeon, Locust ya Frog nahi. [Q996]\n●\n\n⚠️Vesara style Chalukya dynasty ne introduce ki — Chola, Kakatiya ya Gupta nahi. [Q997]\n●\n\n⚠️Makarasan = Crocodile hai — Lion, Leopard ya Cobra nahi. [Q998]\n●\n\n⚠️Matsyasana = Fish hai — Simhasan (Lion), Padmasan (Lotus) ya Dhanurasan (Bow) nahi. [Q999]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Static GK Chapter 25 Miscellaneous Full Mind Map (Q943-Q1001)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0441","t":"01 Ancient History Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / History / Ancient History","x":[" SOURCES OF ANCIENT HISTORY — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Sources + 3 Field Names\n●Archaeological (Zameen se khudi cheezein) · Literary (Kitabein) · Foreign Travelers (Bahar se aaye log)\n●Field names: Archaeology = overall study · Epigraphy = sirf inscriptions · Numismatics = sirf sikke\n TRICK — \"ZKB\" chain\n💡\nZameen khudi (Archaeological) → Kitab padhi (Literary) → Bahar se aaya (Foreign) — teeno ka pehla letter bol ke\nchain yaad karo: Z-K-B.\nField names ke liye size yaad karo: Numismatics sabse chota scope (sirf sikke), Epigraphy medium (sirf abhilekh),\nArchaeology sabse bada (sab kuch). Chota→Bada: Numismatics, Epigraphy, Archaeology.\n2. 5 Inscriptions — Har Ek Ka Apna \"First\"\n●Boghazkoi (Turkey, 1400 BCE) → Aryan migration ka saboot\n●Maski & Gurjara → Ashoka ka asli naam likha mila\n●Prayag Prashasti (Harisena) → Samudragupta ki achievements\n●Eran Inscription (Bhanugupta) → Sati ka pehla likhit saboot\n●Bhitari Pillar (Skandagupta) → Huna invasion ka pehla record\n TRICK — Ek kahani mein pura chain\n💡\nSocho ek time-travel story: \"BOghazkoi mein Aryan Bhaage Iran se → MAski mein Ashoka ka naam mila\n(Devanampriya nahi, asli naam) → PRAyag mein Harisena ne Samudragupta ki tareef likhi → phir Eran mein Sati ho\ngayi (pehli baar likha gaya) → aakhir mein BHItari pe Huna aa dhamke (pehli baar record hua)\".\nShort-code yaad rakho: BO-MA-PRA-E-BHI (Boghazkoi, Maski, Prayag, Eran, Bhitari) — order alphabetically bhi hai\nroughly, so revise karte waqt yehi sequence bolo.\n3. Coins — 3 Dimensions, Confuse Mat Ho\n●Sabse purane: Aahat/Punch-marked (sirf symbol, likhawat nahi)\n●Pehle Gold: Indo-Greek\n●Sabse Zyada Gold: Gupta (Samudragupta — Veena wala sikka)\n●Sabse Pure Gold: Kushan\n TRICK — \"AIGK\" — Age se Purity tak\n💡\nOrder yaad karo time ke hisaab se: Aahat (sabse old, koi likhawat nahi) → Indo-Greek (pehli baar gold aaya) → Gupta\n(gold ki baarish — zyada quantity, Samudragupta ka Veena sikka) → Kushan (gold sabse shuddh, khaalis).\nEk line mein: \"Aahat mein likhawat nahi, Indo-Greek mein gold aaya, Gupta mein gold ki barsaat, Kushan mein gold\nsabse khaalis.\" — A-I-G-K bolke revise karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Pehla\" (First) → Indo-Greek. \"Sabse zyada\" (Most) → Gupta. \"Sabse pure\" (Purest) → Kushan. Teeno alag sawaal hain,\nek dusre se swap mat karna.\n4. Ajivika Caves — Dada-Pota Dono\n●Ashoka → Barabar Hills → 4 caves: Sudama, Karna Chaupad, Vishva Jhopdi, Lomas Rishi\n●Dasharatha (Ashoka ka pota) → Nagarjuni Hills → Gopi, Vedika, Vapiya (3 caves)\n TRICK — \"Bada-4, Chota-3\" trick\n💡"," Ashoka (bada/dada) → Barabar Hills — dono naam mein \"BAR\" common hai (Ashoka=bada, Barabar) → 4 caves.\nDasharatha (chota/pota) → Nagarjuni Hills → 3 caves. Yaad rakho: jo bada hai (Ashoka) uske paas zyada (4) caves\nhain, jo chota/pota hai (Dasharatha) uske paas kam (3).\n5. 4 Vedas — Sabse Zyada Confuse Karne Wala Topic\n●Rigveda → Sabse purana, stuti/mantron ka collection\n●Samaveda → Musical form, Sangeet ka pehla ullekh\n●Yajurveda → Yagya/rituals ke rules\n●Atharvaveda → Jaadu-tona, tantra-mantra\n TRICK — Ek line ka gaana\n💡\n\"Rig ne stuti gaayi (sabse purani), Sama ne sur mein gaayi (Sangeet), Yajur ne yagya karaya (rituals), Atharva ne jaadu\ndikhaya (tantra-mantra).\"\nSabse zyada confuse: Rig vs Sama — dono \"mantra\" lagte hain. Trick: Sama ka naam hi \"Sa-Re-Ga-Ma\" jaisa sunta hai\n→ isliye Sama = Music. Baaki Rig plain mantra hai.\n6. Author → Book — Direct Match Questions\n●Panini → Ashtadhyayi (Sanskrit grammar, pehli kitaab)\n●Kautilya/Chanakya → Arthashastra (Mauryan admin, political system ki pehli kitaab)\n●Kalhana → Rajatarangini (Kashmir history)\n●Patanjali → Mahabhashya (Post-Mauryan/Shunga period)\n TRICK — \"PAKK\" pairing\n💡\nPanini-Ashtadhyayi (grammar) → Kautilya-Arthashastra (admin) → Kalhana-Rajatarangini (Kashmir) → last one\nPatanjali-Mahabhashya (Post-Mauryan).\nVisual hook: Panini = grammar teacher (school), Kautilya = PM/minister (raj-kaaj), Kalhana = Kashmir ka reporter,\nPatanjali = yoga guru ne baad ka system likha (Post-Mauryan). Occupation se yaad rakho, naam se nahi.\n7. Greek Writers — Megasthenes Sabse Important\n●Herodotus → Father of History (kuch fiction bhi)\n●Ctesias → Iran ke raja ka royal physician\n●Megasthenes → Chandragupta Maurya ka ambassador → Indica\n●Ptolemy → Geography\n●Pliny → Natural History\n●Periplus of Erythraean Sea → Anonymous, trade/ports\n TRICK — Book-title = subject trick\n💡\n3 out of 6 ka book-naam hi unka subject bata deta hai — mat ratna, samajh lo: Geography (Ptolemy) = geography,\nNatural History (Pliny) = nature, Indica (Megasthenes) = India ka description.\nSirf 2 yaad rakhne hain bina hint ke: Herodotus = Father of History (fiction bhi), Ctesias = doctor tha Iran mein.\nPeriplus = anonymous, sirf \"trade/ports\" topic yaad rakho.\n8. Chinese Travelers — Saal Ginti Ka Trap\n●Faxian (402 CE) → Chandragupta II ke time → 14 saal\n●Sung Yun (518 CE) → 3 saal, Buddhist texts collect kiye\n●Xuanzang/Hiuen Tsang (630 CE) → Harshavardhana ke time → 15 saal → Si-Yu-Ki\n●I-Tsing (7th century end) → Nalanda/Vikramshila mein padhai"," TRICK — \"FSXI\" century order + number trick\n💡\nCentury ke hisaab se order: Faxian(5th) → Sung Yun(6th) → Xuanzang(7th) → I-Tsing(7th end). Yaad karo: \"Fast Se\nXerox Issue\" — F-S-X-I.\nSaal wala trap: Faxian = 14, Xuanzang = 15 — dono ek dusre se ek number door hain. Trick: \"Fa pehle aaya (4→F se),\ntoh usse chota number 14 milta hai; Xuan baad mein aaya, usse bada number 15\" — pehle wale ko chota number, baad\nwale ko bada number.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n14 saal = Faxian (Chandragupta II, 402 CE). 15 saal = Xuanzang (Harsha, 630 CE). Exam mein ye do numbers swap\nkarke poochte hain — hamesha \"Fa-14, Xuan-15\" bolke check karo.\n9. Arabic Writers & Others\n●Al-Biruni (1017 CE, Mahmud Ghazni ke saath) → Kitab-ul-Hind\n●Ibn Battuta (1333 CE, Muhammad bin Tughlaq ne Qazi banaya) → Rihla\n●Taranatha (Tibetan) → Kangyur & Tangyur\n●Marco Polo (Italian) → Pandya region visit\n TRICK — Naam se hi book yaad karo\n💡\nAl-Biruni ka book naam hi usme hai: Kitab-ul-Hind = \"India ki kitaab\" — seedha connect ho jaata hai.\nIbn Battuta = ghumakkad (traveler) tha, uski book ka naam Rihla khud hi \"Travelogue\" hai — matlab hi bata raha hai.\n1017 (Al-Biruni) vs 1333 (Ibn Battuta) — 300+ saal ka gap yaad rakho taaki timeline confuse na ho.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n🔗\n\"3 Sources: Zameen-Kitab-Bahar → Inscriptions: BO-MA-PRA-E-BHI → Coins: A-I-G-K → Caves: Ashoka-4,\nDasharatha-3 → Vedas: Rig-Sama-Yaju-Athar (Stuti-Sur-Yagya-Jaadu) → Texts: Panini-Kautilya-Kalhana-\nPatanjali → Greek: Megasthenes=Indica → Chinese: F-S-X-I (14-3-15-last) → Arabic: Al-Biruni(1017)-Ibn\nBattuta(1333)\"\nRoz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Coins: First=Indo-Greek, Most=Gupta, Purest=Kushan — kabhi swap mat karna.\n2) Chinese stay-years: Faxian=14, Xuanzang=15 — pehle wale ko chota number.\n3) Caves: Ashoka(dada)=Barabar=4 caves, Dasharatha(pota)=Nagarjuni=3 caves — bada wale ko zyada caves.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Sources of Ancient History"," PRE-HISTORIC AGE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Periods of Indian History — Likhawat Ka Khel\n●Prehistoric → Koi likhawat nahi\n●Protohistoric → Script hai lekin undeciphered (padhi nahi ja sakti) — isliye Bronze Age bhi kehte hain\n●Historic → Script hai AUR deciphered (padhi ja chuki hai) — ~600 BC ke baad\n TRICK — \"Locked vs Unlocked\" trick\n💡\nSocho script ek taala (lock) hai. Prehistoric mein taala hai hi nahi. Protohistoric mein taala hai par chaabi nahi mili\n(undeciphered — jaise Indus script). Historic mein taala khul chuka hai (deciphered).\nProtohistoric = \"proto\" matlab shuruaati/adhoora → adhoori samajh (undeciphered). Historic = poora record\n(deciphered).\n2. 4 Ages Ki Timeline — Ek Saath Yaad Karo\n●Paleolithic: 5,00,000 – 10,000 BCE\n●Mesolithic: 10,000 – 6,000 BCE\n●Neolithic: 6,000 – 1,000 BCE\n●Chalcolithic: ~3,000 – 1,000 BCE (Neolithic ke saath overlap karta hai)\n TRICK — \"PMNC\" — Old Man Now Copper\n💡\nSequence: Paleo → Meso → Neo → Chalco. English mein bol ke yaad rakho: \"Old (Paleo=old stone) Man\n(Meso=middle) Now (Neo=new) Copper (Chalco=copper aaya)\".\nNumbers ghatte jaate hain: 5,00,000 → 10,000 → 6,000 → 3,000 — funnel jaisa, jitna aage utna chota starting number.\n3. Paleolithic Ke 3 Sub-Phases — Tools Halke Se Sharp\n●Lower (5L–1L BCE): Hand axes, Cleavers, Choppers — bhari/basic\n●Middle (1L–40k BCE): Flakes, Borers, Perforators, Scrapers\n●Upper (40k–10k BCE): Blades, Flakes, Burins, Scrapers — sabse sharp\n TRICK — \"Haathi se Blade tak\" trick\n💡\nLower = Haathi jaisa bhaari Chopper (naam bhi \"lower/neeche giraane wala\" bhaari tool jaisa lagta hai).\nMiddle = beech ka size — Flake (patla lekin abhi bhi basic).\nUpper = sabse upar/advanced → patla, sharp Blade. Jitna upar jaao utna sharp —\nLower(bhaari)→Middle(medium)→Upper(sharp).\n4. Paleolithic Sites — Jaldi Match Karo\n●Belan Valley (UP) → Special: teeno phases ke tools yahin mile\n●Bhimbetka (MP) → Rock paintings (hunting/dancing scenes)\n●Patne (Maharashtra) → Ostrich egg evidence\n●Soan Valley (Punjab/Pak), Didwana (Rajasthan), Hunsgi (Karnataka), Nevasa (Maharashtra), Pahalgam (Kashmir)\n TRICK — 3-site memory hook\n💡\nBelan = \"Balanced\" — teeno phases balance karke yahin mile, isliye special.\nBhimbetka = Bhimta hua paint kiya — rock paintings yaad rakhne ke liye \"Bhim ne deewaar pe paint kiya\" socho.\nPatne mein Pane (bird) ka anda — Patne = ostrich egg (dono mein \"P\" sound se bird connect karo)."," 5. Mesolithic — Fire, Dog & Bagor\n●Lifestyle: Hunters & Pastoralists (kheti abhi nahi)\n●Climate: Warm (Holocene) · Tools: Microliths\n●First domesticated animal: Dog · Bagor (Rajasthan) = India ka sabse bada Mesolithic site\n●Adamgarh (MP) bhi ek important site hai\n TRICK — \"Fire Discover vs Use\" + Dog trick\n💡\nDiscovery of fire = Paleolithic. Control/widespread USE of fire = Mesolithic. Yaad rakho: \"Pehle milna\n(Paleo=discover), fir sambhalna (Meso=control)\" — D before C alphabetically bhi.\nDog = Mesolithic ka mascot. Burzahom (agla chapter-Neolithic) mein insaan-dog ko saath bury kiya gaya tha — dono\ncheezein Dog se connect karo taaki age confuse na ho (Dog domesticate hua Mesolithic mein, uska burial evidence mila\nNeolithic Burzahom mein).\nBagor = \"BA-gor\" — bolo \"BAda Ghar\" (bada ghar/site) — sabse bada Mesolithic site.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFire ki Invention/Discovery = Paleolithic. Fire ki Control/widespread Use = Mesolithic. Exam dono wording try karta\nhai — invention/discovery wale sawaal mein Paleolithic hi answer hai.\n6. Neolithic — Kheti Ki Shuruaat\n●Mehrgarh (Balochistan, c.7000 BCE) → Sabse purana agriculture site — Wheat, Barley, Cotton\n●Pottery + Wheel → Neolithic ke later stages mein invent\n●Burzahom (Kashmir) → Humans dogs ke saath bury kiye gaye\n●Gufkral (Kashmir) → \"Potters Caves\" — agriculture + animal domestication dono\n●Koldihwa (Belan Valley, UP) → Sabse purana rice cultivation (c.6000 BCE)\n●Chirand (Bihar) → Bone tools · Sanganakallu/Piklihal/Hallur (Karnataka) → Millet, ash mounds\n TRICK — \"Mehrgarh = Main crop, Koldihwa = Khichdi\" trick\n💡\nMehrgarh — Main overall agriculture site (wheat/barley) — \"M for Main\".\nKoldihwa — sirf rice ka record, so socho \"Koldihwa = Khichdi\" (rice dish) — sirf chawal ke liye famous, overall\nagriculture ke liye nahi.\nBurzahom vs Gufkral dono Kashmir mein hain: \"Bur-zahom\" mein z se \"zinda dogs ke saath dafnaya\" yaad karo;\nGufkral = \"Guf\" jaisa \"Gufa/Cave\" hi hai naam mein — Potters Caves.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Sabse purana agriculture\" → Mehrgarh (wheat & barley). \"Sabse purana rice\" → Koldihwa. Dono ek dusre se alag\nhain, swap mat karna.\n7. Chalcolithic — Copper + Stone, 5 Cultures\n●First metal: Copper · Sources: Malanjkhand (MP), Khetri Mines (Rajasthan) · Culture: Rural\n●Ahar/Banas (Rajasthan) → Metallurgy · Ancient naam Tambavati\n●Kayatha (Chambal valley) → Sturdy pottery\n●Rangpur (Gujarat coast) → Lustrous Red Ware\n●Malwa (Narmada valley) → Sabse fine/best pottery\n●Jorwe (Maharashtra) → Proto-urban · Daimabad = sabse bada Jorwe site\n●Inamgaon (Maharashtra) → Sabse bada Chalcolithic settlement overall — burial customs ka evidence\n TRICK — \"AKRMJ\" culture-region chain\n💡\nAhar-Rajasthan(metal) → Kayatha-Chambal(sturdy) → Rangpur-Gujarat(red ware) → Malwa-Narmada(finest) →\nJorwe-Maharashtra(proto-urban). Bolo: \"A-K-R-M-J\".\nAhar = \"tambavati\" naam mein hi tamba (copper) chhupa hai — metallurgy yaad rakhne ke liye bas naam padho.\nRangpur ka naam \"Rang\" (color) se shuru hota hai → seedha Red Ware se connect ho jaata hai."," Daimabad vs Inamgaon: Daimabad = Jorwe culture ka sabse bada site, Inamgaon = sabse bada Chalcolithic settlement\noverall (burial ke liye famous). \"Dai\" chota scope (ek culture), \"Inam\" bada scope (overall) — Inamgaon = Overall\nsocho (I aur O connect).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCulture ↔ Region match hamesha poochha jaata hai: Ahar=Rajasthan, Kayatha=MP(Chambal), Rangpur=Gujarat,\nMalwa=MP(Narmada), Jorwe=Maharashtra. Inamgaon ko Jorwe ka hi hissa maano (Maharashtra) par ye \"largest\nChalcolithic settlement overall\" hai, na ki sirf largest Jorwe site (wo Daimabad hai).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 Periods: Locked-Unlocked (Proto-Historic) → 4 Ages: PMNC (Old-Man-Now-Copper) → Paleolithic tools:\nHaathi→Blade (Lower-Middle-Upper) → Fire: Discover(Paleo)-Control(Meso) → Dog=Mesolithic first pet,\nBurzahom=Neolithic burial → Agriculture: Mehrgarh(Main)-Koldihwa(Khichdi/rice) → Chalcolithic: A-K-R-M-J\n(Ahar-Kayatha-Rangpur-Malwa-Jorwe) → Daimabad(Jorwe site)-Inamgaon(overall largest)\"\nRoz ek baar bolke revise karo — chain jitni baar dohraoge utni pakki hogi.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Fire: Discovery=Paleolithic, Control/Use=Mesolithic.\n2) Agriculture: Mehrgarh=overall (wheat/barley), Koldihwa=rice only.\n3) Largest sites: Bagor=Mesolithic, Daimabad=largest Jorwe site, Inamgaon=largest Chalcolithic settlement overall.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Pre-Historic Age"," INDUS VALLEY CIVILIZATION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Naming & Discovery — Discoverer vs Excavator\n●Naam Harappa site ke naam pe pada (pehla excavated site)\n●Dayaram Sahni (1921) → Harappa discover kiya\n●R.D. Banerjee (1922) → Mohenjo-daro excavate kiya\n●Sir John Marshall → poori excavation ka Director tha (khud discoverer nahi)\n TRICK — \"Sahni-Sahab pehle, Banerjee ek saal baad\" trick\n💡\nSahni = Sabse pehle (1921, Harappa). Banerjee = Baad mein (1922, Mohenjo-daro) — S before B, 1921 before 1922,\nseedha match hai.\nMarshall = \"Manager/Director\" socho — usne khud khudai nahi ki, sirf supervise kiya. Discoverer ka credit\nSahni/Banerjee ko jaata hai.\n2. 4 Extreme Corners — N-S-E-W\n●North: Manda (J&K) → River Chenab\n●South: Daimabad (Maharashtra) → River Pravara\n●East: Alamgirpur (UP) → River Hindon\n●West: Sutkagendor (Baluchistan) → River Dasht\n TRICK — \"MDAS\" trick\n💡\nN-S-E-W order mein: Manda → Daimabad → Alamgirpur → Sutkagendor = \"MDAS\". Bolo: \"Mera Dost Aaj Soya\" —\nek line yaad karo, letters match ho jaayenge.\nGeography se bhi connect karo: Manda sabse upar (North, J&K), Sutkagendor sabse bahar/door (West, Pakistan\nborder pe) — extremes ka feel rakho.\n3. Largest Sites Ranking — Rakhigarhi Sabse Bada\n●1. Rakhigarhi (Haryana, India) — sabse bada poore subcontinent mein\n●2. Mohenjo-daro (Pakistan)\n●3. Harappa (Pakistan)\n●4. Dholavira (Gujarat, India)\n TRICK — \"Rakhi No.1\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log sochte hain Mohenjo-daro sabse bada hai — NAHI. Rakhigarhi No.1 hai. Yaad rakho: \"Rakhi\nbandhne wali sabse badi behen hai\" — Rakhigarhi = No.1 hamesha.\nDholavira famous hai (3-part city ke liye) isliye log usse bada samajh lete hain — par wo sirf 4th hai, sabse bada nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"India ka sabse bada IVC site\" → Rakhigarhi, na ki Dholavira (jo sirf apni unique 3-part design ke liye famous hai, size\nke liye nahi).\n4. 9 Major Sites — Ek Site, Ek Signature Find\n●Harappa (Sahni,1921) → 12 granaries (6+6 rows), Unicorn seals, Cemetery R-37\n●Mohenjo-daro (Banerjee,1922) → Great Bath, Great Granary, Dancing Girl, Pashupati Seal, Priest King, Cotton cloth\n●Chanhudaro (Majumdar,1931) → Koi Citadel nahi, Bead-factory, Lipstick\n●Kalibangan (A.Ghosh,1951) → Ploughed fields (sabse purana), Fire altars, Camel bones"," ●Kot Diji (Fazal Ahmed,1953) → Bahut badi Fortification wall\n●Rangpur (S.R.Rao,1953-54) → Rice Husks\n●Ropar (Y.D.Sharma,1953-56) → Dog-burial, Independent India ka pehla excavated site\n●Lothal (S.R.Rao,1955-63) → Dockyard, Rice Grains, Double burial, Ivory scale, Doors main-street ki taraf (exception)\n●Banawali (Bisht,1974) → Toy Plough, High-quality Barley, Washbasin\n TRICK — Ek-word signature hook har site ke liye\n💡\nChanhudaro — \"Chance hi nahi mila Citadel ka\" — yaad rakho no-citadel site.\nKalibangan — \"Kali mitti mein khet jote gaye\" — ploughed fields se connect.\nRangpur = Randhawa jaisa naam, chawal ke chhilke (husk) — vs Lothal = poora chawal daana (grain) milta hai\n(dono opposite words, easy match: Husk chota/bekaar cheez → Rangpur; Grain poora/asli cheez → Lothal, jahan poori\ndockyard/city thi).\nRopar — \"Ro-par kutta bhi bury\" — dog burial yaad rakhne ke liye, aur ye \"pehla azaad India site\" bhi hai (R for\nRopar, R for Republic-India connect).\nS.R. Rao ne Rangpur AUR Lothal dono khode the — ek hi excavator, do sites, dono mein rice ka evidence\n(husk/grains) — isiliye ye dono aapas mein zyada confuse hote hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRice Husks = Rangpur. Rice Grains = Lothal. Dono S.R. Rao ne khode the isliye exam confuse karta hai — Husk\nchota/waste jaisa lagta hai (Rangpur, chota naam), Grain bada/asli (Lothal, bada dockyard site).\n5. Urban Planning — Citadel, Grid, Doors\n●Har sheher 2 parts: Citadel (upper/fortified) + Lower Town (residential) — sirf Dholavira 3 parts\n(Citadel+Middle+Lower)\n●Streets grid pattern (right angles), Baked bricks standard material\n●Doors back lanes ki taraf khulte the — Lothal exception: main street ki taraf\n●Great Granary (singular, sabse badi imarat) = Mohenjo-daro. 12 granaries (6+6 rows) = Harappa\n TRICK — \"2 vs 3, Great vs 12\" trick\n💡\nDholavira = \"Dho lo, ye 3 dhulaai hai\" — 3-part city yaad rakhne ka silly hook, baaki sab 2-part hi hain.\nGranary: \"Great (singular) = Mohenjo\" (dono capital G aur M alag lagte hain but socho \"Ghar Mohenjo mein bada hai\").\n\"12 = Harappa\" — 1+2=3 letters in \"Har\"appa jaisa kuch nahi, bas seedha ratna: Harappa=12(6+6).\nDoors: sab peeche khulte the (privacy), sirf Lothal mein seedha bahar (trade-town tha, dockyard ki wajah se shayad\nseedha access chahiye tha) — Lothal=trade hub=exception yaad rakho.\n6. Economy — Barter, Weights, Imports\n●Coins nahi the → Barter system · Measurement Decimal, weights base unit 16 (1,2,4,8,16,32...)\n●Seals: Steatite se bante the · Mesopotamian cylindrical seals — Kalibangan & Mohenjo-daro\n●Imports: Gold(Kolar/Afghanistan/Iran), Copper(Khetri/Baluchistan/Oman), Lapis Lazuli(Badakhshan), Tin(Central Asia)\n TRICK — \"Base-16\" and imports hook\n💡\nWeight base 16 — socho \"16 aane ka rupya\" (purani Hindi saying \"solaah aana sach\") — 16 se easily connect ho jaata\nhai purane Indian measurement se.\nLapis Lazuli ka sirf ek hi source yaad rakhna hai: Badakhshan (Afghanistan) — naam hi itna unique hai ki alag se\nyaad ho jaata hai.\n7. Religion — Pashupati & Funeral Rites\n●Mother Goddess sabse zyada worshipped · Pashupati Seal (Proto-Shiva) — Mohenjo-daro\n●Sacred: Humped bull, Lingam · Symbols: Swastika, Wheel, Cross\n●3 Funeral rites: Complete Burial (sabse common) → Partial Burial (pehle expose) → Cremation"," TRICK — \"D-E-R-T-B\" Pashupati animals + funeral order\n💡\nPashupati seal ke 5 jaanwar (already source ka mnemonic): Deer, Elephant, Rhino, Tiger, Buffalo — \"D-E-R-T-B\"\nbolke ratna.\nFuneral 3 tareeke: \"Complete (poora) → Partial (aadha) → Cremation (jala do)\" — socho ek scale: poora body →\naadha body → koi body nahi (raakh). Kam hoti body ki matra se yaad rakho.\n8. Script & Decline Theories\n●Script: Pictographic, 64 signs + 250-400 pictographs, undeciphered · Direction: Boustrophedon (R→L, phir L→R)\n●Sabse zyada symbol: Fish · Sabse zyada shape: U-shape\n●Gordon Childe & Wheeler → Aryan Invasion · Marshall/Mackay/S.R.Rao → Floods · Aurel Stein/A.N.Ghosh →\nClimate Change · M.R.Sahni → Geological/Tectonic · K.A.R.Kennedy → Epidemic/Malaria\n TRICK — \"Boustrophedon = Bail ka Hal\" + Scholar hooks\n💡\nBoustrophedon yaad rakhne ke liye: naam mein hi \"bous\" (Greek for ox/bail) hai — jaise bail hal chalate waqt line ke\nend pe mudta hai (zig-zag), waisi hi likhawat thi — R→L phir L→R.\nScholars: Wheeler+Childe = War/Invasion (dono \"war-like\" naam se lagte hain — Wheeler=weapon jaisa sound).\nKennedy = Keetanu (germs/epidemic — Ken~Kee rhyme). Baaki (Marshall-Floods, Stein-Climate, Sahni-Geological)\nalag-alag one-line match kar lo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSabse popular/famous theory Aryan Invasion (Childe & Wheeler) hai, lekin exam floods/climate/epidemic bhi seedha\npoochta hai — sab scholar-theory pairs yaad rakho, sirf Aryan Invasion pe atko mat.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Sahni(1921,Harappa)→Banerjee(1922,Mohenjo) → NSEW: MDAS → Largest: Rakhi-Mohenjo-Harappa-Dholavira\n→ Sites: Chanhudaro(no citadel)-Kalibangan(plough)-Rangpur(husk)-Lothal(grain+dockyard)-Ropar(1st-Independent)\n→ Granary: Great=Mohenjo,12=Harappa → Doors: Lothal exception → Pashupati animals: D-E-R-T-B → Funeral:\nComplete→Partial→Cremation → Decline: Childe/Wheeler=Invasion, Kennedy=Epidemic\"\nIsko roz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Discoverer vs Excavator: Sahni=Harappa(1921), Banerjee=Mohenjo-daro(1922), Marshall=sirf Director.\n2) Largest site: Rakhigarhi (NOT Mohenjo-daro, NOT Dholavira).\n3) Rice: Rangpur=Husks, Lothal=Grains — dono S.R.Rao ne khode the.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Indus Valley Civilization"," VEDIC AGE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Rigvedic vs Later Vedic — Khula Samaaj → Rigid Samaaj\n●Rigvedic: Sapta-Sindhu, Copper/Bronze, Tribal life, King NOT hereditary, Women in Sabha+Vidatha, Pashupalan main\n●Later Vedic: PGW pottery, Iron widespread, King HEREDITARY, Women BANNED from Sabha/Samiti, Vidatha\ngaayab, Kuru kingdom-Hastinapur\n TRICK — \"Khula → Band\" ek-line trick\n💡\nEk hi direction mein sab kuch move karta hai: khula → band. Society khuli thi (women shamil) → band ho gayi\n(women banned). King select hota tha → fixed/hereditary ho gaya. Copper (soft metal) → Iron (hard/rigid metal) —\nmetal khud hi \"softness→hardness\" society ke \"open→rigid\" jaisa hai.\nYaad rakhne ka ek line: \"Jaise metal sakht hua (Iron), waise samaaj bhi sakht ho gaya (rigid).\"\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nWomen Rigvedic mein Sabha+Vidatha mein thi → Later Vedic mein Sabha+Samiti se BAN (Vidatha khud hi gayab ho\ngayi thi). King select→hereditary shift bhi saath yaad rakho.\n2. Sapta-Sindhu — 7 Nadiyan + Ancient↔Modern Naam\n●7 Rivers: Indus, Jhelum, Chenab, Beas, Ravi, Sutlej, Sarasvati (Naditama = Best River)\n●Vitasta=Jhelum · Asikuni=Chenab · Parushni=Ravi · Vipasha=Beas · Shatudri=Sutlej · Sarasvati=Ghaggar ·\nKubha=Kabul · Gomal=Gomati\n TRICK — \"VAPS-SKG\" naam-jodi trick\n💡\nHar purana naam ke pehle letter ko modern naam se jodo: Vitasta→Jhelum (V-J), Asikuni→Chenab (A-C),\nParushni→Ravi (P-R), Shatudri→Sutlej (S-S, same letter — easy), Vipasha→Beas (V-B).\nChhota trick line: \"Vitasta ne Jhelum mein Asi (sword) Chalayi, Parushni ne Ravi ko Vipasha Bana diya, Shatudri\nSutlej ban gaya\" — bas ek baar ye kahani padh lo, pairs khud yaad rahenge.\n3. Veda-Trayi vs Samhita — Sabse Bada Trap\n●Samhita = SAARE 4 Vedas (collectively)\n●Veda-Trayi = SIRF 3 Vedas — Rig + Sama + Yajur (Atharvaveda ISME NAHI)\n TRICK — \"Trayi = Teen\" trick\n💡\nTrayi shabd mein hi \"tra-yi\" (teen/three) chhupa hai — jaise \"trimurti\" mein teen. Isliye Veda-Trayi = sirf 3 Vedas.\nAtharvaveda sabse naya (newest) Veda hai — isliye purani \"Trayi\" (teeno purane) mein wo shamil nahi — naya wala\nclub se bahar.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVeda-Trayi mein Atharvaveda shamil NAHI hai. Samhita = sab 4. Ye do terms similar lagte hain par bilkul alag scope\nhain.\n4. 4 Vedas — Priest + Upaveda + Brahmana\n●Rigveda: Hymns · Brahmana: Aitareya, Kaushitaki\n●Samaveda: Song/Music · Priest: Udgata · Upaveda: Gandharvaveda · Upanishads: Chandogya, Kena\n●Yajurveda: Yagya/Sacrifice · Priest: Adhvaryu · Upaveda: Dhanurveda(Archery) · Brahmana: Shatapatha\n●Atharvaveda: Tantra-Mantra · Priest: Brahma · Brahmana: Gopatha · Also called Brahmaveda"," TRICK — Priest-Veda match hook\n💡\nUdgata = Upgaata (gaane wala) → Samaveda (music/gaana).\nAdhvaryu = Amal mein laata (practical rituals) → Yajurveda (Yagya ke practical steps).\nBrahma (khud hi ek naam hai) → Atharvaveda ka priest — kyunki ye alag/unique Veda hai to uska priest bhi unique\nnaam wala (Udgata/Adhvaryu nahi).\nUpaveda: Dhanurveda(archery) = Yajur se (Yagya-Yodha connect), Gandharvaveda(music) = SamaVeda se (dono\nmusic-related).\n5. Rigveda Mention Counts — Exact Numbers\n●Indra: 289 (sabse zyada) · Agni: 218 · Vishnu: 100 · Varuna: 46 · Yamuna: 3 · Ganga: 1 · Prithvi: 1\n TRICK — \"289-218-100-46\" ghatta hua trick\n💡\nNumbers hamesha ghatte jaate hain jaise importance ghatti: Indra(289, war god, sabse powerful) → Agni(218,\nmediator) → Vishnu(100) → Varuna(46, water god).\nGanga sirf 1 baar — yaad rakho \"Rigveda ke time Aryans Ganga se bahut door the (Sapta-Sindhu mein)\" — isliye itni\nkam mention. Ye ek shocking/counter-intuitive fact hai isliye khud hi yaad reh jaata hai.\n6. Rigveda Mandalas — 3, 9, 10\n●Mandala 3 → Vishwamitra → Gayatri Mantra (Savitri devta)\n●Mandala 9 → Soma devta (plant god)\n●Mandala 10 → Sabse latest → Purusha Sukta (4 varna)\n TRICK — \"3-9-10\" trick\n💡\n3 = Vishwamitra (3 aur wa milte-julte lagte hain, bas yaad rakho 3=Vishwamitra=Gayatri).\n10 = sabse badi/latest number hai list mein → \"sabse naya/last Mandala\" bhi 10 hi hai — dono match ho jaate hain\n(number bhi bada, naya bhi hai).\n9 ek hi bacha — usko Soma se jod do bas (process of elimination bhi kaam aayega exam mein).\n7. Upanishads — 4 Famous Pairs\n●Chandogya → Sabse Purana + Devaki-Krishna ka pehla mention\n●Brihadaranyaka → Gargi-Yajnavalkya dialogue\n●Kathopanishad → Yama-Nachiketa dialogue\n●Mundaka → \"Satyameva Jayate\"\n TRICK — Naam se hi connect karo\n💡\nKathopanishad = Katha (story) → Yama-Nachiketa ki kahani/katha.\nMundaka = National motto \"Satyameva Jayate\" ka \"mun\" (mouth se bola jaane wala vaakya) — ya bas seedha ratt lo:\nMundaka=Motto.\nBrihadaranyaka = sabse bada (Brihad) naam → uska dialogue bhi 2 famous logo (Gargi+Yajnavalkya) ke beech —\n\"bada naam, bada dialogue\".\nChandogya = \"Chand\" (moon) se shuru → sabse purana/oldest, jaise chand bhi purane time se dikhta aaya hai.\n8. 6 Vedangas — Mukh & Kaan Wala Trap\n●Shiksha(Phonetics), Kalpa(Rituals), Vyakaran = Mukh/Mouth, Nirukta = Kaan/Ears, Chhanda(Metrics),\nJyotisha(Astronomy)\n TRICK — \"Vyakaran bolta hai, Nirukta sunta hai\" trick\n💡\nVyakaran (Grammar) = Mukh (Mouth) — grammar sahi ho tabhi sahi bola jaata hai, isliye Mouth."," Nirukta (Etymology/meaning) = Kaan (Ears) — matlab samajhne ke liye sunna/samajhna padta hai, isliye Ears.\nBolne (Mukh) se pehle grammar chahiye, samajhne (Kaan) ke liye meaning/etymology chahiye — dono ka role apne\nnaam mein hi chhupa hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Vedon ka Mukh\" → Vyakarana. \"Vedon ke Kaan\" → Nirukta. Ye seedha ulta poochha jaata hai, dono ko unke function\nse yaad rakho (bolna vs samajhna).\n9. Mahabharata, Ramayana & Puranas\n●Mahabharata: Jaya Samhita(8,800) → Bharata(24,000) → Mahabharata(1 Lakh) — 18 Parvas\n●Ramayana: 6,000→24,000 verses — 7 Kandas — Chaturvimshati Sahasri Samhita\n●Puranas: 18 total · Matsya=Satavahana+10 Avatars · Vishnu=Mauryan · Vayu=Gupta\n TRICK — \"8800→24000→1Lakh\" growth + Purana-dynasty hook\n💡\nMahabharata ka size triple-jump kiya: 8.8k(Jaya) → 24k(Bharata, ~3x) → 1 Lakh(Mahabharata, ~4x) — bas yaad\nrakho ye ek kahani jitni baar sunayi gayi utni badi hoti gayi.\nVishnu Purana = Mauryan (V aur M mile-jule alphabet position mein nahi hain but bas seedha ratt lo: V-M).\nVayu Purana = Gupta — dono naam mein koi direct hook nahi, isliye bas ek line: \"Vayu ne Gupt-roop mein udaan\nbhari\" (Vayu=air, Gupta ke sath udaan/flight jod diya).\nMatsya Purana = Vishnu ka Matsya avatar khud isi Purana mein describe hota hai — naam khud hi hint de raha hai\n(Matsya=fish=1st avatar of Vishnu's 10).\n10. Rigvedic Assemblies & Officials\n●Sabha = Elites/Buzurgo · Samiti = Aam Janta · Vidatha = Sabse purani, loot-baantwara\n●Purohita sabse important officer — Vishwamitra(Liberal) vs Vashistha(Conservative) · Senani=Army chief ·\nGomat=Ameer vyakti\n●Jana (~275 mentions, sabse badi unit) > Vish (~170 mentions)\n TRICK — \"S-S-V\" aur Purohita rivalry trick\n💡\nSabha=Senior(buzurg), Samiti=Sabke liye(aam janta), Vidatha=Very old (sabse purani) — teeno S-S-V bolo aur unke\nfunction yaad aa jaayenge.\nDo Purohit rivals: Vishwamitra = Vishwa (world/broad-minded) = Liberal. Vashistha = \"Vashibhoot\" (rules ka\npabandh) = Conservative/Orthodox.\nJana > Vish — \"Janata hamesha bade se bada group hoti hai\" (Jana=biggest unit, phir Vish chota).\n11. Later Vedic Ratnins — 12 Officials\n●King, Yuvraj(Prince), Purohit(Advisor), Mahishi(Chief Queen), Palagala(Messenger), Govikrit(Forest),\nKshetrapal(Guard), Akshavapa(Dice/Accountant), Sangrahita(Treasurer), Bhagadugha(Tax), Gramani(Village Head),\nSuta(Charioteer/Bard)\n TRICK — Total number + funny-role hook\n💡\nShatapatha Brahmana mein exactly 12 Ratnins — \"12\" ko \"12 mahine, 12 officials\" bolke ratt lo (calendar se link).\nSabse confuse karne wale 3: Akshavapa = King ka \"dice-partner\" (Aksha=dice) — funny/unusual role isliye alag se\nyaad rakho. Sangrahita = \"Sangrah\" (collect/store) = Treasurer. Bhagadugha = \"Bhaag\" (share/portion) = Tax/Revenue\ncollector — dono naam mein hi kaam chhupa hai.\n12. 6 Classical Schools — Sage Matching\n●Sankhya→Kapila (sabse purani) · Nyaya→Gautama · Yoga→Patanjali · Vaisheshika→Kanada (Atom theory) ·\nPurva Mimamsa→Jaimini · Uttara Mimamsa(Vedanta)→Badarayana"," TRICK — \"KGP-KJB\" chain\n💡\nOrder se bolo: Kapila(Sankhya) → Gautama(Nyaya) → Patanjali(Yoga) → Kanada(Vaisheshika) →\nJaimini(PurvaMimamsa) → Badarayana(UttaraMimamsa). Short-code: \"K-G-P-K-J-B\".\nKanada naam mein hi \"Kan\" (particle/grain) hai → Atom theory se seedha match, easy hook.\nSabse pehle ye 3 pakke karo (source ka bhi yehi advice hai): Sankhya-Kapila, Vaisheshika-Kanada, Yoga-Patanjali.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Rigvedic(khula)→Later Vedic(band) → Sapta-Sindhu 7 rivers, Naditama=Sarasvati → Veda-Trayi=3(no Athar) vs\nSamhita=4 → Priests: Udgata(Sama)-Adhvaryu(Yaju)-Brahma(Athar) → Mentions: Indra289-Agni218 → Mandala\n3(Vishwamitra)-9(Soma)-10(Purusha Sukta) → Upanishads: Chandogya(oldest)-Brihadaranyaka(Gargi)-\nKathopanishad(Nachiketa)-Mundaka(Satyameva) → Vedanga: Vyakaran=Mukh,Nirukta=Kaan → Mahabharata\n8800→24000→1Lakh → Puranas: Vishnu=Mauryan,Vayu=Gupta,Matsya=Satavahana → Philosophy: K-G-P-K-J-B\"\nRoz ek baar bolke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Veda-Trayi (3 Vedas, no Atharva) vs Samhita (all 4).\n2) King: Rigvedic=selected, Later Vedic=hereditary. Women: Rigvedic=participate, Later Vedic=banned.\n3) Vyakarana=Mouth of Vedas, Nirukta=Ears of Vedas — direct opposite-poochha jaata hai.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Vedic Age"," JAINISM — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Mahavira vs Parshvanath — Founder Ka Trap\n●Parshvanath (23rd) → 4 vows diye (Ahimsa, Satya, Asteya, Aparigraha) · Snake Hood symbol\n●Mahavira (24th) → Asli Founder maane jaate hain · 5th vow Brahmacharya add kiya · Lion symbol\n TRICK — \"23 se 24, 4 se 5\" trick\n💡\nNumber seedha match hota hai: 23rd Tirthankar ne 4 vows diye, 24th ne 5vaan add kiya. Jitna number bada utna vow\nbada — 23→4, 24→5.\n\"Founder kaun?\" → hamesha last/latest wala hi organizer/founder hota hai — Mahavira (24th, sabse aakhri) ne dharm\nko poora organize kiya, isliye founder credit unhi ko.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Jainism ke Sansthapak (Founder)\" → Mahavira, na ki Parshvanath (jinhone sirf 4 vows diye the, dharm sthapit nahi\nkiya).\n2. Mahavira Ki Life — 3 Alag Jagah, Confuse Mat Ho\n●Janm: Kundagram, Vaishali (Bihar) · Clan: Jnatrika (Kshatriya)\n●Gyaan-prapti: Jrimbhikagrama (Rijupalika nadi ke kinare) · 12 saal tapasya\n●Nirvana: Pavapuri (Rajgir ke paas, Bihar) · 72 saal ki umar\n●Family: Pita Siddhartha · Mata Trishala (Chetak ki behen) · Patni Yashoda · Beti Priyadarshana · Damaad/1st shishya\nJamali\n TRICK — \"Kun-Jrim-Pava\" trick\n💡\n3 jagah, 3 stage: Kundagram=Kunwara (bachpan, birth) → Jrimbhikagrama=Gyaan (gyaan milne ki jagah, naam mein\nhi \"jrim\" jaise \"gyaan ki jhalak\") → Pavapuri=Paar (life ka paar/end, nirvana).\nFamily hook: Trishala ne Mahavira ko janma, aur unka pehla shishya khud unka damaad Jamali bana — \"ghar ka hi\nbanda pehla follower bana\" — yaad rakhne layak family-twist.\n3. Royal Patrons — Chandragupta Jain, Bindusara Ajivika!\n●Chandragupta Maurya → Jain · Bhadrabahu ke saath Shravanabelagola gaye · Sallekhana kiya\n●Bindusara (Chandragupta ka beta) → Ajivika sect — Jain NAHI!\n●Bimbisara → Mahavira ke contemporary · Jain texts mein naam \"Shrenika\"\n●Kharavela → Kalinga raja · Amoghavarsha → Rashtrakuta\n TRICK — \"Baap Jain, Beta Ajivika\" trick\n💡\nSabse common galti: log sochte hain baap-beta dono Jain honge. NAHI — Chandragupta=Jain, Bindusara=Ajivika.\nYaad rakho: \"Baap ne Jain dharm chuna, par bete ne apna alag raasta (Ajivika) chun liya\" — generational\nrebellion jaisa socho.\nBimbisara = Shrenika — dono naam mein koi similarity nahi, bas seedha ratt lo: \"Shrenika shreni/rank wala raja —\nBimbisara bhi ek powerful/high-rank raja tha.\"\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChandragupta Maurya = Jain (Sallekhana kiya). Bindusara (uska beta) = Ajivika sect. Pita-putra alag dharm follow karte\nthe — mix mat karo.\n4. Digambara vs Shwetambara — Bada Split"," ●Shwetambara (White-clad) → Leader Sthulabhadra · North India (Magadha) · Women Moksha pa sakti hain\n●Digambara (Sky-clad, no clothes) → Leader Bhadrabahu · South India (Karnataka) · Chandragupta inke saath gaye\n TRICK — \"Sthula-North, Bhadra-South\" trick\n💡\nSthulabhadra = \"Sthul (sthir/settled)\" — wahi North mein settled reh gaye (nahi gaye kahin).\nBhadrabahu = \"bahu door tak gaye\" (bahu = arm/reach, door tak pahunche) — South tak chale gaye, Chandragupta ko\nsaath lekar.\nDigambara = \"Dig + Ambar (disha hi kapda/aakash hi vastra)\" — naam mein hi \"no clothes, sky-clad\" chhupa hai.\nShwetambara = \"Shwet (white)\" — naam mein hi white clothes.\n5. 2 Jain Councils\n●1st: Pataliputra (Bihar) · 300 BCE · President Sthulabhadra · 12 Angas compile · Yahin BADA SPLIT hua\n●2nd: Vallabhi (Gujarat) · 512 CE · President Devardhi Kshamashraman · 12 Angas+12 Upangas final\n TRICK — \"Pata-Split, Vallabhi-Final\" trick\n💡\nPataliputra = \"Pat gaya\" (toot gaya/split ho gaya) — yahin split hua tha, easy wordplay.\nVallabhi = \"Val-lock/final seal\" — yahan final compilation hui (Upangas add hokar poora hua).\nJain councils sirf 2 hain (Buddhist councils se zyada — wo 4 thi), aur Jain councils ki jagah alag hain (Pataliputra,\nVallabhi) — Buddhist wali (Rajgir, Vaishali, Pataliputra, Kashmir) se confuse mat karo, sirf Pataliputra common hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJain 2nd council Vallabhi (Gujarat) mein hui thi — Buddhist councils se confuse mat karo, wo\nRajgir/Vaishali/Pataliputra/Kashmir mein hoti thi.\n6. Tri-Ratna, 5 Vows, Syadvada\n●Tri-Ratna: Samyak Gyan (Right Knowledge) + Samyak Darshan (Right Faith) + Samyak Charitra (Right Conduct)\n●5 Vows: Ahimsa, Satya, Asteya, Aparigraha (Parshvanath) + Brahmacharya (Mahavira, 5th)\n●Syadvada/Anekantavada = \"Theory of Relativity\" — maybe/multiple-angles philosophy\n TRICK — \"GDC\" and \"Maybe\" trick\n💡\nTri-Ratna order: Gyan(Knowledge) → Darshan(Faith) → Charitra(Conduct) = \"G-D-C\" — jaanna(G) → maanna(D) →\nkarna(C), ek natural sequence hai (pehle jaano, phir vishwas karo, phir amal karo).\nSyadvada = \"Syad\" khud sanskrit mein \"shayad/maybe\" hi hota hai — naam se hi seedha meaning nikal aata hai.\n7. Mahavira Ke Samkalin Sects\n●Ajivika — Makkhali Gosala — Niyati/Fatalism (sab pehle se tay)\n●Materialist — Ajita Kesakambalin — Ucchedavada (marne ke baad kuch nahi bachta)\n●Agnostic — Sanjaya Belatthiputta — Suspension of judgment (koi definite jawab nahi)\n TRICK — 3 sects, 3 attitudes\n💡\nAjivika = \"sab fix hai\" (destiny), Materialist = \"sab khatam ho jaata hai\" (nothing after death), Agnostic = \"pata nahi\"\n(no answer). Teeno ek scale pe: Certain(Ajivika) → Nihilistic(Materialist) → Unsure(Agnostic).\nSanjaya naam khud \"sanshay\" (doubt) jaisa sound karta hai → Agnostic/doubt philosophy se seedha match.\n8. Jain Literature — Agama\n●Language: Prakrit (Ardha-Magadhi) · Structure: 12 Angas+12 Upangas+10 Prakirnakas+6 Cheda+4 Moola Sutras\n●Kalpa Sutra (Bhadrabahu) → Tirthankaro ki biographies\n●Bhagavati Sutra → Mahavira jeevan + 16 Mahajanapadas ki list\n●Acharanga Sutra → Monk conduct rules · Parishishtaparvan → Hemchandra Suri"," TRICK — \"Kalpa=Bio, Bhagavati=List\" trick\n💡\nKalpa Sutra = \"Kalendar/history\" jaisa lagta hai → Tirthankaro ki biography/history.\nBhagavati = \"Bhag\" (part/division) — 16 Mahajanapadas ki list (divisions of India) yahin milti hai — dono mein\n\"division\" ka concept common hai.\n9. Architecture — Caves, Temples, Statue\n●Hathigumpha Caves (Odisha) → King Kharavela\n●Dilwara Jain Temple (Mount Abu) → Vimal Shah · Luna Vasahi → Vastupal & Tejpal\n●Pattadakal Jain Temple → Rashtrakuta (Amoghavarsha I)\n●Gommateshwara/Bahubali Statue (Shravanabelagola, Karnataka) → Chamundaraya (Ganga Dynasty minister)\n TRICK — One builder-one monument hook\n💡\nKharavela-Hathigumpha: dono \"K/H\" Odisha se related, seedha ek jagah ek raja.\nChamundaraya-Gommateshwara: \"Chamundaraya\" ne bahubali (Gommateshwara) banwaya — naam mein \"raya\"\n(king's minister) yaad rakho, statue Shravanabelagola mein hai jahan Chandragupta bhi gaye the (dono jagah connect ho\njaati hai).\n10. Tirthankara Symbols — Match The Following\n●1st Rishabhdev=Bull · 2nd Ajitnath=Elephant · 3rd Sambhavnath=Horse · 7th Suparshvanath=Swastika\n●19th Mallinath=Pitcher · 21st Naminatha=Blue Lotus · 22nd Arishtanemi=Conch · 23rd Parshvanath=Snake Hood ·\n24th Mahavira=Lion\n TRICK — Top-4 symbols pehle pakka karo\n💡\nSabse zyada poochhe jaane wale 4: Mahavira=Lion (raja/brave), Parshvanath=Snake (naag), Rishabhdev=Bull (1st\nhi to \"bailon jaisa mazboot\"), Arishtanemi=Conch (Krishna ke cousin, conch=Krishna se bhi juda symbol hota hai).\nBaaki: 2-Elephant, 3-Horse (\"E se Elephant, jaise 2nd number bhi E jaisa lagta hai\" bas order se ratt lo: 1-Bull,2-\nElephant,3-Horse — teen bade jaanwar shuruaati 3 numbers mein).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahavira = Lion, NOT Bull (Bull Rishabhdev ka hai). Symbols ko number ke saath hi lock karo, naam se guess mat\nkaro.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Parshvanath(23,4vows)→Mahavira(24,5th vow Brahmacharya, Founder) → Life: Kundagram(janm)-\nJrimbhikagrama(gyaan)-Pavapuri(nirvana) → Chandragupta=Jain, Bindusara=Ajivika → Bimbisara=Shrenika → Split:\nSthulabhadra(North,Shwetambara) vs Bhadrabahu(South,Digambara) → Councils: Pataliputra(300BCE,split)-\nVallabhi(512CE,final) → Tri-Ratna: G-D-C → Sects: Ajivika-Materialist-Agnostic → Symbols: Mahavira=Lion,\nParshvanath=Snake, Rishabhdev=Bull\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Founder = Mahavira (24th), NOT Parshvanath (23rd, sirf 4 vows diye).\n2) Chandragupta Maurya = Jain, Bindusara (uska beta) = Ajivika sect.\n3) Digambara(South,Bhadrabahu,no clothes) vs Shwetambara(North,Sthulabhadra,white clothes) — mix mat karo."," Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Jainism"," BUDDHISM — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Buddha Ki Family & Key Terms\n●Pita Shuddhodana (Shakya) · Mata Maya Devi (Koliya) · Stepmother Prajapati Gautami (First Bhikkhuni) · Patni\nYashodhara · Beta Rahul (=Bond)\n●Renunciation=Mahabhinishkramana · Enlightenment=Sambodhi/Nirvana · First Sermon=Dharmachakra\nPravartana · Death=Mahaparinirvana\n TRICK — \"Stepmom = First Nun\" hook\n💡\nPrajapati Gautami — Maya Devi guzar gayi to isne Buddha ko pala, aur baad mein khud Sangha ki pehli Bhikkhuni\nbani — \"jisne pala, wahi pehli follower bhi bani\" ek hi line mein dono fact chipak jaate hain.\nRahul = Bandhan (Fetter) — Buddha ne khud apne bete ka naam \"bandhan\" rakha, matlab unhe pata tha ki family\nattachment hi unke ghar chodne mein rukawat hai — is emotional logic se naam yaad rahega.\n2. 7 Life Events — Har Event Ka Apna Symbol\n●Conception=White Elephant · Birth=Lotus/Bull · Renunciation=Horse · Enlightenment=Bodhi Tree · First\nSermon=Wheel · Nirvana=Footprints · Death=Stupa\n TRICK — Sabse zyada poochhe jaane wale 2 symbols\n💡\nGhar chodna = Horse — Buddha ghode (Kanthaka) pe baithke hi bhaage the, seedha connect.\nPehla updesh = Wheel (Chakra) — \"Dharma-chakra\" naam mein hi \"chakra/wheel\" hai — term aur symbol dono\nmatch karte hain.\n3. 4 Sights → Renunciation (29 Saal)\n●Old Man(Aging) → Sick Man(Disease) → Corpse(Death) → Ascetic(Peace/Raasta)\n●Ghoda: Kanthaka · Charioteer: Channa · Umar: 29 saal\n TRICK — \"3 Problems + 1 Solution\" trick\n💡\nPehle 3 sights problems hain (Old-Sick-Dead = zindagi ki 3 buraiyaan), 4th sight (Ascetic) solution hai. Order: 3 dukh\ndikhe, phir 1 raasta dikha.\nKanthaka(ghoda) + Channa(sarthi) — dono naam \"K\" aur \"Ch\" se, alag rakho: \"Kanthaka = Chalne wala (ghoda\nchalta hai), Channa = Chalane wala (sarthi chalata hai)\".\n4. Gurus, Enlightenment & Sermons\n●Guru 1: Alara Kalama (Vaishali, Sankhya) · Guru 2: Udraka Ramaputta (Rajagriha, advanced meditation)\n●5 Ascetics (Uruvela): Kaundinya, Vappa, Bhaddiya, Mahanama, Assaji\n●Enlightenment: 35 saal, Bodh Gaya, Niranjana nadi, Vaishakh Purnima\n●First Sermon → Sarnath (Deer Park) · Most Sermons → Shravasti (Kosala)\n TRICK — \"First vs Most\" trick\n💡\nSarnath = \"Sar\" (sabse pehla/head) → first sermon yahin.\nShravasti = \"Shravak zyada the\" (sunne wale bahut the, Kosala ki capital, bada city) → isliye sabse zyada sermons\nyahin diye — bada shehar, zyada log, zyada updesh.\nDo gurus: Alara pehla (A for pehla/Alphabetically bhi A) → Udraka doosra.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPehla sermon = Sarnath (Deer Park). Sabse zyada sermons = Shravasti (Kosala). Dono alag jagah hain, mix mat karo."," 5. 4 Noble Truths + 8-Fold Path\n●Dukkha(suffering hai) → Samudaya(cause=Desire) → Nirodha(ant possible hai) → Nirodhagamini\nPratipada(raasta=8-fold path)\n●8 Steps: Right View, Resolve, Speech, Action, Livelihood, Effort, Mindfulness, Concentration\n TRICK — \"Doctor ka Checkup\" trick\n💡\n4 Truths = ek doctor visit jaisa: (1) Bimari hai (Dukkha) → (2) Karan pata karo (Samudaya=Desire) → (3) Ilaaj\npossible hai (Nirodha) → (4) Dawai/Prescription (8-fold Path). Ye sequence kabhi mat bhoolo.\n8-fold path yaad rakhne ke liye bas \"Right + 8 areas of life\" socho: View-Resolve-Speech-Action-Livelihood-Effort-\nMindfulness-Concentration — pehla letter chain \"VRSALEMC\" bana lo agar zaroorat pade.\n6. 4 Buddhist Councils — Sabse Important Topic\n●1st (483BCE, Rajagriha, Mahakasyapa, Ajatashatru) → Sutta+Vinaya Pitaka compile\n●2nd (383BCE, Vaishali, Sabakami, Kalashoka) → PEHLA split: Sthaviravadins vs Mahasanghikas\n●3rd (250BCE, Pataliputra, Moggalliputta Tissa, Ashoka) → Abhidhamma Pitaka compile\n●4th (72AD, Kashmir, Vasumitra, Kanishka) → FINAL split: Hinayana vs Mahayana\n TRICK — \"Ra-Va-Pa-Ku\" + \"Aj-Ka-A-K\" (source ka apna mnemonic)\n💡\nPlaces: Rajagriha → Vaishali → Pataliputra → Kushmir(Kashmir) = \"Ra-Va-Pa-Ku\".\nRulers: Ajatashatru → Kalashoka → Ashoka → Kanishka = \"Aj-Ka-A-K\".\nSplits sirf 2nd aur 4th mein hue — even-numbered councils mein split, odd-numbered (1st,3rd) mein sirf compilation.\nYaad rakho: \"Even=Split, Odd=Compile\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n2nd Council = PEHLA split (Sthaviravadins/Mahasanghikas). 4th Council = FINAL split (Hinayana/Mahayana). 1st aur\n3rd mein koi split nahi hua, sirf Pitaka compile hui.\n7. Hinayana vs Mahayana vs Vajrayana\n●Hinayana: Pali · No idol worship · Individual salvation (Arhat)\n●Mahayana: Sanskrit · Idol worship (Buddha=God) · Bodhisattva · Salvation for ALL\n●Vajrayana: Tantric · Medieval period mein emerge hua\n TRICK — \"Hina=Akela, Maha=Sabke liye\" trick\n💡\nHinayana = \"Hi khud\" (matlab khud akela) — individual salvation. Mahayana = \"Maha=Bada/Sabke liye\" —\nsalvation for all. Naam ka size hi unki reach batata hai (Hina=chota/khud, Maha=bada/sab).\nVajrayana = \"Vajra\" (thunderbolt/tantra ka symbol) — seedha Tantric practice se connect ho jaata hai.\n8. Tripitaka & Other Texts\n●Sutta Pitaka (largest, teachings) · Vinaya Pitaka (monk rules) · Abhidhamma Pitaka (philosophy, 3rd council)\n●Milinda Panha: Menander(Indo-Greek) + Nagasena dialogue, Pali\n●Buddhacharita: Ashvaghosha (Kanishka's poet), Sanskrit\n●Jataka Tales: Buddha ke poorv janm\n●First written down: 1st century BCE, Sri Lanka, King Vattagamani\n TRICK — \"SVA\" Pitaka order + text hooks\n💡\nPitaka compile order match councils se: Sutta+Vinaya(1st council) → Abhidhamma(3rd council) — \"S-V-A\", 2nd\ncouncil mein koi naya text nahi bana (sirf split hua).\nMilinda Panha = \"Panha\" khud \"prashna/question\" jaisa lagta hai → Questions of Milinda, seedha naam se meaning."," Buddhacharita = \"charita\" matlab \"life-story/charitra\" — ye Buddha ki biography hai (Sanskrit mein, Ashvaghosha ne\nlikhi).\n9. Stupas — 3 \"Sabse\" Yaad Karo\n●Sabse Bada Stupa: Kesariya (Bihar)\n●Sabse Bada Buddhist Temple: Borobudur (Indonesia, Shailendra Dynasty)\n●Sabse Purana Stupa: Piprahwa (UP, Kapilavastu relics)\n●Dhamek(Sarnath,First Sermon) · Sanchi(MP,Ashoka) · Ramabhar(Kushinagar,cremation) ·\nDharmarajika(Taxila,Ashoka)\n TRICK — \"K-B-P\" superlative trick\n💡\nKesariya=biggest stupa(India), Borobudur=biggest temple(Indonesia), Piprahwa=purana(oldest). Bolo: \"Kitna Bada,\nPurana kitna\" — K-B-P three superlatives, teen alag countries/scale.\nPiprahwa naam mein hi \"pehla/purana\" jaisa \"P\" sound hai — Oldest se connect.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSabse bada stupa=Kesariya(Bihar, India). Sabse bada Buddhist TEMPLE (stupa nahi)=Borobudur(Indonesia). Sabse\npurana stupa=Piprahwa(UP). Teeno alag superlatives hain.\n10. Buddhist Universities — Gupta vs Pala Trap\n●Nalanda → Kumaragupta I (Gupta dynasty), Bihar\n●Vikramashila → Dharmapala (Pala dynasty), Bihar\n●Odantapuri → Gopala (Pala dynasty), Bihar\n TRICK — \"Akela Gupta, Baaki Pala\" trick\n💡\n3 mein se sirf Nalanda GUPTA ne banaya — baaki do (Vikramashila, Odantapuri) PALA ne banaye. Yaad rakho:\n\"Nalanda = odd one out (Gupta), baaki sab Pala\".\nNalanda naam N se, Gupta bhi ek chota naam — dono \"chote/pehle\" feel dete hain (Nalanda sabse pehla/famous bhi\nhai). Baaki Pala University naam bade/complex hain (Vikramashila, Odantapuri) jaise Pala empire khud bada tha.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNalanda = Gupta dynasty (Kumaragupta I). Vikramashila aur Odantapuri = Pala dynasty. Ye common trap hai —\nNalanda ko Pala mat samajh lena.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Family: Shuddhodana-MayaDevi-Prajapati(1st Bhikkhuni) → 4 Sights(Old-Sick-Dead-Ascetic)→29saal ghar\nchhoda(Kanthaka+Channa) → Gurus: Alara-Udraka → 35saal Enlightenment(BodhGaya) → Sermon: Sarnath(first)-\nShravasti(most) → 4Truths: Dukkha-Samudaya-Nirodha-Path → Councils: Ra-Va-Pa-Ku/Aj-Ka-A-K(split@2nd,4th) →\nSects: Hinayana(Pali,solo)-Mahayana(Sanskrit,all)-Vajrayana(Tantric) → Tripitaka: S-V-A → Stupas: Kesariya-\nBorobudur-Piprahwa → Nalanda=Gupta, Vikramashila/Odantapuri=Pala\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Council splits: 2nd=first split (Sthaviravadin/Mahasanghika), 4th=final split (Hinayana/Mahayana).\n2) Sermon: Sarnath=first, Shravasti=most sermons."," 3) Nalanda=Gupta dynasty; Vikramashila & Odantapuri=Pala dynasty.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Buddhism"," MAHAJANAPADAS & MAGADHA EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 7 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 16 Mahajanapadas — Source Confusion\n●Anguttara Nikaya (Buddhist) → 16\n●Bhagavati Sutra (Jain) → 16\n●Digha Nikaya (Buddhist) → 12\n●Ashtadhyayi (Panini) → 40 Janapadas\n TRICK — \"Angu-16, Digha-12\" trick\n💡\nDono Buddhist text hain par count alag: Anguttara = \"A\" se shuru, aur \"A\" alphabet mein pehle aata hai → bada number\n16. Digha = \"D\" baad mein aata hai → chota number 12. (A before D, 16 before 12 — bade se chote).\nAshtadhyayi = Panini ki grammar book, ismein 40 — sabse zyada, kyunki Panini ek grammarian tha jo detail mein sab\njanapadas list karta hai, dharm-text nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAnguttara Nikaya (Buddhist) = 16. Digha Nikaya (Buddhist, dusra text) = 12. Dono Buddhist hain par number alag —\nconfuse mat karo.\n2. Republic vs Monarchy\n●Republic (Gana-Sangha): Vajji, Malla, Kamboja, Kuru, Panchala — Elected Adhyaksh, Oligarchy\n●Monarchy (4 most powerful): Magadha, Kosala, Vatsa, Avanti — Hereditary King\n TRICK — \"VMKKP\" republic trick\n💡\n5 Republics: Vajji-Malla-Kamboja-Kuru-Panchala = \"VMKKP\" — bolo \"Very Many Kings Kaam Parte\" (bahut saare\nrulers milkar kaam karte the, oligarchy).\n4 Monarchies: Magadha-Kosala-Vatsa-Avanti = \"MKVA\" — ye 4 hi sabse powerful the, aage chalke Magadha inme se\nsabse aage nikla.\n3. Magadha Dynasty Timeline\n●Brihadratha (earliest, legendary) → Haryanka (544-412 BCE, patricidal) → Shishunaga (412-344 BCE) → Nanda\n(344-322 BCE, non-Kshatriya)\n TRICK — \"BHSN\" chain\n💡\nBrihadratha → Haryanka → Shishunaga → Nanda = \"BHSN\" — bolo \"Bhai Hamesha Sabse Naya\" (jitna aage jaao utna\n\"naya/historical\" hota gaya — Brihadratha=myth, Haryanka=first real history).\nDates seedha ghatte jaate hain: 544→412→344→322 — bas number ghatna yaad rakho, koi bada jump nahi hai.\n4. Battle of Hydaspes (326 BCE)\n●Jhelum River = Greek naam Hydaspes · Alexander the Great vs Porus\n●Alexander ne Porus ki bahaduri dekhkar unka rajya wapas de diya\n TRICK — \"Hydaspes = Jhelum\" hook\n💡\nYaad rakho: Chapter 4 (Vedic Age) mein Jhelum ka Vedic naam Vitasta tha — ab Greek naam Hydaspes hai. Ek hi\nnadi ke 3 naam, 3 chapters mein: Vitasta(Vedic)→Jhelum(modern)→Hydaspes(Greek). Teeno yaad rakhne se cross-\nchapter confusion nahi hoga."," 5. 16 Mahajanapadas — Ek-Ek Unique Fact\n●Anga(Champa) → Purab se pehla · Magadha(Rajgir/Pataliputra) → Sabse powerful, Iron-rich\n●Vajji(Vaishali) → 8-clan confederacy · Malla(Kushinara) → Buddha ka Mahaparinirvana\n●Kashi(Varanasi) → Sabse purani zinda city · Kosala(Shravasti) → Raja Prasenjit\n●Vatsa(Kaushambi) → Raja Udayana · Chedi(Sothivati) → Raja Shishupala\n●Kuru(Indraprastha) → Yudhishthira/Mahabharata · Panchala(Ahichhatra) → Draupadi\n●Surasena(Mathura) → Krishna · Matsya(Viratnagar) → Pandavas ka exile\n●Avanti(Ujjain) → Magadha ka rival, Raja Pradyota · Ashmaka(Potali) → SIRF South India wala\n●Gandhara(Taxila) → Education/University · Kamboja(Rajpur) → Excellent Horses\n TRICK — Ek-word hook har Mahajanapada ke liye\n💡\nAshmaka = \"Akela South\" (sirf ek hi south mein) — A-sound se yaad rakho.\nKamboja = \"Kamdhenu jaisa ghoda\" — horses se connect (Kam~ghoda ki tarah lagta sound nahi hai but bas ratt lo:\nKamboja=Kashmir=Horses).\nGandhara = \"Gyandhara\" (gyaan/education dhaarne wala) — Taxila University.\nKashi = \"Kadim (purana)\" — sabse purani zinda city.\nEpic-connections yaad rakhne ka trick: Kuru=Yudhishthira, Panchala=Draupadi, Surasena=Krishna,\nMatsya=Pandava-exile, Chedi=Shishupala — sab Mahabharata ke characters, ek hi kahani ke alag-alag places.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAshmaka = South India ka SIRF ek Mahajanapada (Godavari bank, Maharashtra). Ye direct exam question hai.\n6. Bimbisara — Founder + 3 Shaadiyan\n●Jain naam: Shrenika · Anga conquer kiya · Buddha+Mahavira dono ka patron\n●Marriages: Kosala Devi(Kosala, Prasenjit ki behen) · Chellana(Vaishali, Chetaka ki beti) · Khema(Madra/Punjab)\n TRICK — \"3 shaadi, 3 alliance\" trick\n💡\nKosala Devi-Kosala, Chellana-Chetaka(Vaishali), Khema-Khetra alag (Madra) — bas 3 wife-kingdom pairs ko naam ke\npehle letter se match karo: K-C-K nahi, bolo \"Kosala se Kosala Devi mili, Chetaka se Chellana mili, aur teesri Madra se\nKhema\".\nPolitical logic: Bimbisara ne 3 alag disha (Kosala=east, Vaishali=north, Madra=northwest Punjab) mein shaadi ki —\nteeno taraf se surakshit ho gaya, isliye teeno yaad rakhne ke liye \"3 directions\" socho.\n7. Ajatashatru & Udayin — Patricidal Pattern\n●Ajatashatru: Bimbisara ko maara → gaddi · Kosala war jeeta (Vajira se shaadi) · Vaishali war: Rathmusala +\nMahashilakantaka\n●Buddha ka Mahaparinirvana unke 8th saal mein hua · 1st Buddhist Council ke patron (Rajgir)\n●Udayin: Ajatashatru ko maara → gaddi · Pataliputra ka kila banwaya (Ganga-Son sangam)\n TRICK — \"2 Naye Hathiyar\" + patricide chain\n💡\nRath-musala = Rath(chariot) + Musala(gada/mace) — naam mein hi hathiyar bata diya. Maha-shila-kantaka =\nMaha(bada)+Shila(patthar)+Kantaka(kaante/spikes) — \"bada patthar phenkne wala\" — naam se hi kaam samajh aata\nhai.\nPatricide chain: \"Ajatashatru ne Bimbisara ko maara, Udayin ne Ajatashatru ko maara\" — do peedhi tak chala, isliye\n\"Patricidal Dynasty\" naam pada. Nanda dynasty patricidal NAHI thi (wo sirf non-Kshatriya thi) — alag category,\nconfuse mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPataliputra ka kila Udayin ne banwaya (Ganga-Son sangam par) — Kalashoka ne sirf capital WAPAS Pataliputra shift\nki thi, kila unhone nahi banaya."," 8. Shishunaga Dynasty\n●Shishunaga (founder) → Avanti ko destroy kiya · Capital Vaishali shift ki\n●Kalashoka (Kakavarna) → Capital WAPAS Pataliputra shift ki · 2nd Buddhist Council patron (Vaishali)\n TRICK — \"Vaishali jaake wapas aana\" trick\n💡\nShishunaga = \"Shishu (bachcha) ghar se bahar gaya\" (Vaishali gaya) → Kalashoka = \"Kal aake wapas ghar aaya\"\n(Pataliputra wapas laaya). Ek gaya, doosra wapas laaya — order yaad rakhne ka trick.\n9. Nanda Dynasty — Pehli Non-Kshatriya\n●Mahapadma Nanda (founder) → Titles: Ekarat, Sarvakshatrantaka · Kalinga ko PEHLE conquer kiya\n(Hathigumpha inscription)\n●Dhana Nanda (last) → Greek naam Agrammes/Xandrames · Huge army (2 lakh infantry, 3000+ hathi) · Alexander ka\ncontemporary\n TRICK — \"Mahapadma = Kalinga First\" trap-buster\n💡\nCommon galti: log sochte hain Ashoka ne Kalinga sabse pehle jeeta — NAHI. Mahapadma Nanda ne pehle conquer\nkiya, Ashoka ne sirf RE-conquer kiya (261 BCE War). Yaad rakho: \"Nanda ne pehli baar liya, Ashoka ne dobara\nliya\".\nDhana Nanda ki army itni badi thi ki Alexander khud dar gaya — \"Dhan (wealth/army) itna zyada tha ki Alexander\nbhi Dhan-Nanda se dar gaya\" — naam mein hi \"Dhan\" (paisa/power) hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKalinga ko sabse PEHLE conquer karne wale Mahapadma Nanda the, na ki Ashoka (jo sirf 261 BCE mein reconquer\nkiya).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Sources: Anguttara-16, Digha-12, Ashtadhyayi-40 → Republic:VMKKP vs Monarchy:MKVA → Dynasty chain:\nBHSN(Brihadratha-Haryanka-Shishunaga-Nanda) → Hydaspes(Jhelum)=Alexander vs Porus(326BCE) → 16\nMahajanapadas ek-word hooks (Ashmaka=South,Kamboja=Horses,Gandhara=Education) → Bimbisara: 3\nshaadi(KosalaDevi-Chellana-Khema) → Ajatashatru(patricide,Rathmusala+Mahashilakantaka,1st council) →\nUdayin(patricide,Pataliputra fort) → Shishunaga(Vaishali)→Kalashoka(wapas Pataliputra,2nd council) → Mahapadma\nNanda(Kalinga first, Ekarat) → Dhana Nanda(Agrammes,huge army)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Anguttara Nikaya=16 vs Digha Nikaya=12 (dono Buddhist, alag count).\n2) Kalinga sabse pehle Mahapadma Nanda ne jeeta, Ashoka ne sirf reconquer kiya (261 BCE).\n3) Pataliputra ka kila Udayin ne banwaya; Kalashoka ne sirf capital wapas shift ki (nahi banaya).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Mahajanapadas & Magadha Empire"," MAURYAN EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 8 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Peedhi, 3 Dharma — Sabse Bada Trap\n●Chandragupta → Jain (Bhadrabahu, Sallekhana)\n●Bindusara → Ajivika (Greek naam: Amitrochates/Amitraghata)\n●Ashoka → Buddhist (Kalinga War ke baad)\n TRICK — \"J-A-B\" generational trick\n💡\nEk hi family, teen alag dharm: Jain(dada) → Ajivika(beta) → Buddhist(pota) = \"J-A-B\". Bolo: \"Jab teen peedhiyon ne\nteen alag raaste chune\" — JAB khud hi mnemonic ban jaata hai (Jain-Ajivika-Buddhist).\nYe 3 dharm bilkul teen alag chapters (5,6, aur ye khud) mein bhi padhe hain — cross-check karo agar bhoolo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChandragupta=Jain, Bindusara=Ajivika, Ashoka=Buddhist. Teen peedhiyan, teen alag dharm — kabhi swap mat karna.\n2. Chandragupta — Sandrokottos & Seleucus Treaty\n●Greek naam: Sandrokottos (William Jones ne identify kiya) · Army: 6 lakh (Justin ke hisaab se)\n●Seleucus Treaty: Territory (E.Afghanistan, Baluchistan, W.Sindh) mili · Beti Helena se shaadi · 500 hathi gift diye ·\nAmbassador Megasthenes mila\n●Later life: Bhadrabahu ke saath Jain bane, Shravanabelagola mein Sallekhana\n TRICK — \"Territory-Marriage-Elephants-Ambassador\" trick\n💡\nTreaty ka give-and-take yaad rakho ek trade jaisa: Chandragupta ko mila (Territory + Helena) ↔ Seleucus ko mila\n(500 Hathi). Aur beech mein Megasthenes aaya diplomatic link banane — \"do cheez le li, do cheez de di, beech mein\ndoot(ambassador) aaya\".\nSandrokottos naam khud \"Chandragupta\" ka hi Greek pronunciation-twist hai — bas dhyan se bolo, similar sound hai.\n3. Bindusara — Ambassadors & Takshashila Revolts\n●Greek naam: Amitrochates/Amitraghata (Slayer of enemies) · Ajivika patron · 500 ministers, Chief Minister\nKhalatanka\n●Ambassadors: Daimachus(Syria, Antiochus I) · Dionysius(Egypt, Ptolemy Philadelphus)\n●Takshashila 1st revolt → Ashoka bheja gaya · 2nd revolt → Sushima bheja gaya\n TRICK — \"D-D\" ambassador + revolt-order trick\n💡\nDaimachus-Syria, Dionysius-Egypt — dono \"D\" se shuru → yaad rakhne ke liye \"Dono ambassador Doosre desh se\naaye\" bas alphabetically match kar lo (Daimachus pehle bola jaata hai, Syria pehle likha jaata hai — dono \"D\" wale\ngroups).\n1st revolt mein Ashoka gaya (kyunki wo hi baad mein raja bane, so \"pehla/important\" beta pehli baar bheja gaya), 2nd\nrevolt mein Sushima gaya (dusra beta, dusri baar).\n4. Ashoka — Accession, Coronation, Kalinga\n●Accession: 273 BCE (de facto/practically raja) · Coronation: 269 BCE (official, 4-saal gap — bhai-conflict)\n●Kalinga War: 261 BCE (coronation ke 8 saal baad) · 1 lakh maare, 1.5 lakh qaidi\n●Inscriptions: James Prinsep ne pehle padha (deciphered) · Alexander Cunningham ne 1877 mein publish kiya\n TRICK — \"273-269-261\" timeline + Prinsep vs Cunningham\n💡"," Timeline ghatta hua yaad rakho: 273(accession) → 269(coronation, 4 saal baad) → 261(Kalinga, coronation ke 8 saal\nbaad) — bas \"4 saal gap, phir 8 saal gap\" ratt lo, dono gap khud number bhi hint dete hain (4 aur 8, double hai).\nPrinsep = Padhne wala (P for Prinsep, P for Padhna/decipher — pehla). Cunningham = Compile karne wala (baad\nmein, 1877 mein publish). \"Pehle padha (Prinsep), baad mein poora compile hua (Cunningham)\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAccession(273 BCE, de facto) vs Coronation(269 BCE, official) — 4 saal ka gap. James Prinsep=decipher kiya,\nCunningham=1877 mein publish kiya — dono alag kaam.\n5. Edicts — Counts & Key Messages\n●Major Rock: 14 · Minor Rock: 18 · Major Pillar: 7 · Minor Pillar: 7\n●Edict V = Dhamma Mahamatras ki appointment\n●Edict XII = Sarva Dharma Samabhava (religious harmony)\n●Edict XIII = SABSE DETAILED — Kalinga War + neighbouring states + Dhamma diplomacy\n●Ashoka ka naam mila: Maski (Ashoka+Buddha Shakya), Bhabru/Bairat(Piyadasi), Nettur/Gujjara\n TRICK — \"5-12-13\" trick\n💡\n5 = Dhamma Mahamatras (5 ungliyon se \"appoint\" karne ka ishara socho). 12 = Sarva Dharma Samabhava (12=1+2=3,\n\"sam\" jaisa symmetrical number bhi hai, harmony ka symbol). 13 = sabse detailed/bada — unlucky number 13 ko\n\"bahut bada drama\" (Kalinga War) se jodo.\nMaski = pehli jagah jahan \"Ashoka\" naam khud mila — \"Maski mein naam khula (mask utar gaya)\" — Mask-i socho\n\"mask hata di, naam dikha diya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nEdict V=Dhamma Mahamatras appointment. Edict XII=Sarva Dharma Samabhava. Edict XIII=sabse detailed (Kalinga\nWar). Teeno alag numbers, mix mat karo.\n6. Saptanga Theory — 7 Elements of State\n●Swami(King) → Amatya(Minister) → Janapada(Territory) → Durga(Fort) → Kosha(Treasury) → Danda(Army) →\nMitra(Ally)\n TRICK — \"SAJDKDM\" priority-order trick\n💡\nOrder importance ke hisaab se hai: pehle Swami(raja khud) chahiye, phir Amatya(usko advise karne wale), phir\nJanapada(raaj karne ke liye zameen), phir Durga(suraksha), Kosha(paisa), Danda(force), aur last mein Mitra(bahar ka\nsupport) — ek building banane jaisa: pehle n\n\nींव(Swami), phir upar structure.\nLast element Mitra hamesha exam mein poocha jaata hai kyunki log 7th tak yaad nahi rakhte — bas yaad rakho \"list ka\nlast word Mitra/Friend hai\".\n7. Key Administrative Posts — Naam Confuse Na Ho\n●Sannidhata = Chief Treasurer · Samaharta = Chief Tax Collector\n●Nagarika = City/Shehar ka Head · Rajuka = District Officer (ALAG post)\n●Judicial: Criminal Court=Kantaka Shodhana(officer Pradeshta) · Civil Court=Dharmasthiya(officer Vyavaharika)\n TRICK — \"San-Treasure, Sama-Tax\" trick\n💡\nSannidhata = \"Sandook\" (sandook/box jahan khazana rakha jaata hai) → Treasurer. Samaharta = \"Sameta karna\"\n(ikattha karna/collect karna) → Tax Collector — dono naam mein hi kaam chhupa hai.\nNagarika = \"Nagar\" (city) → City head. Rajuka = District officer — Nagarika-Rajuka alag hain, size se yaad rakho:\nNagar(bada, city) vs Rajuka(chota unit, district).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNagarika = City head. Rajuka = District Officer — ye do ALAG posts hain, khaas taur pe city-administration wale"," questions mein confuse hote hain.\n8. 5 Provinces & Capitals\n●Uttarapatha→Taxila · Dakshinapatha→Suvarnagiri · Avanti→Ujjain · Prachi→Pataliputra · Kalinga→Tosali\n TRICK — Direction-se-capital match\n💡\nNaam mein hi disha chhupi hai: Uttarapatha(North)→Taxila(North-West),\nDakshinapatha(South)→Suvarnagiri(Deccan), Prachi(East, \"prachya\"=east)→Pataliputra(East hi hai capital khud),\nAvanti(Central)→Ujjain, Kalinga(alag se, East-coast)→Tosali.\n9. City Admin, Army Strength & Coins\n●Pataliputra city admin: 30 members → 6 Committees → 5 each\n●Army (Pliny): 6 Lakh foot, 30,000 cavalry, 9,000 elephants, 8,000 chariots\n●Coins: Silver=Karshapana, Dharana · Copper=Kakani, Ardhakakani · Royal=Pana\n TRICK — \"30-6-5\" and coin-metal trick\n💡\n30÷6=5 — city admin structure khud hi ek maths fact hai, isse hi ratt lo: 30 members, 6 committees, har committee mein\n5.\nArmy numbers ghatte jaate hain: 6,00,000(foot) → 30,000(cavalry) → 9,000(elephants) → 8,000(chariots) — bas scale\nse yaad rakho, foot-soldiers hamesha sabse zyada hote hain kisi bhi army mein.\nCoins: Silver = bada naam (Karshapana, Dharana — dono lambe naam), Copper = chota naam (Kakani, Ardhakakani\n— \"Kakani\" khud chota lagta hai) — metal ki value se naam ki length match karo (bada metal=bada naam nahi, ulta bhi\nho sakta hai but bas ratt lo).\n10. Megasthenes Ka Contradiction — Slavery\n●Megasthenes+Strabo → \"No Slavery in India\"\n●Kautilya's Arthashastra → Varnashankara/Dasa (slavery) ka mention hai (Ambashtha, Nishada etc.)\n TRICK — \"Megasthenes ke anusaar = No\" trick\n💡\nDo sources, do opposite answers — sawaal ka wording dhyan se padho: \"Megasthenes ke anusaar\" → No slavery.\n\"Arthashastra ke anusaar\" → slavery exist karti thi. Jo bhi naam sawaal mein ho, wahi answer decide karega —\nsource-specific yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Megasthenes ke anusaar India mein slavery thi ya nahi?\" → NAHI thi (Megasthenes/Strabo dono kehte hain). Par\nArthashastra khud slavery ke forms mention karta hai — source specify karke hi answer do.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 dharm: J-A-B(Chandragupta-Bindusara-Ashoka) → Chandragupta: Sandrokottos+Seleucus\ntreaty(Helena,500hathi,Megasthenes) → Bindusara: Amitrochates+Daimachus/Dionysius+Ashoka/Sushima revolts →\nAshoka: 273(accession)-269(coronation)-261(Kalinga) → Prinsep(decipher)-Cunningham(1877 publish) → Edicts: 14-\n18-7-7, Edict5=Mahamatras,12=SarvaDharma,13=detailed → Saptanga: Swami-Amatya-Janapada-Durga-Kosha-\nDanda-Mitra → Sannidhata(treasury) vs Samaharta(tax) → Nagarika(city) vs Rajuka(district) → 5 provinces → City\nadmin 30-6-5 → Coins: Karshapana/Dharana(silver)-Kakani(copper) → Megasthenes=No slavery\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo."," Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) 3 peedhi, 3 dharm: Chandragupta=Jain, Bindusara=Ajivika, Ashoka=Buddhist.\n2) Accession(273)≠Coronation(269) — 4 saal gap. Prinsep=decipher, Cunningham=1877 publish.\n3) Edict V=Mahamatras appointment, Edict XII=Sarva Dharma Samabhava, Edict XIII=sabse detailed.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Mauryan Empire"," POST-MAURYAN EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 9 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Local vs Foreign — 7 Dynasties Ka Overlap\n●Local: Shunga(185-73BCE) → Kanva(73-28BCE) → Satavahana(30BCE-250CE)\n●Foreign: Indo-Greek(~200-100BCE) → Shaka(~100BCE-400CE) → Parthian(~19-45CE) → Kushan(~78-250CE)\n TRICK — \"SKS vs IShPK\" trick\n💡\nLocal 3: Shunga → Kanva → Satavahana = \"SKS\" (ek doosre ko maarke banti hain — Shunga ka minister Kanva bana,\nKanva ko Satavahana ne khatam kiya).\nForeign 4 North-West se order mein aaye: Indo-Greek → Shaka → Parthian → Kushan = \"I-Sh-P-K\" — ye India ke\nandar wali dynasties (SKS) se overlap karti hain, same timeline ka alag hissa nahi samjho.\n2. Shunga Dynasty — Pushyamitra Se Devabhuti Tak\n●Pushyamitra (founder) → Brihadratha (aakhri Maurya) ko maara · 2 Ashwamedha Yagya · Priest Patanjali\n●Agnimitra (bete) → Malavikagnimitram ka hero\n●Bhagabhadra → Darbar mein Heliodorus (Greek ambassador) → Garuda Pillar (Besnagar, Vasudeva ke liye)\n●Devabhuti (aakhri) → Minister Vasudeva ne maara → Kanva shuru\n TRICK — \"Maara-Maara\" chain trick\n💡\nPattern: Pushyamitra ne apne raja ko maara (Brihadratha) → dynasty shuru → Devabhuti khud apne minister se\nmaara gaya (Vasudeva) → dynasty khatam. Shuruaat aur ant, dono \"maarne\" se hi hue — circular story.\nHeliodorus ek Greek tha jo Hindu dharm apnaya — \"Videshi bhi apna gaya\" — is unique fact ko alag se yaad rakho,\nye baar-baar poocha jaata hai.\n3. Kanva Dynasty — Chota Par Important\n●Vasudeva (founder, ex-Shunga minister) · Capital Pataliputra · 4 rulers: Vasudeva-Bhumimitra-Narayana-Susharman\n●Susharman (aakhri) → Simuka (Satavahana) ne maara\n TRICK — \"Minister bana raja, phir South ne khatam kiya\" trick\n💡\nKanva khud ek \"minister se bana dynasty\" tha (Vasudeva). Aur ant hua ek South Indian power (Satavahana) se —\nNorth se South ka connect yaad rakho: \"North ka minister North mein hi khatam hua, lekin South ke haathon\".\n4. Satavahana — 5 Key Rulers\n●Simuka(1st) → Kanva khatam kiya\n●Krishna(bhai) → Nasik tak empire\n●Satakarni I(bhatija) → \"Satakarni\" title pehli baar · Patni Naganika · Naneghat inscription\n●Hala → Poet-king → Gatha Sattasai (700 Prakrit shlokas)\n●Gautamiputra Satakarni(greatest,106-130CE) → Nahapana ko haraya · Capital Paithan · Rudradaman ne 2 baar\nharaya\n TRICK — \"SKS-H-G\" ruler chain + naming trick\n💡\nOrder: Simuka → Krishna(bhai) → Satakarni I(bhatija) → Hala(poet) → Gautamiputra(greatest) = \"SKS-HG\".\nSatavahana naam khud matrilineal the — \"Gautamiputra\" matlab \"Gautami ki santaan\" (maa ka naam beta ke naam\nmein) — property pita se milti thi par NAAM maa se — ye unique social fact hai, isko \"naam-Maa, property-Pita\" bolke\nyaad rakho.\nGautamiputra vs Rudradaman: Gautamiputra ne Nahapana ko haraya (jeeta), lekin khud Rudradaman se 2 baar"," haara — \"jeeta bhi, haara bhi\" dono fact alag context mein sach hain, confuse mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGautamiputra Satakarni ne Nahapana ko haraya, LEKIN khud Rudradaman (Shaka) se 2 baar haare. Dono facts sahi\nhain, alag opponents ke against.\n5. Indo-Greek — Pehli Baar Kaafi Kuch\n●Pehle Gold Coins in India · Pehla Portrait on coins · Hellenistic art → Gandhara Art\n●Menander (165-145BCE) = Milinda → Nagasena ne Buddhist banaya → Milindapanho → Capital Shakal (Sialkot)\n TRICK — \"Pehli baar sab kuch Indo-Greek\" trick\n💡\nIndo-Greeks = \"Pehla-Pehla\" club — gold coins pehli baar, portrait pehli baar. Yaad rakho: sabse pehla foreign\ndynasty aaya, isliye sabse zyada \"firsts\" bhi unhi ke naam hain.\nMenander=Milinda — dono naam yaad rakhne ke liye: \"Milinda Milta-julta lagta hai Menander se\" — dono \"M\" se\nshuru.\n6. Shaka — 5 Branches + Rudradaman\n●5 Branches: Afghanistan, Taxila, Mathura, Nasik, Ujjain (Rudradaman)\n●Rudradaman(130-150CE) → Junagadh Inscription(150CE,Girnar,Sanskrit,oldest poetic) → Sudarshan Lake restore\n→ Gautamiputra ko 2 baar haraya\n●Aakhri Shaka: Rudrasimha III → Chandragupta Vikramaditya ne maara\n TRICK — \"Junagadh Package\" trick\n💡\nEk hi package mein sab yaad rakho: Rudradaman = Junagadh Inscription = Sudarshan Lake restore = Sanskrit ka\npehla poetic likhawat. Sab ek hi raja ke saath jude hain, alag mat karo.\nYaad rakho: Sudarshan Lake originally Pushyagupta (Chandragupta Maurya ke time) ne banaya tha —\nRudradaman ne sirf restore kiya, banaya nahi — Mauryan chapter se cross-link.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJunagadh Inscription = sabse purani Sanskrit POETIC inscription (Girnar, Gujarat, 150 CE) — Rudradaman ne\nlikhwayi, aur usi mein Sudarshan Lake ke restoration ka mention hai.\n7. Indo-Parthians — Chota Par Famous\n●Pehla raja: Maus · Asli founder: Mithridates-I\n●Gondophernes(19-45CE) → Takht-i-Bahi inscription (Kharoshthi) · St. Thomas India aaye unke raaj mein\n TRICK — \"Gondophernes = Christianity Gate\" trick\n💡\nGondophernes = \"Gondh\" bhoolo, bas yaad rakho \"Gondophernes ne Gate khola Christianity ke liye\" (St. Thomas unke\ntime India aaye) — dono \"G\" se easy link.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSt. Thomas India Gondophernes (Indo-Parthian) ke time aaye — Kushan ya Shaka NAHI. Ye ek common galti hai.\n8. Kushan — Yuezhi Se Kanishka Tak\n●Kujula Kadphises(1st) → Sirf copper coins, Buddhist symbols\n●Vima Kadphises → India mein Kushan ke asli founder · Regular gold coins pehli baar · Shaivism(Maheshwara)\n●Kanishka(78-105CE, greatest) → Capital Purushpur/Peshawar · Saka Era(78CE) · 4th Buddhist Council · Court:\nAshwaghosha, Nagarjuna, Charaka(physician)\n●Vasudeva I → aakhri great Kushan"," TRICK — \"KVKV\" ruler chain\n💡\nKujula(copper only) → Vima(gold-first-regular) → Kanishka(greatest,Saka Era) → Vasudeva(last) = \"K-V-K-V\" —\npattern khud ek chain jaisa hai, alternating letters yaad rakhna easy hai.\nVima Kadphises = REGULAR gold (pehli baar systematically), lekin Indo-Greeks = SABSE PEHLA EVER gold\ncoin — inn dono \"pehla\" claims ko alag rakho: Indo-Greek=absolute first, Vima=first REGULAR/systematic.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGold coins: Indo-Greek=sabse pehla EVER. Vima Kadphises=pehla REGULAR/systematic. Kushan=sabse PURE.\nGupta=sabse ZYADA (quantity). Char alag \"firsts\", mix mat karo.\n9. 4th Buddhist Council & Gandhara vs Mathura\n●4th Council: Kashmir (Kundalavana) · President Vasumitra, VP Ashwaghosha · Result: Mahayana finalize\n●Gandhara: Patron Shakas · Realistic · Grey schist · Curly hair (Greco-Roman)\n●Mathura: Patron Kushans · Idealistic · Red sandstone · Kanishka's headless statue\n TRICK — \"4th=Kashmir not Pataliputra\" + Art trick\n💡\n3rd Council = Pataliputra (Ashoka). 4th Council = Kashmir (Kanishka) — bilkul alag jagah, exam ka classic swap-trap.\nGandhara = \"Greek\" (Realistic, Greek-influenced, Shakas ne patronize ki — jo khud ek foreign group thi, isliye Greek-\nstyle art unke saath match). Mathura = \"Madhyam/pure Indian\" (Idealistic, Kushans, red sandstone) — dono naam ki\nstarting sound se style yaad karo (Gan-Greek, Math-Madhyam/pure).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n4th Buddhist Council = Kashmir (Kundalavana), NOT Pataliputra (jo 3rd council ki jagah thi, Ashoka ke time).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Local: SKS(Shunga-Kanva-Satavahana) → Foreign: I-Sh-P-K(IndoGreek-Shaka-Parthian-Kushan) → Shunga:\nPushyamitra(kill Brihadratha)-Agnimitra-Heliodorus-Devabhuti(killed) → Kanva: Vasudeva-Susharman(killed by\nSimuka) → Satavahana: Simuka-Krishna-SatakarniI(Naganika)-Hala(GathaSattasai)-Gautamiputra(beat Nahapana,lost\nto Rudradaman 2x) → IndoGreek: Menander/Milinda,first gold+portrait → Shaka:\nRudradaman(Junagadh,SudarshanLake) → Parthian: Gondophernes(St.Thomas) → Kushan: KujulaKadphises-\nVimaKadphises(regular gold)-Kanishka(SakaEra,4thCouncil@Kashmir)-VasudevaI → Art: Gandhara(Shaka,realistic)\nvs Mathura(Kushan,idealistic)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Gold coins: Indo-Greek=first ever, Vima Kadphises=first regular, Kushan=purest, Gupta=most quantity.\n2) 4th Buddhist Council = Kashmir (Kundalavana), NOT Pataliputra (that was 3rd Council).\n3) St. Thomas aaye Gondophernes (Indo-Parthian) ke time — Kushan ya Shaka nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Post-Mauryan Empire"," GUPTA EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 10 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Founder vs Real Founder + Ruler Order\n●Shri Gupta(275CE) = Founder · Chandragupta I(319CE) = REAL/Actual Founder\n●Order+Titles: Shri Gupta(Adiraj) → Ghatotkacha(Maharaja) → Chandragupta I(Maharajadhiraj) →\nSamudragupta(Parakramanka,Kaviraja) → Chandragupta II(Vikramaditya) → Kumaragupta I(Mahendraditya) →\nSkandagupta(Shakraditya)\n TRICK — \"Shri vs Chandra\" + title-growth trick\n💡\nShri Gupta = naam se hi \"shuru\" wala (Shri=starting honorific) — bas dynasty ka naam shuru kiya. Chandragupta I\n= REAL power leke aaya — jaise chand (Chandra) andhere ko roshan karta hai, waise usne dynasty ko \"roshan/real\"\nbanaya.\nTitles ka pattern dekho — jitna aage utna bada title: Adiraj/Maharaja(chota) → Maharajadhiraj(bada) →\nVikramaditya/Mahendraditya/Shakraditya(\"-aditya\" ending, sabse grand, matlab \"Sun-like\") — later rulers \"aditya\"\n(sun) suffix use karte hain, ye khud yaad rakhne layak pattern hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nShri Gupta = Founder (275 CE). Chandragupta I = Real/Actual Founder (319 CE, Maharajadhiraj title lene wala pehla).\nDono alag jawab hain apne-apne sawaal ke liye.\n2. Samudragupta — India Ka Napoleon\n●V.A. Smith ne \"India's Napoleon\" kaha — kabhi hare nahi · Coins par Veena bajate hue · Nickname Licchhavi\nDauhitra\n●Prayag Prashasti (Allahabad Pillar) — court poet Harishena ne likhi\n●5 Conquest Groups: 1-Doab · 2-Nepal/Assam/Bengal · 3-Atavika/Vindhya · 4-South(12 rajaon ko haraakar CHHOD\ndiya) · 5-Shaka/Kushana\n TRICK — \"5 Groups, Grace to South\" trick\n💡\nGroup 4 (South) mein Samudragupta ne \"jeetke bhi chhod diya\" — Ashoka ki Dhamma-policy jaisi \"grace\" — is\nunique twist ko yaad rakho: baaki groups mein territory li, par South mein sirf loyalty li, rajya wapas de diya.\nHarishena ≠ Kalidasa — Prayag Prashasti Harishena ki hai, Kalidasa to Chandragupta II ke darbar mein tha, alag raja\nalag kavi.\n3. Chandragupta II — Vikramaditya\n●PEHLE Silver Coins introduce kiye (\"Devashri\" likha) · 409CE mein Rudrasimha III(Shaka) ko haraya\n●Shaadi: Ramagupta ki patni Dhruvadevi se · Beti Prabhavati ki shaadi Vakataka raja Rudrasena II se\n●Faxian(399-414CE) aaye · Second capital Ujjain · Mehrauli Iron Pillar mein \"Chandra\" = ye hi\n●Navaratnas (9): Kalidasa, Amarasimha, Shanku, Dhanvantari, Kshapanaka, Vetalabhatta, Vararuchi, Ghatakarpara,\nVarahamihira\n TRICK — \"Vikramaditya = Silver+Navratna\" trick\n💡\nSilver Coins = Chandragupta II (\"first\") — samjho \"Chandra(moon) safed/silver jaisa hi hai\" — naam aur metal ka\ncolor match ho jaata hai (Chandra=chandni=safed=silver).\nNavaratnas mein top-3 pehle pakka karo: Kalidasa(poet), Dhanvantari(Ayurveda), Varahamihira(astronomer) —\nbaaki 6 baad mein.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSilver coins sabse pehle Chandragupta II ne issue kiye — Samudragupta ya Chandragupta I ne NAHI."," 4. Kumaragupta I — 3 \"Sabse\" Facts\n●Nalanda University ki foundation ki — \"Oxford of Mahayana Buddhism\"\n●Sabse zyada inscriptions (18 total) · Bayana Coin Hoard = sabse bada gold hoard (623 coins, Rajasthan)\n●Pushyamitra invasion ko defeat kiya (Bhitari Pillar mein mention) · Coins: Lakshmi+Ganga depictions\n TRICK — \"Kumar = Sabse Zyada\" trick\n💡\nKumaragupta ke naam mein hi \"Kum\" — bolo \"Kumar ne kumti nahi ki, sabse zyada (18 inscriptions, 623 coins)\ncollect kiya\" — thoda ulta wordplay hai par yaad rakhne layak: 'Kumar' = sabse zyada.\nNalanda = Kumaragupta (yaad hai Buddhism chapter se bhi) — cross-check karo agar bhoolo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNalanda University = Kumaragupta I (na ki Chandragupta II ya Samudragupta). Sabse zyada inscriptions (18) aur sabse\nbada coin hoard (Bayana, 623) bhi Kumaragupta I ke time ke hain.\n5. Skandagupta — Hun Repeller\n●Title Shakraditya · Huns ka invasion repel kiya (Bhitari Inscription)\n●Sudarshan Lake dam RECONSTRUCT kiya (Chakrapalita dwara) — pehle Pushyagupta(Maurya) ne banaya,\nRudradaman(Shaka) ne restore kiya, ab Skandagupta ne phir se banwaya\n●Successor Bhanugupta ne Eastern Malwa mein Huna raaj khatam kiya\n●Eran Inscription = Sati ka PEHLA epigraphic evidence (Skandagupta era)\n TRICK — \"3 log, ek jheel\" + Eran vs Bhitari trick\n💡\nSudarshan Lake ka 3-generation story: Pushyagupta(banaya, Maurya) → Rudradaman(restore, Shaka) →\nSkandagupta(phir reconstruct, Gupta) — teen alag empires isi jheel se juda hai, cross-chapter fact.\nEran = Sati ka pehla evidence, Bhitari = Huns invasion ka mention — dono Skandagupta se related inscriptions hain\npar ALAG facts batate hain, mix mat karo (dono \"pehla\" wale facts hain par alag topics ke liye).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSati ka pehla epigraphic evidence = Eran Inscription, NOT Bhitari (jo Huns invasion aur Pushyamitra tribe ke liye\nfamous hai).\n6. Gupta Officers — Naam Se Kaam Pehchano\n●Mahadandanayaka = Chief Judge · Mahasenapati = Army supreme · Mahabaladhikrita = Army Supreme Commander\n●Mahabhandagaradhikrita = Treasury chief · Dhruvadhikarana = Land revenue chief · Dandapashika = Police chief\n●Tax: Bhaga(1/6-1/4 produce) · Uparikara(extra tax) · Visti(forced labor) · Bhoga(fruit-flower supply) ·\nSenabhakti(army ko khana)\n TRICK — \"Danda = Punishment\" hook\n💡\nDanda shabd \"punishment/authority\" ka symbol hai — isliye Mahadanda-nayaka = Chief JUDGE (jo punishment\ndeta hai) aur Danda-pashika = Police chief (jo control rakhta hai) — dono \"Danda\" wale naam justice/control se juda\nhai.\nTax names ka matlab seedha naam mein hai: Bhoga=bhog/offering(phal-phool), Senabhakti=Sena+bhakti(army ki seva\nmein khana), Visti=vishesh seva(forced labor) — sab naam apna kaam khud bata dete hain.\n7. Literary Works — Author Matching\n●Kalidasa (7 works): Abhijnanashakuntalam(pehli Europe-translated), Malavikagnimitram, Raghuwansham,\nRitusanhar, Vikramorvashiyam, Kumarasambhavam, Meghadutam\n●Vishakhadatta (2 works): Mudrarakshasa(Chandragupta Maurya), Devichandraguptam(Chandragupta II)\n●Panchatantra=Vishnu Sharma · Amarakosha=Amarasimha · Aryabhatiyam=Aryabhata ·\nBrihatsamhita=Varahamihira"," TRICK — \"7 Kalidasa, 2 Vishakhadatta\" trick\n💡\nKalidasa = sabse prolific (7 works) — jab bhi koi \"Kalidasa ki kitaab\" poochha jaaye aur naam na yaad ho, safe guess\nKalidasa hi hai (kyunki uski list sabse lambi hai).\nVishakhadatta = sirf 2 par dono \"Chandragupta\" naam wale rulers ke baare mein: Mudrarakshasa(Chandragupta\nMaurya), Devichandraguptam(Chandragupta II) — ek hi author, do alag \"Chandragupta\" pe likha — confuse mat ho\nkonsa kaunsa hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMudrarakshasa = Chandragupta MAURYA ke baare mein. Devichandraguptam = Chandragupta II ke baare mein. Dono\nVishakhadatta ne likhe, par alag-alag \"Chandragupta\" pe.\n8. Science — Aryabhata & Varahamihira\n●Aryabhata(Pataliputra) → Aryabhatiyam: Prithvi gol hai, apni axis pe ghoomti hai, Sun ke around revolve karti hai\n●Varahamihira → Panchasiddhantika(astrology) — Chandragupta II ka Navaratna\n●Dhanvantari → Ayurveda ke founder, Dhanvantari Samhita\n TRICK — \"Copernicus se pehle\" trick\n💡\nAryabhata ne ye baatein Copernicus/Galileo se SADIYON PEHLE bata di — \"Earth round+rotates+revolves\" — is\ntimeline-shock fact se khud hi yaad ho jaata hai ki ye Gupta period ka sabse bada scientific achievement tha.\n9. Temples — MP Sabse Zyada, Deogarh Sabse Famous\n●Madhya Pradesh: 10+ temples (Eran, Bhumara, Sanchi, Tigwa, Nachna Kuthara etc.) — sabse zyada\n●Uttar Pradesh: Dashavatara temple (Deogarh) — SABSE FAMOUS · Krishna temple (Bhitargaon)\n TRICK — \"MP=Quantity, UP=Fame\" trick\n💡\nMP mein sabse zyada temples bane (quantity), par UP ka Deogarh temple sabse famous (quality/fame) — do alag\nsuperlatives, mix mat karo: \"MP jeeta quantity mein, UP jeeta fame mein\".\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Shri Gupta(founder,275)→Chandragupta I(real founder,319) → Samudragupta(Napoleon,Veena,5groups,Harishena) →\nChandragupta II(Vikramaditya,silver coins first,Navaratnas,Faxian) → Kumaragupta I(Nalanda,18 inscriptions,Bayana\n623 coins) → Skandagupta(Huns repel,Sudarshan Lake,Eran=Sati first) → Officers: Mahadandanayaka=Judge →\nLiterature: Kalidasa(7 works)-Vishakhadatta(2 works,dono Chandragupta) → Science: Aryabhata(Earth\nround+rotate+revolve) → Temples: MP(quantity)-UP Deogarh(fame)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Shri Gupta=Founder(275CE) vs Chandragupta I=Real Founder(319CE).\n2) Silver coins first = Chandragupta II. Nalanda founder = Kumaragupta I. Ye do alag rulers hain.\n3) Sati ka pehla evidence = Eran Inscription, NOT Bhitari (jo Huns invasion ke liye famous hai) — dono Skandagupta se\nrelated hain par alag facts.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Gupta Empire"," POST-GUPTA EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 11 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Harshavardhana — Last Hindu Emperor\n●Capital Kannauj · Nickname Shiladitya · 16 saal ki umar mein gaddi (bhai Rajyavardhan ki hatya ke baad)\n●Khud likhi: Nagananda, Ratnavali, Priyadarshika\n●Harshacharita = Banabhatta ne Harsha ke BAARE MEIN likhi (Harsha ne khud NAHI likhi)\n TRICK — \"3 khud, 1 doosre ne\" trick\n💡\nHarsha ne khud 3 kitaabein likhi (Nagananda-Ratnavali-Priyadarshika — teeno naam feminine/soft sound karte hain,\njaise natak/kavya). Par Harshacharita = \"charita\" (biography) — biography khud apne baare mein nahi likhi jaati,\nisliye ye Banabhatta ne likhi, Harsha ne nahi.\nYaad rakho: \"Harsha ne khud teen, Bana ne Harsha ke baare mein ek\" — total 4 books is chapter mein, par author\nalag-alag.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHarsha ne khud Nagananda, Ratnavali, Priyadarshika likhi. Harshacharita Banabhatta ne Harsha ke baare mein likhi —\nHarsha ne khud NAHI likhi.\n2. Southern Campaign — Harsha HAAR Gaye!\n●Pulakeshin II (Chalukya) ne Harsha ko Narmada river ke kinare rok diya, HARAYA (632 CE)\n●Ye Aihole Inscription mein mention hai\n TRICK — \"Powerful bhi haar sakta hai\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log sochte hain Harsha itna powerful tha ki jeet gaya hoga — NAHI, HAAR gaye. Yaad rakho: \"Harsha\nkhud hi Har gaya\" — naam mein hi \"Har\" (haar) chhupa hai, wordplay se seedha yaad reh jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPulakeshin II ne Harsha ko Narmada kinare HARAYA (632 CE, Aihole Inscription) — Harsha jeeta nahi, ye common\ngalti hai.\n3. Harsha Ki Administration\n●Hierarchy: Rashtra → Bhukti → Vishaya → Gram\n●Officers: Avanti(war-peace) · Simhanada(Commander-in-chief) · Kuntal(Ashwamedha) · Skandagupta(elephant army\nchief — sirf ek officer ka naam, Gupta raja NAHI)\n●Taxes: Bhaga(land,1/6th) · Hiranya(cash,traders) · Bali(religious)\n TRICK — \"RBVG\" + officer-name-confusion trick\n💡\nRashtra→Bhukti→Vishaya→Gram = \"RBVG\" — bada se chota, State→Province→District→Village, seedha size-\norder hai.\nYahan ek officer ka naam \"Skandagupta\" hai — ye Gupta dynasty ke Skandagupta RAJA se bilkul ALAG hai. Yaad\nrakho: \"is chapter mein Skandagupta sirf ek hathi-sena ka officer hai, koi raja nahi\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHarsha ke darbar mein \"Skandagupta\" naam ka ek OFFICER tha (elephant army chief) — ye Gupta Empire ke raja\nSkandagupta se bilkul alag hai, naam-confusion mat karo."," 4. 3 Chinese Travelers — Timeline Order\n●Fa-Hien(399-414CE) → Chandragupta II ke time · pehla Buddhist monk China se\n●Huen Tsang(629-645CE) → Harsha ke time · Nalanda gaye (Chancellor Shilabhadra) · ~15 saal rahe\n●I-Tsing(671-695CE) → Sea route se aaye · Buddhist monasteries + Shri Gupta temple\n TRICK — \"F-H-I\" timeline trick\n💡\nFa-Hien(400s) → Huen Tsang(600s) → I-Tsing(670s+) = \"F-H-I\" — alphabetical order bhi hai aur chronological bhi,\ndono match kar jaate hain, isliye easy yaad rahega.\nI-Tsing = akela Sea route wala — baaki dono land route se aaye, ye unique fact isse alag pehchan deta hai.\n5. Vakataka Dynasty\n●Founder Vindhyashakti · Capital Nandivardhana(Nagpur) · Sanskrit ki Vaidarbhi style\n●Pravarasena I → SIRF ye raja \"Maharaja/Emperor\" title paaye · 4 Ashwamedha yagya\n●Rudrasena II → Prabhavati Gupta (Chandragupta II ki beti) se shaadi · Vaishnavism apnaya\n●Pravarasena II → aakhri powerful raja · Setubandha likhi · nayi capital Pravarapura\n TRICK — \"Pravar-I-II\" bookend trick\n💡\nPravarasena I = shuruaat ka sabse bada title wala (sirf yehi \"Maharaja\"). Pravarasena II = end ka sabse bada writer\n(Setubandha likhi) — dono \"Pravarasena\" naam ke rajaon ne alag-alag \"sabse\" record banaya, ek title mein, ek literature\nmein.\nRudrasena II beech mein hai — Gupta se shaadi ka connect isko yaad rakhne layak banata hai: \"Vakataka-Gupta ka\nrishta takatvar bana Rudrasena II ke through\".\n6. Chalukya — 3 Branches\n●Badami (main): Capital Vatapi · Founder(real) Pulakeshin I\n●Western/Kalyani: Founder Tailapa II · vs Cholas · Powerful: Vikramaditya VI\n●Eastern/Vengi: Founder Vishnuvardhana · Telugu ka pehla use yahin\n TRICK — \"Badami-Kalyani-Vengi\" geography trick\n💡\n3 branches, 3 direction: Badami(original/central Karnataka) → Kalyani(Western split) → Vengi(Eastern split, Andhra)\n— jaise ek dynasty do disha mein baant gayi ho, Western aur Eastern dono \"Chalukya\" hi hain par alag founder.\nVengi = Telugu ka pehla use — Vengi khud Andhra region mein hai, isliye Telugu se seedha connect.\n7. Pulakeshin II — Ek Jeeta, Ek Haara\n●vs Harsha(632CE, Narmada) → Pulakeshin II JEETA\n●vs Narsimhavarman(Pallava) → Pulakeshin II HAARA → Narsimhavarman ne \"Vatapikonda\" title liya\n●Aihole Inscription — author Ravikirti (court poet)\n TRICK — \"North mein jeeta, South mein haara\" trick\n💡\nPulakeshin II ka record: North (Harsha) ke against JEETA, South (Pallava-Narsimhavarman) ke against HAARA.\nEk hi raja, do outcomes, do directions — \"jo North ko haraya wahi South se haar gaya\".\nVatapikonda title Pallava ne li (Vatapi=Chalukya ki capital, \"konda\"=jeetne wala) — Chalukya ne khud ye title nahi li,\nunke dushman ne li unki capital jeetne ke baad.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Vatapikonda\" title Pallava raja Narsimhavarman ne li (Vatapi/Chalukya capital jeetne ke baad) — Chalukya ne khud\nNAHI li."," 8. Vesara Style — Aihole & Pattadakal\n●Vesara = Nagara(North) + Dravidian(South) hybrid\n●Aihole: 70 temples · Pehla=Lad Khan(no Shikhara) · Aakhri=Meguti\n●Pattadakal: 10 temples (4 Nagara+6 Dravidian) · Virupaksha(best, Lokamahadevi ne banaya, INDIA KA PEHLA\nGOPURAM, Nataraja 81 mudras)\n TRICK — \"Lad Khan=No spire, Virupaksha=First Gate\" trick\n💡\nLad Khan = \"Ladka bina taj ke\" (bina Shikhara/spire ke) — pehla temple, par sabse simple, Vihar jaisa.\nVirupaksha = sabse bada aur best — India ka PEHLA Gopuram yahin hai, aur Lokamahadevi (rani) ne banaya. Yaad\nrakho: \"Virupaksha = Vishesh/VIP temple\" — sabse zyada \"firsts\" isi ke naam hain.\nLad Khan(no shikhara) ≠ Virupaksha(first gopuram) — dono ke \"missing/first\" facts alag temples ke hain, swap mat\nkaro.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLad Khan Temple (Aihole, pehla) mein Shikhara NAHI hai. First Gopuram = Virupaksha Temple (Pattadakal) mein hai.\nDono alag temples, alag facts.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Harsha: Kannauj,Shiladitya,khud-3-books(Nagananda-Ratnavali-Priyadarshika),Harshacharita=Banabhatta → Southern\ncampaign: Pulakeshin II ne Narmada pe HARAYA → Admin: RBVG, officer-Skandagupta(alag raja se) → Travelers:\nF-H-I(FaHien-HuenTsang-ITsing) → Vakataka: Vindhyashakti-Nandivardhana, PravarasenaI(Maharaja title)-\nRudrasenaII(Prabhavati Gupta)-PravarasenaII(Setubandha) → Chalukya: Badami(Pulakeshin I,II)-Kalyani(Tailapa II)-\nVengi(Vishnuvardhana,Telugu first) → Pulakeshin II: beat Harsha, lost to Narsimhavarman(Vatapikonda) → Vesara:\nAihole(LadKhan,no shikhara)-Pattadakal(Virupaksha,first Gopuram)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Harsha HAARA Pulakeshin II se (Narmada, 632 CE) — jeeta nahi.\n2) Harshacharita = Banabhatta ne likhi (Harsha ke baare mein), Harsha khud ne Nagananda/Ratnavali/Priyadarshika\nlikhi.\n3) Lad Khan=no Shikhara. First Gopuram=Virupaksha Temple. Do alag temples ke do alag facts.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Post-Gupta Empire"," HISTORY OF SOUTH INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 12 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Sangam Powers — Symbol Match\n●Chola = Tiger (Uraiyur→Puhar, cotton trade)\n●Chera = Bow (Vanji/Karur, sabse purana)\n●Pandya = Fish (Madurai, Pearls + Matriarchal rule)\n TRICK — \"TBF\" trick\n💡\nTiger-Chola, Bow-Chera, Fish-Pandya = \"TBF\". Yaad rakho: \"Toh Bola Fish\" — koi bhi silly line bana lo teeno\nletters se.\nPandya = Pearls + Women rule — dono unique facts hain (Megasthenes ki Indica mein mention), Chola aur Chera se\nalag inhe khaas banate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChola=Tiger, Chera=Bow, Pandya=Fish — kabhi swap mat karna. Pandya=pearls+matriarchal rule, Chola=cotton trade,\nChera=sabse purana.\n2. 3 Sangam Councils — Survival Pattern\n●1st (Madurai, Agastya) → KUCH BHI survive nahi hua\n●2nd (Alavai, Tolkappiyar) → SIRF Tolkappiyam survive hui\n●3rd (N.Madurai, Nakkirar) → Zyadatar Tamil literature isi se aayi\n TRICK — \"0-1-Most\" survival trick\n💡\nSurvival pattern ek seedha increasing scale hai: 1st=ZERO → 2nd=ONE (Tolkappiyam) → 3rd=MOST. Jitna baad ka\nSangam utna zyada bacha — naturally bhi sahi lagta hai (naya to zyada surakshit rehta hai).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Sangam se kuch survive NAHI hua. 2nd Sangam se sirf Tolkappiyam bachi. 3rd Sangam se zyadatar Tamil literature\naayi.\n3. Sangam Texts — Author Match\n●Tolkappiyam(Tolkappiyar) = grammar, sabse purani\n●Tirukkural(Tiruvalluvar) = philosophy/aphorisms\n●Silappadikaram(Ilango Adigal) = Kovalan-Kannagi-Madhavi love story\n●Manimekalai(Seethalai Sathanar) = Kovalan-Madhavi ki beti ki kahani\n TRICK — \"Maa-Beti\" story-link trick\n💡\nSilappadikaram = Kovalan-Kannagi ki kahani. Manimekalai = unki BETI ki kahani (Kovalan-Madhavi se) — dono\ntexts ek hi family ki 2 generations cover karte hain, isliye \"maa ki kahani vs beti ki kahani\" bolke yaad rakho.\n4. Pallava — Simhavishnu Se Narasimhavarman II Tak\n●Simhavishnu(founder) → Chola/Pandya/Sinhala/Kalabhra haraya\n●Mahendravarman I → Rock-cut architecture pioneer · Mattavilasa Prahasana likha\n●Narasimhavarman I → Pulakeshin II ko haraya → Vatapikonda title · Mahabalipuram Rathas\n●Narasimhavarman II → Kailasanatha Temple(Kanchi) + Shore Temple"," TRICK — \"I=Ratha, II=Temple\" trick\n💡\nNarasimhavarman I = \"I for Initial/Rathas\" (Mahabalipuram ke chote monolithic rathas banaye, aur Pulakeshin II ko\nharaya). Narasimhavarman II = \"II for bigger structures\" (Kailasanatha jaisa poora bada temple) — I ne chote\nstructures banaye, II ne bade temple.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNarasimhavarman I = Vatapikonda title + Mahabalipuram Rathas. Narasimhavarman II = Kailasanatha Temple + Shore\nTemple. Number confuse mat karo.\n5. Rashtrakuta — Dantidurga & Amoghavarsha\n●Dantidurga(founder) → Chalukyas ke feudatory the pehle · South India mein pehli Nagari script (Samantgarh\ninscription,754CE)\n●Amoghavarsha → Kavirajamarga(pehli Kannada text) · Jain follower · Arab traveler Suleiman aaya\n TRICK — \"Amogha = Kannada Pioneer\" trick\n💡\nAmoghavarsha = \"Amedya/Amazing\" pehli baar Kannada mein poetry — naam khud grand/first-jaisa lagta hai. Yaad\nrakho: \"Amoghavarsha = Adi Kannada likhne wala\".\n6. Imperial Chola — Vijayalaya, Rajaraja I, Rajendra I\n●Vijayalaya(founder,850CE) → Pallava feudatory the\n●Rajaraja I(REAL founder) → original naam Arumolivarman · Brihadeeswara Temple(Thanjavur) · Title Jayagonda\n· Sri Lanka ke Mahendra V ko haraya\n●Rajendra I → \"Napoleon of the South\"(V.A.Smith) · Title Gangaikondachola · SE Asia\nconquest(Kadaram,Srivijaya) · Nayi capital Gangaikondacholapuram\n TRICK — \"Do Brihadeeswara\" trap-buster\n💡\nBrihadeeswara Thanjavur = Rajaraja I (Dravidian style, granite, sabse bada, boundary wall wala pehla) vs\nBrihadeeswara Gangaikondacholapuram = Rajendra I (Vijayanagar style, Kaveri kinare). Yaad rakho: \"Baap ne\nThanjavur mein banaya, bete ne apni nayi capital mein doosra banaya\" — father-son, do temples, same naam.\nRajaraja=Gupta ka Samudragupta jaisa 'India ka Napoleon' nahi — Rajendra=South ka Napoleon. Dono alag\n\"Napoleon\" title, alag empire, confuse mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n2 Brihadeeswara Temples: Thanjavur=Rajaraja I banaya. Gangaikondacholapuram=Rajendra I banaya. Builder se\ndistinguish karo, naam same hone se confuse mat ho.\n7. Chola Administration — Assemblies & Grants\n●Village Assemblies: Ur(common people) · Sabha/Mahasabha(Brahmins) · Nagaram(merchants)\n●Land Grants: Brahmadeya(Brahmins) · Vellanvagi(non-Brahmins) · Devadana(temples) · Pallichchandam(Jains)\n TRICK — \"Sabha-Brahmin, Nagaram-Vyapari\" hook\n💡\nSabha = \"Sanskrit-sadhu jaisa formal naam\" → Brahmins. Nagaram = \"Nagar/city ka business\" → Merchants\n(commercial towns). Ur = plain/basic naam → common people (general village).\n8. Other Dynasties — Temple-Builder Match\n●Kakatiya(Warangal, Rudradeva I) → Woman ruler Rudramadevi\n●Ganga Dynasty(Odisha) → Narasimha Deva Varman = Konark Sun Temple · Anantavarman = Jagannath Temple\n●Kesari Dynasty → Lingaraj Temple (Bhubaneswar)\n●Hoysala(Vishnuvardhana) → Chennakesava Temple · aakhri raja Veer Ballala haraye Malik Kafur se"," ●Yadava(Bhillama V) → Capital Devagiri\n TRICK — \"Odisha 2 dynasty\" + temple hooks\n💡\nOdisha mein 2 alag dynasty confuse karti hain: Ganga(Konark+Jagannath, 2 temples) vs Kesari(sirf Lingaraj, 1\ntemple). Yaad rakho: \"Ganga do dariya jaisi 2 temple leke aayi, Kesari akela sher (Lingaraj) leke aaya\".\nGanga ke andar bhi 2 naam: Narasimha=Konark, Anantavarman=Jagannath — \"NK-AJ\" alphabetically bhi kaam kar\njaata hai.\nHoysala = Chennakesava — \"Chenna\" (sundar) temple, Vishnuvardhana ne banaya, seedha naam-founder match.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKonark Sun Temple = Narasimha Deva Varman. Jagannath Temple = Anantavarman. Dono Ganga Dynasty (Odisha) ke\nhain par alag rajaon ne banaye. Lingaraj Temple = alag dynasty (Kesari).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Symbols: Chola-Tiger,Chera-Bow,Pandya-Fish → Sangam councils: 0-1-Most survival → Texts:\nTolkappiyam,Tirukkural,Silappadikaram-Manimekalai(maa-beti) → Pallava: Simhavishnu-Mahendravarman(rock-cut)-\nNarasimhavarmanI(Vatapikonda,Rathas)-NarasimhavarmanII(Kailasanatha) → Rashtrakuta: Dantidurga-\nAmoghavarsha(Kavirajamarga,Kannada) → Chola: Vijayalaya-RajarajaI(Brihadeeswara Thanjavur,Jayagonda)-\nRajendraI(Napoleon of South,Gangaikondachola) → Admin: Sabha(Brahmin)-Nagaram(merchant) → Odisha:\nGanga(Konark+Jagannath)-Kesari(Lingaraj) → Hoysala(Chennakesava)-Yadava(Devagiri)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Chola=Tiger, Chera=Bow, Pandya=Fish — direct match questions.\n2) 2 Brihadeeswara Temples: Thanjavur=Rajaraja I, Gangaikondacholapuram=Rajendra I.\n3) Konark=Narasimha Deva Varman, Jagannath=Anantavarman (dono Ganga Dynasty), Lingaraj=alag dynasty (Kesari).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.12 History of South India"," EARLY MEDIEVAL PERIOD — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nAncient History · Chapter 13 (Final) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Kashmir — 3 Dynasties + Rajatarangini\n●Rajatarangini(Kalhana,1160CE) → \"Kashmir ki Mahabharata\" · Kalhana = Harsh(Lohar) ke court poet · Ant:\nJayasimha tak\n●Karkota(Durlabhavardhana,625CE) → Lalitaditya Muktapida = sabse famous, Martand Sun Temple banwaya\n●Utpal(Avantivarman,855CE) → Avantipura basaya · Mahila rajas: Sugandha + Queen Didda(980CE)\n●Lohar(Sangramaraja,1003CE) → Harsh(Kalhana ka patron) → Jayasimha(Rajatarangini ka last raja)\n TRICK — \"K-U-L\" Kashmir chain\n💡\n3 dynasties order: Karkota → Utpal → Lohar = \"KUL\" (matlab \"KUL/family\" — poora Kashmir ka \"kul\" 3 dynasty\nmein bata hai).\nLalitaditya = Martand Temple, Karkota dynasty ka — yaad rakho \"Lalitaditya = Largest Karkota achievement\".\n2 mahila rajas Utpal mein: Sugandha aur Didda — dono ek hi dynasty (Utpal) mein, alag mat karo doosri dynasty se.\n2. Pala Dynasty — Vikramashila vs Odantapuri Trap\n●Gopala(founder,750CE) → Odantapuri sthapit ki · Janta ne unhe chuna (unique)\n●Dharmapala(sabse shaandaar) → Vikramashila University banayi · Tripartite struggle mein haare\n●Devapala(sabse powerful) → Mihir Bhoja(Pratihara) ko haraya · Balaputradeva(Java) ne Nalanda ke liye villages\nmaange\n●Mahipala I → Rajendra I(Chola) se haare · Madanapal(aakhri raja)\n TRICK — \"Go-Odanta, Dharma-Vikrama\" trick\n💡\nGopala = Odantapuri (dono naam mein \"o\" sound — Gopala-Odantapuri). Dharmapala = Vikramashila (dono naam\nmein \"pala/shila\" jaisa dharmik-heavy feel hai, bada university). Founder ne CHOTA institute banaya (Odantapuri),\nsuccessor ne BADA university banaya (Vikramashila) — \"jitna aage utna bada\".\n3 alag Pala rajaon ka 3 alag \"sabse\": Gopala=founder, Dharmapala=shaandaar, Devapala=powerful — teeno alag\nsuperlatives, mix mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nOdantapuri = Gopala (Pala founder) ne banayi. Vikramashila = Dharmapala ne banayi. Dono Pala rajaon ki, par alag\nuniversities.\n3. Tripartite Struggle — 3 Dynasty Ki Ladai\n●3 Parties: Pala + Pratihara + Rashtrakuta — Kannauj control ke liye\n●Dharmapala(Pala) sabse pehle enter kiya → Vatsaraja(Pratihara) + Dhruva(Rashtrakuta) se haara\n●Devapala(Pala) → Mihir Bhoja(Pratihara) ko haraya\n TRICK — \"Pehli baar haara, doosri baar jeeta\" trick\n💡\nPala dynasty ka pattern: Dharmapala haara (pehli baar Tripartite mein) → Devapala jeeta (Mihir Bhoja ko haraya) —\nfather-son jaisa continuation, pehle nuksaan phir fayda.\n4. Sena Dynasty — Bengal Ke Aakhri Hindu Raja\n●Samanta Sena(founder, Karnataka se) → Ballala Sena(vidwan raja, Danasagara+Adbhutasagara)\n●Lakshmana Sena(aakhri Hindu raja) → Bhakhtiyar Khilji ne 1202CE mein haraya · Court poet Jayadeva(Gita\nGovinda) · 5 Jewels"," TRICK — \"Gita Govinda = Jayadeva\" hook\n💡\nJayadeva = Lakshmana Sena ke darbar mein → Gita Govinda likhi. Title Piyushavarsha — \"Piyush\" (amrit/nectar)\njaisa madhur kaavya, Krishna-Radha bhakti se juda.\nLakshmana Sena ka title = sabse lamba royal title ever — is unique superlative se hi yaad reh jaata hai ki ye Sena ka\naakhri/sabse important raja tha.\n5. Rajput Agnikula — 4 Branches\n●Gurjara-Pratihara · Chalukya(Solanki) · Paramara · Chahamana(Chauhan) — Mount Abu, sage Vashishtha ki\nyagya-agni se\n TRICK — \"GCPC\" Agnikula trick\n💡\nGurjara-Pratihara, Chalukya, Paramara, Chahamana = \"GCPC\" — bolo \"Garmi Chalne se Panch Chingari\" (agni-theme\nse connect, Agnikula=fire clan).\n6. Battles of Tarain — SABSE IMPORTANT\n●1st Tarain(1191CE): Muhammad Ghori vs Prithviraj Chauhan → Prithviraj JEETA\n●2nd Tarain(1192CE): → Prithviraj HAARA aur maara gaya\n●Battle of Chandawar(1194CE): Ghori ne Jayachandra(Gahadavala) ko haraya\n TRICK — \"1-Jeet, 2-Haar\" trick\n💡\nNumber khud hint deta hai: 1191 = \"pehla, 1 number achha lagta hai\" = JEET. 1192 = \"2, dusra chance nahi mila\" =\nHAAR. Bas \"1=jeet, 2=haar\" — is chhoti si ginti se pura fact lock ho jaata hai.\nSanyogita connect: Jayachandra(Gahadavala) ki beti, jise Prithviraj III ne apharan kiya — ye dushmani hi shayad\nGahadavala ko Ghori ke against support na karne ka reason bani (baad mein Jayachandra khud Chandawar mein haare).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1191 (1st Tarain) = Prithviraj JEETA. 1192 (2nd Tarain) = Prithviraj HAARA aur maara gaya. Saal ke last digit se yaad\nrakho: 1=jeet, 2=haar.\n7. Chalukya(Solanki) — Dilwara Trap\n●Capital Anahilawada · Bhimraj I → Mahmud Ghaznavi ka saamna, Somnath Temple(1025CE loot hua)\n●Bhima I → uske feudal lord Bimal Shah ne Dilwara Jain Temples banaye (Mount Abu) — RAJA ne khud NAHI\n●Bhima II(aakhri) → Qutbuddin Aibak ne attack kiya(1197CE)\n TRICK — \"Bimal ne Dilwara, Raja ne nahi\" trick\n💡\nBimal Shah — Dilwara — dono naam mein \"i\" sound common hai, par yaad rakho ye RAJA nahi, feudal LORD tha.\n\"Bima I ke time mein Bimal ne banaya\" — same-sounding naam se hi warning milti hai ki inhe alag rakho (raja Bhima\nvs subordinate Bimal).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDilwara Jain Temple (Mount Abu) = Bimal Shah ne banaya (Bhima I ka feudal lord), RAJA Bhima I ne khud nahi\nbanaya.\n8. Paramara — Raja Bhoja ≠ Mihira Bhoja\n●Raja Bhoja(1010-1060CE) → Paramara(Malwa) · Titles Navasahasanka · Dharanagari university · Bhojpur basaya\n●Mihira Bhoja(alag raja) → Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty ka\n TRICK — \"2 Bhoja, 2 Dynasty\" trick\n💡"," Do alag \"Bhoja\" naam ke raja: Raja Bhoja = Paramara (Malwa, \"Raja\" + \"Paramara\" dono mein \"Ra\" sound). Mihira\nBhoja = Pratihara (\"Mihira\" + \"Pratihara\" — bilkul alag naam-feel). Naam same (\"Bhoja\") hai par dynasty CONFIRM\nkarke hi answer do.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRaja Bhoja = Paramara dynasty (Malwa, Bhojpur town). Mihira Bhoja = Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty. Dono \"Bhoja\" naam\nse hain par bilkul alag dynasty — exam ka classic trap.\n9. Martand vs Kailasanatha — Cross-Chapter Trap\n●Martand Sun Temple → Lalitaditya Muktapida (Karkota, Kashmir)\n●Kailasanatha Temple → Narasimhavarman II (Pallava, Kanchipuram) — pichhle chapter se\n TRICK — \"Martand=Kashmir Sun, Kailasa=South Shiva\" trick\n💡\nMartand = \"Sun\" god ka mandir → Kashmir (thandi jagah, isliye Sun temple important tha). Kailasanatha = Shiva\n(Kailash Parvat) → South (Pallava) — dono naam khud hi apna region/deity bata dete hain.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Kashmir: KUL(Karkota-Utpal-Lohar), Rajatarangini=Kalhana → Karkota:Lalitaditya-Martand →\nUtpal:Sugandha+Didda → Pala: Gopala-Odantapuri, Dharmapala-Vikramashila, Devapala-powerful → Tripartite:\nPala+Pratihara+Rashtrakuta → Sena: Lakshmana(last Hindu,Jayadeva-GitaGovinda) → Agnikula:GCPC(Gurjara-\nChalukya-Paramara-Chahamana) → Tarain: 1191-jeet,1192-haar → Chandawar(1194,Jayachandra haara) → Solanki:\nBhimraj-Somnath, Bimal Shah-Dilwara(NOT raja) → Paramara: RajaBhoja≠Pratihara's MihiraBhoja →\nMartand(Kashmir) vs Kailasanatha(Pallava)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye last chapter hai, poori Ancient History yahin tak complete hoti hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Tarain: 1191=Prithviraj jeeta, 1192=Prithviraj haara aur maara gaya.\n2) Vikramashila=Dharmapala, Odantapuri=Gopala — dono Pala, alag university.\n3) Raja Bhoja=Paramara (Malwa). Mihira Bhoja=Gurjara-Pratihara. Naam same, dynasty alag.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Early Medieval Period (Final Chapter)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0442","t":"02 Medieval History Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / History / Medieval History","x":[" ARAB & TURK INVASIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. First Muslim Invader — Group vs Individual\n●First Muslim invaders (group) = Arabs\n●First Arab/Muslim invader (individual) = Muhammad bin Qasim (712 CE) → Raja Dahir(Sindh) ko Battle of Rewar\nmein haraya\n TRICK — \"Group vs Individual\" trick\n💡\nSawaal ka wording dhyan se padho: \"Kaun the\" (group) → Arabs. \"Kaun tha\" (specific naam) → Muhammad bin\nQasim. Ek hi fact, do tarah se poocha jaata hai — wording decide karti hai answer ka format.\n2. Mahmud Ghazni vs Muhammad Ghori — Objective Ka Farak\n●Mahmud Ghazni → sirf LOOT/Wealth Plunder, permanent rule NAHI chahiye tha\n●Muhammad Ghori → PERMANENT RULE chahiye tha → Delhi Sultanate ki neenv\n TRICK — \"Ghazni=Khazana, Ghori=Ghar\" trick\n💡\nGhazni = \"Khazana\" (khazana/treasure loot karna, naam mein hi \"khaz\" jaisa sound) — sirf paisa leke wapas. Ghori =\n\"Ghar banaya\" (permanent ghar/rule sthapit kiya) — dono naam \"Gh\" se shuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai, par\nkaam bilkul alag: ek ne khazana liya, doosre ne ghar basaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahmud Ghazni ka maksad = sirf wealth loot (permanent rule NAHI). Muhammad Ghori ka maksad = permanent rule.\nDono ka intention bilkul alag tha.\n3. Mahmud Ghazni — 17 Invasions, Somnath 16th\n●Total 17 invasions (1000-1027 CE) · 1st invasion(1001CE) → Jaipal(Hindu Shahi) ko haraya\n●16th invasion(1025-26CE) = Somnath Temple → Bhim I ko haraya, mandir loota\n TRICK — \"16≠17\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Somnath ko 17th samajhte hain (kyunki total 17 hain, so lagta hai last wali hogi) — GALAT,\nSomnath 16th thi, ek aur invasion baad mein bhi hui. Yaad rakho: \"Somnath = Solah (16)\" — dono mein \"so\" sound\nmatch hota hai, isse seedha 16 yaad rahega.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSomnath Temple attack = 16th invasion (1025-26 CE), NA ki 17th — total 17 invasions the, par Somnath specifically\n16th thi.\n4. Bhim I vs Bhim II — Do Alag Gujarat Raja\n●Bhim I → Somnath(1025-26CE) mein Mahmud Ghazni se HAARA\n●Bhim II → Gujarat/Patan(1178CE) mein Muhammad Ghori ko HARAYA (Ghori ki PEHLI HAAR)\n TRICK — \"I=Haara, II=Jeeta\" trick\n💡\nBhim I (chota number, purana, ~1025) = HAARA hua (Ghazni se). Bhim II (bada number, baad mein, 1178) = JEETA\n(Ghori ko haraya) — number jitna bada, result utna behtar (I=lose, II=win) — is simple pattern se dono yaad rahenge.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠"," Bhim I = Somnath (1025-26 CE) mein Ghazni se HAARA. Bhim II = Gujarat (1178 CE) mein Ghori ko HARAYA —\nGhori ki pehli haar. I aur II ko confuse mat karo.\n5. Muhammad Ghori — Poora Battle Record\n●1175CE: Multan+Kutch(1st invasion) · 1178CE: Gujarat mein Bhim II se HAARA (pehli haar)\n●1191CE(1st Tarain): Prithviraj se HAARA · 1192CE(2nd Tarain): Prithviraj ko HARAYA(decisive)\n●1194CE(Chandawar): Jayachandra ko HARAYA · 1205CE: Khokhar tribe(aakhri campaign)\n TRICK — \"Haar-Haar-Jeet-Jeet\" pattern trick\n💡\nGhori ka pattern: 1178=HAAR (Bhim II) → 1191=HAAR (Prithviraj) → 1192=JEET (Prithviraj) → 1194=JEET\n(Jayachandra). Pehle 2 baar haara, phir 2 baar jeeta — \"do haar, phir do jeet\" — is simple rhythm se poora timeline\nyaad rahega.\nSaal ke last digit se bhi trick nikalti hai: 8(1178)=haar, 1(1191)=haar, 2(1192)=jeet, 4(1194)=jeet — bas \"pehle do haar\nwale, baad ke do jeet wale\" yaad rakho.\n6. 3 Historians of Mahmud Ghazni\n●Utbi → Kitab-ul-Yamini\n●Firdausi → Shahnama (Persian EPIC POETRY, India ki history NAHI)\n●Al-Biruni → Tahqiq-i-Hind (=Kitab-ul-Hind) — India ke baare mein SABSE DETAILED\n TRICK — \"U-F-A\" historian trick\n💡\nUtbi=Yamini, Firdausi=Shahnama(poetry,not history), Al-Biruni=Hind(India-focused,sabse detailed) — teeno naam ke\npehle letter se apni book yaad rakho: U-F-A.\nFirdausi ko trap se bachao: uski Shahnama Persian POETRY hai, India ki history NAHI — baaki 2 (Utbi, Al-Biruni)\nhistory-focused hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nUtbi=Kitab-ul-Yamini. Al-Biruni=Tahqiq-i-Hind(=Kitab-ul-Hind). Firdausi=Shahnama (Persian epic POETRY, India\nhistory nahi) — teeno alag books, mix mat karo.\n7. 4 Slaves of Ghori — Territory Match\n●Tajuddin Yaldoz → Ghazni\n●Qutubuddin Aibak → Lahore+Delhi → Slave Dynasty(1206CE) — SABSE IMPORTANT\n●Nasiruddin Qubacha → Multan\n●Bakhtiyar Khilji → Bengal → Nalanda University DESTROY ki\n TRICK — \"YAQB\" slave-territory trick\n💡\nYaldoz-Ghazni, Aibak-Lahore/Delhi, Qubacha-Multan, Bakhtiyar-Bengal = \"YAQB\" — bolo \"Yaar Aibak Queen Bani\"\n(silly line, letters match ho jaayenge).\nNalanda destroyer = Bakhtiyar Khilji — cross-chapter link: Nalanda banayi thi Kumaragupta I ne (Gupta chapter),\naur destroy ki Bakhtiyar Khilji ne — ek hi jagah, do alag empires, dono extremes yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNalanda University destroy ki Bakhtiyar Khilji ne (Ghori ka slave, Bengal wala) — Muhammad Ghori ya Mahmud\nGhazni ne khud NAHI.\n8. Bonus — Chishti Sufi Order\n●Sheikh Moinuddin Chishti → Ghori ke saath India aaye · India mein Chishti Sufi Order ke founder · Dargah Ajmer,\nRajasthan"," TRICK — \"Ghori ke saath aaya Sufi\" hook\n💡\nYaad rakho: Moinuddin Chishti Ghori ke saath hi aaye the — political invasion (Ghori) aur spiritual movement (Sufi)\ndono saath-saath shuru hue is period mein.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"First Muslim(group)=Arabs, individual=Qasim(712,Raja Dahir haraya) → Ghazni=Loot vs Ghori=Permanent Rule →\nGhazni:17 invasions,16th=Somnath(BhimI haara) → Ghori: 1178-haar(BhimII), 1191-haar(Prithviraj), 1192-jeet, 1194-\njeet(Jayachandra) → Historians: Utbi-Yamini,Firdausi-Shahnama(poetry),Al-Biruni-TahqiqiHind → Slaves:\nYAQB(Yaldoz-Ghazni,Aibak-Lahore/Delhi/1206CE,Qubacha-Multan,Bakhtiyar-Bengal/Nalanda destroy) → Sufi:\nMoinuddin Chishti-Ajmer\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Somnath = 16th invasion (NOT 17th) — total 17 invasions the.\n2) Bhim I=haara(Somnath,Ghazni se). Bhim II=jeeta(Gujarat,Ghori ki pehli haar).\n3) Nalanda destroyer = Bakhtiyar Khilji (Ghori ka slave), na ki Ghori ya Ghazni khud.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Arab & Turk Invasions"," DELHI SULTANATE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 5 Dynasties — Duration Ka Trap\n●Slave(1206-1290) = 84 saal, 11 rulers — PEHLI\n●Khilji(1290-1320) = 30 saal\n●Tughlaq(1320-1412) = 92 saal — SABSE LAMBI\n●Sayyid(1414-1451) = 37 saal\n●Lodi(1451-1526) = 75 saal — AAKHRI (Afghan dynasty)\n TRICK — \"SKTSL — 84-30-92-37-75\" trick\n💡\nOrder: Slave-Khilji-Tughlaq-Sayyid-Lodi = \"SKTSL\". Common galti: log sochte hain Slave(pehli) ya Lodi(aakhri)\nsabse lambi hogi — NAHI, Tughlaq(92 saal, beech ki dynasty) sabse lambi hai.\nYaad rakho: \"Tughlaq = Tug-of-war jaisa lamba khichaa\" — naam mein hi \"lamba khinchna\" jaisa sound hai, isse 92-\nsaal-longest fact lock ho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTughlaq Dynasty (92 saal) = Delhi Sultanate ki SABSE LAMBI dynasty — Slave ya Lodi NAHI.\n2. Diwans (Departments) — Introducer Match\n●Diwan-e-Arz(Military) = Balban ne banaya\n●Diwan-e-Amir-Kohi(Agriculture) = Muhammad bin Tughlaq\n●Diwan-e-Khairat + Diwan-e-Bandagan + Dar-ul-shifa = Firoz Shah Tughlaq ne 3 banaye\n TRICK — \"1-1-3\" department-count trick\n💡\nBalban=1 department(Arz/military — Balban khud \"Blood and Iron\" tha, military-focused). Md bin Tughlaq=1 (Amir-\nKohi/agriculture — uske famous \"experiments\" mein se ek). Firoz Shah=3 departments (welfare-focused raja, isliye\nzyada departments) — \"jitna welfare-minded utne zyada departments\".\n3. Qutub Minar — Started vs Completed\n●Aibak → Qutub Minar START ki · Quwwat-ul-Islam Mosque + Adhai Din Ka Jhopra banwaya\n●Iltutmish → Qutub Minar COMPLETE ki (73 metres)\n●Aibak ki death: Chaugan(Polo) khelte hue, Lahore, 1210 CE — WAR mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Start-Complete\" + Polo-death trick\n💡\nAibak = \"Aarambh\" (shuruaat) — Qutub Minar start ki. Iltutmish = \"Illil poora kiya\" (complete kiya, 73m) — bas \"A se\nstart, I se poora\" yaad rakho.\nAibak ki death = Polo (Chaugan) — ek badshah khel khelte hue mar gaya, war mein nahi — ye unique/ironic fact\nkhud hi yaad reh jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Qutub Minar kisne banayi?\" → Aibak ne START ki, Iltutmish ne COMPLETE ki (73m). \"Built\" ka seedha jawab\nAibak dena galat hai agar \"complete\" poocha jaaye.\n4. Turkan-i-Chahalgani & Razia Sultana\n●Iltutmish → 40 nobles ka group BANAYA (Turkan-i-Chahalgani)\n●Balban → usi group ko ABOLISH kiya"," ●Razia Sultana → Medieval India ki pehli Muslim mahila raja · Purdah reject kiya · Assassination: Kaithal(Haryana),\n13 Oct 1240, Khokhar tribe dwara — Delhi mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Banaya vs Abolish\" + Razia-Kaithal trick\n💡\nIltutmish = \"Istart-Initiate\" (banaya) → Balban = \"Bal todna\" (bal/power todna, abolish kiya) — dono naam alag actions\nse match ho jaate hain (dono \"B\" se hi shuru nahi hote isliye easy distinguish).\nRazia ki death Kaithal mein hui, Delhi mein NAHI — yaad rakho: \"Kaithal mein Khokhar tribe ne Katal kiya\" —\nKa-Kh-Ka teeno sound se location aur culprit dono yaad reh jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTurkan-i-Chahalgani: Iltutmish ne BANAYA, Balban ne ABOLISH kiya. Razia ki assassination Kaithal(Haryana) mein\nhui, Delhi mein NAHI.\n5. Alauddin Khilji — Kohinoor Ka Sahi Jawab\n●Malik Kafur → Warangal campaign(1309CE) → Prataparudra Dev se Kohinoor diamond liya\n●Original naam: Ali Gurshasp · Title: Sikandar-e-Sani · Court poet Amir Khusro(Khazain-ul-Futuh)\n TRICK — \"Kohinoor = Warangal, NOT Gujarat/Chittor\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Kohinoor ko Gujarat ya Chittor se jodte hain (kyunki wo bhi famous campaigns the) — GALAT.\nYaad rakho: \"Warangal mein Kafur ko kohinoor mila\" — \"Kafur\" aur \"Kohinoor\" dono \"K\" se, aur Warangal khud\n\"war\" se shuru hota hai (jaise treasure-war jeetne se mila).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKohinoor Diamond = Malik Kafur ne Warangal(1309CE) campaign mein Prataparudra Dev se liya — Gujarat ya Chittor\nse NAHI.\n6. Muhammad Bin Tughlaq — SAB Experiments FAILED\n●Doab Taxation(10x→20x) → rebellion\n●Capital Shift(Delhi→Devagiri) → FAILED, wapas shift\n●Token Currency(copper/brass) → FAILED (nakli sikke)\n●Karachil Campaign → bhaari nuksaan, FAILED\n TRICK — \"Sab Kuch Fail\" trick\n💡\nEk hi word yaad rakho poore raja ke liye: FAIL. Doab-fail, Capital shift-fail, Token currency-fail, Karachil-fail — 4\nmein se 4 FAILED, isliye hi unhe \"unfortunate/ill-fated\" raja kaha jaata hai. Koi bhi \"successful\" wala option agar aaye\nexam mein, wo galat hoga.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuhammad bin Tughlaq ke SAARE major experiments (Capital Shift, Token Currency, Karachil Campaign, Doab\nTaxation) FAILED hue — koi bhi successful nahi tha.\n7. 2 Books \"Tarikh-i-Firozshahi\" — Author Trap\n●Ziauddin Barani ne likhi → Muhammad bin Tughlaq ke time par\n●Shams-i-Siraj Afif ne likhi → Firoz Shah Tughlaq ke time par\n TRICK — \"Barani=Juna, Afif=Firoz\" trick\n💡\nSame naam ki 2 books, 2 alag authors — yaad rakho pehla-letter match: Barani(pehle likha gaya author, alphabetically\nbhi B pehle) → Md bin Tughlaq(pehla/earlier raja). Afif(baad wala author) → Firoz Shah(baad wala raja). \"Pehla\nauthor-pehla raja, baad wala author-baad wala raja\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠"," \"Tarikh-i-Firozshahi\" naam ki 2 books hain: Ziauddin Barani=Muhammad bin Tughlaq ke baare mein. Shams-i-Siraj\nAfif=Firoz Shah Tughlaq ke baare mein. Author+ruler dono match karo.\n8. Firoz Shah Tughlaq — \"Akbar of Sultanate Period\"\n●Elliot & Elphinstone ne title diya — Muhammad bin Tughlaq ko NAHI\n●Welfare works: Employment Bureau, Kisano ke Takavi loans maaf, PWD found ki, Land Revenue tax 1/5→1/3\n TRICK — \"Welfare = Akbar-jaisa\" trick\n💡\nFiroz = Welfare raja (jaise Akbar bhi welfare/tolerance ke liye jaana jaata hai) — isliye historians ne unhe \"Akbar of\nSultanate Period\" bola. Muhammad bin Tughlaq = Fail raja — welfare wala tag sirf Firoz ko milta hai, uske\npredecessor(Juna Khan) ko nahi.\n9. Agra & Delhi Sultanate Ka Ant\n●Agra = Sikandar Lodi ne 1504CE mein basaya, 1506 se capital — Babur/Akbar ne NAHI\n●First Battle of Panipat(21 April 1526) → Babur ne Ibrahim Lodi ko haraya → Delhi Sultanate khatam, Mughal\nEmpire shuru\n TRICK — \"Sikandar=Agra, Ibrahim=Last\" trick\n💡\nSikandar Lodi = \"Sikandar ne shehar basaya\" (Agra) — dusra Sikandar (Alexander) bhi conqueror+city-builder jaisa\ntha, wordplay se yaad rakho.\nIbrahim Lodi = last domino — Lodi dynasty ka bhi last, poori Delhi Sultanate ka bhi last, battlefield mein hi mara\ngaya (Sikandar Lodi ki maut normal thi) — \"Ibrahim = end of the line\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAgra basaya Sikandar Lodi ne (1504 CE) — Babur ya Akbar ne NAHI, ye common misconception hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"5 dynasties: SKTSL(84-30-92-37-75, Tughlaq longest) → Diwans: Arz-Balban, AmirKohi-MdbinTughlaq,\nKhairat/Bandagan/Darulshifa-FirozShah → Qutub Minar: Aibak-start,Iltutmish-complete(73m) → Aibak death=Polo →\nTurkan-i-Chahalgani: Iltutmish-banaya,Balban-abolish → Razia: Kaithal death → Kohinoor: MalikKafur-\nWarangal(1309) → MdbinTughlaq: sab experiments FAILED → 2 TarikhiFirozshahi: Barani-MdbinTughlaq, Afif-\nFirozShah → Firoz Shah=Akbar of Sultanate → Agra=SikandarLodi(1504) → Panipat(1526)=Babur beat IbrahimLodi\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Tughlaq(92 saal)=Sabse lambi dynasty — Slave ya Lodi nahi.\n2) Qutub Minar: Aibak=started, Iltutmish=completed(73m).\n3) Kohinoor Diamond = Malik Kafur ne Warangal(1309) se liya, Gujarat/Chittor se nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Delhi Sultanate"," VIJAYANAGARA & BAHMANI EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Founders (2, Not 1!) + 4 Dynasties\n●Founders = Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono, sirf ek NAHI) — Kampili kingdom ke ex-ministers, 1336CE\n●Sangama(Harihara I) → Saluva(S.Narasimha) → Tuluva(Vir Narasimha, KDR yahin hai) →\nAravidu(Tirumala,last:Sriranga III)\n TRICK — \"2 Founders + STSA\" trick\n💡\nHarihara + Bukka = do bhai jaise mile founders — \"Har-Buk\" bolo, dono naam saath yaad rakhne ke liye.\n4 dynasty order: Sangama-Tuluva... wait, seedha: Sangama-Saluva-Tuluva-Aravidu = \"STSA\"(sequence thoda alag hai,\nbas yaad rakho S-S-T-A). Krishna Deva Raya = TULUVA, na ki Sangama (jo pehli/founding dynasty thi) — common\ngalti hai kyunki KDR itna famous hai log use founding dynasty se jod dete hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVijayanagara founders = Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono). Krishna Deva Raya = Tuluva dynasty se the, Sangama se\nNAHI.\n2. Religion — State vs Personal\n●State religion = Shaivism\n●Krishna Deva Raya personally = Vaishnavism\n TRICK — \"State-Shiv, KDR-Vishnu\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Rajya(state) Shiva ka bhakt, par Raja(KDR) khud Vishnu ka bhakt\" — ek hi empire mein 2 alag religious\nidentities, dono ko separately yaad rakho.\n3. Battle of Talikota (1565) — Ant Ki Ladai\n●Dusra naam: Rakkasa-Tangadi war · 23-25 Jan 1565\n●Vijayanagara: Sadasiva Raya(nominal raja) + Rama Raya(actual control minister) — HAARE\n●Confederation(4 sultanates): Ahmadnagar+Bijapur+Golkonda+Bidar — JEETE. Bahmani khud shamil NAHI\n(pehle hi toot chuka tha)\n TRICK — \"Raja naam ke liye, Minister kaam ke liye\" trick\n💡\nSadasiva Raya = naam ka raja (nominal), Rama Raya = kaam ka raja (actual control) — dono ek hi side pe the, par\npower alag logo ke haath mein — is unique political setup ko yaad rakho.\n4 sultanates jeete, Bahmani khud NAHI tha — kyunki Bahmani tab tak already 5 tukdo mein toot chuka tha, isliye\n\"confederation\" naam se pukara gaya, Bahmani naam se nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBattle of Talikota mein confederation = 4 sultanates (Ahmadnagar, Bijapur, Golkonda, Bidar) — Bahmani khud is\nconfederation ka hissa NAHI tha (pehle hi toot chuka tha).\n4. Krishna Deva Raya — Works & Titles\n●Amuktamalyada(Telugu) = Polity/raj-neeti · Jambavati Kalyanam(Sanskrit) = drama\n●Titles: Andhra Bhoja, Andhra Pitamaha, Abhinava Bhoja, Yavanraj Sthanacharya\n●Constructions: Hazara Rama Temple, Vithala Swami Temple, Hospet(wife ki yaad), Nagallapur(maa Nagaladevi ki\nyaad)"," TRICK — \"Telugu-Politics, Sanskrit-Drama\" + Hospet-Nagallapur trick\n💡\nAmuktamalyada = \"Aam/Aam-janta ki bhasha (Telugu)\" for raj-neeti (practical politics ke liye local bhasha).\nJambavati Kalyanam = \"classical/Sanskrit\" — drama ke liye traditional bhasha.\nHospet = Patni ki yaad, Nagallapur = Maa ki yaad — dono cities family members ki memory mein, easy match: \"H\"\nfor \"Hamsafar(wife)\", \"Naga\" khud maa ke naam (Nagaladevi) mein hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmuktamalyada = TELUGU (polity). Jambavati Kalyanam = SANSKRIT (drama). Dono Krishna Deva Raya ki\nrachnayein hain, alag bhasha mein.\n5. Ashtadiggajas — Peddana Ki Title Trap\n●Allasani Peddana(#7) = \"Grandfather of Telugu poetry\" (Andhra Kavita Pitamaha) — Manucharita likhi\n●Tenali Ramakrishna(#2) = Humorist, sabse famous story-teller\n TRICK — \"Peddana ki Pitamaha ≠ Raja ki Pitamaha\" trick\n💡\nKDR ka title = \"Andhra Pitamaha\". Peddana ka title = \"Andhra Kavita Pitamaha\" — dono mein \"Pitamaha\"\ncommon hai isliye confuse hota hai, par Peddana ke title mein extra word \"Kavita\" (poetry) hai — \"Kavita wala\nPeddana ka hai, plain wala Raja ka\" — is ek extra word se hi dono alag ho jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKrishna Deva Raya = \"Andhra Pitamaha\". Allasani Peddana = \"Andhra Kavita Pitamaha\" (Grandfather of Telugu\nPOETRY specifically) — dono alag titles, ek word ka farak.\n6. Bahmani Founder — 3 Naam, Ek Aadmi\n●Original: Zafar Khan\n●Nickname: Hasan Gangu\n●Ruler naam: Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah\n●Capital: Gulbarga(renamed Ahsanabad)\n TRICK — \"ZHA\" 3-naam trick\n💡\nZafar Khan(original) → Hasan Gangu(nickname) → Alaunddin Hasan Bahman Shah(ruler-title) = \"Z-H-A\" — bolo\n\"Zindagi Hamesha Aage badhti hai\" (ek naam se doosre naam tak, life-journey jaisa).\n7. Bahmani Capital Shift\n●Gulbarga(founder Alauddin Hasan ne banayi) → Bidar(Shihabuddin Ahmad Shah I ne shift ki)\n TRICK — \"Founder-Gulbarga, Shihab-Bidar\" trick\n💡\nFounder khud pehli capital banata hai (Gulbarga), aur baad ka raja(Shihabuddin) naya shift karta hai(Bidar) —\npattern har dynasty mein common hai (jaise Slave dynasty mein bhi Lahore→Delhi shift hua tha), isliye is pattern se\nyaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahmani capital: Alauddin Hasan(founder) ne Gulbarga banayi. Shihabuddin Ahmad Shah I ne Bidar shift ki — galat\nruler se link mat karo.\n8. Gol Gumbaz vs Charminar — Builder Match\n●Gol Gumbaz = Muhammad Adil Shah(Bijapur) ne banaya\n●Ibrahim Adil Shah(Bijapur) = Kitab-e-Nauras likhi, Dakhani language promote ki — Gol Gumbaz NAHI banaya"," ●Charminar + Hyderabad(Bhagyanagar) = Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah(Golkonda) ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Same first name, alag kaam\" trick\n💡\n2 alag \"Muhammad\" naam ke rajaon ne 2 alag building banayi: Muhammad Adil Shah(Bijapur)=Gol Gumbaz,\nMuhammad Quli Qutb Shah(Golkonda)=Charminar. Naam same-ish hai (\"Muhammad\") par dynasty+building bilkul\nalag — surname (\"Adil\" vs \"Quli\") se differentiate karo.\nIbrahim Adil Shah ≠ Muhammad Adil Shah — dono Bijapur ke hain, par Ibrahim ne kitaab likhi (Kitab-e-Nauras),\nMuhammad ne building banayi (Gol Gumbaz).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGol Gumbaz = Muhammad Adil Shah (Bijapur), Ibrahim Adil Shah NAHI. Charminar+Hyderabad = Muhammad Quli\nQutb Shah (Golkonda, alag dynasty).\n9. 5 Deccan States — Oldest, Newest, Merge\n●Berar(1484,oldest) → Ahmadnagar(1574) mein merge\n●Bijapur(1489) → Mughal-Aurangzeb(1686) ne annex kiya\n●Ahmadnagar(1490) → Mughal-Shah Jahan(1636) ne annex kiya\n●Golkonda(1512) → Mughal-Aurangzeb(1687) ne annex kiya\n●Bidar(1526,newest) → Bijapur(1619) mein merge\n TRICK — \"Berar oldest, Bidar newest\" trick\n💡\nFounded order: 1484(Berar)→1489(Bijapur)→1490(Ahmadnagar)→1512(Golkonda)→1526(Bidar) — Berar sabse\npurana, Bidar sabse naya.\nAurangzeb ne 2 liye(Bijapur+Golkonda), Shah Jahan ne 1(Ahmadnagar) — \"Aurangzeb ne do haath se do state\nliye\" — number se yaad rakho: Aurangzeb=2, Shah Jahan=1.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSabse purana Deccan state = Berar(1484). Sabse naya = Bidar(1526). Aurangzeb ne Bijapur(1686)+Golkonda(1687)\nannex kiye; Shah Jahan ne Ahmadnagar(1636) annex kiya.\n10. Foreign Travelers — Kaun Kiske Time Aaya\n●Nicolo Conti(Italy) → Devaraya I(1420CE)\n●Abdur Razzaq(Persia) → Devaraya II\n●Paes + Barbosa(Portuguese) → Krishna Deva Raya\n●Fernao Nuniz(Portuguese) → Achyuta Deva Raya\n TRICK — \"2 Devarayas, 2 travelers\" trick\n💡\nDevaraya I → Conti(dono naam \"I\"/\"o\" sound se end hote hain lagbhag). Devaraya II → Razzaq. Number I-II se\ntravelers alphabetically bhi roughly match karte hain (C before R).\nKDR ke time 2 Portuguese aaye(Paes+Barbosa) — sabse famous raja ke time sabse zyada travelers, naturally bhi sahi\nlagta hai (bada raja=zyada visitors).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Founders: Harihara I+Bukka(1336) → 4 dynasty: Sangama-Saluva-Tuluva(KDR)-Aravidu → Religion: State-\nShaivism,KDR-Vaishnavism → Talikota(1565): SadasivaRaya+RamaRaya haare, 4 sultanates jeete(Bahmani nahi) →\nKDR: Amuktamalyada(Telugu)-JambavatiKalyanam(Sanskrit), Andhra Pitamaha → Peddana=Andhra KAVITA\nPitamaha(alag) → Bahmani founder: ZafarKhan-HasanGangu-AlauddinHasanBahmanShah → Capital:\nGulbarga(founder)-Bidar(Shihabuddin) → GolGumbaz=MdAdilShah, Charminar=MdQuliQutbShah → 5 Deccan:\nBerar(oldest)-Bidar(newest), Aurangzeb=2states,ShahJahan=1 → Travelers: Conti-DevarayaI, Razzaq-DevarayaII,\nPaes/Barbosa-KDR, Nuniz-AchyutaDevaRaya\""," Roz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Founders=Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono). KDR=Tuluva dynasty, Sangama nahi.\n2) Battle of Talikota: confederation=4 sultanates, Bahmani khud shamil nahi tha.\n3) Gol Gumbaz=Muhammad Adil Shah. Charminar/Hyderabad=Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah — do alag 'Muhammad'\nrajaon ke do alag buildings.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Vijayanagara & Bahmani Empire"," BHAKTI & SUFI MOVEMENT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Saguna vs Nirguna — Guru-Shishya Ka Twist\n●Saguna(Roop wala) → Ramananda, Surdas, Meerabai, Tulsidas, Chaitanya\n●Nirguna(Nirakar) → Kabirdas, Guru Nanak, Dadu Dayal\n●Ramananda(Saguna) ka shishya Kabirdas(Nirguna) — guru-shishya mein philosophy badal gayi\n TRICK — \"Roop vs Nirakar\" + guru-shishya-twist trick\n💡\nSaguna = \"Sa+Guna\"(guno/attributes ke SAATH) → roop wala bhagwan. Nirguna = \"Nir+Guna\"(guno ke\nBINA/nirakar) → formless. Naam mein hi \"sa/nir\" (with/without) ka meaning chhupa hai.\nRamananda(Saguna) → Kabir(Nirguna) — unique example jahan guru ek tarah ka tha, shishya doosri tarah ka ban\ngaya. Ye exact combo yaad rakho: \"Guru roop wala tha, shishya nirakar ban gaya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKabirdas aur Guru Nanak = NIRGUNA. Ramananda, Meerabai, Surdas, Tulsidas = SAGUNA. Ramananda khud Saguna\nthe lekin unke shishya Kabir Nirguna the.\n2. Adi Shankaracharya — 4 Mathas\n●North=Badrinath · East=Puri · West=Dwarka · South=Sringeri\n●Philosophy: Advaita Vedanta · Kitaab: Brahmasutra Bhashya · Smarta Tradition develop ki\n TRICK — \"N-E-W-S\" compass trick\n💡\nCompass directions se seedha match: North-Badrinath, East-Puri, West-Dwarka, South-Sringeri. Bas actual India ka\nmap yaad karo — Badrinath Himalaya(N) mein hai, Puri Odisha(E) mein, Dwarka Gujarat(W) mein, Sringeri\nKarnataka(S) mein — geography se hi lock ho jaata hai.\n3. Meerabai Ka Guru — Chain Yaad Rakho\n●Ramananda → Raidas(Ravidas) → Meerabai\n●Ramananda directly Meerabai ka guru NAHI tha\n TRICK — \"3-generation chain\" trick\n💡\nEk seedhi(ladder) socho: Ramananda(top) → Raidas(middle) → Meerabai(bottom). Meerabai ka SEEDHA guru\nRaidas hai, Ramananda uska \"guru ka guru\" hai — teen level ki chain, skip mat karo beech wala.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMeerabai ka DIRECT guru = Raidas (Ravidas), na ki Ramananda. Ramananda-Raidas-Meerabai — teen-level chain hai.\n4. Bhavartha-Deepika vs Bhavarth Ramayana\n●Bhavartha-Deepika(Gita commentary, Marathi) = Gyaneshwar\n●Bhavarth Ramayana(Ramayana commentary) = Eknath\n TRICK — \"Deepika=Gita, Ramayana=Ramayana\" trick\n💡\nBook naam mein hi doosra text ka naam hai — Bhavarth RAMAYANA = seedha Ramayana ki commentary (Eknath\nne likhi). Bhavartha-DEEPIKA = \"deepika\" (lamp/light) jaisa naam Gita ke gyaan-prakash se match karta hai\n(Gyaneshwar ne likhi) — dono authors ke naam mein bhi \"G\" wala pattern hai jo Gita se hi shuru karta hai\n(Gyaneshwar-Gita)."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBhavartha-Deepika (Gita commentary) = Gyaneshwar. Bhavarth Ramayana (Ramayana commentary) = Eknath. Naam\nsimilar lagte hain par alag authors, alag texts.\n5. 7 Major Philosophies — Suffix Trap\n●Advaita=Shankaracharya · Vishishtadvaita=Ramanujacharya · Dvaitadvaita=Nimbarkacharya\n●Shuddhadvaita=Vallabhacharya · Dvaita=Madhvacharya · Achintya Bhedabheda=Chaitanya · Shaiva\nVishishtadvaita=Shrikantha\n TRICK — \"AVDSD-ACS\" philosophy trick\n💡\nSuffix dekh ke confuse mat ho — sab \"-dvaita/-advaita\" hain par har naam ek SPECIFIC philosopher se juda hai. Yaad\nrakho ek chain: \"Advaita-Shankaracharya, Vishishtadvaita-Ramanuja, Dvaitadvaita-Nimbarka, Shuddhadvaita-\nVallabha, Dvaita-Madhva\" — pehla-syllable(A,Vi,Dvaita,Shuddha,Dvaita) se philosopher yaad rakho, na ki poora\nnaam.\nChaitanya = Achintya Bhedabheda (ye \"dvaita/advaita\" suffix use NAHI karta, isliye alag pehchan aasan hai).\n6. Chishti Order — Oldest, NOT Largest\n●India ka SABSE PURANA(oldest) Sufi Order — sabse bada(largest) NAHI\n●Founder Muinuddin Chishti → Khanqah AJMER mein (Delhi mein NAHI)\n●Nizamuddin Auliya(Chishti) = Mehboob-e-Ilahi · Disciple Amir Khusrau(poet-musician)\n TRICK — \"Oldest≠Largest\" + Ajmer trick\n💡\nChishti = SABSE PEHLA aaya (isliye oldest), par baad mein doosre orders bhi bade ho gaye — \"pehla aana\" aur\n\"sabse bada hona\" alag baatein hain, is distinction ko yaad rakho.\nMuinuddin Chishti = Ajmer — pehle bhi (Ch.1 Medieval, Arab/Turk Invasions mein) yaad kiya tha ki ye Ghori ke\nsaath India aaye the, dargah Ajmer mein hai — cross-chapter consistency check karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChishti Order = India ka SABSE PURANA Sufi Order (largest NAHI). Muinuddin Chishti ka Khanqah AJMER mein\ntha, Delhi mein NAHI.\n7. Tansen Ka Guru — Shattari Order\n●Muhammad Ghaus(Shattari Order, title \"Qutb\") = Tansen ke Guru — Nizamuddin Auliya NAHI\n TRICK — \"Ghaus=Music Guru\" trick\n💡\nMuhammad Ghaus naam mein \"Ghaus\" sound \"Ghazal/music\" jaisa hai — isse Tansen(music legend) ka guru yaad\nrakhna easy ho jaata hai. Nizamuddin Auliya = Amir Khusrau ka guru tha, Tansen ka NAHI — dono \"famous musician-\nconnected sufi\" lagte hain isliye confuse hota hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTansen ka guru = Muhammad Ghaus (Shattari Order). Nizamuddin Auliya (Chishti Order) = Amir Khusrau ka guru tha\n— dono alag hain.\n8. 6 Sufi Orders — Founder + Key Figure\n●Chishti(Muinuddin Chishti,oldest) · Shattari(Shah Abdullah,Tansen's guru Muhammad Ghaus)\n●Firdausi(Sheikh Badruddin, Suhrawardi ki BRANCH) · Naqshbandi(Bahauddin Naqshband, India mein Ahmad\nSirhindi)\n●Suhrawardi(Shihabuddin Suhrawardi) · Qadiri(Abdul Qadir Gilani, follower Dara Shikoh)"," TRICK — \"CSFNSQ\" 6-order trick\n💡\nChishti-Shattari-Firdausi-Naqshbandi-Suhrawardi-Qadiri = \"CSFNSQ\" — koi bhi silly sentence bana lo letters se, jaise\n\"Chai Se Fresh Na Soyi Qismat\".\nFirdausi = Suhrawardi ki hi BRANCH — ye ek is-poore-list mein akela \"sub-order\" hai, baaki sab independent orders\nhain. Qadiri = Dara Shikoh (Mughal prince, Aurangzeb ka bhai) — is royal-connection se yaad rakho.\n9. Sattriya Dance — Shankaradeva (Assam)\n●Shankaradeva(Assam) → Sattriya dance ke founder · Bhakti Assam mein start ki · Borgeets tradition\n TRICK — \"Assam-Sattriya\" hook\n💡\nShankaradeva-Sattriya — dono \"S\" se, Assam ka apna unique dance form (Bharatnatyam/Kathak se confuse mat karo —\nwo alag regions/founders ke hain).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSattriya dance ka founder = Shankaradeva (Assam), na ki Bharatnatyam/Kathak ka koi founder — ye alag classical\ndance forms hain.\n10. Top 5 Sufi Terms\n●Chilla = 40-din meditation · Khanqah = Sufi residence · Fana = Khuda ke prem mein dubna\n●Sama = Music-dance spiritual practice · Wahdat-ul-Wujud = Monism(oneness)\n TRICK — \"CKFSW\" term-meaning trick\n💡\nChilla=40 din (number yaad rakho), Khanqah=ghar/residence, Fana=dubna/immersion, Sama=music, Wahdat-ul-\nWujud=Wujud(existence)=Monism/oneness — last term ka naam khud hi \"ekta/wujud\" bata deta hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Saguna(Ramananda-Surdas-Meera-Tulsi-Chaitanya) vs Nirguna(Kabir-Nanak-Dadu) →\nShankaracharya:4Mathas(NEWS) → Meerabai guru-chain: Ramananda-Raidas-Meerabai → Gyaneshwar(Bhavartha-\nDeepika,Gita) vs Eknath(Bhavarth Ramayana) → 7 philosophies: Advaita-Shankaracharya,Vishishtadvaita-\nRamanuja,Dvaitadvaita-Nimbarka,Shuddhadvaita-Vallabha,Dvaita-Madhva,AchintyaBhedabheda-Chaitanya →\nChishti=oldest(Ajmer,not largest) → Nizamuddin Auliya-Amir Khusrau vs Muhammad Ghaus-Tansen → 6 orders:\nCSFNSQ → Shankaradeva=Sattriya(Assam) → Terms: Chilla-40din,Khanqah-residence,Fana-immersion,Sama-\nmusic,Wahdat-ul-Wujud-monism\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Kabirdas aur Guru Nanak = Nirguna; Ramananda/Meerabai/Surdas/Tulsidas = Saguna.\n2) Meerabai ka guru = Raidas (Ramananda ka shishya), na ki Ramananda directly.\n3) Chishti Order = oldest (largest NAHI), Ajmer mein (Delhi nahi). Tansen ka guru = Muhammad Ghaus (Shattari),\nNizamuddin Auliya nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Bhakti & Sufi Movement"," MUGHAL EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 5 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Babur = Founder, Akbar = Real Founder\n●Babur = Founder(1526) · Akbar = REAL/Actual Founder — same pattern as Gupta(Shri Gupta vs Chandragupta I)\n●Baburnama = Chagatai TURKISH mein likhi (Persian/Arabic NAHI) · Persian translation: Abdur Rahim Khan-i-\nKhana · English: Annette Beveridge\n TRICK — \"Cross-chapter pattern\" trick\n💡\nYe BILKUL same pattern hai jo Gupta chapter mein tha: \"Shri Gupta=founder, Chandragupta I=real founder\" →\nyahan \"Babur=founder, Akbar=real founder\". Ek hi memory-hook dono chapters ke liye use karo.\nBaburnama = Babur ki Boli (Chagatai Turkish, uski matribhasha) mein likha — obvious hai ki khud ki autobiography\nkhud ki bhasha mein likhega, Persian/Arabic uski mother tongue nahi thi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBabur = Founder. Akbar = Real/Actual Founder. Baburnama = Chagatai Turkish mein (Persian/Arabic NAHI) —\nPersian translation baad mein Abdur Rahim ne ki.\n2. Babur Ke 4 Battles — PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA\n●Panipat(1526,Ibrahim Lodi) → Tulughma formation + Ottoman artillery pehli baar use\n●Khanwa(1527,Rana Sanga) → Ghazi title + alcohol ban + Tamgha tax khatam\n●Chanderi(1528,Medini Rai) → Rajput mahilaon ne Jauhar kiya\n●Ghagra(1529,Afghans) → Permanent control India par mila\n TRICK — \"PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA\" trick (source ka apna mnemonic)\n💡\n\"Babur ne PANi piya, KHAna khaya, phir CHAdar odh kar, GHAr gaya\" — PAN=Panipat, KHA=Khanwa,\nCHA=Chanderi, GHA=Ghagra. Har battle ke baad ek naya action: Tulughma(Panipat)-Ghazi(Khanwa)-\nJauhar(Chanderi)-Permanent control(Ghagra).\n3. Humayun's Death & Sher Shah's Purana Qila\n●Humayun ki death: Dinpanah(Library) ki seedhiyon se girke — WAR mein NAHI, 1556CE\n●Purana Qila = Sher Shah Suri ne banaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah ko todkar) — Humayun ne NAHI\n TRICK — \"Library se giri, Qila Sher Shah ne banaya\" trick\n💡\nLane-Poole ne Humayun ke baare mein kaha: \"tumbled through life and tumbled out of it\" — 'tumbled'(girna) = literal\ndeath bhi (seedhiyon se girkar mara)! Ek hi word life aur death dono describe karta hai — ye unique quote-fact khud\nyaad reh jaata hai.\nSher Shah ne Humayun ki hi building(Dinpanah) ko TODKAR apna Purana Qila banaya — \"dushman ki cheez tod\nke apni banayi\" — is political-symbolism se yaad rakho ki QILA Sher Shah ka hai, Humayun ka nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHumayun ki death Dinpanah(library) ki seedhiyon se girke hui, kisi battle mein NAHI. Purana Qila Sher Shah Suri ne\nbanaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah todkar), Humayun ne khud NAHI.\n4. Ain-i-Dahsala vs Ain-i-Akbari\n●Ain-i-Dahsala(1580) = Todar Mal ka Land Revenue System\n●Ain-i-Akbari = Abul Fazl ki Akbarnama ka 3rd part (Akbarnama ki \"soul\")"," TRICK — \"Dahsala=Dus, Akbari=Akbar-ki-kitaab\" trick\n💡\nDahsala = \"Dah(10)\" — 10-saal ki average paidawar ka calculation, Todar Mal ka land-revenue formula. Akbari =\nseedha \"Akbar-naama\" ka hi hissa — naam mein hi \"Akbar ki kitaab\" bata diya, isse Abul Fazl se link ho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAin-i-Dahsala = Todar Mal ka land revenue system (1580). Ain-i-Akbari = Abul Fazl ki Akbarnama ka 3rd part — dono\nbilkul alag cheezein hain.\n5. Ibadat Khana(1575) vs Din-i-Ilahi(1582)\n●Ibadat Khana(1575, Fatehpur Sikri) = inter-religious dialogue centre — 1582 mein band\n●Din-i-Ilahi(1582) = Akbar ka naya \"dharm\" (Tauhid-e-Ilahi)\n TRICK — \"7-saal gap\" trick\n💡\nIbadat Khana(1575) BAND hui usi saal jab Din-i-Ilahi(1582) SHURU hua — 7 saal ka gap, ek khatam hote hi\ndoosra shuru — \"baat-cheet(dialogue) khatam, naya dharm shuru\". Yaad rakho: dialogue centre PEHLE aaya(1575),\nnaya religion BAAD mein(1582).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIbadat Khana(1575)=dialogue centre, band 1582 mein. Din-i-Ilahi(1582)=naya dharm. Dono alag cheezein, 7 saal ka\ngap.\n6. Tansen Ka Guru & Nur Jahan Ka Naam\n●Tansen asli naam Ramtanu Pandey · Guru Muhammad Ghaus(Shattari Order) — Nizamuddin Auliya NAHI (Bhakti-\nSufi chapter se yaad karo)\n●Nur Jahan asli naam Mehrunnisa · Pita Itimad-ud-Daula(asli naam Ghiyas Beg) · Uska tomb Agra mein — Pietra\nDura ka earliest FULL use\n TRICK — Cross-chapter callback trick\n💡\nTansen-Muhammad Ghaus — ye EXACT SAME fact Bhakti-Sufi chapter mein bhi tha, isliye do chapters mein cross-\nverify ho jaata hai, bhoolna mushkil.\nNur Jahan = \"Prakash ki Duniya\" (naam ka matlab) — par uska ASLI naam Mehrunnisa hai, Nur Jahan sirf ek\nTITLE hai jo Jahangir ne diya — \"title ≠ asli naam\" pattern yaad rakho.\n7. Guru Arjan Dev vs Guru Tegh Bahadur — Kisne Kise Maara\n●Guru Arjan Dev(5th Guru) → JAHANGIR ne execute kiya (Khusrau rebellion mein saath dene ke liye)\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th Guru) → AURANGZEB ne execute kiya (Islam accept karne se mana kiya)\n TRICK — \"5th=Jahangir, 9th=Aurangzeb\" trick\n💡\nGuru number aur Mughal raja dono timeline mein match karte hain: 5th Guru(earlier) = Jahangir(earlier raja), 9th\nGuru(baad mein) = Aurangzeb(baad ka raja) — dono \"pehle wala-pehle wala, baad wala-baad wala\" pattern se lock\nho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Arjan Dev = Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur = Aurangzeb ne execute kiya. Bahut common exam\ntrap — number(5th/9th) se raja match karo.\n8. Kohinoor Diamond — Poori Journey\n●Kakatiya dynasty(Golconda) mein originally · Malik Kafur laaya Warangal(1309) se\n●Golkonda-Shahjahan treaty(1636) mein Jumla ne gift kiya · Baad mein Nadir Shah(Persia) ne loota"," TRICK — \"4-stop journey\" trick\n💡\nKohinoor ka safar ek 4-stop train jaisa socho: Kakatiya(origin) → Malik Kafur(1309,laya Delhi) → Jumla-\nShahjahan gift(1636) → Nadir Shah(loota). Har stop pe ek naya \"malik\", ye pura chain yaad rakho, ek bhi step skip\nmat karo.\n9. Dagh & Huliya System — Original Inventor\n●Alauddin Khilji(original inventor) → Sher Shah Suri(revived) → Akbar(bhi use kiya)\n TRICK — \"3 rajaon ne use kiya, sirf ek ne banaya\" trick\n💡\n3 alag rajaon ke naam is system se juda hai — par sirf Alauddin Khilji ORIGINAL inventor hai, baaki do (Sher Shah,\nAkbar) ne sirf use/revive kiya. \"Banane wala sirf ek, chalane wale kayi\" — pattern yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDagh aur Huliya system originally Alauddin Khilji ne banaya (Delhi Sultanate chapter se). Sher Shah ne revive kiya,\nAkbar ne bhi use kiya — original credit Alauddin ka hai.\n10. Key Sources — Author Match\n●Baburnama(Babur,Chagatai) · Humayun-nama(Gulbadan Begum) · Akbarnama(Abul Fazl,3-parts,Part3=Ain-i-\nAkbari)\n●Tabaqat-i-Akbari(Nizamuddin Ahmad) · Tuzuk-i-Jahangiri(Jahangir khud, Persian, autobiography)\n TRICK — Emperor-vs-Courtier author trick\n💡\nKhud-likhi(Babur-Baburnama, Jahangir-Tuzuk) vs Doosre ne likhi(Humayun-nama by Gulbadan Begum(behen),\nAkbarnama by Abul Fazl(courtier)) — jinhone khud likhi wo \"autobiography\", baaki \"biography by someone else\".\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Babur=founder,Akbar=real founder → Baburnama=Chagatai Turkish → 4 battles: PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA(Tulughma-\nGhazi-Jauhar-PermanentControl) → Humayun death=library seedhi → Sher Shah=Purana Qila(NOT Humayun) → Ain-\ni-Dahsala(TodarMal,revenue) vs Ain-i-Akbari(AbulFazl,Akbarnama pt3) → Ibadat Khana(1575)→Din-i-Ilahi(1582) →\nTansen guru=Muhammad Ghaus, Nur Jahan=Mehrunnisa → Guru Arjan Dev-Jahangir, Guru Tegh Bahadur-Aurangzeb\n→ Kohinoor: Kakatiya-MalikKafur(1309)-Jumla gift(1636)-NadirShah loot → Dagh/Huliya: Alauddin(original)-\nSherShah(revive)-Akbar(use)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye SABSE ZYADA weightage wala chapter hai, isko sabse zyada baar dohrao.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Guru Arjan Dev=Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur=Aurangzeb ne execute kiya — swap mat karo.\n2) Purana Qila = Sher Shah Suri ne banaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah todkar), Humayun ne khud nahi.\n3) Ain-i-Dahsala=Todar Mal(revenue system). Ain-i-Akbari=Abul Fazl(Akbarnama ka part) — dono alag.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Mughal Empire (Highest Weightage)"," PROVINCIAL DYNASTIES — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 5 Provinces — Bengal Sabse Pehla Azad\n●Bengal(1338CE) = Delhi se PEHLA azad province — Jaunpur/Malwa/Kashmir/Gujarat sab BAAD mein\n●Order: Bengal(1338) → Malwa(1401) → Gujarat(1407) → Jaunpur, Kashmir\n TRICK — \"Bengal = No.1\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Bengal Bola Bye-bye sabse pehle\" — B se shuru hone wala hi sabse pehle azad hua (1338), coincidence\nnahi, bas is wordplay se lock kar do.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBengal(1338 CE) = Delhi se sabse pehle azad hone wala province — Jaunpur ya Malwa NAHI.\n2. Key Nicknames — Direct Match\n●Shiraz of India = Jaunpur (sheher)\n●Akbar of Kashmir / Budshah = Zain-ul-Abidin\n●Siraj-e-Hind = Ibrahim Shah Sharqi\n●Malik-us-Sharq(Eastern ruler) = Malik Sarwar\n●Begada = Mahmud Begada(Gujarat, 2-forts)\n TRICK — \"Nickname list\" chain trick\n💡\nEk line mein sab: \"Jaunpur=Shiraz, Zain-ul-Abidin=Akbar-of-Kashmir/Budshah, Ibrahim=Siraj-e-Hind,\nSarwar=Malik-us-Sharq, Mahmud=Begada\" — bas ye 5 pairs bolke ratt lo, sab direct-match questions ban jaate hain.\n3. Jaunpur — Founded By vs Named After\n●City founded by = Firoz Shah Tughlaq\n●Naam rakha gaya = Muhammad bin Tughlaq(Jauna Khan) ke naam par — \"Jaunpur\" = \"Jauna+pur\"\n TRICK — \"Banane wala alag, naam wala alag\" trick\n💡\nJaise koi bacha ho jiska naam dada ke naam pe rakha jaaye, par paalne wala koi aur ho — Firoz Shah ne SHEHAR\nbanaya(palan-poshan), naam Muhammad bin Tughlaq(Jauna Khan) ka diya(tribute) — dono Tughlaq hi hain par\nrole alag: builder vs namesake.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJaunpur city founded by Firoz Shah Tughlaq, LEKIN naam Muhammad bin Tughlaq (Jauna Khan) ke naam par rakha\ngaya — dono alag roles hain.\n4. 3 Famous Mosques — Builder Match\n●Adina Mosque(Bengal) = Sikandar Shah(Bengal ka raja)\n●Atala Mosque(1408)(Jaunpur) = Ibrahim Shah Sharqi\n●Jama Masjid Jaunpur(1470) = Hussain Shah Sharqi\n TRICK — \"Alag province, alag raja\" trick\n💡\n3 mosques, 3 alag province/raja combos — Adina=Bengal(Sikandar), Atala=Jaunpur early(Ibrahim,1408), Jama\nMasjid Jaunpur=Jaunpur later(Hussain,1470) — Jaunpur ki 2 mosques ko bhi date se yaad rakho:\n1408(pehla,Ibrahim) → 1470(baad mein,Hussain)."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAdina Mosque(Bengal)=Sikandar Shah. Atala Mosque(Jaunpur,1408)=Ibrahim Shah Sharqi. Jama Masjid\nJaunpur(1470)=Hussain Shah Sharqi — 3 alag builders.\n5. Kashmir — Sikandar Shah vs Zain-ul-Abidin\n●Sikandar Shah(Butshikan) = Sati BAN kiya · Max forced Hindu conversions · orthodox\n●Zain-ul-Abidin(Budshah) = Sati ban REVOKE kiya · Jizya+cow-slaughter BAN · \"Akbar of Kashmir\" · liberal\n TRICK — \"Sikandar=Ban, Zain=Un-ban\" trick\n💡\nEk raja ne rule LAGAYA, doosre ne WAPAS HATA diya — \"Sikandar Sakht(orthodox), Zain Zyada-liberal\" —\ndono naam ke pehle letter se hi personality yaad rakho: Sikandar=Sakht, Zain=Zyada-tolerant.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSikandar Shah(Butshikan) = Sati BAN kiya (orthodox). Zain-ul-Abidin = Sati ban REVOKE kiya (liberal, 'Akbar of\nKashmir') — opposite actions, confuse mat karo.\n6. Gujarat — Founder vs Real Founder (Gupta/Mughal Jaisa Pattern)\n●Zafar Khan(Muzzafar Shah I) = Founder(1407)\n●Ahmed Shah = REAL Founder(1411) → Ahmedabad(1413) basayi — Zafar Khan ne NAHI\n TRICK — \"3rd repeat of same pattern\" trick\n💡\nYe pattern ab 3rd baar dekh rahe ho: Gupta(Shri Gupta/Chandragupta I), Mughal(Babur/Akbar), aur ab Gujarat(Zafar\nKhan/Ahmed Shah) — jab bhi \"founder vs real founder\" sawaal aaye, dusra naam wala hamesha city/stability laata hai.\nAhmed Shah = Ahmedabad — naam mein hi seedha match hai (Ahmed-Ahmedabad), yaad rakhna sabse easy hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nZafar Khan(Muzzafar Shah I) = Founder(1407). Ahmed Shah = Real Founder(1411) — Ahmedabad usne basayi, Zafar\nKhan ne nahi.\n7. Mahmud Begada — \"Be\" Matlab Do\n●2 forts jeete: Girnar Durg(1466) + Champaner Durg(1486) → isliye title \"Begada\"(\"Be\"=do)\n TRICK — \"Be=2\" trick\n💡\nBegada mein \"Be\" khud Persian/Urdu mein \"do\" ka matlab deta hai — 2 forts jeetne se ye title mila, EK fort se nahi.\nYaad rakho: \"Be-gada = 2-gada(fort)\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahmud Begada ka title 2 FORTS jeetne se mila (Girnar+Champaner), ek fort se nahi — \"Be\" ka matlab \"do\" hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Bengal(1338,first) → Nicknames: Jaunpur-Shiraz, ZainulAbidin-Akbar of Kashmir/Budshah, Ibrahim-Siraj-e-Hind,\nSarwar-Malik-us-Sharq, Mahmud-Begada → Jaunpur: Firoz Shah founded, named after Jauna Khan(Md bin Tughlaq)\n→ Mosques: Adina(Bengal-Sikandar), Atala(1408-Ibrahim), JamaMasjid(1470-Hussain) → Kashmir: Sikandar-Sati ban,\nZain-Sati unban(liberal) → Gujarat: ZafarKhan(founder)-AhmedShah(real founder,Ahmedabad) → Begada: 2\nforts(Girnar+Champaner)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo."," Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bengal(1338) = Delhi se pehla azad province — Jaunpur/Malwa nahi.\n2) Kashmir: Sikandar Shah=Sati BAN kiya. Zain-ul-Abidin=Sati ban REVOKE kiya (opposite).\n3) Gujarat: Zafar Khan=Founder(1407). Ahmed Shah=Real Founder(1411,Ahmedabad basayi).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Provincial Dynasties"," LATER MUGHAL PERIOD — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 7 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Rulers Ke Nicknames — Weak Successors\n●Bahadur Shah I = Shah-e-Bekhbar(Unaware King)\n●Jahandar Shah = Lampat Moorkh, Laparwah\n●Farrukhsiyar = Ghranit Kayar(Notorious Coward)\n●Muhammad Shah = Rangila Badshah — sirf positive-sounding naam, par unke time Nadir Shah invasion hua\n TRICK — \"Sab weak, ek 'positive' lekin disaster\" trick\n💡\nSab nicknames NEGATIVE hain(Bekhbar-unaware, Moorkh-foolish, Kayar-coward) — SIRF Rangila\nBadshah(Muhammad Shah) positive lagta hai, par yehi wo raja hai jiske time Nadir Shah ne Delhi loot li — \"positive\nnaam wale ke time hi sabse bada disaster hua\", ye irony yaad rakho.\n2. Jizya Tax — On-Off-Off Pattern\n●Jahandar Shah → Jizya ABOLISH\n●Farrukhsiyar → Jizya RESTORE\n●Muhammad Shah(1720) → Jizya FINALLY abolish (permanent)\n TRICK — \"Off-On-Off\" trick\n💡\nSequence: Off(Jahandar) → On(Farrukhsiyar) → Off-Permanent(Muhammad Shah). \"Finally abolished\" ka\nanswer HAMESHA Muhammad Shah hai — koi aur nahi, ye directly poocha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Jizya finally/permanently abolished\" = Muhammad Shah (1720). Jahandar Shah=abolish(pehli baar),\nFarrukhsiyar=restore — teeno alag actions.\n3. Sayyid Brothers — Kingmakers\n●Sayyid Brothers = Kingmakers(Khargonebar) · 1713-1720 CE administration control\n●Farrukhsiyar ko power diya, baad mein khud hi hataya bhi\n TRICK — \"Banaya aur bigada dono\" trick\n💡\nKingmakers naam khud bata deta hai — \"king BANANE\" wale, par yaad rakho wahi Farrukhsiyar ko baad mein\nhataya bhi — \"jisne banaya, usi ne bigada\" — makers hi breakers bhi ban gaye.\n4. Nadir Shah Invasion(1739) — DONO Liye\n●Battle of Karnal(1739) → Muhammad Shah haare\n●Nadir Shah le gaye: Peacock Throne(Takht-e-Taus) AUR Kohinoor Diamond — dono, sirf ek nahi\n TRICK — \"2 cheezein, ek nahi\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log sochte hain sirf ek cheez li — NAHI, DONO li: Peacock Throne + Kohinoor. Yaad rakho: \"Nadir\nne Nadir(rare) do cheezein churayi\" — dono precious items ek saath gaye, is completeness ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNadir Shah(1739, Battle of Karnal) ne Peacock Throne AUR Kohinoor Diamond DONO liye, sirf ek nahi."," 5. Battle of Buxar(1764) vs Battle of Plassey(1757)\n●Buxar(1764): Shah Alam II + Shuja-ud-Daula(Awadh) + Mir Qasim(Bengal) vs British(Hector Munro) — British jeete\n●Plassey(1757): Siraj-ud-Daula vs Clive — alag battle, alag commander\n TRICK — \"3-vs-1 Buxar, 1-vs-1 Plassey\" trick\n💡\nBuxar = 3-party alliance(Emperor+2 Nawabs) vs British — bada coalition. Plassey = sirf 1 Nawab(Siraj) vs Clive —\nchota, single battle. \"Buxar mein Bahut saare log the(3), Plassey mein Plain/simple(1 vs 1)\" — B for Buxar-\nBahut(many), P for Plassey-Plain(simple).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBattle of Buxar(1764) = Shah Alam II+Shuja-ud-Daula+Mir Qasim vs Hector Munro. Battle of Plassey(1757) = Siraj-\nud-Daula vs Clive — dono alag battles, alag commanders, mix mat karo.\n6. Treaty of Allahabad(1765) — Diwani Rights\n●Robert Clive(EIC representative) · EIC ko Bengal+Bihar+Orissa ki Diwani(revenue collection) rights mili\n●Shah Alam II ko English se pension mili\n TRICK — \"Diwani ≠ Direct rule\" trick\n💡\nDiwani = sirf revenue-collection ka adhikaar, DIRECT political control NAHI (shuru mein) — ye British power ka\n\"pehla kadam\" tha, poora control nahi. Yaad rakho: \"paisa collect karne ka haq mila, raaj karne ka nahi — abhi\".\n7. Bahadur Shah II(Zafar) — Aakhri Mughal\n●Revolt of 1857 ke soldiers ka symbolic leader · British ne arrest kiya\n●Death: Rangoon(Myanmar), 1862CE — Delhi/Agra mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Zafar = Door tak gaya\" trick\n💡\nZafar ko India se bahut door(Rangoon,Myanmar) exile kiya gaya — \"jitna bada raaj, utna door exile\" — ye final irony\nyaad rakho: Mughal Empire jo kabhi poore India pe raaj karta tha, uska aakhri raja Bharat ke bahar hi mara.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahadur Shah II(Zafar) ki death Rangoon(Myanmar) mein hui, 1862 CE mein — Delhi ya Agra mein NAHI.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Jajau(1707)-BahadurShahI wins → Nicknames: Bekhbar-Moorkh-Kayar-Rangila(sab weak) → Jizya: Off(Jahandar)-\nOn(Farrukhsiyar)-Off-Permanent(MdShah1720) → Sayyid Brothers=Kingmakers →\nNadirShah(1739,Karnal)=PeacockThrone+Kohinoor(dono) → Buxar(1764,3-vs-1,HectorMunro) vs Plassey(1757,1-\nvs-1,Clive) → Treaty of Allahabad(1765,Clive,Diwani-Bengal/Bihar/Orissa) → BahadurShahII(Zafar)=Rangoon\ndeath(1862)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Jizya finally/permanently abolished = Muhammad Shah (1720), na ki Jahandar Shah.\n2) Buxar(1764,3-party alliance,Hector Munro) ≠ Plassey(1757,Siraj-ud-Daula,Clive).\n3) Nadir Shah ne Peacock Throne AUR Kohinoor DONO liye. Bahadur Shah II ki death Rangoon mein hui."," Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Later Mughal Period"," RISE OF MARATHA POWER — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 8 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Shivaji — 2 Coronations, Ek Saal\n●1st Coronation: 6 June 1674 · 2nd Coronation: 24 September 1674 — dono 1674 mein hi\n●Perform ki Gaga Bhatta(Kashi scholar) ne · Guru: Ramdas(Bhakti-Sufi chapter se yaad karo, Samarth Sect founder)\n TRICK — \"2 Coronation, 1 Saal, 3 Mahine Gap\" trick\n💡\nJune aur September — dono 1674 mein, beech mein 3 mahine ka gap(July,Aug beech mein) — ek hi saal ke andar do\nbaar taj pehna, unique fact hai isliye alag se yaad rakho: \"pehli baar June mein, dobara confirm karne September mein\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nShivaji ki coronation DO baar hui — 6 June 1674 aur 24 September 1674, dono SAME YEAR(1674) mein, alag mahino\nmein.\n2. Chauth vs Sardeshmukhi — Fraction Ka Trap\n●Chauth = 1/4(25%) — neighbouring states se, non-aggression ke badle\n●Sardeshmukhi = 1/10(10%) — tribute, Sardeshmukhs dwara\n TRICK — \"Chau=4, Sar-Das=10\" trick\n💡\nChauth mein khud \"Chau\"(=4) hai — 1/4. Sardeshmukhi mein \"Das\"(10) chhupa hua nahi hai literally, par yaad\nrakho: \"Sardeshmukhi = Sar+Desh(pura desh ka daswaan hissa)\" — bada naam wali tax, CHOTI percentage(10%);\nchota naam wali tax(Chauth), BADI percentage(25%) — ulta pattern se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChauth = 1/4(25%). Sardeshmukhi = 1/10(10%). Dono alag taxes hain — Chauth non-aggression ke liye, Sardeshmukhi\ntribute ke roop mein.\n3. \"Magna Carta of Marathas\" — Kaunsi Treaty?\n●Magna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty(Balaji Vishwanath + Sayyid Brothers) — Treaty of Purandar NAHI\n TRICK — \"Delhi = Magna Carta\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Treaty of Purandar ko Magna Carta samajh lete hain (kyunki wo bhi famous hai) — GALAT. Yaad\nrakho: \"Delhi mein Balaji Vishwanath ne Sayyid Brothers se badi deal ki, isliye Delhi hi Magna Carta hai\" — Purandar\nShivaji ke time ki hai(purani), Magna Carta baad ki(Peshwa era) hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMagna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty (Balaji Vishwanath + Sayyid Brothers), NOT Treaty of Purandar.\n4. 2 Treaty of Purandar — Naam Same, Century Alag\n●Purandar 1665: Jai Singh(Mughal) + Shivaji — 23/35 forts diye\n●Purandar 1776: Madhavrao Narayan + British\n TRICK — \"1665=Mughal era, 1776=British era\" trick\n💡\nSame naam, 111 saal ka gap! 1665 = Mughal ke saath(Shivaji ka time), 1776 = British ke saath(Peshwa ka time) —\nbas century dekh ke identify karo: 17th century=Mughal, 18th century=British.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠"," 2 alag \"Treaty of Purandar\" hain: 1665(Jai Singh+Shivaji, Mughal-Maratha) aur 1776(Madhavrao Narayan+British) —\nnaam same, 111 saal ka gap.\n5. Peshwa — Minister Se Supreme Power Tak\n●Ashtapradhan mein Peshwa = sirf 1 minister(PM jaisa)\n●Balaji Baji Rao ke time Peshwa office HEREDITARY ban gaya → Chhatrapati sirf symbolic reh gaye\n●Baji Rao I = \"Fighting Peshwa\", Maratha Confederacy ke founder\n TRICK — \"Minister → Supreme\" evolution trick\n💡\nPeshwa ka safar: shuru mein 1-of-8 minister → dheere-dheere supreme power → hereditary(Balaji Baji Rao) —\n\"chota role bada ban gaya\", jaise koi employee CEO ban jaaye apni hi company mein.\nBaji Rao I = Founder of Maratha Confederacy — pehla Peshwa jisne ise sach mein empire jaisa banaya, isliye\n\"Fighting\" nickname bhi mila.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPeshwa Ashtapradhan mein sirf 1 minister tha, par Balaji Baji Rao ke time HEREDITARY ho gaya aur Chhatrapati\npuppet ban gaye.\n6. 4 Maratha Clans — Direct Match\n●Holkar-Indore · Scindia-Gwalior · Gaekwad-Baroda · Bhonsle-Nagpur\n TRICK — \"HSGB\" clan-city trick\n💡\nHolkar-Indore, Scindia-Gwalior, Gaekwad-Baroda, Bhonsle-Nagpur = \"HSGB\" — koi bhi silly sentence bana lo letters\nse, jaise \"Hathi Se Gaya Baazar\".\n7. 3 Anglo-Maratha Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1775-82) = Warren Hastings → Treaty of Salbai\n●2nd(1803-05) = Lord Wellesley → Treaty of Bassein/Deogaon/Surji-Anjangaon\n●3rd(1817-18) = Lord Hastings → Treaty of Poona/Mandasor\n TRICK — \"Warren≠Lord Hastings\" trick\n💡\nWarren Hastings(1st war) aur Lord Hastings(3rd war) — naam mein \"Hastings\" common hai par bilkul ALAG log\nhain, alag wars mein — \"pehla Warren, teesra Lord\" — first-letter se distinguish karo (W for 1st/War-one, L for\nLast/3rd).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nWarren Hastings(1st Anglo-Maratha War) aur Lord Hastings(3rd Anglo-Maratha War) — do ALAG log hain, naam\nsimilar hone se confuse mat karo.\n8. 3rd Battle of Panipat(1761)\n●14 Jan 1761 → Ahmad Shah Abdali(Afghanistan) ne Marathas(Balaji Baji Rao ki forces) ko haraya\n●Mughals ke against NAHI thi ye battle — Abdali ke against\n TRICK — \"3rd Panipat = Marathas vs Abdali\" trick\n💡\nTeeno Panipat battles alag opponents: 1st(1526)=Babur vs Ibrahim Lodi, 2nd(1556)=Akbar vs Hemu,\n3rd(1761)=Abdali vs MARATHAS(Mughals nahi) — 3rd mein Mughal khud involved nahi tha, Marathas the naye\nplayers."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n3rd Battle of Panipat(1761) = Ahmad Shah Abdali vs MARATHAS (Mughals ke against nahi) — Balaji Baji Rao\nPeshwa the us waqt.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Shivaji: 2 coronations(June+Sept 1674), Guru=Ramdas → Chauth(1/4) vs Sardeshmukhi(1/10) → Magna Carta=Delhi\nTreaty(Balaji Vishwanath+SayyidBros), NOT Purandar → 2 Purandar Treaties(1665-Mughal,1776-British) → Peshwa:\nminister→hereditary(BalajiBajiRao) → BajiRaoI=Fighting Peshwa,founder → 4 clans: HSGB(Holkar-Indore,Scindia-\nGwalior,Gaekwad-Baroda,Bhonsle-Nagpur) → 3 wars: WarrenHastings(1st)-Wellesley(2nd)-LordHastings(3rd) →\n3rdPanipat(1761)=Abdali vs Marathas\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Magna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty (Balaji Vishwanath+Sayyid Brothers), NOT Treaty of Purandar.\n2) 2 alag Treaty of Purandar: 1665(Mughal-Shivaji) vs 1776(British-Madhavrao).\n3) Warren Hastings(1st war) ≠ Lord Hastings(3rd war) — do alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Rise of Maratha Power"," RISE OF THE SIKHS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 9 (Final Chapter) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Gurmukhi Script — Guru Nanak Ne NAHI\n●Guru Nanak(1st) = Sikhism founder, Sangat+Langar sthapit ki\n●Guru Angad Dev(2nd) = Gurmukhi script shuru ki + Langar regularise\n TRICK — \"Founder≠Script-maker\" trick\n💡\nNanak ne DHARM banaya, Angad ne SCRIPT banayi — founder aur script-creator do alag log hain, jaise koi\ncompany banane wala aur uska logo design karne wala alag ho sakta hai. \"Angad = Anokhi likhawat(Gurmukhi)\" —\ndono \"An\" sound se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGurmukhi script = Guru Angad Dev(2nd Guru) ne shuru ki — Guru Nanak ne NAHI (unhone sirf Sikhism found ki).\n2. Amritsar City vs Harmandir Sahib — Baap-Beta\n●Amritsar SHEHER = Guru Ram Das(4th Guru) ne basaya\n●Harmandir Sahib(Golden Temple) = Guru Arjan Dev(5th Guru, Ram Das ka beta) ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Baap-Sheher, Beta-Temple\" trick\n💡\nRam Das(baap) ne ZAMEEN(sheher) di, Arjan Dev(beta) ne usi zameen pe MANDIR banaya — ek generation ne\nfoundation rakha, agli generation ne usko poora kiya, jaise ghar-parivaar mein hota hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmritsar city = Guru Ram Das(4th). Harmandir Sahib/Golden Temple = Guru Arjan Dev(5th, Ram Das ka beta) — city\naur temple ke founders ALAG hain.\n3. 2 Guru Executions — Jahangir vs Aurangzeb\n●Guru Arjan Dev(5th) → JAHANGIR ne execute kiya(1606CE, Khusrau revolt support)\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) → AURANGZEB ne execute kiya(Islam accept karne se mana kiya)\n TRICK — \"5th-Jahangir, 9th-Aurangzeb\" cross-chapter trick\n💡\nYe EXACT SAME fact Mughal Empire chapter mein bhi tha — 5th Guru(pehle) = Jahangir(pehle raja), 9th\nGuru(baad mein) = Aurangzeb(baad ka raja) — timeline dono jagah match karti hai, cross-verify karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Arjan Dev(5th) = Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) = Aurangzeb ne execute kiya — number se\nraja match karo, swap mat karo.\n4. Sirf Ek Elected Guru\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) = SIRF ELECTED Guru — baaki sab hereditary/appointed\n●Guru position hereditary Guru Ram Das(4th) se ban gayi thi\n TRICK — \"9th=akela election\" trick\n💡\n10 mein se sirf 1(9th) elected tha — baaki sab family/appointment se aaye. \"Tegh Bahadur = Thoda Alag(unique\nelection)\" — is uniqueness ko yaad rakho, ye common exam pick hai."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Tegh Bahadur(9th) hi SIRF ELECTED Sikh Guru the — Guru Ram Das(4th) ne position hereditary bana di thi.\n5. Khalsa Panth(1699) vs Dal Khalsa(1748)\n●Khalsa Panth(1699) = Guru Gobind Singh(10th) → religious brotherhood\n●Dal Khalsa(1748) = Kapoor Singh(Jassa Singh Ahluwalia ke under) → military-political confederation, 12 Misls mein\nbata\n TRICK — \"Panth=Dharam, Dal=Fauj\" trick\n💡\nKhalsa PANTH = \"panth\" matlab dharmik samuday (religious group) — Guru Gobind Singh ne banaya. DAL Khalsa\n= \"dal\" matlab sena/army (Dal-Sena jaisa sound) — baad mein banaya political-military confederation — naam mein hi\n\"religious vs military\" ka farak chhupa hai.\n49 saal ka gap(1699→1748) — ek generation baad, dharmik samuday se military confederation tak ka safar.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKhalsa Panth(1699,Guru Gobind Singh)=religious brotherhood. Dal Khalsa(1748,Kapoor Singh)=military-political\nconfederation, 12 Misls mein bata — dono alag cheezein.\n6. 2 \"Treaty of Amritsar\" — Year Se Pehchano\n●1809 CE = Ranjit Singh + Charles Metcalfe → Sutlej boundary fix, British supremacy(south of Sutlej) accept ki\n●1849 CE(2nd Anglo-Sikh War end) = British ne Kohinoor liya, Duleep Singh pensioner ban gaye\n TRICK — \"1809=Boundary, 1849=Kohinoor\" trick\n💡\n40 saal ka gap: 1809 = Ranjit Singh KHUD zinda tha, boundary-deal(peaceful). 1849 = Ranjit Singh ki maut ke\nbaad(1839), empire kamzor, Kohinoor bhi gaya — \"pehle deal, baad mein sab kuch gaya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTreaty of Amritsar(1809)=Ranjit Singh+Metcalfe, Sutlej boundary. Treaty of Amritsar(1849, alag context)=2nd Anglo-\nSikh War end, Kohinoor liya — year se identify karo.\n7. 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1845-46) = Lord Hardinge → Treaty of Lahore(1846)\n●2nd(1848-49) = Lord Dalhousie → Kohinoor liya, Duleep Singh pension\n TRICK — \"Hardinge-Lahore, Dalhousie-Kohinoor\" trick\n💡\nHardinge(1st) → Lahore treaty. Dalhousie(2nd) → Kohinoor — dono pairs alphabetically bhi roughly match: H-before-\nD(1st-before-2nd), L-before-K nahi but bas number-order se yaad rakho: 1st Governor-General ne treaty ki, 2nd wale ne\ndiamond liya.\n8. Panj Kakar (5 K's) & Ranjit Singh\n●5 K's: Kesh · Kangha · Kara · Kachha · Kirpan\n●Ranjit Singh: Sukerchakia Misl · pita Maha Singh · 12 saal mein Misl chief bane · Lahore(1799,political capital) →\nAmritsar(1802,cultural capital)\n TRICK — \"5K + Ranjit's 2 capitals\" trick\n💡\n5 K's sab \"K\" se shuru hote hain — bas ginti yaad rakho: 5 K's. Lahore=Political(pehle liya,1799),\nAmritsar=Cultural(baad mein,1802) — political power pehle, cultural/religious center baad mein aaya."," Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Nanak(founder)→Angad(Gurmukhi)→AmarDas→RamDas(Amritsar city,hereditary)→ArjanDev(Harmandir\nSahib,Jahangir executed) → Hargobind(AkalTakht)→HarRai→Harkrishan(youngest)→TeghBahadur(ONLY\nelected,Aurangzeb executed)→GobindSingh(KhalsaPanth1699,5K's,last Guru) → BandaBahadur(1st political\nleader,Farrukhsiyar executed) → DalKhalsa(1748,KapoorSingh) → RanjitSingh(Sukerchakia,Lahore+Amritsar) →\nTreatyofAmritsar1809(Metcalfe,Sutlej) → 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars: Hardinge(1st,Lahore treaty)-Dalhousie(2nd,Kohinoor)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye Medieval History set ka LAST chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Gurmukhi = Guru Angad Dev(2nd), NOT Guru Nanak.\n2) Amritsar city=Guru Ram Das(4th). Harmandir Sahib=Guru Arjan Dev(5th) — do alag Gurus.\n3) Khalsa Panth(1699,Guru Gobind Singh)≠Dal Khalsa(1748,Kapoor Singh) — dharmik vs military-political.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Rise of the Sikhs (Final Chapter)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0443","t":"03 Modern History Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / History / Modern History","x":[" ARRIVAL OF EUROPEAN COMPANIES IN INDIA — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Establishment vs Factory-in-India — SABSE BADA TRAP\n●Europe mein establish: Portuguese(1498) → English(1600) → Dutch(1602) → Danish(1616) → French(1664) →\nSwedish(1731)\n●India mein pehli factory: Portuguese(1503) → Dutch(1605) → English(1613) → Danish(1620) → French(1668)\n TRICK — \"Dutch baad mein bane, PEHLE factory lagayi\" trick\n💡\nDutch(VOC) English se 2 saal BAAD company bani(1602 vs 1600 English), lekin India mein factory 8 saal PEHLE\nlagayi(1605 vs 1613 English) — \"der se aaye, jaldi laga li dukaan\" — is ulta-pattern ko ek line mein yaad rakho, ye\npoore chapter ka SABSE common trap hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDutch VOC(1602) English EIC(1600) ke BAAD bani Europe mein, LEKIN India mein Dutch factory(1605) English\nfactory(1613) se PEHLE lagi — establishment-date aur factory-date do alag timelines hain.\n2. Portuguese — State Power, Company NAHI\n●Portuguese = State power(Portugal desh khud involve) — baaki sab(EIC,VOC,French,Danish) = formal TRADING\nCOMPANIES\n●\"1498\" = sirf arrival date, koi company-formation date nahi\n TRICK — \"Akela State\" trick\n💡\n5 mein se sirf Portuguese State hai, baaki 4 Companies hain — \"Portuguese = Pora desh(poora country) khud aaya\"\n— is akele-alag-hone wale fact ko yaad rakho, exam isi angle se pakadta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPortuguese ek STATE POWER tha, koi trading company nahi. 1498 = sirf arrival date, company-formation date NAHI\n(kyunki company thi hi nahi).\n3. Houtman — India NAHI, Indonesia Gaya\n●Houtman(1596) = Dutch traveler → Indonesia(Sumatra) gaya, India NAHI\n TRICK — \"Houtman = Indonesia\" trick\n💡\nHoutman — \"Hout\" jaisa sound \"Out(bahar/door)\" se milta hai — \"Out-of-India, Indonesia gaya\" — ye ek word-play\nse hi yaad rah jaata hai ki Houtman India nahi gaya tha.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHoutman(1596) Indonesia(Sumatra) gaya tha, India NAHI — chapter ka sabse zyada confuse karne wala naam.\n4. \"1st Factory\" — Context Pe Depend Karta Hai\n●Overall 1st European factory in India = Portuguese, Cochin(1503)\n●English 1st TEMPORARY factory = Masulipatnam(1611, South India)\n●English 1st PERMANENT factory = Surat(1613, Director Thomas Aldworth)\n TRICK — \"3 alag \\\"1st factory\\\" answers\" trick\n💡"," Sawaal ka wording padho: \"India ki PEHLI factory\" → Cochin(Portuguese,1503). \"English ki pehli TEMPORARY\"\n→ Masulipatnam(1611). \"English ki pehli PERMANENT\" → Surat(1613). Teeno alag\nqualifiers(overall/temporary/permanent) — teen alag jawab.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"1st factory in India\" ka jawab wording pe depend karta hai: Overall=Cochin(Portuguese,1503). English\ntemporary=Masulipatnam(1611). English permanent=Surat(1613,Aldworth).\n5. Vasco da Gama — 3 Trips\n●1st(May 1498): Calicut → Zamorin(local raja) se mile\n●2nd(1502): Re-arrival\n●3rd(1524): Cochin mein guzar gaye(death)\n TRICK — \"Aaya-Aaya-Mar gaya\" trick\n💡\n3 trips ka pattern: 1st=arrival(khushi), 2nd=re-arrival(routine), 3rd=death(end) — \"pehli baar naya desh dekha,\ndoosri baar dobara aaya, teesri baar wahin mar gaya\" — ek life-story jaisi teen-step chain.\n6. Portuguese 3 Governors — Alag-Alag Kaam\n●Almeida(1505-09) = 1st Governor · Blue Water Policy(sea control) · Cartaz System(sea-pass)\n●Albuquerque(1509-15) = REAL founder of Portuguese power · Goa capture(1510) · Sati discourage\n●Nino da Cunha(1529-38) = Bassein(1534)+Diu(1535) capture · HQ Cochin→Goa shift\n TRICK — \"Almeida=Policy, Albuquerque=Founder, Cunha=HQ-shift\" trick\n💡\nAlmeida = \"Alag/pehla policy-maker\"(Blue Water+Cartaz). Albuquerque = \"Alpha/asli founder\"(dono naam \"Al\" se\nshuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai — par Albuquerque hi REAL founder hai, Goa bhi usi ne liya). Cunha = \"naya\nHQ laya\"(Goa) — 3 alag roles, 3 alag governors.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBlue Water Policy = Almeida ki (Albuquerque ki NAHI). Albuquerque = Portuguese power ke REAL founder,\nGoa(1510) usne capture kiya.\n7. French — 3 Carnatic Wars, Teeno Mein Haare\n●3 Carnatic Wars(1746-1763) vs British → French TEENO mein haare\n●Pondicherry(1674) = Sher Khan Lodi se mila → French ka main base\n●Surat(1668) = French ki 1st factory, founder Francis Caron\n TRICK — \"3-0 loss\" trick\n💡\nFrench ka Carnatic Wars record = 0 jeet, 3 haar — \"French = Fail teeno baar\" — F se F, French aur Fail dono match\nkarte hain, is simple hook se count(3) aur result(haar) dono yaad reh jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFrench vs British = 3 Carnatic Wars(1746-1763) — French TEENO mein haare. Count kabhi 2 ya 4 mat karna, exact 3\nhai.\n8. Danish Exit vs Dutch Exit — Bilkul Alag Style\n●Dutch → Battle of Bedara/Biderra(1759) mein British se HAARE → exit\n●Danish → Battle mein NAHI haare → 1845 mein factories British ko BECH DI(peacefully)"," TRICK — \"Haara vs Becha\" trick\n💡\nDutch = Lada aur Haara(Bedara, 1759). Danish = Bina lade Becha(1845, peaceful sale) — \"Dutch Defeated(war),\nDanish Deal(sale)\" — dono \"D\" se shuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai, par ek WAR se gaya, doosra SALE se gaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDutch = Battle of Bedara(1759) mein HAARE(defeat se exit). Danish = 1845 mein factories British ko BECH DI (battle\nmein nahi haare) — dono ka exit-style bilkul alag hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Establish order: Portuguese(1498)-English(1600)-Dutch(1602)-Danish(1616)-French(1664)-Swedish(1731) → Factory\norder: Portuguese(1503,Cochin)-Dutch(1605)-English(1613,Surat)-Danish(1620)-French(1668) → Dutch:baad-mein-\nbana,pehle-factory → Portuguese=State not Company → Houtman=Indonesia not India → VascoDaGama:\nCalicut(1498)-rearrival(1502)-death(1524,Cochin) → Governors: Almeida(BlueWater,Cartaz)-Albuquerque(real\nfounder,Goa1510)-Cunha(HQ shift Goa) → French: 3 Carnatic Wars,3 haar,Pondicherry(1674) →\nDutch=haare(Bedara1759) vs Danish=becha(1845)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Dutch(1602) English(1600) ke baad bane, par Dutch factory(1605) English factory(1613) se pehle lagi.\n2) Houtman(1596) Indonesia gaya tha, India NAHI.\n3) Dutch=battle mein haare(Bedara,1759). Danish=battle mein nahi haare, factories BECH di(1845).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.1 European Companies in India"," BRITISH EXPANSION IN INDIAN TERRITORIES — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 2 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Presidencies — 3 Alag Tareeke Se Mili\n●Madras(1639) = LEASE(Francis Day, King of Chandragiri se) → Fort St. George\n●Bombay(1661) = DOWRY(Charles II ki shaadi, Catherine of Braganza se) — Conquest NAHI!\n●Calcutta(1698) = ZAMINDARI RIGHTS KHAREEDI(3 gaon: Sutanuti,Kalikata,Govindpur) → Fort William\n TRICK — \"Lease-Dowry-Kharidi\" trick\n💡\n3 alag \"kaise mila\" answers: Madras=LEASE(kiraya), Bombay=DOWRY(shaadi ka tohfa), Calcutta=BUY(zameen\nkhareedi) — teeno bilkul alag tareeke, ek bhi \"jung/conquest\" se NAHI mila. \"Bombay to shaadi mein mila, ladai\nmein nahi\" — ye SABSE common trap hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBombay CONQUEST mein nahi, DOWRY mein mila (1661, Charles II ki shaadi Catherine of Braganza se) — ye\nchapter ka sabse famous trap hai.\n2. Plassey(1757) vs Buxar(1764) — Commander Trap\n●Plassey(23 June 1757) = Robert Clive vs Siraj-ud-Daulah → Mir Jafar ne betray kiya\n●Buxar(22 Oct 1764) = Hector Munro vs 3-alliance(Mir Qasim+Shuja-ud-Daulah+Shah Alam II)\n TRICK — \"Clive=Plassey, Munro=Buxar\" trick\n💡\n7 saal ka gap(1757→1764), aur commander bhi badal gaya: Clive PEHLE(Plassey), Munro BAAD mein(Buxar) —\n\"Clive Chota war jeeta pehle(1 opponent-Siraj), Munro Mushkil war jeeta baad mein(3 opponents combined)\" — jitna\nbada alliance utna naya commander.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPlassey(1757)=Robert Clive. Buxar(1764)=Hector Munro — Robert Clive ko Buxar mein mat dena, ye sabse common\nexam trap hai.\n3. Black Hole Tragedy(1756) — Holwell Ka Version Use Karo\n●Holwell claim(exam mein yehi use hota): 146 imprisoned, 23 survive\n●Modern historians estimate ALAG hai(~64 imprisoned,~43 died) — par BPSC/BSSC mein Holwell ke figures hi\ncorrect maane jaate hain\n TRICK — \"Exam=Holwell, Reality=Alag\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Holwell ka Hi number chalega exam mein\" — 146/23 — chahe historians disagree karte hon, EXAM\nCONTEXT mein hamesha Holwell ka version sahi jawab hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBlack Hole Tragedy: Holwell ka version(146 imprisoned, 23 survive) exam mein use hota hai — modern\nestimate(~64/~43) NAHI, chahe wo zyada accurate ho.\n4. Mir Jafar — 2 BAAR Nawab\n●Mir Jafar(1757-1760) → Mir Qasim(1760-1763) → Mir Jafar WAPAS(1763-1765)"," TRICK — \"Jafar-Qasim-Jafar\" sandwich trick\n💡\nEk \"sandwich\" pattern: Jafar(bread)-Qasim(filling)-Jafar(bread) — Mir Qasim BEECH mein aaya, Jafar dono\ntaraf(shuru+ant) — \"J-Q-J\" bolke yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMir Jafar DO BAAR Nawab tha: 1757-60 aur phir 1763-65. Beech mein Mir Qasim(1760-63) tha — sequence: Jafar-\nQasim-Jafar.\n5. 3 Carnatic Wars — Treaty Match\n●1st(1746-48) → Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle — status quo\n●2nd(1749-54) → Treaty of Pondicherry(1755) — Dupleix recall\n●3rd(1756-63) → Treaty of Paris(1763) — French power khatam\n●Wandiwash(1760, 3rd war ki battle): Eyre Coote(British,jeeta) vs Count de Lally(French,haara)\n TRICK — \"APP\" treaty trick\n💡\nAix-la-Chapelle(1st) → Pondicherry(2nd) → Paris(3rd) = \"APP\" — bas is short-code se teeno treaty yaad rakho: A\npehle, phir do P's.\nWandiwash = Eyre Coote(jeete) vs Lally(haare) — dono naam exam mein direct poochhe jaate hain, cross mat karo\nwinner-loser.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Carnatic War=Aix-la-Chapelle treaty. 2nd=Pondicherry treaty(Dupleix recall). 3rd=Paris treaty(French power\nkhatam). Wandiwash(1760)=Eyre Coote(British) ne Count de Lally(French) ko haraya.\n6. 4 Anglo-Mysore Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1767-69) → Koi GG nahi mentioned → Treaty of Madras(1769)\n●2nd(1780-84) → Warren Hastings → Treaty of Mangalore(1784)\n●3rd(1790-92) → Cornwallis → Treaty of Seringapatam(1792)\n●4th(1799) → Wellesley → Tipu maare gaye\n TRICK — \"None-Hastings-Cornwallis-Wellesley\" trick\n💡\n4 wars, pehli mein koi GG naam nahi(sabse purani, before-GG-system-established jaisa), phir 3 alag GGs: Warren\nHastings(2nd)-Cornwallis(3rd)-Wellesley(4th) — jaise GG-system dheere-dheere strong hui, waise hi har war mein\nnaya bada naam aaya.\n4th war mein Tipu khud maare gaye — is finality se yaad rakho ki 4th war hi Mysore ka poora ant hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAnglo-Mysore Wars GG: 1st=koi nahi. 2nd=Warren Hastings(Mangalore,1784). 3rd=Cornwallis(Seringapatam,1792).\n4th=Wellesley(Tipu death,1799).\n7. 1st Anglo-Afghan War(1839-42) — DISASTER\n●Lord Auckland ke time → British HAARE, Kabul se RETREAT karna pada — chapter ki EKLAUTI badi British\nhaar\n●Sindh(1843) annex hua — ye ALAG event hai, same time period mein\n TRICK — \"Sirf Afghan mein British haare\" trick\n💡\nPoore chapter mein British ne har jagah jeeta — Mysore,Punjab,Burma sab jagah — SIRF Afghanistan(1st war) mein\nDISASTROUS haar hui. Ye chapter ka SABSE UNIQUE fact hai(only-loss), isse alag se yaad rakho.\nSindh annexation(1843) Afghan war se ALAG event hai — same time period mein hua isliye confuse hota hai, par\ndono independent facts hain."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Anglo-Afghan War(1839-42, Lord Auckland) British ke liye DISASTROUS thi — Kabul se retreat. Sindh(1843)\nannexation ALAG event hai, same period mein.\n8. Punjab — Treaty of Amritsar + 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars\n●Treaty of Amritsar(1809): Ranjit Singh + Lord Metcalfe → Sutlej boundary\n●1st Anglo-Sikh War(1845-46): Sikhs haare → Treaty of Lahore(9 March 1846)\n●2nd(1848-49): Ramnagar→Chillianwala→Gujrat → March 1849 poora Punjab annex\n TRICK — Cross-chapter callback\n💡\nYe detail Rise of the Sikhs chapter mein bhi tha — is chapter mein sirf timeline recall karo: 1809(treaty)→1845-46(1st\nwar)→1848-49(2nd war,annex).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 Presidencies: Madras-Lease,Bombay-Dowry,Calcutta-Buy → Plassey(1757,Clive) vs Buxar(1764,Munro) →\nBlackHole=Holwell(146/23) → Nawabs: Jafar-Qasim-Jafar → Carnatic: APP treaties(AixLaChapelle-Pondicherry-\nParis),Wandiwash(Coote beat Lally) → Mysore GGs: None-WarrenHastings-Cornwallis-Wellesley →\nAfghanWar1(1839-42)=DISASTER(sirf British haar) → Punjab: Amritsar1809-1stAnglo-Sikh1845-46-2ndAnglo-\nSikh1848-49(annex)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGHEST WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bombay=DOWRY mila(1661), conquest se NAHI.\n2) Plassey(1757)=Clive. Buxar(1764)=Hector Munro — swap mat karo.\n3) Anglo-Mysore Wars GG: 1st=none, 2nd=Warren Hastings, 3rd=Cornwallis, 4th=Wellesley.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.2 British Expansion in Indian Territories"," THE REVOLT OF 1857 — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Plassey(1757) + 100 Saal = Revolt(1857)\n●1757 Plassey(British power ki shuruaat) → THEEK 100 saal baad → 1857 Revolt(sabse badi bagawat)\n●GG: Lord Canning(baad mein pehla Viceroy) · British PM: Lord Palmerston\n TRICK — \"100-saal-symmetry\" trick\n💡\n7-5-7 se 8-5-7 — dono saal mein \"57\" common hai(1757, 1857)! Jis saal British power SHURU hui, exactly usi ke 100-\nsaal-baad unhe sabse badi CHALLENGE mili — is symmetry se hi dono dates lock ho jaati hain.\n2. Causes — 4 Categories\n●Political: Doctrine of Lapse(Dalhousie) — Satara(1848),Sambalpur(1849),Jhansi(1853) · Subsidiary\nAlliance(Wellesley)\n●Economic: Permanent Settlement, Ryotwari, Mahalwari — sab kisaan-nuksaan wale\n●Social: Missionaries, racial discrimination, social-reform-backlash(Sati/child-marriage ban)\n●Immediate/Trigger: Enfield Rifle — cartridge mein Cow fat(Hindu) + Pig fat(Muslim) rumour\n TRICK — \"Dalhousie=Lapse, Wellesley=Alliance\" trick\n💡\nDalhousie=Lapse(D-L), Wellesley=Alliance(dono \"W\" jaisa lagta hai but alag) — Doctrine of Lapse aur Subsidiary\nAlliance dono POLITICAL causes hain par ALAG GG ne diye. Enfield Rifle sirf trigger/spark tha, background cause\nNAHI — baaki sab pehle se ubal rahe the.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDoctrine of Lapse = Dalhousie. Subsidiary Alliance = Wellesley. Enfield Rifle = sirf IMMEDIATE/trigger cause, baaki\n3 categories(political/economic/social) background causes hain.\n3. Revolt Ki Shuruaat — 3 Alag Dates\n●29 March 1857(Barrackpore) → Mangal Pandey → 34th Native Infantry → \"Maro Firangi Ko\" → Officers:\nLt.Baugh + Sgt-Major Hewson(\"Major Hudson\" GALAT hai)\n●10 May 1857(Meerut) → ASLI/OFFICIAL start → \"Chalo Delhi\" naara\n●11 May 1857(Delhi) → Bahadur Shah Zafar Emperor ghoshit, real command = General Bakht Khan\n TRICK — \"29-10-11\" three-date trick\n💡\nMangal Pandey(29 Mar) = individual spark(spontaneous, ek akela sipahi). Meerut(10 May) = official/organized\nstart. Delhi(11 May) = symbolic capital capture(agle hi din) — teen alag stages: individual-protest → organized-\nrevolt → symbolic-capital, EK EK din/mahine ka gap.\nBaugh+Hewson — \"Major Hudson\" naam GALAT hai, is verified-correction ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMangal Pandey incident(29 Mar 1857,Barrackpore) ≠ Official revolt start(10 May 1857,Meerut) ≠ Delhi capture(11 May\n1857) — teeno alag dates. Officers ke sahi naam: Lt.Baugh+Sgt-Major HEWSON(NOT 'Major Hudson').\n4. Bahadur Shah Zafar — Symbolic, NOT Real Command\n●Zafar = symbolic/nominal Emperor — declared \"Shahenshah-e-Hindustan\"\n●General Bakht Khan = REAL military command\n TRICK — \"Naam ka raja, kaam ka General\" trick\n💡"," Same pattern jo baar-baar dikha hai(Sadasiva Raya/Rama Raya, Chandragupta/real-founder): Zafar = title-holder,\nBakht Khan = actual power — \"naam-mein Emperor, kaam-mein General\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahadur Shah Zafar sirf SYMBOLIC leader tha. Real military command = General Bakht Khan — ye exam mein direct\npoocha jaata hai.\n5. Centre-Wise Leaders — Direct Match\n●Delhi: Zafar+Bakht Khan vs Nicholson · Lucknow: Begum Hazrat Mahal(Nepal bhaagi) vs Colin Campbell\n●Kanpur: Nana Saheb+Tantia Tope vs Havelock · Jhansi: Rani Laxmibai vs Hugh Rose\n●Arrah/Bihar: Kunwar Singh(~80 saal, SABSE BUDHE) vs William Taylor · Gwalior: Tantia Tope — REVOLT\nYAHIN KHATAM(20 June 1858)\n TRICK — \"Hugh Rose Quote\" + \"Kunwar Singh Age\" trick\n💡\nHugh Rose(British commander) ne Laxmibai ke baare mein kaha: \"The only man among rebels\" — ye QUOTE\nBRITISH ki taraf se hai, Laxmibai khud ne nahi kaha — is direction ko yaad rakho.\nKunwar Singh = ~80 saal, sabse budhe par sabse bahadur rebel — age-fact khud unique hai isliye alag se yaad reh jaata\nhai.\nGwalior = revolt ka AAKHRI centre(20 June 1858) — Tantia Tope wahi tak lade, revolt ka poora ant yahin hua.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"The only man among rebels\" = Hugh Rose(British commander) ka quote Rani Laxmibai ke baare mein — khud\nLaxmibai ka quote NAHI. Kunwar Singh(~80 saal) = sabse budhe rebel leader.\n6. Failure — 4 Reasons\n●South India + Punjab BILKUL SHAANT rahe(limited geographic spread)\n●Limited social base(educated class,zamindars ne saath nahi diya)\n●Central leadership ki kami(Zafar sirf symbolic)\n●British ke better resources(telegraph+railways)\n TRICK — \"South+Punjab Shaant\" trick\n💡\nSouth India aur Punjab poori tarah SHAANT rahe — is geographic-limitation ko sabse pehle yaad rakho, kyunki\nexam isko highlight karta hai. Baaki 3 reasons(social-base, leadership, resources) sab \"kami/weakness\" hain, par\ngeography wala fact SABSE specific hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSouth India aur Punjab revolt ke time BILKUL SHAANT rahe — ye ek key geographic-limitation fact hai jo failure ka\nbada reason tha.\n7. Historians Ki Opinion — Match Karo\n●V.D. Savarkar(\"The Indian War of Independence,1857\") = PEHLE isse \"War of Independence\" kehne wale\n●R.C. Majumdar = \"Neither first, nor national, nor war of independence\" — Savarkar ke bilkul ULTA\n●Disraeli(British MP!) = \"National Revolt\" — khud British hote hue bhi positive view\n●S.N. Sen = Official Government Historian · Ashok Mehta = \"Great Rebellion\" · T.R. Holmes = \"Civilisation vs\nBarbarism\"\n TRICK — \"Savarkar-First, Majumdar-Opposite, Disraeli-Surprising\" trick\n💡\nSavarkar = PEHLA kehne wala(War of Independence). Majumdar = SEEDHA VIRODH(Savarkar ka opposite).\nDisraeli = SURPRISING(British hote hue bhi \"National Revolt\" kaha) — 3 sabse important historians, 3 alag angle:"," pehla, opposite, surprising.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSavarkar = SABSE PEHLE \"War of Independence\" kaha. Majumdar = \"Neither first, nor national, nor war of\nindependence\" (Savarkar ke opposite). Disraeli = British MP hote hue bhi \"National Revolt\" kaha.\n8. After 1857 — Government of India Act, 1858\n●EIC ka rule khatam(1600 se 1858 tak, 258 saal) · Crown(Queen Victoria) supreme authority ban gayi\n●Governor-General → Viceroy designation badla · Lord Canning = FIRST Viceroy\n TRICK — \"258-saal-ka-ant\" trick\n💡\n1600(EIC bani) → 1858(EIC khatam) = poore 258 saal — is bade number se hi yaad rakho ki kitna bada shift tha\n\"Company Rule → Crown Rule\". Canning = same-vyakti jo LAST Governor-General bhi tha aur FIRST Viceroy bhi\n— designation badla, aadmi wahi raha.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Plassey(1757)+100=Revolt(1857) → Causes: Dalhousie-Lapse,Wellesley-Alliance,Enfield-trigger →\n29Mar(MangalPandey,Barrackpore)→10May(Meerut,official)→11May(Delhi,Zafar) →\nZafar=symbolic,BakhtKhan=real command → Centres:\nDelhi,Lucknow(HazratMahal),Kanpur(NanaSaheb+TantiaTope),Jhansi(Laxmibai-HughRose\nquote),Arrah(KunwarSingh~80yrs),Gwalior(revolt ends 20June1858) → Failure: South+Punjab shaant,weak\nleadership,British resources → Historians: Savarkar(first)-Majumdar(opposite)-Disraeli(surprising) → GoI Act1858:\nEIC-258yrs-khatam, Canning=lastGG+1stViceroy\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Mangal Pandey(29 Mar,Barrackpore) ≠ Official start(10 May,Meerut) ≠ Delhi capture(11 May) — teen alag dates.\n2) Bahadur Shah Zafar=symbolic. General Bakht Khan=real military command.\n3) \"The only man among rebels\" = Hugh Rose(British) ka quote Laxmibai ke baare mein, khud unka nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.3 The Revolt of 1857"," PEASANT MOVEMENTS & TRIBAL REVOLTS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Champaran(1917) vs Kheda(1918) — Dono Gandhi Ke, Alag Hain\n●Champaran(1917) = 1st Gandhian Satyagraha · Bihar · Indigo farmers · Tinkathia System ke against\n●Kheda(1918) = Gandhi+Patel · Gujarat · Famine ke time bhi tax badha diya\n TRICK — \"Cham-1st, Kheda-2nd\" trick\n💡\nChamparan = Gandhi ka PEHLA satyagraha(1917,indigo/Bihar) — is \"FIRST\" ka tag hamesha Champaran ke saath\nhi rahega. Kheda(1918) ek saal baad, alag state(Gujarat), alag issue(tax-during-famine) — \"pehla=Champaran,\ndusra=Kheda\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChamparan(1917,Bihar,indigo/Tinkathia) = 1st Gandhian Satyagraha. Kheda(1918,Gujarat,famine-tax) = alag movement\n— dono Gandhi ke hain par mix mat karo.\n2. Bardoli(1928) — \"Sardar\" Title\n●Vallabhbhai Patel ko \"Sardar\" title mila Bardoli(Gujarat) ki jeet ke baad — Gandhi ne NAHI, leader Patel the\n TRICK — \"Bardoli=Sardar\" hook\n💡\nBardoli-Sardar — dono \"ar\" sound se rhyme karte hain, isse seedha yaad rakho ki is jeet se hi Patel ko \"Sardar\" mila.\n3. Santhal(Hul) vs Munda(Ulgulan) — Sabse Bada Trap\n●Santhal Rebellion(Hul,1855-56) = Sidhu & Kanhu · Bengal/Jharkhand · \"Hul\"(Santali) = \"revolt\"\n●Munda Rebellion(Ulgulan,1899-1900) = Birsa Munda · Jharkhand · \"Ulgulan\"(Mundari) = \"Great Tumult\"\n TRICK — \"Hul-Sidhu/Kanhu, Ulgulan-Birsa\" trick\n💡\n44 saal ka gap(1855→1899). Santhal = 2 bhai leaders(Sidhu+Kanhu), Munda = 1 leader(Birsa). \"Hul = Happens-\npehle(1855), Ulgulan = Us-baad(1899)\" — H before U alphabetically bhi, aur time mein bhi pehle.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSanthal Rebellion(Hul,1855-56)=Sidhu&Kanhu. Munda Rebellion(Ulgulan,1899-1900)=Birsa Munda.\n\"Hul\"=revolt(Santali). \"Ulgulan\"=Great Tumult(Mundari) — dono bilkul alag hain.\n4. Tebhaga(1946-47) — 2/3rd, NOT Half-Half\n●Tebhaga = 3 shares — sharecroppers ko 2/3rd, landlord ko sirf 1/3rd (pehle half-half tha)\n●Led by BPKS/All India Kisan Sabha(CPI) — Bengal\n TRICK — \"Tebhaga=Teen bhaag\" trick\n💡\nTebhaga = \"Teen bhaag\"(3 shares) — naam mein hi \"teen\" chhupa hai. Demand: 2 bhaag kisan ko, 1 bhaag zamindar\nko — pehle 1-1(half-half) tha, ab 2:1 ka naya ratio maanga gaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTebhaga demand = sharecroppers ko 2/3rd share (landlord ko sirf 1/3rd) — pehle half-half tha, half-half ko final answer\nmat samajhna."," 5. Paika(1817) vs Sambalpur(1827-62) — Dono Odisha, Alag Leaders\n●Paika Rebellion(1817-25) = Bakshi Jagabandhu · land revenue+salt monopoly\n●Sambalpur Rebellion(1827-62) = Surendra Sai · alag/baad ka movement\n TRICK — \"Paika-Bakshi, Sambalpur-Surendra\" trick\n💡\nDono ODISHA mein hain isliye confuse hote hain — Paika-Bakshi(pehle,1817), Sambalpur-Surendra(baad mein,1827+,\nS-S bhi match karta hai) — same state, alag leader, alag decade.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPaika Rebellion(1817)=Bakshi Jagabandhu. Sambalpur Rebellion(1827-62)=Surendra Sai. Dono Odisha mein hain par\nbilkul ALAG movements/leaders.\n6. Indigo Movement(1859) vs Champaran(1917) — Dono Indigo, Alag Hain\n●Indigo Movement/Neel Vidroh(1859-60) = Digambar Biswas · Bengal · forced indigo cultivation\n●Champaran(1917) = Gandhi · Bihar · Tinkathia system\n TRICK — \"58-saal gap, alag state, alag leader\" trick\n💡\nDono \"indigo\" se related hain isliye confuse hote hain, par: Neel Vidroh(1859,Bengal,Digambar Biswas) vs\nChamparan(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) — 58 saal ka gap, alag state, alag leader — sirf \"crop\"(indigo) common hai, baaki\nsab alag.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndigo Movement/Neel Vidroh(1859-60,Bengal,Digambar Biswas) ≠ Champaran(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) — dono indigo-\nrelated hain par 58 saal ka gap aur alag state/leader.\n7. Moplah Rebellion(1921-22) — 3 Causes, Ek Nahi\n●Khilafat Movement + Anti-Landlord + Anti-British — teeno saath, leader Ali Musliyar, Kerala\n TRICK — \"3-in-1\" trick\n💡\nMoplah = TEEN causes ek saath(Khilafat+Landlord+British) — koi bhi EK causes bolna incomplete hai. \"Moplah =\nMultiple(teen) causes\" — is completeness ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMoplah Rebellion(1921-22) ke 3 causes the: Khilafat Movement + Anti-Landlord + Anti-British — sirf ek causes batana\nincomplete answer hai.\n8. 2 Ranis — Naam Mein Rani, Regions Alag\n●Rani Chennamma = Kittur Rebellion(1824-29), Karnataka\n●Rani Gaidinliu = Naga Rebellion(1931), Nagaland(saath mein Jadonang)\n TRICK — \"Chennamma-South, Gaidinliu-Northeast\" trick\n💡\nChennamma = \"Chennai/South India\" jaisa sound(Karnataka). Gaidinliu = alag/exotic naam(Northeast/Nagaland) —\ndono \"Rani\" hain par region ki sound se hi distinguish karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRani Chennamma = Kittur Rebellion(Karnataka,1824-29). Rani Gaidinliu = Naga Rebellion(Nagaland,1931) — dono\nnaam mein \"Rani\" hai, mix mat karo."," 9. Kuka vs Faraizi — Dono Religious-Reform, Alag Dharam\n●Kuka Movement(1860-70) = Bhagat Jawahar Mal · Punjab · Namdhari Sikh reform\n●Faraizi Movement(1818-60) = Haji Shariatullah · Bengal · Muslim reform\n TRICK — \"Kuka-Sikh, Faraizi-Muslim\" trick\n💡\nKuka = \"gurkul/Sikh\" jaisa sound(Punjab, Namdhari Sikh). Faraizi = \"Faraz/Islamic duty\" (Bengal, Muslim reform) —\nnaam se hi dharm-connect ho jaata hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Champaran(1917,1st,Bihar,indigo) vs Kheda(1918,Gujarat) → Bardoli(1928)=Sardar-Patel → Santhal-\nHul(1855,Sidhu+Kanhu) vs Munda-Ulgulan(1899,Birsa) → Tebhaga=2/3rd(not half-half) → Paika(1817,Bakshi) vs\nSambalpur(1827,Surendra Sai) → IndigoMovement(1859,Bengal,Digambar) vs Champaran(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) →\nMoplah=3causes(Khilafat+Landlord+British) → RaniChennamma(Kittur,Karnataka) vs RaniGaidinliu(Naga,Nagaland)\n→ Kuka(Sikh,Punjab) vs Faraizi(Muslim,Bengal)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Santhal(Hul,1855,Sidhu&Kanhu) ≠ Munda(Ulgulan,1899,Birsa Munda) — dono bilkul alag.\n2) Tebhaga = 2/3rd share sharecroppers ko (half-half NAHI, teen-bhaag ka naya ratio).\n3) Moplah Rebellion ke 3 causes: Khilafat+Anti-Landlord+Anti-British — sirf ek mat batana.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Peasant Movements & Tribal Revolts"," SOCIO-RELIGIOUS REFORM MOVEMENTS — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nModern History · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — 2 Titles, 2 Sources\n●\"Raja\" = Mughal Emperor Akbar II ne diya\n●\"Yugdoot\" = Subhash Chandra Bose ne kaha(\"The Indian Struggle\" kitaab mein)\n●Anti-Sati Bill(1829) = Regulation XVII, William Bentinck ne sign kiya\n TRICK — \"Purana Raja, Naya Yugdoot\" trick\n💡\nRaja = PURANA/Mughal source(Akbar II, khud ek raja tha, isliye \"Raja\" title dene wala bhi raja hi tha — natural\nmatch). Yugdoot = NAYA/Modern source(Subhash Bose, 20th century leader) — \"purana title purane raja se, naya\ntitle naye leader se\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Raja\" title = Akbar II(Mughal Emperor) ne diya. \"Yugdoot\" = Subhash Chandra Bose ne kaha — dono alag sources\nhain, mix mat karo.\n2. Brahmo Samaj — Poora Timeline + Splits\n●1828: Brahmo Samaj(RMMR) → 1839: Tattvabodhini Sabha(Debendranath Tagore)\n●1866 GREAT SPLIT: Adi Brahmo Samaj(Debendranath) vs Indian Brahmo Samaj(Keshab Chandra Sen)\n●1878: Sadharan Brahmo Samaj(Keshab se DOBARA split)\n TRICK — \"Adi=Purana, Sadharan=Doosri baar\" trick\n💡\nAdi Brahmo = \"Adi\"(original/purana) — Debendranath, jo shuru se Samaj mein tha. Indian Brahmo = naya\ngroup — Keshab, jo baad mein aaya(1858) aur split kiya(1866). Sadharan = Keshab SE HI dobara split(1878) —\nmatlab Keshab ka group bhi khud aage jaake toota. Pattern: \"split-pe-split\", teen generations of division.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1866 Great Split: Adi Brahmo Samaj=Debendranath Tagore. Indian Brahmo Samaj=Keshab Chandra Sen. Sadharan\nBrahmo Samaj(1878)=Keshab se DOBARA split hua — teen-way division, sequence yaad rakho.\n3. Arya Samaj — Bombay Se Lahore Tak\n●Founded 1875, Bombay → HQ shift 1877, Lahore → DAV College bhi Lahore(1886)\n●Swami Dayanand Saraswati: \"Go back to the Vedas\" slogan · Satyarth Prakash(1874)\n TRICK — \"3 Lahore-links\" trick\n💡\nTeen cheezein Lahore se juda hai: HQ-shift(1877), DAV College(1886) — bas yaad rakho \"Arya Samaj Bombay\nmein PAIDA hui, Lahore mein BADI hui\" — origin alag, growth-center alag.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArya Samaj founded 1875(Bombay), HQ shift 1877(Lahore). DAV College bhi Lahore mein(1886) — teeno Lahore-\nconnect, Bombay sirf founding-place hai.\n4. Theosophical Society — New York Mein Bani, India Mein NAHI\n●Founded 1875, NEW YORK(Blavatsky+Olcott) — India mein NAHI\n●India HQ = Adyar, Madras · Key India leader = Annie Besant(founder NAHI, later leader)"," TRICK — \"New York=birth, Adyar=India-home\" trick\n💡\nTheosophical Society ka JANM New York mein hua(1875), phir India shift hui(Adyar) — jaise koi videshi\ncompany pehle apne desh mein bane, phir India mein branch khole. Annie Besant sirf India ki BRANCH ki leader\nthi, poore society ki founder NAHI.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTheosophical Society 1875 NEW YORK mein bani(Blavatsky+Olcott), India mein NAHI. Annie Besant = India-branch\nki leader, founder NAHI.\n5. Dharma Sabha(1830) — RMMR Ke KHILAF Thi\n●Radhakanta Dev(founder) → Orthodox organization → Sati ko SUPPORT kiya → RMMR ke reforms ke against\n TRICK — \"Dharma Sabha = Opposite team\" trick\n💡\nNaam \"Dharma Sabha\" sunke lagta hai koi reform group hoga — GALAT, ye RMMR ka VIRODHI(orthodox) group\ntha jo Sati ko SUPPORT karta tha. \"Dharma Sabha = Purani parampara ki team, RMMR = Naye reform ki team\"\n— dono opposite sides.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDharma Sabha(1830,Radhakanta Dev) = ORTHODOX group jo Sati ko support karta tha, RMMR ke reforms ke against\ntha — naam se confuse mat hona.\n6. AMU — College(1875) → University(1920)\n●Sir Syed Ahmed Khan → Muhammadan Anglo-Oriental College(1875) → baad mein AMU(1920)\n●Deoband(1866-67): Nanautavi+Gangohi → Abul Kalam Azad associated\n●Ahmadiyya(1889): Mirza Ghulam Ahmad, Punjab · Rahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha(1851): Dadabhai Naoroji(Parsi,\nIslam se related NAHI)\n TRICK — \"1875-College, 1920-University\" + \"Rahnumai=Parsi\" trick\n💡\nAMU ki DO dates: 1875(college banayi) → 1920(university ban gayi) — 45 saal ka gap, dono yaad rakho.\nRahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha naam Islamic lagta hai par ye PARSI reform movement hai(Dadabhai Naoroji) —\nis naam-trap ko yaad rakho, \"Mazdayasan\" khud Zoroastrianism se related word hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuhammadan Anglo-Oriental College(1875) → AMU(1920). Rahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha(1851,Dadabhai Naoroji) =\nPARSI reform, Islam se related NAHI.\n7. Phule Couple & Vivekananda — Key Dates\n●Savitribai Phule = First Woman Teacher of India · 1848 school banaya\n●Jyotiba Phule: Gulamgiri(1872) — Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) se PEHLE likhi gayi\n●Vivekananda: birth 12 Jan 1863(=National Youth Day) · real naam Narendranath Dutta\n TRICK — \"Book pehle, Samaj baad mein\" + Birthday trick\n💡\nGulamgiri(1872) LIKHI GAYI Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) BANNE SE PEHLE — ek saal ka gap, book pehle aayi\nphir organization bani.\n12 January = Vivekananda ka birthday = National Youth Day(1984 se) — is double-meaning date ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJyotiba Phule ki Gulamgiri(1872) Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) banne se PEHLE likhi gayi thi — order confuse mat karo."," 8. Ranade \"Socrates of India\" + Narayana Guru's 3 Movements\n●M.G. Ranade = \"Socrates of India\" · Prarthana Samaj(1869 join) · Indian National Social Conference(1887,\"Social\nWing of INC\")\n●Shri Narayana Guru(Kerala) = 3 movements: Aravipuram(1888) → Temple Entry(1902) → SNDP Yogam(1902-03)\n TRICK — \"Ranade=Philosopher, Narayana Guru=Kerala-triple\" trick\n💡\nRanade = Socrates(Greek philosopher se comparison, uski wisdom/reasoning-based reform ke liye). Narayana Guru =\nKerala ka SABSE ACTIVE reformer, teen alag movements chalayi — \"ek nahi, TEEN\" yaad rakho, exam isi count pe\npakadta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nShri Narayana Guru = 3 movements(Aravipuram-1888, Temple Entry-1902, SNDP Yogam-1902-03) — Kerala ke sabse\nactive anti-untouchability reformer.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"RMMR: Raja(AkbarII)-Yugdoot(SubhashBose) → BrahmoSamaj: 1828-1839(Tattvabodhini)-1866(Split:Adi-\nDebendranath/Indian-Keshab)-1878(Sadharan) → AryaSamaj: Bombay1875→Lahore1877→DAV1886 →\nTheosophical: NewYork1875→Adyar(India-HQ) → DharmaSabha=orthodox,anti-RMMR → AMU:\ncollege1875→university1920 → Rahnumai=Parsi(not Islam) → Phule: Gulamgiri1872→SatyashodhakSamaj1873 →\nVivekananda=12Jan=NationalYouthDay → Ranade=SocratesOfIndia → NarayanaGuru=3movements(Kerala)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Theosophical Society NEW YORK mein bani(1875), India mein nahi — India HQ=Adyar hai.\n2) Dharma Sabha(1830) orthodox thi, RMMR ke against — naam se confuse mat hona.\n3) 1866 Split: Adi Brahmo=Debendranath. Indian Brahmo=Keshab. Sadharan(1878)=Keshab se dobara split.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Socio-Religious Reform Movements"," PRESS & EDUCATION IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Press Ki Shuruaat — Firsts\n●Bengal Gazette(1780) = India ka PEHLA newspaper(English) — Editor James Augustus Hickey\n●Udant Martand(1826) = PEHLA Hindi newspaper\n●Printing Press: Portuguese(Goa,1557) → EIC(Mumbai,1674)\n TRICK — \"1780-Hickey, 1826-Hindi\" trick\n💡\n46 saal ka gap(1780→1826) — pehle overall newspaper(English,Hickey), phir 46 saal baad pehla HINDI newspaper.\n\"Hickey ka Hindi wala successor 46 saal baad aaya\" — is gap se dono dates lock ho jaati hain.\n2. 7 Press Acts — Chronological Sequence\n●1799 Wellesley(Censorship) → 1823 John Adams(Licensing) → 1835 Metcalfe(\"Liberator\") → 1857\nCanning(Licensing, Revolt ke time) → 1878 Lytton(Vernacular/\"Gagging\") → 1908+1910 Minto II(2 Acts)\n TRICK — \"Restrict-Restrict-FREE-Restrict-Restrict-Restrict×2\" trick\n💡\nPattern: sab acts RESTRICT karte hain, SIRF Metcalfe(1835) FREE karta hai — is ek alag rang ke act ko yaad\nrakho, baaki sab \"control\" ki taraf hain, Metcalfe akela \"freedom\" wala.\nMinto II = 2 Acts EK HI Viceroy ne(1908+1910) — koi aur Viceroy ne double-Act nahi kiya, ye uniqueness yaad\nrakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMetcalfe(1835) = \"Liberator of Press\"(freedom di). Vernacular Press Act(1878,Lytton) = \"Gagging Act\"(restrict kiya).\nMinto II ne 2 Acts pass kiye(1908+1910) — ek hi Viceroy.\n3. Amrit Bazar Patrika — Raatoraat Bengali Se English\n●1868 founded(Sisir Kumar Ghosh+Motilal Ghosh) → 1878 Vernacular Press Act se bachne ke liye 21 March 1878\nko Bengali se ENGLISH mein badal liya\n TRICK — \"Raatoraat bhasha badli\" trick\n💡\nVernacular Press Act sirf VERNACULAR(local-language) papers ko target karta tha, English EXEMPT thi —\nisliye ABP ne SMART move khela: bas bhasha badal di, publication band nahi ki. Ye poore chapter ka SABSE\nDRAMATIC/legendary moment hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmrit Bazar Patrika ne Vernacular Press Act(1878) se bachne ke liye Bengali se English mein badal liya — kyunki Act\nsirf vernacular(local-language) papers cover karta tha.\n4. Macaulay's Minute(1835) vs Wood's Dispatch(1854)\n●Macaulay(1835) = \"Downward Filtration Theory\" — English medium, upper-class target\n●Wood's Dispatch(1854) = \"Magna Carta of Indian Education\" — GG Dalhousie · School=vernacular,\nCollege=English(dual policy)\n TRICK — \"Macaulay=Filter, Wood's=Magna Carta\" trick\n💡\nMacaulay = \"upar se neeche TAPKANA\"(filtration — sirf upper class ko English do, baaki tak \"chhan ke\" pahunche).\nWood's = \"Magna Carta\"(bada constitutional-jaisa document, DUAL policy — vernacular+English dono level pe). 19\nsaal ka gap(1835→1854), dono alag philosophy."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMacaulay's Minute(1835) = Downward Filtration Theory(English-only,upper class). Wood's Dispatch(1854,Dalhousie)\n= Magna Carta of Indian Education(dual: school=vernacular, college=English) — do alag policies.\n5. 6 Education Commissions — Chairman + Key Reform\n●Hunter(1882-83,Ripon) = Wood's Dispatch review, Primary+Secondary focus\n●Indian University Commission(1904,Curzon) = Sir Thomas Raleigh, stricter control\n●Sadler(1917,Chelmsford) = M.E.Sadler → 12th(Intermediate) ko Degree se ALAG kiya\n●Hartog(1929,Irwin) = Philip Hartog → \"Wastage and Stagnation\"\n●Sargent Plan(1944) = Free+Compulsory Education(6-11 saal)\n●Radhakrishnan(1948) = 1st Education Commission of INDEPENDENT India → UGC ka base\n TRICK — \"HISHSR\" 6-commission trick\n💡\nHunter-IndianUniv-Sadler-Hartog-Sargent-Radhakrishnan = \"HISHSR\" — chronological order, British-era 5(Hunter se\nSargent) → phir AAKHRI(Radhakrishnan) Independence ke BAAD ka pehla — ye \"before/after independence\" split\nyaad rakho.\nSadler = 12th ALAG kiya(intermediate concept). Hartog = Wastage+Stagnation(dropout-focused). Dono naam se hi\nkaam yaad nahi aata, bas ratt lo: S-12th, H-Wastage.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRadhakrishnan Committee(1948) = 1ST Education Commission of INDEPENDENT India(UGC ka base). Sadler(1917)\n= 12th ko Degree se alag kiya. Hartog(1929) = Wastage and Stagnation.\n6. Major Institutions — Founder Match\n●Calcutta Madrasa(1781,Warren Hastings) = 1st Oriental Institution\n●Asiatic Society(1784,William Jones) · Banaras Sanskrit College(1791,Jonathan Duncan)\n●Hindu College(1817,RMMR+David Hare) · 3 Universities(1857) — SAME saal Revolt of 1857!\n●Central Hindu College(1898,Annie Besant) → baad mein BHU ban gaya\n TRICK — \"1857 coincidence\" trick\n💡\nCalcutta+Madras+Bombay Universities SAME SAAL bani jis saal Revolt of 1857 hui — is coincidence ko yaad\nrakho, exam isi angle se poochta hai: \"jis saal India ne British ke against ladi, usi saal British ne apna education-system\nbhi establish kiya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n3 Universities(Calcutta,Madras,Bombay) 1857 mein bani — YEHI SAAL Revolt of 1857 ka bhi hai, coincidence yaad\nrakho.\n7. Journals & Books — Author Match Traps\n●Tilak: Kesari(Marathi) + Maratha(English) — 2 journals, 2 alag bhasha\n●Annie Besant: New India + Commonweal — 2 journals\n●Azad: Al-Hilal(journal,Urdu) + India Wins Freedom(book)\n●\"The Independent\" = Motilal Nehru(pita), Jawaharlal NAHI\n●\"Leader\": Founder=Malaviya, Editor=C.Y.Chintamani(alag roles)\n TRICK — \"Motilal not Jawaharlal\" + \"Founder≠Editor\" trick\n💡\n\"The Independent\" = MOTILAL(baap) — \"Jawaharlal\" hamesha option mein diya jaata hai but GALAT hai, yaad\nrakho \"baap ne shuru ki, bete ne nahi\".\n\"Leader\" journal ke 2 roles: Malaviya=Founder(shuru kiya), Chintamani=Editor(chalaya) — MCQ mein dono\noptions mein aa sakte hain, role dhyan se padho."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"The Independent\" journal = Motilal Nehru ne banayi (Jawaharlal NAHI). \"Leader\" journal: Founder=Malaviya,\nEditor=C.Y.Chintamani — do alag roles.\n8. Valentine Chirol — 2 Cheezein Ek Hi Title\n●Valentine Chirol(British journalist,\"Indian Unrest\" book) ne DONO ko \"Father of Indian Unrest\" kaha: Tilak AUR\nArya Samaj\n TRICK — \"Ek title, do winners\" trick\n💡\nSame title EK VYAKTI(Tilak) aur EK ORGANIZATION(Arya Samaj) dono ko diya gaya — \"Chirol ne DO baar\nsame compliment/criticism diya\" — is duplication ko yaad rakho, exam dono options try karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nValentine Chirol ne \"Father of Indian Unrest\" title DONO ko diya: Tilak(vyakti) AUR Arya Samaj(organization) —\ndono associations yaad rakho.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"BengalGazette(1780,Hickey)-UdantMartand(1826,Hindi) → PressActs: Wellesley1799-Adams1823-\nMetcalfe1835(Liberator)-Canning1857-Lytton1878(Gagging)-MintoII1908+1910 → ABP: Bengali→English(1878) →\nMacaulay1835(Filtration) vs Wood's1854(MagnaCarta,Dalhousie) → Commissions: HISHSR(Hunter-IndianUniv-\nSadler-Hartog-Sargent-Radhakrishnan) → Institutions: CalcuttaMadrasa1781-AsiaticSociety1784-HinduCollege1817-\n3Universities1857(=Revolt year) → Journals: Tilak(Kesari-Maratha),Besant(NewIndia-\nCommonweal),TheIndependent=MotilalNOTJawaharlal,Leader=Malaviya(founder)/Chintamani(editor) → Chirol:\nTilak+AryaSamaj dono='FatherOfIndianUnrest'\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) \"The Independent\" = Motilal Nehru(NOT Jawaharlal).\n2) Wood's Dispatch(1854)=Magna Carta of Education. Macaulay's Minute(1835)=Downward Filtration Theory — do\nalag policies.\n3) 3 Universities(Calcutta,Madras,Bombay) 1857 mein bani — Revolt of 1857 ke SAME saal.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Press & Education in India"," FORMATION OF INDIAN NATIONAL CONGRESS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 7 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. INC Formation — 3 Theories, 3 Angle\n●Safety Valve Theory = A.O. Hume(British angle) — Indian gussa release karne ke liye\n●Lightning Conductor Theory = Gokhale(Indian angle) — Indians ne Hume ko istemal kiya\n●Conspiracy Theory = R.P. Dutt(Marxist/critical angle) — poori British saazish\n TRICK — \"3 alag chashme\" trick\n💡\n3 alag \"lens\" se dekha gaya: Hume(khud British) = apna hi bachaav(safety valve), Gokhale(Indian) = ulta\nangle(hum ne unhe use kiya), Dutt(Marxist) = sabse critical(conspiracy). \"Hume-Safety, Gokhale-Lightning, Dutt-\nConspiracy\" — H-S, G-L, D-C bolke ratt lo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSafety Valve Theory=Hume. Lightning Conductor Theory=Gokhale. Conspiracy Theory=R.P.Dutt — teeno alag angle\nse hain, mix mat karo.\n2. Pre-Congress Organizations — 2 \"Sabse\" Trap\n●Landholders' Society(1838,Dwarkanath Tagore) = India ka PEHLA Organized Political Association\n●Indian National Association(1876,Surendranath Banerjee) = SABSE IMPORTANT pre-Congress org — 1886 mein\nSEEDHA INC mein MERGE hui\n TRICK — \"Pehla≠Sabse Important\" trick\n💡\nLandholders' Society = TIME mein pehla(1838), Indian National Association = IMPORTANCE mein\npehla(1876,direct INC predecessor) — dono \"pehla\" hain par ALAG dimension mein: ek TIME-first, doosra\nIMPORTANCE-first(kyunki ye seedha INC mein hi merge ho gayi).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndia ka PEHLA Organized Political Association = Landholders' Society(1838,Dwarkanath Tagore). SABSE\nIMPORTANT pre-Congress org = Indian National Association(1876, jo 1886 mein INC mein merge hui) — dono\nconfuse mat karo.\n3. Dadabhai Naoroji — Har Jagah Naam Aata Hai\n●Bombay Association(1852) + London India Society(1865) + East India Association(1866,London,SOLO founder)\n●Title: \"Grand Old Man of India\" · Drain of Wealth Theory · \"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar use kiya(1906,22nd\nSession)\n TRICK — \"Naoroji = Har jagah\" trick\n💡\nNaoroji 3+ organizations mein involved tha — \"jahan bhi kuch shuru hua, wahan Naoroji zaroor tha\" — is\nomnipresence ko yaad rakho, isliye unhe \"Grand Old Man\" bhi kaha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar Dadabhai NAOROJI ne use kiya(1906,22nd Session,Calcutta) — Gokhale ya Tilak ne NAHI.\n4. INC Founding — Core Facts\n●28 December 1885, Bombay(Gokuldas Tejpal Sanskrit College) · Founder A.O. Hume · 1st President W.C. Bonnerjee\n· Viceroy Lord Dufferin"," ●72 delegates — Bombay se max(38)\n TRICK — \"Founder≠President\" reminder\n💡\nHume(British) = FOUNDER, Bonnerjee(Indian) = 1ST PRESIDENT — do alag roles, do alag log — pattern jo\nbaar-baar dikha hai(jaise founder vs real-founder), yahan founder vs president.\n5. Vande Mataram(1896) vs Jana Gana Mana(1911) — Dono Calcutta\n●Vande Mataram: 12th Session(1896,Calcutta,President Sayani) · Composer Bankim Chandra(Anandamath,1882) ·\nSinger Rabindranath Tagore\n●Jana Gana Mana: 26th Session(1911,Calcutta,President Bishan Narayan Dhar) · Composer+Singer Rabindranath\nTagore(dono role khud)\n TRICK — \"12th vs 26th, dono Calcutta\" trick\n💡\nDono SAME CITY(Calcutta) mein hue, par 15 saal ka gap(1896→1911) — 12th session(chota number)=Vande\nMataram(purana), 26th session(bada number)=Jana Gana Mana(baad ka) — session-number se hi chronology\nyaad rakho.\nVande Mataram mein COMPOSER aur SINGER alag(Bankim+Tagore), Jana Gana Mana mein Tagore ne\nDONO kiya(khud likha, khud gaya) — ye role-difference yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVande Mataram=12th Session(1896,Calcutta) — Composer Bankim Chandra, Singer Tagore(alag log). Jana Gana\nMana=26th Session(1911,Calcutta) — Tagore ne khud likha+gaya dono.\n6. Surat Split(1907) — President Yaad Rakho, Tilak NAHI\n●23rd Session, Surat, 1907 → President Rash Bihari Ghosh(Tilak ya Lal-Bal-Pal NAHI — wo sirf leaders the)\n●Moderates(Naram Dal) vs Extremists(Garam Dal) — 1906 ke 4 resolutions ko poore India mein failane ka mudda\n TRICK — \"Surat ki Surat bigdi\" trick(source ka mnemonic)\n💡\n\"Surat mein Congress ki Surat(shakal) bigad gayi\" — wordplay se hi Surat Split yaad rah jaata hai. President = Rash\nBihari Ghosh — Tilak famous hai isliye log usse president samajh lete hain, GALAT hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSurat Split(1907,23rd Session) ka PRESIDENT = Rash Bihari Ghosh — Tilak ya Lal-Bal-Pal NAHI (wo extremist\nleaders the, president nahi).\n7. 2 Female Presidents — 8 Saal Ka Gap\n●1917(32nd Session,Calcutta): Annie Besant = 1st Female President — VIDESHI(British)\n●1925(Kanpur): Sarojini Naidu = 1st INDIAN Female President\n TRICK — \"Besant-Videshi, Naidu-Desi\" trick\n💡\nBesant PEHLE(1917) par VIDESHI, Naidu BAAD mein(1925) par DESI — 8 saal ka gap. \"Besant = British(pehle),\nNaidu = Native(baad mein)\" — B-before-N bhi alphabetically match karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Female President=Annie Besant(1917,videshi/British). 1st INDIAN Female President=Sarojini Naidu(1925,Kanpur)\n— 8 saal ka gap, dono alag categories.\n8. Gandhi — SIRF EK BAAR President\n●39th Session(1924,Belgaum,Karnataka) = Gandhi ji ki EKLAUTI presidency\n●Youngest President = Abul Kalam Azad(1923,Delhi Special Session)"," ●44th(1929,Lahore,Nehru) = Purna Swaraj resolution · 45th(1931,Karachi,Patel) = Fundamental Rights resolution\n TRICK — \"1924=ek baar\" trick\n💡\nGandhi itne bade leader the, par President SIRF EK BAAR bane(1924,Belgaum) — ye counter-intuitive fact\nhai(itna bada naam, itni kam baar president), isliye alag se yaad rakho: \"1924 = Gandhi ka EK-AUR-EKLAUTA\nsaal\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahatma Gandhi SIRF EK BAAR INC President bane — 1924, Belgaum(Karnataka) session mein. Baaki kisi bhi saal\nnahi.\n9. Kisne Kya Kaha — Quote Match\n●Lord Dufferin(Viceroy) = \"Microscopic Minority\"\n●Lord Curzon(Viceroy) = \"Peaceful demise\" chahta tha\n●Bankim Chandra(writer) = \"padon ke bhookhe\"(hungry for positions)\n●Bipin Chandra Pal(extremist) = \"Petitioning Institution of Moderates\"\n TRICK — \"2 Viceroy + 2 Writer/Leader\" trick\n💡\n4 quotes, 2 categories: 2 VICEROYS(Dufferin+Curzon) = British-official criticism, 2 INDIAN(Bankim+BipinPal)\n= internal/extremist criticism — \"British bahar se critical, apne log andar se critical\" — dono taraf se Congress critique\nhui.\n10. Muslim League(1906) — 3 Alag Naam\n●Initiative: Nawab Salimullah(Dhaka) · 1st President: Aga Khan · HQ: Lucknow\n TRICK — \"Salimullah-Idea, AgaKhan-President, Lucknow-HQ\" trick\n💡\n3 alag roles, 3 alag jagah/naam: Salimullah = shuru KARANE wala(Dhaka), Aga Khan = LEAD karne wala(1st\npresident), Lucknow = sirf HQ(Dhaka mein bani thi, HQ alag city mein) — teeno mix mat karo, exam directly poochta\nhai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuslim League(1906,Dhaka): Initiative=Nawab Salimullah. 1st President=Aga Khan. HQ=Lucknow — teeno alag facts\nhain, ek dusre se swap mat karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 theories: SafetyValve-Hume,LightningConductor-Gokhale,Conspiracy-Dutt → Pre-Congress:\nLandholdersSociety(1838,1st-ever) vs IndianNationalAssociation(1876,most-important,merged1886) → Naoroji: multi-\norg+Swaraj-word(1906) → INC: 28Dec1885,Hume-founder,Bonnerjee-1stPresident,Dufferin-viceroy →\nVandeMataram(1896,12th,Bankim+Tagore) vs JanaGanaMana(1911,26th,Tagore-both) →\nSuratSplit(1907,23rd,RashBihariGhosh) → Females: Besant(1917,videshi)-Naidu(1925,desi) → Gandhi=1924-\nBelgaum(only once) → Quotes: Dufferin-MicroscopicMinority,Curzon-PeacefulDemise,BipinPal-PetitioningInstitution\n→ MuslimLeague: Salimullah-initiative,AgaKhan-president,Lucknow-HQ\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) 1st Female President=Besant(1917,videshi). 1st INDIAN Female=Sarojini Naidu(1925) — 8 saal ka gap."," 2) \"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar Dadabhai Naoroji ne use kiya(1906) — Gokhale/Tilak nahi.\n3) Surat Split(1907) ka President=Rash Bihari Ghosh, Tilak NAHI.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Formation of Indian National Congress"," INDIAN NATIONAL MOVEMENT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 8 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Bengal Partition — 3 Alag Dates\n●Announced: 19 July 1905 · Effective: 16 October 1905 · Cancelled: 1911(Delhi Durbar, Lord Hardinge II)\n●Viceroy jisne partition kiya = Curzon(Divide&Rule) · Viceroy jisne cancel kiya = Hardinge II(alag vyakti)\n TRICK — \"Announce-Effective-Cancel\" 3-stage trick\n💡\nJulai mein Announce, October mein Effective(3 mahine gap, same saal 1905), 1911 mein Cancel(6 saal baad, alag\nViceroy) — teen stage: \"ghoshna→lagu→radd\", teen alag dates ek hi event ke.\nCurzon ne kiya, Hardinge II ne khatam kiya — do alag Viceroy, is symmetry ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBengal Partition: Announced(19 Jul 1905)→Effective(16 Oct 1905)→Cancelled(1911,Hardinge II) — teen alag dates,\nCurzon ne partition kiya par Hardinge II ne cancel kiya.\n2. 16 October 1905 — Ek Din, Do Ulti Reactions\n●Day of Mourning(shok) — poore Bengal mein\n●Rakhi Day(unity) — Rabindranath Tagore ke kehne par\n TRICK — \"Shok + Rakhi, same din\" trick\n💡\nEk hi din DONO opposite emotions manaye gaye — dukh(mourning) AUR ekta(rakhi) SAATH-SAATH — is\nunique double-reaction ko yaad rakho, ye chapter ka most-asked \"same day\" fact hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n16 October 1905 ko EK HI DIN Day of Mourning(shok) AUR Rakhi Day(Tagore ke kehne par unity) DONO manaye\ngaye.\n3. Mitra Mela(1899) → Abhinav Bharat(1904) — EK HI Organization\n●Mitra Mela(1899,Savarkar) ka naam 1904 mein badalkar Abhinav Bharat kar diya gaya\n●Inspiration: Mazzini ki \"Young Italy\"\n TRICK — \"Naam badla, organization wahi\" trick\n💡\n2 ALAG organizations NAHI hain — sirf EK hi hai jiska naam 5 saal baad badla. \"Mitra(dost) se Abhinav(naya)\nban gaya\" — dosti se naya-Bharat tak ka safar, ek hi group.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMitra Mela(1899) aur Abhinav Bharat(1904) DO ALAG organizations NAHI hain — Mitra Mela ka hi naam badla\ngaya, ek hi group hai(Savarkar brothers).\n4. Anushilan Samiti vs Dhaka Anushilan Samiti — Founder Alag\n●Anushilan Samiti(1902,Calcutta) = P. Mitra(Pramathanath Mitra) — \"Blood for Blood\"\n●Dhaka Anushilan Samiti(1905,Dhaka) = Pulin Das(P.Mitra se inspired, par SEPARATE branch, ~500 sub-branches)\n TRICK — \"Mitra=Calcutta, Das=Dhaka\" trick\n💡\nMitra-Calcutta(pehla,1902), Das-Dhaka(baad mein,1905, inspired-by-Mitra par SEPARATE) — M-C aur D-D dono\npairs first-letter match karte hain, isse yaad rakho."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAnushilan Samiti(1902,Calcutta)=P.Mitra. Dhaka Anushilan Samiti(1905,Dhaka)=Pulin Das(inspired by Mitra, par\nseparate organization,~500 branches) — founders confuse mat karo.\n5. Muzaffarpur Bomb Case(1908) — Target ≠ Victim\n●Target: D.H. Kingsford(Judge) — par bomb GALTI SE Kennedy ki gaadi par gira, Kingsford BACH GAYA\n●Khudiram Bose: arrest+phaansi(11 Aug 1908, ~18 saal, youngest hanged revolutionary)\n●Prafulla Chaki: pakde jaane se pehle khud ko goli maar li(suicide)\n TRICK — \"Target-Kingsford, Victim-Kennedy\" trick\n💡\nAsli TARGET Kingsford tha, par galti se KENNEDY ki gaadi pe bomb gira — Kingsford is ghatna mein BACH\nGAYA. \"Kingsford Khatam nahi hua, Kennedy ki gaadi mein hui ghalti\" — dono \"K\" naam se confuse hota hai, target-\nvictim alag rakho.\nKhudiram = phaansi(caught+executed), Chaki = suicide(khud maara) — do alag ends, do alag revolutionaries.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuzaffarpur Bomb Case: TARGET=Kingsford(Judge), par bomb galti se KENNEDY ki gaadi par gira — Kingsford\nbach gaya. Khudiram Bose=phaansi. Prafulla Chaki=suicide.\n6. Nasik Conspiracy(1909) vs Alipore Conspiracy(1908)\n●Nasik(1909): Jackson(Magistrate) ki hatya → Anant Laxman Kanhere(shooter, phaansi 1911) → Savarkar ko Kaala\nPani\n●Alipore(1908): 34 arrested, approver Narendra Gosain ko jail mein Kanailal Dutt+Satyendranath Bose ne maara ·\nAurobindo Ghosh acquitted → sanyas\n TRICK — \"Nasik-Jackson, Alipore-Gosain\" trick\n💡\nNasik = ek naya victim(Jackson), Alipore = andar hi ek TRAITOR maara gaya(Gosain, approver) — Nasik mein\nbahar ke officer ki hatya, Alipore mein jail ke ANDAR apne hi group ke traitor ki hatya. Bilkul alag nature ke cases.\nAlipore ke baad Aurobindo ne SANYAS liya(spiritual life, Puducherry Ashram-1926, Karmayogin-1909 newspaper)\n— is life-transformation ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNasik Conspiracy(1909)=Jackson ki hatya(Kanhere). Alipore Conspiracy(1908)=34 arrests, approver Gosain jail mein\nmaara gaya, Aurobindo Ghosh acquitted — dono ALAG cases.\n7. Revolutionaries Abroad — Country-Wise Match\n●India House(London,1905) = Shyamji Krishna Varma · Madan Lal Dhingra ne yahin se inspire hoke Curzon Wyllie\nko maara(1909)\n●Paris India Society(1905) = Madam Bhikaji Cama+S.R.Rana · Stuttgart(1907) mein PEHLA Tricolour fehraya\n●Ghadar Party(1913,San Francisco) = Founder Lala Hardayal, President Sohan Singh Bhakna(ALAG log)\n TRICK — \"London-Varma, Paris-Cama, Ghadar-2roles\" trick\n💡\n3 alag desh, 3 alag founder: London=Varma, Paris=Cama, USA=Hardayal(founder)+Bhakna(president) — USA\nwale mein DO log hain(founder≠president), baaki dono mein ek-ek.\nMadam Cama = \"Mother of Indian Revolution\" — Stuttgart mein Tiranga fehrane wali PEHLI, is \"first\" ko yaad\nrakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGhadar Party(1913,San Francisco): Founder=Lala Hardayal. President=Sohan Singh Bhakna — DO ALAG log, exam\nmein swap karke poochha jaata hai."," 8. Home Rule Leagues — Bombay City Ka Trap\n●Tilak's League(Apr 1916,Pune) = President Joseph Baptista · Area: Karnataka+CP+Berar+Maharashtra EXCEPT\nBombay City\n●Besant's League(Sep 1916,Madras/Adyar) = Secretary George Arundale · Area: Rest of India INCLUDING Bombay\nCity\n TRICK — \"Tilak-NO Bombay, Besant-YES Bombay\" trick\n💡\nTilak Maharashtra ka hi leader tha, phir bhi BOMBAY CITY uske area mein NAHI thi — ye counter-intuitive\nfact hai isliye SABSE COMMON trap hai. Yaad rakho: \"Apne hi ghar(Maharashtra) mein Tilak ko Bombay City\nnahi mili, Besant(Madras se) ko mil gayi\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBombay City = Annie Besant's League ke area mein aati thi(Tilak's League mein NAHI, chahe Tilak khud Maharashtra\nka tha) — ye sabse common exam trap hai.\n9. Delhi Durbar(1911) — Announcement ≠ Official Shift\n●12 Dec 1911 = King George V welcome + Partition CANCEL + Capital-shift ANNOUNCEMENT(Lord Hardinge II)\n●Delhi OFFICIALLY capital = 1912(agle saal)\n TRICK — \"1911-Announce, 1912-Official\" trick\n💡\n1 saal ka gap: 1911 mein sirf GHOSHNA hui, 1912 mein ASLI/OFFICIAL shift hui — \"pehle bola gaya, agle saal hua\"\n— is 1-year-gap ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDelhi capital-shift ki ANNOUNCEMENT 1911(Delhi Durbar) mein hui, par Delhi OFFICIALLY capital 1912 mein\nbani — 1911 ko hi \"official\" mat samajhna.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"BengalPartition: 19Jul(announce)-16Oct(effective,mourning+rakhi)-1911(cancel,Hardinge) →\nMitraMela1899→AbhinavBharat1904(same org) → AnushilanSamiti(1902,Mitra,Calcutta) vs\nDhakaAnushilan(1905,PulinDas) → Muzaffarpur: target-Kingsford,hit-Kennedy,Khudiram-hanged,Chaki-suicide →\nNasik(1909,Jackson,Kanhere) vs Alipore(1908,34arrested,Gosain-killed,Aurobindo-acquitted) → Abroad: London-\nShyamjiVarma,Paris-MadamCama(Stuttgart1907),Ghadar-Hardayal(founder)/Bhakna(president) → HomeRule:\nTilak(Pune,NO-Bombay) vs Besant(Madras,YES-Bombay) → DelhiDurbar1911(announce)→1912(official)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bombay City = Besant's League mein(Tilak's League mein NAHI, chahe Tilak Maharashtra ka tha).\n2) Muzaffarpur: target Kingsford tha, bomb galti se Kennedy ki gaadi pe gira.\n3) Ghadar Party: Founder=Hardayal, President=Sohan Singh Bhakna — do alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Indian National Movement"," GANDHIAN ERA — FIRST PHASE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 9 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Early Satyagrahas — Har Ek Ka Apna \"First\"\n●Champaran(1917,Bihar) = 1st Civil Disobedience · Bulaya Rajkumar Shukla(sirf bulane wala,leader NAHI) ne\n●Ahmedabad(1918) = 1st Hunger Strike · Plague Bonus issue · 35% bonus mila\n●Kheda(1918,Gujarat) = 1st Asahyog(Non-cooperation) PRAYOG(experiment) · Patel ne bulaya\n TRICK — \"3 Firsts, 3 Alag Weapons\" trick\n💡\nChamparan = Disobedience(seedha inkaar), Ahmedabad = Hunger Strike(khud ko bhookha rakhna), Kheda =\nNon-cooperation(saath na dena) — teen alag \"weapon\", teen alag \"1st\" — bas yaad rakho ye TEENO alag category ke\n\"pehle\" hain, ek dusre se overlap nahi karte.\nRajkumar Shukla = SIRF BULANE WALA tha, team leader nahi(team = Rajendra Prasad+Kripalani+Mahadev\nDesai) — is role-distinction ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChamparan=1st Civil Disobedience. Ahmedabad=1st Hunger Strike. Kheda=1st Non-cooperation experiment — teeno\nalag \"firsts\", mix mat karo. Rajkumar Shukla sirf Gandhi ko BULANE wala tha, team-leader nahi.\n2. \"Mahatma\" Title & Indian Women's Association — Alag-Alag Log\n●\"Mahatma\" title = Rabindranath Tagore(post-Champaran) ne diya — Gokhale NAHI(wo political GURU the, title-\ngiver nahi)\n●Indian Women's Association(1917) = Annie Besant + Margaret Cousins ne banayi — Gandhi NAHI(1917 hone se\nconfuse hota hai, kyunki Champaran bhi 1917 hai)\n TRICK — \"1917 mein 2 alag events\" trick\n💡\n1917 saal mein DO alag cheezein hui: Champaran-safalta(Gandhi) → Mahatma title(Tagore) AUR Indian Women's\nAssociation(Besant) — same year hai isliye confuse hota hai, par teeno alag log/events. \"Same saal, alag kahaniyan\"\nyaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Mahatma\" title = Tagore ne diya(Gokhale nahi). Indian Women's Association(1917) = Annie Besant+Margaret Cousins\nne banayi(Gandhi nahi) — dono common galtiyaan hain.\n3. Rowlatt Act(1919) — Resignations Kahan Se?\n●\"Black Act\" · Slogan \"No Dalil, No Vakil, No Appeal\" · Committee Sidney Rowlatt(1917 bani)\n●Resignations: Malaviya+Mazharul Haq+Jinnah ne CENTRAL LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's Council\nSE NAHI\n TRICK — \"Legislature≠Council\" trick\n💡\nYe 3 leaders ne Central LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's COUNCIL se(jo baad mein Shankaran Nair ne\nkiya, Jallianwala ke context mein) confuse mat karo. Rowlatt = Legislature, Jallianwala = Council — do alag protests,\ndo alag bodies.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRowlatt Act ke against Malaviya+Mazharul Haq+Jinnah ne CENTRAL LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's\nExecutive COUNCIL se NAHI (wo Shankaran Nair ne, Jallianwala Bagh ke against)."," 4. Jallianwala Bagh — 3 Alag Reactions(MOST IMPORTANT)\n●Rabindranath Tagore = Knighthood(\"Sir\") LAUTAYI\n●Mahatma Gandhi = \"Kaiser-i-Hind\" title SURRENDER kiya\n●Shankaran Nair = Viceroy's Executive COUNCIL se RESIGN kiya\n TRICK — \"3 log, 3 alag protest-style\" trick\n💡\nTagore = TITLE(Knighthood) lautayi(honorary British title), Gandhi = TITLE(Kaiser-i-Hind) surrender\nkiya(WWI ke liye mila tha), Nair = POSITION(Council seat) chhodi(active role tha) — teeno alag TAREEKE se\nprotest kiya: 2 ne title choda, 1 ne position choda. Source khud isse \"MOST IMPORTANT MCQ\" bolta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJallianwala Bagh ke baad: Tagore=Knighthood lautayi. Gandhi=Kaiser-i-Hind surrender kiya. Shankaran Nair=Viceroy's\nExecutive Council se resign kiya — teeno alag reactions, exam ka MOST IMPORTANT MCQ.\n5. Khilafat Movement — Start Aur End\n●All India Khilafat Conference(Nov 1919,Delhi) — President GANDHI(Hindu-Muslim unity ka \"sunehra mauka\")\n●Khilafat Day: 31 Aug 1920\n●End(1924): Mustafa Kemal Pasha ne Turkey mein reforms laaye(Caliphate abolish) → movement khud-ba-khud\nkhatam\n TRICK — \"Turkey ke andar ka reform, India ke movement ka end\" trick\n💡\nKhilafat Movement ISLIYE khatam hui kyunki TURKEY KHUD ne apna Caliphate system hata diya — jis cheez ke\nliye India mein movement chal rahi thi, wahi cheez Turkey ne khud khatam kar di. \"Jis Khalifa ko bachana tha,\nTurkey ne khud usko hata diya\" — is irony se end-reason yaad rakho.\n6. NCM — 2 Sessions, C.R. Das Ka U-Turn\n●Calcutta Special Session(Sep 1920): President Lala Lajpat Rai · C.R.Das = OPPOSE(proposal narrowly pass hua)\n●Nagpur Session(Dec 1920): President C.Vijayaraghavachariar · C.R.Das = KHUD move kiya(SUPPORT) → 15-\nmember CWC bani\n TRICK — \"Calcutta-Na, Nagpur-Haan\" trick\n💡\nC.R. Das ne 180-degree U-TURN liya: Calcutta mein \"NA\"(oppose) → Nagpur mein \"HAAN\"(khud propose) — 3\nmahine mein poora ulta stance, isliye ye TRAP-05 hai source mein bhi. \"Calcutta = Cold(opposed), Nagpur = New-\nmind(supported)\" — C-cold, N-new dono \"C/N\" se.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nC.R. Das ne Calcutta Session(1920) mein NCM proposal OPPOSE kiya, par Nagpur Session(1920) mein KHUD move\nkiya(support) — same saal, alag sessions, alag stance.\n7. NCM Start(1 Aug 1920) = Tilak Death — SAME DIN\n●1 August 1920 SUBAH: Tilak ki death → usi din NCM shuru hui\n●Tilak Swaraj Fund(1921): 6 mahine mein 1 Crore rupaye jama\n TRICK — \"Ek yug khatam, doosra shuru\" trick\n💡\nJis din \"Lal-Bal-Pal\" ke Tilak(Extremist era) ki maut hui, usi din Gandhi ka NCM(Mass Movement era) shuru\nhua — jaise ek era doosre ko baton pass kar raha ho, symbolically bhi perfect coincidence hai isliye exam mein bahut\npoocha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1 August 1920 = NCM start date AUR Tilak death date, DONO SAME DIN — ye coincidence bahut common exam\nquestion hai."," 8. Chauri-Chaura(4 Feb 1922) → Bardoli Resolution(12 Feb 1922)\n●Chauri-Chaura(Gorakhpur,UP): bheed ne police station mein aag lagayi → 22 policemen zinda jal gaye\n●Bardoli Resolution(12 Feb): NCM SUSPEND — sirf 8 din baad\n●Gandhi's quote: \"Himalayan Blunder\" · Bose's quote: \"National Calamity\"\n TRICK — \"Gandhi vs Bose\" contrasting-quote trick\n💡\nGandhi(jisne decision liya) = apni hi galti maani(\"Himalayan Blunder\" — khud ki galti). Bose(jo disagree tha) =\nmovement wapas lene ko hi galti bola(\"National Calamity\" — Gandhi ke decision ki criticism). Dono\n\"blunder/calamity\" negative words hain, par POINT OF VIEW alag: Gandhi apne upar, Bose Gandhi ke decision par.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Himalayan Blunder\" = Gandhi ne khud NCM wapas lene ke context mein apni galti maani. \"National Calamity\" =\nSubhash Chandra Bose ne NCM wapas lene ko criticize karte hue kaha — dono alag log, alag angle.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Gandhi India-wapas(9Jan1915) → 3 Satyagrahas: Champaran(1917,1stCivilDisobedience,Shukla-bulaya)-\nAhmedabad(1918,1stHungerStrike)-Kheda(1918,1stAsahyog) → Mahatma-title=Tagore(not Gokhale),\nIndianWomensAssoc=Besant(not Gandhi) → RowlattAct(1919,BlackAct): Malaviya+MazharulHaq+Jinnah resign-\nLEGISLATURE → JallianwalaBagh(13Apr1919): Tagore-Knighthood,Gandhi-KaiserIHind,ShankaranNair-\nCOUNCIL(3 alag) → Khilafat(Nov1919-Gandhi president,end1924-MustafaKemalPasha) → NCM:\nCalcuttaSession(Das-oppose)→NagpurSession(Das-support,CWC) → NCMstart(1Aug1920)=TilakDeath(same din) →\nChauriChaura(4Feb1922,22police)→BardoliResolution(12Feb1922) →\nGandhi='HimalayanBlunder',Bose='NationalCalamity'\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Jallianwala reactions: Tagore=Knighthood, Gandhi=Kaiser-i-Hind, Shankaran Nair=Council — MOST\nIMPORTANT MCQ.\n2) C.R. Das: Calcutta Session=oppose, Nagpur Session=support — U-turn same saal mein.\n3) \"Mahatma\" title=Tagore(not Gokhale). \"Himalayan Blunder\"=Gandhi, \"National Calamity\"=Bose.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Gandhian Era — First Phase"," PHASE OF NATIONAL POLITICS (1922–29) — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nModern History · Chapter 10 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Swaraj Party — No-Changers vs Pro-Changers\n●No-Changers: Rajagopalachari+Vallabhbhai Patel → Constructive work(schools,ashrams), council-entry ke KHILAF\n●Pro-Changers/Swarajists: C.R.Das(President)+Motilal Nehru(Secretary) → Council mein GHUSKE obstruct karna\n●Founded Jan 1923, Prayagraj · Earlier naam: Congress-Khilafat Swaraj Party\n TRICK — \"No=Bahar, Pro=Andar\" trick\n💡\nNo-Changers = \"NO to council\"(bahar rehke kaam karo, ashram/school). Pro-Changers = \"PRO council-\nentry\"(andar ghuso, obstruct karo) — naam mein hi seedha \"haan/na\" chhupa hai council-entry ke liye.\n2. Vitthalbhai vs Vallabhbhai Patel — 2 Bhai, 2 Alag Kaam\n●Vitthalbhai Patel(BADE bhai) = 1925, Speaker/President of Central Legislative Assembly(Swarajists ki sabse badi\njeet)\n●Vallabhbhai Patel(CHOTE bhai) = \"Sardar\" — Bardoli Satyagraha, No-Changer\n TRICK — \"Vit=Vidhan(Assembly), Val=Bardoli\" trick\n💡\nVitthalbhai = \"Vitthal jaisa BADA/senior naam\" → Assembly ka Speaker(bada legislative role). Vallabhbhai =\n\"Valiant Bardoli warrior\" → grassroots movement(Sardar title). Dono bhai hain, naam bhi milte-julte(Vit vs Val) —\nisliye SABSE COMMON trap, roles se differentiate karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVitthalbhai Patel(bade bhai) = 1925 mein Speaker of Central Legislative Assembly. Vallabhbhai Patel(chote bhai) =\n\"Sardar\", Bardoli Satyagraha — dono bhai, roles bilkul alag.\n3. AITUC(1920) vs INTUC(1947) — Alag Union, Alag President\n●AITUC(1920): 1st President Lala Lajpat Rai · Split 1929(Nagpur,Nehru presided)\n●INTUC(May 1947): Founders Vallabhbhai Patel+V.V.Giri · 1st President Vallabhbhai Patel\n TRICK — \"AITUC-Lala, INTUC-Vallabhbhai\" trick\n💡\n27 saal ka gap(1920→1947) — AITUC = Lala Lajpat Rai(purana, pre-independence union), INTUC = Vallabhbhai\nPatel(naya, independence ke around ka union) — do alag unions, do alag \"1st President\", mix mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAITUC(1920) 1st President=Lala Lajpat Rai. INTUC(1947) 1st President=Vallabhbhai Patel — dono ALAG trade\nunions hain.\n4. CPI — 2 Formation Dates(\"Dates Ka Jhol\")\n●Abroad(Tashkent,Uzbekistan): 17 Oct 1920 · M.N.Roy\n●India mein(Kanpur): 26 Dec 1925 · Satyabhakta(presided)\n TRICK — \"Where dekho, date decide hogi\" trick\n💡\nSawaal ka wording padho: \"bahar/abroad\" → 1920,Tashkent,Roy. \"India mein\" → 1925,Kanpur,Satyabhakta. 5 saal\nka gap, do alag jagah — location-keyword hi answer decide karta hai."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCPI abroad(Tashkent) = 17 Oct 1920, M.N.Roy. CPI India mein(Kanpur) = 26 Dec 1925, Satyabhakta — sawaal ka\n\"where\" dekho, wahi date decide karega.\n5. HRA → HSRA — Naam Badla, \"Socialist\" Add Hua\n●HRA(1924,Kanpur) = Sachindranath Sanyal · Objective: Armed Revolution, Federal Republic\n●HSRA(10 Dec 1928,Feroz Shah Kotla,Delhi) = Azad+Bhagat Singh · \"Socialist\" add hua\n TRICK — \"4-saal-baad Socialist add\" trick\n💡\nHRA se HSRA — EK HI organization ka EVOLUTION(naam badla), 2 alag groups NAHI — jaise Mitra\nMela→Abhinav Bharat pattern(Ch.8 se). \"Hindustan Republican(1924) → Hindustan SocialistRepublican(1928)**\" —\nbas beech mein \"Socialist\" add hua, 4 saal baad.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHRA(1924,Sanyal,Kanpur) aur HSRA(1928,Azad+Bhagat,Delhi) DO ALAG organizations NAHI — HRA ka hi naam\nbadalkar HSRA bana, \"Socialist\" word add hua.\n6. Saunders Assassination(17 Dec 1928) — Target ≠ Victim\n●Lala Lajpat Rai ki death(17 Nov 1928) — James Scott ke lathi-charge se\n●Asal TARGET = James Scott, par galti se John Saunders(Assistant SP) MAARA GAYA\n●Revolutionaries: Bhagat Singh+Azad+Rajguru\n TRICK — \"Scott-target, Saunders-victim\" trick(same pattern as Muzaffarpur)\n💡\nYe BILKUL WAHI PATTERN hai jo Muzaffarpur Bomb Case(Ch.8) mein tha — \"target ek(Kingsford/Scott), maara\ndoosra(Kennedy/Saunders)\" — dono chapters mein mistaken-identity ka fact hai, cross-verify karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSaunders assassination: ASAL TARGET James Scott tha(Lalaji ke lathi-charge order dene wala), par galti se John\nSaunders maara gaya.\n7. Assembly Bomb(8 Apr 1929) — 2 Bills, Ek Nahi\n●Bhagat Singh+Batukeshwar Dutt → Public Safety Bill + Trade Disputes Bill DONO ke against\n●Intention: \"To make the deaf hear\" — kisi ko maarna nahi tha\n TRICK — \"2 bills\" trick\n💡\nDO Bills tha protest ka reason, sirf ek mat batana — \"Public Safety AUR Trade Disputes, dono ek saath\" — jaise\nMoplah ke 3 causes(Ancient/Modern cross-pattern), yahan bhi COMPLETENESS zaroori hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAssembly Bomb Incident(1929) ka protest DO bills ke against tha: Public Safety Bill + Trade Disputes Bill — sirf ek\nbatana incomplete hai.\n8. 3 Alag Martyrdom Dates — Confuse Mat Ho\n●Jatin Das: 64-din hunger strike → death 13 Sep 1929\n●Chandrashekhar Azad: 27 Feb 1931, Alfred Park(Prayagraj) → khud ko goli mari, PHAANSI NAHI hui\n●Bhagat Singh+Sukhdev+Rajguru: 23 March 1931(Shaheed Diwas) → PHAANSI hui\n TRICK — \"3 alag deaths, 3 alag tareeke\" trick\n💡"," Jatin Das = BHOOKH se(hunger strike,Sep1929), Azad = KHUD GOLI mari(Feb1931,phaansi NAHI), Bhagat-\nSukhdev-Rajguru = PHAANSI(Mar1931) — teen alag deaths, teen alag tareeke, teen alag mahine — is\nsequence(Sep→Feb→Mar) ko yaad rakho.\nAzad AUR Shaheed-Diwas-trio dono 1931 mein hain, par SIRF EK MAHINE ka gap(27Feb→23Mar) — Azad\nthodi der pehle mara, phir baaki teen ki phaansi hui.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChandrashekhar Azad(27 Feb 1931) ne KHUD ko goli mari, unhe PHAANSI NAHI hui — Shaheed Diwas(23 Mar\n1931,Bhagat Singh+Sukhdev+Rajguru) mein PHAANSI hui. Do alag tareeke, ek mahine ka gap.\n9. Journals — Bande Mataram ≠ New India\n●Bande Mataram = Bipin Chandra Pal\n●New India = Annie Besant(alag journal, alag vyakti)\n●Bandi Jivan = Sanyal ki book, \"Bible of Revolutionaries\"\n TRICK — \"Bande vs New\" trick\n💡\nBande Mataram(purana/nationalist slogan-jaisa naam) = Bipin Pal, New India(\"new\" word hi modern-sounding)\n= Annie Besant — naam ke \"feel\" se hi authors alag pakad lo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBande Mataram(journal) = Bipin Chandra Pal ka hai. New India = Annie Besant ka hai — dono alag journals, exam\nmein swap karke poochha jaata hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Gaya1922(CRDas proposal reject)→SwarajParty(Jan1923,Prayagraj,Das-President/MotilalNehru-Secretary) → No-\nChangers(Rajagopalachari+Vallabhbhai) vs Pro-Changers(Das+MotilalNehru) → Vitthalbhai(1925,Speaker) vs\nVallabhbhai(Sardar,Bardoli) → AITUC1920(LalaLajpatRai) vs INTUC1947(VallabhbhaiPatel) → CPI:\nTashkent1920(Roy) vs Kanpur1925(Satyabhakta) → HRA1924(Sanyal)→HSRA1928(Azad+Bhagat,renamed) →\nSaunders(17Dec1928,target-Scott,killed-Saunders) → AssemblyBomb(8Apr1929,2bills) →\nJatinDas(13Sep1929,64days) → Azad(27Feb1931,self-shot) → ShaheedDiwas(23Mar1931,Bhagat-Sukhdev-Rajguru)\n→ BandeMataram-BipinPal vs NewIndia-Besant\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Vitthalbhai(1925,Speaker CLA) vs Vallabhbhai(Sardar,Bardoli) — do bhai, alag roles.\n2) Azad(27Feb1931,khud goli mari,phaansi nahi) ≠ Bhagat-Sukhdev-Rajguru(23Mar1931,phaansi hui,Shaheed Diwas).\n3) CPI: Tashkent(1920,abroad,Roy) vs Kanpur(1925,India,Satyabhakta) — sawaal ka \"where\" dekho.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Phase of National Politics (1922-29)"," GANDHIAN ERA — SECOND PHASE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 11 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Simon Commission — Poori TARAH British\n●7 members, SAARE British(koi Indian nahi) · Appointed Lord Birkenhead · Chairman Sir John Simon\n●Madras Session(27 Dec 1927): President M.A. Ansari(Nehru NAHI) → complete boycott decision\n TRICK — \"7-British, Ansari-not-Nehru\" trick\n💡\nSimon Commission mein EK BHI Indian nahi tha — isliye \"Simon Go Back\" naara laga. Madras Session ka\npresident ANSARI tha, chahe Nehru active role mein tha — \"active-hona\" aur \"president-hona\" alag baatein hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCongress Madras Session(1927) ka president M.A. Ansari tha — Jawaharlal Nehru NAHI(wo active tha par president\nnahi).\n2. Nehru Report(1928) — Motilal, NOT Jawaharlal\n●Chairman = MOTILAL Nehru(baap) — Jawaharlal ka NAHI\n●Muslim League(Jinnah) ne REJECT kiya → Jinnah ne apni \"14 Points\" di\n TRICK — \"Baap ki report\" trick\n💡\nYe BILKUL WAHI PATTERN hai jo \"The Independent\" journal(Ch.6) mein tha — \"Motilal(baap) = famous cheez ka\ncredit, Jawaharlal(beta) nahi\" — dono cross-chapter examples yaad rakho, ek hi family-trap pattern.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNehru Report(1928) = MOTILAL Nehru(chairman), Jawaharlal Nehru NAHI — baap-bete dono famous hain, alag karo.\n3. Dandi March — 3 Alag Dates\n●12 March 1930: START(Sabarmati Ashram, 78 followers)\n●5 April 1930: Dandi PAHUNCHE(24 din baad)\n●6 April 1930: Namak todkar CDM officially START\n TRICK — \"Start-Reach-Break\" 3-stage trick\n💡\n24 din CHALNA(12Mar→5Apr) → ek din baad KANOON TODNA(6Apr) — teen alag stages: safar-shuru →\nmanzil-pahuncho → kaam-karo(namak todo). \"Chalna, Pahunchna, Todna\" — teen alag verbs, teen alag dates.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDandi March START=12 March 1930. Dandi ARRIVAL=5 April 1930. CDM OFFICIALLY START(namak todkar)=6\nApril 1930 — teen alag dates, mix mat karo.\n4. 3 Round Table Conferences — Congress Ki Attendance\n●1st RTC(1930-31): Congress ABSENT\n●2nd RTC(1931): Gandhi(SOLE rep) · Churchill quote(\"half-naked Fakir\") ISI RTC mein\n●3rd RTC(1932): Congress BOYCOTTED\n●Ambedkar = SIRF EK VYAKTI jo TEENO RTC mein tha\n TRICK — \"Absent-Solo-Boycott\" progression trick\n💡\nCongress ka pattern: 1st=bilkul GAYAB(absent), 2nd=SIRF EK aadmi(Gandhi solo), 3rd=JAAN-BOOJHKAR"," nahi gaye(boycott) — teen alag \"nahi-hone\" ke tareeke. Ambedkar hi EKLAUTA CONSTANT tha — teeno mein\npresent, is uniqueness ko yaad rakho.\nChurchill ka quote SIRF 2nd RTC ke context mein tha — jab Gandhi khud gaye the(kyunki tabhi Churchill ne unhe\ndekha/criticize kiya).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st RTC=Congress Absent. 2nd RTC=Gandhi(sole rep) — Churchill's \"half-naked Fakir\" quote ISI RTC mein. 3rd\nRTC=Congress Boycotted. Ambedkar=teeno mein present, ekmatra vyakti.\n5. Communal Award(1932) → Poona Pact(1932)\n●Communal Award(16 Aug 1932,Ramsay MacDonald): Separate Electorate —\nMuslims+Sikhs+Christians+Europeans+Anglo-Indians AUR Harijans BHI(crucial addition)\n●Gandhi's fast(20 Sep 1932,Yerwada Jail) → Poona Pact(24 Sep 1932)\n●Signatories: Ambedkar(Depressed Classes) + Malaviya(Gandhi/Upper Caste) — Gandhi khud SIGN NAHI kiya\n●Result: Separate Electorate for Depressed Classes ABOLISH · Reserved seats 71→148\n TRICK — \"Harijan-crucial-add\" + \"Gandhi-nahi-signed\" trick\n💡\nCommunal Award mein Harijans ka add hona hi Gandhi ko FAST pe le gaya — baaki groups(Muslim,Sikh etc) se\nGandhi ko utna farq nahi pada, par HARIJAN wala part unhe UNACCEPTABLE laga.\nPoona Pact khud Gandhi ne SIGN NAHI kiya — Malaviya ne unki taraf se sign kiya(Ambedkar ne apni taraf se) —\nye ek IMPORTANT detail hai jo exam mein poochha jaata hai: \"Gandhi + Ambedkar\" bolna technically thoda galat hai,\nactual signers Malaviya+Ambedkar the.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPoona Pact ke actual SIGNATORIES = Ambedkar(Depressed Classes) + Malaviya(Gandhi ki taraf se) — Gandhi khud\nsign NAHI kiya. Communal Award mein Harijans bhi shamil the — yehi crucial addition thi jispe Gandhi fast pe gaye.\n6. 1937 Elections & Tripuri Crisis(1939)\n●Feb 1937 elections: Congress 8/11 provinces jeeti(Chief Minister tenure 28 mahine)\n●Haripura(1938): Bose UNOPPOSED president\n●Tripuri(1939): Bose ne Gandhi ke candidate Pattabhi Sitaramayya ko HARAYA → \"Sitaramayya's defeat is MY\ndefeat\"(Gandhi) → deadlock → Bose RESIGN → successor Rajendra Prasad\n●National Planning Committee(1938): Chairman NEHRU(Bose Congress President tha us waqt, par committee-head\nNehru)\n●Forward Bloc(3 May 1939) = Bose ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Bose jeeta par resign kiya\" + \"Nehru-not-Bose\" trick\n💡\nBose Tripuri mein JEETA, phir bhi RESIGN kiya(deadlock ki wajah se) — counter-intuitive: jeetne wala hi haar\nmaan gaya. \"Jeet ke bhi haar mani\" yaad rakho.\nNational Planning Committee = NEHRU-chairman, jabki BOSE us waqt Congress PRESIDENT tha — is\nmismatch(president ≠ committee-head) ko alag se yaad rakho, exam directly poochta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNational Planning Committee(1938) ka Chairman=Jawaharlal Nehru — Congress President us waqt Subhash Chandra\nBose tha, par committee-head Nehru the.\n7. Congress Socialist Party(1934) — President vs Secretary\n●President = Acharya Narendra Dev · General Secretary = Jayprakash Narayan(JP) · Founders: JP+Narendra\nDev+Lohia\n●Bihar Socialist Party(1931) = JP — ye CSP(1934) se PEHLE bani thi"," TRICK — \"Dev=President, JP=Secretary\" trick\n💡\nNarendra Dev = President(N-D-P, teeno mein koi direct link nahi par bas ratt lo: Dev=top role). JP =\nSecretary(operational role) — dono roles yaad rakho, exam swap karke poochta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCongress Socialist Party(1934): President=Acharya Narendra Dev. General Secretary=Jayprakash Narayan — role swap\nmat karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"SimonCommission(7-British,Birkenhead,JohnSimon) → MadrasSession1927(Ansari,not Nehru) →\nNehruReport1928(Motilal,not Jawaharlal)→Jinnah's14Points →\nLahoreSession1929(Nehru,PurnaSwaraj)→26Jan1930(1stIndependenceDay) → DandiMarch:\n12Mar(start)-5Apr(reach)-6Apr(CDM-officially) → 3RTCs: 1st-Absent,2nd-Gandhi(sole,Churchill-quote),3rd-\nBoycott,Ambedkar-all3 → GandhiIrwinPact(5Mar1931)→2ndRTC →\nCommunalAward(16Aug1932,+Harijans)→Gandhi-fast(20Sep)→PoonaPact(24Sep,Ambedkar+Malaviya-\nsigned,71→148) → GOIAct1935 → 1937elections(8/11)→Haripura1938(Bose-unopposed)→Tripuri1939(Bose beats\nPattabhi,resigns,RajendraPrasad-successor) → NationalPlanningCommittee=Nehru(not Bose) →\nForwardBloc(3May1939) → CSP1934(Dev-President,JP-Secretary)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGHEST-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai poore Modern History mein.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) 3 RTCs: 1st=Absent, 2nd=Gandhi(sole,Churchill quote isi mein), 3rd=Boycott. Ambedkar=teeno mein.\n2) Poona Pact signatories=Ambedkar+Malaviya — Gandhi khud sign NAHI kiya.\n3) National Planning Committee(1938) Chairman=Nehru, jabki Congress President us waqt Bose tha.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Gandhian Era — Second Phase"," TOWARDS INDEPENDENCE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 12 (Final Chapter, Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Pakistan Demand — 3 Alag Log, 3 Alag Stage\n●Idea(1930): Muhammad Iqbal(Allahabad Session) — alag nation ka suggestion\n●Naam \"Pakistan\"(1933): Choudhary Rahmat Ali ne rakha\n●Official Demand(23 Mar 1940,Lahore): Jinnah(Muslim League)\n TRICK — \"Idea-Naam-Demand\" 3-person trick\n💡\nIqbal(Idea,1930) → Rahmat Ali(Rakha naam,1933) → Jinnah(Jor se demand,1940) = \"I-R-J\" chronologically — teen\nalag log, teen alag role: soch(idea), naam(naming), aur formal maang(demand).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPakistan: Idea=Iqbal(1930). Naam=Rahmat Ali(1933). Official Demand=Jinnah(1940,Lahore) — teen alag log, ek\nsequence.\n2. Individual Satyagraha(1940) — Sequence Yaad Rakho\n●1st: Vinoba Bhave(17 Oct,Paunar Ashram) → 2nd: Jawaharlal Nehru → 3rd: Brahma Dutt(state exams mein\npoochha jaata hai)\n TRICK — \"V-N-B\" order trick\n💡\nVinoba → Nehru → Brahma Dutt = \"V-N-B\" — Vinoba SABSE PEHLE isliye kyunki wo Gandhi ke sabse\nvishwasi/spiritual follower the, phir bada naam(Nehru), phir teesra(Brahma Dutt, jo kam-famous hai isliye exam mein\nspecifically poochha jaata hai).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndividual Satyagraha sequence: 1st=Vinoba Bhave, 2nd=Jawaharlal Nehru, 3rd=Brahma Dutt — 3rd wala specifically\nstate exams mein poocha jaata hai.\n3. Cripps Mission(1942) — \"Post-Dated Cheque\"\n●Head: Stafford Cripps(sent by Churchill) · Offer: Dominion Status + Constituent Assembly(after war)\n●Opt-out Clause = SABSE BADA TRAP(states alag ho sakti thi) · Gandhi: \"Post-dated cheque on a failing bank\"\n TRICK — \"Cheque jo kabhi cash nahi hoga\" trick\n💡\nPost-dated cheque = wo cheque jo ABHI kaam nahi aata, future date pe hi chalega — aur bank khud DUB rahi\nhai(failing) — matlab Gandhi keh rahe the ki promise TOH mila hai, par jab tak wo poora hoga, tab tak British power hi\nkhatam ho chuki hogi. Is metaphor ko poora samjho, ye exam mein quote-based hi poocha jaata hai.\n4. Quit India Movement(1942) — Jail + Jagah Ka Trap\n●Launch: 8 Aug 1942, Gowalia Tank Maidan(aaj = August Kranti Maidan), Mumbai\n●Gandhi ki jail = AGHA KHAN PALACE, Pune — Yerwada NAHI(wo 1930 CDM mein tha)\n●Aruna Asaf Ali = Tiranga fehraya · Usha Mehta = Congress Radio(14 Aug)\n TRICK — \"1942≠1930 jail\" trick\n💡\n2 alag movements, 2 alag jail: 1930 CDM → Yerwada Jail, 1942 Quit India → Agha Khan Palace — dono \"Gandhi\nki jail\" se related hain isliye confuse hota hai, par 12 SAAL ka gap aur alag jail. \"Naya movement(1942), Nayi\njail(Agha Khan)\"."," EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nQuit India Movement(1942) mein Gandhi ki jail = Agha Khan Palace(Pune). Yerwada Jail = 1930 CDM mein tha —\ndono alag movements, alag jail.\n5. Parallel Governments — 3 Alag \"Sabse\"\n●Balia(UP,Chittu Pandey) = SABSE PEHLI\n●Satara(Maharashtra,Nana Patil) = SABSE LAMBI(1946 tak)\n●Tamluk(Bengal) = Vidyut Vahini(Armed Electric Force) + cyclone relief\n TRICK — \"Balia-First, Satara-Longest, Tamluk-Unique\" trick\n💡\nTeen alag superlatives: Balia=TIME-first, Satara=DURATION-longest, Tamluk=WORK-unique(cyclone-\nrelief+apni khud ki force) — teen alag dimension mein \"sabse\", mix mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBalia = sabse pehli parallel govt. Satara = sabse lambi(1946 tak). Tamluk = Vidyut Vahini + cyclone relief ke liye\nunique — teen alag facts.\n6. INA — Founder vs Supreme Commander\n●Founder: Captain Mohan Singh(1942, idea Rash Bihari Bose ka bhi tha)\n●Supreme Commander: Bose(July 1943 se) · Provisional Govt(21 Oct 1943,Singapore)\n●Rani Jhansi Regiment(Mahila) = Lakshmi Sehgal\n TRICK — \"Mohan Singh shuru kiya, Bose sambhala\" trick\n💡\nMohan Singh = FOUNDER(shuru kiya,1942), Bose = LEADER(baad mein sambhala,1943) — same pattern jo\nbaar-baar dikhi hai(founder vs real-power) — is bar bhi \"pehle wala shuru karta hai, bada naam baad mein aata hai\"\npattern hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nINA Founder=Captain Mohan Singh(1942). Supreme Commander=Bose(July 1943 se) — dono alag roles, alag time.\n7. Red Fort Trial(1945) — 3 Dharm, 1 Lawyer\n●3 Accused: Dhillon(Sikh) + Sehgal(Hindu) + Shahnawaz(Muslim) — unity symbol\n●Main Lawyer: Bhulabhai Desai(Nehru bhi tha, par lead Desai ne kiya)\n TRICK — \"3 dharm ek saath\" trick\n💡\nTeen accused teen alag dharm se(Sikh-Hindu-Muslim) — INA ki unity ko symbolize karta hai, is TRIO ko yaad rakho.\nBhulabhai Desai = MAIN lawyer, Nehru sirf sahayak tha.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRed Fort Trial(1945) main lawyer=Bhulabhai Desai(Nehru bhi tha par lead nahi kiya). 3 accused=Dhillon(Sikh)\n+Sehgal(Hindu)+Shahnawaz(Muslim).\n8. Cabinet Mission(1946) — \"LCA\" Code\n●Pethick Lawrence(Chairman) + Stafford Cripps + A.V.Alexander = \"LCA\"\n●Cripps DONO missions mein tha: 1942(Cripps Mission,head) + 1946(Cabinet Mission,member)\n●Pakistan alag NAHI accept ki — Loose Federation propose ki\n TRICK — \"Cripps = Double-Appearance\" trick\n💡"," Cripps 2 baar aaya(1942 mein khud head tha, 1946 mein sirf ek member) — is REPEAT-appearance ko yaad rakho,\nexam \"Cripps kis mission mein tha\" ambiguously poochta hai — jawab: DONO.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nStafford Cripps DONO missions mein tha: Cripps Mission(1942, khud HEAD) aur Cabinet Mission(1946, sirf ek\nMEMBER \"LCA\" mein) — dono confuse mat karo.\n9. Interim Govt(1946) & Independence Act — Key Dates\n●Liaqat Ali Khan(ML) = FINANCE portfolio — powerful ministry ek ML member ko, unusual isliye common trap\n●Independence Act 3 dates: Introduced(4 Jul 1947) → Passed/Royal Assent(18 Jul 1947) → Effective(15 Aug 1947)\n TRICK — \"Liaqat-Finance\" + \"4-18-15\" trick\n💡\nLiaqat Ali Khan(ML) ko FINANCE mila — is \"unusual power to opposition\" ko yaad rakho, exam specifically ye\ntrap try karta hai.\n4→18→15: Introduce(4 Jul) → Pass(18 Jul,2 hafte baad) → Effective(15 Aug,ek mahine baad) — teen stage, teen alag\ndates, GAP se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLiaqat Ali Khan(Muslim League member) ko Interim Govt mein FINANCE portfolio mila — unusual/powerful\nassignment. Independence Act: Introduced(4Jul)→Passed(18Jul)→Effective(15Aug1947).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Pakistan: Iqbal(idea1930)-RahmatAli(naam1933)-Jinnah(demand1940) → IndividualSatyagraha: Vinoba-Nehru-\nBrahmaDutt → CrippsMission1942('post-dated cheque') →\nQuitIndia(8Aug1942,GowaliaTank=AugustKrantiMaidan,Gandhi-AghaKhanPalace) → ParallelGovts: Balia(first)-\nSatara(longest)-Tamluk(unique) → INA: MohanSingh(founder)-Bose(SupremeCommander,Jul1943) →\nRedFortTrial(Dhillon-Sehgal-Shahnawaz,BhulabhaiDesai-lawyer) → CabinetMission1946(LCA,Cripps-dono-missions)\n→ InterimGovt(LiaqatAli-Finance) → IndependenceAct: 4Jul(introduce)-18Jul(pass)-15Aug(effective)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye Modern History set ka LAST chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Gandhi ki jail 1942 mein=Agha Khan Palace, 1930 mein=Yerwada — do alag movements.\n2) INA Founder=Mohan Singh(1942). Supreme Commander=Bose(July1943) — do alag roles.\n3) Pakistan: Idea=Iqbal(1930), Naam=Rahmat Ali(1933), Demand=Jinnah(1940) — teen alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Towards Independence (Final Chapter)"," GOVERNOR, GOVERNOR-GENERAL & VICEROY — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 13 (Final Chapter, Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Position Evolution — 3 Baar Naam Badla\n●Governor of Bengal(1757-1773, Plassey ke baad) → GG of Bengal(1773-1833, Regulating Act) → GG of India(1833-\n1858, Charter Act) → Viceroy(1858-1947, GOI Act)\n TRICK — \"G-G-G-V\" evolution trick\n💡\n4 stages: Governor(sirf Bengal,Company) → GG-Bengal(bada scope,Company) → GG-India(poora India,Company) →\nViceroy(Crown direct rule) — jitna aage jaao utna scope BADA hota gaya, aakhri stage mein Company khud khatam ho\ngayi(Crown ne le liya).\n2. GG of Bengal vs GG of India — Dono \"1st\"\n●Warren Hastings = 1st GG of BENGAL(1773, Regulating Act)\n●Lord William Bentinck = 1st GG of INDIA(1833, Charter Act)\n TRICK — \"Bengal-Hastings, India-Bentinck\" trick\n💡\nDono \"1st GG\" hain par ALAG SCOPE ke liye — Hastings = chota scope(Bengal) ka 1st, Bentinck = bada\nscope(poora India) ka 1st — sawaal mein \"Bengal\" ya \"India\" keyword dekho, wahi decide karega.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nWarren Hastings = 1st GG of BENGAL(1773). Lord William Bentinck = 1st GG of INDIA(1833) — dono \"pehle\" hain\npar alag positions ke liye.\n3. Canning — EK HI Vyakti, DO Titles\n●Lord Canning = Last Governor-General + FIRST Viceroy — EK HI PERSON, sirf position ka NAAM badla(GOI\nAct 1858 ke baad)\n TRICK — \"Naam badla, aadmi wahi\" trick\n💡\nCanning khud nahi badla, sirf USKA TITLE badla — 1857 Revolt ke baad jab Crown ne Company se power li, tabhi\n\"Governor-General\" \"Viceroy\" ban gaya, aur Canning us waqt jo bhi tha wahi \"pehla Viceroy\" ban gaya. Same pattern\njo Mughal(Babur-Akbar) mein tha, yahan \"same-person-do-title\" hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLord Canning = Last Governor-General AUR First Viceroy — ek hi vyakti, sirf position ka naam GOI Act 1858 ke baad\nbadla.\n4. Awadh — Misgovernance, DOCTRINE OF LAPSE NAHI\n●Satara(1848,pehla)→Jhansi(1853)→Nagpur(1854) = sab Doctrine of Lapse se\n●Awadh(1856) = \"MISGOVERNANCE\"(kushasan) se liya gaya — Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI\n TRICK — \"Awadh = Odd One Out\" trick\n💡\nDalhousie ki saari annexations mein AWADH AKELA hai jo Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI aaya — baaki sab\nstates(Satara,Jhansi,Nagpur) is theory se liye gaye, Awadh alag reason(misgovernance) se — is \"odd one out\" ko\nhighlight karke yaad rakho, SABSE BADA TRAP hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠"," Awadh(1856) = MISGOVERNANCE se liya gaya, Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI — baaki states(Satara,Jhansi,Nagpur)\nDoctrine of Lapse se the.\n5. Income Tax — James Wilson, Canning NAHI\n●Income Tax Canning ke TENURE mein laga, par LAGAYA James Wilson(1st Finance Member) ne\n TRICK — \"Tenure ≠ Levied by\" trick\n💡\nCanning ke RAAJ mein hua, par Canning ne KHUD nahi lagaya — jaise koi PM ke time koi law banti hai, par usko\nbanane wala Finance Minister hota hai, PM nahi. \"Kis ke time aur kisne kiya\" — do alag sawaal, do alag jawab.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIncome Tax Canning ke TENURE mein laga, par LEVY kiya James Wilson(1st Finance Member) ne — \"who levied\" ka\njawab Wilson hai, Canning nahi.\n6. \"Father of...\" Titles — 5 Alag Log\n●Cornwallis = Father of Civil Service(India)\n●Wellesley(\"Tiger of Bengal\") = Father of Subsidiary Alliance\n●Dalhousie = Father of Doctrine of Lapse\n●Ripon = Father of Local Self-Government\n●Metcalfe = Liberator of Press(1835) — \"Father\" nahi, \"Liberator\"\n TRICK — \"5 Fathers, 5 Systems\" trick\n💡\nCornwallis-CivilService, Wellesley-Subsidiary(Alliance), Dalhousie-Doctrine(Lapse), Ripon-LocalSelfGovt — 4\n\"Fathers\", pehle-letter se match karo: C-C, W-S(alag letter but yaad rakho \"Tiger\"), D-D, R-L. Metcalfe akela\n\"Liberator\" hai, \"Father\" nahi — is exception ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCornwallis=Father of Civil Service. Wellesley=Father of Subsidiary Alliance. Dalhousie=Father of Doctrine of Lapse.\nRipon=Father of Local Self-Govt. Metcalfe=LIBERATOR of Press(not \"Father\").\n7. Curzon — SABSE ZYADA Commissions\n●Famine(1899-1900) · Irrigation(Colin Scott Moncrieff,1901) · Police(Andrew Fraser,1902→CID) ·\nUniversity(Thomas Raleigh,1902)\n●Bengal Partition(1905) = \"Sabse bada political blunder\" · Victoria Memorial = Architect William Emerson\n TRICK — \"4 Commissions\" trick\n💡\nCurzon = SABSE ZYADA commissions banane wala Viceroy(4: Famine,Irrigation,Police,University) — is\n\"commission-obsessed\" image se hi Curzon yaad rakho, aur uska AAKHRI/BADA GALTI(Bengal Partition) bhi isi\ntenure mein hui.\n8. Lord Linlithgow — Sabse Lamba Tenure(8 Saal)\n●1936-44(8 saal) = sabse lamba tenure wala Viceroy · Quit India Movement(1942) isi ke time\n●Cornwallis ka tomb = Ghazipur(UP) · MAO College(1875) = Lytton ke tenure mein(Sir Syed Ahmad Khan ne\nbanayi)\n TRICK — \"Linlithgow = Sabse Lamba\" trick\n💡\n8 saal = sabse LAMBA — is number ko yaad rakho, aur isi lambe tenure mein hi sabse BADA movement(Quit India)\nbhi hua, jaise lamba tenure = zyada bade events dekhne ka mauka."," 9. Mountbatten — Last Viceroy + 1st GG Independent India\n●Mountbatten = Last Viceroy(pre-Independence) + 1st GG of INDEPENDENT India\n●Uske baad C. Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN GG\n TRICK — \"Mountbatten-Videshi-First, Rajaji-Desi-First\" trick\n💡\nMountbatten = 1st GG of independent India(par VIDESHI/British), Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN GG(desi) —\nsame pattern jaisa \"1st Female President(Besant,videshi) vs 1st Indian Female President(Naidu)\" tha(Ch.7) — videshi-\npehle, desi-baad mein pattern yahan bhi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMountbatten = 1st GG of Independent India(British). C. Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN(desi) GG — dono \"1st\" hain par\nalag category.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Evolution:\nGovernor(Clive)→GGBengal(WarrenHastings,1773)→GGIndia(Bentinck,1833)→Viceroy(Canning,1858,last-GG+1st-\nViceroy) → Cornwallis-CivilService,Wellesley-SubsidiaryAlliance(TigerOfBengal) → Bentinck-Sati(1829) →\nDalhousie-DoctrineOfLapse(Awadh=misgovernance-exception),Railway(1853) → IncomeTax=JamesWilson(Canning-\ntenure) → Lytton-VPA(1878)+MAOCollege(1875) → Ripon-LocalSelfGovt(1882) →\nCurzon-4Commissions+BengalPartition(1905) → HardingeII-CapitalShift+PartitionAnnul(1911) → Chelmsford-\nRowlatt+Jallianwala(1919) → Irwin-DandiMarch+GandhiIrwinPact(1931) → Linlithgow-Longest(8yrs)\n+QuitIndia(1942) → Wavell-CabinetMission(1946) → Mountbatten-\nLastViceroy+1stGG(1947)→Rajagopalachari-1stIndianGG\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye POORE Modern History series ka SABSE AAKHRI chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Warren Hastings=1st GG of BENGAL. Bentinck=1st GG of INDIA — alag scope.\n2) Awadh(1856)=Misgovernance se liya, Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI(baaki states iske through the).\n3) Income Tax Canning ke tenure mein laga, par LEVY kiya James Wilson ne.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Governor, GG & Viceroy (Final Chapter)"]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0444","t":"01 Polity Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / Polity","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Constitutional Development of India\nCONSTITUTIONAL DEVELOPMENT OF INDIA —\nMEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi dates, Acts, firsts, titles aur exam-confusion points hain jo baar-baar bhoolte ya\nswap hote hain.\n1. Do Era + 12 Acts — Pehle Skeleton Yaad Karo\n• Company Rule (1773–1858) = 5 major Acts\n• Crown Rule (1858–1947) = 7 major Acts\n• Total = 12 major Acts\n TRICK — “5 Company, 7 Crown”\n💡\nBas 5–7 ka pair yaad rakho: pehle Company ke 5 Acts, phir Crown ke 7 Acts.\nCompany sequence: Regulating 1773\n Pitts 1784\n Charter 1813\n Charter 1833\n Charter 1853.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nCrown sequence: 1858\n 1861\n 1892\n 1909\n 1919\n 1935\n 1947.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n2. Company Rule — 5 Acts Ka Fast Memory Ladder\n• 1773 Regulating Act\n Governor General of Bengal + Supreme Court\n→\n• 1784 Pitts India Act\n Dual Government\n→\n• 1813 Charter Act\n Trade monopoly partly ended + ₹1 lakh education + missionaries\n→\n• 1833 Charter Act\n Governor General of India + Law Commission + monopoly completely ended\n→\n• 1853 Charter Act\n Legislative/Admin separation + Civil Services open competition\n→\n TRICK — “73–84–13–33–53” key-word chain\n💡\n73 = Bengal title, 84 = Dual control, 13 = Education + partial monopoly end, 33 = India title + complete monopoly end,\n53 = Competition + separation.\nBolke revise karo: “73 Bengal, 84 Dual, 13 Education, 33 India, 53 ICS.”\nRegulating Act 1773 — Bengal Wala First\n• Governor of Bengal\n Governor General of Bengal\n→\n• First Governor General of Bengal = Lord Warren Hastings\n• Supreme Court = Calcutta, 1774\n• First Chief Justice = Sir Elijah Impey\n TRICK — “73 Hastings, 74 Court”\n💡\nAct 1773 ko Hastings se jodo; agle saal 1774 mein Calcutta Supreme Court.\nBengal wala title 1773 hai — India wala title 1833 mein aayega.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGovernor General of Bengal = Warren Hastings (1773).\nGovernor General of India = William Bentinck (1833). Dono titles ko swap mat karna."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Constitutional Development of India\nPitts India Act 1784 — Do Body, Do Kaam\n• Commercial matters = Court of Directors\n• Political matters = Board of Control\n• Governor General's Council = 4\n 3\n→\n• Company territory ko “British-Possession in India” kaha gaya\n TRICK — “Company = Commerce, Board = Politics”\n💡\nCourt of Directors ko Company/commercial side samjho.\nBoard of Control ko British Government/political control side samjho.\n1784 ke saath 4\n3 bhi chipka lo.\n→\n3. Charter Acts 1813–1833–1853 — Teen Bhai, Teen Kaam\n• 1813\n Monopoly partly ended; Tea + China exception; ₹1 lakh education; missionaries allowed\n→\n• 1833\n Tea + China monopoly bhi ended; GG of India; Bentinck; Law Commission 1834, Macaulay\n→\n• 1853\n Legislative vs Administrative functions separate; Court of Directors 24\n18; Civil Services open\n→\n→\ncompetition; local representation\n TRICK — “13 = Partial, 33 = Complete, 53 = Competition”\n💡\n1813: monopoly sirf partly khatam.\n1833: monopoly completely khatam + Bengal se India title.\n1853: Civil Services competition + legislative/admin separation.\nShort chant: “13 Partial, 33 Complete, 53 Compete.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n“Trade monopoly abolished” dekh kar wording check karo: Tea/China exception ke saath = 1813; completely abolished\n= 1833.\nCourt of Directors 24\n18 = 1853; Governor General's Council 4\n3 = 1784.\n→\n→\n4. Crown Rule Start — 1858: Company Gayi, Crown Aaya\n• Government of India Act 1858\n Company rule end; rule British Crown ko transfer\n→\n• Governor General of India\n Viceroy of India\n→\n• First Viceroy = Lord Canning\n• Secretary of State for India post created\n• Court of Directors + Board of Control abolished\n TRICK — “Company\n Crown, GG\n Viceroy”\n💡\n→\n→\n1858 ko ek bada title-switch samjho: Company se Crown aur Governor General se Viceroy.\nCanning same person the — pehle Governor General of India, phir first Viceroy.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFirst Viceroy = Lord Canning. Naya insaan nahi aaya; title change hua."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Constitutional Development of India\n5. Indian Councils Acts — 61, 92, 09\n• 1861\n Portfolio system + Viceroy ordinance power + legislative councils expansion\n→\n• 1892\n Indirect elections + questions + budget debate + non-official members\n→\n• 1909\n Morley-Minto + Separate Electorate for Muslims + first Indian in Viceroy's Executive Council:\n→\nSatyendra Prasad Sinha\n TRICK — “61 Portfolio\n 92 Budget\n 09 Muslim Separate”\n💡\n→\n→\nTeen Councils Acts ko sirf ek ladder mein yaad karo:\n1861 = Portfolio, 1892 = Budget/Indirect election, 1909 = Muslim separate electorate.\nShort code: P-B-S\n Portfolio, Budget, Separate.\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSeparate Electorate for Muslims first introduced = 1909.\n1919 mein ye expand hua — introduction aur expansion ko swap mat karna.\n6. 1909 vs 1919 — Naam Bhi Similar, Feature Bhi Trap\n• 1909 Morley-Minto\n Separate electorate for Muslims; Councils expansion; Satyendra Prasad Sinha\n→\n• 1919 Montagu-Chelmsford\n Provincial Dyarchy; Central Bicameralism; Direct elections (limited\n→\nfranchise); separate electorate expanded\n TRICK — “Minto = Muslim; Montagu = Two Levels”\n💡\nMinto ke M se Muslim yaad karo\n 1909 Separate Electorate.\n→\n1919 mein do alag levels: Province = Dyarchy, Centre = Bicameral.\nBolke check karo: “19 Province-Dyarchy, Centre-Bicameral.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDyarchy = Provincial level (1919), Central level nahi.\nBicameral legislature = Central level (1919). Dono same Act, par levels alag.\n7. 1935 & 1947 — Blueprint Se British Exit Tak\n• Government of India Act 1935\n All India Federation provision\n→\n• 3 Lists = Federal, Provincial, Concurrent\n• Federal Judiciary + RBI establishment\n• Bicameral system provinces tak; separate electorates further expanded\n• India Independence Act 1947\n British rule end; Viceroy + Secretary of State posts abolished\n→\n• Princely States: India / Pakistan / Independent option\n• Constituent Assembly ko Constitution banane aur adopt karne ki power\n TRICK — “35 = 3 Lists + RBI; 47 = Finish”\n💡\n1935 ko ‘3’ se jodo: 3 Lists. Saath mein RBI aur federation blueprint.\n1947 = Finish British rule + Constituent Assembly power.\nShort chain: “35 Lists-RBI, 47 Liberty.”"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Constitutional Development of India\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRBI = Government of India Act 1935. 1947 ya Constitution ke baad nahi.\nBicameral Centre = 1919; bicameral provinces tak = 1935.\n8. Important Firsts — Title Ladder\n• First Governor General of Bengal\n Warren Hastings\n Regulating Act 1773\n→\n→\n• First Chief Justice, Supreme Court\n Sir Elijah Impey\n 1774\n→\n→\n• First Governor General of India\n Lord William Bentinck\n Charter Act 1833\n→\n→\n• Law Commission Chairman\n Lord Macaulay\n 1834\n→\n→\n• First Viceroy of India\n Lord Canning\n Government of India Act 1858\n→\n→\n• First Indian in Viceroy's Executive Council\n Satyendra Prasad Sinha\n 1909\n→\n→\n TRICK — “H-I-B-M-C-S” people chain\n💡\nHastings\n Impey\n Bentinck\n Macaulay\n Canning\n Sinha.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nRole chain bolo: Bengal GG\n Chief Justice\n India GG\n Law Commission\n Viceroy\n First Indian Executive\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nCouncillor.\nNaam se zyada role-order yaad rakho.\n9. Numbers Jo Exam Mein Swap Hote Hain\n• 1773 Act\n Supreme Court actually established 1774\n→\n• 1784 Pitts\n Governor General's Council 4\n3\n→\n→\n• 1813 Charter\n ₹1 lakh annually for education\n→\n• 1834\n Law Commission, Chairman Macaulay\n→\n• 1853 Charter\n Court of Directors 24\n18\n→\n→\n TRICK — “4\n3 Pitt; 24\n18 Charter”\n💡\n→\n→\nChhota reduction 4\n3 = Pitts 1784.\n→\nBada reduction 24\n18 = Charter 1853.\n→\nEducation number = ₹1 lakh = Charter 1813; Court year = 1774.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“5 Company + 7 Crown\n 73 Bengal-Hastings/74 Court\n 84 Dual + 4\n3\n 13 Partial monopoly + ₹1L\n 33 India-\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nBentinck + Macaulay + Complete monopoly\n 53 ICS + separation + 24\n18\n 58 Crown-Canning-Viceroy\n 61 Portfolio\n→\n→\n→\n→\n 92 Budget + Indirect\n 09 Minto-Muslim Separate\n 19 Province Dyarchy + Centre Bicameral + Direct\n 35 3 Lists +\n→\n→\n→\n→\nRBI + Provincial Bicameral\n 47 British Finish + CA Power.”\n→\nIs chain ko 2–3 baar bolne se poora chapter chronological order mein recall ho jaata hai.\n Top 3:\n⚠\nBengal GG vs India GG | 1813 partial vs 1833 complete monopoly | 1909 Separate Electorate vs 1919\nDyarchy/Bicameral."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Making of the Constitution\nMAKING OF THE CONSTITUTION — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — dates, CA numbers, committees, key people, Cabinet Mission, original Constitution aur Interim\nCabinet ke wahi facts hain jo exam mein confuse hote hain.\n1. Background Timeline — Demand Se Cabinet Mission Tak\n• 1895 — Swaraj Bill (Bal Gangadhar Tilak)\n Constituent Assembly ka pehla mention\n→\n• 1928 — Nehru Report\n Chairman: Motilal Nehru\n→\n• 1934 — M.N. Roy\n Constituent Assembly ki pehli formal demand\n→\n• 1935 — INC\n Constituent Assembly ki demand\n→\n• 1940 — August Offer\n Viceroy Lord Linlithgow; Individual Satyagraha: Vinoba Bhave 1st, Jawaharlal Nehru\n→\n2nd\n• 1942 — Cripps Mission\n CA formation accepted; Congress complete independence chahta tha\n→\n• 1946 — Cabinet Mission\n CA formation ka practical road clear\n→\n TRICK — “95–28–34–35–40–42–46” ladder\n💡\nSequence ko event-word ke saath bolo: “Tilak\n Nehru\n Roy\n INC\n August\n Cripps\n Cabinet.”\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nSabse important first-trap: 1895 = pehla mention, 1934 = pehli formal demand, 1935 = INC demand.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n“First demand” wording dekhkar context check karo: pehla mention = Swaraj Bill 1895 (Tilak); formal demand = M.N.\nRoy 1934; INC demand = 1935.\n2. Cabinet Mission 1946 — Teen Aadmi, Ek Mission\n• Pethick Lawrence\n Secretary of State for India; Chairman\n→\n• Stafford Cripps\n Trade Board\n→\n• A.V. Alexander\n Naval Board\n→\n• Constituent Assembly formation accepted by Congress & Muslim League\n• Separate Pakistan proposal rejected\n• Muslim League ki communal electorate demand accepted\n TRICK — “P-C-A = Pethick–Cripps–Alexander”\n💡\nTeen members ko P-C-A order mein yaad karo.\nRole hook: Pethick = Chairman, Cripps = Trade, Alexander = Naval.\nDecision hook: CA = YES, Separate Pakistan = NO, Communal Electorate = YES.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCabinet Mission ne separate Pakistan proposal REJECT kiya, lekin communal electorate demand accept ki. Dono ko\nopposite direction mein yaad rakho.\n3. Constituent Assembly Seats — 389 Se 299, Sign 284\n• Before Partition total seats = 389\n• Elected = 296 (292 + 4 Chief Commissioner areas)"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Making of the Constitution\n• Nominated Princely States = 93\n• Representation = 1 seat per 10 lakh people\n• After Partition total = 299\n• Final Constitution par signatures = 284\n• Women members = 15\n• Election results: Congress 208, Muslim League 73, Others 15\n TRICK — “389 > 299 > 284” shrink chain\n💡\nPehle Assembly = 389, Partition ke baad = 299, sign karne wale = 284.\nSide numbers: 296 elected + 93 nominated = 389; women = 15.\nSeats yaad karte waqt sirf ye descending picture banao: 389 > 299 > 284.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n299 final seats the, lekin Constitution par 284 members ne sign kiya — 299 ko signature count mat bana dena.\n4. CA Key Positions — Temporary, Permanent, Advisor\n• Temporary President = Dr. Sachchidananda Sinha\n• Permanent President = Dr. Rajendra Prasad\n• Vice-President = H.C. Mukherjee\n• Constitutional Advisor = B.N. Rau\n• First Parliament = Constituent Assembly itself\n TRICK — “S-R-M-R” role chain\n💡\nSinha = Start/Temporary, Rajendra = Regular/Permanent, Mukherjee = Vice, Rau = Advisor.\nSound hook: “Sinha starts, Rajendra rules, Mukherjee vice, Rau advises.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTemporary President = Sachchidananda Sinha; Permanent President = Rajendra Prasad. Dono alag posts/facts hain.\n5. Sessions & Big Numbers — 11, 165, 2-11-18, 64\n• Total Sessions = 11\n• Working Days = 165\n• First Meeting = 9 Dec 1946; 211 members present\n• First Session = 9–23 Dec 1946\n• Last Session (11th) = 14–26 Nov 1949\n• Total Duration = 2 years 11 months 18 days\n• Total Expense\n ₹64 lakhs\n≈\n• Symbol = Elephant\n• Mahatma Gandhi and Jinnah = NOT members of Constituent Assembly\n TRICK — “11–165–2/11/18–64–Elephant”\n💡\nCA ka number-pack ek saath bolo: “11 sessions, 165 days, 2y-11m-18d, 64 lakh, Elephant.”\nNegative fact ko alag stamp karo: Gandhi + Jinnah = CA members nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Making of the Constitution\n6. Women + Original Constitution — Who Did What\n• Sucheta Kriplani\n 1st Woman Chief Minister of India (UP)\n→\n• Sarojini Naidu\n 1st Woman Governor of India (UP)\n→\n• Amrit Kaur\n 1st Health Minister of India\n→\n• English Calligrapher = Prem Behari Narain Raizada\n• Hindi Calligrapher = Vasant Krishna Vaidya\n• Illustrators = Nandalal Bose + Beohar Rammanohar Sinha\n• National Flag Designer = Pingali Venkayya\n TRICK — “English Prem, Hindi Vasant; Art Nandalal-Beohar; Flag Pingali”\n💡\nCalligraphy pair ko language ke saath yaad karo: English = Prem Behari, Hindi = Vasant Krishna.\nPicture/art = Nandalal + Beohar; Flag = Pingali.\nWomen hook: Sucheta-CM, Sarojini-Governor, Amrit-Health.\n7. 8 Major Committees — Chairman Matching\n• Drafting Committee\n Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n→\n• Steering Committee\n Dr. Rajendra Prasad\n→\n• Union Powers Committee\n Jawaharlal Nehru\n→\n• Provincial Committee\n Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel\n→\n• Flag Committee\n Dr. Rajendra Prasad\n→\n• Minorities Committee\n H.C. Mukherjee\n→\n• House Committee\n Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n→\n• Rules of Procedure Committee\n Dr. Rajendra Prasad\n→\n TRICK — “Rajendra = S-F-R” triple\n💡\nRajendra Prasad ne 3 committees chair ki: Steering, Flag, Rules of Procedure.\nShort code: S-F-R = Steering–Flag–Rules.\nBaaki anchor: Drafting-Ambedkar, Union-Nehru, Provincial-Patel, Minorities-Mukherjee, House-Pattabhi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRajendra Prasad = 3 committees, sirf Flag ya Steering nahi. S-F-R teeno yaad rakho.\n8. Drafting Committee — 7 Members + 2 Replacements\n• Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n Chairman\n→\n• Krishnaswamy Iyer\n• N. Gopalaswami Ayyangar\n• Saadullah Khan\n• B.L. Mitter\n replaced by N. Madhav Rao\n→\n• D.P. Khaitan\n passed away; replaced by T.T. Krishnamachari\n→\n• K.M. Munshi\n TRICK — “A-I-A-S-M-K-M” base chain\n💡\nAmbedkar\n Iyer\n Ayyangar\n Saadullah\n Mitter\n Khaitan\n Munshi.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nReplacement pair alag se yaad karo: Mitter\n Madhav Rao; Khaitan\n Krishnamachari.\n→\n→\nMnemonic line: “Ambedkar-Iyer-Ayyangar-Saadullah, Mitter-Khaitan-Munshi.”"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Making of the Constitution\n9. Critical Dates — Adopted vs Enforced\n• 9 Dec 1946\n First Meeting of Constituent Assembly\n→\n• 22 Jul 1947\n National Flag adopted\n→\n• 4 Nov 1948\n Draft Constitution presented by Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n→\n• 26 Nov 1949\n Constitution ADOPTED (Constitution Day)\n→\n• 24 Jan 1950\n National Anthem & National Song adopted; Rajendra Prasad became First President\n→\n• 26 Jan 1950\n Constitution ENFORCED (Republic Day)\n→\n TRICK — “9D–22J–4N–26N–24J–26J” date chain\n💡\nEvent words ke saath bolo: Meeting\n Flag\n Draft\n Adopted\n Anthem/Song\n Enforced.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nSabse important pair: 26 Nov = Adopted; 26 Jan = Enforced.\n26 January choose hone ka source-link: 26 Jan 1930 Independence Day observance (Purna Swaraj connection).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nConstitution Day = 26 November 1949 (Adopted). Republic Day = 26 January 1950 (Enforced). Same ‘26’, month alag.\n10. Interim Cabinet 1946 — Portfolio Hooks\n• Jawaharlal Nehru\n Vice President of Executive Council; External Affairs\n→\n• Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel\n Home, Information & Broadcasting\n→\n• Baldev Singh\n Defence\n→\n• Jagjivan Ram\n Labour\n→\n• Liaquat Ali Khan\n Finance\n→\n• Ghaznafar Ali\n Health\n→\n• C. Rajagopalachari\n Education\n→\n• Rajendra Prasad\n Food & Agriculture\n→\n• Jogendra Nath Mandal\n Law\n→\n• Abdur Rab Nishtar\n Communication\n→\n• Asaf Ali\n Railways & Transport\n→\n• T.T. Chundrigar\n Commerce\n→\n• John Mathai\n Industries & Supplies\n→\n TRICK — “Big 6 portfolio anchors”\n💡\nNehru = External, Patel = Home, Baldev = Defence, Jagjivan = Labour, Liaquat = Finance, Rajendra Prasad = Food &\nAgriculture.\nBaaki chain: Ghaznafar-Health\n Rajagopalachari-Education\n Mandal-Law\n Nishtar-Communication\n Asaf-\n→\n→\n→\n→\nRailways\n Chundrigar-Commerce\n Mathai-Industries.\n→\n→\nSpecial hook: Liaquat Ali Khan = Finance in 1946 Interim Cabinet.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n1895 Tilak mention\n 1928 Motilal\n 1934 Roy formal\n 1935 INC\n 1940 August (Vinoba1/Nehru2)\n 1942 Cripps\n 1946 Cabinet\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nPCA\n CA 389>299>284; women15; Sinha Temp/Rajendra Perm/Mukherjee Vice/Rau Advisor\n 11/165/2y11m18d/₹64L/Elephant\n\n→\n→\n→\nAmbedkar-Draft; Rajendra-SFR; Nehru-Union; Patel-Provincial\n Draft7 + Mitter-Madhav + Khaitan-Krishnamachari\n 9D46 Meet;\n→\n→\n22J47 Flag; 4N48 Draft; 26N49 Adopt; 24J50 Anthem/Song; 26J50 Enforce.\n Top 3: 1895 mention vs 1934 formal | 389 vs 299 vs 284 | 26 Nov Adopted vs 26 Jan Enforced.\n⚠"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Preamble & Features of the Constitution\nPREAMBLE & FEATURES OF THE CONSTITUTION - MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein - Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai - Preamble ke source, JELF objectives, 42nd Amendment, expert quotes, case laws aur Federal vs Unitary ke\nwahi facts hain jo exam mein baar-baar confuse hote hain.\n1. Preamble Ka Skeleton - Nature + Objectives\n• Nature of State = Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic\n• Objectives = J-E-L-F: Justice, Equality, Liberty, Fraternity\n• Fraternity = dignity of individual + unity and integrity of Nation\nTRICK - “3S + DR, then JELF”\nNature ko bolo: Sovereign - Socialist - Secular - Democratic - Republic = 3S + D + R.\nObjectives ko source ke order mein JELF bolo: Justice - Equality - Liberty - Fraternity.\nPreamble ka short skeleton: “3S-DR gives JELF.”\n2. Preamble Ke Sources - Concept, Language, Basis\n• Preamble text concept = American Constitution\n• Language style = Australian Constitution\n• Inspiration / Basis = Objective Resolution, J.L. Nehru, 13 Dec 1946\n• Preamble = Introduction / Preface; Non-Justiciable; neither gives power nor creates a hurdle to government\nTRICK - “America Concept, Australia Language, Nehru Basis”\nDo A ko alag rakho: America = concept; Australia = language style.\nThird anchor = Nehru ka Objective Resolution = actual basis/inspiration.\nShort code: A-A-N = America, Australia, Nehru.\nEXAM TRAP\nConcept = American aur language style = Australian. Dono ko swap mat karna. Basis = Objective Resolution, 13 Dec 1946.\n3. JELF Objectives - Justice Aur Liberty Ka Number Trap\n• Justice = Social, Economic, Political\n• Economic Justice = 1917 Russian Revolution se inspired\n• Equality = no special privileges + equal before law\n• Liberty = Thought, Expression, Belief, Faith, Worship (5 types)\n• Liberty = French Revolution se inspired\n• Fraternity = brotherhood + dignity + unity & integrity\nTRICK - “Justice = SEP; Liberty = T-E-B-F-W”\nJustice ke 3 types: Social - Economic - Political = S-E-P.\nLiberty ke 5: Thought - Expression - Belief - Faith - Worship. Ek spoken chain banao: “Think, Express, Believe, Faith, Worship.”\nInspiration pair: Economic Justice = Russia 1917; Liberty = France.\nEXAM TRAP\nRussian Revolution ko poori Justice se blindly mat jodo - source specifically Economic Justice ko 1917 Russian Revolution se\nconnect karta hai. Liberty = French Revolution.\n4. Nature of State - 5 Words Ka Meaning\n• Sovereign = internal & external decisions mein free from external influence"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Preamble & Features of the Constitution\n• Socialist = democratic socialism; mixed economy (public + private)\n• Secular = no state religion; equal respect for all religions\n• Democratic = power with people; India = Indirect Democracy through elected representatives\n• Republic = Head of State elected, NOT hereditary\nTRICK - “3S + DR meaning ladder”\nSovereign = Free; Socialist = Mixed; Secular = Equal religion; Democratic = People; Republic = Elected head.\nOne-line recall: “Free - Mixed - Equal - People - Elected.”\nDirect Democracy ka example source mein Switzerland; India = Indirect Democracy.\nEXAM TRAP\nRepublic ka matlab elected Head of State hai, not hereditary. Democratic ka matlab log representatives choose karte hain -\ndono meanings alag hain.\n5. 42nd Amendment 1976 - Sirf Ek Baar, 3 Words\n• Preamble amended only ONCE = 42nd Amendment, 1976\n• Added: Socialist, Secular, Integrity\n• Original: Sovereign Democratic Republic -> after amendment: Sovereign Socialist Secular Democratic Republic\n• Original: Unity of the Nation -> Unity and Integrity of the Nation\nTRICK - “42 = SSI insertion”\n3 added words ka short code: S-S-I = Socialist, Secular, Integrity.\n42nd ko “one amendment, three insertions” ke saath yaad karo.\nSocialist + Secular nature line mein aaye; Integrity fraternity wali unity line mein aaya.\nEXAM TRAP\nPreamble sirf ONCE amend hua hai - 42nd Amendment (1976). Added words = Socialist, Secular, Integrity.\n6. Expert Quotes - Naam Ko Object Se Jodo\n• Ernest Baker = “Key to the Constitution”\n• Krishnaswami Ayyar = “Long-Term Dreams”\n• N.A. Palkhivala = “Identity card of the Constitution”\n• K.M. Munshi = “Horoscope of the Republic”\n• Thakur Bhargava Das = “Soul of the Constitution”\nTRICK - “Key - Dreams - ID - Horoscope - Soul” visual story\nBaker ke haath mein KEY socho; Ayyar sapne dekh rahe hain; Palkhivala ID card dikha rahe hain;\nMunshi horoscope padh rahe hain; Bhargava “soul” ki baat kar rahe hain.\nObject yaad aaya to expert ka naam recall karo.\n7. Landmark Cases - 1960 NO Se 1973 YES Tak\n• Berubari Union Case 1960 = Preamble NOT part of Constitution; cannot be amended\n• Sajjan Singh 1965 = Berubari reconsideration suggested\n• Golaknath 1967 = basic spirit eternal & non-negotiable\n• Kesavananda Bharati 1973 = Preamble IS part; can be amended but basic structure cannot be changed\n• S.R. Bommai 1994 = Preamble integral part\n• LIC v. Union of India 1995 = integral part; yes"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Preamble & Features of the Constitution\nTRICK - “60 NO -> 73 YES -> 94/95 Confirm”\nCase-law ka sabse important turn: Berubari 1960 = NOT part; Kesavananda 1973 = IS part.\nKesavananda formula: Preamble amend ho sakta hai, Basic Structure nahi.\n1994 Bommai + 1995 LIC ne integral-part position ko reinforce kiya.\nEXAM TRAP\nKesavananda Bharati (1973) ko “Preamble amend nahi ho sakta” mat samajhna. Source ke mutabik amendment ho sakta hai,\nlekin Basic Structure nahi badla ja sakta.\n8. 11 Salient Features - 4 Buckets Mein Compress Karo\n• Government: Parliamentary System; Three-Tier Governance; Quasi-Federal with Unitary Bias\n• Constitutional design: Blend of Rigidity & Flexibility; Rule of Law; Supremacy of Constitution\n• Citizens: Universal Adult Franchise; Single Citizenship; Special Provisions for SC/ST & Minorities; Fundamental Rights &\nDuties\n• Guard: Independent & Impartial Judiciary\nTRICK - “Government - Design - Citizens - Guard”\n11 points ko 4 memory boxes mein rakho: Govt / Design / Citizens / Guard.\nGovt = Parliamentary + 3-tier + Quasi-federal. Design = Rigid-Flexible + Rule of Law + Supremacy.\nCitizens = Franchise + Single Citizenship + Special Provisions + FR/Duties. Guard = Independent Judiciary.\n9. Federal vs Unitary - Do Side Ka Balance\n• Federal: Division of Powers; Written Constitution; Bicameral Legislature; Rajya Sabha; Separate Centre/State\nGovernments; Complex Amendment\n• Unitary: Strong Centre; President Rule (Art. 356); Single Citizenship; All-India Services; Governor appointed by\nPresident; Centre stronger during emergencies\n• Conclusion = Quasi-Federal with Unitary Bias\nTRICK - “Normal time = Federal frame, Emergency = Centre remote”\nFederal side ko structure se yaad karo: Powers divided + written document + two houses + two governments + harder\namendment.\nUnitary side ko Centre-control se yaad karo: Strong Centre + 356 + Single Citizenship + All-India Services + Governor +\nEmergency power.\nIsliye source ka final label: Quasi-Federal with Unitary Bias.\nEXAM TRAP\nIndia ko source “Quasi-Federal with Unitary Bias” bolta hai - purely federal ya purely unitary nahi.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN - Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Preamble skeleton 3S+DR -> JELF -> Sources A-A-N (America concept, Australia language, Nehru basis) -> Justice SEP / Liberty\n5 -> State meanings Free-Mixed-Equal-People-Elected -> 42nd = SSI, once -> Quotes Key-Dreams-ID-Horoscope-Soul -> Cases\n1960 NO, 1973 YES, 94/95 confirm -> Features 4 buckets Govt-Design-Citizens-Guard -> Federal structure + Unitary Centre =\nQuasi-Federal with Unitary Bias.”\nTop 3 traps: Concept America vs Language Australia | 42nd = only once + SSI | Berubari 1960 NOT part vs Kesavananda 1973\nIS part."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Sources, Parts, Articles & Schedules\nSOURCES, PARTS, ARTICLES & SCHEDULES — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — sirf country-source matching, key Parts/Articles, 12 Schedules, 7th Schedule lists aur exam traps ko\nfast recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Big Picture — 11 Countries, 22 Parts, 12 Schedules\n• Constitutional Sources = 11 countries / sources\n• Parts = 22\n• Schedules = 12 (Original Constitution mein 8)\n• 7th Schedule = 3 Lists: Union, State, Concurrent\n TRICK — “11–22–12–3” number spine\n💡\nPoore chapter ke 4 master numbers: 11 Sources\n 22 Parts\n 12 Schedules\n 3 Lists.\n→\n→\n→\nRevision start karte hi ye number spine bolo.\n2. Constitutional Sources — Sabse Important Country Matches\n• USA\n Fundamental Rights, Vice-President, Independent Judiciary, Impeachment, Judicial Review\n→\n• UK\n Parliamentary System, Single Citizenship, Cabinet System, Rule of Law, Parliamentary Privileges\n→\n• Ireland\n DPSP, Presidential Election Method, Rajya Sabha nomination\n→\n• Australia\n Concurrent List, Preamble language, Freedom of Trade, Joint Sitting\n→\n• Canada\n Governors appointment, Residuary Powers to Centre, Strong-Centre Federalism\n→\n• Former Soviet Union\n Fundamental Duties, Five-Year Plans, Socio-Economic-Political Justice\n→\n• Germany\n Emergency Powers + Suspension of Fundamental Rights\n→\n• France\n Republic + Liberty, Equality, Fraternity\n→\n• South Africa\n Constitutional Amendment Procedure + Rajya Sabha election\n→\n• Japan\n Procedure Established by Law\n→\n• Govt. of India Act 1935\n Federal System, Judiciary, PSC, Governor's Post, Administrative Details\n→\n TRICK — “R-D-D” core trio\n💡\nRights = USA, DPSP = Ireland, Duties = USSR.\nYe teen sabse direct aur sabse zyada poochhe jaane wale source matches hain.\n TRICK — “A-C-G-S-J” tail chain\n💡\nAustralia = Concurrent/Joint Sitting, Canada = Centre residuary, Germany = Emergency, South Africa = Amendment,\nJapan = Procedure by Law.\nShort line: “Australia Concurrent, Canada Centre, Germany Emergency, South Africa Amendment, Japan Law.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFundamental Rights = USA; Fundamental Duties = USSR; DPSP = Ireland. Teenon ko swap mat karna.\nAmendment Procedure = South Africa, Emergency Powers = Germany."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Sources, Parts, Articles & Schedules\n3. Parts 1–4A — Foundation Block\n• Part 1 (Articles 1–4)\n Union & its Territory\n→\n• Part 2 (5–11)\n Citizenship\n→\n• Part 3 (12–35)\n Fundamental Rights\n→\n• Part 4 (36–51)\n DPSP\n→\n• Part 4A (51A)\n Fundamental Duties\n→\n TRICK — “1 Territory, 2 Citizenship, 3 Rights, 4 Policy, 4A Duty”\n💡\nPart numbers ko subject progression ki tarah bolo.\nMost important anchor: Part 3 = FR, Part 4 = DPSP, Part 4A = Duties.\n4. Key Parts & Articles — Exam Anchors\n• Fundamental Rights\n Articles 12–35, Part 3\n→\n• DPSP\n Articles 36–51, Part 4\n→\n• Fundamental Duties\n Article 51A, Part 4A\n→\n• Panchayats\n Part 9, Articles 243–243O\n→\n• Municipalities\n Part 9A\n→\n• Elections\n Part 15, Articles 324–329(A)\n→\n• Emergency\n Part 18, Articles 352–360\n→\n• Amendment\n Part 20, Article 368\n→\n TRICK — “3–4–4A / 15–18–20” anchor chain\n💡\n3 = Rights, 4 = DPSP, 4A = Duties.\n15 = Elections, 18 = Emergency, 20 = Amendment.\nArticle hooks: 51A Duty, 368 Amendment.\n5. Parts 5–22 — Subject Ladder\n• Part 5\n Union | Part 6\n States | Part 7\n Repealed | Part 8\n Union Territories\n→\n→\n→\n→\n• Part 9\n Panchayats | 9A\n Municipalities | 9B\n Cooperative Societies\n→\n→\n→\n• Part 10\n Scheduled & Tribal Areas | Part 11\n Centre-State Relations\n→\n→\n• Part 12\n Finance/Property/Contracts/Suits | Part 13\n Trade & Commerce\n→\n→\n• Part 14\n Services | 14A\n Tribunals | Part 15\n Elections\n→\n→\n→\n• Part 16\n Special Provisions for Certain Classes | Part 17\n Official Language\n→\n→\n• Part 18\n Emergency | Part 19\n Miscellaneous | Part 20\n Amendment\n→\n→\n→\n• Part 21\n Temporary/Transitional/Special | Part 22\n Short Title/Commencement/Hindi text/Repeals\n→\n→\n TRICK — “5 Union > 6 States > 8 UT > 9 Local > 11 Relations > 18 Emergency > 20 Amendment”\n💡\nSaare 22 Parts ratne ke bajay anchor points yaad karo aur beech ka ladder connect karo.\nLocal-government block = 9, 9A, 9B; emergency-amendment block = 18, 20."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Sources, Parts, Articles & Schedules\n6. 12 Schedules — TEARS OF OLD PM\n• 1st\n Territories\n→\n• 2nd\n Emoluments / Salaries\n→\n• 3rd\n Affirmations / Oaths\n→\n• 4th\n Rajya Sabha seat allocation\n→\n• 5th\n Scheduled Areas & Tribes\n→\n• 6th\n Other Tribal Areas (Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura, Mizoram)\n→\n• 7th\n Federal Lists: Union, State, Concurrent\n→\n• 8th\n Official Languages\n→\n• 9th\n Land Reforms\n→\n• 10th\n Defection\n→\n• 11th\n Panchayat subjects\n→\n• 12th\n Municipality subjects\n→\n TRICK — “TEARS OF OLD PM”\n💡\nT = Territories, E = Emoluments, A = Affirmation, R = Rajya Sabha, S = Scheduled Areas,\nO = Other Tribal, F = Federal Lists, O = Official Languages, L = Land Reforms, D = Defection, P = Panchayats, M =\nMunicipalities.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nOriginal Constitution = 8 Schedules; Present = 12. Later added: 9th, 10th, 11th, 12th.\n7. Later-added Schedules — 9, 10, 11, 12\n• 9th Schedule\n 1st Amendment, 1951\n Land Reforms\n→\n→\n• 10th Schedule\n 52nd Amendment, 1985\n Anti-Defection\n→\n→\n• 11th Schedule\n 73rd Amendment, 1992\n 29 Panchayat subjects\n→\n→\n• 12th Schedule\n 74th Amendment, 1992\n 18 Municipality subjects\n→\n→\n TRICK — “1–52–73–74” amendment ladder\n💡\n9th = 1st Amendment, 10th = 52nd, 11th = 73rd, 12th = 74th.\nLast pair easy: 73rd Panchayat, 74th Municipality.\n8. 8th Schedule Languages — 14 Se 22\n• Original languages = 14\n• Current languages = 22\n• 21st Amendment (1967)\n Sindhi\n→\n• 71st Amendment (1992)\n Konkani, Manipuri, Nepali\n→\n• 92nd Amendment (2003)\n Bodo, Dogri, Maithili, Santhali\n→\n TRICK — “1 + 3 + 4 = 8 additions”\n💡\n14 original + 8 added = 22 current.\nAdditions pattern: 21st\n 1 language; 71st\n 3; 92nd\n 4.\n→\n→\n→\nLast 4: Bodo–Dogri–Maithili–Santhali.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCurrent languages = 22, not 14. Last addition in source notes = 92nd Amendment 2003: Bodo, Dogri, Maithili, Santhali."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Sources, Parts, Articles & Schedules\n9. 7th Schedule — 3 Lists\n• Union List examples\n Banking, Defence, Foreign Affairs, Communication, Railways, Inter-State Trade\n→\n• State List examples\n Health, Agriculture, Police, Trade\n→\n• Concurrent List examples\n Forests, Education, Marriage, Succession, Population Control\n→\n• Union List laws\n Parliament\n→\n• State List laws\n State Legislature (normally)\n→\n• Concurrent List\n Both; conflict mein Parliament prevails\n→\n• Residuary Powers\n Centre / Parliament (borrowed from Canada)\n→\n TRICK — “BDFCR = Union; HAPT = State; FEMSP = Concurrent”\n💡\nUnion: Banking–Defence–Foreign Affairs–Communication–Railways.\nState: Health–Agriculture–Police–Trade.\nConcurrent: Forests–Education–Marriage–Succession–Population Control.\n TRICK — Education shift\n💡\nEducation 42nd Amendment 1976 se State List se Concurrent List mein shift hua.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nResiduary Powers = Centre, source = Canada.\nConcurrent conflict = Parliament prevails.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“11 Sources–22 Parts–12 Schedules–3 Lists\n Rights-USA, DPSP-Ireland, Duties-USSR\n Australia-Concurrent, Canada-\n→\n→\nCentre Residuary, Germany-Emergency, South Africa-Amendment, Japan-Procedure by Law\n Part3 FR 12–35, Part4\n→\nDPSP 36–51, Part4A Duty 51A\n Part9 Panchayat, 9A Municipality, 15 Elections, 18 Emergency 352–360, 20\n→\nAmendment 368\n Schedules TEARS OF OLD PM\n later 9th=1st/1951, 10th=52nd/1985, 11th=73rd/29 subjects,\n→\n→\n12th=74th/18 subjects\n 8th language 14\n22, additions 1+3+4\n 7th Lists: Union/State/Concurrent, Residuary Centre.”\n→\n→\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nRights-USA / DPSP-Ireland / Duties-USSR | Original 8 Schedules vs Current 12 | Residuary Powers-Centre from\nCanada."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Union & Its Territories\nUNION AND ITS TERRITORIES — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part 1, Articles 1–4, reorganization committees, state-formation years, Art. 371 series aur case-law\ntraps ko fast recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Part 1 — Articles 1–4 Ka Master Map\n• Article 1\n Name & Territory of India\n→\n• Article 2\n New State ki Admission / Establishment\n→\n• Article 3\n State ki Area / Name / Boundary ka Reorganization\n→\n• Article 4\n Article 2 & 3 wale changes ke liye Article 368 amendment nahi; Simple Majority enough\n→\n TRICK — “1 Naam, 2 Naya, 3 Naksha, 4 No-368”\n💡\nArticle 1 = Naam/Territory.\nArticle 2 = Naya state admit/establish.\nArticle 3 = Naksha badlo — area/name/boundary.\nArticle 4 = No Article 368; simple majority.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArticle 3 ke under boundaries/name/area change = Simple Majority. Article 368 amendment ki zaroorat nahi.\n2. Article 1 — Indestructible Union\n• India ki territory = States + Union Territories + acquired territories\n• States ko secede karne ka right nahi\n• India = Indestructible Union of Destructible States\n TRICK — “Union Pakka, States Ka Naksha Badal Sakta”\n💡\nUnion ko tod nahi sakte, lekin states ki boundaries/name/area badal sakte ho.\nIsliye phrase yaad rakho: Indestructible Union, Destructible States.\n3. Article 2 vs Article 3 — Admit vs Alter\n• Article 2\n Union mein naye / existing outside states ko admit ya establish karna; example: Sikkim\n→\n• Article 3\n Existing state ki area, boundary, name change; states merge/split ho sakte hain\n→\n• Jammu & Kashmir Reorganization Act 2019\n Article 3 example\n→\n TRICK — “2 = Entry Gate, 3 = Editing Table”\n💡\nArticle 2 ko Union ka entry gate samjho — state ko andar lao.\nArticle 3 ko map-editor samjho — andar ke states ka shape/name/area badlo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nState Legislature ka consent binding nahi. Bill Parliament mein introduce hone se pehle President ki prior approval chahiye;\nstate ki rai binding nahi hai.\n4. Berubari vs Maganbhai — Opposite Case Trap\n• Berubari Case (1960)\n Indian territory doosre country ko transfer = Constitutional Amendment required\n→\n• Maganbhai Patel v. Union of India (1969)\n International boundary dispute settlement = Constitutional Amendment\n→\nnot required; executive can settle\n• 100th Amendment (2015)\n India-Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Union & Its Territories\n TRICK — “Transfer = Berubari = Amendment; Boundary = Maganbhai = No Amendment”\n💡\nT-B-A: Territory Transfer\n Berubari\n Amendment.\n→\n→\nB-M-N: Boundary dispute\n Maganbhai\n No amendment.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBerubari aur Maganbhai ko ulta mat karna — source notes mein dono opposite situations ke liye diye gaye hain.\n5. Reorganization Committees — Dhar, JVP, Fazl Ali\n• SK Dhar Committee (June 1948)\n Linguistic basis reject; administrative convenience\n→\n• JVP Committee (Dec 1948)\n Linguistic basis reject\n→\n• JVP = Jawaharlal Nehru + Vallabhbhai Patel + Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n• Fazl Ali Commission (Dec 1953)\n Linguistic basis accept; One Language One State reject\n→\n• Fazl Ali members\n K.M. Panikkar + H.N. Kunzru\n→\n• Fazl Ali recommendation\n 16 States + 3 UTs\n→\n TRICK — “Dhar NO, JVP NO, Fazl YES”\n💡\nSequence: Dhar NO\n JVP NO\n Fazl Ali YES linguistic basis.\n→\n→\nFazl Ali ka extra trap: linguistic basis YES, lekin ‘One Language One State’ NO.\n TRICK — “FA-PK” members\n💡\nFazl Ali + Panikkar + Kunzru = FA-PK.\nChairman Fazl Ali; members K.M. Panikkar & H.N. Kunzru.\n6. 1956 Reorganization + First Linguistic State\n• 1950 mein states = 4 categories A, B, C, D\n• State Reorganization Act = 1956\n• 7th Constitutional Amendment = 1956\n• Result = 14 States + 6 UTs\n• First linguistic state = Andhra Pradesh (1953), carved from Madras State\n• Demand led by Potti Sriramulu\n TRICK — “1953 Andhra First, 1956 Big Reorganization”\n💡\nAndhra Pradesh pehle 1953 mein bana; Fazl Ali report/reorganization ke baad nahi.\n1956 ka final count: 14 States + 6 UTs.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFirst linguistic state = Andhra Pradesh (1953). Ye Fazl Ali Commission ke baad nahi, usse pehle bana.\n7. States Formed After 1950 — Main Chronology\n• 1953\n Andhra Pradesh\n→\n• 1960\n Maharashtra + Gujarat\n→\n• 1963\n Nagaland\n→\n• 1966\n Haryana\n→\n• 1971\n Himachal Pradesh\n→\n• 1972\n Meghalaya + Manipur + Tripura\n→\n• 1975\n Sikkim\n→\n• 1987\n Goa + Arunachal Pradesh + Mizoram\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Union & Its Territories\n TRICK — “AaM GuNaH Hi Megh ManTra Si GArMi de sakta hai”\n💡\nAa = Andhra, M = Maharashtra, Gu = Gujarat, Na = Nagaland, H = Haryana, Hi = Himachal,\nMegh = Meghalaya, Man = Manipur, Tra = Tripura, Si = Sikkim, G = Goa, Ar = Arunachal, Mi = Mizoram.\n TRICK — Same-year cluster trick\n💡\n1960 = M-G (Maharashtra + Gujarat).\n1972 = M-M-T (Meghalaya + Manipur + Tripura).\n1987 = G-A-M (Goa + Arunachal + Mizoram).\n8. Sikkim — 35\n 36\n 371F\n→\n→\n• 35th Amendment 1974\n Associated State Status\n→\n• 36th Amendment 1975\n Full Statehood; 22nd State\n→\n• Special provision\n Article 371F\n→\n TRICK — “35 Associate, 36 State, F = Sikkim”\n💡\n35th = Associated State; next 36th = Full Statehood.\n371F ko Sikkim ke final special tag ki tarah yaad karo.\n9. Article 371 Series — State Matching\n• 371\n Maharashtra & Gujarat\n→\n• 371A\n Nagaland\n→\n• 371B\n Assam\n→\n• 371C\n Manipur\n→\n• 371D\n Andhra Pradesh & Telangana\n→\n• 371F\n Sikkim\n→\n• 371G\n Mizoram\n→\n• 371H\n Arunachal Pradesh\n→\n• 371I\n Goa\n→\n• 371J\n Karnataka (98th Amendment, 2012)\n→\n TRICK — “A-N, B-A, C-M, D-AP/T, F-S, G-M, H-A, I-G, J-K”\n💡\nLetter-pair chain bolo: A-Nagaland, B-Assam, C-Manipur, D-Andhra/Telangana, F-Sikkim, G-Mizoram, H-Arunachal, I-Goa, J-\nKarnataka.\nPlain 371 = Maharashtra + Gujarat.\n TRICK — “J = Karnataka + 98th”\n💡\n371J ko Karnataka ke saath fix karo; source notes mein 98th Amendment 2012 bhi linked hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part1 Art1–4\n 1 Naam/Territory, 2 Admission, 3 Reorganization, 4 No-368/Simple Majority\n India Indestructible Union\n\n→\n→\n→\nBerubari Transfer=Amendment, Maganbhai Boundary=No Amendment\n Dhar NO, JVP NO, Fazl YES + Panikkar/Kunzru\n\n→\n→\nAndhra 1953 first linguistic\n 1956 = 14 States+6 UTs\n State years: AaM GuNaH Hi Megh ManTra Si GArMi\n Sikkim 35\n→\n→\n→\nAssociate, 36 State, 371F\n 371 chain: 371 MG, A-Naga, B-Assam, C-Manipur, D-AP/Telangana, F-Sikkim, G-Mizoram, H-\n→\nArunachal, I-Goa, J-Karnataka.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nArt.3 = Simple Majority/No Art.368 | Andhra Pradesh 1953 = first linguistic state | Berubari transfer needs\namendment vs Maganbhai boundary dispute does not."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Citizenship\nCITIZENSHIP — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Articles 5–11, Citizenship Act 1955, acquire/lose methods, CAA 2019, OCI–NRI aur exam traps ko\nfast recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Part II + Articles 5–11 — Full Article Chain\n• Part II\n Articles 5–11\n→\n• Single Citizenship\n borrowed from UK\n→\n• Articles 5–8\n Citizenship before 26 Jan 1950\n→\n• Articles 9–11\n Post-Constitution continuation / Parliament law-making framework\n→\n TRICK — “5 Start, 6 Come, 7 Go, 8 Abroad, 9 Stop, 10 Continue, 11 Law”\n💡\n5 = Citizenship at commencement.\n6 = Pakistan\n India migration.\n→\n7 = India\n Pakistan migration.\n→\n8 = Indian origin living abroad.\n9 = Termination, 10 = Continuance, 11 = Parliament makes citizenship law.\n2. Article 6 vs 7 — Direction + Date Trap\n• Article 6\n Pakistan\n India; before 19 July 1948\n→\n→\n• Article 7\n India\n Pakistan; after 1 March 1947\n→\n→\n TRICK — “6 COMES IN, 7 GOES OUT”\n💡\n6 = Pakistan se India aaya (Come In)\n before 19 July 1948.\n→\n7 = India se Pakistan gaya (Go Out)\n after 1 March 1947.\n→\nDirection pehle bolo, phir date.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArticle 6 aur 7 mein direction aur cutoff dono alag hain: 6 = Pak\nIndia / before 19 Jul 1948; 7 = India\nPak / after 1 Mar 1947.\n→\n→\n3. Citizenship Act 1955 — 6 Amendment Years\n• Act enforced\n 30 December 1955\n→\n• 1986\n 1st amendment\n→\n• 1992\n 2nd\n→\n• 2003\n 3rd\n→\n• 2005\n 4th; OCI introduced\n→\n• 2015\n 5th\n→\n• 2019\n 6th; CAA 2019\n→\n TRICK — “86–92–03–05–15–19” year ladder\n💡\nSix amendment years ko pair mein bolo: 86-92 | 03-05 | 15-19.\nDo anchor years: 2005 = OCI, 2019 = CAA."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Citizenship\n4. Citizenship Acquire 5, Lose 3\n5 Ways to Acquire\n• Birth\n• Descent\n• Registration\n 7 years residence\n→\n• Naturalisation\n 12 years residence\n→\n• Incorporation of Territory\n TRICK — “B-D-R-N-I”\n💡\nBirth\n Descent\n Registration\n Naturalisation\n Incorporation.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nNumber hook: Registration = 7, Naturalisation = 12.\n3 Ways to Lose\n• Renunciation\n self-given up\n→\n• Deprivation\n Government deprives\n→\n• Termination\n voluntarily acquiring another country's citizenship\n→\n TRICK — “R-D-T = Renounce, Deprive, Terminate”\n💡\nR = khud chhoda, D = government ne chhin liya, T = doosri citizenship lene se terminate.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRegistration = 7 years; Naturalisation = 12 years. CAA beneficiaries ke liye source notes naturalisation ko 6 years batate hain.\n5. CAA 2019 — 3 Countries + 6 Communities + 3 Dates\n• 3 countries\n Bangladesh, Afghanistan, Pakistan\n→\n• Arrival cutoff\n on or before 31 December 2014\n→\n• 6 communities\n Hindu, Sikh, Parsi, Buddhist, Christian, Jain\n→\n• Naturalisation\n 12 years reduced to 6 years\n→\n• Implemented across country from\n 11 March 2024\n→\n• Muslims from these 3 countries\n not covered\n→\n• Sri Lanka, Myanmar etc.\n not covered\n→\n TRICK — “BAP + Hi-Si-Par-Bu-Ch-Ja”\n💡\nCountries: B-A-P = Bangladesh, Afghanistan, Pakistan.\nCommunities rhythm: Hindu–Sikh–Parsi–Buddhist–Christian–Jain.\nDate chain: 31 Dec 2014 cutoff\n CAA 2019\n 11 Mar 2024 implementation.\n→\n→\n TRICK — “12\n 6 = Half”\n💡\n→\nCAA beneficiaries ke liye source sheet mein naturalisation period 12 se 6 years diya hai — half ho gaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCAA = sirf 3 countries + 6 listed non-Muslim communities. Sri Lanka/Myanmar included nahi; Muslims listed beneficiaries\nmein nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Citizenship\n6. OCI — 2005 Se, Visa Hai; Political Rights Nahi\n• OCI initiated\n 2005 (4th amendment to Citizenship Act)\n→\n• Lifetime visa-free travel to India\n• Educational & cultural benefits\n• Can own non-agricultural property\n• No voting rights\n• Cannot contest elections\n• Cannot hold constitutional posts\n• No agricultural land ownership\n TRICK — “OCI = Overseas Card, not Indian Citizen”\n💡\nOCI ko travel/education/culture benefits milte hain, political citizenship rights nahi.\nEasy contrast: Visa-free YES; Vote NO.\n7. NRI vs OCI — Citizen vs Foreign National\n• NRI = Indian citizen living abroad\n• NRI\n Indian passport + voting rights + full political rights\n→\n• OCI = foreign national; not Indian citizen\n• OCI\n foreign passport + lifetime visa-free entry; no political rights\n→\n TRICK — “NRI = Nation's Real Indian; OCI = Overseas Card Identity”\n💡\nNRI ko pehle 'Indian Citizen' label karo.\nOCI ko pehle 'Foreign National' label karo.\nPhir baaki sab automatically yaad: NRI vote YES; OCI vote NO.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nOCI holder ko lifetime visa-free entry milti hai, lekin voting/election/constitutional post rights nahi. NRI = Indian citizen with\nfull citizenship rights.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part II Art 5–11\n 5 Start, 6 Pak\nIndia, 7 India\nPak, 8 Abroad, 9 Stop, 10 Continue, 11 Parliament Law\n 6 before 19-Jul-48,\n→\n→\n→\n→\n7 after 1-Mar-47\n Citizenship Act 1955; amendments 86-92-03-05-15-19 (05 OCI, 19 CAA)\n Acquire B-D-R-N-I; Registration7,\n→\n→\nNaturalisation12\n Lose R-D-T\n CAA BAP + Hindu-Sikh-Parsi-Buddhist-Christian-Jain; cutoff 31-Dec-2014; 12\n6; 11-Mar-2024\n→\n→\n→\n\n OCI 2005 = visa/education/culture but no politics\n NRI = Indian citizen, OCI = foreign national.”\n→\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nArt.6 Pak\nIndia vs Art.7 India\nPak dates | CAA = 3 countries + 6 communities | NRI = Indian citizen, OCI = foreign\n→\n→\nnational with no political rights."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Fundamental Rights\nFUNDAMENTAL RIGHTS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 7 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part III, 6 Fundamental Rights, article map, Equality/Freedom blocks, writs, emergency exceptions\naur exam traps ko fast recall format mein diya gaya hai.\n1. FR Skeleton — Part III, 12–35, 7 Se 6\n• Fundamental Rights = Part III, Articles 12–35\n• Justiciable = Court mein enforce kiye ja sakte hain\n• Source = US Constitution\n• Originally 7 Fundamental Rights; now 6\n• Right to Property removed by 44th Amendment, 1978\n now Legal Right under Article 300A\n→\n• Article 32 = 'Heart & Soul of the Constitution' — Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n TRICK — “III–12/35–7\n6–300A–32 Heart”\n💡\n→\nChapter ka number spine: Part III\n Art 12–35\n 7 se 6 Rights\n Property = 300A\n Art 32 = Heart & Soul.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n44th Amendment 1978 ko Property removal ke saath chipka lo.\n2. 6 Fundamental Rights — Full Range Trick\n• Right to Equality\n Articles 14–18\n→\n• Right to Freedom\n 19–22\n→\n• Right against Exploitation\n 23–24\n→\n• Freedom of Religion\n 25–28\n→\n• Cultural & Educational Rights\n 29–30\n→\n• Constitutional Remedies\n Article 32\n→\n TRICK — “EVERY FOOL EATS RIPE CUSTARD REGULARLY”\n💡\nEvery = Equality, Fool = Freedom, Eats = Exploitation, Ripe = Religion, Custard = Cultural/Educational, Regularly = Remedies.\nArticle ranges naturally climb: 14–18\n 19–22\n 23–24\n 25–28\n 29–30\n 32.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n3. Citizens Only vs Everyone — High-Frequency Trap\n• Only Indian Citizens\n Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, 30\n→\n• Indians + Foreigners both\n Articles 14, 20, 21, 21A, 22–28\n→\n• Article 19 freedoms = citizens only\n• Article 21 Right to Life = available to all\n TRICK — “15-16-19-29-30 = Citizen Club”\n💡\nCitizen-only cluster ko ek number string bana ke bolo: 15, 16, 19, 29, 30.\nSpecial contrast: 19 = citizen only; 21 = everyone.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt. 19 foreigners ko available nahi; Art. 21 sabke liye available hai.\n4. Right to Equality — Articles 14–18\n• Art 14\n Equality before Law + Equal Protection of Law\n→\n• Art 15\n No discrimination\n→\n• Art 16\n Equal opportunity in public employment\n→\n• Art 17\n Abolition of Untouchability\n→\n• Art 18\n Abolition of Titles\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Fundamental Rights\n TRICK — “DOUBT” for 15–18\n💡\nD = Discrimination (15), O = Opportunity (16), U = Untouchability (17), T = Titles (18).\nArt 14 ko base Equality article ke roop mein alag anchor karo.\nReservation / Equality Hooks\n• 15(3)\n Special provisions for Women & Children\n→\n• 15(4)\n SC/ST/OBC reservation in educational institutions\n→\n• 15(5)\n Reservation in private educational institutions\n→\n• 15(6)\n EWS reservation in educational institutions\n→\n• 16(4)\n SC/ST/OBC reservation in jobs\n→\n• 16(6)\n EWS jobs\n→\n• Art 17 linked in notes with Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955\n TRICK — “15 = Education/Social, 16 = Employment”\n💡\n15 ke reservation clauses ko education/social side samjho; 16 ko public employment/jobs side.\nEWS = 15(6) education + 16(6) jobs.\n5. Right to Freedom — 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22\nArticle 19 — 6 Freedoms\n• Speech & Expression\n• Peaceful Assembly\n• Associations / Unions\n• Move Freely throughout India\n• Reside Anywhere in India\n• Practice Any Profession / Occupation\n TRICK — “S-A-A-M-R-P”\n💡\nSpeech\n Assembly\n Association\n Move\n Reside\n Profession.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nArt. 19 mein originally 7 freedoms thi; property freedom remove hone ke baad 6.\nArticles 20–22\n• Art 20\n No ex-post-facto punishment; No Double Jeopardy; No Self-incrimination\n→\n• Art 21\n Right to Life & Personal Liberty; notes include privacy, sleep, electricity, travel abroad, education, dignity,\n→\nlivelihood\n• Art 21A\n Free & Compulsory Education age 6–14; 86th Amendment 2002; RTE Act 2009, enforced 2010\n→\n• Art 22\n Protection against Arrest & Detention; ordinary arrest safeguards include reason, lawyer, magistrate within\n→\n24 hours\n• Preventive Detention\n maximum 3 months; extension with Advisory Board approval\n→\n TRICK — “20 = Triple NO; 21 = LIFE; 21A = 6–14 School; 22 = Arrest”\n💡\nArt 20 ka 3-NO pack: no ex-post-facto, no double jeopardy, no self-incrimination.\n21A ko age 6–14 se lock karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPreventive detention mein 24-hour magistrate rule apply nahi hota; source notes is safeguard ko ordinary arrest ke liye\nbatate hain.\nArt. 20 & 21 Emergency mein bhi suspend nahi hote."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Fundamental Rights\n6. Exploitation + Religion + Minority Rights\n• Art 23\n Human trafficking, forced labour, begar prohibited\n→\n• Art 24\n Below 14 children: factories/mines/hazardous work prohibited\n→\n• Art 25\n Conscience; profess, practice & propagate religion\n→\n• Art 26\n Manage religious affairs\n→\n• Art 27\n No taxation for religious promotion\n→\n• Art 28\n Religious instruction in educational institutions\n→\n• Art 29\n Minority language/script/culture protection\n→\n• Art 30\n Minorities can establish & administer educational institutions\n→\n TRICK — “23 Begar, 24 Bachcha; 25–28 Religion; 29–30 Minority”\n💡\n23–24 ko exploitation pair samjho.\n25–28 pure religion block hai.\n29–30 minority cultural/education block hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt. 24 = hazardous/factory/mine child labour ban; notes ise Constitution mein complete child-labour ban nahi batate.\nArt. 25 ka 'propagate' = forceful conversion ka right nahi.\n7. Article 32 vs 226 — Supreme Court vs High Court\n• Art 32\n Supreme Court; only Fundamental Rights\n→\n• Art 226\n High Courts; Fundamental Rights + Legal Rights\n→\n• High Court jurisdiction wider\n TRICK — “32 = SC/FR only; 226 = HC/FR + Legal”\n💡\n32 ko Supreme Court ka Fundamental-Rights emergency door samjho.\n226 ka scope wider — FR ke saath legal rights bhi.\n8. 5 Writs — Meaning + Purpose\n• Habeas Corpus\n illegal detention; person ko court ke saamne pesh karo\n→\n• Mandamus\n public authority ko duty perform karne ka command\n→\n• Quo-Warranto\n public office kis authority se hold kiya?\n→\n• Certiorari\n lower court order ko quash\n→\n• Prohibition\n lower court ko jurisdiction exceed karne se stop\n→\n TRICK — “Ha-Ma-Qu-Ce-Pro”\n💡\nHabeas\n Mandamus\n Quo-Warranto\n Certiorari\n Prohibition.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nPurpose code: Body\n Command\n Authority\n Quash\n Stop.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n TRICK — “C = Completed, P = Pending”\n💡\nCertiorari = case decided/completed ke baad quash.\nProhibition = case pending rehte prevent/stop.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCertiorari aur Prohibition ka sabse important distinction: decided-after vs pending-before."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Fundamental Rights\n9. Property + Emergency + Articles 33–35\n• Right to Property\n Legal Right, Article 300A; FR nahi\n→\n• 44th Amendment 1978\n Property FR removed\n→\n• Art 33\n Parliament may restrict rights of Armed Forces\n→\n• Art 34\n Restrictions during Martial Law\n→\n• Art 35\n Parliament's power to legislate for enforcement of certain FRs\n→\n• FR suspension during Emergency\n Articles 358 & 359\n→\n• Art 20 & 21\n never suspended even during Emergency\n→\n• FR amendable, but Basic Structure cannot be destroyed\n TRICK — “33 Army, 34 Martial, 35 Law”\n💡\n33 = Armed Forces restrictions, 34 = Martial Law, 35 = Parliament makes enforcement laws.\nEmergency exception ko red-circle karo: 20 & 21 safe.\n10. Equality Cases — Number Hooks\n• Balaji v. State of Mysore (1963)\n Reservation cap introduced\n→\n• Mandal Commission (1979)\n 2nd Backward Class Commission; OBC reservation\n→\n• Indra Sawhney (1992)\n notes link 50% reservation cap / promotion issue\n→\n• Kesavananda Bharati (1973)\n Basic Structure doctrine\n→\n• EWS 10%\n 103rd Amendment, 2019\n→\n TRICK — “63 Balaji, 73 Keshavananda, 79 Mandal, 92 Indra, 2019 EWS”\n💡\nCase/commission years ko timeline ki tarah yaad karo: 63\n 73\n 79\n 92\n 2019.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nTopic hooks: reservation cap / basic structure / OBC commission / reservation / EWS.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part III 12–35, US source, Justiciable, 7\n6 after 44th/1978; Property=300A\n 6 Rights: Every Fool Eats Ripe Custard Regularly\n→\n→\n Citizen club 15-16-19-29-30\n Equality 14–18: DOUBT (15 Discrimination,16 Opportunity,17 Untouchability,18 Titles)\n\n→\n→\n→\nFreedom: 19 SAAMRP; 20 Triple-NO; 21 Life; 21A 6–14/86th; 22 Arrest/Detention\n 23 Begar,24 Child hazardous work\n 25–28\n→\n→\n\nReligion\n 29–30 Minority\n 32 SC only FR vs 226 HC FR+Legal\n Writs Ha-Ma-Qu-Ce-Pro; C=Completed, P=Pending\n 33\n→\n→\n→\n→\nArmed,34 Martial,35 Parliament Law\n Emergency: 20 & 21 safe.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nArt.19 citizens only vs Art.21 everyone | Art.20 & 21 never suspended in Emergency | Certiorari = decided-after,\nProhibition = pending-before."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Directive Principles of State Policy\nDIRECTIVE PRINCIPLES OF STATE POLICY — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 8 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part IV, Articles 36–51, Socialist/Gandhian/Liberal classification, amendments, FR-vs-DPSP cases\naur high-confusion article pairs ko fast recall format mein diya gaya hai.\n1. DPSP Skeleton — Part IV, 36–51, Irish, Non-Justiciable\n• DPSP = Part IV, Articles 36–51\n• Source = Irish Constitution, specifically Article 45\n• Nature = Non-Justiciable; court mein directly enforce nahi kar sakte\n• Goal = Social & Economic Democracy\n• Article 36 = 'State' definition, same as Article 12\n• Article 37 = Not enforceable, but fundamental in governance\n TRICK — “IV–36/51–Irish–No Court–Governance”\n💡\nChapter ka master spine: Part IV\n Art 36–51\n Irish source\n Non-Justiciable\n Fundamental in Governance.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n36 = State definition; 37 = court nahi, governance mein fundamental.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDPSP enforceable nahi hain, lekin Article 37 ke according governance mein fundamental hain.\n2. Scholar Quotes — Naam Ko Quote Se Lock Karo\n• Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n 'Novel Features of Indian Constitution'\n→\n• Granville Austin\n 'Soul of the Constitution'\n→\n• Prof. K.T. Shah\n 'Cheque payable at the convenience of the bank'\n→\n• K.C. Wheare\n 'Declaration of goals and aspirations'\n→\n• Sir Ivor Jennings\n 'Pious aspiration'\n→\n TRICK — “A-Novel, Austin-Soul, Shah-Cheque, Wheare-Goals, Jennings-Pious”\n💡\nAmbedkar = Novel Features; Granville Austin = Soul.\nShah = Cheque; Wheare = Goals; Jennings = Pious aspiration.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmbedkar ne Article 32/FR ko 'Heart & Soul' kaha, DPSP ko 'Novel Features'. DPSP ka 'Soul of Constitution' = Granville Austin.\n3. DPSP Classification — 3 Buckets\nSocialist Principles\n• 38\n Social order / welfare; 38(2) minimize income inequalities\n→\n• 39\n Livelihood, resources, wealth distribution, equal pay, worker/child protection\n→\n• 39A\n Free Legal Aid\n→\n• 41\n Right to work, education, public assistance\n→\n• 42\n Just & humane work conditions + maternity relief\n→\n• 43\n Living wage for workers (Common)\n→\n• 43A\n Workers' participation in industrial management\n→\n• 47\n Nutrition & standard of living (Common)\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Directive Principles of State Policy\n TRICK — “38 Welfare, 39 Policy, 39A Aid, 41 Work, 42 Work-conditions, 43 Wage, 47 Nutrition”\n💡\nSocialist block ko welfare-worker-equality engine samjho.\nKey anchors: 39A Legal Aid, 41 Work, 42 Maternity, 43 Wage, 47 Nutrition.\nGandhian Principles\n• 40\n Village Panchayats / Gram Swaraj\n→\n• 43\n Living wage (Common)\n→\n• 43B\n Cooperative Societies\n→\n• 46\n SC/ST & weaker sections\n→\n• 47\n Nutrition & standard of living (Common)\n→\n• 48\n Agriculture & animal husbandry\n→\n TRICK — “P-W-C-W-N-A” Gandhian chain\n💡\nPanchayat\n Wage\n Cooperative\n Weaker Sections\n Nutrition\n Agriculture.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nGandhian picture = village, cooperative, weaker sections, agriculture.\nLiberal-Intellectual Principles\n• 44\n Uniform Civil Code (UCC)\n→\n• 45\n Early childhood care & education below 6 years\n→\n• 48\n Agriculture & animal husbandry on modern lines\n→\n• 48A\n Environment protection\n→\n• 49\n Monuments of national importance\n→\n• 50\n Separation of Judiciary from Executive\n→\n• 51\n International peace & security\n→\n TRICK — “44 UCC, 45 Child, 48A Environment, 49 Monument, 50 Judiciary, 51 Peace”\n💡\n44–51 ke end block ko rights/environment/institutions/peace chain samjho.\nMost direct anchors: 44 UCC, 48A Environment, 50 Judiciary separation, 51 Peace.\n4. Common DPSPs — Sirf 2 Articles\n• Article 43 = Living wage for workers\n• Article 47 = Nutrition & standard of living\n• Source notes classify both as Socialist + Gandhian common articles\n TRICK — “43 Wage, 47 Plate”\n💡\n43 = Wage; 47 = Plate/Nutrition.\nDono Common DPSPs — Socialist bhi, Gandhian bhi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCommon articles = 43 & 47. Ye classification question mein frequently trap bante hain.\n5. Article 39(a–f) — Six Clauses Ka Memory Code\n• 39(a)\n Adequate livelihood\n→\n• 39(b)\n Material resources for common good\n→\n• 39(c)\n Avoid concentration of wealth\n→\n• 39(d)\n Equal pay for equal work\n→\n• 39(e)\n Protect workers' health & children's rights\n→\n• 39(f)\n Children grow with freedom & dignity\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Directive Principles of State Policy\n TRICK — “L-M-W-P-H-C”\n💡\nLivelihood\n Material resources\n Wealth concentration\n Pay equal\n Health\n Children.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n39(d) = Equal Pay; 39(f) later amendment list mein bhi yaad aayega.\n6. Amendments — 42, 44, 86, 97\n• 42nd Amendment\n 4 DPSP additions: 39(f), 39A, 43A, 48A\n→\n• 44th Amendment\n Article 38(2): minimize income inequalities\n→\n• 86th Amendment, 2002\n Article 45 modified: now below 6 years childhood care\n→\n• 6–14 years education shifted to Article 21A (Fundamental Right)\n• 97th Amendment\n Article 43B: promotion of cooperative societies\n→\n TRICK — “42 = FOUR adds”\n💡\n42nd ko 4 additions ke saath lock karo: 39(f), 39A, 43A, 48A.\nA-suffix pattern dekho: 39A, 43A, 48A + 39(f).\n TRICK — “44\n38(2), 86\n45, 97\n43B”\n💡\n→\n→\n→\n44th = inequality clause 38(2).\n86th = Article 45 child below 6; 6–14 goes to 21A.\n97th = Cooperative = 43B.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n86th Amendment ke baad Article 45 = below 6 years; 6–14 education = Article 21A (FR).\n7. FR vs DPSP — Part III vs Part IV\n• FR\n Part III, Articles 12–35, Justiciable\n→\n• DPSP\n Part IV, Articles 36–51, Non-Justiciable\n→\n• FR\n Individual-centric; Democratic & Civil Rights\n→\n• DPSP\n Group/Society-centric; Social & Economic Democracy\n→\n• FR\n Restrictions / negative nature\n→\n• DPSP\n Positive duty / directions to State\n→\n TRICK — “III = Individual + Court; IV = Society + Direction”\n💡\nPart III ko individual enforceable rights samjho.\nPart IV ko State ke positive social-economic directions samjho.\n8. FR vs DPSP Cases — Evolution Chain\n• 1951 Champakam Dorairajan\n FR above DPSP\n→\n• 1967 Golaknath\n Parliament cannot curtail FRs to implement DPSPs\n→\n• 1973 Keshavananda Bharati\n Basic Structure Doctrine\n→\n• 1980 Minerva Mills\n FR & DPSP complementary and equal; balance required\n→\n TRICK — “C-G-K-M = Upar\n Protect\n Basic\n Balance”\n💡\n→\n→\n→\nChampakam = FR upar.\nGolaknath = FR protect.\nKeshavananda = Basic Structure.\nMinerva Mills = Balance / both equal.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFinal balance point in source notes = Minerva Mills (1980): FR and DPSP complementary and equal importance."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Directive Principles of State Policy\n9. DPSP Implemented Through Laws — Real-World Hooks\n• Article 41 Right to Work\n MNREGA Act, 2005\n→\n• Right to Education\n RTE Act, 2009; enforced 2010\n→\n• Maternity / Women\n Maternity Benefit Act, 1961\n→\n• Environment\n Wildlife Protection Act, 1972 + Biological Diversity Act, 2002\n→\n• Democratic Decentralization\n 73rd & 74th Amendments + PESA Act, 1996\n→\n• 73rd = Panchayati Raj (Rural), 74th = Nagar Palikas (Urban); passed 1992, effective 1993\n TRICK — “41 = Work = MNREGA”\n💡\nMNREGA ko Article 41 se direct connect karo — DPSP implementation ka clean exam example.\n73 Rural / 74 Urban ko pair mein revise karo.\n10. High-Yield Article Flash Chain\n• 36 State definition | 37 Governance fundamental\n• 39A Legal Aid | 40 Panchayat | 41 Work | 42 Maternity\n• 43 Wage | 43A Worker participation | 43B Cooperative\n• 44 UCC | 45 Child below 6 | 46 Weaker sections | 47 Nutrition\n• 48 Agriculture | 48A Environment | 49 Monuments | 50 Judiciary separation | 51 Peace\n TRICK — “39A Aid\n 40 Village\n 41 Work\n 42 Maternity\n 43 Wage\n 44 UCC\n 45 Child\n 48A\n💡\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nEnvironment\n 50 Judiciary\n 51 Peace”\n→\n→\nYe anchor chain poore Article 36–51 map ko quickly reconstruct karne mein help karega.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part IV 36–51\n Irish Art45\n Non-Justiciable but Art37 fundamental in governance\n Quotes: Ambedkar-Novel, Austin-Soul\n→\n→\n→\n\n 3 categories: Socialist welfare/workers, Gandhian village/cooperative/agri, Liberal UCC/environment/judiciary/peace\n\n→\n→\nCommon 43 Wage + 47 Nutrition\n 39 clauses L-M-W-P-H-C\n Amendments: 42=4 adds (39f,39A,43A,48A), 44=38(2), 86=45\n→\n→\nbelow6 + 21A for 6–14, 97=43B\n Cases CGKM: Champakam FR>DPSP, Golaknath protect FR, Keshavananda Basic Structure,\n→\nMinerva Balance\n Implementation: 41-MNREGA, RTE, Maternity, Environment, 73 Rural/74 Urban.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nSource = Irish Constitution | Common DPSPs = 43 & 47 | 86th Amendment: Art.45 below 6, while 6–14 moved to Art.21A."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Fundamental Duties\nFUNDAMENTAL DUTIES — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 9 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part IV-A, Article 51A, 11 Duties, 42nd/86th Amendments, Swaran Singh & Verma Committees aur\nFR–DPSP–FD traps ko fast recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — IV-A, 51A, 10\n11, USSR\n→\n• Fundamental Duties = Part IV-A, Article 51A\n• Added by 42nd Amendment, 1976\n• Based on Swaran Singh Committee recommendations\n• Source = USSR (Former Soviet Union) Constitution\n• Originally 10 Duties; currently 11\n• 11th Duty added by 86th Amendment, 2002\n• Nature = Non-Justiciable\n• Applicable only to Indian Citizens, not foreigners\n TRICK — “IV-A\n 51A\n 42\n 10\n 86\n 11\n USSR”\n💡\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nNumber chain bolo: Part IV-A, Article 51A, 42nd Amendment se 10 duties, 86th Amendment se 11th duty.\nSource ko end mein lock karo: USSR.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPart IV = DPSP; Part IV-A = Fundamental Duties. Dono ko swap mat karna.\n2. 11 Duties — Main Mnemonic: SCREAM VAN LIP\n• S\n Abide by Constitution; respect ideals, institutions, National Flag & Anthem — 51A(a)\n→\n• C\n Cherish noble ideals of national freedom struggle — 51A(b)\n→\n• R\n Uphold sovereignty, unity & integrity of India — 51A(c)\n→\n• E\n Defend the country & render national service when called — 51A(d)\n→\n• A\n Promote harmony & common brotherhood — 51A(e)\n→\n• M\n Preserve rich heritage of composite culture — 51A(f)\n→\n• V\n Protect & improve natural environment — 51A(g)\n→\n• A\n Develop scientific temper, humanism, inquiry & reform — 51A(h)\n→\n• N\n Safeguard public property & abjure violence — 51A(i)\n→\n• L\n Strive towards excellence — 51A(j)\n→\n• I\n Provide education opportunity to child/ward aged 6–14 — 51A(k)\n→\n TRICK — “SCREAM VAN LIP”\n💡\nS-C-R-E-A-M | V-A-N | L-I — isi order mein Article 51A(a) se 51A(k) tak duties chalte hain.\nLast I ko 'Instruction/Education' se yaad karo — 6–14 years.\n3. 51A(a) to 51A(k) — Letter-to-Article Chain\n• 51A(a) Constitution / Flag / Anthem\n• 51A(b) Freedom struggle ideals\n• 51A(c) Sovereignty, Unity, Integrity\n• 51A(d) Defence / National Service\n• 51A(e) Harmony / Brotherhood\n• 51A(f) Composite Culture\n• 51A(g) Environment\n• 51A(h) Scientific Temper\n• 51A(i) Public Property / Non-violence"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Fundamental Duties\n• 51A(j) Excellence\n• 51A(k) Child Education 6–14\n TRICK — “a to k = Constitution se Child Education tak”\n💡\nAlphabet ladder ko story ki tarah dekho: Constitution\n Freedom ideals\n Unity\n Defence\n Harmony\n Culture\n\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nEnvironment\n Science\n Property\n Excellence\n Education.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nIs story se clause-letter recall fast hota hai.\n4. Duty #11 — 86th Amendment Ka Special Trap\n• 11th Duty = Parent/Guardian must provide education opportunity to child/ward aged 6–14\n• Added by 86th Amendment, 2002\n• Article = 51A(k)\n• Source notes link it with Article 21A (FR) and Article 45 (DPSP)\n TRICK — “86 = Education Triangle”\n💡\n86th Amendment ko teen places se connect karo: 51A(k) parental duty + Art. 21A Right to Education + Art. 45 DPSP\nconnection.\nAge anchor = 6–14.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n42nd Amendment ne original 10 duties add ki; 11th duty 86th Amendment, 2002 se aayi.\n5. High-Yield Duty Hooks\n• Flag & Anthem\n 51A(a)\n→\n• Sovereignty, Unity, Integrity\n 51A(c)\n→\n• Environment\n 51A(g)\n→\n• Scientific Temper\n 51A(h)\n→\n• Public Property + Non-violence\n 51A(i)\n→\n• Excellence\n 51A(j)\n→\n• Education 6–14\n 51A(k)\n→\n TRICK — “a Flag, c Country, g Green, h Head/Science, i Infrastructure, j Excellence, k Kids”\n💡\nClause letters ko visual hooks se lock karo:\ng = Green environment, h = Head/scientific temper, i = Infrastructure/public property, k = Kids/education.\n6. Non-Justiciable — Lekin Meaningless Nahi\n• Fundamental Duties directly legally enforceable nahi\n• Constitution violation ke liye direct punishment mention nahi karta\n• Courts laws interpret karte waqt Duties ko consider kar sakti hain\n• Verma Committee, 1999\n reviewed and recommended strengthening of Fundamental Duties\n→\n• Applicable only to citizens\n TRICK — “No Direct Enforcement, Yes Court Consideration”\n💡\nNon-Justiciable ka matlab 'ignore' nahi.\nDirect constitutional punishment NO; interpretive relevance YES.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNon-Justiciable ≠ legally meaningless. Source notes specifically court consideration aur Verma Committee 1999 mention\nkarte hain."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Fundamental Duties\n7. Swaran Singh vs Verma Committee\n• Swaran Singh Committee\n Fundamental Duties add karne ki recommendation\n→\n• Verma Committee\n 1999 review / strengthening recommendations\n→\n TRICK — “Swaran = Start, Verma = Verify”\n💡\nSwaran Singh = duties ka START/addition recommendation.\nVerma 1999 = later VERIFY/review/strengthening.\n8. FR vs DPSP vs FD — 3-Part Comparison\n• Fundamental Rights\n Part III, Articles 12–35, Justiciable, individual rights\n→\n• DPSP\n Part IV, Articles 36–51, Non-Justiciable, State's duties\n→\n• Fundamental Duties\n Part IV-A, Article 51A, Non-Justiciable, Citizen's duties\n→\n• FR & DPSP were in Original Constitution; Fundamental Duties added in 1976\n TRICK — “III = Rights, IV = State Directions, IV-A = Citizen Duties”\n💡\nPart III = Individual ke rights.\nPart IV = State ko directions/duties.\nPart IV-A = Citizen ke duties.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFR source USA aur Duties source USSR — ye country-source pair ko ulta mat karna.\n9. 20-Second Flash Recall\n• Part IV-A | Article 51A\n• 42nd Amendment 1976 | Swaran Singh\n• USSR source | Non-Justiciable | Citizens only\n• 10 original\n 11 current\n→\n• 86th Amendment 2002\n 51A(k), child education 6–14\n→\n• Verma Committee 1999\n review\n→\n• Mnemonic = SCREAM VAN LIP\n TRICK — “42-Swaran-10 / 86-Education-11 / 99-Verma”\n💡\nThree timeline anchors: 1976 = add 10, 2002 = add 11th, 1999 = Verma review.\nExam mein year/committee/count ko isi triangle se answer karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part IV-A, Art 51A\n 42nd/1976 + Swaran Singh + USSR\n 10 original duties\n SCREAM VAN LIP: Constitution, Cherish\n→\n→\n→\nstruggle, Sovereignty, Defence, Harmony, Culture, Environment, Scientific temper, Public property, Excellence, Education\n\n→\n86th/2002 adds 51A(k), child 6–14 + link 21A/45\n Non-Justiciable, no direct constitutional punishment, courts may consider\n→\n Verma 1999 review\n FR Part III individual/justiciable; DPSP Part IV State/non-justiciable; FD Part IV-A citizen/non-\n→\n→\njusticiable.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nPart IV-A, not Part IV | 42nd = original 10, 86th = 11th duty | Source USSR, while Fundamental Rights source USA."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.10 President of India\nPRESIDENT OF INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 10 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part V Articles 52–73, eligibility, electoral college, powers, pardon, impeachment, key Presidents\naur article traps ko fast recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. President Skeleton — Part V, 52–73, Nominal Executive\n• President = Part V, Articles 52–73\n• Head of State + Supreme Commander + First Citizen\n• President = Nominal / De Jure Executive\n• Prime Minister = Real / De Facto Executive\n• President acts on Cabinet advice — Article 74\n• Term = 5 years; re-election = no limit\n TRICK — “President = Paper Power, PM = Practical Power”\n💡\nPresident ko legal/formal head samjho; real executive authority PM + Council of Ministers ke paas.\nArticle 74 = Cabinet advice anchor.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNominal/De Jure = President; Real/De Facto = Prime Minister. Ye sabse common role-swap trap hai.\n2. Eligibility & Personal Facts — 35, 5, CJI, VP\n• Minimum age = 35 years\n• Must be citizen of India\n• Must have Lok Sabha member eligibility\n• Must not hold office of profit\n• Term = 5 years\n• Salary = ₹5 lakh/month (Consolidated Fund of India)\n• Oath = Chief Justice of India, or senior-most judge\n• Resignation = Vice-President\n• Election dispute = Supreme Court, Article 71\n• Naturalized citizen can also become President (as per source notes)\n TRICK — “35–5–CJI–VP–71 SC”\n💡\n35 age, 5-year term, oath CJI, resignation VP, election dispute Art.71 in Supreme Court.\nEk hi line mein revise karo: “35-5, CJI-VP, 71-SC.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nResignation Vice-President ko; oath CJI dilwate hain. Speaker/VP-oath ke saath confuse mat karna.\n3. Election Formula — Indirect + PR + STV + Secret\n• Election type = Indirect\n• System = Proportional Representation\n• Voting = Single Transferable Vote\n• Ballot = Secret\n• Security deposit = ₹15,000\n• Proposers + Seconders = 50 + 50\n• Dispute = Supreme Court, Article 71"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.10 President of India\n TRICK — “I-PR-STV-S”\n💡\nIndirect\n Proportional Representation\n Single Transferable Vote\n Secret Ballot.\n→\n→\n→\nNumbers: ₹15,000 deposit + 50 proposers + 50 seconders.\n4. Electoral College — Kaun Vote Karta Hai?\n• Elected Lok Sabha MPs\n YES\n→\n• Elected Rajya Sabha MPs\n YES\n→\n• Elected State MLAs\n YES\n→\n• Elected MLAs of Delhi & Puducherry\n YES\n→\n• MLCs / Vidhan Parishad members\n NO\n→\n• Nominated MPs / MLAs\n NO\n→\n TRICK — “Elected = Entry; Nominated/MLC = No Entry”\n💡\nPresidential election mein elected MPs + elected MLAs main voter block hai.\nUT exception in source notes: Delhi & Puducherry elected MLAs.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLegislative Council members vote nahi karte. Nominated MPs/MLAs bhi excluded hain.\n5. President Powers — E-L-J-E\n• Executive\n PM/Ministers, Governors, SC/HC Judges, Commission chairpersons, diplomats appointments\n→\n• Legislative\n Summon/Prorogue Parliament, dissolve Lok Sabha, assent/return/withhold bills, ordinances\n→\n• Judicial\n Article 72 pardoning powers\n→\n• Emergency\n Articles 352, 356, 360\n→\n TRICK — “E-L-J-E = Executive, Legislative, Judicial, Emergency”\n💡\nPresident ki 4 power-buckets ko ELJE bolo.\nEmergency number ladder: 352 National\n 356 President's Rule\n 360 Financial.\n→\n→\n6. Article 72 — 5 Pardoning Powers\n• Pardon\n punishment + conviction completely removed\n→\n• Commutation\n one punishment changed into a lighter punishment\n→\n• Reprieve\n temporary postponement, especially death sentence\n→\n• Respite\n special reason se sentence reduce\n→\n• Remission\n punishment quantity reduce; nature same\n→\n TRICK — “P-C-R-R-R”\n💡\nPardon\n Commutation\n Reprieve\n Respite\n Remission.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nMeaning chain: Finish\n Change\n Postpone\n Special Reduce\n Quantity Reduce.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n TRICK — “72 President, 161 Governor”\n💡\nArticle 72 = President pardoning powers.\nArticle 161 = Governor pardoning powers; source notes mark death-sentence pardon as President-only.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt.72 President vs Art.161 Governor ko swap mat karna."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.10 President of India\n7. Veto Hook — Pocket Veto\n• Giani Zail Singh (1982–87)\n Pocket Veto\n→\n• Postal Bill par assent nahi diya\n• Pocket veto = na assent dena, na return karna\n TRICK — “Zail = Zip the Bill in Pocket”\n💡\nGiani Zail Singh ko Postal Bill pocket mein rakhne wali image se yaad karo.\nNa assent, na return = Pocket Veto.\n8. Impeachment — Article 61\n• Nature = Quasi-judicial\n• Can start in either House\n• 14 days prior notice\n• Special Majority = not less than 2/3 of Total Membership\n• Both Houses must pass\n• Result = President removed\n• No President has been impeached so far (as stated in source notes)\n TRICK — “61–14–2/3–Both”\n💡\nArt.61\n 14-day notice\n 2/3 of total membership\n both Houses.\n→\n→\n→\nYe chaar-number chain impeachment ka core hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nImpeachment majority = 2/3 of TOTAL membership, not merely present & voting.\n9. Election vs Impeachment Voters — Opposite Pair\n• Elected MPs\n Election YES | Impeachment YES\n→\n• Elected MLAs\n Election YES | Impeachment NO\n→\n• Nominated MPs\n Election NO | Impeachment YES\n→\n TRICK — “MLA = Election only; Nominated MP = Impeachment only”\n💡\nDo opposite arrows yaad karo:\nMLA\n Election YES, Impeachment NO.\n→\nNominated MP\n Election NO, Impeachment YES.\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMLAs and nominated MPs ka election/impeachment role ulta hai — ye direct table-trap hai.\n10. Key Article Ladder — 52 to 62, then 71–74\n• 52\n President of India\n→\n• 53\n Union executive power vested in President\n→\n• 54\n Election of President\n→\n• 55\n Election procedure\n→\n• 56\n Term: 5 years\n→\n• 57\n Re-election\n→\n• 58\n Qualifications\n→\n• 59\n Conditions / office of profit\n→\n• 60\n Oath\n→\n• 61\n Impeachment\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.10 President of India\n• 62\n Vacancy\n→\n• 71\n Election dispute\n→\n• 72\n Pardoning powers\n→\n• 73\n Extent of Union executive power\n→\n• 74\n Council of Ministers aid & advice\n→\n TRICK — “52–62 = President Core; 71 Dispute, 72 Pardon, 74 Advice”\n💡\n52 se 62 tak President ke direct core articles.\nUske baad teen exam anchors: 71 SC dispute, 72 Pardon, 74 Cabinet advice.\n11. Presidents — Firsts & Unique Facts\n• Dr. Rajendra Prasad\n First President; longest serving; 2 terms\n→\n• Dr. S. Radhakrishnan\n First Vice-President to become President\n→\n• Dr. Zakir Hussain\n First to die in office\n→\n• V.V. Giri\n First Acting President, later elected; first elected as Independent candidate\n→\n• Justice Hidayatullah\n First CJI to become Acting President\n→\n• Neelam Sanjiva Reddy\n Elected unopposed\n→\n• Giani Zail Singh\n Pocket Veto\n→\n• K.R. Narayanan\n First Dalit President\n→\n• Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam\n Missile Man / People's President\n→\n• Pratibha Patil\n First Woman President\n→\n• Droupadi Murmu\n First Tribal President; 2nd Woman President\n→\n TRICK — “Rajendra–Zakir–Giri–Reddy–Zail–Narayanan–Patil–Murmu” anchors\n💡\nLong list ratne ke bajay exam-firsts ko anchor banao:\nFirst/Longest = Rajendra | Died in office = Zakir | Independent = Giri | Unopposed = Reddy | Pocket = Zail | Dalit =\nNarayanan | Woman = Patil | Tribal = Murmu.\n12. Rashtrapati Bhawan — Tiny Memory Block\n• Architect = Edwin Lutyens\n• Location = New Delhi\n• Mughal Garden\n Amrit Udyan\n→\n• Durbar Hall\n Gantantra Mandap\n→\n• Ashoka Hall\n Ashok Mandap\n→\n TRICK — “Lutyens + A-G-A”\n💡\nArchitect = Lutyens.\nRename chain: Amrit Udyan\n Gantantra Mandap\n Ashok Mandap.\n→\n→\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part V 52–73\n President Nominal/De Jure, PM Real/De Facto, Art74 advice\n 35 age, 5-year term, CJI oath, VP resignation,\n→\n→\n71-SC dispute\n Election I-PR-STV-Secret, ₹15k, 50+50\n Electoral College = elected MPs + elected MLAs incl.\n→\n→\nDelhi/Puducherry; MLC/nominated NO\n Powers ELJE; Emergency 352-356-360\n Art72 PCRRR pardons\n Zail Singh Pocket\n→\n→\n→\nVeto\n Impeachment Art61: 14 days, 2/3 total, both Houses\n MLA election-only, nominated MP impeachment-only\n 52–62\n→\n→\n→\ncore; 71 dispute, 72 pardon, 74 advice\n Firsts: Rajendra first/longest, Zakir died, Giri independent, Reddy unopposed, Zail\n→\npocket, Narayanan Dalit, Patil woman, Murmu tribal.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nPresident nominal vs PM real | Election: elected MPs/MLAs only, not MLC/nominated | Impeachment = 2/3 of total\nmembership in both Houses."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Prime Minister & Council of Ministers\nPRIME MINISTER & COUNCIL OF MINISTERS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 11 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Articles 74–78, Council of Ministers structure, 91st Amendment, PM role, Attorney General, +89\nmemory rule aur Prime Minister firsts ko fast recall format mein diya gaya hai.\n1. PM Skeleton — Part V, 74–78, Real Executive\n• Prime Minister = Real / De Facto Executive\n• President = Nominal / De Jure Executive\n• Council of Ministers aids & advises President\n• Part V\n Articles 74–78\n→\n• Council of Ministers = 3 types\n• 91st Amendment\n Ministers capped at 15% of Lok Sabha strength\n→\n TRICK — “PM = Practical Power, President = Paper/Formal Power”\n💡\nPM ko actual executive authority se jodo; President formal/nominal executive hai.\nChapter ka number spine: Part V\n 74–78\n 3 types\n 15% cap.\n→\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nReal Executive = Prime Minister; Nominal Executive = President.\n2. Council of Ministers — 3 Types\n• Cabinet Ministers\n Senior rank, Cabinet meetings, full portfolio\n→\n• Ministers of State (MoS)\n Independent or attached to Cabinet Minister\n→\n• Deputy Ministers\n Assist Cabinet Minister / MoS\n→\n TRICK — “C-M-D = Cabinet\n MoS\n Deputy”\n💡\n→\n→\nHierarchy ko top-to-bottom bolo: Cabinet\n Minister of State\n Deputy.\n→\n→\nCabinet = senior/full portfolio; MoS = middle; Deputy = assist.\n3. Advice to President — First Return, Second Binding\n• Council of Ministers advice\n first time President may return\n→\n• Second time\n advice binding\n→\n• Source notes link this with 44th Amendment, 1978\n• Council of Ministers collectively responsible to Lok Sabha\n• Loss of Lok Sabha confidence\n collective resignation\n→\n TRICK — “1st Return, 2nd Bind”\n💡\nAdvice rule ko sirf do-step picture mein yaad karo:\nFirst time President can return\n second time must accept.\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCollective responsibility = Lok Sabha ke prati, Rajya Sabha ke prati nahi.\n4. Eligibility & Appointment — 25, 30, 6, 15\n• Lok Sabha eligibility age = 25 years\n• Rajya Sabha eligibility age = 30 years\n• Non-MP minister/PM\n must become MP within 6 months\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Prime Minister & Council of Ministers\n• Maximum ministers = 15% of Lok Sabha strength, including PM\n• PM appointed by President\n• Other ministers appointed by President on PM's advice\n• Resignation\n President\n→\n• Salary\n Consolidated Fund of India, Article 75(6)\n→\n• Term\n 5 years or until Lok Sabha dissolved\n→\n TRICK — “25–30–6–15”\n💡\n25 = Lok Sabha, 30 = Rajya Sabha, 6 months = non-MP window, 15% = ministry cap.\nYe four-number chain eligibility + appointment ka core hai.\n TRICK — “91 = 15%”\n💡\n91st Amendment ko seedha 15% ministry limit se lock karo.\nSource example: Lok Sabha 543\n about 81 ministers including PM.\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n15% limit Lok Sabha strength par based hai, Rajya Sabha strength par nahi.\n5. PM's Core Role — Head, Leader, Link, Inform\n• Head of Council of Ministers\n• Leader of the House (Lok Sabha)\n• Key figure in Parliamentary Democracy\n• Real Executive\n• Link between President and Cabinet\n• Article 78\n PM must inform President about Cabinet decisions and furnish information\n→\n TRICK — “H-L-L-I = Head, Leader, Link, Inform”\n💡\nPM role ko 4 words mein yaad karo: Head of CoM\n Leader of House\n Link to President\n Inform under Art.78.\n→\n→\n→\nArticle 78 = President ko information dena.\n6. PM as Chairperson — N-N-N-I\n• NITI Aayog\n• NDMA — National Disaster Management Authority\n• National Integration Council\n• Indian Board of Wildlife\n• NITI Aayog replaced Planning Commission in 2015\n• PM = Ex-Officio Chairperson of NITI Aayog\n TRICK — “N-N-N-I”\n💡\nNITI\n NDMA\n National Integration Council\n Indian Board of Wildlife.\n→\n→\n→\n2015 = NITI Aayog replaces Planning Commission.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNITI Aayog mein PM Chairperson hai; Vice-Chairperson alag post hai.\n7. Key Articles 74–78 — One-Line Map\n• Article 74\n Council of Ministers to aid & advise President\n→\n• Article 75\n Appointment, tenure, qualifications of PM & Ministers\n→\n• 75(1)\n PM by President; other ministers on PM's advice\n→\n• 75(2)\n Ministers hold office during President's pleasure\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Prime Minister & Council of Ministers\n• 75(6)\n Salaries from Consolidated Fund of India\n→\n• Article 76\n Attorney General of India\n→\n• Article 77\n Conduct of Government business in President's name\n→\n• Article 78\n PM's duty to furnish information to President\n→\n TRICK — “74 Advice, 75 Ministers, 76 AG, 77 Business, 78 Information”\n💡\n74–78 ko ek straight ladder mein bolo:\nAdvice\n Ministers\n Attorney General\n Govt Business\n Information.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n8. Attorney General of India — Article 76\n• Article 76\n Attorney General of India\n→\n• Chief Legal Advisor / highest Law Officer of Government of India\n• Appointed by President\n• Qualification\n eligible to be Supreme Court Judge\n→\n• Can participate in proceedings of both Houses of Parliament\n• Cannot vote\n• Private legal practice not barred in source notes\n• Salary fixed by Government\n• First Attorney General\n M.C. Setalvad\n→\n• Source notes list R. Venkataramani as current Attorney General\n TRICK — “AG = Attend, but No Vote”\n💡\nAttorney General Parliament ke dono Houses mein bol/participate kar sakta hai, vote nahi.\nAG = constitutional post, Article 76.\n TRICK — “76 Centre, 165 State”\n💡\nAttorney General (Centre) = Art.76.\nAdvocate General (State) = Art.165.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAttorney General ≠ Solicitor General. Source notes: AG constitutional post (Art.76); Solicitor General has no constitutional\nbasis.\n9. +89 Rule — Centre to State Memory Trick\n• 74\n 163 : PM/CoM\n CM/State CoM\n→\n→\n• 72\n 161 : President Pardon\n Governor Pardon\n→\n→\n• 76\n 165 : Attorney General\n Advocate General\n→\n→\n• 79\n 168 : Parliament\n State Legislature\n→\n→\n• 80\n 169 : Rajya Sabha\n Legislative Council\n→\n→\n• 81\n 170 : Lok Sabha\n Legislative Assembly\n→\n→\n TRICK — “Centre Article + 89 = State Equivalent”\n💡\nExample: 74+89=163, 76+89=165, 81+89=170.\nYe sirf article-number mnemonic hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n+89 Rule constitutional provision nahi — sirf memory trick hai.\n10. Prime Ministers — High-Yield Firsts & Unique Facts\n• Jawaharlal Nehru\n Longest-serving PM\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Prime Minister & Council of Ministers\n• Gulzarilal Nanda\n First Acting PM\n→\n• Lal Bahadur Shastri\n 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan'; died in Tashkent\n→\n• Indira Gandhi\n First Woman PM; source notes mark her as from Rajya Sabha\n→\n• Morarji Desai\n First Non-Congress PM\n→\n• Charan Singh\n Never faced Lok Sabha\n→\n• Rajiv Gandhi\n Youngest PM\n→\n• V.P. Singh\n source notes mark first PM to resign after no-confidence vote\n→\n• P.V. Narasimha Rao\n First South Indian PM; LPG reforms 1991\n→\n• Atal Bihari Vajpayee\n Shortest tenure: 13 days (first stint)\n→\n• Dr. Manmohan Singh\n First Sikh PM; Rajya Sabha member\n→\n• Narendra Modi\n source notes mark first BJP-majority PM; 3 consecutive terms\n→\n TRICK — “Nehru Long, Vajpayee Short, Indira Woman, Morarji Non-Congress”\n💡\nFirst-round anchors: Nehru = longest, Vajpayee = 13-day shortest, Indira = first woman, Morarji = first non-Congress.\nSecond-round anchors: Charan = never faced LS, Manmohan = first Sikh, Rao = first South Indian, Nanda = first acting.\n11. FR-like Exam Traps — Fast Contrast\n• PM = Real Executive; President = Nominal Executive\n• CoM responsible to Lok Sabha\n• Advice second time binding (source notes: 44th Amendment)\n• 91st Amendment = 15% ministry cap\n• AG can participate but cannot vote\n• AG constitutional; Solicitor General not constitutional\n• +89 is mnemonic only\n TRICK — “Real–Lok Sabha–Second–15%–No Vote–+89 Trick”\n💡\nYe six trap-words exam se pehle ek baar zaroor bolo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part V 74–78\n PM Real/De Facto, President Nominal/De Jure\n CoM 3 types C-M-D\n Advice: 1st Return, 2nd Bind;\n→\n→\n→\nresponsible to Lok Sabha\n Eligibility 25 LS, 30 RS, non-MP 6 months, 91st=15% cap\n PM appointed President, others on PM\n→\n→\nadvice, salary Art75(6)\n PM role H-L-L-I; Art78 Inform President\n Chairpersons N-N-N-I, NITI 2015\n Article ladder 74\n→\n→\n→\nAdvice, 75 Ministers, 76 AG, 77 Business, 78 Information\n AG: attend both Houses but no vote; 76 Centre, 165 State\n +89:\n→\n→\n74\n163,72\n161,76\n165,79\n168,80\n169,81\n170\n PM anchors: Nehru longest, Nanda acting, Indira woman, Morarji non-\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nCongress, Charan no LS, Vajpayee 13 days, Manmohan Sikh, Rao South Indian.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nPM = Real Executive | 91st Amendment = max 15% of Lok Sabha strength | Attorney General can participate in\nParliament but cannot vote."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\nPARLIAMENT OF INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 12 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Lok Sabha vs Rajya Sabha, Speaker/Chairman, sessions, bills, veto, motions, committees,\nbudget/funds aur key Articles ko high-memory-load exam facts ke roop mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Parliament Skeleton — Part V, 79–122, P-L-R\n• Parliament = President + Lok Sabha + Rajya Sabha\n• Part V\n Articles 79–122\n→\n• Bicameral Legislature\n• Lok Sabha = Lower House / House of the People\n• Rajya Sabha = Upper House / Council of States\n• No bill becomes Act without President's assent\n TRICK — “P-L-R = President + Lok Sabha + Rajya Sabha”\n💡\nParliament ko sirf 3 blocks mein dekho: P-L-R.\nArticle 79 ko Parliament formation ka starting anchor banao.\n2. Lok Sabha vs Rajya Sabha — 55/54 vs 25/24 Pattern\n• Lok Sabha: Max 550 | Current 543 | Age 25 | Term 5 years | Dissolution possible\n• Rajya Sabha: Max 250 | Current 245 | Age 30 | Term 6 years per member | Permanent House\n• Rajya Sabha: 1/3 members retire every 2 years\n• Rajya Sabha nominated members = 12\n• Both Houses first session = 13 May 1952\n TRICK — “LS: 550–543–25–5 | RS: 250–245–30–6”\n💡\nLok Sabha numbers end around 5: 550, 543, age 25, term 5.\nRajya Sabha numbers: 250, 245, age 30, term 6.\nRS bonus: 1/3 retire every 2 years + 12 nominated.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRajya Sabha permanent House hai; Lok Sabha dissolve ho sakti hai. Dono ka first session 13 May 1952.\n3. Lok Sabha Special Numbers — 104, 84, Delimitation\n• 104th Amendment (2020)\n Anglo-Indian reservation / 2 nominated seats ended\n→\n• 1st Delimitation Commission\n 1952\n→\n• Total Delimitation Commissions in notes\n 1952, 1963, 1973, 2002\n→\n• 84th Amendment (2001)\n seats frozen till 2026 (as stated in source notes)\n→\n• Emergency: Lok Sabha term may extend 1 year; not beyond 6 months after emergency ends\n TRICK — “52–63–73–02 = Delimitation Four”\n💡\nDelimitation years ko 4-beat rhythm mein bolo: 52, 63, 73, 02.\n84th Amendment = seat-freeze anchor; 104th = Anglo-Indian nomination ended.\n4. Rajya Sabha — 238 + 12 = 250, Permanent Rotation\n• Max = 250\n 238 elected + 12 nominated\n→\n• Current in source notes = 245\n• Indirect election\n Proportional Representation + Single Transferable Vote\n→\n• MLAs vote in Rajya Sabha election\n• Nominated fields = Literature, Art, Science, Social Service"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\n• Bihar\n Rajya Sabha 16 seats; Lok Sabha 40 seats (source notes)\n→\n TRICK — “238 + 12 = 250; 1/3 every 2; term 6”\n💡\nRS ko rotating wheel samjho: 6-year term, har 2 saal mein 1/3 retirement.\n12 nominated = LASS: Literature, Art, Science, Social Service.\n5. Speaker & Chairman — Who Presides Where?\n• Lok Sabha Speaker + Deputy Speaker elected from LS members\n• Joint Sitting (Art. 108)\n Speaker presides\n→\n• If Speaker absent\n Deputy Speaker\n then Deputy Chairman of Rajya Sabha\n→\n→\n• Speaker has casting vote in tie\n• Speaker resignation\n Deputy Speaker; vice versa\n→\n• Rajya Sabha Chairman = Vice-President, Article 89(1)\n• Vice-President is not a member of either House\n• Pro-tem Speaker\n senior-most MP after LS election; appointed by President; administers oath & conducts Speaker\n→\nelection\n TRICK — “Joint Sitting: S > DS > DC”\n💡\nSpeaker\n Deputy Speaker\n Deputy Chairman.\n→\n→\nJoint Sitting hierarchy mein pehle dono Lok Sabha posts aate hain.\n TRICK — “VP = Chairman, not Member”\n💡\nVice-President Rajya Sabha ka Chairman hai, member nahi.\nTie mein Chairman ke roop mein casting vote ka hook yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJoint Sitting ko Rajya Sabha Chairman preside nahi karta; hierarchy Speaker\n Deputy Speaker\n Deputy Chairman.\n→\n→\n6. Disqualification, Defection & Privilege\n• Disqualification\n Article 102\n→\n• Defection\n 52nd Amendment, 1985\n 10th Schedule\n→\n→\n• Independent member joins party\n defection\n→\n• Nominated member joins party after 6 months\n defection\n→\n• Whip violation / joining another party\n defection\n→\n• Merger exception\n 2/3 members\n→\n• Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu (1992)\n Presiding Officer decision subject to judicial review\n→\n• Defection decision\n Speaker (LS) / Chairman (RS)\n→\n• Civil arrest privilege\n 40 days before + session + 40 days after; criminal arrest allowed\n→\n TRICK — “52–85–10”\n💡\nDefection triangle: 52nd Amendment\n 1985\n 10th Schedule.\n→\n→\nMerger ka magic number = 2/3.\n TRICK — “40–Session–40, Civil Only”\n💡\nPrivilege memory image: session ke dono side 40-40 days.\nCriminal case mein arrest allowed.\n7. Sessions & Parliamentary Time — B-M-W\n• Budget Session\n Feb–May (Longest)\n→\n• Monsoon Session\n July–September\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\n• Winter Session\n Nov–Dec (Shortest)\n→\n• Summoning\n President\n→\n• Prorogation\n President\n→\n• Adjournment\n Speaker\n→\n• Sine Die\n adjournment without fixing next date\n→\n• Lame Duck\n LS members who lost election; term from USA\n→\n TRICK — “B-M-W = Budget, Monsoon, Winter”\n💡\nYear ko teen parliamentary seasons mein dekho: Budget\n Monsoon\n Winter.\n→\n→\nLongest = Budget; shortest = Winter.\n TRICK — “S-P-P, A-S”\n💡\nSummoning-President, Prorogation-President, Adjournment-Speaker.\nPresident session bulata/end karta; Speaker sitting temporarily rokta.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSummoning = President; Adjournment = Speaker. Dono ko swap mat karna.\n8. Question Hour vs Zero Hour\n• Question Hour\n 11 AM–12 PM\n→\n• Zero Hour\n 12 PM–1 PM\n→\n• Source notes: Zero Hour Constitution mein mentioned nahi; informal practice\n• Question Hour includes starred, unstarred, short-notice questions\n TRICK — “11 Question, 12 Zero”\n💡\n11 baje Question Hour start; 12 baje Zero Hour start.\nZero Hour = zero constitutional mention.\n9. Bills — Ordinary vs Money vs Constitution Amendment\n• Ordinary/Public Bill\n either House; Joint Sitting possible\n→\n• Private Member Bill\n non-minister introduces; 30 days notice\n→\n• Money Bill\n Article 110; Lok Sabha only; prior President consent\n→\n• Money Bill status decided by Lok Sabha Speaker\n• Rajya Sabha can hold Money Bill only 14 days; no amendment power\n• Money Bill\n No Joint Sitting\n→\n• Constitution Amendment Bill\n No Joint Sitting\n→\n• Source notes: President has no veto on Constitution Amendment Bill after 24th Amendment, 1971\n TRICK — “110 = Money > LS > Speaker > 14 > No Joint”\n💡\nMoney Bill ke 5 anchors ek saath bolo: Art.110, Lok Sabha only, Speaker decides, RS 14 days, no Joint Sitting.\nAll Money Bills are Financial Bills; not vice versa (source notes).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMoney Bill par Rajya Sabha sirf 14 din recommendations de sakti hai; amendment power aur Joint Sitting nahi.\n10. President's Veto — A-S-P, Q Nahi\n• Absolute Veto\n assent completely withheld; bill lapses\n→\n• Suspensive Veto\n bill returned for reconsideration\n→\n• Pocket Veto\n no action; bill pending indefinitely\n→\n• Qualified Veto\n not available to Indian President in source notes\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\n• Giani Zail Singh\n Pocket Veto on India Post Office (Amendment) Bill\n→\n TRICK — “A-S-P; Qualified = Quit India”\n💡\nIndia ke President ke exam-veto anchors: Absolute, Suspensive, Pocket.\nQualified Veto ko 'Q = Quit/Not available' se yaad karo.\n11. Cut Motions — ₹1, Specified, ₹100\n• Policy Cut\n amount reduced to ₹1\n→\n• Economy Cut\n amount reduced by specified amount\n→\n• Token Cut\n amount reduced by ₹100\n→\n TRICK — “P-E-T = 1 – Specific – 100”\n💡\nPolicy = ₹1, Economy = specified, Token = ₹100.\nPolicy aur Token amounts ulte lagte hain — isi liye ₹1 vs ₹100 ko red-circle karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPolicy Cut = ₹1; Token Cut = ₹100.\n12. Joint Sittings — 3 Famous Cases\n• Dowry\n 1961\n→\n• Banking\n 1977\n→\n• POTA\n 2002\n→\n TRICK — “D-B-P = 61–77–02”\n💡\nDowry\n Banking\n POTA.\n→\n→\nYears rhythm: 61\n 77\n 02.\n→\n→\n13. Parliamentary Motions — N-C-A Contrast\n• No-Confidence\n only Lok Sabha; minimum 50 members; no reason required; passed\n Government resigns\n→\n→\n• Censure\n against minister/CoM; Government not bound to resign\n→\n• Adjournment Motion\n urgent public-importance issue; minimum 50; Government does not resign\n→\n• Confidence Motion\n ruling party proves majority in Lok Sabha\n→\n• First No-Confidence Motion\n 1963, J.B. Kriplani against Nehru (not passed)\n→\n TRICK — “N = Knock Government, C = Criticise, A = Attention”\n💡\nNo-Confidence = government gir sakti hai.\nCensure = criticism/embarrassment; government compulsory resign nahi.\nAdjournment = urgent issue par attention.\n TRICK — “50 for N + A, not C”\n💡\nNo-Confidence = 50 members; Adjournment = 50 members; Censure = no minimum number in source notes.\n14. Committees — Numbers That Get Swapped\n• Public Accounts Committee (PAC)\n 22 = 15 LS + 7 RS; oldest; expenditure/CAG; headed by Opposition leader\n→\n• Estimates Committee\n 30, all from Lok Sabha; established 1950\n→\n• Privileges Committee\n 15 = 10 LS + 5 RS\n→\n• Select Committee (JPC in source table)\n 30\n→\n• Joint Select Committee\n 45 = 30 LS + 15 RS\n→\n• Committee on Public Undertakings\n 22 = 15 LS + 7 RS; established 1964\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\n TRICK — “PAC & PSU = 22 (15+7); Estimates = 30 All-LS”\n💡\nPAC aur Public Undertakings dono ka number-pack same: 22 = 15 LS + 7 RS.\nEstimates = 30, aur sab Lok Sabha se.\n TRICK — “Privileges 15; Joint Select 45”\n💡\nPrivileges = 10+5 = 15.\nJoint Select = 30+15 = 45.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPAC = oldest + Opposition leader; Estimates Committee = all 30 members Lok Sabha se.\n15. Budget & 3 Funds — 112 / 266 / 267\n• Budget constitutional name = Annual Financial Statement, Article 112\n• Source notes: word 'Budget' Constitution mein mentioned nahi\n• Presented by Finance Minister\n• Rajya Sabha\n discuss only; budget voting rights nahi\n→\n• Lok Sabha\n voting rights on budget\n→\n• Consolidated Fund\n Article 266(1); withdrawal needs Parliament approval\n→\n• Public Accounts\n Article 266(2); not subject to Parliamentary vote\n→\n• Contingency Fund\n Article 267; emergency reserve held by President; sanction later\n→\n TRICK — “112 = Statement; 266(1) Consolidated, 266(2) Public, 267 Contingency”\n💡\nFunds ko article sequence se yaad karo: 266(1) C, 266(2) P, 267 C.\nEasy logic: Consolidated = Parliament first; Contingency = emergency first, sanction later.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRajya Sabha budget par vote nahi kar sakti — sirf discuss. Consolidated withdrawal needs Parliament approval; Contingency\nemergency withdrawal can precede later sanction.\n16. Key Article Ladder — Parliament Fast Map\n• 79 Parliament | 80 Rajya Sabha | 81 Lok Sabha | 82 Delimitation\n• 83 Duration | 84 Qualifications | 85 Sessions\n• 89 RS Chairman | 93 LS Speaker | 102 Disqualification\n• 107 Bill in either House | 108 Joint Sitting | 110 Money Bill\n• 112 Annual Financial Statement | 114 Appropriation Bill | 117(3) Finance Bill\n• 123 Presidential Ordinance\n• 266(1) Consolidated Fund | 266(2) Public Accounts | 267 Contingency Fund\n TRICK — “79 P, 80 R, 81 L, 82 D — then 108 Joint, 110 Money, 112 Budget”\n💡\nStart ladder: Parliament\n RS\n LS\n Delimitation.\n→\n→\n→\nBill ladder: 108 Joint Sitting\n 110 Money Bill\n 112 Annual Financial Statement.\n→\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Parliament of India\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part V 79–122, Parliament=P-L-R\n LS 550/543/25/5 vs RS 250/245/30/6 + 1/3 every2 + 12 nominated\n Delimitation 52-63-73-\n→\n→\n02; 84 freeze, 104 Anglo-Indian end\n Speaker joint sitting S-DS-DC; VP=RS Chairman not member\n Defection\n→\n→\n52nd/1985/10th + 2/3 merger; privilege Civil 40-session-40\n Sessions B-M-W; Summon/Prorogue President, Adjourn Speaker\n→\n 11 Question,12 Zero\n Money Bill 110-LS-Speaker-14-NoJoint; Constitution Amendment NoJoint/NoVeto in source notes\n\n→\n→\n→\nVeto A-S-P; Cut P-E-T=₹1/specified/₹100\n Joint Sittings DBP=61-77-02\n Motions: NoConfidence Knock, Censure Criticise,\n→\n→\nAdjourn Attention; N+A need 50\n PAC & PSU 22(15+7), Estimates 30 all-LS\n Budget=Art112; Funds 266(1) Consolidated,\n→\n→\n266(2) Public, 267 Contingency.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nRajya Sabha permanent | Money Bill = LS only + RS 14 days + no Joint Sitting | Policy Cut ₹1 vs Token Cut ₹100."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.13 State Executive\nSTATE EXECUTIVE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 13 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Governor, Chief Minister, State Council of Ministers, Advocate General, Centre-State mirror pairs\naur high-confusion Articles ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. State Executive Skeleton — Part VI, 153–167, 4 Components\n• State Executive = Part VI, Articles 153–167\n• 4 components = Governor + Chief Minister + Council of Ministers + Advocate General\n• Governor = Constitutional / Nominal Head\n• Chief Minister = Real Executive Head\n• Council of Ministers = Aid & Advise Governor\n• Advocate General = Highest Legal Officer of State\n TRICK — “G-C-C-A = Governor, CM, CoM, Advocate General”\n💡\nState Executive ko 4-letter spine se yaad karo: G-C-C-A.\nRole picture: Governor formal, CM real, CoM advises, AG legal.\n2. Centre to State — Mirror Image\n• President -> Governor = Constitutional Head\n• Prime Minister -> Chief Minister = Real Executive\n• Attorney General (Art. 76) -> Advocate General (Art. 165)\n• President pardon Art. 72 -> Governor pardon Art. 161\n• President ordinance Art. 123 -> Governor ordinance Art. 213\n• Parliament Art. 79 -> State Legislature Art. 168\n TRICK — “P-G, PM-CM, AG-AdvG, 72-161, 123-213”\n💡\nState Executive ko Centre ka mirror samjho.\nSabse useful number-pairs: 72/161 pardon aur 123/213 ordinance.\n3. Governor — 35, President, 5-but-Pleasure, HC-CJ\n• Minimum age = 35 years\n• Must be citizen of India\n• Must not be MP/MLA\n• Must not hold office of profit\n• Appointed by President — Article 155\n• Term = 5 years, but at pleasure of President\n• Resignation = to President\n• Salary = ₹3.5 lakh/month\n• Salary source = Consolidated Fund of State\n• Oath = Chief Justice of High Court\n• Governor is also Chancellor of State Universities\n• First Female Governor = Sarojini Naidu, UP (United Provinces), 1947\n TRICK — “35 - President - Pleasure - HC”\n💡\nGovernor memory line: age 35, appointment President, term at President's pleasure, oath HC Chief Justice.\nSalary hook: President ₹5L vs Governor ₹3.5L.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGovernor ka 5-year term fixed nahi — source notes ke according 'at the pleasure of President'."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.13 State Executive\n4. Governor Oath & Resignation — President Se Contrast\n• President oath = Chief Justice of India\n• Governor oath = Chief Justice of High Court\n• President resignation = Vice-President\n• Governor resignation = President\n TRICK — “President: CJI -> VP | Governor: HC-CJ -> President”\n💡\nDo-line contrast yaad rakho: President ka oath CJI, resignation VP.\nGovernor ka oath HC Chief Justice, resignation President.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGovernor ka oath CJI nahi dilwata; Chief Justice of High Court dilwata hai.\n5. 7th Amendment 1956 — One Governor, Multiple States\n• 7th Constitutional Amendment, 1956\n• One person can be Governor of more than one State\n• In such cases salary distribution is decided by President (as stated in source notes)\n TRICK — “7th = One Governor, Several States”\n💡\n7 ko multi-state hook banao: ek Governor, ek se zyada States.\n6. Governor Appointments — P-A-E-J-V-F\n• Chairman, State Public Service Commission\n• Advocate General — Article 165\n• Chairman, State Election Commission\n• Judges of Subordinate Courts — Article 233\n• Vice-Chancellors of State Universities — as Chancellor\n• State Finance Commission\n TRICK — “P-A-E-J-V-F”\n💡\nPSC -> Advocate General -> Election Commission -> Judges -> Vice-Chancellors -> Finance Commission.\nArticle hooks: AG = 165, Subordinate Judges = 233.\n7. Governor Powers — Legislature, Ordinance, Pardon, Rule\n• Summon & Prorogue State Legislature\n• Dissolve Legislative Assembly\n• Nominate 1/6 members in Legislative Council\n• Ordinance power = Article 213\n• Pardoning power = Article 161\n• Recommend President's Rule = Article 356\n• Operate State Contingency Fund\n TRICK — “S-D-1/6-213-161-356-Fund”\n💡\nGovernor powers ko number-chain ke saath bolo: 1/6 nomination, 213 ordinance, 161 pardon, 356 President's Rule.\n TRICK — “161 Governor vs 72 President”\n💡\nSource notes: Governor can use suspension, remission, commutation under Art.161.\nSource notes also mark death-penalty pardon and Court Martial jurisdiction as unavailable to Governor."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.13 State Executive\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPardoning trap: President = Art.72; Governor = Art.161. Source notes: Governor death-penalty pardon nahi kar sakta.\n8. Chief Minister — State Ka PM\n• CM = Real Executive Head of State\n• Head of Council of Ministers\n• Leader of majority party in Legislative Assembly\n• Chairman of State Planning Board\n• Minimum age = 25 years\n• Must be citizen of India\n• Must be MLA/MLC or become State Legislature member within 6 months\n• Appointed by Governor — Article 164(1)\n• Term = 5 years, at pleasure of Governor\n• Resignation = Governor\n• Salary = decided by State Legislature\n• Oath = Governor\n TRICK — “25 - 6 - 164(1) - Governor”\n💡\nCM number line: age 25 -> non-member window 6 months -> appointment Art.164(1) -> Governor.\nRole hook: CM = State ka PM = Real Executive.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCM MLA ya MLC dono ho sakta hai; agar member nahi hai to 6 months ke andar State Legislature member banna zaroori.\n9. CM Powers — P-D-A-R-C\n• Presides over Council of Ministers meetings\n• Distributes portfolios among ministers\n• Advises Governor to summon/dissolve Legislative Assembly\n• Recommends appointments & removals of ministers\n• Crisis Manager-in-Chief during emergency\n TRICK — “P-D-A-R-C”\n💡\nPreside -> Distribute -> Advise -> Recommend -> Crisis.\nCM = Governor aur Council ke beech operational centre.\n TRICK — “PM informs President; CM informs Governor”\n💡\nSource notes parallel structure ko highlight karte hain: Centre mein PM-President, State mein CM-Governor.\n10. State Council of Ministers — 15% Max, 12 Min\n• Role = Aid & Advise Governor\n• Members must be State Legislature members, or become within 6 months\n• Appointed by Governor on advice of CM\n• Collectively responsible to State Legislative Assembly\n• Maximum strength = 15% of Legislative Assembly\n• Minimum strength = 12 Ministers\n• 91st Amendment linked with max 15% + min 12\n• Delhi special in source notes = max 10% of Assembly or 7, whichever is less — 69th Amendment"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.13 State Executive\n TRICK — “State CoM = 15 Max, 12 Min”\n💡\nCentre yaad ho to State ka extra number sirf 12 add karo.\n91st Amendment = 15% ceiling + minimum 12 at State level.\n TRICK — “Delhi = 10% or 7”\n💡\nSource notes ka Delhi special rule: 10% of Assembly OR 7, whichever is less.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nState CoM ka minimum 12 source notes mein specifically diya hai.\n11. Advocate General — Article 165\n• Highest Legal Officer of State\n• Article 165\n• Appointed by Governor\n• Qualification = qualified to be Judge of High Court\n• Advises State Government on legal matters\n• Can participate in State Legislature proceedings\n• Cannot vote\n• Term = at pleasure of Governor\n TRICK — “165 = State Legal Officer; HC-Level; Speak, No Vote”\n💡\nAdvocate General ka 3-point hook: Art.165, High Court Judge qualification, Legislature mein participate but no vote.\n TRICK — “76 + 89 = 165”\n💡\nSource notes ka memory relation: Attorney General Art.76 + 89 = Advocate General Art.165.\nAG Centre = SC Judge qualification; Advocate General State = HC Judge qualification.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAdvocate General ki qualification SC Judge level nahi; source notes mein High Court Judge level hai.\n12. Centre vs State — 7 Fast Contrasts\n• President / Governor = Constitutional Heads\n• PM / CM = Real Executives\n• AG Art.76 / Advocate General Art.165\n• Oath: President CJI / Governor HC Chief Justice\n• Head resignation: President -> VP / Governor -> President\n• Pardon: Art.72 / Art.161\n• Ordinance: Art.123 / Art.213\n TRICK — “CJI-HC | VP-President | 72-161 | 123-213”\n💡\nExam se pehle ye 4 contrast-pairs bolna enough hai to common swaps bach jayein.\n13. Key Article Ladder — State Executive Fast Map\n• 153 = Governors of States\n• 154 = Executive Power of State\n• 155 = Governor appointment by President\n• 157 = Governor qualifications\n• 160 = Duties in contingency"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.13 State Executive\n• 161 = Governor pardoning power\n• 162 = Extent of State executive power\n• 163 = CoM to aid & advise Governor\n• 164(1) = CM appointed by Governor\n• 165 = Advocate General\n• 166 = Governor / conduct of State executive business in source notes\n• 213 = Governor ordinance power\n• 233 = Subordinate Court judges appointment\n TRICK — “153 Start -> 155 Appoint -> 157 Qualify -> 161 Pardon -> 163 Advice -> 164 CM -> 165 AG -> 213\n💡\nOrdinance”\nPoora ladder ratne ke bajay anchor articles pakdo: 155, 157, 161, 163, 164, 165, 213.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part VI 153–167, components G-C-C-A -> Governor nominal, CM real -> Centre mirror: P-G, PM-CM, 76-165, 72-161, 123-213 ->\nGovernor: 35, President appoint, 5-but-pleasure, resignation President, ₹3.5L CF-State, oath HC-CJ -> 7th/1956 one Governor\nmultiple States -> appointments P-A-E-J-V-F -> powers 1/6, 213 ordinance, 161 pardon, 356 rule -> CM: age25, 6-month rule,\nArt164(1), oath/resign Governor -> CM powers P-D-A-R-C -> State CoM 15% max, 12 min, Delhi 10% or 7 -> Advocate General\nArt165, HC-level, participate/no vote -> article anchors 155-157-161-163-164-165-213.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nGovernor oath = HC Chief Justice, not CJI | Governor = at pleasure of President | State CoM = max 15%, minimum 12."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.14 State Legislature\nSTATE LEGISLATURE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 14 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Vidhan Sabha vs Vidhan Parishad, 6 bicameral states, Parishad election fractions, bills, presiding\nofficers, privileges, sessions aur key Articles ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — Part VI, 168–212\n• State Legislature = Part VI, Articles 168–212\n• Unicameral = only Vidhan Sabha\n• Bicameral = Vidhan Sabha + Vidhan Parishad\n• Source notes: 22 States + 3 UTs unicameral\n• Source notes: only 6 States bicameral\n• Vidhan Sabha minimum = 60 | Vidhan Parishad minimum = 40\n TRICK — “168–212, One House or Two”\n💡\nChapter start anchor: Part VI + Articles 168–212.\nHouse-count trick: Unicameral = Sabha only; Bicameral = Sabha + Parishad.\n2. 6 Bicameral States — K-B-U-M-A-T\n• Karnataka\n• Bihar\n• Uttar Pradesh\n• Maharashtra\n• Andhra Pradesh\n• Telangana\n TRICK — “K B U M A T”\n💡\nKarnataka – Bihar – UP – Maharashtra – Andhra – Telangana.\nMnemonic sentence: “KaBi UP Mein Andhra Telangana.”\nBihar ko extra star karo — source notes BPSC ke liye must-know bolte hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes ke according Vidhan Parishad sirf in 6 States mein hai.\n3. Vidhan Sabha vs Vidhan Parishad — Lower vs Upper\n• Vidhan Sabha = Lower House, directly elected, dissolvable\n• Vidhan Parishad = Upper House, permanent\n• VS minimum 60, maximum 500\n• VP minimum 40, maximum not more than 1/3 of VS\n• VS term = 5 years | VP member term = 6 years\n• VP = 1/3 members retire every 2 years\n• VS minimum age = 25 | VP minimum age = 30\n TRICK — “VS = LS; VP = RS”\n💡\nVidhan Sabha ko Lok Sabha ka state-version samjho: Lower, age 25, term 5, dissolve ho sakti.\nVidhan Parishad ko Rajya Sabha ka state-version samjho: Upper, age 30, term 6, permanent, 1/3 every 2 years.\n TRICK — “60/500/25/5 vs 40/1/3/30/6”\n💡\nVS number pack: 60 min, 500 max, age 25, term 5.\nVP number pack: 40 min, max 1/3 of VS, age 30, term 6."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.14 State Legislature\n4. Vidhan Sabha Exceptions — S-G-M\n• Sikkim = 32 seats\n• Goa = 40 seats\n• Mizoram = 40 seats\n• These are exceptions to the general minimum 60 rule in source notes\n• Largest Assembly = Uttar Pradesh, 403 seats\n• Bihar Vidhan Sabha = 243 seats\n TRICK — “SGM = 32–40–40”\n💡\nSikkim 32, Goa 40, Mizoram 40.\nUP = 403 largest; Bihar = 243.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGeneral VS minimum 60, but source notes list Sikkim, Goa and Mizoram below 60.\n5. Vidhan Sabha Powers — E-L-E-F\n• Executive\n controls State Government & Council of Ministers\n→\n• Legislative\n laws on State List & Concurrent List\n→\n• Election-related\n MLAs participate in President election; elect Rajya Sabha members\n→\n• Financial\n Budget only in Legislative Assembly; taxes/withdrawal need Assembly approval\n→\n TRICK — “E-L-E-F = Executive, Legislative, Election, Financial”\n💡\nVidhan Sabha ke four power-buckets ko ELEF bolo.\nMoney/budget ka final practical control Sabha ke paas.\n6. Vidhan Parishad — Creation/Abolition Process\n• Creation/Abolition power lies with Parliament\n• Process starts in Legislative Assembly\n• Assembly passes resolution by Special Majority\n• Then Parliament passes by Simple Majority\n TRICK — “State Starts Special, Parliament Passes Simple”\n💡\nStep 1: Vidhan Sabha = Special Majority.\nStep 2: Parliament = Simple Majority.\nPower Parliament ke paas, process start Assembly se.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCreate/abolish power ko State Legislature ka final power mat samajhna — final legislative power Parliament ke paas.\n7. Vidhan Parishad Election — 1/3 + 1/3 + 1/12 + 1/12 + 1/6\n• 1/3\n elected by Legislative Assembly members (MLAs)\n→\n• 1/3\n elected by Local Bodies\n→\n• 1/12\n elected by Teachers\n→\n• 1/12\n elected by Graduates\n→\n• 1/6\n nominated by Governor (Literature, Arts, Science, Social Service)\n→\n TRICK — “MLA–Local–Teacher–Graduate–Governor”\n💡\nOrder ko M-L-T-G-G bolo.\nFractions: 1/3, 1/3, 1/12, 1/12, 1/6.\nCheck: 4/12 + 4/12 + 1/12 + 1/12 + 2/12 = 12/12."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.14 State Legislature\n TRICK — “RS = 12 fixed; VP = 1/6 fraction”\n💡\nRajya Sabha mein President 12 nominate karta hai.\nVidhan Parishad mein Governor 1/6 nominate karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGovernor nomination in VP = 1/6 fraction, fixed 12 nahi.\n8. Presiding Officers — Sabha vs Parishad\n• Vidhan Sabha\n Speaker + Deputy Speaker\n→\n• Speaker resignation\n Deputy Speaker\n→\n• Speaker removal\n Legislative Assembly; 14 days prior notice\n→\n• Speaker oath\n Governor\n→\n• Vidhan Parishad\n Chairman + Deputy Chairman\n→\n• VP Chairman elected from among Vidhan Parishad members\n• Chairman absent\n Deputy Chairman presides\n→\n TRICK — “Speaker: Deputy–14–Governor”\n💡\nSpeaker ka 3-hook pack: resign to Deputy Speaker, removal notice 14 days, oath by Governor.\n TRICK — “RS Chairman Non-member; VP Chairman Member”\n💡\nRajya Sabha Chairman = Vice-President of India, non-member.\nVidhan Parishad Chairman = elected from its own members, so member.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVP Chairman ko Vice-President of India mat samajhna — State Vidhan Parishad Chairman elected member hota hai.\n9. Bills at State Level — 4 Months vs 14 Days\nOrdinary Bill\n• Can be introduced in either House\n• Final authority rests with Legislative Assembly\n• Vidhan Parishad delay = 3 months first time + 1 month after re-passage\n• Total maximum delay = 4 months\n• No Joint Sitting at State level\n TRICK — “Ordinary = 3 + 1 = 4, No Joint”\n💡\nVP ka ordinary bill delay formula: 3 months + 1 month = 4 months max.\nCentre mein Joint Sitting ho sakti hai; source notes ke according State mein NO Joint Sitting.\nMoney Bill\n• Introduced only in Legislative Assembly\n• Vidhan Parishad can withhold for 14 days only\n• VP has no amendment power\n• Budget also only in Legislative Assembly\n• Money Bill status decided by Speaker of Vidhan Sabha\n TRICK — “Money = Sabha Only, Speaker, 14”\n💡\nMoney Bill: Assembly only\n Speaker decides\n Parishad 14 days.\n→\n→\nCentre RS ka 14-day rule aur State VP ka 14-day rule same."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.14 State Legislature\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nState level par Joint Sitting provision nahi; ordinary bill delay 4 months max, Money Bill 14 days.\n10. Privileges — Article 194 vs Parliament 105\n• State Legislature privileges = Article 194\n• Parliament privileges = Article 105\n• Civil arrest immunity in source notes = 40 days before + session + 40 days after\n• Criminal arrest allowed\n• Freedom of Speech in Legislature\n• House proceedings protected from court challenge in source notes\n TRICK — “194 State, 105 Parliament”\n💡\n194 ko State ke saath, 105 ko Parliament ke saath lock karo.\n TRICK — “40–Session–40, Civil Only”\n💡\nCivil arrest protection ko session ke dono side 40–40 days ki image se yaad karo.\nCriminal arrest allowed.\n11. Sessions — Governor vs Presiding Officer\n• Minimum 2 sessions every year\n• Prorogation = Governor\n• Adjournment = Presiding Officer (Speaker/Chairman)\n• Dissolution = Governor, only Vidhan Sabha\n• Vidhan Parishad permanent; not dissolved\n TRICK — “P = Governor, A = Presiding Officer, D = Governor/Sabha only”\n💡\nProrogation Governor; Adjournment Presiding Officer.\nDissolution only Vidhan Sabha ki — Parishad permanent.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nProrogation aur Adjournment ko swap mat karna.\n12. Key Articles — 168 to 212 Fast Map\n• 168\n Composition of State Legislature\n→\n• 169\n Creation/Abolition of Legislative Councils\n→\n• 170\n Structure of Legislative Assembly\n→\n• 172\n Duration of State Legislatures\n→\n• 173\n Qualifications\n→\n• 178\n Speaker & Deputy Speaker\n→\n• 179\n Vacancy/Resignation of Speaker\n→\n• 182\n Chairman & Deputy Chairman of Vidhan Parishad\n→\n• 191\n Disqualification\n→\n• 194\n Privileges\n→\n• 195\n Salaries & Allowances\n→\n• 199\n Money Bill\n→\n• 202\n Annual Financial Statement (State Budget)\n→\n• 212\n Courts not to inquire into legislative proceedings\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.14 State Legislature\n TRICK — “168 Legislature, 169 Parishad, 170 Sabha”\n💡\nFirst 3 anchors straight: 168 State Legislature, 169 Vidhan Parishad create/abolish, 170 Vidhan Sabha.\nFinancial anchors: 199 Money Bill, 202 State Budget.\n13. +89 Memory Bridge — Parliament to State\n• Parliament Art. 79 + 89 = State Legislature Art. 168\n• Rajya Sabha Art. 80 + 89 = Vidhan Parishad Art. 169\n• Lok Sabha Art. 81 + 89 = Vidhan Sabha Art. 170\n TRICK — “79>168, 80>169, 81>170”\n💡\nSource notes ka +89 memory trick state-legislature article numbers yaad karne ke liye use karo.\nYe mnemonic hai, constitutional provision nahi.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part VI 168–212\n Unicameral Sabha only, Bicameral Sabha+Parishad\n 6 states K-B-U-M-A-T\n VS = LS:\n→\n→\n→\n60/500/25/5/dissolve; VP = RS: 40/max1/3/30/6/permanent + 1/3 every2\n VS exceptions SGM=32-40-40, UP403, Bihar243\n\n→\n→\nParishad create: VS Special then Parliament Simple\n VP election M-L-T-G-G = 1/3,1/3,1/12,1/12,1/6\n Speaker: Deputy-14-\n→\n→\nGovernor; VP Chairman = member\n Ordinary Bill 3+1=4, no Joint; Money Bill Assembly only, Speaker, 14 days\n Privileges\n→\n→\n194 vs Parliament105, Civil 40-session-40\n Sessions: Prorogation Governor, Adjourn Presiding Officer\n Articles 168\n→\n→\nLegislature,169 Parishad,170 Sabha,199 Money,202 Budget\n +89 bridge 79-168,80-169,81-170.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\n6 bicameral States = K-B-U-M-A-T | VP nomination = Governor 1/6, not fixed 12 | State level has NO Joint Sitting."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.15 Supreme Court of India\nSUPREME COURT OF INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 15 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Supreme Court ke judge-strength, Collegium/NJAC, qualifications, retirement, removal process,\njurisdictions aur key Articles ko exam-confusion ke hisaab se fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — Part V, 124–147, 34, 65, Delhi\n• Supreme Court = Part V, Articles 124–147\n• Highest Court of India\n• Total judges in source notes = 34 (1 CJI + 33 others)\n• Retirement age = 65 years\n• Seat = Delhi — Article 130\n• Court of Record = Article 129\n• SC decisions binding on all courts = Article 141\n• Judge strength can be increased/decreased by Parliament; Constitution does not fix the number\n TRICK — “124–147 | 34 | 65 | 129 Record | 130 Delhi | 141 Binding”\n💡\nChapter ka number spine isi line mein yaad karo.\nJudge-count trap: originally 8, source notes mein current strength 34; number Parliament decide karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSC judge strength Constitution mein fixed nahi — Parliament decide karta hai.\n2. Supreme Court Firsts — K-B-M-R\n• Harilal J. Kania\n First Chief Justice of India, 1950\n→\n• Fathima Beevi\n First Woman Supreme Court Judge, 1989\n→\n• Indu Malhotra\n First woman advocate directly elevated from Bar to SC, 2018\n→\n• Justice V. Ramaswami\n First removal/impeachment attempt, 1991; not passed\n→\n TRICK — “Kania–Beevi–Malhotra–Ramaswami”\n💡\nFirsts ko K-B-M-R chain mein bolo.\nRole anchors: First CJI\n First Woman Judge\n Direct from Bar\n First Removal Attempt.\n→\n→\n→\n3. Collegium System — CJI + 4\n• Other judges appointed by President\n• Source notes describe CJI appointment through Collegium System / senior-most judge convention\n• Collegium = CJI + 4 senior-most Supreme Court judges\n• Third Judges Case, 1998\n Collegium System confirmed\n→\n TRICK — “CJI + FOUR = Collegium Five”\n💡\nCJI ko centre mein rakho aur 4 senior-most judges uske around — total 5.\nYear hook: Third Judges Case = 1998.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCollegium ka core number = CJI + 4 senior-most SC judges.\n4. NJAC — 99th Added, 2015 Struck\n• NJAC = National Judicial Appointment Commission\n• Added by 99th Constitutional Amendment"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.15 Supreme Court of India\n• Struck down by Supreme Court in 2015\n• Case in source notes = Supreme Court Advocates-on-Record Association v. Union of India\n• After strike-down, Collegium System remained valid\n TRICK — “99 Added — 15 Invalid”\n💡\n99th Amendment se NJAC aaya; 2015 mein SC ne strike down kiya.\nMemory line: “Ninety-Nine came, Twenty-Fifteen went.”\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes ke according NJAC valid system nahi; Collegium remains valid.\n5. SC Judge Qualification — 5 / 10 / Jurist\n• Citizen of India\n• High Court Judge for 5 years\n• High Court Advocate for 10 years\n• OR distinguished jurist in President's opinion\n• No minimum age prescribed in Constitution (as highlighted in source notes)\n• Retirement age = 65 years\n• HC judge retirement age comparison in notes = 62 years\n TRICK — “5 Judge, 10 Advocate, Jurist Option — Retire 65”\n💡\nQualification number pair: Judge 5 years, Advocate 10 years.\nAge trap: minimum age NO; retirement 65.\n TRICK — “SC 65 vs HC 62”\n💡\nSC judge retirement 65; HC judge retirement 62.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSC Judge ke liye minimum age source notes mein prescribed nahi; retirement age 65 hai.\n6. Conditions & Salary — President, 65, CFI\n• Oath / Resignation\n President (as stated in source notes)\n→\n• Acting CJI\n appointed by President when CJI absent\n→\n• Tenure\n until 65 years of age\n→\n• Salary source\n Consolidated Fund of India\n→\n• Salary cannot be reduced during service\n• Source notes' highlighted trap: retired SC judge cannot practice in Supreme Court — Article 124(7)\n• CJI salary in source notes = ₹2.8 lakh/month\n• Other SC Judges = ₹2.5 lakh/month\n TRICK — “President–65–CFI–2.8/2.5”\n💡\nOffice-condition pack: President, age 65, Consolidated Fund of India.\nSalary pair: CJI 2.8, Others 2.5.\n TRICK — “5 > 3.5 > 2.8 > 2.5” Salary Ladder\n💡\nSource notes comparison: President ₹5L > Governor ₹3.5L > CJI ₹2.8L > SC Judge ₹2.5L.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes repeatedly highlight Art.124(7): retired SC judge Supreme Court mein practice nahi kar sakta."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.15 Supreme Court of India\n7. Removal of SC Judge — 100 / 50 / 3 / Special\n• Motion in Lok Sabha\n minimum 100 members sign\n→\n• Motion in Rajya Sabha\n minimum 50 members sign\n→\n• Admission\n Speaker (LS) / Chairman (RS), discretion\n→\n• Inquiry Committee\n 3 members\n→\n• Special Majority\n 2/3 members present & voting + majority of total membership\n→\n• President issues removal order\n• Grounds = misconduct or incapacity\n• Governed by Judges Inquiry Act, 1968\n TRICK — “100–50–3–2/3–President”\n💡\nRemoval chain: LS100 / RS50\n 3-member inquiry\n special majority\n President's order.\n→\n→\n→\nAct year = 1968.\n TRICK — “Ramaswami 1991 = Attempt, Not Success”\n💡\nSource notes: Justice V. Ramaswami first removal attempt; motion did not pass.\nSource notes state no SC/HC judge removal/impeachment has succeeded so far.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPresident judge ko apni marzi se remove nahi karta; Parliament process/recommendation necessary.\n8. Jurisdiction Map — O-A-R-W-A/T\n• Original Jurisdiction\n Article 131\n Centre-State / State-State disputes\n→\n→\n• Appellate Jurisdiction\n Articles 132–134\n→\n• Review Jurisdiction\n Article 137\n→\n• Writ Jurisdiction\n Article 32\n→\n• Advisory Jurisdiction\n Article 143\n→\n• Power of Transfer / expansion\n Article 138\n→\n• Binding decisions\n Article 141\n→\n TRICK — “131 Original, 132-134 Appeal, 137 Review, 143 Advice”\n💡\nJurisdiction ko ascending article chain mein dekho.\n131 = Original; 132/133/134 = Constitutional/Civil/Criminal appeals; 137 = Review; 143 = Advice.\n9. Appellate Jurisdiction — 132 C, 133 Civil, 134 Crime\n• Article 132\n Constitutional appellate matters\n→\n• Article 133\n Civil appellate matters\n→\n• Article 134\n Criminal appellate matters\n→\n TRICK — “132 Constitution, 133 Civil, 134 Criminal”\n💡\nC-C-C sequence ko meaning ke saath bolo: Constitution\n Civil\n Criminal.\n→\n→\nNumbers seedhe 132, 133, 134.\n10. Article 143 Advisory — Ask, SC Can Refuse\n• President can seek SC opinion on public-importance issues\n• Advisory opinion is NOT binding\n• President can ask; SC can refuse"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.15 Supreme Court of India\n TRICK — “143 = ASK, Not ORDER”\n💡\nAdvisory ko 'advice' hi samjho — binding command nahi.\nPresident ASK kar sakta hai; SC REFUSE kar sakta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArticle 143 opinion binding nahi.\n11. Article 32 vs 226 — SC Narrower, HC Wider\n• Article 32\n Supreme Court writ jurisdiction\n→\n• Article 32\n Fundamental Rights violations only\n→\n• Article 226\n High Court\n Fundamental Rights + Legal Rights\n→\n→\n• Source notes: HC jurisdiction wider\n• Article 32 itself is a Fundamental Right\n TRICK — “32 = FR Only; 226 = FR + Legal”\n💡\nSC Article 32 ko FR-only gate samjho.\nHC Article 226 ka gate wider hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt.32 aur Art.226 ko equal scope mat samjho; source notes HC scope wider batate hain.\n12. Court of Record, Seat, Binding — 129 / 130 / 141\n• Article 129\n Supreme Court as Court of Record; contempt power\n→\n• Article 130\n Seat of Supreme Court = Delhi\n→\n• Article 141\n SC decisions binding on all courts in India\n→\n TRICK — “129 Record, 130 Room/Delhi, 141 Rule for All”\n💡\n129 = Record, 130 = Seat/Delhi, 141 = binding law for all courts.\n13. Key Article Ladder — 124 to 147\n• 124\n Composition & Appointment of SC Judges\n→\n• 125\n Salary of SC Judges\n→\n• 129\n Court of Record\n→\n• 130\n Seat of SC\n→\n• 131\n Original Jurisdiction\n→\n• 132\n Constitutional Appeal\n→\n• 133\n Civil Appeal\n→\n• 134\n Criminal Appeal\n→\n• 137\n Review\n→\n• 138\n Expansion / Transfer\n→\n• 139\n Grant of Writ Powers\n→\n• 141\n Decisions binding\n→\n• 143\n Advisory Jurisdiction\n→\n• 147\n Interpretation of Constitution\n→\n TRICK — “124 Compose > 129 Record > 130 Delhi > 131 Original > 132-134 Appeals > 137 Review > 141 Bind\n💡\n\n> 143 Advise”\nExam ke liye ye anchor articles enough hain poora map reconstruct karne ke liye."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.15 Supreme Court of India\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part V 124–147\n SC highest, 34 judges, retire65, Delhi130, Record129, Binding141, strength Parliament\n Firsts Kania-Beevi-\n→\n→\nMalhotra-Ramaswami\n Collegium CJI+4, Third Judges 1998\n NJAC 99th, struck 2015\n Qualification 5-year HC Judge / 10-\n→\n→\n→\nyear HC Advocate / Jurist, no min age, SC65 vs HC62\n Conditions President-65-CFI, salary 2.8/2.5\n Removal 100 LS / 50 RS / 3\n→\n→\n\ncommittee / 2/3+total majority / President, Act1968\n Jurisdiction 131 Original, 132-134 Appeals, 137 Review, 32 Writ, 143\n→\nAdvisory, 138 Transfer, 141 Binding\n 32 FR-only vs 226 FR+Legal.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nJudge strength Parliament decides | SC judge minimum age not prescribed, retirement 65 | Art.143 advisory NOT\nbinding."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.16 High Courts & Subordinate Courts\nHIGH COURTS & SUBORDINATE COURTS — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 16 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — High Court ke key Articles, SC-vs-HC differences, writ jurisdiction, UT mappings, subordinate-court\nappointments, special courts aur high-yield dates ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — Part VI, 214–232, 25, 7, 62\n• High Courts = Part VI, Articles 214–232\n• Total High Courts in source notes = 25\n• Multi-State High Courts = 7\n• Retirement age = 62 years\n• Court of Record = Article 215\n• Delhi & J&K/Ladakh = UTs with their own High Courts\n• Patna High Court = established 1916; Principal Bench Patna\n TRICK — “214–232 | 25 HCs | 7 Multi | 62 Retire | 215 Record”\n💡\nPoore chapter ka number spine: 214–232\n 25\n 7\n 62\n Art.215.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nBihar anchor: Patna HC = 1916.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSC retirement 65 vs HC retirement 62 — 3-year difference.\n2. Key Article Ladder — 214 to 233\n• 214\n High Court in each State\n→\n• 215\n High Court as Court of Record\n→\n• 216\n Constitution of High Court\n→\n• 217\n Appointment & Qualifications of HC Judges\n→\n• 219\n Oath/Affirmation\n→\n• 222\n Transfer of HC Judges\n→\n• 225\n Jurisdiction of HC\n→\n• 226\n Writ Jurisdiction\n→\n• 227\n Superintendence over Subordinate Courts\n→\n• 228\n Transfer of certain cases to HC\n→\n• 231\n One HC for two or more States\n→\n• 233\n District Judge appointment\n→\n TRICK — “214 Start, 215 Record, 217 Judge, 226 Writ, 227 Watch, 233 District”\n💡\nExam anchors ko isi order mein yaad karo.\n226 = Writ; 227 = Subordinate Courts par supervision; 233 = District Judge.\n3. HC Judge Qualification — 10 + 10, Retire 62\n• Citizen of India\n• 10 years as Advocate in a High Court\n• OR 10 years in Judicial Office in India\n• Appointment by President in consultation with CJI + Governor\n• Tenure until 62 years\n• Resignation to President\n• Oath administered by Governor"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.16 High Courts & Subordinate Courts\n• Acting Chief Justice appointed by President\n TRICK — “10 Advocate + 10 Judicial + 62 Retirement”\n💡\nHC judge qualification ka easiest code = 10/10/62.\nSC se contrast: SC qualification source notes mein 5-year HC Judge OR 10-year HC Advocate.\n TRICK — “Appoint President, Oath Governor, Resign President”\n💡\nAppointment aur resignation President; oath Governor.\nIs 3-step contrast ko ek line mein bolo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHC judge ka oath Governor dilwata hai — President/CJI nahi.\n4. Salary & Pension — State Pays Salary, India Pays Pension\n• HC Chief Justice salary in source notes = ₹2.5 lakh/month\n• HC Other Judge = ₹2.25 lakh/month\n• Salary\n Consolidated Fund of State\n→\n• Pension\n Consolidated Fund of India\n→\n• Source notes comparison: SC Judge salary = HC Chief Justice salary = ₹2.5 lakh\n TRICK — “Salary STATE, Pension INDIA”\n💡\nHC ke liye salary aur pension ka source alag hai.\nSalary = State Fund; Pension = India Fund.\n TRICK — “2.8 > 2.5 = 2.5 > 2.25”\n💡\nSource salary ladder: SC CJI 2.8 > SC Judge 2.5 = HC CJ 2.5 > HC Judge 2.25.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHC salary source aur pension source ko same mat samajhna.\n5. HC Jurisdiction — O-W-A-R-S\n• Original Jurisdiction\n FR enforcement, constitutional-case transfer, MP/MLA election disputes\n→\n• Writ Jurisdiction\n Article 226\n→\n• Appellate Jurisdiction\n Civil + Criminal matters\n→\n• Court of Record\n Article 215\n→\n• Superintendence over Subordinate Courts\n Article 227\n→\n• Death sentence must be confirmed by High Court before execution (as emphasized in source notes)\n TRICK — “O-W-A-R-S = Original, Writ, Appeal, Record, Superintendence”\n💡\nHC powers ko 5 buckets mein yaad karo.\nArticle anchors: Writ 226, Record 215, Superintendence 227.\n TRICK — “Death = HC Confirm”\n💡\nSource notes ka direct trap: death sentence execution se pehle HC confirmation mandatory.\n6. Article 226 vs Article 32 — Wider vs Fundamental\n• Article 226 (HC)\n Fundamental Rights + Other Legal Rights\n→\n• Article 32 (SC)\n Fundamental Rights only\n→\n• Source notes: HC writ jurisdiction is wider"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.16 High Courts & Subordinate Courts\n• Chandra Kumar Case\n Article 226 writ jurisdiction is part of Basic Structure\n→\n• Article 32 itself is a Fundamental Right\n TRICK — “226 = FR + Legal; 32 = FR Only”\n💡\nScope ke hisaab se 226 wider.\nNature ke hisaab se Article 32 khud Fundamental Right hai.\n TRICK — “Chandra Kumar = 226 Basic Structure”\n💡\nCase-name ko article se direct chipkao: Chandra Kumar\n Art.226\n Basic Structure.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n226 aur 32 ko same scope mat samjho.\n7. SC vs HC — 3 Must-Know Differences\n• Oath\n SC Judge: President | HC Judge: Governor\n→\n• Retirement\n SC: 65 | HC: 62\n→\n• Salary Source\n SC: CF of India | HC: CF of State\n→\n• Pension Source\n both in source notes: CF of India\n→\n• Writ\n SC Art.32 FR only | HC Art.226 FR + Legal Rights\n→\n• Court of Record\n SC Art.129 | HC Art.215\n→\n TRICK — “Oath–Age–Salary = P/G, 65/62, India/State”\n💡\nExam se pehle sirf ye 3 contrast bolo:\nSC oath President / HC Governor; SC65 / HC62; SC salary India / HC salary State.\n8. UT to High Court Mapping — L-P-A First\n• Lakshadweep\n Kerala High Court (Kochi)\n→\n• Puducherry\n Madras High Court\n→\n• Andaman & Nicobar\n Calcutta High Court\n→\n• Dadra & Nagar Haveli + Daman & Diu\n Bombay High Court\n→\n• Chandigarh\n Punjab & Haryana High Court\n→\n• Delhi\n Delhi High Court (own)\n→\n• J&K + Ladakh\n J&K & Ladakh High Court (own)\n→\n TRICK — “L-K, P-M, A-C”\n💡\nMost common 3 pairs from source notes:\nLakshadweep-Kerala | Puducherry-Madras | Andaman-Calcutta.\n TRICK — “Dadra/Daman-Bombay; Chandigarh-P&H; Delhi/J&K Own”\n💡\nBaaki mapping ko 3 mini-blocks mein yaad karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes: own-HC UTs = Delhi and J&K/Ladakh.\n9. Subordinate Courts — Articles 233–237\n• District Judge appointment\n Governor in consultation with High Court\n→\n• Qualification\n at least 7 years as advocate\n→\n• Restriction in source notes\n must not be in Government service\n→\n• Recommendation\n High Court\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.16 High Courts & Subordinate Courts\n• Article 233\n District Judge appointment\n→\n• Article 235\n Control of High Court over Subordinate Courts\n→\n TRICK — “Governor Appoints, HC Recommends, 7 Years”\n💡\nDistrict Judge ke liye G-H-7 hook yaad karo:\nGovernor appoints\n High Court consult/recommend\n 7-year advocate.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDistrict Judge appoints Governor, President nahi.\n10. Subordinate Court Hierarchy — Civil, Criminal, Revenue\nCivil Side\n• District Judge\n• Subordinate / Civil Judge\n• Munsif / Junior Civil Judge\nCriminal Side\n• Chief Judicial Magistrate\n• Judicial Magistrate First Class\n• Judicial Magistrate Second Class\nRevenue Side\n• Revenue Board\n Commissioner\n Collector\n Tehsildar\n Naib Tehsildar\n→\n→\n→\n→\n TRICK — “Civil: D-S-M | Criminal: C-1-2 | Revenue: B-C-C-T-N”\n💡\nCivil ladder = District\n Subordinate\n Munsif.\n→\n→\nCriminal = CJM\n JM First\n JM Second.\n→\n→\nRevenue = Board\n Commissioner\n Collector\n Tehsildar\n Naib.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n11. Special Courts — Year & Purpose Hooks\n• Gram Nyayalayas\n village-level small disputes; State Govt in consultation with HC\n→\n• Lok Adalat\n quick/low-cost, mutual consent, award final & binding\n→\n• First Lok Adalat in source notes\n 6 Oct 1985, Delhi; Justice P.N. Bhagwati\n→\n• Fast-Track Courts\n speedy criminal cases; example POCSO Courts\n→\n• Mobile Court\n 'Justice on Wheels'; first at Mewat, Haryana (2007); APJ Abdul Kalam credited\n→\n• Consumer Courts\n consumer disputes\n→\n• NGT\n environment protection; established 2010; source notes say not a constitutional body\n→\n• Juvenile Courts\n child/juvenile justice; 3-member Board\n→\n• Court Martial\n military matters\n→\n TRICK — “Lok 1985, Mobile 2007, NGT 2010”\n💡\nSpecial-court dates ko increasing ladder mein bolo: 1985\n 2007\n 2010.\n→\n→\nLok = Bhagwati, Mobile = Kalam, NGT = Environment.\n TRICK — “Lok Award = Final, No Appeal”\n💡\nSource notes ka direct memory hook: Lok Adalat award binding/deemed decree; appeal nahi.\n12. High Court Timeline — Oldest, Bihar, Newest\n• Oldest 3 High Courts\n Madras, Calcutta, Bombay — all 1862\n→\n• Allahabad\n 1866; source notes call it largest HC by number of judges\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.16 High Courts & Subordinate Courts\n• Patna High Court\n 1916\n→\n• 2000 High Courts\n Chhattisgarh, Uttarakhand, Jharkhand\n→\n• 2013 High Courts\n Meghalaya, Manipur, Tripura\n→\n• Newest in source notes\n Telangana + Andhra Pradesh, both 2019\n→\n TRICK — “MCB 1862 > Patna 1916 > C-U-J 2000 > M-M-T 2013 > T-A 2019”\n💡\nTimeline ko year-clusters mein yaad karo.\nOldest 3 = Madras-Calcutta-Bombay; Bihar anchor = Patna 1916.\n13. Bihar Focus — Patna High Court\n• Patna High Court = Bihar's High Court\n• Established = 1916\n• Principal Bench = Patna\n TRICK — “Bihar = Patna = 1916”\n💡\nBPSC ke liye ye 3-word fact direct lock karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part VI 214–232\n 25 HCs, 7 multi, retire62, Record215, Patna1916\n Articles: 214 HC, 215 Record, 217 Judges, 226 Writ, 227\n→\n→\nSuperintend, 233 District\n HC Judge 10 Advocate / 10 Judicial, appointment President+CJI+Governor, oath Governor, resign\n→\nPresident\n Salary State, Pension India; 2.5/2.25\n HC powers O-W-A-R-S; death sentence HC confirm\n 226 FR+Legal vs 32\n→\n→\n→\nFR only; Chandra Kumar=226 Basic Structure\n UT pairs L-K, P-M, A-C; Delhi/J&K own\n District Judge Governor + HC + 7\n→\n→\nyears\n Special: Lok1985-Bhagwati, Mobile2007-Kalam, NGT2010\n Oldest MCB1862, Patna1916, newest Telangana/AP2019.”\n→\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nSC 65 vs HC 62 | HC oath by Governor, not President | Art.226 = FR + Legal Rights, wider than Art.32."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.17 Centre-State Relations\nCENTRE-STATE RELATIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 17 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part XI, 3 relations, 3 Lists, Parliament-on-State-List situations, Finance Commission, Inter-State\nCouncil, Zonal Councils aur river-water disputes ke high-confusion facts ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — Part XI, 245–293, 3 Relations\n• Centre-State Relations = Part XI, Articles 245–293\n• 3 types = Legislative + Administrative + Financial\n• 3-List System based on Government of India Act, 1935\n• Division of subjects = Article 246 + 7th Schedule\n• Legislative Relations = Articles 245–255\n• Administrative Relations = Articles 256–263\n• Financial Relations = Articles 268–293\n TRICK — “L-A-F = Legislative, Administrative, Financial”\n💡\nArticle blocks yaad karo: 245–255 L, 256–263 A, 268–293 F.\nChapter number spine: XI\n 245–293\n L-A-F\n 3 Lists.\n→\n→\n→\n2. Centre-State Commissions — 66, 69, 83, 07\n• 1966\n Setalvad Committee\n Administrative Reforms Commission\n→\n→\n• 1969\n Rajamannar Committee\n Tamil Nadu government; more State autonomy\n→\n→\n• 1983\n Sarkaria Commission\n most important; recommended Inter-State Council\n→\n→\n• 2007\n Punchhi Commission\n reviewed Sarkaria recommendations\n→\n→\n TRICK — “Se-Ra-Sa-Pu = 66–69–83–07”\n💡\nSetalvad\n Rajamannar\n Sarkaria\n Punchhi.\n→\n→\n→\nMost important anchor = Sarkaria 1983.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSarkaria recommended Inter-State Council in 1983; Council itself was established in 1990.\n3. 3 Lists — Current vs Original Numbers\n• Union List\n Current 98 | Original 97\n→\n• State List\n Current 59 | Original 66\n→\n• Concurrent List\n Current 52 | Original 47\n→\n• Union examples\n Defence, Atomic Energy, Foreign Affairs, Citizenship, Banking\n→\n• State examples\n Public Order, Police, Health, Water, Land/Agriculture\n→\n• Concurrent examples\n Criminal Law, Marriage, Education, Forests, Labour\n→\n TRICK — “Current 98–59–52 | Original 97–66–47”\n💡\nCurrent numbers: 98 / 59 / 52.\nOriginal numbers: 97 / 66 / 47.\nState List ka number ghata; Union/Concurrent side additions hue — source notes ka memory point.\n TRICK — “U = Defence-Bank | S = Police-Health | C = Education-Forest”\n💡\nExamples ko category anchors se yaad karo, full list ratne ki zaroorat nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.17 Centre-State Relations\n4. Concurrent Conflict — Article 254\n• Parliament + State Legislature both make law on Concurrent List\n Parliament law prevails\n→\n• Article 254\n• Exception in source notes\n State law with President's assent may prevail in that State\n→\n TRICK — “254 = Centre Wins, President-Assent Exception”\n💡\nDefault: Parliament prevails.\nException: President-assented State law can prevail within that State.\n5. Parliament on State List — National, States, Treaty, Emergency, Rule\n• Article 249\n National Interest\n Rajya Sabha 2/3 majority; valid 1 year, renewable\n→\n→\n• Agreement between two or more States\n States request Parliament (source table leaves article cell blank; overview\n→\nflags Art. 252 among exam articles)\n• Article 253\n International Treaties & Agreements\n→\n• Article 352\n National Emergency\n Parliament can legislate on entire State List (as stated in source notes)\n→\n→\n• Article 356\n President's Rule\n Parliament acts as State Legislature\n→\n→\n• Article 245\n Parliament can make laws for entire country + extra-territorial operation; State Legislature only within\n→\nState boundaries\n TRICK — “249 National – States Agree – 253 Treaty – 352 Emergency – 356 Rule”\n💡\nSituation chain yaad rakho: National Interest\n States' Agreement\n International Treaty\n Emergency\n President's Rule.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n249 ka special number pack: Rajya Sabha 2/3 + 1 year renewable.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt.249 ke liye Rajya Sabha 2/3 majority chahiye; Lok Sabha majority enough nahi.\n6. Administrative Relations — 256–257 + All India Services\n• Article 256\n Centre can direct States to comply with Central laws\n→\n• Article 257\n Union control over States in certain cases; States cannot impede Union executive power\n→\n• All India Services in source notes = IAS, IPS, IFoS\n• Centre full control\n appointment, disciplinary action, promotion, training\n→\n• State immediate control\n suspension only\n→\n• Source notes: State cannot dismiss, remove or compulsorily retire AIS officer\n TRICK — “256 Direction, 257 Control”\n💡\n256 = Centre says 'follow Central law'.\n257 = Union executive power ko State obstruct na kare.\n TRICK — “State = Suspend Only; Centre = Career Control”\n💡\nAIS trap: State ka immediate power = suspension only.\nAppointment/discipline/promotion/training = Centre.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes AIS par State ko dismissal/removal/compulsory retirement power nahi dete.\n7. Financial Relations — 268, 269A, 279A, 280\n• Article 268\n Duties levied by Union, collected by States; example Stamp Duty\n→\n• Article 269A\n Tax distribution between Union & States\n→\n• Article 279A\n GST Council\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.17 Centre-State Relations\n• GST Council\n 101st Amendment, 2016\n→\n• GST Council Chairman = Union Finance Minister\n• Article 280\n Finance Commission\n→\n TRICK — “268 Levy-Union/Collect-State > 269A Tax > 279A GST > 280 FC”\n💡\nFinancial articles ko ascending ladder mein bolo.\nGST anchor: 279A + 101st Amendment + 2016 + Union Finance Minister.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArt.268 mein source notes ka key trap: Union levies, States collect and retain.\n8. Finance Commission — 280, 5 Years, 1+4\n• Article 280\n• Nature = Quasi-judicial body\n• Constituted by President every 5 years or earlier\n• Composition = 1 Chairman + 4 Members\n• First Chairman = K.C. Neogy\n• Source notes list 16th Finance Commission Chairman = Arvind Panagariya\n• Functions = tax distribution, grants-in-aid, augment State funds for Panchayats/Municipalities\n• Recommendations = advisory, not binding\n TRICK — “280 – President – 5 – 1+4 – Neogy”\n💡\nFinance Commission number pack: Art.280, every 5 years, 1 Chairman + 4 members.\nNature = Quasi-judicial; recommendation = advisory.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFinance Commission recommendations binding nahi — advisory hain.\n9. Inter-State Council — Sarkaria 1983, Established 1990\n• Article 263\n• Established by President\n• Recommended by Sarkaria Commission (1983–87)\n• Established in 1990 under PM V.P. Singh\n• Source notes: reconstituted 19 May 2022\n• Meetings = at least 3 times a year\n• Chairman = Prime Minister\n• Members include all State CMs, CMs of UTs with legislatures, UT administrators, 6 Cabinet Ministers\n TRICK — “263 > 83 Recommend > 90 Establish > PM Chair”\n💡\nISC ka four-step chain: Article 263\n Sarkaria 1983\n established 1990\n Chairman PM.\n→\n→\n→\nMeetings hook = at least 3/year.\n TRICK — “PM = Inter-State Council; Home Minister = Zonal Councils”\n💡\nChairman confusion ko isi pair se lock karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1983 recommendation year hai; establishment year 1990."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.17 Centre-State Relations\n10. Zonal Councils — 5 Zones + Separate NE Council\n• Formed under States Reorganization Act, 1956\n• Chairman of all Zonal Councils = Union Home Minister\n• 5 Zonal Councils = Northern, Central, Eastern, Western, Southern\n• North-Eastern Council = separate; not one of the 5\n• Northern HQ = New Delhi\n• Central HQ = Prayagraj\n• Eastern HQ = Kolkata\n• Western HQ = Mumbai\n• Southern HQ = Chennai\n TRICK — “N-C-E-W-S = Delhi–Prayagraj–Kolkata–Mumbai–Chennai”\n💡\nZone order: Northern, Central, Eastern, Western, Southern.\nHQ order: Delhi, Prayagraj, Kolkata, Mumbai, Chennai.\n TRICK — “Bihar = EAST = Kolkata”\n💡\nEastern Zone = Bihar + Jharkhand + Odisha + West Bengal.\nBPSC anchor: Bihar\n Eastern Zonal Council\n HQ Kolkata.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNE Council ko 6th Zonal Council mat samjho — source notes ise separate body batate hain.\n11. North-Eastern Council — 1972, 8 States\n• Established 1972 under North-Eastern Council Act, 1971\n• Initially 7 States\n• Currently 8 States in source notes\n• Sikkim added in 2002\n• Members in source notes\n 1 Chairman + 3 other Members + 8 CMs & Governors\n→\n TRICK — “NEC: Act 71, Start 72, Sikkim 02, Total 8”\n💡\nYear chain: 1971 Act\n 1972 established\n 2002 Sikkim added\n 8 States.\n→\n→\n→\n12. Inter-State River Water Disputes — Article 262\n• Constitutional provision = Article 262\n• Statutory basis = Inter-State River Water Disputes Act, 1956; source notes mention amendment 2017\n• Composition in source notes = 1 Chairperson + 1 Vice-Chairperson + maximum 6 members\n• Chairperson term = 5 years; VP/members till dispute resolved\n• Article 262 allows Parliament by law to exclude Supreme Court jurisdiction\n TRICK — “262 = River Dispute, SC Can Be Shut Out”\n💡\nArt.262 ka biggest trap = Parliament SC jurisdiction exclude kar sakti hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRiver-water dispute mein SC jurisdiction exclusion source notes ka special exam point hai.\n13. River Tribunal Timeline — 1969 Triple\n• Krishna Water Dispute I\n 1969\n→\n• Godavari Water Dispute\n 1969\n→\n• Narmada Water Dispute\n 1969\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.17 Centre-State Relations\n• Ravi & Beas\n 1986\n→\n• Cauvery\n 1990\n→\n• Mahanadi\n 2018\n→\n TRICK — “KGN = 1969 Triple”\n💡\nKrishna + Godavari + Narmada = same year 1969.\nThen Ravi-Beas 1986\n Cauvery 1990\n Mahanadi 2018.\n→\n→\n TRICK — “Cauvery = K-K-T-P”\n💡\nSource notes states: Karnataka, Kerala, Tamil Nadu, Puducherry.\n TRICK — “Mahanadi = O-C”\n💡\nOdisha + Chhattisgarh; source notes list 2018.\n14. 20-Second Article Flash Chain\n• 245\n territory / extra-territorial Parliament power\n→\n• 246\n subject division + 7th Schedule\n→\n• 249\n National Interest, RS 2/3, 1 year\n→\n• 253\n International Treaties\n→\n• 254\n Concurrent conflict\n→\n• 256\n Centre directions\n→\n• 257\n Union control\n→\n• 262\n River disputes\n→\n• 263\n Inter-State Council\n→\n• 268\n Union levy / State collection\n→\n• 279A\n GST Council\n→\n• 280\n Finance Commission\n→\n TRICK — “245 Territory – 246 Lists – 249 National – 253 Treaty – 254 Conflict – 256 Direction – 257 Control\n💡\n\n– 262 River – 263 Council – 268 Tax – 279A GST – 280 FC”\nArticle numbers ko subject-word ke saath rhythm mein bolo; poora chapter reconstruct ho jayega.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part XI 245–293\n L-A-F relations; 3 Lists from 1935 Act, Art246+7th\n Commissions Se-Ra-Sa-Pu 66-69-83-07\n Lists current\n→\n→\n→\n98-59-52 vs original 97-66-47; conflict254 Parliament prevails\n State List situations: 249 National (RS2/3,1yr), States agree,\n→\n253 Treaty, 352 Emergency, 356 Rule; 245 extra-territorial\n Admin 256 Direction,257 Control; AIS State suspend-only\n\n→\n→\nFinancial 268 Union levy/State collect,269A tax,279A GST/101st-2016/FM,280 FC\n FC 5\n→\nyears,1+4,Neogy,quasi-judicial/advisory\n ISC 263: Sarkaria83, established90, PM chair\n Zonal Councils 5, Home Minister;\n→\n→\nN-C-E-W-S HQ Delhi-Prayagraj-Kolkata-Mumbai-Chennai; Bihar East-Kolkata; NEC separate 1972/8\n River Art262, SC\n→\nexclusion; KGN1969 triple, Ravi86, Cauvery90, Mahanadi2018.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nSarkaria 1983 recommended ISC, established 1990 | Art.249 needs RS 2/3 | Inter-State Council Chair = PM, Zonal Councils\nChair = Union Home Minister."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Emergency Provisions\nEMERGENCY PROVISIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 18 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part XVIII, Articles 352–360, 3 emergencies, 44th Amendment safeguards, Art.358 vs 359,\nPresident's Rule, Financial Emergency aur key case-law traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — Part XVIII, 352–360, 3 Emergencies\n• Part XVIII\n Articles 352–360\n→\n• 3 types\n National Emergency, President's Rule, Financial Emergency\n→\n• Source\n Weimar Constitution (Germany) + Government of India Act, 1935\n→\n• Proclamation by President\n entire country or any part thereof\n→\n• National Emergency = Article 352\n• President's Rule = Article 356\n• Financial Emergency = Article 360\n TRICK — “352–356–360 = National–State–Financial”\n💡\nTeen articles ko 4-4 ke jump mein yaad karo: 352\n 356\n 360.\n→\n→\nType mapping: National\n President's Rule\n Financial.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nEmergency source = Germany + GoI Act 1935 — dono yaad rakho.\n2. National Emergency — 3 Times Declared\n• 1962\n Chinese Aggression\n President Dr. S. Radhakrishnan\n→\n→\n• 1971\n India-Pakistan War\n President V.V. Giri\n→\n→\n• 1975\n Internal Disturbance\n President Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed\n→\n→\n• 1975 PM = Indira Gandhi\n• 44th Amendment, 1978 replaced 'Internal Disturbance' with 'Armed Rebellion'\n TRICK — “62 China – 71 Pakistan – 75 Internal”\n💡\nYears ko conflict ke saath lock karo: 1962 China, 1971 Pakistan, 1975 Internal Disturbance.\n1975 person-trap: President Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed; PM Indira Gandhi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1975 Emergency ka ground source notes mein 'Internal Disturbance' hai; baad mein 44th Amendment ne 'Armed Rebellion'\nkiya.\n3. Article 352 Grounds — W-E-A\n• War\n• External Aggression\n• Armed Rebellion\n TRICK — “W-E-A = War, External, Armed”\n💡\nNational Emergency grounds ko WEA bolo.\nArmed Rebellion = 44th Amendment safeguard replacement.\n4. National Emergency Process — 1 Month, 6 Months, Special, Simple\n• Declaration only on written recommendation of Cabinet\n• Approval\n Special Majority in both Houses\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Emergency Provisions\n• Approval deadline\n within 1 month\n→\n• If Lok Sabha dissolved\n within 30 days of first sitting of new Lok Sabha\n→\n• Renewal\n every 6 months\n→\n• Duration\n unlimited as long as Parliament keeps approving\n→\n• Revocation\n Simple Majority of Lok Sabha\n→\n TRICK — “Written–1–6–Unlimited–LS Simple”\n💡\nWritten Cabinet recommendation\n approval in 1 month\n renewal every 6 months\n no fixed max duration.\n→\n→\n→\nApproval = Special Majority; revocation = Lok Sabha Simple Majority.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNational Emergency: Approval Special Majority, Revocation Simple Majority of Lok Sabha — classic majority trap.\n5. National Emergency Effects — What Changes, What Survives\n• Article 19 freedoms can be suspended under source-notes framework\n• Centre can legislate on State List\n• President can direct State executives\n• Lok Sabha term can be extended by 1 year\n• Revenue sharing can be altered\n• Articles 20 & 21 remain protected\n• Post-44th Amendment, Habeas Corpus protection highlighted in source notes\n• Federal structure continues partly\n TRICK — “State List + LS Year + Revenue Change; 20–21 Safe”\n💡\nEffects ko power-shift ke roop mein dekho: Centre stronger, State autonomy narrower.\nEmergency safety lock: Articles 20 & 21 never suspended.\n6. Judicial Review — Minerva Mills + Article 355\n• Minerva Mills Case, 1980\n Emergency subject to Judicial Review\n→\n• Supreme Court can review validity of grounds for Emergency\n• Article 355\n Union's duty to protect States from external aggression & internal disturbance and ensure constitutional\n→\ngovernance\n TRICK — “Minerva = Review; 355 = Duty”\n💡\nCase-word: Minerva Mills\n Emergency reviewable.\n→\nArticle contrast ahead: 355 = duty, 356 = President's Rule power.\n7. President's Rule — Articles 356 & 365\n• Article 356\n Failure of Constitutional Machinery in State\n→\n• Article 365\n State fails to comply with Union's directions\n→\n• First imposed\n Punjab, 20 June 1951\n→\n• Most times in source notes\n Manipur & Uttar Pradesh, 10 times each\n→\n• Approval\n Simple Majority in both Houses\n→\n• Deadline\n 2 months\n→\n• Renewal\n every 6 months\n→\n• Maximum duration\n 3 years\n→\n• Revocation\n President anytime; no Parliament approval needed\n→\n TRICK — “356 Failure, 365 Defiance”\n💡\n356 = constitutional machinery fails.\n365 = State Union directions nahi maanta."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Emergency Provisions\n TRICK — “2–6–3–President”\n💡\nPresident's Rule process: approval in 2 months\n renew every 6 months\n max 3 years\n President can revoke anytime.\n→\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPresident's Rule approval = Simple Majority, not Special Majority.\n8. President's Rule Effects — FR Safe\n• Centre takes over; division of power affected\n• State Council of Ministers\n dissolved/suspended\n→\n• Legislative Assembly\n suspended or dissolved\n→\n• Fundamental Rights\n no effect\n→\n• Laws made during President's Rule\n remain valid for 6 months after revocation (source notes)\n→\n TRICK — “Government/Assembly Hit, FR Not Hit”\n💡\nPresident's Rule state machinery ko affect karta hai, Fundamental Rights ko suspend nahi karta.\n9. S.R. Bommai Case — 1994\n• S.R. Bommai Case, 1994\n• Article 356 proclamation subject to Judicial Review\n• President's Rule cannot be imposed arbitrarily\n• Floor test should be used to test majority\n• President's Rule = last resort, not first option\n TRICK — “Bommai = 356 + Floor Test + Review”\n💡\nBommai ko Article 356 ke saath permanently lock karo.\n10. Financial Emergency — Article 360\n• Ground\n Threat to financial stability\n→\n• Status in source notes\n Never imposed in India's history\n→\n• Declaration\n President on Cabinet advice\n→\n• Approval\n Simple Majority within 2 months\n→\n• Duration\n Unlimited with Parliamentary continuation\n→\n• Revocation\n President anytime\n→\n• Union-State tax distribution may be suspended\n• Salaries/allowances of Union & State employees may be reduced\n• Source notes explicitly include SC & HC Judges' salaries\n• President may direct States on financial matters\n• State Money Bills may be reserved for President's consideration\n TRICK — “360 = Money Crisis, Never Used”\n💡\nFinancial Emergency ka biggest hook = never imposed.\nExam twist: SC/HC Judges ki salary bhi reduce ho sakti hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFinancial Emergency theoretical provision hi raha hai in source notes — never imposed."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Emergency Provisions\n11. Article 358 vs 359 — Most Important Comparison\n• Article 358\n suspends only Article 19\n→\n• Article 358\n applies only during War & External Aggression\n→\n• Article 358\n automatic; no separate Presidential Order\n→\n• Article 358\n does NOT apply to Armed Rebellion\n→\n• Article 359\n applies to all FRs except Articles 20 & 21\n→\n• Article 359\n Presidential Order required\n→\n• Article 359\n applies during War/External Aggression and Armed Rebellion\n→\n• Article 359 may apply to whole country or part\n TRICK — “358 = 19 Auto, War/External Only”\n💡\n358 ko ‘19-Auto’ se lock karo.\nArmed Rebellion mein 358 NO.\n TRICK — “359 = President Order, All Except 20–21”\n💡\n359 ke liye Presidential Order chahiye.\n20 & 21 always protected.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArmed Rebellion mein Art.358 apply nahi; Art.359 apply kar sakta hai.\n12. Articles 20 & 21 — Never Suspended\n• Article 20\n Protection from conviction\n→\n• Article 21\n Right to Life & Liberty\n→\n• 44th Amendment, 1978 explicitly protected both during Emergency\n• Source notes connect this safeguard with the experience of 1975 Emergency and ADM Jabalpur\n TRICK — “20–21 = Emergency-Proof Pair”\n💡\nYe pair poore emergency chapter ka safest memory anchor hai.\n13. All 3 Emergencies — 1–2–2 / Special–Simple–Simple\n• National (352)\n Approval Special Majority; deadline 1 month; max duration unlimited; revoke LS Simple Majority\n→\n• President's Rule (356)\n Approval Simple Majority; deadline 2 months; max 3 years; revoke President anytime\n→\n• Financial (360)\n Approval Simple Majority; deadline 2 months; max unlimited; revoke President anytime\n→\n TRICK — “Deadline = 1–2–2”\n💡\nNational = 1 month.\nPresident's Rule = 2 months.\nFinancial = 2 months.\n TRICK — “Majority = S–Simp–Simp”\n💡\nNational = Special Majority.\n356 and 360 = Simple Majority.\n TRICK — “Revocation = LS / President / President”\n💡\n352\n Lok Sabha Simple Majority.\n→\n356\n President anytime.\n→\n360\n President anytime.\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Emergency Provisions\n14. Criticism Quotes — 3 Names\n• T.T. Krishnamachari\n Fundamental Rights meaningless; democratic foundation undermined\n→\n• Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n Risk of misuse for political objectives\n→\n• Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\n President's Rule is a 'dead letter'\n→\n• K.M. Nambiar\n Emergency powers of President = betrayal of Constitution\n→\n TRICK — “TTK–Ambedkar×2–Nambiar”\n💡\nAmbedkar ke 2 separate quotes yaad rakho: misuse + dead letter.\n15. 44th Amendment Safeguards — A-W-L-20/21-6\n• Armed Rebellion replaced Internal Disturbance\n• Written Cabinet recommendation mandatory\n• Lok Sabha can revoke by Simple Majority\n• Articles 20 & 21 explicitly protected\n• 6-month renewal required for continuation\n• Source notes: 44th Amendment passed in 1978 during Morarji Desai government\n TRICK — “A-W-L-20/21-6”\n💡\nA = Armed Rebellion, W = Written Cabinet advice, L = LS revocation, 20/21 protected, 6-month renewal.\nYe 1975 ke baad ka safeguard package hai.\n16. 20-Second Article Flash Chain\n• 352\n National Emergency\n→\n• 355\n Union's duty to protect States\n→\n• 356\n President's Rule\n→\n• 358\n Art.19 automatic suspension framework\n→\n• 359\n Presidential Order affecting FR enforcement except 20/21\n→\n• 360\n Financial Emergency\n→\n• 365\n State fails to comply with Union directions\n→\n TRICK — “352 Emergency, 355 Duty, 356 Rule, 358 Art19, 359 Order, 360 Finance, 365 Defiance”\n💡\nArticle-word pairing se poora chapter quickly reconstruct ho jayega.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part XVIII 352–360, source Germany+GoI1935\n 3 types 352 National,356 President's Rule,360 Financial\n National years 62\n→\n→\nChina,71 Pakistan,75 Internal; Fakhruddin President\n WEA grounds; 44th makes Armed Rebellion\n 352 process Written\n→\n→\nCabinet, 1 month Special, 6-month renewal, unlimited, LS Simple revoke; 20–21 safe; Minerva1980 review\n 355 Duty vs 356\n→\nRule; President's Rule 2-month Simple, 6-month renew, max3yr, President revoke; first Punjab1951; Bommai1994 floor\ntest/review\n 360 never imposed, 2-month Simple, unlimited, President revoke; judges' salary can reduce\n 358 = Art19 Auto\n→\n→\n+ War/External only; 359 = Presidential Order + all FR except 20/21 + Armed Rebellion too\n All-3 compare: deadlines 1-2-2;\n→\nmajority Special-Simple-Simple; revocation LS-President-President\n 44th safeguards A-W-L-20/21-6.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\n352 approval Special vs 356/360 Simple | Art.358 = only Art.19 + War/External | Articles 20 & 21 never suspended."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\nLOCAL SELF-GOVERNMENT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 19 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Lord Ripon, Panchayati Raj committees, 73rd/74th Amendments, 11th/12th Schedules, municipal\nbodies, PESA, Nyaya Panchayats, Cooperative Societies aur Bihar-specific traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya\ngaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — State List, Rural + Urban\n• Local Self-Government = State List subject\n• Aim = decentralization of power at grassroots level\n• Rural institution = Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs)\n• Urban institution = Municipalities\n• 73rd Amendment, 1992\n Panchayats\n→\n• 74th Amendment, 1992\n Municipalities\n→\n• Bihar special = first State to implement 50% women reservation in Panchayats, 2006\n TRICK — “73 Rural, 74 Urban”\n💡\n73rd ko Panchayat/Rural se lock karo.\n74th ko Municipality/Urban se lock karo.\nChapter ka Bihar star = 50% women reservation, 2006.\n2. Ripon 1882 vs Panchayati Raj 1959\n• Father of Local Self-Government = Lord Ripon\n• Ripon Resolution = 1882\n• Called 'Magna Carta of Local Self-Government'\n• Panchayati Raj launched = 2 October 1959\n• Place = Nagaur, Rajasthan\n• Launched by Jawaharlal Nehru\n• Source notes also mention simultaneous launch in Andhra Pradesh\n TRICK — “1882 = Ripon Idea, 1959 = Panchayat Launch”\n💡\nRipon ko origin/father se jodo; actual Panchayati Raj launch ko 2 Oct 1959 se.\nNagaur + Nehru ek pair hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1882 aur 1959 ko same event mat samajhna.\n3. Historical Timeline — 82, 52, 53, 57, 59, 92, 93\n• 1882\n Ripon Resolution\n→\n• 1952\n Community Development Scheme\n→\n• 1953\n National Extension Service Scheme\n→\n• 1957\n Balwant Rai Mehta Committee\n→\n• 1959\n Panchayati Raj launch\n→\n• 1992\n 73rd & 74th Amendments passed\n→\n• 24 Apr 1993\n 73rd effective\n→\n• 1 Jun 1993\n 74th effective\n→\n• 2010\n Panchayati Raj Diwas celebrations began\n→\n TRICK — “Ripon–CDS–NES–Balwant–Launch–73/74”\n💡\nTimeline ko year se zyada event-chain ki tarah bolo.\n1992 passed, 1993 effective — dono amendments ke liye."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\n4. Panchayati Raj Committees — B-A-S-T-G\n• Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957)\n Architect; democratic decentralization; 3-tier system\n→\n• Ashok Mehta Committee (1977–78)\n 2-tier structure; Mandala Panchayat 15,000–20,000 + District Council\n→\n• L.M. Singhvi Committee (1986)\n Constitutional Status + Nyaya Panchayats\n→\n• P.K. Thungan Committee (1988–89)\n timely elections + fixed 5-year tenure\n→\n• V.N. Gadgil Committee (1988)\n direct election to all 3 tiers\n→\n TRICK — “B-A-S-T-G = 3, 2, Status, Tenure, Direct”\n💡\nBalwant = 3-tier.\nAshok = 2-tier.\nSinghvi = Constitutional Status + Nyaya.\nThungan = 5-year tenure.\nGadgil = direct election all tiers.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBalwant 3-tier implemented; Ashok Mehta 2-tier source notes mein NOT implemented.\n5. 73rd Amendment — Panchayat Pack\n• 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992\n• PM = P.V. Narasimha Rao\n• Effective = 24 April 1993\n Panchayati Raj Diwas\n→\n• Part IX\n• Articles 243–243O\n• 11th Schedule = 29 subjects\n• Gram Sabha = Article 243(A)\n• 3-tier Panchayat = Article 243(B)\n• Term = 5 years\n• Minimum age = 21 years\n• Women reservation = minimum 1/3\n• SC/ST reservation = proportional to population\n• State Finance Commission = every 5 years\n• State Election Commission = conducts elections\n TRICK — “73 = IX + 243–O + 11th/29 + 24 April”\n💡\n73rd ka full pack ek saath bolo: Part IX\n Art.243–243O\n 11th Schedule 29\n effective 24 Apr 1993.\n→\n→\n→\nAge = 21, term = 5, women = 1/3.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPanchayat minimum age = 21; Parliament 25/30 se confuse mat karna.\n6. 3-Tier Panchayat — G-P-Z + D-I-I\n• Tier 1\n Gram Panchayat\n Village\n Direct Election\n→\n→\n→\n• Tier 2\n Panchayat Samiti\n Block\n Indirect Election\n→\n→\n→\n• Tier 3\n Zila Panchayat\n District\n Indirect Election\n→\n→\n→\n TRICK — “G-P-Z = Gram, Panchayat Samiti, Zila”\n💡\nLevel chain: Village\n Block\n District.\n→\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\n TRICK — “D-I-I = Direct, Indirect, Indirect”\n💡\nSirf Gram Panchayat direct; Block aur District indirect.\nGadgil ne all-three direct recommend kiya tha, adopted pattern source notes mein D-I-I hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRecommendation aur adopted pattern ko swap mat karna.\n7. Panchayat Special Cases — 20L, WB, M-M-N\n• States below 20 lakh population\n middle tier/Kshetra Panchayat not compulsory\n→\n• West Bengal\n 4-tier Panchayati Raj system in source notes\n→\n• Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagaland\n no Panchayats; Tribal Councils exist\n→\n TRICK — “<20L No Middle; WB Four; M-M-N Tribal”\n💡\nTeen exceptions ko one-line contrast mein yaad karo.\n8. Reservation — 1/3 Constitution, Bihar 50% First\n• Constitutional minimum women reservation = 1/3\n• SC/ST reservation = proportional to population\n• 1/3 of SC/ST reserved seats also for women\n• Reservation rotates\n• Source notes: Centre allowed 50% women reservation in 2009\n• Bihar = first State to implement 50% in 2006\n• Source notes mention 21+ States currently with 50%\n TRICK — “1/3 India Minimum, Bihar 50 in 2006”\n💡\nBPSC ke liye Bihar-year ko direct lock karo: Bihar\n 50%\n 2006.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nConstitutional minimum 1/3 hai; Bihar special 50% implementation alag fact hai.\n9. 11th vs 12th Schedule — 29 vs 18 = 47\n• 11th Schedule\n Panchayats\n 29 subjects\n→\n→\n• 12th Schedule\n Municipalities\n 18 subjects\n→\n→\n• Source notes total = 47 subjects\n TRICK — “11>29, 12>18, Total 47”\n💡\nSimple number chain: 29 + 18 = 47.\n11th = Rural/Panchayat; 12th = Urban/Municipality.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n29 aur 18 ko ulta mat karna.\n10. 74th Amendment — Municipality Pack\n• 74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992\n• Effective = 1 June 1993\n• Part IXA\n• Articles 243P–243ZG\n• 12th Schedule = 18 subjects"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\n• 1st Municipal Corporation = Madras, 1687\n• Ward Committee = 3 lakh+ population areas, Article 243S\n• District Planning Committee = Article 243ZD\n• Metropolitan Planning Committee = Article 243ZE; 10 lakh+ population\n TRICK — “74 = IXA + P–ZG + 12th/18 + 1 June”\n💡\n74th ka pack: Part IXA\n 243P–243ZG\n 12th Schedule 18\n effective 1 Jun 1993.\n→\n→\n→\nPopulation hooks: Ward = 3L+, Metro Planning = 10L+.\n TRICK — “Madras 1687 = First Municipal Corporation”\n💡\nBombay/Calcutta later; source notes first = Madras.\n11. Municipality Population Ladder — 10K, 20K, 3L\n• Nagar Panchayat = 10,000–20,000\n• Municipal Council = 20,000–3 lakh\n• Municipal Corporation = above 3 lakh\n• Ward Committee mandatory = 3 lakh+ areas\n TRICK — “10K–20K–3L”\n💡\nNagar Panchayat starts 10K.\n20K ke baad Municipal Council.\n3L ke baad Corporation.\n12. Urban Local Bodies — 8 Types\n• Municipal Corporations\n• Municipal Councils\n• Cantonment Boards\n• Town Area Committee\n• Special Purpose Agencies\n• Port Trusts\n• Townships\n• Notified Area Councils\n TRICK — “MC–MC–C–T–S–P–T–N”\n💡\nFirst two Municipal pair, then Cantonment, Town Area, Special, Port, Township, Notified.\nSource trap: Cantonment Boards = military areas, Ministry of Defence; NOT under 74th Amendment.\n13. PESA 1996 — 5th Schedule, Bhuria, 10 States\n• PESA = Panchayats (Extension to Scheduled Areas) Act, 1996\n• Applies to 5th Schedule tribal areas\n• Recommended by Bhuria Commission\n• Implemented in 10 States in source notes\n• Source notes: 5th Schedule areas were outside automatic 73rd Amendment coverage\n• 6th Schedule areas have different tribal-governance arrangements\n TRICK — “PESA = 96 + 5th + Bhuria + 10”\n💡\nPESA number pack: 1996, 5th Schedule, Bhuria Commission, 10 States.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPESA = 5th Schedule; 6th Schedule tribal areas ka arrangement alag."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\n14. Nyaya Panchayat vs Gram Nyayalaya\n• Nyaya Panchayat\n village-level justice\n→\n• Handles civil + criminal cases in source notes\n• Fine range = ₹50–₹1,000\n• Recommended by L.M. Singhvi Committee, 1986\n• Gram Nyayalaya\n separate formal court under Gram Nyayalayas Act, 2008\n→\n TRICK — “Singhvi 1986 = Nyaya Panchayat; Act 2008 = Gram Nyayalaya”\n💡\nInformal Panchayat justice vs formal court-under-Act ko separate rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNyaya Panchayat aur Gram Nyayalaya same nahi hain.\n15. Cooperative Societies — 97th Amendment Trifecta\n• 97th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2011\n• Part IX(B) added\n• Articles 243(ZH)–243(ZT)\n• Constitutional status to Cooperative Societies\n• Connected in source notes with FR Article 19(c) — right to form associations\n• DPSP Article 43B added\n TRICK — “97 = FR + DPSP + Part IXB”\n💡\nOne amendment, three hooks:\nFR side 19(c)\n DPSP 43B\n Part IX(B)/243ZH–ZT.\n→\n→\n16. Panchayat Article Flash Chain\n• 243(A)\n Gram Sabha\n→\n• 243(B)\n 3-tier Panchayats\n→\n• 243(D)\n Reservation\n→\n• 243(E)\n Duration 5 years\n→\n• 243(I)\n State Finance Commission, every 5 years\n→\n• 243(K)\n State Election Commission\n→\n• 243(M)\n non-application to certain areas\n→\n• 243(O)\n court interference restricted in elections\n→\n TRICK — “A Sabha, B Build, D Reservation, E 5 Years, I Finance, K Election”\n💡\nHigh-yield letters ko subject ke saath yaad karo.\n17. Municipality Article Flash Chain\n• 243(P)\n Definitions\n→\n• 243(S)\n Ward Committees, 3L+\n→\n• 243(ZD)\n District Planning Committee\n→\n• 243(ZE)\n Metropolitan Planning Committee, 10L+\n→\n• 243(ZG)\n bar to court interference in elections\n→\n• 243(ZH–ZT)\n Cooperative Societies\n→\n TRICK — “S Ward, ZD District, ZE Metro, ZG Election Bar”\n💡\nPlanning pair: ZD = District, ZE = Metropolitan."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Local Self-Government\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“State List + decentralization\n Ripon1882 Magna Carta vs Panchayat launch 2Oct1959 Nagaur-Nehru\n Committees B-A-S-T-\n→\n→\nG = Balwant3, Ashok2, Singhvi Status/Nyaya, Thungan5yr, Gadgil Direct-all\n 73rd: Part IX, 243–O, 11th/29, 24Apr93, age21,\n→\nterm5, women1/3\n 3-tier G-P-Z with D-I-I; exceptions <20L/WB4/MMN tribal\n Bihar first 50% women 2006\n 11th29 vs\n→\n→\n→\n12th18 = 47\n 74th: Part IXA, 243P–ZG, 12th/18, 1Jun93, Madras1687, Ward3L+, Metro10L+\n municipalities 10K-20K /\n→\n→\n20K-3L / 3L+\n PESA1996 = 5th Schedule + Bhuria + 10 States\n Nyaya Panchayat Singhvi1986 vs Gram Nyayalaya Act2008\n\n→\n→\n→\n97th2011 = FR19(c)+DPSP43B+Part IXB\n Panchayat articles A Sabha, B 3-tier, D reservation, E term, I Finance, K Election.”\n→\n Top 3:\n⚠\nRipon 1882 vs Panchayat launch 1959 | 73rd = 11th Schedule/29 vs 74th = 12th/18 | Bihar first 50% women reservation in\nPanchayats = 2006."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.20 Official Language\nOFFICIAL LANGUAGE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 20 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part XVII, Articles 343–351, 8th Schedule languages, Classical Languages, Hindi Diwas, Official\nLanguage Commission/Committee aur exam traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — XVII, 343–351, 22, 11\n• Official Language provisions = Part XVII, Articles 343–351\n• Official Language of Union = Hindi in Devanagari script — Article 343\n• India has NO National Language in the Constitution\n• 8th Schedule = 22 languages; originally 14\n• Added later = 8 languages\n• Classical Languages = 11 in source notes (as of 2024)\n• Hindi Diwas = 14 September\n TRICK — “XVII–343/351–22–11–14 Sep”\n💡\nChapter number spine: Part XVII\n 343–351\n 22 scheduled\n 11 classical\n Hindi Diwas 14 Sep.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHindi = Official Language, NOT National Language.\n2. Commission & Committee — 1955 Kher, 1957 Pant, 30 Members\n• 1955\n 1st Official Language Commission\n→\n• Chairperson = B.G. Kher\n• Nov 1957\n 1st Joint Parliamentary Committee\n→\n• Chairperson = Govind Vallabh Pant\n• Parliamentary Committee on Official Language = 30 members\n• Composition = 20 Lok Sabha + 10 Rajya Sabha\n• Function = review progress of Hindi in government work & recommend\n TRICK — “55 Kher, 57 Pant, 20+10=30”\n💡\n1955 Commission = B.G. Kher.\n1957 Committee = Govind Vallabh Pant.\nCommittee number pack = 20 LS + 10 RS = 30.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCommission 1955 aur Committee 1957 ko swap mat karna.\n3. Official Language Act Amendment — 1967\n• 1967\n Amendment in Official Language Act\n→\n• Source notes: English continues for government work until non-Hindi speaking States adopt Hindi voluntarily\n TRICK — “1967 = English Continues”\n💡\nOfficial Language Act amendment ko ek hi phrase se lock karo: 1967\n English continues.\n→\n4. 8th Schedule — 14 + 8 = 22\n• Original Scheduled Languages = 14\n• Current Scheduled Languages = 22\n• Added later = 8"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.20 Official Language\n TRICK — “14 + 8 = 22”\n💡\nYe simple arithmetic poore 8th Schedule question ko solve kar deta hai.\n5. Added Languages — 21st, 71st, 92nd\n• 21st Amendment, 1967\n Sindhi (1)\n→\n• 71st Amendment, 1992\n Konkani, Manipuri, Nepali (3)\n→\n• 92nd Amendment, 2003\n Bodo, Dogri, Santhali, Maithili (4)\n→\n TRICK — “21–71–92 = 1–3–4”\n💡\n21st = 1 language.\n71st = 3 languages.\n92nd = 4 languages.\n1 + 3 + 4 = 8 additions.\n TRICK — “K-M-N / B-D-S-M”\n💡\n71st = Konkani–Manipuri–Nepali.\n92nd = Bodo–Dogri–Santhali–Maithili.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMaithili = 92nd Amendment, 2003 — Bihar ke liye direct exam fact.\n6. English vs Sanskrit — Schedule Trap\n• English is NOT in 8th Schedule\n• Sanskrit IS in 8th Schedule\n• Source notes: Kashmiri and Sindhi have no exclusive State/UT territory\n• Source notes: Scheduled-language speakers may use that language in UPSC exam besides Hindi/English\n TRICK — “English OUT, Sanskrit IN”\n💡\nBas ye opposite pair yaad rakho.\n7. Classical Languages — 2004 to 2024 Timeline\n• 2004\n Tamil (first classical language)\n→\n• 2005\n Sanskrit\n→\n• 2008\n Telugu + Kannada\n→\n• 2013\n Malayalam\n→\n• 2014\n Odia\n→\n• 2024\n Pali + Marathi + Prakrit + Assamese + Bengali\n→\n• Total in source notes = 11\n TRICK — “T-S-TK-M-O + PM-PAB”\n💡\nOld 6: Tamil\n Sanskrit\n Telugu/Kannada\n Malayalam\n Odia.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n2024 five: Pali, Marathi, Prakrit, Assamese, Bengali.\n TRICK — “2024 = Five New, Total 11”\n💡\nPali–Marathi–Prakrit–Assamese–Bengali = 5 additions in 2024.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nClassical Language status Constitution mein mentioned nahi — source notes ise government decision batate hain.\nMaithili 8th Schedule mein hai, lekin source notes ke according classical language nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.20 Official Language\n8. Classical Language Criteria — 1500–2000 + Literature + Texts\n• Language must be 1500–2000 years old\n• Related to Traditional Literature\n• Availability of Ancient Texts & Literature\n• Source notes: process based on recommendations from committees formed by Sahitya Akademi\n TRICK — “Age–Literature–Texts”\n💡\nClassical criteria ko 3 words mein yaad karo: Age\n Literature\n Ancient Texts.\n→\n→\n9. Hindi Diwas vs World Hindi Day\n• Hindi Diwas = 14 September 1949\n• Hindi adopted as Official Language by Constituent Assembly\n• Celebrated annually on 14 September\n• World Hindi Day = 10 January\n• First World Hindi Conference = Nagpur, 1975\n• World Hindi Day celebrated globally on 10 January\n TRICK — “14 Sep = India; 10 Jan = World”\n💡\nHindi Diwas = National/India.\nWorld Hindi Day = International/global.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n14 September aur 10 January ko swap mat karna.\n10. Article 343–351 — Fast Map\n• 343\n Official Language of Union = Hindi in Devanagari\n→\n• 344\n Commission & Committee on Official Language\n→\n• 345\n Official Language of State\n→\n• 346\n Communication between States and Union\n→\n• 348\n Language of Judiciary & Legislation\n→\n• 350(A)\n Education in mother tongue at primary stage\n→\n• 351\n Promotion & development of Hindi\n→\n TRICK — “343 Hindi, 344 Committee, 345 State, 346 Communication, 348 Court, 350A Mother Tongue, 351\n💡\n\nPromote Hindi”\nArticle-word pairing se poora Part XVII reconstruct ho jayega.\n11. Article 348 — Court Language Trap\n• Source notes: Supreme Court & High Court proceedings = English\n• Unless President authorizes otherwise\n TRICK — “348 = High Courts Speak English”\n💡\n348 ko Judiciary-English se lock karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes explicitly warn: highest courts ki constitutional language English hai."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.20 Official Language\n12. Article 351 — Centre's Duty\n• Article 351\n Promotion & development of Hindi language\n→\n• Centre's duty to develop Hindi\n TRICK — “351 = Hindi Promote”\n💡\n343 = Hindi official; 351 = Hindi promote/develop.\n13. 20-Second Flash Recall\n• Part XVII, Articles 343–351\n• Hindi = Official, not National\n• 8th Schedule = 22 = 14 + 8\n• 21st/71st/92nd = 1/3/4 additions\n• Maithili = 92nd Amendment, 2003\n• Classical = Tamil first 2004; total 11 in source notes\n• Hindi Diwas = 14 Sep; World Hindi Day = 10 Jan\n• 1955 Kher; 1957 Pant; Committee 20+10=30\n• 343 Hindi, 348 Judiciary-English, 351 Promote Hindi\n TRICK — “Hindi–22–1/3/4–11–14Sep/10Jan–55/57–343/348/351”\n💡\nExam se pehle sirf ye compressed chain ek baar bolna enough hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part XVII 343–351\n Art343 Hindi in Devanagari, NO National Language\n 1955 B.G. Kher Commission, 1957 Govind Vallabh\n→\n→\n\nPant Committee, 20LS+10RS=30\n 1967 English continues\n 8th Schedule 14+8=22; amendments 21-71-92 = 1-3-4: Sindhi / K-\n→\n→\nM-N / B-D-S-M; Maithili 92nd-2003\n English OUT, Sanskrit IN\n Classical: Tamil2004 first, Sanskrit05, Telugu-Kannada08,\n→\n→\nMalayalam13, Odia14, 2024 Pali-Marathi-Prakrit-Assamese-Bengali = total11; classical not constitutional\n Hindi Diwas\n→\n14Sep1949 vs World Hindi Day 10Jan\n Articles: 344 Committee,345 State,346 Communication, 348 Judiciary-English,350A\n→\nMother Tongue,351 Hindi Promotion.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nHindi is Official, not National | 21st/71st/92nd = 1/3/4 additions | Hindi Diwas 14 Sep vs World Hindi Day 10 Jan."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.21 Constitutional Amendment\nCONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 21 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Part XX, Article 368, 3 majority types, amendment procedure, important amendments, Basic\nStructure, scholars aur exam traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Master Skeleton — XX, 368, South Africa, 106\n• Constitutional Amendment = Part XX, Article 368\n• Source = South Africa\n• Source notes: 106 Amendments so far\n• Constitution = rigid + flexible\n• Basic Structure cannot be destroyed by amendment\n• Key case = Keshavananda Bharati, 1973\n TRICK — “XX–368–South Africa–106–Keshavananda”\n💡\nChapter ka master spine isi line mein yaad karo.\nK.C. Wheare = rigidity aur flexibility ka fine balance.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmendment power wide hai, but Basic Structure destroy nahi ki ja sakti.\n2. Amendment Bill — Kahan, Kaun, Kya Nahi\n• Bill can be introduced in either House of Parliament\n• Can be introduced by any minister or private member\n• Prior President approval NOT required\n• President's veto NOT available after 24th Amendment, 1971\n• Joint Sitting NOT available\n• State Legislature cannot introduce Amendment Bill\n• States only ratify when required\n TRICK — “Either House + Any Member; No Prior Approval, No Veto, No Joint”\n💡\nAmendment Bill ka negative pack: NO prior President approval, NO veto, NO joint sitting.\nState ka role = ratification only.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n24th Amendment ke baad President must assent; veto nahi.\n3. Standard Procedure — I-P-S-A\n• I = Introduce in either House\n• P = Pass by Special Majority in each House separately\n• S = States ratify if required — minimum 1/2 State Legislatures\n• A = Assent by President is mandatory\n TRICK — “I-P-S-A = Introduce, Pass, States, Assent”\n💡\nProcedure ko four-step chain mein yaad karo.\nJoint Sitting absent — dono Houses separately pass karte hain."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.21 Constitutional Amendment\n4. Special Majority — Double Condition\n• 2/3 of members present & voting\n• AND majority of total membership of the House\n• Both conditions must be satisfied simultaneously\n TRICK — “2/3 P&V + 50%+ Total”\n💡\nSpecial Majority = double-lock.\nSirf 2/3 present & voting enough nahi; total membership majority bhi chahiye.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSpecial Majority ki dono conditions simultaneously meet honi chahiye.\n5. 3 Types of Majority — Simple / Special / Special+States\nSimple Majority\n• Entry & formation of new States\n• Legislative Council formation/abolition\n• MP salaries/allowances\n• Grant/removal of citizenship\n• 5th & 6th Schedules\n• Source notes: these changes are outside Article 368\n TRICK — “State–Council–Salary–Citizenship–5/6”\n💡\nSimple category ko S-C-S-C-5/6 se yaad karo.\nMost important trap: Simple Majority changes Art.368 ke under constitutional amendments ke roop mein count nahi hote.\nSpecial Majority\n• Fundamental Rights\n• DPSPs\n• All provisions not in Category 1 or 3\n• Example in source notes = 103rd Amendment, EWS 10%\n• Most Constitutional amendments fall here\n TRICK — “FR + DPSP + Most Others = Special”\n💡\nJab neither simple nor federal-state category ho, default memory = Special Majority.\nSpecial Majority + State Ratification\n• Presidential Election & Procedure\n• Centre-State executive power\n• Supreme Court & High Courts\n• GST\n• 7th Schedule subjects\n• Representation of States in Parliament\n• Minimum ratification = half of State Legislatures\n TRICK — “President–Federal–Courts–GST–7th–State Representation”\n💡\nFederal nature ke provisions ko State Ratification se jodo.\nSource notes current arithmetic: 28 States\n minimum 14 ratifications.\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nState ratification = minimum 50% State Legislatures."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.21 Constitutional Amendment\n6. Old Important Amendments — 1, 7, 15, 24, 26, 36, 40\n• 1st (1951)\n 9th Schedule; land reform laws\n→\n• 7th (1956)\n State Reorganization\n→\n• 15th (1963)\n HC retirement age 60 to 62\n→\n• 24th (1971)\n President must assent to Amendment Bill; no veto\n→\n• 26th (1971)\n Privy Purses abolished\n→\n• 36th (1975)\n Sikkim full State, 22nd State\n→\n• 40th (1976)\n Article 297 amended; Exclusive Economic Zone\n→\n TRICK — “1-9th, 7-States, 15-HC62, 24-NoVeto, 26-Purse, 36-Sikkim, 40-EEZ”\n💡\nNumber ko keyword se jodo; full sentence ratne ki zaroorat nahi.\n7. 42nd vs 44th — Opposite Direction Pair\n• 42nd Amendment, 1976 = 'Mini Constitution'\n• Added Socialist, Secular, Integrity in Preamble\n• Fundamental Duties added — Part IV-A\n• President bound by Cabinet advice\n• Source notes: Emergency duration 6 months to 1 year\n• 44th Amendment, 1978\n Right to Property removed from FR; became Legal Right\n→\n• Articles 20 & 21 protected\n• 'Armed Rebellion' replaced 'Internal Disturbance'\n• President can return Cabinet advice once; after resubmission binding\n TRICK — “42 Adds, 44 Repairs/Protects”\n💡\n42 = add/expand changes.\n44 = rollback/protection type changes in source notes.\nCore pair: 42 SSI + Duties | 44 Property Legal + 20/21 + Armed Rebellion.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n42nd = Mini Constitution; 44th ko uske kuch changes reverse/protect karne wale amendment ke roop mein yaad rakho.\n8. 61–88 Amendment Ladder\n• 61st (1989)\n Voting age 21 to 18\n→\n• 69th (1991)\n Delhi = NCT; Vidhan Sabha 70 seats; CoM max 10% / 7\n→\n• 73rd (1992)\n Panchayati Raj constitutional status; 11th Schedule, 29 subjects\n→\n• 74th (1992)\n Municipalities constitutional status; 12th Schedule, 18 subjects\n→\n• 86th (2002)\n Article 21A, free education 6–14 + new Fundamental Duty\n→\n• 88th (2003)\n Service Tax\n→\n TRICK — “61 Vote18, 69 Delhi, 73 Panchayat, 74 Municipality, 86 Education, 88 Service Tax”\n💡\nYe ladder direct exam recall ke liye enough hai.\n9. Recent Amendments 100–106 — Straight Chain\n• 100th (2015)\n Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement\n→\n• 101st (2016)\n GST; Articles 246A, 269A, 279A\n→\n• 102nd (2018)\n Constitutional status to NCBC\n→\n• 103rd (2019)\n 10% EWS reservation\n→\n• 104th (2020)\n Anglo-Indian reserved seats abolished\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.21 Constitutional Amendment\n• 105th (2021)\n States empowered to identify OBCs for own list\n→\n• 106th (2023)\n 1/3 women reservation in Lok Sabha & State Assemblies; Nari Shakti Vandan Act\n→\n TRICK — “100 Land, 101 GST, 102 NCBC, 103 EWS, 104 Anglo, 105 OBC, 106 Women”\n💡\n100 se 106 tak har number ko ek single keyword se lock karo.\n TRICK — “101–103–106 = GST–EWS–Women”\n💡\nRecent trio most asked in source notes: 101 GST, 103 EWS 10%, 106 Women 1/3.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSource notes: 106th women reservation effective after next delimitation (2026+).\n10. Basic Structure — Keshavananda 1973\n• Supremacy of Constitution\n• Democratic & Republican form\n• Secular character\n• Separation of Powers\n• Judicial Review\n• Article 32 / Writ Jurisdiction\n• Federalism\n• Unity & Integrity\n TRICK — “S-D-S-S-J-A-F-U”\n💡\nSupremacy\n Democracy\n Secular\n Separation\n Judicial Review\n Art.32\n Federalism\n Unity.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nBasic Structure = amendment-proof core.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBasic Structure ko destroy karne wala amendment valid nahi.\n11. Important Acts — 54, 56/05, 61, 71\n• 1954\n Special Marriage Act\n inter-faith civil marriage\n→\n→\n• 1956 Hindu Succession Act; 2005 amendment gave daughters equal HUF property rights\n• 1961\n Dowry Prohibition Act\n→\n• 1971\n Prevention of Insults to National Honour Act\n Flag/Anthem disrespect penalized\n→\n→\n• Source notes connect National Honour Act with Article 51A(a)\n TRICK — “54 Marriage, 56/05 Daughter, 61 Dowry, 71 Honour”\n💡\nAct-year memory chain: Marriage\n Succession\n Dowry\n National Honour.\n→\n→\n→\n12. Scholars — Wheare vs Austin\n• K.C. Wheare\n 'fine balance between rigidity & flexibility'\n→\n• Granville Austin\n amendment procedure = most accepted & diverse part of Constitution\n→\n TRICK — “Wheare = Balance, Austin = Accepted & Diverse”\n💡\nScholar-name ko keyword se jodo.\n13. Flexibility vs Rigidity\n• Flexible side\n many provisions by Simple Majority\n→\n• Flexible side\n no separate constituent body needed\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.21 Constitutional Amendment\n• Source notes\n 106 amendments in 75 years\n→\n• Rigid side\n Basic Structure cannot be amended\n→\n• Rigid side\n Special Majority for most changes\n→\n• Rigid side\n State ratification for federal provisions\n→\n TRICK — “Flexible = Simple/No Separate Body; Rigid = Special/States/Basic”\n💡\nExam comparison ko 2-column picture mein yaad karo.\n14. 20-Second Flash Recall\n• Part XX | Art.368 | South Africa | 106\n• No prior President approval | No veto | No Joint Sitting\n• Special Majority = 2/3 present & voting + majority of total membership\n• 3 categories = Simple / Special / Special + States\n• 24th = no veto | 42nd = Mini Constitution | 44th = Property legal + 20/21\n• 61st = vote18 | 73rd = Panchayat | 74th = Municipality | 86th = Education\n• 101 GST | 103 EWS | 106 Women\n• Keshavananda 1973 = Basic Structure\n TRICK — “368–NoVeto–NoJoint–2/3+Total–42/44–101/103/106–Basic”\n💡\nExam se pehle isi chain ko 2 baar bolna.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Part XX Art368, source South Africa, 106 amendments, rigid+flexible\n Bill either House by minister/private member; no\n→\nprior President approval, no veto after 24th/1971, no Joint Sitting, States ratify only\n procedure I-P-S-A\n Special majority =\n→\n→\n2/3 present&voting + majority total\n 3 types: Simple outside368; Special most; Special+States federal provisions, minimum\n→\nhalf States\n old anchors 1-9th,7-StateReorg,15-HC62,24-NoVeto,26-PrivyPurse,36-Sikkim,40-EEZ\n 42 Mini Constitution: SSI +\n→\n→\n\nDuties; 44 Property Legal + 20/21 + Armed Rebellion\n 61 Vote18,69 Delhi,73 Panchayat,74 Municipality,86 Education,88\n→\nServiceTax\n 100 Land,101 GST,102 NCBC,103 EWS,104 Anglo,105 OBC,106 Women\n Keshavananda1973 protects Basic\n→\n→\nStructure; scholars Wheare-Balance, Austin-Accepted&Diverse.”\n Top 3:\n⚠\nAmendment Bill = no President veto + no Joint Sitting | Special Majority = 2/3 present & voting + majority of total\nmembership | 42nd = Mini Constitution vs 44th = key rollback/protection amendment."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\nCONSTITUTIONAL & NON-CONSTITUTIONAL BODIES —\nMEMORY TRICK SHEET\nIndian Polity · Chapter 22 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — Constitutional, Statutory aur Non-Statutory bodies ke Article/Act, tenure, appointment-removal,\nchairperson traps aur high-yield comparisons ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. 3 Categories — Constitution / Act / Resolution\n• Constitutional Bodies\n Constitution mein mentioned; powers Constitution se\n→\n• Statutory Bodies\n Act of Parliament se created\n→\n• Non-Constitutional & Non-Statutory\n Cabinet Resolution / Executive decision\n→\n• Constitutional examples\n ECI 324, UPSC 315, CAG 148, AG 76, NCSC/NCST/NCBC 338/338A/338B, GST Council 279A,\n→\nLinguistic Minorities 350B\n• Statutory examples\n NHRC 1993, CIC RTI 2005, CVC Act 2003, Lokpal Act 2013, NCW Act 1990, CBI under DSPE Act\n→\n1946\n• NITI Aayog\n Non-Constitutional + Non-Statutory\n→\n TRICK — “Constitution = Article, Statutory = Act, NITI = Resolution”\n💡\nBody type identify karne ka fastest rule.\nNITI vs Lokpal vs NHRC: NITI non-statutory; Lokpal statutory; NHRC statutory.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNITI Aayog ko statutory body mat mark karna.\n2. Election Commission — 324–329, 25 Jan, 3 Members\n• ECI = Part XV, Articles 324–329\n• Established = 25 Jan 1950\n• 3 members = 1 CEC + 2 ECs\n• Quasi-judicial body\n• Single-member till 16 Oct 1989; multi-member from 1 Oct 1993\n• 1st CEC = Sukumar Sen\n• National Voters' Day = 25 January since 2011\n• Tenure = 6 years or 65 years, whichever earlier\n TRICK — “324–329 | 25 Jan | 1+2 | 6/65”\n💡\nECI number pack ko ek line mein yaad karo.\nAppointment + Removal\n• Appointed by President\n• Source notes' 2023 committee = PM + LoP (LS) + Union Cabinet Minister nominated by PM\n• CEC removal = like Supreme Court Judge, Special Majority\n• Other ECs removal = on CEC recommendation\n• Resignation = President\n TRICK — “CEC Hard, EC Easy”\n💡\nCEC removal = SC Judge level.\nOther EC removal = CEC recommendation.\n TRICK — “ECI = Parliament/State Legislature + President/VP; SEC = Panchayat/Municipality”\n💡\nPanchayat/Municipality elections State Election Commission Art.243K ke under."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nECI local-body elections conduct nahi karta.\n3. Electoral Reform Committees — 74, 90, 98\n• Tarkunde Committee\n 1974\n→\n• Dinesh Goswami Committee\n 1990\n→\n• Indrajit Gupta Committee\n 1998\n→\n TRICK — “T-D-I = 74–90–98”\n💡\nTarkunde\n Dinesh\n Indrajit; years increasing order.\n→\n→\n4. UPSC vs SPSC — 315–323, 6/65 vs 6/62\n• UPSC = Part XIV, Articles 315–323\n• Established 1926; recommended by Lee Commission\n• UPSC tenure = 6 years / 65 age\n• SPSC tenure = 6 years / 62 age\n• UPSC appointment = President; SPSC appointment = Governor\n• UPSC removal = President after SC inquiry\n• SPSC removal = President; Governor only suspends\n• UPSC salary = CF of India; SPSC salary = CF of State\n• UPSC report = President; SPSC report = Governor\n• Second term = not eligible for both\n TRICK — “UPSC 65, SPSC 62; Appoint P/G, Remove P/P”\n💡\nAppointment differs: President vs Governor.\nRemoval same final authority: President.\n TRICK — “UPSC Chairman = No Govt Job; SPSC Chairman = UPSC/other SPSC possible”\n💡\nPost-retirement difference direct exam trap hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSPSC Chairman ko Governor remove nahi karta — President removes.\n5. Civil Services Hooks — 1926 / Cornwallis / Tagore / 21 April\n• UPSC established = 1926, Lee Commission\n• Father of Civil Services = Lord Cornwallis\n• 1st Indian ICS = Satyendra Nath Tagore\n• Source notes: 1st Civil Services Exam = London & Allahabad, 1922\n• Civil Services Day = 21 April\n• All India Services only 3 in source notes = IAS, IPS, Indian Forest Service\n• Article 312 gives Parliament power to create All India Services\n TRICK — “Cornwallis–Tagore–21 April; AIS = IAS–IPS–Forest”\n💡\nIFS (Foreign) ko All India Service nahi mark karna.\n6. CAG — 148, 6/65, No Reappointment\n• CAG = Article 148\n• Tenure = 6 years / 65 years\n• Appointed by President"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n• Guardian of public finances\n• Audits Union + State expenditure/revenue and Consolidated Fund expenditure\n• Removal = like SC Judge, Special Majority\n• No reappointment after retirement\n• 1st CAG = V. Narahari Rao (1948)\n• PAC examines CAG reports; source notes say PAC chairman = Opposition Leader\n TRICK — “148–6/65–SC Removal–NO Return”\n💡\nCAG ka four-hook pack.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCAG reappointment = NO.\n7. Attorney General — 76 + 89 = 165\n• AG = Article 76, Part V\n• Chief Legal Advisor / 1st Law Officer of India\n• Qualification = eligible to be Supreme Court Judge\n• Appointed by President\n• Can speak in Parliament but cannot vote\n• Private legal practice not barred in source notes\n• 1st AG = M.C. Setalvad\n TRICK — “AG = Speak YES, Vote NO, Practice YES”\n💡\nAG ko Judge ke saath confuse mat karo.\n TRICK — “76 + 89 = 165”\n💡\nAttorney General Art.76\n Advocate General Art.165.\n→\nAG qualification SC Judge-level; Advocate General HC Judge-level.\n8. GST Council — 279A, 101st, Finance Minister\n• GST Council = Article 279A\n• Created by 101st Amendment, 2016\n• Constituted by President\n• Chairman = Union Finance Minister\n• Members include Union MoS Finance + State Finance Minister/nominee\n• Vice-Chairman elected among themselves\n TRICK — “279A–101–FM”\n💡\nGST Council ka straight 3-point code.\n TRICK — “GST = FM; Inter-State Council = PM; NITI = PM”\n💡\nChairperson confusion isi contrast se solve karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGST Council Chairman PM nahi, Union Finance Minister hai.\n9. NCSC–NCST–NCBC — 338 / 338A / 338B\n• NCSC = Art.338\n 65th Amendment, 1990\n→\n• NCST = Art.338A\n 89th Amendment, 2003; effective 2004\n→\n• NCBC = Art.338B\n 102nd Amendment, 2018\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n• NCSC & NCST originally combined; 89th Amendment bifurcated them\n• NCBC earlier Statutory (1993); constitutional status in 2018\n• All 3\n Chairperson + VP + 3 members\n→\n• All appointed by President; tenure = 3 years\n TRICK — “338–338A–338B = SC–ST–BC”\n💡\nBase article 338; A = Tribe, B = Backward Classes.\n TRICK — “65–89–102”\n💡\nNCSC 65th\n NCST 89th\n NCBC 102nd.\n→\n→\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTeen bodies ke amendment numbers alag-alag hain.\n10. Linguistic Minorities — 350B, 7th Amendment\n• Article 350B\n• 7th Constitutional Amendment, 1956\n• Special Officer for Linguistic Minorities\n• One-membered body\n• Appointed by President\n• Works under Union Ministry of Minority Affairs\n• HQ = New Delhi\n TRICK — “350B = Bhasha Officer, One Member”\n💡\nB ko Bhasha se yaad karo.\n11. NHRC — Statutory 1993, 3/70, Former CJI\n• NHRC = Statutory\n• Human Rights Protection Act, 1993\n• Established 12 Oct 1993; source notes also mention in effect 28 Sep 1993\n• 12 members = Chairperson + 11\n• Tenure = 3 years / 70 years\n• Chairperson must be former CJI\n• 1st Chairperson = Ranganath Misra\n• International Human Rights Day = 10 December\n TRICK — “NHRC = 1993–12 Members–3/70–Former CJI–10 Dec”\n💡\nNHRC ka high-yield number pack.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNHRC max age 70; CAG/UPSC 65. Human Rights Day 10 Dec, not 12 Oct.\n12. CIC — RTI 2005, 12 Oct, 3/65\n• CIC = Statutory; RTI Act 2005\n• RTI effective = 12 Oct 2005\n• 1 CIC + up to 10 Information Commissioners\n• Tenure = 3 years / 65 age\n• Appointed by President; resignation to President\n• Union level = CIC; State Information Commission = appointed by Governor"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n TRICK — “CIC = RTI–12 Oct 2005–3/65”\n💡\nDate + tenure ko ek line mein lock karo.\n13. CVC vs CBI — Same Santhanam, Different Job\n• CVC established 1964; K. Santhanam Committee\n• CVC statutory status = CVC Act 2003; Central Agency 2004\n• CVC tenure = 4 years / 65 age\n• CVC composition = 1 Chairman + up to 2 Vigilance Commissioners\n• CVC selection = PM + LoP + Union Home Minister\n• CBI founded 1963; recommended by K. Santhanam Committee\n• CBI governed by DSPE Act, 1946\n• CBI motto = Industry, Impartiality, Integrity\n• CBI under Ministry of Personnel, Pension & Public Grievances\n• CBI Director recommendation committee headed by PM\n TRICK — “Santhanam Twins: CVC Supervises, CBI Investigates”\n💡\nSame committee, different role.\n TRICK — “CVC = PM+LoP+Home; CEC = PM+LoP+Cabinet Minister”\n💡\nLoP common; third member different.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCVC committee mein Home Minister; CEC committee source notes mein nominated Cabinet Minister.\n14. NCW + NCM — 7 Members Each\n• NCW Act 1990; established Jan 1992\n• NCW = 7 members: Chairperson + 5 Members + Member Secretary\n• NCW appointed by Central Government; Chairperson term 3 years\n• 1st NCW Chairperson = Jayanti Patnaik\n• NCM established 1978 by Central Government resolution\n• NCM statutory status = Commission for Minorities Act, 1992\n• NCM = 7 members: Chairperson + VP + 5\n• 6 minorities in source notes = Jain, Buddhist, Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Parsi\n TRICK — “NCW 1990/92 + 7; NCM 1978/92 + 7”\n💡\nDono 7-member bodies; years alag.\n TRICK — “J-B-M-S-C-P = 6 Minorities”\n💡\nJain, Buddhist, Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Parsi.\n15. Lokpal — 2013, 5/70, 1+8, 50–50\n• Lokpal = Statutory; Lokpal & Lokayuktas Act, 2013\n• Tenure = 5 years / 70 age\n• 1 Chairperson + up to 8 members\n• At least 50% from SC/ST/OBC/Minority/Women\n• 50% from Judicial background\n• Appointed by President\n• Covers Group A, B, C, D officers\n• Lokpal Centre; Lokayuktas States"," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n• 1st Lokpal India = Pinaki Chandra Ghose, 2019\n• 1st Lokayukta India = Maharashtra, 1971\n• Source notes: PM inquiry requires 7/8 full-bench approval; some subjects excluded\n TRICK — “Lokpal = 2013–5/70–1+8–50/50”\n💡\nTenure + composition + reservation/background ka one-line pack.\n TRICK — “PM = Included, but Restricted”\n💡\nSource notes: 7/8 approval; International Peace, External Affairs, Atomic Energy excluded.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLokpal PM ko completely exclude nahi karta; source notes mein conditional coverage hai.\n16. NITI Aayog — 1 Jan 2015, PM, Non-Statutory\n• Full name = National Institution for Transforming India\n• Established = 1 Jan 2015\n• Replaced Planning Commission (1950)\n• Nature = Non-Constitutional + Non-Statutory; Cabinet Resolution\n• Chairperson = Prime Minister ex-officio\n• 1st Vice-Chairperson = Arvind Panagariya\n• Source notes list current VC = Suman Bery; CEO = B.V.R. Subrahmanyam\n• Planning Commission also non-statutory in source notes\n• Planning Commission had binding allocations; NITI role advisory\n TRICK — “NITI = 2015–PM–Resolution–Advisory”\n💡\nNo Article, no Act — Cabinet Resolution.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNITI Aayog non-constitutional AND non-statutory.\n17. Tenure/Age Super-Comparison\n• ECI CEC\n 6 years / 65\n→\n• UPSC\n 6 / 65\n→\n• SPSC\n 6 / 62\n→\n• CAG\n 6 / 65\n→\n• NCSC/NCST/NCBC\n 3 years\n→\n• NHRC\n 3 / 70\n→\n• CIC\n 3 / 65\n→\n• CVC\n 4 / 65\n→\n• Lokpal\n 5 / 70\n→\n• NCW Chairperson\n 3 years\n→\n TRICK — “6/65 Club = ECI–UPSC–CAG; 70 Club = NHRC–Lokpal”\n💡\nSPSC outlier = 6/62.\nCVC = 4/65; CIC = 3/65.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n70-year bodies in source comparison = NHRC and Lokpal."," ExamFusion Prep · Indian Polity Memory Tricks · Ch.22 Constitutional & Non-Constitutional Bodies\n18. Appointment/Removal Super-Comparison\n• CEC\n President appoints; removal like SC Judge\n→\n• Other ECs\n removal on CEC recommendation\n→\n• UPSC\n President appoints/removes after SC inquiry\n→\n• SPSC\n Governor appoints; President removes; Governor suspends\n→\n• CAG\n President appoints; removal like SC Judge\n→\n• AG\n President; at President's pleasure\n→\n• NHRC/CIC/CVC/Lokpal\n source comparison lists President appointment\n→\n• NCW\n Central Government\n→\n• NITI VC\n source comparison lists PM / at PM's pleasure\n→\n TRICK — “Governor Appoints SPSC, President Removes SPSC”\n💡\nSabse common appointment-removal mismatch.\n19. Major Political Parties — Year Chain from Source Notes\n• INC\n 1885\n→\n• CPI(M)\n 1964\n→\n• BJP\n 1980\n→\n• BSP\n 1984, Kanshi Ram\n→\n• AAP\n 2012, Arvind Kejriwal\n→\n• NPP\n 2013, P.A. Sangma; source notes say national-party recognition in 2019\n→\n TRICK — “1885–64–80–84–12–13”\n💡\nINC\n CPI(M)\n BJP\n BSP\n AAP\n NPP.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n20. 20-Second Article/Act Flash Chain\n• ECI 324 | UPSC 315 | CAG 148 | AG 76\n• NCSC 338 | NCST 338A | NCBC 338B\n• GST 279A | Linguistic Minorities 350B\n• NHRC 1993 | CIC RTI 2005 | CVC Act 2003 | CBI DSPE 1946\n• NCW Act 1990 | Lokpal Act 2013 | NITI = Cabinet Resolution\n TRICK — “324–315–148–76 / 338-A-B / 279A–350B / Acts 93–05–03–46–90–13 / NITI Resolution”\n💡\nArticle-body mapping aur Act-body mapping ko alag blocks mein revise karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n“Types: Constitution-Article, Statutory-Act, NITI-Resolution\n ECI 324-329, 25Jan, 1+2, 6/65; CEC SC-judge removal, EC on CEC;\n→\nECI not local polls\n UPSC/SPSC 315-323: 6/65 vs 6/62, appoint P/G but remove P/P; UPSC Chairman no govt job\n CAG148 6/65\n→\n→\nSC-removal no reappointment\n AG76 speak/no-vote/private practice; +89=AdvG165\n GST279A/101st/FM\n 338/338A/338B =\n→\n→\n→\n\nNCSC/NCST/NCBC with 65/89/102 amendments\n 350B linguistic one-member\n NHRC1993 3/70 former CJI, Human Rights\n→\n→\nDay10Dec\n CIC RTI2005 12Oct 3/65\n CVC1964/Act2003 PM-LoP-Home vs CBI1963 DSPE1946, both Santhanam\n\n→\n→\n→\nNCW1990/92 7; NCM1978/92 7 + 6 minorities\n Lokpal2013 5/70 1+8 50/50, PM conditional\n NITI1Jan2015 PM non-\n→\n→\nconstitutional/non-statutory advisory\n 6/65 club ECI-UPSC-CAG; 70 club NHRC-Lokpal.”\n→\n Top 5:\n⚠\nNITI = non-statutory | SPSC removal = President | CAG no reappointment | GST Council Chair = Finance Minister |\nNHRC & Lokpal age = 70."]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0445","t":"01 Biology Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / Science / Biology","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Introduction to Biology & the Living World\nINTRODUCTION TO BIOLOGY & THE LIVING WORLD —\nMEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke coined-by vs father, branches, taxonomy, five kingdoms, Monera, symbiosis,\nvirus–viroid–prion aur biological names ko exam-recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Biology Basics — Coined vs Father\n• Biology = study of living organisms\n• Greek roots: Bios = Life; Logos = Study\n• Term “Biology” coined by Lamarck & Treviranus\n• Father of Biology = Aristotle\nTRICK - “Lamarck + Treviranus TERM; Aristotle FATHER”\nCoined-by aur Father ko ek hi person mat samjho.\nBios + Logos = Life + Study.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBiology term = Lamarck & Treviranus; Father of Biology = Aristotle.\n2. Three Core Branches — B-Z-M\n• Botany\n Plants\n Theophrastus\n→\n→\n• Zoology\n Animals\n Aristotle\n→\n→\n• Microbiology\n Microbes\n Antonie van Leeuwenhoek\n→\n→\nTRICK - “B-Z-M = Botany–Zoology–Microbiology”\nFather chain: Theophrastus – Aristotle – Leeuwenhoek.\nVisual hook: Plant\n Animal\n Microbe.\n→\n→\n3. Sub-Branches — Person-to-Topic Anchors\nBranch / Source Association\nStudy\nEndocrinology — Thomas Addison\nHormones / Endocrine system\nImmunology — Edward Jenner\nImmunity\nGenetics — Gregor Mendel\nHeredity & variation\nCytology — Robert Hooke\nCells\nEugenics — Francis Galton\nHuman generations\nTaxonomy — Carolus Linnaeus\nIdentify / Name / Classify\nPaleontology — George Cuvier\nFossils\nEmbryology — Panchanan Maheshwari\nGametes, fertilisation, embryo\nAgronomy — Pietro de Crescenzi\nCrop production & soil\nAgrostology — Johann Scheuchzer\nGrasses\nAnthology\nFlowers\nSerpentology — Patrick Russell\nSnakes\nProtozoology — A. van Leeuwenhoek\nProtozoa\nTRICK - “Addison–Jenner–Mendel–Hooke–Galton–Cuvier”\nHormone = Addison | Immunity = Jenner | Genetics = Mendel | Cell = Hooke | Eugenics = Galton | Fossil = Cuvier.\nGrass = Agrostology; Snake = Serpentology; Protozoa = Protozoology."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Introduction to Biology & the Living World\n4. Taxonomy — Coined vs Father + Binomial Rules\n• Term “Taxonomy” coined by Augustin Pyramus de Candolle\n• Father of Taxonomy = Carolus Linnaeus\n• Taxonomy = Identifying + Naming + Classifying organisms\n• Binomial Nomenclature introduced by Carolus Linnaeus; source references Systema Naturae\n• Scientific name = Genus + Species\n• Genus first letter capital; species small; scientific name italicized\n• Example: Homo sapiens\n Homo = Genus; sapiens = Species\n→\nTRICK - “de Candolle COINED; Linnaeus FATHER + BINOMIAL”\nTaxonomy ka classic 3-way split: coined by de Candolle, father Linnaeus, binomial also Linnaeus.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGenus Capital + species small + whole scientific name italics.\n5. Taxonomic Hierarchy — K-P-C-O-F-G-S\n• Kingdom\n Phylum (Animals) / Division (Plants)\n Class\n Order\n Family\n Genus\n Species\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nTRICK - “King Philip Came Over For Good Soup”\nK = Kingdom, P = Phylum, C = Class, O = Order, F = Family, G = Genus, S = Species.\nEXAM TRAP - “Herbarium = Dry + Press”\nPlants herbarium mein drying & pressing se preserve kiye jaate hain.\n6. Five Kingdom Classification — Whittaker 1969\n• Proposed by Robert Whittaker in 1969\n• Criteria = Cell Structure + Body Organisation + Nutrition + Reproduction + Phylogenetic Relationship\n• Five kingdoms = Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia\nTRICK - “C-B-N-R-P” Criteria\nCell\n Body\n Nutrition\n Reproduction\n Phylogeny.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nTRICK - “M-P-F-P-A” Five Kingdoms\nMonera\n Protista\n Fungi\n Plantae\n Animalia.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nFeature\nMonera\nProtista\nFungi\nPlantae\nAnimalia\nCell\nProkaryotic\nEukaryotic\nEukaryotic\nEukaryotic\nEukaryotic\nWall\nPeptidoglycan\nFew present\nChitin\nCellulose\nAbsent\nNucleus membrane\nAbsent\nPresent\nPresent\nPresent\nPresent\nNutrition\nAuto/Hetero\nAuto/Hetero\nHeterotroph\nAutotroph\nHeterotroph\nTRICK - “Only MONERA = Prokaryotic”\nNuclear membrane absent only in Monera among the five kingdoms.\nWall material: Monera Peptidoglycan | Fungi Chitin | Plantae Cellulose | Animalia None.\nEXAM TRAP -\nFungi wall = Chitin, NOT cellulose. Animalia = no cell wall."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Introduction to Biology & the Living World\n7. Monera Groups — M-H-T / Cyanobacteria / Mycoplasma\n• Methanogens\n methane producing\n Methanobacterium\n→\n→\n• Halophiles\n saline conditions\n Halococcus\n→\n→\n• Thermoacidophiles\n hot sulphur springs\n Sulfolobus\n→\n→\n• Cyanobacteria\n nitrogen fixing, blue-green autotrophic bacteria\n Nostoc, Anabaena\n→\n→\n• Nostoc & Anabaena fix atmospheric N2 through Heterocysts\n• Mycoplasma\n no cell wall; parasitic or saprophytic\n→\nTRICK - “M-H-T = Methane–Salt–Hot Acid”\nMethanogen = Methane; Halophile = Salt; Thermoacidophile = Hot acidic/sulphur.\nNostoc + Anabaena = Heterocyst = N2 fixation.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMycoplasma = no cell wall.\n8. Symbiosis — Lichen vs Mycorrhiza\n• Lichen = Fungi + Algae\n• Fungi absorbs water/minerals; algae photosynthesizes\n• Lichen = pioneer on bare rocks + SO2 air-pollution indicator + litmus dye source\n• Mycorrhiza = Fungi + roots of higher plants\n• Fungi helps mineral absorption (especially phosphorus) and protection; plant provides shelter/nutrition\n• Examples in source = Pinus and Orchids\nTRICK - “Lichen = F + A; Mycorrhiza = F + Root”\nLichen extras: Rock pioneer + SO2 indicator + Litmus.\nMycorrhiza extras: Phosphorus absorption + Pinus/Orchid.\n9. Virus vs Viroid vs Prion — Composition First\nType\nDiscovery / Key Name\nComposition\nDisease / Note\nVirus\nIvanowsky; TMV crystallized by\nStanley\nDNA or RNA + protein capsid\nObligate parasite; living/non-\nliving link\nViroid\nT.O. Diener\nRNA only; no protein coat\nStunt disease in Chrysanthemum\nPrion\nStanley B. Prusiner\nProtein only; no nucleic acid\nScrapie; CJD; Kuru\nTRICK - “V = Nucleic Acid + Coat | Viroid = RNA | Prion = Protein”\nComposition se teenon ko pehle separate karo.\nTMV: Ivanowsky = discovery; Stanley = crystallization.\nEXAM TRAP -\nViroid = RNA only; Prion = protein only; Virus = nucleic acid + capsid."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Introduction to Biology & the Living World\n10. Biological Names — Animal Memory Clusters\nCommon Name\nBiological Name\nCommon Name\nBiological Name\nPeacock\nPavo cristatus\nFrog\nRana tigrina\nCat\nFelis catus\nDog\nCanis lupus familiaris\nCow\nBos taurus\nBuffalo\nBubalus bubalis\nGoat\nCapra aegagrus hircus\nTiger\nPanthera tigris\nLion\nPanthera leo\nLeopard\nPanthera pardus\nBear\nUrsus thibetanus\nRabbit\nOryctolagus cuniculus\nElephant\nElephas maximus indicus\nDolphin\nPlatanista gangetica\nTRICK - “Panthera Trio = Tiger–Lion–Leopard”\nTiger = Panthera tigris | Lion = Panthera leo | Leopard = Panthera pardus.\nSame genus Panthera; species changes.\n11. Biological Names — Plant Memory Clusters\nCommon Name\nBiological Name\nCommon Name\nBiological Name\nCarrot weed\nParthenium hysterophorus\nPea\nPisum sativum\nMustard\nBrassica campestris\nFig\nFicus carica\nTomato\nSolanum lycopersicum\nRice\nOryza sativa\nBanyan\nFicus benghalensis\nSugarcane\nSaccharum officinarum\nOnion\nAllium cepa\nAsafoetida (Hing)\nFerula asafoetida\nCotton\nGossypium\nCoffee\nCoffea arabica\nTea\nCamellia sinensis\nTurmeric (Haldi)\nCurcuma longa\nTRICK - “R-W-P-T = Oryza–Triticum–Solanum–Camellia”\nRice = Oryza sativa | Wheat = Triticum aestivum | Potato = Solanum tuberosum | Tea = Camellia sinensis.\nSame-genus plant pair in listed names: Fig/Banyan = Ficus; Tomato/Potato = Solanum.\n12. Five Taxonomic Example Anchors\nOrganism\nFamily\nOrder\nClass\nPhylum / Division\nHuman — Homo sapiens\nHominidae\nPrimates\nMammalia\nChordata\nHouse Fly — Musca\ndomestica\nMuscidae\nDiptera\nInsecta\nArthropoda\nMango — Mangifera\nindica\nAnacardiaceae\nSapindales\nDicotyledonae\nAngiospermae\nWheat — Triticum\naestivum\nPoaceae\nPoales\nMonocotyledonae\nAngiospermae\nPotato — Solanum\ntuberosum\nSolanaceae\nSolanales\nDicotyledonae\nAngiospermae\nTRICK - “Human–Fly–Mango–Wheat–Potato”\nAnimal examples: Human Chordata; House Fly Arthropoda.\nPlant examples: Mango/Wheat/Potato = Angiospermae."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Introduction to Biology & the Living World\n13. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Biology term: Lamarck & Treviranus ≠ Father Aristotle\n• Taxonomy term: de Candolle ≠ Father Linnaeus\n• Genus Capital; species small; scientific name italics\n• Herbarium = drying & pressing\n• Fungi wall Chitin | Plants Cellulose | Animalia no wall | Monera Peptidoglycan\n• Only prokaryotic kingdom = Monera\n• Lichen = Fungi + Algae; SO2 indicator\n• Virus = capsid+nucleic acid | Viroid = RNA only | Prion = protein only\n• TMV: Ivanowsky discovery vs Stanley crystallization\n• Panthera genus: tigris / leo / pardus\nEXAM TRAP - “Coined-vs-Father | Wall | RNA/Protein | Same Genus”\nChapter ke maximum MCQ traps inhi four families se bante hain.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\nBiology Bios+Logos; Lamarck/Treviranus term, Aristotle father -> B-Z-M: Theophrastus-Aristotle-Leeuwenhoek -> Addison hormone,\nJenner immunity, Mendel genetics, Hooke cell, Galton eugenics, Cuvier fossil -> Taxonomy de Candolle coined / Linnaeus\nfather+binomial; KPCOFGS -> Whittaker1969: C-B-N-R-P, M-P-F-P-A; Monera only prokaryotic; walls\nPeptidoglycan/Chitin/Cellulose/None -> M-H-T + Heterocyst + Mycoplasma no wall -> Lichen F+A/SO2; Mycorrhiza F+root/P -> Virus\nnucleic acid+capsid / Viroid RNA / Prion protein; Ivanowsky discovery vs Stanley crystal -> Panthera trio; Rice Oryza, Wheat\nTriticum, Potato Solanum, Tea Camellia.\nTOP 5: Biology term vs father | Taxonomy coined vs father | Monera only prokaryotic | Fungi=Chitin | Viroid RNA vs Prion\nProtein."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\nPLANT KINGDOM — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke plant features, Cryptogam/Phanerogam split, Algae, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta,\nGymnosperm, Angiosperm aur Monocot-Dicot facts ko exam-recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Plant Basics — S-C-P\n• Plants = eukaryotic + multicellular + sessile\n• Nutrition mainly photosynthetic autotrophic\n• Cell wall = Cellulosic\n• Plastids present\nTRICK - “S-C-P = Sessile - Cellulose - Plastids”\nSource chapter ke 3 highlighted plant features: Sessile + Cellulosic wall + Plastids.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes ke comparison mein animals mein ye 3 highlighted features absent hain.\n2. Big Split — Cryptogam vs Phanerogam\nGroup\nSeeds\nReproductive Organ\nMain Groups\nCryptogams\nAbsent\nHidden / inconspicuous\nThallophyta, Bryophyta,\nPteridophyta\nPhanerogams\nPresent\nCone or flower\nGymnosperm, Angiosperm\nTRICK - “Crypto = Hidden + No Seed; Phanero = Visible + Seed”\nCryptogams reproduce by spores.\nPhanerogams ke seeds present hote hain.\nTRICK - “T-B-P / G-A”\nCryptogam trio = Thallophyta-Bryophyta-Pteridophyta.\nPhanerogam pair = Gymnosperm-Angiosperm.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGymnosperm = naked seed; Angiosperm = ovary/fruit covered seed.\n3. Five Plant Groups — Generation + Vascular Memory\nGroup\nSeed\nVascular\nTrue Root/Stem/Leaf\nDominant\nThallophyta\nNo\nNo\nNo\nGametophyte\nBryophyta\nNo\nNo\nNo; rhizoids\nGametophyte\nPteridophyta\nNo\nYes\nYes\nSporophyte\nGymnosperm\nNaked\nYes\nYes\nSporophyte\nAngiosperm\nCovered\nYes\nYes\nSporophyte\nTRICK - “T-B = Gameto; P-G-A = Sporo”\nThallophyta + Bryophyta = Gametophyte dominant.\nPteridophyta + Gymnosperm + Angiosperm = Sporophyte dominant.\nTRICK - “Vascular starts at P”\nThallophyta/Bryophyta = no vascular tissue.\nPteridophyta se Xylem + Phloem present."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\n4. Algae Basics — Thallus, Pectin-Cellulose, Pyrenoid, Holdfast\n• Thallophyta/Algae body = undifferentiated thallus\n• Vascular + mechanical tissues absent\n• Mostly aquatic; gametophyte dominant\n• Green algae wall = Outer Pectin + Inner Cellulose\n• Green algae starch bodies = Pyrenoids in chloroplast\n• Laminaria attaches to rocks by Holdfast\nTRICK - “P-C-P-H”\nPectin outer\n Cellulose inner\n Pyrenoid starch\n Holdfast attachment.\n→\n→\n→\n5. Algal Products — A-C-A + C-S\nProduct / Role\nSource\nAlgin\nBrown algae\nCarrageenan\nRed algae\nAgar\nGelidium + Gracilaria (Red)\nProtein / Space Food\nChlorella + Spirulina\nFood\nPorphyra + Sargassum\nTRICK - “Algin Brown; Carrageenan Red; Agar G-G Red”\nAgar = Gelidium + Gracilaria.\nProtein/space food = Chlorella + Spirulina.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAlgin aur Carrageenan dono hydrocolloids hain, but source algae color different hai.\n6. Green-Brown-Red Algae — Pigment + Food\nType\nKey Pigment\nStored Food\nExamples\nGreen\nChl-a,b\nStarch\nChlamydomonas, Volvox,\nSpirogyra\nBrown\nFucoxanthin + Chl-a,c\nMannitol + Laminarin\nFucus, Ectocarpus, Sargassum,\nLaminaria\nRed\nPhycoerythrin + Chl-a,d\nFloridean starch\nPolysiphonia, Porphyra,\nGracilaria\nTRICK - “Brown = FUCO + MANNI-LAMI”\nBrown algae unique pigment = Fucoxanthin.\nStored food = Mannitol + Laminarin.\nTRICK - “Red = PHYCO + FLORIDEAN”\nRed algae unique pigment = Phycoerythrin.\nStored food = Floridean starch.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSpirogyra = freshwater filamentous GREEN algae."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\n7. Bryophyta — Amphibian + Rhizoid + Gametophyte\n• Wet/moist habitat\n• True root, stem, leaves absent; rhizoids present\n• Vascular tissue absent\n• Gametophyte dominant; sporophyte depends on gametophyte\n• Called Amphibians of Plant Kingdom\n• Sexual reproduction = Oogamous\nTRICK - “B = Bheega + Bina Vascular + Big Gametophyte”\nBryophyta ko wet habitat, absent vascular tissue aur gametophyte dominance se lock karo.\nType\nExamples / Memory\nLiverworts\nMarchantia, Riccia\nMosses\nFunaria = Cord Moss; Sphagnum = Bog Moss\nTRICK - “Marchantia Liver; Funaria Cord; Sphagnum Bog”\nSource notes Sphagnum ko peat moss/fuel history se bhi link karte hain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBryophyta vascular absent; Pteridophyta vascular present.\n8. Pteridophyta — Vascular Cryptogam\n• Source notes call them “Botanical Snakes of Plant Kingdom (Completely Terrestrial)”\n• First land plants with vascular tissue\n• Damp and shady places\n• True root, stem, leaves present\n• Xylem + Phloem present\n• Seeds absent\n• Water necessary for sexual reproduction\n• Sporophyte dominant\n• Male gametes formed in Antheridium\n• Examples = Selaginella, Pteris, Equisetum, Psilotum\nTRICK - “Pteri = Plant body Proper + Pipes Present, but Seed absent”\nProper root/stem/leaf + vascular pipes = Pteridophyta.\nStill cryptogam, so seeds absent.\nEXAM TRAP - “Equisetum = Only Living Sphenopsida”\nSource marks this as a direct MCQ fact."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\n9. Gymnosperm — Naked Seed Pack\n• Gymno = naked; Sperma = seed\n• Seeds naked; ovary, fruit and true flower absent\n• Sporophyte dominant\n• Root, stem and needle-like leaves present\n• Reproductive organ = unisexual cone\n• Endosperm = Haploid (n)\n• Companion cells of phloem and xylem vessels absent\n• Evergreen woody trees/shrubs\n• Examples = Cycas, Pinus, Ginkgo, Gnetum\nTRICK - “GYM = Naked - No Ovary - No Fruit - Cone - n Endosperm”\nFruit absent because ovary absent.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGymnosperm endosperm = Haploid (n), Angiosperm = Triploid (3n).\n10. Angiosperm — D-T-3n\n• Well-developed flowers + covered seeds\n• Fruit/ovary present; seeds/ovules inside\n• Double fertilisation present\n• Triple Fusion present\n• Endosperm = Triploid (3n)\n• Divided into Monocot and Dicot\nTRICK - “D-T-3 = Double fertilisation - Triple fusion - 3n”\nSource chapter ki highlighted Angiosperm uniqueness.\n11. Gymnosperm vs Angiosperm — Fast Contrast\nFeature\nGymnosperm\nAngiosperm\nSeed\nNaked\nCovered\nFlower\nAbsent\nPresent\nFruit\nAbsent\nPresent\nEndosperm\nHaploid (n)\nTriploid (3n)\nDouble fertilisation\nAbsent\nPresent\nCompanion cells\nAbsent\nPresent\nTRICK - “Gym = No Flower/Fruit/Double; Angio = All Present”\nEndosperm contrast: n vs 3n."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\n12. Monocot vs Dicot — 1-3-P-F vs 2-4/5-R-T\nFeature\nMonocot\nDicot\nCotyledon\n1\n2\nRoot\nFibrous / Adventitious\nTap root\nVascular bundles\nScattered\nRing\nLeaf venation\nParallel\nReticulate\nFlower\nMultiples of 3\nMultiples of 4 or 5\nTRICK - “MONO = 1 - 3x - Parallel - Fibrous”\nOne cotyledon, flower multiples of 3, parallel venation, fibrous roots.\nTRICK - “DI = 2 - 4/5x - Reticulate - Tap”\nTwo cotyledons, flower multiples of 4/5, reticulate venation, tap root.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMonocot vascular bundles scattered; Dicot arranged in ring.\n13. Crop Examples — Monocot vs Dicot\nMonocot Examples\nDicot Examples\nCorn / Maize\nRose\nWheat\nChickpea / Chana\nPearl Millet / Bajra\nTomato\nRice, Bamboo, Sugarcane\nMustard, Pea, Bean\nBanana, Onion\nMango, Apple, Potato\nTRICK - “W-C-R = Wheat-Corn-Rice = Monocot”\nRose-Tomato-Mustard = Dicot high-yield examples."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Plant Kingdom\n14. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Cryptogam = seed absent; Phanerogam = seed present\n• Gymnosperm = naked seed/no ovary-fruit; Angiosperm = covered seed\n• Thallophyta + Bryophyta = Gametophyte dominant; Pteridophyta + seed plants = Sporophyte dominant\n• Algin Brown; Carrageenan Red; Agar Gelidium + Gracilaria\n• Fucoxanthin Brown; Phycoerythrin Red\n• Bryophyta vascular absent; Pteridophyta vascular present\n• Equisetum = only living representative of Sphenopsida\n• Gymnosperm endosperm n; Angiosperm endosperm 3n\n• Angiosperm = Double fertilisation + Triple fusion + 3n endosperm\n• Monocot = 1/Fibrous/Parallel/3; Dicot = 2/Tap/Reticulate/4-or-5\nEXAM TRAP - “Seed - Generation - Pigment - Vascular - Endosperm - Cotyledon”\nChapter ke maximum confusion points in 6 families se bante hain.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Plants SCP = Sessile-Cellulose-Plastids\n Crypto T-B-P no seed vs Phanero G-A seed\n T-B Gametophyte, P-G-A Sporophyte; vascular\n→\n→\nstarts at P\n Algae P-C-P-H = Pectin/Cellulose-Pyrenoid-Holdfast; products Algin Brown, Carrageenan Red, Agar G-G, Chlorella-\n→\nSpirulina protein\n Green Starch; Brown Fucoxanthin + Mannitol/Laminarin; Red Phycoerythrin + Floridean\n Bryophyta\n→\n→\namphibian, rhizoid, no vascular, gametophyte; Marchantia liver, Funaria cord, Sphagnum bog\n Pteridophyta first vascular land\n→\nplant, true R-S-L, seed absent, sporophyte; Equisetum Sphenopsida\n Gymnosperm naked/no ovary-fruit/cone/n endosperm\n\n→\n→\nAngiosperm covered/flower-fruit/D-T-3n\n Monocot 1-3-Parallel-Fibrous-Scattered; Dicot 2-4/5-Reticulate-Tap-Ring; Wheat-Corn-Rice\n→\n\nmono, Rose-Tomato-Mustard dicot.”\nTOP 5: Crypto vs Phanero | T-B Gameto vs P-G-A Sporo | Brown Fucoxanthin vs Red Phycoerythrin | Gym n vs Angio 3n | Mono\n1/3/Parallel vs Dicot 2/4-5/Reticulate."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\nANIMAL WORLD — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke Non-Chordata, Chordata, Vertebrata, fishes, tetrapods, excretory organs,\nexamples/scientific names aur class-wise comparison ko exam recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Animal Basics — E-M-H-M\n• Animals = Eukaryotic + Multicellular + Heterotrophic + generally Motile\n• Cell wall absent\n• Plastids absent\nTRICK - “E-M-H-M = Eukaryotic - Multicellular - Heterotrophic - Motile”\nPlant contrast from source: animal cell mein cellulosic wall aur plastids absent.\n2. Big Split — Notochord Absent vs Present\nDivision\nCore Cue\nMajor Groups\nNon-Chordata\nNotochord absent\nPorifera to Hemichordata\nChordata\nNotochord present at some life stage\nUrochordata, Cephalochordata, Vertebrata\nTRICK - “NO Noto = Non-Chordata; Noto = Chordata”\nChordata ke hallmark 3 = dorsal notochord + dorsal hollow nerve cord + pharyngeal gill slits.\nTRICK - “Herdmania + Amphioxus = Protochordates”\nHerdmania = Urochordata; Amphioxus = Cephalochordata.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHemichordata ko source notes connecting link between Non-chordates and Chordates batate hain.\n3. Non-Chordata Order — 10 Phyla\n• I Porifera\n• II Cnidaria\n• III Ctenophora\n• IV Platyhelminthes\n• V Aschelminthes / Nematoda\n• VI Annelida\n• VII Arthropoda\n• VIII Mollusca\n• IX Echinodermata\n• X Hemichordata\nTRICK - “Po-Cni-Cte-Pla-As-An-Ar-Mo-Ec-He”\n10 phyla ko sound-chain mein bolo; order yaad rahega.\nSize trap: Arthropoda largest, Mollusca second largest.\n4. Porifera - Cnidaria - Ctenophora\nPhylum\nStandout Feature\nExamples\nPorifera\nChoanocytes + canal system + high\nregeneration\nSpongilla, Euspongia, Sycon\nCnidaria\nCnidocytes/Cnidoblasts; Polyp vs Medusa\nHydra, Physalia, Adamsia, Pennatula\nCtenophora\nBioluminescence + 8 comb rows\nCtenoplana"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\nTRICK - “P-C-C = Collar - Cnidocyte - Comb”\nPorifera = Collar cells.\nCnidaria = Cnidocytes.\nCtenophora = 8 Comb rows + light.\nTRICK - “Polyp Sits, Medusa Floats”\nPolyp = sessile; Medusa = free-floating.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPhysalia = Portuguese man-of-war; Spongilla = freshwater sponge.\n5. Flat - Round - Segmented Worms\nGroup\nBody/Coelom\nExcretion\nExamples\nPlatyhelminthes\nFlat; acoelomate\nFlame cells\nTaenia, Fasciola, Planaria\nAschelminthes\nRound; pseudocoelomate\nRenette cells\nAscaris, Wuchereria,\nAncylostoma\nAnnelida\nSegmented; true coelom\nNephridia\nNereis, Pheretima, Hirudinaria\nTRICK - “Flat-Flame, Round-Renette, Ring-Nephridia”\nBody form ko excretory organ ke saath pair karo.\nTRICK - “Taenia Tapeworm; Wuchereria Filarial; Pheretima Earthworm”\nHigh-yield example identity chain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHirudinaria = blood-sucking leech; source notes 33 segments highlight karte hain.\n6. Excretion Super-Chain — F-R-N-M-B-P\nPhylum\nExcretory Structure\nPlatyhelminthes\nFlame cells\nAschelminthes\nRenette cells\nAnnelida\nNephridia\nArthropoda\nMalpighian tubules\nMollusca\nBojanus organs\nHemichordata\nProboscis gland\nEXAM TRAP - “F-R-N-M-B-P”\nFlame\n Renette\n Nephridia\n Malpighian\n Bojanus\n Proboscis.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nYe chapter ka sabse important mix-up chain hai.\n7. Arthropoda — Largest Phylum\n• Largest animal phylum; source notes: about two-thirds species are insects\n• Chitinous exoskeleton + open circulatory system\n• Body commonly head + thorax + abdomen\n• Respiration via gills/book gills/book lungs/trachea\n• Statocysts maintain body balance\n• Excretion = Malpighian tubules"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\nExample\nScientific Name / Note\nHoney bee\nApis indica\nSilkworm\nBombyx mori\nLac insect\nLaccifera lacca\nMosquito vectors\nAnopheles, Culex, Aedes\nLiving fossil\nLimulus - King Crab\nOther\nShrimp, Scorpion, Locusta\nTRICK - “A-B-L = Apis-Bombyx-Laccifera”\nHoney bee = Apis indica; Silkworm = Bombyx mori; Lac insect = Laccifera lacca.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLimulus = King Crab = living fossil.\n8. Mollusca - Echinodermata - Hemichordata\nGroup\nMemory Cue\nExamples\nMollusca\n2nd largest; CaCO3 shell; Ctenidia; Radula;\nBojanus\nPila, Pinctada, Sepia, Octopus\nEchinodermata\nWater vascular system + tube feet; brain\nabsent\nAsterias, Echinus, Cucumaria, Ophiura\nHemichordata\nProboscis + Collar + Trunk; connecting link\nBalanoglossus, Saccoglossus\nTRICK - “Mollusc = C-R-B”\nCtenidia = respiration, Radula = grinding, Bojanus = excretion.\nTRICK - “Echino = Water + Tube Feet + Aristotle”\nSea urchin food grinder = Aristotle’s lantern.\nTRICK - “Hemi = P-C-T + Proboscis Gland”\nBody = Proboscis-Collar-Trunk; excretion = Proboscis gland.\n9. Vertebrata Tree — Jawless to Tetrapods\nBranch\nGroup\nCue\nAgnatha\nCyclostomata\nJawless; sucker-like circular mouth\nGnathostomata\nPisces + Tetrapoda\nJaws present\nPisces\nChondrichthyes + Osteichthyes\nFins\nTetrapoda\nAmphibia + Reptilia + Aves + Mammalia\nFour limbs / two pairs\nTRICK - “A-G = Jawless-Jawed”\nAgnatha = jawless; Gnathostomata = jawed.\nTRICK - “Cyclo examples P-M”\nPetromyzon = Lamprey; Myxine = Hag fish."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\n10. Fish — Chondrichthyes vs Osteichthyes\nFeature\nChondrichthyes\nOsteichthyes\nSkeleton\nCartilage\nBone\nGill slits\n5-7 pairs\n4 pairs\nOperculum\nAbsent\nPresent\nAir bladder\nAbsent\nPresent\nHeart\n2 chambered\n2 chambered\nTemperature\nCold\nCold\nTRICK - “Chondro = Cartilage + Cover NO + Air NO”\nOperculum absent + air bladder absent = source ka direct trap.\nTRICK - “Osteo = Bone + Both Present”\nOperculum present + air bladder present.\nFish / Example\nSpecial Identity\nTorpedo\nElectric organ\nTrygon\nPoison sting\nScoliodon\nDog fish\nPristis\nSawfish\nCarcharodon\nWhite shark\nExocoetus\nFlying fish\nHippocampus\nSea horse\nLabeo\nRohu\nClarias\nWalking catfish\nBetta splendens\nFighting fish\nTRICK - “T-T = Torpedo Electric, Trygon Poison”\nExocoetus flies; Hippocampus horse; Clarias walks.\n11. Tetrapoda Quick Comparison\nClass\nHeart\nTemp.\nSpecial\nAmphibia\n3\nCold\nWater+land; mucous skin;\ntadpole\nReptilia\n3 (Croc 4)\nCold\nDry keratin scales; CaCO3 egg\nAves\n4\nWarm\nFeathers; hollow bones;\ntoothless beak\nMammalia\n4\nWarm\nMammary glands + diaphragm;\nmostly viviparous\nTRICK - “3-3-4-4 / Cold-Cold-Warm-Warm”\nAmphibia-Reptilia = 3 chambered, cold.\nAves-Mammalia = 4 chambered, warm.\nEXAM TRAP -\nReptiles generally 3-chambered, but Crocodile = 4-chambered."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\n12. Amphibia + Reptilia Examples\nClass\nExamples\nAmphibia\nRana tigrina Frog; Bufo Toad; Hyla Tree frog; Ichthyophis\nBlindworm; Proteus\nReptilia\nNaja naja Cobra; Typhlops Blind snake; Lizard; Chameleon; Tortoise;\nDinosaur extinct reptile\nTRICK - “R-B-H-I-P”\nAmphibia: Rana-Bufo-Hyla-Ichthyophis-Proteus.\nTRICK - “Naja = Cobra; Typhlops = Blind Snake”\nScientific/common-name direct pair.\n13. Aves — EOPKC Flightless Chain\n• 4-chambered heart + warm-blooded\n• Dry skin with feathers\n• Eggs with CaCO3 covering\n• Forelimbs = wings; jaws = toothless beak\n• Hind limbs covered with scales\n• Bones hollow/pneumatic\nTRICK - “EOPKC = Emu - Ostrich - Penguin - Kiwi - Cassowary”\nSource ka ready-made flightless birds mnemonic.\nOstrich = world’s largest bird.\nBird\nScientific Name\nParrot\nPsittacula\nPeacock\nPavo cristatus\nPigeon\nColumba\n14. Mammalia — Mammary + Diaphragm + Monotreme\n• 4-chambered heart + warm-blooded\n• Hair/fur generally present\n• Mammary glands = unique highlighted feature\n• Diaphragm present\n• Mostly viviparous\n• Horns, hoofs, nails as exoskeletal structures\nTRICK - “Mammal = Milk + Diaphragm + Mostly Live Birth”\nMammary gland aur diaphragm ko mammal signature pair banao.\nEXAM TRAP - “P-E = Platypus-Echidna = Egg-laying Mammals”\nDono oviparous monotremes.\nMammal\nScientific Name\nHuman\nHomo sapiens\nBat\nPteropus\nKangaroo\nMacropus\nCamel\nCamelus"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Animal World\n15. Scientific/Common Name Rapid Bank\nName\nRemember As\nApis indica\nHoney bee\nBombyx mori\nSilkworm\nLaccifera lacca\nLac insect\nPila\nApple snail\nPinctada\nPearl oyster\nAsterias\nStarfish\nEchinus\nSea urchin\nPetromyzon\nLamprey\nExocoetus\nFlying fish\nHippocampus\nSea horse\nClarias\nWalking catfish\nRana tigrina\nFrog\nNaja naja\nCobra\nPavo cristatus\nPeacock\nHomo sapiens\nHuman\nTRICK - “Bee-Bombyx-Lac / Pila-Pearl / Asterias-Star / Naja-Cobra / Pavo-Peacock”\nName bank ko paired chunks mein revise karo.\n16. Final Exam Traps — One-Glance\n• Porifera = Choanocytes\n• Ctenophora = Bioluminescence + 8 comb rows\n• Platyhelminthes = Flame cells\n• Arthropoda largest; Mollusca second largest\n• Limulus = living fossil / King Crab\n• Hemichordata = connecting link; Balanoglossus common example\n• Chondrichthyes = no operculum + no air bladder; Osteichthyes = both present\n• Crocodile = reptile with 4-chambered heart\n• Flightless birds = EOPKC\n• Platypus + Echidna = oviparous mammals\nEXAM TRAP - “Cell - Light - Flame - Size - Fossil - Link - Fish - Croc - EOPKC - Monotreme”\nChapter ke 10 red-flag areas isi sequence mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Animal E-M-H-M, wall/plastid absent\n NonChordata no notochord vs Chordata N-N-G; Herdmania+Amphioxus protochordates\n\n→\n→\n10 phyla Po-Cni-Cte-Pla-As-An-Ar-Mo-Ec-He\n P-C-C = Collar/Cnidocyte/Comb; Flat-Flame, Round-Renette, Ring-Nephridia\n\n→\n→\nExcretion F-R-N-M-B-P\n Arthropoda largest/chitin/open/Malpighian; Limulus fossil; Apis-Bombyx-Laccifera\n Mollusc C-R-B, Echino\n→\n→\n\nwater/tube feet/Aristotle, Hemi P-C-T/proboscis gland/link\n Vertebrata: Agnatha Cyclo jawless vs Gnathostomata Pisces+Tetrapoda\n→\n Chondro cartilage/no operculum/no air vs Osteo bone/both present; Torpedo electric, Trygon poison, Exocoetus flying,\n→\nHippocampus sea horse, Clarias walking\n Tetrapods 3-3-4-4 and Cold-Cold-Warm-Warm; Croc4\n Aves EOPKC + hollow bones\n\n→\n→\n→\nMammal mammary+diaphragm; Platypus-Echidna oviparous.”\nTOP 5: F-R-N-M-B-P excretion | Arthropoda largest vs Mollusca second | Chondro no/no vs Osteo yes/yes | Crocodile heart 4 |\nPlatypus-Echidna oviparous mammals."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\nCELL — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke cell discovery, size records, prokaryote/eukaryote, plant/animal comparison, membrane\ntransport, organelles, plastids, cell cycle, mitosis-meiosis aur exam traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Discovery Timeline — H-L-SV\nScientist\nYear\nMemory Fact\nRobert Hooke\n1665\nDead cork cells; coined Cellula\nA. van Leeuwenhoek\n1674\nFirst living cells\nSchleiden & Schwann\n1838-39\nCell Theory\nRudolf Virchow\n1855\nNew cells from pre-existing cells\nTRICK - “Hooke Dead, Leeuwenhoek Live, S-S Theory, Virchow Old-to-New”\nOrder: 1665 > 1674 > 1838-39 > 1855.\nCellula = Hooke; Omnis cellula-e-cellula = Virchow.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHooke = dead cork; Leeuwenhoek = first living cells.\n2. Cell Records — O-M-N\n• Largest cell = Ostrich egg; source note 15 x 13 cm, about 1.4 kg\n• Smallest cell = Mycoplasma PPLO; 0.1 micrometre\n• Longest cell = Neuron; 90-100 cm\n• RBC = Biconcave; about 7.2 micrometre\nTRICK - “O-M-N = Ostrich - Mycoplasma - Neuron”\nLargest > Smallest > Longest ko alag records ki tarah yaad karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLargest cell aur longest cell same nahi.\n3. Prokaryote vs Eukaryote — 70/80 + Circle/Linear\nFeature\nProkaryote\nEukaryote\nSize\n0.1-5 micrometre\n10-100 micrometre\nNucleus\nNo true nucleus; nucleoid\nTrue nucleus\nOrganelles\nMembrane-bound absent\nPresent\nRibosome\n70S\n80S cytoplasm; 70S mito/plastid\nDNA\nOne naked circular; no histone\nMultiple linear; histone present\nRespiration\nMesosome - source note\nMitochondria\nTRICK - “Pro = 70 + Circle + No Histone; Eu = 80 + Linear + Histone”\nEukaryote exception: mitochondria/plastids ke ribosomes 70S.\nTRICK - “70 = 50+30; 80 = 60+40”\nRibosome subunit trap ko direct number pair se lock karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEukaryotic cytoplasm 80S, but mitochondria/plastids 70S."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\n4. Plant vs Animal — W-P-V-C\nFeature\nPlant\nAnimal\nCell wall\nPresent - cellulose\nAbsent\nPlastid\nPresent\nAbsent\nVacuole\nLarge central\nVery small/absent\nCentrosome\nAbsent\nPresent\nGolgi\nSmaller; Dictyosomes\nLarger\nMitochondria\nFewer\nMore\nTRICK - “Plant = Wall + Plastid + big Vacuole; Animal = Centrosome”\nPlant Golgi = Dictyosomes.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCentrosome animal; plastid and cell wall plant.\n5. Membrane Transport — D-O-E-E\nProcess\nDirection / Requirement\nHook\nDiffusion\nHigh to Low; no energy\nGas > Liquid > Solid\nOsmosis\nWater across semipermeable membrane\nRoot water absorption\nEndocytosis\nInto cell; energy-dependent\nPhago solid / Pino liquid\nExocytosis\nOut of cell\nCell vomiting\nTRICK - “D-O-E-E = Diffuse - Osmose - Enter - Exit”\nEndocytosis enters; exocytosis exits.\nTRICK - “Phago = Food/Solid; Pino = Pani/Liquid”\nDono Endocytosis ke types.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPhagocytosis solid; Pinocytosis liquid.\n6. Osmosis — Hypo Swell, Iso Same, Hyper Shrink\nSolution\nCondition\nCell Effect\nHypotonic\nOutside concentration < cell\nSwells\nIsotonic\nEqual\nNo change\nHypertonic\nOutside concentration > cell\nShrinks\nTRICK - “HYPO = Hawa Bharo, HYPER = Hatao Pani”\nHypotonic swells; Hypertonic shrinks; Isotonic same.\n• Aquaporins = specialised water-channel proteins responding to osmotic gradient\n7. Cell Boundary + Protoplasm\n• Cell wall = plant only; cellulose; permeable and protective\n• Cell membrane = all cells; very thin, flexible, selectively permeable\n• Source composition = Protein 50% + Lipid 40% + Carbohydrate 10%\n• Protoplasm term coined by J.E. Purkinje, 1839; source notes discovery by Felix Dujardin\n• Huxley called protoplasm the physical basis of life\n• Cytoplasm = protoplasm excluding nucleus"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\n• Nucleoplasm = protoplasm inside nucleus\nTRICK - “50-40-10 = Protein-Lipid-Carb”\nCell membrane composition ka source-number pack.\nTRICK - “Purkinje Protoplasm; Huxley Physical Basis”\nCoiner aur quote ko pair mein yaad karo.\n8. Nucleus — Brown 1831, DNA+Histone, 23 Pairs\n• Nucleus discovered by Robert Brown, 1831\n• Control centre / brain of cell\n• Nuclear membrane = double membrane with pores\n• Nucleolus discovered by Fontana; synthesises r-RNA\n• Chromatin condenses into chromosomes during division\n• Chromosome = DNA + Histone; Gene = functional DNA segment\n• Human = 23 pairs = 22 autosome pairs + 1 sex-chromosome pair\n• Male XY; Female XX\n• Source notes: Safranin used for nucleus staining\nTRICK - “23 = 22 + 1; Male XY, Female XX”\nHuman chromosome pack.\nTRICK - “Brown Nucleus, Fontana Nucleolus”\nNucleus vs nucleolus discoverer trap.\nEXAM TRAP -\nNucleus largest organelle, but large plant vacuole can be exception in source notes.\n9. ER + Ribosome — Rough Protein, Smooth Lipid\n• ER discovered by Keith R. Porter, Albert Claude & Ernest Fullam, 1945\n• RER = ribosomes present; protein/enzyme synthesis\n• SER = ribosomes absent; lipid/steroid synthesis + detoxification\n• Ribosome discovered by G.E. Palade, 1953\n• Ribosome = membrane-less; protein synthesis\n• Polysome = chain of ribosomes attached to m-RNA\nTRICK - “Rough = Ribosome = Protein; Smooth = Steroid/Lipid”\nRER-P, SER-LS.\nTRICK - “Palade 1953 = Protein Factory”\nRibosome discoverer + function pair.\n10. Golgi — 1898 Post Office\n• Discovered by Camillo Golgi, 1898\n• Plant Golgi = Dictyosomes\n• Cis face = convex, toward nucleus\n• Trans face = concave, toward cell membrane\n• Secretion, storage, packaging, processing\n• Forms lysosomes and sperm acrosome\n• Zone of exclusion = cytoplasm around Golgi with no organelles"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\nTRICK - “Cis = Comes from nucleus; Trans = Travels to membrane”\nShape hook: Cis convex, Trans concave.\nTRICK - “Golgi Makes L-A”\nL = Lysosome; A = Acrosome.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGolgi = Post office / Traffic police of cell.\n11. Lysosome + Mitochondria — Suicide vs Power\nOrganelle\nDiscoverer / Year\nCore Memory\nLysosome\nChristian de Duve, 1955\nSuicidal bag; hydrolytic enzymes\nMitochondria\nAlbert von Kolliker, 1857\nPowerhouse; ATP; Cristae\n• Lysosome digests food, foreign particles, damaged organelles, bacteria, viruses and waste\n• Mitochondria = double membrane; inner folds = Cristae\n• ATP = Adenosine Triphosphate; energy currency\n• Mitochondria semi-autonomous: own circular naked DNA, RNA and 70S ribosomes\n• Source notes also link mitochondria with apoptosis\nTRICK - “De Duve Suicide 1955; Kolliker Power 1857”\nLysosome = digestion/self-digestion; Mito = ATP.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCristae = mitochondrial inner folds.\n12. Plastids — C-C-L + A-E-A\nPlastid\nPigment / Colour\nMain Role\nChloroplast\nGreen; chlorophyll\nPhotosynthesis - Kitchen\nChromoplast\nColour except green\nFruit/flower colours\nLeucoplast\nColourless\nStorage\nTRICK - “C-C-L = Chloroplast - Chromoplast - Leucoplast”\nGreen - Colour - Colourless.\nTRICK - “A-E-A = Amyloplast - Elaioplast - Aleuroplast”\nAmyloplast = starch; Elaioplast = oil; Aleuroplast = protein.\n• Source notes credit plastid discovery to Ernst Haeckel and Schimper\n• Plastids = double-membrane, semi-autonomous, plant cells only\nEXAM TRAP -\nChloroplast = Kitchen; Mitochondria = Powerhouse; Lysosome = Suicidal bag; Golgi = Post office.\n13. Vacuole + Centrosome + Peroxisome\n• Vacuole membrane = Tonoplast\n• Vacuole = storage house / dustbin\n• Plant vacuole may occupy 60-90% cell volume; helps turgidity\n• Animal vacuoles very small or absent\n• Centrosome forms poles during animal-cell division"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\n• Centrioles = 9 + 0 arrangement of triplet microtubules\n• Peroxisomes in liver detoxify H2O2 to H2O + O2\nTRICK - “Tono = Vacuole Top Cover”\nTonoplast = vacuole membrane.\nTRICK - “9+0 = Centriole; H2O2 = Peroxisome”\nTwo direct one-liner facts.\n14. Cell Cycle — G1-G0-S-G2-M\nPhase\nMemory Event\nG1\nGrowth; comparatively longest after division\nG0\nQuiescent / non-dividing\nS\nDNA + centrosome replication; histone synthesis\nG2\nPrepare for mitosis; proteins/organelles; DNA check\nM\nKaryokinesis + Cytokinesis\nTRICK - “Grow - Stop - Synthesize DNA - Get Ready - Multiply”\nG1 > G0 > S > G2 > M.\n• Plant-cell cytokinesis = Phragmoplast forms during new cell-wall construction\n15. Mitosis vs Meiosis — 2n Same vs n Half\nFeature\nMitosis\nMeiosis\nCells\nSomatic\nGerm\nDivisions\n1\n2\nChromosome\n2n to 2n\n2n to n\nProducts\n2 identical\n4 haploid, genetically different\nPurpose\nGrowth + repair\nGamete formation + variation\nTRICK - “MITO = Maintain Number; MEIO = Make Half”\nMitosis keeps chromosome number same.\nMeiosis halves it.\nTRICK - “P-M-A-T”\nKaryokinesis stages: Prophase > Metaphase > Anaphase > Telophase.\n• Walther Flemming discovered mitosis by studying chromosomes\n• Uncontrolled mitosis = Cancer\n• Source notes link Turner and Klinefelter syndromes with meiotic chromosome-segregation errors\n• Meiosis-I Prophase-I: Leptotene stage = chromosome condensation\nEXAM TRAP -\nMitosis = 2 identical; Meiosis = 4 haploid/different.\n16. Final Exam Traps — One-Glance\n• Hooke dead cork vs Leeuwenhoek first living cells\n• Largest Ostrich egg; smallest Mycoplasma PPLO; longest Neuron\n• 70S prokaryote + mito/plastid; 80S eukaryotic cytoplasm\n• Centrosome animal; plastid/cell wall plant\n• Phagocytosis solid; Pinocytosis liquid\n• Mito Powerhouse; Lysosome Suicidal; Golgi Post office; Chloroplast Kitchen"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Cell\n• Golgi forms lysosome + sperm acrosome\n• Plant vacuole 60-90%; membrane Tonoplast\n• Mitosis 2n to 2n; Meiosis 2n to n\n• Uncontrolled mitosis = Cancer\nEXAM TRAP - “Dead-Live / O-M-N / 70-80 / Plant-Animal / Phago-Pino / Organelle Nicknames / Division”\nChapter ke major red flags isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Hooke1665 dead Cellula > Leeuwenhoek1674 living > Schleiden-Schwann1838-39 theory > Virchow1855 old-to-new\n records O-M-\n→\nN = Ostrich-Mycoplasma-Neuron\n Pro 70/circular/no histone/mesosome vs Eu 80/linear/histone/mitochondria; mito-plastid 70S\n\n→\n→\nPlant wall+plastid+big vacuole vs Animal centrosome\n transport D-O-E-E; Hypo swell, Iso same, Hyper shrink; Phago solid/Pino\n→\nliquid\n membrane 50-40-10; Purkinje protoplasm/Huxley physical basis\n Brown nucleus1831, Fontana nucleolus, humans\n→\n→\n23=22+1 XY/XX\n RER protein, SER lipid-steroid; Palade ribosome1953\n Golgi1898 Post Office, Cis nucleus/Trans membrane, forms\n→\n→\nLysosome+Acrosome\n De Duve lysosome1955 suicide vs Kolliker mito1857 powerhouse/Cristae/ATP/own DNA-RNA-70S\n plastids\n→\n→\nC-C-L, leucoplast A-E-A; Tonoplast vacuole, centriole9+0, peroxisome H2O2\n cycle G1-G0-S-G2-M\n Mitosis 2n-2n/2 identical vs\n→\n→\nMeiosis 2n-n/4 haploid; PMAT; cancer = uncontrolled mitosis.”\nTOP 5: Hooke dead vs Leeuwenhoek living | 70S/80S exception | Phago solid vs Pino liquid | Golgi makes lysosome+acrosome |\nMitosis same vs Meiosis half."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\nTISSUE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke Plant + Animal tissues, Meristematic/Permanent tissue, Xylem-Phloem, Epidermis-Cork,\nEpithelium, Connective tissue, Muscle aur Nervous tissue ke high-confusion facts ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya\nhai.\n1. Tissue Basics — Cell > Tissue > Organ > System\n• Tissue = similar origin/basic structure wale cells ka group jo ek unit ki tarah function karta hai\n• Multicellular organisms mein tissues division of labour create karte hain\n• Organisation level = Cell > Tissue > Organ > Organ System > Animal\n• Plant tissues = Meristematic + Permanent\n• Animal tissues = Epithelial + Connective + Muscular + Nervous\nTRICK - “ECMN = Epithelial - Connective - Muscular - Nervous”\nAnimal tissue ke 4 types ka direct code.\n2. Meristematic Tissue — A-I-L\n• Immature/undifferentiated cells; continuously divide\n• No intercellular spaces, no vacuoles\n• Prominent nucleus + dense cytoplasm + thin cellulose wall\nMeristem\nLocation\nFunction\nApical\nShoot/root tips\nLength / elongation\nIntercalary\nLeaf base, nodes/internodes\nLength growth\nLateral\nSides of stem/root\nThickness / girth\nTRICK - “A-I-L = Apex Length, Inter-node Length, Lateral Girth”\nApical = tip; Intercalary = node/leaf base; Lateral = side.\nEXAM TRAP -\nProtoderm = apical meristem ka root-associated part, as stated in source notes.\nTRICK - “Cork = Secondary Meristem Product”\nSource notes cork ko secondary meristematic tissue batate hain; cork cells dead + suberin.\n3. Simple Permanent Tissue — P-C-S\nTissue\nLiving/Dead\nWall / Space\nMain Role\nParenchyma\nLiving\nThin wall; spaces present\nStorage\nCollenchyma\nLiving\nCorner thickening; spaces\nusually absent\nSupport + flexibility\nSclerenchyma\nDead\nThick lignified wall; spaces\nabsent\nStrength / safety\nTRICK - “P-C Live, S Dead”\nParenchyma + Collenchyma living; Sclerenchyma dead.\nEXAM TRAP - “Coconut Husk = Sclerenchyma”\nDirect source example."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\n4. Parenchyma Modifications — Chloro vs Aero\nModification\nFeature\nFunction\nChlorenchyma\nChloroplast present\nPhotosynthesis\nAerenchyma\nLarge air spaces\nBuoyancy in aquatic plants\nTRICK - “Chloro = Chlorophyll; Aero = Air”\nChlorenchyma photosynthesis; Aerenchyma floating.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAerenchyma = buoyancy, not photosynthesis.\n5. Complex Permanent Tissue — Xylem vs Phloem\nTissue\nTransport\nKey Components / Fact\nXylem\nUnidirectional water + minerals\nTracheids, vessels, xylem parenchyma,\nfibres\nPhloem\nBidirectional food\nFood-conducting complex tissue\nTRICK - “Xylem = X-it Upward; Phloem = Food Both Ways”\nSource note: Xylem unidirectional roots > stem > leaves.\nPhloem bidirectional food transport.\nEXAM TRAP -\nXylem parenchyma = living component of xylem.\n6. Protective Tissue — Epidermis + Cork\nFeature\nEpidermis\nCork\nNature\nOutermost single layer\nMultilayered dead cells\nSpecial\nCuticle may form waxy layer\nSuberin in walls\nIntercellular space\nNot highlighted\nAbsent\nExtra\nRoot hairs from root epidermis\nWaterproof protection\nTRICK - “Cork = Dead + Suberin + No Space = Waterproof”\nMechanical injury, infection aur water loss se protection.\nTRICK - “Root Hair = Epidermis Extension”\nWater absorption ke liye surface area badhata hai.\n7. Stomata — Dicot Bean, Monocot Dumbbell\n• Stomata = leaf epidermis ke small pores\n• Functions = transpiration + gaseous exchange\n• Water enters guard cells > turgid > stoma opens\n• Water exits > relaxed/shrunken > stoma closes\n• Dicot guard cells = bean-shaped\n• Monocot guard cells = dumbbell-shaped\nTRICK - “D-B / M-D = Dicot-Bean, Monocot-Dumbbell”\nGuard-cell shape ka direct exam pair."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\nEXAM TRAP -\nWater IN = Open; Water OUT = Close.\n8. Epithelial Tissue — SC3 + Stratified\nType\nLocation\nSimple squamous\nBlood vessels, alveoli, mouth, alimentary canal\nStratified squamous\nSkin\nCuboidal\nKidney tubules, sweat/salivary/thyroid glands\nColumnar\nStomach, intestine, gall bladder, bile duct\nCiliated columnar\nTrachea, oviduct, vas deferens\nGlandular single-cell\nGoblet cell\nTRICK - “SC3 = Squamous - Cuboidal - Columnar - Ciliated Columnar”\nSource quick-recall code for simple epithelial forms.\nEXAM TRAP - “Kidney = Cuboidal; Trachea = Ciliated; Skin = Stratified”\n3 highest-yield location traps.\n9. Tendon vs Ligament — M vs B\nTissue\nConnects\nFibre / Flexibility\nTendon\nBone to Muscle\nWhite collagen; strong, less flexible\nLigament\nBone to Bone\nYellow elastin; more flexible\nTRICK - “Tendon = To Muscle; Ligament = Links Bones”\nTendon B-M; Ligament B-B.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCollagen = Tendon; Elastin = Ligament.\n10. Blood & Lymph — 55/45 + RBC Journey\nComponent\nKey Fact\nPlasma\n55%; about 90% water, 8% protein, 2% minerals/ions\nRBC\nFormed bone marrow; destroyed spleen\nWBC\nNeutrophil, Eosinophil, Basophil, Lymphocyte, Monocyte\nPlatelets\nBlood clotting\nLymph\nColourless; RBC absent\nTRICK - “55 Plasma + 45 Cells”\nSource blood ratio.\nTRICK - “RBC: Bone Marrow Birth, Spleen Burial”\nSpleen = graveyard of RBC.\nTRICK - “N-E-B-L-M”\nWBC types: Neutrophil-Eosinophil-Basophil-Lymphocyte-Monocyte.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLymph = colourless + RBC absent."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\n11. Loose Connective — Adipose vs Areolar\nTissue\nWhere / Nature\nFunction\nAdipose\nBelow skin, around organs, bone marrow\nFat storage + insulation + shock absorption\nAreolar\nLoose jelly matrix; below skin / spaces / near\nmuscles-vessels\nRepair + filling spaces\nTRICK - “Adipose = Add Fat; Areolar = Area Fill”\nAdipose stores; Areolar repairs/fills.\n12. Bone vs Cartilage — Hard Salts vs Chondrin\nTissue\nMatrix / Nature\nHigh-Yield Facts\nBone\nHard/stiff; CaPO4 + CaCO3\nOsteoblasts = bone-forming;\nsupport/protection\nCartilage\nFlexible; chondrin + sugar + collagen +\nelastin\nJoints, nose tip, outer ear, trachea, throat\nTRICK - “Bone = CaPO4 + CaCO3; Cartilage = Chondrin”\nHard vs flexible ko matrix ke saath pair karo.\nTRICK - “Osteoblast = Builds Bone”\nStem cells source notes mein bone marrow mein present.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBone salt pair ko CaPO4 + CaCO3 se yaad rakho.\n13. Muscle — Striated / Smooth / Cardiac\nFeature\nStriated\nSmooth\nCardiac\nShape\nCylindrical\nSpindle\nBranched cylindrical\nNuclei\nMulti\nUni\nUni\nBands\nPresent\nAbsent\nPresent\nControl\nVoluntary\nInvoluntary\nInvoluntary\nFatigue\nFast\nSlow/resistant\nNo fatigue\nSpecial\nSkeleton attached\nInternal organs\nIntercalated discs\nTRICK - “Bands = Striated + Cardiac; Voluntary = Striated Only”\nSmooth no bands; Cardiac striated but involuntary.\nTRICK - “Cardiac = Branched + Intercalated + No Fatigue”\nHeart muscle ka signature trio.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCardiac striated hote hue bhi involuntary hai.\n14. Muscle Proteins — A-M\n• Muscle fibres = elongated contractile cells\n• Movement by contraction-relaxation\n• Contractile proteins = Actin + Myosin"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\nTRICK - “A-M = Actin + Myosin = Action of Muscle”\nMuscle movement ka direct protein pair.\n15. Nervous Tissue — Neuron + Neurilemma\n• Functions = sensitivity, excitability, coordination\n• Neuron = structural + functional unit\n• Neuron length source note = up to about 1 m\n• Neurons lack dividing capability\n• Locations = brain, spinal cord, nerves\n• Schwann cells = Neurilemma cells in source notes\nTRICK - “Neuron = Nerve Unit, No Division”\nNeuron structure/function unit + non-dividing.\nEXAM TRAP - “Schwann = Neurilemma”\nSource-specific terminology direct pair.\n16. Additional One-Liners\n• Eosine = luminous red acidic dye\n• Eosine stains cytoplasm, RBC, collagen and muscle fibres\n• Stem cells present in bone marrow\n• Cork cells are dead and contain suberin\n• Robert Hooke observed cork cells and coined “Cellula”\nTRICK - “Eosine = Red Acidic Dye”\nCytoplasm + RBC + collagen + muscle fibres ko stain karta hai.\n17. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Apical tips/length; Intercalary nodes-leaf base/length; Lateral sides/thickness\n• Parenchyma + Collenchyma living; Sclerenchyma dead\n• Aerenchyma buoyancy; Chlorenchyma photosynthesis\n• Xylem unidirectional water; Phloem bidirectional food\n• Dicot guard = bean; Monocot = dumbbell\n• Cork = dead + suberin + no intercellular space\n• Cuboidal kidney; Ciliated trachea/oviduct/vas deferens; Skin stratified squamous\n• Tendon bone-muscle/collagen; Ligament bone-bone/elastin\n• RBC formed marrow, destroyed spleen\n• Bone = CaPO4 + CaCO3; Cartilage = chondrin\n• Cardiac = striated + involuntary + branched + intercalated discs + no fatigue\n• Neuron does not divide; Schwann = Neurilemma\nEXAM TRAP - “A-I-L / P-C-S / Chloro-Aero / X-P / D-B-M-D / Cork / Epi / T-L / RBC / Bone / Cardiac / Neuron”\nChapter ke 12 most-confusable zones isi sequence mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Tissue\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Tissue = similar cells; Plant M+P, Animal ECMN\n Meristem A-I-L: Apical tip-length, Intercalary node-length, Lateral side-girth; no\n→\nvacuole/space\n Simple P-C-S = Parenchyma live/storage, Collenchyma live/flexible, Sclerenchyma dead/strength;\n→\nCoconut=Sclerenchyma; Chloro photosynthesis, Aero buoyancy\n Xylem one-way water, Phloem two-way food, xylem parenchyma\n→\nliving\n Epidermis + Cork; Cork dead+suberin+no space; Root hair epidermis\n Stomata: Dicot bean, Monocot dumbbell; water-in\n→\n→\nopen, water-out close\n Epithelial SC3; kidney cuboidal, trachea ciliated, skin stratified\n Tendon B-M collagen vs Ligament B-B\n→\n→\nelastin\n Blood 55 plasma/45 cells; RBC marrow birth-spleen burial; WBC N-E-B-L-M; lymph colourless/no RBC\n Adipose fat,\n→\n→\nAreolar fill; Bone CaPO4+CaCO3/Osteoblast vs Cartilage Chondrin\n Muscle Actin+Myosin; bands Striated+Cardiac, voluntary\n→\nStriated only; Cardiac branched/intercalated/no fatigue\n Neuron functional unit/no division; Schwann=Neurilemma; Eosine red\n→\nacidic dye.”\nTOP 5: A-I-L meristems | P-C living vs S dead | Xylem one-way vs Phloem two-way | Tendon B-M vs Ligament B-B | Cardiac striated\nbut involuntary."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nBIOLOGICAL PROCESS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 6 · Nutrition + Digestion + Respiration + Blood + Excretion + Plant Transport\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke high-memory facts, numbers, enzyme-location pairs, vitamin deficiencies, heart/blood\nexceptions, nephron path aur plant transport ko exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Life Processes — N-R-E-T\nProcess\nMeaning\nNutrition\nGetting nutrients from food\nRespiration\nEnergy release from food\nExcretion\nRemoval of metabolic wastes\nTransportation\nMoving substances in body\nTRICK - “N-R-E-T = Nutrition - Respiration - Excretion - Transport”\nBiological process chapter ka master four-process code.\n2. Plant Nutrition — Auto + Special Modes\n• Autotrophic nutrition = inorganic substances se organic food banana\n• Photosynthesis chlorophyll ki presence mein hota hai\n• Source equation: 6CO2 + 12H2O + sunlight > C6H12O6 + 6O2 + 6H2O\n• Plant macronutrients listed = C, H, O, N, P, K, Ca, Mg, S\n• Micronutrients listed = Fe, B, Zn, Mn, Cu, Mo, Cl\nTRICK - “Auto = Apna Food; Hetero = Har Baar Bahar”\nAutotroph khud food banata; heterotroph organic source par depend karta.\nSpecial Mode\nExamples / Hook\nInsectivorous\nNepenthes, Drosera, Venus flytrap - N deficient soil\nParasitic\nCuscuta - complete stem parasite; sucker roots\nSymbiotic\nLegume root nodules + Rhizobium - N fixing\nTRICK - “N-D-V / Cuscuta Sucker / Rhizobium Root-N”\nInsectivorous = Nepenthes-Drosera-Venus.\nCuscuta parasite; Rhizobium symbiotic N-fixer.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCuscuta = parasite; Rhizobium = symbiont, parasite nahi.\n3. Heterotrophic Modes — H-S-P\nMode\nProcess\nExamples\nHolozoic\nIngest > Digest > Absorb\nHuman, Amoeba, Goat, Lion\nSaprophytic\nDead/decayed matter ka extracellular\ndigestion\nRhizopus, Yeast, Penicillium\nParasitic\nHost ke inside/outside\nTicks, Lice, Leech, Tapeworm, pathogenic\nbacteria\nTRICK - “H-S-P = Holozoic - Saprophyte - Parasite”\nHolo = ingest; Sapro = dead matter; Para = host.\n4. Energy Values — 9.3 > 4.3 > 4.1\nNutrient\nEnergy / g\nHigh-Yield Fact\nFat\n9.3 Kcal\nHighest energy"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nProtein\n4.3 Kcal\nDeficiency: Marasmus + Kwashiorkor\nCarbohydrate\n4.1 Kcal\nC:H:O = 1:2:1\nTRICK - “F-P-C = 9.3 - 4.3 - 4.1”\nFat > Protein > Carbohydrate energy order.\nTRICK - “Protein kam = M-K”\nM = Marasmus; K = Kwashiorkor.\n• Term “Vitamin” coined by Casimir Funk\n• Body water in source notes = about 65-70%\n• Essential amino acids = His, Ile, Leu, Lys, Met, Phe, Thr, Trp, Val\nTRICK - “HILL-MPTTV”\nEssential amino acids mnemonic chunk: His-Ile-Leu-Lys / Met-Phe-Thr-Trp-Val.\n5. Vitamins — ADEK vs B+C\nTRICK - “ADEK = Fat Soluble; B+C = Water Soluble”\nSolubility ka biggest vitamin trap.\nVitamin\nChemical Name\nDeficiency / Effect\nA\nRetinol / beta-Carotene\nNight blindness, xerophthalmia\nD\nCalciferol\nRickets child; osteoporosis adult\nE\nTocopherol\nSterility/infertility; weak muscles\nK\nNaphthoquinone/Phylloquinone\nBleeding due to clot failure\nTRICK - “A-Night, D-Rickets, E-Sterility, K-Klotting”\nADEK ko deficiency/function se pair karo.\nVitamin\nName\nDeficiency\nB1\nThiamine\nBeri-Beri\nB2\nRiboflavin\nCheilosis\nB3\nNiacin\nPellagra - 3D\nB5\nPantothenic acid\nSkin/growth/hair/fertility effects\nB6\nPyridoxine\nAnaemia, skin disease, cramps\nB7\nBiotin\nSkin disease, hair loss\nB9\nFolic acid\nAnaemia, growth, neural-tube defects\nB12\nCobalamin\nAnaemia + nervous/RBC/DNA effects\nC\nAscorbic acid\nScurvy\nEXAM TRAP - “B1 Beri, B3 3D, C Scurvy, D Rickets, K Klotting”\nB3 Pellagra = Dermatitis + Diarrhoea + Dementia.\n6. Digestion Process — I-D-A-A-D\n• Ingestion > Digestion > Absorption > Assimilation > Defecation\n• Alimentary canal length in source notes = 8-10 m\nTRICK - “I-D-A-A-D”\nFood journey ka 5-step process.\nPart\nSource Length / pH\nCore Function\nPharynx\n12 cm\nFood-air common passage; epiglottis\nprotects trachea\nOesophagus\n22-24 cm\nPeristalsis\nStomach\n25 cm; pH 2.0\nProtein digestion + chyme"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nSmall intestine\n25 cm + 2.4 m + 3.5 m\nComplete digestion + microvilli absorption\nLarge intestine\nCaecum 6 cm + Colon 1.3 m + Rectum 12-15\ncm\nWater absorption + faeces\nTRICK - “Stomach 2; Small Complete; Large Water”\npH 2 stomach, complete digestion small intestine, water absorption large intestine.\n7. Teeth — 2-1-2-3 = 32\n• Adult dental formula per half jaw = 2 incisors, 1 canine, 2 premolars, 3 molars\n• Total adult teeth = 32\n• Child formula = 2,1,0,2\n• Wisdom tooth = third molar\n• Enamel = outer layer and hardest; Dentine = inner layer\nTRICK - “2-1-2-3 x 4 = 32”\nAdult formula ka direct arithmetic trick.\nTongue Zone - Source Note\nTaste\nFront\nSweet\nFront-side\nSalty\nSide\nSour\nBack\nBitter\n8. Digestive Enzymes — Mouth-Stomach-Pancreas-Intestine\nLocation\nKey Enzymes\nActs On\nMouth\nPtyalin / Amylase\nStarch\nStomach\nPepsin, Rennin, Gastric lipase\nProtein, milk protein, fat\nPancreas\nTrypsin, Chymotrypsin, Amylopsin,\nCarboxypeptidase, Lipase\nProtein/starch/polypeptide/fat\nIntestine\nEnterokinase, Erepsine, Maltase, Sucrase,\nLactase, Lipase, Nuclease\nFinal digestion targets\nTRICK - “Mouth A; Stomach P-R-L; Pancreas T-C-A-C-L”\nMouth = Amylase.\nStomach = Pepsin-Rennin-Lipase.\nPancreas = Trypsin-Chymotrypsin-Amylopsin-Carboxypeptidase-Lipase.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSalivary Ptyalin/Amylase acts on starch.\n9. Liver + Pancreas — Largest vs Second Largest\n• Liver = largest gland\n• Kupffer cells = macrophages\n• Bile emulsifies fat; source pH 7.4-8.5\n• Bile stored in gall bladder\n• Bile pigments = bilirubin + biliverdin\n• Liver functions include glycogenesis, detoxification, urea formation, storage of A,D,E,K\n• Pancreas = second largest gland; mixed gland; pancreatic juice\n• Salivary glands = 3 pairs\n• Source note states: Gall stones = Calcium oxalate\nTRICK - “Liver Largest; Pancreas 2nd + Mixed”\nLargest-vs-second-largest direct trap."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nTRICK - “B-B = Bilirubin + Biliverdin; Bile in Gall Bladder”\nPigments + storage ek saath yaad karo.\n10. Respiration — 36 vs 2 ATP\nFeature\nAerobic\nAnaerobic\nO2\nRequired\nNot required\nBreakdown\nComplete\nPartial\nEnergy\n36 ATP\n2 ATP\nLocation\nCytoplasm + mitochondria\nCytoplasm only\nProducts\nCO2 + H2O\nEthanol + CO2 in yeast\nExamples\nMost animals/plants\nYeast, bacteria, exercising human muscle\nTRICK - “AERO = Air + 36; ANAERO = Absent Air + 2”\nEnergy difference is the key exam number.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHuman muscles during exercise = anaerobic; yeast fermentation = anaerobic.\n11. Human Respiratory System — 3 Right, 2 Left\nPart\nHigh-Yield Fact\nNostrils\nMucus + hairs clean/moisten air\nPharynx\nCommon passage; epiglottis\nLarynx\nSound; Adam’s apple in men\nTrachea\n10-12 cm; C-shaped hyaline cartilage rings\nRight lung\nLarge/broad; 3 lobes + 3 bronchi\nLeft lung\nSmall/thin; 2 lobes + 2 bronchi\nAlveoli\nBalloon-shaped, single-layered; gas exchange\nTRICK - “Right 3, Left 2; Alveoli = Exchange”\nLung lobes ka direct pair.\nPhase\nO2\nCO2\nDiaphragm\nInspiration\n21%\n0.03%\nFlattens downward\nExhalation\n16%\n4.4%\nDome-shaped\nTRICK - “Inhale Flat; Exhale Dome”\nDiaphragm shape trick.\n12. Gas Transport — O2 97; CO2 70-23-7\n• O2 transport = 97% by haemoglobin\n• CO2 = 70% bicarbonate + 23% haemoglobin + 7% plasma\nTRICK - “O2 = 97 Hb; CO2 = 70-23-7”\nGas-transport number pack.\n13. Respiratory Surfaces — Membrane-Skin-Gill-Trachea-Lung\nOrganism\nSurface\nAmoeba & Planaria\nCell membrane\nEarthworm & Leech\nMoist skin\nFish, Prawns, Tadpole\nGills\nFrog\nMoist skin + lungs"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nMosquito & Housefly\nTrachea + spiracles\nBirds/Lizards/terrestrial animals\nLungs\nTRICK - “Amoeba Membrane, Worm Skin, Fish Gill, Insect Trachea, Land Lung”\nFrog exception = moist skin + lungs.\nEXAM TRAP -\nInsects = trachea + spiracles, not gills.\n14. Blood — 55/45, pH 7.3-7.5\n• Blood pH = 7.3-7.5, alkaline\n• Adult blood = 5-6 L, about 7-8% body weight\n• Plasma = 55%; cells = 45%\nTRICK - “Blood = 55 Liquid + 45 Cells”\nPlasma-cell composition split.\nCell\nCount / Lifespan\nFormation / Role\nRBC\n4.5-5 million/mm3; 120 days\nBone marrow after birth; gas transport\nWBC\n6,000-8,000/mm3; hours-months\nImmunity\nPlatelets\n1.5-3.5 lakh/mm3; 8-10 days\nMegakaryocytes; clotting\nTRICK - “RBC 120; Platelet 8-10; Neutrophil 60-65”\nBlood-cell exam numbers.\nTRICK - “RBC Birth = Marrow; Graveyard = Spleen”\nFormation-destruction pair from source.\n15. WBC Types — N-E-B / L-M\n• Granular = Neutrophils 60-65%, Eosinophils 2-3%, Basophils 0.5-1%\n• Agranular = Lymphocytes 20-25%, Monocytes 2-10%\n• Neutrophils = most abundant WBC\nTRICK - “Granular N-E-B; Agranular L-M”\nN-E-B / L-M classification.\n16. Blood Groups — L / Castello-Sturli / Rh\n• A, B, O discovered by Landsteiner\n• AB discovered by Von de Castello & Sturli, 1902\n• Source notes: O = Universal Donor; AB = Universal Recipient\n• Rh factor discovered by Landsteiner & Wiener, 1940 in Rhesus monkey\n• Source notes: Rh+ = 85% world, 97% India\nTRICK - “Landsteiner ABO; C-S AB; L-W Rh 1940”\nDiscoverer chain ko 3 blocks mein yaad karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource note uses O = universal donor and AB = universal recipient.\n17. Heart — 4 Chambers + Valve Side Trick\n• Heart = 4 chambered: 2 atria + 2 ventricles"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\n• Atria receive blood; ventricles pump\n• Double-walled pericardium covers heart\n• Source weights: men 280-340 g; women 230-240 g; newborn 20 g\nFeature\nFact\nTricuspid\nRight atrium - right ventricle\nBicuspid / Mitral\nLeft atrium - left ventricle\nSemilunar\nVentricle - artery\nLub\nClosure of AV valves\nDup\nClosure of semilunar valves\nHeart rate\n72-75 beats/min\nOne beat\n0.85 s\nCardiac output\n5 L/min\nBlood pressure\n120/80 mmHg\nPacemaker\nSA Node\nTRICK - “TRI = Right; BI/Mitral = Left”\nTricuspid right, bicuspid/mitral left.\nTRICK - “Lub AV; Dup Semi”\nHeart sound valve-closure trick.\nTRICK - “72-75 / 0.85 / 5 L / 120-80 / SA”\nHeart number pack.\n18. Blood Flow — Right Deoxy, Left Oxy\nChamber\nFlow\nRight atrium\nDeoxygenated blood from vena cava\nRight ventricle\nDeoxygenated to lungs via pulmonary artery\nLeft atrium\nOxygenated from lungs via pulmonary veins\nLeft ventricle\nOxygenated to body via aorta\nTRICK - “RA Receive Deoxy; RV to Lungs; LA Receive Oxy; LV to Body”\nHeart circulation ko R-R-L-L chain mein bolo.\nEXAM TRAP - “Pulmonary Exception = Artery Deoxy, Vein Oxy”\nMajor vessel exception.\n19. Artery vs Vein vs Capillary\nVessel\nDirection / Blood\nWall / Valve\nArtery\nAway; usually oxygenated\nThick; no valves\nVein\nToward; usually deoxygenated\nThin; valves present\nCapillary\nConnect arteries-veins\nExchange surface\nTRICK - “A = Away; V = Visits Heart”\nPulmonary vessels ko exception ke roop mein separate yaad karo.\n• Varicose veins = dilated superficial veins due to incompetent venous valves, commonly legs\n20. Excretion — Plant + Human\nPlant Waste\nMethod\nLiquid\nTranspiration via stomata\nGases\nStomata + lenticels\nSolid\nVacuoles/dead tissues; leaf shedding"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\nUseful waste\nOils, perfumes, gums, resins, rubber, tannin\nTRICK - “Plant Waste = Stoma-Lenticel-Vacuole-Shedding”\nPlant excretion ke routes.\n• Human nitrogenous waste mainly urea; urea produced in liver and removed by kidneys\n• Kidneys = one pair, bean-shaped\n• About 10 lakh nephrons per kidney\n• Nephron = structural + functional unit\n• Urine pH about 6.0, slightly acidic\n• Urine source composition = water 95% + urea 2%\n• Urine colour = urochrome/urobilin\nTRICK - “Liver Makes Urea; Kidney Removes Urea”\nFormation vs excretion organ trap.\n21. Urinary Path + Nephron Path\nOrgan\nRole\nKidney\nForms urine\nUreter\nKidney > bladder\nBladder\nStores urine\nUrethra\nRemoves urine\nTRICK - “K-U-B-U = Kidney-Ureter-Bladder-Urethra”\nUrinary tract order.\nTRICK - “B-P-H-D-C”\nBowman’s capsule > PCT > Henle loop > DCT > Collecting duct.\nTRICK - “B-P-H-D-C > Ureter > Bladder > Urethra”\nSource chapter ka complete nephron-to-exit chain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nNephron = structural & functional unit; about 10 lakh per kidney.\n22. Plant Transport — Xylem vs Phloem\nTransport\nTissue / Material\nDirection\nMechanism\nWater\nXylem; water + minerals\nUpward / unidirectional\nCohesion + adhesion +\ntranspiration pull\nFood\nPhloem; sucrose\nBi-/multidirectional\nMass flow - Munch hypothesis\nTRICK - “Xylem = Water Up; Phloem = Food Both”\nX = xylem-water; P = phloem-food.\nTRICK - “Munch = Mass Flow”\nFood translocation hypothesis.\nEXAM TRAP -\nXylem unidirectional; phloem bidirectional/multidirectional."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Biological Process\n23. Final Exam Traps — 14 Red Flags\n• Cuscuta parasite vs Rhizobium symbiotic N-fixer\n• Fat 9.3 > Protein 4.3 > Carbohydrate 4.1 Kcal/g\n• Protein deficiency = Marasmus + Kwashiorkor\n• ADEK fat-soluble; B-complex + C water-soluble\n• B1 Beri-Beri; B3 Pellagra; C Scurvy; D Rickets; K bleeding\n• Liver largest gland; pancreas second largest + mixed\n• Aerobic 36 ATP vs anaerobic 2 ATP\n• Frog skin+lungs; insects trachea+spiracles\n• RBC 120 days; platelets 8-10 days; neutrophils most abundant\n• Source notes: O universal donor; AB universal recipient\n• Tricuspid right; bicuspid/mitral left; semilunar ventricle-artery\n• Pulmonary artery deoxygenated; pulmonary vein oxygenated\n• Nephron structural-functional unit; urine pH about 6\n• Xylem water one-way; phloem food both ways\nEXAM TRAP - “Nutrition-Energy-Vitamin-Glands-ATP-Gas-Blood-Valves-Pulmonary-Kidney-X/P”\nExam ke major confusion zones isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“NRET life processes\n Auto chlorophyll/photosynthesis; N-D-V insectivorous, Cuscuta sucker parasite, Rhizobium root-N symbiotic;\n→\nhetero H-S-P\n energy F-P-C 9.3-4.3-4.1; protein M-K; Vitamin Casimir Funk; ADEK fat vs B+C water; B1 Beri, B3 3D Pellagra, C\n→\nScurvy, D Rickets, K Klotting\n digestion I-D-A-A-D; canal 8-10m; teeth 2-1-2-3x4=32; Mouth Amylase, Stomach P-R-L, Pancreas T-C-A-\n→\nC-L; Liver largest/bile in gall bladder, Pancreas 2nd mixed\n respiration Aero36 vs Anaero2; Right lung3/Left2; inhale-flat/exhale-\n→\ndome; O2=97Hb, CO2=70-23-7; Frog skin+lung, insect trachea\n blood pH7.3-7.5, 55 plasma/45 cells; RBC120 marrow-birth/spleen-\n→\ngrave; platelets8-10 megakaryocyte; WBC N-E-B/L-M\n Landsteiner ABO, Castello-Sturli AB, L-W Rh1940\n heart4; TRI-right, BI-left,\n→\n→\nLubAV/DupSemi, SA node, 120/80\n RA deoxy in, RV pulmonary artery out; LA oxy in, LV aorta out; pulmonary artery deoxy/vein\n→\noxy\n excretion Liver makes urea/Kidney removes; K-U-B-U; nephron B-P-H-D-C; urine pH6\n plants: Xylem water-up by\n→\n→\ntranspiration pull; Phloem sucrose both-way by Munch mass flow.”\nTOP 5: Fat 9.3 > Protein 4.3 > Carb 4.1 | ADEK fat-soluble | Aero36 vs Anaero2 | Pulmonary artery deoxy / vein oxy | Xylem one-\nway water vs Phloem both-way food."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\nCONTROL, COORDINATION & MOVEMENT — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 7 · Nervous System + Hormones + Muscles + Skeleton + Joints + Plant Coordination\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke impulse pathway, brain-function pairs, endocrine hormones, muscle/skeleton\nsuperlatives, joint examples aur plant movement/hormone traps ko fast exam recall ke liye compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Nervous System — C-P-A\nDivision\nComponents / Role\nCNS\nBrain + Spinal cord\nPNS\n12 pairs cranial nerves + 31 pairs spinal nerves\nANS\nSympathetic + Parasympathetic\nTRICK - “C-P-A = Central - Peripheral - Autonomic”\nPNS number pack = 12 cranial + 31 spinal pairs.\nANS pair = Sympathetic + Parasympathetic.\n2. Impulse Path — S-R-S-C-M-E\n• Stimulus > Receptor > Sensory neuron > Brain/Spinal cord > Motor neuron > Effector organ\n• Reflex action = automatic + involuntary response\n• Source notes associate reflex control with spinal cord\nTRICK - “S-R-S-C-M-E”\nStimulus-Receptor-Sensory-CNS-Motor-Effector.\nEXAM TRAP -\nReflex = automatic/involuntary; source notes mein spinal cord se associated, brain se nahi.\n3. Sensory Receptors + Eye\nOrgan\nFunction\nEar\nHearing + body balance\nEye\nVision\nSkin\nTouch + heat + pain\nNose\nSmell\nTongue\nTaste buds\nEye Part\nFact\nIris\nControls pupil expansion/contraction\nCornea\nTransparent front part\nLacrimal gland\nReleases tears\nSuperior rectus\nControls eye movement\nTRICK - “I-C-L-S = Iris-Cornea-Lacrimal-Superior Rectus”\nIris pupil, Cornea transparent, Lacrimal tears, Superior rectus movement.\nEXAM TRAP -\nNervous coordination = electrical impulses; endocrine coordination = chemical hormones.\n4. Brain — Fore-Mid-Hind\n• Brain weight in source notes = about 1300-1400 g"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\n• Forebrain = higher functions + voluntary actions\n• Midbrain = visual + auditory reflexes\n• Hindbrain = automatic functions + spinal coordination\nTRICK - “FORE Thinks, MID Reflexes, HIND Runs Basics”\nFore = higher functions; Mid = light/sound reflex; Hind = automatic coordination.\n5. Forebrain — O-C-E-H\nPart\nFunction\nOlfactory lobe\nSmell\nCerebrum\nMemory, consciousness, reasoning, learning\nEpithalamus\nPain, sensation, heat/cold perception\nHypothalamus\nAppetite, thirst, affection, disgust, sleep, temperature\nTRICK - “O-C-E-H”\nOlfactory-Smell, Cerebrum-Memory, Epithalamus-Sensation, Hypothalamus-Home regulation.\nEXAM TRAP - “Cerebrum = Memory; Cerebellum = Balance”\nNaam similar, function opposite trap.\n6. Hindbrain — P-C-M\nPart\nFunction\nPons\nRespiratory centre\nCerebellum\nMuscular balance + posture\nMedulla oblongata\nBreathing rhythm + heart rate + hiccups + ANS\nTRICK - “P-C-M = Pons Respire, Cerebellum Balance, Medulla Heart/Breath”\nHindbrain ke 3 direct function pairs.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMedulla = breathing + heart rate; Hypothalamus = appetite/thirst/sleep/temp.\n7. Endocrine Glands — Hormone-Disease Pairs\nGland / Cell\nHormone\nMain Function / Deficiency\nAnterior Pituitary\nGH / Somatotropic\nGrowth; deficiency = dwarfism/stunted\ngrowth\nThyroid\nThyroxine\nBMR; deficiency linked with cretinism/goitre\nAdrenal\nAdrenaline / Nor-adrenaline\nRaises BP/heartbeat; source calls adrenaline\nDo or Die\nPancreas beta-cells\nInsulin\nLowers blood sugar; deficiency = diabetes\nPancreas alpha-cells\nGlucagon\nRaises blood sugar\nTestes\nTestosterone / Androgen\nMale secondary characters +\nspermatogenesis\nOvaries\nOestrogen + Progesterone\nFemale secondary characters, oogenesis,\nuterus prep\nTRICK - “Beta Insulin DOWN; Alpha Glucagon UP”\nbeta-cells lower blood sugar; alpha-cells raise blood sugar.\nTRICK - “GH-Dwarf | Thyroid-Goitre/Cretinism | Insulin-Diabetes”\nDisease-hormone fast pair."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\nEXAM TRAP - “Adrenaline = Do or Die”\nSource ka direct one-liner.\n8. Muscles — V-I-I + Superlatives\nFeature\nStriated/Skeletal\nSmooth\nCardiac\nControl\nVoluntary\nInvoluntary\nInvoluntary\nBands\nPresent\nAbsent\nPresent\nLocation\nSkeleton\nUterus/intestine/pupil/trachea\nHeart\nTRICK - “V-I-I; Bands = Skeletal + Cardiac”\nStriated voluntary; Smooth involuntary; Cardiac involuntary but striated.\nTRICK - “Masseter Strongest; Gluteus Maximus Largest”\nMuscle superlatives.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCardiac muscle striated hote hue bhi involuntary hai.\n9. Skeleton — 206 + Head 8-14-6-1\n• Total adult bones = 206\n• Cranium = 8\n• Face = 14\n• Ear ossicles = 6\n• Hyoid = 1\nTRICK - “Head = 8 + 14 + 6 + 1”\nCranium-Face-Ear-Hyoid.\nTRICK - “Ear = M-I-S; Stapes Smallest”\nMalleus-Incus-Stapes; Stapes = smallest bone.\n10. Vertebral Column — 7-12-5-1-1\nRegion\nAdult Count\nCervical\n7\nThoracic\n12\nLumbar\n5\nSacrum\n1\nCoccyx\n1\nTRICK - “7-12-5-1-1 = 26 Adult Vertebral Bones”\nNeck-Chest-Waist-Sacrum-Coccyx.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes mention sacrum 5 and coccyx 4 in infants, but adult table counts them as 1 each.\n11. Skeleton Superlatives + Limb Numbers\n• Largest & strongest bone = Femur\n• Smallest bone = Stapes\n• Ribs = 24 = 12 pairs"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\n• Sternum = 1\n• Pectoral girdle = Scapula 2 + Clavicle 2 = 4\n• Pelvic girdle = Innominate 2\n• Upper arm = Humerus 2; Lower arm = Radius 2 + Ulna 2\n• Wrist/Carpals = 16\n• Palm/Fingers = Metacarpals 10 + Phalanges 28\n• Lower limb: Femur 2; Tibia 2 + Fibula 2; Patella 2; Tarsal 14 + Metatarsals 10; toe phalanges 28\nTRICK - “Femur Biggest-Strongest; Stapes Smallest; Ribs 24”\n3 skeletal super-facts.\n12. Joints — S-A-E-S\nJoint Type\nMobility\nSource Example\nImmovable\nNo movement\nSkull bones; teeth & jaw joint\nSemi-movable\nLimited\nPubic symphysis / pelvic girdle\nBall & Socket\nAll directions\nShoulder; source table also lists ankles/feet\nHinge\nOne-direction\nElbow, fingertips\nPivotal\nRotation\nAtlas-Axis neck\nSaddle\nTwo-direction\nSource table: wrist & ankle\nTRICK - “Skull None - Atlas Axis Pivot - Elbow Hinge - Shoulder Ball”\nMost-tested examples ka four-point chain.\nTRICK - “Synovial = Smooth Movement”\nMovable joints mein synovial cavity/fluid lubrication.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBall & socket maximum movement; hinge mainly flexion/extension.\n13. Plant Movement — Tropic vs Nastic\nMovement\nNature\nExamples\nTropic\nGrowth-related; direction matters\nPhoto, Geo, Hydro, Chemo\nNastic\nNon-growth; direction-independent\nTouch-me-not / Mimosa; thigmonasty\nTRICK - “Tropic = Turns Toward/Away; Nastic = No Direction”\nTropic mein direction matters; nastic mein direction independent.\nTRICK - “P-G-H-C”\nPhototropism-Light, Geotropism-Gravity, Hydrotropism-Water, Chemotropism-Chemical.\n• Source note: phototropism root = negative / away from light; sunflower example\n• Geotropism: roots positive, shoots negative\n• Hydrotropism: movement towards water\n• Chemotropism: pollen tube grows towards ovule\nEXAM TRAP -\nTouch-me-not = nastic/thigmonasty, tropic nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\n14. Plant Hormones — AGC vs AE\nCategory\nHormone\nKey Function\nGrowth promoter\nAuxin\nApical dominance + cell elongation +\nparthenogenesis\nGrowth promoter\nGibberellin\nBolting + seed germination\nGrowth promoter\nCytokinin\nCell division + delays senescence + breaks\ndormancy\nGrowth inhibitor\nABA\nStress hormone; stomatal closure +\ndormancy + senescence\nGrowth inhibitor\nEthylene\nGaseous hormone; fruit ripening +\nsenescence\nTRICK - “AGC = Auxin-Gibberellin-Cytokinin = Growth Promoters”\nSource ka direct growth-promoter group.\nTRICK - “AE = ABA-Ethylene = Growth Inhibitors”\nABA stress/dormancy; Ethylene fruit ripening.\nTRICK - “Auxin Apex; Gibberellin Bolting; Cytokinin Cell Division”\nA-G-C function hook.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEthylene = only gaseous plant hormone in source notes; ABA = stress hormone.\n15. Final Exam Traps — 11 Red Flags\n• Reflex = automatic/involuntary; source notes associate it with spinal cord\n• Nervous = electrical; Endocrine = chemical/hormonal\n• Cerebrum memory vs Cerebellum balance\n• Medulla breathing/heart rate vs Hypothalamus appetite/thirst/sleep/temp\n• beta-cells insulin lowers sugar vs alpha-cells glucagon raises sugar\n• Adrenaline = Do or Die hormone\n• Cardiac = striated but involuntary; Masseter strongest; Gluteus maximus largest\n• Skeleton = 206; Femur largest & strongest; Stapes smallest\n• Vertebrae = 7-12-5-1-1; Ribs = 24\n• Skull immovable; Atlas-Axis pivotal; Elbow hinge; Shoulder ball & socket\n• Tropic growth/direction vs Nastic non-growth/direction-independent; Ethylene gaseous, ABA stress\nEXAM TRAP - “Reflex-Electric/Chemical-Brain-Sugar-Muscle-Bones-Joints-Plant”\nChapter ke main confusion zones isi chain mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Control, Coordination & Movement\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Nervous C-P-A = CNS brain+cord, PNS 12 cranial+31 spinal, ANS Sympathetic+Parasympathetic; impulse S-R-S-C-M-E; reflex spinal →\nreceptors Ear balance/hear, Eye vision, Skin touch/heat/pain, Nose smell, Tongue taste; Iris pupil, Cornea clear, Lacrimal tears\n\n→\nbrain Fore higher, Mid visual-auditory reflex, Hind automatic; Fore O-C-E-H, Hind P-C-M; Cerebrum memory vs Cerebellum balance,\nMedulla breath-heart, Hypothalamus hunger-thirst-sleep-temp\n endocrine: GH dwarf, thyroid goitre/cretinism, adrenaline Do-or-\n→\nDie, beta insulin DOWN, alpha glucagon UP, testes testosterone, ovaries oestrogen+progesterone\n muscles V-I-I; cardiac\n→\nstriated+involuntary; Masseter strongest, Gluteus largest\n skeleton206; head 8-14-6-1; vertebrae 7-12-5-1-1; Femur\n→\nbiggest/strongest, Stapes smallest, ribs24\n joints Skull none, Atlas-Axis pivot, Elbow hinge, Shoulder ball; synovial lubricates\n\n→\n→\nplant movement Tropic direction/growth vs Nastic no-direction/non-growth; P-G-H-C\n plant hormones AGC promoters = Auxin\n→\napex, Gibberellin bolting, Cytokinin division; AE inhibitors = ABA stress/dormancy + Ethylene gas/fruit ripening.”\nTOP 5: Cerebrum memory vs Cerebellum balance | beta insulin DOWN vs alpha glucagon UP | Cardiac striated but involuntary | 7-\n12-5-1-1 vertebrae | Tropic direction vs Nastic no-direction."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Reproduction\nREPRODUCTION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 8 · Asexual + Vegetative + Flower + Pollination + Human Reproduction\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke asexual methods, vegetative examples, flower parts, double fertilisation, pollination\nterms aur male-female reproductive system ke high-confusion facts ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Asexual vs Sexual — Clone vs Variation\nFeature\nAsexual\nSexual\nParents\nSingle parent (source also notes bisexual)\nTwo parents of different sex\nGametes\nAbsent\nPresent\nFusion\nNo gamete fusion\nFertilisation present\nOffspring\nClone; no variation\nVariation present\nTRICK - “A = Alone + Again Same; S = Sex Cells + Slightly Different”\nAsexual = no gamete fusion + clone.\nSexual = gametes + fertilisation + variation.\nEXAM TRAP -\nClone/no variation = asexual; variation = sexual.\n2. Asexual Routes — F-F-R-B-S-V\n• Fission\n• Fragmentation\n• Regeneration\n• Budding\n• Spore formation\n• Vegetative reproduction\nTRICK - “F-F-R-B-S-V”\nFission-Fragmentation-Regeneration-Budding-Spore-Vegetative.\n3. Fission — Binary vs Multiple\nType\nResult\nExamples\nBinary fission\n2 progenies\nAmoeba, Bacteria, Leishmania, Paramecium\nMultiple fission\nMany progenies\nPlasmodium - malarial parasite\nTRICK - “Binary = 2; Multiple = Many”\nLeishmania binary; Plasmodium multiple.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLeishmania = binary fission; Plasmodium = multiple fission.\n4. Fragmentation - Regeneration - Budding - Spores\nMethod\nExamples\nFragmentation\nSpirogyra, Rhizopus, Ulothrix, Red algae\nRegeneration\nHydra, Planaria\nBudding\nHydra, Yeast\nSpore formation\nChlamydomonas, Rhizopus, Mucor, Puccinia"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Reproduction\nTRICK - “Hydra = R+B”\nHydra dono karta hai: Regeneration + Budding.\nTRICK - “Yeast Buds; Plasmodium Multiplies”\nYeast = budding; Plasmodium = multiple fission.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHydra ko sirf budding ya sirf regeneration mat yaad karo — source mein dono listed hain.\n5. Tissue Culture — M-I-D\n• Tissue culture = Micropropagation = In-vitro propagation\n• Laboratory method\n• Suitable culture medium\n• Used for decorative + disease-free plants in less time\nTRICK - “M-I-D = Micropropagation - In-vitro - Disease-free”\nTeen words ek saath lock karo.\n6. Natural Vegetative Propagation — S-R-L\nPart\nExamples\nStem\nPotato, Sugarcane\nRoot\nRosewood, Sweet potato\nLeaf\nBegonia, Bryophyllum\nTRICK - “Potato Stem - Sweet Potato Root - Bryophyllum Leaf”\nChapter ka most common vegetative trio.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPotato = stem; Sweet potato = root. Dono ko interchange mat karna.\n7. Artificial Vegetative Propagation — Cutting + Layering\nMethod\nExamples\nShoot cutting\nRose, Sugarcane, Banana\nRoot cutting\nLemon, Orange\nLayering\nApple, Pear, Lemon, Strawberry\nTRICK - “Shoot R-S-B; Root L-O; Layer A-P-L-S”\nR-S-B = Rose-Sugarcane-Banana.\nL-O = Lemon-Orange.\nA-P-L-S = Apple-Pear-Lemon-Strawberry.\n8. Flower Parts — C-C-A-G\nPart\nMemory\nCalyx\nGreen part\nCorolla\nColoured part\nAndroecium\nStamens - male organ\nGynoecium\nPistil/Carpel - female organ"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Reproduction\nTRICK - “C-C-A-G = Green - Colour - Male - Female”\nCalyx green, Corolla colour, Androecium male, Gynoecium female.\nTRICK - “A = Andro = Male; G = Gyno = Female”\nMale-female floral organ pair.\n9. Monoecious/Bisexual vs Dioecious — Maize Trap\n• Source bisexual/monoecious examples = Hibiscus, Pea, Rose, Sunflower, Tomato, Mango, Lily\n• Maize = monoecious plant but flowers are unisexual; male + female flowers separate on same plant\n• Dioecious source examples = Papaya, Cucumber, Watermelon, Muskmelon\nTRICK - “Maize = Same Plant, Separate Flowers”\nMonoecious + unisexual flowers.\nTRICK - “P-C-W-M = Separate Plants”\nPapaya-Cucumber-Watermelon-Muskmelon = dioecious in source list.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMaize = monoecious but unisexual flowers; Papaya = dioecious.\n10. Gametogenesis — Micro vs Mega\n• Microsporogenesis = haploid pollen grains in anther\n• Megasporogenesis = haploid embryo sac in ovule\nTRICK - “Micro = Male Pollen; Mega = Female Embryo Sac”\nMicro/anther vs Mega/ovule.\n11. Double Fertilisation — 2n + 3n\nFusion\nProduct\nMale gamete n + Female gamete n\nZygote 2n > Embryo\nMale gamete n + Polar/Secondary nuclei 2n\nEndosperm 3n\nTRICK - “1st = 2n Embryo; 2nd = 3n Endosperm”\nDouble fertilisation source notes mein Angiosperms ki uniqueness hai.\nTRICK - “Ovule Seed; Ovary Fruit”\nAfter fertilisation conversion pair.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEmbryo = 2n; Endosperm = 3n. Ovule = seed; Ovary = fruit.\n12. Pollination Types — A-G-C\nType\nMeaning\nAutogamy\nSame bisexual flower\nGeitonogamy\nDifferent flowers of same plant\nCross-pollination\nDifferent plants"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Reproduction\nTRICK - “Auto = Same Flower; Geito = Same Plant; Cross = Different Plant”\nA-G-C ladder.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes add: Geitonogamy genetically self-pollination-like.\n13. Pollination Agents — A-H-E\nTerm\nAgent\nExamples\nAnemophily\nWind\nMaize, Bamboo, Sugarcane\nHydrophily\nWater\nVallisneria, Hydrilla\nEntomophily\nInsects\nSalvia, Fig, Rose\nTRICK - “A-H-E = Air - H2O - Entomo/Insect”\nAnemo wind, Hydro water, Entomo insects.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAnemophily wind; Hydrophily water; Entomophily insects.\n14. Male Reproductive System — L-S-E-V\nPart / Cell\nFunction\nTestes\nPrimary male organs; sperm + testosterone\nLeydig cells\nTestosterone\nSertoli cells\nNutrition/support of sperms\nEpididymis\nSperm maturation\nVas deferens\nSperm transport\nTRICK - “L = Leydig = Libido/Testosterone; S = Sertoli = Support”\nLeydig testosterone; Sertoli sperm nutrition/support.\nTRICK - “Epididymis = Matures; Vas = Moves”\nMaturation vs transport.\n• Testes located in scrotum, outside abdominal cavity\n• Male accessory glands listed = Prostate, Cowper’s, Perineal\n• Source path components include Seminal vesicle > Urethra > Penis\nEXAM TRAP -\nTestes = scrotum outside abdomen. Leydig/Sertoli interchange mat karna.\n15. Female Reproductive System — O-O-U\nPart\nFunction / Fact\nOvaries\nPrimary female organs; eggs + female hormones\nOviducts\nPair; ovaries to uterus; carry egg\nUterus\nEmbryo development site\n• Ovaries located in abdominal cavity\n• Female hormones listed = Oestrogen + Progesterone\n• Progesterone associated with corpus luteum in source notes\n• Oogenesis = formation of haploid eggs\n• Female accessory glands listed = Bartholin’s + Perineal"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Reproduction\nTRICK - “O-O-U = Ovary - Oviduct - Uterus”\nEgg source > transport > embryo-development site.\n16. Male vs Female — Fast Pairing\nFeature\nMale\nFemale\nPrimary organ\nTestes - scrotum\nOvaries - abdomen\nGamete formation\nSpermatogenesis\nOogenesis\nGamete\nHaploid sperm\nHaploid egg\nHormone side\nLeydig > Testosterone\nCorpus luteum > Oestrogen/Progesterone in\nsource table\nTransport/Maturation\nEpididymis / Vas deferens\nOviduct\nTRICK - “Sperma = Sperm; Oo = Ovum”\nSpermatogenesis male; Oogenesis female; both haploid through meiosis.\nFertilisation > diploid zygote 2n.\n17. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Leishmania binary fission; Plasmodium multiple fission\n• Hydra = budding + regeneration; Yeast = budding\n• Tissue culture = micropropagation = in-vitro propagation\n• Potato stem; Sweet potato root; Bryophyllum leaf\n• Maize monoecious with unisexual flowers on same plant; Papaya dioecious\n• Double fertilisation: embryo 2n; endosperm 3n\n• Ovule > seed; Ovary > fruit\n• Autogamy same flower; Geitonogamy same plant/different flower; Cross = different plants\n• Anemophily wind; Hydrophily water; Entomophily insects\n• Leydig testosterone; Sertoli sperm nutrition/support\n• Spermatogenesis sperm; Oogenesis egg; both haploid\n• Testes scrotum outside abdomen; ovaries abdominal cavity\nEXAM TRAP - “Fission-Hydra-Culture-Veg-Maize-2n/3n-Seed/Fruit-AGC-AHE-LS-Gametes-Location”\n12 source traps ko isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Asexual = alone/no fusion/clone vs Sexual = gametes+fertilisation+variation\n routes F-F-R-B-S-V\n Binary2: Amoeba-Bacteria-\n→\n→\nLeishmania-Paramecium; Multiple many: Plasmodium\n Fragmentation Spirogyra/Rhizopus/Ulothrix/Red; Regeneration Hydra-\n→\nPlanaria; Budding Hydra-Yeast; Spores Chlamydomonas-Rhizopus-Mucor-Puccinia\n Tissue culture = Micropropagation = In-vitro =\n→\ndisease-free\n natural veg: Potato stem, Sweet potato root, Bryophyllum leaf; artificial Shoot R-S-B, Root L-O, Layer A-P-L-S\n Flower\n→\n→\nC-C-A-G = Calyx green, Corolla colour, Andro male, Gyno female; Maize same plant separate unisexual flowers vs Papaya dioecious →\nMicro pollen/anther, Mega embryo-sac/ovule\n Double fertilisation: 2n embryo + 3n endosperm; Ovule seed, Ovary fruit\n\n→\n→\nPollination A-G-C = same flower/same plant/different plants; agents A-H-E = wind/water/insects\n Male: testes scrotum, Leydig\n→\ntestosterone, Sertoli support, Epididymis maturation, Vas transport\n Female: ovaries abdomen, Oestrogen+Progesterone,\n→\nOogenesis, Oviduct transport, Uterus embryo\n Spermatogenesis sperm + Oogenesis egg = haploid; fertilisation = zygote 2n.”\n→\nTOP 5: Leishmania binary vs Plasmodium multiple | Potato stem/Sweet potato root/Bryophyllum leaf | Maize monoecious vs\nPapaya dioecious | Embryo 2n vs Endosperm 3n | Leydig testosterone vs Sertoli support."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\nHEREDITY & EVOLUTION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 9 · Mendel + Crosses + DNA/RNA + Genetic Diseases + Evolution\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke Mendelian laws, F2 ratios, inheritance scientists, DNA/RNA facts, genetic disorders,\nevidences aur evolution theories ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Mendel Basics — M-P-7\n• Gregor Johann Mendel = Father of Genetics\n• Experiment plant = Pisum sativum / Garden pea\n• Studied 7 pairs of contrasting characters\n• Heredity = traits ka parent se offspring transmission\n• Genetics = genetic traits aur inheritance ka study\nTRICK - “M-P-7 = Mendel - Pisum - 7 Pairs”\nMendel ke opening facts ka one-line code.\nTRICK - “T-R-Y-P vs D-W-G-W”\nDominant examples: Tall-Round-Yellow-Purple.\nRecessive examples: Dwarf-Wrinkled-Green-White.\n2. Mendel’s 3 Laws — D-S-I\nLaw\nCore Memory\nDominance\nDominant allele recessive ko mask karta hai\nSegregation\nAlleles gametogenesis mein separate\nIndependent Assortment\nOne trait ki inheritance dusre ko affect nahi karti\nTRICK - “D-S-I = Dominance - Segregation - Independent”\nLaw 1, 2, 3 ka direct order.\nTRICK - “Segregation = Purity of Gametes”\nSource ka exact alternate name.\nTRICK - “Mono = Law 1+2; Di = Law 3”\nMonohybrid supports Dominance + Segregation.\nDihybrid gives Independent Assortment.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSegregation aur Independent Assortment ko interchange mat karna.\n3. Monohybrid Cross — 3:1 / 1:2:1\n• P generation = TT Tall x tt Dwarf\n• F1 = all Tt Hybrid Tall\n• F1 self = Tt x Tt\nF2 Ratio\nResult\nPhenotype\n3 : 1 = Tall : Dwarf\nGenotype\n1 : 2 : 1 = TT : Tt : tt\nTRICK - “Mono = P3, G121”\nPhenotype 3:1; Genotype 1:2:1."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\nEXAM TRAP -\n3:1 phenotype hai; 1:2:1 genotype.\n4. Dihybrid Cross — 9:3:3:1\n• P = RRYY Round Yellow x rryy Wrinkled Green\n• F1 = RrYy Round Yellow\n• F1 gametes = RY, Ry, rY, ry\n• F2 phenotype ratio = 9:3:3:1\nTRICK - “Di = 9-3-3-1”\nRound Yellow : Round Green : Wrinkled Yellow : Wrinkled Green.\nEXAM TRAP - “BbEe x BbEe > BBEE = 1/16”\nSource ka direct probability trap.\n5. Inheritance Scientists — S-B-M\nScientist\nContribution\nSutton & Boveri\nChromosomal theory of inheritance\nT.H. Morgan\nDrosophila experimental verification + gene theory\nT.H. Morgan\nGenes linear on chromosomes like beads\nTRICK - “S-B Theory, Morgan Proof + Line”\nSutton-Boveri = theory.\nMorgan = Drosophila verification + linear gene arrangement.\nEXAM TRAP -\nChromosomal theory = Sutton & Boveri; Morgan = experimental verification/gene theory.\n6. DNA Scientist Timeline — M-HW-WC\nScientist\nYear\nFact\nFriedrich Miescher\n1869\nNucleic acid discovery\nHershey & Chase\n1952\nDNA as genetic material\nWatson & Crick\n1953\nDouble-helix model\nTRICK - “69 Miescher - 52 Hershey/Chase - 53 Watson/Crick”\nDiscovery, proof, model — three different facts.\nEXAM TRAP -\nWatson-Crick = model; Hershey-Chase = genetic material proof.\n7. Nucleoside vs Nucleotide — +P Rule\n• Nucleoside = nitrogenous base + deoxyribose sugar\n• Nucleotide = nucleoside + phosphate\nTRICK - “Nucleotide = Nucleoside + P”\nP = phosphate."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\n8. DNA Bases — AG Purines / TC Pyrimidines\nGroup\nBases\nPurines\nAdenine (A) + Guanine (G)\nPyrimidines\nThymine (T) + Cytosine (C)\nPairing\nA-T and G-C\nTRICK - “PURe As Gold = A-G”\nPurines = A + G.\nPyrimidines = T + C.\nTRICK - “AT / GC = DNA Couples”\nSource base-pairing rule.\n9. DNA vs RNA — DDT vs SRU\nFeature\nDNA\nRNA\nStrands\nDouble\nUsually Single\nSugar\nDeoxyribose\nRibose\nSpecial base\nThymine\nUracil replaces Thymine\nRNA types\n—\nrRNA ~80%, tRNA 10-15%, mRNA 3-5%\nTRICK - “DNA = Double-Deoxy-Thymine; RNA = Single-Ribose-Uracil”\nD-D-T vs S-R-U.\nTRICK - “rRNA 80 > tRNA 10-15 > mRNA 3-5”\nSource abundance order.\nEXAM TRAP -\nRNA has Uracil, not Thymine.\n10. Gene Expression — R-T-T\n• Central flow in source: DNA > Replication > DNA > Transcription > mRNA > Translation > Protein\nTRICK - “Replicate DNA, Transcribe RNA, Translate Protein”\nR-T-T sequence.\n11. Honeybee Ploidy — Male n, Female 2n\nTRICK - “Male = Mini n; Female = Full 2n”\nHoneybee male haploid; female diploid.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMale honeybee = haploid, female = diploid.\n12. Genetic Diseases — Sex-linked Pair\nDisease\nCause / Type\nKey Fact\nHaemophilia\nX-linked recessive\nA = Factor VIII; B = Factor IX\nColour blindness\nX-linked recessive\nRed-green distinction affected"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\nTRICK - “H-A = 8; H-B = 9”\nHaemophilia-A Factor VIII, Haemophilia-B Factor IX.\nTRICK - “X-linked = Males More Expressed”\nSource reason: males have only one X chromosome.\n13. Sickle Cell — 11 / 6 / Valine\n• Sickle-cell anaemia = beta-globin gene mutation\n• Gene on chromosome 11\n• Valine replaces glutamic acid at 6th position\n• RBC becomes sickle-shaped and carries less O2\nTRICK - “Sickle = 11-6-Val”\nChromosome 11, position 6, Valine.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSickle cell chromosome = 11; substitution at 6th position.\n14. Down - Turner - Klinefelter — 47 / 45 / 47\nSyndrome\nChromosome Pattern\nSex / Cue\nDown\nTrisomy 21; total 47\nAutosomal trisomy\nTurner\n44 + X0; total 45\nFemale\nKlinefelter\n44 + XXY; total 47\nMale\nTRICK - “D-T-K = 47-45-47”\nDown 47, Turner 45, Klinefelter 47.\nTRICK - “Turner = X0 Female; Kline = XXY Male”\nSex-chromosome patterns ko name ke saath lock karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDown = Trisomy 21; Turner = 45 female; Klinefelter = 47 male.\n15. Evolution — Descent with Modification\n• Biological evolution = complex organisms ka simple/primitive life forms se development\n• Also called Descent with modification\nTRICK - “Evolution = Descent + Modification”\nSource ka direct alternate phrase.\n16. Fossil Dating — C-U-K\n• Fossils = dead organisms ke remains preserved in primitive rocks of Earth crust\n• Age determination methods = C14 dating, U-Pb dating, K-Ar dating\nTRICK - “C-U-K = Carbon - Uranium/Lead - Potassium/Argon”\nThree dating methods source list se."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\n17. Homologous vs Analogous vs Vestigial\nType\nStructure/Origin\nFunction\nExample\nHomologous\nSimilar\nDifferent\nForelimbs of vertebrates\nAnalogous\nDifferent\nSimilar\nWings of insects and birds\nVestigial\nFunctional in ancestors\nReduced/non-functional now\nAppendix, wisdom teeth, coccyx\nTRICK - “Homo = Same Structure, Different Job”\nHomologous > divergent evolution.\nTRICK - “Analog = Different Structure, Same Job”\nAnalogous > convergent evolution.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHomologous divergent; Analogous convergent.\n18. Connecting Links — V-E-A\nOrganism\nConnects\nVirus\nLiving - Non-living\nEuglena\nAnimal - Plant\nArchaeopteryx\nReptile - Bird\nTRICK - “V-E-A = Virus Life/Nonlife; Euglena Animal/Plant; Archaeopteryx Reptile/Bird”\nThree direct connecting-link pairs.\n19. Evolution Theories — L-D-V\nScientist\nBook / Experiment\nCore Idea\nLamarck\nPhilosophie Zoologique\nAcquired characters; use & disuse\nDarwin\nOn the Origin of Species, 1859\nNatural selection; struggle; survival of fittest\nHugo de Vries\nEvening Primrose\nMutation theory; sudden inherited changes\nTRICK - “L-D-V = Lamarck Acquired, Darwin Selection, de Vries Mutation”\nTheory-scientist pairing.\nTRICK - “Lamarck = Use/Disuse; Darwin = Natural Selection; Vries = Sudden Mutation”\nCore-idea chain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDarwin 1859 Origin; Lamarck Philosophie Zoologique; de Vries Evening Primrose.\n20. Final Exam Traps — 15 Red Flags\n• Segregation = Purity of Gametes; Independent Assortment = dihybrid\n• Monohybrid phenotype 3:1; genotype 1:2:1\n• Dihybrid phenotype 9:3:3:1; BBEE probability 1/16 in source cross\n• Sutton-Boveri theory; Morgan Drosophila verification/gene theory\n• Miescher 1869; Hershey-Chase 1952; Watson-Crick 1953\n• RNA = Uracil, not Thymine\n• Honeybee male n; female 2n\n• Haemophilia-A VIII; Haemophilia-B IX"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Heredity & Evolution\n• Sickle cell = chromosome 11, Valine for glutamic acid at 6th\n• Down = Trisomy 21, 47\n• Turner = 44+X0, 45, female\n• Klinefelter = 44+XXY, 47, male\n• Homologous same structure/different function = divergent\n• Analogous different structure/same function = convergent\n• Archaeopteryx reptile-bird; Euglena animal-plant; Virus living-non-living\nEXAM TRAP - “Laws-Ratios-Scientists-RNA-Ploidy-Disease-Evolution”\nChapter ke highest-confusion areas isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“M-P-7 = Mendel-Pisum-7 pairs; dominant T-R-Y-P vs recessive D-W-G-W\n laws D-S-I; Segregation=Purity, Mono laws1+2, Di law3\n\n→\n→\nMonohybrid P3/G121; Dihybrid 9-3-3-1; BbEe BBEE=1/16\n Sutton-Boveri theory, Morgan Drosophila proof+linear genes\n DNA\n→\n→\ntimeline Miescher1869 > Hershey-Chase1952 > Watson-Crick1953; nucleoside base+sugar, nucleotide +phosphate; Purines AG,\nPyrimidines TC, pairs AT/GC\n DNA D-D-T vs RNA S-R-U; rRNA80 > tRNA10-15 > mRNA3-5; Replicate-Transcribe-Translate\n\n→\n→\nHoneybee male n/female2n\n Haemophilia A8/B9 + colour blindness X-linked; Sickle 11-6-Val; D-T-K = Down47/21, Turner45-X0-\n→\nfemale, Kline47-XXY-male\n Evolution = descent with modification; fossils C-U-K dating\n Homologous same/different divergent;\n→\n→\nAnalogous different/same convergent; vestigial appendix-wisdom-coccyx\n links V-E-A = Virus life/nonlife, Euglena animal/plant,\n→\nArchaeopteryx reptile/bird\n theories L-D-V = Lamarck acquired/use-disuse, Darwin natural selection/Origin1859, de Vries\n→\nmutation/Evening Primrose.”\nTOP 5: Mono 3:1 & 1:2:1 vs Di 9:3:3:1 | Miescher-Hershey/Chase-Watson/Crick | RNA U not T | D-T-K 47-45-47 | Homologous\ndivergent vs Analogous convergent."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Human Disease\nHUMAN DISEASE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Biology · Chapter 10 · Disease Types + Transmission + Pathogens + Vectors + Diagnostic Tests\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke disease-type distinctions, transmission routes, viral/bacterial/protozoan/fungal/worm\ndiseases, vectors, diagnostic tests aur high-confusion disease-pathogen pairs ko fast exam recall format mein compress kiya gaya\nhai.\n1. Disease Types — C-A-I / Non-Infectious\nType\nSource Meaning / Examples\nCongenital\nGenetic/developmental defects during embryonic development;\ncerebral palsy, haemophilia, colour blindness\nAcquired - Acute\nShort-term; cold, cholera\nAcquired - Chronic\nLong-lasting; TB, elephantiasis, arthritis\nInfectious\nSpread through contact/carrier/medium; pathogens include virus,\nbacteria, protozoa, fungi, worms\nTRICK - “C-A-C-I = Congenital - Acute - Chronic - Infectious”\nAcute = short; Chronic = long.\nInfectious = pathogen + transmission route.\n2. Transmission — 5F Rule\n• Air droplets from coughing/sneezing\n• Contaminated food and water\n• Contaminated blood/body fluids\n• Disease vectors such as flies and mosquitoes\n• Indirect contact through contaminated objects\nTRICK - “5F = Flies - Fingers - Fomites - Food - Fluid”\nSource ka ready-made transmission recall rule.\nEXAM TRAP -\nFomites = contaminated objects ke through indirect contact, source framing ke according.\n3. Non-Infectious Disease Traps — As-Cd-F\nCategory\nExamples / Pair\nAllergies\nHay-fever, Asthma\nNutritional deficiency\nMarasmus-protein; Goitre-iodine; Pellagra-B3; Dental cavities-\nfluoride\nDegenerative\nHeart attack, Arthritis, Diabetes, Glaucoma, Cataract\nMental\nStress, Depression, Epilepsy, Anorexia nervosa\nPollution-related\nArsenic-Black foot; Cadmium-Itai-itai; Fluoride-Knock-Knee\nCancer\nUncontrolled cell growth; Leukemia, Carcinoma, Sarcoma\nTRICK - “As Black - Cd Itai - F Knock”\nArsenic = Black foot disease.\nCadmium = Itai-itai.\nFluoride water = Knock-Knee syndrome.\nEXAM TRAP -\nArsenic/Cadmium/Fluoride disease pairs ko interchange mat karna."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Human Disease\n4. Viral Diseases — Air, Aedes, Food, Bite, Blood\nDisease\nPathogen\nTransmission\nSmall Pox\nVariola virus\nAir borne\nChicken Pox\nVaricella Zoster\nAir borne\nMeasles / Rubella\nRubellavirus\nAir borne - as stated in source\nInfluenza\nOrthomyxovirus\nAir borne\nSwine Flu\nInfluenza A subtype H1N1\nAir borne\nYellow Fever\nFlavi virus\nAedes aegypti bite\nDengue\nDENV\nAedes aegypti bite\nChikungunya\nCHIKV\nAedes aegypti bite\nPoliomyelitis\nPolio RNA virus type 1,2,3\nContaminated soil/water/food\nRabies / Hydrophobia\nLyssa virus type-1\nInfected animal bite\nAIDS / Slim disease\nRetrovirus HIV\nUnsafe sex, blood/needles/razor, mother-to-\nfoetus\nTRICK - “Aedes = D-C-Y”\nDengue + Chikungunya + Yellow Fever.\nTRICK - “Swine = H1N1; Rabies = Hydrophobia; AIDS = HIV + ELISA”\nThree viral direct-MCQ pairs.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPolio is stated as eradicated in India in the source notes.\n5. Viral Extra Facts — STD + COVID + Jaundice\n• HIV-AIDS, HPV and Hepatitis-B = Sexually Transmitted Diseases in source notes\n• COVID-19 = zoonotic disease caused by SARS-CoV-2; source notes mention animal origin\n• Jaundice = yellow skin; symptom associated with hepatitis/liver inflammation\nTRICK - “STD Trio = HIV - HPV - Hep-B”\nCOVID = SARS-CoV-2.\nJaundice = symptom, source connects it with hepatitis/liver inflammation.\n6. Bacterial Diseases — Air vs Food/Water vs Other\nDisease\nPathogen\nTransmission\nTB\nMycobacterium tuberculosis\nAir borne\nDiphtheria\nCorynebacterium diphtheriae\nAir borne\nWhooping cough\nBordetella pertussis\nAir borne\nPneumonia\nStreptococcus pneumoniae\nAir borne\nCholera\nVibrio cholerae\nContaminated food/water\nTyphoid\nSalmonella typhi\nContaminated food/water; Widal test\nDiarrhoea\nSalmonella sp. + E. coli; source also notes\nRotavirus\nContaminated food/water\nPlague / Black Death\nYersinia pestis\nRat fleas\nTetanus\nClostridium tetani\nWound contamination\nLeprosy / Hansen disease\nMycobacterium leprae\nDirect contact\nTRICK - “Typhoid WIDAL; AIDS ELISA”\nDiagnostic-test pair sabse important.\nTRICK - “TB + Leprosy = Mycobacterium”\ntuberculosis vs leprae species."," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Human Disease\nTRICK - “Plague Rat Flea; Tetanus Lock Jaw; Leprosy Hansen”\nPlague = Black Death.\nTetanus = Lock Jaw / 8th Day disease.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPlague = rat flea, mosquito nahi.\n7. Bacterial Extra — Trachoma + Gastritis\n• Trachoma = eye disease that may lead to blindness; Chlamydia trachomatis\n• Gastritis in stomach = Helicobacter pylori\nTRICK - “Trachoma-Eye-Chlamydia; Gastritis-Stomach-H. pylori”\nLocation + pathogen pair.\n8. Protozoan Diseases — Water + Vector Chain\nDisease\nPathogen\nTransmission\nDiarrhoea\nGiardia intestinalis\nContaminated water/food\nAmoebiasis\nEntamoeba histolytica\nContaminated water/food\nPyorrhoea\nEntamoeba gingivalis\nSaliva / Kiss\nKala-azar\nLeishmania donovani\nSand fly\nMalaria\nPlasmodium sp.\nFemale Anopheles\nAfrican Sleeping Sickness\nTrypanosoma gambiense / T. brucei\nTse-tse fly\nTRICK - “K-M-S = Kala Sand, Malaria Anopheles, Sleeping Tse-tse”\nVector trio: Sand fly > Kala-azar; Female Anopheles > Malaria; Tse-tse > Sleeping sickness.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMalaria = FEMALE Anopheles; not male, not Aedes.\n9. Worm + Fungal Diseases\nGroup / Disease\nPathogen\nTransmission\nAscariasis - Worm\nAscaris lumbricoides\nContaminated fruits/vegetables\nElephantiasis / Filariasis - Worm\nWuchereria bancrofti\nCulex mosquito\nRingworm - Fungal\nMicrosporum + Trichophyton\nDirect/indirect contact\nCandidiasis - Fungal\nCandida\nDirect/indirect contact\nTRICK - “Ascaris = Ascariasis; Wuchereria = Elephantiasis”\nWorm disease pair.\nEXAM TRAP - “Ringworm = FUNGUS, Not Worm”\nMicrosporum + Trichophyton.\n10. Mosquito Master — ADCy / AM / CE\nMosquito\nDisease(s)\nPathogen\nAedes aegypti\nDengue + Chikungunya + Yellow Fever\nDENV, CHIKV, Flavi virus\nFemale Anopheles\nMalaria\nPlasmodium sp.\nCulex\nElephantiasis / Filariasis\nWuchereria bancrofti"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Human Disease\nTRICK - “ADCy = Aedes-Dengue-Chikungunya-Yellow”\nAedes ka three-disease pack.\nTRICK - “AM = Anopheles-Malaria; CE = Culex-Elephantiasis”\nFemale Anopheles = Malaria.\nCulex = Elephantiasis/Filariasis.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAedes, Anopheles aur Culex ke diseases ko mix mat karna.\n11. Other Vectors — S-T-R-D\nVector\nDisease\nPathogen\nSand fly\nKala-azar\nLeishmania donovani\nTse-tse fly\nAfrican Sleeping Sickness\nTrypanosoma gambiense / T. brucei\nRat flea\nPlague / Black Death\nYersinia pestis\nDog/Wolf/Monkey bite\nRabies / Hydrophobia\nLyssa virus type-1\nTRICK - “S-T-R-D = Sand-Kala, Tse-Sleep, Rat-Plague, Dog-Rabies”\nVector-bite chain ko sequence mein yaad karo.\n12. Diagnostic Tests — E-W\nTest\nDisease\nELISA\nAIDS / HIV\nWidal Test\nTyphoid\nTRICK - “E = HIV; W = Typhoid”\nELISA-AIDS/HIV; Widal-Typhoid.\nEXAM TRAP -\nELISA aur Widal ko interchange mat karna.\n13. Pathogen-Wise Master Buckets\nGroup\nDisease Chain from Source\nViral\nSmall/Chicken Pox; Measles/Rubella; Influenza; Swine H1N1;\nDengue; Chikungunya; Yellow Fever; Polio; Rabies; AIDS\nBacterial\nTB; Diphtheria; Whooping cough; Pneumonia; Cholera; Typhoid;\nPlague; Tetanus; Leprosy; Trachoma; Gastritis\nProtozoan\nMalaria; Kala-azar; Amoebiasis; Pyorrhoea; African Sleeping\nSickness\nFungal + Worm\nRingworm; Candidiasis; Ascariasis; Elephantiasis\nTRICK - “V-B-P-FW”\nViral > Bacterial > Protozoan > Fungal/Worm buckets mein disease recall karo.\n14. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• 5F = Flies, Fingers, Fomites, Food, Fluid\n• Arsenic-Black foot; Cadmium-Itai-itai; Fluoride-Knock-Knee\n• Aedes = Dengue + Chikungunya + Yellow Fever\n• Female Anopheles = Malaria"," ExamFusion Prep · Biology Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Human Disease\n• Culex = Elephantiasis / Filariasis\n• Sand fly = Kala-azar\n• Tse-tse fly = African Sleeping Sickness\n• Rat flea = Plague / Black Death\n• ELISA = AIDS/HIV; Widal = Typhoid\n• Ringworm = fungal disease, not worm disease\n• Rabies = Hydrophobia; infected animal bite\n• Tetanus = Lock Jaw / 8th Day disease; Leprosy = Hansen disease\nEXAM TRAP - “5F - Pollution - 3 Mosquitoes - 3 Flies/Flea - Tests - Names”\nChapter ke most-asked traps isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Disease types C-A-C-I: congenital, acquired acute-short, chronic-long, infectious-pathogen\n transmission 5F = Flies-Fingers-\n→\nFomites-Food-Fluid\n noninfectious pollution: As-Black foot, Cd-Itai-itai, Fluoride-Knock-Knee; cancer uncontrolled growth\n viral:\n→\n→\nSmallpox-Variola, Chickenpox-Varicella, Flu-Orthomyxo, Swine-H1N1, Aedes D-C-Y, Polio contaminated food/water, Rabies\nHydrophobia-Lyssa, AIDS HIV-ELISA; STD HIV-HPV-HepB; COVID SARS-CoV-2; Jaundice hepatitis/liver symptom\n bacterial: TB\n→\nMycobacterium tuberculosis, Typhoid Salmonella-Widal, Cholera Vibrio, Plague Yersinia-rat flea, Tetanus Clostridium-Lock Jaw,\nLeprosy M.leprae-Hansen; Trachoma Chlamydia eye, Gastritis H.pylori\n protozoan: Giardia diarrhoea, Entamoeba\n→\namoebiasis/gingivalis pyorrhoea, Kala-azar Sand-Leishmania, Malaria Female Anopheles-Plasmodium, Sleeping Tse-tse-\nTrypanosoma\n worms: Ascaris ascariasis, Wuchereria filariasis-Culex; fungi: Ringworm Microsporum+Trichophyton, Candidiasis\n→\nCandida\n mosquito code ADCy / AM / CE; other vectors Sand-Kala, Tse-Sleep, Rat-Plague, Dog-Rabies\n tests ELISA-HIV, Widal-\n→\n→\nTyphoid.”\nTOP 5: Aedes D-C-Y | Female Anopheles Malaria | Culex Filariasis | ELISA HIV vs Widal Typhoid | Ringworm = fungus, not worm."]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0446","t":"02 Chemistry Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / Science / Chemistry","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\nMATTER & STATES OF MATTER — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 1 · Matter + States + Solids + Mixtures + Separation + Mole Concept + Gas Laws\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 1 ke source mindmap se high-memory/high-confusion facts, values, classifications, separation\nmethods aur gas-law formulas ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Matter — Mass + Space\n• Matter = anything that has mass and occupies space\n• Matter molecules aur atoms se bana hota hai\n• Source examples: Water, Air, Iron\n• Main particle properties: interstitial space, constant motion, intermolecular attraction\nTRICK - “Matter = MASS + SPACE”\nHas mass + occupies space.\n2. Physical vs Chemical Classification\nClassification\nTypes\nPhysical\nSolid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, BEC\nChemical\nPure substance\n Element/Compound; Mixture\n\n→\n→\nHomogeneous/Heterogeneous\nTRICK - “Physical = 5 States; Chemical = Pure vs Mixture”\nPure substance = Element + Compound.\nMixture = Homogeneous + Heterogeneous.\n3. Earth Crust + Atmosphere — O-S / N-O\nRegion\nSource Composition\nEarth crust\nOxygen 46.8%; Silicon 27.7%; Aluminium 8%; Iron 5%; others\nAtmosphere\nNitrogen 78%; Oxygen 21%; CO₂\n 0.03%\n≈\nTRICK - “Crust = O-S; Air = N-O”\nCrust: Oxygen first, Silicon second.\nAtmosphere: Nitrogen first, Oxygen second.\nEXAM TRAP - “46.8 - 27.7 / 78 - 21”\nCrust O-S / Atmosphere N-O number chain.\n4. Five States — S-L-G-P-B\nState\nShape / Volume / Force\nSource Hook\nSolid\nDefinite shape + volume; strong IMF\nNegligible compressibility\nLiquid\nNo definite shape; definite volume\nMore compressible than solid\nGas\nNo definite shape/volume; weak IMF\nHigh compressibility\nPlasma\nIonised gas\n4th state; Sun & stars\nBEC\nNear absolute zero\n5th state\nTRICK - “S-L-G-P-B = 1-2-3-4-5”\nPlasma = 4th; BEC = 5th.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPlasma 4th, BEC 5th — reverse mat karna."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\n5. BEC — Bose + Einstein + Cornell\n• Source: BEC concept/discovery = Satyendra Nath Bose + Albert Einstein (1924)\n• Formed by dilute gas of bosons near absolute zero: 0 K = -273°C\n• Source: Eric Cornell (2001) experimentally created BEC using Rubidium-85 and Nobel reference\nTRICK - “Bose-Einstein 1924; Cornell 2001; Rb-85”\nBEC memory chain: B-E / C / Rb.\n6. Phase Changes — M-F-V-C-S-D\nChange\nProcess\nExample\nSolid\n Liquid\n→\nMelting / Fusion\nIce\n Water\n→\nLiquid\n Solid\n→\nFreezing\nWater\n Ice\n→\nLiquid\n Gas\n→\nVaporisation\nWater\n Steam\n→\nGas\n Liquid\n→\nCondensation\nSteam\n Water; dew/fog/mist\n→\nSolid\n Gas\n→\nSublimation\nCamphor, Dry Ice, Naphthalene\nGas\n Solid\n→\nDeposition\nFrost formation\nTRICK - “M-F-V-C-S-D”\nMelting-Freezing-Vaporisation-Condensation-Sublimation-Deposition.\nEXAM TRAP - “Sublime = C-D-N-I”\nCamphor - Dry Ice - Naphthalene - Iodine.\n7. Evaporation + Boiling Point\nFactor\nEvaporation Rate\nSurface area ↑\nIncreases\nWind speed ↑\nIncreases\nTemperature ↑\nIncreases\nHumidity ↑\nDecreases\nTRICK - “S-W-T UP\n Evap UP; Humidity UP\n Evap DOWN”\n→\n→\nHumidity opposite direction mein kaam karti hai.\n• Water boiling point at sea level = 100°C\n• Altitude\n\n pressure\n\n boiling point\n↑→\n↓→\n↓\n• Sea water boiling point > normal water because dissolved salts\n• Pressure cooker: pressure\n\n boiling point\n↑→\n↑\nEXAM TRAP - “Altitude LOWERS BP; Pressure Cooker RAISES BP”\nPressure-direction trap.\n8. Crystalline vs Amorphous\nFeature\nCrystalline\nAmorphous\nStructure\nRegular / ordered\nRandom / disordered\nShape\nDefinite geometrical\nIndefinite\nMelting point\nSharp\nRange, not sharp\nDirection property\nAnisotropic\nIsotropic\nExamples\nQuartz, NaCl, Ice\nGlass, Plastic, Rubber\nTRICK - “Crystal = A-S; Amorphous = I-R”\nCrystalline = Anisotropic + Sharp MP.\nAmorphous = Isotropic + Range of MP."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\nEXAM TRAP - “Glass Amorphous; Quartz Crystalline”\nDono source mein SiO₂ forms ke contrast ke roop mein diye gaye hain.\n9. Crystalline Solids — I-M-C-M\nType\nExample\nBonding / Property\nIonic\nNaCl\nElectron transfer; high MP; brittle; molten\nconductor\nMolecular\nIce\nWeak intermolecular force; low MP; soft; poor\nconductor\nCovalent\nDiamond\nCovalent network; very hard; very high MP; non-\nconductor\nMetallic\nAg, Fe\nSea of free electrons; conductor; ductile; malleable;\nlustrous\nTRICK - “I-M-C-M = NaCl - Ice - Diamond - Ag/Fe”\nIonic-Molecular-Covalent-Metallic.\nEXAM TRAP - “Diamond = Covalent; NaCl = Ionic”\nMolecular solids source table mein lowest MP due weak forces.\n10. Element vs Compound vs Pure Substance\nConcept\nSource Recall\nElement\nOne kind of particle; cannot be broken into simpler substances; Fe, Cu,\nAu, O₂, H₂\nCompound\nTwo or more elements in fixed ratio; definite proportions; H₂O, NaCl,\nCaCO₃\nPure Substance\nFixed composition + characteristic properties; includes elements +\ncompounds\nTRICK - “Element = One; Compound = Fixed Combo; Pure = E + C”\nCompound components fixed ratio mein.\n11. Mass Terms + Mole Concept\nItem\nSource Value / Formula\n1 amu\n1.66056 × 10^-24 g\nMolecular mass H₂O\n18.02 amu\nEquivalent weight\nMolecular weight / Valency\nMass %\nMass solute ×100 / Total mass solution\nNo. of moles\nMass(g) / Molecular or Atomic Weight\n1 mole gas at STP\n22.4 L\nAvogadro number\n6.022 × 10^23 particles\nTRICK - “Mole Triple = Gram Formula Weight + 22.4 L + 6.022×10²³”\nMass route, gas-volume route, particle-count route.\nEXAM TRAP - “H₂O = 18.02; amu = 1.66056×10^-24 g”\nNumber pair."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\n12. Mixtures — Homogeneous vs Heterogeneous\nFeature\nHomogeneous\nHeterogeneous\nComposition\nUniform\nNon-uniform\nParticle size\n< 1 nm\n> 10 nm in source\nLight scattering\nNo\nTyndall effect\nFiltration\nCannot\nCan by filtration/settling\nExamples\nSugar/salt in water, air\nOil/soil/chalk in water\nTRICK - “HOMO = Hidden Particles, No Tyndall; HETERO = Tyndall”\nTrue solution homogeneous\n no scattering.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Tyndall = Milk-Fog-Smoke-Colloid”\nSource examples.\n13. Separation Methods — E-C-F-S-C-D-C-D\nMethod\nSource Example\nEvaporation\nSalt from water; dye from ink\nCentrifugation\nButter/cream from milk\nSeparating Funnel\nOil from water\nSublimation\nCamphor / naphthalene\nChromatography\nDrugs from blood; pigments\nDistillation\nHomogeneous mixture of two liquids\nCrystallisation\nSalt from sea water; purifying sugar\nDecantation\nSand / insoluble particles from liquid\nTRICK - “Butter-CENTRI; Oil-FUNNEL; Pigment-CHROMA; Sea Salt-CRYSTAL”\nFour highest-yield separation pairs.\nEXAM TRAP - “Salt from Sea Water = Crystallisation”\nSource explicitly marks this against distillation/evaporation confusion.\n14. Physical vs Chemical Change\nType\nCore\nExamples\nPhysical\nNo new substance; usually reversible\nMelting ice, breaking pencil, tearing paper, boiling\nwater\nChemical\nNew substance; mostly irreversible\nBurning sawdust, curd formation, rusting, cooking\nTRICK - “Physical = Form Changes; Chemical = New Substance”\nP = physical form/state; C = chemical identity change.\nEXAM TRAP - “Candle = BOTH”\nWax melts = physical; wax burns to CO₂ + H₂O = chemical."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\n15. Gas Laws — B-C-G-D\nLaw\nYear\nRelation\nConstant\nBoyle\n1622\nP 1/V; P₁V₁=P₂V₂\n∝\nT, n\nCharles\n1787\nV T; V/T = constant\n∝\nP, n\nGay-Lussac\n1809\nP T; P/T = constant\n∝\nV, n\nDalton\n—\nPtotal = PA + PB + PC + ...\nPartial pressures\nTRICK - “Boyle P-V; Charles V-T; Gay P-T”\nMissing pair tells constant:\nBoyle P-V\n T constant; Charles V-T\n P constant; Gay P-T\n V constant.\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “1622 - 1787 - 1809”\nBoyle - Charles - Gay-Lussac year chain.\nTRICK - “Dalton = Total Pressure = Sum of Partial Pressures”\nPtotal = PA + PB + PC + ...\n16. Ideal Gas — Master Formula\n• Ideal gas source assumption: intermolecular attraction negligible\n• State variables: P, V, T, amount n\n• Combined ideal gas equation: PV = nRT\nTRICK - “Boyle + Charles + Gay\n PV = nRT”\n→\nIdeal-gas master equation.\n17. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Plasma = 4th state; BEC = 5th\n• BEC source chain = Bose & Einstein 1924; Cornell 2001; Rubidium-85\n• Crystalline = anisotropic + sharp MP; amorphous = isotropic + MP range\n• Glass = amorphous; Quartz = crystalline\n• Diamond = covalent; NaCl = ionic\n• Crust: Oxygen first, Silicon second; atmosphere: Nitrogen first\n• Humidity\n\n evaporation\n↑→\n↓\n• Tyndall effect: source ties it to heterogeneous/colloidal mixtures; true solution no Tyndall\n• Butter from milk = centrifugation\n• Salt from sea water = crystallisation\n• Burning candle = both physical + chemical\n• Boyle PV; Charles V/T; Gay P/T\nEXAM TRAP - “P/BEC - Crystal/Glass - Diamond/NaCl - Crust/Air - Humidity - Tyndall - Butter - SeaSalt - Candle -\nGas Laws”\nChapter ke highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Matter & States of Matter\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Matter = mass+space, particles have gaps+motion+attraction\n Physical S-L-G-P-B, Plasma4 BEC5; BEC Bose-Einstein1924,\n→\nCornell2001 Rb-85\n Crust O46.8-Si27.7; atmosphere N78-O21\n phase M-F-V-C-S-D; sublimation C-D-N-I; evaporation SWT\n but\n→\n→\n↑\nhumidity\nrate\n; altitude pressure\n BP\n, cooker pressure\n BP\n\n Solids: crystalline anisotropic+sharp MP vs amorphous\n↑→\n↓\n↓\n↓\n↑\n↑→\nisotropic+range; Glass amorphous, Quartz crystalline; crystalline I-M-C-M = NaCl-Ice-Diamond-Ag/Fe\n Chemical class: Element one,\n→\nCompound fixed ratio, Pure=E+C\n Mole: 1amu1.66056×10^-24g, H2O18.02amu, 1mol STP22.4L, Avogadro6.022×10^23\n Mixture:\n→\n→\nHomo uniform <1nm no Tyndall; Hetero nonuniform source>10nm + Tyndall; Milk/Fog/Smoke colloid\n Separation: Butter-centri,\n→\nOil-funnel, Pigment-chroma, SeaSalt-crystal; Candle BOTH physical+chemical\n Gas laws: Boyle1622 PV/Tconst; Charles1787\n→\nV/T/Pconst; Gay1809 P/T/Vconst; Dalton partial pressures; ideal PV=nRT.”\nTOP 5: Plasma4/BEC5 | Crystal anisotropic vs Amorphous isotropic | 22.4 L + 6.022×10^23 | Butter-centri/SeaSalt-crystal | Boyle-Charles-\nGay = PV / V-T / P-T."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Atomic Structure\nATOMIC STRUCTURE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 2 · Laws + Atomic Models + Particles + Isotopes + Quantum Numbers + Electronic Configuration\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 2 ke source mindmap se discoverers, years, atomic models, particle values, iso-terms, quantum\nnumbers aur electronic-configuration rules ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Atom — Democritus + Kanada + Dalton\n• Atom word Greek origin se: indivisible\n• Source: atom concept discoverer = Democritus\n• Maharishi Kanada ne atom ko indestructible kaha\n• Dalton Atomic Theory = 1808\nTRICK - “D-K-D = Democritus - Kanada - Dalton”\nDemocritus = atom concept; Kanada = indestructible; Dalton = atomic theory 1808.\n2. Chemical Laws — L-P-D\nLaw\nScientist\nYear\nMemory\nConservation of Mass\nAntoine Lavoisier\n1789\nReactant mass = Product mass\nDefinite/Constant Proportion\nJoseph Proust\n1799\nSame compound = same mass ratio\nMultiple Proportion\nDalton\n1803\nSmall whole-number ratio\nTRICK - “L-P-D = 1789-1799-1803”\nLavoisier\n Conservation.\n→\nProust\n Definite/Constant.\n→\nDalton\n Multiple.\n→\nTRICK - “Water H:O = 1:8; CO/CO₂ O-mass = 1:2”\nProust example 1:8; Dalton example 1:2.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDefinite Proportion = Constant Proportion; Multiple Proportion is Dalton, not Proust.\n3. Atomic Models — D-T-R-B Timeline\nModel\nYear\nKey Idea\nDalton\n1808\nAtoms indivisible; same element same\nmass/properties\nThomson\n1898\nWatermelon / Plum Pudding; e- embedded in\npositive sphere\nRutherford\n1911\nNuclear model; most atom empty; nucleus has\npositive charge + most mass\nBohr\n1913\nFixed K-L-M-N orbits; fixed energy; quanta on\ntransitions\nTRICK - “D-T-R-B = 1808-1898-1911-1913”\nDalton\n Thomson\n Rutherford\n Bohr.\n→\n→\n→\nTRICK - “Thomson = Watermelon; Rutherford = Nuclear; Bohr = KLMN”\nThree model labels ko ek chain mein lock karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nRutherford gold-foil alpha scattering; Bohr based on Planck quantum theory."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Atomic Structure\n4. Rutherford Model — Empty Space + Nucleus\n• Most alpha particles pass through\n atom mostly empty space\n→\n• Positive charge + most mass nucleus mein concentrated\n• Electrons and nucleus electrostatic force se bound\n• Alpha particle nucleus hit kare\n repelled\n→\nTRICK - “Rutherford = EMPTY + NUCLEUS”\nGold-foil alpha scattering ka core conclusion.\n5. Stable Particles — NEP\nParticle\nDiscoverer / Year\nCharge\nMass\nLocation\nElectron\nJ.J. Thomson 1897\n-1.6022×10^-19 C\n9.1095×10^-31 kg\nOutside nucleus\nProton\nRutherford 1919\n+1.6022×10^-19 C\n1.672×10^-27 kg\nInside nucleus\nNeutron\nJames Chadwick 1932\n0\n1.675×10^-27 kg\nInside nucleus\nTRICK - “NEP = Neutron-Chadwick, Electron-Thomson, Proton-Rutherford”\nNotice\n Neutron\n Chadwick.\n→\n→\nEvery\n Electron\n Thomson.\n→\n→\nParticle\n Proton\n Rutherford.\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “e mass = 1/1836 of proton”\nProton mass\n neutron mass.\n≈\n6. Millikan + Hydrogen + Nucleons\n• R.A. Millikan Oil Drop experiment = 1909\n• Electron charge = 1.602×10^-19 C\n• Hydrogen nucleus = only proton, no neutron — source special note\n• Protons + Neutrons inside nucleus = Nucleons\n• De-Broglie: particles have dual nature = wave + particle\nEXAM TRAP - “Millikan = Charge; Thomson = Electron”\nDiscovery of electron vs measurement of charge ko mix mat karo.\n7. Unstable Particles — P-M-N-Ap-An\nParticle\nDiscoverer\nYear\nSource Mass Hook\nPositron\nC.D. Anderson\n1932\n= electron mass\nMeson\nYukawa\n1935\n200× electron mass\nNeutrino\nPauli\n1927\nIndefinite\nAnti-Proton\nSegre\n1955\n= proton mass\nAnti-Neutron\nCork\n1956\n= neutron mass\nTRICK - “Pauli 1927 Neutrino; Anderson 1932 Positron; Yukawa 1935 Meson”\nEarly unstable-particle year chain.\n8. Atomic Number vs Mass Number — Z vs A\nSymbol\nMeaning\nFormula\nZ\nAtomic Number\nZ = P = e- in neutral atom\nA\nMass Number\nA = P + N\nN\nNeutrons\nN = A - Z"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Atomic Structure\nTRICK - “Z = Proton; A = All Nucleons”\nNeutral atom mein Z = proton = electron.\nA = proton + neutron.\nTRICK - “Carbon: Z6, A12\n P6, e6, N6”\n→\nFast worked example.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMass number A = P+N, NOT electrons.\n9. Iso-Family — Z-A-N-e\nType\nSame\nDifferent\nExample\nIsotopes\nZ\nA\n1H, 2H, 3H\nIsobars\nA\nZ\nAr-40, K-40, Ca-40\nIsotones\nN\nZ and A\nH-3 and He-4: source says both 2\nneutrons\nIsoelectronic\nElectrons\nZ\nNe, Na+, Mg2+, Al3+ = 10 e-\nTRICK - “IsoTOPE = same Z; IsoBAR = same A; IsoTONE = same N”\nT-Z / B-A / Tone-N.\nTRICK - “IsoELECTRONIC = Same e-”\nNe, Na+, Mg2+, Al3+\n 10 electrons.\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nIsotope same Z; Isobar same A; Isotone same N — classic swap trap.\n10. Special Isotope Facts — Source Recall\n• Hydrogen isotopes: Protium 1H, Deuterium 2H, Tritium 3H\n• Source states Tritium (3H) = lightest isotope and radioactive\n• Source states heaviest stable isotope = Lead-208\n• Source states element with most isotopes = Polonium (Po)\nEXAM TRAP - “H = P-D-T; T Radioactive; Pb-208 Heavy Stable; Po Most”\nYe source-note special-fact chain hai.\n11. Four Quantum Numbers — n-l-m-s\nQuantum No.\nMeaning\nValues\nn Principal\nEnergy level + distance\n1,2,3,4... = K,L,M,N\nl Azimuthal\nOrbital shape\n0 to n-1; s0 p1 d2 f3\nm Magnetic\nOrientation\n-l to +l\ns Spin\nElectron spin direction\n+1/2 or -1/2\nTRICK - “n-l-m-s = Level-Shape-Orientation-Spin”\nn = level; l = shape; m = orientation; s = spin.\nEXAM TRAP - “s-p-d-f = 0-1-2-3”\nAzimuthal quantum number values."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Atomic Structure\n12. Shell Capacity — 2n²\nShell\nn\nMax e-\nK\n1\n2\nL\n2\n8\nM\n3\n18\nN\n4\n32\nTRICK - “K-L-M-N = 2-8-18-32”\nFormula = 2n².\n13. Aufbau — Lower Energy First\n• Aufbau = German “construction/building up”\n• Electrons fill lower-energy orbitals first\n• Source order: 1s < 2s < 2p < 3s < 3p < 4s < 3d < 4p < 5s < 4d < 5p < 6s < 4f < 5d\nEXAM TRAP - “4s BEFORE 3d”\nAufbau ka most common exam trap.\n14. Cr & Cu — Aufbau Exceptions\nElement\nExpected\nActual\nWhy\nCr 24\n3d4 4s2\n3d5 4s1\nHalf-filled d more stable\nCu 29\n3d9 4s2\n3d10 4s1\nFully-filled d more stable\nTRICK - “Cr = d5s1; Cu = d10s1”\nHalf-filled / fully-filled stability.\n15. Pauli vs Hund\nRule\nCore\nPauli Exclusion\nNo two electrons have identical 4 quantum numbers; max 2 e-/orbital;\nopposite spins\nHund Maximum Multiplicity\nEqual-energy orbitals fill singly first, then pairing\nTRICK - “Pauli = Pair Opposite; Hund = Single First”\nPauli limits an orbital to 2 opposite-spin electrons.\nHund says spread first, pair later.\nEXAM TRAP - “p3 =\n\n\n ; p6 =\n\n\n”\n↑↑↑\n↑↓↑↓↑↓\nHalf-filled and fully-filled patterns.\n16. Discoverer + Year Flash\nFact\nPerson\nYear\nConservation Mass\nLavoisier\n1789\nDefinite Proportion\nProust\n1799\nMultiple Proportion\nDalton\n1803\nAtomic Theory\nDalton\n1808\nElectron\nJ.J. Thomson\n1897\nThomson Model\nJ.J. Thomson\n1898\nMillikan Oil Drop\nR.A. Millikan\n1909\nRutherford Model\nRutherford\n1911\nBohr Model\nNiels Bohr\n1913\nProton\nRutherford\n1919\nNeutron\nJames Chadwick\n1932"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Atomic Structure\nTRICK - “1789-99-1803 / 1897-98 / 1909-11-13-19-32”\nLaws\n Thomson\n Millikan/Rutherford/Bohr/Proton/Neutron.\n→\n→\n17. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Thomson = Watermelon/Plum Pudding, not nuclear model\n• Rutherford = nuclear model + source proton discovery 1919\n• Bohr = fixed K-L-M-N orbits; based on Planck quantum theory\n• Electron = Thomson 1897; electron charge = Millikan 1909\n• Electron mass = 1/1836 proton mass\n• Hydrogen source special note: no neutron\n• Atomic number Z = protons; mass number A = P+N\n• Isotope same Z; Isobar same A; Isotone same N\n• Source special: most isotopes = Polonium; heaviest stable = Pb-208\n• Quantum numbers n-l-m-s = level-shape-orientation-spin\n• Aufbau: 4s before 3d; Cr/Cu exceptions\n• Pauli = max 2 opposite spins; Hund = single first\nEXAM TRAP - “Thomson-Rutherford-Bohr-Millikan-1836-H-Z/A-Iso-Po/Pb-nlms-4s/CrCu-Pauli/Hund”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Atom: Democritus concept, Kanada indestructible, Dalton1808\n Laws L-P-D = Lavoisier1789 Conservation, Proust1799\n→\nDefinite/Constant, Dalton1803 Multiple\n Models D-T-R-B = 1808/1898/1911/1913: Thomson Watermelon, Rutherford Nuclear via\n→\nalpha-gold foil, Bohr KLMN + quanta\n Particles NEP: Neutron-Chadwick1932, Electron-Thomson1897, Proton-Rutherford1919; e\n→\ncharge1.602×10^-19C, e mass1/1836 proton; Millikan1909 charge; H nucleus no neutron, P+N=Nucleons\n Z=P=e(neutral), A=P+N,\n→\nN=A-Z\n Iso: isotope sameZ, isobar sameA, isotone sameN, isoelectronic same e; H=P-D-T, source T radioactive, Pb208 heavy stable,\n→\nPo most isotopes\n Quantum n-l-m-s = level-shape-orientation-spin; s-p-d-f=0-1-2-3; shell 2n² = K2 L8 M18 N32\n Aufbau lower-\n→\n→\nenergy first, 4s before3d; Cr3d5 4s1, Cu3d10 4s1 exceptions\n Pauli max2 opposite-spin per orbital; Hund single-first then pair.”\n→\nTOP 5: L-P-D laws | Thomson-Watermelon / Rutherford-Nuclear / Bohr-KLMN | NEP particle discoverers | Iso Z-A-N | 4s before 3d + Cr/Cu\nexceptions."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Periodic Classification of Elements\nPERIODIC CLASSIFICATION OF ELEMENTS — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 3 · Dobereiner + Newland + Mendeleev + Moseley + Groups/Periods + Blocks + Periodic Trends\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 3 ke source mindmap se scientists/years, old vs modern periodic table, groups-periods, s-p-d-f\nblocks aur periodic-property trends ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. History Timeline — D-N-M-M\nStage\nScientist\nYear\nBasis / Hook\nTriads\nWolfgang Dobereiner\n1829\nGroups of 3; atomic mass\nOctaves\nJohn Newland\n1864\nEvery 8th repeats; atomic mass\nPeriodic Table\nDmitri Mendeleev\n1869\nAtomic mass\nModern Table\nHenry Moseley\n1913\nAtomic number\nTRICK - “D-N-M-M = 1829-1864-1869-1913”\nDobereiner\n Newland\n Mendeleev\n Moseley.\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Mass-Mass-Mass\n Number”\n→\nDobereiner, Newland, Mendeleev = atomic mass; Modern/Moseley = atomic number.\n2. Dobereiner Triads — Middle = Average\n• Three elements with similar properties arranged by increasing atomic weight\n• Middle element mass\n average of outer two\n≈\n• Formula: Middle mass = (1st + 3rd)/2\n• Failed because all elements could not be fitted into triads\nTriad\nOuter Masses\nMiddle\nCheck\nLi-Na-K\n7 & 39\nNa 23\n(7+39)/2 = 23\nCa-Sr-Ba\n40 & 137\nSr 87.5\nAverage\n 88.5\n≈\nCl-Br-I\n35.5 & 127\nBr 80\nAverage\n 81.25\n≈\nTRICK - “Triad = THREE; Middle = MEAN”\nLi-Na-K sabse asked calculation.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDobereiner = triads of 3, not octaves of 8.\n3. Newland Octaves — Every 8th\n• John Newland, England, 1864\n• Elements increasing atomic mass mein arranged\n• Every 8th element properties repeat\n• Musical-note analogy: Sa-Re-Ga-Ma-Pa-Da-Ni\n• Applied only up to Calcium; 56 elements known\n• Source says noble-gas discovery ke baad scheme failed\nTRICK - “Newland = Note = 8”\nEvery 8th repeats; up to Calcium.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEvery 8th, not 7th or 9th; basis atomic mass, not atomic number."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Periodic Classification of Elements\n4. Mendeleev — 1869 / 63 / 7 / 9\nFact\nSource Recall\nYear\n1869\nKnown elements\n63\nPeriods\n7\nGroups\n9\nBasis\nAtomic mass\nNoble gas group\nAbsent; zero group absent\nHydrogen / Isotopes\nPosition not fixed\nTitle\nFather of Periodic Table\nTRICK - “Mendeleev = 63-7-9”\n63 elements, 7 periods, 9 groups.\nTRICK - “Mass + Missing Spaces”\nAtomic mass basis; blank spaces left for undiscovered elements.\n5. Eka Elements — B-A-S\n S-G-G\n→\nPredicted Name\nModern Element\nSymbol\nEka-Boron\nScandium\nSc (21)\nEka-Aluminium\nGallium\nGa (31)\nEka-Silicon\nGermanium\nGe (32)\nTRICK - “B-A-S\n S-G-G”\n→\nEka-Boron\nScandium; Eka-Aluminium\nGallium; Eka-Silicon\nGermanium.\n→\n→\n→\nTRICK - “Eka = Sanskrit ‘one’”\nOne step below in group — source note.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEka-Aluminium = Gallium; Eka-Silicon = Germanium.\n6. Mendeleev vs Modern\nFeature\nMendeleev 1869\nModern / Moseley 1913\nBasis\nAtomic Mass\nAtomic Number\nPeriods\n7\n7\nGroups\n9\n18\nElements\n63\n118\nNoble gases\nAbsent / zero group absent\nGroup 18\nH & Isotopes\nPosition not fixed\nFixed positions\nTRICK - “M = Mass + 9; Modern = Number + 18”\nMendeleev vs Moseley ka core contrast.\nEXAM TRAP -\nModern table is based on atomic NUMBER, not atomic mass.\n7. Modern Table — 118 / 18 / 7\n• Henry Moseley, 1913\n• Modern periodic law: properties are periodic function of atomic number\n• 118 elements, 18 groups, 7 periods\n• Source: 11 gaseous elements at normal atmospheric conditions"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Periodic Classification of Elements\nTRICK - “Modern = 118-18-7”\nElements-Groups-Periods.\n8. Important Groups — 1,2,15,16,17,18\nGroup\nName\nBlock\n1\nAlkali Metals\ns\n2\nAlkaline Earth Metals\ns\n3-12\nTransition Elements\nd\n15\nPnictogens\np\n16\nChalcogens\np\n17\nHalogens\np\n18\nNoble / Inert Gases\np\nTRICK - “1 Alkali, 2 Alkaline; 15 Pnic, 16 Chalc, 17 Halo, 18 Noble”\nGroup-name ladder.\nEXAM TRAP -\nNoble gases Group 18 = p-block, separate block nahi.\n9. Lanthanoids vs Actinoids\nSeries\nAtomic No.\nPeriod\nBlock\nSource Hook\nLanthanoids\n58-71\n6\nf\nInner transition; rare earth\nActinoids\n90-103\n7\nf\nInner transition; most\nradioactive/synthetic\nTRICK - “Lantha 58-71 / Acti 90-103”\nPeriod 6 / Period 7; both f-block.\nEXAM TRAP -\nf-block = Lanthanoids + Actinoids.\n10. Period Lengths — 2-8-8-18-18-32-32\nPeriod\nElements\nType / Orbitals\n1\n2\nVery short; 1s\n2\n8\nShort; 2s,2p\n3\n8\nShort; 3s,3p\n4\n18\nLong; 4s,3d,4p\n5\n18\nLong; 5s,4d,5p\n6\n32\nVery long; 6s,4f,5d,6p\n7\n32\nIncomplete; 7s,5f,6d,7p\nTRICK - “2-8-8-18-18-32-32”\nPeriods 1\n7 element-count chain.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Ti Z22 = Group 4, Period 4”\nSource specific placement fact.\n11. Blocks — s-p-d-f\nBlock\nGroups / Series\nExamples\ns\nGroups 1-2\nLi, Na, K, Mg, Ca\np\nGroups 13-18\nC, N, O, F, Cl, Ne\nd\nGroups 3-12\nFe, Cu, Zn, Cr, Ni\nf\nLanthanoids + Actinoids\nCe, Nd, U, Th"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Periodic Classification of Elements\nTRICK - “s 1-2; p 13-18; d 3-12; f inner”\nBlock-group master line.\nEXAM TRAP - “Hydrogen = s-block Group 1 but NON-METAL”\nSource special trap.\n12. Periodic Trends — Down vs Across\nProperty\nDown Group\nAcross Period →\nExtreme\nElectronegativity\nDecreases\nIncreases\nHighest F\nElectron Affinity\nDecreases\nIncreases\nHighest Cl\nAtomic Size\nIncreases\nDecreases\nLargest Cs; smallest F\nIonisation Energy\nDecreases\nIncreases\nNoble gases very high\nMetallic Character\nIncreases\nDecreases\nLose e- more easily down group\nTRICK - “Down: Size+Metal UP; EN-EA-IE DOWN”\nGroup down mnemonic.\nTRICK - “Across: Size+Metal DOWN; EN-EA-IE UP”\nPeriod across = mostly opposite.\nEXAM TRAP - “F = Electronegativity; Cl = Electron Affinity”\nMost common confusion pair.\n13. Valency + Noble Gas\n• Source: valency = number of electrons for bonding\n• Group elements have same valency pattern\n• Source says period across valency increases\n• Noble gases Group 18: zero valency + very high ionisation energy\n• Source says Groups 2, 15, 18 have zero or positive electron affinity\nTRICK - “Noble = 0 Valency + High IE”\nGroup 18 direct recall.\n14. Special Important Facts\nQuestion\nSource Answer\nSmallest Element\nH — Hydrogen\nLargest Element\nCs — Caesium\nLightest Metal\nLi — Lithium\nHighest Melting Point\nW — Tungsten\nMost Electronegative\nF — Fluorine\nHighest Electron Affinity\nCl — Chlorine\nFather of Periodic Table\nDmitri Mendeleev\nTRICK - “H-Cs-Li-W-F-Cl”\nSmallest-Largest-Lightest metal-Highest MP-Most EN-Highest EA.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLightest metal = Li, not H; H is non-metal."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Periodic Classification of Elements\n15. Comparison Flash — Person / Year / Basis\nPerson\nYear\nBasis\nGroup Hook\nDobereiner\n1829\nAtomic Mass / triads\n3-element sets\nNewland\n1864\nAtomic Mass / octaves\nEvery 8th\nMendeleev\n1869\nAtomic Mass\n9 groups\nMoseley\n1913\nAtomic Number\n18 groups\nTRICK - “1829-1864-1869-1913 = 3-8-9-18”\nTriads3\n Octaves8\n Mendeleev9 groups\n Modern18 groups.\n→\n→\n→\n16. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Dobereiner = 1829 triads; middle mass\n average of outer two\n≈\n• Newland = 1864; every 8th; only up to Calcium\n• Mendeleev = 1869, atomic mass, 9 groups, 63 elements\n• Moseley = 1913, atomic number, 18 groups, 118 elements\n• Eka-Aluminium = Gallium; Eka-Silicon = Germanium\n• Group 17 = Halogens; Group 18 = Noble gases\n• Noble gases are p-block\n• Lanthanoids 58-71; Actinoids 90-103\n• Period counts = 2-8-8-18-18-32-32\n• Most electronegative = F; highest electron affinity = Cl\n• Largest atom = Cs; source smallest non-noble = F\n• Lightest metal = Li; highest MP = W\nEXAM TRAP - “D-N-M-M / Eka / 17-18 / p / 58-71 90-103 / 2-8-8... / F-Cl / Cs-F / Li-W”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“History D-N-M-M = Dobereiner1829 triads3 middle=average\n Newland1864 octaves every8th up to Ca\n Mendeleev1869 atomic\n→\n→\nmass, 63 elements,7 periods,9 groups, no noble gas group, blank Eka spaces\n Moseley1913 atomic number,118 elements,18\n→\ngroups,7 periods\n Eka B-A-S\n Sc-Ga-Ge\n Groups:1 Alkali,2 Alkaline,3-12 Transition,15 Pnictogen,16 Chalcogen,17 Halogen,18\n→\n→\n→\nNoble\n f-block Lantha58-71 period6 + Acti90-103 period7; period count 2-8-8-18-18-32-32; blocks s1-2,p13-18,d3-12,f inner; H is s-\n→\nblock Group1 but non-metal\n Trends: down Size+Metal\n while EN/EA/IE\n; across opposite\n F highest electronegativity, Cl highest\n→\n↑\n↓\n→\n\nelectron affinity, Cs largest, source smallest F; Noble gases zero valency + high IE\n Specials H smallest element, Cs largest, Li lightest\n→\n\nmetal, W highest MP, Mendeleev father.”\nTOP 5: 1829-1864-1869-1913 | Mendeleev mass/9 vs Moseley number/18 | Eka B-A-S\nSc-Ga-Ge | s-p-d-f group ranges | F electronegativity\n→\nvs Cl electron affinity."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Chemical Bonds & Reactions\nCHEMICAL BONDS & REACTIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 4 · Bond Types + Sigma/Pi + Shapes + Oxidation No. + Reactions + Redox + Catalysts\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 4 ke source mindmap se bond properties, sigma/pi counts, molecular shapes, oxidation-number\nrules, reaction types, redox logic aur catalyst-process pairs ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Chemical Bond — Stability + Octet\n• Chemical bond = force of attraction between two or more atoms\n• Bond formation ka source reason: stability achieve karna, outermost orbit mein 8 electrons complete karna, potential energy\nreduce karna\n• Source lists 4 major bond types: Ionic, Covalent, Hydrogen, Coordinate\nTRICK - “Bond = Attraction + 8 + Stability”\nOuter shell octet complete\n inert-gas type stability.\n→\n2. Four Bond Types — I-C-H-Co\nBond\nFormation\nExamples\nKey Property\nIonic\nElectron transfer\nNaCl, MgO\nWater soluble; solid bad conductor,\naqueous/molten good\nCovalent\nElectron sharing\nO2, H2O\nUsually water-insoluble; poor\nconductor\nHydrogen\nH with N/O/F\nH2O, NH3, DNA\nWater high BP; DNA H-bonds\nCoordinate\nBoth shared e- from same atom\nH2SO4, H3O+\nDative bond\nTRICK - “I Transfer; C Share; H = N-O-F; Coordinate = Same Donor”\nI-C-H-Co ka formation code.\nEXAM TRAP - “Ionic: Solid BAD, Solution GOOD”\nAqueous/molten ionic compound conducts; solid does not.\n3. Ionic Bond — Cation + Anion\n• One atom loses electron\n cation (+); other gains electron\n anion (-)\n→\n→\n• Na gives 1e- and Cl takes 1e-\n NaCl\n→\n• Mg gives 2e- and O takes 2e-\n MgO\n→\n• High melting point; soluble in water\nTRICK - “Lose = Plus; Gain = Minus”\nElectron loss\n cation; electron gain\n anion.\n→\n→\n4. Covalent Bond — Share + Exceptions\n• Usually non-metals share electron pairs\n• O2 = non-polar covalent (same atoms)\n• H2O = polar covalent (different atoms)\n• Low melting/boiling point in source, exception Diamond\n• Poor conductor in source, exception Graphite\n• Soluble in organic solvents\nEXAM TRAP - “Covalent Exceptions = Diamond HIGH MP + Graphite CONDUCTS”\nD-G = two must-remember exceptions."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Chemical Bonds & Reactions\n5. Hydrogen Bond — N-O-F with H\nType\nWhere\nExamples / Effect\nIntermolecular\nDifferent molecules\nH2O, NH3; high BP of water\nIntramolecular\nSame molecule\nProtein, DNA, RNA, cellulose — as listed in\nsource\nTRICK - “H-Bond = H with N-O-F”\nSource trap: NOT Cl or S.\nEXAM TRAP - “Water High BP + DNA Double Helix = H-Bond”\nHigh-frequency source facts.\n6. Coordinate + Van der Waals\n• Coordinate covalent/dative bond: shared pair ke dono electrons same donor atom se aate hain\n• Source examples: H2SO4 and hydronium H3O+\n• Van der Waals = weak intermolecular attraction/repulsion; chemical bonds se weaker\n• Noble gases ke liquid/solid-state properties mein role\nTRICK - “Coordinate = One Atom Gives BOTH”\nH3O+ is a source example.\n7. Sigma-Pi — 1 / 1+1 / 1+2\nBond\nComposition\nPi Count\nExamples\nSingle\n1 sigma\n0\nH2, CH4, H2O\nDouble\n1 sigma + 1 pi\n1\nO2, CO2, C2H4\nTriple\n1 sigma + 2 pi\n2\nN2, C2H2\nTRICK - “Single 10; Double 11; Triple 12”\nRead as sigma-pi counts: 1σ0π / 1σ1π / 1σ2π.\nEXAM TRAP - “Every Bond has Sigma; Pi only Double/Triple”\nTriple bond = 1σ + 2π, NOT 3σ.\n8. Molecular Shapes — W-A-M-C\nMolecule\nShape\nPolarity\nH2O\nAngular / V-shaped\nPolar\nNH3\nTrigonal pyramidal\nPolar\nCH4\nTetrahedral\nNon-polar\nCO2\nLinear\nNon-polar\nTRICK - “Water V; Ammonia Pyramid; Methane Tetra; CO2 Line”\nW-A-M-C shape chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “H2O Polar; CO2 Non-polar despite polar bonds”\nSource reason: CO2 symmetry.\n9. Valency — Fixed vs Variable\n• Valency = combining ability; electrons used/shared/transferred\n• Fluorine valency always -1; never positive in source\n• Groups IA and IIA: valency = group number (Frankland rule)"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Chemical Bonds & Reactions\n• Cl: 2,8,7\n -1; Na: 2,8,1\n +1\n→\n→\n• Fe, Cu, S, Hg, Sn = variable valency\nTRICK - “F = Always -1”\nMost electronegative; source says never positive.\nTRICK - “Cross-Multiply Valencies\n Formula”\n→\nAl(+3), Cl(-1)\n AlCl3.\n→\n10. Oxidation Number — H-O-F Rules\nSpecies\nUsual ON\nImportant Exception\nH\n+1\n-1 in metal hydrides: NaH, CaH2\nO\n-2\n-1 in H2O2; +2 in OF2; 0 in O2\nF\n-1\nAlways -1\nNa, K\n+1\nAlways +1\nMg, Ca, Sr\n+2\nAlways +2\n• Neutral molecule: sum of oxidation numbers = 0\n• Ion: sum of oxidation numbers = ion charge\n• Oxidation number can be positive, negative, zero or fractional\nTRICK - “H +1, O -2, F -1”\nExceptions: H metal hydride -1; O peroxide -1 / OF2 +2.\nEXAM TRAP -\nF always -1; O is NOT always -2.\n11. Nine Reaction Types — C-D-D-D-E-E-R-I-R\nType\nPattern / Source Hook\nCombination\nA + B\n C\n→\nDecomposition\nAB\n A + B; CaCO3\n CaO + CO2\n→\n→\nDisplacement\nAB + C\n AC + B; more reactive displaces less\n→\nDouble Displacement\nAB + CD\n AD + CB; ion exchange / precipitate\n→\nExothermic\nEnergy released; combustion, respiration\nEndothermic\nEnergy absorbed; digestion, photosynthesis, photochemical\nReversible\nBoth directions; equilibrium\nIrreversible\nOne direction; completion\nRedox\nOxidation + reduction simultaneously\nTRICK - “C-D-D-D-E-E-R-I-R = 9 Reaction Types”\nCombination, Decomposition, Displacement, Double-displacement, Exo, Endo, Reversible, Irreversible, Redox.\nEXAM TRAP - “Respiration EXO; Photosynthesis ENDO”\nEnergy released vs absorbed.\n12. Redox — OIL RIG\nProcess\nElectron\nOxidation No.\nOther Source Clues\nOxidation\nLoss\nIncreases\nGain O/electronegative; lose\nH/electropositive\nReduction\nGain\nDecreases\nGain H/electropositive; lose\nO/electronegative\nTRICK - “OIL RIG”\nOxidation Is Loss; Reduction Is Gain (of electrons)."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Chemical Bonds & Reactions\nEXAM TRAP - “Oxidising Agent gets REDUCED; Reducing Agent gets OXIDISED”\nAgent apne naam ka kaam dusre par karata hai.\n13. Redox Example + Agents\n• Fe + CuSO4\n FeSO4 + Cu\n→\n• Fe: 0\n +2 = oxidised\n→\n• Cu2+: +2\n 0 = reduced\n→\nAgent Type\nSource Examples\nOxidising agents\nH2O2, O2, F2, KMnO4\nReducing agents\nLi, Na, NaBH4, H2\nEXAM TRAP - “H2O2 = BOTH”\nSource says H2O2 can act as both oxidising and reducing agent.\n14. Catalyst — Berzelius + Same/Different State\n• Catalyst increases reaction rate without being consumed\n• Discoverer in source = Berzelius\n• Homogeneous catalysis = catalyst + reactants same physical state\n• Heterogeneous catalysis = different physical states\n• Positive catalyst increases rate; negative catalyst decreases rate\nTRICK - “Catalyst = Rate Change, Not Consumed; Berzelius”\nHomogeneous SAME state; Heterogeneous DIFFERENT state.\n15. Process-Catalyst Master Table\nProcess\nCatalyst / Source Note\nGhee from vegetable oil\nNickel (Ni)\nContact method - H2SO4\nPt powder, V2O5; source highlights V2O5 as most asked\nDeacon process - Cl2\nCupric chloride (CuCl2)\nProtein\n Amino acids\n→\nErepsin enzyme\nVinegar from sugar\nMycoderma aceti\nMilk\n Curd\n→\nLactobacilli (Lactose)\nHaber process - NH3\nFe catalyst + Mo promoter\nTRICK - “Ghee-Ni / Contact-V2O5 / Curd-Lacto / Haber-Fe+Mo”\nFour highest-frequency catalyst pairs.\nEXAM TRAP - “Haber ≠ Contact”\nHaber = Fe + Mo; Contact H2SO4 = V2O5."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Chemical Bonds & Reactions\n16. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Ionic solid = bad conductor; aqueous/molten = good conductor\n• Diamond = covalent but hard/high MP; Graphite = covalent but conducts\n• H-bond only source pair with N/O/F and H\n• DNA double helix held by H-bonds\n• Triple bond = 1σ + 2π, not 3σ\n• H2O V-shaped; CO2 linear\n• F oxidation number always -1; O usually -2 but -1 in H2O2\n• Respiration exothermic; photosynthesis endothermic\n• Displacement: more reactive displaces less reactive\n• Oxidation = electron loss + ON increase; Reduction = electron gain + ON decrease\n• Oxidising agent gets reduced; reducing agent gets oxidised\n• Haber = Fe + Mo; Contact process = V2O5\nEXAM TRAP - “Ionic-D/G-Hbond-Triple-Shapes-F/O-Exo/Endo-Displace-OILRIG-Agents-Haber/Contact”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Bond = attraction + octet stability\n I-C-H-Co: Ionic transfer NaCl/MgO solid bad but solution good; Covalent share O2/H2O with\n→\nDiamond high-MP + Graphite conductor exceptions; H-bond H with N-O-F, water high BP + DNA; Coordinate same atom gives both\nelectrons, H3O+/H2SO4\n Sigma/Pi: single1σ, double1σ1π, triple1σ2π\n Shapes H2O V polar, NH3 pyramidal polar, CH4 tetra non-\n→\n→\npolar, CO2 linear non-polar\n Valency F always-1, variable Fe/Cu/S/Hg/Sn; ON H+1 except hydrides-1, O-2 except peroxide-1/OF2+2,\n→\nF-1 always; neutral sum0, ion sum=charge\n Reactions 9: C-D-D-D-E-E-R-I-R; Respiration exo, Photosynthesis endo; displacement\n→\nmore reactive kicks less; double-displacement ion exchange/precipitate\n Redox OIL RIG: oxidation loss e-/ON\n, reduction gain\n→\n↑\ne-/ON\n; oxidiser gets reduced, reducer gets oxidised; Fe\nFe2+ oxidised, Cu2+\nCu reduced; H2O2 both\n Catalyst Berzelius; Homo\n↓\n→\n→\n→\nsame-state, Hetero different-state; Ghee-Ni, Contact-V2O5, Deacon-CuCl2, Protein-Erepsin, Vinegar-Mycoderma aceti, Curd-\nLactobacilli, Haber Fe+Mo.”\nTOP 5: Ionic solid bad/solution good | Diamond vs Graphite exceptions | Triple=1σ+2π | OIL RIG + agents reverse | Haber Fe+Mo vs\nContact V2O5."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Solution & Colloid\nSOLUTION & COLLOID — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 5 · Solutions + Saturation + Colloid + Suspension + Tyndall + Emulsion + Buffer\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 5 ke source mindmap se particle-size ranges, solution types, saturation-temperature effects,\nSolution–Colloid–Suspension differences, Tyndall effect, colloid applications, emulsions aur buffer facts ko fast exam-recall format\nmein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Solution Basics — Less + More = Solution\n• Solution = homogeneous mixture of two or more substances\n• Solute = dissolved substance; usually less quantity\n• Solvent = dissolving medium; usually more quantity\n• Universal solvent = Water (H2O)\n• Source examples: solute = sugar/salt/NaCl; solvent = water/alcohol/acetone\nTRICK - “Solute LESS + Solvent MORE = Solution”\nUniversal Solvent = Water.\n2. Particle Size Master — <1 / 1–1000 / >1000 nm\nSystem\nParticle Size\nNature\nTyndall\nVisible?\nSeparation\nTrue Solution\n< 1 nm\nHomogeneous\nNo\nNo\nNot by filtration\nColloid\n1–1000 nm\nAppears homogeneous;\nactually heterogeneous\nYes\nNo\nCentrifugation\nSuspension\n> 1000 nm\nHeterogeneous\nYes\nYes\nFiltration\nTRICK - “1 / 1000 Border Rule”\nTrue Solution <1 nm\n Colloid 1–1000 nm\n Suspension >1000 nm.\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Tyndall = Colloid + Suspension; NOT True Solution”\nVisible to naked eye = Suspension only.\n3. Solution Types — Solute in Solvent\nSolution\nSolute\nSolvent\nSource Example\nSolid Solution\nGas\nSolid\nH2 absorbed in Palladium\nSolid Solution\nLiquid\nSolid\nMercury amalgam with Sodium\nSolid Solution\nSolid\nSolid\nZn in Cu = Brass / alloys\nLiquid Solution\nGas\nLiquid\nO2 in water\nLiquid Solution\nLiquid\nLiquid\nAlcohol in water\nLiquid Solution\nSolid\nLiquid\nSugar in water\nGaseous Solution\nGas\nGas\nAir\nGaseous Solution\nLiquid\nGas\nChloroform + N2 = Fog\nGaseous Solution\nSolid\nGas\nCamphor + N2 = Smoke\nTRICK - “Pd-H2 = Gas in Solid; Amalgam = Liquid in Solid; Air = Gas in Gas”\nThree high-frequency type examples.\nEXAM TRAP - “Fog = Liquid in Gas; Smoke = Solid in Gas”\nO2 in water = Gas in Liquid.\n4. Saturated vs Unsaturated\nFeature\nSaturated\nUnsaturated\nAt given T & P\nMaximum solute dissolved\nMore solute can dissolve\nExtra solute\nRemains undissolved\nCan still dissolve\nTemperature ↑\nBecomes unsaturated\nCan dissolve more\nTemperature ↓\nCapacity falls\nCan become saturated"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Solution & Colloid\nTRICK - “Temp UP\n Saturated becomes UNSATURATED”\n→\nMore solute can dissolve after temperature increase.\nEXAM TRAP - “Temp DOWN\n Unsaturated can become SATURATED”\n→\nSolubility capacity decreases.\n• Most solids: solubility increases with temperature\n• Gases in liquids: solubility decreases with temperature\n• Source example: carbonated drinks go flat when warm; O2 solubility in water falls as temperature rises\n5. Solid vs Gas Solubility — Opposite Trend\nSolute Type\nTemperature ↑\nMost solids in liquid\nSolubility ↑\nGases in liquid\nSolubility ↓\nEXAM TRAP - “Solid Likes Heat; Gas Escapes Heat”\nMost solids\n solubility; dissolved gases\n solubility.\n↑\n↓\n6. True Solution vs Colloid vs Suspension\nFeature\nTrue Solution\nColloid\nSuspension\nNature\nHomogeneous\nPseudo-homogeneous / actually\nheterogeneous\nHeterogeneous\nParticle\n<1 nm\n1–1000 nm\n>1000 nm\nTyndall\nNo\nYes\nYes\nNaked eye\nNo\nNo\nYes\nSeparation\nNot by filtration\nCentrifugation\nFiltration\nExamples\nSugar/salt water\nMilk, Ink, Blood, Fog, Smoke\nChalk/Mud in water\nTRICK - “Solution-COLLOID-Suspension = No / CENTRI / FILTER”\nTrue solution not by filtration; colloid centrifugation; suspension filtration.\nEXAM TRAP - “Milk = Colloid, NOT True Solution”\nMilk separated by centrifugation to obtain butter/cream.\n7. Tyndall Effect — Light Scattering\n• Tyndall effect = scattering of a beam of light by colloidal particles\n• Observed in Colloid + Suspension; NOT in True Solution\n• Source examples: sunlight beam in dusty room; headlights in fog\n• Source states blue colour of sky = Tyndall effect because shorter-wavelength blue light scatters more\nTRICK - “Tyndall = Light SCATTER by Colloid”\nHeadlights + Fog; Dusty-room sunlight.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource framing: Blue colour of sky = Tyndall Effect, not reflection."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Solution & Colloid\n8. Colloid Applications — S-C-B-R-D\nApplication\nSource Recall\nSmoke precipitation\nRemoving smoke from chimneys\nCleaning clothes\nDetergent action\nBlood clotting\nFeCl3 as coagulant\nRain formation\nCloud colloids coagulate around dust\nDelta formation\nRiver silt colloid coagulated by sea salt\nTRICK - “S-C-B-R-D = Smoke-Cleaning-Blood-Rain-Delta”\nColloid applications chain.\nTRICK - “Delta = Sea Salt Coagulates River Silt”\nRiver-sea junction exam point.\nEXAM TRAP - “Blood + FeCl3 = Coagulation”\nSource says FeCl3 can stop bleeding.\n9. Emulsion — Two Immiscible Liquids\n• Emulsion = colloidal system of two immiscible liquids\n• All emulsions are colloids; source particle range 1–1000 nm\nType\nMeaning\nExamples\nO/W\nOil droplets in water\nMilk, Mayonnaise, Vanishing cream\nW/O\nWater droplets in oil\nButter, Cold cream, Margarine\nTRICK - “Milk = O/W; Butter = W/O”\nMayonnaise O/W; Cold Cream W/O.\nEXAM TRAP - “O/W = Oil is Inside Water; W/O = Water is Inside Oil”\nSlash ke left wala dispersed phase yaad rakho.\n10. Buffer Solution — pH Stable\n• Buffer = solution whose pH does not change significantly after small acid/base addition\n• Resists change in pH\n• Source example: blood pH\n 7.4 maintained by buffer\n≈\n• Uses: medicine, food preservation, chemical labs\nTRICK - “Buffer = pH Bodyguard”\nSmall acid/base addition par pH ko stable rakhta hai.\nEXAM TRAP - “Blood\n 7.4”\n≈\nBiological buffer number hook."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Solution & Colloid\n11. Quick Example Hooks\nCue\nAnswer\nUniversal solvent\nWater\nH2 in Pd\nGas in Solid\nMercury amalgam\nLiquid in Solid\nAir\nGas in Gas\nFog\nLiquid in Gas\nSmoke\nSolid in Gas\nO2 in water\nGas in Liquid\nMilk\nColloid + O/W emulsion\nButter\nW/O emulsion\nColloid separation\nCentrifugation\nSuspension separation\nFiltration\nBlood pH buffer\n 7.4\n≈\n12. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• True solution <1 nm; Colloid 1–1000 nm; Suspension >1000 nm\n• Tyndall effect = Colloid + Suspension; not True Solution\n• Suspension particles visible; colloid particles not visible to naked eye\n• Colloid appears homogeneous but is actually heterogeneous\n• Colloid\n centrifugation; Suspension\n filtration\n→\n→\n• Milk = colloid, not true solution\n• Milk = O/W; Butter = W/O\n• Temp\n\n saturated solution becomes unsaturated\n↑→\n• Gas solubility in liquid decreases with temperature\n• Fog = liquid in gas; Smoke = solid in gas\n• Delta formation = colloidal coagulation by sea salt\n• Buffer resists pH change; blood pH source\n 7.4\n≈\nEXAM TRAP - “Size-Tyndall-Visible-Hetero-Centri/Filter-Milk-O/W-Temp-Gas-Fog/Smoke-Delta-Buffer”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Solution = Solute LESS + Solvent MORE; water universal\n particle size: True<1nm, Colloid1–1000nm, Suspension>1000nm; Tyndall\n→\nColloid+Suspension only, naked-eye Suspension only\n Solution types: H2/Pd gas-solid, amalgam liquid-solid, Brass solid-solid,\n→\nO2/water gas-liquid, alcohol/water liquid-liquid, sugar/water solid-liquid, Air gas-gas, Fog liquid-gas, Smoke solid-gas\n Saturated\n→\nmax solute at given T/P; Temp\n makes it unsaturated; Temp\n can saturate; most solids solubility\n with heat but gas-in-liquid\n↑\n↓\n↑\nsolubility\n\n True solution homogeneous/no Tyndall/not by filtration; Colloid pseudo-homogeneous actually\n↓→\nheterogeneous/Tyndall/Centrifugation; Suspension heterogeneous/Tyndall/visible/Filtration\n Tyndall = scattering; source links blue\n→\n\nsky, fog headlights, dusty-room beam\n Colloid apps S-C-B-R-D: smoke, clothes, blood FeCl3, rain, delta coagulation\n Emulsion =\n→\n→\ntwo immiscible liquids: Milk/Mayonnaise/Vanishing O/W; Butter/Cold Cream/Margarine W/O\n Buffer = pH bodyguard; blood\n7.4.”\n→\n≈\nTOP 5: <1 / 1–1000 / >1000 nm | Tyndall: Colloid+Suspension | Colloid=Centrifugation vs Suspension=Filtration | Milk O/W vs Butter W/O |\nGas solubility\n with temperature.\n↓"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Acid, Base & Salt\nACID, BASE & SALT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 6 · Acid/Base Concepts + Aqua Regia + Acid Sources + Salts + Indicators + pH\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 6 ke source mindmap se acid-base concepts, natural acid sources, base uses, salt formulas,\nindicator colours, pH values aur high-frequency exam traps ko fast recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Acid vs Base — pH + Taste + Litmus\nProperty\nAcid\nBase\npH\n< 7\n> 7\nTaste\nSour\nBitter\nLitmus\nBlue\n Red\n→\nRed\n Blue\n→\nArrhenius\nGives H+\nGives OH-\nBrønsted\nProton donor\nProton acceptor\nLewis\nAccepts e- pair\nDonates e- pair\nTRICK - “Acid = H+ + Sour + Blue\nRed”\n→\nBase = OH- + Bitter + Red\nBlue.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Lewis = Acid Accepts, Base Donates”\nLewis rule Arrhenius/Bronsted se ulta-feel deta hai, isliye alag yaad karo.\n2. Acid Concepts — A-B-L\nConcept\nAcid Definition\nSource Example\nArrhenius\nReleases H+ in aqueous solution\nHCl, H2SO4\nBrønsted-Lowry\nProton donor\nHCl, H2SO4\nLewis\nElectron-pair acceptor\nBF3, AlCl3\nTRICK - “A-B-L = H+ / Proton / e-Pair Accept”\nArrhenius\n H+ in water.\n→\nBrønsted\n proton donor.\n→\nLewis\n electron-pair acceptor.\n→\n3. Acid Reactions — M-C-B\nReaction\nPattern\nExample\nWith Metal\nAcid + Metal\n Salt + H2\n→\nZn + 2HCl\n ZnCl2 + H2\n→\nWith Carbonate\nAcid + Carbonate\n Salt + H2O + CO2\n→\nCaCO3 + H2SO4\n CaSO4 + H2O + CO2\n→\nWith Base\nAcid + Base\n Salt + Water\n→\nHCl + KOH\n KCl + H2O\n→\nTRICK - “M-C-B = H2 / CO2 / Neutralisation”\nMetal gives H2; carbonate gives CO2; base gives salt+water.\n4. Aqua Regia — Royal 3:1\n• Aqua Regia = fresh mixture of 3 parts concentrated HCl + 1 part concentrated HNO3\n• Called “Royal Water”\n• Dissolves Gold (Au) and Platinum (Pt)\n• Must be freshly prepared\nTRICK - “Aqua Regia = 3 HCl : 1 HNO3”\nGold + Platinum dissolve.\nEXAM TRAP -\nRatio 3:1 HCl:HNO3 — NOT 1:3."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Acid, Base & Salt\n5. Special Acids — HCl / HF / Benzoic / Glacial\nAcid\nSource Special Fact\nHCl\nHelps digestion; stomach acid\nHF\nDissolves glass\nBenzoic acid\nUsed in medicine\nGlacial acetic acid\n99–100% pure acetic/ethanoic acid\nTRICK - “HCl Stomach; HF Glass; Glacial = Pure Acetic”\nHF is the glass-dissolving trap.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGlass dissolves with HF, not HCl.\n6. Natural Acid Sources — F-C-O-A\nAcid\nNatural Source\nMemory Hook\nFormic\nRed ants, scorpions\nAnt sting\nCitric\nLemon, orange, tomato\nCitrus\nOxalic\nSpinach, beetroot\nLeafy/Beet\nAcetic\nVinegar\nVinegar acid\nTRICK - “F-C-O-A = Ant - Citrus - Spinach - Vinegar”\nFormic\nants/scorpions; Citric\nlemon/orange/tomato; Oxalic\nspinach/beetroot; Acetic\nvinegar.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Contact H2SO4 Catalyst = V2O5”\nSource high-frequency acid-production fact.\n7. Bases — Arrhenius / Brønsted / Lewis\nConcept\nBase Definition\nSource Example\nArrhenius\nGives OH- in water\nNaOH, KOH\nBrønsted-Lowry\nAccepts H+\nNH3, H2O\nLewis\nDonates electron pair\nCl-, F-, OH-\nTRICK - “Base = OH- / Proton Accept / e-Pair Donate”\nAcid-base concept mirror.\n• Base taste = bitter\n• Red litmus\n Blue\n→\n• pH > 7\n• Source note: insoluble bases ZnO, FeO react with acids but do not have basic properties in water\n8. Base Uses — M-N-C-K\nBase\nCommon Name\nUse\nMg(OH)2\nMilk of Magnesia\nStomach antacid\nNaOH\nCaustic Soda\nSoap making, petroleum refining\nCa(OH)2\nSlaked Lime\nTreating acid burns\nKOH\nCaustic Potash\nLab reagent; absorbs CO2 & SO2\nTRICK - “M-N-C-K = Magnesia-Stomach / NaOH-Soap / CaOH-Acid burn / KOH-Gas absorb”\nFour source exam-use pairs.\nEXAM TRAP -\nStomach acidity = Mg(OH)2, NOT NaOH."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Acid, Base & Salt\n9. Salt — Neutralisation Product\n• Salt = product of neutralisation reaction of acid + base\n• Acid + Base\n Salt + Water\n→\n• Source example: HNO3 + KOH\n KNO3 + H2O\n→\nSalt Type\nDescription\nExample\nCommon Salt\nSodium chloride\nNaCl\nAcidic Salt\nPartial neutralisation of polyprotic acid\nNaHCO3\nBasic Salt\nPartial neutralisation of weak base with strong\nacid\nMg(OH)Cl\nDouble Salt\nMixing two or more salts\nAlum\nMixed Salt\nOne acid+two bases OR two acids+one base\nCaOCl2\nTRICK - “Acidic-NaHCO3; Basic-Mg(OH)Cl; Double-Alum; Mixed-Bleaching”\nSalt-type mapping.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBleaching powder = Mixed salt, NOT Double salt.\n10. Important Salts — B-W-B-P\nSalt\nFormula\nMain Use\nBaking Soda\nNaHCO3\nFire extinguisher + baking/yeast agent\nWashing Soda\nNa2CO3\nTreats permanent hardness; glass/paper/soap\nBleaching Powder\nCa(OCl)2\nPool cleaning + water disinfection + chloroform\nPlaster of Paris\nCaSO4·1/2H2O\nBroken bones, chalk, toys, decoration\nTRICK - “B-W-B-P = Baking-Washing-Bleaching-POP”\nNaHCO3 / Na2CO3 / Ca(OCl)2 / CaSO4·1/2H2O.\nEXAM TRAP - “POP Half-Water; Gypsum Two-Water”\nPOP = CaSO4·1/2H2O; Gypsum = CaSO4·2H2O.\n11. Crystalline Salt Formulas — E-M-A-B-W\nName\nFormula\nEpsom Salt\nMgSO4·7H2O\nMohr’s Salt\nFeSO4·(NH4)2SO4·6H2O\nAlum\nK2SO4·Al2(SO4)3·24H2O\nBlue Vitriol\nCuSO4·5H2O\nWhite Vitriol\nZnSO4·7H2O\nTRICK - “E-M-A-B-W = 7-6-24-5-7 waters”\nEpsom7; Mohr6; Alum24; Blue5; White7.\nEXAM TRAP - “Blue Vitriol = CuSO4·5H2O; Epsom = MgSO4·7H2O”\nTwo most asked hydrate formulas.\n12. Indicators — Colour Master\nIndicator\nAcid\nBase\nLitmus\nRed\nBlue\nPhenolphthalein\nColourless\nPink\nMethyl Orange\nRed\nYellow\nMethyl Red\nRed\nYellow\nPhenol Red\nYellow\nRed/Pink"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Acid, Base & Salt\nTRICK - “Phenolphthalein = C\nP; Methyl Orange = R\nY; Phenol Red = Y\nR”\n→\n→\n→\nAcid\nBase colour order.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Phenol Red is OPPOSITE of Methyl Orange”\nMethyl Orange acid red/base yellow; Phenol Red acid yellow/base red/pink.\n13. Olfactory Indicators — Smell Rule\n• Clove oil, Vanilla, Onion = olfactory indicators\n• In Base: smell lost\n• In Acid: smell retained\nEXAM TRAP - “Base = Smell BYE; Acid = Aroma Stays”\nClove-Vanilla-Onion same rule.\n14. pH Scale — Sørensen + 0–14\n• pH = measure of H+ concentration\n• Discovered by Sørensen\n• pH = -log[H+]\n• [H+] = 10^(-pH)\n• Acidic = 0–6; Neutral = 7; Basic = 8–14\n• Higher pH = more basic; lower pH = more acidic\nTRICK - “Sørensen = pH; 7 = Neutral”\n0 strongest acid side; 14 strongest base side.\nEXAM TRAP -\npH concept = Sørensen, NOT Arrhenius or Brønsted.\n15. pH Values — Number Hooks\nSubstance\nSource pH\nLemon Juice\n2.0–2.5\nVinegar\n2.4–3.4\nMilk\n6.4–6.8\nSaliva\n6.2–7.6\nPure Water\n7.0\nTears\n7.0–7.5\nBlood Plasma\n7.35–7.45\nSea Water\n7.8–8.4\nTRICK - “Lemon 2; Water 7; Blood 7.4; Sea 8”\nQuick pH ladder.\nEXAM TRAP - “Blood 7.35–7.45; ±0.2 change = Death”\nSource-specific exam statement.\n16. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Lewis Acid accepts e- pair; Lewis Base donates e- pair\n• Aqua Regia = 3:1 HCl:HNO3, not 1:3\n• HF dissolves glass; HCl is stomach acid\n• Glacial acetic acid = 99–100% pure acetic acid\n• Formic acid = red ants/scorpions; Oxalic = spinach/beetroot\n• Mg(OH)2 = stomach antacid; NaOH = soap making"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Acid, Base & Salt\n• Bleaching powder = Mixed salt, not double salt\n• Washing Soda = Na2CO3; Baking Soda = NaHCO3\n• POP = CaSO4·1/2H2O; Gypsum = CaSO4·2H2O\n• Phenolphthalein acid = colourless, base = pink\n• Olfactory indicators lose smell in base, retain in acid\n• pH discovered by Sørensen; blood source pH 7.35–7.45\nEXAM TRAP - “Lewis-Aqua-HF-Glacial-AcidSources-Bases-Mixed-Wash/Bake-POP-Ind-Olfactory-pH”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Acid pH<7 sour blue\nred; Base pH>7 bitter red\nblue; Arrhenius H+/OH-, Brønsted proton donor/acceptor, Lewis acid accepts e-\n→\n→\npair/base donates\n Acid reactions: metal\nH2, carbonate\nCO2, base\nsalt+water\n Aqua Regia fresh 3HCl:1HNO3 dissolves Au/Pt;\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nHCl stomach, HF glass, glacial acetic 99–100%\n Acid sources F-C-O-A = ants/scorpions, citrus, spinach/beetroot, vinegar; H2SO4\n→\nContact catalyst V2O5\n Base uses: Mg(OH)2 antacid, NaOH soap, Ca(OH)2 acid burns, KOH absorbs CO2/SO2\n Salt = neutralisation;\n→\n→\nacidic NaHCO3, basic Mg(OH)Cl, double Alum, mixed CaOCl2; Baking NaHCO3, Washing Na2CO3, Bleaching Ca(OCl)2, POP\nCaSO4·1/2H2O\n Hydrates E-M-A-B-W = Epsom7, Mohr6, Alum24, Blue5, White7\n Indicators: Phenolphthalein C/P, Methyl Orange\n→\n→\nR/Y, Phenol Red Y/R; olfactory smell lost in Base\n pH Sørensen, -log[H+], acid0–6 neutral7 base8–14; Lemon\n2, Water7, Blood7.35–\n→\n≈\n7.45, Sea7.8–8.4.”\nTOP 5: Aqua Regia 3:1 | HF dissolves glass | Baking NaHCO3 vs Washing Na2CO3 | POP half-water vs Gypsum two-water | Phenolphthalein\ncolourless\npink + Sørensen pH.\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\nMETALS, NON-METALS & METALLURGY — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 7 · Reactivity + Ores + Non-metals + Alloys + Water/H2O2 + Metallurgy\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 7 ke source mindmap se metal facts, reactivity series, ores, non-metals/metalloids, alloys,\nhydrogen-water-heavy water/H2O2 aur metallurgy steps ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Metal vs Non-metal — Lose vs Gain\nType\nElectron Behaviour\nIon\nOxide Nature\nMetal\nLose electrons\nCation (+)\nUsually basic / alkaline\nNon-metal\nAccept electrons\nAnion (-)\nUsually acidic\nTRICK - “Metal LOSES\n + ; Non-metal GAINS\n -”\n→\n→\nSource exception: Hydrogen can behave as both metal and non-metal.\n2. Metal Superlatives — Ag-Au-Al-Hg-Li-Os-Ti\nCategory\nSource Answer\nBest conductor\nSilver (Ag)\nMost ductile\nGold (Au); then Silver\nMost abundant metal in Earth crust\nAluminium (Al)\n 8%\n≈\nLiquid metal\nMercury (Hg)\nLightest metal / strongest reducing agent\nLithium (Li)\nHeaviest metal\nOsmium (Os)\nStrategic metal\nTitanium (Ti)\nRadioactive liquid metal — source note\nFrancium (Fr)\nTRICK - “Ag Conducts, Au Ductile, Al Abundant, Hg Liquid, Li Light, Os Heavy, Ti Strategic”\nOne-line metal-superlative chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “Wilson = Copper; Minamata = Mercury”\nExcess Cu\n Wilson’s disease; excess Hg\n Minamata disease.\n→\n→\n3. Reactivity Series — K Na Ca Mg Al Fe Pb H Cu Hg Ag Au\n• Most\n least reactive: K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Fe > Pb > H > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au\n→\n• More reactive metal displaces less reactive metal from solution\n• Example: Fe + CuSO4\n FeSO4 + Cu\n→\n• H is placed between Pb and Cu\nTRICK - “King NaCa Maggi, Al Fe Pb; H Cu-Hg Ag-Au”\nK-Na-Ca-Mg-Al-Fe-Pb-H-Cu-Hg-Ag-Au.\nEXAM TRAP - “Above H = More Active; Below H = Less Active”\nSource series placement trap.\n4. Reactivity\n Extraction Method\n→\nActivity\nMetals\nMethod\nHighly active\nK, Na, Ca, Mg, Al\nElectrolysis in molten state\nMedium: carbonate ores\nZn, Fe, Pb, Cu\nCalcination\n oxide\n reduction/smelting\n→\n→\nMedium: sulphide ores\nZn, Fe, Pb, Cu\nRoasting\n oxide\n reduction\n→\n→\nLess active\nAg, Au\nSimple heating / native-free state\nTRICK - “High = ELECTRO; Carbonate = CALCINE; Sulphide = ROAST; Low = FREE”\nExtraction method directly reactivity/ore type se jodo."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\n5. Metal Properties + Amphoteric\n• Metals generally hard, shiny, malleable and ductile\n• Good conductors of heat/electricity: source highest Ag, lowest Pb\n• Source non-shiny exceptions: Mercury, Caesium, Gallium\n• Metal oxides generally basic\n• Amphoteric oxides/metals in source: Al, Zn, Pb — react with both acid and base\nEXAM TRAP - “Amphoteric = A-Z-P”\nAluminium - Zinc - Lead.\n6. Flame Colours — Na-K-Rb-Li-Ba-Sr\nMetal\nFlame Colour\nNa\nGolden Yellow\nK\nPurple / Lilac\nRb\nRed Violet\nLi\nCrimson Red\nBa\nApple Green\nSr\nRed\nTRICK - “Na Yellow; K Lilac; Ba Apple; Li Crimson; Sr Red”\nFirework/street-lamp colour traps.\n7. Important Metal Uses\nMetal\nSource Use\nNa\nStreet lamps — yellow light\nCu\nWires, utensils, foil\nAl\nWire, space industry\nHg\nThermometer, tube lights\nMg\nFlash bulb making\nFe\nSteel industry\nCd\nModerator in nuclear reactors — source note\nBa / Sr\nGreen / red fireworks\nTRICK - “Na Street; Mg Flash; Fe Steel; Ba Green; Sr Red”\nQuick use-memory chain.\n8. Ores — Main Pair Master\nMetal\nMain / Important Ore\nFormula\nAl\nBauxite; Cryolite/Corundum\nAl2O3·2H2O; Na3AlF6 / Al2O3\nCu\nChalcopyrite\nCuFeS2\nFe\nHaematite; Magnetite\nFe2O3; Fe3O4\nPb\nGalena\nPbS\nZn\nZincblende; Calamine\nZnS; ZnCO3\nMn\nPyrolusite\nMnO2\nAg\nArgentite\nAg2S\nCa\nCalcite\nCaCO3\nMg\nMagnesite; Dolomite\nMgCO3; CaMg(CO3)2\nCd\nGreenockite\nCdS\nTRICK - “Al-Bauxite, Cu-Chalco, Fe-Haema, Pb-Galena, Mn-Pyro”\nFive highest-frequency ore pairs.\nEXAM TRAP - “All Ores are Minerals; NOT all Minerals are Ores”\nOre must allow easy and economical metal extraction."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\n9. Non-metals — 22 = 11 Gas + 1 Liquid + 10 Solid\n• Source total non-metallic elements = 22: 11 gases, 1 liquid, 10 solids\n• Mostly bad conductors; Graphite = good conductor exception\n• Diamond = hardest non-metal / very high melting point\n• Bromine = only liquid non-metal at room temperature\n• Non-metal oxides generally acidic\n• Hydrogen behaves as both metal and non-metal — source exception\nTRICK - “22 = 11G + 1L + 10S”\nLiquid non-metal = Bromine.\nEXAM TRAP - “Graphite Conducts; Diamond Hardest”\nTwo classic carbon exceptions.\n10. Metalloids — 8 in p-block\n• Have both metallic and non-metallic properties\n• Present only in p-block — source note\n• Total metalloids = 8\n• Examples: B, Si, Ge, As, Sb, Te, Po, At\n• Source note: Boron fibre used in bulletproof jackets / lightweight aircraft material\nTRICK - “B-Si-Ge-As-Sb-Te-Po-At = 8 Metalloids”\nAll source-listed in p-block.\n11. Noble Gases — He Ne Ar Kr Xe Rn\nGas\nSource Use\nHe\nBalloons/light aircraft; divers’ artificial respiration; nuclear-reactor coolant\nAr\nWelding; incandescent bulbs; tube lights with Hg vapour\nNe\nAdvertising neon signs\nXe\nPhotography flash tubes; “Stranger gas”\nTRICK - “He-Ne-Ar-Kr-Xe-Rn = 6 Group-18 Gases”\nComplete outer shell = chemically inert in source framing.\nEXAM TRAP - “He Balloons; Ar Welding/Bulb; Ne Signs; Xe Flash”\nUse-based recall.\n12. Alloys — Brass/Bronze/German Silver/Solder/Steel\nAlloy\nComposition\nUse / Trap\nBrass\nCu 70% + Zn 30%\nUtensils, wires, pipes\nBronze\nCu 80% + Sn 20%\nStatues; source calls oldest alloy\nGerman Silver\nCu 50% + Zn 30% + Ni 20%\nJewellery; NO silver\nSolder\nSn 50% + Pb 50%\nLow MP; joining/plating\nStainless Steel\nFe 70% + Cr 18% + Ni 8% + C 1%\nCr gives rust resistance\nAmalgam\nAny metal + Hg\nDental fillings; Fe & Pt do NOT form amalgam\nTRICK - “Brass = Cu+Zn; Bronze = Cu+Sn”\nZn vs Sn is the classic swap.\nEXAM TRAP - “German Silver = NO Ag; Amalgam = Hg, but Fe/Pt NO”\nStainless Steel rust resistance comes from Chromium."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\n13. Hydrogen — Cavendish 1766\n• Hydrogen discovered by Henry Cavendish — 1766\n• Atomic mass = 1.008; electronic configuration = 1s1\n• One proton + one electron; source says no neutron\n• Diatomic H2\n• Source: 70% of Universe by mass; 0.15% of Earth atmosphere; 3rd most abundant on Earth\n• Uses: rocket fuel, NH3 synthesis, fuel cell\nTRICK - “H = Cavendish 1766 + 1p 1e 0n + H2”\nUniverse source figure = 70% by mass.\n14. Water — 4°C + 104.5°\nFact\nSource Recall\nUniversal solvent\nH2O\npH\n7 — neutral pure water\nMaximum density / minimum volume\n4°C\nH-O-H bond angle\n104.5°\nDensity\nIce 0.917; Water 0.997; Gas 0.6\nTRICK - “Water = 4°C + 104.5° + pH7”\nThree-number memory chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “Water Densest at 4°C”\nWater densest at 4°C, NOT 0°C.\n15. Hard vs Soft Water\nType\nCause / Behaviour\nRemoval\nTemporary hardness\nCa/Mg bicarbonates; poor soap lather\nBoiling or Clark’s method\nPermanent hardness\nCa/Mg sulphates & chlorides\nWashing soda, Calgon, ion-exchange/resin\nSoft water\nFree from Ca/Mg salts; good lather\nRainwater naturally soft — source\nEXAM TRAP - “Temporary = BOIL; Permanent = WASH”\nBoiling/Clark vs Washing Soda/Calgon/Ion exchange.\n16. Heavy Water + H2O2\nSubstance\nDiscoverer / Year\nSource Hooks\nHeavy Water D2O\nHarold Urey — 1932\nDeuterium oxide; nuclear-reactor moderator;\nreaction mechanism; deuterium compounds\nHydrogen Peroxide H2O2\nThénard — 1818\n“Oxygenated Water”; both oxidant & reducing\nagent; bleaching/antiseptic; rocket fuel\nTRICK - “D2O = Urey 1932; H2O2 = Thénard 1818”\nHeavy water = reactor moderator.\nEXAM TRAP - “H2O2 = BOTH Oxidant + Reducer”\nSource high-frequency redox trap.\n17. Metallurgy — Ore to Refined Metal\n• Metallurgy = extraction of metal from ore\n• Source sequence: Ore\n Concentration\n Metal Oxide\n Reduction/Smelting\n Crude Metal\n Refining\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\nTRICK - “O-C-O-R-C-R”\nOre - Concentration - Oxide - Reduction - Crude - Refining.\n18. Metallurgy Terms — Mineral/Ore/Flux/Slag\nTerm\nSource Definition / Hook\nMineral\nNaturally occurring inorganic solid; not all minerals are ores\nOre\nMetal extracted easily & economically; all ores are minerals\nFlux\nConverts infusible impurities into fusible slag; CaO basic / SiO2 acid flux\nSlag\nFusible waste formed by flux + impurities\nEXAM TRAP - “Flux + Gangue\n Slag”\n→\nFlux makes impurity fusible/removable.\n19. Calcination vs Roasting\nProcess\nAir\nOre Type\nPurpose\nCalcination\nAbsent / limited air\nCarbonate ores\nRemove volatile impurities; form\noxide\nRoasting\nExcess air\nSulphide ores\nOxidise ore/impurities; form oxide\nTRICK - “CALCINATION = Carbonate + Cut Air”\nROASTING = Sulphide + lots of Oxygen/Air.\nEXAM TRAP - “Calcination ≠ Roasting”\nCalcination = no/limited air; Roasting = excess air.\n20. Refining — Distillation vs Liquation\nMethod\nUsed For\nMetals\nDistillation\nLow boiling-point metals\nZn, Cd, Hg\nLiquation\nLow melting-point metals\nSn, Hg, Pb\nTRICK - “Distil = Z-C-H; Liquate = S-H-P”\nZn-Cd-Hg / Sn-Hg-Pb.\n21. Final Exam Traps — 14 Red Flags\n• Best conductor = Ag; most ductile = Au; most abundant crust metal = Al\n• Liquid metal = Hg; liquid non-metal = Br\n• Wilson = excess Cu; Minamata = excess Hg\n• Reactivity series puts H between Pb and Cu\n• K/Na/Ca/Mg/Al extraction = electrolysis\n• Bauxite = Al main ore; Chalcopyrite = Cu; Haematite = Fe; Galena = Pb\n• Graphite conducts; Diamond hardest non-metal\n• Brass = Cu+Zn; Bronze = Cu+Sn; German Silver has NO Ag\n• Fe and Pt do NOT form amalgam — source note\n• Water max density at 4°C; bond angle 104.5°\n• Temporary hardness = boiling; permanent = washing soda/Calgon/ion exchange\n• D2O = Urey1932; H2O2 = Thénard1818 and both oxidant/reducer\n• Calcination = absent/limited air; Roasting = excess air\n• Distillation: Zn/Cd/Hg; Liquation: Sn/Hg/Pb\nEXAM TRAP - “Ag-Au-Al / Hg-Br / Cu-Hg / H-place / Electro / Ores / Graphite-Diamond / Alloys / Amalgam / 4°-\n104.5° / Hardness / D2O-H2O2 / Calc-Roast / Dist-Liq”\nChapter ke 14 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Metals, Non-metals & Metallurgy\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Metal loses e-\ncation/basic oxide; non-metal gains e-\nanion/acidic oxide; H exception\n Ag best conductor, Au most ductile, Al8%\n→\n→\n→\ncrust, Hg liquid, Li light, Os heavy, Ti strategic; Wilson-Cu, Minamata-Hg\n Reactivity K>Na>Ca>Mg>Al>Fe>Pb>H>Cu>Hg>Ag>Au;\n→\nhigh active electrolysis, carbonate calcination, sulphide roasting, Ag/Au native\n Flames Na yellow, K lilac, Ba apple-green, Li\n→\ncrimson, Sr red\n Ores: Al-Bauxite, Cu-Chalco CuFeS2, Fe-Haema Fe2O3/Magnetite Fe3O4, Pb-Galena PbS, Mn-Pyro MnO2; all ores\n→\nminerals not vice-versa\n Non-metals source22=11G+1L+10S; Graphite conductor, Diamond hard, Bromine liquid; metalloids8 B-Si-\n→\nGe-As-Sb-Te-Po-At; noble gases HeNeArKrXeRn\n Alloys: Brass CuZn, Bronze CuSn, German Silver CuZnNi no Ag, Solder SnPb,\n→\nStainless FeCrNiC with Cr rust resistance, amalgam=Hg but Fe/Pt no\n H Cavendish1766, 1p1e0n; Water pH7, density max4°C,\n→\nangle104.5°; temporary hardness boil, permanent wash/Calgon/ion exchange\n D2O Urey1932 reactor moderator; H2O2\n→\nThénard1818 both oxidant+reducer\n Metallurgy O-C-O-R-C-R; flux+gangue\nslag; Calcination carbonate/no air vs Roasting\n→\n→\nsulphide/excess air; Distil ZnCdHg, Liquate SnHgPb.”\nTOP 5: Reactivity series + extraction | Al-Bauxite/Cu-Chalco/Fe-Haema/Pb-Galena | Brass vs Bronze vs German Silver | Water 4°C/104.5° +\nhardness | Calcination vs Roasting."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Organic Chemistry\nORGANIC CHEMISTRY — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 8 · Carbon + Allotropes + Hydrocarbons + Nomenclature + Functional Groups + Fuels\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 8 ke source mindmap se carbon facts, allotropes, hydrocarbon formulae, nomenclature prefixes,\nfunctional groups, important organic compounds, soap-detergent aur fuel-quality traps ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress\nkiya gaya hai.\n1. Carbon — 6 / 12.011 / +4 / Group 14\nProperty\nSource Recall\nSymbol\nC\nAtomic Number\n6\nAtomic Mass\n12.011\nValency\n+4\nElectronic configuration\n[He] 2s² 2p²\nGroup / Period\n14 / 2\nBond type\nCovalent\nElectrical conduction\nBad conductor; Graphite exception\nTRICK - “Carbon = 6 - 12.011 - 4 - 14/2”\nAtomic no. 6; mass 12.011; valency +4; Group 14 Period 2.\n• Organic chemistry = study of carbon compounds, source excludes CO, CO₂ and carbonates\n• Carbon forms 4 covalent bonds\n• Catenation = self-chain forming ability\n long, branched and ring structures\n→\n• Source says silicon has only limited catenation\nEXAM TRAP - “Catenation = Carbon Chains with Carbon”\nLong chains + branched chains + rings.\n2. Carbon Isotopes — 12 / 13 / 14\nIsotope\nStatus\nSource Hook\nC-12\nStable\n98.9% natural\nC-13\nStable\n1.1% natural\nC-14\nRadioactive\nUsed in carbon dating\nEXAM TRAP - “12-13 Stable; 14 Radioactive”\nC-14\n carbon dating of ancient materials.\n→\n3. Allotropes — Diamond / Graphite / C-60\nAllotrope\nStructure / Conductivity\nKey Facts / Uses\nDiamond\n3D tetrahedral; insulator\nHardest natural substance; transparent/lustrous;\njewellery, glass cutters, sharp tools\nGraphite\nHexagonal planar layers; conductor\nSoft; layers slide; lubricant; pencil tip/electrode;\nsource calls softest carbon form\nFullerene C-60\nFootball shape; 60 carbons\nBuckminsterfullerene;\nsemiconductor/lubricant/tumour research\nTRICK - “Diamond INSULATES; Graphite CONDUCTS”\nOpposite-looking exam trap.\nEXAM TRAP - “C-60 = Kroto + Smalley + Curl”\nBuckminsterfullerene discoverers — all three names."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Organic Chemistry\n4. Hydrocarbon Family — 2n+2 / 2n / 2n-2 / 2n-6\nType\nBond\nFormula\nExample\nAlkane\nSingle C-C\nCₙH₂ₙ₊₂\nCH4 Methane; C2H6 Ethane\nAlkene\nDouble C=C\nCₙH₂ₙ\nC2H4 Ethene/Ethylene\nAlkyne\nTriple C\nC\n≡\nCₙH₂ₙ₋₂\nC2H2 Ethyne/Acetylene\nAromatic\nBenzene ring\nCₙH₂ₙ₋₆ — source formula\nBenzene, Toluene, Naphthalene\nTRICK - “ANE +2, ENE 0, YNE -2”\nAlkane CnH2n+2; Alkene CnH2n; Alkyne CnH2n-2.\nEXAM TRAP - “Acetylene = Ethyne = HC\nCH = C2H2”\n≡\nTriple-bond identity trap.\n5. Saturated vs Unsaturated\nType\nBond\nSeries / Example\nSaturated\nOnly single C-C bonds\nAlkane; Ethane H3C-CH3\nUnsaturated\nDouble or triple bonds\nEthene H2C=CH2; Ethyne HC\nCH\n≡\nTRICK - “SAT = SINGLE; UN-SAT = Double/Triple”\nAlkane saturated; Alkene/Alkyne unsaturated.\n6. Isomers vs Homologous Series\nConcept\nMeaning\nSource Example\nIsomers\nSame molecular formula, different structure\nC2H6O\n CH3OCH3 and C2H5OH\n→\nHomologous Series\nSame functional group; successive members differ\nby -CH2-\nCH3OH\n C2H5OH\n C3H7OH\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “ISOMER = Same Formula, Different Structure”\nHomologue = Same family + CH2 step.\n7. Prefix Ladder — 1 to 10 Carbons\nC atoms\nPrefix\nC atoms\nPrefix\n1\nMeth-\n6\nHex-\n2\nEth-\n7\nHept-\n3\nProp-\n8\nOct-\n4\nBut-\n9\nNon-\n5\nPent-\n10\nDec-\nTRICK - “Meth-Eth-Prop-But-Pent-Hex-Hept-Oct-Non-Dec”\n1C se 10C tak prefix chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “4C = But-, NOT Quad”\nLPG main components Butane 4C + Propane 3C.\n8. Suffix Rules — ane / ene / yne / anol\nClass\nSuffix\nExample\nAlkane\n-ane\nMethane, Ethane\nAlkene\n-ene\nEthene, Propene\nAlkyne\n-yne\nEthyne, Propyne\nAlcohol\n-anol\nMethanol, Ethanol"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Organic Chemistry\nTRICK - “Single ANE; Double ENE; Triple YNE; OH\n ANOL”\n→\nBond/functional-group suffix recall.\n9. Functional Groups — OH / COOH / CHO / CO / NH2 / NO2 / X\nGroup\nName\nExample\n-OH\nHydroxyl / Alcohol\nC2H5OH Ethanol\n-COOH\nCarboxyl / Carboxylic acid\nCH3COOH Acetic acid\n-CHO\nAldehyde\nHCHO Formaldehyde\n-CO-\nKetone\nCH3COCH3 Acetone\n-NH2\nAmino\nC2H5NH2 Ethylamine\n-NO2\nNitro\nC6H5NO2 Nitrobenzene\n-X (Cl, Br)\nHalide\nCH3Cl Chloromethane\nTRICK - “OH Alcohol; COOH Acid; CHO Aldehyde; CO Ketone”\nFour most-tested functional groups.\nEXAM TRAP - “Acetone = Ketone; Formaldehyde = Aldehyde”\nAcetone CH3COCH3; Formaldehyde HCHO.\n10. Methanol vs Ethanol vs Acetic Acid\nCompound\nFormula\nSource Facts\nMethanol / Wood Spirit\nCH3OH\nColourless; poisonous; excess consumption can\ncause blindness/death\nEthanol\nC2H5OH\nLiquid; good solvent; made by fermentation; used\nin tincture iodine/cough syrup\nEthanoic / Acetic acid\nCH3COOH\n3-4% = vinegar; pure form = glacial acetic acid; MP\n290 K\nTRICK - “Methanol = Wood Spirit + Poison; Ethanol = Fermentation”\nVinegar = only 3-4% ethanoic acid.\nEXAM TRAP - “Glacial Acetic = 99-100% Pure; MP 290 K”\nVinegar ≠ pure acetic acid.\n11. Soap vs Detergent\nProperty\nSoap\nDetergent\nActive group\n-COO- carboxylate\n-SO3- sulphonate\nNature\nAlkaline / Basic\nNeutral\nHard water\nNo foam\nFoams\nBiodegradable\nYes\nNo — source note\nMade from\nFats/oils by saponification\nPetroleum derivatives\nTRICK - “Soap = Saponification + Soft Water; Detergent = Does Hard Water”\nSoap no foam in hard water; detergent foams.\nEXAM TRAP - “Soap Alkaline; Detergent Neutral”\nSource contrast.\n12. Fuel Types — Solid / Liquid / Gas\nFuel Class\nSource Examples\nSolid\nWood, Coke, Coal, Charcoal\nLiquid\nPetrol, Diesel, Kerosene, Alcohol\nGaseous\nLPG, CNG, Natural Gas"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Organic Chemistry\nTRICK - “Solid WCCC; Liquid PDKA; Gas LPG-CNG-NG”\nFuel-type grouping.\n13. LPG vs CNG — Butane/Propane vs Methane\nFuel\nFull Form\nMain Composition\nLPG\nLiquefied Petroleum Gas\nMainly Butane (C4) + Propane (C3)\nCNG\nCompressed Natural Gas\nMainly Methane (C1)\nTRICK - “LPG = B+P; CNG = M”\nLPG Butane+Propane; CNG Methane.\nEXAM TRAP - “LPG ≠ Methane; CNG ≠ Butane”\nClassic fuel composition trap.\n14. Petrol / Diesel / Kerosene — Carbon Range\nFuel\nSource Carbon Range\nPetrol\nC5-C10\nDiesel\nC10-C15\nKerosene\nC10-C16\nTRICK - “Petrol 5-10; Diesel 10-15; Kerosene 10-16”\nCarbon-range number chain.\n15. Octane vs Cetane\nNumber\nMeasures\nSource Meaning\nOctane Number\nPetrol quality\nHigher = better; less knocking\nCetane Number\nDiesel quality\nHigher = better combustion\nEXAM TRAP - “O = Octane = Petrol; C = Cetane = Diesel”\nSource also links Octane to 8C and Cetane to 16C in nomenclature notes.\n16. Rapid-Fire Recall\nCue\nAnswer\nCarbon atomic no./valency\n6 / +4\nRadioactive isotope\nC-14\nHardest / conductor allotrope\nDiamond / Graphite\nFullerene\nC-60 Buckminsterfullerene\nAlkane / Alkene / Alkyne\nCnH2n+2 / CnH2n / CnH2n-2\nAcetylene\nEthyne = C2H2\n4-carbon prefix\nBut-\n-CHO / -CO-\nAldehyde / Ketone\nWood spirit\nMethanol CH3OH\nVinegar\n3-4% ethanoic acid\nSoap process\nSaponification\nLPG / CNG\nButane+Propane / Methane\nPetrol / Diesel number\nOctane / Cetane"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Organic Chemistry\n17. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Carbon atomic no. 6, valency +4, Group 14 Period 2\n• C-14 radioactive; C-12 and C-13 stable\n• Diamond = electrical insulator; Graphite = conductor\n• Buckminsterfullerene = C-60; Kroto-Smalley-Curl\n• Alkane CnH2n+2; Alkene CnH2n; Alkyne CnH2n-2\n• Acetylene = Ethyne = HC\nCH = C2H2\n≡\n• Isomer same formula/different structure; homologues differ by CH2\n• 4C prefix = But-, not Quad\n• Acetone = ketone; Formaldehyde = aldehyde\n• Methanol = poisonous wood spirit; Ethanol = made by fermentation\n• Soap alkaline/no foam hard water; detergent neutral/foams hard water\n• LPG = Butane+Propane; CNG = Methane; Octane petrol/Cetane diesel\nEXAM TRAP - “6/4-C14-D/G-C60-Hydrocarbons-Acetylene-Iso/Homo-But-Acetone/Formal-Meth/Eth-Soap/Det-\nLPG/CNG/Oct-Cet”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Carbon = Z6, mass12.011, valency+4, Group14 Period2, covalent; catenation gives chains/branches/rings; C12/13 stable, C14 radioactive\ndating\n Allotropes: Diamond 3D hard insulator, Graphite layered soft conductor/lubricant, Fullerene C60 football Buckminsterfullerene by\n→\nKroto-Smalley-Curl\n Hydrocarbons: Alkane single CnH2n+2 saturated, Alkene double CnH2n, Alkyne triple CnH2n-2, source aromatic\n→\nCnH2n-6; Acetylene=Ethyne C2H2; isomer same formula diff structure, homologous series +CH2\n Prefixes Meth-Eth-Prop-But-Pent-Hex-\n→\nHept-Oct-Non-Dec; suffix single-ane double-ene triple-yne OH-anol\n Groups OH alcohol, COOH acid, CHO aldehyde, CO ketone, NH2 amino,\n→\nNO2 nitro, X halide; Acetone ketone, HCHO formaldehyde aldehyde\n Methanol CH3OH wood spirit poison; Ethanol C2H5OH fermentation;\n→\nVinegar 3-4% CH3COOH, Glacial 99-100% MP290K\n Soap carboxylate alkaline saponification no foam hard water biodegradable; Detergent\n→\nsulphonate neutral foams hard water source-not-biodegradable\n Fuels: LPG=B+P, CNG=Methane; Petrol C5-10, Diesel C10-15, Kerosene C10-\n→\n16; Octane=petrol quality, Cetane=diesel quality.”\nTOP 5: Diamond insulator vs Graphite conductor | Alkane/Alkene/Alkyne formulas | Acetone ketone vs Formaldehyde aldehyde | Soap vs\nDetergent | LPG/CNG + Octane/Cetane."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Chemistry in Everyday Life\nCHEMISTRY IN EVERYDAY LIFE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 9 · Drugs + Dyes + Fibres + Glass + Cement/Fertilisers + Polymers + Rubber + Food Chemistry\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 9 ke source mindmap se drugs, dyes, fibres, glass, cement/fertilisers, polymers, rubber/explosives\naur food-chemistry ke names, uses, formulas, years aur exam traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Drugs — Purpose + Classification\n• Drugs = diagnosis, prevention and treatment of diseases\n• Antacid\n stomach HCl acidity control\n→\n• Antipyretic\n body temperature/fever control\n→\n• Antihistamine\n allergies, asthma, swelling, itching\n→\n• Tranquilizer\n stress, anxiety, mental illness / sleep-related use\n→\n• Analgesic\n pain killer\n→\n• Antibiotic\n bacterial infection control\n→\n• Anaesthetic\n sensory organs temporarily closed during surgery\n→\nTRICK - “A-A-A-T-A-A-A = Acid-Fever-Allergy-Stress-Pain-Bacteria-Surgery”\nAntacid, Antipyretic, Antihistamine, Tranquilizer, Analgesic, Antibiotic, Anaesthetic.\n2. Drug Examples — High-Frequency Pairs\nDrug Type\nSource Examples / Hook\nAntacid\nMg(OH)2, Cimetidine\nAntipyretic\nParacetamol, Aspirin, Brufen\nAntihistamine\nBrompheniramine (Dimetapp), Terfenadine\nTranquilizer\nVeronal; Equanil, Valium; Cocaine, Iproniazid; LSD, Mescaline; Barbiturates\nNarcotic analgesic\nMorphine, Heroin\nNon-narcotic pain killer\nParacetamol, Dichlorofinac\nAnaesthetic\nDiethyl ether, Chloroform\nTRICK - “MgOH2 Acid; Para/Aspirin Fever; Morphine/Heroin Narcotic”\nThree direct exam hooks.\n3. Antibiotics + Quinine + Sulpha\nItem\nSource Recall\nPenicillin\nFirst antibiotic; narrow spectrum; obtained from fungus\nChloramphenicol\nBroad spectrum; Typhoid/high fever\nTetracycline\nBroad spectrum\nQuinine\nAntimalarial; from Cinchona tree\nSulphanyl amide\nFirst sulpha drug — 1908\nSulpha drugs\nSulphur + Nitrogen; prevent bacterial infections\nTRICK - “Penicillin = Fungus + First + Narrow”\nChloramphenicol = Broad + Typhoid.\nEXAM TRAP - “Quinine = Cinchona; Sulphanyl amide = 1908”\nNatural-source + first-sulpha hook.\nEXAM TRAP - “Aspirin = Fever + Pain; NOT Antibiotic”\nParacetamol = antipyretic + non-narcotic pain killer.\n4. Antiseptic / Disinfectant\n• Source framing: Antiseptics / Disinfectants prevent/destroy bacteria in open wounds\n• Examples: Dettol, Iodoform (Iodine), Methylene blue"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Chemistry in Everyday Life\nTRICK - “Dettol - Iodoform - Methylene Blue”\nOpen-wound bacterial control examples from source.\n5. Dyes — Application + Chemistry\nType\nUse / Example\nAcidic dyes\nWool, silk, nylon; Methyl Orange, Congo Red\nBasic dyes\nNylon, polyester; Yellow aniline, Green malachite\nBonding dyes\nAlizarin — Red with Al, Blue with Ba\nAzo dyes\nMethyl Orange\nPhthalein dyes\nPhenolphthalein\nIndigoid dyes\nIndigo, Tyrian purple\nAnthraquinone\nAlizarin — natural\nTriphenylmethane\nGreen malachite\nTRICK - “Methyl Orange = AZO; Phenolphthalein = Phthalein; Indigo = Indigoid”\nAlizarin = Anthraquinone + natural.\nEXAM TRAP - “Alizarin: Al\nRed, Ba\nBlue”\n→\n→\nBonding-dye colour pair.\n6. Fibres — Natural / Semi-Synthetic / Synthetic\nClass\nExamples / Source Use\nNatural plant\nCotton, Flax/Linen\nNatural animal\nWool — sheep; Silk — silkworm\nSemi-synthetic — source list\nPolyester, Metallic fibres, Rayon from cellulose\nNylon\nToothbrush bristles, ropes, parachutes, fishing nets, clothes\nPolyester\nClothes, fire-fighting hosepipes\nCarbon fibre\nSpacecraft parts, sporting goods\nAcrylonitrile\nSynthetic blankets replacing wool\nTRICK - “Nylon = Parachute + Toothbrush + Fishing Net”\nCarbon fibre = Spacecraft; Acrylonitrile = Wool substitute.\nEXAM TRAP - “Carbon Fibre ≠ Clothing”\nSource specifically warns spacecraft parts, not clothing.\n7. Glass — Base Facts\n• Glass = amorphous homogeneous mixture of silicates of alkali metals\n• Ordinary glass formula in source = Na2O·CaO·6SiO2\n• Ordinary glass = partially transparent\nEXAM TRAP - “Glass = AMORPHOUS, not Crystalline”\nHigh-frequency chapter trap.\n8. Types of Glass — Best / Sunglass / Lab / Optics\nGlass\nComposition / Source Hook\nUses\nSoda Glass\nNa2CO3 + CaCO3 + SiO2\nTest tubes, bottles, lab equipment, utensils\nPhoto Chromatic\nUsual + Silver Chloride\nSunglasses\nJena Glass — Best\nZn + Barium Borosilicate\nChemical vessels, scientific instruments\nFlint Glass\nK carbonate + PbO + Silica\nBulbs, cameras, telescope/microscope lens, prism\nCrookes Glass\nCerium oxide + Silica\nSunglass lenses\nPyrex Glass\nBarium silicate + Na silicate\nLab equipment, pharmaceutical vessels\nQuartz/Silica Glass\nMelted SiO2\nUV lamps, reagent containers\nWater Glass\nNa2CO3 + Silica\nSoluble in water; optical fibre, endoscopy — source\nnote"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Chemistry in Everyday Life\nTRICK - “JENA = BEST; Photochromatic = AgCl Sunglass; Crookes = Cerium Sunglass”\nPyrex = lab glass in source.\nEXAM TRAP - “Water Glass = Soluble in Water”\nSource note connects it with optical fibre/endoscopy.\n9. Glass Colouring Agents\nAgent\nColour\nCarbon\nBrown / Black\nCadmium Sulphide\nLemon Yellow\nCobalt Oxide\nDark Blue\nCuprous Oxide\nGlitter Red\nCupric Oxide\nPeacock Blue\nGold Chloride\nRuby Red\nManganese Dioxide\nPink\nFerric Oxide\nBrown\nK Dichromate\nGreen\nTRICK - “Co = Dark Blue; AuCl = Ruby Red; K2Cr2O7 = Green”\nMost asked glass-colour pair hooks.\n10. Cement + Fertilisers\nTopic\nSource Recall\nPortland Cement\nJoseph Aspdin — 1824\nCement CaO\n60–70%\nCement SiO2\n20–25%\nAl2O3 + Fe2O3\n2–3%\nN fertiliser\nUrea, Ammonium sulphate\nP fertiliser\nPhosphatic asphalt — source term\nK fertiliser\nPotassium nitrate & sulphate\nNPK\nNitrogen + Phosphorus + Potassium\nTRICK - “Aspdin 1824 = Portland Cement; CaO 60–70%”\nNPK = N + P + K.\n11. Polymers — Monomer Pairs\nPolymer\nMonomer / Source\nPolythene\nEthylene (CH2=CH2)\nPolystyrene\nStyrene\nPVC\nVinyl Chloride\nBakelite\nFormaldehyde + Phenol\nUrea Formaldehyde Resin\nUrea + Formaldehyde\nMelamine\nMelamine + Formaldehyde\nTRICK - “Poly-Ethylene; PolySty-Styrene; PVC-Vinyl; Bakelite-Phenol+Formaldehyde”\nMonomer-match chain.\n12. Thermoplastic vs Thermosetting\nType\nHeating Behaviour\nExamples / Use\nThermoplastic\nSoftens; can remould/recycle\nPolythene, PVC\nThermosetting\nDoes NOT soften; cannot remould\nBakelite, Melamine\nTRICK - “ThermoPLASTIC = Pliable Again; ThermoSET = Set Forever”\nBakelite = heat/electric insulator; power switches.\nMelamine = fire resistant; firefighter suits — source."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Chemistry in Everyday Life\nEXAM TRAP - “Bakelite = Thermosetting, NOT Thermoplastic”\nOne of chapter’s biggest traps.\n13. Rubber — Isoprene + Vulcanisation\n• Natural rubber from vegetable milk (latex)\n• Natural-rubber monomer = Isoprene\n• Natural rubber: soft/sticky when hot; brittle when cold\n• Synthetic rubber source examples: Neoprene = polymer of Chloroprene; Buna-N\n• Vulcanisation improves rubber quality\nVulcanisation\nSource Value\nTemperature\n313 K\nAdditive\nSulphur compound + ZnO\nTyre\n5% sulphur\nBattery case\n30% sulphur\nResult\nHarder, stronger, more elastic, less sticky\nTRICK - “Rubber = ISOprene; Vulcanise = 313 K + ZnO”\nTyre 5% S; Battery 30% S.\nEXAM TRAP - “5 Tyre / 30 Battery”\nSulphur-percentage swap trap.\n14. Explosives — Nobel vs Henning\nExplosive\nSource Detail\nRDX\nCyclotrimethylene; Henning, Germany — 1899\nTNT / TNG — source label\nTrinitroglycerine (Nobel Oil); Dynamite by Alfred Nobel — 1863\nEXAM TRAP - “Nobel 1863 = TNT/Dynamite; Henning 1899 = RDX”\nPreserved exactly in source framing.\n15. Food Chemistry — Preservatives + Antioxidants\nCategory\nSource Examples\nFood preservatives\nSodium benzoate, NaCl, Sugar, Oil, salts of sorbic & propanoic acid\nVitamin C\nAscorbic acid — fruits & vegetables\nVitamin E\nTocopherol — vegetable oil\nCarotenoids\nOrange/yellow fruits & vegetables\nPolyphenolic antioxidants\nTea, Coffee, Chocolate, Soyabean\nBHA / BHT\nSynthetic antioxidants in packaged food\nTRICK - “Preservative Star = Sodium Benzoate”\nBHA/BHT = packaged-food synthetic antioxidants.\n16. Artificial Sweeteners — 100 / 550 / 600 / 2000\nSweetener\nTimes Sweeter than Sucrose\nSource Hook\nAspartame\n100×\nWidely used; successful\nSaccharin\n550×\nOrtho-sulpho benzamide; not harmful\nSucralose\n600×\nTrichloro derivative of sucrose\nAlitame\n2000×\nStrongest artificial sweetener\nTRICK - “A-S-S-A = 100-550-600-2000”\nAspartame\n Saccharin\n Sucralose\n Alitame.\n→\n→\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Chemistry in Everyday Life\nEXAM TRAP - “Alitame = 2000× = Strongest”\nSource says all listed sweeteners are for diabetics.\n17. Final Exam Traps — 14 Red Flags\n• Penicillin = fungus + first antibiotic + narrow spectrum\n• Chloramphenicol = broad spectrum + typhoid\n• Quinine = antimalarial from Cinchona tree\n• Aspirin = antipyretic + pain killer, not antibiotic\n• Methyl Orange = Azo; Alizarin = Anthraquinone; Phenolphthalein = Phthalein\n• Nylon = parachute/toothbrush/fishing net; Carbon fibre = spacecraft\n• Glass = amorphous, not crystalline\n• Jena = best glass; Photochromatic = AgCl sunglass; Crookes = cerium sunglass\n• Cobalt oxide = dark blue; Gold chloride = ruby red glass\n• Bakelite = thermosetting; PVC = thermoplastic\n• Natural rubber monomer = Isoprene\n• Vulcanisation = 313 K + ZnO; tyre 5% S, battery 30% S\n• Source: Alfred Nobel 1863 = TNT/Dynamite; Henning 1899 = RDX\n• Sweeteners: Aspartame100, Saccharin550, Sucralose600, Alitame2000\nEXAM TRAP - “Penicillin-Chlora-Quinine-Aspirin / Dyes / Fibres / Glass / Jena / Colours / Bakelite / Isoprene / 313K\n/ Nobel-Henning / 100-550-600-2000”\nChapter ke 14 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Drugs: Antacid MgOH2, Antipyretic Para/Aspirin/Brufen, Antihistamine allergy, Tranquilizer stress, Narcotic Morphine/Heroin,\nAnaesthetic Ether/Chloroform; Penicillin fungus+first+narrow, Chloramphenicol broad+Typhoid, Quinine Cinchona, Sulphanyl\namide1908\n Dyes: Methyl Orange Azo, Phenolphthalein Phthalein, Indigo Indigoid, Alizarin Anthraquinone natural + Al red/Ba\n→\nblue\n Fibres: Nylon parachute/toothbrush/net, Carbon fibre spacecraft, Acrylonitrile wool substitute\n Glass amorphous; Jena best\n→\n→\nZn+Barium borosilicate, Photochromatic AgCl sunglass, Crookes cerium sunglass, Pyrex lab; Co oxide dark blue, Au chloride ruby\nred\n Cement Aspdin1824, CaO60–70%; NPK=N+P+K\n Polymers: Polythene-Ethylene, PVC-Vinyl chloride, Bakelite-\n→\n→\nPhenol+Formaldehyde; Thermoplastic Poly/PVC vs Thermosetting Bakelite/Melamine\n Rubber latex, monomer Isoprene;\n→\nvulcanisation313K + ZnO, tyre5%S battery30%S\n Explosives source: Nobel1863 TNT/Dynamite, Henning1899 RDX\n Food: sodium\n→\n→\nbenzoate preservative; antioxidants C/E/carotenoids/polyphenols/BHA-BHT; sweeteners A-S-S-A =100-550-600-2000, Alitame\nstrongest.”\nTOP 5: Penicillin fungus/first/narrow | Jena best + Glass amorphous | Bakelite thermosetting | Isoprene + 313K + 5/30% S | Sweeteners 100-\n550-600-2000."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Environmental Chemistry\nENVIRONMENTAL CHEMISTRY — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Chemistry · Chapter 10 · Pollution + Greenhouse + Smog + Acid Rain + Ozone + BOD + Bhopal + Green Chemistry\nYe full notes nahi hai — Chapter 10 ke source mindmap se environmental-pollution types, greenhouse gases, smog, acid rain, ozone\ndepletion, water-pollution values, Bhopal tragedy, metal limits aur Green Chemistry ke exam facts ko fast recall tricks mein\ncompress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Environmental Pollution — 5 Types\n• Environmental pollution = harmful substances se environment mein adverse changes\n• Affects plants and animals\n• Source pollutant examples: DDT, Plastics, Heavy Metals\nType\nCore Source Hook\nAir\nHarmful gases/particulates; greenhouse gases, smog, acid rain, ozone\ndepletion\nWater\nIndustrial/agricultural/domestic waste; BOD, eutrophication, heavy metals\nSoil\nPesticides, heavy metals, industrial waste; DDT persistent pollutant\nSound\nExcessive noise; source says >85 dB harmful\nRadioactive\nRadioactive substances and nuclear waste\nTRICK - “A-W-S-S-R = Air-Water-Soil-Sound-Radiation”\nFive pollution types.\n2. DDT + PCB — Persistent vs Carcinogenic\nPollutant\nFull Form / Source Fact\nDDT\nDichloro Diphenyl Trichloroethane — persistent pollutant\nPCBs\nPolychlorinated Biphenyls — carcinogenic industrial pollutant\nEXAM TRAP - “DDT = STAYS; PCB = CANCER”\nDDT persistent; PCBs carcinogenic.\n3. Greenhouse Effect — Heat Trap\n• Greenhouse gases trap heat in atmosphere\n Earth temperature increases\n Global Warming\n→\n→\n• Source greenhouse list: CO2, CH4, N2O, CFC (Freon), SO2\n• Source says main greenhouse gas = CO2\n• Source says most potent greenhouse gas = CH4, 25× more potent than CO2\n• CFC = greenhouse gas + ozone depleter\nTRICK - “CO2 = MAIN; CH4 = POTENT; CFC = DOUBLE ROLE”\nCFC source role: greenhouse + ozone depletion.\nEXAM TRAP - “Source Greenhouse List Includes SO2”\nSource greenhouse-gas list includes SO2; preserve this source framing for revision.\n4. Smog — General vs Photochemical\nSmog\nFormation / Composition\nNature\nGeneral\nSmoke + Fog + SO2; coal-burning industrial\nareas\nReducing\nPhotochemical\nNOx + Hydrocarbons + Sunlight; Ozone + NO +\nPAN\nOxidative\nTRICK - “General = REDUCING; Photo = OXIDATIVE”\nGeneral: Smoke+Fog+SO2.\nPhoto: NOx+Hydrocarbon+Sunlight."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Environmental Chemistry\nEXAM TRAP - “PAN = Peroxy Acetyl Nitrate”\nSource formula: CH3CO·O2NO2; eye irritation + plant damage.\n5. Acid Rain — 5.6 Rule\nFact\nSource Recall\nNormal rain pH\n5.6\nAcid rain\npH below 5.6\nResponsible gases\nSO2 + NO2\nCO2 role\nMakes normal rain slightly acidic; source says not acid-rain cause\nDamage\nMarble/limestone monuments, soil, water bodies, forests\nMarble cancer\nAcid-rain erosion of Taj Mahal\nTRICK - “Acid Rain = <5.6 + SO2/NO2”\nNOT below 7.\nEXAM TRAP - “CO2\n Normal Rain 5.6; SO2+NO2\n Acid Rain”\n→\n→\nSource distinction.\n6. Ozone Layer — Stratosphere + CFC\n• Ozone layer present in Stratosphere\n• Protects Earth from harmful UV radiation\n• Main source cause of ozone depletion = CFC + Halogens\n• CFC = Chlorofluorocarbon = Freon; compounds of C, Cl, F\n• Used in refrigerators and AC\n• Source says each CFC molecule can destroy thousands of ozone molecules\n• Ozone hole first discovered over Antarctica\nTRICK - “Ozone = STRATOSPHERE; CFC = FREON; Hole = ANTARCTICA”\nCFC used in Refrigerator + AC.\nEXAM TRAP - “CFC = Ozone Depleter + Greenhouse Gas”\nDual-effect trap.\n7. BOD — Higher = Dirtier\n• BOD = Biochemical Oxygen Demand\n• Amount of O2 consumed by aerobic bacteria to decompose organic matter in polluted water\n• Higher BOD = more polluted\nWater\nSource BOD\nClean Water\n5 ppm\nHighly Polluted Water\n17 ppm\nEXAM TRAP - “BOD HIGH = Pollution HIGH”\nClean 5 ppm; Highly Polluted 17 ppm.\n8. Eutrophication — Nutrient\n Algae\n O2 Down\n→\n→\n• Excess nutrients = nitrates + phosphates from fertilisers/agricultural runoff/sewage\n• Nutrients enter water\n algal bloom\n→\n• Algae/decomposition consume dissolved O2\n• Dissolved O2 depletes\n fish/aquatic life die\n→\nTRICK - “N-P\n ALGAE UP\n O2 DOWN\n FISH DOWN”\n→\n→\n→\nNitrate + Phosphate enrichment chain."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Environmental Chemistry\nEXAM TRAP - “Eutrophication = O2 DOWN”\nEutrophication = dissolved O2 DECREASE, not increase.\n9. Drinking-Water Metal Limits — 0.005 to 5 ppm\nMetal\nMax Source Limit\nRisk / Hook\nFe\n0.2 ppm\nRust taste, staining\nMn\n0.05 ppm\nNeurological effects\nAl\n0.2 ppm\nPossible Alzheimer link — source note\nCu\n3.0 ppm\nLiver/kidney damage\nZn\n5.0 ppm\nNausea at high level\nCd\n0.005 ppm\nKidney damage; Itai-Itai disease\nTRICK - “Cd LOWEST 0.005; Zn HIGHEST 5.0”\nFe = Al = 0.2 ppm.\nEXAM TRAP - “Cd = Itai-Itai”\nSource disease association.\n10. Bhopal Gas Tragedy — 3 Dec 1984\nFact\nSource Recall\nDate\n3 December 1984\nLocation\nBhopal, Madhya Pradesh\nCompany\nUnion Carbide Limited\nGas\nMethyl Isocyanate (MIC)\nFormula\nH3C-N=C=O\nMIC use\nPesticide manufacturing\nTRICK - “3-12-84 + MIC + Union Carbide”\nBhopal master memory.\nEXAM TRAP - “1984 Bhopal, NOT 1986”\nSource contrasts 1986 with Chernobyl.\n11. Green Chemistry — Prevention over Cure\n• Green Chemistry = chemical products/processes designed to reduce or eliminate chemical hazards\n• Aim = pollution prevention at source\n• Source says uses water as solvent: cost-effective, non-flammable, non-carcinogenic\n• 12 principles of Green Chemistry\n• Old Zapper technology developed by TERI\n• TERI = The Energy and Resource Institute\nTRICK - “GREEN = Hazard DOWN at SOURCE”\nPrevention over cure; source solvent = Water.\nEXAM TRAP - “TERI\n Old Zapper”\n→\nThe Energy and Resource Institute."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Environmental Chemistry\n12. Abbreviations Flash\nAbbrev.\nFull Form\nDDT\nDichloro Diphenyl Trichloroethane\nCFC\nChlorofluorocarbon (Freon)\nPAN\nPeroxy Acetyl Nitrate\nBOD\nBiochemical Oxygen Demand\nPCBs\nPolychlorinated Biphenyls\nMIC\nMethyl Isocyanate\nTERI\nThe Energy and Resource Institute\nTRICK - “D-C-P-B-P-M-T”\nDDT-CFC-PAN-BOD-PCB-MIC-TERI abbreviation chain.\n13. Number Flash — 5.6 / 5 / 17 / 0.005 / 5 / 1984\nNumber\nMeaning\n5.6\nNormal-rain pH; acid rain below this\n5 ppm\nClean-water BOD — source\n17 ppm\nHighly polluted-water BOD — source\n0.005 ppm\nCd max limit — lowest\n5.0 ppm\nZn max limit — highest\n3 Dec 1984\nBhopal gas tragedy\nTRICK - “5.6 - 5 - 17 - .005 - 5 - 3/12/84”\nChapter number-lock chain.\n14. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Acid rain pH = below 5.6, not below 7\n• Acid rain source cause = SO2 + NO2; CO2 linked to normal rain pH 5.6\n• General smog = reducing; Photochemical smog = oxidative\n• PAN = Peroxy Acetyl Nitrate\n• Ozone depletion = stratospheric pollution\n• CFC = Freon; refrigerators/AC; ozone depleter + greenhouse gas\n• Bhopal = 3 December 1984; MIC; Union Carbide Limited\n• Higher BOD = more polluted\n• Source BOD: clean 5 ppm; highly polluted 17 ppm\n• Eutrophication = dissolved O2 decreases\n• Cd limit 0.005 ppm lowest; Zn 5.0 ppm highest; Fe=Al=0.2 ppm\n• PCBs = carcinogenic; TERI = The Energy and Resource Institute\nEXAM TRAP - “5.6-SO2NO2 / Smog / PAN / Strato / CFC / 3-12-84 / BOD\n / 5-17 / O2\n / Cd-Zn / PCB-TERI”\n↑\n↓\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi order mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Chemistry Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Environmental Chemistry\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Pollution 5 types A-W-S-S-R; DDT persistent, PCBs carcinogenic\n Greenhouse effect traps heat; source gases CO2-CH4-N2O-CFC-SO2,\n→\n\nmain CO2, potent CH4, CFC dual role\n Smog: General=Smoke+Fog+SO2 reducing; Photo=NOx+Hydrocarbon+sunlight oxidative with\n→\n\nOzone+NO+PAN; PAN=Peroxy Acetyl Nitrate\n Acid rain <5.6, gases SO2+NO2; normal rain 5.6 due dissolved CO2; marble cancer/Taj\n→\ndamage\n Ozone stratosphere, CFC=Freon=C/Cl/F, fridge+AC, hole Antarctica\n BOD = Biochemical Oxygen Demand; HIGH BOD =\n→\n→\nMORE pollution; source clean5 ppm vs highly polluted17 ppm\n Eutrophication Nitrate+Phosphate\n Algal bloom\n dissolved O2\n\n→\n→\n→\n↓\n fish death\n Metal limits: Cd0.005 lowest, Zn5 highest, Fe=Al0.2; Cd-Itai-Itai\n Bhopal 3 Dec1984, Union Carbide, MIC H3C-N=C=O,\n→\n→\n→\npesticide manufacturing\n Green Chemistry = hazards reduce/eliminate at source, source water solvent, 12 principles; TERI = The\n→\nEnergy and Resource Institute\n Old Zapper.”\n→\nTOP 5: Acid Rain <5.6 + SO2/NO2 | General reducing vs Photo oxidative | Ozone Stratosphere + CFC/Freon | BOD high = more pollution |\nBhopal 3 Dec 1984 = MIC + Union Carbide."]},{"f":"./Crux-Tricks/viewer.html?id=ct0447","t":"03 Physics Tricks","b":"Crux & Tricks / Original Memory Tricks / Science / Physics","x":[" ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Physical Quantities & Units\nPHYSICAL QUANTITIES & UNITS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 1 · Units + SI + Practical Units + Prefixes + Dimensions\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke scalar-vector pairs, unit systems, SI units, practical units, derived-unit confusions,\nprefixes aur dimensional formulae ko exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Physical Quantity — Measurable + Number\n• Physical quantity = directly ya indirectly measurable property\n• Fixed numerical value ke saath express ki jaati hai\n• Examples: Mass, Length, Force\nTRICK - “Measure + Number = Physical Quantity”\nNaam ya concept tab physical quantity banta hai jab measurement ke context mein express ho.\n2. Scalar vs Vector — M vs M+D\nScalar = Magnitude Only\nVector = Magnitude + Direction\nDistance\nDisplacement\nSpeed\nVelocity\nMass\nForce\nWork\nAcceleration\nTime\nMomentum\nEnergy\n—\nElectric current\n—\nTemperature\n—\nPressure\n—\nTRICK - “Scalar = Sirf Size; Vector = Size + Side”\nMagnitude only = Scalar.\nMagnitude + direction = Vector.\nEXAM TRAP - “D-S-M / D-V-F”\nDistance-Speed-Mass = Scalar.\nDisplacement-Velocity-Force = Vector.\n3. Fundamental - Derived - Supplementary\nType\nDependency\nExamples\nFundamental\nIndependent\nLength, Mass, Time\nDerived\nFundamental quantities par dependent\nForce, Work, Pressure\nSupplementary\nSource convention: 2 quantities\nPlane angle, Solid angle\nTRICK - “F = Free, D = Dependent, S = 2 Angles”\nFundamental independent; Derived depends; Supplementary source convention mein Plane + Solid angle.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes convention = 7 fundamental + 2 supplementary SI units.\n4. Unit Systems — F-C-M-S\nSystem\nIdentity\nL-M-T\nSource Key Fact\nFPS\nBritish\nFoot-Pound-Second\n1 Pound = 453 gm; source says\nIndia 1826"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Physical Quantities & Units\nCGS\nFrench / Metric\ncm-g-s\nSource says India\nimplementation 1956\nMKS\n—\nm-kg-s\nDeveloped in France\nSI\nInternational\nm-kg-s\nSource links 1960 Paris\nconference; 7+2\nTRICK - “FPS = Foot Pound Second; CGS = Centi Gram Second; MKS = Meter Kilo Second”\nSystem ka naam hi L-M-T base set reveal karta hai.\nTRICK - “SI = 1960 Paris + 7+2”\nSource chapter ka historical recall pair.\n5. Seven Fundamental SI Units — LMT-TELA\nQuantity\nUnit\nSymbol\nLength\nMeter\nm\nMass\nKilogram\nkg\nTime\nSecond\ns\nTemperature\nKelvin\nK\nElectric Current\nAmpere\nA\nLuminous Intensity\nCandela\ncd\nAmount of Substance\nMole\nmol\nTRICK - “LMT-TELA”\nLength - Mass - Time - Temperature - Electric current - Luminous intensity - Amount of substance.\nTRICK - “m kg s / K A cd mol”\nUnit-symbol chain ko 3 + 4 ke block mein bolo.\nSupplementary Quantity\nUnit\nSymbol\nPlane Angle\nRadian\nrad\nSolid Angle\nSteradian\nsr\n6. Astronomy Distance Trio — PC > LY > AU\nUnit\nValue\nUse\nParsec\n3.26 light years = 3.08 x 10^16 m\nAstronomical distance\nLight Year\n9.46 x 10^15 m\nLight travels in one year\nAU\n1.496 x 10^11 m\nEarth-Sun distance\nTRICK - “P-L-A = Parsec > Light Year > AU”\nDistance order: PC > LY > AU.\nEXAM TRAP - “Parsec = 3.26 LIGHT YEARS, not AU”\nDirect source trap.\n7. Tiny / Atomic / FPS Units\nUnit\nValue / Equivalent\nHook\nAngstrom\n10^-10 m\nAtomic distance\namu\n1.66 x 10^-27 kg\nAtomic mass\nSlug\n14.59 kg\nFPS mass\nSvedberg\n10^-13 s\nSedimentation rate"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Physical Quantities & Units\nTRICK - “A-10, amu-27, Svedberg-13”\nAngstrom = 10^-10 m.\namu = 1.66 x 10^-27 kg.\nSvedberg = 10^-13 s.\n8. Special Practical Units — D-C-B-C\nUnit / Limit\nUsed For / Value\nDobson\nOzone layer thickness\nCusec\nFlow of water\nBTU\nHeat\nBarrel\n158.98 litres; oil volume\nChandrasekhar Limit\n1.4 solar masses; white dwarf maximum mass\nTRICK - “Dobson Ozone - Cusec Water - BTU Heat - Barrel Oil”\nSpecial units ko use ke saath pair karo.\nEXAM TRAP - “Chandra = 1.4 Sun”\nChandrasekhar limit = 1.4 solar masses, source notes ke mutabik.\n9. Derived Units — J-N-W-P\nQuantity\nUnit\nSymbol\nWork / Energy\nJoule\nJ\nForce\nNewton\nN\nPower\nWatt\nW\nPressure\nPascal\nPa\nPotential Difference\nVolt\nV\nResistance\nOhm\nOmega\nCapacitance\nFarad\nF\nMagnetic Flux\nWeber\nWb\nFrequency\nHertz\nHz\nCharge\nCoulomb\nC\nTRICK - “Work J, Force N, Power W, Pressure Pa”\nJ-N-W-P = four core mechanical derived units.\nTRICK - “V-O-F-Wb-Hz-C”\nVolt - Ohm - Farad - Weber - Hertz - Coulomb.\nEXAM TRAP - “Weber = Flux; Watt = Power”\nWb aur W ka symbol confusion avoid karo.\n10. Derived Unit Specials — Impulse = Momentum\nQuantity\nUnit\nMomentum\nkg m/s\nImpulse\nN s\nSurface Tension\nN/m\nAngular Velocity\nrad/s\nIlluminance\nLux\nLuminous Flux\nLumen"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Physical Quantities & Units\nTRICK - “Impulse = Force x Time = Ns = Momentum pattern”\nImpulse aur momentum ka dimensional formula same = [MLT^-1].\n11. Prefix Ladder — Exa to Atto\nPower\nPrefix\nSymbol\nPower\nPrefix\nSymbol\n10^18\nExa\nE\n10^-1\nDeci\nd\n10^15\nPeta\nP\n10^-2\nCenti\nc\n10^12\nTera\nT\n10^-3\nMilli\nm\n10^9\nGiga\nG\n10^-6\nMicro\nmu\n10^6\nMega\nM\n10^-9\nNano\nn\n10^3\nKilo\nk\n10^-12\nPico\np\n10^2\nHecto\nh\n10^-15\nFemto\nf\n10^1\nDeca\nda\n10^-18\nAtto\na\nTRICK - “Large: E-P-T-G-M-k-h-da”\n18-15-12-9-6-3-2-1.\nTRICK - “Small: d-c-m-mu-n-p-f-a”\n-1,-2,-3,-6,-9,-12,-15,-18.\nTRICK - “Mega +6 / Micro -6; Giga +9 / Nano -9; Tera +12 / Pico -12”\nOpposite-sign mirror pairs.\nEXAM TRAP - “Kilo = k, Kelvin = K”\nCase-sensitive symbol trap.\n12. Dimensions — Core Ladder\nQuantity\nDimensional Formula\nDensity\n[ML^-3]\nVelocity / Speed\n[LT^-1]\nAcceleration\n[LT^-2]\nMomentum / Impulse\n[MLT^-1]\nForce\n[MLT^-2]\nPressure / Stress / Modulus\n[ML^-1T^-2]\nWork / Energy\n[ML^2T^-2]\nPower\n[ML^2T^-3]\nSurface Tension\n[MT^-2]\nFrequency\n[T^-1]\nTRICK - “v - a - F - W - P = T exponent -1,-2,-2,-2,-3”\nVelocity LT^-1; Acceleration LT^-2; Force MLT^-2; Work ML^2T^-2; Power ML^2T^-3.\nTRICK - “Momentum = Impulse = MLT^-1”\nSame formula pair.\nEXAM TRAP - “Pressure Family = P-S-M = ML^-1T^-2”\nPressure + Stress + Modulus of Elasticity.\n13. Unique Dimension Patterns\nQuantity\nUnique Pattern"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Physical Quantities & Units\nFrequency\n[T^-1] only\nSurface Tension\n[MT^-2] - no L\nDensity\n[ML^-3] - no T\nSpecific Heat\n[L^2T^-2K^-1]\nResistance\n[ML^2T^-3A^-2]\nCapacitance\n[M^-1L^-2T^4A^2]\nElectric Field\n[MLT^-3A^-1]\nTRICK - “Freq only T; Surface no L; Density no T”\nFast elimination ke 3 strongest unique patterns.\n14. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Speed scalar vs Velocity vector\n• Distance scalar vs Displacement vector\n• Mass scalar vs Force vector\n• Source SI convention = 7 fundamental + 2 supplementary\n• 1 Parsec = 3.26 light years, not AU\n• Distance order = Parsec > Light Year > AU\n• Magnetic flux = Weber (Wb), Power = Watt (W)\n• Momentum = Impulse = [MLT^-1]\n• Pressure = Stress = Modulus = [ML^-1T^-2]\n• Kilo symbol k, Kelvin symbol K; Dobson-Ozone, Cusec-Water, BTU-Heat\nEXAM TRAP - “S-V / D-D / M-F / 7+2 / P-L-A / Wb-W / M=I / PSM / k-K / DCB”\n10 traps ko isi short chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Physical quantity = measurable + number\n Scalar sirf magnitude, Vector magnitude+direction; D-S-M scalar vs D-V-F vector\n\n→\n→\nFundamental Free, Derived Dependent, Supplementary source 2 angles\n systems FPS Foot-Pound-Second, CGS cm-g-s, MKS/SI m-kg-\n→\ns; SI source 1960 Paris + 7+2\n LMT-TELA = m kg s K A cd mol; Plane rad, Solid sr\n astronomy P-L-A = Parsec > Light Year > AU;\n→\n→\nParsec = 3.26 LY\n Angstrom 10^-10 m, amu 1.66x10^-27 kg, Slug14.59kg, Svedberg10^-13s\n Dobson ozone, Cusec water, BTU heat,\n→\n→\nBarrel oil, Chandra1.4Sun\n derived J-N-W-P; V-Ohm-Farad-Weber-Hertz-Coulomb; Weber flux not Watt; Impulse Ns = Momentum\n→\nkg m/s\n prefix big E-P-T-G-M-k-h-da and small d-c-m-mu-n-p-f-a; Mega/Micro +/-6, Giga/Nano +/-9, Tera/Pico +/-12; k vs K\n\n→\n→\ndimensions: Density ML^-3, v LT^-1, a LT^-2, Momentum/Impulse MLT^-1, Force MLT^-2, P-S-Modulus ML^-1T^-2, Work ML^2T^-2,\nPower ML^2T^-3, Surface MT^-2, Frequency T^-1.”\nTOP 5: Scalar/Vector pairs | LMT-TELA | Parsec=3.26 LY + P>LY>AU | Weber vs Watt | Momentum=Impulse &\nPressure=Stress=Modulus dimensions."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Motion\nMOTION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 2 · Motion Types + Distance/Displacement + Graphs + Projectile + Circular Motion\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke 1D/2D/3D motion, distance-displacement, speed-velocity, equations, graph rules,\nprojectile formulae aur circular-motion traps ko exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Motion Types — S-R-O\nType\nMeaning\nExamples\nStraight Line\nStraight path\nRunning child; straight-road car\nRotational\nOwn axis about circular path\nFan; bicycle wheel\nOscillatory\nBack-and-forth about mean position\nPendulum; sewing-machine needle\nTRICK - “S-R-O = Straight - Rotate - Oscillate”\nStraight = line; Rotational = own axis; Oscillatory = mean position ke around back-forth.\n2. Dimension of Motion — 1 Car, 2 Projectile, 3 Mosquito\nDimension\nCoordinates\nExamples\n1D\nx only\nCar on straight road\n2D\nx + y\nProjectile, circular motion, planet around\nSun\n3D\nx + y + z\nMosquito, bird, water molecules\nTRICK - “1-Car / 2-Projectile-Circle / 3-Mosquito”\n1D straight road, 2D projectile/circular, 3D flying mosquito.\nEXAM TRAP -\nProjectile = 2D; Circular motion = 2D; Mosquito flying = 3D.\n3. Uniform vs Non-Uniform — Equal vs Unequal\nMotion\nCondition\nDistance-Time Graph\nUniform\nEqual distances in equal time intervals\nStraight line; constant slope\nNon-Uniform\nUnequal distances in equal time intervals\nCurved line\nTRICK - “Uniform = Equal-Equal = Constant Speed”\nDistance-time graph ki constant slope speed ko show karti hai.\n4. Distance vs Displacement — Path vs Shortcut\nFeature\nDistance\nDisplacement\nMeaning\nActual path length\nShortest initial-to-final path\nQuantity\nScalar\nVector\nValue\nAlways positive\nPositive, negative or zero\nFormula\nLength of path\nFinal position - Initial position\nTRICK - “Distance = Drive Path; Displacement = Direct Shortcut”\nDistance scalar; displacement vector.\nEXAM TRAP - “Go 50 + Return 50 = Distance 100, Displacement 0”\nObject move kare to distance zero nahi; displacement zero ho sakta hai."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Motion\n5. Speed vs Velocity — d/t vs x/t\nFeature\nSpeed\nVelocity\nMeaning\nDistance/time\nDisplacement/time + direction\nQuantity\nScalar\nVector\nValue\nAlways positive\nPositive, negative or zero\nAverage\nTotal distance / Total time\nTotal displacement / Total time\nTRICK - “Speed = Scalar + Distance; Velocity = Vector + Displacement”\nS-D / V-D pairing.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSpeed scalar; Velocity vector. Same SI unit m/s, nature different.\n6. Acceleration — Change in Velocity\n• Acceleration = rate of change of velocity\n• a = Delta v / Delta t = (v-u)/t\n• Average acceleration = (v2-v1)/(t2-t1)\n• Vector quantity; SI unit m/s^2\n• Can be positive, negative or zero\n• Negative acceleration = deceleration / retardation\nTRICK - “Acceleration = Velocity Change / Time”\nNegative a = deceleration/retardation.\nEXAM TRAP -\nNegative acceleration ko speed ke saath confuse mat karo; source terminology = deceleration/retardation.\n7. Motion Symbols — U-V-A-T-S\nSymbol\nMeaning\nu\nInitial velocity\nv\nFinal velocity\na\nAcceleration\nt\nTime\ns\nDisplacement\nTRICK - “U-V-A-T-S”\nInitial-Final-Acceleration-Time-Displacement.\n8. Three Equations — V-S-V²\nNo.\nEquation\nUse\n1\nv = u + at\nFinal velocity after time t\n2\ns = ut + 1/2 at^2\nDisplacement after time t\n3\nv^2 = u^2 + 2as\nVelocity-displacement relation\nTRICK - “1st v, 2nd s, 3rd v-square”\nEquation order ko variable se yaad karo: v > s > v^2.\nTRICK - “Free Fall = a\ng, s\nh”\n→\n→\nv = u+gt; h = ut+1/2 gt^2; v^2 = u^2+2gh."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Motion\n9. Graph Master Rule — Slope-Slope-Area\nGraph\nSlope Gives\nArea Rule\nDistance-Time\nSpeed\n—\nDisplacement-Time\nVelocity\n—\nVelocity-Time\nAcceleration\nArea = Displacement\nTRICK - “s-t Slope = Speed/Velocity; v-t Slope = Acceleration; v-t Area = Displacement”\nGraph questions ka master three-rule.\n10. s-t Graph Shapes — Rest / Uniform / Accelerate / Decelerate\nShape\nMotion\nHorizontal line\nRest; v=0\nStraight positive slope\nUniform motion\nUpward curve\nUniform accelerated motion\nDownward curve\nUniform decelerated motion\nEXAM TRAP - “s-t Horizontal = STOP”\nHorizontal s-t line means REST, not uniform motion.\n11. v-t Graph Shapes — Constant / +Slope / -Slope\nShape\nMotion\nHorizontal line\nUniform motion; v constant; a=0\nStraight + slope\nUniform acceleration\nStraight - slope\nUniform deceleration\nUpward curve\nNon-uniform acceleration\nTRICK - “v-t Horizontal = GO Constant”\ns-t horizontal = rest, but v-t horizontal = uniform motion.\nEXAM TRAP - “s-t H = Rest; v-t H = Uniform”\nSame horizontal line, different meaning.\n12. Projectile Formulae — T-H-R\nQuantity\nFormula\nTime of Flight T\n2u sinθ / g\nMaximum Height H\nu^2 sin^2θ / 2g\nRange R\nu^2 sin2θ / g\nTRICK - “Projectile = T-H-R”\nTime-Height-Range formula trio.\n• Path = Parabola\n• Horizontal velocity remains constant if air resistance neglected\n• Vertical velocity changes due to gravity\n• At highest point vertical velocity = 0\nTRICK - “Top Point = Vertical 0, Horizontal Continues”\nHighest point par only vertical component zero."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Motion\n13. Projectile Angles — 45 Range, 90 Height\nCondition\nSource Result\nθ = 45°\nMaximum Range\nθ = 90°\nMaximum Height\nAt maximum range\nRmax = 4 x Hmax - as stated in source notes\nTRICK - “45 = Range; 90 = Height”\n45 ko height aur 90 ko range mat karna.\nTRICK - “Projectile = Parabola”\nSource ideal condition under no-air-resistance framing.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes state: 45° maximum range, 90° maximum height, and Rmax = 4 x Hmax.\n14. Circular Motion — Constant Speed, Changing Velocity\n• Uniform circular motion: speed constant, velocity variable because direction changes\n• Non-uniform circular motion: speed and velocity both variable\n• Examples: electron around nucleus; Moon around Earth\nTRICK - “Circle = Speed Same, Direction Changes, So Velocity Changes”\nUniform circular motion accelerated motion hai because velocity direction changes.\nEXAM TRAP -\nConstant speed ka matlab zero acceleration nahi in uniform circular motion.\n15. Circular Formula Pack — Theta-Omega-v-alpha-a\nQuantity\nFormula / Direction\nAngular displacement θ\nArc Δs / radius r\nAngular velocity ω\nΔθ / Δt\nLinear-angular relation\nv = ωr = 2πnr\nAngular acceleration α\nα = ω/t - source formula\nCentripetal acceleration\na = v^2/r = rω^2; towards centre\nTRICK - “θ\n ω\n v = ωr\n a_c = v²/r”\n→\n→\n→\nCircular-motion formula chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “Centripetal = Centre; Centrifugal = Outward Pseudo”\nDirection trap."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Motion\n16. Master Scalar-Vector Table\nQuantity\nNature\nUnit\nDistance\nScalar\nm\nDisplacement\nVector\nm\nSpeed\nScalar\nm/s\nVelocity\nVector\nm/s\nAcceleration\nVector\nm/s^2\nAngular velocity\nVector\nrad/s\nAngular acceleration\nVector\nrad/s^2\nTRICK - “D-S Scalar; D-V-A-ω-α Vector”\nDistance + Speed = scalar.\nDisplacement + Velocity + Acceleration + angular quantities = vector.\n17. Final Exam Traps — 8 Red Flags\n• Projectile + circular motion = 2D; straight-road car = 1D; mosquito = 3D\n• Distance scalar and always positive; displacement vector and can be zero\n• Speed scalar; velocity and acceleration vectors\n• Negative acceleration = deceleration / retardation\n• s-t slope = speed/velocity; v-t slope = acceleration; v-t area = displacement\n• Horizontal s-t = rest; horizontal v-t = uniform motion\n• Projectile: 45° maximum range; 90° maximum height; path parabola\n• Uniform circular motion = constant speed but variable velocity, so acceleration non-zero\nEXAM TRAP - “2D-3D / D-D / S-V-A / Negative-a / Slope-Area / Horizontal / 45-90 / Circle”\nChapter ke 8 major traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Motion S-R-O = Straight-Rotational-Oscillatory\n dimensions 1-Car, 2-Projectile/Circle, 3-Mosquito\n Uniform equal-equal constant\n→\n→\nspeed, Nonuniform unequal\n Distance path-scalar-positive vs Displacement shortcut-vector +/-/0; Speed distance/time scalar vs\n→\nVelocity displacement/time vector\n Acceleration Δv/Δt, negative = deceleration; UVATS symbols\n equations 1st v=u+at, 2nd\n→\n→\ns=ut+1/2at², 3rd v²=u²+2as; free fall a\ng,s\nh\n graphs: s-t slope speed/velocity, v-t slope acceleration, v-t area displacement; s-t\n→\n→\n→\nhorizontal REST, v-t horizontal UNIFORM\n Projectile THR = 2usinθ/g, u²sin²θ/2g, u²sin2θ/g; path parabola; top vertical v=0; 45\n→\nrange, 90 height; source Rmax=4xHmax\n Circular: constant speed but variable velocity; θ=arc/r, ω=Δθ/Δt, v=ωr=2πnr, source α=ω/t,\n→\ncentripetal a=v²/r=rω² toward centre; centrifugal outward pseudo.”\nTOP 5: Distance vs Displacement | Speed vs Velocity | s-t/v-t slope-area rules | 45° Range vs 90° Height | Uniform circular motion =\nconstant speed but non-zero acceleration."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Laws of Force & Motion\nLAWS OF FORCE & MOTION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 3 · Force + Newton Laws + Momentum + Friction + Circular Force + Torque + Lever\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke force-types, Newton’s laws, momentum-impulse, friction order, centripetal/centrifugal\nforce, torque-couple aur lever classes ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Force — Push/Pull + Shape/Direction/Motion\n• Force object ki shape, direction ya state of motion ko change kar sakta hai\n• Daily-life form = push, pull or hit\n• SI unit = Newton (N); CGS unit = Dyne\n• 1 N = 10^5 dyne; 1 dyne = 10^-5 N\nTRICK - “Force = Shape - Side - State”\nShape, direction aur state of motion ko change karne wala external factor.\nTRICK - “N to Dyne = ×10^5”\n1 Newton = 100000 dyne.\n2. Force Types — C/N + B/U\nType\nMeaning\nExamples / Result\nContact\nPhysical contact required\nFrictional, muscular\nNon-Contact\nNo physical contact\nGravitational, magnetic\nBalanced\nResultant = 0\na = 0; rest OR constant velocity\nUnbalanced\nResultant ≠ 0\na ≠ 0; motion state changes\nTRICK - “C-N = Contact-No Contact; B-U = Balance-Unbalance”\nBalanced = net force zero.\nUnbalanced = net force non-zero.\nTRICK - “200 opposite 200 = 0; 400 opposite 200 = 200 toward larger”\nSource example se resultant-force arithmetic lock karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBalanced force ka matlab hamesha rest nahi; constant velocity bhi ho sakti hai.\n3. Newton’s First Law — Inertia\n• Object at rest remains at rest; moving object uniform straight-line motion continue karta hai unless external force acts\n• Also called Law of Inertia\n• Associated with Galileo’s idea of inertia\n• Inertia = change oppose karne ki tendency\n• Inertia depends on mass; greater mass = greater inertia\n• Types = inertia of rest, motion and direction\nTRICK - “1st = Inertia; Mass = Measure of Inertia”\nFirst law qualitative idea of force deta hai.\nTRICK - “R-M-D = Rest - Motion - Direction”\nInertia ke 3 types.\nEXAM TRAP -\nF = ma First Law se nahi; Second Law se milta hai."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Laws of Force & Motion\n4. Momentum + Newton’s Second Law\n• Linear momentum p = m × v\n• Momentum vector quantity hai\n• SI unit = kg·m/s\n• Newton’s Second Law: rate of change of momentum applied force ke proportional\n• For constant mass: F = ma\nTRICK - “p = mv; 2nd = dp/dt = ma”\nMomentum formula aur quantitative force law ek chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “1 Inertia - 2 F=ma - 3 Action/Reaction”\nNewton laws ka master code.\n5. Impulse — Force-Time = Momentum Change\n• Impulse I = F × Δt\n• I = Δp = m(v-u)\n• SI unit = N·s\n• Examples: hammer strike; catch lete waqt player hands backward move karta hai\nTRICK - “I = FΔt = Δp”\nImpulse = force-time product = change in momentum.\nTRICK - “10 g, 0\n10 m/s = 0.1 N·s”\n→\nSource worked example: 0.01 × 10 = 0.1 N·s.\n6. Newton’s Third Law — Action-Reaction\n• Every action has equal and opposite reaction\n• F1 = -F2\n• Equal magnitude, opposite direction\n• Action-reaction forces different bodies par act karte hain\n• Examples: rocket launch, rowing, swimming, bouncing ball, gun recoil\nTRICK - “3rd = Equal-Opposite-Different Bodies”\nDifferent bodies sabse important trap.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAction-reaction forces cancel nahi karte because they act on different bodies.\n7. Conservation of Linear Momentum\n• Net external force = 0 ho to total linear momentum constant\n• F = dp/dt = 0 > p = constant\n• m1u1 + m2u2 = m1v1 + m2v2\n• Examples: rocket propulsion, gun recoil, person jumps from boat\nTRICK - “External Force ZERO\n Total Momentum SAME”\n→\nMomentum conservation ki necessary source condition.\nTRICK - “10×20 + 4×(-20) = 14v\n v = 8.57 m/s right”\n→\nSource collision example ka final answer."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Laws of Force & Motion\nEXAM TRAP -\nRocket motion source mein momentum conservation + Newton’s Third Law dono se linked hai.\n8. Friction — Formula + Cause\n• Friction contact surfaces ke along tangentially act karta hai\n• Relative motion ko oppose karta hai\n• Cause: surface irregularities + molecular bonding at contact points\n• F = μR\nTRICK - “Friction = μ × Normal Reaction”\nF = μR; μ = coefficient of friction.\n9. Friction Types — L-S-S-R\nType\nMeaning / Condition\nStatic\nBefore motion; self-adjusting\nLimiting\nMaximum static; body about to move; Fs = μsR\nKinetic\nMoving contact surfaces\nSliding\nType of kinetic friction\nRolling\nLeast among listed friction types\nTRICK - “Limiting > Static > Sliding > Rolling”\nSource friction order.\nTRICK - “Rolling = Least\n Wheels/Ball Bearings”\n→\nFriction reduction ka reason.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLimiting friction = maximum static friction.\n10. Friction — Uses, Losses, Control\nIncrease Friction\nDecrease Friction\nGrooves in tyres\nPolish rough surfaces\nSand on snow roads\nLubricants\nRough shoe soles\nLow-friction materials\n—\nBall bearings\n—\nStreamlined shapes in fluids\nTRICK - “Grip = Grooves-Sand-Rough; Glide = Polish-Lube-Bearing-Streamline”\nIncrease vs decrease friction quick split.\n• Advantages: walking, brakes, writing on blackboard\n• Disadvantages: energy loss, lower machine efficiency, wear & tear"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Laws of Force & Motion\n11. Centripetal vs Centrifugal\nFeature\nCentripetal\nCentrifugal\nDirection\nTowards centre\nAway from centre\nNature\nReal/resultant inward force\nApparent / pseudo in rotating frame\nMagnitude form\nF = mv²/r\nSame magnitude form; opposite apparent\ndirection\nExamples\nCar circular path; electron around nucleus\nCream separator; washing-machine dryer\nTRICK - “PETAL Pulls IN; FUGAL Flies OUT”\nCentripetal inward real; centrifugal outward pseudo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCentripetal = centreward real; Centrifugal = outward apparent/pseudo.\n12. Circular Road Formulae\nSituation\nFormula\nMaximum speed on level circular road\nvmax = (μsrg)\n√\nBanking relation\ntan θ = v²/(rg)\nTRICK - “Level Road = μrg; Bank = tanθ = v²/rg”\n√\nCircular-road formula pair.\n13. Torque + Couple\n• Torque = force ka turning tendency about fixed axis\n• τ = r × F = rF sinθ\n• Vector quantity\n• SI unit = N·m\n• Couple = two equal and opposite parallel forces with separated lines of action\n• Moment of couple = Force × perpendicular separation\nTRICK - “Torque = rF sinθ; Unit N·m”\nTurning effect formula + unit.\nTRICK - “Couple = Equal-Opposite-Parallel + Gap”\nGap = perpendicular distance between force lines.\nEXAM TRAP -\nTorque unit N·m hai; source chapter mein vector quantity bhi stated hai.\n14. Lever Basics — P-F-W + Arms\nTerm\nMeaning\nEffort P\nApplied force\nFulcrum F\nRotation point\nLoad W\nLoad to be lifted\nEffort arm a\nEffort-to-fulcrum distance\nLoad arm b\nLoad-to-fulcrum distance\nTRICK - “P-F-W / a-b”\nP effort, F fulcrum, W load; a effort arm, b load arm."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Laws of Force & Motion\n• Principle of moments: P × a = W × b\n• Mechanical Advantage MA = W/P = a/b\nTRICK - “Pa = Wb; MA = W/P = a/b”\nLever ka two-formula pack.\n15. Lever Classes — Middle Person Rule\nClass\nMiddle\nMA\nExamples\n1st\nFulcrum\nCan be >1, =1 or <1\nScissors, see-saw, hammer,\npliers, beam balance\n2nd\nLoad\nAlways >1\nWheelbarrow, lemon squeezer,\nnutcracker, wheel & axle\n3rd\nEffort\nAlways <1\nTongs, ladder, plough\nTRICK - “1-F, 2-L, 3-E”\nClass number se middle element yaad karo.\nTRICK - “L-F-E / F-L-E / F-E-L”\n1st = Fulcrum middle; 2nd = Load middle; 3rd = Effort middle.\nEXAM TRAP - “2nd MA >1; 3rd MA <1; 1st Any”\nMechanical advantage trap.\n16. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Balanced force\n a=0; object constant velocity se move bhi kar sakta hai\n→\n• Gravitational + magnetic = non-contact\n• 1st Inertia; 2nd F=ma; 3rd Action-Reaction\n• Action-reaction different bodies par act karte hain; cancel nahi karte\n• Impulse = FΔt = Δp; unit N·s\n• Momentum conserved only when net external force = 0\n• Limiting = max static; Rolling = least friction\n• Centripetal inward real; Centrifugal outward pseudo\n• Torque τ = rF sinθ; unit N·m\n• Lever: 1st F middle; 2nd L middle; 3rd E middle\nEXAM TRAP - “B-N / 1-2-3 / I / M / Friction / Circular / Torque / Lever”\nChapter ke 10 red flags ko isi sequence mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Force shape-side-state; SI N, CGS dyne, 1N=10^5 dyne\n types Contact/Noncontact + Balanced/Unbalanced; balanced a=0 but\n→\nconstant-v possible\n Newton 1 Inertia, mass measure; inertia R-M-D\n momentum p=mv; 2nd dp/dt\nF=ma; impulse I=FΔt=Δp N·s\n→\n→\n→\n→\n3rd equal-opposite different bodies; rocket-row-swim-recoil\n momentum conservation external F=0, m1u1+m2u2=m1v1+m2v2\n\n→\n→\nfriction F=μR; order Limiting>Static>Sliding>Rolling; rolling least; grip by grooves/sand/rough, reduce by\npolish/lube/bearings/streamline\n centripetal IN real F=mv²/r vs centrifugal OUT pseudo; level-road vmax= μsrg, banking\n→\n√\ntanθ=v²/rg\n torque τ=rFsinθ N·m; couple equal-opposite-parallel with gap\n lever Pa=Wb, MA=W/P=a/b; classes 1-F,2-L,3-E; 2nd\n→\n→\nMA>1,3rd<1,1st any.”\nTOP 5: Balanced force ≠ always rest | 1-2-3 Laws | Impulse=Δp | Limiting>Static>Sliding>Rolling | Lever 1-F, 2-L, 3-E."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Work, Power & Energy\nWORK, POWER & ENERGY — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 4 · Work + Power + KE/PE + Conservation + Energy Conversion\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke work-sign rules, conservative/non-conservative force, power conversions, energy units,\nKE/PE formulae, free-fall conservation aur device-wise energy conversions ko fast exam recall format mein compress kiya gaya\nhai.\n1. Work — F-s-cosθ\n• Work tab hota hai jab applied force displacement produce kare\n• W = F·s·cosθ\n• Work scalar quantity hai; sign angle θ par depend karta hai\n• SI / MKS unit = Joule (J); CGS unit = erg\n• 1 J = 10^7 erg; 1 erg = 1 dyne × 1 cm\nTRICK - “Work = Force × Shift × cosθ”\nF-s-cosθ ko formula order mein yaad karo.\ncosθ hi positive/negative/zero sign decide karta hai.\nTRICK - “J to erg = ×10^7”\n1 J = 10^7 erg; reverse = 1 erg = 10^-7 J.\n2. Work Sign — + / 0 / -\nWork\nAngle\nSource Example\nPositive\n0°\n θ < 90°\n≤\nGravity on freely falling body\nZero\nθ = 90° or 270°\nLifting load sideways; circular motion\nNegative\n90° < θ < 270°\nGravity while lifting body upward\nTRICK - “Same Side + ; Right Angle 0 ; Opposite -”\nFalling body: gravity and displacement same direction\n + work.\n→\nLifting body: gravity opposite displacement\n - work.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Circular = 90° = Work ZERO”\nSource trap: force perpendicular to displacement in circular motion.\n3. Conservative vs Non-Conservative\nFeature\nConservative\nNon-Conservative\nWork depends on\nInitial + final positions only\nInitial/final + path\nPath\nIndependent\nDependent\nClosed path work\n= 0\n≠ 0\nSource examples\nGravitation, electrostatic, magnetic\nFriction, viscous\nTRICK - “Conservative = Coordinates Only + Closed Zero”\nPath independent; closed-path work zero.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSource notes list gravitation, electrostatic and magnetic force under conservative examples.\n4. Power — Work per Time\n• Power = rate of doing work"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Work, Power & Energy\n• P = W/t\n• Scalar quantity\n• SI unit = Watt (W) = J/s\n• 1 HP = 746 W\n• 1 kW = 10^3 W; 1 MW = 10^6 W\nTRICK - “Power = Work / Time; 1 HP = 746 W”\n746 ko 1000 se confuse mat karo.\nTRICK - “kW = 10^3; MW = 10^6”\nKilo 3 zeros; Mega 6 zeros.\nEXAM TRAP -\n1 Horse Power = 746 W, not 1000 W.\n5. Energy — Capacity to Work\n• Energy = capacity to do work\n• Scalar quantity\n• SI unit = Joule\n• Commercial unit of electrical energy = kilowatt-hour (kWh)\nEXAM TRAP - “Work aur Energy dono Joule; Commercial Electricity = kWh”\nkWh energy unit hai, power unit nahi.\n6. Energy Unit Pack — erg / cal / kWh / eV\nUnit\nJoule Equivalent\nerg\n10^-7 J\nCalorie\n4.2 J\nkWh\n3.6 × 10^6 J\neV\n1.6 × 10^-19 J\nTRICK - “7-4.2-3.6-1.6”\nerg 10^-7 J; calorie 4.2 J; kWh 3.6×10^6 J; eV 1.6×10^-19 J.\nEXAM TRAP -\n1 kWh = 3.6×10^6 J; 1 eV = 1.6×10^-19 J.\n7. Forms of Energy — T-E-C-L-S-N-M\nForm\nMemory\nThermal\nHeat\nElectric\nFlow of electric current\nChemical\nChemical reactions\nLight\nSun / light sources\nSound\nSound sources / instruments\nNuclear\nFission or fusion\nMechanical\nKE + PE\nTRICK - “T-E-C-L-S-N-M”\nThermal-Electric-Chemical-Light-Sound-Nuclear-Mechanical."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Work, Power & Energy\nTRICK - “Mechanical = KE + PE”\nSource chapter ka direct definition.\n8. Kinetic Energy — Motion + v²\n• Kinetic energy = energy due to motion\n• KE = 1/2 mv²\n• Momentum relation: KE = p²/(2m) = 1/2 pv\n• Examples: wind mills; fired bullet\n• Kinetic energy always positive in source notes\nTRICK - “KE = Half m v-Square”\nVelocity double ho to v² relation yaad rahe.\nEXAM TRAP - “Same Momentum\n Lighter Mass = Higher KE”\n→\nKE = p²/(2m), so equal p par m kam\n KE zyada.\n→\n9. Potential Energy — Height vs Spring\nType\nFormula\nExamples\nGravitational PE\nU = mgh\nBody at height\nElastic PE\nU = 1/2 kx²\nStretched bow; compressed spring\nTRICK - “Height = mgh; Spring = 1/2 kx²”\nGravitational vs elastic PE formula pair.\nTRICK - “k = spring constant; x = extension/deformation”\nElastic-energy symbols lock karo.\n10. KE vs PE — Motion vs Position\nFeature\nKinetic\nPotential\nDepends on\nMass + velocity\nMass + height/configuration\nFormula\n1/2 mv²\nmgh or 1/2 kx²\nExample\nMoving bullet; running car\nDam water; stretched spring\nCan be zero?\nYes, v = 0\nYes, reference h = 0\nTRICK - “KE = Move; PE = Place”\nMotion vs position/configuration.\n11. Conservation of Energy — Total Constant\n• Energy neither created nor destroyed; only converted from one form to another\n• Total energy of isolated system remains constant\n• Ideal free fall: KE + PE = Total Mechanical Energy = Constant\nTRICK - “Energy Changes Form, Not Total”\nConservation law ka one-line core."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Work, Power & Energy\n12. Free Fall — Top/Mid/Bottom\nPosition\nKE\nPE\nTotal\nHighest\nMinimum (0)\nMaximum\nConstant\nMidway\n1/2 total\n1/2 total\nConstant\nLowest\nMaximum\nMinimum (0)\nConstant\nTRICK - “Top = PE; Bottom = KE; Mid = Half-Half”\nTop PE max/KE0; bottom KE max/PE0.\nEXAM TRAP -\nTotal mechanical energy stays constant in the source free-fall model.\n13. Energy Conversion — Opposite Pairs\nDevice\nConversion\nSolar cell\nSolar/Light\n Electrical\n→\nDynamo\nMechanical\n Electrical\n→\nElectric Motor\nElectrical\n Mechanical\n→\nMicrophone\nSound\n Electrical\n→\nLoudspeaker\nElectrical\n Sound\n→\nSitar\nMechanical\n Sound\n→\nBulb / Tube light / Heater\nElectrical\n Light + Thermal\n→\nBurning candle\nChemical\n Light + Thermal\n→\nBurning coal\nChemical\n Thermal\n→\nBattery / Electric cell\nChemical\n Electrical\n→\nEngine\nThermal\n Mechanical\n→\nPhotoelectric cell\nLight\n Electrical\n→\nTRICK - “Dynamo <-> Motor”\nDynamo: Mechanical\n Electrical.\n→\nMotor: Electrical\n Mechanical.\n→\nTRICK - “Microphone <-> Loudspeaker”\nMicrophone: Sound\n Electrical.\n→\nLoudspeaker: Electrical\n Sound.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Solar Cell + Photoelectric Cell = Light\n Electrical”\n→\nSource notes dono ko same conversion se link karte hain.\n14. Device Chain — C-B-E-S\nTRICK - “Chemical Battery\n Electrical Bulb\n Light/Thermal; Thermal Engine\n Mechanical”\n→\n→\n→\nBattery = Chemical\nElectrical.\n→\nBulb/heater = Electrical\nLight+Thermal.\n→\nEngine = Thermal\nMechanical.\n→\nSitar = Mechanical\nSound.\n→\n15. Source Worked Examples — Number Hooks\nExample\nSource Result\nF=40N, s=10m, θ=30°\nW = 346.41 J\nm=40kg, h=2m, t=4s\nWork 784 J; Power 196 W"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Work, Power & Energy\nm=1500kg, v=72km/h=20m/s\nKE = 3 × 10^5 J\nm=40kg, h=5m, g=10m/s²\nPE = 2000 J\nTRICK - “346.41 / 196 / 3×10^5 / 2000”\nSource ke four worked-example answers ka recall pack.\n16. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Work scalar; W = Fs cosθ; sign cosθ decides\n• Circular motion: force perpendicular displacement\n work = 0\n→\n• 1 J = 10^7 erg; 1 erg = 10^-7 J\n• Power = W/t; SI unit Watt = J/s\n• 1 HP = 746 W, not 1000 W\n• 1 calorie = 4.2 J; 1 kWh = 3.6×10^6 J; 1 eV = 1.6×10^-19 J\n• KE = 1/2mv²; equal momentum par lighter body has higher KE\n• Gravitational PE = mgh; elastic PE = 1/2kx²\n• Highest point: PE max/KE0; lowest: KE max/PE0\n• Dynamo M\nE; Motor E\nM; Microphone S\nE; Loudspeaker E\nS\n→\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “cosθ - Circle - J/erg - Watt - 746 - Units - KE - PE - FreeFall - Devices”\nChapter ke 10 red flags isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Work W=Fs cosθ scalar; J SI, erg CGS, 1J=10^7erg\n sign: same +, 90° zero, opposite -; falling gravity +, lifting gravity -, circular\n→\nwork0\n Conservative path-independent/closed0 vs Non-conservative path-dependent\n Power P=W/t scalar, Watt=J/s, HP746W,\n→\n→\nkW10^3, MW10^6\n Energy capacity-to-work; commercial kWh; units erg10^-7J, cal4.2J, kWh3.6×10^6J, eV1.6×10^-19J\n forms T-E-\n→\n→\nC-L-S-N-M; Mechanical=KE+PE\n KE=1/2mv²=p²/2m=1/2pv; same p lighter mass higher KE\n PE: height mgh, spring1/2kx²\n\n→\n→\n→\nconservation: total isolated constant; free fall Top PE, Mid half-half, Bottom KE\n Conversions: Solar/Photoelectric Light\nElectrical;\n→\n→\nDynamo M\nE <-> Motor E\nM; Microphone S\nE <-> Loudspeaker E\nS; Sitar M\nS; Battery C\nE; Engine T\nM; Candle C\nL+T.”\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nTOP 5: Circular work=0 | HP=746 W | kWh=3.6×10^6 J | Equal momentum: lighter\n higher KE | Dynamo<->Motor &\n→\nMicrophone<->Loudspeaker."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Gravitation\nGRAVITATION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 5 · Newton Law + G/g + Kepler + Satellites + Escape Velocity + Mass/Weight\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke G vs g, g-variation, Kepler laws, orbital/escape velocity, geostationary-polar satellites\naur mass-weight traps ko fast exam-recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Gravitation — Newton + Cavendish\n• Gravitation = universe ke kisi bhi do bodies ke beech attraction force\n• Universal law formulated by Isaac Newton\n• Universal gravitational constant G experimentally determined by Henry Cavendish in 1798\nTRICK - “Newton Law; Cavendish G-1798”\nNewton = law.\nCavendish = G ka experimental determination.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLaw aur G-determination ke scientists ko interchange mat karna.\n2. Universal Law — Product Up, Distance-Square Down\n• F m1m2 / r²\n∝\n• F = G(m1m2)/r²\n• Force masses ke product ke directly proportional\n• Centres ke distance ke square ke inversely proportional\nTRICK - “Mass Product UP; r² DOWN”\nm1m2 numerator; r² denominator.\n3. G vs g — Fixed vs Variable\nFeature\nG\ng\nMeaning\nUniversal gravitational constant\nGravitational acceleration\nValue\n6.67 × 10^-11 N·m²/kg²\nEarth near surface\n 9.8 m/s²\n≈\nNature\nUniversal / fixed\nChanges with location\nDepends on location?\nNo\nYes\nTRICK - “Capital G = Global Fixed; small g = Geography Changes”\nG everywhere same.\ng location ke saath change hota hai.\nEXAM TRAP - “G = 6.67 × 10^-11; g = 9.8”\nValue pair.\n4. g Formula + Core Values\n• g = GMe/Re²\n• Earth surface\n 9.8 m/s²\n≈\n• Moon surface\n 1/6 of Earth\n 1.63 m/s²\n≈\n≈\n• Earth centre = 0\n• g falling body ke mass par depend nahi karta\nTRICK - “Earth 9.8; Moon 1/6; Centre 0”\nThree-value chain."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Gravitation\nEXAM TRAP -\ng does not depend on mass of falling body.\n5. g Variation — P-E-Up-Down-Centre\nLocation\ng\nWhy / Memory\nPoles\nMaximum\nCloser to centre + rotation effect minimum\nEquator\nMinimum\nFarther + rotational effect maximum\nAltitude increases\nDecreases\nDistance from centre increases\nDepth increases\nDecreases\nEffective attracting mass reduces\nEarth centre\n0\nNet pull cancels\nTRICK - “Pole Peak; Equator Low; Up Down Both g Down; Centre Zero”\nP > E; altitude\n g\n; depth\n g\n; centre 0.\n↑\n↓\n↑\n↓\nTRICK - “Altitude\n 1/r²; Depth\n Linear Down”\n≈\n≈\nSource recall: altitude with distance inverse-square; depth approx linearly to zero.\nEXAM TRAP -\ng maximum poles, minimum equator — reverse mat karna.\n6. Kepler’s 3 Laws — E-A-T\nLaw\nName\nKey Point\n1\nLaw of Orbits\nElliptical orbit; Sun at one focus\n2\nLaw of Equal Areas\nEqual areas in equal times; faster perihelion,\nslower aphelion\n3\nHarmonic Law\nT² a³\n∝\nTRICK - “1-Ellipse, 2-Areas, 3-T²a³”\nKepler = E-A-T.\nTRICK - “Peri = Fast; Aphe = Slow”\nSecond-law speed trap.\nEXAM TRAP - “Sun at FOCUS, not Centre”\nLaw 1 ka common MCQ trap.\nTRICK - “Law 2 = Constant Areal Speed = Angular Momentum Link”\nSource notes Law 2 ko conservation of angular momentum se connect karte hain.\n7. Satellite Basics — Free Fall + Weightlessness\n• Satellite = body revolving around a planet\n• Moon = natural satellite; INSAT/GPS-type spacecraft = artificial satellites\n• Orbital velocity near Earth Vo = (gR)\n 8 km/s\n√\n≈\n• Satellite in orbit continuously free fall mein hota hai\n• Apparent weight in orbit = 0; mass unchanged\nTRICK - “Orbit = Free Fall; Weight 0, Mass Same”\nWeightlessness means apparent weight zero, mass zero nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Gravitation\nEXAM TRAP -\nMass unchanged during orbital weightlessness.\n8. Geostationary — 24 / 36,000 / Equator / W\nE\n→\nFeature\nGeostationary\nTime period\n24 h\nHeight\n 36,000 km above Earth\n≈\nOrbital plane\nEquatorial\nDirection\nWest\n East\n→\nAppearance\nStationary relative to Earth surface\nUses\nTV, communication, weather monitoring\nIndian example\nINSAT series\nTRICK - “Geo = 24-36-E-WE”\n24 h, 36,000 km, Equator, West-to-East.\nEXAM TRAP - “36,000 not 3,600”\nZero count ka direct exam trap.\n9. Geostationary vs Polar\nFeature\nGeostationary\nPolar\nOrbit\nEquatorial\nNear poles\nHeight\n 36,000 km\n≈\n 500-800 km\n≈\nPeriod\n24 h\nMuch shorter\nMain use\nCommunication/weather/TV\nRemote sensing/mapping/surveillance\nTRICK - “GEO = Communication; POLAR = Picture/Mapping”\nUse-based distinction.\n10. Orbital vs Escape Velocity — 8 vs 11.2\nQuantity\nFormula\nEarth Value\nOrbital velocity Vo\n(gR)\n√\n 8 km/s\n≈\nEscape velocity Ve\n(2gR)\n√\n11.2 km/s\nRelation\nVe = 2 Vo\n√\n 41% higher\n≈\nTRICK - “Orbit 8; Escape 11.2; Ve = 2 Vo”\n√\n8\n 11.2 relation pack.\n→\nTRICK - “Escape Earth 11.2; Moon 2.35”\nEarth-Moon escape value pair.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEscape velocity projectile mass par depend nahi karta; planet mass/radius par karta hai."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Gravitation\n11. Escape Speed Meaning\n• Minimum launch speed needed to escape planet gravitational field permanently without further propulsion\n• Below 11.2 km/s from Earth: body eventually returns\n• At 11.2 km/s: just escapes\n• Above it: escapes with excess kinetic energy\nTRICK - “Below Return; Equal Just Escape; Above Extra KE”\nEarth escape threshold logic.\n12. Mass vs Weight — m vs mg\nFeature\nMass\nWeight\nMeaning\nAmount of matter / intrinsic property\nGravitational force\nFormula\n—\nW = mg\nSI unit\nkg\nnewton N\nType\nScalar\nVector\nChanges with location?\nNo\nYes\nEarth centre\nSame\n0\nMoon\nSame\n1/6 Earth weight\nTRICK - “Mass = Matter = Same; Weight = mg = g Changes”\nMass fixed; weight location dependent.\nTRICK - “Moon: Mass Same, Weight 1/6”\nClassic exam pair.\nEXAM TRAP -\nWeightlessness = apparent weight 0, mass 0 nahi.\n13. Balance Trap — Spring vs Beam\n• Spring balance measures weight\n• Beam balance compares mass\nEXAM TRAP - “Spring = Weight; Beam = Mass”\nInstrument pair.\n14. Formula + Value Flash Table\nItem\nRecall\nG\n6.67 × 10^-11 N·m²/kg²\ng Earth\n9.8 m/s²\ng Moon\n 1.63 m/s²\n g/6\n≈\n≈\ng Earth centre\n0\nVo Earth\n 8 km/s\n≈\nVe Earth\n11.2 km/s\nVe Moon\n2.35 km/s\nGeo height / period\n 36,000 km / 24 h\n≈\nNewton gravitation\nF = Gm1m2/r²\nWeight\nW = mg\nKepler 3\nT² a³\n∝\nOrbital / Escape\nVo= gR; Ve= 2gR= 2Vo\n√\n√\n√"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Gravitation\nTRICK - “6.67e-11 / 9.8 / 8 / 11.2 / 2.35 / 36k / 24”\nChapter ka number-chain revision.\n15. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Newton gave law; Cavendish determined G in 1798\n• G fixed universal; g varies with location\n• g poles maximum, equator minimum, centre zero\n• Mass same everywhere; weight changes with g\n• Kepler 1 ellipse; Sun at one focus, not centre\n• Kepler 2 equal areas/equal times; perihelion faster, aphelion slower\n• Satellite orbit = continuous free fall; apparent weight zero, mass same\n• Geostationary = 24 h,\n36,000 km, equatorial, West\nEast\n≈\n→\n• Orbital\n8 km/s; Escape Earth 11.2 km/s; Ve= 2Vo\n≈\n√\n• Escape velocity independent of projectile mass\nEXAM TRAP - “Newton/Cavendish - G/g - P/E/C - Mass/Weight - K1/K2 - Satellite - Geo - 8/11.2 - Mass-\nindependent”\nChapter ke 10 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Newton gravitation law F=Gm1m2/r²; Cavendish G-1798; G=6.67×10^-11 fixed vs g=9.8 variable\n g = GMe/Re²; Moon g\n1/6, centre0;\n→\n≈\n\nPole Peak, Equator Low, altitude\ng\n, depth\ng\n\n Kepler E-A-T: 1 ellipse Sun focus, 2 equal areas/peri fast-aphe slow, 3 T² a³; law2\n↑↓\n↑↓→\n∝\nangular-momentum link\n satellite = continuous free fall; Vo= gR\n8 km/s; weightlessness apparent weight0, mass same\n\n→\n√\n≈\n→\nGeostationary 24h + 36,000km + equator + West\nEast + TV/communication/weather; Polar 500-800km + remote sensing/mapping\n\n→\n→\nEscape Ve= 2gR= 2Vo; Earth11.2, Moon2.35; below-return/equal-just-escape/above-extra-KE; independent of projectile mass\n Mass\n√\n√\n→\n\nmatter scalar kg same; Weight W=mg vector N varies; centre weight0, Moon weight1/6; Spring balance weight, Beam balance mass.”\nTOP 5: G fixed vs g variable | Pole max-Equator min-Centre 0 | Kepler 1/2/3 = Ellipse/Areas/T² a³ | Geo 24h-36,000km | Orbit 8 vs\n∝\nEscape 11.2 and Ve= 2Vo.\n√"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\nMECHANICAL PROPERTIES OF MATTER — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 6 · Elasticity + Pressure + Fluids + Flotation + Surface Tension + Viscosity + Bernoulli\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke stress-strain, elastic moduli, atmospheric/fluid pressure, Pascal, Archimedes, surface\ntension, capillarity, viscosity aur Bernoulli ke high-memory facts ko exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Matter States — S-L-G-P-B\nState\nMechanical Hook\nSolid\nElasticity; definite shape + volume\nLiquid\nPressure, flotation, surface tension, capillarity, viscosity\nGas\nAtmospheric pressure\nPlasma\n4th state\nBose-Einstein Condensate\n5th state\nTRICK - “S-L-G-P-B = Solid-Liquid-Gas-Plasma-BEC”\nPlasma = 4th; Bose-Einstein Condensate = 5th.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPlasma 4th, BEC 5th — order ulta mat karna.\n2. Stress vs Strain — Unit vs No Unit\n• Stress = restoring force per unit area; Stress = F/A\n• Stress SI unit = N/m² = Pa\n• Strain = change in dimension / original dimension\n• Strain dimensionless hai; no unit\nStress Type\nMeaning\nLongitudinal-Compressive\nLength decreases\nLongitudinal-Tensile\nLength increases\nNormal Stress\nForce perpendicular to surface\nShear Stress\nForce tangential to surface\nStrain Type\nFormula\nMeaning\nLongitudinal / Linear\nΔL/L\nLength change\nVolumetric\nΔV/V\nVolume change\nShearing\nΔx/L\nAngular deformation\nEXAM TRAP - “Stress has Pa; Strain has NO unit”\nDono ka sabse common exam confusion.\n3. Hooke + Elastic Moduli — Y-β-η\n• Hooke’s Law: elastic limit ke andar Stress Strain\n∝\n• Elastic modulus E = Stress/Strain\n• Modulus unit = N/m²; dimension = [ML^-1T^-2]\n• Law named after Robert Hooke\nModulus\nRatio / Formula\nBest Memory\nYoung’s Y\nLongitudinal Stress / Longitudinal Strain; Y =\nMgL/(πr²ΔL)\nLength\nBulk β\nNormal Stress / Volumetric Strain; β = -PV/ΔV\nVolume\nRigidity η\nShear Stress / Shear Strain; η = F/(Aθ) = FL/(AΔx)\nShape\nTRICK - “Y = Length; β = Volume; η = Shape”\nY-β-η ko Length-Volume-Shape ke saath lock karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\nTRICK - “Liquids/Gases = Bulk Only”\nSource ke mutabik liquids aur gases ke paas Young’s ya rigidity modulus nahi.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBulk modulus mein negative sign compression ke under volume decrease ki wajah se.\n4. Thrust vs Pressure\nFeature\nThrust\nPressure\nMeaning\nForce perpendicular to surface\nThrust per unit area\nFormula\n—\nP = F/A\nSI Unit\nN\nPa = N/m²\nTRICK - “Thrust = Force; Pressure = Force/Area”\nPressure area ke saath inverse effect dikhata hai for same force.\n5. Atmospheric Pressure — Barometer + Altitude\n• 1 atm\n 10^5 Pa\n≈\n• Atmospheric pressure measured by barometer\n• Altitude badhne par atmospheric pressure decreases\nBarometer Trend\nWeather\nFalls suddenly\nStorm\nFalls slowly\nRain\nRises slowly\nClear weather\nTRICK - “Sudden Fall = Storm; Slow Fall = Rain; Slow Rise = Clear”\nBarometer weather chain.\nTRICK - “High Altitude: Pressure\n + Boiling Point\n + Cooking Time\n”\n↓\n↓\n↑\nPressure cooker opposite: pressure\n\n boiling point\n\n cooking faster.\n↑→\n↑→\nEXAM TRAP -\nHigh altitude par pressure aur boiling point dono decrease.\n6. Density + Relative Density\nQuantity\nFormula / Value\nExam Hook\nDensity ρ\nM/V\nSI kg/m³\nRelative Density\nρsubstance / ρwater at 4°C\nNo unit; hydrometer\nPure Water\n10³ kg/m³\nMaximum density at 4°C\nIce\n0.9 g/cm³\nLess dense than water\nTRICK - “Water = 1000 + Max at 4°C; Ice = 0.9”\nDensity number chain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nRelative density has no unit; source notes hydrometer as instrument.\n7. Hydrostatic Pressure + Pascal\n• Pressure at depth h: P = hρg\n• Total pressure: Ptotal = Pa + hρg"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\n• Source example at 10 m water depth: total\n 2.01×10^5 Pa\n 2 atm\n≈\n≈\nTRICK - “Depth\n\n Pressure\n : hρg”\n↑→\n↑\nHydrostatic pressure formula.\n• Pascal’s Law: enclosed fluid par applied pressure equally every direction transmit hota hai\n• Applications: Hydraulic Lift, Hydraulic Brakes, Hydraulic Press\nTRICK - “Pascal = Lift-Brake-Press”\nHydraulic trio.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHydraulic lift/brakes/press = Pascal, Bernoulli nahi.\n8. Archimedes + Flotation\n• Immersed body experiences upward buoyant force equal to weight of displaced fluid\n• Buoyant force / upthrust = weight of displaced fluid\n• Apparent weight in fluid = actual weight - buoyant force\n• Applications: life preservers, submarines, lactometers\nCondition\nResult\nExamples\nWeight > Buoyant force\nSinks\nIron nail\nWeight = Buoyant force\nEquilibrium / submerged float\nSubmarine, neutral body\nWeight < Buoyant force\nRises / partly floats\nShip, wood block\nTRICK - “W>B Sink; W=B Balance; W<B Rise”\nFlotation condition chain.\nTRICK - “Archimedes = Upthrust = Displaced Fluid Weight”\nPrinciple ka one-line core.\n9. Floating Ice — 1/10 Up, 9/10 Down\n• Floating ice ka about 1/10 water ke above aur 9/10 submerged hota hai\n• Floating ice completely melt hone par water level unchanged rehta hai\n• Lactometer aur hydrometer flotation principle par work karte hain\nEXAM TRAP - “Ice = 1 Up : 9 Down; Melt = Level Same”\nIceberg trap ko number ke saath yaad karo.\n10. Surface Tension — F/l\n• Surface tension = force per unit length in liquid surface plane\n• T = F/l = mg/l\n• Unit = N/m\n• Numerically equivalent surface-energy unit = J/m²\n• Surface energy = W/ΔA\nTRICK - “Surface Tension = Force/Length; Surface Energy = Work/Area”\nN/m vs J/m² pair.\nCondition\nEffect\nTemperature increases\nSurface tension decreases\nCritical temperature\nSurface tension = 0\nSoap added\nSurface tension decreases\nKerosene spread\nSurface tension decreases"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\nTRICK - “Heat\n\n ST\n; Critical\n 0”\n↑→\n↓\n→\nTemperature trend.\n• Wet brush hairs stick together\n surface tension\n→\n• Needle can float on water\n surface tension\n→\n• Raindrops spherical\n surface tension minimizes surface area\n→\n11. Capillarity — Thin Tube, More Rise\n• Capillarity = narrow tube mein liquid ka rise/fall due to surface tension\n• Examples: plant roots/stems water transport, lamp wick oil rise, wetting, fine capillary movement\n• Capillary rise 1 / tube radius\n∝\nEXAM TRAP - “Radius Thin\n Rise High”\n→\nCapillary rise inverse to tube radius.\n12. Viscosity — Fluid Internal Friction\n• Viscosity adjacent fluid layers ke relative motion ko oppose karne wali internal friction hai\n• Property of both liquids and gases\n• F = -ηA(Δv/Δz)\n• η = FΔz/(AΔv)\n• SI unit = kg·m^-1·s^-1; also called poiseuille (Pl)\nTRICK - “Viscosity = Fluid Friction”\nSolids ki property nahi; liquids + gases.\nHigh\n Low Viscosity\n→\nOrder\nTypical order\nHoney > Water > Kerosene > Petrol > Gas\nTRICK - “H-W-K-P-G”\nHoney > Water > Kerosene > Petrol > Gas.\n13. Temperature vs Viscosity — Opposite Trend\nSubstance\nTemperature\n\n Viscosity\n↑→\nLiquids\nDecreases\nGases\nIncreases\nEXAM TRAP - “Liquid Low; Gas Grow”\nTemperature badhne par Liquid viscosity\n, Gas viscosity\n.\n↓\n↑\n14. Fluid Flow — Laminar vs Turbulent\nFlow\nNature\nStreamline / Laminar\nOrderly regular paths; usually low velocity\nTurbulent\nIrregular chaotic paths; above critical velocity\nCritical Velocity\nMaximum velocity up to which streamline flow persists\nTRICK - “Laminar = Lines; Turbulent = Trouble”\nOrdered vs chaotic.\n15. Bernoulli — Fast Flow = Low Pressure\n• Ideal incompressible fluid in streamline flow ke liye total energy per unit volume constant\n• P + ρgh + 1/2ρv² = constant\n• Based on conservation of energy"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\n• Fast flow\n low pressure; slow flow\n high pressure\n→\n→\nTRICK - “Bernoulli = Fast LOW, Slow HIGH”\nVelocity-pressure inverse recall.\nApplication\nSource Logic\nAeroplane Wings\nFaster air above\n lower pressure\n lift\n→\n→\nVenturimeter\nNarrow section pressure difference\n flow speed\n→\nMagnus Effect\nSpinning ball pressure difference\n curve\n→\nTin Roof\nFast wind above\n low pressure\n upward lift\n→\n→\nTrain Platform Suction\nFast train lowers nearby pressure\nTRICK - “A-V-M-T-T = Bernoulli Applications”\nAeroplane - Venturimeter - Magnus - Tin roof - Train platform.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBernoulli applies to ideal incompressible fluid in streamline flow.\n16. Formula Flash\nQuantity / Law\nFormula / Unit\nStress\nF/A ; N/m²\nStrain\nΔL/L, ΔV/V, Δx/L ; no unit\nElastic Modulus\nStress/Strain ; N/m²\nPressure\nF/A ; Pa\nHydrostatic Pressure\nhρg\nDensity\nM/V ; kg/m³\nSurface Tension\nF/l ; N/m\nSurface Energy\nW/ΔA ; J/m²\nViscous Force\n-ηA(Δv/Δz)\nBernoulli\nP + ρgh + 1/2ρv² = constant\n17. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Strain dimensionless hai; no unit\n• Plasma 4th state; Bose-Einstein Condensate 5th\n• Liquids/gases have bulk modulus, not Young’s or rigidity modulus\n• High altitude: pressure\n and boiling point\n, so cooking longer\n↓\n↓\n• Water maximum density at 4°C; ice less dense\n• Hydraulic lift/brakes/press = Pascal’s Law\n• Buoyant force = weight of displaced fluid\n• Floating ice melts\n water level unchanged\n→\n• Liquid viscosity\n with temperature; gas viscosity\n↓\n↑\n• Aeroplane lift + Venturimeter = Bernoulli applications\nEXAM TRAP - “Strain-P/BEC-Bulk-Altitude-Water-Pascal-Buoyancy-Ice-Viscosity-Bernoulli”\nChapter ke 10 core traps isi order mein revise karo."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Mechanical Properties of Matter\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Matter S-L-G-P-B: Plasma4, BEC5\n Stress F/A Pa vs Strain ratio no-unit; stress types compress/tensile/normal/shear; strain\n→\nlinear/volume/shear\n Hooke stress strain; moduli Y-length, β-volume, η-shape; liquids+gases bulk only; β negative in compression\n→\n∝\n Thrust force, Pressure F/A; 1 atm\n10^5Pa; barometer sudden fall storm, slow fall rain, slow rise clear; altitude pressure\n +\n→\n≈\n↓\nboiling point\n\n Density M/V; water1000 max at4°C; ice0.9; Hydro P=hρg; Pascal = lift-brake-press\n Archimedes\n↓→\n→\nupthrust=displaced-fluid weight; W>B sink, W=B balance, W<B rise; ice1/10 up-9/10 down, melt level same\n Surface Tension F/l\n→\nN/m, Surface Energy W/ΔA J/m²; heat\n ST\n; capillary thin tube\nhigher rise\n Viscosity fluid friction, H>W>K>P>G; liquid temp\n\n↑\n↓\n→\n→\n↑\nviscosity\n, gas\n\n laminar orderly vs turbulent chaotic\n Bernoulli P+ρgh+1/2ρv² constant, conservation of energy; Fast flow LOW\n↓\n↑→\n→\npressure; Aeroplane-Venturi-Magnus-Tin roof-Train platform.”\nTOP 5: Stress Pa vs Strain no-unit | Y-Length β-Volume η-Shape | Pascal hydraulic trio | Ice melt level same | Liquid viscosity\n but Gas\n↓\nviscosity\n with heat.\n↑"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\nTEMPERATURE, HEAT & THERMODYNAMICS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 7 · Scales + Thermometers + Heat + Expansion + State Change + Heat Transfer + Thermodynamic\nLaws\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke temperature-scale conversions, thermometer ranges, specific/latent heat, thermal\nexpansion, water anomaly, phase-change effects, heat-transfer methods aur thermodynamic laws ko fast exam-recall format mein\ncompress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Temperature vs Heat — Measure vs Transfer\nConcept\nCore Idea\nUnit / Hook\nTemperature\nHotness/coldness ka measure\nKelvin K; thermometer\nHeat\nTemperature difference ke kaaran transferred\nenergy\nJoule J; hot > cold\nThermodynamics\nHeat-mechanical energy relation\nP, V, T variables\nTRICK - “Temperature = Measure; Heat = Transfer”\nHeat naturally hotter body se colder body ki taraf flow karta hai.\nEXAM TRAP -\nTemperature aur heat same cheez nahi: temperature measure hai, heat transferred energy.\n2. Temperature Scales — C-F-R-K-Ra\nScale\nFreezing\nBoiling\nDivisions\nCelsius\n0°C\n100°C\n100\nFahrenheit\n32°F\n212°F\n180\nReaumur\n0°R\n80°R\n80\nKelvin\n273 K\n373 K\n100\nRankin\n492 Ra\n672 Ra\n180\nTRICK - “C-F-R-K-Ra = 100-180-80-100-180”\nScale order ke saath interval divisions lock karo.\nTRICK - “Universal Relation”\n(C-0)/100 = (F-32)/180 = (R-0)/80 = (K-273)/100 = (Ra-492)/180.\nTRICK - “60°F = 288.5 K”\nSource solved conversion example ka final answer.\n3. Fixed Temperature Facts — 0 / -40 / 273.16\nFact\nSource Value\nAbsolute zero\n-273.15°C = 0 K\nCelsius = Fahrenheit\n-40°C = -40°F\nFahrenheit = Kelvin\n574.25°F = 574.25 K\nFahrenheit = Reaumur\n-25.6°F = -25.6°R\nHuman body\n37°C = 98.4°F = 310.5 K\nTriple point of water\n273.16 K\nTRICK - “-40 = C and F Same”\nCelsius-Fahrenheit ka only equal reading source notes mein -40.\nEXAM TRAP - “Absolute 0K; Triple 273.16K”\nAbsolute zero aur triple-point pair."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\n4. Thermometers — Range Memory\nThermometer\nRange\nSpecial Use\nGas (Nitrogen)\n500°C to 1500°C\nVery high temperatures\nPlatinum\n-200°C to 1000°C\nWide range, precision\nThermocouple\n-200°C to 1600°C\nWidest listed range\nTotal Radiation\nAbove 800°C\nVery high temp, no contact\nAlcohol\nBelow -40°C; fp\n -115°C\n≈\nVery low temperatures\nClinical\n35°C to 42°C\nHuman body\nTRICK - “Clinical 35-42; Thermocouple -200 to 1600”\nSource ke two highest-frequency thermometer ranges.\nTRICK - “Alcohol for Very Low; Pyrometer No Contact”\nAlcohol preferred because mercury freezes near -39°C.\nTotal-radiation thermometer very high temperature without contact.\nEXAM TRAP -\nWidest listed thermometer range = Thermocouple, source table ke mutabik.\n5. Heat Units — J-cal-BTU\nItem\nValue / Unit\nSI heat unit\nJoule J\nCGS heat unit\nCalorie cal\nBritish unit\nBTU\n1 BTU\n252 cal\nMechanical equivalent\n1 cal = 4.186 J\nTRICK - “1 cal = 4.186 J; 1 BTU = 252 cal”\n4.186 aur 252 ko number pair mein yaad karo.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBTU = 252 cal, not 1000 cal.\n6. Specific Heat — Q = msΔT\n• Specific heat = unit mass ka temperature 1°C raise karne ke liye required heat\n• s = Q/(mΔT), hence Q = msΔT\n• SI unit = J/kg°C; CGS = cal/g°C\n• Water specific heat = 4186 J/kg°C = 1 cal/g°C\n• Source uses: hot-water bottle, crop frost protection, vehicle radiator cooling\nTRICK - “Specific = Q / mΔT; Water = 4186 = 1 cal/g°C”\nWater ka high specific heat applications se jodo.\nTRICK - “2 kg, 30\n100, s=300 => Q=4.2×10^4 J”\n→\nSource solved example answer.\n7. Latent Heat — State Changes, Temperature Same\n• Latent heat = state change during absorbed/released heat without temperature change\n• L = Q/m\n• SI = J/kg; CGS = cal/g\nType\nChange\nValue"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\nFusion\nSolid > Liquid\n80 cal/g\nVaporisation\nLiquid > Gas\n539 cal/g\nTRICK - “Fusion 80; Vapor 539”\nVaporisation latent heat much larger than fusion.\nEXAM TRAP - “Phase Change = Heat Changes, Temperature Doesn’t”\nState-change ka most important conceptual trap.\nTRICK - “Steam Burn More Severe”\nSource reason: vaporisation latent heat 539 cal/g > fusion 80 cal/g.\n8. Calorimetry — Lost = Gained\n• Heat Lost by Hot Object = Heat Gained by Cold Object\n• Based on conservation of thermal energy in an isolated system\n• Used to determine unknown specific heats\n• Ideal assumption: surroundings ko heat loss nahi\nTRICK - “Hot Lost = Cold Gained”\nCalorimetry ka one-line equation.\n9. Thermal Expansion — α : β : γ = 1 : 2 : 3\nExpansion\nSymbol\nFormula\nDimension Change\nLinear\nα\nΔL/(LΔt)\nLength\nArea/Superficial\nβ\nΔA/(AΔt)\nArea\nVolumetric\nγ\nΔV/(VΔt)\nVolume\nTRICK - “α-β-γ = 1-2-3”\nβ = 2α; γ = 3α.\nTRICK - “Railway Gaps = Summer Expansion”\nThermal-expansion application.\nEXAM TRAP -\nα : β : γ = 1 : 2 : 3 is a direct high-frequency source trap.\n10. Anomalous Water — 0 to 4 Contracts\nTemperature\nBehaviour\n0°C > 4°C\nWater contracts; volume decreases\nAt 4°C\nVolume minimum; density maximum\nAbove 4°C\nWater expands; volume increases\nTRICK - “0\n4 Contract; 4 = Density Max; >4 Expand”\n→\nWater ka anomalous sequence.\nTRICK - “Pond: 4°C Water Sinks, Surface Can Freeze”\nDensest 4°C water sinks; lower water liquid reh sakta hai.\nEXAM TRAP -\nWater densest at 4°C, not 0°C."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\n11. Expansion Order — Gas > Liquid > Solid\n• Gases show greatest volume expansion: Gases > Liquids > Solids\n• Ideal gas volumetric expansion coefficient in source: γp = γv = 1/273.15 per °C\n• Idealized relation mein all ideal gases same coefficient show karte hain\nTRICK - “G-L-S = Greatest to Smallest Expansion”\nGas > Liquid > Solid.\n12. State Changes — Absorb vs Release\nProcess\nTransition\nHeat\nMelting\nSolid > Liquid\nAbsorbed\nFreezing\nLiquid > Solid\nReleased\nBoiling/Evaporation\nLiquid > Gas\nAbsorbed\nCondensation\nGas > Liquid\nReleased\nSublimation\nSolid > Gas\nAbsorbed\nDeposition\nGas > Solid\nReleased\nTRICK - “Up in State = Absorb; Down in State = Release”\nSolid\nLiquid\nGas direction absorbs; reverse releases.\n→\n→\nTRICK - “Sublime: Dry Ice-Camphor-Naphthalene-Iodine”\nD-C-N-I source examples.\n13. Pressure + Impurity Effects\nAction\nMelting Point\nBoiling Point\nIncrease pressure\nDecreases for ice\nIncreases\nDecrease pressure\nIncreases\nDecreases\nAdd impurity\nDecreases\nIncreases\nTRICK - “Pressure Cooker: P\n\n BP\n\n Faster Cooking”\n↑→\n↑→\nHigh altitude opposite: P\n\n BP\n\n slower cooking.\n↓→\n↓→\nEXAM TRAP - “Impurity: MP Down, BP Up”\nSalt lowers freezing/melting point in source notes.\nTRICK - “Triple Point = 273.16 K”\nSolid, liquid and vapour coexist in equilibrium.\n14. Heat Transfer — C-C-R\nMethod\nHow\nMedium / State\nExamples\nConduction\nDirect contact transfer\nMainly solids; also mercury\nHot pan handle, soldering iron\nConvection\nBulk particle motion\nLiquids + gases\nSea/land breeze, hot-water\ncirculation\nRadiation\nElectromagnetic waves\nNo medium; vacuum works\nSunlight, infrared heater\nTRICK - “Conduction Solid; Convection Fluids; Radiation Vacuum”\nC-C-R master rule.\nEXAM TRAP - “Sea/Land Breeze = Convection”\nRadiation nahi."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\nTRICK - “Thermos Cuts All 3”\nSilvered walls reduce radiation; vacuum reduces conduction + convection.\n15. Thermodynamics — PV = μRT\n• Thermodynamics = heat aur mechanical energy ka relation\n• System variables: pressure, volume, temperature\n• Ideal gas equation in source notes: PV = μRT\n• μ = number of moles, R = gas constant, T = absolute temperature\nTRICK - “P-V-T System; PV = μRT”\nSource notation μ for number of moles.\n16. Zeroth, First, Second — Z-F-S\nLaw\nCore Statement\nExam Key\nZeroth\nA and B each thermal equilibrium with C => A and\nB equilibrium\nThermometry basis; Fowler (1931)\nFirst\nHeat supplied = ΔU + work done\nΔQ = ΔU + ΔW; energy conservation\nSecond\n100% heat\nwork impossible; cold\nhot\n→\n→\nspontaneous flow impossible\nNo 100% efficient engine; refrigerator needs work\nTRICK - “Z = Zero Temp Difference; F = First Energy; S = Second Direction”\nZeroth = thermal equilibrium.\nFirst = conservation.\nSecond = direction/limits.\nTRICK - “Fowler 1931 = Zeroth”\nSource-specific scientist/year recall.\nEXAM TRAP - “Cold\n Hot Needs Work”\n→\nRefrigerator/AC external work consume karta hai.\n17. Formula + Number Flash\nItem\nRecall\nScale conversion\nC/100 = (F-32)/180 = (K-273)/100\nSpecific heat\nQ = msΔT\nLatent heat\nL = Q/m\nExpansion\nα:β:γ = 1:2:3\nFirst law\nΔQ = ΔU + ΔW\nIdeal gas\nPV = μRT\n1 calorie\n4.186 J\n1 BTU\n252 cal\nWater specific heat\n4186 J/kg°C\nFusion / Vaporisation\n80 / 539 cal/g"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Temperature, Heat & Thermodynamics\n18. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Phase change ke during temperature constant rehta hai\n• Radiation vacuum mein work karta hai; conduction/convection matter require karte hain\n• Sea breeze + land breeze = convection\n• Water maximum density at 4°C, not 0°C\n• Ice floats because its density liquid water se lower hai\n• Pressure cooker: pressure\n\n boiling point\n\n faster cooking\n↑→\n↑→\n• High altitude: pressure\n\n boiling point\n\n slower cooking\n↓→\n↓→\n• 1 BTU = 252 cal\n• Clinical thermometer = 35°C-42°C; Thermocouple = widest listed -200°C to 1600°C\n• Zeroth = Fowler/thermal equilibrium; First = conservation; Second = no 100% heat-to-work\nEXAM TRAP - “Phase-Radiation-Breeze-Water-Ice-Pressure-Altitude-BTU-Thermometer-Laws”\nChapter ke 10 major traps isi sequence mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Temperature measure vs Heat transfer hot\ncold\n scales C-F-R-K-Ra with divisions 100-180-80-100-180; -40 C=F; absolute0=0K;\n→\n→\ntriple273.16K; body37°C=98.4°F=310.5K\n Clinical35-42; Thermocouple -200 to1600 widest; Alcohol very low; total-radiation no\n→\ncontact\n Heat units J/cal/BTU: 1cal4.186J, 1BTU252cal\n Specific Q=msΔT, water4186; Latent L=Q/m, Fusion80 vs Vapor539; phase\n→\n→\nchange temp same; Calorimetry Hot Lost=Cold Gained\n Expansion α:β:γ=1:2:3; railway gaps; Water0\n4 contracts, 4°C density max,\n→\n→\nabove4 expands; expansion G>L>S\n State up absorbs, down releases; sublimation D-C-N-I; Pressure\n BP\n, altitude P\n BP\n,\n→\n↑\n↑\n↓\n↓\nimpurity MP\n BP\n; Triple273.16K\n Heat transfer C-C-R: conduction solids, convection fluids, radiation vacuum; sea/land breeze\n↓\n↑\n→\nconvection; thermos reduces all3\n Thermo PV=μRT; Zeroth equilibrium/Fowler1931; First ΔQ=ΔU+ΔW conservation; Second 100%\n→\nheat\nwork impossible and cold\nhot needs external work.”\n→\n→\nTOP 5: -40 C=F | Clinical 35-42 vs Thermocouple widest | Fusion80 vs Vapor539 | Water density max 4°C | C-C-R + Zeroth/First/Second law\nsplit."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\nPERIODIC & WAVE MOTION — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 8 · SHM + Pendulum + Waves + EM Spectrum + Sound + Ultrasonic + Echo + Mach\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke SHM/pendulum relations, wave types, EM-spectrum discoverers, sound characteristics,\nhearing ranges, speed-of-sound effects, echo/reverberation aur Mach-number traps ko fast exam-recall format mein compress kiya\ngaya hai.\n1. Periodic Motion vs SHM\nConcept\nCore Idea\nExamples\nPeriodic Motion\nRegular time interval ke baad repeat\nSwing, fan, musical vibrations, satellite motion\nSHM\nMean position ke about oscillation; acceleration\nmean ki taraf\nClock pendulum, spring-mass system\nTRICK - “Periodic = Repeat; SHM = Restore to Mean”\nSHM mein restoring acceleration hamesha mean position ki taraf hota hai.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSHM acceleration constant nahi hota; displacement ke saath vary karta hai.\n2. SHM Formula Pack — T-n-ω\nQuantity\nFormula / Meaning\nTime Period\nT = 2π/ω\nFrequency\nn = 1/T\nTime Period-Frequency\nT = 1/n\nAmplitude\nMaximum displacement from mean position\nPhase\nDirection/state of motion ko express karta hai\nTRICK - “T and n = Reciprocal Twins”\nn = 1/T. Higher frequency\n shorter time period.\n→\nTRICK - “Amplitude = Maximum Displacement”\nMean position se maximum displacement ko amplitude bolte hain.\n3. Simple Pendulum — T = 2π (l/g)\n√\n• Simple pendulum = heavy point mass (bob) + light inextensible string + fixed support\n• T = 2π (l/g)\n√\n• T depends on length l and gravitational acceleration g\n• T does NOT depend on bob mass\nTRICK - “Pendulum T = Length UP, g DOWN”\nl badhe\n T badhe.\n→\ng ghate\n T badhe.\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Mass Changes? T Says NO.”\nBob mass ka time period par no effect."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\n4. Pendulum Conditions — Up/Down/Satellite/Summer/Moon\nCondition\nEffect on T\nReason\nAltitude increases\nT increases\ng decreases\nDepth increases\nT increases\ng decreases\nSatellite\nT = ∞\nEffective g = 0 / weightlessness\nSummer\nT increases\nLength increases\nWinter\nT decreases\nLength decreases\nMoon\nT increases\ng_moon = g_earth/6\nBob mass changes\nNo change\nT independent of mass\nTRICK - “UP bhi T\n, DOWN bhi T\n”\n↑\n↑\nEarth surface se altitude aur depth dono directions mein g decreases, so T increases in source notes.\nTRICK - “Satellite = Infinity; Moon = Longer”\nSatellite mein pendulum oscillate nahi karta in source treatment.\nEXAM TRAP - “Max Pendulum T = 84.6 min”\nSource note: length equal to Earth radius ke liye maximum T = 84.6 minutes.\n5. Wave Motion — v = nλ\n• Wave = disturbance that transports energy from one place to another\n• v = λ/T = nλ\n• λ = v/n\n• Frequency source-set property hai; medium change par unchanged rehti hai\nTRICK - “Wave Triangle = v - n - λ”\nv = nλ; λ = v/n.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMedium change par speed aur wavelength change ho sakte hain, frequency nahi.\n6. Mechanical vs Electromagnetic Waves\nType\nParticle Motion / Medium\nExamples\nLongitudinal Mechanical\nAlong wave direction; medium required\nSound, seismic waves, tsunami, spring vibrations\nTransverse Mechanical\nPerpendicular; medium required\nTransverse spring motion\nElectromagnetic\nTransverse; no material medium required\nLight, radio, microwave, X-ray, gamma\nTRICK - “Sound = Longitudinal + Mechanical + Medium”\nVacuum mein sound travel nahi karta.\nTRICK - “EM = Transverse + Medium-Free”\nVacuum speed = 3 × 10^8 m/s.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMechanical waves need medium; EM waves do not."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\n7. EM Spectrum Order — R-M-I-V-U-X-G\nWave\nDiscoverer (Year)\nKey Use\nRadio\nMarconi (1895)\nRadio & TV communication\nMicrowave\nHeinrich Hertz (1888)\nSatellites, wireless communication\nInfrared\nHerschel (1800)\nRemote control, fog photography\nVisible\nNewton (1666)\nHuman vision, bulb\nUltraviolet\nRitter (1801)\nForged-document detection, food preservation\nX-Ray\nRoentgen (1895)\nBone fractures, lung diseases\nGamma\nPaul Villard (1900)\nCancer treatment, nuclear structure\nTRICK - “R-M-I-V-U-X-G”\nRadio\n Microwave\n Infrared\n Visible\n UV\n X-ray\n Gamma.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nIs order mein wavelength decreases, frequency increases.\nTRICK - “Discoverers = M-H-H-N-R-R-V”\nMarconi-Hertz-Herschel-Newton-Ritter-Roentgen-Villard.\nEXAM TRAP - “Gamma Villard; Named Rutherford”\nMicrowaves generated by magnetron; visible\n 400 nm violet to 700 nm red.\n≈\n8. Sound Characteristics — L-P-Q-I\nCharacteristic\nMeaning / Relation\nExam Hook\nLoudness\nIntensity-linked; Loudness Amplitude²\n∝\nAlso falls approx 1/distance²\nPitch\nShrillness; Frequency\n∝\nHigher f = higher pitch\nQuality / Timbre\nDistinguishes same pitch & loudness\nTone one frequency; Note many\nIntensity\nSound energy per area per second\nUnit W/m²\nTRICK - “Loudness = Amplitude²; Pitch = Frequency”\nL-A² / P-f.\nEXAM TRAP - “Tone One; Note Many”\nSingle frequency vs multiple frequencies.\n9. Sound Levels — Quiet to Jet\nSource\nLoudness\nNormal breathing\n10 dB\nWhisper\n15-30 dB\nGeneral conversation\n30-60 dB\nBusy traffic\n70 dB\nJet plane\n140-150 dB\nTRICK - “10\n 30\n 60\n 70\n 150”\n→\n→\n→\n→\nBreathing\n whisper/conversation\n traffic\n jet.\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “85 dB+ Harmful”\nSource flags noise above 85 dB as harmful to human ears."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\n10. Hearing Range — I-A-U\nRange\nCategory\nExamples / Use\n< 20 Hz\nInfrasonic\nSeismic waves, heartbeat\n20-20,000 Hz\nAudible\nAdult human hearing\n> 20,000 Hz\nUltrasonic\nBat, dog, dolphin, cat; SONAR; medical imaging\nTRICK - “I-A-U = Below20 / 20-20k / Above20k”\nInfrasonic-Audible-Ultrasonic.\nTRICK - “SONAR = Sound Navigation And Ranging”\nUses ultrasonic waves.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAdult hearing range = 20 Hz to 20 kHz.\n11. Animal Hearing — D-B-D-C-H\nAnimal / Entity\nSource Range\nDolphin\n150-1,50,000 Hz\nBat\n1,000-1,20,000 Hz\nDog\n15-45,000 Hz\nCat\n60-65,000 Hz\nChildren\nUp to 25,000 Hz\nHuman Adult\n20-20,000 Hz\nTRICK - “Dolphin Highest Listed 150k; Bat 120k”\nSource animal-range table ka fast recall.\n12. Ultrasonic Applications — M-S-D-I\n• Medical imaging: ultrasonography + echocardiography\n• SONAR: sea depth measurement\n• Detecting submarines and icebergs\n• Industrial cleaning and welding\nTRICK - “M-S-D-I = Medical - SONAR - Detection - Industrial”\nUltrasonic uses ka four-part chain.\n13. Speed of Sound — Solid > Liquid > Gas\nTRICK - “S-L-G = Fast to Slow”\nSpeed of sound: Solid > Liquid > Gas.\nMedium\nSpeed at 25°C\nAluminium\n6420 m/s\nSteel\n5960 m/s\nSea Water\n1531 m/s\nDistilled Water\n1498 m/s\nHydrogen\n1284 m/s\nAir\n340 m/s\nTRICK - “Aluminium Fastest Listed; Air\n 340”\n≈\nSource quick-number pair."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\n14. Temperature, Pressure, Humidity Effects\nCondition\nEffect on Sound Speed\nTemperature increases\nSpeed increases; v T\n∝√\nPressure changes at constant T\nNo effect\nHumidity increases\nSpeed increases; moist air lighter\nTRICK - “T\n = v\n; Pressure@sameT = NO effect; Humidity\n = v\n”\n↑\n↑\n↑\n↑\nT-P-H trend.\nTemperature\nSpeed in Air\n0°C\n332 m/s\n22°C\n344 m/s\n25°C\n346 m/s\nEXAM TRAP -\nAt constant temperature, pressure has NO effect on sound speed.\n15. Echo vs Reverberation\nTerm\nMeaning\nSource Key\nEcho\nDistinct re-hearing of reflected sound\nPersistence 0.1 s; min distance 17.2 m\nReverberation\nProlonged persistence by multiple reflections\nHalls; megaphones/loudspeakers/stethoscope\ncontext\nTRICK - “Echo = Repeat; Reverb = Remains”\nEcho distinct repetition; reverberation prolonged persistence.\nEXAM TRAP - “0.1 s\n 17.2 m”\n→\nPersistence of hearing and source minimum echo distance.\n16. Mach Number — Sub / Super / Hyper\n• Mach Number = speed of body / speed of sound in same medium\n• Named after Ernst Mach\n• Sonic boom occurs when aircraft crosses sound barrier near Mach 1\nMach Range\nClass\nExample\nMach < 1\nSubsonic\nCommercial aircraft\n 0.8\n≈\n1 < Mach\n 5\n≤\nSupersonic\nFighter jets\nMach > 5\nHypersonic\nSpace shuttle during re-entry\nTRICK - “Sub <1; Super 1-5; Hyper >5”\nSource classification.\nEXAM TRAP -\nHypersonic = Mach > 5 in source notes."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Periodic & Wave Motion\n17. Formula + Number Flash\nItem\nRecall\nSHM time period\nT = 2π/ω\nPendulum\nT = 2π (l/g)\n√\nFrequency\nn = 1/T\nWave speed\nv = nλ\nWavelength\nλ = v/n\nSound vs temperature\nv T\n∝√\nEM speed vacuum\n3 × 10^8 m/s\nAdult hearing\n20-20,000 Hz\nPersistence of hearing\n0.1 s\nMinimum echo distance\n17.2 m\nMach number\nv_body / v_sound\n18. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• SHM acceleration always mean position ki taraf; constant nahi\n• Pendulum T bob mass par depend nahi karta\n• Altitude aur depth dono increase karne par T increases in source treatment\n• Satellite pendulum T =\n in source notes\n∞\n• Sound longitudinal mechanical; EM/light transverse\n• Medium change par frequency unchanged\n• Pressure at constant temperature has no effect on sound speed\n• Gamma discovered by Villard but named by Rutherford\n• SONAR uses ultrasonic waves\n• Echo min distance = 17.2 m; Hypersonic = Mach > 5\nEXAM TRAP - “SHM-Mass-UpDown-Satellite-Sound/EM-Frequency-Pressure-Gamma-SONAR-Echo/Mach”\nChapter ke highest-yield traps isi sequence mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Periodic repeats; SHM restores to mean, acceleration toward mean not constant\n T=2π/ω, n=1/T; pendulum T=2π (l/g), mass no\n→\n√\neffect; altitude\n/depth\n/summer/moon all T\n, winter T\n, satellite T=\n, source max84.6min\n Wave v=nλ, medium change\n↑\n↑\n↑\n↓\n∞\n→\nfrequency same\n Sound longitudinal mechanical medium-needed vs EM transverse medium-free speed3×10^8\n EM order R-M-I-\n→\n→\nV-U-X-G, wavelength\n frequency\n; discoverers Marconi-Hertz-Herschel-Newton-Ritter-Roentgen-Villard; gamma named Rutherford\n↓\n↑\n\n Sound L-P-Q-I: Loudness A², Pitch f, Tone one/Note many; >85dB harmful\n hearing I-A-U: <20 infra, 20-20k audible, >20k\n→\n∝\n∝\n→\nultrasonic; SONAR full form + ultrasound\n Sound speed S>L>G; Al6420, air\n340; T\nv\n, pressure@sameT no effect, humidity\nv\n\n→\n≈\n↑↑\n↑↑\n Echo distinct 0.1s / 17.2m vs Reverb prolonged\n Mach = body/sound; Sub<1, Super1-5, Hyper>5; sonic boom near Mach1.”\n→\n→\nTOP 5: Pendulum mass no effect | Sound longitudinal vs EM transverse | R-M-I-V-U-X-G + discoverers | Frequency unchanged across\nmedium | Echo 17.2 m + Hypersonic > Mach 5."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\nELECTROSTATICS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 9 · Charge + Coulomb + Field + Potential + Current + Resistance + Cells + Instruments\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke charge laws, electric field/potential, capacitance, current, Ohm law, resistance\ncombinations, heating effect, cells aur measuring instruments ke high-confusion facts ko fast exam-recall format mein compress\nkiya gaya hai.\n1. Charge — A-Q-C-R\nProperty\nRule\nAdditive\nQ = q1 + q2 + q3\nQuantisation\nQ = ne; e = ±1.6 × 10^-19 C\nConservation\nIsolated system ka total charge constant\nRepel / Attract\nLike repel; unlike attract\nTRICK - “A-Q-C-R = Add - Quantise - Conserve - Repel/Attract”\nCharge properties ka four-part code.\nEXAM TRAP - “Same Repels; Opposite Attracts”\nElectric force gravity ki tarah sirf attractive nahi — source notes attraction + repulsion dono batate hain.\n2. Coulomb’s Law — K q1q2 / r²\n• F = K(q1q2)/r²\n• K = 9 × 10^9 N·m²/C²\n• K = 1/(4πε0)\n• ε0 = 8.85 × 10^-12 C²/(N·m²)\n• Inverse-square law; source treats point charges\nTRICK - “Charge Product UP; Distance-Square DOWN”\nq1q2 numerator; r² denominator.\nEXAM TRAP - “K = 9×10^9; e = 1.6×10^-19”\nChapter ke two core constants.\n3. Conductor - Insulator - Semiconductor\nClass\nSource Behaviour\nExamples\nConductor\nFree electrons; charge flows easily\nSilver, Gold, Copper, Graphite, Sea water\nInsulator\nCharge does not flow easily\nRubber, Oil, Polythene, Pure water, Lead - as listed\nin source\nSemiconductor\nBetween conductor and insulator\nSilicon, Germanium\nTRICK - “Silver Best; Pure Water Insulator; Sea Water Conductor”\nSea water dissolved salts/ions ki wajah se conduct karta hai.\nEXAM TRAP -\nBest conductor in source = Silver, not Copper."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\n4. Electric Field — P\nN, Never Cross\n→\nItem\nRecall\nElectric field intensity\nE = F/q0; vector; N/C\nField-line direction\nPositive\n Negative\n→\nIntersection\nNever intersect\nClosed loops\nDo not form closed loops\nStrength\nCloser lines = stronger field\nConductor surface\nLines perpendicular to surface\nTRICK - “P-to-N; Never Cross; Perpendicular at Conductor”\nField-lines ka 3-rule pack.\nEXAM TRAP -\nField lines intersect karein to ek point par do directions ho jaayengi — source explanation.\n5. Potential + Capacitance — W/q and Q/V\nQuantity\nFormula\nNature / Unit\nElectric Potential\nV = W/q0\nScalar; Volt = J/C\nPotential Difference\nVa - Vb = W/q0\nVolt\nCapacitance\nC = Q/V\nFarad = C/V\nTRICK - “Potential = Work/Charge; Capacitance = Charge/Volt”\nV = W/q; C = Q/V.\nEXAM TRAP - “Farad, Not Volt/Ohm”\nPractical units: μF and pF.\n• Source solved potential example: W=2.25 J, q=12×10^-4 C\n V=1875 V\n→\n• Source solved capacitor example: C=1.0 μF, V=6.0 kV\n Q=6×10^-3 C\n→\n6. Electric Current — i = q/t\n• Current i = q/t\n• SI unit Ampere = C/s\n• 1 A\n 6.25 × 10^18 electrons per second\n≈\n• Conventional current: high potential\n low potential\n→\n• Electron flow direction conventional current ke opposite\n• Solids: free electrons; liquids: ions + electrons; semiconductors: holes + electrons\nTRICK - “Current Goes High\nLow; Electrons Go Opposite”\n→\nConventional current vs electron-flow direction.\nEXAM TRAP -\nCurrent direction aur electron direction same nahi.\n7. AC vs DC\nType\nDirection\nTypical Use\nAC\nPeriodically alternates\nHousehold supply, generators, transformers\nDC\nRemains constant\nBatteries, electronic circuits, charging\nTRICK - “AC Alternates; DC Direct”\nNaam hi direction rule yaad kara deta hai."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\n8. Ohm’s Law — V = IR\n• Proposed by George Simon Ohm in 1827\n• V I when temperature and other physical conditions remain constant\n∝\n• V = IR\nResistance Type\nSource Recall\nOhmic\nObeys V=IR; V-I graph straight; source example manganese wire\nNon-ohmic\nDoes not obey; V-I graph non-linear; diode, bulb\nTRICK - “Ohm 1827 + Constant Conditions”\nTemperature/physical conditions unchanged hona mandatory.\nEXAM TRAP -\nOhm law har condition mein valid nahi — source specifically constant physical conditions kehta hai.\n9. Resistance — Long More, Area More Less\n• R = ρl/A\n• R l\n∝\n• R 1/A\n∝\n• Resistivity ρ material property; unit Ω·m\nTRICK - “Length\n\n R\n; Area\n\n R\n”\n↑→\n↑\n↑→\n↓\nR = ρl/A.\n10. Series vs Parallel — Same I vs Same V\nFeature\nSeries\nParallel\nEquivalent R\nR1+R2+R3\n1/Req = 1/R1+1/R2+1/R3\nCurrent\nSame\nDifferent branches\nVoltage\nDifferent\nSame\nEquivalent R\nGreater than any individual\nLess than smallest individual\nSource Use\nFuse, Ammeter\nDomestic wiring, Voltmeter\nTRICK - “Series = Same I; Parallel = Same V”\nDomestic wiring = parallel.\nTRICK - “Series R Grows; Parallel R Shrinks”\nSeries equivalent > individual; parallel equivalent < smallest.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDomestic wiring series nahi, parallel.\n11. ρ - G - σ\nQuantity\nFormula\nUnit\nResistivity ρ\nρ = RA/l\nΩ·m\nConductance G\nG = 1/R\nSiemens S or Ω^-1\nSpecific Conductivity σ\nσ = 1/ρ\nΩ^-1 m^-1\nTRICK - “Resistance ka Reciprocal = Conductance; Resistivity ka Reciprocal = Conductivity”\nG=1/R; σ=1/ρ.\nTRICK - “Silver 1.60e-8; Copper 1.62e-8”\nSource resistivity table mein Silver slightly lower\n best conductor.\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\n12. Joule Heating + Power — H-W-P\nQuantity\nFormula\nHeating\nH = I²Rt joules = I²Rt/4.2 calories\nElectrical Work / Energy\nW = VIt = I²Rt = V²t/R\nPower\nP = VI = V²/R = I²R\nTRICK - “Heat I²Rt; Work adds t; Power removes t”\nH/W/P formulas ko family ki tarah yaad karo.\nEXAM TRAP - “1 kWh = 1 unit electricity”\nSource high-frequency recall.\n13. Bulb - Heater - Fuse - MCB\nDevice\nMaterial / Principle\nKey Detail\nBulb\nTungsten filament\nHigh resistivity; melting point 3422°C; N2 + Argon\nElectric Iron\nNichrome\nSource: 80% Nickel + 20% Chromium\nHeater\nCeramic plate + Nichrome\nResistance heating\nFuse\nLow-melting alloy\nSource: Cu + Sn + Pb; melts to break circuit\nMCB\nAutomatic protective device\nTrips and resettable\nTRICK - “Bulb = Tungsten; Heater/Iron = Nichrome”\nDo not swap.\nEXAM TRAP - “Fuse Melts; MCB Trips + Resets”\nProtection-device distinction.\n14. Electrolysis — Faraday\n• Current through acidic conducting solution causes ionic decomposition\n• Source associates law of electrolysis with Faraday\n• Applications: electric cell and electroplating\nTRICK - “Faraday = Electrolysis; Cell + Plating”\nChemical effect of electric current.\n15. Cell Basics — Primary vs Secondary\nType\nSource Energy / Rechargeability\nPrimary\nChemical\n Electrical; cannot be recharged\n→\nSecondary\nCharging: Electrical\n Chemical; Discharge: Chemical\n Electrical;\n→\n→\nrechargeable\nTRICK - “Primary = One-Time; Secondary = Recharge”\nRechargeability split.\n• EMF E = W/q; unit Volt\n• Terminal potential V = E - ir\n• Cell current I = E/(R+r)\n• Internal resistance source relation: r = (E/V - 1)R"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\n16. Cell Voltage Memory\nCell\nEMF\nVoltaic\n1.08 V\nLeclanche\n1.46 V\nDry Cell\n1.46 V\nDaniell\n1.1 V\nBichromate\n2.0 V\nWeston Cadmium\n1.018 V\nLead Accumulator\n2.2 V\nAlkaline Accumulator\n1.35 V\nTRICK - “Dry/Leclanche = 1.46; Lead = 2.2”\nSource ke most important cell values.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLead accumulator 2.2 V; dry cell 1.46 V.\n17. Ammeter vs Voltmeter vs Galvanometer\nInstrument\nMeasures\nConnection\nIdeal R\nAmmeter\nCurrent\nSeries\n0\nVoltmeter\nPotential difference\nParallel\n∞\nGalvanometer\nCurrent detect + direction +\nmagnitude\n—\nMedium\nTRICK - “A = Series + Zero R; V = Parallel + Infinite R”\nAmmeter aur voltmeter ka complete exam pair.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAmmeter parallel nahi; voltmeter series nahi.\n18. Galvanometer Conversion — Opposite Additions\nConversion\nAdd\nGalvanometer\n Ammeter\n→\nLow resistance shunt in parallel\nGalvanometer\n Voltmeter\n→\nHigh resistance in series\nTRICK - “To A: Low Parallel; To V: High Series”\nLow-P / High-S.\nEXAM TRAP -\nGalvanometer\nAmmeter: low R parallel;\nVoltmeter: high R series.\n→\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Electrostatics\n19. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Best conductor in source = Silver, not copper\n• Pure water = insulator; sea water = conductor\n• Field lines Positive\nNegative and never intersect\n→\n• Potential scalar; capacitance unit Farad\n• Conventional current opposite electron motion\n• Ohm law only at constant temperature/physical conditions\n• Series = same current; Parallel = same voltage; domestic wiring parallel\n• Bulb = Tungsten; heater/iron = Nichrome\n• Faraday = electrolysis in source\n• Dry/Leclanche = 1.46 V; Lead accumulator = 2.2 V\n• Ammeter series R=0; Voltmeter parallel R=∞\n• Galvanometer\nA: low-R parallel;\nV: high-R series\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP - “Silver-Water-Field-Farad-Current-Ohm-Series-Bulb-Faraday-Cells-A/V-Galvano”\n12 exam traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Charge A-Q-C-R; e=1.6×10^-19C; Coulomb F=Kq1q2/r², K=9×10^9, ε0=8.85×10^-12\n Silver best conductor; pure water insulator, sea\n→\nwater conductor; semiconductor Si-Ge\n Field E=F/q vector N/C, lines P\nN, never cross/loop, conductor surface perpendicular\n\n→\n→\n→\nPotential V=W/q scalar Volt=J/C; Capacitance C=Q/V Farad\n Current i=q/t, 1A\n6.25×10^18 e/s, conventional High\nLow and\n→\n≈\n→\nelectrons opposite; AC alternates, DC constant\n Ohm1827 V=IR only constant conditions; R=ρl/A: length\nR\n, area\nR\n\n Series\n→\n↑↑\n↑↓→\nsame I and R grows; Parallel same V and R shrinks; domestic parallel\n ρ=RA/l, G=1/R, σ=1/ρ; Joule H=I²Rt, W=VIt=I²Rt=V²t/R,\n→\nP=VI=I²R=V²/R; 1kWh=1 unit\n Bulb tungsten; iron/heater nichrome; fuse melts, MCB trips/reset; Faraday electrolysis\n Primary\n→\n→\none-use vs Secondary rechargeable; E=W/q, V=E-ir, I=E/(R+r); Dry/Leclanche1.46V, Lead2.2V\n Ammeter series R0; Voltmeter\n→\nparallel R\n; Galvanometer to A low-R parallel, to V high-R series.”\n∞\nTOP 5: Silver best + pure/sea water split | Field P\nN never crosses | Series same I / Parallel same V | Tungsten vs Nichrome | Ammeter\n→\nseries R0 vs Voltmeter parallel R\n.\n∞"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Magnetism\nMAGNETISM — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 10 · Magnets + Materials + Magnetic Field + Lorentz Force + Fleming Rules + Flux + EMI\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke magnet types, magnetic-material classes, Oersted/Faraday timeline, field rules, Lorentz\nforce, Fleming rules, magnetic flux aur electromagnetic induction ke high-memory facts ko fast exam recall format mein compress\nkiya gaya hai.\n1. Magnet Basics — Dipole Always\n• Magnet iron aur uske ores ko attract karta hai\n• Every magnet has North + South pole; isolated magnetic monopole does not exist\n• Like poles repel; unlike poles attract\n• Freely suspended bar magnet ka North pole geographic North ki taraf point karta hai\n• Magnet ko cut karne par har piece phir N-S dipole ban jaata hai\nTRICK - “Magnet = N + S Forever”\nCut karo, phir bhi monopole nahi milta; smaller dipoles milte hain.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMagnetic monopole does NOT exist in source notes.\n2. Natural vs Artificial Magnet\nType\nSource Detail\nExamples\nNatural\nNature mein found; irregular; weaker\nLodestone / Magnetite = Fe3O4\nArtificial\nMan-made magnetic materials\nBar magnet, electromagnet, horse-shoe,\ncompass\nTRICK - “Lodestone = Magnetite = Fe3O4”\nNatural magnet ka direct equation.\nEXAM TRAP -\nFe3O4 yaad karo; FeO/Fe2O3 nahi.\n3. Magnetic Materials — Dia / Para / Ferro\nClass\nBehaviour\nExamples from Source\nDiamagnetic\nOpposite magnetisation; weakly repelled\nBismuth, Zinc, Gold, Copper, Silver, Diamond, Salt\nParamagnetic\nField direction; weakly attracted\nChromium, Sodium, Aluminium, Oxygen\nFerromagnetic\nDomain formation; strongly attracted\nIron, Nickel, Cobalt, Steel\nTRICK - “Dia = Door; Para = Passes Near; Ferro = Full Attraction”\nDia repels weakly; Para attracts weakly; Ferro attracts strongly.\nTRICK - “Ferro = I-N-C-S”\nIron - Nickel - Cobalt - Steel.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSilver/Copper = Diamagnetic; Aluminium = Paramagnetic.\n4. Oersted vs Faraday — 1820 vs 1831\nScientist\nYear\nDiscovery\nOersted\n1820\nCurrent-carrying conductor produces magnetic\nfield"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Magnetism\nFaraday\n1831\nChanging magnetic flux produces induced\nEMF/current\nTRICK - “Oersted: Current\n Field; Faraday: Changing Flux\n Current”\n→\n→\n1820\n 1831 timeline.\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nOersted aur Faraday ki discoveries interchange mat karna.\n5. Biot-Savart Law — I·l·sinθ / r²\n• B = (μ0/4π) · (IΔl sinθ / r²)\n• B I\n∝\n• B Δl\n∝\n• B sinθ\n∝\n• B 1/r²\n∝\n• μ0/4π = 10^-7 N/A²\n• Source unit of B = N/(A·m)\nTRICK - “Biot = I-L-sin / r²”\nCurrent, length aur sinθ numerator; distance-square denominator.\nTRICK - “μ0/4π = 10^-7”\nDirect numerical recall.\n6. Ampere’s Law\n•\n B·dl = μ0 I\n∮\n• Closed loop ke around magnetic-field line integral = μ0 × enclosed current\n• Source use: symmetric current configurations such as solenoid and toroid\nTRICK - “Ampere = Closed Loop + Enclosed Current”\nSymmetry problems ka source hook.\n7. Direction Rules — Right Hand + Cork Screw\nRule\nThumb / Motion\nFingers / Result\nRight Hand Palm\nThumb\n current I\n→\nFingers\n magnetic field B\n→\nMaxwell Right Hand\nThumb\n current\n→\nCurled fingers\n magnetic field\n→\nCork Screw\nCurrent upward\nField anti-clockwise\nCork Screw\nCurrent downward\nField clockwise\nTRICK - “Current UP = Anti-clockwise; DOWN = Clockwise”\nSource cork-screw rule.\nEXAM TRAP -\nUp/anti-clockwise and down/clockwise ko ulta mat karna.\n8. Lorentz Force — Moving Charge Only\n• Moving charge in magnetic field: F = qvB sinθ = q(v × B)\n• F q, v, B\n∝\n• θ = 0° or 180°\n F = 0\n→\n• θ = 90°\n F maximum\n→\n• Stationary charge v=0\n magnetic force zero\n→"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Magnetism\nTRICK - “Lorentz = q-v-B-sinθ”\nCharge, speed, field aur angle.\nTRICK - “Parallel ZERO; Perpendicular MAX”\n0°/180°\n 0 force; 90°\n max.\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nStationary charge in magnetic field experiences NO magnetic force.\n9. Force on Current-Carrying Conductor\n• F = BIl sinθ\n• Force current aur magnetic field dono ke perpendicular act karta hai\n• θ = 90°\n force maximum\n→\n• Current parallel to B (θ=0°)\n force zero\n→\nTRICK - “Conductor Force = B-I-l-sinθ”\nLorentz qvB aur conductor BIl ko separate yaad karo.\n10. Fleming Rules — Left Motor, Right Generator\nRule\nUsed For\nThumb\nForefinger\nMiddle Finger\nLEFT\nMotor / force\nForce / motion\nMagnetic field B\nCurrent I\nRIGHT\nGenerator / induced current\nMotion of conductor\nMagnetic field B\nInduced current\nTRICK - “LEFT = MOTOR; RIGHT = GENERATOR”\nBoth rules mein Forefinger = Field, Middle finger = Current.\nTRICK - “F-B-I = Thumb-Fore-Middle on Left”\nLeft hand: Force - B - I.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMotor = Left; Generator/Dynamo = Right.\n11. Magnetic Field Lines\nProperty\nSource Recall\nOutside magnet\nNorth\n South\n→\nShape\nClosed continuous loops\nIntersection\nNever intersect\nUniform field\nParallel + equally spaced\nNeutral point\nMagnetic field = 0\nStrength\nCloser lines = stronger field\nTRICK - “N\nS Outside + Closed + Never Cross”\n→\nMagnetic-field lines ka 3-rule pack.\n12. Magnetic vs Electric Field Lines\nFeature\nElectric\nMagnetic\nDirection\n+\n -\n→\nN\n S outside magnet\n→\nClosed loops?\nNo\nYes\nIntersect?\nNo\nNo\nStart/end\nOn charges\nNo start/end; continuous"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Magnetism\nTRICK - “Electric Open; Magnetic Closed”\nDono non-intersecting.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMagnetic field lines closed loops form karte hain; electric field lines nahi.\n13. Electromagnet — Soft Iron + Current\n• Wire coil around iron core + current\n electromagnet\n→\n• Core material = soft iron; easily magnetised and demagnetised\n• More turns + more current + better core material\n greater strength\n→\n• Magnetism only while current flows\n• Applications: electric bells, scrap-iron cranes, MRI machines, electric motors\nTRICK - “Soft Iron + Turns + Current = Strong Electromagnet”\nCurrent off\n magnetism off.\n→\n14. Magnetic Flux — Φ = BA cosθ\nItem\nRecall\nFormula\nΦ = B·A cosθ\nAngle θ\nBetween B and surface normal\nSI unit\nWeber Wb\nOther SI expression\nN·m/A\nCGS unit\nMaxwell\nConversion\n1 Wb = 10^8 Maxwell\nTRICK - “Flux = BA cos NORMAL-angle”\nθ surface ke saath nahi, surface NORMAL ke saath measured hai.\nEXAM TRAP - “Perpendicular to Surface = Flux MAX; Parallel to Surface = ZERO”\nBecause B aligns with normal at max flux.\nTRICK - “1 Weber = 10^8 Maxwell”\n10^8 direct conversion.\n15. Electromagnetic Induction — Changing Flux Needed\n• EMI = changing magnetic flux se conductor mein EMF + induced current generate hona\n• Faraday discovered EMI in 1831\n• Static magnet motionless near coil\n no induced EMF\n→\n• Condition = magnetic flux must change\nTRICK - “EMI = Change Flux, Not Just Field”\nStatic flux\n no induction.\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nPresence of magnetic field alone is insufficient; flux must CHANGE.\n16. EMI Applications\nApplication\nRole\nDynamo / Generator\nMechanical\n Electrical\n→\nTransformer\nChanges AC voltage levels\nArtificial Pacemaker\nRegulates heartbeat\nOther source examples\nInduction cooktop; wireless charging"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Magnetism\nTRICK - “G-T-P-IW = Generator-Transformer-Pacemaker-Induction/Wireless”\nEMI application chain.\nEXAM TRAP - “Generator = EMI; Motor = Magnetic Force”\nGenerator/right hand vs Motor/left hand.\n17. Formula + Number Flash\nItem\nRecall\nBiot-Savart\nB = (μ0/4π) IΔl sinθ / r²\nAmpere\nB·dl = μ0I\n∮\nLorentz Force\nF = qvB sinθ\nConductor Force\nF = BIl sinθ\nFlux\nΦ = BA cosθ\nμ0/4π\n10^-7 N/A²\nOersted\n1820\nFaraday\n1831\nFlux Conversion\n1 Wb = 10^8 Maxwell\nNatural Magnet\nLodestone = Magnetite = Fe3O4\n18. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Lodestone = Magnetite = Fe3O4\n• Magnetic monopoles do not exist\n• Silver/Copper diamagnetic; Aluminium paramagnetic\n• Oersted 1820 = current\nfield; Faraday 1831 = changing flux\nEMI\n→\n→\n• Stationary charge has zero Lorentz magnetic force\n• Left hand = motor; Right hand = generator\n• Magnetic field lines closed; electric field lines not closed\n• 1 Weber = 10^8 Maxwell\n• Flux angle is measured with surface normal\n• EMI requires changing magnetic flux\nEXAM TRAP - “Fe3O4-Monopole-Materials-O/F-Stationary-L/R-Lines-Wb-Normal-Change”\nChapter ke 10 exam traps isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Magnet always N-S dipole; like repel/unlike attract; cut\nsmaller dipoles; Lodestone=Magnetite=Fe3O4\n Materials: Dia weak repel\n→\n→\n(Bi,Zn,Au,Cu,Ag,Diamond,Salt), Para weak attract (Cr,Na,Al,O2), Ferro strong/domain (Fe,Ni,Co,Steel)\n Oersted1820\n→\ncurrent\nmagnetic field; Faraday1831 changing flux\nEMI\n Biot B=(μ0/4π)IΔl sinθ/r² with μ0/4π=10^-7; Ampere\nBdl=μ0I\n\n→\n→\n→\n→\n∮\nDirection: right-hand thumb current/fingers field; current UP anti-clockwise, DOWN clockwise\n Lorentz F=qvBsinθ: stationary0,\n→\nparallel0, perpendicularmax; conductor F=BIl sinθ\n Fleming LEFT motor F-B-I, RIGHT generator motion-B-current\n Magnetic lines\n→\n→\n\nN\nS outside, closed, never intersect; electric open, magnetic closed\n Electromagnet soft iron + turns/current strength; current off\n→\n→\nmagnetism off\n Flux Φ=BAcosθ, θ with normal, Wb; 1Wb=10^8Maxwell; perpendicular-surface max, parallel-surface zero\n EMI\n→\n→\nrequires changing flux; generator, transformer, pacemaker, induction cooktop, wireless charging; generator=EMI, motor=magnetic-\nforce.”\nTOP 5: Fe3O4 Lodestone | Dia/Para/Ferro examples | Oersted1820 vs Faraday1831 | Left Motor vs Right Generator | Flux angle with\nNORMAL + 1 Wb=10^8 Maxwell."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\nLIGHT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 11 · Reflection + Refraction + TIR + Mirrors + Lenses + Dispersion + Eye + Wave Optics +\nPhotoelectric Effect\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke mirror/lens sign traps, TIR conditions, VIBGYOR, human-eye defects, optical\ninstruments, wave-optics scientists aur photon/photoelectric-effect facts ko fast exam-recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Light Basics — EM + Dual Nature\n• Light = energy form; normally straight line mein travel karta hai\n• Material medium required nahi hota\n• Transverse electromagnetic wave\n• Dual nature: wave + particle behaviour\n• Vacuum speed = 3 × 10^8 m/s\n• Visible wavelength = 3900-7800 Å\nTRICK - “Light = No Medium + Transverse EM + Dual”\nVacuum speed 3×10^8 m/s; visible 3900-7800 Å.\nTheory\nScientist / Year\nSource Hook\nParticle\nDescartes 1637; Newton 1700\nReflection/refraction + particle behaviour\nWave\nHuygens 1678\nInterference, diffraction, polarisation\nTRICK - “D-N Particle; H Wave”\nDescartes/Newton = particle side; Huygens = wave side.\n2. Reflection — i = r + Coplanarity\n• Reflection = light ka original medium mein return after striking surface\n• Law 1: angle of incidence = angle of reflection\n• Law 2: incident ray, reflected ray and normal same plane mein\nTRICK - “Reflection = i = r + Same Plane”\nAngles normal se measured hote hain.\n3. Plane Mirror — V-E-S-L\nProperty\nRecall\nNature\nVirtual\nOrientation\nErect\nSize\nEqual to object\nSpecial\nLaterally inverted\nDistance\nImage behind = object distance in front\nTRICK - “Plane Mirror = V-E-S-L”\nVirtual - Erect - Same size - Lateral inversion.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPlane-mirror image real nahi hota.\n4. Spherical Mirrors — Concave vs Convex\nMirror\nNature\nMajor Uses\nConcave\nConverging\nShaving, dentist, torch/headlight, solar cooker\nConvex\nDiverging\nRear-view mirror, eyeglass, street lights"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\nTRICK - “Rear-view = Convex; Shaving/Dentist = Concave”\nConvex wide field + diminished virtual image.\nConcave close object F-P ke beech enlarged virtual image.\nEXAM TRAP - “Convex Always V-E-D”\nVirtual - Erect - Diminished.\n5. Concave Mirror Image Chain\nObject Position\nImage Position\nNature\nInfinity\nF\nReal, inverted, highly diminished\nBeyond C\nBetween C & F\nReal, inverted, diminished\nAt C\nAt C\nReal, inverted, same size\nBetween C & F\nBeyond C\nReal, inverted, enlarged\nAt F\nInfinity\nReal, inverted, highly enlarged\nBetween F & P\nBehind mirror\nVirtual, erect, enlarged\nEXAM TRAP - “Concave Virtual ONLY F-P”\nObject between F and P\n behind mirror, virtual erect enlarged.\n→\n6. Mirror Formula — PLUS\nFormula / Sign\nRecall\nMirror formula\n1/v + 1/u = 1/f\nFocal-radius\nf = R/2\nMagnification\nm = -v/u\nConvex f\nPositive\nConcave f\nNegative\nObject distance u\nNegative in source sign convention\nTRICK - “MIRROR = PLUS”\n1/v + 1/u = 1/f.\nTRICK - “f = R/2”\nSource example: f=10 m\n R=20 m.\n→\n7. Refraction — Snell + Frequency Same\n• Refraction = transparent medium change par light deviation\n• Denser medium mein speed decreases and ray normal ki taraf bends\n• Frequency remains unchanged\n• Snell: sin i / sin r = constant = μ\n• μ = c/v\nTRICK - “Denser = Slower + Toward Normal; Frequency SAME”\nHigher refractive index = optically denser = lower light speed.\nEXAM TRAP -\nMedium change par frequency unchanged.\n8. Total Internal Reflection — D-R + i>c\n• Condition 1: light denser\n rarer medium\n→\n• Condition 2: incidence angle > critical angle\n• sin c = 1/μ\n• Applications: optical fibre, medical endoscope, diamond brilliance, mirage, shining air bubble/crack"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\nTRICK - “TIR = Denser\nRarer + i > Critical”\n→\nD-R + i>c.\nTRICK - “Diamond = Small Critical Angle\n 24°”\n≈\nHigh refractive index\n TIR easily.\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nTIR rarer\ndenser travel mein nahi hota.\n→\n9. Lenses — Convex vs Concave\nLens\nShape/Behaviour\nSign / Uses\nConvex\nThicker centre; converging\nPositive f; farsightedness, magnifying glass,\ncamera\nConcave\nThinner centre; diverging\nNegative f; myopia\nTRICK - “Convex = Converge = Positive; Concave = Cave-in = Diverge = Negative”\nPower sign bhi same: convex +, concave -.\n10. Lens Formula — MINUS\nFormula\nRecall\nLens formula\n1/v - 1/u = 1/f\nMagnification\nm = v/u = I/O\nPower\nP = 1/f (metre)\nUnit\nDiopter D\nTRICK - “MIRROR PLUS, LENS MINUS”\nMirror: 1/v + 1/u = 1/f.\nLens: 1/v - 1/u = 1/f.\nEXAM TRAP - “f = -20 cm\n P = -5 D”\n→\nNegative power = concave lens.\n11. Dispersion — VIBGYOR\nColour\nSource Exam Point\nViolet\nMost deviated; most scattered\nBlue\nStrongly scattered; sky appears blue\nGreen\nPrimary colour of light\nRed\nLeast deviated; least scattered\nTRICK - “Violet MOST; Red LEAST”\nDeviation aur scattering dono mein source same extreme pair deta hai.\nTRICK - “VIBGYOR: Violet\nRed = Deviation/Scattering Down”\n→\nViolet end high, red end low.\n12. Rainbow + Colour Mixing\n• Rainbow: refraction + TIR + refraction in water droplets\n• Sun observer ke behind hota hai\n• Primary colours of light = Red, Green, Blue\n• Primary colours of pigment/paint = Red, Yellow, Blue"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\nMix\nResult\nGreen + Red\nYellow\nBlue + Red\nMagenta\nBlue + Green\nCyan\nRGB\nWhite\nTRICK - “RGB = Light = White”\nR+G=Yellow; B+R=Magenta; B+G=Cyan.\nTRICK - “Complementary: R-C, G-M, B-Y”\nRed-Cyan; Green-Magenta; Blue-Yellow.\n13. Rayleigh Scattering — Shorter More\nObservation\nReason\nViolet scatters most\nShortest visible wavelength side\nSky appears blue\nBlue strongly scattered + eye more sensitive to blue than violet\nSunrise/sunset red\nLong path scatters shorter wavelengths away\nDanger signal red\nRed scatters least\nTRICK - “Shorter λ\n More Scatter; Red = Least”\n→\nDanger signal red because red scatters least.\nEXAM TRAP -\nViolet scatters more than blue, but sky appears blue in source explanation.\n14. Human Eye — C-I-P-L-R-F-B\nPart\nFunction / Hook\nCornea\nTransparent front; light entry\nIris\nColoured opaque part; controls pupil size\nPupil\nControls amount of entering light\nEye lens\nAdjustable converging lens\nRetina\nReal, inverted image forms\nFovea / Yellow spot\nSharpest vision\nBlind spot\nZero light sensitivity\nCiliary muscles\nChange lens focal length\nTRICK - “Retina = Real + Inverted; Fovea = Finest; Blind = Zero”\nThree eye-image traps.\n• Least distance of distinct vision = 25 cm\n• Normal vision range = 25 cm to infinity\n• Power of human eye = 4 D as given in source\nEXAM TRAP -\nRetinal image real and inverted; brain interprets it upright.\n15. Vision Defects — M-H-P-A\nDefect\nSource Symptom\nCorrection\nMyopia\nNear clear; far blurred\nConcave lens\nHypermetropia\nFar clear; near blurred\nConvex lens\nPresbyopia\nOld age; near/far difficulty\nBifocal lens\nAstigmatism\nBlurred all distances; irregular curvature\nCylindrical lens\nColour blindness\nRed-green distinction problem; hereditary\nNo cure / no lens correction"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\nTRICK - “M-H-P-A = Concave-Convex-Bifocal-Cylindrical”\nMyopia\nConcave; Hypermetropia\nConvex; Presbyopia\nBifocal; Astigmatism\nCylindrical.\n→\n→\n→\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nColour blindness has no lens correction in source.\n16. Optical Instruments — Microscope vs Telescope\nInstrument\nSource Formula / Hook\nSimple Microscope\nConvex short-f lens; M = 1 + D/F, D=25 cm\nReflecting Telescope\nConcave mirror objective; bright magnified distant images\nAstronomical Telescope at ∞\nM = -Fo/Fe\nTelescope Setup\nObjective large Fo; eyepiece small Fe; larger Fo/Fe\n more magnification\n→\nTRICK - “Telescope: Objective LONG, Eyepiece SHORT”\nFo large; Fe small.\n17. Wave Optics — Young / Diffraction / Polarisation\nPhenomenon\nSource Recall\nInterference\nThomas Young 1801; bright constructive, dark destructive\nDiffraction\nBending at edges/obstacles; Fresnel nearby source, Fraunhofer parallel\nrays\nPolarisation\nVibrations restricted to one direction; proves light transverse\nTRICK - “Young = Interference 1801”\nSoap-bubble colours = common interference example in source.\nEXAM TRAP - “Polarisation PROVES Transverse”\nNot longitudinal.\n18. Photoelectric Effect + Photon Theory\nScientist / Year\nContribution\nPlanck 1900\nQuantum/photon theory; E = hν\nEinstein 1905\nPhotoelectric effect explanation\nEinstein Nobel 1921\nFor photoelectric effect\n• Photoelectric effect: sufficient-frequency light falls on metal\n electrons emitted\n→\n• Threshold frequency = minimum frequency needed\n• Kinetic energy of emitted electrons depends on frequency, not intensity — source exam point\n• Photon energy E = hν\n• Photon momentum p = h/λ\n• ν = c/λ\nTRICK - “Planck 1900 Photon; Einstein 1905 Photoelectric; Nobel 1921”\nP-E-N timeline.\nEXAM TRAP -\nEinstein’s 1921 Nobel Prize source says photoelectric effect, not relativity."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Light\n19. Formula Flash\nTopic\nFormula / Recall\nMirror\n1/v + 1/u = 1/f\nLens\n1/v - 1/u = 1/f\nMirror magnification\nm = -v/u\nLens magnification\nm = v/u\nPower\nP = 1/f(m) D\nRefractive index\nμ = c/v\nCritical angle\nsin c = 1/μ\nPhoton energy\nE = hν\nPhoton momentum\np = h/λ\nFrequency-wavelength\nν = c/λ\n20. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Mirror formula PLUS; lens formula MINUS\n• Rear-view = convex; shaving/dentist = concave\n• Convex mirror always virtual, erect, diminished\n• Concave mirror virtual image only when object lies between F and P\n• TIR requires denser\nrarer and incidence angle > critical\n→\n• Convex lens power positive; concave lens power negative\n• Violet most deviated/scattered; red least\n• Sky appears blue despite violet scattering more\n• Myopia concave; hypermetropia convex; presbyopia bifocal; astigmatism cylindrical\n• Retinal image = real + inverted\n• Polarisation proves light is transverse\n• Planck1900 photon vs Einstein1905 photoelectric; Nobel1921 photoelectric\nEXAM TRAP - “+/\n - Mirrors - TIR - Power - V/R - Sky - Eye Defects - Retina - Polarisation - Planck/Einstein”\n−\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi chain mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Light no-medium transverse EM + dual; c=3×10^8, visible3900-7800Å; Descartes/Newton particle, Huygens wave\n Reflection\n→\ni=r+same plane; plane mirror V-E-S-L\n concave/convex: rear-view convex, shaving/dentist concave; convex always V-E-D; concave\n→\nvirtual only F-P\n Mirror PLUS 1/v+1/u=1/f, f=R/2, m=-v/u\n Refraction denser=slower+toward normal, frequency same; Snell sin\n→\n→\ni/sin r=μ=c/v\n TIR denser\nrarer + i>c, sin c=1/μ; fibre/endoscope/diamond/mirage\n Convex lens + converge; concave - diverge;\n→\n→\n→\nLens MINUS 1/v-1/u=1/f, P=1/f D\n Dispersion VIBGYOR: violet most, red least; rainbow refraction+TIR+refraction; RGB light\nwhite;\n→\n→\nR-C/G-M/B-Y complementary\n Rayleigh shorter scatters more; sky blue, sunset/danger red\n Eye retina real-inverted, fovea sharp,\n→\n→\nblind spot zero, near point25cm; defects M-H-P-A = concave-convex-bifocal-cylindrical\n Microscope M=1+D/F; telescope objective\n→\nFo large, eyepiece Fe small\n Young1801 interference; diffraction edge-bending; polarisation proves transverse\n Planck1900\n→\n→\nphoton E=hν, p=h/λ; Einstein1905 photoelectric, Nobel1921 for photoelectric.”\nTOP 5: Mirror PLUS vs Lens MINUS | Rear-view convex / Shaving concave | TIR D\nR + i>c | M-H-P-A corrections | Planck1900 vs\n→\nEinstein1905/Nobel1921."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Semiconductor\nSEMICONDUCTOR — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 12 · Intrinsic + Extrinsic + Doping + n-Type/p-Type + Photodiode + Zener + LED + Solar Cell\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke intrinsic/extrinsic semiconductors, doping, n-Type/p-Type carrier traps, temperature\nbehaviour aur semiconductor devices/principles ko fast exam-recall tricks mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Conductor - Semiconductor - Insulator\nMaterial\nConductivity\nBand Gap\nTemperature Effect\nExamples\nConductor\nHigh\nZero / overlapping\nResistance increases\nAg, Cu, Au, Al\nSemiconductor\nMedium\nSmall (~1 eV)\nResistance decreases\nSi, Ge\nInsulator\nVery low\nLarge (>5 eV)\nMinimal change\nGlass, Rubber, Diamond\nTRICK - “C-S-I = High-Medium-Low Conductivity”\nConductor > Semiconductor > Insulator.\nTRICK - “Semiconductor Heats\n Resistance Drops”\n→\nTemperature\n\n semiconductor conductivity\n, resistance\n.\n↑→\n↑\n↓\nSource contrasts this with conductor, where conductivity decreases / resistance rises.\nEXAM TRAP -\nDiamond = insulator, semiconductor nahi.\n2. Intrinsic vs Extrinsic — Pure vs Doped\nFeature\nIntrinsic\nExtrinsic\nPurity\nPure Si or Ge\nDoped Si or Ge\nImpurity\nNone\nAdded intentionally\nCarrier balance\nElectrons = holes\nOne carrier becomes majority\nConductivity\nRelatively low\nHigher\nMain types\n—\nn-Type, p-Type\nTRICK - “Intrinsic = In-Pure; Extrinsic = Extra Impurity”\nIntrinsic = pure semiconductor.\nExtrinsic = doped semiconductor.\nTRICK - “Si-Ge = Pure Pair”\nSilicon + Germanium = intrinsic examples.\nEXAM TRAP - “0 K Intrinsic = Perfect Insulator”\nAt absolute zero free carriers absent.\n3. Doping — Small Impurity, Big Conductivity\n• Doping = pure Si/Ge mein very small impurity add karna\n• Purpose = available charge carriers increase karna\n conductivity increase\n→\n• Added impurity = dopant\n• Extrinsic semiconductor doping ke baad banta hai\nTRICK - “Doping = Dopant Added\n Carriers Added”\n→\nConductivity increase is the exam core."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Semiconductor\n4. n-Type — Penta Gives Extra Electron\nPoint\nn-Type\nDopant valency\nPentavalent = 5\nCommon dopants\nArsenic (As), Antimony (Sb), Phosphorus (P)\nBond idea\n4 electrons bond; 5th becomes extra free electron\nMajority carrier\nElectrons (-)\nMinority carrier\nHoles\nMeaning of n\nNegative carriers = electrons\nTRICK - “n = 5\n Extra Electron”\n→\nPentavalent dopant gives one extra electron.\nTRICK - “A-S-P = n-Type”\nArsenic - Antimony - Phosphorus.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPhosphorus doping gives n-Type.\n5. p-Type — Tri Leaves One Hole\nPoint\np-Type\nDopant valency\nTrivalent = 3\nCommon dopants\nAluminium (Al), Boron (B), Gallium (Ga), Indium (In)\nBond idea\nOne electron missing\n hole\n→\nMajority carrier\nHoles (+)\nMinority carrier\nElectrons\nMeaning of p\nPositive carriers = holes\nTRICK - “p = 3\n One Hole”\n→\nTrivalent dopant leaves one bond incomplete.\nTRICK - “A-B-G-I = p-Type”\nAluminium - Boron - Gallium - Indium.\nEXAM TRAP -\nAluminium gives p-Type even though aluminium itself is a good conductor.\n6. n-Type vs p-Type — 5E vs 3H\nProperty\nn-Type\np-Type\nDopant\nPentavalent (5)\nTrivalent (3)\nExamples\nAs, Sb, P\nAl, B, Ga, In\nMajority carrier\nElectrons\nHoles\nMinority carrier\nHoles\nElectrons\nCarrier sign\nNegative\nPositive\nOverall charge\nNeutral\nNeutral\nTRICK - “5\n Electron; 3\n Hole”\n→\n→\nn = pentavalent + electrons.\np = trivalent + holes."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Semiconductor\nEXAM TRAP - “Carrier Sign ≠ Net Charge”\nBoth n-Type and p-Type electrically neutral overall.\n7. Photodiode — Light Detection\nItem\nPhotodiode\nPurpose\nOptical / light detection\nConversion\nLight\n electrical signal\n→\nPrinciple\nPhotoelectric effect\nUse\nLight intensity detection; light-operated keys\nTRICK - “Photodiode = PHOTOelectric = Detect Light”\nPhotoelectric effect.\n8. Zener Diode — Reverse Bias Regulator\nItem\nZener Diode\nMain purpose\nVoltage regulation / voltage control\nOperation\nReverse bias\nRegion\nReverse-breakdown region\nResult\nNearly constant load voltage\nTRICK - “Zener = Zero-Worry Voltage in Reverse”\nReverse-bias breakdown\n voltage regulation.\n→\nEXAM TRAP -\nZener ko ordinary forward-biased diode ki tarah treat mat karna.\n9. LED — Electrical to Light\nItem\nLED\nFull form\nLight Emitting Diode\nConversion\nElectrical energy\n radiant/light energy\n→\nPrinciple\nElectroluminescence\nInventor\nNick Holonyak\nUses\nRemote control, burglar alarm, optical communication\nTRICK - “LED = Electricity\n Light = Electroluminescence”\n→\nInventor = Nick Holonyak.\nEXAM TRAP -\nLED principle = Electroluminescence; photoelectric/photovoltaic nahi.\n10. Solar Cell — Light to Electrical\nItem\nSolar Cell\nConversion\nSolar/light energy\n electrical energy\n→\nPrinciple\nPhotovoltaic effect\nUses\nRemote-area power generation; artificial-satellite batteries\nTRICK - “Solar = PhotoVOLTAIC = Light\n Voltage/Electricity”\n→\nPhotovoltaic effect."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Semiconductor\n11. Device Principle Master — P-Z-L-S\nDevice\nEnergy / Function\nPrinciple\nPhotodiode\nLight\n electrical signal\n→\nPhotoelectric effect\nZener diode\nVoltage regulation\nReverse breakdown\nLED\nElectrical\n light\n→\nElectroluminescence\nSolar cell\nLight\n electrical\n→\nPhotovoltaic effect\nTRICK - “PhotoDIODE = Photoelectric; Solar = Photovoltaic; LED = Electroluminescence”\nTeen similar-looking principles ko alag-alag lock karo.\nEXAM TRAP - “Zener = Reverse Breakdown”\nFunction-based fourth device.\n12. Temperature Behaviour — Semiconductor vs Conductor\nMaterial\nTemperature ↑\nResult\nSemiconductor\nConductivity ↑\nResistance ↓\nConductor\nConductivity ↓\nResistance ↑\nTRICK - “Semi Hot = Conduct More; Metal Hot = Resist More”\nOpposite temperature behaviour.\nEXAM TRAP -\nSemiconductor conductivity temperature ke saath increases.\n13. Rapid-Fire Recall\nQuestion\nAnswer\nKey intrinsic semiconductors?\nSilicon, Germanium\nDoping means?\nAdding impurity\nAdded impurity called?\nDopant\nn-Type valency?\nPentavalent 5\nn-Type majority?\nElectrons\np-Type valency?\nTrivalent 3\np-Type majority?\nHoles\nAluminium doping?\np-Type\nPhosphorus doping?\nn-Type\nIntrinsic at 0 K?\nPerfect insulator\nPhotodiode principle?\nPhotoelectric effect\nZener use?\nVoltage regulation\nLED principle?\nElectroluminescence\nLED inventor?\nNick Holonyak\nSolar-cell principle?\nPhotovoltaic effect"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Semiconductor\n14. Final Exam Traps — 10 Red Flags\n• Semiconductor resistance decreases as temperature increases\n• Silicon and Germanium = intrinsic semiconductor examples\n• At 0 K intrinsic semiconductor = perfect insulator\n• n-Type = pentavalent 5; electrons majority\n• p-Type = trivalent 3; holes majority\n• Aluminium gives p-Type; Phosphorus gives n-Type\n• n-Type/p-Type overall electrically neutral\n• Photodiode = photoelectric effect\n• LED = electroluminescence; inventor Nick Holonyak\n• Solar cell = photovoltaic; Zener = reverse-bias voltage regulation\nEXAM TRAP - “Temp-SiGe-0K-5E-3H-Al/P-Neutral-PhotoD-LED-Solar/Zener”\nChapter ke 10 highest-yield traps isi order mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“C-S-I = high-medium-low conductivity; semiconductor small ~1eV band gap, Si-Ge examples, heat\n conductivity\n resistance\n;\n↑\n↑\n↓\ndiamond insulator\n Intrinsic = pure Si/Ge, e=holes, low conductivity, 0K perfect insulator; Extrinsic = doped, higher conductivity,\n→\nn/p types\n Doping = tiny impurity add\n carriers\n\n conductivity\n\n n-Type: PENTA5, A-S-P = As-Sb-P, one extra electron,\n→\n→\n↑→\n↑→\nelectrons majority, holes minority\n p-Type: TRI3, A-B-G-I = Al-B-Ga-In, one hole, holes majority, electrons minority\n both overall\n→\n→\nneutral\n Photodiode light\nelectrical by photoelectric; Zener reverse-breakdown voltage regulator; LED electrical\nlight by\n→\n→\n→\nelectroluminescence, Nick Holonyak; Solar light\nelectrical by photovoltaic\n Master split: PhotoD=Photoelectric,\n→\n→\nSolar=Photovoltaic, LED=Electroluminescence, Zener=Reverse Breakdown.”\nTOP 5: Heat\n\n semiconductor R\n | n-Type 5/electron vs p-Type 3/hole | Both neutral | Photodiode-photoelectric vs Solar-photovoltaic vs\n↑→\n↓\nLED-electroluminescence | Zener reverse-bias regulator."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Our Universe\nOUR UNIVERSE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nGeneral Science · Physics · Chapter 13 · Big Bang + Galaxies + Stars + Sun + Solar System + India & Space\nYe full notes nahi hai — source chapter ke universe theories, red/blue shift, galaxy types, star facts, Sun, planets aur Indian space\nmissions ke high-memory names, years, numbers aur exam traps ko fast recall format mein compress kiya gaya hai.\n1. Universe — Number Hooks\nFact\nSource Answer\nAge of Universe\n13.8 billion years\nBig Bang\nGeorge Lemaitre — 1930\nHubble constant\n67 km/s/Mpc\nTotal stars\n 10^22\n≈\nOur galaxy\nMilky Way — Spiral\nNearest star after Sun\nProxima Centauri\nBrightest night-sky star\nSirius — Dog Star\nSunlight to Earth\n8 min 20 sec\nChandrasekhar limit\n1.44 solar masses\nTRICK - “13.8 - 67 - 10²² - 8:20 - 1.44”\nUniverse age\n Hubble constant\n stars\n sunlight time\n Chandrasekhar limit.\n→\n→\n→\n→\n2. Universe Theories — P-C-H-H-L\nTheory\nPropounder\nYear / Core\nGeocentric\nPtolemy\nAncient; Earth at centre\nHeliocentric\nCopernicus\n1543; Sun at centre\nHerschel Theory\nHerschel\n1785; Milky Way shape/structure\nHubble Theory\nEdwin Hubble\n1925; expanding universe\nBig Bang\nGeorge Lemaitre\n1930; origin ~13.8 bya\nTRICK - “P-C-H-H-L = Earth-Sun-Galaxy-Expansion-Origin”\nPtolemy Earth-centre; Copernicus Sun-centre; Herschel Milky Way; Hubble expansion; Lemaitre Big Bang.\nEXAM TRAP - “Big Bang = Lemaitre; Expansion = Hubble”\nYe do facts alag-alag hain.\n3. Red Shift - Blue Shift - Hubble\nConcept\nMeaning\nExam Interpretation\nRed Shift\nLonger/red wavelength\nMoving away\nBlue Shift\nShorter/blue wavelength\nComing closer\nHubble Law\nV = Hd\nRecession velocity = H × distance\nTRICK - “RED = Recedes; BLUE = Back Toward Us”\nMost distant galaxies red shift; source gives Andromeda as blue-shift example.\nEXAM TRAP - “V = H d; H = 67”\nSource Hubble constant = 67 km/s/Mpc.\n4. Galaxies — E-S-I\nType\nShape\nStars/Colour\nSource Example\nElliptical\nOval\nOld; yellow-red; minimum formation\nMaffei-1\nSpiral\nSpiral arms\nArms young/blue; centre old/red;\nmaximum formation\nMilky Way\nIrregular\nNo regular shape\nMixed; variable; intermediate\nformation\nSextans A"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Our Universe\nTRICK - “E-S-I = Maffei - Milky - Sextans”\nElliptical Maffei-1; Spiral Milky Way; Irregular Sextans A.\nEXAM TRAP - “Spiral Arms Blue; Centre Red”\nYoung hot stars in arms; older stars in central bulge.\n5. Star Facts — P-S-Pole-Sun\nCue\nAnswer\nNearest star after Sun\nProxima Centauri\nBrightest night-sky star\nSirius — Dog Star\nPole Star\nNorthern direction; navigation\nSun\nYellow star of Milky Way\nEXAM TRAP - “Proxima = Nearest; Sirius = Brightest”\nNearest aur brightest ko interchange mat karna.\n6. Star Composition + Colour Temperature\nItem\nSource Recall\nHydrogen\n70%\nHelium\n28%\nCarbon\n1.5%\nNitrogen + Neon\n0.5%\nRed stars\nCoolest\n 3000-4000 K\n≈\nYellow stars\n 5000-6000 K; Sun yellow\n≈\nBlue stars\nHottest > 10,000 K\nTRICK - “H-He-C-NN = 70-28-1.5-0.5”\nSource star-gas composition.\nTRICK - “Red Cool - Yellow Medium - Blue Hot”\nColour-temperature order.\n7. Black Hole + Chandrasekhar\n• Black hole gravity itni strong ki light bhi escape nahi kar sakti\n• Chandrasekhar limit = 1.44 solar masses\n• Named after Subrahmanyan Chandrasekhar\n• At/below limit: white dwarf can remain stable\n• Sufficiently massive star beyond limit: after supernova collapse can produce neutron star or black hole\nTRICK - “Chandra = 1.44 Sun”\nWhite-dwarf stability limit.\nEXAM TRAP -\nChandrasekhar limit 1.44 solar masses; nearest star fact se mix mat karna.\n8. Constellations — U-O-C\n• Constellation = recognisable group/pattern of stars\n• Saptarishi = Ursa Major\n• Orion = source notes guide toward Sirius\n• Cassiopeia = important example"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Our Universe\nTRICK - “U-O-C = Ursa Major - Orion - Cassiopeia”\nSaptarishi = Ursa Major.\n9. Sun — 109 / 28 / 8:20 / Photo\nSun Fact\nSource Value\nDiameter\n 109 × Earth diameter\n≈\nGravity\n 28 × Earth gravity\n≈\nLight travel time\n8 min 20 sec\nVisible surface\nPhotosphere\nEnergy source\nNuclear fusion: H\n He\n→\nSource composition\nH 71%, He 26.5%, others 2.5%\nTRICK - “Sun = 109 - 28 - 8:20 - PHOTO”\nDiameter, gravity, light time, visible surface.\nEXAM TRAP - “Photosphere Visible; Chromosphere + Corona Above”\nVisible surface = Photosphere.\n10. Planets Order — M-V-E-M-J-S-U-N\n• Mercury\n Venus\n Earth\n Mars\n Jupiter\n Saturn\n Uranus\n Neptune\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\n→\nTRICK - “M-V-E-M-J-S-U-N”\nSun se outward 8 major planets ka order.\nEXAM TRAP -\nPluto = dwarf planet; eight major planets mein nahi.\n11. Inner vs Outer — M-V-E-M / J-S-U-N\nFeature\nInner / Terrestrial\nOuter / Jovian\nMembers\nMercury, Venus, Earth, Mars\nJupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune\nNature\nRocky, dense\nMostly gaseous / giant\nSize\nGenerally smaller\nMuch larger\nMoons/rings\nFewer\nMany\nTRICK - “Inner = MVEM Rocky; Outer = JSUN Giant”\nFour-four planet split.\n12. Planet High-Yield Facts\nPlanet\nSource Memory Hook\nMercury\nClosest + smallest; source notes no atmosphere; huge temperature variation\nVenus\nHottest + brightest; greenhouse; retrograde rotation\nEarth\nLife + one moon + Blue Planet\nMars\nRed due iron oxide; Phobos + Deimos; MOM\nJupiter\nLargest; Great Red Spot; source lists 95 moons\nSaturn\nLeast dense major planet; rings; source lists 146 moons\nUranus\nRotates nearly on side; tilt ~98°; very cold\nNeptune\nFarthest major planet; strongest winds\nTRICK - “Venus HOT; Jupiter BIG; Mercury SMALL”\nHottest ≠ closest.\nTRICK - “Mars Red; Earth Blue; Uranus Sideways; Neptune Winds”\nColour + motion + weather hooks."," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Our Universe\nEXAM TRAP -\nHottest planet = Venus, not Mercury.\n13. India & Space — Mission Chain\nMission / Satellite\nSource Detail\nSignificance\nMOM / Mangalyaan\nMars Orbiter Mission; 2013\nIndia first interplanetary mission\nGISAT-1\nGeo Imaging Satellite-1\nSource lists as India first satellite in geostationary\norbit\nAPPLE\nAriane Passenger Payload Experiment\nIndia first geostationary telecommunication\nsatellite\nChandrayaan-1\nMoon mission; 2008\nEvidence of water molecules on Moon\nChandrayaan-3\nMoon lander; 2023\nSoft landing in lunar south-polar region; source\nnotes first country near south pole\nAditya-L1\nSolar mission; 2023\nIndia first dedicated solar observatory mission\nTRICK - “MOM = Mangalyaan = Mars = 2013”\nIndia first interplanetary mission.\nTRICK - “APPLE = Ariane Passenger Payload Experiment”\nFull form ko exact yaad karo.\nTRICK - “C1 Water; C3 South Pole; A-L1 Sun”\nChandrayaan-1\n water evidence; Chandrayaan-3\n south-polar landing; Aditya-L1\n solar observatory.\n→\n→\n→\n14. APPLE vs GISAT-1\nSatellite\nSource Distinction\nAPPLE\nFirst geostationary telecommunication satellite named in source\nGISAT-1\nListed separately as Geo Imaging Satellite-1 and India first satellite in\ngeostationary orbit\nEXAM TRAP - “APPLE = Telecom; GISAT = Geo Imaging”\nDono ko same label mat karna.\n15. Rapid-Fire Revision\nQuestion / Cue\nAnswer\nBig Bang\nGeorge Lemaitre — 1930\nHeliocentric\nCopernicus — 1543\nGeocentric\nPtolemy\nHubble Law\nV = Hd\nAge Universe\n13.8 billion years\nOur galaxy\nMilky Way — Spiral\nNearest star after Sun\nProxima Centauri\nBrightest night star\nSirius\nChandrasekhar limit\n1.44 solar masses\nSun visible surface\nPhotosphere\nSunlight to Earth\n8 min 20 sec\nHottest / largest / smallest\nVenus / Jupiter / Mercury\nRed / Blue planet\nMars / Earth\nIndia first interplanetary\nMangalyaan / MOM\nAPPLE full form\nAriane Passenger Payload Experiment"," ExamFusion Prep · Physics Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Our Universe\n16. Final Exam Traps — 12 Red Flags\n• Big Bang = George Lemaitre; Hubble = expansion\n• Red shift = away; Blue shift = approaching\n• Milky Way = Spiral galaxy\n• Nearest star after Sun = Proxima Centauri; brightest night star = Sirius\n• Red stars coolest; Blue stars hottest\n• Chandrasekhar limit = 1.44 solar masses\n• Sun visible surface = Photosphere\n• Sunlight reaches Earth in 8 min 20 sec\n• Hottest = Venus; largest = Jupiter; smallest = Mercury\n• Pluto = dwarf planet\n• MOM = Mangalyaan = India first interplanetary mission\n• APPLE = Ariane Passenger Payload Experiment; do not confuse with GISAT-1\nEXAM TRAP - “Lemaitre/Hubble - Red/Blue - Milky - Proxima/Sirius - Star Colour - 1.44 - Photo - 8:20 - V/J/M -\nPluto - MOM - APPLE”\nChapter ke 12 highest-yield traps isi sequence mein revise karo.\nMASTER MEMORY CHAIN — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\nMASTER - 1-Line Revision Chain\n“Universe 13.8 bya; Big Bang Lemaitre1930, Hubble expansion1925 + V=Hd, H=67; theories P-C-H-H-L = Ptolemy-Copernicus-\nHerschel-Hubble-Lemaitre\n Red away, Blue toward; Andromeda blue-shift example\n Galaxies E-S-I = Maffei-1 / Milky Way /\n→\n→\nSextans A; Milky spiral arms blue, centre red\n Stars: Proxima nearest after Sun, Sirius brightest night/Dog Star, Pole Star north;\n→\ngases H-He-C-NN = 70-28-1.5-0.5; Red cool, Yellow medium, Blue hot\n Black hole light cannot escape; Chandra limit1.44Sun;\n→\nconstellations Ursa Major/Saptarishi-Orion-Cassiopeia\n Sun 109×diameter, 28×gravity, light8:20, Photosphere visible, fusion H\nHe;\n→\n→\nsource comp71/26.5/2.5\n Planets M-V-E-M-J-S-U-N; inner MVEM rocky vs outer JSUN giant; Venus hottest, Jupiter largest, Mercury\n→\nsmallest; Mars red, Earth blue, Uranus side98°, Neptune strongest winds; Pluto dwarf\n India space: MOM=Mangalyaan2013 first\n→\ninterplanetary; C1-2008 water evidence; C3-2023 south-polar soft landing; Aditya-L1-2023 solar; APPLE=Ariane Passenger Payload\nExperiment telecom vs GISAT-1 Geo Imaging.”\nTOP 5: Lemaitre Big Bang vs Hubble expansion | Proxima nearest vs Sirius brightest | Sun Photosphere + 8:20 | Venus hot/Jupiter\nbig/Mercury small | MOM + APPLE full form."]}];
